window.__STUDY4_READ_SYNONYMS = {"reading_u2_1":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>Bovids</span></b></p><p><span>The family of mammals called bovids belongs to the Artiodactyl class, which also includes giraffes. Bovids are a highly diverse group consisting of 137 species, some of which are man's most important domestic animals.</span></p><p><span>Bovids are well represented in most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"c2e7cef4-052e-4b18-9b68-42c1ad71a223\">parts of Eurasia and Southeast Asian islands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, but they are by far the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"c2c575e6-fb35-47cd-a343-e468e1572fa8\">most numerous and diverse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in the latter. Some species of bovid are solitary, but others live in large groups with complex social structures. Although bovids have adapted to a wide range of habitats, from arctic tundra to deep tropical forest, the majority of species <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"cbb15342-b116-4d3d-b8c4-5a1ee457ab69\">favour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"69138141-7f60-4c51-997c-9deb4d7f286b\">open grassland, scrub or desert<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. This diversity of habitat is also matched by great diversity in size and form: at one extreme is the royal antelope of West Africa, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"d5092932-7c58-4d9a-8638-76526d369dcf\">stands a mere 25 cm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> at the shoulder; at the other, the massively built bison of North America and Europe, growing to a shoulder height of 2.2m.</span></p><p><span>Despite differences in size and appearance, bovids are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"c88983bd-e016-45bf-b54e-5544ea1d53e5\">united by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the possession of certain features. All species are ruminants, which means that they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"22fbbb85-57c2-4fb8-9003-0f02c84536f5\">retain undigested food in their stomachs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, and regurgitate it as necessary. Bovids are almost exclusively herbivorous*. Typically their teeth are highly modified for browsing and grazing: grass or foliage is cropped with the upper lip and lower incisors** (the upper incisors are usually absent), and then ground down by the cheek teeth. As well as having cloven, or split hooves, the males of all bovid species and the females of most carry horns. Bovid horns have bony cores covered in a sheath of horny material that is constantly renewed from within; they are unbranched and never shed. They vary in shape and size: the relatively simple horns of a large Indian buffalo may measure around 4 m from tip to tip along the outer curve, while the various gazelles have horns with a variety of elegant curves.</span></p><p><span>Five groups, or sub-families, may be distinguished: Bovinae, Antilopinae, Cephalophinae and Antilocapridae. The sub-family Bovinae <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c5e17de7-1ee4-43b3-8105-aa46c473d278\">comprises<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> most of the larger bovids, including the African bongo and nilgai, eland, bison and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"af4d6517-f90d-4ddd-892e-c277a8980d0c\">cattle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. Unlike most other bovids they are all <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"eb18a788-7e56-4875-a887-c8f26d1c29e7\">non-territorial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. The ancestors of the various species of domestic cattle banteng, gaur, yak and water buffalo are generally rare and endangered in the wild, while the auroch (the ancestor of the domestic cattle of Europe) is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"6a07e75c-4ba7-41b8-9087-f350b6c1b22e\">extinct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The term 'antelope' is not a very precise zoological name – it is used to loosely describe a number of bovids that have followed different lines of development. Antelopes are typically long-legged, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d3bcc0f3-8731-4e58-8c8c-836918fc6032\">fast-running<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> species, often with long horns that may be laid along the back when the animal is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d3bcc0f3-8731-4e58-8c8c-836918fc6032\">in full flight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. There are two main sub-groups of antelope: Hippotraginae, which includes the oryx and the addax, and Antilopinae, which generally contains slighter and more graceful animals such as gazelle and the springbok. Antelopes are mainly grassland species, but many have adapted to flooded grasslands: pukus, waterbucks and lechwes are all good at swimming, usually feeding in deep water, while the sitatunga has long, splayed hooves that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"999bddb4-156d-4c7e-90c5-44126f6a3464\">enable it to walk freely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5a24da27-26f6-438f-8ff1-44d18c4b0805\">on swampy ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The sub-family Caprinae includes the sheep and the goat, together with various relatives such as the goral and the tahr. Most are woolly or have long hair. Several species, such as wild goats, chamois and ibex, are agile cliff and mountain-dwellers. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ec87686c-5e76-49ac-a776-dddf43885d7f\">Tolerance of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e78196f3-ae31-4312-bc44-a498e9eabff5\">extreme conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> is most marked in this group: Barbary and bighorn sheep have adapted to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"df0137ba-4065-49f3-b7d6-65bc6a63ffce\">arid deserts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, while Rocky Mountain sheep survive high up in mountains and musk oxen in arctic tundra.</span></p><p><span>The duiker of Africa belongs to the Cephalophinae sub-family. It is generally small and solitary, often living in thick forest. Although mainly feeding on grass and leaves, some duikers – unlike most other bovids – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"2eef0865-e9ea-4295-8eb0-f1ef84eb057a\">are believed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> eat insects and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"afbf4ede-e9b1-44af-93a5-60e7f6ba91b8\">feed on dead animal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> carcasses, and even to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"afbf4ede-e9b1-44af-93a5-60e7f6ba91b8\">kill small animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The pronghorn is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"65821ca8-5978-43b0-9965-cc68ca0fc044\">sole survivor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> of a New World sub-family of herbivorous ruminants, the Antilocapridae in North America. It is similar in appearance and habits to the Old World antelope. Although greatly reduced in numbers since the arrival of Europeans, and the subsequent enclosure of grasslands, the pronghorn is still found in considerable numbers throughout North America, from Washington State to Mexico. When alarmed by the approach of wolves or other predators, hairs on the pronghorn's rump stand erect, showing and emphasising the white patch there. At this signal, the whole herd gallops off at a speed of over 60 km per hour.</span></p><p><span>___________________________________________________________________</span></p><p><span>*herbivorous: plant-eating</span></p><p><span>**incisors: front teeth</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-3 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309844\" id=\"question-wrapper-309844\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"c2e7cef4-052e-4b18-9b68-42c1ad71a223\">region<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"c2c575e6-fb35-47cd-a343-e468e1572fa8\">biggest range<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of bovids to be found?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Africa</li> <li>B. Eurasia</li> <li>C. North America</li> <li>D. South-east Asia</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309845\" id=\"question-wrapper-309845\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Most bovids have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"cbb15342-b116-4d3d-b8c4-5a1ee457ab69\">preference for living<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. isolation</li> <li>B. small groups</li> <li>C. tropical forest</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"69138141-7f60-4c51-997c-9deb4d7f286b\">wide open spaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309846\" id=\"question-wrapper-309846\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which of the following <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"c88983bd-e016-45bf-b54e-5544ea1d53e5\">features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> do all bovids have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"c88983bd-e016-45bf-b54e-5544ea1d53e5\">in common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Their horns are short</li> <li>B. They have upper incisors</li> <li>C. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"22fbbb85-57c2-4fb8-9003-0f02c84536f5\">store food in the body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></li> <li>D. Their hooves are undivided</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following characteristics (Questions 4-8) and the list of sub-families below. Match each characteristic with the correct sub-family, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 4-8 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once</span></p><p><b><span>List of sub-families</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Antelope</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Bovinae</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Caprinae</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Cephalophinae</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309847\" id=\"question-wrapper-309847\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ec87686c-5e76-49ac-a776-dddf43885d7f\">can endure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e78196f3-ae31-4312-bc44-a498e9eabff5\">very harsh environments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309848\" id=\"question-wrapper-309848\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c5e17de7-1ee4-43b3-8105-aa46c473d278\">includes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"af4d6517-f90d-4ddd-892e-c277a8980d0c\">the ox and the cow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309849\" id=\"question-wrapper-309849\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"2eef0865-e9ea-4295-8eb0-f1ef84eb057a\">may<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"afbf4ede-e9b1-44af-93a5-60e7f6ba91b8\">supplement its diet with meat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309850\" id=\"question-wrapper-309850\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>can usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d3bcc0f3-8731-4e58-8c8c-836918fc6032\">move at speed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309851\" id=\"question-wrapper-309851\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"eb18a788-7e56-4875-a887-c8f26d1c29e7\">does not defend a particular area of land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309852\" id=\"question-wrapper-309852\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"d5092932-7c58-4d9a-8638-76526d369dcf\">smallest species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of Bovid called?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) royal antelope</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309853\" id=\"question-wrapper-309853\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which species of Bovinae has now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"6a07e75c-4ba7-41b8-9087-f350b6c1b22e\">died out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) auroch</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309854\" id=\"question-wrapper-309854\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"999bddb4-156d-4c7e-90c5-44126f6a3464\">facilitates the movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of the sitatunga <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5a24da27-26f6-438f-8ff1-44d18c4b0805\">over wetland<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">splayed hooves [OR] long, splayed hooves</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309855\" id=\"question-wrapper-309855\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What sort of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"df0137ba-4065-49f3-b7d6-65bc6a63ffce\">terrain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> do barbary sheep live in?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(arid) deserts</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309856\" id=\"question-wrapper-309856\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"65821ca8-5978-43b0-9965-cc68ca0fc044\">only living member<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> of the Antilocapridae sub-family?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) pronghorn</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c2e7cef4-052e-4b18-9b68-42c1ad71a223","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"region","passagePhrase":"parts of Eurasia and Southeast Asian islands"},{"uid":"c2c575e6-fb35-47cd-a343-e468e1572fa8","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"biggest range","passagePhrase":"most numerous and diverse"},{"uid":"cbb15342-b116-4d3d-b8c4-5a1ee457ab69","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"preference for living","passagePhrase":"favour"},{"uid":"69138141-7f60-4c51-997c-9deb4d7f286b","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"wide open spaces","passagePhrase":"open grassland, scrub or desert"},{"uid":"d5092932-7c58-4d9a-8638-76526d369dcf","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"smallest species","passagePhrase":"stands a mere 25 cm"},{"uid":"c88983bd-e016-45bf-b54e-5544ea1d53e5","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"features ... in common","passagePhrase":"united by"},{"uid":"22fbbb85-57c2-4fb8-9003-0f02c84536f5","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"store food in the body","passagePhrase":"retain undigested food in their stomachs"},{"uid":"c5e17de7-1ee4-43b3-8105-aa46c473d278","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"includes","passagePhrase":"comprises"},{"uid":"af4d6517-f90d-4ddd-892e-c277a8980d0c","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"the ox and the cow","passagePhrase":"cattle"},{"uid":"eb18a788-7e56-4875-a887-c8f26d1c29e7","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"does not defend a particular area of land","passagePhrase":"non-territorial"},{"uid":"6a07e75c-4ba7-41b8-9087-f350b6c1b22e","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"died out","passagePhrase":"extinct"},{"uid":"d3bcc0f3-8731-4e58-8c8c-836918fc6032","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"move at speed","passagePhrase":"fast-running ... in full flight"},{"uid":"999bddb4-156d-4c7e-90c5-44126f6a3464","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"facilitates the movement","passagePhrase":"enable it to walk freely"},{"uid":"5a24da27-26f6-438f-8ff1-44d18c4b0805","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"over wetland","passagePhrase":"on swampy ground"},{"uid":"ec87686c-5e76-49ac-a776-dddf43885d7f","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"can endure","passagePhrase":"Tolerance of"},{"uid":"e78196f3-ae31-4312-bc44-a498e9eabff5","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"very harsh environments","passagePhrase":"extreme conditions"},{"uid":"df0137ba-4065-49f3-b7d6-65bc6a63ffce","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"terrain","passagePhrase":"arid deserts"},{"uid":"2eef0865-e9ea-4295-8eb0-f1ef84eb057a","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"may","passagePhrase":"are believed to"},{"uid":"afbf4ede-e9b1-44af-93a5-60e7f6ba91b8","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"supplement its diet with meat","passagePhrase":"feed on dead animal ... kill small animals"},{"uid":"65821ca8-5978-43b0-9965-cc68ca0fc044","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"only living member","passagePhrase":"sole survivor"}]},"reading_u2_2":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>A unique golden textile</span></b></p><p><i><span>A two-man project to use spider silk is achieved after 4 years</span></i></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c666b9d8-2f11-4881-a1d7-32e9265379d8\">A rare textile<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> made from the silk of more than a million wild spiders has been on display at the American Museum of Natural History in New York City. To produce this golden cloth, 70 people spent four years collecting golden-orb spiders from telephone poles in Madagascar, while another dozen workers carefully extracted about 80 feet of silk filament from each of the arachnids. The resulting 11-foot-by-4-foot textile is the only large piece of cloth made from natural spider silk in the world today.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Spider silk is very <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e48663c0-16d9-4934-a17b-5337d6b97624\">elastic and </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 23\" data-uid=\"1a2f5426-691e-4b67-87cd-f326c11f8a8e e48663c0-16d9-4934-a17b-5337d6b97624\">strong</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"1a2f5426-691e-4b67-87cd-f326c11f8a8e\"> compared with steel or Kevlar</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, said textile expert Simon Peers, who co-led the project. Kevlar is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e48663c0-16d9-4934-a17b-5337d6b97624\">lightweight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> synthetic fabric, chemically related to nylon, that is used in bullet-proof vests. Kevlar is resistant to wear, tear and heat and has virtually no melting point. But the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e48663c0-16d9-4934-a17b-5337d6b97624\">tensile strength<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of spider silk is even greater than Kevlar’s aramid filaments and higher than that of high-grade steel. Most importantly, spider silk is extremely lightweight: a strand long enough to circle the Earth would weigh less than 500 grams (18 oz). It is also especially <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e48663c0-16d9-4934-a17b-5337d6b97624\">ductile<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, able to stretch up to 140 percent of its length without breaking and to retain its strength below -40 °C, giving it toughness equal to that of leading commercial fibres.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"7022ec01-f0c2-43da-b120-c3da67e04aa3\">Researchers have long been intrigued by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> the unique properties of spider silk. Unfortunately, spider silk is extremely hard to mass-produce. Unlike silkworms—easy to raise in captivity—spiders have a habit of biting off each other’s heads when housed together. According to Peers, there is intensive research worldwide aimed at replicating spider-silk tensile properties for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"f40ae368-55e9-4e90-aa57-68750a3f3c6f\">use in medicine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> and industry, but no one has yet reproduced all the qualities of natural silk.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> Peers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ad455dea-5264-48fe-8b59-ec214883d1c4\">conceived the idea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of weaving spider silk after <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ad455dea-5264-48fe-8b59-ec214883d1c4\">reading about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> French missionary Jacob Paul Camboué, who worked with spiders in Madagascar during the 1880s and 1890s. Camboué built a small hand-driven machine to extract silk from up to 24 spiders at once, without harming them; the spiders were briefly restrained, their silk collected, then released. Peers built a replica of this 24-spider ‘silking’ machine, said co-leader Nicholas Godley. As a test, the pair collected about 20 spiders. ‘When we stuck them in the machine and started turning it, lo and behold, this beautiful gold-coloured silk started coming out,’ Godley recalled.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> To make a textile of any significant size, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"1e533450-6e29-4c5f-b1ec-ccf94561aa22\">scale had to increase dramatically<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2e04b652-978f-4580-991f-8f92cab7c635\">Fourteen thousand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> spiders yield about an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"84973c68-ba09-456b-8845-8501e5629ed4\">ounce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of silk, Godley said, and the finished textile weighs about 2.6 pounds. By the end, handlers had worked with more than one million female golden-orb spiders—abundant in Madagascar and famed for their golden thread. Because the spiders produce silk only in the rainy season, all were collected between October and June. An additional 12 workers used hand-powered machines to extract the silk and twist it into 96-filament yarn. After ‘silking’, the spiders were released; within a week they regenerated their silk, allowing the same individuals to be used again—‘the gift that never stops giving,’ said Godley.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><b><span>F. </span></b><span>Spending four years to produce a single piece of cloth is hardly practical for scientists or companies hoping to exploit spider silk in biomedicine or as a Kevlar alternative. Several groups have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"2579d295-0479-4b90-bc82-1bcd47b2e8a6\">inserted spider genes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> into bacteria and even goats to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"f78e4989-34ee-4fa4-9afd-c971470cf205\">make silk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, but results have been only partly successful. One reason is that spider silk begins as a liquid protein <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"df022007-038a-467a-bcfd-f5eea06554d2\">produced in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> a special gland <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"4257501e-e0b4-453e-a54a-43fef2d1cab8\">in the abdomen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Using the spinneret, the spider applies force that rearranges the protein’s molecular structure, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"d8021f90-bfbe-4afb-a368-363e609cfcc0\">transforming it into solid fibre<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. ‘When we talk about a spider spinning silk, we’re talking about how it applies forces to convert liquid to solid,’ explained spider-silk expert Todd Blackledge of the University of Akron, who was not involved in the project. ‘<span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 22\" data-uid=\"0d7b5ed4-7315-4094-b19a-cb3c9a5e4b2d f4263f08-441e-4c52-8c6b-36eb28cc1281\">Every year we get closer</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"e2c5029e-7568-4d29-a844-ed8654fc7cbe\">mass production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"f4263f08-441e-4c52-8c6b-36eb28cc1281\">but we’re not there yet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.’ For now, we must be content with one extraordinarily beautiful cloth—courtesy of more than a million spiders.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs A–F. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i–ix, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. Experimenting with an old idea</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. Life cycle of Madagascar spiders</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. Advances in the textile industry</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. Resources needed to meet the project’s demands</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e48663c0-16d9-4934-a17b-5337d6b97624\">physical properties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of spider silk</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. Why artificial spider silk remains out of reach</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. A unique work of art</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. Importance of the silk-textile market</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. Difficulties of raising spiders in captivity</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309857\" id=\"question-wrapper-309857\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309858\" id=\"question-wrapper-309858\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309859\" id=\"question-wrapper-309859\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ix</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309860\" id=\"question-wrapper-309860\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309861\" id=\"question-wrapper-309861\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309862\" id=\"question-wrapper-309862\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 20–23) and the list of researchers below. Match each statement with the correct researcher, A, B or C. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 20–23 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Researchers</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Simon Peers</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Nicholas Godley</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Todd Blackledge</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309863\" id=\"question-wrapper-309863\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It takes a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2e04b652-978f-4580-991f-8f92cab7c635\">tremendous number<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of spiders to make a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"84973c68-ba09-456b-8845-8501e5629ed4\">small amount<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of silk.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309864\" id=\"question-wrapper-309864\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Scientists want to use the qualities of spider silk for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"f40ae368-55e9-4e90-aa57-68750a3f3c6f\">medical purposes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309865\" id=\"question-wrapper-309865\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Scientists are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"0d7b5ed4-7315-4094-b19a-cb3c9a5e4b2d\">making some progress<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in their efforts to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"e2c5029e-7568-4d29-a844-ed8654fc7cbe\">manufacture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> spider silk.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309866\" id=\"question-wrapper-309866\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Spider silk <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"1a2f5426-691e-4b67-87cd-f326c11f8a8e\">compares favourably to materials known for their strength<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Producing spider silk in the lab</span></b></p><p><span>Both scientists and manufacturers are interested in producing silk for many different purposes. Some researchers have tried to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"f78e4989-34ee-4fa4-9afd-c971470cf205\">grow silk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"2579d295-0479-4b90-bc82-1bcd47b2e8a6\">introducing genetic material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> into (24)______ and some animals. But these experiments have been somewhat disappointing.</span></p><p><span>It is difficult to make spider silk in a lab setting because the silk comes from a liquid protein <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"df022007-038a-467a-bcfd-f5eea06554d2\">made in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> a (25)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"4257501e-e0b4-453e-a54a-43fef2d1cab8\">inside the spider’s body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. When a spider spins silk, it applies (26)______ that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"d8021f90-bfbe-4afb-a368-363e609cfcc0\">turns this liquid into solid silk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309867\" id=\"question-wrapper-309867\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">bacteria</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309868\" id=\"question-wrapper-309868\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">gland</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309869\" id=\"question-wrapper-309869\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">force</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c666b9d8-2f11-4881-a1d7-32e9265379d8","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"A rare textile"},{"uid":"e48663c0-16d9-4934-a17b-5337d6b97624","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"physical properties","passagePhrase":"elastic and ... lightweight ... tensile strength ... ductile"},{"uid":"1a2f5426-691e-4b67-87cd-f326c11f8a8e e48663c0-16d9-4934-a17b-5337d6b97624","qNum":"15 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"strong"},{"uid":"1a2f5426-691e-4b67-87cd-f326c11f8a8e","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"compares favourably to materials known for their strength","passagePhrase":"compared with steel or Kevlar"},{"uid":"7022ec01-f0c2-43da-b120-c3da67e04aa3","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Researchers have long been intrigued by"},{"uid":"f40ae368-55e9-4e90-aa57-68750a3f3c6f","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"medical purposes","passagePhrase":"use in medicine"},{"uid":"ad455dea-5264-48fe-8b59-ec214883d1c4","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"conceived the idea ... reading about"},{"uid":"1e533450-6e29-4c5f-b1ec-ccf94561aa22","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"scale had to increase dramatically"},{"uid":"2e04b652-978f-4580-991f-8f92cab7c635","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"tremendous number","passagePhrase":"Fourteen thousand"},{"uid":"84973c68-ba09-456b-8845-8501e5629ed4","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"small amount","passagePhrase":"ounce"},{"uid":"2579d295-0479-4b90-bc82-1bcd47b2e8a6","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"introducing genetic material","passagePhrase":"inserted spider genes"},{"uid":"f78e4989-34ee-4fa4-9afd-c971470cf205","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"grow silk","passagePhrase":"make silk"},{"uid":"df022007-038a-467a-bcfd-f5eea06554d2","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"made in","passagePhrase":"produced in"},{"uid":"4257501e-e0b4-453e-a54a-43fef2d1cab8","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"inside the spider’s body","passagePhrase":"in the abdomen"},{"uid":"d8021f90-bfbe-4afb-a368-363e609cfcc0","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"turns this liquid into solid silk","passagePhrase":"transforming it into solid fibre"},{"uid":"0d7b5ed4-7315-4094-b19a-cb3c9a5e4b2d f4263f08-441e-4c52-8c6b-36eb28cc1281","qNum":"19 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Every year we get closer"},{"uid":"e2c5029e-7568-4d29-a844-ed8654fc7cbe","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"manufacture","passagePhrase":"mass production"},{"uid":"f4263f08-441e-4c52-8c6b-36eb28cc1281","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"but we’re not there yet"},{"uid":"0d7b5ed4-7315-4094-b19a-cb3c9a5e4b2d","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"making some progress","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_3":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>Inside the mind of a fan</span></b></p><p><i><span>How watching sport affects the brain</span></i></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> At about the same time that the poet Homer invented the epic hero, the ancient Greeks started a festival in which men competed in a single race, about 200 metres long. The winner received a branch of wild olives. The Greeks called this celebration the Olympics. Though the ancient spirit remains, today the Olympics are far more than that. Indeed, the Games seem to celebrate the dream of progress as embodied in the human form. That the Games are intoxicating to watch is beyond question. During the Athens Olympics in 2004, 3.4 billion people, half the world, watched them on television. Certainly, being a spectator is a thrilling experience: but why?</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> In 1996, three Italian neuroscientists, Giacomo Rizzolatti, Leonardo Fogassi and Vittorio Gallese, examined the premotor cortex of monkeys. They discovered that inside these primate brains there were groups of cells that ‘store <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"a19d1a7e-110b-4698-9f58-25e3683ae2c4\">vocabularies of motor actions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>’. Just as there are grammars of movement. These networks of cells are the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"a19d1a7e-110b-4698-9f58-25e3683ae2c4\">bodily ‘sentences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>’ we use every day, the ones our brain has chosen to retain and refine. Think, for example, about a golf swing. To those who have only watched the Masters’ Tournament on TV, golfing seems easy. To the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"fd992683-acce-44f0-8165-68108c020360\">novice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, however, the skill of casting a smooth arc with a lopsided metal stick is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"4e63ad1f-2865-44bb-bdfc-25c330f5c254\">virtually impossible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. This is because most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"78ac13b6-8bcb-4452-a691-c8070439564c\">novices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"74a57b16-082a-464f-a3c4-bb844aeef6bb\">swing with their consciousness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, using an area of the brain next to the premotor cortex. To the expert, on the other hand, a perfectly balanced stroke is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"7f215a69-c640-4395-b75c-533769f59c87\">second nature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. For him, the motor action has become <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"7f215a69-c640-4395-b75c-533769f59c87\">memorised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, and the movements are embedded in the neurons of his premotor cortex. He hits the ball with the tranquility of his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"7f215a69-c640-4395-b75c-533769f59c87\">perfected autopilot<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>These neurons in the premotor cortex, besides explaining why certain athletes seem to possess almost unbelievable levels of skill, have an even more amazing characteristic, one that caused Rizzolatti, Fogassi and Gallese to give them the lofty title ‘mirror neurons’. They note, ‘The main functional characteristic of mirror neurons is that they become active both when the monkey performs a particular action (for example, grasping an object or holding it) and, astonishingly, when it sees another individual performing a similar action.’ <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"7bab47a5-4060-4fcf-a8db-b3f70de1a640\">Humans have an even </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30 37\" data-uid=\"70c0cf3d-0a17-41bd-80fe-8eee46bde4a2 7bab47a5-4060-4fcf-a8db-b3f70de1a640\">more elaborate</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> mirror neuron <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"7bab47a5-4060-4fcf-a8db-b3f70de1a640\">system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. These peculiar cells mirror, inside the brain, the outside world: they enable us to internalise the actions of another. In order to be activated, though, these cells require what the scientists call ‘goal-orientated movements’. If we are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"42889064-e2b4-4fef-9d49-29601a9e7b58\">staring at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> a photograph, a fixed image of a runner mid-stride, our mirror neurons are totally silent. They only fire when the runner is active: running, moving or sprinting.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> What these electrophysiological studies indicate is that when we watch a golfer or a runner in action, the mirror neurons in our own premotor cortex light up as if we were the ones competing. This phenomenon of neural mirror was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"65045576-f5e6-40aa-bd2c-377ae38f480b\">first discovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in 1954, when two French physiologists, Gastaut and Bert, found that the brains of humans vibrate with two distinct wavelengths, alpha and mu. The mu system is involved in neural mirroring. It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b6387ff9-f20c-47fd-9290-5a8c64379fec\">active when your bodies are still<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, and disappears whenever we do something active, like playing sports or changing the TV channel. The surprising fact is that the mu signal is also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b6387ff9-f20c-47fd-9290-5a8c64379fec\">quiet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> when we watch someone else being active, as on TV, these results are the effect of mirror neurons.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Rizzolatti, Fogassi and Gallese call the idea of mirror neurons the ‘direct matching hypothesis’. They believe that we only understand the movement of sports stars when we ‘map the visual representation of the observed action onto our motor representation of the same action’. According to this theory, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"edb8cf27-caf9-4aea-bb93-87e893abbbdd\">watching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> an ‘Olympic athlete’ causes the motor system of the observer to resonate. The “motor knowledge” of the observer is used to understand the observed action. But mirror neurons are more than just the neural basis for our attitude to sport. It turns out that watching a great golfer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"0710a4cc-ffda-44fe-986a-4fc9e5c157e6\">makes us better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> golfers, and watching a great sprinter actually makes us run faster. This ability to learn by watching is a crucial skill. From the acquisition of language as infants to learning facial expressions, mimesis (copying) is an essential part of being conscious. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"87715d64-18a1-45de-8fd4-62b8fc9e8abc\">best athletes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> are those with a premotor cortex capable of imagining the movements of victory, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"3e918363-ead6-4876-8248-6443648f0083\">together with the physical properties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"87715d64-18a1-45de-8fd4-62b8fc9e8abc\">make those movements real<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>But how many of us regularly watch sports in order to be a better athlete? Rather, we <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27 35\" data-uid=\"3159f073-4448-4d5a-a3ed-9fc42b12981f 95cce797-1eb6-4515-8201-e976ac27ab6a\">watch sport </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27 35\" data-uid=\"3159f073-4448-4d5a-a3ed-9fc42b12981f 566b7cc5-736e-4aa0-9d2d-0a680834991a 95cce797-1eb6-4515-8201-e976ac27ab6a\">for</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27 35\" data-uid=\"566b7cc5-736e-4aa0-9d2d-0a680834991a 95cce797-1eb6-4515-8201-e976ac27ab6a\"> the feeling</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"566b7cc5-736e-4aa0-9d2d-0a680834991a\">, the human drama</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. This feeling also derives from mirror neurons. By letting spectators share in the motions of victory, they also allow us to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"95cce797-1eb6-4515-8201-e976ac27ab6a\">share in its feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. This is because they are directly connected to the amygdalae, one of the main brain regions <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"95cce797-1eb6-4515-8201-e976ac27ab6a\">involved in emotion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. During the Olympics, the mirror neurons of whole nations will be electrically identified, their athletes causing spectators to feel, just for a second or two, the same thing. Watching sports brings people together. Most of us will never run a mile in under four minutes, or hit a home run. Our consolation comes in watching, when we gather around the TV, we all feel, just for a moment, what it is to do something perfectly.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has six paragraphs, A–F. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309870\" id=\"question-wrapper-309870\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an explanation of why watching sport may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"95cce797-1eb6-4515-8201-e976ac27ab6a\">emotionally satisfying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309871\" id=\"question-wrapper-309871\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an explanation of why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"fd992683-acce-44f0-8165-68108c020360\">beginners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> find sporting tasks <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"4e63ad1f-2865-44bb-bdfc-25c330f5c254\">difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309872\" id=\"question-wrapper-309872\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"3e918363-ead6-4876-8248-6443648f0083\">factor that needs to combine with mirroring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"87715d64-18a1-45de-8fd4-62b8fc9e8abc\">attain sporting excellence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309873\" id=\"question-wrapper-309873\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"7bab47a5-4060-4fcf-a8db-b3f70de1a640\">comparison of human and animal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> mirror neurons</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309874\" id=\"question-wrapper-309874\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"65045576-f5e6-40aa-bd2c-377ae38f480b\">first discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of brain activity related to mirror neurons</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309875\" id=\"question-wrapper-309875\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a claim <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"edb8cf27-caf9-4aea-bb93-87e893abbbdd\">linking observation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"0710a4cc-ffda-44fe-986a-4fc9e5c157e6\">improvement in performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 33–35 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309876\" id=\"question-wrapper-309876\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer uses the term ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"a19d1a7e-110b-4698-9f58-25e3683ae2c4\">grammar of movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>’ to mean</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. a level of sporting skill.</li> <li>B. a system&nbsp;of words about movement.</li> <li>C. a pattern of connected cells.</li> <li>D. a type of golf swing.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309877\" id=\"question-wrapper-309877\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer states that expert players perform their actions</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"7f215a69-c640-4395-b75c-533769f59c87\">without conscious thought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</li> <li>B. by planning each phase of movement.</li> <li>C. without regular practice.</li> <li>D. by thinking about the actions of others.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309878\" id=\"question-wrapper-309878\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer states that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"3159f073-4448-4d5a-a3ed-9fc42b12981f\">most common motive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> for watching sport is to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. improve personal performance.</li> <li>B. feel linked with people of different nationalities.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"566b7cc5-736e-4aa0-9d2d-0a680834991a\">experience strong positive emotions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> <li>D. realize what skill consists of.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36–40 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309879\" id=\"question-wrapper-309879\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"78ac13b6-8bcb-4452-a691-c8070439564c\">Inexpert sports players<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"74a57b16-082a-464f-a3c4-bb844aeef6bb\">too aware of what they are doing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309880\" id=\"question-wrapper-309880\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Monkeys have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"70c0cf3d-0a17-41bd-80fe-8eee46bde4a2\">more complex<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> mirror neuron system than humans.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309881\" id=\"question-wrapper-309881\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Looking at a photograph can activate mirror neurons.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309882\" id=\"question-wrapper-309882\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Gastaut and Bert were both researchers and sports players.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309883\" id=\"question-wrapper-309883\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The mu system is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b6387ff9-f20c-47fd-9290-5a8c64379fec\">at rest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> when we are engaged in an activity.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a19d1a7e-110b-4698-9f58-25e3683ae2c4","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"grammar of movement","passagePhrase":"vocabularies of motor actions ... bodily ‘sentences"},{"uid":"fd992683-acce-44f0-8165-68108c020360","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"beginners","passagePhrase":"novice"},{"uid":"4e63ad1f-2865-44bb-bdfc-25c330f5c254","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"difficult","passagePhrase":"virtually impossible"},{"uid":"78ac13b6-8bcb-4452-a691-c8070439564c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Inexpert sports players","passagePhrase":"novices"},{"uid":"74a57b16-082a-464f-a3c4-bb844aeef6bb","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"too aware of what they are doing","passagePhrase":"swing with their consciousness"},{"uid":"7f215a69-c640-4395-b75c-533769f59c87","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"without conscious thought","passagePhrase":"second nature ... memorised ... perfected autopilot"},{"uid":"7bab47a5-4060-4fcf-a8db-b3f70de1a640","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"comparison of human and animal","passagePhrase":"Humans have an even ... system"},{"uid":"70c0cf3d-0a17-41bd-80fe-8eee46bde4a2 7bab47a5-4060-4fcf-a8db-b3f70de1a640","qNum":"30 37","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"more elaborate"},{"uid":"42889064-e2b4-4fef-9d49-29601a9e7b58","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"staring at"},{"uid":"65045576-f5e6-40aa-bd2c-377ae38f480b","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"first discovery","passagePhrase":"first discovered"},{"uid":"b6387ff9-f20c-47fd-9290-5a8c64379fec","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"at rest","passagePhrase":"active when your bodies are still ... quiet"},{"uid":"edb8cf27-caf9-4aea-bb93-87e893abbbdd","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"linking observation","passagePhrase":"watching"},{"uid":"0710a4cc-ffda-44fe-986a-4fc9e5c157e6","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"improvement in performance","passagePhrase":"makes us better"},{"uid":"87715d64-18a1-45de-8fd4-62b8fc9e8abc","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"attain sporting excellence","passagePhrase":"best athletes ... make those movements real"},{"uid":"3e918363-ead6-4876-8248-6443648f0083","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"factor that needs to combine with mirroring","passagePhrase":"together with the physical properties"},{"uid":"3159f073-4448-4d5a-a3ed-9fc42b12981f 95cce797-1eb6-4515-8201-e976ac27ab6a","qNum":"27 35","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"watch sport"},{"uid":"3159f073-4448-4d5a-a3ed-9fc42b12981f 566b7cc5-736e-4aa0-9d2d-0a680834991a 95cce797-1eb6-4515-8201-e976ac27ab6a","qNum":"27 35","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"for"},{"uid":"566b7cc5-736e-4aa0-9d2d-0a680834991a 95cce797-1eb6-4515-8201-e976ac27ab6a","qNum":"27 35","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the feeling"},{"uid":"566b7cc5-736e-4aa0-9d2d-0a680834991a","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"experience strong positive emotions","passagePhrase":", the human drama"},{"uid":"95cce797-1eb6-4515-8201-e976ac27ab6a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"emotionally satisfying","passagePhrase":"share in its feelings ... involved in emotion"},{"uid":"3159f073-4448-4d5a-a3ed-9fc42b12981f","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"most common motive","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"70c0cf3d-0a17-41bd-80fe-8eee46bde4a2","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"more complex","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_4":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>A Brief History of Tea</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"1\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> The story of tea began in ancient China over 5,000 years ago. According to legend, the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 13\" data-uid=\"68ddb6d6-a0a7-4d0f-b09e-18d648a0fbb7 88742ae0-6495-4849-8b2c-239ad30b27a4\">Emperor Shen Nung</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"d18fe434-cde0-41ed-9a8a-cf1877f724de\">was a skilled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"88742ae0-6495-4849-8b2c-239ad30b27a4\">ruler<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, creative scientist and patron of the arts. His far-sighted edicts required, among other things, that all drinking water be boiled as a hygienic precaution. One summer day, while visiting a distant region of his realm, he and the court stopped to rest. In accordance with his ruling, the servants began to boil water for the court to drink. Dried leaves from a nearby bush fell into the boiling water, and as the leaves infused the water turned brown. As a scientist, the Emperor was <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 13\" data-uid=\"31055acd-1f66-427f-b272-e69a30962b6c 68ddb6d6-a0a7-4d0f-b09e-18d648a0fbb7\">intrigued by the new liquid</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, drank some, and found it very refreshing. And so, according to legend, tea was created.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"2\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Tea consumption spread throughout Chinese culture, reaching into every aspect of society. The first definitive book was written on tea – a book clearly reflecting Zen Buddhist philosophy – 1,200 years ago. The first tea seeds were brought to Japan by a returning Buddhist priest, who had seen the value of tea in enhancing meditation in China. As a result, he is known as the 'Father of Tea' in Japan. Because of this early association, tea in Japan has always been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"e68905f7-3687-427d-b6fb-79a63d06f3c7\">linked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"668a12c6-8c5a-4d8e-94d7-123333cca1f9\">Zen Buddhism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Tea received the Japanese Emperor's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"668a12c6-8c5a-4d8e-94d7-123333cca1f9\">support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> almost instantly and spread rapidly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"668a12c6-8c5a-4d8e-94d7-123333cca1f9\">from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the royal court and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"668a12c6-8c5a-4d8e-94d7-123333cca1f9\">monasteries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> to other sections of society.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"3\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> Tea was elevated to an art form in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"32486cdd-8590-4cc7-9870-8bf16b5f274b\">Japanese tea ceremony<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, in which supreme importance is given to making tea in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"32486cdd-8590-4cc7-9870-8bf16b5f274b\">most perfect, most polite, most graceful, most charming manner possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. Such a purity of expression prompted the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"1b11f731-96d9-44a4-8d6f-a00284c1d22d\">creation of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"706b282a-b96a-4f09-88d7-add16efe1e9f\">a particular form of architecture for 'tea house<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>', duplicating the simplicity of a forest cottage. The cultural/artistic hostesses of Japan, the geishas, began to specialize in the presentation of the tea ceremony. However, as more and more people became involved in the excitement surrounding tea, the purity of the original concept was lost, and for a period the tea ceremony became corrupted, boisterous and highly embellished. Efforts were then made to return to the earlier simplicity, with the result that, in the 15th and 16th centuries, tea was viewed as the ultimate gift. Even warlords paused for tea before battles.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"4\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> While tea was at this high level of development in parts of Asia, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9e022aba-d1b1-4b5f-8ac1-88246091ee43\">information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> concerning the then unknown beverage <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9e022aba-d1b1-4b5f-8ac1-88246091ee43\">began to filter back to Europe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Earlier traders had mentioned it, but were unclear as to whether tea should be eaten or drunk. The first European to personally encounter tea and write about it was Portuguese – Portugal, with her technologically advanced navy, had been successful in gaining the first right of trade with China.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"5\"><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Tea finally arrived in Europe in the 16th century, brought to Holland by the country's navy, and became very fashionable in the Dutch capital, the Hague. This was due in part to tea being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"29425631-3ddf-4c6d-9d1f-f59f16c7e978\">very expensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> (over $100 per pound), which immediately made it the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"29425631-3ddf-4c6d-9d1f-f59f16c7e978\">domain of the wealthy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. Slowly, as the amount of tea imported increased, the price fell, and by 1675 it was available in common food shops throughout Holland.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"6\"><b><span>F.</span></b><span> As the consumption of tea increased dramatically in Dutch society, doctors and university authorities in Holland <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"3fa1ea2d-5d14-477c-9165-915c28809b66\">argued as to its benefits or drawbacks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. The <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c48e58d2-2867-4fe7-8cd0-6a19c36bcbad\">public largely ignored the </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 9\" data-uid=\"3fa1ea2d-5d14-477c-9165-915c28809b66 c48e58d2-2867-4fe7-8cd0-6a19c36bcbad\">scholarly debate</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c48e58d2-2867-4fe7-8cd0-6a19c36bcbad\"> and continued to enjoy</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> their new beverage, though the controversy lasted from 1635 to roughly 1657. Throughout this period, France and Holland led Europe in the use of tea.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"7\"><b><span>G.</span></b><span> As the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"6c0756c0-3106-4b2a-bb72-437ee17bce3e\">craze for all things oriental<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> swept through Europe, tea became part of the way of life. Adding milk to the drink was first mentioned in 1680. Around that time, Dutch inns provided the first restaurant service of tea. Innkeepers would furnish guests with a portable tea set complete with a heating unit. The Dutchman would then prepare tea for himself and his friends outside in the inn garden. Tea <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"6c0756c0-3106-4b2a-bb72-437ee17bce3e\">remained popular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in France for only about fifty years, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 10\" data-uid=\"1c3847ef-6ba9-4cb3-beb6-4083ad3a6e30 59184d2c-667e-4140-a5b0-720e531a4b67\">being replaced by a preference</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"1c3847ef-6ba9-4cb3-beb6-4083ad3a6e30\"> for wine, chocolate, and exotic coffees</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. Tea was introduced into England in 1660 by King Charles II and his Portuguese queen, who were both confirmed tea drinkers. Tea mania swept across England as it had earlier spread throughout France and Holland. By 1708, tea importation had risen to thirteen times the 1699 level. Tea was drunk by all levels of society.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"H\" data-question-number=\"8\"><b><span>H.</span></b><span> The Russian interest in tea began as early as 1618, when the Chinese embassy in Moscow presented several chests of tea to the Emperor, Czar Alexis. Later in the century, a trade treaty between Russia and China allowed caravans to cross back and forth freely between the two countries. Still, the journey <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"28c2d748-87b8-4631-88be-21c398fc32d5\">was not easy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. The average caravan <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"00105b43-04c1-4286-a610-5d3b0d89726c\">consisted of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"7cc8d338-0ba9-4258-a400-608e05ce892e\">200 to 300 camels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, and the 18,000-kilometre trip took over 16 months to complete. Eventually, however, tea became – as it still is – one of the most popular drinks in the country.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has eight paragraphs, A-H. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i-xi, in boxes 1-8 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. Not enough tea to meet demand</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. Religious objections</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"6c0756c0-3106-4b2a-bb72-437ee17bce3e\">In<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> – and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"59184d2c-667e-4140-a5b0-720e531a4b67\">sometimes out of – </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"59184d2c-667e-4140-a5b0-720e531a4b67 6c0756c0-3106-4b2a-bb72-437ee17bce3e\">fashion</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"e68905f7-3687-427d-b6fb-79a63d06f3c7\">connection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> between tea and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"668a12c6-8c5a-4d8e-94d7-123333cca1f9\">religion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"29425631-3ddf-4c6d-9d1f-f59f16c7e978\">A luxury item<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9e022aba-d1b1-4b5f-8ac1-88246091ee43\">News of tea reaches another continent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"3fa1ea2d-5d14-477c-9165-915c28809b66\">Is tea a good or bad thing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"68ddb6d6-a0a7-4d0f-b09e-18d648a0fbb7\">A chance discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. The benefits for health</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"x\"><span>x. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"32486cdd-8590-4cc7-9870-8bf16b5f274b\">Tea-making as a ritual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"xi\"><span>xi. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"28c2d748-87b8-4631-88be-21c398fc32d5\">Difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in importing tea from a particular country</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309884\" id=\"question-wrapper-309884\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309885\" id=\"question-wrapper-309885\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309886\" id=\"question-wrapper-309886\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">x</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309887\" id=\"question-wrapper-309887\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309888\" id=\"question-wrapper-309888\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309889\" id=\"question-wrapper-309889\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309890\" id=\"question-wrapper-309890\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph G</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309891\" id=\"question-wrapper-309891\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph H</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">xi</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 9-13) and the list of countries below. Match each statement with the correct country, A-G. Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Countries</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. China</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Japan</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Portugal</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Holland</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. France</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. England</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. Russia</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309892\" id=\"question-wrapper-309892\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c48e58d2-2867-4fe7-8cd0-6a19c36bcbad\">Claims that tea might be harmful failed to affect its popularity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309893\" id=\"question-wrapper-309893\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Tea <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"1c3847ef-6ba9-4cb3-beb6-4083ad3a6e30\">lost favour to other drinks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309894\" id=\"question-wrapper-309894\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"706b282a-b96a-4f09-88d7-add16efe1e9f\">Special buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"1b11f731-96d9-44a4-8d6f-a00284c1d22d\">were constructed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in which to drink tea.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309895\" id=\"question-wrapper-309895\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"7cc8d338-0ba9-4258-a400-608e05ce892e\">Animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"00105b43-04c1-4286-a610-5d3b0d89726c\">involved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in importing tea.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309896\" id=\"question-wrapper-309896\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"88742ae0-6495-4849-8b2c-239ad30b27a4\">A ruler's<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"d18fe434-cde0-41ed-9a8a-cf1877f724de\">specialist knowledge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> led to an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"31055acd-1f66-427f-b272-e69a30962b6c\">interest in tea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"68ddb6d6-a0a7-4d0f-b09e-18d648a0fbb7 88742ae0-6495-4849-8b2c-239ad30b27a4","qNum":"1 13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Emperor Shen Nung"},{"uid":"d18fe434-cde0-41ed-9a8a-cf1877f724de","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"specialist knowledge","passagePhrase":"was a skilled"},{"uid":"88742ae0-6495-4849-8b2c-239ad30b27a4","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"A ruler's","passagePhrase":"ruler"},{"uid":"31055acd-1f66-427f-b272-e69a30962b6c 68ddb6d6-a0a7-4d0f-b09e-18d648a0fbb7","qNum":"1 13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"intrigued by the new liquid"},{"uid":"e68905f7-3687-427d-b6fb-79a63d06f3c7","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"connection","passagePhrase":"linked"},{"uid":"668a12c6-8c5a-4d8e-94d7-123333cca1f9","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"religion","passagePhrase":"Zen Buddhism ... support ... from ... monasteries"},{"uid":"32486cdd-8590-4cc7-9870-8bf16b5f274b","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Tea-making as a ritual","passagePhrase":"Japanese tea ceremony ... most perfect, most polite, most graceful, most charming manner possible"},{"uid":"1b11f731-96d9-44a4-8d6f-a00284c1d22d","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"were constructed","passagePhrase":"creation of"},{"uid":"706b282a-b96a-4f09-88d7-add16efe1e9f","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Special buildings","passagePhrase":"a particular form of architecture for 'tea house"},{"uid":"9e022aba-d1b1-4b5f-8ac1-88246091ee43","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"News of tea reaches another continent","passagePhrase":"information ... began to filter back to Europe"},{"uid":"29425631-3ddf-4c6d-9d1f-f59f16c7e978","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"A luxury item","passagePhrase":"very expensive ... domain of the wealthy"},{"uid":"3fa1ea2d-5d14-477c-9165-915c28809b66","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Is tea a good or bad thing","passagePhrase":"argued as to its benefits or drawbacks"},{"uid":"c48e58d2-2867-4fe7-8cd0-6a19c36bcbad","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Claims that tea might be harmful failed to affect its popularity","passagePhrase":"public largely ignored the ... and continued to enjoy"},{"uid":"3fa1ea2d-5d14-477c-9165-915c28809b66 c48e58d2-2867-4fe7-8cd0-6a19c36bcbad","qNum":"6 9","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"scholarly debate"},{"uid":"6c0756c0-3106-4b2a-bb72-437ee17bce3e","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"In","passagePhrase":"craze for all things oriental ... remained popular"},{"uid":"1c3847ef-6ba9-4cb3-beb6-4083ad3a6e30 59184d2c-667e-4140-a5b0-720e531a4b67","qNum":"7 10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"being replaced by a preference"},{"uid":"1c3847ef-6ba9-4cb3-beb6-4083ad3a6e30","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"lost favour to other drinks","passagePhrase":"for wine, chocolate, and exotic coffees"},{"uid":"28c2d748-87b8-4631-88be-21c398fc32d5","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Difficulties","passagePhrase":"was not easy"},{"uid":"00105b43-04c1-4286-a610-5d3b0d89726c","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"involved","passagePhrase":"consisted of"},{"uid":"7cc8d338-0ba9-4258-a400-608e05ce892e","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Animals","passagePhrase":"200 to 300 camels"},{"uid":"59184d2c-667e-4140-a5b0-720e531a4b67","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"sometimes out of –","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"59184d2c-667e-4140-a5b0-720e531a4b67 6c0756c0-3106-4b2a-bb72-437ee17bce3e","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"fashion","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"68ddb6d6-a0a7-4d0f-b09e-18d648a0fbb7","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"A chance discovery","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"31055acd-1f66-427f-b272-e69a30962b6c","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"interest in tea","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_5":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>Bird Migration</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>A. </span></b><span>Birds possess a remarkable set of design features that enables them to perform such astonishing feats of endurance. They are equipped with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c77e82d0-9a55-473f-938d-ebee4d211bac\">lightweight, hollow bones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c77e82d0-9a55-473f-938d-ebee4d211bac\">intricately structured feathers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> that provide both lift and thrust during sustained flight. Their navigation systems are superior to any device humans have developed. An ingenious heat-conserving design concentrates blood circulation beneath layers of warm, waterproof plumage, leaving them able to face the harshest of climates. Their respiratory systems must function efficiently during long flights at altitude, so their system of extracting oxygen far exceeds that of any other animal. During the later stages of the breeding season, when food is plentiful, their bodies accumulate considerable layers of fat to provide sufficient energy for long migratory flights.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"90474a89-bd97-4d47-98d8-fb623a970b00\">fundamental reason<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> that birds migrate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"90474a89-bd97-4d47-98d8-fb623a970b00\">is to find adequate food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> during the winter months, when supplies become scarce. This particularly applies to species that breed in the temperate and Arctic regions of the Northern Hemisphere, where food is abundant only during the short growing season. Many species can tolerate cold temperatures while food remains plentiful, but they are forced to leave once it disappears. However, several intriguing questions still surround these journeys. </span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> One puzzling fact is that many birds <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 21\" data-uid=\"14c89214-2d7c-4775-9436-7cbc4c2269ea e0903046-7625-4ae2-a2be-7b843368fdad\">travel much further than would be necessary</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> simply to find food and favourable weather. It remains unclear, for instance, why British swallows, which could presumably survive equally well if they spent the winter in equatorial Africa, instead fly several thousand miles further to their preferred winter home in South Africa's Cape Province. Another mystery involves the huge migration performed by arctic terns and certain shorebirds that breed close to the Polar Regions. In general, the further north a migrant species breeds, the further south it spends the winter. For arctic terns, this necessitates an annual round trip of 25,000 miles. Yet, en route to their far-flung southern destinations, these individuals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e0903046-7625-4ae2-a2be-7b843368fdad\">overfly vast areas of seemingly suitable habitat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> spanning two hemispheres. Although we may not fully understand these choices, we can marvel at their feats.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> One of the greatest mysteries is how young birds know how to find the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"33583d4d-21f5-4d0f-8907-6d193151c5c1\">traditional wintering areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 23\" data-uid=\"185b891b-1e17-4ef9-8492-0126b6eb47cb e3697144-fc73-4d3f-a2c0-fa675cfacf8b\">without parental guidance</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Very few adults migrate with juveniles in tow, and young birds may have no knowledge of their parents' appearance. A familiar example is the cuckoo, which lays its eggs in another species' nest and never encounters its young again. It is mind-boggling to consider that, once raised by its host species, the young cuckoo makes its own way to ancestral wintering grounds in the tropics before returning alone to northern Europe the next season to seek a mate among its own kind. The obvious implication is that it inherits from its parents an inbuilt route map and direction-finding capability, as well as a mental image of what another cuckoo looks like. Yet exactly how this is possible remains entirely unknown.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"cceac893-eb65-4c86-9ee2-d2024528c0f9\">Mounting evidence has confirmed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that birds <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"94996c01-0180-415c-868b-54c454b8723e\">use the positions of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the sun and stars to obtain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b036486c-cbbc-48ad-8ad4-a9b1abcdcb9e\">compass directions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> during their journeys. They also seem able to detect the Earth's magnetic field, probably because of minute crystals of magnetite in the region of their brains. Some species also perceive the plane of polarized light from the setting sun, which calibrates their direction-finding. However, true navigation also requires an awareness of position and time, especially when an individual is lost. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"cceac893-eb65-4c86-9ee2-d2024528c0f9\">Experiments have shown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that after being taken thousands of miles over an unfamiliar landmass, birds remain capable of returning rapidly to their nest sites. Such phenomenal powers are the product of combining a number of sophisticated cues, including an inborn map of the night sky and the pull of the Earth's magnetic field. How birds actually use these instruments remains unknown, but their sensory perception of the world clearly exceeds our own.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><b><span>F. </span></b><span>Nevertheless, every journey involves considerable risk, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"edabaa28-26d4-469d-9432-551e10423402\">part of the skill<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of arriving safely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"edabaa28-26d4-469d-9432-551e10423402\">lies in setting off at the right moment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Most small birds choose to migrate at night, which brings several benefits. First, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"906c3173-7a16-43d2-ba52-5deb458414e8\">daytime predators are entirely avoided<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. In addition, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"4bc5062d-e4db-4431-bb24-d014d7424d28\">danger of dehydration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"49598f93-4a10-4346-ba2f-860f860851f9\">during long flights<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> through warm, sunlit skies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"4bc5062d-e4db-4431-bb24-d014d7424d28\">is greatly reduced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. Furthermore, the night air is generally cooler and less turbulent, making it conducive to sustained, stable flight. Choosing the right moment also means forecasting the weather accurately and utilizing favourable winds. Birds are adept at both, and in laboratory tests some species have been shown to detect the minute difference in barometric pressure between the floor and ceiling of a room. Often, birds react to weather changes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"92680b84-4cd4-4b19-afba-2a58e721a6d3\">before there is any visible sign<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> of them. Lapwings, which feed on grassland, flee west from the Netherlands to the British Isles, France and Spain at the onset of a cold snap. When the ground surface freezes, the birds would otherwise starve. Yet they return to Holland ahead of a thaw, their arrival linked to a pressure change signalling an improvement.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"20\"><b><span>G.</span></b><span> In one instance, a Welsh Manx shearwater carried to America and released was back in its burrow on Skokholm Island, off the Pembrokeshire coast, one day before a letter announcing its release! Conversely, each autumn a small number of North American birds are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"0e1ecbe8-a954-47d5-b883-8d491fa17552\">blown across the Atlantic by fast-moving westerly tail winds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Not only do they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"ed7f1eae-f48e-4b39-a0c5-43c770a98738\">arrive safely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in Europe, but, based on ringing evidence, some make it back to North America the following spring, after probably spending the winter with European migrants in sunny African climates.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i-x, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"edabaa28-26d4-469d-9432-551e10423402\">The best moment to migrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. The unexplained <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e0903046-7625-4ae2-a2be-7b843368fdad\">rejection of closer feeding ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. The influence of weather on the migration route</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c77e82d0-9a55-473f-938d-ebee4d211bac\">Physical characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> that allow birds to migrate</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"90474a89-bd97-4d47-98d8-fb623a970b00\">The main reason why birds migrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. The best wintering grounds for birds</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"cceac893-eb65-4c86-9ee2-d2024528c0f9\">Research findings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> on how birds migrate</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"ed7f1eae-f48e-4b39-a0c5-43c770a98738\">Successful migration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"0e1ecbe8-a954-47d5-b883-8d491fa17552\">despite trouble of wind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. Contrast between long-distance migration and short-distance migration</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"x\"><span>x. Mysterious migration despite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"e3697144-fc73-4d3f-a2c0-fa675cfacf8b\">lack of teaching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309897\" id=\"question-wrapper-309897\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309898\" id=\"question-wrapper-309898\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309899\" id=\"question-wrapper-309899\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309900\" id=\"question-wrapper-309900\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">x</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309901\" id=\"question-wrapper-309901\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309902\" id=\"question-wrapper-309902\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309903\" id=\"question-wrapper-309903\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph G</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose TWO letters, A-E. Write the correct letters in boxes 21 and 22 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>Which TWO of the following statements are true of bird migration?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Birds often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"14c89214-2d7c-4775-9436-7cbc4c2269ea\">fly further than they need to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Birds travelling in family groups are safe.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"49598f93-4a10-4346-ba2f-860f860851f9\">Birds flying at night<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"4bc5062d-e4db-4431-bb24-d014d7424d28\">need less water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Birds have visual abilities similar to those of mammals such as humans.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Only shorebirds are resistant to strong winds.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309904\" id=\"question-wrapper-309904\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309905\" id=\"question-wrapper-309905\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Write your answers in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309906\" id=\"question-wrapper-309906\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It is a great mystery that young birds like cuckoos can find their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"33583d4d-21f5-4d0f-8907-6d193151c5c1\">wintering grounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> without ______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(parental) guidance</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309907\" id=\"question-wrapper-309907\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Evidence shows birds can tell <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b036486c-cbbc-48ad-8ad4-a9b1abcdcb9e\">directions like a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> ______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"94996c01-0180-415c-868b-54c454b8723e\">by observing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the sun and the stars.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">compass</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309908\" id=\"question-wrapper-309908\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>One advantage for birds flying at night is that they can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"906c3173-7a16-43d2-ba52-5deb458414e8\">avoid contact with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> ______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(daytime) predators</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309909\" id=\"question-wrapper-309909\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Laboratory tests show that birds can detect weather <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"92680b84-4cd4-4b19-afba-2a58e721a6d3\">without<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> ______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"92680b84-4cd4-4b19-afba-2a58e721a6d3\">signs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">visible</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c77e82d0-9a55-473f-938d-ebee4d211bac","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Physical characteristics","passagePhrase":"lightweight, hollow bones ... intricately structured feathers"},{"uid":"90474a89-bd97-4d47-98d8-fb623a970b00","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"The main reason why birds migrate","passagePhrase":"fundamental reason ... is to find adequate food"},{"uid":"14c89214-2d7c-4775-9436-7cbc4c2269ea e0903046-7625-4ae2-a2be-7b843368fdad","qNum":"16 21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"travel much further than would be necessary"},{"uid":"e0903046-7625-4ae2-a2be-7b843368fdad","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"rejection of closer feeding ground","passagePhrase":"overfly vast areas of seemingly suitable habitat"},{"uid":"33583d4d-21f5-4d0f-8907-6d193151c5c1","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"wintering grounds","passagePhrase":"traditional wintering areas"},{"uid":"185b891b-1e17-4ef9-8492-0126b6eb47cb e3697144-fc73-4d3f-a2c0-fa675cfacf8b","qNum":"17 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"without parental guidance"},{"uid":"cceac893-eb65-4c86-9ee2-d2024528c0f9","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Research findings","passagePhrase":"Mounting evidence has confirmed ... Experiments have shown"},{"uid":"94996c01-0180-415c-868b-54c454b8723e","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"by observing","passagePhrase":"use the positions of"},{"uid":"b036486c-cbbc-48ad-8ad4-a9b1abcdcb9e","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"directions like a","passagePhrase":"compass directions"},{"uid":"edabaa28-26d4-469d-9432-551e10423402","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"The best moment to migrate","passagePhrase":"part of the skill ... lies in setting off at the right moment"},{"uid":"906c3173-7a16-43d2-ba52-5deb458414e8","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"avoid contact with","passagePhrase":"daytime predators are entirely avoided"},{"uid":"4bc5062d-e4db-4431-bb24-d014d7424d28","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"need less water","passagePhrase":"danger of dehydration ... is greatly reduced"},{"uid":"49598f93-4a10-4346-ba2f-860f860851f9","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Birds flying at night","passagePhrase":"during long flights"},{"uid":"92680b84-4cd4-4b19-afba-2a58e721a6d3","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"without ... signs","passagePhrase":"before there is any visible sign"},{"uid":"0e1ecbe8-a954-47d5-b883-8d491fa17552","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"despite trouble of wind","passagePhrase":"blown across the Atlantic by fast-moving westerly tail winds"},{"uid":"ed7f1eae-f48e-4b39-a0c5-43c770a98738","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Successful migration","passagePhrase":"arrive safely"},{"uid":"e3697144-fc73-4d3f-a2c0-fa675cfacf8b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"lack of teaching","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"14c89214-2d7c-4775-9436-7cbc4c2269ea","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"fly further than they need to","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_6":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education</span></b></p><p><span>One consequence of population mobility is an increasing diversity within schools. To illustrate, in the city of Toronto in Canada, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"7495995b-8162-4656-bc11-753f3469359d\">58% of kindergarten pupils come from homes where English is not their native language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Schools in Europe and North America have experienced this diversity for years, and educational policies and practices vary widely between countries and even within countries. Some political parties and groups search for ways to solve the problem of diverse communities and their integration in schools and society. However, they see few positive consequences for the host society and worry that this diversity threatens the identity of the host society. Consequently, they promote unfortunate educational policies that will make the 'problem' disappear. If students retain their culture and language, they are viewed as less capable of identifying with the mainstream culture and learning the mainstream language of the society.</span></p><p><span>The challenge for educators and policy-makers is to shape the evolution of national identity in such a way that the rights of all citizens (including school children) are respected, and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"4c4fae01-592b-434e-96f6-dfa82c9d6827\">cultural, linguistic, and economic resources of the nation are maximised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. To waste the resources of the nation by discouraging children from developing their mother tongues is quite simply unintelligent from the point of view of national self-interest. A first step in providing an appropriate education for culturally and linguistically diverse children is to examine what the existing research says about the role of children's mother tongues in their educational development.</span></p><p><span>In fact, the research is very clear. When children continue to develop their abilities in two or more languages throughout their primary school, they gain a deeper understanding of language and how to use it effectively. They have more practice in processing language, especially when they develop literacy in both. More than 150 research studies conducted during the past 25 years <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"086af791-3c75-4722-8433-ba705eb0e636\">strongly support what Goethe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, the famous eighteenth-century German philosopher, once <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"086af791-3c75-4722-8433-ba705eb0e636\">said<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>: the person who knows only one language does not truly know that language. Research suggests that bilingual children may also develop more flexibility in their thinking as a result of processing information through two different languages.</span></p><p><span>The level of development of children's mother tongue is a strong predictor of their second language development. Children who come to school with a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"5ca6b767-4a51-4024-a661-e4aa3013aea0\">solid foundation in their mother tongue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> develop stronger literacy abilities in the school language. When parents and other caregivers (e.g. grandparents) are able to spend time with their children and tell stories or discuss issues with them in a way that develops their mother tongue, children come to school well-prepared to learn the school language and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"62d67bf2-cb4d-4db8-bcb0-cea32e1eff7d\">succeed educationally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Children's knowledge and skills transfer across languages from the mother tongue to the school language. Transfer across languages can be two-way: both languages nurture each other when the educational environment permits children access to both languages.</span></p><p><span>Some educators and parents are suspicious of mother tongue-based teaching programs because they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"3331db0b-9492-4780-a210-5dc742333076\">worry that they take time away from the majority language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. For example, in a bilingual program, when 50% of the time is spent teaching through children's home language and 50% through the majority language, surely children won't progress as far in the latter? One of the most strongly established findings of educational research, however, is that well-implemented bilingual programs can promote literacy and subject-matter knowledge in a minority language without any negative effects on children's development in the majority language. Within Europe, the Foyer program in Belgium, which develops children's speaking and literacy abilities in three languages (their mother tongue, Dutch and French), most clearly illustrates the benefits of bilingual and trilingual education (see Cummins, 2000).</span></p><p><span>It is easy to understand how this happens. When children are learning through a minority language, they are learning concepts and intellectual skills too. Pupils who know how to tell the time in their mother tongue understand the concept of telling time. In order to tell time in the majority language, they do not need to re-learn the concept. Similarly, at more advanced stages, there is transfer across languages in other skills such as knowing how to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b16179a3-df16-4bfb-a922-1a4a2979c51a\">distinguish the main idea from the supporting details<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> of a written passage or story, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b16179a3-df16-4bfb-a922-1a4a2979c51a\">distinguishing fact from opinion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Studies of secondary school pupils are providing interesting findings in this area, and it would be worth extending this research.</span></p><p><span>Many people marvel at how quickly bilingual children seem to '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"41437bdf-35df-49d5-8424-678dd37943a8\">pick up' conversational skills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in the majority language at school (although it takes much longer for them to catch up with native speakers in academic language skills). However, educators are often much less aware of how quickly children can lose their ability to use their mother tongue, even in the home context. The extent and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"5f929135-362d-400c-a98f-001cb9e2af78\">rapidity of language loss<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> will vary according to the concentration of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"8ce31c29-3691-44cb-ade5-72c9317d5e6b\">families from a particular linguistic group in the neighborhood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. Where the mother tongue is used extensively in the community, then language loss among young children will be less. However, where language communities are not concentrated in particular neighborhoods, children can lose their ability to communicate in their mother tongue within 2–3 years of starting school. They may retain receptive skills in the language but they will use the majority language in speaking with their peers and siblings and in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"34871446-f505-4b2a-b67d-ee14df9be8c5\">responding to their parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. By the time children become adolescents, the linguistic division between parents and children has become an emotional chasm. Pupils frequently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"e4612297-f39a-4be0-9da7-6326c657b47c\">become alienated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> from the cultures of both home and school with predictable results.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27–30 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309910\" id=\"question-wrapper-309910\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What point did the writer make in the second paragraph?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Some present studies on children's mother tongues are misleading.</li> <li>B. A culturally rich education programme benefits some children more than others.</li> <li>C. Bilingual children can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"4c4fae01-592b-434e-96f6-dfa82c9d6827\">make a valuable contribution to the wealth of a country<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>D. The law on mother tongue use at school should be strengthened.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309911\" id=\"question-wrapper-309911\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why does the writer refer to something that Goethe said?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"086af791-3c75-4722-8433-ba705eb0e636\">lend weight to his argument<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></li> <li>B. to contradict some research</li> <li>C. to introduce a new concept</li> <li>D. to update current thinking</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309912\" id=\"question-wrapper-309912\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer believes that when young children have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"5ca6b767-4a51-4024-a661-e4aa3013aea0\">firm grasp of their mother tongue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They can teach older family members what they learnt at school.</li> <li>B. They go on to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"62d67bf2-cb4d-4db8-bcb0-cea32e1eff7d\">do much better throughout their time at school<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>C. They can read stories about their cultural background.</li> <li>D. They develop stronger relationships with their family than with their peers.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309913\" id=\"question-wrapper-309913\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why are some people suspicious about mother-tongue-based teaching programmes?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They worry that children will be slow to learn to read in either language.</li> <li>B. They think that children will confuse words in the two languages.</li> <li>C. They believe that the programmes will make children less interested in their lessons.</li> <li>D. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"3331db0b-9492-4780-a210-5dc742333076\">fear that the programmes will use up valuable time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> in the school day.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, A–J, below. Write the correct letter, A–J, in boxes 31–35 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. educators</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. institution</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. alienation</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. pace</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. duration</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. parents</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. interaction</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. category</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. capacity</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"J\"><span>J. neighbourhood</span></p><p><b><span>Bilingual Children</span></b></p><p><span>It was often recorded that bilingual children <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"41437bdf-35df-49d5-8424-678dd37943a8\">acquire the (31)______ to converse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in the majority language remarkably quickly. The fact that the mother tongue can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"5f929135-362d-400c-a98f-001cb9e2af78\">disappear at a similar (32<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>)______ is less well understood. This phenomenon depends, to a certain extent, on the proportion of people with the same linguistic background who have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"8ce31c29-3691-44cb-ade5-72c9317d5e6b\">settled in a particular (33<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>)______. If this is limited, children are likely to lose the active use of their mother tongue, and thus <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"34871446-f505-4b2a-b67d-ee14df9be8c5\">no longer employ it even with (34<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>)______, although they may still understand it. It follows that teenage children in these circumstances <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"e4612297-f39a-4be0-9da7-6326c657b47c\">experience a sense of (35<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>)______ in relation to all aspects of their lives.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309914\" id=\"question-wrapper-309914\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309915\" id=\"question-wrapper-309915\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309916\" id=\"question-wrapper-309916\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">J</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309917\" id=\"question-wrapper-309917\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309918\" id=\"question-wrapper-309918\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36–40 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309919\" id=\"question-wrapper-309919\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Less than half of the children who attend kindergarten in Toronto have English as their mother tongue.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309920\" id=\"question-wrapper-309920\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Research proves that learning the host country language at school can have an adverse effect on a child's mother tongue.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309921\" id=\"question-wrapper-309921\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Foyer program is to be accepted by the French education system.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309922\" id=\"question-wrapper-309922\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Bilingual children are taught to tell the time earlier than monolingual children.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309923\" id=\"question-wrapper-309923\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Bilingual children can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b16179a3-df16-4bfb-a922-1a4a2979c51a\">apply reading comprehension strategies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> acquired in one language when reading in the other.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7495995b-8162-4656-bc11-753f3469359d","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"58% of kindergarten pupils come from homes where English is not their native language"},{"uid":"4c4fae01-592b-434e-96f6-dfa82c9d6827","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"make a valuable contribution to the wealth of a country","passagePhrase":"cultural, linguistic, and economic resources of the nation are maximised"},{"uid":"086af791-3c75-4722-8433-ba705eb0e636","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"lend weight to his argument","passagePhrase":"strongly support what Goethe ... said"},{"uid":"5ca6b767-4a51-4024-a661-e4aa3013aea0","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"firm grasp of their mother tongue","passagePhrase":"solid foundation in their mother tongue"},{"uid":"62d67bf2-cb4d-4db8-bcb0-cea32e1eff7d","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"do much better throughout their time at school","passagePhrase":"succeed educationally"},{"uid":"3331db0b-9492-4780-a210-5dc742333076","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"fear that the programmes will use up valuable time","passagePhrase":"worry that they take time away from the majority language"},{"uid":"b16179a3-df16-4bfb-a922-1a4a2979c51a","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"apply reading comprehension strategies","passagePhrase":"distinguish the main idea from the supporting details ... distinguishing fact from opinion"},{"uid":"41437bdf-35df-49d5-8424-678dd37943a8","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"acquire the (31)______ to converse","passagePhrase":"pick up' conversational skills"},{"uid":"5f929135-362d-400c-a98f-001cb9e2af78","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"disappear at a similar (32","passagePhrase":"rapidity of language loss"},{"uid":"8ce31c29-3691-44cb-ade5-72c9317d5e6b","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"settled in a particular (33","passagePhrase":"families from a particular linguistic group in the neighborhood"},{"uid":"34871446-f505-4b2a-b67d-ee14df9be8c5","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"no longer employ it even with (34","passagePhrase":"responding to their parents"},{"uid":"e4612297-f39a-4be0-9da7-6326c657b47c","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"experience a sense of (35","passagePhrase":"become alienated"}]},"reading_u2_7":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>The pesticide-free village</span></b></p><p><i><span>Gerry Marten and Dona Glen Williams report on the Indian village of Punukula, so nearly destroyed by reliance on pesticides</span></i></p><p><span>Around 20 years ago, a handful of families migrated from the Guntur district of Andhra Pradesh, south-east India, into Punukula, a community of around 900 people farming plots of between two and ten acres. The outsiders from Guntur brought <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"dd562584-f939-4430-bd23-6b4d6b651e09\">cotton culture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> with them, and this attracted resident farmers by promising to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d1e6419d-e429-4e12-a677-d3142576ea0c\">bring in more hard cash<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> than the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4ede1652-ee94-4a0e-9979-04d2b7380582\">mixed crops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> they were already growing to eat and sell, such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4ede1652-ee94-4a0e-9979-04d2b7380582\">millet, mung beans, chilli and rice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. But growing cotton meant using pesticides – and fertilisers – until then a mystery to the mostly illiterate farmers of the community.</span></p><p><span>Local agrochemical dealers obligingly filled the need for information and supplies. These ‘middlemen’ sold commercial seeds, fertilisers and insecticides on credit, and guaranteed purchase of the crop. They offered technical advice provided by the companies that supplied their products. The farmers depended on the dealers. If they wanted to grow cotton – and they did – it seemed they had no choice. A quick ‘high’ of booming yields and incomes hooked growers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"679f46a0-ae6e-4689-a42e-28408e99e30f\">during the early years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of cotton in the region. Outlay on insecticides was fairly low because cotton pests hadn’t moved in yet. Many farmers were so impressed with the chemicals that they started using them on their other crops as well. The immediate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b7a0d417-ab06-42ca-95f8-d384e5181073\">payoffs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> from chemically-dependent cotton agriculture both ensured and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"a744375a-f171-4600-91a5-8957e8f00fac\">obscured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the fact that the black dirt fields had gone into a freefall of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b7a0d417-ab06-42ca-95f8-d384e5181073\">environmental degradation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, dragged down by a chain of cause and effect.</span></p><p><span>Soon cotton-eaters, such as bollworms and aphids, plagued the fields. Repeated spraying killed off the most susceptible pests and left the strongest to reproduce and pass on their resistance to generations of ever-harder offspring. As the bugs grew tougher and more abundant, farmers applied ever-increasing intensity and quantity of poisons, sometimes mixing cocktails of as many as ten insecticides. At the same time, cotton was gobbling up the nutrients in the soil, leaving the growers no option but to invest in chemical fertilisers. By the time some farmers tried to break free of their chemical dependence, insecticides had already decimated the birds, wasps, beetles, and other predators that had once provided natural control of crop pests. Without their balancing presence, pests ran riot if insecticide was cut back. As outlays for fertilisers and insecticides escalated, the cost of producing cotton mounted. Eventually, the expense of chemical inputs outgrew the cash value of the crop, and farmers fell further and further into debt and poverty.</span></p><p><span>Their vicious cycle was only broken by the willingness of a prominent village elder to experiment with something different. He had been among the first villagers to grow cotton, and he would be the first to try it without chemicals, as set out by a programme in Non-Pesticide Management (NPM). This had been devised for Punukula with the help of a Non-Government Organisation called SECURE that had become aware of the hardships caused by the pesticide trap. It involved <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d4b25cf1-1af9-43c2-a44b-cbc047587689\">turning to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> neem, a fast-growing, broad-leaved evergreen tree related to mahogany. Neem protects itself against insects by producing a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"aa5f0646-d34f-4a8d-9463-19f53ded634f\">multitude<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of natural pesticides that have evolved specifically to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"74de110a-7bc9-4c95-87e5-b206b0d3571b\">defeat plant-eating insects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. Thus, they are generally harmless to humans and other animals, including birds and insects that eat pests.</span></p><p><span>The plant is native to India and Burma, where it has been used for centuries to control pests and to promote health. To protect cotton, neem seeds are simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d7a3ca57-33f1-4afd-a549-9ff4daedfd8b\">ground into a powder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"4d1c0332-cc9d-4d7c-8f98-d527db14e38a\">soaked overnight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in water, and sprayed onto the crop at least every 10 days. Neem cake <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"3255af36-89e5-4fd8-a5b1-2d37ba91eb69\">applied to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> the soil kills insect pests and doubles as an organic fertilizer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"dfb8b4c0-8daa-4c20-8508-034807ecb6c6\">high in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> nitrogen. As neem grows locally and is easy to process, it is much less expensive than the chemical insecticides sold for profit by the dealers and their corporate suppliers. Quick, short-term gains had once pushed Punukula into chemical-dependent agriculture. Now they found that similar immediate rewards were helping to speed change in the other direction: the harvest of the next 20 NPM farmers was as good as the harvest of farmers using insecticides, and they came out ahead because they weren’t buying insecticides. Instead of investing cash (in short supply) in chemicals, they invested time and labour in NPM practices.</span></p><p><span>By 2000, all the farmers in Punukula village were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"2d7adaf0-8c91-4832-844c-1f819e10df29\">using NPM rather than chemicals for cotton<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, and they began to use it on other crops as well. The change <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a34b5849-31d8-4eaf-b89a-d32766b12cb1\">gathered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> momentum as NPM became even more effective once everyone was using it. The status and economic opportunities of women improved – neem became a source of income for some of them, as they gathered seeds from the surrounding area to sell for NPM in other villages. The improved situation meant that families could afford to put more land under cultivation. In 2004, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a12ba6dd-abf2-410d-aa36-74d69400b0f2\">the panchayat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (village government) formally declared Punukula to be a pesticide-free village. And they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"bee47554-f3ac-435f-8aa7-56881d3cc1db\">have big plans for the future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, such as water purification. The village now serves as a model for disseminating NPM to other communities, with around 2000 farmers visiting each year. What began as a few farmers desperate to find a way to farm without poisons has become a movement with the potential to pull an entire region back from ecological disaster.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1 – 4 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309924\" id=\"question-wrapper-309924\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"dd562584-f939-4430-bd23-6b4d6b651e09\">Cotton growing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> was expected to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d1e6419d-e429-4e12-a677-d3142576ea0c\">raise more money<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4ede1652-ee94-4a0e-9979-04d2b7380582\">other crops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309925\" id=\"question-wrapper-309925\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some of the local agrochemical dealers had been farmers in the past.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309926\" id=\"question-wrapper-309926\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"679f46a0-ae6e-4689-a42e-28408e99e30f\">Initially<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, the farmers’ cotton yields were low.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309927\" id=\"question-wrapper-309927\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>At first, the farmers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"a744375a-f171-4600-91a5-8957e8f00fac\">failed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to notice the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b7a0d417-ab06-42ca-95f8-d384e5181073\">negative effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> on their fields of pesticide use.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 5 – 10 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Non-Pesticide-Management Programme</span></b></p><p><span>• Developed with the aid of SECURE</span></p><p><span>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d4b25cf1-1af9-43c2-a44b-cbc047587689\">Based on use of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> an (5)______ called neem</span></p><p><span>• Neem contains <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"aa5f0646-d34f-4a8d-9463-19f53ded634f\">many<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (6)______ that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"74de110a-7bc9-4c95-87e5-b206b0d3571b\">target plant-eating predators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></span></p><p><b><span>Neem</span></b></p><p><b><span>• Used as a pesticide</span></b></p><p><span>○ (7)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d7a3ca57-33f1-4afd-a549-9ff4daedfd8b\">formed by grinding seeds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></span></p><p><span>○ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"4d1c0332-cc9d-4d7c-8f98-d527db14e38a\">left (8)______ to soak in water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></span></p><p><span>○ Sprayed regularly</span></p><p><b><span>• Used as a pesticide and as a fertiliser</span></b></p><p><span>○ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"3255af36-89e5-4fd8-a5b1-2d37ba91eb69\">added in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)______ form to soil</span></p><p><span>○ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"dfb8b4c0-8daa-4c20-8508-034807ecb6c6\">contains a lot of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)______</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309928\" id=\"question-wrapper-309928\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">evergreen tree</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309929\" id=\"question-wrapper-309929\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">natural pesticides</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309930\" id=\"question-wrapper-309930\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(a) powder</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309931\" id=\"question-wrapper-309931\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">overnight</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309932\" id=\"question-wrapper-309932\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">cake</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309933\" id=\"question-wrapper-309933\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">nitrogen</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 11 – 13 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309934\" id=\"question-wrapper-309934\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In which year did farmers finally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"2d7adaf0-8c91-4832-844c-1f819e10df29\">stop using chemicals on cotton crops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in Punukula?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">2000</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309935\" id=\"question-wrapper-309935\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What did the women of Punukula <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a34b5849-31d8-4eaf-b89a-d32766b12cb1\">collect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> to make money?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">seeds</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309936\" id=\"question-wrapper-309936\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What project do <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a12ba6dd-abf2-410d-aa36-74d69400b0f2\">the authorities in Punukula<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"bee47554-f3ac-435f-8aa7-56881d3cc1db\">hope to set up in the future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Water purification</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"dd562584-f939-4430-bd23-6b4d6b651e09","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Cotton growing","passagePhrase":"cotton culture"},{"uid":"d1e6419d-e429-4e12-a677-d3142576ea0c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"raise more money","passagePhrase":"bring in more hard cash"},{"uid":"4ede1652-ee94-4a0e-9979-04d2b7380582","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"other crops","passagePhrase":"mixed crops ... millet, mung beans, chilli and rice"},{"uid":"679f46a0-ae6e-4689-a42e-28408e99e30f","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Initially","passagePhrase":"during the early years"},{"uid":"b7a0d417-ab06-42ca-95f8-d384e5181073","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"negative effects","passagePhrase":"payoffs ... environmental degradation"},{"uid":"a744375a-f171-4600-91a5-8957e8f00fac","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"failed","passagePhrase":"obscured"},{"uid":"d4b25cf1-1af9-43c2-a44b-cbc047587689","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Based on use of","passagePhrase":"turning to"},{"uid":"aa5f0646-d34f-4a8d-9463-19f53ded634f","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"many","passagePhrase":"multitude"},{"uid":"74de110a-7bc9-4c95-87e5-b206b0d3571b","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"target plant-eating predators","passagePhrase":"defeat plant-eating insects"},{"uid":"d7a3ca57-33f1-4afd-a549-9ff4daedfd8b","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"formed by grinding seeds","passagePhrase":"ground into a powder"},{"uid":"4d1c0332-cc9d-4d7c-8f98-d527db14e38a","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"left (8)______ to soak in water","passagePhrase":"soaked overnight"},{"uid":"3255af36-89e5-4fd8-a5b1-2d37ba91eb69","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"added in","passagePhrase":"applied to"},{"uid":"dfb8b4c0-8daa-4c20-8508-034807ecb6c6","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"contains a lot of","passagePhrase":"high in"},{"uid":"2d7adaf0-8c91-4832-844c-1f819e10df29","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"stop using chemicals on cotton crops","passagePhrase":"using NPM rather than chemicals for cotton"},{"uid":"a34b5849-31d8-4eaf-b89a-d32766b12cb1","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"collect","passagePhrase":"gathered"},{"uid":"a12ba6dd-abf2-410d-aa36-74d69400b0f2","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"the authorities in Punukula","passagePhrase":"the panchayat"},{"uid":"bee47554-f3ac-435f-8aa7-56881d3cc1db","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"hope to set up in the future","passagePhrase":"have big plans for the future"}]},"reading_u2_8":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>Corporate Social Responsibility</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> An excellent definition was developed in the 1980s by Norwegian Prime Minister Gro Harlem Brundtland and used by the World Business Council for Sustainable Development: '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"f8da85de-088a-498e-b2f8-9d3bd9643600\">Meeting the needs of the present without compromising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the ability of future generations to meet their own needs.' Nowadays, governments and companies need to account for the social consequences of their actions. As a result, corporate social responsibility (CSR) has become a priority for business leaders around the world. When a well-run business applies its vast resources and expertise to social problems that it understands and in which it has a stake, it can have a greater impact than any other organisation. The notion of licence to operate derives from the fact that every company needs tacit or explicit permission from governments, communities, and numerous other stakeholders. To secure that permission, companies pursue CSR initiatives which justify their presence, improve a company's image, strengthen its brand, enliven morale and even raise the value of its stock.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> To advance CSR, we must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"00cfbedc-e1af-493c-a080-e4e60b001b21\">root it in a broad understanding of the interrelationship between a corporation and society<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Successful corporations need a healthy society. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"396fdc65-a846-46ca-840c-6336f980410b\">Education, health care, and equal opportunity are essential to a productive workforce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Safe products and working conditions not only attract customers but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"912eb391-9329-4415-9225-0a2cbef654af\">lower the internal costs of accidents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. Efficient utilisation of land, water, energy, and other natural resources makes business more productive. Good government, the rule of law, and property rights are essential for efficiency and innovation. Strong regulatory standards protect both consumers and competitive companies from exploitation. Ultimately, a healthy society creates expanding demand for business, as more human needs are met and aspirations grow. Any business that pursues its ends at the expense of the society in which it operates will find its success to be illusory and ultimately temporary. At the same time, a healthy society needs successful companies. No social programme can rival the business sector when it comes to creating the jobs, wealth, and innovation that improve standards of living and social conditions over time.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> A company's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"28cee2d3-6860-4245-8426-db89fde5801e\">impact on society also changes over time, as social standards evolve and science progresses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Asbestos, now understood as a serious health risk, was thought to be safe in the early 1900s, given the scientific knowledge then available. Knowledge of its risks gradually mounted for more than 50 years before any company was held liable for the harm it can cause. Many firms that failed to anticipate the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"28cee2d3-6860-4245-8426-db89fde5801e\">consequences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of this evolving body of research have been bankrupted by the results. No longer can companies be content to monitor only the obvious social impacts of today. Without a careful process for identifying evolving <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"28cee2d3-6860-4245-8426-db89fde5801e\">social effects of tomorrow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, firms may risk their very survival.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> No business can solve all of society's problems or bear the cost of doing so. Instead, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1e1b9e5e-73ab-434e-8f2c-bb6e9aaa3e5e\">each company must select issues that intersect with its particular business<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Other social agendas are best left to those companies in other industries, NGOs, or government institutions that are better positioned to address them. The essential test that should guide CSR is not whether a cause is worthy but whether it presents an opportunity to create shared value – that is, a meaningful benefit for society that is also valuable to the business. Each company can identify the particular set of societal problems that it is best equipped to help resolve and from which it can gain the greatest competitive benefit.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> The best corporate citizenship initiatives involve far more than writing a cheque: they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"80704fde-6ac7-43d1-bbef-68da64e78496\">specify clear, measurable goals and track results over time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. A good example is General Electric's programme to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"618cc30f-16e3-477a-af97-d52bd9adc022\">adopt underperforming public high schools<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> near several of its major U.S. facilities. The company contributes between $250,000 and $1 million over a five-year period to each school and makes in-kind donations as well. GE managers and employees take an active role by working with school administrators to assess needs and mentor or tutor students. In an independent study of ten schools in the programme between 1989 and 1999, nearly all showed significant improvement, while the graduation rate in four of the five worst-performing schools doubled from an average of 30 to 60%. Effective corporate citizenship initiatives such as this one create goodwill and improve relations with local governments and other important constituencies. What's more, GE's employees feel great pride in their participation. Their effect is inherently limited, however. No matter how beneficial the programme is, it remains incidental to the company's business, and the direct effect on GE's recruiting and retention is modest.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><b><span>F.</span></b><span> Microsoft's Working Connections partnership with the American Association of Community Colleges (AACC) is a good example of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"a1812e8f-1a36-4967-b41d-4646374d29e2\">shared-value opportunity arising from investments in context<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. The shortage of information-technology workers is a significant constraint on Microsoft's growth; currently, there are more than 450,000 unfilled IT positions in the United States alone. Community colleges, which enrol 45% of all U.S. undergraduates, could be a major source of these workers. Microsoft recognises, however, that community colleges face special challenges: IT curricula are not standardised, technology used in classrooms is often outdated, and there are no systematic professional development programmes to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f29f0882-26d4-4d76-bfd9-f51cc75ed6bb\">keep faculty up to date<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Microsoft's $50 million five-year initiative was aimed at all three problems. In addition to contributing money and products, Microsoft sent employee volunteers to colleges to assess needs, contribute expertise, and volunteer as instructors. Microsoft has achieved results that have benefited many communities while having a direct and potentially significant impact on the company.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"20\"><b><span>G.</span></b><span> At the heart of any strategy is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"d7ce99aa-76b8-471d-b20f-3ab8a911847b\">unique value proposition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>: a set of needs a company can meet for its chosen customers that its competitors cannot. The most strategic CSR occurs when a company <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"d7ce99aa-76b8-471d-b20f-3ab8a911847b\">adds a social dimension to its value proposition, making social impact integral<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to the overall strategy. Consider Whole Foods Market, whose value proposition is to sell organic, natural, and healthy food products to customers who are passionate about food and the environment. The company's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e49ace54-f538-4a39-b460-ad0dc8e6cf52\">sourcing emphasises purchases from local farmers through each store's procurement process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. Buyers screen out foods containing any of nearly 100 common ingredients that the company considers unhealthy or environmentally damaging. The same standards apply to products made internally. Whole Foods' commitment to natural and environmentally friendly operating practices extends well beyond sourcing. Stores are constructed using a minimum of virgin raw materials. Recently, the company purchased renewable wind-energy credits equal to 100% of its electricity use in all of its stores and facilities, the only Fortune 500 company to offset its electricity consumption entirely. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"ec2c9c54-6c70-4735-986e-e9ec0040c723\">Spoiled produce and biodegradable waste are trucked to regional centres for composting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Whole Foods' vehicles are being converted to run on biofuels. Even the cleaning products used in its stores are environmentally friendly. And through its philanthropy, the company has created the Animal Compassion Foundation to develop more natural and humane ways of raising farm animals. In short, nearly every aspect of the company's value chain reinforces the social dimensions of its value proposition, distinguishing Whole Foods from its competitors.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A–G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. How CSR may help one business to expand</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. CSR in many aspects of a company’s business</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. A CSR initiative without a financial gain</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. Lack of action by the state on social issues</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. Drivers or pressures motivate companies to address CSR</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. The past illustrates businesses are responsible for future outcomes</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. Companies applying CSR should be selective</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. Reasons that business and society benefit each other</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309937\" id=\"question-wrapper-309937\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309938\" id=\"question-wrapper-309938\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309939\" id=\"question-wrapper-309939\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309940\" id=\"question-wrapper-309940\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309941\" id=\"question-wrapper-309941\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309942\" id=\"question-wrapper-309942\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309943\" id=\"question-wrapper-309943\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph G</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 21–22 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The implementation of CSR – How?</span></b></p><p><span>Promotion of CSR requires the understanding of interdependence between business and society. Corporations’ workers’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"396fdc65-a846-46ca-840c-6336f980410b\">productivity generally needs health care, education, and (21<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>)______. Restrictions imposed by the government and companies both protect consumers from being treated unfairly. Improvement of the safety standard can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"912eb391-9329-4415-9225-0a2cbef654af\">reduce the (22)______ of accidents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in the workplace. Similarly, society becomes a pool of more human needs and aspirations.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309944\" id=\"question-wrapper-309944\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">equal opportunity</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309945\" id=\"question-wrapper-309945\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(internal) costs</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following opinions or deeds (Questions 23–26) and the list of companies below. Match each opinion or deed with the correct company, A, B or C. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 23–26 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Companies</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. General Electric</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Microsoft</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Whole Foods Market</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309946\" id=\"question-wrapper-309946\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"ec2c9c54-6c70-4735-986e-e9ec0040c723\">Sending organic remains for off-site decomposition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309947\" id=\"question-wrapper-309947\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e49ace54-f538-4a39-b460-ad0dc8e6cf52\">way the company purchases its goods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309948\" id=\"question-wrapper-309948\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"618cc30f-16e3-477a-af97-d52bd9adc022\">Helping the underdeveloped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309949\" id=\"question-wrapper-309949\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f29f0882-26d4-4d76-bfd9-f51cc75ed6bb\">Ensuring that people have the latest information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f8da85de-088a-498e-b2f8-9d3bd9643600","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Meeting the needs of the present without compromising"},{"uid":"00cfbedc-e1af-493c-a080-e4e60b001b21","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"root it in a broad understanding of the interrelationship between a corporation and society"},{"uid":"396fdc65-a846-46ca-840c-6336f980410b","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"productivity generally needs health care, education, and (21","passagePhrase":"Education, health care, and equal opportunity are essential to a productive workforce"},{"uid":"912eb391-9329-4415-9225-0a2cbef654af","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"reduce the (22)______ of accidents","passagePhrase":"lower the internal costs of accidents"},{"uid":"28cee2d3-6860-4245-8426-db89fde5801e","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"impact on society also changes over time, as social standards evolve and science progresses ... consequences ... social effects of tomorrow"},{"uid":"1e1b9e5e-73ab-434e-8f2c-bb6e9aaa3e5e","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"each company must select issues that intersect with its particular business"},{"uid":"80704fde-6ac7-43d1-bbef-68da64e78496","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"specify clear, measurable goals and track results over time"},{"uid":"618cc30f-16e3-477a-af97-d52bd9adc022","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"Helping the underdeveloped","passagePhrase":"adopt underperforming public high schools"},{"uid":"a1812e8f-1a36-4967-b41d-4646374d29e2","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"shared-value opportunity arising from investments in context"},{"uid":"f29f0882-26d4-4d76-bfd9-f51cc75ed6bb","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Ensuring that people have the latest information","passagePhrase":"keep faculty up to date"},{"uid":"d7ce99aa-76b8-471d-b20f-3ab8a911847b","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"unique value proposition ... adds a social dimension to its value proposition, making social impact integral"},{"uid":"e49ace54-f538-4a39-b460-ad0dc8e6cf52","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"way the company purchases its goods","passagePhrase":"sourcing emphasises purchases from local farmers through each store's procurement process"},{"uid":"ec2c9c54-6c70-4735-986e-e9ec0040c723","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Sending organic remains for off-site decomposition","passagePhrase":"Spoiled produce and biodegradable waste are trucked to regional centres for composting"}]},"reading_u2_9":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><span>Charles Darwin, the brilliant anthropologist and creator of the theory of evolution, is not normally associated with the modern business world. Nevertheless, Darwinian evolutionary theory is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"78380b82-51b7-406f-994f-9eef986214c2\">foundation of a new wave of ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> about human behaviour in general and particularly the way people behave in the workplace; these ideas have given the title of ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"78380b82-51b7-406f-994f-9eef986214c2\">evolutionary psychology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>’. Evolutionary psychology revolves around the notion that our brains, like our bodies, have an inherited evolutionary design that has scarcely changed for 10,000 years. As respected evolutionary psychology experts Leda Cosmides and John Tooby comment, ‘our modern skulls house a Stone Age mind’. The US biologist Edward O. Wilson sees evolutionary psychology as being a discipline which is based on both sociobiology, which is the study of the biological basis of social behaviour, and psychology, which is the systematic study of human behaviour.</span></p><p><span>Nigel Nicholson, an organisational psychologist from the London Business School, is a strong supporter of evolutionary psychology and on this subject has published Managing the Human Animal. His book takes the reader on a journey from the Stone Age plains of the savannah to the modern office, and includes a discussion of Darwinism and behavioural psychology, together with a dissection of dysfunctional organisational behaviour. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"0ea7f612-269b-4670-a20c-37fc06d0ed3c\">It is an effective approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4e4dd92-f555-4518-abb2-1130bcb3fb5c\">explaining why people behave as they do, particularly at work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Evolutionary psychology is increasingly being cited in management circles, where managers are trying to understand puzzling aspects of human behaviour and, by doing so, improve the workplace. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"0ea7f612-269b-4670-a20c-37fc06d0ed3c\">Nicholson believes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> that evolutionary psychology can help managers understand what goes wrong in organisational life and what they can do about it.</span></p><p><span>Nicholson maintains that evolutionary psychology dismisses the long-held assumption that our minds are like blank pages just waiting for culture and experience to write on them and shape our nature. He points out that sophisticated research shows the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7382b0d8-5623-4c34-9527-fa34fcc15888\">brain actually houses a store of knowledge when we are born<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, and now genetic research is establishing there are certain genes that account for abilities, tastes and tendencies. The stored knowledge in the human brain has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"82705dc7-930c-40d2-9ebc-1a05e4626043\">not<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> changed much since the Stone Age. As Tooby and Cosmides stress, there have not been enough generations for a brain that is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"82705dc7-930c-40d2-9ebc-1a05e4626043\">well-adapted to our post-industrial life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> to evolve through natural selection.</span></p><p><span>The evolutionary psychology version of human nature revolves around some key elements which we have inherited from our hunter-gatherer minds. One key element is emotion. Emotion was originally essential to keep early man alive and safe from predators. Emotion was, and continues to be, our <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"ccc10a6b-87c5-4490-81e7-5406e971b0cf\">radar, guiding us throughout today’s </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29 34\" data-uid=\"8a8a45de-4baf-46c4-8a1a-74ec32c69520 ccc10a6b-87c5-4490-81e7-5406e971b0cf\">techno-defined business world</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Despite this, the business world emphasises rational, not emotional, behaviour, and does not admit the importance of emotion. We still use the emotional part of our minds to make sense of other people’s behaviour and to create an impression, so we can often be taken in by appearances. This mental predisposition actually works best in small communities (the tribe), not in much larger environments filled with people we barely know (the modern workplace). Our minds naturally try to re-create our ancestral communities with networks of no more than 150 people, where there are clear hierarchies and leaders. As a consequence, it takes very little to trigger people’s innate distrust of others because our safety in antiquity depended on supporting our near family and friends, whom we valued more than other people.</span></p><p><span>So what advice does Nicholson have for the corporate world? He thinks that by knowing the reasons for people’s behaviour it is possible to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"7972f2e6-67c0-455b-9da3-439e5eadd1a3\">mould corporate environments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> into places that have more chance of working efficiently and being pleasant places to work in. Nicholson admits that not everybody in the business world agrees with his belief in the effectiveness of evolutionary psychology in the workplace. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"0a5559f2-60b2-4570-8d84-cd05af69bf48\">One group that resists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> the theory of evolutionary psychology is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"0a5559f2-60b2-4570-8d84-cd05af69bf48\">young MBA graduates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> who are just beginning their careers and feel that evolutionary psychology will make their lives at work more difficult. Older and wiser executives point out that they still tend to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"5a2945e9-e748-4daf-87b0-dee88e9447cd\">cling to the idea of a magic formula<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> to bring people into line with corporate strategy. But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"26c18298-8b41-404c-b17d-c07c564f419c\">that is back-to-front thinking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, according to Nicholson, who contends that we <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"d685ee31-8d23-4d0d-8bd9-6d9e5e728106\">should be reinventing our business structures, </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"26c18298-8b41-404c-b17d-c07c564f419c d685ee31-8d23-4d0d-8bd9-6d9e5e728106\">not our fundamental human nature</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>At the end of his book, Nicholson gives his forecast of what will and will not change in the business world. He believes that most people will still prefer more traditional forms of work and throughout their lives will continue to aim at lifelong status advancement. He also maintains that the line between work and home will be less defined, but that people will prefer traditional working patterns if working from home leaves them isolated from their work community. He doubts that the high-tech ideas of virtual companies will ever be very successful because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b5b8005f-fca9-4f65-8f94-4d3818fa242b\">people will still want to meet each other face-to-face<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Nicholson describes his ideal organisation in the future: it would be decentralised, with small sub-units; the staff would be from diverse backgrounds and be allowed a high degree of self-determination. New endeavours and creativity would replace systems and rationality. Nicholson acknowledges that there is a long way to go in terms of the translation of his ideas of evolutionary psychology into practical propositions, but he is confident more and more people will come round to his way of thinking.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309950\" id=\"question-wrapper-309950\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer’s purpose in the first paragraph is to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. oppose the views of Charles Darwin.</li> <li>B. compare experts’ opinions of Darwin’s theory.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"78380b82-51b7-406f-994f-9eef986214c2\">explain the theory of evolutionary psychology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>D. name experts in the field of evolutionary psychology.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309951\" id=\"question-wrapper-309951\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the third paragraph, which view about evolutionary psychology matches Nicholson’s opinion?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Our characters determine our career choices.</li> <li>B. We begin life without any preconceived notions.</li> <li>C. Our interests and skills depend on our environment.</li> <li>D. We <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7382b0d8-5623-4c34-9527-fa34fcc15888\">inherit ideas and characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> from our ancestors.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309952\" id=\"question-wrapper-309952\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer discusses the key element of emotion in order to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. criticise primitive survival strategies.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"ccc10a6b-87c5-4490-81e7-5406e971b0cf\">explain attitudes and actions at work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>C. demonstrate the slowness of evolution.</li> <li>D. suggest companies today are poorly structured.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309953\" id=\"question-wrapper-309953\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which of the following does Nicholson predict will happen in the business world?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Companies will remain in city centres.</li> <li>B. Promotion will no longer motivate people.</li> <li>C. Employees will be less independent than now.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b5b8005f-fca9-4f65-8f94-4d3818fa242b\">Social interaction will remain important<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to workers.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309954\" id=\"question-wrapper-309954\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which of the following is the most suitable title for Reading Passage 3?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. How successful companies manage change.</li> <li>B. Understanding the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4e4dd92-f555-4518-abb2-1130bcb3fb5c\">origins of workplace behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Darwin’s theories rejected by modern management.</li> <li>D. Why post-industrial organisations need to evolve more quickly.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 32–35 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309955\" id=\"question-wrapper-309955\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"0ea7f612-269b-4670-a20c-37fc06d0ed3c\">Nicholson makes a persuasive argument<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> in his book.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309956\" id=\"question-wrapper-309956\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Tooby and Cosmides believe natural selection through the generations has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"82705dc7-930c-40d2-9ebc-1a05e4626043\">prepared us for modern times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309957\" id=\"question-wrapper-309957\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"8a8a45de-4baf-46c4-8a1a-74ec32c69520\">reliance on technology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> causes emotional problems in the workplace.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309958\" id=\"question-wrapper-309958\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People today are more trusting than they used to be.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, A–I, below. Write the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 36–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. business leaders </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. MBA graduates </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. promotion structures</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. reward strategy </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. magic formula </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. strategic planning</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. back-to-front thinking </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. business environments </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. human nature</span></p><p><b><span>Nicholson’s advice to the corporate world</span></b></p><p><span>Nicholson believes that if we know why people act the way they do, we can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"7972f2e6-67c0-455b-9da3-439e5eadd1a3\">change (36<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>)______ so employees will work more efficiently. Nicholson’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"0a5559f2-60b2-4570-8d84-cd05af69bf48\">ideas are unwelcome to (37<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>)______, but some executives are more open to what evolutionary psychology says. However, these executives still <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"5a2945e9-e748-4daf-87b0-dee88e9447cd\">believe that there is a (38<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>)______ that will make employees act according to the company’s practices. According to Nicholson, these senior executives are engaging in (39)______, and we should not try to change (40)______ but instead we should change our business structures.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309959\" id=\"question-wrapper-309959\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309960\" id=\"question-wrapper-309960\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309961\" id=\"question-wrapper-309961\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309962\" id=\"question-wrapper-309962\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309963\" id=\"question-wrapper-309963\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"78380b82-51b7-406f-994f-9eef986214c2","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"explain the theory of evolutionary psychology","passagePhrase":"foundation of a new wave of ideas ... evolutionary psychology"},{"uid":"0ea7f612-269b-4670-a20c-37fc06d0ed3c","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Nicholson makes a persuasive argument","passagePhrase":"It is an effective approach ... Nicholson believes"},{"uid":"d4e4dd92-f555-4518-abb2-1130bcb3fb5c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"origins of workplace behaviour","passagePhrase":"explaining why people behave as they do, particularly at work"},{"uid":"7382b0d8-5623-4c34-9527-fa34fcc15888","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"inherit ideas and characteristics","passagePhrase":"brain actually houses a store of knowledge when we are born"},{"uid":"82705dc7-930c-40d2-9ebc-1a05e4626043","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"prepared us for modern times","passagePhrase":"not ... well-adapted to our post-industrial life"},{"uid":"ccc10a6b-87c5-4490-81e7-5406e971b0cf","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"explain attitudes and actions at work","passagePhrase":"radar, guiding us throughout today’s"},{"uid":"8a8a45de-4baf-46c4-8a1a-74ec32c69520 ccc10a6b-87c5-4490-81e7-5406e971b0cf","qNum":"29 34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"techno-defined business world"},{"uid":"7972f2e6-67c0-455b-9da3-439e5eadd1a3","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"change (36","passagePhrase":"mould corporate environments"},{"uid":"0a5559f2-60b2-4570-8d84-cd05af69bf48","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"ideas are unwelcome to (37","passagePhrase":"One group that resists ... young MBA graduates"},{"uid":"5a2945e9-e748-4daf-87b0-dee88e9447cd","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"believe that there is a (38","passagePhrase":"cling to the idea of a magic formula"},{"uid":"26c18298-8b41-404c-b17d-c07c564f419c","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"that is back-to-front thinking"},{"uid":"d685ee31-8d23-4d0d-8bd9-6d9e5e728106","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"should be reinventing our business structures,"},{"uid":"26c18298-8b41-404c-b17d-c07c564f419c d685ee31-8d23-4d0d-8bd9-6d9e5e728106","qNum":"39 40","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"not our fundamental human nature"},{"uid":"b5b8005f-fca9-4f65-8f94-4d3818fa242b","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Social interaction will remain important","passagePhrase":"people will still want to meet each other face-to-face"},{"uid":"8a8a45de-4baf-46c4-8a1a-74ec32c69520","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"reliance on technology","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_10":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>Thomas Young: The last man who knew everything</span></b></p><p><i><span>In the 21st century, it would be quite impossible for even the most learned man to know everything. However, as recently as the 18th century, there were those whose knowledge encompassed most of the information available at that time.</span></i></p><p><i><span>This is a review of a biography of one such man.</span></i></p><p><span>Thomas Young (1773–1829) contributed 63 articles to the great British encyclopaedia, </span><i><span>Encyclopaedia Britannica</span></i><span>, including 46 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"3b97fbdd-6b0a-4f7d-a30c-1a2741c76418\">biographical entries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (mostly on scientists and classical scholars) and substantial essays on ‘Bridge’ (a card game), ‘Egypt’, ‘Languages’ and ‘Tides’. Was someone who could write authoritatively about so many subjects a genius, or a dilettante? In an ambitious biography, Andrew Robinson argues that Young is a good contender to be described as ‘the last man who knew everything’. Young has competition, however: the phrase, which Robinson uses as the title of his biography of Young, also serves as the subtitle of two other recent biographies – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b0211dbf-65cf-41da-85ca-791aee1d9a68\">Leonard Warren’s life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of palaeontologist Joseph Leidy (1823–1891) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b0211dbf-65cf-41da-85ca-791aee1d9a68\">and Paula Findlen’s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> 2004 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b0211dbf-65cf-41da-85ca-791aee1d9a68\">book<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> on Athanasius Kircher (1602–1680).</span></p><p><span>Young, of course, did more than write encyclopaedia entries. He presented his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"501383c5-6c64-465a-acea-4e0a54915ec6\">first paper, on the human eye<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, to the prestigious academic institution, the Royal Society of London, at the age of 20 and was elected a Fellow of the Society shortly afterwards. In the paper, which sought to explain how the eye focuses on objects at varying distances, Young hypothesised that this was achieved by changes in the shape of the lens. He also theorised that light travels in waves and believed that, to be able to see in colour, there must be three receptors in the eye corresponding to the three principal colours (red, green and violet) to which the retina could respond. All these hypotheses were subsequently proved correct.</span></p><p><span>Later in his life, when he was in his forties, Young was instrumental in cracking the code that unlocked the unknown script on the Rosetta Stone, a tablet found in Egypt by the Napoleonic army in 1799. The stone has text in three alphabets: Greek, Egyptian hieroglyphs and another script that was originally unrecognisable. The unrecognisable script is now known as demotic and, as Young deduced, is directly related to Egyptian hieroglyphs. His initial work on this appeared in the ‘</span><i><span>Britannica</span></i><span> entry ‘Egypt’. In another entry, Young <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"9718d1dc-4d43-4490-8c2b-2ebde8c06a78\">coined the term ‘Indo-European<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>’ to describe the family of languages spoken throughout most of Europe and northern India. These works are landmark achievements for a man who was a child prodigy but who, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"5a05cf0a-49d3-4f9c-a6f7-80e638f385f8\">unlike many remarkable children, did not fade into obscurity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> as an adult.</span></p><p><span>Born in 1773 in Somerset, England, Young lived with his maternal grandfather from an early age. He devoured books from the age of two and excelled at Latin, Greek, mathematics and natural philosophy (the 18th-century term for science). After leaving school, he was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ded84484-ca42-409f-a6ed-6407a547ec40\">greatly encouraged by Richard Brocklesby<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, a physician and Fellow of the Royal Society. Following Brocklesby’s lead, Young <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ded84484-ca42-409f-a6ed-6407a547ec40\">decided to pursue a career in medicine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. He studied in London and then moved on to more formal education in Edinburgh, Göttingen and Cambridge. After completing his medical training at the University of Cambridge in 1808, Young set up practice as a physician in London and, a few years later, was appointed physician at St George’s Hospital.</span></p><p><span>Young’s <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"456ee792-6d19-4116-9eeb-b29dc06a7dc9\">skill as a physician<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, however, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"456ee792-6d19-4116-9eeb-b29dc06a7dc9\">did not equal his talent as a scholar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of natural philosophy or linguistics. In 1801, he had been appointed to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"50f519ef-7b0f-45df-a613-357794ce8a30\">professorship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> of natural philosophy at the Royal Institution, where he delivered as many as 60 lectures a year. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"1f63bfb3-214e-4a7f-8282-b9277b4be4f7\">His opinions were sought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b33bbc80-d71e-4113-8630-eda30f596312\">civic and national authorities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> on matters such as the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"43d855a9-2a74-4499-9862-88498d99a520\">introduction of gas lighting to London streets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> and methods of ship construction. From 1819, he was Superintendent of the</span><i><span> Nautical Almanac </span></i><span>and Secretary to the Board of Longitude. Between 1816 and 1825, he contributed many entries to the Encyclopaedia </span><i><span>Britannica</span></i><span>, and throughout his career he <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"ea37089b-24e2-4445-ab70-d7467a730751\">authored numerous other essays, papers and books<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Young is a perfect subject for a biography – perfect, but daunting. Few men contributed so much to so many technical fields. Robinson’s aim is to introduce non-scientists to Young’s work and life. He succeeds, providing clear expositions of the technical material (especially that on optics and Egyptian hieroglyphs). Some readers of this book will, like Robinson, find Young’s accomplishments impressive; others will see him, as some historians have, as a dilettante. Yet despite the rich material presented in this book, readers will not end up knowing Young personally. We catch glimpses of a playful Young, doodling Greek and Latin phrases in his notes on medical lectures and translating the verses that a young lady had written on the walls of a summerhouse into Greek elegiacs. Young was introduced into elite society, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b45714ec-b0be-4191-b806-52fc6dc0b693\">attended the theatre and learned to dance and play the flute<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. In addition, he was an accomplished <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b45714ec-b0be-4191-b806-52fc6dc0b693\">horseman<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. However, his personal life looks pale next to his vibrant career and studies.</span></p><p><span>Young married Eliza Maxwell in 1804, and according to Robinson, ‘their marriage was happy and she appreciated his work’. Almost all we know about her is that she sustained her husband through some acrimonious disputes about optics and that she worried about money when his medical career was slow to take off. Little evidence survives concerning the complexities of Young’s relationships with his mother and father, and Robinson does not credit them with shaping Young’s extraordinary mind. Despite the lack of personal detail, anyone interested in what it means to be a genius should read this book.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1 – 7 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309964\" id=\"question-wrapper-309964\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b0211dbf-65cf-41da-85ca-791aee1d9a68\">Other people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> have been referred to as ‘</span><i><span>the last man who knew everything</span></i><span>’.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309965\" id=\"question-wrapper-309965\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The fact that Young’s <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"5a05cf0a-49d3-4f9c-a6f7-80e638f385f8\">childhood brilliance continued into adulthood was normal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309966\" id=\"question-wrapper-309966\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Young’s <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"456ee792-6d19-4116-9eeb-b29dc06a7dc9\">talents as a doctor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> are described as <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"456ee792-6d19-4116-9eeb-b29dc06a7dc9\">surpassing his other skills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309967\" id=\"question-wrapper-309967\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"1f63bfb3-214e-4a7f-8282-b9277b4be4f7\">Young’s advice was sought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b33bbc80-d71e-4113-8630-eda30f596312\">several bodies responsible for local and national matters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309968\" id=\"question-wrapper-309968\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"ea37089b-24e2-4445-ab70-d7467a730751\">All Young’s written works were published in the </span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"ea37089b-24e2-4445-ab70-d7467a730751\">Encyclopaedia Britannica<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></i><span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309969\" id=\"question-wrapper-309969\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Young was interested in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b45714ec-b0be-4191-b806-52fc6dc0b693\">range of social pastimes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309970\" id=\"question-wrapper-309970\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Young suffered from poor health in his later years.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8 – 13 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309971\" id=\"question-wrapper-309971\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>How many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"3b97fbdd-6b0a-4f7d-a30c-1a2741c76418\">life stories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> did Thomas Young write for the </span><i><span>Encyclopaedia Britannica</span></i><span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">46/forty-six</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309972\" id=\"question-wrapper-309972\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What was the subject of Thomas Young’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"501383c5-6c64-465a-acea-4e0a54915ec6\">first academic paper<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) human eye</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309973\" id=\"question-wrapper-309973\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"9718d1dc-4d43-4490-8c2b-2ebde8c06a78\">name did Young give to a group of languages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Indo-European</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309974\" id=\"question-wrapper-309974\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ded84484-ca42-409f-a6ed-6407a547ec40\">inspired Young to enter the medical profession<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Richard Brocklesby</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309975\" id=\"question-wrapper-309975\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>At which place of higher learning did Young hold a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"50f519ef-7b0f-45df-a613-357794ce8a30\">teaching position<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">The Royal Institution</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309976\" id=\"question-wrapper-309976\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"43d855a9-2a74-4499-9862-88498d99a520\">improvement to London’s roads<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> was Young consulted about?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">gas lighting</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"3b97fbdd-6b0a-4f7d-a30c-1a2741c76418","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"life stories","passagePhrase":"biographical entries"},{"uid":"b0211dbf-65cf-41da-85ca-791aee1d9a68","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Other people","passagePhrase":"Leonard Warren’s life ... and Paula Findlen’s ... book"},{"uid":"501383c5-6c64-465a-acea-4e0a54915ec6","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"first academic paper","passagePhrase":"first paper, on the human eye"},{"uid":"9718d1dc-4d43-4490-8c2b-2ebde8c06a78","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"name did Young give to a group of languages","passagePhrase":"coined the term ‘Indo-European"},{"uid":"ded84484-ca42-409f-a6ed-6407a547ec40","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"inspired Young to enter the medical profession","passagePhrase":"greatly encouraged by Richard Brocklesby ... decided to pursue a career in medicine"},{"uid":"50f519ef-7b0f-45df-a613-357794ce8a30","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"teaching position","passagePhrase":"professorship"},{"uid":"1f63bfb3-214e-4a7f-8282-b9277b4be4f7","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Young’s advice was sought","passagePhrase":"His opinions were sought"},{"uid":"b33bbc80-d71e-4113-8630-eda30f596312","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"several bodies responsible for local and national matters","passagePhrase":"civic and national authorities"},{"uid":"43d855a9-2a74-4499-9862-88498d99a520","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"improvement to London’s roads","passagePhrase":"introduction of gas lighting to London streets"},{"uid":"b45714ec-b0be-4191-b806-52fc6dc0b693","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"range of social pastimes","passagePhrase":"attended the theatre and learned to dance and play the flute ... horseman"}]},"reading_u2_11":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>Playing Soccer</span></b></p><p><i><span>There are many differences between playing soccer in the street and joining a youth team in an organized league in the USA.</span></i></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> Street soccer, as its name implies, is an informal variation of the sport, often played on the street, particularly in urban areas. There are many reasons for the widespread popularity of street soccer. Unlike youth soccer, its more formally organized counterpart, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"da84d7e9-a624-47c1-b6cb-4e87055a3024\">no large space is needed, and goal posts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, corner markers, and marked lines, associated with the formal game, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"da84d7e9-a624-47c1-b6cb-4e87055a3024\">are typically absent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, as are game officials or referees. Another attraction of street soccer is that it is played frequently and competitively, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"5da57242-a5f7-4d48-acfc-35886bdaf00a\">does not necessarily require standard 11-a-side teams<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> or fixed playing positions. Unlike in youth soccer, inexperienced street soccer players rarely learn from repetitive technical and tactical drills. Instead, they learn from their poor performance in competition, unconscious of the skills they are nonetheless developing, and without older adults or coaches present. Players learn without effort through playing the game, and soon attain an almost natural feeling for the sport.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> However, there are lots of cities in the world today where conditions are such that street soccer is no longer possible. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"f3638f22-65aa-4c1f-b33f-7fe96433bbad\">Congested traffic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> now dominates where games were once played. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"f3638f22-65aa-4c1f-b33f-7fe96433bbad\">Parks and open fields are used as hangouts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> for older teenagers with other interests. Add to this the requirement in many localities for official permits to use public spaces and the managed schedules that many young people have today, and spontaneous play of any kind is hard to imagine.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> In spite of all these obstacles, which are probably solvable in most instances, there is another sociological explanation of why in many places street soccer doesn’t enjoy the same popularity it once did. In his book How Soccer Explains the World, US writer Franklin Foer observes: But for all the talk of freedom, the 1960s parenting style had a far less relaxed side too. Like the 1960s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9e3fe2e7-03c7-4d8b-9a23-e10e4292d09a\">consumer movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, which brought <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9e3fe2e7-03c7-4d8b-9a23-e10e4292d09a\">seat belts and airbags to cars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, the (youth) soccer movement felt like it could create a set of ... regulations that would protect both the child’s body and mind from damage. Soccer leagues like the one I played in as a child <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a6e636da-443c-4034-b751-b26e83395515\">handed out ‘participation’ prizes to every player<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, no matter how few games his (or her) team won. Where most of the world accepts the practice of using your head to hit the ball as an essential element of the game, some (youth) soccer parents have worried over the potential for injury to the brain. An entire industry grew up to manufacture protective headgear. Even though very little medical evidence supports this fear, some youth leagues <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"bd12e4c7-43d5-4c74-b3c8-aa31581842fe\">prohibited heading the ball altogether<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> A growing body of people don’t believe street soccer involves a legitimate educational method. They argue that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"12e8b1e4-382b-495e-9034-2cdc829ba227\">children need to be taught by experts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Youth soccer instruction now begins with four-year-olds, so that they will have an advantage as six-year-olds. This need to get ahead brings with it a fear of falling behind that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"12e8b1e4-382b-495e-9034-2cdc829ba227\">only expert instruction can prevent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. This type of instruction leaves no room for the trial-and-error approach of street soccer.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> One of the basic ideas of street soccer is that young players are assigned a particular role by a better player and are expected to play for the good of the team. Such an assignment runs counter to the idea of youth soccer that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a250ffe5-2933-41b1-af0f-5a20349230c3\">every child needs to learn every position<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and will benefit from doing so. In street soccer, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a250ffe5-2933-41b1-af0f-5a20349230c3\">you fill the role that you are best able to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> at a particular time. While this role assignment can change from game to game, the purpose is always the same: to get the best out of each individual at any given moment.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>In street soccer, children have to learn patience, to wait their turn, to realize that they are not entitled to make decisions, or even be listened to simply because they show up. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"0f26ae3e-24cf-4022-8754-ca8b8e18fc84\">Positions of responsibility are earned through competition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> within the team. Younger players in street soccer must wait to attain those positions. In youth soccer, however, with its overly democratic values, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"0f26ae3e-24cf-4022-8754-ca8b8e18fc84\">youngsters are guaranteed their time in the spotlight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Whether it’s their turn to be captain, to play a central position or to take a crucial shot, youth soccer players come to believe that hard work and patience aren’t really necessary.</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>Not only does every youth soccer player get a chance, but it is also assumed that each individual has played well. Everyone’s a winner; no one’s a loser’ is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"72d7d5ec-9ca2-4f52-9ff0-cef0f29e964a\">guiding principle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of youth soccer. This ensures each individual goes away positive about themselves. No one can leave a game or a practice feeling bad. But, if there really are no losers, then why try at all? Since giving less than your best <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"cbfd78e3-b676-42c0-b0d3-2f5c126fe991\">receives the same reward<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> as giving your best, why go to any extra effort?</span></p><p><span>In street soccer, every game results in a winner and a loser and everyone knows who is who. Losing a game is a common experience and players learn early on how to handle this. As a result, unlike most youth soccer players, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"3712cc37-6ede-4328-9448-bc5ba50d2487\">acquire resilience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. A further difference between these two strands of soccer is that in street soccer, a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"435da0c7-7367-44a7-b2d5-c10f25ab9d93\">formal record is not kept<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. You can lose one day and win the next. The results are only temporary and are forgotten within minutes of the end of the match. But in organized youth soccer, the position each person plays and the results are formally noted and maintained throughout a season.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven sections, A–G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309977\" id=\"question-wrapper-309977\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a contrast between the ways young players gain experience of playing different positions</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309978\" id=\"question-wrapper-309978\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>examples outside sport of greater emphasis on individual safety</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309979\" id=\"question-wrapper-309979\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a description of methods of selection for leadership on soccer teams</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309980\" id=\"question-wrapper-309980\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>details of urban changes that discourage street soccer</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309981\" id=\"question-wrapper-309981\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a reference to how repeated defeats help street players <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"3712cc37-6ede-4328-9448-bc5ba50d2487\">become emotionally tougher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309982\" id=\"question-wrapper-309982\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an explanation of why youth soccer emphasises <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"12e8b1e4-382b-495e-9034-2cdc829ba227\">the need for coaches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose TWO letters, A–E. Write the correct letters in boxes 20 and 21 on your answer sheet. The list below gives some possible reasons for the popularity of street soccer.</span></p><p><span>Which TWO of these reasons are mentioned by the writer of the text?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Many famous soccer players got their start in street soccer.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Young people can begin playing street soccer at a very early age.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. You <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"da84d7e9-a624-47c1-b6cb-4e87055a3024\">do not need elaborate facilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to play street soccer.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Inexperienced street soccer players are not criticised for mistakes.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Street soccer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"5da57242-a5f7-4d48-acfc-35886bdaf00a\">teams can have varying numbers of players<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309983\" id=\"question-wrapper-309983\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309984\" id=\"question-wrapper-309984\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E/C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose TWO letters, A–E. Write the correct letters in boxes 22 and 23 on your answer sheet. The list below gives some possible results of the 1960s parenting style.</span></p><p><span>Which TWO of these results are mentioned by Franklin Foer in the excerpt from How Soccer Explains the World?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Participation in youth soccer became much more expensive.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Some youth soccer leagues <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"bd12e4c7-43d5-4c74-b3c8-aa31581842fe\">adopted more restrictive rules<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of play.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Fewer young people joined youth soccer teams.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Youth soccer players were sometimes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a6e636da-443c-4034-b751-b26e83395515\">rewarded for simply playing games<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Soccer equipment manufacturers directed advertising towards parents.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309985\" id=\"question-wrapper-309985\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309986\" id=\"question-wrapper-309986\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D/B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Winners and losers</span></b></p><p><span>For youth soccer players, a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"72d7d5ec-9ca2-4f52-9ff0-cef0f29e964a\">key (24<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>)______ is that they should always come away from the game with a positive attitude. In this respect, regardless of the effort the players make, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"cbfd78e3-b676-42c0-b0d3-2f5c126fe991\">get some kind of (25<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>)______ at the end of a game. In street soccer, however, players gain resilience because they have to learn to cope with failure. But the outcome of a match isn’t remembered for long. In fact, no one ever <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"435da0c7-7367-44a7-b2d5-c10f25ab9d93\">keeps a (26<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>)______ of the results of games.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309987\" id=\"question-wrapper-309987\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">principle</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309988\" id=\"question-wrapper-309988\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">reward</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309989\" id=\"question-wrapper-309989\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">record</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"da84d7e9-a624-47c1-b6cb-4e87055a3024","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"do not need elaborate facilities","passagePhrase":"no large space is needed, and goal posts ... are typically absent"},{"uid":"5da57242-a5f7-4d48-acfc-35886bdaf00a","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"teams can have varying numbers of players","passagePhrase":"does not necessarily require standard 11-a-side teams"},{"uid":"f3638f22-65aa-4c1f-b33f-7fe96433bbad","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Congested traffic ... Parks and open fields are used as hangouts"},{"uid":"9e3fe2e7-03c7-4d8b-9a23-e10e4292d09a","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"consumer movement ... seat belts and airbags to cars"},{"uid":"a6e636da-443c-4034-b751-b26e83395515","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"rewarded for simply playing games","passagePhrase":"handed out ‘participation’ prizes to every player"},{"uid":"bd12e4c7-43d5-4c74-b3c8-aa31581842fe","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"adopted more restrictive rules","passagePhrase":"prohibited heading the ball altogether"},{"uid":"12e8b1e4-382b-495e-9034-2cdc829ba227","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"the need for coaches","passagePhrase":"children need to be taught by experts ... only expert instruction can prevent"},{"uid":"a250ffe5-2933-41b1-af0f-5a20349230c3","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"every child needs to learn every position ... you fill the role that you are best able to"},{"uid":"0f26ae3e-24cf-4022-8754-ca8b8e18fc84","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Positions of responsibility are earned through competition ... youngsters are guaranteed their time in the spotlight"},{"uid":"72d7d5ec-9ca2-4f52-9ff0-cef0f29e964a","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"key (24","passagePhrase":"guiding principle"},{"uid":"cbfd78e3-b676-42c0-b0d3-2f5c126fe991","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"get some kind of (25","passagePhrase":"receives the same reward"},{"uid":"3712cc37-6ede-4328-9448-bc5ba50d2487","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"become emotionally tougher","passagePhrase":"acquire resilience"},{"uid":"435da0c7-7367-44a7-b2d5-c10f25ab9d93","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"keeps a (26","passagePhrase":"formal record is not kept"}]},"reading_u2_12":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>The Analysis of Fear</span></b></p><p><i><span>Researchers are investigating the processes in the brain that give rise to fear in animals. The results may lead to new ways to treat human anxiety.</span></i></p><p><span>Over the years, the majority of people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"1884fcb5-d4c4-4e46-b185-1f45f8b4a3f3\">acquire a range of skills for coping with frightening situations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. They will attempt to placate a vexed teacher or boss and will shout and run when chased by a hostile stranger. But some individuals become overwhelmed in circumstances others would consider only minimally stressful: fear of ridicule might cause them to shake uncontrollably when called on to speak in a group, or terror of strangers might lead them to hide at home, unable to work or shop for groceries. Why do certain people fall prey to excessive fear?</span></p><p><span>Ned H. Kalin and Steven E. Shelton at the University of Wisconsin–Madison are addressing this problem by identifying specific brain processes that regulate fear and its associated behaviors. Despite the availability of non-invasive computer-imaging techniques, such information is still extremely difficult to obtain in humans. Hence, they have turned their attention to another primate, the rhesus monkey. These animals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a87be9d6-9c86-41bc-b340-de2fb6c9cafe\">undergo many of the same physiological and psychological developmental stages that humans do<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, but in a more compressed time span. As we gain more insight into the nature and operation of neural circuits that modulate fear in monkeys, it should be possible to pinpoint the brain processes that cause inordinate anxiety in people, and to devise new therapies to counteract it. Effective interventions would be particularly valuable if they were applied at an early age, as growing evidence suggests overly fearful youngsters are at high risk of later emotional distress.</span></p><p><span>When they began their studies two decades ago, Kalin and Shelton knew that they would first have to find cues that elicit fear and identify behaviors that reflect different types of anxiety. Following this, they could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"3798f4af-f7ce-45f6-b881-929963fcaefb\">proceed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"3808b420-41ec-4a70-8a51-2d9e77c37a72\">determine the age at which monkeys begin to match defensive behaviors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> selectively to specific cues. Finally, by determining the parts of the brain that reach maturity during the same time span, they could gain clues to the regions that underlie the regulation of fear and fear-related behavior.</span></p><p><span>The experiments were carried out at the University of Wisconsin–Madison. Kalin and Shelton discerned varied behaviors by exposing monkeys between six and 12 months old to three related situations. In the alone condition, an animal was separated from its mother and left by itself in a cage for ten minutes. In the no-eye-contact condition, a person stood motionless outside the cage and avoided looking at the solitary infant. In the stare condition, a person was again present and motionless but, assuming a neutral expression, peered directly at the animal. These positions are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e28b447f-a7bb-4a3b-8894-07386af06ce6\">no more frightening than those that primates encounter frequently in the wild<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, or those that human infants meet whenever they are left at a day-care centre.</span></p><p><span>In the alone condition, most monkeys became very active and emitted <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"eae1e915-0582-469e-a44d-acdcc685242d\">frequent gentle “coo” calls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> made with pursed lips. More than 40 years ago it was deduced that when an infant monkey is separated from its mother, it yearns to regain the closeness and security provided by nearness to the parent. These <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"6dd74c16-3785-4b12-b147-ff52ee20cf8f\">responses help to draw the mother’s attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. In contrast, in the more frightening no-eye-contact situation, the monkeys <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"67c81b86-f5fe-4428-bbd5-cd92115b044c\">reduced their activity greatly and sometimes froze<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> for extended periods of time. When an infant spots a potential predator, its goal shifts from attracting the mother to becoming inconspicuous. Inhibiting motion and freezing are common attempts to achieve this in many species. If the infant perceives that it has been detected, its aim shifts to warding off an attack. So the stare condition evoked a third set of responses. The monkeys made several <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4df4fcc-f64c-4120-8543-89dfdf527d50\">hostile gestures: barking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> (forcing air from the abdomen through the vocal cords to emit a harsh, growl-like sound) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4df4fcc-f64c-4120-8543-89dfdf527d50\">and staring back<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Sometimes the animals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"ea543b8f-3837-490e-8162-552398a18d8c\">mixed the threatening displays with submissive ones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, such as fear grimaces, which look something like wary grins, or grinding of teeth.</span></p><p><span>Having identified three categories of defensive behaviours, Kalin and Shelton set about determining when infant monkeys first begin to apply them effectively. Several lines of work had led them to surmise that the ability to make such choices emerges when an infant is around two months old. To establish the critical period of development, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"fe5d2afa-d6c2-438d-a8fa-d5fb4715c7a0\">examined four groups of infant monkeys ranging in age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> up to 12 weeks old. The babies were separated from their mothers, left to acclimatise to a cage, and then exposed to the alone, no-eye-contact and stare conditions. All sessions were videotaped for analysis. They found that the infants in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"615b2460-db1b-43be-b551-11005e97c1c8\">youngest group<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> (no more than two weeks old) engaged in defensive behaviours, but they lacked some motor control and seemed to act randomly, as if they had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"78d28cf3-b433-44cf-9b7e-cb9ed0682715\">not noticed the human beings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> that were present. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"f5bcc915-4b75-4eb1-8a1a-0ac31a99aae9\">Babies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> in the two intermediate-age groups <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"f5bcc915-4b75-4eb1-8a1a-0ac31a99aae9\">had good motor control<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, but their actions seemed unrelated to the test condition. Only animals in the oldest group (nine- to 12-week-old) conducted themselves differently in each situation, and their reactions were both appropriate and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"9125d15d-9d07-4a79-9ce5-bd972bbdd9ea\">identical to those of mature monkeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. This finding meant motor control was not the prime determinant of selective responding and that nine to 12 weeks is the critical age for the appearance of a monkey’s ability to adaptively modulate its defensive activity to meet changing demands.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309990\" id=\"question-wrapper-309990\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the first paragraph, the writer points out that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. fear&nbsp;and stress are different feelings.</li> <li>B. most&nbsp;humans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"1884fcb5-d4c4-4e46-b185-1f45f8b4a3f3\">develop strategies for dealing with fear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>C. business situations cause more fear than others.</li> <li>D. some&nbsp;people never experience fear.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309991\" id=\"question-wrapper-309991\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>When discussing the use of rhesus monkeys as experimental subjects, the writer notes that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. they react more quickly to fear than humans.</li> <li>B. they are more influenced by fear than humans.</li> <li>C. their mental growth <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a87be9d6-9c86-41bc-b340-de2fb6c9cafe\">resembles that of humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>D. their&nbsp;brains work more slowly than those of humans.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309992\" id=\"question-wrapper-309992\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which of the following did Kalin and Shelton outline as the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"3798f4af-f7ce-45f6-b881-929963fcaefb\">second stage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> in their research project?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the identification of expressions of anxiety in monkeys</li> <li>B. the identification of situations that arouse stress in monkeys</li> <li>C. an analysis of brain development in monkeys</li> <li>D. the study of reactions to fear in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"3808b420-41ec-4a70-8a51-2d9e77c37a72\">monkeys of different ages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309993\" id=\"question-wrapper-309993\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the fourth paragraph, the writer notes that the three related situations</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e28b447f-a7bb-4a3b-8894-07386af06ce6\">reflect common experiences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> for infant humans and monkeys.</li> <li>B. highlight the similarities between monkey and human infant care.</li> <li>C. were predicted to cause monkeys more distress than human infants.</li> <li>D. were graded in terms of their potential effect on young monkeys.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following responses of monkeys and the list of conditions below. Match each response with the correct condition, A, B or C. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Conditions</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. the alone condition</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. the no-eye-contact condition</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. the stare condition</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309994\" id=\"question-wrapper-309994\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4df4fcc-f64c-4120-8543-89dfdf527d50\">aggressive facial expressions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309995\" id=\"question-wrapper-309995\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"67c81b86-f5fe-4428-bbd5-cd92115b044c\">prolonged stillness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309996\" id=\"question-wrapper-309996\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"ea543b8f-3837-490e-8162-552398a18d8c\">combination of contradictory signals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309997\" id=\"question-wrapper-309997\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"6dd74c16-3785-4b12-b147-ff52ee20cf8f\">appeals for maternal protection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309998\" id=\"question-wrapper-309998\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"eae1e915-0582-469e-a44d-acdcc685242d\">production of soft sounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND / OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>Once they had identified three types of defensive behaviour, Kalin and Shelton <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"fe5d2afa-d6c2-438d-a8fa-d5fb4715c7a0\">grouped the monkeys according to their (36<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>)______, in order to discover precisely when they were able to respond appropriately to different fear-related cues. They videotaped their results and found that monkeys as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"615b2460-db1b-43be-b551-11005e97c1c8\">young as (37<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>)______ reacted to the cues but in a haphazard fashion. The researchers noted that they seemed to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"78d28cf3-b433-44cf-9b7e-cb9ed0682715\">unaware of the (38<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>)______ who were around them. Despite demonstrating (39)______, the monkeys in the middle groups failed to react in ways corresponding to the experimental situation. The oldest group, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"9125d15d-9d07-4a79-9ce5-bd972bbdd9ea\">reacted in the same way as (40<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>)______ and the researchers concluded that monkeys are capable of selective responding between nine and 12 weeks old.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309999\" id=\"question-wrapper-309999\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">age</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310000\" id=\"question-wrapper-310000\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">2/two weeks (old)</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310001\" id=\"question-wrapper-310001\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">human beings</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310002\" id=\"question-wrapper-310002\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">good motor control</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310003\" id=\"question-wrapper-310003\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">mature monkeys</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"1884fcb5-d4c4-4e46-b185-1f45f8b4a3f3","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"develop strategies for dealing with fear","passagePhrase":"acquire a range of skills for coping with frightening situations"},{"uid":"a87be9d6-9c86-41bc-b340-de2fb6c9cafe","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"resembles that of humans","passagePhrase":"undergo many of the same physiological and psychological developmental stages that humans do"},{"uid":"3798f4af-f7ce-45f6-b881-929963fcaefb","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"second stage","passagePhrase":"proceed to"},{"uid":"3808b420-41ec-4a70-8a51-2d9e77c37a72","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"monkeys of different ages","passagePhrase":"determine the age at which monkeys begin to match defensive behaviors"},{"uid":"e28b447f-a7bb-4a3b-8894-07386af06ce6","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"reflect common experiences","passagePhrase":"no more frightening than those that primates encounter frequently in the wild"},{"uid":"eae1e915-0582-469e-a44d-acdcc685242d","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"production of soft sounds","passagePhrase":"frequent gentle “coo” calls"},{"uid":"6dd74c16-3785-4b12-b147-ff52ee20cf8f","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"appeals for maternal protection","passagePhrase":"responses help to draw the mother’s attention"},{"uid":"67c81b86-f5fe-4428-bbd5-cd92115b044c","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"prolonged stillness","passagePhrase":"reduced their activity greatly and sometimes froze"},{"uid":"d4df4fcc-f64c-4120-8543-89dfdf527d50","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"aggressive facial expressions","passagePhrase":"hostile gestures: barking ... and staring back"},{"uid":"ea543b8f-3837-490e-8162-552398a18d8c","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"combination of contradictory signals","passagePhrase":"mixed the threatening displays with submissive ones"},{"uid":"fe5d2afa-d6c2-438d-a8fa-d5fb4715c7a0","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"grouped the monkeys according to their (36","passagePhrase":"examined four groups of infant monkeys ranging in age"},{"uid":"615b2460-db1b-43be-b551-11005e97c1c8","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"young as (37","passagePhrase":"youngest group"},{"uid":"78d28cf3-b433-44cf-9b7e-cb9ed0682715","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"unaware of the (38","passagePhrase":"not noticed the human beings"},{"uid":"f5bcc915-4b75-4eb1-8a1a-0ac31a99aae9","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Babies ... had good motor control"},{"uid":"9125d15d-9d07-4a79-9ce5-bd972bbdd9ea","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"reacted in the same way as (40","passagePhrase":"identical to those of mature monkeys"}]},"reading_u2_13":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>Wood: A Valuable Resource in New Zealand’s Economy</span></b></p><p><span>During the settlement of New Zealand by European immigrants, natural timbers played a major role. Wood was easily accessible and relatively cheap. A tradition of wooden houses arose, supported by the recognition that they were <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"977e59fc-4bf8-409a-99b3-8a72cf3c9cc8\">less likely to collapse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> suddenly during earthquakes, a not-infrequent event in this part of the world. But in addition to demand from the domestic market, there was also demand for forest products from overseas.</span></p><p><span>Early explorers recognised the suitability of the tall, straight trunks of the kauri for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f4193369-8ed2-48ed-a9cf-9f8700b66590\">constructing sailing vessels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. The kauri is a species of coniferous tree found only in small areas of the southern hemisphere. So, from the early 1800s, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f4193369-8ed2-48ed-a9cf-9f8700b66590\">huge amounts of this type of wood were sold to Australia and the UK<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> for that purpose. For a period, the forestry industry was the country’s major export earner, but the rate of harvest was unsustainable and, by the beginning of the 20th century, indigenous timber exports were rapidly declining.</span></p><p><span>From the 1940s, newly established plantations of an imported species of tree called radiata pine supplied timber and other wood products in increasing quantities. By the 1960s, plantation-grown timber was providing most of the country’s sawn-timber needs, especially for construction. Today, less than two percent of timber is cut from indigenous forests, and almost all of that is used for higher-value end uses such as furniture and fittings. As the pine industry developed, it became apparent that this type of wood was also <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"48fd9639-99f2-4b4f-a701-fb1fb3541493\">well suited for many uses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. It makes excellent pulp*, and is frequently used for posts, poles, furnishings and mouldings, particleboard, fibreboard, and for plywood and ‘engineered’ wood products. Pine by-products are used in the chemical and pharmaceutical industries and residues are consumed for fuel. This <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"48fd9639-99f2-4b4f-a701-fb1fb3541493\">amazing versatility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> has encouraged the development of an integrated forest-products industry which is almost unique in the world.</span></p><p><span>Exporters of wood products have largely targeted the rapidly growing markets of South and East Asia and Australia. Eighty percent of exports by value go to only five markets: Japan, Korea, China, the United States and Australia. The product mix remains heavily based towards raw materials, with logs, sawn wood, pulp and paper comprising 75 percent of export value. However, finished wood products such as panels and furniture components are exported to more than 50 countries.</span></p><p><span>In New Zealand itself, the construction industry is the principal user of solid wood products, servicing 20,000 new house starts annually. However, the small size of New Zealand’s population (just over four million), plus its small manufacturing and remanufacturing base, limits the forestry industry’s domestic opportunities. For the last few years local wood consumption has been around only four million cubic metres. Accordingly, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"25e708d8-1571-4693-aed3-6ac2a0c613e0\">development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of the export market <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"d47b4b68-f665-4b92-8f07-2e02f1be207b\">is the key to the industry’s growth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> and contribution to the national economy in decades to come.</span></p><p><span>In 2004, forestry export receipts were about 11 percent of the country’s total export income, their value having increased steadily for ten years, until <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"ae39bc8e-22c1-44f1-9f66-16a1c0e420f6\">affected by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"ae39bc8e-22c1-44f1-9f66-16a1c0e420f6\">exchange fluctuations and shipping costs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> of recent years. The forestry industry is New Zealand’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"e2df2216-a54e-42b8-927d-2781c594af9a\">third-largest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> export sector, generating around $3.3 billion annually from logs and processed wood products. But it is generally agreed that it is operating well below its capacity and, with the domestic market already at its peak, almost all of the extra wood produced in the future will have to be marketed overseas. That presents a major marketing challenge for the industry.</span></p><p><span>Although the export of logs will continue to provide valuable earnings for forest owners, there is broad acceptance that the industry must be based on value-added products in the future. So the industry is investigating various processing, infrastructure and investment strategies with a view to increasing the level of local manufacturing before export. The keys to future success will depend on a variety of factors — better international marketing, product innovation, internationally competitive processing, improved infrastructure and a suitable political, regulatory and investment environment. The industry claims that, given the right conditions, by 2025 the forestry sector could be the country’s biggest export earner, generating $20 billion a year and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"a501f0d6-a2e5-4a36-a47e-cbfadaddbc46\">employing 60,000 people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>One competitive advantage that New Zealand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"71bb0d8e-28e0-4871-89e6-7b330c766ef9\">has is its ability to source large quantities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> of softwood from renewable forests. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"4ce9c80d-1d9e-4814-b601-255061f1b3d9\">Consumers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in several key wood markets <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"4ce9c80d-1d9e-4814-b601-255061f1b3d9\">are becoming more worried about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> sustainability, and the industry is supporting the development of national standards as well as the recognition of these internationally. However, New Zealand is not the only country with a plantation-style forestry industry; Chile, Brazil, Argentina, South Africa and Australia all have extensive plantings of fast-growing species (hardwood and softwood), and in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"74f6a015-852e-4b21-b7a7-46e2d5986d88\">northern hemisphere<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, Scandinavian countries have all expanded their forests or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"71740d1e-ca6e-44d5-8a64-1eceb813e576\">controlled their use in the interests of future production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Finally, in addition to competition from other wood producers, New Zealand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"5641c18f-6375-49c9-9955-631c7ab34286\">faces competition from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"07a9a61f-e89a-4e03-97ed-c49aad0941a0\">goods such as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> wood substitutes. These include steel framing for houses. This further underlines the necessity for globally competitive production and marketing strategies.</span></p><p><span>___________________________________________________________________</span></p><p><span>*pulp: wood which is crushed until soft enough to form the basis of paper</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1–6 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310004\" id=\"question-wrapper-310004\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Settlers realised that wooden houses were <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"977e59fc-4bf8-409a-99b3-8a72cf3c9cc8\">more dangerous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> than other types of structure.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310005\" id=\"question-wrapper-310005\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>During the 1800s, New Zealand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f4193369-8ed2-48ed-a9cf-9f8700b66590\">exported wood for use in boat-building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310006\" id=\"question-wrapper-310006\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Plantation-grown wood is generally better for construction than native forest wood.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310007\" id=\"question-wrapper-310007\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"48fd9639-99f2-4b4f-a701-fb1fb3541493\">Pine has a narrow range of uses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310008\" id=\"question-wrapper-310008\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Demand for housing in New Zealand is predicted to fall in the next few years.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310009\" id=\"question-wrapper-310009\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the future, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"25e708d8-1571-4693-aed3-6ac2a0c613e0\">expansion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of New Zealand’s wood industry <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"d47b4b68-f665-4b92-8f07-2e02f1be207b\">will depend on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> its exports.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310010\" id=\"question-wrapper-310010\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Apart from exchange rates, which factor has had a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"ae39bc8e-22c1-44f1-9f66-16a1c0e420f6\">negative impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> on New Zealand’s forestry exports?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">shipping costs</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310011\" id=\"question-wrapper-310011\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In which area of New Zealand’s economy does the forestry industry <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"e2df2216-a54e-42b8-927d-2781c594af9a\">rank third<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">export (sector)</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310012\" id=\"question-wrapper-310012\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the New Zealand forestry industry, what could be the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"a501f0d6-a2e5-4a36-a47e-cbfadaddbc46\">size of its workforce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> by 2025?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">60(,)000 (people)</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310013\" id=\"question-wrapper-310013\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What type of wood is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"71bb0d8e-28e0-4871-89e6-7b330c766ef9\">available in large quantities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> from renewable forests?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">softwood</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310014\" id=\"question-wrapper-310014\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which aspect of timber production are New Zealand’s main <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"4ce9c80d-1d9e-4814-b601-255061f1b3d9\">customers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> increasingly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"4ce9c80d-1d9e-4814-b601-255061f1b3d9\">concerned about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">sustainability</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310015\" id=\"question-wrapper-310015\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"74f6a015-852e-4b21-b7a7-46e2d5986d88\">nations above the equator<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> now rival New Zealand in the timber sector by taking steps to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"71740d1e-ca6e-44d5-8a64-1eceb813e576\">secure future wood supplies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Scandinavian countries</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310016\" id=\"question-wrapper-310016\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"07a9a61f-e89a-4e03-97ed-c49aad0941a0\">group of products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> is New Zealand’s forestry industry now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"5641c18f-6375-49c9-9955-631c7ab34286\">having to compete with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">wood substitutes</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f4193369-8ed2-48ed-a9cf-9f8700b66590","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"exported wood for use in boat-building","passagePhrase":"constructing sailing vessels ... huge amounts of this type of wood were sold to Australia and the UK"},{"uid":"25e708d8-1571-4693-aed3-6ac2a0c613e0","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"expansion","passagePhrase":"development"},{"uid":"d47b4b68-f665-4b92-8f07-2e02f1be207b","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"will depend on","passagePhrase":"is the key to the industry’s growth"},{"uid":"ae39bc8e-22c1-44f1-9f66-16a1c0e420f6","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"negative impact","passagePhrase":"affected by ... exchange fluctuations and shipping costs"},{"uid":"e2df2216-a54e-42b8-927d-2781c594af9a","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"rank third","passagePhrase":"third-largest"},{"uid":"a501f0d6-a2e5-4a36-a47e-cbfadaddbc46","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"size of its workforce","passagePhrase":"employing 60,000 people"},{"uid":"71bb0d8e-28e0-4871-89e6-7b330c766ef9","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"available in large quantities","passagePhrase":"has is its ability to source large quantities"},{"uid":"4ce9c80d-1d9e-4814-b601-255061f1b3d9","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"customers ... concerned about","passagePhrase":"Consumers ... are becoming more worried about"},{"uid":"74f6a015-852e-4b21-b7a7-46e2d5986d88","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"nations above the equator","passagePhrase":"northern hemisphere"},{"uid":"71740d1e-ca6e-44d5-8a64-1eceb813e576","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"secure future wood supplies","passagePhrase":"controlled their use in the interests of future production"},{"uid":"5641c18f-6375-49c9-9955-631c7ab34286","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"having to compete with","passagePhrase":"faces competition from"},{"uid":"07a9a61f-e89a-4e03-97ed-c49aad0941a0","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"group of products","passagePhrase":"goods such as"}]},"reading_u2_14":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>The Fascinating World of Attine Ants</span></b></p><p><i><span>Nicholas Wade examines leaf-cutter ants and their amazing agriculture</span></i></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>Leaf-cutting ants and their fungus ‘farm’ are a marvel of nature and perhaps the best-known example of symbiosis — the mutual dependence of two species. Ants cultivate a mushroom-like fungus in ‘farms’. Both the ants and their so-called ‘agriculture’ have been extensively studied over the years, but recent research has uncovered intriguing new findings.</span></p><p><span>Ants invented agriculture 50 million years before people did, and the leaf-cutters, members of the large attine ant family, practise the most sophisticated example of it. They grow their fungus in underground chambers that can reach the size of a football. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"6a03c5cb-3fb4-43c4-b577-d6fda02a7ce5\">single leaf-cutter nest may contain a thousand such chambers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, embedded in an underground metropolis up to 18 feet deep, and support a society of more than a million ants.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>These ant communities are the dominant plant-eaters of the Neotropics, the region comprising South and Central America, Mexico and the Caribbean. Biologists believe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"de2f9534-dbba-4675-b92e-12da80f3c7c0\">15 percent of the leaf production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of tropical forests <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"de2f9534-dbba-4675-b92e-12da80f3c7c0\">disappears down the nests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of leaf-cutter ants. In the nest, the leaves are shredded and added to the fungus, which digests the leaves and is in turn eaten by the ants. The attine ants’ achievement is remarkable because it allows them to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"3f000cc6-e71b-4018-ba50-50839b46b88f\">consume<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, courtesy of their mushroom’s digestive powers, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"3f000cc6-e71b-4018-ba50-50839b46b88f\">the harvest of tropical forests whose leaves are laden with poisonous chemicals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>There are more than 200 known species of the attine ant tribe, divided into 12 groups, or genera. The leaf-cutters use fresh vegetation; the other groups, known as the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a82c9fd3-e2c5-426e-97a1-1c190b4eadfe\">lower attines because their nests are smaller<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and their techniques more primitive, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"73dadd5a-9622-4fb7-a2df-2978d0155625\">feed their gardens with similar leaves that have fallen on the ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and insects that lie on the forest floor. Lower attine ants are all a similar size. However, leaf-cutter worker ants come in made-to-fit sizes — large ants to saw off leaves, medium ones to shred them, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"f3b885a6-76cc-480e-a719-ed295f1d0cf2\">miniature workers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> to seed them with fungus and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"6f8f3556-96b6-429f-a84f-c073cd2c4861\">clean off alien growths<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>In 1994, biologists from the United States Department of Agriculture analysed the DNA of ant fungi. They found that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e853c314-f7bb-4e37-aa19-567f3918795c\">the leaf-cutters’ fungus was </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 23\" data-uid=\"8d1303cc-8ca1-448f-b80f-4510b9e05f09 e853c314-f7bb-4e37-aa19-567f3918795c\">descended from a single pure strain</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"8d1303cc-8ca1-448f-b80f-4510b9e05f09\">, propagated for at least 23 million years</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. However, the fungi grown by lower attine ants fell into four different groups, as if the ants had domesticated wild fungi at least four times in evolutionary history. What could be driving these two patterns of fungus gardening — the pure clone cultivation of the leaf-cutters and the multiple varieties of the lower attines?</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>The answer has been suggested by Cameron Currie of the University of Toronto. The pure strain of fungus grown by the leaf-cutters, it seemed to him, resembled the single crops grown by humans to the exclusion of all others, such as potato growing. These ‘monocultures’, which lack the genetic diversity to respond to changing environmental threats, are particularly vulnerable to parasites — organisms that live and feed on their host, often causing harm. Currie felt there had to be a parasite in the ant-fungus system. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ba448d29-9dba-4c77-8b83-928d79018df0\">But a century of ant research had provided no evidence for his idea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Textbooks describe how leaf-cutter ants scrupulously weed their gardens of all foreign organisms. “People kept telling me the ants keep their gardens free of parasites,” said Currie. Nevertheless, after three years of sifting through attine ant gardens, Currie discovered several alien organisms, particularly a family of parasitic moulds called ‘Escovopsis’.</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> Escovopsis is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"bc6e5233-fffe-4545-861b-26644115e2b1\">deadly disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"bc6e5233-fffe-4545-861b-26644115e2b1\">devastate a fungus garden<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in a couple of days. It blooms like a white cloud which envelops the whole garden. Other ants won’t go near it, and the ants associated with the garden just <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"bc6e5233-fffe-4545-861b-26644115e2b1\">starve to death<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Evidently, the ants usually manage to keep Escovopsis and other parasites under control. Nevertheless, with any lapse in control Escovopsis will quickly burst forth. Although new leaf-cutter gardens start off free of Escovopsis, within two years some 60 percent become infected.</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>The discovery of Escovopsis’s role brings a new level of understanding to the evolution of the attine ants. In the last decade, evolutionary biologists have been increasingly aware of the role of parasites as driving forces in evolution. With Currie’s work, there is now a possible reason for the different varieties of fungus in the lower attine mushroom gardens — <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"df5b17f1-e0a7-44a8-ab19-6f1a606454fc\">to stay one step ahead of the relentless Escovopsis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Interestingly, the leaf-cutters had, in general, fewer alien moulds in their gardens than the lower attines, yet more Escovopsis infections. Clearly, the price they pay for cultivating a pure variety of fungus is a higher risk from Escovopsis.</span></p><p><b><span>H. </span></b><span>So how do attine ants keep this parasite under control? People have known for a hundred years that ants have a whitish growth on their body surface. It was thought to be wax but, after examining it under a microscope, Currie discovered a specialised patch on the ants’ bodies that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e6cb5bf6-72e1-4ab7-b211-ed890f5a1201\">harbours a particular kind of bacterium<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, one well known to the pharmaceutical industry and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e6cb5bf6-72e1-4ab7-b211-ed890f5a1201\">source of half the antibiotics used in medicine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. This bacterium is a potent poisoner of Escovopsis, inhibiting its growth and suppressing spore formation.</span></p><p><span>Astoundingly, the leaf-cutter ants are accomplishing feats beyond the power of humans: they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8c4b37a1-afbb-4d9a-bcca-b8b4ac5d038e\">growing a monocultural crop year after year without disaster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, and they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8c4b37a1-afbb-4d9a-bcca-b8b4ac5d038e\">using an antibiotic apparently so wisely that, unlike people, they are not provoking antibiotic resistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in the target disease-producing organism.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A–H. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310017\" id=\"question-wrapper-310017\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>two things at which leaf-cutter ants have succeeded but humans have failed.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310018\" id=\"question-wrapper-310018\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a comparison between the nests of leaf-cutter ants and lower attine ants.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310019\" id=\"question-wrapper-310019\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an assessment of the impact leaf-cutter ants have on their environment.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310020\" id=\"question-wrapper-310020\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the effect Escovopsis has on ant communities.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310021\" id=\"question-wrapper-310021\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the advantage for lower attine ants of growing a range of fungi.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310022\" id=\"question-wrapper-310022\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the discovery of the age of an attine-ant fungus.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Classify the following descriptions as relating to</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Leaf-cutting ants</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Lower attines</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Both leaf-cutting ants and lower attine ants</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310023\" id=\"question-wrapper-310023\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the use of dead vegetation to cultivate their fungus</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310024\" id=\"question-wrapper-310024\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"f3b885a6-76cc-480e-a719-ed295f1d0cf2\">very small ants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"6f8f3556-96b6-429f-a84f-c073cd2c4861\">that keep the fungus free of foreign organisms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310025\" id=\"question-wrapper-310025\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the ability to safely eat harmful plants</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310026\" id=\"question-wrapper-310026\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e853c314-f7bb-4e37-aa19-567f3918795c\">cultivation of a single fungus<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310027\" id=\"question-wrapper-310027\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"6a03c5cb-3fb4-43c4-b577-d6fda02a7ce5\">nest with a very large number of rooms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> for growing fungus</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 25 and 26 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310028\" id=\"question-wrapper-310028\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the writer say about Cameron Currie’s research?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. No previous work had been done in this area.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ba448d29-9dba-4c77-8b83-928d79018df0\">Earlier studies did not support his theory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Textbooks on this subject lacked specific detail.</li> <li>D. Currie’s initial theory had proven to be incorrect.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310029\" id=\"question-wrapper-310029\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Using a microscope, Currie was the first to discover that the body of attine ants</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. has a white covering.</li> <li>B. is covered in wax.</li> <li>C. is poisonous to humans.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e6cb5bf6-72e1-4ab7-b211-ed890f5a1201\">carry a microorganism valuable to humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"6a03c5cb-3fb4-43c4-b577-d6fda02a7ce5","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"nest with a very large number of rooms","passagePhrase":"single leaf-cutter nest may contain a thousand such chambers"},{"uid":"de2f9534-dbba-4675-b92e-12da80f3c7c0","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"15 percent of the leaf production ... disappears down the nests"},{"uid":"3f000cc6-e71b-4018-ba50-50839b46b88f","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"consume ... the harvest of tropical forests whose leaves are laden with poisonous chemicals"},{"uid":"a82c9fd3-e2c5-426e-97a1-1c190b4eadfe","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"lower attines because their nests are smaller"},{"uid":"73dadd5a-9622-4fb7-a2df-2978d0155625","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"feed their gardens with similar leaves that have fallen on the ground"},{"uid":"f3b885a6-76cc-480e-a719-ed295f1d0cf2","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"very small ants","passagePhrase":"miniature workers"},{"uid":"6f8f3556-96b6-429f-a84f-c073cd2c4861","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"that keep the fungus free of foreign organisms","passagePhrase":"clean off alien growths"},{"uid":"e853c314-f7bb-4e37-aa19-567f3918795c","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"cultivation of a single fungus","passagePhrase":"the leaf-cutters’ fungus was"},{"uid":"8d1303cc-8ca1-448f-b80f-4510b9e05f09 e853c314-f7bb-4e37-aa19-567f3918795c","qNum":"19 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"descended from a single pure strain"},{"uid":"8d1303cc-8ca1-448f-b80f-4510b9e05f09","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":", propagated for at least 23 million years"},{"uid":"ba448d29-9dba-4c77-8b83-928d79018df0","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"Earlier studies did not support his theory","passagePhrase":"But a century of ant research had provided no evidence for his idea"},{"uid":"bc6e5233-fffe-4545-861b-26644115e2b1","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"deadly disease ... devastate a fungus garden ... starve to death"},{"uid":"df5b17f1-e0a7-44a8-ab19-6f1a606454fc","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"to stay one step ahead of the relentless Escovopsis"},{"uid":"e6cb5bf6-72e1-4ab7-b211-ed890f5a1201","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"carry a microorganism valuable to humans","passagePhrase":"harbours a particular kind of bacterium ... source of half the antibiotics used in medicine"},{"uid":"8c4b37a1-afbb-4d9a-bcca-b8b4ac5d038e","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"growing a monocultural crop year after year without disaster ... using an antibiotic apparently so wisely that, unlike people, they are not provoking antibiotic resistance"}]},"reading_u2_15":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>What makes a musical expert?</span></b></p><p><i><span>How does someone </span></i><i><span>become expert</span></i><i><span> in music?</span></i></p><p><i><span>And is it really possible to have a talent for music?</span></i></p><p><span>Does that class of people acknowledged to be musical experts just have more of the same basic skills we are all endowed with? Research increasingly suggests otherwise. Instead, they appear to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"512f39fe-4b6c-440d-a232-5415ef32ca16\">possess<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"f09df710-8da5-465f-8963-384efe97fa7a\">neural structures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"512f39fe-4b6c-440d-a232-5415ef32ca16\">that are different from those of the rest of us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Are high levels of musical achievement simply the result of training and practice, or are they based on innate brain structure — what we refer to as talent? Talent can be defined as something that originates in genetic structures and that is identifiable by trained people who can recognize its existence before a person has achieved exceptional levels of performance. The emphasis on early identification means that to investigate it, we study the development of skills in children.</span></p><p><span>It is evident that some children acquire skills more rapidly than others: the age of onset for walking and talking varies widely, even between children in the same household. There may be genetic factors at work, but these are closely linked with other factors — with a presumably environmental component — such as motivation and family dynamics. Similar factors can influence musical development and can mask the contribution of genetics to musical ability.</span></p><p><span>Brain studies, so far, haven’t been of much use in sorting out the issues. Gottfried Schlaug at Harvard collected brain scans of individuals with absolute pitch* (AP) and showed that a region in the brain called the planum temporale is larger in these people than in others. This suggests that the planum is involved in AP, but it’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"634e690a-e743-440c-9743-5caab5689538\">not clear if it starts out larger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in people who eventually acquire AP, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"634e690a-e743-440c-9743-5caab5689538\">or if the acquisition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of AP <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"634e690a-e743-440c-9743-5caab5689538\">makes the planum increase in size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Results of research into the areas of the brain involved in skilled motor movement are more conclusive. Studies of violin players have shown that the region of the brain responsible for controlling the movement of the left hand (the hand that requires greater precision in violin playing) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"64765d54-e787-46a7-a7e1-a22b093626f5\">increases in size as a result of practice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. We do not know yet if the propensity for increase pre-exists in some people and not others.</span></p><p><span>The evidence against talent comes from research on how much training the experts do. Like experts in mathematics, chess, or sports, experts in music require lengthy periods of instruction and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"0885347b-e517-4256-b039-df9d1317d08a\">practice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. In several studies, the very best music students were found to have practised more than twice as much as the others. In another study, students were secretly divided into two groups based on teachers’ perceptions of their talent. Several years later, it was found that the students who achieved the highest performance ratings had practised the most, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"0885347b-e517-4256-b039-df9d1317d08a\">irrespective of which talent group they had been assigned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to, suggesting that practice does not merely correlate with achievement, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"0885347b-e517-4256-b039-df9d1317d08a\">causes it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Anders Ericsson, at Florida State University, approaches the topic of musical expertise as a general problem in cognitive psychology. He takes as a starting point the assumption that there are certain issues involved in becoming an expert at anything; that we can learn about musical expertise by studying expert chess players, athletes, artists, mathematicians, as well as the musicians themselves. The emerging picture from such studies is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8b06601d-75f6-4d91-b981-ed465f628c44\">ten thousand hours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of practice is required to achieve the level of mastery associated with being a world-class expert — in anything. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8b06601d-75f6-4d91-b981-ed465f628c44\">In study after study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, of composers, ice-skaters, concert pianists, chess players and master criminals, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8b06601d-75f6-4d91-b981-ed465f628c44\">this number<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8b06601d-75f6-4d91-b981-ed465f628c44\">comes up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> again and again. Someone would do this amount of practice if they practised, for example, roughly 20 hours a week for ten years. Of course, this <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"eee7f70c-a525-40ef-9794-94c00a5d0a70\">does not address<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> why some people do not seem to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"e4d84445-55ee-40db-872e-8102dee3945e\">get anywhere<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"722dff8d-34ca-489a-8f83-8e7ba8a834fc\">when they practise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, and why some people <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"e4d84445-55ee-40db-872e-8102dee3945e\">get more out of their </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"722dff8d-34ca-489a-8f83-8e7ba8a834fc e4d84445-55ee-40db-872e-8102dee3945e\">practice sessions</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> than others. But <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"425dbee4-6ab4-46f6-adf5-b6d37c1cae5d\">no one has yet found a case<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> in which true world-class expertise was accomplished in less time. It seems that it takes the brain this long to assimilate all that it needs to know to achieve true mastery.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3e485a50-2aa2-4e22-bc7c-d9e03dc9101c\">The ten-thousand-hour theory is consistent with what we know about how the brain learns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Learning requires the assimilation and consolidation of information in neural tissue. The more experiences we have with something, the stronger the memory/learning trace for that experience becomes. Although people differ in how long it takes them to consolidate information neurally, it remains true that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3e485a50-2aa2-4e22-bc7c-d9e03dc9101c\">increased practice leads to a greater number of neural traces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, which create stronger memory representations.</span></p><p><span>The classic rebuttal to this theory goes something like this: What about Mozart? I hear that he composed his first symphony at the age of four! First, there is a factual error here: Mozart <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5c759a31-6701-4dfc-be1a-6d4891f315fe\">did not </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5c759a31-6701-4dfc-be1a-6d4891f315fe 815c4b7e-32cb-4cbd-8bd6-9047ff9418d1\">write it</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5c759a31-6701-4dfc-be1a-6d4891f315fe\"> until he was</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> eight. Still, this is unusual, to say the least. However, this early work <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"b0ced630-f31a-45fb-ad8c-619ced3a1fdf\">received little acclaim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> and was not performed very often. In fact, the only reason we know about it is because the child who wrote it grew up to become Mozart. And Mozart <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e5f87896-5e68-4d9a-bfeb-0c0bf6c2d5d8\">had an expert teacher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> in his father, who was renowned as a teacher of musicians all over Europe. We do not know how much Mozart practised, but if he started at age two and worked thirty-two hours a week (quite possible, given that his father was a stern task-master) he would have made his ten thousand hours by the time he composed his first symphony. This does not mean that there are no <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"fee630e5-ab11-401c-a10d-97c28d367f20\">genetic factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> involved in Mozart’s greatness, but that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"fee630e5-ab11-401c-a10d-97c28d367f20\">inborn traits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> may not be the only cause.</span></p><p><span>___________________________________________________________________________</span></p><p><span>*individuals with absolute pitch: people who can identify or sing any musical note correctly without help</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310030\" id=\"question-wrapper-310030\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the first paragraph, the writer suggests that a talented musician is someone</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. who is aware of being set apart from other people.</li> <li>B. whose <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"f09df710-8da5-465f-8963-384efe97fa7a\">brain structure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"512f39fe-4b6c-440d-a232-5415ef32ca16\">is unlike that of other people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>C. who can perform extremely well in early childhood.</li> <li>D. whose essential skills are more varied than those of ordinary people.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310031\" id=\"question-wrapper-310031\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the writer, what is unclear about the findings of Gottfried Schlaug?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. which part of the brain is linked to a particular musical skill.</li> <li>B. which type of musical skill leads to the greatest change in the brain.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"634e690a-e743-440c-9743-5caab5689538\">whether a feature of the brain is a cause or an effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of a musical skill.</li> <li>D. whether the acquisition of a musical skill is easier for some people than others.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310032\" id=\"question-wrapper-310032\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the writer, what has been established by studies of violin players?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"64765d54-e787-46a7-a7e1-a22b093626f5\">Changes may occur in the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> following violin practice.</li> <li>B. Left-handed violinists have a different brain structure from other people.</li> <li>C. A violinist’s hand size is not due to practice but to genetic factors.</li> <li>D. Violinists are born with brains that have a particular structure.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310033\" id=\"question-wrapper-310033\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the writer, findings on the amount of practice done by expert musicians suggest that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"0885347b-e517-4256-b039-df9d1317d08a\">talent may have little to do with expertise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>B. practice may actually prevent the development of talent.</li> <li>C. talent may not be recognised by teachers.</li> <li>D. expertise may be related to quality of instruction.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310034\" id=\"question-wrapper-310034\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Anders Ericsson’s work with cognitive psychology has influenced other researchers.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310035\" id=\"question-wrapper-310035\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8b06601d-75f6-4d91-b981-ed465f628c44\">Different areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of expertise seem to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8b06601d-75f6-4d91-b981-ed465f628c44\">have one specific thing in common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310036\" id=\"question-wrapper-310036\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In order to be useful, practice must be carried out regularly every day.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310037\" id=\"question-wrapper-310037\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"722dff8d-34ca-489a-8f83-8e7ba8a834fc\">Practice by itself<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"eee7f70c-a525-40ef-9794-94c00a5d0a70\">guarantees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> that every learner can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"e4d84445-55ee-40db-872e-8102dee3945e\">become a world-level expert<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310038\" id=\"question-wrapper-310038\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"425dbee4-6ab4-46f6-adf5-b6d37c1cae5d\">Occasionally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, someone can become an expert at a global level with fewer than 10,000 hours’ practice.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310039\" id=\"question-wrapper-310039\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3e485a50-2aa2-4e22-bc7c-d9e03dc9101c\">Existing knowledge of learning and cognitive skills supports the importance of practice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, A-J, below. Write the correct letter, A-J, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. popular </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. artistic </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. completed </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. eight</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. tuition </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. encouragement </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. inherited </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. four</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. practice </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"J\"><span>J. two</span></p><hr><p><b><span>Mozart<br></span></b><span>The case of Mozart could be quoted as evidence against the 10,000-hour practice theory. However, the writer corrects this, stating that Mozart <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5c759a31-6701-4dfc-be1a-6d4891f315fe\">was actually<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> (37)______ when he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"815c4b7e-32cb-4cbd-8bd6-9047ff9418d1\">wrote his first symphony<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. This early work was not (38)______ and may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"50dc5994-fe4b-468d-9ab0-3b87e2198066\">of only academic interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. The writer then points out that the young Mozart received a lot of (39)______ from his father, so he may already have completed extensive practice before composing it. The case therefore supports the view that expertise is not solely the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"fee630e5-ab11-401c-a10d-97c28d367f20\">result of (40)______ characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310040\" id=\"question-wrapper-310040\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310041\" id=\"question-wrapper-310041\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310042\" id=\"question-wrapper-310042\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310043\" id=\"question-wrapper-310043\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"512f39fe-4b6c-440d-a232-5415ef32ca16","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"is unlike that of other people","passagePhrase":"possess ... that are different from those of the rest of us"},{"uid":"f09df710-8da5-465f-8963-384efe97fa7a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"brain structure","passagePhrase":"neural structures"},{"uid":"634e690a-e743-440c-9743-5caab5689538","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"whether a feature of the brain is a cause or an effect","passagePhrase":"not clear if it starts out larger ... or if the acquisition ... makes the planum increase in size"},{"uid":"64765d54-e787-46a7-a7e1-a22b093626f5","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Changes may occur in the brain","passagePhrase":"increases in size as a result of practice"},{"uid":"0885347b-e517-4256-b039-df9d1317d08a","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"talent may have little to do with expertise","passagePhrase":"practice ... irrespective of which talent group they had been assigned ... causes it"},{"uid":"8b06601d-75f6-4d91-b981-ed465f628c44","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Different areas ... have one specific thing in common","passagePhrase":"ten thousand hours ... In study after study ... this number ... comes up"},{"uid":"e4d84445-55ee-40db-872e-8102dee3945e","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"become a world-level expert","passagePhrase":"get anywhere ... get more out of their"},{"uid":"722dff8d-34ca-489a-8f83-8e7ba8a834fc","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Practice by itself","passagePhrase":"when they practise"},{"uid":"722dff8d-34ca-489a-8f83-8e7ba8a834fc e4d84445-55ee-40db-872e-8102dee3945e","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"practice sessions"},{"uid":"3e485a50-2aa2-4e22-bc7c-d9e03dc9101c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Existing knowledge of learning and cognitive skills supports the importance of practice","passagePhrase":"The ten-thousand-hour theory is consistent with what we know about how the brain learns ... increased practice leads to a greater number of neural traces"},{"uid":"5c759a31-6701-4dfc-be1a-6d4891f315fe","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"was actually","passagePhrase":"did not ... until he was"},{"uid":"5c759a31-6701-4dfc-be1a-6d4891f315fe 815c4b7e-32cb-4cbd-8bd6-9047ff9418d1","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"write it"},{"uid":"b0ced630-f31a-45fb-ad8c-619ced3a1fdf","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"received little acclaim"},{"uid":"e5f87896-5e68-4d9a-bfeb-0c0bf6c2d5d8","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"had an expert teacher"},{"uid":"fee630e5-ab11-401c-a10d-97c28d367f20","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"result of (40)______ characteristics","passagePhrase":"genetic factors ... inborn traits"},{"uid":"815c4b7e-32cb-4cbd-8bd6-9047ff9418d1","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"wrote his first symphony","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"50dc5994-fe4b-468d-9ab0-3b87e2198066","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"of only academic interest","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_16":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Origin of Paper</span></b></p><p><span>The word paper derives from the Greek term for the ancient Egyptian writing material called papyrus. In about 2400 BC, the Egyptians discovered how to make a writing surface out of papyrus, a type of reed that grows along waterways in southern Europe and North Africa. The Egyptians cut the plant into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"6fbec1d3-a519-4005-b814-b724066fd59c\">strips<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> which they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"205f9a78-f7f4-4964-a057-81d2d2cbc1ab\">softened in water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. Papyrus was cross-woven into a mat and then pounded into a hard, thin sheet.</span></p><p><span>As the papyrus plant requires subtropical conditions to grow, papyrus was not much used in Europe at that time; instead, the main material used for writing was parchment. This was made from animal skin and was extremely expensive. In fact, it has been estimated that a single book written on parchment required the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"8b2c67f9-9b61-43aa-bb65-8f8f849688f0\">skins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of 300 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"dd1255c5-8567-4967-9143-88492f94cada\">sheep<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. The skins had to be specially prepared by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"36ace8a7-3520-48a3-ba8a-65318c43a1d0\">drying them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and they were then stretched on a special frame. It is not known when parchment was first introduced, but it was the main writing material in Europe for hundreds of years.</span></p><p><span>Paper—made from pulp, rags and fibres of plants—seems to have been invented in China and is considered to be one of the Four Great Inventions of Ancient China. In 105 AD, under the Han Dynasty emperor Ho-Ti, a government official in China named Ts’ai Lun was the first to start a papermaking industry. Ts’ai Lun seems to have made his paper by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"8b419e18-d2ba-4ae1-9810-ff485ff38cac\">mixing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> finely chopped <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9b430e44-6e56-43e3-9e5d-1798ecc55726\">mulberry bark<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> and hemp rags with water, mashing the mixture flat with a stone mortar, and then pressing out the water and letting it dry in the sun. He may have based his idea on bark cloth, which was very common in China and also made from mulberry.</span></p><p><span>Previously, during the Shang (1600–1050 BC) and Zhou (1050–256 BC) dynasties of Ancient China, documents were ordinarily written on bone or bamboo (on tablets or bamboo strips bound and rolled together into scrolls), making them very heavy and awkward to transport. The light material of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"b86287aa-2bb6-4565-bb5c-4f169b026ce8\">silk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"8095a291-b452-4a70-949f-7a58b494ff79\">sometimes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"e2b3556c-6223-45c6-8864-08f2ec6de87d\">used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, but was normally too expensive to consider. When paper was first invented, it was used for purposes of wrapping or padding protection for delicate bronze mirrors. Although paper for writing became popular by the 3rd century AD, it continued to be used for wrapping and other purposes.</span></p><p><span>During the Tang Dynasty (618–907 AD) paper was folded and sewn into square bags to preserve the flavour of tea. During the same period, according to a written account, tea was served from baskets with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"4ce2a2bf-a311-4ca2-9b30-28b3de64629a\">multi-coloured paper cups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> and paper napkins of different sizes and shapes. During the Chinese Song Dynasty (960–1279 AD) not only did the government produce the world’s first known printed paper money, or banknote, but paper money bestowed as gifts was wrapped in special paper envelopes.</span></p><p><span>Paper spread widely outside China; other Asian cultures, even after seeing paper, could not make it themselves. Instruction in the manufacturing process was required, and the Chinese were reluctant to share their secrets. It made its true push westward in 751 AD when the Tang Dynasty was at war with the Islamic world. During a battle on the banks of the Talas River, a Chinese caravan was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"70305375-e746-4d6a-b479-5dfe11c67b49\">captured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> which happened to include <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f94c1f91-ba44-44af-8739-32251d7c4e02\">several papermakers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. They were <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5 9\" data-uid=\"12909a4e-8b70-4683-916e-0d2a759bbe40 859d4300-e3dd-40fb-8d3e-99e514d87896\">taken away to Samarkand</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, which was a good place to make paper because it had an abundant supply of hemp and flax. Samarkanders changed the technology of manufacturing paper. They began to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"ad5557a1-ecfa-4e83-aa0e-b79158ebb8a6\">prepare it in stone mills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> and Samarkand became an important papermaking centre.</span></p><p><span>The rudimentary and laborious process of papermaking was refined, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"d1fe835b-0ef1-4b0b-8ad3-cc081e6361be\">bulk manufacturing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> of paper began in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"7d3dc3f7-0094-43d5-b4f8-e51b8a54f310\">Iran<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, where they invented a method to make a thicker sheet of paper, which helped transform papermaking from an art into an important business.</span></p><p><span>Gradually papermakers made their way further west through the Arab world—to Baghdad, Damascus and Cairo. Finally, when the Moors from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"e8d28460-369c-461c-999c-9bc8ddca6e24\">North Africa<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> invaded Spain and Portugal, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"2020207b-c5f0-4e4d-95f6-11bc5ca368fe\">brought the technology with them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> and so it was that papermaking <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"dc686148-f8b8-4eeb-9ac8-e376a149646e\">entered Europe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in the 12th century.</span></p><p><span>In Europe, the preferred medium for the artists and literati of the time was still the smooth and lustrous parchment. The notion of paper being used as a practical everyday item did not occur until the 15th century, when Johannes Gutenberg <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"323918ed-344e-48cd-bebb-104009337a58\">perfected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> movable-type printing, which included the use of metal moulds and alloys, a special press, and oil-based inks, allowing the mass production of printed books. The birth of the modern paper and printing industry is commonly marked from this date.</span></p><p><span>Printing technology rapidly developed and created an ever-increasing demand for paper. The early European papers were made from recycled cotton and linen—and a huge trade quickly developed around the trading of old rags. It is said that the disease known as the Black Death entered England from Europe on these old rags. Yet soon this source became <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"011dc846-bf66-4afd-9119-e50219cc2dbd\">insufficient<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> and some curious attempts were made to find <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b04fcfb8-f58b-41e2-8526-a5b9a709fe88\">new materials<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. Experiments with fibres such as straw, cabbage, wasp nests and finally wood resulted in inexpensive—and replaceable—materials for papermaking. Today, the long, soft fibres of softwoods such as spruce have become the most suitable source of pulp for the mass production of paper.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the table below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1- 6 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The Development of Paper</span></b></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"859d4300-e3dd-40fb-8d3e-99e514d87896\">Place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Date of introduction</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Materials used</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Method of production</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Egypt</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>about 2400 BC</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>a plant called papyrus</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(1)______ of the plant were softened in water, woven and pounded</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Europe</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>unknown</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>parchment made from the skin of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"dd1255c5-8567-4967-9143-88492f94cada\">animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> such as (2)______</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>skin was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"36ace8a7-3520-48a3-ba8a-65318c43a1d0\">dried<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and (3)______</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>China</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>105 AD</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(4)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9b430e44-6e56-43e3-9e5d-1798ecc55726\">of a mulberry tree<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> and hemp rags</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>ingredients were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"8b419e18-d2ba-4ae1-9810-ff485ff38cac\">mixed with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> water, pressed and put outside in the sun</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(5)______</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>751 AD</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>flax and hemp</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"ad5557a1-ecfa-4e83-aa0e-b79158ebb8a6\">mills made of (6<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>)_____ were used</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310044\" id=\"question-wrapper-310044\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">strips</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310045\" id=\"question-wrapper-310045\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">sheep</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310046\" id=\"question-wrapper-310046\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">stretched</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310047\" id=\"question-wrapper-310047\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">bark</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310048\" id=\"question-wrapper-310048\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Samarkand</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310049\" id=\"question-wrapper-310049\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">stone</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet, write</p> <p>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</p> <p>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</p> <p>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310050\" id=\"question-wrapper-310050\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In Ancient China, writing was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"8095a291-b452-4a70-949f-7a58b494ff79\">occasionally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"e2b3556c-6223-45c6-8864-08f2ec6de87d\">done on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"b86287aa-2bb6-4565-bb5c-4f169b026ce8\">silk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310051\" id=\"question-wrapper-310051\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"4ce2a2bf-a311-4ca2-9b30-28b3de64629a\">Coloured paper<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> was invented during the Tang Dynasty.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310052\" id=\"question-wrapper-310052\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f94c1f91-ba44-44af-8739-32251d7c4e02\">Papermakers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> from Samarkand were captured by the Chinese.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310053\" id=\"question-wrapper-310053\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Iran was the first place where paper was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"d1fe835b-0ef1-4b0b-8ad3-cc081e6361be\">produced in large quantities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310054\" id=\"question-wrapper-310054\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Papermaking skills were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"dc686148-f8b8-4eeb-9ac8-e376a149646e\">brought to Europe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"2020207b-c5f0-4e4d-95f6-11bc5ca368fe\">via<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> North Africa.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310055\" id=\"question-wrapper-310055\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>When Gutenberg <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"323918ed-344e-48cd-bebb-104009337a58\">invented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> movable-type printing, the supplies needed for making paper were very expensive.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310056\" id=\"question-wrapper-310056\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>European papermakers searched for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b04fcfb8-f58b-41e2-8526-a5b9a709fe88\">alternative raw supplies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> because rags were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"011dc846-bf66-4afd-9119-e50219cc2dbd\">difficult to transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"6fbec1d3-a519-4005-b814-b724066fd59c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"strips"},{"uid":"205f9a78-f7f4-4964-a057-81d2d2cbc1ab","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"softened in water"},{"uid":"8b2c67f9-9b61-43aa-bb65-8f8f849688f0","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"skins"},{"uid":"dd1255c5-8567-4967-9143-88492f94cada","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"animals","passagePhrase":"sheep"},{"uid":"36ace8a7-3520-48a3-ba8a-65318c43a1d0","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"dried","passagePhrase":"drying them"},{"uid":"8b419e18-d2ba-4ae1-9810-ff485ff38cac","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"mixed with","passagePhrase":"mixing"},{"uid":"9b430e44-6e56-43e3-9e5d-1798ecc55726","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"of a mulberry tree","passagePhrase":"mulberry bark"},{"uid":"b86287aa-2bb6-4565-bb5c-4f169b026ce8","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"silk","passagePhrase":"silk"},{"uid":"8095a291-b452-4a70-949f-7a58b494ff79","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"occasionally","passagePhrase":"sometimes"},{"uid":"e2b3556c-6223-45c6-8864-08f2ec6de87d","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"done on","passagePhrase":"used"},{"uid":"4ce2a2bf-a311-4ca2-9b30-28b3de64629a","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Coloured paper","passagePhrase":"multi-coloured paper cups"},{"uid":"70305375-e746-4d6a-b479-5dfe11c67b49","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"captured"},{"uid":"f94c1f91-ba44-44af-8739-32251d7c4e02","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Papermakers","passagePhrase":"several papermakers"},{"uid":"12909a4e-8b70-4683-916e-0d2a759bbe40 859d4300-e3dd-40fb-8d3e-99e514d87896","qNum":"5 9","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"taken away to Samarkand"},{"uid":"ad5557a1-ecfa-4e83-aa0e-b79158ebb8a6","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"mills made of (6","passagePhrase":"prepare it in stone mills"},{"uid":"d1fe835b-0ef1-4b0b-8ad3-cc081e6361be","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"produced in large quantities","passagePhrase":"bulk manufacturing"},{"uid":"7d3dc3f7-0094-43d5-b4f8-e51b8a54f310","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Iran"},{"uid":"e8d28460-369c-461c-999c-9bc8ddca6e24","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"North Africa"},{"uid":"2020207b-c5f0-4e4d-95f6-11bc5ca368fe","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"via","passagePhrase":"brought the technology with them"},{"uid":"dc686148-f8b8-4eeb-9ac8-e376a149646e","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"brought to Europe","passagePhrase":"entered Europe"},{"uid":"323918ed-344e-48cd-bebb-104009337a58","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"invented","passagePhrase":"perfected"},{"uid":"011dc846-bf66-4afd-9119-e50219cc2dbd","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"difficult to transport","passagePhrase":"insufficient"},{"uid":"b04fcfb8-f58b-41e2-8526-a5b9a709fe88","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"alternative raw supplies","passagePhrase":"new materials"},{"uid":"859d4300-e3dd-40fb-8d3e-99e514d87896","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Place","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_17":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>The plan to bring an asteroid to Earth</span></b></p><p><i><span>Moving in orbit around our Sun are millions of rocks known as asteroids.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Now scientists have plans to capture one.</span></i></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>A. </span></b><span>Send a robot into space, catch an asteroid and bring it back to Earth’s orbit. This, say scientists and engineers at the California Institute of Technology (Caltech), could be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"0b5f3e2a-048e-412e-aa08-8dbdf795a0f7\">feasible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. A four-day workshop was dedicated to investigating the feasibility of capturing a near-Earth asteroid, bringing it closer to our planet and using it as a base for future manned space-flight missions.</span></p><p><span>This is not something the scientists are imagining could be done someday in the future. It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"bbd5556b-208a-46a6-aff1-372d6a3df70a\">possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> with the technology we have today and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"bbd5556b-208a-46a6-aff1-372d6a3df70a\">could be accomplished<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> within a decade. A robotic probe could anchor to an asteroid with simple magnets or grab it with specialised claws. Alternatively, a large spacecraft could use its gravitational field to shift the orbit of a larger asteroid, sending it towards Earth.</span></p><p><span>‘Once you get over the initial reaction — </span><i><span>You want to do what?! </span></i><span>— it actually starts to seem like a reasonable idea,’ says engineer John Brophy, who helped organise the workshop. In fact, many of these ideas have been on the drawing board for years as part of NASA’s planetary-defence programme against large space-based objects that might threaten Earth. And there’s no shortage of potential targets: NASA estimates there are 19,500 asteroids at least 100 metres wide within 45 million kilometres of Earth.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span>Though rearranging the heavens may seem an excessive undertaking, this US mission has its merits. The US already has plans to send astronauts to a near-Earth asteroid, a mission that would mean confining them in a tiny capsule for three to six months and would involve all the risks of a deep-space voyage. Instead, robots could bring an asteroid close enough for them to get there in just a month.</span></p><p><span>An asteroid would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"2deb6664-7d60-4fb5-b025-e77871870c75\">provide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> a stationary <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"f66f5393-cdfb-4d0d-9e08-d110a4d1cec6\">base from which to launch missions further into space<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. There are several advantages to this. For one, launching missions carrying materials from Earth requires a lot of power, fuel and, consequently, money, because of our planet’s strong <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"0df86150-8969-4458-847b-a447cbcd6ab1\">force of gravity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. Since this would be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"ee858589-fe7c-43b0-a0b7-4dad3872abde\">far weaker<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> on an asteroid, materials <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9e39d401-ecff-4e46-93c9-379837bfdc23\">mined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> there could be more easily taken off the asteroid and shuttled around the solar system.</span></p><p><span>Many asteroids have a lot to offer. Some are rich in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"c203fdb6-56ca-4879-9066-aa04b42b4209\">metals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, which can be mined and used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"142aa85d-887c-41b2-a2c0-8efb91fb36fc\">build space-based habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"21a1fef1-7b8c-48ba-b5c6-aed89ab014cb\">brought back to Earth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Others are up to one-quarter <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"2aef75cc-8cd5-48bc-bd3e-b97f15226151\">water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, which could be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"d6cb6d55-b68f-4be7-b460-c0009dc0094f\">used for life support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> or broken down into hydrogen and oxygen to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 26\" data-uid=\"7cfad6fc-8399-4a92-b0bd-527358b6c150 9e39d401-ecff-4e46-93c9-379837bfdc23\">make fuel</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Astronomers would also have the chance to get a close-up look at one of the solar system’s earliest relics, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9e39d401-ecff-4e46-93c9-379837bfdc23\">generating important scientific data<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. ‘Executing the asteroid-retrieval plan would help demonstrate and greatly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"d0362d5e-eed0-4cdf-b0c4-b2741e760b71\">expand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> mankind’s space-based <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"d0362d5e-eed0-4cdf-b0c4-b2741e760b71\">engineering capabilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>,’ says engineer Louis Friedman, another co-organiser of the Caltech workshop. For instance, the mission would teach engineers how to capture an unco-operative target, which could be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"6621c7f2-9698-466a-9b2e-cfc0b078d0e0\">useful practice for planetary-defence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> missions in the event of a threat from a meteoroid or comet approaching our planet,’ he adds.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span>Former astronaut Rusty Schweickart, co-founder of the B612 Foundation, an organisation dedicated to protecting Earth from asteroid strikes, points out that although it would be technically feasible, shifting such a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"87c06478-79d2-4bf1-a3b7-062d0c7989f0\">hefty and substantial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> target would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"94738e21-fc6b-410e-bfc2-19bcc5e6971a\">not be easy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>: ‘You’re moving the largest mother-lode imaginable,’ he says.</span></p><p><span>Engineers would need to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"0ceffbae-dd7d-41fc-b0c0-92d68da73a96\">absolutely certain they could control<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> such a potentially dangerous object. ‘It’s the opposite of planetary-defence; if you do something wrong you have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"958dd5ad-2137-4ca1-996c-55ab99a3e6a5\">Tunguska event<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>,’ says engineer Marco Tantardini from the Planetary Society, referring to the powerful 1908 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"958dd5ad-2137-4ca1-996c-55ab99a3e6a5\">explosion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> above a remote Russian region thought to have been caused by a meteoroid or comet.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span>Still, these obstacles only add to the appeal of the project for engineers, who love to go over every potential difficulty in order to solve it. And if the challenges posed by a large asteroid seem too daunting, researchers could always <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3df839de-2dd6-4ca5-ae88-f803c8218dd0\">start with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c8668637-d59d-4d1d-867b-7be376fd1009\">smaller asteroid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, perhaps two to ten metres across. Last year, Brophy helped conduct a study to look at the feasibility of bringing a two-metre, 1 000-kilogram asteroid — of which there might conceivably be millions — to the International Space Station. The study suggested the asteroid could be captured robotically in something as simple as a large bag. Of course, such a small object might not have the same emotional impact as a larger target. ‘NASA <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"569ba8e2-ddac-45d4-a1d6-96aeae7d60a9\">isn’t going to want to go to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> something that is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ef1f9c76-445a-4edf-b396-b2ade99676e0\">smaller than our spaceships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>,’ says engineer Dan Mazanek from NASA’s Langley Research Center.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>E. </span></b><span>No matter the size of the asteroid, these plans would require hefty investments. Even capturing a small asteroid would consume at least a billion dollars. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5102ba38-9ed7-484a-9c02-70b2e4b85397\">Convincing taxpayers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to foot such a bill could be difficult. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5102ba38-9ed7-484a-9c02-70b2e4b85397\">private industry might be interested<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in getting involved. One possibility would be to push the asteroid into near-Earth orbit and then invite anyone who wants to develop the capabilities to reach and mine the object.</span></p><p><span>However, although the undertaking might be scientifically exciting and provide great insight into the solar system’s formation, this is not enough on its own to justify the expense of bringing an asteroid to Earth. Investigations of asteroids can be done much <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"7827ad59-932a-4be3-a707-9056675ad230\">more cheaply<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> with an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"a69012d5-0c96-4464-9582-119bf4adadbb\">unmanned spacecraft<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, says chemist Joseph A. Nuth from NASA’s Goddard Space Flight Center. According to Brophy, ultimately we would be working towards bringing an asteroid closer to Earth in order to help humanity move out into the solar system.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has five sections, A–E. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"0ceffbae-dd7d-41fc-b0c0-92d68da73a96\">need for skill and care<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. Choosing the richest asteroid</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. The safest way to protect an asteroid</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5102ba38-9ed7-484a-9c02-70b2e4b85397\">Obtaining support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> for the project</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. An <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"bbd5556b-208a-46a6-aff1-372d6a3df70a\">achievable goal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"0b5f3e2a-048e-412e-aa08-8dbdf795a0f7\">not an impossible dream<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. The need for global cooperation</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3df839de-2dd6-4ca5-ae88-f803c8218dd0\">Beginning with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c8668637-d59d-4d1d-867b-7be376fd1009\">less challenging task<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9e39d401-ecff-4e46-93c9-379837bfdc23\">Practical, economic and research justifications<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310057\" id=\"question-wrapper-310057\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310058\" id=\"question-wrapper-310058\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310059\" id=\"question-wrapper-310059\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310060\" id=\"question-wrapper-310060\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310061\" id=\"question-wrapper-310061\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following experts (Questions 19 – 22) and the list of statements below. Match each expert with the correct statement, A–G. Write the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 19 – 22 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of statements</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. A mistake could have serious consequences for Earth.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. It might be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"569ba8e2-ddac-45d4-a1d6-96aeae7d60a9\">difficult to arouse interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in an asteroid of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ef1f9c76-445a-4edf-b396-b2ade99676e0\">limited size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. The project could be an early step in space exploration.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. An asteroid’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"87c06478-79d2-4bf1-a3b7-062d0c7989f0\">weight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> makes the project <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"94738e21-fc6b-410e-bfc2-19bcc5e6971a\">extremely challenging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"d0362d5e-eed0-4cdf-b0c4-b2741e760b71\">skill gained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> could be useful for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"6621c7f2-9698-466a-9b2e-cfc0b078d0e0\">defending<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> Earth from future space threats.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. An asteroid could be a useful landing place for a spaceship.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. Capturing an asteroid would be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"7827ad59-932a-4be3-a707-9056675ad230\">less cost-effective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> than using a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"a69012d5-0c96-4464-9582-119bf4adadbb\">robotic spacecraft<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310062\" id=\"question-wrapper-310062\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Louis Friedman</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310063\" id=\"question-wrapper-310063\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Rusty Schweickart</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310064\" id=\"question-wrapper-310064\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Dan Mazanek</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310065\" id=\"question-wrapper-310065\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Joseph A. Nuth</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23 – 26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The merits of the US mission</span></b></p><p><span>Capture of an asteroid would reduce the time that astronauts travelling to it needed to spend in space. An asteroid could also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"2deb6664-7d60-4fb5-b025-e77871870c75\">act as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> a (23)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"f66f5393-cdfb-4d0d-9e08-d110a4d1cec6\">for further space travel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> and exploration. The fact that an asteroid would have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"ee858589-fe7c-43b0-a0b7-4dad3872abde\">weaker<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> (24)______ would allow easier movement of resources.</span></p><p><span>These resources include (25)______ which could be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"142aa85d-887c-41b2-a2c0-8efb91fb36fc\">used in space<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> or on Earth, and (26)______ which could be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"d6cb6d55-b68f-4be7-b460-c0009dc0094f\">consumed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> or used as a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"7cfad6fc-8399-4a92-b0bd-527358b6c150\">source of power<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The mission could provide data on the history of our Sun and planets. It could also be good practice if there was a threat to Earth from a body from space.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310066\" id=\"question-wrapper-310066\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">base</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310067\" id=\"question-wrapper-310067\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">gravity</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310068\" id=\"question-wrapper-310068\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">metals</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310069\" id=\"question-wrapper-310069\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">water</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0b5f3e2a-048e-412e-aa08-8dbdf795a0f7","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"not an impossible dream","passagePhrase":"feasible"},{"uid":"bbd5556b-208a-46a6-aff1-372d6a3df70a","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"achievable goal","passagePhrase":"possible ... could be accomplished"},{"uid":"2deb6664-7d60-4fb5-b025-e77871870c75","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"act as","passagePhrase":"provide"},{"uid":"f66f5393-cdfb-4d0d-9e08-d110a4d1cec6","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"for further space travel","passagePhrase":"base from which to launch missions further into space"},{"uid":"0df86150-8969-4458-847b-a447cbcd6ab1","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"force of gravity"},{"uid":"ee858589-fe7c-43b0-a0b7-4dad3872abde","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"weaker","passagePhrase":"far weaker"},{"uid":"9e39d401-ecff-4e46-93c9-379837bfdc23","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Practical, economic and research justifications","passagePhrase":"mined ... generating important scientific data"},{"uid":"c203fdb6-56ca-4879-9066-aa04b42b4209","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"metals"},{"uid":"142aa85d-887c-41b2-a2c0-8efb91fb36fc","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"used in space","passagePhrase":"build space-based habitats"},{"uid":"21a1fef1-7b8c-48ba-b5c6-aed89ab014cb","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"brought back to Earth"},{"uid":"2aef75cc-8cd5-48bc-bd3e-b97f15226151","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"water"},{"uid":"d6cb6d55-b68f-4be7-b460-c0009dc0094f","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"consumed","passagePhrase":"used for life support"},{"uid":"7cfad6fc-8399-4a92-b0bd-527358b6c150 9e39d401-ecff-4e46-93c9-379837bfdc23","qNum":"15 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"make fuel"},{"uid":"d0362d5e-eed0-4cdf-b0c4-b2741e760b71","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"skill gained","passagePhrase":"expand ... engineering capabilities"},{"uid":"6621c7f2-9698-466a-9b2e-cfc0b078d0e0","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"defending","passagePhrase":"useful practice for planetary-defence"},{"uid":"87c06478-79d2-4bf1-a3b7-062d0c7989f0","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"weight","passagePhrase":"hefty and substantial"},{"uid":"94738e21-fc6b-410e-bfc2-19bcc5e6971a","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"extremely challenging","passagePhrase":"not be easy"},{"uid":"0ceffbae-dd7d-41fc-b0c0-92d68da73a96","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"need for skill and care","passagePhrase":"absolutely certain they could control"},{"uid":"958dd5ad-2137-4ca1-996c-55ab99a3e6a5","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Tunguska event ... explosion"},{"uid":"3df839de-2dd6-4ca5-ae88-f803c8218dd0","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Beginning with","passagePhrase":"start with"},{"uid":"c8668637-d59d-4d1d-867b-7be376fd1009","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"less challenging task","passagePhrase":"smaller asteroid"},{"uid":"569ba8e2-ddac-45d4-a1d6-96aeae7d60a9","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"difficult to arouse interest","passagePhrase":"isn’t going to want to go to"},{"uid":"ef1f9c76-445a-4edf-b396-b2ade99676e0","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"limited size","passagePhrase":"smaller than our spaceships"},{"uid":"5102ba38-9ed7-484a-9c02-70b2e4b85397","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Obtaining support","passagePhrase":"Convincing taxpayers ... private industry might be interested"},{"uid":"7827ad59-932a-4be3-a707-9056675ad230","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"less cost-effective","passagePhrase":"more cheaply"},{"uid":"a69012d5-0c96-4464-9582-119bf4adadbb","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"robotic spacecraft","passagePhrase":"unmanned spacecraft"},{"uid":"7cfad6fc-8399-4a92-b0bd-527358b6c150","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"source of power","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_18":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Art of Deception</span></b></p><p><i><span>Do tiny changes of facial expression show whether someone is telling lies?</span></i></p><p><span>Forty years ago, the research psychologist Dr Paul Ekman was addressing a group of young <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"9d85715d-da1f-4763-ba69-1eb11c9ad9ff\">psychiatrists in training<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> when he was asked a question, the answer to which has kept him busy ever since. Suppose the group wanted to know whether a particular patient who swears they are telling the truth really is. They look and sound sincere. So here is the question: is there any way you can be sure they are telling the truth? Ekman did not know the answer then, but he wanted to find out.</span></p><p><span>As part of his research, he had already filmed a series of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"52dd2d62-ac66-4db8-a5bb-4d11352d344c\">12-minute interviews<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> with psychiatric patients. In a subsequent conversation, one of the patients told him that she had lied to him. So Ekman sat and looked at the film but saw nothing noteworthy. Then he slowed it down and looked again. Then he slowed it down even further. And suddenly, there, across just two frames of the film, he saw it: an intense expression of extreme anguish. It lasted less than a fifteenth of a second, but once he had spotted the first expression, he soon found three more examples in that same interview. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"e8dde727-cfb8-475a-9d00-0b9684ff15e7\">termed his discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> “micro-expressions”: very rapid, intense demonstrations of emotion that the subject intended to conceal.</span></p><p><span>Over the course of the next four decades, Ekman successfully demonstrated a proposition first suggested by Charles Darwin: that the ways in which we express rage, disgust, contempt, fear, surprise, happiness and sadness are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"0652dc26-d2fa-4ce9-80e8-7f69e07f1fa2\">universal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. The facial muscles triggered by those seven basic emotions are, he has shown, essentially <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"2572580a-ea71-4d28-b582-119dca9af72a\">standard, regardless of language and culture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, from the US to Japan and Brazil to Papua New Guinea. What is more, expressions of emotion are impossible to suppress and, particularly when we are lying, micro-expressions of powerfully felt emotions will inevitably flit across our face before we get the chance to stop them.</span></p><p><span>Fortunately for liars, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"2a021cb2-6a83-4c55-84c3-1cae398541c7\">most people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> will fail to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9ee756f9-64d0-4067-af44-bed4cbaefd07\">spot these fleeting signals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of inner torment. Of the 15,000 Ekman has tested, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5bd7d7f0-3a30-4971-9e5a-130e7f3a468b\">only 50 people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, whom he calls “naturals”, have been able to do it. But given a little more training, Ekman says, almost anyone can develop the skill. He should know: since these tests were completed in the mid-1980s and the first publication of his research, he has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"0a982eb1-4124-4914-bf5d-1c43cbfaf2c9\">called in by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> the FBI and CIA (among <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"0a982eb1-4124-4914-bf5d-1c43cbfaf2c9\">countless<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> more law enforcement and other agencies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"0a982eb1-4124-4914-bf5d-1c43cbfaf2c9\">around the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>), not just to solve cases, but to teach them how to use his technique for themselves. He has held workshops for defence and prosecution lawyers, health professionals, even jealous spouses, all of them wanting to know exactly when someone is not being 100 percent candid.</span></p><p><span>Most recently, Ekman’s research has resulted in a new television series about the exploits of the fictional Dr Cal Lightman, a scientist who studies involuntary body language to discover not only if you are lying, but why you might have been motivated to do so. According to the publicity blurb, Lightman is a human lie detector, even more accurate than a polygraph test. Ekman concedes he was sceptical when the producer first approached him with the idea of turning his life’s work into a TV series, and initially would have stopped the project if he could. In particular, he was fearful that the show would exaggerate the effectiveness of his techniques and create the quite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"76986eac-2421-4145-b1b8-687da69918e0\">inaccurate impression<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8e571dcd-a916-4b9d-80a0-dc3962ba6ee4\">among audiences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> that criminals could no longer hope to get away with lying. In the worst-case scenario, he was concerned about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"c2cb946e-56d3-4efa-a81b-9cad5ef9c00b\">unfair convictions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>—that one day someone not properly trained in his techniques might be sitting on a jury and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"c2cb946e-56d3-4efa-a81b-9cad5ef9c00b\">wrongly find someone guilty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of a crime simply on the basis of a television programme.</span></p><p><span>In the end, though, he was won over because the series is unusual in several respects. It is the first time, as far as Ekman is aware, that a commercial TV drama has been based on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"3e0a4078-a2f7-4b1c-9df1-4588eb849288\">work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"300dfaf8-ef13-4101-b55e-665d546c34a5\">just one scientist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. That scientist is also deeply involved in the project, talking through plot ideas and checking five successive drafts of each script to ensure details are correct. He was also impressed with the producer’s manifestly serious and well-intentioned <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"a81702ae-7c17-4d01-8db8-a24cab66e888\">reasons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> for making the programme. Now that the first series has been completed, he believes probably 80–90 per cent of the show is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"94087082-6ce9-41e7-8b04-7c5ca0694411\">based on fact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> and that’s good enough for what it is. After all, it is a drama, not a documentary.</span></p><p><span>Ekman, incidentally, professes to have been a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"b2141f59-b198-4f20-8131-9c365dcf3c6c\">terrible liar ever since he was a small boy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> and observes that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"658ec8a5-296b-45d8-bc52-897512c159c9\">ability to detect a lie<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"e8bbc276-cc30-4309-b958-b0a29531b8f8\">ability to lie successfully<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> are completely unrelated. He has been asked by people running for high office if he could teach them to become more credible with the public but has always refused to use his skills in that way on ethical grounds. He also insists that there are various kinds of lies. A “true” lie can be identified by having two essential characteristics: there must be a deliberate intent to mislead and there must be no notification that this is what is occurring. This means that an actor or a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"87abd084-1628-43b3-94b3-c110fc98b9de\">poker player<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> isn’t a true liar. They are supposed to deceive you—it’s part of the game—and the same is true of flattery. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"fc1147f8-f231-48e5-9095-8638ae2e4d73\">prefers to focus on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> the kinds of lies where the liar would be in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"d4483480-0ada-4d28-9b6d-bace4b8e8dbb\">grave trouble<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> if they were found out, and where the target would feel properly aggrieved if they knew.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27 – 31 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310070\" id=\"question-wrapper-310070\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the writer, Ekman became interested in lying after a question from a group of</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. senior psychologists</li> <li>B. people receiving treatment</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"9d85715d-da1f-4763-ba69-1eb11c9ad9ff\">trainee doctors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>D. university lecturers</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310071\" id=\"question-wrapper-310071\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer refers to the 12-minute interviews in order to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. illustrate how frequently patients lie.</li> <li>B. describe the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"e8dde727-cfb8-475a-9d00-0b9684ff15e7\">origins of Ekman’s theories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>C. compare Ekman’s research to previous studies.</li> <li>D. show how patients’ behaviour is affected by filming.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310072\" id=\"question-wrapper-310072\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the writer’s point in the third paragraph?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Emotional facial signs are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"0652dc26-d2fa-4ce9-80e8-7f69e07f1fa2\">shared worldwide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Recent research has refuted an old idea.</li> <li>C. With practice we can learn to control our micro-expressions.</li> <li>D. Human society is too complex to allow for generalisations.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310073\" id=\"question-wrapper-310073\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What are we told about Ekman’s conclusions from his tests?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It’s natural for people to lie.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5bd7d7f0-3a30-4971-9e5a-130e7f3a468b\">Few<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"2a021cb2-6a83-4c55-84c3-1cae398541c7\">untrained people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9ee756f9-64d0-4067-af44-bed4cbaefd07\">detect lying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Most liars suffer from periods of depression.</li> <li>D. All of his subjects were trained to identify micro-expressions.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310074\" id=\"question-wrapper-310074\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What point does the writer make about Ekman’s techniques in the fourth paragraph?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They take a decade to teach.</li> <li>B. They have been in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"0a982eb1-4124-4914-bf5d-1c43cbfaf2c9\">great demand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>C. They have aroused the suspicions of some agencies.</li> <li>D. They can be used by a limited range of occupations.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, A–I, below. Write the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 32 – 36 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. consequences </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. crimes </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"76986eac-2421-4145-b1b8-687da69918e0\">false beliefs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"a81702ae-7c17-4d01-8db8-a24cab66e888\">motives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. justice </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"94087082-6ce9-41e7-8b04-7c5ca0694411\">accuracy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. acting </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"3e0a4078-a2f7-4b1c-9df1-4588eb849288\">research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. ratings</span></p><p><b><span>The television series based on Ekman’s work</span></b></p><p><span>A new TV series based on Ekman’s work features a hero named Lightman, who detects lies. Initially, Ekman was unenthusiastic about the TV project because he feared the possibility of encouraging <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8e571dcd-a916-4b9d-80a0-dc3962ba6ee4\">viewers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>’ (32)______. For example, he was worried that one day the programme could result in (33)______ not being carried out. Ultimately, though, he has given the show his blessing because he is not aware of any other comparable programme based on a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"300dfaf8-ef13-4101-b55e-665d546c34a5\">single person<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>’s (34)______. The (35)______ of the show’s producer have been another pleasant surprise considering the genre of the programme. Ekman is happy with the show’s overall (36)______.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310075\" id=\"question-wrapper-310075\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310076\" id=\"question-wrapper-310076\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310077\" id=\"question-wrapper-310077\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310078\" id=\"question-wrapper-310078\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310079\" id=\"question-wrapper-310079\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 37 – 40 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310080\" id=\"question-wrapper-310080\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Ekman regrets the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"b2141f59-b198-4f20-8131-9c365dcf3c6c\">lies he told as a child<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310081\" id=\"question-wrapper-310081\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People who are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"e8bbc276-cc30-4309-b958-b0a29531b8f8\">good at lying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> tend to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"658ec8a5-296b-45d8-bc52-897512c159c9\">good at detecting lies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310082\" id=\"question-wrapper-310082\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Ekman has used <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"87abd084-1628-43b3-94b3-c110fc98b9de\">card games<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> as part of his research into lying.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310083\" id=\"question-wrapper-310083\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Ekman is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"fc1147f8-f231-48e5-9095-8638ae2e4d73\">more interested in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> the types of lies with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"d4483480-0ada-4d28-9b6d-bace4b8e8dbb\">serious consequences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"9d85715d-da1f-4763-ba69-1eb11c9ad9ff","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"trainee doctors","passagePhrase":"psychiatrists in training"},{"uid":"52dd2d62-ac66-4db8-a5bb-4d11352d344c","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"12-minute interviews"},{"uid":"e8dde727-cfb8-475a-9d00-0b9684ff15e7","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"origins of Ekman’s theories","passagePhrase":"termed his discovery"},{"uid":"0652dc26-d2fa-4ce9-80e8-7f69e07f1fa2","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"shared worldwide","passagePhrase":"universal"},{"uid":"2572580a-ea71-4d28-b582-119dca9af72a","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"standard, regardless of language and culture"},{"uid":"2a021cb2-6a83-4c55-84c3-1cae398541c7","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"untrained people","passagePhrase":"most people"},{"uid":"9ee756f9-64d0-4067-af44-bed4cbaefd07","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"detect lying","passagePhrase":"spot these fleeting signals"},{"uid":"5bd7d7f0-3a30-4971-9e5a-130e7f3a468b","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Few","passagePhrase":"only 50 people"},{"uid":"0a982eb1-4124-4914-bf5d-1c43cbfaf2c9","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"great demand","passagePhrase":"called in by ... countless ... around the world"},{"uid":"76986eac-2421-4145-b1b8-687da69918e0","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"false beliefs","passagePhrase":"inaccurate impression"},{"uid":"8e571dcd-a916-4b9d-80a0-dc3962ba6ee4","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"viewers","passagePhrase":"among audiences"},{"uid":"c2cb946e-56d3-4efa-a81b-9cad5ef9c00b","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"unfair convictions ... wrongly find someone guilty"},{"uid":"3e0a4078-a2f7-4b1c-9df1-4588eb849288","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"research","passagePhrase":"work"},{"uid":"300dfaf8-ef13-4101-b55e-665d546c34a5","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"single person","passagePhrase":"just one scientist"},{"uid":"a81702ae-7c17-4d01-8db8-a24cab66e888","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"motives","passagePhrase":"reasons"},{"uid":"94087082-6ce9-41e7-8b04-7c5ca0694411","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"accuracy","passagePhrase":"based on fact"},{"uid":"b2141f59-b198-4f20-8131-9c365dcf3c6c","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"lies he told as a child","passagePhrase":"terrible liar ever since he was a small boy"},{"uid":"658ec8a5-296b-45d8-bc52-897512c159c9","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"good at detecting lies","passagePhrase":"ability to detect a lie"},{"uid":"e8bbc276-cc30-4309-b958-b0a29531b8f8","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"good at lying","passagePhrase":"ability to lie successfully"},{"uid":"87abd084-1628-43b3-94b3-c110fc98b9de","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"card games","passagePhrase":"poker player"},{"uid":"fc1147f8-f231-48e5-9095-8638ae2e4d73","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"more interested in","passagePhrase":"prefers to focus on"},{"uid":"d4483480-0ada-4d28-9b6d-bace4b8e8dbb","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"serious consequences","passagePhrase":"grave trouble"}]},"reading_u2_19":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1–13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Sydney Opera House</span></b></p><p><i><span>Sydney Opera House is an example of late modern architecture; it is admired internationally and treasured by the people of Australia.</span></i></p><p><span>In 1956, the Premier of New South Wales, Australia, announced an international competition for the design of an opera house for Sydney. It attracted more than 200 entries from around the world and was won by Jørn Utzon, a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"1cdbaf36-1fb6-48cc-baa9-bf6ab14c8d2a\">relatively little-known<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"0a553af6-3e96-4403-b351-ff54a156ac30\">architect from Denmark<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. The story goes that during the judging of the competition, one judge, American architect Eero Saarinen, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"a0907f53-5640-4440-94c9-039de6c0fe9d\">arrived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in Sydney <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"a0907f53-5640-4440-94c9-039de6c0fe9d\">after the other three judges had started<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> assessing the entries. He looked through their <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6bd983b6-2130-4a52-aad9-fca38fef1b06\">rejected entries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and stopped at the Utzon design, declaring it to be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6bd983b6-2130-4a52-aad9-fca38fef1b06\">outstanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>It was Utzon’s life and travels that had shaped his design for the Sydney Opera House. Though he had never visited the site, he used his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"8283272c-8001-4846-b3fa-466c006a0c6d\">maritime background<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> to study the naval charts of Sydney Harbour. His early exposure to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"8283272c-8001-4846-b3fa-466c006a0c6d\">shipbuilding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> provided the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"22962405-db70-461d-b56f-12a6679912e9\">inspiration for the design<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"d3f09bdb-12f2-41c0-92da-76be251acd93\">roof<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, which is a series of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"d3f09bdb-12f2-41c0-92da-76be251acd93\">curved ‘shells<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>’ that look like the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"d3f09bdb-12f2-41c0-92da-76be251acd93\">sails<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of a sailing ship billowing in the wind. From his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be1edd44-315a-4768-9ddd-9fc5b5951c43\">travels to Mexico<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, he had the idea of placing his building on a wide horizontal platform.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d62e6579-f5dc-4981-a5ab-a797d565c0cc\">Construction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of the platform <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d62e6579-f5dc-4981-a5ab-a797d565c0cc\">began in 1959<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"1f7f9586-9430-4009-87cb-6b3d50662f54\">throughout the early 1960s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, Utzon <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"854b4093-3022-416e-a006-a1b4250ff226\">amended his original designs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in order to develop a way to build the large ‘shells’ that cover the two main halls. The construction of the roof brought together some of the world’s best engineers and craftsmen, devising innovative techniques to create a major visual impact in accordance with Utzon’s vision. The design was one of the first examples of the use of computer-aided design for complex shapes.</span></p><p><span>Although Utzon had spectacular plans for the interior, he was unable to realise them. Cost overruns contributed to criticism of the project and, after a change of government, the Minister of Works began questioning Utzon’s schedules and cost estimates. Payments to Utzon were stopped and he was forced to withdraw as chief architect in 1966. Following his resignation, there were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"747cc314-ecec-49fa-a980-9fa40759c7f6\">protests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> through the streets <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"747cc314-ecec-49fa-a980-9fa40759c7f6\">led<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> by prominent architect <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"5d0f20d3-031d-4648-a65e-38a4b9fef19d\">Harry Seidler<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> and others, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"747cc314-ecec-49fa-a980-9fa40759c7f6\">demanding that Utzon be reinstated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> as architect. However, Utzon was not reinstated and left Australia in 1966. He <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"b20b9e2f-c93e-4d2f-8e15-83061e23290a\">never returned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, and new architects were appointed to complete the building in his absence. The original cost estimate for the Opera House was $7 million, with the completion date set for 26 January 1963. However, the Opera House was not formally completed until 1973, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"6533b55d-5c9e-412e-8886-8450587307ae\">having cost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> $102 million.</span></p><p><span>Since its opening in 1973, Sydney Opera House has earned a reputation as a world-class performing-arts centre and become a symbol of both Sydney and Australia. Situated at Bennelong Point on Sydney Harbour, it consists of a series of large precast ‘shells’ made of concrete, each composed of sections of a sphere of 75.2 metres radius, forming the roofs of the structure, set on a monumental platform. The building is 183 metres long and 120 metres wide at its widest point. It is supported on 588 concrete piers, which are sunk approximately 25 metres below sea level.</span></p><p><span>Although the roof structures are commonly referred to as ‘shells’, they are precast concrete panels supported by concrete ribs. The ‘shells’ are covered with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"45b42401-5371-4489-8231-a6a55063e1e6\">1,056,006<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> white and cream-coloured <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"45b42401-5371-4489-8231-a6a55063e1e6\">tiles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"1a731564-8e32-4bc3-a07c-89b84421dda3\">manufactured in a factory in Sweden<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> that generally produced stoneware tiles for the paper-mill industry. The design solution and construction of the shell structure took eight years to complete, and the development of the special ceramic tiles took over three years. Apart from the tiles covering the ‘shells’, the building’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"fa76bc20-91c2-4d3e-8bc5-361c56c3d3c7\">exterior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> is mostly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"dc477e87-2360-42ad-975e-06967b4c031b\">clad with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> granite quarried in Australia.</span></p><p><span>Contrary to its name, Sydney Opera House includes multiple performance venues. It is among the busiest performing-arts centres in the world, holding over 1,500 performances each year. It hosts a large number of performing-arts companies, including <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"aec4e92f-0665-4b7c-a731-ae78e29307cc\">the four resident companies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>: Opera Australia, the Australian Ballet, the Sydney Theatre Company and the Sydney Symphony Orchestra.</span></p><p><span>With its grand setting and cathedral-like atmosphere, the Concert Hall is Sydney Opera House’s most prestigious performance space. The largest of all interior venues, it delivers outstanding acoustics thanks to its high ceiling and wood panelling. There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"eeae538f-469b-48d1-8314-5cd27043ceb5\">a sizable outdoor forecourt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> from which people ascend to the main entrance. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"e241dc0b-d496-4d5b-8c1b-05ab0dc8589a\">The steps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, which lead up <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"e241dc0b-d496-4d5b-8c1b-05ab0dc8589a\">from the forecourt to the main performance venues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, are nearly 100 metres wide.</span></p><p><span>In 1999, Utzon was re-engaged to develop a set of design principles to act as a guide for future changes to the building. All of this design work he did from his base in Europe. These principles help to ensure that the building’s architectural integrity is maintained. The first alteration to the exterior was the addition of a new colonnade, which shades <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"5f517f86-8df9-4039-ae54-a5e2ee9c7d1a\">nine large glass openings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in the previously solid exterior wall. This Utzon-led project, completed in 2006, enabled theatre patrons to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"1727d009-67d8-4938-a05e-3ed5691b490b\">see<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the harbour for the first time <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"16849d68-7eb5-499f-b6f2-a4f99b384fa1\">from the theatre foyers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. The design also incorporates the first public lift and interior escalators to assist less-mobile patrons.</span></p><p><span>Since 2007, the cultural, heritage and architectural importance of Sydney Opera House has been protected by its inclusion on the World Heritage List.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310084\" id=\"question-wrapper-310084\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Utzon was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"1cdbaf36-1fb6-48cc-baa9-bf6ab14c8d2a\">famous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> for his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"0a553af6-3e96-4403-b351-ff54a156ac30\">work before he designed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> the Opera House.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310085\" id=\"question-wrapper-310085\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Utzon’s design was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6bd983b6-2130-4a52-aad9-fca38fef1b06\">favoured by the four judges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of the competition <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"a0907f53-5640-4440-94c9-039de6c0fe9d\">from the beginning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310086\" id=\"question-wrapper-310086\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Utzon’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"8283272c-8001-4846-b3fa-466c006a0c6d\">knowledge of boats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"22962405-db70-461d-b56f-12a6679912e9\">gave him the idea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"d3f09bdb-12f2-41c0-92da-76be251acd93\">parts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of the Opera House.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310087\" id=\"question-wrapper-310087\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Utzon was impressed by the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be1edd44-315a-4768-9ddd-9fc5b5951c43\">opera houses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> he had seen <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be1edd44-315a-4768-9ddd-9fc5b5951c43\">in Mexico<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310088\" id=\"question-wrapper-310088\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Utzon <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"854b4093-3022-416e-a006-a1b4250ff226\">changed his designs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"1f7f9586-9430-4009-87cb-6b3d50662f54\">in the 1960s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d62e6579-f5dc-4981-a5ab-a797d565c0cc\">after construction began<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310089\" id=\"question-wrapper-310089\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"5d0f20d3-031d-4648-a65e-38a4b9fef19d\">Seidler<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"747cc314-ecec-49fa-a980-9fa40759c7f6\">defended Utzon’s role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> as architect.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310090\" id=\"question-wrapper-310090\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Utzon <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"b20b9e2f-c93e-4d2f-8e15-83061e23290a\">went back to Australia<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in 1973 for the opening of the Opera House.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"1a731564-8e32-4bc3-a07c-89b84421dda3\">from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8 – 13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Sydney Opera House</span></b></p><p><b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"6533b55d-5c9e-412e-8886-8450587307ae\">Final cost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></span></b></p><p><span>• $ (8)______</span></p><p><b><span>Construction</span></b></p><p><span>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"eeae538f-469b-48d1-8314-5cd27043ceb5\">A large<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> platform acting as a base for the building</span></p><p><span>• Concrete panels used to make ‘shells’, which are covered in tiles</span></p><p><span>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"45b42401-5371-4489-8231-a6a55063e1e6\">Over a million tiles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> from (9)______</span></p><p><span>• (10)______ from Australia <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"dc477e87-2360-42ad-975e-06967b4c031b\">covering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"fa76bc20-91c2-4d3e-8bc5-361c56c3d3c7\">outside walls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span></span></p><p><b><span>Use</span></b></p><p><span>• More than 1,500 performances annually</span></p><p><span>• (11)______ performing-arts companies have their home base at the Opera</span></p><p><b><span>House</span></b></p><p><span>Outside</span></p><p><span>• A large (12)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"e241dc0b-d496-4d5b-8c1b-05ab0dc8589a\">at the foot of a wide staircase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span></span></p><p><b><span>Alterations</span></b></p><p><span>• A colonnade was added in 2006</span></p><p><span>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"5f517f86-8df9-4039-ae54-a5e2ee9c7d1a\">Openings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> made the (13)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"1727d009-67d8-4938-a05e-3ed5691b490b\">visible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"16849d68-7eb5-499f-b6f2-a4f99b384fa1\">from foyers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310091\" id=\"question-wrapper-310091\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">102 million [OR] 102(,)000(,)000</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310092\" id=\"question-wrapper-310092\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Sweden</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310093\" id=\"question-wrapper-310093\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">granite</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310094\" id=\"question-wrapper-310094\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">four/4</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310095\" id=\"question-wrapper-310095\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">forecourt</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310096\" id=\"question-wrapper-310096\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">harbo(u)r</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0a553af6-3e96-4403-b351-ff54a156ac30","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"work before he designed","passagePhrase":"architect from Denmark"},{"uid":"a0907f53-5640-4440-94c9-039de6c0fe9d","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"from the beginning","passagePhrase":"arrived ... after the other three judges had started"},{"uid":"8283272c-8001-4846-b3fa-466c006a0c6d","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"knowledge of boats","passagePhrase":"maritime background ... shipbuilding"},{"uid":"22962405-db70-461d-b56f-12a6679912e9","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"gave him the idea","passagePhrase":"inspiration for the design"},{"uid":"d3f09bdb-12f2-41c0-92da-76be251acd93","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"parts","passagePhrase":"roof ... curved ‘shells ... sails"},{"uid":"be1edd44-315a-4768-9ddd-9fc5b5951c43","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"opera houses ... in Mexico","passagePhrase":"travels to Mexico"},{"uid":"d62e6579-f5dc-4981-a5ab-a797d565c0cc","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"after construction began","passagePhrase":"Construction ... began in 1959"},{"uid":"1f7f9586-9430-4009-87cb-6b3d50662f54","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"in the 1960s","passagePhrase":"throughout the early 1960s"},{"uid":"854b4093-3022-416e-a006-a1b4250ff226","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"changed his designs","passagePhrase":"amended his original designs"},{"uid":"747cc314-ecec-49fa-a980-9fa40759c7f6","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"defended Utzon’s role","passagePhrase":"protests ... led ... demanding that Utzon be reinstated"},{"uid":"5d0f20d3-031d-4648-a65e-38a4b9fef19d","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Seidler","passagePhrase":"Harry Seidler"},{"uid":"6533b55d-5c9e-412e-8886-8450587307ae","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Final cost","passagePhrase":"having cost"},{"uid":"45b42401-5371-4489-8231-a6a55063e1e6","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Over a million tiles","passagePhrase":"1,056,006 ... tiles"},{"uid":"1a731564-8e32-4bc3-a07c-89b84421dda3","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"from","passagePhrase":"manufactured in a factory in Sweden"},{"uid":"fa76bc20-91c2-4d3e-8bc5-361c56c3d3c7","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"outside walls","passagePhrase":"exterior"},{"uid":"dc477e87-2360-42ad-975e-06967b4c031b","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"covering","passagePhrase":"clad with"},{"uid":"aec4e92f-0665-4b7c-a731-ae78e29307cc","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the four resident companies"},{"uid":"eeae538f-469b-48d1-8314-5cd27043ceb5","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"A large","passagePhrase":"a sizable outdoor forecourt"},{"uid":"e241dc0b-d496-4d5b-8c1b-05ab0dc8589a","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"at the foot of a wide staircase","passagePhrase":"The steps ... from the forecourt to the main performance venues"},{"uid":"5f517f86-8df9-4039-ae54-a5e2ee9c7d1a","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"Openings","passagePhrase":"nine large glass openings"},{"uid":"1727d009-67d8-4938-a05e-3ed5691b490b","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"visible","passagePhrase":"see"},{"uid":"16849d68-7eb5-499f-b6f2-a4f99b384fa1","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"from foyers","passagePhrase":"from the theatre foyers"}]},"reading_u2_20":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14–26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Investment in Shares vs. Investment in Other Assets</span></b></p><p><b><span>Which Gives the Greater Gain?</span></b></p><p><i><span>How one university collected the data to try and answer this question</span></i></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> It all began in 1958 with a phone call from Louis Engel, a banker <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a723218f-a7a0-4aa8-8545-f18145bd8645\">at Merrill Lynch, a US- based financial management company<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"11651f6d-5ea3-4f94-88ba-a1397c2ea5ed\">wanted to know<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> how investors in shares had performed relative to investors in other assets such as low-risk investments with guaranteed returns. ‘I don’t know, but if you gave me $50,000, I could find out,’ replied Jim Lorie, a dean at the University of Chicago’s business school. Louis Engel soon agreed to provide the funding, and more. The result, in 1960, was the launch of the University’s Center for Research in Security Prices. Half a century later CRSP (pronounced ‘crisp’) data are everywhere. They provided the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2932916e-e5e1-4286-80ea-e1e75558b4c5\">foundation of at least one-third of all empirical research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in finance over the past 40 years, according to a presentation at a symposium held this month. They probably influenced much of the rest.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"572bddf8-38f7-4226-89fc-76db8d46cbef\">Getting the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> CRSP <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"572bddf8-38f7-4226-89fc-76db8d46cbef\">data together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> was a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"c6266e87-bfd3-44f4-89fc-399fe6f37862\">tough process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in what were then the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ca2422d3-27f5-4359-aafe-fc2242caf19d\">early days of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> computers. Up to three million pieces of information on all the shares traded on the New York Stock Exchange between 1926 and 1960 were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"3ddb17b0-db49-4d1d-8afd-327f483a8cd4\">transferred from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> paper in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8be11c4f-45a1-4c83-bd14-761a011c82ea\">exchange’s archive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> to magnetic tape. A lot of time was spent adjusting prices to take account of complexities in the market. Lorie and his co-researcher, Lawrence Fisher, chose January 1926 as the start date because they wanted the data to span at least one complete business cycle from boom to bust, or vice versa.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> When these two economists published the first study based on the CRSP data in 1964, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"3d581b4e-3dc4-4b2a-ab83-06e941ced29f\">reported that the annual compound return<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> on the shares over the entire 35-year period was (depending on the tax status of the investor) between 6.8% and 9%. Acknowledging that good data on the performance of other assets were not available, the study claimed that the rate of return on shares was ‘substantially higher than for alternative investment media’, providing the first empirical support for the still-popular idea that shares outperform other investments over the long run. Fisher and Lorie also observed that many people <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5a9d6835-ce6d-4a86-9906-9b40d07218e3\">chose to invest in assets with </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5a9d6835-ce6d-4a86-9906-9b40d07218e3 dfc98cbd-9b19-4e7d-aadc-72503ae20a6e\">lower returns</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5a9d6835-ce6d-4a86-9906-9b40d07218e3\"> because they were cautious</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> by nature and were concerned about the risk of loss inherent in investing in the stock market. Economists today call the amount of extra return that investors need to compensate them for this additional risk the ‘equity risk premium’, although they differ greatly on how big investors should expect it to be.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> After Fisher and Lorie’s 1964 report there was no stopping the love affair between financial economists and the data that studying these numbers produced. Myron Scholes, now a Nobel laureate, became director of CRSP in 1974, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"7319289e-a24b-4ba0-91a7-69c5ebc726aa\">ensured the database was<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> both kept up to date and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"7319289e-a24b-4ba0-91a7-69c5ebc726aa\">made readily available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to academic economists everywhere. In turn, this resource became ever more useful as computing power became more affordable. The CRSP database has since been expanded to include a full range of different types of investments. It has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"695fa06a-688c-42ae-91ad-365796f65376\">replicated across the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>E. </span></b><span>One of the earliest uses of CRSP data was by Eugene Fama, an economist at the University of Chicago, to support his ‘efficient-market hypothesis’. He found that over a lengthy period, share prices tended to rise and fall randomly, without showing much of a pattern. Markets are efficient, he said, because all relevant information is reflected in share prices at any given moment, meaning there are no predictable movements in prices for smart investors to exploit. Fama did concede that there was some evidence of <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 23\" data-uid=\"49d74cd2-1c86-47fd-ba0c-8665453fb7a1 73e68e84-1494-4180-a61b-4a7494c4e231 ed4bdb78-5cb7-429e-b790-16c00c34034c\">temporary</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 23\" data-uid=\"49d74cd2-1c86-47fd-ba0c-8665453fb7a1 ed4bdb78-5cb7-429e-b790-16c00c34034c\"> short-term predictability</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> in share prices, however. That stipulation has resulted in a vast number of papers based on discovering such ‘variations’ through data mining. In theory, such <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ed4bdb78-5cb7-429e-b790-16c00c34034c\">anomalies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> are potentially lucrative for investors, but as believers in efficient markets observe with satisfaction, it seems that no sooner are such anomalies discovered and reported in journals than they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ed4bdb78-5cb7-429e-b790-16c00c34034c\">typically disappear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><b><span>F. </span></b><span>However, the sheer volume of material means that financial economists are be<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"2942ae65-7ff0-4af7-97ee-e75b7cdbf254\">coming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> increasingly specialised, which may have costs as well as benefits. Some economists worry that much of this statistical analysis is creating some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"151510f4-083f-43ef-9357-3a503789d15c\">interference that drowns out serious thinking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> about the big questions, such as why the financial system nearly collapsed in 2008 and how a repeat can be avoided. Robert Shiller, an economist at Yale University and a long-time sceptic about the efficient-market hypothesis, feels that with the creation of the CRSP database economists suddenly believed that finance had become scientific. According to Shiller, conventional ideas about investing and financial markets – and about their vulnerabilities – seemed out of date to the new empiricists. He worries that academic departments are full of economists who are so <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"151510f4-083f-43ef-9357-3a503789d15c\">specialised in data analysis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> that they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"8b12474e-636a-465c-bd95-e66a817e4c74\">fail to see and understand the whole<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. They get a sense of authority from work that contains lots of data. To have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"2942ae65-7ff0-4af7-97ee-e75b7cdbf254\">seen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"32abf45e-cd4c-4852-8a4c-069925bf793f\">2008 global financial crisis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> coming, he argues, it would have been better to ‘go back to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"8505a589-970d-4316-8406-55f8fbf86d61\">old-fashioned readings of history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, studying institutions and laws. We should have talked to grandpa.’</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"20\"><b><span>G.</span></b><span> Scholes responds to this criticism with the contention that the usefulness of this empirical analysis is proven by the fact that demand for it continues to grow. At CRSP’s 50th-anniversary symposium, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"28117382-ecaf-4d80-8482-fbdc0ffb9491\">plans were unveiled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to publish indicators on an expanding range of investments, as well as for growth and value stocks. These indicators, CRSP claims, will be more academically rigorous and cheaper than existing ones. For believers in the efficiency of markets, that should be enough to ensure CRSP’s continuing success.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A–G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"7319289e-a24b-4ba0-91a7-69c5ebc726aa\">growing availability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"695fa06a-688c-42ae-91ad-365796f65376\">influence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of CRSP data</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"3d581b4e-3dc4-4b2a-ab83-06e941ced29f\">Initial findings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of the CRSP project</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"11651f6d-5ea3-4f94-88ba-a1397c2ea5ed\">request<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2932916e-e5e1-4286-80ea-e1e75558b4c5\">far-reaching result<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"c6266e87-bfd3-44f4-89fc-399fe6f37862\">Difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"572bddf8-38f7-4226-89fc-76db8d46cbef\">collecting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> CRSP data</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"28117382-ecaf-4d80-8482-fbdc0ffb9491\">What the future holds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"151510f4-083f-43ef-9357-3a503789d15c\">Too much data<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> for people to have an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"8b12474e-636a-465c-bd95-e66a817e4c74\">overall understanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. Other university departments which depend on CRSP</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. CRSP data <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ed4bdb78-5cb7-429e-b790-16c00c34034c\">not always being a useful basis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> for investment</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310097\" id=\"question-wrapper-310097\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310098\" id=\"question-wrapper-310098\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310099\" id=\"question-wrapper-310099\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310100\" id=\"question-wrapper-310100\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310101\" id=\"question-wrapper-310101\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310102\" id=\"question-wrapper-310102\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310103\" id=\"question-wrapper-310103\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph G</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements (21–23) and the list of economists below. Match each statement with the correct economist A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 21–23 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Economists</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Fisher and Lorie</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Myron Scholes</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Eugene Fama</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Robert Shiller</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310104\" id=\"question-wrapper-310104\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"8505a589-970d-4316-8406-55f8fbf86d61\">traditional approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> may have helped <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"2942ae65-7ff0-4af7-97ee-e75b7cdbf254\">predict<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"32abf45e-cd4c-4852-8a4c-069925bf793f\">financial downturn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310105\" id=\"question-wrapper-310105\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5a9d6835-ce6d-4a86-9906-9b40d07218e3\">invest conservatively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and as a result <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"dfc98cbd-9b19-4e7d-aadc-72503ae20a6e\">make less money<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310106\" id=\"question-wrapper-310106\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It may be possible to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"49d74cd2-1c86-47fd-ba0c-8665453fb7a1\">forecast share prices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"73e68e84-1494-4180-a61b-4a7494c4e231\">not over the long term<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The beginnings of CRSP</span></b></p><p><span>In 1958, a (24)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a723218f-a7a0-4aa8-8545-f18145bd8645\">working for a financial management company<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> telephoned Jim Lorie to ask how well investments in shares performed in comparison to investments in low-risk assets. Lorie offered to find out and as a result the University of Chicago’s Center for Research in Security Prices (CRSP) was launched. Compiling the CRSP data was difficult because (25)______ were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ca2422d3-27f5-4359-aafe-fc2242caf19d\">still being developed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and information that had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"3ddb17b0-db49-4d1d-8afd-327f483a8cd4\">previously been on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26)______ needed to be put onto magnetic tape.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310107\" id=\"question-wrapper-310107\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">banker</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310108\" id=\"question-wrapper-310108\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">computers</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310109\" id=\"question-wrapper-310109\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">paper</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a723218f-a7a0-4aa8-8545-f18145bd8645","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"working for a financial management company","passagePhrase":"at Merrill Lynch, a US- based financial management company"},{"uid":"11651f6d-5ea3-4f94-88ba-a1397c2ea5ed","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"request","passagePhrase":"wanted to know"},{"uid":"2932916e-e5e1-4286-80ea-e1e75558b4c5","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"far-reaching result","passagePhrase":"foundation of at least one-third of all empirical research"},{"uid":"572bddf8-38f7-4226-89fc-76db8d46cbef","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"collecting","passagePhrase":"Getting the ... data together"},{"uid":"c6266e87-bfd3-44f4-89fc-399fe6f37862","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Difficulties","passagePhrase":"tough process"},{"uid":"ca2422d3-27f5-4359-aafe-fc2242caf19d","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"still being developed","passagePhrase":"early days of"},{"uid":"3ddb17b0-db49-4d1d-8afd-327f483a8cd4","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"previously been on","passagePhrase":"transferred from"},{"uid":"8be11c4f-45a1-4c83-bd14-761a011c82ea","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"exchange’s archive"},{"uid":"3d581b4e-3dc4-4b2a-ab83-06e941ced29f","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Initial findings","passagePhrase":"reported that the annual compound return"},{"uid":"5a9d6835-ce6d-4a86-9906-9b40d07218e3","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"invest conservatively","passagePhrase":"chose to invest in assets with ... because they were cautious"},{"uid":"5a9d6835-ce6d-4a86-9906-9b40d07218e3 dfc98cbd-9b19-4e7d-aadc-72503ae20a6e","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"lower returns"},{"uid":"7319289e-a24b-4ba0-91a7-69c5ebc726aa","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"growing availability","passagePhrase":"ensured the database was ... made readily available"},{"uid":"695fa06a-688c-42ae-91ad-365796f65376","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"influence","passagePhrase":"replicated across the world"},{"uid":"49d74cd2-1c86-47fd-ba0c-8665453fb7a1 73e68e84-1494-4180-a61b-4a7494c4e231 ed4bdb78-5cb7-429e-b790-16c00c34034c","qNum":"18 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"temporary"},{"uid":"49d74cd2-1c86-47fd-ba0c-8665453fb7a1 ed4bdb78-5cb7-429e-b790-16c00c34034c","qNum":"18 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"short-term predictability"},{"uid":"ed4bdb78-5cb7-429e-b790-16c00c34034c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"not always being a useful basis","passagePhrase":"anomalies ... typically disappear"},{"uid":"2942ae65-7ff0-4af7-97ee-e75b7cdbf254","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"predict","passagePhrase":"coming ... seen"},{"uid":"151510f4-083f-43ef-9357-3a503789d15c","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Too much data","passagePhrase":"interference that drowns out serious thinking ... specialised in data analysis"},{"uid":"8b12474e-636a-465c-bd95-e66a817e4c74","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"overall understanding","passagePhrase":"fail to see and understand the whole"},{"uid":"32abf45e-cd4c-4852-8a4c-069925bf793f","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"financial downturn","passagePhrase":"2008 global financial crisis"},{"uid":"8505a589-970d-4316-8406-55f8fbf86d61","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"traditional approach","passagePhrase":"old-fashioned readings of history"},{"uid":"28117382-ecaf-4d80-8482-fbdc0ffb9491","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"What the future holds","passagePhrase":"plans were unveiled"},{"uid":"dfc98cbd-9b19-4e7d-aadc-72503ae20a6e","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"make less money","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"49d74cd2-1c86-47fd-ba0c-8665453fb7a1","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"forecast share prices","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"73e68e84-1494-4180-a61b-4a7494c4e231","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"not over the long term","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_21":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Book Review:</span></b></p><p><i><span>The Discovery of Slowness </span></i><span>by Sten Nadolny, translated by Ralph Freedman | Canongate, 311 pp</span></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_1/reading/images/dc1017369208bb9c3e1eeccef734e170a897ab692a86110f732064efbd6d331e.png\" title=\"\"></span></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> The English explorer and writer John Franklin (1786–1847) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"1ef3fd6b-68f5-4348-bec3-6999a46ea331\">joined the Navy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> at the age of 14, and fought at the battle of Trafalgar. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"a2280a29-36e5-4b4c-bb7a-ebad3d0801fd\">When peace came<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, he turned his attention to Arctic exploration, and in particular to solving the conundrum of the Northwest Passage, a mythical clear-water route through the ice which would, if it existed, link the Pacific Ocean on America’s West Coast with the Atlantic on its East. The first expedition Franklin led to the Arctic was an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"a2280a29-36e5-4b4c-bb7a-ebad3d0801fd\">arduous overland journey lasting from 1819 to 1822<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, in which he and his twenty-strong team covered 8,880 kilometres on foot. Their expedition was a triumph of surveying – they managed to chart hundreds of kilometres of previously unknown coastline – but food ran out on their journey back to civilization, and the men were forced to eat their belts and their boots (which they boiled up to make leather soup).</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e44aca70-568f-4e1a-b8f3-42babf4c8a94\">There </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"b3dfb3d2-ac80-42e1-a179-519926af0de3 e44aca70-568f-4e1a-b8f3-42babf4c8a94\">followed a career</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"b3dfb3d2-ac80-42e1-a179-519926af0de3\"> as a travel writer and public speaker</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> (‘the man who ate his boots’ was Franklin’s tag-line). Then in 1845, Franklin set off back to the Arctic with two ships – the Erebus and the </span><i><span>Terror </span></i><span>– and 129 men. Nothing was heard of them for 14 years, although more than 30 expeditions were dispatched in search of them. Eventually, it was discovered that Franklin and all his team had perished after their ships were trapped in the ice.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> In his personal correspondence and published memoirs, Franklin comes across as a man dedicated to the external duties of war and exploration, who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"fc5fa7d1-f7b4-4795-9dde-72e4d810426e\">kept introspection and self- analysis to a minimum<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. His blandness makes him an amenably malleable subject for a novelist, and Sten Nadolny has taken full advantage of this in his book. Most importantly, Nadolny has endowed John Franklin with a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a402578c-dc16-494b-aa4e-4eb7c2129152\">defining trait<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> for which there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"b6b568e6-f091-4c16-901d-12964cd26de9\">no historical evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>: </span><i><span>Langsamkeit </span></i><span>(‘slowness’, or ‘calmness’).</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>Slowness influences not only Franklin’s behaviour, but also his vision, his thoughts and his speech. The opening scene of </span><i><span>The Discovery of Slowness</span></i><span> depicts Franklin as a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"b44624c8-1e05-4991-86fd-094d0671fd0b\">young boy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, failing to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"e7ac3c87-3faa-465d-a182-8366963dafdf\">catch a ball<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> because his reaction time is too slow. Despite the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"11cd63c6-5a35-40df-8ece-511a6446111f\">bullying of his peers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, Franklin <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"11cd63c6-5a35-40df-8ece-511a6446111f\">resolves not to fall into step<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> with ‘their way of doing things’. For Nadolny, Franklin’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7beb1bd4-7d33-4f66-a64b-209099062013\">fascination with the Arctic stems from his desire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> to find an environment suited to his peculiar slowness. He describes Franklin as a boy dreaming of the ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7faa88ce-9f16-4b80-a826-8441c6d5934b\">time without hours and days<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>’ which exists in the far north, a place ‘where nobody would find him too slow’.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"ad103f21-230e-44a5-b356-de1a8101f871\">Ice is a slow mover<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. The compressed blue ice inside an Alpine crevasse will have fallen as snow several decades earlier. Polar <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"c3a3aecc-cd8a-4f52-8d9d-53c1731a9249\">pack<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> ice takes at least two years to form. The film of crystals, which first appears on the surface of the sea, thickens into a silkily pliant layer called <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"c3a3aecc-cd8a-4f52-8d9d-53c1731a9249\">nilas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>; this in turn consolidates into <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29 36\" data-uid=\"ad103f21-230e-44a5-b356-de1a8101f871 c3a3aecc-cd8a-4f52-8d9d-53c1731a9249\">young ice</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, which then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"ad103f21-230e-44a5-b356-de1a8101f871\">deepens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> during several seasons <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"ad103f21-230e-44a5-b356-de1a8101f871\">to become pack<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Ice demands a corresponding patience from those who venture onto it. The explorers who have thrived at high latitudes and at high altitudes haven’t usually been men of great speed. They have tended instead to demonstrate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"cb1c468d-8792-45bc-9835-c9c72e5f6b77\">unusual self-possession<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, a considerable <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"cb1c468d-8792-45bc-9835-c9c72e5f6b77\">capacity for boredom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, and a talent for the uncomplaining <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"cb1c468d-8792-45bc-9835-c9c72e5f6b77\">endurance of suffering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>These were all qualities which the historical Franklin possessed in abundance, and so Nadolny’s exaggeration of them isn’t unreasonable. Even as an adult, Franklin’s slowness of thought means that he is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e8425dcf-000c-4b0e-b8cc-7ac8f5eb7718\">unable to speak fluently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, so he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ba3b2178-5655-4941-9faf-9f9f1fdda0cb\">learns by heart ‘entire fleets of words and batteries of responses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>’, and speaks a languid, bric-à-brac language. In the Navy, his method of thinking first and acting later <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"a2e98633-3102-4c02-ac5b-669e6e636a6f\">initially provokes mockery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> from his fellow sailors. But Franklin persists in doing things his way, and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"a2e98633-3102-4c02-ac5b-669e6e636a6f\">gradually </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"07f2517d-570f-4752-9c6e-3ce04f5904a2 a2e98633-3102-4c02-ac5b-669e6e636a6f\">earns the respect</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of those around him. To a commodore who tells him to speed up his report of an engagement, he replies: ‘When I tell something, sir, I use my own rhythm.’ A lieutenant says approvingly of him: ‘Because Franklin is so slow, he never loses time.’</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>Nadolny also brings his central metaphor of slowness to bear on the novel’s language. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0e3ebe60-4d8c-4d6c-bb68-0eda1a6acfeb\">chapters describing Franklin’s early years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> are a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"227ec441-9647-4318-b83c-b3da554a52bf\">medley of separate fragments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, rhetorical questions, associative jumps and exclamation marks. In the later sections recounting Franklin’s first Arctic expedition, Nadolny brilliantly sets the narrative pace to the rhythms of the frozen landscape, and to the ‘slowness which is bred by hunger’.</span></p><p><b><span>H. </span></b><span>Since it was first published in Germany in 1983, </span><i><span>The Discovery of Slowness</span></i><span> has <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30 40\" data-uid=\"d1aeff59-7433-4dd3-a3bc-bee11e0404b3 ee7ecf1f-4ceb-4b30-b654-493e7b764ece\">sold more than a million copies</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"d1aeff59-7433-4dd3-a3bc-bee11e0404b3\"> and been translated into 15 languages</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. It has been adopted as a manual and manifesto by European pressure groups and institutions representing causes as diverse as sustainable development, management science and motoring policy, even becoming involved in the debate about speed limits on German roads. The various groups that have taken the novel up have one thing in common: a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"4b71cb9c-9437-421a-8b0f-2e8b40177c4a\">dislike of the high-speed culture of Post-modernity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Nadolny’s Franklin appeals to them because he is immune to ‘the compulsion to be constantly occupied’, and to the idea that ‘someone was better if he could do the same thing fast’. It’s easy to see where the attraction lies for those in management. The novel is crammed with quotations about time-efficiency, punctiliousness and profitability: ‘What did “too late” mean? They hadn’t waited for it long enough, that’s what it meant.’</span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has eight paragraphs, A–H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310110\" id=\"question-wrapper-310110\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a summary of Franklin’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"1ef3fd6b-68f5-4348-bec3-6999a46ea331\">occupation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"a2280a29-36e5-4b4c-bb7a-ebad3d0801fd\">period before his first expedition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310111\" id=\"question-wrapper-310111\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a reference to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a402578c-dc16-494b-aa4e-4eb7c2129152\">feature of Franklin’s character<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in Nadolny’s novel that has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"b6b568e6-f091-4c16-901d-12964cd26de9\">no definite basis in fact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310112\" id=\"question-wrapper-310112\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a connection between the central theme of the novel and an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"ad103f21-230e-44a5-b356-de1a8101f871\">environmental process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310113\" id=\"question-wrapper-310113\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a reference to the widespread appeal of Nadolny’s novel</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310114\" id=\"question-wrapper-310114\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a summary of events <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e44aca70-568f-4e1a-b8f3-42babf4c8a94\">following Franklin’s return from his first expedition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, A–L, below. Write the correct letter, A–L, in boxes 32–35 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. a bully </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. discoveries </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. educational</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. family </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. isolation </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. an outsider</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. personality </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. problems </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. remoteness</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"J\"><span>J. a scholar </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"K\"><span>K. sporting </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"L\"><span>L. timelessness</span></p><p><b><span>John Franklin and the Quality of Slowness</span></b></p><p><span>Little is known from Franklin’s correspondence and published writings about his (32)______. The author, Nadolny, suggests that Franklin’s whole life can be explained by the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7faa88ce-9f16-4b80-a826-8441c6d5934b\">quality of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> ‘slowness’. He begins the book by showing how this affects the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"b44624c8-1e05-4991-86fd-094d0671fd0b\">young Franklin’s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> (33)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"e7ac3c87-3faa-465d-a182-8366963dafdf\">activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, and makes him become (34)______. As a child, it is the quality of (35)______ that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7beb1bd4-7d33-4f66-a64b-209099062013\">attracts Franklin to the Arctic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310115\" id=\"question-wrapper-310115\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310116\" id=\"question-wrapper-310116\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">K</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310117\" id=\"question-wrapper-310117\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310118\" id=\"question-wrapper-310118\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">L</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 36–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310119\" id=\"question-wrapper-310119\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In paragraph E, the writer describes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"c3a3aecc-cd8a-4f52-8d9d-53c1731a9249\">different types of ice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> in order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"cb1c468d-8792-45bc-9835-c9c72e5f6b77\">illustrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the&nbsp;extreme conditions that Polar explorers have to face.</li> <li>B. the unusual quality of the beauty of Polar regions.</li> <li>C. the vital importance of preserving the Arctic environment.</li> <li>D. the&nbsp;personal qualities required of an explorer in Arctic conditions.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310120\" id=\"question-wrapper-310120\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is said about the way Franklin <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e8425dcf-000c-4b0e-b8cc-7ac8f5eb7718\">communicates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. He expresses a very limited range of ideas.</li> <li>B. He is only willing to discuss things he is familiar with.</li> <li>C. He uses words and phrases that he has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ba3b2178-5655-4941-9faf-9f9f1fdda0cb\">previously memorised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</li> <li>D. He is only fluent when talking about naval matters.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310121\" id=\"question-wrapper-310121\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>How does the attitude of the other <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"a2e98633-3102-4c02-ac5b-669e6e636a6f\">sailors change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> towards Franklin?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They no longer notice his slowness.</li> <li>B. They start to copy his approach to work.</li> <li>C. They begin to recognise his efforts to overcome his problems.</li> <li>D. They eventually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"07f2517d-570f-4752-9c6e-3ce04f5904a2\">appreciate his good qualities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310122\" id=\"question-wrapper-310122\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0e3ebe60-4d8c-4d6c-bb68-0eda1a6acfeb\">chapters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of </span><i><span>The Discovery of Slowness</span></i><span> which describe Franklin’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0e3ebe60-4d8c-4d6c-bb68-0eda1a6acfeb\">early years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"227ec441-9647-4318-b83c-b3da554a52bf\">contain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. text from a wide variety of sources.</li> <li>B. short, disconnected pieces of text.</li> <li>C. descriptions of the Arctic landscape.</li> <li>D. information about other explorers like Franklin.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310123\" id=\"question-wrapper-310123\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><i><span>The Discovery of Slowness</span></i><span> has achieved <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"ee7ecf1f-4ceb-4b30-b654-493e7b764ece\">widespread popularity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. it reflects&nbsp;many people’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"4b71cb9c-9437-421a-8b0f-2e8b40177c4a\">concern about one aspect of modern life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> <li>B. it offers achievable solutions to many of the problems of today.</li> <li>C. it tells the story of someone’s triumph over personal problems.</li> <li>D. it shows how life in the past was less pressured than it is now.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"1ef3fd6b-68f5-4348-bec3-6999a46ea331","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"occupation","passagePhrase":"joined the Navy"},{"uid":"a2280a29-36e5-4b4c-bb7a-ebad3d0801fd","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"period before his first expedition","passagePhrase":"When peace came ... arduous overland journey lasting from 1819 to 1822"},{"uid":"e44aca70-568f-4e1a-b8f3-42babf4c8a94","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"following Franklin’s return from his first expedition","passagePhrase":"There"},{"uid":"b3dfb3d2-ac80-42e1-a179-519926af0de3 e44aca70-568f-4e1a-b8f3-42babf4c8a94","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"followed a career"},{"uid":"b3dfb3d2-ac80-42e1-a179-519926af0de3","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"as a travel writer and public speaker"},{"uid":"fc5fa7d1-f7b4-4795-9dde-72e4d810426e","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"kept introspection and self- analysis to a minimum"},{"uid":"a402578c-dc16-494b-aa4e-4eb7c2129152","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"feature of Franklin’s character","passagePhrase":"defining trait"},{"uid":"b6b568e6-f091-4c16-901d-12964cd26de9","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"no definite basis in fact","passagePhrase":"no historical evidence"},{"uid":"b44624c8-1e05-4991-86fd-094d0671fd0b","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"young Franklin’s","passagePhrase":"young boy"},{"uid":"e7ac3c87-3faa-465d-a182-8366963dafdf","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"activities","passagePhrase":"catch a ball"},{"uid":"11cd63c6-5a35-40df-8ece-511a6446111f","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"bullying of his peers ... resolves not to fall into step"},{"uid":"7beb1bd4-7d33-4f66-a64b-209099062013","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"attracts Franklin to the Arctic","passagePhrase":"fascination with the Arctic stems from his desire"},{"uid":"7faa88ce-9f16-4b80-a826-8441c6d5934b","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"quality of","passagePhrase":"time without hours and days"},{"uid":"ad103f21-230e-44a5-b356-de1a8101f871","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"environmental process","passagePhrase":"Ice is a slow mover ... deepens ... to become pack"},{"uid":"c3a3aecc-cd8a-4f52-8d9d-53c1731a9249","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"different types of ice","passagePhrase":"pack ... nilas"},{"uid":"ad103f21-230e-44a5-b356-de1a8101f871 c3a3aecc-cd8a-4f52-8d9d-53c1731a9249","qNum":"29 36","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"young ice"},{"uid":"cb1c468d-8792-45bc-9835-c9c72e5f6b77","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"illustrate","passagePhrase":"unusual self-possession ... capacity for boredom ... endurance of suffering"},{"uid":"e8425dcf-000c-4b0e-b8cc-7ac8f5eb7718","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"communicates","passagePhrase":"unable to speak fluently"},{"uid":"ba3b2178-5655-4941-9faf-9f9f1fdda0cb","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"previously memorised","passagePhrase":"learns by heart ‘entire fleets of words and batteries of responses"},{"uid":"a2e98633-3102-4c02-ac5b-669e6e636a6f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"sailors change","passagePhrase":"initially provokes mockery ... gradually"},{"uid":"07f2517d-570f-4752-9c6e-3ce04f5904a2 a2e98633-3102-4c02-ac5b-669e6e636a6f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"earns the respect"},{"uid":"0e3ebe60-4d8c-4d6c-bb68-0eda1a6acfeb","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"chapters ... early years","passagePhrase":"chapters describing Franklin’s early years"},{"uid":"227ec441-9647-4318-b83c-b3da554a52bf","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"contain","passagePhrase":"medley of separate fragments"},{"uid":"d1aeff59-7433-4dd3-a3bc-bee11e0404b3 ee7ecf1f-4ceb-4b30-b654-493e7b764ece","qNum":"30 40","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"sold more than a million copies"},{"uid":"d1aeff59-7433-4dd3-a3bc-bee11e0404b3","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"and been translated into 15 languages"},{"uid":"4b71cb9c-9437-421a-8b0f-2e8b40177c4a","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"concern about one aspect of modern life","passagePhrase":"dislike of the high-speed culture of Post-modernity"},{"uid":"07f2517d-570f-4752-9c6e-3ce04f5904a2","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"appreciate his good qualities","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"ee7ecf1f-4ceb-4b30-b654-493e7b764ece","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"widespread popularity","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_22":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1–13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Fishbourne Roman Palace</span></b></p><p><span>Fishbourne Roman Palace is in the village of Fishbourne in West Sussex, England. The site has a long history: <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"1 7\" data-uid=\"1eeea28e-38f7-4146-b42b-71fed69dcab8 48377601-9917-4c24-be96-3dcf60f76433\">grain stores</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"f8a224ec-1c4e-4cd3-a369-0b9149db7a93\">belonging to the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> Roman army had been <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"14fb9ea2-e976-404f-b159-db21826b6bdb 1eeea28e-38f7-4146-b42b-71fed69dcab8\">established there</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"1eeea28e-38f7-4146-b42b-71fed69dcab8\"> after the invasion</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, during the reign of the Roman Emperor Claudius in 43 AD. The palace itself came later, built around thirty years afterwards in the 1st century AD, following the Roman conquest of Britain. The rectangular <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a99f37f8-8fb2-4b99-a86b-ed9fb40add78\">palace was built around<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> formal gardens, the northern half of which has been reconstructed. There were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"7a83c0f7-b03f-4e58-916c-783fe32d33b7\">extensive alterations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f914b881-4b4d-4e2e-abc5-5b871fddf5c4\">in the 2nd and 3rd centuries AD<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, with many of the original black-and-white mosaic floors being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"41b0104f-9094-49b3-92bd-9c79bb8e5b29\">overlaid with more sophisticated coloured ones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, including a perfectly preserved mosaic of a dolphin in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"0f9ed510-b652-498c-82ad-6d8c7eaaa8e9\">north wing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. More alterations were in progress when the palace <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"8f552678-3113-4be7-a45a-e0cd11b86cbf\">burnt down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> in around 270 AD, after which it was abandoned.</span></p><p><span>Local people had long believed that a Roman palace once existed in the area. However, it was not until 1960 that the archaeologist Barry Cunliffe of Oxford University first systematically excavated the site, after workmen had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"282c6501-4d66-41ee-944e-d64ce79b742d\">accidentally uncovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> a wall <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f6673a6a-cedd-4701-a7f3-e6fc9df1d099\">while they were laying a water main<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. The Roman villa excavated by Cunliffe’s team was so grand that it became known as Fishbourne Roman Palace, and a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"72e6b0db-3906-46f9-bb49-015af003c8ca\">museum was erected to preserve some of the remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. This is administered by the Sussex Archaeological Society.</span></p><p><span>In its day, the completed palace would have comprised four large wings with colonnaded fronts. The north and east wings consisted of suites of private rooms built around courtyards, with a monumental entrance in the middle of the east wing. In the north-east corner there was an assembly hall. The west wing contained state rooms, a large ceremonial reception room and a gallery. The south wing contained the owner’s private apartments. The palace included as many as fifty mosaic floors, under-floor central heating and a bathhouse. In size, Fishbourne Palace would have been <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"fc4a9b2b-abf8-4855-8cd8-15c33d08a22a\">approximately equivalent to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"6c1f5444-72ee-4250-b2cd-6178b94e278a\">some of the great Roman palaces of Italy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, and was by far the largest known Roman residence north of the European Alps, at about 500 feet (150 m) square. A team of volunteers and professional archaeologists is involved in an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"65b75346-9cdc-47f8-821e-9ef0f88984d9\">ongoing archaeological excavation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> on the site of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a4ec487a-2809-4941-be29-3c36cec55c1b\">nearby<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, possibly military, buildings.</span></p><p><span>The first buildings to be erected on the site were constructed in the early part of the conquest in 43 AD. Later, two timber buildings were constructed, one with clay-and-mortar floors and plaster walls, which appears to have been a house of some comfort. These buildings were demolished in the 60s AD and replaced by a substantial stone house, which included colonnades and a bath suite. It has been suggested that the palace itself, incorporating the previous house in its south-east corner, was constructed around 73–75 AD. However, Dr Miles Russell of Bournemouth University re-interpreted the ground plan and the collection of objects found, and has suggested that, given the extremely close parallels with the imperial palace of Domitian in Rome, its construction may more plausibly date to after 92 AD.</span></p><p><span>With regard to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"df02720f-e8fe-48a2-8b8d-12d10e1861bb\">who lived in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> Fishbourne Palace, there are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"fda9fa6f-e403-4390-8f92-e081f88294d7\">a number of theories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. For example, one proposed by Professor Cunliffe is that, in its early phase, the palace was the residence of Tiberius Claudius Cogidubnus, a local chieftain who supported the Romans and who may have been installed as king of a number of territories following the first stage of the conquest. Cogidubnus is known from a reference to his loyalty in Agricola, a work by the Roman writer Tacitus, and from an inscription commemorating a temple dedicated to the gods Neptune and Minerva found in the nearby city of Chichester. Another theory is that it was built for Sallustius Lucullus, a Roman governor of Britain in the late 1st century, who may have been the son of the British prince Adminius. Two inscriptions recording the presence of Lucullus have been found in Chichester, and the redating by Miles Russell suggests that, if the palace was designed for Lucullus, then it may have been in use for only a few years, as the Roman historian Suetonius records that Lucullus was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5df8936f-0e1d-4f8f-8413-536eacd21395\">executed by the Emperor Domitian in or shortly after<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> 93 AD.</span></p><p><span>Additional theories suggest that either Verica, a British king of the Roman Empire in the years preceding the Claudian invasion, was the owner of the palace, or Tiberius Claudius Catuarus, following the recent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"69f47095-95e3-4794-af49-0bff33f56f2f\">discovery of a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> gold ring <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"69f47095-95e3-4794-af49-0bff33f56f2f\">belonging to him<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. The palace outlasted the original owner, whoever he was, and was extensively re-planned early in the 2nd century AD and subdivided into a series of smaller apartments. Further redevelopment was begun in the late 3rd century AD, but these alterations were incomplete when the north wing was destroyed in a fire in around 270 AD. The damage was too great to repair, and the palace was abandoned and later dismantled.</span></p><p><span>A modern museum has been built by the Sussex Archaeological Society, incorporating most of the visible remains, including one wing of the palace. The gardens have been replanted using authentic plants from the Roman period.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1–6 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310124\" id=\"question-wrapper-310124\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Fishbourne Palace was the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"1eeea28e-38f7-4146-b42b-71fed69dcab8\">first structure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"14fb9ea2-e976-404f-b159-db21826b6bdb\">built on its site<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310125\" id=\"question-wrapper-310125\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Fishbourne Palace was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"7a83c0f7-b03f-4e58-916c-783fe32d33b7\">renovated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f914b881-4b4d-4e2e-abc5-5b871fddf5c4\">more than once<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310126\" id=\"question-wrapper-310126\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Fishbourne Palace was burnt down by local people. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310127\" id=\"question-wrapper-310127\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Fishbourne Palace was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"fc4a9b2b-abf8-4855-8cd8-15c33d08a22a\">larger than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"6c1f5444-72ee-4250-b2cd-6178b94e278a\">many Roman palaces in Italy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310128\" id=\"question-wrapper-310128\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"65b75346-9cdc-47f8-821e-9ef0f88984d9\">Research is continuing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a4ec487a-2809-4941-be29-3c36cec55c1b\">area close to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> Fishbourne Palace.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310129\" id=\"question-wrapper-310129\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Researchers <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"fda9fa6f-e403-4390-8f92-e081f88294d7\">agree on the identity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"df02720f-e8fe-48a2-8b8d-12d10e1861bb\">person for whom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> Fishbourne Palace <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"df02720f-e8fe-48a2-8b8d-12d10e1861bb\">was constructed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Fishbourne Palace</span></b></p><p><b><span>Construction</span></b></p><p><span>• The first buildings on the site contained <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"48377601-9917-4c24-be96-3dcf60f76433\">food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"f8a224ec-1c4e-4cd3-a369-0b9149db7a93\">for the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> (7)______.</span></p><p><span>• The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"0f9ed510-b652-498c-82ad-6d8c7eaaa8e9\">palace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a99f37f8-8fb2-4b99-a86b-ed9fb40add78\">building surrounded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)______.</span></p><p><span>• In the 2nd and 3rd centuries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"41b0104f-9094-49b3-92bd-9c79bb8e5b29\">colour was added<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to the (9)______ of the palace.</span></p><p><b><span>Discovery</span></b></p><p><span>• The palace was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"282c6501-4d66-41ee-944e-d64ce79b742d\">first discovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f6673a6a-cedd-4701-a7f3-e6fc9df1d099\">when a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f6673a6a-cedd-4701-a7f3-e6fc9df1d099\">was found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>Possible inhabitants</span></b></p><p><span>• Cogidubnus - he is named in several writings.</span></p><p><span>• Sallustius Lucullus - he may have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5df8936f-0e1d-4f8f-8413-536eacd21395\">lived there until approximately<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)______ AD.</span></p><p><span>• Verica - a British king.</span></p><p><span>• Catuarus - his (12)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"69f47095-95e3-4794-af49-0bff33f56f2f\">was found there<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>Present Day</span></b></p><p><span>• A (13)______ has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"72e6b0db-3906-46f9-bb49-015af003c8ca\">built on the site to help protect it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310130\" id=\"question-wrapper-310130\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Roman army</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310131\" id=\"question-wrapper-310131\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(formal) gardens</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310132\" id=\"question-wrapper-310132\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(mosaic) floors</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310133\" id=\"question-wrapper-310133\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Wall</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310134\" id=\"question-wrapper-310134\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">93/ninety-three</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310135\" id=\"question-wrapper-310135\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(gold) ring</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310136\" id=\"question-wrapper-310136\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(modern) museum</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"1eeea28e-38f7-4146-b42b-71fed69dcab8 48377601-9917-4c24-be96-3dcf60f76433","qNum":"1 7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"grain stores"},{"uid":"f8a224ec-1c4e-4cd3-a369-0b9149db7a93","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"for the","passagePhrase":"belonging to the"},{"uid":"14fb9ea2-e976-404f-b159-db21826b6bdb 1eeea28e-38f7-4146-b42b-71fed69dcab8","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"established there"},{"uid":"a99f37f8-8fb2-4b99-a86b-ed9fb40add78","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"building surrounded","passagePhrase":"palace was built around"},{"uid":"7a83c0f7-b03f-4e58-916c-783fe32d33b7","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"renovated","passagePhrase":"extensive alterations"},{"uid":"f914b881-4b4d-4e2e-abc5-5b871fddf5c4","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"more than once","passagePhrase":"in the 2nd and 3rd centuries AD"},{"uid":"41b0104f-9094-49b3-92bd-9c79bb8e5b29","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"colour was added","passagePhrase":"overlaid with more sophisticated coloured ones"},{"uid":"0f9ed510-b652-498c-82ad-6d8c7eaaa8e9","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"palace","passagePhrase":"north wing"},{"uid":"8f552678-3113-4be7-a45a-e0cd11b86cbf","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"burnt down"},{"uid":"282c6501-4d66-41ee-944e-d64ce79b742d","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"first discovered","passagePhrase":"accidentally uncovered"},{"uid":"f6673a6a-cedd-4701-a7f3-e6fc9df1d099","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"when a ... was found","passagePhrase":"while they were laying a water main"},{"uid":"72e6b0db-3906-46f9-bb49-015af003c8ca","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"built on the site to help protect it","passagePhrase":"museum was erected to preserve some of the remains"},{"uid":"6c1f5444-72ee-4250-b2cd-6178b94e278a","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"many Roman palaces in Italy","passagePhrase":"some of the great Roman palaces of Italy"},{"uid":"65b75346-9cdc-47f8-821e-9ef0f88984d9","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Research is continuing","passagePhrase":"ongoing archaeological excavation"},{"uid":"a4ec487a-2809-4941-be29-3c36cec55c1b","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"area close to","passagePhrase":"nearby"},{"uid":"df02720f-e8fe-48a2-8b8d-12d10e1861bb","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"person for whom ... was constructed","passagePhrase":"who lived in"},{"uid":"5df8936f-0e1d-4f8f-8413-536eacd21395","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"lived there until approximately","passagePhrase":"executed by the Emperor Domitian in or shortly after"},{"uid":"69f47095-95e3-4794-af49-0bff33f56f2f","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"was found there","passagePhrase":"discovery of a ... belonging to him"},{"uid":"14fb9ea2-e976-404f-b159-db21826b6bdb","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"built on its site","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"48377601-9917-4c24-be96-3dcf60f76433","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"food","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_23":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14–26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Return of Monkey Life</span></b></p><p><i><span>Rainforest trees growing anew on Central American farmland are helping scientists find ways for </span></i><i><span>monkey</span></i><i><span> and agriculture to benefit one another.</span></i></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>Hacienda La Pacifica, a remote working cattle ranch in Guanacaste Province of northern Costa Rica, has for decades been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7092faf7-94b6-4649-a807-7d76c17f557d\">home to a community of mantled howler monkeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7092faf7-94b6-4649-a807-7d76c17f557d\">Other native primates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>—white-faced capuchin monkeys and spider monkeys—were once common in this area too, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7092faf7-94b6-4649-a807-7d76c17f557d\">vanished<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> after the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e3541407-5c3a-47be-a5df-e17830f51b5b\">Pan-American Highway<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> was built nearby in the 1950s and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"c38346f7-e467-4bc9-aef5-06456e0aa10d\">most of the surrounding land was cleared for cattle-raising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. At Hacienda La Pacifica, however, an enlightened ranch owner chose to leave some strips of native trees growing. He used these as windbreaks to protect both cattle and their food crops from dry-season winds. In the process, the farmer unwittingly founded a unique laboratory for the study of monkeys.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>Ken Glander, a primatologist from Duke University in the USA, is studying La Pacifica’s monkeys in an effort to understand the relationship between howlers and regenerating forests at the edges of grazing lands. Studying such disturbed woodlands is increasingly important because throughout much of the New World Tropics, these are the only forests left. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"764db662-4a02-4662-9999-88596c8dee63\">In the 18th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"7feaae78-a49a-4714-b3e6-aa0d9aad52b4\">tropical dry forests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> once covered most of Central America, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"764db662-4a02-4662-9999-88596c8dee63\">by the 1980s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c0b45a53-d966-4e6f-ac17-c4ebfd312506\">less than two percent remained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> undisturbed, and less than one percent was protected.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>Howlers persist at La Pacifica, Glander explains, because they are leaf-eaters. They eat fruit when it is available but, unlike capuchin and spider monkeys, do not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"6648f2a7-35ac-4e73-9dec-3493cbd46af6\">depend on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> large areas of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"88f9abb3-dac0-4659-8377-dfa7f2241417\">fruiting trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Glander is particularly interested in howlers’ ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"07938a12-ceb6-488d-911d-d220f6965af4\">thrive on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"ed8bc5f9-954b-4d56-8924-4347ef8733b3\">leaves loaded with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> toxins—poisonous substances designed to protect the plants. For leaf-eaters, long-term exposure to a specific plant toxin can increase their ability to neutralise the poisonous substances and absorb the leaf nutrients. Watching generations of howlers at La Pacifica has shown Glander that the monkeys keep their systems primed by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"6e4e1f23-4b91-4efd-83cc-9b231ab808fc\">sampling a variety of plants and then focusing on a small number of the most nutritious food items<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. The leaves that grow in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"1ba53f85-fe00-4e6a-aa4e-380fa3c5cde4\">regenerating forests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, like those at La Pacifica, are actually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"556f8350-10c9-4e39-a84c-2c0329453f8f\">more howler-friendly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> than those produced by the centuries-old trees that survive farther south. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"1ba53f85-fe00-4e6a-aa4e-380fa3c5cde4\">younger forests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, trees put most of their limited energy into growing wood, leaves and fruit, so they produce much lower levels of toxin than do <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e4ba7cc8-b28f-4622-9c7d-c33d43e45e80\">well-established, old-growth trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>The value of maturing forests to primates is also a subject of study at Santa Rosa National Park, about 35 miles northwest of La Pacifica. Large areas of Santa Rosa’s forests had at one time been burnt to make space for cattle ranching and coffee farming, thereby devastating local monkey habitat. But in 1971, the government protected the area by designating it a national park, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"1eca7146-bb07-4f6d-bf03-ff6531367239\">species of indigenous trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> which had been absent for decades <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"3f676143-b211-4368-90c4-c5d7f5215bab\">began to invade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the abandoned pastures. Capuchins were the first to begin using the reborn forests, followed by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"2981c4ad-968c-4c44-80b4-d18988680cd2\">howlers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Eventually, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"2981c4ad-968c-4c44-80b4-d18988680cd2\">even spider monkeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, fruit-eaters that need large areas of continuous forest, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"2981c4ad-968c-4c44-80b4-d18988680cd2\">returned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. In the first 28 years following protection of the area, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"2981c4ad-968c-4c44-80b4-d18988680cd2\">capuchin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> population doubled, while the number of howlers increased sevenfold.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Some of the same traits that allow howlers to survive at La Pacifica also explain their population boom in Santa Rosa. Howler reproduction is <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"4b58c00e-3247-4896-9dba-df3a50dbae55\">faster than that of other </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"4b58c00e-3247-4896-9dba-df3a50dbae55 78c5dcd4-ab38-4df1-b4f3-ac4a299937e2\">native monkey species</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. They give birth for the first time at about 3.5 years of age, compared with seven years for capuchins, and eight or more for spider monkeys. Also, while a female spider monkey will have a baby about once every four years, well-fed howlers can produce an infant every two years. Another factor is diet. Howlers are very adaptable feeders and need only a comparatively small home range. Spider monkeys, on the other hand, need to occupy a huge home range. Also crucial is the fact that the leaves howlers eat hold plenty of water, so the monkeys can survive away from open streams and water-holes. This ability gives them a real advantage over capuchin and spider monkeys, which have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"4d3f50d7-04f7-40e5-8a1e-d8b8bee4a0bf\">suffered during the long, ongoing drought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in the area.</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> Alejandro Estrada, an ecologist at Estación de Biología Los Tuxtlas in Veracruz, Mexico, has been studying the ecology of a group of howler monkeys that thrive in a habitat totally altered by humans: a cacao plantation in Tabasco State, Mexico. Cacao plants need shade to grow, so 40 years ago the owners of Cholula Cacao Farm planted figs, monkey-pod and other tall trees to form a protective canopy over their crop. The howlers moved in about 25 years ago after nearby forests were cut. This strange habitat seems to support about as many monkeys as would a same-sized patch of wild forest. The howlers eat the leaves and fruit of the shade trees, leaving the valuable cacao pods alone.</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>Estrada believes the monkeys <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b0792b86-5dce-4d60-ba72-ae7b043b0c33\">bring under-appreciated benefits to such plantations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b0792b86-5dce-4d60-ba72-ae7b043b0c33\">dispersing the seeds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of fruits such as fig and other shade trees, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b0792b86-5dce-4d60-ba72-ae7b043b0c33\">fertilising the soil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. Spider monkeys also forage for fruit here, though they need nearby areas of forest to survive in the long term. He hopes that farmers will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"d51f3652-448e-4208-b928-41fd383bf0bd\">begin to see the advantages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of associating with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"785476ff-587d-48ac-ab91-0ba562d49c44\">wild monkeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, which could include potential ecotourism projects. ‘Conservation is usually viewed as a conflict between farming practices and the need to preserve nature,’ Estrada says. ‘We’re <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"d51f3652-448e-4208-b928-41fd383bf0bd\">moving away from that vision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and beginning to consider ways in which commercial activities may become a tool for the conservation of primates in human-modified landscapes.’</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A–G in boxes 14–17 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310137\" id=\"question-wrapper-310137\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a reason why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"1ba53f85-fe00-4e6a-aa4e-380fa3c5cde4\">newer forests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> provide howlers with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"556f8350-10c9-4e39-a84c-2c0329453f8f\">better feeding opportunities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e4ba7cc8-b28f-4622-9c7d-c33d43e45e80\">older forests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310138\" id=\"question-wrapper-310138\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a reference to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"d51f3652-448e-4208-b928-41fd383bf0bd\">change in farmers’ attitudes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> towards <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"785476ff-587d-48ac-ab91-0ba562d49c44\">wildlife<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310139\" id=\"question-wrapper-310139\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a description of the means by which howlers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"6e4e1f23-4b91-4efd-83cc-9b231ab808fc\">select the best available diet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> for themselves</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310140\" id=\"question-wrapper-310140\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>figures relating to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c0b45a53-d966-4e6f-ac17-c4ebfd312506\">reduction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"7feaae78-a49a-4714-b3e6-aa0d9aad52b4\">natural wildlife habitat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> over a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"764db662-4a02-4662-9999-88596c8dee63\">period of time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 18–21 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Why do howlers have an advantage over other <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"78c5dcd4-ab38-4df1-b4f3-ac4a299937e2\">Central American monkeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>?</span></b></p><p><span>Unlike capuchin and spider monkeys, howlers can survive without <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"6648f2a7-35ac-4e73-9dec-3493cbd46af6\">relying on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"88f9abb3-dac0-4659-8377-dfa7f2241417\">trees that bear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> (18)____, which allows them to occupy a relatively small habitat area. Their diet is more flexible, and they are able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"07938a12-ceb6-488d-911d-d220f6965af4\">tolerate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"ed8bc5f9-954b-4d56-8924-4347ef8733b3\">leaves containing high levels of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> (19)______. </span></p><p><span>Another factor behind howlers’ survival advantage is their more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"4b58c00e-3247-4896-9dba-df3a50dbae55\">rapid rate of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> (20)______ compared with other native monkey species. Because their leaf-based diet provides sufficient water intake, they are also better able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"4d3f50d7-04f7-40e5-8a1e-d8b8bee4a0bf\">withstand periods of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> (21)______.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310141\" id=\"question-wrapper-310141\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">fruit</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310142\" id=\"question-wrapper-310142\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">toxins</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310143\" id=\"question-wrapper-310143\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">reproduction</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310144\" id=\"question-wrapper-310144\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">drought</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following features (Questions 22–26) and the list of locations below. Match each feature with the correct location, A, B or C. Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 22–26 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Locations</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Hacienda La Pacifica</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Santa Rosa National Park</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Cholula Cacao Farm</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310145\" id=\"question-wrapper-310145\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It has seen the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"3f676143-b211-4368-90c4-c5d7f5215bab\">return<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"1eca7146-bb07-4f6d-bf03-ff6531367239\">native tree species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310146\" id=\"question-wrapper-310146\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7092faf7-94b6-4649-a807-7d76c17f557d\">supports only one species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of native monkey.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310147\" id=\"question-wrapper-310147\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Its monkey population <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b0792b86-5dce-4d60-ba72-ae7b043b0c33\">helps the agriculture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of the area.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310148\" id=\"question-wrapper-310148\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It is home to populations of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"2981c4ad-968c-4c44-80b4-d18988680cd2\">all three local monkey species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310149\" id=\"question-wrapper-310149\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e3541407-5c3a-47be-a5df-e17830f51b5b\">major road<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> was constructed, and much of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"c38346f7-e467-4bc9-aef5-06456e0aa10d\">landscape was altered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7092faf7-94b6-4649-a807-7d76c17f557d","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"supports only one species","passagePhrase":"home to a community of mantled howler monkeys ... Other native primates ... vanished"},{"uid":"e3541407-5c3a-47be-a5df-e17830f51b5b","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"major road","passagePhrase":"Pan-American Highway"},{"uid":"c38346f7-e467-4bc9-aef5-06456e0aa10d","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"landscape was altered","passagePhrase":"most of the surrounding land was cleared for cattle-raising"},{"uid":"764db662-4a02-4662-9999-88596c8dee63","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"period of time","passagePhrase":"In the 18th century ... by the 1980s"},{"uid":"7feaae78-a49a-4714-b3e6-aa0d9aad52b4","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"natural wildlife habitat","passagePhrase":"tropical dry forests"},{"uid":"c0b45a53-d966-4e6f-ac17-c4ebfd312506","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"reduction","passagePhrase":"less than two percent remained"},{"uid":"6648f2a7-35ac-4e73-9dec-3493cbd46af6","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"relying on","passagePhrase":"depend on"},{"uid":"88f9abb3-dac0-4659-8377-dfa7f2241417","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"trees that bear","passagePhrase":"fruiting trees"},{"uid":"07938a12-ceb6-488d-911d-d220f6965af4","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"tolerate","passagePhrase":"thrive on"},{"uid":"ed8bc5f9-954b-4d56-8924-4347ef8733b3","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"leaves containing high levels of","passagePhrase":"leaves loaded with"},{"uid":"6e4e1f23-4b91-4efd-83cc-9b231ab808fc","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"select the best available diet","passagePhrase":"sampling a variety of plants and then focusing on a small number of the most nutritious food items"},{"uid":"1ba53f85-fe00-4e6a-aa4e-380fa3c5cde4","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"newer forests","passagePhrase":"regenerating forests ... younger forests"},{"uid":"556f8350-10c9-4e39-a84c-2c0329453f8f","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"better feeding opportunities","passagePhrase":"more howler-friendly"},{"uid":"e4ba7cc8-b28f-4622-9c7d-c33d43e45e80","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"older forests","passagePhrase":"well-established, old-growth trees"},{"uid":"1eca7146-bb07-4f6d-bf03-ff6531367239","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"native tree species","passagePhrase":"species of indigenous trees"},{"uid":"3f676143-b211-4368-90c4-c5d7f5215bab","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"return","passagePhrase":"began to invade"},{"uid":"2981c4ad-968c-4c44-80b4-d18988680cd2","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"all three local monkey species","passagePhrase":"howlers ... even spider monkeys ... returned ... capuchin"},{"uid":"4b58c00e-3247-4896-9dba-df3a50dbae55","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"rapid rate of","passagePhrase":"faster than that of other"},{"uid":"4b58c00e-3247-4896-9dba-df3a50dbae55 78c5dcd4-ab38-4df1-b4f3-ac4a299937e2","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"native monkey species"},{"uid":"4d3f50d7-04f7-40e5-8a1e-d8b8bee4a0bf","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"withstand periods of","passagePhrase":"suffered during the long, ongoing drought"},{"uid":"b0792b86-5dce-4d60-ba72-ae7b043b0c33","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"helps the agriculture","passagePhrase":"bring under-appreciated benefits to such plantations ... dispersing the seeds ... fertilising the soil"},{"uid":"d51f3652-448e-4208-b928-41fd383bf0bd","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"change in farmers’ attitudes","passagePhrase":"begin to see the advantages ... moving away from that vision"},{"uid":"785476ff-587d-48ac-ab91-0ba562d49c44","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"wildlife","passagePhrase":"wild monkeys"},{"uid":"78c5dcd4-ab38-4df1-b4f3-ac4a299937e2","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Central American monkeys","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_24":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The benefits of learning an instrument</span></b></p><p><i><span>Studies show that learning a musical instrument can bring about significant improvements in your brain.</span></i></p><p><span>Are music lessons the way to get smarter? That’s what a lot of parents and experts believe: studying an instrument gives children an advantage in the development of their intellectual, perceptual, and cognitive skills. This may, however, turn out to be wishful thinking. Two highly <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"557ff3af-956b-4ffc-8e25-418aa3b6415e\">convincing trials<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> carried out recently have <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"28 31\" data-uid=\"2d8d0207-dc5c-4d5a-b362-42f2f0d383de 557ff3af-956b-4ffc-8e25-418aa3b6415e\">found no evidence</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"2d8d0207-dc5c-4d5a-b362-42f2f0d383de\"> to support this idea</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>; the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"1278b114-ed33-4e99-b387-81fd3fff5991\">IQs of </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28 31\" data-uid=\"1278b114-ed33-4e99-b387-81fd3fff5991 96d2d27e-fcbd-4606-84ae-b432f0fdd7c1\">pre-school children</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"96d2d27e-fcbd-4606-84ae-b432f0fdd7c1\"> who attended several weeks of music classes</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> as part of these studies did not differ significantly from the IQs of those who had not.</span></p><p><span>But that does not mean that the advantages of learning to play music are limited to expressing yourself, impressing friends, or just having fun. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"ed76bcd5-4341-42cf-998e-4f5603cba55c\">A growing number of studies show<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that learning an instrument in childhood can do something perhaps more valuable for the brain: it can provide <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"ce1d97d1-65b5-4f08-9336-8d1a5a80f395\">benefits as we age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, in the form of an added defence against memory loss, cognitive decline, and impaired hearing. Not only that, you may well get those benefits even if you haven’t picked up your instrument in years, or decide to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29 32\" data-uid=\"810283b0-bab7-4224-8bab-7477fd3af255 c9c031bd-fc8c-4880-afef-a4c6a715b88a\">take up music</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"810283b0-bab7-4224-8bab-7477fd3af255\"> for the first time in mid-life or beyond</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. According to neuropsychologist Brenda Hanna-Pladdy of Emory University in Atlanta, the time spent learning and practising <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"a6d7d462-018b-430a-97f5-b9d98ae12d5c\">specific types of motor control and coordination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>—each finger on each hand doing something different, and for wind and brass instruments, also using your mouth and breathing—contributes to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"23c6709e-78a5-46a5-80f5-19b7fa849fe8\">brain boost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that shows up later in life.</span></p><p><span>You can even map the impact of musical training on the brain itself. In one study, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"b020fe28-1efa-401f-83ca-c6f2321fe3c2\">Harvard neurologist Gottfried Schlaug found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"37b44452-16d4-4dd9-93f3-4dc0812d58d1\">brains of adult professional musicians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> had a larger volume of grey matter <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"37b44452-16d4-4dd9-93f3-4dc0812d58d1\">than the brains of non-musicians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> had. Schlaug and colleagues also found that after 15 months of musical training in early childhood, structural brain changes associated with motor and auditory improvements begin to appear. ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"d0162889-c4bb-40d5-8156-c8b207eeb31f\">What’s unique about playing an instrument<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> is that it requires a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"88d31a2a-c12a-4089-87a7-75c52d71fd48\">wide array of brain regions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> and cognitive functions to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"88d31a2a-c12a-4089-87a7-75c52d71fd48\">work together simultaneously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, in both the right and left hemispheres of the brain,’ says Alison Balbag of the University of Southern California. ‘Playing music may be an efficient way to stimulate the brain,’ she says, ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"2fd8128b-ee3f-4b27-acbf-8175f72f209e\">cutting across a broad swath of its regions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> and cognitive functions, and with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"2fd8128b-ee3f-4b27-acbf-8175f72f209e\">ripple effects through the decades<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.’</span></p><p><span>More research is showing this might well be the case. In her first study on the subject, Hanna-Pladdy divided 70 healthy adults between the ages of 60 and 83 into three groups: musicians who had studied an instrument for at least ten years, those who had played between one and nine years, and a control group who had never learned an instrument. The group who had studied for at least ten years scored the highest when tested in such areas as non-verbal and visuo-spatial memory, naming objects, and taking in and adapting new information. Her follow-up study a year later confirmed those findings and further suggested that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"3e13b776-746c-4253-bcea-84cabe5252b5\">starting musical training before the age of nine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> and keeping at it for ten years or more may yield the greatest benefits. Interestingly, it was the group who had the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"f10a688d-25ce-43c8-8f1c-99c09c0dcc8e\">lowest level of general education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> which showed the greatest gap in scores between those who had studied an instrument in childhood and those who had not. Hanna-Pladdy suspects that musical training could have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"3e9a776b-7c9c-4e79-9808-a6350ceb7d79\">made up for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"f10a688d-25ce-43c8-8f1c-99c09c0dcc8e\">lack of cognitive stimulation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> these people had.</span></p><p><span>Neuroscientist Nina Kraus of Northwestern University in Chicago has found still more positive effects of early musical training. She measured the electrical activity in the auditory brainstem of adults, aged 55 to 70, as they responded to the synthesised speech syllable ‘da’. Although none of the subjects had played a musical instrument in 40 years, those who had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"be57ea01-64d9-41ed-bba2-b63c9e5b4f5c\">trained the longest—between four and fourteen years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>—responded the fastest. ‘That’s significant,’ says Kraus, ‘because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"1f57c0e7-be3c-4d39-ab9b-cc06f6fa8c48\">hearing tends to decline as we age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, including the ability to quickly and accurately discern consonants, a skill crucial to understanding and participating in conversation. If your nervous system is not keeping up with the timing necessary for encoding consonants, you will lose out on the flow and meaning of the conversation, and that can potentially create a downward spiral leading to a sense of social isolation,’ says Kraus. In addition, the fact that musical training appears to enhance auditory working memory might help reinforce in later life the memory capacity that facilitates verbal interaction.</span></p><p><span>In another study at the University of South Florida, assistant professor of music education <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"74afe0b2-cb27-4590-9423-a37034cee267\">Jennifer Bugos studied the impact of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"7569a895-a341-456a-8c5d-e5a53daf252a\">elementary piano instruction on adults between the ages of 60 and 85<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. After six months, those who had received piano lessons showed more robust gains in memory, verbal fluency, the speed at which they processed information, planning ability, and other cognitive functions compared with those who had not received the lessons. Bugos believes that playing an instrument has beneficial effects, regardless of how old the person is when he or she begins. ‘Musical training contains all the components of a cognitive training programme that sometimes are overlooked,’ she says. ‘And just as we work out our bodies, we should work out our minds.’</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310150\" id=\"question-wrapper-310150\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Many parents indicate that their children struggle to learn a musical instrument.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310151\" id=\"question-wrapper-310151\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"1278b114-ed33-4e99-b387-81fd3fff5991\">findings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of the recent research into pre-school children’s IQs are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"557ff3af-956b-4ffc-8e25-418aa3b6415e\">unreliable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310152\" id=\"question-wrapper-310152\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The main reasons people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"c9c031bd-fc8c-4880-afef-a4c6a715b88a\">take up an instrument<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> are that they enjoy playing music and being creative.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310153\" id=\"question-wrapper-310153\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"ed76bcd5-4341-42cf-998e-4f5603cba55c\">Evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> about the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"ce1d97d1-65b5-4f08-9336-8d1a5a80f395\">long-term advantages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of learning an instrument <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"ed76bcd5-4341-42cf-998e-4f5603cba55c\">is increasing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310154\" id=\"question-wrapper-310154\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The studies mentioned in the first paragraph</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. confirm a link between musical training and intelligence.</li> <li>B. present misleading information about the value of learning an instrument.</li> <li>C. suggest that there are undiscovered benefits to studying music.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"2d8d0207-dc5c-4d5a-b362-42f2f0d383de\">cast doubt on a belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> about the effects of taking music lessons.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310155\" id=\"question-wrapper-310155\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the second paragraph, there may be many benefits to studying music,</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. even for those who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"810283b0-bab7-4224-8bab-7477fd3af255\">begin learning in adulthood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</li> <li>B. providing the person learns the correct techniques.</li> <li>C. especially if the person practises on a regular basis.</li> <li>D. particularly if the person plays a range of different instruments.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310156\" id=\"question-wrapper-310156\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The phrase ‘this might well be the case’ in the fourth paragraph suggests that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. music lessons and long-term physical well-being may be connected.</li> <li>B. the&nbsp;ability to learn music may depend on neurological features.</li> <li>C. learning an instrument may have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"2fd8128b-ee3f-4b27-acbf-8175f72f209e\">lasting impact on brain function<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</li> <li>D. older people’s brains may be better suited to studying music than those of children.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310157\" id=\"question-wrapper-310157\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which aspect of playing an instrument was included in Hanna-Pladdy’s follow-up study but not in her first study?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the number of years that the person had played.</li> <li>B. at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"3e13b776-746c-4253-bcea-84cabe5252b5\">which age the person began<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> having lessons.</li> <li>C. the length of time since the person last played.</li> <li>D. how the person had practised as a child.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310158\" id=\"question-wrapper-310158\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What do Hanna-Pladdy’s studies suggest about people’s general education?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Studying music <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"3e9a776b-7c9c-4e79-9808-a6350ceb7d79\">compensates for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> an otherwise <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"f10a688d-25ce-43c8-8f1c-99c09c0dcc8e\">limited level of education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Learning to play an instrument improves educational performance.</li> <li>C. Highly educated people are more likely to benefit from music training.</li> <li>D. Level of education makes no difference to a person’s musical ability.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below. Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"37b44452-16d4-4dd9-93f3-4dc0812d58d1\">comparing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> the brains of people who had never played an instrument with those who played for a living.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"88d31a2a-c12a-4089-87a7-75c52d71fd48\">activating many different parts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of the brain at the same time.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"7569a895-a341-456a-8c5d-e5a53daf252a\">teaching a group of older people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to play an instrument.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"a6d7d462-018b-430a-97f5-b9d98ae12d5c\">engaging complex physical skills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. discovering which group of people becomes the best musicians.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. having played an instrument for a considerable length of time.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310159\" id=\"question-wrapper-310159\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Brenda Hanna-Pladdy believes musical training <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"23c6709e-78a5-46a5-80f5-19b7fa849fe8\">strengthens the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> by</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310160\" id=\"question-wrapper-310160\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The research undertaken by Gottfried Schlaug <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"b020fe28-1efa-401f-83ca-c6f2321fe3c2\">focused on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310161\" id=\"question-wrapper-310161\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to Alison Balbag, playing an instrument is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"d0162889-c4bb-40d5-8156-c8b207eeb31f\">unique experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> because it involves</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310162\" id=\"question-wrapper-310162\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Nina Kraus believes there is a link between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"1f57c0e7-be3c-4d39-ab9b-cc06f6fa8c48\">better hearing in later life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> and the experience of</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310163\" id=\"question-wrapper-310163\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"74afe0b2-cb27-4590-9423-a37034cee267\">Jennifer Bugos’s study involved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"2d8d0207-dc5c-4d5a-b362-42f2f0d383de 557ff3af-956b-4ffc-8e25-418aa3b6415e","qNum":"28 31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"found no evidence"},{"uid":"2d8d0207-dc5c-4d5a-b362-42f2f0d383de","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"cast doubt on a belief","passagePhrase":"to support this idea"},{"uid":"1278b114-ed33-4e99-b387-81fd3fff5991","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"findings","passagePhrase":"IQs of"},{"uid":"1278b114-ed33-4e99-b387-81fd3fff5991 96d2d27e-fcbd-4606-84ae-b432f0fdd7c1","qNum":"28 31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"pre-school children"},{"uid":"96d2d27e-fcbd-4606-84ae-b432f0fdd7c1","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"who attended several weeks of music classes"},{"uid":"ed76bcd5-4341-42cf-998e-4f5603cba55c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Evidence ... is increasing","passagePhrase":"A growing number of studies show"},{"uid":"ce1d97d1-65b5-4f08-9336-8d1a5a80f395","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"long-term advantages","passagePhrase":"benefits as we age"},{"uid":"810283b0-bab7-4224-8bab-7477fd3af255 c9c031bd-fc8c-4880-afef-a4c6a715b88a","qNum":"29 32","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"take up music"},{"uid":"810283b0-bab7-4224-8bab-7477fd3af255","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"begin learning in adulthood","passagePhrase":"for the first time in mid-life or beyond"},{"uid":"a6d7d462-018b-430a-97f5-b9d98ae12d5c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"engaging complex physical skills","passagePhrase":"specific types of motor control and coordination"},{"uid":"23c6709e-78a5-46a5-80f5-19b7fa849fe8","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"strengthens the brain","passagePhrase":"brain boost"},{"uid":"b020fe28-1efa-401f-83ca-c6f2321fe3c2","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"focused on","passagePhrase":"Harvard neurologist Gottfried Schlaug found"},{"uid":"37b44452-16d4-4dd9-93f3-4dc0812d58d1","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"comparing","passagePhrase":"brains of adult professional musicians ... than the brains of non-musicians"},{"uid":"d0162889-c4bb-40d5-8156-c8b207eeb31f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"unique experience","passagePhrase":"What’s unique about playing an instrument"},{"uid":"88d31a2a-c12a-4089-87a7-75c52d71fd48","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"activating many different parts","passagePhrase":"wide array of brain regions ... work together simultaneously"},{"uid":"2fd8128b-ee3f-4b27-acbf-8175f72f209e","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"lasting impact on brain function","passagePhrase":"cutting across a broad swath of its regions ... ripple effects through the decades"},{"uid":"3e13b776-746c-4253-bcea-84cabe5252b5","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"which age the person began","passagePhrase":"starting musical training before the age of nine"},{"uid":"f10a688d-25ce-43c8-8f1c-99c09c0dcc8e","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"limited level of education","passagePhrase":"lowest level of general education ... lack of cognitive stimulation"},{"uid":"3e9a776b-7c9c-4e79-9808-a6350ceb7d79","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"compensates for","passagePhrase":"made up for"},{"uid":"be57ea01-64d9-41ed-bba2-b63c9e5b4f5c","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"trained the longest—between four and fourteen years"},{"uid":"1f57c0e7-be3c-4d39-ab9b-cc06f6fa8c48","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"better hearing in later life","passagePhrase":"hearing tends to decline as we age"},{"uid":"74afe0b2-cb27-4590-9423-a37034cee267","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Jennifer Bugos’s study involved","passagePhrase":"Jennifer Bugos studied the impact of"},{"uid":"7569a895-a341-456a-8c5d-e5a53daf252a","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"teaching a group of older people","passagePhrase":"elementary piano instruction on adults between the ages of 60 and 85"},{"uid":"c9c031bd-fc8c-4880-afef-a4c6a715b88a","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"take up an instrument","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_25":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Rubber</span></b></p><p><i><span>T. and W. Musgrove discuss the origins and early uses of rubber</span></i></p><p><span>Rubber plants are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"da1fee1c-0a7e-4e5b-824f-cfa5daef8493\">spread right across the globe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"da1fee1c-0a7e-4e5b-824f-cfa5daef8493\">grow in many different habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. One might think, therefore, that humankind has known about rubber for thousands of years. Yet, unlike other crops of economic importance, rubber led a relatively anonymous life until the last 150 years or so. The Indians of South America appear to be the first people to have understood the properties of rubber. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"b5a0a5b1-5584-4b58-9b97-f7e1b6fd0fba\">Aztecs of what is now Mexico<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> were the first to be recorded using the substance. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c19ff34a-09c0-40f9-a13e-0165f3e51685\">wall painting from the sixth century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> depicts a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"1ad7c084-d79f-4d18-bddd-ae82aaee0844\">tribute offering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of crude rubber. After Columbus arrived and the Spanish influx followed, more evidence of Native American use began to appear. Antonio de Herrera y Tordesillas describes a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"1ad7c084-d79f-4d18-bddd-ae82aaee0844\">ritual game<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> played with a rubber ball at the court of the Aztec Emperor Montezuma II. The Mayan and Toltec people are known to have taken part in similar activities.</span></p><p><span>Rubber was also used to make raincoats, shoes, jars, torches and musical instruments. All of these were made from the indigenous <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"95e88425-5f09-49a2-98b2-5d1b980ef82a\">Castilla elastica<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. The Para rubber plant, now favoured for rubber cultivation, does not grow in the Mexican region. The first description of latex (liquid rubber) extraction was made by Juan de Torquemada. He noted that the Native Americans had a clever solution if no receptacle was at hand. They would place the latex on their bodies to allow it to solidify. However, no real European interest in rubber was shown for many years.</span></p><p><span>This finally changed in 1735. That year, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"004b8d93-139c-46e6-b135-98258642b03e\">Charles de la Condamine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, a French mathematician, published an account of his journey to South America. The journey was undertaken on behalf of the Paris Academy of Sciences. Its purpose was to measure an arc of the meridian line on the equator. However, the journey home was to turn out to be more significant than the true purpose of the trip. Condamine explored Brazil and Peru along the way. He discovered how the local people used a single piece of coagulated latex to make boots. The boots were impervious to water, and when smoked they looked like real leather.</span></p><p><span>In 1747, the first description of the rubber tree and latex tapping was made. It came from François Fresneau, a military engineer and amateur botanist. Fresneau was posted to French Guiana at the time. His detailed observations gave Europeans a clearer picture of how rubber could be collected. Together, the publications of Condamine and Fresneau created considerable excitement among French scientists. They began searching for a solvent that could turn crude rubber into a substance for commercial exploitation.</span></p><p><span>In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"94647195-959f-440c-8c0d-fb40e7f71c24\">1818<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, a British medical student named James Syme <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a0dd950f-adb2-48a7-b6d1-ebcc04d2b574\">first used rubber to make<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> waterproof cloth. Another early use of the substance was as an eraser of pencil marks, which is how it got the name 'rubber'. This was complemented by balloons, rubber bands, braces, boots for the army and other ideas. These met with varying degrees of success. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"c123d272-470b-4fa8-b03e-77d88a21747e\">1820<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, Thomas Hancock invented a machine he called the 'masticator'. Hancock was an English manufacturer of rubber goods such as driving belts, industrial rollers and hoses. His <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"70273333-c89f-4aec-84b0-0c474cf34377\">machine chewed up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> waste strips <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"70273333-c89f-4aec-84b0-0c474cf34377\">for re-use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. It was discovered that the masticated rubber was more malleable, while keeping much of its elasticity. In Scotland at the same time, Charles Mackintosh had discovered a way to use rubber as a waterproofing material, and he patented this process in 1823. Hancock and Mackintosh joined forces in 1834. Three years later, Hancock invented a machine for spreading rubber onto material.</span></p><p><span>Despite their beneficial qualities, such as waterproofing, rubber goods were still not particularly popular. They had some major flaws, including the fact that they dissolved malodorously. They also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"09532d65-5c43-4e4e-a45f-e63cfb5037e9\">became pliant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8b14967e-2e51-434c-9b71-aba6cf1078be\">warm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"49df6cc4-f183-4492-9f66-3683457bda43\">rigid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8b14967e-2e51-434c-9b71-aba6cf1078be\">cold<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Then in 1839, the American Charles Goodyear discovered that it was possible <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"ee15a8b2-32ef-4916-a16f-3fbf28808b1d\">to stabilise rubber<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. The method involved mixing it with sulphur while exposing it to heat. He called this process <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5 10\" data-uid=\"898a8558-0fba-4cd7-aaff-ee6028c2cbf4 bc661db7-2287-4e92-bbb8-5a13ffc8a1fc\">vulcanisation</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. With this discovery, the full versatility of this extraordinary substance <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"49df6cc4-f183-4492-9f66-3683457bda43\">became<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> apparent. Rubber goods could now be manufactured with all the beneficial qualities of the material. These included durability, elasticity and variability. The goods were no longer sticky, soluble or governed by the vagaries of the weather. The economic potential of rubber was now clearly evident. It played an important role in the Industrial Revolution. It was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3aa3f22f-b35a-434f-9d0e-13183ccdf3f3\">used in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the steam engines found in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"cfe8dc9e-8936-44af-b28f-2beaca5d7ced\">factories, mills, mines and railways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Rubber made a triumphant entrance as a new and innovative material at the Great Exhibition of 1851. Shoes, airbeds, furniture and clothing made from newly improved rubber were proudly displayed there.</span></p><p><span>One of the most important rubber inventions was made in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"e93a7580-a86c-4681-a49e-99dfabd304ec\">1888<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. An Irishman called <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"dac523f4-2e3a-42fb-a037-ec026730cad5\">John Boyd Dunlop produced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> the first pneumatic tyre. Solid rubber tyres had been used for the previous 18 years. However, Dunlop's new design, which he updated in 1890, immediately became popular. In 1895, Dunlop's tyres were first used in motor cars. With the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"d038e35b-0725-481b-b2b3-9f7c4e21896e\">mass production of cars just over the horizon<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, the rubber industry had never looked healthier. The <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9ca0799f-1064-4587-a648-effa5604416f\">import levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of rubber over the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"3befc3d1-3ce2-44f3-b38a-c1b614ffb9c7\">nineteenth century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> bear witness to its irrepressible <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9ca0799f-1064-4587-a648-effa5604416f\">rise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. In 1830, Britain had imported just 211 kg of crude rubber. By 1857, this had risen to 10,000 kg. By 1874, levels were just under six times as much again.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1–6 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310164\" id=\"question-wrapper-310164\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Rubber plants <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"da1fee1c-0a7e-4e5b-824f-cfa5daef8493\">grow only in certain regions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of the world.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310165\" id=\"question-wrapper-310165\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"b5a0a5b1-5584-4b58-9b97-f7e1b6fd0fba\">area now known as Mexico<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> had already made <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"1ad7c084-d79f-4d18-bddd-ae82aaee0844\">practical use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of rubber <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c19ff34a-09c0-40f9-a13e-0165f3e51685\">by the sixth century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310166\" id=\"question-wrapper-310166\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Rubber from the Castilla elastica plant is of poorer quality than that from the Para plant.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310167\" id=\"question-wrapper-310167\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"004b8d93-139c-46e6-b135-98258642b03e\">French mathematician<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> inspired real interest in rubber amongst Europeans.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310168\" id=\"question-wrapper-310168\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The process of vulcanisation was discovered by accident.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310169\" id=\"question-wrapper-310169\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9ca0799f-1064-4587-a648-effa5604416f\">Imports<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of crude rubber into Britain <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9ca0799f-1064-4587-a648-effa5604416f\">fell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> during the nineteenth century.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The Commercial Development of Rubber</span></b></p><p><span>Early European travellers gave accounts of various rubber objects in use in Central and South America, and these accounts created interest in the commercial exploitation of rubber. In 1818, (7)______ was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a0dd950f-adb2-48a7-b6d1-ebcc04d2b574\">produced using rubber<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, and in 1820, a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"70273333-c89f-4aec-84b0-0c474cf34377\">machine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> was invented <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"70273333-c89f-4aec-84b0-0c474cf34377\">for recycling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)______ of rubber. Over the next few years, other attempts were made <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"ee15a8b2-32ef-4916-a16f-3fbf28808b1d\">to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> improve rubber, but some problems remained. For example, rubber products smelt bad when they were dissolved, and could <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"09532d65-5c43-4e4e-a45f-e63cfb5037e9 49df6cc4-f183-4492-9f66-3683457bda43\">turn</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> either <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"09532d65-5c43-4e4e-a45f-e63cfb5037e9\">soft<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> or (9)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8b14967e-2e51-434c-9b71-aba6cf1078be\">depending on the temperature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. However, in 1839, a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"bc661db7-2287-4e92-bbb8-5a13ffc8a1fc\">new process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to (10)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"ee15a8b2-32ef-4916-a16f-3fbf28808b1d\">the substance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> greatly increased its potential. During the Industrial Revolution, rubber was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3aa3f22f-b35a-434f-9d0e-13183ccdf3f3\">fitted into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)______ operating in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"cfe8dc9e-8936-44af-b28f-2beaca5d7ced\">several workplaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Then in 1888, the (12)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"dac523f4-2e3a-42fb-a037-ec026730cad5\">was developed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, and a few years later, the (13)______ of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"d038e35b-0725-481b-b2b3-9f7c4e21896e\">motor car just about to begin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. </span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310170\" id=\"question-wrapper-310170\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">waterproof cloth</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310171\" id=\"question-wrapper-310171\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">waste strips</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310172\" id=\"question-wrapper-310172\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">rigid</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310173\" id=\"question-wrapper-310173\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">stabilise/stabilize</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310174\" id=\"question-wrapper-310174\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">steam engines</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310175\" id=\"question-wrapper-310175\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">pneumatic tyre</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310176\" id=\"question-wrapper-310176\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">mass production</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b5a0a5b1-5584-4b58-9b97-f7e1b6fd0fba","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"area now known as Mexico","passagePhrase":"Aztecs of what is now Mexico"},{"uid":"c19ff34a-09c0-40f9-a13e-0165f3e51685","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"by the sixth century","passagePhrase":"wall painting from the sixth century"},{"uid":"1ad7c084-d79f-4d18-bddd-ae82aaee0844","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"practical use","passagePhrase":"tribute offering ... ritual game"},{"uid":"95e88425-5f09-49a2-98b2-5d1b980ef82a","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Castilla elastica"},{"uid":"004b8d93-139c-46e6-b135-98258642b03e","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"French mathematician","passagePhrase":"Charles de la Condamine"},{"uid":"94647195-959f-440c-8c0d-fb40e7f71c24","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"1818"},{"uid":"a0dd950f-adb2-48a7-b6d1-ebcc04d2b574","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"produced using rubber","passagePhrase":"first used rubber to make"},{"uid":"c123d272-470b-4fa8-b03e-77d88a21747e","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"1820"},{"uid":"70273333-c89f-4aec-84b0-0c474cf34377","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"machine ... for recycling","passagePhrase":"machine chewed up ... for re-use"},{"uid":"09532d65-5c43-4e4e-a45f-e63cfb5037e9","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"soft","passagePhrase":"became pliant"},{"uid":"8b14967e-2e51-434c-9b71-aba6cf1078be","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"depending on the temperature","passagePhrase":"warm ... cold"},{"uid":"49df6cc4-f183-4492-9f66-3683457bda43","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"rigid ... became"},{"uid":"ee15a8b2-32ef-4916-a16f-3fbf28808b1d","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"to ... the substance","passagePhrase":"to stabilise rubber"},{"uid":"898a8558-0fba-4cd7-aaff-ee6028c2cbf4 bc661db7-2287-4e92-bbb8-5a13ffc8a1fc","qNum":"5 10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"vulcanisation"},{"uid":"3aa3f22f-b35a-434f-9d0e-13183ccdf3f3","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"fitted into","passagePhrase":"used in"},{"uid":"cfe8dc9e-8936-44af-b28f-2beaca5d7ced","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"several workplaces","passagePhrase":"factories, mills, mines and railways"},{"uid":"e93a7580-a86c-4681-a49e-99dfabd304ec","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"1888"},{"uid":"dac523f4-2e3a-42fb-a037-ec026730cad5","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"was developed","passagePhrase":"John Boyd Dunlop produced"},{"uid":"d038e35b-0725-481b-b2b3-9f7c4e21896e","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"motor car just about to begin","passagePhrase":"mass production of cars just over the horizon"},{"uid":"3befc3d1-3ce2-44f3-b38a-c1b614ffb9c7","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"nineteenth century"},{"uid":"09532d65-5c43-4e4e-a45f-e63cfb5037e9 49df6cc4-f183-4492-9f66-3683457bda43","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"turn","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"bc661db7-2287-4e92-bbb8-5a13ffc8a1fc","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"new process","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_26":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Learning from the Romans </span></b></p><p><i><span>How an ancient building material is influencing modern construction</span></i></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> In a quest to make concrete more durable and sustainable, an international team of geologists and engineers has found inspiration in the concrete used by the ancient Romans. The chemical secrets of Roman concrete have been uncovered in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"e7d15516-7c47-48a9-879c-2954e3941e06\">samples taken from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> a concrete Roman <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"90292daa-2a6e-43a3-b268-ded48cc6c3a7\">breakwater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. A breakwater is a barrier that is built out into the sea to protect coasts and harbors from the force of waves. This particular breakwater has spent the last 2,000 years submerged in seawater. The international team of researchers that collected the samples was led by Paulo Monteiro, a professor of civil and environmental engineering at the University of California, Berkeley. An analysis of samples from the ancient underwater site in Pozzuoli Bay, near Naples, Italy, pinpointed why the best Roman concrete was superior to most modern concrete.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>Concrete was the Roman Empire’s construction material of choice. It was used in land monuments such as the Pantheon in Rome, as well as in underwater and partially underwater coastal and harbor structures. Monteiro and his team were particularly interested in how the coastal and harbor structures endured the unforgiving saltwater environment. Chemical analysis of Roman concrete showed that it differs from the modern kind in several ways. One is the content of the cement that binds the material in the concrete. The most commonly used cement in recent decades has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e4412a5b-5ee7-4b33-bceb-c746532724b7\">Portland cement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Portland cement is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a5906fe9-a86b-4a31-9c46-f8798a8d4bfd\">compound of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> calcium, silicates, and hydrates (C-S-H). However, analysis of Roman concrete shows that it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a5906fe9-a86b-4a31-9c46-f8798a8d4bfd\">contains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> a significantly different cement. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"42a37bb5-2253-482b-a9ac-ad29d221ee16\">Roman cement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> contains aluminum, which is not found in Portland cement, and less silicon than is found in Portland cement. The resulting calcium-aluminum-silicate-hydrate (C-A-S-H) is an exceptionally stable cement.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> The recipe for the contents of Roman concrete was first described around 30 BC by Vitruvius, an engineer for the Roman Emperor Augustus. Volcanic ash was one of the ingredients, and it is now understood that this is crucial, as it is volcanic ash that contains the aluminum that ultimately gives Roman concrete its great durability. The Romans devised an efficient method of making concrete for coastal structures. They combined volcanic ash with lime, which added the calcium to the mix. This was then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"69067560-3cfa-4905-84b2-b4d579b8445c\">packed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, together with stones and chunks of rock, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"69067560-3cfa-4905-84b2-b4d579b8445c\">into wooden molds, which were then immersed in seawater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. The seawater instantly triggered a hot chemical reaction. The lime was hydrated by the seawater, which means that it incorporated water molecules into its structure, and reacted with the volcanic ash to cement the whole mixture together. This reaction formed the concrete that was used to build some of the most enduring structures in Western civilization.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> According to Marie Jackson, a member of the research team, Roman concrete is one of the most durable construction materials on the planet, and that was no accident. Shipping was the lifeline of political, economic, and military stability for the Roman Empire, so constructing harbors that would last was critical. ‘Over time, the Romans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3e99528f-c673-4718-8a52-592118568b48\">used less and less<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> concrete.’ ‘As the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ae2cb347-1a35-4115-971a-00c55c84b4a2\">Roman Empire declined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, and shipping declined, the need for the seawater concrete declined,’ said Jackson. ‘You could also argue that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ae2cb347-1a35-4115-971a-00c55c84b4a2\">original structures were built so well<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> that, once they were in place, they didn’t need to be replaced,’ she added.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Producing Roman concrete also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"9ebb1726-1ad3-421d-a6d3-1f2f09494057\">left a smaller carbon footprint than its modern counterpart<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. ‘It’s not that modern concrete isn’t good—it’s so good we use 19 billion tons of it a year,’ says Monteiro. ‘The problem is that manufacturing Portland cement accounts for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"56676bd2-c749-4b3f-a4b7-8408a4f26612\">seven percent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of the carbon dioxide that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c940737d-3f22-46bd-a6b8-d19840e6d2ec\">industry puts into the air<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.’ Portland cement holds most modern concrete together. However, making Portland cement <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"81214715-9b71-4b86-88de-ae58005beb45\">releases carbon dioxide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> into the atmosphere <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"81214715-9b71-4b86-88de-ae58005beb45\">from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"7860d3c5-6f70-4e42-b694-1e2ea88706cd\">burning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> fuel in order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"f6de3d87-6e5a-4f6d-918d-76e5a1f1457c\">heat a mix of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> limestone <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"f6de3d87-6e5a-4f6d-918d-76e5a1f1457c\">and clays<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to 1,450 degrees Celsius. The production of Roman concrete, however, was much cleaner, as less heat was needed. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"c965aa3b-9f65-49ce-ae1e-2fade9f620e3\">temperature that was a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> third <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"c965aa3b-9f65-49ce-ae1e-2fade9f620e3\">lower than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> that required for making Portland cement was sufficient for making Roman concrete.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"197eec61-d257-44fd-bd40-849843f63337 535a2c46-a321-497e-879e-3315a52ca000\">Some modern concrete no longer contains Portland cement</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>; <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"169a35f7-70ff-4d3f-b89f-b94f8cd76a8d 4a1141f4-fbdd-44d4-b549-5960068b9055\">instead, fly ash is used</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, which <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"5275fc8d-186d-45e9-922d-07ced6b3d772 6428949e-415e-495f-afec-fa5d06bb2a86\">causes fewer greenhouse gas emissions</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"5275fc8d-186d-45e9-922d-07ced6b3d772 6428949e-415e-495f-afec-fa5d06bb2a86\">Fly ash</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> is a waste product from burning coal, and the researchers are investigating whether volcanic ash would be a good, large-volume replacement in countries that cannot access fly ash easily. ‘There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ab03e58e-1eb4-4b79-8b2f-2a9217b8053e\">not enough fly ash in this world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> to replace half of the Portland cement being used,’ said Monteiro. ‘Many countries don’t have fly ash, so the idea is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"f755c3db-f15f-4eda-8cbd-c228982f0b21\">find alternative local materials<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that will work, including the kind of volcanic ash that the Romans used. Using these alternatives could replace 40 percent of the world’s demand for Portland cement.’</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> Cutting greenhouse gas emissions is one powerful incentive for finding a better way to provide the concrete the world needs; another is the need for stronger, longer-lasting buildings, bridges, and other structures. ‘In the middle 20th century, concrete <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"d3d1b35e-3a0b-4052-a5b5-a2c1962196b3\">structures were designed to last 50 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, and a lot of them are on borrowed time,’ Monteiro says. ‘Now we design buildings to last 100 to 120 years.’ Yet Roman <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"d3d1b35e-3a0b-4052-a5b5-a2c1962196b3\">harbor installations have survived 2,000 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of chemical attack from seawater and wave action. Stronger, longer-lasting modern concrete may be the legacy of a deeper understanding of how the Romans made their incomparable concrete.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A–G in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310177\" id=\"question-wrapper-310177\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an opinion on why the Romans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3e99528f-c673-4718-8a52-592118568b48\">reduced the amount<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of concrete they made for use in seawater</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310178\" id=\"question-wrapper-310178\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a5906fe9-a86b-4a31-9c46-f8798a8d4bfd\">list of the contents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of both Portland and Roman cement</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310179\" id=\"question-wrapper-310179\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an argument for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"f755c3db-f15f-4eda-8cbd-c228982f0b21\">finding substitutes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> for a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ab03e58e-1eb4-4b79-8b2f-2a9217b8053e\">limited resource<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that is used in making concrete</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310180\" id=\"question-wrapper-310180\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>information about the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"90292daa-2a6e-43a3-b268-ded48cc6c3a7\">structure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> from which the scientists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"e7d15516-7c47-48a9-879c-2954e3941e06\">took their<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> Roman concrete <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"e7d15516-7c47-48a9-879c-2954e3941e06\">samples<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310181\" id=\"question-wrapper-310181\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"9ebb1726-1ad3-421d-a6d3-1f2f09494057\">comparison of the environmental impacts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of making modern and Roman concrete</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310182\" id=\"question-wrapper-310182\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"d3d1b35e-3a0b-4052-a5b5-a2c1962196b3\">comparison of the durability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of Roman concrete with concrete produced today</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310183\" id=\"question-wrapper-310183\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>details of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"69067560-3cfa-4905-84b2-b4d579b8445c\">how the Romans used seawater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to make concrete</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Write the correct letters in boxes 21 and 22 on your answer sheet. According to the passage, which TWO of the following statements about fly ash are true?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"5275fc8d-186d-45e9-922d-07ced6b3d772\">Fly ash<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> results in <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"5275fc8d-186d-45e9-922d-07ced6b3d772 6428949e-415e-495f-afec-fa5d06bb2a86\">less damage</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> to the environment than Portland cement.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6428949e-415e-495f-afec-fa5d06bb2a86\">Fly ash<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> was used by the Romans as an alternative to volcanic ash.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Fly ash is <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"197eec61-d257-44fd-bd40-849843f63337 535a2c46-a321-497e-879e-3315a52ca000\">already used</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in the production of some concrete.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. All countries have access to fly ash resources.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Fly ash will soon replace volcanic ash.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310184\" id=\"question-wrapper-310184\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310185\" id=\"question-wrapper-310185\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23–26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The environmental effects of concrete production</span></b></p><p><span>Compared to modern concrete, which is produced using Portland cement, Roman concrete is more environmentally sustainable. According to Monteiro, the manufacture of Portland cement makes up as much as seven percent of the carbon dioxide <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c940737d-3f22-46bd-a6b8-d19840e6d2ec\">emitted by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> (23)______. This is because its production requires (24)______ to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"7860d3c5-6f70-4e42-b694-1e2ea88706cd\">burned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"81214715-9b71-4b86-88de-ae58005beb45\">generate the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> necessary <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"81214715-9b71-4b86-88de-ae58005beb45\">heat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. Specifically, a temperature of 1,450 degrees Celsius is required to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"f6de3d87-6e5a-4f6d-918d-76e5a1f1457c\">combine clays and<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> (25)______. By contrast, this level of heat was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"c965aa3b-9f65-49ce-ae1e-2fade9f620e3\">reduced by a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26)______ in the creation of Roman concrete, substantially diminishing its environmental impact.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310186\" id=\"question-wrapper-310186\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">industry</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310187\" id=\"question-wrapper-310187\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">fuel</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310188\" id=\"question-wrapper-310188\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">limestone</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310189\" id=\"question-wrapper-310189\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">third</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e7d15516-7c47-48a9-879c-2954e3941e06","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"took their ... samples","passagePhrase":"samples taken from"},{"uid":"90292daa-2a6e-43a3-b268-ded48cc6c3a7","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"structure","passagePhrase":"breakwater"},{"uid":"e4412a5b-5ee7-4b33-bceb-c746532724b7","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Portland cement"},{"uid":"a5906fe9-a86b-4a31-9c46-f8798a8d4bfd","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"list of the contents","passagePhrase":"compound of ... contains"},{"uid":"42a37bb5-2253-482b-a9ac-ad29d221ee16","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Roman cement"},{"uid":"69067560-3cfa-4905-84b2-b4d579b8445c","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"how the Romans used seawater","passagePhrase":"packed ... into wooden molds, which were then immersed in seawater"},{"uid":"3e99528f-c673-4718-8a52-592118568b48","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"reduced the amount","passagePhrase":"used less and less"},{"uid":"ae2cb347-1a35-4115-971a-00c55c84b4a2","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Roman Empire declined ... original structures were built so well"},{"uid":"9ebb1726-1ad3-421d-a6d3-1f2f09494057","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"comparison of the environmental impacts","passagePhrase":"left a smaller carbon footprint than its modern counterpart"},{"uid":"56676bd2-c749-4b3f-a4b7-8408a4f26612","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"seven percent"},{"uid":"c940737d-3f22-46bd-a6b8-d19840e6d2ec","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"emitted by","passagePhrase":"industry puts into the air"},{"uid":"81214715-9b71-4b86-88de-ae58005beb45","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"generate the ... heat","passagePhrase":"releases carbon dioxide ... from"},{"uid":"7860d3c5-6f70-4e42-b694-1e2ea88706cd","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"burned","passagePhrase":"burning"},{"uid":"f6de3d87-6e5a-4f6d-918d-76e5a1f1457c","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"combine clays and","passagePhrase":"heat a mix of ... and clays"},{"uid":"c965aa3b-9f65-49ce-ae1e-2fade9f620e3","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"reduced by a","passagePhrase":"temperature that was a ... lower than"},{"uid":"197eec61-d257-44fd-bd40-849843f63337 535a2c46-a321-497e-879e-3315a52ca000","qNum":"21 22","questionPhrase":"already used","passagePhrase":"Some modern concrete no longer contains Portland cement"},{"uid":"169a35f7-70ff-4d3f-b89f-b94f8cd76a8d 4a1141f4-fbdd-44d4-b549-5960068b9055","qNum":"21 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"instead, fly ash is used"},{"uid":"5275fc8d-186d-45e9-922d-07ced6b3d772 6428949e-415e-495f-afec-fa5d06bb2a86","qNum":"21 22","questionPhrase":"less damage","passagePhrase":"causes fewer greenhouse gas emissions ... Fly ash"},{"uid":"ab03e58e-1eb4-4b79-8b2f-2a9217b8053e","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"limited resource","passagePhrase":"not enough fly ash in this world"},{"uid":"f755c3db-f15f-4eda-8cbd-c228982f0b21","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"finding substitutes","passagePhrase":"find alternative local materials"},{"uid":"d3d1b35e-3a0b-4052-a5b5-a2c1962196b3","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"comparison of the durability","passagePhrase":"structures were designed to last 50 years ... harbor installations have survived 2,000 years"},{"uid":"5275fc8d-186d-45e9-922d-07ced6b3d772","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Fly ash","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"6428949e-415e-495f-afec-fa5d06bb2a86","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Fly ash","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_27":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Robert Louis Stevenson</span></b></p><p><i><span>The writer of some of the best-known stories in the English language, including Treasure Island and The Strange Case of Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde</span></i></p><p><span>It is more than 100 years since the death of the Scottish writer Robert Louis Stevenson on the South Pacific island of Samoa. And it seems that time has not been kind to Stevenson’s memory. Immediately after his death, his family and friends set to work to fashion the legend of Robert Louis Stevenson, or R.L.S. as he became known—one of the few writers familiar from his initials alone. Subsequent works of biography then turned him into a writer of almost religious importance. One example was critic Balfour, who in 1901 portrayed Stevenson’s family as ministering angels to the dying genius during his final illness. Similarly, the biographer Crouch <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"35c0b79e-c3d6-4e23-87c8-63a2313fb3c3\">absurdly overstated Stevenson’s significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"35c0b79e-c3d6-4e23-87c8-63a2313fb3c3\">placing him in the same company as those most revered names<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in English literature. The reaction to this nonsense was a number of highly critical assessments of Stevenson’s legacy in the 1920s.</span></p><p><span>Normally, the critical pendulum can be relied on to swing back again, but there are several aspects of Stevenson’s work that have until recently acted against a more balanced appraisal. First is the allegation that Stevenson was a mere master of linguistic fireworks who lacked moral depth. Some critics accused him of being a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a1598eb8-304a-44a3-81ca-eefa8dd69372\">literary charlatan, juggling words very prettily<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to strike effects that overawed an ignorant public and served <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a1598eb8-304a-44a3-81ca-eefa8dd69372\">to distract from the inadequacy of his ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Then there has been a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"a924bcfd-6bf2-4482-8a71-e020dc789711\">prejudice against the adventure story<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> as the proper medium for deep moral seriousness, a prejudice which is still extremely influential today. It seems that we can accept that an adventure film <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"cea20679-f043-4bfb-a420-6ef54b92ff76\">can successfully express profound moral truths<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, but we reject the same idea for a book. The absurdity of this becomes apparent when we think of writers like Joseph Conrad and Graham Greene, but it is no use pretending that this bias against adventure stories is not part of our high culture. A further problem is that Stevenson has often not found favour in the land of his birth because his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"ac78fd6b-4b48-4b8c-88d8-cf10d9271c54\">conservatism so often collides with the strong radical tradition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"a1883d63-789b-47b0-bb78-4e662a14edff\">Scotland<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. His many escapist stories and preference for living abroad have led to accusations that he camouflaged Scotland’s real problems. Lastly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"c5d2869f-dd33-4a12-b083-30feb070d143\">the high adventure of Stevenson’s own lifestyle has sometimes obscured his output<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. His globe-trotting, and above all the final phase of his life in Samoa, tended to make his own life a greater story than any he could devise. This was precisely what his friends feared would happen towards the end of his short life: his art might be overwhelmed by the drama of life in Samoa.</span></p><p><span>One consequence of this has been that Stevenson’s influence on other writers has too often been neglected. The writer and poet Oscar Wilde was deeply influenced by Stevenson, even though he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"d1041426-3819-453d-ba47-30302719ff35\">declared that Stevenson would have produced better work if he had lived in London<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> rather than Samoa. Stevenson tends to stick in the throat even of those writers who would like to spit him out, such as Shaw, who claimed to have learned from him that the romantic hero is always mocked by reality. Likewise, the writer Galsworthy, who was a determined critic, later changed his mind and said that the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"bb8da726-5bd2-44b8-a807-5588a9715cf5\">superiority of Stevenson over the novelist Hardy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> was that Stevenson was all life and Hardy, all death. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"390495d0-a5ff-4842-8be6-683ed40056b7\">influence on the novelist Chesterton<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"cc755611-0e6b-4652-8865-72c8234f8a35\">would also repay detailed study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, for it was through him that Stevenson has managed to cross the ages, emerging as an influence on the modernist movement and our own contemporary Latin American school of magical realism.</span></p><p><span>When making an assessment of his life and work, one question must inevitably be asked: was Robert Louis <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a405cbd2-c69f-45a8-bb93-fe8479fc3a60\">Stevenson<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> Scotland’s greatest writer of English prose? For most commentators this honour falls to Sir Walter Scott, author of Ivanhoe among many other classic novels, and it is true that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f2b84f18-4f4e-415f-b0db-4553d8352064\">in terms of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"ee551932-175d-46ae-988d-2a7ef0432d04\">craftsmanship, precision and the ability to minutely regulate language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> to create the desired effect, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f2b84f18-4f4e-415f-b0db-4553d8352064\">Scott takes the prize<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. However, this is not the same thing at all as inherent talent: by way of comparison one may take the example of the two great Russian composers Shostakovich and Prokofiev, of whom the former had learned more precise skills of execution but the latter’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"096bb7d8-c092-4043-bcb1-4222e7600364\">intrinsic genius was greater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, and so it seems to be with Scott and Stevenson. Admittedly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"cd5c6b73-b83a-44ab-80bd-f5dc6c7afa43\">Scott’s detailed style<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> does permit his stories to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"664bd9fb-d608-4b3a-a6d8-9d63fcb29af7\">explore levels of tragedy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> that are beyond Stevenson’s reach, but in this regard they have the musty smell of the museum, somehow artificial and removed from modern-day reality. On the other hand, Stevenson’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"502f15fc-82a2-409c-8088-aba50bc70419\">skill with plotting and narrative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> give his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e6c54add-ebb2-4b69-9862-8a6931880e8d\">books<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> a timeless quality, so that they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e6c54add-ebb2-4b69-9862-8a6931880e8d\">still live today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. And Stevenson was also the shrewder <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"73b306d2-67ee-4ef8-ac54-c46639507ba8\">judge of behaviour and psychology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. For example, his compelling description of a man with a split personality in The Strange Case of Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde has proved so accessible and accurate that the expression “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8478b2ed-f808-4475-8693-b2e13183b00a\">Jekyll and Hyde” has entered common English usage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Even if we do not see a revival of critical interest in this great Scottish writer, it is to be hoped that readers go back to Robert Louis Stevenson’s magnificent stories and reassess this neglected genius.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310190\" id=\"question-wrapper-310190\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the opinion of the writer, the biographers Balfour and Crouch</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. misunderstood Stevenson’s religious beliefs.</li> <li>B. overestimated other writers’ influence on Stevenson.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"35c0b79e-c3d6-4e23-87c8-63a2313fb3c3\">elevated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> Stevenson <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"35c0b79e-c3d6-4e23-87c8-63a2313fb3c3\">above his true status<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> as a writer.</li> <li>D. understated the role played by Stevenson’s family.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310191\" id=\"question-wrapper-310191\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the writer’s main point about Stevenson in the second paragraph?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The ethical nature of his stories was often criticised.</li> <li>B. The public judges him more fairly than the critics.</li> <li>C. Recent criticism of him has been justified.</li> <li>D. Critics&nbsp;argued that his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a1598eb8-304a-44a3-81ca-eefa8dd69372\">style covered up his faults<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310192\" id=\"question-wrapper-310192\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the writer, the adventure story</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. can be used by writers to tell moral stories.</li> <li>B. is more fashionable today than in the past.</li> <li>C. has been used by other writers but not by Stevenson.</li> <li>D. is more appropriate for books than for films.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310193\" id=\"question-wrapper-310193\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What point does the writer make about Stevenson and Scotland?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. His unflattering stories about Scotland angered many Scots.</li> <li>B. His <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"ac78fd6b-4b48-4b8c-88d8-cf10d9271c54\">ideas contrasted with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> those of many Scots.</li> <li>C. He demonstrated great sympathy for Scotland’s problems.</li> <li>D. He was not considered a true Scot as he was not born there.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310194\" id=\"question-wrapper-310194\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the writer, Stevenson’s own lifestyle</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. attracted more attention than his books.</li> <li>B. did not prepare him for living in Samoa.</li> <li>C. was envied by his friends.</li> <li>D. was responsible for his early death.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310195\" id=\"question-wrapper-310195\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Although Oscar Wilde admired Robert Louis Stevenson very much, he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"d1041426-3819-453d-ba47-30302719ff35\">believed Stevenson could have written greater works<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310196\" id=\"question-wrapper-310196\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Robert Louis Stevenson encouraged Oscar Wilde to start writing in the first place.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310197\" id=\"question-wrapper-310197\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Galsworthy <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"bb8da726-5bd2-44b8-a807-5588a9715cf5\">respected Hardy’s works more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> than Stevenson’s.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310198\" id=\"question-wrapper-310198\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>There is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"cc755611-0e6b-4652-8865-72c8234f8a35\">need to study in detail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> Stevenson’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"390495d0-a5ff-4842-8be6-683ed40056b7\">influence on Chesterton<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Complete the summary using the list of words, A–I, below. Write the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 36–40 on your answer sheet.</p> <p>A. natural ability</p> <p>B. romance</p> <p>C. colorful language</p> <p>D. critical acclaim</p> <p>E. humor</p> <p>F. technical control</p> <p>G. storytelling</p> <p>H. depth</p> <p>I. human nature</p> <p><strong>Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson</strong></p> <p>A lot of people believe that Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson are the most influential writers in the history of Scotland, but Sir Walter Scott is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f2b84f18-4f4e-415f-b0db-4553d8352064\">more proficient in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> (36)______, while Stevenson has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"096bb7d8-c092-4043-bcb1-4222e7600364\">better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> (37)______.</p> <p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"cd5c6b73-b83a-44ab-80bd-f5dc6c7afa43\">Scott’s books<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"664bd9fb-d608-4b3a-a6d8-9d63fcb29af7\">illustrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> (38)______, especially in terms of tragedy, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e6c54add-ebb2-4b69-9862-8a6931880e8d\">many readers prefer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> Stevenson’s (39)______. What’s more, Stevenson’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"73b306d2-67ee-4ef8-ac54-c46639507ba8\">understanding of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> (40)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8478b2ed-f808-4475-8693-b2e13183b00a\">gave his works a lasting appeal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310199\" id=\"question-wrapper-310199\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310200\" id=\"question-wrapper-310200\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310201\" id=\"question-wrapper-310201\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310202\" id=\"question-wrapper-310202\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310203\" id=\"question-wrapper-310203\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"35c0b79e-c3d6-4e23-87c8-63a2313fb3c3","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"elevated ... above his true status","passagePhrase":"absurdly overstated Stevenson’s significance ... placing him in the same company as those most revered names"},{"uid":"a1598eb8-304a-44a3-81ca-eefa8dd69372","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"style covered up his faults","passagePhrase":"literary charlatan, juggling words very prettily ... to distract from the inadequacy of his ideas"},{"uid":"a924bcfd-6bf2-4482-8a71-e020dc789711","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"prejudice against the adventure story"},{"uid":"cea20679-f043-4bfb-a420-6ef54b92ff76","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"can successfully express profound moral truths"},{"uid":"ac78fd6b-4b48-4b8c-88d8-cf10d9271c54","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"ideas contrasted with","passagePhrase":"conservatism so often collides with the strong radical tradition"},{"uid":"a1883d63-789b-47b0-bb78-4e662a14edff","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Scotland"},{"uid":"c5d2869f-dd33-4a12-b083-30feb070d143","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the high adventure of Stevenson’s own lifestyle has sometimes obscured his output"},{"uid":"d1041426-3819-453d-ba47-30302719ff35","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"believed Stevenson could have written greater works","passagePhrase":"declared that Stevenson would have produced better work if he had lived in London"},{"uid":"390495d0-a5ff-4842-8be6-683ed40056b7","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"influence on Chesterton","passagePhrase":"influence on the novelist Chesterton"},{"uid":"cc755611-0e6b-4652-8865-72c8234f8a35","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"need to study in detail","passagePhrase":"would also repay detailed study"},{"uid":"a405cbd2-c69f-45a8-bb93-fe8479fc3a60","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Stevenson"},{"uid":"f2b84f18-4f4e-415f-b0db-4553d8352064","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"more proficient in","passagePhrase":"in terms of ... Scott takes the prize"},{"uid":"ee551932-175d-46ae-988d-2a7ef0432d04","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"craftsmanship, precision and the ability to minutely regulate language"},{"uid":"096bb7d8-c092-4043-bcb1-4222e7600364","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"better","passagePhrase":"intrinsic genius was greater"},{"uid":"cd5c6b73-b83a-44ab-80bd-f5dc6c7afa43","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"Scott’s books","passagePhrase":"Scott’s detailed style"},{"uid":"664bd9fb-d608-4b3a-a6d8-9d63fcb29af7","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"illustrate","passagePhrase":"explore levels of tragedy"},{"uid":"502f15fc-82a2-409c-8088-aba50bc70419","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"skill with plotting and narrative"},{"uid":"e6c54add-ebb2-4b69-9862-8a6931880e8d","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"many readers prefer","passagePhrase":"books ... still live today"},{"uid":"73b306d2-67ee-4ef8-ac54-c46639507ba8","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"understanding of","passagePhrase":"judge of behaviour and psychology"},{"uid":"8478b2ed-f808-4475-8693-b2e13183b00a","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"gave his works a lasting appeal","passagePhrase":"Jekyll and Hyde” has entered common English usage"}]},"reading_u2_28":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>A survivor’s story</span></b></p><p><i><span>One native bird in New Zealand that has managed to survive the introduction of non-native species</span></i></p><p><span>As an island country with a fauna dominated by birds, New Zealand was once home to an owl species which is now extinct, the laughing owl, named for its distinctive cry. This bird was widespread throughout the islands when European settlers arrived in the middle of the 19th century and it remained in good numbers for some years thereafter. Where other native birds <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"537a2450-41d6-42bb-8255-4d3d5cd6ed51\">suffered from predation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> by the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"d32dfa7c-cfba-4317-95e1-ef6bb9d43f5e\">Polynesian rat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, the laughing owl turned the tables and adapted its diet to include the rodent. It was also capable of catching and killing the other New Zealand owl, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"2c10dc14-7243-45c3-ac50-f07d9d15ba13\">morepork<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, and even larger birds, such as the weka. However, the laughing owl was wiped out around the beginning of the 20th century, its demise caused by specimen collectors, habitat changes, and non-native predators, including cats and stoats. Surprisingly, it is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"c9c4550b-d65e-4dbc-9006-b77a2620b657\">smaller owl<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, the morepork, that has managed to survive until this day.</span></p><p><span>Speckled dark brown, with yellow eyes and long tails, they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"bbf0c384-eff2-4acb-baca-761c6c4716fd\">around<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> 29 centimetres <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"b10e4869-92e0-4822-a979-0f9d1c07a1bd\">long from head to tail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> and 175 grams in weight. Moreporks have fringes on the edge of their feathers, so they can fly almost silently and not alert potential prey. They have acute hearing and their large eyes are very sensitive to light.</span></p><p><span>Moreporks nest in tree hollows, in clumps of plants, or in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b5000e3c-1437-46b3-b5cc-254d1868d1b9\">cavities among<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"65c241d0-26ea-4db0-9acd-ecc6b7c34ee2\">rocks and roots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. In the wild, moreporks usually start nesting in October, although two specimens have been recorded nesting in mid-winter, possibly stimulated by an ample food supply. The female lays up to three white eggs, which she incubates for 20 to 30 days. During this time, she rarely hunts, and the male brings food to her.</span></p><p><span>Once the chicks hatch, she stays mainly in the nest until the young owls are fully feathered. When hatched, chicks are covered in light grey down and have their eyes closed. The eyes do not open until the eighth day after hatching. They can fly at around 35 days.</span></p><p><span>By day, moreporks sleep in roosts. By night, they hunt a variety of animals – mainly large invertebrates including scarab and huhu beetles, moths, caterpillars and spiders. They also take small birds and mice. They can find suitable food in a pine forest as well as a native forest. A morepork uses its sharp talons to catch or stun its prey, which it then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"7b4d66d9-5197-4900-93f0-c650fc1ede23\">carries away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"3a9857b4-ecd7-42ec-af76-243b0aec3d34\">in its bill<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. Moreporks are clever hunters, and birds such as robins, grey warblers and fantails can end up as their prey. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"f88da3c2-dd46-4831-893c-3856b1a7662b\">In the day<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, these small birds sometimes mob drowsy moreporks and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"21abfd64-5fc6-4f13-860f-e42e15c1f8ae\">chase them away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> from their roosts; they force the sleepy predators to search for a more peaceful spot.</span></p><p><span>Moreporks have proved to be ungracious hosts. Scientists trying to establish a population of plovers on Motuora Island in New Zealand’s Hauraki Gulf were mystified as to why only two birds survived out of the 75 placed there. The culprits turned out to be five pairs of moreporks that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"4b4bede3-1301-44ac-8be5-2612943966bb\">ate or chased away the new arrivals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Although moreporks are still considered to be relatively common, it is likely that numbers are in gradual decline due to predation and loss of habitat. As the female is a hole-nester, she is vulnerable to predators such as stoats and possums during the breeding season, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"5e0487b7-8843-45f0-8a8a-3fcd73dbb8e9\">eggs and chicks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> will also be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"aceff9cb-8064-477a-86e8-a43064a8756b\">at risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> from rats. The use of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"666847a7-d8a2-4f2e-a68f-bd228b10b1b0\">pesticides<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> is another possible threat to the owls, though not a direct one. As moreporks are at the top of the food chain, they could be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"e01df79b-2f97-4702-8a27-aeceeb176b4b\">affected by an accumulative poison<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> by consuming prey that has ingested poison.</span></p><p><span>The New Zealand Department of Conservation is taking steps to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"63adff9e-28b7-47ee-8936-67a50e0c7315\">ensure the preservation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of New Zealand’s only native owl. The department is involved in measuring the population of moreporks and has put transmitters on a number of birds to determine survival and mortality. As well as being New Zealand’s only native owl, the morepork has symbolic and spiritual importance, so in monitoring the birds, it is hoped that the morepork will continue to survive and thrive.</span></p><p><span>At dusk, the melancholy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"7e6eee00-e2bb-464f-9970-861b0566bb3e\">sound of the morepork can be heard in forests and parks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> as it calls to other moreporks and claims territory. Its Māori name (ruru) echoes its two-part cry. In the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"2fd033ff-b928-46ff-a96c-fc2b3ebe41ef\">tradition of the Māori people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> of New Zealand, the morepork, or ruru, was often seen as a careful guardian. A number of sayings referred to the bird’s alertness. As a bird of the night, it was associated with the spirit world. Moreporks were believed to act as messengers to the gods in the heavens, flying along spiritual paths in the sky. They were the mediums used to communicate with the gods. The occasional high, piercing call of the morepork signified bad news, but the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"aec44648-cb75-42f8-ad35-49e60814d0d5\">lower-pitched<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and more common “ruru” call <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9cee08c5-37b1-4922-802e-c99e575f3978\">heralded good news<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1 – 7 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310204\" id=\"question-wrapper-310204\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"c15aa1f4-97dd-4214-9b04-8c5ffba5f65c\">Early European settlers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> made detailed studies of the morepork.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310205\" id=\"question-wrapper-310205\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Polynesian rat had a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"537a2450-41d6-42bb-8255-4d3d5cd6ed51\">negative effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> on the number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"43b6d3b8-016f-4dcb-b67d-22efbd18a2f4\">laughing owls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310206\" id=\"question-wrapper-310206\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The laughing owl was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"c9c4550b-d65e-4dbc-9006-b77a2620b657\">larger than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the morepork.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310207\" id=\"question-wrapper-310207\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9851c925-98d0-4f4d-a752-9f0de05caf70\">Rats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> pose a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"aceff9cb-8064-477a-86e8-a43064a8756b\">risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"5e0487b7-8843-45f0-8a8a-3fcd73dbb8e9\">young moreporks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310208\" id=\"question-wrapper-310208\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The New Zealand Department of Conservation is hoping to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"63adff9e-28b7-47ee-8936-67a50e0c7315\">limit the population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of moreporks.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310209\" id=\"question-wrapper-310209\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Other bird species are frightened away when they hear the morepork’s cry.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310210\" id=\"question-wrapper-310210\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"2fd033ff-b928-46ff-a96c-fc2b3ebe41ef\">Māori tradition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"aec44648-cb75-42f8-ad35-49e60814d0d5\">low call<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> of the morepork had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9cee08c5-37b1-4922-802e-c99e575f3978\">negative associations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8 – 13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The Morepork</span></b></p><p><b><span>Appearance</span></b></p><p><span>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"bbf0c384-eff2-4acb-baca-761c6c4716fd\">approximately<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"b10e4869-92e0-4822-a979-0f9d1c07a1bd\">in length<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></span></p><p><span>• feathers with fringes to enable quiet flight</span></p><p><b><span>Nesting</span></b></p><p><span>• nests in trees, plants or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b5000e3c-1437-46b3-b5cc-254d1868d1b9\">spaces in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"65c241d0-26ea-4db0-9acd-ecc6b7c34ee2\">roots and (9<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>)______</span></p><p><span>• after about 35 days, baby moreporks are capable of leaving the nest</span></p><p><b><span>Hunting</span></b></p><p><span>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"7b4d66d9-5197-4900-93f0-c650fc1ede23\">transports its prey<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"3a9857b4-ecd7-42ec-af76-243b0aec3d34\">using its (10<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>)______</span></p><p><span>• can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"21abfd64-5fc6-4f13-860f-e42e15c1f8ae\">chased away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> by other birds <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"f88da3c2-dd46-4831-893c-3856b1a7662b\">during the (11<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>)______</span></p><p><span>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"4b4bede3-1301-44ac-8be5-2612943966bb\">attacked (12<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>)______ that had been introduced to Motuora Island</span></p><p><b><span>Threats</span></b></p><p><span>• may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"e01df79b-2f97-4702-8a27-aeceeb176b4b\">take in (13<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>)______ by eating prey affected by pesticides. </span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310211\" id=\"question-wrapper-310211\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">29/twenty-nine centimeters/cm/centimetres</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310212\" id=\"question-wrapper-310212\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">rocks</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310213\" id=\"question-wrapper-310213\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">bill</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310214\" id=\"question-wrapper-310214\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">day</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310215\" id=\"question-wrapper-310215\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">plovers</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310216\" id=\"question-wrapper-310216\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Poison</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"537a2450-41d6-42bb-8255-4d3d5cd6ed51","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"negative effect","passagePhrase":"suffered from predation"},{"uid":"d32dfa7c-cfba-4317-95e1-ef6bb9d43f5e","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Polynesian rat"},{"uid":"2c10dc14-7243-45c3-ac50-f07d9d15ba13","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"morepork"},{"uid":"c9c4550b-d65e-4dbc-9006-b77a2620b657","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"larger than","passagePhrase":"smaller owl"},{"uid":"bbf0c384-eff2-4acb-baca-761c6c4716fd","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"approximately","passagePhrase":"around"},{"uid":"b10e4869-92e0-4822-a979-0f9d1c07a1bd","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"in length","passagePhrase":"long from head to tail"},{"uid":"b5000e3c-1437-46b3-b5cc-254d1868d1b9","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"spaces in","passagePhrase":"cavities among"},{"uid":"65c241d0-26ea-4db0-9acd-ecc6b7c34ee2","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"roots and (9","passagePhrase":"rocks and roots"},{"uid":"7b4d66d9-5197-4900-93f0-c650fc1ede23","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"transports its prey","passagePhrase":"carries away"},{"uid":"3a9857b4-ecd7-42ec-af76-243b0aec3d34","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"using its (10","passagePhrase":"in its bill"},{"uid":"f88da3c2-dd46-4831-893c-3856b1a7662b","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"during the (11","passagePhrase":"In the day"},{"uid":"21abfd64-5fc6-4f13-860f-e42e15c1f8ae","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"chased away","passagePhrase":"chase them away"},{"uid":"4b4bede3-1301-44ac-8be5-2612943966bb","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"attacked (12","passagePhrase":"ate or chased away the new arrivals"},{"uid":"5e0487b7-8843-45f0-8a8a-3fcd73dbb8e9","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"young moreporks","passagePhrase":"eggs and chicks"},{"uid":"aceff9cb-8064-477a-86e8-a43064a8756b","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"risk","passagePhrase":"at risk"},{"uid":"666847a7-d8a2-4f2e-a68f-bd228b10b1b0","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"pesticides"},{"uid":"e01df79b-2f97-4702-8a27-aeceeb176b4b","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"take in (13","passagePhrase":"affected by an accumulative poison"},{"uid":"63adff9e-28b7-47ee-8936-67a50e0c7315","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"limit the population","passagePhrase":"ensure the preservation"},{"uid":"7e6eee00-e2bb-464f-9970-861b0566bb3e","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"sound of the morepork can be heard in forests and parks"},{"uid":"2fd033ff-b928-46ff-a96c-fc2b3ebe41ef","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Māori tradition","passagePhrase":"tradition of the Māori people"},{"uid":"aec44648-cb75-42f8-ad35-49e60814d0d5","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"low call","passagePhrase":"lower-pitched"},{"uid":"9cee08c5-37b1-4922-802e-c99e575f3978","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"negative associations","passagePhrase":"heralded good news"},{"uid":"c15aa1f4-97dd-4214-9b04-8c5ffba5f65c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Early European settlers","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"43b6d3b8-016f-4dcb-b67d-22efbd18a2f4","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"laughing owls","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"9851c925-98d0-4f4d-a752-9f0de05caf70","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Rats","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_29":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14–26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 on the following pages.</span></p><p><b><span>A new look for Talbot Park</span></b></p><p><i><span>Talbot Park, a housing project in Auckland, New Zealand, was once described as a ghetto, troubled by high rates of crime and vandalism. However, it has just been rebuilt at a cost of $48 m and the project reflects some new thinking about urban design.</span></i></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> The new Talbot Park is immediately eye-catching because the buildings look quite different to other state-housing projects in Auckland. 'There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d82e93e9-222d-45bf-b4ca-5bab0429c052\">no reason why<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> state housing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d82e93e9-222d-45bf-b4ca-5bab0429c052\">should look cheap<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in my view,' says architect Neil Cotton, one of the design team. 'In fact, I was anticipating a backlash by those who objected to the quality of what is provided with government money.' The tidy brick and wood apartments and townhouses would not look out of place in some of the city's most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d82e93e9-222d-45bf-b4ca-5bab0429c052\">affluent suburbs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, and this is a central theme of the Talbot Park philosophy. </span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Talbot Park is a triangle of government-owned land, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"db9d36c8-1ee3-4de2-b931-1aebff2bf279\">in the early 1960s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> was developed for state housing built around a linear garden that ran through the middle. Initially, there was a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3be5f932-7449-49e1-b43f-f3ef7da5d8b5\">strong sense of neighbourliness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Former residents recall how the garden played a big part in their childhoods — a place where kids came together to play softball, cricket and bullrush. 'We had respect for our neighbours and addressed them by title — Mr and Mrs so-and-so,' recalls Georgie Thompson, who grew up there in the 1960s. </span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> Exactly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"83e95aec-a62e-4ca5-a52f-d9fa0ea11456\">what went wrong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> with Talbot Park is unclear. The community began to change in the late 1970s as more immigrants moved in. The new arrivals didn't always integrate with the community and a 'them and us' mentality developed. In the process, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"83e95aec-a62e-4ca5-a52f-d9fa0ea11456\">standards dropped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> and the neighbourhood began to look <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"83e95aec-a62e-4ca5-a52f-d9fa0ea11456\">shabbier<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. The buildings themselves were also deteriorating and becoming run-down, petty crime was on the rise and the garden was considered <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"83e95aec-a62e-4ca5-a52f-d9fa0ea11456\">unsafe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. In 2002, Housing New Zealand decided the properties needed upgrading. The question was, how to avoid repeating the mistakes of the past? </span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> One controversial aspect of the upgrade is that the new development has actually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5f308408-cdaa-4c09-a8b0-90ec12f620ef\">made the density<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of housing in Talbot Park <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5f308408-cdaa-4c09-a8b0-90ec12f620ef\">greater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, putting 52 more homes on the same site. Doing this required a fresh approach summed up as 'mix and match'. The first priority was to mix up the housing by employing a <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 25\" data-uid=\"1b2a90e0-8051-461d-90e7-e7c68faaff61 d416b7e9-3a48-498e-9ab1-ec08d40c12ae\">variety of plans by different</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"d416b7e9-3a48-498e-9ab1-ec08d40c12ae\"> architects</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>: some of the accommodation is free-standing houses, some semi-detached, some low-level, multi-apartment blocks. By doing so, the development avoids the uniform appearance of so many state-housing projects, which residents complain denies them any sense of individual identity. The next goal was to prevent overspending by using efficient designs to maximise space from minimum room sizes. A no-frills, industrial approach to kitchens, bathrooms and flooring also helped optimise durability and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f54c0ba4-3e95-41f6-913d-207702bbeb72\">keep the project </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 26\" data-uid=\"0a4876ae-8f58-4314-805b-d16342b35a37 f54c0ba4-3e95-41f6-913d-207702bbeb72\">within</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"0a4876ae-8f58-4314-805b-d16342b35a37\"> budget</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Architecturally, the buildings are relatively conservative: fairly plain houses standing in a small garden. There's a slight reflection of the traditional Pacific beach house (a fale) but it's not over-played. 'It seems to us that low-cost housing is about getting as much amenity as you can for the money,' says architect Michael Thompson. Another key aspect of the 'mix and match' approach is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"43287397-724f-4ef2-9177-9dd418a09e90\">openness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>: one that not only lets residents see what is going on but also lets them know they are seen. The plan ensures there are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"43287397-724f-4ef2-9177-9dd418a09e90\">no cul-de-sacs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> or properties hidden from view, that the gardens are not enclosed by trees and that most boundary fences are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"43287397-724f-4ef2-9177-9dd418a09e90\">see-through<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> — a community contained but without walls. </span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><b><span>F.</span></b><span> The population today is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"af8f1a0c-f8a9-4c8c-b561-fb5ea372c8f9\">cosmopolitan<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>: 50% Pacific Islanders, 20% Māori, 15% Asian, 10% New Zealand European and the rest composed of immigrants from Russia, Ukraine and Iran. 'It was important that the buildings were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"79df72b8-fd26-4626-a076-a84f05281e9d\">sufficiently flexible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> to cater for the needs of people from a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"b4ddaa8a-9f3c-4f5f-83a9-02d2f4afb651\">wide variety of cultural backgrounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>,' explains designer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"e1f4d15b-bbbb-43e8-93ba-aa0d80e81f67\">James Lundy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Despite the quality of the buildings, however, there should be no doubt that Talbot Park and its surrounding suburb of Tāmaki are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"756074f0-034b-4167-8af4-5aaad63d7f22\">low socio-economic areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Of the 5,000 houses there, 55% are state houses, 28% privately owned (compared to about 65% nationally) and 17% private rental. The area has a high density of households with incomes in the $5,000 to $15,000 range and very few with an income over $70,000. That's in sharp contrast to the more affluent suburbs in Auckland. </span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"20\"><b><span>G.</span></b><span> Another important part of the new development is what Housing New Zealand calls '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"cefc7014-0e60-4160-a738-db42639e2ebb\">intensive tenancy management<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>'. Opponents of the project call it social control. 'The focus is on <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"436d3281-bd17-4705-8a06-5eba2ba080e3\">frequent </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20 22\" data-uid=\"436d3281-bd17-4705-8a06-5eba2ba080e3 cefc7014-0e60-4160-a738-db42639e2ebb\">inspections</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"436d3281-bd17-4705-8a06-5eba2ba080e3\">setting clear guidelines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and boundaries regarding the sort of behaviour we expect from tenants,' says <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"381ee1dc-1ba7-4013-a5da-67ed18d5ae18\">Graham Bodman<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, Housing New Zealand's regional manager. Strict rules apply: no loud parties after 10 pm, no washing on balcony rails and a requirement to keep properties tidy. The Tenancy Manager walks the site every day, knows everyone by name and deals with problems quickly. 'It's all based on the intensification,' adds <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"2424c773-c513-457c-a5e0-e8212b448add\">Stuart Bracey<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, project manager, noting that organising morning teas and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7b44df78-014b-4381-8398-1274a4826f65\">street barbecues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> helps tightly-packed residents <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20 23\" data-uid=\"57745dd7-7f00-4a92-b7e9-b180fdc036fe cefc7014-0e60-4160-a738-db42639e2ebb\">bond</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. So far it seems to be working, and many involved believe Talbot Park represents the way forward for state housing. </span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A–G. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i–x, in boxes 14 – 20 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. Some of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"83e95aec-a62e-4ca5-a52f-d9fa0ea11456\">problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that developed at Talbot Park </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. Where the residents lived while the work was being completed </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"d416b7e9-3a48-498e-9ab1-ec08d40c12ae\">Diverse building plans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> built within <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"0a4876ae-8f58-4314-805b-d16342b35a37\">financial limits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. The unexpectedly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d82e93e9-222d-45bf-b4ca-5bab0429c052\">high standard<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of the housing </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"af8f1a0c-f8a9-4c8c-b561-fb5ea372c8f9\">diverse population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"756074f0-034b-4167-8af4-5aaad63d7f22\">low-income area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. The experiences of one family living at Talbot Park today </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. How to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"cefc7014-0e60-4160-a738-db42639e2ebb\">co-ordinate and assist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> the people who live at Talbot Park </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. Raising the money to pay for the makeover </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3be5f932-7449-49e1-b43f-f3ef7da5d8b5\">close community<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"db9d36c8-1ee3-4de2-b931-1aebff2bf279\">original<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> Talbot Park development </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"x\"><span>x. An emphasis on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"43287397-724f-4ef2-9177-9dd418a09e90\">openness and visibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in the new design</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310217\" id=\"question-wrapper-310217\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310218\" id=\"question-wrapper-310218\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ix</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310219\" id=\"question-wrapper-310219\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310220\" id=\"question-wrapper-310220\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310221\" id=\"question-wrapper-310221\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">x</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310222\" id=\"question-wrapper-310222\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310223\" id=\"question-wrapper-310223\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph G</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following people (Questions 21–23) and the list of ideas below. Match each person with the correct idea, A–F. Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 21–23 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Ideas</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Good tenant management involves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"436d3281-bd17-4705-8a06-5eba2ba080e3\">supervision and regulation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. State housing must be built at minimum expense to the public.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Organising <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7b44df78-014b-4381-8398-1274a4826f65\">social events<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> helps tenants to live close together.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Mixed-race communities require <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"79df72b8-fd26-4626-a076-a84f05281e9d\">adaptable and responsive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> designs.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Complaints were expected about the high standard of the development.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. Too many rules and regulations will cause resentment from tenants.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310224\" id=\"question-wrapper-310224\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>James Lundy</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310225\" id=\"question-wrapper-310225\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Graham Bodman</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310226\" id=\"question-wrapper-310226\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Stuart Bracey</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The ‘mix and match’ strategy</span></b></p><p><span>A particular worry for critics was that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5f308408-cdaa-4c09-a8b0-90ec12f620ef\">increasing the (24<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>)______ of accommodation on the same site might revive the community's earlier social problems. To prevent this, a team of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"1b2a90e0-8051-461d-90e7-e7c68faaff61\">various (25<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>)______ worked on the project to ensure the buildings were not uniform. Further, they created pleasant, functional interiors that could still be built <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f54c0ba4-3e95-41f6-913d-207702bbeb72\">within their (26<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>)______. Finally, the absence of walls means Talbot Park is characterised by openness, making it easier to regulate behaviour within the community.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310227\" id=\"question-wrapper-310227\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">density</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310228\" id=\"question-wrapper-310228\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">architects</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310229\" id=\"question-wrapper-310229\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">budget</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"d82e93e9-222d-45bf-b4ca-5bab0429c052","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"high standard","passagePhrase":"no reason why ... should look cheap ... affluent suburbs"},{"uid":"db9d36c8-1ee3-4de2-b931-1aebff2bf279","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"original","passagePhrase":"in the early 1960s"},{"uid":"3be5f932-7449-49e1-b43f-f3ef7da5d8b5","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"close community","passagePhrase":"strong sense of neighbourliness"},{"uid":"83e95aec-a62e-4ca5-a52f-d9fa0ea11456","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"problems","passagePhrase":"what went wrong ... standards dropped ... shabbier ... unsafe"},{"uid":"5f308408-cdaa-4c09-a8b0-90ec12f620ef","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"increasing the (24","passagePhrase":"made the density ... greater"},{"uid":"1b2a90e0-8051-461d-90e7-e7c68faaff61 d416b7e9-3a48-498e-9ab1-ec08d40c12ae","qNum":"17 25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"variety of plans by different"},{"uid":"d416b7e9-3a48-498e-9ab1-ec08d40c12ae","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Diverse building plans","passagePhrase":"architects"},{"uid":"f54c0ba4-3e95-41f6-913d-207702bbeb72","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"within their (26","passagePhrase":"keep the project"},{"uid":"0a4876ae-8f58-4314-805b-d16342b35a37 f54c0ba4-3e95-41f6-913d-207702bbeb72","qNum":"17 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"within"},{"uid":"0a4876ae-8f58-4314-805b-d16342b35a37","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"financial limits","passagePhrase":"budget"},{"uid":"43287397-724f-4ef2-9177-9dd418a09e90","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"openness and visibility","passagePhrase":"openness ... no cul-de-sacs ... see-through"},{"uid":"af8f1a0c-f8a9-4c8c-b561-fb5ea372c8f9","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"diverse population","passagePhrase":"cosmopolitan"},{"uid":"79df72b8-fd26-4626-a076-a84f05281e9d","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"adaptable and responsive","passagePhrase":"sufficiently flexible"},{"uid":"b4ddaa8a-9f3c-4f5f-83a9-02d2f4afb651","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"wide variety of cultural backgrounds"},{"uid":"e1f4d15b-bbbb-43e8-93ba-aa0d80e81f67","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"James Lundy"},{"uid":"756074f0-034b-4167-8af4-5aaad63d7f22","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"low-income area","passagePhrase":"low socio-economic areas"},{"uid":"cefc7014-0e60-4160-a738-db42639e2ebb","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"co-ordinate and assist","passagePhrase":"intensive tenancy management"},{"uid":"436d3281-bd17-4705-8a06-5eba2ba080e3","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"supervision and regulation","passagePhrase":"frequent ... setting clear guidelines"},{"uid":"436d3281-bd17-4705-8a06-5eba2ba080e3 cefc7014-0e60-4160-a738-db42639e2ebb","qNum":"20 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"inspections"},{"uid":"381ee1dc-1ba7-4013-a5da-67ed18d5ae18","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Graham Bodman"},{"uid":"2424c773-c513-457c-a5e0-e8212b448add","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Stuart Bracey"},{"uid":"7b44df78-014b-4381-8398-1274a4826f65","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"social events","passagePhrase":"street barbecues"},{"uid":"57745dd7-7f00-4a92-b7e9-b180fdc036fe cefc7014-0e60-4160-a738-db42639e2ebb","qNum":"20 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"bond"},{"uid":"1b2a90e0-8051-461d-90e7-e7c68faaff61","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"various (25","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_30":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Pacific Navigation and Voyaging</span></b></p><p><i><span>How people migrated to the Pacific islands</span></i></p><p><span>The many tiny islands of the Pacific Ocean had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"011079f5-a1d2-4015-a817-ff424408af05\">no human population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> until ancestors of today’s islanders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"7e616a44-d3a7-44f5-99b4-eeaf1f1eabcb\">sailed from Southeast Asia<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in ocean-going canoes approximately 2,000 years ago. At the present time, the debate continues about exactly how they migrated such vast distances across the ocean, without any of the modern technologies we take for granted.</span></p><p><span>Although the romantic vision of some early twentieth-century writers of fleets of heroic navigators simultaneously setting sail <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a505734e-d26d-48e2-b983-5e79e6f0ce38\">had come to be considered by later investigators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to be exaggerated, no considered assessment of Pacific voyaging was forthcoming until 1956 when the American historian Andrew Sharp published his research. Sharp challenged the ‘heroic vision’ by asserting that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"f658e2e1-0b23-4d56-b2d9-c404cb6d1050\">expertise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of the navigators <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"f658e2e1-0b23-4d56-b2d9-c404cb6d1050\">was limited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, and that the settlement of the islands was not systematic, being more dependent on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"a4554ec0-dfb2-44dc-9336-4f0953212172\">good fortune<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> by drifting canoes. Sharp’s theory was widely challenged, and deservedly so. If nothing else, however, it did <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"8e8e8eda-090e-4ecb-954a-813788a12fb9\">spark renewed interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> in the topic and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"8e8e8eda-090e-4ecb-954a-813788a12fb9\">precipitated valuable new research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Since the 1960s a wealth of investigations has been conducted, and most of them, thankfully, have been of the ‘non-armchair’ variety. While it would be wrong to denigrate all ‘armchair’ research — that based on an examination of available published materials — it has turned out that so little progress had been made in the area of Pacific voyaging because most writers relied on the same old sources — travelers’ journals or missionary narratives compiled by unskilled observers. After Sharp, this began to change, and researchers conducted most of their investigations not in libraries, but in the field.</span></p><p><span>In 1965, David Lewis, a physician and experienced yachtsman, set to work using his own <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"2b7e0cf0-e4b2-40e0-81c8-5407d1e08af6\">unique philosophy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>: he took the yacht he had owned for many years and navigated through the islands in order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"bc54132d-c4ce-4ff3-8c0d-f4241bfb431d\">contact those men<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> who still find their way at sea using traditional methods. He then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c711f7b5-ea6a-497f-a448-6f0b5a1af4ca\">accompanied these men<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, in their traditional canoes, on test voyages from which all modern instruments were banished from sight, though Lewis secretly used them to confirm the navigator’s calculations. His most famous such voyage was a return trip of around 1,000 nautical miles between two islands in mid-ocean. Far from drifting, as proposed by Sharp, Lewis <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"fac09c29-0027-40e9-8731-fae29c320e53\">found that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> ancient navigators would have known <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"da7cc746-6e87-4e83-aa82-f8de0bf1ec22\">which course to steer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> by memorizing which stars rose and set in certain positions along the horizon, and this gave them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"da7cc746-6e87-4e83-aa82-f8de0bf1ec22\">fixed directions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> by which to steer their boats.</span></p><p><span>The geographer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"00fc5b90-1029-4a4f-a984-722ef96f9998\">Edwin Doran<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> followed a quite different approach. He was interested in obtaining <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"1db3be00-67dd-44cf-9a73-58ae311ff02a\">exact data<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> on canoe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"9bc35417-9c28-461a-8d72-df585640ef36\">sailing performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, and to that end employed the latest <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"56487178-7476-4fd5-99c7-9512fcdfb399\">electronic instrumentation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Doran traveled on board traditional sailing canoes in some of the most remote parts of the Pacific, all the while using his instruments to record canoe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"9bc35417-9c28-461a-8d72-df585640ef36\">speeds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> in different wind strengths — from gales to calms — and the angle canoes could sail relative to the wind. In the process, he provided the first really precise attributes of traditional sailing canoes.</span></p><p><span>A further contribution was made by Steven Horvath. As a physiologist, Horvath’s interest was not in navigation techniques or in canoes, but in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"dda825fb-a4be-44a9-975d-41505648b2a4\">physical capabilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of the men themselves. By adapting standard physiological techniques, Horvath was able to calculate the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"3bcb0765-05b9-4329-9eff-76890cf62406\">energy expenditure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> required to paddle canoes of this sort at times when there was no wind to fill the sails, or when the wind was contrary. He concluded that paddles, or perhaps long oars, could indeed have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"2a9c527d-a207-4fed-8c05-d0ff9d770b83\">propelled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> for long distances what were primarily sailing vessels.</span></p><p><span>Finally, a team led by P. Wall Garrard conducted important research, in this case by making investigations while remaining safely in the laboratory. Wall Garrard’s unusual method was to use the findings of linguists who had studied the languages of the Pacific islands, many of which are remarkably similar although the islands where they are spoken are sometimes thousands of kilometres apart. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f596a871-5c64-4e1d-b887-9024e700cc29\">Clever adaptation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of computer simulation techniques <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f596a871-5c64-4e1d-b887-9024e700cc29\">pioneered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> in other disciplines allowed him to produce convincing models suggesting the migrations were indeed systematic, but not simultaneous. Wall Garrard proposed the migrations should be seen not as a single journey made by a massed fleet of canoes, but as a series of ever more ambitious voyages, each pushing further into the unknown ocean.</span></p><p><span>What do we learn about Pacific navigation and voyaging from this research? Quite correctly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"1237a0b4-b0bd-40f4-bc63-61dc1c1488be\">none of the researchers tried to use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> their findings <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"1237a0b4-b0bd-40f4-bc63-61dc1c1488be\">to prove one theory or another<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>; experiments such as these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"8abcd921-62a0-488b-9c40-3fafa1c9ade5\">cannot categorically confirm or negate a hypothesis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"86788929-2783-4dd4-866f-73ab5f724aa9\">strength of this research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> lies in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"bb233168-000d-4433-b30d-7e0ecb0b0d77\">range of methodologies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> employed. When we splice together these findings we can propose that traditional navigators used a variety of canoe types, sources of information and navigation techniques, and it was this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0fc8453d-05d2-456d-9b50-493243e86e05\">adaptability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> which was their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e1037581-40c4-41af-88e9-67f0ece4b8e1\">greatest accomplishment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. These navigators observed the conditions prevailing at sea at the time a voyage was made and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0fc8453d-05d2-456d-9b50-493243e86e05\">altered their techniques accordingly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Furthermore, the canoes of the navigators were not drifting helplessly at sea but were most likely part of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"805cdff8-c6e5-44ea-8d22-cbdf2c915e14\">a systematic migration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>; as such, the Pacific peoples were able to view the ocean as an avenue, not a barrier, to communication <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"f13a8157-43cb-4b04-b3fd-b369e3d2921b\">before any other race on Earth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Finally, one unexpected but most welcome consequence of this research has been a renaissance in the practice of traditional voyaging. In some groups of islands in the Pacific today, young people are resurrecting the skills of their ancestors, when a few decades ago it seemed they would be lost forever.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310230\" id=\"question-wrapper-310230\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Pacific islands were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"011079f5-a1d2-4015-a817-ff424408af05\">uninhabited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> when migrants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"7e616a44-d3a7-44f5-99b4-eeaf1f1eabcb\">arrived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> by sea from Southeast Asia.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310231\" id=\"question-wrapper-310231\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Andrew Sharp was the first person to write about the migrants to the islands.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310232\" id=\"question-wrapper-310232\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Andrew Sharp believed migratory voyages were based more on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"a4554ec0-dfb2-44dc-9336-4f0953212172\">luck<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> than on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"f658e2e1-0b23-4d56-b2d9-c404cb6d1050\">skill<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310233\" id=\"question-wrapper-310233\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Despite being controversial, Andrew Sharp’s research had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"8e8e8eda-090e-4ecb-954a-813788a12fb9\">positive results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310234\" id=\"question-wrapper-310234\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Edwin Doran disagreed with the findings of Lewis’s research.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310235\" id=\"question-wrapper-310235\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>David Lewis’s research was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"2b7e0cf0-e4b2-40e0-81c8-5407d1e08af6\">different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. he observed traditional navigators at work</li> <li>B. he conducted test voyages using his own yacht</li> <li>C. he carried no modern instruments on test voyages</li> <li>D. he spoke the same language as the islanders he sailed with</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310236\" id=\"question-wrapper-310236\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What did David Lewis’s research <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"fac09c29-0027-40e9-8731-fae29c320e53\">discover<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> about traditional navigators?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They used the sun and moon to find their position</li> <li>B. They could not sail further than about 1,000 nautical miles</li> <li>C. They knew which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"da7cc746-6e87-4e83-aa82-f8de0bf1ec22\">direction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> they were sailing in</li> <li>D. They were able to drift for long distances</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310237\" id=\"question-wrapper-310237\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What are we told about Edwin Doran’s research?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Data were collected after the canoes had returned to land</li> <li>B. Canoe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"9bc35417-9c28-461a-8d72-df585640ef36\">characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> were recorded using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"56487178-7476-4fd5-99c7-9512fcdfb399\">modern instruments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span></li> <li>C. Research was conducted in the most densely populated regions</li> <li>D. Navigators were not allowed to see the instruments Doran used</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310238\" id=\"question-wrapper-310238\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which of the following did Steven Horvath discover during his research?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Canoe design was less important than human strength</li> <li>B. New research methods had to be developed for use in canoes</li> <li>C. Navigators became very tired on the longest voyages</li> <li>D. Human <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"3bcb0765-05b9-4329-9eff-76890cf62406\">energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> may have been used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"2a9c527d-a207-4fed-8c05-d0ff9d770b83\">assist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> sailing canoes</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310239\" id=\"question-wrapper-310239\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the writer’s opinion of Wall Garrard’s research?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. He is disappointed it was conducted in the laboratory</li> <li>B. He is impressed by the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f596a871-5c64-4e1d-b887-9024e700cc29\">originality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of the techniques used</li> <li>C. He is surprised it was used to help linguists with their research</li> <li>D. He is concerned that the islands studied are long distances apart</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A–F, below. Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. was the variety of experimental techniques used</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. was not of interest to young islanders today</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"1237a0b4-b0bd-40f4-bc63-61dc1c1488be\">not conclusive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> evidence in support of a single theory</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. was being able to change their practices when necessary</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"f13a8157-43cb-4b04-b3fd-b369e3d2921b\">the first time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> humans intentionally crossed an ocean </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. was the speed with which it was conducted</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310240\" id=\"question-wrapper-310240\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>One <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"8abcd921-62a0-488b-9c40-3fafa1c9ade5\">limitation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in the information produced by all of this research is that it</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310241\" id=\"question-wrapper-310241\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"86788929-2783-4dd4-866f-73ab5f724aa9\">best thing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> about this type of research</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310242\" id=\"question-wrapper-310242\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e1037581-40c4-41af-88e9-67f0ece4b8e1\">important achievement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of traditional navigators</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310243\" id=\"question-wrapper-310243\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"805cdff8-c6e5-44ea-8d22-cbdf2c915e14\">The migration of people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> from Asia to the Pacific</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"011079f5-a1d2-4015-a817-ff424408af05","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"uninhabited","passagePhrase":"no human population"},{"uid":"7e616a44-d3a7-44f5-99b4-eeaf1f1eabcb","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"arrived","passagePhrase":"sailed from Southeast Asia"},{"uid":"a505734e-d26d-48e2-b983-5e79e6f0ce38","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"had come to be considered by later investigators"},{"uid":"f658e2e1-0b23-4d56-b2d9-c404cb6d1050","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"skill","passagePhrase":"expertise ... was limited"},{"uid":"a4554ec0-dfb2-44dc-9336-4f0953212172","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"luck","passagePhrase":"good fortune"},{"uid":"8e8e8eda-090e-4ecb-954a-813788a12fb9","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"positive results","passagePhrase":"spark renewed interest ... precipitated valuable new research"},{"uid":"2b7e0cf0-e4b2-40e0-81c8-5407d1e08af6","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"different","passagePhrase":"unique philosophy"},{"uid":"bc54132d-c4ce-4ff3-8c0d-f4241bfb431d","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"contact those men"},{"uid":"c711f7b5-ea6a-497f-a448-6f0b5a1af4ca","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"accompanied these men"},{"uid":"fac09c29-0027-40e9-8731-fae29c320e53","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"discover","passagePhrase":"found that"},{"uid":"da7cc746-6e87-4e83-aa82-f8de0bf1ec22","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"direction","passagePhrase":"which course to steer ... fixed directions"},{"uid":"00fc5b90-1029-4a4f-a984-722ef96f9998","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Edwin Doran"},{"uid":"1db3be00-67dd-44cf-9a73-58ae311ff02a","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"exact data"},{"uid":"9bc35417-9c28-461a-8d72-df585640ef36","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"characteristics","passagePhrase":"sailing performance ... speeds"},{"uid":"56487178-7476-4fd5-99c7-9512fcdfb399","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"modern instruments","passagePhrase":"electronic instrumentation"},{"uid":"dda825fb-a4be-44a9-975d-41505648b2a4","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"physical capabilities"},{"uid":"3bcb0765-05b9-4329-9eff-76890cf62406","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"energy","passagePhrase":"energy expenditure"},{"uid":"2a9c527d-a207-4fed-8c05-d0ff9d770b83","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"assist","passagePhrase":"propelled"},{"uid":"f596a871-5c64-4e1d-b887-9024e700cc29","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"originality","passagePhrase":"Clever adaptation ... pioneered"},{"uid":"1237a0b4-b0bd-40f4-bc63-61dc1c1488be","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"not conclusive","passagePhrase":"none of the researchers tried to use ... to prove one theory or another"},{"uid":"8abcd921-62a0-488b-9c40-3fafa1c9ade5","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"limitation","passagePhrase":"cannot categorically confirm or negate a hypothesis"},{"uid":"86788929-2783-4dd4-866f-73ab5f724aa9","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"best thing","passagePhrase":"strength of this research"},{"uid":"bb233168-000d-4433-b30d-7e0ecb0b0d77","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"range of methodologies"},{"uid":"0fc8453d-05d2-456d-9b50-493243e86e05","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"adaptability ... altered their techniques accordingly"},{"uid":"e1037581-40c4-41af-88e9-67f0ece4b8e1","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"important achievement","passagePhrase":"greatest accomplishment"},{"uid":"805cdff8-c6e5-44ea-8d22-cbdf2c915e14","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"The migration of people","passagePhrase":"a systematic migration"},{"uid":"f13a8157-43cb-4b04-b3fd-b369e3d2921b","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"the first time","passagePhrase":"before any other race on Earth"}]},"reading_u2_31":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>The Impact of the Potato</span></b></p><p><i><span>Jeff Chapman relates the story of history's most important vegetable</span></i></p><p><span>The potato was first cultivated in South America between three and seven thousand years ago, though scientists believe wild varieties grew there far earlier. Some researchers suggest that wild potatoes may have flourished in the region for as long as 13,000 years before any human cultivation began. The genetic patterns of potato distribution across the continent reveal valuable clues about the plant's early history and gradual geographical spread. These patterns indicate that the potato probably originated in the mountainous west-central region before spreading slowly to surrounding areas over many centuries.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"605747b7-51a0-4aa7-a99a-189bf70f7282\">Early Spanish chroniclers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> misused the Indian word batata, meaning sweet potato, as the name for the potato while noting its importance to the Incan Empire. The Incas had learned to preserve their crop for long storage by dehydrating and mashing potatoes into a substance they called chuño. This preserved food could be stored in a single room for up to 10 years, providing excellent insurance against possible crop failures during difficult seasons. As well as using the food as a staple crop in daily life, the Incas thought potatoes made childbirth easier and used them to treat injuries.</span></p><p><span>The Spanish conquistadors first encountered the potato when they arrived in Peru in 1532, having <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"32d2372a-ea0f-443d-b88e-0df5769b2ce4\">come to the region in search of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> gold. They noted Inca miners eating chuño deep in the mines, but failed to realise that the potato represented a treasure more valuable than silver or gold. Over time, however, they gradually began to use potatoes as basic rations aboard their ships during the long voyages back to Europe. After the arrival of the potato in Spain in 1570, a few farmers began to cultivate it on a small scale, mainly as livestock fodder.</span></p><p><span>Throughout Europe, potatoes were regarded with suspicion, distaste and fear by most people who considered them unfit for human consumption at the time. People used the tubers only as animal fodder and sustenance for the starving, and in northern Europe they grew mainly as an exotic botanical novelty. Even peasants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"d4cf5453-c75a-47ae-87d4-ffa7051c27e8\">refused to eat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> from a plant that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c00beb7f-fc49-4b68-8f3e-1c5eb92585e6\">produced ugly, misshapen tubers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, especially since it came from a heathen civilization across the seas. Some felt that the potato plant's resemblance to plants in the nightshade family hinted it was the creation of witches or devils.</span></p><p><span>In meat-loving England, farmers and urban workers regarded potatoes with extreme distaste, despite the Royal Society recommending cultivation of the tuber to the government in 1662. However, this official recommendation had little <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"506c4045-c295-4834-8ff6-6aacef838650\">impact on public opinion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> until <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"1c6116b2-d9d8-4aca-b837-1018737aed18\">food shortages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> associated with the Revolutionary Wars finally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"25fd4789-3187-4f2e-8ca5-87beb283e873\">made potatoes a staple<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. During this period, the English government began to officially encourage potato cultivation across the country to help feed the growing urban population. In 1795, the Board of Agriculture issued a pamphlet entitled \"Hints Respecting the Culture and Use of Potatoes\", followed shortly by recipes in The Times.</span></p><p><span>A similar pattern emerged across the English Channel in the Netherlands, Belgium and France, where the potato slowly gained ground in eastern regions. It often remained the only crop after marauding soldiers plundered wheat fields and vineyards, though it did not achieve widespread acceptance until the late 1700s. The peasants remained suspicious despite a 1771 paper from the Faculté de Paris testifying that the potato was not harmful but actually beneficial for health. Public attitudes finally shifted once the plant <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620\">received the royal seal of approval, with </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"3525898f-c5db-44f2-83fa-4b5a2651d646 58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620\">Louis XVI</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"55559a44-d726-4f4a-81bd-0467e9377aa3 58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620\">sporting</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620\"> a potato flower in </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620 b66df05b-c0b0-4d7f-b135-1e60501876bd\">his buttonhole</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620\"> at court</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. Marie-Antoinette also wore a purple potato blossom in her hair as a fashionable accessory, helping to popularise the plant among aristocrats.</span></p><p><span>Frederick the Great of Prussia saw the potato's potential to help feed his nation and lower the price of bread for ordinary people. However, he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4c7b7778-6552-433f-8cd5-731c8d13f099\">faced the considerable challenge of overcoming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"c9f6147b-15ab-41c6-9462-fc93957169f8\">his subjects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>' prejudice <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"93e5f7e6-0227-412a-84bb-0a6267d1bfb6\">against a plant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> they had never trusted as proper food. In 1774, he issued an order for his subjects to grow potatoes as protection against famine, but the response was far from enthusiastic. The town of Kolberg replied that the things had neither smell nor taste, and that not even the dogs would eat them. Frederick soon realised that direct orders alone would never convince his deeply suspicious subjects to accept this strange new crop.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"8235d36f-57b2-4991-988e-d16b0f7cacda\">Frederick<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> therefore decided to try a less direct approach, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"19ebdc82-2965-471b-acb4-cddd5c515d6c\">using a bit of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> reverse psychology to change his subjects' attitudes towards the new crop. He planted a royal field of potato plants on his own private land and stationed a heavy guard to protect it from any potential thieves. Nearby peasants naturally assumed that anything worth guarding so closely must be worth stealing, so they soon began sneaking into the field. They snatched the plants for their home gardens under cover of darkness, which was, of course, entirely in line with Frederick's original wishes.</span></p><p><span>Historians continue to debate whether the potato was primarily a cause or an effect of the huge population boom in industrial-era England and Wales. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"28b57858-3f9d-425b-897a-841151b7b9bf\">Prior to 1800<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, the English diet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"082c6f6a-e7aa-46d7-832d-8aff7f7eeea5\">had consisted primarily of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> meat, supplemented by bread, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"11d272af-1860-4955-bf14-47feb12c4c90\">butter and cheese<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> in most households of the period. Few vegetables were consumed because most were regarded as nutritionally worthless, and some people even believed that vegetables could be potentially harmful to health. This long-standing view began to change gradually in the late 1700s for a variety of social, economic and agricultural reasons.</span></p><p><span>The Industrial Revolution drew an ever-increasing percentage of the populace into crowded cities, where only the richest could afford homes with proper ovens or coal storage rooms. Most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"5f5152de-b992-4eed-9fa2-3ed82d5aedd0\">workers lived in cramped lodgings with very limited cooking facilities, and they worked 12 to 16-hour days<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> in the new factories. Such long shifts left them with little time or energy to prepare proper meals at home for themselves or for their growing families. High-yielding, easily prepared potato crops <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"9020dc47-20d7-4a0f-96f6-faa85d632044\">were the obvious solution to England's food problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, since the tuber could be cooked quickly without special equipment.</span></p><p><span>Most of England's neighbours regarded the potato with suspicion when it first arrived, and they had to be persuaded to use it by their upper classes. However, the Irish peasantry embraced the tuber more passionately than anyone since the Incas had cultivated it thousands of years earlier in South America. The potato was well suited to the Irish <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"86079a92-5b3e-4b17-b3fd-86bf9f275a05\">soil and climate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> from the very beginning, and its high yield addressed farmers' most important concern. They simply wanted to feed their growing families with enough nutritious food throughout the year, which the new crop could reliably provide.</span></p><p><span>The most dramatic example of the potato's potential to alter population patterns occurred in Ireland, where it had become a staple food by 1800. Between 1780 and 1841, the Irish population doubled to eight million without any significant expansion of industry or reform of agricultural techniques. The widespread <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"217b61d9-0757-4bf5-806a-6db1be91cf45\">cultivation of the potato<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> was therefore the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"6deb5c78-65a4-40db-ac78-54ba7e9e1faa\">main factor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> behind this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"2bcffd00-369e-4d1b-b72c-b87e3447db9e\">remarkable demographic change in such a relatively short period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. Few other agricultural developments contributed to the population boom in any meaningful way during these decades of rapid Irish growth.</span></p><p><span>Although Irish landholding practices were primitive in comparison with those of England, the potato's high yields allowed even the poorest farmers to thrive on their small plots. They could produce more than enough healthy food for their families <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"70f29339-1458-4a73-b850-3f0f9e7454a6\">with scarcely any<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> investment or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"dadd5cf6-20a6-4c1c-abc6-ba2c9ff5f796\">hard labour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> required on their part. Even children could easily plant, harvest and cook potatoes, since the crop required no threshing, curing or grinding before being eaten. The abundance provided by potatoes greatly decreased infant mortality among Irish families and encouraged early marriage among the rural population at the time.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1–5 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322462\" id=\"question-wrapper-322462\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"605747b7-51a0-4aa7-a99a-189bf70f7282\">Early Spanish writers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> used the same term for the potato as the Incas used for its preserved form.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322463\" id=\"question-wrapper-322463\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Spanish originally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"32d2372a-ea0f-443d-b88e-0df5769b2ce4\">went to Peru for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the crop that later became important in Europe.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322464\" id=\"question-wrapper-322464\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Spanish considered potatoes nutritionally comparable to other vegetables.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322465\" id=\"question-wrapper-322465\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Peasants at the time <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"d4cf5453-c75a-47ae-87d4-ffa7051c27e8\">avoided<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> potatoes partly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c00beb7f-fc49-4b68-8f3e-1c5eb92585e6\">because of their appearance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322466\" id=\"question-wrapper-322466\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In England, potatoes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"25fd4789-3187-4f2e-8ca5-87beb283e873\">became accepted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> mainly because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"1c6116b2-d9d8-4aca-b837-1018737aed18\">a period of scarcity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"506c4045-c295-4834-8ff6-6aacef838650\">changed public attitudes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322467\" id=\"question-wrapper-322467\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In France, public opinion began to change after the crop was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620\">visibly endorsed at court<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"3525898f-c5db-44f2-83fa-4b5a2651d646\">the king<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"55559a44-d726-4f4a-81bd-0467e9377aa3\">wore<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> a potato ______ as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b66df05b-c0b0-4d7f-b135-1e60501876bd\">part of his clothing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">flower</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322468\" id=\"question-wrapper-322468\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Frederick understood the crop’s usefulness, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4c7b7778-6552-433f-8cd5-731c8d13f099\">first needed to overcome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"c9f6147b-15ab-41c6-9462-fc93957169f8\">his people’s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> deep-rooted ______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"93e5f7e6-0227-412a-84bb-0a6267d1bfb6\">towards it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">prejudice</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322469\" id=\"question-wrapper-322469\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"8235d36f-57b2-4991-988e-d16b0f7cacda\">The King of Prussia<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"19ebdc82-2965-471b-acb4-cddd5c515d6c\">adopted a form of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> ______ psychology to make people accept potatoes.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">reverse</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322470\" id=\"question-wrapper-322470\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"28b57858-3f9d-425b-897a-841151b7b9bf\">Before 1800<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, the English diet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"082c6f6a-e7aa-46d7-832d-8aff7f7eeea5\">was based chiefly on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> ______, with bread and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"11d272af-1860-4955-bf14-47feb12c4c90\">dairy products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> added.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">meat</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322471\" id=\"question-wrapper-322471\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>For <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"5f5152de-b992-4eed-9fa2-3ed82d5aedd0\">overworked urban labourers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> with limited cooking facilities, easily prepared potato ______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"9020dc47-20d7-4a0f-96f6-faa85d632044\">offered a practical answer to food supply problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">crops</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322472\" id=\"question-wrapper-322472\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"86079a92-5b3e-4b17-b3fd-86bf9f275a05\">natural condition, together with climate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, made Ireland especially suitable for growing potatoes?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">soil</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322473\" id=\"question-wrapper-322473\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"217b61d9-0757-4bf5-806a-6db1be91cf45\">potato-related activity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> was the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"6deb5c78-65a4-40db-ac78-54ba7e9e1faa\">main reason<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> for Ireland’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"2bcffd00-369e-4d1b-b72c-b87e3447db9e\">rapid population growth between 1780 and 1841<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">cultivation</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322474\" id=\"question-wrapper-322474\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Other than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"dadd5cf6-20a6-4c1c-abc6-ba2c9ff5f796\">physical effort<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, what did poor Irish farmers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"70f29339-1458-4a73-b850-3f0f9e7454a6\">need very little of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to produce enough food from potatoes?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">investment</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"605747b7-51a0-4aa7-a99a-189bf70f7282","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Early Spanish writers","passagePhrase":"Early Spanish chroniclers"},{"uid":"32d2372a-ea0f-443d-b88e-0df5769b2ce4","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"went to Peru for","passagePhrase":"come to the region in search of"},{"uid":"d4cf5453-c75a-47ae-87d4-ffa7051c27e8","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"avoided","passagePhrase":"refused to eat"},{"uid":"c00beb7f-fc49-4b68-8f3e-1c5eb92585e6","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"because of their appearance","passagePhrase":"produced ugly, misshapen tubers"},{"uid":"506c4045-c295-4834-8ff6-6aacef838650","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"changed public attitudes","passagePhrase":"impact on public opinion"},{"uid":"1c6116b2-d9d8-4aca-b837-1018737aed18","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"a period of scarcity","passagePhrase":"food shortages"},{"uid":"25fd4789-3187-4f2e-8ca5-87beb283e873","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"became accepted","passagePhrase":"made potatoes a staple"},{"uid":"58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"visibly endorsed at court","passagePhrase":"received the royal seal of approval, with ... a potato flower in ... at court"},{"uid":"3525898f-c5db-44f2-83fa-4b5a2651d646 58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Louis XVI"},{"uid":"55559a44-d726-4f4a-81bd-0467e9377aa3 58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"sporting"},{"uid":"58afcafa-76b2-43f3-8e92-fa9229522620 b66df05b-c0b0-4d7f-b135-1e60501876bd","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"his buttonhole"},{"uid":"4c7b7778-6552-433f-8cd5-731c8d13f099","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"first needed to overcome","passagePhrase":"faced the considerable challenge of overcoming"},{"uid":"c9f6147b-15ab-41c6-9462-fc93957169f8","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"his people’s","passagePhrase":"his subjects"},{"uid":"93e5f7e6-0227-412a-84bb-0a6267d1bfb6","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"towards it","passagePhrase":"against a plant"},{"uid":"8235d36f-57b2-4991-988e-d16b0f7cacda","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"The King of Prussia","passagePhrase":"Frederick"},{"uid":"19ebdc82-2965-471b-acb4-cddd5c515d6c","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"adopted a form of","passagePhrase":"using a bit of"},{"uid":"28b57858-3f9d-425b-897a-841151b7b9bf","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Before 1800","passagePhrase":"Prior to 1800"},{"uid":"082c6f6a-e7aa-46d7-832d-8aff7f7eeea5","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"was based chiefly on","passagePhrase":"had consisted primarily of"},{"uid":"11d272af-1860-4955-bf14-47feb12c4c90","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"dairy products","passagePhrase":"butter and cheese"},{"uid":"5f5152de-b992-4eed-9fa2-3ed82d5aedd0","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"overworked urban labourers","passagePhrase":"workers lived in cramped lodgings with very limited cooking facilities, and they worked 12 to 16-hour days"},{"uid":"9020dc47-20d7-4a0f-96f6-faa85d632044","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"offered a practical answer to food supply problems","passagePhrase":"were the obvious solution to England's food problems"},{"uid":"86079a92-5b3e-4b17-b3fd-86bf9f275a05","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"natural condition, together with climate","passagePhrase":"soil and climate"},{"uid":"217b61d9-0757-4bf5-806a-6db1be91cf45","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"potato-related activity","passagePhrase":"cultivation of the potato"},{"uid":"6deb5c78-65a4-40db-ac78-54ba7e9e1faa","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"main reason","passagePhrase":"main factor"},{"uid":"2bcffd00-369e-4d1b-b72c-b87e3447db9e","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"rapid population growth between 1780 and 1841","passagePhrase":"remarkable demographic change in such a relatively short period"},{"uid":"70f29339-1458-4a73-b850-3f0f9e7454a6","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"need very little of","passagePhrase":"with scarcely any"},{"uid":"dadd5cf6-20a6-4c1c-abc6-ba2c9ff5f796","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"physical effort","passagePhrase":"hard labour"},{"uid":"3525898f-c5db-44f2-83fa-4b5a2651d646","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"the king","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"55559a44-d726-4f4a-81bd-0467e9377aa3","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"wore","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"b66df05b-c0b0-4d7f-b135-1e60501876bd","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"part of his clothing","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_32":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Is Graffiti Art or Crime?</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>The term graffiti derives from the Italian graffio meaning ‘scratching’ and can be defined as uninvited markings or writing scratched or applied to objects, built structures and natural features. It is not a new phenomenon: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"28a36eb9-8ec6-4c36-ad1c-4d50b478cd08\">examples can be found on ancient structures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> around the world, in some cases predating the Greeks and Romans. In such circumstances, it has acquired invaluable historical and archaeological significance, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5d482a84-a437-4e40-a7f4-4e0d89933b82\">providing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> a social history of life and events at that time. Graffiti is now a problem that has become pervasive, as a result of the availability of cheap and quick means of mark-making.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> It is usually considered a priority to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e02ed308-6361-4fe8-8d17-d134a33e6038\">remove graffiti as quickly as possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> after it appears. This is for several reasons. The first is to prevent ‘copy-cat’ emulation, which can occur rapidly once a clean surface is defaced. It may also be of a racist or otherwise offensive nature and many companies and councils have a policy of removing this type of graffiti within an hour or two of it being reported. Also, as paints, glues and inks dry out over time they can become increasingly difficult to remove and are usually best dealt with as soon as possible after the incident. Graffiti can also lead to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e17be3b1-c2e1-4416-9552-53ced1933a49\">more serious forms of vandalism and, ultimately, the deterioration of an area, contributing to social decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>Although graffiti may be regarded as an eyesore, any <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"84531d4f-0f6a-4bfe-8101-aaa25421b245\">proposal to remove it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e69394f6-0435-45d0-bf37-9d9ebd78af91\">sensitive historic surfaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> should be carefully considered: techniques designed for more robust or utilitarian surfaces may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d8e01a79-4e4f-4b85-9d72-2f648e2a023c\">result in considerable damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"adc93042-59b1-402f-9689-dfa0af096029\">In the event of graffiti incidents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, it is important that the owners of buildings or other structures and their consultants are aware of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d75a933a-3c02-483e-99a2-5600fc94891e\">approach they should take in dealing with the problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. The police should be informed, as there may be other related attacks occurring locally. An incidence pattern can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"067dd803-df02-46a9-8a64-9ec78c5e2373\">identify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> possible culprits, as can stylised signatures or nicknames, known as tags, which may already be familiar to local police. Photographs are useful to record graffiti incidents and may assist the police in bringing a prosecution. Such images are also required for insurance claims, and can be helpful to cleaning operatives, allowing them to see the problem area before arriving on site.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>There are a variety of methods that are used to remove graffiti. Broadly, these divide between chemical and mechanical systems. Chemical preparations are based on dissolving the media; these solvents can range from water to potentially <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"9ac694ee-4a40-43ae-a0bc-ec33ecdd82fb\">hazardous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> chemical ‘cocktails’. Mechanical systems such as wire-brushing and grit-blasting attempt to abrade or chip the media from the surface. Care should be taken to comply with health and safety legislation with regard to the protection of both passers-by and any person carrying out the cleaning. Operatives should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"4c180faf-605c-44b8-b1c8-92488a50ec6d\">follow product guidelines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> in terms of application and removal, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"2d3acd91-c2da-40fd-bf66-93192e3de855\">wear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"6f2e0759-e14e-41d5-964b-9727c44d9299\">appropriate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> protective equipment. Measures must be taken to ensure that run-off, aerial mists, drips and splashes do not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"9ac694ee-4a40-43ae-a0bc-ec33ecdd82fb\">threaten unprotected members of the public<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. When examining a graffiti incident, it is important to assess the ability of the substrate to withstand the prescribed treatment. If there is any doubt regarding this, then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"cf0ec7b1-cbfd-481c-94fe-3edf192a52fd\">small trial areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> should be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"858d3a78-2436-4a3c-acf3-ac2031992eb5\">undertaken to assess the impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"e72484d1-c7ad-4cb4-ac2d-a570d7b12112\">more extensive treatment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> A variety of preventive strategies can be adopted to combat a recurring problem of graffiti at a given site. As no two sites are the same, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"87244001-6067-486a-b2d0-dae842d995b0\">no one set of protection measures will be suitable for all situations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Each site must be looked at individually. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"b3db9388-55df-4b9b-8094-ab6176ad9d94\">Surveillance systems such as closed-circuit television<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> may also help. In cities and towns around the country, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"0f4fe015-a486-44dd-924d-e4731494d3d0\">prominently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"aca0108d-b47f-4954-9bd9-bbde0f6d6f37\">placed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"b3db9388-55df-4b9b-8094-ab6176ad9d94\">cameras<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> have been shown to reduce anti-social behaviour of all types including graffiti. Security patrols will also act as a deterrent to prevent recurring attacks. However, the cost of this may be too high for most situations. Physical barriers such as a wall, railings, doors or gates can be introduced to discourage unauthorised access to a vulnerable site. However, consideration has to be given to the impact of the measures that may have on the structure being protected. In the worst cases, they can be almost as damaging to the quality of the environment as the graffiti they prevent. In others, they might simply provide a new surface for graffiti.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>One of the most significant problems associated with graffiti removal is the need to remove it from surfaces that are repeatedly attacked. Under these circumstances the repeated removal of graffiti using even the gentlest methods will ultimately cause damage to the surface material. There may be situations where the preventive strategies mentioned above do not work or are not a viable proposition at a given site. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"bb23d545-fbdb-4fc1-a65f-0f11150ae4c6\">Anti-graffiti coatings are usually applied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> by brush or spray leaving a thin veneer that essentially serves to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"030ec026-0233-457d-9fc4-e1ad5124ee6e\">isolate the graffiti from the surface<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>Removal of graffiti from a surface that has been treated in this way is much easier, usually using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"75d432f7-cc0f-4ca0-998c-64165aba60fd\">low-pressure water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"2a3a230e-90f3-4738-952c-63f2f4f367ea\">reduces the possibility of damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Depending on the type of barrier selected, it may be necessary to reapply the coating after each graffiti removal exercise.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>This passage has seven paragraphs, A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Paragraph A</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Paragraph B</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Paragraph C</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Paragraph D</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Paragraph E</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. Paragraph F</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. Paragraph G</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322475\" id=\"question-wrapper-322475\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the possibility that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"84531d4f-0f6a-4bfe-8101-aaa25421b245\">graffiti removal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d8e01a79-4e4f-4b85-9d72-2f648e2a023c\">harm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e69394f6-0435-45d0-bf37-9d9ebd78af91\">heritage sites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322476\" id=\"question-wrapper-322476\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"2a3a230e-90f3-4738-952c-63f2f4f367ea\">risk-reduction effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of a beforehand shield during <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"75d432f7-cc0f-4ca0-998c-64165aba60fd\">later rinsing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322477\" id=\"question-wrapper-322477\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e17be3b1-c2e1-4416-9552-53ced1933a49\">damaging and cumulative impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of graffiti on the community</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322478\" id=\"question-wrapper-322478\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"87244001-6067-486a-b2d0-dae842d995b0\">need for different preventive measures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> taken to cope with graffiti</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322479\" id=\"question-wrapper-322479\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d75a933a-3c02-483e-99a2-5600fc94891e\">steps building owners should take<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"adc93042-59b1-402f-9689-dfa0af096029\">after an attack occurs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322480\" id=\"question-wrapper-322480\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the importance of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e02ed308-6361-4fe8-8d17-d134a33e6038\">timely graffiti response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose TWO letters, A-E. Write your answers in boxes 20-21 on your answer sheet. Which TWO statements are true concerning the removal of graffiti?</span></p><p><span>A. chemical 'cocktails' are safer to use than water-based treatments</span></p><p><span>B. a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"cf0ec7b1-cbfd-481c-94fe-3edf192a52fd\">small sample section<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> should be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"858d3a78-2436-4a3c-acf3-ac2031992eb5\">tested<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> before <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"e72484d1-c7ad-4cb4-ac2d-a570d7b12112\">full-scale application<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p><p><span>C. chemical treatments are the most expensive way of removing graffiti</span></p><p><span>D. there are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"9ac694ee-4a40-43ae-a0bc-ec33ecdd82fb\">risks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> associated with both chemical and mechanical methods</span></p><p><span>E. mechanical removal is much more applicable than chemical treatments</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322481\" id=\"question-wrapper-322481\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322482\" id=\"question-wrapper-322482\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose TWO letters, A-E. Write your answers in boxes 22-23 on your answer sheet. Which TWO of the following are mentioned in the passage as effective ways of dealing with graffiti?</span></p><p><span>A. organising more anti-graffiti movement </span></p><p><span>B. reducing police patrols on the street</span></p><p><span>C. constructing new buildings from water-repellent materials</span></p><p><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"aca0108d-b47f-4954-9bd9-bbde0f6d6f37\">installing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"0f4fe015-a486-44dd-924d-e4731494d3d0\">visible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"b3db9388-55df-4b9b-8094-ab6176ad9d94\">security cameras<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span></span></p><p><span>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"bb23d545-fbdb-4fc1-a65f-0f11150ae4c6\">pre-treating surfaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"030ec026-0233-457d-9fc4-e1ad5124ee6e\">keep graffiti off the material beneath<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322483\" id=\"question-wrapper-322483\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D/E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322484\" id=\"question-wrapper-322484\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D/E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Use NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322485\" id=\"question-wrapper-322485\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"28a36eb9-8ec6-4c36-ad1c-4d50b478cd08\">Ancient graffiti<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> is of significance and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5d482a84-a437-4e40-a7f4-4e0d89933b82\">records<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the ______ of life for that period.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(social) history</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322486\" id=\"question-wrapper-322486\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The police can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"067dd803-df02-46a9-8a64-9ec78c5e2373\">recognize<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> newly committed incidents of graffiti through the familiar signatures which are called ______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">tags</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322487\" id=\"question-wrapper-322487\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Operatives ought to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"4c180faf-605c-44b8-b1c8-92488a50ec6d\">comply with relevant rules<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> during the operation, including <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"2d3acd91-c2da-40fd-bf66-93192e3de855\">putting on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"6f2e0759-e14e-41d5-964b-9727c44d9299\">suitable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> ______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">protective equipment</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"28a36eb9-8ec6-4c36-ad1c-4d50b478cd08","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Ancient graffiti","passagePhrase":"examples can be found on ancient structures"},{"uid":"5d482a84-a437-4e40-a7f4-4e0d89933b82","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"records","passagePhrase":"providing"},{"uid":"e02ed308-6361-4fe8-8d17-d134a33e6038","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"timely graffiti response","passagePhrase":"remove graffiti as quickly as possible"},{"uid":"e17be3b1-c2e1-4416-9552-53ced1933a49","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"damaging and cumulative impact","passagePhrase":"more serious forms of vandalism and, ultimately, the deterioration of an area, contributing to social decline"},{"uid":"84531d4f-0f6a-4bfe-8101-aaa25421b245","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"graffiti removal","passagePhrase":"proposal to remove it"},{"uid":"e69394f6-0435-45d0-bf37-9d9ebd78af91","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"heritage sites","passagePhrase":"sensitive historic surfaces"},{"uid":"d8e01a79-4e4f-4b85-9d72-2f648e2a023c","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"harm","passagePhrase":"result in considerable damage"},{"uid":"adc93042-59b1-402f-9689-dfa0af096029","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"after an attack occurs","passagePhrase":"In the event of graffiti incidents"},{"uid":"d75a933a-3c02-483e-99a2-5600fc94891e","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"steps building owners should take","passagePhrase":"approach they should take in dealing with the problem"},{"uid":"067dd803-df02-46a9-8a64-9ec78c5e2373","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"recognize","passagePhrase":"identify"},{"uid":"9ac694ee-4a40-43ae-a0bc-ec33ecdd82fb","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"risks","passagePhrase":"hazardous ... threaten unprotected members of the public"},{"uid":"4c180faf-605c-44b8-b1c8-92488a50ec6d","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"comply with relevant rules","passagePhrase":"follow product guidelines"},{"uid":"2d3acd91-c2da-40fd-bf66-93192e3de855","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"putting on","passagePhrase":"wear"},{"uid":"6f2e0759-e14e-41d5-964b-9727c44d9299","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"suitable","passagePhrase":"appropriate"},{"uid":"cf0ec7b1-cbfd-481c-94fe-3edf192a52fd","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"small sample section","passagePhrase":"small trial areas"},{"uid":"858d3a78-2436-4a3c-acf3-ac2031992eb5","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"tested","passagePhrase":"undertaken to assess the impact"},{"uid":"e72484d1-c7ad-4cb4-ac2d-a570d7b12112","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"full-scale application","passagePhrase":"more extensive treatment"},{"uid":"87244001-6067-486a-b2d0-dae842d995b0","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"need for different preventive measures","passagePhrase":"no one set of protection measures will be suitable for all situations"},{"uid":"b3db9388-55df-4b9b-8094-ab6176ad9d94","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"security cameras","passagePhrase":"Surveillance systems such as closed-circuit television ... cameras"},{"uid":"0f4fe015-a486-44dd-924d-e4731494d3d0","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"visible","passagePhrase":"prominently"},{"uid":"aca0108d-b47f-4954-9bd9-bbde0f6d6f37","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"installing","passagePhrase":"placed"},{"uid":"bb23d545-fbdb-4fc1-a65f-0f11150ae4c6","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"pre-treating surfaces","passagePhrase":"Anti-graffiti coatings are usually applied"},{"uid":"030ec026-0233-457d-9fc4-e1ad5124ee6e","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"keep graffiti off the material beneath","passagePhrase":"isolate the graffiti from the surface"},{"uid":"75d432f7-cc0f-4ca0-998c-64165aba60fd","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"later rinsing","passagePhrase":"low-pressure water"},{"uid":"2a3a230e-90f3-4738-952c-63f2f4f367ea","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"risk-reduction effect","passagePhrase":"reduces the possibility of damage"}]},"reading_u2_33":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>Decisions, decisions!</span></b></p><p><i><span>Research explores when we can make a vital decision quickly and when we need to proceed more deliberately.</span></i></p><p><span>A widely recognised legend tells us that in Gordium in the fourth century BC an oxcart was roped to a pole with a complex knot. It was said that the first person to untie it would become the king of Asia. Unfortunately, the knot proved impossible to untie. The story continues that when confronted with this problem, rather than deliberating on how to untie the Gordian knot, Alexander, the famous ruler of the Greeks in the ancient world, simply took out his sword and cut it in two – then went on to conquer Asia. Ever since, the notion of a 'Gordian solution' has referred to the attractiveness of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"58564f33-2a26-41a3-8892-b80095ed1112\">simple answer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to an otherwise <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"deb4dcfa-e09c-465f-91e8-b9d985a8ff48\">intractable problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Among researchers in the psychology of decision making, however, such solutions have traditionally held little appeal. In particular, the 'conflict model' of decision making proposed by psychologists Irving Janis and Leon Mann in their 1977 book, Decision Making, argued that a complex decision-making process is essential for guarding individuals and groups from the peril of 'group-think'. Decisions made without <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"edb44224-a164-422b-9d3c-00c7d50812ab\">thorough canvassing, surveying, weighing, examining and reexamining relevant information and options<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> would be suboptimal and often disastrous. One foreign affairs decision made by a well-known US political leader in the 1960s is typically held as an example of the perils of inadequate thought, whereas his successful handling of a later crisis is cited as an example of the advantages of careful deliberation. However, examination of these historical events by Peter Suedfeld, a psychologist at the University of British Columbia, and Roderick Kramer, a psychologist at the Stanford Graduate School of Business, found little difference in the two decision-making processes; both crises required and received complex consideration by the political administration, but later only the second one was deemed to be the effective.</span></p><p><span>In general, however, organizational and political science offer little evidence that complex decisions fare better than simpler ones. In fact, a growing body of work suggests that in many situations simple '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"f7183dd4-e690-4a70-a70f-928bea783a99\">snap' decisions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> will be routinely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"463ac275-7e5c-4e64-a2eb-d675900995ab\">superior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to more complex ones – an idea that gained widespread public appeal with Malcolm Gladwell's best-selling book Blink (2005).</span></p><p><span>An article by Ap Dijksterhuis of the University of Amsterdam and his colleagues, 'On Making the Right Choice: the Deliberation-without-attention Effect', runs very much in the spirit of Gladwell's influential text. Its core argument is that to be effective, conscious deliberative decision making requires cognitive resources. Because increasingly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"204810bd-f964-43c3-a50b-2d9af4c4d2ff\">complex decisions place increasing strain on those resources, the quality of our decisions declines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> as their complexity increases. In short, complex decisions overrun our cognitive powers. On the other hand, unconscious decision making, what the author refers to as 'deliberation without attention', requires no cognitive resources, so task complexity does not degrade effectiveness. The seemingly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"9124c41c-0e74-40e1-88d6-9edbce28f583\">counter-intuitive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> conclusion is that although conscious thought enhances simple decisions, the opposite holds true for more complex decisions.</span></p><p><span>Dijksterhuis reports four simple but elegant studies supporting this argument. In one, participants assessed the quality of four hypothetical cars by considering either four attributes (a simple task) or 12 attributes (a complex task). Among participants who considered four attributes, those who were allowed to engage in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ebcb9ca4-a937-45b8-b585-20255ec2bdef\">undistracted deliberative thought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"7c6f3d96-9354-484f-9c1c-afaccbf09fcd\">did better at discriminating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> between the best and worst cars. Those who were distracted and thus unable to deliberate had to rely on their unconscious thinking and did less well. The opposite pattern emerged when people considered 12 criteria. In this case, conscious deliberation led to inferior discrimination and poor decisions.</span></p><p><span>In another study, Dijksterhuis surveyed people shopping for clothes ('simple' products) and furniture ('complex' products). Compared with those who said they had deliberated long and hard, shoppers <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c7c64b4d-df10-48d6-abd1-933b8fa93fb6\">who </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"51be7c19-aba7-47db-8407-97a7250e9f40 c7c64b4d-df10-48d6-abd1-933b8fa93fb6\">bought with little conscious deliberation</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"51be7c19-aba7-47db-8407-97a7250e9f40\">felt less happy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> with their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"b85813b1-872c-492b-84f4-31f199c9d156\">simple clothing purchase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> but happier with the complex <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"9ec7a724-ef20-4fcc-8bef-7e4a9725908f\">furniture purchases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"4f9f63fa-f1e0-424f-a6f2-a4b2ddd81285\">Deliberation without attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> actually produced better results as the decisions became more complex.</span></p><p><span>From there, however, the researchers take a big leap. They write: There is no reason to assume that the deliberation-without-attention effect does not generalize to other types of choices – political, managerial or otherwise. In such cases, it should benefit the individual to think consciously about simple <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"530f1d88-e8e5-4b00-95b3-95b2d53188c3\">matters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> and to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"7112b917-93a0-4921-8217-7a241eb25c7d\">delegate thinking about more complicated matters to the unconscious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>This radical inference <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"69ad7636-ce1c-44c5-b7a5-d55a47a77a64\">contradicts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> standard political and managerial theory but doubtless comforts those in politics and management who always find the simple solution to the complex problem an attractive proposition. Indeed, one suspects many of our political leaders already <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"d1d32deb-30a7-4363-9719-b7350533e3a9\">embrace this wisdom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Still it is there, in the realms of society and its governance, that the more problematic implications of deliberation without attention begin to surface. Variables that can be neatly circumscribed in decisions about shopping lose clarity in a world of group dynamics, social interaction, history and politics. Two pertinent questions arise. First, what counts as a complex decision? And second, what counts as a good outcome?</span></p><p><span>As social psychologist Kurt Lewin (1890 – 1947) noted, a ‘good’ decision that nobody respects is actually bad, his classic studies of decision making showed that participating in deliberative processes makes people more likely to abide by the results. The issue here is that when political decision-makers make mistakes, it is their politics, or the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"3b0fe39a-d84d-482d-b6ea-c01fdc0e7e98\">relationship between their politics and our own<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, rather than psychology which is at fault.</span></p><p><span>Gladwell’s book and Dijksterhuis’s paper are invaluable in pointing out the limitations of the conventional wisdom that decision quality rises with decision-making complexity. But this work still tempts us to believe that decision making is simply a matter of psychology. Yet a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2406c11a-79f3-482c-98d1-4227fe74a1ed\">more useful examination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> would also consider the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"5d7cc3b8-26e1-4ba3-ba12-6daa613296d3\">social context<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> in which decisions are made, including politics, ideology and group membership.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27 – 31 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322488\" id=\"question-wrapper-322488\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The legend of the Gordian knot is used to illustrate the idea that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. anyone can solve a difficult problem</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"deb4dcfa-e09c-465f-91e8-b9d985a8ff48\">difficult problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> can have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"58564f33-2a26-41a3-8892-b80095ed1112\">easy solutions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></li> <li>C. the solution to any problem requires a lot of thought</li> <li>D. people who can solve complex problems make good leaders</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322489\" id=\"question-wrapper-322489\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The 'conflict model' of decision making proposed by Janis and Mann requires that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. opposing political parties be involved</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"edb44224-a164-422b-9d3c-00c7d50812ab\">all important facts be considered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></li> <li>C. people be encouraged to have different ideas</li> <li>D. previous similar situations be thoroughly examined</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322490\" id=\"question-wrapper-322490\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to recent thinking reinforced by Malcolm Gladwell, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"463ac275-7e5c-4e64-a2eb-d675900995ab\">the best decisions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. involve consultation</li> <li>B. involve complex thought</li> <li>C. are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"f7183dd4-e690-4a70-a70f-928bea783a99\">made very quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></li> <li>D. are the most attractive options</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322491\" id=\"question-wrapper-322491\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Dijksterhuis and his colleagues claim in their article that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. our cognitive resources improve as tasks become more complex</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"204810bd-f964-43c3-a50b-2d9af4c4d2ff\">conscious decision making is negatively affected by task complexity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></li> <li>C. unconscious decision making is a popular approach</li> <li>D. deliberation without attention defines the way we make decisions</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322492\" id=\"question-wrapper-322492\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Dijksterhuis's car study found that, in simple tasks, participants</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. were involved in lengthy discussions</li> <li>B. found it impossible to make decisions quickly</li> <li>C. were unable to differentiate between the options</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"7c6f3d96-9354-484f-9c1c-afaccbf09fcd\">could make a better choice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ebcb9ca4-a937-45b8-b585-20255ec2bdef\">allowed to concentrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words A – I below. Write the correct letter, A – I, in boxes 32 – 35 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. more</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"9124c41c-0e74-40e1-88d6-9edbce28f583\">surprising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. simple</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. better</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. conscious</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. obvious</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. complex</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. less</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. worse</span></p><p><b><span>Dijksterhuis's shopping study and its conclusions</span></b></p><p><span>Using clothing and furniture as examples of different types of purchases, Dijksterhuis questioned shoppers on their satisfaction with what they had bought. People who spent (32)______ time <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"b85813b1-872c-492b-84f4-31f199c9d156\">choosing simple clothing items<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"51be7c19-aba7-47db-8407-97a7250e9f40\">were more satisfied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> than those <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c7c64b4d-df10-48d6-abd1-933b8fa93fb6\">who decided quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. However, when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"9ec7a724-ef20-4fcc-8bef-7e4a9725908f\">buying furniture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, shoppers made (33)______ purchasing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"530f1d88-e8e5-4b00-95b3-95b2d53188c3\">decisions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> if they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"4f9f63fa-f1e0-424f-a6f2-a4b2ddd81285\">didn't think too hard<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. From this, the researchers concluded that in other choices, perhaps more important than shopping, (34)______ decisions are best <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"7112b917-93a0-4921-8217-7a241eb25c7d\">made by the unconscious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. The writer notes that this conclusion, though (35)______, is supported by the study results.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322493\" id=\"question-wrapper-322493\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322494\" id=\"question-wrapper-322494\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322495\" id=\"question-wrapper-322495\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322496\" id=\"question-wrapper-322496\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36 – 40 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322497\" id=\"question-wrapper-322497\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Dijksterhuis's findings <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"69ad7636-ce1c-44c5-b7a5-d55a47a77a64\">agree with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> conventional thinking in politics and organisational studies.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322498\" id=\"question-wrapper-322498\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some political leaders seem to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"d1d32deb-30a7-4363-9719-b7350533e3a9\">use deliberation without attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> when making complex decisions.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322499\" id=\"question-wrapper-322499\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>All political decisions are complex ones.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322500\" id=\"question-wrapper-322500\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>We judge political errors <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"3b0fe39a-d84d-482d-b6ea-c01fdc0e7e98\">according to our own political beliefs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322501\" id=\"question-wrapper-322501\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"5d7cc3b8-26e1-4ba3-ba12-6daa613296d3\">Social considerations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> may need to be taken into account for any study of decision making to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2406c11a-79f3-482c-98d1-4227fe74a1ed\">truly meaningful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"58564f33-2a26-41a3-8892-b80095ed1112","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"easy solutions","passagePhrase":"simple answer"},{"uid":"deb4dcfa-e09c-465f-91e8-b9d985a8ff48","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"difficult problems","passagePhrase":"intractable problem"},{"uid":"edb44224-a164-422b-9d3c-00c7d50812ab","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"all important facts be considered","passagePhrase":"thorough canvassing, surveying, weighing, examining and reexamining relevant information and options"},{"uid":"f7183dd4-e690-4a70-a70f-928bea783a99","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"made very quickly","passagePhrase":"snap' decisions"},{"uid":"463ac275-7e5c-4e64-a2eb-d675900995ab","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"the best decisions","passagePhrase":"superior"},{"uid":"204810bd-f964-43c3-a50b-2d9af4c4d2ff","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"conscious decision making is negatively affected by task complexity","passagePhrase":"complex decisions place increasing strain on those resources, the quality of our decisions declines"},{"uid":"9124c41c-0e74-40e1-88d6-9edbce28f583","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"surprising","passagePhrase":"counter-intuitive"},{"uid":"ebcb9ca4-a937-45b8-b585-20255ec2bdef","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"allowed to concentrate","passagePhrase":"undistracted deliberative thought"},{"uid":"7c6f3d96-9354-484f-9c1c-afaccbf09fcd","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"could make a better choice","passagePhrase":"did better at discriminating"},{"uid":"c7c64b4d-df10-48d6-abd1-933b8fa93fb6","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"who decided quickly","passagePhrase":"who"},{"uid":"51be7c19-aba7-47db-8407-97a7250e9f40 c7c64b4d-df10-48d6-abd1-933b8fa93fb6","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"bought with little conscious deliberation"},{"uid":"b85813b1-872c-492b-84f4-31f199c9d156","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"choosing simple clothing items","passagePhrase":"simple clothing purchase"},{"uid":"9ec7a724-ef20-4fcc-8bef-7e4a9725908f","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"buying furniture","passagePhrase":"furniture purchases"},{"uid":"4f9f63fa-f1e0-424f-a6f2-a4b2ddd81285","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"didn't think too hard","passagePhrase":"Deliberation without attention"},{"uid":"530f1d88-e8e5-4b00-95b3-95b2d53188c3","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"decisions","passagePhrase":"matters"},{"uid":"7112b917-93a0-4921-8217-7a241eb25c7d","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"made by the unconscious","passagePhrase":"delegate thinking about more complicated matters to the unconscious"},{"uid":"d1d32deb-30a7-4363-9719-b7350533e3a9","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"use deliberation without attention","passagePhrase":"embrace this wisdom"},{"uid":"3b0fe39a-d84d-482d-b6ea-c01fdc0e7e98","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"according to our own political beliefs","passagePhrase":"relationship between their politics and our own"},{"uid":"2406c11a-79f3-482c-98d1-4227fe74a1ed","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"truly meaningful","passagePhrase":"more useful examination"},{"uid":"5d7cc3b8-26e1-4ba3-ba12-6daa613296d3","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Social considerations","passagePhrase":"social context"}]},"reading_u2_34":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>Ambergris</span></b></p><p><i><span>What is it and where does it come from?</span></i></p><p><span>In the ancient world, the waxy grey substance we now refer to as ambergris was highly prized for its medicinal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b69dbb6c-950a-4ac7-bc05-fcbc326f3803\">properties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, and was widely used as a spice, which was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"178a5529-83df-4943-976f-c646aa1f7980\">believed to be an<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> aphrodisiac when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"ec31d69c-8f11-4863-98e0-32ed26cdebca\">added to food or wine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Ambergris itself is pleasantly aromatic, especially when warmed, and it was also highly valued as a fixing agent in the making of perfume, since it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"cbfaabd4-caf8-4af6-95e6-f9abb3363897\">enabled a scent to retain its fragrance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> for much longer than might otherwise have been possible. Most ambergris was found in the form of lumps floating on the surface of the sea, or washed up on the shores of tropical and temperate oceans. At one time, ambergris was worth its weight in gold, but there was much confusion about its origins.</span></p><p><span>Ambergris was known to the Arabs as ‘ambar’ and was originally called amber in the West in the Middle Ages. This eventually led to further confusion in the popular mind between ambergris and true amber, the mineral known to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b7d7e245-6822-440f-ad5c-833b70a1bd61\">mineralogists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> as succinite, which is actually fossilised tree resin, and generally yellow in colour. Both substances were rare and costly, and both were associated with the sea, largely because for Europeans the most common source of amber was the shores of the Baltic. In Chapter 92 of </span><i><span>Moby Dick</span></i><span>, the American writer Herman Melville pours scorn on those who believed the two substances to be the same: ‘Though the word ambergris is but the French compound for grey amber, yet the two substances are quite distinct. For amber, though at times found on the sea-coast, is also dug up in some far-inland soils, whereas ambergris is never found except upon the sea. Besides, amber is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"1b2cba2a-2fdf-45ad-9ac6-9576ee710e6f\">hard<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"714f14c8-7e6e-45b3-869a-966628f276e2\">transparent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7ae1dd33-0c66-451c-8db9-d29a3ffa4488\">brittle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, odorless substance, used for mouth-pieces to pipes, for beads and ornaments; but ambergris is soft, waxy, and so highly fragrant that it is largely used in perfumery.’</span></p><p><i><span>Moby Dick </span></i><span>was published in 1851, by which time the mystery of the origins of ambergris had been resolved by the scientific community. In 1783, the botanist Joseph Banks, who had accompanied Captain James Cook on his voyages of discovery in the Pacific, presented a paper to the Royal Society of London by the German physician Dr Franz Xavier Schwediawer in which it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"eacaa3a9-11e6-4a70-bf42-6ee53ae66555\">conclusively proved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> that ambergris <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"761811d1-440f-42c8-a672-3057e35c0e24\">came from sperm whales<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. In this, he was confirming an observation made in the 13th century by the great Venetian traveller Marco Polo who, while on the island of Socotra in the Indian Ocean, had witnessed a sperm whale vomiting up ambergris. But whereas Marco Polo <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a9a3cd20-4250-4572-8a42-46113feb2172\">thought that the whale had swallowed the lump<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in the depths of the sea, Schwediawer showed that the origin of the material was inside the whale itself.</span></p><p><span>The sperm whale is the largest of the odontocetes, or toothed whales. Males can grow up to 20 metres in length. Melville described the sperm whale as ‘the king of whales’, and his novel </span><i><span>Moby Dick</span></i><span> is based on the pursuit of one such creature. Sperm whales are renowned for their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"77701e7a-2d51-4f73-b03e-44e5a4fc1f2a\">ability to dive to great depths, possibly as far as 3,000 metres below the surface<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, and for remaining underwater for periods of two hours or more in pursuit of their favourite prey, the giant squid.</span></p><p><span>It is from the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a0809541-3ebe-4f8a-bd00-f0c75d9e293c\">problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the whales have in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"510deff2-baaf-493c-994c-8dde7ff10f87\">digesting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the beaks of such creatures that ambergris has its origins. The beak is sharp and irritates the whale’s lower intestine, which responds by producing a black, foul-smelling liquid. It is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"7e51437a-9727-4150-b938-b510df70b6ed\">not clear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to scientists whether this secretion should be considered a normal response by the whale’s digestive system or a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f1ca2601-7158-4cd9-b3f8-148d23f312a8\">pathological<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> one, but from time to time, large quantities of the liquid are vomited up by the whale. Once outside the whale’s body and exposed to air, the substance hardens, acquiring the waxy, greyish and pleasantly aromatic characteristics of ambergris. Often, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5c9b5af4-072e-424b-b1de-edacce8d7fe3\">beaks of squid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> are still found <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5c9b5af4-072e-424b-b1de-edacce8d7fe3\">embedded in lumps of ambergris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, some of which can weigh several hundred kilograms. Melville took some delight in contrasting the origins of ambergris with the high value placed upon it by refined society: ‘Who would think, then, that such fine ladies and gentlemen should regale themselves with an essence found in the inglorious bowels of a sick whale!’</span></p><p><span>Sperm whales were ruthlessly pursued by commercial whalers in the 19th and 20th centuries. In 1963-64 alone, almost 30,000 individuals were killed, and only the imposition of a ban on the hunting of sperm whales in 1984 saved the species from extinction. Ambergris was by far the most valuable product to be extracted during the processing of the whales’ carcasses, and over 90 per cent of the ambergris used in the perfume industry, even today, is by-product of commercial whaling. However, even before the ban on hunting sperm whales was imposed, the 1972 Marine Mammal Protection Act had prohibited trade in ambergris. Just as petroleum and plastic products were replacing other natural products of whaling, so ambergris was supplanted in the making of perfume by other materials, some natural and some synthetic in origin. Nevertheless, it is possible that, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"cd9100a7-230e-4275-aaea-8614f814465b\">as sperm-whale populations recover<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to their former numbers in the wild, so the sight of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"37bb7ee9-a08f-450f-b8e9-0c9e82d41198\">lumps of ambergris washed ashore along the tide-line<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"ea88f577-135e-4590-972d-3d55d77e08e1\">will once again become a familiar one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to beach-combers the world over.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>Ambergris: use, identity, origin, and formation</span></b></p><p><b><span>Earlier value and use</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Ambergris was once believed to have useful (1)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b69dbb6c-950a-4ac7-bc05-fcbc326f3803\">effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></li><li><span>When <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"ec31d69c-8f11-4863-98e0-32ed26cdebca\">mixed with food or drink<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"178a5529-83df-4943-976f-c646aa1f7980\">thought to work as an<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> (2)______.</span></li><li><span>In perfume production, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"cbfaabd4-caf8-4af6-95e6-f9abb3363897\">helped a smell remain noticeable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> for longer by acting as a (3)______.</span></li></ul><p><b><span>Confusion with amber</span></b></p><ul><li><span>True amber is referred to by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b7d7e245-6822-440f-ad5c-833b70a1bd61\">specialists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> as (4)______.</span></li><li><span>Unlike ambergris, amber is described as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"1b2cba2a-2fdf-45ad-9ac6-9576ee710e6f\">firm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"714f14c8-7e6e-45b3-869a-966628f276e2\">clear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7ae1dd33-0c66-451c-8db9-d29a3ffa4488\">easily broken<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, as well as (5)______.</span></li></ul><p><b><span>Scientific explanation</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Ambergris was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"eacaa3a9-11e6-4a70-bf42-6ee53ae66555\">finally proved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> in 1783 to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"761811d1-440f-42c8-a672-3057e35c0e24\">come from a single species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, the (6)______.</span></li><li><span>Ambergris develops because whales have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a0809541-3ebe-4f8a-bd00-f0c75d9e293c\">difficulty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"510deff2-baaf-493c-994c-8dde7ff10f87\">processing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the (7)______ of giant squid.</span></li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322502\" id=\"question-wrapper-322502\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">medicinal</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322503\" id=\"question-wrapper-322503\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">aphrodisiac</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322504\" id=\"question-wrapper-322504\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">fixing agent</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322505\" id=\"question-wrapper-322505\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">succinite</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322506\" id=\"question-wrapper-322506\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">odorless/odourless</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322507\" id=\"question-wrapper-322507\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">sperm whale(s)</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322508\" id=\"question-wrapper-322508\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">beaks</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322509\" id=\"question-wrapper-322509\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Marco Polo correctly understood that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a9a3cd20-4250-4572-8a42-46113feb2172\">ambergris was produced inside the whale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322510\" id=\"question-wrapper-322510\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Sperm whales are able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"77701e7a-2d51-4f73-b03e-44e5a4fc1f2a\">remain below the surface for exceptionally long periods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322511\" id=\"question-wrapper-322511\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Scientists are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"7e51437a-9727-4150-b938-b510df70b6ed\">certain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> that the production of the black liquid is an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f1ca2601-7158-4cd9-b3f8-148d23f312a8\">abnormal condition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322512\" id=\"question-wrapper-322512\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Ambergris <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5c9b5af4-072e-424b-b1de-edacce8d7fe3\">containing squid remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> is usually smaller than other pieces of ambergris. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322513\" id=\"question-wrapper-322513\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Synthetic substitutes are cheaper to use in perfume production than ambergris.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322514\" id=\"question-wrapper-322514\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"37bb7ee9-a08f-450f-b8e9-0c9e82d41198\">Beach finds of ambergris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"ea88f577-135e-4590-972d-3d55d77e08e1\">may become more common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> again <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"cd9100a7-230e-4275-aaea-8614f814465b\">in the future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b69dbb6c-950a-4ac7-bc05-fcbc326f3803","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"effects","passagePhrase":"properties"},{"uid":"178a5529-83df-4943-976f-c646aa1f7980","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"thought to work as an","passagePhrase":"believed to be an"},{"uid":"ec31d69c-8f11-4863-98e0-32ed26cdebca","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"mixed with food or drink","passagePhrase":"added to food or wine"},{"uid":"cbfaabd4-caf8-4af6-95e6-f9abb3363897","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"helped a smell remain noticeable","passagePhrase":"enabled a scent to retain its fragrance"},{"uid":"b7d7e245-6822-440f-ad5c-833b70a1bd61","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"specialists","passagePhrase":"mineralogists"},{"uid":"1b2cba2a-2fdf-45ad-9ac6-9576ee710e6f","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"firm","passagePhrase":"hard"},{"uid":"714f14c8-7e6e-45b3-869a-966628f276e2","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"clear","passagePhrase":"transparent"},{"uid":"7ae1dd33-0c66-451c-8db9-d29a3ffa4488","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"easily broken","passagePhrase":"brittle"},{"uid":"eacaa3a9-11e6-4a70-bf42-6ee53ae66555","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"finally proved","passagePhrase":"conclusively proved"},{"uid":"761811d1-440f-42c8-a672-3057e35c0e24","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"come from a single species","passagePhrase":"came from sperm whales"},{"uid":"77701e7a-2d51-4f73-b03e-44e5a4fc1f2a","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"remain below the surface for exceptionally long periods","passagePhrase":"ability to dive to great depths, possibly as far as 3,000 metres below the surface"},{"uid":"a0809541-3ebe-4f8a-bd00-f0c75d9e293c","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"difficulty","passagePhrase":"problems"},{"uid":"510deff2-baaf-493c-994c-8dde7ff10f87","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"processing","passagePhrase":"digesting"},{"uid":"f1ca2601-7158-4cd9-b3f8-148d23f312a8","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"abnormal condition","passagePhrase":"pathological"},{"uid":"5c9b5af4-072e-424b-b1de-edacce8d7fe3","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"containing squid remains","passagePhrase":"beaks of squid ... embedded in lumps of ambergris"},{"uid":"cd9100a7-230e-4275-aaea-8614f814465b","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"in the future","passagePhrase":"as sperm-whale populations recover"},{"uid":"37bb7ee9-a08f-450f-b8e9-0c9e82d41198","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"Beach finds of ambergris","passagePhrase":"lumps of ambergris washed ashore along the tide-line"},{"uid":"ea88f577-135e-4590-972d-3d55d77e08e1","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"may become more common","passagePhrase":"will once again become a familiar one"}]},"reading_u2_35":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>Photovoltaics on the rooftop</span></b></p><p><i><span>A natural choice for powering the family home</span></i></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> In the past, urban homeowners have not always had much choice in the way electricity is supplied to their homes. Now, however, there is a choice, and a rapidly increasing number of households worldwide are choosing the solar energy option. Solar energy, the conversion of sunlight into energy, is made possible through the use of 'photovoltaics', which are simple appliances that fit onto the roof of a house.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>The photovoltaic-powered home remains connected to the power lines, but <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"4f986c80-1b7e-4dee-8d0a-3e3f001481f4\">no storage is required on-site<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, only a box of electronics the inverter to the interface between the photovoltaics and the grid network. Figure 1 illustrates the system. During the day, when the home may not be using much electricity, excess power from the solar array is fed back into the grid to be used elsewhere and credited to the house owner. At night, power flows the opposite way. The grid network effectively provides storage. If the demand for electricity is well matched to when the sun shines, solar energy is especially valuable. This occurs in places like <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"fadb0023-e6fa-4702-b24c-d092751e4657\">California in the US and Japan<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"be1cbefa-b824-413a-92df-38f6a5e5e521\">air-conditioning loads for offices and factories are large but heating loads for homes are small<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> The first systematic creation of the use of photovoltaics on homes began in the US during the 1970s. A well-conceived program started with the siting of a number of 'residential experiment stations' at selected locations around the country, representing different climatic zones. These stations contained a number of 'dummy' houses, each with a different solar-energy system design. Homes within the communities close to these stations were monitored to see how well their energy use matched the energy generated by the stations' dummy roofs. A change in US government priorities in the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"9bb1c765-53a1-4305-b9ed-6f303b2d5e2d\">early 1980s halted this program<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>With the US effort dropping away, the Japanese Sunshine Project came to the fore. A large residential test station was installed on Rokko Island beginning in 1986. This installation consists of 18 'dummy' homes. Each is equipped with its own 2 - 5 kilowatt photovoltaic system (about 20 – 50 square meters for each system). Some of these simulated homes have their own electrical appliances inside, such as TV sets, refrigerators and air conditioning units, which switch on and off under computer control, providing a lavish lifestyle for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"c437df91-1643-43a4-8f8b-c80944473720\">non-existent occupants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. For the other systems, electronics simulate these household loads. This test station has allowed the technical issues involved in using photovoltaics within the electricity network to be explored in a systematic way, under well-controlled test conditions. With no insurmountable problems identified, the Japanese have used the experience gained from this station to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"de04824b-fe53-4f1d-b193-7102faa5d7da\">begin their own massive residential photovoltaics campaign<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. While the US prioritized rapid expansion, the Japanese approach emphasized careful technical validation.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Meanwhile, Germany began a very important '1,000 roof program' in 1990, aimed at installing photovoltaics on the roofs of 1,000 private homes. Large federal and regional government subsidies were involved, accounting in most cases for 70% of the total system costs. The program proved immensely popular, forcing its extension to over 2,000 homes scattered across Germany. The success of this program stimulated other European countries to launch similar programs. Japan's 'one million roof program' was prompted by the experience gained in the Rokko Island test site and the success of the German 1,000 roof program. The initially quoted aims of the Japanese New Energy Development Organization were to have 70,000 homes equipped with photovoltaics by the year 2000, on the way to 1 million by 2010. The program <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7fcd4837-33fb-46f5-bd91-c3ebb681f23c\">made a modest start in 1994<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, when 539 systems were installed with a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"84611c33-043a-4630-9c36-02bb2e019672\">government subsidy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c462bf20-713e-4080-8143-b81dcab85b41\">50 percent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Under this program, entire new suburban developments are using photovoltaics. The Japanese initiative in embracing residential photovoltaics on a large scale prompted responses in both Europe and the US. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"59674e7a-1923-4f41-8039-2715bd5c5dc0\">European Commission<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> has called for one million solar residential systems before the year 2010, with 500,000 in Europe and 500,000 in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e38a2cba-29d9-4638-b7dc-e6a24b1ecf33\">developing world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0f1e5d8e-8258-43cd-92b4-a6fadb287703\">subsidised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> by the Commission. In 1997, a similar one million roof target was announced in the US. Since then, several other countries, including Germany, Italy, the Netherlands and Australia, have announced their own targets for residential photovoltaics. However, the success of these national programs <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"1e1afb4a-e8be-4cc2-82f7-50abb61857a6\">cannot be judged simply<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> by the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"514446aa-2585-4195-9082-b26b570cb095\">number of systems installed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Critics argue that government subsidies create dependency rather than market-driven adoption.</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> This is good news, not only for the photovoltaic industry, but for everyone concerned with the environment. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"d2ad35d2-86e7-4fe2-8caa-500aa5ff003e\">use of fossil fuels to generate electricity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> is not only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"b405f273-4d59-405a-b3ff-e1d2e2473d73\">costly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in financial terms, but also in terms of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"b405f273-4d59-405a-b3ff-e1d2e2473d73\">environmental damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Gases produced by the burning of fossil fuels in the production of electricity are a major contributor to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"b405f273-4d59-405a-b3ff-e1d2e2473d73\">greenhouse effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. To deal with this problem, many governments are now proposing stringent targets on the amount of greenhouse gas emissions permitted. These targets mean that all sources of greenhouse gas emissions, including residential electricity use, will receive closer attention in the future. Although there is an initial cost in attaching the system to the rooftop, the householder's outlay is soon compensated with the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"b9276a07-04ca-4523-a185-b63c1a9719ec\">savings on energy bills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. In addition, everyone living on the planet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"b9276a07-04ca-4523-a185-b63c1a9719ec\">stands to gain from the more benign environmental impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> It is likely that in the future governments will develop building codes that attempt to constrain the energy demand of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"d3c29725-f5f1-4d99-b33b-9c96d5ab1fdf\">new housing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. For example, the use of photovoltaics or the equivalent may be stipulated to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e06ef50a-662b-48b2-9aa0-fc07188deb00\">lessen demands on the grid network<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and hence reduce fossil fuel emissions. Approvals for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"a9de4356-c37c-4f39-9153-94b55cfd6e5a\">building renovations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> may also be conditional upon taking such energy-saving measures. If this were to happen, everyone would benefit.</span></p><p><b><span>Figure 1</span></b></p><p><i><b><span>Photovoltaics on the family home</span></b></i></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_2/reading/images/a559f64bfceb7efa5559197d17b92363ed8d19f1f53a1da5042715ddad08697b.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A–G in boxes 14 – 19 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322515\" id=\"question-wrapper-322515\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"fadb0023-e6fa-4702-b24c-d092751e4657\">places<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"be1cbefa-b824-413a-92df-38f6a5e5e521\">electricity use is greater during the day than at night<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322516\" id=\"question-wrapper-322516\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a detailed description of an experiment that led to photovoltaics being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"de04824b-fe53-4f1d-b193-7102faa5d7da\">promoted throughout the country<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322517\" id=\"question-wrapper-322517\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"b405f273-4d59-405a-b3ff-e1d2e2473d73\">negative effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"d2ad35d2-86e7-4fe2-8caa-500aa5ff003e\">conventional means of generating electricity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322518\" id=\"question-wrapper-322518\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an explanation of the photovoltaics system</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322519\" id=\"question-wrapper-322519\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"b9276a07-04ca-4523-a185-b63c1a9719ec\">long-term benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of using photovoltaics</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322520\" id=\"question-wrapper-322520\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"59674e7a-1923-4f41-8039-2715bd5c5dc0\">wealthy countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0f1e5d8e-8258-43cd-92b4-a6fadb287703\">prepared to help<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e38a2cba-29d9-4638-b7dc-e6a24b1ecf33\">less wealthy countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> have access to photovoltaics</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2? In boxes 20 – 24 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322521\" id=\"question-wrapper-322521\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Photovoltaic-powered homes <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"4f986c80-1b7e-4dee-8d0a-3e3f001481f4\">need their own equipment to keep unused electricity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> for later use.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322522\" id=\"question-wrapper-322522\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Government backing for residential photovoltaics in the US <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"9bb1c765-53a1-4305-b9ed-6f303b2d5e2d\">carried on steadily from the 1970s into the following decade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322523\" id=\"question-wrapper-322523\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The solar-powered houses on Rokko Island are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"c437df91-1643-43a4-8f8b-c80944473720\">uninhabited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322524\" id=\"question-wrapper-322524\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>When <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7fcd4837-33fb-46f5-bd91-c3ebb681f23c\">Japan’s residential photovoltaic scheme began<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, householders received <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"84611c33-043a-4630-9c36-02bb2e019672\">public funding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c462bf20-713e-4080-8143-b81dcab85b41\">half the installation cost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322525\" id=\"question-wrapper-322525\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Germany, Italy, the Netherlands and Australia all have strict goals with regard to greenhouse gas emissions.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter A–D in boxes 25-26 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322526\" id=\"question-wrapper-322526\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is suggested about national photovoltaic programs?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"514446aa-2585-4195-9082-b26b570cb095\">Counting how many systems were fitted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"1e1afb4a-e8be-4cc2-82f7-50abb61857a6\">does not fully show whether a program worked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Countries using subsidies gained attention faster than those using trials.</li> <li>C. Germany’s funding model was copied by the most successful programs.</li> <li>D. The US and Japan used similar approaches, though Japan acted earlier.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322527\" id=\"question-wrapper-322527\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What may governments require in relation to future housing?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. All existing homes may be forced to replace conventional energy systems with photovoltaics.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"d3c29725-f5f1-4d99-b33b-9c96d5ab1fdf\">New buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"a9de4356-c37c-4f39-9153-94b55cfd6e5a\">some renovations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> may need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e06ef50a-662b-48b2-9aa0-fc07188deb00\">reduce pressure on the electricity network<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Building codes may prevent householders from carrying out major renovations.</li> <li>D. Energy-saving measures may be required only in areas without access to the grid.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"fadb0023-e6fa-4702-b24c-d092751e4657","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"places","passagePhrase":"California in the US and Japan"},{"uid":"be1cbefa-b824-413a-92df-38f6a5e5e521","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"electricity use is greater during the day than at night","passagePhrase":"air-conditioning loads for offices and factories are large but heating loads for homes are small"},{"uid":"c437df91-1643-43a4-8f8b-c80944473720","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"uninhabited","passagePhrase":"non-existent occupants"},{"uid":"de04824b-fe53-4f1d-b193-7102faa5d7da","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"promoted throughout the country","passagePhrase":"begin their own massive residential photovoltaics campaign"},{"uid":"7fcd4837-33fb-46f5-bd91-c3ebb681f23c","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Japan’s residential photovoltaic scheme began","passagePhrase":"made a modest start in 1994"},{"uid":"84611c33-043a-4630-9c36-02bb2e019672","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"public funding","passagePhrase":"government subsidy"},{"uid":"c462bf20-713e-4080-8143-b81dcab85b41","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"half the installation cost","passagePhrase":"50 percent"},{"uid":"59674e7a-1923-4f41-8039-2715bd5c5dc0","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"wealthy countries","passagePhrase":"European Commission"},{"uid":"e38a2cba-29d9-4638-b7dc-e6a24b1ecf33","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"less wealthy countries","passagePhrase":"developing world"},{"uid":"0f1e5d8e-8258-43cd-92b4-a6fadb287703","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"prepared to help","passagePhrase":"subsidised"},{"uid":"1e1afb4a-e8be-4cc2-82f7-50abb61857a6","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"does not fully show whether a program worked","passagePhrase":"cannot be judged simply"},{"uid":"514446aa-2585-4195-9082-b26b570cb095","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"Counting how many systems were fitted","passagePhrase":"number of systems installed"},{"uid":"d2ad35d2-86e7-4fe2-8caa-500aa5ff003e","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"conventional means of generating electricity","passagePhrase":"use of fossil fuels to generate electricity"},{"uid":"b405f273-4d59-405a-b3ff-e1d2e2473d73","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"negative effects","passagePhrase":"costly ... environmental damage ... greenhouse effect"},{"uid":"b9276a07-04ca-4523-a185-b63c1a9719ec","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"long-term benefits","passagePhrase":"savings on energy bills ... stands to gain from the more benign environmental impact"},{"uid":"d3c29725-f5f1-4d99-b33b-9c96d5ab1fdf","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"New buildings","passagePhrase":"new housing"},{"uid":"e06ef50a-662b-48b2-9aa0-fc07188deb00","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"reduce pressure on the electricity network","passagePhrase":"lessen demands on the grid network"},{"uid":"a9de4356-c37c-4f39-9153-94b55cfd6e5a","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"some renovations","passagePhrase":"building renovations"}]},"reading_u2_36":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The New Zealand writer Margaret Mahy</span></b></p><p><span>In a career spanning some fifty years, Margaret Mahy has come to occupy a unique place in New Zealand writing with innovative fiction and original characterisation. In our solidly realist tradition, the linguistic fireworks of Mahy’s children’s fiction and the explorations of human behaviour at the heart of her supernatural teenage fiction <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"146b8fe7-ee4d-4c26-8e9f-23fcc4209668\">stand gloriously alone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Mahy’s clearest heir, I have always thought, is Elizabeth Knox — and maybe the true inheritance there is sheer singularity. Just as there is no one else like Knox in New Zealand writing, Mahy, too, has ventured into imaginative territory unknown to other local writers. So it was with great pleasure that I visited Mahy recently at her Governor’s Bay home to talk about her new book. As with all journalists, she is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"70114abf-693f-481f-946d-bbad60e20299\">generous to a fault with her time and attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>; and, as always — despite her careful consideration of questions and thoughtful answers — I’m reminded she <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"4f08dceb-e578-4e74-bdda-55426a403894\">isn’t truly comfortable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> making herself or her life the heart of any conversation.</span></p><p><span>Certainly, any consideration of the style of Mahy’s novels and picture books throws up some irresistible theories. As a writer committed to supporting herself through her art, she has seldom had the time for formal research. Rather, it has been a matter of going out and finding inspiration from her <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"5e761a94-edb2-43bb-b434-6f2bd2fc487c\">immediate environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>: the writing on the side of a bus; a spelling mistake in a note to herself; the similarity between a cat and a fur hat. But despite these sometimes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"5e761a94-edb2-43bb-b434-6f2bd2fc487c\">mundane origins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, the settings for her stories are delightfully varied, as these books celebrate the dramatic plot twists and unpredictability of adventures on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"c47d47d9-af28-4c57-bbb0-5c704757808e\">high seas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> or in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"c47d47d9-af28-4c57-bbb0-5c704757808e\">Antarctica<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, and also in quite unassuming places like the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"95733cbe-152c-430f-841e-1781521f6213\">library<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> or even down the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"95733cbe-152c-430f-841e-1781521f6213\">back of a chair<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> at home. Mahy has a lifelong affection for characters who are agents of upheaval and disturbance. Her junior and picture books are peppered with pirates, robbers and lions, though they appear alongside librarians, mothers and children, working against comfortable stereotypes. Her fictions often have at their heart a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"bbc4ea53-4c93-4872-987c-e78bd84b30e1\">young adult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> burdened with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"69a107e7-4b0e-4722-82be-5cab99c32c3d\">special powers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, such as the ability to cast spells in order to transform their world in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"69a107e7-4b0e-4722-82be-5cab99c32c3d\">supernatural<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> and fantastical ways. Another common feature is that, while the conclusions of her tales are usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"ffd8c457-b857-4a6e-9600-736a35a0dae9\">predictable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"180297c6-671f-4b50-a399-518196c2cd2f\">leave the reader feeling absolutely complete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, the moral questions resulting from our hero’s powers having been resolved.</span></p><p><span>Many of these themes can be found in her new novel, </span><i><span>The Magician of Hoad</span></i><span>. The book was begun more than 15 years ago and envisioned as an ‘entire’ fantasy — one set in a fully imagined world with detailed history and complex tribal inter-relationships, a classical hero quest at its heart. The story <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"dbc7cf6f-356b-4de3-a9ce-e4ee5bd0919b\">ballooned at one point to 800 pages and has been through at least two substantial rewrites. Now half its original size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, it is a fascinating read — an adventure, a romance, and a gold mine of Mahy’s literary preoccupations.</span></p><p><span>The other splendid Mahy publication this year is a re-issue of </span><i><span>Bubble Trouble</span></i><span> in a now-illustrated edition. This tongue-twister tale first appeared in 1991, was included in </span><i><span>100 New Zealand Poems</span></i><span> (1993) and has been recited by Mahy at countless private and public functions. Perhaps more than any other work, </span><i><span>Bubble Trouble</span></i><span> is the Mahy that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"730529b3-6732-4de2-acf2-c41294dd5636\">New Zealand children and their parents know so well<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, the rollicking story of a clown who serves up a joyous torrent of word-play and unexpected rhyme.</span></p><p><span>Those <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"3f61b678-145b-4ce8-8989-e67360ee712a\">connections are four or five deep now<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. I read </span><i><span>The Lion in the Meadow</span></i><span> in the </span><i><span>School Journal</span></i><span> in the late 1960s; my step-daughter listened to </span><i><span>The Boy Who Was Followed Home </span></i><span>over and over in the 1970s; my own children sat very still mouthing </span><i><span>The Great White Man-Eating Shark</span></i><span> in the 80s and 90s; now, in the 21st century, my grandchildren have heard </span><i><span>Down the Dragon’s Tongue</span></i><span>, </span><i><span>A Summery Saturday Morning</span></i><span> and </span><i><span>Dashing Dog</span></i><span> many times.</span></p><p><span>Of course, readers are important to any working writer, but Mahy’s espousal of the act of reading goes beyond that: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e061b62b-4aee-43bf-8a9e-77b5a896b692\">a book is not properly finished<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, she has often said, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e061b62b-4aee-43bf-8a9e-77b5a896b692\">until it has been read<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, because a reader brings something important to the book. So, doubtless out of need to build a market — she’s not ignorant of her popularity — but also out of genuine care for that other dynamic part of the author-reader relationship, Mahy has, until recently, kept up a punishing schedule of public appearances.</span></p><p><span>Private conversation with Mahy has always been a wild ride — marvellous, in the true sense of the word, the product of a hungry head and an infinite capacity to be astonished. She races away at one stage to consult an encyclopaedia for L. M. Montgomery’s date of death, and speculates about the ‘real’ Montgomery, creator of the ever-popular </span><i><span>Anne of Green Gables</span></i><span>. Although I’d come to talk about her new book, I couldn’t help but be captivated by her infectious curiosity.</span></p><p><span>A few years ago, the writer David Hill told a funny story. Though his writing was, he conceded, very different from Mahy’s, he had been affected by her peculiarly alert <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"e5c6dacf-1008-4b3a-91b5-4a7f44e381cb\">way of looking at the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, particularly the mad, slippery life of language. Once, Hill said, in a motel room, a sign on a door caught his eye: ‘This door is alarmed.’ Mahy would like that, thought Hill. She would enjoy the comedy just below the surface of the formal warning; she would leap immediately to the possibilities for story and language play: ‘Yes, and this window is concerned, this light fitting is irritated.’ His story was a wonderful <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"e5c6dacf-1008-4b3a-91b5-4a7f44e381cb\">comment on Mahy’s vision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322528\" id=\"question-wrapper-322528\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Mahy’s fiction is shown as <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"146b8fe7-ee4d-4c26-8e9f-23fcc4209668\">fitting neatly into the dominant style<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of New Zealand writing.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322529\" id=\"question-wrapper-322529\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Mahy’s books for younger readers are presented as having attracted more attention than her fiction for teenagers.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322530\" id=\"question-wrapper-322530\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Mahy and Knox have sometimes criticised each other’s work.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322531\" id=\"question-wrapper-322531\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Mahy is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"70114abf-693f-481f-946d-bbad60e20299\">welcoming to interviewers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322532\" id=\"question-wrapper-322532\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Mahy is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"4f08dceb-e578-4e74-bdda-55426a403894\">at ease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> speaking about her experiences.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below using the list of words and phrases A–I. Write the correct letter A–I in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. disruptive and unpredictable </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"5e761a94-edb2-43bb-b434-6f2bd2fc487c\">everyday<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. loveable</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. controversial </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"c47d47d9-af28-4c57-bbb0-5c704757808e\">exotic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"95733cbe-152c-430f-841e-1781521f6213\">ordinary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. isolated</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. unconfident </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"ffd8c457-b857-4a6e-9600-736a35a0dae9\">unsurprising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"180297c6-671f-4b50-a399-518196c2cd2f\">satisfying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"69a107e7-4b0e-4722-82be-5cab99c32c3d\">magical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span></span></p><p><b><span>Theories about Mahy’s style</span></b></p><p><span>Mahy’s determination to earn a living from writing has encouraged her to find the ideas for her work in (32)______ places</span><b><span>. </span></b><span>The stories themselves are set in locations that are (33)______. In terms of characterisation, almost all of her books feature unruly people, and very often an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"bbc4ea53-4c93-4872-987c-e78bd84b30e1\">adolescent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> who possesses (34)______ abilities. Finally, the endings of the stories tend to be (35)______.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322533\" id=\"question-wrapper-322533\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322534\" id=\"question-wrapper-322534\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322535\" id=\"question-wrapper-322535\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322536\" id=\"question-wrapper-322536\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter A–D in boxes 36–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322537\" id=\"question-wrapper-322537\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the writer say about The Magician of Hoad?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is partly based on true history.</li> <li>B. It was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"dbc7cf6f-356b-4de3-a9ce-e4ee5bd0919b\">restructured in the writing process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</li> <li>C. It is quite different from conventional stories.</li> <li>D. It does not reflect the usual themes of Mahy’s work.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322538\" id=\"question-wrapper-322538\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the writer, Bubble Trouble</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. was first illustrated in 1991.</li> <li>B. is written in plain language.</li> <li>C. is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"730529b3-6732-4de2-acf2-c41294dd5636\">an old favourite for many families<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</li> <li>D. has not been read aloud by Mahy before.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322539\" id=\"question-wrapper-322539\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer’s purpose in the fifth paragraph is to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. show how Mahy’s style has changed through generations.</li> <li>B. criticise Mahy’s children’s stories for being repetitive.</li> <li>C. describe how new media have changed entertainment.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"3f61b678-145b-4ce8-8989-e67360ee712a\">illustrate&nbsp;Mahy’s popularity with generations of children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322540\" id=\"question-wrapper-322540\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the sixth paragraph, which of the following is true?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Readers sometimes do not finish Mahy’s books.</li> <li>B. Mahy actively encourages feedback from readers.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e061b62b-4aee-43bf-8a9e-77b5a896b692\">The reading of a book is part of its creation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Mahy does not realise how important she is to some readers.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322541\" id=\"question-wrapper-322541\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the writer doing in the final paragraph?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"e5c6dacf-1008-4b3a-91b5-4a7f44e381cb\">illustrating Mahy’s view of the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></li> <li>B. comparing Mahy with another writer</li> <li>C. correcting a misconception about Mahy</li> <li>D. suggesting reasons for Mahy’s approach</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"70114abf-693f-481f-946d-bbad60e20299","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"welcoming to interviewers","passagePhrase":"generous to a fault with her time and attention"},{"uid":"5e761a94-edb2-43bb-b434-6f2bd2fc487c","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"everyday","passagePhrase":"immediate environment ... mundane origins"},{"uid":"c47d47d9-af28-4c57-bbb0-5c704757808e","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"exotic","passagePhrase":"high seas ... Antarctica"},{"uid":"95733cbe-152c-430f-841e-1781521f6213","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"ordinary","passagePhrase":"library ... back of a chair"},{"uid":"bbc4ea53-4c93-4872-987c-e78bd84b30e1","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"adolescent","passagePhrase":"young adult"},{"uid":"69a107e7-4b0e-4722-82be-5cab99c32c3d","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"magical","passagePhrase":"special powers ... supernatural"},{"uid":"ffd8c457-b857-4a6e-9600-736a35a0dae9","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"unsurprising","passagePhrase":"predictable"},{"uid":"180297c6-671f-4b50-a399-518196c2cd2f","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"satisfying","passagePhrase":"leave the reader feeling absolutely complete"},{"uid":"dbc7cf6f-356b-4de3-a9ce-e4ee5bd0919b","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"restructured in the writing process","passagePhrase":"ballooned at one point to 800 pages and has been through at least two substantial rewrites. Now half its original size"},{"uid":"730529b3-6732-4de2-acf2-c41294dd5636","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"an old favourite for many families","passagePhrase":"New Zealand children and their parents know so well"},{"uid":"3f61b678-145b-4ce8-8989-e67360ee712a","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"illustrate Mahy’s popularity with generations of children","passagePhrase":"connections are four or five deep now"},{"uid":"e061b62b-4aee-43bf-8a9e-77b5a896b692","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"The reading of a book is part of its creation","passagePhrase":"a book is not properly finished ... until it has been read"},{"uid":"e5c6dacf-1008-4b3a-91b5-4a7f44e381cb","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"illustrating Mahy’s view of the world","passagePhrase":"way of looking at the world ... comment on Mahy’s vision"}]},"reading_u2_37":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Listening to the Ocean</span></b></p><p><i><span>The results of some recent research answer some long-standing questions</span></i></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> The oceans cover more than 70 per cent of the planet’s surface, yet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"829075e4-e700-4d24-8b1d-7c29aff227ed\">until quite recently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d3daebb8-a38a-48b4-a388-ba637e74a883\">knew less about their depths than about the surface of the Moon<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. The Moon has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"0f896025-e479-46e6-b95e-09dc7ff5701e\">far more accessible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> to study because astronomers have long been able to look at its surface, first with the naked eye and then with the telescope, both instruments that focus light. Until the twentieth century, however, no instruments were available for the study of Earth’s oceans: light, which can travel trillions of kilometres through the vast vacuum of space, cannot penetrate very far in seawater.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> It turns out that for penetrating water, the best instrument is sound. Curious investigators have long been fascinated by sound and the way it travels in water. As early as 1490, the artist and scientist Leonardo da Vinci observed: ‘If you cause your ship to stop and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c63327ed-4984-4410-89f4-8c2d1ad7c066\">place the head of a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> long tube in the water and place the outer extremity to your ear, you will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"49c946d9-c2a9-43c9-8038-38c8b60721e2\">hear ships at a great distance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> from you.’ It was not until 1826 that two scientists, Colladon and Sturm, accurately measured the speed of sound in water. Using a long tube to listen underwater (as da Vinci had suggested), they recorded how fast the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"190ca9ad-19ed-4da6-b149-4e22d09bd55d\">sound of a submerged bell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> travelled across Lake Geneva in Switzerland. What these investigators demonstrated was that water is an excellent medium for sound, transmitting it almost five times faster than its speed in air.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> A number of factors influence how far sound travels underwater and how long it lasts, including particles, salinity, temperature and pressure. Particles in seawater can reflect, scatter and absorb certain frequencies of sound, just as certain wavelengths of light may be reflected, scattered and absorbed by specific types of particles in the atmosphere. In 1943, Maurice Ewing and J. L. Worzel conducted an experiment to test the theory that low-frequency waves, which are less vulnerable than higher frequencies to scattering and absorption, should be able to travel great distances, if the sound source is placed correctly. The researchers set off an underwater explosion and learned that it was detected easily by receivers 3,200 kilometres away. In analysing the results of this test, they discovered a kind of ‘sound <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"13d63843-73b5-469e-ad44-993cf4ae5edf\">pipeline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>’, known as the ‘deep sound <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"13d63843-73b5-469e-ad44-993cf4ae5edf\">channel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>’. Sound introduced into this channel of water could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"53daa186-7aba-45a7-ba5c-2b017064c4b8\">travel thousands of kilometres with minimal loss of signal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>The US Navy was quick to appreciate the usefulness of low-frequency sound and the deep sound channel. They developed the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d6071d9c-959f-4992-a822-ad1c8a14c218\">Sound Surveillance System<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (SOSUS), which involved <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"1a0378ca-9011-4ea6-901f-1d2fb218f632\">underwater microphones, called hydrophones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, that were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d6071d9c-959f-4992-a822-ad1c8a14c218\">placed on the ocean bottom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> and connected by cables to on-shore processing centres. It was Christopher Clark of Cornell University who soon realised that SOSUS could be used to listen to whales. Using a SOSUS receiver in the West Indies, he could hear whales that were 1,770 kilometres away.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Whales are the biggest of Earth’s creatures, yet these animals are also remarkably elusive. Scientists wishing to observe blue <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"fef50728-7298-4b28-87db-d08a72190737\">whale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>s must simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"48aa17c1-93f7-4c0c-a74e-03723b5008c9\">wait in their ships for the whales to surface<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. A few whales have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"104f3a27-6e42-479b-ab94-11758fc95766\">tracked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> briefly in the wild in this way but <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"dcec3d9e-8179-40f9-956e-296877bd89ef\">not for very great distances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, and much about them remains unknown. But by using SOSUS, scientists can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"062b0572-2ba0-43dc-ab8b-e6a79cd42cbe\">track<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> the whales and position them on a map. Moreover, they can track <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c44c7353-a820-400f-91f5-a31aa0ee37ba\">not just one whale at a time, but many creatures simultaneously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. They can also learn to distinguish whale <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c9bfd8d5-d9bb-42c4-b3e0-ca172f944bba\">calls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>; researchers have <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9f7c6edb-5517-43a4-b054-f44567132c2a\">detected changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> in the calls of finback whales <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"3e0070d4-c425-44c2-861c-a94332652790\">as the seasons change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, and have found that blue whales in different regions of the Pacific Ocean have different calls.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>SOSUS has also proved instrumental in obtaining information crucial to our understanding of climate. The system has enabled researchers to begin making ocean-temperature measurements on a global scale, measurements that are key to understanding the workings of heat transfer between the ocean and the atmosphere. The ocean plays an enormous role in determining air temperature — the heat capacity in only the upper few metres of ocean is thought to be equal to all of the heat in the entire atmosphere. For sound waves travelling horizontally in the ocean, speed is largely a function of temperature. Thus, the travel time of a wave of sound between two points is a sensitive indicator of the average temperature along its path. Transmitting sound in numerous directions through the deep sound channel can give scientists measurements spanning vast areas of the globe. Thousands of sound paths in the ocean can be pieced together into a map of global ocean temperatures, and by repeating measurements along the same paths over time, scientists can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"caecfa89-d01f-4bc9-8f4d-2a76cc099d80\">track changes in temperature over months or years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> Researchers are also using other acoustic techniques to monitor the climate. Oceanographer Jeff Nystuen, for example, has explored the use of sound to measure <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"d391242a-6c48-456c-b03e-4b23e07867a0\">rainfall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> over the ocean. Monitoring changing global rainfall patterns will contribute to understanding major climate change as well as the weather phenomenon known as El Niño. Since 1985, Nystuen has used hydrophones to listen to rain over the ocean, acoustically <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8\" data-uid=\"45e7ed55-1038-4507-af72-715a6856ecad 9a2702f1-a497-4bb2-acfa-48c43a7deed5\">measuring</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"45e7ed55-1038-4507-af72-715a6856ecad\"> not only the rainfall rate but also the </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"45e7ed55-1038-4507-af72-715a6856ecad d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c\">rainfall type</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c\">, </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 13\" data-uid=\"d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c dc488001-047f-495e-b956-55fd53793cdf\">ranging from</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8\" data-uid=\"3392d096-9665-4038-aeb4-524f50c8953a d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c\">drizzle</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c\"> to </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8\" data-uid=\"d4cf506f-857f-44d4-bc28-7fc24d77a462 d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c\">thunderstorms</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. By using the sound of rain underwater as a ‘natural’ rain gauge, the measurement of rainfall over the oceans will become available to climatologists. In this way, modern society continues to benefit from the investigations of those who, like Leonardo da Vinci, pursued the answers to some basic questions of nature.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 1– 8 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322542\" id=\"question-wrapper-322542\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"829075e4-e700-4d24-8b1d-7c29aff227ed\">In the past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"0f896025-e479-46e6-b95e-09dc7ff5701e\">easier<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> for scientists to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d3daebb8-a38a-48b4-a388-ba637e74a883\">study the Moon than the oceans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322543\" id=\"question-wrapper-322543\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Techniques for investigating the Moon are the same as techniques for researching the ocean.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322544\" id=\"question-wrapper-322544\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"48aa17c1-93f7-4c0c-a74e-03723b5008c9\">Direct observation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of blue whales has enabled scientists to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"104f3a27-6e42-479b-ab94-11758fc95766\">follow their movements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> over <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"dcec3d9e-8179-40f9-956e-296877bd89ef\">considerable distances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322545\" id=\"question-wrapper-322545\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c9bfd8d5-d9bb-42c4-b3e0-ca172f944bba\">vocal signals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> produced by finback whales <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9f7c6edb-5517-43a4-b054-f44567132c2a\">remain consistent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"3e0070d4-c425-44c2-861c-a94332652790\">throughout the year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322546\" id=\"question-wrapper-322546\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The use of SOSUS meant that researchers could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"062b0572-2ba0-43dc-ab8b-e6a79cd42cbe\">follow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c44c7353-a820-400f-91f5-a31aa0ee37ba\">only one </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c44c7353-a820-400f-91f5-a31aa0ee37ba fef50728-7298-4b28-87db-d08a72190737\">marine mammal</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c44c7353-a820-400f-91f5-a31aa0ee37ba\"> on each occasion</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322547\" id=\"question-wrapper-322547\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"caecfa89-d01f-4bc9-8f4d-2a76cc099d80\">Measuring temperature changes in the ocean using sound<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> is more time-consuming than other methods. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322548\" id=\"question-wrapper-322548\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Hydrophones can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"45e7ed55-1038-4507-af72-715a6856ecad\">distinguish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c\">different kinds of rain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322549\" id=\"question-wrapper-322549\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"9a2702f1-a497-4bb2-acfa-48c43a7deed5\">Data collected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> by Nystuen were more dependable during <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"d4cf506f-857f-44d4-bc28-7fc24d77a462\">severe storms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> than during <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"3392d096-9665-4038-aeb4-524f50c8953a\">light precipitation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the table below.</span></p><p><span>Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer.</span></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>Researcher or organisation</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>Year</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>Development in underwater sound research</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Leonardo da Vinci</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>1490</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>He proposed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"49c946d9-c2a9-43c9-8038-38c8b60721e2\">detecting distant vessels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c63327ed-4984-4410-89f4-8c2d1ad7c066\">through a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)__________</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Colladon and Sturm</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>1826</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Their calculation relied on a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"190ca9ad-19ed-4da6-b149-4e22d09bd55d\">noise produced beneath the lake surface<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> by a (10)__________</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Maurice Ewing and J. L. Worzel</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>1943</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Their experiment identified the (11)__________, a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"13d63843-73b5-469e-ad44-993cf4ae5edf\">pathway<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"53daa186-7aba-45a7-ba5c-2b017064c4b8\">sound signals remained strong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> over long distances.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>The US Navy</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>—</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d6071d9c-959f-4992-a822-ad1c8a14c218\">seabed detection network<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> depended on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"1a0378ca-9011-4ea6-901f-1d2fb218f632\">instruments known as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12)__________</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Jeff Nystuen</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Since 1985</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>His recordings allowed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"d391242a-6c48-456c-b03e-4b23e07867a0\">precipitation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to be classified, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"dc488001-047f-495e-b956-55fd53793cdf\">conditions varying from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)__________.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322550\" id=\"question-wrapper-322550\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(long) tube</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322551\" id=\"question-wrapper-322551\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(submerged) bell</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322552\" id=\"question-wrapper-322552\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">deep sound channel</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322553\" id=\"question-wrapper-322553\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">hydrophones [OR] underwater microphones</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322554\" id=\"question-wrapper-322554\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">drizzle to thunderstorms</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"829075e4-e700-4d24-8b1d-7c29aff227ed","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"In the past","passagePhrase":"until quite recently"},{"uid":"d3daebb8-a38a-48b4-a388-ba637e74a883","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"study the Moon than the oceans","passagePhrase":"knew less about their depths than about the surface of the Moon"},{"uid":"0f896025-e479-46e6-b95e-09dc7ff5701e","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"easier","passagePhrase":"far more accessible"},{"uid":"c63327ed-4984-4410-89f4-8c2d1ad7c066","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"through a","passagePhrase":"place the head of a"},{"uid":"49c946d9-c2a9-43c9-8038-38c8b60721e2","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"detecting distant vessels","passagePhrase":"hear ships at a great distance"},{"uid":"190ca9ad-19ed-4da6-b149-4e22d09bd55d","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"noise produced beneath the lake surface","passagePhrase":"sound of a submerged bell"},{"uid":"13d63843-73b5-469e-ad44-993cf4ae5edf","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"pathway","passagePhrase":"pipeline ... channel"},{"uid":"53daa186-7aba-45a7-ba5c-2b017064c4b8","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"sound signals remained strong","passagePhrase":"travel thousands of kilometres with minimal loss of signal"},{"uid":"d6071d9c-959f-4992-a822-ad1c8a14c218","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"seabed detection network","passagePhrase":"Sound Surveillance System ... placed on the ocean bottom"},{"uid":"1a0378ca-9011-4ea6-901f-1d2fb218f632","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"instruments known as","passagePhrase":"underwater microphones, called hydrophones"},{"uid":"fef50728-7298-4b28-87db-d08a72190737","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"whale"},{"uid":"48aa17c1-93f7-4c0c-a74e-03723b5008c9","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Direct observation","passagePhrase":"wait in their ships for the whales to surface"},{"uid":"104f3a27-6e42-479b-ab94-11758fc95766","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"follow their movements","passagePhrase":"tracked"},{"uid":"062b0572-2ba0-43dc-ab8b-e6a79cd42cbe","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"follow","passagePhrase":"track"},{"uid":"c9bfd8d5-d9bb-42c4-b3e0-ca172f944bba","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"vocal signals","passagePhrase":"calls"},{"uid":"3e0070d4-c425-44c2-861c-a94332652790","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"throughout the year","passagePhrase":"as the seasons change"},{"uid":"caecfa89-d01f-4bc9-8f4d-2a76cc099d80","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Measuring temperature changes in the ocean using sound","passagePhrase":"track changes in temperature over months or years"},{"uid":"d391242a-6c48-456c-b03e-4b23e07867a0","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"precipitation","passagePhrase":"rainfall"},{"uid":"45e7ed55-1038-4507-af72-715a6856ecad 9a2702f1-a497-4bb2-acfa-48c43a7deed5","qNum":"7 8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"measuring"},{"uid":"45e7ed55-1038-4507-af72-715a6856ecad","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"distinguish","passagePhrase":"not only the rainfall rate but also the"},{"uid":"45e7ed55-1038-4507-af72-715a6856ecad d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"rainfall type"},{"uid":"d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"different kinds of rain","passagePhrase":", ... to"},{"uid":"d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c dc488001-047f-495e-b956-55fd53793cdf","qNum":"7 13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"ranging from"},{"uid":"3392d096-9665-4038-aeb4-524f50c8953a d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c","qNum":"7 8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"drizzle"},{"uid":"d4cf506f-857f-44d4-bc28-7fc24d77a462 d871d27e-285d-4dbc-bf69-eb52b3b8482c","qNum":"7 8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"thunderstorms"},{"uid":"c44c7353-a820-400f-91f5-a31aa0ee37ba fef50728-7298-4b28-87db-d08a72190737","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"marine mammal","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"9a2702f1-a497-4bb2-acfa-48c43a7deed5","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Data collected","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"d4cf506f-857f-44d4-bc28-7fc24d77a462","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"severe storms","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"3392d096-9665-4038-aeb4-524f50c8953a","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"light precipitation","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"dc488001-047f-495e-b956-55fd53793cdf","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"conditions varying from","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_38":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14–26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Roller coaster: the great fairground attraction</span></b></p><p><b><span>How they move</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>Like a passenger train, a roller coaster consists of a series of connected cars that move on a track. Unlike a passenger train, however, it has no engine or independent power source. For most of the ride, movement depends entirely on the forces of inertia and gravity. The only significant exertion of energy occurs at the beginning, when the train is pulled to the top of the lift hill. The traditional <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"2f636863-2f60-4192-a880-988c7bf83657\">lifting mechanism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, which has remained largely unchanged for over a century, consists of a chain running beneath the track and fastened in a loop around a gear at both the top and bottom of the hill. Driven by a motor, the chain moves continually, functioning much like an extended conveyor belt. The coaster cars grip this chain, which transports them to the summit, where they are released <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"94942341-587b-4a42-bc76-309429604f75\">to commence their descent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. On large modern coasters, the lifting chain may extend for more than 300 metres — a deceptively simple solution to a substantial engineering challenge.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> The purpose of the initial ascent is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"98664cd8-e45e-47cc-b667-53ac7b38a5b3\">build a reservoir of potential energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. As the train climbs higher, the distance through which gravity can subsequently pull it downward increases proportionally. Once the train begins descending, this stored potential energy is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"d84c5222-134d-4020-95f1-a312331967f8\">converted into kinetic energy, causing the train to accelerate rapidly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. At the bottom of the hill, kinetic energy reaches its maximum and propels the train upward once more, where it is gradually reconverted into potential energy. Throughout the ride, energy is continually exchanged between these two forms. It is precisely this fluctuation in acceleration — the abrupt shifts from increasing to decreasing speed — that creates the sensations riders find so compelling. Although modern coasters commonly reach heights of 30 to 60 metres and may exceed speeds of 100 kilometres per hour, the underlying principle remains unchanged: gravity and inertia drive the entire experience.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>The historical development of the roller coaster can be traced through several distinct phases of innovation. Its direct ancestors were the ice slides that became popular in Russia during the 16th and 17th centuries. These structures consisted of long wooden ramps <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"12f1fa92-b602-4c3d-8b12-6ad910ff0fb8\">covered with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> ice, often erected in town squares as winter amusements. Riders climbed stairs to platforms as high as 21 metres before descending in sleds made from wood or blocks of ice, some of which stretched for more than 150 metres. At the bottom, the sleds would crash into sand piles that brought them to a halt. Although structurally rudimentary, these attractions established the essential principle behind the roller coaster: harnessing gravity to generate excitement through speed and controlled descent.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>The concept was subsequently imported into France, where it underwent significant modification. Because the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1a581b97-4d24-4cce-b5ca-dea501c4e164\">warmer climate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c1d48eaa-e9bc-4fc3-9615-ad13a0c53421\">melted the ice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> for much of the year, French designers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"8ec95666-33fa-49ce-82e8-20c3a81c76d5\">replaced it with waxed surfaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. To <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"45ba24cc-ae0e-4282-8feb-ddfe495e6c7b\">reduce friction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> further and improve overall movement, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"8870a1ba-34a2-42ac-9503-a6c457ec2631\">added<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> wheels, and in 1817 a train was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"1637d60b-9fa7-4a6f-8514-a835195ca541\">attached to the track for the first time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> — an innovation that would prove fundamental to all subsequent designs. Engineers continued to experiment with increasingly complex track layouts featuring multiple cars and numerous twists and turns.</span></p><p><span>The first American roller coaster, constructed in Pennsylvania in 1873, was conceived <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"df55285d-859b-4355-bdb5-8d6801b4bbbf\">not for entertainment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> but for a strictly industrial purpose: it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"cd7df5d8-15d2-42b2-9ad0-f5cb77107ec0\">originally built<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"74c3945d-e477-4c7b-9894-b13697097da2\">transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> coal 29 kilometres down a mountainside to the railway below. After unloading, a crew would attach the carts to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"deaa2d2b-39f3-4373-b679-52efa88aaf48\">teams of mules<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, which dragged them back to the top. These animals were eventually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"05f2d397-218b-4010-bdc8-0754ca52f9d5\">replaced by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> steam engines, significantly improving operational efficiency.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Soon after these improvements, a new railway tunnel brought freight trains much closer to the mine, rendering the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ee004157-e81f-47d2-a61f-02825ac5a436\">original route<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> unnecessary. Rather than abandoning it, the company <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2e17c5e0-94ae-46a6-ae87-8f12d6c10f97\">configured the track as a scenic attraction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. For one dollar, tourists could enjoy a leisurely trip to the summit followed by a thrilling descent — a transformation that anticipated the modern theme-park economy by more than a century. The venture proved highly successful and attracted more than 10,000 visitors annually.</span></p><p><span>Scenic rides continued to flourish and were soon joined by wooden roller coasters resembling those seen today. Many became major attractions in amusement parks, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e3728808-d287-4da4-9373-92fd7147beeb\">particularly those at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> Coney Island in New York. By 1926, the roller-coaster industry had reached its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"736b73a8-44a2-466f-b286-c3a42e45ad27\">peak of national popularity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, with approximately 2,000 rides operating across the United States.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>The Great Depression precipitated a sharp decline in roller-coaster construction during the early 1930s, and the industry would not recover its earlier momentum for several decades. However, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"98fdd01f-46d4-4725-ad55-9cd1a1e103b9\">amusement sector<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"52b923e1-bd8c-4a6f-a90b-269dcc7a74ff\">experienced a substantial revival<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> during the 1970s and early 1980s. This period <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"52b923e1-bd8c-4a6f-a90b-269dcc7a74ff\">invigorated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> the field and introduced a series of <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"52b923e1-bd8c-4a6f-a90b-269dcc7a74ff\">significant </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 24\" data-uid=\"52b923e1-bd8c-4a6f-a90b-269dcc7a74ff e2d0382a-4b4b-423c-9faa-e1acc66fad93\">innovations</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, most notably <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"c02deada-fa6d-47e5-8e89-765e8beedbaa\">tubular steel coasters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, which permitted track configurations that had been impossible to construct in wood. By 1980, more than 250 major roller coasters were operating across the United States.</span></p><p><span>Although public interest weakened later in the decade, a second wave of expansion began in the early 1990s. New launching systems and other technological advances dramatically broadened design possibilities. Some rides exceeded 90 metres in height, while others were engineered to simulate the sensation of flight. Contemporary coasters can travel at speeds in excess of 200 kilometres per hour, and more than 5,000 are now in operation worldwide.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 14–18.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322555\" id=\"question-wrapper-322555\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ee004157-e81f-47d2-a61f-02825ac5a436\">former transport corridor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2e17c5e0-94ae-46a6-ae87-8f12d6c10f97\">converted into a recreational trail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322556\" id=\"question-wrapper-322556\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an explanation of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"98664cd8-e45e-47cc-b667-53ac7b38a5b3\">retained force<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"d84c5222-134d-4020-95f1-a312331967f8\">transformed into rapid motion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322557\" id=\"question-wrapper-322557\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a phase characterised by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"52b923e1-bd8c-4a6f-a90b-269dcc7a74ff\">major progress<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"98fdd01f-46d4-4725-ad55-9cd1a1e103b9\">amusement rides<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322558\" id=\"question-wrapper-322558\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"8ec95666-33fa-49ce-82e8-20c3a81c76d5\">an adjustment made<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1a581b97-4d24-4cce-b5ca-dea501c4e164\">local weather patterns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c1d48eaa-e9bc-4fc3-9615-ad13a0c53421\">made the original model impractical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322559\" id=\"question-wrapper-322559\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"2f636863-2f60-4192-a880-988c7bf83657\">system used to elevate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the ride <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"94942341-587b-4a42-bc76-309429604f75\">before descent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 19–23 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The development of roller coasters</span></b></p><p><span>Modern roller coasters can be traced back to Russian installations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"12f1fa92-b602-4c3d-8b12-6ad910ff0fb8\">surfaced with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> (19)______. After the concept was introduced to France, it was adapted, and (20)______ were later <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"8870a1ba-34a2-42ac-9503-a6c457ec2631\">fitted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"45ba24cc-ae0e-4282-8feb-ddfe495e6c7b\">reduce resistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. In America, an early version <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"cd7df5d8-15d2-42b2-9ad0-f5cb77107ec0\">served the practical purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"74c3945d-e477-4c7b-9894-b13697097da2\">carrying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> (21)______, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"df55285d-859b-4355-bdb5-8d6801b4bbbf\">not amusement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. The loaded carts initially had to be taken back up by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"deaa2d2b-39f3-4373-b679-52efa88aaf48\">animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, until this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"05f2d397-218b-4010-bdc8-0754ca52f9d5\">labour was later performed by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> (22)______. Over time, such rides became widely enjoyed at leisure venues, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e3728808-d287-4da4-9373-92fd7147beeb\">especially those at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> (23)______.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322560\" id=\"question-wrapper-322560\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ice</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322561\" id=\"question-wrapper-322561\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">wheels</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322562\" id=\"question-wrapper-322562\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">coal</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322563\" id=\"question-wrapper-322563\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">steam engines</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322564\" id=\"question-wrapper-322564\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Coney Island</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Match each development with the correct period.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–E, in boxes 24–26.</span></p><p><b><span>Periods</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Russian ice-slide era</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. French adaptation period</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Early American industrial use</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. 1920s </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Revival from the 1970s onwards</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322565\" id=\"question-wrapper-322565\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e2d0382a-4b4b-423c-9faa-e1acc66fad93\">adoption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"c02deada-fa6d-47e5-8e89-765e8beedbaa\">new structural approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322566\" id=\"question-wrapper-322566\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"1637d60b-9fa7-4a6f-8514-a835195ca541\">earliest use of guided vehicles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322567\" id=\"question-wrapper-322567\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"736b73a8-44a2-466f-b286-c3a42e45ad27\">national high in operational numbers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"2f636863-2f60-4192-a880-988c7bf83657","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"system used to elevate","passagePhrase":"lifting mechanism"},{"uid":"94942341-587b-4a42-bc76-309429604f75","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"before descent","passagePhrase":"to commence their descent"},{"uid":"98664cd8-e45e-47cc-b667-53ac7b38a5b3","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"retained force","passagePhrase":"build a reservoir of potential energy"},{"uid":"d84c5222-134d-4020-95f1-a312331967f8","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"transformed into rapid motion","passagePhrase":"converted into kinetic energy, causing the train to accelerate rapidly"},{"uid":"12f1fa92-b602-4c3d-8b12-6ad910ff0fb8","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"surfaced with","passagePhrase":"covered with"},{"uid":"1a581b97-4d24-4cce-b5ca-dea501c4e164","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"local weather patterns","passagePhrase":"warmer climate"},{"uid":"c1d48eaa-e9bc-4fc3-9615-ad13a0c53421","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"made the original model impractical","passagePhrase":"melted the ice"},{"uid":"8ec95666-33fa-49ce-82e8-20c3a81c76d5","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"an adjustment made","passagePhrase":"replaced it with waxed surfaces"},{"uid":"45ba24cc-ae0e-4282-8feb-ddfe495e6c7b","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"reduce resistance","passagePhrase":"reduce friction"},{"uid":"8870a1ba-34a2-42ac-9503-a6c457ec2631","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"fitted","passagePhrase":"added"},{"uid":"1637d60b-9fa7-4a6f-8514-a835195ca541","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"earliest use of guided vehicles","passagePhrase":"attached to the track for the first time"},{"uid":"df55285d-859b-4355-bdb5-8d6801b4bbbf","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"not amusement","passagePhrase":"not for entertainment"},{"uid":"cd7df5d8-15d2-42b2-9ad0-f5cb77107ec0","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"served the practical purpose","passagePhrase":"originally built"},{"uid":"74c3945d-e477-4c7b-9894-b13697097da2","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"carrying","passagePhrase":"transport"},{"uid":"deaa2d2b-39f3-4373-b679-52efa88aaf48","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"animals","passagePhrase":"teams of mules"},{"uid":"05f2d397-218b-4010-bdc8-0754ca52f9d5","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"labour was later performed by","passagePhrase":"replaced by"},{"uid":"ee004157-e81f-47d2-a61f-02825ac5a436","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"former transport corridor","passagePhrase":"original route"},{"uid":"2e17c5e0-94ae-46a6-ae87-8f12d6c10f97","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"converted into a recreational trail","passagePhrase":"configured the track as a scenic attraction"},{"uid":"e3728808-d287-4da4-9373-92fd7147beeb","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"especially those at","passagePhrase":"particularly those at"},{"uid":"736b73a8-44a2-466f-b286-c3a42e45ad27","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"national high in operational numbers","passagePhrase":"peak of national popularity"},{"uid":"98fdd01f-46d4-4725-ad55-9cd1a1e103b9","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"amusement rides","passagePhrase":"amusement sector"},{"uid":"52b923e1-bd8c-4a6f-a90b-269dcc7a74ff","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"major progress","passagePhrase":"experienced a substantial revival ... invigorated ... significant"},{"uid":"52b923e1-bd8c-4a6f-a90b-269dcc7a74ff e2d0382a-4b4b-423c-9faa-e1acc66fad93","qNum":"16 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"innovations"},{"uid":"c02deada-fa6d-47e5-8e89-765e8beedbaa","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"new structural approach","passagePhrase":"tubular steel coasters"},{"uid":"e2d0382a-4b4b-423c-9faa-e1acc66fad93","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"adoption","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_39":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>How should reading be taught?</span></b></p><p><i><span>By Keith Rayner and Barbara R. Foorman</span></i></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> Learning to speak is automatic for nearly every child, developing quite naturally as they grow up surrounded by the spoken language of those around them. Becoming a reader, however, is a markedly different matter; it requires elaborate instruction and conscious effort on the part of the learner, and it does not simply happen of its own accord. The contrast between the ease of acquiring speech and the difficulty of acquiring reading has long preoccupied those responsible for the education of the young.</span></p><p><span>Well aware of these difficulties, educators have devoted a great deal of thought to identifying the most effective ways of helping children acquire reading skills, and a range of teaching methods have emerged over the years as a result. Despite these sustained efforts, however, no single approach has triumphed over the rest. In fact, heated arguments concerning the most appropriate form of reading instruction continue to polarise those within the teaching profession, with various groups holding firm to their preferred methods.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"27\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"b70638a4-a548-4a9a-a4c8-8e5e36cf7a43\">Three general approaches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> have been tried. In one, called whole-word instruction, children learn by rote how to recognise at a glance a vocabulary of 50 to 100 words. Then they gradually acquire other words, often through seeing them used over and over again in the context of a story.</span></p><p><span>Speakers of most languages learn the relationship between letters and the sounds associated with them phonemes. That is, children are taught how to use their knowledge of the alphabet to sound out words. This procedure constitutes a second approach to teaching reading – phonics.</span></p><p><span>Many schools have adopted a different approach: the whole-language method. The strategy here relies on the child's experience with language. For example, students are offered engaging books and are encouraged to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e935a250-0756-484c-8fdd-782892b178fc\">guess the words that they do not know by considering the context of the sentence or by looking for clues in the storyline and illustrations, rather than trying to sound them out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"53b949b7-9ee6-433b-88ac-4f8541276ace\">Many teachers adopted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> the whole-language approach because of its intuitive appeal. Making reading fun promises to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"aedd6519-d8e9-4dd8-8fb2-ac5cc242ec29\">keep children motivated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, and learning to read depends more on what the student does than on what the teacher does. The presumed benefits of whole-language instruction – and the contrast to the perceived dullness of phonics – led to its growing acceptance across America during the 1990s, and a movement away from phonics.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"28\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span>However, many linguists and psychologists objected strongly to the abandonment of phonics in American schools. Why was this so? In short, because research had clearly demonstrated that understanding how letters relate to the component sounds in words is critically important in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"27b4bc55-0595-4c87-91fc-9d2d706117af\">reading<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. This conclusion rests, in part, on knowledge of how experienced readers make sense of words on a page. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7a3d89d7-b65a-4375-9ab0-78616645f736\">Advocates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of whole-language instruction have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7a3d89d7-b65a-4375-9ab0-78616645f736\">argue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>d forcefully that people often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"27b4bc55-0595-4c87-91fc-9d2d706117af\">derive meanings directly from print<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> without ever determining the sound of the word. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7a3d89d7-b65a-4375-9ab0-78616645f736\">Some<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> psychologists today <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7a3d89d7-b65a-4375-9ab0-78616645f736\">accept<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> this view, but most believe that reading is typically a process of rapidly sounding out words mentally. Compelling evidence for this comes from experiments which show that subjects often confuse <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"9e92f596-3c5a-4b32-86e4-ebe84dadbdcb\">homophones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. This supports the idea that readers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"835579b2-f2c2-4945-bb93-cea33c1ff7c0\">convert strings of letters to sounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"29\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span>In order to evaluate different approaches to teaching reading, a number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"30dd74bd-b056-4c01-a5de-174958d6cc64\">experiments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> have been carried out, firstly with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"30dd74bd-b056-4c01-a5de-174958d6cc64\">college students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, then with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"30dd74bd-b056-4c01-a5de-174958d6cc64\">school pupils<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Investigators trained English-speaking college students to read using unfamiliar symbols such as Arabic letters the phonics approach, while another group learned entire words associated with certain strings of Arabic letters whole-word. Then both groups were required to read a new set of words constructed from the original characters. In general, readers who were taught the rules of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"62ca6064-68a2-47f5-8c05-8bb6ebc33691\">phonics could read many more new words<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> than those trained with a whole-word procedure.</span></p><p><span>Classroom studies comparing phonics with either whole-word or whole-language instruction are also quite illuminating. One particularly persuasive study compared two programmes used in 20 first-grade classrooms. Half the students were offered traditional reading instruction, which included the use of phonics drills and applications. The other half were taught using an individualised method that drew from their experiences with language; these children produced their own booklets of stories and developed sets of words to be recognised as common components of the whole-language approach. This study found that the first group <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"62ca6064-68a2-47f5-8c05-8bb6ebc33691\">scored higher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> at year's end on tests of reading and comprehension.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"30\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> If researchers are so convinced about the need for phonics instruction, why does the debate continue? The answer is that the controversy is enmeshed in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5345702f-3018-4564-a421-72867f9e7b00\">philosophical differences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> between traditional and progressive approaches, differences that have divided educators for many years. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5345702f-3018-4564-a421-72867f9e7b00\">disagreement lies deep<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> within educational thinking and extends well beyond the specific question of how reading is best taught, which helps explain why the dispute has proved so persistent in spite of the accumulating research evidence.</span></p><p><span>The progressives <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5343e933-9f59-4f7a-bd9b-da2b558d3c47\">challenge the results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> of laboratory tests and classroom studies on the basis of a broad philosophical <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5343e933-9f59-4f7a-bd9b-da2b558d3c47\">scepticism about the value of such research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Rather than placing their trust in such evidence, they champion student-centred learning and teacher empowerment as their guiding educational principles. Sadly, however, they fail to realise that these very admirable educational values are equally <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"d44f2c1d-33ad-4102-9bc4-a5dce8a189b2\">consistent with the teaching of phonics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, and that the two <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"d44f2c1d-33ad-4102-9bc4-a5dce8a189b2\">need not be viewed as opposing positions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"31\"><b><span>F.</span></b><span> If schools of education insisted that would-be reading teachers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"d16678ed-cc4c-4ad7-9347-279ebea1abdb\">learned something about the vast research in linguistics and psychology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> that bears on reading, their graduates would be more eager to use phonics and would be prepared to do so effectively. They could allow their pupils to apply the principles of phonics while reading for pleasure. Using whole-language activities to supplement phonics instruction certainly helps to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"0f2548be-15ab-4126-99a6-525555a9e51f\">make reading fun and meaningful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> for children, so no one would want to see such tools discarded. Indeed, recent work has indicated that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"90fae873-a26b-4cdd-bdf7-0bca9820f996\">combination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of literature-based instruction and phonics is more powerful than either method used alone.</span></p><p><span>Teachers need to strike a balance. But in doing so, we urge them to remember that reading must be grounded in a firm understanding of the connections between letters and sounds. Educators who deny this reality are neglecting decades of research. They are also neglecting the needs of their students.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has six sections, A-F. Choose the correct heading for sections B-F from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7a3d89d7-b65a-4375-9ab0-78616645f736\">Disagreement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> about the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"27b4bc55-0595-4c87-91fc-9d2d706117af\">reading process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5345702f-3018-4564-a421-72867f9e7b00\">The roots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of the debate</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"90fae873-a26b-4cdd-bdf7-0bca9820f996\">A combined approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"b70638a4-a548-4a9a-a4c8-8e5e36cf7a43\">Methods of teaching reading<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. A controversial approach</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. Inconclusive research</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"30dd74bd-b056-4c01-a5de-174958d6cc64\">Research with learners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. Allowing teachers more control</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. A debate amongst educators</span></p><p><b><span>Example</span></b></p><p><span>Section A ix</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322568\" id=\"question-wrapper-322568\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322569\" id=\"question-wrapper-322569\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322570\" id=\"question-wrapper-322570\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322571\" id=\"question-wrapper-322571\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322572\" id=\"question-wrapper-322572\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322573\" id=\"question-wrapper-322573\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The whole-language approach <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e935a250-0756-484c-8fdd-782892b178fc\">relates letters to sounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322574\" id=\"question-wrapper-322574\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"53b949b7-9ee6-433b-88ac-4f8541276ace\">Many educators favoured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> the whole-language approach because it could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"aedd6519-d8e9-4dd8-8fb2-ac5cc242ec29\">help learners remain interested<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322575\" id=\"question-wrapper-322575\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Experiments involving <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"9e92f596-3c5a-4b32-86e4-ebe84dadbdcb\">similar-sounding words<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> suggest that people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"835579b2-f2c2-4945-bb93-cea33c1ff7c0\">mentally hear what they read<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322576\" id=\"question-wrapper-322576\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Research has shown that the whole-word approach is less effective than the whole-language approach.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322577\" id=\"question-wrapper-322577\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Research has shown that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"62ca6064-68a2-47f5-8c05-8bb6ebc33691\">phonics is more successful than both<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> the whole-word and whole-language approaches.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary of sections E and F using the list of words, A-G, below. Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. the phonics method</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. the whole-word method</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. the whole-language method</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. traditionalists</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. progressives</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. linguistics</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. research studies</span></p><p><span>In the teaching community, (37)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5343e933-9f59-4f7a-bd9b-da2b558d3c47\">question the usefulness of research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> into methods of teaching reading. These critics <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"d44f2c1d-33ad-4102-9bc4-a5dce8a189b2\">believe that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> (38)______ <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"d44f2c1d-33ad-4102-9bc4-a5dce8a189b2\">is incompatible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> with student-centred learning. In the future, teachers need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"d16678ed-cc4c-4ad7-9347-279ebea1abdb\">be aware of studies in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> (39)______ so that they understand the importance of phonics. They should not, however, ignore the ideas of (40)______ which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"0f2548be-15ab-4126-99a6-525555a9e51f\">make reading enjoyable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> for learners.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322578\" id=\"question-wrapper-322578\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322579\" id=\"question-wrapper-322579\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322580\" id=\"question-wrapper-322580\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322581\" id=\"question-wrapper-322581\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b70638a4-a548-4a9a-a4c8-8e5e36cf7a43","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Methods of teaching reading","passagePhrase":"Three general approaches"},{"uid":"53b949b7-9ee6-433b-88ac-4f8541276ace","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Many educators favoured","passagePhrase":"Many teachers adopted"},{"uid":"aedd6519-d8e9-4dd8-8fb2-ac5cc242ec29","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"help learners remain interested","passagePhrase":"keep children motivated"},{"uid":"27b4bc55-0595-4c87-91fc-9d2d706117af","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"reading process","passagePhrase":"reading ... derive meanings directly from print"},{"uid":"7a3d89d7-b65a-4375-9ab0-78616645f736","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Disagreement","passagePhrase":"Advocates ... argue ... Some ... accept"},{"uid":"9e92f596-3c5a-4b32-86e4-ebe84dadbdcb","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"similar-sounding words","passagePhrase":"homophones"},{"uid":"835579b2-f2c2-4945-bb93-cea33c1ff7c0","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"mentally hear what they read","passagePhrase":"convert strings of letters to sounds"},{"uid":"30dd74bd-b056-4c01-a5de-174958d6cc64","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Research with learners","passagePhrase":"experiments ... college students ... school pupils"},{"uid":"62ca6064-68a2-47f5-8c05-8bb6ebc33691","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"phonics is more successful than both","passagePhrase":"phonics could read many more new words ... scored higher"},{"uid":"5345702f-3018-4564-a421-72867f9e7b00","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"The roots","passagePhrase":"philosophical differences ... disagreement lies deep"},{"uid":"5343e933-9f59-4f7a-bd9b-da2b558d3c47","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"question the usefulness of research","passagePhrase":"challenge the results ... scepticism about the value of such research"},{"uid":"d16678ed-cc4c-4ad7-9347-279ebea1abdb","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"be aware of studies in","passagePhrase":"learned something about the vast research in linguistics and psychology"},{"uid":"0f2548be-15ab-4126-99a6-525555a9e51f","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"make reading enjoyable","passagePhrase":"make reading fun and meaningful"},{"uid":"90fae873-a26b-4cdd-bdf7-0bca9820f996","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"A combined approach","passagePhrase":"combination"}]},"reading_u2_40":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1–13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Importance of Business Cards</span></b></p><p><i><span>The exchange of business cards is as close to a universal ritual as you can find in the business world.</span></i></p><p><span>The ritual may be universal, but the details of business cards and how they are swapped vary across countries. Americans throw their cards casually across a table; the Japanese make the exchange of cards a formal ceremony. While there are cards that are discreet and understated, others are crammed full of details and titles. Some businesspeople hand out 24-carat gold cards, and there are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"e37e8953-83fb-4fc8-bfab-d55269d38ff2\">kindergarten children who have cards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> with not only their own contact details, but also with the job descriptions of their parents and even grandparents. This practice has become so common <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"68e6e2c9-80fc-4a93-9b4d-69e993166c3a\">in parts of New York<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, for example, that the use of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"e37e8953-83fb-4fc8-bfab-d55269d38ff2\">such cards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> is now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"c7e134e0-2b4b-426f-b928-285a3c07ef61\">prohibited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"68e6e2c9-80fc-4a93-9b4d-69e993166c3a\">by some kindergartens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Cards have been around a long time in one form or another. The Chinese invented calling cards in the 15th century to give people notice that they intended to pay them a visit, but these were for social purposes only. Then, in the 17th century, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"e9103e4d-3344-4964-8de9-4f57cc1d0510\">European businesspeople<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> invented a new type of card to act as miniature advertisements, signalling the advent of the business card. In today’s world, business cards can cause people to have strong emotional reactions. According to one experienced company director, very few things can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"bb0cc15f-8555-4abe-a626-30b0d40dd4c4\">provoke more heated discussion at a board meeting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> than the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"2e0259e5-624f-4e3a-abf3-52414d283c9f\">composition of the company’s business cards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Lots of companies try to promote themselves by altering the form of the card. Employees at one famous toy company give out little plastic figures with their contact details stamped on them. One fast-food company has business cards which are shaped like a portion of French fries. A Canadian divorce lawyer once gave out cards that could be torn in two – one half for each of the spouses. For many business <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"122f9ebe-dde6-4e84-a0cf-d8ab46118702\">commentators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, such gimmicky business cards prove that the use of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"1375015b-82c8-48f8-95a3-205ed78f0908\">physical business card is nearly at an end<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. After all, why bother exchanging bits of thick paper at all when you can simply swap electronic versions by smartphone?</span></p><p><span>However, one can just as well argue the opposite: that business cards are here to stay, and, in a business world full of meetings and correspondence, it is more important than ever that your card is unique. Attempts to reinvent business cards for the digital age have not been successful. Digital options may include QR codes that open an online profile or smartphone apps that transfer contact details instantly between devices, without requiring a printed card. Yet even at the latest technology conferences, people still greet each other by handing out little rectangles made from paper rather than using a digital alternative.</span></p><p><span>To understand business cards, it is necessary to understand how business works. That business cards are thriving in a digital age is a forceful reminder that there is much about business that is timeless. According to Kate Jones, a business lecturer, there is one eternal and inescapable issue. Her 2006 study of more than 200 business executives in North America found that trust was the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"a772f90d-0db5-435f-b835-03202c2727ec\">key element<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> for running a successful business. It is vital to look someone in the eye and decide what sort of person they are. Such personal contact can transform acquaintanceships into relationships over the longer term.</span></p><p><span>A good proportion of business life will always involve building social connections, such as having dinner or playing sports with clients and colleagues. While <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"88075218-5b30-4ccc-b37f-f27152de67f8\">computers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"75b6ae90-559b-40df-b80d-3f28ba5ef8f5\">can deal with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> administrative tasks, human beings must manage the emotional side. The advance of globalization makes this harder: managers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"cd2331d4-3504-42dd-b0c4-70eb96eb5813\">put more effort<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"2731a4bd-c820-426b-8d15-ffa574c17060\">dealings with international counterparts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, especially when they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"ea18870b-3996-48a4-b515-ce2cd49ca7f9\">do not share<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> a language. A UK survey found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"2aee9629-da69-4bad-bc8a-004ee184978f\">global chief executives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b3e5d891-5188-48d6-a47b-7f3916036419\">routinely spend three out of every four weeks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"a7e5ecce-a100-4c86-9716-c7447677f2da\">international<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> travel. In these situations, cards quickly establish connections and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"49200d44-5f64-411f-8f1a-efa645f48b0b\">strengthen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> memory of face-to-face meetings in a way that uniform electronic lists cannot.</span></p><p><span>Janet McIntyre, a leading expert on business cards today, maintains that as companies become more complex, cards are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"721e413b-361b-4bb9-9c2f-f1e8ec96241b\">essential in showing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the exact status of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"7bda4271-5fcf-4ffd-a2ee-d3230d129035\">contacts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"4f216a4d-364b-4750-a287-837176ea02aa\">multinational corporations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Exchanging them is also an effective way of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"03804462-fb60-4930-818f-9044e77e1f83\">initiating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> a conversation, since it provides a ritual <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"01cedffa-8f6d-4af7-b8d6-873b1c360350\">when people first meet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. The business world is obsessed with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"85cd8794-4313-4cf7-8347-325664ff59b8\">creating and inventing new things<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> that will change how we work, and such innovation does lead to progress. Nevertheless, Janet argues that some practices do not need to be changed, and that tradition has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"79a96b3c-c838-4386-84db-dac9ed088d26\">an equally valuable role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. The exchange of business cards is therefore likely to continue.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1–5 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322582\" id=\"question-wrapper-322582\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"e37e8953-83fb-4fc8-bfab-d55269d38ff2\">Children’s business cards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"c7e134e0-2b4b-426f-b928-285a3c07ef61\">banned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"68e6e2c9-80fc-4a93-9b4d-69e993166c3a\">in some places<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322583\" id=\"question-wrapper-322583\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"e9103e4d-3344-4964-8de9-4f57cc1d0510\">the Chinese who first began the practice of using business cards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322584\" id=\"question-wrapper-322584\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"2e0259e5-624f-4e3a-abf3-52414d283c9f\">Designing business cards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> can be a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"bb0cc15f-8555-4abe-a626-30b0d40dd4c4\">controversial process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> for some companies.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322585\" id=\"question-wrapper-322585\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A famous toy company has boosted its sales by using one type of unusual business card.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322586\" id=\"question-wrapper-322586\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"122f9ebe-dde6-4e84-a0cf-d8ab46118702\">observers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"1375015b-82c8-48f8-95a3-205ed78f0908\">predict that printed cards are becoming obsolete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>How business works</span></b></p><p><b><span>Kate Jones’s research</span></b></p><p><span>• The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"a772f90d-0db5-435f-b835-03202c2727ec\">most important aspect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of business is having (6)______ in others.</span></p><p><b><span>The human side of business</span></b></p><p><span>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"88075218-5b30-4ccc-b37f-f27152de67f8\">Machines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"75b6ae90-559b-40df-b80d-3f28ba5ef8f5\">only suitable for handling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> (7)______ tasks. </span></p><p><b><span>Business and globalisation</span></b></p><p><span>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"cd2331d4-3504-42dd-b0c4-70eb96eb5813\">Additional work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> may be required when managers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"2731a4bd-c820-426b-8d15-ffa574c17060\">communicate with overseas associates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"ea18870b-3996-48a4-b515-ce2cd49ca7f9\">without a common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)______.</span></p><p><span>• A UK survey indicates that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"a7e5ecce-a100-4c86-9716-c7447677f2da\">overseas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b3e5d891-5188-48d6-a47b-7f3916036419\">takes up the largest part of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"2aee9629-da69-4bad-bc8a-004ee184978f\">business leaders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b3e5d891-5188-48d6-a47b-7f3916036419\">time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>• A business person’s (10)______ of a meeting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"49200d44-5f64-411f-8f1a-efa645f48b0b\">can be improved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> by looking at business cards.</span></p><p><b><span>Janet McIntyre</span></b></p><p><span>• Within <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"4f216a4d-364b-4750-a287-837176ea02aa\">multinational firms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, these items <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"721e413b-361b-4bb9-9c2f-f1e8ec96241b\">help clarify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"7bda4271-5fcf-4ffd-a2ee-d3230d129035\">associate’s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)______.</span></p><p><span>• This ritual helps <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"01cedffa-8f6d-4af7-b8d6-873b1c360350\">unfamiliar professionals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"03804462-fb60-4930-818f-9044e77e1f83\">begin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> a (12)______.</span></p><p><span>• Janet feels that in the business world, (13)______ is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"79a96b3c-c838-4386-84db-dac9ed088d26\">just as important as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"85cd8794-4313-4cf7-8347-325664ff59b8\">innovation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322587\" id=\"question-wrapper-322587\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">trust</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322588\" id=\"question-wrapper-322588\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">administrative</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322589\" id=\"question-wrapper-322589\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">language</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322590\" id=\"question-wrapper-322590\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">travel</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322591\" id=\"question-wrapper-322591\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">memory</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322592\" id=\"question-wrapper-322592\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">status</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322593\" id=\"question-wrapper-322593\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">conversation</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322594\" id=\"question-wrapper-322594\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">tradition</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e37e8953-83fb-4fc8-bfab-d55269d38ff2","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Children’s business cards","passagePhrase":"kindergarten children who have cards ... such cards"},{"uid":"68e6e2c9-80fc-4a93-9b4d-69e993166c3a","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"in some places","passagePhrase":"in parts of New York ... by some kindergartens"},{"uid":"c7e134e0-2b4b-426f-b928-285a3c07ef61","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"banned","passagePhrase":"prohibited"},{"uid":"bb0cc15f-8555-4abe-a626-30b0d40dd4c4","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"controversial process","passagePhrase":"provoke more heated discussion at a board meeting"},{"uid":"2e0259e5-624f-4e3a-abf3-52414d283c9f","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Designing business cards","passagePhrase":"composition of the company’s business cards"},{"uid":"122f9ebe-dde6-4e84-a0cf-d8ab46118702","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"observers","passagePhrase":"commentators"},{"uid":"1375015b-82c8-48f8-95a3-205ed78f0908","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"predict that printed cards are becoming obsolete","passagePhrase":"physical business card is nearly at an end"},{"uid":"a772f90d-0db5-435f-b835-03202c2727ec","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"most important aspect","passagePhrase":"key element"},{"uid":"88075218-5b30-4ccc-b37f-f27152de67f8","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Machines","passagePhrase":"computers"},{"uid":"75b6ae90-559b-40df-b80d-3f28ba5ef8f5","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"only suitable for handling","passagePhrase":"can deal with"},{"uid":"cd2331d4-3504-42dd-b0c4-70eb96eb5813","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Additional work","passagePhrase":"put more effort"},{"uid":"2731a4bd-c820-426b-8d15-ffa574c17060","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"communicate with overseas associates","passagePhrase":"dealings with international counterparts"},{"uid":"ea18870b-3996-48a4-b515-ce2cd49ca7f9","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"without a common","passagePhrase":"do not share"},{"uid":"2aee9629-da69-4bad-bc8a-004ee184978f","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"business leaders","passagePhrase":"global chief executives"},{"uid":"b3e5d891-5188-48d6-a47b-7f3916036419","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"takes up the largest part of ... time","passagePhrase":"routinely spend three out of every four weeks"},{"uid":"a7e5ecce-a100-4c86-9716-c7447677f2da","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"overseas","passagePhrase":"international"},{"uid":"49200d44-5f64-411f-8f1a-efa645f48b0b","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"can be improved","passagePhrase":"strengthen"},{"uid":"721e413b-361b-4bb9-9c2f-f1e8ec96241b","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"help clarify","passagePhrase":"essential in showing"},{"uid":"7bda4271-5fcf-4ffd-a2ee-d3230d129035","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"associate’s","passagePhrase":"contacts"},{"uid":"4f216a4d-364b-4750-a287-837176ea02aa","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"multinational firms","passagePhrase":"multinational corporations"},{"uid":"03804462-fb60-4930-818f-9044e77e1f83","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"begin","passagePhrase":"initiating"},{"uid":"01cedffa-8f6d-4af7-b8d6-873b1c360350","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"unfamiliar professionals","passagePhrase":"when people first meet"},{"uid":"85cd8794-4313-4cf7-8347-325664ff59b8","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"innovation","passagePhrase":"creating and inventing new things"},{"uid":"79a96b3c-c838-4386-84db-dac9ed088d26","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"just as important as","passagePhrase":"an equally valuable role"}]},"reading_u2_41":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14–26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Mammoth Kill</span></b></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> Mammoths were characterised by long and curved tusks and the northern species were covered by long hair. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"7cb7f5e5-3eac-4ac3-80eb-a99749c799a6\">belonged to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the Elephantidae family which also included the two classes of the current elephant species and their antecedents. Mammoths had a reputation for being huge, with the largest reaching four metres at the shoulder and weighing up to eight tonnes, while extraordinarily large males would reach more than twelve tonnes. In most cases, however, mammoth species only reached the size of current Asian elephants. A small set of tusks first appeared at about six months of age and was later replaced by a long-lasting set that grew at approximately one to six inches per year. Studies of the current elephant species indicated that mammoths most likely had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"d206b3ab-8451-41f4-9469-a4ff2742cb02\">twenty-two months<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of gestation before culminating in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"8ed559dd-767a-496f-90d6-bfc379681dfe\">birth of one calf<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. They almost certainly had social structures resembling the current Asian and African elephants, which are comprised of an all-female herd and a matriarch leader, while the males had solitary lives or formed lax groups after they reached maturity. </span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> It is hard to fathom in this age of modernisation, urbanisation and automobiles, that North America was once home to mammoths, ground sloths, bear-sized beavers, camels, and other strong beasts. About 11,000 years ago, these huge mammals, approximately 70 species in total, became extinct. The extinction nearly corresponded with the arrival of humans in the New World and dramatic climatic change factors that bore theories concerning perishing. Recent findings support the contentious hypothesis that humans were responsible for hunting the megafauna to extinction. John Alroy, a paleoecologist at the University of California, argued that extinction as a result of hunting was believable and inevitable. By using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"04056e75-f597-476e-bb9c-fa57ad022b36\">computer simulation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, he demonstrated that even an ordinary volume of hunting was enough to wipe out the animals. Assuming 100 humans at the beginning with a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"63426a66-d727-46a3-a6e2-8d16cc3a5b0e\">population growth of 2<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>% per year, Alroy found that a group of 50 was able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"63426a66-d727-46a3-a6e2-8d16cc3a5b0e\">kill 15 to 20 mammals each year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, so they could wipe out the entire animal populations within 1,000 years. Yet Ross MacPhee, a mammalogist from New York City's Natural History Museum, objects: only a handful of stone tools have been found embedded in the bones of mammoths. </span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> Despite years of scientific research, the precise cause is still unknown. The overkill model came about in the 1960s when Paul S. Martin brought the agenda to Arizona University. Critics of the model have since proposed that there is no evidence to sustain the argument that early Americans hunted the animals to the level of extinction. In particular, large mammals are susceptible to pressure because their gestation period is longer than that of smaller mammals and their offspring need protracted care. Despite this, Alroy's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"7376d574-232f-4dbf-93f9-35eb252172b6\">assessment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> does not have universal consensus. To start with, the outcome of his simulation is subject, in part, to the estimated population size of extinct animals and the estimates are not reliable. MacPhee continues his deeply pointed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1c0cc86b-5330-46d5-a59b-85933059e3c1\">criticism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of Alroy's findings by calling attention to pertinent archaeological records which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9041f5e8-fb79-4e94-b656-5afeeb11a455\">show no widespread pattern of human predation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, and none of the few <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e2b3451a-3647-4580-bb0c-93d49a0f80bd\">stone tools recovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> are recognised as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e2b3451a-3647-4580-bb0c-93d49a0f80bd\">coming from other megafaunal corpses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. This is contrary to the expectation that hunting drove these mammals to their extinction. </span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> Certain animal species had vast ranges and an example is the humongous ground sloth that lived in the far north region up to Yukon and far south down to Mexico. The range itself would make it improbable to slaughter the animals to the extent of causing extinction. MacPhee therefore agrees that human beings were most likely responsible for the extinction of the mammoths and other species that existed at the same time, but not in a direct way. His suggestion is that people likely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8164432d-23df-4684-9279-008492a24dcc\">initiated very lethal diseases, probably through parasites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> or the dogs, causing a widespread epidemic among species with poor immunity in the new biosphere. The newly arrived <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"cf8bc56f-0501-4eb0-99ce-df57f2723b8d\">humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, along with their dogs, would have carried pathogens that the native fauna had never before encountered. Although direct evidence is scarce, MacPhee is confident that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6b35730a-4690-45f9-8252-0c31f9762f55\">DNA and tissue analyses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> from the last species of mammoths would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"621cdef9-6013-43d5-92d8-4ab071a28efa\">reveal the deadly microbes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Similar to Paul Martin's overkill model, large mammal populations would find it hard to recover from such an epidemic, and the recurrent lethal disease outbreaks would quickly lead to extinction. However, MacPhee <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d317a9c8-045b-4ae1-9562-bea4c1cac156\">does not present any<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> empirical evidence to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"bb20d388-914d-44df-bb1c-2db9e9ada88f\">support his hypothesis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. It can also be difficult to find such evidence since lethal disease would have killed these animals far too quickly to leave signatures on the bones. Another proposition on what caused the extinction of North American mammoths has nothing to do with human beings at all. Supporters of the new proposition <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"6e2f8d42-90be-485d-bbb1-30576c6fb793\">blame<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> the weather for the loss, and the Pleistocene epoch was characterised by significant <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"c3740013-2dbb-4f3b-8714-520fa94d87cb\">climatic instability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> as Russell Graham, a paleontologist, explains. He notes that conditions across North America shifted rapidly during this period. </span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"0474722e-474a-4726-827a-4b021cfcac34\">harsh weather<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> caused the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"0474722e-474a-4726-827a-4b021cfcac34\">disappearance of some habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> and some of the species that had formed communities were driven apart. Some animals seized the opportunities and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"dd5c698c-36d8-46bf-a20b-79620ec5a7fd\">flourished<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. However, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2b5e006f-776c-4e9d-8dac-f4e0fe043d46\">intensifying harsh environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> may have been too much for megafauna and caused their geographic range to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"56b8c234-201f-4104-93c8-035e7ff37a7c\">diminish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. This spelled doom for the huge animals which needed larger spaces to survive. As Graham stated, although sizable populations survived the Pleistocene, the Younger Dryas occurrence was too much for them. Alroy is certain that the demise of the titans can be traced to human hunters in the period of extreme cold, the Ice Age. However, Graham believes that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"401bad5c-5cce-4598-8e6b-3b968ed64b15\">changing climate scenarios<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> could predict with accuracy that these species <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"a7f9dce6-2b68-4dd9-ba22-c2d7f7c908dd\">would still become extinct eventually<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. </span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>Being a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"7cb7f5e5-3eac-4ac3-80eb-a99749c799a6\">member of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the (14)______ family, the mammoths were a group of animals that were closely related to modern elephants. They were large, highly social, and a female <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"8ed559dd-767a-496f-90d6-bfc379681dfe\">produced a single calf<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> after a (15)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"d206b3ab-8451-41f4-9469-a4ff2742cb02\">lasting almost two years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Today, many scientists are trying to determine the cause of their extinction. A researcher from the University of California believes that human hunting was the cause. However, this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"7376d574-232f-4dbf-93f9-35eb252172b6\">argument<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> does not have (16)______. MacPhee <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1c0cc86b-5330-46d5-a59b-85933059e3c1\">counters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that the (17)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9041f5e8-fb79-4e94-b656-5afeeb11a455\">show no trace of systematic killing by people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, and that the handful of tools recovered cannot be tied to any other giant species. Another argument is that disease may have killed the mammoths, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d317a9c8-045b-4ae1-9562-bea4c1cac156\">there is no<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> (18)______ evidence to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"bb20d388-914d-44df-bb1c-2db9e9ada88f\">support this idea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. A third explanation leaves humans out altogether: a paleontologist <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"6e2f8d42-90be-485d-bbb1-30576c6fb793\">points to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"c3740013-2dbb-4f3b-8714-520fa94d87cb\">unstable climate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of the (19)______ epoch, arguing that megafauna may not have been able to adapt to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2b5e006f-776c-4e9d-8dac-f4e0fe043d46\">changing environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"56b8c234-201f-4104-93c8-035e7ff37a7c\">reduced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> their (20)______.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322595\" id=\"question-wrapper-322595\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Elephantidae</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322596\" id=\"question-wrapper-322596\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">gestation</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322597\" id=\"question-wrapper-322597\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(universal) consensus</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322598\" id=\"question-wrapper-322598\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">archaeological records</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322599\" id=\"question-wrapper-322599\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">empirical</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322600\" id=\"question-wrapper-322600\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Pleistocene</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322601\" id=\"question-wrapper-322601\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(geographic) range</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements and the list of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"cf8bc56f-0501-4eb0-99ce-df57f2723b8d\">people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-C. Write the correct letter, A-C, in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p><b><span>List of People</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. John Alroy</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Ross MacPhee</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Russell Graham</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322602\" id=\"question-wrapper-322602\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>We can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"04056e75-f597-476e-bb9c-fa57ad022b36\">calculate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> the rate of extinction by measuring the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"63426a66-d727-46a3-a6e2-8d16cc3a5b0e\">rate of hunting against the stable increase of the human population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322603\" id=\"question-wrapper-322603\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>We can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6b35730a-4690-45f9-8252-0c31f9762f55\">analyse the bodies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of extinct mammals to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"621cdef9-6013-43d5-92d8-4ab071a28efa\">look for signs of disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322604\" id=\"question-wrapper-322604\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some species can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"dd5c698c-36d8-46bf-a20b-79620ec5a7fd\">thrive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> in more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"0474722e-474a-4726-827a-4b021cfcac34\">challenging environments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322605\" id=\"question-wrapper-322605\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>If mammoths were extensively hunted, we would expect to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e2b3451a-3647-4580-bb0c-93d49a0f80bd\">find stone tools near their remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322606\" id=\"question-wrapper-322606\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The mammoths were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"a7f9dce6-2b68-4dd9-ba22-c2d7f7c908dd\">fated to become extinct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"401bad5c-5cce-4598-8e6b-3b968ed64b15\">regardless of human activity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322607\" id=\"question-wrapper-322607\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Humans could have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8164432d-23df-4684-9279-008492a24dcc\">brought parasites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> that could kill mammoths.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7cb7f5e5-3eac-4ac3-80eb-a99749c799a6","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"member of","passagePhrase":"belonged to"},{"uid":"d206b3ab-8451-41f4-9469-a4ff2742cb02","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"lasting almost two years","passagePhrase":"twenty-two months"},{"uid":"8ed559dd-767a-496f-90d6-bfc379681dfe","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"produced a single calf","passagePhrase":"birth of one calf"},{"uid":"04056e75-f597-476e-bb9c-fa57ad022b36","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"calculate","passagePhrase":"computer simulation"},{"uid":"63426a66-d727-46a3-a6e2-8d16cc3a5b0e","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"rate of hunting against the stable increase of the human population","passagePhrase":"population growth of 2 ... kill 15 to 20 mammals each year"},{"uid":"7376d574-232f-4dbf-93f9-35eb252172b6","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"argument","passagePhrase":"assessment"},{"uid":"1c0cc86b-5330-46d5-a59b-85933059e3c1","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"counters","passagePhrase":"criticism"},{"uid":"9041f5e8-fb79-4e94-b656-5afeeb11a455","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"show no trace of systematic killing by people","passagePhrase":"show no widespread pattern of human predation"},{"uid":"e2b3451a-3647-4580-bb0c-93d49a0f80bd","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"find stone tools near their remains","passagePhrase":"stone tools recovered ... coming from other megafaunal corpses"},{"uid":"8164432d-23df-4684-9279-008492a24dcc","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"brought parasites","passagePhrase":"initiated very lethal diseases, probably through parasites"},{"uid":"cf8bc56f-0501-4eb0-99ce-df57f2723b8d","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"people","passagePhrase":"humans"},{"uid":"6b35730a-4690-45f9-8252-0c31f9762f55","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"analyse the bodies","passagePhrase":"DNA and tissue analyses"},{"uid":"621cdef9-6013-43d5-92d8-4ab071a28efa","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"look for signs of disease","passagePhrase":"reveal the deadly microbes"},{"uid":"d317a9c8-045b-4ae1-9562-bea4c1cac156","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"there is no","passagePhrase":"does not present any"},{"uid":"bb20d388-914d-44df-bb1c-2db9e9ada88f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"support this idea","passagePhrase":"support his hypothesis"},{"uid":"6e2f8d42-90be-485d-bbb1-30576c6fb793","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"points to","passagePhrase":"blame"},{"uid":"c3740013-2dbb-4f3b-8714-520fa94d87cb","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"unstable climate","passagePhrase":"climatic instability"},{"uid":"0474722e-474a-4726-827a-4b021cfcac34","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"challenging environments","passagePhrase":"harsh weather ... disappearance of some habitats"},{"uid":"dd5c698c-36d8-46bf-a20b-79620ec5a7fd","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"thrive","passagePhrase":"flourished"},{"uid":"2b5e006f-776c-4e9d-8dac-f4e0fe043d46","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"changing environment","passagePhrase":"intensifying harsh environment"},{"uid":"56b8c234-201f-4104-93c8-035e7ff37a7c","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"reduced","passagePhrase":"diminish"},{"uid":"401bad5c-5cce-4598-8e6b-3b968ed64b15","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"regardless of human activity","passagePhrase":"changing climate scenarios"},{"uid":"a7f9dce6-2b68-4dd9-ba22-c2d7f7c908dd","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"fated to become extinct","passagePhrase":"would still become extinct eventually"}]},"reading_u2_42":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The fluoridation controversy</span></b></p><p><i><span>The long-standing debate about whether to fluoridate our drinking water continues</span></i></p><p><span>Fluoridation is the addition of fluorine to public water supplies with the aim of reducing tooth decay. Fluorine, when mixed with water, forms fluoride, and the desired concentration of fluoride in public water is approximately 1 part per million, depending on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2fff16f3-b07d-46a3-b005-0ca64a7f405a\">regional temperature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> and, hence, the amount of water people are likely to drink. Many studies, such as those by McClure in 1970 and Burt in 1983, have shown that when children drink fluoridated water, their average rate of tooth decay appears to be greatly reduced. A typical figure claimed is a 50 percent reduction. This apparently enormous benefit for children's teeth is the major argument in favor of fluoridation.</span></p><p><span>Three main grounds for opposition to fluoridation have been expressed. First, opponents claim the benefits are exaggerated or not established. Second, there are claims of health risks to parts of the population, for example, allergic reactions. It is also accepted that high levels of fluoride can cause discoloration of otherwise healthy teeth. Proponents do not consider this to be a problem in such small concentrations, whereas opponents disagree—especially because some people drink more water and obtain much more than the standard 1 milligram of fluoride per day. Third, fluoridation is thought to be an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"783186f6-252f-468d-885f-fc7122c383e0\">infringement on individual rights<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> because it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"965f1cc1-f0bf-4e4e-8e32-4be02f6593ea\">compulsory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> medication for all members of a community.</span></p><p><span>An understanding of the fluoridation issue has important implications. If, according to the experts, fluoridation is unquestionably a beneficial and non-hazardous measure, then the wisdom of allowing the public to vote on, and reject it must be questioned. Almost all studies that have been done have assumed that the scientific aspects of the controversy are unproblematic, and they have excluded science from sociological examination. The traditional view is that science is a special kind of knowledge, which is established through scientific methods and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"160b17d3-60aa-426d-a736-ad29338414ce\">objectively applied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> by members of a scientific community.</span></p><p><span>However, in recent years there has been a major challenge to this picture by a sociology of science that shows how scientific knowledge is socially negotiated, and inevitably linked to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"586a5388-d4a7-466d-b8aa-9effb110eb68\">values of the relevant parties, both scientists and nonscientists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. These challengers do not see scientific knowledge as exempt from social inquiry. Kuhn (1970) argued that scientific knowledge does not always develop as an orderly process, but is characterized by periodic revolutions, in which the methods of study and the assessment criteria change in a fragmented way. According to Kuhn, the shift from one scientific way of thinking to another is not made solely on the basis of clear rules of formal scientific practice, but can include <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"1e3892e6-5a19-427e-b4e0-5463dc7d394f\">social factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, though Kuhn has never developed a full analysis of what these might be.</span></p><p><span>Collins (1975) took this concept further when he asserted that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"e235a306-3983-4336-9e14-adf6cc4aa8d4\">outcome of experiments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"0887c849-c976-4625-95b2-c65383e5311c\">not<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> something whose meaning could be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"0887c849-c976-4625-95b2-c65383e5311c\">immediately comprehended<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, but rather something for interpretation, discussion between scientists, and reinterpretation in the light of other experiments. One interpretation of this analysis of science is that traditional distinctions between facts and theories, and between scientific knowledge and values, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"65354dc8-5d79-4451-8d4e-e89e14fa56c7\">can no longer be justified<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Because social processes are involved at all stages of the creation, evaluation, and establishment of scientific knowledge, social values may also be involved.</span></p><p><span>In the same way as many scientists who study fluoridation have overlooked social values, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"74e9357d-05d3-43ad-85da-cbdf8978a357\">sociologists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> have also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"8300b5d9-ebfc-4071-8f1a-dfc5c080d0ce\">downplayed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> an important part of the debate by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"8300b5d9-ebfc-4071-8f1a-dfc5c080d0ce\">ignoring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> the number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"5b612940-f0ce-48de-9618-844cab47cf45\">eminent scientists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> who have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"ca31a11b-4cbb-4f65-8636-5d54aaff2fe7\">questioned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> aspects of fluoridation. An example is the study by Sutton in 1960, which analyzed the classic North American studies of the effect of fluoridation on tooth decay, and found that each showed significant <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"af6703e5-71cf-47e3-963a-1f63f5d58478\">methodological shortcomings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Sutton's detailed study throws doubt as to the extent of reductions in tooth decay from fluoridation. Yet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"119e3818-1b69-40de-b75b-2d4c41549805\">Sutton's book<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> is not cited in a single analysis of the fluoridation issue by any sociologist.</span></p><p><span>In a situation of some scientific uncertainty, differences in values are highlighted. A supporter of fluoridation might argue, 'The evidence for the benefits of fluoridation is quite substantial, while the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"39849c1e-c4c3-4136-b71c-2fc83462ffc9\">evidence for harm is limited and dubious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. I think the likely benefits outweigh the possible dangers; hence I support fluoridation because it is the cheapest and easiest way to make sure every child reaps the benefits.'</span></p><p><span>An opponent might argue, 'Though the evidence for the benefits of fluoridation is substantial, there is some doubt about it. Since fluoridation is not necessary for good teeth, we should forgo the benefits if there is some slight chance of harm. Some scientists claim that a small percentage of the population could be harmed by fluoride. Therefore, I oppose fluoridation of water supplies and favor the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"18ec401d-f0b4-4afa-af9c-4e8430d1ee05\">voluntary use of fluoride tablets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> by those who want to take them.'</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"3f5389aa-acb4-4620-a114-fbed9ea393cb\">Both arguments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> consider the scientific evidence concerning fluoridation, but differ in their assessments of the social benefits and costs. This difference is not between rationality and irrationality but is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"43938cbe-383e-4624-abad-42bd52a1c60e\">legitimate difference in values<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, for example, the positive value placed on good teeth, the negative value placed on possible health risks, and the social benefits or costs of compulsory or voluntary intake of fluorides.</span></p><p><span>From the sociological point of view, opposition to fluoridation is not necessarily irrational. Rather, claims to rationality and to scientific authority are better seen as part of a strategy to promote fluoridation than as incontrovertible statements of fact. Second, social values are likely to be bound up in any decision about fluoridation, so this is not an issue on which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"7ec0bd4b-0a46-42a8-8d3a-ff65955f95f4\">declarations by scientific experts ought to be considered the final word<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27 – 31 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322608\" id=\"question-wrapper-322608\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The optimum amount of fluoride in fluoridated water is calculated partly according to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2fff16f3-b07d-46a3-b005-0ca64a7f405a\">how hot the area is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>B. how warm the water is.</li> <li>C. how poor the area's dental health is.</li> <li>D. how much fluoride residents vote for.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322609\" id=\"question-wrapper-322609\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>One reason given by the writer for opposing fluoridation is that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. it may contribute to tooth decay.</li> <li>B. it will be unacceptably expensive for the public.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"965f1cc1-f0bf-4e4e-8e32-4be02f6593ea\">obligatory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> fluoridation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"783186f6-252f-468d-885f-fc7122c383e0\">takes away personal freedom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>D. excessive fluoride could be added to the water by mistake.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322610\" id=\"question-wrapper-322610\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer mentions Kuhn in order to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. provide a contrast with the view of Collins.</li> <li>B. support the rational nature of scientific inquiry.</li> <li>C. demonstrate&nbsp;that Kuhn did not argue his case adequately.</li> <li>D. show that science can be influenced by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"1e3892e6-5a19-427e-b4e0-5463dc7d394f\">non-scientific considerations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322611\" id=\"question-wrapper-322611\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What did Sutton’s research discover about earlier studies in North America?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. There were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"af6703e5-71cf-47e3-963a-1f63f5d58478\">failings in the way they were carried out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>B. The scientists involved had achieved unique results.</li> <li>C. Proponents of fluoridation had not understood its long-term effects.</li> <li>D. Fluoridation had a greater effect on tooth decay than previously believed.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322612\" id=\"question-wrapper-322612\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the last paragraph, what does the writer say about scientists?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They should reveal their true motivations.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"7ec0bd4b-0a46-42a8-8d3a-ff65955f95f4\">They should not decide the fluoridation policy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>C. They are solely concerned with scientific truths.</li> <li>D. They cannot reach agreement on the fluoridation issue.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 32–35 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322613\" id=\"question-wrapper-322613\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Scientific knowledge can <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"65354dc8-5d79-4451-8d4e-e89e14fa56c7\">remain detached<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> from communal beliefs.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322614\" id=\"question-wrapper-322614\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Many sociologists have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"8300b5d9-ebfc-4071-8f1a-dfc5c080d0ce\">disregarded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"ca31a11b-4cbb-4f65-8636-5d54aaff2fe7\">doubts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"5b612940-f0ce-48de-9618-844cab47cf45\">certain distinguished scholars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> have concerning fluoridation.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322615\" id=\"question-wrapper-322615\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"119e3818-1b69-40de-b75b-2d4c41549805\">Sutton’s findings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> have been given insufficient attention by <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"74e9357d-05d3-43ad-85da-cbdf8978a357\">scientists outside of North America<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322616\" id=\"question-wrapper-322616\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>There are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"43938cbe-383e-4624-abad-42bd52a1c60e\">valid arguments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"3f5389aa-acb4-4620-a114-fbed9ea393cb\">both sides<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of the fluoridation debate.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A–G, below. Write the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 36–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"e235a306-3983-4336-9e14-adf6cc4aa8d4\">results of scientific research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"0887c849-c976-4625-95b2-c65383e5311c\">not always grasped on first encounter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. science is an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"160b17d3-60aa-426d-a736-ad29338414ce\">unbiased discipline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"18ec401d-f0b4-4afa-af9c-4e8430d1ee05\">individuals ought to have the freedom to decide on their fluoride consumption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"39849c1e-c4c3-4136-b71c-2fc83462ffc9\">evidence of possible harm is too weak<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> to warrant withholding the measure.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. the grave harms caused by fluoride substantially exceed any benefits it confers.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. the advantages of fluoride supplementation extend beyond the population of children.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. scientific knowledge is affected by the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"586a5388-d4a7-466d-b8aa-9effb110eb68\">beliefs of everyone concerned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322617\" id=\"question-wrapper-322617\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The traditional view of science is that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322618\" id=\"question-wrapper-322618\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A sociological view of science argues that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322619\" id=\"question-wrapper-322619\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Collins is of the opinion that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322620\" id=\"question-wrapper-322620\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer suggests that a supporter of fluoridation may conclude that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322621\" id=\"question-wrapper-322621\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer suggests that an opponent of fluoridation may conclude that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"2fff16f3-b07d-46a3-b005-0ca64a7f405a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"how hot the area is","passagePhrase":"regional temperature"},{"uid":"783186f6-252f-468d-885f-fc7122c383e0","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"takes away personal freedom","passagePhrase":"infringement on individual rights"},{"uid":"965f1cc1-f0bf-4e4e-8e32-4be02f6593ea","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"obligatory","passagePhrase":"compulsory"},{"uid":"160b17d3-60aa-426d-a736-ad29338414ce","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"unbiased discipline","passagePhrase":"objectively applied"},{"uid":"586a5388-d4a7-466d-b8aa-9effb110eb68","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"beliefs of everyone concerned","passagePhrase":"values of the relevant parties, both scientists and nonscientists"},{"uid":"1e3892e6-5a19-427e-b4e0-5463dc7d394f","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"non-scientific considerations","passagePhrase":"social factors"},{"uid":"e235a306-3983-4336-9e14-adf6cc4aa8d4","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"results of scientific research","passagePhrase":"outcome of experiments"},{"uid":"0887c849-c976-4625-95b2-c65383e5311c","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"not always grasped on first encounter","passagePhrase":"not ... immediately comprehended"},{"uid":"8300b5d9-ebfc-4071-8f1a-dfc5c080d0ce","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"disregarded","passagePhrase":"downplayed ... ignoring"},{"uid":"5b612940-f0ce-48de-9618-844cab47cf45","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"certain distinguished scholars","passagePhrase":"eminent scientists"},{"uid":"ca31a11b-4cbb-4f65-8636-5d54aaff2fe7","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"doubts","passagePhrase":"questioned"},{"uid":"af6703e5-71cf-47e3-963a-1f63f5d58478","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"failings in the way they were carried out","passagePhrase":"methodological shortcomings"},{"uid":"119e3818-1b69-40de-b75b-2d4c41549805","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Sutton’s findings","passagePhrase":"Sutton's book"},{"uid":"39849c1e-c4c3-4136-b71c-2fc83462ffc9","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"evidence of possible harm is too weak","passagePhrase":"evidence for harm is limited and dubious"},{"uid":"18ec401d-f0b4-4afa-af9c-4e8430d1ee05","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"individuals ought to have the freedom to decide on their fluoride consumption","passagePhrase":"voluntary use of fluoride tablets"},{"uid":"3f5389aa-acb4-4620-a114-fbed9ea393cb","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"both sides","passagePhrase":"Both arguments"},{"uid":"43938cbe-383e-4624-abad-42bd52a1c60e","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"valid arguments","passagePhrase":"legitimate difference in values"},{"uid":"7ec0bd4b-0a46-42a8-8d3a-ff65955f95f4","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"They should not decide the fluoridation policy","passagePhrase":"declarations by scientific experts ought to be considered the final word"}]},"reading_u2_43":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1–13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Book review: Triumph of the City</span></b></p><p><span>A. Triumph of the City, by Edward Glaeser, is a readable and often thrilling book. It is a hymn of praise to the city — an invention so important that we often take it for granted. Cities now shape global life. In 2018, 55 per cent of the world's population lived in urban areas. This figure is expected to reach 68 per cent by 2050. People continue to flood into cities to find jobs and opportunities. The crowds and poverty in some modern cities may horrify observers. However, the book <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"abf5c160-5ba7-4350-97f9-74120587bd0a\">does not present<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> these conditions <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"abf5c160-5ba7-4350-97f9-74120587bd0a d27d687c-8b3a-452d-9ee2-983ade93a4e9\">only</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"ba524562-ad94-4cb0-a691-be8db12ea4ef\">evidence of failure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. It also sees them as signs of economic movement, growth and aspiration.</span></p><p><span>B. This view has faced more than two hundred years of resistance. The Industrial Revolution began in Britain. Soon after, the Romantic poets turned away from urban smoke and factories. They celebrated the air and light of untouched nature. In nineteenth-century America, Henry David Thoreau retreated to Walden Pond in 1845. He later published a book called Walden in 1854. In it, he described a solitary, simple life outside the city. His writing influenced generations of Americans. These readers came to associate cities with moral and physical decline. They regarded nature as a healthier alternative. However, the book sets this tradition beside the practical history of cities. The disadvantages of early urban life were real, but they were not permanent.</span></p><p><span>C. Early industrial cities were dirty. They lacked efficient waste-disposal systems. As a result, disease spread rapidly through crowded neighbourhoods. However, these cities were also profitable. This created strong commercial and political <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"74c421fa-2982-4177-afa4-584d6958babf\">incentives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> to improve them. Paris is one of the clearest examples. Between 1853 and 1870, Napoleon III gave Baron Haussmann <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"96312077-549d-49ba-b594-c233f689f7a0\">exceptionally unrestricted authority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"4734e6eb-99ce-4a2f-bf46-5075d74c05fb\">reconstruct the city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. Wide boulevards, sewers, parks and public spaces replaced many overcrowded and slum-infested districts. New York developed through a less centralised process. It began with the Commissioners' Plan of 1811. This plan imposed the Manhattan street grid on the city. The grid later supported large-scale commercial and residential growth. Both cities became major centres of ideas, trade and innovation.</span></p><p><span>D. The book also looks at the spectacle of urban poverty from an economic point of view. Poor people often flock to cities. Urban jobs give them a greater chance of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"ddceb631-eb52-4a2d-be6b-b3dce5a6d098\">becoming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> richer. Their labour also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"28ccd620-40ce-4e2e-9418-d211d0a6ae3d\">helps to reinvigorate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"2717f558-bc73-488f-9214-1b412f433c76\">city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> economy. It is therefore <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"cd303ad0-d395-43cc-a904-0ad416e8c768\">folly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to push them out through strict planning rules. Such rules limit new housing and cause property prices to soar. In some cities, jobs grow faster than the supply of homes. In these cities, poorer residents face the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"cd303ad0-d395-43cc-a904-0ad416e8c768\">greatest difficulty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> in finding a place to live. Building more housing and improving infrastructure can make urban opportunities more accessible. In contrast, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"cd303ad0-d395-43cc-a904-0ad416e8c768\">excessive restrictions place tremendous pressure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> on existing neighbourhoods and transport systems.</span></p><p><span>E. Problems arise when municipal authorities fail to balance preservation with growth. Paris is a good example. One of the city's great virtues is the historic character of Haussmann's nineteenth-century boulevards. The book defends the preservation of this central landscape. However, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c66658c9-c370-40db-8dc0-c49f09c3f13e\">questions the decision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5436a716-1e4c-450c-921b-7f11f1516190\">put large-scale office development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> at La Défense. La Défense is on the western outskirts of Paris. The authority responsible for developing the district was set up in 1958. La Défense then grew <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"058334ff-a8a0-49f0-9501-e385804a2491\">into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> a major high-rise business centre outside the historic core. The book argues that commercial development around Montparnasse could have revitalised parts of central Paris instead. This would not have destroyed its architectural fabric. Some critics also argue that excessive preservation can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"058334ff-a8a0-49f0-9501-e385804a2491\">turn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"b82e5da2-1154-4688-8bb6-91c228d28957\">historic centres<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> into a living museum rather than a dynamic urban environment.</span></p><p><span>F. Mumbai shows a different problem. The issue is the link between building restrictions and outward expansion. The city's population grew from about 8.2 million in 1981 to about 12.5 million in the 2011 census. This growth happened within an area of roughly 603 square kilometres. As demand for homes and workplaces increased, restrictions were imposed on the height and volume of new buildings. This limited the usable space available in established urban locations. As a result, the city expanded into surrounding areas in an inefficient way. This sprawl also increased travel demands for many residents. The example supports the book's broader point. Dense cities cannot work well unless their planning systems allow enough housing and commercial space to be built where people need it.</span></p><p><span>G. In the United States, suburban expansion created another set of urban-planning problems. The book is repentant about the appeal of suburban life to families. It also recognises the legitimate financial pressures behind this choice. Petrol was relatively cheap. Planning rules <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"911433e6-c5fa-40c3-b31b-67a9c8626e64\">raised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5c28fd38-19bf-4974-9642-03b86c2bbb4a\">inner-city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> property <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"911433e6-c5fa-40c3-b31b-67a9c8626e64\">prices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. As a result, moving to the suburbs became almost inevitable for many middle-class households. Suburbanites generally mingle less in dense public spaces. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"45fd5db7-a89f-4477-a58a-0b2c56bf7106\">reduces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a623125f-f7f8-45c5-b424-ad6544f0873d\">face-to-face<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> contact associated with urban creativity. Detached homes are also costlier to heat and cool than flats. Car-dependent households may drive around 15,000 miles a year. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"98bea792-9e18-4bfb-899a-4ff64c34637c\">Greater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> household <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"84b910e0-a605-4969-a610-0ad92b279cfa\">energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> consumption and reliance on cars contribute to a larger carbon footprint. This strengthens the environmental case for compact cities.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1–5 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322622\" id=\"question-wrapper-322622\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"abf5c160-5ba7-4350-97f9-74120587bd0a\">Glaeser believes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> that congestion and poverty in some modern cities <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"abf5c160-5ba7-4350-97f9-74120587bd0a d27d687c-8b3a-452d-9ee2-983ade93a4e9\">solely</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"ba524562-ad94-4cb0-a691-be8db12ea4ef\">indicate serious problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322623\" id=\"question-wrapper-322623\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer Henry David Thoreau discussed the ideas of the Romantic poets in his work.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322624\" id=\"question-wrapper-322624\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Haussmann faced <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"96312077-549d-49ba-b594-c233f689f7a0\">few limits on his power<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"4734e6eb-99ce-4a2f-bf46-5075d74c05fb\">redesigning Paris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322625\" id=\"question-wrapper-322625\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Strict planning regulations may be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"cd303ad0-d395-43cc-a904-0ad416e8c768\">beneficial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> for a city’s development.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322626\" id=\"question-wrapper-322626\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In his book, Glaeser <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c66658c9-c370-40db-8dc0-c49f09c3f13e\">criticises the decision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5436a716-1e4c-450c-921b-7f11f1516190\">concentrate business development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> at La Défense.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Cities</span></b></p><p><b><span>• Problems with early cities</span></b></p><p><span>– dirt</span></p><p><span>– (6)______</span></p><p><span>but there were commercial and (7)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"74c421fa-2982-4177-afa4-584d6958babf\">reasons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> for redeveloping them</span></p><p><b><span>• Urban poverty is not a major problem because poor people</span></b></p><p><span>– are more likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"ddceb631-eb52-4a2d-be6b-b3dce5a6d098\">end up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)______</span></p><p><span>– <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"28ccd620-40ce-4e2e-9418-d211d0a6ae3d\">help to develop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"2717f558-bc73-488f-9214-1b412f433c76\">urban<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)______</span></p><p><b><span>• Cities do have some problems – e.g.</span></b></p><p><span>– <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"b82e5da2-1154-4688-8bb6-91c228d28957\">the centre of Paris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"058334ff-a8a0-49f0-9501-e385804a2491\">becoming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> a (10)______</span></p><p><span>– Mumbai is negatively affected by height restrictions on new buildings.</span></p><p><b><span>• In the US, the middle classes have moved to the suburbs due to</span></b></p><p><span>– cheap petrol</span></p><p><span>– the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"911433e6-c5fa-40c3-b31b-67a9c8626e64\">high cost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of (11)______ in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5c28fd38-19bf-4974-9642-03b86c2bbb4a\">central urban areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span></span></p><p><b><span>• Disadvantages of suburbs</span></b></p><p><span>– <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"45fd5db7-a89f-4477-a58a-0b2c56bf7106\">less<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a623125f-f7f8-45c5-b424-ad6544f0873d\">personal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12)______</span></p><p><span>– <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"98bea792-9e18-4bfb-899a-4ff64c34637c\">increased<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)______ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"84b910e0-a605-4969-a610-0ad92b279cfa\">resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> such as heating – which damages the environment</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322627\" id=\"question-wrapper-322627\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">disease</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322628\" id=\"question-wrapper-322628\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">political</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322629\" id=\"question-wrapper-322629\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">richer</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322630\" id=\"question-wrapper-322630\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">economy</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322631\" id=\"question-wrapper-322631\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">museum</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322632\" id=\"question-wrapper-322632\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">property</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322633\" id=\"question-wrapper-322633\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">contact</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322634\" id=\"question-wrapper-322634\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">consumption</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"abf5c160-5ba7-4350-97f9-74120587bd0a d27d687c-8b3a-452d-9ee2-983ade93a4e9","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"solely","passagePhrase":"only"},{"uid":"ba524562-ad94-4cb0-a691-be8db12ea4ef","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"indicate serious problems","passagePhrase":"evidence of failure"},{"uid":"74c421fa-2982-4177-afa4-584d6958babf","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"reasons","passagePhrase":"incentives"},{"uid":"96312077-549d-49ba-b594-c233f689f7a0","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"few limits on his power","passagePhrase":"exceptionally unrestricted authority"},{"uid":"4734e6eb-99ce-4a2f-bf46-5075d74c05fb","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"redesigning Paris","passagePhrase":"reconstruct the city"},{"uid":"ddceb631-eb52-4a2d-be6b-b3dce5a6d098","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"end up","passagePhrase":"becoming"},{"uid":"28ccd620-40ce-4e2e-9418-d211d0a6ae3d","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"help to develop","passagePhrase":"helps to reinvigorate"},{"uid":"2717f558-bc73-488f-9214-1b412f433c76","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"urban","passagePhrase":"city"},{"uid":"c66658c9-c370-40db-8dc0-c49f09c3f13e","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"criticises the decision","passagePhrase":"questions the decision"},{"uid":"5436a716-1e4c-450c-921b-7f11f1516190","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"concentrate business development","passagePhrase":"put large-scale office development"},{"uid":"058334ff-a8a0-49f0-9501-e385804a2491","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"becoming","passagePhrase":"into ... turn"},{"uid":"b82e5da2-1154-4688-8bb6-91c228d28957","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the centre of Paris","passagePhrase":"historic centres"},{"uid":"911433e6-c5fa-40c3-b31b-67a9c8626e64","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"high cost","passagePhrase":"raised ... prices"},{"uid":"5c28fd38-19bf-4974-9642-03b86c2bbb4a","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"central urban areas","passagePhrase":"inner-city"},{"uid":"45fd5db7-a89f-4477-a58a-0b2c56bf7106","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"less","passagePhrase":"reduces"},{"uid":"a623125f-f7f8-45c5-b424-ad6544f0873d","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"personal","passagePhrase":"face-to-face"},{"uid":"98bea792-9e18-4bfb-899a-4ff64c34637c","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"increased","passagePhrase":"Greater"},{"uid":"84b910e0-a605-4969-a610-0ad92b279cfa","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"resources","passagePhrase":"energy"}]},"reading_u2_44":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Ancient Storytelling</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> The first stories were probably narrated to people crouching around a bonfire. These included tales of mighty adventures, like near-death encounters, hunting excursions, or an escape from mortal peril, or perhaps a mystery or divine anecdotes. However, irrespective of the subject, there was one <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a3808add-cacb-4d94-a0d1-702b9f0aa47e\">principal objective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"0cc33e2e-9199-4245-8722-18b719086161\">behind all these tales<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>: to keep the listener intrigued and engaged, to make them overlook their worries or fatigue, and only one query must prevail in their mind — what happens next?</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"4f947363-dcbc-46cf-a33f-3e52ab72ce17\">Finding the initial stories ever told<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in human history is like <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2fce5390-a487-415d-8973-f183d811a6e8\">herding cats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, as these were preserved in the minds of the storytellers. This kind of storage or memorisation, however, shall not be deemed as ineffective. Several documented oral traditions of Australia, the Balkans, and other parts of the world apprise us of master storytellers and poets of the time that could recite thousands of verses and prose from their memory, word to word! However, while such memorisation seems like art or sorcery, the essential idea of creating <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"569aaec1-5044-4ae0-b964-48947427eaf4\">symbols<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> is to have a <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"f219ac9a-1049-4061-9ab6-e8a9636f3a57\">system of </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 23\" data-uid=\"569aaec1-5044-4ae0-b964-48947427eaf4 f219ac9a-1049-4061-9ab6-e8a9636f3a57\">reminders or mnemonics</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> that helps one <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7a92d54a-0c80-4682-ae92-26becf58bb59\">recall specific information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> in one's mind.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span>In a few Polynesian societies, the storytellers used <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"147962e9-8b70-49dc-ae62-d884a00cf6cb\">a notched memory stick<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"9fbbb739-164a-4f44-a2ec-1ff8da4e9dbd\">assistance in successive stages of recitation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. However, among many other global communities, the art of storytelling <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c91a19b6-c3af-45fd-b0b4-2ae0a366b862\">led to the invention or development of writing systems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. For instance, the onset of literacy in ancient Greece is attributed to the fact that the epic tales of the Trojan War and the Voyage of Odysseus were so captivating that there was a need to preserve them. Thus, the Greeks, in 750 B.C. — 700 B.C. borrowed the alphabet system from their Eastern Mediterranean neighbours, the Phoenicians.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span>The pristine practice of documenting stories on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"af35f001-3f20-4982-b731-f70b7249cefc\">parchment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and other materials can be traced to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"516bb96e-8994-4c71-9014-74b119965a80\">many ancient civilisations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. The priestly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"af35f001-3f20-4982-b731-f70b7249cefc\">papyrus<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> archives of ancient <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"516bb96e-8994-4c71-9014-74b119965a80\">Egypt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"af35f001-3f20-4982-b731-f70b7249cefc\">birch-bark scrolls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> used by North American <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"516bb96e-8994-4c71-9014-74b119965a80\">Ojibway Indians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> are excellent examples. It has emerged as a tried and tested practice, thanks to which stories are today synonymous with words on paper. Even the practice of oral storytelling is believed to have been taken over by journals, novels, comic strips, etc. However, written texts are not the primary source for humans to access stories. But then, what is it?</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Each year, over seven billion people head towards the silver screens to watch the latest offerings of national and international cinema. Yes, the chief storyteller of the day is none other than the Cinema! The movies encompass storytelling in the form of motion pictures, which is a contemporary phenomenon in comparison to reading information on paper or still photography. It is more so an illusion that was originally accepted by the method of sequencing images in a particular order. Even so, it is imperative to acknowledge that the art of visual storytelling must hold a profoundly atavistic vibe to it. In spite of the advantage, the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 21\" data-uid=\"12fdefd4-371e-4c0f-9ba6-3938fde255a4 5cc8068d-f25f-46d7-b018-50723db3ad2e\">conventional patterns</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of storyline and characterisation that have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"12fdefd4-371e-4c0f-9ba6-3938fde255a4\">instilled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in storytelling <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"12fdefd4-371e-4c0f-9ba6-3938fde255a4\">for ages are indispensable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> for a good story.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>While thousands of scripts collect dust on the desks of major film studios, all an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"412cb4da-2f10-49a5-8836-7cfd27ce6f50\">aspiring screenwriter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> needs to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"1df304d1-b195-4a44-b4ef-cf6e5da881a4\">look up to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"49464e56-08fe-459b-8aaa-9fde07a708ee\">the fourth-century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> Greek philosopher, Aristotle. In his incomplete work, </span><i><span>The Poetics</span></i><span>, he left several lecture notes describing the art of storytelling in multiple literary and dramatic mediums. Though it is highly unlikely that he envisaged the popcorn-fuelled atmosphere of today's multiplexes, he had ample perception of how to gather and retain large crowds to such creative centres. Aristotle examined the process with impressive rationalism. He states that when a story fascinates us, we lose the sense of where we are, our fears, and accept fiction. This is one of Aristotle's principles of theatre, which he calls — 'the suspension of disbelief.'</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>The audience knows the feeling! They might have experienced episodes of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a7e27fc7-46b2-47df-91b0-dc508a5dc00c\">horror, grief, astonishment or ecstasy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, sitting on the theatre seats or even days after the show, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"01187464-cc5e-4dfd-a285-2afe0d25dffc\">knowing that it is all fiction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> yet letting it impact their state of mind. They seldom think through why they are caught in the web of the storyteller.</span></p><p><b><span>H. </span></b><span>Aristotle taught at Athens, the city where theatre emerged as a prime mode of public leisure and entertainment. So it is evident that he might have observed suspended disbelief in action. Two theatrical storytelling types, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ef41b6ae-6114-4aa4-8350-d0c8b571847d\">tragedy and comedy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, made Athenians immerse themselves in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"64af0065-3d14-4bde-b1ed-20e2a4925042\">gloom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"99abb3b5-7b50-4f25-97d2-1e0df1b00c03\">glee<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, respectively. Of which, Aristotle explicitly acknowledged tragedy as a potent weapon to trigger the most heartfelt emotions of the spectators, so he explored the factors in the storyteller's art that brought about such a subconscious commotion. For this, he studied the masterpieces of classical Greek tragedies by Euripides, Aeschylus, Sophocles, and even the epic poetry of Homer. Even at that time, Homer's stories commanded the same awe as today. His </span><i><span>Iliad</span></i><span> and the </span><i><span>Odyssey</span></i><span> were considered literary landmarks and used as a scale to measure all other stories.</span></p><p><b><span>I. </span></b><span>So what is the mystery behind Homer's captivating narratives? Homer conceived credible heroes that were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"1ebcb604-7bd8-441d-bc4a-faf6ed2e5558\">powerful and majestic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> but did not turn into fantasy figures in the end. He made them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"30b950ce-cb62-481f-ad2f-936c37c0a622\">sulk, quarrel, cheat, and whine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. These were the characteristics that an audience could relate to, or wish to follow. This naturally intrigued them to know what happens next. As Aristotle observed, the heroes with a human side, a mix of flaws and vulnerability to which humans are inclined, are aptly dramatic.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A–E from the list below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><b><span>i. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"af35f001-3f20-4982-b731-f70b7249cefc\">Material methods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"516bb96e-8994-4c71-9014-74b119965a80\">adopted across many cultures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><b><span>ii. </span></b><span>The psychological condition Aristotle described</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><b><span>iii. </span></b><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"f219ac9a-1049-4061-9ab6-e8a9636f3a57\">deliberate technique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> behind oral storage</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><b><span>iv. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5cc8068d-f25f-46d7-b018-50723db3ad2e\">Old impulses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> behind a modern format</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><b><span>v. </span></b><span>Public spectacle as emotional instrument</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><b><span>vi. </span></b><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a3808add-cacb-4d94-a0d1-702b9f0aa47e\">enduring purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"0cc33e2e-9199-4245-8722-18b719086161\">behind effective narration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><b><span>vii. </span></b><span>Storytelling and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c91a19b6-c3af-45fd-b0b4-2ae0a366b862\">emergence of writing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><b><span>viii. </span></b><span>Why imperfect protagonists succeed</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322635\" id=\"question-wrapper-322635\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322636\" id=\"question-wrapper-322636\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322637\" id=\"question-wrapper-322637\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322638\" id=\"question-wrapper-322638\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322639\" id=\"question-wrapper-322639\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?<br> Write the correct letter, </span><b><span>A–I</span></b><span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322640\" id=\"question-wrapper-322640\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a suggestion that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"49464e56-08fe-459b-8aaa-9fde07a708ee\">ancient<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> teachings can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"1df304d1-b195-4a44-b4ef-cf6e5da881a4\">help engage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"412cb4da-2f10-49a5-8836-7cfd27ce6f50\">modern audiences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322641\" id=\"question-wrapper-322641\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2fce5390-a487-415d-8973-f183d811a6e8\">analogy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> used to illustrate the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"4f947363-dcbc-46cf-a33f-3e52ab72ce17\">difficulty of identifying the earliest tales<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322642\" id=\"question-wrapper-322642\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a modern example demonstrating the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"12fdefd4-371e-4c0f-9ba6-3938fde255a4\">endurance of core storytelling principles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322643\" id=\"question-wrapper-322643\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"147962e9-8b70-49dc-ae62-d884a00cf6cb\">a physical device<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> once used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"9fbbb739-164a-4f44-a2ec-1ff8da4e9dbd\">assist storytellers' memory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-E, below. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ef41b6ae-6114-4aa4-8350-d0c8b571847d\">dramas containing either </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"64af0065-3d14-4bde-b1ed-20e2a4925042 ef41b6ae-6114-4aa4-8350-d0c8b571847d\">sorrowful events</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ef41b6ae-6114-4aa4-8350-d0c8b571847d\"> or stories with </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"99abb3b5-7b50-4f25-97d2-1e0df1b00c03 ef41b6ae-6114-4aa4-8350-d0c8b571847d\">cheerful endings</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a7e27fc7-46b2-47df-91b0-dc508a5dc00c\">strong emotional responses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"01187464-cc5e-4dfd-a285-2afe0d25dffc\">to events known to be fictional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"569aaec1-5044-4ae0-b964-48947427eaf4\">certain memory devices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7a92d54a-0c80-4682-ae92-26becf58bb59\">retain large pieces of information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. frightening scenes that overwhelm rational thinking</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. characters who may display <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"30b950ce-cb62-481f-ad2f-936c37c0a622\">controversial behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> despite their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"1ebcb604-7bd8-441d-bc4a-faf6ed2e5558\">admirable qualities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322644\" id=\"question-wrapper-322644\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Storytellers in the past created</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322645\" id=\"question-wrapper-322645\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A good story triggers</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322646\" id=\"question-wrapper-322646\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Athenians were particularly interested in</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322647\" id=\"question-wrapper-322647\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Homer made engaging stories by using </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a3808add-cacb-4d94-a0d1-702b9f0aa47e","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"enduring purpose","passagePhrase":"principal objective"},{"uid":"0cc33e2e-9199-4245-8722-18b719086161","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"behind effective narration","passagePhrase":"behind all these tales"},{"uid":"4f947363-dcbc-46cf-a33f-3e52ab72ce17","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"difficulty of identifying the earliest tales","passagePhrase":"Finding the initial stories ever told"},{"uid":"2fce5390-a487-415d-8973-f183d811a6e8","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"analogy","passagePhrase":"herding cats"},{"uid":"569aaec1-5044-4ae0-b964-48947427eaf4","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"certain memory devices","passagePhrase":"symbols"},{"uid":"f219ac9a-1049-4061-9ab6-e8a9636f3a57","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"deliberate technique","passagePhrase":"system of"},{"uid":"569aaec1-5044-4ae0-b964-48947427eaf4 f219ac9a-1049-4061-9ab6-e8a9636f3a57","qNum":"15 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"reminders or mnemonics"},{"uid":"7a92d54a-0c80-4682-ae92-26becf58bb59","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"retain large pieces of information","passagePhrase":"recall specific information"},{"uid":"147962e9-8b70-49dc-ae62-d884a00cf6cb","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"a physical device","passagePhrase":"a notched memory stick"},{"uid":"9fbbb739-164a-4f44-a2ec-1ff8da4e9dbd","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"assist storytellers' memory","passagePhrase":"assistance in successive stages of recitation"},{"uid":"c91a19b6-c3af-45fd-b0b4-2ae0a366b862","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"emergence of writing","passagePhrase":"led to the invention or development of writing systems"},{"uid":"af35f001-3f20-4982-b731-f70b7249cefc","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Material methods","passagePhrase":"parchment ... papyrus ... birch-bark scrolls"},{"uid":"516bb96e-8994-4c71-9014-74b119965a80","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"adopted across many cultures","passagePhrase":"many ancient civilisations ... Egypt ... Ojibway Indians"},{"uid":"12fdefd4-371e-4c0f-9ba6-3938fde255a4 5cc8068d-f25f-46d7-b018-50723db3ad2e","qNum":"18 21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"conventional patterns"},{"uid":"12fdefd4-371e-4c0f-9ba6-3938fde255a4","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"endurance of core storytelling principles","passagePhrase":"instilled ... for ages are indispensable"},{"uid":"412cb4da-2f10-49a5-8836-7cfd27ce6f50","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"modern audiences","passagePhrase":"aspiring screenwriter"},{"uid":"1df304d1-b195-4a44-b4ef-cf6e5da881a4","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"help engage","passagePhrase":"look up to"},{"uid":"49464e56-08fe-459b-8aaa-9fde07a708ee","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"ancient","passagePhrase":"the fourth-century"},{"uid":"a7e27fc7-46b2-47df-91b0-dc508a5dc00c","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"strong emotional responses","passagePhrase":"horror, grief, astonishment or ecstasy"},{"uid":"01187464-cc5e-4dfd-a285-2afe0d25dffc","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"to events known to be fictional","passagePhrase":"knowing that it is all fiction"},{"uid":"ef41b6ae-6114-4aa4-8350-d0c8b571847d","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"dramas containing either ... or stories with","passagePhrase":"tragedy and comedy"},{"uid":"64af0065-3d14-4bde-b1ed-20e2a4925042","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"gloom"},{"uid":"99abb3b5-7b50-4f25-97d2-1e0df1b00c03","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"glee"},{"uid":"1ebcb604-7bd8-441d-bc4a-faf6ed2e5558","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"admirable qualities","passagePhrase":"powerful and majestic"},{"uid":"30b950ce-cb62-481f-ad2f-936c37c0a622","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"controversial behaviour","passagePhrase":"sulk, quarrel, cheat, and whine"},{"uid":"5cc8068d-f25f-46d7-b018-50723db3ad2e","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Old impulses","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"64af0065-3d14-4bde-b1ed-20e2a4925042 ef41b6ae-6114-4aa4-8350-d0c8b571847d","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"sorrowful events","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"99abb3b5-7b50-4f25-97d2-1e0df1b00c03 ef41b6ae-6114-4aa4-8350-d0c8b571847d","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"cheerful endings","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_45":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>Putting the brakes on climate change</span></b></p><p><i><span>Are hydrogen cars the answer?</span></i></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> It is tempting to treat the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"3a472a52-833d-4a51-870f-6c9c603f7830\">survival of coral reefs and rainforests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> as a concern remote from traffic queues and polluted urban air, but it is not — scientists are now confident that rapid changes in the Earth's climate are already disrupting and altering many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"3a472a52-833d-4a51-870f-6c9c603f7830\">wildlife habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c3e338fb-b3bf-4eae-b753-16e2d74213fd\">pollution from vehicles forming a significant part of the problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. The ramifications are not restricted to distant ecosystems, since the same carbon-intensive transport paradigm that warms seas and changes rainfall patterns also exposes city dwellers to harmful air and makes decarbonisation politically urgent.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change has warned that continued warming increases the likelihood of forest fires, drought-related dieback on land, and coral bleaching in increasingly warm oceans, while few species, if any, will remain immune to related changes in temperature, rainfall and sea level. In 2023, global energy-related carbon dioxide emissions reached about 37.4 gigatonnes, a scale that demonstrates why avoiding catastrophic disruption requires more than individual restraint: governments must slow deforestation while replacing coal, oil and gas, still the principal sources of energy in many economies, with credible alternatives.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> Several technologies can reduce or eliminate carbon dioxide generated during daily energy consumption: wind and solar power have expanded rapidly, battery electric cars are becoming commonplace, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7a4fb69d-11a7-4362-ae64-f49792c060aa\">hydrogen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> fuel cells have re-entered public debate. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7a4fb69d-11a7-4362-ae64-f49792c060aa\">Battery vehicles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> can be extremely efficient for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"49d1308d-3802-4580-8e5d-1a076d5226b1\">ordinary journeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, yet charging times, mineral supply chains and access to charging in dense cities may pose practical limitations for some users; hydrogen advocates therefore argue that rapid refuelling and long range could be useful for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"49d1308d-3802-4580-8e5d-1a076d5226b1\">buses, freight vehicles and other heavily used fleets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. Fuel-cell technology was invented in the nineteenth century, but because the motor industry concentrated on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a906ea22-fc1c-47c6-97e0-0138cf4bf030\">refining the combustion engine for mass production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, early designs <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"04b11493-fb96-45fa-8b3a-e9aa1a7aecc8\">did not become an established transport system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> In a modern fuel-cell car, whether a prototype or a commercially produced model, hydrogen is carried under pressure rather than stored solely in a large battery, while the vehicle resembles a conventional electric car in its quiet operation and responsive acceleration. Inside the cell, hydrogen combines electrochemically with oxygen to generate electricity for the motor, and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"64f081a5-3198-4cfa-bb3f-6711859091f2\">only tailpipe emission is water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>; unlike a battery, the cell does not run down while its supply of fuel continues. Systems of different sizes can power buses, backup generators or portable equipment, and fuel cells can achieve efficiencies of around 60 per cent, compared with approximately 20–30 per cent for a typical petrol-powered vehicle.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> The apparent cleanliness of the exhaust, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"ddf85374-3903-4326-bfec-632b2e0602b9\">does not settle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> the question of lifecycle emissions, because hydrogen is an energy carrier rather than a freely available source of energy. Water is an abundant source from which industry can exploit hydrogen through electrolysis, yet, when the electricity required for that process comes from a coal- or gas-fired station, the supposed climate benefit can shrink dramatically. At present, renewable electricity is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"845ee78c-2fde-4013-8b4d-297722c9112e\">not always sufficiently cheap<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> or continuously available for hydrogen to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"845ee78c-2fde-4013-8b4d-297722c9112e\">manufactured on the immense scale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> required for road transport <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"845ee78c-2fde-4013-8b4d-297722c9112e\">in an economically viable way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, with recent estimates placing green hydrogen production at approximately US$2.8–6.4 per kilogram rather than the US$1 target sought for competitive deployment.</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> A transitional route uses natural gas, separating methane into its constituent components of hydrogen and carbon dioxide, with the latter captured and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"7ebb9510-5d16-457b-b10c-57b7f680cf7c\">placed underground through so-called geological sequestration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Companies including Norway's Statoil, now Equinor, have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"f955b4d4-9169-4556-8898-120c7004937e\">stored carbon dioxide beneath the seabed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, and supporters propose this approach as a supply route pending cheaper renewable hydrogen. Whether public finance should assist such an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5b94e73d-b6bd-41a2-8ff9-84000d2f376b\">interim, gas-dependent option<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> or accelerate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"92f6bc74-1709-484d-89a1-9ac49ff37ef2\">fully renewable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> systems instead is ultimately a matter of policy priorities as well as technological feasibility.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> Critics also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"8830c20b-1797-4858-bfe6-6b6e6f3e8809\">challenge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the thermodynamic feasibility of hydrogen cars when electricity could be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"8daffb91-a4db-4faa-b2c0-32269e00efa8\">deployed more directly in battery vehicles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, since energy is lost in electrolysis, compression, distribution and its eventual reconversion inside the fuel cell. As one group of analysts puts it, “the energy required to produce, compress and distribute hydrogen makes the technology less efficient than direct electrification”, a criticism that does not make fuel cells useless but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"2881f618-a92f-45dc-adda-ff1b4fd6c017\">narrows the circumstances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in which their energy return on investment may justify the infrastructural cost. Hydrogen may therefore be more persuasive for vehicles that travel long distances, return predictably to depots, or cannot afford lengthy charging stops <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d5917fb9-a0c1-4055-a59a-84ec0e9d9971\">than for small privately owned cars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> used mainly on urban journeys.</span></p><p><b><span>H.</span></b><span> The market cannot solve that infrastructure problem simply by putting attractive vehicles in showrooms, because drivers will not buy cars without reliable stations and investors will not finance stations without assured demand. Although freak weather conditions have intensified pressure for action, a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"d4fc0891-a844-4585-9f7c-a3debe24ab7d\">nationwide hydrogen infrastructure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> rollout <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f116b50e-0284-489f-bb56-3a0ab3fcab96\">would require<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> coordinated standards, safe storage facilities and dependable fuel supplies; centrally managed bus fleets and courier vans offer a rational starting point because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"32ed8f5b-4515-4b44-b4ff-4250d85ffd1c\">a limited number of depots can serve many vehicles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> each day. This pattern identifies why public transport adoption is not merely a publicity exercise but a practical first step in testing reliability and reducing risk before any large consumer market can emerge.</span></p><p><b><span>I.</span></b><span> Policy makers, markets and engineers consequently face different, although connected, decisions: governments can fund research and set emissions standards, manufacturers in the automotive industry can improve durability and scalability, and purchasers can decide whether performance justifies cost. By 2024, more than 50 countries had published hydrogen strategies or road maps, yet policy ambition alone cannot guarantee technological readiness, affordable supply or low lifecycle emissions. Fuel-cell transport should therefore be treated <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"31a58c2e-4603-4a20-acd6-1d5e2ceb65a0\">neither as the sole solution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> nor as an expensive distraction: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"c4824a7c-ea37-41a5-aea3-9330913ed0f0\">supported alongside renewable electricity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, batteries and improved public transit, it could form <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"c4824a7c-ea37-41a5-aea3-9330913ed0f0\">one carefully targeted part of a long-term strategy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> for climate and wildlife protection.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter A–D in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322648\" id=\"question-wrapper-322648\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which relationship does the writer emphasise at the beginning of the passage?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Urban pollution should receive attention before the protection of remote ecosystems.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"3a472a52-833d-4a51-870f-6c9c603f7830\">Environmental damage in natural areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> is partly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c3e338fb-b3bf-4eae-b753-16e2d74213fd\">connected with emissions generated by road transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Changes to rainfall patterns are a greater threat to wildlife than increasing temperatures.</li> <li>D. Reducing private vehicle ownership is the only effective way to protect endangered habitats.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322649\" id=\"question-wrapper-322649\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why does the writer discuss several forms of cleaner transport technology in paragraph C?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. To suggest that motorists are increasingly unwilling to consider conventional vehicles</li> <li>B. To indicate that different <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7a4fb69d-11a7-4362-ae64-f49792c060aa\">low-carbon solutions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> may be appropriate for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"49d1308d-3802-4580-8e5d-1a076d5226b1\">different transport demands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></li> <li>C. To argue that manufacturers have underestimated the difficulties of producing electric vehicles</li> <li>D. To demonstrate that vehicles powered by batteries are likely to remain commercially dominant</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322650\" id=\"question-wrapper-322650\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which environmental benefit of fuel-cell vehicles is highlighted in paragraph D?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"64f081a5-3198-4cfa-bb3f-6711859091f2\">do not give off carbon dioxide while the car is in use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>B. They require fewer raw materials during the manufacturing process than other electric cars.</li> <li>C. They can operate efficiently without requiring any externally produced energy supply.</li> <li>D. They remove harmful pollutants already present in the surrounding atmosphere.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322651\" id=\"question-wrapper-322651\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What reservation does the writer raise about obtaining hydrogen from natural gas?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"92f6bc74-1709-484d-89a1-9ac49ff37ef2\">Directing resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> towards this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5b94e73d-b6bd-41a2-8ff9-84000d2f376b\">bridging solution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"92f6bc74-1709-484d-89a1-9ac49ff37ef2\">could delay greater reliance on energy systems not dependent on fossil gas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>B. The fuel produced in this way would be unsuitable for use in heavy commercial vehicles.</li> <li>C. The method is unlikely to attract investment from governments or energy companies.</li> <li>D. The process would force manufacturers to redesign fuel-cell engines completely.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322652\" id=\"question-wrapper-322652\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which conclusion does the writer draw after considering the efficiency criticism of hydrogen transport?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is most likely to succeed first among private drivers in large urban areas.</li> <li>B. Its technical disadvantages make it unsuitable for vehicles operated on demanding schedules.</li> <li>C. Its advantages may justify its use in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"2881f618-a92f-45dc-adda-ff1b4fd6c017\">particular transport operations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d5917fb9-a0c1-4055-a59a-84ec0e9d9971\">rather than in everyday private motoring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Its future depends principally on persuading consumers that it performs as well as petrol vehicles.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322653\" id=\"question-wrapper-322653\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why are bus and delivery fleets regarded as suitable early users of hydrogen vehicles?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Their operators can test new vehicles without having to provide regular services.</li> <li>B. Their fixed routes make them less dependent on the performance of the fuel itself.</li> <li>C. Their vehicles can obtain fuel through a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"32ed8f5b-4515-4b44-b4ff-4250d85ffd1c\">concentrated rather than widely dispersed supply system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Their organisations are more likely than private motorists to receive government subsidies.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Although a fuel-cell vehicle produces very little pollution from its exhaust, this alone does not show how environmentally friendly it is. To <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"ddf85374-3903-4326-bfec-632b2e0602b9\">judge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> its overall impact, we must consider its (33)__________, including pollution created before the fuel reaches the vehicle. When hydrogen is produced from natural gas, one suggested solution for the carbon dioxide released is (34)__________, where the gas is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"7ebb9510-5d16-457b-b10c-57b7f680cf7c\">stored underground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Critics also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"8daffb91-a4db-4faa-b2c0-32269e00efa8\">compare hydrogen with sending electricity directly to battery-powered vehicles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"8830c20b-1797-4858-bfe6-6b6e6f3e8809\">questioning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> its (35)__________ because energy is lost when hydrogen is produced, transported and converted back into electricity. Finally, because drivers need easy access to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"d4fc0891-a844-4585-9f7c-a3debe24ab7d\">fuel stations before hydrogen vehicles can become common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, a major (36)__________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f116b50e-0284-489f-bb56-3a0ab3fcab96\">would be needed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322654\" id=\"question-wrapper-322654\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">lifecycle emissions</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322655\" id=\"question-wrapper-322655\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(geological) sequestration</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322656\" id=\"question-wrapper-322656\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">thermodynamic feasibility</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322657\" id=\"question-wrapper-322657\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(hydrogen) infrastructure rollout</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322658\" id=\"question-wrapper-322658\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer suggests that fuel-cell vehicles <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"04b11493-fb96-45fa-8b3a-e9aa1a7aecc8\">became established<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> during the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a906ea22-fc1c-47c6-97e0-0138cf4bf030\">petrol-car era<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322659\" id=\"question-wrapper-322659\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Renewable hydrogen is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"845ee78c-2fde-4013-8b4d-297722c9112e\">not yet practical for large-scale transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322660\" id=\"question-wrapper-322660\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"f955b4d4-9169-4556-8898-120c7004937e\">Storing carbon dioxide underground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> carries significant safety risks.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322661\" id=\"question-wrapper-322661\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Hydrogen transport should be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"c4824a7c-ea37-41a5-aea3-9330913ed0f0\">part of a wider low-carbon strategy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"31a58c2e-4603-4a20-acd6-1d5e2ceb65a0\">not the only replacement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> for fossil-fuelled travel.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"3a472a52-833d-4a51-870f-6c9c603f7830","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Environmental damage in natural areas","passagePhrase":"survival of coral reefs and rainforests ... wildlife habitats"},{"uid":"c3e338fb-b3bf-4eae-b753-16e2d74213fd","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"connected with emissions generated by road transport","passagePhrase":"pollution from vehicles forming a significant part of the problem"},{"uid":"7a4fb69d-11a7-4362-ae64-f49792c060aa","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"low-carbon solutions","passagePhrase":"hydrogen ... Battery vehicles"},{"uid":"49d1308d-3802-4580-8e5d-1a076d5226b1","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"different transport demands","passagePhrase":"ordinary journeys ... buses, freight vehicles and other heavily used fleets"},{"uid":"a906ea22-fc1c-47c6-97e0-0138cf4bf030","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"petrol-car era","passagePhrase":"refining the combustion engine for mass production"},{"uid":"64f081a5-3198-4cfa-bb3f-6711859091f2","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"do not give off carbon dioxide while the car is in use","passagePhrase":"only tailpipe emission is water"},{"uid":"ddf85374-3903-4326-bfec-632b2e0602b9","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"judge","passagePhrase":"does not settle"},{"uid":"845ee78c-2fde-4013-8b4d-297722c9112e","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"not yet practical for large-scale transport","passagePhrase":"not always sufficiently cheap ... manufactured on the immense scale ... in an economically viable way"},{"uid":"7ebb9510-5d16-457b-b10c-57b7f680cf7c","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"stored underground","passagePhrase":"placed underground through so-called geological sequestration"},{"uid":"f955b4d4-9169-4556-8898-120c7004937e","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Storing carbon dioxide underground","passagePhrase":"stored carbon dioxide beneath the seabed"},{"uid":"5b94e73d-b6bd-41a2-8ff9-84000d2f376b","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"bridging solution","passagePhrase":"interim, gas-dependent option"},{"uid":"92f6bc74-1709-484d-89a1-9ac49ff37ef2","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Directing resources ... could delay greater reliance on energy systems not dependent on fossil gas","passagePhrase":"fully renewable"},{"uid":"8830c20b-1797-4858-bfe6-6b6e6f3e8809","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"questioning","passagePhrase":"challenge"},{"uid":"8daffb91-a4db-4faa-b2c0-32269e00efa8","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"compare hydrogen with sending electricity directly to battery-powered vehicles","passagePhrase":"deployed more directly in battery vehicles"},{"uid":"2881f618-a92f-45dc-adda-ff1b4fd6c017","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"particular transport operations","passagePhrase":"narrows the circumstances"},{"uid":"d5917fb9-a0c1-4055-a59a-84ec0e9d9971","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"rather than in everyday private motoring","passagePhrase":"than for small privately owned cars"},{"uid":"d4fc0891-a844-4585-9f7c-a3debe24ab7d","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"fuel stations before hydrogen vehicles can become common","passagePhrase":"nationwide hydrogen infrastructure"},{"uid":"f116b50e-0284-489f-bb56-3a0ab3fcab96","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"would be needed","passagePhrase":"would require"},{"uid":"32ed8f5b-4515-4b44-b4ff-4250d85ffd1c","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"concentrated rather than widely dispersed supply system","passagePhrase":"a limited number of depots can serve many vehicles"},{"uid":"31a58c2e-4603-4a20-acd6-1d5e2ceb65a0","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"not the only replacement","passagePhrase":"neither as the sole solution"},{"uid":"c4824a7c-ea37-41a5-aea3-9330913ed0f0","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"part of a wider low-carbon strategy","passagePhrase":"supported alongside renewable electricity ... one carefully targeted part of a long-term strategy"}]},"reading_u2_46":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Ancient societies classification</span></b></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> Sociologists and anthropologists classify societal groups according to their access to resources, prestige, and power. These factors help researchers understand how societies are organised and how authority is distributed among their members. Throughout history, scholars have generally recognised four main classifications of society. Although societies differ widely across regions and time periods, they can usually be grouped according to population size, economic organisation, and political structure. At the bottom end of the societal scale are clans, followed by tribes and chiefdoms, while states occupy the highest level. Clans are typically small and mobile, tribes are larger and often rely on farming or livestock, chiefdoms introduce ranked leadership, and states develop formal governments capable of collecting taxes, enforcing laws, and maintaining standing administrations.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>Clans consist of small groups of people who are typically hunters or gatherers. People in a group tend to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"8ecabe6c-98dd-4d35-8950-183c9e207337\">number fewer than 100<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> and hold no specific home, which allows for flexibility in exploiting wild food resources. Members of clans are typically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"8d5e419a-f1c1-4c86-9873-ca4c64c078eb\">related to each other<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> through marriage or descent, and the group as a whole does not possess any formal ranks of leadership. Consequently, economic disparity between members is virtually non-existent because most individuals perform similar activities and enjoy comparable access to resources. Archaeologists believe that this form of social organisation was the dominant human lifestyle for tens of thousands of years before the emergence of agriculture approximately 12,000 years ago.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>Today there are relatively few societal groups that fit this profile, and most have been relegated to remote regions. One well-known example is the Hadza of northern Tanzania, whose population numbers approximately 1,300 people. Researchers estimate that groups with a lifestyle similar to that of the Hadza have existed in East Africa for more than 10,000 years. Experts consider such communities particularly important because they provide valuable insight into how humans survived before farming became widespread. The Hadza <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6a1d947a-aba3-453d-a4bc-3eaef4dd8e2f\">continue to use many methods that resemble those employed by their distant ancestors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8c4dc9e4-d5b4-4b67-867e-8354204f31d9\">hunt animals with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> hand-made bows and arrows and construct shelters from dried grass and branches. As was the case centuries ago, they possess very few possessions, especially when compared with their modern-day counterparts in industrialised societies.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> Clans are also highly mobile, and their temporary homes often consist of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"01996c43-3256-4b62-ab42-6a0842872f99\">seasonally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> occupied camps and other specialised sites that may be used only during certain times of the year. One feature that remains consistent is their tendency to seek out areas where large mammals can be killed and butchered. Equally important is access to locations containing suitable raw materials for making tools or carrying out other sensitive activities. Archaeological evidence from numerous continents indicates that mobile camps of this kind <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"732b85f9-5d8e-43a6-8de8-46dfa790e810\">remained common until agriculture gradually replaced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> hunting and gathering as the dominant means of subsistence.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Tribes are generally larger than mobile hunter-gatherer clans, and it is common for such groups to include populations ranging from 2,000 to more than 10,000 people. They tend to nourish themselves primarily through cultivated plants and domesticated animals. Members of tribal societies are often farmers, although <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"b649eaeb-042c-4a41-ac75-b5028a8a4bd4\">some remain nomadic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, maintaining a mobile economy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"da7bb8fe-7be8-4f9f-8937-a1e939c86e74\">based on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the exploitation of livestock. Tribes are usually multi-community societies whose separate settlements are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"6e1e4d91-902c-475a-85ce-5646de47e1f4\">integrated into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the larger group through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e6fcc16d-e591-4319-a150-dc0f91a2aa7c\">strong kinship ties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Archaeological evidence of tribal societies has been discovered in many parts of the world. Examples include the first farming communities of the Danube Valley, where agriculture appeared around 5500 BC, the Pueblos of the American Southwest, and Catalhoyuk in present-day Turkey, which dates to approximately 7500 BC. Although some tribes possess officials and even a central settlement functioning as a capital, these leaders generally lack the economic base required for the effective exercise of power.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>Chiefs are ranked according to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"e0cce59e-073f-4ee2-b5d9-7bb8da0786c5\">prestige<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, with senior members enjoying greater authority than others. The highest-ranking chiefs are responsible for governing society, and prestige is largely <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7a51e7d5-8050-42a9-bae7-d0dd301f7613\">determined by how closely an individual is related to a senior chief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. Despite these distinctions, there is no complete stratification into separate social classes. Chiefs often reside in centres of power and enjoy access to luxuries unavailable to most members of society, particularly temples and residences. Their privileged position is further reinforced through the receipt of surplus food and local craft products, which are paid as tribute by ordinary people. In some documented chiefdoms, households contributed several kilograms of grain or other produce annually. Chiefs could retain a portion of these resources for themselves, redistribute them among followers, or use them to support workers and specialists. Chiefdoms vary considerably in size, but populations commonly range between 5,000 and 20,000 people.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> Statesmen share many characteristics with chiefs but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d29af39f-e199-45ae-abf2-503906a2bc63\">differ in one crucial respect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. Statesmen often possess <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d8df87b4-df69-47ef-864e-6f442afe2882\">absolute authority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> as kings or queens, granting them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d8df87b4-df69-47ef-864e-6f442afe2882\">explicit power<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> to create laws and enforce them through armed forces. The ruling lineage is generally regarded as the ultimate owner of the land, and its luxuries extend far beyond the temples enjoyed by chiefs. Such systems are sustained by lower-ranking members of society who have an obligation to pay taxes. In some ancient states, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"1cb5dcf4-da0f-40a7-8282-4a8acb6582f7\">agricultural taxes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> could amount to approximately 10 percent of annual production. Statesmen are typically located close to capitals, where a bureaucratic administration oversees the collection of revenue and the management of key responsibilities. This centralised structure facilitates the distribution of resources to government officials, military personnel, and craft specialists. Early states developed increasingly sophisticated redistribution systems in order to support essential services and ensure the efficient functioning of government.</span></p><p><b><span>H.</span></b><span> Elman Service, William Sanders, and Joseph Marino are among the scholars most closely associated with the study of social hierarchy. Service, in particular, developed an influential framework that helped organise anthropological thinking about societal development. Through a series of books and academic papers, he proposed what became known as the managerial-benefits theory. This theory hypothesises that societies organised into four levels of hierarchy and governed through centralised leadership were ultimately beneficial to their members. According to Service, leaders provided services and protections that increased in complexity as societies expanded and became more sophisticated. His research also led him to conclude that class conflict was largely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"22be030a-52ea-420f-84b5-c7555bd7719b\">absent from ancient civilisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. Rather than being compelled by force, many people willingly carried out social obligations because they believed the system benefited the wider community. Service further argued that political competition and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"c7c43e81-7fd5-422b-a776-76a5adfdc0b4\">conflict occurred primarily among members of the political elite<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE If the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE If the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN If there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322662\" id=\"question-wrapper-322662\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Clans usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"8ecabe6c-98dd-4d35-8950-183c9e207337\">comprise a restricted number of individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322668\" id=\"question-wrapper-322668\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Hadza <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6a1d947a-aba3-453d-a4bc-3eaef4dd8e2f\">no longer rely on their customary ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of surviving.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322663\" id=\"question-wrapper-322663\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Temporary settlements <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"732b85f9-5d8e-43a6-8de8-46dfa790e810\">became more widespread after<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the rise of agriculture.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322664\" id=\"question-wrapper-322664\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e6fcc16d-e591-4319-a150-dc0f91a2aa7c\">Shared family ties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> are the means by which tribal groups <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"6e1e4d91-902c-475a-85ce-5646de47e1f4\">remain connected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322665\" id=\"question-wrapper-322665\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In chiefdoms, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"e0cce59e-073f-4ee2-b5d9-7bb8da0786c5\">social standing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7a51e7d5-8050-42a9-bae7-d0dd301f7613\">gained mainly through a person’s wealth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322666\" id=\"question-wrapper-322666\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In some early states, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"1cb5dcf4-da0f-40a7-8282-4a8acb6582f7\">revenue from taxes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> was collected every month.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322667\" id=\"question-wrapper-322667\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to Service, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"c7c43e81-7fd5-422b-a776-76a5adfdc0b4\">conflict mainly took place between rulers and ordinary people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322669\" id=\"question-wrapper-322669\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In clans, what forms of relationship commonly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"8d5e419a-f1c1-4c86-9873-ca4c64c078eb\">bind members<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">marriage or descent</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322670\" id=\"question-wrapper-322670\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What implement do the Hadza <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8c4dc9e4-d5b4-4b67-867e-8354204f31d9\">employ to capture prey<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">bows and arrows</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322671\" id=\"question-wrapper-322671\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What type of accommodations were occupied by mobile groups during <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"01996c43-3256-4b62-ab42-6a0842872f99\">specific seasons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(seasonally occupied) camps [OR] (mobile) camps</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322672\" id=\"question-wrapper-322672\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What resource do <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"b649eaeb-042c-4a41-ac75-b5028a8a4bd4\">some nomadic groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"da7bb8fe-7be8-4f9f-8937-a1e939c86e74\">depend on for their livelihood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">livestock</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322673\" id=\"question-wrapper-322673\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d8df87b4-df69-47ef-864e-6f442afe2882\">feature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d29af39f-e199-45ae-abf2-503906a2bc63\">distinguishes statesmen from chiefs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">absolute authority [OR] explicit power</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322674\" id=\"question-wrapper-322674\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What did Service discover to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"22be030a-52ea-420f-84b5-c7555bd7719b\">missing in ancient civilisations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">class conflict</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"8ecabe6c-98dd-4d35-8950-183c9e207337","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"comprise a restricted number of individuals","passagePhrase":"number fewer than 100"},{"uid":"8d5e419a-f1c1-4c86-9873-ca4c64c078eb","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"bind members","passagePhrase":"related to each other"},{"uid":"8c4dc9e4-d5b4-4b67-867e-8354204f31d9","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"employ to capture prey","passagePhrase":"hunt animals with"},{"uid":"01996c43-3256-4b62-ab42-6a0842872f99","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"specific seasons","passagePhrase":"seasonally"},{"uid":"b649eaeb-042c-4a41-ac75-b5028a8a4bd4","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"some nomadic groups","passagePhrase":"some remain nomadic"},{"uid":"da7bb8fe-7be8-4f9f-8937-a1e939c86e74","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"depend on for their livelihood","passagePhrase":"based on"},{"uid":"6e1e4d91-902c-475a-85ce-5646de47e1f4","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"remain connected","passagePhrase":"integrated into"},{"uid":"e6fcc16d-e591-4319-a150-dc0f91a2aa7c","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Shared family ties","passagePhrase":"strong kinship ties"},{"uid":"e0cce59e-073f-4ee2-b5d9-7bb8da0786c5","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"social standing","passagePhrase":"prestige"},{"uid":"d29af39f-e199-45ae-abf2-503906a2bc63","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"distinguishes statesmen from chiefs","passagePhrase":"differ in one crucial respect"},{"uid":"d8df87b4-df69-47ef-864e-6f442afe2882","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"feature","passagePhrase":"absolute authority ... explicit power"},{"uid":"1cb5dcf4-da0f-40a7-8282-4a8acb6582f7","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"revenue from taxes","passagePhrase":"agricultural taxes"},{"uid":"22be030a-52ea-420f-84b5-c7555bd7719b","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"missing in ancient civilisations","passagePhrase":"absent from ancient civilisation"}]},"reading_u2_47":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Nutrition and Education</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>At the Msekeni Primary School in Malawi, children are gathered under the shade of yellow-blossomed acacia trees for their lessons. There are not enough classrooms for every class at the school, but even so, one purpose-built classroom has been emptied and turned into a storeroom for sacks of grain. Here in Malawi, it is clear that food matters more than shelter.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Malawi is a landlocked southern African country of great beauty and even greater poverty, and Msekeni is one of its poorer regions. Malawians are fortunate not to be experiencing the problems of war, overcrowding, or infertile ground, but still, they have trouble finding enough food to eat. Half of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"57998011-c7ca-4739-81f7-daf783033e7c\">children under five<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> years of age are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b6e52197-625b-458c-9a48-d7da3e19280b\">underfed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to the point of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"31b2d7d6-48ea-4a45-977b-bd6f9a81a31f\">stunting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"883068ab-7659-401d-a0ca-949f8aba427c\">their growth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Hunger affects most aspects of Malawian life, so the country is an excellent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"94075273-082d-4fd7-8c31-bcc053fe49a5\">subject for research into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> how nutrition and development are intertwined.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span>Bernard Kumanda is the headmaster at the Msekeni school, and he has strong views on the topic. Kumanda stated that food is essential to learning, and since 1999, his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"22a5acd8-07d8-4c6f-bf23-f091c4aea8e8\">students have been receiving free school lunches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of grain made up of mixed maize and soybean flour, enriched with vitamin A, which is donated through the World Food programme. Local <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"a5ab884e-1cb6-4a4e-9427-4a35a75a1155\">volunteers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> do the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"37a57f99-2f7d-4526-852a-d22bcc864850\">cooking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"a19f80ae-86fc-40d2-b8e3-124ab8baa977\">turning the dry grain into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"e8ea8d21-f902-49be-ba10-7d25609cdffc\">a bland yet nutritious porridge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> to be spooned out onto plastic plates. The children eagerly line up for their share, often singing a cheerful song they call “We are getting porridge”.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span>Interestingly, the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4887a319-70bd-4b2c-ab43-06148dfc7ef3\">enrolment of students at the Msekeni school </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 22\" data-uid=\"4887a319-70bd-4b2c-ab43-06148dfc7ef3 6bac095f-b54f-4100-b8f3-ee12349292df\">doubled</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> when the school's food programme was introduced. A number of pupils transferred from other nearby schools, but most new <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"a737f9d3-ddaa-4562-9b30-d75a36f5baf8\">enrolment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>s were children whose families had previously kept them at home to work. These families were so poor that the long-term benefits of educating their children paled against the short-term gain of sending their children out to work in the fields or to gather firewood. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4887a319-70bd-4b2c-ab43-06148dfc7ef3\">offer of one plate of porridge a day at school completely altered the situation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. On average, when a school in Malawi starts providing free food, there is a 38% <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"fc069a2f-3190-483b-8d3f-b56a17691b03\">rise in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"2cc9b2b6-d079-424e-9ee5-10ae2f3916ae\">attendance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of girls and 24% in boys. A child receiving food at school will not cry so plaintively for food at home. As an extra incentive, girls, who are more likely than boys to be kept at home, are even given extra snacks to take home.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> You would expect that a school suddenly taking on significantly more students from poor homes would see a decrease in pass marks, because in most parts of the world, students from poor homes tend to perform worse than those from more prosperous backgrounds. Combining the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"dbd64085-8a54-44e2-b2be-407ff4e9bf19\">influx of students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in Msekeni with no increase in teacher numbers, you would expect the pass rates to fall even further. However, in the case of Msekeni, the opposite has proved true. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9156b30d-45e0-464a-9244-df9c5027a196\">Pass rates have actually improved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> from 30% to 85%. Although this is a particularly dramatic example of rises in pass rates, national data show that the results of school food programmes are good overall. While the pass rates for boys tend to remain the same, the rates for girls increase by 9.5%. The fact that the effect of feeding is more pronounced in girls than in boys gives a clue to who is eating first in Malawian households – it isn’t the girls.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>F. </span></b><span>Better <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"13e06c22-9f7c-4e52-b4eb-91a6bf884d00\">nutrition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> generally means <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"98fe4674-3993-492e-be4b-165a68d4923f\">brighter children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Almost immediately, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"1b0c2318-bf8d-45e9-be59-0221d4a439c0\">well-fed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> children find it easier to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"8a35efee-658e-49b3-8d71-9e1975dd2083\">concentrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> on their lessons – it can be well imagined what would happen to a child if his stomach is always crying out for food. “It would be easy to identify children who were critically undernourished. They were the ones who stared into space and didn’t respond when you asked them questions, ”Kumanda says. Even more importantly, though, sufficient nutritious food helps young brains grow and develop. Like all organs, the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"98fe4674-3993-492e-be4b-165a68d4923f\">brain needs both </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 25\" data-uid=\"98fe4674-3993-492e-be4b-165a68d4923f f0319bea-b935-4725-9e75-3fe9db183cff\">exercise</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"98fe4674-3993-492e-be4b-165a68d4923f\"> and nutrition</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Lacking necessary calories, protein, and micronutrients, its growth will be stunted, just like the growth of muscles. This is why feeding children at school makes such a dramatic impact.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"19\"><b><span>G. </span></b><span>Three hundred years ago, chronic malnutrition was more or less a worldwide problem. However, now, on a global scale, people are eating better than ever before. Humans grow to around 50% larger than before the industrial revolution, and malnutrition is extremely rare in rich countries. Even in developing countries, where the majority of Earth's population lives, plates and bowls are fuller than ever before. The percentage of children under the age of five in developing countries who are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"54a05662-eb16-4a86-9e8c-d19d556b09bc\">malnourished fell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> from 39% in 1990 to 30% in 2000, according to the World Health Organization. In other places, too, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"54a05662-eb16-4a86-9e8c-d19d556b09bc\">fight against hunger appears to be quite successful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Better nutrition has the effect of making people smarter and more energetic, which in turn helps them to grow more prosperous. And ironically, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"b3185268-f257-4ddf-ba39-3997a81c7bc7\">going from poor to well-off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, people suddenly start to worry about becoming <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"daac9e58-c8da-4f6e-bb9f-a3ccb8f475e6\">obese<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs B-G from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"22a5acd8-07d8-4c6f-bf23-f091c4aea8e8\">The beneficiary of a food programme<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4887a319-70bd-4b2c-ab43-06148dfc7ef3\">Food as a motivational factor in attending school<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9156b30d-45e0-464a-9244-df9c5027a196\">Higher pass rates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"dbd64085-8a54-44e2-b2be-407ff4e9bf19\">an increase in the number of students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. Reasons to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"94075273-082d-4fd7-8c31-bcc053fe49a5\">focus research on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> Malawi</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"98fe4674-3993-492e-be4b-165a68d4923f\">What contributes to the development of intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. The dangers of malnutrition for poor families</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. The importance of food in Malawi</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. The problems of free school meals</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"54a05662-eb16-4a86-9e8c-d19d556b09bc\">Winning in the war against malnutrition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p><b><span>Example Answer</span></b></p><p><span>Paragraph A vii</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322675\" id=\"question-wrapper-322675\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322676\" id=\"question-wrapper-322676\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322677\" id=\"question-wrapper-322677\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322678\" id=\"question-wrapper-322678\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322679\" id=\"question-wrapper-322679\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322680\" id=\"question-wrapper-322680\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph G</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ix</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below. Choose ONE option from the list, A-J, for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A-J, in boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>List of Words</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. academic performance </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"e8ea8d21-f902-49be-ba10-7d25609cdffc\">cooked cereal meal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. family income</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"883068ab-7659-401d-a0ca-949f8aba427c\">physical development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"2cc9b2b6-d079-424e-9ee5-10ae2f3916ae\">lesson presence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. food shortage</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"f0319bea-b935-4725-9e75-3fe9db183cff\">cognitive activity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"a737f9d3-ddaa-4562-9b30-d75a36f5baf8\">pupil registration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"daac9e58-c8da-4f6e-bb9f-a3ccb8f475e6\">excessive weight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"J\"><span>J. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"8a35efee-658e-49b3-8d71-9e1975dd2083\">mental engagement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322681\" id=\"question-wrapper-322681\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In Malawi, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b6e52197-625b-458c-9a48-d7da3e19280b\">poor diet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> among the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"57998011-c7ca-4739-81f7-daf783033e7c\">youngest children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> is serious enough to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"31b2d7d6-48ea-4a45-977b-bd6f9a81a31f\">hold back their normal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> (20)______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322682\" id=\"question-wrapper-322682\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>At Msekeni school, donated grain is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"37a57f99-2f7d-4526-852a-d22bcc864850\">prepared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> by local <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"a5ab884e-1cb6-4a4e-9427-4a35a75a1155\">helpers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"a19f80ae-86fc-40d2-b8e3-124ab8baa977\">served as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> (21)______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322683\" id=\"question-wrapper-322683\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The introduction of school meals at Msekeni led to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6bac095f-b54f-4100-b8f3-ee12349292df\">a doubling of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> (22)______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322684\" id=\"question-wrapper-322684\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In Malawian schools, providing meals has been linked to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"fc069a2f-3190-483b-8d3f-b56a17691b03\">higher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> (23)______ among both boys and girls.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322685\" id=\"question-wrapper-322685\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Children who are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"1b0c2318-bf8d-45e9-be59-0221d4a439c0\">properly fed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> generally show greater (24)______ with their lessons.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">J</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322686\" id=\"question-wrapper-322686\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>For the brain to develop fully, it requires not only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"13e06c22-9f7c-4e52-b4eb-91a6bf884d00\">nourishment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> but also (25)______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322687\" id=\"question-wrapper-322687\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>After <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"b3185268-f257-4ddf-ba39-3997a81c7bc7\">moving from poverty to greater prosperity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, people may begin to worry about becoming (26)______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"57998011-c7ca-4739-81f7-daf783033e7c","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"youngest children","passagePhrase":"children under five"},{"uid":"b6e52197-625b-458c-9a48-d7da3e19280b","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"poor diet","passagePhrase":"underfed"},{"uid":"31b2d7d6-48ea-4a45-977b-bd6f9a81a31f","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"hold back their normal","passagePhrase":"stunting"},{"uid":"883068ab-7659-401d-a0ca-949f8aba427c","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"physical development","passagePhrase":"their growth"},{"uid":"94075273-082d-4fd7-8c31-bcc053fe49a5","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"focus research on","passagePhrase":"subject for research into"},{"uid":"22a5acd8-07d8-4c6f-bf23-f091c4aea8e8","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"The beneficiary of a food programme","passagePhrase":"students have been receiving free school lunches"},{"uid":"a5ab884e-1cb6-4a4e-9427-4a35a75a1155","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"helpers","passagePhrase":"volunteers"},{"uid":"37a57f99-2f7d-4526-852a-d22bcc864850","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"prepared","passagePhrase":"cooking"},{"uid":"a19f80ae-86fc-40d2-b8e3-124ab8baa977","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"served as","passagePhrase":"turning the dry grain into"},{"uid":"e8ea8d21-f902-49be-ba10-7d25609cdffc","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"cooked cereal meal","passagePhrase":"a bland yet nutritious porridge"},{"uid":"4887a319-70bd-4b2c-ab43-06148dfc7ef3","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Food as a motivational factor in attending school","passagePhrase":"enrolment of students at the Msekeni school ... offer of one plate of porridge a day at school completely altered the situation"},{"uid":"4887a319-70bd-4b2c-ab43-06148dfc7ef3 6bac095f-b54f-4100-b8f3-ee12349292df","qNum":"16 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"doubled"},{"uid":"a737f9d3-ddaa-4562-9b30-d75a36f5baf8","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"pupil registration","passagePhrase":"enrolment"},{"uid":"fc069a2f-3190-483b-8d3f-b56a17691b03","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"higher","passagePhrase":"rise in"},{"uid":"2cc9b2b6-d079-424e-9ee5-10ae2f3916ae","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"lesson presence","passagePhrase":"attendance"},{"uid":"dbd64085-8a54-44e2-b2be-407ff4e9bf19","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"an increase in the number of students","passagePhrase":"influx of students"},{"uid":"9156b30d-45e0-464a-9244-df9c5027a196","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Higher pass rates","passagePhrase":"Pass rates have actually improved"},{"uid":"13e06c22-9f7c-4e52-b4eb-91a6bf884d00","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"nourishment","passagePhrase":"nutrition"},{"uid":"98fe4674-3993-492e-be4b-165a68d4923f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"What contributes to the development of intelligence","passagePhrase":"brighter children ... brain needs both ... and nutrition"},{"uid":"1b0c2318-bf8d-45e9-be59-0221d4a439c0","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"properly fed","passagePhrase":"well-fed"},{"uid":"8a35efee-658e-49b3-8d71-9e1975dd2083","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"mental engagement","passagePhrase":"concentrate"},{"uid":"98fe4674-3993-492e-be4b-165a68d4923f f0319bea-b935-4725-9e75-3fe9db183cff","qNum":"18 25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"exercise"},{"uid":"54a05662-eb16-4a86-9e8c-d19d556b09bc","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Winning in the war against malnutrition","passagePhrase":"malnourished fell ... fight against hunger appears to be quite successful"},{"uid":"b3185268-f257-4ddf-ba39-3997a81c7bc7","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"moving from poverty to greater prosperity","passagePhrase":"going from poor to well-off"},{"uid":"daac9e58-c8da-4f6e-bb9f-a3ccb8f475e6","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"excessive weight","passagePhrase":"obese"},{"uid":"f0319bea-b935-4725-9e75-3fe9db183cff","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"cognitive activity","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"6bac095f-b54f-4100-b8f3-ee12349292df","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"a doubling of","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_48":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Marketing and The Information Age</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>For the early practitioners of marketing in the late 19th and early 20th centuries, the business of selling was simply a matter of continually finding new customers. By contrast, marketing managers in the current era recognise the importance of gathering information about the market and about potential customers. They recognise that if companies are to be profitable, customers must gain and retain their perceptions of value from the brands they buy over a long time frame, rather than from a single transaction. This also means that customers must see value in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"6606a50f-c40b-4db7-a082-2a479baf0eaf\">returning continually to the stores<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> where they shop, as well as to the service providers they deal with.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Marketing practitioners and marketing scientists have never worked more closely than they currently do. There are many reasons for this, including the fact that this is the information age where convergence in telecommunications, media and technology is causing old ways to be challenged, and new methods and tools to be tested. Customer expectations have risen as new technologies allow new approaches. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"bbd55539-128a-4f9f-aab5-11c81927f0cc\">For instance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, the subscriber-TV music channel Channel V encourages its viewers to sign up for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"5d4f8841-0ce6-4908-b01b-c52af45818d2\">text messages and email alerts that tell them when their favourite artists and songs are about to be broadcast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Competitive advantage lies in being able to recognise which customers can be given greater attention, not just because they demand it but because it makes commercial sense to provide high levels of product quality and service.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> Modern marketing information systems rely on information technology to enable marketing intelligence to be gathered and to store and analyse marketing research information. While some of the information used is gathered by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"77ac0590-b53b-483b-9887-74b32c52be3f\">government bodies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> such as the Australian Bureau of Statistics and Statistics New Zealand, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c1ce6c03-292f-4c5d-8f2c-3c0c7b0f99a3\">most of it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> is purposefully gathered by <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1f8ebc08-9747-4ef2-8de5-9be3e640ddc9\">marketing organisations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> for client companies. In the process, computer technology is used to manipulate the data and then to present the information in such a way that executives can readily identify any problems or issues, and quickly arrive at solutions.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>In order to produce superior value and satisfaction for customers, marketing managers need information at almost every turn. They need information about customers – end-users and resellers – as well as competitors and governmental and other forces in the marketplace. One marketing executive put it this way: ‘To manage a business well is to manage its future; and to manage the future is to manage information.’ Increasingly, marketers are viewing information not just as an input for making better decisions but also as an important strategic asset and marketing tool. As <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"bd5abf7d-17b2-45be-899a-8360731c156c\">household incomes increase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"7d2768ee-1f8b-4ee7-a02f-33fb763889ed\">choice widens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> and buyers become <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"7d2768ee-1f8b-4ee7-a02f-33fb763889ed\">better at discriminating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, so sellers need information about how buyers respond to different products and advertising campaigns.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> The supply of information has also increased greatly. It has been suggested by the futurist and best-selling author John Naisbitt that the United States and, by observation, developed countries such as Australia, New Zealand and Singapore are moving from industrial to information-based economies. These post-industrial economies earn 70–80% of their Gross Domestic Product from services, and have entered what some commentators have termed the ‘Information Age’ or the ‘Information Technology Era’.</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> One study found that with all the information now available through supermarket scanners, a packaged-goods product controller is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"56a8a889-e66e-482e-8104-a8a2b01431eb\">bombarded with one million to one billion new numbers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> each week. As Naisbitt points out: ‘Running out of information is not a problem, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"56a8a889-e66e-482e-8104-a8a2b01431eb\">drowning in it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> is.’ Yet marketers frequently complain that they lack information of the right kind but have plenty of the wrong kind, or they claim that marketing information is so widely spread throughout the organisation that it takes great effort to locate even simple facts. In addition, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"796e11eb-1ef9-4e7c-a241-793fb4d85571\">subordinates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"a18f0caa-1682-45d8-acaa-83c4509cc089\">withhold<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> information they believe will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"aa258456-69a9-4c00-af29-ddfa63e3d278\">reflect badly on their performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> and important information often arrives too late to be useful, or on-time information is not accurate. So marketing managers need better information. Although marketing organisations have greater capacity to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"de59a07f-3c9d-47d7-b63d-67608ff6e65d\">provide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> managers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"de59a07f-3c9d-47d7-b63d-67608ff6e65d\">with information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, they often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"83c2e720-8e68-46be-ace1-b090190bf239\">do not use it well<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. As a result, many marketing organisations are now studying their managers’ information needs and designing information systems specifically to meet those needs.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> One solution is to use a Marketing Information System (MIS). This consists of people, equipment, and procedures which, when put together, are able to gather, analyse, evaluate and distribute needed, timely, and accurate information to marketing decision-makers. The MIS begins and ends with marketing managers. First, it interacts with these managers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"8407f321-c0e6-497c-bfe6-fa8771608209\">assess<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> the information needs <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ba2c2753-8e3b-4f58-88f4-01155363939d\">they have<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. Next, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"ecda0a64-cc7e-4cd5-b9fe-31682846a657\">develops the needed information from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> internal records, marketing intelligence activities, and the research process. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"d5a7f179-22cc-45d6-91d7-fd97e83e0af6\">The analysis unit processes the data<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to make it more useful, and finally, the MIS distributes it to managers in the right form and at the right time to help them make better marketing decisions.</span></p><p><b><span>H. </span></b><span>However, the costs of obtaining, processing, storing and delivering information can mount quickly. In some cases, additional information will do little to change or improve a manager’s decision, or the costs of the information will exceed the returns from the improved decision. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"229b3c13-27b6-494c-9e4e-57e697937fe1\">For example<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, if an organisation estimates that launching a new product without any further information will yield a profit of $500,000, then it would be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"71a4f82c-3c5b-4fed-9392-b8590430d158\">foolish to spend $30,000 for additional information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that would increase the profit to only $525,000. By itself, information is valueless – its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"b270572d-3e0d-4d7e-a7d7-6d4b4475f5fa\">value comes from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"238e00b8-ff8a-494e-95e7-4a6e00a91246\">its use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has eight paragraphs, A–H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322688\" id=\"question-wrapper-322688\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the fact that there may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"56a8a889-e66e-482e-8104-a8a2b01431eb\">too much information to cope with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322689\" id=\"question-wrapper-322689\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the relevance of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"6606a50f-c40b-4db7-a082-2a479baf0eaf\">generating repeat business<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322690\" id=\"question-wrapper-322690\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"bbd55539-128a-4f9f-aab5-11c81927f0cc\">example<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"5d4f8841-0ce6-4908-b01b-c52af45818d2\">personalised marketing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322691\" id=\"question-wrapper-322691\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"229b3c13-27b6-494c-9e4e-57e697937fe1\">illustration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of a situation where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"71a4f82c-3c5b-4fed-9392-b8590430d158\">commissioning new information research might not be advisable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322692\" id=\"question-wrapper-322692\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>how the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"bd5abf7d-17b2-45be-899a-8360731c156c\">greater wealth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of customers enables them to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"7d2768ee-1f8b-4ee7-a02f-33fb763889ed\">select from a broader range of products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 32–36 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322693\" id=\"question-wrapper-322693\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c1ce6c03-292f-4c5d-8f2c-3c0c7b0f99a3\">The majority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of marketing statistics are collected through <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1f8ebc08-9747-4ef2-8de5-9be3e640ddc9 77ac0590-b53b-483b-9887-74b32c52be3f\">state-run agencies</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322694\" id=\"question-wrapper-322694\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>New Zealand’s information economy is ahead of Australia’s.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322695\" id=\"question-wrapper-322695\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"796e11eb-1ef9-4e7c-a241-793fb4d85571\">Employees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> sometimes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"a18f0caa-1682-45d8-acaa-83c4509cc089\">suppress<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> findings that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"aa258456-69a9-4c00-af29-ddfa63e3d278\">give a poor impression of them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322696\" id=\"question-wrapper-322696\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Managers often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"83c2e720-8e68-46be-ace1-b090190bf239\">mishandle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"de59a07f-3c9d-47d7-b63d-67608ff6e65d\">material available to them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322697\" id=\"question-wrapper-322697\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"b270572d-3e0d-4d7e-a7d7-6d4b4475f5fa\">Information only matters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> when it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"238e00b8-ff8a-494e-95e7-4a6e00a91246\">influences action<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the flow-chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The Marketing Information System (MIS)</span></b></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_2/reading/images/8b2ab7d9a24f9b1fe4c5bac7720db55c057a5719b83bf4f0f21db4bed76297cc.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322698\" id=\"question-wrapper-322698\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">marketing managers</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322699\" id=\"question-wrapper-322699\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(information) needs</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322700\" id=\"question-wrapper-322700\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">internal records</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322701\" id=\"question-wrapper-322701\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">analysis unit</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"6606a50f-c40b-4db7-a082-2a479baf0eaf","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"generating repeat business","passagePhrase":"returning continually to the stores"},{"uid":"bbd55539-128a-4f9f-aab5-11c81927f0cc","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"example","passagePhrase":"For instance"},{"uid":"5d4f8841-0ce6-4908-b01b-c52af45818d2","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"personalised marketing","passagePhrase":"text messages and email alerts that tell them when their favourite artists and songs are about to be broadcast"},{"uid":"77ac0590-b53b-483b-9887-74b32c52be3f","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"government bodies"},{"uid":"c1ce6c03-292f-4c5d-8f2c-3c0c7b0f99a3","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"The majority","passagePhrase":"most of it"},{"uid":"bd5abf7d-17b2-45be-899a-8360731c156c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"greater wealth","passagePhrase":"household incomes increase"},{"uid":"7d2768ee-1f8b-4ee7-a02f-33fb763889ed","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"select from a broader range of products","passagePhrase":"choice widens ... better at discriminating"},{"uid":"56a8a889-e66e-482e-8104-a8a2b01431eb","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"too much information to cope with","passagePhrase":"bombarded with one million to one billion new numbers ... drowning in it"},{"uid":"796e11eb-1ef9-4e7c-a241-793fb4d85571","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Employees","passagePhrase":"subordinates"},{"uid":"a18f0caa-1682-45d8-acaa-83c4509cc089","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"suppress","passagePhrase":"withhold"},{"uid":"aa258456-69a9-4c00-af29-ddfa63e3d278","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"give a poor impression of them","passagePhrase":"reflect badly on their performance"},{"uid":"de59a07f-3c9d-47d7-b63d-67608ff6e65d","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"material available to them","passagePhrase":"provide ... with information"},{"uid":"83c2e720-8e68-46be-ace1-b090190bf239","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"mishandle","passagePhrase":"do not use it well"},{"uid":"8407f321-c0e6-497c-bfe6-fa8771608209","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"assess"},{"uid":"ba2c2753-8e3b-4f58-88f4-01155363939d","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"they have"},{"uid":"ecda0a64-cc7e-4cd5-b9fe-31682846a657","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"develops the needed information from"},{"uid":"d5a7f179-22cc-45d6-91d7-fd97e83e0af6","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The analysis unit processes the data"},{"uid":"229b3c13-27b6-494c-9e4e-57e697937fe1","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"illustration","passagePhrase":"For example"},{"uid":"71a4f82c-3c5b-4fed-9392-b8590430d158","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"commissioning new information research might not be advisable","passagePhrase":"foolish to spend $30,000 for additional information"},{"uid":"b270572d-3e0d-4d7e-a7d7-6d4b4475f5fa","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Information only matters","passagePhrase":"value comes from"},{"uid":"238e00b8-ff8a-494e-95e7-4a6e00a91246","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"influences action","passagePhrase":"its use"},{"uid":"1f8ebc08-9747-4ef2-8de5-9be3e640ddc9 77ac0590-b53b-483b-9887-74b32c52be3f","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"state-run agencies","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_49":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1–13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Blockbuster Phenomenon: A New Museum Trend</span></b></p><p><i><span>Museums in Australia, like other pleasure-giving public organizations, are adapting their activities so that they more closely reflect the marketplace.</span></i></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> Since the 1980s, the word </span><i><span>blockbuster</span></i><span> has become a fashionable term in the museum world. It refers to spectacular and high-profile exhibitions that attract large crowds. In 1984, Eisen <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"1d10d161-bbc5-4ba9-b976-cd137d4cf9f1\">defined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> a blockbuster as a large-scale loan exhibition. He said even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"897bb581-57ef-496a-95f5-5a3ff01bbc17\">people who rarely visit museums<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> were willing to queue for one. The model was visible at the British Museum in London. </span><i><span>The Treasures of Tutankhamun</span></i><span> ran from 30 March to 30 December 1972. It was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"cb4559f4-738f-4a2a-8cc5-ef4bd7733868\">originally planned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> for six months. However, it was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"95ae35dc-76f4-4b75-8bca-dc233d01017f\">extended because of demand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. The exhibition displayed 50 objects. It attracted 1,694,117 visitors — more than 7,000 a day. Once a successful exhibition reaches its local audience, it may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"ef90ecde-39be-49f3-8ae0-c26e828d63ba\">offered to other institutions for a fee<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. In this way, one museum can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"79b8fdec-b48d-4e43-86b5-dc3f4f350012\">boost its takings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. It can also earn income from another museum's audience.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Visitors lured by a major temporary exhibition may not leave after viewing its main objects. They may continue through the galleries, partaking in a broader museum experience. Betty Churcher was Director of the Australian National Gallery from 1990 to 1997. The gallery was later renamed the National Gallery of Australia. She argued that people arriving for a blockbuster often <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"fa6d2858-faa3-4369-8850-aea0867ebaea\">stayed to examine the permanent collection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. This gave the museum's existing holdings greater exposure. A similar attraction occurred in New York in 2010. </span><i><span>Picasso in The Metropolitan Museum of Art</span></i><span> (the Met) drew 703,256 visitors in 17 weeks. The exhibition <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"dae39f16-09ae-450b-99f0-9dd4e18ae000\">included 300 works from the Met's own collection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> Museums in the UK, USA, Canada and Australia frequently operate under a system of plural funding. Part of their revenue comes from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"2f3e3dfe-4c0d-435a-ab72-af82ac8c13c9\">government contributions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> at the federal, state or local level. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"04a935f9-38c2-487a-9ac1-f8058dba05d8\">The rest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"04a935f9-38c2-487a-9ac1-f8058dba05d8\">come from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> admission <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"1da33168-dd0a-402d-8be9-2f96fea733f0\">charges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, memberships, shops, restaurants or special exhibitions. Maintaining visitor levels is therefore paramount. Museums now make regular changes to their programmes. They also compete for major travelling shows. As a result, the public may be described as customers rather than visitors. Curators often take on administrative duties. Meanwhile, directors <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"ef98f544-ff42-40ec-a45d-632a0341f973\">require<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> public relations skills. These skills help their institutions compete successfully to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"3b48489d-082c-4871-8dea-9cee0512e3ca\">stage exhibitions that attract large audiences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> The growing convergence of museums, tourism and commerce has produced what some call the </span><i><span>new museology</span></i><span>. This trend has caused debate. Some writers describe blockbusters as non-elitist and too commercial. Others extol the virtues of cooperation across museums. They say such projects can cater for a wide community rather than an elite one. The Museum of Modern Art in New York (MoMA) collaborated with Tate and museums in Paris on </span><i><span>Matisse Picasso</span></i><span>. The exhibition was shown at MoMA from 13 February to 19 May 2003. Whatever commentators say, museum managers continue to combine culture with commerce.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Blockbusters can bring an institution a surplus. However, their financial benefits vary. The British Museum states that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"fe3003eb-dfc3-4049-a4c7-b5b2220443d2\">profits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> from its 1972 Tutankhamun exhibition were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"39b20d3f-1530-4d41-a265-308e43982680\">donated to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> major cultural projects in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"91fcdd28-2028-45cb-9c65-adff47460185\">Egypt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. The Louvre provides a later example of remarkable public demand. Its </span><i><span>Leonardo da Vinci</span></i><span> exhibition was held from 24 October 2019 to 24 February 2020. It received 1,071,840 visitors in 104 days. This was higher than the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"7c96ea01-ec29-4a27-987e-40b81dc0842a\">540,000<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> visitors recorded for its 2018 </span><i><span>Delacroix</span></i><span> retrospective. Such income can help museums fund new acquisitions. It can also pay for specific repairs, such as leaking roofs and faulty temperature controls. In Australia, a blockbuster may also illustrate that a museum is recovering part of its running costs. Its positive spin-offs may extend to hotels, restaurants, shops and public transport. This supports claims that the arts have sustained economic benefits.</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> The attraction of large attendance figures should not hide the costs. Blockbusters require major capital expenditure. This includes money for loans, insurance, shipping, security, installation and marketing. One published Australian estimate placed the cost of mounting a major imported blockbuster at A$3.5–4.5 million. There is also a cost in staff time. A touring exhibition draws resources from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"93714e98-27ce-4a9c-b9dc-fef58bd13d16\">several functional departments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. Staff in services, front-of-house, technical, promotional, educational and administrative roles may all have to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"b9bca1f7-2f7e-49e6-bab0-6c93ce967465\">perform<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> additional tasks. As the Met, MoMA, the Louvre and Australian galleries compete for attention, the market becomes crowded. Successful shows may therefore be less likely to produce enough profit to subsidize other activities. This is because of the competitive nature of the market.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> Experience in the UK and USA suggests that the blockbuster ideology can create a false expectation. Some museums believe that the momentum behind a successful programme can be sustained indefinitely. However, mounting major shows is tiring for staff. Some institutional costs are also difficult to calculate. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"be0beabf-3c60-4871-82fd-3137915f7699\">narrow focus on ticket income<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"775de910-728c-4de5-aa1f-4ced74c65dad\">squeeze<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"167419b4-2e6f-41af-b635-1d63fc00bdfe\">intellectual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> substance <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"775de910-728c-4de5-aa1f-4ced74c65dad\">out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> of an exhibition. If content is weakened, the exhibition may fail both educationally and financially. A museum therefore needs to balance major events with regular exhibitions. This approach is easier where there is enough gallery space and alternative funding for less heavily promoted fare. The best course is to study what the local community wants. At the same time, museums must ensure that their everyday programme remains enduring.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 1–6 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322702\" id=\"question-wrapper-322702\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The </span><i><span>Treasures of Tutankhamun </span></i><span><span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"95ae35dc-76f4-4b75-8bca-dc233d01017f\">ended according to the British Museum’s </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"95ae35dc-76f4-4b75-8bca-dc233d01017f cb4559f4-738f-4a2a-8cc5-ef4bd7733868\">initial schedule</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322703\" id=\"question-wrapper-322703\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A museum can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"79b8fdec-b48d-4e43-86b5-dc3f4f350012\">raise its income<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"ef90ecde-39be-49f3-8ae0-c26e828d63ba\">letting another venue host<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> a successful exhibition.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322704\" id=\"question-wrapper-322704\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Betty Churcher believed that major temporary exhibitions <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"fa6d2858-faa3-4369-8850-aea0867ebaea\">distracted visitors from a museum’s own displays<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322705\" id=\"question-wrapper-322705\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Met’s 2010 Picasso exhibition was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"dae39f16-09ae-450b-99f0-9dd4e18ae000\">made up entirely of works borrowed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> from other institutions.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322706\" id=\"question-wrapper-322706\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Louvre charged a higher admission fee for its Leonardo da Vinci exhibition than for its earlier Delacroix retrospective.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322707\" id=\"question-wrapper-322707\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The institutions involved in Matisse Picasso shared the exhibition costs equally.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322708\" id=\"question-wrapper-322708\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Eisen <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"1d10d161-bbc5-4ba9-b976-cd137d4cf9f1\">described<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> a blockbuster as a__________ exhibition that could attract <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"897bb581-57ef-496a-95f5-5a3ff01bbc17\">infrequent museum visitors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(large-scale) loan</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322709\" id=\"question-wrapper-322709\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In addition to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"2f3e3dfe-4c0d-435a-ab72-af82ac8c13c9\">financial support from public authorities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, museums may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"04a935f9-38c2-487a-9ac1-f8058dba05d8\">raise revenue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> through__________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"1da33168-dd0a-402d-8be9-2f96fea733f0\">fees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">admission</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322710\" id=\"question-wrapper-322710\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Museum directors now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"ef98f544-ff42-40ec-a45d-632a0341f973\">need<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>__________ to help their institutions <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"3b48489d-082c-4871-8dea-9cee0512e3ca\">put on shows that draw big crowds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">public relations skills</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322711\" id=\"question-wrapper-322711\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the British Museum, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"fe3003eb-dfc3-4049-a4c7-b5b2220443d2\">money made<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> from the Tutankhamun display <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"39b20d3f-1530-4d41-a265-308e43982680\">helped fund<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> major__________ in the artefacts’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"91fcdd28-2028-45cb-9c65-adff47460185\">source country<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">cultural projects</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322712\" id=\"question-wrapper-322712\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>At the Louvre, an earlier retrospective, focusing on__________, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"7c96ea01-ec29-4a27-987e-40b81dc0842a\">drew about half as many visitors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> as the later record-breaking exhibition.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Delacroix</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322713\" id=\"question-wrapper-322713\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>When an institution hosts a touring exhibition, staff from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"93714e98-27ce-4a9c-b9dc-fef58bd13d16\">different departments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> may be required to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"b9bca1f7-2f7e-49e6-bab0-6c93ce967465\">carry out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>__________.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">additional tasks</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322714\" id=\"question-wrapper-322714\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"be0beabf-3c60-4871-82fd-3137915f7699\">strong emphasis on revenue from ticket sales<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"775de910-728c-4de5-aa1f-4ced74c65dad\">reduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"167419b4-2e6f-41af-b635-1d63fc00bdfe\">scholarly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>__________ of an exhibition.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">substance</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"1d10d161-bbc5-4ba9-b976-cd137d4cf9f1","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"described","passagePhrase":"defined"},{"uid":"897bb581-57ef-496a-95f5-5a3ff01bbc17","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"infrequent museum visitors","passagePhrase":"people who rarely visit museums"},{"uid":"cb4559f4-738f-4a2a-8cc5-ef4bd7733868","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"originally planned"},{"uid":"ef90ecde-39be-49f3-8ae0-c26e828d63ba","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"letting another venue host","passagePhrase":"offered to other institutions for a fee"},{"uid":"79b8fdec-b48d-4e43-86b5-dc3f4f350012","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"raise its income","passagePhrase":"boost its takings"},{"uid":"2f3e3dfe-4c0d-435a-ab72-af82ac8c13c9","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"financial support from public authorities","passagePhrase":"government contributions"},{"uid":"04a935f9-38c2-487a-9ac1-f8058dba05d8","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"raise revenue","passagePhrase":"The rest ... come from"},{"uid":"1da33168-dd0a-402d-8be9-2f96fea733f0","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"fees","passagePhrase":"charges"},{"uid":"ef98f544-ff42-40ec-a45d-632a0341f973","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"need","passagePhrase":"require"},{"uid":"3b48489d-082c-4871-8dea-9cee0512e3ca","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"put on shows that draw big crowds","passagePhrase":"stage exhibitions that attract large audiences"},{"uid":"fe3003eb-dfc3-4049-a4c7-b5b2220443d2","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"money made","passagePhrase":"profits"},{"uid":"39b20d3f-1530-4d41-a265-308e43982680","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"helped fund","passagePhrase":"donated to"},{"uid":"91fcdd28-2028-45cb-9c65-adff47460185","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"source country","passagePhrase":"Egypt"},{"uid":"7c96ea01-ec29-4a27-987e-40b81dc0842a","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"drew about half as many visitors","passagePhrase":"540,000"},{"uid":"93714e98-27ce-4a9c-b9dc-fef58bd13d16","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"different departments","passagePhrase":"several functional departments"},{"uid":"b9bca1f7-2f7e-49e6-bab0-6c93ce967465","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"carry out","passagePhrase":"perform"},{"uid":"be0beabf-3c60-4871-82fd-3137915f7699","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"strong emphasis on revenue from ticket sales","passagePhrase":"narrow focus on ticket income"},{"uid":"775de910-728c-4de5-aa1f-4ced74c65dad","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"reduce","passagePhrase":"squeeze ... out"},{"uid":"167419b4-2e6f-41af-b635-1d63fc00bdfe","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"scholarly","passagePhrase":"intellectual"},{"uid":"95ae35dc-76f4-4b75-8bca-dc233d01017f cb4559f4-738f-4a2a-8cc5-ef4bd7733868","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"initial schedule","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_50":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Coastal Archaeology of Britain</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>A. </span></b><span>The recognition of the wealth and diversity of England’s coastal archaeology has been one of the most important developments of recent decades. Some elements of this enormous resource have long been known. The so-called ‘submerged forests’ off the coasts of England, sometimes containing clear evidence of human activity, had attracted the attention of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"79d876e1-6afd-4d29-b746-bb82a04595a2\">antiquarians since at least the 1740s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. However, serious and systematic investigation of the archaeological potential of the coast <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2f49f395-84cd-448b-9682-19ea54393881\">began only in the early 1980s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, transforming what had once been a specialist interest into a significant area of research.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span>It is possible to trace <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"65e2dfbb-18b6-4c60-99f0-167f9f066b26\">a variety of causes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"84d9501d-156e-4ebd-9e69-a29c1ce5ea98\">this concentration of effort and interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. During the 1980s and 1990s, scientific research into climate change and its environmental impact spilled into a much broader public debate as awareness of these issues increased. In particular, reports published in 1983 and 1992 drew attention to the prospect of rising sea levels and their consequences for coastal environments. At the same time, archaeologists became increasingly concerned that the destruction caused by natural processes of coastal erosion, together with human activity, was having a growing impact on archaeological remains. Between 1985 and 1995, the number of coastal surveys undertaken in England more than doubled.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span>The dominant process affecting the physical form of England during the post-glacial period was the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"3ebcf85c-1b62-4cb4-8d9a-bd7243a461f7\">rise in the altitude of sea level<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> relative to the land as glaciers melted and the landmass readjusted. In some regions, relative sea level increased by approximately 35 metres. The encroachment of the sea led to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"693d0764-ac8e-46ea-87eb-dde0923685e5\">loss of vast areas of land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> now beneath the North Sea and the English Channel, including the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 22\" data-uid=\"693d0764-ac8e-46ea-87eb-dde0923685e5 924949a4-d59f-46f9-a6d2-dd83536d6b55\">disappearance of the land bridge</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"924949a4-d59f-46f9-a6d2-dd83536d6b55\"> that once connected Britain and France</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. These developments must have been immensely significant for prehistoric populations. Yet despite the fact that sea-level change is comparatively well documented, its effects on human communities have received surprisingly limited attention from archaeologists.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ab8225ad-3713-40d6-9e1b-65e5a44823b6\">So great has been the rise in sea level and the consequent regression of the coast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> that much of the archaeological evidence now exposed in coastal areas, whether being eroded or revealed as buried land surfaces, is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"f6dd0b6f-7467-4dd1-b9d1-cea05da08190\">derived from what was originally terrestrial occupation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Its present location is therefore often the result of later processes unrelated to the activities that created it. Nevertheless, coastal environments frequently provide <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"4a816d1c-0f7b-4481-9dc8-9ac69887080f\">excellent conditions for preservation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Important examples include the Neolithic structure excavated at the Stumble in Essex, where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ead73696-73d6-4da9-ac82-3d97344a84a3\">organic materials survived in remarkably good condition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> In some locations, these buried land surfaces do contain evidence for human exploitation of coastal environments, and similar discoveries have been made elsewhere around the modern shoreline. However, our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7b1f6f9b-ccfe-46ca-b648-6938988766fd\">understanding remains limited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. We are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 24\" data-uid=\"2398a280-a73b-4c24-b56c-65c05a41065c 7b1f6f9b-ccfe-46ca-b648-6938988766fd\">not yet in a position to make even preliminary estimates</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> regarding such fundamental issues as the overall <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"25610222-a5a9-4690-a83e-ec9cab6d02e8\">importance of the coast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in past societies, the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"ba7e603e-2f34-4e50-b4fd-f1472917a4e4\">extent to which people </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 24\" data-uid=\"25610222-a5a9-4690-a83e-ec9cab6d02e8 ba7e603e-2f34-4e50-b4fd-f1472917a4e4\">depended upon marine resources</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, or whether coastal settlements differed significantly from those located inland.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>The most striking evidence for the use of the sea is found in boats. Most known wrecks around Britain are of post-medieval date and offer an unparalleled opportunity for research. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"c42a84ce-affc-4705-8bb2-1b8e4e779635\">Earlier vessels are far rarer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. The prehistoric sewn-plank boats discovered in locations such as Dover and the Humber estuary belong largely to the period between 1800 BC and 1000 BC. After this, there is a <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 25\" data-uid=\"8245a989-075f-4348-b5bc-5616e7e64327 c42a84ce-affc-4705-8bb2-1b8e4e779635\">gap in the archaeological record</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> of roughly one thousand years before boats <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"b04f510c-a8b7-4252-9733-1d8d9c5c175b\">reappeared using a very different technology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Boatbuilding must have been a major activity along much of the coast. These vessels were among the most sophisticated artefacts created by premodern societies, and further research into their production and use has the potential to improve our understanding of technological development.</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>Boats required places to land, yet our knowledge of these facilities remains very patchy. In many cases, natural beaches and shorelines would have sufficed, leaving little archaeological evidence behind. In later periods, however, ports, harbours, quays, wharves, and jetties became increasingly common. While some attention has been given to the waterfront archaeology of important Roman and medieval towns, the multitude of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"6ff8169d-9c19-41e2-a9d9-e0a00c6dd749\">smaller landing places<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"078cbab1-3820-40e9-8290-dd22a81848b9\">received far less study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Unfortunately, modern redevelopment and other forms of coastal change are subjecting many of these sites to unprecedented pressure, and only a limited number of surveys have been undertaken.</span></p><p><b><span>H. </span></b><span>One of the most important revelations of recent research has been the scale of industrial activity along the coast. More than 60 percent of documented coastal industries are connected with fishing or salt production. Although many methods of fishing leave little archaeological trace, surveys have revealed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"bf7d1787-1890-4a5e-acca-4c8520b8f00d\">extensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> facilities for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"07e5a755-9b7f-48a1-b10c-786029a48c8f\">procuring fish and shellfish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Particularly impressive are the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"fb3d0546-9ff1-40bb-accc-b826f6a5a523\">elaborate wooden fish weirs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> found in areas such as Essex and the Severn Estuary. Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"bf7d1787-1890-4a5e-acca-4c8520b8f00d\">extend for more than 300 metres<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and are highly responsive to aerial photography in shallow water. Salt production was also significant, with some coastal sites capable of producing several hundred tonnes annually. Other industries exploited resources that outcropped near the coast, taking advantage of convenient transport links. Despite their importance, many of these activities remain poorly documented.</span></p><p><b><span>I. </span></b><span>Some appreciation of the variety and significance of archaeological remains preserved within the coastal zone, albeit still incomplete, can be gained from recent research. At the same time, the difficulty of protecting this resource is becoming increasingly apparent. Human <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"33db1ea1-faf4-46ad-a65e-f555ac0adc0b\">threats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> include <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"22f438ef-52ae-4b5b-8a67-2efc5723bd56\">urban expansion, the redevelopment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> of historic waterfronts, and the growing provision of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"22f438ef-52ae-4b5b-8a67-2efc5723bd56\">tourist facilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> such as marinas. Natural pressures remain equally serious. The most significant concern is the continuing rise in sea level, which is currently predicted to average between 3 and 4 millimetres per year in some parts of England. More than 1,000 coastal archaeological sites are considered vulnerable to future damage. The complex web of organisations responsible for managing the coastline means that responding effectively to these threats will continue to pose a major challenge for archaeologists.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A–E from the list below.</span></p><p><span>List of Headings</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"79d876e1-6afd-4d29-b746-bb82a04595a2\">Early scholarly interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2f49f395-84cd-448b-9682-19ea54393881\">before systematic investigation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. Pressures arising from recreational coastal development</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"693d0764-ac8e-46ea-87eb-dde0923685e5\">Landscape transformation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> caused by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"3ebcf85c-1b62-4cb4-8d9a-bd7243a461f7\">elevated water levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7b1f6f9b-ccfe-46ca-b648-6938988766fd\">Unresolved questions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> concerning <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"25610222-a5a9-4690-a83e-ec9cab6d02e8\">maritime communities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"65e2dfbb-18b6-4c60-99f0-167f9f066b26\">Factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> contributing to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"84d9501d-156e-4ebd-9e69-a29c1ce5ea98\">renewed academic attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ead73696-73d6-4da9-ac82-3d97344a84a3\">Durability of archaeological evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"4a816d1c-0f7b-4481-9dc8-9ac69887080f\">favourable settings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. A documentary gap in the record of watercraft</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. The inland expansion of agricultural practices</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322715\" id=\"question-wrapper-322715\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322716\" id=\"question-wrapper-322716\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322717\" id=\"question-wrapper-322717\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322718\" id=\"question-wrapper-322718\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322719\" id=\"question-wrapper-322719\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–I.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322720\" id=\"question-wrapper-322720\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"8245a989-075f-4348-b5bc-5616e7e64327\">an absence in the record<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"b04f510c-a8b7-4252-9733-1d8d9c5c175b\">before an alternative technique emerged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322721\" id=\"question-wrapper-322721\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"fb3d0546-9ff1-40bb-accc-b826f6a5a523\">physical structures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> showing how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"07e5a755-9b7f-48a1-b10c-786029a48c8f\">food was harvested from the sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"bf7d1787-1890-4a5e-acca-4c8520b8f00d\">on a large scale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322722\" id=\"question-wrapper-322722\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ab8225ad-3713-40d6-9e1b-65e5a44823b6\">account of why<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> some coastal finds <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"f6dd0b6f-7467-4dd1-b9d1-cea05da08190\">originated from earlier land-based activity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322723\" id=\"question-wrapper-322723\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"924949a4-d59f-46f9-a6d2-dd83536d6b55\">geographical change that would have affected movement between two areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322724\" id=\"question-wrapper-322724\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>evidence that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"6ff8169d-9c19-41e2-a9d9-e0a00c6dd749\">minor transport sites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"078cbab1-3820-40e9-8290-dd22a81848b9\">comparatively neglected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose THREE letters from A-G. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet. Which THREE of the following statements are mentioned in the passage?</span></p><p><span>A. One particular scholar is credited with the earliest record of a submerged forest.</span></p><p><span>B. It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"2398a280-a73b-4c24-b56c-65c05a41065c\">hard to judge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"ba7e603e-2f34-4e50-b4fd-f1472917a4e4\">how far earlier societies relied on the sea for their living<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>C. Prehistoric communities had a clear grasp of climate change.</span></p><p><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"c42a84ce-affc-4705-8bb2-1b8e4e779635\">Our knowledge of boat evidence is limited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>E. Some finding grounds were converted to ports.</span></p><p><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"22f438ef-52ae-4b5b-8a67-2efc5723bd56\">Human development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"33db1ea1-faf4-46ad-a65e-f555ac0adc0b\">threatens the archaeological remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>G. Coastal archaeology will become more important in the future.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322725\" id=\"question-wrapper-322725\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322726\" id=\"question-wrapper-322726\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322727\" id=\"question-wrapper-322727\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"79d876e1-6afd-4d29-b746-bb82a04595a2","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Early scholarly interest","passagePhrase":"antiquarians since at least the 1740s"},{"uid":"2f49f395-84cd-448b-9682-19ea54393881","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"before systematic investigation","passagePhrase":"began only in the early 1980s"},{"uid":"65e2dfbb-18b6-4c60-99f0-167f9f066b26","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Factors","passagePhrase":"a variety of causes"},{"uid":"84d9501d-156e-4ebd-9e69-a29c1ce5ea98","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"renewed academic attention","passagePhrase":"this concentration of effort and interest"},{"uid":"3ebcf85c-1b62-4cb4-8d9a-bd7243a461f7","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"elevated water levels","passagePhrase":"rise in the altitude of sea level"},{"uid":"693d0764-ac8e-46ea-87eb-dde0923685e5","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Landscape transformation","passagePhrase":"loss of vast areas of land"},{"uid":"693d0764-ac8e-46ea-87eb-dde0923685e5 924949a4-d59f-46f9-a6d2-dd83536d6b55","qNum":"16 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"disappearance of the land bridge"},{"uid":"924949a4-d59f-46f9-a6d2-dd83536d6b55","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"geographical change that would have affected movement between two areas","passagePhrase":"that once connected Britain and France"},{"uid":"ab8225ad-3713-40d6-9e1b-65e5a44823b6","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"account of why","passagePhrase":"So great has been the rise in sea level and the consequent regression of the coast"},{"uid":"f6dd0b6f-7467-4dd1-b9d1-cea05da08190","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"originated from earlier land-based activity","passagePhrase":"derived from what was originally terrestrial occupation"},{"uid":"4a816d1c-0f7b-4481-9dc8-9ac69887080f","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"favourable settings","passagePhrase":"excellent conditions for preservation"},{"uid":"ead73696-73d6-4da9-ac82-3d97344a84a3","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Durability of archaeological evidence","passagePhrase":"organic materials survived in remarkably good condition"},{"uid":"7b1f6f9b-ccfe-46ca-b648-6938988766fd","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Unresolved questions","passagePhrase":"understanding remains limited"},{"uid":"2398a280-a73b-4c24-b56c-65c05a41065c 7b1f6f9b-ccfe-46ca-b648-6938988766fd","qNum":"18 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"not yet in a position to make even preliminary estimates"},{"uid":"25610222-a5a9-4690-a83e-ec9cab6d02e8","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"maritime communities","passagePhrase":"importance of the coast"},{"uid":"ba7e603e-2f34-4e50-b4fd-f1472917a4e4","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"how far earlier societies relied on the sea for their living","passagePhrase":"extent to which people"},{"uid":"25610222-a5a9-4690-a83e-ec9cab6d02e8 ba7e603e-2f34-4e50-b4fd-f1472917a4e4","qNum":"18 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"depended upon marine resources"},{"uid":"c42a84ce-affc-4705-8bb2-1b8e4e779635","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"Our knowledge of boat evidence is limited","passagePhrase":"Earlier vessels are far rarer"},{"uid":"8245a989-075f-4348-b5bc-5616e7e64327 c42a84ce-affc-4705-8bb2-1b8e4e779635","qNum":"19 25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"gap in the archaeological record"},{"uid":"b04f510c-a8b7-4252-9733-1d8d9c5c175b","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"before an alternative technique emerged","passagePhrase":"reappeared using a very different technology"},{"uid":"6ff8169d-9c19-41e2-a9d9-e0a00c6dd749","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"minor transport sites","passagePhrase":"smaller landing places"},{"uid":"078cbab1-3820-40e9-8290-dd22a81848b9","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"comparatively neglected","passagePhrase":"received far less study"},{"uid":"bf7d1787-1890-4a5e-acca-4c8520b8f00d","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"on a large scale","passagePhrase":"extensive ... extend for more than 300 metres"},{"uid":"07e5a755-9b7f-48a1-b10c-786029a48c8f","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"food was harvested from the sea","passagePhrase":"procuring fish and shellfish"},{"uid":"fb3d0546-9ff1-40bb-accc-b826f6a5a523","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"physical structures","passagePhrase":"elaborate wooden fish weirs"},{"uid":"33db1ea1-faf4-46ad-a65e-f555ac0adc0b","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"threatens the archaeological remains","passagePhrase":"threats"},{"uid":"22f438ef-52ae-4b5b-8a67-2efc5723bd56","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Human development","passagePhrase":"urban expansion, the redevelopment ... tourist facilities"},{"uid":"8245a989-075f-4348-b5bc-5616e7e64327","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"an absence in the record","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"2398a280-a73b-4c24-b56c-65c05a41065c","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"hard to judge","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_51":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>Does class size matter?</span></b></p><p><span>A. Of all the reforms advanced as remedies for educational underperformance, few possess the uncomplicated public appeal of placing fewer children with each teacher, because the proposal appears to promise individual attention without requiring families to understand complex theories of learning. During the past generation, class-size reduction has therefore moved beyond a specialised academic debate and become a highly visible political intervention, with many education authorities adopting policies intended to limit pupil numbers in the early years. Yet its intuitive attractiveness <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"20447ebc-d2c6-4950-bcde-20e37e015b08\">should not be mistaken for proof that it is the decisive influence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> on educational success, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"20447ebc-d2c6-4950-bcde-20e37e015b08\">since teachers, curricula, family circumstances and school resources also shape what children achieve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>B.Some investigators have examined administrative records and identified a broad decline in pupil–teacher ratios over time, while national assessment outcomes have not improved in a similarly straightforward manner; however, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"e76ec262-a558-4ba5-ad14-7fb531e403cc\">this trend does not necessarily demonstrate that smaller classes make no difference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, because such figures combine pupils educated under markedly different circumstances. Schools strive not merely to raise test performance but also to reduce dropout rates, support pupils with learning difficulties and retain young people who might otherwise leave education early, any of which can alter average results independently of class size. In addition, a cohort containing more pupils from financially well-off households, whose parents have high educational attainment and can support learning in the language of instruction, cannot be reliably compared with one facing greater socioeconomic disadvantage. Similar problems arise when teachers differ in experience or mastery of their subjects, or when some schools are more generously outfitted with libraries, technology and specialist support. For this reason, observational comparisons may confound the effect of smaller classes with many other influences, making strong causal conclusions from existing records methodologically unsafe.</span></p><p><span>C. Among the many studies conducted over several decades, the notable exception in design quality was the STAR project, a controlled study in which children beginning school were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"abb30177-e1df-4240-bb53-277c38b7392b\">allocated by chance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> either to small classes or to regular classes and then remained in the assigned category until the end of their third year. Teachers were also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"abb30177-e1df-4240-bb53-277c38b7392b\">allocated randomly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> so that instructional quality would not systematically differ between the two conditions, a safeguard intended to make any subsequent contrast in pupil outcomes a fairer test of class size rather than of staffing advantage. Because the project <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b283d2d9-a3c5-4ad6-9f79-04cded2cfe9d\">deployed neither specialised curricular materials nor extensive preparation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> for small-class teachers, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"1d346d76-25a7-4e76-b15a-da90e1875ade\">examined the class-size intervention without simultaneously introducing an entirely different teaching model<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Although no field study can eliminate every complication, this methodological structure provided considerably more robust evidence than retrospective records and made STAR central to subsequent debate about educational policy.</span></p><p><span>D. Reviews of STAR identified an array of benefits for pupils in smaller classrooms, with improvements appearing slightly stronger among <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"775d0ee8-cbb3-4824-800d-30b9adc351c7\">Black and Hispanic children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, an outcome with particular significance from a policy standpoint because achievement gaps frequently reflect wider demographic and economic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"61a22aa4-2547-4b50-a1f8-bb56bfa9075e\">disadvantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Nevertheless, the evidence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"4411cd2e-8f51-4cd5-9a94-805391a20852\">cannot establish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> that these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"420cb6dc-fd9e-408b-8a7e-62eca3153ba7\">gains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"c0a6763f-5670-42f1-98a0-969b49c25530\">persist for many years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> after children return to ordinary classrooms, so it would be unsafe to extrapolate an immediate advantage into a permanent educational transformation. A further complication was that too many pupils moved from regular classes into smaller ones during the project, apparently because school personnel caved in to pressure from parents, thereby <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8464c631-b634-4e27-a78c-2573a8b9c375\">weakening the separation between the comparison groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. This breach of implementation fidelity complicates interpretation, but it does not undermine the statistically significant <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"336045c3-9cac-41e6-81f1-7e6c6ef3df0b\">conclusion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> that pupils placed in smaller classes obtained a measurable short-term benefit.</span></p><p><span>E. The large-scale California programme stands less as a model worthy of emulation than as evidence that promising research can be poorly translated into statewide practice, because it imposed class-size reduction <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"5901b130-0f85-4fa2-b36f-45fe44e80cb2\">across both prosperous and disadvantaged districts despite a serious shortage of suitably qualified teachers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, especially in poorer communities. Such a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"5901b130-0f85-4fa2-b36f-45fe44e80cb2\">uniform approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> may have been politically expedient, since it offered the same headline reform everywhere, but it ignored the heterogeneous capacities of schools to recruit effective staff and consequently exacerbated the disparity between rich and poor districts. Better-paying, more affluent communities were able to attract stronger teachers, including some who had previously worked in schools serving children with greater needs, so a reform intended to promote opportunity partly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"fa61fa27-4ed3-4743-9dec-b7aa4daafac8\">redistributed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"a8ffadfb-1bbf-43ca-9b0f-b41b3fc750b6\">existing expertise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> away from its most vulnerable pupils. California recorded only modest achievement benefits, whereas the smaller SAGE programme was noteworthy because it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"b4e49489-6587-4d1f-bd3b-3cde861d7f24\">concentrated support on schools serving substantial numbers of low-income children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> rather than assuming every district faced the same problem. This deliberate stratification did not, by itself, settle every question about cost or long-term outcomes, but it offered a more targeted basis for examining whether reduced classes might assist disadvantaged communities.</span></p><p><span>F. Taken together, STAR and SAGE make it difficult to maintain that smaller classes never assist learning, while California demonstrates that the same strategy, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"76441cca-66aa-4c1b-a139-10716911490f\">introduced with insufficient forethought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> about teacher supply and local conditions, can absorb enormous public expenditure while producing only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"6924575a-614f-4c90-9dc2-c1e81c0b7642\">minuscule gains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and even worsening inequalities in the short term. The broader lesson is not that governments should abandon class-size reduction, nor that they should make it the dominant educational priority, but that effectiveness depends on where the reform is directed, how faithfully it is implemented and what resources accompany it. Legislators and administrators therefore <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b96c66f6-c165-42f0-8a52-e91818f47743\">require<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"5768d6f7-75dd-4712-83c8-df508cdc197e\">reliable comparisons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> between this approach and alternatives such as teacher development, early intervention or additional support for disadvantaged schools <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b96c66f6-c165-42f0-8a52-e91818f47743\">before they can reach sensible policy decisions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. A popular reform becomes a defensible policy only when its anticipated benefits, financial cost and potential for unintended harm have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"5768d6f7-75dd-4712-83c8-df508cdc197e\">evaluated together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322728\" id=\"question-wrapper-322728\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"20447ebc-d2c6-4950-bcde-20e37e015b08\">Lowering class size alone is sufficient<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to enhance pupils’ academic attainment.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322729\" id=\"question-wrapper-322729\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"e76ec262-a558-4ba5-ad14-7fb531e403cc\">Administrative records offer reliable proof that smaller classes do not lead to better learning outcomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322730\" id=\"question-wrapper-322730\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Assigning teachers by chance would be too difficult for later studies to copy.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 30-35 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322731\" id=\"question-wrapper-322731\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why was it important that STAR <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b283d2d9-a3c5-4ad6-9f79-04cded2cfe9d\">did not rely on specialised materials or additional teacher training<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It reduced transfer pressure by keeping pupils in fixed groups and restricting class changes.</li> <li>B. It enabled researchers to compare achievement across demographic groups over time.</li> <li>C. It reduced costs by limiting the need for extra teacher training and support staff.</li> <li>D. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"1d346d76-25a7-4e76-b15a-da90e1875ade\">isolated the effect of smaller classes without changing educational approaches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322732\" id=\"question-wrapper-322732\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why are STAR's results for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"775d0ee8-cbb3-4824-800d-30b9adc351c7\">Black and Hispanic pupils<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> especially important?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They suggest the programme worked best with specially trained teachers.</li> <li>B. They imply class-size reduction may help address <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"61a22aa4-2547-4b50-a1f8-bb56bfa9075e\">inequality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>C. They show minority pupils kept their gains after returning to regular classes.</li> <li>D. They prove classroom size is the main cause of achievement differences.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322733\" id=\"question-wrapper-322733\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>How does the writer view pupil transfers into smaller STAR classes?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8464c631-b634-4e27-a78c-2573a8b9c375\">blurred the difference between the groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> but left the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"336045c3-9cac-41e6-81f1-7e6c6ef3df0b\">main finding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> intact.</li> <li>B. They showed parents could identify the most effective approach.</li> <li>C. They confirmed transferred pupils quickly caught up.</li> <li>D. They revealed insufficient initial recruitment by researchers.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322734\" id=\"question-wrapper-322734\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why is the California programme seen as a warning?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It reduced class sizes only where qualified teachers were already available.</li> <li>B. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"5901b130-0f85-4fa2-b36f-45fe44e80cb2\">applied one policy despite differences in personnel resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</li> <li>C. It shifted responsibility for standards to individual schools.</li> <li>D. It improved results but exceeded spending expectations.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322735\" id=\"question-wrapper-322735\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What distinguished SAGE from the California programme?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It examined whether benefits persisted after larger classes resumed.</li> <li>B. It offered incentives to retain experienced teachers.</li> <li>C. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"b4e49489-6587-4d1f-bd3b-3cde861d7f24\">targeted schools with higher levels of economic disadvantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</li> <li>D. It compared smaller classes with teacher-development programmes.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322736\" id=\"question-wrapper-322736\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which best reflects the writer's overall view?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Smaller classes have potential, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"76441cca-66aa-4c1b-a139-10716911490f\">poor implementation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"6924575a-614f-4c90-9dc2-c1e81c0b7642\">undermine results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Evidence from smaller projects is insufficient to justify public funding.</li> <li>C. Statewide reforms are more reliable than controlled studies.</li> <li>D. Teacher quality matters far more than class size.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, A–G, below. Write the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 36-40</span></p><p><span>A differentiation</span></p><p><span>B <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"c0a6763f-5670-42f1-98a0-969b49c25530\">durability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span></span></p><p><span>C <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"5768d6f7-75dd-4712-83c8-df508cdc197e\">evaluation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></span></p><p><span>D pressure</span></p><p><span>E priorities</span></p><p><span>F <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"abb30177-e1df-4240-bb53-277c38b7392b\">randomisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></span></p><p><span>G <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"fa61fa27-4ed3-4743-9dec-b7aa4daafac8\">redistribution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p><p><b><span>Research into smaller classes</span></b></p><p><span>The evidential value of earlier administrative records was limited because schools seek to fulfil a range of (36)__________ beyond performance in examinations. The STAR project generated more reliable findings through (37)__________, thereby preventing either parents or schools from influencing pupils’ initial class allocation. Although STAR recorded measurable early gains, the (38)__________ of these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"420cb6dc-fd9e-408b-8a7e-62eca3153ba7\">benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> after pupils returned to ordinary classrooms <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"4411cd2e-8f51-4cd5-9a94-805391a20852\">remains uncertain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. In California, the reform produced unintended <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"a8ffadfb-1bbf-43ca-9b0f-b41b3fc750b6\">staff<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> (39)__________, as more advantaged districts recruited effective teachers away from schools serving pupils with greater needs. The writer therefore argues that (40)__________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b96c66f6-c165-42f0-8a52-e91818f47743\">should precede any decision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to favour this approach over alternative educational measures.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322737\" id=\"question-wrapper-322737\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322738\" id=\"question-wrapper-322738\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322739\" id=\"question-wrapper-322739\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322740\" id=\"question-wrapper-322740\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322741\" id=\"question-wrapper-322741\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"abb30177-e1df-4240-bb53-277c38b7392b","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"randomisation","passagePhrase":"allocated by chance ... allocated randomly"},{"uid":"b283d2d9-a3c5-4ad6-9f79-04cded2cfe9d","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"did not rely on specialised materials or additional teacher training","passagePhrase":"deployed neither specialised curricular materials nor extensive preparation"},{"uid":"1d346d76-25a7-4e76-b15a-da90e1875ade","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"isolated the effect of smaller classes without changing educational approaches","passagePhrase":"examined the class-size intervention without simultaneously introducing an entirely different teaching model"},{"uid":"775d0ee8-cbb3-4824-800d-30b9adc351c7","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Black and Hispanic pupils","passagePhrase":"Black and Hispanic children"},{"uid":"61a22aa4-2547-4b50-a1f8-bb56bfa9075e","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"inequality","passagePhrase":"disadvantage"},{"uid":"4411cd2e-8f51-4cd5-9a94-805391a20852","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"remains uncertain","passagePhrase":"cannot establish"},{"uid":"420cb6dc-fd9e-408b-8a7e-62eca3153ba7","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"benefits","passagePhrase":"gains"},{"uid":"c0a6763f-5670-42f1-98a0-969b49c25530","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"durability","passagePhrase":"persist for many years"},{"uid":"8464c631-b634-4e27-a78c-2573a8b9c375","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"blurred the difference between the groups","passagePhrase":"weakening the separation between the comparison groups"},{"uid":"336045c3-9cac-41e6-81f1-7e6c6ef3df0b","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"main finding","passagePhrase":"conclusion"},{"uid":"5901b130-0f85-4fa2-b36f-45fe44e80cb2","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"applied one policy despite differences in personnel resources","passagePhrase":"across both prosperous and disadvantaged districts despite a serious shortage of suitably qualified teachers ... uniform approach"},{"uid":"fa61fa27-4ed3-4743-9dec-b7aa4daafac8","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"redistribution","passagePhrase":"redistributed"},{"uid":"a8ffadfb-1bbf-43ca-9b0f-b41b3fc750b6","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"staff","passagePhrase":"existing expertise"},{"uid":"b4e49489-6587-4d1f-bd3b-3cde861d7f24","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"targeted schools with higher levels of economic disadvantage","passagePhrase":"concentrated support on schools serving substantial numbers of low-income children"},{"uid":"76441cca-66aa-4c1b-a139-10716911490f","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"poor implementation","passagePhrase":"introduced with insufficient forethought"},{"uid":"6924575a-614f-4c90-9dc2-c1e81c0b7642","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"undermine results","passagePhrase":"minuscule gains"},{"uid":"b96c66f6-c165-42f0-8a52-e91818f47743","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"should precede any decision","passagePhrase":"require ... before they can reach sensible policy decisions"},{"uid":"5768d6f7-75dd-4712-83c8-df508cdc197e","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"evaluation","passagePhrase":"reliable comparisons ... evaluated together"}]},"reading_u2_52":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>How to spot a liar?</span></b></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> However much we may abhor it, deception is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"5b0950db-e433-49ed-92b1-6e9da7e80e60\">common in nature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. Some birds protect their young by feigning injury. They move away from their nests so that hungry predators follow them instead of attacking the nesting birds. Spider crabs use disguise. By adorning themselves with strips of kelp and other debris, they become difficult to see and can escape their enemies. Nature amply rewards successful <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"9240400e-0273-4f10-aed9-f7bc151e2804\">deceive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>rs because they survive long enough to reproduce. Humans also lie. According to psychologist Gerald Jellison of the University of Southern California, people are lied to about 200 times a day. Each untruth may have a purpose. People often deceive others to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"bde67e8e-9ae3-445b-83c3-86c83b2b1c47\">protect themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> or to gain something they cannot obtain in another way.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"55ba0f6b-b357-4b34-be4c-4d3c86bb8cc7\">Detecting deceit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> can be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"94e2b321-fddc-4899-8de1-4cc17251617e\">just as important as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9888e198-b7d6-4e98-b13c-7b1bfd1324c5\">telling a successful lie<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Someone who recognises falsehood may avoid being swindled by an unscrupulous business associate or hoodwinked by a devious partner. There are several observable signs that can help people identify dissemblers. A liar’s account may become tangled when details do not match. Facial expressions, body language and tone of voice can also provide telltale evidence. In 2006, researchers Charles Bond and Bella DePaulo examined studies involving 24,483 judges. They found that people identified truths and lies correctly only 54 per cent of the time without special equipment or training. This shows that observing lying behaviour is possible, but not easy.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> Good liars <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"0725dbf3-75cb-4ffd-aa8c-055c0602125c\">need to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"38c99983-479f-4105-9474-c3cbc4a5815b\">understand how other people feel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. They must judge whether another person is suspicious, calm or convinced. The same skill is essential for people who try to detect lies. One important emotion to notice is stress. A person may feel stress when there is a conflict between the truth and what they are saying. However, stress alone does not prove that a person is lying. Someone may also feel nervous because they are frightened, embarrassed or under pressure. For this reason, lie detection usually depends on several signs rather than one movement or reaction.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> Polygraphs are often called lie detectors, but they do not detect lies directly. They merely measure physical changes in the body while a person answers questions. A polygraph records <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"8b46bbc7-d8be-4508-980c-2855f12ea2d4\">respiration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"bbb89038-d22f-4f88-9288-c1a2d10ebcd0\">heart rate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> and skin conductivity. These measures often increase when a person is nervous. Nervous people may perspire, and the salts in perspiration carry electricity. A sudden leap in skin conductivity may therefore suggest nervousness. The person may be worried about being caught while being economical with the truth. However, hot television studio lights could produce a similar reaction. This is one reason <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a60edd7c-4e4f-4982-9686-1f10bd4b1f5d\">polygraph results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"803e8ef8-2853-4f7a-84a1-f9a0f355800b\">often inadmissible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in court. Reliable observers therefore examine clusters of signs rather than depending on one physical reaction.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Many useful clues appear on the face. The musculature of the face is linked to parts of the brain involved in emotion. As a result, the countenance can show emotions before a person is able to hide them. In 1978, Paul Ekman and Wallace Friesen published a system for classifying visible facial movements. Studies have suggested that genuine and insincere expressions are not always produced in the same way. For example, a patient paralyzed by a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"aed62b19-a4aa-49e4-9b06-318608736121\">stroke<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> on one side of the face may be asked to smile deliberately. In this case, only the mobile side of the mouth rises. However, when the patient hears a funny joke, a full and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"13ba51f7-2c11-4473-8256-875ec40c11b3\">spontaneous smile<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> may appear. This example shows that real emotion can affect facial movement automatically.</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> Very few people can control every facial movement. Most notably, actors and politicians may become <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"a40c68be-be39-4a3d-a20f-bc7b6dc4d384\">skilled at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"241aea0e-caef-470e-944f-a7318e6f9ede\">hiding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"775c51e4-0d3f-4814-92ef-2cff9bfed492\">real feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Even so, an emotion may briefly leak through before the person is conscious of it. Sadness is especially difficult to fake or conceal. When someone is truly sad, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a60223d5-5d39-4df0-a009-c4a684133b81\">forehead wrinkles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10 13\" data-uid=\"a1e6a7f0-cb93-442e-a433-e9287130763d a4c3928b-7e2d-4196-bc57-a7c865c0f852\">grief</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, and the inner corners of the eyebrows <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"7b6ed4d2-4009-40e4-9962-1429d0552497\">move upwards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. In Ekman’s tests, fewer than 15 per cent of participants could make this eyebrow movement voluntarily. Anger is easier to imitate. The lowered eyebrows of an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a23e775b-1e93-4b81-b2cc-8cf81e92bedd\">angry scowl<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> can be replicated by almost everyone. Therefore, a person who claims to be sad but does not show raised inner eyebrows may not be expressing real sadness.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> A smile is easier to counterfeit than sadness. Only two zygomaticus major muscles are needed to produce a false grin by pulling the corners of the lips upwards. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"b718dfd4-40da-4836-bc57-4d14db2b4e2c\">genuine smile<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> involves more than the mouth. It also affects the orbicularis oculi, the muscle around the eye. This action produces the distinctive <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"750808ad-542b-4e7d-8f70-8a903088b587\">lines commonly called crow’s-feet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. A false smile may be unmasked when the mouth rises but the surrounding eye area does not change naturally. In a real smile, the eyes may crinkle and the eyebrows may move slightly downwards. Without these signs, a false smile can appear unnatural and strained.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322742\" id=\"question-wrapper-322742\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Deception is a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"5b0950db-e433-49ed-92b1-6e9da7e80e60\">uniquely human behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322743\" id=\"question-wrapper-322743\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"9240400e-0273-4f10-aed9-f7bc151e2804\">tell lies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"bde67e8e-9ae3-445b-83c3-86c83b2b1c47\">self-protection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322744\" id=\"question-wrapper-322744\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Scientists have used computers to analyse which part of the brain is responsible for telling lies.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322745\" id=\"question-wrapper-322745\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9888e198-b7d6-4e98-b13c-7b1bfd1324c5\">Lying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> as a survival skill is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"94e2b321-fddc-4899-8de1-4cc17251617e\">more important than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"55ba0f6b-b357-4b34-be4c-4d3c86bb8cc7\">detecting a lie<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322746\" id=\"question-wrapper-322746\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>To be a good liar, one <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"0725dbf3-75cb-4ffd-aa8c-055c0602125c\">has to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"38c99983-479f-4105-9474-c3cbc4a5815b\">understand other people’s emotions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6–9 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322747\" id=\"question-wrapper-322747\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Apart from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"8b46bbc7-d8be-4508-980c-2855f12ea2d4\">breathing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"bbb89038-d22f-4f88-9288-c1a2d10ebcd0\">pulse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, which bodily response is measured by a lie detector?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">skin conductivity</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322748\" id=\"question-wrapper-322748\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In what setting are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a60edd7c-4e4f-4982-9686-1f10bd4b1f5d\">lie-detector findings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"803e8ef8-2853-4f7a-84a1-f9a0f355800b\">frequently not accepted as evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(in) court</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322749\" id=\"question-wrapper-322749\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"aed62b19-a4aa-49e4-9b06-318608736121\">medical condition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> showed that real emotional expressions can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"13ba51f7-2c11-4473-8256-875ec40c11b3\">bypass conscious control<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(a) stroke</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322750\" id=\"question-wrapper-322750\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Who might be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"a40c68be-be39-4a3d-a20f-bc7b6dc4d384\">good at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"241aea0e-caef-470e-944f-a7318e6f9ede\">concealing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"775c51e4-0d3f-4814-92ef-2cff9bfed492\">true emotional state<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">actors and politicians</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Classify the following facial traits as referring to</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10 13\" data-uid=\"a1e6a7f0-cb93-442e-a433-e9287130763d a4c3928b-7e2d-4196-bc57-a7c865c0f852\">Sadness</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a23e775b-1e93-4b81-b2cc-8cf81e92bedd\">Anger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"b718dfd4-40da-4836-bc57-4d14db2b4e2c\">Happiness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span></span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter A, B or C in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322751\" id=\"question-wrapper-322751\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Inner corner of eyebrows <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"7b6ed4d2-4009-40e4-9962-1429d0552497\">raised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322752\" id=\"question-wrapper-322752\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The whole eyebrows lowered.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322753\" id=\"question-wrapper-322753\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"750808ad-542b-4e7d-8f70-8a903088b587\">Lines formed around the eyes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322754\" id=\"question-wrapper-322754\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a60223d5-5d39-4df0-a009-c4a684133b81\">Lines formed above eyebrows<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"9240400e-0273-4f10-aed9-f7bc151e2804","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"tell lies","passagePhrase":"deceive"},{"uid":"bde67e8e-9ae3-445b-83c3-86c83b2b1c47","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"self-protection","passagePhrase":"protect themselves"},{"uid":"55ba0f6b-b357-4b34-be4c-4d3c86bb8cc7","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"detecting a lie","passagePhrase":"Detecting deceit"},{"uid":"9888e198-b7d6-4e98-b13c-7b1bfd1324c5","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Lying","passagePhrase":"telling a successful lie"},{"uid":"0725dbf3-75cb-4ffd-aa8c-055c0602125c","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"has to","passagePhrase":"need to"},{"uid":"38c99983-479f-4105-9474-c3cbc4a5815b","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"understand other people’s emotions","passagePhrase":"understand how other people feel"},{"uid":"8b46bbc7-d8be-4508-980c-2855f12ea2d4","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"breathing","passagePhrase":"respiration"},{"uid":"bbb89038-d22f-4f88-9288-c1a2d10ebcd0","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"pulse","passagePhrase":"heart rate"},{"uid":"a60edd7c-4e4f-4982-9686-1f10bd4b1f5d","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"lie-detector findings","passagePhrase":"polygraph results"},{"uid":"803e8ef8-2853-4f7a-84a1-f9a0f355800b","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"frequently not accepted as evidence","passagePhrase":"often inadmissible"},{"uid":"aed62b19-a4aa-49e4-9b06-318608736121","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"medical condition","passagePhrase":"stroke"},{"uid":"13ba51f7-2c11-4473-8256-875ec40c11b3","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"bypass conscious control","passagePhrase":"spontaneous smile"},{"uid":"a40c68be-be39-4a3d-a20f-bc7b6dc4d384","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"good at","passagePhrase":"skilled at"},{"uid":"241aea0e-caef-470e-944f-a7318e6f9ede","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"concealing","passagePhrase":"hiding"},{"uid":"775c51e4-0d3f-4814-92ef-2cff9bfed492","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"true emotional state","passagePhrase":"real feelings"},{"uid":"a60223d5-5d39-4df0-a009-c4a684133b81","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"Lines formed above eyebrows","passagePhrase":"forehead wrinkles"},{"uid":"a1e6a7f0-cb93-442e-a433-e9287130763d a4c3928b-7e2d-4196-bc57-a7c865c0f852","qNum":"10 13","questionPhrase":"Sadness","passagePhrase":"grief"},{"uid":"7b6ed4d2-4009-40e4-9962-1429d0552497","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"raised","passagePhrase":"move upwards"},{"uid":"a23e775b-1e93-4b81-b2cc-8cf81e92bedd","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Anger","passagePhrase":"angry scowl"},{"uid":"b718dfd4-40da-4836-bc57-4d14db2b4e2c","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Happiness","passagePhrase":"genuine smile"},{"uid":"750808ad-542b-4e7d-8f70-8a903088b587","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Lines formed around the eyes","passagePhrase":"lines commonly called crow’s-feet"}]},"reading_u2_53":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Aqua product: New Zealand's Algae Biodiesel</span></b></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> In May 2006, New Zealand's Aquaflow Bionomic Corporation announced a new biodiesel derived from sewage pond microalgae. The technology reached a major breakthrough in December 2007, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b0591ca0-dbdc-4e13-9da0-edf0eadcea5a\">when Massey University hosted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> the world's first public demonstration of this wild algae-based fuel. During the event, David Parker, Minister for Energy, successfully test-drove a Land Rover powered by Aquaflow's B5 blend, with politicians and media representatives in attendance. This successful trial confirmed the viability of wild algae as a low-cost, clean-energy feedstock for the country's future.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span>Algae-based biodiesel is anticipated to become an economical and cleaner fuel alternative for New Zealand's automobiles, with applications extending to boats, buses, heating systems, and power generation. A key advantage lies in supply: algae are available in abundance, thriving in nutrient-rich wastewater such as the settling ponds of Effluent Management Systems (EMS). They are both indigenous and renewable, capable of doubling their biomass within 24 hours under favourable conditions. Through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"23e048a6-522b-4acf-9a99-0e1b8af7adcd\">photosynthesis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, algae produce and store energy in the form of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"23e048a6-522b-4acf-9a99-0e1b8af7adcd\">lipids and combustible elements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> — the same compounds Aquaflow is striving to extract at competitive cost. Industry analysts estimate that algae growing in optimised ponds can yield up to 5,000 tonnes of biomass per hectare annually, generating multiple beneficial byproducts.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span>The process began when Aquaflow <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 21\" data-uid=\"1538f096-6be0-495a-af48-caf72aa0618e b9408816-2d91-44ab-ba90-cf74accd53db\">agreed</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1538f096-6be0-495a-af48-caf72aa0618e\"> to commence a pilot project with Marlborough District Council</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in 2005, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"b506bddc-691a-42ab-860a-7b3809d6508f\">extracting </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"831fd7ef-3677-4da5-ae5c-aef909040358 b506bddc-691a-42ab-860a-7b3809d6508f\">algae</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> from the council's 50-hectare Blenheim-based EMS ponds. By treating the primary contaminant of these ponds as a fuel feedstock, Aquaflow is simultaneously aiding the council's bioremediation process of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"344e5620-a047-4d35-a488-3bc8565264b6\">cleaning up water discharge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. The dual-purpose model carries significant <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"09758a9e-922f-46a9-972d-e44eba01c6d7\">cross-industry implications<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>: dairy farmers, food-processing facilities, and municipal water-treatment authorities could each adopt the same methodology to reap revenue from waste streams that currently incur disposal costs. Estimates suggest that fewer than 200 participating farms nationally could yield enough algal biomass to supply 8 percent of New Zealand's diesel demand by 2015.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"00167e45-96d7-4681-a899-5351d81a4554\">Compared with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"6bafbf32-bfd8-46a5-9d01-924441f6b211\">conventional biofuels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, algal biodiesel offers measurable advantages. Corn-based ethanol typically requires 0.6 hectares of arable land per 1,000 litres produced, while soy-based biodiesel needs approximately 1.5 hectares for the same output. Algae cultivation, by contrast, occupies no agricultural land and yields between 10 and 100 times more oil per hectare than soy. Production economics also favour algae: industry projections place mature algal biodiesel at NZ$0.85 per litre, against NZ$1.20 for soy-derived biodiesel and NZ$1.05 for corn ethanol. Crucially, algae do not compete with food crops for arable land, water, or fertiliser, sidestepping the food-versus-fuel controversy that has dogged first-generation biofuels since the mid-2000s and prompted policy reviews in the European Union and the United States.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>E. </span></b><span>The biofuels are blended with mineral diesel rather than used in raw form, helping meet <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"2a6a2e0e-9de3-4e04-a39f-cc718e0f23d0\">New Zealand's </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 22\" data-uid=\"2a6a2e0e-9de3-4e04-a39f-cc718e0f23d0 e63cde89-7383-4a73-9242-0d8addb8a8c4\">B5 target</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"588357fb-f1ae-4019-a553-6cab6f5ff301\">5 percent blending<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> introduced in 2008. Aquaflow plans to augment its production capacity from current <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1c66e795-8423-42f6-99af-b438417f44d5\">pilot-scale output<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to one million litres annually within the coming year, with a longer-term target of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"e63cde89-7383-4a73-9242-0d8addb8a8c4\">50 million litres<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> by 2015. The company is preparing a prospectus for potential investors before Christmas, aiming to woo capital for full commercial rollout. Independent carbon analysis suggests that algal biodiesel produces roughly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1eef603d-ca92-411f-884b-c985c138f372\">75 percent fewer net CO2 emissions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> over its full life cycle than fossil diesel — a credential the company actively highlights as evidence that the technology can contribute meaningfully to national emissions-reduction <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1eef603d-ca92-411f-884b-c985c138f372\">commitments under the Kyoto Protocol<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>F. </span></b><span>Not all observers share Aquaflow's optimism. Independent biofuel researchers have raised three <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7ca6fd6d-8208-4ac7-a183-892706ae6b83\">principal concern<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>s. First, scaling laboratory yields to industrial volumes has historically proven <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7ca6fd6d-8208-4ac7-a183-892706ae6b83\">difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>; several international algae-fuel ventures <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"bf2b90ab-3de4-4153-8006-6f3bb63c4d66\">failed to reach cost parity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> with fossil diesel between 2008 and 2012. Second, excessive algal blooms in untreated ponds may generate unbearable stench and tinting of water, creating <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7ca6fd6d-8208-4ac7-a183-892706ae6b83\">environmental risks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> if extraction lags behind growth. Third, downstream refining of lipid-rich algae into transport-grade fuel remains <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7ca6fd6d-8208-4ac7-a183-892706ae6b83\">energy-intensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, potentially offsetting the carbon advantage. A 2009 University of Auckland study concluded that algal biodiesel would become <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c4c67ab8-7014-4ab4-bd5f-35d36d881fde\">commercially viable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> only if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"0983a062-85f4-4e40-a017-f234bfe63cc5\">extraction efficiency improved by 30 percent and feedstock collection became fully automated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"19\"><b><span>G. </span></b><span>Beyond fuel, algae underpin an ethnic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"39e28237-f896-4931-be30-98fd41d76ffd\">dietary tradition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> spanning continents — Japanese cuisine incorporates over 20 species, while Chinese cooking uses more than 70. Commercially cultivated strains, including Spirulina, Chlorella, and Dunaliella, are marketed as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"39e28237-f896-4931-be30-98fd41d76ffd\">health supplements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> rich in B-vitamins, iodine, iron, and calcium. Algal pigments serve as an eco-friendly alternative to synthetic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"39e28237-f896-4931-be30-98fd41d76ffd\">dyes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, while seaweed-derived compounds are routinely processed as <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 24\" data-uid=\"39e28237-f896-4931-be30-98fd41d76ffd cd67688f-eb1c-47a9-be0a-86ac42094c58\">fertiliser</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> or <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 24\" data-uid=\"39e28237-f896-4931-be30-98fd41d76ffd cd67688f-eb1c-47a9-be0a-86ac42094c58\">livestock feed</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. Aquaflow's invention is subject to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"98b0c284-6b03-4507-be1e-28b58309a894\">provisional patent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> that prevents competitors from using the technology illegally. From a sustainability perspective, the noticeable feature of algaculture is that growth inputs — wastewater, sunlight, and carbon dioxide — exist naturally in plentiful supply, making the complete production cycle a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"f94d851e-15a1-4ff4-8e8f-f69d2b3c6b9e\">sustainable disposal route for organic effluent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and a prominent component of broader aquaculture.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs B-G from the list below. Write the correct number, </span><b><span>i-x</span></b><span>, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>List of Headings</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7ca6fd6d-8208-4ac7-a183-892706ae6b83\">Limits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"bf2b90ab-3de4-4153-8006-6f3bb63c4d66\">slow wider fuel adoption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. A pioneering <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1538f096-6be0-495a-af48-caf72aa0618e\">partnership<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"09758a9e-922f-46a9-972d-e44eba01c6d7\">wide-ranging relevance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. Government policy on renewable energy</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"23e048a6-522b-4acf-9a99-0e1b8af7adcd\">biological foundations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of algae as fuel feedstock</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. Failure of international biofuel ventures</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. How algal biodiesel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"00167e45-96d7-4681-a899-5351d81a4554\">compares<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"6bafbf32-bfd8-46a5-9d01-924441f6b211\">earlier alternatives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"39e28237-f896-4931-be30-98fd41d76ffd\">Non-fuel uses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"f94d851e-15a1-4ff4-8e8f-f69d2b3c6b9e\">ecological balance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. Public unveiling of a new fuel innovation</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. The chemistry of converting biomass to liquid fuel</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"x\"><span>x. From <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1c66e795-8423-42f6-99af-b438417f44d5\">trial output<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"e63cde89-7383-4a73-9242-0d8addb8a8c4\">national fuel use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1eef603d-ca92-411f-884b-c985c138f372\">climate value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p><span>Example: Paragraph A — viii</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322755\" id=\"question-wrapper-322755\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>B. Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322756\" id=\"question-wrapper-322756\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>C. Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322757\" id=\"question-wrapper-322757\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>D. Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322758\" id=\"question-wrapper-322758\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>E. Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">x</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322759\" id=\"question-wrapper-322759\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>F. Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322760\" id=\"question-wrapper-322760\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>G. Paragraph G</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements [Questions 20-23] and the list of organisations below. Match each statement with the correct organisation, A-E. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Organisations</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Aquaflow Bionomic Corporation</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Marlborough District Council</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Massey University</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. New Zealand Government</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. University of Auckland</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322761\" id=\"question-wrapper-322761\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b0591ca0-dbdc-4e13-9da0-edf0eadcea5a\">provided the venue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> for the public demonstration of the biodiesel</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322762\" id=\"question-wrapper-322762\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"b9408816-2d91-44ab-ba90-cf74accd53db\">permitted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"b506bddc-691a-42ab-860a-7b3809d6508f\">collection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"831fd7ef-3677-4da5-ae5c-aef909040358\">algae-bearing material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> for fuel production</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322763\" id=\"question-wrapper-322763\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>set a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"2a6a2e0e-9de3-4e04-a39f-cc718e0f23d0\">national rule<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> requiring a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"588357fb-f1ae-4019-a553-6cab6f5ff301\">fixed renewable share<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in diesel sales</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322764\" id=\"question-wrapper-322764\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>stated the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"0983a062-85f4-4e40-a017-f234bfe63cc5\">improvements needed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> before the technology could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c4c67ab8-7014-4ab4-bd5f-35d36d881fde\">make money<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322765\" id=\"question-wrapper-322765\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Algae have already been widely applied in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"cd67688f-eb1c-47a9-be0a-86ac42094c58\">agriculture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, such as being processed as ______ for soil.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">fertilizer/fertiliser</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322766\" id=\"question-wrapper-322766\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Growing algae in places like ponds for the purpose of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"344e5620-a047-4d35-a488-3bc8565264b6\">addressing water contaminants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> is known as ______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">bioremediation</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322767\" id=\"question-wrapper-322767\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"98b0c284-6b03-4507-be1e-28b58309a894\">protect its intellectual property rights<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> on the algae biodiesel, a ______ is essential for Aquaflow.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">patent</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b0591ca0-dbdc-4e13-9da0-edf0eadcea5a","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"provided the venue","passagePhrase":"when Massey University hosted"},{"uid":"23e048a6-522b-4acf-9a99-0e1b8af7adcd","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"biological foundations","passagePhrase":"photosynthesis ... lipids and combustible elements"},{"uid":"1538f096-6be0-495a-af48-caf72aa0618e b9408816-2d91-44ab-ba90-cf74accd53db","qNum":"15 21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"agreed"},{"uid":"1538f096-6be0-495a-af48-caf72aa0618e","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"partnership","passagePhrase":"to commence a pilot project with Marlborough District Council"},{"uid":"b506bddc-691a-42ab-860a-7b3809d6508f","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"collection","passagePhrase":"extracting"},{"uid":"831fd7ef-3677-4da5-ae5c-aef909040358 b506bddc-691a-42ab-860a-7b3809d6508f","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"algae"},{"uid":"344e5620-a047-4d35-a488-3bc8565264b6","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"addressing water contaminants","passagePhrase":"cleaning up water discharge"},{"uid":"09758a9e-922f-46a9-972d-e44eba01c6d7","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"wide-ranging relevance","passagePhrase":"cross-industry implications"},{"uid":"00167e45-96d7-4681-a899-5351d81a4554","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"compares","passagePhrase":"Compared with"},{"uid":"6bafbf32-bfd8-46a5-9d01-924441f6b211","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"earlier alternatives","passagePhrase":"conventional biofuels"},{"uid":"2a6a2e0e-9de3-4e04-a39f-cc718e0f23d0","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"national rule","passagePhrase":"New Zealand's"},{"uid":"2a6a2e0e-9de3-4e04-a39f-cc718e0f23d0 e63cde89-7383-4a73-9242-0d8addb8a8c4","qNum":"17 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"B5 target"},{"uid":"588357fb-f1ae-4019-a553-6cab6f5ff301","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"fixed renewable share","passagePhrase":"5 percent blending"},{"uid":"1c66e795-8423-42f6-99af-b438417f44d5","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"trial output","passagePhrase":"pilot-scale output"},{"uid":"e63cde89-7383-4a73-9242-0d8addb8a8c4","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"national fuel use","passagePhrase":"50 million litres"},{"uid":"1eef603d-ca92-411f-884b-c985c138f372","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"climate value","passagePhrase":"75 percent fewer net CO2 emissions ... commitments under the Kyoto Protocol"},{"uid":"7ca6fd6d-8208-4ac7-a183-892706ae6b83","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Limits","passagePhrase":"principal concern ... difficult ... environmental risks ... energy-intensive"},{"uid":"bf2b90ab-3de4-4153-8006-6f3bb63c4d66","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"slow wider fuel adoption","passagePhrase":"failed to reach cost parity"},{"uid":"c4c67ab8-7014-4ab4-bd5f-35d36d881fde","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"make money","passagePhrase":"commercially viable"},{"uid":"0983a062-85f4-4e40-a017-f234bfe63cc5","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"improvements needed","passagePhrase":"extraction efficiency improved by 30 percent and feedstock collection became fully automated"},{"uid":"39e28237-f896-4931-be30-98fd41d76ffd","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Non-fuel uses","passagePhrase":"dietary tradition ... health supplements ... dyes"},{"uid":"39e28237-f896-4931-be30-98fd41d76ffd cd67688f-eb1c-47a9-be0a-86ac42094c58","qNum":"19 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fertiliser ... livestock feed"},{"uid":"98b0c284-6b03-4507-be1e-28b58309a894","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"protect its intellectual property rights","passagePhrase":"provisional patent"},{"uid":"f94d851e-15a1-4ff4-8e8f-f69d2b3c6b9e","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"ecological balance","passagePhrase":"sustainable disposal route for organic effluent"},{"uid":"b9408816-2d91-44ab-ba90-cf74accd53db","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"permitted","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"831fd7ef-3677-4da5-ae5c-aef909040358","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"algae-bearing material","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"cd67688f-eb1c-47a9-be0a-86ac42094c58","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"agriculture","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_54":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Jean Piaget (1896–1980)</span></b></p><p><i><span>Seymour Papert looks at the work of the pioneering Swiss philosopher and psychologist</span></i></p><p><span>Jean Piaget spent much of his professional life listening to children, watching children and poring over reports of researchers around the world who were doing the same. He found, to put it most succinctly, that children don’t think like grown-ups. After thousands of interactions with young people often barely old enough to talk, Piaget began to suspect that behind their cute and seemingly irrational utterances were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"0bc6bcf7-3364-4c24-9b16-64c242b4f2ce\">thought processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> that had their own kind of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"a80cdb2c-bae1-4c0a-aab0-1549ac705956\">order and their own special logic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Einstein called it “a discovery so simple that only a genius could have thought of it.”</span></p><p><span>Although not an educational reformer, Piaget championed a way of thinking about children that provided <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"7508a925-2156-4de3-bd7c-466d9514684d\">the foundation for today’s education-reform movements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. It was a shift comparable to the way modern anthropology displaced stories of primitive tribes being ‘</span><i><span>noble savages</span></i><span>’ and ‘cannibals’. One might say that Piaget was the first to take children’s thinking seriously. </span></p><p><span>He has been revered by generations of teachers inspired by the belief that children are not empty vessels to be filled with knowledge [as traditional pedagogical theory had it] but active builders of knowledge—little scientists who are constantly creating and testing their own <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"28b66ee1-e233-4e6c-bb67-7bce97e19ade\">hypotheses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> about the world. And though he may not be as famous as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f0ec4099-9d3d-4007-831a-0c6e0d0a4066\">Sigmund Freud or even B. F. Skinner<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, his <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31 34\" data-uid=\"b1ab429c-224e-4353-b819-3d7d08e3c3d6 c1727836-a2d8-48b0-beb6-5cc1fbb8fe4b\">influence</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"c1727836-a2d8-48b0-beb6-5cc1fbb8fe4b\"> on psychology</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> may be longer lasting.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"d35836e9-c82a-49a2-a525-86690ae6ddbc\">In 1920<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, while doing research in a child-psychology laboratory in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"d35836e9-c82a-49a2-a525-86690ae6ddbc\">Paris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, Piaget noticed that children of the same age made similar errors on intelligence tests. Fascinated by their reasoning processes, he began to suspect that the key to human knowledge might be discovered by observing how the child’s mind develops. On his return to Switzerland he began watching children play, scrupulously recording their words and actions as their minds raced to find reasons for why things are the way they are. In one of his most famous experiments, Piaget asked children, ‘</span><i><span>What makes the wind?</span></i><span>’ A typical dialogue would be:</span></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Piaget</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><i><span>What makes the wind?</span></i></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Julia</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><i><span>The trees.</span></i></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Piaget</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><i><span>How do you know?</span></i></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Julia</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><i><span>I saw them waving their arms.</span></i></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Piaget</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><i><span>How does that make the wind?</span></i></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"2\"><p><b><span>Julia</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><i><span>(waving her hand in front of his face)</span></i></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><i><span>Like this. Only they are bigger. And there are lots of trees.</span></i></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><span>Piaget recognised that five-year-old Julia’s beliefs, while not correct by any adult criterion, are not ‘incorrect’ either. They are entirely sensible and coherent within the framework of the child’s way of knowing. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"28a238c4-1485-4f4a-85fe-cde2e03f159d\">Classifying them as ‘</span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"28a238c4-1485-4f4a-85fe-cde2e03f159d\">true</span></span></i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"28a238c4-1485-4f4a-85fe-cde2e03f159d\">’ or ‘</span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"28a238c4-1485-4f4a-85fe-cde2e03f159d\">false<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></i><span>’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a46baaaa-fdc5-4564-aeab-2eb68822d9ea\">misses the point<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and shows a lack of respect for the child. What Piaget was after was a theory that the wind dialogue demonstrated coherence, ingenuity and the practice of a kind of explanatory principle that stands young children in very good stead when they don’t know enough or don’t have enough skill to handle the kind of explanation that grown-ups prefer.</span></p><p><span>Piaget was not an educator and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"12b3a75a-1a58-46cd-8187-1c090ad1dd99\">never laid down rules<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> about how to intervene in such situations. But his work strongly suggests that the automatic reaction of putting the child right may well be counter-productive. If their theories are always greeted by ‘</span><i><span>Nice try, but this is how it really is________</span></i><span>’ they might <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"0452d17c-8cf6-4781-9c58-05b0611aaf02\">give up after a while on making theories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. As Piaget put it, ‘</span><i><span>children have real understanding only of that which they invent themselves, and each time that we try to teach them something too quickly, we keep them from inventing it themselves.</span></i><span>’</span></p><p><span>Disciples of Piaget have a tolerance for—indeed a fascination with—children’s primitive laws of physics: that things disappear when they are out of sight; that the moon and the sun follow you around; that big things float and small things sink. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"910a4766-d7e5-40cf-8b84-129c447c3aff\">Einstein was intrigued by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> Piaget’s findings, especially by the idea that seven-year-olds <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"089508a2-674b-4231-b61d-ec215b4f6c6d\">insist that going faster can take more time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>—perhaps because this, like Einstein’s own theories of relativity, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"089508a2-674b-4231-b61d-ec215b4f6c6d\">runs so contrary to common sense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Although every teacher <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"22f80d0f-df58-43e5-894f-9e3f4981ee4a\">in training<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> still memorises Piaget’s successive stages of childhood development, the greater part of Piaget’s work is less well known, perhaps because schools of education regard it as ‘</span><i><span>too deep</span></i><span>’ for teachers. Piaget never thought of himself as a child psychologist. His real interest was epistemology—the theory of knowledge—which, like physics, was considered a branch of philosophy until Piaget came along and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e81d1370-f0fc-4a4e-b706-266392e74196\">made it a science<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Through epistemology, Piaget explored multiple ways of knowing. He acknowledged them and examined them non-judgementally, yet with a philosopher’s analytic rigour. Since Piaget, the territory has been widely colonised by those who write about women’s ways of knowing, Afrocentric ways of knowing, even the computer’s ways of knowing. Indeed, artificial intelligence and the information-processing model of the mind owe more to Piaget than its proponents may realise.</span></p><p><span>The core of Piaget is his belief that looking carefully at how knowledge develops in children will elucidate the nature of knowledge in general. Whether this has in fact led to deeper understanding remains, like everything about Piaget, controversial. In the past decade, Piaget has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"74652c12-161e-4aae-9a2a-6f39aa7c163e\">vigorously challenged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> by the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"530e0209-0649-478c-a53c-33b659b90e48\">current fashion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"92f317ef-7870-45b9-bfef-5bf188473afa\">viewing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> knowledge <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"92f317ef-7870-45b9-bfef-5bf188473afa\">as an intrinsic property of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> the brain. Ingenious experiments have demonstrated that newborn infants already have some of the knowledge that Piaget believed children constructed. But for those, like me, who still see Piaget as the giant in the field of cognitive theory, the difference between what the baby brings and what the adult has is so immense that the new discoveries do not significantly reduce the gap, but only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"a55dff92-47c2-489f-9fc1-cf30f6ad02d0\">increase the mystery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322768\" id=\"question-wrapper-322768\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the second paragraph, the writer mentions the example of modern anthropology to illustrate</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the&nbsp;universality of Piaget’s insights into the workings of the mind.</li> <li>B. the similarity between children’s thought-processing in different cultures.</li> <li>C. how Piaget’s work represents a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"7508a925-2156-4de3-bd7c-466d9514684d\">crucial turning-point in our approach to education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>D. how Piaget’s work has aided our understanding of humankind’s evolution from primitive origins.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322769\" id=\"question-wrapper-322769\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the writer, what point is illustrated by the dialogue about the wind?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"28a238c4-1485-4f4a-85fe-cde2e03f159d\">factual accuracy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of what children say is of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a46baaaa-fdc5-4564-aeab-2eb68822d9ea\">minor significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Children want to learn about scientific principles.</li> <li>C. Children’s reasoning processes can be amusing to adults.</li> <li>D. Children often pretend that they know the answers to questions.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322770\" id=\"question-wrapper-322770\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Piaget believed in the importance of</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. preventing children from making false assumptions.</li> <li>B. giving children honest feedback on their hypotheses.</li> <li>C. showing children how to formulate their own ideas about the world.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"0452d17c-8cf6-4781-9c58-05b0611aaf02\">maintaining children’s confidence in their ability to interpret the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322771\" id=\"question-wrapper-322771\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the writer suggest in the seventh paragraph?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Children’s sense of their surroundings changes as they get older.</li> <li>B. Children are able to grasp certain complex ideas as well as adults are.</li> <li>C. Even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"089508a2-674b-4231-b61d-ec215b4f6c6d\">apparently irrational ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"910a4766-d7e5-40cf-8b84-129c447c3aff\">worthy of interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Sometimes the simplest explanations are the best.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322772\" id=\"question-wrapper-322772\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer’s main purpose is to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. outline Piaget’s contribution to a range of scientific fields.</li> <li>B. summarise how education has benefited from Piaget’s findings.</li> <li>C. discuss Piaget’s role in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"c1727836-a2d8-48b0-beb6-5cc1fbb8fe4b\">development of 20th-century psychology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>D. express&nbsp;doubts about a number of Piaget’s theories.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, A–I, below. Write the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 32–36 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. correct </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"28b66ee1-e233-4e6c-bb67-7bce97e19ade\">theories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. brain</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. simple </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. teachers </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. psychology</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"a80cdb2c-bae1-4c0a-aab0-1549ac705956\">logical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. thought </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. philosophers</span></p><p><span>Piaget maintained that children’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"0bc6bcf7-3364-4c24-9b16-64c242b4f2ce\">mental processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> were far more (32)______ than they might appear. He encouraged the view that a child was not a ‘blank slate’ waiting to be filled with information, but rather a systematic builder of knowledge who regularly tries out his or her own (33)______ about the world. Piaget’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"b1ab429c-224e-4353-b819-3d7d08e3c3d6\">impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> on the area of (34)______ could well outlast that of more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f0ec4099-9d3d-4007-831a-0c6e0d0a4066\">celebrated pioneers of this discipline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. His principles are still widely used in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"22f80d0f-df58-43e5-894f-9e3f4981ee4a\">professional development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of (35)______, although the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"530e0209-0649-478c-a53c-33b659b90e48\">current view<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"92f317ef-7870-45b9-bfef-5bf188473afa\">associating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> knowledge <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"92f317ef-7870-45b9-bfef-5bf188473afa\">exclusively with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> the (36)______ has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"74652c12-161e-4aae-9a2a-6f39aa7c163e\">cast doubts over<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> his ideas.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322773\" id=\"question-wrapper-322773\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322774\" id=\"question-wrapper-322774\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322775\" id=\"question-wrapper-322775\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322776\" id=\"question-wrapper-322776\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322777\" id=\"question-wrapper-322777\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322778\" id=\"question-wrapper-322778\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Piaget’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"d35836e9-c82a-49a2-a525-86690ae6ddbc\">early work in Paris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> involved innovative research techniques.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322779\" id=\"question-wrapper-322779\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Piaget <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"12b3a75a-1a58-46cd-8187-1c090ad1dd99\">gave clear guidelines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> as to how adults should give information to children.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322780\" id=\"question-wrapper-322780\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Piaget <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e81d1370-f0fc-4a4e-b706-266392e74196\">made a significant contribution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> to the field of epistemology.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322781\" id=\"question-wrapper-322781\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"a55dff92-47c2-489f-9fc1-cf30f6ad02d0\">We still have much to learn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> about the nature of knowledge.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0bc6bcf7-3364-4c24-9b16-64c242b4f2ce","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"mental processes","passagePhrase":"thought processes"},{"uid":"a80cdb2c-bae1-4c0a-aab0-1549ac705956","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"logical","passagePhrase":"order and their own special logic"},{"uid":"7508a925-2156-4de3-bd7c-466d9514684d","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"crucial turning-point in our approach to education","passagePhrase":"the foundation for today’s education-reform movements"},{"uid":"28b66ee1-e233-4e6c-bb67-7bce97e19ade","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"theories","passagePhrase":"hypotheses"},{"uid":"f0ec4099-9d3d-4007-831a-0c6e0d0a4066","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"celebrated pioneers of this discipline","passagePhrase":"Sigmund Freud or even B. F. Skinner"},{"uid":"b1ab429c-224e-4353-b819-3d7d08e3c3d6 c1727836-a2d8-48b0-beb6-5cc1fbb8fe4b","qNum":"31 34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"influence"},{"uid":"c1727836-a2d8-48b0-beb6-5cc1fbb8fe4b","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"development of 20th-century psychology","passagePhrase":"on psychology"},{"uid":"d35836e9-c82a-49a2-a525-86690ae6ddbc","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"early work in Paris","passagePhrase":"In 1920 ... Paris"},{"uid":"28a238c4-1485-4f4a-85fe-cde2e03f159d","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"factual accuracy","passagePhrase":"Classifying them as ‘ ... true ... ’ or ‘ ... false"},{"uid":"a46baaaa-fdc5-4564-aeab-2eb68822d9ea","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"minor significance","passagePhrase":"misses the point"},{"uid":"910a4766-d7e5-40cf-8b84-129c447c3aff","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"worthy of interest","passagePhrase":"Einstein was intrigued by"},{"uid":"089508a2-674b-4231-b61d-ec215b4f6c6d","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"apparently irrational ideas","passagePhrase":"insist that going faster can take more time ... runs so contrary to common sense"},{"uid":"22f80d0f-df58-43e5-894f-9e3f4981ee4a","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"professional development","passagePhrase":"in training"},{"uid":"e81d1370-f0fc-4a4e-b706-266392e74196","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"made a significant contribution","passagePhrase":"made it a science"},{"uid":"74652c12-161e-4aae-9a2a-6f39aa7c163e","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"cast doubts over","passagePhrase":"vigorously challenged"},{"uid":"530e0209-0649-478c-a53c-33b659b90e48","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"current view","passagePhrase":"current fashion"},{"uid":"92f317ef-7870-45b9-bfef-5bf188473afa","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"associating ... exclusively with","passagePhrase":"viewing ... as an intrinsic property of"},{"uid":"a55dff92-47c2-489f-9fc1-cf30f6ad02d0","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"We still have much to learn","passagePhrase":"increase the mystery"},{"uid":"b1ab429c-224e-4353-b819-3d7d08e3c3d6","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"impact","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_55":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The History of the Pencil</span></b></p><p><i><span>How a chance discovery in an English valley reshaped writing, warfare and industry</span></i></p><p><span>The history of the pencil begins, improbably, with a violent thunderstorm. When particularly ferocious weather struck the Lake District in north-west England during the sixteenth century, villagers in Borrowdale found that a large tree had been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"8da6722e-be64-410e-bfb6-e0f063079079\">uprooted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. Beneath its exposed roots lay an unfamiliar black substance, slightly shiny and smooth to the touch, which left a dark smear on the hands of anyone who handled it. Why the deposit had remained unnoticed for so long is debatable: some historians attribute it to the remoteness of the valley, while others argue that the local economy simply had no use for such a material until the storm forced it into view. Either way, the consequences of that single event would extend far beyond a quiet farming community.</span></p><p><span>The first recorded use of the material was strik<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c0659f76-672b-4b08-8831-52a6b6c92e6c\">in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>gly humble. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"9dc40235-c204-4529-8104-4d5aed44b7b6\">Local farmers used it to mark<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> their sheep, since it adhered stuck to wool and resisted rain. Before long, however, others recognised a more far-reaching possibility, namely that the substance could be used to write on paper. In its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e3a41821-b81d-4c93-9bce-173e7b682387\">untreated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> state it was extremely soft, and therefore <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f98027a3-af8b-4051-bf35-14bd0d3e7f4b\">messy to handle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, so people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c0659f76-672b-4b08-8831-52a6b6c92e6c\">enclosed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> a thin core of it in stiff <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"365ed9dc-6170-4385-9be5-2d9dd192df40\">sheep hides<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> or in lengths of rope. Because chemistry was still in its infancy, the new material was poorly understood. Searching for a name, scholars settled on plumbago, Latin for that which acts or writes like lead. The label was later corrected to graphite once it became clear that the deposit contained no lead at all, yet language proved more durable than chemistry: we still speak of the lead of a pencil, a small linguistic fossil of an error long since disproved.</span></p><p><span>Graphite owes its strategic importance to a single physical property. With a melting point of roughly 3,500 degrees Celsius, it could withstand temperatures that destroyed most other linings, and this made it invaluable to the British army and navy. The Royal Ordnance, the weaponry division of the armed forces, used graphite to line the moulds in which cannonballs were cast. Because the moulds resisted heat and released the metal cleanly, Britain could produce cannonballs faster and more cheaply than its European rivals, gaining an advantage that was as much economic as military. Recognising this dual value, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"69028fcd-89fa-4378-993e-44d159c57820\">government assumed control<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of the Borrowdale mines during the sixteenth century. Armed guards escorted the graphite all the way to the metal foundries beside the naval shipyards in southern England. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"71b44737-2bff-4990-b17a-1ee5bb2fb9cc\">deposit was so valuable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> that locals, who called it wadd, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"812707e1-2798-466a-a756-adc3e6dca7d8\">began<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> stealing it, and in 1752 an Act of Parliament made the theft of graphite punishable by imprisonment, a measure that reveals just how precious the material had become.</span></p><p><span>If Britain controlled the raw material, it was elsewhere that the pencil took its modern shape. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"3378e580-c053-4e99-8260-aae63ec404f5\">Italian craftsmen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> are usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"aacaa860-839f-419c-9524-a8a7b69ae816\">credited with inventing the wooden casing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>: they hollowed out two thin sections of cedar, laid a rod of graphite into one, glued the second over the top, and left the halves to set, producing the familiar object recognisable today. German manufacturers then transformed the craft into an industry by applying early mass-production techniques. The most significant breakthrough, however, came from France. In the late 1700s, Nicolas-Jacques Conté, an officer in Napoleon Bonaparte’s army, devised a method of mixing powdered graphite with clay and firing the mixture in a kiln. The proportions could be adjusted at will: adding more clay <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"539e4c31-89bc-4b50-ae4c-ab4b0b773193\">produced a harder, sharper and more precise mark<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, while adding more graphite produced one that was softer, thicker and darker. For the first time, the quality of a pencil could be controlled rather than left to the chance composition of the ore.</span></p><p><span>Conté’s innovation had a lasting and somewhat unexpected consequence. Because hardness and blackness could now be varied deliberately, manufacturers needed a way to describe the differences, and the result was the grading system still used worldwide. In it, H denotes the hardness of the pencil and B its blackness, with an HB pencil occupying the middle ground as a standard, all-purpose tool; further letters and numbers designate the remaining grades. It is worth noting that this orderly system was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"1fa2d136-e0dd-4047-b0b4-e9d0eb9ff3dc\">not imposed from above but emerged gradually<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> as different makers converged on a shared vocabulary, which helps explain why it took hold so thoroughly and why no rival scheme ever displaced it.</span></p><p><span>The geography of graphite has shifted considerably since those early days. China now produces most of the world’s pencils, yet the Borrowdale mines remain the only significant source of graphite in its near-pure form anywhere in the world. The highest grade there is now exhausted, although lower grades survive, and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"7246f7a7-a551-4257-a592-1ccebf2b14d8\">England’s pencil industry continues to thrive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in the nearby town of Keswick. The pencil itself has proved remarkably resilient, surviving well into the high-tech age, a persistence often illustrated by a popular anecdote. The story claims that the American space programme spent millions developing a pen that could write in zero gravity, while the Russians simply handed their astronauts ordinary pencils. The tale is appealing but false. In reality, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"2e141e19-36d9-4984-986c-96d7cd8e08c4\">astronauts of both nations used pencils on their earliest flights<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, and a private company later developed the zero-gravity pen that astronauts of every nation now use. The myth endures less because it is accurate than because it flatters a particular view of practical wisdom over expensive ingenuity. Whatever the truth of that contrast, pencils remain in use in every classroom, drawing office and art studio in the world, and there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a910808d-1aae-40ef-8b11-9ad5a1b8e201\">little to suggest we will soon find anything better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"8104a268-8bbe-4f35-ba82-a4c4094a6369\">graphite to write with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below. </span></p><p><span>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 1–6 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The early history of graphite in Britain</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Graphite was first discovered beneath a (1)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"8da6722e-be64-410e-bfb6-e0f063079079\">blown down in a storm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></li><li><span>Graphite’s earliest practical role was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"9dc40235-c204-4529-8104-4d5aed44b7b6\">helping farmers identify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> (2)________</span></li><li><span>The characteristics of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e3a41821-b81d-4c93-9bce-173e7b682387\">raw<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> graphite:</span></li></ul><ul><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f98027a3-af8b-4051-bf35-14bd0d3e7f4b\">dirty to use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> because it is so (3)________</span></li><li><span>originally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c0659f76-672b-4b08-8831-52a6b6c92e6c\">covered in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> (4)________ or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"365ed9dc-6170-4385-9be5-2d9dd192df40\">animal skin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to make it usable as a pencil.</span></li></ul><ul><li><span>Graphite came to the notice of the government for military and commercial purposes.</span></li></ul><ul><li><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"69028fcd-89fa-4378-993e-44d159c57820\">government completely took over<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> the (5)________ at Borrowdale.</span></li><li><span>They employed guards to protect the graphite on its journey south.</span></li></ul><ul><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"71b44737-2bff-4990-b17a-1ee5bb2fb9cc\">The prospect of making money<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> led nearby residents to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"812707e1-2798-466a-a756-adc3e6dca7d8\">start<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (6)________ graphite.</span></li></ul><ul><li><span>The government passed a law to protect the graphite industry.</span></li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322782\" id=\"question-wrapper-322782\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">tree</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322783\" id=\"question-wrapper-322783\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">sheep</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322784\" id=\"question-wrapper-322784\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">soft</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322785\" id=\"question-wrapper-322785\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">rope</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322786\" id=\"question-wrapper-322786\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">mines</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322787\" id=\"question-wrapper-322787\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">stealing</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 7–13 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322788\" id=\"question-wrapper-322788\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"3378e580-c053-4e99-8260-aae63ec404f5\">The Italians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> were the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"aacaa860-839f-419c-9524-a8a7b69ae816\">first to make pencils out of wood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322789\" id=\"question-wrapper-322789\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Germans used different types of wood to produce pencils.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322790\" id=\"question-wrapper-322790\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Adding more clay to a pencil makes it <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"539e4c31-89bc-4b50-ae4c-ab4b0b773193\">write more darkly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322791\" id=\"question-wrapper-322791\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The HB grading system was the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"1fa2d136-e0dd-4047-b0b4-e9d0eb9ff3dc\">result of a single official decision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322792\" id=\"question-wrapper-322792\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"7246f7a7-a551-4257-a592-1ccebf2b14d8\">English pencil factories have now all closed down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322793\" id=\"question-wrapper-322793\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"2e141e19-36d9-4984-986c-96d7cd8e08c4\">American astronauts used pencils on their early journeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> into space.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322794\" id=\"question-wrapper-322794\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The author believes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"8104a268-8bbe-4f35-ba82-a4c4094a6369\">graphite pencils<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a910808d-1aae-40ef-8b11-9ad5a1b8e201\">unlikely to be replaced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in the near future.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"8da6722e-be64-410e-bfb6-e0f063079079","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"blown down in a storm","passagePhrase":"uprooted"},{"uid":"c0659f76-672b-4b08-8831-52a6b6c92e6c","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"covered in","passagePhrase":"in ... enclosed"},{"uid":"9dc40235-c204-4529-8104-4d5aed44b7b6","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"helping farmers identify","passagePhrase":"Local farmers used it to mark"},{"uid":"e3a41821-b81d-4c93-9bce-173e7b682387","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"raw","passagePhrase":"untreated"},{"uid":"f98027a3-af8b-4051-bf35-14bd0d3e7f4b","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"dirty to use","passagePhrase":"messy to handle"},{"uid":"365ed9dc-6170-4385-9be5-2d9dd192df40","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"animal skin","passagePhrase":"sheep hides"},{"uid":"69028fcd-89fa-4378-993e-44d159c57820","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"government completely took over","passagePhrase":"government assumed control"},{"uid":"71b44737-2bff-4990-b17a-1ee5bb2fb9cc","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"The prospect of making money","passagePhrase":"deposit was so valuable"},{"uid":"812707e1-2798-466a-a756-adc3e6dca7d8","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"start","passagePhrase":"began"},{"uid":"3378e580-c053-4e99-8260-aae63ec404f5","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"The Italians","passagePhrase":"Italian craftsmen"},{"uid":"aacaa860-839f-419c-9524-a8a7b69ae816","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"first to make pencils out of wood","passagePhrase":"credited with inventing the wooden casing"},{"uid":"2e141e19-36d9-4984-986c-96d7cd8e08c4","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"American astronauts used pencils on their early journeys","passagePhrase":"astronauts of both nations used pencils on their earliest flights"},{"uid":"a910808d-1aae-40ef-8b11-9ad5a1b8e201","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"unlikely to be replaced","passagePhrase":"little to suggest we will soon find anything better"},{"uid":"8104a268-8bbe-4f35-ba82-a4c4094a6369","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"graphite pencils","passagePhrase":"graphite to write with"}]},"reading_u2_56":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Bringing Back the Bittern</span></b></p><p><span>How research, not luck, reversed the decline of one of Britain’s most secretive birds</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><b><span>A. </span></b><span>The bittern is a heron-like wetland bird whose fortunes in Britain have swung dramatically over little more than a century. Breeding birds had vanished entirely by 1886, yet after re-colonisation in the early 1900s the population climbed to a peak of roughly 70 booming, or singing, males in the 1950s. From there it fell sharply, dropping below 20 by the 1990s. By the late 1980s it was obvious that the species was again in trouble, but conservationists faced an awkward problem: they could see the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a2acbf31-f065-45b0-a384-059a5136e76a\">decline </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14 24\" data-uid=\"2e5e3373-3653-47a8-b417-90b4746cfeaf a2acbf31-f065-45b0-a384-059a5136e76a\">without understanding its causes</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, and almost no reliable information existed on which to base a recovery. Saving the bird would therefore depend less on goodwill than on first <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"2e5e3373-3653-47a8-b417-90b4746cfeaf\">learning how it lived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span>That task was complicated by the bittern itself. Its mottled plumage and retiring habits keep it hidden deep within reedbeds, so the first challenge was simply to develop a dependable way of monitoring a bird that is rarely seen. The solution lay in sound. During the breeding season the male produces a distinctive booming call, and researchers discovered that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"68cf2cc0-8c92-4eb8-b680-6ddbeda28404\">acoustic pattern of each bird is effectively unique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. By analysing these patterns they could not only establish how many males were present nationally, but also recognise individuals from one year to the next, which in turn allowed local survival rates to be estimated. A bird that resisted direct observation had, in effect, been persuaded to identify itself.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span>With a counting method in place, attention turned to habitat. The earliest insight came not from new fieldwork but from comparison: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"0c58aa40-7fce-49ee-9c60-ef8dcca3594c\">sites that had lost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> their booming males were set against <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"0c58aa40-7fce-49ee-9c60-ef8dcca3594c\">those that had kept them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"0c58aa40-7fce-49ee-9c60-ef8dcca3594c\">contrast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> was revealing. Bitterns had persisted precisely where the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"79382014-d421-4615-bd1a-9fc59168b526\">natural<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> drying out of reedbeds, a process known as succession, had been deliberately <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"35f30265-b3a3-4b66-a2fe-101c95f08870\">slowed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> through management. This finding translated directly into action. Broad recommendations on restoring and maintaining reedbeds were drawn up, and EU LIFE funding enabled work at thirteen sites across the core breeding range. Although the project was led by the RSPB, its success depended on many other organisations, an early sign that recovery would be collaborative rather than the work of a single body.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span>General advice, however, was not the same as precise instruction, and the next phase aimed to replace broad guidance with exact prescriptions. By fitting male bitterns with radio tags at the Minsmere and Leighton Moss reserves, researchers could follow where the birds actually fed. A clear <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"02a0d1db-c7c3-4626-93c1-43c98269bd39\">preference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> emerged for the wetter margins of the reedbed, especially the fringes beside larger pools of open water. The average <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"81390653-3143-4e5b-a9c0-a74fbabe405f\">territory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> covered around twenty hectares, a figure that gave managers a concrete target for how much reedbed a new or restored site would need. The females told a different but equally important story: since they alone <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"81390653-3143-4e5b-a9c0-a74fbabe405f\">incubate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> the eggs and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"81390653-3143-4e5b-a9c0-a74fbabe405f\">raise the young<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, their needs mattered just as much. Of the eighty-seven <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"81390653-3143-4e5b-a9c0-a74fbabe405f\">nests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> located, most lay in unbroken vegetation well inside the reedbed, yet always where water remained even in the driest weeks of the season.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><b><span>E. </span></b><span>The effect of applying these prescriptions was striking. At Minsmere, where reedbeds were lowered to halt the drying process, the number of booming males climbed steadily from one to ten. Nationally, the population reached its lowest point of just eleven booming males in 1997 and then, for the first time since the 1950s, began to rise. The recovery was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"9e573e0a-7065-45b2-815c-5c678bf79cac\">not coincidental<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>; it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"9e573e0a-7065-45b2-815c-5c678bf79cac\">tracked the management work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> closely, with the clearest gains appearing exactly where the research-based methods had been applied. For a programme that had begun with almost no usable data, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"9e573e0a-7065-45b2-815c-5c678bf79cac\">match between effort and outcome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> was persuasive evidence that the underlying science was sound.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><b><span>F. </span></b><span>Even so, counting adults could not by itself secure the future, and a later phase examined the diet, survival and movements of the chicks. Tiny radio tags fitted to nestlings traced their fate up to fledging and beyond, and the findings were sobering: many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"84fbbee1-9162-4a8d-a0a3-45a1975c77e9\">chicks never survived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"cee30e3d-eab1-426b-8b1c-96f27ee23de0\">starvation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"07b5094e-cb49-4669-8a5f-8d27526850fe\">most probable cause<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. The fish they were fed came overwhelmingly from species that penetrate into the reed edge, which shifted the focus of conservation once again. If the chicks were starving, the reedbed had to support not only the birds but the fish on which they depended. Recent studies, including doctoral research at the University of Hull, have therefore concentrated on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"cee30e3d-eab1-426b-8b1c-96f27ee23de0\">water conditions needed to sustain native fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ff1f59c8-e1d7-47bd-81b6-7a94820fc29b\">treating the bird and its food supply as a single system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"20\"><b><span>G. </span></b><span>The final concern was longer term. Tracking showed that once independent, young bitterns disperse in their first winter to seek out new wetlands, and that some will settle to breed wherever conditions are suitable. This pointed to an obvious strategy: rather than concentrate the birds in a few vulnerable strongholds, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"71a32274-c166-43dd-ab3c-26bd0046d791\">create a spread of new sites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> for them to colonise. A second EU LIFE project has pursued exactly this, building a network of nineteen sites so that breeding can occur well beyond the original core. The logic is one of insurance as much as expansion, for a <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20 26\" data-uid=\"64c86338-d5c5-49d5-a969-6b952c75a401 71a32274-c166-43dd-ab3c-26bd0046d791\">dispersed population</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"64c86338-d5c5-49d5-a969-6b952c75a401\"> is far less exposed to chance disasters</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and to the rising sea levels that threaten low-lying reedbeds. By 2004 the number of booming males had recovered to 55, almost all of the increase occurring on sites managed according to the research. Science had been central to the story, but its lessons took effect only through the patience and sometimes drastic intervention of the landowners and wardens who applied them.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>The reading passage has seven paragraphs, A–G.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, i–ix, in boxes 14–20 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. Mapping the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"81390653-3143-4e5b-a9c0-a74fbabe405f\">species’ breeding needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"9e573e0a-7065-45b2-815c-5c678bf79cac\">Proof of intentional recovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a2acbf31-f065-45b0-a384-059a5136e76a\">Mystery downturn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. Creating space between nesting territories</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"68cf2cc0-8c92-4eb8-b680-6ddbeda28404\">Voice-based identification<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. The illusion of mature habitat abundance</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"cee30e3d-eab1-426b-8b1c-96f27ee23de0\">An unseen risk below the surface<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"0c58aa40-7fce-49ee-9c60-ef8dcca3594c\">Learning from opposite outcomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"71a32274-c166-43dd-ab3c-26bd0046d791\">Spreading the population to reduce future risks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322795\" id=\"question-wrapper-322795\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322796\" id=\"question-wrapper-322796\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322797\" id=\"question-wrapper-322797\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322798\" id=\"question-wrapper-322798\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322799\" id=\"question-wrapper-322799\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322800\" id=\"question-wrapper-322800\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322801\" id=\"question-wrapper-322801\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph G</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ix</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 21–23 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>How the bittern was counted and understood</span></b></p><p><span>Because the bittern is so difficult to observe, researchers based their first count on the male’s acoustic pattern, which proved to be unique to each bird and so allowed individuals to be recognised over time. Studies of habitat showed that the birds survived where the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"79382014-d421-4615-bd1a-9fc59168b526\">gradual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> (21)______ of the reedbed had been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"35f30265-b3a3-4b66-a2fe-101c95f08870\">restrained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Radio-tracking later revealed that males were especially <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"02a0d1db-c7c3-4626-93c1-43c98269bd39\">drawn to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the reedbed’s wetter (22)______, near expanses of open water. Research into the young birds found that (23)______ was probably the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"07b5094e-cb49-4669-8a5f-8d27526850fe\">main cause<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"84fbbee1-9162-4a8d-a0a3-45a1975c77e9\">high chick mortality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322802\" id=\"question-wrapper-322802\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">drying/succession</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322803\" id=\"question-wrapper-322803\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">margins/fringes</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322804\" id=\"question-wrapper-322804\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">starvation</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter A-D in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322805\" id=\"question-wrapper-322805\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the writer suggest was the main obstacle to saving the bittern in the late 1980s?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The population had already become too small to recover.</li> <li>B. There was insufficient funding for conservation work.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"2e5e3373-3653-47a8-b417-90b4746cfeaf\">Too little was understood about how the bird lived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Landowners were unwilling to change their practices.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322806\" id=\"question-wrapper-322806\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The reference to native fish in paragraph F shows that conservationists came to see that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ff1f59c8-e1d7-47bd-81b6-7a94820fc29b\">bittern could be saved only by managing its food supply as well<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</li> <li>B. fish were competing with bitterns for space in the reedbed.</li> <li>C. doctoral research had little practical value for the project.</li> <li>D. adult bitterns were more important to protect than chicks.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322807\" id=\"question-wrapper-322807\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why does the writer describe the second EU LIFE project as a form of “insurance”?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It guaranteed long-term funding for the existing reserves.</li> <li>B. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"64c86338-d5c5-49d5-a969-6b952c75a401\">spread the population so that local disasters would be less damaging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</li> <li>C. It protected the birds against disease in crowded reedbeds.</li> <li>D. It compensated landowners for managing their sites.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a2acbf31-f065-45b0-a384-059a5136e76a","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Mystery downturn","passagePhrase":"decline"},{"uid":"2e5e3373-3653-47a8-b417-90b4746cfeaf a2acbf31-f065-45b0-a384-059a5136e76a","qNum":"14 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"without understanding its causes"},{"uid":"2e5e3373-3653-47a8-b417-90b4746cfeaf","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Too little was understood about how the bird lived","passagePhrase":"learning how it lived"},{"uid":"68cf2cc0-8c92-4eb8-b680-6ddbeda28404","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Voice-based identification","passagePhrase":"acoustic pattern of each bird is effectively unique"},{"uid":"0c58aa40-7fce-49ee-9c60-ef8dcca3594c","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Learning from opposite outcomes","passagePhrase":"sites that had lost ... those that had kept them ... contrast"},{"uid":"79382014-d421-4615-bd1a-9fc59168b526","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"gradual","passagePhrase":"natural"},{"uid":"35f30265-b3a3-4b66-a2fe-101c95f08870","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"restrained","passagePhrase":"slowed"},{"uid":"02a0d1db-c7c3-4626-93c1-43c98269bd39","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"drawn to","passagePhrase":"preference"},{"uid":"81390653-3143-4e5b-a9c0-a74fbabe405f","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"species’ breeding needs","passagePhrase":"territory ... incubate ... raise the young ... nests"},{"uid":"9e573e0a-7065-45b2-815c-5c678bf79cac","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Proof of intentional recovery","passagePhrase":"not coincidental ... tracked the management work ... match between effort and outcome"},{"uid":"84fbbee1-9162-4a8d-a0a3-45a1975c77e9","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"high chick mortality","passagePhrase":"chicks never survived"},{"uid":"cee30e3d-eab1-426b-8b1c-96f27ee23de0","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"An unseen risk below the surface","passagePhrase":"starvation ... water conditions needed to sustain native fish"},{"uid":"07b5094e-cb49-4669-8a5f-8d27526850fe","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"main cause","passagePhrase":"most probable cause"},{"uid":"ff1f59c8-e1d7-47bd-81b6-7a94820fc29b","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"bittern could be saved only by managing its food supply as well","passagePhrase":"treating the bird and its food supply as a single system"},{"uid":"71a32274-c166-43dd-ab3c-26bd0046d791","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Spreading the population to reduce future risks","passagePhrase":"create a spread of new sites"},{"uid":"64c86338-d5c5-49d5-a969-6b952c75a401 71a32274-c166-43dd-ab3c-26bd0046d791","qNum":"20 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"dispersed population"},{"uid":"64c86338-d5c5-49d5-a969-6b952c75a401","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"spread the population so that local disasters would be less damaging","passagePhrase":"is far less exposed to chance disasters"}]},"reading_u2_57":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Conformity</span></b></p><p><i><span>A review of conformity and some of the studies that have been done on it</span></i></p><p><span>During your childhood, there will have been some kind of craze which affected all the people in your school. It may have been to do with a particular toy or possibly a must-have item of clothing. It may have been something as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"822c4083-85c0-45dc-80de-d2accf57ac9a\">simple as a type of pen or as expensive as an electronic games console<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Fashion designers, toy manufacturers and anyone else involved in the retail trade love conformity. Set up a craze, especially in the young, and everyone will go for it. In fact, it's an ideal way to sell huge quantities of merchandise. The levels of conformity in consumerism are phenomenal. When you actually stand back and consider how easily we are persuaded that having certain items is the only way we can ensure peace of mind, you see what an important concept conformity is.</span></p><p><span>Conformity has been described as “yielding to group pressure” (Crutchfield 1962). However, this implies that other people put pressure on us to make us conform, and this is not always the case. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"503368d5-880e-4983-81e3-628bce098d47\">A better definition is given by Aronson<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> (1976), who said it was a “change in a person's behaviour or opinions as a result of real or imagined pressure from a person or group of people.” This would make more sense, as often the pressure we feel is imagined. The person or group he refers to would have to be important to us at the time, regardless of their status.</span></p><p><span>There has been considerable research on conformity. One of the first studies looked at the answers people gave when asked to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ecb09ef4-5bb2-4e89-964c-5818ad6791df\">estimate the number of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> beans in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3301833c-e32e-448e-814c-80461071b13c\">bottle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> (Jennes, 1932). If you have ever entered a 'guess the number' competition, you probably looked at the previous estimates made and based your judgment on what other people had guessed. This is more or less what happened in the Jennes study. First of all, he asked the respondents to give their own estimates, and then he asked them to decide a group estimate. Finally, he asked them alone again and discovered that they had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"4b6a5712-2b5b-4d67-a6dc-399d64a3ec2b\">stayed with the group answer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Probably the most famous study on conformity was undertaken by Asch (1951), when he created a situation where many of his subjects <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"ad7bcff0-3ae4-4a0a-90ef-c2943ce76804\">gave<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> answers which were blatantly untrue, rather than contradict the people they were with. He did this by getting his subject to sit round a table with six <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f5785136-b415-4826-8e6c-5aee3de44b06\">stooges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> so that the subject was second to last. He showed them all a large card which had three lines of different lengths drawn on it, labelled A, B and C. He then gave them a card with a single line and asked them to match this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"de940d05-7242-4b9d-8334-e31dbadc710f\">in terms of length<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> to one of the lines A, B or C. The stooges gave untrue responses in a number of the trials, and the subjects were left in the situation where they either reported what they saw with their own eyes or conformed to the norm of the group.</span></p><p><span>When the results were assessed, Asch found that in one out of every three trials where the wrong answer was given, the subject gave the same wrong answer as the stooges. This led to an average level of conformity of 32 per cent. Asch interviewed his subjects after the trials to try to find out why they conformed to an answer which was so obviously wrong. Most of them said that they did not want to cause problems within the group, although they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0b3501d4-2e29-4285-90d5-0a3e32cf31fb\">admitted that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> when they did give wrong answers it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0b3501d4-2e29-4285-90d5-0a3e32cf31fb\">made them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> anxious. [Asch found that when there was just one other person present who did not go along with the majority, no matter how many others there were, it was sufficient to make the subject give the right answer.]</span></p><p><span>Kelman (1953) described three ways in which people may conform. The first is compliance. In this case, individuals outwardly accept the group’s position, although their personal opinion remains unchanged. This response reduces the risk of tension or unpleasantness within the group and allows relationships to remain harmonised. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"1cba75c8-3308-47de-b96c-bdd6ecaca4c4\">findings from the study by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> Asch show this clearly: participants publicly followed the group’s answer, while privately disagreeing with it. In other situations, people may experience internalisation. Here, individuals come to believe that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ab307ed9-7ec2-40bd-99f1-7de25753a5c8\">group’s judgement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"6943c439-6a1a-4ec6-bb92-c0c71f44891f\">is the more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> valid one. They may rationalise this shift by telling themselves that their own perception was unreliable, such as assuming their eyesight was poor. Sometimes, however, subjects actually seem to change their beliefs because they want to become more like their heroes. If they really want to become part of an in-group, they will start to identify with that group and take on the group's values and beliefs, even if they are different to their own. Kelman calls this identification. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"3e891a08-ff1f-4837-9a9e-3634832ddfe3\">frequently happens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> with teenagers who want to become more like a peer group in order to be accepted, and suddenly seem to go against all the values and beliefs of their parents. </span></p><p><span>So why is it that we have to conform? Some people feel confident most of the time, have high self-esteem and do not have to go along with the majority. For most of us, though, how confident we feel varies from day to day, depending on the situation we are in, and this can influence behaviour.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322808\" id=\"question-wrapper-322808\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Childhood crazes can center on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"822c4083-85c0-45dc-80de-d2accf57ac9a\">items of any value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322809\" id=\"question-wrapper-322809\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Children are more vulnerable to crazes now than they used to be.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322810\" id=\"question-wrapper-322810\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Consumers make too many quick decisions in shops.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322811\" id=\"question-wrapper-322811\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Crutchfield's definition of conformity is the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"503368d5-880e-4983-81e3-628bce098d47\">most reliable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Studies on conformity</span></b></p><p><span>In the Jennes study, people had to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ecb09ef4-5bb2-4e89-964c-5818ad6791df\">guess how many<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> (31)________ were in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3301833c-e32e-448e-814c-80461071b13c\">container<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Jennes found that, in most cases, people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"4b6a5712-2b5b-4d67-a6dc-399d64a3ec2b\">opted for an estimate given by a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> (32)________</span></p><p><span>Asch had his subjects (33)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"de940d05-7242-4b9d-8334-e31dbadc710f\">line lengths<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. To test the extent to which people would conform, he placed his subjects with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f5785136-b415-4826-8e6c-5aee3de44b06\">colleagues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"ad7bcff0-3ae4-4a0a-90ef-c2943ce76804\">provided<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> (34)________ responses. He found that his subjects agreed with his colleagues 32% of the time, although they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0b3501d4-2e29-4285-90d5-0a3e32cf31fb\">admitted to feeling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> (35)________ about giving their answer.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322812\" id=\"question-wrapper-322812\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">beans</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322813\" id=\"question-wrapper-322813\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">group</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322814\" id=\"question-wrapper-322814\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">match</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322815\" id=\"question-wrapper-322815\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">untrue/wrong</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322816\" id=\"question-wrapper-322816\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">anxious</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>Kelman's processes of social conformity</span></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Compliance</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>- people support the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ab307ed9-7ec2-40bd-99f1-7de25753a5c8\">majority view<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> despite their own ideas</span></p><p><span>- social harmony is maintained</span></p><p><span>- illustrated by the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"1cba75c8-3308-47de-b96c-bdd6ecaca4c4\">results of the research conducted by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> (</span><b><span>36)________</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(</span><b><span>37)________</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>- majority view is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"6943c439-6a1a-4ec6-bb92-c0c71f44891f\">considered more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> (</span><b><span>38)</span></b><b><span>________</span></b> </p><p><span>- people persuade themselves despite their own ideas</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(</span><b><span>39)________</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>- people change their ideas to those of the majority</span></p><p><span>- <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"3e891a08-ff1f-4837-9a9e-3634832ddfe3\">typical of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> (40)________</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322817\" id=\"question-wrapper-322817\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Asch</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322818\" id=\"question-wrapper-322818\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">internalization/internalisation</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322819\" id=\"question-wrapper-322819\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">valid</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322820\" id=\"question-wrapper-322820\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">identification</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322821\" id=\"question-wrapper-322821\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">teenagers</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"822c4083-85c0-45dc-80de-d2accf57ac9a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"items of any value","passagePhrase":"simple as a type of pen or as expensive as an electronic games console"},{"uid":"ecb09ef4-5bb2-4e89-964c-5818ad6791df","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"guess how many","passagePhrase":"estimate the number of"},{"uid":"3301833c-e32e-448e-814c-80461071b13c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"container","passagePhrase":"bottle"},{"uid":"4b6a5712-2b5b-4d67-a6dc-399d64a3ec2b","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"opted for an estimate given by a","passagePhrase":"stayed with the group answer"},{"uid":"ad7bcff0-3ae4-4a0a-90ef-c2943ce76804","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"provided","passagePhrase":"gave"},{"uid":"f5785136-b415-4826-8e6c-5aee3de44b06","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"colleagues","passagePhrase":"stooges"},{"uid":"de940d05-7242-4b9d-8334-e31dbadc710f","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"line lengths","passagePhrase":"in terms of length"},{"uid":"0b3501d4-2e29-4285-90d5-0a3e32cf31fb","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"admitted to feeling","passagePhrase":"admitted that ... made them"},{"uid":"1cba75c8-3308-47de-b96c-bdd6ecaca4c4","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"results of the research conducted by","passagePhrase":"findings from the study by"},{"uid":"ab307ed9-7ec2-40bd-99f1-7de25753a5c8","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"majority view","passagePhrase":"group’s judgement"},{"uid":"6943c439-6a1a-4ec6-bb92-c0c71f44891f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"considered more","passagePhrase":"is the more"},{"uid":"3e891a08-ff1f-4837-9a9e-3634832ddfe3","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"typical of","passagePhrase":"frequently happens"}]},"reading_u2_58":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Starting school later has positive effects on teens</span></b></p><p><span>A growing body of evidence demonstrates that adolescents benefit substantially from additional sleep. When school districts postpone the start of the academic day, measurable improvements tend to follow. With lessons that commence as early as 7 a.m. and buses that arrive well before sunrise, roughly 80 per cent of US children in grades 6 through 12 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f4ca316a-59cb-4f38-8a59-90cf85da2ff2\">fail to obtain the recommended quantity of sleep<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> during term time, according to research by the National Sleep Foundation, a sleep advocacy organisation. These <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"af83d1c4-f01d-45c4-b564-31ec51d09fad\">premature start times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> appear to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"59dad813-9d60-4e03-89d5-da7c848d8dd1\">contribute to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> a multitude of difficulties. Exhausted children, studies indicate, not only struggle with irritability, but also with symptoms of depression. They tend to gain weight, their academic grades deteriorate, and many resort to caffeine, with dubious consequences for productivity and uncertain effects upon the development of immature brains.</span></p><p><span>Now, propelled by accumulating research suggesting that adolescents are biologically predisposed to sleep late, and that delaying school start times by even a mere 30 minutes generates a pronounced difference in how well teenagers feel and perform, an increasing number of institutions across the United States are beginning the school day later than they formerly did. Many more are deliberating the question. Simultaneously, however, there remain entrenched pockets of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"18afb1f0-6510-4e31-940c-5dbdd767c278\">resistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> from administrators and parents who contend that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f7a6de69-a0f2-4c11-9bf0-7d785541413c\">bus schedules will become excessively complicated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, that a later commencement will interfere with extracurricular programmes, or that children will simply remain awake later if they realise they can sleep in somewhat longer.</span></p><p><span>According to Kyla Wahlstrom, director of the Center for Applied Research and Educational Improvement at the University of Minnesota, although the two districts she examined <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ef579917-decb-4083-8f0c-dccd23a00c3f\">could not have been more different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> in terms of race, socioeconomic status and other factors, beneficial changes in both places became apparent almost immediately.</span></p><p><span>Several of the outcomes were notably significant. For instance, students were perceptibly more alert during the first two periods of the day. Furthermore, the cafeteria was calmer, and fewer altercations erupted in the corridors. Students, who were now obtaining nearly an additional hour of sleep each night, reported that they felt less depressed. Even parents informed teachers that they considered their children <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"b82a43f1-b93e-4815-bb15-b9f634c3ca20\">easier to live with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> than before.</span></p><p><b><span>The melatonin shift</span></b></p><p><span>Biology, rather than laziness, should be held responsible for adolescents’ reluctance to rise in the morning. As children mature and approach puberty, a phase of profound biological transformation, their bodies begin to circulate melatonin—the hormone that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4e369176-7d92-4fa0-8444-a7ed9c31ea54\">induces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> sleepiness—approximately two hours later than they previously did.</span></p><p><span>Consequently, teenagers find it virtually impossible to fall asleep before roughly 11 p.m., even when they make a deliberate attempt to retire earlier. Yet adolescents nonetheless require an average of 9.25 hours of slumber each night. Superimposed upon this shift in natural sleeping and waking rhythms lies a second factor: a phase of intense drowsiness that afflicts both adults and adolescents during the early-morning hours. In adults, this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"20432659-2f9b-44f7-ad42-52c41b41f68c\">trough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in alertness occurs between 3 a.m. and 5 a.m.; in adolescents, it descends between approximately 5 a.m. and 7 a.m. The implication is that, while their alarm clocks instruct teenagers to leave their beds and demand that their brains perform, their bodies are simultaneously signalling them to continue sleeping.</span></p><p><span>Beyond these mood, behavioural and learning consequences, scientists are progressively uncovering more subtle mechanisms through which such chronic sleep deprivation can damage children. Certain studies, for example, demonstrate that insufficient sleep compromises the immune system. Others suggest that, when sleep is inadequate, the body <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"5f08258c-46ca-4a82-84c2-d2c725d9a75c\">secretes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"e65a6e0b-9021-4473-a123-3abb8f089df8\">elevated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> quantities of the hormones that trigger hunger, a process that may plausibly contribute to escalating rates of obesity.</span></p><p><span>In order to remain awake, young people frequently resort to coffee, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"31d9b0e9-4ecb-44ce-b190-101dc99a18d7\">soda<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> and other caffeinated beverages. At one public high school in the eastern US state of Massachusetts, 95 per cent of the students surveyed reported consuming caffeine within the preceding fortnight—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"70792794-4e0d-4cdf-8b20-71e97b58242b\">predominantly in the form of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> soda rather than coffee, and most commonly during the afternoon and evening hours—Dr Amy Wolfson and a colleague reported in the journal Health Education and Behavior. According to Dr Wolfson, no published guidelines currently specify how much caffeine constitutes an excessive amount for adolescents. The substance, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"172abbf7-9f52-4d5a-b023-9f0b273af5ea\">persists within the body for up to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> five hours—three hours longer than was originally assumed—thereby depriving teenagers of an indeterminate number of hours of sleep. Even when caffeinated teenagers do manage to fall asleep, caffeine demonstrably <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"23821bff-f762-470b-8b48-cf96d1e072fa\">renders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> the quality of that sleep <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"23821bff-f762-470b-8b48-cf96d1e072fa\">worse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. Finally, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"c91da057-4f83-49f0-a4a2-7ddeba1284f1\">no one yet understands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> how caffeine may influence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"5fb58787-59dd-4f1b-a8a6-f0665ce85790\">developing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> brains, although numerous experts remain concerned about the apparent connection between the sugar contained in soda and consequent weight gain.</span></p><p><b><span>Schools respond</span></b></p><p><span>As the body of sleep research continues to accumulate, an expanding number of schools are gravitating towards later start times. No one has formally documented precisely how many institutions have implemented the change, yet experts report that they are receiving a steadily increasing volume of enquiries from districts throughout the US, requesting advice on whether and how to adopt a later schedule. Whatever the practical obstacles, adolescents need to obtain sufficient sleep, and altering school start times has proven to be one effective means of achieving that objective.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 1–5 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322822\" id=\"question-wrapper-322822\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f4ca316a-59cb-4f38-8a59-90cf85da2ff2\">Sleep deprivation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> among children in the US is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"59dad813-9d60-4e03-89d5-da7c848d8dd1\">partly a result of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"af83d1c4-f01d-45c4-b564-31ec51d09fad\">current school starting times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322823\" id=\"question-wrapper-322823\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Research indicates that most overweight children need more sleep.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322824\" id=\"question-wrapper-322824\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f7a6de69-a0f2-4c11-9bf0-7d785541413c\">Concerns about rearranging bus timetables<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> make some people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"18afb1f0-6510-4e31-940c-5dbdd767c278\">oppose later school start times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322825\" id=\"question-wrapper-322825\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The two school districts in the Minnesota experiment had <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ef579917-decb-4083-8f0c-dccd23a00c3f\">similar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> groups of students.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322826\" id=\"question-wrapper-322826\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Parents and children in the two Minnesota school districts which were studied <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"b82a43f1-b93e-4815-bb15-b9f634c3ca20\">got along better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> than before.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 6–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The melatonin shift</span></b></p><p><b><span>Biological changes</span></b></p><ul><li><span>As teenagers approach (6)________, their internal body clock shifts, delaying the release of melatonin by about two hours.</span></li><li><span>Melatonin is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4e369176-7d92-4fa0-8444-a7ed9c31ea54\">responsible for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> feelings of (7)________ .</span></li></ul><p><b><span>Sleep and awake times</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Big <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"20432659-2f9b-44f7-ad42-52c41b41f68c\">drop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in (8)________ occurs later in the night</span></li><li><span>5 a.m.–7 a.m. for teens</span></li><li><span>3 a.m.–5 a.m. for adults</span></li></ul><p><b><span>Sleep loss</span></b></p><ul><li><span>leads to a weakened immune system</span></li><li><span>hormones that are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"5f08258c-46ca-4a82-84c2-d2c725d9a75c\">released<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"e65a6e0b-9021-4473-a123-3abb8f089df8\">increase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)________, causing risk of weight-related health problems</span></li></ul><p><b><span>Caffeine</span></b></p><ul><li><span>teens in the Massachusetts study <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"70792794-4e0d-4cdf-8b20-71e97b58242b\">usually get<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> caffeine by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"31d9b0e9-4ecb-44ce-b190-101dc99a18d7\">drinking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)________</span></li><li><span>effects can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"172abbf7-9f52-4d5a-b023-9f0b273af5ea\">last for a maximum of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)________</span></li><li><span>leads to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"23821bff-f762-470b-8b48-cf96d1e072fa\">decline in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> sleep (12)________</span></li><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"c91da057-4f83-49f0-a4a2-7ddeba1284f1\">no information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> on its impact on how the young people’s (13)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"5fb58787-59dd-4f1b-a8a6-f0665ce85790\">mature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></span></li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322827\" id=\"question-wrapper-322827\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">puberty</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322828\" id=\"question-wrapper-322828\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">sleepiness</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322829\" id=\"question-wrapper-322829\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">alertness</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322830\" id=\"question-wrapper-322830\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">hunger</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322831\" id=\"question-wrapper-322831\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">soda</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322832\" id=\"question-wrapper-322832\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">five/5 hours</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322833\" id=\"question-wrapper-322833\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">quality</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322834\" id=\"question-wrapper-322834\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">brains</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f4ca316a-59cb-4f38-8a59-90cf85da2ff2","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Sleep deprivation","passagePhrase":"fail to obtain the recommended quantity of sleep"},{"uid":"af83d1c4-f01d-45c4-b564-31ec51d09fad","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"current school starting times","passagePhrase":"premature start times"},{"uid":"59dad813-9d60-4e03-89d5-da7c848d8dd1","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"partly a result of","passagePhrase":"contribute to"},{"uid":"18afb1f0-6510-4e31-940c-5dbdd767c278","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"oppose later school start times","passagePhrase":"resistance"},{"uid":"f7a6de69-a0f2-4c11-9bf0-7d785541413c","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Concerns about rearranging bus timetables","passagePhrase":"bus schedules will become excessively complicated"},{"uid":"b82a43f1-b93e-4815-bb15-b9f634c3ca20","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"got along better","passagePhrase":"easier to live with"},{"uid":"4e369176-7d92-4fa0-8444-a7ed9c31ea54","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"responsible for","passagePhrase":"induces"},{"uid":"20432659-2f9b-44f7-ad42-52c41b41f68c","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"drop","passagePhrase":"trough"},{"uid":"5f08258c-46ca-4a82-84c2-d2c725d9a75c","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"released","passagePhrase":"secretes"},{"uid":"e65a6e0b-9021-4473-a123-3abb8f089df8","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"increase","passagePhrase":"elevated"},{"uid":"31d9b0e9-4ecb-44ce-b190-101dc99a18d7","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"drinking","passagePhrase":"soda"},{"uid":"70792794-4e0d-4cdf-8b20-71e97b58242b","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"usually get","passagePhrase":"predominantly in the form of"},{"uid":"172abbf7-9f52-4d5a-b023-9f0b273af5ea","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"last for a maximum of","passagePhrase":"persists within the body for up to"},{"uid":"23821bff-f762-470b-8b48-cf96d1e072fa","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"decline in","passagePhrase":"renders ... worse"},{"uid":"c91da057-4f83-49f0-a4a2-7ddeba1284f1","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"no information","passagePhrase":"no one yet understands"},{"uid":"5fb58787-59dd-4f1b-a8a6-f0665ce85790","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"mature","passagePhrase":"developing"}]},"reading_u2_59":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Boring Buildings</span></b></p><p><i><span>There could be more than an economic or nostalgic price to impersonal retail and high-rise construction; boring architecture may take an emotional toll on the people forced to live with it.</span></i></p><p><b><span>A </span></b><span>A growing body of research in cognitive science illuminates the physical and mental toll that bland cityscapes take on residents. Generally, these researchers argue that humans are healthier when they live surrounded by variety, or work in well-designed, unique spaces, rather than in unattractive, generic ones. Urban policy professor Justin Hollander and architect Ann Sussman review scientific data to help architects and urban planners understand how, exactly, people respond to their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"74f4a136-c95d-40dc-af7a-1308784e9c93\">built surroundings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1b1313b4-6f75-4854-9827-22d0ca11bdeb\">particularly at work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. People, they argue, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1b1313b4-6f75-4854-9827-22d0ca11bdeb\">function best<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"74f4a136-c95d-40dc-af7a-1308784e9c93\">intricate settings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, not ‘big, blank, boxy offices’.</span></p><p><b><span>B </span></b><span>Indeed, that is what Colin Nellard, a neuroscientist at the University of Waterloo in Canada, has found in his work. Five years ago, Nellard became interested in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"59c31fed-33e8-4d03-be6b-9b12daa0d50b\">a certain building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> — the gigantic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"59c31fed-33e8-4d03-be6b-9b12daa0d50b\">Whole Foods Market<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> ‘plopped into’ a notoriously textured part of lower Manhattan in New York. Nellard partnered with the Guggenheim Museum to analyse what happens when someone walks out of a tiny neighbourhood restaurant and encounters a full city block with nothing but ‘the long, blank facade of the Whole Foods Market’ building.</span></p><p><span>In 2011, Nellard led small groups on Lower East Side walks to measure the effect of the urban environment on them. Participants recorded their responses to questions at each stopping point and wore sensors that measured skin conductance, a response to emotional excitement. Passing the monolithic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"bb1b1a2a-b5e4-45e6-8f3b-472c49a9b322\">Whole Foods Market<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, people’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"00c3bbae-c6bd-4bcb-adeb-f8a867cffa83\">state of arousal plummeted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Physiologically, Nellard explained, they were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"aae41916-265c-4612-bf4f-4303e3138793\">bored<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, and to describe this place they used words like ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"aae41916-265c-4612-bf4f-4303e3138793\">bland<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>’ and ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"aae41916-265c-4612-bf4f-4303e3138793\">passionless<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>’. In contrast, one block east at the other test site — a ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"bb1b1a2a-b5e4-45e6-8f3b-472c49a9b322\">lively sea of restaurants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> with lots of open doors and windows’ — people measured <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"00c3bbae-c6bd-4bcb-adeb-f8a867cffa83\">high levels of excitement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, and they listed words like ‘lively’ and ‘socialising’. Nellard explains that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"1f15f3a5-904a-453d-ad92-09a1cced0959\">main objective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"26993fad-63c6-4a6b-89eb-14ef23842e4f\">urban design<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> should be to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"509205bc-9898-4a56-830d-2104a3ee6ce5\">produce some kind of novelty or change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> every few seconds; otherwise, we become cognitively disengaged.</span></p><p><b><span>C </span></b><span>The trick, it seems, is to design a world that excites but does not overload our faculties with a constant barrage of information. ‘We are, as animals, programmed to respond to thrill,’ said professor Brendan Walker. In Walker’s ‘thrill laboratory’ at the University of Nottingham in the UK, devices measure heart rate and skin conductance to see how people respond to adrenaline-producing experiences such as a roller-coaster ride. A thrilling encounter moves us quickly from a state of equilibrium to a desirable ‘disorientation’. ‘Humans want a certain element of turmoil or confusion,’ he said. ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"9fc0e6a8-9779-4c50-8318-a3894e319390\">Complexity is thrilling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, whether in an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"479d193e-0a86-406f-9459-887ee7f17a00\">amusement park<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> or in architecture.’</span></p><p><b><span>D </span></b><span>Psychologists have found that awe-inspiring moments can potentially improve our well-being. One study, conducted by Melanie Rudd, Kathleen Vohs and Jennifer Aaker of Stanford University in the US, showed that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"1029048d-d222-41bb-b7c5-b287bd4f8d04\">feeling of ‘awe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>’ can make people more patient and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"a91beab7-05ba-4b38-8310-d75710fab646\">less materialistic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. In an experiment, the researchers showed students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"390665e1-bdbe-41b2-9740-e6bceebc8ccf\">60-second clips<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of waterfalls, whales, or astronauts in space. After only a minute of these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"390665e1-bdbe-41b2-9740-e6bceebc8ccf\">virtual images<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, those who said they were awed also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"4b9d8392-d8da-43b0-8417-20b1ccc34d88\">felt less pressed for time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. In another variation, people made hypothetical choices between physical and experiential goods of equal monetary value. Those who had just ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"1029048d-d222-41bb-b7c5-b287bd4f8d04\">felt awe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>’ were more likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"a91beab7-05ba-4b38-8310-d75710fab646\">choose an experience over a possession<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, a choice that is linked with greater satisfaction in the long run. In other words, a visual buzz — whether architectural or natural — might have the ability to change our frame of mind, making modern-day life more satisfying and interactive.</span></p><p><b><span>E </span></b><span>It is important to note, however, that architectural boredom is not about how pristine a street is. People often confuse successful architecture with whether an area looks <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6ca4e442-7125-499b-ac94-d936c47fff71\">pleasant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. On the contrary, when it comes to city buildings, people often focus too narrowly on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6ca4e442-7125-499b-ac94-d936c47fff71\">aesthetics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, said Charles Montgomery, author of Happy City: Transforming Our Lives Through Urban Design. Some of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5a91f6cd-264f-4a8b-8c03-56e90727643a\">happiest blocks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in New York City, he argues, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5a91f6cd-264f-4a8b-8c03-56e90727643a\">are ‘kind of ugly and messy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>’.</span></p><p><span>In 2014, Montgomery’s Happy City lab conducted an experiment in which he found a strong correlation between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"d7abab3b-c20f-4c29-b6b0-93dc4ac169cf\">messier blocks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b814aeda-3c28-4226-9512-6cafaf4c00eb\">pro-social behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Montgomery sent researchers, posing as lost tourists, to places he coded as either ‘active’ or ‘inactive’ facades. He concluded that the former had a high level of interest — that is, they were messy — while the latter had no special features, such as long warehouse blocks. Pedestrians at active sites were nearly five times more likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b814aeda-3c28-4226-9512-6cafaf4c00eb\">offer assistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> than at inactive ones, and of those who assisted, seven times as many at the active site offered the use of their phone.</span></p><p><b><span>F </span></b><span>Fortunately, it is not necessarily a dichotomy — new architecture can achieve the optimal level of cacophony and beauty. Take the 2006 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"7b92058c-13f1-4d57-8648-0544107f306b\">Hearst Tower<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in midtown Manhattan. Designed by architect Norman Foster, Hearst Tower is a glass-and-steel skyscraper, 40 stories of which are designed in a triangular pattern, differing in style from the 1920s Art Deco base. From the outside, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"4bb9458b-4df3-4893-9553-68c3c62b1981\">facade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"05d64279-c9b4-4087-94eb-1c7d1fb74c15\">jolts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"47fda1b6-1978-465b-a72d-1f7e2ab145df\">city dwellers from their daily commutes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, while <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14 24\" data-uid=\"05d64279-c9b4-4087-94eb-1c7d1fb74c15 0e978d43-7eda-43ef-96a0-27516ac71263\">energising</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"0e978d43-7eda-43ef-96a0-27516ac71263\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14 24\" data-uid=\"0e978d43-7eda-43ef-96a0-27516ac71263 47fda1b6-1978-465b-a72d-1f7e2ab145df\">employees</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> who enter it each morning. For many who walk by, Hearst Tower’s design may not be the easiest to understand; it is both sleek and old, and the top looks as though it travelled from the future. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"e1950b4d-1ea0-4b42-9824-80ff564c6bdb\">Inside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"5aec55d1-89a9-4de7-8dcb-33101f3e3b1a\">workers travel upon<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> diagonal escalators, up a three-story water sculpture, through the tower’s historic atrium, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"833d42ef-1119-46f3-91c7-01f1246e526b\">flooded with light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Few New Yorkers who pass by would find this building boring — and they are likely to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"0e978d43-7eda-43ef-96a0-27516ac71263\">happier<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, maybe even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"0e978d43-7eda-43ef-96a0-27516ac71263\">nicer to each other<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, because of it.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six sections, A–F.</span></p><p><span>Which section contains the following information?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322835\" id=\"question-wrapper-322835\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"7b92058c-13f1-4d57-8648-0544107f306b\">description of a building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> that has a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"0e978d43-7eda-43ef-96a0-27516ac71263\">positive effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322836\" id=\"question-wrapper-322836\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"74f4a136-c95d-40dc-af7a-1308784e9c93\">architecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> affecting people’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1b1313b4-6f75-4854-9827-22d0ca11bdeb\">performance in their jobs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322837\" id=\"question-wrapper-322837\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>examples of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"00c3bbae-c6bd-4bcb-adeb-f8a867cffa83\">intensity of people’s reactions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"bb1b1a2a-b5e4-45e6-8f3b-472c49a9b322\">two urban settings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322838\" id=\"question-wrapper-322838\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>details of a study where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"390665e1-bdbe-41b2-9740-e6bceebc8ccf\">seeing certain pictures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"4b9d8392-d8da-43b0-8417-20b1ccc34d88\">reduced people’s stress<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322839\" id=\"question-wrapper-322839\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a claim about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"9fc0e6a8-9779-4c50-8318-a3894e319390\">feelings experienced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in response to both architecture and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"479d193e-0a86-406f-9459-887ee7f17a00\">leisure settings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 19–23) and the list of researchers below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct researcher, A, B, C or D.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 19–23 on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><i><span>NB</span></i><i><span>You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of Researchers</span></b></p><p><span>A Colin Nellard</span></p><p><span>B Brendan Walker</span></p><p><span>C Rudd, Vohs and Aaker</span></p><p><span>D Charles Montgomery</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322840\" id=\"question-wrapper-322840\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"1f15f3a5-904a-453d-ad92-09a1cced0959\">aim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"26993fad-63c6-4a6b-89eb-14ef23842e4f\">good city planning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"509205bc-9898-4a56-830d-2104a3ee6ce5\">provide variety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in architecture.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322841\" id=\"question-wrapper-322841\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"d7abab3b-c20f-4c29-b6b0-93dc4ac169cf\">untidy areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b814aeda-3c28-4226-9512-6cafaf4c00eb\">more helpful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322842\" id=\"question-wrapper-322842\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People who had recently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"1029048d-d222-41bb-b7c5-b287bd4f8d04\">felt amazed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"a91beab7-05ba-4b38-8310-d75710fab646\">placed less importance on material goods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322843\" id=\"question-wrapper-322843\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6ca4e442-7125-499b-ac94-d936c47fff71\">Attractive’ places<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5a91f6cd-264f-4a8b-8c03-56e90727643a\">not necessarily the most enjoyable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> places to be.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322844\" id=\"question-wrapper-322844\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"59c31fed-33e8-4d03-be6b-9b12daa0d50b\">One particular building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"aae41916-265c-4612-bf4f-4303e3138793\">failed to provide visual stimulation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>Hearst Tower</span></b></p><p><span>Norman Foster’s Hearst Tower was built in 2006. The 40-storey modern triangular-patterned building is made of glass and steel, contrasting with the base, which is in the style of the 1920s. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"4bb9458b-4df3-4893-9553-68c3c62b1981\">sight of the building’s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> (24)________ has a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"05d64279-c9b4-4087-94eb-1c7d1fb74c15\">striking impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"47fda1b6-1978-465b-a72d-1f7e2ab145df\">commuters and employees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. Some passers-by may find the building’s design confusing, as it mixes old and new elements. (25)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"5aec55d1-89a9-4de7-8dcb-33101f3e3b1a\">transport employees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"e1950b4d-1ea0-4b42-9824-80ff564c6bdb\">through the tower<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, passing a large water sculpture on the way in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"833d42ef-1119-46f3-91c7-01f1246e526b\">light-filled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26)________</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322845\" id=\"question-wrapper-322845\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">facade</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322846\" id=\"question-wrapper-322846\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">escalators</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322847\" id=\"question-wrapper-322847\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">atrium</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"74f4a136-c95d-40dc-af7a-1308784e9c93","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"architecture","passagePhrase":"built surroundings ... intricate settings"},{"uid":"1b1313b4-6f75-4854-9827-22d0ca11bdeb","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"performance in their jobs","passagePhrase":"particularly at work ... function best"},{"uid":"59c31fed-33e8-4d03-be6b-9b12daa0d50b","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"One particular building","passagePhrase":"a certain building ... Whole Foods Market"},{"uid":"bb1b1a2a-b5e4-45e6-8f3b-472c49a9b322","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"two urban settings","passagePhrase":"Whole Foods Market ... lively sea of restaurants"},{"uid":"00c3bbae-c6bd-4bcb-adeb-f8a867cffa83","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"intensity of people’s reactions","passagePhrase":"state of arousal plummeted ... high levels of excitement"},{"uid":"aae41916-265c-4612-bf4f-4303e3138793","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"failed to provide visual stimulation","passagePhrase":"bored ... bland ... passionless"},{"uid":"1f15f3a5-904a-453d-ad92-09a1cced0959","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"aim","passagePhrase":"main objective"},{"uid":"26993fad-63c6-4a6b-89eb-14ef23842e4f","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"good city planning","passagePhrase":"urban design"},{"uid":"509205bc-9898-4a56-830d-2104a3ee6ce5","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"provide variety","passagePhrase":"produce some kind of novelty or change"},{"uid":"9fc0e6a8-9779-4c50-8318-a3894e319390","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"feelings experienced","passagePhrase":"Complexity is thrilling"},{"uid":"479d193e-0a86-406f-9459-887ee7f17a00","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"leisure settings","passagePhrase":"amusement park"},{"uid":"1029048d-d222-41bb-b7c5-b287bd4f8d04","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"felt amazed","passagePhrase":"feeling of ‘awe ... felt awe"},{"uid":"a91beab7-05ba-4b38-8310-d75710fab646","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"placed less importance on material goods","passagePhrase":"less materialistic ... choose an experience over a possession"},{"uid":"390665e1-bdbe-41b2-9740-e6bceebc8ccf","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"seeing certain pictures","passagePhrase":"60-second clips ... virtual images"},{"uid":"4b9d8392-d8da-43b0-8417-20b1ccc34d88","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"reduced people’s stress","passagePhrase":"felt less pressed for time"},{"uid":"6ca4e442-7125-499b-ac94-d936c47fff71","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Attractive’ places","passagePhrase":"pleasant ... aesthetics"},{"uid":"5a91f6cd-264f-4a8b-8c03-56e90727643a","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"not necessarily the most enjoyable","passagePhrase":"happiest blocks ... are ‘kind of ugly and messy"},{"uid":"d7abab3b-c20f-4c29-b6b0-93dc4ac169cf","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"untidy areas","passagePhrase":"messier blocks"},{"uid":"b814aeda-3c28-4226-9512-6cafaf4c00eb","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"more helpful","passagePhrase":"pro-social behaviour ... offer assistance"},{"uid":"7b92058c-13f1-4d57-8648-0544107f306b","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"description of a building","passagePhrase":"Hearst Tower"},{"uid":"4bb9458b-4df3-4893-9553-68c3c62b1981","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"sight of the building’s","passagePhrase":"facade"},{"uid":"05d64279-c9b4-4087-94eb-1c7d1fb74c15","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"striking impact","passagePhrase":"jolts"},{"uid":"47fda1b6-1978-465b-a72d-1f7e2ab145df","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"commuters and employees","passagePhrase":"city dwellers from their daily commutes"},{"uid":"05d64279-c9b4-4087-94eb-1c7d1fb74c15 0e978d43-7eda-43ef-96a0-27516ac71263","qNum":"14 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"energising"},{"uid":"0e978d43-7eda-43ef-96a0-27516ac71263","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"positive effect","passagePhrase":"happier ... nicer to each other"},{"uid":"0e978d43-7eda-43ef-96a0-27516ac71263 47fda1b6-1978-465b-a72d-1f7e2ab145df","qNum":"14 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"employees"},{"uid":"e1950b4d-1ea0-4b42-9824-80ff564c6bdb","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"through the tower","passagePhrase":"Inside"},{"uid":"5aec55d1-89a9-4de7-8dcb-33101f3e3b1a","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"transport employees","passagePhrase":"workers travel upon"},{"uid":"833d42ef-1119-46f3-91c7-01f1246e526b","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"light-filled","passagePhrase":"flooded with light"}]},"reading_u2_60":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Communication of Science</span></b></p><p><span>Science plays an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"e54eb814-43c0-477c-8ca1-857006223279\">increasingly significant role in people’s lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, making the communication by journalists in the popular media of scientific developments more important than ever. Yet such communication is fraught with challenges that can easily distort discussions and lead to unnecessary confusion. Some problems stem from the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"727a4cb8-3bc3-4d95-9846-ba8cbcd26932\">esoteric nature of current research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and the associated difficulty of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"aa04f32d-552f-48e5-8627-5c508bdc69bd\">coming up with sufficiently faithful terminology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. Abstraction and complexity are not signs that a given scientific direction is wrong, but are instead a tribute to the success of human ingenuity in meeting the challenges that nature presents. They can, however, make communication more difficult.</span></p><p><span>But many of the biggest challenges for scientific reporting arise because, in areas of evolving research, scientists tend to be specialists, and often only partly realise the significance of any particular advance or development. Since that partial understanding applies to most of the scientific developments that directly affect people’s lives, such as cancer research and diet studies, learning how to overcome it is critical to stimulating a more informed scientific debate among the broader public.</span></p><p><span>Ambiguous word choices are the source of some misunderstandings. Scientists often employ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"248ab3b9-6353-46c2-b075-7238c391cb45\">common terminology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, to which they then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"6107e286-f8fe-40b4-a77d-feb2bcb64cd4\">assign a specific meaning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that is impossible to fathom without a precise definition. Take Einstein’s famous theory of relativity. The term ‘relativity’ here is intrinsically misleading. Many interpret the theory to mean that everything is relative and there are no absolutes. Yet although the measurements any observer makes depend on his coordinates and reference frame, according to Einstein’s theory, the physical phenomena he measures, in fact, have an invariant description that transcends that observer’s particular coordinates. The physical phenomena are not relative. Even Einstein admitted that the term relativity was probably misleading.</span></p><p><span>But not all communication problems stem solely from poor word choices. Some are inherent in the intrinsically complex nature of much of modern science. Science sometimes transcends this limitation: remarkably, chemists were able to detail the precise <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b88cbbd0-c2ad-4b5f-a462-f6e0d04421ec\">chemical processes involved in the destruction of the ozone layer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, so the evidence that chlorofluorocarbon gases (Freon, for example) were destroying the ozone layer was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b928e411-8570-4b75-a434-d96901bef9d8\">successfully conveyed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to the public.</span></p><p><span>How journalists report scientific developments on vital issues of the day that are less well understood, or in which the connection is less direct, is a more complicated question. Global warming patterns are a case in point. Even if we understand some effects of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere, it is difficult to predict the precise chain of events that a marked increase in carbon dioxide will cause. The distillation of results presented to the public in such cases should reflect at least some of the subtleties of the most current developments.</span></p><p><span>Balanced reporting, of course, can help public understanding when there is genuine uncertainty or when competing interpretations are still strongly supported by evidence. Journalists should seek to provide opposing or competing views on controversial issues only when those views reflect a real division within the scientific community. Almost all newly discovered results will have some supporters and some opponents, and only time and further evidence will clarify the true story. However, in the global warming debate, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"d49c7f69-d187-4324-9ae8-6bc20fb44a33\">press often continued to present<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the issue as though scientists were evenly divided, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"d49c7f69-d187-4324-9ae8-6bc20fb44a33\">even after<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the bulk of the scientific community had recognised the seriousness of the problem. In this case, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d6df10b5-53fc-496c-aade-e338f50db4a4\">attempt to give equal weight to both sides<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"78f55596-2299-4744-80bf-6c505f0842d9\">did not improve public understanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"7494bc6e-d17d-4cde-913c-a3fedf916fc1\">instead, it created a misleading impression<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of uncertainty.</span></p><p><span>A better understanding by the general public of the mathematical significance of results would <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"1d4a1acc-aae3-4230-ae3d-394a62a82ca2\">help to clarify many scientific discussions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. Statistical analysis can show whether particular results are significant or could occur simply by chance. A few years ago, the Harvard University faculty was tortured by empty debates over the relative intrinsic differences in the scientific abilities of men and women. One of the more amusing aspects of the discussion was that those who believed in the differences and those who didn’t used the same evidence in their opposing arguments about gender-specific scientific ability. How could that be? The answer is that the data did show gender differences, but no statistically significant differences in inherent scientific ability based on gender.</span></p><p><span>There are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"1df92aab-08cf-41f1-80b8-0ef70d5b48b1\">steps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> we can take to improve public understanding of scientific developments. The first would be to inculcate greater understanding and acceptance of indirect scientific evidence not directly observable <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3c8e3e79-8d76-4f55-9631-0fe1aeabd0c1\">by human scientists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. The information from an unmanned space mission is no less legitimate than the information from one in which people are on board. Second, we might need different standards for evaluating science with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"3ffa6d0a-984d-4d7e-bb53-2bb86278c5fb\">urgent policy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> implications, as opposed to research with a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f7f88f30-4b1e-4c9f-810a-eb67c5545a27\">purely theoretical value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Third, it would be better if scientists were more prepared to discuss the mathematical significance of their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ef2dc8f7-cf63-4b6c-924c-e6fda8518b42\">results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, and if the public didn’t treat <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"7a85254f-542c-4f5c-873b-28a6059b235c\">maths<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> as quite so scary: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"7a85254f-542c-4f5c-873b-28a6059b235c\">statistics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, which tell us the uncertainty in a measurement, give us the tools to evaluate new developments fully.</span></p><p><span>But fourth, and most important, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8908569c-6ef0-4a2b-acf2-56b4b20969ff\">people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> have to recognise that science can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"eb85326e-ae8c-43b2-8440-9d13f4e892e7\">complex<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. If we accept only straightforward stories, the description will necessarily be distorted. When advances are subtle or complicated, scientists should be willing to go the extra distance to give proper explanations, and the public should be more patient about the truth. Even so, some difficulties are unavoidable. Most developments reflect work in progress, so the story is complex because no one yet knows the big picture. Although the more involved story might not have the same immediate appeal, the truth in the end will always be far more interesting.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter A-D in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322848\" id=\"question-wrapper-322848\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why does the writer say we particularly need to pay attention to the communication of science?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Scientific discoveries now have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"e54eb814-43c0-477c-8ca1-857006223279\">growing influence on ordinary life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Current research is rarely covered in enough depth.</li> <li>C. The volume of scientific investigation has become difficult to follow.</li> <li>D. Researchers depend increasingly on approval from the general public.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322849\" id=\"question-wrapper-322849\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the first paragraph, the writer suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"aa04f32d-552f-48e5-8627-5c508bdc69bd\">finding suitable language to describe new scientific work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> can be hard because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the implications of new research are often open to several readings.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"727a4cb8-3bc3-4d95-9846-ba8cbcd26932\">many contemporary areas of science are difficult by their very nature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>C. specialist knowledge is needed before any research can be discussed.</li> <li>D. scientific claims are usually met with suspicion by ordinary readers.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322850\" id=\"question-wrapper-322850\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer refers to the term relativity as an example of</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Einstein’s deliberate deception of the public.</li> <li>B. a scientific word used to describe a physical phenomenon.</li> <li>C. the use of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"248ab3b9-6353-46c2-b075-7238c391cb45\">a generally used word<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"6107e286-f8fe-40b4-a77d-feb2bcb64cd4\">describe a scientific concept<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>D. the absolute nature of scientific theories.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322851\" id=\"question-wrapper-322851\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What example does the writer cite as a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b928e411-8570-4b75-a434-d96901bef9d8\">successful scientific explanation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of a complicated issue?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. evidence about how food choices affect health</li> <li>B. findings from research into serious diseases</li> <li>C. an account of a major theory in physics</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b88cbbd0-c2ad-4b5f-a462-f6e0d04421ec\">the chemical mechanism behind atmospheric damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 31–34 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322852\" id=\"question-wrapper-322852\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d6df10b5-53fc-496c-aade-e338f50db4a4\">Reporting of different viewpoints<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> on global warming tends to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"78f55596-2299-4744-80bf-6c505f0842d9\">lead to a fuller appreciation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of the issues.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322853\" id=\"question-wrapper-322853\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The media’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"d49c7f69-d187-4324-9ae8-6bc20fb44a33\">attempt to present both sides<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of the global warming issue <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"d49c7f69-d187-4324-9ae8-6bc20fb44a33\">went on for too long<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322854\" id=\"question-wrapper-322854\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"1d4a1acc-aae3-4230-ae3d-394a62a82ca2\">Explaining the mathematical significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of experimental results <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"1d4a1acc-aae3-4230-ae3d-394a62a82ca2\">would confuse the public<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322855\" id=\"question-wrapper-322855\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the Harvard debate, it would have been better to pay more attention to the discoveries made by male and female scientists.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, A–J, below.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A–J, in boxes 35–40 on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"eb85326e-ae8c-43b2-8440-9d13f4e892e7\">complicated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. witnessed</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. data </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. proposals</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. immediate </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. misunderstandings</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. open </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. distorted</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. applications</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"J\"><span>J. miscalculations</span></p><p><span>Several possible <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"1df92aab-08cf-41f1-80b8-0ef70d5b48b1\">changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> could reduce (35)________ in the reporting of science. The public needs to recognise that scientific evidence does not need to be (36)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3c8e3e79-8d76-4f55-9631-0fe1aeabd0c1\">by people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> to be valid. The way <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f7f88f30-4b1e-4c9f-810a-eb67c5545a27\">theoretical research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> is judged may be different from the way research with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"3ffa6d0a-984d-4d7e-bb53-2bb86278c5fb\">practical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> (37)________ is. Scientists should be more (38)________ about the mathematical significance of their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ef2dc8f7-cf63-4b6c-924c-e6fda8518b42\">findings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, and the public should learn to be more comfortable with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"7a85254f-542c-4f5c-873b-28a6059b235c\">numerical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> (39)________ . Most importantly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8908569c-6ef0-4a2b-acf2-56b4b20969ff\">scientists, journalists and the public<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> must accept that science and science reporting is necessarily (40)________ .</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322856\" id=\"question-wrapper-322856\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322857\" id=\"question-wrapper-322857\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322858\" id=\"question-wrapper-322858\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322859\" id=\"question-wrapper-322859\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322860\" id=\"question-wrapper-322860\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322861\" id=\"question-wrapper-322861\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e54eb814-43c0-477c-8ca1-857006223279","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"growing influence on ordinary life","passagePhrase":"increasingly significant role in people’s lives"},{"uid":"727a4cb8-3bc3-4d95-9846-ba8cbcd26932","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"many contemporary areas of science are difficult by their very nature","passagePhrase":"esoteric nature of current research"},{"uid":"aa04f32d-552f-48e5-8627-5c508bdc69bd","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"finding suitable language to describe new scientific work","passagePhrase":"coming up with sufficiently faithful terminology"},{"uid":"248ab3b9-6353-46c2-b075-7238c391cb45","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"a generally used word","passagePhrase":"common terminology"},{"uid":"6107e286-f8fe-40b4-a77d-feb2bcb64cd4","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"describe a scientific concept","passagePhrase":"assign a specific meaning"},{"uid":"b88cbbd0-c2ad-4b5f-a462-f6e0d04421ec","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"the chemical mechanism behind atmospheric damage","passagePhrase":"chemical processes involved in the destruction of the ozone layer"},{"uid":"b928e411-8570-4b75-a434-d96901bef9d8","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"successful scientific explanation","passagePhrase":"successfully conveyed"},{"uid":"d49c7f69-d187-4324-9ae8-6bc20fb44a33","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"attempt to present both sides ... went on for too long","passagePhrase":"press often continued to present ... even after"},{"uid":"d6df10b5-53fc-496c-aade-e338f50db4a4","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Reporting of different viewpoints","passagePhrase":"attempt to give equal weight to both sides"},{"uid":"7494bc6e-d17d-4cde-913c-a3fedf916fc1","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"instead, it created a misleading impression"},{"uid":"1df92aab-08cf-41f1-80b8-0ef70d5b48b1","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"changes","passagePhrase":"steps"},{"uid":"3c8e3e79-8d76-4f55-9631-0fe1aeabd0c1","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"by people","passagePhrase":"by human scientists"},{"uid":"3ffa6d0a-984d-4d7e-bb53-2bb86278c5fb","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"practical","passagePhrase":"urgent policy"},{"uid":"f7f88f30-4b1e-4c9f-810a-eb67c5545a27","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"theoretical research","passagePhrase":"purely theoretical value"},{"uid":"ef2dc8f7-cf63-4b6c-924c-e6fda8518b42","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"findings","passagePhrase":"results"},{"uid":"7a85254f-542c-4f5c-873b-28a6059b235c","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"numerical","passagePhrase":"maths ... statistics"},{"uid":"8908569c-6ef0-4a2b-acf2-56b4b20969ff","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"scientists, journalists and the public","passagePhrase":"people"},{"uid":"eb85326e-ae8c-43b2-8440-9d13f4e892e7","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"complicated","passagePhrase":"complex"}]},"reading_u2_61":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions</span></b> <b><span>1-13</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>LEISURE TIME IN AMERICA</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"1\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"63a5fc67-2b01-49f1-8722-66be05535d6c\">As most Americans will tell you<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> if you can stop them long enough to ask, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"63a5fc67-2b01-49f1-8722-66be05535d6c\">working people in the United States are as busy as ever<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. Sure, technology and competition are boosting the economy; but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"63a5fc67-2b01-49f1-8722-66be05535d6c\">nearly everyone thinks they have increased the demands on people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> at home and in the workplace. But is the overworked American a creature of myth?</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"2\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> A pair of economists have looked closely at how Americans actually spend their time. Mark Aguiar, at the Federal Reserve Bank of Boston, and Erik Hurst, at the University of Chicago's Graduate School of Business, constructed four different measures of leisure. The narrowest includes only activities that nearly everyone considers relaxing or fun; the broadest counts anything that is not related to a paying job, housework, or errands as \"leisure\". No matter how the two economists slice the data, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"5f21c987-a862-4a49-8a08-032869ee8520\">the popular story of a nation with no time to spare does not hold up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"3\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> Over the past four decades, depending on which of their measures one uses, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"ca265213-a2bb-4bd6-a03e-f28c8efcf412\">the amount of time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> that working-age Americans are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"ca265213-a2bb-4bd6-a03e-f28c8efcf412\">devoting to leisure activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"0d1dc8d2-726f-4f50-9962-e893fc065440\">risen by 4-8 hours a week<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. For somebody working 40 hours a week, that is equivalent to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"0d1dc8d2-726f-4f50-9962-e893fc065440\">5-10 weeks of extra holiday a year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. Nearly every category of American has gained: single or married, with or without children, both men and women. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"bcca6268-139b-4301-baaf-8d13452f15c6\">Americans may put in longer hours at the office<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"249c60e2-5361-484d-afef-c0c48dfcf54c\">workers elsewhere<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, but that is because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"3bfb941a-5c99-4a12-ab2d-f3991ffac078\">average hours in the workplace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"249c60e2-5361-484d-afef-c0c48dfcf54c\">in other rich countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"3bfb941a-5c99-4a12-ab2d-f3991ffac078\">have dropped sharply<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"4\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> How, then, have Messrs Aguiar and Hurst uncovered a more relaxed America? A large part of the answer lies in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e6c8202b-b6eb-4fce-bf83-eea1d0a4fe72\">what counts as work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e6c8202b-b6eb-4fce-bf83-eea1d0a4fe72\">The hours spent at your employer's<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, they argue, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e6c8202b-b6eb-4fce-bf83-eea1d0a4fe72\">are too narrow a definition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Americans also devote substantial time to shopping, cooking, running errands and keeping house — unpaid labour that feels every bit as obligatory as a shift at the office. These chores are among the main reasons why people say they are so overstretched, especially working women with children. Any honest accounting of how busy Americans are, the economists insist, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e6c8202b-b6eb-4fce-bf83-eea1d0a4fe72\">must add this domestic burden to the ledger alongside paid employment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"5\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Once <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"37f10525-343d-4abb-8fe6-f1fac4473c3d\">household tasks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> are counted as work, however, a surprising picture emerges: Americans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"37f10525-343d-4abb-8fe6-f1fac4473c3d\">devote far fewer hours to them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> than they did 40 years ago. There has been a revolution in the household economy. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"37f10525-343d-4abb-8fe6-f1fac4473c3d\">Dishwashers, microwaves and washing machines have stripped hours from the weekly routine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"37f10525-343d-4abb-8fe6-f1fac4473c3d\">home delivery, the internet and 24-hour shopping have made errands quicker<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>; and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"37f10525-343d-4abb-8fe6-f1fac4473c3d\">more varied and affordable domestic services<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> mean that many tasks can now be handed to someone else entirely. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"37f10525-343d-4abb-8fe6-f1fac4473c3d\">A burden that once consumed much of the week has quietly shrunk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, and the hours saved have flowed into free time.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"6\"><b><span>F.</span></b><span> Where does the evidence for all this come from? Most American labour studies rely on well-known official surveys, such as those collected by the Bureau of Labour Statistics (BLS) and the Census Bureau, which concentrate on paid employment. These are good at gleaning trends in factories and offices, but they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"fcf0a570-ca7c-41c0-8f31-d35159cfd53e\">give only a murky impression of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> how Americans use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"22ec6c76-59e2-4c39-bbbb-c0e026d8a65e\">the rest of their time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Messrs Aguiar and Hurst turned instead to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e989349b-fdc3-4f71-96e4-99c97b1640e0\">time-use diaries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> that American social scientists have been collecting methodically, once a decade, since 1965. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e989349b-fdc3-4f71-96e4-99c97b1640e0\">These diaries ask people to give detailed information on everything they did the day before, and for how long they did it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 12\" data-uid=\"086f03b9-a4f6-4624-a921-273a38167013 e989349b-fdc3-4f71-96e4-99c97b1640e0\">The beauty of such surveys</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, which are also collected in Australia and many European countries, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e989349b-fdc3-4f71-96e4-99c97b1640e0\">is that they </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 12\" data-uid=\"a7413ced-c1ee-46a4-990c-512aca2269f5 e989349b-fdc3-4f71-96e4-99c97b1640e0\">cover the whole day</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, not just the time at work, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e989349b-fdc3-4f71-96e4-99c97b1640e0\">they have a built-in accuracy check<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, since they must always account for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a7413ced-c1ee-46a4-990c-512aca2269f5\">every hour of the day<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"7\"><b><span>G.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"ca0aac26-acf5-489d-9047-f110b5ac32d0\">One large group of Americans was left out of the study altogether: the growing number of retired folk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, who are the biggest leisure-gainers in the population. The two economists excluded anyone who has reached 65 years old, as well as anyone under that age who retired early. Far from inflating their findings, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"ca0aac26-acf5-489d-9047-f110b5ac32d0\">this omission works in the opposite direction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> — <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"ca0aac26-acf5-489d-9047-f110b5ac32d0\">America's true leisure boom is even bigger than their estimate suggests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"H\" data-question-number=\"8\"><b><span>H.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a4ec7c43-543b-489d-9cc6-466dd147a1c0\">The biggest theoretical problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> with time diaries is \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a4ec7c43-543b-489d-9cc6-466dd147a1c0\">multi-tasking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>\". <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a4ec7c43-543b-489d-9cc6-466dd147a1c0\">Do you measure the time you spend cleaning your house while listening to portable music as \"leisure\" or \"work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>\"? This problem may be exaggerated: usually people seem to combine two work activities, using a laptop computer on a plane, or two leisure ones, watching television and doing something else. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b16f6c63-c83b-4341-a7bc-ed663142d926\">Where the two did overlap<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> — reading a novel while commuting, say, or goofing off on the internet at the office — <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"c881193b-2359-449f-b69f-32770e5ffba8\">the economists generally classified the time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"10cde08a-cf5c-4523-92c0-5ed52e66fd95\">as work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"I\" data-question-number=\"9\"><b><span>I.</span></b><span> Is all this leisure a good thing? Some part-time workers might well wish they had less leisure and more income. For most Americans, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"06984687-585c-4481-a1a2-394418947042\">the leisure dividend appears to be a bonus<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Using average hourly wages after tax, Steven Davis, a colleague of Mr Hurst's, reckons that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"06984687-585c-4481-a1a2-394418947042\">the nation's five extra hours a week are worth $570 billion — or $3,300 per worker — every year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has nine sections, A-I. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><b><span>i.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a4ec7c43-543b-489d-9cc6-466dd147a1c0\">A difficulty in categorising simultaneous activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><b><span>ii.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"37f10525-343d-4abb-8fe6-f1fac4473c3d\">Less time needed for household responsibilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><b><span>iii.</span></b><span> Research findings <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"5f21c987-a862-4a49-8a08-032869ee8520\">contradict a common belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><b><span>iv. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"06984687-585c-4481-a1a2-394418947042\">Putting a price on the nation's extra free time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><b><span>v. </span></b><span>Evidence that Americans are busier than ever before</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><b><span>vi. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"0d1dc8d2-726f-4f50-9962-e893fc065440\">A substantial rise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"ca265213-a2bb-4bd6-a03e-f28c8efcf412\">hours available for relaxation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><b><span>vii.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"ca0aac26-acf5-489d-9047-f110b5ac32d0\">Why the findings may understate the trend<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><b><span>viii.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e6c8202b-b6eb-4fce-bf83-eea1d0a4fe72\">The need for a wider description of work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><b><span>ix.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e989349b-fdc3-4f71-96e4-99c97b1640e0\">An effective system for measuring time spent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"x\"><b><span>x.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"63a5fc67-2b01-49f1-8722-66be05535d6c\">How Americans think about their time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"xi\"><b><span>xi</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> Weaknesses in official employment data</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"xii\"><b><span>xii.</span></b><span> Workers who would prefer money to free time</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325706\" id=\"question-wrapper-325706\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">x</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325707\" id=\"question-wrapper-325707\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325708\" id=\"question-wrapper-325708\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325709\" id=\"question-wrapper-325709\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325710\" id=\"question-wrapper-325710\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325711\" id=\"question-wrapper-325711\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ix</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325712\" id=\"question-wrapper-325712\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph G </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325713\" id=\"question-wrapper-325713\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph H</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325714\" id=\"question-wrapper-325714\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph I </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>,</span> <b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D.</span></b></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325715\" id=\"question-wrapper-325715\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"bcca6268-139b-4301-baaf-8d13452f15c6\">Americans seem to spend more time in the office<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"249c60e2-5361-484d-afef-c0c48dfcf54c\">people in other rich countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Americans have recently extended their working week.</li> <li>B. Employees in other countries now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"3bfb941a-5c99-4a12-ab2d-f3991ffac078\">spend fewer hours at work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Americans have taken on more unpaid responsibilities.</li> <li>D. Workers in other countries have shifted more of their work to the home.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325716\" id=\"question-wrapper-325716\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>One problem with data from the BLS is that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"fcf0a570-ca7c-41c0-8f31-d35159cfd53e\">It gives an unclear picture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of how people use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"22ec6c76-59e2-4c39-bbbb-c0e026d8a65e\">non-working hours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</li> <li>B. It only covers people employed in factories and office buildings.</li> <li>C. It relies on respondents remembering what they did weeks earlier.</li> <li>D. It is poor at identifying long-term patterns in paid employment.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325717\" id=\"question-wrapper-325717\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"086f03b9-a4f6-4624-a921-273a38167013\">one advantage of the economists' chosen source of data<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It compares data collected from participants in just two countries.</li> <li>B. It does not depend on people remembering what they did.</li> <li>C. Its design means <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a7413ced-c1ee-46a4-990c-512aca2269f5\">no part of a respondent's day goes unrecorded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Its figures can be verified against official employment records.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325718\" id=\"question-wrapper-325718\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b16f6c63-c83b-4341-a7bc-ed663142d926\">When an activity mixed relaxation with obligations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"c881193b-2359-449f-b69f-32770e5ffba8\">the researchers generally recorded that time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. as leisure</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"10cde08a-cf5c-4523-92c0-5ed52e66fd95\">as work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></li> <li>C. as neither leisure nor work</li> <li>D. as both work and leisure</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"63a5fc67-2b01-49f1-8722-66be05535d6c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"How Americans think about their time","passagePhrase":"As most Americans will tell you ... working people in the United States are as busy as ever ... nearly everyone thinks they have increased the demands on people"},{"uid":"5f21c987-a862-4a49-8a08-032869ee8520","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"contradict a common belief","passagePhrase":"the popular story of a nation with no time to spare does not hold up"},{"uid":"ca265213-a2bb-4bd6-a03e-f28c8efcf412","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"hours available for relaxation","passagePhrase":"the amount of time ... devoting to leisure activities"},{"uid":"0d1dc8d2-726f-4f50-9962-e893fc065440","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"A substantial rise","passagePhrase":"risen by 4-8 hours a week ... 5-10 weeks of extra holiday a year"},{"uid":"bcca6268-139b-4301-baaf-8d13452f15c6","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"Americans seem to spend more time in the office","passagePhrase":"Americans may put in longer hours at the office"},{"uid":"249c60e2-5361-484d-afef-c0c48dfcf54c","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"people in other rich countries","passagePhrase":"workers elsewhere ... in other rich countries"},{"uid":"3bfb941a-5c99-4a12-ab2d-f3991ffac078","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"spend fewer hours at work","passagePhrase":"average hours in the workplace ... have dropped sharply"},{"uid":"e6c8202b-b6eb-4fce-bf83-eea1d0a4fe72","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"The need for a wider description of work","passagePhrase":"what counts as work ... The hours spent at your employer's ... are too narrow a definition ... must add this domestic burden to the ledger alongside paid employment"},{"uid":"37f10525-343d-4abb-8fe6-f1fac4473c3d","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Less time needed for household responsibilities","passagePhrase":"household tasks ... devote far fewer hours to them ... Dishwashers, microwaves and washing machines have stripped hours from the weekly routine ... home delivery, the internet and 24-hour shopping have made errands quicker ... more varied and affordable domestic services ... A burden that once consumed much of the week has quietly shrunk"},{"uid":"fcf0a570-ca7c-41c0-8f31-d35159cfd53e","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"It gives an unclear picture","passagePhrase":"give only a murky impression of"},{"uid":"22ec6c76-59e2-4c39-bbbb-c0e026d8a65e","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"non-working hours","passagePhrase":"the rest of their time"},{"uid":"e989349b-fdc3-4f71-96e4-99c97b1640e0","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"An effective system for measuring time spent","passagePhrase":"time-use diaries ... These diaries ask people to give detailed information on everything they did the day before, and for how long they did it ... is that they ... they have a built-in accuracy check"},{"uid":"086f03b9-a4f6-4624-a921-273a38167013 e989349b-fdc3-4f71-96e4-99c97b1640e0","qNum":"6 12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The beauty of such surveys"},{"uid":"a7413ced-c1ee-46a4-990c-512aca2269f5 e989349b-fdc3-4f71-96e4-99c97b1640e0","qNum":"6 12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"cover the whole day"},{"uid":"a7413ced-c1ee-46a4-990c-512aca2269f5","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"no part of a respondent's day goes unrecorded","passagePhrase":"every hour of the day"},{"uid":"ca0aac26-acf5-489d-9047-f110b5ac32d0","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Why the findings may understate the trend","passagePhrase":"One large group of Americans was left out of the study altogether: the growing number of retired folk ... this omission works in the opposite direction ... America's true leisure boom is even bigger than their estimate suggests"},{"uid":"a4ec7c43-543b-489d-9cc6-466dd147a1c0","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"A difficulty in categorising simultaneous activities","passagePhrase":"The biggest theoretical problem ... multi-tasking ... Do you measure the time you spend cleaning your house while listening to portable music as \"leisure\" or \"work"},{"uid":"b16f6c63-c83b-4341-a7bc-ed663142d926","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"When an activity mixed relaxation with obligations","passagePhrase":"Where the two did overlap"},{"uid":"c881193b-2359-449f-b69f-32770e5ffba8","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"the researchers generally recorded that time","passagePhrase":"the economists generally classified the time"},{"uid":"10cde08a-cf5c-4523-92c0-5ed52e66fd95","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"as work","passagePhrase":"as work"},{"uid":"06984687-585c-4481-a1a2-394418947042","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Putting a price on the nation's extra free time","passagePhrase":"the leisure dividend appears to be a bonus ... the nation's five extra hours a week are worth $570 billion — or $3,300 per worker — every year"},{"uid":"086f03b9-a4f6-4624-a921-273a38167013","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"one advantage of the economists' chosen source of data","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_62":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 14-26</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>A New Threat in Yellowstone</span></b></p><p><span>It has long been known that Yellowstone National Park lies over an enormous supervolcano. The term 'supervolcano' implies a volcanic centre that has had an eruption of magnitude 8 on the Volcanic Explosivity Index (VEI), meaning the measured deposits for that eruption are greater than 1,000 cubic kilometres. This sounds worrying, and Professor George Peters details the possible results if something were to happen. \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"7d86b84c-53a4-4a40-a198-93ec78c8b43a\">A major eruption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> would obliterate the surroundings within a radius of hundreds of kilometres and cover the rest of the United States and Canada with multiple inches of ash. This would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"da807505-f142-44cc-bbb2-5b1b6f4e445a\">shut down agriculture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> and cause global climate cooling for as long as a decade.\" To calm everyone down, geologist Tony Masters explains that there is little to fear today. \"All <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0f0fc486-2959-471e-bb10-ddc29a2797e7\">VEI 8 eruptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, including <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0f0fc486-2959-471e-bb10-ddc29a2797e7\">the last at Yellowstone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ac8f88f4-9c40-4cb0-87c6-c75d50d57417\">occurred tens of thousands to millions of years ago<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Another eruption could occur, but it is very unlikely to happen in the next million years or so.\"</span></p><p><span>Yellowstone is no stranger to controversy. There was a previous media accusation that US Geological Survey (USGS) geologists had not done their work properly and that Yellowstone was not identified as a supervolcano until scientists looked at photographs of it from space. The Yellowstone scientists denied this. Spokeswoman Alice Wheeler clarifies their position. \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"86317f9e-f8e2-4be5-8ce4-53b21135f03b\">The scientist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> who first identified <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"02857d7d-2476-4bed-9d37-3324ddcf45e4\">the three Yellowstone calderas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> was from the USGS, and he told the world about the great eruptions that formed them. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"0577fe1e-d0de-45dd-ba65-5a6135ddb14b\">traced out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> the caldera boundaries through old-fashioned field work, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"8fff9656-7ecd-4660-93a9-14504b179806\">walking around<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> with a hammer and hand lens and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"8fff9656-7ecd-4660-93a9-14504b179806\">looking carefully at the rocks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and their distributions.\" The National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) also agreed. Stan Forsyth, their spokesman, explains. \"Several authors have written that these large calderas in Yellowstone were discovered from space, but we suspect that the rumour probably got started because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2f1499f2-5028-4a82-8efc-d9daecd9b1c2\">the initial field work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> that identified them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"94eb71c5-8ad5-4c27-bb97-f15d4ee49409\">was partly funded by NASA<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.\"</span></p><p><span>A new problem in Yellowstone is that the supervolcano has now been discovered to be larger than originally thought, and this has made people more nervous. Seismologists at the University of Utah have worked with several other institutions to create an image of the Yellowstone magma reservoir using a technique called seismic tomography. Master's student Julia Grey explains the results. \"By looking closely at data from thousands of earthquakes, we have discovered that there are two magma reservoirs, one shallow and one deep, and that they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ae00cf99-177a-48f9-9024-4e98f139bbae\">much larger than originally believed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. The shallow one was previously known to us, but the deeper one is a new finding.\"</span></p><p><span>To create an image of this second magma reservoir beneath Yellowstone, the research teams reviewed data from thousands of earthquakes. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"ee3789be-2b16-4718-bd07-10131635fda6\">Seismic waves travel more slowly through hot, partially molten rock and faster through cold, solid rock<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"00dba53d-a51f-4d9a-a609-6ab4ff1af7d4\">The researchers made a map of the locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> where seismic waves travel more slowly, which provided <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"00dba53d-a51f-4d9a-a609-6ab4ff1af7d4\">a subsurface image<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of the hot or partially molten bodies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"00dba53d-a51f-4d9a-a609-6ab4ff1af7d4\">in the crust beneath Yellowstone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. The deeper magma storage region extends from 20 to 50 kilometres in depth, contains about 2 per cent melt, and is about 4.5 times larger than the shallow magma body. The shallower magma storage region is about 90 kilometres long, extends from 5 to 17 kilometres in depth, and is 2.5 times larger than a prior, less accurate study indicated. This magma reservoir contains between about 5 and 15 per cent molten rock. Although this is the crustal magma storage region that has fuelled Yellowstone's past volcanic activity, magma typically does not erupt unless it has greater than 50 per cent melt.</span></p><p><span>The US and world media were quick to dramatise the discovery and exaggerate the threat that these findings represent. Yellowstone park scientist Amy Brent has calming words. \"These findings do not increase the assessment of volcanic hazard for Yellowstone. The research simply makes a better image of the magmatic system. Simply, we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"773f36bc-f2e8-4f59-a9be-ee74766f7c97\">have more key information about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"fe759a75-66b5-4743-93da-6a5a10ae5b76\">how the Yellowstone volcano works<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.\"</span></p><p><span>Many independent reports back up Brent's comments and have shown that the Yellowstone area has been on a long cycle of periodic eruptions. Eruptions are extremely infrequent in supervolcanoes, and eventually the cycle ends in the volcano's death. US government geologist Andrea Haller explains the state of the Yellowstone supervolcano. \"By investigating the patterns of behaviour in two previously completed caldera cycles, we can suggest that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"1f179ee1-17d8-43e9-915e-1f605a574605\">the current activity of Yellowstone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"eefab85d-9418-497a-a88e-bc06fbc27d66\">in the dying cycle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.\" This is based on comparisons with other supervolcanoes. Scientists know the behaviour of the past and they know at what comparative stage Yellowstone is right now. It is believed that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"d010f132-3c46-49c3-92f1-6e004417b5e7\">Yellowstone is currently in a third and dying cycle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"5747f44a-65ea-4668-a135-25882744b55c\">can be concluded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> from the fact that dying volcanoes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"a842e7c7-3e08-4f3a-9a54-ae964ad2ec9c\">produce less fresh molten material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> from the Earth's crust. Haller continues. \"We've observed a lot of material in the magma chambers that represents recycled volcanic rocks, which were once buried inside the calderas and are now getting reused. Yellowstone has erupted enough of this material already to suggest that the future melting potential of the crust is becoming exhausted.\"</span></p><p><span>Whatever the truth about Yellowstone, it seems that within the lifetimes of most people the park's geological status can still prove hazardous. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"ed15e803-8542-4053-bff1-267522305dd2\">The park<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"0073565a-9949-48c5-ba28-3e30362b0b2e\">has often been closed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> due to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"a516f570-c332-42fa-b6ae-f1d0de78d26d\">volcanic activity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> in the past, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"0073565a-9949-48c5-ba28-3e30362b0b2e\">this is likely to happen again<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> before the volcano becomes harmless.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements (</span><b><span>questions 14-20</span></b><span>) and the list of people below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct person’s initials.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct initials in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>14-20</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. George Peters</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Tony Masters</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Alice Wheeler</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Stan Forsyth</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Julia Grey</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. Amy Brent</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. Andrea Haller</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325719\" id=\"question-wrapper-325719\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"1f179ee1-17d8-43e9-915e-1f605a574605\">Yellowstone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"eefab85d-9418-497a-a88e-bc06fbc27d66\">in the final stage of its life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"1f179ee1-17d8-43e9-915e-1f605a574605\">as an active volcano<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325720\" id=\"question-wrapper-325720\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"02857d7d-2476-4bed-9d37-3324ddcf45e4\">The boundaries of the Yellowstone calderas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"0577fe1e-d0de-45dd-ba65-5a6135ddb14b\">were mapped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"86317f9e-f8e2-4be5-8ce4-53b21135f03b\">a researcher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"8fff9656-7ecd-4660-93a9-14504b179806\">examining rocks on foot<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325721\" id=\"question-wrapper-325721\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>If Yellowstone were to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"7d86b84c-53a4-4a40-a198-93ec78c8b43a\">erupt on a catastrophic scale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"da807505-f142-44cc-bbb2-5b1b6f4e445a\">farming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> across Canada would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"da807505-f142-44cc-bbb2-5b1b6f4e445a\">come to a standstill<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325722\" id=\"question-wrapper-325722\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The volumes of magma beneath the park <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ae00cf99-177a-48f9-9024-4e98f139bbae\">exceed earlier estimates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325723\" id=\"question-wrapper-325723\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ac8f88f4-9c40-4cb0-87c6-c75d50d57417\">An extremely long time has passed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> since <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0f0fc486-2959-471e-bb10-ddc29a2797e7\">Yellowstone last erupted violently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325724\" id=\"question-wrapper-325724\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"fe759a75-66b5-4743-93da-6a5a10ae5b76\">The way the Yellowstone volcano operates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> is now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"773f36bc-f2e8-4f59-a9be-ee74766f7c97\">better understood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> by scientists.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325725\" id=\"question-wrapper-325725\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"94eb71c5-8ad5-4c27-bb97-f15d4ee49409\">NASA has provided money in the past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2f1499f2-5028-4a82-8efc-d9daecd9b1c2\">research on the Yellowstone supervolcano<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Label the diagram below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>21-23</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>The Yellowstone Supervolcano</span></b></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_3/reading/images/1db405ee0c3eac0c2a4342e49b5761c7b24b45f0a9a6563cb184643b34d0818d.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325726\" id=\"question-wrapper-325726\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">50/fifty</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325727\" id=\"question-wrapper-325727\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">2% [OR] 2/two per( )cent</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325728\" id=\"question-wrapper-325728\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">50% [OR] 50/fifty per( )cent</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>24-26</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325729\" id=\"question-wrapper-325729\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"00dba53d-a51f-4d9a-a609-6ab4ff1af7d4\">Images of the magma chambers can be made<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"ee3789be-2b16-4718-bd07-10131635fda6\">seismic waves move at different speeds through rock in different states<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</li> <li>B. seismic waves slow down when they pass through cold and solid rock.</li> <li>C. seismic waves are produced by the molten bodies in the crust below.</li> <li>D. seismic waves from thousands of past eruptions have been mapped out.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325730\" id=\"question-wrapper-325730\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"d010f132-3c46-49c3-92f1-6e004417b5e7\">The death of the Yellowstone supervolcano<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. will happen when the two earlier caldera cycles repeat themselves once more.</li> <li>B. will be delayed because buried volcanic rocks offer a fresh supply of magma.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"5747f44a-65ea-4668-a135-25882744b55c\">can be foreseen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"a842e7c7-3e08-4f3a-9a54-ae964ad2ec9c\">the falling amounts of new magma being produced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</li> <li>D. cannot be estimated because eruptions are so infrequent in supervolcanoes.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325731\" id=\"question-wrapper-325731\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"ed15e803-8542-4053-bff1-267522305dd2\">The Yellowstone National Park<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"0073565a-9949-48c5-ba28-3e30362b0b2e\">will probably have to be closed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"a516f570-c332-42fa-b6ae-f1d0de78d26d\">at certain times of danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</li> <li>B. will probably never open again due to the dangers.</li> <li>C. will never need to be closed in the lifetimes of people today.</li> <li>D. will be shut permanently once the volcano stops being active.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7d86b84c-53a4-4a40-a198-93ec78c8b43a","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"erupt on a catastrophic scale","passagePhrase":"A major eruption"},{"uid":"da807505-f142-44cc-bbb2-5b1b6f4e445a","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"farming ... come to a standstill","passagePhrase":"shut down agriculture"},{"uid":"0f0fc486-2959-471e-bb10-ddc29a2797e7","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Yellowstone last erupted violently","passagePhrase":"VEI 8 eruptions ... the last at Yellowstone"},{"uid":"ac8f88f4-9c40-4cb0-87c6-c75d50d57417","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"An extremely long time has passed","passagePhrase":"occurred tens of thousands to millions of years ago"},{"uid":"86317f9e-f8e2-4be5-8ce4-53b21135f03b","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"a researcher","passagePhrase":"The scientist"},{"uid":"02857d7d-2476-4bed-9d37-3324ddcf45e4","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"The boundaries of the Yellowstone calderas","passagePhrase":"the three Yellowstone calderas"},{"uid":"0577fe1e-d0de-45dd-ba65-5a6135ddb14b","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"were mapped","passagePhrase":"traced out"},{"uid":"8fff9656-7ecd-4660-93a9-14504b179806","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"examining rocks on foot","passagePhrase":"walking around ... looking carefully at the rocks"},{"uid":"2f1499f2-5028-4a82-8efc-d9daecd9b1c2","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"research on the Yellowstone supervolcano","passagePhrase":"the initial field work"},{"uid":"94eb71c5-8ad5-4c27-bb97-f15d4ee49409","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"NASA has provided money in the past","passagePhrase":"was partly funded by NASA"},{"uid":"ae00cf99-177a-48f9-9024-4e98f139bbae","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"exceed earlier estimates","passagePhrase":"much larger than originally believed"},{"uid":"ee3789be-2b16-4718-bd07-10131635fda6","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"seismic waves move at different speeds through rock in different states","passagePhrase":"Seismic waves travel more slowly through hot, partially molten rock and faster through cold, solid rock"},{"uid":"00dba53d-a51f-4d9a-a609-6ab4ff1af7d4","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Images of the magma chambers can be made","passagePhrase":"The researchers made a map of the locations ... a subsurface image ... in the crust beneath Yellowstone"},{"uid":"773f36bc-f2e8-4f59-a9be-ee74766f7c97","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"better understood","passagePhrase":"have more key information about"},{"uid":"fe759a75-66b5-4743-93da-6a5a10ae5b76","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"The way the Yellowstone volcano operates","passagePhrase":"how the Yellowstone volcano works"},{"uid":"1f179ee1-17d8-43e9-915e-1f605a574605","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Yellowstone ... as an active volcano","passagePhrase":"the current activity of Yellowstone"},{"uid":"eefab85d-9418-497a-a88e-bc06fbc27d66","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"in the final stage of its life","passagePhrase":"in the dying cycle"},{"uid":"d010f132-3c46-49c3-92f1-6e004417b5e7","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"The death of the Yellowstone supervolcano","passagePhrase":"Yellowstone is currently in a third and dying cycle"},{"uid":"5747f44a-65ea-4668-a135-25882744b55c","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"can be foreseen","passagePhrase":"can be concluded"},{"uid":"a842e7c7-3e08-4f3a-9a54-ae964ad2ec9c","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"the falling amounts of new magma being produced","passagePhrase":"produce less fresh molten material"},{"uid":"ed15e803-8542-4053-bff1-267522305dd2","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"The Yellowstone National Park","passagePhrase":"The park"},{"uid":"0073565a-9949-48c5-ba28-3e30362b0b2e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"will probably have to be closed","passagePhrase":"has often been closed ... this is likely to happen again"},{"uid":"a516f570-c332-42fa-b6ae-f1d0de78d26d","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"at certain times of danger","passagePhrase":"volcanic activity"}]},"reading_u2_63":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 27-40</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>An Ageing Population</span></b></p><p><span>People are living longer and, in some parts of the world, healthier lives. This represents one of the crowning achievements of the last century, but also a significant challenge. Longer lives must be planned for. Societal ageing may affect economic growth and lead to many other issues, including the sustainability of families, the ability of states and communities to provide resources for older citizens, and international relations. The Global Burden of Disease, a study conducted by the World Health Organization, predicts a very large increase in age-related chronic disease in all regions of the world. Dealing with this will be a significant challenge for all countries' health services.</span></p><p><span>Population ageing is driven by declines in fertility and improvements in health and longevity. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"71d082c8-aa59-45db-b30e-d54dad193df4\">In more developed countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ad61b5d0-35b0-49f8-b41e-ad5c8e73068b\">falling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> fertility beginning in the early 1900s has resulted in current levels being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ceb1aee0-6ea9-454c-a569-338458b34e6f\">below<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the population replacement rate of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"fcb5e3cf-23eb-4b58-90cd-9e0b3d5812f5\">two live births per woman<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Perhaps <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"4f46cebf-6513-487a-a90f-ceed90b3fa66\">the most surprising demographic development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"52d0c753-8c7e-4f5e-85bd-78bea7ea8e88\">the past 20 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"ad2e99c7-95a9-4beb-8c6e-8d6a71adbcac\">the pace of fertility decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in many less developed countries. In 2006, for example, the total fertility rate was at or below the replacement rate in 44 less developed countries.</span></p><p><span>One central issue for policymakers in regard to pension funds is the relationship between the official retirement age and the actual retirement age. Over several decades <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e8830c26-7dcf-406e-a210-0180bc224d6c\">in the latter part of the 20th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, many of the more developed nations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"47ddfd4c-9912-4668-b81d-722da9c70fad\">lowered the official age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"20df9781-6120-427d-a208-a005fe7619df\">at which people become fully entitled to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> public pension benefits. This was propelled by general economic conditions, changes in welfare philosophy, and private pension trends. Despite the recent trend towards <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"fe14f459-0879-488b-a463-ca6af2fe5561\">increase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>d workforce participation at older ages, a significant gap between official and actual ages of retirement persists. This trend is emerging in rapidly ageing developing countries as well. Many countries have already taken steps towards much-needed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9628edca-ba8f-47e9-8c32-839cc359eacc\">reform<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of their old-age social insurance programmes. One common reform has been to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e90835c0-6dda-4bb2-8c22-3377dee34134\">raise the age at which workers are eligible for full public pension benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Another strategy for bolstering economic security for older people has been to increase the contributions <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"fe14f459-0879-488b-a463-ca6af2fe5561\">made by workers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Other measures to enhance income for older people include new financial instruments for private savings, tax incentives for individual retirement savings, and supplemental occupational pension plans.</span></p><p><span>As <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"23131b38-a9fe-4572-8fa9-346c4d806ef2\">life expectancy increases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in most nations, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"f514e586-9c51-46d4-9aaf-e8e6e8c98e2f\">so do the odds of different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> generations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"f3da8421-b368-447d-9a6b-c268ae0af9b6\">within a family coexisting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"ca14a62e-b675-4f01-a867-53d3a60c8de5\">In more developed countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"d5ace762-1357-4d9c-aa0b-4bb2f6d9fa93\">this has manifested itself as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the 'beanpole family', <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"3d2a62e4-8e33-41b1-aa48-3d602f779404\">a vertical extension of family structure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> characterised by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"ee5a6220-d01e-47af-811b-95212da649fe\">an increase in the number of living generations within a lineage and a decrease in the number of people within each generation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. As mortality rates continue to improve, more people in their 50s and 60s will have surviving parents, aunts and uncles. Consequently, more children will know their grandparents and even their great-grandparents, especially their great-grandmothers. There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"1bb7ef82-c7ee-4b51-a272-adc51e9eaf09\">no historical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> precedent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"f4878ddd-ac49-4e05-91aa-59b000709134\">for a majority of middle-aged and older adults having living parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The World Health Organization study The Global Burden of Disease predicts that in a few decades the loss of health and life worldwide will be greater from non-communicable or chronic diseases than from infectious diseases, childhood diseases and accidents. The study estimates that today, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"edf0b0c5-fe7a-4ff2-ac08-db550f24fb29\">non-communicable diseases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> account for 85 per cent of the burden of disease in high-income countries and a surprising 44 per cent of the burden of disease in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"072953a7-fd48-4acf-99c8-e798f4783899\">low- and middle-income countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Non-<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"32b86d66-2672-4436-a31b-8a3dd5a1ea80\">communicable diseases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> already account for as much of the burden of disease in low- and middle-income countries as all communicable diseases, maternal and perinatal conditions, and nutritional conditions combined. By 2030, according to projections, the share of the burden attributed to non-communicable diseases in low- and middle-income countries will reach 54 per cent, while the share attributed to communicable diseases will fall to 32 per cent. If we restrict attention to older ages, non-communicable diseases already account for more than 87 per cent of the burden for the over-60 population in low-, middle- and high-income countries. The critical issue for low- and middle-income countries is how to mobilise and allocate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"fe98e37a-1a0f-423e-8b04-663dffbbf82f\">resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> to address non-communicable diseases as they <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"478f4453-d4f6-404d-98f7-532bbb467bd0\">continue to struggle with the persistently high prevalence of communicable diseases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Of course, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"1f99d1d4-b41b-42bc-a302-6cc4caf82a6b\">a significant jump in disability numbers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> has accompanied <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"f685dd16-92bf-4b65-a8cd-6038affdaea2\">the increase in longevity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Because countries age at different paces, it is possible for the elements of production – labour and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"01e1cdba-0587-48a1-8f50-7778cce5df8c\">capital<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> – to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e71ea412-812e-4dd6-8a3d-02eed741504a\">flow across national boundaries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> and mitigate the impact of population ageing. Studies predict that, in the near term, surplus <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e71ea412-812e-4dd6-8a3d-02eed741504a\">capital<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"2bbead1d-6473-44c0-b33f-569dbe229013\">flow from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"59c153bc-05ef-4454-b6b0-9aea0434fed4\">Europe and North America<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"2bbead1d-6473-44c0-b33f-569dbe229013\">to emerging markets in Asia and Latin America<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, where the population is younger, labour is cheaper, and supplies of capital are relatively low. In another 20 years, when the baby boom generation in the West has mostly retired, capital <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"30df84af-0060-42c1-a7ef-25ffd1a363e4\">will most likely flow in the opposite direction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. However, these studies rest on the uncertain assumption that capital will flow easily across national boundaries.</span></p><p><span>Despite the weight of scientific evidence, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"53a6ded1-a059-4dcd-8b0a-9d623a12da8e\">the significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"85e02b73-11a2-4f2d-bbbb-77f7caef590a\">population ageing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"53a6ded1-a059-4dcd-8b0a-9d623a12da8e\">and its global implications<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"4d9014e4-5393-4e99-9b3a-ef91c68b3320\">have yet to be wholly appreciated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. There is a need to raise awareness not only about global ageing issues, but also about the importance of rigorous cross-national scientific research and policy dialogue that will help us address the challenges and opportunities of an ageing world. Preparing financially for longer lives and finding ways to reduce ageing-related disability should become national and global priorities. Experience shows that for nations, as for individuals, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"bf1aace5-0fe3-41bc-bc94-c23a2ae7c485\">it is critical to address problems sooner rather than later<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Waiting significantly increases the costs and difficulties of addressing these challenges.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></b><span> for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>27-33</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>An Ageing Population</span></b></p><p><span>Societies are growing older because women are having fewer children while better health keeps people alive for longer. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"71d082c8-aa59-45db-b30e-d54dad193df4\">In wealthier nations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"fcb5e3cf-23eb-4b58-90cd-9e0b3d5812f5\">the average number of children born per woman<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ad61b5d0-35b0-49f8-b41e-ad5c8e73068b\">has now fallen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ceb1aee0-6ea9-454c-a569-338458b34e6f\">lower than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the (27)________. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"4f46cebf-6513-487a-a90f-ceed90b3fa66\">What has surprised experts most<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"ad2e99c7-95a9-4beb-8c6e-8d6a71adbcac\">how quickly birth rates have also dropped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in many (28)________ countries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"52d0c753-8c7e-4f5e-85bd-78bea7ea8e88\">over the past two decades<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>For governments, a central problem is that the official retirement <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"47ddfd4c-9912-4668-b81d-722da9c70fad\">age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> no longer matches when people actually stop working. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e8830c26-7dcf-406e-a210-0180bc224d6c\">During the late 20th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, the age <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"20df9781-6120-427d-a208-a005fe7619df\">at which full<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> (29)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"20df9781-6120-427d-a208-a005fe7619df\">could be claimed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"47ddfd4c-9912-4668-b81d-722da9c70fad\">brought down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> as a result of economic circumstances and changing ideas about welfare. To <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9628edca-ba8f-47e9-8c32-839cc359eacc\">repair<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> their systems of support for the elderly, several states have since <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e90835c0-6dda-4bb2-8c22-3377dee34134\">pushed this age back up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, while others now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"fe14f459-0879-488b-a463-ca6af2fe5561\">require employees to pay larger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> (30)________. Further options include tax incentives and new products designed to encourage private savings.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"23131b38-a9fe-4572-8fa9-346c4d806ef2\">Rising life expectancy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"f514e586-9c51-46d4-9aaf-e8e6e8c98e2f\">increases the number of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"f3da8421-b368-447d-9a6b-c268ae0af9b6\">family<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> (31)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"f3da8421-b368-447d-9a6b-c268ae0af9b6\">being alive at the same time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"ca14a62e-b675-4f01-a867-53d3a60c8de5\">In richer countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"d5ace762-1357-4d9c-aa0b-4bb2f6d9fa93\">this has produced the so-called<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> '(32)________' – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"3d2a62e4-8e33-41b1-aa48-3d602f779404\">a taller, thinner family tree<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"ee5a6220-d01e-47af-811b-95212da649fe\">with more levels but fewer people on each one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"1bb7ef82-c7ee-4b51-a272-adc51e9eaf09\">History offers no<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> (33)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"f4878ddd-ac49-4e05-91aa-59b000709134\">for such a change in family demographics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325732\" id=\"question-wrapper-325732\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(population) replacement rate</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325733\" id=\"question-wrapper-325733\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">less developed</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325734\" id=\"question-wrapper-325734\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(public) pension benefits</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325735\" id=\"question-wrapper-325735\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">contributions</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325736\" id=\"question-wrapper-325736\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">generations</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325737\" id=\"question-wrapper-325737\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">beanpole family</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325738\" id=\"question-wrapper-325738\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">precedent</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer of the text?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes </span></i><i><b><span>34-39</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet write:</span></i></p><p><b><span>YES</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the writer’s views</span></p><p><b><span>NO</span></b><span> if the statement doesn’t agree with the writer’s views</span></p><p><b><span>NOT</span></b> <b><span>GIVEN</span></b><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325739\" id=\"question-wrapper-325739\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"072953a7-fd48-4acf-99c8-e798f4783899\">Poorer nations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> can now shift their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"fe98e37a-1a0f-423e-8b04-663dffbbf82f\">health spending<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"edf0b0c5-fe7a-4ff2-ac08-db550f24fb29\">long-term illnesses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, as <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"32b86d66-2672-4436-a31b-8a3dd5a1ea80 478f4453-d4f6-404d-98f7-532bbb467bd0\">infections</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"478f4453-d4f6-404d-98f7-532bbb467bd0\"> are no longer a major problem</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325740\" id=\"question-wrapper-325740\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>As <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"f685dd16-92bf-4b65-a8cd-6038affdaea2\">people have lived longer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"1f99d1d4-b41b-42bc-a302-6cc4caf82a6b\">disability has become less common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325741\" id=\"question-wrapper-325741\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Studies suggest that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"01e1cdba-0587-48a1-8f50-7778cce5df8c\">money<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"2bbead1d-6473-44c0-b33f-569dbe229013\">invested abroad<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"59c153bc-05ef-4454-b6b0-9aea0434fed4\">richer Western nations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"30df84af-0060-42c1-a7ef-25ffd1a363e4\">is likely to return to them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> in the future.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325742\" id=\"question-wrapper-325742\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e71ea412-812e-4dd6-8a3d-02eed741504a\">The movement of money across borders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> could lead to conflict between nations.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325743\" id=\"question-wrapper-325743\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"4d9014e4-5393-4e99-9b3a-ef91c68b3320\">The world still does not fully grasp<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"53a6ded1-a059-4dcd-8b0a-9d623a12da8e\">what<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"85e02b73-11a2-4f2d-bbbb-77f7caef590a\">older societies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"53a6ded1-a059-4dcd-8b0a-9d623a12da8e\">will mean for everyone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325744\" id=\"question-wrapper-325744\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Governments <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"bf1aace5-0fe3-41bc-bc94-c23a2ae7c485\">would be wiser to postpone their response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> to older populations.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in box </span></i><i><b><span>40</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325745\" id=\"question-wrapper-325745\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the writer’s purpose in Reading Passage 3?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. To describe the origins and consequences of population ageing in wealthy countries.</li> <li>B. To provide an overview of the causes and effects of the world's ageing population.</li> <li>C. To explain why the world's population is ageing and how the trend might be reversed.</li> <li>D. To provide a historical analysis of the causes of today's ageing population.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"71d082c8-aa59-45db-b30e-d54dad193df4","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"In wealthier nations","passagePhrase":"In more developed countries"},{"uid":"ad61b5d0-35b0-49f8-b41e-ad5c8e73068b","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"has now fallen","passagePhrase":"falling"},{"uid":"ceb1aee0-6ea9-454c-a569-338458b34e6f","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"lower than","passagePhrase":"below"},{"uid":"fcb5e3cf-23eb-4b58-90cd-9e0b3d5812f5","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"the average number of children born per woman","passagePhrase":"two live births per woman"},{"uid":"4f46cebf-6513-487a-a90f-ceed90b3fa66","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"What has surprised experts most","passagePhrase":"the most surprising demographic development"},{"uid":"52d0c753-8c7e-4f5e-85bd-78bea7ea8e88","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"over the past two decades","passagePhrase":"the past 20 years"},{"uid":"ad2e99c7-95a9-4beb-8c6e-8d6a71adbcac","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"how quickly birth rates have also dropped","passagePhrase":"the pace of fertility decline"},{"uid":"e8830c26-7dcf-406e-a210-0180bc224d6c","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"During the late 20th century","passagePhrase":"in the latter part of the 20th century"},{"uid":"47ddfd4c-9912-4668-b81d-722da9c70fad","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"age ... brought down","passagePhrase":"lowered the official age"},{"uid":"20df9781-6120-427d-a208-a005fe7619df","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"at which full ... could be claimed","passagePhrase":"at which people become fully entitled to"},{"uid":"fe14f459-0879-488b-a463-ca6af2fe5561","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"require employees to pay larger","passagePhrase":"increase ... made by workers"},{"uid":"9628edca-ba8f-47e9-8c32-839cc359eacc","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"repair","passagePhrase":"reform"},{"uid":"e90835c0-6dda-4bb2-8c22-3377dee34134","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"pushed this age back up","passagePhrase":"raise the age at which workers are eligible for full public pension benefits"},{"uid":"23131b38-a9fe-4572-8fa9-346c4d806ef2","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Rising life expectancy","passagePhrase":"life expectancy increases"},{"uid":"f514e586-9c51-46d4-9aaf-e8e6e8c98e2f","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"increases the number of","passagePhrase":"so do the odds of different"},{"uid":"f3da8421-b368-447d-9a6b-c268ae0af9b6","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"family ... being alive at the same time","passagePhrase":"within a family coexisting"},{"uid":"ca14a62e-b675-4f01-a867-53d3a60c8de5","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"In richer countries","passagePhrase":"In more developed countries"},{"uid":"d5ace762-1357-4d9c-aa0b-4bb2f6d9fa93","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"this has produced the so-called","passagePhrase":"this has manifested itself as"},{"uid":"3d2a62e4-8e33-41b1-aa48-3d602f779404","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"a taller, thinner family tree","passagePhrase":"a vertical extension of family structure"},{"uid":"ee5a6220-d01e-47af-811b-95212da649fe","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"with more levels but fewer people on each one","passagePhrase":"an increase in the number of living generations within a lineage and a decrease in the number of people within each generation"},{"uid":"1bb7ef82-c7ee-4b51-a272-adc51e9eaf09","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"History offers no","passagePhrase":"no historical"},{"uid":"f4878ddd-ac49-4e05-91aa-59b000709134","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"for such a change in family demographics","passagePhrase":"for a majority of middle-aged and older adults having living parents"},{"uid":"edf0b0c5-fe7a-4ff2-ac08-db550f24fb29","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"long-term illnesses","passagePhrase":"non-communicable diseases"},{"uid":"072953a7-fd48-4acf-99c8-e798f4783899","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Poorer nations","passagePhrase":"low- and middle-income countries"},{"uid":"32b86d66-2672-4436-a31b-8a3dd5a1ea80","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"communicable diseases"},{"uid":"fe98e37a-1a0f-423e-8b04-663dffbbf82f","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"health spending","passagePhrase":"resources"},{"uid":"f685dd16-92bf-4b65-a8cd-6038affdaea2","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"people have lived longer","passagePhrase":"the increase in longevity"},{"uid":"01e1cdba-0587-48a1-8f50-7778cce5df8c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"money","passagePhrase":"capital"},{"uid":"e71ea412-812e-4dd6-8a3d-02eed741504a","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"The movement of money across borders","passagePhrase":"flow across national boundaries ... capital"},{"uid":"2bbead1d-6473-44c0-b33f-569dbe229013","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"invested abroad","passagePhrase":"flow from ... to emerging markets in Asia and Latin America"},{"uid":"59c153bc-05ef-4454-b6b0-9aea0434fed4","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"richer Western nations","passagePhrase":"Europe and North America"},{"uid":"30df84af-0060-42c1-a7ef-25ffd1a363e4","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"is likely to return to them","passagePhrase":"will most likely flow in the opposite direction"},{"uid":"53a6ded1-a059-4dcd-8b0a-9d623a12da8e","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"what ... will mean for everyone","passagePhrase":"the significance ... and its global implications"},{"uid":"85e02b73-11a2-4f2d-bbbb-77f7caef590a","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"older societies","passagePhrase":"population ageing"},{"uid":"4d9014e4-5393-4e99-9b3a-ef91c68b3320","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"The world still does not fully grasp","passagePhrase":"have yet to be wholly appreciated"},{"uid":"32b86d66-2672-4436-a31b-8a3dd5a1ea80 478f4453-d4f6-404d-98f7-532bbb467bd0","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"infections","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_64":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions</span></b> <b><span>1-13</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Rosetta Stone</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"1\"><b><span>A. </span></b><span>The Rosetta Stone is 45 inches high at its tallest point, 28.5 inches wide, and 11 inches thick. The stone is inscribed with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f0b07a24-a14f-48d8-a729-c3b7914c7898\">a decree setting up the cult of the pharaoh for Ptolemy V<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, who was the fifth ruler of the Hellenistic Ptolemaic Dynasty. Ptolemy V began his rule when he was five years old, and thus much of the ruling of Egypt during his reign was done by regents and royal priests. With the Rosetta Stone, these priests continued the precedent set by Ptolemy III of <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 7\" data-uid=\"7b2c82da-fd3b-40c5-b321-738cb20b9122 c567f0d5-b003-4017-8a2d-0a1f9742f922\">issuing decrees to the populace</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> themselves, rather than having the pharaoh do so. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"c567f0d5-b003-4017-8a2d-0a1f9742f922\">had the decrees inscribed on stone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"c567f0d5-b003-4017-8a2d-0a1f9742f922\">erected throughout Egypt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. The Rosetta Stone is a copy of a decree issued in the city of Memphis.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"2\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span>After the downfall of Cleopatra, Egypt fell under Roman rule. Within one hundred years, the Romans <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"8736674c-1075-4add-9152-12522ef43dff\">lost all </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"8736674c-1075-4add-9152-12522ef43dff f7f1525f-2bfd-44c7-9a9b-7ae8473d4990\">knowledge</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f7f1525f-2bfd-44c7-9a9b-7ae8473d4990\"> of Egyptian hieroglyphics</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, as most Romans did not value them or even consider them a language at all. When the Roman Empire fell, the Middle Ages began and Egypt experienced an era of relative chaos. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2 8\" data-uid=\"8736674c-1075-4add-9152-12522ef43dff d49c6236-1742-4348-99b2-a8321ff87d3c\">Some knowledge of hieroglyphics continued</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"8736674c-1075-4add-9152-12522ef43dff\">, however</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, because of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"80e0a3b8-1cf2-4270-a34f-5562a5d42780\">the idea that the bitumen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> used in the preparation of Egyptian mummies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"80e0a3b8-1cf2-4270-a34f-5562a5d42780\">had healing properties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a3bc2497-00d4-481e-88bb-03a2fe7a6fe3\">The trade in mummies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> allowed examples of hieroglyphs to reach Europe. In 1633, a Jesuit priest named Athanasius Kircher made some minor translations of the hieroglyphs by substituting ideas for images, which was one correct approach to reading them. However, any progress in translation was very slow.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"3\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span>When Napoleon reached Egypt in 1798, he brought many scientists and archaeologists to the region. Napoleon originally expected to take Egypt quickly, but, due to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"deab01b3-16f3-4e6b-8fa1-3847d1da020b\">British naval opposition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"a42eedf3-471a-4c6d-95fc-9f09a0a3cab6\">he and his forces were compelled to stay for three years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. This allowed the 167 scientists, technicians, mathematicians, and artists the army had brought with them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"6e39f578-8abd-4f64-88f1-39bad258e4f9\">ample time to study Egyptian culture and artifacts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"fc3f678b-3a72-4077-94ca-a5129f2af884\">The French Army engineer Pierre-François Bouchard found the stone on July 15, 1799<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, while he was guiding construction works near the Egyptian port city of Rosetta (present-day Rashid). He recognised its importance and sent it to Cairo. After <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"236b3e65-6c39-4451-b2a9-d721f0436f48\">the French surrender<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, a dispute arose over the fate of French archaeological and scientific discoveries in Egypt. Finally, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3 10\" data-uid=\"67ac864d-112e-4baa-a148-375922353521 f0bf6a16-0bfb-4b89-a293-6222f9f4f175\">the British took the stone to the UK</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f0bf6a16-0bfb-4b89-a293-6222f9f4f175\"> as </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3 10\" data-uid=\"236b3e65-6c39-4451-b2a9-d721f0436f48 f0bf6a16-0bfb-4b89-a293-6222f9f4f175\">one of the spoils of war</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> in February 1802. It was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"dc0e698e-0d52-465d-9fdf-efb281c6cf42\">first presented to the Society of Antiquities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> and was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"1d5f63cb-99d2-49af-95d5-c5181255dd1c\">later taken to the British Museum, where it has remained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> almost continuously ever since.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"4\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span>The Rosetta Stone was inscribed with three scripts, so that it could be read not only by the local populace, but also by visiting priests and government officials. The first script was Egyptian hieroglyphs, the script used for religious documents and other important communications. The second was Demotic Egyptian, which was the common script of Egypt. The third was Greek, which was the language of the court. The stone displays the same Ptolemaic decree of 196 BCE in all three scripts. The linguistic value of the stone lies in the fact that someone who can understand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"790ba409-5605-4fc4-b206-9c587bbb3535\">ancient Greek<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> would therefore have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"fbc5b614-6b70-4bae-a272-d5bad09930da\">a guide to the other two unknown languages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. In 1822, the Frenchman Jean-François Champollion, who understood ancient Greek, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"fbc5b614-6b70-4bae-a272-d5bad09930da\">was able to decipher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> Egyptian hieroglyphs and Demotic Egyptian. Although this has not affected its financial and cultural worth, the Rosetta Stone is no longer unique, as other fragments of decrees in the same languages have since been discovered. Together, the stones have unlocked the previously indecipherable languages found at archaeological sites all over Egypt.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"5\"><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Except when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"71b89f82-abde-48d4-92be-635d3f704c4b\">on temporary loan for other museum exhibits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, the Rosetta Stone has been exhibited in the British Museum since 1802, with only one break, from 1917 to 1919. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d19c01ce-b6fc-4f86-b8ae-2a3dfff44104\">Toward the end of the First World War<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, in 1917, when the Museum was concerned about heavy bombing in London, the Rosetta Stone was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"11256c80-14b5-4420-abab-a15830347193\">moved to safety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> along with other portable, important objects. The Rosetta Stone spent the next two years in a station on the Postal Tube Railway, 50 feet underground at Holborn.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"6\"><b><span>F. </span></b><span>In July 2003, Dr. Zahi Hawass, secretary general of the Supreme Council of Antiquities in Cairo, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b80eda04-c5a4-4c4a-a554-489dcd870e24\">demanded the return<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of the Rosetta Stone. After quite a long period of negotiations, Dr. Hawass proposed to drop his claim for the permanent return of the Rosetta Stone if the British Museum would loan the stone to Egypt for three months, for the opening of the Grand Egyptian Museum at Giza in 2013, and would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"9e509434-1082-4ca1-9827-7f2cadadbec9\">provide a life-size replica of the Rosetta Stone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> as a compromise, to be put on display in the newly opened Rashid National Museum. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"f2889eec-18dd-4a11-a505-f42d671766a0\">This proposal was agreed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. Like many museums around the world that hold treasures from other countries, the British Museum has been unwilling to relinquish its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b80eda04-c5a4-4c4a-a554-489dcd870e24\">claim to the Rosetta Stone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, and one commentator was reported to have said that the Rosetta Stone will soon have spent longer in the British Museum than it ever did in Rosetta. The British Museum is also under pressure from Greece to return the Elgin Marbles, which were taken from the Parthenon in Athens in the early nineteenth century. The legal situation is slightly different, as the British Museum claims that the Elgin Marbles were taken with the permission of the then Greek government and that, in any case, a statute of limitations would apply, the removal being so long ago. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"79694439-c61b-4253-93ba-766bf73fa873\">The disputes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> over both archaeological treasures <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"79694439-c61b-4253-93ba-766bf73fa873\">continue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>The text on the previous pages has 6 paragraphs (</span><b><span>A – F</span></b><span>).</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct number (</span></i><i><b><span>i – viii</span></b></i><i><span>) in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>1-6</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><b><span>i. </span></b><span>How <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"790ba409-5605-4fc4-b206-9c587bbb3535\">one version of the text<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"fbc5b614-6b70-4bae-a272-d5bad09930da\">solved a puzzle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><b><span>ii.</span></b><span> How <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f7f1525f-2bfd-44c7-9a9b-7ae8473d4990\">the meaning of the symbols<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"8736674c-1075-4add-9152-12522ef43dff\">almost forgotten<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><b><span>iii.</span></b><span> An early scholar's complete success</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><b><span>iv.</span></b><span> An <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"fc3f678b-3a72-4077-94ca-a5129f2af884\">accidental find<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f0bf6a16-0bfb-4b89-a293-6222f9f4f175\">changed hands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><b><span>v.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"11256c80-14b5-4420-abab-a15830347193\">Protecting the stone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d19c01ce-b6fc-4f86-b8ae-2a3dfff44104\">during wartime<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><b><span>vi.</span></b><span> Damage caused by enemy bombing</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><b><span>vii.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f0b07a24-a14f-48d8-a729-c3b7914c7898\">The stone's background<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"7b2c82da-fd3b-40c5-b321-738cb20b9122\">purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><b><span>viii.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"79694439-c61b-4253-93ba-766bf73fa873\">The unresolved question<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b80eda04-c5a4-4c4a-a554-489dcd870e24\">rightful ownership<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325746\" id=\"question-wrapper-325746\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325747\" id=\"question-wrapper-325747\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325748\" id=\"question-wrapper-325748\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325749\" id=\"question-wrapper-325749\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325750\" id=\"question-wrapper-325750\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325751\" id=\"question-wrapper-325751\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>7-10</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325752\" id=\"question-wrapper-325752\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Rosetta Stone was originally created as</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. a declaration issued personally by the young king.</li> <li>B. the first decree of its kind in Egypt.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"c567f0d5-b003-4017-8a2d-0a1f9742f922\">a means of announcing official orders to the public<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</li> <li>D. a religious text intended only for priests.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325753\" id=\"question-wrapper-325753\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"d49c6236-1742-4348-99b2-a8321ff87d3c\">Some understanding of hieroglyphics survived into later eras<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the Romans regarded them as a genuine language.</li> <li>B. a priest had produced a complete translation of them.</li> <li>C. Egypt remained politically stable after Roman rule ended.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a3bc2497-00d4-481e-88bb-03a2fe7a6fe3\">mummies were traded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"80e0a3b8-1cf2-4270-a34f-5562a5d42780\">their supposed medicinal value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325754\" id=\"question-wrapper-325754\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Napoleon’s French archaeologists were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"6e39f578-8abd-4f64-88f1-39bad258e4f9\">able to study ancient Egypt for so long<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Napoleon had planned a lengthy stay from the start.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"deab01b3-16f3-4e6b-8fa1-3847d1da020b\">British military opposition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"a42eedf3-471a-4c6d-95fc-9f09a0a3cab6\">delayed Napoleon<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</li> <li>C. the archaeologists were also in Napoleon’s army.</li> <li>D. they were needed to supervise building work.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325755\" id=\"question-wrapper-325755\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"67ac864d-112e-4baa-a148-375922353521\">The British were able to get possession of the Rosetta Stone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"236b3e65-6c39-4451-b2a9-d721f0436f48\">they&nbsp;had defeated the French in battle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</li> <li>B. the French willingly gave up all their discoveries.</li> <li>C. the&nbsp;British Museum had requested it.</li> <li>D. its finder had sent it straight to Britain instead of to Cairo.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>THREE</span></b><span> letters, </span><b><span>A – F</span></b><span>. Write the correct letters, </span><b><span>A – F</span></b><span>, in any order in boxes </span><b><span>11-13</span></b><span> on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>THREE</span></b><span> of the following happened to the Rosetta Stone whilst in British possession?</span></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> It became less valuable, as other similar stones were found.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> It has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"71b89f82-abde-48d4-92be-635d3f704c4b\">occasionally been shown at other institutions for limited periods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"dc0e698e-0d52-465d-9fdf-efb281c6cf42\">passed through a learned body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> before <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"1d5f63cb-99d2-49af-95d5-c5181255dd1c\">settling in its present home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> It was lent to Egypt for the opening of a museum in Rashid.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> The museum <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"f2889eec-18dd-4a11-a505-f42d671766a0\">accepted a deal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> that included <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"9e509434-1082-4ca1-9827-7f2cadadbec9\">giving Egypt a duplicate of it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> It shares a display room in the British Museum with the Elgin Marbles.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325756\" id=\"question-wrapper-325756\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325757\" id=\"question-wrapper-325757\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325758\" id=\"question-wrapper-325758\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f0b07a24-a14f-48d8-a729-c3b7914c7898","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"The stone's background","passagePhrase":"a decree setting up the cult of the pharaoh for Ptolemy V"},{"uid":"7b2c82da-fd3b-40c5-b321-738cb20b9122 c567f0d5-b003-4017-8a2d-0a1f9742f922","qNum":"1 7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"issuing decrees to the populace"},{"uid":"c567f0d5-b003-4017-8a2d-0a1f9742f922","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"a means of announcing official orders to the public","passagePhrase":"had the decrees inscribed on stone ... erected throughout Egypt"},{"uid":"8736674c-1075-4add-9152-12522ef43dff","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"almost forgotten","passagePhrase":"lost all ... , however"},{"uid":"8736674c-1075-4add-9152-12522ef43dff f7f1525f-2bfd-44c7-9a9b-7ae8473d4990","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"knowledge"},{"uid":"f7f1525f-2bfd-44c7-9a9b-7ae8473d4990","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"the meaning of the symbols","passagePhrase":"of Egyptian hieroglyphics"},{"uid":"8736674c-1075-4add-9152-12522ef43dff d49c6236-1742-4348-99b2-a8321ff87d3c","qNum":"2 8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Some knowledge of hieroglyphics continued"},{"uid":"80e0a3b8-1cf2-4270-a34f-5562a5d42780","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"their supposed medicinal value","passagePhrase":"the idea that the bitumen ... had healing properties"},{"uid":"a3bc2497-00d4-481e-88bb-03a2fe7a6fe3","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"mummies were traded","passagePhrase":"The trade in mummies"},{"uid":"deab01b3-16f3-4e6b-8fa1-3847d1da020b","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"British military opposition","passagePhrase":"British naval opposition"},{"uid":"a42eedf3-471a-4c6d-95fc-9f09a0a3cab6","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"delayed Napoleon","passagePhrase":"he and his forces were compelled to stay for three years"},{"uid":"6e39f578-8abd-4f64-88f1-39bad258e4f9","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"able to study ancient Egypt for so long","passagePhrase":"ample time to study Egyptian culture and artifacts"},{"uid":"fc3f678b-3a72-4077-94ca-a5129f2af884","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"accidental find","passagePhrase":"The French Army engineer Pierre-François Bouchard found the stone on July 15, 1799"},{"uid":"236b3e65-6c39-4451-b2a9-d721f0436f48","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"they had defeated the French in battle","passagePhrase":"the French surrender"},{"uid":"67ac864d-112e-4baa-a148-375922353521 f0bf6a16-0bfb-4b89-a293-6222f9f4f175","qNum":"3 10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the British took the stone to the UK"},{"uid":"f0bf6a16-0bfb-4b89-a293-6222f9f4f175","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"changed hands","passagePhrase":"as"},{"uid":"236b3e65-6c39-4451-b2a9-d721f0436f48 f0bf6a16-0bfb-4b89-a293-6222f9f4f175","qNum":"3 10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"one of the spoils of war"},{"uid":"dc0e698e-0d52-465d-9fdf-efb281c6cf42","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"passed through a learned body","passagePhrase":"first presented to the Society of Antiquities"},{"uid":"1d5f63cb-99d2-49af-95d5-c5181255dd1c","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"settling in its present home","passagePhrase":"later taken to the British Museum, where it has remained"},{"uid":"790ba409-5605-4fc4-b206-9c587bbb3535","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"one version of the text","passagePhrase":"ancient Greek"},{"uid":"fbc5b614-6b70-4bae-a272-d5bad09930da","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"solved a puzzle","passagePhrase":"a guide to the other two unknown languages ... was able to decipher"},{"uid":"71b89f82-abde-48d4-92be-635d3f704c4b","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"occasionally been shown at other institutions for limited periods","passagePhrase":"on temporary loan for other museum exhibits"},{"uid":"d19c01ce-b6fc-4f86-b8ae-2a3dfff44104","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"during wartime","passagePhrase":"Toward the end of the First World War"},{"uid":"11256c80-14b5-4420-abab-a15830347193","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Protecting the stone","passagePhrase":"moved to safety"},{"uid":"b80eda04-c5a4-4c4a-a554-489dcd870e24","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"rightful ownership","passagePhrase":"demanded the return ... claim to the Rosetta Stone"},{"uid":"9e509434-1082-4ca1-9827-7f2cadadbec9","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"giving Egypt a duplicate of it","passagePhrase":"provide a life-size replica of the Rosetta Stone"},{"uid":"f2889eec-18dd-4a11-a505-f42d671766a0","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"accepted a deal","passagePhrase":"This proposal was agreed"},{"uid":"79694439-c61b-4253-93ba-766bf73fa873","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"The unresolved question","passagePhrase":"The disputes ... continue"},{"uid":"7b2c82da-fd3b-40c5-b321-738cb20b9122","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"purpose","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"d49c6236-1742-4348-99b2-a8321ff87d3c","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Some understanding of hieroglyphics survived into later eras","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"67ac864d-112e-4baa-a148-375922353521","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"The British were able to get possession of the Rosetta Stone","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_65":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 14-26</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>We Have Star Performers!</span></b></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> The difference between companies is people. With capital and technology in plentiful supply, the critical resource for companies in the knowledge era will be human talent. Companies full of achievers will, by definition, outperform organisations of plodders. Ergo, compete ferociously for the best people. Poach and pamper stars; ruthlessly weed out second-raters. This, in essence, has been the recruitment strategy of the ambitious company of the past decade. The 'talent mindset' was given definitive form in two reports by the consultancy McKinsey, famously entitled </span><i><span>The War for Talent</span></i><span>. Although <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"b8d773b2-1713-4a47-9623-4f377f5d95c5\">the intensity of the warfare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> subsequently subsided along with the air in the internet bubble, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"44b3ba50-d728-4fa1-b184-8332f7e10f36\">has been warming up again<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ed481753-8243-402c-9d55-1321450d8d2f\">as the economy tightens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>: labour shortages, for example, are the reason the government has laid out the welcome mat for immigrants from the new Europe.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Yet while the diagnosis – people are important – is evident to the point of platitude, the apparently logical prescription – hire the best – is, like so much in management, not only not obvious; it is in fact profoundly wrong. The first suspicions dawned with the crash to earth of the dotcom meteors, which showed that dumb is dumb, whatever the IQ of those who perpetrate it. The point was illuminated in brilliant relief by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9901e388-8f85-4886-9381-a0b49b205701\">Enron, whose leaders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, as a New Yorker article called 'The Talent Myth' entertainingly related, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e01f385d-c403-4ad7-a3d6-4f0d2d8aa1af\">were so convinced of their own cleverness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> that they never twigged that collective intelligence is not the sum of a lot of individual intelligence. In fact, in a profound sense, the two are opposites. Enron <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e01f385d-c403-4ad7-a3d6-4f0d2d8aa1af\">believed in stars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, noted author Malcolm Gladwell, because they didn't believe in systems. But companies don't just create: 'they execute and compete and coordinate the efforts of many people, and the organisations that are most successful at that task are the ones where the system is the star'. The truth is that you can't win the talent wars by hiring stars – only lose them. New light on why this should be so is thrown by an analysis of star behaviour in this month's Harvard Business Review. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6d04eb67-90cc-4827-81d2-f0d31f6bedb0\">a study of the careers of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"abd3d444-9067-4acd-942f-96c47880400f\">1,000 star<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> stock analysts in the 1990s, the researchers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a2869aa7-9ebe-4131-a7d5-d82a03682d95\">found that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c6992b9a-e032-4521-a4fd-202164385508\">a company recruited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> a star performer, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"690b0a1a-b19d-4dcc-a40d-0291ecd20bb4\">three things happened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> First, stardom doesn't easily transfer from one organisation to another. In many cases, performance <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"85f7a9af-e62f-4c81-be82-fb3a857b148b\">dropped sharply when<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e110443f-7493-488d-a6e0-e1c044cd2e0b\">high performers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"85f7a9af-e62f-4c81-be82-fb3a857b148b\">switched employers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> and, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"9dee35f5-3c3f-4052-abb9-2fc3c8845cbf\">in some instances, never recovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. More of success than commonly supposed is due to the working environment – systems, processes, leadership, accumulated embedded learning – which are absent from the new firm and cannot be transported to it. Moreover, precisely because of their past stellar performance, stars were unwilling to learn new tricks and antagonised those (on whom they now unwittingly depended) who could teach them. So <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"976c9e60-46dd-4f7d-a1aa-e8c1eabbf060\">they moved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"5f114606-986f-4173-97ba-56db65c15bc5\">upping<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> their salaries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"bcd7c814-7883-4aeb-8c4d-c81a7bd00e0d\">as they did<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> – 36 per cent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"976c9e60-46dd-4f7d-a1aa-e8c1eabbf060\">moved on within three years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"976c9e60-46dd-4f7d-a1aa-e8c1eabbf060\">fast even for Wall Street<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Second, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"19ae8e40-df6b-4fb2-ac8c-c341cb847af6\">group performance suffered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> as a result of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"92237672-1d64-4042-9946-003cc72de0c3\">tensions and resentment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> among rivals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"0792484b-d96b-4de3-9e27-04cd01377c6e\">within the team<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. One respondent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3fea8e55-ed03-431f-a8ed-234a48cb5ece\">likened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"17fe3027-81d3-430c-9a41-8191cf7e135a\">hiring a star<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3fea8e55-ed03-431f-a8ed-234a48cb5ece\">to an organ transplant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"17fe3027-81d3-430c-9a41-8191cf7e135a\">The new organ can damage others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> by hogging the blood supply; other organs can start aching or threaten to stop working, or the body can reject the transplant altogether, he said. 'You should think about it very carefully before you do a transplant to a healthy body.' Third, investors punished the offender by selling its stock. This is ironic since the motive for importing stars was often a suffering share price in the first place. Shareholders evidently believe that the company is overpaying, the new hire is cashing in on a glorious past rather than preparing for a glowing present, and a spending spree is in the offing.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> The result of mass star hirings as well as individual ones seems to confirm such doubts. Look at County NatWest and Barclays de Zoete Wedd, both of which hired teams of stars with loud fanfare to do great things in investment banking in the 1990s. Both failed dismally. Everyone accepts the cliché that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"b59bfde3-7b75-4472-8984-af87853f7852\">people make the organisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> – but <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5a8f58e8-c0dc-4d01-b722-60ddbff26056\">much more does the organisation make the people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. When researchers studied the performance of fund managers in the 1990s, they discovered that just 30 per cent of the variation in fund performance was due to the individual, compared to 70 per cent to the company-specific setting.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> That will be no surprise to those familiar with systems thinking. W. Edwards Deming used to say that there was no point in beating up on people when 90 per cent of performance variation was down to the system within which they worked. Consistent improvement, he said, is a matter not of raising the level of individual intelligence, but of the learning of the organisation as a whole. The star system is glamorous – for the few. But it rarely benefits the company that thinks it is working. And the knock-on consequences indirectly affect everyone else too. As one internet response to Gladwell's New Yorker article put it: after Enron, 'the rest of corporate America is stuck with overpaid, arrogant, underachieving, and relatively useless talent.'</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c92ca21f-8f58-4a6b-81c5-6614d5e635e4\">Football is another illustration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of the star-vs-systems strategic choice. As with investment banks and stockbrokers, it seems obvious that success should ultimately be down to money. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"abfa2ccc-6f7f-417e-9532-9c8509e863c1\">Great players are scarce and expensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. So the club that can afford more of them than anyone else will win. But the performance of Arsenal and Manchester United on one hand and Chelsea and Real Madrid on the other proves that it's not as easy as that. While Chelsea and Real have the funds to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"abfa2ccc-6f7f-417e-9532-9c8509e863c1\">compulsive star collectors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> – as with Juan Sebastián Verón – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2f0d4910-2538-4e07-aa4d-8dc74e5f41b4\">they are less successful than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> Arsenal and United, which, like Liverpool before them, have put much more emphasis on developing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"431cbcdf-45e5-4d7a-95cc-27ffc51d4d24\">a setting within which stars-in-the-making can flourish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. Significantly, Thierry Henry, Patrick Vieira and Robert Pirès are much bigger stars than when Arsenal bought them, their value (in all senses) enhanced by the Arsenal system. At Chelsea, by contrast, the only context is the stars themselves – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0949dda1-ac8f-4a35-95d1-9d4e94f1021b\">managers with different outlooks come and go every couple of seasons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"72afd00d-9ffd-40fb-b58b-ff62a061e0ab\">There is no settled system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> for the stars to blend into. The Chelsea context has not only failed to add value, but it has also subtracted it. The side is less than the sum of its exorbitantly expensive parts. Even Real Madrid's galácticos, the most extravagantly gifted on the planet, are being outperformed by less talented but better-integrated Spanish sides. In football, too, stars are trumped by systems.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> So if not by hiring stars, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"b37c89ca-2f1a-48b4-a948-9946b9d1ea6b\">how do you compete in the war for talent? You grow your own<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. This worked for investment analysts, where some companies were not only better at creating stars but also at retaining them. Because they had a much more sophisticated view of the interdependent relationship between star and system, they kept them longer without resorting to the exorbitant salaries that were so destructive to rivals.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>The Reading Passage has seven paragraphs A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325759\" id=\"question-wrapper-325759\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c92ca21f-8f58-4a6b-81c5-6614d5e635e4\">An example from the world of sport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"431cbcdf-45e5-4d7a-95cc-27ffc51d4d24\">a well-established structure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2f0d4910-2538-4e07-aa4d-8dc74e5f41b4\">outperforms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"abfa2ccc-6f7f-417e-9532-9c8509e863c1\">costly individual talent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325760\" id=\"question-wrapper-325760\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9901e388-8f85-4886-9381-a0b49b205701\">A company whose leaders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e01f385d-c403-4ad7-a3d6-4f0d2d8aa1af\">placed too much faith in the intelligence of exceptional individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325761\" id=\"question-wrapper-325761\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"b37c89ca-2f1a-48b4-a948-9946b9d1ea6b\">The writer's recommendation for how a company should obtain the talent it needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325762\" id=\"question-wrapper-325762\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3fea8e55-ed03-431f-a8ed-234a48cb5ece\">A comparison with a medical procedure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that shows <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"17fe3027-81d3-430c-9a41-8191cf7e135a\">the risks of bringing in a star<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 2? In boxes 18–21 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325763\" id=\"question-wrapper-325763\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"b8d773b2-1713-4a47-9623-4f377f5d95c5\">The fierce competition for talented workers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"44b3ba50-d728-4fa1-b184-8332f7e10f36\">is becoming more intense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ed481753-8243-402c-9d55-1321450d8d2f\">because of economic conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325764\" id=\"question-wrapper-325764\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"b59bfde3-7b75-4472-8984-af87853f7852\">Individual employees can shape their workplace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5a8f58e8-c0dc-4d01-b722-60ddbff26056\">more strongly than the workplace can shape its employees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325765\" id=\"question-wrapper-325765\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Deming's views on performance variation were based on studies of financial firms.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325766\" id=\"question-wrapper-325766\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Chelsea has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"72afd00d-9ffd-40fb-b58b-ff62a061e0ab\">unable to establish a lasting framework<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0949dda1-ac8f-4a35-95d1-9d4e94f1021b\">its managers are replaced so often<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22–26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6d04eb67-90cc-4827-81d2-f0d31f6bedb0\">An investigation carried out on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"abd3d444-9067-4acd-942f-96c47880400f\">1,000 high-performing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> (22)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a2869aa7-9ebe-4131-a7d5-d82a03682d95\">found that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c6992b9a-e032-4521-a4fd-202164385508\">a company hiring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> a (23)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"690b0a1a-b19d-4dcc-a40d-0291ecd20bb4\">suffers several negative effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. For instance, the (24)________ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e110443f-7493-488d-a6e0-e1c044cd2e0b\">such hires<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"85f7a9af-e62f-4c81-be82-fb3a857b148b\">frequently declines steeply at the new firm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"9dee35f5-3c3f-4052-abb9-2fc3c8845cbf\">may never return to its former level<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"976c9e60-46dd-4f7d-a1aa-e8c1eabbf060\">They also tend to leave their new firms quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"5f114606-986f-4173-97ba-56db65c15bc5\">increasing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> their (25)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"bcd7c814-7883-4aeb-8c4d-c81a7bd00e0d\">each time they move<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Secondly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"19ae8e40-df6b-4fb2-ac8c-c341cb847af6\">group results decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> because of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"92237672-1d64-4042-9946-003cc72de0c3\">friction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> with (26)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"0792484b-d96b-4de3-9e27-04cd01377c6e\">in the same unit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Lastly, the hiring company sees its share price fall as investors sell its stock.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325767\" id=\"question-wrapper-325767\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(stock) analysts</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325768\" id=\"question-wrapper-325768\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">star performer</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325769\" id=\"question-wrapper-325769\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">performance</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325770\" id=\"question-wrapper-325770\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">salaries</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325771\" id=\"question-wrapper-325771\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">rivals</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b8d773b2-1713-4a47-9623-4f377f5d95c5","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"The fierce competition for talented workers","passagePhrase":"the intensity of the warfare"},{"uid":"44b3ba50-d728-4fa1-b184-8332f7e10f36","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"is becoming more intense","passagePhrase":"has been warming up again"},{"uid":"ed481753-8243-402c-9d55-1321450d8d2f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"because of economic conditions","passagePhrase":"as the economy tightens"},{"uid":"9901e388-8f85-4886-9381-a0b49b205701","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"A company whose leaders","passagePhrase":"Enron, whose leaders"},{"uid":"e01f385d-c403-4ad7-a3d6-4f0d2d8aa1af","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"placed too much faith in the intelligence of exceptional individuals","passagePhrase":"were so convinced of their own cleverness ... believed in stars"},{"uid":"6d04eb67-90cc-4827-81d2-f0d31f6bedb0","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"An investigation carried out on","passagePhrase":"a study of the careers of"},{"uid":"abd3d444-9067-4acd-942f-96c47880400f","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"1,000 high-performing","passagePhrase":"1,000 star"},{"uid":"a2869aa7-9ebe-4131-a7d5-d82a03682d95","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"found that","passagePhrase":"found that"},{"uid":"c6992b9a-e032-4521-a4fd-202164385508","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"a company hiring","passagePhrase":"a company recruited"},{"uid":"690b0a1a-b19d-4dcc-a40d-0291ecd20bb4","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"suffers several negative effects","passagePhrase":"three things happened"},{"uid":"85f7a9af-e62f-4c81-be82-fb3a857b148b","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"frequently declines steeply at the new firm","passagePhrase":"dropped sharply when ... switched employers"},{"uid":"e110443f-7493-488d-a6e0-e1c044cd2e0b","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"such hires","passagePhrase":"high performers"},{"uid":"9dee35f5-3c3f-4052-abb9-2fc3c8845cbf","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"may never return to its former level","passagePhrase":"in some instances, never recovered"},{"uid":"976c9e60-46dd-4f7d-a1aa-e8c1eabbf060","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"They also tend to leave their new firms quickly","passagePhrase":"they moved ... moved on within three years ... fast even for Wall Street"},{"uid":"5f114606-986f-4173-97ba-56db65c15bc5","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"increasing","passagePhrase":"upping"},{"uid":"bcd7c814-7883-4aeb-8c4d-c81a7bd00e0d","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"each time they move","passagePhrase":"as they did"},{"uid":"19ae8e40-df6b-4fb2-ac8c-c341cb847af6","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"group results decline","passagePhrase":"group performance suffered"},{"uid":"92237672-1d64-4042-9946-003cc72de0c3","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"friction","passagePhrase":"tensions and resentment"},{"uid":"0792484b-d96b-4de3-9e27-04cd01377c6e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"in the same unit","passagePhrase":"within the team"},{"uid":"3fea8e55-ed03-431f-a8ed-234a48cb5ece","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"A comparison with a medical procedure","passagePhrase":"likened ... to an organ transplant"},{"uid":"17fe3027-81d3-430c-9a41-8191cf7e135a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"the risks of bringing in a star","passagePhrase":"hiring a star ... The new organ can damage others"},{"uid":"b59bfde3-7b75-4472-8984-af87853f7852","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Individual employees can shape their workplace","passagePhrase":"people make the organisation"},{"uid":"c92ca21f-8f58-4a6b-81c5-6614d5e635e4","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"An example from the world of sport","passagePhrase":"Football is another illustration"},{"uid":"abfa2ccc-6f7f-417e-9532-9c8509e863c1","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"costly individual talent","passagePhrase":"Great players are scarce and expensive ... compulsive star collectors"},{"uid":"2f0d4910-2538-4e07-aa4d-8dc74e5f41b4","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"outperforms","passagePhrase":"they are less successful than"},{"uid":"431cbcdf-45e5-4d7a-95cc-27ffc51d4d24","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"a well-established structure","passagePhrase":"a setting within which stars-in-the-making can flourish"},{"uid":"0949dda1-ac8f-4a35-95d1-9d4e94f1021b","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"its managers are replaced so often","passagePhrase":"managers with different outlooks come and go every couple of seasons"},{"uid":"72afd00d-9ffd-40fb-b58b-ff62a061e0ab","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"unable to establish a lasting framework","passagePhrase":"There is no settled system"},{"uid":"b37c89ca-2f1a-48b4-a948-9946b9d1ea6b","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"The writer's recommendation for how a company should obtain the talent it needs","passagePhrase":"how do you compete in the war for talent? You grow your own"}]},"reading_u2_66":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 27-40</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Architecture in Britain</span></b></p><p><span>From the Middle Ages to the 20th century, what are the influences and movements that have shaped the changing face of British architecture?</span></p><p><span>Architecture is about evolution, not revolution. It used to be thought that once the Romans pulled out of Britain in the fifth century, their elegant villas, carefully planned towns and engineering marvels like Hadrian's Wall simply fell into decay as British culture was plunged into the Dark Ages. It took the Norman Conquest of 1066 to bring back the light, and the Gothic cathedral-builders of the Middle Ages played an important part in the revival of British culture. However, the truth is not as simple as that. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c2d8c95a-ff1f-41e6-9ea2-5adf120888cb\">Romano-British culture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>—and that included architecture along with language, religion, political organisation and the arts—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cf0c45ed-0be6-4475-a927-c1c3f5d9a41f\">survived long<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"06072fa2-e826-4df5-918d-38ffd9784d9b\">after the Roman withdrawal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. And although the Anglo-Saxons had a sophisticated building style of their own, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c6bfc5e8-e11d-45ba-8b0f-fa60d695bd5a\">little survives to bear witness to their achievements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"5d139072-f19e-45e7-bd97-cc98f5170379\">the vast majority of Anglo-Saxon buildings were made of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> wood.</span></p><p><span>Even so, the period between the Norman landing at Pevensey in 1066 and the day in 1485 when Richard III lost his horse and his head at Bosworth, ushering in the Tudors and the Early Modern period, marks a rare flowering of British buildings. And it is all the more remarkable because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a22e8ecb-fb20-4105-8398-04f1f93941c0\">the underlying ethos of medieval architecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> was \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bdf54624-9019-431e-8582-d71483aced90\">fitness for purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>\". The great cathedrals and parish churches that lifted up their towers to heaven were not only acts of devotion in stone; they were also fiercely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bdf54624-9019-431e-8582-d71483aced90\">functional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> buildings. Castles <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bdf54624-9019-431e-8582-d71483aced90\">served their particular purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, and their battlements and turrets were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bdf54624-9019-431e-8582-d71483aced90\">for use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> rather than ornament. The rambling manor houses of the later Middle Ages, however, were primarily homes, their owners achieving respect and maintaining status by their hospitality and good lordship rather than the grandeur of their buildings. In a sense, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"119a6030-a4a9-479a-b651-f006c5417fe5\">the buildings of the 16th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> were also governed by fitness for purpose—only now, the purpose was very different. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"119a6030-a4a9-479a-b651-f006c5417fe5\">domestic architecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, in particular, buildings were used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"e6eb42e3-6a60-4b21-9d7f-630826906ce9\">display<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> status and wealth.</span></p><p><span>This stately and curious workmanship showed itself in various ways. A greater sense of security led to more outward-looking buildings, as opposed to the medieval arrangement where the need for defence created houses that faced inward onto a courtyard or series of courtyards. This allowed for much more in the way of exterior ornament. The rooms themselves tended to be bigger and lighter—as an expensive commodity, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"8986ab1a-9834-4e07-99bb-9bbf685a8821\">the use of great expanses of glass<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> was in itself a statement of wealth. There was also a general move towards <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e3b962e1-df97-46e0-a55c-6ebdf6886ad8\">balanced and symmetrical exteriors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> with central entrances. </span></p><p><span>With the exception of Inigo Jones (1573–1652), whose <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a67ee43c-0f16-48be-b608-fb5d4fce4e06\">confident handling of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> classical <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"3ef996fa-290c-40c6-8d82-7e8c3a52cf2d\">detail and proportion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"3992118f-06f6-4c35-bc85-a068a5f342f1\">set him apart from all other architects of the period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, most early 17th-century buildings tended to take the innocent exuberance of late Tudor work one step further. But during the 1640s and 50s, the Civil War and its aftermath sent many gentlemen and nobles to the Continent, either to escape the fighting or, when the war was lost, to follow Charles II into exile. There they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"c253a1d2-07ee-460b-bade-e02e8a75a89a\">came into contact with French, Dutch and Italian architecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> and, with Charles's restoration in 1660, there was a flurry of building activity as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"cfd5a6e2-fee1-415e-951f-537314eb3e19\">royalists reclaimed their property<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"c253a1d2-07ee-460b-bade-e02e8a75a89a\">built themselves houses reflecting the latest European trends<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. The British Baroque was a reassertion of authority, an expression of absolutist ideology by men who remembered a world turned upside down during the Civil War. The style is heavy and rich, sometimes overblown and melodramatic. The politics which underpin it are questionable, but its products are breathtaking.</span></p><p><span>The huge glass-and-iron Crystal Palace, designed by Joseph Paxton to house the Great Exhibition of 1851, shows another strand to 19th century architecture—one which embraced new industrial processes. But it wasn't long before even this confidence in progress came to be regarded with suspicion. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"1b497149-1342-4fba-800d-780a0a5b7c4a\">Mass production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> resulted in buildings and furnishings that were too perfect, as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"441e8cb2-4e6c-40c8-b8f3-f0af1fd794aa\">the individual craftsman no longer had a major role in their creation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Railing against the dehumanising effects of industrialisation, reformers like John Ruskin and William Morris made a concerted effort to return to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"1eeb27db-d970-4566-8d37-9787ec477f1a\">hand-crafted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, pre-industrial manufacturing techniques. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"d83d8ce4-9edd-41e3-b365-17c337393db5\">Morris's influence grew<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"c6772e05-ea76-45a7-ac83-cd5d867e5ea9\">from the production of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> furniture and textiles until, by the 1880s, a generation of principled young architects was following his call for good, honest construction.</span></p><p><span>The most important trends in early 20th-century architecture simply passed Britain by. Whilst Gropius was working on cold, hard expanses of glass, and Le Corbusier was experimenting with the use of reinforced concrete frames, we had <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 39\" data-uid=\"67151013-eada-439f-9d8b-3a2551b1a346 9a8bd851-ff81-45d9-9f60-c80908ae2a95\">staid establishment</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"9a8bd851-ff81-45d9-9f60-c80908ae2a95\"> architects</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> like Edwin Lutyens <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 39\" data-uid=\"32b31655-b6e6-4f1c-9f21-c61460cf8352 67151013-eada-439f-9d8b-3a2551b1a346\">producing Neo-Georgian and Renaissance country houses</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> for an outmoded landed class. In addition, there were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"9a8bd851-ff81-45d9-9f60-c80908ae2a95\">slightly batty architect-craftsmen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, the heirs of William Morris, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"32b31655-b6e6-4f1c-9f21-c61460cf8352\">still trying to turn the clock back<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to before the Industrial Revolution by making chairs and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"32b31655-b6e6-4f1c-9f21-c61460cf8352\">spurning new technology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Only a handful of Modern Movement buildings of any real merit were produced here during the 1920s and 1930s, and most of these were the work of foreign architects such as Serge Chermayeff, Berthold Lubetkin and Erno Goldfinger who had settled in this country.</span></p><p><span>After the Second World War, the situation began to change. The Modern Movement's belief in progress and the future struck a chord with the mood of post-war Britain and, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"403543f6-da4b-459c-8755-af7327f7be7f\">as reconstruction began<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> under Attlee's Labour government in 1945, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"403543f6-da4b-459c-8755-af7327f7be7f\">there was </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"403543f6-da4b-459c-8755-af7327f7be7f aa317e37-87b6-424d-82c7-87bf9a4aeef3\">a desperate need</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"aa317e37-87b6-424d-82c7-87bf9a4aeef3\"> for cheap housing which could be produced quickly</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. The use of prefabricated elements, metal frames, concrete cladding and the absence of decoration—all of which had been embraced by Modernists abroad and viewed with suspicion by the British—were adopted to varying degrees for housing developments and schools. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"9dde5c52-8217-4646-9de5-deef8f9f9166\">Local authorities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, charged with the task of rebuilding city centres, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"9dde5c52-8217-4646-9de5-deef8f9f9166\">became important patrons of architecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. This represented a shift away from the private individuals who had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"c3147b18-3fcc-4472-84f9-05ca883e8ea1\">dominated the architectural scene<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"a71557f9-7bb3-4d14-88aa-7046785d5dec\">for centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Since the War, it has been corporate bodies like these local authorities, together with national and multinational companies, and large educational institutions, which have dominated British architecture. By the late 1980s, the Modern Movement, unfairly blamed for the social experiments implicit in high-rise housing, had lost out to irony and spectacle in the shape of post-modernism, with its cheerful borrowings from anywhere and any period. But now, in the new Millennium, even post-modernism is showing signs of age. What comes next?</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>27-33</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325772\" id=\"question-wrapper-325772\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What happened to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c2d8c95a-ff1f-41e6-9ea2-5adf120888cb\">Roman culture in Britain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"06072fa2-e826-4df5-918d-38ffd9784d9b\">after the Roman withdrawal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It was largely neglected.</li> <li>B. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cf0c45ed-0be6-4475-a927-c1c3f5d9a41f\">continued to influence British life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>C. It disappeared almost immediately.</li> <li>D. It was preserved mainly through buildings.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325773\" id=\"question-wrapper-325773\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a22e8ecb-fb20-4105-8398-04f1f93941c0\">The overriding principle of medieval architecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> was that buildings should be</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. immense.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bdf54624-9019-431e-8582-d71483aced90\">useful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>C. decorative.</li> <li>D. durable.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325774\" id=\"question-wrapper-325774\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which of the following architectural features characterises 16th-century architecture in Britain?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. inward-facing design</li> <li>B. plain exteriors</li> <li>C. small windows</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e3b962e1-df97-46e0-a55c-6ebdf6886ad8\">symmetrical layouts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325775\" id=\"question-wrapper-325775\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>How did 17th-century British buildings come to be influenced by styles from continental Europe?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"cfd5a6e2-fee1-415e-951f-537314eb3e19\">Returning royalists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"c253a1d2-07ee-460b-bade-e02e8a75a89a\">adopted ideas they had encountered abroad<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>B. British craftsmen were trained by European builders.</li> <li>C. Charles II recruited foreign designers to replace British architects.</li> <li>D. Continental firms were hired to rebuild damaged British houses.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325776\" id=\"question-wrapper-325776\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"441e8cb2-4e6c-40c8-b8f3-f0af1fd794aa\">Craftsmen became less involved in construction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> as a result of</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the construction of the Crystal Palace.</li> <li>B. a return to earlier working methods.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"1b497149-1342-4fba-800d-780a0a5b7c4a\">the growth of factory-based manufacturing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>D. the demands of the Great Exhibition.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325777\" id=\"question-wrapper-325777\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why did so few notable Modern Movement buildings appear in Britain before the Second World War?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"9a8bd851-ff81-45d9-9f60-c80908ae2a95\">Most British architects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"32b31655-b6e6-4f1c-9f21-c61460cf8352\">remained committed to older styles and craft traditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Experimental buildings were too expensive for most clients.</li> <li>C. Modernist architects from abroad were unable to settle in Britain.</li> <li>D. Britain lacked the materials required for Modernist construction.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325778\" id=\"question-wrapper-325778\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"403543f6-da4b-459c-8755-af7327f7be7f\">the main practical reason for the design choices made after the Second World War<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. a wish to preserve traditional styles</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"aa317e37-87b6-424d-82c7-87bf9a4aeef3\">an urgent lack of homes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></li> <li>C. admiration for architects overseas</li> <li>D. the demands of rich clients</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>34-40</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325779\" id=\"question-wrapper-325779\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c6bfc5e8-e11d-45ba-8b0f-fa60d695bd5a\">The lack of Anglo-Saxon architecture that remains today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> is explained by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"5d139072-f19e-45e7-bd97-cc98f5170379\">builders' reliance on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> (34)_______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">wood</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325780\" id=\"question-wrapper-325780\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"119a6030-a4a9-479a-b651-f006c5417fe5\">Owners of 16th-century houses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, unlike their medieval predecessors, used their homes to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"e6eb42e3-6a60-4b21-9d7f-630826906ce9\">demonstrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> their (35)_______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">status and wealth</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325781\" id=\"question-wrapper-325781\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the 16th century, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"8986ab1a-9834-4e07-99bb-9bbf685a8821\">large windows<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> were fashionable, even though glass was an (36)_______ at the time.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">expensive commodity</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325782\" id=\"question-wrapper-325782\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Inigo Jones <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"3992118f-06f6-4c35-bc85-a068a5f342f1\">stood apart from his contemporaries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a67ee43c-0f16-48be-b608-fb5d4fce4e06\">his skilled use of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> (37)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"3ef996fa-290c-40c6-8d82-7e8c3a52cf2d\">features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">classical</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325783\" id=\"question-wrapper-325783\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"d83d8ce4-9edd-41e3-b365-17c337393db5\">William Morris first became influential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"c6772e05-ea76-45a7-ac83-cd5d867e5ea9\">through his making of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> (38)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"1eeb27db-d970-4566-8d37-9787ec477f1a\">by hand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">furniture and textiles</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325784\" id=\"question-wrapper-325784\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the early 20th century, architects like (39)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"67151013-eada-439f-9d8b-3a2551b1a346\">were still producing conservative designs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Edwin Lutyens</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325785\" id=\"question-wrapper-325785\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Before <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"9dde5c52-8217-4646-9de5-deef8f9f9166\">public bodies took on a leading role in British architecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"c3147b18-3fcc-4472-84f9-05ca883e8ea1\">the field had<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"a71557f9-7bb3-4d14-88aa-7046785d5dec\">for hundreds of years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"c3147b18-3fcc-4472-84f9-05ca883e8ea1\">been shaped mainly by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> (40)_______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">private individuals</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c2d8c95a-ff1f-41e6-9ea2-5adf120888cb","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Roman culture in Britain","passagePhrase":"Romano-British culture"},{"uid":"cf0c45ed-0be6-4475-a927-c1c3f5d9a41f","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"continued to influence British life","passagePhrase":"survived long"},{"uid":"06072fa2-e826-4df5-918d-38ffd9784d9b","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"after the Roman withdrawal","passagePhrase":"after the Roman withdrawal"},{"uid":"c6bfc5e8-e11d-45ba-8b0f-fa60d695bd5a","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"The lack of Anglo-Saxon architecture that remains today","passagePhrase":"little survives to bear witness to their achievements"},{"uid":"5d139072-f19e-45e7-bd97-cc98f5170379","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"builders' reliance on","passagePhrase":"the vast majority of Anglo-Saxon buildings were made of"},{"uid":"a22e8ecb-fb20-4105-8398-04f1f93941c0","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The overriding principle of medieval architecture","passagePhrase":"the underlying ethos of medieval architecture"},{"uid":"bdf54624-9019-431e-8582-d71483aced90","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"useful","passagePhrase":"fitness for purpose ... functional ... served their particular purpose ... for use"},{"uid":"119a6030-a4a9-479a-b651-f006c5417fe5","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Owners of 16th-century houses","passagePhrase":"the buildings of the 16th century ... domestic architecture"},{"uid":"e6eb42e3-6a60-4b21-9d7f-630826906ce9","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"demonstrate","passagePhrase":"display"},{"uid":"8986ab1a-9834-4e07-99bb-9bbf685a8821","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"large windows","passagePhrase":"the use of great expanses of glass"},{"uid":"e3b962e1-df97-46e0-a55c-6ebdf6886ad8","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"symmetrical layouts","passagePhrase":"balanced and symmetrical exteriors"},{"uid":"a67ee43c-0f16-48be-b608-fb5d4fce4e06","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"his skilled use of","passagePhrase":"confident handling of"},{"uid":"3ef996fa-290c-40c6-8d82-7e8c3a52cf2d","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"features","passagePhrase":"detail and proportion"},{"uid":"3992118f-06f6-4c35-bc85-a068a5f342f1","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"stood apart from his contemporaries","passagePhrase":"set him apart from all other architects of the period"},{"uid":"c253a1d2-07ee-460b-bade-e02e8a75a89a","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"adopted ideas they had encountered abroad","passagePhrase":"came into contact with French, Dutch and Italian architecture ... built themselves houses reflecting the latest European trends"},{"uid":"cfd5a6e2-fee1-415e-951f-537314eb3e19","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Returning royalists","passagePhrase":"royalists reclaimed their property"},{"uid":"1b497149-1342-4fba-800d-780a0a5b7c4a","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"the growth of factory-based manufacturing","passagePhrase":"Mass production"},{"uid":"441e8cb2-4e6c-40c8-b8f3-f0af1fd794aa","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Craftsmen became less involved in construction","passagePhrase":"the individual craftsman no longer had a major role in their creation"},{"uid":"1eeb27db-d970-4566-8d37-9787ec477f1a","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"by hand","passagePhrase":"hand-crafted"},{"uid":"d83d8ce4-9edd-41e3-b365-17c337393db5","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"William Morris first became influential","passagePhrase":"Morris's influence grew"},{"uid":"c6772e05-ea76-45a7-ac83-cd5d867e5ea9","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"through his making of","passagePhrase":"from the production of"},{"uid":"67151013-eada-439f-9d8b-3a2551b1a346 9a8bd851-ff81-45d9-9f60-c80908ae2a95","qNum":"32 39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"staid establishment"},{"uid":"9a8bd851-ff81-45d9-9f60-c80908ae2a95","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Most British architects","passagePhrase":"architects ... slightly batty architect-craftsmen"},{"uid":"32b31655-b6e6-4f1c-9f21-c61460cf8352 67151013-eada-439f-9d8b-3a2551b1a346","qNum":"32 39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"producing Neo-Georgian and Renaissance country houses"},{"uid":"32b31655-b6e6-4f1c-9f21-c61460cf8352","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"remained committed to older styles and craft traditions","passagePhrase":"still trying to turn the clock back ... spurning new technology"},{"uid":"403543f6-da4b-459c-8755-af7327f7be7f","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"the main practical reason for the design choices made after the Second World War","passagePhrase":"as reconstruction began ... there was"},{"uid":"403543f6-da4b-459c-8755-af7327f7be7f aa317e37-87b6-424d-82c7-87bf9a4aeef3","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a desperate need"},{"uid":"aa317e37-87b6-424d-82c7-87bf9a4aeef3","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"an urgent lack of homes","passagePhrase":"for cheap housing which could be produced quickly"},{"uid":"9dde5c52-8217-4646-9de5-deef8f9f9166","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"public bodies took on a leading role in British architecture","passagePhrase":"Local authorities ... became important patrons of architecture"},{"uid":"c3147b18-3fcc-4472-84f9-05ca883e8ea1","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"the field had ... been shaped mainly by","passagePhrase":"dominated the architectural scene"},{"uid":"a71557f9-7bb3-4d14-88aa-7046785d5dec","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"for hundreds of years","passagePhrase":"for centuries"},{"uid":"67151013-eada-439f-9d8b-3a2551b1a346","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"were still producing conservative designs","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_67":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions</span></b> <b><span>1-13</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Anxiety</span></b></p><p><span>Anxiety is a common experience that can be a useful motivator or even a lifesaver in situations that are objectively dangerous. However, when the anxiety is out of proportion to the danger inherent in a given situation, is persistent, and is markedly disabling, an anxiety disorder can develop.</span></p><p><span>Anxiety is an emotion that all people experience from time to time, and we do so for very good reasons. It has been built into us; we have inherited it from our evolutionary past because, in general, anxiety has a survival function. If there was a real danger for primitive man, then anxiety kicked in in an adaptive way. We freeze, we stop doing whatever we were doing, we devote all of our attention to the danger, and our bodies react with a big release of adrenaline, an increase in blood flow to the muscles, getting us ready to run as fast as we can or fight as fiercely as we can.</span></p><p><span>So <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f2ff34ce-51c3-408b-9222-8d82c5169bfe\">some anxiety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> is adaptive, not only for primitive man but in modern society as well. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f9bd1f79-26e6-4176-8442-9134f7ad6755\">helps us to focus on things when we have deadlines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, and if someone is driving too fast when we cross the road, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f9bd1f79-26e6-4176-8442-9134f7ad6755\">helps us to jump out of the way quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. So, there is nothing wrong with anxiety in general, and in fact, we would have difficulties if we did not experience it to some extent, but of course it can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"d99dfb1b-5619-486e-bab1-d8181d053a34\">become problematic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> if the danger is one that is imagined rather than real, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6e2eb772-a088-4203-8fbc-5582d55eb94a\">the danger is exaggerated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. In those cases, particularly if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6e2eb772-a088-4203-8fbc-5582d55eb94a\">the perceived danger is out of proportion to the real danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, and it is persistent and disabling, then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"d99dfb1b-5619-486e-bab1-d8181d053a34\">there is a risk of an anxiety disorder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"418baf33-e6b9-4aab-8a67-37f7fd1afae3\">About 17 per cent of the population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> will have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"aafecea6-f47a-4f84-bcad-cce0bcc85489\">an anxiety disorder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"fde05ace-8998-476b-bf18-48f7a888cb82\">at some stage in their lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Anxiety can be caused in a variety of different ways, but any mental disorder is always difficult to diagnose. Scientists are looking at what role genes play in the development of these disorders and are also investigating the effects of environmental factors, such as pollution, physical and psychological stress, and diet. Several parts of the brain are key actors in the production of fear and anxiety. Using brain imaging technology and neurochemical techniques, scientists have discovered that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"5e941504-8edb-4c67-b8a1-04a9f3fc2ecd\">the amygdala<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"929edd62-b880-4efa-ad70-a69f1b8e390f\">plays a significant role in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ad0ce012-0d93-4b1c-982d-6115af81bd3d\">most anxiety disorders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. By learning more about how the brain creates fear and anxiety, scientists may be able to devise better treatments for these disorders.</span></p><p><span>Anxiety disorders are a very costly problem for society. Some published figures show that, in the US, they cost $60 billion in one year in terms of lost productivity and the excessive medical investigations that many people with anxiety seek, often thinking they have a physical problem.</span></p><p><span>Given all of this, it is rather worrying that anxiety also has a rather low treatment-seeking rate. Only 10 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d81f9ef5-e046-4fcc-ba46-0721a0f50385\">per cent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"f41b2c0b-95c0-4b99-8f17-6ce89d1d83b7\">people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> with an anxiety disorder <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c5fc1545-a2b1-456f-8f87-e77f570c461d\">will seek treatment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. That seems to be largely because people do not realise there are effective treatments available. Most people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"a3440c9d-f6f9-445b-a694-83af10e1ce6d\">tend to think<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"f41b2c0b-95c0-4b99-8f17-6ce89d1d83b7\">have had it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> for most of their lives, so <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"a3440c9d-f6f9-445b-a694-83af10e1ce6d\">it is just<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> their personality and they cannot change their personality, and so they feel rather hopeless about it.</span></p><p><span>The first psychotherapy treatment that was shown to be effective was exposure therapy, which essentially encourages people, in a graded <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"fafd8357-5b26-4916-a051-8eab7992245a\">way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"0a2ce19f-f3c8-4b29-9d1d-b08e911e59e0\">go into their feared situations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and stay in them for as long as they can, building up <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f8ebe188-a185-4ed9-92cf-bcd05db53fc4\">their<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> confidence that way. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"2d8ea332-d95b-420d-b96a-7c04bdf74575\">Often<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, the therapist will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"3f63ef3b-4327-4512-8a2a-d5c53cf290fc\">accompany<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> the person to a feared situation to provide support and guidance. Group cognitive behaviour therapy has also been shown to be effective. This is a talking therapy that helps people to understand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"db9b7c75-f2ac-4292-a953-79b3000975cc\">the link between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> negative thoughts and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8b9e3d16-bb20-48e2-96b4-12d9f26dbb6a\">mood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, and how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c43ec5fb-1819-46fd-a43b-16301f5fcd1b\">altering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> their behaviour can enable them to manage anxiety and feel in control.</span></p><p><span>There are, of course, drugs that can help people with anxiety. Medication will not cure an anxiety disorder, but it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"06dbe167-c136-48b9-b889-3eb8bcf190af\">can keep it under control while the person receives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> psychotherapy. The principal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3efe296d-9205-41a1-aadc-5b1e58f93037\">medication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>s used for anxiety disorders are antidepressants, anti-anxiety drugs, and beta-blockers to control some of the physical symptoms. With proper treatment, many people with anxiety disorders can lead normal, fulfilling lives.</span></p><p><span>There is plenty of evidence that exercise can help with anxiety problems. When stress affects the brain, with its many nerve connections, the rest of the body feels the impact as well. Exercise and other physical activity <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"0952e5eb-4de2-4762-a2f4-6fcd080c70fb\">produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> endorphins, which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"f5e6a3a3-2e7e-4bc0-aad7-30d2737d4631\">chemicals in the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"c1ed9dd5-6634-4088-9d3e-13efaf7aff57\">act as natural painkillers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. In addition to this, getting physically tired can help people fall asleep faster and have deeper and more relaxing sleep. As many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"75905fda-2d86-4c82-a99d-bbc9ed21e439\">people suffering from anxiety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"fcd1b2e8-adba-4c71-9a88-2ac0be01c978\">have problems with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> insomnia, just the ability to get a good night's rest can change people's whole perspective.</span></p><p><span>Anxiety is a normal, but highly subjective, human emotion. While normal anxiety serves a beneficial and adaptive purpose, anxiety can also become the cause of tremendous suffering for millions of people. It is important that people recognise excessive anxiety in themselves as soon as possible, as treatment can be very successful and living untreated can be a misery.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending (</span><b><span>A – E</span></b><span>) below.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter (</span></i><i><b><span>A – E</span></b></i><i><span>) in answer boxes </span></i><i><b><span>1-3</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A. </span></b><span>prove <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f9bd1f79-26e6-4176-8442-9134f7ad6755\">useful in daily life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span>disappear without any professional help.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"d99dfb1b-5619-486e-bab1-d8181d053a34\">lead to unhelpful levels of anxiety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span>affect <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"418baf33-e6b9-4aab-8a67-37f7fd1afae3\">almost a fifth of the population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"fde05ace-8998-476b-bf18-48f7a888cb82\">at some point<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E. </span></b><span>be reduced through changes to what people eat.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325786\" id=\"question-wrapper-325786\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Experiencing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f2ff34ce-51c3-408b-9222-8d82c5169bfe\">small doses of anxiety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> can</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325787\" id=\"question-wrapper-325787\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6e2eb772-a088-4203-8fbc-5582d55eb94a\">Misjudging how dangerous a situation is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> can</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325788\" id=\"question-wrapper-325788\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"aafecea6-f47a-4f84-bcad-cce0bcc85489\">A severe problem with anxiety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> can</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below.</span></p><p><span>Write</span> <b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>4-6</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325789\" id=\"question-wrapper-325789\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"5e941504-8edb-4c67-b8a1-04a9f3fc2ecd\">area of the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> has research <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"929edd62-b880-4efa-ad70-a69f1b8e390f\">linked to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ad0ce012-0d93-4b1c-982d-6115af81bd3d\">most anxiety-related conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) amygdala</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325790\" id=\"question-wrapper-325790\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d81f9ef5-e046-4fcc-ba46-0721a0f50385\">share<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of people with an anxiety disorder <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c5fc1545-a2b1-456f-8f87-e77f570c461d\">does treatment actually reach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(only) 10% [OR] (only) 10 per( )cent</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325791\" id=\"question-wrapper-325791\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is anxiety <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"a3440c9d-f6f9-445b-a694-83af10e1ce6d\">often mistaken for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"f41b2c0b-95c0-4b99-8f17-6ce89d1d83b7\">the people who have it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(their) personality</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the table below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>7-13</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>Treatment for Anxiety</span></b></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Exposure Therapy</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Patients <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"0a2ce19f-f3c8-4b29-9d1d-b08e911e59e0\">face their fears<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in a (7)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"fafd8357-5b26-4916-a051-8eab7992245a\">fashion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"2d8ea332-d95b-420d-b96a-7c04bdf74575\">often<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"3f63ef3b-4327-4512-8a2a-d5c53cf290fc\">with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> their (8)________.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Group Cognitive Behaviour Therapy</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>A talking therapy.</span></p><p><span>It explores how:</span></p><p><span>- (9)________ can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"db9b7c75-f2ac-4292-a953-79b3000975cc\">influence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8b9e3d16-bb20-48e2-96b4-12d9f26dbb6a\">feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>- <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f8ebe188-a185-4ed9-92cf-bcd05db53fc4\">People’s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c43ec5fb-1819-46fd-a43b-16301f5fcd1b\">can be changed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3efe296d-9205-41a1-aadc-5b1e58f93037\">Drugs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span></span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"06dbe167-c136-48b9-b889-3eb8bcf190af\">Can be used alongside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)______.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Exercise</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"c1ed9dd5-6634-4088-9d3e-13efaf7aff57\">Pain-relieving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"f5e6a3a3-2e7e-4bc0-aad7-30d2737d4631\">brain chemicals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> known as (12)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"0952e5eb-4de2-4762-a2f4-6fcd080c70fb\">are released<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>It can also help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"75905fda-2d86-4c82-a99d-bbc9ed21e439\">sufferers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"fcd1b2e8-adba-4c71-9a88-2ac0be01c978\">struggle with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)______.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325792\" id=\"question-wrapper-325792\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">graded</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325793\" id=\"question-wrapper-325793\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">therapist</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325794\" id=\"question-wrapper-325794\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">negative thoughts</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325795\" id=\"question-wrapper-325795\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">behavio(u)r</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325796\" id=\"question-wrapper-325796\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">psychotherapy</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325797\" id=\"question-wrapper-325797\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">endorphins</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325798\" id=\"question-wrapper-325798\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">insomnia</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f2ff34ce-51c3-408b-9222-8d82c5169bfe","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"small doses of anxiety","passagePhrase":"some anxiety"},{"uid":"f9bd1f79-26e6-4176-8442-9134f7ad6755","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"useful in daily life","passagePhrase":"helps us to focus on things when we have deadlines ... helps us to jump out of the way quickly"},{"uid":"d99dfb1b-5619-486e-bab1-d8181d053a34","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"lead to unhelpful levels of anxiety","passagePhrase":"become problematic ... there is a risk of an anxiety disorder"},{"uid":"6e2eb772-a088-4203-8fbc-5582d55eb94a","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Misjudging how dangerous a situation is","passagePhrase":"the danger is exaggerated ... the perceived danger is out of proportion to the real danger"},{"uid":"418baf33-e6b9-4aab-8a67-37f7fd1afae3","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"almost a fifth of the population","passagePhrase":"About 17 per cent of the population"},{"uid":"aafecea6-f47a-4f84-bcad-cce0bcc85489","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"A severe problem with anxiety","passagePhrase":"an anxiety disorder"},{"uid":"fde05ace-8998-476b-bf18-48f7a888cb82","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"at some point","passagePhrase":"at some stage in their lives"},{"uid":"5e941504-8edb-4c67-b8a1-04a9f3fc2ecd","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"area of the brain","passagePhrase":"the amygdala"},{"uid":"929edd62-b880-4efa-ad70-a69f1b8e390f","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"linked to","passagePhrase":"plays a significant role in"},{"uid":"ad0ce012-0d93-4b1c-982d-6115af81bd3d","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"most anxiety-related conditions","passagePhrase":"most anxiety disorders"},{"uid":"d81f9ef5-e046-4fcc-ba46-0721a0f50385","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"share","passagePhrase":"per cent"},{"uid":"f41b2c0b-95c0-4b99-8f17-6ce89d1d83b7","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"the people who have it","passagePhrase":"people ... have had it"},{"uid":"c5fc1545-a2b1-456f-8f87-e77f570c461d","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"does treatment actually reach","passagePhrase":"will seek treatment"},{"uid":"a3440c9d-f6f9-445b-a694-83af10e1ce6d","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"often mistaken for","passagePhrase":"tend to think ... it is just"},{"uid":"fafd8357-5b26-4916-a051-8eab7992245a","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"fashion","passagePhrase":"way"},{"uid":"0a2ce19f-f3c8-4b29-9d1d-b08e911e59e0","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"face their fears","passagePhrase":"go into their feared situations"},{"uid":"f8ebe188-a185-4ed9-92cf-bcd05db53fc4","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"People’s","passagePhrase":"their"},{"uid":"2d8ea332-d95b-420d-b96a-7c04bdf74575","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"often","passagePhrase":"Often"},{"uid":"3f63ef3b-4327-4512-8a2a-d5c53cf290fc","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"with","passagePhrase":"accompany"},{"uid":"db9b7c75-f2ac-4292-a953-79b3000975cc","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"influence","passagePhrase":"the link between"},{"uid":"8b9e3d16-bb20-48e2-96b4-12d9f26dbb6a","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"feelings","passagePhrase":"mood"},{"uid":"c43ec5fb-1819-46fd-a43b-16301f5fcd1b","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"can be changed","passagePhrase":"altering"},{"uid":"06dbe167-c136-48b9-b889-3eb8bcf190af","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Can be used alongside","passagePhrase":"can keep it under control while the person receives"},{"uid":"3efe296d-9205-41a1-aadc-5b1e58f93037","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Drugs","passagePhrase":"medication"},{"uid":"0952e5eb-4de2-4762-a2f4-6fcd080c70fb","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"are released","passagePhrase":"produce"},{"uid":"f5e6a3a3-2e7e-4bc0-aad7-30d2737d4631","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"brain chemicals","passagePhrase":"chemicals in the brain"},{"uid":"c1ed9dd5-6634-4088-9d3e-13efaf7aff57","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Pain-relieving","passagePhrase":"act as natural painkillers"},{"uid":"75905fda-2d86-4c82-a99d-bbc9ed21e439","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"sufferers","passagePhrase":"people suffering from anxiety"},{"uid":"fcd1b2e8-adba-4c71-9a88-2ac0be01c978","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"struggle with","passagePhrase":"have problems with"}]},"reading_u2_68":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 14-26</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Comets</span></b></p><p><span>Comets <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3c60a746-779c-4d69-b96d-8dc87aa9a4b2\">arrive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to grace our skies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3c60a746-779c-4d69-b96d-8dc87aa9a4b2\">every year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>; some are new to the inner Solar System, and some are old friends on a repeat visit, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2b546d3c-38a8-46bb-9346-1e509c2437b7\">only comparatively rarely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> do they reach sufficient brightness to become apparent to the unaided eye.</span></p><p><span>Comets do not behave like any other object that we can observe in the night sky with the unaided eye. Stars remain fixed in the pattern of their constellations, and are regular in their motion through the sky from one night to the next, and from one month to the next. A planet follows a fairly slow but expected path. By comparison, a comet is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a56f60b6-0316-49ce-bfea-2f412c770836\">a totally different kind of event<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>: it will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"49aa4f4b-8ea6-401b-827c-5ca6187724e9\">appear unexpectedly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"49aa4f4b-8ea6-401b-827c-5ca6187724e9\">at any place in the sky<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, it will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"49aa4f4b-8ea6-401b-827c-5ca6187724e9\">change position from one night to the next<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> relative to the background of stars, and its path will be along <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"49aa4f4b-8ea6-401b-827c-5ca6187724e9\">a separate direction and path<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> across the sky from the planets and stars. During the few weeks or months that it is observable, it will first steadily increase in brightness from one night to the next, may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"1a455145-5e66-40ed-be5d-91276e10e6aa\">change its shape – growing bigger, longer or extra tails<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> – and then wane to invisibility, never to be seen again. Throughout history, comets have always <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ba57fd92-68fe-44ae-bf3f-b9cc0a6af4f3\">signified<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> evil, war and death, and they were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ba57fd92-68fe-44ae-bf3f-b9cc0a6af4f3\">supposed to leave<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> chaos and calamity in their wake. Indeed, plenty of past comets have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ba57fd92-68fe-44ae-bf3f-b9cc0a6af4f3\">blamed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> by the astrologers of their day for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ba57fd92-68fe-44ae-bf3f-b9cc0a6af4f3\">bringing or marking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> misfortune.</span></p><p><span>There have been many spectacular comets throughout history; on average we are visited by what is termed a ‘great comet’ about three times a century. This appellation is saved for those comets that reach exceptional brightness. The most famous of all comets is Halley’s comet; not that it is the most spectacular, but the study of its orbit by the English astronomer, Edmond Halley, was fundamental to pinning down the real nature of comets. During the 17th century, Halley was using Newton’s new mathematics of calculus to try to characterise the orbits of twenty-four comets from sightings recorded <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"22bb060d-3825-480c-bf56-074a78ebb912\">over the previous four centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. He realised that the orbital path of the bright comet recently seen in 1682 was very similar to that followed by two other comets – one observed in 1531 and one in 1607. All moved in a retrograde direction (i.e. opposite to the revolution of the planets round the Sun), following an elliptical orbit that had a similar orientation to the plane of the planets’ motion. The great comet of 1456 was also known to have travelled in a retrograde direction. Halley’s inspiration was to realise that these were four apparitions of the same comet, following a set path around the Sun, but which only became apparent to observers on Earth when its orbit returned the comet to the inner Solar System, after an interval of about 76 years. Although he did not live to see the success of his prediction of the comet’s return in 1758, when the comet was spotted on schedule, it was given his name. Subsequently, at least 23 previous appearances of Halley’s comet have been identified in historical records, the first known in a Chinese text dating to 240BC.</span></p><p><span>The nucleus is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"9a93cc30-4c8a-49b0-a510-08068ae41124\">the sole<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> solid <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"9a93cc30-4c8a-49b0-a510-08068ae41124\">component<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of a comet, and the only part that is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0bc8026a-3978-489d-90c8-69d9cc23f8fe\">always present<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. It resembles a dark-coloured iceberg; it is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"1b7561be-7581-4b1c-9c61-1380367d8881\">frozen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> chunk of ice ranging between 5 and 20 km in size, and with a somewhat irregular shape. The ice is not just water ice, but also contains <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"827268d0-b176-4917-9372-3a32e8e15087\">the ices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of frozen ammonia, carbon dioxide, methane and carbon monoxide. The ices are blackened, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"9ff8ea69-d746-456a-90f7-dc3c3fb00250\">as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"7e5d99a0-c9c4-4c13-a1ba-a8d19896837b\">contain small fragments of dust embedded within them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, and the whole nucleus is of a low density, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"9dcea04f-0e5d-46c2-86ee-d4e5ce795aa2\">suggesting it to be a partially porous body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"43476b56-98c4-441d-bddc-d412a017ee13\">When travelling along the outer reaches of its orbit, far from the Sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, the nucleus <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"1e54d83f-75ef-47ed-9213-31d62065acfe\">remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> frozen and dormant. As soon as its path brings the icy block into the inner Solar System, it begins to warm up, and its surface becomes active. The solid ice turns directly into gas, in a process known as ‘sublimation,’ and is liberated from the surface. The process is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"16635fed-f4db-4421-bb96-d1cd86f77154\">particularly apparent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> on the sunward <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"5374be18-1e9e-407d-ba42-1bb6ebc8bd8d\">flank<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of the nucleus, where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7f901ed0-d3ba-4382-a489-97086dd9d16e\">the gases escape as jets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, particularly through any fissures that open up in the structure. These jets also push out the particles of solid dust that are embedded in the ice.</span></p><p><span>The closer an orbit brings a nucleus to the Sun, the warmer it becomes, and the more spectacular tails are generated with them, sometimes being visible during the day. There are two types of comet tails: dust and gas ion. A dust tail contains small, solid particles that are about the same size as those found in cigarette smoke. This tail forms because sunlight pushes on these small particles, gently shoving them away from the comet’s nucleus. Because the pressure from sunlight is relatively weak, the dust particles end up forming a diffuse curved tail in the direction of the comet’s orbit. A gas ion tail forms when ultraviolet sunlight rips one or more electrons from gas atoms in the coma, making them into ions. The solar wind then carries these ions straight outward away from the Sun. As a comet heads away from the Sun, its tails dissipate, and the matter contained in its nucleus freezes into a rock-like material.</span></p><p><u><i><b><span>Glossary</span></b></i></u></p><p><i><span>Constellation – a recognised pattern of bodies in the sky.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Elliptical – oval-shaped.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Sublimation – the change of a substance from solid to gas without an intermediate liquid stage.</span></i></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the words in the box below.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>14-18</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>COMETS</span></b></p><p><span>Comets are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3c60a746-779c-4d69-b96d-8dc87aa9a4b2\">quite common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in our solar system, but they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2b546d3c-38a8-46bb-9346-1e509c2437b7\">seldom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> (14)________. Comets <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a56f60b6-0316-49ce-bfea-2f412c770836\">behave differently to other sky objects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>; they are seemingly quite (15)________ in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"49aa4f4b-8ea6-401b-827c-5ca6187724e9\">their movements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and (16)________. Comets have often been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ba57fd92-68fe-44ae-bf3f-b9cc0a6af4f3\">seen as predicting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> (17)________. Halley’s comet is probably the best known ‘great comet.’ Using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"22bb060d-3825-480c-bf56-074a78ebb912\">past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> (18)________, Edmond Halley was able to predict the comet’s next appearance, although it occurred after his death.</span></p><p><b><span>observations dangerous visible beautiful naming</span></b></p><p><b><span>disaster success unpredictable properties star</span></b></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325799\" id=\"question-wrapper-325799\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">visible</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325800\" id=\"question-wrapper-325800\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">unpredictable</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325801\" id=\"question-wrapper-325801\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">properties</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325802\" id=\"question-wrapper-325802\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">disaster</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325803\" id=\"question-wrapper-325803\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">observations</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>19-23</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325804\" id=\"question-wrapper-325804\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The nucleus of a comet is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"9a93cc30-4c8a-49b0-a510-08068ae41124\">the only part that is known to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> (19)_______ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0bc8026a-3978-489d-90c8-69d9cc23f8fe\">never disappear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">solid</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325805\" id=\"question-wrapper-325805\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"827268d0-b176-4917-9372-3a32e8e15087\">frozen components<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of a comet’s nucleus are (20)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"9ff8ea69-d746-456a-90f7-dc3c3fb00250\">due to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"7e5d99a0-c9c4-4c13-a1ba-a8d19896837b\">the presence of dust particles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">blackened</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325806\" id=\"question-wrapper-325806\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The nucleus of a comet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"9dcea04f-0e5d-46c2-86ee-d4e5ce795aa2\">has been theorised to be porous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> because of its (21)_______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(low) density</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325807\" id=\"question-wrapper-325807\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A comet’s nucleus <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"1e54d83f-75ef-47ed-9213-31d62065acfe\">is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"1b7561be-7581-4b1c-9c61-1380367d8881\">icy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and (22)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"43476b56-98c4-441d-bddc-d412a017ee13\">when it is far from the Sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">dormant</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325808\" id=\"question-wrapper-325808\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7f901ed0-d3ba-4382-a489-97086dd9d16e\">Gas jets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"16635fed-f4db-4421-bb96-d1cd86f77154\">most noticeable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> on the (23)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"5374be18-1e9e-407d-ba42-1bb6ebc8bd8d\">side<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of the nucleus.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">sunward</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Label the diagram below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.</span></i><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_3/reading/images/215db4f3a0f3c0ff8bf106989ea5486b9be37b389970346de8fc1623e0112940.jpg\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325809\" id=\"question-wrapper-325809\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">dust</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325810\" id=\"question-wrapper-325810\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">gas ion</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325811\" id=\"question-wrapper-325811\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">dissipate</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"3c60a746-779c-4d69-b96d-8dc87aa9a4b2","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"quite common","passagePhrase":"arrive ... every year"},{"uid":"2b546d3c-38a8-46bb-9346-1e509c2437b7","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"seldom","passagePhrase":"only comparatively rarely"},{"uid":"a56f60b6-0316-49ce-bfea-2f412c770836","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"behave differently to other sky objects","passagePhrase":"a totally different kind of event"},{"uid":"49aa4f4b-8ea6-401b-827c-5ca6187724e9","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"their movements","passagePhrase":"appear unexpectedly ... at any place in the sky ... change position from one night to the next ... a separate direction and path"},{"uid":"1a455145-5e66-40ed-be5d-91276e10e6aa","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"change its shape – growing bigger, longer or extra tails"},{"uid":"ba57fd92-68fe-44ae-bf3f-b9cc0a6af4f3","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"seen as predicting","passagePhrase":"signified ... supposed to leave ... blamed ... bringing or marking"},{"uid":"22bb060d-3825-480c-bf56-074a78ebb912","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"past","passagePhrase":"over the previous four centuries"},{"uid":"9a93cc30-4c8a-49b0-a510-08068ae41124","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"the only part that is known to be","passagePhrase":"the sole ... component"},{"uid":"0bc8026a-3978-489d-90c8-69d9cc23f8fe","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"never disappear","passagePhrase":"always present"},{"uid":"1b7561be-7581-4b1c-9c61-1380367d8881","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"icy","passagePhrase":"frozen"},{"uid":"827268d0-b176-4917-9372-3a32e8e15087","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"frozen components","passagePhrase":"the ices"},{"uid":"9ff8ea69-d746-456a-90f7-dc3c3fb00250","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"due to","passagePhrase":"as"},{"uid":"7e5d99a0-c9c4-4c13-a1ba-a8d19896837b","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the presence of dust particles","passagePhrase":"contain small fragments of dust embedded within them"},{"uid":"9dcea04f-0e5d-46c2-86ee-d4e5ce795aa2","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"has been theorised to be porous","passagePhrase":"suggesting it to be a partially porous body"},{"uid":"43476b56-98c4-441d-bddc-d412a017ee13","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"when it is far from the Sun","passagePhrase":"When travelling along the outer reaches of its orbit, far from the Sun"},{"uid":"1e54d83f-75ef-47ed-9213-31d62065acfe","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"is","passagePhrase":"remains"},{"uid":"16635fed-f4db-4421-bb96-d1cd86f77154","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"most noticeable","passagePhrase":"particularly apparent"},{"uid":"5374be18-1e9e-407d-ba42-1bb6ebc8bd8d","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"side","passagePhrase":"flank"},{"uid":"7f901ed0-d3ba-4382-a489-97086dd9d16e","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Gas jets","passagePhrase":"the gases escape as jets"}]},"reading_u2_69":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 27-40</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Homeschooling</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>Homeschooling is a method of education where children do not attend a traditional school. Instead, usually parents take over the responsibility for the education of their children, either by doing it all themselves or by using a company that specialises in providing homeschooling curricula and materials. Homeschooled children can excel in standardised testing, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f6b7d059-1842-46b8-b34d-537483b486df\">universities and colleges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"75f59f04-94a3-43a0-9cdf-d76279b2c862\">have no qualms about accepting them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"d604280d-faf4-49f7-a96c-e5030aa933ab\">Supporters also claim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that because they have been trained early on to be independent learners, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"a7de6772-7c29-4572-a8df-5da2e7579cec\">homeschooled individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"df7bd34c-e2b0-4a1a-bda7-d526b65c43d7\">grow up to become<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"c41f0082-0e6e-4ecf-a2bc-1b76c4ad55b6\">reliable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"aeef91a9-90da-45e8-89ea-6c587bf2e177\">resourceful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> adults.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>Homeschooling offers various benefits. Almost all <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"ce5ec0fc-6201-4fc9-a0d6-cb280cbc21fc\">homeschooling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> families say that homeschooling has played an essential role in bringing their family closer, as the time that parents spend teaching their children, and the time the children spend learning together, can foster a loving relationship in the family. Homeschooled children <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"24104935-90bd-496c-9d77-f65f5246f8d9\">do not have to worry about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"76d9f88c-1c5a-42ce-babb-0a5594cc6578\">bullying, peer pressure and spiteful competition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, so their self-esteem <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"24104935-90bd-496c-9d77-f65f5246f8d9\">does not have to suffer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> needlessly, and many parents with children who have been the target of bullying have resorted to homeschooling to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"24104935-90bd-496c-9d77-f65f5246f8d9\">protect their children from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the harmful effects of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"76d9f88c-1c5a-42ce-babb-0a5594cc6578\">harassment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Another key advantage of homeschooling is that parents and children no longer have to work their lives around homework and school hours. They usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f62cf726-3d26-4bca-b027-9898a90bb98f\">accomplish in a few hours each day what typically takes a week or more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> to complete in a classroom setting. Because they spend more time in hands-on learning, homeschooled children can do away with homework, which is what usually keeps public-schooled children up late at night. Additionally, families <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"2cab979d-4c25-4ef6-82a4-7664a37586cb\">can schedule off-season vacations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, go on field trips or visit museums, zoos and parks during the week as part of their learning experience. A more controversial benefit of homeschooling is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"7b38fc8c-46a3-4959-b7b9-1f10af625cce\">parents frequently have much more say in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> what is taught to their children, so that they can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"1e7e4491-bbcd-427f-9f02-9b5f4cee9394\">avoid subjects of which they disapprove<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>Homeschooling is, however, sharply criticised in some quarters. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"24b48f11-628f-4cd0-8a61-24ddfdf9d085\">A common criticism is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"900ee669-59b3-4382-86a8-b81b423f1227\">homeschooled children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d3fc788f-2718-4c7c-9093-6b07890feff4\">may not have as many opportunities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d8be3063-23b7-4f8e-b5c1-9a55e28f5b0f\">interact with other children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> as those who attend regular schools. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d8be3063-23b7-4f8e-b5c1-9a55e28f5b0f\">Forming bonds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and socialising with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"058e3be7-f72c-40f3-b8ef-18c6b5b55b1c\">children of his or her own age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> is important for a child's developmental health and the development of social skills. If homeschooled, children <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d3fc788f-2718-4c7c-9093-6b07890feff4\">may be deprived of the chance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d8be3063-23b7-4f8e-b5c1-9a55e28f5b0f\">form friendships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and may suffer socially. The lack of socialisation may affect them in later stages of life.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"cf375a7d-c21d-47ad-8bd5-78dcbda3c1a1\">Parents choosing to homeschool their children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> may also be faced with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"a21ba490-e3db-4ab0-9cc1-63854d11b281\">the common problem of time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. Parents <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"a21ba490-e3db-4ab0-9cc1-63854d11b281\">need to set aside time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> to make it work. The task of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"23094686-f203-44d5-b058-07fce5d543c1\">homeschooling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> a child is certainly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"a21ba490-e3db-4ab0-9cc1-63854d11b281\">not easy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, whether for working parents, single parents or stay-at-home parents. They have to take time to organise and prepare lessons, teach, give tests, and plan field trips. Also, in comparison to public schools, where education is free, homeschooling <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"26cf1f86-daa2-4840-91d1-c652eeb2c717\">can be costly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, as purchasing the newest curriculum and teaching tools <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"26cf1f86-daa2-4840-91d1-c652eeb2c717\">can be very expensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Parents may choose to use a pre-prepared paid homeschooling programme, but, in spite of the possible added benefits of such programmes, they may increase the cost of the child's education. There are also other costs to keep in mind, like project materials, stationery, books, computer software, and field trips.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>There is also the issue of the different relationships between parents and their children and teachers and their students. Public and private schools provide for many children a safe haven, in which they are both regarded and respected independently and individually. Family love is intense, and children need it to survive and thrive. It is also deeply contingent on the existence and nature of the family ties. The unconditional <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"c97c957e-740b-4064-908c-a9a437e8c8dc\">love children receive at home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> is actually <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"1d4ecb0d-04f4-4291-bc54-f7219caa49ae\">anything but unconditional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>: it is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"1d4ecb0d-04f4-4291-bc54-f7219caa49ae\">conditioned on the fact that they are their parents' children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. School, either public or private, ideally provides a welcome respite. Children are regarded and respected at school not because they are their parents' children, but because they are students. They are valued for traits and for status that are independent of their status as the parents' genetic or adoptive offspring. The ideal teacher cares about a child as an individual, a learner and an actively curious person. The teacher does not care about the child because the child is his or hers, and the child is regarded with respect equal to that shown to all the children in the class. In these ways, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"19081818-bf4a-475a-92e1-bca61fca9de0\">the school classroom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, and the relations within it, are ideally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c4adfb4f-1373-4c2d-87e2-736d02b783c8\">a model of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cb08296a-538c-4f82-9f50-c592ccdd162b\">some core aspects of citizenship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>A final criticism of homeschooling is that there is a public health risk. Children who attend public schools are required to have immunisations to begin classes. It is hard in many countries to ensure that mandatory immunisation is verified. Thus, unregulated homeschooling means that homeschooled children are effectively exempt from immunisation requirements. The children are more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"16246378-fe11-444f-ab38-6711d439492e\">susceptible to the diseases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> against which immunisation gives some protection, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"16246378-fe11-444f-ab38-6711d439492e\">others around them, particularly the elderly, are also consequently in danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>Even given these potential harms, there remain good reasons to permit homeschooling in plenty of circumstances. Parents often justifiably wish to shield their children from public schools that too often ill serve children who are at risk of bullying, or who are hurt by the culture of middle and high schools. Some children also have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d4c4d0bb-1f20-4c01-8afc-a991acf84b70\">special abilities or needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, or simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d4c4d0bb-1f20-4c01-8afc-a991acf84b70\">idiosyncratic learning styles or habits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, and many of these children can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"8ca1cb06-af22-4f5b-8f9a-f293993c70da\">best or even only be educated by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> those who know them best.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>The text on the previous pages has 7 paragraphs </span><b><span>A – G</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>27-33</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325812\" id=\"question-wrapper-325812\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"19081818-bf4a-475a-92e1-bca61fca9de0\">A regular school<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> can provide <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c4adfb4f-1373-4c2d-87e2-736d02b783c8\">an example of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cb08296a-538c-4f82-9f50-c592ccdd162b\">how people should treat one another as members of society<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325813\" id=\"question-wrapper-325813\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"24b48f11-628f-4cd0-8a61-24ddfdf9d085\">Critics say<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"900ee669-59b3-4382-86a8-b81b423f1227\">children taught at home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d3fc788f-2718-4c7c-9093-6b07890feff4\">miss out on chances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d8be3063-23b7-4f8e-b5c1-9a55e28f5b0f\">build relationships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"058e3be7-f72c-40f3-b8ef-18c6b5b55b1c\">others their own age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325814\" id=\"question-wrapper-325814\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Homeschooling can sometimes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"8ca1cb06-af22-4f5b-8f9a-f293993c70da\">better adapt to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> a child’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d4c4d0bb-1f20-4c01-8afc-a991acf84b70\">unusual learning needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325815\" id=\"question-wrapper-325815\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"a7de6772-7c29-4572-a8df-5da2e7579cec\">Homeschooled children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"d604280d-faf4-49f7-a96c-e5030aa933ab\">are believed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"df7bd34c-e2b0-4a1a-bda7-d526b65c43d7\">become<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"c41f0082-0e6e-4ecf-a2bc-1b76c4ad55b6\">dependable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"aeef91a9-90da-45e8-89ea-6c587bf2e177\">capable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"df7bd34c-e2b0-4a1a-bda7-d526b65c43d7\">in the future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325816\" id=\"question-wrapper-325816\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some parents may find that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"23094686-f203-44d5-b058-07fce5d543c1\">teaching their children at home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"26cf1f86-daa2-4840-91d1-c652eeb2c717\">puts a strain on their budget<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325817\" id=\"question-wrapper-325817\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Homeschooling has been accused of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"16246378-fe11-444f-ab38-6711d439492e\">spreading disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325818\" id=\"question-wrapper-325818\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Families who homeschool <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"2cab979d-4c25-4ef6-82a4-7664a37586cb\">have greater freedom over when they take vacations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>34-37</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325819\" id=\"question-wrapper-325819\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the passage suggest about homeschooled students applying to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f6b7d059-1842-46b8-b34d-537483b486df\">higher education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Institutions are generally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"75f59f04-94a3-43a0-9cdf-d76279b2c862\">willing to admit them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Institutions tend to doubt whether they are academically prepared.</li> <li>C. They must choose institutions that use a similar teaching approach.</li> <li>D. They usually have to provide extra proof of their academic ability.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325820\" id=\"question-wrapper-325820\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Compared with children in regular schools, homeschooled children may</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. face stronger pressure to compete with other children.</li> <li>B. experience lower self-esteem because they learn at home.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"24104935-90bd-496c-9d77-f65f5246f8d9\">be better protected from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"76d9f88c-1c5a-42ce-babb-0a5594cc6578\">hostile treatment by other children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> <li>D. feel greater pressure to gain the approval of their peers.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325821\" id=\"question-wrapper-325821\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to Paragraph B, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"ce5ec0fc-6201-4fc9-a0d6-cb280cbc21fc\">home-based education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. normally requires more study time than classroom learning.</li> <li>B. takes about the same amount of time as classroom learning.</li> <li>C. can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f62cf726-3d26-4bca-b027-9898a90bb98f\">allow the same work to be completed much faster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</li> <li>D. often requires children to continue studying late into the evening.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325822\" id=\"question-wrapper-325822\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Homeschooling can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"7b38fc8c-46a3-4959-b7b9-1f10af625cce\">give parents the option of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. removing formal assessment altogether.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"1e7e4491-bbcd-427f-9f02-9b5f4cee9394\">leaving out curriculum areas they object to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</li> <li>C. preventing their children from taking educational trips.</li> <li>D. teaching only the subjects they themselves are good at.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer of the text?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 38–40 on your answer sheet write:</span></p><p><b><span>YES</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NO </span></b><span>if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NOT GIVEN </span></b><span>if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325823\" id=\"question-wrapper-325823\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"a21ba490-e3db-4ab0-9cc1-63854d11b281\">Finding enough time can be a difficulty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"cf375a7d-c21d-47ad-8bd5-78dcbda3c1a1\">parents who educate their children at home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325824\" id=\"question-wrapper-325824\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"c97c957e-740b-4064-908c-a9a437e8c8dc\">Parents' love for their children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"1d4ecb0d-04f4-4291-bc54-f7219caa49ae\">unconditional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325825\" id=\"question-wrapper-325825\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Local health authorities should check whether homeschooled children have received the required vaccinations.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f6b7d059-1842-46b8-b34d-537483b486df","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"higher education","passagePhrase":"universities and colleges"},{"uid":"75f59f04-94a3-43a0-9cdf-d76279b2c862","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"willing to admit them","passagePhrase":"have no qualms about accepting them"},{"uid":"d604280d-faf4-49f7-a96c-e5030aa933ab","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"are believed to","passagePhrase":"Supporters also claim"},{"uid":"a7de6772-7c29-4572-a8df-5da2e7579cec","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Homeschooled children","passagePhrase":"homeschooled individuals"},{"uid":"df7bd34c-e2b0-4a1a-bda7-d526b65c43d7","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"become ... in the future","passagePhrase":"grow up to become"},{"uid":"c41f0082-0e6e-4ecf-a2bc-1b76c4ad55b6","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"dependable","passagePhrase":"reliable"},{"uid":"aeef91a9-90da-45e8-89ea-6c587bf2e177","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"capable","passagePhrase":"resourceful"},{"uid":"ce5ec0fc-6201-4fc9-a0d6-cb280cbc21fc","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"home-based education","passagePhrase":"homeschooling"},{"uid":"24104935-90bd-496c-9d77-f65f5246f8d9","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"be better protected from","passagePhrase":"do not have to worry about ... does not have to suffer ... protect their children from"},{"uid":"76d9f88c-1c5a-42ce-babb-0a5594cc6578","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"hostile treatment by other children","passagePhrase":"bullying, peer pressure and spiteful competition ... harassment"},{"uid":"f62cf726-3d26-4bca-b027-9898a90bb98f","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"allow the same work to be completed much faster","passagePhrase":"accomplish in a few hours each day what typically takes a week or more"},{"uid":"2cab979d-4c25-4ef6-82a4-7664a37586cb","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"have greater freedom over when they take vacations","passagePhrase":"can schedule off-season vacations"},{"uid":"7b38fc8c-46a3-4959-b7b9-1f10af625cce","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"give parents the option of","passagePhrase":"parents frequently have much more say in"},{"uid":"1e7e4491-bbcd-427f-9f02-9b5f4cee9394","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"leaving out curriculum areas they object to","passagePhrase":"avoid subjects of which they disapprove"},{"uid":"24b48f11-628f-4cd0-8a61-24ddfdf9d085","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Critics say","passagePhrase":"A common criticism is"},{"uid":"900ee669-59b3-4382-86a8-b81b423f1227","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"children taught at home","passagePhrase":"homeschooled children"},{"uid":"d3fc788f-2718-4c7c-9093-6b07890feff4","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"miss out on chances","passagePhrase":"may not have as many opportunities ... may be deprived of the chance"},{"uid":"d8be3063-23b7-4f8e-b5c1-9a55e28f5b0f","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"build relationships","passagePhrase":"interact with other children ... Forming bonds ... form friendships"},{"uid":"058e3be7-f72c-40f3-b8ef-18c6b5b55b1c","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"others their own age","passagePhrase":"children of his or her own age"},{"uid":"cf375a7d-c21d-47ad-8bd5-78dcbda3c1a1","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"parents who educate their children at home","passagePhrase":"Parents choosing to homeschool their children"},{"uid":"a21ba490-e3db-4ab0-9cc1-63854d11b281","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"Finding enough time can be a difficulty","passagePhrase":"the common problem of time ... need to set aside time ... not easy"},{"uid":"23094686-f203-44d5-b058-07fce5d543c1","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"teaching their children at home","passagePhrase":"homeschooling"},{"uid":"26cf1f86-daa2-4840-91d1-c652eeb2c717","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"puts a strain on their budget","passagePhrase":"can be costly ... can be very expensive"},{"uid":"c97c957e-740b-4064-908c-a9a437e8c8dc","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Parents' love for their children","passagePhrase":"love children receive at home"},{"uid":"19081818-bf4a-475a-92e1-bca61fca9de0","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"A regular school","passagePhrase":"the school classroom"},{"uid":"c4adfb4f-1373-4c2d-87e2-736d02b783c8","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"an example of","passagePhrase":"a model of"},{"uid":"cb08296a-538c-4f82-9f50-c592ccdd162b","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"how people should treat one another as members of society","passagePhrase":"some core aspects of citizenship"},{"uid":"16246378-fe11-444f-ab38-6711d439492e","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"spreading disease","passagePhrase":"susceptible to the diseases ... others around them, particularly the elderly, are also consequently in danger"},{"uid":"d4c4d0bb-1f20-4c01-8afc-a991acf84b70","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"unusual learning needs","passagePhrase":"special abilities or needs ... idiosyncratic learning styles or habits"},{"uid":"8ca1cb06-af22-4f5b-8f9a-f293993c70da","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"better adapt to","passagePhrase":"best or even only be educated by"}]},"reading_u2_70":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions</span></b> <b><span>1-13</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Pearl</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>Long known as the “Queen of Gems”, pearls possess a history and allure far beyond what today’s wearer may recognize. Throughout much of recorded history, a natural pearl necklace composed of matched spheres was a treasure of almost incomparable value; in fact, the most expensive jewelry in the world. Before the creation of cultured pearls in the early 1900s, natural pearls were so rare and expensive that they were reserved almost exclusively for the noble and very rich. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e8440ca1-5f66-4fb9-ada5-8916ad8211a8\">The ancient Egyptians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"537485cf-5e56-472e-94bc-ecc2b1b1f8b3\">particularly fond of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> their pearls. Many Egyptian <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"b21b207f-436c-45ea-bd6e-6f9ce97c1930\">leaders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"537485cf-5e56-472e-94bc-ecc2b1b1f8b3\">treasured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> pearls so much that they <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"e054abd4-f279-4e29-97c1-e2de3c720f40\">were often </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3 5\" data-uid=\"90c8cca9-f9fb-4dbb-b9e2-91383706c907 e054abd4-f279-4e29-97c1-e2de3c720f40\">buried</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"90c8cca9-f9fb-4dbb-b9e2-91383706c907\"> along with </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3 5\" data-uid=\"90c8cca9-f9fb-4dbb-b9e2-91383706c907 f408322a-4ad9-4a8a-b334-03deb01b0ec4\">their cherished pearl collection</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e8440ca1-5f66-4fb9-ada5-8916ad8211a8\">the Orient and Persian Empire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, pearls were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"90c8cca9-f9fb-4dbb-b9e2-91383706c907\">ground into costly powders to cure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> anything from heart disease to epilepsy, with possible aphrodisiac uses as well. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e8440ca1-5f66-4fb9-ada5-8916ad8211a8\">China’s long recorded history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> also provides ample evidence of the importance of pearls.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>Pearls usually fall into three categories—natural pearls, cultured pearls and simulated pearls. A natural pearl forms when an irritant, such as a piece of sand, works its way into a particular species of oyster, mussel, or clam. As a defense mechanism, the mollusk secretes a fluid to coat the irritant. Layer upon layer of this coating is deposited on the irritant until a lustrous pearl is formed. A cultured pearl undergoes the same process. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"071070a3-ec11-4989-8c5f-5fdfb7aca82a\">The only difference between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> natural pearls and cultured pearls is that the irritant is a surgically implanted bead or piece of shell called Mother of Pearl. Often, these shells are ground oyster shells that are worth significant amounts of money in their own right as irritant-catalysts for quality pearls. The resulting core is much larger than in a natural pearl. Imitation pearls are a different story altogether. In most cases, a glass bead is dipped into a solution made from fish scales. This coating is thin and may eventually wear off. One can usually tell an imitation by biting on it. The island of Mallorca in Spain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"6ddda0c4-cc49-4f93-8efc-9b2b9a5118bd\">is known for its imitation pearl industry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>Regardless of the method used to acquire a pearl, the process usually takes several years. Mussels must reach a mature age, which can take up to 3 years, and then be implanted or naturally receive an irritant. Once the irritant is in place, it can take up to another 3 years for the pearl to reach its full size. Often, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"bb4fd8b6-8f74-4cd4-8f9d-eaa1d4f9633e\">the irritant may be rejected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, the pearl will terribly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"bb4fd8b6-8f74-4cd4-8f9d-eaa1d4f9633e\">misshapen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, or the oyster may simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"bb4fd8b6-8f74-4cd4-8f9d-eaa1d4f9633e\">die from disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> or countless other <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"bb4fd8b6-8f74-4cd4-8f9d-eaa1d4f9633e\">complications<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. By <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"59b98855-79ae-4c4e-ab6a-f10d7af1b77a\">the end of a 5 to 10 year cycle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, only 50% of the oysters will have survived. And of the pearls produced, only approximately 5% are of a quality substantial enough for top jewelry makers.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>How can untrained eyes determine a pearl’s worth? Luster and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"fa18ae33-b45d-4aac-bb2d-97828c2a5741\">size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> are generally considered the two main factors to look for. Luster, for instance, depends on the fineness and evenness of the layers. The deeper the glow, the more perfect the shape and surface, the more valuable they are. Size, on the other hand, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"daae94d4-7768-4868-9b0e-7ce53c863afd\">has to do with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"d44a999c-53aa-4c31-b835-6f105d92829c\">the age of the oyster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> that created the pearl (the more mature oysters produce larger pearls) and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"d44a999c-53aa-4c31-b835-6f105d92829c\">the location<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in which the pearl was cultured. The South Sea waters of Australia <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4f02f171-2423-4271-bfe5-7cddd52d6194\">tend to produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"aeddb723-0a3d-4202-965d-3f1fa9a4fd54\">the larger pearls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9ee15853-fb32-4381-86c6-804585f9dd37\">probably because<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"713f898b-ff5a-44ee-96bd-c99cd093e1f3\">the water along the coastline is supplied with rich nutrients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> from the ocean floor. Also, the mussel species common to the area seems to have a predilection for producing comparatively large pearls.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>In general, cultured pearls are less valuable than natural pearls, whereas <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"f6156f76-a3ce-4c5d-b1f1-7015d186d0a2\">imitation pearls almost have no value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. One way that jewelers can determine whether a pearl is cultured or natural is to have a gem lab perform an X-ray of the pearl. If the X-ray reveals a nucleus, the pearl is likely a bead nucleated saltwater pearl. If no nucleus is present, but irregular and small dark inner spots indicating a cavity are visible, combined with concentric rings of organic substance, the pearl is likely a cultured freshwater. Among cultured pearls, Akoya <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"d03bf946-76d2-4c5c-9171-1ed5a96b3ce3\">pearls from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> Japan are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"7fe69d80-d1b2-47c8-9856-e82bc9882624\">some of the most lustrous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. Although imitation pearls look the part, they do not have the same weight or smoothness as real pearls, and their luster will also dim greatly.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"d66c721d-2217-4cb1-bcd3-df1458be7209\">Historically<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"5bbefe1d-ea05-4d41-93ee-634caa97351d\">the world’s best pearls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> came from the Persian Gulf, especially around <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"d09f121e-c2a8-46f4-8ec8-af41bb5e0d60\">what is now<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> Bahrain. The pearls of the Persian Gulf were naturally created and collected by breath-hold divers. Unfortunately, the natural pearl industry of the Persian Gulf ended abruptly in the early 1930s with the discovery of large deposits of oil. The water pollution resulting from spilled oil and indiscriminate over-fishing of oysters essentially ruined the pristine waters of the Gulf once producing pearls. Still, Bahrain remains one of the foremost trading centers for high-quality pearls. In fact, cultured pearls are banned from the Bahrain pearl market, in an effort to preserve the location’s heritage. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"304aa92b-2e4a-45ea-9896-ff0cd35eebe7\">Nowadays<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"4cb4f781-0aa9-48d9-b098-8e48f656fe16\">the largest stock of natural pearls </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f89c7b9c-173b-4fe8-bedf-ac9b3102afd7\">probably<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"4cb4f781-0aa9-48d9-b098-8e48f656fe16\"> resides in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> India. Ironically, much of India’s stock of natural pearls came originally from Bahrain. Unlike Bahrain, which has essentially lost its pearl resource, traditional pearl fishing is still practiced on a small scale in India.</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>Pearls also come in many colours. The most popular colours are white, cream, and pink. Silver, black, and gold are also gaining increasing interest. In fact, a deep lustrous black pearl is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a2256577-d56d-4516-83bf-d817da56f82e\">one of the rarest finds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in the pearling industry, usually only being found in the South Sea near Australia. Thus, they can be one of the more costly items. Nowadays, pearls predominantly come from Japan, Australia, Indonesia, Myanmar, China, India, the Philippines, and Tahiti. Japan, however, controls roughly 80% of the world pearl market, with Australia and China coming in second and third, respectively.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325826\" id=\"question-wrapper-325826\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"bb4fd8b6-8f74-4cd4-8f9d-eaa1d4f9633e\">difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in the cultivation process</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325827\" id=\"question-wrapper-325827\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"d44a999c-53aa-4c31-b835-6f105d92829c\">factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"daae94d4-7768-4868-9b0e-7ce53c863afd\">affecting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"fa18ae33-b45d-4aac-bb2d-97828c2a5741\">the size of pearls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325828\" id=\"question-wrapper-325828\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"90c8cca9-f9fb-4dbb-b9e2-91383706c907\">how pearls were used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"537485cf-5e56-472e-94bc-ecc2b1b1f8b3\">regarded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e8440ca1-5f66-4fb9-ada5-8916ad8211a8\">early civilizations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325829\" id=\"question-wrapper-325829\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>how the formation of a cultured pearl <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"071070a3-ec11-4989-8c5f-5fdfb7aca82a\">differs from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> that of a natural one</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A–K.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter in boxes 5–10 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Pearls: origins and sources</span></b></p><p><span>Pearls have been valued for thousands of years, and their story spans several continents. Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"b21b207f-436c-45ea-bd6e-6f9ce97c1930\">rulers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in (5)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"e054abd4-f279-4e29-97c1-e2de3c720f40\">were laid to rest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> together with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"f408322a-4ad9-4a8a-b334-03deb01b0ec4\">the pearls they collected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. There are essentially three types of pearls: natural, cultured and imitation. Natural and cultured pearls share a similar growing process, while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"6ddda0c4-cc49-4f93-8efc-9b2b9a5118bd\">imitation pearls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> are made in a different way; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"6ddda0c4-cc49-4f93-8efc-9b2b9a5118bd\">producing them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"6ddda0c4-cc49-4f93-8efc-9b2b9a5118bd\">is a recognized local specialty in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (6)________. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"aeddb723-0a3d-4202-965d-3f1fa9a4fd54\">Pearls of exceptional size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4f02f171-2423-4271-bfe5-7cddd52d6194\">usually come from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> (7)________, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9ee15853-fb32-4381-86c6-804585f9dd37\">thanks to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"713f898b-ff5a-44ee-96bd-c99cd093e1f3\">nutrient-rich water near its shores<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, while (8)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"d03bf946-76d2-4c5c-9171-1ed5a96b3ce3\">is the source of pearls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"7fe69d80-d1b2-47c8-9856-e82bc9882624\">a particularly brilliant sheen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"d66c721d-2217-4cb1-bcd3-df1458be7209\">In the past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"5bbefe1d-ea05-4d41-93ee-634caa97351d\">the finest pearls in the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> came from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"d09f121e-c2a8-46f4-8ec8-af41bb5e0d60\">the area now known as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)________. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"304aa92b-2e4a-45ea-9896-ff0cd35eebe7\">At present<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, (10)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f89c7b9c-173b-4fe8-bedf-ac9b3102afd7\">is thought to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"4cb4f781-0aa9-48d9-b098-8e48f656fe16\">have the greatest surviving reserve of natural pearls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> Tahiti </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Philippines </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> Australia</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> Bahrain </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> China </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><b><span>F.</span></b><span> Japan</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><b><span>G.</span></b><span> India </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><b><span>H.</span></b><span> Egypt </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><b><span>I.</span></b><span> Myanmar</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"J\"><b><span>J. </span></b><span>Persia </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"K\"><b><span>K. </span></b><span>Mallorca</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325830\" id=\"question-wrapper-325830\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325831\" id=\"question-wrapper-325831\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">K</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325832\" id=\"question-wrapper-325832\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325833\" id=\"question-wrapper-325833\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325834\" id=\"question-wrapper-325834\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325835\" id=\"question-wrapper-325835\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes </span></i><i><b><span>11-13</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet, write</span></i></p><p><b><span>TRUE</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><b><span>FALSE</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><b><span>NOT</span></b> <b><span>GIVEN</span></b><span> if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325836\" id=\"question-wrapper-325836\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Roughly half of the oysters used in pearl production do not live through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"59b98855-79ae-4c4e-ab6a-f10d7af1b77a\">the full growing cycle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325837\" id=\"question-wrapper-325837\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Imitation pearls are usually <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"f6156f76-a3ce-4c5d-b1f1-7015d186d0a2\">the same price as natural ones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325838\" id=\"question-wrapper-325838\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Because of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a2256577-d56d-4516-83bf-d817da56f82e\">their rarity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, black pearls are now being produced artificially in large numbers.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e8440ca1-5f66-4fb9-ada5-8916ad8211a8","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"early civilizations","passagePhrase":"The ancient Egyptians ... the Orient and Persian Empire ... China’s long recorded history"},{"uid":"537485cf-5e56-472e-94bc-ecc2b1b1f8b3","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"regarded","passagePhrase":"particularly fond of ... treasured"},{"uid":"b21b207f-436c-45ea-bd6e-6f9ce97c1930","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"rulers","passagePhrase":"leaders"},{"uid":"e054abd4-f279-4e29-97c1-e2de3c720f40","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"were laid to rest","passagePhrase":"were often"},{"uid":"90c8cca9-f9fb-4dbb-b9e2-91383706c907 e054abd4-f279-4e29-97c1-e2de3c720f40","qNum":"3 5","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"buried"},{"uid":"90c8cca9-f9fb-4dbb-b9e2-91383706c907","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"how pearls were used","passagePhrase":"along with ... ground into costly powders to cure"},{"uid":"90c8cca9-f9fb-4dbb-b9e2-91383706c907 f408322a-4ad9-4a8a-b334-03deb01b0ec4","qNum":"3 5","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"their cherished pearl collection"},{"uid":"071070a3-ec11-4989-8c5f-5fdfb7aca82a","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"differs from","passagePhrase":"The only difference between"},{"uid":"6ddda0c4-cc49-4f93-8efc-9b2b9a5118bd","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"imitation pearls ... producing them ... is a recognized local specialty in","passagePhrase":"is known for its imitation pearl industry"},{"uid":"bb4fd8b6-8f74-4cd4-8f9d-eaa1d4f9633e","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"difficulties","passagePhrase":"the irritant may be rejected ... misshapen ... die from disease ... complications"},{"uid":"59b98855-79ae-4c4e-ab6a-f10d7af1b77a","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"the full growing cycle","passagePhrase":"the end of a 5 to 10 year cycle"},{"uid":"fa18ae33-b45d-4aac-bb2d-97828c2a5741","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"the size of pearls","passagePhrase":"size"},{"uid":"daae94d4-7768-4868-9b0e-7ce53c863afd","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"affecting","passagePhrase":"has to do with"},{"uid":"d44a999c-53aa-4c31-b835-6f105d92829c","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"factors","passagePhrase":"the age of the oyster ... the location"},{"uid":"4f02f171-2423-4271-bfe5-7cddd52d6194","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"usually come from","passagePhrase":"tend to produce"},{"uid":"aeddb723-0a3d-4202-965d-3f1fa9a4fd54","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Pearls of exceptional size","passagePhrase":"the larger pearls"},{"uid":"9ee15853-fb32-4381-86c6-804585f9dd37","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"thanks to","passagePhrase":"probably because"},{"uid":"713f898b-ff5a-44ee-96bd-c99cd093e1f3","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"nutrient-rich water near its shores","passagePhrase":"the water along the coastline is supplied with rich nutrients"},{"uid":"d03bf946-76d2-4c5c-9171-1ed5a96b3ce3","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"is the source of pearls","passagePhrase":"pearls from"},{"uid":"7fe69d80-d1b2-47c8-9856-e82bc9882624","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"a particularly brilliant sheen","passagePhrase":"some of the most lustrous"},{"uid":"d66c721d-2217-4cb1-bcd3-df1458be7209","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"In the past","passagePhrase":"Historically"},{"uid":"5bbefe1d-ea05-4d41-93ee-634caa97351d","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"the finest pearls in the world","passagePhrase":"the world’s best pearls"},{"uid":"d09f121e-c2a8-46f4-8ec8-af41bb5e0d60","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"the area now known as","passagePhrase":"what is now"},{"uid":"304aa92b-2e4a-45ea-9896-ff0cd35eebe7","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"At present","passagePhrase":"Nowadays"},{"uid":"4cb4f781-0aa9-48d9-b098-8e48f656fe16","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"have the greatest surviving reserve of natural pearls","passagePhrase":"the largest stock of natural pearls ... resides in"},{"uid":"f89c7b9c-173b-4fe8-bedf-ac9b3102afd7","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"is thought to","passagePhrase":"probably"},{"uid":"a2256577-d56d-4516-83bf-d817da56f82e","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"their rarity","passagePhrase":"one of the rarest finds"},{"uid":"f408322a-4ad9-4a8a-b334-03deb01b0ec4","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"the pearls they collected","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_71":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 14-26</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Being Left-handed in a Right-handed World</span></b></p><p><i><span>The world is designed for right-handed people. Why does a tenth of the population prefer the left?</span></i></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"b64188f8-e40b-4a4e-89bb-e4b100d19f12\">The probability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"97522f5e-11af-4adc-8d1b-caa96827af39\">two right-handed people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> would have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9450512a-2a49-4062-a74a-3a156c042aa2\">a left-handed child<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> is only about 9.5 percent. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"b64188f8-e40b-4a4e-89bb-e4b100d19f12\">The chance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> rises to 19.5 percent if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"97522f5e-11af-4adc-8d1b-caa96827af39\">one parent is a lefty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and to 26 percent if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"97522f5e-11af-4adc-8d1b-caa96827af39\">both parents are left-handed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. The preference, however, could also stem from an infant's imitation of their parents. To test genetic influence, starting in the 1970s, British biologist Marian Annett of the University of Leicester hypothesized that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"469dc730-1c57-4caf-8aa6-dcc420bce9dd\">no single gene determines handedness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Rather, during fetal development, a certain molecular factor helps to strengthen the brain's left hemisphere, which increases the probability that the right hand will be dominant, because the left side of the brain controls the right side of the body, and vice versa. Among the minority of people who lack this factor, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"b5de6cf3-55e0-4f9a-bbbd-33c5635cc972\">handedness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> develops entirely by chance. Research conducted on twins complicates the theory, however. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"df18122b-2b92-4b15-9882-df502b80ae36\">One in five sets of identical twins involves one right-handed and one left-handed person<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a4b9be2f-3cef-491a-833a-f2eca866c554\">despite the fact that their genetic material is the same<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a4b9be2f-3cef-491a-833a-f2eca866c554\">Genes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, therefore, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a4b9be2f-3cef-491a-833a-f2eca866c554\">are not solely responsible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> for handedness.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Genetic theory is also undermined by results from Peter Hepper and his team at Queen's University in Belfast, Northern Ireland. In 2004 the psychologists used ultrasound to show that by the 15th week of pregnancy, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"09eef882-7336-4101-a4b0-5702e91a3fb6\">fetuses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> already have a preference as to which thumb they suck. In most cases, the preference continued after birth. At 15 weeks, though, the brain does not yet have control over the body's limbs. Hepper speculates that fetuses tend to prefer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"0f907f41-0bb6-443c-a074-3d2bc4ed93c4\">whichever side of the body is developing more quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"09eef882-7336-4101-a4b0-5702e91a3fb6\">their movements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, in turn, influence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"47108180-cd33-49d8-9e40-787a4741f54a\">the brain's development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Whether this early preference is temporary or holds up throughout development and infancy is unknown. Genetic predetermination is also contradicted by the widespread observation that children do not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"a2109ac8-bc59-4b95-a957-361eb3583413\">settle on either their right or left hand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> until they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"cbbf8066-7554-461e-bf6a-a66eadf985b1\">two or three years old<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> But even if these correlations were true, they did not explain what actually causes left-handedness. Furthermore, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"9548d62f-3abb-4a59-857f-ba35687b8438\">specialization on either side of the body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> is common among animals. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"42cb5a54-858f-4bb9-a5cb-2dcb93dfd8ca\">Cats will favor one paw over another<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> when fishing toys out from under the couch. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"42cb5a54-858f-4bb9-a5cb-2dcb93dfd8ca\">Horses stomp more frequently with one hoof<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> than the other. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"42cb5a54-858f-4bb9-a5cb-2dcb93dfd8ca\">Certain crabs gesture predominantly with the left or right claw<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. In evolutionary terms, focusing power and dexterity in one limb is more efficient than having to train two, four or even eight limbs equally. Yet for most animals, the preference for one side or the other is seemingly random. The overwhelming dominance of the right hand is associated only with humans. That fact directs attention toward the brain's two hemispheres and perhaps toward language.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> Interest in hemispheres dates back to at least 1836. That year, at a medical conference, French physician Marc Dax <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7374f437-ba89-4fe7-bbc8-f6e3774b79cb\">reported on an unusual commonality among his patients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. During his many years as a country doctor, Dax <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7374f437-ba89-4fe7-bbc8-f6e3774b79cb\">had encountered more than 40 men and women for whom speech was difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, the result of some kind of brain damage. What was unique was that every individual had suffered damage to the left side of the brain. At the conference, Dax <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"84f510d1-ce94-43ec-bc7b-75f4792c5e55\">elaborated on his theory, stating that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"eaeecf9a-0d39-48ad-bb5d-9bac885c53d8\">each half of the brain was responsible for certain functions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> and that the left hemisphere controlled speech. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"f0323233-fd14-4c35-8fd3-02a4bea2fa80\">Other experts showed little interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in the Frenchman's ideas. Over time, however, scientists found more and more evidence of people experiencing speech difficulties following injury to the left brain. Patients with damage to the right hemisphere most often displayed disruptions in perception or concentration. Major advances in understanding the brain's asymmetry were made in the 1960s as a result of so-called split-brain surgery, developed to help patients with epilepsy. During this operation, doctors severed the corpus callosum—the nerve bundle that connects the two hemispheres. The surgical cut also stopped almost all normal communication between the two hemispheres, which offered researchers the opportunity to investigate each side's activity.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> In 1949, neurosurgeon Juhn Wada devised the first test to provide access to the brain's functional organization of language. By injecting an anesthetic into the right or left carotid artery, Wada temporarily paralyzed one side of a healthy brain, enabling him to study the other side's capabilities more closely. Based on this approach, Brenda Milner and the late Theodore Rasmussen of the Montreal Neurological Institute published a major study in 1975 that confirmed the theory the country doctor Dax had formulated nearly 140 years earlier: in 96 percent of right-handed people, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"f93d993e-7f92-481d-b89c-20069e8c2f31\">language is processed much more intensely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in the left hemisphere. The correlation is not as clear in lefties, however. For two thirds of them, the left hemisphere is still the most active language processor, but for the remaining third, either the right side is dominant or both sides work equally, controlling different language functions. That last statistic has slowed acceptance of the notion that the predominance of right-handedness is driven by left-hemisphere dominance in language processing. It is not at all clear why language control should somehow have dragged the control of body movement with it.</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> Some experts think one reason the left hemisphere reigns over language is that the organs of speech processing—the larynx and tongue—are positioned on the body's symmetry axis. Because these structures were centered, it may have been unclear, in evolutionary terms, which side of the brain should control them, and it seems unlikely that shared operation would result in smooth motor activity. Language and handedness could have developed preferentially for very different reasons as well. For example, some researchers, including evolutionary psychologist Michael C. Corballis of the University of Auckland in New Zealand, think that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"ee5051db-a0b9-490d-9535-3c7233af0278\">the origin of human speech lies in gestures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. Gestures predated words and helped language emerge. If the left hemisphere began to dominate speech, it would have dominated gestures too, and because the left brain controls the right side of the body, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5d9881ec-0b49-4eb4-aba4-a24ed19ab212\">the right hand developed more strongly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> Perhaps we will know more soon. In the meantime, we can revel in what, if any, differences handedness brings to our human talents. Popular wisdom says right-handed, left-brained people excel at logical, analytical thinking. Left-handed, right-brained individuals are thought to possess more creative skills and may be better at combining the functional features emergent in both sides of the brain. Yet some neuroscientists see such claims as pure speculation. Few scientists are ready to claim that left-handedness means greater creative potential. Yet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"0a38f7fb-7692-4a34-89ef-60f71e6a6020\">lefties are prevalent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> among <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"b61968e7-d5ab-4e83-b280-71b4ba814026\">artists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"b61968e7-d5ab-4e83-b280-71b4ba814026\">composers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"b61968e7-d5ab-4e83-b280-71b4ba814026\">generally acknowledged great political thinkers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Possibly, if these individuals are among the lefties whose language abilities are evenly distributed between hemispheres, the intense interplay required could lead to unusual mental capabilities. Or perhaps some lefties become highly creative simply because they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8b001dad-5ae3-42a2-89f0-35c3b6a98465\">must be more clever to get by in our right-handed world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8b001dad-5ae3-42a2-89f0-35c3b6a98465\">This battle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, which begins during <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"68879f43-8b00-4a77-b863-9d554c4e1458\">the very early stages of childhood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, may lay the groundwork for exceptional achievements.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A–G.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325839\" id=\"question-wrapper-325839\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"42cb5a54-858f-4bb9-a5cb-2dcb93dfd8ca\">Examples<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"9548d62f-3abb-4a59-857f-ba35687b8438\">side preference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in animals</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325840\" id=\"question-wrapper-325840\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>How <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"97522f5e-11af-4adc-8d1b-caa96827af39\">the parents’ dominant hands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> affect <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"b64188f8-e40b-4a4e-89bb-e4b100d19f12\">the likelihood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9450512a-2a49-4062-a74a-3a156c042aa2\">their child will become left-handed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325841\" id=\"question-wrapper-325841\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"cbbf8066-7554-461e-bf6a-a66eadf985b1\">The stage of childhood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> at which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"a2109ac8-bc59-4b95-a957-361eb3583413\">a dominant hand usually becomes established<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325842\" id=\"question-wrapper-325842\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"b61968e7-d5ab-4e83-b280-71b4ba814026\">Fields<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"0a38f7fb-7692-4a34-89ef-60f71e6a6020\">left-handed people appear relatively common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325843\" id=\"question-wrapper-325843\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7374f437-ba89-4fe7-bbc8-f6e3774b79cb\">Clinical observations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"84f510d1-ce94-43ec-bc7b-75f4792c5e55\">led to the proposal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"eaeecf9a-0d39-48ad-bb5d-9bac885c53d8\">the two halves of the brain do different things<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following researchers (Questions 19–22) and the list of ideas below.</span></p><p><span>Match each researcher with the correct idea, A–F.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 19–22 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Ideas</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"ee5051db-a0b9-490d-9535-3c7233af0278\">The gestural origins of speech<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> may have contributed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5d9881ec-0b49-4eb4-aba4-a24ed19ab212\">stronger use of one hand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"469dc730-1c57-4caf-8aa6-dcc420bce9dd\">Hand dominance cannot be determined by one gene alone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Each hemisphere of the brain is in charge of different body functions.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"f93d993e-7f92-481d-b89c-20069e8c2f31\">Language processing is mainly centered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in the left hemisphere of the brain.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Temporarily disabling one hemisphere made it possible to study the other.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"0f907f41-0bb6-443c-a074-3d2bc4ed93c4\">Uneven physical development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> may influence both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"09eef882-7336-4101-a4b0-5702e91a3fb6\">fetal movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"47108180-cd33-49d8-9e40-787a4741f54a\">brain development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325844\" id=\"question-wrapper-325844\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Marian Annett</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325845\" id=\"question-wrapper-325845\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Peter Hepper </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325846\" id=\"question-wrapper-325846\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Brenda Milner &amp; Theodore Rasmussen </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325847\" id=\"question-wrapper-325847\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Michael Corballis </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 2? Choose:</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer in the text</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325848\" id=\"question-wrapper-325848\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"df18122b-2b92-4b15-9882-df502b80ae36\">Findings from identical twins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> show that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"b5de6cf3-55e0-4f9a-bbbd-33c5635cc972\">hand preference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a4b9be2f-3cef-491a-833a-f2eca866c554\">cannot be determined by heredity only<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325849\" id=\"question-wrapper-325849\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Dax’s proposal <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"f0323233-fd14-4c35-8fd3-02a4bea2fa80\">received broad support from the other specialists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> at the conference.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325850\" id=\"question-wrapper-325850\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Wada's procedure was considered unsafe for those he tested.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325851\" id=\"question-wrapper-325851\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8b001dad-5ae3-42a2-89f0-35c3b6a98465\">Left-handedness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> a greater <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8b001dad-5ae3-42a2-89f0-35c3b6a98465\">disadvantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> in adulthood than in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"68879f43-8b00-4a77-b863-9d554c4e1458\">childhood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b64188f8-e40b-4a4e-89bb-e4b100d19f12","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the likelihood","passagePhrase":"The probability ... The chance"},{"uid":"97522f5e-11af-4adc-8d1b-caa96827af39","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the parents’ dominant hands","passagePhrase":"two right-handed people ... one parent is a lefty ... both parents are left-handed"},{"uid":"9450512a-2a49-4062-a74a-3a156c042aa2","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"their child will become left-handed","passagePhrase":"a left-handed child"},{"uid":"469dc730-1c57-4caf-8aa6-dcc420bce9dd","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Hand dominance cannot be determined by one gene alone","passagePhrase":"no single gene determines handedness"},{"uid":"b5de6cf3-55e0-4f9a-bbbd-33c5635cc972","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"hand preference","passagePhrase":"handedness"},{"uid":"df18122b-2b92-4b15-9882-df502b80ae36","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Findings from identical twins","passagePhrase":"One in five sets of identical twins involves one right-handed and one left-handed person"},{"uid":"a4b9be2f-3cef-491a-833a-f2eca866c554","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"cannot be determined by heredity only","passagePhrase":"despite the fact that their genetic material is the same ... Genes ... are not solely responsible"},{"uid":"09eef882-7336-4101-a4b0-5702e91a3fb6","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"fetal movement","passagePhrase":"fetuses ... their movements"},{"uid":"0f907f41-0bb6-443c-a074-3d2bc4ed93c4","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Uneven physical development","passagePhrase":"whichever side of the body is developing more quickly"},{"uid":"47108180-cd33-49d8-9e40-787a4741f54a","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"brain development","passagePhrase":"the brain's development"},{"uid":"a2109ac8-bc59-4b95-a957-361eb3583413","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"a dominant hand usually becomes established","passagePhrase":"settle on either their right or left hand"},{"uid":"cbbf8066-7554-461e-bf6a-a66eadf985b1","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"The stage of childhood","passagePhrase":"two or three years old"},{"uid":"9548d62f-3abb-4a59-857f-ba35687b8438","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"side preference","passagePhrase":"specialization on either side of the body"},{"uid":"42cb5a54-858f-4bb9-a5cb-2dcb93dfd8ca","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Examples","passagePhrase":"Cats will favor one paw over another ... Horses stomp more frequently with one hoof ... Certain crabs gesture predominantly with the left or right claw"},{"uid":"7374f437-ba89-4fe7-bbc8-f6e3774b79cb","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Clinical observations","passagePhrase":"reported on an unusual commonality among his patients ... had encountered more than 40 men and women for whom speech was difficult"},{"uid":"84f510d1-ce94-43ec-bc7b-75f4792c5e55","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"led to the proposal","passagePhrase":"elaborated on his theory, stating that"},{"uid":"eaeecf9a-0d39-48ad-bb5d-9bac885c53d8","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"the two halves of the brain do different things","passagePhrase":"each half of the brain was responsible for certain functions"},{"uid":"f93d993e-7f92-481d-b89c-20069e8c2f31","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Language processing is mainly centered","passagePhrase":"language is processed much more intensely"},{"uid":"ee5051db-a0b9-490d-9535-3c7233af0278","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"The gestural origins of speech","passagePhrase":"the origin of human speech lies in gestures"},{"uid":"5d9881ec-0b49-4eb4-aba4-a24ed19ab212","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"stronger use of one hand","passagePhrase":"the right hand developed more strongly"},{"uid":"0a38f7fb-7692-4a34-89ef-60f71e6a6020","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"left-handed people appear relatively common","passagePhrase":"lefties are prevalent"},{"uid":"b61968e7-d5ab-4e83-b280-71b4ba814026","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Fields","passagePhrase":"artists ... composers ... generally acknowledged great political thinkers"},{"uid":"8b001dad-5ae3-42a2-89f0-35c3b6a98465","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Left-handedness ... disadvantage","passagePhrase":"must be more clever to get by in our right-handed world ... This battle"},{"uid":"68879f43-8b00-4a77-b863-9d554c4e1458","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"childhood","passagePhrase":"the very early stages of childhood"}]},"reading_u2_72":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 27-40</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Accidental Scientists</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>A paradox lies close to the heart of scientific discovery. If you know just what you are looking for, finding it can hardly count as a discovery, since it was fully anticipated. But if, on the other hand, you have no notion of what you are looking for, you cannot know when you have found it, and discovery, as such, is out of the question. In the philosophy of science, these extremes map onto the purest forms of deductivism and inductivism: in the former, the outcome is supposed to be logically contained in the premises you start with; in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"262da15a-3fd5-484b-8e7c-9f4d2014a9cc\">the latter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, you are recommended to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"de6d1dff-9807-4dec-a4b9-21e81f347822\">start with no expectations whatsoever and see what turns up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"27\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span>As in so many things, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"944f5e3d-b310-4788-9e69-ebdc48a6da30\">the ideal position is widely supposed to reside somewhere in between these two impossible-to-realise extremes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. You want to have a good enough idea of what you are looking for to be surprised when you find something else of value, and you want to be ignorant enough of your end point so you can entertain alternative outcomes. Scientific discovery should, therefore, have an accidental aspect, but not too much of one. \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"944f5e3d-b310-4788-9e69-ebdc48a6da30\">Serendipity\" is a word that expresses a position something like that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. It is a fascinating word, and the late Robert King Merton — \"the father of the sociology of science\" — liked it well enough to compose its biography, assisted by the French cultural historian Elinor Barber.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"28\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a\">The word did not appear in the published literature until the early 19th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and did not become well enough known to use without explanation until sometime in the first third of the 20th century. \"Serendipity\" means a \"happy accident\" or \"pleasant surprise\" — specifically, the accident of finding something good or useful without looking for it. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28 38\" data-uid=\"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a 6f9b1843-a492-48d9-914b-b07401135924\">The first noted use of</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a\"> \"serendipity\" </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28 38\" data-uid=\"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a 6f9b1843-a492-48d9-914b-b07401135924\">in the English language was by</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28 38\" data-uid=\"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a 2e9fe940-0438-4ff3-9410-fe6a12b0c5fa\">Horace Walpole</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. He explained that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28 39\" data-uid=\"1f13034c-d823-4498-b820-46ce595f1e24 284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a\">it came from</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28 39\" data-uid=\"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a a00577b6-1589-4dba-9158-6504cc924513\">a fairy tale</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a\"> called *The Three Princes of Serendip</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>* (the ancient name for Ceylon, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"f7cabeba-1c48-41a8-bb4a-6731929fcaa5\">present-day<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> Sri Lanka), whose heroes \"were always making discoveries, by accidents and sagacity, of things which they were not in quest of\".</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"29\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"07584a73-a1d9-4c82-9f24-16729baed40c\">Antiquarians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, following Walpole, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"07584a73-a1d9-4c82-9f24-16729baed40c\">found use for it, as they were always rummaging about for curiosities, and unexpected but pleasant surprises were not unknown to them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Some people just seemed to have a knack for that sort of thing, and \"serendipity\" was used to express that special capacity. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"07584a73-a1d9-4c82-9f24-16729baed40c\">The other community that came to dwell on serendipity to say something important about their practice was that of scientists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, and here usages cut to the heart of the matter and were often vigorously contested. Many scientists, including the Harvard physiologist Walter Cannon and, later, the British immunologist Peter Medawar, liked to emphasise how much of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c68523c0-89a2-42ef-b214-56dd602fa05d\">scientific discovery was unplanned and even accidental<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. One example is Hans Christian Ørsted's discovery of electromagnetism when he unintentionally brought a current-carrying wire parallel to a magnetic needle. The rhetoric about the sufficiency of rational methods was so much hot air. Indeed, as Medawar <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c1407242-a6a5-4d5b-a4f0-3111130a69cd\">insisted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c1407242-a6a5-4d5b-a4f0-3111130a69cd\">There is no such thing as The Scientific Method, no way at all of systematising the process of discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.\" Really important <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c68523c0-89a2-42ef-b214-56dd602fa05d\">discoveries had a way of showing up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> when they had a mind to do so and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c68523c0-89a2-42ef-b214-56dd602fa05d\">not when you were looking for them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Maybe some scientists, like some book collectors, had a happy knack; maybe serendipity described the situation rather than a personal skill or capacity.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"30\"><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Some scientists using the word meant to stress those accidents belonging to the situation; some treated serendipity as a personal capacity; many others exploited the ambiguity of the notion. Yet what Cannon and Medawar took as a benign nose-thumbing at dreams of method, other scientists found incendiary. To say that science had a significant serendipitous aspect was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"5d91bc44-096e-483b-8a0d-577f342949c3\">taken by some as dangerous denigration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. If scientific discovery were really accidental, then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"20f087c0-a8f0-4ef0-b10b-ef4fbf50dc99\">what was the special basis of expert authority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>? In this connection, the aphorism of choice came from no less an authority on scientific discovery than Louis Pasteur: \"Chance favours <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"89c173f7-bfd1-45fe-88a2-97c16ed7a402\">the prepared mind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.\" Accidents may happen, and things may turn up unplanned and unforeseen as one is looking for something else, but the ability to notice such events, to see their potential bearing and meaning, to exploit their occurrence and make constructive use of them — these are the results of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"89c173f7-bfd1-45fe-88a2-97c16ed7a402\">systematic mental preparation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"8f39bd31-f24b-4b2d-915c-f33e8a270462\">What seems like an accident<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> is just another form of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"89c173f7-bfd1-45fe-88a2-97c16ed7a402\">expertise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. On closer inspection, it is insisted, the accident dissolves into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"89c173f7-bfd1-45fe-88a2-97c16ed7a402\">sagacity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"31\"><b><span>F. </span></b><span>The context in which scientific serendipity was most contested and had its greatest resonance was that connected with the idea of planned science. The serendipitists were not all inhabitants of academic ivory towers. As Merton and Barber note, two of the great early-20th-century American pioneers of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"1c62db03-59fd-4b53-8b93-225599f92695\">industrial research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> — Willis Whitney and Irving Langmuir, both of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"1c62db03-59fd-4b53-8b93-225599f92695\">General Electric<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> — made much play of serendipity in the course of arguing against overly rigid research planning. Langmuir <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"38092046-7ab2-49e8-99c4-7489526fb5e2\">thought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that misconceptions about the certainty and rationality of the research process did much harm and that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"6b0a2a30-9166-43e0-b749-e3d98a7d7e25\">a mature acceptance of uncertainty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"63673d82-607d-44ca-9179-343dc0ccbf19\">far more likely to result in productive research policies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. For his own part, Langmuir said that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ff567582-104c-49eb-aab4-3022229d2cb4\">satisfactory outcomes \"occurred as though we were just drifting with the wind. These things came about by accident<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.\" If there is no very determinate relationship between cause and effect in research, he said, \"then planning does not get us very far.\" So, from within the bowels of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"1c62db03-59fd-4b53-8b93-225599f92695\">corporate capitalism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> came powerful arguments, by way of serendipity, for scientific spontaneity and autonomy. The notion that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"1c62db03-59fd-4b53-8b93-225599f92695\">industry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> was invariably committed to the regimentation of scientific research just doesn't wash.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"32\"><b><span>G. </span></b><span>For Merton himself — who, one supposes, must have been the senior author — serendipity represented the keystone in the arch of his social scientific work. In 1936, as a very young man, Merton wrote a seminal essay on \"The Unanticipated Consequences of Purposive Social Action\". It is, he argued, the nature of social action that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"03bddb6b-3f31-4439-a0a3-05b58b214660\">what one intends is rarely what one gets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>: intending to provide resources for buttressing the Christian religion, the natural philosophers of the Scientific Revolution laid the groundwork for secularism; people wanting to be alone with nature in Yosemite Valley wind up crowding one another. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 37\" data-uid=\"03bddb6b-3f31-4439-a0a3-05b58b214660 70bd6b6d-ad06-47eb-8bfc-f3ce296be943\">We just don't know enough</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"70bd6b6d-ad06-47eb-8bfc-f3ce296be943\"> — and we can never know enough</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> — <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"03bddb6b-3f31-4439-a0a3-05b58b214660\">to ensure that the past is an adequate guide to the future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"03bddb6b-3f31-4439-a0a3-05b58b214660\">Uncertainty about outcomes, even of our best-laid plans, is endemic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"03bddb6b-3f31-4439-a0a3-05b58b214660\">All social action<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, including that undertaken with the best evidence and formulated according to the most rational criteria, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"03bddb6b-3f31-4439-a0a3-05b58b214660\">is uncertain in its consequences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A-G.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for paragraphs B–G from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, i–x, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"07584a73-a1d9-4c82-9f24-16729baed40c\">How different groups took up the word<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. Why the term was slow to gain acceptance</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"944f5e3d-b310-4788-9e69-ebdc48a6da30\">Resolving the contradiction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. Defining the scientific method</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. Two incompatible routes to new knowledge</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. How <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"8f39bd31-f24b-4b2d-915c-f33e8a270462\">apparent luck<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> can reflect <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"89c173f7-bfd1-45fe-88a2-97c16ed7a402\">trained judgement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. Serendipity as a special personal talent</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"03bddb6b-3f31-4439-a0a3-05b58b214660\">Reality doesn't always match expectation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a\">How the word came into being<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"x\"><span>x. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ff567582-104c-49eb-aab4-3022229d2cb4\">Illustration of serendipity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"1c62db03-59fd-4b53-8b93-225599f92695\">in the business sector<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p><p><b><span>Example Answer</span></b></p><p><span>Paragraph A v</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325852\" id=\"question-wrapper-325852\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325853\" id=\"question-wrapper-325853\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ix</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325854\" id=\"question-wrapper-325854\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325855\" id=\"question-wrapper-325855\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325856\" id=\"question-wrapper-325856\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">x</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325857\" id=\"question-wrapper-325857\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph G</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B , C or D . </span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter in boxes 33-37 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325858\" id=\"question-wrapper-325858\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In paragraph A, the word \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"262da15a-3fd5-484b-8e7c-9f4d2014a9cc\">inductivism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>\" refers to the practice of</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. anticipating results from the start.</li> <li>B. working from prepared premises.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"de6d1dff-9807-4dec-a4b9-21e81f347822\">beginning without any preconceived aims<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</li> <li>D. testing a single hypothesis.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325859\" id=\"question-wrapper-325859\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Medawar <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c1407242-a6a5-4d5b-a4f0-3111130a69cd\">rejects the idea of a fixed method of discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. discoveries are made by people with determined minds.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c68523c0-89a2-42ef-b214-56dd602fa05d\">discoveries tend to happen unexpectedly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</li> <li>C. discoveries depend on a personal gift for noticing things.</li> <li>D. rational methods have been proven ineffective.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325860\" id=\"question-wrapper-325860\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"5d91bc44-096e-483b-8a0d-577f342949c3\">Some scientists dislike<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the idea of serendipity because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. it is&nbsp;easily misunderstood and abused.</li> <li>B. it is too unpredictable.</li> <li>C. it is&nbsp;beyond their comprehension.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"20f087c0-a8f0-4ef0-b10b-ef4fbf50dc99\">it devalues their scientific expertise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325861\" id=\"question-wrapper-325861\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Langmuir <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"38092046-7ab2-49e8-99c4-7489526fb5e2\">believed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. research planning is always pointless.</li> <li>B. industrial development depends on uncertainty.</li> <li>C. people tend to misunderstand the relationship between cause and effect.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"6b0a2a30-9166-43e0-b749-e3d98a7d7e25\">recognising unpredictability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"63673d82-607d-44ca-9179-343dc0ccbf19\">leads to better research policy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325862\" id=\"question-wrapper-325862\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to Merton, the past cannot be a reliable guide to the future because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"70bd6b6d-ad06-47eb-8bfc-f3ce296be943\">our knowledge will always be incomplete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</li> <li>B. social conditions change too quickly.</li> <li>C. people rarely act on rational criteria.</li> <li>D. the best evidence is often ignored.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below.</span></p><p><span>Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325863\" id=\"question-wrapper-325863\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"2e9fe940-0438-4ff3-9410-fe6a12b0c5fa\">writer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"6f9b1843-a492-48d9-914b-b07401135924\">introduced the term \"serendipity\" into English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Horace Walpole</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325864\" id=\"question-wrapper-325864\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"a00577b6-1589-4dba-9158-6504cc924513\">type of story<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> does <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"1f13034c-d823-4498-b820-46ce595f1e24\">the word \"serendipity\" come from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">fairy tale</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325865\" id=\"question-wrapper-325865\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"f7cabeba-1c48-41a8-bb4a-6731929fcaa5\">the present name<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> of Serendip?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">Sri Lanka</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"262da15a-3fd5-484b-8e7c-9f4d2014a9cc","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"inductivism","passagePhrase":"the latter"},{"uid":"de6d1dff-9807-4dec-a4b9-21e81f347822","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"beginning without any preconceived aims","passagePhrase":"start with no expectations whatsoever and see what turns up"},{"uid":"944f5e3d-b310-4788-9e69-ebdc48a6da30","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Resolving the contradiction","passagePhrase":"the ideal position is widely supposed to reside somewhere in between these two impossible-to-realise extremes ... Serendipity\" is a word that expresses a position something like that"},{"uid":"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"How the word came into being","passagePhrase":"The word did not appear in the published literature until the early 19th century ... \"serendipity\" ... called *The Three Princes of Serendip"},{"uid":"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a 6f9b1843-a492-48d9-914b-b07401135924","qNum":"28 38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The first noted use of ... in the English language was by"},{"uid":"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a 2e9fe940-0438-4ff3-9410-fe6a12b0c5fa","qNum":"28 38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Horace Walpole"},{"uid":"1f13034c-d823-4498-b820-46ce595f1e24 284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a","qNum":"28 39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"it came from"},{"uid":"284b573f-5881-4a29-9787-ebd036810c7a a00577b6-1589-4dba-9158-6504cc924513","qNum":"28 39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a fairy tale"},{"uid":"f7cabeba-1c48-41a8-bb4a-6731929fcaa5","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"the present name","passagePhrase":"present-day"},{"uid":"07584a73-a1d9-4c82-9f24-16729baed40c","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"How different groups took up the word","passagePhrase":"Antiquarians ... found use for it, as they were always rummaging about for curiosities, and unexpected but pleasant surprises were not unknown to them ... The other community that came to dwell on serendipity to say something important about their practice was that of scientists"},{"uid":"c68523c0-89a2-42ef-b214-56dd602fa05d","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"discoveries tend to happen unexpectedly","passagePhrase":"scientific discovery was unplanned and even accidental ... discoveries had a way of showing up ... not when you were looking for them"},{"uid":"c1407242-a6a5-4d5b-a4f0-3111130a69cd","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"rejects the idea of a fixed method of discovery","passagePhrase":"insisted ... There is no such thing as The Scientific Method, no way at all of systematising the process of discovery"},{"uid":"5d91bc44-096e-483b-8a0d-577f342949c3","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Some scientists dislike","passagePhrase":"taken by some as dangerous denigration"},{"uid":"20f087c0-a8f0-4ef0-b10b-ef4fbf50dc99","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"it devalues their scientific expertise","passagePhrase":"what was the special basis of expert authority"},{"uid":"89c173f7-bfd1-45fe-88a2-97c16ed7a402","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"trained judgement","passagePhrase":"the prepared mind ... systematic mental preparation ... expertise ... sagacity"},{"uid":"8f39bd31-f24b-4b2d-915c-f33e8a270462","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"apparent luck","passagePhrase":"What seems like an accident"},{"uid":"1c62db03-59fd-4b53-8b93-225599f92695","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"in the business sector","passagePhrase":"industrial research ... General Electric ... corporate capitalism ... industry"},{"uid":"38092046-7ab2-49e8-99c4-7489526fb5e2","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"believed","passagePhrase":"thought"},{"uid":"6b0a2a30-9166-43e0-b749-e3d98a7d7e25","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"recognising unpredictability","passagePhrase":"a mature acceptance of uncertainty"},{"uid":"63673d82-607d-44ca-9179-343dc0ccbf19","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"leads to better research policy","passagePhrase":"far more likely to result in productive research policies"},{"uid":"ff567582-104c-49eb-aab4-3022229d2cb4","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Illustration of serendipity","passagePhrase":"satisfactory outcomes \"occurred as though we were just drifting with the wind. These things came about by accident"},{"uid":"03bddb6b-3f31-4439-a0a3-05b58b214660","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Reality doesn't always match expectation","passagePhrase":"what one intends is rarely what one gets ... to ensure that the past is an adequate guide to the future ... Uncertainty about outcomes, even of our best-laid plans, is endemic ... All social action ... is uncertain in its consequences"},{"uid":"03bddb6b-3f31-4439-a0a3-05b58b214660 70bd6b6d-ad06-47eb-8bfc-f3ce296be943","qNum":"32 37","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"We just don't know enough"},{"uid":"70bd6b6d-ad06-47eb-8bfc-f3ce296be943","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"our knowledge will always be incomplete","passagePhrase":"— and we can never know enough"},{"uid":"2e9fe940-0438-4ff3-9410-fe6a12b0c5fa","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"writer","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"6f9b1843-a492-48d9-914b-b07401135924","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"introduced the term \"serendipity\" into English","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"a00577b6-1589-4dba-9158-6504cc924513","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"type of story","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"1f13034c-d823-4498-b820-46ce595f1e24","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"the word \"serendipity\" come from","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_73":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions</span></b> <b><span>1-13</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Bricks – The Versatile Building Material</span></b></p><p><span>Bricks are one of the oldest known building materials, dating back to 7000 BCE. The oldest found were sun-dried mud bricks in southern Turkey, and these would have been standard in those days. Although sun-dried mud bricks worked reasonably well, especially in moderate climates, fired bricks were found to be more resistant to harsher weather conditions, and so fired bricks are much more reliable for use in permanent buildings. Fired bricks are also <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"5518b54b-f0a7-482f-a84a-a047d8ac79a2\">useful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"15dd3c32-85fd-4b9b-8dbe-5fa68a81a95d\">hotter climates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, as they can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"e02f8267-5c37-466f-b3b8-824eb70f1926\">absorb any heat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> generated throughout the day and then release it at night.</span></p><p><span>The Romans also distinguished between the bricks they used that were dried by the sun and air and the bricks that were fired in a kiln. The Romans were real brick connoisseurs. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"137b371f-98cb-4307-bf59-20433fd9f74e\">preferred<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> to make their bricks <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"41240b0d-92df-4d80-9af6-d4b179468d95\">in the spring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and hold on to their bricks for two years before they were used or sold. They only used clay that was whitish or red for their bricks. The Romans passed on their skills around their sphere of influence and were especially successful at using their mobile kilns to introduce kiln-fired bricks to the whole of the Roman Empire.</span></p><p><span>During the twelfth century, bricks were introduced to northern Germany from northern Italy. This created the ‘brick Gothic period,’ which was a reduced style of Gothic architecture previously very common in northern Europe. The buildings around this time were mainly built from fired red clay bricks. The brick Gothic period can be categorised by the lack of figural architectural sculptures that had previously been carved in stone, as the Gothic figures were impossible to create out of bulky bricks at that time.</span></p><p><span>Bricks suffered a setback <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"085efdb4-f942-44e8-a10b-94cdcb36877e\">during the Renaissance and Baroque periods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"268d0afa-3004-415e-8dfa-91aafccc4685\">exposed brick walls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c4c5640e-19fb-436e-8169-2ecd94992df2\">becoming unpopular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> and brickwork being generally covered by plaster. Only during the mid-eighteenth century did visible brick walls again regain some popularity.</span></p><p><span>Bricks today are more commonly used in the construction of buildings than any other material, except wood. Brick architecture is dominant within its field, and a great industry has developed and invested in the manufacture of many different types of bricks of all shapes and colours. With modern machinery, earth moving equipment, powerful electric motors and modern tunnel kilns, making bricks has become much more productive and efficient. Bricks can be made from a variety of materials, the most common being clay, but they can also be made of calcium silicate and concrete.</span></p><p><span>Good quality bricks have major advantages over stone as they are reliable, weather-resistant and can tolerate acids, pollution and fire. They are also much cheaper than cut stonework. Bricks can be made to any specification in colour, size and shape, which makes them easier to build with than stone. On the other hand, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"bcd9765b-35e3-44d1-87fd-5a3e56c4ff9d\">some bricks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> are more porous and therefore <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5b7d75a4-f4df-41cb-90b3-a34ba5c9bb86\">more susceptible to damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"fec7b590-adc5-4f46-8810-bce3e92fed70\">dampness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> when exposed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"fec7b590-adc5-4f46-8810-bce3e92fed70\">water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. For best results in any construction work, the correct brick must be chosen in accordance with the job specifications.</span></p><p><span>Today, bricks are mainly manufactured in factories, usually employing one of three principal methods – the soft mud process, the stiff mud process and the dry clay process. In the past, bricks were largely manufactured <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"79cc6309-ef8c-4a5b-874b-4b66b4703c08\">by hand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, and there are still artisanal companies that specialise in this product. The process involves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"4c3c0414-a417-4b65-8d57-e3961f23de1d\">putting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the clay, water, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"5aa59c33-c4ed-4dc7-8d44-1cb1862e82bf\">additives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9993d18b-0096-4f7f-8778-81a9708023f9\">into a large pit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, where they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"abf3c91d-f573-45fc-b8ff-5abcdcb01def\">mixed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> by a tempering wheel, often still powered by horsepower. Once the mixture is of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"cba9193d-1f7f-44b8-9879-91a65239268c\">the correct consistency<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"1829dec4-fd4f-4c95-b166-9f147fabe0f6\">it is pressed into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> moulds by hand. To <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"eab210ea-70d4-46e0-91ae-f0da9028504e\">prevent the brick from sticking to the mould<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, the brick <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c0731a62-a211-4281-ab3e-e49f935e98ff\">is coated in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> either sand or water, though coating a brick with sand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f8fdc4f3-ed4e-4de1-ade9-9a79de09dfda\">gives an overall better finish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to it. Once shaped, the bricks are laid outside to dry by air and sun for three to four days. If these bricks left outside for drying are exposed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"a75dedca-0de2-4061-95f6-49d004f24bc8\">a shower<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, water can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"4a4f3283-a946-49a3-b64b-49c17d69f36a\">leave indentations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> on the bricks, which, although <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c948c34b-ece9-4f7e-83a0-ee2b6d9770f0\">not affecting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> the bricks' strength, are considered very undesirable. After drying, the bricks are then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"62306b75-0ac6-4160-98b0-8d6a732b8aa7\">transferred to the kiln for firing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, and this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"afb31964-6db6-4d7c-8ade-fb518791a98b\">creates the finished product<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Bricks are now more generally made by manufacturing processes using machinery. This is a large-scale effort and produces bricks that have been fired in patent kilns.</span></p><p><span>Today’s bricks are also specially designed to be efficient at insulation. If their composition is correct and their laying accurate, a good brick wall around a house can save the occupants a significant amount of money. This is primarily achieved today through cavity wall insulation. Insulating bricks are built in two separate leaves, as they are called in the trade. The gap between the inner and outer leaves of brickwork depends on the type of insulation used, but there should be enough space for a gap of twenty millimetres between the insulating material in the cavity and the two leaves on either side. The air in these gaps is an efficient insulator by itself. Cavity walls have also replaced solid walls, because they are more resistant to rain penetration. Because two leaves are necessary, a strong brick manufacturing industry is essential, so that enough good-quality insulating bricks are plentifully available.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes </span></i><i><b><span>1-5</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet write:</span></i></p><p><b><span>TRUE</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><b><span>FALSE</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><b><span>NOT</span></b> <b><span>GIVEN</span></b><span> if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325866\" id=\"question-wrapper-325866\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Because of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"e02f8267-5c37-466f-b3b8-824eb70f1926\">heat they take in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, fired bricks <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"5518b54b-f0a7-482f-a84a-a047d8ac79a2\">perform poorly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"15dd3c32-85fd-4b9b-8dbe-5fa68a81a95d\">warm regions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325867\" id=\"question-wrapper-325867\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Romans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"137b371f-98cb-4307-bf59-20433fd9f74e\">favoured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"41240b0d-92df-4d80-9af6-d4b179468d95\">a particular time of year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> for producing their bricks. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325868\" id=\"question-wrapper-325868\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Builders in northern Germany regarded brick as a better material than stone. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325869\" id=\"question-wrapper-325869\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"268d0afa-3004-415e-8dfa-91aafccc4685\">Buildings showing brickwork<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c4c5640e-19fb-436e-8169-2ecd94992df2\">generally not liked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"085efdb4-f942-44e8-a10b-94cdcb36877e\">during the Renaissance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325870\" id=\"question-wrapper-325870\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"fec7b590-adc5-4f46-8810-bce3e92fed70\">Moisture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5b7d75a4-f4df-41cb-90b3-a34ba5c9bb86\">poses a risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"bcd9765b-35e3-44d1-87fd-5a3e56c4ff9d\">some types of brick<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the flow chart below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>6-11</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>Making Hand-made Bricks</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"4c3c0414-a417-4b65-8d57-e3961f23de1d\">Place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> </span><b><span>(6)______</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9993d18b-0096-4f7f-8778-81a9708023f9\">in a pit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> with water and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"5aa59c33-c4ed-4dc7-8d44-1cb1862e82bf\">other ingredients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>Use a </span><b><span>(7)______</span></b><span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"abf3c91d-f573-45fc-b8ff-5abcdcb01def\">blend<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the contents to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"cba9193d-1f7f-44b8-9879-91a65239268c\">the desired consistency<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>Shape the material <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"79cc6309-ef8c-4a5b-874b-4b66b4703c08\">manually<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"1829dec4-fd4f-4c95-b166-9f147fabe0f6\">forcing it into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> </span><b><span>(</span></b><b><span>8</span></b><b><span>)______</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c0731a62-a211-4281-ab3e-e49f935e98ff\">Apply<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> water or </span><b><span>(9)______</span></b><span> (<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f8fdc4f3-ed4e-4de1-ade9-9a79de09dfda\">gives a smoother final appearance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>) to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"eab210ea-70d4-46e0-91ae-f0da9028504e\">prevent adhesion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>Leave the pieces outdoors to dry. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"a75dedca-0de2-4061-95f6-49d004f24bc8\">Rain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"4a4f3283-a946-49a3-b64b-49c17d69f36a\">dent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> them, but their </span><b><span>(10)______</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c948c34b-ece9-4f7e-83a0-ee2b6d9770f0\">remains unchanged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"afb31964-6db6-4d7c-8ade-fb518791a98b\">Complete the process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"62306b75-0ac6-4160-98b0-8d6a732b8aa7\">firing them inside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a </span><b><span>(11)______</span></b><span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325871\" id=\"question-wrapper-325871\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">clay</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325872\" id=\"question-wrapper-325872\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">tempering wheel</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325873\" id=\"question-wrapper-325873\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">mo(u)lds</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325874\" id=\"question-wrapper-325874\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">sand</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325875\" id=\"question-wrapper-325875\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">strength</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325876\" id=\"question-wrapper-325876\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">kiln</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Label the diagram below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>12</span></b></i><i><span> and </span></i><i><b><span>13</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_3/reading/images/333aaf63139c825aa495c66b39a8a8dd72c647afb4f09eb4b041d1e314ee1899.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325877\" id=\"question-wrapper-325877\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">leaves</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325878\" id=\"question-wrapper-325878\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">20/twenty millimetres/millimeters/mm</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"15dd3c32-85fd-4b9b-8dbe-5fa68a81a95d","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"warm regions","passagePhrase":"hotter climates"},{"uid":"e02f8267-5c37-466f-b3b8-824eb70f1926","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"heat they take in","passagePhrase":"absorb any heat"},{"uid":"137b371f-98cb-4307-bf59-20433fd9f74e","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"favoured","passagePhrase":"preferred"},{"uid":"41240b0d-92df-4d80-9af6-d4b179468d95","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"a particular time of year","passagePhrase":"in the spring"},{"uid":"085efdb4-f942-44e8-a10b-94cdcb36877e","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"during the Renaissance","passagePhrase":"during the Renaissance and Baroque periods"},{"uid":"268d0afa-3004-415e-8dfa-91aafccc4685","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Buildings showing brickwork","passagePhrase":"exposed brick walls"},{"uid":"c4c5640e-19fb-436e-8169-2ecd94992df2","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"generally not liked","passagePhrase":"becoming unpopular"},{"uid":"bcd9765b-35e3-44d1-87fd-5a3e56c4ff9d","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"some types of brick","passagePhrase":"some bricks"},{"uid":"5b7d75a4-f4df-41cb-90b3-a34ba5c9bb86","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"poses a risk","passagePhrase":"more susceptible to damage"},{"uid":"fec7b590-adc5-4f46-8810-bce3e92fed70","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Moisture","passagePhrase":"dampness ... water"},{"uid":"79cc6309-ef8c-4a5b-874b-4b66b4703c08","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"manually","passagePhrase":"by hand"},{"uid":"4c3c0414-a417-4b65-8d57-e3961f23de1d","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Place","passagePhrase":"putting"},{"uid":"5aa59c33-c4ed-4dc7-8d44-1cb1862e82bf","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"other ingredients","passagePhrase":"additives"},{"uid":"9993d18b-0096-4f7f-8778-81a9708023f9","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"in a pit","passagePhrase":"into a large pit"},{"uid":"abf3c91d-f573-45fc-b8ff-5abcdcb01def","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"blend","passagePhrase":"mixed"},{"uid":"cba9193d-1f7f-44b8-9879-91a65239268c","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"the desired consistency","passagePhrase":"the correct consistency"},{"uid":"1829dec4-fd4f-4c95-b166-9f147fabe0f6","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"forcing it into","passagePhrase":"it is pressed into"},{"uid":"eab210ea-70d4-46e0-91ae-f0da9028504e","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"prevent adhesion","passagePhrase":"prevent the brick from sticking to the mould"},{"uid":"c0731a62-a211-4281-ab3e-e49f935e98ff","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Apply","passagePhrase":"is coated in"},{"uid":"f8fdc4f3-ed4e-4de1-ade9-9a79de09dfda","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"gives a smoother final appearance","passagePhrase":"gives an overall better finish"},{"uid":"a75dedca-0de2-4061-95f6-49d004f24bc8","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"Rain","passagePhrase":"a shower"},{"uid":"4a4f3283-a946-49a3-b64b-49c17d69f36a","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"dent","passagePhrase":"leave indentations"},{"uid":"c948c34b-ece9-4f7e-83a0-ee2b6d9770f0","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"remains unchanged","passagePhrase":"not affecting"},{"uid":"62306b75-0ac6-4160-98b0-8d6a732b8aa7","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"firing them inside","passagePhrase":"transferred to the kiln for firing"},{"uid":"afb31964-6db6-4d7c-8ade-fb518791a98b","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Complete the process","passagePhrase":"creates the finished product"}]},"reading_u2_74":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 14-26</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>WATER TREATMENT: REED BED</span></b></p><p><span>In recent years, it has been shown that plants, more accurately roots, play a crucial part in purifying dirty water before it enters seas and rivers. In 15th-century Britain, dirty water was purified by passing through the wetlands. People began to realize that the “natural” way of water purification was effective. Nowadays, subsurface flow wetlands (SSFW) are a common alternative in Europe for the treatment of wastewater in rural areas. Mainly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"9976e55c-ad86-490f-9a44-2dcaf55d8c85\">in the last 10 to 12 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, there has been a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"4d94817f-9572-4efc-b815-fbd1a477b303\">significant growth in the number and size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of the systems in use. The conventional mechanism of water purification used in big cities where there are large volumes of water to be purified is inappropriate in rural areas.</span></p><p><span>The common reed has the ability to transfer oxygen from its leaves, down through its stem and rhizomes, and out via its root system. As a result of this action, a very high population of microorganisms occurs in the root system, in zones of aerobic, anoxic, and anaerobic conditions. As the wastewater moves very slowly through the mass of reed roots, this liquid can be successfully treated. The reason why they are so effective is often that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"eec1e425-bcdf-44b4-b392-cdc4309d09d1\">within the bed’s root sector<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"52c4b9ea-b81a-4152-8d5d-e0a0f41787b2\">natural biological, physical, and chemical processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> interact with one another to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"c7a3b557-283c-4e8e-bf5e-c88fbcd32c34\">degrade or remove<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> a good range of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"aad1f4ed-d17a-4663-b520-706073e76a41\">pollutants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Dirty water from households, farms and factories consumes a lot of oxygen in the water, which will lead to the death of aquatic creatures. Several aquatic plants are important in purifying water. They not only absorb carbon dioxide and release oxygen into the water, improving the environment for fish, but also absorb nutrients from the water as well. Britain and the G.S. differ in their preference for plants to purify water. Bulrushes (Scirpus spp.) and rushes (Juncus spp.) are excellent water purifiers. They remove excess nutrients from the water as well as oil and bacteria such as Escherichia coli and Salmonella. However, algae grow freely in summer and die off in winter. Their remains foul the bottom of the pool.</span></p><p><span>Artificial reed beds purify water in both horizontal and downflow ways. The reeds succeed best when a dense layer of root hairs has formed. It takes three years for the roots to fully develop. Which type of wetland a certain country applies varies widely depending on the country in Europe and its main lines of development. Besides the development of horizontal or vertical flow wetlands for wastewater treatment, the use of wetlands for sludge treatment has been very successful in Europe. Some special design lines offer the retention of microbiological organisms in constructed wetlands, the treatment of agricultural wastewater, the treatment of some kinds of industrial wastewater, and the control of diffuse pollution.</span></p><p><span>If the water is slightly polluted, a horizontal system is used. Horizontal-flow wetlands may be of two types: free-water surface-flow (FWF) or sub-surface water-flow (SSF). In the former, the effluent flows freely above the sand/gravel bed in which the reeds etc. are planted; in the latter, effluent passes through the sand/gravel bed. In FWF-type wetlands, effluent is treated by plant stems, leaves and rhizomes. Such FWF wetlands are densely planted and typically have water depths of less than 0.4m. However, dense planting can limit the diffusion of oxygen into the water. These systems work particularly well for low-strength effluents or effluents that have undergone some forms of pretreatment and play an invaluable role in tertiary treatment and the polishing of effluents. The horizontal reed flow system uses a long reed bed, where the liquid slowly flows horizontally through it. The length of the reed bed is about 100 meters. The downside of horizontal reed beds is that they use up lots of land space, and they do take quite a long time to produce clean water.</span></p><p><span>A vertical flow (downflow) reed bed is a sealed, gravel-filled trench with reeds growing in it. The reeds in a downflow system are planted in a bed 60cm deep. In vertical flow reed beds, the wastewater is applied to the top of the reed bed, flows down through a rhizome zone with sludge as a substrate, then through a root zone with sand as a substrate, followed by a layer of gravel for drainage, and is collected in an underdrainage system of large stones. The effluent flows onto the surface of the bed and percolates slowly through the different layers into an outlet pipe, which leads to a horizontal flow bed where it is cleaned by millions of bacteria, algae, fungi, and microorganisms that digest the waste, including sewage. There is no standing water, so there should be no unpleasant smells.</span></p><p><span>Vertical flow reed bed systems are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"6db6bb03-97f4-420b-92ca-1e5d49158f7c\">much more effective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> than horizontal flow reed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e22d71f4-8d8e-4c4d-b125-f5d13e9c2d93\">beds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, not only in reducing biochemical oxygen demand (BOD) and suspended solids (SS) levels but also in reducing ammonia levels and eliminating smells. Usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"aaa22958-93e3-4e21-a0f3-f10e090592d0\">considerably smaller<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> than horizontal flow beds, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"0b0b55d8-d453-4720-8444-a1ac324a2a05\">are capable of handling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"e7e0b176-9356-4fcf-b072-de00af7cc2fb\">much stronger effluents which contain heavily polluted matter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and have a longer lifetime value. A vertical reed bed system works more efficiently than a horizontal reed bed system, but it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"787bef7f-3b50-40e3-bc1b-341a3a526ec5\">requires more management<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, and its reed beds are often operated for a few days then rested, so <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"99fc9cab-caef-4233-8b22-d24fa88ec2e3\">several<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> beds and a distribution system <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a22bf6f2-0ff4-44ce-a6c2-8d6fe4e2c048\">are needed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The natural way of water purification has many advantages over the conventional mechanism. The natural way <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"4818987a-003c-4918-8327-541dec735580\">requires less expenditure for installation, operation and maintenance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Besides, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"c47d71b6-538f-47dd-87d7-cbb16271f04e\">looks attractive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and can improve the surrounding landscape. Reed beds are natural habitats found in floodplains, waterlogged depressions and estuaries. The natural bed systems are a biologically proven, environmentally friendly and visually unobtrusive way of treating wastewater, and have the extra virtue of frequently being better than mechanical wastewater treatment systems. Over the medium to long term, reed bed systems are, in most cases, more cost-effective to install than any other wastewater treatment. They are naturally environmentally sound, protecting groundwater, dams, creeks, rivers and estuaries.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes </span></i><i><b><span>14-16</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet, write</span></i></p><p><b><span>TRUE</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><b><span>FALSE</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><b><span>NOT</span></b> <b><span>GIVEN</span></b><span> if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325879\" id=\"question-wrapper-325879\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The use of subsurface flow wetlands has <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"4d94817f-9572-4efc-b815-fbd1a477b303\">remained largely unchanged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"9976e55c-ad86-490f-9a44-2dcaf55d8c85\">over the past decade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325880\" id=\"question-wrapper-325880\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"52c4b9ea-b81a-4152-8d5d-e0a0f41787b2\">A range of processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"eec1e425-bcdf-44b4-b392-cdc4309d09d1\">taking place around the roots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"c7a3b557-283c-4e8e-bf5e-c88fbcd32c34\">helps to break down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"aad1f4ed-d17a-4663-b520-706073e76a41\">contaminants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325881\" id=\"question-wrapper-325881\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Escherichia coli is the most difficult bacterium to eliminate.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Label the diagram below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 17-19 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_3/reading/images/55c3b341c9ee916fc856bf95fa68fc92baa50da9026f2812f80504dd96d9939b.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325882\" id=\"question-wrapper-325882\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">sludge</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325883\" id=\"question-wrapper-325883\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">sand</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325884\" id=\"question-wrapper-325884\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">gravel</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose FIVE answers from the list and write the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet. </span></p><p><span>Compared with horizontal-flow systems, some advantages of the downflow systems are:</span></p><p><span>- (20)______</span></p><p><span>- (21)________ </span></p><p><span>- (22)________. </span></p><p><span>However, they have certain disadvantages such as: </span></p><p><span>- (23)________ </span></p><p><span>- (24)________. </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> Greater space requirements</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"aaa22958-93e3-4e21-a0f3-f10e090592d0\">Lower space requirements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"787bef7f-3b50-40e3-bc1b-341a3a526ec5\">Greater management demands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> Less frequent operator attention</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a22bf6f2-0ff4-44ce-a6c2-8d6fe4e2c048\">Need for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"99fc9cab-caef-4233-8b22-d24fa88ec2e3\">multiple<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e22d71f4-8d8e-4c4d-b125-f5d13e9c2d93\">treatment units<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><b><span>F.</span></b><span> Simpler construction</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><b><span>G.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"6db6bb03-97f4-420b-92ca-1e5d49158f7c\">Greater treatment efficiency<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><b><span>H.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"0b0b55d8-d453-4720-8444-a1ac324a2a05\">Capacity to handle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"e7e0b176-9356-4fcf-b072-de00af7cc2fb\">more contaminated wastewater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325885\" id=\"question-wrapper-325885\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/G/H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325886\" id=\"question-wrapper-325886\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/G/H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325887\" id=\"question-wrapper-325887\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/G/H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325888\" id=\"question-wrapper-325888\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325889\" id=\"question-wrapper-325889\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose two correct letters from the following </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>D</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>E</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>25 – 26</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><span>What are the </span><b><span>TWO</span></b><span> advantages of the natural water purification system mentioned in the passage?</span></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> It treats water faster than mechanical systems.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"4818987a-003c-4918-8327-541dec735580\">cheap to run<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> It prevents flooding.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"c47d71b6-538f-47dd-87d7-cbb16271f04e\">pleasant to look at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span> It can function in all climates.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325890\" id=\"question-wrapper-325890\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325891\" id=\"question-wrapper-325891\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"9976e55c-ad86-490f-9a44-2dcaf55d8c85","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"over the past decade","passagePhrase":"in the last 10 to 12 years"},{"uid":"eec1e425-bcdf-44b4-b392-cdc4309d09d1","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"taking place around the roots","passagePhrase":"within the bed’s root sector"},{"uid":"52c4b9ea-b81a-4152-8d5d-e0a0f41787b2","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"A range of processes","passagePhrase":"natural biological, physical, and chemical processes"},{"uid":"c7a3b557-283c-4e8e-bf5e-c88fbcd32c34","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"helps to break down","passagePhrase":"degrade or remove"},{"uid":"aad1f4ed-d17a-4663-b520-706073e76a41","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"contaminants","passagePhrase":"pollutants"},{"uid":"6db6bb03-97f4-420b-92ca-1e5d49158f7c","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Greater treatment efficiency","passagePhrase":"much more effective"},{"uid":"e22d71f4-8d8e-4c4d-b125-f5d13e9c2d93","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"treatment units","passagePhrase":"beds"},{"uid":"aaa22958-93e3-4e21-a0f3-f10e090592d0","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Lower space requirements","passagePhrase":"considerably smaller"},{"uid":"0b0b55d8-d453-4720-8444-a1ac324a2a05","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Capacity to handle","passagePhrase":"are capable of handling"},{"uid":"e7e0b176-9356-4fcf-b072-de00af7cc2fb","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"more contaminated wastewater","passagePhrase":"much stronger effluents which contain heavily polluted matter"},{"uid":"787bef7f-3b50-40e3-bc1b-341a3a526ec5","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Greater management demands","passagePhrase":"requires more management"},{"uid":"99fc9cab-caef-4233-8b22-d24fa88ec2e3","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"multiple","passagePhrase":"several"},{"uid":"a22bf6f2-0ff4-44ce-a6c2-8d6fe4e2c048","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Need for","passagePhrase":"are needed"},{"uid":"4818987a-003c-4918-8327-541dec735580","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"cheap to run","passagePhrase":"requires less expenditure for installation, operation and maintenance"},{"uid":"c47d71b6-538f-47dd-87d7-cbb16271f04e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"pleasant to look at","passagePhrase":"looks attractive"}]},"reading_u2_75":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 27-40</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>THE DRINKING OF WINE</span></b></p><p><span>The birth of the cult of fine wine can be dated precisely. On April 10th 1663, Samuel Pepys, diarist and man-about-London, noted that he had enjoyed \"a sort of French wine called Ho Bryan that hath a good and most particular taste that I never met with\".</span></p><p><span>The owners of Ho Bryan were the Pontacs. They were the top winemaking family of their day, and founded a fashionable restaurant called Pontack's Head in London in 1663. John Locke, the philosopher whose theory of the social contract inspired America's revolutionaries but who had worldlier interests too, spotted <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"158c4e52-b8bc-4350-be1f-761f233abe8d\">the reasons for the superiority of Ho Bryan<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> on a visit to the vineyard in 1667. He found \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"336792f9-c07b-4607-86d8-402f63edc693\">a little rise of ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>…<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"336792f9-c07b-4607-86d8-402f63edc693\">white sand mixed with a little gravel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>; scarcely fit to bear anything.\" He added that \"they say the wine in the next vineyard to it, tho' seeming equal to me, is not so good.\" Today that vineyard is still rated just below its neighbour.</span></p><p><span>Locke had seized on the essential concept of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"336792f9-c07b-4607-86d8-402f63edc693\">terroir<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"336792f9-c07b-4607-86d8-402f63edc693\">the combination of soil, subsoil, drainage and microclimate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> which provides the conditions for the production of fine wine. Another <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ffff07ea-9b93-421d-a763-442485452083\">connoisseur<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, the 18th-century <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ffff07ea-9b93-421d-a763-442485452083\">economist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> Adam Smith, noted that \"the vine is more affected by the difference of soils than any other fruit tree. From some it derives a flavour which no culture or management can equal.\"</span></p><p><span>By the early 18th century, claret was getting more popular, partly because it was getting better. The craft of claret-making had developed. The wine was designed to be kept for years, not months, notably by being carefully stored in oak casks. Better corks allowed wine to be stored longer and more safely. Bottles were produced that could be \"binned\"—laid down on their sides to mature.</span></p><p><span>In the latter part of the 18th century, drinking claret helped the rich to distinguish themselves from England's port-sodden squirearchy. Port was not only the more traditional drink but also—because it attracted much lower duties—far cheaper. John Hervey, the first Earl of Bristol, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"47dde751-fad7-49b7-ae61-384dd93c4dae\">spent four times as much on claret as on port<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, whereas the lusty trenchermen who gathered in the Barbers Hall in the City of London spent a mere £2 on claret as against £850 on port.</span></p><p><span>When Britain made peace with France in 1713, claret became more accessible and the wine trade flourished. Claret was pricey, but rich Londoners, who were also by then big spenders on theatres, spas and music produced by fashionable immigrants such as Handel, consumed conspicuous quantities. Sir Robert Walpole, Britain's first prime minister, used navy ships to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"85f9e246-d577-4f8c-a33a-814ad0e66ad3\">smuggle his favourite wines from France<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. The most expensive one he bought was old burgundy, but that—as now—was available only in tiny quantities. So he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"cb278663-dd9c-4e27-850b-5d2a97d6e6c7\">relied largely on claret<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, buying four hogsheads of 24 dozen bottles of Margaux and one hogshead of Lafite every three months. In a single year his wine bill amounted to over £1,200 (£100,000 today). British consumers bought the best stuff and paid top prices. By the time of the French Revolution, the British were paying five times as much for their claret as the wine's other main customers, the notoriously parsimonious Dutch, who preferred the cheaper, lower-grade stuff.</span></p><p><span>By the late 19th century, claret was beginning to flow down the social hierarchy. A free-trade treaty between Britain and France in 1860 drastically reduced the duty on French wines, thus encouraging the British middle classes to ape their social superiors; and in that year the chancellor of the exchequer, William Gladstone, keen to stiffen the nation's moral spine, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e595836a-4855-4335-841d-4fb4e1f129aa\">cut the duty on table wines to 40% of that on more intoxicating fortified wines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> such as port and sherry.</span></p><p><span>The following year came the Single Bottle Act, allowing grocers to sell wine by the bottle. A much-despised, enormously popular drink called \"grocers' claret\" was born, with the result that, between 1859 and 1878, sales of French wines, largely from Bordeaux, rose sixfold to 36m bottles. The Gilbey family, one of the most remarkable commercial dynasties of Victorian England, franchised 2,000 grocers licensed to sell wine, largely claret. Their business grew so fast that by 1875 they were able to buy Château Loudenne in the Médoc to hold their gigantic stocks of claret. As the middle classes turned to claret, so the upper classes abandoned this increasingly common tipple in favour of hock and champagne.</span></p><p><span>Then the fortunes of the claret business turned. In the late 1870s and 1880s, an attack of mildew tainted the wines: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"1bfd201d-354b-4c54-a941-e97ef045a9af\">the reputation of Lafite, for instance, was ruined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> when the 1884 vintage turned mouldy after only a couple of years in bottle. At the same time, the phylloxera bug <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c203d5ad-8c3f-4006-9c19-ed16f133d357\">began to devastate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> Bordeaux's vineyards.</span></p><p><span>Claret <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"33b7e73a-9ef8-40e6-85e2-a7f54b95fffa\">came back into its own<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> in 1960, when the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"758c5e3f-1065-42cf-bd1b-68a07ae74590\">splendid 1959 vintage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"e80a6f49-5a3c-407d-8d1d-0753d0cdca07\">coincided with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the arrival of big <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"769630f5-9a0d-4650-ab2f-2e0b663fb9b5\">American buyers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Its popularity has risen steadily since. London remains at the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"6dc688c7-8283-405b-9c8c-5e3bdb3f0e03\">centre<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of the fine-wine business—home of organisations such as the Institute of Masters of Wine, of Decanter and World of Fine Wine magazines, and of most of the world's biggest wine auctions. Liv-ex, the world's first stock market for fine wine, is based in London; and its figures show that nine-tenths of the wine trade is still in \"classed growth\" (leading) clarets. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"c6dd5b8f-7114-41a7-98bd-95ac3ad70ab0\">Newcomers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> from vineyards in a dozen countries, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f4ed979b-b12a-46b2-8cf8-cbb00f96502e\">trying to launch<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5023f850-859a-4cc1-9a2c-6575d47edda8\">their finest wines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f4ed979b-b12a-46b2-8cf8-cbb00f96502e\">on the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> world market, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"e61d16ff-97d6-418e-b308-b144bea0c63f\">come to London first for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> validation. Yet though London may still have much of the knowledge and the market, as consumers the British may be past their best. This year, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"89d891b3-b420-4e4f-8f29-7d28e4fec92f\">57% of the fine wine that Sotheby's sold globally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"c97068a3-5daa-4da0-9940-9fd04f67b0a2\">by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> value, was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"8f983749-4757-4d53-9adc-6476410981a9\">bought by Asians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>; four-fifths of those buyers were from China and Hong Kong.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 27-32) and the list of people below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct person, A-F.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> John Hervey</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Adam Smith</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> John Locke</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> William Gladstone</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Robert Walpole</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325892\" id=\"question-wrapper-325892\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"336792f9-c07b-4607-86d8-402f63edc693\">identified the natural conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> that could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"158c4e52-b8bc-4350-be1f-761f233abe8d\">explain Ho Bryan's distinctive quality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325893\" id=\"question-wrapper-325893\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"85f9e246-d577-4f8c-a33a-814ad0e66ad3\">brought wine into the country illegally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325894\" id=\"question-wrapper-325894\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e595836a-4855-4335-841d-4fb4e1f129aa\">wanted to discourage people from drinking strong wines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325895\" id=\"question-wrapper-325895\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"47dde751-fad7-49b7-ae61-384dd93c4dae\">paid out far more for claret than for port<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325896\" id=\"question-wrapper-325896\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ffff07ea-9b93-421d-a763-442485452083\">expert on both wine and economics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325897\" id=\"question-wrapper-325897\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"cb278663-dd9c-4e27-850b-5d2a97d6e6c7\">bought more claret than any other kind of wine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>In the late 19th century, claret suffered two serious setbacks. One of these was when the wines were tainted by (33)________, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"1bfd201d-354b-4c54-a941-e97ef045a9af\">ruined the good name of Lafite<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, and the other was when Bordeaux’s vineyards <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"c203d5ad-8c3f-4006-9c19-ed16f133d357\">were hit by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the (34)________. It took many years for the wine to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"33b7e73a-9ef8-40e6-85e2-a7f54b95fffa\">recover<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. In 1960, this recovery <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"e80a6f49-5a3c-407d-8d1d-0753d0cdca07\">was helped by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the production of an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"758c5e3f-1065-42cf-bd1b-68a07ae74590\">excellent claret in 1959<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and the (35)________ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"769630f5-9a0d-4650-ab2f-2e0b663fb9b5\">buyers from the United States<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Today, London remains the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"6dc688c7-8283-405b-9c8c-5e3bdb3f0e03\">hub<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of the (36)________ business. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"c6dd5b8f-7114-41a7-98bd-95ac3ad70ab0\">People<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f4ed979b-b12a-46b2-8cf8-cbb00f96502e\">trying to enter the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> (37)________ with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5023f850-859a-4cc1-9a2c-6575d47edda8\">new wines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"e61d16ff-97d6-418e-b308-b144bea0c63f\">need to get<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> (38)________ for them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"e61d16ff-97d6-418e-b308-b144bea0c63f\">in London<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. The growing market for fine wines, however, now seems to be coming from outside the UK. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"8f983749-4757-4d53-9adc-6476410981a9\">Asian purchasers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"89d891b3-b420-4e4f-8f29-7d28e4fec92f\">account for more than half of Sotheby's worldwide fine-wine sales<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"c97068a3-5daa-4da0-9940-9fd04f67b0a2\">measured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> (39)________.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325898\" id=\"question-wrapper-325898\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">mildew</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325899\" id=\"question-wrapper-325899\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(phylloxera) bug</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325900\" id=\"question-wrapper-325900\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">arrival</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325901\" id=\"question-wrapper-325901\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">fine(-)wine</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325902\" id=\"question-wrapper-325902\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(world) market</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325903\" id=\"question-wrapper-325903\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">validation</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325904\" id=\"question-wrapper-325904\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">by value</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C </span></b><span>or</span><b><span> D</span></b><span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325905\" id=\"question-wrapper-325905\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The main purpose of the passage is to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. explain how claret became associated with social status in Britain.</li> <li>B. trace the development of claret and its market over time.</li> <li>C. examine the major crises that disrupted the claret trade.</li> <li>D. describe how changes in British drinking habits affected the popularity of claret.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"158c4e52-b8bc-4350-be1f-761f233abe8d","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"explain Ho Bryan's distinctive quality","passagePhrase":"the reasons for the superiority of Ho Bryan"},{"uid":"336792f9-c07b-4607-86d8-402f63edc693","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"identified the natural conditions","passagePhrase":"a little rise of ground ... white sand mixed with a little gravel ... terroir ... the combination of soil, subsoil, drainage and microclimate"},{"uid":"ffff07ea-9b93-421d-a763-442485452083","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"expert on both wine and economics","passagePhrase":"connoisseur ... economist"},{"uid":"47dde751-fad7-49b7-ae61-384dd93c4dae","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"paid out far more for claret than for port","passagePhrase":"spent four times as much on claret as on port"},{"uid":"85f9e246-d577-4f8c-a33a-814ad0e66ad3","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"brought wine into the country illegally","passagePhrase":"smuggle his favourite wines from France"},{"uid":"cb278663-dd9c-4e27-850b-5d2a97d6e6c7","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"bought more claret than any other kind of wine","passagePhrase":"relied largely on claret"},{"uid":"e595836a-4855-4335-841d-4fb4e1f129aa","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"wanted to discourage people from drinking strong wines","passagePhrase":"cut the duty on table wines to 40% of that on more intoxicating fortified wines"},{"uid":"1bfd201d-354b-4c54-a941-e97ef045a9af","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"ruined the good name of Lafite","passagePhrase":"the reputation of Lafite, for instance, was ruined"},{"uid":"c203d5ad-8c3f-4006-9c19-ed16f133d357","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"were hit by","passagePhrase":"began to devastate"},{"uid":"33b7e73a-9ef8-40e6-85e2-a7f54b95fffa","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"recover","passagePhrase":"came back into its own"},{"uid":"758c5e3f-1065-42cf-bd1b-68a07ae74590","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"excellent claret in 1959","passagePhrase":"splendid 1959 vintage"},{"uid":"e80a6f49-5a3c-407d-8d1d-0753d0cdca07","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"was helped by","passagePhrase":"coincided with"},{"uid":"769630f5-9a0d-4650-ab2f-2e0b663fb9b5","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"buyers from the United States","passagePhrase":"American buyers"},{"uid":"6dc688c7-8283-405b-9c8c-5e3bdb3f0e03","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"hub","passagePhrase":"centre"},{"uid":"c6dd5b8f-7114-41a7-98bd-95ac3ad70ab0","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"People","passagePhrase":"Newcomers"},{"uid":"f4ed979b-b12a-46b2-8cf8-cbb00f96502e","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"trying to enter the","passagePhrase":"trying to launch ... on the"},{"uid":"5023f850-859a-4cc1-9a2c-6575d47edda8","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"new wines","passagePhrase":"their finest wines"},{"uid":"e61d16ff-97d6-418e-b308-b144bea0c63f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"need to get ... in London","passagePhrase":"come to London first for"},{"uid":"89d891b3-b420-4e4f-8f29-7d28e4fec92f","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"account for more than half of Sotheby's worldwide fine-wine sales","passagePhrase":"57% of the fine wine that Sotheby's sold globally"},{"uid":"c97068a3-5daa-4da0-9940-9fd04f67b0a2","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"measured","passagePhrase":"by"},{"uid":"8f983749-4757-4d53-9adc-6476410981a9","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Asian purchasers","passagePhrase":"bought by Asians"}]},"reading_u2_76":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions</span></b> <b><span>1-13</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Soap</span></b></p><p><span>One substance everyone uses every day is soap, whether it be for washing our hands using a bar of soap, doing the laundry or washing the floor with detergent. Technically, soaps are ionic compounds from fatty acids and they are used for a variety of cleaning purposes. Soaps allow particles that cannot usually be dissolved in water to be soluble and then be washed away. Although made in a different way, synthetic detergents operate in a similar fashion.</span></p><p><span>The human skin is under daily attack from various things, such as scorching sun, drying winds, biting cold weather, bacteria and dirt, and so our distant ancestors learned quickly that preserving the health of skin is a way for a better and longer life. Popular in different civilisations, the benefits of soap finally managed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"b5e6c159-c121-42df-9740-0599a19c034a\">appeal to a wide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"ca523588-5c94-4db8-b52a-853aa2b8a247\">European </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"b5e6c159-c121-42df-9740-0599a19c034a ca523588-5c94-4db8-b52a-853aa2b8a247\">population</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"7d90a27a-9fa6-428b-8ec3-0aebfd99119b\">in the 17th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, and, since then, the tradition of maintaining high personal hygiene has experienced only constant growth. With its ability to clean people’s clothes and disinfect their surroundings from harmful bacteria and dirt, soaps remain one of the most useful and fundamental hygiene tools that mankind ever created.</span></p><p><span>The first concrete evidence we have of a soap-like substance is dated around 2800 BC. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"ef6b9f29-c215-4729-9201-4552b9b3cc2f\">The first soap makers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> were Babylonians, Mesopotamians, Egyptians, as well as the ancient Greeks and Romans. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"0ef0eb3b-705b-4bb3-9fac-5059e695e81e\">All of them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"3cfc8565-00e9-4086-b6fe-b03f3f17a3d6\">made soap by mixing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> fat, oils and salts. Soap was not made and used for bathing and personal hygiene, but was rather produced for cleaning cooking utensils or goods or was used for medicinal purposes. According to Roman legend, their natural soap was first discovered near a mountain called ‘Sapo’, where animals were sacrificed. Rain used to wash the fat from sacrificed animals along with wood ashes into the River Tiber, where the women who were washing clothes in it found the mixture made their washing easier. It is a nice story, but unfortunately there is no such place on record and no evidence for the mythical story.</span></p><p><span>Soaps today come in three principal forms: bars, powders and liquids. Some liquid products are so viscous that they are gels. Raw materials are chosen according to many criteria, including their human and environmental safety, cost, compatibility with other ingredients, and the desired form and performance characteristics of the finished product. In ancient times, soap was made from animal fats and wood ashes. Today, it is still produced from vegetable or animal fats and alkali. The main sources of fats are beef and mutton tallow, while palm, coconut and palm kernel oils are the principal oils.</span></p><p><span>In the early beginnings of soap making, it was an exclusive technique used by small groups of soap makers. The demand for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"abc9dc28-f634-4834-b375-c1498026ec14\">early soap<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> was high, but it was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b1c23ba4-354b-4651-ac43-56265a8730d8\">very expensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, and there was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b1c23ba4-354b-4651-ac43-56265a8730d8\">a monopoly on soap production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> in many areas. Over time, recipes for soap making became more widely known, but soap was still expensive.</span></p><p><span>Modern soap was made by the batch kettle boiling method until shortly after World War II, when continuous processes were developed. Continuous processes are preferred today because of their flexibility, speed and economics. The first part of the manufacturing process is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"f05e824f-ead6-4873-a9cb-67a9dae6220e\">heat the raw materials<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a5873ef2-13d0-47d8-9991-2adbae396e28\">remove<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> impurities. This is followed by saponification, which involves adding a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"820e277b-585f-40ca-b262-76b8924f02a5\">powerful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> alkali to the heated raw materials. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"98cbbb4e-a97f-4909-b0d9-cf7fac6442b4\">releases the fatty acids<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (known as ‘neat soap’) that are the basis of the soap <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"98cbbb4e-a97f-4909-b0d9-cf7fac6442b4\">and a valuable by-product, glycerine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. The glycerine is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"38b77e87-07d8-4b7a-a3ce-c079fe5f47de\">recovered by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> chemical treatment, followed by evaporation and refining. Refined glycerine is an important industrial material used in foods, cosmetics, drugs and many other products. The next processing step for the soap is vacuum spray drying to convert the neat soap into dry soap pellets. The moisture <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"aed53ec6-f5a5-43fa-afca-47878f592fa8\">content<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of the pellets will be determined by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"3c60e19a-4ea6-46b0-ad41-6144443492b8\">the desired characteristics of the soap bar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. In the final processing step, the dry soap pellets pass through a bar soap finishing line. The first unit in the line is a mixer, called an amalgamator, in which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b78c4d99-f776-41de-9234-9cb24d768419\">the soap pellets are blended together with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> fragrance, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"96f5268c-f695-4e62-a933-91ac2f9aff88\">shades<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"e1c98297-2c10-40b9-b0ec-e4133acac672\">all other ingredients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. The mixture is then homogenised and refined through rolling mills and refining plodders to achieve thorough blending and a uniform texture. Finally, the mixture is cut into bar-size units and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"69d250ce-c480-4913-8c71-2e65f2158046\">stamped into its final shape in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> a soap press.</span></p><p><span>The history of liquid soaps and gels started only recently, when the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ed97820e-2b2b-414b-ab4d-551c9b198535\">technological and chemical advancements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of the modern age <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"9fdcc69b-a250-4364-9c1d-a69b2c620a11\">enabled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> countless inventors <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"9fdcc69b-a250-4364-9c1d-a69b2c620a11\">to start experimenting with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"2e9b5c71-0abc-4216-8aeb-10e7e4ec4049\">more complicated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> recipes. The first appearance of liquid soap happened in the mid 1800’s with the exploits of several inventors. In 1865, William Shepphard patented liquid soap; however, the popularity of this product would not arrive until the creation of Palmolive soap in 1898 by B.J. Johnson.</span></p><p><span>Advancements in modern chemistry enabled the creation of shower gel. The main difference between liquid soaps and shower gels is that gels do not contain saponified oil. They are based mostly on petroleum, have numerous chemical ingredients that help with easier cleaning of skin, lather better in hard water areas, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"ad754c80-1621-4dcf-9ebd-8f30a0bf88d9\">do not leave<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> a residue on the skin and bathtub, and are in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"eb3b73ee-a705-4430-a161-3d8e08934ddf\">a balanced pH state<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, so that they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"eb3b73ee-a705-4430-a161-3d8e08934ddf\">do not cause<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> skin irritations. Because some shower gels can cause drying of the skin after use, many manufacturers insert various moisturisers into their recipes. Some use menthol, an ingredient that gives skin a sensation of coldness and freshness.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes </span></i><i><b><span>1-4</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet write:</span></i></p><p><b><span>TRUE</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><b><span>FALSE</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><b><span>NOT</span></b> <b><span>GIVEN</span></b><span> if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325906\" id=\"question-wrapper-325906\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Traditional soap is less effective at cleaning than synthetic detergents.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325907\" id=\"question-wrapper-325907\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"ca523588-5c94-4db8-b52a-853aa2b8a247\">Europeans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"b5e6c159-c121-42df-9740-0599a19c034a\">widely used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> soap for <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"7d90a27a-9fa6-428b-8ec3-0aebfd99119b\">more than a thousand years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325908\" id=\"question-wrapper-325908\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Fat was an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"3cfc8565-00e9-4086-b6fe-b03f3f17a3d6\">ingredient<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"0ef0eb3b-705b-4bb3-9fac-5059e695e81e\">common to all<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"ef6b9f29-c215-4729-9201-4552b9b3cc2f\">the earliest soaps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325909\" id=\"question-wrapper-325909\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"abc9dc28-f634-4834-b375-c1498026ec14\">The first soaps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b1c23ba4-354b-4651-ac43-56265a8730d8\">within the reach of ordinary people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the flow chart below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>5-10</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>Soap Production</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"f05e824f-ead6-4873-a9cb-67a9dae6220e\">Heating the starting ingredients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a5873ef2-13d0-47d8-9991-2adbae396e28\">gets rid of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> (5)________.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>Adding a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"820e277b-585f-40ca-b262-76b8924f02a5\">strong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (6)________ brings about saponification, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"98cbbb4e-a97f-4909-b0d9-cf7fac6442b4\">yields fatty acids and glycerine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>Glycerine is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"38b77e87-07d8-4b7a-a3ce-c079fe5f47de\">treated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, then undergoes (7)________ and purification before use in other industries.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"3c60e19a-4ea6-46b0-ad41-6144443492b8\">The qualities required of the finished bar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> determine the (8)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"aed53ec6-f5a5-43fa-afca-47878f592fa8\">level<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of the pellets produced by vacuum spray drying.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"96f5268c-f695-4e62-a933-91ac2f9aff88\">Colour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, (9)___ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"e1c98297-2c10-40b9-b0ec-e4133acac672\">other components<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b78c4d99-f776-41de-9234-9cb24d768419\">are mixed into the pellets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> by an amalgamator.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>Homogenisation, refining and blending take place.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>After cutting, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"69d250ce-c480-4913-8c71-2e65f2158046\">the final shape is produced by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> a (10)___.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325910\" id=\"question-wrapper-325910\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">impurities</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325911\" id=\"question-wrapper-325911\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">alkali</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325912\" id=\"question-wrapper-325912\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">evaporation</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325913\" id=\"question-wrapper-325913\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">moisture (content)</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325914\" id=\"question-wrapper-325914\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">fragrance</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325915\" id=\"question-wrapper-325915\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(soap) press</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>11-13</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325916\" id=\"question-wrapper-325916\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"2e9b5c71-0abc-4216-8aeb-10e7e4ec4049\">More complex<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> soap (11)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"9fdcc69b-a250-4364-9c1d-a69b2c620a11\">were developed as a result of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ed97820e-2b2b-414b-ab4d-551c9b198535\">improvements in technology and chemistry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">recipes</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325917\" id=\"question-wrapper-325917\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"ad754c80-1621-4dcf-9ebd-8f30a0bf88d9\">The absence of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> a (12)_______ on the skin after washing is one benefit of using a shower gel.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">residue</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325918\" id=\"question-wrapper-325918\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"eb3b73ee-a705-4430-a161-3d8e08934ddf\">A poor pH balance in soap can cause<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)_______ for users.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(skin) irritations</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b5e6c159-c121-42df-9740-0599a19c034a","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"widely used","passagePhrase":"appeal to a wide"},{"uid":"ca523588-5c94-4db8-b52a-853aa2b8a247","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Europeans","passagePhrase":"European"},{"uid":"b5e6c159-c121-42df-9740-0599a19c034a ca523588-5c94-4db8-b52a-853aa2b8a247","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"population"},{"uid":"ef6b9f29-c215-4729-9201-4552b9b3cc2f","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"the earliest soaps","passagePhrase":"The first soap makers"},{"uid":"0ef0eb3b-705b-4bb3-9fac-5059e695e81e","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"common to all","passagePhrase":"All of them"},{"uid":"3cfc8565-00e9-4086-b6fe-b03f3f17a3d6","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"ingredient","passagePhrase":"made soap by mixing"},{"uid":"abc9dc28-f634-4834-b375-c1498026ec14","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"The first soaps","passagePhrase":"early soap"},{"uid":"f05e824f-ead6-4873-a9cb-67a9dae6220e","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Heating the starting ingredients","passagePhrase":"heat the raw materials"},{"uid":"a5873ef2-13d0-47d8-9991-2adbae396e28","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"gets rid of","passagePhrase":"remove"},{"uid":"820e277b-585f-40ca-b262-76b8924f02a5","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"strong","passagePhrase":"powerful"},{"uid":"98cbbb4e-a97f-4909-b0d9-cf7fac6442b4","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"yields fatty acids and glycerine","passagePhrase":"releases the fatty acids ... and a valuable by-product, glycerine"},{"uid":"38b77e87-07d8-4b7a-a3ce-c079fe5f47de","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"treated","passagePhrase":"recovered by"},{"uid":"aed53ec6-f5a5-43fa-afca-47878f592fa8","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"level","passagePhrase":"content"},{"uid":"3c60e19a-4ea6-46b0-ad41-6144443492b8","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"The qualities required of the finished bar","passagePhrase":"the desired characteristics of the soap bar"},{"uid":"b78c4d99-f776-41de-9234-9cb24d768419","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"are mixed into the pellets","passagePhrase":"the soap pellets are blended together with"},{"uid":"96f5268c-f695-4e62-a933-91ac2f9aff88","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Colour","passagePhrase":"shades"},{"uid":"e1c98297-2c10-40b9-b0ec-e4133acac672","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"other components","passagePhrase":"all other ingredients"},{"uid":"69d250ce-c480-4913-8c71-2e65f2158046","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the final shape is produced by","passagePhrase":"stamped into its final shape in"},{"uid":"ed97820e-2b2b-414b-ab4d-551c9b198535","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"improvements in technology and chemistry","passagePhrase":"technological and chemical advancements"},{"uid":"9fdcc69b-a250-4364-9c1d-a69b2c620a11","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"were developed as a result of","passagePhrase":"enabled ... to start experimenting with"},{"uid":"2e9b5c71-0abc-4216-8aeb-10e7e4ec4049","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"More complex","passagePhrase":"more complicated"},{"uid":"ad754c80-1621-4dcf-9ebd-8f30a0bf88d9","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"The absence of","passagePhrase":"do not leave"},{"uid":"eb3b73ee-a705-4430-a161-3d8e08934ddf","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"A poor pH balance in soap can cause","passagePhrase":"a balanced pH state ... do not cause"}]},"reading_u2_77":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 14-26</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Bluefin Tuna</span></b></p><p><span>Three species of bluefin tuna are found around the world – Northern or Atlantic bluefin tuna, Southern bluefin tuna, and Pacific bluefin tuna. Atlantic bluefin tuna is divided into two stocks. The western stock is harvested off the coast of North America by Canada, Japan, and the United States, and the eastern stock is harvested off the coasts of Europe and Africa and in the Mediterranean Sea.</span></p><p><span>Fisheries for bluefin tuna date back thousands of years in the Mediterranean, but did not emerge in the western Atlantic until the 1950s. Although today they are widely known as the most prized species of tuna, there was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"98617f0d-1fb5-4730-aec4-a6f9fa0f679f\">no commercial market for western Atlantic bluefin tuna<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"6511b2da-c758-45c5-92c9-498dfa61de4b\">until then<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. In fact, fishermen <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"edf35367-d675-4d5f-9c2d-2f660a9d34a9\">regarded giant bluefin tuna as a nuisance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> because of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"6a9be4af-dcff-459c-8036-85605e80d9cc\">the damage they caused to fishing gear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. However, as sushi and sashimi markets in Japan developed in the 1970s and 1980s, the demand and prices for bluefin tuna increased, and so did fishing pressure around the world.</span></p><p><span>Since bluefin tuna are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"983ab7f9-54df-4853-886d-c6131576195c\">late to mature, slow-growing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, and long-lived, they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"70fa0dc7-75e6-4537-a807-da1059dec92c\">especially susceptible to fishing pressure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> compared to faster-growing, more productive species. Bluefin tuna grow more slowly than other tuna and have a long lifespan of up to 20 years or more, and they generally do not spawn until they are about eight years old. Because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9220890c-db5c-4e75-9a09-9f6d3969f4b6\">many nations harvest bluefin tuna<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"6b89fd03-ad56-4e87-8c96-ced768b883f4\">effective conservation and management<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of this resource depend on strong international cooperation. The United States has taken many steps to conserve and manage US fisheries for Atlantic bluefin tuna since the early 1980s. It is due in part to these measures and US efforts internationally that Atlantic bluefin tuna are no longer subject to overfishing.</span></p><p><span>Today, international fisheries for western Atlantic bluefin tuna are highly regulated. The most recent annual catch level set is expected to support continued growth and recovery of the stock. Strict controls are in place to ensure compliance on the water, in port, and at the marketplace <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"04dd8f32-1a91-4c19-a4f6-fda2fd79b3f1\">through the implementation of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the catch documentation scheme, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"b08b2505-c8b5-438d-8489-4e3009f004b8\">allows trade tracking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"aa93362f-850d-4da1-b905-a2b42746f0a4\">individual shipments of fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Finally, because the western and eastern stocks mix, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e377deb5-5855-43c4-b3ee-cd9efba602d1\">western Atlantic bluefin tuna are also affected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> by the fishing pressure that took place <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"58ec17dd-be54-42a7-a151-287b15360ef0\">in the eastern Atlantic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>/Mediterranean during the 1990s and early 2000s. However, in recent years, catches in the eastern Atlantic have been reduced to levels consistent with scientific advice, and new monitoring and control measures have been adopted to address illegal, unreported, and unregulated fishing on that stock. Scientists advise that improved stock conservation in the eastern Atlantic would likely benefit the western stock as well.</span></p><p><span>The news is not so good for bluefin tuna in other parts of the world. Data recently released show that there are almost no more bluefin tuna to be fished in some of the oldest fishing grounds, especially in the western Mediterranean. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b4490f9e-1c7d-40e0-b0be-62fa750605ee\">Around Spain's Balearic Islands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b7a706ff-40ea-42d4-b247-9354ee1c71be\">catches of bluefin tuna<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> are down to only 15 per cent of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b5a80a65-0ea3-4aab-9390-e2429c6ff9e9\">what they were<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> just <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"bf784863-1165-4d89-be66-fc2603fba7f6\">a decade ago<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. In Australia, there is a similar story: the southern bluefin tuna stock is at historically low levels, with less than 10 per cent of the virgin stock left, and little significant progress has been made in preventing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0d09ffd7-b76a-402f-aa68-c73117743637\">the overharvesting that is driving the species further towards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ddb8147d-0f7e-4646-b6c7-c25359b1f0e7\">extinction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Because of the value of bluefin tuna, scientists are trying to work out ways of farming the species. The vision is to have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"859c935b-b000-4be0-ab72-2109fd68b5bc\">huge land-based tanks holding bluefin tuna<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that spawn <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"93cb8ff0-c358-49fd-b001-32f33cbf09e1\">year-round<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> on demand, producing millions of eggs. These eggs would hatch and grow into a plentiful supply of tuna. There are, however, problems associated with rearing bluefin tuna. First of all, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"b2dfe3a1-4c78-41c2-9503-c351498af41d\">the larvae<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> that hatch from the eggs are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"ca117425-b6a4-4062-a8ff-4ec02646f0be\">extremely fragile<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Because of their heavy heads, the larvae tend to sink downwards. If they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"ca117425-b6a4-4062-a8ff-4ec02646f0be\">hit the bottom of a tank<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, the shock is too much and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"ca117425-b6a4-4062-a8ff-4ec02646f0be\">they do not survive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Beyond this, a significant problem is the appetite of the bluefin tuna. A bluefin tuna's natural diet consists of large quantities of other fish. Just supplying the amount of fish needed for bluefin tuna to grow would be difficult and expensive, without even considering the harm to the environment of taking that many wild feed fish from the sea. Right now, there are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"8922d065-5234-4e43-94b9-0d1b5b069541\">tuna ranches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> that capture young tuna in the ocean and then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"85b03f71-a5b6-4848-a78b-caecc6152696\">fatten them up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in big net pens. These ranches feed their tuna about 15 pounds of fish, such as sardines or mackerel, for each additional pound of tuna that can be sold to consumers. This kind of tuna production is environmentally costly.</span></p><p><span>Some scientists have theorised that it will be possible to reduce this ratio or even create tuna feed that does not rely so heavily on other fish as an ingredient. The effect on the taste of the bluefin tuna's flesh, though, may make the product less valuable and defeat the whole point of producing bluefin tuna cheaply.</span></p><p><span>Other experts say that these problems show that bluefin tuna farming is not the path to follow, as farming bluefin tuna just increases the population of a predator species that itself demands a lot of food. It might do more good to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"e3884643-7b7a-4515-89ff-06dc8531d793\">eat a little lower on the marine food chain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. People could eat more mussels or sardines and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f4c5f963-abac-4f05-9d2e-9982e699acad\">let more tuna roam free to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> sustainably caught within quota systems and premium-priced.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending (</span><b><span>A – E</span></b><span>) below.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter (</span></i><i><b><span>A – E</span></b></i><i><span>) in answer boxes </span></i><i><b><span>14-16</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A.</span></b> <span>they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"983ab7f9-54df-4853-886d-c6131576195c\">take a long time to grow to adulthood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"6a9be4af-dcff-459c-8036-85605e80d9cc\">the fish damaged their equipment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C.</span></b> <span>the fish are not found in freshwater.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> the fish were suspected to cause various types of cancer.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> there was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"98617f0d-1fb5-4730-aec4-a6f9fa0f679f\">no significant market<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> for them.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325919\" id=\"question-wrapper-325919\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Unlike today, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"98617f0d-1fb5-4730-aec4-a6f9fa0f679f\">western Atlantic bluefin tuna had little commercial value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"6511b2da-c758-45c5-92c9-498dfa61de4b\">before the 1950s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> because</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325920\" id=\"question-wrapper-325920\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Fishermen in the past <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"edf35367-d675-4d5f-9c2d-2f660a9d34a9\">did not want to catch bluefin tuna<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, because </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325921\" id=\"question-wrapper-325921\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Bluefin tuna are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"70fa0dc7-75e6-4537-a807-da1059dec92c\">extremely vulnerable to overfishing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> because </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>17-21</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325922\" id=\"question-wrapper-325922\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>(17)_______ between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9220890c-db5c-4e75-9a09-9f6d3969f4b6\">the relevant countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> will be needed if bluefin tuna resources are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"6b89fd03-ad56-4e87-8c96-ced768b883f4\">to be managed in a sustainable fashion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(strong) (international) co(-)operation</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325923\" id=\"question-wrapper-325923\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"aa93362f-850d-4da1-b905-a2b42746f0a4\">Each shipment of bluefin tuna<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"b08b2505-c8b5-438d-8489-4e3009f004b8\">can be tracked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"04dd8f32-1a91-4c19-a4f6-fda2fd79b3f1\">by using<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the (18)_______</span><b><span>. </span></b></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">catch documentation scheme</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325924\" id=\"question-wrapper-325924\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>(19)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"58ec17dd-be54-42a7-a151-287b15360ef0\">on the eastern stock<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e377deb5-5855-43c4-b3ee-cd9efba602d1\">also affected the western Atlantic bluefin tuna population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) (fishing) pressure</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325925\" id=\"question-wrapper-325925\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b4490f9e-1c7d-40e0-b0be-62fa750605ee\">Near the Balearic Islands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b7a706ff-40ea-42d4-b247-9354ee1c71be\">the amount of bluefin tuna caught<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> is now (20)_______ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b5a80a65-0ea3-4aab-9390-e2429c6ff9e9\">the level recorded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"bf784863-1165-4d89-be66-fc2603fba7f6\">ten years earlier<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(only) 15% [OR] (only) 15 per( )cent</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325926\" id=\"question-wrapper-325926\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>(21)_______ is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ddb8147d-0f7e-4646-b6c7-c25359b1f0e7\">a real danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0d09ffd7-b76a-402f-aa68-c73117743637\">due to the overharvesting of the southern bluefin tuna<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">extinction</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the words in the box below.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>22-26</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>eggs</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>protecting </span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>sea</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>luxury </span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>simple</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>fragility</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>strength</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>reproducing</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>juveniles</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>predatory</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><b><span>FARMING BLUEFIN TUNA</span></b></p><p><span>Scientists are working on developing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"859c935b-b000-4be0-ab72-2109fd68b5bc\">large-scale bluefin tuna farms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> to rear them from egg to adulthood, with fish (22)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"93cb8ff0-c358-49fd-b001-32f33cbf09e1\">all year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. Obstacles are the (23)________ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"b2dfe3a1-4c78-41c2-9503-c351498af41d\">bluefin larvae<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, which means they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"ca117425-b6a4-4062-a8ff-4ec02646f0be\">die easily<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, and the amount of fish needed to feed them until they reach harvest size. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"8922d065-5234-4e43-94b9-0d1b5b069541\">Some operating farms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> capture (24)________ to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"85b03f71-a5b6-4848-a78b-caecc6152696\">feed them up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, but this too is environmentally damaging.</span></p><p><span>One solution is to use a non-fish-based feed, but this may affect the product’s taste. It could be that bluefin tuna are not meant to be farmed and that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"e3884643-7b7a-4515-89ff-06dc8531d793\">people should eat fewer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> (25)________ fish and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f4c5f963-abac-4f05-9d2e-9982e699acad\">allow the bluefin tuna to remain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> a (26)________ meal.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325927\" id=\"question-wrapper-325927\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">reproducing</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325928\" id=\"question-wrapper-325928\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">fragility</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325929\" id=\"question-wrapper-325929\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">juveniles</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325930\" id=\"question-wrapper-325930\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">predatory</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325931\" id=\"question-wrapper-325931\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">luxury</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"98617f0d-1fb5-4730-aec4-a6f9fa0f679f","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"no significant market ... western Atlantic bluefin tuna had little commercial value","passagePhrase":"no commercial market for western Atlantic bluefin tuna"},{"uid":"6511b2da-c758-45c5-92c9-498dfa61de4b","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"before the 1950s","passagePhrase":"until then"},{"uid":"edf35367-d675-4d5f-9c2d-2f660a9d34a9","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"did not want to catch bluefin tuna","passagePhrase":"regarded giant bluefin tuna as a nuisance"},{"uid":"6a9be4af-dcff-459c-8036-85605e80d9cc","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the fish damaged their equipment","passagePhrase":"the damage they caused to fishing gear"},{"uid":"983ab7f9-54df-4853-886d-c6131576195c","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"take a long time to grow to adulthood","passagePhrase":"late to mature, slow-growing"},{"uid":"70fa0dc7-75e6-4537-a807-da1059dec92c","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"extremely vulnerable to overfishing","passagePhrase":"especially susceptible to fishing pressure"},{"uid":"9220890c-db5c-4e75-9a09-9f6d3969f4b6","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"the relevant countries","passagePhrase":"many nations harvest bluefin tuna"},{"uid":"6b89fd03-ad56-4e87-8c96-ced768b883f4","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"to be managed in a sustainable fashion","passagePhrase":"effective conservation and management"},{"uid":"04dd8f32-1a91-4c19-a4f6-fda2fd79b3f1","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"by using","passagePhrase":"through the implementation of"},{"uid":"b08b2505-c8b5-438d-8489-4e3009f004b8","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"can be tracked","passagePhrase":"allows trade tracking"},{"uid":"aa93362f-850d-4da1-b905-a2b42746f0a4","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Each shipment of bluefin tuna","passagePhrase":"individual shipments of fish"},{"uid":"e377deb5-5855-43c4-b3ee-cd9efba602d1","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"also affected the western Atlantic bluefin tuna population","passagePhrase":"western Atlantic bluefin tuna are also affected"},{"uid":"58ec17dd-be54-42a7-a151-287b15360ef0","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"on the eastern stock","passagePhrase":"in the eastern Atlantic"},{"uid":"b4490f9e-1c7d-40e0-b0be-62fa750605ee","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Near the Balearic Islands","passagePhrase":"Around Spain's Balearic Islands"},{"uid":"b7a706ff-40ea-42d4-b247-9354ee1c71be","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the amount of bluefin tuna caught","passagePhrase":"catches of bluefin tuna"},{"uid":"b5a80a65-0ea3-4aab-9390-e2429c6ff9e9","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the level recorded","passagePhrase":"what they were"},{"uid":"bf784863-1165-4d89-be66-fc2603fba7f6","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"ten years earlier","passagePhrase":"a decade ago"},{"uid":"0d09ffd7-b76a-402f-aa68-c73117743637","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"due to the overharvesting of the southern bluefin tuna","passagePhrase":"the overharvesting that is driving the species further towards"},{"uid":"ddb8147d-0f7e-4646-b6c7-c25359b1f0e7","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"a real danger","passagePhrase":"extinction"},{"uid":"859c935b-b000-4be0-ab72-2109fd68b5bc","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"large-scale bluefin tuna farms","passagePhrase":"huge land-based tanks holding bluefin tuna"},{"uid":"93cb8ff0-c358-49fd-b001-32f33cbf09e1","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"all year","passagePhrase":"year-round"},{"uid":"b2dfe3a1-4c78-41c2-9503-c351498af41d","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"bluefin larvae","passagePhrase":"the larvae"},{"uid":"ca117425-b6a4-4062-a8ff-4ec02646f0be","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"die easily","passagePhrase":"extremely fragile ... hit the bottom of a tank ... they do not survive"},{"uid":"8922d065-5234-4e43-94b9-0d1b5b069541","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Some operating farms","passagePhrase":"tuna ranches"},{"uid":"85b03f71-a5b6-4848-a78b-caecc6152696","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"feed them up","passagePhrase":"fatten them up"},{"uid":"e3884643-7b7a-4515-89ff-06dc8531d793","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"people should eat fewer","passagePhrase":"eat a little lower on the marine food chain"},{"uid":"f4c5f963-abac-4f05-9d2e-9982e699acad","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"allow the bluefin tuna to remain","passagePhrase":"let more tuna roam free to be"}]},"reading_u2_78":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 27-40</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Tickling and Laughter</span></b></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> The fingers of an outstretched arm are nearing your body; you <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e4f231fe-22b2-42fc-bd34-7a44448e52bd\">bend away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e4f231fe-22b2-42fc-bd34-7a44448e52bd\">folding your torso<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e4f231fe-22b2-42fc-bd34-7a44448e52bd\">tilting your head to your shoulder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"be97095d-9da0-41b8-8f06-f9ad43fe51cd\">in hopes that you won't get tickled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. But the inevitable occurs: you are tickled and, in hysterics, you chuckle, titter, and burst into uncontrollable laughter. Why do we laugh when we are tickled?</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Tickling is caused by a light sensation across our skin. At times this light sensation can cause itching; however, most of the time it causes giggling. If a feather is gently moved across the surface of the skin, it can also cause tickling and giggling. Heavy laughter is caused by someone or something placing repeated pressure on a person and tickling a particular area. The spots most often tickled are the feet, toes, sides, underarms, and neck, which cause a great deal of laughter. Yngve Zotterman of the Karolinska Institute has found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c3746208-37da-4d2c-a11e-9027a3573946\">tickling sensations involve signals from nerve fibers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. These nerve fibers are associated with pain and touch. Zotterman has also discovered that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3c31474a-7599-4a5b-86cd-f3b801fffd6a\">tickling sensations are associated not only with nerve fibers but also with the sense of touch<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, because people who have lost pain sensations still laugh when tickled. But really, why do we laugh? Why are we not able to tickle ourselves? What part of the brain is responsible for laughter and humor? Why do we say some people have no sense of humor?</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> Research has shown that laughter is more than just a person's voice and movement, and that it requires the coordination of many muscles throughout the body. Laughter also increases blood pressure and heart rate, changes breathing, reduces levels of certain neurochemicals (catecholamines and hormones), and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"c05c1fc4-4b74-400f-8c48-17183d77d023\">provides a boost to the immune system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. Can laughter improve health? It may be a good way for people to relax, because muscle tension is reduced after laughing. Human tests have found some evidence that humorous videos and tapes can reduce feelings of pain, prevent negative stress reactions, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"c05c1fc4-4b74-400f-8c48-17183d77d023\">boost the brain's biological battle against infection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> Researchers believe we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"717eeaf0-c8fb-4376-876c-c16762d01c0a\">process humor and laughter through<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"18c0c9a4-feb6-410c-8e53-d83993de11bf\">a complex pathway of brain activity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> that encompasses three main brain components. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"f0672895-d99e-4576-add1-e4787c897b07\">one new study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, researchers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"7f0b8705-6c55-4f97-b70b-70a49cbaa228\">used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> imaging equipment <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"7f0b8705-6c55-4f97-b70b-70a49cbaa228\">to photograph the brain activity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of healthy volunteers while they underwent the sidesplitting assignment of reading written jokes, viewing cartoons from </span><i><span>The New Yorker</span></i><span> magazine as well as </span><i><span>The Far Side</span></i><span>, and listening to digital recordings of laughter. Preliminary results indicate that the humor-processing pathway includes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0883542e-d20c-4415-96e8-b2f4f77f06ea\">parts of the frontal lobe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"ad97182d-90d5-4c62-bea5-291317d94d43\">important for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> cognitive processing; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0883542e-d20c-4415-96e8-b2f4f77f06ea\">the supplementary motor area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, important for movement; and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0883542e-d20c-4415-96e8-b2f4f77f06ea\">the nucleus accumbens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"ad97182d-90d5-4c62-bea5-291317d94d43\">associated with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> pleasure. Investigations support the notion that parts of the frontal lobe are involved in humor. Subjects' brains were imaged while they were listening to jokes. An area of the frontal lobe was activated only when they thought a joke was funny. In a study that compared healthy individuals with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8500a1ee-1580-49a8-bbfa-90db40a6cf90\">people who had damage to their frontal lobes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8500a1ee-1580-49a8-bbfa-90db40a6cf90\">the subjects with damaged frontal lobes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"96a4c515-a22e-4e27-824f-988cb87a6bf6\">were more likely to choose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> the wrong punch lines to write jokes and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"20cd1686-071b-4677-b048-db34dae37aec\">didn't laugh or smile as much at funny cartoons or jokes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Even though we may know more about which parts of the brain are responsible for humor, it is still hard to explain why we don't laugh or giggle when we tickle ourselves. Darwin theorized in </span><i><span>The Expression of the Emotions in Man and Animals</span></i><span> that there was a link between tickling and laughter because of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"855c2dec-d1af-4b37-80ad-3893e85e6092\">the anticipation of pleasure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Because we cannot tickle ourselves and cause laughter, Darwin speculated that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"0f6b6d5e-d05b-46ee-ac31-bf2551047374\">the surprise of another person touching a sensitive spot<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> must be what causes laughter. Some scientists believe that laughing caused by tickling is a built-in reflex that even babies have. If we tickle ourselves in the same spot where our friend tickled us, we do not laugh as we did previously. The information sent to our spinal cord and brain should be exactly the same. Apparently, for tickling to work, the brain needs tension and surprise. When we tickle ourselves, we know exactly what will happen—there is no tension or surprise. How the brain uses this information about tension and surprise is still a mystery, but there is some evidence that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e8bd7a89-8388-4892-8249-50650c1277a7\">the cerebellum<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"dbfaf6a1-6e9c-442a-bf98-8a9a3cfb1663\">be involved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, because one part of the brain tells another: \"It's just you. Don't get excited.\" Investigations suggest that during self-tickling, the cerebellum tells an area called <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e8bd7a89-8388-4892-8249-50650c1277a7\">the somatosensory cortex<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> what sensation to expect, and that dampens the tickling sensation. It looks as if the killjoy is found in the cerebellum. Further explorations to understand tickling and laughter were conducted by Christenfeld and Harris. In \"The Mystery of Ticklish Laughter\" and \"Can a Machine Tickle?\", they explained that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"a6521671-f6ed-477c-b2c7-467ffdde0276\">people laughed equally whether tickled by a machine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> or by a person. The participants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"68c9006a-6aa3-40b4-b524-d9bcac178354\">were not aware of who or what was tickling them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>; however, the laughter resounded equally. It is suggested that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e5122b6a-a80f-48f7-be66-92eff1b7927c\">the tickling response is a reflex<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, which, as Darwin suggested earlier, is dependent on the element of surprise.</span></p><p><b><span>F.</span></b><span> Damage to any one part of the brain may affect one's overall ability to process humor. Peter Derks, a professor of psychology, conducted his research with a group of scientists at NASA-Langley in Hampton. Using a sophisticated electroencephalogram (EEG), they measured the brain activity of 10 people exposed to humorous stimuli. How quickly our brain recognizes the incongruity involved in most humor and attaches an abstract meaning to it determines whether we laugh. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f4144ee4-f897-4989-8b4f-52b5350c4f71\">different people find different jokes funny<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. That can be due to a number of factors, including differences in personality, intelligence, mental state, and probably mood. But according to Derks, the majority of people recognize when a situation is meant to be humorous. In a series of experiments, he noticed that several patients recovering from brain injuries could not distinguish between something funny and something not.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> Dr. Shibata of the University of Rochester School of Medicine said our neurons get tickled when we hear a joke. The brain's \"funny bone\" is located in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"fb9be5a1-4b5f-485d-abcf-ea6659d1e4e2\">the right frontal lobe just above the right eye<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> and appears critical to our ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"65c7f6c7-99f8-47a1-b508-553ef63c3d60\">recognize a joke<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Dr. Shibata gave his patients MRI scans to measure brain activity, trying to find out what part of the brain is particularly active during the punch line of a joke as opposed to the rest of the joke, and during the funny parts of cartoons in comparison to the parts that are not funny. The jokes \"tickled\" the frontal lobes. The scans also showed activity in the nucleus accumbens, which is likely related to our feeling of mirth after hearing a good joke and our \"addiction\" to humor. While his research was about humor, the results could help lead to answers and solutions for depression. Parts of the brain that are active during humor are actually abnormal in patients with depression. Eventually, brain scans might be used to assess <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"611ecfec-35c5-4e58-ac9a-c1112375742f\">patients with depression and other mood disorders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. The research may also explain why some stroke victims lose their sense of humor or suffer from other personality changes. The same part of the brain is also associated with social and emotional judgment and planning.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>The Reading Passage has 7 paragraphs, </span><b><span>A-G</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write the appropriate letter, </span></i><i><b><span>A-G</span></b></i><i><span>, in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>27-33</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>NB</span></b> <i><span>You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325932\" id=\"question-wrapper-325932\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"fb9be5a1-4b5f-485d-abcf-ea6659d1e4e2\">The exact spot in the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> that allows us to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"65c7f6c7-99f8-47a1-b508-553ef63c3d60\">identify a joke<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325933\" id=\"question-wrapper-325933\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Laughter <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"c05c1fc4-4b74-400f-8c48-17183d77d023\">enhances immunity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325934\" id=\"question-wrapper-325934\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e4f231fe-22b2-42fc-bd34-7a44448e52bd\">The physical avoidance reaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"be97095d-9da0-41b8-8f06-f9ad43fe51cd\">the possibility of tickling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325935\" id=\"question-wrapper-325935\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e8bd7a89-8388-4892-8249-50650c1277a7\">Parts of the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"dbfaf6a1-6e9c-442a-bf98-8a9a3cfb1663\">responsible for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e5122b6a-a80f-48f7-be66-92eff1b7927c\">tickling reflex<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325936\" id=\"question-wrapper-325936\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"18c0c9a4-feb6-410c-8e53-d83993de11bf\">Neuropsychological mechanisms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"717eeaf0-c8fb-4376-876c-c16762d01c0a\">by which humor and laughter work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325937\" id=\"question-wrapper-325937\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c3746208-37da-4d2c-a11e-9027a3573946\">The connection between tickling and nerve fibers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325938\" id=\"question-wrapper-325938\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"611ecfec-35c5-4e58-ac9a-c1112375742f\">Patients with emotional disorders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following researchers (listed </span><b><span>34-37</span></b><span>) and findings (listed </span><b><span>A-F</span></b><span>).</span></p><p><span>Match each researcher with the correct finding(s).</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>34-37</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"0f6b6d5e-d05b-46ee-ac31-bf2551047374\">The surprise factor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, combined with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"855c2dec-d1af-4b37-80ad-3893e85e6092\">the anticipation of pleasure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, causes laughter when tickled.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Laughing caused by tickling is a built-in reflex even babies have.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"a6521671-f6ed-477c-b2c7-467ffdde0276\">People also laugh when tickled by a machine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> if they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"68c9006a-6aa3-40b4-b524-d9bcac178354\">not aware of it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f4144ee4-f897-4989-8b4f-52b5350c4f71\">People have different tastes for jokes and humour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Jokes and funny cartoons activate the frontal lobes.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><b><span>F.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3c31474a-7599-4a5b-86cd-f3b801fffd6a\">Tickling sensations involve more than nerve fibers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325939\" id=\"question-wrapper-325939\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Darwin </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325940\" id=\"question-wrapper-325940\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Christenfeld and Harris </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325941\" id=\"question-wrapper-325941\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Yngve Zotterman </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325942\" id=\"question-wrapper-325942\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Peter Derks </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below using </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></b><span> from the passage for each blank.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>38-40</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><span>Researchers believe three brain components to be involved in the processing of humor and laughter. Results from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"f0672895-d99e-4576-add1-e4787c897b07\">one study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"7f0b8705-6c55-4f97-b70b-70a49cbaa228\">using the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> (38)________ indicate that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0883542e-d20c-4415-96e8-b2f4f77f06ea\">parts of the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"ad97182d-90d5-4c62-bea5-291317d94d43\">responsible for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> (39)________, movement and pleasure are involved through a sophisticated pathway. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8500a1ee-1580-49a8-bbfa-90db40a6cf90\">People with frontal-lobe damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"96a4c515-a22e-4e27-824f-988cb87a6bf6\">had greater chances of picking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> (40)________ of jokes or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"20cd1686-071b-4677-b048-db34dae37aec\">did not respond to funny cartoons or jokes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325943\" id=\"question-wrapper-325943\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">imaging equipment</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325944\" id=\"question-wrapper-325944\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">cognitive processing</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325945\" id=\"question-wrapper-325945\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) wrong punch( )lines</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e4f231fe-22b2-42fc-bd34-7a44448e52bd","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"The physical avoidance reaction","passagePhrase":"bend away ... folding your torso ... tilting your head to your shoulder"},{"uid":"be97095d-9da0-41b8-8f06-f9ad43fe51cd","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"the possibility of tickling","passagePhrase":"in hopes that you won't get tickled"},{"uid":"c3746208-37da-4d2c-a11e-9027a3573946","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"The connection between tickling and nerve fibers","passagePhrase":"tickling sensations involve signals from nerve fibers"},{"uid":"3c31474a-7599-4a5b-86cd-f3b801fffd6a","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Tickling sensations involve more than nerve fibers","passagePhrase":"tickling sensations are associated not only with nerve fibers but also with the sense of touch"},{"uid":"c05c1fc4-4b74-400f-8c48-17183d77d023","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"enhances immunity","passagePhrase":"provides a boost to the immune system ... boost the brain's biological battle against infection"},{"uid":"717eeaf0-c8fb-4376-876c-c16762d01c0a","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"by which humor and laughter work","passagePhrase":"process humor and laughter through"},{"uid":"18c0c9a4-feb6-410c-8e53-d83993de11bf","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Neuropsychological mechanisms","passagePhrase":"a complex pathway of brain activity"},{"uid":"f0672895-d99e-4576-add1-e4787c897b07","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"one study","passagePhrase":"one new study"},{"uid":"7f0b8705-6c55-4f97-b70b-70a49cbaa228","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"using the brain","passagePhrase":"used ... to photograph the brain activity"},{"uid":"0883542e-d20c-4415-96e8-b2f4f77f06ea","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"parts of the brain","passagePhrase":"parts of the frontal lobe ... the supplementary motor area ... the nucleus accumbens"},{"uid":"ad97182d-90d5-4c62-bea5-291317d94d43","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"responsible for","passagePhrase":"important for ... associated with"},{"uid":"8500a1ee-1580-49a8-bbfa-90db40a6cf90","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"People with frontal-lobe damage","passagePhrase":"people who had damage to their frontal lobes ... the subjects with damaged frontal lobes"},{"uid":"96a4c515-a22e-4e27-824f-988cb87a6bf6","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"had greater chances of picking","passagePhrase":"were more likely to choose"},{"uid":"20cd1686-071b-4677-b048-db34dae37aec","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"did not respond to funny cartoons or jokes","passagePhrase":"didn't laugh or smile as much at funny cartoons or jokes"},{"uid":"855c2dec-d1af-4b37-80ad-3893e85e6092","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"the anticipation of pleasure","passagePhrase":"the anticipation of pleasure"},{"uid":"0f6b6d5e-d05b-46ee-ac31-bf2551047374","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"The surprise factor","passagePhrase":"the surprise of another person touching a sensitive spot"},{"uid":"e8bd7a89-8388-4892-8249-50650c1277a7","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Parts of the brain","passagePhrase":"the cerebellum ... the somatosensory cortex"},{"uid":"dbfaf6a1-6e9c-442a-bf98-8a9a3cfb1663","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"responsible for","passagePhrase":"be involved"},{"uid":"a6521671-f6ed-477c-b2c7-467ffdde0276","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"People also laugh when tickled by a machine","passagePhrase":"people laughed equally whether tickled by a machine"},{"uid":"68c9006a-6aa3-40b4-b524-d9bcac178354","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"not aware of it","passagePhrase":"were not aware of who or what was tickling them"},{"uid":"e5122b6a-a80f-48f7-be66-92eff1b7927c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"tickling reflex","passagePhrase":"the tickling response is a reflex"},{"uid":"f4144ee4-f897-4989-8b4f-52b5350c4f71","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"People have different tastes for jokes and humour","passagePhrase":"different people find different jokes funny"},{"uid":"fb9be5a1-4b5f-485d-abcf-ea6659d1e4e2","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"The exact spot in the brain","passagePhrase":"the right frontal lobe just above the right eye"},{"uid":"65c7f6c7-99f8-47a1-b508-553ef63c3d60","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"identify a joke","passagePhrase":"recognize a joke"},{"uid":"611ecfec-35c5-4e58-ac9a-c1112375742f","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Patients with emotional disorders","passagePhrase":"patients with depression and other mood disorders"}]},"reading_u2_79":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions</span></b> <b><span>1-13</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Igloo</span></b></p><p><span>The igloo is the traditional shelter of the Inuit living in the far northern regions. It is built of blocks of snow in a circular shape, in which the walls curve inward towards the top to form a snow vault with a self-supporting arched ceiling. An outstanding example of human ingenuity and adaptability to the environment, the igloo retains heat and protects against the cold, since snow and ice act as excellent insulation. The design includes a tunnel entrance that forms a cold trap to preserve heat inside. The sleeping and sitting areas are raised above this and so maintain a higher temperature.</span></p><p><span>A similar construction is the 'quinzhee', which is a shelter made by hollowing out a pile of settled snow and is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"3d537792-a946-4334-926a-406cad6b656d\">intended only for temporary use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. In contemporary times, this type of snow shelter has become popular among those who enjoy winter camping, as well as in survival situations. Some contemporary Inuit, though, continue to use igloos, especially as temporary shelters while hunting. However, the warming climate of the early twenty-first century has reduced the availability of appropriate snow for igloo construction. Although the traditional art of igloo construction by the Inuit may have declined, the igloo and variations upon it, such as ice hotels, have gained in popularity among those who enjoy the winter experience.</span></p><p><span>The word 'igloo' in the Inuit language simply means 'house', and the Inuit do not restrict the use of this term exclusively to snow houses, but include traditional tents, sod houses, homes constructed of driftwood, and modern buildings. Although the origin of the igloo may have been lost in antiquity, it is known that the Inuit have constructed snow igloos for hundreds of years. For people living in an area where snow and ice predominate, particularly in the long, dark winter above the Arctic Circle, the igloo is the perfect shelter. Snow is used because the air pockets trapped in it make it an excellent insulator. Outside, temperatures may be as low as minus 45 degrees Celsius, but inside an igloo, the temperature may <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"db5ee16c-ba4a-4e76-b8cc-095411c3cd85\">range from minus 7 degrees Celsius to 16 degrees Celsius<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> when warmed by body heat alone. A highly functional shelter, the igloo is also aesthetically pleasing, with a shape that is both strong and beautiful.</span></p><p><span>There is a fairly standard procedure for building an igloo. The first thing to do is to find a good spot. It is vital to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"da1fc90c-74f1-4544-b050-4c7266747863\">choose a safe location<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> away from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"eb80033c-2688-48c6-80bc-df022ae49731\">slopes that are prone to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> avalanches. Next, mark a circle in the snow. For two people, a circle of around two metres in diameter is needed, and for four people, around four metres. The igloo body is the next step. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7152eb5d-429a-4d9a-874e-13137e34c3e0\">Shovel a pile of snow into a large, reasonably steep mound<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> and try to keep the sloping sides at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"e7a3c3df-3d90-4e8e-b987-ead045e3be08\">an angle of around 35 degrees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> or higher, which is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d5c50379-12ca-44f9-b860-6508ad17f8e7\">best for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> stability. Wide, short snow shelters are more prone to collapse. If possible, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"ebe5979e-86a9-4fdb-9c20-704c2dc2d901\">mix snow of different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> temperatures to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"7ec21a9b-ea08-4c7d-96f9-39062e344bf6\">help it harden<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. The entrance is made by digging a trench downwards into the snow towards the mound. This should be on the downhill side and out of the wind. The snow that is removed from the trench should be placed on top of the mound. In these conditions, make the trench as deep as a standing person. Then, leave everything for about 90 minutes if possible. Next, finish the tunnel entrance. Make the tunnel slightly wider than a body's width and dig at a slightly upward angle. Ideally, the floor of the snow shelter should be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"03a55e45-d083-4e7a-92ba-15cd959198e4\">at least 30 centimetres above the entrance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, which will help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"7b987f37-c987-41b3-a580-025762953398\">prevent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> warm air <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"7b987f37-c987-41b3-a580-025762953398\">from escaping<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the shelter. After the initial entrance is made, it is easier to hollow out the inside from the top down. The walls should be 30 to 60 centimetres thick, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"34bf64c5-304a-43e2-b6e7-97efec2bc5c6\">smoothing the inside walls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> will help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"8f0bdf5a-9407-4dc6-aecb-940e98ebd764\">prevent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> dripping. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8ee13df1-faa9-4e1b-80eb-bc05a2fb4f17\">Leave an<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> elevated <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8ee13df1-faa9-4e1b-80eb-bc05a2fb4f17\">platform for sleeping on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. As heat rises, the occupants will be in the warmest part of the igloo when sleeping. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"fbc679bb-29a7-4150-b02b-6e54f3ddee19\">A very important point<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> is to make an air vent in the wall of the shelter, which will prevent the occupants from suffocating in the night. Finally, block the entrance with a block of snow or a rucksack.</span></p><p><span>Igloo hotels are a new variation on the traditional igloo. In several winter destinations, villages of igloos are built for tourists, where guests <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a74fb080-1ccd-47b6-8cb2-22a57f0af0c8\">use sleeping bags placed on top of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> reindeer hides for overnight stays. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"68bd3b55-03ff-4dcd-9954-e0b31aa37d6f\">Ice hotels are found in many places in Norway, Finland, and Sweden<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>; they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a90d8f9c-4ed9-47eb-a273-b5c8a97e3475\">constructed each winter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> and melt <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"09f6f08f-5d25-4b09-a58f-ca6e97ddd7b2\">in the spring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. The Ice Hotel in the village of Jukkasjärvi, located next to the town of Kiruna in Sweden, is a famous attraction. Originally, the creators started out building a simple igloo, which later turned into the elaborate and now famous 'hotel'. It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"fa683f03-a446-4895-81e0-8d76cd00c2ac\">made from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a3ddf0f4-f7ef-4e6b-aadb-4255917f0141\">the waters of the adjacent River Torne<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, whose pure waters produce beautiful, clear ice that is used to create interior decorations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"fa683f03-a446-4895-81e0-8d76cd00c2ac\">made entirely of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> snow and ice.</span></p><p><span>The igloo is a subject that has fascinated people from all over the world. Although the traditional art of igloo construction by the Inuit may have declined, the igloo and variations on it have gained in popularity among those who enjoy the novelty and the winter experience.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes </span></i><i><b><span>1-3</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet write:</span></i></p><p><b><span>TRUE</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><b><span>FALSE</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><b><span>NOT</span></b> <b><span>GIVEN</span></b><span> if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325946\" id=\"question-wrapper-325946\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A quinzhee is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"3d537792-a946-4334-926a-406cad6b656d\">designed to provide permanent accommodation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325947\" id=\"question-wrapper-325947\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some governments have allocated grants to keep the art of building igloos alive. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325948\" id=\"question-wrapper-325948\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Although relatively warm, the temperature inside an igloo in winter Arctic conditions will <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"db5ee16c-ba4a-4e76-b8cc-095411c3cd85\">never rise above zero degrees Celsius<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the flow chart below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"7b987f37-c987-41b3-a580-025762953398\">in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> boxes </span></i><i><b><span>4-10</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>Building An Igloo</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"da1fc90c-74f1-4544-b050-4c7266747863\">Choose a good spot<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, away from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"eb80033c-2688-48c6-80bc-df022ae49731\">places that can be affected by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> (4)________.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>Mark a circle in the snow (2m diameter for 2 people and 4m for 4 people)</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7152eb5d-429a-4d9a-874e-13137e34c3e0\">Create a large mound of snow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"e7a3c3df-3d90-4e8e-b987-ead045e3be08\">35-degree side angles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d5c50379-12ca-44f9-b860-6508ad17f8e7\">for greater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> (5)________. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"ebe5979e-86a9-4fdb-9c20-704c2dc2d901\">Use snow with various<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (6)________ to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"7ec21a9b-ea08-4c7d-96f9-39062e344bf6\">help it set<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>Dig an entrance tunnel on the downhill side and away from the wind. Place dug snow on top of the mound – leave everything for 90 minutes.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>Continue and finish the entrance tunnel – wider than a body and slightly upwards, as the igloo floor should be approx. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"03a55e45-d083-4e7a-92ba-15cd959198e4\">30cm higher than the entrance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"7b987f37-c987-41b3-a580-025762953398\">keep<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the (7)________ in.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span>Hollow the igloo from the inside – the walls should be 30-60cm thick.</span></p><p><span>↓</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"34bf64c5-304a-43e2-b6e7-97efec2bc5c6\">Smooth the inside walls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"8f0bdf5a-9407-4dc6-aecb-940e98ebd764\">stop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)________; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8ee13df1-faa9-4e1b-80eb-bc05a2fb4f17\">the sleeping area should be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)________; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"fbc679bb-29a7-4150-b02b-6e54f3ddee19\">it is vital<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to make an (10)________; block the entrance with snow or a rucksack.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325949\" id=\"question-wrapper-325949\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">avalanches</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325950\" id=\"question-wrapper-325950\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">stability</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325951\" id=\"question-wrapper-325951\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">temperatures</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325952\" id=\"question-wrapper-325952\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">warm air</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325953\" id=\"question-wrapper-325953\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">dripping</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325954\" id=\"question-wrapper-325954\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">elevated</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325955\" id=\"question-wrapper-325955\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">air vent</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>11-13</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>The Jukkasjarvi Ice Hotel</span></b></p><p><span>Igloo hotels are popular novelties, where guests can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a74fb080-1ccd-47b6-8cb2-22a57f0af0c8\">sleep in sleeping bags on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)________. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"68bd3b55-03ff-4dcd-9954-e0b31aa37d6f\">These hotels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (in northern countries) are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a90d8f9c-4ed9-47eb-a273-b5c8a97e3475\">built every year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> and (12)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"09f6f08f-5d25-4b09-a58f-ca6e97ddd7b2\">when it warms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. The famous Jukkasjarvi Ice Hotel is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"fa683f03-a446-4895-81e0-8d76cd00c2ac\">completely made from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a3ddf0f4-f7ef-4e6b-aadb-4255917f0141\">nearby river water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> – even the (13)________.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325956\" id=\"question-wrapper-325956\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">reindeer hides</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325957\" id=\"question-wrapper-325957\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">melt</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325958\" id=\"question-wrapper-325958\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(interior) decorations</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"da1fc90c-74f1-4544-b050-4c7266747863","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Choose a good spot","passagePhrase":"choose a safe location"},{"uid":"eb80033c-2688-48c6-80bc-df022ae49731","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"places that can be affected by","passagePhrase":"slopes that are prone to"},{"uid":"7152eb5d-429a-4d9a-874e-13137e34c3e0","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Create a large mound of snow","passagePhrase":"Shovel a pile of snow into a large, reasonably steep mound"},{"uid":"e7a3c3df-3d90-4e8e-b987-ead045e3be08","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"35-degree side angles","passagePhrase":"an angle of around 35 degrees"},{"uid":"d5c50379-12ca-44f9-b860-6508ad17f8e7","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"for greater","passagePhrase":"best for"},{"uid":"ebe5979e-86a9-4fdb-9c20-704c2dc2d901","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Use snow with various","passagePhrase":"mix snow of different"},{"uid":"7ec21a9b-ea08-4c7d-96f9-39062e344bf6","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"help it set","passagePhrase":"help it harden"},{"uid":"03a55e45-d083-4e7a-92ba-15cd959198e4","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"30cm higher than the entrance","passagePhrase":"at least 30 centimetres above the entrance"},{"uid":"7b987f37-c987-41b3-a580-025762953398","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"in ... keep","passagePhrase":"prevent ... from escaping"},{"uid":"34bf64c5-304a-43e2-b6e7-97efec2bc5c6","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Smooth the inside walls","passagePhrase":"smoothing the inside walls"},{"uid":"8f0bdf5a-9407-4dc6-aecb-940e98ebd764","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"stop","passagePhrase":"prevent"},{"uid":"8ee13df1-faa9-4e1b-80eb-bc05a2fb4f17","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"the sleeping area should be","passagePhrase":"Leave an ... platform for sleeping on"},{"uid":"fbc679bb-29a7-4150-b02b-6e54f3ddee19","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"it is vital","passagePhrase":"A very important point"},{"uid":"a74fb080-1ccd-47b6-8cb2-22a57f0af0c8","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"sleep in sleeping bags on","passagePhrase":"use sleeping bags placed on top of"},{"uid":"68bd3b55-03ff-4dcd-9954-e0b31aa37d6f","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"These hotels","passagePhrase":"Ice hotels are found in many places in Norway, Finland, and Sweden"},{"uid":"a90d8f9c-4ed9-47eb-a273-b5c8a97e3475","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"built every year","passagePhrase":"constructed each winter"},{"uid":"09f6f08f-5d25-4b09-a58f-ca6e97ddd7b2","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"when it warms","passagePhrase":"in the spring"},{"uid":"fa683f03-a446-4895-81e0-8d76cd00c2ac","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"completely made from","passagePhrase":"made from ... made entirely of"},{"uid":"a3ddf0f4-f7ef-4e6b-aadb-4255917f0141","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"nearby river water","passagePhrase":"the waters of the adjacent River Torne"}]},"reading_u2_80":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 14-26</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Rise of Agritourism</span></b></p><p><span>In advanced industrialised countries, small farmers have been challenged by changing economic and social conditions, such as increased global competition, falling commodity prices, and capital- and technology-intensive agricultural production. In addition, there has been added <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"fcc81ee0-626d-4009-8366-017b5851a35a\">public pressure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to make expensive <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"fffb1e3a-1d8d-4322-b0ce-4978e26abe04\">changes in farming methods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, due to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"fffb1e3a-1d8d-4322-b0ce-4978e26abe04\">public environmental concerns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> about industrialised agricultural production in combination with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"b9ba4f45-5fa7-4b03-a5a5-7cc8c558e2cc\">political pressures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3104dc79-2660-4892-b86e-4699d22f91c8\">reduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a0a26e29-f0ba-475d-b95c-aaefed0d912d\">agricultural subsidies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. These changing economic and social conditions have disproportionately impacted smaller farms in Europe and the US.</span></p><p><span>Agritourism is becoming an increasingly popular way for rural property owners to earn additional income from agricultural properties. In addition to more traditional farm tours and seasonal activities, such as hay rides, corn mazes and u-pick fruits, farm owners are devising new ways to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e703a764-c9c4-4070-b9cd-6f51c27590f0\">bring people to their door<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> by offering more entertainment-oriented activities. Some farmers are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"1538cea6-0be7-4ce8-8f0b-5344f8d6e87b\">offering their barns as venues for weddings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, parties, dances and other special events. Others are opening their homes to visitors for vacations, so guests can experience life on a working farm by helping out with routine farm chores, such as feeding or herding the livestock, milking the animals, making cheese, collecting eggs, picking vegetables and preparing farm-fresh meals. Agritourism works in combination with a growing public desire to engage in rural experiences and outdoor recreational activities. By combining agriculture and tourism, agritourism offers these rural experiences to urban residents and economic diversification to farmers.</span></p><p><span>Part of the attraction of agritourism is the nostalgia it creates for a simpler time and its authenticity. Tourists are being sold not only on beautiful scenery and visual aesthetics, but also on experiences that are meant to open up a new world for these customers who are tired of the hustle and bustle of city life. Authenticity has been an abiding theme in tourism studies, and it may have a special meaning in this combination of agriculture and tourism. For one thing, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9c40accc-fe69-4934-8156-03857cc7b141\">the image<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of the family farm <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9c40accc-fe69-4934-8156-03857cc7b141\">remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> imbued with deep authenticity, the surviving representation of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9c40accc-fe69-4934-8156-03857cc7b141\">an old world ideal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. To partake in agritourism is therefore likely to convey the sense of having a deeply authentic experience. Critics have claimed that this desire to reconnect with the lifeworld of one’s ancestors may conflict with the nature of modern agriculture and whether the tourist will want to face its true realities. It seems therefore that often the most distinctive innovative effort involves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"667b7df4-c773-40d7-8e82-47d0c2b27201\">the reinvention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"cff0c990-4680-49f2-adc9-a5503b089703\">tradition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> and rural tourism products. Examples are the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"667b7df4-c773-40d7-8e82-47d0c2b27201\">recreation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"cff0c990-4680-49f2-adc9-a5503b089703\">home-produced products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"4e07504e-fd03-43a7-8c0f-676f6cc0eb09\">long since replaced by manufactured commodities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> and the provision of hands-on experiences in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"cff0c990-4680-49f2-adc9-a5503b089703\">crafts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> often recreated for tourists. As a result, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"66fe58d0-136c-4e62-83d7-6bb6d0439998\">some critics argue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"a566c61e-b2c8-48f2-b5d3-c6a46730eca7\">the tourists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> who are running to the countryside are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"a566c61e-b2c8-48f2-b5d3-c6a46730eca7\">overcrowding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bc5a91bf-3e73-41fd-b8c8-f1a06eccc836\">ruining the pristine beauty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> that they so desperately want to experience.</span></p><p><span>Agritourism can benefit the life and economy of local communities, as well as the farms themselves. Agritourism firstly means that some farms can continue in business and employ workers. Employment underscores the genuine importance of agritourism farms to local economies, as rural communities are usually areas that both have high unemployment and few alternatives for the unemployed to find work. Secondly, a significant number of agritourists come from areas reasonably local to the visited farms. This means that tourist spending on agritourism often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"8f35605e-ee78-412e-bf70-f28eabfb8837\">stays<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"31265357-096b-434f-984a-aef0d71b21ab\">in the region<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"8e212fc5-359c-4779-b49c-3e28b10c429f\">helping to </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"8e212fc5-359c-4779-b49c-3e28b10c429f df824d79-fdf0-4c55-acd1-cd651bf729d9\">generate</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"df824d79-fdf0-4c55-acd1-cd651bf729d9\"> taxable revenues</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> and more disposable incomes. The U.S. Department of Agriculture’s agricultural census, taken every five years, found that last year approximately 23,000 farms took part in agritourism.</span></p><p><span>These farms each earned $24,300 from agritourism, compared to five years ago, when farms engaged in this brought in only $7,200 per farm. The trend is clearly growing, and the money generated will stimulate local economies. Thirdly, agritourism benefits the local community in terms of education. Many farms offer tours for elementary school-age children, who can learn where their food is coming from and how it is produced.</span></p><p><span>Farms choosing to develop agritourism have had reasonable government support. Over the last 20 years, European Union countries have spent 2 billion euros to subsidise agritourism development in rural farming areas that cannot compete in a global market with declining commodity prices. This, in turn, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"da8e988f-7acd-42d9-b90a-67784b6e307d\">helps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> governments by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"f03ed1ed-779e-4444-bd66-211ceaadfa69\">keeping farmers on land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"ca103184-d817-4f18-9154-92b701cc228e\">protecting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> picturesque rural landscapes that attract tourists, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"477880fb-a0c5-422e-928a-d3485768b72a\">supporting the production of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> regional agricultural products. As well as finance, local and national governments should create in the areas under their jurisdiction favourable environments for the development of agritourism by changing regulatory and tax constraints, so that more farms are encouraged to enter the industry.</span></p><p><span>It is clear that there are strong economic and social benefits that agritourism can provide farmers, customers and the local areas where the farms are situated. Agritourism contributes to and enhances the quality of life in communities by expanding recreational opportunities, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"aa6377ea-f834-4877-a4a0-bf5ebe9c0b43\">diversifying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> rural economies, and promoting the retention of agricultural lands. Working agricultural landscapes reflect the efforts of generations of farm families and often provide a defining sense of culture, heritage, and rural character. Agritourism provides educational opportunities for school children and adults to learn about this agrarian heritage, the production of food, and resource stewardship. Finally, many agritourism operations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"9b2125d6-1ef5-4726-99eb-39e1b077531e\">provide consumers with direct access to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> fresh farm goods. Agritourism is an industry with an enormous growth potential. With it, farming could become more efficient and sustainable, rural areas could become more beautiful, and farmers could become better off and more significant employers and contributors to economies.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>14-19</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325959\" id=\"question-wrapper-325959\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Farmers today <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"fcc81ee0-626d-4009-8366-017b5851a35a\">face demands from the public<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> about</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. responding more effectively to international competition.</li> <li>B. improving the working conditions of their agricultural labourers.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"fffb1e3a-1d8d-4322-b0ce-4978e26abe04\">changing to more environmentally friendly production methods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</li> <li>D. cutting the overall costs involved in producing their goods.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325960\" id=\"question-wrapper-325960\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Farmers today are experiencing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"b9ba4f45-5fa7-4b03-a5a5-7cc8c558e2cc\">pressure from governments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, as the latter wish to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3104dc79-2660-4892-b86e-4699d22f91c8\">cut<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a0a26e29-f0ba-475d-b95c-aaefed0d912d\">financial support for agriculture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</li> <li>B. increase the taxes paid by farms.</li> <li>C. require farms to employ more workers.</li> <li>D. impose stricter limits on pesticide use.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325961\" id=\"question-wrapper-325961\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Farmers can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e703a764-c9c4-4070-b9cd-6f51c27590f0\">attract tourists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> by</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. offering holidays at lower prices.</li> <li>B. being close to transport hubs.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"1538cea6-0be7-4ce8-8f0b-5344f8d6e87b\">letting people get married on the farm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</li> <li>D. promoting their services on a door-by-door basis.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325962\" id=\"question-wrapper-325962\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Farming authenticity partly depends on</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the&nbsp;farms' distance from urban areas.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9c40accc-fe69-4934-8156-03857cc7b141\">long-established ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> about the family farm.</li> <li>C. the appearance and behaviour of farm employees.</li> <li>D. the kinds of animals raised on the property.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325963\" id=\"question-wrapper-325963\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Farms can create authenticity by</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. making tourist workers get up very early in the morning.</li> <li>B. demonstrating the latest agricultural technology to tourists.</li> <li>C. preventing visitors from seeing all stages of animal production.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"667b7df4-c773-40d7-8e82-47d0c2b27201\">re-establishing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"cff0c990-4680-49f2-adc9-a5503b089703\">old processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"4e07504e-fd03-43a7-8c0f-676f6cc0eb09\">have largely disappeared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325964\" id=\"question-wrapper-325964\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"66fe58d0-136c-4e62-83d7-6bb6d0439998\">One criticism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of agritourism is that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. people employed on the farms are at risk of losing their positions.</li> <li>B. the&nbsp;presence of tourists forces changes in how farms are run.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"a566c61e-b2c8-48f2-b5d3-c6a46730eca7\">the&nbsp;extra numbers of people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in the countryside <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bc5a91bf-3e73-41fd-b8c8-f1a06eccc836\">spoil its appeal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</li> <li>D. the&nbsp;additional income generated goes to nobody except the farmer.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></b><span> for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>20-26</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>The Benefits of Agritourism</span></b></p><p><span>● Farms continue in business and are employers.</span></p><p><span>● Tourist (20)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"8f35605e-ee78-412e-bf70-f28eabfb8837\">remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"31265357-096b-434f-984a-aef0d71b21ab\">in the area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>● It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"df824d79-fdf0-4c55-acd1-cd651bf729d9\">generates taxes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"8e212fc5-359c-4779-b49c-3e28b10c429f\">creates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> (21)________</span></p><p><span>● Local economies grow because of the extra money spent.</span></p><p><span>● Children can learn about farming.</span></p><p><b><span>● </span></b><span>(22)</span><b><span>________</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"da8e988f-7acd-42d9-b90a-67784b6e307d\">benefit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"f03ed1ed-779e-4444-bd66-211ceaadfa69\">keeping farms in operation on the land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>● Rural (23)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"ca103184-d817-4f18-9154-92b701cc228e\">are preserved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>● </span></b><span>(24)</span><b><span>________</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"477880fb-a0c5-422e-928a-d3485768b72a\">continue to be manufactured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>● Improved quality of life and more recreational possibilities in communities.</span></p><p><span>● (25)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"aa6377ea-f834-4877-a4a0-bf5ebe9c0b43\">become more varied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>● Land remains in use by agriculture.</span></p><p><span>● Education for all.</span></p><p><span>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"9b2125d6-1ef5-4726-99eb-39e1b077531e\">People can easily buy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26)________</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325965\" id=\"question-wrapper-325965\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">spending (on agritourism)</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325966\" id=\"question-wrapper-325966\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">more disposable incomes [OR] disposable incomes [OR] incomes</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325967\" id=\"question-wrapper-325967\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">governments</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325968\" id=\"question-wrapper-325968\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">landscapes</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325969\" id=\"question-wrapper-325969\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(regional) agricultural products</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325970\" id=\"question-wrapper-325970\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">rural economies</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325971\" id=\"question-wrapper-325971\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(fresh) farm goods</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"fcc81ee0-626d-4009-8366-017b5851a35a","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"face demands from the public","passagePhrase":"public pressure"},{"uid":"fffb1e3a-1d8d-4322-b0ce-4978e26abe04","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"changing to more environmentally friendly production methods","passagePhrase":"changes in farming methods ... public environmental concerns"},{"uid":"b9ba4f45-5fa7-4b03-a5a5-7cc8c558e2cc","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"pressure from governments","passagePhrase":"political pressures"},{"uid":"3104dc79-2660-4892-b86e-4699d22f91c8","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"cut","passagePhrase":"reduce"},{"uid":"a0a26e29-f0ba-475d-b95c-aaefed0d912d","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"financial support for agriculture","passagePhrase":"agricultural subsidies"},{"uid":"e703a764-c9c4-4070-b9cd-6f51c27590f0","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"attract tourists","passagePhrase":"bring people to their door"},{"uid":"1538cea6-0be7-4ce8-8f0b-5344f8d6e87b","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"letting people get married on the farm","passagePhrase":"offering their barns as venues for weddings"},{"uid":"9c40accc-fe69-4934-8156-03857cc7b141","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"long-established ideas","passagePhrase":"the image ... remains ... an old world ideal"},{"uid":"667b7df4-c773-40d7-8e82-47d0c2b27201","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"re-establishing","passagePhrase":"the reinvention ... recreation"},{"uid":"cff0c990-4680-49f2-adc9-a5503b089703","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"old processes","passagePhrase":"tradition ... home-produced products ... crafts"},{"uid":"4e07504e-fd03-43a7-8c0f-676f6cc0eb09","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"have largely disappeared","passagePhrase":"long since replaced by manufactured commodities"},{"uid":"66fe58d0-136c-4e62-83d7-6bb6d0439998","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"One criticism","passagePhrase":"some critics argue"},{"uid":"a566c61e-b2c8-48f2-b5d3-c6a46730eca7","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"the extra numbers of people","passagePhrase":"the tourists ... overcrowding"},{"uid":"bc5a91bf-3e73-41fd-b8c8-f1a06eccc836","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"spoil its appeal","passagePhrase":"ruining the pristine beauty"},{"uid":"8f35605e-ee78-412e-bf70-f28eabfb8837","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"remains","passagePhrase":"stays"},{"uid":"31265357-096b-434f-984a-aef0d71b21ab","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"in the area","passagePhrase":"in the region"},{"uid":"8e212fc5-359c-4779-b49c-3e28b10c429f","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"creates","passagePhrase":"helping to"},{"uid":"8e212fc5-359c-4779-b49c-3e28b10c429f df824d79-fdf0-4c55-acd1-cd651bf729d9","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"generate"},{"uid":"df824d79-fdf0-4c55-acd1-cd651bf729d9","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"generates taxes","passagePhrase":"taxable revenues"},{"uid":"da8e988f-7acd-42d9-b90a-67784b6e307d","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"benefit","passagePhrase":"helps"},{"uid":"f03ed1ed-779e-4444-bd66-211ceaadfa69","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"keeping farms in operation on the land","passagePhrase":"keeping farmers on land"},{"uid":"ca103184-d817-4f18-9154-92b701cc228e","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"are preserved","passagePhrase":"protecting"},{"uid":"477880fb-a0c5-422e-928a-d3485768b72a","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"continue to be manufactured","passagePhrase":"supporting the production of"},{"uid":"aa6377ea-f834-4877-a4a0-bf5ebe9c0b43","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"become more varied","passagePhrase":"diversifying"},{"uid":"9b2125d6-1ef5-4726-99eb-39e1b077531e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"People can easily buy","passagePhrase":"provide consumers with direct access to"}]},"reading_u2_81":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 27-40</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>History of the Telegraph in Communication</span></b></p><p><span>Jean-Antoine Nollet was a French clergyman and physicist. In 1746, he gathered about two hundred monks into a circle about a mile (1.6 km) in circumference, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ce7a2fec-7d7b-4d3b-ab2a-10eab37a3bd2\">pieces of iron wire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> connecting them. He then <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c1c5da71-adcb-49b3-a7cb-1ccafbbd090c\">discharged a battery of Leyden jars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> through the human chain and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c1c5da71-adcb-49b3-a7cb-1ccafbbd090c\">observed that each man reacted at substantially the same time to the electric shock<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, showing that the speed at which electricity propagated was very high. Given a more humane detection system, this could have provided a way of signalling over long distances. In 1748, Nollet invented one of the first electrometers, the electroscope, which detected the presence of an electric charge using electrostatic attraction and repulsion.</span></p><p><span>After the introduction of European semaphore lines <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"747e3af0-1641-4bac-95f8-65abd6a82148\">in 1792<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"001f7d68-6da7-48ec-9adf-35fef547c265\">the world’s desire to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a6cbf7f8-b818-4687-9307-6b7b7ddd03a0\">improve its ability to communicate over long distances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"001f7d68-6da7-48ec-9adf-35fef547c265\">only grew<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. People wanted a way to send and receive news from remote locations so that they could better understand what was happening in the world around them—not just what was going on in their immediate town or city. This type of communication appealed not only to the media industry but also to private individuals and companies that wished to stay in touch with their contacts. In 1840, Charles Wheatstone of Britain, together with William Cooke, obtained a new patent for a telegraphic arrangement. The new apparatus required only a single pair of wires, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"8a98d22d-f9ff-4c51-85ed-371cd9021122\">the telegraph<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> was still <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"4cc93769-df8c-4f99-be7e-d19c8e99b5b2\">too costly for general use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. In 1845, however, Cooke and Wheatstone succeeded in producing the single-needle apparatus, which they patented, and from that time onwards, the electric telegraph became a practical instrument and was soon adopted on railway lines throughout the country.</span></p><p><span>It was the European optical telegraph, or semaphore, that was the predecessor of the electrical recording telegraph, which changed the history of communication forever. Building on the success of the optical telegraph, Samuel F. B. Morse completed a working version of the electrical recording telegraph, which required only a single wire to transmit a code of dots and dashes. At first, it was imagined that only a few highly skilled operators would be able to use it, but it soon became clear that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"15a3040d-d8ea-4a39-8f1a-ebee28a6b8d9\">many people could become proficient in Morse code<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. A system of lines strung between telegraph poles began to spread across Europe and America.</span></p><p><span>In the 1840s and 1850s, several individuals proposed or advocated the construction of a telegraph cable across the Atlantic Ocean, including Edward Thornton and Alonzo Jackman. At that time, no suitable material was available for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"98f3b502-e44d-43c0-bf7b-f7ede1857a34\">cable insulation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, and the first breakthrough came with the discovery of a rubber-like latex called gutta-percha. Introduced to Britain in 1843, gutta-percha is the gum of a tree native to the Malay Peninsula and Malaysia. After the failure of their first cable in 1850, the British brothers John and Jacob Brett laid a successful submarine cable from Dover to Calais in 1851. This cable used two layers of gutta-percha insulation and an armoured outer layer. With its thin wire and thick insulation, it floated and therefore had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0abd3b9d-b7be-4473-803a-1c72735adfc3\">to be weighed down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> with lead pipe.</span></p><p><span>In the case of early submarine-cable telegraphy, one limitation was the lack of knowledge about how the cable's electrical properties were affected by water. The voltage that could be applied to the cable was limited to a definite value. Moreover, for certain reasons, the cable had an impedance associated with it at the sending end, which could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"2dd56ffb-176d-454f-bfd4-11757e4b9fe8\">cause the voltage on the cable to differ from that applied to the sending-end apparatus<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. In fact, the cable was too large for a single boat to carry, so two vessels had to start in the middle of the Atlantic, join their cables, and sail in opposite directions. Amazingly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"98e2bb30-0a0d-4018-8a91-91557ec06eaa\">the first official telegram to pass between the two continents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> was a letter of congratulation from Queen Victoria of the United Kingdom to the President of the United States, James Buchanan, on August 16, 1858. However, the signal quality declined rapidly, slowing transmission to an almost unusable speed, and the cable was destroyed the following month.</span></p><p><span>To complete the link between England and Australia, John Pender formed the British-Australian Telegraph Company. The first stage was to lay a 557-nautical-mile cable from Singapore to Batavia on the island of Java in 1870. It seemed likely that the telegraph line would come ashore at the northern port of Darwin, from where it could connect around the coast to Queensland and New South Wales. It was an undertaking even more ambitious than spanning an ocean. Flocks of sheep had to be driven alongside the 400 workers to provide food. They needed horses and bullock carts and, for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"66e54449-8424-42fc-b01f-c1108cd8533f\">the parched interior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, camels. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"b612800f-15cf-41d5-b6ba-ed65e36971f7\">In the north<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, tropical rains <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"162cd646-ee32-4099-9570-0443e74af097\">left the teams surrounded by floodwaters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. In the centre, it seemed that they would die of thirst. One critical section in the red heart of Australia involved finding a route through the McDonnell mountain range and then locating water on the other side. The water was essential not only for the construction teams. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"6b937833-cb62-4765-a951-9c87f4fde49f\">Telegraph repeater stations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> had to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"6b937833-cb62-4765-a951-9c87f4fde49f\">established every few hundred miles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> to boost the signal, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3c7d9479-40d8-4f81-83d4-17418ebaf478\">the staff obviously needed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e06f8a74-23ac-4be0-b1d3-419f026d65df\">a reliable water supply<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>On August 22, 1872, the northern and southern sections of the Overland Telegraph Line were connected, uniting the Australian continent. Within a few months, Australia was at last in direct contact with England via the submarine cable as well. This allowed the Australian Government to receive news from around the world almost instantaneously for the first time. It could cost several pounds to send a message, and it might take several hours for it to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"df446c34-43e6-44f5-abfe-3c1788ba8f41\">reach its destination on the other side of the globe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, but the world would never be the same again. The telegraph was the first form of communication over great distances and represented a landmark in human history.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes </span></i><i><b><span>27-32</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet, write</span></i></p><p><b><span>TRUE</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><b><span>FALSE</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><b><span>NOT</span></b> <b><span>GIVEN</span></b><span> if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325972\" id=\"question-wrapper-325972\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In Nollet’s experiment, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ce7a2fec-7d7b-4d3b-ab2a-10eab37a3bd2\">metal lines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c1c5da71-adcb-49b3-a7cb-1ccafbbd090c\">were used to send messages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325973\" id=\"question-wrapper-325973\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"001f7d68-6da7-48ec-9adf-35fef547c265\">People increasingly hoped to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a6cbf7f8-b818-4687-9307-6b7b7ddd03a0\">explore ways of long-distance communication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"747e3af0-1641-4bac-95f8-65abd6a82148\">in the late eighteenth century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325974\" id=\"question-wrapper-325974\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In practice, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"15a3040d-d8ea-4a39-8f1a-ebee28a6b8d9\">Morse code could be mastered only by a small number of highly trained individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325975\" id=\"question-wrapper-325975\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Morse was a famous inventor before he invented the code. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325976\" id=\"question-wrapper-325976\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e06f8a74-23ac-4be0-b1d3-419f026d65df\">A steady supply of water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3c7d9479-40d8-4f81-83d4-17418ebaf478\">mattered greatly to those working at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"6b937833-cb62-4765-a951-9c87f4fde49f\">early telegraph repeater stations on the continent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325977\" id=\"question-wrapper-325977\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Australian Government offered funds for the first overland line across the continent. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>33-40</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325978\" id=\"question-wrapper-325978\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why did <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"8a98d22d-f9ff-4c51-85ed-371cd9021122\">Charles Wheatstone’s telegraph system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"4cc93769-df8c-4f99-be7e-d19c8e99b5b2\">fail to come into common use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> in the beginning? </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(too) costly</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325979\" id=\"question-wrapper-325979\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What material was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"98f3b502-e44d-43c0-bf7b-f7ede1857a34\">used for insulating cable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> across the sea?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">gutta-percha</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325980\" id=\"question-wrapper-325980\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What was used by British pioneers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0abd3b9d-b7be-4473-803a-1c72735adfc3\">increase the weight of the cable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> in the sea?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">lead pipe</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325981\" id=\"question-wrapper-325981\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What electrical property at the sending end could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"2dd56ffb-176d-454f-bfd4-11757e4b9fe8\">cause a difference between the cable voltage and the applied voltage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(an) impedance</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325982\" id=\"question-wrapper-325982\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Who received <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"98e2bb30-0a0d-4018-8a91-91557ec06eaa\">the first official transatlantic telegram<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> from Queen Victoria?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">James Buchanan</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325983\" id=\"question-wrapper-325983\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which animals carried supplies through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"66e54449-8424-42fc-b01f-c1108cd8533f\">the driest part<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of Australia?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">camels</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325984\" id=\"question-wrapper-325984\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What weather condition <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"162cd646-ee32-4099-9570-0443e74af097\">delayed construction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"b612800f-15cf-41d5-b6ba-ed65e36971f7\">in northern Australia<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>? </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">tropical rains</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325985\" id=\"question-wrapper-325985\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>How long did it take to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"df446c34-43e6-44f5-abfe-3c1788ba8f41\">send a telegraph message from Australia to England<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> in 1872? </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">several hours</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"ce7a2fec-7d7b-4d3b-ab2a-10eab37a3bd2","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"metal lines","passagePhrase":"pieces of iron wire"},{"uid":"747e3af0-1641-4bac-95f8-65abd6a82148","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"in the late eighteenth century","passagePhrase":"in 1792"},{"uid":"001f7d68-6da7-48ec-9adf-35fef547c265","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"People increasingly hoped to","passagePhrase":"the world’s desire to ... only grew"},{"uid":"a6cbf7f8-b818-4687-9307-6b7b7ddd03a0","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"explore ways of long-distance communication","passagePhrase":"improve its ability to communicate over long distances"},{"uid":"8a98d22d-f9ff-4c51-85ed-371cd9021122","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Charles Wheatstone’s telegraph system","passagePhrase":"the telegraph"},{"uid":"4cc93769-df8c-4f99-be7e-d19c8e99b5b2","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"fail to come into common use","passagePhrase":"too costly for general use"},{"uid":"98f3b502-e44d-43c0-bf7b-f7ede1857a34","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"used for insulating cable","passagePhrase":"cable insulation"},{"uid":"0abd3b9d-b7be-4473-803a-1c72735adfc3","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"increase the weight of the cable","passagePhrase":"to be weighed down"},{"uid":"2dd56ffb-176d-454f-bfd4-11757e4b9fe8","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"cause a difference between the cable voltage and the applied voltage","passagePhrase":"cause the voltage on the cable to differ from that applied to the sending-end apparatus"},{"uid":"98e2bb30-0a0d-4018-8a91-91557ec06eaa","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"the first official transatlantic telegram","passagePhrase":"the first official telegram to pass between the two continents"},{"uid":"66e54449-8424-42fc-b01f-c1108cd8533f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"the driest part","passagePhrase":"the parched interior"},{"uid":"b612800f-15cf-41d5-b6ba-ed65e36971f7","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"in northern Australia","passagePhrase":"In the north"},{"uid":"162cd646-ee32-4099-9570-0443e74af097","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"delayed construction","passagePhrase":"left the teams surrounded by floodwaters"},{"uid":"6b937833-cb62-4765-a951-9c87f4fde49f","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"early telegraph repeater stations on the continent","passagePhrase":"Telegraph repeater stations ... established every few hundred miles"},{"uid":"3c7d9479-40d8-4f81-83d4-17418ebaf478","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"mattered greatly to those working at","passagePhrase":"the staff obviously needed"},{"uid":"e06f8a74-23ac-4be0-b1d3-419f026d65df","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"A steady supply of water","passagePhrase":"a reliable water supply"},{"uid":"df446c34-43e6-44f5-abfe-3c1788ba8f41","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"send a telegraph message from Australia to England","passagePhrase":"reach its destination on the other side of the globe"}]},"reading_u2_82":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions</span></b> <b><span>1-13</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Erie Canal</span></b></p><p><span>Begun in 1817 and opened in its entirety in 1825, the Erie Canal is considered by some to be the engineering marvel of the nineteenth century. When the federal government concluded that the project was too ambitious to undertake, the State of New York took on the task of carving 363 miles of canal through the wilderness, with nothing but the muscle power of men and horses.</span></p><p><span>Once derided as 'Clinton's Folly' for the Governor who lent his vision and political muscle to the project, the Erie Canal experienced unparalleled success almost overnight. The iconic waterway established settlement patterns for most of the United States during the nineteenth century, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b28dfa93-d6eb-486c-a183-4357911217b7\">made New York the financial capital of the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"0ea5368e-7300-4ee6-8696-108aa3fdde76\">provided a critical supply line that helped the North<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> win the Civil War, and precipitated a series of social and economic changes throughout a young America.</span></p><p><span>Explorers had long searched for a water route to the west. Throughout the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries, the lack of an efficient and safe transportation network kept populations and trade largely confined to coastal areas. At the beginning of the nineteenth century, the Allegheny Mountains were the Western Frontier. The Northwest Territories that would later become Illinois, Indiana, Michigan and Ohio were rich in timber, minerals, and fertile land <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a6476f59-de29-4733-8166-238b8d50d3a1\">for farming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, but it took weeks to reach these things. Travellers were faced with rutted turnpike roads that baked to hardness in the summer sun. In the winter, the roads dissolved into mud.</span></p><p><span>An imprisoned <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"00dd6fc0-0b0d-43f7-8516-76c525cf82ef\">flour merchant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> named Jesse Hawley <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"12ac9f2c-dddc-4348-b99b-161296486290\">envisioned a better way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>: a canal from Buffalo on the eastern shore of Lake Erie to Albany on the upper Hudson River, a distance of almost 400 miles. Long a proponent of efficient water transportation, Hawley had gone bankrupt trying to move his products to market. Hawley's ideas caught the interest of Assemblyman Joshua Forman, who submitted the first state legislation related to the Erie Canal in 1808, calling for a series of surveys to be made examining the practicality of a water route between Lake Erie and the Hudson River. In 1810, Thomas Eddy and State Senator Jonas Platt, hoping to get plans for the canal moving forward, approached influential Senator De Witt Clinton, former mayor of New York City, to enlist his support. Though Clinton had been recruited to the canal effort by Eddy and Platt, he quickly became one of the canal's most active supporters and went on to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"2e0a14e7-b1f0-44dc-b2d8-bed813eead27\">successfully tie his very political fate to its success<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>On April 15th, 1817, the New York State Legislature finally approved construction of the Erie Canal. The Legislature authorised $7 million for construction of the 363-mile-long waterway, which was to be 40 feet wide and 18 feet deep. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"ff5ac3df-ef4d-4835-acb8-716f6ea23314\">Construction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> began on July 4th, 1817, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8b42ccd7-ccb0-4110-ace5-7ee02b201195\">took eight years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Like most canals, the Erie Canal depended on a lock system in order to compensate for changes in water levels over distance. A lock is a section of canal or river that is closed off to control the water level, so that boats can be raised or lowered as they pass through it. Locks have two sets of sluice gates (top and bottom), which seal off and then open the entrances to the chamber, which is where a boat waits while the movement up or down takes place. In addition, locks also have valves at the bottom of the sluice gates, and it is by opening these valves that water is allowed into and out of the chamber to raise or lower the water level, and hence the boat.</span></p><p><span>The effect of the Erie Canal was both immediate and dramatic, and settlers poured west. The explosion of trade prophesied by Governor Clinton began, spurred by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e32ef925-d025-4a55-beba-4333339de77a\">freight rates from Buffalo to New York of $10 per ton by canal, compared with $100 per ton by road<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. In 1829, there were 3,640 bushels of wheat transported down the canal from Buffalo. By 1837, this figure had increased to 500,000 bushels and, four years later, it reached one million. In nine years, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"36f2ca0c-49fb-480d-8242-ebc92ad4e919\">canal tolls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> more than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"75e3255e-f131-46fc-9d23-fd701d0c8b16\">recouped the entire cost of construction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. Within 15 years of the canal's opening, New York was the busiest port in America, moving tonnages greater than Boston, Baltimore and New Orleans combined. Today, it can still be seen that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"56acac5f-89fa-4c20-882d-15acccaaa461\">every major city in New York State falls along the trade route established by the Erie Canal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"56acac5f-89fa-4c20-882d-15acccaaa461\">nearly 80 per cent of upstate New York's inhabitants live within 25 miles of the Erie Canal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The completion of the Erie Canal spurred the first great westward movement of American settlers, gave access to the resources west of the Appalachians, and made New York the preeminent commercial city in the United States. At one time, more than 50,000 people depended on the Erie Canal for their livelihood. From its inception, the Erie Canal helped form a whole new culture revolving around canal life. For those who travelled along the canal in packet boats or passenger vessels, the canal was an exciting place. Gambling and entertainment were frequent pastimes, and often families would meet each year at the same locations to share stories and adventures. Today, the canal has returned to its former glory and is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"1dad8148-16c7-4320-820c-4c8999db2844\">filled with pleasure boats, fishermen, holidaymakers and cyclists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> riding the former towpaths where mules once trod. The excitement of the past is alive and well.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>SIX</span></b><span> letters, </span><b><span>A-K</span></b><span>. </span><i><span>Write the correct letters, </span></i><i><b><span>A-K</span></b></i><i><span>, in any order in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>1-6</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>SIX</span></b><span> of the following are described as effects of the Erie Canal?</span></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> It made minerals the principal resource transported from the Northwest Territories.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b28dfa93-d6eb-486c-a183-4357911217b7\">established the financial dominance of New York City<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> It reduced the journey to western resources from several weeks to only a few days.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b><b><span>. </span></b><span>It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"0ea5368e-7300-4ee6-8696-108aa3fdde76\">gave the northern states an important logistical advantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> during the Civil War.</span></p><p><b><span>E.</span></b><span> It increased the amount of fertile farmland available in the Northwest Territories.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"2e0a14e7-b1f0-44dc-b2d8-bed813eead27\">became an important factor in a politician’s career<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> It doubled the price farmers received for their wheat.</span></p><p><b><span>H. </span></b><span>It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"e32ef925-d025-4a55-beba-4333339de77a\">made the transportation of goods to market less expensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>I. </span></b><span>It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"56acac5f-89fa-4c20-882d-15acccaaa461\">influenced New York State’s population distribution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>J.</span></b><span> It allowed commercial freight to use the canal without paying charges.</span></p><p><b><span>K. </span></b><span>It has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"1dad8148-16c7-4320-820c-4c8999db2844\">become a popular destination for recreation and leisure activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325986\" id=\"question-wrapper-325986\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F/H/I/K</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325987\" id=\"question-wrapper-325987\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F/H/I/K</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325988\" id=\"question-wrapper-325988\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F/H/I/K</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325989\" id=\"question-wrapper-325989\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F/H/I/K</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325990\" id=\"question-wrapper-325990\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F/H/I/K</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325991\" id=\"question-wrapper-325991\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F/H/I/K</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>7-10</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325992\" id=\"question-wrapper-325992\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What natural feature made the Northwest Territories <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a6476f59-de29-4733-8166-238b8d50d3a1\">suitable for growing crops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">fertile land</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325993\" id=\"question-wrapper-325993\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In what <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"00dd6fc0-0b0d-43f7-8516-76c525cf82ef\">commodity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> did the person who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"12ac9f2c-dddc-4348-b99b-161296486290\">came up with the idea of the Erie Canal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"00dd6fc0-0b0d-43f7-8516-76c525cf82ef\">trade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>? </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">flour</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325994\" id=\"question-wrapper-325994\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8b42ccd7-ccb0-4110-ace5-7ee02b201195\">How long did it take<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"ff5ac3df-ef4d-4835-acb8-716f6ea23314\">build the Erie Canal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>? </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">8/eight years</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325995\" id=\"question-wrapper-325995\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"36f2ca0c-49fb-480d-8242-ebc92ad4e919\">source of income<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"75e3255e-f131-46fc-9d23-fd701d0c8b16\">repaid the money spent on constructing the canal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(canal) tolls</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Label the diagram below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>11-13</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_3/reading/images/315f763de9c0611fd45e730282992252d2e4685cd659d258e30d1f8c8cf6d997.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325996\" id=\"question-wrapper-325996\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(sluice) gates</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325997\" id=\"question-wrapper-325997\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) chamber</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325998\" id=\"question-wrapper-325998\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">valves</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b28dfa93-d6eb-486c-a183-4357911217b7","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"established the financial dominance of New York City","passagePhrase":"made New York the financial capital of the world"},{"uid":"0ea5368e-7300-4ee6-8696-108aa3fdde76","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"gave the northern states an important logistical advantage","passagePhrase":"provided a critical supply line that helped the North"},{"uid":"a6476f59-de29-4733-8166-238b8d50d3a1","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"suitable for growing crops","passagePhrase":"for farming"},{"uid":"00dd6fc0-0b0d-43f7-8516-76c525cf82ef","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"commodity ... trade","passagePhrase":"flour merchant"},{"uid":"12ac9f2c-dddc-4348-b99b-161296486290","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"came up with the idea of the Erie Canal","passagePhrase":"envisioned a better way"},{"uid":"2e0a14e7-b1f0-44dc-b2d8-bed813eead27","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"became an important factor in a politician’s career","passagePhrase":"successfully tie his very political fate to its success"},{"uid":"ff5ac3df-ef4d-4835-acb8-716f6ea23314","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"build the Erie Canal","passagePhrase":"Construction"},{"uid":"8b42ccd7-ccb0-4110-ace5-7ee02b201195","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"How long did it take","passagePhrase":"took eight years"},{"uid":"e32ef925-d025-4a55-beba-4333339de77a","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"made the transportation of goods to market less expensive","passagePhrase":"freight rates from Buffalo to New York of $10 per ton by canal, compared with $100 per ton by road"},{"uid":"36f2ca0c-49fb-480d-8242-ebc92ad4e919","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"source of income","passagePhrase":"canal tolls"},{"uid":"75e3255e-f131-46fc-9d23-fd701d0c8b16","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"repaid the money spent on constructing the canal","passagePhrase":"recouped the entire cost of construction"},{"uid":"56acac5f-89fa-4c20-882d-15acccaaa461","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"influenced New York State’s population distribution","passagePhrase":"every major city in New York State falls along the trade route established by the Erie Canal ... nearly 80 per cent of upstate New York's inhabitants live within 25 miles of the Erie Canal"},{"uid":"1dad8148-16c7-4320-820c-4c8999db2844","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"become a popular destination for recreation and leisure activities","passagePhrase":"filled with pleasure boats, fishermen, holidaymakers and cyclists"}]},"reading_u2_83":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 14-26</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Grand Banks</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b><span>. The Grand Banks are a large area of submerged highlands southeast of Newfoundland and east of the Laurentian Channel on the North American continental shelf. Covering 93,200 square kilometres, the Grand Banks are relatively shallow, ranging from 25 to 100 metres in depth. It is in this area that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"b57e9cae-6891-4741-abc4-dc62fbd78ecb\">the cold Labrador Current mixes with the warm waters of the Gulf Stream<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. The mixing of these waters and the shape of the ocean bottom lift nutrients to the surface, creating <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"35f19382-bddc-44de-a145-fbe0b02d409a\">one of the richest fishing grounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in the world. Extensive marine life flourishes in the Grand Banks, whose range extends beyond the Canadian 200-nautical-mile exclusive economic zone (EEZ) and into international waters. This has made it an important part of both the Canadian and the high seas fisheries, with fishermen risking their lives in an extremely inhospitable environment characterized by rogue waves, fog, icebergs, sea ice, hurricanes, winter storms, and earthquakes.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b><span>. While the area’s ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"4d1dd7d6-6c4f-4a66-8e3e-9546f0249d2a\">official’ discovery is credited to John Cabot in 1497<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"211cd2f2-7d13-4307-a2f9-cc8988f46f04\">English and Portuguese vessels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> are known to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"211cd2f2-7d13-4307-a2f9-cc8988f46f04\">have first sought out these waters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"6f452902-1426-49bc-9f64-f97112f7e3b2\">prior to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> that, based upon <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"3cb477d7-852d-44b9-a344-6770578676a9\">reports they received from earlier Viking voyages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> to Newfoundland. Several navigators, including Basque fishermen, are known to have fished these waters in the fifteenth century. Some texts from that era refer to a land called Bacalao, ‘the land of the codfish’, which was possibly Newfoundland. However, it was not until <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"167b7cec-858e-4881-9236-d68db24e238e\">John Cabot noted the waters’ abundance of sea life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that the existence of these fishing grounds became widely known in Europe. Soon, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"4c94db13-2682-498e-9295-9be1ce53cdd6\">fishermen and merchants from France, Spain, Portugal, and England<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5f1e6e4f-d6ba-45da-8b22-91ff0c831e33\">developed seasonal inshore fisheries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> producing for European markets. In what was known as the ‘dry’ fishery, cod were split, salted, and dried on shore over the summer before crews returned to Europe. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"aa582ec3-2a94-42de-942a-bef2d808f898\">The French<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"dc1d7791-c734-4b49-ac91-7b03953cf718\">pioneered the ‘wet’ or ‘green’ fishery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> on the Grand Banks proper around 1550, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"dc1d7791-c734-4b49-ac91-7b03953cf718\">heavily salting the cod on board<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b1849745-783c-4e59-ac38-981f02c3aed9\">immediately returning home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b><span>. The Grand Banks were possibly the world’s most important international fishing area in the nineteenth and twentieth centuries. Technological advances in fishing, such as sonar and large factory ships—including the massive factory freezer trawlers introduced in the 1950s—led to overfishing and a serious decline in fish stocks. Based upon the many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"46c09a93-c505-414b-9e98-66d7e646af44\">foreign policy agreements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8bd0a298-2154-4156-a3f2-c2731de9eca8\">Newfoundland had entered into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8db52028-4034-47e6-a88c-9c164514b985\">prior to its admittance into the Canadian Confederation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"9e32dd50-2a18-4f9d-93d9-35f921d14994\">foreign fleets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, some from as far away as Russia, came to the Grand Banks in force, catching unprecedented quantities of fish.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b><span>. Between 1973 and 1982, the United Nations and its member states negotiated the Third Convention on the Law of the Sea, one component of which was the concept of nations being allowed to declare an EEZ. Many nations worldwide declared 200-nautical-mile EEZs, including Canada and the United States. On the whole, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"83e35d61-ecfe-4baa-b0c2-5f193fa1fcbe\">the EEZ was very well received<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5407356d-9d2f-4495-8321-d40b730bf3a5\">fishermen in eastern Canada<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> because it meant they could fish unhindered out to the limit without fear of competing with foreign fleets. During the late 1970s and early 1980s, Canada’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"9d18b799-6775-459e-a210-9fa75131bdf4\">domestic offshore fleet grew<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> as fishermen and fish-processing companies rushed to take advantage. It was during this time that it was noticed that foreign fleets were pushing out to areas of the Grand Banks off Newfoundland that sat outside <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"92f47ec1-f00a-44f4-bdac-8cb3628d155c\">the Canadian EEZ<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. By the late 1980s, dwindling catches of Atlantic cod were being reported throughout Newfoundland and eastern Canada, and the federal government and citizens of coastal regions in the area began to face the reality that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1a819b30-b810-4829-befd-958d327a1cba\">domestic and foreign overfishing had taken its toll<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. The Canadian government was finally forced to take drastic action in 1992, when a total moratorium was indefinitely declared for the northern cod.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b><span>. Over the last ten years, it has been noted that cod <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"6843d525-f8ad-43d2-a934-acf9b3d5e620\">appear to be returning to the Grand Banks in small numbers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. The reasons for this <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"6843d525-f8ad-43d2-a934-acf9b3d5e620\">fragile recovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> are still unknown. Perhaps the damage done by trawlers is not permanent, and the marine fauna and ecosystems can rebuild themselves if given a prolonged period of time without any commercial activity. Either way, the early-stage recovery of the Grand Banks is encouraging news, but caution is needed; after nearly twenty years of severe limitations, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"6b30cf07-280b-4e74-9a06-ae9acfc6e852\">cod stocks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> are still <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"ea9e5404-ad79-4206-9aae-8925003bd211\">only at approximately ten per cent of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"cafd999d-e10b-4d19-bd3b-eacef7b01749\">1960s levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. It is hoped that in another ten to twenty years, stocks may be close to a full recovery, although this would require political pressure to maintain strict limitations on commercial fishing. If cod do come back to the Grand Banks in meaningful numbers, it is hoped that Canadians will not make the same mistakes again.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b><span>. Further riches have now been found in the Grand Banks. Petroleum reserves have been discovered, and a number of oil fields are under development in the region. The vast Hibernia oil field was discovered in 1979, and following several years of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"3923d75b-6c61-4311-8861-ed4defab31b8\">aborted start-up attempts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, the Hibernia megaproject began construction of the production platform and gravity base structures in the early 1990s. Production commenced on November 17, 1997, with initial production rates in excess of 50,000 barrels of crude oil per day from a single well. Hibernia has proven to be the most prolific oil well in Canada. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"f72c16ea-672d-41a5-a304-f35dd92f7b56\">earthquake and iceberg activity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in the Grand Banks poses a potential ecological disaster that could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"275674aa-b696-49c6-83c0-5b31c9fc1ed1\">devastate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4bf7c769-1f5d-4de5-a2fb-756a7d4acf37\">the fishing grounds that are only now starting to recover<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>The text on the previous pages has 6 paragraphs </span><b><span>A – F</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>14-20</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>NB</span></b> <i><span>You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325999\" id=\"question-wrapper-325999\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"9e32dd50-2a18-4f9d-93d9-35f921d14994\">Many countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> could legally fish Newfoundland waters because of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"46c09a93-c505-414b-9e98-66d7e646af44\">treaties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8bd0a298-2154-4156-a3f2-c2731de9eca8\">Newfoundland had made<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8db52028-4034-47e6-a88c-9c164514b985\">before becoming part of Canada<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326000\" id=\"question-wrapper-326000\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The establishment of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"92f47ec1-f00a-44f4-bdac-8cb3628d155c\">the EEZ<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1a819b30-b810-4829-befd-958d327a1cba\">did not stop overfishing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in the Grand Banks. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326001\" id=\"question-wrapper-326001\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"f72c16ea-672d-41a5-a304-f35dd92f7b56\">Natural disasters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"275674aa-b696-49c6-83c0-5b31c9fc1ed1\">destroy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4bf7c769-1f5d-4de5-a2fb-756a7d4acf37\">what is left of the Grand Banks ecosystem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326002\" id=\"question-wrapper-326002\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"b57e9cae-6891-4741-abc4-dc62fbd78ecb\">The meeting of waters with contrasting temperatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> helps make the region <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"35f19382-bddc-44de-a145-fbe0b02d409a\">exceptionally productive for fishing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326003\" id=\"question-wrapper-326003\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5407356d-9d2f-4495-8321-d40b730bf3a5\">Fishermen in eastern Canada<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"83e35d61-ecfe-4baa-b0c2-5f193fa1fcbe\">generally happy with the establishment of the Canadian EEZ<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326004\" id=\"question-wrapper-326004\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"6b30cf07-280b-4e74-9a06-ae9acfc6e852\">Grand Banks’ cod stocks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"ea9e5404-ad79-4206-9aae-8925003bd211\">about 90 per cent lower than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"cafd999d-e10b-4d19-bd3b-eacef7b01749\">what they were in the 1960s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326005\" id=\"question-wrapper-326005\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"aa582ec3-2a94-42de-942a-bef2d808f898\">French crews<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"dc1d7791-c734-4b49-ac91-7b03953cf718\">introduced a method of preserving cod at sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b1849745-783c-4e59-ac38-981f02c3aed9\">before sailing home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>21-23</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326006\" id=\"question-wrapper-326006\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"211cd2f2-7d13-4307-a2f9-cc8988f46f04\">English and Portuguese ships already made their way to the area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"6f452902-1426-49bc-9f64-f97112f7e3b2\">before<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"4d1dd7d6-6c4f-4a66-8e3e-9546f0249d2a\">Cabot arrived in 1497<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They were following guidance from Basque fishing crews.</li> <li>B. They were trying to identify the place called Bacalao.</li> <li>C. They had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"3cb477d7-852d-44b9-a344-6770578676a9\">received accounts derived from earlier Viking expeditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</li> <li>D. They were seeking new supplies for European cod markets.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326007\" id=\"question-wrapper-326007\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What followed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"167b7cec-858e-4881-9236-d68db24e238e\">Cabot’s description of the area’s rich marine life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. England&nbsp;claimed exclusive fishing rights there.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"4c94db13-2682-498e-9295-9be1ce53cdd6\">Fleets&nbsp;from several European nations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"5f1e6e4f-d6ba-45da-8b22-91ff0c831e33\">began operating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> there.</li> <li>C. Basque crews stopped fishing there because of increased competition.</li> <li>D. Preserving cod at sea quickly replaced drying it on shore.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326008\" id=\"question-wrapper-326008\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The establishment of the Canadian EEZ</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"9d18b799-6775-459e-a210-9fa75131bdf4\">enabled domestic offshore operations to expand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</li> <li>B. was followed by an immediate complete ban on northern cod fishing.</li> <li>C. temporarily stopped the overfishing of cod in the Grand Banks.</li> <li>D. gave foreign fleets unrestricted access within the new boundary.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes </span></i><i><b><span>24-26</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet write:</span></i></p><p><b><span>TRUE</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><b><span>FALSE</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><b><span>NOT</span></b> <b><span>GIVEN</span></b><span> if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326009\" id=\"question-wrapper-326009\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Even now, cod stocks have shown <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"6843d525-f8ad-43d2-a934-acf9b3d5e620\">no signs of recovery in the Grand Banks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326010\" id=\"question-wrapper-326010\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"3923d75b-6c61-4311-8861-ed4defab31b8\">Initial efforts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to extract oil from the Grand Banks’ Hibernia oil field <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"3923d75b-6c61-4311-8861-ed4defab31b8\">were unsuccessful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326011\" id=\"question-wrapper-326011\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Because of the risks posed by earthquakes and iceberg activity in the Grand Banks, oil exploration companies are now under strict safety regulations.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b57e9cae-6891-4741-abc4-dc62fbd78ecb","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"The meeting of waters with contrasting temperatures","passagePhrase":"the cold Labrador Current mixes with the warm waters of the Gulf Stream"},{"uid":"35f19382-bddc-44de-a145-fbe0b02d409a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"exceptionally productive for fishing","passagePhrase":"one of the richest fishing grounds"},{"uid":"4d1dd7d6-6c4f-4a66-8e3e-9546f0249d2a","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Cabot arrived in 1497","passagePhrase":"official’ discovery is credited to John Cabot in 1497"},{"uid":"211cd2f2-7d13-4307-a2f9-cc8988f46f04","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"English and Portuguese ships already made their way to the area","passagePhrase":"English and Portuguese vessels ... have first sought out these waters"},{"uid":"6f452902-1426-49bc-9f64-f97112f7e3b2","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"before","passagePhrase":"prior to"},{"uid":"3cb477d7-852d-44b9-a344-6770578676a9","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"received accounts derived from earlier Viking expeditions","passagePhrase":"reports they received from earlier Viking voyages"},{"uid":"167b7cec-858e-4881-9236-d68db24e238e","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Cabot’s description of the area’s rich marine life","passagePhrase":"John Cabot noted the waters’ abundance of sea life"},{"uid":"4c94db13-2682-498e-9295-9be1ce53cdd6","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Fleets from several European nations","passagePhrase":"fishermen and merchants from France, Spain, Portugal, and England"},{"uid":"5f1e6e4f-d6ba-45da-8b22-91ff0c831e33","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"began operating","passagePhrase":"developed seasonal inshore fisheries"},{"uid":"aa582ec3-2a94-42de-942a-bef2d808f898","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"French crews","passagePhrase":"The French"},{"uid":"dc1d7791-c734-4b49-ac91-7b03953cf718","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"introduced a method of preserving cod at sea","passagePhrase":"pioneered the ‘wet’ or ‘green’ fishery ... heavily salting the cod on board"},{"uid":"b1849745-783c-4e59-ac38-981f02c3aed9","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"before sailing home","passagePhrase":"immediately returning home"},{"uid":"46c09a93-c505-414b-9e98-66d7e646af44","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"treaties","passagePhrase":"foreign policy agreements"},{"uid":"8bd0a298-2154-4156-a3f2-c2731de9eca8","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Newfoundland had made","passagePhrase":"Newfoundland had entered into"},{"uid":"8db52028-4034-47e6-a88c-9c164514b985","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"before becoming part of Canada","passagePhrase":"prior to its admittance into the Canadian Confederation"},{"uid":"9e32dd50-2a18-4f9d-93d9-35f921d14994","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Many countries","passagePhrase":"foreign fleets"},{"uid":"83e35d61-ecfe-4baa-b0c2-5f193fa1fcbe","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"generally happy with the establishment of the Canadian EEZ","passagePhrase":"the EEZ was very well received"},{"uid":"5407356d-9d2f-4495-8321-d40b730bf3a5","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Fishermen in eastern Canada","passagePhrase":"fishermen in eastern Canada"},{"uid":"9d18b799-6775-459e-a210-9fa75131bdf4","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"enabled domestic offshore operations to expand","passagePhrase":"domestic offshore fleet grew"},{"uid":"92f47ec1-f00a-44f4-bdac-8cb3628d155c","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the EEZ","passagePhrase":"the Canadian EEZ"},{"uid":"1a819b30-b810-4829-befd-958d327a1cba","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"did not stop overfishing","passagePhrase":"domestic and foreign overfishing had taken its toll"},{"uid":"6b30cf07-280b-4e74-9a06-ae9acfc6e852","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Grand Banks’ cod stocks","passagePhrase":"cod stocks"},{"uid":"ea9e5404-ad79-4206-9aae-8925003bd211","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"about 90 per cent lower than","passagePhrase":"only at approximately ten per cent of"},{"uid":"cafd999d-e10b-4d19-bd3b-eacef7b01749","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"what they were in the 1960s","passagePhrase":"1960s levels"},{"uid":"3923d75b-6c61-4311-8861-ed4defab31b8","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"Initial efforts ... were unsuccessful","passagePhrase":"aborted start-up attempts"},{"uid":"f72c16ea-672d-41a5-a304-f35dd92f7b56","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Natural disasters","passagePhrase":"earthquake and iceberg activity"},{"uid":"275674aa-b696-49c6-83c0-5b31c9fc1ed1","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"destroy","passagePhrase":"devastate"},{"uid":"4bf7c769-1f5d-4de5-a2fb-756a7d4acf37","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"what is left of the Grand Banks ecosystem","passagePhrase":"the fishing grounds that are only now starting to recover"}]},"reading_u2_84":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 27-40</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>What Is Meaning?</span></b></p><p><i><span>Why do we respond to words and symbols in the ways we do?</span></i></p><p><span>Semantics, in general, is the subdivision of linguistics concerned with meaning. Semantics attempts the systematic study of the assignment of meanings to minimal meaning-bearing elements and the combination of these in the production of more complex meaningful expressions. Elementary word groups may be combined in a relationship of content, forming thematic groups and semantic and lexical \"fields\". For example, all the means of expressing the concept of joy in a given language constitute the lexical-semantic field \"joy\". Because of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"9a4d6859-0d78-4853-ac18-3b7eacc723c8\">trained patterns of response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, people listen more respectfully to the health advice of someone who has \"MD\" after his name than to that of someone who doesn't. A \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"9a4d6859-0d78-4853-ac18-3b7eacc723c8\">pattern of reactions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>\", then, is the sum of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"fb15474f-1c15-4f02-a5f1-8604116ce139\">the ways we act in response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to events, to words, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"fb15474f-1c15-4f02-a5f1-8604116ce139\">to symbols<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Words and word meanings are among the most important information cues used in speaking and understanding, as well as in reading. Indeed, a person's life experience and cultural experience (even reading comic strips) are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"c311463e-bf0e-4fb3-80ea-fdbd95409827\">highly relevant to the development of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"16d4671a-4a76-4114-ba9e-aca93f56287f\">linguistic \"meaning-making<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>\" in any language, which is very important in the communication process. Words, from the perspective of a person's native language and culture, can carry special associations. For instance, the Spanish words for hammock, tobacco, and potato are derived from Taíno words for these items. Therefore, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"3ab38337-b111-4d5d-9177-a96023a5c3c3\">when people's semantic habits are reasonably similar to those of most people around them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"ff1fd475-4f79-44e9-a8da-3c5822959434\">regarded as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> \"normal\" or perhaps \"dull\". If <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"3ab38337-b111-4d5d-9177-a96023a5c3c3\">their semantic habits are noticeably different from those of others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, they are regarded as \"individualistic\" or \"original\", or, if the differences are disapproved of or viewed with alarm, as \"crazy\".</span></p><p><span>A definition states the meaning of a word using other words. It is clear that to define a word, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d5056721-ed54-4d5f-b289-b6cb07513330\">as a dictionary does<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, is simply to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"7a87ccab-8d26-432f-9984-af9953d3dc24\">explain the word with more words<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d5056721-ed54-4d5f-b289-b6cb07513330\">defining words with more words<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"bb3b6c2d-67b7-4e08-be65-0bd8d1ff0bf1\">leads people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> (especially children) at once <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"bb3b6c2d-67b7-4e08-be65-0bd8d1ff0bf1\">into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> what mathematicians call <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29 37\" data-uid=\"7a87ccab-8d26-432f-9984-af9953d3dc24 bb3b6c2d-67b7-4e08-be65-0bd8d1ff0bf1\">an \"infinite regress</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>\", an infinite series of occurrences or concepts. For example, it can lead people into the kind of run-around that they sometimes encounter when they look up \"impertinence\" and find it defined as \"impudence\", so they look up \"impudence\" and find it defined as \"impertinence\". Yet—and here we come to another common reaction pattern—people often act as if words can be explained fully with more words. To a person who asked for a definition of jazz, Louis Armstrong is said to have replied, \"If you have to ask what jazz is, you'll never know\", <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"a1b44569-ca0b-4076-873d-eb270b29d0d3\">proving himself to be an intuitive semanticist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> as well as a great trumpet player.</span></p><p><span>Semantics, then, seeks the \"operational\" definition instead of the dictionary definition. Bridgman, the 1946 Nobel Prize winner and physicist, once wrote, \"The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"5060891c-3048-495f-8c44-f9bfe0286126\">true meaning of a term is to be found by observing what a man does with it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, not by what he says about it.\" He made an enormous contribution to science by showing that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"5060891c-3048-495f-8c44-f9bfe0286126\">the meaning of a scientific term lies in the operations—the things that are done<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>—that establish its validity, rather than in verbal definitions. An example of an operational definition of the term \"weight\" of an object, operationalized to a degree, would be the following: \"weight is the number that appears when that object is placed on a weighing scale\". Accordingly, specifying how one reads the numbers on the scale would make the operational definition more complete. But if people say—and revolutionists have started uprisings with just this statement—\"Man is born free, but everywhere he is in chains!\", <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e2ce854d-b5ac-4566-88cf-1f9a8e137195\">what operations could we perform to demonstrate its accuracy or inaccuracy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>?</span></p><p><span>Next, if this suggestion of \"operationalism\" is taken outside the physical sciences where Bridgman applied it, what \"operations\" are people expected to perform as a result of both the language they use and the language other people use in communicating with them? Here is a personnel manager studying an application form. He comes to the words \"Education: Harvard University\" and drops the application form into the wastebasket (that's the \"operation\") because, as he would say if you asked him, \"I don't like Harvard men\". This is an instance of \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"4a239b7d-fc1f-40b2-8412-f262b47a0aa8\">meaning\" at work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>—but it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"4a239b7d-fc1f-40b2-8412-f262b47a0aa8\">not a meaning that can be found in dictionaries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>So far as we know, human beings are the only creatures that have, over and above the biological equipment which we have in common with other creatures, the additional capacity for manufacturing symbols and systems of symbols. When we react to a flag, we are not reacting simply to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"408b5013-c53b-4448-bdee-0533f9f4a631\">a piece of cloth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, but to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"158109f9-4c57-4f05-9204-817ed1b9b567\">the meaning with which it has been symbolically endowed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. When we react to a word, we are not reacting to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"408b5013-c53b-4448-bdee-0533f9f4a631\">a set of sounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, but to the meaning with which that set of sounds has been symbolically endowed. As a matter of fact, how sound symbolism is processed in our brains has not yet been fully explained in the field.</span></p><p><span>Simply put, the key point of semantics lies not in the definition of words, but in our own semantic reactions, which occur when we respond to things the way they \"should\" be, rather than to the way they are. If a person were to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"70bc8ef4-a576-400b-89bc-80ebf77c02e7\">tell a shockingly obscene story in Arabic or Hindustani or Swahili before an audience that understood only English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0c3723e6-1d85-4949-9927-b6d964932123\">no one would blush or be angry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>; the story would be neither shocking nor obscene—indeed, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"e8f00f7c-b515-47bb-a4bd-c6d101081b26\">it would not even be a story<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Likewise, the value of a dollar bill is not in the bill, but in our social agreement to accept it as a symbol of value. If that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"f10bf03d-556a-4859-ba3b-8f9e9250a75b\">agreement were to break down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> through the collapse of our government, the dollar bill would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"55c4ce3c-d21f-48a7-aa1e-fc43d7f02b2d\">become only a scrap of paper<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. We do not understand a dollar bill by staring at it long and hard. We understand it by observing how people act with respect to it. We understand it by understanding the social mechanisms and the loyalties that keep it meaningful. Therefore, semantics belongs to social studies and potentially underpins the integrity of the social sciences.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>27-31</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326012\" id=\"question-wrapper-326012\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What point is made in the first paragraph?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. People with medical qualifications tend to give more trustworthy advice.</li> <li>B. Semantics focuses on the definition of words.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"fb15474f-1c15-4f02-a5f1-8604116ce139\">People respond to symbols<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> according to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"9a4d6859-0d78-4853-ac18-3b7eacc723c8\">reaction patterns they have acquired<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Humans and other animals interpret symbols in similar ways.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326013\" id=\"question-wrapper-326013\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the second paragraph, people are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"ff1fd475-4f79-44e9-a8da-3c5822959434\">judged by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. their level of education.</li> <li>B. the closely-related people around them.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"3ab38337-b111-4d5d-9177-a96023a5c3c3\">how conventional their responses are<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>D. complex situations.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326014\" id=\"question-wrapper-326014\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What point is made in the third paragraph?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d5056721-ed54-4d5f-b289-b6cb07513330\">Standard ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"bb3b6c2d-67b7-4e08-be65-0bd8d1ff0bf1\">incapable of defining words precisely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>B. A dictionary often provides clear definitions of words.</li> <li>C. Infinite regress is an uncommon occurrence in defining words.</li> <li>D. Mathematicians were the first to identify infinite regress in language.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326015\" id=\"question-wrapper-326015\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the writer suggest about Louis Armstrong?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. He is a language expert.</li> <li>B. He demonstrated there are similarities between music and language.</li> <li>C. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"a1b44569-ca0b-4076-873d-eb270b29d0d3\">provided insights into how words are defined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>D. His good skill in music helped him do research in other fields.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326016\" id=\"question-wrapper-326016\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the writer intend to show with the example of the “personnel manager”?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The manager hates applicants from Harvard University.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"4a239b7d-fc1f-40b2-8412-f262b47a0aa8\">Meaning can be unique to one person<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>C. The manager has a bad memory of Harvard University.</li> <li>D. People’s behaviour usually doesn’t agree with their words.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes </span></i><i><b><span>32-35</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet, write:</span></i></p><p><b><span>YES</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NO</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NOT</span></b> <b><span>GIVEN</span></b><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326017\" id=\"question-wrapper-326017\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some statements are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e2ce854d-b5ac-4566-88cf-1f9a8e137195\">incapable of being proved or disproved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326018\" id=\"question-wrapper-326018\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Meaning that is unique to an individual is less worthy of study than shared meanings. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326019\" id=\"question-wrapper-326019\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Flags and words influence people because of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"158109f9-4c57-4f05-9204-817ed1b9b567\">what they represent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> rather than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"408b5013-c53b-4448-bdee-0533f9f4a631\">their physical form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326020\" id=\"question-wrapper-326020\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"e8f00f7c-b515-47bb-a4bd-c6d101081b26\">A story can still be perceived by its listeners as a coherent narrative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> without being understood.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, below.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, </span></i><i><b><span>A-H</span></b></i><i><span>, in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>36-40</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0c3723e6-1d85-4949-9927-b6d964932123\">fail to provoke the intended emotional effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"c311463e-bf0e-4fb3-80ea-fdbd95409827\">contribute to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> a person's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"16d4671a-4a76-4114-ba9e-aca93f56287f\">ability to interpret language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> is a symbol that has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"55c4ce3c-d21f-48a7-aa1e-fc43d7f02b2d\">lost its meaning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> can be understood only in its social context.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"7a87ccab-8d26-432f-9984-af9953d3dc24\">provide only an inadequate definition of meaning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><b><span>F.</span></b><span> reflects the variability of human behaviours.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><b><span>G.</span></b><span> emphasizes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"5060891c-3048-495f-8c44-f9bfe0286126\">the importance of analyzing how words were used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><b><span>H.</span></b><span> suggests that certain types of behaviour carry more meaning than others.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326021\" id=\"question-wrapper-326021\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A comic strip </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326022\" id=\"question-wrapper-326022\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A dictionary </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326023\" id=\"question-wrapper-326023\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Bridgman </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326024\" id=\"question-wrapper-326024\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"70bc8ef4-a576-400b-89bc-80ebf77c02e7\">A story told in a language the audience cannot understand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326025\" id=\"question-wrapper-326025\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A dollar bill <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"f10bf03d-556a-4859-ba3b-8f9e9250a75b\">without public acceptance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"9a4d6859-0d78-4853-ac18-3b7eacc723c8","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"reaction patterns they have acquired","passagePhrase":"trained patterns of response ... pattern of reactions"},{"uid":"fb15474f-1c15-4f02-a5f1-8604116ce139","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"People respond to symbols","passagePhrase":"the ways we act in response ... to symbols"},{"uid":"c311463e-bf0e-4fb3-80ea-fdbd95409827","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"contribute to","passagePhrase":"highly relevant to the development of"},{"uid":"16d4671a-4a76-4114-ba9e-aca93f56287f","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"ability to interpret language","passagePhrase":"linguistic \"meaning-making"},{"uid":"3ab38337-b111-4d5d-9177-a96023a5c3c3","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"how conventional their responses are","passagePhrase":"when people's semantic habits are reasonably similar to those of most people around them ... their semantic habits are noticeably different from those of others"},{"uid":"ff1fd475-4f79-44e9-a8da-3c5822959434","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"judged by","passagePhrase":"regarded as"},{"uid":"d5056721-ed54-4d5f-b289-b6cb07513330","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Standard ways","passagePhrase":"as a dictionary does ... defining words with more words"},{"uid":"7a87ccab-8d26-432f-9984-af9953d3dc24","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"provide only an inadequate definition of meaning","passagePhrase":"explain the word with more words"},{"uid":"bb3b6c2d-67b7-4e08-be65-0bd8d1ff0bf1","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"incapable of defining words precisely","passagePhrase":"leads people ... into"},{"uid":"7a87ccab-8d26-432f-9984-af9953d3dc24 bb3b6c2d-67b7-4e08-be65-0bd8d1ff0bf1","qNum":"29 37","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"an \"infinite regress"},{"uid":"a1b44569-ca0b-4076-873d-eb270b29d0d3","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"provided insights into how words are defined","passagePhrase":"proving himself to be an intuitive semanticist"},{"uid":"5060891c-3048-495f-8c44-f9bfe0286126","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"the importance of analyzing how words were used","passagePhrase":"true meaning of a term is to be found by observing what a man does with it ... the meaning of a scientific term lies in the operations—the things that are done"},{"uid":"e2ce854d-b5ac-4566-88cf-1f9a8e137195","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"incapable of being proved or disproved","passagePhrase":"what operations could we perform to demonstrate its accuracy or inaccuracy"},{"uid":"4a239b7d-fc1f-40b2-8412-f262b47a0aa8","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Meaning can be unique to one person","passagePhrase":"meaning\" at work ... not a meaning that can be found in dictionaries"},{"uid":"408b5013-c53b-4448-bdee-0533f9f4a631","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"their physical form","passagePhrase":"a piece of cloth ... a set of sounds"},{"uid":"158109f9-4c57-4f05-9204-817ed1b9b567","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"what they represent","passagePhrase":"the meaning with which it has been symbolically endowed"},{"uid":"70bc8ef4-a576-400b-89bc-80ebf77c02e7","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"A story told in a language the audience cannot understand","passagePhrase":"tell a shockingly obscene story in Arabic or Hindustani or Swahili before an audience that understood only English"},{"uid":"0c3723e6-1d85-4949-9927-b6d964932123","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"fail to provoke the intended emotional effect","passagePhrase":"no one would blush or be angry"},{"uid":"f10bf03d-556a-4859-ba3b-8f9e9250a75b","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"without public acceptance","passagePhrase":"agreement were to break down"},{"uid":"55c4ce3c-d21f-48a7-aa1e-fc43d7f02b2d","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"lost its meaning","passagePhrase":"become only a scrap of paper"}]},"reading_u2_85":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions</span></b> <b><span>1-13</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Great Fire of London</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"1\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> The Great Fire of London swept through London in September 1666, devastating many buildings, including 13,200 houses and 87 parish churches. The Royal Exchange, the Guildhall and St. Paul's Cathedral, all built during the Middle Ages, were also destroyed. Although <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"557dd412-bd30-457c-a4b5-2697ecb8ea1a\">the verified death toll was only six people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, it is unknown how many people died in the Great Fire of London, because many more died from indirect causes. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c\">The financial losses caused by the fire were estimated to be £10 million<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, at a time when London's annual income was only £12,000. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 11\" data-uid=\"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c c340ffcb-ef1a-47eb-8f56-2703132f9bf9\">Many people</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c\"> were </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 11\" data-uid=\"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c d1a4bd16-234d-421f-be5a-818c95440ff0\">financially ruined</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c\">, and </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 11\" data-uid=\"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c d1a4bd16-234d-421f-be5a-818c95440ff0\">debtors</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c\">' prisons became overcrowded</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"2\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> The Great Fire of London started on Sunday, 2 September 1666, in a baker's shop in Pudding Lane, belonging to Thomas Farynor. Although he claimed to have extinguished the fire, three hours later, at 1 a.m., his house was a blazing inferno. It is not certain how the fire actually began, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"bb4fd775-0dc8-4cac-aa53-dd8c2f30c1b4\">it is likely that it was caused by a spark from Farynor's oven falling onto a pile of fuel nearby<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. In 1979, archaeologists excavated the remains of a burnt-out shop on Pudding Lane that was very close to the bakery where the fire started. In the cellar, they found the charred remnants of 20 barrels of pitch. Pitch burns very easily and would have helped to spread the fire.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"3\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"da401a80-8660-4d9e-86a5-a924f7726c61\">The fire spread quickly down Pudding Lane<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"da401a80-8660-4d9e-86a5-a924f7726c61\">carried on down Fish Hill<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"da401a80-8660-4d9e-86a5-a924f7726c61\">towards the Thames<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. The fire continued to spread rapidly, helped by a strong wind from the east. When it reached the Thames, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"da401a80-8660-4d9e-86a5-a924f7726c61\">it hit warehouses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> that were stocked with combustible products, such as oil and rope. Fortunately, the fire could not spread south of the river, because a previous blaze in 1633 had already wrecked a section of London Bridge. As the fire was spreading so quickly, most Londoners concentrated on escaping rather than fighting the fire.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"4\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> In the 17th century, people were not as aware of the dangers of fire as they are today. Buildings were made of timber covered in pitch and tightly packed together. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"aee80240-b939-4443-a93e-7ec4abfed908\">The design of buildings meant flames could easily spread from building to building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Following a long, dry summer, the city was suffering a drought; water was scarce, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"aee80240-b939-4443-a93e-7ec4abfed908\">the wooden houses had dried out, making them easier to burn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"5\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> Samuel Pepys, a diarist of the period and Clerk to the Royal Navy, observed the fire and recommended to the King that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"9bfd5114-e029-49e4-b989-5b4de20ae0ad\">buildings should be pulled down, as it could be the only way to stop the fire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. The Mayor made the order to pull down burning houses using fire hooks, but the fire continued to spread. Pepys then spoke to the Admiral of the Navy, and they agreed that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"9bfd5114-e029-49e4-b989-5b4de20ae0ad\">they should blow up houses in the path of the fire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. The hope was that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"9bfd5114-e029-49e4-b989-5b4de20ae0ad\">by doing this, they would create a space to stop the fire spreading from house to house<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. The Navy carried out the request and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"9bfd5114-e029-49e4-b989-5b4de20ae0ad\">by the next morning, the fire had been successfully stopped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"6\"><b><span>F.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9\">London had to be almost totally reconstructed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, and many people went to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"75a51ed6-3951-48e3-89c0-1e27b6f1f0f0\">the fields outside London<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. They stayed there for many days, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"7ed972a5-79c5-4646-8735-a1d52cb23554\">sheltering in tents and shacks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, and some people were forced to live in this way for months and even years. Throughout 1667, people cleared rubble and surveyed the burnt area. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9\">Much time was spent planning new street layouts and drawing up new building regulations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9\">Public buildings were paid for with money from a new coal tax<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, but by the end of the year only 150 new houses had been built. The new regulations were designed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"dbb786c0-8321-4eeb-b6a3-c039e8e11bf0\">prevent such a disaster from happening again<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 12\" data-uid=\"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9 e7380f99-ab29-44d8-9d34-8ac21ad86ae4\">Houses now had to</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9\"> be </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 12\" data-uid=\"108af179-326c-40e6-9896-dc6f442a8704 633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9\">faced in</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9\"> brick instead of wood</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9\">Some streets were widened, and two new streets were created<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9\">Pavements and new sewers were laid, and London's quaysides were improved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. Initially, however, only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f9990d69-0249-43e2-9cee-ee30bfece175\">temporary buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> were erected that were ill-equipped, and this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f5ad1994-5afb-4a77-8438-355e2a384319\">enabled the plague<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, which was common in London at that time, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f5ad1994-5afb-4a77-8438-355e2a384319\">to spread easily<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. Many people died from this and the harsh winter that followed the fire.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"7\"><b><span>G.</span></b><span> In 1666, there was no organised fire brigade. Firefighting was very basic, with little skill or knowledge involved. Leather buckets, axes and water squirts were used to fight the fire, but they had little effect. As a result of the Great Fire of London, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"6fb825d9-a59a-41eb-b77a-7efe5718af72\">early fire brigades were formed by insurance companies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. Building insurance was very profitable, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"6fb825d9-a59a-41eb-b77a-7efe5718af72\">many more insurance companies were set up, establishing their own fire brigades<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. These brigades were sent to insured properties if a fire occurred to minimise damage and cost. Firemarks were used to identify – and advertise – different insurance companies. They were placed on the outside of an insured building and brigades would use them to determine whether a building was insured by them. If a building was on fire, several brigades would attend. If they did not see their specific firemark attached to the building, they would leave the property to burn. Some old firemarks can still be seen on London buildings today. Also, firefighters wore brightly coloured uniforms to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"8ec160cf-0f83-4e61-a9d9-3671ec3ae700\">distinguish themselves from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"2395cd67-d81e-4736-800d-6bc12d712336\">rival insurance brigades<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. Although this was a step in the right direction, firefighters received little training, and the equipment used remained very basic.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>The text on the previous pages has 7 paragraphs (</span><b><span>A – G</span></b><span>).</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct number (</span></i><i><b><span>i – x</span></b></i><i><span>) in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>1-7</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><b><span>i. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"aee80240-b939-4443-a93e-7ec4abfed908\">Vulnerable Buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><b><span>ii.</span></b><span> The Effect on Trade</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><b><span>iii</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"bb4fd775-0dc8-4cac-aa53-dd8c2f30c1b4\">The Likely Origin of the Disaster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><b><span>iv</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"6fb825d9-a59a-41eb-b77a-7efe5718af72\">The Emergence of Firefighting Services<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><b><span>v.</span></b><span> Food Shortages</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><b><span>vi.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"da401a80-8660-4d9e-86a5-a924f7726c61\">The Movement of the Fire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><b><span>vii.</span></b><span> The Effects of the Smoke</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><b><span>viii.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"9bfd5114-e029-49e4-b989-5b4de20ae0ad\">Extinguishing the Fire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><b><span>ix.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c\">The Costs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"x\"><b><span>x.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9\">A New London<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326026\" id=\"question-wrapper-326026\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ix</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326027\" id=\"question-wrapper-326027\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326028\" id=\"question-wrapper-326028\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326029\" id=\"question-wrapper-326029\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326030\" id=\"question-wrapper-326030\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326031\" id=\"question-wrapper-326031\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">x</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326032\" id=\"question-wrapper-326032\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph G </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>FOUR</span></b></i><i><span> letters, </span></i><i><b><span>A-G</span></b></i><i><span>. Write the correct letter, </span></i><i><b><span>A-G</span></b></i><i><span>, in any order in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>8-11</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><span>What </span><b><span>FOUR</span></b><span> of the following were consequences of the Great Fire of London?</span></p><p><b><span>A</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"557dd412-bd30-457c-a4b5-2697ecb8ea1a\">Only a small number of fatalities were officially recorded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> London’s yearly income fell to £12,000 after the disaster.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> Some residents <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"7ed972a5-79c5-4646-8735-a1d52cb23554\">remained in makeshift accommodation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"75a51ed6-3951-48e3-89c0-1e27b6f1f0f0\">outside the city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> for years.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> Most of the permanent rebuilding had been completed by the end of 1667.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f9990d69-0249-43e2-9cee-ee30bfece175\">Temporary accommodation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f5ad1994-5afb-4a77-8438-355e2a384319\">increased the transmission of disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> The city authorities established the first organised firefighting service.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"c340ffcb-ef1a-47eb-8f56-2703132f9bf9\">A large number of London citizens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> were left <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"d1a4bd16-234d-421f-be5a-818c95440ff0\">unable to meet their financial obligations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326033\" id=\"question-wrapper-326033\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/E/G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326034\" id=\"question-wrapper-326034\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/E/G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326035\" id=\"question-wrapper-326035\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/E/G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326036\" id=\"question-wrapper-326036\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/E/G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Write</span> <b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>12</span></b></i><i><span> and </span></i><i><b><span>13</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326037\" id=\"question-wrapper-326037\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>One measure to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"dbb786c0-8321-4eeb-b6a3-c039e8e11bf0\">prevent further fires<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> was to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"e7380f99-ab29-44d8-9d34-8ac21ad86ae4\">ensure that London houses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"108af179-326c-40e6-9896-dc6f442a8704\">have<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"108af179-326c-40e6-9896-dc6f442a8704\">facades<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in the future.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">brick</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326038\" id=\"question-wrapper-326038\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Firefighters working for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"2395cd67-d81e-4736-800d-6bc12d712336\">competing insurers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"8ec160cf-0f83-4e61-a9d9-3671ec3ae700\">be told apart<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> by their (13)_______.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">uniforms</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"557dd412-bd30-457c-a4b5-2697ecb8ea1a","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Only a small number of fatalities were officially recorded","passagePhrase":"the verified death toll was only six people"},{"uid":"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"The Costs","passagePhrase":"The financial losses caused by the fire were estimated to be £10 million ... were ... , and ... ' prisons became overcrowded"},{"uid":"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c c340ffcb-ef1a-47eb-8f56-2703132f9bf9","qNum":"1 11","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Many people"},{"uid":"63c42aea-f1f7-44a7-8f0f-17303f82f90c d1a4bd16-234d-421f-be5a-818c95440ff0","qNum":"1 11","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"financially ruined ... debtors"},{"uid":"bb4fd775-0dc8-4cac-aa53-dd8c2f30c1b4","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"The Likely Origin of the Disaster","passagePhrase":"it is likely that it was caused by a spark from Farynor's oven falling onto a pile of fuel nearby"},{"uid":"da401a80-8660-4d9e-86a5-a924f7726c61","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"The Movement of the Fire","passagePhrase":"The fire spread quickly down Pudding Lane ... carried on down Fish Hill ... towards the Thames ... it hit warehouses"},{"uid":"aee80240-b939-4443-a93e-7ec4abfed908","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Vulnerable Buildings","passagePhrase":"The design of buildings meant flames could easily spread from building to building ... the wooden houses had dried out, making them easier to burn"},{"uid":"9bfd5114-e029-49e4-b989-5b4de20ae0ad","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Extinguishing the Fire","passagePhrase":"buildings should be pulled down, as it could be the only way to stop the fire ... they should blow up houses in the path of the fire ... by doing this, they would create a space to stop the fire spreading from house to house ... by the next morning, the fire had been successfully stopped"},{"uid":"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"A New London","passagePhrase":"London had to be almost totally reconstructed ... Much time was spent planning new street layouts and drawing up new building regulations ... Public buildings were paid for with money from a new coal tax ... be ... brick instead of wood ... Some streets were widened, and two new streets were created ... Pavements and new sewers were laid, and London's quaysides were improved"},{"uid":"75a51ed6-3951-48e3-89c0-1e27b6f1f0f0","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"outside the city","passagePhrase":"the fields outside London"},{"uid":"7ed972a5-79c5-4646-8735-a1d52cb23554","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"remained in makeshift accommodation","passagePhrase":"sheltering in tents and shacks"},{"uid":"dbb786c0-8321-4eeb-b6a3-c039e8e11bf0","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"prevent further fires","passagePhrase":"prevent such a disaster from happening again"},{"uid":"633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9 e7380f99-ab29-44d8-9d34-8ac21ad86ae4","qNum":"6 12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Houses now had to"},{"uid":"108af179-326c-40e6-9896-dc6f442a8704 633dc590-b25d-4c3c-a7e2-b6add4b26eb9","qNum":"6 12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"faced in"},{"uid":"f9990d69-0249-43e2-9cee-ee30bfece175","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"Temporary accommodation","passagePhrase":"temporary buildings"},{"uid":"f5ad1994-5afb-4a77-8438-355e2a384319","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"increased the transmission of disease","passagePhrase":"enabled the plague ... to spread easily"},{"uid":"6fb825d9-a59a-41eb-b77a-7efe5718af72","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"The Emergence of Firefighting Services","passagePhrase":"early fire brigades were formed by insurance companies ... many more insurance companies were set up, establishing their own fire brigades"},{"uid":"8ec160cf-0f83-4e61-a9d9-3671ec3ae700","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"be told apart","passagePhrase":"distinguish themselves from"},{"uid":"2395cd67-d81e-4736-800d-6bc12d712336","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"competing insurers","passagePhrase":"rival insurance brigades"},{"uid":"c340ffcb-ef1a-47eb-8f56-2703132f9bf9","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"A large number of London citizens","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"d1a4bd16-234d-421f-be5a-818c95440ff0","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"unable to meet their financial obligations","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"e7380f99-ab29-44d8-9d34-8ac21ad86ae4","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"ensure that London houses","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"108af179-326c-40e6-9896-dc6f442a8704","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"have ... facades","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_86":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 14-26</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Giant Panda and Global Warming</span></b></p><p><span>Despite giant pandas being star attractions at zoos around the world—bringing joy to millions of visitors each year—and despite the birth of a giant panda cub in captivity always making headline news, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"5b97a9f1-d731-48b9-be2b-61b7cc62f03d\">the survival<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of giant pandas <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c8f1d232-eeeb-474d-85b3-8b6b4b455565\">in the wild<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"5b97a9f1-d731-48b9-be2b-61b7cc62f03d\">is highly uncertain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>This charismatic and universally loved species is one of the rarest and most endangered bears in the world. It was once found throughout China, northern Vietnam and northern Burma, but the giant panda is now found in the wild in just six isolated mountain ranges in the provinces of Gansu, Shaanxi and Sichuan in south-central China. This distinctive <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9c48e38b-5fab-405d-83f4-d5641f71beab\">black-and-white<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> creature <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1d9a35d4-1a3c-4b7c-b940-c3a4793a341f\">typically leads a solitary life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. It is a good swimmer and an excellent tree climber, but it spends most of its time feeding.</span></p><p><span>Three-quarters of all wild giant pandas now live in nature reserves, but despite this, they are still endangered. The wild giant panda population <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"a2f58e8c-d6fb-4fba-b9c8-e6a1c2586712\">declined by nearly half<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> between the early 1970s and the late 1990s, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"8eb198ae-a610-4e5a-b3a1-701d59f27aa7\">mainly owing to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"53361bb1-cf12-4475-aa4a-3c72087ae294\">habitat destruction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> and poaching. Habitat loss and fragmentation remain the main threats today, and these processes occur in a variety of ways. For example, roads and railways increasingly cut through forests, isolating giant panda populations and reducing their opportunities to breed.</span></p><p><span>It is well known that the giant panda <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"a7d2a944-62cc-4cfa-a0f4-691b69c4883c\">feeds almost exclusively on bamboo<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, despite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ce87bb6c-993d-45bc-9545-76e2cfd3ff00\">its taxonomic classification as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> a carnivore. Because of this, scientists from Michigan State University have recently produced comprehensive <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d5f0f089-8d29-4cca-bc6f-e487af3d1eca\">forecasts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"988ca498-df0b-4e24-8559-cc9559b16f77\">climate change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> may affect the most common bamboo species covering the forest floors of prime giant panda habitat in north-western China. Even the most optimistic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d5f0f089-8d29-4cca-bc6f-e487af3d1eca\">scenarios<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> indicate that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"109916d3-0592-419c-904e-c6304e06a318\">bamboo die-offs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> could make this giant panda <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"109916d3-0592-419c-904e-c6304e06a318\">habitat inhospitable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> by the end of the twenty-first century.</span></p><p><span>The scientists studied possible climate-change scenarios in the Qinling Mountains in Shaanxi Province. Located at the northern edge of the giant panda’s range in China, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"2a69b75c-9232-410d-9416-975049d9cc03\">the Qinling Mountains are home to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> about 275 wild giant pandas, representing 17 per cent of the remaining wild population. Having been isolated by thousands of years of human settlement around the mountain range, the Qinling giant pandas are genetically distinct from other giant pandas. The geographic isolation of this population makes it particularly valuable for conservation but also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"148f2d5e-722c-4981-889a-c0e54ddb37b9\">especially vulnerable to climate change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. The study aims to improve understanding of the effects of climate change and provide scientific evidence to support sound conservation decisions. Examining the effects of climate change on bamboo can help conservationists prepare for the challenges that giant pandas are likely to face in the future.</span></p><p><span>Bamboo is a vital component of forest ecosystems, serving not only as the preferred food of giant pandas but also as an essential source of food and shelter for other wildlife, including endangered species such as the ploughshare tortoise and the purple-winged ground-dove. However, bamboo can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"494cec50-0b77-4db3-9ec5-f418b86b82fb\">a </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"6ea0ba45-7d19-42d2-bd17-8276e6e2a05f\">risky<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"494cec50-0b77-4db3-9ec5-f418b86b82fb\"> food source on which to depend<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> because of its reproductive cycle. The species studied flower and reproduce only once every 30 to 35 years, which limits their ability to adapt to a changing climate and can jeopardise the food supply. Bamboo naturally dies off every 40 to 120 years, depending on the species. Before human activity transformed the landscape, giant pandas could move from areas affected by bamboo die-offs to areas where healthy bamboo remained. However, as human populations have expanded and fragmented giant panda habitats, the animals have become unable to “follow” the bamboo and can therefore become trapped in areas without sufficient food.</span></p><p><span>The Michigan scientists developed specialised models using field data on bamboo distribution, multiple climate projections, historical records of precipitation and temperature, and greenhouse-gas emissions scenarios to evaluate how the three dominant bamboo species would fare in China’s Qinling Mountains. Few scientists have studied bamboo in detail, but limited <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"98ee3fae-e299-4e8a-8eaf-d18ad94118d7\">evidence from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> fossil records suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"db926c4c-8a28-4d48-b56f-22db9f7078e0\">bamboo growth and distribution have shifted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"4eca879d-9d5f-4186-b055-170e96c6b7b4\">as climatic conditions have changed over time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The fate of giant pandas will be determined not only by nature but also by human actions. If, as the study’s models predict, large areas of bamboo become unavailable because of climate change and human-caused changes in land use, giant pandas will lose clear, accessible routes between feeding areas. The models can guide <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"dc6e6042-e451-4a06-98ac-103b238a812b\">authorities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> in developing proactive conservation plans, such as protecting areas that are likely to remain climatically suitable and provide adequate food, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"dc6e6042-e451-4a06-98ac-103b238a812b\">creating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> habitat corridors that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"667bfa1f-71a0-4dde-9485-879303b9706d\">allow giant pandas to move away from areas affected by bamboo die-offs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The results of the Michigan study show that climate change will severely affect both giant panda habitat and efforts to protect it. The models predict that climate change could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"33b9dfc6-a795-498f-8810-e762d2505616\">reduce suitable giant panda habitat by nearly 60 per cent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> over the next 70 years. The research provides <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"8b3d1165-3636-4d44-adc1-54df47f48bc3\">compelling evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"935c4f47-4dc2-4d10-94d9-dc5866342a49\">protected areas need to be expanded throughout much of the species’ current range<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Independent conservationists have also advised China to increase connectivity between existing habitats and areas that may become suitable in the future. Although the Michigan study does not directly address this issue, it is clear that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"2fba49f4-0c0b-4832-ab9c-487357d624d1\">further research is needed to determine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"bc3a2f08-0ce3-4a0d-8d86-196659d979c2\">how best to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"971ca86c-1c1c-411f-8593-f23cb85e1e26\">maintain connectivity between suitable giant panda habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"4abbadfc-51f5-42dd-ba04-46b80ba1aaca\">conserve habitats for other species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Urgent action is essential before giant panda numbers fall too low and genetic diversity becomes too limited.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the words in the box below.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>14-18</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><span>Despite its global (14)________, the giant panda <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"5b97a9f1-d731-48b9-be2b-61b7cc62f03d\">remains at risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c8f1d232-eeeb-474d-85b3-8b6b4b455565\">outside captivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and is now confined to six disconnected mountain regions. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1d9a35d4-1a3c-4b7c-b940-c3a4793a341f\">generally lives by itself<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, and its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9c48e38b-5fab-405d-83f4-d5641f71beab\">appearance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> makes it instantly (15)________. Although it is an able swimmer and climber, feeding takes up most of its time. Between the early 1970s and the late 1990s, the wild population <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"a2f58e8c-d6fb-4fba-b9c8-e6a1c2586712\">almost halved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"8eb198ae-a610-4e5a-b3a1-701d59f27aa7\">chiefly because of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> (16)________ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"53361bb1-cf12-4475-aa4a-3c72087ae294\">the loss of living space<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Despite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"a7d2a944-62cc-4cfa-a0f4-691b69c4883c\">relying almost entirely on bamboo<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ce87bb6c-993d-45bc-9545-76e2cfd3ff00\">scientists regard the species as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> a (17)________. Current <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d5f0f089-8d29-4cca-bc6f-e487af3d1eca\">projections<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> indicate that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"988ca498-df0b-4e24-8559-cc9559b16f77\">rising temperatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> may have (18)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"109916d3-0592-419c-904e-c6304e06a318\">effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> on bamboo within panda habitat by 2100.</span></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>popularity</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>hunting</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>carnivore</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>distribution</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>disease</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>herbivore</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>identifiable</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>pollution</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>negative</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>approachable</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>gradual</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>unpredictable</span></b></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326039\" id=\"question-wrapper-326039\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">popularity</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326040\" id=\"question-wrapper-326040\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">identifiable</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326041\" id=\"question-wrapper-326041\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">hunting</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326042\" id=\"question-wrapper-326042\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">carnivore</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326043\" id=\"question-wrapper-326043\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">negative</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below.</span></p><p><span>Write</span> <b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>19-23</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326044\" id=\"question-wrapper-326044\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What proportion of wild giant pandas <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"2a69b75c-9232-410d-9416-975049d9cc03\">live in the Qinling Mountains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">17% [OR] 17 per( )cent</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326045\" id=\"question-wrapper-326045\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What feature of the Qinling population means that it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"148f2d5e-722c-4981-889a-c0e54ddb37b9\">highly susceptible to a changing climate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) geographic isolation</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326046\" id=\"question-wrapper-326046\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which specific attribute of bamboo makes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"494cec50-0b77-4db3-9ec5-f418b86b82fb\">an exclusive diet of it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"6ea0ba45-7d19-42d2-bd17-8276e6e2a05f\">hazardous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> to pandas?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(its) reproductive cycle</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326047\" id=\"question-wrapper-326047\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"98ee3fae-e299-4e8a-8eaf-d18ad94118d7\">source indicates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"db926c4c-8a28-4d48-b56f-22db9f7078e0\">bamboo has changed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"4eca879d-9d5f-4186-b055-170e96c6b7b4\">in response to earlier climates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">fossil records</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326048\" id=\"question-wrapper-326048\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"dc6e6042-e451-4a06-98ac-103b238a812b\">authorities establish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"667bfa1f-71a0-4dde-9485-879303b9706d\">help pandas reach areas where food remains available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">habitat corridors</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending (</span><b><span>A – E</span></b><span>) below.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter (</span></i><i><b><span>A – E</span></b></i><i><span>) in answer boxes </span></i><i><b><span>24-26</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> bring heavier rainfall to areas occupied by pandas.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"971ca86c-1c1c-411f-8593-f23cb85e1e26\">keep suitable panda areas linked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"4abbadfc-51f5-42dd-ba04-46b80ba1aaca\">preserve habitat used by other wildlife<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"33b9dfc6-a795-498f-8810-e762d2505616\">leave wild pandas with far less usable territory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> expand captive-breeding activity in zoos.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"935c4f47-4dc2-4d10-94d9-dc5866342a49\">bring more of the panda’s present range under formal protection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326049\" id=\"question-wrapper-326049\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Michigan models indicate that a changing climate will</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326050\" id=\"question-wrapper-326050\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Michigan study’s findings are presented as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"8b3d1165-3636-4d44-adc1-54df47f48bc3\">strong justification<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326051\" id=\"question-wrapper-326051\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"2fba49f4-0c0b-4832-ab9c-487357d624d1\">Scientists still need to establish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"bc3a2f08-0ce3-4a0d-8d86-196659d979c2\">the most effective ways to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"5b97a9f1-d731-48b9-be2b-61b7cc62f03d","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"remains at risk","passagePhrase":"the survival ... is highly uncertain"},{"uid":"c8f1d232-eeeb-474d-85b3-8b6b4b455565","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"outside captivity","passagePhrase":"in the wild"},{"uid":"9c48e38b-5fab-405d-83f4-d5641f71beab","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"appearance","passagePhrase":"black-and-white"},{"uid":"1d9a35d4-1a3c-4b7c-b940-c3a4793a341f","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"generally lives by itself","passagePhrase":"typically leads a solitary life"},{"uid":"a2f58e8c-d6fb-4fba-b9c8-e6a1c2586712","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"almost halved","passagePhrase":"declined by nearly half"},{"uid":"8eb198ae-a610-4e5a-b3a1-701d59f27aa7","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"chiefly because of","passagePhrase":"mainly owing to"},{"uid":"53361bb1-cf12-4475-aa4a-3c72087ae294","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"the loss of living space","passagePhrase":"habitat destruction"},{"uid":"a7d2a944-62cc-4cfa-a0f4-691b69c4883c","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"relying almost entirely on bamboo","passagePhrase":"feeds almost exclusively on bamboo"},{"uid":"ce87bb6c-993d-45bc-9545-76e2cfd3ff00","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"scientists regard the species as","passagePhrase":"its taxonomic classification as"},{"uid":"d5f0f089-8d29-4cca-bc6f-e487af3d1eca","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"projections","passagePhrase":"forecasts ... scenarios"},{"uid":"988ca498-df0b-4e24-8559-cc9559b16f77","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"rising temperatures","passagePhrase":"climate change"},{"uid":"109916d3-0592-419c-904e-c6304e06a318","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"effects","passagePhrase":"bamboo die-offs ... habitat inhospitable"},{"uid":"2a69b75c-9232-410d-9416-975049d9cc03","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"live in the Qinling Mountains","passagePhrase":"the Qinling Mountains are home to"},{"uid":"148f2d5e-722c-4981-889a-c0e54ddb37b9","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"highly susceptible to a changing climate","passagePhrase":"especially vulnerable to climate change"},{"uid":"494cec50-0b77-4db3-9ec5-f418b86b82fb","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"an exclusive diet of it","passagePhrase":"a ... food source on which to depend"},{"uid":"6ea0ba45-7d19-42d2-bd17-8276e6e2a05f","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"hazardous","passagePhrase":"risky"},{"uid":"98ee3fae-e299-4e8a-8eaf-d18ad94118d7","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"source indicates","passagePhrase":"evidence from"},{"uid":"db926c4c-8a28-4d48-b56f-22db9f7078e0","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"bamboo has changed","passagePhrase":"bamboo growth and distribution have shifted"},{"uid":"4eca879d-9d5f-4186-b055-170e96c6b7b4","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"in response to earlier climates","passagePhrase":"as climatic conditions have changed over time"},{"uid":"dc6e6042-e451-4a06-98ac-103b238a812b","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"authorities establish","passagePhrase":"authorities ... creating"},{"uid":"667bfa1f-71a0-4dde-9485-879303b9706d","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"help pandas reach areas where food remains available","passagePhrase":"allow giant pandas to move away from areas affected by bamboo die-offs"},{"uid":"33b9dfc6-a795-498f-8810-e762d2505616","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"leave wild pandas with far less usable territory","passagePhrase":"reduce suitable giant panda habitat by nearly 60 per cent"},{"uid":"8b3d1165-3636-4d44-adc1-54df47f48bc3","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"strong justification","passagePhrase":"compelling evidence"},{"uid":"935c4f47-4dc2-4d10-94d9-dc5866342a49","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"bring more of the panda’s present range under formal protection","passagePhrase":"protected areas need to be expanded throughout much of the species’ current range"},{"uid":"2fba49f4-0c0b-4832-ab9c-487357d624d1","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Scientists still need to establish","passagePhrase":"further research is needed to determine"},{"uid":"bc3a2f08-0ce3-4a0d-8d86-196659d979c2","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"the most effective ways to","passagePhrase":"how best to"},{"uid":"971ca86c-1c1c-411f-8593-f23cb85e1e26","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"keep suitable panda areas linked","passagePhrase":"maintain connectivity between suitable giant panda habitats"},{"uid":"4abbadfc-51f5-42dd-ba04-46b80ba1aaca","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"preserve habitat used by other wildlife","passagePhrase":"conserve habitats for other species"}]},"reading_u2_87":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 27-40</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Children and Playing</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>Childhood is in every sense a preparation for adulthood, in terms of both physical and mental maturation. It is an essential stepping stone that allows all young people to adjust optimally to the requirements that collective expectations and rules set for any adult individual, so that they can integrate into, benefit from and enjoy living within society. By definition, individuals who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"74bdc662-525a-490d-bde1-52aa2f331fee\">fail to meet these criteria<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"39d76769-4c52-4944-8fd7-852b425b9368\">are classified as anti-social<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> or in some way <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"74bdc662-525a-490d-bde1-52aa2f331fee\">incapable of coping with societal expectations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, and therefore unlikely to experience a positive quality of life. Aspects of human brain maturation continue from birth until the late teens. During this long developmental period, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"24c96f9e-b11a-40d4-bfeb-be03ceb67bce\">a child<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> will learn from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"24c96f9e-b11a-40d4-bfeb-be03ceb67bce\">interactions with parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, siblings, relatives, peers and teachers, and will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"1e03c899-294e-43fd-943f-0091d1f584f7\">have both positive and negative emotional experiences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> as a result of these and other life events. Not only is this a phase of intense adaptation and information gathering, but the process of maturation is organised so as to structure it progressively in the most effective way. Of course, a child is strongly influenced by being taught by other individuals, but every child also has at their disposal a highly effective self-help tuition kit. This is play.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>Play is a fundamental behaviour of juveniles in all species of birds and mammals. Although adults can also show it, at a much reduced frequency, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f3c88a04-fa9a-49ef-b5d4-3d70a7f48ed0\">they often give the impression that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"6cabc795-bea7-4161-bcd7-e72de64099f0\">an attractive but wasteful expression of leisure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that only the young, with minimal responsibilities, can indulge in. In truth, it is this play of youth that prepares an individual in an important variety of ways for adulthood. While the building blocks for brain development are created before birth, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"a5b5a4d6-e4de-4277-afed-d3c720855c2a\">the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"7e3eabbb-3f37-46c0-b51e-545c465958d9\">only about 25 per cent complete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"a5b5a4d6-e4de-4277-afed-d3c720855c2a\">at birth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. The brain maturation process continues during the first two decades of life, although, of course, brain networks can continue to adapt in the light of experience throughout the whole of an individual's life. The types of play that humans exhibit change during the various maturational stages of the brain.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cee951db-aefb-4250-ba8c-ec3c38b8543e\">Between birth and age one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, play involves practice of the movement and sensory systems, with interest in patterns, colours and sounds, exploring textures, grasping objects and performing simple actions with them. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"494849ff-1f09-4770-a604-0089348ed09f\">Play is highly repetitive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, like a form of practice. Over the next two years or so, examples of pretend play are seen, indicating that individuals are capable of symbolic thought. The brain's specialised language production and comprehension regions develop as language communication expands rapidly. Language is also played with rhymes, songs and 'silly' sounds, and pretend characters can talk, express emotions and perform actions. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"24686416-44dd-407f-85fa-5981459d9b9a\">Between the ages of three and eight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, play <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"62ca3fd8-548d-4f4e-8991-ba1003e08aec\">becomes more elaborate and extensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Children engage in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"62ca3fd8-548d-4f4e-8991-ba1003e08aec\">complex theme play involving roles, scripts and costumes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. By the age of six, games with rules become a pervasive play activity, as do rule negotiations and discussions of 'fairness'. Both co-operation and competition occur in these games, as well as in spontaneously invented ones. Through this kind of play, children <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ed7055f4-1dda-4e9d-80a3-7ff39cb88b36\">demonstrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> extensive symbolic thought capacities and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ed7055f4-1dda-4e9d-80a3-7ff39cb88b36\">the ability to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> self-regulate and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"62909a20-30bc-47df-af4b-a0a7721b891d\">explain their own behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. From ages eight to fourteen, play becomes increasingly sophisticated and symbolic, with pretend themes often carrying on for months. Symbolic board and computer games are also popular. At this stage, many children will have been introduced to more organised, adult-controlled games, such as sport, which require greater control of motor, social and cognitive processes.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>While young animals of most species show mainly relatively simple forms of play up to the age of puberty, it is notable that the species that tend to have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"487cc7e6-2ccd-45ae-8069-94e21168b4ca\">the most complex lifestyles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> engage in play the most and with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"26f20c52-11a9-43be-bef4-0bb9cb59b865\">the most sophisticated repertoire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. This naturally includes non-human primates, and particularly the great apes, in which quite complex forms of social and object play are seen. Dolphins are also notable for the range and complexity of the games they play. It has been claimed that captive bottlenose dolphins can show 317 distinct forms of play behaviour. One of these is blowing bubbles and catching them in the mouth before they reach the surface. To add interest and competition, they can apparently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"9399dbca-684f-41cb-be2a-cec999ceb4f6\">make the task more and more difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> by releasing the bubbles closer and closer to the surface or by modifying their swimming style while the bubbles are released.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Amongst mammals other than humans, it is the species that rely on their group hunting skills that show the greatest amount of play behaviour as juveniles. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"0d5d2378-0b1f-4edb-9460-597a927c5897\">Hunting species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> also seem happy to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"ec602cf8-57fa-4282-9960-a1275f2482d9\">play with objects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, presumably because this represents practice for catching and manipulating prey. Apart from developing sensorimotor dexterity, these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"b95b48b4-50ba-4ae0-96be-cf8e06e8680d\">play interactions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> also help to sort out dominance relationships and promote social alliances and cohesion within the group, though <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"22209892-d2d4-4223-a470-066aed50a807\">not with outsiders to the group<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. Play for all species is a key adaptive tool for survival, and therefore, like all important behaviour, its expression is linked to the brain's dopamine reward systems.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e3d05950-323f-455b-aeba-322844dd22b7\">Play deprivation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> can have a significant effect on humans. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31 39\" data-uid=\"cc15e494-ebc6-4b43-84cf-dabe1fb1fb04 e3d05950-323f-455b-aeba-322844dd22b7\">Children who have been deprived of play</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> are likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"b5251003-7ceb-4e6b-b70b-726bdd7808ea\">have been neglected in many other ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. The effects can include an inability to make friends and socialise, leading to an isolated childhood and adolescence, which in turn can lead to a lonely and isolated adulthood, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"47280013-388b-4217-ae52-bc03f1478121\">individuals unable to understand their own or others' emotions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. A childhood without adequate play experiences can lead to a lack of physical skills and abilities, which often results in obesity and poor health, as well as a lack of confidence in one's own abilities.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has six paragraphs, A–F.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>27-34</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><i><span>NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326052\" id=\"question-wrapper-326052\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cee951db-aefb-4250-ba8c-ec3c38b8543e\">In their first year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, babies tend to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"494849ff-1f09-4770-a604-0089348ed09f\">repeat the same play actions again and again<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326053\" id=\"question-wrapper-326053\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some animals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"9399dbca-684f-41cb-be2a-cec999ceb4f6\">deliberately make their games more challenging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326054\" id=\"question-wrapper-326054\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"a5b5a4d6-e4de-4277-afed-d3c720855c2a\">A newborn baby’s brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"7e3eabbb-3f37-46c0-b51e-545c465958d9\">only about a quarter developed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326055\" id=\"question-wrapper-326055\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"62ca3fd8-548d-4f4e-8991-ba1003e08aec\">Children’s role-playing develops in complexity and scope<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"24686416-44dd-407f-85fa-5981459d9b9a\">from about age three<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326056\" id=\"question-wrapper-326056\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e3d05950-323f-455b-aeba-322844dd22b7\">Missing out on play in childhood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> can leave <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"47280013-388b-4217-ae52-bc03f1478121\">a person struggling to comprehend feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326057\" id=\"question-wrapper-326057\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"74bdc662-525a-490d-bde1-52aa2f331fee\">unable to conform to what society requires<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"39d76769-4c52-4944-8fd7-852b425b9368\">be seen as failing to fit in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326058\" id=\"question-wrapper-326058\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The animals whose <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"487cc7e6-2ccd-45ae-8069-94e21168b4ca\">lives are the most complicated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> also display <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"26f20c52-11a9-43be-bef4-0bb9cb59b865\">the widest range of play behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326059\" id=\"question-wrapper-326059\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"ec602cf8-57fa-4282-9960-a1275f2482d9\">Using physical items as part of play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> is especially common among <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"0d5d2378-0b1f-4edb-9460-597a927c5897\">predatory animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>35-39</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326060\" id=\"question-wrapper-326060\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"24c96f9e-b11a-40d4-bfeb-be03ceb67bce\">Children’s interactions with parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. matter less than interactions with teachers.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"1e03c899-294e-43fd-943f-0091d1f584f7\">do not always produce positive feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> <li>C. are the only way a child gathers information.</li> <li>D. become less important as the brain matures.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326061\" id=\"question-wrapper-326061\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The way adults behave often suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f3c88a04-fa9a-49ef-b5d4-3d70a7f48ed0\">they regard play as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"6cabc795-bea7-4161-bcd7-e72de64099f0\">an enjoyable but pointless activity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</li> <li>B. an everyday part of their own lives.</li> <li>C. an activity to share with their children.</li> <li>D. something&nbsp;they should do more often.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326062\" id=\"question-wrapper-326062\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>When children first start to play games with rules, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ed7055f4-1dda-4e9d-80a3-7ff39cb88b36\">develop an ability to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. identify when other children are cheating.</li> <li>B. predict how other players will behave.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"62909a20-30bc-47df-af4b-a0a7721b891d\">justify their actions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</li> <li>D. decide which players should form a team.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326063\" id=\"question-wrapper-326063\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"b95b48b4-50ba-4ae0-96be-cf8e06e8680d\">Play routines for hunting animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"22209892-d2d4-4223-a470-066aed50a807\">do not help them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. improve their skill at seizing prey.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"22209892-d2d4-4223-a470-066aed50a807\">form social ties with animals from other groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li> <li>C. develop relationships with familiar companions.</li> <li>D. improve their physical coordination.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326064\" id=\"question-wrapper-326064\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"cc15e494-ebc6-4b43-84cf-dabe1fb1fb04\">children who lack play opportunities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. develop excessive confidence in their own abilities.</li> <li>B. suffer mainly physical rather than social difficulties.</li> <li>C. become isolated in adulthood but not in childhood.</li> <li>D. have usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"b5251003-7ceb-4e6b-b70b-726bdd7808ea\">experienced other forms of neglect as well<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in box </span></i><i><b><span>40</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326065\" id=\"question-wrapper-326065\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the writer’s purpose in Reading Passage 3?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. To explain the problems faced by children who do not experience enough play.</li> <li>B. To compare the different forms of play found in humans and other animals.</li> <li>C. To assess the role and importance of play in humans and animals.</li> <li>D. To argue that adults should play as frequently as children do.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"74bdc662-525a-490d-bde1-52aa2f331fee","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"unable to conform to what society requires","passagePhrase":"fail to meet these criteria ... incapable of coping with societal expectations"},{"uid":"39d76769-4c52-4944-8fd7-852b425b9368","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"be seen as failing to fit in","passagePhrase":"are classified as anti-social"},{"uid":"24c96f9e-b11a-40d4-bfeb-be03ceb67bce","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Children’s interactions with parents","passagePhrase":"a child ... interactions with parents"},{"uid":"1e03c899-294e-43fd-943f-0091d1f584f7","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"do not always produce positive feelings","passagePhrase":"have both positive and negative emotional experiences"},{"uid":"f3c88a04-fa9a-49ef-b5d4-3d70a7f48ed0","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"they regard play as","passagePhrase":"they often give the impression that"},{"uid":"6cabc795-bea7-4161-bcd7-e72de64099f0","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"an enjoyable but pointless activity","passagePhrase":"an attractive but wasteful expression of leisure"},{"uid":"a5b5a4d6-e4de-4277-afed-d3c720855c2a","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"A newborn baby’s brain","passagePhrase":"the brain ... at birth"},{"uid":"7e3eabbb-3f37-46c0-b51e-545c465958d9","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"only about a quarter developed","passagePhrase":"only about 25 per cent complete"},{"uid":"cee951db-aefb-4250-ba8c-ec3c38b8543e","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"In their first year","passagePhrase":"Between birth and age one"},{"uid":"494849ff-1f09-4770-a604-0089348ed09f","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"repeat the same play actions again and again","passagePhrase":"Play is highly repetitive"},{"uid":"24686416-44dd-407f-85fa-5981459d9b9a","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"from about age three","passagePhrase":"Between the ages of three and eight"},{"uid":"62ca3fd8-548d-4f4e-8991-ba1003e08aec","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Children’s role-playing develops in complexity and scope","passagePhrase":"becomes more elaborate and extensive ... complex theme play involving roles, scripts and costumes"},{"uid":"ed7055f4-1dda-4e9d-80a3-7ff39cb88b36","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"develop an ability to","passagePhrase":"demonstrate ... the ability to"},{"uid":"62909a20-30bc-47df-af4b-a0a7721b891d","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"justify their actions","passagePhrase":"explain their own behaviour"},{"uid":"487cc7e6-2ccd-45ae-8069-94e21168b4ca","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"lives are the most complicated","passagePhrase":"the most complex lifestyles"},{"uid":"26f20c52-11a9-43be-bef4-0bb9cb59b865","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"the widest range of play behaviour","passagePhrase":"the most sophisticated repertoire"},{"uid":"9399dbca-684f-41cb-be2a-cec999ceb4f6","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"deliberately make their games more challenging","passagePhrase":"make the task more and more difficult"},{"uid":"0d5d2378-0b1f-4edb-9460-597a927c5897","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"predatory animals","passagePhrase":"Hunting species"},{"uid":"ec602cf8-57fa-4282-9960-a1275f2482d9","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Using physical items as part of play","passagePhrase":"play with objects"},{"uid":"b95b48b4-50ba-4ae0-96be-cf8e06e8680d","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"Play routines for hunting animals","passagePhrase":"play interactions"},{"uid":"22209892-d2d4-4223-a470-066aed50a807","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"do not help them ... form social ties with animals from other groups","passagePhrase":"not with outsiders to the group"},{"uid":"e3d05950-323f-455b-aeba-322844dd22b7","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Missing out on play in childhood","passagePhrase":"Play deprivation"},{"uid":"cc15e494-ebc6-4b43-84cf-dabe1fb1fb04 e3d05950-323f-455b-aeba-322844dd22b7","qNum":"31 39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Children who have been deprived of play"},{"uid":"b5251003-7ceb-4e6b-b70b-726bdd7808ea","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"experienced other forms of neglect as well","passagePhrase":"have been neglected in many other ways"},{"uid":"47280013-388b-4217-ae52-bc03f1478121","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"a person struggling to comprehend feelings","passagePhrase":"individuals unable to understand their own or others' emotions"},{"uid":"cc15e494-ebc6-4b43-84cf-dabe1fb1fb04","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"children who lack play opportunities","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_88":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions</span></b> <b><span>1-13</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The nature of Yawning</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>While fatigue, drowsiness or boredom easily bring on yawns, scientists are discovering there is more to yawning than most people think. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e561f1f2-bbb3-497d-bcb8-a9a3d1c3f165\">Not much is known about why we yawn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> or if it serves any useful function. People have already learned that yawning can be infectious. “Contagious yawning” is the increase in likelihood that you will yawn after watching or hearing someone else yawn, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e561f1f2-bbb3-497d-bcb8-a9a3d1c3f165\">not much is known about the underlying causes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e561f1f2-bbb3-497d-bcb8-a9a3d1c3f165\">very little research has been done on the subject<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. However, scientists at the University of Albany, as well as the University of Leeds and the University of London, have done some exploration.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"64017c71-eb84-4d82-b53a-58ddcbb4cc37\">commonly believed that people yawn as a result of being sleepy or tired<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> because they need oxygen. However, the latest research shows that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"3c1ffd44-ef9d-42db-8c5e-d66f5540a67a\">a yawn can help<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"821f5c6a-5c68-4ba5-b82a-d58c7d47ec1c\">cool the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and help it work more effectively, which is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"604de0d6-6c77-4246-831a-5727775f91b9\">quite different from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"64017c71-eb84-4d82-b53a-58ddcbb4cc37\">the popular belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> that yawning promotes sleep and is a sign of tiredness. Dr Andrew Gallup and his colleagues at the University of Albany in New York State said their experiments on 44 students showed that raising or lowering oxygen and carbon dioxide levels in the blood <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"604de0d6-6c77-4246-831a-5727775f91b9\">did not produce that reaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. In the study, participants were shown videos of people laughing and yawning, and researchers counted how many times the volunteers responded to the “contagious yawns”. The researchers found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"c2712ecf-d2fa-4027-9921-fd46f3507167\">those who breathed through the nose rather than the mouth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"15ad1792-fc48-41b0-b10f-30777088ed6d\">were less likely to yawn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> when watching a video of other people yawning. The same effect was found among those who held a cool pack to their forehead, whereas those who held a warm pack yawned while watching the video. Since yawning occurs when brain temperature rises, sending cool blood to the brain serves to maintain the best levels of mental efficiency.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>Yawning is universal to humans and many animals. Cats, dogs, and fish yawn just like humans do, but they yawn spontaneously. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"7a6ee775-3951-4387-bf03-4861d0712cfe\">Only humans and chimpanzees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, our closest relatives in the animal kingdom, have shown definite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"5f5e0a62-6756-4565-9b28-0de1cbeb311b\">contagious yawning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Though much of yawning is due to suggestibility, sometimes people do not need to actually see a person yawn to involuntarily yawn themselves: hearing someone yawning or even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"44d34eb7-66e9-4106-944e-77cea44e6176\">reading about yawning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d6352495-d330-4a99-b45d-6beb12a60d5c\">cause the same reaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>However, contagious yawning goes beyond mere suggestibility. Recent studies show that contagious yawning is also related to our predisposition toward empathy— the ability to understand and connect with others’ emotional states. So empathy is important, sure, but how could it possibly be related to contagious yawning? Leave it up to psychologists at Leeds University in England to answer that. In their study, researchers selected 40 psychology students and 40 engineering students. Generally, psychology students are more likely to feel empathy for others, while engineering students are thought to be concerned with objects and science. Each student was made to wait individually in a waiting room, along with an undercover assistant who yawned 10 times in as many minutes. The students were then administered an emotional quotient test: students were shown 40 images of eyes and asked what emotion each one displayed. The results of the test support the idea that contagious yawning is linked to empathy. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b3176140-4848-4e38-9648-e5b5774699b5\">The psychology students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b3176140-4848-4e38-9648-e5b5774699b5\">whose future profession requires them to focus on others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"4ee6b753-c1a1-4956-a97d-568d345de318\">yawned an average of 5.5 times contagiously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> in the waiting room and scored 28 out of 40 on the emotional test. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"599b4657-cf9b-4269-908f-86fe1e9e8135\">The engineering students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"599b4657-cf9b-4269-908f-86fe1e9e8135\">who tend to focus on things like numbers and systems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"4ee6b753-c1a1-4956-a97d-568d345de318\">yawned an average of 1.5 times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and scored 25.5 out of 40 on the subsequent test. The difference doesn’t sound like much, but researchers consider it significant. Strangely enough, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e7d665fe-cf73-4d6f-89c6-000e1a780288\">women<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, who are generally considered more emotionally attuned, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e7d665fe-cf73-4d6f-89c6-000e1a780288\">didn’t score any higher than men<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Another study, led by Atsushi Senju, a cognitive researcher at the University of London, also sought to answer that question. People with autism disorder are considered to be developmentally impaired emotionally. Autistics have trouble connecting with others and find it difficult to feel empathy. Since autistics have difficulty feeling empathy, they shouldn’t be susceptible to contagious yawning. To find out, Senju and his colleagues placed 49 kids aged 7 to 15 in a room with a television. 24 of the test subjects had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"83f341ff-4c18-470b-85d0-876344a3a52f\">been diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>; the other 25 were non-autistic kids. The test subjects were shown short clips of people yawning as well as clips of people opening their mouths but not yawning. While <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"83f341ff-4c18-470b-85d0-876344a3a52f\">the kids with autism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"20ec50fb-cf2f-4fa8-93c6-c2d0378bca3f\">had the same lack of reaction to both kinds of clips<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, the non-autistic kids yawned more after the clips of people yawning.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>There also have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"8890ca52-9623-46af-9a7e-001d8229f9e5\">studies that suggest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> yawning, especially psychological “contagious” yawning, may have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c87d689c-1afb-4346-853d-42ac08a12a3d\">developed as a way of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> keeping a group of animals alert and bonding <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"cf2305c5-bb75-458e-acd1-8e824f215b5e\">members of a group<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"2bec7cdd-f8aa-4e0f-8615-b9e00b92fcf1\">into a more united one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. If <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a4f36530-25bf-46cb-b009-4ba8d846fb0f\">an animal is drowsy or bored<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, it may not be as alert as it should be to be prepared to spring into action, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a4f36530-25bf-46cb-b009-4ba8d846fb0f\">its yawning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> is practically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"c2819a07-d8e5-4506-98c2-948421dac68a\">saying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, “Hey, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"cba39d9e-b0e2-4071-b540-0e637ed672fa\">I need some<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> rest; you stay awake”. Therefore, a contagious yawn could be an instinctual reaction to a signal from one member of the herd reminding the others to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"b4009144-72f8-4b19-b275-360d6af21e42\">stay alert<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> when danger <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"9643e378-ac8a-4605-8153-253db0830276\">comes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. So <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"95a071d5-4ee8-4933-b8c3-e9dc2985936a\">the theory suggests evidence that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> yawning <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"62ecee59-3c74-43c2-93a0-457b4a13cb93\">comes from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the evolution <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"62ecee59-3c74-43c2-93a0-457b4a13cb93\">of early humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to be ready to physically exert themselves at any given moment.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Read paragraphs </span><b><span>A-F</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><b><span>NB</span></b> <i><span>You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326066\" id=\"question-wrapper-326066\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"44d34eb7-66e9-4106-944e-77cea44e6176\">Exposure to written information about yawning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d6352495-d330-4a99-b45d-6beb12a60d5c\">provoke the same response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326067\" id=\"question-wrapper-326067\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"3c1ffd44-ef9d-42db-8c5e-d66f5540a67a\">Yawning is used to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"821f5c6a-5c68-4ba5-b82a-d58c7d47ec1c\">regulate brain temperature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326068\" id=\"question-wrapper-326068\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>An acknowledgement that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e561f1f2-bbb3-497d-bcb8-a9a3d1c3f165\">the reasons behind yawning remain largely unstudied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326069\" id=\"question-wrapper-326069\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Evidence that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"5f5e0a62-6756-4565-9b28-0de1cbeb311b\">the tendency to imitate yawns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"7a6ee775-3951-4387-bf03-4861d0712cfe\">been confirmed in only two species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326070\" id=\"question-wrapper-326070\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Experimental evidence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"604de0d6-6c77-4246-831a-5727775f91b9\">challenged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"64017c71-eb84-4d82-b53a-58ddcbb4cc37\">a widely held explanation for why people yawn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Match each of the following research findings with the university where the study was conducted.</span></p><p><b><span>NB</span></b> <i><span>You may use any letter more than once</span></i><span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> University of Albany</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> University of Leeds</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C.</span></b><span> University of London</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326071\" id=\"question-wrapper-326071\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e7d665fe-cf73-4d6f-89c6-000e1a780288\">Female participants showed no advantage over males<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> in identifying other people’s feelings.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326072\" id=\"question-wrapper-326072\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"83f341ff-4c18-470b-85d0-876344a3a52f\">Children with a developmental condition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"20ec50fb-cf2f-4fa8-93c6-c2d0378bca3f\">showed less response to yawning cues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> from others.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326073\" id=\"question-wrapper-326073\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"c2712ecf-d2fa-4027-9921-fd46f3507167\">The route through which participants breathed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"15ad1792-fc48-41b0-b10f-30777088ed6d\">affected their susceptibility to contagious yawning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326074\" id=\"question-wrapper-326074\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b3176140-4848-4e38-9648-e5b5774699b5\">Students in a people-focused field<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"4ee6b753-c1a1-4956-a97d-568d345de318\">showed a stronger tendency to copy yawns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"599b4657-cf9b-4269-908f-86fe1e9e8135\">those in a technical field<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>ONE WORD</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>10-13</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"8890ca52-9623-46af-9a7e-001d8229f9e5\">Another theory shows that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> yawning <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c87d689c-1afb-4346-853d-42ac08a12a3d\">is used for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"cf2305c5-bb75-458e-acd1-8e824f215b5e\">individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"2bec7cdd-f8aa-4e0f-8615-b9e00b92fcf1\">into a tighter social unit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. For example, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a4f36530-25bf-46cb-b009-4ba8d846fb0f\">a tired animal's yawn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"c2819a07-d8e5-4506-98c2-948421dac68a\">tells the rest of the group<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"cba39d9e-b0e2-4071-b540-0e637ed672fa\">it needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)________ and that they should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"b4009144-72f8-4b19-b275-360d6af21e42\">keep an eye on their surroundings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, so everyone is ready when (12)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"9643e378-ac8a-4605-8153-253db0830276\">draws near<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"95a071d5-4ee8-4933-b8c3-e9dc2985936a\">This theory suggests that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> yawning is a behaviour that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"62ecee59-3c74-43c2-93a0-457b4a13cb93\">developed through human<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)________.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326075\" id=\"question-wrapper-326075\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">bonding</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326076\" id=\"question-wrapper-326076\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">rest</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326077\" id=\"question-wrapper-326077\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">danger</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326078\" id=\"question-wrapper-326078\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">evolution</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e561f1f2-bbb3-497d-bcb8-a9a3d1c3f165","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"the reasons behind yawning remain largely unstudied","passagePhrase":"Not much is known about why we yawn ... not much is known about the underlying causes ... very little research has been done on the subject"},{"uid":"64017c71-eb84-4d82-b53a-58ddcbb4cc37","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"a widely held explanation for why people yawn","passagePhrase":"commonly believed that people yawn as a result of being sleepy or tired ... the popular belief"},{"uid":"3c1ffd44-ef9d-42db-8c5e-d66f5540a67a","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Yawning is used to","passagePhrase":"a yawn can help"},{"uid":"821f5c6a-5c68-4ba5-b82a-d58c7d47ec1c","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"regulate brain temperature","passagePhrase":"cool the brain"},{"uid":"604de0d6-6c77-4246-831a-5727775f91b9","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"challenged","passagePhrase":"quite different from ... did not produce that reaction"},{"uid":"c2712ecf-d2fa-4027-9921-fd46f3507167","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"The route through which participants breathed","passagePhrase":"those who breathed through the nose rather than the mouth"},{"uid":"15ad1792-fc48-41b0-b10f-30777088ed6d","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"affected their susceptibility to contagious yawning","passagePhrase":"were less likely to yawn"},{"uid":"7a6ee775-3951-4387-bf03-4861d0712cfe","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"been confirmed in only two species","passagePhrase":"Only humans and chimpanzees"},{"uid":"5f5e0a62-6756-4565-9b28-0de1cbeb311b","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"the tendency to imitate yawns","passagePhrase":"contagious yawning"},{"uid":"44d34eb7-66e9-4106-944e-77cea44e6176","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Exposure to written information about yawning","passagePhrase":"reading about yawning"},{"uid":"d6352495-d330-4a99-b45d-6beb12a60d5c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"provoke the same response","passagePhrase":"cause the same reaction"},{"uid":"b3176140-4848-4e38-9648-e5b5774699b5","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Students in a people-focused field","passagePhrase":"The psychology students ... whose future profession requires them to focus on others"},{"uid":"4ee6b753-c1a1-4956-a97d-568d345de318","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"showed a stronger tendency to copy yawns","passagePhrase":"yawned an average of 5.5 times contagiously ... yawned an average of 1.5 times"},{"uid":"599b4657-cf9b-4269-908f-86fe1e9e8135","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"those in a technical field","passagePhrase":"The engineering students ... who tend to focus on things like numbers and systems"},{"uid":"e7d665fe-cf73-4d6f-89c6-000e1a780288","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Female participants showed no advantage over males","passagePhrase":"women ... didn’t score any higher than men"},{"uid":"83f341ff-4c18-470b-85d0-876344a3a52f","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Children with a developmental condition","passagePhrase":"been diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder ... the kids with autism"},{"uid":"20ec50fb-cf2f-4fa8-93c6-c2d0378bca3f","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"showed less response to yawning cues","passagePhrase":"had the same lack of reaction to both kinds of clips"},{"uid":"8890ca52-9623-46af-9a7e-001d8229f9e5","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"Another theory shows that","passagePhrase":"studies that suggest"},{"uid":"c87d689c-1afb-4346-853d-42ac08a12a3d","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"is used for","passagePhrase":"developed as a way of"},{"uid":"cf2305c5-bb75-458e-acd1-8e824f215b5e","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"individuals","passagePhrase":"members of a group"},{"uid":"2bec7cdd-f8aa-4e0f-8615-b9e00b92fcf1","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"into a tighter social unit","passagePhrase":"into a more united one"},{"uid":"a4f36530-25bf-46cb-b009-4ba8d846fb0f","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"a tired animal's yawn","passagePhrase":"an animal is drowsy or bored ... its yawning"},{"uid":"c2819a07-d8e5-4506-98c2-948421dac68a","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"tells the rest of the group","passagePhrase":"saying"},{"uid":"cba39d9e-b0e2-4071-b540-0e637ed672fa","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"it needs","passagePhrase":"I need some"},{"uid":"b4009144-72f8-4b19-b275-360d6af21e42","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"keep an eye on their surroundings","passagePhrase":"stay alert"},{"uid":"9643e378-ac8a-4605-8153-253db0830276","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"draws near","passagePhrase":"comes"},{"uid":"95a071d5-4ee8-4933-b8c3-e9dc2985936a","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"This theory suggests that","passagePhrase":"the theory suggests evidence that"},{"uid":"62ecee59-3c74-43c2-93a0-457b4a13cb93","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"developed through human","passagePhrase":"comes from ... of early humans"}]},"reading_u2_89":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 14-26</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Sun: Our Nearest Star</span></b></p><p><span>The Sun is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"39e85bcb-6197-4dab-ba15-ea27af822d65\">our<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> nearest star, and it dominates our sky from a distance of 'only' 150 million kilometres. Even though it appears to be the same size as the full Moon, it is over 400,000 times brighter, and it dictates when we have night and day here on Earth. The Sun is the largest body in the Solar System, and it is also the most massive, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3ef8ede6-a9ad-406f-9980-af5ee0cc7ff7\">containing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"ca782643-a7ec-49e6-bf8c-93d7d1887791\">99.9 per cent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of the total mass <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"83b35410-166a-4923-8f63-02cc1027b4a1\">of all the planets, moons, dwarf planets, asteroids and comets combined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. This concentration of mass, and the accompanying gravitational force, is why the Sun sits at the very centre of the Solar System, pulling all the other bodies into orbit around it. We are entirely dependent on the Sun for the habitability of our planet, as it provides us with the energy, in the form of heat and light, that we require to survive. But it also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"7133bd9f-7355-494a-9bd8-2d855b20651f\">brings many potential hazards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, from the continual flow of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"11cf006e-c5ed-496f-841c-93e1d464aba6\">hazardous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> radiation that always lurks just beyond Earth's atmosphere, to the sporadic and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c663165c-f70d-4c5f-afa0-3df382cda70c\">violent space weather<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that threatens much of our society's infrastructure.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"e1ce7e4b-4f43-4bf0-8d46-93f963fd3a54\">Given that the Sun has a volume that is over a million times that of the Earth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, yet contains only 330,000 times the mass, we can immediately deduce that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"876464be-dbca-4f5e-8193-005631f41ffc\">its average<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> density <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"876464be-dbca-4f5e-8193-005631f41ffc\">is far lower than that of a terrestrial planet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Indeed, its average density is about the same as that of water, and less than a quarter of the density of the Earth. The Sun is made mainly of the lightest elements, hydrogen (the Sun's fuel) and helium, in gaseous form.</span></p><p><span>The source of the Sun's energy remained a mystery until Einstein's 1905 special theory of relativity highlighted the promise of efficient nuclear fusion. For nuclear fusion to occur, matter <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"3c03bc4f-d303-4cac-837b-c0600795e823\">needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to be under conditions of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c8bbf735-1dbe-4b14-962e-ff596913df29\">tremendous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> pressure and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"732c4c41-cbc1-4c8d-89c6-fb4e6a623329\">extreme heat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, so that the electric repulsion can be overcome and the nuclei can get close enough to smash into each other. It was the English astronomer Sir Arthur Eddington who realised in the 1920s that the physical conditions within the core of the Sun were extreme enough to permit the necessary nuclear reactions. The Sun <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5b95ecfd-0516-4ad1-a804-08ae0de3b9d0\">converts 600,000 million kilograms of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> hydrogen <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5b95ecfd-0516-4ad1-a804-08ae0de3b9d0\">to helium<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> every second to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"424da357-459c-4177-ad0e-57c93192ab77\">sustain its phenomenal energy output<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The Sun's core is approximately 15,000,000 degrees Celsius and is the site of nuclear fusion. The energy from the core travels outwards through the radiation zone by the transfer of energy from one molecule to another. Heated gases move the energy from the radiation zone through to the convection zone, where the gases start to cool, causing them to sink back down to the radiation zone. Outside the convection zone is the photosphere, which is approximately 500 kilometres thick and is the surface layer of the Sun. Beyond this, there is a thin layer of gas surrounding the photosphere called the chromosphere. Finally, the corona is another layer of gas that extends a long way beyond the Sun.</span></p><p><span>Observations of more evolved objects around us in the galaxy have led to our understanding of the eventual fate of the Sun. The Sun has sufficient hydrogen at the right temperature and density to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"271f4e74-8785-47a0-9546-672a21f34fa0\">continue creating helium<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"bf3d81a5-9cc4-4933-b7be-372807b21f25\">for a further six billion years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Then the supply of fuel, and all possibility of future nuclear reactions, will eventually be exhausted. By this point, the Sun will appear very different from how it does today. It will have become a red giant: a much cooler, redder and far more bloated version of itself, with an atmosphere puffed up so large as to swallow the planets Mercury and Venus and make conditions rather uncomfortable on Earth. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"6b3b2dd6-ff6b-443c-ac1f-e8fc359a814f\">Eventually<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a491081b-6522-449e-80b8-84885b2df1af\">the outer envelope<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of the red giant will be lost, expanding away to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e94e9210-aac6-47d0-941b-2fe805d81496\">form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> a planetary nebula. The remaining hot core of the star will be left exposed as a white dwarf, which will slowly cool and fade over billions of years, until it finally fades into a cold, dark and dense ball of compressed matter.</span></p><p><span>From time to time, there are eruptions of matter from the Sun. The magnetic energy in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"4355e7ec-d8f0-4de0-a666-408cebdca566\">an exceptionally powerful solar flare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"0232b4cc-4d8f-404c-a51f-8c2ea8cc15c2\">heat and speed up a huge cloud of charged particles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to form a coronal mass ejection. The cloud produced by such an eruption escapes out into interplanetary space, but it can cause concern if directed towards Earth. When a coronal mass ejection reaches the Earth, it rattles the Earth's magnetic field to generate what is known as a 'geomagnetic storm'. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f1916a25-acc9-4229-88f8-1777171fd3a9\">The occurrence of the flare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> gives us advance notice that this event will arrive between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8575880a-1fd0-45e8-8381-64bcb37983db\">15 hours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and a couple of days <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"63570e8d-299e-4636-bb8f-7932863f5570\">later<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, depending on how fast it is moving and how clear the passage between the Sun and Earth is. The major effect of a coronal mass ejection for humans is on our satellites, which can be seriously damaged. Power cuts on Earth can also take place.</span></p><p><span>Although we may now understand the basics of the Sun, we remain unable to reliably predict everything about it. There is still much to understand and learn about it, and it seems the more intensely it is studied, the more questions there are to answer!</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>14–19</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>THE SUN</span></b></p><p><span>● The Sun is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"39e85bcb-6197-4dab-ba15-ea27af822d65\">the Earth’s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> (14)________ </span></p><p><span>● The Sun <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3ef8ede6-a9ad-406f-9980-af5ee0cc7ff7\">makes up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"ca782643-a7ec-49e6-bf8c-93d7d1887791\">virtually all<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"83b35410-166a-4923-8f63-02cc1027b4a1\">of the Solar System’s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> (15)________.</span></p><p><span>● Although it sustains life, the Sun can also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"7133bd9f-7355-494a-9bd8-2d855b20651f\">threaten Earth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"11cf006e-c5ed-496f-841c-93e1d464aba6\">harmful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> (16)________ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c663165c-f70d-4c5f-afa0-3df382cda70c\">severe space weather<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"e1ce7e4b-4f43-4bf0-8d46-93f963fd3a54\">In spite of its size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"876464be-dbca-4f5e-8193-005631f41ffc\">the Sun has a low average<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> (17)________ </span></p><p><span>● Nuclear fusion <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"3c03bc4f-d303-4cac-837b-c0600795e823\">requires<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c8bbf735-1dbe-4b14-962e-ff596913df29\">extreme<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> (18)________ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"732c4c41-cbc1-4c8d-89c6-fb4e6a623329\">very high temperatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, which the Sun can provide.</span></p><p><span>● During nuclear fusion, (19)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5b95ecfd-0516-4ad1-a804-08ae0de3b9d0\">is used to produce helium<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"424da357-459c-4177-ad0e-57c93192ab77\">release a huge amount of energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326079\" id=\"question-wrapper-326079\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">nearest star</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326080\" id=\"question-wrapper-326080\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(total) mass</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326081\" id=\"question-wrapper-326081\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">radiation</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326082\" id=\"question-wrapper-326082\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">density</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326083\" id=\"question-wrapper-326083\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">pressure</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326084\" id=\"question-wrapper-326084\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">hydrogen</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Label the diagram below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>20-22</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><b><span>The Different Sections of the Sun</span></b></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_3/reading/images/0939ebbaf3f6b0b16eef80deba836a6f9c995849cfa251cbceb62944dde454c7.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326085\" id=\"question-wrapper-326085\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) radiation zone</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326086\" id=\"question-wrapper-326086\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) photosphere</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326087\" id=\"question-wrapper-326087\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) corona</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>23-26</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326088\" id=\"question-wrapper-326088\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"bf3d81a5-9cc4-4933-b7be-372807b21f25\">How much longer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> is the Sun expected to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"271f4e74-8785-47a0-9546-672a21f34fa0\">keep producing energy in its current way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">6/six billion years [OR] 6(,)000(,)000(,)000 years</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326089\" id=\"question-wrapper-326089\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a491081b-6522-449e-80b8-84885b2df1af\">the outer section<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of the Sun <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e94e9210-aac6-47d0-941b-2fe805d81496\">become<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"6b3b2dd6-ff6b-443c-ac1f-e8fc359a814f\">following<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the red giant stage? </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(a) planetary nebula</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326090\" id=\"question-wrapper-326090\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What source within <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"4355e7ec-d8f0-4de0-a666-408cebdca566\">a major solar eruption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"0232b4cc-4d8f-404c-a51f-8c2ea8cc15c2\">raises the temperature and speed of the charged material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(the) magnetic energy</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326091\" id=\"question-wrapper-326091\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8575880a-1fd0-45e8-8381-64bcb37983db\">the shortest time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"63570e8d-299e-4636-bb8f-7932863f5570\">after<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f1916a25-acc9-4229-88f8-1777171fd3a9\">a solar flare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> that a geomagnetic storm may reach Earth?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">15/fifteen hours</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"39e85bcb-6197-4dab-ba15-ea27af822d65","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"the Earth’s","passagePhrase":"our"},{"uid":"3ef8ede6-a9ad-406f-9980-af5ee0cc7ff7","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"makes up","passagePhrase":"containing"},{"uid":"ca782643-a7ec-49e6-bf8c-93d7d1887791","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"virtually all","passagePhrase":"99.9 per cent"},{"uid":"83b35410-166a-4923-8f63-02cc1027b4a1","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"of the Solar System’s","passagePhrase":"of all the planets, moons, dwarf planets, asteroids and comets combined"},{"uid":"7133bd9f-7355-494a-9bd8-2d855b20651f","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"threaten Earth","passagePhrase":"brings many potential hazards"},{"uid":"11cf006e-c5ed-496f-841c-93e1d464aba6","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"harmful","passagePhrase":"hazardous"},{"uid":"c663165c-f70d-4c5f-afa0-3df382cda70c","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"severe space weather","passagePhrase":"violent space weather"},{"uid":"e1ce7e4b-4f43-4bf0-8d46-93f963fd3a54","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"In spite of its size","passagePhrase":"Given that the Sun has a volume that is over a million times that of the Earth"},{"uid":"876464be-dbca-4f5e-8193-005631f41ffc","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"the Sun has a low average","passagePhrase":"its average ... is far lower than that of a terrestrial planet"},{"uid":"3c03bc4f-d303-4cac-837b-c0600795e823","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"requires","passagePhrase":"needs"},{"uid":"c8bbf735-1dbe-4b14-962e-ff596913df29","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"extreme","passagePhrase":"tremendous"},{"uid":"732c4c41-cbc1-4c8d-89c6-fb4e6a623329","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"very high temperatures","passagePhrase":"extreme heat"},{"uid":"5b95ecfd-0516-4ad1-a804-08ae0de3b9d0","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"is used to produce helium","passagePhrase":"converts 600,000 million kilograms of ... to helium"},{"uid":"424da357-459c-4177-ad0e-57c93192ab77","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"release a huge amount of energy","passagePhrase":"sustain its phenomenal energy output"},{"uid":"271f4e74-8785-47a0-9546-672a21f34fa0","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"keep producing energy in its current way","passagePhrase":"continue creating helium"},{"uid":"bf3d81a5-9cc4-4933-b7be-372807b21f25","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"How much longer","passagePhrase":"for a further six billion years"},{"uid":"6b3b2dd6-ff6b-443c-ac1f-e8fc359a814f","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"following","passagePhrase":"Eventually"},{"uid":"a491081b-6522-449e-80b8-84885b2df1af","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"the outer section","passagePhrase":"the outer envelope"},{"uid":"e94e9210-aac6-47d0-941b-2fe805d81496","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"become","passagePhrase":"form"},{"uid":"4355e7ec-d8f0-4de0-a666-408cebdca566","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"a major solar eruption","passagePhrase":"an exceptionally powerful solar flare"},{"uid":"0232b4cc-4d8f-404c-a51f-8c2ea8cc15c2","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"raises the temperature and speed of the charged material","passagePhrase":"heat and speed up a huge cloud of charged particles"},{"uid":"f1916a25-acc9-4229-88f8-1777171fd3a9","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"a solar flare","passagePhrase":"The occurrence of the flare"},{"uid":"8575880a-1fd0-45e8-8381-64bcb37983db","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"the shortest time","passagePhrase":"15 hours"},{"uid":"63570e8d-299e-4636-bb8f-7932863f5570","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"after","passagePhrase":"later"}]},"reading_u2_90":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><b><span>Questions 27-40</span></b><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>US Shale Gas Fracking</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b><span>. We have had widespread drilling for oil and gas deposits for more than 100 years in the United States. Until the 1990s, most of this recovery occurred from conventional wells that were drilled down to rock formations, from which hydrocarbons could be pumped to the surface. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"69b9d50f-208b-49ce-a879-ae953e96a81e\">The discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"564dfe41-ff23-4aee-81c0-241c80a84dab\">hydraulic fracking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"69b9d50f-208b-49ce-a879-ae953e96a81e\">in the late 1940s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"69b9d50f-208b-49ce-a879-ae953e96a81e\">has long allowed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> companies to extract gas and oil from shale, but the perfection of these techniques over the past few decades has allowed the process to become cost-effective. There are numerous shale plays in the United States from which shale gas can be extracted, and firms are busy drilling wells in many areas of the country.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d525b0e7-6726-402c-8049-e97f6baefa43\">Shale gas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d525b0e7-6726-402c-8049-e97f6baefa43\">natural methane<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in rock formations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"e5945564-ad02-40d2-84a8-9d174474f3af\">deep underground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> that, before fracking, was not feasible to extract. Its removal today depends on hydraulic fracturing and horizontal drilling. Hydraulic fracturing is the use of pressure to force liquids containing proppants (often sand) into rock strata so that hydrocarbons are available for extraction. Current technology uses water, sand, and miscellaneous fluids, all of which must be imported to the well site. A wellbore is drilled, and then the fracturing fluid is forced through holes in the casing into the plays. High pressures are used to create fissures where the proppants are deposited to hold the fissures open, so that hydrocarbons can be released. Hydraulic fracturing occurs in a number of stages, and the fracturing fluid is forced into a small portion of the wellbore at each stage. After the hydraulic fracturing is completed, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7baa1f55-e8b6-4975-8699-016dccdbf8c4\">some of the fracturing fluid comes back up the well<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7baa1f55-e8b6-4975-8699-016dccdbf8c4\">the flowback and wastewater from a well can be toxic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, they must be disposed of in a manner that does not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7b530178-e453-44c8-9bfa-a650da577c6b\">create any health, safety, or environmental problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"34a6239c-d7f5-4c19-a002-344548d85e6c\">The underground areas from which the gas is extracted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> may be left with cavities, which in turn can sometimes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"5123b2a0-91d4-4e64-bd96-27f566abdedd\">cause ground subsidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>The development of American shale gas deposits has been accompanied by notable benefits and a significant impact on the American economy. Next year, it is estimated that the development of America's shale gas resources will employ 869,000 people. The shale gas industry will have capital expenditures of $48 billion and pay more than $28 billion in federal and state taxes this year. Due to shale gas, the US is using less coal, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"04a41071-1331-4d8d-a3e5-81440a93b502\">the country's electricity costs have been lowered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> by about ten per cent. Shale gas has also contributed to a decrease in imports of foreign natural gas.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>Yet not everything is positive. The development of shale gas resources is associated with toxic pollutants and environmental problems. It needs to be mentioned that the American federal and state governments were not prepared for the problems that accompany shale gas development. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"174f45d6-ec57-44cf-805b-7f2a59cbfbb0\">lack of sufficient regulatory oversight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> in the US <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"d8bb4110-aa5f-416b-a3ef-8ad1a3cb564c\">when the industry began<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> allowed some unfortunate situations and instances of damage that could have been prevented.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b><span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a833b5f9-dad0-439c-90ee-8714aaf40b52\">Sites where wells are drilled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> for extracting shale gas often cover about two hectares and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f64f27ab-b3bb-494d-8ca2-9cdbd3821e1d\">involve </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37 38\" data-uid=\"692a89fd-fbdb-463f-84a8-238d8fce608a f64f27ab-b3bb-494d-8ca2-9cdbd3821e1d\">increased</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f64f27ab-b3bb-494d-8ca2-9cdbd3821e1d\"> traffic</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, noise, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"692a89fd-fbdb-463f-84a8-238d8fce608a\">light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, dangerous equipment, and toxic chemicals. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"9f1cf9cd-390f-4fdf-b8ff-329be63af767\">The activities and conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> at a site therefore create a potential for contamination and environmental degradation. The major risk involves damage from the toxic chemicals used in hydraulic fracturing. The fracking fluid is approximately 99.5 per cent water and sand and 0.5 per cent additives used to enhance hydrocarbon recovery. An average of 5,000 gallons of chemical additives may be used to frack a well, and some of them are toxic. Since different chemicals and different amounts are used <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"717aa976-3db7-45a1-b806-4eb0788b3e62\">at each well<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"6f068aa0-14a7-4660-b1de-1075f4680c7c\">toxicities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ad6cfe6a-f7de-45b5-af15-af5f0f7d277a\">may vary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>Under US federal law, the chemicals used at a well are exempted from full reporting requirements. Under most state laws, the supplier or the service company of a fracturing operation must disclose information, unless the chemicals are claimed as a trade secret. Recently, it was estimated that in approximately two-thirds of cases <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"e4d3fe28-b5ab-4981-b6ec-5a5531e82100\">the complete chemical compositions were not reported<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"e4d3fe28-b5ab-4981-b6ec-5a5531e82100\">Chemical secrecy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> is a problem, because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"a18cebb4-8780-4a8c-84d8-bd8afcfeca82\">persons working at wells and persons who come into contact with chemicals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> used at a well <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"5f75f294-288b-46f6-ae7c-ee09e18efdee\">do not have sufficient information to know whether they need medical attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Without timely information about the chemicals involved in a spill or release, first responders to emergencies, health professionals, and property owners may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"5f75f294-288b-46f6-ae7c-ee09e18efdee\">lack key information for deciding what actions they should take<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>Issues are also being raised about the need for better management practices to reduce the risks that accompany shale gas development. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e3dd95b8-6c17-4d2e-a481-9710bf580ca0\">Hundreds of best management practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> have been identified to employ during energy development and extraction, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e3dd95b8-6c17-4d2e-a481-9710bf580ca0\">most of these<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> are currently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"cbe54e20-050c-4212-ab82-afa25e824b5b\">voluntary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. In the absence of mandatory management practices covering all of the stages of shale gas development, there are not sufficient assurances that people and the environment are adequately protected against health and safety problems. By adopting more mandatory management practices, the industry may be able to reduce the risks, and shale gas development would be beneficial overall.</span></p><p><b><span>H. </span></b><span>The American experiences can be helpful in discerning whether other countries might proceed with shale gas development. The activities connected with developing shale gas can be assessed to learn about the risks, dangers, and problems that need to be addressed. Then, existing laws and regulations can be evaluated to determine their probable success in addressing the risks. Additional regulations can be developed if they are needed, and firms can be required to adopt best management practices. Governments can require disclosure of dangerous materials and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1577c11f-23e3-4dab-90d4-69333d0f5ecb\">establish funding mechanisms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to pay for regulatory oversight and for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1577c11f-23e3-4dab-90d4-69333d0f5ecb\">collecting monies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to be used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1f0559da-f9b1-40d4-aba0-4ec2533d56df\">remedy future damages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> caused by fracking.</span></p><p><b><span>*Glossary</span></b></p><p><i><span>Shale play – An underground formation of a type of rock containing natural gas.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Proppant – A solid material used in fracking to keep holes open during the fracking process.</span></i></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>The text above has 8 paragraphs </span><b><span>A – H</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>27-34</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326092\" id=\"question-wrapper-326092\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"6f068aa0-14a7-4660-b1de-1075f4680c7c\">The danger posed by additives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ad6cfe6a-f7de-45b5-af15-af5f0f7d277a\">not the same<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"717aa976-3db7-45a1-b806-4eb0788b3e62\">at every drilling site<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326093\" id=\"question-wrapper-326093\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d525b0e7-6726-402c-8049-e97f6baefa43\">The gas reserves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"e5945564-ad02-40d2-84a8-9d174474f3af\">lie far beneath the Earth’s surface<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326094\" id=\"question-wrapper-326094\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e3dd95b8-6c17-4d2e-a481-9710bf580ca0\">Most recommended safeguards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> for shale-gas operations are still <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"cbe54e20-050c-4212-ab82-afa25e824b5b\">optional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326095\" id=\"question-wrapper-326095\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The US government <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"174f45d6-ec57-44cf-805b-7f2a59cbfbb0\">did not<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"d8bb4110-aa5f-416b-a3ef-8ad1a3cb564c\">initially<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"174f45d6-ec57-44cf-805b-7f2a59cbfbb0\">enforce enough control on the fracking industry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326096\" id=\"question-wrapper-326096\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"564dfe41-ff23-4aee-81c0-241c80a84dab\">Fracking techniques<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"69b9d50f-208b-49ce-a879-ae953e96a81e\">have been available since the 1940s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326097\" id=\"question-wrapper-326097\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Governments can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1577c11f-23e3-4dab-90d4-69333d0f5ecb\">create financial reserves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1f0559da-f9b1-40d4-aba0-4ec2533d56df\">cover damage that may emerge later<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326098\" id=\"question-wrapper-326098\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some companies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"e4d3fe28-b5ab-4981-b6ec-5a5531e82100\">do not publicise the chemicals that they use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> for fracking. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326099\" id=\"question-wrapper-326099\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Using shale gas has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"04a41071-1331-4d8d-a3e5-81440a93b502\">reduced US expenditure on electricity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>FIVE</span></b></i><i><span> letters, </span></i><i><b><span>A – I</span></b></i><i><span>. Write the correct letter, </span></i><i><b><span>A – I</span></b></i><i><span>, in any order in boxes </span></i><i><b><span>35-39</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p><span>Which FIVE of the following statements describe disadvantages or risks associated with the US shale gas fracking industry?</span></p><p><b><span>A.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7baa1f55-e8b6-4975-8699-016dccdbf8c4\">Toxic liquid can flow up a drilling installation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7b530178-e453-44c8-9bfa-a650da577c6b\">potentially create pollution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>B.</span></b><span> Underground gas explosions can be a risk to local communities.</span></p><p><b><span>C.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"34a6239c-d7f5-4c19-a002-344548d85e6c\">The ground over the fracking areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> can sometimes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"5123b2a0-91d4-4e64-bd96-27f566abdedd\">become unsafe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D.</span></b><span> Oil deposits can sometimes be lost during gas fracking.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a833b5f9-dad0-439c-90ee-8714aaf40b52\">Drilling sites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f64f27ab-b3bb-494d-8ca2-9cdbd3821e1d\">bring heavier traffic to nearby areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"9f1cf9cd-390f-4fdf-b8ff-329be63af767\">Operations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"692a89fd-fbdb-463f-84a8-238d8fce608a\">expose nearby areas to additional artificial lighting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>G.</span></b><span> Sand used in fracking can pollute the water table.</span></p><p><b><span>H.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"a18cebb4-8780-4a8c-84d8-bd8afcfeca82\">Workers contaminated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> during fracking operations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"5f75f294-288b-46f6-ae7c-ee09e18efdee\">can have proper treatment delayed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>I.</span></b><span> Tax dollars are taken out of the country by overseas extraction companies.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326100\" id=\"question-wrapper-326100\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/E/F/H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326101\" id=\"question-wrapper-326101\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/E/F/H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326102\" id=\"question-wrapper-326102\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/E/F/H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326103\" id=\"question-wrapper-326103\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/E/F/H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326104\" id=\"question-wrapper-326104\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/E/F/H</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><b><span>Question</span></b> <b><span>40</span></b></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, </span><b><span>A</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>B</span></b><span>, </span><b><span>C</span></b><span> or </span><b><span>D</span></b><span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in box </span></i><i><b><span>40</span></b></i><i><span> on your answer sheet.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326105\" id=\"question-wrapper-326105\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the writer’s purpose in Reading Passage 3?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. To examine whether government supervision of shale-gas development has been adequate.</li> <li>B. To argue that the environmental costs of shale gas outweigh its economic advantages.</li> <li>C. To explain the technology used to obtain shale gas from underground deposits.</li> <li>D. To provide an overview of the benefits, risks and regulatory lessons of US shale-gas development.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"69b9d50f-208b-49ce-a879-ae953e96a81e","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"have been available since the 1940s","passagePhrase":"The discovery ... in the late 1940s ... has long allowed"},{"uid":"564dfe41-ff23-4aee-81c0-241c80a84dab","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Fracking techniques","passagePhrase":"hydraulic fracking"},{"uid":"d525b0e7-6726-402c-8049-e97f6baefa43","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The gas reserves","passagePhrase":"Shale gas ... natural methane"},{"uid":"e5945564-ad02-40d2-84a8-9d174474f3af","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"lie far beneath the Earth’s surface","passagePhrase":"deep underground"},{"uid":"7baa1f55-e8b6-4975-8699-016dccdbf8c4","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Toxic liquid can flow up a drilling installation","passagePhrase":"some of the fracturing fluid comes back up the well ... the flowback and wastewater from a well can be toxic"},{"uid":"7b530178-e453-44c8-9bfa-a650da577c6b","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"potentially create pollution","passagePhrase":"create any health, safety, or environmental problems"},{"uid":"34a6239c-d7f5-4c19-a002-344548d85e6c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"The ground over the fracking areas","passagePhrase":"The underground areas from which the gas is extracted"},{"uid":"5123b2a0-91d4-4e64-bd96-27f566abdedd","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"become unsafe","passagePhrase":"cause ground subsidence"},{"uid":"04a41071-1331-4d8d-a3e5-81440a93b502","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"reduced US expenditure on electricity","passagePhrase":"the country's electricity costs have been lowered"},{"uid":"174f45d6-ec57-44cf-805b-7f2a59cbfbb0","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"did not ... enforce enough control on the fracking industry","passagePhrase":"lack of sufficient regulatory oversight"},{"uid":"d8bb4110-aa5f-416b-a3ef-8ad1a3cb564c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"initially","passagePhrase":"when the industry began"},{"uid":"a833b5f9-dad0-439c-90ee-8714aaf40b52","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"Drilling sites","passagePhrase":"Sites where wells are drilled"},{"uid":"f64f27ab-b3bb-494d-8ca2-9cdbd3821e1d","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"bring heavier traffic to nearby areas","passagePhrase":"involve ... traffic"},{"uid":"692a89fd-fbdb-463f-84a8-238d8fce608a f64f27ab-b3bb-494d-8ca2-9cdbd3821e1d","qNum":"37 38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"increased"},{"uid":"692a89fd-fbdb-463f-84a8-238d8fce608a","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"expose nearby areas to additional artificial lighting","passagePhrase":"light"},{"uid":"9f1cf9cd-390f-4fdf-b8ff-329be63af767","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"Operations","passagePhrase":"The activities and conditions"},{"uid":"717aa976-3db7-45a1-b806-4eb0788b3e62","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"at every drilling site","passagePhrase":"at each well"},{"uid":"6f068aa0-14a7-4660-b1de-1075f4680c7c","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"The danger posed by additives","passagePhrase":"toxicities"},{"uid":"ad6cfe6a-f7de-45b5-af15-af5f0f7d277a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"not the same","passagePhrase":"may vary"},{"uid":"e4d3fe28-b5ab-4981-b6ec-5a5531e82100","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"do not publicise the chemicals that they use","passagePhrase":"the complete chemical compositions were not reported ... Chemical secrecy"},{"uid":"a18cebb4-8780-4a8c-84d8-bd8afcfeca82","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Workers contaminated","passagePhrase":"persons working at wells and persons who come into contact with chemicals"},{"uid":"5f75f294-288b-46f6-ae7c-ee09e18efdee","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"can have proper treatment delayed","passagePhrase":"do not have sufficient information to know whether they need medical attention ... lack key information for deciding what actions they should take"},{"uid":"e3dd95b8-6c17-4d2e-a481-9710bf580ca0","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Most recommended safeguards","passagePhrase":"Hundreds of best management practices ... most of these"},{"uid":"cbe54e20-050c-4212-ab82-afa25e824b5b","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"optional","passagePhrase":"voluntary"},{"uid":"1577c11f-23e3-4dab-90d4-69333d0f5ecb","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"create financial reserves","passagePhrase":"establish funding mechanisms ... collecting monies"},{"uid":"1f0559da-f9b1-40d4-aba0-4ec2533d56df","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"cover damage that may emerge later","passagePhrase":"remedy future damages"}]},"reading_u2_91":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>The Invention of Television</span></b></p><p><span>The question “Who invented television?” is simple enough, but the answer is surprisingly controversial. No single person was responsible for producing what we think of as television today. Instead, its development depended on the work of several inventors, whose ideas often built on one another.</span></p><p><span>One of the earliest important contributors was the German inventor Paul Nipkow. He devised a method of “scanning” an image using a spinning disk with a spiral of small pinholes. As the disk rotated at high speed, each hole allowed light reflected from the object being photographed to fall on a selenium cell. The amount of voltage generated by the cell depended on the amount of light it received, and one complete rotation of the disk produced one frame of “video”. At the receiving end, the process was reversed: a similar disk spun in synchronisation while a neon lamp responded to changes in voltage and projected the image onto a screen. Although Nipkow created the disk and acquired a patent for his invention, he <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"00fd51cb-1d87-4f57-bba5-0eebccbd0706\">did not create the apparatus<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"2222cd2a-ecb5-4e00-80cb-34cfaed9d64c\">to project images<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. The patent eventually expired <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"2e6c8149-030d-4304-a7a5-a66e4cce9668\">after 15 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, as the work <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"fc015258-69f9-4a63-8106-ab30c9467486\">attracted no interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"2e6c8149-030d-4304-a7a5-a66e4cce9668\">during that period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. His ideas were later incorporated into practical television systems, and Nipkow became a celebrated scientist in Germany. Eventually, however, the mechanical nature of his disk caused the system to fade into obscurity with the arrival of the cathode ray tube.</span></p><p><span>Another German scientist, Arthur Korn, also contributed to the technological foundations on which later television systems depended. His early work focused on visual telegraphic transmission and made use of advances in amplification tube technology. In 1906, he transmitted a picture of the German Crown Prince over a distance of 1,800 kilometres, and in 1923 he sent a picture of the Pope across the Atlantic. Korn’s work helped to develop Nipkow’s ideas, which in turn contributed to Baird’s later breakthroughs. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"c6a336fc-9ff2-481f-813a-0d5947c3085f\">His technology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> also found practical applications outside broadcasting: from 1928, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"edb3877e-0287-40f2-b683-29b86217dbca\">the German police used it to transmit photographs and fingerprints<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>It was partly on these earlier developments that the Scotsman John Logie Baird built some of the first practical television systems. Baird had shown signs of inventive ingenuity from an early stage, once setting up a telephone exchange to connect his house with those of nearby friends. His interest in television began in 1903 after he read a German book describing the photoelectric properties of selenium. In 1873, this element was discovered to have the capacity to generate an electric current proportional to the amount of light applied to it. While working in Hastings, England, Baird <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"ed0134c2-27de-4934-867f-33d1446ec129\">constructed an experimental apparatus<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"5fea1916-4b60-4711-a6e6-65aa1b87f038\">an old hatbox<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> bought in a second-hand shop, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"5fea1916-4b60-4711-a6e6-65aa1b87f038\">a pair of scissors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"5fea1916-4b60-4711-a6e6-65aa1b87f038\">some needles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"5fea1916-4b60-4711-a6e6-65aa1b87f038\">bicycle-light lenses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"5fea1916-4b60-4711-a6e6-65aa1b87f038\">an old tea chest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. His system made use of Nipkow’s disk and also drew on Korn’s earlier work, bringing together several developments that had preceded him.</span></p><p><span>In February 1924, Baird demonstrated moving silhouette images on a “television”. Later that year, after almost destroying his house and nearly killing himself with an electric shock, he moved to London, where he gave the first public display of his invention. On 2 October 1925, he used his office assistant, William Taynton, as the subject of a transmission. Taynton became <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"ec930f69-a6c4-4b13-b123-ef4a79477643\">the first person to be televised moving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and in full tonal range. Baird later demonstrated what were claimed to be the first colour television images on 3 July 1928, although the identity of the inventor of colour television is also disputed. In the same year, he transmitted television pictures across the Atlantic for the first time. Although Baird was well known for his invention, he gained further fame by refusing a £100,000 offer for shares in his company—an enormous sum at the time. He reportedly said that he would not be able to sleep at night knowing that he had so much money.</span></p><p><span>Baird, however, was not the only person who could claim an early breakthrough in television. The American inventor Charles Francis Jenkins, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"ed106648-ce56-4305-802e-4ce6825d2e9c\">already well known<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> for inventing the motion-picture projector, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"147d0226-5ce4-4e8c-9622-a551cbbdb755\">transmitted a silhouette picture from one room to another<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in 1922. He later founded a broadcasting company in 1928, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d6d2a95a-a50f-41f1-99a9-c0e108894773\">the financial crash of 1929<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"f46df4be-9de0-4a7c-ac16-333944577389\">forced him out of business<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. Most accounts place Baird’s first public television demonstration a couple of years before Jenkins’s, although this chronology remains disputed in some sources.</span></p><p><span>Meanwhile, a different approach to television was emerging in the United States: electronic television. In 1927, Philo Farnsworth successfully demonstrated an electronic television system in San Francisco. His system used a television camera to break a picture into a series of electrical lines. These were transmitted so rapidly that the human eye would merge them into an image. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"1e6b3058-471e-41e5-8b6e-74e94f22e47d\">Farnsworth’s own invention, the image dissector<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, then converted the electrical information back into a picture. The Russian inventor Vladimir Zworykin subsequently built on this work. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be42c39d-64d4-42ba-a3e5-458485dfb3c3\">His designs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"6021494d-3746-4477-b5f3-f4e136357565\">were eventually adopted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"24878358-8b48-452d-9a6f-e8ff84fc6e79\">by the BBC<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> in the United Kingdom <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9e60fc59-7f31-4614-965b-1c07b0680642\">to replace Baird’s mechanical system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>It is therefore plain that the identity of the inventor of television remains controversial. The technology emerged from a succession of related discoveries rather than from the work of one person alone. Some inventors provided important mechanical principles, others advanced the transmission of images, and still others developed practical mechanical or electronic television systems. In many cases, the answer to the question “Who invented television?” simply depends on the country of the person answering it.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the different significant people in the process of the invention of television (questions 1 – 7) and match them to their roles in this process (A – I). </span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of roles</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A</span></b><span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be42c39d-64d4-42ba-a3e5-458485dfb3c3\">His work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"6021494d-3746-4477-b5f3-f4e136357565\">was adopted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9e60fc59-7f31-4614-965b-1c07b0680642\">in place of an older system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"24878358-8b48-452d-9a6f-e8ff84fc6e79\">at a broadcaster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B</span></b><span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"c6a336fc-9ff2-481f-813a-0d5947c3085f\">His work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"edb3877e-0287-40f2-b683-29b86217dbca\">used to help fight crime<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C</span></b><span>. He was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"ec930f69-a6c4-4b13-b123-ef4a79477643\">the first person to move on television<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D</span></b><span>. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"ed0134c2-27de-4934-867f-33d1446ec129\">built his device<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> from used <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"5fea1916-4b60-4711-a6e6-65aa1b87f038\">everyday objects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E</span></b><span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"f46df4be-9de0-4a7c-ac16-333944577389\">His business was destroyed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d6d2a95a-a50f-41f1-99a9-c0e108894773\">an economic crisis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><b><span>F</span></b><span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"1e6b3058-471e-41e5-8b6e-74e94f22e47d\">He invented the image dissector<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><b><span>G</span></b><span>. His work <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"fc015258-69f9-4a63-8106-ab30c9467486\">received little attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"2e6c8149-030d-4304-a7a5-a66e4cce9668\">for a period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><b><span>H</span></b><span>. He sold his shares in his company for a large sum.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. He invented the cathode ray tube.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326119\" id=\"question-wrapper-326119\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>John Logie Baird</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326120\" id=\"question-wrapper-326120\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>William Taynton</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326121\" id=\"question-wrapper-326121\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Philo Farnsworth</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326122\" id=\"question-wrapper-326122\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Vladimir Zworykin</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326123\" id=\"question-wrapper-326123\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paul Nipkow</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326124\" id=\"question-wrapper-326124\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Arthur Korn</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326125\" id=\"question-wrapper-326125\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Charles Francis Jenkins</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Label the diagram below. </span></p><p><span>Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer. </span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 8-10 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Transmitting an Image using a Nipkow Disk</span></b></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_4/reading/images/f0223efb1544b182aee4d9a1c7388320cf0e2be16ea3a22909b574f3c9ed9129.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326126\" id=\"question-wrapper-326126\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(SMALL) PINHOLES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326127\" id=\"question-wrapper-326127\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(SELENIUM) CELL</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326128\" id=\"question-wrapper-326128\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(NEON) LAMP</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326129\" id=\"question-wrapper-326129\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Nipkow <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"00fd51cb-1d87-4f57-bba5-0eebccbd0706\">built a working device<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"2222cd2a-ecb5-4e00-80cb-34cfaed9d64c\">could display the images<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> his disk scanned.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326130\" id=\"question-wrapper-326130\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Korn and Nipkow often met to discuss their work.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326131\" id=\"question-wrapper-326131\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Charles Francis Jenkins <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"ed106648-ce56-4305-802e-4ce6825d2e9c\">was already famous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"147d0226-5ce4-4e8c-9622-a551cbbdb755\">when he experimented with television<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"2222cd2a-ecb5-4e00-80cb-34cfaed9d64c","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"could display the images","passagePhrase":"to project images"},{"uid":"2e6c8149-030d-4304-a7a5-a66e4cce9668","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"for a period","passagePhrase":"after 15 years ... during that period"},{"uid":"fc015258-69f9-4a63-8106-ab30c9467486","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"received little attention","passagePhrase":"attracted no interest"},{"uid":"c6a336fc-9ff2-481f-813a-0d5947c3085f","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"His work","passagePhrase":"His technology"},{"uid":"edb3877e-0287-40f2-b683-29b86217dbca","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"used to help fight crime","passagePhrase":"the German police used it to transmit photographs and fingerprints"},{"uid":"ed0134c2-27de-4934-867f-33d1446ec129","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"built his device","passagePhrase":"constructed an experimental apparatus"},{"uid":"5fea1916-4b60-4711-a6e6-65aa1b87f038","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"everyday objects","passagePhrase":"an old hatbox ... a pair of scissors ... some needles ... bicycle-light lenses ... an old tea chest"},{"uid":"ec930f69-a6c4-4b13-b123-ef4a79477643","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"the first person to move on television","passagePhrase":"the first person to be televised moving"},{"uid":"ed106648-ce56-4305-802e-4ce6825d2e9c","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"was already famous","passagePhrase":"already well known"},{"uid":"147d0226-5ce4-4e8c-9622-a551cbbdb755","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"when he experimented with television","passagePhrase":"transmitted a silhouette picture from one room to another"},{"uid":"d6d2a95a-a50f-41f1-99a9-c0e108894773","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"an economic crisis","passagePhrase":"the financial crash of 1929"},{"uid":"f46df4be-9de0-4a7c-ac16-333944577389","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"His business was destroyed","passagePhrase":"forced him out of business"},{"uid":"1e6b3058-471e-41e5-8b6e-74e94f22e47d","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"He invented the image dissector","passagePhrase":"Farnsworth’s own invention, the image dissector"},{"uid":"be42c39d-64d4-42ba-a3e5-458485dfb3c3","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"His work","passagePhrase":"His designs"},{"uid":"6021494d-3746-4477-b5f3-f4e136357565","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"was adopted","passagePhrase":"were eventually adopted"},{"uid":"24878358-8b48-452d-9a6f-e8ff84fc6e79","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"at a broadcaster","passagePhrase":"by the BBC"},{"uid":"9e60fc59-7f31-4614-965b-1c07b0680642","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"in place of an older system","passagePhrase":"to replace Baird’s mechanical system"}]},"reading_u2_92":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>Speaking of Nothing</span></b></p><p><i><span>Why we talk about the weather and other trivia</span></i></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><span>Some workers are happier in their jobs than others, but this is not only to do with the work itself. Consider <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d66efbb8-d4ba-4f6c-b951-5321f2faa8dd\">security guards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d66efbb8-d4ba-4f6c-b951-5321f2faa8dd\">truck drivers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d66efbb8-d4ba-4f6c-b951-5321f2faa8dd\">salespeople<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>: year after year, these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d66efbb8-d4ba-4f6c-b951-5321f2faa8dd\">occupations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> appear on lists of the unhappiest careers. It is true that many factors can make a job cheerless, including unusual hours, low pay and a lack of opportunities for advancement. However, these three types of work stand out for another reason: they involve either <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c24bb1a8-f30d-489b-9698-b3e4a60ffedc\">little conversation or obligatory small talk that is largely superficial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. Typical subjects include the weather, holiday destinations and food. Psychologists have long argued that connecting with others through meaningful exchanges is central to well-being, but exactly how much conversation we require is still under investigation.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><span>Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire of the University of Arizona in the United States wanted to investigate the types of conversations people have. Their team used a device to record short verbal exchanges periodically while participants went about their daily activities. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"12d9a28e-0e61-48ea-8a86-51f209ad570e\">The researchers monitored undergraduates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> for four days, then classified each recorded conversation as either ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"2e6e663c-9cbd-4f95-96f2-ab911f3e1291\">small talk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>’ or ‘substantive’. They found that people who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"72f4934d-0ab4-4c37-91d1-c1272cdceea5\">had more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"2e6e663c-9cbd-4f95-96f2-ab911f3e1291\">substantive conversations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> were more likely to report <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"eeb91ff7-05fe-4dfb-bb80-b16beca47ffe\">feeling happy and fulfilled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> overall. In fact, the happiest students had roughly twice as many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"33904d4a-6408-4548-b469-68ef7f813c07\">substantive conversations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> as the unhappiest ones. Small talk, meanwhile, accounted for only 10 per cent of the conversations of the happiest students, compared with almost 30 per cent among the least content.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><span>However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"041ed7ec-d2f2-4164-8e64-0e3055a0190d\">small talk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> still has a role to play. Rather than conveying information, scientists believe that it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"92ce1af1-be5f-4acb-a5ca-d407ddde649f\">can promote social bonding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Ipek Kulahci and her team at University College Cork in Ireland examined the relationship between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"38c4b529-9f6f-4680-a2c4-de1280ea0b85\">vocal exchanges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and grooming in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6c7ae472-7194-4686-b4ab-734ffedbd958\">lemurs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. The researchers found that the animals reserved their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"38c4b529-9f6f-4680-a2c4-de1280ea0b85\">call-and-response conversations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, the equivalent of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6c7ae472-7194-4686-b4ab-734ffedbd958\">human<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"38c4b529-9f6f-4680-a2c4-de1280ea0b85\">chitchat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, for those they groomed most often. This suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"38c4b529-9f6f-4680-a2c4-de1280ea0b85\">small talk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> can help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"2a41e3a5-d74d-4b8e-806d-96ed255e9aed\">maintain closeness with familiar companions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> rather than serving merely as a way of managing awkward exchanges with strangers. It appears that, even among animals, vocal exchanges can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"2a41e3a5-d74d-4b8e-806d-96ed255e9aed\">indicate strong social bonds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> between group members.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><span>Connecting with others seems to increase happiness, yet strangers in close proximity routinely ignore one another. To examine the experience of connecting with strangers, psychologists Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder of the University of Chicago <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"99861776-1c74-412a-8f0a-1c54a45f8f45\">gave volunteers different instructions about whether to </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 24\" data-uid=\"99861776-1c74-412a-8f0a-1c54a45f8f45 d8aecc3f-de9a-463b-bbc8-c74a5742a235\">talk to</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"d8aecc3f-de9a-463b-bbc8-c74a5742a235\"> fellow commuters on their </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 24\" data-uid=\"4d444405-a46e-4aec-98b7-51604f3dcb1f d8aecc3f-de9a-463b-bbc8-c74a5742a235\">regular train journey to work</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>—something they would normally avoid. Those told to chat with others reported a more pleasant journey than those told to ‘enjoy your solitude’ or behave as they normally would. All the volunteers who initiated conversations reported a positive reaction from the people they spoke to. Yet the participants had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1bede164-05cf-4da9-a839-aac720e5154b\">predicted precisely the opposite<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>: they had expected the other commuters to prefer being left alone.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><span>When we buy a cup of coffee at a café, we sometimes chat with the service staff, but on other occasions we say as little as possible in order to save time. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"f369d9d3-4a96-4836-8cec-9953613b29bf\">Every day<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, we have opportunities to transform potentially impersonal exchanges into genuine social interactions. In other words, treating a service provider as we would an acquaintance might make us happier. In a study by Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn, people who <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 20\" data-uid=\"0e6f80b4-67fe-4394-b16a-ba7993f2872f 98bc50a6-79fe-4d8d-bdef-1af1da11d428\">interacted socially</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"0e6f80b4-67fe-4394-b16a-ba7993f2872f\"> with a server</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"f369d9d3-4a96-4836-8cec-9953613b29bf\">coffee shop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 20\" data-uid=\"58f2038a-d512-4a53-866d-00c496e5c1c9 cc777cf3-18fb-4c1d-915a-8d424cebc5e7\">felt better emotionally</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> than those who were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"316c78a7-f2fa-41fa-9a70-0fe8d61b870a\">in a rush to get everything done<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. As well as feeling happier, the first group had a stronger sense of belonging. Similar results have emerged in other settings. When volunteers broke the silence in an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"f369d9d3-4a96-4836-8cec-9953613b29bf\">art gallery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 25\" data-uid=\"75c60d69-b43f-48cc-95f4-2b74cd9a41c7 98bc50a6-79fe-4d8d-bdef-1af1da11d428\">chat with other visitors</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, those visitors <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"cc777cf3-18fb-4c1d-915a-8d424cebc5e7\">felt happier and </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 25\" data-uid=\"0c5a72da-3eb9-4117-8542-8f086a75de8e cc777cf3-18fb-4c1d-915a-8d424cebc5e7\">more connected</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"0c5a72da-3eb9-4117-8542-8f086a75de8e\"> to</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> the paintings than people who were not approached. The pleasure of connection also appears to be contagious: in a laboratory waiting room, participants who were spoken to reported experiences that were just as positive as those of the people instructed to start the conversation.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><span>Of course, some of us are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"21bafa1e-d0dc-4932-887d-1570b66fe927\">better than others at small talk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. In a study by Todd Kashdan and his team at George Mason University in the United States, people rated as ‘<span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 23\" data-uid=\"5e04c5a8-612d-441a-9c10-132308dfc4d6 cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb\">less curious</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> about all aspects of life’ <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 23\" data-uid=\"21bafa1e-d0dc-4932-887d-1570b66fe927 cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb\">had difficulty starting conversations</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb\"> on their own</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. However, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8f91adfc-4a1e-44ae-9210-b2a73ae68ec4\">were more successful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"fb60e8d9-f0ff-41cb-b749-93d0d66a33e2\">building closeness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> with others <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8f91adfc-4a1e-44ae-9210-b2a73ae68ec4\">when supplied with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> topics that encouraged people to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"fb60e8d9-f0ff-41cb-b749-93d0d66a33e2\">open up about themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and their lives. By contrast, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb\">people judged to be ‘</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 23\" data-uid=\"5e04c5a8-612d-441a-9c10-132308dfc4d6 cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb\">curious</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb\">’ </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 23\" data-uid=\"21bafa1e-d0dc-4932-887d-1570b66fe927 cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb\">needed no help</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e3d068b9-f8fe-4517-8c2f-df8fa4b74ba9\">moving from ordinary subjects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> such as favourite holidays <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e3d068b9-f8fe-4517-8c2f-df8fa4b74ba9\">to more personal areas of conversation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. In another experiment, William Fleeson of Wake Forest University divided participants into two groups: those who were naturally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5e04c5a8-612d-441a-9c10-132308dfc4d6\">outgoing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and those who were more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5e04c5a8-612d-441a-9c10-132308dfc4d6\">reserved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in social situations. They were then instructed to behave in the opposite manner to their usual <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5e04c5a8-612d-441a-9c10-132308dfc4d6\">disposition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Participants reported more positive feelings when instructed to act <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5e04c5a8-612d-441a-9c10-132308dfc4d6\">extroverted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> than when instructed to act <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5e04c5a8-612d-441a-9c10-132308dfc4d6\">introverted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. The overall conclusion, therefore, is that everyone <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"975aa0a2-9db9-4faa-a232-b77a47be5a98\">can benefit from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> more conversation—the more meaningful, the better.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A–F.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, i–ix, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. Why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"041ed7ec-d2f2-4164-8e64-0e3055a0190d\">seemingly trivial exchanges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"92ce1af1-be5f-4acb-a5ca-d407ddde649f\">have a social function<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. The practical difficulties of observing everyday conversation</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"d8aecc3f-de9a-463b-bbc8-c74a5742a235\">An experiment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1bede164-05cf-4da9-a839-aac720e5154b\">produced an unexpected result<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"12d9a28e-0e61-48ea-8a86-51f209ad570e\">A study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> comparing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"2e6e663c-9cbd-4f95-96f2-ab911f3e1291\">different patterns of everyday conversation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. How <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"5e04c5a8-612d-441a-9c10-132308dfc4d6\">personality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"21bafa1e-d0dc-4932-887d-1570b66fe927\">influences conversational ease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"975aa0a2-9db9-4faa-a232-b77a47be5a98\">benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. Why people expect strangers to avoid conversation</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d66efbb8-d4ba-4f6c-b951-5321f2faa8dd\">Jobs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c24bb1a8-f30d-489b-9698-b3e4a60ffedc\">little genuine interaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. The disadvantages of relying on familiar topics in conversation</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"f369d9d3-4a96-4836-8cec-9953613b29bf\">Everyday situations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"98bc50a6-79fe-4d8d-bdef-1af1da11d428\">social interaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"cc777cf3-18fb-4c1d-915a-8d424cebc5e7\">improves the experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326132\" id=\"question-wrapper-326132\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326133\" id=\"question-wrapper-326133\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326134\" id=\"question-wrapper-326134\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326135\" id=\"question-wrapper-326135\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326136\" id=\"question-wrapper-326136\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ix</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326137\" id=\"question-wrapper-326137\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements and the list of researchers below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct researcher, A–E.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–E, in boxes 20–23 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Researchers</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Matthias R. Mehl and Simine Vazire</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Ipek Kulahci</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Gillian Sandstrom and Elizabeth Dunn</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Todd Kashdan</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326138\" id=\"question-wrapper-326138\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Turning <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"316c78a7-f2fa-41fa-9a70-0fe8d61b870a\">a routine transaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"0e6f80b4-67fe-4394-b16a-ba7993f2872f\">a social exchange<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"58f2038a-d512-4a53-866d-00c496e5c1c9\">improve how people feel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326139\" id=\"question-wrapper-326139\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"72f4934d-0ab4-4c37-91d1-c1272cdceea5\">engage more often<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"33904d4a-6408-4548-b469-68ef7f813c07\">meaningful conversation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> tend to report <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"eeb91ff7-05fe-4dfb-bb80-b16beca47ffe\">greater well-being<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326140\" id=\"question-wrapper-326140\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6c7ae472-7194-4686-b4ab-734ffedbd958\">more than one species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> whose members <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"38c4b529-9f6f-4680-a2c4-de1280ea0b85\">communicate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"2a41e3a5-d74d-4b8e-806d-96ed255e9aed\">for social reasons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326141\" id=\"question-wrapper-326141\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e3d068b9-f8fe-4517-8c2f-df8fa4b74ba9\">move beyond ordinary conversational topics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb\">varies between people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326142\" id=\"question-wrapper-326142\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the train experiment, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"99861776-1c74-412a-8f0a-1c54a45f8f45\">participants were asked to talk to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> fellow (24)______ they encountered during their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"4d444405-a46e-4aec-98b7-51604f3dcb1f\">daily travel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMMUTERS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326143\" id=\"question-wrapper-326143\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the art-gallery experiment, people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"0c5a72da-3eb9-4117-8542-8f086a75de8e\">related more to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> the (25)_______ when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"75c60d69-b43f-48cc-95f4-2b74cd9a41c7\">another visitor spoke to them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PAINTINGS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326144\" id=\"question-wrapper-326144\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Less curious participants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8f91adfc-4a1e-44ae-9210-b2a73ae68ec4\">benefited from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26)_______ that helped them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"fb60e8d9-f0ff-41cb-b749-93d0d66a33e2\">deepen their exchanges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> with others.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TOPICS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"d66efbb8-d4ba-4f6c-b951-5321f2faa8dd","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Jobs","passagePhrase":"security guards ... truck drivers ... salespeople ... occupations"},{"uid":"c24bb1a8-f30d-489b-9698-b3e4a60ffedc","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"little genuine interaction","passagePhrase":"little conversation or obligatory small talk that is largely superficial"},{"uid":"12d9a28e-0e61-48ea-8a86-51f209ad570e","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"A study","passagePhrase":"The researchers monitored undergraduates"},{"uid":"2e6e663c-9cbd-4f95-96f2-ab911f3e1291","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"different patterns of everyday conversation","passagePhrase":"small talk ... substantive conversations"},{"uid":"72f4934d-0ab4-4c37-91d1-c1272cdceea5","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"engage more often","passagePhrase":"had more"},{"uid":"eeb91ff7-05fe-4dfb-bb80-b16beca47ffe","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"greater well-being","passagePhrase":"feeling happy and fulfilled"},{"uid":"33904d4a-6408-4548-b469-68ef7f813c07","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"meaningful conversation","passagePhrase":"substantive conversations"},{"uid":"041ed7ec-d2f2-4164-8e64-0e3055a0190d","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"seemingly trivial exchanges","passagePhrase":"small talk"},{"uid":"92ce1af1-be5f-4acb-a5ca-d407ddde649f","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"have a social function","passagePhrase":"can promote social bonding"},{"uid":"38c4b529-9f6f-4680-a2c4-de1280ea0b85","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"communicate","passagePhrase":"vocal exchanges ... call-and-response conversations ... chitchat ... small talk"},{"uid":"6c7ae472-7194-4686-b4ab-734ffedbd958","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"more than one species","passagePhrase":"lemurs ... human"},{"uid":"2a41e3a5-d74d-4b8e-806d-96ed255e9aed","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"for social reasons","passagePhrase":"maintain closeness with familiar companions ... indicate strong social bonds"},{"uid":"99861776-1c74-412a-8f0a-1c54a45f8f45","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"participants were asked to talk to","passagePhrase":"gave volunteers different instructions about whether to"},{"uid":"99861776-1c74-412a-8f0a-1c54a45f8f45 d8aecc3f-de9a-463b-bbc8-c74a5742a235","qNum":"17 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"talk to"},{"uid":"d8aecc3f-de9a-463b-bbc8-c74a5742a235","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"An experiment","passagePhrase":"fellow commuters on their"},{"uid":"4d444405-a46e-4aec-98b7-51604f3dcb1f d8aecc3f-de9a-463b-bbc8-c74a5742a235","qNum":"17 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"regular train journey to work"},{"uid":"1bede164-05cf-4da9-a839-aac720e5154b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"produced an unexpected result","passagePhrase":"predicted precisely the opposite"},{"uid":"f369d9d3-4a96-4836-8cec-9953613b29bf","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Everyday situations","passagePhrase":"Every day ... coffee shop ... art gallery"},{"uid":"0e6f80b4-67fe-4394-b16a-ba7993f2872f 98bc50a6-79fe-4d8d-bdef-1af1da11d428","qNum":"18 20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"interacted socially"},{"uid":"0e6f80b4-67fe-4394-b16a-ba7993f2872f","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"a social exchange","passagePhrase":"with a server"},{"uid":"58f2038a-d512-4a53-866d-00c496e5c1c9 cc777cf3-18fb-4c1d-915a-8d424cebc5e7","qNum":"18 20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"felt better emotionally"},{"uid":"316c78a7-f2fa-41fa-9a70-0fe8d61b870a","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"a routine transaction","passagePhrase":"in a rush to get everything done"},{"uid":"75c60d69-b43f-48cc-95f4-2b74cd9a41c7 98bc50a6-79fe-4d8d-bdef-1af1da11d428","qNum":"18 25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"chat with other visitors"},{"uid":"cc777cf3-18fb-4c1d-915a-8d424cebc5e7","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"improves the experience","passagePhrase":"felt happier and"},{"uid":"0c5a72da-3eb9-4117-8542-8f086a75de8e cc777cf3-18fb-4c1d-915a-8d424cebc5e7","qNum":"18 25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"more connected"},{"uid":"0c5a72da-3eb9-4117-8542-8f086a75de8e","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"related more to","passagePhrase":"to"},{"uid":"21bafa1e-d0dc-4932-887d-1570b66fe927","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"influences conversational ease","passagePhrase":"better than others at small talk"},{"uid":"5e04c5a8-612d-441a-9c10-132308dfc4d6 cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb","qNum":"19 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"less curious ... curious"},{"uid":"21bafa1e-d0dc-4932-887d-1570b66fe927 cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb","qNum":"19 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"had difficulty starting conversations ... needed no help"},{"uid":"cb9638f8-c21d-43b7-b5b0-722595be46fb","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"varies between people","passagePhrase":"on their own ... people judged to be ‘ ... ’"},{"uid":"8f91adfc-4a1e-44ae-9210-b2a73ae68ec4","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"benefited from","passagePhrase":"were more successful ... when supplied with"},{"uid":"fb60e8d9-f0ff-41cb-b749-93d0d66a33e2","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"deepen their exchanges","passagePhrase":"building closeness ... open up about themselves"},{"uid":"e3d068b9-f8fe-4517-8c2f-df8fa4b74ba9","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"move beyond ordinary conversational topics","passagePhrase":"moving from ordinary subjects ... to more personal areas of conversation"},{"uid":"5e04c5a8-612d-441a-9c10-132308dfc4d6","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"personality","passagePhrase":"outgoing ... reserved ... disposition ... extroverted ... introverted"},{"uid":"975aa0a2-9db9-4faa-a232-b77a47be5a98","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"benefits","passagePhrase":"can benefit from"},{"uid":"98bc50a6-79fe-4d8d-bdef-1af1da11d428","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"social interaction","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"58f2038a-d512-4a53-866d-00c496e5c1c9","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"improve how people feel","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"4d444405-a46e-4aec-98b7-51604f3dcb1f","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"daily travel","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"75c60d69-b43f-48cc-95f4-2b74cd9a41c7","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"another visitor spoke to them","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_93":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>Antibiotic Resistance</span></b></p><p><span>An antibiotic is a drug that kills or prevents the growth of bacteria. The term \"antibiotic\", coined by Selman Waksman, originally described only those antibiotics derived from living organisms, in contrast to \"chemotherapeutic agents\", which are purely synthetic. Currently, the term antibiotic is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"9a4b8ede-f51c-4ce1-9286-45f81b8c0cac\">also applied to synthetic antimicrobials<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Overuse or misuse of antibiotics may result in the development of antibiotic resistance in the infecting organisms, similar to the development of pesticide resistance in insects. Doctor Iain Nicholson explains: \"The concept of genetic selection requires that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"9dc5270a-c73f-4488-9979-d1c93f057971\">as close as possible to 100 per cent of the infecting organisms be killed off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"17bfdde4-74fb-436a-8517-0cdfb2f3945d\">avoid selection of resistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. If a small subset of the population <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"2f15f9fd-1f2a-4841-bb33-095b5ab78792\">survives the treatment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and is allowed to multiply, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bc53efe4-4ce1-46b6-a0e0-ba68e5d90248\">the average susceptibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"ed89bbba-9801-417f-ad4c-ae4b377237ac\">this new population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to the compound will be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bc53efe4-4ce1-46b6-a0e0-ba68e5d90248\">much lower than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> that of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bc53efe4-4ce1-46b6-a0e0-ba68e5d90248\">original population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, since they have descended from those few organisms that survived the original treatment.\"</span></p><p><span>Antibiotic resistance <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"1b3076a4-89bd-4902-b232-07ba4d7948df\">has become a serious problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"add6be5a-fba5-43ff-86fa-eab56be19246\">both developed and developing nations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. In certain settings, such as hospitals, the rate of antibiotic resistance is so high today that the normal, low-cost antibiotics are virtually useless for the treatment of frequently seen infections. This leads to more common use of newer and more expensive compounds, which in turn leads to the rise of resistance to those drugs. Drug company spokesperson Emma Thompson explains the challenge facing the drug industry: \"A continuous race to discover new and different antibiotics results in an attempt to keep humanity from losing ground in the battle <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"2ed7680c-156f-4743-a12b-4a39aa60084b\">again<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>st infection. The fear is that we will eventually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"a8d160e3-8c75-41e1-9f86-aa938f9daa2c\">fail to keep up in this race<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, and that people may again face <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"6dec1003-fd79-4e5e-a79c-14af3cf16eff\">life-threatening<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> bacterial infections.\"</span></p><p><span>An example of antibiotic resistance is Staphylococcus aureus, which used to be treated successfully with penicillin in the 1940s and 1950s. At present, nearly all strains are resistant to penicillin, and many are resistant to other antibiotics, leaving only a narrow selection of drugs useful for treatment. The situation is worsened by the fact that genes coding for antibiotic resistance can be transferred between bacteria, making it possible for bacteria never exposed to an antibiotic to acquire resistance from those which have been.</span></p><p><span>Microbial resistance to antibiotics is a natural consequence of selective pressures placed on bacteria. However, humans have greatly accelerated the evolution of resistant bacteria through the overuse and misuse of antibiotics in the community. Government health official Georgina Haynes explains: \"One of the major problems is when antibiotics are used to treat disorders for which they have no efficacy, such as the common cold or other viral complaints, and when they are used widely as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"c38a486c-8907-40e5-8f64-d4fc87f5983c\">prophylaxis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> rather than treatment, because this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"aaee18cc-3f08-4ad2-be84-3a6252e7c106\">exposes more bacteria to selection for resistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.\" Similarly, in order to kill all the bacteria of an infection, antibiotics must be taken for a whole course and not stopped just when symptoms improve. The discoverer of penicillin himself, Alexander Fleming, warned the scientific community: \"The administration of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"9473bbe9-342e-4076-802b-1057f7731fd7\">too small doses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"82d2b004-e134-42fd-b9ea-7d663cf0f7b1\">leads to the production of resistant strains of bacteria<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.\" This can happen due to patient ignorance and improper pharmacy practices, usually in the developing world. In developing countries, antibiotic prescriptions are often broken up. For example, in some Asian countries, it is common for pharmacies to sell as many tablets as the patient can afford, which may be only two or three. This is an insufficient dose to cure an infection and will only further contribute to the evolution of resistant strains of bacteria. Recent reports have also shown that containers of medicine from some African countries sometimes contain only half the drug content indicated on the label. This may be due to \"counterfeit\" medicines or improper storage, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"abbc20c0-9677-4a18-b9a1-21ea72d6ea9a\">tropical conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, such as those <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"83a15d32-8b29-456c-81dd-1b5b3015b536\">often found in Africa<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, also readily cause <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a7694d28-7d18-4e4a-a7a6-4ae6ee31cc1d\">degradation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"71d0f8b7-ed84-4dac-bdeb-baed779de817\">medical compounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Chenbo Okonkwa, a pharmaceutical wholesaler, describes the problem: \"Although local regulations may require pharmacies to store drugs in air-conditioned premises, most undergo frequent power outages, and warehouses are rarely kept cool. Furthermore, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"0e5d9338-9f8d-44dc-8551-ce957a6bcc48\">unauthorised dealers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"165c294f-6130-475b-8be8-73286bfb9205\">rarely bother to follow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"4fd9f884-1e98-4cd2-a3a1-709213a09a4c\">official storage guidelines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.\"</span></p><p><span>Another problem contributing to antibiotic resistance is that antibiotics are widely used in food-producing animals, which contributes to the emergence of antibiotic-resistant bacteria in them. These resistant bacteria can <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"427283b7-e7cb-4ca9-bb6a-99b8f9bac4ad\">contaminate the foods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> that come from these animals, and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"427283b7-e7cb-4ca9-bb6a-99b8f9bac4ad\">people who consume these foods can develop antibiotic-resistant infections<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. This can be seen, for instance, in the fish farming industry. It is common to put upwards of 100,000 fish into each pen, which creates cramped and stressful conditions. This increases the susceptibility of fish to certain bacterial diseases, such as furunculosis. Furunculosis, an infection of the kidneys, is easily transmitted through water and so is devastating to fish farms. To combat the disease, antibiotics were added to fish food pellets, but these were unpalatable to the fish. The fish were already suffering from loss of appetite due to their infections, and so most of the antibiotics ended up at the bottom of the pens, allowing residual drugs to spread throughout the marine environment. Fish farmer Jo Hardwick explains that this is different now: \"Today, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"8d9c3773-8f21-4089-9eb1-486ab9987bef\">vaccines are replacing the antibiotic pellets as a treatment for the disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, but unfortunately, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"230cbdca-7fe6-4da3-af98-e9f27d7f18a2\">most of the damage has already been done<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.\"</span></p><p><span>In conclusion, antibiotics must be used judiciously in both humans and animals, because both uses contribute to the emergence, persistence, and spread of resistant bacteria. Resistant bacteria in food-producing animals are of particular concern. Food animals serve as a reservoir of resistant pathogens and resistance mechanisms that can directly or indirectly result in antibiotic-resistant infections in humans. If people do not wish to be faced with an attack of all the diseases they thought they had conquered in the twentieth century, society has to change its approach to antibiotic use.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements (questions 27-33) and the list of people below. </span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct person. </span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 27–33 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>NB</span></b><span> You can use any letter more than once.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A</span></b><span>. Iain Nicholson</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B</span></b><span>. Emma Thompson</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C</span></b><span>. Georgina Haynes</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D</span></b><span>. Alexander Fleming</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E</span></b><span>. Chenbo Okonkwa</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><b><span>F</span></b><span>. Jo Hardwick</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326145\" id=\"question-wrapper-326145\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"82d2b004-e134-42fd-b9ea-7d663cf0f7b1\">Bacterial resistance can develop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> when treatment is given in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"9473bbe9-342e-4076-802b-1057f7731fd7\">inadequate amounts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326146\" id=\"question-wrapper-326146\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"2f15f9fd-1f2a-4841-bb33-095b5ab78792\">Survival through the original treatment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> can result in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"ed89bbba-9801-417f-ad4c-ae4b377237ac\">later bacterial population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bc53efe4-4ce1-46b6-a0e0-ba68e5d90248\">reduced susceptibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to the drug.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326147\" id=\"question-wrapper-326147\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Using antibiotics as a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"c38a486c-8907-40e5-8f64-d4fc87f5983c\">preventative measure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"aaee18cc-3f08-4ad2-be84-3a6252e7c106\">a key factor in the development of antibiotic resistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326148\" id=\"question-wrapper-326148\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"8d9c3773-8f21-4089-9eb1-486ab9987bef\">Improving disease-management practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> on fish farms may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"230cbdca-7fe6-4da3-af98-e9f27d7f18a2\">too late to prevent antibiotics from spreading into the surrounding environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326149\" id=\"question-wrapper-326149\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"a8d160e3-8c75-41e1-9f86-aa938f9daa2c\">Failure to develop new antibiotics quickly enough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> could leave people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"2ed7680c-156f-4743-a12b-4a39aa60084b\">once more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> vulnerable to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"6dec1003-fd79-4e5e-a79c-14af3cf16eff\">potentially fatal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> bacterial infections.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326150\" id=\"question-wrapper-326150\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"17bfdde4-74fb-436a-8517-0cdfb2f3945d\">Preventing resistance from emerging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> through genetic selection depends on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"9dc5270a-c73f-4488-9979-d1c93f057971\">eliminating virtually all<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> infecting organisms.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326151\" id=\"question-wrapper-326151\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"4fd9f884-1e98-4cd2-a3a1-709213a09a4c\">Official requirements for storing medicines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"165c294f-6130-475b-8be8-73286bfb9205\">generally ignored<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"0e5d9338-9f8d-44dc-8551-ce957a6bcc48\">sellers operating outside regulated channels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? In boxes 34-38 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326152\" id=\"question-wrapper-326152\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The current definition of an antibiotic <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"9a4b8ede-f51c-4ce1-9286-45f81b8c0cac\">only includes drugs originating from live organisms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326153\" id=\"question-wrapper-326153\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"add6be5a-fba5-43ff-86fa-eab56be19246\">Countries at very different stages of economic development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"1b3076a4-89bd-4902-b232-07ba4d7948df\">face a major problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> from antibiotic resistance.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326154\" id=\"question-wrapper-326154\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some hospitals nowadays have to fund new antibiotic research themselves.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326155\" id=\"question-wrapper-326155\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"abbc20c0-9677-4a18-b9a1-21ea72d6ea9a\">Climate conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"83a15d32-8b29-456c-81dd-1b5b3015b536\">in some parts of Africa<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a7694d28-7d18-4e4a-a7a6-4ae6ee31cc1d\">damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"71d0f8b7-ed84-4dac-bdeb-baed779de817\">antibiotics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in their containers.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326156\" id=\"question-wrapper-326156\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The risks associated with resistant bacteria in food-producing animals <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"427283b7-e7cb-4ca9-bb6a-99b8f9bac4ad\">do not extend beyond the animals themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Label the diagram below. </span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer. </span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 39 and 40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The Misuse of Antibiotics in the Fish Farm Industry</span></b></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_4/reading/images/e8251cb1403cd73f7afaad15e1b069e1064f6ce93bc25edf0f082d95a2cc582e.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326157\" id=\"question-wrapper-326157\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(FOOD) PELLETS [OR] (FISH) FOOD</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326158\" id=\"question-wrapper-326158\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">APPETITE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"9dc5270a-c73f-4488-9979-d1c93f057971","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"eliminating virtually all","passagePhrase":"as close as possible to 100 per cent of the infecting organisms be killed off"},{"uid":"17bfdde4-74fb-436a-8517-0cdfb2f3945d","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Preventing resistance from emerging","passagePhrase":"avoid selection of resistance"},{"uid":"2f15f9fd-1f2a-4841-bb33-095b5ab78792","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Survival through the original treatment","passagePhrase":"survives the treatment"},{"uid":"bc53efe4-4ce1-46b6-a0e0-ba68e5d90248","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"reduced susceptibility","passagePhrase":"the average susceptibility ... much lower than ... original population"},{"uid":"ed89bbba-9801-417f-ad4c-ae4b377237ac","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"later bacterial population","passagePhrase":"this new population"},{"uid":"1b3076a4-89bd-4902-b232-07ba4d7948df","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"face a major problem","passagePhrase":"has become a serious problem"},{"uid":"add6be5a-fba5-43ff-86fa-eab56be19246","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Countries at very different stages of economic development","passagePhrase":"both developed and developing nations"},{"uid":"2ed7680c-156f-4743-a12b-4a39aa60084b","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"once more","passagePhrase":"again"},{"uid":"a8d160e3-8c75-41e1-9f86-aa938f9daa2c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Failure to develop new antibiotics quickly enough","passagePhrase":"fail to keep up in this race"},{"uid":"6dec1003-fd79-4e5e-a79c-14af3cf16eff","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"potentially fatal","passagePhrase":"life-threatening"},{"uid":"c38a486c-8907-40e5-8f64-d4fc87f5983c","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"preventative measure","passagePhrase":"prophylaxis"},{"uid":"aaee18cc-3f08-4ad2-be84-3a6252e7c106","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"a key factor in the development of antibiotic resistance","passagePhrase":"exposes more bacteria to selection for resistance"},{"uid":"9473bbe9-342e-4076-802b-1057f7731fd7","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"inadequate amounts","passagePhrase":"too small doses"},{"uid":"82d2b004-e134-42fd-b9ea-7d663cf0f7b1","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Bacterial resistance can develop","passagePhrase":"leads to the production of resistant strains of bacteria"},{"uid":"abbc20c0-9677-4a18-b9a1-21ea72d6ea9a","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"Climate conditions","passagePhrase":"tropical conditions"},{"uid":"83a15d32-8b29-456c-81dd-1b5b3015b536","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"in some parts of Africa","passagePhrase":"often found in Africa"},{"uid":"a7694d28-7d18-4e4a-a7a6-4ae6ee31cc1d","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"damage","passagePhrase":"degradation"},{"uid":"71d0f8b7-ed84-4dac-bdeb-baed779de817","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"antibiotics","passagePhrase":"medical compounds"},{"uid":"0e5d9338-9f8d-44dc-8551-ce957a6bcc48","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"sellers operating outside regulated channels","passagePhrase":"unauthorised dealers"},{"uid":"165c294f-6130-475b-8be8-73286bfb9205","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"generally ignored","passagePhrase":"rarely bother to follow"},{"uid":"4fd9f884-1e98-4cd2-a3a1-709213a09a4c","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Official requirements for storing medicines","passagePhrase":"official storage guidelines"},{"uid":"8d9c3773-8f21-4089-9eb1-486ab9987bef","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Improving disease-management practices","passagePhrase":"vaccines are replacing the antibiotic pellets as a treatment for the disease"},{"uid":"230cbdca-7fe6-4da3-af98-e9f27d7f18a2","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"too late to prevent antibiotics from spreading into the surrounding environment","passagePhrase":"most of the damage has already been done"}]},"reading_u2_94":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Cranberries</span></b></p><p><i><span>The story of a unique North American crop</span></i></p><p><span>Cranberries are among the few fruits native to North America to have been cultivated commercially for centuries. These small, crimson berries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"16d46f00-36e6-47ff-a227-2dbf4244cf9b\">flourish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> only under <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b53f3bc7-1193-4205-b383-2da5c662a104\">a narrow set of environmental conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, particularly in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b53f3bc7-1193-4205-b383-2da5c662a104\">sandy, acidic soil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. This type of ground drains readily while retaining enough moisture for the plants' shallow roots. Because ordinary farmland rarely provides this balance, cranberries are generally grown in low-lying areas known as bogs. These natural basins, bordered by gentle ridges, enable growers to control water levels precisely. The resulting environment is quite different from that required by most other fruit crops.</span></p><p><span>Many bogs used for cranberry farming were created thousands of years ago when retreating glaciers carved deep hollows known as kettle ponds. Over time, layers of sand and clay formed within these basins, creating a natural filtration system that helps keep pollutants out of the water. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"3f1f7ef0-aeaa-4d73-878a-9e488b870c3e\">The clay floor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> serves as a barrier, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"1f0cfac7-1c28-426b-96aa-5a5e0acfa52b\">preventing harmful substances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> from entering the pond and helping to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"1f0cfac7-1c28-426b-96aa-5a5e0acfa52b\">preserve the clean water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> needed by healthy vines. Together with deliberate control of water levels, these geological features make kettle-pond sites particularly suitable for cranberry cultivation.</span></p><p><span>Long before European settlement, Wampanoag communities used cranberries in several practical ways. The fruit could be dried and combined with other foods, allowing it to be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"dd12722a-79cf-4416-baaa-2baf18cee633\">kept for periods when fresh plants were scarce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. These methods produced compact foodstuffs that could be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"dd12722a-79cf-4416-baaa-2baf18cee633\">consumed during colder months<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. Cranberries also played a role in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"84f4d2e1-a244-42be-b2fb-c453f3e6b857\">first aid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>: crushed fruit was applied to sores and minor wounds, reflecting practical knowledge of its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"84f4d2e1-a244-42be-b2fb-c453f3e6b857\">cleansing qualities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>When <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5efc5229-3437-4b6b-be96-662997cf4c79\">European settlers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> arrived in the seventeenth century, they found cranberries growing in coastal hollows and quickly recognised their usefulness. Rather than trying to establish European varieties, they <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"9753a1a7-1caa-4b97-835e-9357f8c3daef\">adopted the native species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> already suited to local conditions. Colonists used the fruit in preserves and beverages and valued its nutritional contribution during winter voyages and periods of food shortage inland. Over time, cranberries became part of colonial cooking and later of North American holiday traditions.</span></p><p><span>In the early nineteenth century, planned cultivation expanded through local experimentation. Captain Henry Hall, a Massachusetts grower, noticed that windblown sand falling onto his cranberry beds improved both fruit quality and yield. He began spreading sand deliberately and found that it improved soil texture while reducing pest problems. Hall's manipulation of the land and surface materials represented an important step towards systematic cranberry farming.</span></p><p><span>Cranberry production follows a seasonal routine in which each operation is closely linked to weather conditions. In winter, farmers often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"0ef3aaa8-a57a-4874-b415-1569a17331a0\">flood the bogs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"995a31a6-ed6c-4b49-9ff7-e29487c5d15c\">As the water freezes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"0be95cfd-9032-4cf7-85ef-19460bb45e0c\">forms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> an insulating <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"09e35eb5-42b4-4252-8e76-8d6695487575\">layer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> that protects the vines from severe cold and drying winds. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"96b757ed-9c38-43ad-a903-63ef3b95dede\">Sand may also be spread across the frozen surface<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> so that, after thawing, it works down into the bed, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"a68e2a26-950c-4595-96e0-9ed6d0f36c96\">improving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> drainage and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"fafb698c-aed3-4b55-84cd-a6c8e2c6d3c3\">helping new shoots become established<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Growers also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f4442356-36d4-4f0b-bbcc-f75eb13331c7\">clear trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> and scrub from around the bogs, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"d9106e1d-1128-4f88-a664-f992b9d998b8\">allowing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> air <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"d9106e1d-1128-4f88-a664-f992b9d998b8\">to circulate more freely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> and reducing humidity, which helps lower the risk of disease.</span></p><p><span>In spring, the frozen cover is managed and water levels are adjusted. Growers may apply water during vulnerable periods to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"0275f442-ebf8-483b-aed2-da2a10a9df7a\">protect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"954fc31a-c5fc-4c11-9177-2b8773b570a6\">emerging shoots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"0275f442-ebf8-483b-aed2-da2a10a9df7a\">from sudden frosts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. They also carry out <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"ee9246c0-5703-4e7b-93c4-73c1b61f9d5d\">routine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> maintenance on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a5ee64a3-9519-4d02-a508-734746aa3c1f\">channels, pumps and irrigation lines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> and take measures to limit pest pressure <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"fd5b5958-12ea-4e60-a82b-3b00e404324a\">before the plants enter full growth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. By early summer, the vines are active and attention shifts to the even development of the fruit. Farmers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"0c5b26bb-a6b3-4b50-ab5b-5492792e6cbb\">inspect the beds for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> weeds that would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"0bdf4e87-1d2a-485e-8341-8db96b9a4ffe\">compete with the crop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> and remove them promptly to protect potential yields.</span></p><p><span>As autumn approaches, ripening fruit signals the start of harvest. In many operations, the bogs are flooded again so that the buoyant berries rise to the surface and can be separated from the vines more easily. Although mechanical aids and modern equipment have altered some aspects of the work, successful cranberry production continues to depend on a careful balance between soil conditions, water management and human intervention. From the practical uses developed by the Wampanoag to the innovations of later growers, cranberry cultivation remains closely tied to seasonal management of a distinctive landscape.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326159\" id=\"question-wrapper-326159\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Cranberries require a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b53f3bc7-1193-4205-b383-2da5c662a104\">specific soil type<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"16d46f00-36e6-47ff-a227-2dbf4244cf9b\">grow successfully<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326160\" id=\"question-wrapper-326160\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"3f1f7ef0-aeaa-4d73-878a-9e488b870c3e\">The material forming the bottom of kettle ponds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> helps <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"1f0cfac7-1c28-426b-96aa-5a5e0acfa52b\">prevent the water from becoming contaminated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326161\" id=\"question-wrapper-326161\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Wampanoag's use of cranberries was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"dd12722a-79cf-4416-baaa-2baf18cee633\">limited to the season in which they were gathered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326162\" id=\"question-wrapper-326162\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Wampanoag people took advantage of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"84f4d2e1-a244-42be-b2fb-c453f3e6b857\">the medicinal properties of cranberries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326163\" id=\"question-wrapper-326163\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5efc5229-3437-4b6b-be96-662997cf4c79\">Early European newcomers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"9753a1a7-1caa-4b97-835e-9357f8c3daef\">chose to plant non-native varieties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> instead of the type already growing in the region.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326164\" id=\"question-wrapper-326164\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Hall had experience cultivating several other kinds of fruit before he began working with cranberries.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326165\" id=\"question-wrapper-326165\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It took a long time for Hall's methods of cultivation to become popular among other cranberry producers.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><b><span>The seasonal management of cranberry bogs</span></b></p><p><b><span>Winter</span></b></p><ul><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"0ef3aaa8-a57a-4874-b415-1569a17331a0\">Water is deliberately added to the bogs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> so that, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"995a31a6-ed6c-4b49-9ff7-e29487c5d15c\">once frozen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"0be95cfd-9032-4cf7-85ef-19460bb45e0c\">provides<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> an (8)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"09e35eb5-42b4-4252-8e76-8d6695487575\">covering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> for the vines.</span></li><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"96b757ed-9c38-43ad-a903-63ef3b95dede\">Sand is put on frozen bogs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"a68e2a26-950c-4595-96e0-9ed6d0f36c96\">facilitate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)______ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"fafb698c-aed3-4b55-84cd-a6c8e2c6d3c3\">encourage growth afterwards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </span></li><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f4442356-36d4-4f0b-bbcc-f75eb13331c7\">Trees are removed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"d9106e1d-1128-4f88-a664-f992b9d998b8\">promote the movement of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)______.</span></li></ul><p><b><span>Spring</span></b></p><ul><li><span>(11)______ can make <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"954fc31a-c5fc-4c11-9177-2b8773b570a6\">new shoots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"0275f442-ebf8-483b-aed2-da2a10a9df7a\">less vulnerable to frost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> during cold spells.</span></li><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a5ee64a3-9519-4d02-a508-734746aa3c1f\">Water-control equipment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> receives <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"ee9246c0-5703-4e7b-93c4-73c1b61f9d5d\">regular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"fd5b5958-12ea-4e60-a82b-3b00e404324a\">before vigorous plant growth begins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></li></ul><p><b><span>Summer</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Once the vines become fully active, growers concentrate on achieving even fruit development.</span></li><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"0c5b26bb-a6b3-4b50-ab5b-5492792e6cbb\">Beds are checked for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)______ that could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"0bdf4e87-1d2a-485e-8341-8db96b9a4ffe\">reduce the resources available to the crop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></li></ul><p><b><span>Autumn</span></b></p><ul><li><span>Ripening berries indicate that harvesting can begin.</span></li><li><span>On many farms, the bogs are flooded again so that the fruit rises to the surface and can be separated from the vines more easily.</span></li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326166\" id=\"question-wrapper-326166\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INSULATING</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326167\" id=\"question-wrapper-326167\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DRAINAGE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326168\" id=\"question-wrapper-326168\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AIR</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326169\" id=\"question-wrapper-326169\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WATER</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326170\" id=\"question-wrapper-326170\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MAINTENANCE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326171\" id=\"question-wrapper-326171\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WEEDS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"16d46f00-36e6-47ff-a227-2dbf4244cf9b","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"grow successfully","passagePhrase":"flourish"},{"uid":"b53f3bc7-1193-4205-b383-2da5c662a104","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"specific soil type","passagePhrase":"a narrow set of environmental conditions ... sandy, acidic soil"},{"uid":"3f1f7ef0-aeaa-4d73-878a-9e488b870c3e","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"The material forming the bottom of kettle ponds","passagePhrase":"The clay floor"},{"uid":"1f0cfac7-1c28-426b-96aa-5a5e0acfa52b","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"prevent the water from becoming contaminated","passagePhrase":"preventing harmful substances ... preserve the clean water"},{"uid":"84f4d2e1-a244-42be-b2fb-c453f3e6b857","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"the medicinal properties of cranberries","passagePhrase":"first aid ... cleansing qualities"},{"uid":"5efc5229-3437-4b6b-be96-662997cf4c79","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Early European newcomers","passagePhrase":"European settlers"},{"uid":"0ef3aaa8-a57a-4874-b415-1569a17331a0","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Water is deliberately added to the bogs","passagePhrase":"flood the bogs"},{"uid":"995a31a6-ed6c-4b49-9ff7-e29487c5d15c","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"once frozen","passagePhrase":"As the water freezes"},{"uid":"0be95cfd-9032-4cf7-85ef-19460bb45e0c","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"provides","passagePhrase":"forms"},{"uid":"09e35eb5-42b4-4252-8e76-8d6695487575","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"covering","passagePhrase":"layer"},{"uid":"96b757ed-9c38-43ad-a903-63ef3b95dede","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Sand is put on frozen bogs","passagePhrase":"Sand may also be spread across the frozen surface"},{"uid":"a68e2a26-950c-4595-96e0-9ed6d0f36c96","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"facilitate","passagePhrase":"improving"},{"uid":"fafb698c-aed3-4b55-84cd-a6c8e2c6d3c3","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"encourage growth afterwards","passagePhrase":"helping new shoots become established"},{"uid":"f4442356-36d4-4f0b-bbcc-f75eb13331c7","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"Trees are removed","passagePhrase":"clear trees"},{"uid":"d9106e1d-1128-4f88-a664-f992b9d998b8","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"promote the movement of","passagePhrase":"allowing ... to circulate more freely"},{"uid":"0275f442-ebf8-483b-aed2-da2a10a9df7a","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"less vulnerable to frost","passagePhrase":"protect ... from sudden frosts"},{"uid":"954fc31a-c5fc-4c11-9177-2b8773b570a6","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"new shoots","passagePhrase":"emerging shoots"},{"uid":"ee9246c0-5703-4e7b-93c4-73c1b61f9d5d","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"regular","passagePhrase":"routine"},{"uid":"a5ee64a3-9519-4d02-a508-734746aa3c1f","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Water-control equipment","passagePhrase":"channels, pumps and irrigation lines"},{"uid":"fd5b5958-12ea-4e60-a82b-3b00e404324a","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"before vigorous plant growth begins","passagePhrase":"before the plants enter full growth"},{"uid":"0c5b26bb-a6b3-4b50-ab5b-5492792e6cbb","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"Beds are checked for","passagePhrase":"inspect the beds for"},{"uid":"0bdf4e87-1d2a-485e-8341-8db96b9a4ffe","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"reduce the resources available to the crop","passagePhrase":"compete with the crop"}]},"reading_u2_95":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>Australia's camouflaged creatures</span></b></p><p><i><span>Many species of animals in Australia protect themselves by using camouflage—a way of ‘hiding’ by blending into their surroundings.</span></i></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c5db5867-b039-448a-a701-881109aaa870\">Most species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"470d5a1a-e65b-4525-bbe9-31b06f2bdc23\">camouflage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c5db5867-b039-448a-a701-881109aaa870\">to some extent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. If they are convincing, they survive to pass their genes on to future generations. After generations of natural selection, animals can develop astonishingly complex camouflage techniques, manipulating shape, colour and movement. ‘The principle of camouflage is to make it economically unviable for a predator to pursue a particular species of prey,’ explains Professor Mark Elgar of the University of Melbourne. ‘Camouflage <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"86175e30-479f-4d47-9b0e-fa39172d776e\">increases the search time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and, as a consequence, the predator will simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"19957c0b-a9c6-4dc5-b316-c1bc6bb977a4\">target another species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, either because it does not see the camouflaged individual or because it finds something more obvious to pursue.’</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p><span>The easiest way for an animal to disguise itself is to become effectively invisible in its surroundings. To that end, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"720e2e4c-6771-412b-a245-923d67e26160\">stick and leaf insects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> have evolved complex camouflage to hide themselves from predators. Many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"049e52f4-c5ac-4702-bac6-4a4f36ec8503\">have the texture of sticks or dry leaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, while others <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"049e52f4-c5ac-4702-bac6-4a4f36ec8503\">imitate living foliage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, even the veins in a leaf. Some insects develop blemishes to match the spots caused by disease. A convincing appearance works only if its owner also acts the part, so during the day a creature using this type of camouflage remains motionless or sways like a dead leaf in the breeze. If disturbed, it falls to the ground and stays still. Entomologist Paul Zborowski, who has spent decades photographing inconspicuous creatures, rates the desert insects of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c5dc54ad-bb3e-4ed7-90bd-279a52a1f1a3\">Central Australia<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> as the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c5dc54ad-bb3e-4ed7-90bd-279a52a1f1a3\">most convincingly disguised creatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> he has seen. ‘It is an incredibly old habitat, so the creatures have had a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"ac8a18c4-8ad2-4b57-bfa6-f1528e98a6fe\">long time to adapt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>,’ Zborowski explains. Most of them behave like stones and remain motionless throughout the day, feeding only at night.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p><span>A tawny frogmouth sitting motionless on a stump also illustrates the importance of pairing a convincing appearance with appropriate behaviour. Professor Gisela Kaplan of the University of New England in Australia says the frogmouth's skill at camouflage involves learned behaviour. Although adopting a pose may be a reflex and can be observed during a hatchling's first week, the ability to choose a background that matches its colouration <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"524077d5-0a14-4c49-a67b-6924e1bbb7f6\">does not develop for four to six months<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. When the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3ea836a7-c4b4-4eac-9a6d-89b760dafff5\">chicks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> land, they are usually highly conspicuous, and their parents try to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"204820d9-f306-49e6-a739-804705692c54\">signal to them to move<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ff88a803-7b96-45d8-9f85-05297fd1a9d5\">safer location<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p><span>Fixed camouflage is effective only in a relatively unchanging environment, so some animals, such as the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ed7dc77e-d8f6-47f4-bd78-d77ec0cd557e\">cuttlefish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, have evolved an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c31f014f-b816-4f3a-8816-3efc8e1475e8\">adaptable disguise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. The cuttlefish can almost instantly change its colour, pattern and texture to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e0d546c4-bfd4-4694-aec3-cb031f568100\">match its surroundings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, using specialised cells and muscles. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a2ee1848-3b4f-4600-b087-413fad822da9\">On Queensland's<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> reefs, scientists have been studying another ocean dweller that changes colour, although not in order to blend into its surroundings. Dr Karen Cheney of the University of Queensland says the bluestriped fangblenny alters its colouration to mimic other species of fish, allowing it to travel with them and benefit from safety in numbers. Its most impressive <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"92e1e70e-7fe6-4460-af6e-a8aa1b291379\">impersonation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> is of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ebbbf21a-9340-462a-b41e-86f459a456cd\">the black-and-neon-blue-striped cleaner wrasse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"c0880f91-4a48-4ad3-950c-4dba5abd36f0\">eats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> parasites found on larger fish. Not only does the fangblenny benefit from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"6d74edfa-3022-4564-bbb1-53f5eb9bf22e\">the reduced predation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> associated with the wrasse's beneficial relationships with other fish, but the disguise also allows it to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"117152eb-1b83-440b-b4fb-6bae687f6e5c\">get closer to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> its prey. It darts out from the safety of the wrasse's cleaning station to nip at unsuspecting fish passing by, but does not attack those coming to be cleaned.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p><span>The most famous form of mimicry, however, is used for defence rather than attack. Batesian mimicry refers to animals that gain protection from predators by imitating a dangerous organism, often using conspicuous colours. The nineteenth-century naturalist Henry Bates <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"2247e77b-b07b-42e7-9d93-0def422363f9\">first suggested this camouflage technique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> after noticing that several Amazonian <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"4a630b09-7eaa-460c-889d-ffb5fe665e08\">butterfly species looked alike<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. The technique was later named after him. In Australian waters, the harmless harlequin snake eel has the same black-and-white bands as the highly toxic yellow-lipped sea krait, helping to deter predators. However, the success of Batesian mimicry depends on the ratio of mimics to originals. If a predator encounters too many mimics that are edible, it may simply assume that none of the animals with those markings are dangerous, explains Martyn Robinson, an educational naturalist with the Australian Museum.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p><span>An imitation of a more dangerous creature need not be exact; it only has to be convincing enough to make a potential predator hesitate. The hawk moth caterpillar has markings resembling a snake's eyes on its abdomen. When confronted, the caterpillar pulls its head in and the ‘eyes’ flash open. Whether the potential predator thinks it has seen a snake or is simply startled is unclear, but the outcome is that the caterpillar lives to see another day.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b></p><p><span>In Queensland's Tablelands, the chameleon gecko has another way of making predators hesitate. Its body is brown, but its tail is banded in black and white. Robinson explains that, if attacked, the chameleon gecko <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"89277728-3628-48b2-b80d-af4b3ba37e94\">drops its tail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, which then wriggles around on the ground. Many lizards do this, but in the case of the chameleon gecko, the tail bones actually rub against one another, causing it to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"b2254ca1-16e3-4d95-bd8c-9c415c53fb23\">squeak<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. ‘The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6693cac2-a194-4482-b00d-f5883b0197b5\">predator is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, of course, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6693cac2-a194-4482-b00d-f5883b0197b5\">thoroughly absorbed by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> this black-and-white-striped, wriggling, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"b2254ca1-16e3-4d95-bd8c-9c415c53fb23\">squeaking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> thing on the ground, and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"77fdf7f2-97f5-4de1-babc-b34e7b4f80e9\">the </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 22\" data-uid=\"54408c9e-15e9-4931-a6ca-05402c92678e 77fdf7f2-97f5-4de1-babc-b34e7b4f80e9\">gecko can sneak away</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>,’ Robinson says. It is a one-time-only trick: the regrown tail is brown, the same colour as the gecko's body. Such precise disguise and elaborate trickery illustrate the limitless possibilities of nature. But, as Robinson points out, only the most successful illusionists are here to tell the tale.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven sections, A–G.</span></p><p><span>Which section contains the following information?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326172\" id=\"question-wrapper-326172\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a species that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"204820d9-f306-49e6-a739-804705692c54\">directs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3ea836a7-c4b4-4eac-9a6d-89b760dafff5\">young<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ff88a803-7b96-45d8-9f85-05297fd1a9d5\">more concealed areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326173\" id=\"question-wrapper-326173\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an example of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"b2254ca1-16e3-4d95-bd8c-9c415c53fb23\">sound<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> being used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"77fdf7f2-97f5-4de1-babc-b34e7b4f80e9\">help an animal escape<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326174\" id=\"question-wrapper-326174\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ed7dc77e-d8f6-47f4-bd78-d77ec0cd557e\">a creature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c31f014f-b816-4f3a-8816-3efc8e1475e8\">use camouflage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e0d546c4-bfd4-4694-aec3-cb031f568100\">match a range of different backgrounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326175\" id=\"question-wrapper-326175\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c5db5867-b039-448a-a701-881109aaa870\">a general observation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> about how common <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"470d5a1a-e65b-4525-bbe9-31b06f2bdc23\">concealment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> is among animals</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326176\" id=\"question-wrapper-326176\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"720e2e4c-6771-412b-a245-923d67e26160\">examples of animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"049e52f4-c5ac-4702-bac6-4a4f36ec8503\">use camouflage to resemble plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements and the list of people below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct person, A–F.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 19–23 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of people</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Martyn Robinson</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Professor Gisela Kaplan</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Professor Mark Elgar</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Henry Bates</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Paul Zborowski</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. Dr Karen Cheney</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326177\" id=\"question-wrapper-326177\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Predators may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"19957c0b-a9c6-4dc5-b316-c1bc6bb977a4\">switch to an alternative source of food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"86175e30-479f-4d47-9b0e-fa39172d776e\">finding a particular type becomes too difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326178\" id=\"question-wrapper-326178\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>One camouflage skill <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"524077d5-0a14-4c49-a67b-6924e1bbb7f6\">develops only some time after birth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326179\" id=\"question-wrapper-326179\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The discovery of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"4a630b09-7eaa-460c-889d-ffb5fe665e08\">closely resembling butterfly species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"2247e77b-b07b-42e7-9d93-0def422363f9\">gave rise to an early theory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of survival through imitation.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326180\" id=\"question-wrapper-326180\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"54408c9e-15e9-4931-a6ca-05402c92678e\">Escape is made possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> when a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"89277728-3628-48b2-b80d-af4b3ba37e94\">shed body part<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> becomes the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"6693cac2-a194-4482-b00d-f5883b0197b5\">focus of a predator's attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326181\" id=\"question-wrapper-326181\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"ac8a18c4-8ad2-4b57-bfa6-f1528e98a6fe\">long period of adaptation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> may explain why camouflage is so <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"c5dc54ad-bb3e-4ed7-90bd-279a52a1f1a3\">effective in one region<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The bluestriped fangblenny</span></b></p><p><span>Dr Karen Cheney's research focuses on bluestriped fangblennies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a2ee1848-3b4f-4600-b087-413fad822da9\">inhabiting Queensland's<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> (24)_______. She found that the fangblenny could resemble other fish by changing its colouration. The fangblenny <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"92e1e70e-7fe6-4460-af6e-a8aa1b291379\">imitates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ebbbf21a-9340-462a-b41e-86f459a456cd\">the striped cleaner wrasse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, a fish welcomed by other species because it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"c0880f91-4a48-4ad3-950c-4dba5abd36f0\">gets rid of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> their (25)_______. By camouflaging as the cleaner wrasse, the fangblenny <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"6d74edfa-3022-4564-bbb1-53f5eb9bf22e\">lowers its own risk of attack<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"117152eb-1b83-440b-b4fb-6bae687f6e5c\">gaining easier access to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> its own (26)_______.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326182\" id=\"question-wrapper-326182\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">REEFS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326183\" id=\"question-wrapper-326183\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PARASITES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326184\" id=\"question-wrapper-326184\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PREY</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c5db5867-b039-448a-a701-881109aaa870","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"a general observation","passagePhrase":"Most species ... to some extent"},{"uid":"470d5a1a-e65b-4525-bbe9-31b06f2bdc23","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"concealment","passagePhrase":"camouflage"},{"uid":"86175e30-479f-4d47-9b0e-fa39172d776e","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"finding a particular type becomes too difficult","passagePhrase":"increases the search time"},{"uid":"19957c0b-a9c6-4dc5-b316-c1bc6bb977a4","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"switch to an alternative source of food","passagePhrase":"target another species"},{"uid":"720e2e4c-6771-412b-a245-923d67e26160","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"examples of animals","passagePhrase":"stick and leaf insects"},{"uid":"049e52f4-c5ac-4702-bac6-4a4f36ec8503","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"use camouflage to resemble plants","passagePhrase":"have the texture of sticks or dry leaves ... imitate living foliage"},{"uid":"c5dc54ad-bb3e-4ed7-90bd-279a52a1f1a3","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"effective in one region","passagePhrase":"Central Australia ... most convincingly disguised creatures"},{"uid":"ac8a18c4-8ad2-4b57-bfa6-f1528e98a6fe","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"long period of adaptation","passagePhrase":"long time to adapt"},{"uid":"524077d5-0a14-4c49-a67b-6924e1bbb7f6","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"develops only some time after birth","passagePhrase":"does not develop for four to six months"},{"uid":"3ea836a7-c4b4-4eac-9a6d-89b760dafff5","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"young","passagePhrase":"chicks"},{"uid":"204820d9-f306-49e6-a739-804705692c54","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"directs","passagePhrase":"signal to them to move"},{"uid":"ff88a803-7b96-45d8-9f85-05297fd1a9d5","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"more concealed areas","passagePhrase":"safer location"},{"uid":"ed7dc77e-d8f6-47f4-bd78-d77ec0cd557e","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"a creature","passagePhrase":"cuttlefish"},{"uid":"c31f014f-b816-4f3a-8816-3efc8e1475e8","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"use camouflage","passagePhrase":"adaptable disguise"},{"uid":"e0d546c4-bfd4-4694-aec3-cb031f568100","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"match a range of different backgrounds","passagePhrase":"match its surroundings"},{"uid":"a2ee1848-3b4f-4600-b087-413fad822da9","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"inhabiting Queensland's","passagePhrase":"On Queensland's"},{"uid":"92e1e70e-7fe6-4460-af6e-a8aa1b291379","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"imitates","passagePhrase":"impersonation"},{"uid":"ebbbf21a-9340-462a-b41e-86f459a456cd","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"the striped cleaner wrasse","passagePhrase":"the black-and-neon-blue-striped cleaner wrasse"},{"uid":"c0880f91-4a48-4ad3-950c-4dba5abd36f0","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"gets rid of","passagePhrase":"eats"},{"uid":"6d74edfa-3022-4564-bbb1-53f5eb9bf22e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"lowers its own risk of attack","passagePhrase":"the reduced predation"},{"uid":"117152eb-1b83-440b-b4fb-6bae687f6e5c","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"gaining easier access to","passagePhrase":"get closer to"},{"uid":"2247e77b-b07b-42e7-9d93-0def422363f9","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"gave rise to an early theory","passagePhrase":"first suggested this camouflage technique"},{"uid":"4a630b09-7eaa-460c-889d-ffb5fe665e08","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"closely resembling butterfly species","passagePhrase":"butterfly species looked alike"},{"uid":"89277728-3628-48b2-b80d-af4b3ba37e94","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"shed body part","passagePhrase":"drops its tail"},{"uid":"b2254ca1-16e3-4d95-bd8c-9c415c53fb23","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"sound","passagePhrase":"squeak ... squeaking"},{"uid":"6693cac2-a194-4482-b00d-f5883b0197b5","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"focus of a predator's attention","passagePhrase":"predator is ... thoroughly absorbed by"},{"uid":"77fdf7f2-97f5-4de1-babc-b34e7b4f80e9","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"help an animal escape","passagePhrase":"the"},{"uid":"54408c9e-15e9-4931-a6ca-05402c92678e 77fdf7f2-97f5-4de1-babc-b34e7b4f80e9","qNum":"15 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"gecko can sneak away"},{"uid":"54408c9e-15e9-4931-a6ca-05402c92678e","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Escape is made possible","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_96":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>The Effectiveness of Online Courses</span></b></p><p><span>As access to the internet expanded, web-based learning grew rapidly. One set of estimates suggested that approximately half of households in the United States—representing around 150 million people—had internet access, while about two million students were taking post-secondary courses delivered entirely online. Millions more at primary, secondary and post-secondary levels were participating in some form of online education. Despite this growth, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"2bf16b4b-b807-433f-898a-7a52862ace85\">questions remain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> about the effectiveness of online courses, particularly in relation to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"aaa2511f-cd89-41c3-ac20-a43bdf92c7c7\">individual students' needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, perceptions and learning outcomes.</span></p><p><span>Two central features of learning in a conventional classroom are the social and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"4ec44174-e7bc-4576-8cb9-398c51d37e1f\">communicative interactions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> between students and teachers and among students themselves. Asking a question, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"4ec44174-e7bc-4576-8cb9-398c51d37e1f\">sharing an opinion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> with a fellow student, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"4ec44174-e7bc-4576-8cb9-398c51d37e1f\">disagreeing with a point of view<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in a reading assignment are all fundamental learning activities. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"1fbbb0c9-d607-4e9a-8571-cea6d90a2551\">web-based education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"3ce962ee-dff8-494a-95e2-54cb28689e08\">both students and teachers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> may need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"77c53397-ba55-440f-8155-8c0c3edd160c\">adapt their behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5d2c1fd5-8f93-4fe4-a2d4-ed3cc5fd4c80\">such interactions are to occur successfully<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Many online courses therefore provide electronic bulletin boards or discussion forums through which students can communicate with instructors and with one another.</span></p><p><span>Although most studies have found a relationship between interaction and satisfaction in web-based courses, some researchers caution that interaction is not automatically beneficial. Ruberg, Taylor and Moore, for example, argue that students must adjust to the nonlinear nature of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"e7c006d9-1e6f-48a1-9369-88a87da54c06\">online learning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. Unlike a conventional discussion that may concentrate on a single topic at a time, an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"e7c006d9-1e6f-48a1-9369-88a87da54c06\">online session<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> can contain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"2ef380f1-95f1-47cd-8215-6e35b31936c8\">several discussion threads developing simultaneously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. Students may respond not only to the teacher but also to different classmates, depending on their interests and points of view.</span></p><p><span>Sproull and Kiesler warn that inaccurate information may continue to circulate in online discussions because an instructor <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d00a548d-2f77-40e4-bed9-16a9ab9f807d\">cannot always correct or clarify a comment immediately<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Students therefore need sufficient experience and knowledge to distinguish reliable contributions from misinformation. The sheer volume of interaction can create a further difficulty: information overload. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"3bc3beb4-27c1-490b-908a-a51e272ab405\">Online comments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> also tend to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"118b62d0-5be1-41e3-ab1c-3c8a5f39bf45\">longer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> than those made in face-to-face discussions. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"4f34584e-d33c-4692-a19b-235a79747c1d\">Faced with large quantities of material from many different sources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, students must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"6c824672-00f0-4f9f-893c-0b89da146686\">pay close attention both to who is contributing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> and to what is being said. As the economist Herbert Simon observed, “a wealth of information creates a poverty of attention.”</span></p><p><span>Research into interaction has also focused on the concept of presence—the sense of being in a particular place and of belonging to a group. It is often assumed that students attending a face-to-face course experience a stronger sense of belonging than those studying online. A student who is physically present can listen to others, raise a hand to comment or ask a question, and develop relationships during breaks and other informal moments. Physical attendance, however, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"561ea1f3-26e1-4103-ac2d-5b6f44ecbe6b\">does not guarantee<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> such a feeling: some students may still <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"757cf5e8-135a-4aa1-9198-39c453a3e905\">experience alienation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> in a conventional classroom.</span></p><p><span>The concept of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"63d095a6-546f-4c5c-aaf1-cbfc03a6c1af\">presence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> has therefore been redefined <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"63d095a6-546f-4c5c-aaf1-cbfc03a6c1af\">in relation to online learning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. In its simplest form, it refers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"f3dcedf0-f46d-4fa0-8c89-74dd96a43140\">a student's sense of being enrolled in and belonging to a course<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, together with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"f3dcedf0-f46d-4fa0-8c89-74dd96a43140\">the ability to interact with others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> despite the absence of physical contact. The concept has since <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0e91f251-f582-4dcf-aef3-b24002836df6\">broadened to include forms such as telepresence, cognitive presence, social presence and teaching presence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Closely related is the idea of community, which refers to groups such as the students taking a particular course. In online education, this has led to terms such as communities of inquiry, communities of learners and knowledge-building communities.</span></p><p><span>As definitions of presence have expanded, researchers have increasingly distinguished presence from interaction. The two concepts are related, but they are not identical. Interaction may provide evidence of presence, yet a student can participate actively in online exchanges without necessarily feeling that he or she belongs to the class or group.</span></p><p><span>Professor Anthony Picciano investigated these issues using questionnaires to examine students' attitudes towards interaction and learning in online courses. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"46161cbc-0d36-4613-bb04-a20f00ddda62\">His study went beyond<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"20c4db63-3cc8-4411-9610-59af3db199bd\">participants' perceptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> by also measuring social presence, participation in course activities and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"5d837907-fdf3-4e97-8ec7-384f8b21685f\">actual academic performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Although previous research generally supports a strong relationship between perceived interaction and perceived learning, Picciano's results showed that the relationship between actual interaction and performance is mixed.</span></p><p><span>Interaction remains an important component of many online courses. Nevertheless, exactly how it affects <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"62e1d339-aec9-4128-b678-359f47480343\">learning outcomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>—and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"dd4e7c02-e3c3-4a62-abc3-920dc66754dc\">how closely the two are related<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>—remains uncertain and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"435a2589-0c56-48c4-b93f-55826ab30628\">requires further investigation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326185\" id=\"question-wrapper-326185\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which activity is described as fundamental to learning in a conventional classroom?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. evaluating whether contributions are reliable</li> <li>B. coping with a large quantity of written material</li> <li>C. keeping track of who is contributing information</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"4ec44174-e7bc-4576-8cb9-398c51d37e1f\">exchanging views with other people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326186\" id=\"question-wrapper-326186\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to Ruberg, Taylor and Moore, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"e7c006d9-1e6f-48a1-9369-88a87da54c06\">online students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> need to adapt to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. think about topics in a fixed sequence</li> <li>B. investigate every point of view presented</li> <li>C. follow <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"2ef380f1-95f1-47cd-8215-6e35b31936c8\">more than one discussion at a time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></li> <li>D. restrict their responses to other students</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326187\" id=\"question-wrapper-326187\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What problem did Sproull and Kiesler identify with online discussions?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d00a548d-2f77-40e4-bed9-16a9ab9f807d\">There is a delay in giving feedback<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to students</li> <li>B. Teachers have difficulty monitoring the length of comments</li> <li>C. Students lose the chance to talk to each other in person</li> <li>D. Students concentrate less than they would in a classroom</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326188\" id=\"question-wrapper-326188\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer refers to the concept of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"63d095a6-546f-4c5c-aaf1-cbfc03a6c1af\">online presence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> as</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. being physically in the same room as one's classmates</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"f3dcedf0-f46d-4fa0-8c89-74dd96a43140\">a sense of connection with fellow learners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></li> <li>C. contributing regularly to class discussions</li> <li>D. having frequent contact with the instructor</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326189\" id=\"question-wrapper-326189\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"46161cbc-0d36-4613-bb04-a20f00ddda62\">distinguished Picciano's study from much previous research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It included <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"5d837907-fdf3-4e97-8ec7-384f8b21685f\">actual results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> as well as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"20c4db63-3cc8-4411-9610-59af3db199bd\">students' perceptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></li> <li>B. It relied mainly on students' views of their own learning</li> <li>C. It treated social presence as the main indicator of success</li> <li>D. It measured participation instead of academic performance</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>YES - if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO - if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN - if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326190\" id=\"question-wrapper-326190\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The suitability of online study for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"aaa2511f-cd89-41c3-ac20-a43bdf92c7c7\">learners with different individual requirements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"2bf16b4b-b807-433f-898a-7a52862ace85\">has not yet been fully resolved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326191\" id=\"question-wrapper-326191\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some researchers advise students to limit how closely they get to know their online classmates.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326192\" id=\"question-wrapper-326192\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Physical attendance alone is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"561ea1f3-26e1-4103-ac2d-5b6f44ecbe6b\">sufficient to ensure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> a student <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"757cf5e8-135a-4aa1-9198-39c453a3e905\">develops a sense of belonging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> to the class.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326193\" id=\"question-wrapper-326193\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The concept of presence in online education has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0e91f251-f582-4dcf-aef3-b24002836df6\">developed beyond a single defined form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326194\" id=\"question-wrapper-326194\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The shared idea of a learning community existed before the rise of online education. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-G, below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. can by itself create a strong sense of belonging.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. remains uncertain and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"435a2589-0c56-48c4-b93f-55826ab30628\">requires more study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. becomes particularly important when students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"4f34584e-d33c-4692-a19b-235a79747c1d\">receive input from many contributors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. may require <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"3ce962ee-dff8-494a-95e2-54cb28689e08\">teachers and learners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"77c53397-ba55-440f-8155-8c0c3edd160c\">change how they behave<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. provides a dependable indication of academic performance.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. are generally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"118b62d0-5be1-41e3-ab1c-3c8a5f39bf45\">more extended<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> than equivalent face-to-face comments.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. is harder to maintain when several discussion threads develop at once.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326195\" id=\"question-wrapper-326195\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5d2c1fd5-8f93-4fe4-a2d4-ed3cc5fd4c80\">Effective communication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"1fbbb0c9-d607-4e9a-8571-cea6d90a2551\">in online learning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326196\" id=\"question-wrapper-326196\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"6c824672-00f0-4f9f-893c-0b89da146686\">Keeping track of who produced each online comment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326197\" id=\"question-wrapper-326197\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"3bc3beb4-27c1-490b-908a-a51e272ab405\">Online discussion contributions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326198\" id=\"question-wrapper-326198\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"dd4e7c02-e3c3-4a62-abc3-920dc66754dc\">The relationship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> between interaction and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"62e1d339-aec9-4128-b678-359f47480343\">learning achievement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"2bf16b4b-b807-433f-898a-7a52862ace85","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"has not yet been fully resolved","passagePhrase":"questions remain"},{"uid":"aaa2511f-cd89-41c3-ac20-a43bdf92c7c7","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"learners with different individual requirements","passagePhrase":"individual students' needs"},{"uid":"4ec44174-e7bc-4576-8cb9-398c51d37e1f","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"exchanging views with other people","passagePhrase":"communicative interactions ... sharing an opinion ... disagreeing with a point of view"},{"uid":"1fbbb0c9-d607-4e9a-8571-cea6d90a2551","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"in online learning","passagePhrase":"web-based education"},{"uid":"3ce962ee-dff8-494a-95e2-54cb28689e08","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"teachers and learners","passagePhrase":"both students and teachers"},{"uid":"77c53397-ba55-440f-8155-8c0c3edd160c","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"change how they behave","passagePhrase":"adapt their behaviour"},{"uid":"5d2c1fd5-8f93-4fe4-a2d4-ed3cc5fd4c80","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"Effective communication","passagePhrase":"such interactions are to occur successfully"},{"uid":"e7c006d9-1e6f-48a1-9369-88a87da54c06","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"online students","passagePhrase":"online learning ... online session"},{"uid":"2ef380f1-95f1-47cd-8215-6e35b31936c8","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"more than one discussion at a time","passagePhrase":"several discussion threads developing simultaneously"},{"uid":"d00a548d-2f77-40e4-bed9-16a9ab9f807d","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"There is a delay in giving feedback","passagePhrase":"cannot always correct or clarify a comment immediately"},{"uid":"3bc3beb4-27c1-490b-908a-a51e272ab405","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Online discussion contributions","passagePhrase":"Online comments"},{"uid":"118b62d0-5be1-41e3-ab1c-3c8a5f39bf45","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"more extended","passagePhrase":"longer"},{"uid":"4f34584e-d33c-4692-a19b-235a79747c1d","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"receive input from many contributors","passagePhrase":"Faced with large quantities of material from many different sources"},{"uid":"6c824672-00f0-4f9f-893c-0b89da146686","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"Keeping track of who produced each online comment","passagePhrase":"pay close attention both to who is contributing"},{"uid":"63d095a6-546f-4c5c-aaf1-cbfc03a6c1af","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"online presence","passagePhrase":"presence ... in relation to online learning"},{"uid":"f3dcedf0-f46d-4fa0-8c89-74dd96a43140","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"a sense of connection with fellow learners","passagePhrase":"a student's sense of being enrolled in and belonging to a course ... the ability to interact with others"},{"uid":"0e91f251-f582-4dcf-aef3-b24002836df6","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"developed beyond a single defined form","passagePhrase":"broadened to include forms such as telepresence, cognitive presence, social presence and teaching presence"},{"uid":"46161cbc-0d36-4613-bb04-a20f00ddda62","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"distinguished Picciano's study from much previous research","passagePhrase":"His study went beyond"},{"uid":"20c4db63-3cc8-4411-9610-59af3db199bd","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"students' perceptions","passagePhrase":"participants' perceptions"},{"uid":"5d837907-fdf3-4e97-8ec7-384f8b21685f","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"actual results","passagePhrase":"actual academic performance"},{"uid":"62e1d339-aec9-4128-b678-359f47480343","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"learning achievement","passagePhrase":"learning outcomes"},{"uid":"dd4e7c02-e3c3-4a62-abc3-920dc66754dc","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"The relationship","passagePhrase":"how closely the two are related"},{"uid":"435a2589-0c56-48c4-b93f-55826ab30628","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"requires more study","passagePhrase":"requires further investigation"}]},"reading_u2_97":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Health in the Wild</span></b></p><p><i><span>Many animals seem able to treat their illnesses themselves. Humans may have a thing or two to learn from them.</span></i></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4ea634d1-5260-40be-b9a0-b995662302d1\">For the past decade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, Dr Cindy Engel, a lecturer in Environmental Sciences at Britain's Open University, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"cc1a13e1-4319-4dd9-9249-c6868f4a685a\">has been collating examples<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"6daed99e-c90e-40ae-805c-98ccda94c0db\">self-medicating behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in wild animals. In a talk on the subject, she explained that the idea that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"73fef3ef-2e46-4dbb-b824-1478332b1a54\">animals can treat themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f2799bdd-81dd-4f37-aac9-90593d5f6ea9\">had generally been regarded with some scepticism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> by other animal behaviourists. However, a growing number of researchers came to believe that wild animals can and do deal with their own medical needs.</span></p><p><span>Dr William Karesh of the Wildlife Conservation Society in New York, for example, studied the health of a wide range of wild animals, including anaconda snakes, macaws, penguins, impala and buffalo. The animals were mostly in good physical condition, which is not surprising since weak individuals quickly die in the wild. However, blood tests showed that many had encountered unpleasant viral and bacterial diseases in the past, including diseases that are often fatal in captive animals even when treated by vets. Moreover, when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"113ac413-6a93-46c5-9b55-715b79aa2d57\">healthy wild animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> are brought into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"a9162c71-3ea2-4e97-8790-da7143e556e9\">captivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"89e6cade-20cf-4c32-80f7-af14e7c8dc41\">health often deteriorates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> unless great care is taken over their living conditions. Such observations suggest that wild animals can do something to keep themselves healthy that captive animals cannot.</span></p><p><span>One example of self-medication was discovered in 1987. Dr Michael Huffman and Mohamedi Seifu, working in the Mahale Mountains National Park in Tanzania, noticed that local chimpanzees <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"15890f3f-b460-4df4-b674-15673d93c672\">suffering from intestinal worms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5386c51c-4580-4d21-a85a-c22f6901b261\">dose themselves with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> the pith—the white substance between the skin and the flesh—of a plant called Vernonia. This plant produces poisonous <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"d2f82a7b-f6c2-45a3-967f-3df78d39db91\">chemicals called<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> terpenes. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"5ada2b8e-1462-4f57-8fb0-6820b1abdf19\">Its pith contains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> a concentration strong enough to kill gut parasites but not strong enough to kill chimpanzees—or humans, for that matter. Local people use the pith for the same purpose.</span></p><p><span>Since the Vernonia-eating chimpanzees were discovered, further evidence has suggested that animals often consume substances for medical rather than nutritional reasons. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"466a6b83-eff6-409a-a60d-fcbe9e8a8c8f\">Many species, for example, eat soil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"466a6b83-eff6-409a-a60d-fcbe9e8a8c8f\">a behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"a1313625-e030-4216-8cef-80307287cf23\">known as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> geophagy. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"8d2723ae-2e7a-4948-a7aa-3c7819678d92\">An earlier explanation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> was that soil <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"82fb7907-0ae4-4811-b1ef-860b4c83000e\">supplied minerals such as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> salt. However, geophagy also occurs in areas where the soil is not a useful source of minerals, and in places where minerals can be obtained more easily from plants known to be rich in them. This suggests that animals gain some other benefit from eating soil.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"f1c3566b-c41a-487d-8d43-170222681659\">Researchers therefore proposed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> that soil—and particularly the clay it contains—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"1edab723-8183-481e-ac4e-c258cef8fd3e\">may help to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> detoxify the defensive poisons produced by some plants to prevent themselves from being eaten. Evidence for the detoxifying effect of clay came in 1999 from an experiment carried out on macaws by Dr James Gilardi and his colleagues at the University of California, Davis. Macaws eat seeds containing alkaloids, a group of chemicals that includes some highly toxic substances, such as strychnine. In the wild, the birds are frequently seen perched on eroding riverbanks eating clay. Dr Gilardi fed one group of macaws a mixture of harmless alkaloid and clay, and a second group only the alkaloid. Several hours later, the birds that had eaten the clay <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"b99570f8-122c-45a5-baad-4b16aa98ca87\">had 60% less<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> alkaloid <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"f52dd261-ee50-49c1-9824-7dd9e7059c01\">in their bloodstreams<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> than those that had not, supporting the hypothesis that clay has a detoxifying effect.</span></p><p><span>A third example of animal self-medication involves the use of mechanical scouring to remove gut parasites. In 1972, Dr Richard Wrangham, a researcher at the Gombe Stream Reserve in Tanzania, noticed chimpanzees eating the leaves of a tree called Aspilia. The chimpanzees selected the leaves carefully by testing them in their mouths. After choosing a leaf, a chimpanzee would fold it into a fan and swallow it. Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"80ccad7c-1089-41ad-908e-b47219a7c1b8\">were seen wrinkling their noses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> as they swallowed the leaves, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"01b98828-2336-4ad3-bf91-62db23100be8\">suggesting that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> the experience was unpleasant. Later, undigested leaves were found on the forest floor.</span></p><p><span>Dr Wrangham correctly guessed that the leaves served a medicinal purpose—one of the earliest interpretations of a behaviour pattern now known as self-medication. However, his explanation of the mechanism was wrong. He and other researchers assumed that Aspilia released a drug, which led to more than two decades of phytochemical research aimed at identifying the chemical the chimpanzees were seeking. By the 1990s, however, chimpanzees across Africa had been observed swallowing leaves from 19 different species that appeared to have few suitable chemicals in common. The drug hypothesis therefore became increasingly doubtful.</span></p><p><span>Dr Huffman eventually identified the mechanism by examining what passed through the chimpanzees rather than concentrating only on what they swallowed. He found that the expelled leaves were covered with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8928692d-a666-4fa1-869c-c0f630f62fc2\">intestinal worms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. The feature common to all 19 species of leaves was a surface covered in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"0285e9c4-b391-4180-abc8-d2df9eee76de\">microscopic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> hooks. These hooks <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"53ba5156-7abc-4648-b170-c5551a8b74ac\">caught<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> the worms and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"53ba5156-7abc-4648-b170-c5551a8b74ac\">dragged them from their position in the gut<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Dr Engel has also considered how knowledge of animal self-medication might be used to improve the health of livestock. Humans may have something to learn as well—and may already have done so. Geophagy, for example, is common in many parts of the world. Medical stalls in African markets <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"f17524ab-076c-4249-b3b0-7cabc58dc0be\">frequently sell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> tablets made from different types of clay <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"09ea539b-ea36-451e-b55a-230f6e92010d\">for different medical conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Africans brought to the Americas as slaves continued this tradition, although their owners often treated the practice with contempt. Yet, as Dr Engel points out, Rwandan mountain gorillas eat a type of clay rather similar to kaolinite, the main ingredient of many over-the-counter medicines sold in the West for digestive complaints. Eating soil, therefore, can sometimes have genuine medical benefits.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326199\" id=\"question-wrapper-326199\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Dr Engel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"cc1a13e1-4319-4dd9-9249-c6868f4a685a\">has been collecting evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> that animals can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"6daed99e-c90e-40ae-805c-98ccda94c0db\">treat their own illnesses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4ea634d1-5260-40be-b9a0-b995662302d1\">for ten years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326200\" id=\"question-wrapper-326200\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Animal behaviourists <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f2799bdd-81dd-4f37-aac9-90593d5f6ea9\">have always accepted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the idea that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"73fef3ef-2e46-4dbb-b824-1478332b1a54\">animals know how to heal themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326201\" id=\"question-wrapper-326201\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A medical team assisted Dr Karesh during his research.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326202\" id=\"question-wrapper-326202\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"a9162c71-3ea2-4e97-8790-da7143e556e9\">Confinement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"89e6cade-20cf-4c32-80f7-af14e7c8dc41\">can damage the health<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"113ac413-6a93-46c5-9b55-715b79aa2d57\">animals that were fit in their natural habitat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the table below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>Researchers</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>Subjects</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5386c51c-4580-4d21-a85a-c22f6901b261\">Food used as self-treatment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>Findings</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Michael Huffman &amp; Mohamedi Seifu, 1987</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Chimpanzees <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"15890f3f-b460-4df4-b674-15673d93c672\">infected with intestinal worms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>The (5)______ of </span><i><span>Vernonia</span></i> </p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"d2f82a7b-f6c2-45a3-967f-3df78d39db91\">Compounds known as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (6)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"5ada2b8e-1462-4f57-8fb0-6820b1abdf19\">are found in this part of the plant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>James Gilardi, 1999</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Macaws that consume poison-bearing seeds</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Clay</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Clay <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"b99570f8-122c-45a5-baad-4b16aa98ca87\">reduces the level of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> (7)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"f52dd261-ee50-49c1-9824-7dd9e7059c01\">in the blood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Richard Wrangham</span></p><p><span>1972</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Chimpanzees with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8928692d-a666-4fa1-869c-c0f630f62fc2\">gut parasites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><i><span>Aspilia</span></i><span> leaves</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>The leaves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"01b98828-2336-4ad3-bf91-62db23100be8\">seemed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)______ for the chimpanzees to swallow, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"80ccad7c-1089-41ad-908e-b47219a7c1b8\">judging from their facial expressions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>It was proposed that the leaves contain some medicinal chemical.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Michael Huffman</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Chimpanzees across Africa</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Leaves from 19 plant species </span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>The gut parasites <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"53ba5156-7abc-4648-b170-c5551a8b74ac\">were removed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> by the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"0285e9c4-b391-4180-abc8-d2df9eee76de\">tiny<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)______ on the leaves.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326203\" id=\"question-wrapper-326203\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PITH</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326204\" id=\"question-wrapper-326204\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TERPENES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326205\" id=\"question-wrapper-326205\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ALKALOID(S)</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326206\" id=\"question-wrapper-326206\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">UNPLEASANT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326207\" id=\"question-wrapper-326207\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HOOKS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><b><span>Soil as Medication</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"a1313625-e030-4216-8cef-80307287cf23\">Scientists use the term<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)______ for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"466a6b83-eff6-409a-a60d-fcbe9e8a8c8f\">the widespread practice of eating soil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"8d2723ae-2e7a-4948-a7aa-3c7819678d92\">Initially, people believed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> that animals ate soil to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"82fb7907-0ae4-4811-b1ef-860b4c83000e\">obtain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"82fb7907-0ae4-4811-b1ef-860b4c83000e\">and other minerals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. However, researchers found that soil was not always a rich source of minerals and that, in some areas, plants provided them more easily.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"f1c3566b-c41a-487d-8d43-170222681659\">One theory put forward<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> is that the clay found in soil <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"1edab723-8183-481e-ac4e-c258cef8fd3e\">is able to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12)______ poisons. The possible medical value of clay is also reflected in human practices: in African markets, clay is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"f17524ab-076c-4249-b3b0-7cabc58dc0be\">widely sold<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in the form of (13)______ as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"09ea539b-ea36-451e-b55a-230f6e92010d\">treatment for a range of illnesses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326208\" id=\"question-wrapper-326208\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GEOPHAGY</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326209\" id=\"question-wrapper-326209\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SALT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326210\" id=\"question-wrapper-326210\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DETOXIFY</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326211\" id=\"question-wrapper-326211\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TABLETS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"4ea634d1-5260-40be-b9a0-b995662302d1","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"for ten years","passagePhrase":"For the past decade"},{"uid":"cc1a13e1-4319-4dd9-9249-c6868f4a685a","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"has been collecting evidence","passagePhrase":"has been collating examples"},{"uid":"6daed99e-c90e-40ae-805c-98ccda94c0db","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"treat their own illnesses","passagePhrase":"self-medicating behaviour"},{"uid":"73fef3ef-2e46-4dbb-b824-1478332b1a54","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"animals know how to heal themselves","passagePhrase":"animals can treat themselves"},{"uid":"113ac413-6a93-46c5-9b55-715b79aa2d57","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"animals that were fit in their natural habitat","passagePhrase":"healthy wild animals"},{"uid":"a9162c71-3ea2-4e97-8790-da7143e556e9","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Confinement","passagePhrase":"captivity"},{"uid":"89e6cade-20cf-4c32-80f7-af14e7c8dc41","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"can damage the health","passagePhrase":"health often deteriorates"},{"uid":"15890f3f-b460-4df4-b674-15673d93c672","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"infected with intestinal worms","passagePhrase":"suffering from intestinal worms"},{"uid":"5386c51c-4580-4d21-a85a-c22f6901b261","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Food used as self-treatment","passagePhrase":"dose themselves with"},{"uid":"d2f82a7b-f6c2-45a3-967f-3df78d39db91","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Compounds known as","passagePhrase":"chemicals called"},{"uid":"5ada2b8e-1462-4f57-8fb0-6820b1abdf19","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"are found in this part of the plant","passagePhrase":"Its pith contains"},{"uid":"466a6b83-eff6-409a-a60d-fcbe9e8a8c8f","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the widespread practice of eating soil","passagePhrase":"Many species, for example, eat soil ... a behaviour"},{"uid":"a1313625-e030-4216-8cef-80307287cf23","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"Scientists use the term","passagePhrase":"known as"},{"uid":"8d2723ae-2e7a-4948-a7aa-3c7819678d92","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Initially, people believed","passagePhrase":"An earlier explanation"},{"uid":"82fb7907-0ae4-4811-b1ef-860b4c83000e","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"obtain ... and other minerals","passagePhrase":"supplied minerals such as"},{"uid":"f1c3566b-c41a-487d-8d43-170222681659","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"One theory put forward","passagePhrase":"Researchers therefore proposed"},{"uid":"1edab723-8183-481e-ac4e-c258cef8fd3e","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"is able to","passagePhrase":"may help to"},{"uid":"b99570f8-122c-45a5-baad-4b16aa98ca87","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"reduces the level of","passagePhrase":"had 60% less"},{"uid":"f52dd261-ee50-49c1-9824-7dd9e7059c01","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"in the blood","passagePhrase":"in their bloodstreams"},{"uid":"80ccad7c-1089-41ad-908e-b47219a7c1b8","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"judging from their facial expressions","passagePhrase":"were seen wrinkling their noses"},{"uid":"01b98828-2336-4ad3-bf91-62db23100be8","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"seemed","passagePhrase":"suggesting that"},{"uid":"8928692d-a666-4fa1-869c-c0f630f62fc2","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"gut parasites","passagePhrase":"intestinal worms"},{"uid":"0285e9c4-b391-4180-abc8-d2df9eee76de","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"tiny","passagePhrase":"microscopic"},{"uid":"53ba5156-7abc-4648-b170-c5551a8b74ac","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"were removed","passagePhrase":"caught ... dragged them from their position in the gut"},{"uid":"f17524ab-076c-4249-b3b0-7cabc58dc0be","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"widely sold","passagePhrase":"frequently sell"},{"uid":"09ea539b-ea36-451e-b55a-230f6e92010d","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"treatment for a range of illnesses","passagePhrase":"for different medical conditions"}]},"reading_u2_98":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>Babies Cry in Their Mother Tongue</span></b></p><p><i><span>A newborn baby's cry may sound much the same to sleep-deprived parents around the world, but scientists say that comparisons of babies only a few days old reveal similarities between their cries and the language spoken by their parents. The likely explanation lies in the different intonation patterns of their mother tongues, which babies begin to perceive before birth and later reproduce.</span></i></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p><span>It is already known that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"3ca5be7f-d808-4a60-86bb-820c0f1428a9\">human </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 23\" data-uid=\"3ca5be7f-d808-4a60-86bb-820c0f1428a9 78e4503b-fd88-46e1-a1de-00138f978dd0\">foetuses</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> become attentive listeners during the final trimester of pregnancy. “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"2079b567-bbe0-4949-92eb-ca8e8d54469f\">The mother's voice in particular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a390c01d-242f-4257-9530-975aedeb99ea\">is sensed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"2de11b75-7092-4184-a16a-96c65ec857fc\">early on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>,” explains Professor Amelia Finlayson of the Institute for Human Cognitive and Brain Sciences in Leipzig. “Human foetuses <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5726789e-3120-4acc-951e-834bd83cfb00\">perceive information filtered at around 400 hertz<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, but they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5726789e-3120-4acc-951e-834bd83cfb00\">cannot hear the actual words<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"fa29c12d-1bee-4de1-aa0d-e32d16fed121\">It is a bit like holding your head under water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> while someone is talking beside the bath.”</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"2bdf9b7a-f28f-47fd-a9d1-8702b011456a\">Finlayson's research suggests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5d3205c6-4197-4071-bcb9-36721407077f\">newborn babies probably cannot distinguish between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> accents such as Welsh and Northern Scottish, or between Low German and Upper Bavarian. They can, however, recognise major differences in the intonation patterns of their respective mother tongues. The Leipzig researchers had demonstrated this in an earlier experiment using physiological <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"eb0e1e9e-ddb0-4593-a322-ce6bace32d64\">measurements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> from babies aged three to four months. The babies wore hoods <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"eb0e1e9e-ddb0-4593-a322-ce6bace32d64\">fitted with electrodes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9162c31b-f156-4d75-a8a6-68b264c66239\">recordings of different intonation patterns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> were played to them. Their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9162c31b-f156-4d75-a8a6-68b264c66239\">brainwaves responded to the differences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> even when they were asleep.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p><span>Dr Katya Williams of the University of Würzburg was among the first to suggest, in her PhD thesis, that babies' crying might represent a stage in linguistic development. “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"98d71d31-cabd-49f7-abae-ae9a4f0a3322\">It used to be thought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> that a baby's cry was simply <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20 25\" data-uid=\"778eacbd-bedc-49fc-ab46-6b72afe29fc5 cb72506e-5dba-4f1b-b3bb-0b319259839c\">an alarm signal</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"cb72506e-5dba-4f1b-b3bb-0b319259839c\"> to call its mother</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>,” Williams explains. “This assumption was challenged when we noticed that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"79e8b1d9-a4d6-45c1-89de-9089febb9832\">cries are not the same<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"2031f893-cbe8-49e4-8ee6-dce08d782b77\">from week to week<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. What biological purpose would that serve? If <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"778eacbd-bedc-49fc-ab46-6b72afe29fc5\">a fire siren<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"010d30ec-1f9b-4dff-b016-68f69bfa2248\">sounded different every day<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, we might <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"010d30ec-1f9b-4dff-b016-68f69bfa2248\">eventually fail to recognise it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.”</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p><span>This raised the question of whether babies' cries already displayed the intonation patterns of their different mother tongues. To investigate this, the Leipzig brain researchers and the University of Würzburg team collaborated with colleagues at the Laboratory of Cognitive Sciences and Linguistics at the École Normale Supérieure in Paris. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a1fb6ded-dfa3-43bc-bede-da14ddd31ed3\">German and French babies were selected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3b341f4c-3737-44ce-a5c9-325d441c181f\">because<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> the intonation patterns of these two languages differ particularly clearly. For example, the German word </span><i><span>Papa</span></i><span> is stressed on the first syllable, whereas in French the stress falls on the second.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p><span>The three research groups compared recordings from 60 healthy newborns between two and five days old: 30 from French-speaking families and 30 from German-speaking families. Whenever the babies were hungry, thirsty or simply wanted their mothers and began to cry, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d3d87552-d7c9-4e08-be26-35a472147179\">the researchers recorded them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d3d87552-d7c9-4e08-be26-35a472147179\">More than 20 hours of recordings were subsequently entered into a computer for analysis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p><span>The striking result, published in the journal </span><i><span>Current Biology</span></i><span>, was that only a few days after birth, babies were already using acoustic information perceived in the uterus to adapt their vocal production to their mother tongue. The cries of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"af64b86f-9c68-46fd-916b-1d4697d5404d\">the German babies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> generally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"6509b7d7-045f-416b-80a9-e45b61bc318d\">began loudly and at a high pitch before following a downward curve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, whereas <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"af64b86f-9c68-46fd-916b-1d4697d5404d\">the French babies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> more often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"6509b7d7-045f-416b-80a9-e45b61bc318d\">produced a rising melodic contour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. In other words, the babies reproduced characteristic intonation patterns of the languages to which they had been exposed. The researchers argued that these cries represented attempts to communicate specifically with their mothers. “Newborns <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"804e1c99-d78a-4d2c-b606-94f1227b77bb\">are </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4a673e78-2932-4d56-ac38-a0cce20d062e\">probably<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"804e1c99-d78a-4d2c-b606-94f1227b77bb\"> highly motivated to imitate their mother's behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4a673e78-2932-4d56-ac38-a0cce20d062e\">in order to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> attract her and foster bonding and therefore physical nourishment,” they wrote.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b></p><p><span>The findings also support the hypothesis that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f1c8ef19-8716-4454-9203-5cdff6f9bde4\">linguistic development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> does not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f1c8ef19-8716-4454-9203-5cdff6f9bde4\">begin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"08222d32-2ba8-4f28-b8d9-d3c533578449\">at around nine or ten months<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"619548f4-0461-4940-ac96-e39a372d7a20\">when babies start producing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> language-like babbling such as “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"1b7dc1f7-abe1-43c1-9bdd-d0d78df890bd\">mam-mam-mam” or “ba-ba-ba<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>”, but with the very first sounds they produce. “We are born to learn language. And that starts right away,” says Williams. Williams's colleague, Walter Meade, found that this early sensitivity to the melodic features of language helps infants subsequently learn their mother tongue. “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"63ecba0c-f68d-40c5-b4ca-562e02b1c47d\">The melodic patterns practised in crying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0a3d0255-981f-4061-add4-9447194d8a36\">are building blocks for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"07f0e950-6b5c-42b6-be2d-7a1191ff9570\">later sound production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, from gurgling and babbling through to the first words and sentences,” he explains.</span></p><p><b><span>H</span></b></p><p><span>The results also highlighted a difference between human infants and other primates. According to Williams, the “crying melody” of baby chimpanzees is closely associated with the build-up and release of pressure in the lungs rather than being generated by a mental process. “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"0c609b5e-c102-4857-b6af-5ca88461128d\">In comparison with the sounds of other primates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, the cries of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"758b1816-25f2-41e0-a301-0ef024c3350c\">a newborn human baby<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> display <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"fcb82ae0-d40a-4836-9cd5-e44ba999e686\">a remarkable repertoire of melodic and rhythmic variations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>,” she adds. “Our babies are expert vocalists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"0c609b5e-c102-4857-b6af-5ca88461128d\">compared with other animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. Perhaps that offers some small consolation to exhausted parents.”</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A–H.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326212\" id=\"question-wrapper-326212\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>details of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d3d87552-d7c9-4e08-be26-35a472147179\">the method used to capture and examine infants' crying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326213\" id=\"question-wrapper-326213\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3b341f4c-3737-44ce-a5c9-325d441c181f\">rationale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a1fb6ded-dfa3-43bc-bede-da14ddd31ed3\">choosing the participants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of an experiment</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326214\" id=\"question-wrapper-326214\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4a673e78-2932-4d56-ac38-a0cce20d062e\">possible reasons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> why newborns <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"804e1c99-d78a-4d2c-b606-94f1227b77bb\">try to mimic their mothers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326215\" id=\"question-wrapper-326215\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a description of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9162c31b-f156-4d75-a8a6-68b264c66239\">how babies' reactions to sounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"eb0e1e9e-ddb0-4593-a322-ce6bace32d64\">measured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in a study</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326216\" id=\"question-wrapper-326216\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"fa29c12d-1bee-4de1-aa0d-e32d16fed121\">illustration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5726789e-3120-4acc-951e-834bd83cfb00\">the limitations on what babies can hear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"78e4503b-fd88-46e1-a1de-00138f978dd0\">before birth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326217\" id=\"question-wrapper-326217\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>evidence that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"af64b86f-9c68-46fd-916b-1d4697d5404d\">babies with different mother tongues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"6509b7d7-045f-416b-80a9-e45b61bc318d\">produce different patterns of crying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements and the list of researchers below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct researcher, A, B or C.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 20–23 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Researchers</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Professor Amelia Finlayson</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Dr Katya Williams</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Walter Meade</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326218\" id=\"question-wrapper-326218\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"778eacbd-bedc-49fc-ab46-6b72afe29fc5\">A warning signal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"010d30ec-1f9b-4dff-b016-68f69bfa2248\">must remain consistent to be understood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326219\" id=\"question-wrapper-326219\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"07f0e950-6b5c-42b6-be2d-7a1191ff9570\">Speech development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0a3d0255-981f-4061-add4-9447194d8a36\">can build on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"63ecba0c-f68d-40c5-b4ca-562e02b1c47d\">the sounds infants make when they cry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326220\" id=\"question-wrapper-326220\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"0c609b5e-c102-4857-b6af-5ca88461128d\">Compared with other species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"758b1816-25f2-41e0-a301-0ef024c3350c\">human newborns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"fcb82ae0-d40a-4836-9cd5-e44ba999e686\">a strikingly wide range of vocal sounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326221\" id=\"question-wrapper-326221\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"3ca5be7f-d808-4a60-86bb-820c0f1428a9\">Unborn babies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a390c01d-242f-4257-9530-975aedeb99ea\">pick up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"2079b567-bbe0-4949-92eb-ca8e8d54469f\">one specific voice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"2de11b75-7092-4184-a16a-96c65ec857fc\">from an early stage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326222\" id=\"question-wrapper-326222\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"2bdf9b7a-f28f-47fd-a9d1-8702b011456a\">According to Finlayson<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, (24)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5d3205c6-4197-4071-bcb9-36721407077f\">all sound the same to a newborn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ACCENTS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326223\" id=\"question-wrapper-326223\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A baby's cry <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"98d71d31-cabd-49f7-abae-ae9a4f0a3322\">was once assumed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to be simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"cb72506e-5dba-4f1b-b3bb-0b319259839c\">a way of attracting its mother's attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, until <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"79e8b1d9-a4d6-45c1-89de-9089febb9832\">it proved to change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"2031f893-cbe8-49e4-8ee6-dce08d782b77\">from one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> (25)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"2031f893-cbe8-49e4-8ee6-dce08d782b77\">to the next<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WEEK</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326224\" id=\"question-wrapper-326224\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Babies may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f1c8ef19-8716-4454-9203-5cdff6f9bde4\">start acquiring language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> even before <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"619548f4-0461-4940-ac96-e39a372d7a20\">the onset of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"1b7dc1f7-abe1-43c1-9bdd-d0d78df890bd\">repetitive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"08222d32-2ba8-4f28-b8d9-d3c533578449\">late in their first year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BABBLING</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"3ca5be7f-d808-4a60-86bb-820c0f1428a9","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Unborn babies","passagePhrase":"human"},{"uid":"3ca5be7f-d808-4a60-86bb-820c0f1428a9 78e4503b-fd88-46e1-a1de-00138f978dd0","qNum":"18 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"foetuses"},{"uid":"2079b567-bbe0-4949-92eb-ca8e8d54469f","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"one specific voice","passagePhrase":"The mother's voice in particular"},{"uid":"a390c01d-242f-4257-9530-975aedeb99ea","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"pick up","passagePhrase":"is sensed"},{"uid":"2de11b75-7092-4184-a16a-96c65ec857fc","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"from an early stage","passagePhrase":"early on"},{"uid":"5726789e-3120-4acc-951e-834bd83cfb00","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"the limitations on what babies can hear","passagePhrase":"perceive information filtered at around 400 hertz ... cannot hear the actual words"},{"uid":"fa29c12d-1bee-4de1-aa0d-e32d16fed121","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"illustration","passagePhrase":"It is a bit like holding your head under water"},{"uid":"2bdf9b7a-f28f-47fd-a9d1-8702b011456a","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"According to Finlayson","passagePhrase":"Finlayson's research suggests"},{"uid":"5d3205c6-4197-4071-bcb9-36721407077f","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"all sound the same to a newborn","passagePhrase":"newborn babies probably cannot distinguish between"},{"uid":"eb0e1e9e-ddb0-4593-a322-ce6bace32d64","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"measured","passagePhrase":"measurements ... fitted with electrodes"},{"uid":"9162c31b-f156-4d75-a8a6-68b264c66239","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"how babies' reactions to sounds","passagePhrase":"recordings of different intonation patterns ... brainwaves responded to the differences"},{"uid":"98d71d31-cabd-49f7-abae-ae9a4f0a3322","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"was once assumed","passagePhrase":"It used to be thought"},{"uid":"778eacbd-bedc-49fc-ab46-6b72afe29fc5 cb72506e-5dba-4f1b-b3bb-0b319259839c","qNum":"20 25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"an alarm signal"},{"uid":"cb72506e-5dba-4f1b-b3bb-0b319259839c","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"a way of attracting its mother's attention","passagePhrase":"to call its mother"},{"uid":"79e8b1d9-a4d6-45c1-89de-9089febb9832","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"it proved to change","passagePhrase":"cries are not the same"},{"uid":"2031f893-cbe8-49e4-8ee6-dce08d782b77","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"from one ... to the next","passagePhrase":"from week to week"},{"uid":"778eacbd-bedc-49fc-ab46-6b72afe29fc5","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"A warning signal","passagePhrase":"a fire siren"},{"uid":"010d30ec-1f9b-4dff-b016-68f69bfa2248","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"must remain consistent to be understood","passagePhrase":"sounded different every day ... eventually fail to recognise it"},{"uid":"a1fb6ded-dfa3-43bc-bede-da14ddd31ed3","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"choosing the participants","passagePhrase":"German and French babies were selected"},{"uid":"3b341f4c-3737-44ce-a5c9-325d441c181f","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"rationale","passagePhrase":"because"},{"uid":"d3d87552-d7c9-4e08-be26-35a472147179","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"the method used to capture and examine infants' crying","passagePhrase":"the researchers recorded them ... More than 20 hours of recordings were subsequently entered into a computer for analysis"},{"uid":"af64b86f-9c68-46fd-916b-1d4697d5404d","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"babies with different mother tongues","passagePhrase":"the German babies ... the French babies"},{"uid":"6509b7d7-045f-416b-80a9-e45b61bc318d","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"produce different patterns of crying","passagePhrase":"began loudly and at a high pitch before following a downward curve ... produced a rising melodic contour"},{"uid":"804e1c99-d78a-4d2c-b606-94f1227b77bb","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"try to mimic their mothers","passagePhrase":"are ... highly motivated to imitate their mother's behaviour"},{"uid":"4a673e78-2932-4d56-ac38-a0cce20d062e","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"possible reasons","passagePhrase":"probably ... in order to"},{"uid":"f1c8ef19-8716-4454-9203-5cdff6f9bde4","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"start acquiring language","passagePhrase":"linguistic development ... begin"},{"uid":"08222d32-2ba8-4f28-b8d9-d3c533578449","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"late in their first year","passagePhrase":"at around nine or ten months"},{"uid":"619548f4-0461-4940-ac96-e39a372d7a20","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"the onset of","passagePhrase":"when babies start producing"},{"uid":"1b7dc1f7-abe1-43c1-9bdd-d0d78df890bd","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"repetitive","passagePhrase":"mam-mam-mam” or “ba-ba-ba"},{"uid":"63ecba0c-f68d-40c5-b4ca-562e02b1c47d","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"the sounds infants make when they cry","passagePhrase":"The melodic patterns practised in crying"},{"uid":"0a3d0255-981f-4061-add4-9447194d8a36","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"can build on","passagePhrase":"are building blocks for"},{"uid":"07f0e950-6b5c-42b6-be2d-7a1191ff9570","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Speech development","passagePhrase":"later sound production"},{"uid":"0c609b5e-c102-4857-b6af-5ca88461128d","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Compared with other species","passagePhrase":"In comparison with the sounds of other primates ... compared with other animals"},{"uid":"758b1816-25f2-41e0-a301-0ef024c3350c","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"human newborns","passagePhrase":"a newborn human baby"},{"uid":"fcb82ae0-d40a-4836-9cd5-e44ba999e686","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"a strikingly wide range of vocal sounds","passagePhrase":"a remarkable repertoire of melodic and rhythmic variations"},{"uid":"78e4503b-fd88-46e1-a1de-00138f978dd0","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"before birth","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_99":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>THEORIES OF PLANET FORMATION QUESTIONED</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 33\" data-uid=\"a7e987b8-4d22-4ddd-8042-aea645e9fe43 b0fc87cf-87f9-4e5e-b749-e1d50e40e4e0\">The traditional view</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"a7e987b8-4d22-4ddd-8042-aea645e9fe43\"> in astronomy has been</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> that planets <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"38265baa-ab06-4418-aa47-edcc78ef0436\">form slowly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> as material comes together within the disk of gas, dust and ice surrounding a young star. First, gravity gathers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c660b224-2122-41b4-b4e8-9301c2750f86\">particles of dust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"5afa9fed-1683-40ae-9c02-c1e8770a60bb\">merge to form boulder-sized bodies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, which in turn <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"5afa9fed-1683-40ae-9c02-c1e8770a60bb\">combine into progressively larger objects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. In about a million years, these develop into rocky planets such as Earth and Mars. Over the next few million years, gas from the disk settles around some of these solid bodies, causing them to grow much larger and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"f17a5fcf-ef8c-483d-af73-0e68b5db8c60\">eventually become<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> giants such as Saturn and Jupiter. This theory of planet formation is known as the core-accretion model. However, several astronomers have argued that this model may not provide a complete explanation of how planets form.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p><span>These astronomers have developed an alternative theory in which planets as massive as Jupiter, whether orbiting our Sun or a distant star, can form within only a few hundred years rather than over millions of years. Both theories begin with the same reservoir of planet-forming material. A spinning cloud of gas, dust and ice rapidly flattens into a structure known as a proto-planetary disk, and gravity then causes material within the disk to gather into planet-sized objects. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"df96e295-3a40-47d9-8e06-a4f0d56d90f1\">The main difference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"b7badfcc-9598-4e7a-8acb-c9e3a7bb4add\">the two models<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> lies in the speed at which this clustering occurs and the size of the initial clumps.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"8c69f6c9-6111-49cb-9765-b893e01367d2\">According to the core-accretion model<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, the formation of Jupiter required a solid core with five to ten times the mass of Earth to develop first. This process would have taken about a million years. Most astronomers believe that the large core then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ac141436-ef63-48ab-b46f-c0f7debfb8c2\">had sufficient gravity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"0f8e22c4-4d38-4978-a5db-13ea04ccc5ed\">attract a huge amount of gas from the surrounding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> proto-planetary disk, creating a planet of Jupiter's enormous size. Under the core-accretion model, such <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"46719b96-6e51-4a01-8ae6-da25368f995b\">gas giants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"38265baa-ab06-4418-aa47-edcc78ef0436\">may take as long as ten million years to form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p><span>Lucio Mayer of Zurich University argues that this process takes several million years too long. Direct telescope observations suggest that proto-planetary disks <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"81354e6b-3c03-406a-bfc7-cf8bc42eb5d2\">do not survive for more than about seven million years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, while studies of the environments in which stars form indicate that many disks <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"81354e6b-3c03-406a-bfc7-cf8bc42eb5d2\">may disappear much sooner<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Mayer points out that most stars in the Milky Way form within dense clouds of gas, dust and ice. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"2f901173-336c-49da-a0f3-09f1cb039510\">The stars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> can be extremely hot, and the ultraviolet light they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"2f901173-336c-49da-a0f3-09f1cb039510\">emit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"876f96a5-f77f-4595-b76f-0b08c62d7f67\">can evaporate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"c7886ea2-d074-4ae7-bb86-fa15fa4f0c25\">a proto-planetary disk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> in less than 100,000 years. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f4768955-a0ba-4a91-8bbb-e3f1800d8bd0\">Under the core-accretion model<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, this <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34 39\" data-uid=\"81354e6b-3c03-406a-bfc7-cf8bc42eb5d2 d40addcc-e500-43d9-88d4-164ef01d7568\">would not leave enough time</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"d40addcc-e500-43d9-88d4-164ef01d7568\"> for </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34 39\" data-uid=\"267d774f-ddea-4ccd-911b-3b8f7af2b36b d40addcc-e500-43d9-88d4-164ef01d7568\">a Jupiter-like planet</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"d40addcc-e500-43d9-88d4-164ef01d7568\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34 39\" data-uid=\"d40addcc-e500-43d9-88d4-164ef01d7568 f4768955-a0ba-4a91-8bbb-e3f1800d8bd0\">to form</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p><span>Computer simulations have also shown that when individual stars form, the gravitational pull <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"c6b906d8-6a70-4f3f-a4fd-4ad6d9a22f7c\">between them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b0d417a4-e46b-4f6d-a8df-cc67de68bf57\">destroy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2600c11e-3093-460d-87c7-4561f8245563\">the outer gaseous parts of proto-planetary disks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> in 100,000 years or less. Thomas Quinn of the University of Washington therefore concludes that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"3e6e2276-6113-4b6b-8895-5df36f375910\">if a gas giant cannot form quickly, it will probably never form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. He also argues that if the core-accretion model is correct, gas giants such as Jupiter should be rare. Yet by the time of these studies, astronomers had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2ffe17ab-6c34-45a8-bde4-a2316ee3d3df\">identified more than one hundred planets as large as Jupiter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> outside our solar system.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p><span>Quinn and his colleagues analysed the standard core-accretion model to investigate whether giant planets could form more quickly. They examined the work of Gerard Kuiper, who in the 1950s had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"4d166188-1ce0-4407-ac2d-b25e03f79dfb\">proposed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"1971c0d7-59a1-4bb0-8562-21c4297f9027\">rapid formation was possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Alan P. Boss of the Carnegie Institute <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"9d59c810-1dc7-43bf-b07d-2f6a3b050af9\">carried out more extensive work on the subject in the late 1980s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Using computer simulations, he was surprised to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"52f27b31-e518-45cc-bcf3-f2353e395fdb\">find that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> gravity could cause <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a6188a70-7c8e-486b-a689-60c6e96cdc0d\">a proto-planetary disk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, after only a few orbits of its parent star, to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"94f80051-c2e2-49a6-82da-c17e4c5254c1\">break into clumps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"7ceda6d3-dea0-4898-bb04-88fb200d28d6\">as large as an average planet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. These clumps would continue to attract gas, ice and dust. This alternative process is known as the gravitational-instability model of planet formation.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b></p><p><span>Calculations have suggested a further problem for the traditional theory: many of the solid bodies that might eventually become the rocky cores of Jupiter-sized planets could spiral into their parent stars before the giant planets had time to form. Further analysis has also identified <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d2358e25-466b-4f60-99aa-cd70c8d61b76\">other processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> that could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4bc26f6-cb39-482d-bd77-9fa436e90bff\">make a proto-planetary disk unstable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4bc26f6-cb39-482d-bd77-9fa436e90bff\">cause it to split into large fragments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d2358e25-466b-4f60-99aa-cd70c8d61b76\">For example<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, electrically charged material could accumulate within a disk and lead to fragmentation. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d2358e25-466b-4f60-99aa-cd70c8d61b76\">Alternatively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, a powerful gravitational disturbance, such as the pull of a nearby passing star, could destabilise the disk.</span></p><p><b><span>H</span></b></p><p><span>Nevertheless, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"ef056810-53cb-4c17-8661-e8f01351f797\">the gravitational-instability model<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e9557bab-2b77-4be0-b299-33f03137ffc6\">difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of its own. It is mathematically complicated and requires sophisticated computer simulations. As a result, researchers have not yet studied such simulations for long enough to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"6445a718-35e2-4890-9a83-700524b02e00\">establish conclusively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that the model can produce massive planets.</span></p><p><b><span>I</span></b></p><p><span>In response, Mayer argues that his team has carried out an unusually extensive simulation based on the gravitational-instability model. They spent two years refining calculations to track the development of a proto-planetary disk over a period of one thousand years, longer than previous simulations had done. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"d00c574d-7b46-49cc-a99a-3c1b56a40b99\">Mayer and his colleagues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b96d4148-830f-449e-85f3-b916a7b48241\">had relevant experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> from earlier simulations of the formation and evolution of galaxies. Through this work, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b96d4148-830f-449e-85f3-b916a7b48241\">had already developed fast computer code<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> capable of running in parallel on machines with hundreds of processors, and this expertise helped them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"36bb3d74-2dc9-431a-b2b5-b60ffb12c256\">investigate the gravitational-instability model<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has nine paragraphs, A–I.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–I, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326225\" id=\"question-wrapper-326225\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>the significance of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2ffe17ab-6c34-45a8-bde4-a2316ee3d3df\">the discovery of a large number of massive planets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326226\" id=\"question-wrapper-326226\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"df96e295-3a40-47d9-8e06-a4f0d56d90f1\">the factors that distinguish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"b7badfcc-9598-4e7a-8acb-c9e3a7bb4add\">the two proposed mechanisms of planet formation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326227\" id=\"question-wrapper-326227\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e9557bab-2b77-4be0-b299-33f03137ffc6\">obstacles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"6445a718-35e2-4890-9a83-700524b02e00\">obtaining firm support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"ef056810-53cb-4c17-8661-e8f01351f797\">the newer model<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of planet creation</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326228\" id=\"question-wrapper-326228\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>reasons why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"d00c574d-7b46-49cc-a99a-3c1b56a40b99\">Mayer's team<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"b96d4148-830f-449e-85f3-b916a7b48241\">was well equipped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"36bb3d74-2dc9-431a-b2b5-b60ffb12c256\">carry out their research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326229\" id=\"question-wrapper-326229\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d2358e25-466b-4f60-99aa-cd70c8d61b76\">alternative triggers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> that could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4bc26f6-cb39-482d-bd77-9fa436e90bff\">cause a planet-forming disk to break apart<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326230\" id=\"question-wrapper-326230\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c660b224-2122-41b4-b4e8-9301c2750f86\">tiny particles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"b0fc87cf-87f9-4e5e-b749-e1d50e40e4e0\">conventionally thought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"5afa9fed-1683-40ae-9c02-c1e8770a60bb\">grow into planets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A–G, below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 33–37 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Endings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"3e6e2276-6113-4b6b-8895-5df36f375910\">giant planets either take shape fast or not at all<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. computer simulations have conclusively proved the newer model to be correct.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"1971c0d7-59a1-4bb0-8562-21c4297f9027\">large planets might form quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, an idea <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"9d59c810-1dc7-43bf-b07d-2f6a3b050af9\">later investigated more thoroughly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"46719b96-6e51-4a01-8ae6-da25368f995b\">a giant planet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"f17a5fcf-ef8c-483d-af73-0e68b5db8c60\">the end product of a process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"38265baa-ab06-4418-aa47-edcc78ef0436\">lasting millions of years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. rocky planets develop only after gas giants have already formed.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. proto-planetary disks <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"81354e6b-3c03-406a-bfc7-cf8bc42eb5d2\">may not last long enough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"267d774f-ddea-4ccd-911b-3b8f7af2b36b\">a giant planet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f4768955-a0ba-4a91-8bbb-e3f1800d8bd0\">to be built the traditional way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"a6188a70-7c8e-486b-a689-60c6e96cdc0d\">a disk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> can quickly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"94f80051-c2e2-49a6-82da-c17e4c5254c1\">separate into pieces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"7ceda6d3-dea0-4898-bb04-88fb200d28d6\">the size of planets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326231\" id=\"question-wrapper-326231\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"a7e987b8-4d22-4ddd-8042-aea645e9fe43\">Traditionally, astronomers have believed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326232\" id=\"question-wrapper-326232\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Lucio Mayer argues that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326233\" id=\"question-wrapper-326233\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Thomas Quinn believes that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326234\" id=\"question-wrapper-326234\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Gerard Kuiper <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"4d166188-1ce0-4407-ac2d-b25e03f79dfb\">suggested<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326235\" id=\"question-wrapper-326235\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Alan P. Boss <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"52f27b31-e518-45cc-bcf3-f2353e395fdb\">discovered that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words and phrases, A–F, below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 38–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Words and Phrases</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. core</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. disk</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. ultraviolet light</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. gravitational pull</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. dust</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. clumps</span></p><p><b><span>The core-accretion model and its difficulties</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"8c69f6c9-6111-49cb-9765-b893e01367d2\">In the traditional model<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, an initially solid (38)________ grows until its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ac141436-ef63-48ab-b46f-c0f7debfb8c2\">gravitational force is strong enough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"0f8e22c4-4d38-4978-a5db-13ea04ccc5ed\">draw in large amounts of nearby gas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>This model has been challenged because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"2f901173-336c-49da-a0f3-09f1cb039510\">young stars give off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> (39)________, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"876f96a5-f77f-4595-b76f-0b08c62d7f67\">can disperse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"c7886ea2-d074-4ae7-bb86-fa15fa4f0c25\">a planet-forming disk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"d40addcc-e500-43d9-88d4-164ef01d7568\">before a gas giant completes its development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Nearby stars can also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b0d417a4-e46b-4f6d-a8df-cc67de68bf57\">strip away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2600c11e-3093-460d-87c7-4561f8245563\">the outer gas of these disks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"c6b906d8-6a70-4f3f-a4fd-4ad6d9a22f7c\">their mutual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> (40)________.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326236\" id=\"question-wrapper-326236\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326237\" id=\"question-wrapper-326237\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326238\" id=\"question-wrapper-326238\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a7e987b8-4d22-4ddd-8042-aea645e9fe43 b0fc87cf-87f9-4e5e-b749-e1d50e40e4e0","qNum":"32 33","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The traditional view"},{"uid":"a7e987b8-4d22-4ddd-8042-aea645e9fe43","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Traditionally, astronomers have believed","passagePhrase":"in astronomy has been"},{"uid":"38265baa-ab06-4418-aa47-edcc78ef0436","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"lasting millions of years","passagePhrase":"form slowly ... may take as long as ten million years to form"},{"uid":"c660b224-2122-41b4-b4e8-9301c2750f86","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"tiny particles","passagePhrase":"particles of dust"},{"uid":"5afa9fed-1683-40ae-9c02-c1e8770a60bb","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"grow into planets","passagePhrase":"merge to form boulder-sized bodies ... combine into progressively larger objects"},{"uid":"f17a5fcf-ef8c-483d-af73-0e68b5db8c60","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"the end product of a process","passagePhrase":"eventually become"},{"uid":"df96e295-3a40-47d9-8e06-a4f0d56d90f1","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"the factors that distinguish","passagePhrase":"The main difference"},{"uid":"b7badfcc-9598-4e7a-8acb-c9e3a7bb4add","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"the two proposed mechanisms of planet formation","passagePhrase":"the two models"},{"uid":"8c69f6c9-6111-49cb-9765-b893e01367d2","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"In the traditional model","passagePhrase":"According to the core-accretion model"},{"uid":"ac141436-ef63-48ab-b46f-c0f7debfb8c2","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"gravitational force is strong enough","passagePhrase":"had sufficient gravity"},{"uid":"0f8e22c4-4d38-4978-a5db-13ea04ccc5ed","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"draw in large amounts of nearby gas","passagePhrase":"attract a huge amount of gas from the surrounding"},{"uid":"46719b96-6e51-4a01-8ae6-da25368f995b","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"a giant planet","passagePhrase":"gas giants"},{"uid":"81354e6b-3c03-406a-bfc7-cf8bc42eb5d2","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"may not last long enough","passagePhrase":"do not survive for more than about seven million years ... may disappear much sooner"},{"uid":"2f901173-336c-49da-a0f3-09f1cb039510","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"young stars give off","passagePhrase":"The stars ... emit"},{"uid":"876f96a5-f77f-4595-b76f-0b08c62d7f67","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"can disperse","passagePhrase":"can evaporate"},{"uid":"c7886ea2-d074-4ae7-bb86-fa15fa4f0c25","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"a planet-forming disk","passagePhrase":"a proto-planetary disk"},{"uid":"f4768955-a0ba-4a91-8bbb-e3f1800d8bd0","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"to be built the traditional way","passagePhrase":"Under the core-accretion model"},{"uid":"81354e6b-3c03-406a-bfc7-cf8bc42eb5d2 d40addcc-e500-43d9-88d4-164ef01d7568","qNum":"34 39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"would not leave enough time"},{"uid":"d40addcc-e500-43d9-88d4-164ef01d7568","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"before a gas giant completes its development","passagePhrase":"for"},{"uid":"267d774f-ddea-4ccd-911b-3b8f7af2b36b d40addcc-e500-43d9-88d4-164ef01d7568","qNum":"34 39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a Jupiter-like planet"},{"uid":"d40addcc-e500-43d9-88d4-164ef01d7568 f4768955-a0ba-4a91-8bbb-e3f1800d8bd0","qNum":"34 39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"to form"},{"uid":"c6b906d8-6a70-4f3f-a4fd-4ad6d9a22f7c","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"their mutual","passagePhrase":"between them"},{"uid":"b0d417a4-e46b-4f6d-a8df-cc67de68bf57","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"strip away","passagePhrase":"destroy"},{"uid":"2600c11e-3093-460d-87c7-4561f8245563","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"the outer gas of these disks","passagePhrase":"the outer gaseous parts of proto-planetary disks"},{"uid":"3e6e2276-6113-4b6b-8895-5df36f375910","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"giant planets either take shape fast or not at all","passagePhrase":"if a gas giant cannot form quickly, it will probably never form"},{"uid":"2ffe17ab-6c34-45a8-bde4-a2316ee3d3df","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"the discovery of a large number of massive planets","passagePhrase":"identified more than one hundred planets as large as Jupiter"},{"uid":"4d166188-1ce0-4407-ac2d-b25e03f79dfb","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"suggested","passagePhrase":"proposed"},{"uid":"1971c0d7-59a1-4bb0-8562-21c4297f9027","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"large planets might form quickly","passagePhrase":"rapid formation was possible"},{"uid":"9d59c810-1dc7-43bf-b07d-2f6a3b050af9","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"later investigated more thoroughly","passagePhrase":"carried out more extensive work on the subject in the late 1980s"},{"uid":"52f27b31-e518-45cc-bcf3-f2353e395fdb","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"discovered that","passagePhrase":"find that"},{"uid":"a6188a70-7c8e-486b-a689-60c6e96cdc0d","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"a disk","passagePhrase":"a proto-planetary disk"},{"uid":"94f80051-c2e2-49a6-82da-c17e4c5254c1","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"separate into pieces","passagePhrase":"break into clumps"},{"uid":"7ceda6d3-dea0-4898-bb04-88fb200d28d6","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"the size of planets","passagePhrase":"as large as an average planet"},{"uid":"d2358e25-466b-4f60-99aa-cd70c8d61b76","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"alternative triggers","passagePhrase":"other processes ... For example ... Alternatively"},{"uid":"d4bc26f6-cb39-482d-bd77-9fa436e90bff","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"cause a planet-forming disk to break apart","passagePhrase":"make a proto-planetary disk unstable ... cause it to split into large fragments"},{"uid":"ef056810-53cb-4c17-8661-e8f01351f797","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"the newer model","passagePhrase":"the gravitational-instability model"},{"uid":"e9557bab-2b77-4be0-b299-33f03137ffc6","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"obstacles","passagePhrase":"difficulties"},{"uid":"6445a718-35e2-4890-9a83-700524b02e00","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"obtaining firm support","passagePhrase":"establish conclusively"},{"uid":"d00c574d-7b46-49cc-a99a-3c1b56a40b99","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Mayer's team","passagePhrase":"Mayer and his colleagues"},{"uid":"b96d4148-830f-449e-85f3-b916a7b48241","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"was well equipped","passagePhrase":"had relevant experience ... had already developed fast computer code"},{"uid":"36bb3d74-2dc9-431a-b2b5-b60ffb12c256","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"carry out their research","passagePhrase":"investigate the gravitational-instability model"},{"uid":"b0fc87cf-87f9-4e5e-b749-e1d50e40e4e0","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"conventionally thought","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"267d774f-ddea-4ccd-911b-3b8f7af2b36b","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"a giant planet","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_100":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><b><span>New Understanding of Giraffes in the Wild</span></b></p><p><span>Even as the tallest animals on Earth, giraffes can be easy to overlook. Despite being a favourite in zoos, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"bd02d0e9-80b1-41a0-ae2c-4541c910902b\">for many years relatively little </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"6bbfd2d9-9c11-4bd8-a878-36a410eb13f7 bd02d0e9-80b1-41a0-ae2c-4541c910902b\">research</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"bd02d0e9-80b1-41a0-ae2c-4541c910902b\"> was conducted</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"41fe9433-e414-4ef2-baec-3dfb0aef1713\">giraffes in the wild<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. “When I first became interested in giraffes in 2008 and started looking through the scientific literature, I was really surprised to see how little had been done,” said Megan Strauss, an animal researcher at the University of Minnesota, USA. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"bd02d0e9-80b1-41a0-ae2c-4541c910902b\">This began to change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> as a growing number of researchers sought to understand the biology and complex behaviour of this graceful giant in its natural habitat.</span></p><p><span>At the time of these studies, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"62caad8b-ee4a-4148-961a-9a6f156aebd1\">giraffes, found throughout sub-Saharan Africa<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, were generally classified as a single species with up to nine subspecies differing in features such as head shape and whether the fur on their legs was plain or patterned. They were not then listed as endangered, although researchers pointed to evidence that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"6a64dec1-b53b-40d7-9760-7a939bd34dff\">their population had fallen by about 40 per cent over the previous 15 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Studies of giraffes' social structures have provided researchers with new insights. Groups of females, for example, have been found to form close relationships that can last for years. “We're just at the beginnings of trying to understand this kind of behaviour,” Dr Strauss said. Female giraffes can live for 20 years or more, and it is possible that they benefit from remaining in groups by sharing information about good feeding grounds, helping to care for their young or reducing stress.</span></p><p><span>Mother giraffes have displayed signs of grief after losing their young, known as calves, to lions. Dr Strauss described one case in which a mother spent four days at the place where a lion had eaten her calf, refusing food and often remaining in the company of two other adult females. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"88989d40-16ba-47c0-bc80-9b879e133bf1\">Giraffe calves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> are extremely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"88989d40-16ba-47c0-bc80-9b879e133bf1\">vulnerable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to predators. Mothers will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"88989d40-16ba-47c0-bc80-9b879e133bf1\">fight vigorously to protect them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c3e7c1f1-81a3-4a46-a463-4c47df00d4be\">kicking both forwards and backwards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, yet around half of all calves are killed during their first year of life.</span></p><p><span>Male giraffes, known as bulls, generally become more dominant with age, and older bulls display this both physically and behaviourally. As their neck muscles grow, their posture becomes prouder and more vertical. Observations have shown that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"02a57e8a-4e26-489c-ace6-9928884526db c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec\">young bulls</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec\"> left on their own may </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"53839efb-3624-42e5-8e53-da540534e2ef c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec\">imitate their elders</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, holding their heads high and puffing out their necks. However, when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b390ae76-70ba-4382-baa0-bc6316ddae28\">a dominant older bull comes into view<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, the younger males <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b57cd03d-93be-4a5c-bae4-d28e4ce17561\">immediately try to make themselves appear small and harmless<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The younger bulls have good reason to fear their elders. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"58b64323-0775-45b6-bb9c-200d7c41d5ab\">Fights<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4225cb82-05f1-4980-9bb2-919c41367810\">adult males<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> have been observed in which each bull repeatedly “necks” the other, using its massive neck to drive its head against its opponent. One bull was even found to have survived <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"74289331-a862-4fd5-9e1c-6f30d2a2f20e\">a broken neck<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>Physical features of giraffes: study findings</span></b></p><p><span>A giraffe's skin is mostly grey. Its coat has dark patches separated by lighter hair, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"486a91b5-0bca-4464-8712-bb89ad487857\">providing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> camouflage by allowing the animal to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"645c1b23-a9fe-45bd-a07e-487c13b2d129\">blend into the patterns of light and shade around the acacia trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> on which it feeds. Feeding giraffes can therefore be difficult to spot even from only a few metres away.</span></p><p><span>Research indicates that giraffes also have excellent eyesight. They can see in colour and over long distances, helping them to detect lions and keep track of other giraffes. Their unusual mouths are also highly adapted for feeding: the lips and tongue can work together to grasp a branch and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"9ccec01f-5139-4c54-be49-b37cf3136b61\">remove the leaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> while avoiding thorns, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"53995699-4436-49d7-820d-76d4714e340f\">much as humans might grasp something with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> their hands. Each day, a giraffe consumes about 30 kilograms of leaves, shoots and vines, which are digested in its four-chambered stomach.</span></p><p><span>A giraffe may stand more than six metres tall. Its neck and legs are each roughly one third of its total height. The length of the neck results from elongated vertebrae rather than from having more vertebrae than other mammals. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"5ee3cfce-7d33-44e0-8215-48bf4ee54c8d\">Most of the neck's growth occurs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"3d9203a8-f6d5-43df-8cc9-0af8ef54d186\">during early childhood rather than before birth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, since <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"576233d0-8e15-4ab4-946f-b44ff8e22606\">giving birth to a calf with a much longer neck would be considerably more difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. Large muscles attached to the lower spine support the animal's head and neck.</span></p><p><span>Another major challenge concerns the cardiovascular system: blood must be pumped to the giraffe's head high above the heart and also returned from the lower parts of the body. The walls of the veins are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a5a4197b-21b1-46c0-8ed2-16b6dc41a4c3\">extremely thick<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, helping to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"b6d3264d-f4ee-4a0c-baef-76b99761077c\">prevent blood from leaking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> into the surrounding tissue. Other cardiovascular adaptations allow the giraffe to lower its head to drink and then raise it again rapidly without fainting.</span></p><p><span>Researchers were also surprised to discover that a giraffe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"ac760eaf-7c20-4ca4-8dd2-2db0edb583ea\">does not have an unusually large<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> heart. It accounts for about half a per cent of body mass, approximately the same proportion as in a mouse. The amount of blood pumped into circulation is also modest and, in proportion to body size, lower than in humans. This may help explain why giraffes rarely run for long periods: sufficient oxygen cannot be delivered to their muscles quickly enough to maintain sustained running.</span></p><p><span>The nervous system may create another limitation. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"63458991-7780-4ad3-9b17-dfb1779a099b\">Nerve signals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> travel at about the same speed in giraffes as they do in rats and other mammals. Because those signals have a much greater distance to travel before reaching the brain, giraffes may face <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"9eb80351-b411-42fb-9909-68f3eda6df13\">difficulties reacting quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to hazards such as a rock beneath the hoof or a bite to the ankle.</span></p><p><span>A better understanding of giraffe physiology and behaviour may also assist conservation efforts. Researchers hope that such knowledge will improve their ability to protect the animals as suitable habitat declines and giraffe populations become scarcer.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326239\" id=\"question-wrapper-326239\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"6bbfd2d9-9c11-4bd8-a878-36a410eb13f7\">Scientific interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"41fe9433-e414-4ef2-baec-3dfb0aef1713\">giraffes outside captivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"bd02d0e9-80b1-41a0-ae2c-4541c910902b\">was slow to develop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326240\" id=\"question-wrapper-326240\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Megan Strauss found that earlier studies of giraffes had concentrated on animals in zoos.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326241\" id=\"question-wrapper-326241\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>There are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"6a64dec1-b53b-40d7-9760-7a939bd34dff\">now more </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"62caad8b-ee4a-4148-961a-9a6f156aebd1 6a64dec1-b53b-40d7-9760-7a939bd34dff\">giraffes in Africa</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"6a64dec1-b53b-40d7-9760-7a939bd34dff\"> than there used to be</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326242\" id=\"question-wrapper-326242\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Unlike females, male giraffes seldom live beyond twenty years.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326243\" id=\"question-wrapper-326243\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Mother giraffes sometimes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c3e7c1f1-81a3-4a46-a463-4c47df00d4be\">use their legs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"88989d40-16ba-47c0-bc80-9b879e133bf1\">defend their young<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326244\" id=\"question-wrapper-326244\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b390ae76-70ba-4382-baa0-bc6316ddae28\">An older bull's arrival<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec\">the cue for </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"02a57e8a-4e26-489c-ace6-9928884526db c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec\">younger males</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec\"> to </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"b57cd03d-93be-4a5c-bae4-d28e4ce17561 c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec\">start </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"53839efb-3624-42e5-8e53-da540534e2ef b57cd03d-93be-4a5c-bae4-d28e4ce17561 c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec\">copying him</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326245\" id=\"question-wrapper-326245\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"58b64323-0775-45b6-bb9c-200d7c41d5ab\">Clashes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4225cb82-05f1-4980-9bb2-919c41367810\">mature males<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> can result in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"74289331-a862-4fd5-9e1c-6f30d2a2f20e\">serious injury<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the table below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Giraffes: physical features</span></b></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>Physical feature</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>Study finding</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Skin/coat</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"486a91b5-0bca-4464-8712-bb89ad487857\">serves as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"645c1b23-a9fe-45bd-a07e-487c13b2d129\">when the animal is close to trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Eyes</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>help them to spot lions and keep track of each other</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Mouth</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"53995699-4436-49d7-820d-76d4714e340f\">can be used like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)________ to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"9ccec01f-5139-4c54-be49-b37cf3136b61\">get leaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Neck</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"5ee3cfce-7d33-44e0-8215-48bf4ee54c8d\">its growth is concentrated in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"3d9203a8-f6d5-43df-8cc9-0af8ef54d186\">the period after<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)________, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"576233d0-8e15-4ab4-946f-b44ff8e22606\">making delivery easier<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> for mothers</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Cardiovascular system</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a5a4197b-21b1-46c0-8ed2-16b6dc41a4c3\">extra-strong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)________ to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"b6d3264d-f4ee-4a0c-baef-76b99761077c\">keep blood from spilling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>the size of the (12)________ is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"ac760eaf-7c20-4ca4-8dd2-2db0edb583ea\">surprisingly normal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> for a large animal. </span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Nerves</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"9eb80351-b411-42fb-9909-68f3eda6df13\">slower reaction time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> due to the (13)________ a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"63458991-7780-4ad3-9b17-dfb1779a099b\">neural message<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> has to travel</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326246\" id=\"question-wrapper-326246\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CAMOUFLAGE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326247\" id=\"question-wrapper-326247\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HANDS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326248\" id=\"question-wrapper-326248\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BIRTH</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326249\" id=\"question-wrapper-326249\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VEINS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326250\" id=\"question-wrapper-326250\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HEART</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326251\" id=\"question-wrapper-326251\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DISTANCE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"bd02d0e9-80b1-41a0-ae2c-4541c910902b","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"was slow to develop","passagePhrase":"for many years relatively little ... was conducted ... This began to change"},{"uid":"6bbfd2d9-9c11-4bd8-a878-36a410eb13f7 bd02d0e9-80b1-41a0-ae2c-4541c910902b","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"research"},{"uid":"41fe9433-e414-4ef2-baec-3dfb0aef1713","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"giraffes outside captivity","passagePhrase":"giraffes in the wild"},{"uid":"62caad8b-ee4a-4148-961a-9a6f156aebd1","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"giraffes, found throughout sub-Saharan Africa"},{"uid":"88989d40-16ba-47c0-bc80-9b879e133bf1","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"defend their young","passagePhrase":"Giraffe calves ... vulnerable ... fight vigorously to protect them"},{"uid":"c3e7c1f1-81a3-4a46-a463-4c47df00d4be","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"use their legs","passagePhrase":"kicking both forwards and backwards"},{"uid":"02a57e8a-4e26-489c-ace6-9928884526db c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"younger males","passagePhrase":"young bulls"},{"uid":"53839efb-3624-42e5-8e53-da540534e2ef c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"imitate their elders"},{"uid":"b390ae76-70ba-4382-baa0-bc6316ddae28","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"An older bull's arrival","passagePhrase":"a dominant older bull comes into view"},{"uid":"58b64323-0775-45b6-bb9c-200d7c41d5ab","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Clashes","passagePhrase":"Fights"},{"uid":"4225cb82-05f1-4980-9bb2-919c41367810","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"mature males","passagePhrase":"adult males"},{"uid":"74289331-a862-4fd5-9e1c-6f30d2a2f20e","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"serious injury","passagePhrase":"a broken neck"},{"uid":"486a91b5-0bca-4464-8712-bb89ad487857","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"serves as","passagePhrase":"providing"},{"uid":"645c1b23-a9fe-45bd-a07e-487c13b2d129","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"when the animal is close to trees","passagePhrase":"blend into the patterns of light and shade around the acacia trees"},{"uid":"9ccec01f-5139-4c54-be49-b37cf3136b61","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"get leaves","passagePhrase":"remove the leaves"},{"uid":"53995699-4436-49d7-820d-76d4714e340f","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"can be used like","passagePhrase":"much as humans might grasp something with"},{"uid":"5ee3cfce-7d33-44e0-8215-48bf4ee54c8d","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"its growth is concentrated in","passagePhrase":"Most of the neck's growth occurs"},{"uid":"3d9203a8-f6d5-43df-8cc9-0af8ef54d186","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the period after","passagePhrase":"during early childhood rather than before birth"},{"uid":"576233d0-8e15-4ab4-946f-b44ff8e22606","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"making delivery easier","passagePhrase":"giving birth to a calf with a much longer neck would be considerably more difficult"},{"uid":"a5a4197b-21b1-46c0-8ed2-16b6dc41a4c3","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"extra-strong","passagePhrase":"extremely thick"},{"uid":"b6d3264d-f4ee-4a0c-baef-76b99761077c","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"keep blood from spilling","passagePhrase":"prevent blood from leaking"},{"uid":"ac760eaf-7c20-4ca4-8dd2-2db0edb583ea","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"surprisingly normal","passagePhrase":"does not have an unusually large"},{"uid":"63458991-7780-4ad3-9b17-dfb1779a099b","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"neural message","passagePhrase":"Nerve signals"},{"uid":"9eb80351-b411-42fb-9909-68f3eda6df13","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"slower reaction time","passagePhrase":"difficulties reacting quickly"},{"uid":"6bbfd2d9-9c11-4bd8-a878-36a410eb13f7","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Scientific interest","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"62caad8b-ee4a-4148-961a-9a6f156aebd1 6a64dec1-b53b-40d7-9760-7a939bd34dff","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"giraffes in Africa","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"53839efb-3624-42e5-8e53-da540534e2ef b57cd03d-93be-4a5c-bae4-d28e4ce17561 c708f7fc-3524-4f82-b6b6-0bced9c876ec","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"copying him","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_101":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Healthy Buildings, Productive People</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><span>Have you felt tired at your desk lately? According to new research, some often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ddef3293-1d5c-46c8-a97f-a9117ef35158\">overlooked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> environmental factors within buildings — the degree or type of ventilation, airborne contaminants, lighting and noise levels, for example — can play a surprisingly large role in how good or bad you feel, and even how well you think. It is estimated that we spend more than 90 percent of our time inside, but builders in general have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ddef3293-1d5c-46c8-a97f-a9117ef35158\">paid little attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c4545021-30b5-4c63-8cbe-701f6b0944ce\">the health aspects of indoor spaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, instead focusing on superficial design features and on meeting minimum environmental standards to keep costs down.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><span>Researchers at Harvard University in the US looked at the effects of indoor air quality on workers' cognitive performance — important both for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"7460d3b6-895d-4f20-9a20-e3f09f837f1d\">health<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and for companies' bottom lines, says Joseph Allen, assistant professor of environmental health and principal investigator of the studies. '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"f592d5a7-7e07-4483-8042-f468028757c6\">The true cost of running our buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2e9bc5af-fe6f-469d-b39b-d17aeeba8c3e\">should take into account<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"23bf20ef-761c-40cf-b699-103bade612c3\">health and productivity of </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 20\" data-uid=\"0642c76e-a341-4796-bf6c-2cea37057fb6 23bf20ef-761c-40cf-b699-103bade612c3\">people in those buildings</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>,' Allen says. In fact, an analysis by the team showed that the cost of making alterations that could boost cognitive performance significantly was minuscule compared with the related increase in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"5b771e18-3444-4e87-b534-6fffe26c73ca\">productivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> — <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"5ad9af8d-9acc-4855-8ae1-3fb93c08b67b\">about $40 per person, per year, compared with a $6,500 increase in employee productivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b828b7cf-1da8-4cc4-ae23-564113cdf871\">The team's first study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, published in </span><i><span>Environmental Health Perspectives</span></i><span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"9786facc-f019-4689-9a9f-dc99b2560026\">was conducted at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the Syracuse Center of Excellence, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b9a79cb7-a55d-4a4c-b832-f9b60aa6a183\">a US research organization<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"bdd102c2-6561-47d6-9dc8-926a64c955df\">devoted to studying and developing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> sustainability. The center houses a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c22bd2ec-4431-4641-8e84-f9191a62d91e\">laboratory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that allows researchers to test a wide range of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e23d560c-4766-4cdc-b0a6-12ec0907810d\">indoor air quality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> factors using sophisticated ventilation. Each day, the indoor environment was regulated by a ventilation system which adjusted the levels of carbon dioxide and of volatile organic compounds, or VOCs — the toxic by-products of office supplies commonly found in the workplace. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"b617a286-c995-4651-89c9-f5fcbd075a58\">office workers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> were blinded to the conditions. For six days over two weeks, 24 office workers with administrative, technical, professional or managerial jobs came to the lab and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"830e94a0-70a9-4e87-aabc-5d6c69982f48\">performed their regular work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> under <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"a09da3e8-2df1-47a8-a1ec-23cf6fa8e05a\">minimal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> supervision, as well as participating in an hour and a half of cognitive testing at the end of the day. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"a1f85600-b3a7-4bdf-9451-c5ca144e567c\">cognitive tasks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> used in the study had participants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"cac46b70-7d0f-4883-915b-83a0f6a6e4ec\">respond to online scenarios that mimic real-life situations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"663c0033-9824-4dac-882d-85bedc552686\">such as running a city as a mayor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. The findings are remarkable for showing, in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c22bd2ec-4431-4641-8e84-f9191a62d91e\">a well-controlled study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e6ca6a72-7790-4b42-a410-3b7f69a62670\">indoor air quality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"62771391-a677-4c0b-b44b-733b7276f6ee\">can </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 23\" data-uid=\"62771391-a677-4c0b-b44b-733b7276f6ee cbdf6bd1-73ba-4e95-98d1-fe4314bcf304\">significantly</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"62771391-a677-4c0b-b44b-733b7276f6ee\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 23\" data-uid=\"62771391-a677-4c0b-b44b-733b7276f6ee bedca949-9afc-462a-b5e9-52c8c1c1aa96\">lower cognitive performance</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> in buildings that would otherwise meet current building standards, notes environmental psychologist Craig Zimring, director of Georgia Tech University's SimTigrate Design Lab in the US. 'If these findings are replicated in other labs and in real-world work environments,' he says, 'they could lead to designs that provide much more outside air through mechanical ventilation or operable windows, for example' — in turn, promoting better health and performance.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><span>In a second study, reported in </span><i><span>Building and Environment</span></i><span>, the Harvard–Syracuse team moved from the lab to the real world. Using the same methodology, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"d41ea16b-03b1-4b20-8b7c-0bd1e7fd3113\">compared test scores of 109 people working in 10 buildings — about 11 people per site<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> — in two buildings <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"fe33d538-ca0f-4de3-a048-3798ff1086ea\">in each of five cities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. In each city, one building had been officially certified as meeting recognised 'green' environmental standards and the other had not. When the team examined the buildings for differences, they found that certified buildings had lower humidity levels and brighter light than the non-certified buildings. That said, the differences in humidity and lighting didn't entirely explain the differing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"807d725c-a505-4622-8f38-18abaa472f13\">cognitive function scores of people on the job<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. This has led researchers to believe that other factors, such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"303b5ceb-8dac-4d79-a047-d52a868ff1fd\">how someone feels about their working environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"9c9768f7-81b3-4780-b5bb-e9ed633ac2a6\">may also play a part<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, notes Harvard research fellow Piers MacNaughton, who led the study.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"6a364621-b2da-409e-84a6-8944b9ecbc5c\">A recently constructed building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> on the Washington University campus in St. Louis, US, is providing another opportunity to examine how green building design can affect health and behavior. Hillman Hall was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"6a364621-b2da-409e-84a6-8944b9ecbc5c\">designed with the highest environmental and energy standards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> available, as well as design elements intended to foster more collaboration and physical activity, says Amy Eyler, associate professor and assistant dean for public health at the Brown School at Washington University. The design includes easy access to stairways, plenty of natural light, generous spaces for collaboration, desks that allow <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"631992b8-2099-4dad-aa01-53d8790ce273\">people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> to sit or stand up, and inviting places to walk. Unlike traditional hallways designed as long corridors with private offices to either side, for example, these hallways include classrooms, offices and spaces to sit, so they are multi-use — 'you have many reasons to walk them,' says Eyler. To test <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7bc7aa9b-a72d-4129-888f-12212332ecad\">how the building might affect people's behavior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, Eyler conducted a pre-test before people moved in, and a post-test one year later. Her team collected data on the three main features the designers were attempting to foster: physical activity, collaboration and sustainable practices. Results showed that people were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"50595751-1b0e-48bf-9310-ec4fd639975c\">more likely to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"347f040e-a459-4840-9bbb-c914019e0c63\">take part in spontaneous collaborations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"4f833d80-9f6f-4a23-84a8-17c939700f0c\">the new space<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> than in the older ones, and to be physically active.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><span>Like other researchers in this growing field, Eyler sees <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e9c64440-f47b-4ad3-8c89-c9dfb283b86e\">multidisciplinary collaboration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"69255e14-9f85-44d8-a5e5-4073c94b159f\">the key to success<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Administrators, public health faculty and architects worked together to create a building that captured the university's vision for a space that fosters collegial work and health for faculty, staff and students — a shared goal evidenced by the fact that the architecture firm that designed the building also funded part of the research. 'Complex projects like this one need <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e9c64440-f47b-4ad3-8c89-c9dfb283b86e\">teams of people with varied backgrounds and expertise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in order to solve them,' Eyler says.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A–F.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7bc7aa9b-a72d-4129-888f-12212332ecad\">The effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"6a364621-b2da-409e-84a6-8944b9ecbc5c\">a new environmentally friendly building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7bc7aa9b-a72d-4129-888f-12212332ecad\">its users<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. The reasons people spend so much of their lives indoors</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"d41ea16b-03b1-4b20-8b7c-0bd1e7fd3113\">assessment of workplaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"fe33d538-ca0f-4de3-a048-3798ff1086ea\">several locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ddef3293-1d5c-46c8-a97f-a9117ef35158\">low priority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> given to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"c4545021-30b5-4c63-8cbe-701f6b0944ce\">making buildings healthy for users<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"69255e14-9f85-44d8-a5e5-4073c94b159f\">The value of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e9c64440-f47b-4ad3-8c89-c9dfb283b86e\">involving specialists from different fields<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c22bd2ec-4431-4641-8e84-f9191a62d91e\">A controlled experiment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> on how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e23d560c-4766-4cdc-b0a6-12ec0907810d\">the air in a building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"62771391-a677-4c0b-b44b-733b7276f6ee\">affects thinking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. Workplace changes based on worker feedback </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"5ad9af8d-9acc-4855-8ae1-3fb93c08b67b\">financial benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"23bf20ef-761c-40cf-b699-103bade612c3\">healthier workplaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326252\" id=\"question-wrapper-326252\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326253\" id=\"question-wrapper-326253\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326254\" id=\"question-wrapper-326254\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326255\" id=\"question-wrapper-326255\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326256\" id=\"question-wrapper-326256\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326257\" id=\"question-wrapper-326257\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 20–23) and the list of researchers below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct researcher, A–D.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–D, in boxes 20–23 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Researchers</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Joseph Allen </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Craig Zimring </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Piers MacNaughton </span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Amy Eyler</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326258\" id=\"question-wrapper-326258\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>When <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"f592d5a7-7e07-4483-8042-f468028757c6\">working out what a building costs to run<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"7460d3b6-895d-4f20-9a20-e3f09f837f1d\">wellbeing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"5b771e18-3444-4e87-b534-6fffe26c73ca\">output<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"0642c76e-a341-4796-bf6c-2cea37057fb6\">occupants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2e9bc5af-fe6f-469d-b39b-d17aeeba8c3e\">ought to be factored in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326259\" id=\"question-wrapper-326259\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"807d725c-a505-4622-8f38-18abaa472f13\">A worker’s performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"9c9768f7-81b3-4780-b5bb-e9ed633ac2a6\">may depend partly on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"303b5ceb-8dac-4d79-a047-d52a868ff1fd\">what they themselves think of their workspace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326260\" id=\"question-wrapper-326260\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"631992b8-2099-4dad-aa01-53d8790ce273\">Employees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"50595751-1b0e-48bf-9310-ec4fd639975c\">more inclined to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"347f040e-a459-4840-9bbb-c914019e0c63\">work together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"4f833d80-9f6f-4a23-84a8-17c939700f0c\">the layout of their workplace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> encourages it.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326261\" id=\"question-wrapper-326261\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People may find that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e6ca6a72-7790-4b42-a410-3b7f69a62670\">their working environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> leaves them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"cbdf6bd1-73ba-4e95-98d1-fe4314bcf304\">markedly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"bedca949-9afc-462a-b5e9-52c8c1c1aa96\">less able to think clearly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Write </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>The first Harvard study</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"9786facc-f019-4689-9a9f-dc99b2560026\">The setting for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b828b7cf-1da8-4cc4-ae23-564113cdf871\">Allen's first study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b9a79cb7-a55d-4a4c-b832-f9b60aa6a183\">an institution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"bdd102c2-6561-47d6-9dc8-926a64c955df\">whose research is concerned with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> (24)________. In this study, an advanced air-handling system was used to control the levels of certain pollutants in the test environment. There was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"a09da3e8-2df1-47a8-a1ec-23cf6fa8e05a\">very little<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> (25) ________ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"b617a286-c995-4651-89c9-f5fcbd075a58\">participants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> as they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"830e94a0-70a9-4e87-aabc-5d6c69982f48\">carried out their usual jobs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. They were later given <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"a1f85600-b3a7-4bdf-9451-c5ca144e567c\">tasks assessing their thinking skills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"cac46b70-7d0f-4883-915b-83a0f6a6e4ec\">placed them in lifelike roles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"663c0033-9824-4dac-882d-85bedc552686\">such as that of a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26) ________. </span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326262\" id=\"question-wrapper-326262\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">sustainability</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326263\" id=\"question-wrapper-326263\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">supervision</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326264\" id=\"question-wrapper-326264\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">mayor</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"ddef3293-1d5c-46c8-a97f-a9117ef35158","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"low priority","passagePhrase":"overlooked ... paid little attention"},{"uid":"c4545021-30b5-4c63-8cbe-701f6b0944ce","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"making buildings healthy for users","passagePhrase":"the health aspects of indoor spaces"},{"uid":"7460d3b6-895d-4f20-9a20-e3f09f837f1d","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"wellbeing","passagePhrase":"health"},{"uid":"f592d5a7-7e07-4483-8042-f468028757c6","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"working out what a building costs to run","passagePhrase":"The true cost of running our buildings"},{"uid":"2e9bc5af-fe6f-469d-b39b-d17aeeba8c3e","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"ought to be factored in","passagePhrase":"should take into account"},{"uid":"23bf20ef-761c-40cf-b699-103bade612c3","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"healthier workplaces","passagePhrase":"health and productivity of"},{"uid":"0642c76e-a341-4796-bf6c-2cea37057fb6 23bf20ef-761c-40cf-b699-103bade612c3","qNum":"15 20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"people in those buildings"},{"uid":"5b771e18-3444-4e87-b534-6fffe26c73ca","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"output","passagePhrase":"productivity"},{"uid":"5ad9af8d-9acc-4855-8ae1-3fb93c08b67b","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"financial benefits","passagePhrase":"about $40 per person, per year, compared with a $6,500 increase in employee productivity"},{"uid":"b828b7cf-1da8-4cc4-ae23-564113cdf871","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Allen's first study","passagePhrase":"The team's first study"},{"uid":"9786facc-f019-4689-9a9f-dc99b2560026","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"The setting for","passagePhrase":"was conducted at"},{"uid":"b9a79cb7-a55d-4a4c-b832-f9b60aa6a183","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"an institution","passagePhrase":"a US research organization"},{"uid":"bdd102c2-6561-47d6-9dc8-926a64c955df","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"whose research is concerned with","passagePhrase":"devoted to studying and developing"},{"uid":"c22bd2ec-4431-4641-8e84-f9191a62d91e","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"A controlled experiment","passagePhrase":"laboratory ... a well-controlled study"},{"uid":"e23d560c-4766-4cdc-b0a6-12ec0907810d","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"the air in a building","passagePhrase":"indoor air quality"},{"uid":"b617a286-c995-4651-89c9-f5fcbd075a58","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"participants","passagePhrase":"office workers"},{"uid":"830e94a0-70a9-4e87-aabc-5d6c69982f48","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"carried out their usual jobs","passagePhrase":"performed their regular work"},{"uid":"a09da3e8-2df1-47a8-a1ec-23cf6fa8e05a","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"very little","passagePhrase":"minimal"},{"uid":"a1f85600-b3a7-4bdf-9451-c5ca144e567c","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"tasks assessing their thinking skills","passagePhrase":"cognitive tasks"},{"uid":"cac46b70-7d0f-4883-915b-83a0f6a6e4ec","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"placed them in lifelike roles","passagePhrase":"respond to online scenarios that mimic real-life situations"},{"uid":"663c0033-9824-4dac-882d-85bedc552686","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"such as that of a","passagePhrase":"such as running a city as a mayor"},{"uid":"e6ca6a72-7790-4b42-a410-3b7f69a62670","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"their working environment","passagePhrase":"indoor air quality"},{"uid":"62771391-a677-4c0b-b44b-733b7276f6ee","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"affects thinking","passagePhrase":"can"},{"uid":"62771391-a677-4c0b-b44b-733b7276f6ee cbdf6bd1-73ba-4e95-98d1-fe4314bcf304","qNum":"16 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"significantly"},{"uid":"62771391-a677-4c0b-b44b-733b7276f6ee bedca949-9afc-462a-b5e9-52c8c1c1aa96","qNum":"16 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"lower cognitive performance"},{"uid":"d41ea16b-03b1-4b20-8b7c-0bd1e7fd3113","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"assessment of workplaces","passagePhrase":"compared test scores of 109 people working in 10 buildings — about 11 people per site"},{"uid":"fe33d538-ca0f-4de3-a048-3798ff1086ea","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"several locations","passagePhrase":"in each of five cities"},{"uid":"807d725c-a505-4622-8f38-18abaa472f13","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"A worker’s performance","passagePhrase":"cognitive function scores of people on the job"},{"uid":"303b5ceb-8dac-4d79-a047-d52a868ff1fd","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"what they themselves think of their workspace","passagePhrase":"how someone feels about their working environment"},{"uid":"9c9768f7-81b3-4780-b5bb-e9ed633ac2a6","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"may depend partly on","passagePhrase":"may also play a part"},{"uid":"6a364621-b2da-409e-84a6-8944b9ecbc5c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"a new environmentally friendly building","passagePhrase":"A recently constructed building ... designed with the highest environmental and energy standards"},{"uid":"631992b8-2099-4dad-aa01-53d8790ce273","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Employees","passagePhrase":"people"},{"uid":"7bc7aa9b-a72d-4129-888f-12212332ecad","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"The effects ... its users","passagePhrase":"how the building might affect people's behavior"},{"uid":"50595751-1b0e-48bf-9310-ec4fd639975c","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"more inclined to","passagePhrase":"more likely to"},{"uid":"347f040e-a459-4840-9bbb-c914019e0c63","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"work together","passagePhrase":"take part in spontaneous collaborations"},{"uid":"4f833d80-9f6f-4a23-84a8-17c939700f0c","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"the layout of their workplace","passagePhrase":"the new space"},{"uid":"e9c64440-f47b-4ad3-8c89-c9dfb283b86e","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"involving specialists from different fields","passagePhrase":"multidisciplinary collaboration ... teams of people with varied backgrounds and expertise"},{"uid":"69255e14-9f85-44d8-a5e5-4073c94b159f","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"The value of","passagePhrase":"the key to success"},{"uid":"0642c76e-a341-4796-bf6c-2cea37057fb6","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"occupants","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"cbdf6bd1-73ba-4e95-98d1-fe4314bcf304","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"markedly","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"bedca949-9afc-462a-b5e9-52c8c1c1aa96","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"less able to think clearly","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_102":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>What is social history?</span></b></p><p><span>Ever since its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"7f50317f-04bf-4da2-9d67-882b18aba6cf\">elevation to the status of an academic discipline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, history has been very largely concerned with problems of its own making. These may be gaps which the young researcher is advised by supervisors to fill, or established views which he or she is encouraged to challenge. In either case, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"a61461d1-24eb-4c91-ae8a-b31061523bf5\">the need<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> for the researcher to provide <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"a61461d1-24eb-4c91-ae8a-b31061523bf5\">new insights<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2ebdb8ec-9be7-4c16-b286-d9a2bf85c64a\">in order to gain professional advancement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> often counts for more than the intrinsic interest of the topic.</span></p><p><span>Social history is quite different. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"838cc1ac-b5da-4cd2-a8bb-7a97e1959ed3\">touches on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, and arguably helps to focus, major issues of public debate. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"838cc1ac-b5da-4cd2-a8bb-7a97e1959ed3\">mobilises<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"9c94339e-8e07-4bce-a6ee-e83ccf5e80df\">popular enthusiasm and </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"838cc1ac-b5da-4cd2-a8bb-7a97e1959ed3\">engages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"9c94339e-8e07-4bce-a6ee-e83ccf5e80df\"> popular passions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. It prides itself on being concerned with everyday things rather than sensational events and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"f2da3bed-1316-4d64-bc4e-9e4b00551a84\">is directed against<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"6622e607-c66e-4a95-8380-e5cfc2dac4df\">Great Man’ theories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e5a7e8df-7dfd-48cc-8a0a-35e6ca599e3f\">originally characterised history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, and the tedious focus on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"38643401-e366-4da4-b792-8e54bf7e001a\">bureaucratic issues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"3c48cbc6-327e-4089-b8f1-62569aed1672\">subsequently dominated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> the 1920s and 1930s. This is also reflected in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e9cef483-3f4b-4f0c-8b82-18daaaf48615\">the way it is taught<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"0a0285e9-3ee0-403b-896b-db6660a07c87\">the adoption of multidisciplinary perspectives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> rather than a narrow historical interpretation.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"4f4904c1-4873-480d-8f48-cb2da8cd672a\">Social history emerged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, both as a popular enthusiasm and as a scholarly practice, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"4f4904c1-4873-480d-8f48-cb2da8cd672a\">from the cultural revolution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of the 1960s in North America and Europe, and reproduces its leading inspirations. The spirit of social history was pre-eminently a modernising one, as reflected in its choice of subject matter. Whereas <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"8ce2ea48-ddcd-4c94-a860-eecd5467a89b\">traditional history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> had focused on the 12th to 17th centuries, social history was apt to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"e107eb63-d3c2-4089-af50-87dc479cb7c3\">make its historical homeland in the 19th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, while more recently it has extended its inquiry to contemporary events and movements.</span></p><p><span>The subject matter favoured by the new social history, with its move away from the aristocracy and the establishment, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"10b453a6-b656-4266-b6df-52a5af5b1534\">corresponds to other cultural manifestations of the 1960s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, as for instance <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"d7c03c4c-d41d-414d-af3f-63c674768084\">New Wave British cinema<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, with its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"d35cd586-57ac-4deb-aba9-a466b0bc68f6\">working-class protagonists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, or ‘pop art’, with its use of everyday artefacts. Similarly, the anti-institutional bias of the new social history—the renewed determination to write the history of ‘ordinary’ people rather than that of statecraft—could be said to echo a much more widespread <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"d9eb4a9d-e7e4-4e1b-a79f-e7357fc6ca59\">collapse of social deference and a questioning of authority figures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of all kinds.</span></p><p><span>Another major 1960s influence on the new social history—very different in its origins and effects—was the ‘nostalgia industry’, which focused on the sale of memorabilia and artefacts from recent history. This emerged as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"2969057f-1cf4-4a1d-b603-dd627148ba5c\">a kind of negative counterpart to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"61e0d6cd-7da8-4536-84c4-8351c441a82c\">the otherwise dominant modernisation of the decade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> and reflected a disenchantment, no less apparent on the Left of the political spectrum than on the Right, with post-war social change.</span></p><p><span>Industrial archaeology, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"577b0455-b6fa-4e52-b75b-3d0e3eefcf6c\">an invention of the 1960s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"577b0455-b6fa-4e52-b75b-3d0e3eefcf6c\">elevated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ac5fcf6a-6c0d-405d-b47d-559428ecc200\">disused factories and mills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"577b0455-b6fa-4e52-b75b-3d0e3eefcf6c\">to the status of national monuments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Following in the same track, property restorers turned houses built for 19th-century factory workers, once emblems of poverty, overcrowding and ill-health, into picturesque residences. In another sphere one could point to the proliferation of folk clubs and the discovery of industrial folk song as prefiguring one of the major themes of the new social history: the dignity of labour.</span></p><p><span>So far as historical work was concerned, by the 1970s the sense of disenchantment had crystallised into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"822ceea3-f667-4b72-9ba6-958979b6ba1b\">an idealised view of the past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"822ceea3-f667-4b72-9ba6-958979b6ba1b\">a nostalgic regard for disappearing communities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. Restoration of the vanished components of the world we have lost became a major impetus in historical writing and research. The dignity of ordinary people could be said to be the unifying theme of this line of historical inquiry and retrieval, a celebration of everyday life, even, perhaps especially, when it involved hardship and suffering.</span></p><p><span>Despite the novelty of its subject matter, social history reproduces many of the characteristic biases of its predecessors. Social historians are good at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"621ed3c9-456c-41ce-a10e-a23a2cd6cd66\">amassing details<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> on household artefacts, budgets and daily purchases, but at times the evidence is assumed to speak for itself, and the simple reproduction of fact masquerades as explanation. The facts accumulated may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"181ede35-6608-4fa5-a8c3-33acb3bc18ed\">leave no conceptual space for the great absences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, for the many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"181ede35-6608-4fa5-a8c3-33acb3bc18ed\">areas where the documentary record is silent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The indulgence which social historians extend towards their subjects and the desire to establish ‘empathy’—seeing the past in terms of its own values rather than those of today—can also serve to flatter our self-esteem, making history a field in which, at no great cost to ourselves, we can demonstrate our enlarged sympathies and benevolence. Recognising our kinship to people in the past, and tracing, or discovering, their likeness to ourselves, we are flattered in the belief that underneath we are all lovable; eccentric perhaps and even absurd, but large-hearted, generous and frank. This sense of integration with the past can thus serve as a comfortable alternative to critical awareness and self-questioning, allowing us to dignify the present by illegitimate association with the past.</span></p><p><span>Social history, if it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b468c5da-0b95-4bc6-9864-fb3182a68a4e\">to fulfil its subversive potential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, needs to be a great deal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"ae85ad4a-546f-4ab6-9a7d-4f7c11ee2777\">more disturbing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. If it is to celebrate a common humanity, and to bring past and present closer together, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"64f3f745-4512-4c87-a0c6-cb1823cca9e7\">far more weight needs to be given to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"ae85ad4a-546f-4ab6-9a7d-4f7c11ee2777\">the effects of insecurities and emergencies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"ae85ad4a-546f-4ab6-9a7d-4f7c11ee2777\">the fears that shadow the growing up of children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, the oppositions we encounter during our lives—experiences which may be hard for an individual to categorise but which nevertheless have a significance which goes beyond that individual.</span></p><p><span>Perhaps too we might recognise that there is a profound condescension in the notion of ‘ordinary people’—that unified totality in which social historians are apt to deal. Implicitly, it is a category from which we tend to exclude ourselves, although in fact we are exceptional only by our privilege of hindsight. ‘There are … no masses,’ Raymond Williams wrote, ‘only ways of seeing people as masses.’ It is perhaps time for historians to scrutinise the term ‘ordinary people’ in the same way.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words and phrases, A–H, below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e9cef483-3f4b-4f0c-8b82-18daaaf48615\">methodology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. needs</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"a61461d1-24eb-4c91-ae8a-b31061523bf5\">originality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"6622e607-c66e-4a95-8380-e5cfc2dac4df\">important people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. accuracy</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"9c94339e-8e07-4bce-a6ee-e83ccf5e80df\">interests and feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. explanation</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"38643401-e366-4da4-b792-8e54bf7e001a\">organisational matters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></span></p><p><b><span>How is social history different from historical study?</span></b></p><p><span>Since it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"7f50317f-04bf-4da2-9d67-882b18aba6cf\">became a university subject<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, historical study has been overly preoccupied with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"a61461d1-24eb-4c91-ae8a-b31061523bf5\">a search for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> (27)________ by scholars <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2ebdb8ec-9be7-4c16-b286-d9a2bf85c64a\">hoping to develop their careers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Social history, however, is more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"838cc1ac-b5da-4cd2-a8bb-7a97e1959ed3\">closely tied to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> the (28)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"9c94339e-8e07-4bce-a6ee-e83ccf5e80df\">of the general public<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"f2da3bed-1316-4d64-bc4e-9e4b00551a84\">rejects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> history's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"e5a7e8df-7dfd-48cc-8a0a-35e6ca599e3f\">traditional emphasis on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> (29)________ and its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"3c48cbc6-327e-4089-b8f1-62569aed1672\">later preoccupation with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> (30)________. It also differs from traditional history in its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e9cef483-3f4b-4f0c-8b82-18daaaf48615\">teaching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> (31)________, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"0a0285e9-3ee0-403b-896b-db6660a07c87\">draws on a range of academic subjects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326265\" id=\"question-wrapper-326265\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326266\" id=\"question-wrapper-326266\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326267\" id=\"question-wrapper-326267\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326268\" id=\"question-wrapper-326268\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326269\" id=\"question-wrapper-326269\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 32–35 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326270\" id=\"question-wrapper-326270\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"4f4904c1-4873-480d-8f48-cb2da8cd672a\">The rise of social history led to the cultural revolution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of the 1960s.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326271\" id=\"question-wrapper-326271\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Social historians tend to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"e107eb63-d3c2-4089-af50-87dc479cb7c3\">study a later period of history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"8ce2ea48-ddcd-4c94-a860-eecd5467a89b\">traditional historians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> did.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326272\" id=\"question-wrapper-326272\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"d35cd586-57ac-4deb-aba9-a466b0bc68f6\">choice of subjects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"d7c03c4c-d41d-414d-af3f-63c674768084\">1960s British cinema<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"10b453a6-b656-4266-b6df-52a5af5b1534\">reflected a cultural trend also seen in social history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326273\" id=\"question-wrapper-326273\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"d9eb4a9d-e7e4-4e1b-a79f-e7357fc6ca59\">loss of respect for authority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> in the 1960s was a leading cause of social problems.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter in boxes 36–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326274\" id=\"question-wrapper-326274\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What point is made about the ‘nostalgia industry’?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Its products were not always genuine historical items.</li> <li>B. It led to the abandonment of modernisation.</li> <li>C. Its origins were political rather than industrial.</li> <li>D. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"2969057f-1cf4-4a1d-b603-dd627148ba5c\">opposed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"61e0d6cd-7da8-4536-84c4-8351c441a82c\">the dominant trend of the time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326275\" id=\"question-wrapper-326275\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the sixth paragraph, the writer makes the point that in the 1960s</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. construction workers gained greater status.</li> <li>B. there was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"577b0455-b6fa-4e52-b75b-3d0e3eefcf6c\">a new interest in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ac5fcf6a-6c0d-405d-b47d-559428ecc200\">traditional industrial buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</li> <li>C. architects applied industrial techniques to home design.</li> <li>D. many older homes were unsuitable as places of residence.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326276\" id=\"question-wrapper-326276\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>By the 1970s, historians had come to believe that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. researchers should focus on the immediate past.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"822ceea3-f667-4b72-9ba6-958979b6ba1b\">modern life is not necessarily an improvement on the past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li> <li>C. they should not overemphasise the difficulties of life in the past.</li> <li>D. there was a need for more ordinary people to do research into the past.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326277\" id=\"question-wrapper-326277\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>One problem related to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"621ed3c9-456c-41ce-a10e-a23a2cd6cd66\">the use of detail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> by social historians is that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the wrong types of facts are collected.</li> <li>B. some information may be hard to categorise.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"181ede35-6608-4fa5-a8c3-33acb3bc18ed\">more important issues may be ignored<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</li> <li>D. some of the data may be incorrect.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326278\" id=\"question-wrapper-326278\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer recommends that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"b468c5da-0b95-4bc6-9864-fb3182a68a4e\">to be effective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, social history must</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"64f3f745-4512-4c87-a0c6-cb1823cca9e7\">give greater attention to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"ae85ad4a-546f-4ab6-9a7d-4f7c11ee2777\">troubling aspects of ordinary experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> <li>B. build on what has already been established by historians.</li> <li>C. try to provide an objective view of the recent past.</li> <li>D. offer solutions to the pressing problems of our day.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7f50317f-04bf-4da2-9d67-882b18aba6cf","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"became a university subject","passagePhrase":"elevation to the status of an academic discipline"},{"uid":"a61461d1-24eb-4c91-ae8a-b31061523bf5","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"originality ... a search for","passagePhrase":"the need ... new insights"},{"uid":"2ebdb8ec-9be7-4c16-b286-d9a2bf85c64a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"hoping to develop their careers","passagePhrase":"in order to gain professional advancement"},{"uid":"838cc1ac-b5da-4cd2-a8bb-7a97e1959ed3","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"closely tied to","passagePhrase":"touches on ... mobilises ... engages"},{"uid":"9c94339e-8e07-4bce-a6ee-e83ccf5e80df","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"interests and feelings ... of the general public","passagePhrase":"popular enthusiasm and ... popular passions"},{"uid":"f2da3bed-1316-4d64-bc4e-9e4b00551a84","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"rejects","passagePhrase":"is directed against"},{"uid":"6622e607-c66e-4a95-8380-e5cfc2dac4df","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"important people","passagePhrase":"Great Man’ theories"},{"uid":"e5a7e8df-7dfd-48cc-8a0a-35e6ca599e3f","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"traditional emphasis on","passagePhrase":"originally characterised history"},{"uid":"38643401-e366-4da4-b792-8e54bf7e001a","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"organisational matters","passagePhrase":"bureaucratic issues"},{"uid":"3c48cbc6-327e-4089-b8f1-62569aed1672","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"later preoccupation with","passagePhrase":"subsequently dominated"},{"uid":"e9cef483-3f4b-4f0c-8b82-18daaaf48615","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"methodology ... teaching","passagePhrase":"the way it is taught"},{"uid":"0a0285e9-3ee0-403b-896b-db6660a07c87","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"draws on a range of academic subjects","passagePhrase":"the adoption of multidisciplinary perspectives"},{"uid":"8ce2ea48-ddcd-4c94-a860-eecd5467a89b","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"traditional historians","passagePhrase":"traditional history"},{"uid":"e107eb63-d3c2-4089-af50-87dc479cb7c3","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"study a later period of history","passagePhrase":"make its historical homeland in the 19th century"},{"uid":"10b453a6-b656-4266-b6df-52a5af5b1534","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"reflected a cultural trend also seen in social history","passagePhrase":"corresponds to other cultural manifestations of the 1960s"},{"uid":"d7c03c4c-d41d-414d-af3f-63c674768084","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"1960s British cinema","passagePhrase":"New Wave British cinema"},{"uid":"d35cd586-57ac-4deb-aba9-a466b0bc68f6","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"choice of subjects","passagePhrase":"working-class protagonists"},{"uid":"d9eb4a9d-e7e4-4e1b-a79f-e7357fc6ca59","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"loss of respect for authority","passagePhrase":"collapse of social deference and a questioning of authority figures"},{"uid":"2969057f-1cf4-4a1d-b603-dd627148ba5c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"opposed","passagePhrase":"a kind of negative counterpart to"},{"uid":"61e0d6cd-7da8-4536-84c4-8351c441a82c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"the dominant trend of the time","passagePhrase":"the otherwise dominant modernisation of the decade"},{"uid":"577b0455-b6fa-4e52-b75b-3d0e3eefcf6c","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"a new interest in","passagePhrase":"an invention of the 1960s ... elevated ... to the status of national monuments"},{"uid":"ac5fcf6a-6c0d-405d-b47d-559428ecc200","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"traditional industrial buildings","passagePhrase":"disused factories and mills"},{"uid":"822ceea3-f667-4b72-9ba6-958979b6ba1b","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"modern life is not necessarily an improvement on the past","passagePhrase":"an idealised view of the past ... a nostalgic regard for disappearing communities"},{"uid":"621ed3c9-456c-41ce-a10e-a23a2cd6cd66","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"the use of detail","passagePhrase":"amassing details"},{"uid":"181ede35-6608-4fa5-a8c3-33acb3bc18ed","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"more important issues may be ignored","passagePhrase":"leave no conceptual space for the great absences ... areas where the documentary record is silent"},{"uid":"b468c5da-0b95-4bc6-9864-fb3182a68a4e","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"to be effective","passagePhrase":"to fulfil its subversive potential"},{"uid":"ae85ad4a-546f-4ab6-9a7d-4f7c11ee2777","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"troubling aspects of ordinary experience","passagePhrase":"more disturbing ... the effects of insecurities and emergencies ... the fears that shadow the growing up of children"},{"uid":"64f3f745-4512-4c87-a0c6-cb1823cca9e7","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"give greater attention to","passagePhrase":"far more weight needs to be given to"}]},"reading_u2_103":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>Otters</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p><span>Otters have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c76ef0b3-372b-4092-aa30-ad86ffea3290\">long, slender bodies and short legs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, a shape well suited to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6f1ca9eb-086e-4893-b872-8772214de6ba\">pushing through<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"35842b60-c017-448e-8ed4-cbf505cc733e\">dense undergrowth and hunting in tunnels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. An adult male may grow to about 4 feet in length and weigh up to 30 lb; females are typically smaller. The Eurasian otter’s nose is among the smallest of the otter species and has a characteristic shape resembling a shallow ‘W’. An otter’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c76ef0b3-372b-4092-aa30-ad86ffea3290\">tail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, sometimes referred to as its rudder or stern, is stout at the base and tapers towards the tip, where it becomes flatter. It forms part of the animal’s propulsion system when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6f1ca9eb-086e-4893-b872-8772214de6ba\">swimming rapidly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"35842b60-c017-448e-8ed4-cbf505cc733e\">underwater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ef3743ac-4ee7-4d58-a758-0084c63ca955\">Otter fur<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> consists of two types of hair: stout guard hairs, which form <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3158234d-54fa-40c0-898c-69b16047082f\">a waterproof outer covering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, and dense, fine underfur, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5abe13c5-e431-4db7-8517-71711a7cb441\">which provides insulation and helps retain body heat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ef3743ac-4ee7-4d58-a758-0084c63ca955\">The coat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> must be kept in good condition through regular grooming. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"bb79c492-4339-4623-9709-b8109697534d\">Seawater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"85a6987c-534c-4a54-8b3f-adc6675830a6\">reduces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3158234d-54fa-40c0-898c-69b16047082f\">its waterproofing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5abe13c5-e431-4db7-8517-71711a7cb441\">insulating qualities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> when it penetrates the fur. This is why freshwater pools are particularly important to otters living on the coast. After swimming in the sea, they wash their coats in these pools and then squirm on the ground, rubbing themselves dry against vegetation.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p><span>Otters use their sense of smell when hunting on land, communicating with one another and detecting danger. Their sense of smell is thought to be similar in sensitivity to that of dogs. Otters have small eyes and are probably short-sighted on land. However, they can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"909cc36a-9bab-4fcf-9339-5a104b7ef8e3\">alter the shape of the lens in the eye<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, making it more spherical and thereby <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"909cc36a-9bab-4fcf-9339-5a104b7ef8e3\">compensating for the refraction of light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b95928b5-3bce-4784-bf08-5e53326371e4\">in water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. In clear water and good light, they can therefore hunt fish by sight. The eyes and nostrils are positioned high on the head, allowing an otter to see and breathe while most of its body remains submerged. Underwater, it holds its legs close to the body except when steering, while the rear of the body moves in a series of vertical undulations. River otters have webbing extending along much of each digit, though not quite to the tips. Giant otters and sea otters have even more extensive webbing, whereas Asian short-clawed otters have almost none. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"128f4297-f65b-42ed-ab7e-6a1e0d8c2677\">They<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"17172786-1131-4ae0-a539-aea99c94d0ed\">hunt for shrimps in ditches and paddy fields<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, so they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"2a4a44c6-7c1b-44c9-9db9-66887c09a7c5\">do not need the same<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> swimming speed as species that pursue prey through open water. Otters’ ears are small for streamlining, but their hearing is highly sensitive. The ears are also protected by valves that close against water pressure.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p><span>A number of requirements and preferences limit the habitats suitable for otters. Water is essential, and rivers must be large enough to support a healthy population of fish. Because otters are shy and wary animals, they tend to prefer territories where human activity causes relatively little disturbance. There must also be no other otter already occupying the same territory, a factor that becomes increasingly important as populations recover. Coastal otters generally have a more abundant food supply, and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"3c3a79b2-f442-43eb-ac1b-ae4ce4a66ccb\">ranges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> of both males and females <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"3c3a79b2-f442-43eb-ac1b-ae4ce4a66ccb\">may extend for only a few kilometres<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> along the coast. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"7bf44e5b-3734-4d95-9106-fc033f7908ce\">A male’s range<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"27acd843-7b01-4efd-b52a-f290535aa95e\">may overlap<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"7bf44e5b-3734-4d95-9106-fc033f7908ce\">those of two or three females<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Otters will eat almost anything they can catch, and there are records of them consuming sparrows, snakes and slugs. Apart from fish, their most common prey includes crayfish, crabs and water birds. Small mammals are taken occasionally, most commonly rabbits but sometimes even moles.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p><span>Eurasian otters <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9985e49c-b09a-4be0-8cc5-cc83b1b2f461\">can breed at any time of year when<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"e7d737c0-09ed-447f-b972-93ded023ca64\">food is readily available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. In places where conditions are more severe, such as Sweden, where lakes remain frozen for much of the winter, cubs are generally born in spring. This ensures that they are well grown before severe weather returns. In the Shetland Islands, by contrast, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9985e49c-b09a-4be0-8cc5-cc83b1b2f461\">cubs are born in summer, when </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9985e49c-b09a-4be0-8cc5-cc83b1b2f461 e7d737c0-09ed-447f-b972-93ded023ca64\">fish are more abundant</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. Although otters are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4e7e61d6-f8f8-47d3-a423-303480ced6d9\">capable of breeding every year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4e7e61d6-f8f8-47d3-a423-303480ced6d9\">some do not<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"22dcbe8f-f982-4a4b-a05a-843bba063003\">Again<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4e7e61d6-f8f8-47d3-a423-303480ced6d9\">this<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"7d976dd2-54c2-4a4b-81e9-ab0d89677a69\">depends partly on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"e7d737c0-09ed-447f-b972-93ded023ca64\">food availability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. Other factors, such as the range of food available and the condition of the female, may also have an effect. Gestation in the Eurasian otter lasts about 63 days. By contrast, in </span><i><span>Lutra canadensis</span></i><span>, the embryos may undergo delayed implantation.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p><span>Otters normally give birth in secure dens where there is little risk of disturbance. Nests are lined with bedding such as reeds, waterside plants and grass to keep the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a59c64c6-6df9-4155-b86e-62cca3810440\">cubs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> warm while the mother is away feeding. Litter size varies from one to five <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"61bf02af-0302-487f-afeb-81bfa715b566\">cubs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. For reasons that are not fully understood, coastal otters tend to produce smaller litters. At about five weeks, when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a59c64c6-6df9-4155-b86e-62cca3810440\">a cub<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> weighs around 700 g, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c634be51-f653-4c75-9a12-5acbd74819a5\">its eyes open<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. At seven weeks, cubs <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5 8\" data-uid=\"c634be51-f653-4c75-9a12-5acbd74819a5 cd08110e-6c52-432b-8570-2cd9f3f21666\">begin to be weaned onto solid food</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. At ten weeks, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"61bf02af-0302-487f-afeb-81bfa715b566\">they<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c634be51-f653-4c75-9a12-5acbd74819a5\">leave the nest and encounter daylight for the first time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. By around three months, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c634be51-f653-4c75-9a12-5acbd74819a5\">enter the water and begin learning to swim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. At eight months, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c634be51-f653-4c75-9a12-5acbd74819a5\">are able to hunt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, although <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"f108db4a-d7b4-4c70-8d24-b77fde66d387\">the mother still supplies a considerable amount of food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. By about nine months, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a59c64c6-6df9-4155-b86e-62cca3810440\">the young<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c634be51-f653-4c75-9a12-5acbd74819a5\">sufficiently independent for the mother to drive them away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"96f608c9-8abf-40be-a7b6-e60daa746c12\">The decline of the British otter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> was recognised in the early 1960s, although its principal cause was not identified until the late 1970s. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"82fe95b6-819d-471a-a557-f7c8d0b2a5d5\">Pesticides such as dieldrin and aldrin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> had first been introduced in 1955 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"82fe95b6-819d-471a-a557-f7c8d0b2a5d5\">for use in agriculture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and other industries. These chemicals are highly persistent and had already been linked to major declines in populations of peregrine falcons, sparrowhawks and other predators. The pesticides <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"7de0f05c-c80b-4393-9442-bd2f960133f6\">entered river systems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"7de0f05c-c80b-4393-9442-bd2f960133f6\">passed through the food chain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, from micro-organisms to fish and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"7de0f05c-c80b-4393-9442-bd2f960133f6\">finally to otters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, with the concentration of the chemicals increasing at each stage. From 1962, these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"7ceb4982-c99f-45fe-8d7d-78ef52048319\">pesticides were gradually phased out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. However, although some affected species recovered quickly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"96f608c9-8abf-40be-a7b6-e60daa746c12\">otter numbers did not and continued to fall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> into the 1980s. This was probably due mainly to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"520b96f4-6d7e-41ae-8a12-1668215da778\">habitat destruction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"0d40a14c-a31e-4f79-9614-f820e38209e5\">deaths on roads<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Because otter populations had already been fragmented by the severe decline of the 1950s and 1960s, the loss of even a small number of animals in one area could make an entire local population unviable and lead to its disappearance.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b></p><p><span>Otter numbers have been recovering across Britain. Populations have grown in the few areas where they survived and have expanded from these centres into other parts of the country. This recovery is due largely to legislation, conservation measures, efforts to slow and reverse the destruction of suitable habitat, and the reintroduction of captive-bred animals. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"80de1a9d-4b96-4fcd-bd26-4e9dc94a9d2e\">Releasing captive-bred otters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> is regarded by many conservationists as a last resort. The argument is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c\">where suitable habitat does not exist, released animals will not survive, while where appropriate habitat is available, natural populations should eventually be able to expand into the area without assistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c\">However, </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 10\" data-uid=\"70c369d1-1cf2-418d-b3a7-76c5b24656c5 80de1a9d-4b96-4fcd-bd26-4e9dc94a9d2e c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c\">introducing animals</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c\"> into </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 10\" data-uid=\"41f3d00d-5b16-4e13-b436-a756a8906b88 c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c\">a fragmented and fragile population</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c\"> may </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 10\" data-uid=\"3422bd72-ca5f-4d4a-adb5-b00f41f7cca4 c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c\">provide enough additional support</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> for it to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 10\" data-uid=\"3422bd72-ca5f-4d4a-adb5-b00f41f7cca4 dc083590-6372-4b16-8c07-418a5a6b244d\">stabilise and expand rather than disappear</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. This was the approach taken by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c4b312b6-c68d-400f-8abc-dcabf326eadb\">the Otter Trust in Norfolk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"41f3d00d-5b16-4e13-b436-a756a8906b88\">the otter population may have fallen to as few as twenty animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> at the beginning of the 1980s. The Otter Trust eventually ended its captive-breeding programme altogether—a positive development because it indicated that such intervention was no longer considered necessary.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–G, in boxes 1–6 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>NB</span></b><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326279\" id=\"question-wrapper-326279\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A description of how otters <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"909cc36a-9bab-4fcf-9339-5a104b7ef8e3\">adjust their vision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b95928b5-3bce-4784-bf08-5e53326371e4\">underwater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326280\" id=\"question-wrapper-326280\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c76ef0b3-372b-4092-aa30-ad86ffea3290\">Physical characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> that help otters <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6f1ca9eb-086e-4893-b872-8772214de6ba\">move effectively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"35842b60-c017-448e-8ed4-cbf505cc733e\">certain environments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326281\" id=\"question-wrapper-326281\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>An explanation of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"82fe95b6-819d-471a-a557-f7c8d0b2a5d5\">agricultural practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"7de0f05c-c80b-4393-9442-bd2f960133f6\">contributed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"96f608c9-8abf-40be-a7b6-e60daa746c12\">a decline in otter numbers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326282\" id=\"question-wrapper-326282\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>An explanation of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"7bf44e5b-3734-4d95-9106-fc033f7908ce\">the territories of different otters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"27acd843-7b01-4efd-b52a-f290535aa95e\">may intersect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326283\" id=\"question-wrapper-326283\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A description of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a59c64c6-6df9-4155-b86e-62cca3810440\">otter cubs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c634be51-f653-4c75-9a12-5acbd74819a5\">develop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326284\" id=\"question-wrapper-326284\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c\">Different views<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"80de1a9d-4b96-4fcd-bd26-4e9dc94a9d2e\">one method<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"dc083590-6372-4b16-8c07-418a5a6b244d\">restoring otter populations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><b><span>TRUE</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><b><span>FALSE</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b><span> if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326285\" id=\"question-wrapper-326285\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"e7d737c0-09ed-447f-b972-93ded023ca64\">Food supply<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"7d976dd2-54c2-4a4b-81e9-ab0d89677a69\">influences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"22dcbe8f-f982-4a4b-a05a-843bba063003\">both<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9985e49c-b09a-4be0-8cc5-cc83b1b2f461\">when otters give birth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4e7e61d6-f8f8-47d3-a423-303480ced6d9\">how frequently they reproduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326286\" id=\"question-wrapper-326286\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"61bf02af-0302-487f-afeb-81bfa715b566\">Otter cubs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"f108db4a-d7b4-4c70-8d24-b77fde66d387\">stop receiving food from their mother<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> when they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"cd08110e-6c52-432b-8570-2cd9f3f21666\">start eating solid food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326287\" id=\"question-wrapper-326287\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>After <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"7ceb4982-c99f-45fe-8d7d-78ef52048319\">pesticides were withdrawn from use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"0d40a14c-a31e-4f79-9614-f820e38209e5\">road deaths<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> posed a greater threat to otters than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"520b96f4-6d7e-41ae-8a12-1668215da778\">the loss of their habitat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326288\" id=\"question-wrapper-326288\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c4b312b6-c68d-400f-8abc-dcabf326eadb\">The Otter Trust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"70c369d1-1cf2-418d-b3a7-76c5b24656c5\">released captive-bred otters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c4b312b6-c68d-400f-8abc-dcabf326eadb\">in Norfolk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"3422bd72-ca5f-4d4a-adb5-b00f41f7cca4\">to strengthen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"41f3d00d-5b16-4e13-b436-a756a8906b88\">a surviving wild population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326289\" id=\"question-wrapper-326289\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"bb79c492-4339-4623-9709-b8109697534d\">substance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> can make <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ef3743ac-4ee7-4d58-a758-0084c63ca955\">an otter’s coat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"85a6987c-534c-4a54-8b3f-adc6675830a6\">less<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3158234d-54fa-40c0-898c-69b16047082f\">waterproof<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"85a6987c-534c-4a54-8b3f-adc6675830a6\">less effective at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"5abe13c5-e431-4db7-8517-71711a7cb441\">keeping it warm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SEAWATER</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326290\" id=\"question-wrapper-326290\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which aspect of swimming is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"2a4a44c6-7c1b-44c9-9db9-66887c09a7c5\">less important<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"128f4297-f65b-42ed-ab7e-6a1e0d8c2677\">Asian short-clawed otters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"17172786-1131-4ae0-a539-aea99c94d0ed\">because of where they hunt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SWIMMING SPEED</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326291\" id=\"question-wrapper-326291\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which type of otter may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"3c3a79b2-f442-43eb-ac1b-ae4ce4a66ccb\">occupy a relatively small stretch of habitat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COASTAL OTTERS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c76ef0b3-372b-4092-aa30-ad86ffea3290","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Physical characteristics","passagePhrase":"long, slender bodies and short legs ... tail"},{"uid":"6f1ca9eb-086e-4893-b872-8772214de6ba","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"move effectively","passagePhrase":"pushing through ... swimming rapidly"},{"uid":"35842b60-c017-448e-8ed4-cbf505cc733e","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"certain environments","passagePhrase":"dense undergrowth and hunting in tunnels ... underwater"},{"uid":"ef3743ac-4ee7-4d58-a758-0084c63ca955","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"an otter’s coat","passagePhrase":"Otter fur ... The coat"},{"uid":"3158234d-54fa-40c0-898c-69b16047082f","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"waterproof","passagePhrase":"a waterproof outer covering ... its waterproofing"},{"uid":"5abe13c5-e431-4db7-8517-71711a7cb441","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"keeping it warm","passagePhrase":"which provides insulation and helps retain body heat ... insulating qualities"},{"uid":"bb79c492-4339-4623-9709-b8109697534d","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"substance","passagePhrase":"Seawater"},{"uid":"85a6987c-534c-4a54-8b3f-adc6675830a6","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"less ... less effective at","passagePhrase":"reduces"},{"uid":"909cc36a-9bab-4fcf-9339-5a104b7ef8e3","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"adjust their vision","passagePhrase":"alter the shape of the lens in the eye ... compensating for the refraction of light"},{"uid":"b95928b5-3bce-4784-bf08-5e53326371e4","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"underwater","passagePhrase":"in water"},{"uid":"128f4297-f65b-42ed-ab7e-6a1e0d8c2677","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Asian short-clawed otters","passagePhrase":"They"},{"uid":"17172786-1131-4ae0-a539-aea99c94d0ed","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"because of where they hunt","passagePhrase":"hunt for shrimps in ditches and paddy fields"},{"uid":"2a4a44c6-7c1b-44c9-9db9-66887c09a7c5","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"less important","passagePhrase":"do not need the same"},{"uid":"3c3a79b2-f442-43eb-ac1b-ae4ce4a66ccb","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"occupy a relatively small stretch of habitat","passagePhrase":"ranges ... may extend for only a few kilometres"},{"uid":"7bf44e5b-3734-4d95-9106-fc033f7908ce","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"the territories of different otters","passagePhrase":"A male’s range ... those of two or three females"},{"uid":"27acd843-7b01-4efd-b52a-f290535aa95e","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"may intersect","passagePhrase":"may overlap"},{"uid":"9985e49c-b09a-4be0-8cc5-cc83b1b2f461","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"when otters give birth","passagePhrase":"can breed at any time of year when ... cubs are born in summer, when"},{"uid":"e7d737c0-09ed-447f-b972-93ded023ca64","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Food supply","passagePhrase":"food is readily available ... food availability"},{"uid":"9985e49c-b09a-4be0-8cc5-cc83b1b2f461 e7d737c0-09ed-447f-b972-93ded023ca64","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fish are more abundant"},{"uid":"4e7e61d6-f8f8-47d3-a423-303480ced6d9","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"how frequently they reproduce","passagePhrase":"capable of breeding every year ... some do not ... this"},{"uid":"22dcbe8f-f982-4a4b-a05a-843bba063003","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"both","passagePhrase":"Again"},{"uid":"7d976dd2-54c2-4a4b-81e9-ab0d89677a69","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"influences","passagePhrase":"depends partly on"},{"uid":"a59c64c6-6df9-4155-b86e-62cca3810440","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"otter cubs","passagePhrase":"cubs ... a cub ... the young"},{"uid":"61bf02af-0302-487f-afeb-81bfa715b566","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Otter cubs","passagePhrase":"cubs ... they"},{"uid":"c634be51-f653-4c75-9a12-5acbd74819a5","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"develop","passagePhrase":"its eyes open ... leave the nest and encounter daylight for the first time ... enter the water and begin learning to swim ... are able to hunt ... sufficiently independent for the mother to drive them away"},{"uid":"c634be51-f653-4c75-9a12-5acbd74819a5 cd08110e-6c52-432b-8570-2cd9f3f21666","qNum":"5 8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"begin to be weaned onto solid food"},{"uid":"96f608c9-8abf-40be-a7b6-e60daa746c12","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"a decline in otter numbers","passagePhrase":"The decline of the British otter ... otter numbers did not and continued to fall"},{"uid":"82fe95b6-819d-471a-a557-f7c8d0b2a5d5","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"agricultural practices","passagePhrase":"Pesticides such as dieldrin and aldrin ... for use in agriculture"},{"uid":"7de0f05c-c80b-4393-9442-bd2f960133f6","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"contributed to","passagePhrase":"entered river systems ... passed through the food chain ... finally to otters"},{"uid":"7ceb4982-c99f-45fe-8d7d-78ef52048319","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"pesticides were withdrawn from use","passagePhrase":"pesticides were gradually phased out"},{"uid":"520b96f4-6d7e-41ae-8a12-1668215da778","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"the loss of their habitat","passagePhrase":"habitat destruction"},{"uid":"0d40a14c-a31e-4f79-9614-f820e38209e5","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"road deaths","passagePhrase":"deaths on roads"},{"uid":"80de1a9d-4b96-4fcd-bd26-4e9dc94a9d2e","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"one method","passagePhrase":"Releasing captive-bred otters"},{"uid":"c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Different views","passagePhrase":"where suitable habitat does not exist, released animals will not survive, while where appropriate habitat is available, natural populations should eventually be able to expand into the area without assistance ... However, ... into ... may"},{"uid":"70c369d1-1cf2-418d-b3a7-76c5b24656c5 80de1a9d-4b96-4fcd-bd26-4e9dc94a9d2e c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c","qNum":"6 10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"introducing animals"},{"uid":"41f3d00d-5b16-4e13-b436-a756a8906b88 c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c","qNum":"6 10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a fragmented and fragile population"},{"uid":"3422bd72-ca5f-4d4a-adb5-b00f41f7cca4 c531c23a-6c15-456a-bf99-0a495d67652c","qNum":"6 10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"provide enough additional support"},{"uid":"3422bd72-ca5f-4d4a-adb5-b00f41f7cca4 dc083590-6372-4b16-8c07-418a5a6b244d","qNum":"6 10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"stabilise and expand rather than disappear"},{"uid":"c4b312b6-c68d-400f-8abc-dcabf326eadb","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"The Otter Trust ... in Norfolk","passagePhrase":"the Otter Trust in Norfolk"},{"uid":"41f3d00d-5b16-4e13-b436-a756a8906b88","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"a surviving wild population","passagePhrase":"the otter population may have fallen to as few as twenty animals"},{"uid":"dc083590-6372-4b16-8c07-418a5a6b244d","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"restoring otter populations","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"cd08110e-6c52-432b-8570-2cd9f3f21666","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"start eating solid food","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"70c369d1-1cf2-418d-b3a7-76c5b24656c5","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"released captive-bred otters","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"3422bd72-ca5f-4d4a-adb5-b00f41f7cca4","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"to strengthen","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_104":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Follow Your Nose</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p><span>At the time of the research, aromatherapy was the most widely used complementary therapy in the National Health Service and was most commonly used in the treatment of dementia. For elderly patients who have difficulty interacting verbally and to whom conventional medicine has little to offer, aromatherapy can bring benefits in terms of better sleep, improved motivation and less disturbed behaviour. At least, that is the assumption. However, a systematic review of healthcare databases found almost no evidence that aromatherapy is effective in the treatment of dementia. Other findings suggest that aromatherapy may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"daed875e-bd9f-498e-a59b-898a80f0d6b3\">effective only when patients believe that it will work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. In fact, the only research that has unequivocally shown it to have an effect has been carried out on animals.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"14\"><span>Behavioural studies have consistently shown that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"65440b7e-3266-48d6-9532-24c79b8ad50b\">odours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> elicit emotional memories far more readily than other sensory cues. Rachel Herz, of Brown University in Providence, Rhode Island, and her colleagues used functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI) to examine brain activity associated with this effect. They scanned the brains of five women while the participants either <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"158d29ff-b652-4425-b62c-9f41deb2669e\">looked at a photograph<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of a bottle of perfume that evoked a pleasant memory for them or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"65440b7e-3266-48d6-9532-24c79b8ad50b\">smelled the perfume itself<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. One woman, for instance, recalled that as a child living in Paris, she would watch with excitement as her mother dressed to go out and sprayed herself with the perfume. The women described the perfume as far more evocative than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"158d29ff-b652-4425-b62c-9f41deb2669e\">the photograph<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, and Herz and her colleagues found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"65440b7e-3266-48d6-9532-24c79b8ad50b\">the scent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"380429ec-e160-493c-8466-9d378eb49525\">activated the amygdala and other brain regions associated with emotion processing far more strongly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> than the photograph. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"65440b7e-3266-48d6-9532-24c79b8ad50b\">the odour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"af05b215-0282-4c93-88d9-dab43507f760\">did not enable the women to recall their memories in any greater detail or with greater clarity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> than the photograph did. “<span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"af05b215-0282-4c93-88d9-dab43507f760\">People </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"14 24\" data-uid=\"af05b215-0282-4c93-88d9-dab43507f760 cfc9d4f3-83ef-42db-bb30-69cd8e5718d7\">don’t remember any more detail</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"af05b215-0282-4c93-88d9-dab43507f760\"> or with any more clarity when the memory is recalled with an odour</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>,” Herz says. “However, with the odour, you have this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"c110783f-6a0c-430e-9442-cc47f1929abe\">intense emotional feeling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> that’s really visceral.”</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"15\"><span>This is hardly surprising, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"7dc3ead5-af33-4fc7-b80d-66bd52363871\">Herz argues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"28d0a896-87a1-409e-91a8-2f5a7811323a\">given how the brain has evolved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. “The way I like to think about it is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"79e12e6f-7a8c-4c50-9954-80055a828e91\">emotion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"f1f4f27b-40d3-4b98-a519-a43fef04d2b2\">olfaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"c4612b84-e4a1-4257-80d6-c52f7d85acd0\">are essentially the same things<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>,” <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"7dc3ead5-af33-4fc7-b80d-66bd52363871\">she says<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. “<span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 26\" data-uid=\"79e12e6f-7a8c-4c50-9954-80055a828e91 bb27893b-84b9-4166-83bf-b1d8d4e81705\">The part of the brain that controls emotion</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 26\" data-uid=\"28d0a896-87a1-409e-91a8-2f5a7811323a e403b95e-0d8a-4287-97a8-4521286f6f6e\">literally grew out of</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 26\" data-uid=\"f1f4f27b-40d3-4b98-a519-a43fef04d2b2 fd801fea-a618-4028-8ec4-2ddb0adaa665\">the part of the brain that controls smell</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.” <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"7dc3ead5-af33-4fc7-b80d-66bd52363871\">She suggests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> that this may explain why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"60432eef-6c56-4146-9c42-153e9403a27c\">memories associated with emotionally powerful odours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"91ffd943-1598-4d27-8438-a039c492dc41\">become so deeply entrenched<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"f1f4f27b-40d3-4b98-a519-a43fef04d2b2\">Smell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"28d0a896-87a1-409e-91a8-2f5a7811323a\">originally served a survival function<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, signalling whether something should be approached or avoided.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"16\"><span>Eric Vermetten, a psychiatrist at the University of Utrecht in the Netherlands, says that doctors have long known about the potential of smells to act as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"a550a0bd-b53d-4514-8db2-f271a75871a4\">traumatic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"fbc74ed3-f87b-4db5-bf2a-163b802afbfa\">reminders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, although the evidence has been largely anecdotal. Vermetten and his colleagues attempted to document this effect by describing three cases of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"a550a0bd-b53d-4514-8db2-f271a75871a4\">post-traumatic stress disorder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> (PTSD) in which patients reported either that a particular smell <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"fbc74ed3-f87b-4db5-bf2a-163b802afbfa\">triggered their flashbacks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> or that smell was a feature of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"a550a0bd-b53d-4514-8db2-f271a75871a4\">the flashback itself<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. The researchers concluded that odours could be used in exposure therapy or to recondition patients’ fear responses.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"17\"><span>After Vermetten presented his findings at a conference, doctors in the audience described ways in which they had attempted to use this association therapeutically. PTSD patients often undergo group therapy, but the therapy itself can expose them to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"08500f3d-a211-46af-aebb-2b0acdb9d887\">traumatic reminders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. “Some clinicians put a strip of vanilla or a strong, pleasant, everyday odorant such as coffee under their patients’ noses, so that they have this continuous olfactory stimulation,” says Vermetten. With this continuous pleasant olfactory stimulus, patients <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c956b060-46b8-461d-8c2c-4fd38a3794e5\">appear to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1c4a35b9-e9a4-4ff7-858e-538038f5511d\">better protected against<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"08500f3d-a211-46af-aebb-2b0acdb9d887\">flashbacks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c956b060-46b8-461d-8c2c-4fd38a3794e5\">The evidence is purely anecdotal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, and nobody knows what is happening in the brain, Vermetten says. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c956b060-46b8-461d-8c2c-4fd38a3794e5\">it is possible that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> the neural pathways through which the odour evokes a pleasant everyday memory <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 22\" data-uid=\"1c4a35b9-e9a4-4ff7-858e-538038f5511d 1d8f601c-81fb-40e7-85db-822c31671de3\">override</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1c4a35b9-e9a4-4ff7-858e-538038f5511d\"> the </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 22\" data-uid=\"1c4a35b9-e9a4-4ff7-858e-538038f5511d 2aa3e394-ba55-4ace-a243-0061d45daec7\">fear-conditioned neural pathways</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that respond to verbal cues.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"18\"><span>According to Herz, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"122fb77b-3816-437e-afa2-3875c83f6213\">therapeutic potential of odours could lie in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"f02f7fc3-07cd-4dd0-ba90-c784523b84ad\">their very unreliability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Her perfume-bottle experiment showed that odours <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"1e231e9b-ecf2-4bac-b2da-d5c4a140b41c\">do not produce more accurate or detailed recall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, even when the memories they evoke feel more real. Research also shows that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"f02f7fc3-07cd-4dd0-ba90-c784523b84ad\">smell can be influenced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> because, as predominantly visual and verbal creatures, we tend to place greater trust in visual and verbal information. In 2001, for instance, Gil Morrot, of the National Institute for Agronomic Research in Montpellier, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"fdc4054f-9756-43b6-9220-83fc45e6cda9\">tricked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> 54 oenology students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"fdc4054f-9756-43b6-9220-83fc45e6cda9\">by secretly colouring a white wine with an odourless red dye<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> just before they were asked to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 23\" data-uid=\"8645cbc2-74f7-47f1-8153-cb5cf495c66b fd7efa30-d3c6-4749-946f-c4a043b71e91\">describe the odours</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of a range of red and white wines. The students described the coloured wine using terms typically reserved for red wines. They also used terms referring to the wine’s redness and darkness—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"fd7efa30-d3c6-4749-946f-c4a043b71e91\">visual rather than olfactory qualities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Smell, the researchers concluded, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"eefd9a10-d43f-43e2-9792-fca1cd4c840f\">cannot be separated from the other senses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"19\"><span>In a later experiment, Jay Gottfried and Ray Dolan of the Wellcome Department of Imaging Neuroscience in London investigated how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0c43abc6-d1ac-4c53-a2f2-c81dabf21a3e\">visual information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> affected the recognition of odours. They measured how quickly participants could identify <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb 0c43abc6-d1ac-4c53-a2f2-c81dabf21a3e\">an odour</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb\"> when it was accompanied either by a semantically related image or by an unrelated one</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, while their brains were scanned using fMRI. Participants might, for example, smell vanilla while seeing either a picture of ice cream or one of cheese. Participants <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"19 21\" data-uid=\"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7 ab95d877-671c-47d9-aa43-0262964df321\">identified the odours more quickly</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7\"> when </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"19 21\" data-uid=\"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7 8b7a97d0-dcda-4cbf-bb0b-838c7b9744e8\">the accompanying image was semantically related to the smell</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. When this occurred, a structure called <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb\">the hippocampus was strongly activated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. The researchers interpreted this as evidence that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"26cd4397-0cde-4cd4-a79c-cef727bdace1\">the hippocampus helps integrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0c43abc6-d1ac-4c53-a2f2-c81dabf21a3e\">information from different senses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"26cd4397-0cde-4cd4-a79c-cef727bdace1\">which the brain then uses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> to determine what it is perceiving.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-G.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Example</span></b></p><p><span>Paragraph A — ix</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"14 18\" data-uid=\"1e231e9b-ecf2-4bac-b2da-d5c4a140b41c af05b215-0282-4c93-88d9-dab43507f760\">Remembering the past more clearly</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\">ii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"fbc74ed3-f87b-4db5-bf2a-163b802afbfa\">Bringing back<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"a550a0bd-b53d-4514-8db2-f271a75871a4\">painful memories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\">iii. The <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"28d0a896-87a1-409e-91a8-2f5a7811323a\">evolutionary </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"28d0a896-87a1-409e-91a8-2f5a7811323a c4612b84-e4a1-4257-80d6-c52f7d85acd0\">link</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"c4612b84-e4a1-4257-80d6-c52f7d85acd0\"> between </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"c4612b84-e4a1-4257-80d6-c52f7d85acd0 f1f4f27b-40d3-4b98-a519-a43fef04d2b2\">smell</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"c4612b84-e4a1-4257-80d6-c52f7d85acd0\"> and </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"79e12e6f-7a8c-4c50-9954-80055a828e91 c4612b84-e4a1-4257-80d6-c52f7d85acd0\">emotion</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\">iv. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"14 19\" data-uid=\"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb 380429ec-e160-493c-8466-9d378eb49525\">Different brain responses</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb\"> to </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"14 19\" data-uid=\"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb 65440b7e-3266-48d6-9532-24c79b8ad50b\">scent</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb\"> and </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"14 19\" data-uid=\"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb 158d29ff-b652-4425-b62c-9f41deb2669e\">image</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\">v. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7\">The </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"18 19\" data-uid=\"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7 f02f7fc3-07cd-4dd0-ba90-c784523b84ad\">unreliability</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7\"> of </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"18 19\" data-uid=\"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7 fd7efa30-d3c6-4749-946f-c4a043b71e91\">smell perception</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\">vi. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"18 19\" data-uid=\"26cd4397-0cde-4cd4-a79c-cef727bdace1 eefd9a10-d43f-43e2-9792-fca1cd4c840f\">How the brain combines</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"eefd9a10-d43f-43e2-9792-fca1cd4c840f\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"18 19\" data-uid=\"0c43abc6-d1ac-4c53-a2f2-c81dabf21a3e eefd9a10-d43f-43e2-9792-fca1cd4c840f\">information from different senses</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\">vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c956b060-46b8-461d-8c2c-4fd38a3794e5\">Possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"1c4a35b9-e9a4-4ff7-858e-538038f5511d\">protection against<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"08500f3d-a211-46af-aebb-2b0acdb9d887\">reliving the past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\">viii. A therapeutic effect confirmed by brain scans</p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\">ix. Doubts about a widely used therapy</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326292\" id=\"question-wrapper-326292\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p> Paragraph B</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326293\" id=\"question-wrapper-326293\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p> Paragraph C</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326294\" id=\"question-wrapper-326294\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p> Paragraph D</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326295\" id=\"question-wrapper-326295\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p> Paragraph E</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326296\" id=\"question-wrapper-326296\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p> Paragraph F</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326297\" id=\"question-wrapper-326297\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p> Paragraph G</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p> </p><p>Look at the following statements and the list of researchers below.</p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct researcher, A-D.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>NB</span></b><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Researchers</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Rachel Herz</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\">B. Eric Vermetten</p><p data-pool-key=\"C\">C. Gil Morrot</p><p data-pool-key=\"D\">D. Jay Gottfried and Ray Dolan</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326298\" id=\"question-wrapper-326298\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>The unreliability of smell may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"122fb77b-3816-437e-afa2-3875c83f6213\">contribute to its therapeutic potential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326299\" id=\"question-wrapper-326299\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"8b7a97d0-dcda-4cbf-bb0b-838c7b9744e8\">Consistency between visual and olfactory information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ab95d877-671c-47d9-aa43-0262964df321\">improve the speed of odour recognition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326300\" id=\"question-wrapper-326300\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>Pleasant smells might be used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"1d8f601c-81fb-40e7-85db-822c31671de3\">disrupt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"2aa3e394-ba55-4ace-a243-0061d45daec7\">brain processes associated with fear responses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326301\" id=\"question-wrapper-326301\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>People's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"8645cbc2-74f7-47f1-8153-cb5cf495c66b\">judgements about smells<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"fdc4054f-9756-43b6-9220-83fc45e6cda9\">influenced by information that is not itself related to smell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326302\" id=\"question-wrapper-326302\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>A memory triggered by smell may have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"c110783f-6a0c-430e-9442-cc47f1929abe\">stronger emotional impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"cfc9d4f3-83ef-42db-bb30-69cd8e5718d7\">without being recalled in greater detail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p> </p><p>Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 25 and 26 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326303\" id=\"question-wrapper-326303\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>What do some findings suggest about the effectiveness of aromatherapy?</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is greatest among patients with dementia.</li> <li>B. It may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"daed875e-bd9f-498e-a59b-898a80f0d6b3\">influenced by whether patients believe in its effectiveness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</li> <li>C. It increases when conventional medicine is ineffective.</li> <li>D. It has been demonstrated more clearly in humans than in animals.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326304\" id=\"question-wrapper-326304\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"7dc3ead5-af33-4fc7-b80d-66bd52363871\">According to Rachel Herz<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, why might <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"60432eef-6c56-4146-9c42-153e9403a27c\">memories associated with emotionally powerful smells<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"91ffd943-1598-4d27-8438-a039c492dc41\">become deeply established<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>?</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"bb27893b-84b9-4166-83bf-b1d8d4e81705\">The brain system responsible for emotion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e403b95e-0d8a-4287-97a8-4521286f6f6e\">developed from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"fd801fea-a618-4028-8ec4-2ddb0adaa665\">the system involved in processing smells<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Smells enable people to remember past events in greater detail than visual images do.</li> <li>C. Memories associated with dangerous smells are more strongly retained than other types of memories.</li> <li>D. Humans have gradually come to depend more heavily on smell than on visual and verbal information.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"daed875e-bd9f-498e-a59b-898a80f0d6b3","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"influenced by whether patients believe in its effectiveness","passagePhrase":"effective only when patients believe that it will work"},{"uid":"65440b7e-3266-48d6-9532-24c79b8ad50b","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"odours ... smelled the perfume itself ... the scent ... the odour"},{"uid":"158d29ff-b652-4425-b62c-9f41deb2669e","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"looked at a photograph ... the photograph"},{"uid":"380429ec-e160-493c-8466-9d378eb49525","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"activated the amygdala and other brain regions associated with emotion processing far more strongly"},{"uid":"af05b215-0282-4c93-88d9-dab43507f760 cfc9d4f3-83ef-42db-bb30-69cd8e5718d7","qNum":"14 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"don’t remember any more detail"},{"uid":"c110783f-6a0c-430e-9442-cc47f1929abe","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"stronger emotional impact","passagePhrase":"intense emotional feeling"},{"uid":"7dc3ead5-af33-4fc7-b80d-66bd52363871","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"According to Rachel Herz","passagePhrase":"Herz argues ... she says ... She suggests"},{"uid":"28d0a896-87a1-409e-91a8-2f5a7811323a","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"evolutionary","passagePhrase":"given how the brain has evolved ... originally served a survival function"},{"uid":"79e12e6f-7a8c-4c50-9954-80055a828e91","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"emotion"},{"uid":"f1f4f27b-40d3-4b98-a519-a43fef04d2b2","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"olfaction ... Smell"},{"uid":"c4612b84-e4a1-4257-80d6-c52f7d85acd0","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"between ... and","passagePhrase":"are essentially the same things"},{"uid":"79e12e6f-7a8c-4c50-9954-80055a828e91 bb27893b-84b9-4166-83bf-b1d8d4e81705","qNum":"15 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The part of the brain that controls emotion"},{"uid":"28d0a896-87a1-409e-91a8-2f5a7811323a e403b95e-0d8a-4287-97a8-4521286f6f6e","qNum":"15 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"literally grew out of"},{"uid":"f1f4f27b-40d3-4b98-a519-a43fef04d2b2 fd801fea-a618-4028-8ec4-2ddb0adaa665","qNum":"15 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the part of the brain that controls smell"},{"uid":"60432eef-6c56-4146-9c42-153e9403a27c","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"memories associated with emotionally powerful smells","passagePhrase":"memories associated with emotionally powerful odours"},{"uid":"91ffd943-1598-4d27-8438-a039c492dc41","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"become deeply established","passagePhrase":"become so deeply entrenched"},{"uid":"a550a0bd-b53d-4514-8db2-f271a75871a4","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"painful memories","passagePhrase":"traumatic ... post-traumatic stress disorder ... the flashback itself"},{"uid":"fbc74ed3-f87b-4db5-bf2a-163b802afbfa","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Bringing back","passagePhrase":"reminders ... triggered their flashbacks"},{"uid":"08500f3d-a211-46af-aebb-2b0acdb9d887","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"reliving the past","passagePhrase":"traumatic reminders ... flashbacks"},{"uid":"c956b060-46b8-461d-8c2c-4fd38a3794e5","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Possible","passagePhrase":"appear to be ... The evidence is purely anecdotal ... it is possible that"},{"uid":"1c4a35b9-e9a4-4ff7-858e-538038f5511d","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"protection against","passagePhrase":"better protected against ... the"},{"uid":"1c4a35b9-e9a4-4ff7-858e-538038f5511d 1d8f601c-81fb-40e7-85db-822c31671de3","qNum":"17 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"override"},{"uid":"1c4a35b9-e9a4-4ff7-858e-538038f5511d 2aa3e394-ba55-4ace-a243-0061d45daec7","qNum":"17 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fear-conditioned neural pathways"},{"uid":"122fb77b-3816-437e-afa2-3875c83f6213","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"contribute to its therapeutic potential","passagePhrase":"therapeutic potential of odours could lie in"},{"uid":"f02f7fc3-07cd-4dd0-ba90-c784523b84ad","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"their very unreliability ... smell can be influenced"},{"uid":"fdc4054f-9756-43b6-9220-83fc45e6cda9","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"influenced by information that is not itself related to smell","passagePhrase":"tricked ... by secretly colouring a white wine with an odourless red dye"},{"uid":"8645cbc2-74f7-47f1-8153-cb5cf495c66b fd7efa30-d3c6-4749-946f-c4a043b71e91","qNum":"18 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"describe the odours"},{"uid":"fd7efa30-d3c6-4749-946f-c4a043b71e91","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"visual rather than olfactory qualities"},{"uid":"0c43abc6-d1ac-4c53-a2f2-c81dabf21a3e","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"visual information ... information from different senses"},{"uid":"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb 0c43abc6-d1ac-4c53-a2f2-c81dabf21a3e","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"an odour"},{"uid":"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7 ab95d877-671c-47d9-aa43-0262964df321","qNum":"19 21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"identified the odours more quickly"},{"uid":"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7 8b7a97d0-dcda-4cbf-bb0b-838c7b9744e8","qNum":"19 21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the accompanying image was semantically related to the smell"},{"uid":"26cd4397-0cde-4cd4-a79c-cef727bdace1","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the hippocampus helps integrate ... which the brain then uses"},{"uid":"28d0a896-87a1-409e-91a8-2f5a7811323a c4612b84-e4a1-4257-80d6-c52f7d85acd0","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"link","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"c4612b84-e4a1-4257-80d6-c52f7d85acd0 f1f4f27b-40d3-4b98-a519-a43fef04d2b2","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"smell","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"79e12e6f-7a8c-4c50-9954-80055a828e91 c4612b84-e4a1-4257-80d6-c52f7d85acd0","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"emotion","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb 380429ec-e160-493c-8466-9d378eb49525","qNum":"14 19","questionPhrase":"Different brain responses","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb 65440b7e-3266-48d6-9532-24c79b8ad50b","qNum":"14 19","questionPhrase":"scent","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"016bedce-0e48-4e2d-a4dd-69f2190dc6bb 158d29ff-b652-4425-b62c-9f41deb2669e","qNum":"14 19","questionPhrase":"image","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7 f02f7fc3-07cd-4dd0-ba90-c784523b84ad","qNum":"18 19","questionPhrase":"unreliability","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"821d4425-c1a7-4073-8732-565f1e3bdfc7 fd7efa30-d3c6-4749-946f-c4a043b71e91","qNum":"18 19","questionPhrase":"smell perception","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"26cd4397-0cde-4cd4-a79c-cef727bdace1 eefd9a10-d43f-43e2-9792-fca1cd4c840f","qNum":"18 19","questionPhrase":"How the brain combines","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"0c43abc6-d1ac-4c53-a2f2-c81dabf21a3e eefd9a10-d43f-43e2-9792-fca1cd4c840f","qNum":"18 19","questionPhrase":"information from different senses","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"8b7a97d0-dcda-4cbf-bb0b-838c7b9744e8","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Consistency between visual and olfactory information","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"ab95d877-671c-47d9-aa43-0262964df321","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"improve the speed of odour recognition","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"1d8f601c-81fb-40e7-85db-822c31671de3","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"disrupt","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"2aa3e394-ba55-4ace-a243-0061d45daec7","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"brain processes associated with fear responses","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"8645cbc2-74f7-47f1-8153-cb5cf495c66b","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"judgements about smells","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"cfc9d4f3-83ef-42db-bb30-69cd8e5718d7","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"without being recalled in greater detail","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"bb27893b-84b9-4166-83bf-b1d8d4e81705","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"The brain system responsible for emotion","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"e403b95e-0d8a-4287-97a8-4521286f6f6e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"developed from","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"fd801fea-a618-4028-8ec4-2ddb0adaa665","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"the system involved in processing smells","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_105":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>Grimm’s Fairy Tales</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p><span>The Brothers Grimm, Jacob and Wilhelm, named their story collection </span><i><span>Children’s and Household Tales</span></i><span> and published the first of its seven editions in Germany in 1812. The table of contents reads like an A-list of fairy-tale celebrities: Cinderella, Sleeping Beauty, Snow White, Little Red Riding Hood, Rapunzel, Rumpelstiltskin, Hansel and Gretel, and the Frog King. Drawn mostly from oral narratives, the 210 stories in the Grimms’ collection represent an anthology of fairy tales, animal fables, rustic farces and religious allegories that remain unrivalled to this day.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p><span>Such lasting fame would have shocked the humble Grimms. During their lifetimes, the collection sold modestly in Germany, at first only a few hundred copies a year. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97 e5a75cf4-535b-4fff-96f0-1d9a6bdb7e8a\">The early editions</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97\"> were not even </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"05f510f9-3012-48e8-aeb4-0d9e287e3897 5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97\">aimed at</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2c1c9997-c16b-4533-8e15-a30b095a0ba2 5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97\">children</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. The brothers initially refused to consider illustrations, and scholarly footnotes took up almost as much space as the tales themselves. Jacob and Wilhelm viewed themselves as patriotic folklorists, not as children’s entertainers. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"779041ac-1d54-4fb1-8100-235e1fa1591f\">began their work at a time when Germany had been overrun by the French under Napoleon<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"779041ac-1d54-4fb1-8100-235e1fa1591f\">who was intent on </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"1119f96d-6907-4bf9-913e-2b4b3ff30fb5 779041ac-1d54-4fb1-8100-235e1fa1591f\">suppressing local culture</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. As young, workaholic scholars, single and sharing a cramped flat, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"35744117-4131-4d59-9952-4fc7f1f9fd67\">the Brothers Grimm undertook the fairy-tale collection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> with the goal of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"1119f96d-6907-4bf9-913e-2b4b3ff30fb5\">preserving Germany’s endangered oral tradition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p><span>For much of the 19th century, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"499ed4de-f65a-48ab-bc40-fbc145847551\">teachers, parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"902df0b6-6c43-4fed-a325-0fb907f956ed\">religious figures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, particularly in the United States, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"4d1c1913-1a00-43ce-92f4-ea2dc2275fa6\">deplored the Grimms’ collection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> for its raw, uncivilised content. Offended adults <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"4d1c1913-1a00-43ce-92f4-ea2dc2275fa6\">objected to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the gruesome punishments inflicted on the stories’ villains. In the original “Snow White”, the evil stepmother is forced to dance in red-hot iron shoes until she falls down dead. Even today, some protective parents shy away from the Grimms’ tales because of their reputation for violence.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p><span>Despite its sometimes rocky reception, </span><i><span>Children’s and Household Tales</span></i><span> gradually took root with the public. The brothers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"3db19467-5197-4bf8-b54a-619ca11ed9a9\">had not foreseen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> that the appearance of their work would coincide with a great flowering of children’s literature in Europe. English publishers led the way, issuing high-quality picture books such as </span><i><span>Jack and the Beanstalk</span></i><span> and handsome folktale collections, all to satisfy a newly literate audience seeking virtuous material for the nursery. Once the Brothers Grimm recognised <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"eded577d-c230-4d0d-94b6-5470eb205129\">this </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30 33\" data-uid=\"3db19467-5197-4bf8-b54a-619ca11ed9a9 eded577d-c230-4d0d-94b6-5470eb205129\">new readership</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, they <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30 33\" data-uid=\"45362364-fc3d-4692-a956-7c997b0efab3 813ab3ad-bf81-4c98-9d3f-d75a50ed7121\">set about </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"30 33\" data-uid=\"45362364-fc3d-4692-a956-7c997b0efab3 813ab3ad-bf81-4c98-9d3f-d75a50ed7121 9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6\">refining and softening</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30 33\" data-uid=\"45362364-fc3d-4692-a956-7c997b0efab3 813ab3ad-bf81-4c98-9d3f-d75a50ed7121\"> their tales</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"1e9df7a1-eee0-4373-864a-32c932bffd6e\">had originated centuries earlier as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"33834b2c-d8a1-4c56-a530-e80c57f65bfb\">earthy peasant fare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. In the Grimms’ hands, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"30 34\" data-uid=\"9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6 eaca4d0b-cddb-4fed-9a1f-6466f6250110\">cruel mothers</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6\"> became nasty stepmothers</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"30 34\" data-uid=\"9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6 eaca4d0b-cddb-4fed-9a1f-6466f6250110\">unmarried lovers</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6\"> were made chaste</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6\">the </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"30 34\" data-uid=\"9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6 eaca4d0b-cddb-4fed-9a1f-6466f6250110\">incestuous father</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6\"> was recast as the devil</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p><span>During the 20th century, the Grimms’ fairy tales came to dominate the bookshelves of children’s bedrooms. The stories read like dreams come true: handsome lads and beautiful damsels, armed with magic, triumph over giants, witches and wild beasts. They outwit mean, selfish adults. Inevitably, the boy and girl fall in love and live happily ever after. Parents also keep reading because they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"6143b9e9-1fec-4db3-8fa7-81a2e4c8e125\">approve of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"033b1892-ad4f-48dd-9b79-ba35b6ed371f\">finger-wagging lessons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> inserted into the stories: keep your promises, don’t talk to strangers, work hard and obey your parents. According to the Grimms, the collection served as “a manual of manners”.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p><span>Altogether, some 40 people delivered tales to the Grimms. Many of the storytellers came to the Grimms’ house in Kassel. The brothers particularly welcomed the visits of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e5eb9a59-b1dd-44de-9381-e89ba31e10c9\">Dorothea Viehmann<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, a widow who walked to town to sell produce from her garden. An innkeeper’s daughter, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e5eb9a59-b1dd-44de-9381-e89ba31e10c9\">Viehmann<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> had grown up listening to stories from travellers on the road to Frankfurt. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8ba9d7b3-df25-4fd4-af18-a6a0f0f37d55\">Among her treasures was “Aschenputtel”—Cinderella<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Marie Hassenpflug, a 20-year-old friend of their sister Charlotte, came from a well-bred, French-speaking family. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"121abb4b-a92d-48b5-ba71-8a9268b7e284\">Marie’s wonderful stories </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"32 35\" data-uid=\"059d36a7-f8ef-4487-8eab-07b0aabaa079 121abb4b-a92d-48b5-ba71-8a9268b7e284\">blended</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"121abb4b-a92d-48b5-ba71-8a9268b7e284\"> motifs from the oral tradition and from </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"32 35\" data-uid=\"121abb4b-a92d-48b5-ba71-8a9268b7e284 282a5f5d-e58d-43b1-bd6e-d18cbed5f1d0 99e08a56-0dae-42c1-95b9-81a2a337f6b3\">Perrault’s influential 1697 book</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"99e08a56-0dae-42c1-95b9-81a2a337f6b3\">, </span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"99e08a56-0dae-42c1-95b9-81a2a337f6b3\">Tales of My Mother Goose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></i><span>, which contained elaborate versions of “Little Red Riding Hood”, “Snow White” and “Sleeping Beauty”, among others. Many of these had been adapted from earlier Italian tales.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b></p><p><span>Given that the origins of many of the Grimm fairy tales reach throughout Europe and into the Middle East and Asia, the question must be asked: How German are the Grimm tales? Very, says scholar Heinz Rolleke. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f0171460-66a6-458c-8d26-3bfb8fc8a9ac\">Love of the underdog, rustic simplicity and creative energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>—these are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"a93e5c49-6f12-4cd5-8534-543e19ceff76\">Teutonic traits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"133e385a-6d01-47df-a501-a7a112b222d2\">The coarse texture of life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"0693bbf8-6c40-42bf-ac40-75f010f3624e\">during medieval times in Germany<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, when many of the tales entered the oral tradition, also coloured the narratives. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"0693bbf8-6c40-42bf-ac40-75f010f3624e\">Throughout Europe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"0ab2baa4-528d-49e1-8e4f-57ce4f535c44\">children were often neglected and abandoned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, like Hansel and Gretel. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"cebb4165-0beb-4e89-8774-d7872a0f79b9\">Accused witches were burned at the stake<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, like the evil mother-in-law in “The Six Swans”. “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"cebb4165-0beb-4e89-8774-d7872a0f79b9\">The cruelty in the stories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"3d5506e3-c68e-469d-be03-37996c4672ea\">was not the Grimms’ fantasy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>,” Rolleke points out. “It reflected <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"133e385a-6d01-47df-a501-a7a112b222d2\">the law-and-order system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"0693bbf8-6c40-42bf-ac40-75f010f3624e\">the old times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.”</span></p><p><b><span>H</span></b></p><p><span>The editorial fingerprints left by the Grimms betray the specific values of 19th-century Christian, bourgeois German society. But that has not stopped the tales from being embraced by almost every culture and nationality in the world. What accounts for this widespread, enduring popularity? Bernhard Lauer points to the “universal style” of the writing: “You have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"78c3bb47-0ee8-4d90-8ca6-dca217f66a7d\">no concrete descriptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"221d862f-f260-4d59-b577-7ae0c2004a76\">the land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, or the clothes, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"221d862f-f260-4d59-b577-7ae0c2004a76\">the forest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"221d862f-f260-4d59-b577-7ae0c2004a76\">the castles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"c6132f99-5449-42f0-b906-9dd17ef10187\">It makes the stories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"78ae252b-c1da-422a-8dfd-76e8726fef53\">timeless and placeless<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.” “The tales <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"10ac4c45-4c5a-4ad3-91ec-e098a5d31ba7\">allow us to express our utopian longings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>,” says Jack Zipes of the University of Minnesota, whose 1987 translation of the complete fairy tales captures the rustic vigour of the original text. “They show <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0da6f5fa-d063-4c59-95a4-a278b80a37d2\">a striving for happiness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> that none of us knows but that we sense is possible. We can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"9d8b76a7-2fbd-4a97-b9b5-c03da530bdf4\">identify with the heroes of the tales<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> and become, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"10ac4c45-4c5a-4ad3-91ec-e098a5d31ba7\">in our minds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"443b9960-7eac-4a69-81d2-9b65855fa9b5\">the masters and mistresses of our own destinies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.”</span></p><p><b><span>I</span></b></p><p><span>Fairy tales provide a workout for the unconscious, psychoanalysts maintain. Bruno Bettelheim famously promoted the therapeutic value of the Grimms’ stories, calling fairy tales the “great comforters”. By <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2086bc01-55bb-4df4-9697-01daf4e207d1\">confronting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2d3e359f-4fed-4b4c-8a1f-eb340be375f4\">fears and phobias<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, symbolised by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2d3e359f-4fed-4b4c-8a1f-eb340be375f4\">witches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2d3e359f-4fed-4b4c-8a1f-eb340be375f4\">heartless stepmothers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2d3e359f-4fed-4b4c-8a1f-eb340be375f4\">hungry wolves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"0ba2c10e-8b5a-422c-a9c4-38f6c5f6d977\">children find they can<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"7521bd71-c8af-4f22-8237-761f504fa719\">master their anxieties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"0ba2c10e-8b5a-422c-a9c4-38f6c5f6d977\">Bettelheim’s theory continues to be hotly debated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. But most young readers are not interested in exercising their unconscious minds. The Grimm tales, in fact, please in an infinite number of ways. Something about them seems to mirror whatever moods or interests we bring to our reading of them. The flexibility of interpretation suits them for almost any time and any culture.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326305\" id=\"question-wrapper-326305\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2c1c9997-c16b-4533-8e15-a30b095a0ba2 5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97\">Children</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97\"> formed part of the </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"05f510f9-3012-48e8-aeb4-0d9e287e3897 5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97\">readership</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"05f510f9-3012-48e8-aeb4-0d9e287e3897\"> the Grimms had in mind</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"e5a75cf4-535b-4fff-96f0-1d9a6bdb7e8a\">when the collection first appeared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326306\" id=\"question-wrapper-326306\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"35744117-4131-4d59-9952-4fc7f1f9fd67\">The Grimms’ collecting project<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> was partly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"779041ac-1d54-4fb1-8100-235e1fa1591f\">a response to political circumstances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"1119f96d-6907-4bf9-913e-2b4b3ff30fb5\">threatened German oral culture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326307\" id=\"question-wrapper-326307\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"902df0b6-6c43-4fed-a325-0fb907f956ed\">Religious figures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"4d1c1913-1a00-43ce-92f4-ea2dc2275fa6\">objected to the collection's content more strongly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"499ed4de-f65a-48ab-bc40-fbc145847551\">teachers or parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> did.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326308\" id=\"question-wrapper-326308\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"813ab3ad-bf81-4c98-9d3f-d75a50ed7121\">In revising the tales<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"eded577d-c230-4d0d-94b6-5470eb205129\">the new readership<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, the Grimms <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6\">moved them closer to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"33834b2c-d8a1-4c56-a530-e80c57f65bfb\">the earthy peasant stories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"1e9df7a1-eee0-4373-864a-32c932bffd6e\">from which they had originated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326309\" id=\"question-wrapper-326309\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Parents <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"6143b9e9-1fec-4db3-8fa7-81a2e4c8e125\">value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> the tales partly for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"033b1892-ad4f-48dd-9b79-ba35b6ed371f\">reasons other than their fantasy elements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326310\" id=\"question-wrapper-326310\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e5eb9a59-b1dd-44de-9381-e89ba31e10c9\">Dorothea Viehmann's<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> telling of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"8ba9d7b3-df25-4fd4-af18-a6a0f0f37d55\">Cinderella<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"121abb4b-a92d-48b5-ba71-8a9268b7e284\">influenced by </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"121abb4b-a92d-48b5-ba71-8a9268b7e284 99e08a56-0dae-42c1-95b9-81a2a337f6b3\">Perrault</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"99e08a56-0dae-42c1-95b9-81a2a337f6b3\">'s collection</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter in boxes 33-35 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326311\" id=\"question-wrapper-326311\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does paragraph D suggest about the collection’s increasing popularity?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It resulted from publishers promoting the Grimms’ work as an alternative to English picture books.</li> <li>B. It was helped by the brothers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"45362364-fc3d-4692-a956-7c997b0efab3\">adapting their work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"3db19467-5197-4bf8-b54a-619ca11ed9a9\">readership they had not originally expected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</li> <li>C. It reflected a growing preference for traditional folk material in its unaltered form.</li> <li>D. It occurred as readers became less concerned about the moral content of children’s books.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326312\" id=\"question-wrapper-326312\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which description best reflects the changes made to the tales at the end of paragraph D?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They shifted blame for wrongdoing from family members to supernatural characters.</li> <li>B. They altered <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"eaca4d0b-cddb-4fed-9a1f-6466f6250110\">sensitive family and sexual content<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> to make the tales more acceptable to contemporary readers.</li> <li>C. They simplified events that might have been difficult for inexperienced readers to follow.</li> <li>D. They introduced clearer punishments to emphasise the consequences of bad behaviour.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326313\" id=\"question-wrapper-326313\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the example of Marie Hassenpflug’s stories suggest about some material collected by the Grimms?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"059d36a7-f8ef-4487-8eab-07b0aabaa079\">combined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> oral traditions with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"282a5f5d-e58d-43b1-bd6e-d18cbed5f1d0\">material from published stories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> <li>B. It came mainly from contributors who had read the stories in books.</li> <li>C. It was more detailed than traditional oral versions.</li> <li>D. It originated with Perrault before entering the oral tradition.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-H, below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Endings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. reflects the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"133e385a-6d01-47df-a501-a7a112b222d2\">harsh realities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"0693bbf8-6c40-42bf-ac40-75f010f3624e\">earlier European society<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"0ba2c10e-8b5a-422c-a9c4-38f6c5f6d977\">may help children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"7521bd71-c8af-4f22-8237-761f504fa719\">gain control over their anxieties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"c6132f99-5449-42f0-b906-9dd17ef10187\">allows the stories to seem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"78ae252b-c1da-422a-8dfd-76e8726fef53\">independent of any particular time or place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. is interpreted as reflecting a particular <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"a93e5c49-6f12-4cd5-8534-543e19ceff76\">national character<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"10ac4c45-4c5a-4ad3-91ec-e098a5d31ba7\">encourages readers to imagine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"443b9960-7eac-4a69-81d2-9b65855fa9b5\">greater control over their own futures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. suggests that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"3d5506e3-c68e-469d-be03-37996c4672ea\">the Grimms themselves created the violent material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in the stories.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. makes the tales valuable mainly as records of German history.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. leads readers to reject the moral lessons contained in the stories.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326314\" id=\"question-wrapper-326314\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f0171460-66a6-458c-8d26-3bfb8fc8a9ac\">distinctive outlook<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> expressed in some of the tales</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326315\" id=\"question-wrapper-326315\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"cebb4165-0beb-4e89-8774-d7872a0f79b9\">The depiction of cruelty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"0ab2baa4-528d-49e1-8e4f-57ce4f535c44\">abandonment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in some stories</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326316\" id=\"question-wrapper-326316\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"78c3bb47-0ee8-4d90-8ca6-dca217f66a7d\">The lack of specific descriptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"221d862f-f260-4d59-b577-7ae0c2004a76\">places and surroundings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326317\" id=\"question-wrapper-326317\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"9d8b76a7-2fbd-4a97-b9b5-c03da530bdf4\">Identifying with the heroes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> and with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"0da6f5fa-d063-4c59-95a4-a278b80a37d2\">their pursuit of happiness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326318\" id=\"question-wrapper-326318\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2086bc01-55bb-4df4-9697-01daf4e207d1\">Confronting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2d3e359f-4fed-4b4c-8a1f-eb340be375f4\">frightening figures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> such as witches and wolves</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97 e5a75cf4-535b-4fff-96f0-1d9a6bdb7e8a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The early editions"},{"uid":"05f510f9-3012-48e8-aeb4-0d9e287e3897 5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"readership","passagePhrase":"aimed at"},{"uid":"2c1c9997-c16b-4533-8e15-a30b095a0ba2 5f554ed3-eff1-40f7-b1e2-92cfde159a97","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Children","passagePhrase":"children"},{"uid":"779041ac-1d54-4fb1-8100-235e1fa1591f","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"a response to political circumstances","passagePhrase":"began their work at a time when Germany had been overrun by the French under Napoleon ... who was intent on"},{"uid":"1119f96d-6907-4bf9-913e-2b4b3ff30fb5 779041ac-1d54-4fb1-8100-235e1fa1591f","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"suppressing local culture"},{"uid":"35744117-4131-4d59-9952-4fc7f1f9fd67","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The Grimms’ collecting project","passagePhrase":"the Brothers Grimm undertook the fairy-tale collection"},{"uid":"1119f96d-6907-4bf9-913e-2b4b3ff30fb5","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"threatened German oral culture","passagePhrase":"preserving Germany’s endangered oral tradition"},{"uid":"499ed4de-f65a-48ab-bc40-fbc145847551","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"teachers or parents","passagePhrase":"teachers, parents"},{"uid":"902df0b6-6c43-4fed-a325-0fb907f956ed","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Religious figures","passagePhrase":"religious figures"},{"uid":"4d1c1913-1a00-43ce-92f4-ea2dc2275fa6","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"objected to the collection's content more strongly","passagePhrase":"deplored the Grimms’ collection ... objected to"},{"uid":"3db19467-5197-4bf8-b54a-619ca11ed9a9","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"readership they had not originally expected","passagePhrase":"had not foreseen"},{"uid":"eded577d-c230-4d0d-94b6-5470eb205129","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"the new readership","passagePhrase":"this"},{"uid":"3db19467-5197-4bf8-b54a-619ca11ed9a9 eded577d-c230-4d0d-94b6-5470eb205129","qNum":"30 33","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"new readership"},{"uid":"45362364-fc3d-4692-a956-7c997b0efab3 813ab3ad-bf81-4c98-9d3f-d75a50ed7121","qNum":"30 33","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"set about ... their tales"},{"uid":"45362364-fc3d-4692-a956-7c997b0efab3 813ab3ad-bf81-4c98-9d3f-d75a50ed7121 9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6","qNum":"30 33","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"refining and softening"},{"uid":"1e9df7a1-eee0-4373-864a-32c932bffd6e","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"from which they had originated","passagePhrase":"had originated centuries earlier as"},{"uid":"33834b2c-d8a1-4c56-a530-e80c57f65bfb","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"the earthy peasant stories","passagePhrase":"earthy peasant fare"},{"uid":"9d8ab040-2dbe-4866-9f85-ce4f298095a6 eaca4d0b-cddb-4fed-9a1f-6466f6250110","qNum":"30 34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"cruel mothers ... unmarried lovers ... incestuous father"},{"uid":"6143b9e9-1fec-4db3-8fa7-81a2e4c8e125","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"value","passagePhrase":"approve of"},{"uid":"033b1892-ad4f-48dd-9b79-ba35b6ed371f","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"reasons other than their fantasy elements","passagePhrase":"finger-wagging lessons"},{"uid":"e5eb9a59-b1dd-44de-9381-e89ba31e10c9","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Dorothea Viehmann's","passagePhrase":"Dorothea Viehmann ... Viehmann"},{"uid":"8ba9d7b3-df25-4fd4-af18-a6a0f0f37d55","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Cinderella","passagePhrase":"Among her treasures was “Aschenputtel”—Cinderella"},{"uid":"059d36a7-f8ef-4487-8eab-07b0aabaa079 121abb4b-a92d-48b5-ba71-8a9268b7e284","qNum":"32 35","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"blended"},{"uid":"121abb4b-a92d-48b5-ba71-8a9268b7e284 282a5f5d-e58d-43b1-bd6e-d18cbed5f1d0 99e08a56-0dae-42c1-95b9-81a2a337f6b3","qNum":"32 35","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Perrault’s influential 1697 book"},{"uid":"99e08a56-0dae-42c1-95b9-81a2a337f6b3","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"'s collection","passagePhrase":", ... Tales of My Mother Goose"},{"uid":"f0171460-66a6-458c-8d26-3bfb8fc8a9ac","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"distinctive outlook","passagePhrase":"Love of the underdog, rustic simplicity and creative energy"},{"uid":"a93e5c49-6f12-4cd5-8534-543e19ceff76","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"national character","passagePhrase":"Teutonic traits"},{"uid":"133e385a-6d01-47df-a501-a7a112b222d2","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"harsh realities","passagePhrase":"The coarse texture of life ... the law-and-order system"},{"uid":"0693bbf8-6c40-42bf-ac40-75f010f3624e","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"earlier European society","passagePhrase":"during medieval times in Germany ... Throughout Europe ... the old times"},{"uid":"0ab2baa4-528d-49e1-8e4f-57ce4f535c44","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"abandonment","passagePhrase":"children were often neglected and abandoned"},{"uid":"cebb4165-0beb-4e89-8774-d7872a0f79b9","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"The depiction of cruelty","passagePhrase":"Accused witches were burned at the stake ... The cruelty in the stories"},{"uid":"78c3bb47-0ee8-4d90-8ca6-dca217f66a7d","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"The lack of specific descriptions","passagePhrase":"no concrete descriptions"},{"uid":"221d862f-f260-4d59-b577-7ae0c2004a76","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"places and surroundings","passagePhrase":"the land ... the forest ... the castles"},{"uid":"c6132f99-5449-42f0-b906-9dd17ef10187","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"allows the stories to seem","passagePhrase":"It makes the stories"},{"uid":"78ae252b-c1da-422a-8dfd-76e8726fef53","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"independent of any particular time or place","passagePhrase":"timeless and placeless"},{"uid":"10ac4c45-4c5a-4ad3-91ec-e098a5d31ba7","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"encourages readers to imagine","passagePhrase":"allow us to express our utopian longings ... in our minds"},{"uid":"0da6f5fa-d063-4c59-95a4-a278b80a37d2","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"their pursuit of happiness","passagePhrase":"a striving for happiness"},{"uid":"9d8b76a7-2fbd-4a97-b9b5-c03da530bdf4","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Identifying with the heroes","passagePhrase":"identify with the heroes of the tales"},{"uid":"443b9960-7eac-4a69-81d2-9b65855fa9b5","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"greater control over their own futures","passagePhrase":"the masters and mistresses of our own destinies"},{"uid":"2086bc01-55bb-4df4-9697-01daf4e207d1","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Confronting","passagePhrase":"confronting"},{"uid":"2d3e359f-4fed-4b4c-8a1f-eb340be375f4","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"frightening figures","passagePhrase":"fears and phobias ... witches ... heartless stepmothers ... hungry wolves"},{"uid":"0ba2c10e-8b5a-422c-a9c4-38f6c5f6d977","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"may help children","passagePhrase":"children find they can ... Bettelheim’s theory continues to be hotly debated"},{"uid":"7521bd71-c8af-4f22-8237-761f504fa719","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"gain control over their anxieties","passagePhrase":"master their anxieties"},{"uid":"05f510f9-3012-48e8-aeb4-0d9e287e3897","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"the Grimms had in mind","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"e5a75cf4-535b-4fff-96f0-1d9a6bdb7e8a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"when the collection first appeared","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"813ab3ad-bf81-4c98-9d3f-d75a50ed7121","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"In revising the tales","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"121abb4b-a92d-48b5-ba71-8a9268b7e284 99e08a56-0dae-42c1-95b9-81a2a337f6b3","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Perrault","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"45362364-fc3d-4692-a956-7c997b0efab3","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"adapting their work","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"eaca4d0b-cddb-4fed-9a1f-6466f6250110","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"sensitive family and sexual content","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"059d36a7-f8ef-4487-8eab-07b0aabaa079","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"combined","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"282a5f5d-e58d-43b1-bd6e-d18cbed5f1d0","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"material from published stories","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_106":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>Traditional Farming in Zambia's Luapula Province</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"7d88573b-1155-4281-80a5-2c07a2b53fa6\">By tradition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"7d88573b-1155-4281-80a5-2c07a2b53fa6\">land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in Luapula Province is not owned by individuals but, as in many other parts of Africa, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"7d88573b-1155-4281-80a5-2c07a2b53fa6\">is allocated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> by the headman or headwoman of a village <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"7d88573b-1155-4281-80a5-2c07a2b53fa6\">to people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of either sex <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"2a08eba9-e25b-41a2-9e75-ccabcd7b5992\">according to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> need. Since land is generally prepared by hand, a single family group cannot take on a very large area, so land has not been a limiting resource over large parts of the province. However, this is no longer the case <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"7eb6d4b0-723a-4ed4-94d4-755a95dd5bc4\">near the main towns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"6f817d1f-3ce5-4c76-8c77-699cf90a28ed\">land for cultivation has long been scarce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"7eb6d4b0-723a-4ed4-94d4-755a95dd5bc4\">the river valley<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. In both areas, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"a5776465-c56a-4d67-8e7f-a261e032cc26\">registered forms of land ownership<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"08a1ec85-3a29-4175-b3dd-75a5b855910e\">have become increasingly common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Most traditional cropping in Luapula Province is based on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"d49012be-5745-4b9d-9553-a1539d1dea89\">citemene, a system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> whereby <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"46f70c02-131d-4135-bf0c-c20b28a9780b\">crops are grown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> on the ashes of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"2f40be20-a995-45de-afc0-4027863efcfb\">tree branches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. As a rule, entire trees are pollarded—that is, their upper branches are cut back—rather than felled, so that they can regenerate. Branches are cut over an area of land of varying size early in the dry season and then stacked to dry out. The wood is fired before the onset of the rains, and in the first year, the area is planted with the African cereal called finger millet. The grain is used to brew local drinks such as cipumu, a drink that contributes several B-complex vitamins to people's diets. Cipumu is also used in cementing reciprocal working relationships (Pottier 1985).</span></p><p><span>During the second year, and possibly for a few years more, the area <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f42a2aac-81cd-4b84-8ef4-877072a4ea97\">is planted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> with various combinations of annual crops such as maize, pumpkins, sweet potatoes, groundnuts, beans and leafy vegetables, with some crop rotation. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"4bd4b163-8923-4db4-883d-d9d04b0e6484\">The diverse sequence ends with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> cassava, which is often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f42a2aac-81cd-4b84-8ef4-877072a4ea97\">planted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> alongside the preceding crop before that crop is harvested.</span></p><p><span>Richards (1969) observed that the practice of citemene entails a definite division of labour; men and women perform different tasks. The men mark out plots discreetly, since explicitly marking boundaries is considered provocative to one's neighbours. The dangerous work of cutting branches is also the responsibility of the men. Branches are then stacked by women and fired by men. Men and women cooperate in planting, but harvesting is always done by women.</span></p><p><span>At the beginning of the citemene cycle, little weeding is necessary, since the firing of the branches effectively destroys weeds. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"696b4636-75bc-4830-a960-cc329de878b5\">As the cycle progresses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"120c30cd-f7be-460c-80bf-f976aca73cde\">weeds increase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"1d16c370-6f1a-4f81-8c83-c6c21eb4aa88\">soil nutrients are eventually depleted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> to the point where further effort with annual crops is no longer worthwhile. At this stage, cassava is planted, since it can produce a crop on soil that is almost exhausted. Thereafter, the plot is abandoned, and trees in a new area are pollarded for the next cycle.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4 12\" data-uid=\"3ecb8a0f-7f8a-4a80-9bb0-f62efa28601b 5eca5deb-a997-4c3c-8932-5692019c8f65\">Where forest is unavailable</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>—a situation that has become increasingly common—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d07975c8-cce9-447a-aaf2-47aa0770c88e\">a series of ridges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> is built, in which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"6d7acae0-c96e-439e-8a76-dbd3668e4f6f\">combinations of maize, beans, groundnuts and sweet potatoes are then planted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, usually followed by cassava. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d07975c8-cce9-447a-aaf2-47aa0770c88e\">These plots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a72f8756-e6a5-45ad-b25a-afaf2d25c948\">normally tended by women<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> and are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"4edef6a0-1c7a-492b-b045-3e6fa3d04b84\">used </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"40177bd4-c021-41fc-9170-b9cdfdea15da 4edef6a0-1c7a-492b-b045-3e6fa3d04b84\">mainly</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"4edef6a0-1c7a-492b-b045-3e6fa3d04b84\"> for subsistence</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"412d3769-f847-4976-bec4-7f2d74a64fe9\">Where their roots have year-round access to water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"beeab6ac-5a50-412a-ba2d-c824fa30fd4f\">mango, guava and oil-palm trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"6a700777-375f-496b-863e-77cdac9fb6d0\">are often grown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5d02f7b5-ab23-4720-b337-cd21d037b062\">around<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> houses, forming a traditional agroforestry system, and some of their fruit is sold by the roadside or in local markets. In addition, local varieties of rice are sometimes planted in waterlogged ground during the rainy season.</span></p><p><span>Fishing has always been a far more remunerative activity in Luapula than crop husbandry. It provides a much-needed protein supplement to the diet, as well as being the one substantial source of cash. Much of the catch is dried and sold in areas away from the main waterways. The Mweru and Bangweulu Lake Basins are the main areas of year-round <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8a6a8c96-29f3-4edd-a6d5-db87b5946c31\">fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>ing, but the Luapula River is also exploited during the latter part of the dry season. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8c1ecfc0-0c4b-4e7c-b883-b35a15072a8d\">Several previously abundant and desirable species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"452b36e1-2d2c-44f2-bf21-2edcbcf47293\">have all but disappeared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> from Lake Mweru, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b897ac2c-cc81-4317-8c5d-c0f3d4919f4c\">apparently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"eef89128-715e-4901-ac24-e24cbdb7509c\">due to overfishing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (Huckaby 1979).</span></p><p><span>Regarding animal husbandry, only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"ce9108d4-a8fa-4b25-b1e5-6b39502ca0a4\">small numbers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of cattle or oxen are kept in the province owing to the prevalence of the tsetse fly. The resulting absence of animal power for pulling machinery greatly limits people's ability to plough and cultivate land: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a5de5ca0-3a68-48f7-8b5b-4d15b604de01\">a married couple<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> can rarely prepare more than half a hectare <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"56f49a27-da83-490d-98c7-ea35e07aa4fa\">by hoeing the land by hand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"47b14475-5b99-4558-8476-6c50fbbfe61a\">most people keep<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> free-ranging chickens and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"327d7e27-491f-4057-928a-937059ef5ed4\">goats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. These <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"47b14475-5b99-4558-8476-6c50fbbfe61a\">act as </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"47b14475-5b99-4558-8476-6c50fbbfe61a 74f2479b-17c4-4697-9b0b-d5e65a279cfb\">a reserve for bartering</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"309fbbc6-3315-48b5-91f5-9429bd40b1f9\">may also occasionally be slaughtered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"1e3e35ff-05d8-45a8-85c1-3fc7fa00da55\">for ceremonies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"1e3e35ff-05d8-45a8-85c1-3fc7fa00da55\">for entertaining important visitors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. These animals are not a standard part of most people's diet.</span></p><p><span>Traditionally, citemene has been an ingenious system for producing seasonal, high-quality cereals and vegetables in regions with acidic, heavily leached soils. Nutritionally, the most serious deficiency has been that of protein. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"a116cf58-58f4-4bd4-8765-decc98adf6d2\">This deficiency could be alleviated where fish were available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"65c31175-9c94-4ef4-9f2f-6f118725bd93\">provided that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"dd27434b-7c78-4946-a380-6d4468c6e696\">cultivators lived near the valley<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> or had access to dried <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"245b665d-8096-4881-b876-7fdb999cc458\">fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. The citemene/fishing system was well adapted to the ecology of the woodland regions and sustainable for long periods, but only as long as human population densities remained low.</span></p><p><span>Although population densities in Luapula remain much lower than in many other parts of the world, neither the fisheries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"edcf73d4-b1b6-4d9d-8b37-f972317e2d1c\">nor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the woodlands of Luapula <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"edcf73d4-b1b6-4d9d-8b37-f972317e2d1c\">can sustainably support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"8dbd7795-7fa1-4f19-a15d-7aa729325e29\">the expanding population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> under unmodified traditional practices. For instance, even in a normal season, diets suffer from a lack of energy, protein, vitamins and minerals. It will therefore be necessary to intensify and diversify productive systems.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the sentences below. Write </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326319\" id=\"question-wrapper-326319\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In Luapula Province, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"7d88573b-1155-4281-80a5-2c07a2b53fa6\">land has traditionally been given to people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"2a08eba9-e25b-41a2-9e75-ccabcd7b5992\">on the basis of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> (1)________.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NEED</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326320\" id=\"question-wrapper-326320\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"d49012be-5745-4b9d-9553-a1539d1dea89\">The citemene system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"46f70c02-131d-4135-bf0c-c20b28a9780b\">involves planting crops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> on the (2)________ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"2f40be20-a995-45de-afc0-4027863efcfb\">wood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ASHES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326321\" id=\"question-wrapper-326321\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the citemene system, (3)________ is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"4bd4b163-8923-4db4-883d-d9d04b0e6484\">the last crop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f42a2aac-81cd-4b84-8ef4-877072a4ea97\">to be planted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CASSAVA</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326322\" id=\"question-wrapper-326322\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"3ecb8a0f-7f8a-4a80-9bb0-f62efa28601b\">areas without trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"6d7acae0-c96e-439e-8a76-dbd3668e4f6f\">crops are planted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> in a (4)________.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SERIES OF RIDGES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326323\" id=\"question-wrapper-326323\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"412d3769-f847-4976-bec4-7f2d74a64fe9\">If conditions are right<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"beeab6ac-5a50-412a-ba2d-c824fa30fd4f\">fruit trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"6a700777-375f-496b-863e-77cdac9fb6d0\">may be planted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5d02f7b5-ab23-4720-b337-cd21d037b062\">near<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> (5)________.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HOUSES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements and the list of animals below. </span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct animal, A, B or C. </span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 6–9 on your answer sheet. </span></p><p><b><span>NB</span></b><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Animals</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Fish</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Goats</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Oxen</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326324\" id=\"question-wrapper-326324\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"a116cf58-58f4-4bd4-8765-decc98adf6d2\">The benefit </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"245b665d-8096-4881-b876-7fdb999cc458 a116cf58-58f4-4bd4-8765-decc98adf6d2\">they</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"a116cf58-58f4-4bd4-8765-decc98adf6d2\"> can provide</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"65c31175-9c94-4ef4-9f2f-6f118725bd93\">partly dependent on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"dd27434b-7c78-4946-a380-6d4468c6e696\">where cultivators live<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326325\" id=\"question-wrapper-326325\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"74f2479b-17c4-4697-9b0b-d5e65a279cfb\">The reason </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"327d7e27-491f-4057-928a-937059ef5ed4 74f2479b-17c4-4697-9b0b-d5e65a279cfb\">they</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"74f2479b-17c4-4697-9b0b-d5e65a279cfb\"> are </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"47b14475-5b99-4558-8476-6c50fbbfe61a 74f2479b-17c4-4697-9b0b-d5e65a279cfb\">normally retained</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> differs from <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"1e3e35ff-05d8-45a8-85c1-3fc7fa00da55\">the reason they are </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"1e3e35ff-05d8-45a8-85c1-3fc7fa00da55 309fbbc6-3315-48b5-91f5-9429bd40b1f9\">sometimes killed</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326326\" id=\"question-wrapper-326326\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"ce9108d4-a8fa-4b25-b1e5-6b39502ca0a4\">limited numbers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> leave <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a5de5ca0-3a68-48f7-8b5b-4d15b604de01\">couples<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> largely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"56f49a27-da83-490d-98c7-ea35e07aa4fa\">dependent on manual labour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> when cultivating land.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326327\" id=\"question-wrapper-326327\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8c1ecfc0-0c4b-4e7c-b883-b35a15072a8d\">Some previously common and valued types<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8a6a8c96-29f3-4edd-a6d5-db87b5946c31\">them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b897ac2c-cc81-4317-8c5d-c0f3d4919f4c\">appear to have<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"452b36e1-2d2c-44f2-bf21-2edcbcf47293\">become scarce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"eef89128-715e-4901-ac24-e24cbdb7509c\">through excessive exploitation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 10–12 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326328\" id=\"question-wrapper-326328\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"7eb6d4b0-723a-4ed4-94d4-755a95dd5bc4\">parts of Luapula<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"6f817d1f-3ce5-4c76-8c77-699cf90a28ed\">land for cultivation is scarce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"a5776465-c56a-4d67-8e7f-a261e032cc26\">registered forms of land ownership<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"08a1ec85-3a29-4175-b3dd-75a5b855910e\">are becoming more common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326329\" id=\"question-wrapper-326329\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"120c30cd-f7be-460c-80bf-f976aca73cde\">Weeds become more common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"696b4636-75bc-4830-a960-cc329de878b5\">during the citemene cycle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"1d16c370-6f1a-4f81-8c83-c6c21eb4aa88\">the soil gradually loses nutrients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326330\" id=\"question-wrapper-326330\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"5eca5deb-a997-4c3c-8932-5692019c8f65\">Where forest is unavailable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d07975c8-cce9-447a-aaf2-47aa0770c88e\">ridge plots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a72f8756-e6a5-45ad-b25a-afaf2d25c948\">generally managed by women<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"40177bd4-c021-41fc-9170-b9cdfdea15da\">mainly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"4edef6a0-1c7a-492b-b045-3e6fa3d04b84\">to produce crops for sale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326331\" id=\"question-wrapper-326331\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the writer's opinion about traditional productive practices in Luapula Province?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They meet all the dietary needs of the local population.</li> <li>B. The region's natural resources have not been fully exploited.</li> <li>C. They will be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"edcf73d4-b1b6-4d9d-8b37-f972317e2d1c\">inadequate to support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"8dbd7795-7fa1-4f19-a15d-7aa729325e29\">a growing population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</li> <li>D. A larger labour force will be required for maximum efficiency.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7d88573b-1155-4281-80a5-2c07a2b53fa6","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"land has traditionally been given to people","passagePhrase":"By tradition ... land ... is allocated ... to people"},{"uid":"2a08eba9-e25b-41a2-9e75-ccabcd7b5992","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"on the basis of","passagePhrase":"according to"},{"uid":"7eb6d4b0-723a-4ed4-94d4-755a95dd5bc4","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"parts of Luapula","passagePhrase":"near the main towns ... the river valley"},{"uid":"6f817d1f-3ce5-4c76-8c77-699cf90a28ed","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"land for cultivation is scarce","passagePhrase":"land for cultivation has long been scarce"},{"uid":"a5776465-c56a-4d67-8e7f-a261e032cc26","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"registered forms of land ownership","passagePhrase":"registered forms of land ownership"},{"uid":"08a1ec85-3a29-4175-b3dd-75a5b855910e","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"are becoming more common","passagePhrase":"have become increasingly common"},{"uid":"d49012be-5745-4b9d-9553-a1539d1dea89","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"The citemene system","passagePhrase":"citemene, a system"},{"uid":"46f70c02-131d-4135-bf0c-c20b28a9780b","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"involves planting crops","passagePhrase":"crops are grown"},{"uid":"2f40be20-a995-45de-afc0-4027863efcfb","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"wood","passagePhrase":"tree branches"},{"uid":"f42a2aac-81cd-4b84-8ef4-877072a4ea97","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"to be planted","passagePhrase":"is planted ... planted"},{"uid":"4bd4b163-8923-4db4-883d-d9d04b0e6484","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"the last crop","passagePhrase":"The diverse sequence ends with"},{"uid":"696b4636-75bc-4830-a960-cc329de878b5","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"during the citemene cycle","passagePhrase":"As the cycle progresses"},{"uid":"120c30cd-f7be-460c-80bf-f976aca73cde","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Weeds become more common","passagePhrase":"weeds increase"},{"uid":"1d16c370-6f1a-4f81-8c83-c6c21eb4aa88","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"the soil gradually loses nutrients","passagePhrase":"soil nutrients are eventually depleted"},{"uid":"3ecb8a0f-7f8a-4a80-9bb0-f62efa28601b 5eca5deb-a997-4c3c-8932-5692019c8f65","qNum":"4 12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Where forest is unavailable"},{"uid":"d07975c8-cce9-447a-aaf2-47aa0770c88e","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"ridge plots","passagePhrase":"a series of ridges ... These plots"},{"uid":"6d7acae0-c96e-439e-8a76-dbd3668e4f6f","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"crops are planted","passagePhrase":"combinations of maize, beans, groundnuts and sweet potatoes are then planted"},{"uid":"a72f8756-e6a5-45ad-b25a-afaf2d25c948","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"generally managed by women","passagePhrase":"normally tended by women"},{"uid":"40177bd4-c021-41fc-9170-b9cdfdea15da 4edef6a0-1c7a-492b-b045-3e6fa3d04b84","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"mainly"},{"uid":"412d3769-f847-4976-bec4-7f2d74a64fe9","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"If conditions are right","passagePhrase":"Where their roots have year-round access to water"},{"uid":"beeab6ac-5a50-412a-ba2d-c824fa30fd4f","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"fruit trees","passagePhrase":"mango, guava and oil-palm trees"},{"uid":"6a700777-375f-496b-863e-77cdac9fb6d0","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"may be planted","passagePhrase":"are often grown"},{"uid":"5d02f7b5-ab23-4720-b337-cd21d037b062","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"near","passagePhrase":"around"},{"uid":"8a6a8c96-29f3-4edd-a6d5-db87b5946c31","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"them","passagePhrase":"fish"},{"uid":"8c1ecfc0-0c4b-4e7c-b883-b35a15072a8d","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Some previously common and valued types","passagePhrase":"Several previously abundant and desirable species"},{"uid":"452b36e1-2d2c-44f2-bf21-2edcbcf47293","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"become scarce","passagePhrase":"have all but disappeared"},{"uid":"b897ac2c-cc81-4317-8c5d-c0f3d4919f4c","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"appear to have","passagePhrase":"apparently"},{"uid":"eef89128-715e-4901-ac24-e24cbdb7509c","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"through excessive exploitation","passagePhrase":"due to overfishing"},{"uid":"ce9108d4-a8fa-4b25-b1e5-6b39502ca0a4","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"limited numbers","passagePhrase":"small numbers"},{"uid":"a5de5ca0-3a68-48f7-8b5b-4d15b604de01","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"couples","passagePhrase":"a married couple"},{"uid":"56f49a27-da83-490d-98c7-ea35e07aa4fa","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"dependent on manual labour","passagePhrase":"by hoeing the land by hand"},{"uid":"47b14475-5b99-4558-8476-6c50fbbfe61a","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"most people keep ... act as"},{"uid":"327d7e27-491f-4057-928a-937059ef5ed4","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"goats"},{"uid":"47b14475-5b99-4558-8476-6c50fbbfe61a 74f2479b-17c4-4697-9b0b-d5e65a279cfb","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"normally retained","passagePhrase":"a reserve for bartering"},{"uid":"309fbbc6-3315-48b5-91f5-9429bd40b1f9","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"may also occasionally be slaughtered"},{"uid":"1e3e35ff-05d8-45a8-85c1-3fc7fa00da55","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"the reason they are","passagePhrase":"for ceremonies ... for entertaining important visitors"},{"uid":"a116cf58-58f4-4bd4-8765-decc98adf6d2","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"The benefit ... can provide","passagePhrase":"This deficiency could be alleviated where fish were available"},{"uid":"65c31175-9c94-4ef4-9f2f-6f118725bd93","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"partly dependent on","passagePhrase":"provided that"},{"uid":"dd27434b-7c78-4946-a380-6d4468c6e696","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"where cultivators live","passagePhrase":"cultivators lived near the valley"},{"uid":"245b665d-8096-4881-b876-7fdb999cc458","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fish"},{"uid":"edcf73d4-b1b6-4d9d-8b37-f972317e2d1c","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"inadequate to support","passagePhrase":"nor ... can sustainably support"},{"uid":"8dbd7795-7fa1-4f19-a15d-7aa729325e29","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"a growing population","passagePhrase":"the expanding population"},{"uid":"3ecb8a0f-7f8a-4a80-9bb0-f62efa28601b","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"areas without trees","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"245b665d-8096-4881-b876-7fdb999cc458 a116cf58-58f4-4bd4-8765-decc98adf6d2","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"they","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"74f2479b-17c4-4697-9b0b-d5e65a279cfb","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"The reason ... are","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"327d7e27-491f-4057-928a-937059ef5ed4 74f2479b-17c4-4697-9b0b-d5e65a279cfb","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"they","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"1e3e35ff-05d8-45a8-85c1-3fc7fa00da55 309fbbc6-3315-48b5-91f5-9429bd40b1f9","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"sometimes killed","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"5eca5deb-a997-4c3c-8932-5692019c8f65","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Where forest is unavailable","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"40177bd4-c021-41fc-9170-b9cdfdea15da","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"mainly","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_107":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>WHAT IS AN UNFAIR ADVANTAGE IN SPORT?</span></b></p><p><i><span>Olympic athletes increasingly depend on technology to help them win—but is that fair?</span></i></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><span>What happened to the Australian athlete Ron Clarke in the 10,000 metres at the Mexico City Olympics of 1968 is <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"0b7f8bfe-7a17-4aa1-8059-e7e0035285cc aa87506e-9948-4cf8-aea8-cc4a2e0cc074\">now virtually forgotten</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, though at the time it was headline news. At that time, Clarke was <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"14 21 22\" data-uid=\"28a15827-b7e4-4612-b503-4a2121233f28 4ad85444-92ce-40f0-8daa-058d13922b97 c2ae6a02-8a4f-4de3-a8d2-7a5fb0c0a682\">the greatest distance runner in history</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>; he <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"14 21 22\" data-uid=\"28a15827-b7e4-4612-b503-4a2121233f28 4ad85444-92ce-40f0-8daa-058d13922b97 c2ae6a02-8a4f-4de3-a8d2-7a5fb0c0a682\">had broken more world records than anybody else</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e489946a-5bf0-4852-ace2-88665f224e83\">But<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in front of 55,000 horrified spectators, the event went disastrously wrong. In the third lap, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"3a5c7132-4e11-4da2-bae5-1a60c375ba0d 9fa864b2-ddfc-4d77-9310-4fa714fdb4ac\">one runner keeled over</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and, with six laps to go, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"3a5c7132-4e11-4da2-bae5-1a60c375ba0d 9fa864b2-ddfc-4d77-9310-4fa714fdb4ac\">two more were carried away</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e489946a-5bf0-4852-ace2-88665f224e83\">Yet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the race was being conducted at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8fc49fee-b176-4f66-8cce-9dd386cc31b8\">a relatively leisurely speed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8fc49fee-b176-4f66-8cce-9dd386cc31b8\">the halfway time was the slowest since the Paris Olympics of 1924<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"5271ce56-60e9-4921-b928-51eb0809ffc5 d0018ce1-2df1-441f-9122-13bb4df36289\">With two laps to go</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, Clarke <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"68306030-4b06-415a-9bb9-f9f7e9bc529b c75c4df5-eb75-4f6c-b58d-0faebff090e4\">was in the leading pack</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. “I had never felt better in a race,” he says. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e489946a-5bf0-4852-ace2-88665f224e83\">But suddenly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> he too began to struggle, and as the frontrunners moved up a gear, a gap opened up. Clarke remembers nothing of his last lap, which he ran in 90 seconds. “Normally I would run it in 64,” he explains. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"59498343-8bd0-446d-b97f-5561d243c488\">stumbled across the line in sixth place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"59498343-8bd0-446d-b97f-5561d243c488\">collapsed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. He was administered oxygen and stretchered off the track.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><span>Mexico City is surrounded by mountains and is over 2,240 metres above sea level. That the altitude would have an impact on the Games was predicted. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"2aa45d05-69f4-4c95-819e-708493b49af7 d217b7e0-83c3-4997-87d2-7242e1f19254\">Clarke </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 21 22\" data-uid=\"176c7aca-da00-47cd-96dc-799207aaae66 2aa45d05-69f4-4c95-819e-708493b49af7 d217b7e0-83c3-4997-87d2-7242e1f19254\">had raised the issue himself</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, but <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 21 22\" data-uid=\"4ffcc3e1-441a-4f40-9ed2-5b9e70818d3c 6031e048-6a51-4442-87c1-9768c653ac6f a17dfb77-af66-4872-b87b-5e6e395c034c\">had been told</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> by the Australian sports authorities that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 21 22\" data-uid=\"4ffcc3e1-441a-4f40-9ed2-5b9e70818d3c 6031e048-6a51-4442-87c1-9768c653ac6f a17dfb77-af66-4872-b87b-5e6e395c034c\">complaining was regarded as bad sportsmanship</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"71df40a4-3344-4e71-81e9-b18d295f0e9e\">As it turned out, he had good reason to do so<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Clearly, the link between athletic performance and altitude needed further investigation.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><span>Although there were few standout performances in distance running at the Mexico Games, they marked a turning point: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4cadcbb0-b1ee-40c9-97a0-41f21fb74389\">the start of an astonishing record of success<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> by East Africans. While Clarke lay crumpled in a heap, runners from Kenya and Ethiopia were celebrating their gold and silver medals. The record books showed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4cadcbb0-b1ee-40c9-97a0-41f21fb74389\">how firmly established this pattern had become<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. By 2011, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4cadcbb0-b1ee-40c9-97a0-41f21fb74389\">the seven fastest men in history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> over 5,000 metres were all from either Kenya or Ethiopia. Between 1997 and 2011, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4cadcbb0-b1ee-40c9-97a0-41f21fb74389\">the men’s 10,000-metre world record was broken five times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, each time by a Kenyan or an Ethiopian. While there is a complex mix of explanations for the pre-eminence of East Africans, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"53853eb2-a0b1-49a5-86e5-75bd647e4fc9\">one factor is surely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that many of these athletes have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"53853eb2-a0b1-49a5-86e5-75bd647e4fc9\">lived most of their lives in thin air<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"db979358-a447-43df-a77b-cd518ec7bb4b\">At high altitudes, a number of physiological alterations occur<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Most importantly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"db979358-a447-43df-a77b-cd518ec7bb4b\">more red blood cells and haemoglobin are produced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. This increases the capacity of the blood to carry oxygen, which feeds the muscles and gives athletes an advantage when they return to sea level. However, it is impossible to train with the same <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"bb85b486-e609-4685-8930-6472cdd684a9\">level of intensity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in the mountains: aerobic capacity and cardiorespiratory function both suffer at altitude. As a result, the consensus is that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"91a8cfc7-386c-4799-ac36-486fcacdbc04\">the optimum </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"91a8cfc7-386c-4799-ac36-486fcacdbc04 e146fdaa-57f4-42a5-bc48-387be19a8dae\">approach</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"e146fdaa-57f4-42a5-bc48-387be19a8dae\"> to athletic preparation</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"91a8cfc7-386c-4799-ac36-486fcacdbc04\">Live High, Train Low<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> (LHTL). Yet that has obvious practical drawbacks. Not many people live in the mountains, and those who do would prefer not to spend several hours each day driving up and down winding, treacherous roads.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><span>That is where the altitude tent—sometimes called the hypoxic tent—comes in. Two scientists independently arrived at a similar idea: if they could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ad1d193b-8b12-4a51-ac37-14d4f1c3549a\">artificially control the atmosphere<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> within a confined space, they could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ad1d193b-8b12-4a51-ac37-14d4f1c3549a\">simulate the effects of high altitude<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> and save an athlete at sea level the time and expense of travelling to higher ground. Over time, altitude tents became less hot, less noisy and much cheaper than the early prototypes. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"4bd4f76f-5965-4018-9628-b5d27f175938\">In 2006, WADA<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, the World Anti-Doping Agency, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 23\" data-uid=\"4bd4f76f-5965-4018-9628-b5d27f175938 8f4d9cee-0893-438f-9f39-25c2057d94b4\">considered whether</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"8f4d9cee-0893-438f-9f39-25c2057d94b4\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 23\" data-uid=\"7a182c8f-4556-49d9-be8e-3ffe703307fe 8f4d9cee-0893-438f-9f39-25c2057d94b4\">artificially induced hypoxic conditions</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"8f4d9cee-0893-438f-9f39-25c2057d94b4\"> should be prohibited</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 23\" data-uid=\"8f4d9cee-0893-438f-9f39-25c2057d94b4 b5f0a175-de73-468b-a25b-09954e020145\">Its ethics panel concluded that hypoxic devices were contrary to the spirit of sport</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. After consulting stakeholders, however, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"44a20d95-d88f-41fb-b42d-783fc4be9adb\">WADA </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 23\" data-uid=\"44a20d95-d88f-41fb-b42d-783fc4be9adb d173b6b2-f11c-4d26-9c21-712d1426f082\">decided not to add them to its Prohibited List</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. By 2011, altitude tents were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d173b6b2-f11c-4d26-9c21-712d1426f082\">routinely used by athletes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in endurance sports.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><span>However, it is not the case that all new technologies gain approval. In 2008, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bd2cf366-c5b6-4db1-bd8b-e4af76d62c44\">a staggering 105 world records were broken<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in swimming, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bd2cf366-c5b6-4db1-bd8b-e4af76d62c44\">the vast majority achieved by competitors wearing the new Speedo LZR Racer suit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"cedba363-6102-4f96-96d3-02a01d15916e\">These suits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"c54da8e7-38db-4b71-8292-35f2ef13df5a\">a high-tech fabric<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> tested in NASA’s wind tunnels, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"739995df-efa3-4fe7-8649-10a540da21c3\">reduces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> drag and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"2b5c08ba-01ad-43d7-9ba3-e118ba3a89bc\">improves buoyancy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 24\" data-uid=\"057314a7-8947-4f15-afec-d4a00f49338c cedba363-6102-4f96-96d3-02a01d15916e\">The LZR</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"057314a7-8947-4f15-afec-d4a00f49338c\"> was initially sanctioned by FINA</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, the international swimming body. But as better suits were produced by Speedo and other manufacturers, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bd2cf366-c5b6-4db1-bd8b-e4af76d62c44\">more records were broken<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"36aeb8e4-17c5-46db-90df-940347423f7a\">became increasingly controversial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. In a 2009 ruling, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 24\" data-uid=\"05f79a00-f5ce-4e3d-b69b-d7c2023d9a71 36aeb8e4-17c5-46db-90df-940347423f7a\">FINA changed its mind</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 24\" data-uid=\"05f79a00-f5ce-4e3d-b69b-d7c2023d9a71 36aeb8e4-17c5-46db-90df-940347423f7a\">banning all suits made with this high-tech fabric</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"G\" data-question-number=\"20\"><span>Going faster, higher, stronger is integral to the logic of athletics in general, and the Olympics in particular. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"2a49b332-b1f4-4d54-8d16-f36f02e987c7\">Athletes believe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"32906c1a-46cb-4ec5-8a00-73662bf5d966\">need records all the time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"6e7bc4c0-64a5-432d-b160-59dfa15e462c\">The only way athletes can continue to break records is by improving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> their clothing, equipment, training, and nutrition, as even a minute difference of 0.0001 seconds can separate one competitor from another. But <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20 26\" data-uid=\"aa9ab6cb-58b4-461f-9430-14fc25d09bf6 e3dc5662-74b0-402b-ba25-16205fe24e6d\">when a new technology is invented</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20 26\" data-uid=\"aa9ab6cb-58b4-461f-9430-14fc25d09bf6 f6bf43ab-285e-4266-8fa6-b86863132a51\">the relevant sports authority</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"aa9ab6cb-58b4-461f-9430-14fc25d09bf6\"> has to consider </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20 26\" data-uid=\"aa9ab6cb-58b4-461f-9430-14fc25d09bf6 e3dc5662-74b0-402b-ba25-16205fe24e6d\">whether to embrace or reject it</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. In some cases, athletes are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"fe011424-fb14-437b-bd94-d01d4c2758cf\">granted permission<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to use the technology; in others, it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"fe011424-fb14-437b-bd94-d01d4c2758cf\">banned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. But whatever the outcome, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20 26\" data-uid=\"6f7595f1-fc32-4f6e-b5a4-3a39041dfc2b f6bf43ab-285e-4266-8fa6-b86863132a51\">rulings</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"6f7595f1-fc32-4f6e-b5a4-3a39041dfc2b\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20 26\" data-uid=\"6f7595f1-fc32-4f6e-b5a4-3a39041dfc2b cf491f6c-617d-4fac-a1b7-35354e529f63\">should not appear</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"6f7595f1-fc32-4f6e-b5a4-3a39041dfc2b\"> arbitrary</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"6f7595f1-fc32-4f6e-b5a4-3a39041dfc2b\">arguments have to be examined and weighed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"6f7595f1-fc32-4f6e-b5a4-3a39041dfc2b\">the rules of logic ought to apply in every case<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-G.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. </span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 14-20.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ad1d193b-8b12-4a51-ac37-14d4f1c3549a\">An artificial substitute<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d173b6b2-f11c-4d26-9c21-712d1426f082\">survives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"8f4d9cee-0893-438f-9f39-25c2057d94b4\">an ethical challenge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. The inconvenience of commuting between high- and low-altitude locations</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"59498343-8bd0-446d-b97f-5561d243c488\">A result<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e489946a-5bf0-4852-ace2-88665f224e83\">at odds with both<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"28a15827-b7e4-4612-b503-4a2121233f28\">reputation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8fc49fee-b176-4f66-8cce-9dd386cc31b8\">race conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. The case for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"6f7595f1-fc32-4f6e-b5a4-3a39041dfc2b\">consistent criteria<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"aa9ab6cb-58b4-461f-9430-14fc25d09bf6 fe011424-fb14-437b-bd94-d01d4c2758cf\">regulating</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"aa9ab6cb-58b4-461f-9430-14fc25d09bf6\"> sporting innovation</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4cadcbb0-b1ee-40c9-97a0-41f21fb74389\">A sustained pattern of success<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"91a8cfc7-386c-4799-ac36-486fcacdbc04\">with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"53853eb2-a0b1-49a5-86e5-75bd647e4fc9\">possible environmental basis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bd2cf366-c5b6-4db1-bd8b-e4af76d62c44\">Success<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"36aeb8e4-17c5-46db-90df-940347423f7a\">turns </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"057314a7-8947-4f15-afec-d4a00f49338c\">an approved innovation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"36aeb8e4-17c5-46db-90df-940347423f7a\"> into a regulatory problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"176c7aca-da00-47cd-96dc-799207aaae66\">A concern<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"6031e048-6a51-4442-87c1-9768c653ac6f\">dismissed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> before <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"71df40a4-3344-4e71-81e9-b18d295f0e9e\">circumstances proved it justified<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. The difficulty of explaining exceptional performance by one factor alone</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"e146fdaa-57f4-42a5-bc48-387be19a8dae\">A training strategy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"91a8cfc7-386c-4799-ac36-486fcacdbc04\">balances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"db979358-a447-43df-a77b-cd518ec7bb4b\">altitude adaptation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"bb85b486-e609-4685-8930-6472cdd684a9\">exercise intensity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326332\" id=\"question-wrapper-326332\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>Paragraph A</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326333\" id=\"question-wrapper-326333\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>Paragraph B</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326334\" id=\"question-wrapper-326334\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>Paragraph C</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">v</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326335\" id=\"question-wrapper-326335\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>Paragraph D</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ix</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326336\" id=\"question-wrapper-326336\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>Paragraph E</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">i</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326337\" id=\"question-wrapper-326337\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>Paragraph F</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326338\" id=\"question-wrapper-326338\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p>Paragraph G</p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose TWO letters, A–E. Write the correct letters in boxes 21 and 22 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>TWO</span></b><span> of the following statements about Ron Clarke are made in the passage?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Clarke <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"4ad85444-92ce-40f0-8daa-058d13922b97 c2ae6a02-8a4f-4de3-a8d2-7a5fb0c0a682\">was not performing well immediately prior to the Mexico Games</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"2aa45d05-69f4-4c95-819e-708493b49af7 d217b7e0-83c3-4997-87d2-7242e1f19254\">The worries Clarke had before the Mexico Games</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"4ffcc3e1-441a-4f40-9ed2-5b9e70818d3c a17dfb77-af66-4872-b87b-5e6e395c034c\">were not taken into account</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Clarke's experiences at the Mexico Games are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"0b7f8bfe-7a17-4aa1-8059-e7e0035285cc aa87506e-9948-4cf8-aea8-cc4a2e0cc074\">widely talked about today</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"5271ce56-60e9-4921-b928-51eb0809ffc5 d0018ce1-2df1-441f-9122-13bb4df36289\">At one stage</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of the Mexico Games 10,000 metres, Clarke <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"68306030-4b06-415a-9bb9-f9f7e9bc529b c75c4df5-eb75-4f6c-b58d-0faebff090e4\">was near the front</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Clarke was <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21 22\" data-uid=\"3a5c7132-4e11-4da2-bae5-1a60c375ba0d 9fa864b2-ddfc-4d77-9310-4fa714fdb4ac\">the only runner</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> at the Mexico Games who appeared to be affected by the altitude.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326339\" id=\"question-wrapper-326339\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326340\" id=\"question-wrapper-326340\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D/B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><b><span>The use of technology in sport</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"4bd4f76f-5965-4018-9628-b5d27f175938\">In 2006, WADA considered whether<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"7a182c8f-4556-49d9-be8e-3ffe703307fe\">artificially created low-oxygen conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> should be (23)______. Although <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"b5f0a175-de73-468b-a25b-09954e020145\">its ethics panel objected to the use of such devices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, WADA <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"44a20d95-d88f-41fb-b42d-783fc4be9adb\">ultimately decided not to add them to its Prohibited List<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>By contrast, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"cedba363-6102-4f96-96d3-02a01d15916e\">the LZR swimsuit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, made from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"c54da8e7-38db-4b71-8292-35f2ef13df5a\">a special fabric<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"2b5c08ba-01ad-43d7-9ba3-e118ba3a89bc\">improves buoyancy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"739995df-efa3-4fe7-8649-10a540da21c3\">reduces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> (24)______, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"05f79a00-f5ce-4e3d-b69b-d7c2023d9a71\">was eventually banned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"2a49b332-b1f4-4d54-8d16-f36f02e987c7\">Athletes believe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"32906c1a-46cb-4ec5-8a00-73662bf5d966\">need to keep setting new<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> (25)______, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"6e7bc4c0-64a5-432d-b160-59dfa15e462c\">seek to do so through improvements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> in areas such as clothing, equipment, training and nutrition. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f6bf43ab-285e-4266-8fa6-b86863132a51\">decisions by sports authorities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e3dc5662-74b0-402b-ba25-16205fe24e6d\">about new technologies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"cf491f6c-617d-4fac-a1b7-35354e529f63\">should never seem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26)______.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326341\" id=\"question-wrapper-326341\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PROHIBITED</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326342\" id=\"question-wrapper-326342\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DRAG</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326343\" id=\"question-wrapper-326343\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RECORDS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326344\" id=\"question-wrapper-326344\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ARBITRARY</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"28a15827-b7e4-4612-b503-4a2121233f28 4ad85444-92ce-40f0-8daa-058d13922b97 c2ae6a02-8a4f-4de3-a8d2-7a5fb0c0a682","qNum":"14 21 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the greatest distance runner in history ... had broken more world records than anybody else"},{"uid":"e489946a-5bf0-4852-ace2-88665f224e83","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"at odds with both","passagePhrase":"But ... Yet ... But suddenly"},{"uid":"8fc49fee-b176-4f66-8cce-9dd386cc31b8","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"race conditions","passagePhrase":"a relatively leisurely speed ... the halfway time was the slowest since the Paris Olympics of 1924"},{"uid":"5271ce56-60e9-4921-b928-51eb0809ffc5 d0018ce1-2df1-441f-9122-13bb4df36289","qNum":"21 22","questionPhrase":"At one stage","passagePhrase":"With two laps to go"},{"uid":"68306030-4b06-415a-9bb9-f9f7e9bc529b c75c4df5-eb75-4f6c-b58d-0faebff090e4","qNum":"21 22","questionPhrase":"was near the front","passagePhrase":"was in the leading pack"},{"uid":"59498343-8bd0-446d-b97f-5561d243c488","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"A result","passagePhrase":"stumbled across the line in sixth place ... collapsed"},{"uid":"2aa45d05-69f4-4c95-819e-708493b49af7 d217b7e0-83c3-4997-87d2-7242e1f19254","qNum":"21 22","questionPhrase":"The worries Clarke had before the Mexico Games","passagePhrase":"Clarke"},{"uid":"176c7aca-da00-47cd-96dc-799207aaae66 2aa45d05-69f4-4c95-819e-708493b49af7 d217b7e0-83c3-4997-87d2-7242e1f19254","qNum":"15 21 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"had raised the issue himself"},{"uid":"4ffcc3e1-441a-4f40-9ed2-5b9e70818d3c 6031e048-6a51-4442-87c1-9768c653ac6f a17dfb77-af66-4872-b87b-5e6e395c034c","qNum":"15 21 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"had been told ... complaining was regarded as bad sportsmanship"},{"uid":"71df40a4-3344-4e71-81e9-b18d295f0e9e","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"circumstances proved it justified","passagePhrase":"As it turned out, he had good reason to do so"},{"uid":"4cadcbb0-b1ee-40c9-97a0-41f21fb74389","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"A sustained pattern of success","passagePhrase":"the start of an astonishing record of success ... how firmly established this pattern had become ... the seven fastest men in history ... the men’s 10,000-metre world record was broken five times"},{"uid":"53853eb2-a0b1-49a5-86e5-75bd647e4fc9","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"possible environmental basis","passagePhrase":"one factor is surely ... lived most of their lives in thin air"},{"uid":"db979358-a447-43df-a77b-cd518ec7bb4b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"altitude adaptation","passagePhrase":"At high altitudes, a number of physiological alterations occur ... more red blood cells and haemoglobin are produced"},{"uid":"bb85b486-e609-4685-8930-6472cdd684a9","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"exercise intensity","passagePhrase":"level of intensity"},{"uid":"91a8cfc7-386c-4799-ac36-486fcacdbc04","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"with ... balances","passagePhrase":"the optimum ... Live High, Train Low"},{"uid":"91a8cfc7-386c-4799-ac36-486fcacdbc04 e146fdaa-57f4-42a5-bc48-387be19a8dae","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"approach"},{"uid":"e146fdaa-57f4-42a5-bc48-387be19a8dae","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"A training strategy","passagePhrase":"to athletic preparation"},{"uid":"ad1d193b-8b12-4a51-ac37-14d4f1c3549a","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"An artificial substitute","passagePhrase":"artificially control the atmosphere ... simulate the effects of high altitude"},{"uid":"4bd4f76f-5965-4018-9628-b5d27f175938","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"In 2006, WADA considered whether","passagePhrase":"In 2006, WADA"},{"uid":"4bd4f76f-5965-4018-9628-b5d27f175938 8f4d9cee-0893-438f-9f39-25c2057d94b4","qNum":"18 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"considered whether"},{"uid":"8f4d9cee-0893-438f-9f39-25c2057d94b4","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"an ethical challenge","passagePhrase":"should be prohibited"},{"uid":"7a182c8f-4556-49d9-be8e-3ffe703307fe 8f4d9cee-0893-438f-9f39-25c2057d94b4","qNum":"18 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"artificially induced hypoxic conditions"},{"uid":"8f4d9cee-0893-438f-9f39-25c2057d94b4 b5f0a175-de73-468b-a25b-09954e020145","qNum":"18 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Its ethics panel concluded that hypoxic devices were contrary to the spirit of sport"},{"uid":"44a20d95-d88f-41fb-b42d-783fc4be9adb","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"ultimately decided not to add them to its Prohibited List","passagePhrase":"WADA"},{"uid":"44a20d95-d88f-41fb-b42d-783fc4be9adb d173b6b2-f11c-4d26-9c21-712d1426f082","qNum":"18 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"decided not to add them to its Prohibited List"},{"uid":"d173b6b2-f11c-4d26-9c21-712d1426f082","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"survives","passagePhrase":"routinely used by athletes"},{"uid":"bd2cf366-c5b6-4db1-bd8b-e4af76d62c44","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Success","passagePhrase":"a staggering 105 world records were broken ... the vast majority achieved by competitors wearing the new Speedo LZR Racer suit ... more records were broken"},{"uid":"cedba363-6102-4f96-96d3-02a01d15916e","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"the LZR swimsuit","passagePhrase":"These suits"},{"uid":"c54da8e7-38db-4b71-8292-35f2ef13df5a","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"a special fabric","passagePhrase":"a high-tech fabric"},{"uid":"739995df-efa3-4fe7-8649-10a540da21c3","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"reduces","passagePhrase":"reduces"},{"uid":"2b5c08ba-01ad-43d7-9ba3-e118ba3a89bc","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"improves buoyancy","passagePhrase":"improves buoyancy"},{"uid":"057314a7-8947-4f15-afec-d4a00f49338c cedba363-6102-4f96-96d3-02a01d15916e","qNum":"19 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The LZR"},{"uid":"057314a7-8947-4f15-afec-d4a00f49338c","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"an approved innovation","passagePhrase":"was initially sanctioned by FINA"},{"uid":"36aeb8e4-17c5-46db-90df-940347423f7a","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"turns ... into a regulatory problem","passagePhrase":"became increasingly controversial"},{"uid":"05f79a00-f5ce-4e3d-b69b-d7c2023d9a71 36aeb8e4-17c5-46db-90df-940347423f7a","qNum":"19 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"FINA changed its mind ... banning all suits made with this high-tech fabric"},{"uid":"2a49b332-b1f4-4d54-8d16-f36f02e987c7","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"Athletes believe","passagePhrase":"Athletes believe"},{"uid":"32906c1a-46cb-4ec5-8a00-73662bf5d966","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"need to keep setting new","passagePhrase":"need records all the time"},{"uid":"6e7bc4c0-64a5-432d-b160-59dfa15e462c","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"seek to do so through improvements","passagePhrase":"The only way athletes can continue to break records is by improving"},{"uid":"aa9ab6cb-58b4-461f-9430-14fc25d09bf6 e3dc5662-74b0-402b-ba25-16205fe24e6d","qNum":"20 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"when a new technology is invented ... whether to embrace or reject it"},{"uid":"aa9ab6cb-58b4-461f-9430-14fc25d09bf6 f6bf43ab-285e-4266-8fa6-b86863132a51","qNum":"20 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the relevant sports authority"},{"uid":"aa9ab6cb-58b4-461f-9430-14fc25d09bf6","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"sporting innovation","passagePhrase":"has to consider"},{"uid":"fe011424-fb14-437b-bd94-d01d4c2758cf","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"granted permission ... banned"},{"uid":"6f7595f1-fc32-4f6e-b5a4-3a39041dfc2b f6bf43ab-285e-4266-8fa6-b86863132a51","qNum":"20 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"rulings"},{"uid":"6f7595f1-fc32-4f6e-b5a4-3a39041dfc2b","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"consistent criteria","passagePhrase":"arbitrary ... arguments have to be examined and weighed ... the rules of logic ought to apply in every case"},{"uid":"6f7595f1-fc32-4f6e-b5a4-3a39041dfc2b cf491f6c-617d-4fac-a1b7-35354e529f63","qNum":"20 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"should not appear"},{"uid":"28a15827-b7e4-4612-b503-4a2121233f28","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"reputation","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"aa9ab6cb-58b4-461f-9430-14fc25d09bf6 fe011424-fb14-437b-bd94-d01d4c2758cf","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"regulating","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"176c7aca-da00-47cd-96dc-799207aaae66","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"A concern","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"6031e048-6a51-4442-87c1-9768c653ac6f","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"dismissed","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"4ffcc3e1-441a-4f40-9ed2-5b9e70818d3c a17dfb77-af66-4872-b87b-5e6e395c034c","qNum":"21 22","questionPhrase":"were not taken into account","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"7a182c8f-4556-49d9-be8e-3ffe703307fe","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"artificially created low-oxygen conditions","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"b5f0a175-de73-468b-a25b-09954e020145","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"its ethics panel objected to the use of such devices","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"05f79a00-f5ce-4e3d-b69b-d7c2023d9a71","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"was eventually banned","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"f6bf43ab-285e-4266-8fa6-b86863132a51","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"decisions by sports authorities","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"e3dc5662-74b0-402b-ba25-16205fe24e6d","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"about new technologies","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"cf491f6c-617d-4fac-a1b7-35354e529f63","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"should never seem","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_108":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>Elephant Communication</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>O’Connell-Rodwell, a postdoctoral researcher at Stanford University, has travelled to Namibia’s first-ever wildlife reserve to explore the mystical and complicated realm of elephant communication. She, along with her colleagues, is part of a scientific revolution that started almost 20 years ago. This revolution has led to a remarkable discovery: elephants are capable of communicating with each other over long distances using infrasound, low-frequency sound that is below the range of human hearing.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>As might be expected, the ability of African elephants to detect seismic signals may be related to their ears. The hammer bone in an elephant’s middle ear is proportionally huge for a mammal, but it is rather normal for animals that use vibrational signals. This may suggest that elephants can use seismic signals to communicate.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>Other aspects of elephant anatomy also support this ability. First, their massive bodies, which enable them to give out low-frequency sounds almost as powerful as the sound a jet makes during takeoff, serve as ideal frames for receiving ground vibrations and transmitting them to the inner ear. Second, the elephant’s toe bones are set on a fatty pad, which might be of help when focusing vibrations from the ground into the bone. Finally, the elephant has an enormous brain that sits in the cranial cavity behind the eyes in line with the auditory canal. The front of the skull is riddled with sinus cavities, which might function as resonating chambers for ground vibrations.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>It remains unclear how the elephants detect such vibrations, but O’Connell-Rodwell suggests that the pachyderms are ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"66be7f73-0ff3-4ba1-8afa-b0a241b9c950\">listening<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>’ with their trunks and feet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"40bb1dd8-ca13-4b02-b601-0109570eedf7\">instead of their ears<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. The elephant trunk may just be the most versatile appendage in nature. Its utilization encompasses drinking, bathing, smelling, feeding, and scratching. Both trunk and feet contain two types of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"85cc116f-92a1-4024-94c6-7a68ab516669\">nerve endings that are sensitive to pressure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> – one <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"136893d6-763b-4b98-90d4-82dee4a7daab\">detects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> infrasonic vibration, and another <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"0cfe7372-a2f5-4f3f-be8a-1c85954a388d\">responds to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> vibrations at higher frequencies. In O’Connell-Rodwell’s view, this research has a boundless and unpredictable future. ‘Our work is really <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"fb67c275-d589-45ef-9e49-fad423a87a2d\">at the interface of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> geophysics, neurophysiology and ecology,’ she says. ‘We’re raising questions that have never even been considered before.’</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Scientists have long known that seismic communication is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"143df9df-7e55-4e75-96e7-558a345c9023\">widespread among small animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, such as spiders, scorpions, insects and many vertebrate species, such as white-lipped frogs, blind mole rats, kangaroo rats and golden moles. Nevertheless, O’Connell-Rodwell first argued that a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"54e77eb4-7d95-4da7-8d1f-4d7cf11bf181\">giant land animal is also<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0e418c9f-6172-4f92-8aa8-6819c82634a6\">sending and receiving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> seismic signals. ‘I used to lay a male planthopper on a stem and replay the calling sound of a female, and then the male would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"6e4adc98-eec1-43c7-b5ed-32b3182232d7\">exhibit the same kind of behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that happens in elephants—he would freeze, then press down on his legs, move forward a little, then stay still again. I find it so fascinating, and it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"7f87b5f5-8b3a-41c4-9d37-9f8bdfaf2bd7\">got me thinking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that perhaps auditory communication <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f10c3572-8d4c-4e18-813b-99c796ac1cf9\">is not the only thing that is going on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.’</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>Scientists have confirmed that an elephant’s capacity to communicate over long distances is essential for survival, especially in places like Etosha, where more than 2,400 savanna elephants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ae752bd5-9846-43ae-8524-f503a1b7c714\">range over an area larger than New Jersey<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e8f701f9-081e-4d38-b86b-52a0e40e20a5\">It is already difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> for an elephant to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"839ed4e2-b3ba-424e-be98-af6374c96a26\">find<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> a mate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ae752bd5-9846-43ae-8524-f503a1b7c714\">in such a vast wild land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, and elephants’ reproductive biology only complicates it. Breeding herds also use low-frequency sounds to send alerts regarding predators. Even though grown-up elephants have no predators other than humans, baby elephants are vulnerable to attacks by lions and hyenas. At the sight of a predator, older elephants in the herd will clump together for protection before running away.</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>We now know that elephants can respond to warning calls in the air, but can they detect signals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ecaf1a2e-44df-45df-a53f-67a7fed98955\">transmitted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> solely through the ground? To look into that matter, the research team designed an experiment in 2002, which used electronic devices that enabled them to transmit signals through the ground at Mushara. ‘The outcomes of our 2002 study revealed that elephants could indeed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"9316bcde-eeed-4b98-9e57-49c67d52bf7b\">sense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"fd602c33-e05b-44e8-afd0-65e7f7592ac4\">warning signals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> through the ground,’ O’Connell-Rodwell observes.</span></p><p><b><span>H. </span></b><span>A later experiment was designed to investigate these responses further. It used three different recordings—the 1994 warning call from Mushara, an anti-predator call recorded by scientist Joyce Poole in Kenya and a made-up warble tone. ‘The data I’ve observed to this point implies that the elephants were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"254990b3-e685-4c09-a1af-60501d04a1a3\">responding the way I always expected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"1775937d-8713-4fe3-b96e-7f3a54f16e26\">the fascinating finding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"1775937d-8713-4fe3-b96e-7f3a54f16e26\">the anti-predator call from Kenya<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, which is unfamiliar to them, caused them to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"52845c25-9030-4d5e-9ef0-24caad86b196\">gather around, tense up, and rumble aggressively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> as well—but they didn’t always flee. I <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"7c7bcc7f-e6f1-4c2a-ad70-e22ff3f30eff\">didn’t expect the results to be that clear-cut<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.’</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Label the diagram below. Choose </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 27-31. </span></p><p> <span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_4/reading/images/ea50283af92d3d1803c619e9bbc856256ff11411ff535e2b32cda44ea7f0d7cb.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326345\" id=\"question-wrapper-326345\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HAMMER</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326346\" id=\"question-wrapper-326346\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MASSIVE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326347\" id=\"question-wrapper-326347\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PAD</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326348\" id=\"question-wrapper-326348\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(ENORMOUS) BRAIN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326349\" id=\"question-wrapper-326349\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(SINUS) CAVITIES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below. Choose</span><b><span> NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-38.</span></p><p><b><span>How vibration-based communication may work</span></b></p><p><span>O'Connell-Rodwell argues that elephants may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"40bb1dd8-ca13-4b02-b601-0109570eedf7\">not rely primarily on their ears<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"9316bcde-eeed-4b98-9e57-49c67d52bf7b\">detect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> vibrations. Instead, these signals may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"66be7f73-0ff3-4ba1-8afa-b0a241b9c950\">picked up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> through their (32)__________, which contain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"85cc116f-92a1-4024-94c6-7a68ab516669\">pressure-sensitive nerve endings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> responsive to different frequency ranges. One type <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"136893d6-763b-4b98-90d4-82dee4a7daab\">is sensitive to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> (33)__________ vibration, while the other <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"0cfe7372-a2f5-4f3f-be8a-1c85954a388d\">reacts to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> higher frequencies.</span></p><p><span>Beyond this physical mechanism, her research <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"fb67c275-d589-45ef-9e49-fad423a87a2d\">combines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> geophysics, neurophysiology and (34)_______. This interdisciplinary approach has allowed her to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"54e77eb4-7d95-4da7-8d1f-4d7cf11bf181\">extend to elephants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> a form of communication already <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"143df9df-7e55-4e75-96e7-558a345c9023\">documented in much smaller animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, involving the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0e418c9f-6172-4f92-8aa8-6819c82634a6\">transmission and reception<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of (35)__________. Earlier observations of planthoppers had also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"7f87b5f5-8b3a-41c4-9d37-9f8bdfaf2bd7\">led her to question<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> whether (36)__________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"f10c3572-8d4c-4e18-813b-99c796ac1cf9\">alone could account for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"6e4adc98-eec1-43c7-b5ed-32b3182232d7\">behavioural pattern she observed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The value of long-distance signalling is particularly apparent where elephants are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ae752bd5-9846-43ae-8524-f503a1b7c714\">widely dispersed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, since an individual may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e8f701f9-081e-4d38-b86b-52a0e40e20a5\">have difficulty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"839ed4e2-b3ba-424e-be98-af6374c96a26\">locating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> a (37)__________. Such signalling also has a defensive function. Later experiments showed that elephants could detect <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"fd602c33-e05b-44e8-afd0-65e7f7592ac4\">warning information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> even when the signal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ecaf1a2e-44df-45df-a53f-67a7fed98955\">travelled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> solely through the (38)__________.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326350\" id=\"question-wrapper-326350\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUNKS AND FEET</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326351\" id=\"question-wrapper-326351\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INFRASONIC</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326352\" id=\"question-wrapper-326352\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ECOLOGY</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326353\" id=\"question-wrapper-326353\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(SEISMIC) SIGNALS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326354\" id=\"question-wrapper-326354\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AUDITORY COMMUNICATION</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326355\" id=\"question-wrapper-326355\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MATE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326356\" id=\"question-wrapper-326356\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GROUND</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 39-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326357\" id=\"question-wrapper-326357\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the elephants' response to the Kenyan call indicate?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Elephants only recognise threats communicated by calls from their own group.</li> <li>B. An unfamiliar warning call can still produce a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"52845c25-9030-4d5e-9ef0-24caad86b196\">defensive response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Elephants react in the same way to warning calls and artificial sounds.</li> <li>D. Unfamiliar calls cause elephants to flee immediately.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326358\" id=\"question-wrapper-326358\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>How did O'Connell-Rodwell view the results of the later experiment?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They challenged her earlier ideas about elephant communication.</li> <li>B. They were too inconsistent to support her expectations.</li> <li>C. They generally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"254990b3-e685-4c09-a1af-60501d04a1a3\">matched her expectations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"1775937d-8713-4fe3-b96e-7f3a54f16e26\">one response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"7c7bcc7f-e6f1-4c2a-ad70-e22ff3f30eff\">clearer than expected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> <li>D. They showed that familiar and unfamiliar calls produced identical responses.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"66be7f73-0ff3-4ba1-8afa-b0a241b9c950","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"picked up","passagePhrase":"listening"},{"uid":"40bb1dd8-ca13-4b02-b601-0109570eedf7","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"not rely primarily on their ears","passagePhrase":"instead of their ears"},{"uid":"85cc116f-92a1-4024-94c6-7a68ab516669","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"pressure-sensitive nerve endings","passagePhrase":"nerve endings that are sensitive to pressure"},{"uid":"136893d6-763b-4b98-90d4-82dee4a7daab","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"is sensitive to","passagePhrase":"detects"},{"uid":"0cfe7372-a2f5-4f3f-be8a-1c85954a388d","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"reacts to","passagePhrase":"responds to"},{"uid":"fb67c275-d589-45ef-9e49-fad423a87a2d","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"combines","passagePhrase":"at the interface of"},{"uid":"143df9df-7e55-4e75-96e7-558a345c9023","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"documented in much smaller animals","passagePhrase":"widespread among small animals"},{"uid":"54e77eb4-7d95-4da7-8d1f-4d7cf11bf181","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"extend to elephants","passagePhrase":"giant land animal is also"},{"uid":"0e418c9f-6172-4f92-8aa8-6819c82634a6","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"transmission and reception","passagePhrase":"sending and receiving"},{"uid":"6e4adc98-eec1-43c7-b5ed-32b3182232d7","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"behavioural pattern she observed","passagePhrase":"exhibit the same kind of behaviour"},{"uid":"7f87b5f5-8b3a-41c4-9d37-9f8bdfaf2bd7","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"led her to question","passagePhrase":"got me thinking"},{"uid":"f10c3572-8d4c-4e18-813b-99c796ac1cf9","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"alone could account for","passagePhrase":"is not the only thing that is going on"},{"uid":"ae752bd5-9846-43ae-8524-f503a1b7c714","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"widely dispersed","passagePhrase":"range over an area larger than New Jersey ... in such a vast wild land"},{"uid":"e8f701f9-081e-4d38-b86b-52a0e40e20a5","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"have difficulty","passagePhrase":"It is already difficult"},{"uid":"839ed4e2-b3ba-424e-be98-af6374c96a26","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"locating","passagePhrase":"find"},{"uid":"ecaf1a2e-44df-45df-a53f-67a7fed98955","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"travelled","passagePhrase":"transmitted"},{"uid":"9316bcde-eeed-4b98-9e57-49c67d52bf7b","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"detect","passagePhrase":"sense"},{"uid":"fd602c33-e05b-44e8-afd0-65e7f7592ac4","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"warning information","passagePhrase":"warning signals"},{"uid":"254990b3-e685-4c09-a1af-60501d04a1a3","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"matched her expectations","passagePhrase":"responding the way I always expected"},{"uid":"1775937d-8713-4fe3-b96e-7f3a54f16e26","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"one response","passagePhrase":"the fascinating finding ... the anti-predator call from Kenya"},{"uid":"52845c25-9030-4d5e-9ef0-24caad86b196","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"defensive response","passagePhrase":"gather around, tense up, and rumble aggressively"},{"uid":"7c7bcc7f-e6f1-4c2a-ad70-e22ff3f30eff","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"clearer than expected","passagePhrase":"didn’t expect the results to be that clear-cut"}]},"reading_u2_109":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>Lie Detector</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p><span>However much we may abhor it, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"34d03f1d-c3ec-480e-be01-516c56f04a1c\">deception comes naturally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"3981ccb6-89bf-4f16-9f84-1239fef1194d\">all living things<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. Birds do it by feigning injury to lead hungry predators away from nesting young. Spider crabs do it by disguise: adorning themselves with strips of kelp and other debris, they pretend to be something they are not - and so escape their enemies. Nature amply rewards successful <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"21c81fab-9fa3-480c-8668-a663154e3979\">deceive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>rs by allowing them to survive long enough to mate and reproduce. So it may come as no surprise to learn that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"72b97e33-1aad-4976-a51c-cebd62875d9d\">human beings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>–who, according to psychologist Gerald Jellison of the University of Southern California, are lied to about 200 times a day, roughly one untruth every five minutes–often deceive for exactly the same reasons: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c6ad9a3c-7087-4818-a861-9b02d92d5625\">to save their own skins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"a3ad8e38-09ef-42b9-ad32-a1bcb15b0012\">to get something they can’t get by other means<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p><span>But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"35dcd637-e25e-494a-877d-b3375c5d85a2\">knowing how to catch deceit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e8c564ad-f302-40fb-84ce-7f847b3f0902\">just as important a survival skill<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"89afdcb1-cce3-47a7-9055-768aa2c60cea\">knowing how to tell a lie and get away with it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. A person able to spot falsehood quickly is unlikely to be swindled by an unscrupulous business associate or hoodwinked by a devious spouse. Luckily, nature provides more than enough clues to trap dissemblers in their own tangled webs - if you know where to look. By closely observing facial expressions, body language and tone of voice, practically anyone can recognize the telltale signs of lying. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"0bc90383-cc14-4501-a688-5c3f23d486b8\">Researchers are even programming computers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>–like those used in lie detectors - to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"0d8f1d2f-2518-4e82-9c1a-e01e6ef0cf07\">get at the truth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> by analyzing <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"555253cc-7dde-46c3-bba7-57b41c5a1d2f\">the same physical cues available to the naked eye and ear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. “With the proper training, many people can learn to reliably detect lies,” says Paul Ekman, professor of psychology at the University of California, San Francisco, who has spent the past 15 years studying the secret art of deception.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p><span>In order to know what kind of lies work best, successful liars need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a5de86bb-572d-46f3-b2c1-42ca77ec6d79\">accurately assess other people’s emotional states<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. Ekman’s research shows that this same emotional intelligence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"1f8f3eb8-583d-43b3-9d80-805cf8499c0b\">is essential for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"34569e5f-f270-49e7-88b2-3675b30fd50a\">good lie detectors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, too. The emotional state to watch out for is stress, which may result from the conflict between the truth and what liars actually say or do.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p><span>Even high-tech lie detectors don’t detect lies as such; they merely detect the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9eba75ee-5963-4b03-a781-6a5c4da787f9\">physical cues of emotions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, which may or may not correspond to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"02d69653-d96e-4432-8a00-1c502271d28f\">what the person being tested is saying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. Polygraphs, for instance, measure <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9eba75ee-5963-4b03-a781-6a5c4da787f9\">respiration, heart rate and skin conductivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, which tend to increase when people are nervous–as they usually are when lying. Nervous people typically perspire, and the salts contained in perspiration conduct electricity. That’s why a sudden leap in skin conductivity indicates nervousness–perhaps about being caught—which could, in turn, suggest that someone is being economical with the truth. On the other hand, it might also mean that the lights in the television studio are too hot–which is one reason polygraph tests are inadmissible in court. “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"720c6448-3cf2-4894-9661-d8ae9345ae06\">Good lie detectors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9c3cb345-e205-4ce3-b4de-26ad5612582f\">don’t rely on a single sign<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>,” Ekman says, “but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4157a644-4d75-4e82-af2a-921a43373508\">interpret<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9c3cb345-e205-4ce3-b4de-26ad5612582f\">clusters of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a61276e9-2c6c-4603-9aa2-7d8a3857385a\">verbal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"e70c4af7-3945-4aab-9dee-81a0cedfebaf\">nonverbal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> clues that suggest someone might be lying.”</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p><span>Those clues are written all over the face. Because the musculature of the face is directly connected to the areas of the brain that process emotion, the countenance can be a window to the soul. Neurological studies even suggest that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"cc5e9bde-5a5d-40f6-a0ca-89cac1b40b0c\">genuine emotions travel different pathways through the brain than insincere ones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. If a patient paralyzed by a stroke on one side of the face, for example, is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"424a2539-9e5d-4c02-94c4-9cd44082e709\">asked to smile deliberately<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, only the mobile side of the mouth is raised. But tell that same person a funny joke, and the patient breaks into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"f53eee7f-25cd-4b97-8ce0-b385edc7c827\">a full and spontaneous smile<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. Very few people–most notably, actors and politicians–<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"2bd12637-cc6d-49e5-ae15-ad575aa5c4be\">are able to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f6a19f84-60e5-4f84-a926-b067401b7621\">consciously control all of their facial expressions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Lies can often be caught when the liar’s true feelings briefly leak through the mask of deception. “We don’t think before we feel,” Ekman says. “Expressions tend to show up on the face before we’re even conscious of experiencing an emotion.”</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b59e59e4-8f9e-4e9e-aafe-77e611bad0bb\">One of the most difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> facial expressions <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b59e59e4-8f9e-4e9e-aafe-77e611bad0bb\">to </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"25d4318f-0c91-42c8-b124-b07c9b850be2 b59e59e4-8f9e-4e9e-aafe-77e611bad0bb\">fake</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b59e59e4-8f9e-4e9e-aafe-77e611bad0bb\"> - or </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b14fbca2-1884-48db-bdcf-8fb1a54af616 b59e59e4-8f9e-4e9e-aafe-77e611bad0bb\">conceal</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b14fbca2-1884-48db-bdcf-8fb1a54af616\">, if it is genuinely felt</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>–is sadness. When someone is truly sad, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"cf235085-495e-4867-b9ec-1c3e84603d80\">the forehead wrinkles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> with grief and the inner corners of the eyebrows are pulled up. Fewer than 15% of the people Ekman tested were able to produce this eyebrow movement voluntarily. By contrast, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"ec0660ef-ecce-4dfa-b8a4-14eb9c43d76a\">the lowering of the eyebrows<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> associated with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"720aadab-9ee2-4242-bcad-2f9281ed74fc\">an angry scowl<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"52d13cc7-c35b-4586-bfb5-413575a59198\">replicated at will<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"e1d2cca3-fefc-4a00-95a5-d5404cb53dec\">almost everybody<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. “If someone claims they are sad and the inner corners of their eyebrows don’t go up,” Ekman says, “the sadness is probably false.”</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b></p><p><span>The smile, on the other hand, is one of the easiest facial expressions to counterfeit. It takes just two muscles–the zygomaticus major muscles that extend from the cheekbones to the corners of the lips–to produce a grin. But there’s a catch. A genuine smile affects not only the corners of the lips but also the orbicularis oculi, the muscle around the eye that produces the distinctive “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"59d639f0-1496-4501-98b6-0920f1f03080\">crow's-feet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>” associated with people who laugh a lot. A counterfeit grin can be unmasked if the lip corners go up, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"59d639f0-1496-4501-98b6-0920f1f03080\">the eyes crinkle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> but the inner corners of the eyebrows are not lowered, a movement controlled by the orbicularis oculi that is difficult to fake. The absence of lowered eyebrows is one reason why false smiles look so strained and stiff.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326359\" id=\"question-wrapper-326359\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"3981ccb6-89bf-4f16-9f84-1239fef1194d\">Every kind of creature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"34d03f1d-c3ec-480e-be01-516c56f04a1c\">is capable of deceit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326360\" id=\"question-wrapper-326360\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"72b97e33-1aad-4976-a51c-cebd62875d9d\">People<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> are more likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"21c81fab-9fa3-480c-8668-a663154e3979\">lie<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"a3ad8e38-09ef-42b9-ad32-a1bcb15b0012\">personal gain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> than to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c6ad9a3c-7087-4818-a861-9b02d92d5625\">protect themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326361\" id=\"question-wrapper-326361\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"89afdcb1-cce3-47a7-9055-768aa2c60cea\">Deceiving successfully<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"35dcd637-e25e-494a-877d-b3375c5d85a2\">recognizing deception<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e8c564ad-f302-40fb-84ce-7f847b3f0902\">equally valuable for survival<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326362\" id=\"question-wrapper-326362\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"0bc90383-cc14-4501-a688-5c3f23d486b8\">Computers are being trained by scientists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"0d8f1d2f-2518-4e82-9c1a-e01e6ef0cf07\">identify deception<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> from <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"555253cc-7dde-46c3-bba7-57b41c5a1d2f\">signals that a human observer would miss<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326363\" id=\"question-wrapper-326363\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a5de86bb-572d-46f3-b2c1-42ca77ec6d79\">Reading how other people feel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> is a skill that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"1f8f3eb8-583d-43b3-9d80-805cf8499c0b\">benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> both liars and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"34569e5f-f270-49e7-88b2-3675b30fd50a\">those trying to catch them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 6-9 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326364\" id=\"question-wrapper-326364\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>How does a lie detector work?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It detects whether a person's emotional state is stable.</li> <li>B. It detects <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9eba75ee-5963-4b03-a781-6a5c4da787f9\">physical reactions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"02d69653-d96e-4432-8a00-1c502271d28f\">while a person is speaking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</li> <li>C. It detects a person's level of brain activity.</li> <li>D. It analyses a person's spoken answers word by word.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326365\" id=\"question-wrapper-326365\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does Ekman’s comment at the end of paragraph D imply about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"720c6448-3cf2-4894-9661-d8ae9345ae06\">effective lie detection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Each clue needs to be interpreted separately before the different results are compared.</li> <li>B. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"e70c4af7-3945-4aab-9dee-81a0cedfebaf\">physical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> reaction becomes significant when it conflicts with what the person is saying.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"4157a644-4d75-4e82-af2a-921a43373508\">A judgement should be based on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9c3cb345-e205-4ce3-b4de-26ad5612582f\">the overall pattern formed by several<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a61276e9-2c6c-4603-9aa2-7d8a3857385a\">spoken<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and physical <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9c3cb345-e205-4ce3-b4de-26ad5612582f\">signs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Spoken clues are mainly useful when physical measurements produce an uncertain result.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326366\" id=\"question-wrapper-326366\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the example of the stroke patient contribute to the writer’s argument?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It suggests why people with facial paralysis may find it harder to conceal what they are feeling.</li> <li>B. It shows that emotional stimulation can temporarily restore voluntary movement to muscles affected by stroke.</li> <li>C. It demonstrates that genuine <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"424a2539-9e5d-4c02-94c4-9cd44082e709\">expressions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> depend more heavily on the unaffected side of the face.</li> <li>D. It supports the idea that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"424a2539-9e5d-4c02-94c4-9cd44082e709\">deliberate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"f53eee7f-25cd-4b97-8ce0-b385edc7c827\">spontaneous expressions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> arise through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"cc5e9bde-5a5d-40f6-a0ca-89cac1b40b0c\">different neural processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326367\" id=\"question-wrapper-326367\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer refers to politicians as examples of people who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"2bd12637-cc6d-49e5-ae15-ad575aa5c4be\">can<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f6a19f84-60e5-4f84-a926-b067401b7621\">keep their true feelings from appearing on their face<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</li> <li>B. become aware of an emotion before it shows on their face.</li> <li>C. hide what they feel by controlling their voice.</li> <li>D. experience emotions less strongly than others.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements about facial expressions and the list of emotions below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct emotion, A, B or C.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 10–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>NB You may use any letter more than once.</span></p><p><b><span>List of emotions</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A. </span></b><span>Happiness</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span>Anger</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span>Sadness</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326368\" id=\"question-wrapper-326368\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"e1d2cca3-fefc-4a00-95a5-d5404cb53dec\">Nearly everyone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"52d13cc7-c35b-4586-bfb5-413575a59198\">deliberately produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"ec0660ef-ecce-4dfa-b8a4-14eb9c43d76a\">the eyebrow movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> linked to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"720aadab-9ee2-4242-bcad-2f9281ed74fc\">this emotion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326369\" id=\"question-wrapper-326369\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"59d639f0-1496-4501-98b6-0920f1f03080\">Lines appear at the outer edges of the eyes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326370\" id=\"question-wrapper-326370\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"cf235085-495e-4867-b9ec-1c3e84603d80\">Lines form above the eyebrows<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326371\" id=\"question-wrapper-326371\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b14fbca2-1884-48db-bdcf-8fb1a54af616\">Hiding this emotion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b59e59e4-8f9e-4e9e-aafe-77e611bad0bb\">is as hard as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"25d4318f-0c91-42c8-b124-b07c9b850be2\">pretending to feel it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"34d03f1d-c3ec-480e-be01-516c56f04a1c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"is capable of deceit","passagePhrase":"deception comes naturally"},{"uid":"3981ccb6-89bf-4f16-9f84-1239fef1194d","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Every kind of creature","passagePhrase":"all living things"},{"uid":"21c81fab-9fa3-480c-8668-a663154e3979","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"lie","passagePhrase":"deceive"},{"uid":"72b97e33-1aad-4976-a51c-cebd62875d9d","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"People","passagePhrase":"human beings"},{"uid":"c6ad9a3c-7087-4818-a861-9b02d92d5625","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"protect themselves","passagePhrase":"to save their own skins"},{"uid":"a3ad8e38-09ef-42b9-ad32-a1bcb15b0012","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"personal gain","passagePhrase":"to get something they can’t get by other means"},{"uid":"35dcd637-e25e-494a-877d-b3375c5d85a2","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"recognizing deception","passagePhrase":"knowing how to catch deceit"},{"uid":"e8c564ad-f302-40fb-84ce-7f847b3f0902","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"equally valuable for survival","passagePhrase":"just as important a survival skill"},{"uid":"89afdcb1-cce3-47a7-9055-768aa2c60cea","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Deceiving successfully","passagePhrase":"knowing how to tell a lie and get away with it"},{"uid":"0bc90383-cc14-4501-a688-5c3f23d486b8","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Computers are being trained by scientists","passagePhrase":"Researchers are even programming computers"},{"uid":"0d8f1d2f-2518-4e82-9c1a-e01e6ef0cf07","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"identify deception","passagePhrase":"get at the truth"},{"uid":"a5de86bb-572d-46f3-b2c1-42ca77ec6d79","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Reading how other people feel","passagePhrase":"accurately assess other people’s emotional states"},{"uid":"1f8f3eb8-583d-43b3-9d80-805cf8499c0b","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"benefits","passagePhrase":"is essential for"},{"uid":"34569e5f-f270-49e7-88b2-3675b30fd50a","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"those trying to catch them","passagePhrase":"good lie detectors"},{"uid":"9eba75ee-5963-4b03-a781-6a5c4da787f9","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"physical reactions","passagePhrase":"physical cues of emotions ... respiration, heart rate and skin conductivity"},{"uid":"02d69653-d96e-4432-8a00-1c502271d28f","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"while a person is speaking","passagePhrase":"what the person being tested is saying"},{"uid":"720c6448-3cf2-4894-9661-d8ae9345ae06","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"effective lie detection","passagePhrase":"Good lie detectors"},{"uid":"9c3cb345-e205-4ce3-b4de-26ad5612582f","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"the overall pattern formed by several ... signs","passagePhrase":"don’t rely on a single sign ... clusters of"},{"uid":"4157a644-4d75-4e82-af2a-921a43373508","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"A judgement should be based on","passagePhrase":"interpret"},{"uid":"a61276e9-2c6c-4603-9aa2-7d8a3857385a","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"spoken","passagePhrase":"verbal"},{"uid":"e70c4af7-3945-4aab-9dee-81a0cedfebaf","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"physical","passagePhrase":"nonverbal"},{"uid":"cc5e9bde-5a5d-40f6-a0ca-89cac1b40b0c","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"different neural processes","passagePhrase":"genuine emotions travel different pathways through the brain than insincere ones"},{"uid":"424a2539-9e5d-4c02-94c4-9cd44082e709","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"expressions ... deliberate","passagePhrase":"asked to smile deliberately"},{"uid":"f53eee7f-25cd-4b97-8ce0-b385edc7c827","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"spontaneous expressions","passagePhrase":"a full and spontaneous smile"},{"uid":"2bd12637-cc6d-49e5-ae15-ad575aa5c4be","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"can","passagePhrase":"are able to"},{"uid":"f6a19f84-60e5-4f84-a926-b067401b7621","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"keep their true feelings from appearing on their face","passagePhrase":"consciously control all of their facial expressions"},{"uid":"b59e59e4-8f9e-4e9e-aafe-77e611bad0bb","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"is as hard as","passagePhrase":"One of the most difficult ... to ... - or"},{"uid":"25d4318f-0c91-42c8-b124-b07c9b850be2 b59e59e4-8f9e-4e9e-aafe-77e611bad0bb","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fake"},{"uid":"b14fbca2-1884-48db-bdcf-8fb1a54af616 b59e59e4-8f9e-4e9e-aafe-77e611bad0bb","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"conceal"},{"uid":"b14fbca2-1884-48db-bdcf-8fb1a54af616","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"Hiding this emotion","passagePhrase":", if it is genuinely felt"},{"uid":"cf235085-495e-4867-b9ec-1c3e84603d80","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Lines form above the eyebrows","passagePhrase":"the forehead wrinkles"},{"uid":"ec0660ef-ecce-4dfa-b8a4-14eb9c43d76a","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the eyebrow movement","passagePhrase":"the lowering of the eyebrows"},{"uid":"720aadab-9ee2-4242-bcad-2f9281ed74fc","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"this emotion","passagePhrase":"an angry scowl"},{"uid":"52d13cc7-c35b-4586-bfb5-413575a59198","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"deliberately produce","passagePhrase":"replicated at will"},{"uid":"e1d2cca3-fefc-4a00-95a5-d5404cb53dec","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"Nearly everyone","passagePhrase":"almost everybody"},{"uid":"59d639f0-1496-4501-98b6-0920f1f03080","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Lines appear at the outer edges of the eyes","passagePhrase":"crow's-feet ... the eyes crinkle"},{"uid":"25d4318f-0c91-42c8-b124-b07c9b850be2","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"pretending to feel it","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_110":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>Children’s Literature</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p><span>Stories and poems aimed at children have an exceedingly long history: lullabies, for example, were sung in Roman times, and a few nursery games and rhymes are almost as ancient. Yet so far as written-down literature is concerned, while there were <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"eb51e2b0-575b-452b-91c1-c5f072cd6426\">stories in print before 1700 that children often seized on when they had the chance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, such as translations of Aesop’s fables, fairy stories and popular ballads and romances, these were not aimed at young people in particular. Since the only genuinely child-oriented literature at this time would have been a few instructional works to help with reading and general knowledge, plus the odd Puritanical tract as an aid to morality, the only course for keen child readers was to read adult literature. This still occurs today, especially with adult thrillers or romances that include more exciting, graphic detail than is normally found in the literature for younger readers. </span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p><span>By the middle of the 18th century there were enough eager child readers, and enough parents glad to cater to this interest, for publishers to specialize in children’s books whose first aim was pleasure rather than education or morality. In Britain, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"91c0dcdf-d650-45dd-a460-47e46a3357b4\">a London merchant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> named Thomas Boreham produced Cajanus, the Swedish Giant in 1742, while the more famous John Newbery published A Little Pretty Pocket Book in 1744. Its contents—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"bfb3d5c3-0166-41f7-baed-8548ccf3a4d7\">rhymes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, stories, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a9237b8e-979c-44df-b803-12c1fb63ee5e\">children’s games<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3f5d9b1c-1978-44c9-86d1-4e4214444a94\">plus<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a65a544a-bd69-49f4-b377-06e1fdaba017\">a free gift<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> (‘A ball and a pincushion’)—in many ways anticipated the similar lucky-dip contents of twentieth-century children’s annuals. It is a tribute to Newbery’s flair that he hit upon a winning formula so quickly; the book <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"f957542c-7b21-4cff-921d-8ca5ebaa425d\">was pirated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"8a9b8006-30af-42f2-9ca9-6a866c3d5e69\">almost immediately<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in America.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p><span>Such pleasing levity was not to last. Influenced by Rousseau, whose Émile (1762) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a5420daa-e54f-45fd-9b70-dd75e7fc1160\">decreed that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"77255b80-3030-49b9-a03b-65dff217f046\">all books for children save Robinson Crusoe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a5420daa-e54f-45fd-9b70-dd75e7fc1160\">were a dangerous diversion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, contemporary critics saw to it that children’s literature should be instructive and uplifting. Prominent among such voices was Mrs. Sarah Trimmer, whose magazine The Guardian of Education (1802) carried the first regular reviews of children’s books. It was she who <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"cd3eb901-7589-4fda-8050-c7a8215e5882\">condemned </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"cd3eb901-7589-4fda-8050-c7a8215e5882 d41f66d2-1a60-4626-843d-4cb91ed8bf05\">fairy tales</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"cd3eb901-7589-4fda-8050-c7a8215e5882\"> for their violence and general absurdity</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2e44d34d-b89b-4ddc-8ae6-92c252956811\">Her own stories, Fabulous Histories (1786) described talking animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> who were always <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"40c8fd2d-63d5-436f-84d1-c28a8ee0b2ff\">models of sense and decorum<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p><span>So the moral story for children was always threatened from within, given the way children have of drawing out entertainment from the sternest moralist. But the greatest blow to the improving children’s book was to come from an unlikely source indeed: early 19th century <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4aa18be8-92fd-4123-8a74-efaf43ba7991\">interest in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> folklore. Both <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a4a018c2-0176-43d9-9bf2-45d034ceb364\">the Grimm brothers’ </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19 24\" data-uid=\"3f2ce3a0-1f02-4b8a-a061-a78bb137ef79 a4a018c2-0176-43d9-9bf2-45d034ceb364\">collection of fairy stories</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"4106ed33-3443-43a1-ae14-6703e52d0071\">swiftly translated into English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in 1823, and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"ea9d0c07-afdf-4548-989f-970b7e31161c\">the </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 24\" data-uid=\"675ffdd3-e1fb-46dd-bd49-b169c1f55c1b ea9d0c07-afdf-4548-989f-970b7e31161c\">nursery rhymes</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"ea9d0c07-afdf-4548-989f-970b7e31161c\"> selected by James Orchard Halliwell</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> for a folklore society in 1842 soon rocketed to popularity among young readers.This quickly led to new editions, each one more child-centred than the last. From now on younger children could expect stories written for their particular interest and with the needs of their own limited experience of life kept well to the fore.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p><span>What eventually determined the reading of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"e736ca93-0954-4b22-b394-14bf56dab349\">older children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> was often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"5c4d624f-e629-4ac7-9e04-affc8e35ef6a\">not the availability of special children’s literature as such but access to books<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> that contained <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"775e4c8d-f40b-40d9-b29e-5bb7f1a4b620\">characters, such as young people or animals, with whom they could more easily empathize<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, or action, such as exploring or fighting, that made few demands on adult maturity or understanding.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p><span>The final apotheosis of literary childhood as something to be protected from unpleasant reality came with the arrival in the late 1930s of child-centered best-sellers intended primarily as escapist entertainment. In Britain, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"86b73e1c-7579-4a61-9acb-ba9dc5f78a35\">novelists such as Enid Blyton and Richmal Crompton described children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> who were always free to have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"38d95631-2b16-461f-88a5-c40d505ab63c\">the most unlikely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> adventures, secure in the knowledge that nothing bad could ever happen to them in the end. The fact that war broke out again during the period of her books’ greatest popularity fails to register at all in the self-enclosed world inhabited by Enid Blyton’s young characters. Reaction against such dream-worlds was inevitable after World War II, coinciding with the growth of paperback sales, children’s libraries and a new spirit of moral and social concern. Urged on by committed publishers and progressive librarians, writers slowly began to explore new areas of interest while also shifting the settings of their plots from the middle-class world to which their chiefly adult patrons had always previously belonged.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b></p><p><span>Critical emphasis, during this development, has been divided. For some the most important task was to rid children’s books of the social prejudice and exclusiveness no longer found acceptable. Others concentrated more on the positive achievements of contemporary children’s literature. That <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"41d373ed-700f-447c-a713-25d14e28e166\">writers of these works<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"c71f333c-b734-4f1d-8dff-065999e6466d\">now<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e3eba4c5-2b36-4573-bd58-55c9a5530999\">recommended to adult as well as child readers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> echoes the 19th-century belief that children’s literature can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e3eba4c5-2b36-4573-bd58-55c9a5530999\">shared by the generations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, rather than being a defensive barrier between childhood and the necessary growth towards adult understanding.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the table below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.</span></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>DATE</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>FEATURES</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>AIM</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><span>EXAMPLE</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Before 1700</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Most printed stories were not specifically written for children</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Education and morality</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Puritanical tract</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>By the middle of 18th century</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a65a544a-bd69-49f4-b377-06e1fdaba017\">A bonus item<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> was included <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3f5d9b1c-1978-44c9-86d1-4e4214444a94\">alongside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"bfb3d5c3-0166-41f7-baed-8548ccf3a4d7\">verses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a9237b8e-979c-44df-b803-12c1fb63ee5e\">play ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and (14)________</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Pleasure</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>A Little Pretty Pocket Book - (15)________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"8a9b8006-30af-42f2-9ca9-6a866c3d5e69\">was quick to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"f957542c-7b21-4cff-921d-8ca5ebaa425d\">produce its own unauthorised version<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Early 19th century</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4aa18be8-92fd-4123-8a74-efaf43ba7991\">A growing enthusiasm for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> (16)________</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Greater appeal to children</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(17)________ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"675ffdd3-e1fb-46dd-bd49-b169c1f55c1b\">age-old verse for small children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Late 1930s</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"38d95631-2b16-461f-88a5-c40d505ab63c\">Improbable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> (18)________ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"86b73e1c-7579-4a61-9acb-ba9dc5f78a35\">young protagonists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Escapist entertainment</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Enid Blyton and Richmal Crompton’s novels</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326372\" id=\"question-wrapper-326372\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STORIES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326373\" id=\"question-wrapper-326373\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AMERICA</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326374\" id=\"question-wrapper-326374\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOLKLORE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326375\" id=\"question-wrapper-326375\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FAIRY STORIES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326376\" id=\"question-wrapper-326376\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ADVENTURES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 19–21) and the list of people below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct person, A–E.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–E, in boxes 19–21 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of people</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Thomas Boreham</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Sarah Trimmer</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. The Grimm Brothers</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. John Newbery</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. James Orchard Halliwell</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326377\" id=\"question-wrapper-326377\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"3f2ce3a0-1f02-4b8a-a061-a78bb137ef79\">Their stories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"4106ed33-3443-43a1-ae14-6703e52d0071\">became available to readers in English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326378\" id=\"question-wrapper-326378\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"2e44d34d-b89b-4ddc-8ae6-92c252956811\">characters created by them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"40c8fd2d-63d5-436f-84d1-c28a8ee0b2ff\">contrasted with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"cd3eb901-7589-4fda-8050-c7a8215e5882\">the features they criticised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"d41f66d2-1a60-4626-843d-4cb91ed8bf05\">another kind of children’s literature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326379\" id=\"question-wrapper-326379\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"91c0dcdf-d650-45dd-a460-47e46a3357b4\">main occupation was in commerce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> rather than in books.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text?</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326380\" id=\"question-wrapper-326380\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Children <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"eb51e2b0-575b-452b-91c1-c5f072cd6426\">did not start to read books until 1700<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326381\" id=\"question-wrapper-326381\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"77255b80-3030-49b9-a03b-65dff217f046\">one work of fiction escaped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a5420daa-e54f-45fd-9b70-dd75e7fc1160\">Rousseau's warning about what the young should read<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326382\" id=\"question-wrapper-326382\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"ea9d0c07-afdf-4548-989f-970b7e31161c\">Halliwell's collection of verses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> sold better than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a4a018c2-0176-43d9-9bf2-45d034ceb364\">the Grimm brothers' stories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326383\" id=\"question-wrapper-326383\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"e736ca93-0954-4b22-b394-14bf56dab349\">For older children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"775e4c8d-f40b-40d9-b29e-5bb7f1a4b620\">being able to identify with characters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"5c4d624f-e629-4ac7-9e04-affc8e35ef6a\">could be more important than whether a book was written specifically for children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326384\" id=\"question-wrapper-326384\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e3eba4c5-2b36-4573-bd58-55c9a5530999\">Appeal across age groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"c71f333c-b734-4f1d-8dff-065999e6466d\">currently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> a deliberate goal for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"41d373ed-700f-447c-a713-25d14e28e166\">authors of fiction for the young<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"91c0dcdf-d650-45dd-a460-47e46a3357b4","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"main occupation was in commerce","passagePhrase":"a London merchant"},{"uid":"bfb3d5c3-0166-41f7-baed-8548ccf3a4d7","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"verses","passagePhrase":"rhymes"},{"uid":"a9237b8e-979c-44df-b803-12c1fb63ee5e","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"play ideas","passagePhrase":"children’s games"},{"uid":"3f5d9b1c-1978-44c9-86d1-4e4214444a94","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"alongside","passagePhrase":"plus"},{"uid":"a65a544a-bd69-49f4-b377-06e1fdaba017","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"A bonus item","passagePhrase":"a free gift"},{"uid":"f957542c-7b21-4cff-921d-8ca5ebaa425d","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"produce its own unauthorised version","passagePhrase":"was pirated"},{"uid":"8a9b8006-30af-42f2-9ca9-6a866c3d5e69","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"was quick to","passagePhrase":"almost immediately"},{"uid":"a5420daa-e54f-45fd-9b70-dd75e7fc1160","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Rousseau's warning about what the young should read","passagePhrase":"decreed that ... were a dangerous diversion"},{"uid":"77255b80-3030-49b9-a03b-65dff217f046","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"one work of fiction escaped","passagePhrase":"all books for children save Robinson Crusoe"},{"uid":"cd3eb901-7589-4fda-8050-c7a8215e5882","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the features they criticised","passagePhrase":"condemned ... for their violence and general absurdity"},{"uid":"cd3eb901-7589-4fda-8050-c7a8215e5882 d41f66d2-1a60-4626-843d-4cb91ed8bf05","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fairy tales"},{"uid":"2e44d34d-b89b-4ddc-8ae6-92c252956811","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"characters created by them","passagePhrase":"Her own stories, Fabulous Histories (1786) described talking animals"},{"uid":"40c8fd2d-63d5-436f-84d1-c28a8ee0b2ff","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"contrasted with","passagePhrase":"models of sense and decorum"},{"uid":"4aa18be8-92fd-4123-8a74-efaf43ba7991","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"A growing enthusiasm for","passagePhrase":"interest in"},{"uid":"a4a018c2-0176-43d9-9bf2-45d034ceb364","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"the Grimm brothers' stories","passagePhrase":"the Grimm brothers’"},{"uid":"3f2ce3a0-1f02-4b8a-a061-a78bb137ef79 a4a018c2-0176-43d9-9bf2-45d034ceb364","qNum":"19 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"collection of fairy stories"},{"uid":"4106ed33-3443-43a1-ae14-6703e52d0071","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"became available to readers in English","passagePhrase":"swiftly translated into English"},{"uid":"ea9d0c07-afdf-4548-989f-970b7e31161c","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Halliwell's collection of verses","passagePhrase":"the ... selected by James Orchard Halliwell"},{"uid":"675ffdd3-e1fb-46dd-bd49-b169c1f55c1b ea9d0c07-afdf-4548-989f-970b7e31161c","qNum":"17 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"nursery rhymes"},{"uid":"e736ca93-0954-4b22-b394-14bf56dab349","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"For older children","passagePhrase":"older children"},{"uid":"5c4d624f-e629-4ac7-9e04-affc8e35ef6a","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"could be more important than whether a book was written specifically for children","passagePhrase":"not the availability of special children’s literature as such but access to books"},{"uid":"775e4c8d-f40b-40d9-b29e-5bb7f1a4b620","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"being able to identify with characters","passagePhrase":"characters, such as young people or animals, with whom they could more easily empathize"},{"uid":"86b73e1c-7579-4a61-9acb-ba9dc5f78a35","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"young protagonists","passagePhrase":"novelists such as Enid Blyton and Richmal Crompton described children"},{"uid":"38d95631-2b16-461f-88a5-c40d505ab63c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Improbable","passagePhrase":"the most unlikely"},{"uid":"41d373ed-700f-447c-a713-25d14e28e166","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"authors of fiction for the young","passagePhrase":"writers of these works"},{"uid":"c71f333c-b734-4f1d-8dff-065999e6466d","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"currently","passagePhrase":"now"},{"uid":"e3eba4c5-2b36-4573-bd58-55c9a5530999","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Appeal across age groups","passagePhrase":"recommended to adult as well as child readers ... shared by the generations"},{"uid":"675ffdd3-e1fb-46dd-bd49-b169c1f55c1b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"age-old verse for small children","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"3f2ce3a0-1f02-4b8a-a061-a78bb137ef79","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Their stories","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"d41f66d2-1a60-4626-843d-4cb91ed8bf05","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"another kind of children’s literature","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_111":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p> <b><span>All in the Family</span></b></p><p><i><span>A person’s brothers and sisters can have a powerful effect on their adult behaviour.</span></i></p><p><span>We can choose our friends, the saying goes, but we cannot choose our family of origin. Our parents <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"b372f05f-ad71-4f62-9346-437a079102f7\">provide our genetic material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"d2cbc450-7a6b-429a-beb0-666f4f5f5dbf\">serve as powerful early role models<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, but <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"af078f6a-83d3-4194-9a5c-f88271968c9c\">even more influential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in determining <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"a9c898ed-d49c-4188-814b-52fbc71a0558\">what kind of adults we become<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"e6f07c5d-484c-4bf9-8369-001a5041ff2b\">our brothers and sisters—our siblings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. They occupy a position of unique intimacy in our lives and cast a longer shadow than many recognise or are prepared to acknowledge. By turns enraging and lovable, familiar and mysterious, our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"13290cbe-cc8d-4b68-9c86-68ca69fef974\">brothers and sisters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> are the people who populate our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"61598edc-b945-4015-8e44-ce723a22a278\">first social relationships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. A sibling relationship is also the most enduring relationship many of us will ever have, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d4ee457f-d5ec-4736-b0ed-646b51f48992\">no less emotionally intense than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the bonds we form with our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"936b27c3-a099-4acb-899c-310f00656b90\">spouses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> and our own children, if only because it began when we were so young.</span></p><p><span>Research by Dr Gene Brody found that having <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"995da44a-0cf2-40df-9e6c-fa2fd0a869d3\">older children who do well at school and are well liked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> by other children can lead to parental ‘basking’, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"42f6e27c-d5f0-48a4-8aba-fdd0b341cc9d\">increasing mothers’ self-esteem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. This, in turn, is associated with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"42f6e27c-d5f0-48a4-8aba-fdd0b341cc9d\">more positive parenting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e5a32507-1e5f-4839-b550-7f4da85139d4\">younger children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e5a32507-1e5f-4839-b550-7f4da85139d4\">show fewer behavioural problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Conversely, parents whose first child is difficult may experience a negative spiral of tension within the household.</span></p><p><span>Rugby player Piri Weepu is known for his toughness, but at least some of this temperament was forged long ago in the family home. His older brother Billy began tackling Piri in rugby when he was just four, in an attempt to ‘harden him up’. It seemed to work: Piri followed his brother into an under-sevens league before he even started school. There are as many such stories as there are families. In the formative hothouse of the family, siblings interact in complex ways with the powerful forces of parents, genetics and personality already at work. It begins with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"10916f5a-be23-442e-8291-eb8c54abc6c4\">birth order<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, which determines <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"a82dc263-8cee-423f-8d75-617466f24f10\">childhood play roles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>: the firstborn as leader, the middle child as mediator and the youngest as rebel. These are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3cb4c85c-ddd8-4de5-9483-d4fdc8391b64\">roles that can persist throughout life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Clinical psychologist Claire Cartwright says she has clients who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"b00504f3-4ed4-4dff-884a-df8f7dca0415\">believe they were treated differently from their siblings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e1fa4051-454f-41b0-b76b-774b0c20ceca\">although this may not actually have been the case<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Some are convinced that one child in the family was preferred over the others, or that the judgements made about them were harsher and that they were always the ones who got into trouble. Later, in the workplace, such a person <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"cb7f0a7f-8962-4205-93b9-e69dabf495f0\">might become particularly defensive and behave in ways that attract harsh judgements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>However, being Mummy or Daddy’s favourite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"d85a5b00-a6a4-488a-b49c-064776f0a159\">has its own pitfalls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. If you were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"419e9aa9-71c9-482f-9ce1-37dcacf66f39\">the easy-going, cooperative child at home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, you probably became <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"cb06f9db-fda3-4afb-8aac-e7f97da1016d\">skilled at pleasing parents and, later, bosses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. But as an adult, you might find it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"cb06f9db-fda3-4afb-8aac-e7f97da1016d\">difficult to be assertive with authority figures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"cb06f9db-fda3-4afb-8aac-e7f97da1016d\">lack a clear sense of direction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. On the other hand, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"419e9aa9-71c9-482f-9ce1-37dcacf66f39\">a sibling who was disruptive and annoying as a child<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"d85a5b00-a6a4-488a-b49c-064776f0a159\">may later reinterpret that role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"d85a5b00-a6a4-488a-b49c-064776f0a159\">turning attention-seeking characteristics into </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"cb06f9db-fda3-4afb-8aac-e7f97da1016d d85a5b00-a6a4-488a-b49c-064776f0a159\">strengths</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"cb06f9db-fda3-4afb-8aac-e7f97da1016d\"> such as determination and leadership</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>How is it that full siblings, despite sharing DNA, can turn out so differently? One answer is that, in effect, each sibling grows up in a different family—a unique micro-culture. The firstborn, for example, is for a time an only child and therefore experiences the parents in a very different way from children born later. The parents themselves are changing too, experiencing hardship or good fortune, so <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f49857f0-9627-4a63-bcd0-c775a645eda3\">one sibling may grow up amid stability and closeness while another may be raised during a period of crisis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>There are, of course, many positive aspects of sibling relationships. Annette Henderson, a lecturer in psychology, says firstborn children learn vocabulary more quickly than their siblings because they do not have to compete for one-to-one time with their parents. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"8201fd21-4fdf-4f69-8a3c-f6f8dae6670c\">Younger children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, in turn, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"fe5e1e64-b2aa-46e5-9bee-d9afdfbc84fd\">benefit from unintentional instruction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"131f02b2-7a6b-43e1-b926-8a314e282ff9\">from their older brothers and sisters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"fe5e1e64-b2aa-46e5-9bee-d9afdfbc84fd\">acquiring entire phrases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"fe5e1e64-b2aa-46e5-9bee-d9afdfbc84fd\">an understanding of social concepts such as politeness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Similarly, a Cambridge University study of 140 children found that even where there was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"5923fae6-d4b0-479c-8844-c2164feaab54\">considerable conflict<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, siblings <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"1c5eda28-21ec-40a5-a103-54ff66976c6c\">still created<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> a rich world of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"bbc44da3-38f6-4f82-8d16-443ec728796e\">play and make-believe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that contributed to their development. Love–hate relationships were common, but even those who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"5923fae6-d4b0-479c-8844-c2164feaab54\">fought most frequently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> had as many positive interactions as other sibling pairs. Children also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e52ec37f-2f5f-4ecf-81ca-71eb7582885a\">compete for parental attention by differentiating themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> from their brothers and sisters, particularly when they are close in age. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f45c9592-1d1d-4f7d-8960-0cc26bf2162a\">A 2003 study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> of adolescents from 185 families found that those who differentiated themselves more strongly from their siblings received greater parental warmth and developed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"4a3c9f93-7c39-4475-9c71-75e9cce4022a\">stronger personalities and a clearer sense of identity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Another consideration is that contemporary <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"a3eb3efc-72f1-4320-859d-f36bff334728\">families<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> are often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"a3eb3efc-72f1-4320-859d-f36bff334728\">smaller<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> and more intimate than their historical counterparts. This may be advantageous because siblings in smaller families may <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"88614ffe-ace3-46f1-924c-5d2a65d815a4\">know one another better and remain </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"88614ffe-ace3-46f1-924c-5d2a65d815a4 9aaf9d41-b291-4b94-811c-0ec426570413\">lifelong</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"88614ffe-ace3-46f1-924c-5d2a65d815a4\"> friends</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, whereas those in larger or more widely spaced families may be more likely to lose touch <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"9aaf9d41-b291-4b94-811c-0ec426570413\">after leaving home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. A 2010 American study <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"30939a1f-6b3f-4049-b5a8-a5e100acc83b\">found that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> having a sister, whether younger or older, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"30939a1f-6b3f-4049-b5a8-a5e100acc83b\">meant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"7afc9dfd-ca10-413d-896d-e4f6e5c49f32\">10- to 14-year-olds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"468e14b0-228a-4d66-ac51-68cd5a8561e2\">less likely to feel lonely, unloved, self-conscious or fearful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. The same study found that having <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"baf7872a-0b75-4baf-b303-6b8c4a14fdc5\">a loving sibling of either gender<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8cc0067e-3ca0-4728-b86e-b5fe308aad08\">promoted more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"e6f15f2d-8bd2-4464-a9b1-7cd7493f67b2\">generous behaviour, such as helping a neighbour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> around the house or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"e6f15f2d-8bd2-4464-a9b1-7cd7493f67b2\">helping other children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> at school.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><b><span>YES</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NO</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NOT GIVEN </span></b><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326385\" id=\"question-wrapper-326385\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"b372f05f-ad71-4f62-9346-437a079102f7\">Genetic inheritance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"d2cbc450-7a6b-429a-beb0-666f4f5f5dbf\">parental influence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"af078f6a-83d3-4194-9a5c-f88271968c9c\">have a greater effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"a9c898ed-d49c-4188-814b-52fbc71a0558\">adult personality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"e6f07c5d-484c-4bf9-8369-001a5041ff2b\">relationships with siblings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326386\" id=\"question-wrapper-326386\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"61598edc-b945-4015-8e44-ce723a22a278\">The earliest social bonds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> people form tend to be with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"13290cbe-cc8d-4b68-9c86-68ca69fef974\">siblings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of their own gender.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326387\" id=\"question-wrapper-326387\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A person’s relationship with their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"936b27c3-a099-4acb-899c-310f00656b90\">husband or wife<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> usually <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d4ee457f-d5ec-4736-b0ed-646b51f48992\">involves stronger feelings than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the one they have with their siblings. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326388\" id=\"question-wrapper-326388\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"995da44a-0cf2-40df-9e6c-fa2fd0a869d3\">A firstborn's achievements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"e5a32507-1e5f-4839-b550-7f4da85139d4\">indirectly help later-born children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"42f6e27c-d5f0-48a4-8aba-fdd0b341cc9d\">altering how the parents act<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326389\" id=\"question-wrapper-326389\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the discussion of birth order suggest about the influence of siblings?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Sibling influence is strongest when children deliberately try to shape one another’s behaviour.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3cb4c85c-ddd8-4de5-9483-d4fdc8391b64\">Adults may still act out </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3cb4c85c-ddd8-4de5-9483-d4fdc8391b64 a82dc263-8cee-423f-8d75-617466f24f10\">the part</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"a82dc263-8cee-423f-8d75-617466f24f10\"> assigned to them</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"10916f5a-be23-442e-8291-eb8c54abc6c4\">their position among their siblings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Behaviour learned from siblings tends to become less important once parental influence declines.</li> <li>D. The roles children adopt within the family mainly reinforce characteristics they have inherited.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326390\" id=\"question-wrapper-326390\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the account of Claire Cartwright’s clients suggest about childhood experiences?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"b00504f3-4ed4-4dff-884a-df8f7dca0415\">A person’s impression of family treatment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"cb7f0a7f-8962-4205-93b9-e69dabf495f0\">can influence behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e1fa4051-454f-41b0-b76b-774b0c20ceca\">even when that interpretation is questionable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Adults who remember being judged harshly usually discover that their siblings had similar experiences.</li> <li>C. Unequal treatment by parents is most damaging when children remain unaware of it at the time.</li> <li>D. Workplace difficulties can confirm that a person’s childhood view of parental favouritism was accurate.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326391\" id=\"question-wrapper-326391\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What broader point is illustrated by the two types of child described in the fifth paragraph?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Qualities encouraged by parents are more likely to create difficulties outside the family than qualities they discourage.</li> <li>B. Children who seek parental approval tend to retain their childhood behaviour more consistently than disruptive children.</li> <li>C. Adult success depends partly on abandoning the role that attracted the most attention during childhood.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"cb06f9db-fda3-4afb-8aac-e7f97da1016d\">The adult value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"419e9aa9-71c9-482f-9ce1-37dcacf66f39\">a childhood role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"d85a5b00-a6a4-488a-b49c-064776f0a159\">may differ<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> from the way that role was regarded within the family.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326392\" id=\"question-wrapper-326392\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is meant by the claim that each sibling grows up in a different ‘family’?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f49857f0-9627-4a63-bcd0-c775a645eda3\">circumstances a child is brought up in can vary sharply<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> even within a single home.</li> <li>B. Parents gradually alter their approach as they become more skilled at bringing up children.</li> <li>C. Differences between siblings arise because each child responds differently to the same family conditions.</li> <li>D. Birth order exposes children to influences that can eventually outweigh the effects of shared genes.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words and phrases, A–K, below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–K, in boxes 35–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. parental love</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"bbc44da3-38f6-4f82-8d16-443ec728796e\">imaginative games<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. physical development</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"e6f15f2d-8bd2-4464-a9b1-7cd7493f67b2\">acts of kindness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. strong marriages</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"4a3c9f93-7c39-4475-9c71-75e9cce4022a\">greater individuality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"fe5e1e64-b2aa-46e5-9bee-d9afdfbc84fd\">learning experiences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. career success</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"88614ffe-ace3-46f1-924c-5d2a65d815a4\">closer relationships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"J\"><span>J. healthy competition</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"K\"><span>K. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"468e14b0-228a-4d66-ac51-68cd5a8561e2\">mental well-being<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p><p><b><span>The positive aspects of sibling relationships</span></b></p><p><span>Annette Henderson suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"8201fd21-4fdf-4f69-8a3c-f6f8dae6670c\">young children's<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"131f02b2-7a6b-43e1-b926-8a314e282ff9\">interactions with older siblings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> involve (35)________. Also, a Cambridge study found that (36)____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"1c5eda28-21ec-40a5-a103-54ff66976c6c\">continued to feature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> in sibling relationships <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"5923fae6-d4b0-479c-8844-c2164feaab54\">marked by frequent quarrels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"f45c9592-1d1d-4f7d-8960-0cc26bf2162a\">Research conducted in 2003<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> suggests that (37)________ emerges from children's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e52ec37f-2f5f-4ecf-81ca-71eb7582885a\">efforts to stand out to their parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Another factor is the modern shift towards <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"a3eb3efc-72f1-4320-859d-f36bff334728\">fewer children per home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, which may lead to (38)____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"9aaf9d41-b291-4b94-811c-0ec426570413\">in later life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. A 2010 American study <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"30939a1f-6b3f-4049-b5a8-a5e100acc83b\">linked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> having a sister <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"30939a1f-6b3f-4049-b5a8-a5e100acc83b\">with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> (39)________ among <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"7afc9dfd-ca10-413d-896d-e4f6e5c49f32\">early adolescents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. The same study also indicates that children with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"baf7872a-0b75-4baf-b303-6b8c4a14fdc5\">an affectionate brother or sister<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8cc0067e-3ca0-4728-b86e-b5fe308aad08\">tend to show more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> (40)________. </span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326393\" id=\"question-wrapper-326393\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326394\" id=\"question-wrapper-326394\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326395\" id=\"question-wrapper-326395\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326396\" id=\"question-wrapper-326396\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326397\" id=\"question-wrapper-326397\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">K</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326398\" id=\"question-wrapper-326398\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b372f05f-ad71-4f62-9346-437a079102f7","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Genetic inheritance","passagePhrase":"provide our genetic material"},{"uid":"d2cbc450-7a6b-429a-beb0-666f4f5f5dbf","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"parental influence","passagePhrase":"serve as powerful early role models"},{"uid":"a9c898ed-d49c-4188-814b-52fbc71a0558","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"adult personality","passagePhrase":"what kind of adults we become"},{"uid":"e6f07c5d-484c-4bf9-8369-001a5041ff2b","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"relationships with siblings","passagePhrase":"our brothers and sisters—our siblings"},{"uid":"13290cbe-cc8d-4b68-9c86-68ca69fef974","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"siblings","passagePhrase":"brothers and sisters"},{"uid":"61598edc-b945-4015-8e44-ce723a22a278","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The earliest social bonds","passagePhrase":"first social relationships"},{"uid":"936b27c3-a099-4acb-899c-310f00656b90","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"husband or wife","passagePhrase":"spouses"},{"uid":"995da44a-0cf2-40df-9e6c-fa2fd0a869d3","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"A firstborn's achievements","passagePhrase":"older children who do well at school and are well liked"},{"uid":"42f6e27c-d5f0-48a4-8aba-fdd0b341cc9d","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"altering how the parents act","passagePhrase":"increasing mothers’ self-esteem ... more positive parenting"},{"uid":"e5a32507-1e5f-4839-b550-7f4da85139d4","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"indirectly help later-born children","passagePhrase":"younger children ... show fewer behavioural problems"},{"uid":"10916f5a-be23-442e-8291-eb8c54abc6c4","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"their position among their siblings","passagePhrase":"birth order"},{"uid":"a82dc263-8cee-423f-8d75-617466f24f10","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"assigned to them","passagePhrase":"childhood play roles"},{"uid":"3cb4c85c-ddd8-4de5-9483-d4fdc8391b64","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Adults may still act out","passagePhrase":"roles that can persist throughout life"},{"uid":"b00504f3-4ed4-4dff-884a-df8f7dca0415","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"A person’s impression of family treatment","passagePhrase":"believe they were treated differently from their siblings"},{"uid":"e1fa4051-454f-41b0-b76b-774b0c20ceca","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"even when that interpretation is questionable","passagePhrase":"although this may not actually have been the case"},{"uid":"cb7f0a7f-8962-4205-93b9-e69dabf495f0","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"can influence behaviour","passagePhrase":"might become particularly defensive and behave in ways that attract harsh judgements"},{"uid":"d85a5b00-a6a4-488a-b49c-064776f0a159","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"may differ","passagePhrase":"has its own pitfalls ... may later reinterpret that role ... turning attention-seeking characteristics into"},{"uid":"419e9aa9-71c9-482f-9ce1-37dcacf66f39","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"a childhood role","passagePhrase":"the easy-going, cooperative child at home ... a sibling who was disruptive and annoying as a child"},{"uid":"cb06f9db-fda3-4afb-8aac-e7f97da1016d","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"The adult value","passagePhrase":"skilled at pleasing parents and, later, bosses ... difficult to be assertive with authority figures ... lack a clear sense of direction ... such as determination and leadership"},{"uid":"cb06f9db-fda3-4afb-8aac-e7f97da1016d d85a5b00-a6a4-488a-b49c-064776f0a159","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"strengths"},{"uid":"f49857f0-9627-4a63-bcd0-c775a645eda3","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"circumstances a child is brought up in can vary sharply","passagePhrase":"one sibling may grow up amid stability and closeness while another may be raised during a period of crisis"},{"uid":"8201fd21-4fdf-4f69-8a3c-f6f8dae6670c","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"young children's","passagePhrase":"Younger children"},{"uid":"fe5e1e64-b2aa-46e5-9bee-d9afdfbc84fd","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"learning experiences","passagePhrase":"benefit from unintentional instruction ... acquiring entire phrases ... an understanding of social concepts such as politeness"},{"uid":"131f02b2-7a6b-43e1-b926-8a314e282ff9","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"interactions with older siblings","passagePhrase":"from their older brothers and sisters"},{"uid":"5923fae6-d4b0-479c-8844-c2164feaab54","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"marked by frequent quarrels","passagePhrase":"considerable conflict ... fought most frequently"},{"uid":"1c5eda28-21ec-40a5-a103-54ff66976c6c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"continued to feature","passagePhrase":"still created"},{"uid":"bbc44da3-38f6-4f82-8d16-443ec728796e","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"imaginative games","passagePhrase":"play and make-believe"},{"uid":"e52ec37f-2f5f-4ecf-81ca-71eb7582885a","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"efforts to stand out to their parents","passagePhrase":"compete for parental attention by differentiating themselves"},{"uid":"f45c9592-1d1d-4f7d-8960-0cc26bf2162a","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"Research conducted in 2003","passagePhrase":"A 2003 study"},{"uid":"4a3c9f93-7c39-4475-9c71-75e9cce4022a","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"greater individuality","passagePhrase":"stronger personalities and a clearer sense of identity"},{"uid":"a3eb3efc-72f1-4320-859d-f36bff334728","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"fewer children per home","passagePhrase":"families ... smaller"},{"uid":"88614ffe-ace3-46f1-924c-5d2a65d815a4","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"closer relationships","passagePhrase":"know one another better and remain ... friends"},{"uid":"88614ffe-ace3-46f1-924c-5d2a65d815a4 9aaf9d41-b291-4b94-811c-0ec426570413","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"lifelong"},{"uid":"9aaf9d41-b291-4b94-811c-0ec426570413","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"in later life","passagePhrase":"after leaving home"},{"uid":"30939a1f-6b3f-4049-b5a8-a5e100acc83b","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"linked ... with","passagePhrase":"found that ... meant"},{"uid":"7afc9dfd-ca10-413d-896d-e4f6e5c49f32","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"early adolescents","passagePhrase":"10- to 14-year-olds"},{"uid":"468e14b0-228a-4d66-ac51-68cd5a8561e2","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"mental well-being","passagePhrase":"less likely to feel lonely, unloved, self-conscious or fearful"},{"uid":"baf7872a-0b75-4baf-b303-6b8c4a14fdc5","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"an affectionate brother or sister","passagePhrase":"a loving sibling of either gender"},{"uid":"8cc0067e-3ca0-4728-b86e-b5fe308aad08","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"tend to show more","passagePhrase":"promoted more"},{"uid":"e6f15f2d-8bd2-4464-a9b1-7cd7493f67b2","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"acts of kindness","passagePhrase":"generous behaviour, such as helping a neighbour ... helping other children"},{"uid":"3cb4c85c-ddd8-4de5-9483-d4fdc8391b64 a82dc263-8cee-423f-8d75-617466f24f10","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"the part","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_112":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>Consecutive and Simultaneous </span></b><b><span>Interpreting</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p><span>When encountering a foreign language barrier, people often turn to professionals to translate or interpret for them. The term ‘translation’ can be used broadly for the process of transferring meaning or expression from one language (the source language) into another (the target language), whether the medium is spoken, written or signed. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"2bba059e-86b4-4531-9623-1f348829e0eb\">certain professional contexts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"cae01d43-c9b3-4c69-b373-57b2cdcc10a6\">a distinction is drawn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> between people who work with spoken or signed language (<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"527d66d7-05ad-4504-9b31-e1727eaa68e3\">interpreters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>) and those who work with the written language (<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"527d66d7-05ad-4504-9b31-e1727eaa68e3\">translators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>). While both professions involve transferring information from a source language into a target language, they are still considered distinct, and it is hard to find a person who enjoys both. Some writers on translation, indeed, consider the interpreting task to be more suitable for extroverts and the translating task for introverts.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p><span>Interpreting is today widely known for its use in international political life. When senior ministers from different cultures and language backgrounds meet, the television coverage invariably shows a pair of interpreters hovering in the background. At major conferences, such as the United Nations General Assembly, the presence of headphones is a clear indication that an important linguistic exercise is going on. In everyday circumstances, interpreters are frequently needed too, especially in cosmopolitan societies formed by new generations of immigrants and foreign workers. Often, the business of law courts, hospitals, local health clinics, classrooms or industrial tribunals cannot be carried on without interpreters. Given <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"4b99a9b8-b336-462e-8a6d-65e4d3ade559\">the importance and frequency of this work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6e825e5d-274c-46ef-ac8f-a34ef08fc76a\">remarkable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"b4cce839-88f1-49a3-8d88-2fc1bafed667\">so little study has been made of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"b9edd7e4-d364-4967-b6e3-559953f12b3c\">what actually happens when interpreting takes place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, and of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"a3ad075a-2586-4653-9afb-8a7f2e339a30\">how successful an exercise it is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p><span>There are two categories of interpretation: consecutive and simultaneous. In a consecutive mode of interpreting, the interpreter provides the interpretation after the original speech or some section of it has been finished. During the course of the speech, the interpreter has to focus attention on comprehending and analysing its content. Here the length of each segment to be translated makes a difference to the interpreter's strategies and outcomes. If the segment is just one sentence or two, the interpreter <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"fa5d943b-3f80-4dc8-91d2-22b9550e89e7\">closely follows the original speech<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. Nevertheless, the interpreter is often expected to translate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f0ae0d50-059c-4e44-b486-2ff29871324e\">a long speech which may last for many minutes or even longer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. Faced with this situation, he has to remember a great number of messages and keep them in mind until he begins his translation. For this to be possible, the interpreter must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"a61cd2af-860e-427e-8981-419c0c2f0fdc\">record key information using a system of symbols<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. Studying and practising this set of symbols is an integral part of interpreter training and a special exercise to improve memory.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c4e7625e-351b-48d8-ad8c-47391c0bbd19\">Consecutive interpreting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, which is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"8e189763-728f-42c6-848e-2464a516893d\">widely employed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> in informal situations, as well as in committee meetings and small conferences, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"2cb5ba52-dde9-4e67-afc9-13473ae6f58b 2e102189-7596-4f4b-8f90-a9100170cda0\">presumably</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"2cb5ba52-dde9-4e67-afc9-13473ae6f58b\"> dates from the Tower of Babel</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. In this kind of interpretation, the interpreter translates after the speaker has finished speaking. It does break the rhythm of the original language, but that is the nature of it. In larger and more formal events, therefore, where the meaning needs to be delivered effectively and accurately, it has been generally replaced by simultaneous interpreting, whose development arose from the availability of modern audio equipment and the growth of international interaction following the Second World War.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p><span>The simultaneous mode has attracted great interest because of the complexity of the task and the remarkable skills required. In no other con<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"bb4868a4-2f40-46ec-a1ee-2c2b6770322d\">text<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> of human communication is anyone routinely required to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"cfcbb821-eb38-4b14-b074-146b679a29a3\">listen and speak at the same time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, preserving an exact semantic correspondence between the two procedures. Strictly speaking, the term ‘simultaneous’ does not accurately describe the process. Actually, the interpreter might not be able to utter even a single word until the interpreter has <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a48d969d-e50b-4c2b-96b4-a2328007b596\">grasped enough of the meaning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, and he needs time to assimilate what is being said in the source language and to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"f1e476ed-9f81-4bd6-87b3-e06373b6ea64\">convert it into an acceptable form in the target language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, so there is invariably a delay of a few words between the stimulus and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"f1e476ed-9f81-4bd6-87b3-e06373b6ea64\">the response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. This ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9f357686-a464-4256-81aa-adb70b354620\">ear-voice span<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>’ is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9e26fc94-683e-4954-8443-285d3d889893\">usually<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"0dc58a75-fda9-4085-8277-fc91f0b4f7c5\">about 2 or 3<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> seconds, but it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"420bbc44-ddf6-4bb9-9fa0-c00ee3551af6\">may be as much as 10 seconds or so<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> if the text is complex. The brain has to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"f92dd569-15e6-4e1a-b9c9-d4a1f4d1df75\">memorise what has just been said<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"4586bf90-ab3c-4925-9b76-32a5222f6c95 9c885dd7-ee07-4c1f-9faf-a6e19c7e81c5\">attend to what is currently being said</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"9c885dd7-ee07-4c1f-9faf-a6e19c7e81c5\">anticipate the construction of what is about to be said<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p><span>How it is all done is not at all clear. That it is done at all is a source of some wonder, given the often lengthy periods of interpreting required, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ce8c3239-5d87-45a7-876b-9091bdf0fb8b\">the confined environment of the interpreting booth, the presence of background noise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"00db2f6c-20ad-4a4d-8d15-9f74f698638b\">the awareness that important decisions may depend on the accuracy of the interpretation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. Other considerations, such as cultural background, also require interpreters to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"96fb167c-8bb6-43b9-b6ba-5981c6411df5\">pay close attention to the backgrounds of speakers and listeners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> and to differences between the source and target languages.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b> </p><p><span>Recent research has now begun to look at how far these factors and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"d12415b7-d946-49d9-8e95-ce43cd88b503\">the speed at which the source language is spoken<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> affect interpreting performance. It seems that an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"9901bf6c-9298-482a-aadc-0af7d24d0395\">input speed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"c5b892d7-30a8-4e2b-b682-9a9bb946fe9f\">between 100 and 120<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> words per minute is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"221af8ef-c4cd-4d40-95fe-2451f7827562\">a comfortable rate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> for interpreting with an upper limit of around 200 w.p.m. Even small changes in speed can dramatically affect the accuracy of output. In one controlled study, when speeds were gradually increased in a series of stages from 95 to 194 w.p.m., the ear-voice span also extended with each stage, and the amount correctly interpreted showed a clear decline. Moreover, as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"408391e3-085b-4536-ba58-ffa95d333132\">the translating load increased<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, not only were there more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"468aa130-f90c-4d7a-8535-44e7d3a51371\">errors of commission, such as mistranslations and vague renderings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, there were also more omissions. These are significant findings, considering the need for accuracy and precision in international communication. What is needed is a more detailed identification of the problem areas, and of the strategies speakers, listeners and interpreters adopt to solve them. There is an urgent need to investigate further what has so far been one of the most neglected fields of communication research.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326399\" id=\"question-wrapper-326399\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What point does the writer make about the terms ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"527d66d7-05ad-4504-9b31-e1727eaa68e3\">translation’ and ‘interpreting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>’ in paragraph A?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The distinction between them reflects differences in the personalities suited to each profession.</li> <li>B. Whether they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"cae01d43-c9b3-4c69-b373-57b2cdcc10a6\">kept apart<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> depends on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"2bba059e-86b4-4531-9623-1f348829e0eb\">the field in which the work is done<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Interpreting has a broader meaning because it includes both spoken and signed communication.</li> <li>D. Work with signed languages is normally classed as translation rather than interpreting.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326400\" id=\"question-wrapper-326400\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the writer regard as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"6e825e5d-274c-46ef-ac8f-a34ef08fc76a\">surprising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> about interpreting in paragraph B?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Its public profile is much greater internationally than in everyday services.</li> <li>B. Its expansion in immigrant communities has outpaced the supply of trained professionals.</li> <li>C. Research has focused on where it is used rather than on how well it works.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"4b99a9b8-b336-462e-8a6d-65e4d3ade559\">How widely it is relied on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> contrasts with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"b4cce839-88f1-49a3-8d88-2fc1bafed667\">how much is known about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"b9edd7e4-d364-4967-b6e3-559953f12b3c\">the process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"a3ad075a-2586-4653-9afb-8a7f2e339a30\">its results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326401\" id=\"question-wrapper-326401\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What changes when a consecutive interpreter has to deal with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"f0ae0d50-059c-4e44-b486-2ff29871324e\">an extended stretch of talk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"fa5d943b-3f80-4dc8-91d2-22b9550e89e7\">Close tracking of the speaker's wording<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> gives way to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"a61cd2af-860e-427e-8981-419c0c2f0fdc\">noting down only the essential points<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Analysis of the speech is postponed until the speaker has completed the whole section.</li> <li>C. Translation begins before the speaker finishes so that less information has to be remembered.</li> <li>D. Complete sentences are recorded to prevent important details from being lost.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326402\" id=\"question-wrapper-326402\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer mentions the Tower of Babel to illustrate</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the mystery of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c4e7625e-351b-48d8-ad8c-47391c0bbd19\">consecutive interpretation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"2e102189-7596-4f4b-8f90-a9100170cda0\">the precise time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> when consecutive interpretation appeared.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"2cb5ba52-dde9-4e67-afc9-13473ae6f58b\">the long history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of consecutive interpretation.</li> <li>D. the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"8e189763-728f-42c6-848e-2464a516893d\">antiquated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> nature of consecutive interpretation.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326403\" id=\"question-wrapper-326403\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the description of the ‘ear-voice span’ show about simultaneous interpreting?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Complex material can force interpreters to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"4586bf90-ab3c-4925-9b76-32a5222f6c95\">stop listening<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"cfcbb821-eb38-4b14-b074-146b679a29a3\">while<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> they prepare a response.</li> <li>B. Interpreters may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"f1e476ed-9f81-4bd6-87b3-e06373b6ea64\">speaking one part<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"f92dd569-15e6-4e1a-b9c9-d4a1f4d1df75\">retaining<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"9c885dd7-ee07-4c1f-9faf-a6e19c7e81c5\">processing other parts of the message<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Interpreters usually <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a48d969d-e50b-4c2b-96b4-a2328007b596\">wait until a whole sentence has been understood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> before they start speaking.</li> <li>D. Interpreters keep the delay short mainly by predicting the speaker’s exact next words.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p>Choose <b><span>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER </span></b><span>from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><b><span>Simultaneous interpreting</span></b></p><p><span>Although the term </span><i><span>simultaneous </span></i><span>suggests that hearing and producing speech happen together, interpreters actually begin their response after a brief delay. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9f357686-a464-4256-81aa-adb70b354620\">Output </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9e26fc94-683e-4954-8443-285d3d889893 9f357686-a464-4256-81aa-adb70b354620\">normally</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"9f357686-a464-4256-81aa-adb70b354620\"> trails input by</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"0dc58a75-fda9-4085-8277-fc91f0b4f7c5\">only two or three<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (6)_______, though (7)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"bb4868a4-2f40-46ec-a1ee-2c2b6770322d\">content<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"420bbc44-ddf6-4bb9-9fa0-c00ee3551af6\">widen the gap considerably<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Research into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"9901bf6c-9298-482a-aadc-0af7d24d0395\">delivery rate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> indicates that interpreters <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"221af8ef-c4cd-4d40-95fe-2451f7827562\">can manage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> input of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"c5b892d7-30a8-4e2b-b682-9a9bb946fe9f\">up to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)_______ w.p.m. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"221af8ef-c4cd-4d40-95fe-2451f7827562\">without strain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. As <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"408391e3-085b-4536-ba58-ffa95d333132\">the source speech becomes faster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, a smaller proportion is rendered accurately. In addition to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"468aa130-f90c-4d7a-8535-44e7d3a51371\">rendering content wrongly or imprecisely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, interpreters also make more (9)_______.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326404\" id=\"question-wrapper-326404\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SECONDS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326405\" id=\"question-wrapper-326405\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMPLEX</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326406\" id=\"question-wrapper-326406\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">120</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326407\" id=\"question-wrapper-326407\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OMISSIONS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose FOUR letters, A–G.</span></p><p><span>Which FOUR of the following factors may affect the accuracy of simultaneous interpreting?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letters in boxes 10–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. mastery of textual structure and grammar</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"d12415b7-d946-49d9-8e95-ce43cd88b503\">the pace at which the original speaker talks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ce8c3239-5d87-45a7-876b-9091bdf0fb8b\">the physical conditions in which they work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. the psychological quality of interpreters</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"96fb167c-8bb6-43b9-b6ba-5981c6411df5\">awareness of cultural differences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"00db2f6c-20ad-4a4d-8d15-9f74f698638b\">knowing that the outcome of the interpretation has high stakes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. the ability of listeners to understand</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326408\" id=\"question-wrapper-326408\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/E/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326409\" id=\"question-wrapper-326409\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/E/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326410\" id=\"question-wrapper-326410\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/E/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326411\" id=\"question-wrapper-326411\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/E/F</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"2bba059e-86b4-4531-9623-1f348829e0eb","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"the field in which the work is done","passagePhrase":"certain professional contexts"},{"uid":"cae01d43-c9b3-4c69-b373-57b2cdcc10a6","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"kept apart","passagePhrase":"a distinction is drawn"},{"uid":"527d66d7-05ad-4504-9b31-e1727eaa68e3","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"translation’ and ‘interpreting","passagePhrase":"interpreters ... translators"},{"uid":"4b99a9b8-b336-462e-8a6d-65e4d3ade559","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"How widely it is relied on","passagePhrase":"the importance and frequency of this work"},{"uid":"6e825e5d-274c-46ef-ac8f-a34ef08fc76a","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"surprising","passagePhrase":"remarkable"},{"uid":"b4cce839-88f1-49a3-8d88-2fc1bafed667","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"how much is known about","passagePhrase":"so little study has been made of"},{"uid":"b9edd7e4-d364-4967-b6e3-559953f12b3c","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"the process","passagePhrase":"what actually happens when interpreting takes place"},{"uid":"a3ad075a-2586-4653-9afb-8a7f2e339a30","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"its results","passagePhrase":"how successful an exercise it is"},{"uid":"fa5d943b-3f80-4dc8-91d2-22b9550e89e7","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Close tracking of the speaker's wording","passagePhrase":"closely follows the original speech"},{"uid":"f0ae0d50-059c-4e44-b486-2ff29871324e","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"an extended stretch of talk","passagePhrase":"a long speech which may last for many minutes or even longer"},{"uid":"a61cd2af-860e-427e-8981-419c0c2f0fdc","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"noting down only the essential points","passagePhrase":"record key information using a system of symbols"},{"uid":"c4e7625e-351b-48d8-ad8c-47391c0bbd19","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"consecutive interpretation","passagePhrase":"Consecutive interpreting"},{"uid":"2cb5ba52-dde9-4e67-afc9-13473ae6f58b 2e102189-7596-4f4b-8f90-a9100170cda0","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"presumably"},{"uid":"2cb5ba52-dde9-4e67-afc9-13473ae6f58b","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"the long history","passagePhrase":"dates from the Tower of Babel"},{"uid":"bb4868a4-2f40-46ec-a1ee-2c2b6770322d","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"content","passagePhrase":"text"},{"uid":"cfcbb821-eb38-4b14-b074-146b679a29a3","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"while","passagePhrase":"listen and speak at the same time"},{"uid":"f1e476ed-9f81-4bd6-87b3-e06373b6ea64","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"speaking one part","passagePhrase":"convert it into an acceptable form in the target language ... the response"},{"uid":"9f357686-a464-4256-81aa-adb70b354620","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Output ... trails input by","passagePhrase":"ear-voice span"},{"uid":"9e26fc94-683e-4954-8443-285d3d889893","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"usually"},{"uid":"0dc58a75-fda9-4085-8277-fc91f0b4f7c5","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"only two or three","passagePhrase":"about 2 or 3"},{"uid":"420bbc44-ddf6-4bb9-9fa0-c00ee3551af6","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"widen the gap considerably","passagePhrase":"may be as much as 10 seconds or so"},{"uid":"f92dd569-15e6-4e1a-b9c9-d4a1f4d1df75","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"retaining","passagePhrase":"memorise what has just been said"},{"uid":"4586bf90-ab3c-4925-9b76-32a5222f6c95 9c885dd7-ee07-4c1f-9faf-a6e19c7e81c5","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"attend to what is currently being said"},{"uid":"9c885dd7-ee07-4c1f-9faf-a6e19c7e81c5","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"processing other parts of the message","passagePhrase":"anticipate the construction of what is about to be said"},{"uid":"ce8c3239-5d87-45a7-876b-9091bdf0fb8b","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"the physical conditions in which they work","passagePhrase":"the confined environment of the interpreting booth, the presence of background noise"},{"uid":"00db2f6c-20ad-4a4d-8d15-9f74f698638b","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"knowing that the outcome of the interpretation has high stakes","passagePhrase":"the awareness that important decisions may depend on the accuracy of the interpretation"},{"uid":"96fb167c-8bb6-43b9-b6ba-5981c6411df5","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"awareness of cultural differences","passagePhrase":"pay close attention to the backgrounds of speakers and listeners"},{"uid":"d12415b7-d946-49d9-8e95-ce43cd88b503","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the pace at which the original speaker talks","passagePhrase":"the speed at which the source language is spoken"},{"uid":"9901bf6c-9298-482a-aadc-0af7d24d0395","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"delivery rate","passagePhrase":"input speed"},{"uid":"c5b892d7-30a8-4e2b-b682-9a9bb946fe9f","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"up to","passagePhrase":"between 100 and 120"},{"uid":"221af8ef-c4cd-4d40-95fe-2451f7827562","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"can manage ... without strain","passagePhrase":"a comfortable rate"},{"uid":"408391e3-085b-4536-ba58-ffa95d333132","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"the source speech becomes faster","passagePhrase":"the translating load increased"},{"uid":"468aa130-f90c-4d7a-8535-44e7d3a51371","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"rendering content wrongly or imprecisely","passagePhrase":"errors of commission, such as mistranslations and vague renderings"},{"uid":"9e26fc94-683e-4954-8443-285d3d889893 9f357686-a464-4256-81aa-adb70b354620","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"normally","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_113":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>How Fish Swim</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>The underwater world presents many challenges, one of the most basic being movement. The density of water makes it difficult for animals to move, and forward movement requires a complex interaction of forces. In addition, water itself moves, and strong currents can easily sweep creatures away. These challenges result in a variety of swimming methods used by a wide range of aquatic animals, creating a dazzling underwater ballet.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>Fish rely on their skeletons, fins and muscles to move. The primary function of the skeleton is to aid the movement of other body parts. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"8f8fc46d-2889-47ef-bbc3-0263141afed1\">The skull<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5a91bec3-af70-4f67-9902-ef4c05d1c458\">acts as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d1aafdf7-a325-4b42-8184-5f0a5e56f1c8\">a fulcrum<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"8f8fc46d-2889-47ef-bbc3-0263141afed1\">the vertebrae<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5a91bec3-af70-4f67-9902-ef4c05d1c458\">act as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d1aafdf7-a325-4b42-8184-5f0a5e56f1c8\">levers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. The vertebral column consists of a series of vertebrae held together by ligaments, but not so tightly as to prevent slight sideways movement between each pair of vertebrae. The whole spine is therefore flexible. The skull is the only truly fixed part of a fish. It does not itself move but acts as a point of stability for the other bones. These bones act as levers that enable movement of the fish’s body.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b><span>. While the bones provide the framework for movement, the muscles supply the power. A typical fish has hundreds of muscles running in all directions throughout its body. This is why a fish can turn, twist and change direction quickly. The muscles on either side of the spine contract alternately in sequence from head to tail, causing a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3e37dbeb-1f06-4b5f-b38f-56bf64e7970f\">wave-like movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to pass down the body. Such movement may be very pronounced in fish such as eels, but hardly perceptible in others, such as mackerel. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"72b52d8c-7990-48cc-b5b0-a57f14bd1f5d\">The frequency of these waves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"6670eaf0-f11e-463f-b09f-bb940a2b3f8a\">varies from about 50 per minute in the dogfish to 170 per minute in the mackerel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. As the head and body thrust sideways and backwards against the water, the water exerts an opposing force that pushes the fish sideways and forwards. When the corresponding set of muscles on the other side contracts, the fish experiences a similar force from the water on that side. The two sideways forces are equal and opposite, unless the fish is turning, so they cancel each other out, leaving the two forward forces to combine.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"b84e47f4-318b-4874-92b2-edc86d8cb747\">The muscles involved in swimming are of two main types<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"07906752-75bd-4368-a57b-43326e303228\">The bulk of a fish's body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> is composed of so-called <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"b84e47f4-318b-4874-92b2-edc86d8cb747\">white muscle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"b84e47f4-318b-4874-92b2-edc86d8cb747\">red muscle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> occurs in much smaller areas at the roots of the fins and in a strip along the centre of each flank. Red muscle receives a good supply of blood and contains <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"76f3bc46-b642-4bda-8869-0ea5be44ffe4\">larger quantities of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"328ee047-6a56-41a5-9f50-71e91049cd7e\">fat and glycogen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, the latter being a storage form of glucose. Red muscle is used for most day-to-day swimming movements. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"76f3bc46-b642-4bda-8869-0ea5be44ffe4\">In contrast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, white muscle has a poor blood supply and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"76f3bc46-b642-4bda-8869-0ea5be44ffe4\">fewer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"328ee047-6a56-41a5-9f50-71e91049cd7e\">energy stores<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, and is used largely for short-term, fast swimming. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a3b288ef-625f-4416-b784-3aafb3efaa1e\">It might seem odd<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> that an animal so efficiently adapted to its environment should be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"07906752-75bd-4368-a57b-43326e303228\">composed almost entirely of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> a type of muscle that it rarely uses. However, this huge <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"1eaf40de-6700-4554-999d-94d4da88bd9f\">auxiliary power pack<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> is of crucial importance <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"fa3ec223-39b9-48b7-a8f2-946da6dbc9cf\">when the fish is threatened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>—for example, by a predator—because it enables the fish to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"fa3ec223-39b9-48b7-a8f2-946da6dbc9cf\">swim rapidly away from danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>The fins are among the most distinctive features of a fish. They consist of bony spines protruding from the body and covered by skin, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ee796f5f-efa8-4cfa-947b-86179f5cadf2\">joins them together either in a webbed form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, as in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"fbdc36ad-5fa4-4ce0-9242-396e0a961382\">most bony fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ee796f5f-efa8-4cfa-947b-86179f5cadf2\">or in a more flipper-like form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, as in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"fbdc36ad-5fa4-4ce0-9242-396e0a961382\">sharks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Although fins play an important role in swimming, most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"d9a48dc7-6f48-4ece-9c48-5599aba3e73d\">propulsive movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> is produced by the muscular body as a whole, and in only a few fish do the fins contribute significant <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"d9a48dc7-6f48-4ece-9c48-5599aba3e73d\">propulsive force<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"912fc1dc-baa9-4d53-b217-741a870275b1\">Their main function<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"7a1765f3-bba5-41a6-a4f1-399ff41405b6\">maintain stability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"400241b2-b344-4cd0-9d72-505c8c1c4762\">control direction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"7497317c-f336-47d7-9a26-3b928bd885c5\">As water passes over its body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, a fish <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"7497317c-f336-47d7-9a26-3b928bd885c5\">uses its fins to </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"400241b2-b344-4cd0-9d72-505c8c1c4762 7497317c-f336-47d7-9a26-3b928bd885c5\">guide its movement</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"400241b2-b344-4cd0-9d72-505c8c1c4762\"> in the direction it wishes to go</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>Fins located in different parts of a fish serve different purposes, such as moving forwards, turning and maintaining an upright position. The tail fin, in its final lash, may contribute as much as 40 per cent of the forward thrust. The median fins, particularly the dorsal and anal fins, control rolling and yawing movements by increasing the vertical surface area presented to the water. The paired fins—the pectoral and pelvic fins—act as hydroplanes and control the pitch of the fish. Depending on the angle at which they are held relative to the water, they can cause the fish to move downwards or upwards. The pectoral fins lie in front of the centre of gravity and, being readily mobile, are chiefly responsible for directing the fish up or down. The paired fins also enable the fish to slow down and stop.</span></p><p><b><span>G. </span></b><span>The swimming speed of fish is not always as high as one might expect from watching their rapid movements in aquaria or ponds. Tuna have been recorded at about 44 mph, trout at 23 mph, pike at 20 mph for short bursts and roach at about 10 mph, while the majority of small fish probably do not exceed 2 or 3 mph. Many attempts have been made to measure accurately the speeds at which different fish swim, either by timing them over known distances in their natural environment or by determining their performance in artificial swimming channels. From these studies, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"521fb318-27fc-4e9e-a358-f145170850da\">fish can be broadly categorised into four groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>: “sneakers”, such as eels, which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"bd17e867-0157-4c21-af2f-0a4992c97613\">capable only of slow speeds but have some staying power<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>; “stayers”, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"bd17e867-0157-4c21-af2f-0a4992c97613\">can swim quite fast over long periods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>; “sprinters”, such as pike, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"bd17e867-0157-4c21-af2f-0a4992c97613\">can generate short bursts of high speed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>; and “crawlers”, such as bream, which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"bd17e867-0157-4c21-af2f-0a4992c97613\">generally sluggish swimmers although capable of slight acceleration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>H. </span></b><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a0df914a-4c47-4693-9e16-3fc20bd0c413\">A species of sailfish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> is considered to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"796c04d6-2ab2-4c52-915b-51525b39ac76\">the fastest fish over short distances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, reaching 68 mph <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"defe2cff-4d98-4bb4-94bb-17eaf80e736c\">over a three-second period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, while anglers have recorded speeds above 40 mph over longer periods for several species of tuna. Swimming ability is often considered in relation to body size. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"43e1455b-f935-44a5-a517-cb28612c8d32\">Relative to its size, a small fish is generally a more capable swimmer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> than a much larger one. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"0067d403-d76a-4d46-ac5a-8859061c8f72\">In terms of absolute speed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> in miles per hour, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"0067d403-d76a-4d46-ac5a-8859061c8f72\">a large fish will<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, all other things being equal, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"0067d403-d76a-4d46-ac5a-8859061c8f72\">be able to swim faster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> than a smaller fish.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A–H. Which paragraph contains the following information? </span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–H, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326412\" id=\"question-wrapper-326412\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"521fb318-27fc-4e9e-a358-f145170850da\">a system for classifying fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"bd17e867-0157-4c21-af2f-0a4992c97613\">according to their swimming performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326413\" id=\"question-wrapper-326413\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a0df914a-4c47-4693-9e16-3fc20bd0c413\">an aquatic species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"796c04d6-2ab2-4c52-915b-51525b39ac76\">the highest recorded </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"796c04d6-2ab2-4c52-915b-51525b39ac76 defe2cff-4d98-4bb4-94bb-17eaf80e736c\">burst</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"796c04d6-2ab2-4c52-915b-51525b39ac76\"> swimming speed</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326414\" id=\"question-wrapper-326414\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ee796f5f-efa8-4cfa-947b-86179f5cadf2\">a contrast in the way the fins are constructed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"fbdc36ad-5fa4-4ce0-9242-396e0a961382\">two different groups of fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326415\" id=\"question-wrapper-326415\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"6670eaf0-f11e-463f-b09f-bb940a2b3f8a\">differences between species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"72b52d8c-7990-48cc-b5b0-a57f14bd1f5d\">how often the body </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3e37dbeb-1f06-4b5f-b38f-56bf64e7970f 72b52d8c-7990-48cc-b5b0-a57f14bd1f5d\">flexes</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"72b52d8c-7990-48cc-b5b0-a57f14bd1f5d\"> from side to side</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326416\" id=\"question-wrapper-326416\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5a91bec3-af70-4f67-9902-ef4c05d1c458\">an analogy between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"8f8fc46d-2889-47ef-bbc3-0263141afed1\">parts of a fish's skeleton<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"d1aafdf7-a325-4b42-8184-5f0a5e56f1c8\">mechanical components<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326417\" id=\"question-wrapper-326417\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"76f3bc46-b642-4bda-8869-0ea5be44ffe4\">a comparison<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"328ee047-6a56-41a5-9f50-71e91049cd7e\">energy reserves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"b84e47f4-318b-4874-92b2-edc86d8cb747\">two types of swimming muscle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Label the diagram below. Choose NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 20–23 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p> <span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Collection_4/reading/images/e740f17397c3c675d8dfb650aedae946497dc070292e96b0e2cf7229c54f3fd0.png\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326418\" id=\"question-wrapper-326418\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FORWARD THRUST</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326419\" id=\"question-wrapper-326419\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ROLLING + YAWING</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326420\" id=\"question-wrapper-326420\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PECTORAL + PELVIC</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326421\" id=\"question-wrapper-326421\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PITCH</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326422\" id=\"question-wrapper-326422\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a3b288ef-625f-4416-b784-3aafb3efaa1e\">noteworthy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> about the way muscle is distributed in a fish’s body?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The muscle used for routine swimming makes up the greatest proportion of the body.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"07906752-75bd-4368-a57b-43326e303228\">Most muscle tissue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> provides <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"1eaf40de-6700-4554-999d-94d4da88bd9f\">reserve power<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"fa3ec223-39b9-48b7-a8f2-946da6dbc9cf\">occasions demanding a swift escape<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</li> <li>C. The muscle with the best energy supply is concentrated near the fins because these produce most propulsion.</li> <li>D. White muscle supports everyday movement by supplying stored energy to red muscle.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326423\" id=\"question-wrapper-326423\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the writer say in paragraph E about the fins?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Their contribution to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"d9a48dc7-6f48-4ece-9c48-5599aba3e73d\">forward movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> is greatest in fish whose bodies generate little thrust.</li> <li>B. Differences in their structure determine whether they are used for stability or propulsion.</li> <li>C. They are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"912fc1dc-baa9-4d53-b217-741a870275b1\">used chiefly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"7a1765f3-bba5-41a6-a4f1-399ff41405b6\">steady the fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"400241b2-b344-4cd0-9d72-505c8c1c4762\">guide the course it takes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</li> <li>D. They are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"7497317c-f336-47d7-9a26-3b928bd885c5\">used mainly to resist the forces produced as water moves past the body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326424\" id=\"question-wrapper-326424\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the writer say in paragraph H about body size and swimming ability?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"0067d403-d76a-4d46-ac5a-8859061c8f72\">Being big brings a speed advantage in raw terms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"43e1455b-f935-44a5-a517-cb28612c8d32\">being small brings one in proportional terms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</li> <li>B. A larger fish achieves higher speeds mainly because it can maintain them over longer distances.</li> <li>C. A smaller fish’s advantage becomes greater when swimming speed is measured over short distances.</li> <li>D. Differences in swimming ability between large and small fish disappear when other factors are equal.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"8f8fc46d-2889-47ef-bbc3-0263141afed1","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"parts of a fish's skeleton","passagePhrase":"The skull ... the vertebrae"},{"uid":"5a91bec3-af70-4f67-9902-ef4c05d1c458","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"an analogy between","passagePhrase":"acts as ... act as"},{"uid":"d1aafdf7-a325-4b42-8184-5f0a5e56f1c8","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"mechanical components","passagePhrase":"a fulcrum ... levers"},{"uid":"3e37dbeb-1f06-4b5f-b38f-56bf64e7970f","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"wave-like movement"},{"uid":"72b52d8c-7990-48cc-b5b0-a57f14bd1f5d","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"how often the body ... from side to side","passagePhrase":"The frequency of these waves"},{"uid":"6670eaf0-f11e-463f-b09f-bb940a2b3f8a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"differences between species","passagePhrase":"varies from about 50 per minute in the dogfish to 170 per minute in the mackerel"},{"uid":"b84e47f4-318b-4874-92b2-edc86d8cb747","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"two types of swimming muscle","passagePhrase":"The muscles involved in swimming are of two main types ... white muscle ... red muscle"},{"uid":"07906752-75bd-4368-a57b-43326e303228","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Most muscle tissue","passagePhrase":"The bulk of a fish's body ... composed almost entirely of"},{"uid":"76f3bc46-b642-4bda-8869-0ea5be44ffe4","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"a comparison","passagePhrase":"larger quantities of ... In contrast ... fewer"},{"uid":"328ee047-6a56-41a5-9f50-71e91049cd7e","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"energy reserves","passagePhrase":"fat and glycogen ... energy stores"},{"uid":"a3b288ef-625f-4416-b784-3aafb3efaa1e","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"noteworthy","passagePhrase":"It might seem odd"},{"uid":"1eaf40de-6700-4554-999d-94d4da88bd9f","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"reserve power","passagePhrase":"auxiliary power pack"},{"uid":"fa3ec223-39b9-48b7-a8f2-946da6dbc9cf","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"occasions demanding a swift escape","passagePhrase":"when the fish is threatened ... swim rapidly away from danger"},{"uid":"ee796f5f-efa8-4cfa-947b-86179f5cadf2","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"a contrast in the way the fins are constructed","passagePhrase":"joins them together either in a webbed form ... or in a more flipper-like form"},{"uid":"fbdc36ad-5fa4-4ce0-9242-396e0a961382","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"two different groups of fish","passagePhrase":"most bony fish ... sharks"},{"uid":"d9a48dc7-6f48-4ece-9c48-5599aba3e73d","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"forward movement","passagePhrase":"propulsive movement ... propulsive force"},{"uid":"912fc1dc-baa9-4d53-b217-741a870275b1","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"used chiefly","passagePhrase":"Their main function"},{"uid":"7a1765f3-bba5-41a6-a4f1-399ff41405b6","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"steady the fish","passagePhrase":"maintain stability"},{"uid":"400241b2-b344-4cd0-9d72-505c8c1c4762","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"guide the course it takes","passagePhrase":"control direction ... in the direction it wishes to go"},{"uid":"400241b2-b344-4cd0-9d72-505c8c1c4762 7497317c-f336-47d7-9a26-3b928bd885c5","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"guide its movement"},{"uid":"521fb318-27fc-4e9e-a358-f145170850da","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"a system for classifying fish","passagePhrase":"fish can be broadly categorised into four groups"},{"uid":"bd17e867-0157-4c21-af2f-0a4992c97613","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"according to their swimming performance","passagePhrase":"capable only of slow speeds but have some staying power ... can swim quite fast over long periods ... can generate short bursts of high speed ... generally sluggish swimmers although capable of slight acceleration"},{"uid":"a0df914a-4c47-4693-9e16-3fc20bd0c413","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"an aquatic species","passagePhrase":"A species of sailfish"},{"uid":"796c04d6-2ab2-4c52-915b-51525b39ac76","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the highest recorded ... swimming speed","passagePhrase":"the fastest fish over short distances"},{"uid":"defe2cff-4d98-4bb4-94bb-17eaf80e736c","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"over a three-second period"},{"uid":"43e1455b-f935-44a5-a517-cb28612c8d32","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"being small brings one in proportional terms","passagePhrase":"Relative to its size, a small fish is generally a more capable swimmer"},{"uid":"0067d403-d76a-4d46-ac5a-8859061c8f72","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Being big brings a speed advantage in raw terms","passagePhrase":"In terms of absolute speed ... a large fish will ... be able to swim faster"},{"uid":"796c04d6-2ab2-4c52-915b-51525b39ac76 defe2cff-4d98-4bb4-94bb-17eaf80e736c","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"burst","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"3e37dbeb-1f06-4b5f-b38f-56bf64e7970f 72b52d8c-7990-48cc-b5b0-a57f14bd1f5d","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"flexes","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_114":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><b><span>The Good-Enough Mother</span></b></p><p><span>Throughout history, new parents have experienced the pressures and responsibilities that come with rearing a child. Mothers in particular, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ebbc3648-3f15-4d33-8baa-78169ec49bd6\">for biological and societal reasons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2197a903-189a-4942-8fe6-37f9f040fa9c\">are under pressure to fulfil </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2197a903-189a-4942-8fe6-37f9f040fa9c 810e2442-b031-43e0-8020-9b0d708f4509\">the expectations</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"810e2442-b031-43e0-8020-9b0d708f4509\"> that</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ebbc3648-3f15-4d33-8baa-78169ec49bd6\">they and </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"810e2442-b031-43e0-8020-9b0d708f4509 ebbc3648-3f15-4d33-8baa-78169ec49bd6\">society</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"810e2442-b031-43e0-8020-9b0d708f4509\"> place on them</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Donald Winnicott, a British paediatrician and psychoanalyst, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bc1a3cce-1e59-4940-acc5-e63f8081bcd3\">broke new ground with his original views<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> on the relationship between children and their mothers, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"27549f69-3da2-4a93-b43e-0d52529bc797\">departing from </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"27549f69-3da2-4a93-b43e-0d52529bc797 83df94e6-2918-408b-87f2-8c3412cf133a\">prevailing ideas</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"83df94e6-2918-408b-87f2-8c3412cf133a\"> about parenting</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"27549f69-3da2-4a93-b43e-0d52529bc797\">Rather than endorsing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"83df94e6-2918-408b-87f2-8c3412cf133a\">the traditional and idealised view of parenting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, he offered a theoretical approach and guidance that were more grounded in the realities of parenthood. Winnicott’s notions of the ‘good-enough’ mother and the facilitating environment that he described remain important in the study of child development.</span></p><p><span>It would not be an exaggeration to say that most parents try to provide the best they can for their children, and many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"5e79ede7-ddd7-4aa0-8f93-48239553c237\">feel guilty when they are unable to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> do so, especially as many women and men in the modern world <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"9e30cf41-bcfb-45c4-a37f-5da18588a4d7\">try to balance their personal and professional lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> with the ideal of perfect parenthood. As a result, parenting has been intensively studied and various theories of parenting have been developed. While <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"cd8d7cbf-f52d-4803-824d-3241aa3d7457\">a variety of models<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> have informed the development of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"7d56c741-e7b4-4267-9006-e4b8e7aaea4c\">parenting programmes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"acfba371-de25-44ff-90de-6da2051d1483\">four theoretical approaches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> commonly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"594bc7c3-9aa3-4cf3-91d8-d45c53ca4982\">underpin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9505885b-dd30-4167-99f1-88943850bb0e\">many of them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Social learning theory is based on the assumption that children’s behaviour <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3847a221-917d-46e7-a863-62a1e6d802e2\">will improve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> when it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"4b5e891e-6bcf-4742-b5e2-988091d1b443\">appropriately reinforced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>: good behaviour is rewarded, while bad behaviour is either ignored or appropriately sanctioned. Programmes based on social learning theory <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"df3c60ce-5e6d-46be-a4a4-0523c2af8ba0\">teach parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> strategies for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1bc141d4-5fc2-4032-b7b4-91d4db40ecd9\">managing misconduct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c0f302bf-d71c-4565-a9fb-538a82de0f6b\">reinforcing positive behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Attachment theory is based on the notion that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"c9e1e045-a79f-4d5f-9ab2-13d9ed3a4567\">an infant’s ability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> to form a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"0f248cf0-56d8-44ef-878a-e2d293e149f9\">strong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> emotional bond with their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"9fc58b61-a57c-42a0-9d3d-e9da3b1ed80c\">primary caregiver<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"c9e1e045-a79f-4d5f-9ab2-13d9ed3a4567\">is a natural part of their development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"d94bf4e5-50f3-472f-95a5-3a78eea76018\">The security of this bond<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, also known as attachment security, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"d94bf4e5-50f3-472f-95a5-3a78eea76018\">is largely determined </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34 37\" data-uid=\"77bcc992-6659-4d41-955e-7b1d06caf4b3 d94bf4e5-50f3-472f-95a5-3a78eea76018\">by</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ac2f62c8-fc34-4f8a-ac2b-a66219a07e3b\">how sensitively and appropriately parents respond to their infant’s bids for attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Programmes based on attachment theory therefore aim to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"1b9aeb67-a720-4d44-aab6-4552a1586717\">improve parental sensitivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"2265b265-41e5-47cd-bbf6-de465fd7d9b9\">increasing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> parents’ understanding of their children’s needs and attachment-related behaviour.</span></p><p><span>Parenting styles theory is based on research suggesting that children’s behaviour is directly related to their parents’ child-rearing practices. Parents who combine high levels of parental warmth with high levels of supervision are likely to have children who are more confident, more autonomous and more socially responsible. This parenting style is often referred to as an authoritative style of parenting and recognises the child as an individual in their own right. For this reason, many parenting programmes include elements that encourage parents to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"02acf435-0d62-422b-b4da-394a08106f5a\">allow their children to engage in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> risk-taking <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"34a753ee-086d-4c0c-ab4b-e3eb03ae9e31\">while remaining under close supervision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The model of human ecology assumes that a child’s development is determined by their interaction with individual, family, school, community and cultural environments. Each of these environments contains elements that can either improve a child’s life outcomes or place them at risk of adversity. Every family has its own combination of risk and protective factors. Programmes based on this model consider ways to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"21718dd9-3dc1-4f87-b002-218eac0f2d72\">strengthen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> protective factors in order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"bfc1f946-e4cf-4db8-9346-f37599a98a19\">manage any ongoing risks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </span></p><p><span>Winnicott’s idea of a facilitating environment created for a child by a ‘good-enough mother’, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"da23be9d-e920-4f51-a67b-f465db9d74fc\">supported by the adults around her<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, has clear affinities with attachment theory. For Winnicott, this facilitating environment arises from <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e88b7e30-2859-4da7-b19d-327128d5cac8\">an unconscious process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> within an ordinary mother who is fond of her baby. He suggests that during pregnancy, a mother develops a state of heightened sensitivity, which continues for some weeks after the baby’s birth. When this heightened state passes, the mother experiences what Winnicott calls a ‘flight into sanity’ and becomes aware of the world beyond her state of primary maternal preoccupation with her infant.</span></p><p><span>The good-enough mother continues to provide an environment that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"d94bf4e5-50f3-472f-95a5-3a78eea76018\">supports the baby’s healthy maturational processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. She protects the baby from unpredictable disruptions and provides care through holding, handling and the general management of the child. In addition to meeting the baby’s physical needs, she provides emotional warmth and love. She must also protect the baby from the consequences of the hostile, even murderous, feelings that may arise in her when, for example, the baby screams and cries continuously. By containing these hateful feelings rather than acting on them, she can use her awareness of them to understand the baby’s own terror and hate. At first, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ac2f62c8-fc34-4f8a-ac2b-a66219a07e3b\">she adapts closely to the baby’s needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, allowing the baby to experience a sense of omnipotence. As the baby gradually begins to feel secure enough to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"593e0632-6363-4889-bcb4-196dcd70656d\">relinquish this sense of omnipotence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"e0d8a8d7-8b78-4248-80e4-7e96657dcf45\">the process of integration can begin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, and the baby starts to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"e0d8a8d7-8b78-4248-80e4-7e96657dcf45\">develop a distinction between ‘me’ and ‘not me<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>’. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"dc250e7d-176e-419c-8d9c-6c577b11a5f4\">To support this development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, the good-enough mother <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"6735b5c2-7ce0-4947-b4db-5b92c9296f7c\">must gradually ‘fail’ to adapt fully to the baby’s needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, allowing the baby to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"593e0632-6363-4889-bcb4-196dcd70656d\">learn to tolerate the frustrations of the world beyond the mother–infant relationship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Winnicott <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"4b83286a-304a-4e58-b48f-1c0b1c09f6aa\">intended to take the pressure off mothers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, but critics have argued that his idea of the good-enough mother has placed undue expectations on actual mothers, suggesting that they must shoulder most of the responsibility for caring for their babies. Furthermore, mothers are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"2012313e-2543-4da7-9cbb-cb7ebf6ec840\">held responsible for how well their babies flourish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>As with many theories of child development, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"4524a613-df50-4c13-9440-5f6cc0414f58\">real-life parenting does not fit neatly within a single </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"4524a613-df50-4c13-9440-5f6cc0414f58 7972e79e-b536-4ac1-9d77-079fc798f996\">theoretical model</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Most parents display elements associated with several approaches <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"0fcf1a19-3ef6-4952-b616-226f0bf96a4f\">as they adapt naturally to different situations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Nevertheless, Winnicott’s ideas have been a source of comfort and hope to many mothers who have struggled with the challenges of motherhood.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><b><span>YES</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NO</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326425\" id=\"question-wrapper-326425\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"810e2442-b031-43e0-8020-9b0d708f4509\">What society demands of mothers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ebbc3648-3f15-4d33-8baa-78169ec49bd6\">not the only reason<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> they may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2197a903-189a-4942-8fe6-37f9f040fa9c\">feel pushed to reach certain standards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326426\" id=\"question-wrapper-326426\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Winnicott's <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bc1a3cce-1e59-4940-acc5-e63f8081bcd3\">main aim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> was to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"27549f69-3da2-4a93-b43e-0d52529bc797\">make<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"83df94e6-2918-408b-87f2-8c3412cf133a\">conventional notions of raising children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"27549f69-3da2-4a93-b43e-0d52529bc797\">easier to apply, not to question those notions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326427\" id=\"question-wrapper-326427\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"9e30cf41-bcfb-45c4-a37f-5da18588a4d7\">Difficulty in reconciling work and family life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> makes women suffer more than men from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"5e79ede7-ddd7-4aa0-8f93-48239553c237\">feeling they have let their children down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326428\" id=\"question-wrapper-326428\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Despite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"cd8d7cbf-f52d-4803-824d-3241aa3d7457\">the range of frameworks available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9505885b-dd30-4167-99f1-88943850bb0e\">most<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"7d56c741-e7b4-4267-9006-e4b8e7aaea4c\">schemes designed to help parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"594bc7c3-9aa3-4cf3-91d8-d45c53ca4982\">rest on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"acfba371-de25-44ff-90de-6da2051d1483\">a small number of them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the table below.</span></p><p><span>Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 31–36 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Four Theoretical Approaches to Parenting</span></b></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Social Learning Theory</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>The theory assumes that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"4b5e891e-6bcf-4742-b5e2-988091d1b443\">the correct response to what children do<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3847a221-917d-46e7-a863-62a1e6d802e2\">make<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> their (31)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3847a221-917d-46e7-a863-62a1e6d802e2\">better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. </span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"df3c60ce-5e6d-46be-a4a4-0523c2af8ba0\">Parents learn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> (32)_______ for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1bc141d4-5fc2-4032-b7b4-91d4db40ecd9\">dealing with misconduct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"c0f302bf-d71c-4565-a9fb-538a82de0f6b\">encouraging positive behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Attachment Theory</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"c9e1e045-a79f-4d5f-9ab2-13d9ed3a4567\">Babies are born with the ability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> to develop a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"0f248cf0-56d8-44ef-878a-e2d293e149f9\">firm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> (33)______ with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"9fc58b61-a57c-42a0-9d3d-e9da3b1ed80c\">whoever looks after them most<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </span></p><p><span>Parents <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"1b9aeb67-a720-4d44-aab6-4552a1586717\">become more responsive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"77bcc992-6659-4d41-955e-7b1d06caf4b3\">thanks to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"2265b265-41e5-47cd-bbf6-de465fd7d9b9\">deepened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> (34)_______ of their children.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Parenting Styles Theory</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Children’s behaviour is linked to their parents’ child-rearing practices. </span></p><p><span>A combination of warmth and supervision is associated with an authoritative parenting style. </span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"02acf435-0d62-422b-b4da-394a08106f5a\">Children can try<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> (35)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"34a753ee-086d-4c0c-ab4b-e3eb03ae9e31\">under parental supervision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Human Ecology</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>A child’s development is influenced by interactions with several environments. </span></p><p><span>(36)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"21718dd9-3dc1-4f87-b002-218eac0f2d72\">are reinforced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> so that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"bfc1f946-e4cf-4db8-9346-f37599a98a19\">continuing risks can be dealt with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326429\" id=\"question-wrapper-326429\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BEHAVIO(U)R</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326430\" id=\"question-wrapper-326430\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STRATEGIES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326431\" id=\"question-wrapper-326431\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EMOTIONAL BOND</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326432\" id=\"question-wrapper-326432\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">UNDERSTANDING</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326433\" id=\"question-wrapper-326433\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RISK-TAKING</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326434\" id=\"question-wrapper-326434\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PROTECTIVE FACTORS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, **A, B, C or D**. Write the correct letter in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326435\" id=\"question-wrapper-326435\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why does the writer say Winnicott’s facilitating environment has “clear affinities” with attachment theory?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Both regard <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"da23be9d-e920-4f51-a67b-f465db9d74fc\">support from other adults<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> as essential to the child’s development.</li> <li>B. Both make <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"ac2f62c8-fc34-4f8a-ac2b-a66219a07e3b\">the caregiver’s responsiveness to the infant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"d94bf4e5-50f3-472f-95a5-3a78eea76018\">central to healthy development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Both assume parents should <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e88b7e30-2859-4da7-b19d-327128d5cac8\">consciously interpret<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> the infant’s behaviour before responding.</li> <li>D. Both see intense maternal preoccupation as necessary throughout the infant’s early life.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326436\" id=\"question-wrapper-326436\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why must the good-enough mother <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"6735b5c2-7ce0-4947-b4db-5b92c9296f7c\">gradually “fail” to adapt fully<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> to the baby’s needs?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. To transfer some of the baby’s dependence from the mother to other adults.</li> <li>B. To protect the baby from the mother’s hostile feelings as awareness increases.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"dc250e7d-176e-419c-8d9c-6c577b11a5f4\">To help<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> the baby <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"593e0632-6363-4889-bcb4-196dcd70656d\">accept limits to its own control<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"e0d8a8d7-8b78-4248-80e4-7e96657dcf45\">a separate sense of self develops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li> <li>D. To reduce dependence on physical care while preserving emotional dependence on the mother.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326437\" id=\"question-wrapper-326437\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What contradiction do critics identify in Winnicott’s idea of the good-enough mother?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"4b83286a-304a-4e58-b48f-1c0b1c09f6aa\">set out to ease the burden on mothers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> yet may leave them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"2012313e-2543-4da7-9cbb-cb7ebf6ec840\">feeling answerable for how their babies turn out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</li> <li>B. It acknowledges help from other adults but could make mothers less sure of their own judgement.</li> <li>C. It admits that mothers can feel anger towards their babies but might encourage them to show it.</li> <li>D. It promotes gradual independence but could lead mothers to withdraw care before babies are ready.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326438\" id=\"question-wrapper-326438\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What conclusion does the writer draw about parenting theories in the final paragraph?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Parents usually move between theories deliberately as circumstances change.</li> <li>B. Parenting theories are useful only when adapted to a family's specific needs.</li> <li>C. Winnicott's model remains relevant because it combines elements of several approaches.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"4524a613-df50-4c13-9440-5f6cc0414f58\">No one </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"4524a613-df50-4c13-9440-5f6cc0414f58 7972e79e-b536-4ac1-9d77-079fc798f996\">framework</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"4524a613-df50-4c13-9440-5f6cc0414f58\"> accounts for everything parents do</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"0fcf1a19-3ef6-4952-b616-226f0bf96a4f\">as situations vary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"ebbc3648-3f15-4d33-8baa-78169ec49bd6","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"not the only reason","passagePhrase":"for biological and societal reasons ... they and"},{"uid":"2197a903-189a-4942-8fe6-37f9f040fa9c","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"feel pushed to reach certain standards","passagePhrase":"are under pressure to fulfil"},{"uid":"2197a903-189a-4942-8fe6-37f9f040fa9c 810e2442-b031-43e0-8020-9b0d708f4509","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the expectations"},{"uid":"810e2442-b031-43e0-8020-9b0d708f4509","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"What society demands of mothers","passagePhrase":"that ... place on them"},{"uid":"810e2442-b031-43e0-8020-9b0d708f4509 ebbc3648-3f15-4d33-8baa-78169ec49bd6","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"society"},{"uid":"27549f69-3da2-4a93-b43e-0d52529bc797 83df94e6-2918-408b-87f2-8c3412cf133a","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"prevailing ideas"},{"uid":"83df94e6-2918-408b-87f2-8c3412cf133a","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"conventional notions of raising children","passagePhrase":"about parenting ... the traditional and idealised view of parenting"},{"uid":"5e79ede7-ddd7-4aa0-8f93-48239553c237","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"feeling they have let their children down","passagePhrase":"feel guilty when they are unable to"},{"uid":"9e30cf41-bcfb-45c4-a37f-5da18588a4d7","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Difficulty in reconciling work and family life","passagePhrase":"try to balance their personal and professional lives"},{"uid":"cd8d7cbf-f52d-4803-824d-3241aa3d7457","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"the range of frameworks available","passagePhrase":"a variety of models"},{"uid":"7d56c741-e7b4-4267-9006-e4b8e7aaea4c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"schemes designed to help parents","passagePhrase":"parenting programmes"},{"uid":"acfba371-de25-44ff-90de-6da2051d1483","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"a small number of them","passagePhrase":"four theoretical approaches"},{"uid":"594bc7c3-9aa3-4cf3-91d8-d45c53ca4982","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"rest on","passagePhrase":"underpin"},{"uid":"9505885b-dd30-4167-99f1-88943850bb0e","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"most","passagePhrase":"many of them"},{"uid":"3847a221-917d-46e7-a863-62a1e6d802e2","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"make ... better","passagePhrase":"will improve"},{"uid":"4b5e891e-6bcf-4742-b5e2-988091d1b443","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"the correct response to what children do","passagePhrase":"appropriately reinforced"},{"uid":"df3c60ce-5e6d-46be-a4a4-0523c2af8ba0","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Parents learn","passagePhrase":"teach parents"},{"uid":"1bc141d4-5fc2-4032-b7b4-91d4db40ecd9","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"dealing with misconduct","passagePhrase":"managing misconduct"},{"uid":"c0f302bf-d71c-4565-a9fb-538a82de0f6b","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"encouraging positive behaviour","passagePhrase":"reinforcing positive behaviour"},{"uid":"c9e1e045-a79f-4d5f-9ab2-13d9ed3a4567","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Babies are born with the ability","passagePhrase":"an infant’s ability ... is a natural part of their development"},{"uid":"0f248cf0-56d8-44ef-878a-e2d293e149f9","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"firm","passagePhrase":"strong"},{"uid":"9fc58b61-a57c-42a0-9d3d-e9da3b1ed80c","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"whoever looks after them most","passagePhrase":"primary caregiver"},{"uid":"d94bf4e5-50f3-472f-95a5-3a78eea76018","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"central to healthy development","passagePhrase":"The security of this bond ... is largely determined ... supports the baby’s healthy maturational processes"},{"uid":"77bcc992-6659-4d41-955e-7b1d06caf4b3 d94bf4e5-50f3-472f-95a5-3a78eea76018","qNum":"34 37","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"by"},{"uid":"ac2f62c8-fc34-4f8a-ac2b-a66219a07e3b","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"the caregiver’s responsiveness to the infant","passagePhrase":"how sensitively and appropriately parents respond to their infant’s bids for attention ... she adapts closely to the baby’s needs"},{"uid":"1b9aeb67-a720-4d44-aab6-4552a1586717","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"become more responsive","passagePhrase":"improve parental sensitivity"},{"uid":"2265b265-41e5-47cd-bbf6-de465fd7d9b9","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"deepened","passagePhrase":"increasing"},{"uid":"02acf435-0d62-422b-b4da-394a08106f5a","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Children can try","passagePhrase":"allow their children to engage in"},{"uid":"34a753ee-086d-4c0c-ab4b-e3eb03ae9e31","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"under parental supervision","passagePhrase":"while remaining under close supervision"},{"uid":"21718dd9-3dc1-4f87-b002-218eac0f2d72","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"are reinforced","passagePhrase":"strengthen"},{"uid":"bfc1f946-e4cf-4db8-9346-f37599a98a19","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"continuing risks can be dealt with","passagePhrase":"manage any ongoing risks"},{"uid":"da23be9d-e920-4f51-a67b-f465db9d74fc","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"support from other adults","passagePhrase":"supported by the adults around her"},{"uid":"593e0632-6363-4889-bcb4-196dcd70656d","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"accept limits to its own control","passagePhrase":"relinquish this sense of omnipotence ... learn to tolerate the frustrations of the world beyond the mother–infant relationship"},{"uid":"e0d8a8d7-8b78-4248-80e4-7e96657dcf45","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"a separate sense of self develops","passagePhrase":"the process of integration can begin ... develop a distinction between ‘me’ and ‘not me"},{"uid":"dc250e7d-176e-419c-8d9c-6c577b11a5f4","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"To help","passagePhrase":"To support this development"},{"uid":"6735b5c2-7ce0-4947-b4db-5b92c9296f7c","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"gradually “fail” to adapt fully","passagePhrase":"must gradually ‘fail’ to adapt fully to the baby’s needs"},{"uid":"4b83286a-304a-4e58-b48f-1c0b1c09f6aa","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"set out to ease the burden on mothers","passagePhrase":"intended to take the pressure off mothers"},{"uid":"2012313e-2543-4da7-9cbb-cb7ebf6ec840","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"feeling answerable for how their babies turn out","passagePhrase":"held responsible for how well their babies flourish"},{"uid":"4524a613-df50-4c13-9440-5f6cc0414f58","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"No one ... accounts for everything parents do","passagePhrase":"real-life parenting does not fit neatly within a single"},{"uid":"4524a613-df50-4c13-9440-5f6cc0414f58 7972e79e-b536-4ac1-9d77-079fc798f996","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"framework","passagePhrase":"theoretical model"},{"uid":"0fcf1a19-3ef6-4952-b616-226f0bf96a4f","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"as situations vary","passagePhrase":"as they adapt naturally to different situations"},{"uid":"77bcc992-6659-4d41-955e-7b1d06caf4b3","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"thanks to","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_115":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>The world's first cities</span></b></p><p><b><span>The creation of Mesopotamian cities</span></b></p><p><span>The inhabitants of Mesopotamia, which now lies within Iraq and parts of eastern Syria and southeastern Turkey, lived for thousands of years on individual farms or in small, isolated communities, working relentlessly just to meet their basic needs. But then, about 6,000 years ago, something remarkable happened. The people left the security of their family homes and villages and came together to create something far more complex and difficult: the world’s first city, Uruk.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4d81184f-4614-48e1-bfe0-2f00f74ba83a\">Not much of Uruk remains today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. Located about 250 kilometres <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"8aa0c792-4255-4bf2-a8bc-2b152379a7ff\">south of Baghdad, the capital of Iraq<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4d81184f-4614-48e1-bfe0-2f00f74ba83a\">enough of the city survives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> to show that this initial experiment in urban living was extraordinarily successful. At its height, around 5,000 years ago, Uruk was home to more than 40,000 people. The outlines of the city walls indicate an enclosed area of about 600 hectares.</span></p><p><span>The archaeological record of Uruk reveals intensive building and rebuilding that continued for four or five centuries after the city was established. During this period, the people of Uruk built a dozen or so large public buildings. They would carefully level the previous structure and then build another on top, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"79b0c263-21e3-48cb-b2e1-89df2cceb533\">often<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"66f990aa-6102-4f69-a24d-0766c2db5c1c\">experimenting with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"3f7937f6-3073-484f-9100-5bdbb1ab53d6\">a different building material or an innovative technique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. They seemed to be searching for ways in which architecture could express the new social structures that had come into being there.</span></p><p><span>Soon, Uruk was not the only Mesopotamian city. People throughout the flat plains of southern Mesopotamia were enjoying many of the benefits of city life. By about 4,500 years ago, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"7f5dfc7f-d8ec-4f41-9ace-4c67babfb3e5\">80 per cent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of the Mesopotamian population lived in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c73fa34d-e481-4187-b8e5-315687cb9723\">cities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> over 40 hectares in size, with populations of between 15,000 and 30,000. The emergence of these thriving communities, made up largely of people who were not related by blood, was unprecedented in human history. Why did these extraordinary developments occur?</span></p><p><b><span>Reasons for the creation of cities in Mesopotamia</span></b></p><p><span>Smaller communities in Mesopotamia sometimes decided to come together to defend themselves more effectively from their enemies. But the underlying reason for the creation of cities lay in the harshness of this particular environment. The area was a place of extremes, where narrow fertile river valleys were bounded by thousands of kilometres of desert and unproductive wetlands.</span></p><p><span>As the low level of rainfall in the region was insufficient to sustain more than very limited agriculture, it was only through sophisticated irrigation that isolated areas of land could be kept fertile. The Tigris and Euphrates rivers provided water for irrigation and also formed the basis of a communication network that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"26af3c6c-5306-4666-923b-871ddde01d51\">led to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"3d36d421-662e-4592-9885-6a3f872a03b2\">the spread of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"ceff9126-bb10-4f5c-89a1-2146af05bc5f\">the latest farming ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>In such a region, the only way for people to prosper was to form groups that could work together. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"be44f296-c701-4dc7-b9f2-08c953607f00\">The threat of famine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, which could be caused by a prolonged drought or a sudden change in the course of a river, forced people to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"76a04f31-edaa-4fc4-a8c9-dfdb24162439\">look beyond their families and work with their neighbours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"8201356e-804e-4642-ad45-e89059f19f63\">create an elaborate system of dams, channels and canals to manage water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. These projects required specific skills and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"76a04f31-edaa-4fc4-a8c9-dfdb24162439\">labour from beyond the farmer’s own family<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. This reliance on people outside the family more firmly established the patterns of dependence that are at the heart of civilization.</span></p><p><b><span>Changes in the organisation of farming</span></b></p><p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"664f103f-8128-43d5-a56e-47e784167d6b\">intensive farming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> that developed in Mesopotamia was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"664f103f-8128-43d5-a56e-47e784167d6b\">more efficient and productive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and therefore generated a surplus of food, allowing crops from good harvests to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"e71b2294-c457-4fe6-b1f5-22b93d0010e0\">stored<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> as a safeguard against <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"5e7b1371-98ce-4a2a-8b1f-0cab66ce02ab\">poorer harvests in future years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. It also allowed more land to be used for the production of a wider range of crops. This created a need for traders and skilled craftsmen; in short, it marked the beginning of industry and consumerism.</span></p><p><span>Specialisation emerged within the population, with increasing numbers of soldiers, builders, musicians, doctors and fortune-tellers, all supported directly or indirectly by agriculture. At the same time, this growing specialisation increased the control that powerful institutions, gradually emerging in the early cities, had over the urban population. Although large numbers of people were freed from the struggle of subsistence farming, they were now totally dependent on the institutions that employed them for their daily sustenance.</span></p><p><b><span>The role of the temples</span></b></p><p><span>The earliest and most powerful of these institutions was centred on the temple. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"674ba067-fdca-43ed-b556-e14d8278bdd9\">Increasing numbers of temple structures were erected as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"203879ee-a166-468c-810d-b859660fbfe5\">massive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> pyramids <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"59c2fdb8-a430-405e-8f0b-ee27cc0ad7c7\">with enormous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> storerooms for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c5e1164c-d18d-4dde-b58a-450ca050f496\">produce from the farming estates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Over time, the temples acquired these farms and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"bf70104b-1117-483c-8af6-dab88484a9b1\">appointed a large number of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> staff to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"b83619f6-142c-4dd9-bcd0-1437895bf5bd\">administer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> them and manage the storage of produce.</span></p><p><span>The temples’ greatest advantage was that each citizen was expected to devote some time to working for them. This allowed the temples to store huge amounts of agricultural produce, which could then be used to buy more land. In addition, the revenue they generated allowed the temples to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"dad46679-2686-40b8-803e-d644214db2a7\">serve as primitive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> banks by making loans to people during <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"1f8ac5b0-09a1-4bc4-9f20-0491e98d7dbc\">difficult economic times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>The emergence of writing</span></b></p><p><span>We know a surprising amount about this period thanks to the development of an important new technology: writing. In Mesopotamia, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"42c557ab-7b76-4a93-bb8a-90a675bc052d\">basic records were inscribed on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> wet clay rather than on the fragile papyrus used in ancient Egypt and Greece. These first writings were largely lists of people and things used for simple bookkeeping. But within several hundred years, writing systems had become more advanced and capable of recording concepts as well as lists. The clay tablets used for writing were durable, and fires that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"06fa7aaf-9796-4461-8875-744af928165d\">destroyed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the archives where they were stored often simply baked the tablets, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"aaa72b92-e083-4bfd-8d3c-ac56af652baa\">preserving them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> for future generations.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326439\" id=\"question-wrapper-326439\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4d81184f-4614-48e1-bfe0-2f00f74ba83a\">physical evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of Uruk <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4d81184f-4614-48e1-bfe0-2f00f74ba83a\">still exists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"8aa0c792-4255-4bf2-a8bc-2b152379a7ff\">in Iraq<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326440\" id=\"question-wrapper-326440\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The people of Uruk lived in large apartment buildings.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326441\" id=\"question-wrapper-326441\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Builders in Uruk <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"79b0c263-21e3-48cb-b2e1-89df2cceb533\">frequently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"66f990aa-6102-4f69-a24d-0766c2db5c1c\">tried out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"3f7937f6-3073-484f-9100-5bdbb1ab53d6\">new construction methods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326442\" id=\"question-wrapper-326442\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"c73fa34d-e481-4187-b8e5-315687cb9723\">Urban settlements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> had attracted <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"7f5dfc7f-d8ec-4f41-9ace-4c67babfb3e5\">only a minority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of Mesopotamia’s population by about 4,500 years ago.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326443\" id=\"question-wrapper-326443\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Tigris and Euphrates <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"26af3c6c-5306-4666-923b-871ddde01d51\">enabled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"ceff9126-bb10-4f5c-89a1-2146af05bc5f\">new agricultural concepts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"3d36d421-662e-4592-9885-6a3f872a03b2\">circulate more widely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326444\" id=\"question-wrapper-326444\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"be44f296-c701-4dc7-b9f2-08c953607f00\">times of food shortages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, farmers could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"8201356e-804e-4642-ad45-e89059f19f63\">construct water-management infrastructure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"76a04f31-edaa-4fc4-a8c9-dfdb24162439\">only with the help of their relatives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose</span><b><span> ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Early changes in Mesopotamia</span></b></p><p><b><span>Changes in the organisation of farming</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"664f103f-8128-43d5-a56e-47e784167d6b\">Improved agricultural methods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> led to:</span></p><ul><li><span>a food (7)______ being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"e71b2294-c457-4fe6-b1f5-22b93d0010e0\">set aside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"5e7b1371-98ce-4a2a-8b1f-0cab66ce02ab\">less productive years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></span></li><li><span>a wider range of crops being grown</span></li><li><span>the development of industry and consumerism</span></li><li><span>increased specialisation among workers</span></li><li><span>greater control by institutions</span></li></ul><p><b><span>Temples</span></b></p><ul><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"674ba067-fdca-43ed-b556-e14d8278bdd9\">new temple buildings increasingly took the form of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"203879ee-a166-468c-810d-b859660fbfe5\">large<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)______</span></li><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"59c2fdb8-a430-405e-8f0b-ee27cc0ad7c7\">included extensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)______ for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c5e1164c-d18d-4dde-b58a-450ca050f496\">goods from farms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></li><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"bf70104b-1117-483c-8af6-dab88484a9b1\">employed several<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)______ to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"b83619f6-142c-4dd9-bcd0-1437895bf5bd\">run<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> their farms </span></li><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"dad46679-2686-40b8-803e-d644214db2a7\">had a role similar to that of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)______ during <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"1f8ac5b0-09a1-4bc4-9f20-0491e98d7dbc\">periods of financial hardship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span></span></li></ul><p><b><span>The development of writing</span></b></p><ul><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"42c557ab-7b76-4a93-bb8a-90a675bc052d\">people wrote on surfaces made of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12)______ </span></li><li><span>while their archives <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"06fa7aaf-9796-4461-8875-744af928165d\">were lost in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)______, the written records <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"aaa72b92-e083-4bfd-8d3c-ac56af652baa\">remained undamaged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></span></li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326445\" id=\"question-wrapper-326445\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SURPLUS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326446\" id=\"question-wrapper-326446\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PYRAMIDS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326447\" id=\"question-wrapper-326447\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STOREROOMS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326448\" id=\"question-wrapper-326448\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STAFF</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326449\" id=\"question-wrapper-326449\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BANKS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326450\" id=\"question-wrapper-326450\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CLAY</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326451\" id=\"question-wrapper-326451\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FIRES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"4d81184f-4614-48e1-bfe0-2f00f74ba83a","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"physical evidence ... still exists","passagePhrase":"Not much of Uruk remains today ... enough of the city survives"},{"uid":"8aa0c792-4255-4bf2-a8bc-2b152379a7ff","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"in Iraq","passagePhrase":"south of Baghdad, the capital of Iraq"},{"uid":"79b0c263-21e3-48cb-b2e1-89df2cceb533","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"frequently","passagePhrase":"often"},{"uid":"66f990aa-6102-4f69-a24d-0766c2db5c1c","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"tried out","passagePhrase":"experimenting with"},{"uid":"3f7937f6-3073-484f-9100-5bdbb1ab53d6","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"new construction methods","passagePhrase":"a different building material or an innovative technique"},{"uid":"c73fa34d-e481-4187-b8e5-315687cb9723","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Urban settlements","passagePhrase":"cities"},{"uid":"26af3c6c-5306-4666-923b-871ddde01d51","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"enabled","passagePhrase":"led to"},{"uid":"3d36d421-662e-4592-9885-6a3f872a03b2","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"circulate more widely","passagePhrase":"the spread of"},{"uid":"ceff9126-bb10-4f5c-89a1-2146af05bc5f","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"new agricultural concepts","passagePhrase":"the latest farming ideas"},{"uid":"be44f296-c701-4dc7-b9f2-08c953607f00","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"times of food shortages","passagePhrase":"The threat of famine"},{"uid":"8201356e-804e-4642-ad45-e89059f19f63","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"construct water-management infrastructure","passagePhrase":"create an elaborate system of dams, channels and canals to manage water"},{"uid":"664f103f-8128-43d5-a56e-47e784167d6b","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Improved agricultural methods","passagePhrase":"intensive farming ... more efficient and productive"},{"uid":"e71b2294-c457-4fe6-b1f5-22b93d0010e0","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"set aside","passagePhrase":"stored"},{"uid":"5e7b1371-98ce-4a2a-8b1f-0cab66ce02ab","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"less productive years","passagePhrase":"poorer harvests in future years"},{"uid":"674ba067-fdca-43ed-b556-e14d8278bdd9","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"new temple buildings increasingly took the form of","passagePhrase":"Increasing numbers of temple structures were erected as"},{"uid":"203879ee-a166-468c-810d-b859660fbfe5","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"large","passagePhrase":"massive"},{"uid":"59c2fdb8-a430-405e-8f0b-ee27cc0ad7c7","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"included extensive","passagePhrase":"with enormous"},{"uid":"c5e1164c-d18d-4dde-b58a-450ca050f496","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"goods from farms","passagePhrase":"produce from the farming estates"},{"uid":"bf70104b-1117-483c-8af6-dab88484a9b1","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"employed several","passagePhrase":"appointed a large number of"},{"uid":"b83619f6-142c-4dd9-bcd0-1437895bf5bd","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"run","passagePhrase":"administer"},{"uid":"dad46679-2686-40b8-803e-d644214db2a7","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"had a role similar to that of","passagePhrase":"serve as primitive"},{"uid":"1f8ac5b0-09a1-4bc4-9f20-0491e98d7dbc","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"periods of financial hardship","passagePhrase":"difficult economic times"},{"uid":"42c557ab-7b76-4a93-bb8a-90a675bc052d","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"people wrote on surfaces made of","passagePhrase":"basic records were inscribed on"},{"uid":"06fa7aaf-9796-4461-8875-744af928165d","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"were lost in","passagePhrase":"destroyed"},{"uid":"aaa72b92-e083-4bfd-8d3c-ac56af652baa","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"remained undamaged","passagePhrase":"preserving them"}]},"reading_u2_116":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>The Cultures of Chimpanzees</span></b></p><p><b><span>A</span></b></p><p><span>The similarities between chimpanzees and humans have been studied for years, and research conducted over a decade has shown that these resemblances run much deeper than was previously thought. For instance, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"f0b28ced-87be-473c-b3e5-f1e0f2d69240\">the nut-cracking behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> observed in the Taï Forest is far from simple; rather, it is a distinctive adaptation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"0e0dcf9a-edd4-4e5c-b386-2a37f388b560\">found only in that particular part of Africa<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> and a trait that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ad06d278-c0c7-48d8-9d16-121b0bc4006c\">biologists regard as an expression of chimpanzee culture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Scientists frequently use the term ‘culture’ to describe simple animal behaviours—such as regional dialects among different songbird populations—but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"91c48fbc-9018-4224-ac78-9445fbde08d6\">the rich and varied cultural traditions found among chimpanzees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"7ad61bc6-3c5f-411a-8379-32abb8bdf8f5\">second only to human traditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"91c48fbc-9018-4224-ac78-9445fbde08d6\">complexity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"db9f575c-c32a-4f52-ae97-2370f64de3c9\">Over a two-year period, an unprecedented scientific collaboration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> involving every major research group studying chimpanzees <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"3da34950-d181-4453-aa5b-4f7c418bb0cd\">documented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> numerous distinct cultural patterns across Africa, ranging from tool use to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"3f7e85f9-f56b-4504-8719-7941fe5d8322\">forms of communication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and social customs. This emerging picture of chimpanzees not only affects how we think of these animals but also alters our conception of our own uniqueness and hints at the ancient foundations of our extraordinary capacity for culture.</span></p><p><b><span>C</span></b></p><p><span>Homo sapiens and Pan troglodytes have coexisted for hundreds of millennia and share more than 98 per cent of their genetic material, yet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"d0c53f0d-18f4-4435-9500-7b961c74b352\">until systematic field studies began<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in the 1960s, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"d0c53f0d-18f4-4435-9500-7b961c74b352\">very little was known<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"0240a547-e8bc-42df-8017-165637aabbff\">chimpanzee behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"7f79ad0c-5db8-4f09-8b1f-06e200fd4235\">in the wild<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. This changed when Toshisada Nishida of Kyoto University in Japan and Jane Goodall began studying wild chimpanzees at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"fbf4deef-bb67-4e60-b2f2-3e05519b4016\">two field sites in Tanzania<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Goodall’s research station at Gombe—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"2b1630a7-b62c-40f3-b05b-b3fa62eb4a29\">the first of its kind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>—is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"b772de68-5590-4b81-807f-dda32e87508c\">more famous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, while Nishida’s site at Mahale is the second-oldest chimpanzee research site in the world.</span></p><p><b><span>D</span></b></p><p><span>In these initial studies, as the chimpanzees <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"6128cc09-a8ae-4d74-bac7-7d211b75ffe9\">became accustomed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> close observation, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"7ae19674-8173-42cc-be2f-dce960ba5f2a\">remarkable findings began to emerge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Researchers witnessed a range of unexpected behaviours, including fashioning and using tools, hunting, meat-eating, food sharing and lethal fights between members of neighbouring communities. In the years that followed, other primatologists established research sites elsewhere, and despite the financial, political and logistical problems that can beset fieldwork in Africa, several of these sites developed into long-term projects. As a result, these studies have produced a detailed and comprehensive scientific record of chimpanzees’ lives, not just for one but for several communities spread across Africa.</span></p><p><b><span>E</span></b></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"b1b6ce33-74ae-48f5-ab6a-97df1abdc985\">As early as 1973<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, Goodall recorded 13 forms of tool use as well as eight social activities. These appeared to differ between the Gombe chimpanzees and populations elsewhere. She suggested that some of these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"7ca8b7a1-df7a-4c19-92cd-03b5379bf74c\">variations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"633b2da5-a861-4121-a82c-cfa98ab23087\">had<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> what she termed a cultural origin. But what exactly did Goodall mean by “culture”? According to the Oxford Encyclopedic English Dictionary, culture is defined as “the customs … and achievements of a particular time or people.” The diversity of human cultures extends from technological variations to marriage rituals, from culinary habits to myths and legends. Animals do not have myths and legends. But they do have the capacity to pass on behavioural traits from generation to generation, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"19cfdb22-faa0-48d3-8f03-a50921a78472\">not through genetic inheritance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"794f9ed2-eac2-4841-8308-87dd7b9bdcf4\">through learning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. For biologists, this is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"2a225f16-3a4f-40a4-8110-c6436b836122\">the fundamental criterion for a cultural trait<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>: it must be something that can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"794f9ed2-eac2-4841-8308-87dd7b9bdcf4\">learned by observing skills already practised by others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and thus passed on to future generations.</span></p><p><b><span>F</span></b></p><p><span>What, then, are the implications for chimpanzees themselves? Chimpanzee populations are declining severely even as scientific understanding of these animals has become more complete. Their numbers have fallen dramatically over roughly a century and continue to decline as a result of illegal trapping, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3aa7bf81-821c-4ac9-aa3c-4e9fcbcae77a\">logging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and the bushmeat trade. The bushmeat trade is particularly alarming: logging has led to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"02c00c0c-b445-47a9-b98a-a69cc9230791\">roads being built<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> into the forests, which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"02c00c0c-b445-47a9-b98a-a69cc9230791\">used to transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> meat from wild animals—including chimpanzee meat—to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"32fb12c1-cf06-4157-b866-59e98d526f4c\">consumers as far away as Europe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. Such destruction threatens not only the animals themselves but also a diverse range of ape cultures.</span></p><p><b><span>G</span></b></p><p><span>However, the cultural richness of chimpanzees may itself contribute to their conservation. Some conservation efforts have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"53e7632e-f8e5-48d6-bda9-ff0e87fa0c16\">altered the attitudes of some local people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. A few organisations have begun to show <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c9648011-de95-4fbb-a4a0-f8ec8c6f1e3b\">videotapes illustrating the cognitive abilities of chimpanzees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. One Zairian viewer exclaimed, “Ah, this ape is so like me, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"53e7632e-f8e5-48d6-bda9-ff0e87fa0c16\">I can no longer eat him<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.”</span></p><p><b><span>H</span></b></p><p><span>The international team of chimpanzee experts conducted the most comprehensive survey of chimpanzees ever attempted. Scientists had been investigating chimpanzee culture for several decades, but many of their studies shared a crucial limitation. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"34fa3aa1-3aeb-4012-8748-c8e739e661a2\">Most previous attempts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> to document cultural diversity among chimpanzees had <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"739ce162-ffbc-406b-bc10-59e74bc20b78 aa885893-ca24-4e73-b03f-c24a111581a7\">relied</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"aa885893-ca24-4e73-b03f-c24a111581a7\"> solely on published reports</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of the behaviours recorded at each research site. This approach was likely to overlook considerable cultural variation for three reasons.</span></p><p><b><span>I</span></b></p><p><span>First, scientists typically did not publish extensive records of activities that were not observed at a particular site. Yet knowing which behaviours were and were not observed at each site was essential. Second, many reports described chimpanzee behaviours without indicating how common they were; without this information, researchers could not determine whether a particular action was an isolated occurrence or a routine event that should be considered part of the animals’ culture. Finally, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"1cfc29f1-54dd-4379-b27c-615c902b51be\">researchers’ descriptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of potentially significant chimpanzee behaviours frequently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"620a8f89-42c3-4823-b745-2479d27c71ea\">lacked sufficient detail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, making it difficult for scientists working at other sites to determine whether those behaviours were present or absent.</span></p><p><b><span>J</span></b></p><p><span>To address these problems, the researchers adopted a new approach. Field researchers at each site were asked to provide a list of all behaviours they suspected were local traditions. Using this information, the researchers compiled a comprehensive list of 65 candidate cultural behaviours.</span></p><p><b><span>K</span></b></p><p><span>The resulting list was then distributed to the team leaders at each site. In consultation with their colleagues, the team leaders classified each behaviour according to its occurrence or absence in the chimpanzee community being studied. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ab1aac6c-421d-4ca6-be61-ed660f9954e8\">The key categories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> were customary, habitual, present, absent and unknown. A behaviour was classified as customary if it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c0f2a1c3-615c-4666-8543-ac64248fab7d\">observed in most or all<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> able-bodied members of at least one age or sex class, such as all adult males; habitual if it was less common than customary but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c0f2a1c3-615c-4666-8543-ac64248fab7d\">occurred repeatedly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in several individuals; present if it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c0f2a1c3-615c-4666-8543-ac64248fab7d\">had been observed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> at the site but was not habitual; and absent if it had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c0f2a1c3-615c-4666-8543-ac64248fab7d\">never been observed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> at the site.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has eleven paragraphs, A–K.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–K, in boxes 14–18 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326452\" id=\"question-wrapper-326452\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3aa7bf81-821c-4ac9-aa3c-4e9fcbcae77a\">one commercial activity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"02c00c0c-b445-47a9-b98a-a69cc9230791\">made it easier for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the meat of wild animals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"02c00c0c-b445-47a9-b98a-a69cc9230791\">to reach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"32fb12c1-cf06-4157-b866-59e98d526f4c\">distant markets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326453\" id=\"question-wrapper-326453\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"aa885893-ca24-4e73-b03f-c24a111581a7\">the single source of evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> on which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"34fa3aa1-3aeb-4012-8748-c8e739e661a2\">most earlier studies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of chimpanzee culture <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"739ce162-ffbc-406b-bc10-59e74bc20b78\">depended<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326454\" id=\"question-wrapper-326454\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"f0b28ced-87be-473c-b3e5-f1e0f2d69240\">a practical skill<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"0e0dcf9a-edd4-4e5c-b386-2a37f388b560\">found in only one region<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ad06d278-c0c7-48d8-9d16-121b0bc4006c\">biologists see as evidence of culture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326455\" id=\"question-wrapper-326455\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ab1aac6c-421d-4ca6-be61-ed660f9954e8\">the labels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> showing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"c0f2a1c3-615c-4666-8543-ac64248fab7d\">how widely a possible tradition was seen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in one group</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">K</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326456\" id=\"question-wrapper-326456\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an example of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"53e7632e-f8e5-48d6-bda9-ff0e87fa0c16\">a shift in a person's perception<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> after <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c9648011-de95-4fbb-a4a0-f8ec8c6f1e3b\">seeing what chimpanzees can do<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? In boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326457\" id=\"question-wrapper-326457\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"91c48fbc-9018-4224-ac78-9445fbde08d6\">Chimpanzee cultural traditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"7ad61bc6-3c5f-411a-8379-32abb8bdf8f5\">just as </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"7ad61bc6-3c5f-411a-8379-32abb8bdf8f5 91c48fbc-9018-4224-ac78-9445fbde08d6\">sophisticated</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"7ad61bc6-3c5f-411a-8379-32abb8bdf8f5\"> as those of humans</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326458\" id=\"question-wrapper-326458\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"db9f575c-c32a-4f52-ae97-2370f64de3c9\">The collaborative study, which lasted two years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"3da34950-d181-4453-aa5b-4f7c418bb0cd\">covered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"3f7e85f9-f56b-4504-8719-7941fe5d8322\">the ways chimpanzees communicate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326459\" id=\"question-wrapper-326459\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"fbf4deef-bb67-4e60-b2f2-3e05519b4016\">the two Tanzanian sites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"b772de68-5590-4b81-807f-dda32e87508c\">the better-known one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> was also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"2b1630a7-b62c-40f3-b05b-b3fa62eb4a29\">set up earlier<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326460\" id=\"question-wrapper-326460\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A behaviour <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"2a225f16-3a4f-40a4-8110-c6436b836122\">qualifies as cultural<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> if it is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"19cfdb22-faa0-48d3-8f03-a50921a78472\">encoded in genes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> rather than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"794f9ed2-eac2-4841-8308-87dd7b9bdcf4\">acquired socially<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326461\" id=\"question-wrapper-326461\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"1cfc29f1-54dd-4379-b27c-615c902b51be\">Earlier reports<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"620a8f89-42c3-4823-b745-2479d27c71ea\">gave too little detail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> because of word limits imposed by academic journals.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Answer the questions below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326462\" id=\"question-wrapper-326462\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In which decade did scientists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"d0c53f0d-18f4-4435-9500-7b961c74b352\">first begin to gain real knowledge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"0240a547-e8bc-42df-8017-165637aabbff\">how chimpanzees behave<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"7f79ad0c-5db8-4f09-8b1f-06e200fd4235\">in their natural habitat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(IN THE) 1960S [OR] THE 1960S</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326463\" id=\"question-wrapper-326463\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"6128cc09-a8ae-4d74-bac7-7d211b75ffe9\">gradually became familiar to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> the chimpanzees at the first two sites as researchers made <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"7ae19674-8173-42cc-be2f-dce960ba5f2a\">important discoveries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(CLOSE) OBSERVATION</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326464\" id=\"question-wrapper-326464\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What did Goodall believe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"633b2da5-a861-4121-a82c-cfa98ab23087\">accounted for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> some of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"7ca8b7a1-df7a-4c19-92cd-03b5379bf74c\">behavioural differences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> she noted in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"b1b6ce33-74ae-48f5-ab6a-97df1abdc985\">the early 1970s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CULTURAL ORIGIN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f0b28ced-87be-473c-b3e5-f1e0f2d69240","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"a practical skill","passagePhrase":"the nut-cracking behaviour"},{"uid":"0e0dcf9a-edd4-4e5c-b386-2a37f388b560","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"found in only one region","passagePhrase":"found only in that particular part of Africa"},{"uid":"ad06d278-c0c7-48d8-9d16-121b0bc4006c","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"biologists see as evidence of culture","passagePhrase":"biologists regard as an expression of chimpanzee culture"},{"uid":"91c48fbc-9018-4224-ac78-9445fbde08d6","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Chimpanzee cultural traditions","passagePhrase":"the rich and varied cultural traditions found among chimpanzees ... complexity"},{"uid":"db9f575c-c32a-4f52-ae97-2370f64de3c9","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"The collaborative study, which lasted two years","passagePhrase":"Over a two-year period, an unprecedented scientific collaboration"},{"uid":"3da34950-d181-4453-aa5b-4f7c418bb0cd","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"covered","passagePhrase":"documented"},{"uid":"3f7e85f9-f56b-4504-8719-7941fe5d8322","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the ways chimpanzees communicate","passagePhrase":"forms of communication"},{"uid":"d0c53f0d-18f4-4435-9500-7b961c74b352","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"first begin to gain real knowledge","passagePhrase":"until systematic field studies began ... very little was known"},{"uid":"0240a547-e8bc-42df-8017-165637aabbff","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"how chimpanzees behave","passagePhrase":"chimpanzee behaviour"},{"uid":"7f79ad0c-5db8-4f09-8b1f-06e200fd4235","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"in their natural habitat","passagePhrase":"in the wild"},{"uid":"fbf4deef-bb67-4e60-b2f2-3e05519b4016","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"the two Tanzanian sites","passagePhrase":"two field sites in Tanzania"},{"uid":"2b1630a7-b62c-40f3-b05b-b3fa62eb4a29","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"set up earlier","passagePhrase":"the first of its kind"},{"uid":"b772de68-5590-4b81-807f-dda32e87508c","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"the better-known one","passagePhrase":"more famous"},{"uid":"6128cc09-a8ae-4d74-bac7-7d211b75ffe9","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"gradually became familiar to","passagePhrase":"became accustomed to"},{"uid":"7ae19674-8173-42cc-be2f-dce960ba5f2a","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"important discoveries","passagePhrase":"remarkable findings began to emerge"},{"uid":"b1b6ce33-74ae-48f5-ab6a-97df1abdc985","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"the early 1970s","passagePhrase":"As early as 1973"},{"uid":"7ca8b7a1-df7a-4c19-92cd-03b5379bf74c","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"behavioural differences","passagePhrase":"variations"},{"uid":"633b2da5-a861-4121-a82c-cfa98ab23087","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"accounted for","passagePhrase":"had"},{"uid":"794f9ed2-eac2-4841-8308-87dd7b9bdcf4","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"acquired socially","passagePhrase":"through learning ... learned by observing skills already practised by others"},{"uid":"2a225f16-3a4f-40a4-8110-c6436b836122","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"qualifies as cultural","passagePhrase":"the fundamental criterion for a cultural trait"},{"uid":"3aa7bf81-821c-4ac9-aa3c-4e9fcbcae77a","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"one commercial activity","passagePhrase":"logging"},{"uid":"02c00c0c-b445-47a9-b98a-a69cc9230791","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"made it easier for ... to reach","passagePhrase":"roads being built ... used to transport"},{"uid":"32fb12c1-cf06-4157-b866-59e98d526f4c","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"distant markets","passagePhrase":"consumers as far away as Europe"},{"uid":"53e7632e-f8e5-48d6-bda9-ff0e87fa0c16","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"a shift in a person's perception","passagePhrase":"altered the attitudes of some local people ... I can no longer eat him"},{"uid":"c9648011-de95-4fbb-a4a0-f8ec8c6f1e3b","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"seeing what chimpanzees can do","passagePhrase":"videotapes illustrating the cognitive abilities of chimpanzees"},{"uid":"34fa3aa1-3aeb-4012-8748-c8e739e661a2","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"most earlier studies","passagePhrase":"Most previous attempts"},{"uid":"739ce162-ffbc-406b-bc10-59e74bc20b78 aa885893-ca24-4e73-b03f-c24a111581a7","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"relied"},{"uid":"aa885893-ca24-4e73-b03f-c24a111581a7","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the single source of evidence","passagePhrase":"solely on published reports"},{"uid":"1cfc29f1-54dd-4379-b27c-615c902b51be","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Earlier reports","passagePhrase":"researchers’ descriptions"},{"uid":"620a8f89-42c3-4823-b745-2479d27c71ea","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"gave too little detail","passagePhrase":"lacked sufficient detail"},{"uid":"ab1aac6c-421d-4ca6-be61-ed660f9954e8","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"the labels","passagePhrase":"The key categories"},{"uid":"c0f2a1c3-615c-4666-8543-ac64248fab7d","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"how widely a possible tradition was seen","passagePhrase":"observed in most or all ... occurred repeatedly ... had been observed ... never been observed"},{"uid":"739ce162-ffbc-406b-bc10-59e74bc20b78","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"depended","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"7ad61bc6-3c5f-411a-8379-32abb8bdf8f5 91c48fbc-9018-4224-ac78-9445fbde08d6","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"sophisticated","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_117":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><b><span>Personality and appearance</span></b></p><p><span>When Charles Darwin applied to serve as a gentleman companion to Robert Fitzroy, the Beagle’s captain, who was seeking an “energetic young man”, he was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cd369bc6-cb4d-4806-b0b7-5403fd463a1c\">nearly rejected because of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> a supposed shortcoming that was as plain as the nose on his face. Fitzroy believed in physiognomy—the idea that a person’s character can be inferred from their appearance. As Darwin’s daughter Henrietta later recalled, Fitzroy had “made up his mind that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cd369bc6-cb4d-4806-b0b7-5403fd463a1c\">no man with such a nose could have energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>”. This judgment was far from accurate. Fortunately, the rest of Darwin’s visage compensated for his sluggardly proboscis: “His brow saved him.”</span></p><p><span>The idea that a person’s character can be glimpsed in their face dates back to the ancient Greeks. It was most notably popularised in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"020911f1-6ff0-4238-8165-416086029137\">the late 18th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> by the Swiss poet Johann Lavater, whose ideas became a talking point in intellectual circles. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"001a4313-0f9f-4388-87fa-1ecb54953f41\">By Darwin’s time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, such ideas were largely accepted without question. It was only after physiognomy became associated with phrenology, which fell into disrepute in the late 19th century, that physiognomy was dismissed as pseudoscience.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"41ae4b9d-f2d8-4450-b347-73e18dbfc4d1\">First impressions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> are highly influential, despite the well-worn admonition not to judge a book by its cover. Within a tenth of a second of seeing an unfamiliar face, we form a judgment about the person’s character—caring, trustworthy, aggressive, extroverted, competent, and so on. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"eb91aea4-859a-4b48-bda2-b644179eea34\">Once formed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"41ae4b9d-f2d8-4450-b347-73e18dbfc4d1\">that snap judgment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"54c5f014-b958-449e-a3e0-6dc76a514088\">surprisingly difficult to change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. People also act on these snap judgments. Politicians with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"10229259-ce9d-4783-8c00-153181fa9e8b\">competent-looking faces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"15452e02-c762-4995-a659-58c352b46bb3\">more likely to be elected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, and CEOs who look dominant are more likely to head profitable companies. There is also a well-established “attractiveness halo”. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"91e443d0-b5a0-43e1-a3c3-f75c36398431\">People seen as good-looking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> not only get the most valentines but are also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"4ce80504-25c9-4968-b453-a2af56902e3e\">judged to be more outgoing, socially competent, powerful, intelligent, and healthy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>In 1966, psychologists at the University of Michigan asked 84 undergraduates who had never met one another before to rate one another on five personality traits solely on the basis of appearance, while they sat for 15 minutes in silence. For three traits—extroversion, conscientiousness, and openness—their rapid judgments corresponded with actual personality scores significantly more often than would be expected by chance. In later research, Anthony Little of the University of Stirling and David Perrett of the University of St Andrews, both in the UK, re-examined the link between appearance and personality. They pointed out that the Michigan research was not tightly controlled for confounding factors. But when Little and Perrett re-ran the experiment using mugshots rather than live subjects, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"f5a3b5bd-f394-4650-8ce6-80ccdd136ecd\">also found a link between facial appearance and personality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>—though <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"a16242ec-0044-4db1-9588-e3fb3909bdff\">only for extroversion and conscientiousness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. They reported that the correlation appeared only at the extremes of personality.</span></p><p><span>Justin Carre and Cheryl McCormick of Brock University in Ontario, Canada, studied 90 ice hockey players. They found that a higher <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"e5b3059e-bc07-498f-8a79-df3e01a60726\">ratio of cheekbone-to-cheekbone distance to the distance between the brow and upper lip<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"fdf1094c-2e50-4a05-b43e-e5309809ea61\">significantly associated with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> the number of penalty minutes players received for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"a1d2c25a-076e-4f18-a164-5f18994c031f\">violent acts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, including slashing, elbowing, checking from behind and fighting. Findings such as these suggest that there may be a kernel of truth in facial judgments. However, this is not the only explanation for our readiness to make them. Leslie Zebrowitz, a psychologist at Brandeis University in Waltham, Massachusetts, says that in many cases snap judgments are not accurate. Such judgments, she says, are often an “overgeneralisation” of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"b83f1c5d-93da-4301-a6d3-97c63a2cf595\">more fundamental response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. A classic example of overgeneralisation is predators’ response to eye spots, the conspicuous circular markings found on some moths, butterflies and fish. These markings deter predators because they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f2daa880-8603-48d8-8d61-591cbfa1a0e3\">mimic the eyes of creatures that may be perceived as threatening<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Another researcher who leans towards overgeneralisation is Alexander Todorov. Together with Princeton colleague Nikolaas Oosterhof, he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"f607915f-845f-4400-be94-56f0e7cf639b\">put forward a theory to explain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"de200a34-ffa5-461d-9f88-4a6c37538c68\">snap judgments of faces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> in terms of how threatening they appear. Todorov and Oosterhof asked people for their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"de200a34-ffa5-461d-9f88-4a6c37538c68\">immediate reactions to pictures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of emotionally neutral faces, analysed the responses, and reduced them to two underlying factors: how trustworthy and how dominant each face appeared. They concluded that personality judgments based on faces are an overgeneralisation of an evolved ability to read emotions from facial expressions and, from them, infer a person’s intention and ability to cause harm. Todorov, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3113bfda-9564-4c5d-b24a-8b2f8a615839\">stresses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that overgeneralisation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"d400050a-f26b-41c8-a706-60e106f2859c\">does not rule out the idea that there is sometimes a kernel of truth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> in such personality assessments.</span></p><p><span>If there is a kernel of truth, then where does it come from? Perrett suspects that the link arises when our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5b4825d5-b1dd-4557-9a3c-4173a503e870\">prejudices about faces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> turn into self-fulfilling prophecies—an idea investigated by other researchers in 1977. Our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5b4825d5-b1dd-4557-9a3c-4173a503e870\">expectations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"45a2a6f8-b797-4271-a1e7-c165547c9592\">influence other people’s behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in ways that eventually confirm those expectations: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"45a2a6f8-b797-4271-a1e7-c165547c9592\">if someone is consistently treated as untrustworthy, they may eventually behave that way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Sometimes, however, the effect works in the opposite direction, particularly for people who look cute. The Nobel Prize-winning ethologist Konrad Lorenz once suggested that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"5b4cc5bb-9ed6-40b5-95e2-ee29a5b0fc1a\">baby-faced features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"7853711b-4385-4165-8734-53696b9ca771\">evoke a nurturing response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. Related work by Zebrowitz found that the sight of baby-faced boys and men stimulates the amygdala, an emotional centre of the brain. However, there is a twist. Baby-faced men are, on average, better educated and more assertive, and tend to win more military medals than their mature-looking counterparts. They are also more likely to be criminals; Al Capone is one example. Similarly, Zebrowitz found baby-faced boys to be quarrelsome and hostile, and more likely to be high academic achievers. She calls this the “self-defeating prophecy effect”: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"41a306a4-a6bc-479b-acf5-74058fdbc099\">a man with a baby face<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"5263cbaf-ef74-462a-964e-9a69e7957ae7\">strives to defy expectations and ends up overcompensating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>There is another theory that recalls the old parental warning not to pull faces because they might freeze that way. According to this theory, our personality moulds <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"922272b0-3ca7-423f-9043-394896cc00a8\">the way our faces look<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Support for this theory comes from an earlier study which found that older people described as angry tended to look cross even when asked to adopt a neutral expression. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"5d8b59e5-cc8e-44f3-891a-6d7ae810c3a2\">A lifetime of scowling, grumpiness and grimaces seemed to have left its mark<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes </span><b><span>27–31</span></b><span> on your answer sheet, write:</span></p><p><b><span>YES</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NO</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326465\" id=\"question-wrapper-326465\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Darwin’s nose was the main feature that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cd369bc6-cb4d-4806-b0b7-5403fd463a1c\">convinced Fitzroy of his suitability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> for the position.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326466\" id=\"question-wrapper-326466\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The principles of physiognomy remained essentially unchanged between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"020911f1-6ff0-4238-8165-416086029137\">Lavater’s time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"001a4313-0f9f-4388-87fa-1ecb54953f41\">Darwin’s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326467\" id=\"question-wrapper-326467\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People generally find it <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"54c5f014-b958-449e-a3e0-6dc76a514088\">easy to revise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"41ae4b9d-f2d8-4450-b347-73e18dbfc4d1\">an initial judgment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"eb91aea4-859a-4b48-bda2-b644179eea34\">after forming it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326468\" id=\"question-wrapper-326468\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A politician’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"10229259-ce9d-4783-8c00-153181fa9e8b\">perceived competence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"15452e02-c762-4995-a659-58c352b46bb3\">influence electoral success<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> even when that perception is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"10229259-ce9d-4783-8c00-153181fa9e8b\">based solely on facial appearance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326469\" id=\"question-wrapper-326469\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It is unfair that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"91e443d0-b5a0-43e1-a3c3-f75c36398431\">attractive people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> are often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"4ce80504-25c9-4968-b453-a2af56902e3e\">given favourable assumptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter in boxes 32–36 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326470\" id=\"question-wrapper-326470\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is true about Anthony Little and David Perrett’s experiment?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It assumed that none of the Michigan findings was accurate.</li> <li>B. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"f5a3b5bd-f394-4650-8ce6-80ccdd136ecd\">confirmed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"a16242ec-0044-4db1-9588-e3fb3909bdff\">some of the Michigan findings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</li> <li>C. It reproduced the conditions of the Michigan experiment.</li> <li>D. It used a wider variety of faces than the Michigan experiment.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326471\" id=\"question-wrapper-326471\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What conclusion could be drawn from Carre and McCormick's results?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"e5b3059e-bc07-498f-8a79-df3e01a60726\">Certain facial proportions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"fdf1094c-2e50-4a05-b43e-e5309809ea61\">linked to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"a1d2c25a-076e-4f18-a164-5f18994c031f\">violent behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Facial structure determines players' disciplinary records.</li> <li>C. Referees penalise players with wider faces more heavily.</li> <li>D. Different facial shapes lead to different forms of violence.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326472\" id=\"question-wrapper-326472\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What point is illustrated by the writer's reference to eye spots?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Animals can usually spot danger quickly.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"b83f1c5d-93da-4301-a6d3-97c63a2cf595\">Basic reactions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f2daa880-8603-48d8-8d61-591cbfa1a0e3\">triggered when no real threat exists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Animals can learn to recognise threats through experience.</li> <li>D. Predators differ in how they respond to threatening signals.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326473\" id=\"question-wrapper-326473\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What was the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"f607915f-845f-4400-be94-56f0e7cf639b\">aim of Todorov and Oosterhof’s research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. To identify the facial features that signal a person’s potential for harm</li> <li>B. To determine whether facial appearance accurately reflects personality</li> <li>C. To investigate the basis of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"de200a34-ffa5-461d-9f88-4a6c37538c68\">immediate personality judgments made from faces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></li> <li>D. To examine how accurately people can identify emotions from neutral faces</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326474\" id=\"question-wrapper-326474\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does Todorov <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3113bfda-9564-4c5d-b24a-8b2f8a615839\">emphasise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> about overgeneralisation in facial judgements?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It applies only to judgements of trustworthiness.</li> <li>B. It conflicts with the idea of self-fulfilling prophecies.</li> <li>C. It shows that facial judgements have no evolutionary basis.</li> <li>D. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"d400050a-f26b-41c8-a706-60e106f2859c\">leaves room for some judgements to be accurate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A–F, below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Endings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. judge other people by their expressions.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. tend to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"7853711b-4385-4165-8734-53696b9ca771\">trigger protective instincts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> in those who see them.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. are more likely than most to break the law.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"45a2a6f8-b797-4271-a1e7-c165547c9592\">partly influence how reliable certain individuals become<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. may come to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"5d8b59e5-cc8e-44f3-891a-6d7ae810c3a2\">reflect a person’s habitual emotional responses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"5263cbaf-ef74-462a-964e-9a69e7957ae7\">compensate for the impressions their appearance creates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326475\" id=\"question-wrapper-326475\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Perrett suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5b4825d5-b1dd-4557-9a3c-4173a503e870\">social perceptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326476\" id=\"question-wrapper-326476\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Lorenz argued that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"5b4cc5bb-9ed6-40b5-95e2-ee29a5b0fc1a\">youthful facial characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326477\" id=\"question-wrapper-326477\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Zebrowitz describes a tendency for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"41a306a4-a6bc-479b-acf5-74058fdbc099\">men with youthful features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326478\" id=\"question-wrapper-326478\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer describes a theory that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"922272b0-3ca7-423f-9043-394896cc00a8\">facial features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"020911f1-6ff0-4238-8165-416086029137","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Lavater’s time","passagePhrase":"the late 18th century"},{"uid":"001a4313-0f9f-4388-87fa-1ecb54953f41","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Darwin’s","passagePhrase":"By Darwin’s time"},{"uid":"41ae4b9d-f2d8-4450-b347-73e18dbfc4d1","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"an initial judgment","passagePhrase":"First impressions ... that snap judgment"},{"uid":"eb91aea4-859a-4b48-bda2-b644179eea34","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"after forming it","passagePhrase":"Once formed"},{"uid":"10229259-ce9d-4783-8c00-153181fa9e8b","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"perceived competence ... based solely on facial appearance","passagePhrase":"competent-looking faces"},{"uid":"15452e02-c762-4995-a659-58c352b46bb3","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"influence electoral success","passagePhrase":"more likely to be elected"},{"uid":"91e443d0-b5a0-43e1-a3c3-f75c36398431","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"attractive people","passagePhrase":"People seen as good-looking"},{"uid":"4ce80504-25c9-4968-b453-a2af56902e3e","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"given favourable assumptions","passagePhrase":"judged to be more outgoing, socially competent, powerful, intelligent, and healthy"},{"uid":"f5a3b5bd-f394-4650-8ce6-80ccdd136ecd","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"confirmed","passagePhrase":"also found a link between facial appearance and personality"},{"uid":"a16242ec-0044-4db1-9588-e3fb3909bdff","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"some of the Michigan findings","passagePhrase":"only for extroversion and conscientiousness"},{"uid":"e5b3059e-bc07-498f-8a79-df3e01a60726","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Certain facial proportions","passagePhrase":"ratio of cheekbone-to-cheekbone distance to the distance between the brow and upper lip"},{"uid":"fdf1094c-2e50-4a05-b43e-e5309809ea61","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"linked to","passagePhrase":"significantly associated with"},{"uid":"a1d2c25a-076e-4f18-a164-5f18994c031f","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"violent behaviour","passagePhrase":"violent acts"},{"uid":"b83f1c5d-93da-4301-a6d3-97c63a2cf595","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Basic reactions","passagePhrase":"more fundamental response"},{"uid":"f2daa880-8603-48d8-8d61-591cbfa1a0e3","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"triggered when no real threat exists","passagePhrase":"mimic the eyes of creatures that may be perceived as threatening"},{"uid":"f607915f-845f-4400-be94-56f0e7cf639b","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"aim of Todorov and Oosterhof’s research","passagePhrase":"put forward a theory to explain"},{"uid":"de200a34-ffa5-461d-9f88-4a6c37538c68","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"immediate personality judgments made from faces","passagePhrase":"snap judgments of faces ... immediate reactions to pictures"},{"uid":"3113bfda-9564-4c5d-b24a-8b2f8a615839","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"emphasise","passagePhrase":"stresses"},{"uid":"d400050a-f26b-41c8-a706-60e106f2859c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"leaves room for some judgements to be accurate","passagePhrase":"does not rule out the idea that there is sometimes a kernel of truth"},{"uid":"5b4825d5-b1dd-4557-9a3c-4173a503e870","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"social perceptions","passagePhrase":"prejudices about faces ... expectations"},{"uid":"45a2a6f8-b797-4271-a1e7-c165547c9592","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"partly influence how reliable certain individuals become","passagePhrase":"influence other people’s behaviour ... if someone is consistently treated as untrustworthy, they may eventually behave that way"},{"uid":"5b4cc5bb-9ed6-40b5-95e2-ee29a5b0fc1a","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"youthful facial characteristics","passagePhrase":"baby-faced features"},{"uid":"7853711b-4385-4165-8734-53696b9ca771","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"trigger protective instincts","passagePhrase":"evoke a nurturing response"},{"uid":"41a306a4-a6bc-479b-acf5-74058fdbc099","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"men with youthful features","passagePhrase":"a man with a baby face"},{"uid":"5263cbaf-ef74-462a-964e-9a69e7957ae7","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"compensate for the impressions their appearance creates","passagePhrase":"strives to defy expectations and ends up overcompensating"},{"uid":"922272b0-3ca7-423f-9043-394896cc00a8","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"facial features","passagePhrase":"the way our faces look"},{"uid":"5d8b59e5-cc8e-44f3-891a-6d7ae810c3a2","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"reflect a person’s habitual emotional responses","passagePhrase":"A lifetime of scowling, grumpiness and grimaces seemed to have left its mark"}]},"reading_u2_118":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1.</span></p><p><b><span>Reef Fish Study</span></b></p><p><i><span>Tom Holmes examines the relationship between size and survival in fish on Australia's Great Barrier Reef</span></i></p><p><span>It is widely believed among those who study animals that larger size confers some form of advantage throughout life. The possibility that certain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"106b4074-fef9-43f6-8780-2836e52a593e\">body characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> may influence an animal’s chances of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d798af9f-9b1a-47d5-b18e-d819fab18622\">surviving a predatory attack<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> has received considerable attention and has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"cbd1818b-9315-4fb7-8575-ee2404624ae0\">investigated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"9ab38762-10a4-4928-ae54-01e8e5fab634\">across a wide range of species and habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. Body size, weight, growth rate, overall condition, sensory development and escape speed have all been linked to survival. Of these, body size has received the most attention from researchers, leading to the development of several theories about how it may influence the predator–prey relationship. One of the most popular is known as the ‘bigger is better’ hypothesis. This theory predicts that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"abe7ce8d-38fd-455e-9cd4-87e592527322\">greater body size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> should improve an individual’s ability to escape from predators because it is associated with characteristics such as strength and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"5c942d5f-7b80-4231-9e65-be897dacc2aa\">visual development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Bigger is generally thought to be better, but this is not necessarily the case for every species or at every stage of life.</span></p><p><span>Compared with other habitats and ecosystems, relatively little is known <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"8e7b2e12-37d7-4265-a6f8-7e1f9f047fdb\">about predator–prey relationships within tropical reef communities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"8e7b2e12-37d7-4265-a6f8-7e1f9f047fdb\">What is known<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> is largely limited to predator identity and, to some extent, what these predators eat. Much less is understood about what drives these interactions or how body size influences their outcome. These questions have led our research team to Lizard Island, in the northern sector of the Great Barrier Reef. We want to examine predator–prey interactions around settlement, when tropical fish move from the larval phase into the early juvenile stage. We also want to determine whether predators choose prey according to characteristics such as the prey’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"cccafb78-8a4d-474d-a80d-4a3b97be5a9c\">size, weight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"37b178a8-f1aa-47c4-915a-b1176559dd87\">swimming speed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, all of which <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"7009c385-9c64-48a8-b34a-0446ff2455a0\">vary among individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"8a666c44-20bf-4d0b-95b3-67c556a46835\">at the beginning of the juvenile stage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"ce52506f-1062-4f5d-8812-5d165b6b2800\">coral reef fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> have a life cycle consisting of an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7b48b5ea-ea06-471e-a11c-4b620d4ef678\">open-ocean<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> larval <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a66ea43a-9fb4-4053-a9c1-c0d49def38c8\">phase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"75474d08-8ad4-4dfc-85f9-989dc5e620b4\">followed by juvenile and adult stages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"d04d1c2d-6379-4771-bc25-126deffbd65c\">near<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the reef. The transition from the larval to the juvenile stage involves rapid and dramatic physical changes and a sudden move from the open ocean to coral reef habitats. This transition is commonly known as ‘settlement’. Mortality is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"2d3fe799-63e7-4f65-a50b-cb3fc636428f\">particularly high<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> during <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9be6e242-ed77-458f-964f-012db176ecef\">the first 48 hours after settlement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, as individuals must adapt both to life on the reef and to a previously unknown set of predators.</span></p><p><span>However, studying predator–prey interactions around settlement is no easy task. On the northern Great Barrier Reef, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"0e7e6c13-d923-4ecb-b91b-6d15609ca16b\">coral reef fish settlement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> usually occurs <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"352aa04c-b29c-4639-88bf-2d9b2121a0f5\">within 2–3 days of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> a new moon <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"4d6c888d-9cf6-405a-a618-3e26aacc09ce\">during the warmer summer months<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. These short windows of opportunity, combined with the difficulties of working underwater, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"94229303-f665-4e4b-8115-0c7e5b6c2c7c\">transporting fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"7e4cc942-f692-4521-ab3d-ff1047641f6e\">acclimatising them to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> laboratory conditions, often make research a daunting task. These obstacles are overcome through a combination of innovative techniques, long working hours and sheer persistence. Immediately before settlement, we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c565d7b1-82b9-48c2-8286-78d200ac0898\">collect larval fish using purpose-built traps that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"04d134ed-fe37-4815-9788-a4a42b1924a9\">use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> artificial light to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c565d7b1-82b9-48c2-8286-78d200ac0898\">attract and retain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> only fish at this life stage. The larval fish, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"97033c79-4f1e-4aa8-bc71-f24871bb9995\">together with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> predatory fish, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"97033c79-4f1e-4aa8-bc71-f24871bb9995\">are then transported to an aquarium<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> before being used in a series of aquarium-based and field-based trials.</span></p><p><span>According to the ‘bigger is better’ hypothesis, individuals that are larger at settlement should have a greater chance of surviving predator attacks immediately afterwards. However, our initial research suggests that this is not always true. There may be several reasons for this.</span></p><p><span>Reef predator communities can differ considerably over relatively short distances. Species that are abundant in one location may be particularly rare in a similar habitat just 100 metres away. Just as predators differ in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"7c91f556-fd66-4da3-9dee-13e1d9e1bee2\">types<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> of prey they favour, they also differ in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"7c91f556-fd66-4da3-9dee-13e1d9e1bee2\">sizes of prey<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> they prefer. These <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"7c91f556-fd66-4da3-9dee-13e1d9e1bee2\">preferences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"7c91f556-fd66-4da3-9dee-13e1d9e1bee2\">are influenced by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> predators’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"06ecd688-5ebb-4d0d-a58d-a45d6b8f7df4\">physical characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"63714727-3d14-4602-b990-b3d42870f247\">such as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> mouth size, as well as by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"8df389b6-6463-4ca7-ae6d-585daf04a7f7\">behavioural differences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> between species. As a result, the predator community into which a reef fish settles may determine which individuals survive.</span></p><p><span>A further explanation for why larger individuals do not survive more often than smaller fish during this period may lie in an alternative hypothesis known as ‘optimal foraging theory’. According to this theory, being either very large or very small may reduce the likelihood of being selected as prey. Predators are expected to favour individuals that provide the greatest energy return. This generally involves a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"bcfc71d4-adc5-4538-b45d-d7793acfea86\">trade-off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"c0f1058d-f0e0-4498-b960-9f75bb7ecb58\">the energy gained from eating a fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a77ed13f-70c8-4a12-ab69-57b5e74c117b\">the amount of energy required to catch it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. Larger prey provide a higher energy return, but smaller prey generally require less energy to catch. This usually results in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"73dded25-9c48-424c-a5aa-499007a37f2f\">preference for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> medium-sized prey.</span></p><p><span>At the time of settlement, juvenile reef fish vary in the characteristics that can help them survive a predatory attack. However, these characteristics are not strongly associated with body size. For example, larger individuals are not necessarily faster, which means that they may be no harder to catch than smaller prey. If this is the case, the usual trade-off is altered and, according to optimal foraging theory, predators should prefer larger prey because of their greater energy return. Consequently, larger individuals may be targeted by some predators at the time of settlement. Our research aims to determine whether larger size may, in fact, be a distinct disadvantage during certain life stages.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes 1–4 on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326479\" id=\"question-wrapper-326479\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Scientists have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"cbd1818b-9315-4fb7-8575-ee2404624ae0\">examined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> the link between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"106b4074-fef9-43f6-8780-2836e52a593e\">physical features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d798af9f-9b1a-47d5-b18e-d819fab18622\">survival from predators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"9ab38762-10a4-4928-ae54-01e8e5fab634\">in only a few species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326480\" id=\"question-wrapper-326480\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the 'bigger is better' hypothesis, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"abe7ce8d-38fd-455e-9cd4-87e592527322\">larger animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"5c942d5f-7b80-4231-9e65-be897dacc2aa\">better eyesight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326481\" id=\"question-wrapper-326481\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"8a666c44-20bf-4d0b-95b3-67c556a46835\">When reef fish first become juveniles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"cccafb78-8a4d-474d-a80d-4a3b97be5a9c\">build<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"37b178a8-f1aa-47c4-915a-b1176559dd87\">swimming performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"7009c385-9c64-48a8-b34a-0446ff2455a0\">uniform across individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326482\" id=\"question-wrapper-326482\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>There is little scientific value in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"8e7b2e12-37d7-4265-a6f8-7e1f9f047fdb\">what has already been learned about reef predators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 5–7 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Life cycle of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"ce52506f-1062-4f5d-8812-5d165b6b2800\">fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> in the Lizard Island study</span></b></p><p><i><span>Phase 1: </span></i><span>(5)________</span><i><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"a66ea43a-9fb4-4053-a9c1-c0d49def38c8\">stage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></i></p><ul><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"75474d08-8ad4-4dfc-85f9-989dc5e620b4\">Before settlement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, fish <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7b48b5ea-ea06-471e-a11c-4b620d4ef678\">live in the open sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></li></ul><p><i><span>Phase 2: Juvenile stage</span></i></p><ul><li><span>fish <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"d04d1c2d-6379-4771-bc25-126deffbd65c\">remain close to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the (6)________ </span></li><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9be6e242-ed77-458f-964f-012db176ecef\">the early part of this stage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> is characterised by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"2d3fe799-63e7-4f65-a50b-cb3fc636428f\">increased levels of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> (7)________ </span></li></ul><p><i><span>Phase 3: Adult stage</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326483\" id=\"question-wrapper-326483\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LARVAL</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326484\" id=\"question-wrapper-326484\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">REEF</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326485\" id=\"question-wrapper-326485\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MORTALITY</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 8–13 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Lizard Island study</span></b></p><p><i><span>Practical difficulties</span></i></p><ul><li><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"4d6c888d-9cf6-405a-a618-3e26aacc09ce\">in summer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"0e7e6c13-d923-4ecb-b91b-6d15609ca16b\">larvae transform into juveniles and reach the reef<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"352aa04c-b29c-4639-88bf-2d9b2121a0f5\">shortly before or after<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> a (8)______</span></li><li><span>much of the research has to be carried out underwater</span></li><li><span>the team must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"94229303-f665-4e4b-8115-0c7e5b6c2c7c\">move the fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"7e4cc942-f692-4521-ab3d-ff1047641f6e\">help them adjust to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)______</span></li></ul><p><i><span>Method</span></i></p><ul><li><span>larval fish <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"c565d7b1-82b9-48c2-8286-78d200ac0898\">are drawn into a special trap<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"04d134ed-fe37-4815-9788-a4a42b1924a9\">with the aid of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)______</span></li><li><span>(11)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"97033c79-4f1e-4aa8-bc71-f24871bb9995\">are also taken to the aquarium<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> </span></li><li><span>both groups later undergo aquarium-based and field-based trials</span></li></ul><p><i><span>Why larger fish may not always survive better</span></i></p><ul><li><span>the number and type of predatory fish on the reef can vary from place to place</span></li><li><span>a predator's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"06ecd688-5ebb-4d0d-a58d-a45d6b8f7df4\">physical features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"63714727-3d14-4602-b990-b3d42870f247\">e.g<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. (12)____, and its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"8df389b6-6463-4ca7-ae6d-585daf04a7f7\">behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"7c91f556-fd66-4da3-9dee-13e1d9e1bee2\">affect which prey it tends to eat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span></span></li><li><span>predators generally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"73dded25-9c48-424c-a5aa-499007a37f2f\">opt for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> prey that are (13)______ as a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"bcfc71d4-adc5-4538-b45d-d7793acfea86\">compromise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"c0f1058d-f0e0-4498-b960-9f75bb7ecb58\">the food value of a catch<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a77ed13f-70c8-4a12-ab69-57b5e74c117b\">the effort involved in making it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></span></li><li><span>however, during settlement, larger juveniles are not necessarily faster than smaller ones, making them an attractive option</span></li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326486\" id=\"question-wrapper-326486\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NEW MOON</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326487\" id=\"question-wrapper-326487\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LABORATORY CONDITIONS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326488\" id=\"question-wrapper-326488\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(ARTIFICIAL) LIGHT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326489\" id=\"question-wrapper-326489\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PREDATORY FISH [OR] PREDATORS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326490\" id=\"question-wrapper-326490\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MOUTH SIZE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326491\" id=\"question-wrapper-326491\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MEDIUM-SIZED</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"106b4074-fef9-43f6-8780-2836e52a593e","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"physical features","passagePhrase":"body characteristics"},{"uid":"d798af9f-9b1a-47d5-b18e-d819fab18622","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"survival from predators","passagePhrase":"surviving a predatory attack"},{"uid":"cbd1818b-9315-4fb7-8575-ee2404624ae0","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"examined","passagePhrase":"investigated"},{"uid":"abe7ce8d-38fd-455e-9cd4-87e592527322","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"larger animals","passagePhrase":"greater body size"},{"uid":"5c942d5f-7b80-4231-9e65-be897dacc2aa","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"better eyesight","passagePhrase":"visual development"},{"uid":"8e7b2e12-37d7-4265-a6f8-7e1f9f047fdb","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"what has already been learned about reef predators","passagePhrase":"about predator–prey relationships within tropical reef communities ... What is known"},{"uid":"cccafb78-8a4d-474d-a80d-4a3b97be5a9c","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"build","passagePhrase":"size, weight"},{"uid":"37b178a8-f1aa-47c4-915a-b1176559dd87","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"swimming performance","passagePhrase":"swimming speed"},{"uid":"8a666c44-20bf-4d0b-95b3-67c556a46835","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"When reef fish first become juveniles","passagePhrase":"at the beginning of the juvenile stage"},{"uid":"ce52506f-1062-4f5d-8812-5d165b6b2800","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"fish","passagePhrase":"coral reef fish"},{"uid":"7b48b5ea-ea06-471e-a11c-4b620d4ef678","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"live in the open sea","passagePhrase":"open-ocean"},{"uid":"a66ea43a-9fb4-4053-a9c1-c0d49def38c8","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"stage","passagePhrase":"phase"},{"uid":"75474d08-8ad4-4dfc-85f9-989dc5e620b4","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Before settlement","passagePhrase":"followed by juvenile and adult stages"},{"uid":"d04d1c2d-6379-4771-bc25-126deffbd65c","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"remain close to","passagePhrase":"near"},{"uid":"2d3fe799-63e7-4f65-a50b-cb3fc636428f","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"increased levels of","passagePhrase":"particularly high"},{"uid":"9be6e242-ed77-458f-964f-012db176ecef","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"the early part of this stage","passagePhrase":"the first 48 hours after settlement"},{"uid":"0e7e6c13-d923-4ecb-b91b-6d15609ca16b","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"larvae transform into juveniles and reach the reef","passagePhrase":"coral reef fish settlement"},{"uid":"352aa04c-b29c-4639-88bf-2d9b2121a0f5","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"shortly before or after","passagePhrase":"within 2–3 days of"},{"uid":"4d6c888d-9cf6-405a-a618-3e26aacc09ce","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"in summer","passagePhrase":"during the warmer summer months"},{"uid":"94229303-f665-4e4b-8115-0c7e5b6c2c7c","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"move the fish","passagePhrase":"transporting fish"},{"uid":"7e4cc942-f692-4521-ab3d-ff1047641f6e","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"help them adjust to","passagePhrase":"acclimatising them to"},{"uid":"c565d7b1-82b9-48c2-8286-78d200ac0898","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"are drawn into a special trap","passagePhrase":"collect larval fish using purpose-built traps that ... attract and retain"},{"uid":"04d134ed-fe37-4815-9788-a4a42b1924a9","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"with the aid of","passagePhrase":"use"},{"uid":"97033c79-4f1e-4aa8-bc71-f24871bb9995","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"are also taken to the aquarium","passagePhrase":"together with ... are then transported to an aquarium"},{"uid":"7c91f556-fd66-4da3-9dee-13e1d9e1bee2","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"affect which prey it tends to eat","passagePhrase":"types ... sizes of prey ... preferences ... are influenced by"},{"uid":"06ecd688-5ebb-4d0d-a58d-a45d6b8f7df4","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"physical features","passagePhrase":"physical characteristics"},{"uid":"63714727-3d14-4602-b990-b3d42870f247","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"e.g","passagePhrase":"such as"},{"uid":"8df389b6-6463-4ca7-ae6d-585daf04a7f7","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"behaviour","passagePhrase":"behavioural differences"},{"uid":"bcfc71d4-adc5-4538-b45d-d7793acfea86","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"compromise","passagePhrase":"trade-off"},{"uid":"c0f1058d-f0e0-4498-b960-9f75bb7ecb58","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"the food value of a catch","passagePhrase":"the energy gained from eating a fish"},{"uid":"a77ed13f-70c8-4a12-ab69-57b5e74c117b","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"the effort involved in making it","passagePhrase":"the amount of energy required to catch it"},{"uid":"73dded25-9c48-424c-a5aa-499007a37f2f","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"opt for","passagePhrase":"preference for"}]},"reading_u2_119":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2.</span></p><p><b><span>Are Artists Liars?</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><span>Shortly before his death, Marlon Brando was working on a series of instructional videos about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"de56b76d-ec5f-4cca-8cea-fa80d1e486f3\">acting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, to be called “Lying for a Living”. In the surviving footage, Brando can be seen dispensing gnomic advice on his craft to a group of enthusiastic, if somewhat bemused, Hollywood stars, including Leonardo DiCaprio and Sean Penn. Brando also recruited people at random from the streets of Los Angeles and persuaded them to improvise; the footage is said to include a memorable scene featuring two dwarves and a giant Samoan. “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"aeec9946-c100-4dde-b4c7-6853d7189670\">If you can lie, you can act<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>,” Brando told Jod Kaftan, a writer for Rolling Stone and one of the few people to have viewed the footage. “Are you good at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"45adb977-3230-46b3-a957-776b38098725\">lying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>?” asked Kaftan. “Jesus,” said Brando, “I’m fabulous at it.”</span></p><p><b><span>B</span></b><span>. </span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><span>Brando was not the first person to note that the line between an artist and a liar is a fine one. If art is a kind of lying, then lying is a form of art, albeit of a lower order—as Oscar Wilde and Mark Twain have observed. Indeed, lying and artistic storytelling spring from a common neurological root—one revealed in the cases of psychiatric patients who suffer from a particular kind of impairment. Both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"2d5a2544-210e-4e2a-ad40-3f2c8862a1f4\">liars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and artists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1c64834f-b62e-4695-bc2a-d3e310c5c8e9\">refuse to accept the tyranny of reality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Both carefully craft convincing stories—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"0dc35df5-17e6-49c8-8a7a-fb3acdf1ed65\">a skill requiring intellectual sophistication, emotional sensitivity and physical self-control<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. In this sense, liars are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3345d63f-e6bb-4c8e-946b-d9deb5c70790\">both<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> writers and performers of their own work. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3345d63f-e6bb-4c8e-946b-d9deb5c70790\">Such parallels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> are hardly coincidental.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><span>A case study published in 1985 by neurologist Antonio Damasio describes a middle-aged woman whose brain had been damaged by a series of strokes. Although she retained abilities such as coherent speech, what she said was often unpredictable. In psychiatric terms, she was “confabulating”. Chronic confabulation is a rare <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"9caee57d-f1ae-4234-aca3-95f80805a678\">memory disorder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> defined as <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 20\" data-uid=\"23eb265b-ec0c-436c-b209-6094f8e20444 b156e4de-8f9a-4bab-af1e-704aa8788011\">the production of fabricated, distorted or misinterpreted memories</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 20\" data-uid=\"179134a0-e797-42b9-a12e-2f28f3c78bd1 6fabc4e1-9acf-41ca-931c-08548a228cc9\">without a conscious intention to deceive</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Whereas amnesiacs make errors of omission—leaving gaps they cannot fill—confabulators make errors of commission: they invent information. They are also usually unaware of their condition and may sincerely offer highly implausible explanations of their circumstances. One patient, for example, claimed that a teenage girl had shot him three times in the head during the Second World War, killing him, before surgery brought him back to life. Confabulators are not trying to deceive anyone. They engage in what neuropsychologist Morris Moscovitch calls “honest lying”. Faced with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"15fefb12-f472-4de5-b4c2-d57429680ca8\">uncertainty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"bca1fa18-d86e-4194-9e8b-73181d6d8ea7\">may experience a “compulsion to narrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>”: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"11c73023-f498-4818-b2af-330587e1810f\">a deep-seated need to shape, order and explain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"15fefb12-f472-4de5-b4c2-d57429680ca8\">what they do not understand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. They can also be highly inventive with language; one patient, asked what happened to Queen Marie Antoinette, replied that she had been “suicided” by her family. In this respect, confabulators can resemble novelists in their ability to turn almost anything into material. Unlike writers, however, they have little or no control over what they produce.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><span>The wider significance of this condition lies in what it tells us about ourselves. Evidently, there is a gushing river of verbal creativity in the normal human mind, from which both artistic invention and lying are drawn. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"cc366314-a8f2-4a6a-8431-113e981fa872\">We are born storytellers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, spinning narrative out of our experience and imagination and straining against the leash that keeps us tethered to reality. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"f2bc2bfc-346b-47ad-8139-227f8cc06727\">This is a wonderful thing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>; it gives us the ability to conceive of alternative futures and different worlds. It also helps us to understand our own lives through the entertaining stories of others. But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"a2e1223e-7f58-42ad-847f-ea7567f67f26\">it can lead us into trouble<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, particularly when we try to persuade others that our inventions are real. Most of the time, as our stories bubble up to consciousness, we exercise our cerebral censors, controlling which stories we tell and to whom. Yet people lie for all sorts of reasons, including the fact that making things up can be dangerously fun.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><span>During a high-profile libel case in 1996, Jonathan Aitken, a former cabinet minister, challenged claims made by the </span><i><span>Guardian</span></i><span> about his relationships with Saudi arms dealers, including meetings he allegedly held with them during a trip to Paris. During the case, Aitken also recounted a story to illustrate the difficulties he had endured after the newspaper damaged his reputation. He claimed that after journalists confronted him outside his home, he drove away with his daughter and was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e3715308-d526-478c-a2ef-5fd9c2ec18b5\">pursued<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"c063718b-63db-4786-ad21-677c95f644e4\">through central London<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> by reporters in a van. What amazed many in hindsight was <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 25\" data-uid=\"6a32b4ff-fc6f-4dff-83fe-809d86a2e703 a6f931bf-8ef0-4897-ad64-65fce6767522\">the sheer superfluity of the lies</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"a6f931bf-8ef0-4897-ad64-65fce6767522\"> Aitken told</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> during his testimony. Some were needed to sustain his original story, but others seemed to be told simply for the pleasure of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"589c023e-423d-45e5-83be-83c9ee4b4cb8\">invention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. His <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"22fc3c80-ae76-4487-a589-6e3d1391ed9a\">charm, fluency<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and flair for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"cfa2f37a-446c-411f-a3e5-607e2f039721\">theatrical displays of sincerity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> made it appear that he might win the case. However, a documentary crew <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ef4f2be8-6d5d-4e62-9809-80fb11929add\">later<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> produced <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 26\" data-uid=\"0a7ba71a-b094-4d4d-a10c-f43b5139cd93 8f4de6c6-e8b7-4775-8574-b9e0a70dc48e\">unedited</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0a7ba71a-b094-4d4d-a10c-f43b5139cd93\"> footage </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 26\" data-uid=\"0a7ba71a-b094-4d4d-a10c-f43b5139cd93 f7020ea5-9d57-4a6e-ac51-8f048cce1d13\">showing that</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f7020ea5-9d57-4a6e-ac51-8f048cce1d13\"> Aitken’s daughter </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 26\" data-uid=\"0a7ba71a-b094-4d4d-a10c-f43b5139cd93 f7020ea5-9d57-4a6e-ac51-8f048cce1d13\">had not been</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f7020ea5-9d57-4a6e-ac51-8f048cce1d13\"> with him</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> that day and that he had simply driven away, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f7020ea5-9d57-4a6e-ac51-8f048cce1d13\">with no vehicle in pursuit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. The case <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ef4f2be8-6d5d-4e62-9809-80fb11929add\">finally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> collapsed in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"57889372-45bf-43bb-88bd-81e802de4eda\">June 1997<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, when the defence found <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 26\" data-uid=\"0a7ba71a-b094-4d4d-a10c-f43b5139cd93 ce33c06a-5982-4a4d-a4c0-3732f279ce05\">indisputable evidence</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> concerning his Paris trip.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><span>Of course, unlike Aitken, actors, playwrights and novelists are not literally attempting to deceive us, because the convention is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"947dc02a-7dbb-4701-9bec-db9c272ce81b\">understood in advance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>: audiences enter a theatre or open a novel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"947dc02a-7dbb-4701-9bec-db9c272ce81b\">knowing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"f7dd77c4-6720-45ab-9e0d-94fa584bf51f\">what follows is invented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. Perhaps this is why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"f6117a83-5f32-4e16-a5b7-95a195b238ac\">art<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> was invented in the first place—as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"5c965694-2300-458b-b4c1-77a86b21257c\">a safe space into which our lies can be corralled and channelled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> into something socially useful. Given <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"b3ef410e-c10a-4689-8f79-e35ac61cada0\">the universal compulsion to tell stories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, art is the best way to refine and enjoy the particularly outlandish or insightful ones. But that is not the whole story. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"2a84a15e-510e-437b-94c2-cbb298c9db7f\">The key way in which<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"64bf2f69-02e8-4505-9da1-0f0a031782f2\">artistic “lies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>” <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"2a84a15e-510e-437b-94c2-cbb298c9db7f\">differ from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"a6809891-f00e-43c3-85a9-829ac5822921\">ordinary lies and from the “honest lying” of chronic confabulators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> is that they carry meaning and resonance beyond their creator. Liars lie on their own behalf; artists tell lies on behalf of everyone. If writers share a compulsion to narrate, they direct it towards finding insights into the human condition. Mario Vargas Llosa has written that novels “express a curious truth that can only be expressed in a furtive and veiled fashion, masquerading as what it is not.” Art is a lie whose secret ingredient is truth.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A–F.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"2a84a15e-510e-437b-94c2-cbb298c9db7f\">from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, i–viii, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>List of Headings </span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><b><span>i</span></b><span> The thrill some people get from fabricating events</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><b><span>ii</span></b><span> A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"9caee57d-f1ae-4234-aca3-95f80805a678\">memory condition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that prompts <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"179134a0-e797-42b9-a12e-2f28f3c78bd1\">involuntary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"23eb265b-ec0c-436c-b209-6094f8e20444\">invention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><b><span>iii</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"aeec9946-c100-4dde-b4c7-6853d7189670\">A proposed link between </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"aeec9946-c100-4dde-b4c7-6853d7189670 de56b76d-ec5f-4cca-8cea-fa80d1e486f3\">performance</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"aeec9946-c100-4dde-b4c7-6853d7189670\"> and </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"45adb977-3230-46b3-a957-776b38098725 aeec9946-c100-4dde-b4c7-6853d7189670\">deception</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><b><span>iv</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"2a84a15e-510e-437b-94c2-cbb298c9db7f\">What distinguishes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"64bf2f69-02e8-4505-9da1-0f0a031782f2\">creative fiction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"a6809891-f00e-43c3-85a9-829ac5822921\">other forms of untruth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><b><span>v</span></b><span> Why certain performers seem more credible than others</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><b><span>vi</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"f2bc2bfc-346b-47ad-8139-227f8cc06727\">The benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"a2e1223e-7f58-42ad-847f-ea7567f67f26\">risks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"cc366314-a8f2-4a6a-8431-113e981fa872\">a natural storytelling impulse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><b><span>vii</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3345d63f-e6bb-4c8e-946b-d9deb5c70790\">Shared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"1c64834f-b62e-4695-bc2a-d3e310c5c8e9\">attitudes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"0dc35df5-17e6-49c8-8a7a-fb3acdf1ed65\">abilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"3345d63f-e6bb-4c8e-946b-d9deb5c70790\">among<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> artists and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"2d5a2544-210e-4e2a-ad40-3f2c8862a1f4\">deceivers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><b><span>viii</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"a6f931bf-8ef0-4897-ad64-65fce6767522\">An elaborate false account<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ef4f2be8-6d5d-4e62-9809-80fb11929add\">ultimately<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0a7ba71a-b094-4d4d-a10c-f43b5139cd93\">disproved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326492\" id=\"question-wrapper-326492\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326493\" id=\"question-wrapper-326493\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326494\" id=\"question-wrapper-326494\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326495\" id=\"question-wrapper-326495\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">vi</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326496\" id=\"question-wrapper-326496\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">viii</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326497\" id=\"question-wrapper-326497\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paragraph F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">iv</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose TWO letters, A–E.</span></p><p><span>Which TWO of the following statements are true of people with chronic confabulation?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A. </span></b><span>Their memory errors mainly involve leaving gaps rather than adding invented details.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B. </span></b><span>They may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"b156e4de-8f9a-4bab-af1e-704aa8788011\">produce false accounts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"6fabc4e1-9acf-41ca-931c-08548a228cc9\">without consciously intending to mislead anyone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C. </span></b><span>They are usually aware that the explanations they give are unreliable.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D. </span></b><span>They may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"bca1fa18-d86e-4194-9e8b-73181d6d8ea7\">feel compelled to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"11c73023-f498-4818-b2af-330587e1810f\">impose an explanation on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"15fefb12-f472-4de5-b4c2-d57429680ca8\">situations they find confusing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E. </span></b><span>They can control the narratives they produce in much the same way as novelists can.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326498\" id=\"question-wrapper-326498\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326499\" id=\"question-wrapper-326499\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose TWO letters, A-E. Which TWO of the following statements about playwrights and novelists are true?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><b><span>A.</span></b><span> Their audiences <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"947dc02a-7dbb-4701-9bec-db9c272ce81b\">already know<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"f7dd77c4-6720-45ab-9e0d-94fa584bf51f\">the events presented are not factual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><b><span>B.</span></b><span> They create fictional accounts mainly to serve their own personal interests.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><b><span>C</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> Their inventions arise through mental processes different from those that produce ordinary lies.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><b><span>D.</span></b><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"f6117a83-5f32-4e16-a5b7-95a195b238ac\">Their work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> succeeds only when the public accepts invented events as factual.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><b><span>E</span></b><b><span>.</span></b><span> Their work gives people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"5c965694-2300-458b-b4c1-77a86b21257c\">a harmless outlet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"b3ef410e-c10a-4689-8f79-e35ac61cada0\">imaginative impulses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326500\" id=\"question-wrapper-326500\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326501\" id=\"question-wrapper-326501\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose</span><b><span> ONE WORD ONLY </span></b><span>from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Jonathan Aitken’s libel case</span></b></p><p><span>In a widely publicised 1996 libel case, Jonathan Aitken, who had served as a government minister, rejected a newspaper’s allegations concerning his connections with Saudi weapons dealers and meetings in the French capital. To illustrate the difficulties caused by the newspaper’s allegations, he claimed that reporters had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e3715308-d526-478c-a2ef-5fd9c2ec18b5\">chased<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> him and his (24) __________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"c063718b-63db-4786-ad21-677c95f644e4\">through the city centre<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Although his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"22fc3c80-ae76-4487-a589-6e3d1391ed9a\">polished manner<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"cfa2f37a-446c-411f-a3e5-607e2f039721\">dramatic displays of honesty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> initially strengthened his case, he told <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"6a32b4ff-fc6f-4dff-83fe-809d86a2e703\">numerous unnecessary falsehoods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, apparently out of sheer (25)______ in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"589c023e-423d-45e5-83be-83c9ee4b4cb8\">fabrication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. His account unravelled when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"8f4de6c6-e8b7-4775-8574-b9e0a70dc48e\">raw<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26)______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f7020ea5-9d57-4a6e-ac51-8f048cce1d13\">exposed his story as false<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"ce33c06a-5982-4a4d-a4c0-3732f279ce05\">conclusive evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> about the trip caused the case to collapse <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"57889372-45bf-43bb-88bd-81e802de4eda\">in the following year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326502\" id=\"question-wrapper-326502\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DAUGHTER</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326503\" id=\"question-wrapper-326503\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PLEASURE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326504\" id=\"question-wrapper-326504\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOOTAGE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"de56b76d-ec5f-4cca-8cea-fa80d1e486f3","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"acting"},{"uid":"aeec9946-c100-4dde-b4c7-6853d7189670","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"A proposed link between ... and","passagePhrase":"If you can lie, you can act"},{"uid":"45adb977-3230-46b3-a957-776b38098725","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"lying"},{"uid":"2d5a2544-210e-4e2a-ad40-3f2c8862a1f4","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"deceivers","passagePhrase":"liars"},{"uid":"1c64834f-b62e-4695-bc2a-d3e310c5c8e9","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"attitudes","passagePhrase":"refuse to accept the tyranny of reality"},{"uid":"0dc35df5-17e6-49c8-8a7a-fb3acdf1ed65","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"abilities","passagePhrase":"a skill requiring intellectual sophistication, emotional sensitivity and physical self-control"},{"uid":"3345d63f-e6bb-4c8e-946b-d9deb5c70790","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Shared ... among","passagePhrase":"both ... Such parallels"},{"uid":"9caee57d-f1ae-4234-aca3-95f80805a678","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"memory condition","passagePhrase":"memory disorder"},{"uid":"23eb265b-ec0c-436c-b209-6094f8e20444 b156e4de-8f9a-4bab-af1e-704aa8788011","qNum":"16 20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the production of fabricated, distorted or misinterpreted memories"},{"uid":"179134a0-e797-42b9-a12e-2f28f3c78bd1 6fabc4e1-9acf-41ca-931c-08548a228cc9","qNum":"16 20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"without a conscious intention to deceive"},{"uid":"15fefb12-f472-4de5-b4c2-d57429680ca8","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"situations they find confusing","passagePhrase":"uncertainty ... what they do not understand"},{"uid":"bca1fa18-d86e-4194-9e8b-73181d6d8ea7","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"feel compelled to","passagePhrase":"may experience a “compulsion to narrate"},{"uid":"11c73023-f498-4818-b2af-330587e1810f","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"impose an explanation on","passagePhrase":"a deep-seated need to shape, order and explain"},{"uid":"cc366314-a8f2-4a6a-8431-113e981fa872","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"a natural storytelling impulse","passagePhrase":"We are born storytellers"},{"uid":"f2bc2bfc-346b-47ad-8139-227f8cc06727","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"The benefits","passagePhrase":"This is a wonderful thing"},{"uid":"a2e1223e-7f58-42ad-847f-ea7567f67f26","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"risks","passagePhrase":"it can lead us into trouble"},{"uid":"e3715308-d526-478c-a2ef-5fd9c2ec18b5","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"chased","passagePhrase":"pursued"},{"uid":"c063718b-63db-4786-ad21-677c95f644e4","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"through the city centre","passagePhrase":"through central London"},{"uid":"6a32b4ff-fc6f-4dff-83fe-809d86a2e703 a6f931bf-8ef0-4897-ad64-65fce6767522","qNum":"18 25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the sheer superfluity of the lies"},{"uid":"a6f931bf-8ef0-4897-ad64-65fce6767522","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"An elaborate false account","passagePhrase":"Aitken told"},{"uid":"589c023e-423d-45e5-83be-83c9ee4b4cb8","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"fabrication","passagePhrase":"invention"},{"uid":"22fc3c80-ae76-4487-a589-6e3d1391ed9a","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"polished manner","passagePhrase":"charm, fluency"},{"uid":"cfa2f37a-446c-411f-a3e5-607e2f039721","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"dramatic displays of honesty","passagePhrase":"theatrical displays of sincerity"},{"uid":"ef4f2be8-6d5d-4e62-9809-80fb11929add","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"ultimately","passagePhrase":"later ... finally"},{"uid":"0a7ba71a-b094-4d4d-a10c-f43b5139cd93 8f4de6c6-e8b7-4775-8574-b9e0a70dc48e","qNum":"18 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"unedited"},{"uid":"0a7ba71a-b094-4d4d-a10c-f43b5139cd93","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"disproved","passagePhrase":"footage"},{"uid":"0a7ba71a-b094-4d4d-a10c-f43b5139cd93 f7020ea5-9d57-4a6e-ac51-8f048cce1d13","qNum":"18 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"showing that ... had not been"},{"uid":"f7020ea5-9d57-4a6e-ac51-8f048cce1d13","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"exposed his story as false","passagePhrase":"Aitken’s daughter ... with him ... with no vehicle in pursuit"},{"uid":"57889372-45bf-43bb-88bd-81e802de4eda","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"in the following year","passagePhrase":"June 1997"},{"uid":"0a7ba71a-b094-4d4d-a10c-f43b5139cd93 ce33c06a-5982-4a4d-a4c0-3732f279ce05","qNum":"18 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"indisputable evidence"},{"uid":"947dc02a-7dbb-4701-9bec-db9c272ce81b","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"already know","passagePhrase":"understood in advance ... knowing"},{"uid":"f7dd77c4-6720-45ab-9e0d-94fa584bf51f","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"the events presented are not factual","passagePhrase":"what follows is invented"},{"uid":"f6117a83-5f32-4e16-a5b7-95a195b238ac","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Their work","passagePhrase":"art"},{"uid":"5c965694-2300-458b-b4c1-77a86b21257c","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"a harmless outlet","passagePhrase":"a safe space into which our lies can be corralled and channelled"},{"uid":"b3ef410e-c10a-4689-8f79-e35ac61cada0","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"imaginative impulses","passagePhrase":"the universal compulsion to tell stories"},{"uid":"2a84a15e-510e-437b-94c2-cbb298c9db7f","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"from ... What distinguishes","passagePhrase":"The key way in which ... differ from"},{"uid":"64bf2f69-02e8-4505-9da1-0f0a031782f2","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"creative fiction","passagePhrase":"artistic “lies"},{"uid":"a6809891-f00e-43c3-85a9-829ac5822921","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"other forms of untruth","passagePhrase":"ordinary lies and from the “honest lying” of chronic confabulators"},{"uid":"179134a0-e797-42b9-a12e-2f28f3c78bd1","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"involuntary","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"23eb265b-ec0c-436c-b209-6094f8e20444","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"invention","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"aeec9946-c100-4dde-b4c7-6853d7189670 de56b76d-ec5f-4cca-8cea-fa80d1e486f3","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"performance","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"45adb977-3230-46b3-a957-776b38098725 aeec9946-c100-4dde-b4c7-6853d7189670","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"deception","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"b156e4de-8f9a-4bab-af1e-704aa8788011","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"produce false accounts","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"6fabc4e1-9acf-41ca-931c-08548a228cc9","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"without consciously intending to mislead anyone","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"6a32b4ff-fc6f-4dff-83fe-809d86a2e703","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"numerous unnecessary falsehoods","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"8f4de6c6-e8b7-4775-8574-b9e0a70dc48e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"raw","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"ce33c06a-5982-4a4d-a4c0-3732f279ce05","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"conclusive evidence","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_120":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"5ce18e1a-30ce-4787-bf95-8f5fbcc91a4a\">From ancient times to the present, historians have asked the same question<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>: how and why did an ordinary little town in central Italy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c5fc1e99-2ecc-433c-a411-f28271139d5b\">grow so much larger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> than any other in the ancient Mediterranean <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c5fc1e99-2ecc-433c-a411-f28271139d5b\">and come to control such a vast empire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>? During the first century BCE, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"c276e463-d3b2-4cc6-ab9b-5e4daa79bed9\">Roman writers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> themselves began to study systematically the earlier centuries of their city and empire. Yet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bf191e55-a367-48b7-a757-c57b69933046\">these historians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> had little more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"aa2df824-049f-4c5c-889d-fdec755641a8\">direct evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"767dc892-2285-4aa4-a9ee-38d5d5e25d18\">the earliest phases of Rome’s history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> than modern historians do. In some respects, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"c276e463-d3b2-4cc6-ab9b-5e4daa79bed9\">may even have had less<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, since no documents or archives from the earliest period had survived. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"0cb10a03-6448-41ac-a929-e293b316aaaa\">Their ‘histories’ of the foundation of ancient Rome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> tell us a good deal about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"0fa9c8cf-8d15-40eb-9839-874aa58c5c7b\">how the Romans viewed their city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> and about their values and failings. However, they <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"579d4e8d-675f-41bf-8fa4-2a9d561cea01\">tell us very little<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> about the subject they claim to describe: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"3d4be8e5-00f4-4ec6-86bc-aa0d0b17aa7b\">what earliest Rome was actually like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"c48192d0-a968-4077-9588-b60f9cf7908f\">One fact is clear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Rome <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"7a28a2bb-1227-45d7-bb4b-0b96878e7591\">was already a very old city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> by 63 BCE, when its first emperor was born. But how, then, can we obtain reliable information about the origins of Rome?</span></p><p><span>One approach is to look beyond the histories of Roman writers for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"8ee036b9-6b31-4dc7-8d5f-f627082a6b98\">clues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in the Latin language or in later Roman institutions <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"8ee036b9-6b31-4dc7-8d5f-f627082a6b98\">that may point back to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"143c21de-86b2-4bbf-9de0-7a1b429a1f47\">features of earliest Rome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Archaeological evidence, however, is much more tangible. Dig deep beneath Rome’s visible ancient monuments, and traces of a much earlier settlement—or settlements—survive. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"f4563cec-dc4d-4b74-a67e-764360aebcd0\">Beneath the Forum<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> itself, an ancient marketplace at the centre of the city, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"f4563cec-dc4d-4b74-a67e-764360aebcd0\">lie the remains of an early cemetery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, which caused tremendous excitement when first unearthed at the start of the 20th century. Cemeteries imply the existence of a community, and the faint outlines of huts found beneath several parts of the later city may represent traces of such a community. These include remains on the Palatine, the most central of Rome’s seven hills. We know little about the nature of these huts beyond the fact that they were constructed from wood, clay and thatch, and still less about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"99258a0d-6d49-46e3-ad2d-af90548537c3\">the way of life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> associated with them. But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"b50f56e2-3504-494c-873a-43b39f54ddf9\">some of these gaps can be filled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> by looking just outside Rome. One of the best-preserved and most carefully excavated <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33 39\" data-uid=\"928f5ba7-be1b-4c5b-8140-27896edcce6e e545ebc9-af74-48a0-a9d4-2b45702aa2bc\">early structures</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33 39\" data-uid=\"928f5ba7-be1b-4c5b-8140-27896edcce6e e545ebc9-af74-48a0-a9d4-2b45702aa2bc\">found at Fidenae</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, a few miles north of the city, in the 1980s. The building was rectangular, about six by five metres, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"412074a4-fba5-42cb-be43-2699a4ff580b\">made of wood and rammed earth—a construction method<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"d5eafc65-f647-4891-bb48-85058edd9a25\">still used today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>—with a simple porch around it formed by the overhanging roof. Inside were a central hearth, large pottery storage jars, and traces of typical foodstuffs and domestic animals.</span></p><p><span>There are vivid glimpses here of human life and other forms of life, but the question is what these glimpses add up to. The archaeological remains certainly demonstrate that there is a long and rich prehistory behind the ancient Rome we can still see, but how far back that prehistory extends is another matter.</span></p><p><span>Part of the problem lies in the conditions under which excavation takes place in the city itself. Rome has been so <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e1c61559-ca1f-4f47-8644-ddcb5a6336c6\">intensively built on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> over the centuries that traces of early occupation survive only in areas that have escaped later disturbance. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"5024c3cd-fed8-4874-8a04-e399b6f92c8a\">The foundations dug in the first and second centuries CE<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> for the vast marble temples of the Forum <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"2ebf54e2-87ee-40a6-a7b9-ab24b352f48c\">obliterated much of what then lay beneath the surface<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"5024c3cd-fed8-4874-8a04-e399b6f92c8a\">the cellars of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> grand Renaissance houses <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"2ebf54e2-87ee-40a6-a7b9-ab24b352f48c\">cut through archaeological remains from still earlier periods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> in other parts of the city. So we have tiny snapshots, never the big picture. This is archaeology at its most difficult and, although new fragments of evidence continue to emerge, the interpretation—and reinterpretation—of that evidence is almost always contested and often controversial. For example, there is continuing debate over whether the small pieces of wattle and daub found during excavations in the Forum in the mid-20th century indicate that an early hut settlement once existed there, or whether they were accidentally brought in with rubble used a few centuries later to raise the ground level. The Forum site, though suitable for a cemetery, would have been rather damp and marshy for a village.</span></p><p><span>Precise dating is even more contentious. There is no certain independent date for any of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"58c962e5-ca46-4226-be33-271a3f240d34\">the archaeological material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> from early Rome or the surrounding area, and the age of almost every major find remains disputed. Over many decades, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"05849443-002c-4529-9b31-e48e225ea172\">archaeologists have drawn on evidence such as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> wheel-made pottery, which is assumed to be later than handmade pottery; <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"05849443-002c-4529-9b31-e48e225ea172 20e0b0f2-a7e3-44b3-9cc0-ef64b83ba3d4\">Greek ceramics</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> found occasionally in graves, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"05849443-002c-4529-9b31-e48e225ea172\">whose dating is better established<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> but still imperfect; and careful comparisons between sites. Together, these indicators <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"179bd33b-ed3c-4b97-acdd-4b4fcf3edc5d\">have produced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"876d2eb5-4d8c-4745-a228-fe8c8fe70f62\">only a rough chronological scheme<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> for the period from around 1000 to 600 BCE.</span></p><p><span>On that basis, the earliest burials in Rome would date to around 1000 BCE, and the earliest known settlements to around 750–700 BCE. Even these dates, however, are far from certain. Alternative scientific dating methods, including radiocarbon analysis, which estimates the age of organic material, have suggested that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"5f599945-d7c0-4be5-9a11-9f5072aca41c\">conventional dates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> may underestimate the true age of the remains by as much as a century. The building at Fidenae, for example, was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"c4f117fe-e954-4af9-9da6-37c5564cdcc7\">dated to around the middle of the eighth century BCE according to traditional archaeological criteria, whereas radiocarbon analysis places it around the end of the ninth century BCE<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. If anything, Rome appears to be getting older.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes </span><b><span>27–32</span></b><span> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><b><span>YES</span></b><span> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NO</span></b><span> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326505\" id=\"question-wrapper-326505\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c5fc1e99-2ecc-433c-a411-f28271139d5b\">The rise of the Roman Empire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"5ce18e1a-30ce-4787-bf95-8f5fbcc91a4a\">has attracted relatively little curiosity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326506\" id=\"question-wrapper-326506\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"c276e463-d3b2-4cc6-ab9b-5e4daa79bed9\">Modern historians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> may in fact <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"c276e463-d3b2-4cc6-ab9b-5e4daa79bed9\">have more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"aa2df824-049f-4c5c-889d-fdec755641a8\">first-hand material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"767dc892-2285-4aa4-a9ee-38d5d5e25d18\">early Rome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to draw on <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"c276e463-d3b2-4cc6-ab9b-5e4daa79bed9\">than </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bf191e55-a367-48b7-a757-c57b69933046 c276e463-d3b2-4cc6-ab9b-5e4daa79bed9\">the Roman writers</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"bf191e55-a367-48b7-a757-c57b69933046\"> of the first century BCE</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> did.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326507\" id=\"question-wrapper-326507\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>An unrealistically flattering <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"0fa9c8cf-8d15-40eb-9839-874aa58c5c7b\">picture of the city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> emerges from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"0cb10a03-6448-41ac-a929-e293b316aaaa\">the writings of most Roman historians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326508\" id=\"question-wrapper-326508\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Roman authors' accounts of how the city was founded <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"579d4e8d-675f-41bf-8fa4-2a9d561cea01\">provide a full description<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"3d4be8e5-00f4-4ec6-86bc-aa0d0b17aa7b\">its earliest period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326509\" id=\"question-wrapper-326509\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"c48192d0-a968-4077-9588-b60f9cf7908f\">It is certain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> that the city of Rome <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"7a28a2bb-1227-45d7-bb4b-0b96878e7591\">had already existed for a considerable period of time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> by 63 BCE. </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326510\" id=\"question-wrapper-326510\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>No other ancient city has undergone as much <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"e1c61559-ca1f-4f47-8644-ddcb5a6336c6\">reconstruction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> as Rome.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter in boxes 33–36 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326511\" id=\"question-wrapper-326511\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"e545ebc9-af74-48a0-a9d4-2b45702aa2bc\">the find at Fidenae<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> so valuable to archaeologists?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"b50f56e2-3504-494c-873a-43b39f54ddf9\">offered some insight into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"99258a0d-6d49-46e3-ad2d-af90548537c3\">how people lived at the time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</li> <li>B. It was the first evidence of an ancient Roman settlement in the area.</li> <li>C. It overturned common assumptions about the diet of ancient Romans.</li> <li>D. It showed how sophisticated domestic Roman architecture could be.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326512\" id=\"question-wrapper-326512\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What did Rome's marble temples and Renaissance houses have in common?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They were the most enduring buildings of their respective eras.</li> <li>B. They were evidence of Rome's enormous wealth.</li> <li>C. They were built on previously unoccupied sites.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"2ebf54e2-87ee-40a6-a7b9-ab24b352f48c\">Evidence from earlier periods was lost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"5024c3cd-fed8-4874-8a04-e399b6f92c8a\">when they were built<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326513\" id=\"question-wrapper-326513\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does the writer say in the fifth paragraph about the dating of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"58c962e5-ca46-4226-be33-271a3f240d34\">excavated remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The age of most major finds has now been settled.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"876d2eb5-4d8c-4745-a228-fe8c8fe70f62\">Only an approximate sequence of eras<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"179bd33b-ed3c-4b97-acdd-4b4fcf3edc5d\">can be established<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Serious attempts at dating began only a few decades ago.</li> <li>D. More thorough investigations will result in reliable dates.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326514\" id=\"question-wrapper-326514\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the final paragraph, the writer makes the point that</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. traditional archaeological methods of dating have been discredited.</li> <li>B. many archaeologists are reluctant to abandon traditional methods of dating.</li> <li>C. radiocarbon dating is more accurate than archaeological methods.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"c4f117fe-e954-4af9-9da6-37c5564cdcc7\">the findings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"5f599945-d7c0-4be5-9a11-9f5072aca41c\">traditional archaeology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> and radiocarbon dating <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"c4f117fe-e954-4af9-9da6-37c5564cdcc7\">differ<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A–F, below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, A–F, in boxes 37–40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><b><span>Endings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"412074a4-fba5-42cb-be43-2699a4ff580b\">built using a technique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"d5eafc65-f647-4891-bb48-85058edd9a25\">has never gone out of use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. was possibly brought to the site with later building rubble.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"f4563cec-dc4d-4b74-a67e-764360aebcd0\">was constructed on the site of an earlier burial ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"05849443-002c-4529-9b31-e48e225ea172\">is used to determine the relative dates of various Roman artefacts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. was chosen as the area for the greatest number of archaeological excavations.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"8ee036b9-6b31-4dc7-8d5f-f627082a6b98\">can shed some light on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"143c21de-86b2-4bbf-9de0-7a1b429a1f47\">what Rome was originally like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326515\" id=\"question-wrapper-326515\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Latin language </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326516\" id=\"question-wrapper-326516\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Roman Forum </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326517\" id=\"question-wrapper-326517\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"928f5ba7-be1b-4c5b-8140-27896edcce6e\">The building unearthed at Fidenae<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326518\" id=\"question-wrapper-326518\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"20e0b0f2-a7e3-44b3-9cc0-ef64b83ba3d4\">Ancient Greek pottery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> </span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c5fc1e99-2ecc-433c-a411-f28271139d5b","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"The rise of the Roman Empire","passagePhrase":"grow so much larger ... and come to control such a vast empire"},{"uid":"c276e463-d3b2-4cc6-ab9b-5e4daa79bed9","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Modern historians ... have more ... than","passagePhrase":"Roman writers ... may even have had less"},{"uid":"bf191e55-a367-48b7-a757-c57b69933046","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"of the first century BCE","passagePhrase":"these historians"},{"uid":"aa2df824-049f-4c5c-889d-fdec755641a8","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"first-hand material","passagePhrase":"direct evidence"},{"uid":"767dc892-2285-4aa4-a9ee-38d5d5e25d18","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"early Rome","passagePhrase":"the earliest phases of Rome’s history"},{"uid":"0cb10a03-6448-41ac-a929-e293b316aaaa","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"the writings of most Roman historians","passagePhrase":"Their ‘histories’ of the foundation of ancient Rome"},{"uid":"0fa9c8cf-8d15-40eb-9839-874aa58c5c7b","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"picture of the city","passagePhrase":"how the Romans viewed their city"},{"uid":"3d4be8e5-00f4-4ec6-86bc-aa0d0b17aa7b","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"its earliest period","passagePhrase":"what earliest Rome was actually like"},{"uid":"c48192d0-a968-4077-9588-b60f9cf7908f","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"It is certain","passagePhrase":"One fact is clear"},{"uid":"7a28a2bb-1227-45d7-bb4b-0b96878e7591","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"had already existed for a considerable period of time","passagePhrase":"was already a very old city"},{"uid":"8ee036b9-6b31-4dc7-8d5f-f627082a6b98","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"can shed some light on","passagePhrase":"clues ... that may point back to"},{"uid":"143c21de-86b2-4bbf-9de0-7a1b429a1f47","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"what Rome was originally like","passagePhrase":"features of earliest Rome"},{"uid":"f4563cec-dc4d-4b74-a67e-764360aebcd0","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"was constructed on the site of an earlier burial ground","passagePhrase":"Beneath the Forum ... lie the remains of an early cemetery"},{"uid":"99258a0d-6d49-46e3-ad2d-af90548537c3","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"how people lived at the time","passagePhrase":"the way of life"},{"uid":"b50f56e2-3504-494c-873a-43b39f54ddf9","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"offered some insight into","passagePhrase":"some of these gaps can be filled"},{"uid":"928f5ba7-be1b-4c5b-8140-27896edcce6e e545ebc9-af74-48a0-a9d4-2b45702aa2bc","qNum":"33 39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"early structures ... found at Fidenae"},{"uid":"412074a4-fba5-42cb-be43-2699a4ff580b","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"built using a technique","passagePhrase":"made of wood and rammed earth—a construction method"},{"uid":"d5eafc65-f647-4891-bb48-85058edd9a25","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"has never gone out of use","passagePhrase":"still used today"},{"uid":"e1c61559-ca1f-4f47-8644-ddcb5a6336c6","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"reconstruction","passagePhrase":"intensively built on"},{"uid":"5024c3cd-fed8-4874-8a04-e399b6f92c8a","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"when they were built","passagePhrase":"The foundations dug in the first and second centuries CE ... the cellars of"},{"uid":"2ebf54e2-87ee-40a6-a7b9-ab24b352f48c","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Evidence from earlier periods was lost","passagePhrase":"obliterated much of what then lay beneath the surface ... cut through archaeological remains from still earlier periods"},{"uid":"58c962e5-ca46-4226-be33-271a3f240d34","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"excavated remains","passagePhrase":"the archaeological material"},{"uid":"05849443-002c-4529-9b31-e48e225ea172","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"is used to determine the relative dates of various Roman artefacts","passagePhrase":"archaeologists have drawn on evidence such as ... whose dating is better established"},{"uid":"05849443-002c-4529-9b31-e48e225ea172 20e0b0f2-a7e3-44b3-9cc0-ef64b83ba3d4","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Greek ceramics"},{"uid":"179bd33b-ed3c-4b97-acdd-4b4fcf3edc5d","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"can be established","passagePhrase":"have produced"},{"uid":"876d2eb5-4d8c-4745-a228-fe8c8fe70f62","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Only an approximate sequence of eras","passagePhrase":"only a rough chronological scheme"},{"uid":"5f599945-d7c0-4be5-9a11-9f5072aca41c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"traditional archaeology","passagePhrase":"conventional dates"},{"uid":"c4f117fe-e954-4af9-9da6-37c5564cdcc7","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"the findings ... differ","passagePhrase":"dated to around the middle of the eighth century BCE according to traditional archaeological criteria, whereas radiocarbon analysis places it around the end of the ninth century BCE"},{"uid":"bf191e55-a367-48b7-a757-c57b69933046 c276e463-d3b2-4cc6-ab9b-5e4daa79bed9","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"the Roman writers","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"e545ebc9-af74-48a0-a9d4-2b45702aa2bc","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"the find at Fidenae","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"928f5ba7-be1b-4c5b-8140-27896edcce6e","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"The building unearthed at Fidenae","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"20e0b0f2-a7e3-44b3-9cc0-ef64b83ba3d4","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Ancient Greek pottery","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_121":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>A disaster of Titanic proportions</span></b></p><p><span>At 11.39 p. m. on the evening of Sunday 14 April 1912, lookouts Frederick Fleet and Reginald Lee on the forward mast of the </span><i><span>Titanic</span></i><span> sighted an eerie, black mass coming into view directly in front of the ship. Fleet <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 2\" data-uid=\"b3f3ad09-cb3d-4949-bf5e-38c99774f9bd df318203-7c55-4fb0-ae95-64c3613a9ce4\">picked up the phone</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> to the helm, waited for Sixth Officer Moody to answer, and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 2\" data-uid=\"b3f3ad09-cb3d-4949-bf5e-38c99774f9bd df318203-7c55-4fb0-ae95-64c3613a9ce4\">yelled</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> 'Iceberg, right ahead!' The greatest disaster in mari<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4b7de8a0-bd8f-4253-94ed-ba86bd7f7fa8\">time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> history was about to be set in motion.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"ae8dc99e-240f-45a4-b5d3-e4b6c532f0a6\">Thirty-seven seconds later<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, despite the efforts of officers in the bridge and engine room to steer around the iceberg, the </span><i><span>Titanic</span></i><span> struck a piece of submerged ice, bursting rivets in the ship's hull and flooding the first five watertight compartments. The ship's designer, Thomas Andrews, carried out a visual inspection of the ship's damage and informed Captain Smith at midnight that the ship would sink in less than two hours. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"632ba278-fe13-4818-bfd9-1359d76920c4\">By 12.30 a. m<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>., the lifeboats were being filled with women and children, after Smith <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"d588e5b6-3e1b-4cb4-ae12-7ef69e78957b\">had given the command<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> for them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"074512c8-58de-47e5-9e09-b29709cf75a4\">to be uncovered and swung out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"632ba278-fe13-4818-bfd9-1359d76920c4\">15 minutes earlier<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. The first lifeboat was successfully lowered 15 minutes later, with only 28 of its 65 seats occupied. By 1.15 a. m., the waterline was beginning to reach the </span><i><span>Titanic</span></i><span>'s name on the ship's bow, and over the next hour every lifeboat would be released as officers struggled to maintain order amongst the growing panic on board.</span></p><p><span>The closing moments of the </span><i><span>Titanic</span></i><span>'s sinking began shortly after 2 a. m., as the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"390c6445-7086-434b-8d48-ba4c75f78592\">last<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> lifeboat was lowered and the ship's propellers lifted out of the water, leaving the 1,500 passengers still on board to surge towards the stern. At 2.17 a. m., Harold Bride and Jack Philips <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"08bfcc6d-791f-4c41-ad2c-96a4d36fb718\">tapped out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> their last wireless message after being relieved of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"f5987f5d-08cb-47a6-9f0c-6e94ac866de9\">duty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> as the ship's wireless operators, and the ship's band stopped playing. Less than a minute later, occupants of the lifeboats witnessed the ship's lights flash once, then go black, and a huge roar signalled the </span><i><span>Titanic</span></i><span>'s contents plunging towards the bow, causing the front half of the ship to break off and go under. The </span><i><span>Titanic'</span></i><span>s stern bobbed up momentarily, and at 2.20 a. m., the ship finally disappeared beneath the frigid waters.</span></p><p><span>What or who was responsible for the scale of this catastrophe? Explanations abound, some that focus on very small details. Due to a last minute change in the ship's officer line-up, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"6151d186-6ee8-47f2-a8ed-b227f3a66179\">iceberg lookouts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> Frederick Fleet and Reginald Lee were making do without <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"8ebf5637-3c6b-4c1d-9bab-d0074b20e73e\">a pair of binoculars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> that an officer transferred off the ship in Southampton had left in a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"8a51c2aa-2862-4aa1-8c69-555141d7f461\">cupboard<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> onboard, unbeknownst to any of the ship's crew. Fleet, who survived the sinking, insisted at a subsequent inquiry that he could have identified the iceberg in time to avert disaster if he had been in possession of the binoculars.</span></p><p><span>Less than an hour before the </span><i><span>Titanic</span></i><span> struck the iceberg, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"73c08f02-3b67-4a4f-99c9-0547ba33f876\">wireless operator Cyril Evans on the </span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"73c08f02-3b67-4a4f-99c9-0547ba33f876\">Californian</span></span></i><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"73c08f02-3b67-4a4f-99c9-0547ba33f876\">, located just 20 miles to the north, tried to contact operator Jack Philips on the </span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"73c08f02-3b67-4a4f-99c9-0547ba33f876\">Titanic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></i><span> to warn him of pack ice in the area. '<span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"73c08f02-3b67-4a4f-99c9-0547ba33f876\">Shut up, shut up, you're jamming my signal', Philips replied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. 'I'm busy.' The </span><i><span>Titanic'</span></i><span>s wireless system had broken down for several hours earlier that day, and Philips was clearing a backlog of personal messages that passengers had requested to be sent to family and friends in the USA. Nevertheless, Captain Smith had maintained the ship's speed of 22 knots despite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"0fc03f4b-f85a-4a58-93ff-745e3d1a254d\">multiple earlier warnings of ice ahead<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. It has been suggested that Smith was under pressure to make headlines by arriving early in New York, but maritime historians such as Richard Howell have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"adfbf880-736a-4dc8-bdc1-2f8b1124859e\">countered this perception<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, noting that Smith was simply <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"e7d7f038-42eb-4b3f-95f7-bc8d1b3bcf2a\">following common procedure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> at the time, and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"e7d7f038-42eb-4b3f-95f7-bc8d1b3bcf2a\">not behaving recklessly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>One of the strongest explanations for the severe loss of life has been the fact that the </span><i><span>Titanic</span></i><span> did not carry enough lifeboats for everyone on board. Maritime regulations at the time tied lifeboat capacity to ship size, not to the number of passengers on board. This meant that the </span><i><span>Titanic</span></i><span> , <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"b827b2b0-2940-41d0-a8da-54c3d3b59cca\">with room for 1,178 of its 2,222 passengers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"b827b2b0-2940-41d0-a8da-54c3d3b59cca\">actually surpassed the Board of Trade's requirement that it carry lifeboats for 1,060 of its passengers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. Nevertheless, with lifeboats being lowered less than half full in many cases, and only 712 passengers surviving despite a two and a half hour window of opportunity, more lifeboats would not have guaranteed more survivors in the absence of better training and preparation. Many passengers were confused about where to go after the order to launch lifeboats was given; a lifeboat drill scheduled for earlier on the same day that the Titanic struck the iceberg was cancelled by Captain Smith, in order to allow passengers to attend church.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the table below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the text for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 1-6.</span></i></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"8\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"ae8dc99e-240f-45a4-b5d3-e4b6c532f0a6\">Time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p></td><td colspan=\"9\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Person's</span></p></td><td colspan=\"9\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"f5987f5d-08cb-47a6-9f0c-6e94ac866de9\">Position<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p></td><td colspan=\"23\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Action</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"8\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>11.39 p.m.</span></p></td><td colspan=\"9\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(1)_______</span></p></td><td colspan=\"9\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(2)_______</span></p></td><td colspan=\"23\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b3f3ad09-cb3d-4949-bf5e-38c99774f9bd\">Reported<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> sighting of iceberg</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"8\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(3)_______</span></p></td><td colspan=\"9\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Andrews</span></p></td><td colspan=\"9\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Ship's designer</span></p></td><td colspan=\"23\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"df318203-7c55-4fb0-ae95-64c3613a9ce4\">Reported<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> how long the </span><i><span>Titanic </span></i><span>could</span></p><p><span>stay aflo<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4b7de8a0-bd8f-4253-94ed-ba86bd7f7fa8\">at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"8\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"632ba278-fe13-4818-bfd9-1359d76920c4\">12.15 a.m<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p></td><td colspan=\"9\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Smith</span></p></td><td colspan=\"9\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Captain</span></p></td><td colspan=\"23\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"d588e5b6-3e1b-4cb4-ae12-7ef69e78957b\">Ordered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> (4)_______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"074512c8-58de-47e5-9e09-b29709cf75a4\">to be released<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"8\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>2.17 a.m.</span></p></td><td colspan=\"9\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Bride &amp; Philips</span></p></td><td colspan=\"9\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(5)_______</span></p></td><td colspan=\"23\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"08bfcc6d-791f-4c41-ad2c-96a4d36fb718\">Relayed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"390c6445-7086-434b-8d48-ba4c75f78592\">final<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (6)_______</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37339\" id=\"question-wrapper-37339\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(FREDERICK) FLEET</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37340\" id=\"question-wrapper-37340\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LOOKOUT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37341\" id=\"question-wrapper-37341\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MIDNIGHT [OR] 12(.00) A.M./AM</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37342\" id=\"question-wrapper-37342\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LIFEBOATS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37343\" id=\"question-wrapper-37343\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WIRELESS OPERATORS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37344\" id=\"question-wrapper-37344\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(WIRELESS) MESSAGE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 7-13, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>TRUE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>FALSE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if there is no information on this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37345\" id=\"question-wrapper-37345\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"8ebf5637-3c6b-4c1d-9bab-d0074b20e73e\">The binoculars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"6151d186-6ee8-47f2-a8ed-b227f3a66179\">the men on watch<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> had been left in a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"8a51c2aa-2862-4aa1-8c69-555141d7f461\">crew locker<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in Southampton.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37346\" id=\"question-wrapper-37346\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The missing binoculars were the major factor leading to the collision with the iceberg.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37347\" id=\"question-wrapper-37347\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Philips missed notification about the ice from Evans because <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"73c08f02-3b67-4a4f-99c9-0547ba33f876\">the Titanic's wireless system was not functioning at the time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37348\" id=\"question-wrapper-37348\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Captain Smith <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"0fc03f4b-f85a-4a58-93ff-745e3d1a254d\">knew there was ice in the area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37349\" id=\"question-wrapper-37349\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Howell <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"adfbf880-736a-4dc8-bdc1-2f8b1124859e\">believed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the captains failure to reduce speed was an <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"e7d7f038-42eb-4b3f-95f7-bc8d1b3bcf2a\">irresponsible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> action.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37350\" id=\"question-wrapper-37350\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Titanic was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"b827b2b0-2940-41d0-a8da-54c3d3b59cca\">able to seat more passengers in lifeboats than the Board of Trade required<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37351\" id=\"question-wrapper-37351\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A lifeboat drill would have saved more lives.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b3f3ad09-cb3d-4949-bf5e-38c99774f9bd df318203-7c55-4fb0-ae95-64c3613a9ce4","qNum":"1 2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"picked up the phone ... yelled"},{"uid":"4b7de8a0-bd8f-4253-94ed-ba86bd7f7fa8","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"at","passagePhrase":"time"},{"uid":"ae8dc99e-240f-45a4-b5d3-e4b6c532f0a6","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Time","passagePhrase":"Thirty-seven seconds later"},{"uid":"632ba278-fe13-4818-bfd9-1359d76920c4","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"12.15 a.m","passagePhrase":"By 12.30 a. m ... 15 minutes earlier"},{"uid":"d588e5b6-3e1b-4cb4-ae12-7ef69e78957b","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Ordered","passagePhrase":"had given the command"},{"uid":"074512c8-58de-47e5-9e09-b29709cf75a4","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"to be released","passagePhrase":"to be uncovered and swung out"},{"uid":"390c6445-7086-434b-8d48-ba4c75f78592","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"final","passagePhrase":"last"},{"uid":"08bfcc6d-791f-4c41-ad2c-96a4d36fb718","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Relayed","passagePhrase":"tapped out"},{"uid":"f5987f5d-08cb-47a6-9f0c-6e94ac866de9","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Position","passagePhrase":"duty"},{"uid":"6151d186-6ee8-47f2-a8ed-b227f3a66179","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"the men on watch","passagePhrase":"iceberg lookouts"},{"uid":"8ebf5637-3c6b-4c1d-9bab-d0074b20e73e","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"The binoculars","passagePhrase":"a pair of binoculars"},{"uid":"0fc03f4b-f85a-4a58-93ff-745e3d1a254d","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"knew there was ice in the area","passagePhrase":"multiple earlier warnings of ice ahead"},{"uid":"adfbf880-736a-4dc8-bdc1-2f8b1124859e","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"believed","passagePhrase":"countered this perception"},{"uid":"b827b2b0-2940-41d0-a8da-54c3d3b59cca","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"able to seat more passengers in lifeboats than the Board of Trade required","passagePhrase":"with room for 1,178 of its 2,222 passengers ... actually surpassed the Board of Trade's requirement that it carry lifeboats for 1,060 of its passengers"},{"uid":"b3f3ad09-cb3d-4949-bf5e-38c99774f9bd","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Reported","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"df318203-7c55-4fb0-ae95-64c3613a9ce4","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Reported","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_122":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Three dimensional films</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><span>A. In the theatre of the Ambassador Hotel in Los Angeles, on the evening of 27 September <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"818dea92-da5b-4ef7-95d2-f59092c1188f\">1922<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, a new form of film-making <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"944f3854-92a1-4b98-b744-a4512e953395\">made its commercial debut<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>: 3-D </span><sup><span>1</span></sup><span> . The film, </span><i><span>The Power of Love</span></i><span> , was then shown in New York City to exhibitors and press, but was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"944f3854-92a1-4b98-b744-a4512e953395\">subsequently not picked up for distribution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and is now believed to be lost. The following three decades were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"944f3854-92a1-4b98-b744-a4512e953395\">a period of quiet experimentation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> for 3-D pioneers, as they adapted to new technologies and steadily improved the viewing experience. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"818dea92-da5b-4ef7-95d2-f59092c1188f\">1952<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"944f3854-92a1-4b98-b744-a4512e953395\">the 'golden era<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>' of 3-D is considered to have begun with the release of </span><i><span>Bwana Devil</span></i><span> , and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"818dea92-da5b-4ef7-95d2-f59092c1188f\">over the next several years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> audiences met with a string of films that used the technology. Over <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"818dea92-da5b-4ef7-95d2-f59092c1188f\">the following decades<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"944f3854-92a1-4b98-b744-a4512e953395\">waxed and waned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> within film-making circles, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"944f3854-92a1-4b98-b744-a4512e953395\">peaking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in the 1970s and again in the 1990s when IMAX gained traction, but it is only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"818dea92-da5b-4ef7-95d2-f59092c1188f\">in the last few years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> that 3-D appears to have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"944f3854-92a1-4b98-b744-a4512e953395\">firmly entered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> mainstream production.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><span>B. Released worldwide in December 2009, the fantasy film </span><i><span>Avatar</span></i><span> quickly became the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97\">highest-grossing film </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"785ee64c-8585-485a-9580-b6d5a68d620e cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97\">ever made</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97\">knocking </span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97\">Titanic</span></span></i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97\"> from the top slot<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. </span><i><span>Avatar</span></i><span> , set in 2154 on a planet in a distant solar system, went on to become the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97\">only film to have earned US$2 billion world-wide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, and is now approaching the $3 billion mark. The main reason for its runaway popularity appears to be its visual splendour; though most critics praised the film, it was mostly on account of its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97\">ground-breaking special effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Kenneth Turan of the </span><i><span>Los Angeles Times</span></i><span> praised </span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"9ad9cd2f-ae59-4038-8802-1edc284ea95d\">Avatar's</span></span></i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"9ad9cd2f-ae59-4038-8802-1edc284ea95d\"> 'powerful' visual accomplishments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, but suggested <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"b464a47d-5ffe-4dba-b323-2f41ecc60c83\">the dialogue was 'flat' and the characterisations 'obvious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>'. A film analyst at Exhibitor Relations has agreed, noting that </span><i><span>Avatar</span></i><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5d38133c-fe4d-40f3-8f06-b6f503c11f5c\">has cemented the use of 3-D<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> as a production and promotional tool for blockbuster films, rather than as a mere niche or novelty experiment. '<span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 24\" data-uid=\"4c751513-b17d-460a-a6e9-100e3b6661bc 785ee64c-8585-485a-9580-b6d5a68d620e\">This is why all these 3-D venues were built</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>', he said. '<span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97\">This is the one. The behemoth... </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 24\" data-uid=\"4c751513-b17d-460a-a6e9-100e3b6661bc cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97\">The holy grail of 3-D</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"4c751513-b17d-460a-a6e9-100e3b6661bc\"> has finally arrived</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>'.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><span>C. Those who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"8a09f63d-29a5-4a46-b282-7c57a8a7b670\">embrace 3-D<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> note that it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"8a09f63d-29a5-4a46-b282-7c57a8a7b670\">spices up a trip to the cinema<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"8a09f63d-29a5-4a46-b282-7c57a8a7b670\">adding a more active 'embodied' layer of experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> instead of the viewer passively receiving the film through eyes and ears only. A blogger on Animation Ideas writes, '...when 3-D <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"edd22a57-1566-4bed-8360-191933edb7eb\">is done well<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>—like in the flying scenes in </span><i><span>Up</span></i><span> , </span><i><span>How to Train Your Dragon</span></i><span> and </span><i><span>Avatar</span></i><span> , there is an added feeling of vertigo. If you have any <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"b2b0676f-16c0-496c-96eb-25246b486d7a\">fear of heights<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, the 3-D really <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 22\" data-uid=\"8a09f63d-29a5-4a46-b282-7c57a8a7b670 a8ce3a2a-f2e7-48a5-8343-1b6b462c332e\">adds to</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"8a09f63d-29a5-4a46-b282-7c57a8a7b670\"> this element</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>...' Kevin Carr argues that the backlash against 3-D is similar to that which occurred against CGI </span><sup><span>2</span></sup><span> several years ago, and points out that CGI is now widely regarded as part of the film-maker's artistic toolkit. He also notes that new technology is frequently seen to be a 'gimmick' in its early days, pointing out that many commentators slapped the first 'talkie' films of the early 1920s with this same label.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><span>D. But not everyone greets the rise of 3-D with open arms. Some ophthalmologists point out that 3-D can have unsettling physical effects for many viewers. Dr. Michael Rosenberg, a professor at Northwestern University, has pointed out that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b\">many people </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 23\" data-uid=\"8404b2c1-8009-4ab0-932b-95cfb39dd166 9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b\">go through life with</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 23\" data-uid=\"9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b e9671f56-8823-466e-8a8f-a0f871208a84\">minor eye disturbances</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e9671f56-8823-466e-8a8f-a0f871208a84\">—a slight muscular imbalance</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, for example—that does not interrupt day-to-day activities. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"4caac4c1-1485-4b56-bcbb-c67e463b1559\">the experience of a 3-D movie<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, however, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b\">this problem </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 23\" data-uid=\"1ea30fda-d14e-4129-b409-617fa9baefa8 9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b\">can be exacerbated</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b\"> through the viewer trying to concentrate on unusual visual phenomena</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Dr. Deborah Friedman, from the University of Rochester Medical Center, notes that the perception of depth conjured through three dimensions <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"203a5ae4-288f-4fdf-a030-b5e1a36e7193\">does not complement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"99aae8e8-27a3-4173-9295-fe2a0c63de2d\">the angles from which we take in the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b\">Eyestrains, headaches and nausea are therefore a problem for around 15% of a 3-D film audience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><span>E. Film critic Roger Ebert warns that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"548b9881-e0e0-4399-be64-64eab7adcc1c\">3-D<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d\">is detrimental to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"3ae702ce-4abe-4ec9-b605-863470f9bc29\">good film-making<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Firstly, he argues, the technology is simply unnecessary; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"1e1832ba-ba5b-4c22-99c7-d8a6ea7e091d\">2-D movies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> are 'already' 3-D, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"85973c1c-6dba-4f8e-8cf3-3d22e8c01ce6\">as far as our minds are concerned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Adding the extra dimension with technology, instead of letting our minds do the work, can actually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d\">be counter-purposeful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d\">make the over-all effect seem clumsy and contrived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Ebert also points out that the special glasses <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d\">dim the effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> by soaking up light from the screen, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d\">making 3-D films a slightly duller experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> than they might otherwise be. Finally, Ebert suggests that 3-D <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d\">encourages film-makers to </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 21\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d 1187fb8c-7507-4e73-a4a3-0cb4c16e7321\">undercut</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d\"> drama and narrative in favour of simply </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 21\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d 1187fb8c-7507-4e73-a4a3-0cb4c16e7321\">piling on</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d\"> more </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 21\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d 29d8107e-0dd3-443a-85c4-d67d03416737\">gimmicks and special effects</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. 'Hollywood is racing headlong toward the kiddie market,' he says, pointing to Disney's announcement that it will no longer make traditional films <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"1187fb8c-7507-4e73-a4a3-0cb4c16e7321\">in favour of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> animation, franchises, and superheroes.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><span>F. Whether or not 3-D becomes a powerful force for the film-maker's vision and the film-going experience, or goes down in history as an over-hyped, expensive novelty, the technology certainly shows no signs of fading in the popularity stakes at the moment. </span><i><span>Clash of the Titans</span></i><span> , </span><i><span>Alice in Wonderland</span></i><span> and </span><i><span>How to Train Your Dragon</span></i><span> have all recently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0c9e8b50-ee34-47d2-a58d-7caf39362b68\">benefited at the box office<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> due to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0c9e8b50-ee34-47d2-a58d-7caf39362b68\">added sales<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> that 3-D provides, and with </span><i><span>Avatar's</span></i><span> record set to last some time as a totem of 3-D's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0c9e8b50-ee34-47d2-a58d-7caf39362b68\">commercial possibilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, studios <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0c9e8b50-ee34-47d2-a58d-7caf39362b68\">are not prepared to back down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>*1. Three Dimensional</span></p><p><span>*2. Computer Generated Imagery</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Reading Passage 2 has six sections, A-F.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct headings for sections A-F from the list of headings below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct number, i-x, in boxes 14-19.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. Construction of special cinemas for 3-D</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"0c9e8b50-ee34-47d2-a58d-7caf39362b68\">Good returns forecast for immediate future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97\">greatest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> 3-D film <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"785ee64c-8585-485a-9580-b6d5a68d620e\">of all time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. End of traditional movies for children</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"818dea92-da5b-4ef7-95d2-f59092c1188f\">Early<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"944f3854-92a1-4b98-b744-a4512e953395\">developments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"548b9881-e0e0-4399-be64-64eab7adcc1c\">New technology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d\">diminishes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"3ae702ce-4abe-4ec9-b605-863470f9bc29\">the art<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. The golden age of movies</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"8a09f63d-29a5-4a46-b282-7c57a8a7b670\">defence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of 3-D</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. 3-D is here to stay</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"x\"><span>x. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b\">Undesirable visual effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37352\" id=\"question-wrapper-37352\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37353\" id=\"question-wrapper-37353\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37354\" id=\"question-wrapper-37354\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37355\" id=\"question-wrapper-37355\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">X</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37356\" id=\"question-wrapper-37356\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37357\" id=\"question-wrapper-37357\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 20-26) and the list of people below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Match each statement with the correct person, A-G.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 20-26.</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NB</span></b></i><i><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NB</span></b></i><i><span> Some options may not be used.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of People</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Kenneth Turan</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Exhibitor Relations' analyst</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Animation Ideas' blogger</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Kevin Carr</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Dr Michael Rosenberg</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. Dr Deborah Friedman</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. Roger Ebert</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37358\" id=\"question-wrapper-37358\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>3-D <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"203a5ae4-288f-4fdf-a030-b5e1a36e7193\">conflicts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> with our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"99aae8e8-27a3-4173-9295-fe2a0c63de2d\">mental construct of our surroundings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37359\" id=\"question-wrapper-37359\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>3-D encourages an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"1187fb8c-7507-4e73-a4a3-0cb4c16e7321\">over-emphasis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"29d8107e-0dd3-443a-85c4-d67d03416737\">quick visual thrills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37360\" id=\"question-wrapper-37360\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"edd22a57-1566-4bed-8360-191933edb7eb\">Effective use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of 3-D technology may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"a8ce3a2a-f2e7-48a5-8343-1b6b462c332e\">increase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"b2b0676f-16c0-496c-96eb-25246b486d7a\">sensation of elevation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37361\" id=\"question-wrapper-37361\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"4caac4c1-1485-4b56-bcbb-c67e463b1559\">3-D viewing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"1ea30fda-d14e-4129-b409-617fa9baefa8\">worsen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"8404b2c1-8009-4ab0-932b-95cfb39dd166\">existing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e9671f56-8823-466e-8a8f-a0f871208a84\">visual disorder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37362\" id=\"question-wrapper-37362\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Avatar is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5d38133c-fe4d-40f3-8f06-b6f503c11f5c\">most powerful example of 3-D<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"4c751513-b17d-460a-a6e9-100e3b6661bc\">yet to arrive in cinemas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37363\" id=\"question-wrapper-37363\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"9ad9cd2f-ae59-4038-8802-1edc284ea95d\">Avatar's strength is found in its visual splendour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"b464a47d-5ffe-4dba-b323-2f41ecc60c83\">not in aspects of story<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37364\" id=\"question-wrapper-37364\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"85973c1c-6dba-4f8e-8cf3-3d22e8c01ce6\">already have the mental capacity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> to see <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"1e1832ba-ba5b-4c22-99c7-d8a6ea7e091d\">ordinary movies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> in three dimensions.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"818dea92-da5b-4ef7-95d2-f59092c1188f","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Early","passagePhrase":"1922 ... 1952 ... over the next several years ... the following decades ... in the last few years"},{"uid":"944f3854-92a1-4b98-b744-a4512e953395","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"developments","passagePhrase":"made its commercial debut ... subsequently not picked up for distribution ... a period of quiet experimentation ... the 'golden era ... waxed and waned ... peaking ... firmly entered"},{"uid":"cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"greatest","passagePhrase":"highest-grossing film ... knocking ... Titanic ... from the top slot ... only film to have earned US$2 billion world-wide ... ground-breaking special effects ... This is the one. The behemoth..."},{"uid":"785ee64c-8585-485a-9580-b6d5a68d620e cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"ever made"},{"uid":"9ad9cd2f-ae59-4038-8802-1edc284ea95d","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"Avatar's strength is found in its visual splendour","passagePhrase":"Avatar's ... 'powerful' visual accomplishments"},{"uid":"b464a47d-5ffe-4dba-b323-2f41ecc60c83","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"not in aspects of story","passagePhrase":"the dialogue was 'flat' and the characterisations 'obvious"},{"uid":"5d38133c-fe4d-40f3-8f06-b6f503c11f5c","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"most powerful example of 3-D","passagePhrase":"has cemented the use of 3-D"},{"uid":"4c751513-b17d-460a-a6e9-100e3b6661bc 785ee64c-8585-485a-9580-b6d5a68d620e","qNum":"15 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"This is why all these 3-D venues were built"},{"uid":"4c751513-b17d-460a-a6e9-100e3b6661bc cff728e9-3d82-4aed-9f41-ca2a5026eb97","qNum":"15 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The holy grail of 3-D"},{"uid":"4c751513-b17d-460a-a6e9-100e3b6661bc","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"yet to arrive in cinemas","passagePhrase":"has finally arrived"},{"uid":"8a09f63d-29a5-4a46-b282-7c57a8a7b670","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"defence","passagePhrase":"embrace 3-D ... spices up a trip to the cinema ... adding a more active 'embodied' layer of experience ... this element"},{"uid":"edd22a57-1566-4bed-8360-191933edb7eb","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Effective use","passagePhrase":"is done well"},{"uid":"b2b0676f-16c0-496c-96eb-25246b486d7a","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"sensation of elevation","passagePhrase":"fear of heights"},{"uid":"8a09f63d-29a5-4a46-b282-7c57a8a7b670 a8ce3a2a-f2e7-48a5-8343-1b6b462c332e","qNum":"16 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"adds to"},{"uid":"9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Undesirable visual effects","passagePhrase":"many people ... this problem ... through the viewer trying to concentrate on unusual visual phenomena ... Eyestrains, headaches and nausea are therefore a problem for around 15% of a 3-D film audience"},{"uid":"8404b2c1-8009-4ab0-932b-95cfb39dd166 9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b","qNum":"17 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"go through life with"},{"uid":"9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b e9671f56-8823-466e-8a8f-a0f871208a84","qNum":"17 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"minor eye disturbances"},{"uid":"e9671f56-8823-466e-8a8f-a0f871208a84","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"visual disorder","passagePhrase":"—a slight muscular imbalance"},{"uid":"4caac4c1-1485-4b56-bcbb-c67e463b1559","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"3-D viewing","passagePhrase":"the experience of a 3-D movie"},{"uid":"1ea30fda-d14e-4129-b409-617fa9baefa8 9b30bd58-23be-457e-b0de-6336908f710b","qNum":"17 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"can be exacerbated"},{"uid":"203a5ae4-288f-4fdf-a030-b5e1a36e7193","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"conflicts","passagePhrase":"does not complement"},{"uid":"99aae8e8-27a3-4173-9295-fe2a0c63de2d","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"mental construct of our surroundings","passagePhrase":"the angles from which we take in the world"},{"uid":"548b9881-e0e0-4399-be64-64eab7adcc1c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"New technology","passagePhrase":"3-D"},{"uid":"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"diminishes","passagePhrase":"is detrimental to ... be counter-purposeful ... make the over-all effect seem clumsy and contrived ... dim the effect ... making 3-D films a slightly duller experience ... encourages film-makers to ... drama and narrative in favour of simply ... more"},{"uid":"3ae702ce-4abe-4ec9-b605-863470f9bc29","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"the art","passagePhrase":"good film-making"},{"uid":"1e1832ba-ba5b-4c22-99c7-d8a6ea7e091d","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"ordinary movies","passagePhrase":"2-D movies"},{"uid":"85973c1c-6dba-4f8e-8cf3-3d22e8c01ce6","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"already have the mental capacity","passagePhrase":"as far as our minds are concerned"},{"uid":"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d 1187fb8c-7507-4e73-a4a3-0cb4c16e7321","qNum":"18 21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"undercut ... piling on"},{"uid":"0ea64137-4035-4949-abdf-505ef0d4073d 29d8107e-0dd3-443a-85c4-d67d03416737","qNum":"18 21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"gimmicks and special effects"},{"uid":"1187fb8c-7507-4e73-a4a3-0cb4c16e7321","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"over-emphasis","passagePhrase":"in favour of"},{"uid":"0c9e8b50-ee34-47d2-a58d-7caf39362b68","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Good returns forecast for immediate future","passagePhrase":"benefited at the box office ... added sales ... commercial possibilities ... are not prepared to back down"},{"uid":"785ee64c-8585-485a-9580-b6d5a68d620e","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"of all time","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"29d8107e-0dd3-443a-85c4-d67d03416737","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"quick visual thrills","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"a8ce3a2a-f2e7-48a5-8343-1b6b462c332e","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"increase","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"1ea30fda-d14e-4129-b409-617fa9baefa8","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"worsen","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"8404b2c1-8009-4ab0-932b-95cfb39dd166","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"existing","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_123":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Does water have memory?</span></b></p><p><span>The practice of homeopathy was first developed by the German physician Samuel Hahnemann. During research in the 1790s, Hahnemann began experimenting with quinine, an alkaloid derived from cinchona bark that was well known at the time to have a positive effect on fever. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c1217f2e-a9a1-4127-83b7-2550bd76332d\">Hahnemann started dosing himself with quinine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c9e30259-0387-4522-836a-4c2958b5ce18\">in a state of good health<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c1217f2e-a9a1-4127-83b7-2550bd76332d\">reported in his journals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> that his extremities went cold, he experienced palpitations, an 'infinite anxiety', a trembling and weakening of the limbs, reddening cheeks and thirst—'in short', he concluded, '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ff5f01c4-4f63-4dde-b87b-f0bbcba3e046\">all the symptoms of relapsing fever presented themselves successively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>...' Hahnemann's main observation was that things which create problems for healthy people cure those problems in sick people, and this became his first principle of homeopathy: </span><i><span>simila similibus</span></i><span> (with help from the same). While diverging from the principle of apothecary practice at the time—which was </span><i><span>contraria contrariis</span></i><span> (with help from the opposite)—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d0adf02e-e617-48f3-8dd5-6f766bb47eff\">the efficacy of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> </span><i><span>simila similibus</span></i><span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"b7a4ab5d-f09d-43ac-887d-17c07341f599\">reaffirmed by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"73cde1ab-9ee7-41f4-8f9c-9310dba573ee\">subsequent developments in the field of vaccinations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Hahnemann's second principle was minimal dosing—treatments should be taken in the most diluted form at which they remain effective. This negated any possible toxic effects of </span><i><span>simila similibus</span></i><span> . In 1988 the French immunologist Jacques Benveniste took minimal dosing to new extremes when he published a paper in the prestigious scientific journal </span><i><span>Nature</span></i><span> in which he suggested that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"61880f38-5980-49ee-9539-d73e3e4fa78e\">very high dilutions of the anti-lgE antibody could affect human basophil granulocytes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"61880f38-5980-49ee-9539-d73e3e4fa78e\">the least common of the granulocytes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"61880f38-5980-49ee-9539-d73e3e4fa78e\">make up about 0.01% to 0.3% of white blood cells<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. The point of controversy, however, was that the water in Benveniste's test had been so diluted that any molecular evidence of the antibodies no longer existed. Water molecules, the researcher concluded, had a biologically active component that a journalist later termed 'water memory'. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"f4545f9a-7a21-4b16-a81e-ef40337fc55c\">A number of efforts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> from scientists in Britain, France and the Netherlands <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"f4545f9a-7a21-4b16-a81e-ef40337fc55c\">to duplicate Benveniste's research were unsuccessful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, however, and to this day <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"f4545f9a-7a21-4b16-a81e-ef40337fc55c\">no peer-reviewed study under broadly accepted conditions has been able to confirm the validity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of 'water memory'.</span></p><p><span>The third principle of homeopathy is 'the single remedy'. Exponents of this principle believe that it would be too difficult, if not impossible, to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e488f7d2-c018-4b52-bf96-a539555df6a2\">ascertain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"c3ba53c9-c9a2-45e1-9dbc-35d118c25b8e\">potential effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"bac66165-b9f8-4818-b5c3-3c859611c6a2\">multiple homeopathic remedies delivered simultaneously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. If it did work, they suggest, one could not know quite why it worked, turning homeopathy into an ambiguous guessing game. If it did not work, neither patient nor practitioner would know whether the ingredients were all ineffective, or whether they were only ineffective in combination with one another. Combination remedies are gaining in popularity, but classical homeopaths who rely on the single remedy approach warn these are not more potent, nor do they provide more treatment options. The availability of combination remedies, these homeopaths suggest, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"f957b050-bcb1-448f-a106-4b5027ab8281\">has been led by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"6ce8749a-a09a-4ad6-93e0-501b88ab59d8\">consumers wanting more options<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, not from homeopathic research indicating their efficacy.</span></p><p><span>Homeopathy is an extremely contentious form of medicine, with strong assertions coming from both critics and supporters of the practice. 'Homeopathy: There's nothing in it' announces the tagline to 10:23, a major British anti-homeopathy campaign. At 10.23 a.m. on 30 January 2010, over 400 supporters of the 10:23 stood outside Boots pharmacies and swallowed an entire bottle each of homeopathic pills in an attempt to raise awareness about the fact that these remedies are made of sugar and water, with no active <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"2ab9cfa5-4659-4f8e-b257-b2bd1f448df3\">components<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. This, defenders of homeopathy say, is entirely the point. Homeopathic products do not rely on ingredients that become toxic at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f47439c7-2bd2-4339-b4aa-d962108b18fc\">high doses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, because the water retains the 'memory' that allows the original treatment to function.</span></p><p><span>Critics also point out the fact that homeopathic preparations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0802f208-fa6b-442a-aed9-8bd6c9bd3d3e\">have no<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> systematic design to them, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"fa589d12-85ab-4f36-a2cf-7ca3baa7f501\">making it hard to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> monitor <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"a2a49b3c-bde8-4af9-a24b-2e02c1a53063\">whether or not a particular treatment has been efficacious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Homeopaths embrace this uncertainty. While results may be less certain, they argue, the non-toxic nature of homeopathy means that practitioner and patient <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"419b8781-ae62-4237-aa85-994ad4927977\">can experiment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> until they find something that works <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"c9e76a5e-7be4-4af2-b107-40587a9f33f1\">without concern for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> side effects. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"571d9ea3-1a84-4651-8ae9-43b148bc8595\">Traditional medicine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, they argue, assaults the body with a cocktail of drugs that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"6301f1af-0969-48ce-9862-85d24687943a\">only<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> tackles the symptoms of disease, while homeopathy has its sights aimed on the causes.</span></p><p><span>Homeopaths suggest this approach leads to kinder, gentler, more effective treatment. Finally, critics allege that when homeopathy has produced good results, these are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e2675446-a4c8-4f86-ba54-623f44c0d739\">exceedingly dependent on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> the placebo effect, and cannot justify the resources, time and expense that the homeopathic tradition absorbs. The placebo effect is a term that describes beneficial outcomes from a treatment than can be attributed to the patient's expectations concerning the treatment rather than from the treatment itself. Basically, the patient 'thinks' himself into feeling better. Defenders suggest that homeopathy can go beyond this psychological level. They point to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2f6fb6d1-b82b-4387-9dd9-8c699707cec1\">the successful results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> of homeopathy on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"5e27318f-06a8-4f0f-8f67-6fe1d3b2af7c\">patients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> who are unconscious at the time of treatment, as well as on animals.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-K, below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-K, in boxes 27-32.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"e488f7d2-c018-4b52-bf96-a539555df6a2\">avoid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"c3ba53c9-c9a2-45e1-9dbc-35d118c25b8e\">unpredictable outcomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"bac66165-b9f8-4818-b5c3-3c859611c6a2\">combining many remedies at once<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. explain the success of 18th century apothecary medicine.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ff5f01c4-4f63-4dde-b87b-f0bbcba3e046\">produce fever-like symptoms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c9e30259-0387-4522-836a-4c2958b5ce18\">in a healthy person<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. keep antibody molecules active in parts as low as 0.01%.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"b7a4ab5d-f09d-43ac-887d-17c07341f599\">support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"d0adf02e-e617-48f3-8dd5-6f766bb47eff\">the notion of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> </span><i><span>simila similibus</span></i><span> .</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. offer more remedial choice.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. produce a less effective dose.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"f4545f9a-7a21-4b16-a81e-ef40337fc55c\">recreate the original results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"61880f38-5980-49ee-9539-d73e3e4fa78e\">retain qualities of an antibody to which they were previously exposed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"J\"><span>J. satisfy the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"6ce8749a-a09a-4ad6-93e0-501b88ab59d8\">demand of buyers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"K\"><span>K. treat effectively someone with a fever.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37365\" id=\"question-wrapper-37365\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the late 18th century, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c1217f2e-a9a1-4127-83b7-2550bd76332d\">Hahnemann discovered that quinine was able to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37366\" id=\"question-wrapper-37366\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"73cde1ab-9ee7-41f4-8f9c-9310dba573ee\">effectiveness of vaccinations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> also helps to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37367\" id=\"question-wrapper-37367\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Benveniste argued in the journal Nature that water molecules possess the ability to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37368\" id=\"question-wrapper-37368\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"f4545f9a-7a21-4b16-a81e-ef40337fc55c\">Attempts to verify Benvenistes findings were unable to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37369\" id=\"question-wrapper-37369\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The purpose of the single remedy is to</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37370\" id=\"question-wrapper-37370\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Classical homeopaths suggest combination remedies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"f957b050-bcb1-448f-a106-4b5027ab8281\">have been created to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">J</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the table below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the text for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 33-40.</span></i></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"32\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Arguments against homeopathy</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"29\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Arguments for homeopathy</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"32\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Has no (33)____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"2ab9cfa5-4659-4f8e-b257-b2bd1f448df3\">ingredients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p></td><td colspan=\"29\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Does not become (34)______ when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"f47439c7-2bd2-4339-b4aa-d962108b18fc\">taken in large quantities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"32\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0802f208-fa6b-442a-aed9-8bd6c9bd3d3e\">Lack of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> a (35)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"fa589d12-85ab-4f36-a2cf-7ca3baa7f501\">makes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"a2a49b3c-bde8-4af9-a24b-2e02c1a53063\">success or failure of treatments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"fa589d12-85ab-4f36-a2cf-7ca3baa7f501\">difficult to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></span></p><p><span>(36)______</span></p></td><td colspan=\"29\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Remedies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"419b8781-ae62-4237-aa85-994ad4927977\">can be trialed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"c9e76a5e-7be4-4af2-b107-40587a9f33f1\">with no risk of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> (37)_____ ; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"571d9ea3-1a84-4651-8ae9-43b148bc8595\">treatments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> tackle causes and not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"6301f1af-0969-48ce-9862-85d24687943a\">just<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> (38)______ .</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"32\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"e2675446-a4c8-4f86-ba54-623f44c0d739\">Too much reliance on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> the (39)______ . Works psychologically but not physically.</span></p></td><td colspan=\"29\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2f6fb6d1-b82b-4387-9dd9-8c699707cec1\">Proven<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to work on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"5e27318f-06a8-4f0f-8f67-6fe1d3b2af7c\">people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> who are (40)______.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37371\" id=\"question-wrapper-37371\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ACTIVE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37372\" id=\"question-wrapper-37372\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TOXIC</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37373\" id=\"question-wrapper-37373\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SYSTEMATIC DESIGN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37374\" id=\"question-wrapper-37374\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MONITOR</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37375\" id=\"question-wrapper-37375\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SIDE-EFFECTS [OR] SIDE EFFECTS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37376\" id=\"question-wrapper-37376\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SYMPTOMS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37377\" id=\"question-wrapper-37377\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PLACEBO EFFECT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37378\" id=\"question-wrapper-37378\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">UNCONSCIOUS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c1217f2e-a9a1-4127-83b7-2550bd76332d","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Hahnemann discovered that quinine was able to","passagePhrase":"Hahnemann started dosing himself with quinine ... reported in his journals"},{"uid":"c9e30259-0387-4522-836a-4c2958b5ce18","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"in a healthy person","passagePhrase":"in a state of good health"},{"uid":"ff5f01c4-4f63-4dde-b87b-f0bbcba3e046","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"produce fever-like symptoms","passagePhrase":"all the symptoms of relapsing fever presented themselves successively"},{"uid":"d0adf02e-e617-48f3-8dd5-6f766bb47eff","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"the notion of","passagePhrase":"the efficacy of"},{"uid":"b7a4ab5d-f09d-43ac-887d-17c07341f599","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"support","passagePhrase":"reaffirmed by"},{"uid":"73cde1ab-9ee7-41f4-8f9c-9310dba573ee","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"effectiveness of vaccinations","passagePhrase":"subsequent developments in the field of vaccinations"},{"uid":"61880f38-5980-49ee-9539-d73e3e4fa78e","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"retain qualities of an antibody to which they were previously exposed","passagePhrase":"very high dilutions of the anti-lgE antibody could affect human basophil granulocytes ... the least common of the granulocytes ... make up about 0.01% to 0.3% of white blood cells"},{"uid":"f4545f9a-7a21-4b16-a81e-ef40337fc55c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"recreate the original results ... Attempts to verify Benvenistes findings were unable to","passagePhrase":"A number of efforts ... to duplicate Benveniste's research were unsuccessful ... no peer-reviewed study under broadly accepted conditions has been able to confirm the validity"},{"uid":"e488f7d2-c018-4b52-bf96-a539555df6a2","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"avoid","passagePhrase":"ascertain"},{"uid":"c3ba53c9-c9a2-45e1-9dbc-35d118c25b8e","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"unpredictable outcomes","passagePhrase":"potential effects"},{"uid":"bac66165-b9f8-4818-b5c3-3c859611c6a2","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"combining many remedies at once","passagePhrase":"multiple homeopathic remedies delivered simultaneously"},{"uid":"f957b050-bcb1-448f-a106-4b5027ab8281","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"have been created to","passagePhrase":"has been led by"},{"uid":"6ce8749a-a09a-4ad6-93e0-501b88ab59d8","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"demand of buyers","passagePhrase":"consumers wanting more options"},{"uid":"2ab9cfa5-4659-4f8e-b257-b2bd1f448df3","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"ingredients","passagePhrase":"components"},{"uid":"f47439c7-2bd2-4339-b4aa-d962108b18fc","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"taken in large quantities","passagePhrase":"high doses"},{"uid":"0802f208-fa6b-442a-aed9-8bd6c9bd3d3e","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Lack of","passagePhrase":"have no"},{"uid":"fa589d12-85ab-4f36-a2cf-7ca3baa7f501","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"makes ... difficult to","passagePhrase":"making it hard to"},{"uid":"a2a49b3c-bde8-4af9-a24b-2e02c1a53063","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"success or failure of treatments","passagePhrase":"whether or not a particular treatment has been efficacious"},{"uid":"419b8781-ae62-4237-aa85-994ad4927977","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"can be trialed","passagePhrase":"can experiment"},{"uid":"c9e76a5e-7be4-4af2-b107-40587a9f33f1","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"with no risk of","passagePhrase":"without concern for"},{"uid":"571d9ea3-1a84-4651-8ae9-43b148bc8595","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"treatments","passagePhrase":"Traditional medicine"},{"uid":"6301f1af-0969-48ce-9862-85d24687943a","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"just","passagePhrase":"only"},{"uid":"e2675446-a4c8-4f86-ba54-623f44c0d739","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Too much reliance on","passagePhrase":"exceedingly dependent on"},{"uid":"2f6fb6d1-b82b-4387-9dd9-8c699707cec1","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Proven","passagePhrase":"the successful results"},{"uid":"5e27318f-06a8-4f0f-8f67-6fe1d3b2af7c","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"people","passagePhrase":"patients"}]},"reading_u2_124":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>The way in which information is taught</span></b></p><p><span>The way in which information is taught can vary greatly across cultures and time-periods. Entering a British primary school classroom from the early 1900s, for example, one gains a sense of austerity, discipline and a rigid way of teaching. Desks are typically seated apart from one another, with straight-backed wooden chairs that face directly to the teacher and the chalkboard. In the present day, British classrooms look very different. Desks are often grouped together so that students face each other rather than the teacher, and a large floor area is typically set aside for the class to come together for group discussion and learning.</span></p><p><span>Traditionally, it was felt that teachers should be in firm control of the learning process, and that the teacher's task was to prepare and present material for students to understand. Within this approach, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"44cbbc37-bb8d-40b0-acf2-daf98f951e5d\">the relationship students have with their teachers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"6fbbc7e4-c30a-47ee-973f-5bab7e48ea7d\">not considered important<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> , nor is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"196fd363-a215-4575-b6df-93fcee1c7831\">the relationship students have with each other<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> in the classroom. A student's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"dfd2cfc8-1be8-486f-ba51-f82a6453a6de\">participation in class is likely to be minimal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, aside from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"dfd2cfc8-1be8-486f-ba51-f82a6453a6de\">asking questions directed at the teacher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"dfd2cfc8-1be8-486f-ba51-f82a6453a6de\">responding to questions that the teacher has directed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> at the student. This style encourages students to develop respect for positions of power as a source of control and discipline. It is frequently described as the 'formal authority' model of teaching.</span></p><p><span>A less rigid form of teacher-centred education is the 'demonstrator' model. This maintains the formal authority model's notion of the teacher as a 'flashlight' who illuminates the material for his or her class to learn, but emphasises a more individualised approach to form. The demonstrator acts as both a role model and a guide, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"e27ab5dc-5892-4710-98d9-82813a7f055b\">demonstrating skills and processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and then helping students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"16dcd847-a597-48fe-9e23-3542461a109a\">develop and apply these independently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Instructors who are drawn to the demonstrator style are generally confident that their own way of performing a task represents a good base model, but they are sensitive to differing learning styles and expect to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"5a9443b6-8c69-4e3a-9426-a6f0cf2e4d52\">provide students with help on an individual basis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Many education researchers argue for student-centred learning instead, and suggest that the learning process is more successful when students are in control. Within the student-centred paradigm, the 'delegator' style is popular. The delegator teacher maintains general authority, but they delegate much of the responsibility for learning to the class as a way for students to become independent thinkers who take pride in their own work. Students are often encouraged to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a6c261d6-7f2d-43a4-a0d9-3f82189491f4\">work on their own or in groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, and if the delegator style is implemented successfully they will build not only a working knowledge of course specific topics, but also serf-discipline and the ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a6c261d6-7f2d-43a4-a0d9-3f82189491f4\">co-ordinate group work and interpersonal roles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Another style that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b343e55e-640f-4a38-a3a2-9a5b5932c835\">emphasises<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> student-centred education is the 'facilitator' mode of learning. Here, while a set of specific curriculum demands are already in place, students are encouraged to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b7273464-1c76-48c4-9a72-ff0fd51def66\">take the initiative for creating ways to meet these learning requirements together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. The teacher typically designs activities that encourage active learning, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"961c48a6-d554-45ae-b0b4-be50d4e72a19\">group collaboration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> and problem solving, and students are encouraged to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"a052753c-50c4-4a4c-930b-80d8d5c9cc41\">process and apply the course content in creative and original ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. Whereas the delegator style <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"91479f2f-11ff-489e-8a88-c896c243c955\">emphasises<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> content, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"69e7da8f-afee-40fc-91ee-df8a63de9b0d\">the responsibility students can have for generating and directing their own knowledge base<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, the facilitator style emphasises form, and the fluid and diverse possibilities that are available in the process of learning. Until the 1960s,formal authority was common in almost all Western <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"01492c3b-6c6e-421f-9ed1-3705f1329f2c\">schools and universities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. As a professor would enter a university lecture theatre, a student would be expected to rush up, take his bag to the desk, and pull out the chair for the professor to sit down on . This style <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"4e4cfbc8-c6c4-422f-9962-090a3120ab36\">has become outmoded over time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Now at university, students and professors typically have more relaxed, collegiate relationships, address each other on a first name basis, and acknowledge that students have much to contribute in class. Teacher-centred education has a lingering appeal in the form of the demonstrator style, however, which remains useful in subjects where skills must be demonstrated to an external standard and the learning process remains fixed in the earlier years of education. A student of mathematics, sewing or metalwork will likely be familiar with the demonstrator style. At the highest levels of education, however, the demonstrator approach must be abandoned in all fields as students are required to produce innovative work that makes unique contributions to knowledge. Thesis and doctoral students lead their own research in facilitation with supervisors.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"d27ed5e4-e823-428e-b330-f8c6f665c70f\">The delegator style is valuable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> when the course is likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"d27ed5e4-e823-428e-b330-f8c6f665c70f\">lead students to careers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> that require group projects. Often, someone who has a high level of expertise in a particular field does not make for the best employee because they have not learnt to apply their abilities in a co-ordinated manner. The delegator style confronts this problem by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"c8f31265-adcb-4b20-adc1-ea089cb2c8f8\">recognising that interpersonal communication is not just a means to learning but an important skill set in itself<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. The facilitator model is probably the most creative model, and is therefore not suited to subjects where the practical component necessitates a careful and highly disciplined manner, such as training to be a medical practitioner. It may, however, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"96a430f1-1787-40cd-9779-213f1bb1652e\">suit more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> experimental and theoretical fields ranging from English, music and the social sciences,to science and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a97cabb2-0c28-4f09-9a42-9ab3192b3107\">medical valuable research that takes place in research labs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. In these areas, 'mistakes' in form are important and aspects of the learning and development process.</span></p><p><span>Overall, a dear evolution has taken place in the West from a rigid, dogmatic and teacher-dominated way of learning, to a flexible, creative and student-centred approach. Nevertheless, different subjects, ages and skill levels suit different styles of teaching, and it is unlikely that there will ever be one recommended approach for everyone.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 1-8) and the styles of teaching below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Match each statement with the correct teaching style, AD.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, AD, in boxes 1-8.</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NB</span></b></i><i><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of Teaching Styles</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Formal authority</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Demonstrator</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Delegator</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Facilitator</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37409\" id=\"question-wrapper-37409\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"b343e55e-640f-4a38-a3a2-9a5b5932c835\">The emphasis is on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"69e7da8f-afee-40fc-91ee-df8a63de9b0d\">students directing the learning process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37410\" id=\"question-wrapper-37410\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The teacher <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"e27ab5dc-5892-4710-98d9-82813a7f055b\">shows the class how to do something<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, then students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"16dcd847-a597-48fe-9e23-3542461a109a\">try it on their own<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37411\" id=\"question-wrapper-37411\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"44cbbc37-bb8d-40b0-acf2-daf98f951e5d\">Student-teacher interaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"196fd363-a215-4575-b6df-93fcee1c7831\">student-student interaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"6fbbc7e4-c30a-47ee-973f-5bab7e48ea7d\">limited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37412\" id=\"question-wrapper-37412\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"91479f2f-11ff-489e-8a88-c896c243c955\">The emphasis is on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"b7273464-1c76-48c4-9a72-ff0fd51def66\">the process of solving problems together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37413\" id=\"question-wrapper-37413\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Students are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"dfd2cfc8-1be8-486f-ba51-f82a6453a6de\">expected to adjust to the teachers way of presenting information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37414\" id=\"question-wrapper-37414\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The teacher designs <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"961c48a6-d554-45ae-b0b4-be50d4e72a19\">group activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> that encourage <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"a052753c-50c4-4a4c-930b-80d8d5c9cc41\">constructive interaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37415\" id=\"question-wrapper-37415\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"5a9443b6-8c69-4e3a-9426-a6f0cf2e4d52\">Time is set aside for one-on-one instruction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> between teacher and student.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37416\" id=\"question-wrapper-37416\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a6c261d6-7f2d-43a4-a0d9-3f82189491f4\">Group and individual work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> is encouraged independently of the teacher.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></i></p><p><i><span>In boxes 9-12, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>TRUE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>FALSE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if there is no information on this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37417\" id=\"question-wrapper-37417\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The formal authority model <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"4e4cfbc8-c6c4-422f-9962-090a3120ab36\">remains popular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"01492c3b-6c6e-421f-9ed1-3705f1329f2c\">educational institutions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of the West.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37418\" id=\"question-wrapper-37418\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The demonstrator model is never used at tertiary level.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37419\" id=\"question-wrapper-37419\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"d27ed5e4-e823-428e-b330-f8c6f665c70f\">Graduates of delegator style teaching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"c8f31265-adcb-4b20-adc1-ea089cb2c8f8\">good communicators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37420\" id=\"question-wrapper-37420\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The facilitator style is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"96a430f1-1787-40cd-9779-213f1bb1652e\">not appropriate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"a97cabb2-0c28-4f09-9a42-9ab3192b3107\">the field of medicine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in box 13.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37421\" id=\"question-wrapper-37421\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the best title for Reading Passage 1?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Teaching styles and their application</li> <li>B. Teaching: then and now</li> <li>C. When students become teachers</li> <li>D. Why student-centred learning is best</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"44cbbc37-bb8d-40b0-acf2-daf98f951e5d","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Student-teacher interaction","passagePhrase":"the relationship students have with their teachers"},{"uid":"6fbbc7e4-c30a-47ee-973f-5bab7e48ea7d","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"limited","passagePhrase":"not considered important"},{"uid":"196fd363-a215-4575-b6df-93fcee1c7831","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"student-student interaction","passagePhrase":"the relationship students have with each other"},{"uid":"dfd2cfc8-1be8-486f-ba51-f82a6453a6de","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"expected to adjust to the teachers way of presenting information","passagePhrase":"participation in class is likely to be minimal ... asking questions directed at the teacher ... responding to questions that the teacher has directed"},{"uid":"e27ab5dc-5892-4710-98d9-82813a7f055b","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"shows the class how to do something","passagePhrase":"demonstrating skills and processes"},{"uid":"16dcd847-a597-48fe-9e23-3542461a109a","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"try it on their own","passagePhrase":"develop and apply these independently"},{"uid":"5a9443b6-8c69-4e3a-9426-a6f0cf2e4d52","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Time is set aside for one-on-one instruction","passagePhrase":"provide students with help on an individual basis"},{"uid":"a6c261d6-7f2d-43a4-a0d9-3f82189491f4","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Group and individual work","passagePhrase":"work on their own or in groups ... co-ordinate group work and interpersonal roles"},{"uid":"b343e55e-640f-4a38-a3a2-9a5b5932c835","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"The emphasis is on","passagePhrase":"emphasises"},{"uid":"b7273464-1c76-48c4-9a72-ff0fd51def66","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"the process of solving problems together","passagePhrase":"take the initiative for creating ways to meet these learning requirements together"},{"uid":"961c48a6-d554-45ae-b0b4-be50d4e72a19","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"group activities","passagePhrase":"group collaboration"},{"uid":"a052753c-50c4-4a4c-930b-80d8d5c9cc41","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"constructive interaction","passagePhrase":"process and apply the course content in creative and original ways"},{"uid":"91479f2f-11ff-489e-8a88-c896c243c955","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"The emphasis is on","passagePhrase":"emphasises"},{"uid":"69e7da8f-afee-40fc-91ee-df8a63de9b0d","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"students directing the learning process","passagePhrase":"the responsibility students can have for generating and directing their own knowledge base"},{"uid":"01492c3b-6c6e-421f-9ed1-3705f1329f2c","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"educational institutions","passagePhrase":"schools and universities"},{"uid":"d27ed5e4-e823-428e-b330-f8c6f665c70f","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Graduates of delegator style teaching","passagePhrase":"The delegator style is valuable ... lead students to careers"},{"uid":"c8f31265-adcb-4b20-adc1-ea089cb2c8f8","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"good communicators","passagePhrase":"recognising that interpersonal communication is not just a means to learning but an important skill set in itself"},{"uid":"a97cabb2-0c28-4f09-9a42-9ab3192b3107","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"the field of medicine","passagePhrase":"medical valuable research that takes place in research labs"}]},"reading_u2_125":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>The Flavour Industry</span></b></p><p><span>A. Read through the nutritional information on the food in your <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"adc57065-ad69-404d-9eac-6301bb9c4703\">freezer, refrigerator or kitchen pantry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, and you are likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ccbef6a8-0e70-4237-b56f-4fc0c043bfbf\">find<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> a simple, innocuous-looking ingredient <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ccbef6a8-0e70-4237-b56f-4fc0c043bfbf\">recurring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> on a number of products: 'natural flavour'. The story of what natural flavour is, how it got into your food, and where it came from, is the result of more complex processes than you might imagine.</span></p><p><span>B. During the 1980s, health watchdogs and nutritionists began turning their attention to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0c0deb44-4dcc-4a39-97c2-69835fee4174\">cholesterol<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, a waxy steroid metabolite that we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0c0deb44-4dcc-4a39-97c2-69835fee4174\">mainly consume from animal-sourced products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> such as cheese, egg yolks, beef, poultry, shrimp and pork. Nutritionists blamed cholesterol for contributing to the growing rates of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"bc62ca02-e19d-4136-bc53-826c4adc5aea\">obesity, heart disease, diabetes and several cancers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in Western societies. As <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"b2c756de-4adc-43e3-a93c-dc33ff3afcf6\">extensive recognition of the matter grew amongst the common people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e22c2559-5b68-478e-af70-1ed64fb8e281\">McDonalds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"ab755bf8-7b73-4d76-880f-f3180d6a6637\">stopped cooking their French fries in a mixture of cottonseed oil and beef tallow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, and in 1990 the The restaurant chain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"ab755bf8-7b73-4d76-880f-f3180d6a6637\">began using 100% vegetable oil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> instead.</span></p><p><span>C. This substantially <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"77159cc8-9717-46c9-9bba-912b4757e09f\">lowered the amount of cholesterol in McDonalds' fries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, but it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3ab13f85-a74c-458a-968a-73a42e4a7e41\">created<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> a new <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"d77ce2d8-aa1a-436e-98b6-ac4174a070ec\">dilemma<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. The beef tallow and cottonseed oil mixture gave the French fries high cholesterol content, but it also gifted them with a rich aroma and 'mouth-feel ' that even James Beard, an American food critic, admitted he enjoyed. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"95e89b73-333c-42ba-9515-8f79217b77d7\">Pure vegetable oil is bland<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in comparison. Looking at the current ingredients' list of McDonalds' French fries, however, it is easy to see how they overcame this predicament. Aside from a few preservatives, there are essentially three main ingredients: potato, soybean oil, and the mysterious component of 'natural flavour'.</span></p><p><span>D. Natural flavour also entered our diet through the rise in processed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"b5dfb873-190f-4687-a3fd-f3a977ca3bad\">foods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, which now make up over 90% (and growing) of the American diet, as well as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"29d1d3fb-ef40-4b4e-b60b-84869da297db\">representing a burgeoning industry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in developing countries such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"05059bb3-5aad-4c98-84d2-65f8b77ba8d6\">China and India<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. Processed foods are essentially any foods that have been boxed, bagged, canned or packaged, and have a list of ingredients on the label. Sometimes, the processing involves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"97e13c4a-2c76-4211-a938-ef4bb5afe615\">adding a little sodium or sugar, and a few preservatives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Often, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"97e13c4a-2c76-4211-a938-ef4bb5afe615\">it is coloured, bleached , stabilised, emulsified, dehydrated, odour-concealed and sweetened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. This process <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"5c443b20-45e2-4a44-8da7-a486cede45bb\">typically<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"19 25\" data-uid=\"14d6cb42-f3b8-4c12-aaa8-0c7ef661f11e 97e13c4a-2c76-4211-a938-ef4bb5afe615\">saps any original flavour out of the product</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, and so, of course, flavour must be added back in as well.</span></p><p><span>E. Often this is 'natural flavour', but while the term may bring to mind images of fresh barley, hand-ground spices and dried herbs being traded in a bustling street market, most of these natural sources are in fact <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"b9f9c6c4-7ddd-4f1b-b5a6-a59bba29d6f9\">engineered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to culinary perfection in a set of factories and plants off the New Jersey Turnpike outside of New York. Here, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3dc7b9d6-1a6c-439b-a5be-4d414f3ba7bc\">firms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e8ab6bd0-37c8-4a34-a076-a7587394ad83\">such as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> International Flavors &amp; Fragrances, Harmen &amp; Reimer, Flavor Dynamics, Frutarom and Elan Chemical isolate and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"b9f9c6c4-7ddd-4f1b-b5a6-a59bba29d6f9\">manufacture the tastes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> that are incorporated in much of what we eat and drink. The sweet, summery burst of naturally squeezed orange juice, the wood-smoked aroma in barbeque sauces, and the creamy, buttery, fresh taste in many dairy products do not come from sundrenched meadows or backyard grills, but are formed in the labs and test tubes of these flavour industry giants.</span></p><p><span>F. The scientists—dubbed 'flavourists'—who create the potent chemicals that set our olfactory senses to overdrive use a mix of techniques that have been refined over many years. Part of it is dense, intricate chemistry: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"aecbc5ac-c669-4e3f-aa5a-3aa8aa88d97a\">spectrometers, gas chromatographs and headspace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> -vapour analysers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"e84e128b-3bdf-40d3-ac4f-c85de5c79dca\">can<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"d0d8d884-f68d-4fe0-910c-cbab9b8d4a15\">break down components of a flavour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in amounts as minute as one part per billion. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"bb577ed5-b8cd-4c43-9628-7a6e84832e4d\">Not to be outdone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, however, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"64e129a5-1dfb-48ec-a895-c068957b5e5b\">human<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> nose can isolate aromas down to three parts per trillion. Flavourists therefore consider their work as much an art as a science, and flavourism requires a nose 'trained' with a delicate and poetic sense of balance.</span></p><p><span>G. Should we be wary of the industrialisation of natural flavour? On its own, the trend may not present any clear reason for alarm. Nutritionists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"978c189b-b5f8-4045-b92e-40877866f0d9\">widely agree<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that the real assault on health in the last few decades stems from an 'unholy trinity' of sugar, fat and sodium in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"69fb9399-34b9-4868-bb31-1a3466486a76\">processed foods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"28497ec1-ed25-4590-af14-4d3c2188f981\">Natural flavour on its own is not a health risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. It does play a role, however, in helping these processed foods to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"d48c3db9-3e25-4142-bee4-2bff16dc82cd\">taste fresh and nutritious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, even when they are not. So while the natural flavour industry should not be considered the culprit, we might think of it as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"28497ec1-ed25-4590-af14-4d3c2188f981\">a willing accomplice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-G.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 14-21.</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NB</span></b></i><i><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37422\" id=\"question-wrapper-37422\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e8ab6bd0-37c8-4a34-a076-a7587394ad83\">examples<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3dc7b9d6-1a6c-439b-a5be-4d414f3ba7bc\">companies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"b9f9c6c4-7ddd-4f1b-b5a6-a59bba29d6f9\">create natural flavours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37423\" id=\"question-wrapper-37423\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an instance of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"e22c2559-5b68-478e-af70-1ed64fb8e281\">multi-national franchise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"ab755bf8-7b73-4d76-880f-f3180d6a6637\">responding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"b2c756de-4adc-43e3-a93c-dc33ff3afcf6\">public pressure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37424\" id=\"question-wrapper-37424\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"978c189b-b5f8-4045-b92e-40877866f0d9\">statement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"28497ec1-ed25-4590-af14-4d3c2188f981\">health effects of natural flavours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37425\" id=\"question-wrapper-37425\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an instance where a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"77159cc8-9717-46c9-9bba-912b4757e09f\">solution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3ab13f85-a74c-458a-968a-73a42e4a7e41\">turns into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"d77ce2d8-aa1a-436e-98b6-ac4174a070ec\">problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37426\" id=\"question-wrapper-37426\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"adc57065-ad69-404d-9eac-6301bb9c4703\">place in the home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> where one may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"ccbef6a8-0e70-4237-b56f-4fc0c043bfbf\">encounter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the term natural flavour</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37427\" id=\"question-wrapper-37427\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>details about the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"97e13c4a-2c76-4211-a938-ef4bb5afe615\">transformation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> that takes place in processed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"b5dfb873-190f-4687-a3fd-f3a977ca3bad\">grocery items<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37428\" id=\"question-wrapper-37428\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"bb577ed5-b8cd-4c43-9628-7a6e84832e4d\">comparison<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"64e129a5-1dfb-48ec-a895-c068957b5e5b\">personal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"aecbc5ac-c669-4e3f-aa5a-3aa8aa88d97a\">technological<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"e84e128b-3bdf-40d3-ac4f-c85de5c79dca\">abilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"d0d8d884-f68d-4fe0-910c-cbab9b8d4a15\">flavour detection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37429\" id=\"question-wrapper-37429\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0c0deb44-4dcc-4a39-97c2-69835fee4174\">diet-related<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"bc62ca02-e19d-4136-bc53-826c4adc5aea\">health conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 22-25, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>TRUE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>FALSE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if there is no information on this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37430\" id=\"question-wrapper-37430\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"95e89b73-333c-42ba-9515-8f79217b77d7\">On their own, vegetable oils do not have a strong flavour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37431\" id=\"question-wrapper-37431\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Soybean oil is lower in cholesterol than cottonseed oil.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37432\" id=\"question-wrapper-37432\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Processed foods are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"29d1d3fb-ef40-4b4e-b60b-84869da297db\">becoming more popular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"05059bb3-5aad-4c98-84d2-65f8b77ba8d6\">in some Asian countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37433\" id=\"question-wrapper-37433\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"5c443b20-45e2-4a44-8da7-a486cede45bb\">All<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> food processing <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"14d6cb42-f3b8-4c12-aaa8-0c7ef661f11e\">involves the use of added flavourings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in box 26.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37434\" id=\"question-wrapper-37434\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer of Reading Passage 2 concludes that natural flavours</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. are the major cause of dietary health problems.</li> <li>B. are unhealthy, but not as bad as sugar, fat and sodium.</li> <li>C. have health benefits that other ingredients tend to cancel out.</li> <li>D. help make <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"69fb9399-34b9-4868-bb31-1a3466486a76\">unhealthy foods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"d48c3db9-3e25-4142-bee4-2bff16dc82cd\">taste better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"adc57065-ad69-404d-9eac-6301bb9c4703","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"place in the home","passagePhrase":"freezer, refrigerator or kitchen pantry"},{"uid":"ccbef6a8-0e70-4237-b56f-4fc0c043bfbf","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"encounter","passagePhrase":"find ... recurring"},{"uid":"0c0deb44-4dcc-4a39-97c2-69835fee4174","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"diet-related","passagePhrase":"cholesterol ... mainly consume from animal-sourced products"},{"uid":"bc62ca02-e19d-4136-bc53-826c4adc5aea","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"health conditions","passagePhrase":"obesity, heart disease, diabetes and several cancers"},{"uid":"b2c756de-4adc-43e3-a93c-dc33ff3afcf6","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"public pressure","passagePhrase":"extensive recognition of the matter grew amongst the common people"},{"uid":"e22c2559-5b68-478e-af70-1ed64fb8e281","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"multi-national franchise","passagePhrase":"McDonalds"},{"uid":"ab755bf8-7b73-4d76-880f-f3180d6a6637","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"responding","passagePhrase":"stopped cooking their French fries in a mixture of cottonseed oil and beef tallow ... began using 100% vegetable oil"},{"uid":"77159cc8-9717-46c9-9bba-912b4757e09f","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"solution","passagePhrase":"lowered the amount of cholesterol in McDonalds' fries"},{"uid":"3ab13f85-a74c-458a-968a-73a42e4a7e41","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"turns into","passagePhrase":"created"},{"uid":"d77ce2d8-aa1a-436e-98b6-ac4174a070ec","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"problem","passagePhrase":"dilemma"},{"uid":"95e89b73-333c-42ba-9515-8f79217b77d7","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"On their own, vegetable oils do not have a strong flavour","passagePhrase":"Pure vegetable oil is bland"},{"uid":"b5dfb873-190f-4687-a3fd-f3a977ca3bad","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"grocery items","passagePhrase":"foods"},{"uid":"29d1d3fb-ef40-4b4e-b60b-84869da297db","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"becoming more popular","passagePhrase":"representing a burgeoning industry"},{"uid":"05059bb3-5aad-4c98-84d2-65f8b77ba8d6","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"in some Asian countries","passagePhrase":"China and India"},{"uid":"97e13c4a-2c76-4211-a938-ef4bb5afe615","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"transformation","passagePhrase":"adding a little sodium or sugar, and a few preservatives ... it is coloured, bleached , stabilised, emulsified, dehydrated, odour-concealed and sweetened"},{"uid":"14d6cb42-f3b8-4c12-aaa8-0c7ef661f11e 97e13c4a-2c76-4211-a938-ef4bb5afe615","qNum":"19 25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"saps any original flavour out of the product"},{"uid":"b9f9c6c4-7ddd-4f1b-b5a6-a59bba29d6f9","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"create natural flavours","passagePhrase":"engineered ... manufacture the tastes"},{"uid":"3dc7b9d6-1a6c-439b-a5be-4d414f3ba7bc","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"companies","passagePhrase":"firms"},{"uid":"e8ab6bd0-37c8-4a34-a076-a7587394ad83","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"examples","passagePhrase":"such as"},{"uid":"aecbc5ac-c669-4e3f-aa5a-3aa8aa88d97a","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"technological","passagePhrase":"spectrometers, gas chromatographs and headspace"},{"uid":"e84e128b-3bdf-40d3-ac4f-c85de5c79dca","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"abilities","passagePhrase":"can"},{"uid":"d0d8d884-f68d-4fe0-910c-cbab9b8d4a15","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"flavour detection","passagePhrase":"break down components of a flavour"},{"uid":"bb577ed5-b8cd-4c43-9628-7a6e84832e4d","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"comparison","passagePhrase":"Not to be outdone"},{"uid":"64e129a5-1dfb-48ec-a895-c068957b5e5b","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"personal","passagePhrase":"human"},{"uid":"978c189b-b5f8-4045-b92e-40877866f0d9","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"statement","passagePhrase":"widely agree"},{"uid":"69fb9399-34b9-4868-bb31-1a3466486a76","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"unhealthy foods","passagePhrase":"processed foods"},{"uid":"28497ec1-ed25-4590-af14-4d3c2188f981","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"health effects of natural flavours","passagePhrase":"Natural flavour on its own is not a health risk ... a willing accomplice"},{"uid":"d48c3db9-3e25-4142-bee4-2bff16dc82cd","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"taste better","passagePhrase":"taste fresh and nutritious"}]},"reading_u2_126":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Austerity Measures</span></b></p><p><span>Austerity measures are actions that a state undertakes in order to pay back its creditors. These measures typically involve <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"1430cb6e-c86e-47bf-adf8-ae25e6c8c9ca\">slashing government expenditure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2f339d7c-867b-4acc-b089-54c988830dfd\">hiking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> taxes, and most of the time these are imposed on a country when its national deficit is believed to have become unsustainable. In this situation, banks may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"dd875fea-6d37-4e33-94c0-df0e65b36ee2\">lose trust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"aa5d122d-d662-459a-b25e-0fd7e6fde2a3\">government's ability or willingness to repay existing debts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, and in return can refuse to roll over current loans and demand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"00cf6de9-379b-4bc7-9dc7-57261553f900\">cripplingly excessive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> interest rates on new lending. Governments frequently then turn to the International Monetary Fund ( IMF), an inter-governmental organisation that functions as a lender of last resort. In return, the IMF typically demands austerity measures so that the indebted country is able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"bff1bd82-94c3-4d83-b924-6c66a4db9be6\">curtail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> its budget deficit and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"da9423f5-c7ac-49db-94fe-802db54b7876\">fulfil their loan<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> obligations.</span></p><p><span>A wave of austerity measures across Europe in 2010 has seen cuts and freezes to pensions, welfare and public sector salaries as well as hikes to some taxes and excises. The Greek programme attempts to narrow its budget shortfall from 8.1 percent of GDP in 2010 to 2.6 percent of GDP in 2014 primarily by freezing public sector incomes during that period and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 33 34 35\" data-uid=\"3dedce85-c6e3-43b7-b9f3-1789297000f1 d43ebb73-1ef3-4e83-9939-651b09c0cb56 e685c9d6-f661-4a93-ae8a-15dc97083d4f f67a36e1-977e-4c53-b02f-3f84df1b96a5\">reducing public sector allowances by 8 percent</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Additionally, VAT—the Greek <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 33 34 35\" data-uid=\"2d483411-e69f-4d02-9edd-e7024d0da986 6c2a0063-aad1-4f08-ad8f-4e248aeff2ab 8445d5bb-9b58-4e8f-b57d-fe9c4eba220f e50522f6-81c5-406e-bb6d-52e04d5373ec\">sales tax—will be elevated to 23 percent</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 33 34 35\" data-uid=\"06beca80-a63e-48be-95f5-aac33be6eb57 960d0320-4c09-4de7-ad56-b8010e326ce5 b19f67f2-525f-402f-b4d7-b81cbb049df0 ba3b289f-9b5f-416d-8d2b-b3350f010edb\">excises on fuel, tobacco and alcohol are also subject to an increase</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 33 34 35\" data-uid=\"4a37839b-2cbe-4fc5-8723-e3e9b6fafe20 65260ff8-12b9-4e58-9dcf-513a66bc8fef 772cf5a8-2962-4150-8110-172d086860b4 cc32d86e-5991-495a-bc55-ebbfec51c3e6\">The statutory retirement age for women will be raised to 65, matching it with the current retirement age for men</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. These reforms have been deeply unpopular in Greece, prompting a succession of general strikes that have further dented the economy.</span></p><p><span>IMF-imposed austerity measures have been indicted for encouraging the deep recession following the Asian financial crisis of 1997. Starting from the early 1990s, international investors from wealthier countries such as Japan and the United States began pouring money into Southeast Asia, looking to make some quick returns, and the soaring economies of Thailand, Philippines, Malaysia and others earned themselves the title 'the Asian tigers'. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"dfb13bac-b47b-4c4e-807d-46332ac3caa2\">When things started to turn sour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, however, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"2384dcca-f889-4d76-801f-70e20a039f9d\">foreign investors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> panicked and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"1eb52c12-06a8-4033-984c-29641f4f5619\">retracted their investments en masse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"bec986bc-2e6f-44f6-b537-a8bce353f441\">decimating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> Asian currencies and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"05f8b5a5-50da-4586-bc9f-a240e9ba8446\">turning millions of employees out of work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. The IMF's role in the recovery was to impose austerity measures that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"01d338bc-10d6-439d-99ed-349ba98c6802\">kept interest rates high<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"f18834cb-5ec3-4dc7-afa4-7a5be23d7759\">driving down wages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> and labour standards at a time when workers were already suffering.According to one former IMF economist, these interventions on a global scale have caused the deaths of 6 million children every year.</span></p><p><span>Many economists consequently view austerity measures as a terrible blunder. John Maynard Keynes was the first to propose an alternative method, long before the Asian financial crisis. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"451c1b00-a22c-4f04-b7be-c85ddea5c0fe\">Governments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, he attempted to demonstrate, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"451c1b00-a22c-4f04-b7be-c85ddea5c0fe\">could conceivably spend their national economy out of debt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Although logically implausible at first blush, this argument is based on the notion that recessions deepen from a persistent cycle of low incomes, low consumer spending and low business growth. A government can theoretically reverse this downward spiral by injecting the economy with much needed (albeit borrowed) capital . This is not equivalent to an indebted consumer spending further into the red, Keynes argued, because while the consumer gains no further income on that expenditure, the government's dollar goes into the economy and then partially boomerangs later on in the form of taxation.</span></p><p><span>Nobel-prize winning economist Joseph Stiglitz follows up on this approach by noting that households across the world are currently burdened with debt. For businesses to grow, he argues, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"a99b34ff-54a3-445c-9127-8e7a7cfa4c64\">government and consumer expenditure must kick in first<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Austerity measures lower the spending capacity of households , and are therefore considered under-productive. Another recipient of the Nobel Prize, Paul Krugman, points to the recent experiences of countries such as Ireland, Latvia and Estonia. Countries that implement austerity are the 'good soldiers' of the crisis, he notes , implementing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"88605a71-99cc-4f82-a41a-6afa2747cf64\">savage spending cuts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. 'But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"c1fb4ea1-39d6-4ee6-9fd7-0296eafda6a6\">their reward has been a slump<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>—and financial markets continue to treat them as a serious default risk'.</span></p><p><span>In the United Kingdom, Prime Minister David Cameron defended the necessity of austerity measures for his country by denouncing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"75bb317d-112f-4be9-bb24-bb4cc4b5752b\">the frivolity of governments that ratchet up spending at a time the economy is contracting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. This is in line with the counter-Keynesian viewpoint, known broadly as the neoclassical position. Neoclassical economists argue that business is 'inspired' by fiscally conservative governments, and this 'confidence' helps re-ignite the economy. A British think-tank economist, Marshall Auerback, questions this line of thinking, wondering if Cameron suggests questions governments should only '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"924930a2-d393-4f3b-8d15-2f60af0e4261\">ratchet up spending<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> when the economy is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"9c17f7c9-0537-4d6c-8c68-bf79bc546c16\">growing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.' This, Auerback warns, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"5e3716db-4be6-432a-a632-55325e4cb316\">should be avoided<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> because it presents genuine inflationary dangers.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the summary below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 27-31.</span></i></p><p><span>A government can undergo austerity measures by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"1430cb6e-c86e-47bf-adf8-ae25e6c8c9ca\">cutting spending<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> and/or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"2f339d7c-867b-4acc-b089-54c988830dfd\">raising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> (27)_____. If banks <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"dd875fea-6d37-4e33-94c0-df0e65b36ee2\">do not believe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> that a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"aa5d122d-d662-459a-b25e-0fd7e6fde2a3\">government will settle its debts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, they may ask for (28)_____ that are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"00cf6de9-379b-4bc7-9dc7-57261553f900\">too high<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to pay back. In these cases, the IMF is sometimes prepared to lend money to these governments. One of the conditions of IMF loans is that recipient countries undergo austerity measures to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"bff1bd82-94c3-4d83-b924-6c66a4db9be6\">reduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> their (29)_____ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"da9423f5-c7ac-49db-94fe-802db54b7876\">repay any debts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The IMF has attracted criticism for its role in Asia after the 1997 financial crisis. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"dfb13bac-b47b-4c4e-807d-46332ac3caa2\">The crisis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> was caused when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"2384dcca-f889-4d76-801f-70e20a039f9d\">international investors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"1eb52c12-06a8-4033-984c-29641f4f5619\">pulled their money out of the region at once<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, causing __ (30)_____ to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"bec986bc-2e6f-44f6-b537-a8bce353f441\">fail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"05f8b5a5-50da-4586-bc9f-a240e9ba8446\">unemployment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to rise. The IMF's austerity measures <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"01d338bc-10d6-439d-99ed-349ba98c6802\">set conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"f18834cb-5ec3-4dc7-afa4-7a5be23d7759\">lowered incomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> and (31)_____. These policies have caused great suffering internationally.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37435\" id=\"question-wrapper-37435\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TAXES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37436\" id=\"question-wrapper-37436\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INTEREST RATES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37437\" id=\"question-wrapper-37437\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BUDGET DEFICIT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37438\" id=\"question-wrapper-37438\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ASIAN CURRENCIES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37439\" id=\"question-wrapper-37439\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LABO(U)R STANDARDS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>FOUR</span></b></i><i><span> letters, A-G.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letters in boxes 32-35.</span></i></p><p><span>Which four items are identified as features of the Greek government's austerity measure programme in 2010?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. reducing public sector wages between 2010 and 2014</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. . <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 33 34 35\" data-uid=\"3dedce85-c6e3-43b7-b9f3-1789297000f1 d43ebb73-1ef3-4e83-9939-651b09c0cb56 e685c9d6-f661-4a93-ae8a-15dc97083d4f f67a36e1-977e-4c53-b02f-3f84df1b96a5\">cutting allowances for public sector workers</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 33 34 35\" data-uid=\"2d483411-e69f-4d02-9edd-e7024d0da986 6c2a0063-aad1-4f08-ad8f-4e248aeff2ab 8445d5bb-9b58-4e8f-b57d-fe9c4eba220f e50522f6-81c5-406e-bb6d-52e04d5373ec\">raising the sales tax</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 33 34 35\" data-uid=\"4a37839b-2cbe-4fc5-8723-e3e9b6fafe20 65260ff8-12b9-4e58-9dcf-513a66bc8fef 772cf5a8-2962-4150-8110-172d086860b4 cc32d86e-5991-495a-bc55-ebbfec51c3e6\">making the compulsory retirement age the same for both genders</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. multiple general strikes</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32 33 34 35\" data-uid=\"06beca80-a63e-48be-95f5-aac33be6eb57 960d0320-4c09-4de7-ad56-b8010e326ce5 b19f67f2-525f-402f-b4d7-b81cbb049df0 ba3b289f-9b5f-416d-8d2b-b3350f010edb\">making cigarettes more expensive</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. eliminating the budget deficit</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37440\" id=\"question-wrapper-37440\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37441\" id=\"question-wrapper-37441\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37442\" id=\"question-wrapper-37442\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37443\" id=\"question-wrapper-37443\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/D/F</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 36-40) and the list of people below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Match each person with an appropriate statement, A-F.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 36-40.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of Statements</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Businesses will grow after <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"a99b34ff-54a3-445c-9127-8e7a7cfa4c64\">the government and consumers spend more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"88605a71-99cc-4f82-a41a-6afa2747cf64\">Harsh austerity measures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"c1fb4ea1-39d6-4ee6-9fd7-0296eafda6a6\">caused some economies to decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"451c1b00-a22c-4f04-b7be-c85ddea5c0fe\">Government spending can help a country get out of debt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Governments <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"5e3716db-4be6-432a-a632-55325e4cb316\">should not<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"924930a2-d393-4f3b-8d15-2f60af0e4261\">raise spending<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> while the economy is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"9c17f7c9-0537-4d6c-8c68-bf79bc546c16\">expanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> .</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"75bb317d-112f-4be9-bb24-bb4cc4b5752b\">It is wasteful for governments to spend while the economy is getting smaller<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. Governments that introduce austerity measures are rewarded with economic success.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37444\" id=\"question-wrapper-37444\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>John Maynard Keynes</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37445\" id=\"question-wrapper-37445\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>David Cameron</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37446\" id=\"question-wrapper-37446\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Marshall Auerback</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37447\" id=\"question-wrapper-37447\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Joseph Stiglitz</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37448\" id=\"question-wrapper-37448\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Paul Krugman</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"1430cb6e-c86e-47bf-adf8-ae25e6c8c9ca","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"cutting spending","passagePhrase":"slashing government expenditure"},{"uid":"2f339d7c-867b-4acc-b089-54c988830dfd","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"raising","passagePhrase":"hiking"},{"uid":"dd875fea-6d37-4e33-94c0-df0e65b36ee2","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"do not believe","passagePhrase":"lose trust"},{"uid":"aa5d122d-d662-459a-b25e-0fd7e6fde2a3","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"government will settle its debts","passagePhrase":"government's ability or willingness to repay existing debts"},{"uid":"00cf6de9-379b-4bc7-9dc7-57261553f900","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"too high","passagePhrase":"cripplingly excessive"},{"uid":"bff1bd82-94c3-4d83-b924-6c66a4db9be6","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"reduce","passagePhrase":"curtail"},{"uid":"da9423f5-c7ac-49db-94fe-802db54b7876","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"repay any debts","passagePhrase":"fulfil their loan"},{"uid":"3dedce85-c6e3-43b7-b9f3-1789297000f1 d43ebb73-1ef3-4e83-9939-651b09c0cb56 e685c9d6-f661-4a93-ae8a-15dc97083d4f f67a36e1-977e-4c53-b02f-3f84df1b96a5","qNum":"32 33 34 35","questionPhrase":"cutting allowances for public sector workers","passagePhrase":"reducing public sector allowances by 8 percent"},{"uid":"2d483411-e69f-4d02-9edd-e7024d0da986 6c2a0063-aad1-4f08-ad8f-4e248aeff2ab 8445d5bb-9b58-4e8f-b57d-fe9c4eba220f e50522f6-81c5-406e-bb6d-52e04d5373ec","qNum":"32 33 34 35","questionPhrase":"raising the sales tax","passagePhrase":"sales tax—will be elevated to 23 percent"},{"uid":"06beca80-a63e-48be-95f5-aac33be6eb57 960d0320-4c09-4de7-ad56-b8010e326ce5 b19f67f2-525f-402f-b4d7-b81cbb049df0 ba3b289f-9b5f-416d-8d2b-b3350f010edb","qNum":"32 33 34 35","questionPhrase":"making cigarettes more expensive","passagePhrase":"excises on fuel, tobacco and alcohol are also subject to an increase"},{"uid":"4a37839b-2cbe-4fc5-8723-e3e9b6fafe20 65260ff8-12b9-4e58-9dcf-513a66bc8fef 772cf5a8-2962-4150-8110-172d086860b4 cc32d86e-5991-495a-bc55-ebbfec51c3e6","qNum":"32 33 34 35","questionPhrase":"making the compulsory retirement age the same for both genders","passagePhrase":"The statutory retirement age for women will be raised to 65, matching it with the current retirement age for men"},{"uid":"dfb13bac-b47b-4c4e-807d-46332ac3caa2","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"The crisis","passagePhrase":"When things started to turn sour"},{"uid":"2384dcca-f889-4d76-801f-70e20a039f9d","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"international investors","passagePhrase":"foreign investors"},{"uid":"1eb52c12-06a8-4033-984c-29641f4f5619","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"pulled their money out of the region at once","passagePhrase":"retracted their investments en masse"},{"uid":"bec986bc-2e6f-44f6-b537-a8bce353f441","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"fail","passagePhrase":"decimating"},{"uid":"05f8b5a5-50da-4586-bc9f-a240e9ba8446","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"unemployment","passagePhrase":"turning millions of employees out of work"},{"uid":"01d338bc-10d6-439d-99ed-349ba98c6802","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"set conditions","passagePhrase":"kept interest rates high"},{"uid":"f18834cb-5ec3-4dc7-afa4-7a5be23d7759","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"lowered incomes","passagePhrase":"driving down wages"},{"uid":"451c1b00-a22c-4f04-b7be-c85ddea5c0fe","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Government spending can help a country get out of debt","passagePhrase":"Governments ... could conceivably spend their national economy out of debt"},{"uid":"a99b34ff-54a3-445c-9127-8e7a7cfa4c64","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"the government and consumers spend more","passagePhrase":"government and consumer expenditure must kick in first"},{"uid":"88605a71-99cc-4f82-a41a-6afa2747cf64","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Harsh austerity measures","passagePhrase":"savage spending cuts"},{"uid":"c1fb4ea1-39d6-4ee6-9fd7-0296eafda6a6","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"caused some economies to decline","passagePhrase":"their reward has been a slump"},{"uid":"75bb317d-112f-4be9-bb24-bb4cc4b5752b","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"It is wasteful for governments to spend while the economy is getting smaller","passagePhrase":"the frivolity of governments that ratchet up spending at a time the economy is contracting"},{"uid":"924930a2-d393-4f3b-8d15-2f60af0e4261","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"raise spending","passagePhrase":"ratchet up spending"},{"uid":"9c17f7c9-0537-4d6c-8c68-bf79bc546c16","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"expanding","passagePhrase":"growing"},{"uid":"5e3716db-4be6-432a-a632-55325e4cb316","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"should not","passagePhrase":"should be avoided"}]},"reading_u2_127":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Bioluminescence</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"1\"><span>A. In the pitch-black waters of the ocean's aphotic zone—depths from 1000m to the sea floor—good eye sight does not count for very much on its own. Caves, in addition, frequently present a similar problem: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"30cd60ed-430c-4188-bba6-a796f3608dae\">the complete absence of natural light at any time of the day<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. This has not stopped some organisms from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"30cd60ed-430c-4188-bba6-a796f3608dae\">turning these inhospitable environments into their homes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, and in the process many have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d24d8523-f29f-4f78-a7a5-f58f8365a990\">created their own forms of light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d24d8523-f29f-4f78-a7a5-f58f8365a990\">developing one of the stunning visual marvels of the biological universe —bioluminescence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"2\"><span>B. Many people will encounter <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c527aca2-6b64-4a78-a9c0-eda3fa24184b\">bioluminescence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> at some point in their life, typically in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c527aca2-6b64-4a78-a9c0-eda3fa24184b\">some form of glowworm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, which is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c527aca2-6b64-4a78-a9c0-eda3fa24184b\">found on most continents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. North and South America are home to the '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c527aca2-6b64-4a78-a9c0-eda3fa24184b\">firefly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>', a glowing beetle which is known as a glow- worm during its larvae stage. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c527aca2-6b64-4a78-a9c0-eda3fa24184b\">Flightless glowing beetles and worms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> are also found in Europe, Asia, Australia and New Zealand. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c527aca2-6b64-4a78-a9c0-eda3fa24184b\">Less common flies, centipedes, mollusks and snails have bioluminescent qualities as well, as do some mushrooms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. The most dramatic examples of bioluminescence , however, are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"3606486d-ebc0-48f0-ac58-b013e81d0d34\">found deep below the ocean's surface<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, where no sunlight can penetrate at all. Here, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"3606486d-ebc0-48f0-ac58-b013e81d0d34\">anglerfish, cookie-cutter sharks, flashlight fish, lantern fish, gulper eels, viper fish and many other species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> have developed bioluminescence in unique and creative ways to facilitate their lives.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"3\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010\">The natural uses of bioluminescence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> vary widely, and organisms have learnt to be very creative with its use. Fireflies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010\">employ bioluminescence primarily for reproductive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> means—their flashing patterns <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7 8 9\" data-uid=\"349b6ab2-23ba-48f0-8cf3-f866692c15e7 81e3de59-1fc9-4ad1-bae9-e58d03303a8c b6d01257-953e-4ccf-9967-90f3e07cb0de ea854dac-9430-4d24-a39f-997475fb389d\">advertise a firefly's readiness to breed</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Some fish use it as <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3 6 7 8 9\" data-uid=\"6223ecb8-1a0a-463d-bddc-907ef2f0049e 8d85ee41-efa5-424c-a631-c4e988df7512 9b11ff9d-2eb6-4412-b8df-d50229f6b57e bd2d94d3-7e2a-4820-8679-b767f726966d eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010\">a handy spotlight to help them locate prey</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Others <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3 6 7 8 9\" data-uid=\"2562008e-9a79-43c9-83c6-d3a3e8ddfb2d 28438363-e775-4d64-a99c-c47fe1ca1fc9 9f4d6b52-968a-467a-b1df-47f30ea31518 ca34d032-31fd-436d-aae6-8626e7331b77 eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010\">use it as a lure</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>; the anglerfish, for example, dangles a luminescent flare that draws in gullible, smaller fishes which get snapped up by the anglerfish in an automated reflex. Sometimes bioluminescence <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010\">is </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3 6 7 8 9\" data-uid=\"0b679ee3-5309-4d81-a2d7-97bb4e455cda a30f1760-bae8-4bf0-9580-aa9c60e4a042 cd087b76-9270-46ae-9ac2-76d23eee18ba d001ba78-2164-4115-ac7d-2c66f15dbd8c eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010\">used to resist predators</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Vampire squids <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"de403854-d537-48fa-a7f6-290e3dbe135d\">eject<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> a thick cloud of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"d7321f18-fcc9-4c08-8892-792f76dd1632\">glowing liquid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> from the tip of its arms when threatened, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"a59db89e-0497-406e-ac58-fbc6ac3328a4\">can be disorientating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. Other species use a single, bright flash <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010\">to temporarily blind their attacker<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, with an effect similar to that of an oncoming car which has not dipped its headlights.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"4\"><span>D. Humans have captured and utilised <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"5f170a04-34a9-47b0-835b-8ee8928a8ec6\">bioluminescence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> by developing, over the last decade, a technology known as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be6e944d-fa12-45d3-a51f-e1a3b95d4b41\">Bioluminescence Imaging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> (BLI). BLI involves the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"1842f842-6097-44b1-8e5f-13aa56779401\">extraction of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a DNA protein <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"1842f842-6097-44b1-8e5f-13aa56779401\">from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a bioluminescent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"62ada379-09bf-4a2b-b2e1-5244dc97d406\">organism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, and then the integration of this protein into a laboratory animal through trans-geneticism. Researchers have been able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be6e944d-fa12-45d3-a51f-e1a3b95d4b41\">use luminised pathogens and cancer cell lines to track the respective spread of infections and cancers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Through BLI, cancers and infections <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"fbb11d87-ca25-4595-8e01-6da8901fa076\">can be observed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"37145c53-b28a-439e-b237-0fa8fb65a8a2\">without intervening in a way that affects their independent development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. In other words , while an ultra-sensitive camera and bioluminescent proteins add a visual element, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"37145c53-b28a-439e-b237-0fa8fb65a8a2\">do not disrupt or mutate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"dca80ea5-fe93-4ff9-95bb-759ad61e0931\">the natural processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. As a result, when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be6e944d-fa12-45d3-a51f-e1a3b95d4b41\">testing drugs and treatments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, researchers are permitted a single perspective of a therapy's progression.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"5\"><span>E. Once scientists learn how to engineer bioluminescence and keep it stable in large quantities, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d0f51ec0-a0ee-4da6-b8f4-3dc72ee4e4e8\">a number of other human uses for it will become available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f\">Glowing trees have been proposed as replacements for electric lighting along busy roads<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, for example, which would reduce our dependence on non-renewable energy sources. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f\">The same technology used in Christmas trees for the family home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> would also eliminate the fire danger from electrical fairy lights. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f\">It may also be possible for crops and plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to luminesce when they require watering, and for meat and dairy products to 'tell us' when they have become contaminated by bacteria. In a similar way, forensic investigators could <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5 13\" data-uid=\"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f f9c5695a-bf96-4620-b398-7566e9d66fd6\">detect bacterial species</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f\"> on </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5 13\" data-uid=\"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f 755c2dfc-1657-400e-9484-0378a5507f97\">corpses</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> through bioluminescence. Finally, there is the element of pure novelty. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f\">Children's toys and stickers are often made with glow-in-the-dark qualities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, and a biological form would allow rabbits, mice, fish, and other pets to glow as well.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct headings for sections A-E from the list of headings below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 1-5.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. Mushrooms that glow in the dark</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"c527aca2-6b64-4a78-a9c0-eda3fa24184b\">Bright creatures on land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"3606486d-ebc0-48f0-ac58-b013e81d0d34\">in the sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"d24d8523-f29f-4f78-a7a5-f58f8365a990\">Evolution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>'s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"30cd60ed-430c-4188-bba6-a796f3608dae\">solution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. Cave-dwelling organisms</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"d0f51ec0-a0ee-4da6-b8f4-3dc72ee4e4e8\">Future opportunities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f\">biological engineering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"5f170a04-34a9-47b0-835b-8ee8928a8ec6\">Nature's gift<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be6e944d-fa12-45d3-a51f-e1a3b95d4b41\">medicine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. Bioluminescence in humans</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010\">Purposes of bioluminescence in the wild<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. Luminescent pets</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37499\" id=\"question-wrapper-37499\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37500\" id=\"question-wrapper-37500\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37501\" id=\"question-wrapper-37501\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37502\" id=\"question-wrapper-37502\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37503\" id=\"question-wrapper-37503\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>FOUR</span></b></i><i><span> letters, A-G.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letters in boxes 6-9.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>FOUR</span></b><span> uses are listed for bioluminescence in nature?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7 8 9\" data-uid=\"2562008e-9a79-43c9-83c6-d3a3e8ddfb2d 28438363-e775-4d64-a99c-c47fe1ca1fc9 9f4d6b52-968a-467a-b1df-47f30ea31518 ca34d032-31fd-436d-aae6-8626e7331b77\">ways of attracting food</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. tracing the spread of diseases</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7 8 9\" data-uid=\"349b6ab2-23ba-48f0-8cf3-f866692c15e7 81e3de59-1fc9-4ad1-bae9-e58d03303a8c b6d01257-953e-4ccf-9967-90f3e07cb0de ea854dac-9430-4d24-a39f-997475fb389d\">mating signals</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. growing trees for street lighting</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. drug trials</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7 8 9\" data-uid=\"0b679ee3-5309-4d81-a2d7-97bb4e455cda a30f1760-bae8-4bf0-9580-aa9c60e4a042 cd087b76-9270-46ae-9ac2-76d23eee18ba d001ba78-2164-4115-ac7d-2c66f15dbd8c\">defensive tactics</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7 8 9\" data-uid=\"6223ecb8-1a0a-463d-bddc-907ef2f0049e 8d85ee41-efa5-424c-a631-c4e988df7512 9b11ff9d-2eb6-4412-b8df-d50229f6b57e bd2d94d3-7e2a-4820-8679-b767f726966d\">a torch to identify food</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37504\" id=\"question-wrapper-37504\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/F/G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37505\" id=\"question-wrapper-37505\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/F/G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37506\" id=\"question-wrapper-37506\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/F/G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37507\" id=\"question-wrapper-37507\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C/F/G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 10-13.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37508\" id=\"question-wrapper-37508\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"d7321f18-fcc9-4c08-8892-792f76dd1632\">The luminescent fluid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> that a Vampire Squid <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"de403854-d537-48fa-a7f6-290e3dbe135d\">emits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"a59db89e-0497-406e-ac58-fbc6ac3328a4\">has a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"a59db89e-0497-406e-ac58-fbc6ac3328a4\">effect on its predator<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DISORIENTATING</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37509\" id=\"question-wrapper-37509\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In order to use bioluminescence in a trans-genetic environment, (11)_____ must first <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"1842f842-6097-44b1-8e5f-13aa56779401\">be removed from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a bioluminescent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"62ada379-09bf-4a2b-b2e1-5244dc97d406\">creature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DNA PROTEIN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37510\" id=\"question-wrapper-37510\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>One advantage of BLI is that it could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"fbb11d87-ca25-4595-8e01-6da8901fa076\">allow researchers to see<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"dca80ea5-fe93-4ff9-95bb-759ad61e0931\">how a treatment is working<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"37145c53-b28a-439e-b237-0fa8fb65a8a2\">without altering or disturbing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NATURAL PROCESSES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37511\" id=\"question-wrapper-37511\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In the future, (13)_____ may be able to use bioluminescence to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"f9c5695a-bf96-4620-b398-7566e9d66fd6\">identify evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"755c2dfc-1657-400e-9484-0378a5507f97\">dead bodies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FORENSIC INVESTIGATORS/SCIENTISTS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"30cd60ed-430c-4188-bba6-a796f3608dae","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"solution","passagePhrase":"the complete absence of natural light at any time of the day ... turning these inhospitable environments into their homes"},{"uid":"d24d8523-f29f-4f78-a7a5-f58f8365a990","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Evolution","passagePhrase":"created their own forms of light ... developing one of the stunning visual marvels of the biological universe —bioluminescence"},{"uid":"c527aca2-6b64-4a78-a9c0-eda3fa24184b","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Bright creatures on land","passagePhrase":"bioluminescence ... some form of glowworm ... found on most continents ... firefly ... Flightless glowing beetles and worms ... Less common flies, centipedes, mollusks and snails have bioluminescent qualities as well, as do some mushrooms"},{"uid":"3606486d-ebc0-48f0-ac58-b013e81d0d34","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"in the sea","passagePhrase":"found deep below the ocean's surface ... anglerfish, cookie-cutter sharks, flashlight fish, lantern fish, gulper eels, viper fish and many other species"},{"uid":"eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Purposes of bioluminescence in the wild","passagePhrase":"The natural uses of bioluminescence ... employ bioluminescence primarily for reproductive ... is ... to temporarily blind their attacker"},{"uid":"349b6ab2-23ba-48f0-8cf3-f866692c15e7 81e3de59-1fc9-4ad1-bae9-e58d03303a8c b6d01257-953e-4ccf-9967-90f3e07cb0de ea854dac-9430-4d24-a39f-997475fb389d","qNum":"6 7 8 9","questionPhrase":"mating signals","passagePhrase":"advertise a firefly's readiness to breed"},{"uid":"6223ecb8-1a0a-463d-bddc-907ef2f0049e 8d85ee41-efa5-424c-a631-c4e988df7512 9b11ff9d-2eb6-4412-b8df-d50229f6b57e bd2d94d3-7e2a-4820-8679-b767f726966d eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010","qNum":"3 6 7 8 9","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a handy spotlight to help them locate prey"},{"uid":"2562008e-9a79-43c9-83c6-d3a3e8ddfb2d 28438363-e775-4d64-a99c-c47fe1ca1fc9 9f4d6b52-968a-467a-b1df-47f30ea31518 ca34d032-31fd-436d-aae6-8626e7331b77 eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010","qNum":"3 6 7 8 9","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"use it as a lure"},{"uid":"0b679ee3-5309-4d81-a2d7-97bb4e455cda a30f1760-bae8-4bf0-9580-aa9c60e4a042 cd087b76-9270-46ae-9ac2-76d23eee18ba d001ba78-2164-4115-ac7d-2c66f15dbd8c eb18a3d9-1d7d-4ac3-8093-885fd187f010","qNum":"3 6 7 8 9","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"used to resist predators"},{"uid":"de403854-d537-48fa-a7f6-290e3dbe135d","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"emits","passagePhrase":"eject"},{"uid":"d7321f18-fcc9-4c08-8892-792f76dd1632","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"The luminescent fluid","passagePhrase":"glowing liquid"},{"uid":"a59db89e-0497-406e-ac58-fbc6ac3328a4","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"has a ... effect on its predator","passagePhrase":"can be disorientating"},{"uid":"5f170a04-34a9-47b0-835b-8ee8928a8ec6","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Nature's gift","passagePhrase":"bioluminescence"},{"uid":"be6e944d-fa12-45d3-a51f-e1a3b95d4b41","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"medicine","passagePhrase":"Bioluminescence Imaging ... use luminised pathogens and cancer cell lines to track the respective spread of infections and cancers ... testing drugs and treatments"},{"uid":"1842f842-6097-44b1-8e5f-13aa56779401","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"be removed from","passagePhrase":"extraction of ... from"},{"uid":"62ada379-09bf-4a2b-b2e1-5244dc97d406","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"creature","passagePhrase":"organism"},{"uid":"fbb11d87-ca25-4595-8e01-6da8901fa076","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"allow researchers to see","passagePhrase":"can be observed"},{"uid":"37145c53-b28a-439e-b237-0fa8fb65a8a2","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"without altering or disturbing","passagePhrase":"without intervening in a way that affects their independent development ... do not disrupt or mutate"},{"uid":"dca80ea5-fe93-4ff9-95bb-759ad61e0931","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"how a treatment is working","passagePhrase":"the natural processes"},{"uid":"d0f51ec0-a0ee-4da6-b8f4-3dc72ee4e4e8","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Future opportunities","passagePhrase":"a number of other human uses for it will become available"},{"uid":"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"biological engineering","passagePhrase":"Glowing trees have been proposed as replacements for electric lighting along busy roads ... The same technology used in Christmas trees for the family home ... It may also be possible for crops and plants ... on ... Children's toys and stickers are often made with glow-in-the-dark qualities"},{"uid":"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f f9c5695a-bf96-4620-b398-7566e9d66fd6","qNum":"5 13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"detect bacterial species"},{"uid":"14d754a4-16af-4e79-a2f4-f3444b37009f 755c2dfc-1657-400e-9484-0378a5507f97","qNum":"5 13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"corpses"},{"uid":"2562008e-9a79-43c9-83c6-d3a3e8ddfb2d 28438363-e775-4d64-a99c-c47fe1ca1fc9 9f4d6b52-968a-467a-b1df-47f30ea31518 ca34d032-31fd-436d-aae6-8626e7331b77","qNum":"6 7 8 9","questionPhrase":"ways of attracting food","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"0b679ee3-5309-4d81-a2d7-97bb4e455cda a30f1760-bae8-4bf0-9580-aa9c60e4a042 cd087b76-9270-46ae-9ac2-76d23eee18ba d001ba78-2164-4115-ac7d-2c66f15dbd8c","qNum":"6 7 8 9","questionPhrase":"defensive tactics","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"6223ecb8-1a0a-463d-bddc-907ef2f0049e 8d85ee41-efa5-424c-a631-c4e988df7512 9b11ff9d-2eb6-4412-b8df-d50229f6b57e bd2d94d3-7e2a-4820-8679-b767f726966d","qNum":"6 7 8 9","questionPhrase":"a torch to identify food","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"f9c5695a-bf96-4620-b398-7566e9d66fd6","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"identify evidence","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"755c2dfc-1657-400e-9484-0378a5507f97","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"dead bodies","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_128":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>CHANGES IN MALE BODY IMAGE</span></b></p><p><span>A. The pressures on women to look slender, youthful and attractive have been extensively documented, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"4c220e1e-e027-42f5-88ba-ddf7a326b23f\">changing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7a03cbe-2822-4291-956f-6fff920a1f88\">expectations for women's bodies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> have varied widely. From <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7a03cbe-2822-4291-956f-6fff920a1f88\">voluptuous and curvy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"4c220e1e-e027-42f5-88ba-ddf7a326b23f\">in the days of Marilyn Monroe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7a03cbe-2822-4291-956f-6fff920a1f88\">slender and androgynous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> when Twiggy hit the London scene <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"4c220e1e-e027-42f5-88ba-ddf7a326b23f\">in the mid-1960s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, and then on to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7a03cbe-2822-4291-956f-6fff920a1f88\">towering Amazonian models<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"4c220e1e-e027-42f5-88ba-ddf7a326b23f\">the 1980s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and the '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7a03cbe-2822-4291-956f-6fff920a1f88\">heroin chic' and size-zero obsession<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"4c220e1e-e027-42f5-88ba-ddf7a326b23f\">today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, it is not just clothes that go in and out of fashion for women. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7a03cbe-2822-4291-956f-6fff920a1f88\">prevailing notion of the perfect body for men<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, however, has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"4c220e1e-e027-42f5-88ba-ddf7a326b23f\">remained remarkably static<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7a03cbe-2822-4291-956f-6fff920a1f88\">broad shoulders, a big chest and arms, and rippling, visible abdominal muscles and powerful legs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> have long been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"4c220e1e-e027-42f5-88ba-ddf7a326b23f\">the staple ingredients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of a desirable <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7a03cbe-2822-4291-956f-6fff920a1f88\">male physique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>B. A growing body of evidence suggests this is changing, however. Rootsteins, a mannequin design company in Britain, has released its newest male model—the </span><i><span>homme nouveau</span></i><span> —with a cinched-in 27-inch waist. 'To put that into perspective ,' says one female fashion reporter, 'I had a 27-inch waist when I was thirteen...and I was really skinny.' The company suggests that the </span><i><span>homme nouveau</span></i><span> 'redresses the prevailing 'beefcake' figure by carving out a far more streamlined, sinuous silhouette to match the edgier attitude of a new generation'.</span></p><p><span>C. Elsewhere in the fashion industry, the label American Apparel is releasing a line of trousers in sizes no larger than a 30-inch waist, which squeezes out most of the younger male market who have an average waistline over five inches larger. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"aa61f823-31ef-4b20-a364-0d00d0e47aa0\">Slender young men are naturally starting to dominate the catwalks and magazine pages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> as well. '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"aa61f823-31ef-4b20-a364-0d00d0e47aa0\">No one wanted the big guys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>,' model David Gandy has said, describing how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"aa61f823-31ef-4b20-a364-0d00d0e47aa0\">his muscled physique was losing him jobs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. 'It was all the skinny, androgynous look. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"aa61f823-31ef-4b20-a364-0d00d0e47aa0\">People would look at me very, very strangely when I went to castings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.'</span></p><p><span>D. Achieving such a physique can be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ef239cf3-740e-43ee-a3db-89e8030123f2\">unattainable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> for those <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"2fb65d08-27b8-4d1f-84ed-3a71939018d1\">without the natural genetic make-up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. 'I don't know that anyone would consider my body archetypal or as an exemplar to work towards,' notes model Davo McConville. 'You <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"2fb65d08-27b8-4d1f-84ed-3a71939018d1\">couldn' t aim for this<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>; it's defined by a vacuum of flesh, by what it's not.' Nevertheless, statistics suggest it is not just an obsession of models, celebrities and the media—more and more ordinary men are prepared to go to great lengths for a slender body. One indication is the growing number of men who are discovering surgical reconstruction. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"bd1c39e1-29e0-4e0b-bcd0-228bfd10dab7\">Male breast-reduction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> has become <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"2c9c76e6-2f69-42d3-98f5-fcc8521dd051\">especially popular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>; in 2009 the year-on-year growth rate for this procedure rose to 44 percent in the United Kingdom. Liposuction also remains popular in the market for male body reconstructive surgery, with 35,000 such procedures being performed on men every year.</span></p><p><span>E. Additionally, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c0721f80-472a-4141-bfdf-b394e48bb20e\">more men<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> now have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"e74ac3a4-7688-46ff-94a6-0a28d590f1b7\">eating disorders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> than ever before. These are characterised by normal eating habits, typically either the consumption of insufficient or excessive amounts of food. Eating disorders are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"949a5f32-6a6c-48ff-bc83-c6b81ba87769\">detrimental to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"dfdc3069-a1ed-4cd1-9f05-3ec0ae13e12d\">physical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"76eb8e95-2236-4f5d-82fc-cb12d956e634\">mental condition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of people who suffer from them , and the desire to achieve unrealistic physiques has been implicated as a cause. In 1990 only 10% of people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c2c91822-0e8c-4a55-a15f-d106980f5014\">suffering from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> anorexia or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"f3bda614-c606-4e53-a4be-f7f90f650bae\">bulimia<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> were believed to be male, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c0721f80-472a-4141-bfdf-b394e48bb20e\">this figure has climbed steadily<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to around one quarter today. Around two in five binge eaters are men. Women still <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e229e601-ddbe-4597-a339-b1be256e4e48\">make up the majority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of those afflicted by eating disorders, but the perception of it being a 'girly' problem has contributed to men being less likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b851b7e0-a5d1-484f-8825-2ae8f351d40f\">pursue treatment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. In 2008,male eating disorders were thrust into the spotlight when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c68c17a9-5d67-4cd3-aef8-95e88de0cba6\">former British Deputy Prime Minister, John Prescott<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, admitted to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"f3bda614-c606-4e53-a4be-f7f90f650bae\">habitually gorging on junk food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> and then inducing himself to vomit while in office. 'I never <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ed552be9-f2d0-43db-ac86-3fcae6aa5a0b\">admitted to this out of the shame and embarrassment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>,' he said. 'I <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ed552be9-f2d0-43db-ac86-3fcae6aa5a0b\">found it difficult as a man like me to admit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that I suffered from bulimia.'</span></p><p><span>F. In some respects, the slim male silhouette seems to be complementing, rather than displacing, the GI Joe physique. </span><i><span>Men's Health</span></i><span> , one of the only titles to weather the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"67f82682-905b-4c45-9585-afbada915e30\">floundering magazine market<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"67f82682-905b-4c45-9585-afbada915e30\">sales increasing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to a quarter of a million per issue, has a staple diet of bulky men on the cover who entice readers with the promise of big, powerful muscles. Advertising executives and fashion editors suggest that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"829068ce-d66a-4f8a-875c-0a530b12bb4f\">in times of recession and political uncertainty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"73b2d40d-4ec0-4b33-a325-ae18b094f2ad\">the more robust male body image once again becomes desirable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Academic research supports this claim, indicating that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"73b2d40d-4ec0-4b33-a325-ae18b094f2ad\">more 'feminine' features are desirable for men<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"829068ce-d66a-4f8a-875c-0a530b12bb4f\">in comfortable and secure societies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, while '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"73b2d40d-4ec0-4b33-a325-ae18b094f2ad\">masculine' physical traits are more attractive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"829068ce-d66a-4f8a-875c-0a530b12bb4f\">where survival comes back to the individual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. A University of Aberdeen study, conducted using 4,500 women from over 30 countries, found a pronounced correlation between levels of public healthcare and the amount of effeminacy women preferred in their men. In Sweden, the country considered to have the best healthcare, 68 percent of women <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"73b2d40d-4ec0-4b33-a325-ae18b094f2ad\">preferred the men who were shown with feminine facial features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. In Brazil, the country with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"829068ce-d66a-4f8a-875c-0a530b12bb4f\">the worst healthcare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in the study, only 45 percent of women were so inclined. 'The results suggest that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"829068ce-d66a-4f8a-875c-0a530b12bb4f\">as healthcare improves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"73b2d40d-4ec0-4b33-a325-ae18b094f2ad\">more masculine men fall out of favour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>,' the researchers concluded.more masculine men fall out of favour,' the researchers concluded.</span></p><p><span>G. Ultimately, columnist Polly Vernon has written, we are left with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"06f95bbb-521d-48ee-95a5-308ee7cf4d33\">two polarised ideals of masculine beauty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. One is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"06f95bbb-521d-48ee-95a5-308ee7cf4d33\">the sleek, slender silhouette<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> that exudes cutting-edge style and a wealthy, comfortable lifestyle. The other is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"06f95bbb-521d-48ee-95a5-308ee7cf4d33\">the 'strong, muscular, austerity-resistant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>' form that suggests a man can look after himself with his own bare hands. These ideals co-exist by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"b4922a82-e594-4a20-9ad7-c5ad85a7f8cc\">pulling men in different directions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"b4922a82-e594-4a20-9ad7-c5ad85a7f8cc\">encouraging them to believe they must always be chasing physical perfection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, while simultaneously <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"b4922a82-e594-4a20-9ad7-c5ad85a7f8cc\">destabilising any firm notions of what physical perfection requires<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>H. As a result, attaining the ideal body becomes an ever more futile and time-consuming task. Vernon concludes that this means less time for the more important things in life, and both sexes should resist the compulsive obsession with beauty.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A-H.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 14-20.</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NB</span></b></i><i><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37512\" id=\"question-wrapper-37512\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an opinion on whether <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"06f95bbb-521d-48ee-95a5-308ee7cf4d33\">body image changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"b4922a82-e594-4a20-9ad7-c5ad85a7f8cc\">have positive or negative effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37513\" id=\"question-wrapper-37513\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"4c220e1e-e027-42f5-88ba-ddf7a326b23f\">historical comparison<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7a03cbe-2822-4291-956f-6fff920a1f88\">gendered body images<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37514\" id=\"question-wrapper-37514\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"ed552be9-f2d0-43db-ac86-3fcae6aa5a0b\">humiliating confession<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"f3bda614-c606-4e53-a4be-f7f90f650bae\">overeating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> by a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"c68c17a9-5d67-4cd3-aef8-95e88de0cba6\">public figure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37515\" id=\"question-wrapper-37515\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"bd1c39e1-29e0-4e0b-bcd0-228bfd10dab7\">a cosmetic operation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that has become <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"2c9c76e6-2f69-42d3-98f5-fcc8521dd051\">increasingly popular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37516\" id=\"question-wrapper-37516\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"e74ac3a4-7688-46ff-94a6-0a28d590f1b7\">a health condition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c2c91822-0e8c-4a55-a15f-d106980f5014\">afflicting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c0721f80-472a-4141-bfdf-b394e48bb20e\">increasing numbers of men<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37517\" id=\"question-wrapper-37517\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"aa61f823-31ef-4b20-a364-0d00d0e47aa0\">the effect of changing body ideals on a male model<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37518\" id=\"question-wrapper-37518\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>an explanation of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"829068ce-d66a-4f8a-875c-0a530b12bb4f\">living standards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> affect <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"73b2d40d-4ec0-4b33-a325-ae18b094f2ad\">the desirability of male physiques<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 21-26, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>YES</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NO</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37519\" id=\"question-wrapper-37519\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A thin body is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ef239cf3-740e-43ee-a3db-89e8030123f2\">achievable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> for men <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"2fb65d08-27b8-4d1f-84ed-3a71939018d1\">regardless of their genes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37520\" id=\"question-wrapper-37520\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Male liposuction is more popular than male breast-reduction.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37521\" id=\"question-wrapper-37521\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Eating disorders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"949a5f32-6a6c-48ff-bc83-c6b81ba87769\">harm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"76eb8e95-2236-4f5d-82fc-cb12d956e634\">the mind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"dfdc3069-a1ed-4cd1-9f05-3ec0ae13e12d\">body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37522\" id=\"question-wrapper-37522\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Women <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b851b7e0-a5d1-484f-8825-2ae8f351d40f\">seek help for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> eating disorders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e229e601-ddbe-4597-a339-b1be256e4e48\">more often than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> men.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37523\" id=\"question-wrapper-37523\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Men's Health has <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"67f82682-905b-4c45-9585-afbada915e30\">suffered from a downturn in magazine sales<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37524\" id=\"question-wrapper-37524\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>As public healthcare improves men become more feminine.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"4c220e1e-e027-42f5-88ba-ddf7a326b23f","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"historical comparison","passagePhrase":"changing ... in the days of Marilyn Monroe ... in the mid-1960s ... the 1980s ... today ... remained remarkably static ... the staple ingredients"},{"uid":"a7a03cbe-2822-4291-956f-6fff920a1f88","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"gendered body images","passagePhrase":"expectations for women's bodies ... voluptuous and curvy ... slender and androgynous ... towering Amazonian models ... heroin chic' and size-zero obsession ... prevailing notion of the perfect body for men ... broad shoulders, a big chest and arms, and rippling, visible abdominal muscles and powerful legs ... male physique"},{"uid":"aa61f823-31ef-4b20-a364-0d00d0e47aa0","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"the effect of changing body ideals on a male model","passagePhrase":"Slender young men are naturally starting to dominate the catwalks and magazine pages ... No one wanted the big guys ... his muscled physique was losing him jobs ... People would look at me very, very strangely when I went to castings"},{"uid":"bd1c39e1-29e0-4e0b-bcd0-228bfd10dab7","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"a cosmetic operation","passagePhrase":"Male breast-reduction"},{"uid":"2c9c76e6-2f69-42d3-98f5-fcc8521dd051","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"increasingly popular","passagePhrase":"especially popular"},{"uid":"c0721f80-472a-4141-bfdf-b394e48bb20e","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"increasing numbers of men","passagePhrase":"more men ... this figure has climbed steadily"},{"uid":"e74ac3a4-7688-46ff-94a6-0a28d590f1b7","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"a health condition","passagePhrase":"eating disorders"},{"uid":"949a5f32-6a6c-48ff-bc83-c6b81ba87769","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"harm","passagePhrase":"detrimental to"},{"uid":"dfdc3069-a1ed-4cd1-9f05-3ec0ae13e12d","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"body","passagePhrase":"physical"},{"uid":"76eb8e95-2236-4f5d-82fc-cb12d956e634","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"the mind","passagePhrase":"mental condition"},{"uid":"c2c91822-0e8c-4a55-a15f-d106980f5014","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"afflicting","passagePhrase":"suffering from"},{"uid":"f3bda614-c606-4e53-a4be-f7f90f650bae","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"overeating","passagePhrase":"bulimia ... habitually gorging on junk food"},{"uid":"e229e601-ddbe-4597-a339-b1be256e4e48","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"more often than","passagePhrase":"make up the majority"},{"uid":"b851b7e0-a5d1-484f-8825-2ae8f351d40f","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"seek help for","passagePhrase":"pursue treatment"},{"uid":"c68c17a9-5d67-4cd3-aef8-95e88de0cba6","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"public figure","passagePhrase":"former British Deputy Prime Minister, John Prescott"},{"uid":"ed552be9-f2d0-43db-ac86-3fcae6aa5a0b","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"humiliating confession","passagePhrase":"admitted to this out of the shame and embarrassment ... found it difficult as a man like me to admit"},{"uid":"829068ce-d66a-4f8a-875c-0a530b12bb4f","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"living standards","passagePhrase":"in times of recession and political uncertainty ... in comfortable and secure societies ... where survival comes back to the individual ... the worst healthcare ... as healthcare improves"},{"uid":"73b2d40d-4ec0-4b33-a325-ae18b094f2ad","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the desirability of male physiques","passagePhrase":"the more robust male body image once again becomes desirable ... more 'feminine' features are desirable for men ... masculine' physical traits are more attractive ... preferred the men who were shown with feminine facial features ... more masculine men fall out of favour"},{"uid":"06f95bbb-521d-48ee-95a5-308ee7cf4d33","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"body image changes","passagePhrase":"two polarised ideals of masculine beauty ... the sleek, slender silhouette ... the 'strong, muscular, austerity-resistant"},{"uid":"b4922a82-e594-4a20-9ad7-c5ad85a7f8cc","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"have positive or negative effects","passagePhrase":"pulling men in different directions ... encouraging them to believe they must always be chasing physical perfection ... destabilising any firm notions of what physical perfection requires"}]},"reading_u2_129":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>EATS, SHOOTS AND LEAVES</span></b></p><p><b><span>—a book review</span></b></p><p><span>The title of </span><i><span>Eats, Shoots and Leaves</span></i><span> refers to a famously misplaced comma in a wildlife manual that ended up suggesting a panda rather violently 'eats, shoots and leaves' instead of eating shoots and leaves. The author of this book, journalist Lynne Truss, is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"be6bfaba-696c-4ac2-a80b-fd651a44197e\">something akin to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> a militant linguist, dedicating this 'zero tolerance' manifesto on grammar to the striking Bolshevik printers of St. Petersburg who, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"6e753f9f-2e2e-4766-856c-1a3925d2acf6\">in demanding the same remuneration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> for punctuation as they received for letters, ended up <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"50c09701-4743-440a-bd04-a6e39e9e8e7c\">setting in motion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the first Russian Revolution.</span></p><p><span>Some of the book involves humorous attacks on erroneous punctuation. There is the confused Shakespearian thespian who inadvertently turns a frantic plea: 'Go, get him surgeons!' into the cheerful encouragement of 'Go get him, surgeons!' Street and shop signs have a ubiquitous presence. A bakery declares 'FRESH DONUT'S SOLD HERE' and a florist curiously announces that 'Pansy's here!' (Is she?). The shame<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"dc9c9fea-24c2-4cb3-8245-b783eca9ff4c\">less<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> title of a Hollywood film </span><i><span>Two Weeks Notice</span></i><span> is reeled in for criticism—'Would they similarly call it </span><i><span>One Weeks Notice</span></i><span> ?', Truss enquires—and sometimes, as in the case of signs promoting '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"444e8f95-db64-42a6-9a90-b5453392c9a6\">ANTIQUE'S' and 'Potatoe's<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>'—one questions whether we are bearing witness to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"58f06300-0270-44e5-82e1-cbc74b811aaa\">new depths of grammar ignorance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, or a postmodern caricature of atrocious punctuation. </span><i><span>Eats, Shoots and Leaves</span></i><span> is not just a piece of comedy and ridicule, however, and Truss has plenty to offer on the question of proper grammar usage. If you have ever wondered whether it is acceptable to simply use an 'em dash' </span><sup><span>1</span></sup><span> in place of a comma—the verdict from Truss is that you can. 'The dash is less formal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"dc9c9fea-24c2-4cb3-8245-b783eca9ff4c\">than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"1d25d580-e346-4f22-9f56-f7e158385b8a\">the semicolon<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, which makes it more attractive,' she suggests. 'It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e12e9df1-15e3-4ce6-a41b-7f6359a15977\">enhances conversational tone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>; and...it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e12e9df1-15e3-4ce6-a41b-7f6359a15977\">capable of quite subtle effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.' The author concludes, with characteristic wry condescension, that the em dash's popularity largely rests on people knowing it is almost impossible to use incorrectly. Truss is a personal champion of the semicolon, a historically contentious punctuation mark elsewhere maligned by novelist Kurt Vonnegut Jr., as a 'transvestite hermaphrodite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"77984b57-9f3f-4c70-b0ec-8c4682302b12\">representing absolutely nothing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>'. Coming to the semicolon's defense, Truss suggests that, while it can certainly be over-used—she refers to the dying words of one 20th century writer: 'I should have used fewer semicolons'—the semicolon can perform the role of a 'a kind of Special Policeman in the event of comma fights'.</span></p><p><span>Truss has come under criticism on two broad points. The first argument criticises the legitimacy of her authority as a punctuation autocrat. Louis Menand, writing in the </span><i><span>New Yorker</span></i><span> , details </span><i><span>Eats, Shoots</span></i><i><span>and Leaves'</span></i><span> numerous grammatical and punctuation sins: a comma-free non-restrictive clause; a superfluous ellipsis; a misplaced apostrophe; a misused parenthesis; two misused semicolons; an erroneous hyphen in the word 'abuzz', and so on. In fact, as Menand notes, half the semicolons in the Truss book are spuriously deployed because they stem from the author's open flouting of the rule that semicolons must only connect two independent clauses. 'Why would a person not just vague about the rules but disinclined to follow them bother to produce a guide to punctuation?' Menand inquires. Ultimately, he holds Truss accused of producing a book that pleases those who 'just need to vent' and concludes that </span><i><span>Eats, Shoots and Leaves</span></i><span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"48ba46b4-faa3-4ad0-8cf1-10d3a44cd0aa\">actually a tirade against the decline of language and print<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"48ba46b4-faa3-4ad0-8cf1-10d3a44cd0aa\">disguises itself<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, thinly and poorly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"48ba46b4-faa3-4ad0-8cf1-10d3a44cd0aa\">as some kind of a style manual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Linguist David Chrystal has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9e160c48-0a90-48a7-b05c-16135f0ef467\">criticised what he describes as a 'linguistic purism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>' coursing through Truss' book. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9e160c48-0a90-48a7-b05c-16135f0ef467\">Linguistic purism is the notion that one variety of language is somehow more pure than others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, with this sense of purity often based on an idealised historical point in the language's development, but sometimes simply in reference to an abstract ideal. In </span><i><span>The Fight for English: How Language Pundits Ate</span></i><span> , </span><i><span>Shot and Left</span></i><span> , Chrystal—a former colleague of Truss—condemns the no-holds-barred approach to punctuation and grammar. 'Zero tolerance does not allow for flexibility,' he argues. 'It is prescriptivism taken to extremes. It suggests that language is in a state where all the rules are established with 100 per cent certainty. The suggestion is false. We do not know what all the rules of punctuation are. And <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"fd7a3909-7475-4a44-a332-4aed45d5e75d\">no rule of punctuation is followed by all of the people all of the time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.'</span></p><p><span>Other detractors of Truss' 'prescriptivism' are careful to disassociate needless purism from robust and sensible criticism, an oppositional stance they call descriptivism. 'Don't ever imagine,' Geoffrey K. Pullum on the Language Log emphasises, 'that I think all honest attempts at using English are just as good as any others. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"6368a21a-3e04-40c5-9608-9bd1e5290aa6\">Bad writing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> needs to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ec32f5a7-7f49-4774-9cf4-a8a0d410839f\">be fixed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. But let's make sure we fix the right things.' In other words, we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"145979d5-b427-43da-ac6c-5569ca7fd11d\">do not require a dogmatic approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ec32f5a7-7f49-4774-9cf4-a8a0d410839f\">clean up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"6368a21a-3e04-40c5-9608-9bd1e5290aa6\">misused language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Charles Gaulke concurs, noting that his opposition to 'prescriptivism' does not require contending with the existence of standards themselves, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"ffbcdefd-859c-48ff-aa28-2ca2c8583982\">questioning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"4bac036b-8bdd-4fb9-bd6a-f6dba902387a\">whether our standards should determine what works, or whether what works should determine our standards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Ultimately, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"049bb4c7-1cf6-40f2-b297-7659dc8a1ee1 d8ec2d23-a2a7-4fc8-add2-ee762c523df1 dad12b8a-fe4f-409f-8790-e16210172eac\">it is unlikely the purists and pedagogues will ever make absolute peace with</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> those who see language as a fluid, creative process within which everyone has a role to play. Both sides can <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"5e0a03a2-e1ae-4ac2-a29a-3eb524ef9889 e56a2d1d-895b-4115-af18-79d7690c8c90 e6634ed2-3852-4b5a-9662-80f628798e73\">learn to live in a sort of contentious harmony</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, however. Creativity typically involves extending, adapting and critiquing the status quo, and revising and reviving old traditions while constructing new ones. Rules must exist in order for this process to take place, if only for them to be broken. On the flip side, rules have <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"7b1c1f39-2990-40f7-bd91-8c6bf2eb5896 878c5d02-d707-47f4-9f80-fe537f2fbaf0 91267de3-551b-4ca3-9b03-718b169e2c06\">an important role</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to play in <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"3ee429ce-9527-4689-b6c9-915b657ac2f9 4cce5f35-c7a3-4fc6-a9ce-a94d76ffd8be 899a3564-f4a2-4883-863a-290c30c1a38a\">guiding our language into forms that can be accessed by people across all manner of differences</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, so it is vital to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"ada00090-00ce-4b47-a4a1-4a88199eabcb b3bad828-70fb-49ec-abd8-78cdfa3bfff2 d44ef878-eca6-42d9-84b1-b0b063671c55\">acknowledge the extent to which they can be democratic</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, rather than <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"66b9ae10-a91d-4317-b0b6-dd7dfd81980d a24e54e4-f3b4-4712-a746-fae139587c91 ba6e4dcf-7212-478d-9104-ca9d22ee3cba\">merely autocratic in function</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Nevertheless, all the regulations in the world cannot stem the natural spring of language, which bursts through rivets and snakes around the dams that linguistic authorities may try to put in place. We should celebrate rather than curse these inevitable tensions.</span></p><p><span>*1. Em dash=——</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 27-32) and the list of people below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Match each statement with the correct person, A-E.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 27-32.</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NB</span></b></i><i><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of People</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Kurt Vonnegut Jr.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Louis Menand</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. David Chrystal</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Geoffrey K. Pullum</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Charles Gaulke</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37525\" id=\"question-wrapper-37525\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"6368a21a-3e04-40c5-9608-9bd1e5290aa6\">Mistakes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"ec32f5a7-7f49-4774-9cf4-a8a0d410839f\">be corrected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"145979d5-b427-43da-ac6c-5569ca7fd11d\">on the basis of common sense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37526\" id=\"question-wrapper-37526\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"fd7a3909-7475-4a44-a332-4aed45d5e75d\">No one has legitimacy as an ultimate authority on punctuation use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37527\" id=\"question-wrapper-37527\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Eats, Shoots and Leaves is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"48ba46b4-faa3-4ad0-8cf1-10d3a44cd0aa\">not the type of book it claims to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37528\" id=\"question-wrapper-37528\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9e160c48-0a90-48a7-b05c-16135f0ef467\">The idea that some forms of language can be better than others is wrong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37529\" id=\"question-wrapper-37529\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The semicolon <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"77984b57-9f3f-4c70-b0ec-8c4682302b12\">has no real purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37530\" id=\"question-wrapper-37530\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>We can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"ffbcdefd-859c-48ff-aa28-2ca2c8583982\">ask<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"4bac036b-8bdd-4fb9-bd6a-f6dba902387a\">whether rules are helpful without undermining the need for rules<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the summary below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the p<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"dc9c9fea-24c2-4cb3-8245-b783eca9ff4c\">as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>sage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 33-37.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Eats, Shoots and Leaves</span></i><span> is a book on punctuation by journalist Lynne Truss, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"be6bfaba-696c-4ac2-a80b-fd651a44197e\">who could be described as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> a (33)_____. She dedicates the book to the Bolshevik Printers who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"50c09701-4743-440a-bd04-a6e39e9e8e7c\">started<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the (34)_____ by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"6e753f9f-2e2e-4766-856c-1a3925d2acf6\">protesting for better pay conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. The book is partly a humorous criticism of incorrect punctuation. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"444e8f95-db64-42a6-9a90-b5453392c9a6\">Some of the examples<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"58f06300-0270-44e5-82e1-cbc74b811aaa\">so bad<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> it is possible that they are actually a (35)_____.</span></p><p><span>Truss also guides the reader on correct punctuation usage. She likes the em dash because it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"dc9c9fea-24c2-4cb3-8245-b783eca9ff4c\">not as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> (36)_____ as the semicolon, for example, but remains a (37)_____ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"1d25d580-e346-4f22-9f56-f7e158385b8a\">the latter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> due to its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e12e9df1-15e3-4ce6-a41b-7f6359a15977\">ability to discipline areas of text that are crowded with commas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37531\" id=\"question-wrapper-37531\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MILITANT LINGUIST</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37532\" id=\"question-wrapper-37532\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FIRST RUSSIAN REVOLUTION</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37533\" id=\"question-wrapper-37533\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POSTMODERN CARICATURE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37534\" id=\"question-wrapper-37534\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FORMAL</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37535\" id=\"question-wrapper-37535\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PERSONAL CHAMPION</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>THREE</span></b></i><i><span> letters, A-G.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letters in boxes 38-40.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>THREE</span></b><span> of the following statements form part of the author's conclusion?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Rules prevent the creation of new things.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"7b1c1f39-2990-40f7-bd91-8c6bf2eb5896 878c5d02-d707-47f4-9f80-fe537f2fbaf0 91267de3-551b-4ca3-9b03-718b169e2c06\">A centralised point of control</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"3ee429ce-9527-4689-b6c9-915b657ac2f9 4cce5f35-c7a3-4fc6-a9ce-a94d76ffd8be 899a3564-f4a2-4883-863a-290c30c1a38a\">effectively guide the flow of language</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Both the descriptivists and prescriptivists have important roles to play in language evolution.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"049bb4c7-1cf6-40f2-b297-7659dc8a1ee1 d8ec2d23-a2a7-4fc8-add2-ee762c523df1 dad12b8a-fe4f-409f-8790-e16210172eac\">Disputes over matters of language rules</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"5e0a03a2-e1ae-4ac2-a29a-3eb524ef9889 e56a2d1d-895b-4115-af18-79d7690c8c90 e6634ed2-3852-4b5a-9662-80f628798e73\">need not be condemned</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Prescriptivists and descriptivists are both wrong.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. Rules <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"ada00090-00ce-4b47-a4a1-4a88199eabcb b3bad828-70fb-49ec-abd8-78cdfa3bfff2 d44ef878-eca6-42d9-84b1-b0b063671c55\">help everyone use language</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> and do not <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"66b9ae10-a91d-4317-b0b6-dd7dfd81980d a24e54e4-f3b4-4712-a746-fae139587c91 ba6e4dcf-7212-478d-9104-ca9d22ee3cba\">merely prescribe usage</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. An essential part of creativity is the rejection of that which has come before.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37536\" id=\"question-wrapper-37536\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37537\" id=\"question-wrapper-37537\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37538\" id=\"question-wrapper-37538\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D/F</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"be6bfaba-696c-4ac2-a80b-fd651a44197e","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"who could be described as","passagePhrase":"something akin to"},{"uid":"6e753f9f-2e2e-4766-856c-1a3925d2acf6","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"protesting for better pay conditions","passagePhrase":"in demanding the same remuneration"},{"uid":"50c09701-4743-440a-bd04-a6e39e9e8e7c","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"started","passagePhrase":"setting in motion"},{"uid":"dc9c9fea-24c2-4cb3-8245-b783eca9ff4c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"as ... not as","passagePhrase":"less ... than"},{"uid":"444e8f95-db64-42a6-9a90-b5453392c9a6","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Some of the examples","passagePhrase":"ANTIQUE'S' and 'Potatoe's"},{"uid":"58f06300-0270-44e5-82e1-cbc74b811aaa","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"so bad","passagePhrase":"new depths of grammar ignorance"},{"uid":"1d25d580-e346-4f22-9f56-f7e158385b8a","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"the latter","passagePhrase":"the semicolon"},{"uid":"e12e9df1-15e3-4ce6-a41b-7f6359a15977","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"ability to discipline areas of text that are crowded with commas","passagePhrase":"enhances conversational tone ... capable of quite subtle effects"},{"uid":"77984b57-9f3f-4c70-b0ec-8c4682302b12","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"has no real purpose","passagePhrase":"representing absolutely nothing"},{"uid":"48ba46b4-faa3-4ad0-8cf1-10d3a44cd0aa","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"not the type of book it claims to be","passagePhrase":"actually a tirade against the decline of language and print ... disguises itself ... as some kind of a style manual"},{"uid":"9e160c48-0a90-48a7-b05c-16135f0ef467","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"The idea that some forms of language can be better than others is wrong","passagePhrase":"criticised what he describes as a 'linguistic purism ... Linguistic purism is the notion that one variety of language is somehow more pure than others"},{"uid":"fd7a3909-7475-4a44-a332-4aed45d5e75d","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"No one has legitimacy as an ultimate authority on punctuation use","passagePhrase":"no rule of punctuation is followed by all of the people all of the time"},{"uid":"6368a21a-3e04-40c5-9608-9bd1e5290aa6","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Mistakes","passagePhrase":"Bad writing ... misused language"},{"uid":"ec32f5a7-7f49-4774-9cf4-a8a0d410839f","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"be corrected","passagePhrase":"be fixed ... clean up"},{"uid":"145979d5-b427-43da-ac6c-5569ca7fd11d","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"on the basis of common sense","passagePhrase":"do not require a dogmatic approach"},{"uid":"ffbcdefd-859c-48ff-aa28-2ca2c8583982","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"ask","passagePhrase":"questioning"},{"uid":"4bac036b-8bdd-4fb9-bd6a-f6dba902387a","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"whether rules are helpful without undermining the need for rules","passagePhrase":"whether our standards should determine what works, or whether what works should determine our standards"},{"uid":"049bb4c7-1cf6-40f2-b297-7659dc8a1ee1 d8ec2d23-a2a7-4fc8-add2-ee762c523df1 dad12b8a-fe4f-409f-8790-e16210172eac","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"Disputes over matters of language rules","passagePhrase":"it is unlikely the purists and pedagogues will ever make absolute peace with"},{"uid":"5e0a03a2-e1ae-4ac2-a29a-3eb524ef9889 e56a2d1d-895b-4115-af18-79d7690c8c90 e6634ed2-3852-4b5a-9662-80f628798e73","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"need not be condemned","passagePhrase":"learn to live in a sort of contentious harmony"},{"uid":"7b1c1f39-2990-40f7-bd91-8c6bf2eb5896 878c5d02-d707-47f4-9f80-fe537f2fbaf0 91267de3-551b-4ca3-9b03-718b169e2c06","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"A centralised point of control","passagePhrase":"an important role"},{"uid":"3ee429ce-9527-4689-b6c9-915b657ac2f9 4cce5f35-c7a3-4fc6-a9ce-a94d76ffd8be 899a3564-f4a2-4883-863a-290c30c1a38a","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"effectively guide the flow of language","passagePhrase":"guiding our language into forms that can be accessed by people across all manner of differences"},{"uid":"ada00090-00ce-4b47-a4a1-4a88199eabcb b3bad828-70fb-49ec-abd8-78cdfa3bfff2 d44ef878-eca6-42d9-84b1-b0b063671c55","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"help everyone use language","passagePhrase":"acknowledge the extent to which they can be democratic"},{"uid":"66b9ae10-a91d-4317-b0b6-dd7dfd81980d a24e54e4-f3b4-4712-a746-fae139587c91 ba6e4dcf-7212-478d-9104-ca9d22ee3cba","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"merely prescribe usage","passagePhrase":"merely autocratic in function"}]},"reading_u2_130":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>'Freebie' marketing</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"1\"><span>A. In the late 1890s, while travelling as an itinerant salesperson for the Crown, Cork and Seal Company, King C. Gillette observed how his corked bottle caps were discarded immediately after opening. Nevertheless, his company turned a healthy profit and there was immense business value, Gillette soon <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4d1ac8f2-cab4-4447-9cfe-f268c24eeb6a\">came to realise, in a product that was used only a few times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. Gillette had his own personal breakthrough while struggling with a straight-bladed razor—a slow, fiddly and potentially dangerous instrument that required sharpening on a regular basis . <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4d1ac8f2-cab4-4447-9cfe-f268c24eeb6a\">A simple, disposable blade that could be thrown away when it dulled would meet a real need and generate strong profits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, he correctly reasoned. After founding the American Safety Razor Company in 1901, his sales leapt from 168 blades in 1903 to 123,648 blades only a year later.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"2\"><span>B. What King C. Gillette pioneered is for more than a convenient and affordable way for men to shave, however; it is the business practice now known as '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91\">freebie marketing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>' that has inspired many more companies over the years. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91\">Gillette's </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2 7\" data-uid=\"1e684ba3-1e99-4636-a25a-978d0ba1b3e4 cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91\">approach</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91\"> was </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2 7\" data-uid=\"34dbc505-672f-4942-b3b1-2dd4d344fe03 cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91\">contrary</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91\"> to the received wisdom of </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2 7\" data-uid=\"28c9dc41-4686-4dd5-a9e2-06453160fa71 cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91\">his era</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, which held that a single, durable, high-quality and relatively expensive consumer item with a high profit margin was the best foundation for a business. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91\">Freebie marketing involves two sets of items: a master product that is purchased once, and a consumable product that is frequently disposed of and repurchased on an ongoing basis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. In this instance, the master product is often sold with little to no profit margin and is sometimes even dispensed at a loss. As the consumables are purchased over months and years, however,this can yield a much greater overall profit.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"3\"><span>C. Freebie marketing only works if the producer of the master item is also able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"b1a201ae-2797-43f9-b9be-fb1f1968d24f\">maintain control over the creation and distribution of the consumables<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"1a75476c-567e-41f2-bff7-be6355f4d7f9\">If this does not happen, then cheaper versions of the consumable items may be produced, leaving the original company without a source of profit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. The video game company Atari, for example, initially sold its Atom 2600 consoles at cost price while relying on game sales for profit. Several programmers left Atari, however, and began a new company called Activision which produced cheaper games of a similar quality. Suddenly, Atari was left with no way to make money. Lawsuits to block Activision failed, and Atari survived only by adding licensing measures to its subsequent 5200 and 7800 consoles.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"4\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"55966b72-50c6-45b4-8ee0-6c8cf8335fd3\">In other instances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4 8\" data-uid=\"acbe95b2-ef30-4397-925f-21fc7054d8e8 ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb\">consumers</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb\"> sometimes find that uses for a master product </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4 8\" data-uid=\"d8d1eeb7-9373-4dec-8f0e-951b4c44e3d3 ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb\">circumvent the need</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb\"> to </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4 8\" data-uid=\"08a1d0ac-3346-44cd-899f-4946edb22bb9 ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb\">purchase</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb\"> consumables</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. This phe<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8974a201-73c0-47d0-b7ce-2cd8db7b2f5f\">no<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>menon is well known to have afflicted the producers of CueCat barcode readers. These were given away free through Wired magazine with the intention that they would be used by customers to scan barcodes next to advertisements in the publication and thus generate new revenue flows. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb\">Users discovered, however, that the machines could be easily modified and used for other purposes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, such as building a personal database of book and CD collections . As no licensing agreement <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8974a201-73c0-47d0-b7ce-2cd8db7b2f5f\">was ever reached<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"7cf03aa6-b58d-4ddc-95a3-8446cbb4c985\">between Wired and its magazine subscribers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, CueCat were powerless to intervene, and after <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"08d30eed-bf57-40c3-be98-7260609f3fe4\">company liquidation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the barcode readers soon became available in quantities over 500,000 for as little as US$0.30 each.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"5\"><span>E. Not all forms of freebie marketing are legal. One notable example of this is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5bec8e15-e49b-457d-b178-a355f826073c\">the use of freebie marketing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to 'push' <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"e8841e8a-88f6-4b1f-afe1-9e6cdc97641d\">habit-forming goods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in areas where there is otherwise no market. For illegal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"9a47451b-28cf-4940-9b31-bf242def2e1e\">substances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> this is already <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5 10\" data-uid=\"49af4e04-bed9-4e2a-a546-acef99215008 5bec8e15-e49b-457d-b178-a355f826073c\">restricted</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5bec8e15-e49b-457d-b178-a355f826073c\"> on the basis of the product's </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5 10\" data-uid=\"49af4e04-bed9-4e2a-a546-acef99215008 5bec8e15-e49b-457d-b178-a355f826073c\">illegality</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"e6e02634-e475-4413-8d88-93bef9bab1f6\">the use of freebie marketing to promote<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> legal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"9a47451b-28cf-4940-9b31-bf242def2e1e\">goods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> such as tobacco, alcohol and pharmaceuticals is also <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5 10\" data-uid=\"49af4e04-bed9-4e2a-a546-acef99215008 5bec8e15-e49b-457d-b178-a355f826073c\">outlawed</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> because the short-term gain to a small number of commercial outlets is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"4b715dde-af15-45d4-8571-29988fc5ccef\">not deemed worth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the social cost of widespread substance abuse.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"6\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"565122a5-937a-4045-bc50-52bbb1190051\">Another practice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> that is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"eb09a973-3e90-4ebe-90af-460e497abc84\">prohibited under antitrust laws<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> is a form of freebie marketing known as '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"565122a5-937a-4045-bc50-52bbb1190051\">tying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>'. This is when a <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"565122a5-937a-4045-bc50-52bbb1190051\">seller makes the sale of </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 12\" data-uid=\"565122a5-937a-4045-bc50-52bbb1190051 6e6c9af1-a41f-4080-8734-bccfba4d1cd1\">one good</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"565122a5-937a-4045-bc50-52bbb1190051\"> conditional on </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 12\" data-uid=\"40cccdb0-1447-4763-85c4-e069a5a38715 565122a5-937a-4045-bc50-52bbb1190051\">the acquisition of a second good</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. In these instances the first good is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"fcb17da3-03f0-4ef4-861b-126f55231b47\">typically<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> important and highly desirable, while the second is inferior and undesirable. A music distributor who has the rights to an album that is in high demand, for example, might only allow stores to purchase copies of this album if they also buy unpopular stock that does not sell very easily. Because this typically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"495c5650-232b-4d61-8949-bcc76d938312\">relies on the manipulation of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> a natural monopoly on the port of the distributor, such practices are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"4b5f24cb-bac5-4323-b80a-9f101d802298\">widely understood to constitute<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> anti-competitive behaviour.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has six sections, A-F.</span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct headings for sections A-F from the list of headings below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct number, ix, in boxes 1-6.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5bec8e15-e49b-457d-b178-a355f826073c\">No give-aways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"e8841e8a-88f6-4b1f-afe1-9e6cdc97641d\">addictive products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. Sales of razor blades increase astronomically</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"b1a201ae-2797-43f9-b9be-fb1f1968d24f\">Monopoly of consumables<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"1a75476c-567e-41f2-bff7-be6355f4d7f9\">vital for success<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. Video gaming a risky business</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"565122a5-937a-4045-bc50-52bbb1190051\">novel method of dual marketing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"eb09a973-3e90-4ebe-90af-460e497abc84\">ruled out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. Freebie marketing restricted to legal goods</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb\">Buyer ingenuity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> may lead to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"08d30eed-bf57-40c3-be98-7260609f3fe4\">bankruptcy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91\">marketing innovation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"4d1ac8f2-cab4-4447-9cfe-f268c24eeb6a\">product innovation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"x\"><span>x. More money to be made from high quality products</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37579\" id=\"question-wrapper-37579\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IX</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37580\" id=\"question-wrapper-37580\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37581\" id=\"question-wrapper-37581\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37582\" id=\"question-wrapper-37582\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37583\" id=\"question-wrapper-37583\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37584\" id=\"question-wrapper-37584\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the text for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 7-9.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37585\" id=\"question-wrapper-37585\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"1e684ba3-1e99-4636-a25a-978d0ba1b3e4\">new tactic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> of freebie marketing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"34dbc505-672f-4942-b3b1-2dd4d344fe03\">ran against<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the (7)_____ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"28c9dc41-4686-4dd5-a9e2-06453160fa71\">Gillette's time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RECEIVED WISDOM</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37586\" id=\"question-wrapper-37586\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"55966b72-50c6-45b4-8ee0-6c8cf8335fd3\">Occasionally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"acbe95b2-ef30-4397-925f-21fc7054d8e8\">people who buy a master product<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> find ways of using it that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"d8d1eeb7-9373-4dec-8f0e-951b4c44e3d3\">get around the necessity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"08a1d0ac-3346-44cd-899f-4946edb22bb9\">buying more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CONSUMABLES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37587\" id=\"question-wrapper-37587\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Wired <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"8974a201-73c0-47d0-b7ce-2cd8db7b2f5f\">never had<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> a (9)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"7cf03aa6-b58d-4ddc-95a3-8446cbb4c985\">with its customers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> about the use of the barcode readers.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LICENSING AGREEMENT</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose </span><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b><span> from the text for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 10-13.</span></p><p><span>Freebie marketing is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"49af4e04-bed9-4e2a-a546-acef99215008\">not permitted by law<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> for either illegal or legal (10)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"9a47451b-28cf-4940-9b31-bf242def2e1e\">products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"e6e02634-e475-4413-8d88-93bef9bab1f6\">This type of promotion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of goods such as tobacco and alcohol is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"4b715dde-af15-45d4-8571-29988fc5ccef\">not considered worth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the (11)_____ and has consequently been outlawed.</span></p><p><span>'Tying' is also prohibited. This is when the sale of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"6e6c9af1-a41f-4080-8734-bccfba4d1cd1\">an attractive product<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> is (12)_____ on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"40cccdb0-1447-4763-85c4-e069a5a38715\">the purchase of another<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"fcb17da3-03f0-4ef4-861b-126f55231b47\">It tends to occur<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> when the seller <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"495c5650-232b-4d61-8949-bcc76d938312\">takes advantage of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> a natural monopoly and is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"4b5f24cb-bac5-4323-b80a-9f101d802298\">generally considered to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)_____.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37588\" id=\"question-wrapper-37588\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HABIT-FORMING</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37589\" id=\"question-wrapper-37589\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOCIAL COST</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37590\" id=\"question-wrapper-37590\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CONDITIONAL</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37591\" id=\"question-wrapper-37591\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ANTI-COMPETITIVE BEHAVIO(U)R</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"4d1ac8f2-cab4-4447-9cfe-f268c24eeb6a","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"product innovation","passagePhrase":"came to realise, in a product that was used only a few times ... A simple, disposable blade that could be thrown away when it dulled would meet a real need and generate strong profits"},{"uid":"cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"marketing innovation","passagePhrase":"freebie marketing ... Gillette's ... was ... to the received wisdom of ... Freebie marketing involves two sets of items: a master product that is purchased once, and a consumable product that is frequently disposed of and repurchased on an ongoing basis"},{"uid":"1e684ba3-1e99-4636-a25a-978d0ba1b3e4 cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91","qNum":"2 7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"approach"},{"uid":"34dbc505-672f-4942-b3b1-2dd4d344fe03 cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91","qNum":"2 7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"contrary"},{"uid":"28c9dc41-4686-4dd5-a9e2-06453160fa71 cd62a0cb-f195-4cd7-8fe1-3fe1faec8d91","qNum":"2 7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"his era"},{"uid":"b1a201ae-2797-43f9-b9be-fb1f1968d24f","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Monopoly of consumables","passagePhrase":"maintain control over the creation and distribution of the consumables"},{"uid":"1a75476c-567e-41f2-bff7-be6355f4d7f9","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"vital for success","passagePhrase":"If this does not happen, then cheaper versions of the consumable items may be produced, leaving the original company without a source of profit"},{"uid":"55966b72-50c6-45b4-8ee0-6c8cf8335fd3","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Occasionally","passagePhrase":"In other instances"},{"uid":"acbe95b2-ef30-4397-925f-21fc7054d8e8 ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb","qNum":"4 8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"consumers"},{"uid":"ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Buyer ingenuity","passagePhrase":"sometimes find that uses for a master product ... to ... consumables ... Users discovered, however, that the machines could be easily modified and used for other purposes"},{"uid":"d8d1eeb7-9373-4dec-8f0e-951b4c44e3d3 ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb","qNum":"4 8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"circumvent the need"},{"uid":"08a1d0ac-3346-44cd-899f-4946edb22bb9 ff3bd4b1-66a0-4840-8769-0f0ccdb4affb","qNum":"4 8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"purchase"},{"uid":"8974a201-73c0-47d0-b7ce-2cd8db7b2f5f","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"never had","passagePhrase":"no ... was ever reached"},{"uid":"7cf03aa6-b58d-4ddc-95a3-8446cbb4c985","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"with its customers","passagePhrase":"between Wired and its magazine subscribers"},{"uid":"08d30eed-bf57-40c3-be98-7260609f3fe4","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"bankruptcy","passagePhrase":"company liquidation"},{"uid":"5bec8e15-e49b-457d-b178-a355f826073c","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"No give-aways","passagePhrase":"the use of freebie marketing ... on the basis of the product's"},{"uid":"e8841e8a-88f6-4b1f-afe1-9e6cdc97641d","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"addictive products","passagePhrase":"habit-forming goods"},{"uid":"9a47451b-28cf-4940-9b31-bf242def2e1e","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"products","passagePhrase":"substances ... goods"},{"uid":"49af4e04-bed9-4e2a-a546-acef99215008 5bec8e15-e49b-457d-b178-a355f826073c","qNum":"5 10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"restricted ... illegality ... outlawed"},{"uid":"e6e02634-e475-4413-8d88-93bef9bab1f6","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"This type of promotion","passagePhrase":"the use of freebie marketing to promote"},{"uid":"4b715dde-af15-45d4-8571-29988fc5ccef","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"not considered worth","passagePhrase":"not deemed worth"},{"uid":"565122a5-937a-4045-bc50-52bbb1190051","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"novel method of dual marketing","passagePhrase":"Another practice ... tying ... seller makes the sale of ... conditional on"},{"uid":"eb09a973-3e90-4ebe-90af-460e497abc84","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"ruled out","passagePhrase":"prohibited under antitrust laws"},{"uid":"565122a5-937a-4045-bc50-52bbb1190051 6e6c9af1-a41f-4080-8734-bccfba4d1cd1","qNum":"6 12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"one good"},{"uid":"40cccdb0-1447-4763-85c4-e069a5a38715 565122a5-937a-4045-bc50-52bbb1190051","qNum":"6 12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the acquisition of a second good"},{"uid":"fcb17da3-03f0-4ef4-861b-126f55231b47","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"It tends to occur","passagePhrase":"typically"},{"uid":"495c5650-232b-4d61-8949-bcc76d938312","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"takes advantage of","passagePhrase":"relies on the manipulation of"},{"uid":"4b5f24cb-bac5-4323-b80a-9f101d802298","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"generally considered to be","passagePhrase":"widely understood to constitute"},{"uid":"1e684ba3-1e99-4636-a25a-978d0ba1b3e4","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"new tactic","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"34dbc505-672f-4942-b3b1-2dd4d344fe03","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"ran against","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"28c9dc41-4686-4dd5-a9e2-06453160fa71","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Gillette's time","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"acbe95b2-ef30-4397-925f-21fc7054d8e8","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"people who buy a master product","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"d8d1eeb7-9373-4dec-8f0e-951b4c44e3d3","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"get around the necessity","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"08a1d0ac-3346-44cd-899f-4946edb22bb9","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"buying more","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"49af4e04-bed9-4e2a-a546-acef99215008","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"not permitted by law","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"6e6c9af1-a41f-4080-8734-bccfba4d1cd1","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"an attractive product","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"40cccdb0-1447-4763-85c4-e069a5a38715","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"the purchase of another","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_131":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><b><span>Tacoma Narrows Bridge</span></b></p><p><span>- Disaster Strikes</span></p><p><span>When the Tacoma Narrows Bridge opened for traffic on 1 July 1940, it was celebrated as a major engineering achievement. Even before construction was completed, however, flaws in the design were apparent; workers sucked on lemon slices to avoid motion sickness as the structure swayed in the relatively mild winds. Engineers tried three different revisions during construction to address the vibration problem. Initially, tie-down cables were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"9e0f5fd4-2562-408f-8ee9-f40cb46f2563\">anchored<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"88b0f4ff-4c1f-4e4e-8f09-73a328924a1f\">fifty-tonne bulkheads<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"7d66933d-dc9c-49fe-904d-9edfb128446e\">river banks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. These were ineffective, as the cables soon detached. Then a pair of inclined cable locks was introduced to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"19203b5b-95ba-4669-8905-bac6cb685cb1\">connect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> the main cables to the bridge deck at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"03ec9fcf-0311-4527-9be8-35c76bd344a9\">mid-span<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. These stayed throughout the bridge's lifespan, but did nothing to reduce vibration.A further measure—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"b2012067-b0dc-40de-b1fb-4726855fc831\">the installation of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> hydraulic dampers between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e221b67b-d90e-42d3-ad2d-877b1c49a576\">the towers and the floor system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>—was nullified because the dampers were compromised when the bridge was sand-blasted before painting.</span></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Simulation/reading/images/8581a66b2829c43594e1c5a8a417f214239bb3ca0b0bd1967eaa93f7628cccef.jpg\" title=\"\"></span></p><p><span>Shortly after opening, the bridge quickly acquired the fond nickname of 'Galloping Gertie' because of the way it would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"64d68df5-7277-47e5-bd1f-02df9c0e798e\">roll in either side-to-side<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"a37c81bc-f8f8-4a05-90b1-1d87feb33f3d\">length-ways movements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>—known in physics terms as the longitudinal and transverse modes of vibration respectively. These movements did not compromise the core integrity of the structure, but did make the crossing a somewhat white-knuckle affair. Many drivers reported seeing cars ahead disappear from sight several times as they sank into troughs from transverse vibrations (imagine the ripple across a packed stadium during a Mexican wave). The experience of a longitudinal wave is closely analogous, but more accurately associated with the waves one would encounter in the ocean. On a suspension bridge though,these waves are a unique experience—some dare-devils were happy to pay the 75c toll just for the thrill!</span></p><p><span>Four months later, however, a never-before-seen type of vibration began afflicting the bridge in what were still fairly gentle winds (about 40 kmph). Rather than the simple 'wave' motion that characterises longitudinal and transverse vibration, the left side of the bridge would rise while the right side fell, but the centre line of the road would remain completely level. This was proved when two men walked along the centre of the bridge completely unaffected by the rocking motions around them. Visually the bridge's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"a8753123-55a0-46b8-aaa6-970408e63348\">movements seemed to be more like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> a butterfly flapping its wings than a simple rolling motion. Engineers now understand this to be the torsional mode of vibration, and it is extremely hard to detect. In aeroplane design, for example, even minute shifts of the aircraft 's mass distribution and an alteration in one component can affect a component with which it has no logical connection. In its milder forms this can cause a light buzzing noise, similar to that which a wasp or a bumble bee makes, but when allowed to develop unchecked it can eventually cause the total destruction of an aeroplane.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"6964875b-28cb-4e2a-a793-7d1f529fe347\">The torsional mode of vibration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"e79a5a4b-e7c3-4fea-896e-4d16b3add343\">is the consequence of a set of actions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> known as aerostatic flutter. This involves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"13f0abf0-aa3b-4bc2-b1cf-8faf505742fe\">several different elements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of a structure <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"348f5fc5-a45c-45d2-bc27-7c578782bbee\">oscillating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> from the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"13416e9f-a646-4049-a61d-5314ca022686\">effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of wind, with each cycle of fluttering building more energy into the bridge's movements and neutralising any structural damping effects. Because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"a18f5d50-8075-43a3-9708-9b82a056e511\">the wind pumps in more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> energy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"60c22f4a-0d72-4388-ba36-51ba6a7c0d07\">than the structure can dissipate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, and the oscillations feed off each other to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"28cd12c5-ad71-499b-970c-96600c9a69c2\">become progressively stronger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, the aerostatic fluttering and torsional vibrations were all but assured to destroy the Tacoma Bridge on the morning of 7 November. At 11.00 am the fluttering had increased to such amplitude that the suspender cables were placed under excessive strain. When these buckled, the weight of the deck transferred to the adjacent cables which in turn were unable to support the weight.These cables buckled, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"6b5e53eb-9569-413f-9ccc-4adffaadaaaa\">leaving nothing to stop the central deck breaking off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> into the Tacoma River.</span></p><p><span>It was at around 10.15 am on 7 November that torsional vibration began afflicting the bridge. This made driving treacherous, and newspaper editor Leonard Coatsworth's <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"4e5b86f4-10c3-4e9d-8b29-5dabf3ea87b9 cdd7da43-2495-44b8-bb8d-65457a93e8c6\">car was jammed against the curb in the centre of the bridge</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> as he attempted to cross. Coatsworth tried to rescue his daughter's <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"3f96d031-2baf-4e39-8794-1123f040a998 e84c355a-d772-44a6-9fd3-3000bf9313fa\">cocker spaniel</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> from the back seat but was unsuccessful, and fearing for his life, crawled and staggered to safety on his own. At this point, an engineering professor named Bert Farquharson proceeded onto the bridge in an <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"3f96d031-2baf-4e39-8794-1123f040a998 e84c355a-d772-44a6-9fd3-3000bf9313fa\">attempt to save the frightened animal</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Farquharson had been video-recording from the banks of the river and had just returned from purchasing more rolls of film. As an avowed dog lover he felt obliged to attempt a rescue. Unfortunately, the professor too was bitten and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"3f96d031-2baf-4e39-8794-1123f040a998 e84c355a-d772-44a6-9fd3-3000bf9313fa\">retreated empty handed</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> ,walking off <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"83e986ff-5c71-462a-9e23-524d32cb608f a09cb2fc-d43b-4bac-a8ad-5aa2081e4d31\">just moments before the cables snapped and the giant concrete mass of the central deck caved inwards and disappeared into the river</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the notes below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 14-16.</span></i></p><p><span>Engineers used various techniques while building the bridge to reduce wobble:</span></p><p><span>● they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"9e0f5fd4-2562-408f-8ee9-f40cb46f2563\">attached<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> (14)_____ to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"88b0f4ff-4c1f-4e4e-8f09-73a328924a1f\">heavy blocks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"7d66933d-dc9c-49fe-904d-9edfb128446e\">shoreline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p><span>● they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"19203b5b-95ba-4669-8905-bac6cb685cb1\">fastened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> main cables to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"03ec9fcf-0311-4527-9be8-35c76bd344a9\">middle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of the (15)_____</span></p><p><span>● (16)_____ were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"b2012067-b0dc-40de-b1fb-4726855fc831\">placed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"e221b67b-d90e-42d3-ad2d-877b1c49a576\">the tallest parts of the structure and the deck<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37592\" id=\"question-wrapper-37592\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TIE-DOWN CABLES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37593\" id=\"question-wrapper-37593\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BRIDGE DECK</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37594\" id=\"question-wrapper-37594\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HYDRAULIC DAMPERS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the table below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>ONE WORD ONLY</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 17-19.</span></i></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"17\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Mode of Vibration</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"21\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Description</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"17\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(17)_____</span></p></td><td colspan=\"21\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"64d68df5-7277-47e5-bd1f-02df9c0e798e\">moves repeatedly to the left and right<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"17\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(18)_____</span></p></td><td colspan=\"21\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"89406880-ff30-45ac-89b3-4e26ec59681d\">up and down motion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"a37c81bc-f8f8-4a05-90b1-1d87feb33f3d\">like a wave<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"17\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>torsional</span></p></td><td colspan=\"21\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"a8753123-55a0-46b8-aaa6-970408e63348\">resembles motions of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> a (19)_____</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37595\" id=\"question-wrapper-37595\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LONGITUDINAL</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37596\" id=\"question-wrapper-37596\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRANSVERSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37597\" id=\"question-wrapper-37597\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BUTTERFLY</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the summary below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 20-24.</span></i></p><p><span>(20)_____ is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"e79a5a4b-e7c3-4fea-896e-4d16b3add343\">a series of actions leading to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"6964875b-28cb-4e2a-a793-7d1f529fe347\">torsional oscillation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"13f0abf0-aa3b-4bc2-b1cf-8faf505742fe\">Various components<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"348f5fc5-a45c-45d2-bc27-7c578782bbee\">move back and forth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> from the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"13416e9f-a646-4049-a61d-5314ca022686\">force<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of the (21)_____. Eventually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"a18f5d50-8075-43a3-9708-9b82a056e511\">the structure absorbs more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> (22)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"60c22f4a-0d72-4388-ba36-51ba6a7c0d07\">than it is able to disperse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and the (23)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"28cd12c5-ad71-499b-970c-96600c9a69c2\">increase in intensity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> until the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"6b5e53eb-9569-413f-9ccc-4adffaadaaaa\">structure collapses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> under the (24)_____.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37598\" id=\"question-wrapper-37598\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AEROSTATIC FLUTTER</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37599\" id=\"question-wrapper-37599\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WIND</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37600\" id=\"question-wrapper-37600\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ENERGY</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37601\" id=\"question-wrapper-37601\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OSCILLATIONS/VIBRATIONS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37602\" id=\"question-wrapper-37602\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(EXCESSIVE) STRAIN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>TWO</span></b></i><i><span> letters AE.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 25 and 26.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>TWO</span></b><span> of the following were on the bridge <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"83e986ff-5c71-462a-9e23-524d32cb608f a09cb2fc-d43b-4bac-a8ad-5aa2081e4d31\">at the time of the collapse</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. filming equipment</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"3f96d031-2baf-4e39-8794-1123f040a998 e84c355a-d772-44a6-9fd3-3000bf9313fa\">a small dog</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Leonard Coatsworth's daughter</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"4e5b86f4-10c3-4e9d-8b29-5dabf3ea87b9 cdd7da43-2495-44b8-bb8d-65457a93e8c6\">a vehicle</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Professor Farquharson</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37603\" id=\"question-wrapper-37603\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37604\" id=\"question-wrapper-37604\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"9e0f5fd4-2562-408f-8ee9-f40cb46f2563","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"attached","passagePhrase":"anchored"},{"uid":"88b0f4ff-4c1f-4e4e-8f09-73a328924a1f","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"heavy blocks","passagePhrase":"fifty-tonne bulkheads"},{"uid":"7d66933d-dc9c-49fe-904d-9edfb128446e","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"shoreline","passagePhrase":"river banks"},{"uid":"19203b5b-95ba-4669-8905-bac6cb685cb1","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"fastened","passagePhrase":"connect"},{"uid":"03ec9fcf-0311-4527-9be8-35c76bd344a9","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"middle","passagePhrase":"mid-span"},{"uid":"b2012067-b0dc-40de-b1fb-4726855fc831","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"placed","passagePhrase":"the installation of"},{"uid":"e221b67b-d90e-42d3-ad2d-877b1c49a576","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"the tallest parts of the structure and the deck","passagePhrase":"the towers and the floor system"},{"uid":"64d68df5-7277-47e5-bd1f-02df9c0e798e","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"moves repeatedly to the left and right","passagePhrase":"roll in either side-to-side"},{"uid":"a37c81bc-f8f8-4a05-90b1-1d87feb33f3d","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"like a wave","passagePhrase":"length-ways movements"},{"uid":"a8753123-55a0-46b8-aaa6-970408e63348","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"resembles motions of","passagePhrase":"movements seemed to be more like"},{"uid":"6964875b-28cb-4e2a-a793-7d1f529fe347","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"torsional oscillation","passagePhrase":"The torsional mode of vibration"},{"uid":"e79a5a4b-e7c3-4fea-896e-4d16b3add343","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"a series of actions leading to","passagePhrase":"is the consequence of a set of actions"},{"uid":"13f0abf0-aa3b-4bc2-b1cf-8faf505742fe","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Various components","passagePhrase":"several different elements"},{"uid":"348f5fc5-a45c-45d2-bc27-7c578782bbee","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"move back and forth","passagePhrase":"oscillating"},{"uid":"13416e9f-a646-4049-a61d-5314ca022686","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"force","passagePhrase":"effect"},{"uid":"a18f5d50-8075-43a3-9708-9b82a056e511","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"the structure absorbs more","passagePhrase":"the wind pumps in more"},{"uid":"60c22f4a-0d72-4388-ba36-51ba6a7c0d07","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"than it is able to disperse","passagePhrase":"than the structure can dissipate"},{"uid":"28cd12c5-ad71-499b-970c-96600c9a69c2","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"increase in intensity","passagePhrase":"become progressively stronger"},{"uid":"6b5e53eb-9569-413f-9ccc-4adffaadaaaa","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"structure collapses","passagePhrase":"leaving nothing to stop the central deck breaking off"},{"uid":"4e5b86f4-10c3-4e9d-8b29-5dabf3ea87b9 cdd7da43-2495-44b8-bb8d-65457a93e8c6","qNum":"25 26","questionPhrase":"a vehicle","passagePhrase":"car was jammed against the curb in the centre of the bridge"},{"uid":"3f96d031-2baf-4e39-8794-1123f040a998 e84c355a-d772-44a6-9fd3-3000bf9313fa","qNum":"25 26","questionPhrase":"a small dog","passagePhrase":"cocker spaniel ... attempt to save the frightened animal ... retreated empty handed"},{"uid":"83e986ff-5c71-462a-9e23-524d32cb608f a09cb2fc-d43b-4bac-a8ad-5aa2081e4d31","qNum":"25 26","questionPhrase":"at the time of the collapse","passagePhrase":"just moments before the cables snapped and the giant concrete mass of the central deck caved inwards and disappeared into the river"},{"uid":"89406880-ff30-45ac-89b3-4e26ec59681d","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"up and down motion","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_132":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Ebonics</span></b></p><p><span>Ebonics—also known by a host of other names such as African American Vernacular English, Black English, Black Vernacular, and so on—is an African-American language that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"272090cf-c477-4dbe-b653-74002e410961\">has its roots in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the trans-Atlantic slave trade, as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"cd06ea36-f334-4fb8-b2f7-5c982d64c444\">African captives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"2063ac8e-86a8-4044-939a-e641c6acb43c\">devised the means to communicate with each other<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and with their captors. In the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"b40b2c02-5e86-4c36-a0cc-f516db01b2cd\">South of the United States<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"bbd82879-d6cd-45c2-bad6-a9e83bfaf711\">these Pan-African languages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> ​​<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d9c3bb82-2316-4e8d-ba1e-b0fa5d869379\">co-mingled with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> Standard English and the Southern dialect. Many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9b3669de-44cb-4643-aa5d-3314c7495d64\">uniquely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> African-American components <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"391de275-53c4-4318-8a7c-33cb69776e0f\">have arisen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"bb34d592-17c7-48bf-9796-81d0e0664833\">over the last two centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, and all of these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"3f18a5d9-b27e-4cc5-9e00-fcb7ad62f4a4\">influences have forged what is now known as Ebonics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>In 1996, debates around the nature of 'Ebonics' in the United States came to a head. That year, the Oakland Unified School District in California <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"1d9b5412-59b5-43c9-a1d5-042dfd5945c9\">enacted Resolution 597-003<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"fef33008-5005-4544-b225-c28ea1577c03\">officially recognised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> that African-American students 'as part of their culture' and history as African people possess and utilize a language'. Alternatively referred to as Ebonics (literally 'black sounds'), African Communication Behaviours, and African Language Systems, this language was declared to be '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"88ebd4a7-a1ae-4813-ae9c-ab28af1808a2\">genetically-based<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>' rather than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"0376769e-19cc-4fe6-b231-7e1b96a2e245\">a dialect of Standard English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Within the profession of language research and pedagogy, a strong consensus formed behind the OUSD's decision to recognise Ebonics. Linguistics professor John Rickford noted that Ebonics was not simply characterised by erroneous grammar and a large slang vocabulary, but that underlying this language was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"b00b8921-2814-41e3-8c96-bf40fbb578c0\">a structured form and process of grammar and phonology that made English learning for Ebonics speakers far more complex<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> a task than simply dropping bad habits. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"d35ddd20-5958-4187-9c17-d39ac3a0a655\">English teachers, Rickford counselled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, must therefore <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"002cab5a-72d7-4957-9700-4cf5ae6ff26a\">accept and embrace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> these complexities.</span></p><p><span>The Linguistic Society of America (LSA) concurred with Rickford, adding that whether or not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"47f99fb4-8ea4-4adb-9f7f-2b09bce667cc\">Ebonics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> should be defined as a dialect or a language does not matter in terms of its 'validity'. While linguists studying Ebonics typically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"d002feda-b55a-4297-a509-aa246f609b47\">restrain from prescribing edicts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"98e91993-9dda-4b8e-afb1-2eab65b9c5e2\">in favour of tracking changes in form and style<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"5f5a48e0-6b77-4391-aac6-8cd15fa0f1f8\">the LSA did point to the fact that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> speakers of Swedish and Norwegian can typically understand each other while conversing in different 'languages' whereas Mandarin and Cantonese speakers cannot understand each other's 'dialects' to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"5f5a48e0-6b77-4391-aac6-8cd15fa0f1f8\">conclude that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"8d2783b4-bc70-4fd5-82f4-be2c6ed0ab3e\">spatial and social tensions, rather than strict linguistic criteria, were the crucial factors in defining these terms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>For many others, however, the OUSD's decision was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"dcfc24fc-edb9-4547-b810-b1a02ca773c6\">tantamount to endorsing lazy, vulgar and 'broken' English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>—the equivalent, perhaps, of acknowledging 'txt' speak or Internet slang as a valid form of expression. Recognising and fostering the use of informal, culturally-specific spoken language, say these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0b32a198-adec-4b86-a609-99b1cb9fc312\">detractors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, traps users in a kind of linguistic ghetto in which they can interact with other disenfranchised and excluded citizens, but cannot engage within the public sphere in a meaningful way. Because of the dominance of Standard English in the United States, Ebonics-only speakers are essentially unable to go to university and work in high-valued professions, and they are unlikely to be electable to any kind of public office (even in areas with a high density of black residents ,those who lose their Ebonics-tinged speech patterns tend to be more trusted).</span></p><p><span>Psychology professor Ladonna Lewis Rush has noted, however, that the OUSD's resolution did not promote Ebonics instruction as an alternative to Standard English in an either-or approach, but was intended to provide a better springboard for black achievement in English education. The systematic de-valuation of Ebonics in American society parallels, Rush has argued, the de-valuation of African-Americans in general. While a demeaning attitude can lead to social exclusion, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"7e8ee65f-7772-4550-97b7-8675031e329f\">teachers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3773eb33-a47d-4a19-921d-76036d147c0c\">are suggested to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"43a99bd6-aceb-4692-83fc-c91bca4b8545\">think inclusively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"43a99bd6-aceb-4692-83fc-c91bca4b8545\">encourage Ebonics speakers to use and celebrate their way of speaking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"994619de-618b-4559-a963-b66d9d8c727d\">understanding that the language of the workplace, and of academics, is Standard English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Nobel Prize-winning journalist Toni Morrison has also found a reciprocal, mutually enriching use for both Ebonics and Standard English. '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"7721d51c-b37a-4e4b-90ef-59a59767751a\">There are certain ideas and ways of thinking I cannot say without recourse to my Ebonics language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>...I know the Standard English. I want to use it to restore the other language, the lingua franca.'</span></p><p><span>In the media, the Ebonics controversy has mostly been portrayed as a revival of black-versus-white confrontation—this time over linguistic differences—but journalist Joan Walsh thinks there are basic elements inherent in the dispute that people do not want to openly discuss. She considers that there is <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"1a94df1b-a166-4fdb-9031-211782c7d1b3 c211b915-eef9-4745-8e2b-8a7de71062aa ca012a88-25dc-4b56-a7e6-f8455ed5b815\">increasing resentment by black parents and teachers</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> who see <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"8797c47f-5375-4f79-87a7-fa13a7468593 e9fd8d78-c345-4f34-84aa-a0f74c44a4cf fc1ac4ae-0b75-4527-a61c-dc8e98625f02\">enormous amounts of federal and state support going into Asian and Latino bilingual programmes</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. As immigration continues to increase, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"8797c47f-5375-4f79-87a7-fa13a7468593 e9fd8d78-c345-4f34-84aa-a0f74c44a4cf fc1ac4ae-0b75-4527-a61c-dc8e98625f02\">a greater proportion of the school budget</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> is going into these programmes. The question has to be raised:why should immigrant children get English-language assistance as well as reinforcement of their own language and culture while <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"27f82163-ae40-49db-9fa0-dab7b7be7a51 899e591f-1cc5-4a16-94db-c6aae45563f9 dd8188e8-8230-44e6-8b95-c00005997472\">native-born African-Americans</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"5ad2ad47-4238-4f0c-8657-d09843fed725 9d4d2441-5b2f-48d0-9348-ad4ce1764eb5 fb29a150-6ac2-4c7b-aae2-3a014e490f20\">get no such resources</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>? Walsh maintains inner city black children are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"5ad2ad47-4238-4f0c-8657-d09843fed725 9d4d2441-5b2f-48d0-9348-ad4ce1764eb5 fb29a150-6ac2-4c7b-aae2-3a014e490f20\">more isolated</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"1565f28c-1089-462b-b4ea-10718c9bdcf9 410fbd73-5c99-4886-bf28-2fc9af52a07d a295867b-6c9d-46f7-bd8c-067b7757c8c4\">in the past</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"5ad2ad47-4238-4f0c-8657-d09843fed725 9d4d2441-5b2f-48d0-9348-ad4ce1764eb5 fb29a150-6ac2-4c7b-aae2-3a014e490f20\">have less social interaction with those fluent in Standard English</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. For this reason they need help by trained teachers to translate the native tongue they hear at home into the English of the classroom.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"b654069b-560e-4461-8d9c-a0634918e7d4 d4030be9-d798-4e91-9b19-85af824a0985 f94365b3-69fd-48a6-bc90-058966db1280\">Ebonics should be treated as a black contribution to culture</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> in the way that jazz and rock-and-roll has been welcomed—<span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"b654069b-560e-4461-8d9c-a0634918e7d4 d4030be9-d798-4e91-9b19-85af824a0985 f94365b3-69fd-48a6-bc90-058966db1280\">the new vocabulary and imagery has added to the American language</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"b654069b-560e-4461-8d9c-a0634918e7d4 d4030be9-d798-4e91-9b19-85af824a0985 f94365b3-69fd-48a6-bc90-058966db1280\">rather than devalued it</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. In Walsh's eyes there has always been 'white mistrust of how black people handle their business', but 'in the public realm, white disdain yields black intransigence more reliable than 'i' comes before 'e'.'</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the summary below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the text for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 27-30.</span></i></p><p><span>Ebonics <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"272090cf-c477-4dbe-b653-74002e410961\">originated from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the (27)_____. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"cd06ea36-f334-4fb8-b2f7-5c982d64c444\">The prisoners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"2063ac8e-86a8-4044-939a-e641c6acb43c\">found a way to talk to other enslaved Africans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> as well as to (28)_____. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"b40b2c02-5e86-4c36-a0cc-f516db01b2cd\">southern USA<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"bbd82879-d6cd-45c2-bad6-a9e83bfaf711\">several African languages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> ​​<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"d9c3bb82-2316-4e8d-ba1e-b0fa5d869379\">mixed with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> English and the local (29)_____. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"bb34d592-17c7-48bf-9796-81d0e0664833\">Over time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"9b3669de-44cb-4643-aa5d-3314c7495d64\">distinctive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> (30)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"391de275-53c4-4318-8a7c-33cb69776e0f\">have been added to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"3f18a5d9-b27e-4cc5-9e00-fcb7ad62f4a4\">produce the Ebonics language of today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37605\" id=\"question-wrapper-37605\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(TRANS-ATLANTIC) SLAVE TRADE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37606\" id=\"question-wrapper-37606\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">THEIR CAPTORS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37607\" id=\"question-wrapper-37607\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(SOUTHERN) DIALECT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37608\" id=\"question-wrapper-37608\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(AFRICAN-AMERICAN) COMPONENTS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, AK, below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, AK, in boxes 31-37.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"7721d51c-b37a-4e4b-90ef-59a59767751a\">use Ebonics in order to express specific concepts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. to recognize the genetic differences between African -American students and others.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"002cab5a-72d7-4957-9700-4cf5ae6ff26a\">acknowledge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"b00b8921-2814-41e3-8c96-bf40fbb578c0\">systematic differences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> that Ebonics speakers must learn to overcome.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"dcfc24fc-edb9-4547-b810-b1a02ca773c6\">consider Ebonics as lazy English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> rather than a unique form of expression.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. to admit Ebonics users to university to gain more knowledge.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"8d2783b4-bc70-4fd5-82f4-be2c6ed0ab3e\">to make a statement about particular geo-societal relationships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. to compare Scandinavian languages ​​and Chinese dialects.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"fef33008-5005-4544-b225-c28ea1577c03\">declare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> Ebonics an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"88ebd4a7-a1ae-4813-ae9c-ab28af1808a2\">independent language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, and not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"0376769e-19cc-4fe6-b231-7e1b96a2e245\">a variation on English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"43a99bd6-aceb-4692-83fc-c91bca4b8545\">honour positive aspects of Ebonics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"994619de-618b-4559-a963-b66d9d8c727d\">emphasising the necessity of Standard English for formal use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"J\"><span>J. to approve the language of text messaging as a legitimate mode of communication.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"K\"><span>K. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"98e91993-9dda-4b8e-afb1-2eab65b9c5e2\">describe how Ebonics has developed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"d002feda-b55a-4297-a509-aa246f609b47\">without dictating rules for proper usage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> .</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37609\" id=\"question-wrapper-37609\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In 1996, the Oakland Unified School District <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"1d9b5412-59b5-43c9-a1d5-042dfd5945c9\">passed a measure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37610\" id=\"question-wrapper-37610\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"d35ddd20-5958-4187-9c17-d39ac3a0a655\">According to John Rickford, it is a good idea when teaching Standard English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37611\" id=\"question-wrapper-37611\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Linguists studying <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"47f99fb4-8ea4-4adb-9f7f-2b09bce667cc\">Black speech patterns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> are only able</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">K</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37612\" id=\"question-wrapper-37612\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"5f5a48e0-6b77-4391-aac6-8cd15fa0f1f8\">The LSA ruled that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"8d2783b4-bc70-4fd5-82f4-be2c6ed0ab3e\">definitions of dialect and language are generally a way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37613\" id=\"question-wrapper-37613\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"0b32a198-adec-4b86-a609-99b1cb9fc312\">Critics of vernacular alternatives to Standard English<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> tend</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37614\" id=\"question-wrapper-37614\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Ladonna Rush argues that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"3773eb33-a47d-4a19-921d-76036d147c0c\">it is important for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"7e8ee65f-7772-4550-97b7-8675031e329f\">educators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37615\" id=\"question-wrapper-37615\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Toni Morrison finds it necessary</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>THREE</span></b></i><i><span> letters, AG.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letters in boxes 38-40.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>THREE</span></b><span> statements below represent the views of Joan Walsh?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Linguistic issues are impeding black academic success rather than social issues.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"b654069b-560e-4461-8d9c-a0634918e7d4 d4030be9-d798-4e91-9b19-85af824a0985 f94365b3-69fd-48a6-bc90-058966db1280\">Ebonics deserves to be considered as nothing less than a gift to American society</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Children of non-English-speaking immigrants should be denied access to limited educational resources.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Ebonics is a debate that reflects <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"1a94df1b-a166-4fdb-9031-211782c7d1b3 c211b915-eef9-4745-8e2b-8a7de71062aa ca012a88-25dc-4b56-a7e6-f8455ed5b815\">rising multi-minority tensions and frustration</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> over <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"8797c47f-5375-4f79-87a7-fa13a7468593 e9fd8d78-c345-4f34-84aa-a0f74c44a4cf fc1ac4ae-0b75-4527-a61c-dc8e98625f02\">funding issues</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Ebonics is just another hostile encounter between black and white opponents.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. Many <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"27f82163-ae40-49db-9fa0-dab7b7be7a51 899e591f-1cc5-4a16-94db-c6aae45563f9 dd8188e8-8230-44e6-8b95-c00005997472\">urban African-American children</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"5ad2ad47-4238-4f0c-8657-d09843fed725 9d4d2441-5b2f-48d0-9348-ad4ce1764eb5 fb29a150-6ac2-4c7b-aae2-3a014e490f20\">do not have the same exposure to accepted norms of English</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> that they <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38 39 40\" data-uid=\"1565f28c-1089-462b-b4ea-10718c9bdcf9 410fbd73-5c99-4886-bf28-2fc9af52a07d a295867b-6c9d-46f7-bd8c-067b7757c8c4\">used to</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. Blacks need more flexibility in their dealings with the white public.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37616\" id=\"question-wrapper-37616\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37617\" id=\"question-wrapper-37617\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37618\" id=\"question-wrapper-37618\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D/F</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"272090cf-c477-4dbe-b653-74002e410961","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"originated from","passagePhrase":"has its roots in"},{"uid":"cd06ea36-f334-4fb8-b2f7-5c982d64c444","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The prisoners","passagePhrase":"African captives"},{"uid":"2063ac8e-86a8-4044-939a-e641c6acb43c","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"found a way to talk to other enslaved Africans","passagePhrase":"devised the means to communicate with each other"},{"uid":"b40b2c02-5e86-4c36-a0cc-f516db01b2cd","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"southern USA","passagePhrase":"South of the United States"},{"uid":"bbd82879-d6cd-45c2-bad6-a9e83bfaf711","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"several African languages","passagePhrase":"these Pan-African languages"},{"uid":"d9c3bb82-2316-4e8d-ba1e-b0fa5d869379","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"mixed with","passagePhrase":"co-mingled with"},{"uid":"9b3669de-44cb-4643-aa5d-3314c7495d64","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"distinctive","passagePhrase":"uniquely"},{"uid":"391de275-53c4-4318-8a7c-33cb69776e0f","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"have been added to","passagePhrase":"have arisen"},{"uid":"bb34d592-17c7-48bf-9796-81d0e0664833","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Over time","passagePhrase":"over the last two centuries"},{"uid":"3f18a5d9-b27e-4cc5-9e00-fcb7ad62f4a4","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"produce the Ebonics language of today","passagePhrase":"influences have forged what is now known as Ebonics"},{"uid":"1d9b5412-59b5-43c9-a1d5-042dfd5945c9","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"passed a measure","passagePhrase":"enacted Resolution 597-003"},{"uid":"fef33008-5005-4544-b225-c28ea1577c03","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"declare","passagePhrase":"officially recognised"},{"uid":"88ebd4a7-a1ae-4813-ae9c-ab28af1808a2","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"independent language","passagePhrase":"genetically-based"},{"uid":"0376769e-19cc-4fe6-b231-7e1b96a2e245","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"a variation on English","passagePhrase":"a dialect of Standard English"},{"uid":"b00b8921-2814-41e3-8c96-bf40fbb578c0","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"systematic differences","passagePhrase":"a structured form and process of grammar and phonology that made English learning for Ebonics speakers far more complex"},{"uid":"d35ddd20-5958-4187-9c17-d39ac3a0a655","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"According to John Rickford, it is a good idea when teaching Standard English","passagePhrase":"English teachers, Rickford counselled"},{"uid":"002cab5a-72d7-4957-9700-4cf5ae6ff26a","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"acknowledge","passagePhrase":"accept and embrace"},{"uid":"47f99fb4-8ea4-4adb-9f7f-2b09bce667cc","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Black speech patterns","passagePhrase":"Ebonics"},{"uid":"d002feda-b55a-4297-a509-aa246f609b47","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"without dictating rules for proper usage","passagePhrase":"restrain from prescribing edicts"},{"uid":"98e91993-9dda-4b8e-afb1-2eab65b9c5e2","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"describe how Ebonics has developed","passagePhrase":"in favour of tracking changes in form and style"},{"uid":"5f5a48e0-6b77-4391-aac6-8cd15fa0f1f8","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"The LSA ruled that","passagePhrase":"the LSA did point to the fact that ... conclude that"},{"uid":"8d2783b4-bc70-4fd5-82f4-be2c6ed0ab3e","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"to make a statement about particular geo-societal relationships ... definitions of dialect and language are generally a way","passagePhrase":"spatial and social tensions, rather than strict linguistic criteria, were the crucial factors in defining these terms"},{"uid":"dcfc24fc-edb9-4547-b810-b1a02ca773c6","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"consider Ebonics as lazy English","passagePhrase":"tantamount to endorsing lazy, vulgar and 'broken' English"},{"uid":"0b32a198-adec-4b86-a609-99b1cb9fc312","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Critics of vernacular alternatives to Standard English","passagePhrase":"detractors"},{"uid":"7e8ee65f-7772-4550-97b7-8675031e329f","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"educators","passagePhrase":"teachers"},{"uid":"3773eb33-a47d-4a19-921d-76036d147c0c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"it is important for","passagePhrase":"are suggested to"},{"uid":"43a99bd6-aceb-4692-83fc-c91bca4b8545","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"honour positive aspects of Ebonics","passagePhrase":"think inclusively ... encourage Ebonics speakers to use and celebrate their way of speaking"},{"uid":"994619de-618b-4559-a963-b66d9d8c727d","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"emphasising the necessity of Standard English for formal use","passagePhrase":"understanding that the language of the workplace, and of academics, is Standard English"},{"uid":"7721d51c-b37a-4e4b-90ef-59a59767751a","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"use Ebonics in order to express specific concepts","passagePhrase":"There are certain ideas and ways of thinking I cannot say without recourse to my Ebonics language"},{"uid":"1a94df1b-a166-4fdb-9031-211782c7d1b3 c211b915-eef9-4745-8e2b-8a7de71062aa ca012a88-25dc-4b56-a7e6-f8455ed5b815","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"rising multi-minority tensions and frustration","passagePhrase":"increasing resentment by black parents and teachers"},{"uid":"8797c47f-5375-4f79-87a7-fa13a7468593 e9fd8d78-c345-4f34-84aa-a0f74c44a4cf fc1ac4ae-0b75-4527-a61c-dc8e98625f02","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"funding issues","passagePhrase":"enormous amounts of federal and state support going into Asian and Latino bilingual programmes ... a greater proportion of the school budget"},{"uid":"27f82163-ae40-49db-9fa0-dab7b7be7a51 899e591f-1cc5-4a16-94db-c6aae45563f9 dd8188e8-8230-44e6-8b95-c00005997472","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"urban African-American children","passagePhrase":"native-born African-Americans"},{"uid":"5ad2ad47-4238-4f0c-8657-d09843fed725 9d4d2441-5b2f-48d0-9348-ad4ce1764eb5 fb29a150-6ac2-4c7b-aae2-3a014e490f20","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"do not have the same exposure to accepted norms of English","passagePhrase":"get no such resources ... more isolated ... have less social interaction with those fluent in Standard English"},{"uid":"1565f28c-1089-462b-b4ea-10718c9bdcf9 410fbd73-5c99-4886-bf28-2fc9af52a07d a295867b-6c9d-46f7-bd8c-067b7757c8c4","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"used to","passagePhrase":"in the past"},{"uid":"b654069b-560e-4461-8d9c-a0634918e7d4 d4030be9-d798-4e91-9b19-85af824a0985 f94365b3-69fd-48a6-bc90-058966db1280","qNum":"38 39 40","questionPhrase":"Ebonics deserves to be considered as nothing less than a gift to American society","passagePhrase":"Ebonics should be treated as a black contribution to culture ... the new vocabulary and imagery has added to the American language ... rather than devalued it"}]},"reading_u2_133":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><b><span>The development of travel under the ocean</span></b></p><p><span>For millennia humans have been intrigued by what lies beneath the sea, and although sub-marine travel was attempted from time to time, it did not become commonplace until the middle of last century. Several clever and innovative people had experimented with designs for submersible boats before then, but there was much loss of life and little success.</span></p><p><span>There had long been use of a primitive diving bell <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"50d495bc-67c2-4039-ba32-702ff1143e15\">for explorative purposes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> but it was as a war machine that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"aca34d0f-34da-4893-b880-26df7f1cadd8\">submarine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> came into its own. The first development in the history of American submarines was a small submersible with a hand-cranked screw-like oar and a crew of one. It was built before the American Revolutionary War (1775-1783) but was adapted for use against the British during this war. Although its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"17e18e5e-f104-4d18-85dc-a53b0138a733\">pilot<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> twice failed to fasten explosive devices to British ships before <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f53626f4-2a71-4f96-a13a-af8f45a1f8c8\">losing control of his vessel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, he escaped harm.</span></p><p><span>In 1800, an American inventor, Robert Fulton, designed an underwater machine that he called the Nautilus. His version brought in features that can still be found in some modern submarines, notably adjustable diving planes for better underwater manoeuvring, dual systems of propulsion, and a compressed air system that allowed it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"0c6c0826-2d5a-4029-b689-d0c5ce3b57c5\">to stay down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"38ee5ad4-86a6-444d-824c-0d0e7cad9a45\">for about four hours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> without surfacing.</span></p><p><span>Development of submersible vessels lagged a long way behind the continued progress in the design of surface ships until the American Civil War (1861-1865) when both sides tried out various designs. One of those, called the Hunley—named after its financier rather than its inventor—sank twice during training missions with 11 crew members losing their lives including Hunley himself. Notwithstanding these failures, it was commissioned again in 1864 to attack a ship in Charleston Harbor. A torpedo was used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"294090f6-e875-422f-a3cb-71e81ebdc3d0\">strike and scuttle the ship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9677fda3-e7cf-43c4-8e94-2f22ae25e85e\">a first in naval history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>—but the submarine never reappeared and once again the whole crew perished. Its potential had been recognised but there still remained the challenge of operating safely under the water.</span></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Simulation/reading/images/8de705f0b73dfb9b7b81fe2ea6872ab2d7ff2798950c4d914c41ef6a72a5b21f.jpg\" title=\"\"></span></p><p><span>The US Navy could appreciate the strategic benefits of having submarines in its fleet and held a competition to encourage design and construction of these underwater craft. The inventor, John Holland, won the competition and it was his sixth prototype, the Holland, that the navy bought and added to its fleet in 1900. This submarine was quite different from previous designs. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"39a1d4ef-4b96-4a72-be97-4a761e713e1c\">was propelled by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> a gasoline engine that turned a propeller while the vessel was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"28ad3429-7aa1-477b-a3e3-88fa40877066\">on the surface<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. When it submerged, the engine ran a generator to charge batteries to operate an electric motor. The improved propulsion methods were, unfortunately, highly dangerous. Not only is gasoline flammable and unstable, using it in the restricted environment of a submarine posed quite a hazard for the crewmen. There was another problem too: the batteries were not only heavy, cumbersome and inefficient but they were also extremely volatile.</span></p><p><span>During the same period as Holland's efforts were being trialled, a German scientist by the name of Rudolf Diesel, created an engine which used a fuel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"223d856e-65a5-4a58-83c5-9ca8a9f689cf\">less explosive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> than gasoline and which could consequently be stored safely. Another advantage was that there was no necessity for an electric spark to ignite the fuel. These safety improvements combined with better fuel economy allowed Diesel engines to power a submarine for longer on the surface; however, batteries were still needed to supply energy for underwater operation.</span></p><p><span>Although diesel-powered submarines were successful and used by the US Navy for almost 50 years, the search for a single power source carried on. It wasn't long before the concept of nuclear power was realised in Germany and taken up by an American physicist, Ross Gunn, who could envisage its potential in submersibles. A research team was put together to adapt the concept of nuclear power for use in submarines. In effect, modern nuclear submarines have on board a small nuclear power plant which produces a great amount of energy. This is used to heat water and create steam which drives a huge turbine which turns the propeller.</span></p><p><span>There have been many adaptations and technological improvements made to submarines over the years but the shape is basically the same. Obviously, it is a totally enclosed craft, cigar-shaped with narrowed ends. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"df2c582a-69c0-40f3-9635-fd50e7479525\">The outer hull is the largest part of the boat and forms the body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. The inner hull is designed to resist the considerable water pressure and insulates the crew from the cold. This is where the crew works, eats and sleeps. It also contains the engine room and the apparatus that makes clean air and clean water. Between the hulls are the ballast tanks for controlling buoyancy. There is a tall fin-shaped sail that comes up out of the hull. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"adc4e49a-cffa-48ee-aca1-c164c8ce2bef\">Inside the sail is the conning tower and extending from this, to the fore, there is a periscope<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (through which the captain can see the sea and sky when the submarine is near the surface of the water). Sonar is used for navigation deep below the surface. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f96c322e-8684-407e-970f-36218d176ef9\">The other projection from the conning tower is the radio antenna<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Underwater, there are two controls for steering the submarine. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"b1611998-7396-434d-bc4c-8992dd994536\">The rudder (like a tail fin) controls side-to-side movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> and diving planes influence rise and descent. There are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a121edc0-1ef4-426f-b4eb-9d28131ac6d4\">two </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 12\" data-uid=\"a121edc0-1ef4-426f-b4eb-9d28131ac6d4 d0d24a24-eba3-4192-995a-184c09ab63c9\">sets of diving planes</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a121edc0-1ef4-426f-b4eb-9d28131ac6d4\">: the forward sail planes</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> and the stern planes, which are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11 12\" data-uid=\"0c8e9929-82bd-4bbe-9f53-636b0e5c9165 d0d24a24-eba3-4192-995a-184c09ab63c9\">located at the back</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"0c8e9929-82bd-4bbe-9f53-636b0e5c9165\"> with the rudder</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> and propeller.</span></p><p><span>Advancing technology will undoubtedly result in different shapes and modes of operation and it is quite possible that, in the future, submarines will be manned by robots or computer technology that communicates information to land bases via satellite.</span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Answer the questions below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the text for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 1-6.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37659\" id=\"question-wrapper-37659\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What kind of underwater device was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"50d495bc-67c2-4039-ba32-702ff1143e15\">used to investigate the ocean<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> before <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"aca34d0f-34da-4893-b880-26df7f1cadd8\">submersible boats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> were invented?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(A) (PRIMITIVE) DIVING BELL</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37660\" id=\"question-wrapper-37660\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What was the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"17e18e5e-f104-4d18-85dc-a53b0138a733\">crewman<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of the first American-built submarine trying to do before his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"f53626f4-2a71-4f96-a13a-af8f45a1f8c8\">mission failed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FASTEN EXPLOSIVE DEVICES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37661\" id=\"question-wrapper-37661\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What gave the Nautilus <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"0c6c0826-2d5a-4029-b689-d0c5ce3b57c5\">the ability to remain submerged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"38ee5ad4-86a6-444d-824c-0d0e7cad9a45\">for a long time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMPRESSED AIR (SYSTEM)</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37662\" id=\"question-wrapper-37662\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>When was a submarine <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9677fda3-e7cf-43c4-8e94-2f22ae25e85e\">first used successfully<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"294090f6-e875-422f-a3cb-71e81ebdc3d0\">sink an enemy boat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(IN) 1864</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37663\" id=\"question-wrapper-37663\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What new type of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"39a1d4ef-4b96-4a72-be97-4a761e713e1c\">propulsion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> did the Holland use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"28ad3429-7aa1-477b-a3e3-88fa40877066\">on top of the water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(A) GASOLINE ENGINE [OR] GASOLINE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37664\" id=\"question-wrapper-37664\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>For what reason was Diesel's fuel considered <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"223d856e-65a5-4a58-83c5-9ca8a9f689cf\">safer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> than Holland's?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LESS EXPLOSIVE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the text for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 7-13.</span></i></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Simulation/reading/images/8c4d4aa84a2ac2ae617ee38a8883957063a4f92bef609526beced23430d171de.jpg\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37665\" id=\"question-wrapper-37665\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SAIL PLANES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37666\" id=\"question-wrapper-37666\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PERISCOPE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37667\" id=\"question-wrapper-37667\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RADIO ANTENNA</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37668\" id=\"question-wrapper-37668\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RUDDER</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37669\" id=\"question-wrapper-37669\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PROPELLER</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37670\" id=\"question-wrapper-37670\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STERN PLANES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37671\" id=\"question-wrapper-37671\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OUTER HULL</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"50d495bc-67c2-4039-ba32-702ff1143e15","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"used to investigate the ocean","passagePhrase":"for explorative purposes"},{"uid":"aca34d0f-34da-4893-b880-26df7f1cadd8","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"submersible boats","passagePhrase":"submarine"},{"uid":"17e18e5e-f104-4d18-85dc-a53b0138a733","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"crewman","passagePhrase":"pilot"},{"uid":"f53626f4-2a71-4f96-a13a-af8f45a1f8c8","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"mission failed","passagePhrase":"losing control of his vessel"},{"uid":"0c6c0826-2d5a-4029-b689-d0c5ce3b57c5","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"the ability to remain submerged","passagePhrase":"to stay down"},{"uid":"38ee5ad4-86a6-444d-824c-0d0e7cad9a45","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"for a long time","passagePhrase":"for about four hours"},{"uid":"294090f6-e875-422f-a3cb-71e81ebdc3d0","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"sink an enemy boat","passagePhrase":"strike and scuttle the ship"},{"uid":"9677fda3-e7cf-43c4-8e94-2f22ae25e85e","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"first used successfully","passagePhrase":"a first in naval history"},{"uid":"39a1d4ef-4b96-4a72-be97-4a761e713e1c","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"propulsion","passagePhrase":"was propelled by"},{"uid":"28ad3429-7aa1-477b-a3e3-88fa40877066","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"on top of the water","passagePhrase":"on the surface"},{"uid":"223d856e-65a5-4a58-83c5-9ca8a9f689cf","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"safer","passagePhrase":"less explosive"},{"uid":"df2c582a-69c0-40f3-9635-fd50e7479525","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The outer hull is the largest part of the boat and forms the body"},{"uid":"adc4e49a-cffa-48ee-aca1-c164c8ce2bef","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Inside the sail is the conning tower and extending from this, to the fore, there is a periscope"},{"uid":"f96c322e-8684-407e-970f-36218d176ef9","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The other projection from the conning tower is the radio antenna"},{"uid":"b1611998-7396-434d-bc4c-8992dd994536","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The rudder (like a tail fin) controls side-to-side movement"},{"uid":"a121edc0-1ef4-426f-b4eb-9d28131ac6d4","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"two ... : the forward sail planes"},{"uid":"a121edc0-1ef4-426f-b4eb-9d28131ac6d4 d0d24a24-eba3-4192-995a-184c09ab63c9","qNum":"7 12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"sets of diving planes"},{"uid":"0c8e9929-82bd-4bbe-9f53-636b0e5c9165 d0d24a24-eba3-4192-995a-184c09ab63c9","qNum":"11 12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"located at the back"},{"uid":"0c8e9929-82bd-4bbe-9f53-636b0e5c9165","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"with the rudder"}]},"reading_u2_134":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Vitamins - </span></b><i><b><span>To supplement or not?</span></b></i></p><p><span>Mineral, vitamin, and anti-oxidant health supplements make up a multi-billion dollar industry in the united states alone, but do they really work? Evidence suggests supplementation is clearly indicated in special circumstances, but can actually be harmful in others. For the general population, however, supplements have negligible or no impact on the prevention of common cancers, cardiovascular diseases, cognitive decline, mortality or any other major indicators of health. In the pursuit of a longer, happier and healthier life, there are certainly better investments for most people than a tube of vitamin supplements.</span></p><p><span>Particular sub-groups of the population can gain a proven <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"7c274f74-e0f8-4f6a-a97f-04396f1a1763\">benefit from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> supplementation. Folic acid has long been indicated as a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"485a013b-06ca-4672-aa3c-47c3d9ac9664\">prenatal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> supplement due to its assistance in foetal cell division and corresponding ability to prevent neural-tube birth defects. Since Canada and the United States decided to require white flour to be fortified with folic acid, spinal birth defects have plummeted by 75%, and rates of neuroblastoma (a ravaging form of infant cancer) are now 50% lower. In countries without such fortification, or for women on low-carbohydrate diets, a prenatal multivitamin could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"7c274f74-e0f8-4f6a-a97f-04396f1a1763\">make the crucial difference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. The United States Department of Health and Human services has concluded that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e11d6f8d-39e1-4dc5-83bf-d35dc1b311d5\">the elderly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> may also benefit from extra <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"350034ea-fbda-418c-8f08-d2eab9d7fdf7\">vitamin D<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"350034ea-fbda-418c-8f08-d2eab9d7fdf7\">calcium<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14 22\" data-uid=\"7c274f74-e0f8-4f6a-a97f-04396f1a1763 a7f8b22e-bf04-4b11-baf5-97d46c458200\">help prevent</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"a7f8b22e-bf04-4b11-baf5-97d46c458200\"> bone fractures</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>; and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"350034ea-fbda-418c-8f08-d2eab9d7fdf7\">zinc<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"350034ea-fbda-418c-8f08-d2eab9d7fdf7\">anti-oxidants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14 22\" data-uid=\"8aa958f3-d711-4918-874b-e670ecb7b58c a7f8b22e-bf04-4b11-baf5-97d46c458200\">maintain vision</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> while <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14 22\" data-uid=\"8aa958f3-d711-4918-874b-e670ecb7b58c a7f8b22e-bf04-4b11-baf5-97d46c458200\">deflecting macular degeneration</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8aa958f3-d711-4918-874b-e670ecb7b58c\"> in people who would otherwise be likely to develop this affliction</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>There is mounting evidence, however, for many people to steer clear of multivitamins. The National Institutes of Health has noted a 'disturbing evidence of risk' in tobacco users; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"cc63ea39-69a5-4d02-b007-6ba31ae85694\">beta-carotene<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, a common ingredient in multivitamins, was found over a six-year study to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e5fa6464-f2b5-4761-afd7-7cc2dcc26c2e\">significantly contribute to higher lung cancer and mortality rates in smokers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Meanwhile, excessive vitamin A (a supplement often taken to boost the immune system) has been proven to increase women's risk of a hip fracture, and vitamin E, thought to improve cardiovascular health, was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9102cc7b-2467-4af5-8a82-212803a67557\">contraindicated in a study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"5e6b7914-ebdc-4121-8625-3728646bac17\">demonstrated higher rates of congestive heart failure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> among such vitamin users. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a3245ac7-2fe6-4e3c-93f0-f6e74dcc5251\">Antioxidant supplementation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"094ad784-b6f6-481f-b75b-ae798ccf9c17\">has no purpose nor does it achieve anything<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, according to the Food and Nutrition Board of the National Academy of Sciences, and the Medical Letter Group has gone further in suggesting they may interfere with treatment and promote some cancers. Antioxidants are generally regarded as counteracting the destructive effect of free radicals in the body, but according to the Medical Letter's theory, free radicals may also serve the purpose of sending a powerful signal to the body's immune system to fix the damage. By taking supplements, we risk <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"50e430ec-d1b2-495a-863b-d8930ccf13e6\">undermining that message<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"50e430ec-d1b2-495a-863b-d8930ccf13e6\">upsetting the balance of antioxidants and free radicals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in the body. The supplements <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"50e430ec-d1b2-495a-863b-d8930ccf13e6\">counteract the free radicals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"50e430ec-d1b2-495a-863b-d8930ccf13e6\">the immune system is not placed on alert<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, and the disease could sneak through the gates.</span></p><p><span>One problem with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9e670e63-3725-4525-80c4-02d8ec50813b\">supplementation by tablet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> is the poor record on digestibility. These tablets are often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ccdc6249-4efa-4ad5-a42c-0113e8137900\">stocked with metal-based minerals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that are essentially miniature rocks, and our bodies are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ccdc6249-4efa-4ad5-a42c-0113e8137900\">unable digest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> them. Even <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e6ca6f70-8caf-4b7e-9a44-bc4171f8cb2e\">the vitamin elements of these pills that are theoretically digestible are often unable to be effectively extracted by our bodies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> when they arrive in such a condensed form. In salt lake city, for example, over 150 gallons of vitamin and mineral pills are retrieved from the sewer filters each month. According to the physician's desk reference, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e6ca6f70-8caf-4b7e-9a44-bc4171f8cb2e\">only about 10%-20% of multivitamins are absorbed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> by the body. The National Advisory Board is even more damning, suggesting that every 100 mg of tablet corresponds to about 8.3 mg of blood concentration, although noting that this can still <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"bd9db7a5-cd2d-40ef-8877-797dcec6771e\">potentially perform a helpful role in some cases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. In effect, for every $100 you spend on vitamin supplements, over $90 of that is quite literally flushed down the toilet.</span></p><p><span>A final argument against <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"94166754-db02-475e-a5b7-1f9c7804061a\">multivitamins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> is the notion that they can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"c1b9941e-db02-4cb4-be8f-9bc9feb81855\">lead people—consciously or not—to the conclusion that supplementation fills in the gaps of an unhealthy diet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and mops up afterwards, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"c1b9941e-db02-4cb4-be8f-9bc9feb81855\">leaving their bodies none the wiser<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> that instead of preparing a breakfast of fresh fruit and muesli, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"c1b9941e-db02-4cb4-be8f-9bc9feb81855\">popped a tiny capsule with coffee and a chocolate bar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. In a seven year study, however, the Heart Protection study did not find any positive outcome whatsoever from multivitamins and concluded that while vitamins in the diet are important, multivitamin tablets are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"f3c1079f-93ee-4d6e-ac19-60b969519bd1\">safe but completely useless<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. There is evidently no shortcut around the task of buying, preparing and consuming fresh fruit and vegetables every day. Boosting, supplementing and fortifying products <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"6e638272-5952-41ac-9f5b-e46ddbba1530\">alter people's very perception of what healthy food is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>; instead of heading for the fresh produce aisle in the supermarket, they are likely <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"6e638272-5952-41ac-9f5b-e46ddbba1530\">to seek out sugary, processed foods with a handful of extra B vitamins as a healthy choice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. We cannot supplement our way out of a bad diet.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter in boxes 14-16.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37672\" id=\"question-wrapper-37672\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The writer does not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"7c274f74-e0f8-4f6a-a97f-04396f1a1763\">recommend multivitamin supplementation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> for</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"485a013b-06ca-4672-aa3c-47c3d9ac9664\">pregnant women<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</li> <li>B. young children.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"8aa958f3-d711-4918-874b-e670ecb7b58c\">anyone prone to eye problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"e11d6f8d-39e1-4dc5-83bf-d35dc1b311d5\">old people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37673\" id=\"question-wrapper-37673\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>According to the writer, Vitamin E <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9102cc7b-2467-4af5-8a82-212803a67557\">has been shown to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"5e6b7914-ebdc-4121-8625-3728646bac17\">lead to heart problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</li> <li>B. be good for heart health.</li> <li>C. support the immune system.</li> <li>D. have no effect.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37674\" id=\"question-wrapper-37674\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Medical Letter group believes antioxidant supplementation</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. is ineffective in attacking free radicals.</li> <li>B. alerts the immune system to the presence of free radicals.</li> <li>C. attacks both free radicals and the immune system.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"50e430ec-d1b2-495a-863b-d8930ccf13e6\">prevents the immune system from responding to free radicals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></i></p><p><i><span>In boxes 17-21, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>YES</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NO</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37675\" id=\"question-wrapper-37675\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9e670e63-3725-4525-80c4-02d8ec50813b\">Some multivitamin tablets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"ccdc6249-4efa-4ad5-a42c-0113e8137900\">indigestible ingredients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37676\" id=\"question-wrapper-37676\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Some individual vitamins are better absorbed than others in a tablet form.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37677\" id=\"question-wrapper-37677\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Our bodies <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"e6ca6f70-8caf-4b7e-9a44-bc4171f8cb2e\">cannot distinguish food-based from supplement-based vitamins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37678\" id=\"question-wrapper-37678\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Multivitamins can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"c1b9941e-db02-4cb4-be8f-9bc9feb81855\">lead to poorer overall eating habits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in a person's life.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37679\" id=\"question-wrapper-37679\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"6e638272-5952-41ac-9f5b-e46ddbba1530\">typically know that fortified processed foods are not good for them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Classify the following groups of people according to whether they believe</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22 26\" data-uid=\"350034ea-fbda-418c-8f08-d2eab9d7fdf7 94166754-db02-475e-a5b7-1f9c7804061a\">Supplementation</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> may have a <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22 25\" data-uid=\"a7f8b22e-bf04-4b11-baf5-97d46c458200 bd9db7a5-cd2d-40ef-8877-797dcec6771e\">positive effect</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"cc63ea39-69a5-4d02-b007-6ba31ae85694\">Supplementation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> may have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"e5fa6464-f2b5-4761-afd7-7cc2dcc26c2e\">negative effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"a3245ac7-2fe6-4e3c-93f0-f6e74dcc5251\">Supplementation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24 26\" data-uid=\"094ad784-b6f6-481f-b75b-ae798ccf9c17 f3c1079f-93ee-4d6e-ac19-60b969519bd1\">has no effect</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter A, B or C, in boxes 22-26.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37680\" id=\"question-wrapper-37680\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The United States Department of Health and Human Services</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37681\" id=\"question-wrapper-37681\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>National Institutes of Health</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37682\" id=\"question-wrapper-37682\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Food and Nutrition Board of the National Academy of Sciences</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37683\" id=\"question-wrapper-37683\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The National Advisory Board</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37684\" id=\"question-wrapper-37684\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Heart Protection group</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7c274f74-e0f8-4f6a-a97f-04396f1a1763","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"recommend multivitamin supplementation","passagePhrase":"benefit from ... make the crucial difference"},{"uid":"485a013b-06ca-4672-aa3c-47c3d9ac9664","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"pregnant women","passagePhrase":"prenatal"},{"uid":"e11d6f8d-39e1-4dc5-83bf-d35dc1b311d5","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"old people","passagePhrase":"the elderly"},{"uid":"350034ea-fbda-418c-8f08-d2eab9d7fdf7","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"vitamin D ... calcium ... zinc ... anti-oxidants"},{"uid":"7c274f74-e0f8-4f6a-a97f-04396f1a1763 a7f8b22e-bf04-4b11-baf5-97d46c458200","qNum":"14 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"help prevent"},{"uid":"a7f8b22e-bf04-4b11-baf5-97d46c458200","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"bone fractures"},{"uid":"8aa958f3-d711-4918-874b-e670ecb7b58c a7f8b22e-bf04-4b11-baf5-97d46c458200","qNum":"14 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"maintain vision ... deflecting macular degeneration"},{"uid":"8aa958f3-d711-4918-874b-e670ecb7b58c","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"anyone prone to eye problems","passagePhrase":"in people who would otherwise be likely to develop this affliction"},{"uid":"cc63ea39-69a5-4d02-b007-6ba31ae85694","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Supplementation","passagePhrase":"beta-carotene"},{"uid":"e5fa6464-f2b5-4761-afd7-7cc2dcc26c2e","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"negative effect","passagePhrase":"significantly contribute to higher lung cancer and mortality rates in smokers"},{"uid":"9102cc7b-2467-4af5-8a82-212803a67557","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"has been shown to","passagePhrase":"contraindicated in a study"},{"uid":"5e6b7914-ebdc-4121-8625-3728646bac17","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"lead to heart problems","passagePhrase":"demonstrated higher rates of congestive heart failure"},{"uid":"a3245ac7-2fe6-4e3c-93f0-f6e74dcc5251","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Supplementation","passagePhrase":"Antioxidant supplementation"},{"uid":"094ad784-b6f6-481f-b75b-ae798ccf9c17","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"has no purpose nor does it achieve anything"},{"uid":"50e430ec-d1b2-495a-863b-d8930ccf13e6","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"prevents the immune system from responding to free radicals","passagePhrase":"undermining that message ... upsetting the balance of antioxidants and free radicals ... counteract the free radicals ... the immune system is not placed on alert"},{"uid":"9e670e63-3725-4525-80c4-02d8ec50813b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Some multivitamin tablets","passagePhrase":"supplementation by tablet"},{"uid":"ccdc6249-4efa-4ad5-a42c-0113e8137900","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"indigestible ingredients","passagePhrase":"stocked with metal-based minerals ... unable digest"},{"uid":"bd9db7a5-cd2d-40ef-8877-797dcec6771e","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"potentially perform a helpful role in some cases"},{"uid":"94166754-db02-475e-a5b7-1f9c7804061a","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"multivitamins"},{"uid":"c1b9941e-db02-4cb4-be8f-9bc9feb81855","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"lead to poorer overall eating habits","passagePhrase":"lead people—consciously or not—to the conclusion that supplementation fills in the gaps of an unhealthy diet ... leaving their bodies none the wiser ... popped a tiny capsule with coffee and a chocolate bar"},{"uid":"f3c1079f-93ee-4d6e-ac19-60b969519bd1","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"safe but completely useless"},{"uid":"350034ea-fbda-418c-8f08-d2eab9d7fdf7 94166754-db02-475e-a5b7-1f9c7804061a","qNum":"22 26","questionPhrase":"Supplementation","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"a7f8b22e-bf04-4b11-baf5-97d46c458200 bd9db7a5-cd2d-40ef-8877-797dcec6771e","qNum":"22 25","questionPhrase":"positive effect","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"094ad784-b6f6-481f-b75b-ae798ccf9c17 f3c1079f-93ee-4d6e-ac19-60b969519bd1","qNum":"24 26","questionPhrase":"has no effect","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_135":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>The Birth of Suburbia</span></b></p><p><b><span>A. </span></b><span>There is no single pivotal moment that could be separated out from any other as the conception of the suburban lifestyle; from the early 1800s, various types of suburban development have sprung up and evolved in their own localised ways, from the streetcar suburbs of New York to the dormitory towns outside of London. It is William Levitt, however, who is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"dd3c52a2-4d98-4995-bac1-9b890c005441\">generally regarded as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"67ed52f0-3370-48e0-8dc8-bae7970c3fc3\">father<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"4b9e8093-b1bc-495f-8c58-ed5214f30546\">modern suburbia<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. During World War II, Levitt served in the United States Navy where he developed expertise in the mass construction of military housing, a process that he streamlined using uniform and interchangeable parts. In 1947, the budding developer used this utilitarian knowledge to begin work with his father and architect brother constructing a planned community on Long Island, New York. With an emphasis on speed, efficiency, and cost-effective production, the Levitts were soon able to produce over 30 units a day.</span></p><p><b><span>B. </span></b><span>William Levitt correctly predicted the demand for affordable, private, quiet, and comfortable homes from returning GIS after World War II and with the baby boom starting to kick in. All the original lots sold out in a matter of days, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"8e1e002b-6cf7-4c0e-bd8c-25e50d7fadaa\">by 1951<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, nearly 18,000 homes in the area had been constructed by the Levitt fit Sons Company. Levit town quickly became <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4f8e559-f4d6-4090-91b3-ed8c603cdeb5\">the prototype of mass-produced housing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4f8e559-f4d6-4090-91b3-ed8c603cdeb5\">spurring the construction of similar projects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and even Puerto Rico, followed by a new industry, and soon a new way of life and a new ideal for the American family.</span></p><p><b><span>C. </span></b><span>One of the major criticisms of suburbia is that it can lead to isolation and social dislocation. With properties spread out over great swathes of land, sealed off from one another by bushes, fences and trees, the emphasis of suburban life is placed squarely on privacy rather than community. In the densely populated urban settlements that predated suburbs (and that are still the predominant way of life for some people), activities such as childcare and household chores as well as sources of emotional and moral support were widely socialised. This insured that any one family would be able to draw on a pool of social resources from their neighbours, building cohabitants and family on nearby streets. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"139d9d71-3e7f-4a3d-a036-84a48875965a\">Suburbia<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> breaks these networks down into individual and nuclear family units <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"0f5e429a-2e1a-4cb4-b4ca-887098f65c47\">resulting in an increase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"139d9d71-3e7f-4a3d-a036-84a48875965a\">anti-social behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> even amongst the wealthy. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"d0d1bacc-285c-412a-a85c-897e924251eb\">Teens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> from wealthy suburban families, for example, are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"0f5e429a-2e1a-4cb4-b4ca-887098f65c47\">more likely to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5909d683-bf6b-42ee-81bd-97522b254ab2\">smoke, drink alcohol, and use drugs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> than their poorer urban peers, and are also more likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"d0d1bacc-285c-412a-a85c-897e924251eb\">experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5909d683-bf6b-42ee-81bd-97522b254ab2\">depression and anxiety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p><p><b><span>D. </span></b><span>Another major problem with the suburban lifestyle is its damaging ecological impact. The comparison of leafy, quiet, and low-density suburbs with life in the concrete towers of sooty, congested urban conurbations is actually quite misleading; as it turns out if you want to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"907f691b-61bf-4e51-857d-0363dcd5ca08\">be kind to the natural environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"36f691d1-358d-4c76-bfe0-840371c26570\">the key<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"7c37225d-743a-4753-a0b2-1fc0f85555bb\">stay away from it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Suburbia fails the environmental friendliness test on a number of counts. Firstly, due to their low population density, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"87ad737e-6f1e-449b-862b-768e4f4b5bcd\">suburbs consume natural land at a much higher rate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> than high-density row housing or apartment buildings. Secondly, they <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27 34\" data-uid=\"87ad737e-6f1e-449b-862b-768e4f4b5bcd e039d679-43dc-4cc0-9f7f-cc4d005bd28c\">encourage</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"87ad737e-6f1e-449b-862b-768e4f4b5bcd\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27 34\" data-uid=\"3018cd62-dc1e-4779-a37a-f5b6a5b820e4 87ad737e-6f1e-449b-862b-768e4f4b5bcd\">the use of personal motor vehicles</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, often at a rate of one per family member, at the expense of public transport. It is also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"87ad737e-6f1e-449b-862b-768e4f4b5bcd\">much less efficient to provide electricity and water to individual suburban houses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> instead of individual units in an apartment building. In his comparison of urban and suburban pollution, Edward L. Glaeser concluded that we need to “<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cf7886ef-fa0d-4198-9416-8e70e1e4f11f\">build more sky towers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> – especially in California”. Virtually everywhere, he found cities to be cleaner than suburbs. And the difference in carbon dioxide emissions between high-density cities and their suburbs (for example, in New York) was the highest. Urban residents of New York can claim on average to produce nearly 15,000 pounds of carbon dioxide less than their suburban peers.</span></p><p><b><span>E. </span></b><span>Another negative aspect of suburban life is its stifling conformity and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"c115b15b-bde4-4dda-b71b-c0c61a8d0d09\">monotony of social experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. It was not just the nuts and bolts and the concrete foundations of suburban houses that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"c115b15b-bde4-4dda-b71b-c0c61a8d0d09\">got replicated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> street on street, block upon block, and suburb upon suburb; it was everything <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"c115b15b-bde4-4dda-b71b-c0c61a8d0d09\">from the shops and cultural life to people’s hopes, dreams, and aspirations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Suburbia gave birth to the “strip mall”, a retail establishment that is typically composed of a collection of national or global chain stores, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"587f7fdd-6723-4ef5-b041-8d948de3a27c\">all stocked with a centrally dictated, homogeneous array of products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. The isolation and lack of interaction in suburbs have also encouraged the popularity of television, a passively receptive medium for the viewer that, in the early days at least, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"16458e95-30e3-4799-9712-0126c5c5f3b0\">offered an extremely limited scope of cultural exposure compared with the wealth of experiences available in the inner city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Meanwhile, much of the inner-city “public sphere” has been lost with the suburban flight. The public sphere is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a9521563-a007-4695-8dbc-25adebcf5648\">the area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of social life in which people come together to freely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7b360dbc-8dca-4bc6-a043-cffcb7a4d577\">discuss and identify social problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"4173cd0d-6ba1-4416-98c5-490f992bfdb7\">In the city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, this has traditionally occurred around newsstands, in coffee houses, salons, theatres, meeting halls, and so on. Suburbia has not found a way to replace this special type of social experience, however. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"9d629f53-94b4-4791-b144-a177c750633c\">Social meeting points in the suburbs tend to be based exclusively around specific interests such as sports or cultural clubs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, with no broad forms of daily social interaction.</span></p><p><b><span>F. </span></b><span>These points do not suggest the idea of suburbia itself is flawed, but that it has not been executed in a way that takes into account the full spectrum of human needs and desires. This likely reflects the hasty, thrown-together nature of early suburban development. With <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"30987f53-f83e-4e33-a528-1f068f1192d9 d0feb6cd-8223-45c3-9999-a5bfdb918003\">the baby boom rippling</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> across Western countries and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"30987f53-f83e-4e33-a528-1f068f1192d9 d0feb6cd-8223-45c3-9999-a5bfdb918003\">demand for family-friendly housing skyrocketing</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, developers and city planners were <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"5c17f681-df52-4f7d-9b85-f3e7f9ae9978 dd831be7-0ed0-4f3b-9bb1-18aafd6fae0c\">unable to develop sophisticated models</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Now, however, we should take time to consider what has gone wrong and how we can <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"73958530-9fb1-44d4-a186-4ef4dc85419b 7b0ce668-1762-4c8c-93d8-b0afe303ac24\">reconfigure the suburb</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. How can we <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"15583c00-146c-4527-96df-0f281e2a0f5e 1e47cdcf-6d4b-4c85-a7d8-284562f6cb36\">imbue suburban life with the lost sphere of public discussion and debate</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>? How can people <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"15583c00-146c-4527-96df-0f281e2a0f5e 1e47cdcf-6d4b-4c85-a7d8-284562f6cb36\">maintain their privacy without sacrificing a sense of community</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>? How can we <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"15583c00-146c-4527-96df-0f281e2a0f5e 1e47cdcf-6d4b-4c85-a7d8-284562f6cb36\">use new technologies to make suburbs environmentally friendly</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>? These are questions for which the developers of tomorrow will have to find answers, lest the dream of suburbia become the nightmare of Disturbia.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has six paragraphs, A-F.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 27-31.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37685\" id=\"question-wrapper-37685\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"87ad737e-6f1e-449b-862b-768e4f4b5bcd\">reason<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"cf7886ef-fa0d-4198-9416-8e70e1e4f11f\">construct taller buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37686\" id=\"question-wrapper-37686\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a9521563-a007-4695-8dbc-25adebcf5648\">Where<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> people might <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"7b360dbc-8dca-4bc6-a043-cffcb7a4d577\">discuss issues of societal concern<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"4173cd0d-6ba1-4416-98c5-490f992bfdb7\">in urban locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37687\" id=\"question-wrapper-37687\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"67ed52f0-3370-48e0-8dc8-bae7970c3fc3\">founder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of what is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"dd3c52a2-4d98-4995-bac1-9b890c005441\">broadly understood as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"4b9e8093-b1bc-495f-8c58-ed5214f30546\">contemporary \"suburbs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>\"</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37688\" id=\"question-wrapper-37688\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5909d683-bf6b-42ee-81bd-97522b254ab2\">Examples of problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"d0d1bacc-285c-412a-a85c-897e924251eb\">suffered by youth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"139d9d71-3e7f-4a3d-a036-84a48875965a\">suburban lifestyles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"0f5e429a-2e1a-4cb4-b4ca-887098f65c47\">make worse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37689\" id=\"question-wrapper-37689\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4f8e559-f4d6-4090-91b3-ed8c603cdeb5\">model for suburban development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"8e1e002b-6cf7-4c0e-bd8c-25e50d7fadaa\">in the latter half of the 20th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 32-38, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>YES</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NO</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37690\" id=\"question-wrapper-37690\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"36f691d1-358d-4c76-bfe0-840371c26570\">good principle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"907f691b-61bf-4e51-857d-0363dcd5ca08\">ecological preservation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"7c37225d-743a-4753-a0b2-1fc0f85555bb\">avoid human interference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37691\" id=\"question-wrapper-37691\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In some countries, suburbs are more environmentally friendly than in the USA.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37692\" id=\"question-wrapper-37692\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Suburban development <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"e039d679-43dc-4cc0-9f7f-cc4d005bd28c\">fosters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the use of both public and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"3018cd62-dc1e-4779-a37a-f5b6a5b820e4\">private forms of transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37693\" id=\"question-wrapper-37693\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>People <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"c115b15b-bde4-4dda-b71b-c0c61a8d0d09\">cannot relate to each other in suburbs because their lives are too different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37694\" id=\"question-wrapper-37694\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"587f7fdd-6723-4ef5-b041-8d948de3a27c\">not much variety amongst the goods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> at a strip mall.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37695\" id=\"question-wrapper-37695\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Television has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"16458e95-30e3-4799-9712-0126c5c5f3b0\">not tended to offer the same diversity as urban cultural outlets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37696\" id=\"question-wrapper-37696\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>There are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"9d629f53-94b4-4791-b144-a177c750633c\">no ways for people to get together and interact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> in suburbs.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>TWO</span></b></i><i><span> letters A-E.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 39 and 40.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>TWO</span></b><span> of the following does the author conclude?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. The very concept of a healthy suburban lifestyle is problematic.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"30987f53-f83e-4e33-a528-1f068f1192d9 d0feb6cd-8223-45c3-9999-a5bfdb918003\">The speed of suburban growth</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"5c17f681-df52-4f7d-9b85-f3e7f9ae9978 dd831be7-0ed0-4f3b-9bb1-18aafd6fae0c\">contributed to its imperfections</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. By <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"15583c00-146c-4527-96df-0f281e2a0f5e 1e47cdcf-6d4b-4c85-a7d8-284562f6cb36\">thinking about human and ecological needs</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"73958530-9fb1-44d4-a186-4ef4dc85419b 7b0ce668-1762-4c8c-93d8-b0afe303ac24\">suburbs can become better places to live</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Developers will have to think about ways of living that do not require suburbs.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Suburbs have their downsides, but they are the best way for parents to raise children.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37697\" id=\"question-wrapper-37697\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37698\" id=\"question-wrapper-37698\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"dd3c52a2-4d98-4995-bac1-9b890c005441","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"broadly understood as","passagePhrase":"generally regarded as"},{"uid":"67ed52f0-3370-48e0-8dc8-bae7970c3fc3","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"founder","passagePhrase":"father"},{"uid":"4b9e8093-b1bc-495f-8c58-ed5214f30546","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"contemporary \"suburbs","passagePhrase":"modern suburbia"},{"uid":"8e1e002b-6cf7-4c0e-bd8c-25e50d7fadaa","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"in the latter half of the 20th century","passagePhrase":"by 1951"},{"uid":"d4f8e559-f4d6-4090-91b3-ed8c603cdeb5","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"model for suburban development","passagePhrase":"the prototype of mass-produced housing ... spurring the construction of similar projects"},{"uid":"139d9d71-3e7f-4a3d-a036-84a48875965a","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"suburban lifestyles","passagePhrase":"Suburbia ... anti-social behaviour"},{"uid":"0f5e429a-2e1a-4cb4-b4ca-887098f65c47","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"make worse","passagePhrase":"resulting in an increase ... more likely to"},{"uid":"d0d1bacc-285c-412a-a85c-897e924251eb","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"suffered by youth","passagePhrase":"Teens ... experience"},{"uid":"5909d683-bf6b-42ee-81bd-97522b254ab2","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Examples of problems","passagePhrase":"smoke, drink alcohol, and use drugs ... depression and anxiety"},{"uid":"907f691b-61bf-4e51-857d-0363dcd5ca08","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"ecological preservation","passagePhrase":"be kind to the natural environment"},{"uid":"36f691d1-358d-4c76-bfe0-840371c26570","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"good principle","passagePhrase":"the key"},{"uid":"7c37225d-743a-4753-a0b2-1fc0f85555bb","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"avoid human interference","passagePhrase":"stay away from it"},{"uid":"87ad737e-6f1e-449b-862b-768e4f4b5bcd","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"reason","passagePhrase":"suburbs consume natural land at a much higher rate ... much less efficient to provide electricity and water to individual suburban houses"},{"uid":"87ad737e-6f1e-449b-862b-768e4f4b5bcd e039d679-43dc-4cc0-9f7f-cc4d005bd28c","qNum":"27 34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"encourage"},{"uid":"3018cd62-dc1e-4779-a37a-f5b6a5b820e4 87ad737e-6f1e-449b-862b-768e4f4b5bcd","qNum":"27 34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the use of personal motor vehicles"},{"uid":"cf7886ef-fa0d-4198-9416-8e70e1e4f11f","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"construct taller buildings","passagePhrase":"build more sky towers"},{"uid":"587f7fdd-6723-4ef5-b041-8d948de3a27c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"not much variety amongst the goods","passagePhrase":"all stocked with a centrally dictated, homogeneous array of products"},{"uid":"16458e95-30e3-4799-9712-0126c5c5f3b0","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"not tended to offer the same diversity as urban cultural outlets","passagePhrase":"offered an extremely limited scope of cultural exposure compared with the wealth of experiences available in the inner city"},{"uid":"a9521563-a007-4695-8dbc-25adebcf5648","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Where","passagePhrase":"the area"},{"uid":"7b360dbc-8dca-4bc6-a043-cffcb7a4d577","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"discuss issues of societal concern","passagePhrase":"discuss and identify social problems"},{"uid":"4173cd0d-6ba1-4416-98c5-490f992bfdb7","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"in urban locations","passagePhrase":"In the city"},{"uid":"30987f53-f83e-4e33-a528-1f068f1192d9 d0feb6cd-8223-45c3-9999-a5bfdb918003","qNum":"39 40","questionPhrase":"The speed of suburban growth","passagePhrase":"the baby boom rippling ... demand for family-friendly housing skyrocketing"},{"uid":"5c17f681-df52-4f7d-9b85-f3e7f9ae9978 dd831be7-0ed0-4f3b-9bb1-18aafd6fae0c","qNum":"39 40","questionPhrase":"contributed to its imperfections","passagePhrase":"unable to develop sophisticated models"},{"uid":"73958530-9fb1-44d4-a186-4ef4dc85419b 7b0ce668-1762-4c8c-93d8-b0afe303ac24","qNum":"39 40","questionPhrase":"suburbs can become better places to live","passagePhrase":"reconfigure the suburb"},{"uid":"15583c00-146c-4527-96df-0f281e2a0f5e 1e47cdcf-6d4b-4c85-a7d8-284562f6cb36","qNum":"39 40","questionPhrase":"thinking about human and ecological needs","passagePhrase":"imbue suburban life with the lost sphere of public discussion and debate ... maintain their privacy without sacrificing a sense of community ... use new technologies to make suburbs environmentally friendly"},{"uid":"e039d679-43dc-4cc0-9f7f-cc4d005bd28c","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"fosters","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"3018cd62-dc1e-4779-a37a-f5b6a5b820e4","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"private forms of transport","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_136":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><i><b><span>Nu shu</span></b></i></p><p><span>— </span><i><b><span>a secret language</span></b></i><span> —</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"1\"><span>A. It is sometimes said that men and women communicate in different languages. For hundreds of years in the Jianyong County of Hunan province, China, this was quite literally the case. Sometime between 400 and 1,000 years ago women <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f1a81a86-56d7-4111-9e76-535592cfb75b\">defied the patriarchal norms of the time that forbade them to read or write<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f1a81a86-56d7-4111-9e76-535592cfb75b\">conceived of </span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f1a81a86-56d7-4111-9e76-535592cfb75b\">Nu shu<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></i><span> —literally, 'women's language'—a secretive script and language of their own. Through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"87e742bc-7fb1-44b5-b83a-880f05d5cad4\">building informal networks of 'sworn sisters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>' who committed themselves to teaching the language only to other women, and by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"87e742bc-7fb1-44b5-b83a-880f05d5cad4\">using it artistically in ways that could be passed off as artwork<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> (such as writing characters on a decorative fan), </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> was able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"87e742bc-7fb1-44b5-b83a-880f05d5cad4\">grow and spread<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> without attracting too much suspicion.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"2\"><span>B. </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> has many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"4dcc02d2-a582-44dd-8c7a-94b3389566fe\">orthographical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> distinctions from the standard Chinese <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"4dcc02d2-a582-44dd-8c7a-94b3389566fe\">script<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Whereas standard Chinese has large, bold strokes that look as if they might have been shaped with a thick permanent marker pen, </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"4dcc02d2-a582-44dd-8c7a-94b3389566fe\">characters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"464f7c4e-4152-4224-a52f-8e94864487c7\">thin, slanted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"464f7c4e-4152-4224-a52f-8e94864487c7\">slightly 'scratchy' appearance that bears more similarity to calligraphy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Whereas standard Chinese is logographic, with characters that represent words and meanings, </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"464f7c4e-4152-4224-a52f-8e94864487c7\">completely phonetic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>—each character represents a sound; the meaning must be acquired from the context of what is being said. Users of </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> developed coded meanings for various words and phrases, but it is likely that only a tiny fraction of these will ever be known. Many secrets of </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> have gone to the grave.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"3\"><span>C. </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> was developed as <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22\">a way to allow women to </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3 6 7\" data-uid=\"4f8ad21b-0fcc-43b2-9904-241e59127054 9c3d750f-82c5-496d-8f53-3387c75dca59 dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22\">communicate with one another</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22\"> in confidence</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. To some extent this demand came from <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7\" data-uid=\"1efc8dfe-dc15-4d5a-9ac8-2135a5afdfbd 69daf254-7b84-4456-85e1-f8f918317af8\">a desire</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> for privacy, and </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22\">allowed women a forum for personal written communication in a society that was dominated by a male-orientated social culture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. There was also a practical element to the rise of </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> , however: until the mid 20th century, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7\" data-uid=\"69257c46-1a60-486e-a6ac-5574ab15f4b0 a5beaa86-8c5a-4c82-84da-7dc2dc7f9653\">women were rarely encouraged to become literate</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in the standard Chinese script. </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22\">provided </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3 6 7\" data-uid=\"69257c46-1a60-486e-a6ac-5574ab15f4b0 a5beaa86-8c5a-4c82-84da-7dc2dc7f9653 dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22\">a practical and easy-to-learn alternative</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. Women who were separated from their families and friends by marriage could therefore <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3 6 7\" data-uid=\"4f8ad21b-0fcc-43b2-9904-241e59127054 9c3d750f-82c5-496d-8f53-3387c75dca59 dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22\">send 'letters' to each other</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. Unlike traditional correspondence, however, </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> characters were painted or embroidered onto everyday items like fans, pillowcases and handkerchiefs and embodied in 'artwork' in order to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7\" data-uid=\"b625105b-e10c-42f7-a943-098e67d82f9b c0569887-3829-417b-ad5c-af8fcec4a813\">avoid making men suspicious</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"4\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"2a247639-0a10-43f2-9b77-e5ab052de3cb\">After the Chinese Revolution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a10f0104-fb4b-46c1-94d4-e110155a760d\">more women were encouraged to become literate in the standard Chinese script<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be985227-8507-4318-a2e7-0f330fd56740\">much of the need for a special form of women's communication was dampened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. When the Red Guard discovered the script in the 1960s, they thought it to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c06b4420-5177-44e8-a926-5b9f8ab46f70\">a code used for espionage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Upon learning that it was a secret women's language they were suspicious and fearful. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be985227-8507-4318-a2e7-0f330fd56740\">Numerous letters, weavings, embroideries and other artifacts were destroyed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be985227-8507-4318-a2e7-0f330fd56740\">women were forbidden to practise </span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be985227-8507-4318-a2e7-0f330fd56740\">Nu shu</span></span></i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be985227-8507-4318-a2e7-0f330fd56740\"> customs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. As a consequence, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\">the </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4 11\" data-uid=\"096ba422-c254-4dfe-8782-10e5c9cf79f7 97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\">generational chains of linguistic transmission</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\"> were </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4 11\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af c2d43e62-5e43-495a-a0d9-b5309c121858\">broken up</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\">the language </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4 11\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af c2d43e62-5e43-495a-a0d9-b5309c121858\">ceased</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4 11\" data-uid=\"096ba422-c254-4dfe-8782-10e5c9cf79f7 97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\">being passed down through sworn sisters</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. There is <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4 11\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af c2d43e62-5e43-495a-a0d9-b5309c121858\">no longer anyone alive</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\"> who has learnt </span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\">Nu shu</span></span></i><span><span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\"> in this </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4 11\" data-uid=\"096ba422-c254-4dfe-8782-10e5c9cf79f7 97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\">traditional manner</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>; Yang Huanyi, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\">the last proficient user of the language, died<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> on September 20, 2004, in her late 90s.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"5\"><span>E. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7741316e-110c-4d05-a2f1-da733c4ad5a2\">recent years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7741316e-110c-4d05-a2f1-da733c4ad5a2\">popular and scholarly interest in </span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7741316e-110c-4d05-a2f1-da733c4ad5a2\">Nu shu</span></span></i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7741316e-110c-4d05-a2f1-da733c4ad5a2\"> has blossomed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. The Ford Foundation granted US $209,000 to build a </span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"01e7375e-8ff1-483c-bd5c-e54a7ce90091\">Nu shu</span></span></i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"01e7375e-8ff1-483c-bd5c-e54a7ce90091\"> Museum that houses artifacts such as audio recordings, manuscripts and articles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, some of which date back over 100 years. The investment from Hong Kong SAR is also being used to build <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"01e7375e-8ff1-483c-bd5c-e54a7ce90091\">infrastructure at potential tourist sites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in Hunan, and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5 13\" data-uid=\"01e7375e-8ff1-483c-bd5c-e54a7ce90091 60d8c17c-abb2-4566-b886-2b5d62643aa4\">some schools in the area have begun instruction in the language</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. Incidentally, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"01e7375e-8ff1-483c-bd5c-e54a7ce90091\">the use of </span></span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"01e7375e-8ff1-483c-bd5c-e54a7ce90091\">Nu shu</span></span></i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"01e7375e-8ff1-483c-bd5c-e54a7ce90091\"> is also a theme in Lisa See's historical novel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, </span><i><span>Snow Flower and the</span></i><i><span>Secret Fan</span></i><span> , which has since been adapted for film.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has five sections A-E.</span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct number i-viii in boxes 1-5.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. Financial costs</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"be985227-8507-4318-a2e7-0f330fd56740\">Decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af\">disuse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"f1a81a86-56d7-4111-9e76-535592cfb75b\">Birth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"87e742bc-7fb1-44b5-b83a-880f05d5cad4\">development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. Political uses of </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22\">social role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. Last of the </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> speakers</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"464f7c4e-4152-4224-a52f-8e94864487c7\">Characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"4dcc02d2-a582-44dd-8c7a-94b3389566fe\">written<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"01e7375e-8ff1-483c-bd5c-e54a7ce90091\">Revival<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7741316e-110c-4d05-a2f1-da733c4ad5a2\">contemporary interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37739\" id=\"question-wrapper-37739\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37740\" id=\"question-wrapper-37740\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37741\" id=\"question-wrapper-37741\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37742\" id=\"question-wrapper-37742\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37743\" id=\"question-wrapper-37743\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>TWO</span></b></i><i><span> letters A-E.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 6-7.</span></i></p><p><span>Why was there <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7\" data-uid=\"1efc8dfe-dc15-4d5a-9ac8-2135a5afdfbd 69daf254-7b84-4456-85e1-f8f918317af8\">a need for</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> </span><i><span>Nu shu</span></i><span> ?</span></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>TWO</span></b><span> reasons are given in the text?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. It provided new artistic opportunities for female artisans.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. It was <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7\" data-uid=\"69257c46-1a60-486e-a6ac-5574ab15f4b0 a5beaa86-8c5a-4c82-84da-7dc2dc7f9653\">a way for uneducated women to read and write</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Not enough women were taking an interest in literature.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. It was a way for women to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7\" data-uid=\"4f8ad21b-0fcc-43b2-9904-241e59127054 9c3d750f-82c5-496d-8f53-3387c75dca59\">correspond</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6 7\" data-uid=\"b625105b-e10c-42f7-a943-098e67d82f9b c0569887-3829-417b-ad5c-af8fcec4a813\">without men knowing</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. It helped women believe in themselves and their abilities.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37744\" id=\"question-wrapper-37744\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37745\" id=\"question-wrapper-37745\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 8-13, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>TRUE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>FALSE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if there is no information on this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37746\" id=\"question-wrapper-37746\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"2a247639-0a10-43f2-9b77-e5ab052de3cb\">post-Revolution government<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a10f0104-fb4b-46c1-94d4-e110155a760d\">did not want women to read or write in any language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37747\" id=\"question-wrapper-37747\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>At first, the Red Guard thought Nu shu might be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"c06b4420-5177-44e8-a926-5b9f8ab46f70\">a tool for spies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37748\" id=\"question-wrapper-37748\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Women could be punished with the death penalty for using Nu shu .</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37749\" id=\"question-wrapper-37749\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"096ba422-c254-4dfe-8782-10e5c9cf79f7\">customary way of learning Nu shu<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"c2d43e62-5e43-495a-a0d9-b5309c121858\">died out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37750\" id=\"question-wrapper-37750\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>There is a lot of money to be made out of public interest in Nu shu.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37751\" id=\"question-wrapper-37751\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Nu shu is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"60d8c17c-abb2-4566-b886-2b5d62643aa4\">now being openly taught<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f1a81a86-56d7-4111-9e76-535592cfb75b","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Birth","passagePhrase":"defied the patriarchal norms of the time that forbade them to read or write ... conceived of ... Nu shu"},{"uid":"87e742bc-7fb1-44b5-b83a-880f05d5cad4","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"development","passagePhrase":"building informal networks of 'sworn sisters ... using it artistically in ways that could be passed off as artwork ... grow and spread"},{"uid":"4dcc02d2-a582-44dd-8c7a-94b3389566fe","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"written","passagePhrase":"orthographical ... script ... characters"},{"uid":"464f7c4e-4152-4224-a52f-8e94864487c7","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Characteristics","passagePhrase":"thin, slanted ... slightly 'scratchy' appearance that bears more similarity to calligraphy ... completely phonetic"},{"uid":"dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"social role","passagePhrase":"a way to allow women to ... in confidence ... allowed women a forum for personal written communication in a society that was dominated by a male-orientated social culture ... provided"},{"uid":"4f8ad21b-0fcc-43b2-9904-241e59127054 9c3d750f-82c5-496d-8f53-3387c75dca59 dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22","qNum":"3 6 7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"communicate with one another ... send 'letters' to each other"},{"uid":"1efc8dfe-dc15-4d5a-9ac8-2135a5afdfbd 69daf254-7b84-4456-85e1-f8f918317af8","qNum":"6 7","questionPhrase":"a need for","passagePhrase":"a desire"},{"uid":"69257c46-1a60-486e-a6ac-5574ab15f4b0 a5beaa86-8c5a-4c82-84da-7dc2dc7f9653","qNum":"6 7","questionPhrase":"a way for uneducated women to read and write","passagePhrase":"women were rarely encouraged to become literate"},{"uid":"69257c46-1a60-486e-a6ac-5574ab15f4b0 a5beaa86-8c5a-4c82-84da-7dc2dc7f9653 dde528c7-ed1f-4872-9087-d05e52b47b22","qNum":"3 6 7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a practical and easy-to-learn alternative"},{"uid":"b625105b-e10c-42f7-a943-098e67d82f9b c0569887-3829-417b-ad5c-af8fcec4a813","qNum":"6 7","questionPhrase":"without men knowing","passagePhrase":"avoid making men suspicious"},{"uid":"2a247639-0a10-43f2-9b77-e5ab052de3cb","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"post-Revolution government","passagePhrase":"After the Chinese Revolution"},{"uid":"be985227-8507-4318-a2e7-0f330fd56740","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Decline","passagePhrase":"much of the need for a special form of women's communication was dampened ... Numerous letters, weavings, embroideries and other artifacts were destroyed ... women were forbidden to practise ... Nu shu ... customs"},{"uid":"c06b4420-5177-44e8-a926-5b9f8ab46f70","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"a tool for spies","passagePhrase":"a code used for espionage"},{"uid":"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"disuse","passagePhrase":"the ... were ... the language ... who has learnt ... Nu shu ... in this ... the last proficient user of the language, died"},{"uid":"096ba422-c254-4dfe-8782-10e5c9cf79f7 97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af","qNum":"4 11","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"generational chains of linguistic transmission ... being passed down through sworn sisters ... traditional manner"},{"uid":"97294a3d-6c0f-4148-9e07-c9c7ba2367af c2d43e62-5e43-495a-a0d9-b5309c121858","qNum":"4 11","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"broken up ... ceased ... no longer anyone alive"},{"uid":"7741316e-110c-4d05-a2f1-da733c4ad5a2","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"contemporary interest","passagePhrase":"recent years ... popular and scholarly interest in ... Nu shu ... has blossomed"},{"uid":"01e7375e-8ff1-483c-bd5c-e54a7ce90091","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Revival","passagePhrase":"Nu shu ... Museum that houses artifacts such as audio recordings, manuscripts and articles ... infrastructure at potential tourist sites ... the use of ... Nu shu ... is also a theme in Lisa See's historical novel"},{"uid":"01e7375e-8ff1-483c-bd5c-e54a7ce90091 60d8c17c-abb2-4566-b886-2b5d62643aa4","qNum":"5 13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"some schools in the area have begun instruction in the language"},{"uid":"4f8ad21b-0fcc-43b2-9904-241e59127054 9c3d750f-82c5-496d-8f53-3387c75dca59","qNum":"6 7","questionPhrase":"correspond","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"096ba422-c254-4dfe-8782-10e5c9cf79f7","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"customary way of learning Nu shu","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"c2d43e62-5e43-495a-a0d9-b5309c121858","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"died out","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"60d8c17c-abb2-4566-b886-2b5d62643aa4","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"now being openly taught","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_137":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Venus Flytraps</span></b></p><p><span>A. From <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"8554d870-090a-403b-aa99-58df2e177776\">indigenous myths<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to John Wyndham's </span><i><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"8554d870-090a-403b-aa99-58df2e177776\">Day of the Triffids<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></i><span> and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"8554d870-090a-403b-aa99-58df2e177776\">off-Broadway musical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </span><i><span>Little Shop of</span></i><i><span>Horrors</span></i><span> , the idea of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"2a532b35-d5c7-48f7-8c88-b0838832b5a7\">cerebral, carnivorous flora<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> has spooked audiences and readers for centuries. While shrubs and shoots have yet to uproot themselves or show any interest in human beings, however, for some of earth's smaller inhabitants—arachnids and insects—the risk of being trapped and ingested by a plant can be a threat to their daily existence. Easily the most famous of these predators is the Venus Flytrap, one of only two types of 'snap traps' in the world. Though rarely found growing wild, the Flytrap has captured popular imagination and can be purchased in florists and plant retailers around the world.</span></p><p><span>B. Part of the Venus Flytrap's mysterious aura begins with the title itself. While it is fairly clear that the second-half of the epithet has been given for its insect-trapping ability, the origin of 'Venus' is somewhat more ambiguous. According to the International Carnivorous Plant Society, the plant was first studied in the 17th and 18th Centuries, when puritanical mores ruled Western societies and obsession was rife with forbidden human impulses and urges. Women were often portrayed in these times as seductresses and temptresses, and botanists are believed to have seen <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9e7f63d9-444e-4a91-a236-44fd19bef240\">a parallel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7880ad2-0a7d-4957-927d-55c264a886f8\">the behaviour of the plant in luring and devouring insects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, and t<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7880ad2-0a7d-4957-927d-55c264a886f8\">he imagined behaviour of women in luring and 'trapping' witless men<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. The plant was thus named after the pagan goddess of love and money—Venus.</span></p><p><span>C. The Venus Flytrap is a small plant with six to seven leaves growing out of a bulb-like stem. At the end of each leaf is a trap, which is an opened pod with cilia around the edges like stiff eyelashes. The pod is lined with anthocynin pigments and sweet-smelling sap to attract flies and other insects. When they fly in, trigger hairs inside the pod sense the intruder's movement, and the pod snaps shut. The trigger mechanism is so sophisticated that the plant can differentiate between living creatures and non-edible debris by requiring two trigger hairs to be touched within twenty seconds of each other, or one hair to be touched in quick succession. The plant has no nervous system, and researchers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"414fa716-8873-420b-9e04-c96a148eaa5a\">can only hypothesize<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> as to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"4aa2566c-04a7-43eb-b07c-492ddeb5bf1e\">how the rapid shutting movement works<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"414fa716-8873-420b-9e04-c96a148eaa5a\">uncertainty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> adds to the Venus Flytrap's allure.</span></p><p><span>D. The pod shuts quickly, but does not seal entirely at first; scientists have found that this mechanism allows <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"18d2e364-d758-4dc2-8926-455532edca9c\">miniscule<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> insects to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"29e3b166-44fc-4738-a452-9c422d0db72d\">escape<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, as they will not be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"3323f76f-f537-4601-955f-b49a41c57711\">a source of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> useful nourishment for the plant. If the creature is large enough, however, the plant's flaps will eventually meet to form an airtight compress, and at this point the digestive process begins. A Venus Flytrap's digestive system is remarkably similar to how a human stomach works. For somewhere between five and twelve days the trap <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"07920987-e804-4809-9e79-5dea24b5a67b\">secretes acidic digestive juices that dissolve the soft tissue and cell membranes of the insect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. These juices also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"07920987-e804-4809-9e79-5dea24b5a67b\">kill any bacteria that have entered with the food, ensuring the plant maintains its hygiene<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> so that it does not begin to rot. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"07920987-e804-4809-9e79-5dea24b5a67b\">Enzymes in the acid help with the digestion of DNA, amino acids and cell molecules so that every fleshy part of the animal can be consumed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"87d98e66-0304-4ea1-b645-2684f1bb01a5\">Once the plant has reabsorbed the digestive fluid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>—this time with the added nourishment—the trap re-opens and the exoskeleton <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"cda9ebf6-e2cb-4f68-b8ea-b8d108aad6c5\">blows away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in the wind.</span></p><p><span>E. Although transplanted to other locations around the world, the Venus Flytrap is only found natively in an area around Wilmington, North Carolina in the United States. It thrives in bogs, marshes and wetlands and grows in wet sand and peaty soils. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"725f4e08-ed16-440a-955e-1bc82fa04bec\">Because<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> these environments are so <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"e3316da4-e3dd-440a-baa2-49fcdb41a1dd\">depleted in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> nitrogen, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"550e64fa-009b-4ff2-9b72-1f74b3df4779\">they asphyxiate other flora<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, but the Flytrap overcomes this nutritional poverty by sourcing protein from its insect prey. One of the plant's curious <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"6e9c8a23-e685-421e-8271-48c645e2dada\">features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"6d03010e-5de0-44c1-90d9-da25d6049946\">resilience to flame<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>—it is speculated that the Flytrap evolved this to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"6d03010e-5de0-44c1-90d9-da25d6049946\">endure through periodic blazes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> and to act as a means of survival that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5dfad8eb-b4a6-4a83-a695-4b51a3d7a810\">its competition lacks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>F. While the Venus Flytrap will not become extinct anytime soon (an estimated 3-6 million plants are presently in cultivation)—its natural existence is uncertain. In the last survey, only 35,800 Flytraps were found <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"1ff6be65-2c5e-40e9-af7a-8360e780feae\">remaining in the wild<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, and some prominent conservationists have suggested the plant be given the status of 'vulnerable'. Since this research is considerably <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"f4a2d7e1-4768-4498-9879-a2e20ba9d3f3\">dated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, having taken place <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"f4a2d7e1-4768-4498-9879-a2e20ba9d3f3\">in 1992<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"f4a2d7e1-4768-4498-9879-a2e20ba9d3f3\">the present number is considerably lower<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"6595adc7-38c6-4d33-85fa-14de38e4d362\">The </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 26\" data-uid=\"6595adc7-38c6-4d33-85fa-14de38e4d362 e3dc39b4-5f4c-44fd-a8ef-6b20a7c84a09\">draining and destruction of natural wetlands</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> where the Flytrap lives is considered to be the <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 26\" data-uid=\"3586236c-f884-4d6e-984c-81bbe01ebbd6 6595adc7-38c6-4d33-85fa-14de38e4d362\">biggest threat to its existence</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, as well as <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"6595adc7-38c6-4d33-85fa-14de38e4d362\">people </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 26\" data-uid=\"6595adc7-38c6-4d33-85fa-14de38e4d362 e3dc39b4-5f4c-44fd-a8ef-6b20a7c84a09\">removing the plants</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e3dc39b4-5f4c-44fd-a8ef-6b20a7c84a09\"> from their </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 26\" data-uid=\"5c9be2e9-278d-43d2-b4cf-e2a8fee2862a e3dc39b4-5f4c-44fd-a8ef-6b20a7c84a09\">natural habitat</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"6595adc7-38c6-4d33-85fa-14de38e4d362\">Punitive measures have been introduced to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4fd8f6a9-dcd7-467e-9ecc-a38b3b8f72ac\">prevent people from doing this<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Ironically, while cultural depictions of perennial killers may persist, the bigger threat is not what meat-eating plants might do to us, but what we may do to them.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A-F.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-19.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37752\" id=\"question-wrapper-37752\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>An overview of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"07920987-e804-4809-9e79-5dea24b5a67b\">how the Flytrap eats its prey<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37753\" id=\"question-wrapper-37753\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"9e7f63d9-444e-4a91-a236-44fd19bef240\">comparison<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a7880ad2-0a7d-4957-927d-55c264a886f8\">human and plant behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37754\" id=\"question-wrapper-37754\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"6595adc7-38c6-4d33-85fa-14de38e4d362\">measure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> designed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4fd8f6a9-dcd7-467e-9ecc-a38b3b8f72ac\">preserve Flytraps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"5c9be2e9-278d-43d2-b4cf-e2a8fee2862a\">native environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37755\" id=\"question-wrapper-37755\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>An example of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"8554d870-090a-403b-aa99-58df2e177776\">cultural and artistic portrayal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"2a532b35-d5c7-48f7-8c88-b0838832b5a7\">meat-eating plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37756\" id=\"question-wrapper-37756\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"6e9c8a23-e685-421e-8271-48c645e2dada\">characteristic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of the Venus Flytrap that is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"5dfad8eb-b4a6-4a83-a695-4b51a3d7a810\">exceptional in the botanical world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37757\" id=\"question-wrapper-37757\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"4aa2566c-04a7-43eb-b07c-492ddeb5bf1e\">an aspect of the Venus Flytrap’s biology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> that is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"414fa716-8873-420b-9e04-c96a148eaa5a\">not fully understood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the sentences below with words taken from Reading Passage 2.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Use </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 20-22.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37758\" id=\"question-wrapper-37758\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>If they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"18d2e364-d758-4dc2-8926-455532edca9c\">too small<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"3323f76f-f537-4601-955f-b49a41c57711\">provide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> (20)_____, the closing pod allows insects to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"29e3b166-44fc-4738-a452-9c422d0db72d\">get out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">USEFUL NOURISHMENT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37759\" id=\"question-wrapper-37759\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Only the (21)_____ is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"cda9ebf6-e2cb-4f68-b8ea-b8d108aad6c5\">left<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"87d98e66-0304-4ea1-b645-2684f1bb01a5\">after the Flytrap has finished digesting an insect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EXOSKELETON</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37760\" id=\"question-wrapper-37760\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"550e64fa-009b-4ff2-9b72-1f74b3df4779\">Many plants cannot survive in bogs and wetlands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"725f4e08-ed16-440a-955e-1bc82fa04bec\">owing to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"e3316da4-e3dd-440a-baa2-49fcdb41a1dd\">the lack of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> (22)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NITROGEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 23-26, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>TRUE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>FALSE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if there is no information on this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37761\" id=\"question-wrapper-37761\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Venus Flytrap can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"6d03010e-5de0-44c1-90d9-da25d6049946\">withstand some exposure to fire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37762\" id=\"question-wrapper-37762\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Many botanists would like the Venus Flytrap to be officially recognised as an endangered plant species.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37763\" id=\"question-wrapper-37763\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"f4a2d7e1-4768-4498-9879-a2e20ba9d3f3\">Only 35,800 Venus Flytraps now<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"1ff6be65-2c5e-40e9-af7a-8360e780feae\">survive in their natural habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37764\" id=\"question-wrapper-37764\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e3dc39b4-5f4c-44fd-a8ef-6b20a7c84a09\">Human interference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"3586236c-f884-4d6e-984c-81bbe01ebbd6\">major factor in the decline of wild Venus Flytraps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"8554d870-090a-403b-aa99-58df2e177776","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"cultural and artistic portrayal","passagePhrase":"indigenous myths ... Day of the Triffids ... off-Broadway musical"},{"uid":"2a532b35-d5c7-48f7-8c88-b0838832b5a7","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"meat-eating plants","passagePhrase":"cerebral, carnivorous flora"},{"uid":"9e7f63d9-444e-4a91-a236-44fd19bef240","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"comparison","passagePhrase":"a parallel"},{"uid":"a7880ad2-0a7d-4957-927d-55c264a886f8","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"human and plant behaviour","passagePhrase":"the behaviour of the plant in luring and devouring insects ... he imagined behaviour of women in luring and 'trapping' witless men"},{"uid":"414fa716-8873-420b-9e04-c96a148eaa5a","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"not fully understood","passagePhrase":"can only hypothesize ... uncertainty"},{"uid":"4aa2566c-04a7-43eb-b07c-492ddeb5bf1e","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"an aspect of the Venus Flytrap’s biology","passagePhrase":"how the rapid shutting movement works"},{"uid":"18d2e364-d758-4dc2-8926-455532edca9c","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"too small","passagePhrase":"miniscule"},{"uid":"29e3b166-44fc-4738-a452-9c422d0db72d","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"get out","passagePhrase":"escape"},{"uid":"3323f76f-f537-4601-955f-b49a41c57711","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"provide","passagePhrase":"a source of"},{"uid":"07920987-e804-4809-9e79-5dea24b5a67b","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"how the Flytrap eats its prey","passagePhrase":"secretes acidic digestive juices that dissolve the soft tissue and cell membranes of the insect ... kill any bacteria that have entered with the food, ensuring the plant maintains its hygiene ... Enzymes in the acid help with the digestion of DNA, amino acids and cell molecules so that every fleshy part of the animal can be consumed"},{"uid":"87d98e66-0304-4ea1-b645-2684f1bb01a5","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"after the Flytrap has finished digesting an insect","passagePhrase":"Once the plant has reabsorbed the digestive fluid"},{"uid":"cda9ebf6-e2cb-4f68-b8ea-b8d108aad6c5","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"left","passagePhrase":"blows away"},{"uid":"725f4e08-ed16-440a-955e-1bc82fa04bec","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"owing to","passagePhrase":"Because"},{"uid":"e3316da4-e3dd-440a-baa2-49fcdb41a1dd","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"the lack of","passagePhrase":"depleted in"},{"uid":"550e64fa-009b-4ff2-9b72-1f74b3df4779","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Many plants cannot survive in bogs and wetlands","passagePhrase":"they asphyxiate other flora"},{"uid":"6e9c8a23-e685-421e-8271-48c645e2dada","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"characteristic","passagePhrase":"features"},{"uid":"6d03010e-5de0-44c1-90d9-da25d6049946","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"withstand some exposure to fire","passagePhrase":"resilience to flame ... endure through periodic blazes"},{"uid":"5dfad8eb-b4a6-4a83-a695-4b51a3d7a810","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"exceptional in the botanical world","passagePhrase":"its competition lacks"},{"uid":"1ff6be65-2c5e-40e9-af7a-8360e780feae","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"survive in their natural habitats","passagePhrase":"remaining in the wild"},{"uid":"6595adc7-38c6-4d33-85fa-14de38e4d362","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"measure","passagePhrase":"The ... people ... Punitive measures have been introduced to"},{"uid":"6595adc7-38c6-4d33-85fa-14de38e4d362 e3dc39b4-5f4c-44fd-a8ef-6b20a7c84a09","qNum":"16 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"draining and destruction of natural wetlands ... removing the plants"},{"uid":"3586236c-f884-4d6e-984c-81bbe01ebbd6 6595adc7-38c6-4d33-85fa-14de38e4d362","qNum":"16 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"biggest threat to its existence"},{"uid":"e3dc39b4-5f4c-44fd-a8ef-6b20a7c84a09","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Human interference","passagePhrase":"from their"},{"uid":"5c9be2e9-278d-43d2-b4cf-e2a8fee2862a e3dc39b4-5f4c-44fd-a8ef-6b20a7c84a09","qNum":"16 26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"natural habitat"},{"uid":"4fd8f6a9-dcd7-467e-9ecc-a38b3b8f72ac","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"preserve Flytraps","passagePhrase":"prevent people from doing this"},{"uid":"5c9be2e9-278d-43d2-b4cf-e2a8fee2862a","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"native environment","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"3586236c-f884-4d6e-984c-81bbe01ebbd6","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"major factor in the decline of wild Venus Flytraps","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_138":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Development</span></b></p><p><span>Shortly after World War Ⅱ, 'development' as we now understand it was set in motion. Western governments and donors poured money into new agencies that set about trying to stimulate the economies of underdeveloped countries. Because of this emphasis, it is now widely regarded as the Growth Model. Although we might expect poverty reduction to be the central objective, planners at this stage <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"95aea9a0-2504-45fa-ae78-6da82a7c710a\">were primarily concerned with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> industrial development. It was hoped that the benefits of this would trickle down to poor people through raising incomes and providing employment opportunities, thereby indirectly lifting them above the ascribed poverty threshold of a dollar a day. The weaknesses of these assumptions were revealed, however, when poverty rates and economic growth were found to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a27d90f9-023e-4a29-87c1-cdce5fb30204\">rise simultaneously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in many countries.</span></p><p><span>During the 1970s, a new trend took over—trickle-up development. Instead of focusing on macro-economic policy and large-scale industrial projects, planners shifted attention to the core living requirements of individuals and communities. This became known as the Basic Needs Approach to development. It was hoped that through the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"618081d4-0bc7-465e-8d46-eb0db02d501c\">provision of services<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"00636595-2f67-42a8-adc1-4c76a03fe58b\">community sanitation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> and literacy p<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"5f59a004-2615-488d-8fb7-5a7eb8d05969\">rogrammes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, poverty could be eliminated from below. Economic growth was desirable but superfluous—Basic Needs redefined poverty from involving a lack of money to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"696c9a2f-cd4c-4466-bcc4-8fa7b74ccf86\">lacking the capability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"ae3aeb5f-5c36-4153-8d05-69633972bb53\">to attain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> full human potential. The trouble with Basic Needs programmes, however, was their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"21f3b50d-9845-4391-b7f6-0cec0207438e\">expensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, resource-intensive nature that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3770c4db-3d8f-42f1-9610-fbb9052ef74d\">entailed continuous management and funding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Since the 1980s, development planners have moved towards the Sustainable Livelihoods Approach, which emphasises good livelihoods (materially and socially) that, most importantly, are independent and sustainable. 'Sustainable' in this sense means that people are able to recover from the shocks and stresses of daily life, absolving agencies of the need to persistently monitor their lives. This approach emphasises a view of poverty that comes not from the rich but from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"649c3492-1204-48b3-8d44-1898ad8fd577\">the impoverished<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> themselves, who are considered to be most suitably positioned to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"71cbb731-325f-425c-b170-f67df4267f7d\">determine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the poverty indicators that contribute to the multiple facets of their own deprivation. Although the Sustainable Livelihoods Approach has been criticised for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"bc6a8821-818a-4e92-b4d2-24c7c2b8c9c5\">lacking an environmental platform strong enough to respond to climate change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, and for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"b462db5f-0553-491b-bb72-d2183bf13dfd\">disassociating aspects of power and societal status<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> from being a contestable part of development, it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"83bd043a-4e59-49c9-ad34-2023273c14c8\">currently the preferred model for development projects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Though there is some linearity to the trajectory of development practice, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"bb6935c0-84ae-4f63-8e55-a6b3f4b5d92b\">paradigms shifting in and out of fashion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"c86cf6a9-c07a-436a-8b06-e1623a1b616f\">vigorous scholarly debate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"045719a7-bd7b-4122-a7ab-79a3d24d4cfe\">persists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> around all approaches. The Growth Model, for example, is still defended by many theorists, particularly economists. Those who believe in the Growth Model insist that nothing trumps economic development as a tool for poverty alleviation for the developing countries (although there is often less enthusiasm for its applicability to the post-industrial West). Many countries that have focused explicitly on growth have managed to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"7b0e353f-d7aa-4651-bff7-ab50ffbc6908\">make considerable inroads into reducing poverty, even in the absence of a development programme<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>; Japan and Germany followed this route after World War Ⅱ, as has China from the 1970s. On the other hand, some countries with massive inflows of funding for aid-based 'development projects'—particularly those in sub-Saharan Africa—have struggled to progress with meeting poverty reduction targets.</span></p><p><span>There is a good reason to be sceptical about the Growth Model, however, as is evidenced by the numerous societies that have partly imploded as a consequence of prioritising economic growth above the work of human development. The experiences of many eastern European countries with health and employment crises in the early 1990s are particularly traumatic examples of this. The Growth Model also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ae23041f-40f1-4daf-851d-e4c12b6b63bd\">suffers from an undemocratic, and 'technocratic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>', if not autocratic, method—underdeveloped countries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ae23041f-40f1-4daf-851d-e4c12b6b63bd\">frequently make policy decisions based on consultation with Western economists and institutions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> on how to generate growth. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ae23041f-40f1-4daf-851d-e4c12b6b63bd\">dissolves the autonomy of communities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> to make their own decisions about what matters to them, and what kind of society they would like to build. The move to the Sustainable Livelihood Approach is a positive move in this regard, because by operating on a principle that decisions should be made by those who are affected by them, it introduces a role for localised decision-making.</span></p><p><span>It will be difficult, if not impossible, for any country in the near future to ignore economic growth as a development indicator while continuing to meet development targets. It is important, however, that we move away from seeing this type of growth as the prime objective for development. Development is ultimately about people, and human development must be placed at the forefront; <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"2b9e05b8-b55b-4d9b-9111-c17fc6826a60 c52764c9-ddaa-4171-afb8-1286186a8741\">economic growth is simply one tool out of many that can help us along the way</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. We also need to recognise that foreign advisers, whatever qualifications and knowledge they may possess, can sometimes be a hindrance; local autonomy must be respected for real development to occur. The Growth Model may have failed, but this does not render economic growth irrelevant. The Sustainable Livelihood Approach offers helpful and realistic alternatives. But <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"3a66d95a-0bae-4218-8391-c7c2b21afb65 976ab508-6d9a-466e-ae76-b3d8a186b463\">it is folly to commit ourselves to a strictly-defined, systematic programme</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>—<span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"3a66d95a-0bae-4218-8391-c7c2b21afb65 976ab508-6d9a-466e-ae76-b3d8a186b463\">less constrictive mindsets will help us break the development fashion cycle</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the table below.</span></i><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"20\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Growth Model</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"22\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Basic Needs Approach</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"21\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>SLA</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"20\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(27)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"95aea9a0-2504-45fa-ae78-6da82a7c710a\">was the main goal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p></td><td colspan=\"22\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Typified by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"618081d4-0bc7-465e-8d46-eb0db02d501c\">small-scale aid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"00636595-2f67-42a8-adc1-4c76a03fe58b\">health<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> and (29)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"5f59a004-2615-488d-8fb7-5a7eb8d05969\">projects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p></td><td colspan=\"21\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Tries to encourage ways of living that are more self-sufficient</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"20\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Poverty described as living on less than a dollar a day</span></p></td><td colspan=\"22\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Poverty seen as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"696c9a2f-cd4c-4466-bcc4-8fa7b74ccf86\">an inability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"ae3aeb5f-5c36-4153-8d05-69633972bb53\">to reach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> (30)_____</span></p></td><td colspan=\"21\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"649c3492-1204-48b3-8d44-1898ad8fd577\">Poor people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"71cbb731-325f-425c-b170-f67df4267f7d\">identify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> their own (32)_____</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"20\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>It was discovered that poverty could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"a27d90f9-023e-4a29-87c1-cdce5fb30204\">increase in step with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> (28)_____</span></p></td><td colspan=\"22\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Projects <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"21f3b50d-9845-4391-b7f6-0cec0207438e\">costly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> and (31)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"3770c4db-3d8f-42f1-9610-fbb9052ef74d\">requiring ongoing involvement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p></td><td colspan=\"21\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"bc6a8821-818a-4e92-b4d2-24c7c2b8c9c5\">The problem of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> (33)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"bc6a8821-818a-4e92-b4d2-24c7c2b8c9c5\">not adequately addressed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>; &amp; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"b462db5f-0553-491b-bb72-d2183bf13dfd\">ignores issues of social dominance and authority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37765\" id=\"question-wrapper-37765\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INDUSTRIAL DEVELOPMENT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37766\" id=\"question-wrapper-37766\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ECONOMIC GROWTH</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37767\" id=\"question-wrapper-37767\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LITERACY</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37768\" id=\"question-wrapper-37768\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HUMAN POTENTIAL</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37769\" id=\"question-wrapper-37769\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RESOURCE-INTENSIVE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37777\" id=\"question-wrapper-37777\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POVERTY INDICATORS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37778\" id=\"question-wrapper-37778\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CLIMATE CHANGE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 34-38 on your answer sheet, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>YES</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NO</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37770\" id=\"question-wrapper-37770\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"83bd043a-4e59-49c9-ad34-2023273c14c8\">most favoured method of development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> is the Sustainable Livelihoods Approach.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37771\" id=\"question-wrapper-37771\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>While <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"bb6935c0-84ae-4f63-8e55-a6b3f4b5d92b\">institutions often follow development trends<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"c86cf6a9-c07a-436a-8b06-e1623a1b616f\">academic disputes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"045719a7-bd7b-4122-a7ab-79a3d24d4cfe\">more timeless<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37772\" id=\"question-wrapper-37772\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Growth Model is more popular with Third World scholars than Western scholars.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37773\" id=\"question-wrapper-37773\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"7b0e353f-d7aa-4651-bff7-ab50ffbc6908\">not possible to reduce poverty without an explicit development policy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37774\" id=\"question-wrapper-37774\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The Growth Model <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"ae23041f-40f1-4daf-851d-e4c12b6b63bd\">takes some authority away from local forms of organisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>TWO</span></b></i><i><span> letters A-E.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 39-40.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>TWO</span></b><span> of the following statements form part of the author's conclusion?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Economic growth is the primary development goal, but there are other factors to consider.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"3a66d95a-0bae-4218-8391-c7c2b21afb65 976ab508-6d9a-466e-ae76-b3d8a186b463\">It is preferable not to think about development in rigid, structured terms</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Development projects are likely to fail in the absence of highly-educated experts.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. The Sustainable Livelihoods Approach is more effective than the Growth Model.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39 40\" data-uid=\"2b9e05b8-b55b-4d9b-9111-c17fc6826a60 c52764c9-ddaa-4171-afb8-1286186a8741\">Economic growth should only be considered as a means for development, not an endpoint</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37775\" id=\"question-wrapper-37775\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37776\" id=\"question-wrapper-37776\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"95aea9a0-2504-45fa-ae78-6da82a7c710a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"was the main goal","passagePhrase":"were primarily concerned with"},{"uid":"a27d90f9-023e-4a29-87c1-cdce5fb30204","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"increase in step with","passagePhrase":"rise simultaneously"},{"uid":"618081d4-0bc7-465e-8d46-eb0db02d501c","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"small-scale aid","passagePhrase":"provision of services"},{"uid":"00636595-2f67-42a8-adc1-4c76a03fe58b","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"health","passagePhrase":"community sanitation"},{"uid":"5f59a004-2615-488d-8fb7-5a7eb8d05969","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"projects","passagePhrase":"rogrammes"},{"uid":"696c9a2f-cd4c-4466-bcc4-8fa7b74ccf86","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"an inability","passagePhrase":"lacking the capability"},{"uid":"ae3aeb5f-5c36-4153-8d05-69633972bb53","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"to reach","passagePhrase":"to attain"},{"uid":"21f3b50d-9845-4391-b7f6-0cec0207438e","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"costly","passagePhrase":"expensive"},{"uid":"3770c4db-3d8f-42f1-9610-fbb9052ef74d","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"requiring ongoing involvement","passagePhrase":"entailed continuous management and funding"},{"uid":"649c3492-1204-48b3-8d44-1898ad8fd577","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Poor people","passagePhrase":"the impoverished"},{"uid":"71cbb731-325f-425c-b170-f67df4267f7d","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"identify","passagePhrase":"determine"},{"uid":"bc6a8821-818a-4e92-b4d2-24c7c2b8c9c5","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"The problem of ... not adequately addressed","passagePhrase":"lacking an environmental platform strong enough to respond to climate change"},{"uid":"b462db5f-0553-491b-bb72-d2183bf13dfd","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"ignores issues of social dominance and authority","passagePhrase":"disassociating aspects of power and societal status"},{"uid":"83bd043a-4e59-49c9-ad34-2023273c14c8","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"most favoured method of development","passagePhrase":"currently the preferred model for development projects"},{"uid":"bb6935c0-84ae-4f63-8e55-a6b3f4b5d92b","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"institutions often follow development trends","passagePhrase":"paradigms shifting in and out of fashion"},{"uid":"c86cf6a9-c07a-436a-8b06-e1623a1b616f","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"academic disputes","passagePhrase":"vigorous scholarly debate"},{"uid":"045719a7-bd7b-4122-a7ab-79a3d24d4cfe","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"more timeless","passagePhrase":"persists"},{"uid":"ae23041f-40f1-4daf-851d-e4c12b6b63bd","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"takes some authority away from local forms of organisation","passagePhrase":"suffers from an undemocratic, and 'technocratic ... frequently make policy decisions based on consultation with Western economists and institutions ... dissolves the autonomy of communities"},{"uid":"2b9e05b8-b55b-4d9b-9111-c17fc6826a60 c52764c9-ddaa-4171-afb8-1286186a8741","qNum":"39 40","questionPhrase":"Economic growth should only be considered as a means for development, not an endpoint","passagePhrase":"economic growth is simply one tool out of many that can help us along the way"},{"uid":"3a66d95a-0bae-4218-8391-c7c2b21afb65 976ab508-6d9a-466e-ae76-b3d8a186b463","qNum":"39 40","questionPhrase":"It is preferable not to think about development in rigid, structured terms","passagePhrase":"it is folly to commit ourselves to a strictly-defined, systematic programme ... less constrictive mindsets will help us break the development fashion cycle"}]},"reading_u2_139":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>The Development of the Modern Hot Air Balloon</span></b></p><p><span>The modern hot air balloon is constructed by <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"c2c706f3-12fd-4b12-a111-11ddea3b5040\">suspending a wicker basket underneath </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2 3\" data-uid=\"64d94795-3059-4963-b1f6-2d42990337b7 c2c706f3-12fd-4b12-a111-11ddea3b5040\">a large bag of nylon fabric</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"64d94795-3059-4963-b1f6-2d42990337b7\">, known as an envelope</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"c2c706f3-12fd-4b12-a111-11ddea3b5040\">The wicker basket carries the balloon's pilot, any other passengers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, and the propane tanks that provide the balloon with a source of fuel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"f7fc525f-46cb-4111-a4ee-bc1122e917cf\">The propane tanks are connected by hose to a pair of burners, which are located between the basket and the envelope<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. When the burners ignite, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"05c90f3a-e384-4b9d-a67a-9961bd3837e9\">their heat passes through the balloon's skirt—a circular sheath of fire-resistant material at the mouth of the envelope<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>—and finally into the envelope itself. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"6bfc8485-ef82-464c-9434-293551318da8\">Located at the top of the envelope is a parachute vent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, a mechanism that allows the pilot to release hot air and increase the balloon's rate of descent when required. This is controlled by a parachute valve cord that extends through the balloon, and into the basket.</span></p><p><span>The use of hot air balloons can be traced back to the Three Kingdoms era of Chinese history (220-280 AD). Zhuge Liang used these early incarnations, known as Kongming lanterns, as military signals. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"8ae686e1-9cbe-413d-bb15-2e8276bde5e6\">first manned flight on record<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> took place in France on October 15th, 1783. In a balloon constructed by Jacques-Etienne Montgolfier, a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"8ae686e1-9cbe-413d-bb15-2e8276bde5e6\">Frenchman<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> named Pilatre de Rozier was elevated eighty feet off the ground. Modern hot air balloons, with their capacity to ascend or descend and occasionally 'steer' at the pilot's will, were first developed by Ed Yost in the 1950s. The Bristol Belle is generally regarded as the first modern hot air balloon, and had its inaugural flight in 1967. Since then, balloon technology has become extremely sophisticated. Some hot air balloons have reached altitudes of 21,000 metres, travelled over 7,500 kilometres, and reached speeds of up to 400 kilometres per hour.</span></p><p><span>Hot-air ballooning is generally a safe activity, and serious accidents are rare. In the event that something does go wrong, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8 9\" data-uid=\"6b1c5acf-8f29-44b4-bd7c-c870ae7064c9 c807091a-2e00-4064-b661-8de712fe9e65 dbec154d-99f4-46d5-8156-ae23e0a8afc0\">several items of safety gear</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8 9\" data-uid=\"55bfda83-394a-40d1-93e8-85ab2fb08a9d 6f5b5bab-3df2-4589-9a64-b5e2f2dc3628 894b7cee-25a3-436f-a088-f86aad061b94\">useful</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to have on board. In case the pilot light and the auxiliary piezo ignition fail, it is a good idea to have a <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8 9\" data-uid=\"42535f04-85c0-4734-a6f9-05f4c8196ff9 5273acb3-f18e-415f-8df2-912042d7bd91 b9008bd0-974b-4509-b81a-7aa5e4657bed\">welding torch flint sparker</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> available for the pilot's use. Given the propane combustion used to propel the hot air balloon, a fire extinguisher is an absolute necessity. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8 9\" data-uid=\"57d5c7fc-d69c-42d5-8415-c29ff0aaaf89 71b8a740-36cb-4990-bb13-4eaf7467b8cb 9978b0a2-d955-472f-8799-ac9d0b99f9c3\">Flame-resistant gauntlets</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> made out of either leather or nomex are required for the pilot so that a gas valve can be disabled even if an open flame is present. While nomex is a specially-manufactured synthetic form of fire-retardant material, synthetic clothing is generally a hindrance to fire safety, and clothing made of natural fibre is a superior option for pilots. Finally, a <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8 9\" data-uid=\"50b52118-efc1-467b-b60f-189ba3ed55f5 dbb57c25-8d89-46b2-81db-5e3b9c535d56 e49a49d1-8010-46bb-a8ad-63cb8bf5f3b4\">handling line</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>—a long rope that can be thrown overboard—is a vital precautionary measure that allows people on the ground to steer the balloon away from trouble.</span></p><p><span>To ensure balloon longevity and safety in operation, it is vital that hot air balloons be maintained and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"696e33bd-c3eb-472c-8a8f-26f0708448d7\">repair<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>ed while not in use. Keeping the envelope clean and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"45de9d9a-c779-498f-8cfb-7278a118e11f\">dehumidified<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> is an important step that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f98a2dc1-7f64-4dc3-8442-a6d3deffd910\">prevent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>s mould from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"5ab22a0c-3129-42d0-a916-669a0c246a22\">forming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> on the fabric. This is especially important if the balloon has landed in a wet or muddy environment. The burner and fuel system also requires <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"d6b46b74-a05a-4ec6-9b02-9f5262cdf39c\">regular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> maintenance. This can involve the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"621268f2-b6e3-4815-b559-35ceb893d810\">replacement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> or repair of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"0fff945d-a469-42bd-8164-698ffacdaf5b\">damaged hoses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> and any sticking or leaky valves. The wicker basket has skids on its bottom to help it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"bd18e825-e030-4f32-8512-fb20d670a3c7\">gain traction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d7d52159-8451-44e7-81ba-84149b89f96f\">upon landing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>; over time these are worn down, and will need to be replaced. International regulations stipulate that balloons must be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a7ff5315-a35d-4d88-ab26-a118daa6f4cb\">given a full inspection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> every one hundred flight hours, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a7ff5315-a35d-4d88-ab26-a118daa6f4cb\">twelve months<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. This ensures that any problems can be rectified before they become hazardous.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the diagram below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from Reading Passage 1 for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 1-5.</span></i></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Simulation/reading/images/c74592154d855c18f325a2e8524d6e0badc9d8754ca0c0f300646f4684bc10cf.jpg\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37819\" id=\"question-wrapper-37819\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PARACHUTE VENT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37820\" id=\"question-wrapper-37820\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ENVELOPE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37821\" id=\"question-wrapper-37821\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(WICKER) BASKET</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37822\" id=\"question-wrapper-37822\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BURNERS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37823\" id=\"question-wrapper-37823\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SKIRT</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answer in box 6.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37824\" id=\"question-wrapper-37824\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Who was the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"8ae686e1-9cbe-413d-bb15-2e8276bde5e6\">first person to ascend in a hot air balloon<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Zhuge Liang</li> <li>B. Jacques-Etienne Montgolfier</li> <li>C. Pilatre de Rozier</li> <li>D. Ed Yost</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>THREE</span></b></i><i><span> letters, A-G.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 7-9.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>THREE</span></b><span> of the following seven pieces of <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8 9\" data-uid=\"6b1c5acf-8f29-44b4-bd7c-c870ae7064c9 c807091a-2e00-4064-b661-8de712fe9e65 dbec154d-99f4-46d5-8156-ae23e0a8afc0\">safety equipment</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8 9\" data-uid=\"55bfda83-394a-40d1-93e8-85ab2fb08a9d 6f5b5bab-3df2-4589-9a64-b5e2f2dc3628 894b7cee-25a3-436f-a088-f86aad061b94\">suggested for use</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> with a hot air balloon?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8 9\" data-uid=\"50b52118-efc1-467b-b60f-189ba3ed55f5 dbb57c25-8d89-46b2-81db-5e3b9c535d56 e49a49d1-8010-46bb-a8ad-63cb8bf5f3b4\">Drop line</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Gas valve</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Piezo ignition</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Synthetic clothing</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8 9\" data-uid=\"57d5c7fc-d69c-42d5-8415-c29ff0aaaf89 71b8a740-36cb-4990-bb13-4eaf7467b8cb 9978b0a2-d955-472f-8799-ac9d0b99f9c3\">Fire-proof gloves</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7 8 9\" data-uid=\"42535f04-85c0-4734-a6f9-05f4c8196ff9 5273acb3-f18e-415f-8df2-912042d7bd91 b9008bd0-974b-4509-b81a-7aa5e4657bed\">Flint spark lighter</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. Propane combustion</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37825\" id=\"question-wrapper-37825\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37826\" id=\"question-wrapper-37826\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37827\" id=\"question-wrapper-37827\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E/F</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the sentences below with words taken from Reading Passage 1.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Use </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 10-13.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37828\" id=\"question-wrapper-37828\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"45de9d9a-c779-498f-8cfb-7278a118e11f\">dry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> envelope helps to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"f98a2dc1-7f64-4dc3-8442-a6d3deffd910\">stop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"5ab22a0c-3129-42d0-a916-669a0c246a22\">the growth of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10)_____ on the material.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MOULD</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37829\" id=\"question-wrapper-37829\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"d6b46b74-a05a-4ec6-9b02-9f5262cdf39c\">Frequent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)_____ is important: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"696e33bd-c3eb-472c-8a8f-26f0708448d7\">fixing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"621268f2-b6e3-4815-b559-35ceb893d810\">changing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"0fff945d-a469-42bd-8164-698ffacdaf5b\">faulty parts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of the propulsion system when necessary.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MAINTENANCE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37830\" id=\"question-wrapper-37830\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>(12)_____ help the basket <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"bd18e825-e030-4f32-8512-fb20d670a3c7\">grip the ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d7d52159-8451-44e7-81ba-84149b89f96f\">when it sets down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SKIDS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37831\" id=\"question-wrapper-37831\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Balloons must be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"a7ff5315-a35d-4d88-ab26-a118daa6f4cb\">checked annually<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> according to (13)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INTERNATIONAL REGULATIONS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c2c706f3-12fd-4b12-a111-11ddea3b5040","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"suspending a wicker basket underneath ... The wicker basket carries the balloon's pilot, any other passengers"},{"uid":"64d94795-3059-4963-b1f6-2d42990337b7 c2c706f3-12fd-4b12-a111-11ddea3b5040","qNum":"2 3","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a large bag of nylon fabric"},{"uid":"64d94795-3059-4963-b1f6-2d42990337b7","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":", known as an envelope"},{"uid":"f7fc525f-46cb-4111-a4ee-bc1122e917cf","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The propane tanks are connected by hose to a pair of burners, which are located between the basket and the envelope"},{"uid":"05c90f3a-e384-4b9d-a67a-9961bd3837e9","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"their heat passes through the balloon's skirt—a circular sheath of fire-resistant material at the mouth of the envelope"},{"uid":"6bfc8485-ef82-464c-9434-293551318da8","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Located at the top of the envelope is a parachute vent"},{"uid":"8ae686e1-9cbe-413d-bb15-2e8276bde5e6","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"first person to ascend in a hot air balloon","passagePhrase":"first manned flight on record ... Frenchman"},{"uid":"6b1c5acf-8f29-44b4-bd7c-c870ae7064c9 c807091a-2e00-4064-b661-8de712fe9e65 dbec154d-99f4-46d5-8156-ae23e0a8afc0","qNum":"7 8 9","questionPhrase":"safety equipment","passagePhrase":"several items of safety gear"},{"uid":"55bfda83-394a-40d1-93e8-85ab2fb08a9d 6f5b5bab-3df2-4589-9a64-b5e2f2dc3628 894b7cee-25a3-436f-a088-f86aad061b94","qNum":"7 8 9","questionPhrase":"suggested for use","passagePhrase":"useful"},{"uid":"42535f04-85c0-4734-a6f9-05f4c8196ff9 5273acb3-f18e-415f-8df2-912042d7bd91 b9008bd0-974b-4509-b81a-7aa5e4657bed","qNum":"7 8 9","questionPhrase":"Flint spark lighter","passagePhrase":"welding torch flint sparker"},{"uid":"57d5c7fc-d69c-42d5-8415-c29ff0aaaf89 71b8a740-36cb-4990-bb13-4eaf7467b8cb 9978b0a2-d955-472f-8799-ac9d0b99f9c3","qNum":"7 8 9","questionPhrase":"Fire-proof gloves","passagePhrase":"Flame-resistant gauntlets"},{"uid":"50b52118-efc1-467b-b60f-189ba3ed55f5 dbb57c25-8d89-46b2-81db-5e3b9c535d56 e49a49d1-8010-46bb-a8ad-63cb8bf5f3b4","qNum":"7 8 9","questionPhrase":"Drop line","passagePhrase":"handling line"},{"uid":"696e33bd-c3eb-472c-8a8f-26f0708448d7","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"fixing","passagePhrase":"repair"},{"uid":"45de9d9a-c779-498f-8cfb-7278a118e11f","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"dry","passagePhrase":"dehumidified"},{"uid":"f98a2dc1-7f64-4dc3-8442-a6d3deffd910","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"stop","passagePhrase":"prevent"},{"uid":"5ab22a0c-3129-42d0-a916-669a0c246a22","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the growth of","passagePhrase":"forming"},{"uid":"d6b46b74-a05a-4ec6-9b02-9f5262cdf39c","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Frequent","passagePhrase":"regular"},{"uid":"621268f2-b6e3-4815-b559-35ceb893d810","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"changing","passagePhrase":"replacement"},{"uid":"0fff945d-a469-42bd-8164-698ffacdaf5b","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"faulty parts","passagePhrase":"damaged hoses"},{"uid":"bd18e825-e030-4f32-8512-fb20d670a3c7","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"grip the ground","passagePhrase":"gain traction"},{"uid":"d7d52159-8451-44e7-81ba-84149b89f96f","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"when it sets down","passagePhrase":"upon landing"},{"uid":"a7ff5315-a35d-4d88-ab26-a118daa6f4cb","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"checked annually","passagePhrase":"given a full inspection ... twelve months"}]},"reading_u2_140":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Which Voting System is Better?</span></b></p><p><span>Voting is often portrayed as a very simple activity—all that is required being a list of names, boxes and a pen with which to tick the preferred option—but it is actually an intricate process that can take many different forms on which everyone from mathematicians to political scholars, interest groups, politicians and voters often have divergent opinions. Two of the most popular of these voting systems are known as First-Past-the-Post (FPP) and Mixed-Member Proportional (MMP), and they have quite different features.</span></p><p><span>FPP is one of the simplest voting systems. Voters <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"6fc54b37-46e4-4e5c-b209-4d957a9b7e52\">select one person from a list of candidates in their electorate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, and the candidate with the highest number of votes is elected to represent them. While this might sound simple and fair, it can have several undesirable effects. Firstly, because of the 'all or nothing' result, FPP produces <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"6be46ed8-aae4-47f2-be79-0f7865b2f9e3\">a large number of wasted votes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>—votes which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"4860260f-20a6-4b04-a45b-55390090bafa\">do not affect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"7d628c0f-f525-4fbf-bed2-4357a77c8cc0\">the outcome of the election<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. This is the case in the majority of electorates, which are safe or relatively safe. Consequently, the party that gains the highest number of seats in Parliament may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bbc48adc-75c1-47ad-84c8-94ffedf24e54\">not actually gain the most votes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>—in the 2005 UK elections, for example, the Labour party <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bbc48adc-75c1-47ad-84c8-94ffedf24e54\">governed alone with only 35 percent of the vote<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Because of the pressure on voters not to 'waste' their vote, FPP tends to foster tactical voting for a rival but less popular candidate, thus sidelining minority voices and third party candidacies in favour of a race between two, often similar, contestants.</span></p><p><span>MMP attempts to create a parliament that represents a national consensus, rather than combining the results from dozens of local 'mini-elections'. Voters select their electorate candidate, as in FPP, but they also select a party, which will gain seats in Parliament proportionate to the party vote. This opens the door for representation amongst parties that may have broad support nationally, but not enough support in any single geographical area to win an electorate seat. While Parliament as a whole may be more representative, however, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9780b536-06fc-445b-9617-f771e8df723e\">ability to affect change within parliament<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> can often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"b460ff03-e514-4937-8e2b-618a4ccf9922\">accrue to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3f90fb22-1fd6-4548-9c8f-45dcfd4ddeed\">centrist, smaller party<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that has the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9780b536-06fc-445b-9617-f771e8df723e\">ability to essentially choose the government<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, by selecting between the major parties as coalition partners. This phenomenon is known as the 'tail wagging the dog'. Finally, the party vote tends to bring in Members of Parliament (MPs) in an order that is chosen, not by the electorate, but by the party itself. This is one of MMP's undemocratic moves that favours party establishment and hierarchy over the will of the public.</span></p><p><span>New Zealand's transition from FPP to MMP demonstrates the benefits and drawbacks of each system. In the 1970s, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"4f058b6d-58ce-4c34-9596-014a42acfaa0\">many New Zealanders grew disillusioned with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> the two-party system. FPP did not provide voters with another viable option; however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"e77bcaaa-53ab-43af-976c-25cce10c29fd\">the leading third party received a considerable 16 percent of the vote<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in 1978 but gained only one of the 92 seats in parliament—three years later their vote share was up to 21 percent, but they gained only two seats. A Royal Commission subsequently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"8c95ad3b-4e91-44e9-ac58-d1d308a5a409\">recommended a shift to MMP<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, and in 1993 a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"e151d2b5-3d21-48e3-b533-e8cc4859f012\">state-wide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> referendum was held that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"18 22\" data-uid=\"ac637d49-5c54-4da7-9060-27d6fac2720c f790179a-e258-4b68-bfa0-736adeaff22f\">passed</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"ac637d49-5c54-4da7-9060-27d6fac2720c\"> in favour of the reform</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The 1996 elections wore away much public enthusiasm for MMP, however. The result was indecisive, and with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bbc48adc-75c1-47ad-84c8-94ffedf24e54\">neither major party able to govern alone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, the power to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bbc48adc-75c1-47ad-84c8-94ffedf24e54\">form a coalition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> rested upon a third party, New Zealand First. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5bbc70e2-5667-4ecc-8438-4238885156f4\">Instead of forming a coalition with Labour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>—a party that many voters considered to be its natural ally—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"383286bd-d24b-4cb0-8c68-b1db4966453e\">the New Zealand First party sided with the National party<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. This was followed by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"88242ef2-6b89-477f-a539-b535caf3a8de\">a subsequent rise in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> party-hopping—Members of Parliament (MPs) leaving the parties from which they were elected. Eventually, the coalition disbanded with Prime Minister Jenny Shipley sacking New Zealand First leader, Winston Peters, from Cabinet.</span></p><p><span>Nevertheless, after these initial teething problems, New Zealand voters and politicians have grown accustomed to MMP and learnt to focus on its possibilities rather than its hindrances. One of the most notable benefits is that Parliament has become far more representative of the diversity in modern New Zealand society. MMP <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"f9e38045-a569-4b74-8711-98c8273675df\">introduced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"c178766f-c91a-46c1-ab8e-411211ff4c89\">a number of MPs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> who had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"4ab527bf-565e-4a76-9d3f-3b8ed418241f\">previously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> been marginalised from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"c8b56360-9031-41b7-bd2c-046d563bbe1d\">mainstream politics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>: women, people from diverse ethnic backgrounds, and community activists. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"d39ec2b6-93a1-4730-9d78-f22dde807b71\">Relationships between major and minor parties have also grown more stable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, and in many ways <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"426bb1cd-a924-4bcf-b408-63bbb2c80d6e\">minor parties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"7813e784-d5e2-4691-8144-9efead57b110\">function as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> auditors keeping a check on the major parties. MMP is not without its flaws, but the transition has generally been a positive experience.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 14-19, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>TRUE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>FALSE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if there is no information on this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37832\" id=\"question-wrapper-37832\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Under FPP the voter <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"6fc54b37-46e4-4e5c-b209-4d957a9b7e52\">always selects the candidate that the voter likes best<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37833\" id=\"question-wrapper-37833\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"6be46ed8-aae4-47f2-be79-0f7865b2f9e3\">Many votes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"4860260f-20a6-4b04-a45b-55390090bafa\">have no role in determining<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"7d628c0f-f525-4fbf-bed2-4357a77c8cc0\">the electoral result<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in the FPP system.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37834\" id=\"question-wrapper-37834\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>FPP uses geographically-determined electorates as a basis for electing MPs.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37835\" id=\"question-wrapper-37835\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>MMP may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"b460ff03-e514-4937-8e2b-618a4ccf9922\">give<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"3f90fb22-1fd6-4548-9c8f-45dcfd4ddeed\">minor parties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"9780b536-06fc-445b-9617-f771e8df723e\">disproportionate influence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37836\" id=\"question-wrapper-37836\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"8c95ad3b-4e91-44e9-ac58-d1d308a5a409\">A change in the electoral system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"f790179a-e258-4b68-bfa0-736adeaff22f\">rejected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> by New Zealand voters in the early 1990s.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37837\" id=\"question-wrapper-37837\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>In both FPP and MMP systems <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"bbc48adc-75c1-47ad-84c8-94ffedf24e54\">government may not be formed based on a majority voter mandate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the summary below with words taken from Reading Passage 2.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Use </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 20-26.</span></i></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"4f058b6d-58ce-4c34-9596-014a42acfaa0\">Public dissatisfaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> with elections came about as a result of the (20)_____ in New Zealand, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"e77bcaaa-53ab-43af-976c-25cce10c29fd\">many people voted for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> a (21)_____ instead. However, the parliamentary representation was disproportionate to the number of votes received and, after investigation, this situation eventually led to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"e151d2b5-3d21-48e3-b533-e8cc4859f012\">national<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> (22)_____ which asked the people to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"ac637d49-5c54-4da7-9060-27d6fac2720c\">express their preference for a particular electoral system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. The first experience was messy, however: (23)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"88242ef2-6b89-477f-a539-b535caf3a8de\">ensued after<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"383286bd-d24b-4cb0-8c68-b1db4966453e\">New Zealand First party decided to go into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> (24)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"383286bd-d24b-4cb0-8c68-b1db4966453e\">with National<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"5bbc70e2-5667-4ecc-8438-4238885156f4\">instead of the Labour party<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>New Zealanders have since become used to MMP, and its advantages are now clearer. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"c178766f-c91a-46c1-ab8e-411211ff4c89\">People<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"4ab527bf-565e-4a76-9d3f-3b8ed418241f\">once<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> (25)_____ from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"c8b56360-9031-41b7-bd2c-046d563bbe1d\">affairs of state<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"f9e38045-a569-4b74-8711-98c8273675df\">gained access to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> Parliament, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"d39ec2b6-93a1-4730-9d78-f22dde807b71\">and major and minor parties now get along better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"426bb1cd-a924-4bcf-b408-63bbb2c80d6e\">the latter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"7813e784-d5e2-4691-8144-9efead57b110\">taking on the role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> of (26)_____.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37838\" id=\"question-wrapper-37838\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TWO-PARTY SYSTEM</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37839\" id=\"question-wrapper-37839\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">THIRD PARTY</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37840\" id=\"question-wrapper-37840\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">REFERENDUM</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37841\" id=\"question-wrapper-37841\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PARTY-HOPPING</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37842\" id=\"question-wrapper-37842\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COALITION</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37843\" id=\"question-wrapper-37843\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MARGINALISED/MARGINALIZED</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37844\" id=\"question-wrapper-37844\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AUDITORS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"6be46ed8-aae4-47f2-be79-0f7865b2f9e3","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Many votes","passagePhrase":"a large number of wasted votes"},{"uid":"4860260f-20a6-4b04-a45b-55390090bafa","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"have no role in determining","passagePhrase":"do not affect"},{"uid":"7d628c0f-f525-4fbf-bed2-4357a77c8cc0","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the electoral result","passagePhrase":"the outcome of the election"},{"uid":"bbc48adc-75c1-47ad-84c8-94ffedf24e54","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"government may not be formed based on a majority voter mandate","passagePhrase":"not actually gain the most votes ... governed alone with only 35 percent of the vote ... neither major party able to govern alone ... form a coalition"},{"uid":"9780b536-06fc-445b-9617-f771e8df723e","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"disproportionate influence","passagePhrase":"ability to affect change within parliament ... ability to essentially choose the government"},{"uid":"b460ff03-e514-4937-8e2b-618a4ccf9922","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"give","passagePhrase":"accrue to"},{"uid":"3f90fb22-1fd6-4548-9c8f-45dcfd4ddeed","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"minor parties","passagePhrase":"centrist, smaller party"},{"uid":"4f058b6d-58ce-4c34-9596-014a42acfaa0","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Public dissatisfaction","passagePhrase":"many New Zealanders grew disillusioned with"},{"uid":"e77bcaaa-53ab-43af-976c-25cce10c29fd","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"many people voted for","passagePhrase":"the leading third party received a considerable 16 percent of the vote"},{"uid":"8c95ad3b-4e91-44e9-ac58-d1d308a5a409","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"A change in the electoral system","passagePhrase":"recommended a shift to MMP"},{"uid":"e151d2b5-3d21-48e3-b533-e8cc4859f012","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"national","passagePhrase":"state-wide"},{"uid":"ac637d49-5c54-4da7-9060-27d6fac2720c f790179a-e258-4b68-bfa0-736adeaff22f","qNum":"18 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"passed"},{"uid":"ac637d49-5c54-4da7-9060-27d6fac2720c","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"express their preference for a particular electoral system","passagePhrase":"in favour of the reform"},{"uid":"5bbc70e2-5667-4ecc-8438-4238885156f4","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"instead of the Labour party","passagePhrase":"Instead of forming a coalition with Labour"},{"uid":"383286bd-d24b-4cb0-8c68-b1db4966453e","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"New Zealand First party decided to go into ... with National","passagePhrase":"the New Zealand First party sided with the National party"},{"uid":"88242ef2-6b89-477f-a539-b535caf3a8de","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"ensued after","passagePhrase":"a subsequent rise in"},{"uid":"f9e38045-a569-4b74-8711-98c8273675df","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"gained access to","passagePhrase":"introduced"},{"uid":"c178766f-c91a-46c1-ab8e-411211ff4c89","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"People","passagePhrase":"a number of MPs"},{"uid":"4ab527bf-565e-4a76-9d3f-3b8ed418241f","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"once","passagePhrase":"previously"},{"uid":"c8b56360-9031-41b7-bd2c-046d563bbe1d","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"affairs of state","passagePhrase":"mainstream politics"},{"uid":"d39ec2b6-93a1-4730-9d78-f22dde807b71","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"and major and minor parties now get along better","passagePhrase":"Relationships between major and minor parties have also grown more stable"},{"uid":"426bb1cd-a924-4bcf-b408-63bbb2c80d6e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"the latter","passagePhrase":"minor parties"},{"uid":"7813e784-d5e2-4691-8144-9efead57b110","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"taking on the role","passagePhrase":"function as"}]},"reading_u2_141":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><span>Neurologists tend to divide the experience of love into three distinct categories: attraction, lust and attachment. The combination of all three can make for an intoxicating and lasting bond, but they are not always experienced together. Frequently, for example, we lust after those with whom we have no desire of having a long-term relationship; at other times, we feel 'attached' to people in the sense of being drawn to them emotionally or spiritually, but not drawn to them physically. It is accurate to describe these as 'stages' of love—lust tends to come first, then attraction, which lasts for months or years, and finally attachment, which can keep people together for decades. These are separate chemical substrates, so they can overlap; however, evidence suggests that attraction has a limited lifespan.</span></p><p><i><span>Lust</span></i><span> is typically experienced soon after puberty. This is when estrogen and testosterone—the underlying chemical substrates for lust in women and men respectively—activate themselves in our bodies for the first time. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"29c0ff6f-4aa6-4559-ac9b-daad55e4e53b\">The primary purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of lust is believed to be procreation, and the experience is one of feeling physically drawn, or even 'pulled' towards another person. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"9e2487ea-771d-4cbb-b4da-948aa8c86475\">Pheromones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"28226ff8-92de-4d2b-903a-87862f08cc61\">physical attractiveness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and our socialised predispositions for what we seek in a mate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"6d076c8c-4bdd-44e3-ac8e-9d6cab32a12d\">are the factors that activate the sensation of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> lust. Despite the strength it can have over our psyche, lust on its own is a very fleeting experience. It can firmly steer people together for their initial encounters, but it has no power to keep them there.</span></p><p><span>If the relationship is to last, something called </span><i><span>attraction</span></i><span> must take place. Attraction is the intoxicating sensation experienced in the initial period of knowing someone. The 'symptoms' include dizziness, flushed skin, and a loss of appetite and sleep. These are a result of a chemical cocktail of dopamine and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"3dfbc266-3fab-4f61-97e7-70978d0002fb\">norepinephrine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that PEA—a transmitter chemical—unleashes into the bloodstream when attraction takes place. Dopamine is responsible for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"624d23d2-55f9-4cd9-bc01-5503378bf3b2\">the blissful feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of self-confidence, joy and motivation that new love brings about; norepinephrine, similar to adrenaline, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"cd772bbf-c486-4981-a963-87f5901643d4\">brings about palpitations and anxiety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Attraction has more staying power than lust; while its intensity fades after a few weeks, the effect of the PEA transmission <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"0e74a306-79d0-469a-b56b-b5ed8062df8c\">can continue for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> some time between eighteen months and four years. After that, our bodies build up a natural tolerance.</span></p><p><span>At this stage, a transition to a phase called </span><i><span>attachment</span></i><span> can occur. The 'rush' of attraction is replaced by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"303974d2-8842-465b-a573-cccdc22b1f5e\">endorphins like oxytocin and vasopressin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> that feel like a gentle, warm sort of pleasantness—a safe feeling that calms the mind, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"8e9ae874-422e-42c5-9efc-0484353117bc\">numbs pain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> and soothes anxiety. This is a much more pleasant feeling in which to spend an extended period of time—potentially, forty, fifty or more years, depending on when you meet your partner. It allows you to live your life with someone, without their being the central obsession of your life. Unfortunately, there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"149da4b3-b2c9-4134-bf6c-52eedd1a2335\">no guarantee that PEA transmission will evolve into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the endorphin stage—in many instances, it will be replaced by a feeling of emptiness and dissatisfaction. It is not a coincidence that peak divorce rates occur at between four and seven years, as PEA transmission wears away and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"84d74349-99a9-45e6-b86d-a897af46e826\">attachment does not materialise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> in many people's brains.</span></p><p><span>Even neurologists agree that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"0155dc03-3959-4514-9d6d-2bd7f6055938\">chemistry isn't everything<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. There are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"0155dc03-3959-4514-9d6d-2bd7f6055938\">numerous other factors such as culture and personality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, for which science <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"0155dc03-3959-4514-9d6d-2bd7f6055938\">may never have an explanation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. While dopamine is bliss, however, ignorance is not—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"6650b8f4-fb7e-4b4a-9898-2e04d8a9f6cf\">neurology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> has much to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"38e2fcd4-54dc-4f01-a51d-7fdf0e951871\">contribute to satisfaction in our personal lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"b1a312ee-db53-439f-8a2d-faa4ffbd384f\">It may not be a good idea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"d3cbfb3a-84fd-4668-8e39-f565412a57ec\">commit to marriage or spending the rest of your life with someone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"b1a312ee-db53-439f-8a2d-faa4ffbd384f\">if you still feel the blissful rush of PEA transmission<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, for example. Once your brain has succumbed to the warming opiates of oxytocin and vasopressin, this will be a safer commitment. Attachment brings other needs to the foreground, however; while people enjoy the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"99be7f29-bf69-4444-a9ae-27c4741d1c94\">security<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5087e43f-ae6e-423e-8efe-e5ec6559ee19\">attachment brings about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, they do not lose their desires for either lust or attraction. Losing the ability to give your partner the rush of PEA transmission, while knowing that he may feel this for other people, can bring about jealousy and anxiety in people. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"3f18fc4b-4229-4e0e-bed7-aa995b557ea3\">Acknowledging and discussing these insecurities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"7fff658b-e2d6-49f9-b801-9f357cfef1fa\">alleviate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> them as it is likely that, to some extent, both partners will be feeling them.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the notes below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 27-33.</span></i></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"15\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Lust</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"34\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Attraction</span></b></p></td><td colspan=\"31\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><b><span>Attachment</span></b></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"15\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"29c0ff6f-4aa6-4559-ac9b-daad55e4e53b\">Designed to encourage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> (27)_____</span></p></td><td colspan=\"34\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Two chemicals are released through a third one called PEA</span></p></td><td colspan=\"31\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"303974d2-8842-465b-a573-cccdc22b1f5e\">Chemicals in the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> work to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"8e9ae874-422e-42c5-9efc-0484353117bc\">reduce physical &amp; mental suffering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, and calm (31)_____</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"15\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"6d076c8c-4bdd-44e3-ac8e-9d6cab32a12d\">Generated by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"9e2487ea-771d-4cbb-b4da-948aa8c86475\">natural scent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"28226ff8-92de-4d2b-903a-87862f08cc61\">looks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, and (28)_____</span></p></td><td colspan=\"34\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>(29)_____ is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"624d23d2-55f9-4cd9-bc01-5503378bf3b2\">a feel-good chemical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"3dfbc266-3fab-4f61-97e7-70978d0002fb\">norepinephrine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"cd772bbf-c486-4981-a963-87f5901643d4\">brings about elevated heart-rate and nervousness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p></td><td colspan=\"31\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Separate chemical processes mean <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"149da4b3-b2c9-4134-bf6c-52eedd1a2335\">PEA transmission does not always progress to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> (32)_____</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"15\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>Has weak staying power</span></p></td><td colspan=\"34\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"0e74a306-79d0-469a-b56b-b5ed8062df8c\">Can last for up to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></span></p><p><span>(30)_____</span></p></td><td colspan=\"31\" rowspan=\"1\"><p><span>There is a relationship between (33)_____ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"84d74349-99a9-45e6-b86d-a897af46e826\">the failure of attachment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> to occur</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37845\" id=\"question-wrapper-37845\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PROCREATION</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37846\" id=\"question-wrapper-37846\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOCIALISED/SOCIALIZED PREDISPOSITIONS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37847\" id=\"question-wrapper-37847\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DOPAMINE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37848\" id=\"question-wrapper-37848\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOUR/4 YEARS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37849\" id=\"question-wrapper-37849\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ANXIETY [OR] THE MIND</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37850\" id=\"question-wrapper-37850\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ENDORPHIN STAGE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37851\" id=\"question-wrapper-37851\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DIVORCE RATES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 34-39, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>YES</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NO</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37852\" id=\"question-wrapper-37852\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>We <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"0155dc03-3959-4514-9d6d-2bd7f6055938\">cannot explain all romantic decisions on the basis of chemical processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37853\" id=\"question-wrapper-37853\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"6650b8f4-fb7e-4b4a-9898-2e04d8a9f6cf\">Knowing about brain chemistry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> can actually <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"38e2fcd4-54dc-4f01-a51d-7fdf0e951871\">harm our happiness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37854\" id=\"question-wrapper-37854\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"d3cbfb3a-84fd-4668-8e39-f565412a57ec\">Long-term relationship commitments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"b1a312ee-db53-439f-8a2d-faa4ffbd384f\">should be made after attraction has faded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37855\" id=\"question-wrapper-37855\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Relationship <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"99be7f29-bf69-4444-a9ae-27c4741d1c94\">insecurities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5087e43f-ae6e-423e-8efe-e5ec6559ee19\">fade away once the attachment phase begins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37856\" id=\"question-wrapper-37856\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Growing resistance to PEA transmission is experienced as mental anguish.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37857\" id=\"question-wrapper-37857\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"3f18fc4b-4229-4e0e-bed7-aa995b557ea3\">Talking about the effects of PEA resistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> on a relationship can <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"7fff658b-e2d6-49f9-b801-9f357cfef1fa\">make anxiety worse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answer in box 40.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37858\" id=\"question-wrapper-37858\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which is the most suitable title for Passage 3?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The chemical progression of love</li> <li>B. Is it lust or is it love?</li> <li>C. How love fades over time</li> <li>D. Why nuptials and neurology don't mix</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"29c0ff6f-4aa6-4559-ac9b-daad55e4e53b","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Designed to encourage","passagePhrase":"The primary purpose"},{"uid":"9e2487ea-771d-4cbb-b4da-948aa8c86475","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"natural scent","passagePhrase":"Pheromones"},{"uid":"28226ff8-92de-4d2b-903a-87862f08cc61","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"looks","passagePhrase":"physical attractiveness"},{"uid":"6d076c8c-4bdd-44e3-ac8e-9d6cab32a12d","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Generated by","passagePhrase":"are the factors that activate the sensation of"},{"uid":"3dfbc266-3fab-4f61-97e7-70978d0002fb","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"norepinephrine","passagePhrase":"norepinephrine"},{"uid":"624d23d2-55f9-4cd9-bc01-5503378bf3b2","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"a feel-good chemical","passagePhrase":"the blissful feelings"},{"uid":"cd772bbf-c486-4981-a963-87f5901643d4","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"brings about elevated heart-rate and nervousness","passagePhrase":"brings about palpitations and anxiety"},{"uid":"0e74a306-79d0-469a-b56b-b5ed8062df8c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Can last for up to","passagePhrase":"can continue for"},{"uid":"303974d2-8842-465b-a573-cccdc22b1f5e","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Chemicals in the brain","passagePhrase":"endorphins like oxytocin and vasopressin"},{"uid":"8e9ae874-422e-42c5-9efc-0484353117bc","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"reduce physical & mental suffering","passagePhrase":"numbs pain"},{"uid":"149da4b3-b2c9-4134-bf6c-52eedd1a2335","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"PEA transmission does not always progress to","passagePhrase":"no guarantee that PEA transmission will evolve into"},{"uid":"84d74349-99a9-45e6-b86d-a897af46e826","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"the failure of attachment","passagePhrase":"attachment does not materialise"},{"uid":"0155dc03-3959-4514-9d6d-2bd7f6055938","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"cannot explain all romantic decisions on the basis of chemical processes","passagePhrase":"chemistry isn't everything ... numerous other factors such as culture and personality ... may never have an explanation"},{"uid":"6650b8f4-fb7e-4b4a-9898-2e04d8a9f6cf","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Knowing about brain chemistry","passagePhrase":"neurology"},{"uid":"b1a312ee-db53-439f-8a2d-faa4ffbd384f","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"should be made after attraction has faded","passagePhrase":"It may not be a good idea ... if you still feel the blissful rush of PEA transmission"},{"uid":"d3cbfb3a-84fd-4668-8e39-f565412a57ec","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Long-term relationship commitments","passagePhrase":"commit to marriage or spending the rest of your life with someone"},{"uid":"3f18fc4b-4229-4e0e-bed7-aa995b557ea3","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Talking about the effects of PEA resistance","passagePhrase":"Acknowledging and discussing these insecurities"}]},"reading_u2_142":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Clutter Bugs Beware</span></b></p><p><span>Having an abundance of stuff is a symptom of 21st Century materialism—people are conditioned by society to think that more is better—but take heed: it can suck your energy and your time. An unruly assortment of stuff littering your room or your home can be both annoying and unsettling. Precious items and anything with real sentimental value should be stored carefully, of course, but <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"77326579-924a-4312-8dd8-c845e6fb2ae2\">clutter such as old receipts, outdated invitations, catalogues, your collection of trashy magazines and unwanted gifts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> should be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"c63e976b-09ae-4a7f-af24-d840f0a92b54\">disposed of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. If you added up the time spent looking for misplaced objects or sifting through unnecessary papers to find what you need, what would that amount to? <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"e1a179d9-f232-4a57-8cfa-7a958a0ba7ee\">There is a lot to be said<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"82ad7c52-ba32-4beb-be07-a6a631c0e4a3\">the old adage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>: a place for everything and everything in its place.</span></p><p><span>This ancient organising truism can help you get your life in order and be free from clutter forever. Firstly, develop a system with a restricted series of options. Put all incoming material into your 'inbox' at work, or whatever the equivalent is at home, then deal with the tasks one by one. Either do them immediately or prioritise them into A, B or C tasks ensuring that the 'A' tasks take precedence over all others.</span></p><p><span>Another simple tip: find a home for everything. Before you toss something down on the countertop or sofa, ask yourself, 'Is that where it belongs?' If it does not have a home, designate a place for that object and use the same spot every time. Label boxes and containers, drawers and cupboards and, remember, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7ce69de0-9aa2-4705-9d48-8cf4af380a5a\">procrastination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"58bdca42-75c9-4e5f-9e58-20f228a28be2\">to be avoided at all costs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. Stow belongings and equipment in their assigned places straight away. Get into the habit—concentrate your energy on it until it becomes automatic. Clear off all flat surfaces like the desk in your office, the bench top in the kitchen or the bed in the bedroom.</span></p><p><span>Be aware of transition stages, when you are moving from one task to another, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"15b40a04-458c-46b1-a136-ba63270d451c\">exploit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> this phase <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"f8b3b612-cba4-4176-847f-a7e85de0aeda\">productively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"fdfe41b3-cc17-4623-97e1-9a12e91d6b36\">clean and clear up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9ff7cb6f-12b9-4917-aa79-983b373b06cb\">It is a good idea to have<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> an evaluation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"fee07ec6-096f-4a0c-a761-2ebedddd665a\">now and then<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> to review your <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"cb7932cf-7c3b-430b-b57e-f4a4d05bdc65\">organising system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and make adjustments. Perhaps there is more to de-clutter or perhaps you need to rearrange items, for example, if they are stored in one room but you use them in another. Clutter is also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"45c7849f-b7cd-48bf-ba3d-f07f30933147\">categorized as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"dea2430b-9d20-4200-ab69-e8a05c45a90b\">anything that is not finished<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> so, if you have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"dea2430b-9d20-4200-ab69-e8a05c45a90b\">incomplete projects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, make time to get them over and done with. Once you are clutter-free and well-organised, your life may change for the better.</span></p><p><span>Feng shui principles discourage the accumulation of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"11e314a6-22d4-44dc-b58b-b5064967e5ad\">clutter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> as 'chi' or energy cannot move freely around masses of material, causing stagnation and a breeding ground for negative energy. For harmony and productivity, chi has to be free flowing and unrestricted. (Interestingly, the word 'clutter' comes from an Old English word which means 'to cause to become blocked or obscured'.) Apparently, hoarding creates excessive 'yin' energy which interferes with the natural flow and causes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f34a6fd1-5d2a-442b-9a2b-dfc6c1f4fd7e\">imbalance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"aa1b122c-3180-4d73-826e-f5d9490a0661\">Some of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> the consequences of this are purported to be poor concentration, stress, resentfulness and a lowered immune system. Clutter is stuck energy that affects people on all levels: physically, mentally, emotionally, and spiritually. Clutter <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"926ad47b-23f7-4ef9-8864-66661782d6c3\">traps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> people in the past. It also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"bbfb1f2f-d964-4e55-b3e0-18825174e660\">shapes their self-image<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> and others' perception of them—perhaps as neglected, unworthy, disorganised or ignored, if it is true that your surroundings reflect your inner self, then cleaning up clutter must surely bring positive change into your life.</span></p><p><span>Call it feng shui or call it common sense: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"6f5b6b4b-3f17-43bf-8573-ab804d9b209d\">on a practical level<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ce221c3e-8339-49b4-9173-75c5a5027f8d\">the accumulation of junk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> hinders cleaning and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"04a8a0a9-29f7-4b9d-aace-bde63f371fa1\">fosters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> dirt and bacteria. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"c77ba982-dfc7-4f6c-9e7b-9cfb31317bd0\">creates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> chaos, obstructs new opportunities, takes up physical space and harms relationships in your life. So, why do people hoard?</span></p><p><span>There have been many reasons posited as to why people collect and hang on to junk. Psychologists used to say it sprang from an impoverished childhood with a scarcity of food and material possessions but more recently it has been argued that it arises from an adolescence deprived of emotional support and comfort. Fear obviously has a great deal to do with it, too: fear of not having enough; fear of letting go of the memories associated with the objects; or fear of loss of control or security. Perhaps egotism has a part to play in that people buy and accumulate material objects as a demonstration of their personal power. Others may do it as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"8b8a815d-90e7-4859-8624-a9d231d2d274\">a form of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> self compensation to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"4ed3e909-d4f5-4204-b936-9bf26df9d13a\">conceal unresolved emotional problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Whatever the reason for it, it is said that clutter in your home and in your life is disempowering, that it undermines your energy, erodes your spirit and holds you in the past. It also thwarts financial prosperity. Aim for a harmonious and balanced flow of 'chi' in your home and you may reap the rewards of a cleaner, more attractive, safer and nurturing place that is not only more comfortable but will allow you to pursue more effectively and successfully your true goals in life. Clean up and enjoy better health, wealth and happiness.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 1-5, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>YES</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NO</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37899\" id=\"question-wrapper-37899\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"77326579-924a-4312-8dd8-c845e6fb2ae2\">Anything that causes untidiness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in your dwelling should be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"c63e976b-09ae-4a7f-af24-d840f0a92b54\">thrown out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37900\" id=\"question-wrapper-37900\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"82ad7c52-ba32-4beb-be07-a6a631c0e4a3\">The ancient saying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> \"a place for everything and everything in its place\" <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"e1a179d9-f232-4a57-8cfa-7a958a0ba7ee\">is a good rule to follow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in the 21st Century.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37901\" id=\"question-wrapper-37901\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Organising systems should be limited to a set of no more than three options.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37902\" id=\"question-wrapper-37902\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>It is a good idea to identify individual items with tags.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37903\" id=\"question-wrapper-37903\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"7ce69de0-9aa2-4705-9d48-8cf4af380a5a\">Putting off things<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"58bdca42-75c9-4e5f-9e58-20f228a28be2\">a bad habit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the sentences below with words taken from Reading Passage 1.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Use </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 6-8.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37904\" id=\"question-wrapper-37904\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"15b40a04-458c-46b1-a136-ba63270d451c\">Use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (6)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"f8b3b612-cba4-4176-847f-a7e85de0aeda\">constructively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> as a time for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"fdfe41b3-cc17-4623-97e1-9a12e91d6b36\">tidying up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRANSITION STAGES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37905\" id=\"question-wrapper-37905\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Any <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"cb7932cf-7c3b-430b-b57e-f4a4d05bdc65\">management scheme for orderliness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"9ff7cb6f-12b9-4917-aa79-983b373b06cb\">benefit from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"fee07ec6-096f-4a0c-a761-2ebedddd665a\">occasional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> (7)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EVALUATION</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37906\" id=\"question-wrapper-37906\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"dea2430b-9d20-4200-ab69-e8a05c45a90b\">Any unfinished undertaking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> may also be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"45c7849f-b7cd-48bf-ba3d-f07f30933147\">classified as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (8)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CLUTTER</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the summary below with words taken from Reading Passage 1.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Use </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 9-13.</span></i></p><p><span>Feng shui is concerned with the flow of energy. There are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"aa1b122c-3180-4d73-826e-f5d9490a0661\">many<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> negative (9)_____ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f34a6fd1-5d2a-442b-9a2b-dfc6c1f4fd7e\">unbalanced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> 'chi'. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"11e314a6-22d4-44dc-b58b-b5064967e5ad\">Amassing a great deal of stuff<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"926ad47b-23f7-4ef9-8864-66661782d6c3\">holds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> people to the (10)_____ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"bbfb1f2f-d964-4e55-b3e0-18825174e660\">affects their self image<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"6f5b6b4b-3f17-43bf-8573-ab804d9b209d\">a matter of fact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ce221c3e-8339-49b4-9173-75c5a5027f8d\">a build-up of mess<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"04a8a0a9-29f7-4b9d-aace-bde63f371fa1\">creates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)_____ but on another level it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"c77ba982-dfc7-4f6c-9e7b-9cfb31317bd0\">generates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12)_____. People hoard junk for all sorts of reasons—most of them psychological, such as fear, egotism or even as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"8b8a815d-90e7-4859-8624-a9d231d2d274\">a kind of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)_____, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"4ed3e909-d4f5-4204-b936-9bf26df9d13a\">covering up various issues in their lives that have never been cleared up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37907\" id=\"question-wrapper-37907\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CONSEQUENCES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37908\" id=\"question-wrapper-37908\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PAST</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37909\" id=\"question-wrapper-37909\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DIRT/BACTERIA</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37910\" id=\"question-wrapper-37910\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CHAOS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37911\" id=\"question-wrapper-37911\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SELF COMPENSATION</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c63e976b-09ae-4a7f-af24-d840f0a92b54","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"thrown out","passagePhrase":"disposed of"},{"uid":"e1a179d9-f232-4a57-8cfa-7a958a0ba7ee","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"is a good rule to follow","passagePhrase":"There is a lot to be said"},{"uid":"82ad7c52-ba32-4beb-be07-a6a631c0e4a3","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"The ancient saying","passagePhrase":"the old adage"},{"uid":"7ce69de0-9aa2-4705-9d48-8cf4af380a5a","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Putting off things","passagePhrase":"procrastination"},{"uid":"58bdca42-75c9-4e5f-9e58-20f228a28be2","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"a bad habit","passagePhrase":"to be avoided at all costs"},{"uid":"15b40a04-458c-46b1-a136-ba63270d451c","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Use","passagePhrase":"exploit"},{"uid":"f8b3b612-cba4-4176-847f-a7e85de0aeda","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"constructively","passagePhrase":"productively"},{"uid":"fdfe41b3-cc17-4623-97e1-9a12e91d6b36","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"tidying up","passagePhrase":"clean and clear up"},{"uid":"9ff7cb6f-12b9-4917-aa79-983b373b06cb","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"benefit from","passagePhrase":"It is a good idea to have"},{"uid":"fee07ec6-096f-4a0c-a761-2ebedddd665a","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"occasional","passagePhrase":"now and then"},{"uid":"cb7932cf-7c3b-430b-b57e-f4a4d05bdc65","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"management scheme for orderliness","passagePhrase":"organising system"},{"uid":"45c7849f-b7cd-48bf-ba3d-f07f30933147","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"classified as","passagePhrase":"categorized as"},{"uid":"dea2430b-9d20-4200-ab69-e8a05c45a90b","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Any unfinished undertaking","passagePhrase":"anything that is not finished ... incomplete projects"},{"uid":"11e314a6-22d4-44dc-b58b-b5064967e5ad","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"Amassing a great deal of stuff","passagePhrase":"clutter"},{"uid":"f34a6fd1-5d2a-442b-9a2b-dfc6c1f4fd7e","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"unbalanced","passagePhrase":"imbalance"},{"uid":"aa1b122c-3180-4d73-826e-f5d9490a0661","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"many","passagePhrase":"Some of"},{"uid":"926ad47b-23f7-4ef9-8864-66661782d6c3","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"holds","passagePhrase":"traps"},{"uid":"bbfb1f2f-d964-4e55-b3e0-18825174e660","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"affects their self image","passagePhrase":"shapes their self-image"},{"uid":"6f5b6b4b-3f17-43bf-8573-ab804d9b209d","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"a matter of fact","passagePhrase":"on a practical level"},{"uid":"ce221c3e-8339-49b4-9173-75c5a5027f8d","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"a build-up of mess","passagePhrase":"the accumulation of junk"},{"uid":"04a8a0a9-29f7-4b9d-aace-bde63f371fa1","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"creates","passagePhrase":"fosters"},{"uid":"c77ba982-dfc7-4f6c-9e7b-9cfb31317bd0","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"generates","passagePhrase":"creates"},{"uid":"8b8a815d-90e7-4859-8624-a9d231d2d274","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"a kind of","passagePhrase":"a form of"},{"uid":"4ed3e909-d4f5-4204-b936-9bf26df9d13a","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"covering up various issues in their lives that have never been cleared up","passagePhrase":"conceal unresolved emotional problems"}]},"reading_u2_143":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>FLUORIDATION OF PUBLIC WATER SUPPLIES</span></b></p><p><span>Water fluoridation is the process of releasing small amounts of fluoride into the public water supply as a way to reduce dental health problems. The process of reducing tooth decay through fluoridation is clearly understood, and research confirms water fluoridation's effect on limiting instances of tooth decay. Nevertheless, fluoride is not harmless in all quantities. At levels moderately above those desired, it can result in something known as fluorosis, and at very high levels acute fluoride poisoning can occur.</span></p><p><span>Fluoride's function is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3180bf26-f3c8-4667-b7d3-9f18295958e9\">intervene in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the demineralisation mechanism of tooth decay. Demineralisation is a process that begins when sugary carbohydrates are eaten, and organic acids are subsequently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"7bfa9200-c038-41c7-937c-9cc4b20eba23\">generated by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"91ac38d7-ffde-441a-9a90-3dc25bef3cc9\">bacteria within the dental plaque<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. When a certain level of acidity is produced (<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"44b6776e-cd8a-4b4d-83cf-8467b4ce6aad\">pH in the oral cavity dips below 5.5<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>), the acids <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"2e18148a-9d86-4db7-99d8-f2cae2e8bc50\">waste away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> the main component of tooth enamel, a substance known as carbonated hydroxyapatite. If this erosion persists for months and years without adequate remineralisation, then tooth decay occurs, and dental cavities form.</span></p><p><span>Fluoride can greatly assist the mouth with the remineralisation of decaying enamel. Fluoridation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"4f1fd573-6712-4ea3-bb69-62610ce6b742\">creates fluoride ions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in saliva that can restore some of the lost <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"640cf65a-0a14-4999-a25c-e6bcc1fb91f6\">mineral content<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> from enamel after sugary acids have left the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"05e5b65e-4ad7-4f8d-89e7-b303cea1d7ff\">oral cavity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. When these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"b1457531-2807-44e7-9624-5259c36b29ac\">ions exist in plaque fluid alongside dissolved carbonated hydroxyapatite<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, and the pH is higher than 4.5, a fluorapatite veneer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"49f3d96f-a001-4db1-9b55-e8ef5b5afdd5\">covers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7e1c051d-2c0d-423b-a835-c3dd3fdaaa66\">the dental enamel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. This veneer has the benefit of being more acid-resistant than the tooth's hydroxyapatite, and is formed more quickly than by the natural remineralisation mechanism. Blood plasma <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"a71be3bc-e61d-4c74-94fa-a5056dca94df\">transports<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> any <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"24d265bc-ec61-4cb9-a78c-b7d297998914\">fluoride that has been ingested<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> to calcium-rich areas such as the teeth, supporting dental infrastructure from the inside as well.</span></p><p><span>The U.S. Center for Disease Control has listed fluoridation of the water supply as one of the greatest public health achievements of the 20th century. While tooth decay is rarely a threat to mortality, it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"45855b29-34ac-46c0-a273-9af5d3b94745\">one of the most prevalent chronic diseases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> globally and affects 60-90 percent of children across <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"06851714-8bc6-4c57-a807-2c91a88eca23\">industrialised countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Research suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"545ccba3-922b-4710-b877-74035311cb93\">the presence of fluoride in saliva at all times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> (but in small quantities) is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0fc1f59a-4919-4a78-b5a1-03a7234637c1\">the single most effective preventative measure of tooth decay<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Water fluoridation is perfectly geared towards helping to ensure this. Drinking water is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"c787006d-46e2-4f49-a761-c9bcce7f7243\">the largest source of fluoride for people globally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, and evidence demonstrates its efficacy in reducing cavities, particularly among poorer households without regular access to dentists.</span></p><p><span>Although not considered to be an essential ingredient (a substance necessary to perpetuate human life and biological development), fluoride can be considered a nutrient that counteracts harmful processes from lifestyle or environmental factors. Nevertheless, in doses higher than those desirable, a side effect known as dental fluorosis can occur. Its primary symptoms—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"17b5393f-5cd5-4d95-9aca-596155403eee\">pale streaking across the incisors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>—are considered a cosmetic problem for many people. The key risk period for developing fluorosis is ages one to four, with any likelihood of getting it having depleted by age eight. Young children are therefore encouraged to have their fluoride ingestion monitored—reduction of fluoride in infant formula and children's toothpaste has assisted this process.</span></p><p><span>Far more serious than mild dental fluorosis, however, yet much rarer, is a condition known as acute fluoride poisoning. This does not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b099198b-5b01-460f-a422-65d8a33d2d75\">happen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> very often, as it is unlikely that most people would ever come into contact with large amounts of fluoride. When it does happen, it is typically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"203c1a70-d8f9-42f4-be94-0fae3b832aa5\">a consequence of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> water technicians <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"89c1b1e8-6bba-437d-8830-10dbac7da132\">accidentally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"74a55329-280e-4968-982c-deece1d6fd95\">allowing excess amounts of fluoride into the system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, which is then ingested by an unsuspecting public. In one of the worst instances of fluoride poisoning, 262 people became ill and one person died in Alaska in 1992. During 2010 in Asheboro, North Carolina, 60 gallons of fluoride were released into the water supply in 90 minutes; this amount was intended for release over a 24-hour period. These incidents highlight the importance of careful monitoring to ensure public safety.</span></p><p><span>Not everyone supports water <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"0b5447bb-b81a-4195-8e79-424d16f8ffe9\">fluoridation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Paul Connett, a chemistry professor from St. Lawrence University, has listed many reasons to oppose the practice. Firstly, he suggests, studies that have tracked the effects of discontinuing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"859ee5e6-4f7c-4c20-bbff-b861fedb3e3a\">fluoridation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> in communities from Canada, Germany, Cuba and Finland have found that instances of dental decay actually dropped considerably as a result of halting the practice. Secondly, Connett finds that once water supplies are fluoridated it is impossible to control individual doses. This is because some people (manual labourers, athletes, diabetics, and people with kidney disease) drink more water than others, and we also receive fluoride from sources other than tap water.</span></p><p><span>Connett also expresses concern for purely ethical reasons, believing fluoridation to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"ce61dfe7-0302-4744-883e-c480739adf40 ff23f9e1-95be-4609-9b9d-990b2f5b3ab3\">contradict the medical ethic of informed consent</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Informed consent requires patients to be fully informed about medical operations before consenting to them—fluoridation <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"ce61dfe7-0302-4744-883e-c480739adf40 ff23f9e1-95be-4609-9b9d-990b2f5b3ab3\">evades this process</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Finally, Connett points to the World Health Organisation's acknowledgement that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"0b4f5b13-a76c-4d4a-8cbf-96db930b872e 80bb48fb-cc29-4586-b1c5-0262ed45b615\">fluoride's benefits are primarily achieved topically, that is, applied to the surface of teeth, rather than systemically</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (ingested).</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Answer the questions below using </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 14-19.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37912\" id=\"question-wrapper-37912\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does fluoridation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"3180bf26-f3c8-4667-b7d3-9f18295958e9\">affect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in order to prevent tooth decay?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DEMINERALISATION/DELIMINERALIZATION MECHANISM</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37913\" id=\"question-wrapper-37913\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What do <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"91ac38d7-ffde-441a-9a90-3dc25bef3cc9\">dental bacteria<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"7bfa9200-c038-41c7-937c-9cc4b20eba23\">produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ORGANIC ACIDS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37914\" id=\"question-wrapper-37914\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>When <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"44b6776e-cd8a-4b4d-83cf-8467b4ce6aad\">mouth pH goes below 5.5<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, what is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"2e18148a-9d86-4db7-99d8-f2cae2e8bc50\">dissolved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TOOTH ENAMEL [OR] CARBONATED HYDROXYAPATITE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37915\" id=\"question-wrapper-37915\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What does fluoridation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"4f1fd573-6712-4ea3-bb69-62610ce6b742\">form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"05e5b65e-4ad7-4f8d-89e7-b303cea1d7ff\">in the mouth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to restore <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"640cf65a-0a14-4999-a25c-e6bcc1fb91f6\">mineral density<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in teeth?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(FLUORIDE) IONS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37916\" id=\"question-wrapper-37916\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"49f3d96f-a001-4db1-9b55-e8ef5b5afdd5\">the coating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"b1457531-2807-44e7-9624-5259c36b29ac\">remineralisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> forms on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"7e1c051d-2c0d-423b-a835-c3dd3fdaaa66\">teeth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FLUORAPATITE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37917\" id=\"question-wrapper-37917\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Through what mechanism does <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"24d265bc-ec61-4cb9-a78c-b7d297998914\">swallowed fluoride<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"a71be3bc-e61d-4c74-94fa-a5056dca94df\">go to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> teeth?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BLOOD PLASMA</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-J, below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-J, in boxes 20-24 on your answer sheet.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"c787006d-46e2-4f49-a761-c9bcce7f7243\">the way most people around the world get fluoride<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. is a threat to public safety.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b099198b-5b01-460f-a422-65d8a33d2d75\">occur<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"203c1a70-d8f9-42f4-be94-0fae3b832aa5\">as a result of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"89c1b1e8-6bba-437d-8830-10dbac7da132\">mishaps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"74a55329-280e-4968-982c-deece1d6fd95\">adding fluoride to water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. can be regarded as nutritious.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"45855b29-34ac-46c0-a273-9af5d3b94745\">a widespread health issue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"06851714-8bc6-4c57-a807-2c91a88eca23\">developed countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. is not as common in infants.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"0fc1f59a-4919-4a78-b5a1-03a7234637c1\">the best protection against tooth decay<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"H\"><span>H. is required to sustain our material survival and biological growth.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"I\"><span>I. is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"17b5393f-5cd5-4d95-9aca-596155403eee\">visible as faint lines across the teeth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"J\"><span>J. is difficult to achieve amongst poorer people.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37918\" id=\"question-wrapper-37918\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Tooth decay</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37919\" id=\"question-wrapper-37919\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"545ccba3-922b-4710-b877-74035311cb93\">A constant, low level of fluoride in the mouth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37920\" id=\"question-wrapper-37920\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Drinking water</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37921\" id=\"question-wrapper-37921\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Dental fluorosis</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37922\" id=\"question-wrapper-37922\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Acute fluoride poisoning</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>TWO</span></b></i><i><span> letters A-E.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 25-26.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>TWO</span></b><span> of the following statements form part of Connett's opposition to fluoridation?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Fluoridation is proven to be poisonous.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Individuals react differently to fluoride.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. People may <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"0b5447bb-b81a-4195-8e79-424d16f8ffe9 859ee5e6-4f7c-4c20-bbff-b861fedb3e3a\">be fluoridated</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"ce61dfe7-0302-4744-883e-c480739adf40 ff23f9e1-95be-4609-9b9d-990b2f5b3ab3\">against their knowledge or will</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25 26\" data-uid=\"0b4f5b13-a76c-4d4a-8cbf-96db930b872e 80bb48fb-cc29-4586-b1c5-0262ed45b615\">Drinking water is not the most effective way to fluoridate teeth</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. When fluoridation stops, occurrences of tooth decay increase only slightly.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37923\" id=\"question-wrapper-37923\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37924\" id=\"question-wrapper-37924\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"3180bf26-f3c8-4667-b7d3-9f18295958e9","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"affect","passagePhrase":"intervene in"},{"uid":"7bfa9200-c038-41c7-937c-9cc4b20eba23","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"produce","passagePhrase":"generated by"},{"uid":"91ac38d7-ffde-441a-9a90-3dc25bef3cc9","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"dental bacteria","passagePhrase":"bacteria within the dental plaque"},{"uid":"44b6776e-cd8a-4b4d-83cf-8467b4ce6aad","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"mouth pH goes below 5.5","passagePhrase":"pH in the oral cavity dips below 5.5"},{"uid":"2e18148a-9d86-4db7-99d8-f2cae2e8bc50","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"dissolved","passagePhrase":"waste away"},{"uid":"4f1fd573-6712-4ea3-bb69-62610ce6b742","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"form","passagePhrase":"creates fluoride ions"},{"uid":"640cf65a-0a14-4999-a25c-e6bcc1fb91f6","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"mineral density","passagePhrase":"mineral content"},{"uid":"05e5b65e-4ad7-4f8d-89e7-b303cea1d7ff","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"in the mouth","passagePhrase":"oral cavity"},{"uid":"b1457531-2807-44e7-9624-5259c36b29ac","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"remineralisation","passagePhrase":"ions exist in plaque fluid alongside dissolved carbonated hydroxyapatite"},{"uid":"49f3d96f-a001-4db1-9b55-e8ef5b5afdd5","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"the coating","passagePhrase":"covers"},{"uid":"7e1c051d-2c0d-423b-a835-c3dd3fdaaa66","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"teeth","passagePhrase":"the dental enamel"},{"uid":"a71be3bc-e61d-4c74-94fa-a5056dca94df","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"go to","passagePhrase":"transports"},{"uid":"24d265bc-ec61-4cb9-a78c-b7d297998914","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"swallowed fluoride","passagePhrase":"fluoride that has been ingested"},{"uid":"45855b29-34ac-46c0-a273-9af5d3b94745","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"a widespread health issue","passagePhrase":"one of the most prevalent chronic diseases"},{"uid":"06851714-8bc6-4c57-a807-2c91a88eca23","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"developed countries","passagePhrase":"industrialised countries"},{"uid":"545ccba3-922b-4710-b877-74035311cb93","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"A constant, low level of fluoride in the mouth","passagePhrase":"the presence of fluoride in saliva at all times"},{"uid":"0fc1f59a-4919-4a78-b5a1-03a7234637c1","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"the best protection against tooth decay","passagePhrase":"the single most effective preventative measure of tooth decay"},{"uid":"c787006d-46e2-4f49-a761-c9bcce7f7243","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"the way most people around the world get fluoride","passagePhrase":"the largest source of fluoride for people globally"},{"uid":"17b5393f-5cd5-4d95-9aca-596155403eee","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"visible as faint lines across the teeth","passagePhrase":"pale streaking across the incisors"},{"uid":"b099198b-5b01-460f-a422-65d8a33d2d75","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"occur","passagePhrase":"happen"},{"uid":"203c1a70-d8f9-42f4-be94-0fae3b832aa5","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"as a result of","passagePhrase":"a consequence of"},{"uid":"89c1b1e8-6bba-437d-8830-10dbac7da132","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"mishaps","passagePhrase":"accidentally"},{"uid":"74a55329-280e-4968-982c-deece1d6fd95","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"adding fluoride to water","passagePhrase":"allowing excess amounts of fluoride into the system"},{"uid":"0b5447bb-b81a-4195-8e79-424d16f8ffe9","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fluoridation"},{"uid":"859ee5e6-4f7c-4c20-bbff-b861fedb3e3a","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fluoridation"},{"uid":"ce61dfe7-0302-4744-883e-c480739adf40 ff23f9e1-95be-4609-9b9d-990b2f5b3ab3","qNum":"25 26","questionPhrase":"against their knowledge or will","passagePhrase":"contradict the medical ethic of informed consent ... evades this process"},{"uid":"0b4f5b13-a76c-4d4a-8cbf-96db930b872e 80bb48fb-cc29-4586-b1c5-0262ed45b615","qNum":"25 26","questionPhrase":"Drinking water is not the most effective way to fluoridate teeth","passagePhrase":"fluoride's benefits are primarily achieved topically, that is, applied to the surface of teeth, rather than systemically"},{"uid":"0b5447bb-b81a-4195-8e79-424d16f8ffe9 859ee5e6-4f7c-4c20-bbff-b861fedb3e3a","qNum":"25 26","questionPhrase":"be fluoridated","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_144":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Employment, Underemployment and Unemployment</span></b></p><p><span>The last few decades have been turbulent for the global employment market, particularly in post-industrial countries. Around one third of the OECD labour force is unemployed, and global unemployment figures reached a historical peak of 185.9 million workers in 2003. Beyond this, a phenomenon known as 'underemployment' is becoming <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"d7040690-dc3e-494d-afd8-3f22a5bbd13d\">the normative practice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in many industries. Once considered a passing aberration, underemployment is now <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"d7040690-dc3e-494d-afd8-3f22a5bbd13d\">an entrenched and seemingly intractable feature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of the economy that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"cf599652-bd36-4278-89b3-fb4577463cb1\">involves people scraping by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"8ec609f2-2691-4a39-8455-a833c786efde\">precarious and temporary forms of work—typically casual, seasonal, or fixed-term work and often on part-time contracts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"77cac3d3-3b95-4b96-87b8-4df5ede663c1\">scholars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> have offered their own theorisations of the employment crisis and put forward some possible solutions. Certainly, almost all of these understandings differ over the finer analytical details, but more significantly there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"41b91965-2c4c-4770-a138-dcc774cf53d5\">almost no consensus around<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"857a4606-f368-4e86-b30b-6f9abe0b88d2\">what anchors the disruptive changes to employment patterns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5f5998bf-04d6-4b1d-8d88-7fcc573b43bc\">A majority of theorists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> stick to traditional models of unemployment, and argue that policy-makers in the West should now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"294dcbb8-55c6-4b7b-bbf5-be9bbf1c0c19\">focus on finding salvation in the 'knowledge economy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>', but others find this to be a mythical possibility. Broadly, it is too soon to say who is the closest to being correct, but history is sure to pick a winner.</span></p><p><span>One common denominator amongst <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"f5c60df2-08e3-48d6-8420-b3118651a420\">nearly every scholar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> is an unwillingness to reflect adequately upon work as an existing social practice, and as such <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"5e912d4e-25d4-4637-9c4d-d8ac695344f1\">solutions are put forward that are overly-derived from possibilities (that may not even be feasible) further down the track<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Andre Gorz, for example, emphasises the need for governments to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"79d4adff-b007-4389-a965-5147a65f6042\">shift the locus of work away from the abstracted labour that characterises private employment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"79d4adff-b007-4389-a965-5147a65f6042\">towards social labour that involves more public activities such as communal childcare, artistic exploration, community work, charities and so on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. This, he suggests, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"4f7e8915-cd1e-465a-b862-af4d1740b2bc\">strengthens and integrates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"75862e49-754c-43ed-8d8c-b72b42b4f1f6\">human relationships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> while supporting people in finding outlets for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"5eed6a62-ec33-4ffa-aeb4-a9c8163e4567\">their own creative and personal needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Similarly, Ulrich Beck suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"d9287af8-b9be-41a0-a51a-b4cbc01d80ae\">global employment markets are now riddled with risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"d9287af8-b9be-41a0-a51a-b4cbc01d80ae\">precariousness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"b2f16b4c-de74-429e-ac1f-02e9701ad546\">demands alleviation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"1054bc60-eb19-4920-8438-f527b74785f1\">The solution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, he suggests, is activating paid civil labour within national voluntary sectors while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"04e8b8e0-df4e-4efe-996f-edc678ce9d14\">activating this labour internationally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> as well. Both of these sound like good ideas, but are they plausible given the present constraints upon governments and people? Neither Gorz nor Beck says.</span></p><p><span>Another problem with analyses of the crisis tends to be a narrow sectoral focus that fails to problematise existing notions of work and employment. Jeremy Rifkin, for example, argues that the employment crisis is a result of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"58ffe02a-c1a9-419c-8c88-50cb59794f24\">accelerated technological growth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> that in turn <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2ffb0ec3-9dbe-4ccb-8942-cdbc1296760e\">displaces the labour intensitivity of some work practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. This process is not itself unprecedented, he suggests—in the early 20th century, for example, more efficient technologies in agriculture displaced farm labour in the south of the United States. At that time, however, new opportunities in the industrialising north of the country were able to absorb these surpluses. Rifkin's thesis posits that this is no longer happening—technological growth is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"44475b6e-dfa3-48ab-bd83-f4f7d29a1369\">making labour redundant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"b9289a9a-6adb-4f7d-8310-45449c912131\">without new opportunities emerging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Gorz builds on this theorisation to advocate policies, not of generating 'new' employment, but rather of distributing employment so that everyone can access a job. In doing so, he suggests, we can use the labour-saving gains of technology to free up time for other more socially meaningful pursuits. The problem with Rifkin's and Gorz's approaches, however, is that they assume the divisions between employment and non-employment are still pertinent and ultimately determinative of working practices. As Hasmet M. Uluorta indicates, however, the employment crisis may not be so much a crisis of jobs (or the number of jobs), technologies or tensions between paid and unpaid work, but rather a crisis of social reproduction—that is, the ways in which we sustain or perpetuate our social structure.</span></p><p><span>Whereas most scholars look to a renewed labour market for answers, or suggest that we need to bolster the voluntary sector as a supportive mechanism, Uluorta implores us to return to the drawing board and think about what really constitutes 'work'. It is not, he argues, solely the domain of employment <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"51e65148-5f7c-4090-9350-2aa66776383a\">geared towards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"271c9ab5-13f3-491d-88b6-4447156defde\">production and consumption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, but is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"271c9ab5-13f3-491d-88b6-4447156defde\">characterised by production in a broader sense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> for the purposes of social reproduction as well. We should no longer be asking 'How is it possible to generate employment?' but rather 'How is it possible to (re) produce our social existence?' The answers to the crisis, Uluorta argues, are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5a363d71-42e7-4008-9a50-d78d48edd4b8\">already being constituted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> as people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e026faa9-3665-4c14-933e-fb1f6d5ff760\">renegotiate work even in the absence of labour market employment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"71f7a256-d202-49bb-b862-1834afd8b5af\">legal and institutional mechanisms have yet to respond to these changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>We are ultimately left with a situation in which almost everyone agrees that there is a global crisis of employment, but there is widespread divergence of opinions over its nature. For some, the solution requires simply encouraging new forms of employment in the knowledge economy. Others believe that we need to balance employment with increased emphasis on voluntary and civil sector projects. Yet others believe that the crisis has in part come about because of a valorisation of employment over other forms of work, namely the work of social reproduction.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 27-32, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>YES</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NO</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37925\" id=\"question-wrapper-37925\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Underemployment is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"d7040690-dc3e-494d-afd8-3f22a5bbd13d\">a temporary misalignment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> from normal economic processes.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37926\" id=\"question-wrapper-37926\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"8ec609f2-2691-4a39-8455-a833c786efde\">Steady permanent work practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"cf599652-bd36-4278-89b3-fb4577463cb1\">characterise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> underemployment.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37927\" id=\"question-wrapper-37927\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"77cac3d3-3b95-4b96-87b8-4df5ede663c1\">Experts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"41b91965-2c4c-4770-a138-dcc774cf53d5\">do not agree on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"857a4606-f368-4e86-b30b-6f9abe0b88d2\">fundamental points of the employment problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37928\" id=\"question-wrapper-37928\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"5f5998bf-04d6-4b1d-8d88-7fcc573b43bc\">Most scholars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> think <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"294dcbb8-55c6-4b7b-bbf5-be9bbf1c0c19\">solutions lie in emphasising information-based employment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37929\" id=\"question-wrapper-37929\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"f5c60df2-08e3-48d6-8420-b3118651a420\">Almost all academics in this field<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"5e912d4e-25d4-4637-9c4d-d8ac695344f1\">are concerned with options for the future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37930\" id=\"question-wrapper-37930\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>There will need to be drastic changes to the world economy to fix the problem.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 33-40) and the list of people in the box below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Match each statement with the correct person A-D.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the appropriate letter A-D in boxes 33-40.</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NB</span></b></i><i><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Gorz</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Beck</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Rifkin</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Uluorta</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37931\" id=\"question-wrapper-37931\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Work <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"51e65148-5f7c-4090-9350-2aa66776383a\">involves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"271c9ab5-13f3-491d-88b6-4447156defde\">more than just those activities taking place in the employment market<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37932\" id=\"question-wrapper-37932\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"44475b6e-dfa3-48ab-bd83-f4f7d29a1369\">Today jobs are being lost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> but there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"b9289a9a-6adb-4f7d-8310-45449c912131\">no social capacity to make new ones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37933\" id=\"question-wrapper-37933\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"d9287af8-b9be-41a0-a51a-b4cbc01d80ae\">The instabilities beneath current employment practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"b2f16b4c-de74-429e-ac1f-02e9701ad546\">need to be removed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37934\" id=\"question-wrapper-37934\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"75862e49-754c-43ed-8d8c-b72b42b4f1f6\">Social cohesion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"5eed6a62-ec33-4ffa-aeb4-a9c8163e4567\">individual expression<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"4f7e8915-cd1e-465a-b862-af4d1740b2bc\">work in harmony<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37935\" id=\"question-wrapper-37935\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>\"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"e026faa9-3665-4c14-933e-fb1f6d5ff760\">New\" ways of creating work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5a363d71-42e7-4008-9a50-d78d48edd4b8\">already in existence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"71f7a256-d202-49bb-b862-1834afd8b5af\">not formally recognised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37936\" id=\"question-wrapper-37936\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Job creation is unnecessary if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"79d4adff-b007-4389-a965-5147a65f6042\">existing work is shared out in better ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37937\" id=\"question-wrapper-37937\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"1054bc60-eb19-4920-8438-f527b74785f1\">Employment problems can be alleviated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"04e8b8e0-df4e-4efe-996f-edc678ce9d14\">cross-border co-operation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37938\" id=\"question-wrapper-37938\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"58ffe02a-c1a9-419c-8c88-50cb59794f24\">Changes in production methods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> sometimes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"2ffb0ec3-9dbe-4ccb-8942-cdbc1296760e\">cut down the demand for labour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"cf599652-bd36-4278-89b3-fb4577463cb1","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"characterise","passagePhrase":"involves people scraping by"},{"uid":"77cac3d3-3b95-4b96-87b8-4df5ede663c1","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Experts","passagePhrase":"scholars"},{"uid":"41b91965-2c4c-4770-a138-dcc774cf53d5","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"do not agree on","passagePhrase":"almost no consensus around"},{"uid":"857a4606-f368-4e86-b30b-6f9abe0b88d2","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"fundamental points of the employment problems","passagePhrase":"what anchors the disruptive changes to employment patterns"},{"uid":"5f5998bf-04d6-4b1d-8d88-7fcc573b43bc","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Most scholars","passagePhrase":"A majority of theorists"},{"uid":"294dcbb8-55c6-4b7b-bbf5-be9bbf1c0c19","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"solutions lie in emphasising information-based employment","passagePhrase":"focus on finding salvation in the 'knowledge economy"},{"uid":"f5c60df2-08e3-48d6-8420-b3118651a420","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Almost all academics in this field","passagePhrase":"nearly every scholar"},{"uid":"5e912d4e-25d4-4637-9c4d-d8ac695344f1","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"are concerned with options for the future","passagePhrase":"solutions are put forward that are overly-derived from possibilities (that may not even be feasible) further down the track"},{"uid":"79d4adff-b007-4389-a965-5147a65f6042","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"existing work is shared out in better ways","passagePhrase":"shift the locus of work away from the abstracted labour that characterises private employment ... towards social labour that involves more public activities such as communal childcare, artistic exploration, community work, charities and so on"},{"uid":"4f7e8915-cd1e-465a-b862-af4d1740b2bc","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"work in harmony","passagePhrase":"strengthens and integrates"},{"uid":"75862e49-754c-43ed-8d8c-b72b42b4f1f6","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Social cohesion","passagePhrase":"human relationships"},{"uid":"5eed6a62-ec33-4ffa-aeb4-a9c8163e4567","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"individual expression","passagePhrase":"their own creative and personal needs"},{"uid":"d9287af8-b9be-41a0-a51a-b4cbc01d80ae","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"The instabilities beneath current employment practices","passagePhrase":"global employment markets are now riddled with risk ... precariousness"},{"uid":"b2f16b4c-de74-429e-ac1f-02e9701ad546","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"need to be removed","passagePhrase":"demands alleviation"},{"uid":"1054bc60-eb19-4920-8438-f527b74785f1","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Employment problems can be alleviated","passagePhrase":"The solution"},{"uid":"04e8b8e0-df4e-4efe-996f-edc678ce9d14","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"cross-border co-operation","passagePhrase":"activating this labour internationally"},{"uid":"58ffe02a-c1a9-419c-8c88-50cb59794f24","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Changes in production methods","passagePhrase":"accelerated technological growth"},{"uid":"2ffb0ec3-9dbe-4ccb-8942-cdbc1296760e","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"cut down the demand for labour","passagePhrase":"displaces the labour intensitivity of some work practices"},{"uid":"44475b6e-dfa3-48ab-bd83-f4f7d29a1369","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Today jobs are being lost","passagePhrase":"making labour redundant"},{"uid":"b9289a9a-6adb-4f7d-8310-45449c912131","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"no social capacity to make new ones","passagePhrase":"without new opportunities emerging"},{"uid":"51e65148-5f7c-4090-9350-2aa66776383a","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"involves","passagePhrase":"geared towards"},{"uid":"271c9ab5-13f3-491d-88b6-4447156defde","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"more than just those activities taking place in the employment market","passagePhrase":"production and consumption ... characterised by production in a broader sense"},{"uid":"5a363d71-42e7-4008-9a50-d78d48edd4b8","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"already in existence","passagePhrase":"already being constituted"},{"uid":"e026faa9-3665-4c14-933e-fb1f6d5ff760","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"New\" ways of creating work","passagePhrase":"renegotiate work even in the absence of labour market employment"},{"uid":"71f7a256-d202-49bb-b862-1834afd8b5af","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"not formally recognised","passagePhrase":"legal and institutional mechanisms have yet to respond to these changes"}]},"reading_u2_145":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>HYBRID SOLAR LIGHTING</span></b></p><p><span>—Light the Interiors of Buildings with Sunlight!</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"ad32212e-b085-435b-9727-fa11feaa7060\">Hybrid solar lighting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> is a system that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"aff37946-e9e9-4523-ac69-0b0b30dd1a5a\">captures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> sunlight on a roof top and uses optical fibres <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"fe4b863b-27a8-4c44-8a88-bed06b5123d9\">to channel it directly into a building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. The only power needed to operate it is a 9-volt battery and the energy cost reduction, worker productivity and health benefits are immense.</span></p><p><span>It was originally developed by the US Department of Energy at its Oak Ridge National Laboratory and licensed to a company called Sunlight Direct. It has already been installed in a large number and a wide range of buildings in the USA including higher education institutions, museums, department stores and other specialty stores. Initial reports declare that retail sales <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"68d257bf-463e-459a-bfd7-2b7654bc8155\">increase by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> as much as 40% when the switch is made from fluorescent lighting to hybrid solar. Furthermore, there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"4619d902-3f96-4888-a8cf-ccb8edb16277\">a major improvement in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the attention spans and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"c9b63e6c-27a6-4200-a3a5-7a11068f1ec6\">academic attainment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"b8cc27d1-e363-4867-bc01-fb600679ddc8\">undergraduates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> in classrooms or lecture theatres lit by hybrid solar. It is to be hoped that the technology can soon be made financially feasible for households as well as commercial buildings.</span></p><p><span>It has been suggested that 30% of the electricity used in the USA is just for lighting and, for retailers, the estimate increases to 45%. Obviously, that figure could decrease significantly if sunlight could be brought inside. Hybrid solar lighting is predicted not only to save millions of dollars in energy costs but it is attractive for its quality which is almost identical to daylight.</span></p><p><span>A solar collector consisting of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"280d5928-1856-4f50-91b3-bd06cf3abfbb\">a 1.2 metre parabolic primary mirror concentrates the light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> toward <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"5add4c2f-897c-4921-8f40-37cb2e7c37d4\">a secondary mirror which has a special multi-layer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> coating that reflects only the visible wavelengths which effectively strips off the ultra-violet and infra-red wavelengths from the reflected light. This is important to reduce heat in the fibre optics which would otherwise melt. The visible light is focused from the secondary mirror <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"4d20de65-e63f-4096-82fc-c2141f903c5d\">towards a receiver module where it is homogenized<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> to guarantee uniformity before it enters the fibre optic bundle which then passes into the building interior for lighting. The fibres are easily installed and replaced and unlike fluorescent lights that require energy, the hybrid solar system only needs one 9-volt battery to power the solar tracking system for a week.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"85053d9e-63d7-4beb-ad94-fef5e6b700c5\">The solar tracker mechanism consists of two motors that are controlled by a GPS<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> (global positioning system) micro processor situated beneath it. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"ccc28f6e-7b2a-4337-9b9d-9d2965cc73f9\">compute<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>s the exact position of the sun (based on the latitude, longitude, date and time) to within point one degree. The light collected shines brightly. Just two of these fibres emit enough light to be equivalent to a 60 Watt light bulb and there are 127 of fibres in one bundle. What if it is cloudy or rainy outside? That's where the hybrid comes in. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"5ee2d9e1-162b-41d2-97fd-c22f26f90412\">The lighting fixtures combine the sunlight with the artificial light from fluorescent or incandescent lamps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to create a hybrid luminaire. A photo sensor in the room <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b41c735f-66ca-4d6b-a4b4-c4ad4d550d87\">monitors the intensity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and automatic adjustments are made in order to keep a constant level of illumination.</span></p><p><span>A room lit entirely by fluorescence has an orange glow which is not very natural. If the lighting is changed to 80% solar and 20% fluorescent, it is far more aesthetically appealing. It is estimated that hybrid solar lighting could reduce their energy bill of most retailers by 60%; and retail stores have been some of the first adopters of the new technology because of the health benefits gained from natural lighting. Studies have shown that 20% of workers under <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a19f0b0b-3c22-4a76-aa05-ac75febbced3\">artificial light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"898c3244-ec21-42f4-ac92-288c85aef957\">suffer symptoms of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> depression from Seasonal Affective Disorder (SAD). In addition, retail stores with natural lighting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d4a16d55-4efc-46be-90ae-b65c2a7290c0\">sold 40% more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> merchandise than stores with artificial light. Research has shown that biological rhythms and circadian rhythms are the secret to having successful and productive employees. Bringing in the natural light helps regulate these biological processes.</span></p><p><span>The technology has made such an impression that other scientists are looking at alternative applications: utilizing the UV light energy for hot water heating, for example. There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b31372ea-c7ba-41fc-910c-1821aa62e294\">one limitation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to the technology, however: although <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"2882f113-f3ba-432e-b7ce-b336c9e5af93\">the plastic optical fibres are very low cost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, they also have very low transmittance and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"6b6db0e0-d6d8-4b32-875b-3aef97da429c\">extend for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> only around 15 metres from the solar collector. This is why currently solar hybrid lighting is primarily focused on the top and main floors of a building.</span></p><p><span>Overall, the potential electricity savings and carbon dioxide reductions are enormous. The units are designed to last twenty years and, as volumes of sales increase, the price should come down considerably. It may be a while before individual households can enjoy hybrid solar lighting but, in the meantime, there is a substantial benefit in that it is making many work and study spaces as natural and comfortable for humans as possible.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the summary below with words taken from Reading Passage 1.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Use </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 1-3.</span></i></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"ad32212e-b085-435b-9727-fa11feaa7060\">A hybrid solar lighting system has been developed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"aff37946-e9e9-4523-ac69-0b0b30dd1a5a\">uses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> (1)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"fe4b863b-27a8-4c44-8a88-bed06b5123d9\">to illuminate buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. Numerous advantages have been described, such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"68d257bf-463e-459a-bfd7-2b7654bc8155\">a boost in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> (2)_____ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"4619d902-3f96-4888-a8cf-ccb8edb16277\">increased<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> (3)_____ and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"c9b63e6c-27a6-4200-a3a5-7a11068f1ec6\">educational achievement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> amongst <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"b8cc27d1-e363-4867-bc01-fb600679ddc8\">students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37978\" id=\"question-wrapper-37978\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SUNLIGHT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37979\" id=\"question-wrapper-37979\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RETAIL SALES</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37980\" id=\"question-wrapper-37980\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ATTENTION SPANS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the diagram below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 4-8.</span></i></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Simulation/reading/images/d18f59b5a6867799bc834e3a1846a297cf4854c2a31567f0476b35688264bc1c.jpg\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37981\" id=\"question-wrapper-37981\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PRIMARY MIRROR</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37982\" id=\"question-wrapper-37982\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SECONDARY MIRROR</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37983\" id=\"question-wrapper-37983\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RECEIVER MODULE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37984\" id=\"question-wrapper-37984\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRACKER [OR] SOLAR TRACKER</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37985\" id=\"question-wrapper-37985\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EXACT POSITION</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the notes below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes 9-13.</span></p><p><span>● 127 fibres = 1 bundle</span></p><p><span>● 2 fibres = 60 Watt bulb</span></p><p><span>● A (9)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"b41c735f-66ca-4d6b-a4b4-c4ad4d550d87\">measures amount of light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> &amp; a (10)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"5ee2d9e1-162b-41d2-97fd-c22f26f90412\">mixes light from different sources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to keep levels constant</span></p><p><span>● Higher % of natural light, more attractive and biologically advantageous—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"a19f0b0b-3c22-4a76-aa05-ac75febbced3\">fluorescence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"898c3244-ec21-42f4-ac92-288c85aef957\">contributes to feelings of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11)_____ whereas natural or hybrid light gives rise to more productivity (&amp; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d4a16d55-4efc-46be-90ae-b65c2a7290c0\">the sale of more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12)_____ in shops) because it helps workers (&amp; shoppers) feel good and maintain biological rhythms.</span></p><p><span>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"2882f113-f3ba-432e-b7ce-b336c9e5af93\">Plastic fibres are cheap<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"6b6db0e0-d6d8-4b32-875b-3aef97da429c\">length from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the (13)_____ is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"b31372ea-c7ba-41fc-910c-1821aa62e294\">a limiting factor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37986\" id=\"question-wrapper-37986\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PHOTO SENSOR</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37987\" id=\"question-wrapper-37987\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HYBRID LUMINAIRE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37988\" id=\"question-wrapper-37988\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DEPRESSION</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37989\" id=\"question-wrapper-37989\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MERCHANDISE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37990\" id=\"question-wrapper-37990\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOLAR COLLECTOR</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"ad32212e-b085-435b-9727-fa11feaa7060","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"A hybrid solar lighting system has been developed","passagePhrase":"Hybrid solar lighting"},{"uid":"aff37946-e9e9-4523-ac69-0b0b30dd1a5a","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"uses","passagePhrase":"captures"},{"uid":"fe4b863b-27a8-4c44-8a88-bed06b5123d9","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"to illuminate buildings","passagePhrase":"to channel it directly into a building"},{"uid":"68d257bf-463e-459a-bfd7-2b7654bc8155","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"a boost in","passagePhrase":"increase by"},{"uid":"4619d902-3f96-4888-a8cf-ccb8edb16277","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"increased","passagePhrase":"a major improvement in"},{"uid":"c9b63e6c-27a6-4200-a3a5-7a11068f1ec6","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"educational achievement","passagePhrase":"academic attainment"},{"uid":"b8cc27d1-e363-4867-bc01-fb600679ddc8","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"students","passagePhrase":"undergraduates"},{"uid":"280d5928-1856-4f50-91b3-bd06cf3abfbb","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a 1.2 metre parabolic primary mirror concentrates the light"},{"uid":"5add4c2f-897c-4921-8f40-37cb2e7c37d4","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a secondary mirror which has a special multi-layer"},{"uid":"4d20de65-e63f-4096-82fc-c2141f903c5d","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"towards a receiver module where it is homogenized"},{"uid":"85053d9e-63d7-4beb-ad94-fef5e6b700c5","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The solar tracker mechanism consists of two motors that are controlled by a GPS"},{"uid":"ccc28f6e-7b2a-4337-9b9d-9d2965cc73f9","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"compute"},{"uid":"5ee2d9e1-162b-41d2-97fd-c22f26f90412","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"mixes light from different sources","passagePhrase":"The lighting fixtures combine the sunlight with the artificial light from fluorescent or incandescent lamps"},{"uid":"b41c735f-66ca-4d6b-a4b4-c4ad4d550d87","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"measures amount of light","passagePhrase":"monitors the intensity"},{"uid":"a19f0b0b-3c22-4a76-aa05-ac75febbced3","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"fluorescence","passagePhrase":"artificial light"},{"uid":"898c3244-ec21-42f4-ac92-288c85aef957","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"contributes to feelings of","passagePhrase":"suffer symptoms of"},{"uid":"d4a16d55-4efc-46be-90ae-b65c2a7290c0","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"the sale of more","passagePhrase":"sold 40% more"},{"uid":"b31372ea-c7ba-41fc-910c-1821aa62e294","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"a limiting factor","passagePhrase":"one limitation"},{"uid":"2882f113-f3ba-432e-b7ce-b336c9e5af93","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"Plastic fibres are cheap","passagePhrase":"the plastic optical fibres are very low cost"},{"uid":"6b6db0e0-d6d8-4b32-875b-3aef97da429c","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"length from","passagePhrase":"extend for"}]},"reading_u2_146":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>The Rise of Adjuncts</span></b></p><p data-heading-para=\"A\" data-question-number=\"14\"><span>A. Academia is often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a5823a7a-fc2c-4dda-a39c-a5ac4d26de78\">thought of as an occupation with immense job security<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a5823a7a-fc2c-4dda-a39c-a5ac4d26de78\">The traditional image is one of a middle-aged professor with his own office, his own car park, and a cosy job with a middle-class salary that remains unaffected by upturns and downturns in the 'real' business economy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. But in the United States today <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2ec072e5-a292-49fb-aeb9-194f9f7274cd\">only a minority of professors have anything resembling this lifestyle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. For the vast majority, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2ec072e5-a292-49fb-aeb9-194f9f7274cd\">the actual conditions of their employment are very different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2ec072e5-a292-49fb-aeb9-194f9f7274cd\">scrape by with low pay, short-term contracts and few or no employee benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2ec072e5-a292-49fb-aeb9-194f9f7274cd\">Many even qualify for food stamps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. This shift in employment conditions has far-reaching consequences not only for academics, but also for students and the quality of education they receive, and for academic freedom more generally.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"B\" data-question-number=\"15\"><span>B. Originally, almost all professors were in full-time positions and employed under a system known as 'life tenure'. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"f6de78b3-fd00-4423-b121-99f0d6503cb7\">Tenure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> all but guarantees professors a well-paid job until retirement; their position can only be terminated with 'just cause'. Proving just cause is a lengthy, difficult process that happens rarely—only around 50 of 280,000 tenured professors lose their status every year. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"0a18be23-fb81-4560-acd0-3ccbc386eb48\">The purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of tenure is to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 20\" data-uid=\"74464db6-acdc-4441-a42e-d476290c144c f6de78b3-fd00-4423-b121-99f0d6503cb7\">provide shelter for</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"74464db6-acdc-4441-a42e-d476290c144c\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 20\" data-uid=\"74464db6-acdc-4441-a42e-d476290c144c a35161f5-7884-4567-b738-359e8786e06b\">researchers</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a35161f5-7884-4567-b738-359e8786e06b\"> who dissent from dominant opinions, disagree with the authorities of universities, donors or political authorities</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a35161f5-7884-4567-b738-359e8786e06b\">choose to research topics that may have social importance but seem unimportant or unnecessary to others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. In this way it <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 20\" data-uid=\"0a18be23-fb81-4560-acd0-3ccbc386eb48 f6de78b3-fd00-4423-b121-99f0d6503cb7\">seeks to</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"f6de78b3-fd00-4423-b121-99f0d6503cb7\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15 20\" data-uid=\"74464db6-acdc-4441-a42e-d476290c144c f6de78b3-fd00-4423-b121-99f0d6503cb7\">keep intellectual pursuits 'pure</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>' <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"be60ae89-780b-4aa0-ab0d-ab5b12b56124\">rather than at the whim of external interests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Without tenure, professors might prefer uncontroversial research on popular topics, and draw dishonest conclusions in a bid to please authorities and keep their jobs.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"C\" data-question-number=\"16\"><span>C. In an era of perpetual cost-cutting and budget-tightening, however, guaranteeing large numbers of academics lifetime employment with related benefits is increasing untenable. The proportion of university teachers with tenure has slid from 75 percent in 1960 to just 27 percent today. Rising in their place are '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"d0bd6f13-93a9-4913-b3ad-645bd3c265cb\">professor adjuncts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>'. Adjuncts are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"d0bd6f13-93a9-4913-b3ad-645bd3c265cb\">temporary, part-time employees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> who were initially brought in only occasionally as special guest lecturers or to provide cover for tenured professors on parental or research leave. Adjuncts <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"d0bd6f13-93a9-4913-b3ad-645bd3c265cb\">teach individual classes and have no research or administrative responsibilities, and their contracts typically run for a single semester<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, after which they might be renewed. Over the last few decades <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"3f3dd770-e3a0-47b6-9a95-c71fe7e0bbf6\">their use has been extended beyond these temporary exigencies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, and adjuncts have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"3f3dd770-e3a0-47b6-9a95-c71fe7e0bbf6\">become a permanent, institutionalised aspect of academic employment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"D\" data-question-number=\"17\"><span>D. This has created several problems for adjunct professors, who are considered by some to make up a growing 'academic underclass'. Firstly, because contracts are always temporary, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ace75586-057e-41e9-9d8e-b55b048f420c\">adjuncts </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 21\" data-uid=\"37d2947f-b0fb-4019-86e2-c147c3f0434d ace75586-057e-41e9-9d8e-b55b048f420c\">rarely qualify for insurance and health benefits, such as time off with remuneration for illness</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, in the same way as tenured professors. Secondly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"37d2947f-b0fb-4019-86e2-c147c3f0434d\">recompense for adjuncts is often very low<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. In order to make a living from their work, adjuncts <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"37d2947f-b0fb-4019-86e2-c147c3f0434d\">typically need to win contracts with multiple universities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. As a consequence of this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"fcfac14a-8bbc-410d-be44-15d01652bef1\">high teaching workload<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>—and the lack of paid research opportunities—adjuncts tend to <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 22\" data-uid=\"849c63f6-32c2-4ed8-b329-5a10e281df9b fcfac14a-8bbc-410d-be44-15d01652bef1\">find it hard to publish articles</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"849c63f6-32c2-4ed8-b329-5a10e281df9b\"> and win research grants</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, therefore <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 22\" data-uid=\"849c63f6-32c2-4ed8-b329-5a10e281df9b c283dbc7-2a75-4c53-a225-8e431047d4e1\">making promotion increasingly unlikely</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"c283dbc7-2a75-4c53-a225-8e431047d4e1\"> with every year that passes</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> (academic promotion is governed by what is known as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"849c63f6-32c2-4ed8-b329-5a10e281df9b\">a 'publish or perish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>' culture).</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"E\" data-question-number=\"18\"><span>E. The culture of using adjuncts also has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430\">flow-on effects for the quality of teaching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that students receive. Because adjuncts <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"d5a824f4-b20d-46e8-8513-f9afb400e46b\">come in only for classes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, they do not have offices or office hours on campus, and usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"542e95fe-3e57-426f-8171-47a021a353c6\">do not have the time to meet up with students in small groups or for one-on-one sessions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. The disengagement between students and teachers can <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 23\" data-uid=\"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430 542e95fe-3e57-426f-8171-47a021a353c6\">make it difficult for struggling students to find guidance outside of lectures</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"7861665e-018e-41de-9d84-2f4766ea3bc1\">Adjuncts are also less 'tied' to the universities they teach at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 24\" data-uid=\"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430 e5c40966-514b-43ca-9607-22d3e61e39b5\">fail to</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430\"> accumulate reputations over time</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"4348c877-bb05-45e3-994b-84ab87af4dde\">in the same way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b85d7b89-1f7c-4f75-a419-c891b12b8596\">full-time professors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. As such, they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430\">not as personally invested in the quality and outcome of their teaching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Finally, it has been reported that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430\">many adjuncts practice </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 25\" data-uid=\"10333e19-3142-4bbc-b138-698ccf593287 4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430\">grade inflation</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430\">—</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18 25\" data-uid=\"10333e19-3142-4bbc-b138-698ccf593287 4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430\">raising grades higher than deserved</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430\">—in order to maintain their job security by keeping students pleased</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. These outcomes are not because adjuncts are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"bc7d7b66-ccb2-4680-a571-c0bd353d1501\">malfeasant or incompetent professors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, but rather <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"3e170e67-b7fe-491d-bd09-08414a60ded3\">because of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> the structural pressures this type of work involves—precisely what the tenure system sought to overcome.</span></p><p data-heading-para=\"F\" data-question-number=\"19\"><span>F. The rising use of adjunct professors also has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"aa5ac234-3406-403b-a55b-c8f2f682bf1e\">implications for the research and pedagogical autonomy of teachers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Because adjuncts do not have tenure, they can be fired with the simplest of explanations. Furthermore, administrators who do not want to give any reason at all can choose to simply not renew an adjunct's contract after the semester finishes. As such, there is immense pressure on adjuncts to teach in ways that please those who employ them. While only 50 tenured professors lose their jobs in the USA every year, reports emerge every day about adjuncts who have been fired or not had contracts renewed after disputes with faculty or administrators over course design, teaching, or employment issues. As the pool of growing numbers of adjuncts compete desperately for the shrinking amount of tenure-track positions, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"aa5ac234-3406-403b-a55b-c8f2f682bf1e\">intellectual conformity can grow as candidates position themselves as safe, mainstream choices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. As theoretical physicist Lee Smolin has written, '...<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"aa5ac234-3406-403b-a55b-c8f2f682bf1e\">it is practically career suicide for young theoretical physicists not to join the field of string theory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>...'</span></p><p><span>The rising use of adjunct professors is mainly rooted in a need for cost efficiency in education, but it has more diffuse effects on the wellbeing of academic professionals and students, the quality of the education they receive, and academic freedom in general. Everyone who is concerned about more than the fiscal 'bottom line' needs to follow this trend carefully.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the correct number i-ix in boxes 14-19.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of Headings</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"i\"><span>i. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"aa5ac234-3406-403b-a55b-c8f2f682bf1e\">Uncertain future for academic freedom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ii\"><span>ii. Low pay causes problems</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iii\"><span>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"37d2947f-b0fb-4019-86e2-c147c3f0434d\">Tough life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"849c63f6-32c2-4ed8-b329-5a10e281df9b\">worse prospects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"iv\"><span>iv. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"f6de78b3-fd00-4423-b121-99f0d6503cb7\">A safety net for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a35161f5-7884-4567-b738-359e8786e06b\">intellectual risk-takers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"v\"><span>v. The necessity for economic reform</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vi\"><span>vi. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430\">Educational standards decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"vii\"><span>vii. Adverse effects on health of adjuncts</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"viii\"><span>viii. Academic life: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"a5823a7a-fc2c-4dda-a39c-a5ac4d26de78\">perception<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> versus <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"2ec072e5-a292-49fb-aeb9-194f9f7274cd\">reality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p><p data-pool-key=\"ix\"><span>ix. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"3f3dd770-e3a0-47b6-9a95-c71fe7e0bbf6\">Exploitation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"d0bd6f13-93a9-4913-b3ad-645bd3c265cb\">a stop-gap system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37991\" id=\"question-wrapper-37991\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section A</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37992\" id=\"question-wrapper-37992\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section B</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37993\" id=\"question-wrapper-37993\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section C</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IX</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37994\" id=\"question-wrapper-37994\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section D</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37995\" id=\"question-wrapper-37995\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section E</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37996\" id=\"question-wrapper-37996\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Section F</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 20-22.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37997\" id=\"question-wrapper-37997\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"0a18be23-fb81-4560-acd0-3ccbc386eb48\">the motivation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> behind the tenure system?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. To <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"74464db6-acdc-4441-a42e-d476290c144c\">allow professors to pursue their research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"be60ae89-780b-4aa0-ab0d-ab5b12b56124\">without outside influence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</li> <li>B. To prevent academic positions from being used for research that is not useful.</li> <li>C. To discipline professors who make claims that are not true.</li> <li>D. To provide professors with a secure income so that they can focus on research.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37998\" id=\"question-wrapper-37998\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which of the following is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"ace75586-057e-41e9-9d8e-b55b048f420c\">NOT a feature of adjunct employment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Contracts that expire after a limited period</li> <li>B. Paid sick leave</li> <li>C. Lecturing responsibilities</li> <li>D. Difficulty securing funding for research</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"37999\" id=\"question-wrapper-37999\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Why do adjuncts have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"c283dbc7-2a75-4c53-a225-8e431047d4e1\">low prospects for improving their academic position<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They are unable to receive medical care.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"fcfac14a-8bbc-410d-be44-15d01652bef1\">They do not have enough time for writing articles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</li> <li>C. They work at more than one institution.</li> <li>D. They are under-qualified.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the sentences below with words taken from Reading Passage 2.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Use </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 23-26.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38000\" id=\"question-wrapper-38000\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Because adjuncts are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"d5a824f4-b20d-46e8-8513-f9afb400e46b\">paid only to teach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"542e95fe-3e57-426f-8171-47a021a353c6\">cannot always provide support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> for (23)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(STRUGGLING) STUDENTS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38001\" id=\"question-wrapper-38001\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"7861665e-018e-41de-9d84-2f4766ea3bc1\">Adjuncts do not have the same bonds with one particular institution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"b85d7b89-1f7c-4f75-a419-c891b12b8596\">permanent staff<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> do so they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"e5c40966-514b-43ca-9607-22d3e61e39b5\">do not<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> (24)_____ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"4348c877-bb05-45e3-994b-84ab87af4dde\">in the same way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ACCUMULATE REPUTATIONS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38002\" id=\"question-wrapper-38002\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"10333e19-3142-4bbc-b138-698ccf593287\">Giving better marks than warranted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> enhances adjuncts (25)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">JOB SECURITY</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38003\" id=\"question-wrapper-38003\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Adjuncts do not deliver quality education, not because they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"bc7d7b66-ccb2-4680-a571-c0bd353d1501\">bad lecturers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> but as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"3e170e67-b7fe-491d-bd09-08414a60ded3\">a result of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STRUCTURAL PRESSURES</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a5823a7a-fc2c-4dda-a39c-a5ac4d26de78","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"perception","passagePhrase":"thought of as an occupation with immense job security ... The traditional image is one of a middle-aged professor with his own office, his own car park, and a cosy job with a middle-class salary that remains unaffected by upturns and downturns in the 'real' business economy"},{"uid":"2ec072e5-a292-49fb-aeb9-194f9f7274cd","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"reality","passagePhrase":"only a minority of professors have anything resembling this lifestyle ... the actual conditions of their employment are very different ... scrape by with low pay, short-term contracts and few or no employee benefits ... Many even qualify for food stamps"},{"uid":"f6de78b3-fd00-4423-b121-99f0d6503cb7","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"A safety net for","passagePhrase":"Tenure"},{"uid":"0a18be23-fb81-4560-acd0-3ccbc386eb48","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the motivation","passagePhrase":"The purpose"},{"uid":"74464db6-acdc-4441-a42e-d476290c144c f6de78b3-fd00-4423-b121-99f0d6503cb7","qNum":"15 20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"provide shelter for ... keep intellectual pursuits 'pure"},{"uid":"74464db6-acdc-4441-a42e-d476290c144c","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"allow professors to pursue their research","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"74464db6-acdc-4441-a42e-d476290c144c a35161f5-7884-4567-b738-359e8786e06b","qNum":"15 20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"researchers"},{"uid":"a35161f5-7884-4567-b738-359e8786e06b","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"intellectual risk-takers","passagePhrase":"who dissent from dominant opinions, disagree with the authorities of universities, donors or political authorities ... choose to research topics that may have social importance but seem unimportant or unnecessary to others"},{"uid":"0a18be23-fb81-4560-acd0-3ccbc386eb48 f6de78b3-fd00-4423-b121-99f0d6503cb7","qNum":"15 20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"seeks to"},{"uid":"be60ae89-780b-4aa0-ab0d-ab5b12b56124","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"without outside influence","passagePhrase":"rather than at the whim of external interests"},{"uid":"d0bd6f13-93a9-4913-b3ad-645bd3c265cb","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"a stop-gap system","passagePhrase":"professor adjuncts ... temporary, part-time employees ... teach individual classes and have no research or administrative responsibilities, and their contracts typically run for a single semester"},{"uid":"3f3dd770-e3a0-47b6-9a95-c71fe7e0bbf6","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Exploitation","passagePhrase":"their use has been extended beyond these temporary exigencies ... become a permanent, institutionalised aspect of academic employment"},{"uid":"ace75586-057e-41e9-9d8e-b55b048f420c","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"NOT a feature of adjunct employment","passagePhrase":"adjuncts"},{"uid":"37d2947f-b0fb-4019-86e2-c147c3f0434d ace75586-057e-41e9-9d8e-b55b048f420c","qNum":"17 21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"rarely qualify for insurance and health benefits, such as time off with remuneration for illness"},{"uid":"37d2947f-b0fb-4019-86e2-c147c3f0434d","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Tough life","passagePhrase":"recompense for adjuncts is often very low ... typically need to win contracts with multiple universities"},{"uid":"fcfac14a-8bbc-410d-be44-15d01652bef1","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"They do not have enough time for writing articles","passagePhrase":"high teaching workload"},{"uid":"849c63f6-32c2-4ed8-b329-5a10e281df9b fcfac14a-8bbc-410d-be44-15d01652bef1","qNum":"17 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"find it hard to publish articles"},{"uid":"849c63f6-32c2-4ed8-b329-5a10e281df9b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"worse prospects","passagePhrase":"and win research grants ... a 'publish or perish"},{"uid":"849c63f6-32c2-4ed8-b329-5a10e281df9b c283dbc7-2a75-4c53-a225-8e431047d4e1","qNum":"17 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"making promotion increasingly unlikely"},{"uid":"c283dbc7-2a75-4c53-a225-8e431047d4e1","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"low prospects for improving their academic position","passagePhrase":"with every year that passes"},{"uid":"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Educational standards decline","passagePhrase":"flow-on effects for the quality of teaching ... accumulate reputations over time ... not as personally invested in the quality and outcome of their teaching ... many adjuncts practice ... — ... —in order to maintain their job security by keeping students pleased"},{"uid":"d5a824f4-b20d-46e8-8513-f9afb400e46b","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"paid only to teach","passagePhrase":"come in only for classes"},{"uid":"542e95fe-3e57-426f-8171-47a021a353c6","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"cannot always provide support","passagePhrase":"do not have the time to meet up with students in small groups or for one-on-one sessions"},{"uid":"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430 542e95fe-3e57-426f-8171-47a021a353c6","qNum":"18 23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"make it difficult for struggling students to find guidance outside of lectures"},{"uid":"7861665e-018e-41de-9d84-2f4766ea3bc1","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Adjuncts do not have the same bonds with one particular institution","passagePhrase":"Adjuncts are also less 'tied' to the universities they teach at"},{"uid":"4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430 e5c40966-514b-43ca-9607-22d3e61e39b5","qNum":"18 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fail to"},{"uid":"4348c877-bb05-45e3-994b-84ab87af4dde","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"in the same way","passagePhrase":"in the same way"},{"uid":"b85d7b89-1f7c-4f75-a419-c891b12b8596","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"permanent staff","passagePhrase":"full-time professors"},{"uid":"10333e19-3142-4bbc-b138-698ccf593287 4289378e-8aab-4be0-9b11-d575779dc430","qNum":"18 25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"grade inflation ... raising grades higher than deserved"},{"uid":"bc7d7b66-ccb2-4680-a571-c0bd353d1501","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"bad lecturers","passagePhrase":"malfeasant or incompetent professors"},{"uid":"3e170e67-b7fe-491d-bd09-08414a60ded3","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"a result of","passagePhrase":"because of"},{"uid":"aa5ac234-3406-403b-a55b-c8f2f682bf1e","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Uncertain future for academic freedom","passagePhrase":"implications for the research and pedagogical autonomy of teachers ... intellectual conformity can grow as candidates position themselves as safe, mainstream choices ... it is practically career suicide for young theoretical physicists not to join the field of string theory"},{"uid":"e5c40966-514b-43ca-9607-22d3e61e39b5","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"do not","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"10333e19-3142-4bbc-b138-698ccf593287","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"Giving better marks than warranted","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_147":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>Good Parenting</span></b></p><p><span>—</span><i><b><span>it's up for discussion</span></b></i><span>—</span></p><p><span>Raising a baby may, at first, appear to be a highly personal, intimate affair between child and caregiver. In fact, there are often very public battles over every facet of child care, however: Breastfeeding or bottle-feeding? Breastfeeding in public? Toilet training—when and how? Nothing escapes judgment or scrutiny. Restlessness and crying at bedtimes are no different, and three different schools of thought have emerged around how parents should respond to this problem. These have been called extinction, attachment parenting and graduated extinction.</span></p><p><span>Attachment parenting, a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"e7a751e7-73bd-4374-8830-6b5e38bfea0e\">term<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"335a8e66-16b7-4e0f-8b0e-83cde93aecd8\">coined by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> paediatrician William Sears, suggests that children form powerful emotional bonds with caregivers during early childhood that have implications for their development through life. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"fe6cc426-cdef-49f2-bda0-04ebe3cbf0fb\">The basis for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> this theory was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"89d3d472-7dd2-4f91-ab25-bc915d6a7b06\">generated within the field of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> developmental psychology during the 1950s, when researcher John Bowlby proposed that maternal deprivation during infancy could decrease a person's ability to form healthy adult relationships years later. Attachment parenting seeks to avoid this tendency by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"d89528dc-ea55-4b97-b5ae-0a210eb47feb\">placing great importance on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"235d5991-e8a8-4bbc-8a22-e23fbff5de9c\">childhood bonding through the caregiver's holding and cuddling her baby when he is upset<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Attachment parenting also suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"19289ffb-2d46-4bb2-b509-9a3a28514c7a\">babies' ability to communicate their requirements is limited to crying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, and that parents need to learn to understand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"19289ffb-2d46-4bb2-b509-9a3a28514c7a\">what different types of crying signal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"19289ffb-2d46-4bb2-b509-9a3a28514c7a\">No crying is considered superfluous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>—even if the baby merely wants to be comforted rather than fall asleep—caregivers are encouraged to affirm these desires.</span></p><p><span>The extinction method proposes that, so long as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"42cb64e1-658a-4ca6-8314-9f2ddd6dfd5e\">a baby has had adequate calorie intake<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> during the day, he or she can reasonably be expected to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7058184b-4776-414c-a8f5-54ed72175d3c\">maintain nocturnal somnolence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"c33086a4-e2a1-443f-9818-2112a32ca40e\">core postulates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"baf1d185-3976-49e2-a01d-da9b0d075d2b\">approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"549ab56f-6b26-4c4b-a442-3988d6912dee\">laid down by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> Emmett Holt but they have been extrapolated upon by authors such as Warwick Reilly and further adapted recently by Melinda Collins to form the extinction method of today. Caregivers are encouraged to develop <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"9b83f744-1703-49eb-a836-41ed2334041a\">a gentle evening routine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> that involves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"9b83f744-1703-49eb-a836-41ed2334041a\">feeding 45 minutes before bed, bathing, dressing and laying the baby in his sleeping sack, walking out and closing the door<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4d4649a-3d1d-4cfc-9183-b9286716fdff\">remaining out of the child's presence until dawn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> even if he cries for extensive periods of time. It is expected that sooner or later children will realise that crying is ineffective, and that they must learn to comfort themselves into a slumber.</span></p><p><span>Graduated extinction is a modulated version of the extinction method. It postulates that a process of learning needs to be undertaken in order for children to sleep through the night. Richard Ferber, the doctor who popularised this method in the 1980s, emphasised <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"f5a216f6-0a9a-4a43-9aad-5b3ef2496e21\">the progressive withdrawal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"c3cb333a-a568-4740-ad3d-dd356f455a61\">the caregiver's company with the child in bed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> as a way to solve infant sleep problems. At first, for example, the caregiver is encouraged to hold and caress the baby until he or she is asleep. Once this routine is established, the caregiver should lie down next to the baby but touch it less and less until the baby can sleep without contact. Eventually the caregiver can sit on a chair nearby, and finally it is hoped that he or she can retreat from the room altogether. The key to this approach is that the caregiver must never capitulate to a child's demands for comfort if he starts to become restless or vocal as the method unfolds over time. Doing so is said to let the baby know that he does not need to learn to sleep through the night without comfort or interaction, and also to lessen the chances that the caregiver will complete the programme, knowing that a 'quick fix' is available. Ferber <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"f7b3d799-2d4f-4644-9574-aec94b91a387\">has since altered his stance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"6031a480-71f6-4786-a576-228a02795cbb\">acknowledge the acceptability of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> co-sleeping and suggests that there is no single method or golden rule for overcoming sleep difficulties.</span></p><p><span>Each of these systems has its critics. Attachment parenting, for example, is often held accused of being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"159eef58-4cf6-4ab4-91bd-38fb6c3403ab\">exceedingly strenuous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> and demanding for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"519a3cfa-2d2d-4bcd-8f92-b91a983fdfb9\">caregivers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> because they must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"bfb5c353-94fb-4bc7-bc6a-d0bc923e5288\">be at the beck and call of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> their baby's every demand. In doing so it is likely to create tensions between partners who are raising a child together, and between caregivers and their friends or co-workers, none of which is helpful for the overall development of the household. Critics also point out <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5417c823-2c72-4ef7-babb-0a97a035b586\">the absence of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> conclusive research <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"c984e4c7-b480-42b7-90e0-41553fe6590e\">behind the efficacy of attachment parenting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Many disapprove of the extinction method because, while it may allow <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"fd661d54-6547-4aa2-b611-b231f1ce60d6\">a quiet night's sleep<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> for baby and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"629a29d7-cafe-4141-8fb0-4fcb52fd966f\">caregiver and anyone else in the household<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, it is not because the baby has become settled and comfortable but rather for the reason that he has become detached and apathetic. This, it is suggested, can lead to various emotional problems in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"51e654de-e0cd-40e2-8956-7b4814231dc6\">early adulthood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> among which might be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"146e8053-74d0-4d7f-bbac-d7a528c77e2b\">depression and insecurity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"90a61418-f25e-4c5a-ba08-3a971f719d78\">At the mid-point on the spectrum<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> is graduated extinction, which has, therefore, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"4fa829d1-bfa1-498d-8369-5291db6e062b\">dodged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> any vociferous attacks. Advocates of attachment argue that there is no need to teach babies to live without soothing affirmation, however, and advocates of extinction suggest that it is better to use a method of going cold turkey—that is, to withdraw soothing affirmation swiftly rather than as a drawn out process.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the sentences below with words taken from Reading Passage 3.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Use </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 27-30.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38004\" id=\"question-wrapper-38004\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"e7a751e7-73bd-4374-8830-6b5e38bfea0e\">phrase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> attachment parenting was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"335a8e66-16b7-4e0f-8b0e-83cde93aecd8\">invented by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> a (27)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">P(A)EDIATRICIAN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38005\" id=\"question-wrapper-38005\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"fe6cc426-cdef-49f2-bda0-04ebe3cbf0fb\">The principles of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> attachment parenting are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"89d3d472-7dd2-4f91-ab25-bc915d6a7b06\">derived from the discipline of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> (28)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DEVELOPMENTAL PSYCHOLOGY</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38006\" id=\"question-wrapper-38006\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"c33086a4-e2a1-443f-9818-2112a32ca40e\">key points<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of the \"extinction\" <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"baf1d185-3976-49e2-a01d-da9b0d075d2b\">school of thought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"549ab56f-6b26-4c4b-a442-3988d6912dee\">originated from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the work of (29)_____.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(EMMETT) HOLT</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38007\" id=\"question-wrapper-38007\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Dr Ferber initially thought the parent should not spend the night with the child but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"f7b3d799-2d4f-4644-9574-aec94b91a387\">now thinks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> (30)_____ is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"6031a480-71f6-4786-a576-228a02795cbb\">all right<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CO-SLEEPING</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 31-35) and the methods in the box below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Match each statement with the correct parenting method A-C.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write the appropriate letter A-C in boxes 31-35.</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NB</span></b></i><i><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p><p><b><span>List of Parenting Methods</span></b></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. attachment parenting</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. extinction</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. graduated extinction</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38008\" id=\"question-wrapper-38008\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>After <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"9b83f744-1703-49eb-a836-41ed2334041a\">a strict bedtime schedule<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, the child is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"d4d4649a-3d1d-4cfc-9183-b9286716fdff\">unattended till morning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38009\" id=\"question-wrapper-38009\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"19289ffb-2d46-4bb2-b509-9a3a28514c7a\">All crying is a vocalisation of important needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38010\" id=\"question-wrapper-38010\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"c3cb333a-a568-4740-ad3d-dd356f455a61\">Caregiver presence as the child drifts to sleep<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"f5a216f6-0a9a-4a43-9aad-5b3ef2496e21\">decrease over time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38011\" id=\"question-wrapper-38011\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"d89528dc-ea55-4b97-b5ae-0a210eb47feb\">The emphasis is on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"235d5991-e8a8-4bbc-8a22-e23fbff5de9c\">physical closeness between baby and caregiver at any time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38012\" id=\"question-wrapper-38012\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"42cb64e1-658a-4ca6-8314-9f2ddd6dfd5e\">Well-fed babies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"7058184b-4776-414c-a8f5-54ed72175d3c\">sleep through the night<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the notes below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 36-40.</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>Critique:</span></b></i></p><p><u><span>Attachment Parenting</span></u></p><p><span>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"159eef58-4cf6-4ab4-91bd-38fb6c3403ab\">very stressful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"519a3cfa-2d2d-4bcd-8f92-b91a983fdfb9\">parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> have to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"bfb5c353-94fb-4bc7-bc6a-d0bc923e5288\">give in to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> (36)_____ of the baby but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"5417c823-2c72-4ef7-babb-0a97a035b586\">not yet any<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> (37)_____ to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"c984e4c7-b480-42b7-90e0-41553fe6590e\">show that it works<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></span></p><p><u><span>Extinction Method</span></u></p><p><span>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"fd661d54-6547-4aa2-b611-b231f1ce60d6\">a good night's sleep<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> is attained by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"629a29d7-cafe-4141-8fb0-4fcb52fd966f\">family members<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> because baby is (38)_____ and _____, but can lead to (39)_____ such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"146e8053-74d0-4d7f-bbac-d7a528c77e2b\">despair &amp; unhappiness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"51e654de-e0cd-40e2-8956-7b4814231dc6\">later in life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p><p><u><span>Graduated Extinction</span></u></p><p><span>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"90a61418-f25e-4c5a-ba08-3a971f719d78\">a central position<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> so (40)_____ have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"4fa829d1-bfa1-498d-8369-5291db6e062b\">avoided<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38013\" id=\"question-wrapper-38013\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EVERY DEMAND</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38014\" id=\"question-wrapper-38014\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CONCLUSIVE RESEARCH</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38015\" id=\"question-wrapper-38015\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DETACHED + APATHETIC</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38016\" id=\"question-wrapper-38016\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EMOTIONAL PROBLEMS</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38017\" id=\"question-wrapper-38017\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VOCIFEROUS ATTACKS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e7a751e7-73bd-4374-8830-6b5e38bfea0e","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"phrase","passagePhrase":"term"},{"uid":"335a8e66-16b7-4e0f-8b0e-83cde93aecd8","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"invented by","passagePhrase":"coined by"},{"uid":"fe6cc426-cdef-49f2-bda0-04ebe3cbf0fb","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The principles of","passagePhrase":"The basis for"},{"uid":"89d3d472-7dd2-4f91-ab25-bc915d6a7b06","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"derived from the discipline of","passagePhrase":"generated within the field of"},{"uid":"d89528dc-ea55-4b97-b5ae-0a210eb47feb","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"The emphasis is on","passagePhrase":"placing great importance on"},{"uid":"235d5991-e8a8-4bbc-8a22-e23fbff5de9c","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"physical closeness between baby and caregiver at any time","passagePhrase":"childhood bonding through the caregiver's holding and cuddling her baby when he is upset"},{"uid":"19289ffb-2d46-4bb2-b509-9a3a28514c7a","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"All crying is a vocalisation of important needs","passagePhrase":"babies' ability to communicate their requirements is limited to crying ... what different types of crying signal ... No crying is considered superfluous"},{"uid":"42cb64e1-658a-4ca6-8314-9f2ddd6dfd5e","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Well-fed babies","passagePhrase":"a baby has had adequate calorie intake"},{"uid":"7058184b-4776-414c-a8f5-54ed72175d3c","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"sleep through the night","passagePhrase":"maintain nocturnal somnolence"},{"uid":"c33086a4-e2a1-443f-9818-2112a32ca40e","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"key points","passagePhrase":"core postulates"},{"uid":"baf1d185-3976-49e2-a01d-da9b0d075d2b","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"school of thought","passagePhrase":"approach"},{"uid":"549ab56f-6b26-4c4b-a442-3988d6912dee","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"originated from","passagePhrase":"laid down by"},{"uid":"9b83f744-1703-49eb-a836-41ed2334041a","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"a strict bedtime schedule","passagePhrase":"a gentle evening routine ... feeding 45 minutes before bed, bathing, dressing and laying the baby in his sleeping sack, walking out and closing the door"},{"uid":"d4d4649a-3d1d-4cfc-9183-b9286716fdff","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"unattended till morning","passagePhrase":"remaining out of the child's presence until dawn"},{"uid":"f5a216f6-0a9a-4a43-9aad-5b3ef2496e21","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"decrease over time","passagePhrase":"the progressive withdrawal"},{"uid":"c3cb333a-a568-4740-ad3d-dd356f455a61","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Caregiver presence as the child drifts to sleep","passagePhrase":"the caregiver's company with the child in bed"},{"uid":"f7b3d799-2d4f-4644-9574-aec94b91a387","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"now thinks","passagePhrase":"has since altered his stance"},{"uid":"6031a480-71f6-4786-a576-228a02795cbb","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"all right","passagePhrase":"acknowledge the acceptability of"},{"uid":"159eef58-4cf6-4ab4-91bd-38fb6c3403ab","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"very stressful","passagePhrase":"exceedingly strenuous"},{"uid":"519a3cfa-2d2d-4bcd-8f92-b91a983fdfb9","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"parents","passagePhrase":"caregivers"},{"uid":"bfb5c353-94fb-4bc7-bc6a-d0bc923e5288","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"give in to","passagePhrase":"be at the beck and call of"},{"uid":"5417c823-2c72-4ef7-babb-0a97a035b586","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"not yet any","passagePhrase":"the absence of"},{"uid":"c984e4c7-b480-42b7-90e0-41553fe6590e","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"show that it works","passagePhrase":"behind the efficacy of attachment parenting"},{"uid":"fd661d54-6547-4aa2-b611-b231f1ce60d6","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"a good night's sleep","passagePhrase":"a quiet night's sleep"},{"uid":"629a29d7-cafe-4141-8fb0-4fcb52fd966f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"family members","passagePhrase":"caregiver and anyone else in the household"},{"uid":"51e654de-e0cd-40e2-8956-7b4814231dc6","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"later in life","passagePhrase":"early adulthood"},{"uid":"146e8053-74d0-4d7f-bbac-d7a528c77e2b","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"despair & unhappiness","passagePhrase":"depression and insecurity"},{"uid":"90a61418-f25e-4c5a-ba08-3a971f719d78","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"a central position","passagePhrase":"At the mid-point on the spectrum"},{"uid":"4fa829d1-bfa1-498d-8369-5291db6e062b","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"avoided","passagePhrase":"dodged"}]},"reading_u2_148":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><i><b><span>The Sun—A Mixed Blessing</span></b></i></p><p><span>A. People in Western countries have very mixed feelings about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"342b56f7-5c25-4e20-8242-fb9095956ea3\">the sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. On the one hand it evokes memories of beaches, summer holidays and playful times. Children's books often personify the sun as a smiling, happy face—typically contrasted with angry, moody rain clouds. In fact, the sun has such <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c543c720-ba22-4fea-97ca-f65aca8793fe\">positive connotations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> that the descriptor '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c543c720-ba22-4fea-97ca-f65aca8793fe\">sunny<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>' refers not only to a state of weather but also to '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c543c720-ba22-4fea-97ca-f65aca8793fe\">cheery, cheerful, or joyous' moods and dispositions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> amongst humans. On the other hand, many people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c543c720-ba22-4fea-97ca-f65aca8793fe\">fear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> the sun because of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c543c720-ba22-4fea-97ca-f65aca8793fe\">its association with cosmetic degeneration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> that can cause people to look much older than they actually are. Even more seriously, many people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c543c720-ba22-4fea-97ca-f65aca8793fe\">see the sun as a killer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>—this is because excessive sun exposure can lead to skin cancer which has a very high mortality rate. So is the sun our friend or a foe? The answers are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c543c720-ba22-4fea-97ca-f65aca8793fe\">complex and contradictory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>B. Let's start with the worst news about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e4bcd74a-420e-4e7f-a3fe-85e0c921e5c7\">the sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. It is a carcinogen. As the National Toxicology Program Report on Carcinogens from the Department of Health and Human Services reports, broad-spectrum UV radiation and solar radiation (what is known as 'sun rays') are thought to contribute to most of the estimated 1.5 million skin cancers diagnosed in the United States each year. This gives the sun the unfavourable distinction of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e4bcd74a-420e-4e7f-a3fe-85e0c921e5c7\">being the leading carcinogen in the United States—ahead of genetic mutations, bad diets, cigarettes, alcohol, chemical exposure and other lifestyle factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. Of these diagnoses, 8,000 sufferers will perish from the condition. The primary cause of this mortality is metastic melanoma—moles that become cancerous and then spread mutated cells into the lymph nodes and eventually through the rest of the body.</span></p><p><span>C. Even if you are lucky enough to avoid skin cancer, the sun can still have damaging effects on your skin. This is known as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"17a11484-f66b-40aa-8a04-617809543d33\">premature aging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, so-called because sun damage mimics the skin's natural aging process, but does so at a much earlier age. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12\">The sun causes premature aging by </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 7\" data-uid=\"141ea0d7-f654-4a90-872b-2dd58ef8f978 1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12\">breaking down and mutating collagen</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>—a fibrous, 'glue'-like substance that supports and connects tissue and is responsible for the firmness, suppleness, elasticity and overall appearance of the skin. Skin's collagen production slows and eventually stops due to aging anyway, but sun exposure accelerates this process. It also mutates collagen cells, producing visible abnormalities on the skin. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12\">The slowing collagen production appears as wrinkles, sagging and fine lines, while the mutated cells can take the form of </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 7\" data-uid=\"1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12 a471dde8-8848-4484-90e1-85a4c0218be9\">a leathery skin texture</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12\">, </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1 7\" data-uid=\"1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12 8ddf97c8-026d-478d-bbd8-4cf7944f11ea\">facial ruddiness</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12\"> and blemishes known as liver spots</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. Together these can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"17a11484-f66b-40aa-8a04-617809543d33\">dissolve signs of youth and vitality from a person's looks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>—an image that contrasts starkly with the smooth, tanned and youthful-looking models we often associate with summer!</span></p><p><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"5939dff9-c02a-411c-b4b3-6ec9759f35f1\">The sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> does have a lot of positive things to offer humans, however. Firstly, it <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"3 8\" data-uid=\"5939dff9-c02a-411c-b4b3-6ec9759f35f1 e97eb211-c0df-4daf-a8f4-2f54e268f6d5\">staves off</span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"5939dff9-c02a-411c-b4b3-6ec9759f35f1\"> </span><span class=\"paraitem antonym synonym\" data-question=\"3 8\" data-uid=\"1501da77-be96-4ca6-ae62-f967e0dde460 5939dff9-c02a-411c-b4b3-6ec9759f35f1\">Seasonal Affective Disorder</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> (SAD), an appropriate acronym for a mood disorder caused by insufficient exposure to light—as such, it is typically associated with winters and is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"1501da77-be96-4ca6-ae62-f967e0dde460\">sometimes called 'winter blues' or 'winter depression<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>'. SAD, once treated with scepticism by health experts but <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"24f1f199-276a-4c89-b6c1-0aa8a680c0ce\">now widely acknowledged to be a legitimate condition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, can create a number of distressing problems. Sufferers may oversleep and find it difficult to be roused in the morning, crave 'comfort foods' high in carbohydrates, lack energy, find it difficult to concentrate and may withdraw from social exposure. Together these symptoms can lead to depression, pessimistic feelings of hopelessness and an inability to find pleasurable activities. Researchers are not yet sure of the exact physical mechanism that causes SAD, but they do know that exposure to bright life is an effective remedy. The sun definitely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e97eb211-c0df-4daf-a8f4-2f54e268f6d5\">has a palliative effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> here.</span></p><p><span>E. In other ways, the health-improving effects of the sun can be even more powerful. These effects typically relate to Vitamin D, of which the sun is a great source for two reasons. Firstly, it is completely free, and secondly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3fb4faca-7739-4db5-9e24-52aa5ace9397\">our bodies have natural mechanisms that prevent an overdose from internally-generated Vitamin D from the sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Although this vitamin can be sourced from milk, cod liver oil and supplements, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"00f1bc96-424d-463d-aa90-0d2d01fd0402\">solar radiation is still the primary source for most humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. It's preventative role is important: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"3355f2aa-e5f8-4bfc-9cc2-d962884a2063\">Vitamin D seems to protect against prostate, breast, colon, kidney and ovarian cancers, benefit bone health<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, as well as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"3355f2aa-e5f8-4bfc-9cc2-d962884a2063\">reduce overall mortality and the occurrence of cardiovascular events<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>—mortality from strokes and heart attacks is up to forty percent higher in some countries during winter months, a connection linked to lack of sun exposure. In fact, skin cancer rates rise with proximity to the equator amongst light-skinned people, but the prognosis of most other cancers is exactly the opposite. Indeed, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"99483d1f-62de-461d-9697-36f1a4d83e2c\">overall benefits of sun exposure outweigh the risks when it comes to cancer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, even though the sun is a well-documented carcinogen.</span></p><p><span>F. Ultimately, moderation and protection may be the key when it comes to sun exposure. This is true of other carcinogens such as alcohol as well—studies suggest that binge drinkers and teetotallers experience higher levels of many health problems than people who drink moderate amounts of alcohol on social occasions. Healthy access to the sun involves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"5dc41d91-e50c-4ff5-9752-2d55d1bfd87f\">wearing broad-spectrum sunscreen before every exposure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> (even in winter)and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"5dc41d91-e50c-4ff5-9752-2d55d1bfd87f\">not staying in the sun any longer than is necessary, which is about five minutes for adequate Vitamin D exposure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. With these simple steps, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"9f4ddca6-5aee-453b-b454-675cff4c7a78\">the sun once again becomes our friend and not our foe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has six paragraphs, A-F.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-6.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38059\" id=\"question-wrapper-38059\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A description of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12\">physical process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"17a11484-f66b-40aa-8a04-617809543d33\">makes someone look older<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38060\" id=\"question-wrapper-38060\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"5dc41d91-e50c-4ff5-9752-2d55d1bfd87f\">Recommendations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> for how to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"9f4ddca6-5aee-453b-b454-675cff4c7a78\">be safe in the sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38061\" id=\"question-wrapper-38061\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"1501da77-be96-4ca6-ae62-f967e0dde460\">Examples of emotional ailments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> that contact with the sun can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e97eb211-c0df-4daf-a8f4-2f54e268f6d5\">treat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38062\" id=\"question-wrapper-38062\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Evidence that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"3355f2aa-e5f8-4bfc-9cc2-d962884a2063\">sun can lower death rates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38063\" id=\"question-wrapper-38063\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>An explanation of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"342b56f7-5c25-4e20-8242-fb9095956ea3\">a single word<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> can have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"c543c720-ba22-4fea-97ca-f65aca8793fe\">contrasting connotations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38064\" id=\"question-wrapper-38064\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"e4bcd74a-420e-4e7f-a3fe-85e0c921e5c7\">Several causes of cancer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answer in box 7.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38065\" id=\"question-wrapper-38065\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which of the following is NOT given as a symptom of premature aging?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"141ea0d7-f654-4a90-872b-2dd58ef8f978\">Loose skin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></li> <li>B. Organ problems</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"8ddf97c8-026d-478d-bbd8-4cf7944f11ea\">Redness on face<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a471dde8-8848-4484-90e1-85a4c0218be9\">Rough, dry feel to skin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><i><span>In boxes 8-13, write</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>TRUE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement agrees with the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>FALSE</span></b></i><i><span> if the statement contradicts the information</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NOT GIVEN</span></b></i><i><span> if there is no information on this</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38066\" id=\"question-wrapper-38066\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"5939dff9-c02a-411c-b4b3-6ec9759f35f1\">Sun exposure can result in SAD<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38067\" id=\"question-wrapper-38067\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Experts <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"24f1f199-276a-4c89-b6c1-0aa8a680c0ce\">no longer consider SAD to be a health problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38068\" id=\"question-wrapper-38068\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Artificial sources of light are not very good at treating SAD.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38069\" id=\"question-wrapper-38069\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3fb4faca-7739-4db5-9e24-52aa5ace9397\">The sun cannot give us too much Vitamin D<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38070\" id=\"question-wrapper-38070\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"00f1bc96-424d-463d-aa90-0d2d01fd0402\">Most people get their Vitamin D from the sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38071\" id=\"question-wrapper-38071\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>The sun can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"99483d1f-62de-461d-9697-36f1a4d83e2c\">both cause and prevent cancer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"342b56f7-5c25-4e20-8242-fb9095956ea3","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"a single word","passagePhrase":"the sun"},{"uid":"c543c720-ba22-4fea-97ca-f65aca8793fe","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"contrasting connotations","passagePhrase":"positive connotations ... sunny ... cheery, cheerful, or joyous' moods and dispositions ... fear ... its association with cosmetic degeneration ... see the sun as a killer ... complex and contradictory"},{"uid":"e4bcd74a-420e-4e7f-a3fe-85e0c921e5c7","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Several causes of cancer","passagePhrase":"the sun ... being the leading carcinogen in the United States—ahead of genetic mutations, bad diets, cigarettes, alcohol, chemical exposure and other lifestyle factors"},{"uid":"17a11484-f66b-40aa-8a04-617809543d33","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"makes someone look older","passagePhrase":"premature aging ... dissolve signs of youth and vitality from a person's looks"},{"uid":"1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"physical process","passagePhrase":"The sun causes premature aging by ... The slowing collagen production appears as wrinkles, sagging and fine lines, while the mutated cells can take the form of ... , ... and blemishes known as liver spots"},{"uid":"141ea0d7-f654-4a90-872b-2dd58ef8f978 1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12","qNum":"1 7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"breaking down and mutating collagen"},{"uid":"1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12 a471dde8-8848-4484-90e1-85a4c0218be9","qNum":"1 7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a leathery skin texture"},{"uid":"1613e5b7-4581-44d5-8f21-f841c5adce12 8ddf97c8-026d-478d-bbd8-4cf7944f11ea","qNum":"1 7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"facial ruddiness"},{"uid":"5939dff9-c02a-411c-b4b3-6ec9759f35f1 e97eb211-c0df-4daf-a8f4-2f54e268f6d5","qNum":"3 8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"staves off"},{"uid":"1501da77-be96-4ca6-ae62-f967e0dde460 5939dff9-c02a-411c-b4b3-6ec9759f35f1","qNum":"3 8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Seasonal Affective Disorder"},{"uid":"1501da77-be96-4ca6-ae62-f967e0dde460","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Examples of emotional ailments","passagePhrase":"sometimes called 'winter blues' or 'winter depression"},{"uid":"e97eb211-c0df-4daf-a8f4-2f54e268f6d5","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"treat","passagePhrase":"has a palliative effect"},{"uid":"3fb4faca-7739-4db5-9e24-52aa5ace9397","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"The sun cannot give us too much Vitamin D","passagePhrase":"our bodies have natural mechanisms that prevent an overdose from internally-generated Vitamin D from the sun"},{"uid":"00f1bc96-424d-463d-aa90-0d2d01fd0402","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Most people get their Vitamin D from the sun","passagePhrase":"solar radiation is still the primary source for most humans"},{"uid":"3355f2aa-e5f8-4bfc-9cc2-d962884a2063","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"sun can lower death rates","passagePhrase":"Vitamin D seems to protect against prostate, breast, colon, kidney and ovarian cancers, benefit bone health ... reduce overall mortality and the occurrence of cardiovascular events"},{"uid":"99483d1f-62de-461d-9697-36f1a4d83e2c","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"both cause and prevent cancer","passagePhrase":"overall benefits of sun exposure outweigh the risks when it comes to cancer"},{"uid":"5dc41d91-e50c-4ff5-9752-2d55d1bfd87f","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Recommendations","passagePhrase":"wearing broad-spectrum sunscreen before every exposure ... not staying in the sun any longer than is necessary, which is about five minutes for adequate Vitamin D exposure"},{"uid":"9f4ddca6-5aee-453b-b454-675cff4c7a78","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"be safe in the sun","passagePhrase":"the sun once again becomes our friend and not our foe"},{"uid":"141ea0d7-f654-4a90-872b-2dd58ef8f978","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Loose skin","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"8ddf97c8-026d-478d-bbd8-4cf7944f11ea","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Redness on face","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"a471dde8-8848-4484-90e1-85a4c0218be9","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Rough, dry feel to skin","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_149":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>A New Planet Is Discovered</span></b></p><p><span>[</span><i><span>Humans have long been fascinated by the possibility of extra-terrestrial fife. Novels, films and folk-tales have encouraged curiosity and speculation about what might be 'out there' in space. More recently, scientists have joined in on the collective wonderment after the first discovery by astronomers of a new planet—Gliese 581g—that could almost certainly support such organisms. In fact, Steven Vogt—one of the two astronomers credited with discovering the planet—has declared that ' the chances of life on this planet are 100 percent' and that he has 'almost no doubt about it'.</span></i><span> ]</span></p><p><span>A. Although we currently know very little about Gliese 581g, a couple of its features strongly indicate that this planet might harbour the existence of organisms. Firstly, Gliese 581g is located at almost exactly the right distance from its red dwarf parent star (Gliese 581) in order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"e5d3d81a-2234-4b8a-ade5-2325f3bac1f9\">sustain liquid water, which is the only known criterion for organic formation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Planets that orbit too close to or too far away from their stars do not have a suitable climate; this can only be found in a slender strip of solar space around each star known to astronomers as a 'habitable zone'. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"7370577a-8408-4136-9422-9b8fae3ad322\">Around our star—the Sun—Earth is the only planet that occupies this zone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, although it nearly stretches to Venus and Mars. Gliese 581g is also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"e5d3d81a-2234-4b8a-ade5-2325f3bac1f9\">the right size for organic life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. It is about 3.1 to 4.3 times the size of Earth, and this relatively low mass means it should be made mostly of rock. Planets that grow beyond 10 times the size of Earth tend to become gaseous and uninhabitable, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"e5d3d81a-2234-4b8a-ade5-2325f3bac1f9\">without the solid or liquid infrastructure necessary for organisms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"67ba797e-ecaa-4bdd-a319-4e6e6474226a\">Gliese 581g is part of a string of planets in the Gliese 581 solar system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Two of Gliese 581g's siblings—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"a2bc868c-0334-4f14-a39d-e927a48ed113\">Gliese 581e and Gliese 581b—orbit too close to their parent star to support any kind of life on them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 21\" data-uid=\"67ba797e-ecaa-4bdd-a319-4e6e6474226a 7838d202-fefd-4bbf-80bd-6f17cb89e76d\">Gliese 581c skims the near side of the habitable zone</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, but scientists suggest that it does not have enough of a toehold in this zone to provide a stable infrastructure for organic formations—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"8c98f6e2-3ee2-4678-ab5f-78431c0ccbf9\">roughly the same goes for Gliese 581d, which has a stronger presence in the habitable zone on its far side<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, but may not be hot enough for liquid water—opinion is not 'completely settled' on this matter, says James Kasting of Pennsylvania State University. Kasting, who has studied the two Gliese 581 planets on the outer edges of the habitable zone, suggests that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17 22\" data-uid=\"67ba797e-ecaa-4bdd-a319-4e6e6474226a c13b6f27-a81c-4f17-871f-d0027f9c5b07\">Gliese581g is 'smack dab in the middle' of the zone</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> which, along with its size and composition, makes it the most exciting and realistic prospect for extra-terrestrial life yet.</span></p><p><span>C. The comparisons between the Earth and Gliese 581g should not be overstated, however. Even if Gliese 581g can sustain organisms, it would be a very different place to live. The main difference is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"d0f0a0fe-f857-4a7d-a20b-a48ea3184eb5\">Gliese 581g orbits much closer to its star<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> than the Earth does to the Sun. Because Gliese 581 is only one percent as bright as the Sun, it exudes little warmth, and its habitable zone lies much closer than the Sun's. At this closer distance, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"d0f0a0fe-f857-4a7d-a20b-a48ea3184eb5\">planets in the zone get locked into strong gravitational pulls that tend to </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 24\" data-uid=\"7d8a517b-4f1a-42b9-9477-104a151cf400 d0f0a0fe-f857-4a7d-a20b-a48ea3184eb5\">slow their circular movements over time</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"d0f0a0fe-f857-4a7d-a20b-a48ea3184eb5\">Eventually, they become </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16 24\" data-uid=\"7d8a517b-4f1a-42b9-9477-104a151cf400 d0f0a0fe-f857-4a7d-a20b-a48ea3184eb5\">stuck with one side constantly facing the star</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>—<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"c8ea50ff-4c11-412c-81dc-c16f28c1d6d0\">just as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the Moon always shows the Earth the same face. Because of this, it is likely that Gliese 581g experiences permanent daytime on the side facing the star and permanent shadow on the other side. It is estimated therefore that average temperatures on the star side would be about 71 degrees C and average temperatures on the other much chillier: -34℃. Nevertheless, Steven Vogt suggests that Gliese 581g probably has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ecd20de7-8a5d-4c76-b002-45f3afbf0cae\">a comfortable area along the midpoint<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, known as the terminator. Any life here would always see the star sitting on the horizon and consequently experience <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"98320a2e-b650-4c67-8134-306e6018c8a3\">eternal sunrise or sunset<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>D. Even if there is no life on Gliese 581g, its discovery reveals that habitable planets are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"2c8125a2-36f6-4263-8469-f27fc7d59962\">quite common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, with around 10 to 20 percent of red dwarves and sun-like stars boasting them. Gliese 581 is one of just nine stars at that particular distance which astronomers have searched with high enough precision to uncover a planet in the habitable zone. While the odds may prove to be slightly lower than 10 percent, the evidence of life—or at least, the high possibility of life—is still overwhelming. There are at least a few hundred billion stars in our galaxy, which means that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a4262595-8f6a-4d46-8cc1-936d9c8bd7ae\">around 20 to 40 billion planets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"0f45c7bd-b7f9-4d01-af32-755dbd13367e\">have the potential for the development of organisms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>E. And so, the search for life continues. Unfortunately, Gliese 581g is not particularly amenable to observation. The next step in finding out the chances of life on the planet would be to measure its light spectrum, a process that would reveal molecular oxygen if indeed it exists. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"006b9750-eb0d-4650-9887-0b7c402c4a79\">The glare from the parent star makes this impossible to do with current instruments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, however. Another way to gather information would be to transport a vessel to and from the planet. The technology currently exists to do this, but at 20 light years from earth, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"006b9750-eb0d-4650-9887-0b7c402c4a79\">it would take 200 years for astronomers to receive the result<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. Luckily, new information may just be a few years away. Astronomers suggest that many rocky planets are likely to be found in habitable zones during the coming years, and some of these will provide a better platform for research with current instruments.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has five paragraphs, A-E.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 14-18.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38072\" id=\"question-wrapper-38072\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A reason <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"006b9750-eb0d-4650-9887-0b7c402c4a79\">why we cannot learn much more about Gliese 581g in the near future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38073\" id=\"question-wrapper-38073\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"a4262595-8f6a-4d46-8cc1-936d9c8bd7ae\">An estimate of the number of planets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"0f45c7bd-b7f9-4d01-af32-755dbd13367e\">in habitable zones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38074\" id=\"question-wrapper-38074\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>An explanation for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"d0f0a0fe-f857-4a7d-a20b-a48ea3184eb5\">why Gliese 581g may not rotate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38075\" id=\"question-wrapper-38075\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"67ba797e-ecaa-4bdd-a319-4e6e6474226a\">Gliese 581g's location in relation to other planets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38076\" id=\"question-wrapper-38076\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"e5d3d81a-2234-4b8a-ade5-2325f3bac1f9\">pre-requisite for the beginning of life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Complete the diagram below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct letter A-E from the box below.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 19-23.</span></i></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Gliese 581c</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. Gliese 581d</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Gliese 581e</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. Gliese 581g</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Earth</span></p><p><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://s4-media1.study4.com/media/IELTS_Simulation/reading/images/3c0c284b29903baa1e6c384d766551103c433c29bc2ca38e257dbf8a96251908.jpg\" title=\"\"></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38077\" id=\"question-wrapper-38077\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38078\" id=\"question-wrapper-38078\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38079\" id=\"question-wrapper-38079\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38080\" id=\"question-wrapper-38080\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38081\" id=\"question-wrapper-38081\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Answer the questions below using </span></i><i><b><span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span></b></i><i><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 24-26.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38082\" id=\"question-wrapper-38082\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>To what can Gliese 581g be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"c8ea50ff-4c11-412c-81dc-c16f28c1d6d0\">compared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> because of its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"7d8a517b-4f1a-42b9-9477-104a151cf400\">lack of circular motion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(THE) MOON</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38083\" id=\"question-wrapper-38083\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What is the name for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"ecd20de7-8a5d-4c76-b002-45f3afbf0cae\">the central meridian<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> on Gliese 581g where there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"25\" data-uid=\"98320a2e-b650-4c67-8134-306e6018c8a3\">no darkness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(THE) TERMINATOR</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38084\" id=\"question-wrapper-38084\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>What do astronomers now realise are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"2c8125a2-36f6-4263-8469-f27fc7d59962\">not rare occurrences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HABITABLE PLANETS</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e5d3d81a-2234-4b8a-ade5-2325f3bac1f9","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"pre-requisite for the beginning of life","passagePhrase":"sustain liquid water, which is the only known criterion for organic formation ... the right size for organic life ... without the solid or liquid infrastructure necessary for organisms"},{"uid":"7370577a-8408-4136-9422-9b8fae3ad322","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Around our star—the Sun—Earth is the only planet that occupies this zone"},{"uid":"67ba797e-ecaa-4bdd-a319-4e6e6474226a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Gliese 581g's location in relation to other planets","passagePhrase":"Gliese 581g is part of a string of planets in the Gliese 581 solar system"},{"uid":"a2bc868c-0334-4f14-a39d-e927a48ed113","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Gliese 581e and Gliese 581b—orbit too close to their parent star to support any kind of life on them"},{"uid":"67ba797e-ecaa-4bdd-a319-4e6e6474226a 7838d202-fefd-4bbf-80bd-6f17cb89e76d","qNum":"17 21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Gliese 581c skims the near side of the habitable zone"},{"uid":"8c98f6e2-3ee2-4678-ab5f-78431c0ccbf9","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"roughly the same goes for Gliese 581d, which has a stronger presence in the habitable zone on its far side"},{"uid":"67ba797e-ecaa-4bdd-a319-4e6e6474226a c13b6f27-a81c-4f17-871f-d0027f9c5b07","qNum":"17 22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Gliese581g is 'smack dab in the middle' of the zone"},{"uid":"d0f0a0fe-f857-4a7d-a20b-a48ea3184eb5","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"why Gliese 581g may not rotate","passagePhrase":"Gliese 581g orbits much closer to its star ... planets in the zone get locked into strong gravitational pulls that tend to ... Eventually, they become"},{"uid":"7d8a517b-4f1a-42b9-9477-104a151cf400 d0f0a0fe-f857-4a7d-a20b-a48ea3184eb5","qNum":"16 24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"slow their circular movements over time ... stuck with one side constantly facing the star"},{"uid":"c8ea50ff-4c11-412c-81dc-c16f28c1d6d0","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"compared","passagePhrase":"just as"},{"uid":"ecd20de7-8a5d-4c76-b002-45f3afbf0cae","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"the central meridian","passagePhrase":"a comfortable area along the midpoint"},{"uid":"98320a2e-b650-4c67-8134-306e6018c8a3","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"no darkness","passagePhrase":"eternal sunrise or sunset"},{"uid":"2c8125a2-36f6-4263-8469-f27fc7d59962","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"not rare occurrences","passagePhrase":"quite common"},{"uid":"a4262595-8f6a-4d46-8cc1-936d9c8bd7ae","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"An estimate of the number of planets","passagePhrase":"around 20 to 40 billion planets"},{"uid":"0f45c7bd-b7f9-4d01-af32-755dbd13367e","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"in habitable zones","passagePhrase":"have the potential for the development of organisms"},{"uid":"006b9750-eb0d-4650-9887-0b7c402c4a79","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"why we cannot learn much more about Gliese 581g in the near future","passagePhrase":"The glare from the parent star makes this impossible to do with current instruments ... it would take 200 years for astronomers to receive the result"},{"uid":"7d8a517b-4f1a-42b9-9477-104a151cf400","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"lack of circular motion","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_150":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><b><span>READING WARS</span></b></p><p><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"31015a4d-744e-45f5-b76e-4fea2196f703\">In many developed countries literacy skills are under siege<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. This is true even in societies where access to primary education is universal and governments invest heavily in education. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"31015a4d-744e-45f5-b76e-4fea2196f703\">New Zealand, for example, was leading the world in literacy rates in 1970, but tumbled to thirteenth place in 2001 and then again to twenty-fourth just a few years later<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. Test scores in the USA also slumped ten percent during the 1990s despite the country riding an economic boom for much of the decade. In some cases these statistics reverse trends that were in motion for over a century and a haft. The steady, gradual expansion of literacy across social groups and classes was one of the greatest successes of the period of industrialisation that began in the mid-1850s.</span></p><p><span>B. This reversal of fortunes has lead to widespread contention over the pedagogy of teaching literacy. What was once a dry and technical affair—the esoteric business of linguists and policy analysts—rapidly escalated into a series of skirmishes that were played out in high-visibility forums: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"9ae3cfc2-dcbb-4621-a5a4-3617f317a540\">Newspapers ran special features, columns and letters-to-the-editor on the literacy crisis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"4434626f-0910-41fc-81dc-5444356fb248\">politicians successfully ran their national campaigns on improving reading test scores<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"db30636d-9ef2-4afb-a445-995a6222242b\">and parents had their say by joining Parent Teacher Associations (PTAs) and lobby groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>C. The arguments around reading pooled into two different classroom methodologies: constructivism and behaviourism. The constructivist methodology grew from a holistic conception of knowledge creation that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34 35 36\" data-uid=\"2ff18e56-4402-4b86-9565-2b1e3a9f21b0 8b9ab57b-db55-4f55-8bad-7437c52970bf eee74c15-04ec-4fec-957d-d30f0abf54f8\">understood reading and writing to be innate</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, humanistic and interpretative practices that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34 35 36\" data-uid=\"4b5002d1-a05d-440b-b277-9e28ee5e4d1d 69b25644-a1be-4bde-a40f-fef12fcd34d5 6b4e1a9d-a429-4489-b549-78eb1254924e\">suffered when they were spliced and formalised within rigid doctrines, strict rules and universal skill-sets</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Constructivists associate words with meanings; each word might be thought of as a Chinese ideogram. Students are encouraged to learn individual words and skip over and guess words they do not understand, or <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34 35 36\" data-uid=\"0a212b44-bbe9-4488-bb96-4ba589d7b2dd 727bd406-4c4e-4844-a2a6-a4e9287ce3bf 7c7254ea-50e3-4464-b467-b5832a8da18b\">learn to interpret those words by situating them within the lexical infrastructure of the sentence and the story's wider narrative</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. These practices materialise as learning processes centred on guided group reading and independent reading of high-quality, culturally diverse literature or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"42290969-e6b6-439e-8edb-1d2a7f8a924b\">textual composition that emphasises pupils conveying their own thoughts and feelings for real purposes such as letters to pen pals or journal entries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>D. Behaviourism sees the pedagogical process in a less dialectical fashion—<span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37 38 39\" data-uid=\"0048dd5d-5e0b-4adb-afc9-01855eda52a6 3ea111d8-fe33-4f46-8a0d-a2a016e780e9 4e766b70-9c95-4991-8206-d4071d1db7ef\">words are initially taught not lexically</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, as vehicles to convey meaning, <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37 38 39\" data-uid=\"0048dd5d-5e0b-4adb-afc9-01855eda52a6 3ea111d8-fe33-4f46-8a0d-a2a016e780e9 4e766b70-9c95-4991-8206-d4071d1db7ef\">but rather sub-lexically, as a combination of features that can be separated and learnt in a schematic process</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. The behaviourist approach does not focus on words at all in the early stages of learning. Rather, it is centred on a universally applicable method of <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37 38 39\" data-uid=\"30987104-7eb4-4cd2-8e24-67f5de547820 65a6b5e0-c460-4228-bf1d-ce059a39c953 b7038d95-ff69-41fd-b64c-5c9fcd3bab92\">teaching students to isolate graphemes and phonemes</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> with the intention that <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37 38 39\" data-uid=\"30987104-7eb4-4cd2-8e24-67f5de547820 65a6b5e0-c460-4228-bf1d-ce059a39c953 b7038d95-ff69-41fd-b64c-5c9fcd3bab92\">students will eventually learn to synthesise these individual parts and make sense of spoken words textually</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. In this way, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"703401d0-855c-48ee-8a76-244539aed259\">individual components<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> are not equated with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"6182674a-5342-4693-81a4-5b0524d560e9\">the strokes of a brush on a Chinese ideogram<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, but rather as the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"703401d0-855c-48ee-8a76-244539aed259\">focal pieces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of interpretation—as in, for example, learning to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"6182674a-5342-4693-81a4-5b0524d560e9\">read musical notations or Morse Code<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Because of its emphasis on universal rules, behaviourism is much more conducive to formal examination and the consolidation of results across regions and countries. The ability to master language is considered to rest in the acquisition of a set of skills that exist independently of individuals. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37 38 39\" data-uid=\"40eb8366-6f13-416b-b90a-12ebd9a44fec 9be83679-0fa0-4009-bc93-3c4a72969490 cb330a67-deb9-4790-8429-fa6f1a9067df\">Classroom learning is therefore based upon the transmission of knowledge from tutor to student</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, rather than seen as an internalised process that erupts within the students themselves.</span></p><p><span>E. So who comes out on top? It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ac4cd74e-3e08-44ae-a65d-7d8c1e3ae0c0\">not easy to say<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Champions of behaviourism have claimed victory because constructivist learning took over in the late 1980s, just before test scores on literacy began sinking across the West. Constructivists, however, can make the valid claim that the behaviourist approach has a heavy methodological bias towards testing and examination, and that test results do not represent the ability of individuals to use and interpret language freely and creatively. Furthermore, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ac4cd74e-3e08-44ae-a65d-7d8c1e3ae0c0\">different socio-economic groups respond in different ways to each method<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c502b65f-7c95-4165-ac9b-ce7f46cabb2d\">Those from wealthier families<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> tend to do well regardless of the method, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c502b65f-7c95-4165-ac9b-ce7f46cabb2d\">thrive on the constructivist approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> implemented in the 1990s. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c502b65f-7c95-4165-ac9b-ce7f46cabb2d\">Children from poorer families, however, are better served by behaviourism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. These outcomes have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c502b65f-7c95-4165-ac9b-ce7f46cabb2d\">ramped up levels of socio-economic based educational disparities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in educational systems that have pushed the constructivist method.</span></p><p><span>F. It is unlikely that either constructivism or behaviourism will be permanently sidelined from curricula in the near future. Most teachers find it easier to incorporate aspects of each approach. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30 40\" data-uid=\"6d7114a7-a837-4bb9-a0ed-007855d36657 9c3834d9-9fdb-4ca5-af29-97f29589c9ad\">Constructivism may ultimately hold the trump card</span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"6d7114a7-a837-4bb9-a0ed-007855d36657\"> because of its proven success with pupils who come from families where they are introduced to reading and writing in various forms from a young age</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>—this process of 'living and learning' and immersing oneself in language is a sound principle. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8166b379-2f27-4327-84f3-dc447ff45691\">In a world rife with social inequities, </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30 40\" data-uid=\"6d7114a7-a837-4bb9-a0ed-007855d36657 8166b379-2f27-4327-84f3-dc447ff45691\">households with illiterate parents and a scarcity of funding for education, however, the behaviourist approach may have the upper hand</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> in teaching children to access the basic skills of literacy quickly and efficiently, even if some linguistic creativity is crushed in the process.</span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has six paragraphs, A-F.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><i><span>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 27-33.</span></i></p><p><i><b><span>NB</span></b></i><i><span> You may use any letter more than once.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38085\" id=\"question-wrapper-38085\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A reason <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"c502b65f-7c95-4165-ac9b-ce7f46cabb2d\">why constructivism might increase inequalities in society<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38086\" id=\"question-wrapper-38086\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"28\" data-uid=\"9ae3cfc2-dcbb-4621-a5a4-3617f317a540\">Ways in which people debated the merits of different ways of teaching reading<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38087\" id=\"question-wrapper-38087\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"6182674a-5342-4693-81a4-5b0524d560e9\">comparison between forms of communication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that build meaning from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"703401d0-855c-48ee-8a76-244539aed259\">isolated parts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38088\" id=\"question-wrapper-38088\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Reasons why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"6d7114a7-a837-4bb9-a0ed-007855d36657\">a method that is theoretically superior might not always work effectively in practice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38089\" id=\"question-wrapper-38089\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>An explanation of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"ac4cd74e-3e08-44ae-a65d-7d8c1e3ae0c0\">why measuring the success of different reading methods is difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38090\" id=\"question-wrapper-38090\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"42290969-e6b6-439e-8edb-1d2a7f8a924b\">An example of an activity that teachers might use to develop writing skills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38091\" id=\"question-wrapper-38091\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Evidence of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"31015a4d-744e-45f5-b76e-4fea2196f703\">a national decline in reading standards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>THREE</span></b></i><i><span> letters, A-G.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 34-36.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>THREE</span></b><span> of the following are features of constructivism?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. Students learn best by working on their own.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. People are <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34 35 36\" data-uid=\"2ff18e56-4402-4b86-9565-2b1e3a9f21b0 8b9ab57b-db55-4f55-8bad-7437c52970bf eee74c15-04ec-4fec-957d-d30f0abf54f8\">naturally inclined to develop language abilities</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. It is vital that a disciplined and regulated approach is used.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. It is important that students understand every word they encounter.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Language is <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34 35 36\" data-uid=\"4b5002d1-a05d-440b-b277-9e28ee5e4d1d 69b25644-a1be-4bde-a40f-fef12fcd34d5 6b4e1a9d-a429-4489-b549-78eb1254924e\">best learnt as a single, organic process</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. Everyone learns to read and write in a similar manner.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34 35 36\" data-uid=\"0a212b44-bbe9-4488-bb96-4ba589d7b2dd 727bd406-4c4e-4844-a2a6-a4e9287ce3bf 7c7254ea-50e3-4464-b467-b5832a8da18b\">Context can provide helpful cues to understanding words</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38092\" id=\"question-wrapper-38092\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E/G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38093\" id=\"question-wrapper-38093\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E/G</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38094\" id=\"question-wrapper-38094\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E/G</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose </span></i><i><b><span>THREE</span></b></i><i><span> letters A-G.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answers in boxes 37-39.</span></i></p><p><span>Which </span><b><span>THREE</span></b><span> of the following are features of behaviourism?</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"A\"><span>A. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37 38 39\" data-uid=\"0048dd5d-5e0b-4adb-afc9-01855eda52a6 3ea111d8-fe33-4f46-8a0d-a2a016e780e9 4e766b70-9c95-4991-8206-d4071d1db7ef\">The whole of a word is less important than its parts</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"B\"><span>B. There is not a common set of conventions.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"C\"><span>C. Students learn best by working on their own.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"D\"><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37 38 39\" data-uid=\"30987104-7eb4-4cd2-8e24-67f5de547820 65a6b5e0-c460-4228-bf1d-ce059a39c953 b7038d95-ff69-41fd-b64c-5c9fcd3bab92\">Meaning is created by connecting word fragments</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"E\"><span>E. Linguistic capacities are built into people.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"F\"><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem-group\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37 38 39\" data-uid=\"40eb8366-6f13-416b-b90a-12ebd9a44fec 9be83679-0fa0-4009-bc93-3c4a72969490 cb330a67-deb9-4790-8429-fa6f1a9067df\">Students learn by receiving information from teachers</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p data-pool-key=\"G\"><span>G. It is difficult to judge how well students are doing collectively.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38095\" id=\"question-wrapper-38095\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38096\" id=\"question-wrapper-38096\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/D/F</div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38097\" id=\"question-wrapper-38097\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/D/F</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span></span></p><p><i><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></i></p><p><i><span>Write your answer in box 40.</span></i></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"38098\" id=\"question-wrapper-38098\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <p><span>Which of the following statements best summarises the writer's general conclusion?</span></p> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Constructivism is better, while behaviourism leads to negative social effects.</li> <li>B. Each method complements the other, and their application should be integrated.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"9c3834d9-9fdb-4ca5-af29-97f29589c9ad\">Ideally constructivism would be used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"8166b379-2f27-4327-84f3-dc447ff45691\">behaviourism is more pragmatic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Neither is particularly useful, and there needs to be a new alternative.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"31015a4d-744e-45f5-b76e-4fea2196f703","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"a national decline in reading standards","passagePhrase":"In many developed countries literacy skills are under siege ... New Zealand, for example, was leading the world in literacy rates in 1970, but tumbled to thirteenth place in 2001 and then again to twenty-fourth just a few years later"},{"uid":"9ae3cfc2-dcbb-4621-a5a4-3617f317a540","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Ways in which people debated the merits of different ways of teaching reading","passagePhrase":"Newspapers ran special features, columns and letters-to-the-editor on the literacy crisis"},{"uid":"4434626f-0910-41fc-81dc-5444356fb248","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"politicians successfully ran their national campaigns on improving reading test scores"},{"uid":"db30636d-9ef2-4afb-a445-995a6222242b","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"and parents had their say by joining Parent Teacher Associations (PTAs) and lobby groups"},{"uid":"2ff18e56-4402-4b86-9565-2b1e3a9f21b0 8b9ab57b-db55-4f55-8bad-7437c52970bf eee74c15-04ec-4fec-957d-d30f0abf54f8","qNum":"34 35 36","questionPhrase":"naturally inclined to develop language abilities","passagePhrase":"understood reading and writing to be innate"},{"uid":"4b5002d1-a05d-440b-b277-9e28ee5e4d1d 69b25644-a1be-4bde-a40f-fef12fcd34d5 6b4e1a9d-a429-4489-b549-78eb1254924e","qNum":"34 35 36","questionPhrase":"best learnt as a single, organic process","passagePhrase":"suffered when they were spliced and formalised within rigid doctrines, strict rules and universal skill-sets"},{"uid":"0a212b44-bbe9-4488-bb96-4ba589d7b2dd 727bd406-4c4e-4844-a2a6-a4e9287ce3bf 7c7254ea-50e3-4464-b467-b5832a8da18b","qNum":"34 35 36","questionPhrase":"Context can provide helpful cues to understanding words","passagePhrase":"learn to interpret those words by situating them within the lexical infrastructure of the sentence and the story's wider narrative"},{"uid":"42290969-e6b6-439e-8edb-1d2a7f8a924b","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"An example of an activity that teachers might use to develop writing skills","passagePhrase":"textual composition that emphasises pupils conveying their own thoughts and feelings for real purposes such as letters to pen pals or journal entries"},{"uid":"0048dd5d-5e0b-4adb-afc9-01855eda52a6 3ea111d8-fe33-4f46-8a0d-a2a016e780e9 4e766b70-9c95-4991-8206-d4071d1db7ef","qNum":"37 38 39","questionPhrase":"The whole of a word is less important than its parts","passagePhrase":"words are initially taught not lexically ... but rather sub-lexically, as a combination of features that can be separated and learnt in a schematic process"},{"uid":"30987104-7eb4-4cd2-8e24-67f5de547820 65a6b5e0-c460-4228-bf1d-ce059a39c953 b7038d95-ff69-41fd-b64c-5c9fcd3bab92","qNum":"37 38 39","questionPhrase":"Meaning is created by connecting word fragments","passagePhrase":"teaching students to isolate graphemes and phonemes ... students will eventually learn to synthesise these individual parts and make sense of spoken words textually"},{"uid":"703401d0-855c-48ee-8a76-244539aed259","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"isolated parts","passagePhrase":"individual components ... focal pieces"},{"uid":"6182674a-5342-4693-81a4-5b0524d560e9","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"comparison between forms of communication","passagePhrase":"the strokes of a brush on a Chinese ideogram ... read musical notations or Morse Code"},{"uid":"40eb8366-6f13-416b-b90a-12ebd9a44fec 9be83679-0fa0-4009-bc93-3c4a72969490 cb330a67-deb9-4790-8429-fa6f1a9067df","qNum":"37 38 39","questionPhrase":"Students learn by receiving information from teachers","passagePhrase":"Classroom learning is therefore based upon the transmission of knowledge from tutor to student"},{"uid":"ac4cd74e-3e08-44ae-a65d-7d8c1e3ae0c0","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"why measuring the success of different reading methods is difficult","passagePhrase":"not easy to say ... different socio-economic groups respond in different ways to each method"},{"uid":"c502b65f-7c95-4165-ac9b-ce7f46cabb2d","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"why constructivism might increase inequalities in society","passagePhrase":"Those from wealthier families ... thrive on the constructivist approach ... Children from poorer families, however, are better served by behaviourism ... ramped up levels of socio-economic based educational disparities"},{"uid":"6d7114a7-a837-4bb9-a0ed-007855d36657 9c3834d9-9fdb-4ca5-af29-97f29589c9ad","qNum":"30 40","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Constructivism may ultimately hold the trump card"},{"uid":"6d7114a7-a837-4bb9-a0ed-007855d36657","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"a method that is theoretically superior might not always work effectively in practice","passagePhrase":"because of its proven success with pupils who come from families where they are introduced to reading and writing in various forms from a young age"},{"uid":"8166b379-2f27-4327-84f3-dc447ff45691","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"behaviourism is more pragmatic","passagePhrase":"In a world rife with social inequities,"},{"uid":"6d7114a7-a837-4bb9-a0ed-007855d36657 8166b379-2f27-4327-84f3-dc447ff45691","qNum":"30 40","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"households with illiterate parents and a scarcity of funding for education, however, the behaviourist approach may have the upper hand"},{"uid":"9c3834d9-9fdb-4ca5-af29-97f29589c9ad","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Ideally constructivism would be used","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_151":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Let’s Go Bats</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong> </p><p>Bats have a problem: how to find their way around in the dark. They hunt at night, and cannot use light to help them find prey and avoid obstacles. You might say that this is a problem of their own making, one that they could avoid simply by changing their habits and hunting by day. But the daytime economy is already heavily exploited by other creatures such as birds. Given that there is a living to be made at night, and given that alternative daytime trades are thoroughly occupied, natural selection has favoured bats that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13d1d70e-8614-40c2-9a90-202642a4d837\" data-question=\"3\">make a go of the night-hunting trade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. It is probable that the nocturnal trades go way back in the ancestry of all mammals. In the time when the dinosaurs dominated the daytime economy, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac295e6d-c2bb-4771-beba-182fb43d48a2\" data-question=\"2\">our mammalian ancestors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> probably only managed to survive at all because they found ways of scraping a living at night. Only after the mysterious mass extinction of the dinosaurs about 65 million years ago were our ancestors able to emerge into the daylight in any substantial numbers.</p><p><strong>B</strong> </p><p>Bats have an engineering problem: how to find their way and find their prey in the absence of light. Bats are not the only creatures to face this difficulty today. Obviously the night-flying insects that they prey on must find their way about somehow. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0f1092c3-e04e-4db2-9253-274e72d23b09\" data-question=\"1\">Deep-sea fish and whales<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> have little or no light by day or by night. Fish and dolphins that live in extremely muddy water cannot see because, although there is light, it is obstructed and scattered by the dirt in the water. Plenty of other modern animals make their living in conditions where seeing is difficult or impossible.</p><p><strong>C</strong> </p><p>Given the questions of how to manoeuvre in the dark, what solutions might an engineer consider? The first one that might occur to him is to manufacture light, to use a lantern or a searchlight. Fireflies and some fish (usually with the help of bacteria) have the power to manufacture their own light, but the process seems to consume a large amount of energy. Fireflies use their light for attracting mates. This doesn’t require a prohibitive amount of energy: a male’s tiny pinprick of light can be seen by a female from some distance on a dark night, since her eyes are exposed directly to the light source itself. However using light to find one’s own way around requires vastly more energy, since the eyes have to detect the tiny fraction of the light that bounces off each part of the scene. The light source must therefore be immensely brighter if it is to be used as a headlight to illuminate the path, than if it is to be used as a signal to others. In any event, whether or not the reason is the energy expense, it seems to be the case that, with the possible exception of some weird deep-sea fish, no animal apart from man uses manufactured light to find its way about.</p><p><strong>D</strong> </p><p>What else might the engineer think of? Well, blind humans sometimes seem to have an uncanny sense of obstacles in their path. It has been given the name ‘facial vision’, because blind people have reported that it feels a bit like the sense of touch, on the face. One report tells of a totally blind boy who could ride his tricycle at good speed round the block near his home, using facial vision. Experiments showed that, in fact, facial vision is nothing to do with touch or the front of the face, although the sensation may be referred to the front of the face, like the referred pain in a phantom <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b8e221ba-4d5e-441d-9326-699392c9f926\" data-question=\"6\">limb<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. The sensation of facial vision, it turns out, really goes in through the ears. Blind people, without even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56c59e59-5f38-431f-8683-653d86901df5\" data-question=\"7\">being aware<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> of the fact, are actually using echoes of their own footsteps and of other sounds, to sense the presence of obstacles. Before this was discovered, engineers had already built instruments to exploit the principle, for example to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"00e35df6-c714-4577-85f4-55f8e72970bd\" data-question=\"8\">measure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> the depth of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d08275ba-f700-4ab3-a221-fdcbc81e4ad4\" data-question=\"8\">sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> under a ship. After <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5816fe42-7697-4d5e-ba5c-21e3f709220a\" data-question=\"5\">this technique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> had been invented, it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d1710dac-f9a8-4511-8b42-07bb5d7e4fd1\" data-question=\"5\">only a matter of time before<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> weapons designers adapted it for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ed3c86fc-961f-4cfd-81f5-fea1f44713fc\" data-question=\"9\">detection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of submarines. Both sides in the Second World War relied heavily on these devices, under such codenames as Asdic (British) and Sonar (American), as well as Radar (American) or RDF (British), which uses radio echoes rather than sound echoes.</p><p><strong>E</strong> </p><p>The Sonar and Radar pioneers didn’t know it then, but all the world now knows that bats, or rather natural selection working on bats, had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa4adf41-1d14-46a9-b588-efe4bee03f60\" data-question=\"10\">perfected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> the system <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0320fd13-ecfb-4317-b142-1917dec79e76\" data-question=\"10\">tens of millions of years earlier<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, and their radar achieves feats of detection and navigation that would strike an engineer dumb with admiration. It is technically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93d45e34-4bda-4d5c-a115-f3f0d9c23cfa\" data-question=\"11\">incorrect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> to talk about bat ‘radar’, since they do not use radio waves. It is sonar but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67494482-33d5-4e9b-a792-3d6fc02823ca\" data-question=\"12\">the underlying mathematical theories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> of radar and sonar are very similar and much of our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ef0e68d3-626e-4484-8b77-54173f8682cb\" data-question=\"4\">scientific understanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of the details of what bats are doing has come from applying radar theory to them. The American zoologist Donald Griffin, who was largely responsible for the discovery of sonar in bats, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d81c1dc-c4ff-451b-80cd-b7a2296eab7b\" data-question=\"13\">coined the term<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> ‘echolocation’ to cover both sonar and radar, whether used by animals or by human instruments.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 1 has five paragraphs, A-E. Which paragraph contains the following information?<br>Write the correct letter. A-E, in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28599\" id=\"question-wrapper-28599\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0f1092c3-e04e-4db2-9253-274e72d23b09\" data-question=\"1\">wildlife other than bats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> which do not rely on vision to navigate by </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28600\" id=\"question-wrapper-28600\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> How <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac295e6d-c2bb-4771-beba-182fb43d48a2\" data-question=\"2\">early mammals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> avoided dying out </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28601\" id=\"question-wrapper-28601\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Why bats <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13d1d70e-8614-40c2-9a90-202642a4d837\" data-question=\"3\">hunt in the dark<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28602\" id=\"question-wrapper-28602\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> How a particular discovery has helped <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ef0e68d3-626e-4484-8b77-54173f8682cb\" data-question=\"4\">our understanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of bats </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28603\" id=\"question-wrapper-28603\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d1710dac-f9a8-4511-8b42-07bb5d7e4fd1\" data-question=\"5\">Early<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> military uses of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5816fe42-7697-4d5e-ba5c-21e3f709220a\" data-question=\"5\">echolocation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below. Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>Facial Vision</strong><br>Blind people report that so-called ‘facial vision’ is comparable to the sensation of touch on the face. In fact, the sensation is more similar to the way in which pain from a (6)……………………<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b8e221ba-4d5e-441d-9326-699392c9f926\" data-question=\"6\">arm or leg<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> might be felt. The ability actually comes from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56c59e59-5f38-431f-8683-653d86901df5\" data-question=\"7\">perceiving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> (7)………..…………..through the ears. However, even before this was understood, the principle had been applied in the design of instruments which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"00e35df6-c714-4577-85f4-55f8e72970bd\" data-question=\"8\">calculated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> the (8)……….…………..of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d08275ba-f700-4ab3-a221-fdcbc81e4ad4\" data-question=\"8\">seabed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. This was followed by a wartime application in devices for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ed3c86fc-961f-4cfd-81f5-fea1f44713fc\" data-question=\"9\">finding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9)………………</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28604\" id=\"question-wrapper-28604\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PHANTOM</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28605\" id=\"question-wrapper-28605\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ECHOES/OBSTACLES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28606\" id=\"question-wrapper-28606\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DEPTH</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28607\" id=\"question-wrapper-28607\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SUBMARINES</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the sentences below. Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28608\" id=\"question-wrapper-28608\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0320fd13-ecfb-4317-b142-1917dec79e76\" data-question=\"10\">Long before<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> the invention of radar,…………… had resulted in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa4adf41-1d14-46a9-b588-efe4bee03f60\" data-question=\"10\">sophisticated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> radar-like system in bats. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NATURAL SELECTION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28609\" id=\"question-wrapper-28609\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Radar is an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93d45e34-4bda-4d5c-a115-f3f0d9c23cfa\" data-question=\"11\">inaccurate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> term when referring to bats because………………are not used in their navigation system. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RADIO WAVES/ECHOES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28610\" id=\"question-wrapper-28610\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Radar and sonar are based on similar……………………. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MATHEMATICAL THEORIES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28611\" id=\"question-wrapper-28611\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The word ‘echolocation’ was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d81c1dc-c4ff-451b-80cd-b7a2296eab7b\" data-question=\"13\">first used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> by someone working as a…………………. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ZOOLOGIST</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"13d1d70e-8614-40c2-9a90-202642a4d837","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"hunt in the dark","passagePhrase":"make a go of the night-hunting trade"},{"uid":"ac295e6d-c2bb-4771-beba-182fb43d48a2","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"early mammals","passagePhrase":"our mammalian ancestors"},{"uid":"0f1092c3-e04e-4db2-9253-274e72d23b09","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"wildlife other than bats","passagePhrase":"Deep-sea fish and whales"},{"uid":"b8e221ba-4d5e-441d-9326-699392c9f926","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"arm or leg","passagePhrase":"limb"},{"uid":"56c59e59-5f38-431f-8683-653d86901df5","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"perceiving","passagePhrase":"being aware"},{"uid":"00e35df6-c714-4577-85f4-55f8e72970bd","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"calculated","passagePhrase":"measure"},{"uid":"d08275ba-f700-4ab3-a221-fdcbc81e4ad4","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"seabed","passagePhrase":"sea"},{"uid":"5816fe42-7697-4d5e-ba5c-21e3f709220a","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"echolocation","passagePhrase":"this technique"},{"uid":"d1710dac-f9a8-4511-8b42-07bb5d7e4fd1","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Early","passagePhrase":"only a matter of time before"},{"uid":"ed3c86fc-961f-4cfd-81f5-fea1f44713fc","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"finding","passagePhrase":"detection"},{"uid":"fa4adf41-1d14-46a9-b588-efe4bee03f60","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"sophisticated","passagePhrase":"perfected"},{"uid":"0320fd13-ecfb-4317-b142-1917dec79e76","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"Long before","passagePhrase":"tens of millions of years earlier"},{"uid":"93d45e34-4bda-4d5c-a115-f3f0d9c23cfa","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"inaccurate","passagePhrase":"incorrect"},{"uid":"67494482-33d5-4e9b-a792-3d6fc02823ca","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the underlying mathematical theories"},{"uid":"ef0e68d3-626e-4484-8b77-54173f8682cb","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"our understanding","passagePhrase":"scientific understanding"},{"uid":"9d81c1dc-c4ff-451b-80cd-b7a2296eab7b","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"first used","passagePhrase":"coined the term"}]},"reading_u2_152":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Making Every Drop Count</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong> </p><p>The history of human civilisation is entwined with the history of the ways we have learned to manipulate water resources. As towns gradually expanded, water was brought from increasingly remote sources, leading to sophisticated engineering efforts such as dams and aqueducts. At the height of the Roman Empire, nine major systems, with an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f2c3253-b2f0-4e7c-9c1d-cb8d58b3a731\" data-question=\"14\">innovative layout of pipes and well-built sewers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, supplied the occupants of Rome with <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"14a708bf-4b9a-430c-9675-985fa56defc7\" data-question=\"21\">as much water per person as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> is provided in many parts of the industrial world today.</p><p><strong>B</strong> </p><p>During the industrial revolution and population explosion of the 19th and 20th centuries, the demand for water rose dramatically. Unprecedented construction of tens of thousands of monumental engineering projects designed to control floods, protect clean water supplies, and provide water for irrigation and hydropower brought great benefits to hundreds of millions of people. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f1c00f6-1931-4787-a367-a4f5563b951b\" data-question=\"22\">Food production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> has kept pace with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dab7302c-cee9-458e-907e-71191fa6f244\" data-question=\"22\">soaring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> populations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d518abb9-73d2-480f-9f40-30a2ef43cbe9\" data-question=\"22\">mainly because of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the expansion of artificial irrigation systems that make possible the growth of 40 % of the world’s food. Nearly one fifth of all the electricity generated worldwide is produced by turbines spun by the power of falling water.</p><p><strong>C</strong> </p><p>Yet there is a dark side to this picture: despite our progress, half of the world’s population still suffers, with water services inferior to those available to the ancient Greeks and Romans. As the United Nations report on access to water reiterated in November 2001, more than one billion people lack access to clean drinking water; some two and a half billion do not have adequate sanitation services. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d017823f-155b-492d-91ac-ede2e398bff3\" data-question=\"15\">Preventable water-related diseases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> kill an estimated 10,000 to 20,000 children every day, and the latest evidence suggests that we are falling behind in efforts to solve these problems.</p><p><strong>D</strong> </p><p>The consequences of our water policies extend beyond jeopardising human health. Tens of millions of people have been forced to move from their homes – often with little warning or compensation – to make way for the reservoirs behind dams. More than 20 % of all freshwater fish species are now threatened or endangered because dams and water withdrawals have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c8d3a93-9ff2-4673-8a8f-9d232a0d17d1\" data-question=\"16\">destroyed the free-flowing river ecosystems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> where they thrive. Certain irrigation practices degrade soil quality and reduce agricultural productivity. Groundwater aquifers are being pumped down faster than they are naturally replenished in parts of India, China, the USA and elsewhere. And disputes over shared water resources have led to violence and continue to raise local, national and even international tensions.</p><p><strong>E</strong> </p><p>At the outset of the new millennium, however, the way resource planners think about water is beginning to change. The focus is slowly shifting back to the provision of basic human and environmental needs as top priority – ensuring ‘some for all,’ instead of ‘more for some’. Some water <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47b2b2a1-ebef-429f-ad05-4cc4fc6f7b63\" data-question=\"17\">experts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> are now demanding that existing infrastructure be used in smarter ways rather than building new facilities, which is increasingly considered the option of last, not first, resort. This shift in philosophy has not been universally accepted, and it comes with strong opposition from some established water organisations. Nevertheless, it may be the only way to address successfully the pressing problems of providing everyone with clean water to drink, adequate water to grow food and a life free from preventable water-related illness.</p><p><strong>F</strong> </p><p>Fortunately – and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a2304e3-3758-403d-8071-405db08a5abc\" data-question=\"18\">unexpectedly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> – the demand for water is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0e71987-8616-4bc9-b5e6-89d98e7bfbe9\" data-question=\"18\">not rising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> as rapidly as some predicted. As a result, the pressure to build new water infrastructures has diminished over the past two decades. Although population, industrial output and economic productivity have continued to soar in developed nations, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"72a2e1cc-12be-4ebd-929a-51e8708c5589\" data-question=\"24\">the rate at which people withdraw water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> from aquifers, rivers and lakes <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"72a2e1cc-12be-4ebd-929a-51e8708c5589\" data-question=\"24\">has slowed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. And in a few parts of the world, demand has actually fallen.</p><p><strong>G</strong> </p><p>What explains this remarkable turn of events? Two factors: people have figured out how to use water more efficiently, and communities are rethinking their priorities for water use. Throughout the first three-quarters of the 20th century, the quantity of freshwater consumed per person doubled on average; in the USA, water withdrawals increased tenfold while the population quadrupled. But since 1980, the amount of water consumed per person has actually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"532d0d1f-7f62-41b7-8259-016535d55c86\" data-question=\"25\">decreased<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, thanks to a range of new technologies that help to conserve water in homes and industry. In 1965, for instance, Japan used approximately 13 million gallons of water to produce $1 million of commercial output; by 1989 this had dropped to 3.5 million gallons (even accounting for inflation) – almost a quadrupling of water productivity. In the USA, water withdrawals have fallen by more than 20 % from their peak in 1980.</p><p><strong>H</strong> </p><p>On the other hand, dams, aqueducts and other kinds of infrastructure will still have to be built, particularly in developing countries where basic human needs have not been met. But such projects <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57356337-ffeb-4e44-8fdd-b5ab7c677261\" data-question=\"20\">must be built to higher specifications and with more accountability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to local people and their environment than in the past. And even in regions where new projects seem warranted, we must find ways to meet demands with fewer resources, respecting ecological criteria and to a smaller budget.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-H. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A and C-H from the list of headings below.</p><p>Write the correct number, i-xi, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>Example: Passage B </strong>-<strong> </strong>iii</p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><ul><li>i <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47b2b2a1-ebef-429f-ad05-4cc4fc6f7b63\" data-question=\"17\">Scientists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>’ call for revision of policy</li><li>ii An explanation for reduced water use</li><li>iii How a global challenge was met</li><li>iv Irrigation systems fall into disuse</li><li>v <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c8d3a93-9ff2-4673-8a8f-9d232a0d17d1\" data-question=\"16\">Environmental effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></li><li>vi The financial cost of recent technological improvements</li><li>vii The relevance to health</li><li>viii Addressing the concern over increasing populations</li><li>ix A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a2304e3-3758-403d-8071-405db08a5abc\" data-question=\"18\">surprising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0e71987-8616-4bc9-b5e6-89d98e7bfbe9\" data-question=\"18\">downward<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> trend in demand for water</li><li>x The need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57356337-ffeb-4e44-8fdd-b5ab7c677261\" data-question=\"20\">raise standards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></li><li>xi A description of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f2c3253-b2f0-4e7c-9c1d-cb8d58b3a731\" data-question=\"14\">ancient water supplies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28612\" id=\"question-wrapper-28612\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">XI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28613\" id=\"question-wrapper-28613\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28614\" id=\"question-wrapper-28614\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28615\" id=\"question-wrapper-28615\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28616\" id=\"question-wrapper-28616\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IX</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28617\" id=\"question-wrapper-28617\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28618\" id=\"question-wrapper-28618\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph H </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">X</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with information given in Reading Passage 2. In boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28619\" id=\"question-wrapper-28619\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Water use per person is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"14a708bf-4b9a-430c-9675-985fa56defc7\" data-question=\"21\">higher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in the industrial world than it was in Ancient Rome. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28620\" id=\"question-wrapper-28620\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f1c00f6-1931-4787-a367-a4f5563b951b\" data-question=\"22\">Feeding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> increasing populations is possible <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d518abb9-73d2-480f-9f40-30a2ef43cbe9\" data-question=\"22\">due primarily to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> improved irrigation systems. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28621\" id=\"question-wrapper-28621\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Modern water systems imitate those of the ancient Greeks and Romans. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28622\" id=\"question-wrapper-28622\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Industrial growth is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"72a2e1cc-12be-4ebd-929a-51e8708c5589\" data-question=\"24\">increasing the overall demand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> for water. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28623\" id=\"question-wrapper-28623\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Modern technologies have led to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"532d0d1f-7f62-41b7-8259-016535d55c86\" data-question=\"25\">reduction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> in the domestic water consumption. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28624\" id=\"question-wrapper-28624\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the future, governments should maintain ownership of water infrastructures. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7f2c3253-b2f0-4e7c-9c1d-cb8d58b3a731","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"ancient water supplies","passagePhrase":"innovative layout of pipes and well-built sewers"},{"uid":"5f1c00f6-1931-4787-a367-a4f5563b951b","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Feeding","passagePhrase":"Food production"},{"uid":"dab7302c-cee9-458e-907e-71191fa6f244","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"soaring"},{"uid":"d518abb9-73d2-480f-9f40-30a2ef43cbe9","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"due primarily to","passagePhrase":"mainly because of"},{"uid":"d017823f-155b-492d-91ac-ede2e398bff3","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Preventable water-related diseases"},{"uid":"5c8d3a93-9ff2-4673-8a8f-9d232a0d17d1","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Environmental effects","passagePhrase":"destroyed the free-flowing river ecosystems"},{"uid":"47b2b2a1-ebef-429f-ad05-4cc4fc6f7b63","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Scientists","passagePhrase":"experts"},{"uid":"8a2304e3-3758-403d-8071-405db08a5abc","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"surprising","passagePhrase":"unexpectedly"},{"uid":"b0e71987-8616-4bc9-b5e6-89d98e7bfbe9","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"downward","passagePhrase":"not rising"},{"uid":"532d0d1f-7f62-41b7-8259-016535d55c86","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"reduction","passagePhrase":"decreased"},{"uid":"57356337-ffeb-4e44-8fdd-b5ab7c677261","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"raise standards","passagePhrase":"must be built to higher specifications and with more accountability"}]},"reading_u2_153":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>EDUCATING PSYCHE</strong></p><p>Educating Psyche by Bernie Neville is a book which looks at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9316dda-4d0d-4185-bfd3-9a44bb2c0719\" data-question=\"27\">radical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> new approaches to learning, describing the effects of emotion, imagination and the unconscious on learning. One theory discussed in the book is that proposed by George Lozanov, which focuses on the power of suggestion.</p><p>Lozanov’s instructional technique is based on the evidence that the connections made in the brain through unconscious processing (which he calls non-specific mental reactivity) are more durable than those made through conscious processing. Besides the laboratory evidence for this, we know from our experience that we often remember what we have perceived peripherally, long after we have forgotten what we set out to learn. If <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4aaf276c-c68e-4acd-8b8a-f9300261f538\" data-question=\"29\">we think of a book<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> we studied months or years ago, we will find it easier to recall <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"082f008c-45ce-4af7-a8a3-41207fec52a1\" data-question=\"28\">peripheral details<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> – the colour, the binding, the typeface, the table at the library where we sat while studying it – than the content on which we were concentrating. If <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4aaf276c-c68e-4acd-8b8a-f9300261f538\" data-question=\"29\">we think of a lecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> we listened to with great concentration, we will recall the lecturer’s appearance and mannerisms, our place in the auditorium, the failure of the air-conditioning, much more easily than the ideas we went to learn. Even if these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"082f008c-45ce-4af7-a8a3-41207fec52a1\" data-question=\"28\">peripheral details<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> are a bit elusive, they come back readily in hypnosis or when we relive the event imaginatively, as in psychodrama. The details of the content of the lecture, on the other hand, seem to have gone forever.</p><p>This phenomenon can be partly attributed to the common counterproductive approach to study (making extreme efforts to memorise, tensing muscles, inducing fatigue), but it also simply reflects the way the brain functions. Lozanov therefore made <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db4b96b5-a98c-41a4-adc4-f61a9990c9c5\" data-question=\"30\">indirect instruction (suggestion) central to his teaching system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. In suggestopedia, as he called his method, consciousness is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"793e5a22-0bad-4629-8f50-6fcd2ce90278\" data-question=\"30\">shifted away from the curriculum to focus on something peripheral<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. The curriculum then becomes peripheral and is dealt with by the reserve capacity of the brain.</p><p>The suggestopedic approach to foreign language learning provides a good illustration. In its most recent variant (1980), it consists of the reading of vocabulary and text while the class is listening to music. The first session is in two parts. In the first part, the music is classical (Mozart, Beethoven, Brahms) and the teacher reads the text slowly and solemnly, with attention to the dynamics of the music. The students follow the text in their books. This is followed by several minutes of silence. In the second part, they listen to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b40fea5f-3e13-4632-a5ad-9219e0e3e806\" data-question=\"31\">baroque music<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> (Bach, Corelli, Handel) while the teacher reads the text in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b40fea5f-3e13-4632-a5ad-9219e0e3e806\" data-question=\"31\">normal speaking voice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. During this time they have their books closed. During the whole of this session, their attention is passive; they listen to the music but make no attempt to learn the material.</p><p>Beforehand, the students have been carefully prepared for the language learning experience. Through meeting with the staff and satisfied students they develop the expectation that learning will be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a4b0cd58-8d71-4856-a65e-9153fd8d9fdf\" data-question=\"32\">easy and pleasant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> and that they will successfully learn several hundred words of the foreign language during the class. In a preliminary talk, the teacher introduces them to the material to be covered, but does not ‘teach’ it. Likewise, the students are instructed not to try to learn it during this introduction.</p><p>Some hours after the two-part session, there is a follow-up class at which the students are stimulated to recall the material presented. Once again the approach is indirect. The students do not focus their attention on trying to remember the vocabulary, but focus on using the language to communicate (e.g. through games or improvised dramatisations). Such methods are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c5c600e-b60d-40ad-9a94-ec2be5a06146\" data-question=\"33\">not unusual in language teaching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. What is distinctive in the suggestopedic method is that they are devoted entirely to assist recall. The ‘learning’ of the material is assumed to be automatic and effortless, accomplished while listening to music. The teacher’s task is to assist the students to apply what they have learned paraconsciously, and in doing so to make it easily accessible to consciousness. Another difference from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"770e4ba9-9df1-42a7-a9eb-babaf6793c18\" data-question=\"36\">conventional teaching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> is the evidence that students can regularly learn 1000 new words of a foreign language during a suggestopedic session, as well as grammar and idiom.</p><p>Lozanov experimented with teaching by direct suggestion during sleep, hypnosis and trance states, but found such procedures unnecessary. Hypnosis, yoga, Silva mind-control, religious ceremonies and faith healing are all associated with successful suggestion, but none of their techniques seem to be essential to it. Such rituals may be seen as placebos. Lozanov <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5680d234-6418-4baa-a53d-45abf34f79c4\" data-question=\"38\">acknowledges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> that the ritual surrounding suggestion in his own system is also a placebo, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e60b5d04-d726-40f0-b181-664a7e477c83\" data-question=\"37\">maintains that without such<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> a placebo people are unable or afraid to tap the reserve capacity of their brains. Like any placebo, it must be dispensed with authority to be effective. Just as a doctor calls on the full power of autocratic suggestion by insisting that the patient take precisely this white capsule precisely three times a day before meals, Lozanov is categoric in insisting that the suggestopedic session be conducted exactly in the manner designated, by trained and accredited suggestopedic teachers.</p><p>While suggestopedia has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e3297c6-0e29-4764-9b89-a395dfe0aade\" data-question=\"39\">gained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> some notoriety through success in the teaching of modern languages, few teachers are able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7a258a0d-3add-4caa-a2cd-c9f6f25a9e72\" data-question=\"40\">emulate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> the spectacular results of Lozanov and his associates. We can, perhaps, attribute mediocre results to an inadequate placebo effect. The students have not developed the appropriate mind set. They are often not motivated to learn through this method. They do not have enough ‘faith’. They do not see it as ‘real teaching’, especially as it does not seem to involve the ‘work’ they have learned to believe is essential to learning.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28625\" id=\"question-wrapper-28625\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The book Educating Psyche is mainly concerned with </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the power of suggestion in learning</li> <li>B. a particular technique for leaning based on emotions</li> <li>C. the effects of emotion on the imagination and the unconscious</li> <li>D. ways of learning which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9316dda-4d0d-4185-bfd3-9a44bb2c0719\" data-question=\"27\">not traditional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28626\" id=\"question-wrapper-28626\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Lozanov’s theory claims that, when we try to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03ddd725-9f80-486b-b8af-3f88978c6500\" data-question=\"28\">remember<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> things, </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"082f008c-45ce-4af7-a8a3-41207fec52a1\" data-question=\"28\">unimportant details<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> are the easiest to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03ddd725-9f80-486b-b8af-3f88978c6500\" data-question=\"28\">recall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></li> <li>B. concentrating hard produces the best results</li> <li>C. the most significant facts are most easily recalled</li> <li>D. peripheral vision is not important</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28627\" id=\"question-wrapper-28627\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In this passage, the author uses the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4aaf276c-c68e-4acd-8b8a-f9300261f538\" data-question=\"29\">examples of a book and a lecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to illustrate that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. both these are important for developing concentration</li> <li>B. his theory about methods of learning is valid</li> <li>C. reading is a better technique for learning than listening</li> <li>D. we can remember things more easily under hypnosis</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28628\" id=\"question-wrapper-28628\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Lozanov claims that teachers should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db4b96b5-a98c-41a4-adc4-f61a9990c9c5\" data-question=\"30\">train students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. memorise details of the curriculum</li> <li>B. develop their own sets of indirect instructions</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"793e5a22-0bad-4629-8f50-6fcd2ce90278\" data-question=\"30\">think about something other than the curriculum content<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></li> <li>D. avoid overloading the capacity of the brain</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statement agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet, write:</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28629\" id=\"question-wrapper-28629\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the example of suggestopedic teaching in the fourth paragraph, the only variable that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b40fea5f-3e13-4632-a5ad-9219e0e3e806\" data-question=\"31\">changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> is the music. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28630\" id=\"question-wrapper-28630\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Prior to the suggestopedia class, students are made aware that the language experience will be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a4b0cd58-8d71-4856-a65e-9153fd8d9fdf\" data-question=\"32\">demanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28631\" id=\"question-wrapper-28631\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the follow-up class, the teaching activities are similar to those used in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c5c600e-b60d-40ad-9a94-ec2be5a06146\" data-question=\"33\">conventional classes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28632\" id=\"question-wrapper-28632\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> As an indirect benefit, students notice improvements in their memory. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28633\" id=\"question-wrapper-28633\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Teachers say they prefer suggestopedia to traditional approaches to language teaching. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28634\" id=\"question-wrapper-28634\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Students in a suggestopedia class retain more new vocabulary than those in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"770e4ba9-9df1-42a7-a9eb-babaf6793c18\" data-question=\"36\">ordinary classes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary using the list of words, A-K, below. Write the correct letter A-K in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.</p><p>Sugestopedia uses a less direct method of suggestion than other techniques such as hypnosis. However, Lozanov <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5680d234-6418-4baa-a53d-45abf34f79c4\" data-question=\"38\">admits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> that a certain amount of (37)……………… is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e60b5d04-d726-40f0-b181-664a7e477c83\" data-question=\"37\">necessary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in order to convince students, even if this is just a (38)……………………. Furthermore, if the method is to succeed, teachers must follow a set procedure. Although Lozanov’s method has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e3297c6-0e29-4764-9b89-a395dfe0aade\" data-question=\"39\">become<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> quite (39)………………., the result of most other teachers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7a258a0d-3add-4caa-a2cd-c9f6f25a9e72\" data-question=\"40\">using<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> this method have been (40)……………………</p><div><ul><li><strong>A </strong>spectacular </li><li><strong>B </strong>teaching </li><li><strong>C</strong> lesson </li><li><strong>D </strong>authoritarian </li><li><strong>E </strong>unpopular</li><li><strong>F </strong>ritual </li><li><strong>G </strong>unspectacular </li><li><strong>H </strong>placebo </li><li><strong>I </strong>involved </li><li><strong>J </strong>appropriate</li><li><strong>K </strong>well known</li></ul></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28635\" id=\"question-wrapper-28635\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28636\" id=\"question-wrapper-28636\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28637\" id=\"question-wrapper-28637\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">K</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28638\" id=\"question-wrapper-28638\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e9316dda-4d0d-4185-bfd3-9a44bb2c0719","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"not traditional","passagePhrase":"radical"},{"uid":"4aaf276c-c68e-4acd-8b8a-f9300261f538","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"examples of a book and a lecture","passagePhrase":"we think of a book ... we think of a lecture"},{"uid":"082f008c-45ce-4af7-a8a3-41207fec52a1","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"unimportant details","passagePhrase":"peripheral details ... peripheral details"},{"uid":"db4b96b5-a98c-41a4-adc4-f61a9990c9c5","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"train students","passagePhrase":"indirect instruction (suggestion) central to his teaching system"},{"uid":"793e5a22-0bad-4629-8f50-6fcd2ce90278","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"think about something other than the curriculum content","passagePhrase":"shifted away from the curriculum to focus on something peripheral"},{"uid":"b40fea5f-3e13-4632-a5ad-9219e0e3e806","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"changes","passagePhrase":"baroque music ... normal speaking voice"},{"uid":"4c5c600e-b60d-40ad-9a94-ec2be5a06146","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"conventional classes","passagePhrase":"not unusual in language teaching"},{"uid":"770e4ba9-9df1-42a7-a9eb-babaf6793c18","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"ordinary classes","passagePhrase":"conventional teaching"},{"uid":"5680d234-6418-4baa-a53d-45abf34f79c4","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"admits","passagePhrase":"acknowledges"},{"uid":"e60b5d04-d726-40f0-b181-664a7e477c83","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"necessary","passagePhrase":"maintains that without such"},{"uid":"8e3297c6-0e29-4764-9b89-a395dfe0aade","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"become","passagePhrase":"gained"},{"uid":"7a258a0d-3add-4caa-a2cd-c9f6f25a9e72","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"using","passagePhrase":"emulate"},{"uid":"03ddd725-9f80-486b-b8af-3f88978c6500","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"remember ... recall","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_154":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Why Pagodas Don’t Fall Down</strong></p><p>In a land swept by typhoons and shaken by earthquakes, how have Japan’s tallest and seemingly flimsiest old buildings – 500 or so wooden pagodas – remained standing for centuries? Records show that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"320bceb8-8289-4dc5-aad6-1fab335c1e92\" data-question=\"1\">only two have collapsed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> during the past 1400 years. Those that have disappeared were destroyed by fire as a result of lightning or civil war. The disastrous Hanshin earthquake in 1995 killed 6,400 people, toppled elevated highways, flattened office blocks and devastated the port area of Kobe. Yet it <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f5a6ef6f-07ec-460b-b320-54fe6df69946\" data-question=\"2\">left the magnificent five-storey pagoda at the Toji temple in nearby Kyoto unscathed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, though it levelled a number of buildings in the neighbourhood.</p><p>Japanese scholars have been mystified for ages about why these tall, slender buildings are so stable. It was only thirty years ago that the building industry felt confident enough to erect office blocks of steel and reinforced concrete that had more than a dozen floors. With its special shock absorbers to dampen the effect of sudden sideways movements from an earthquake, the thirty-six-storey Kasumigaseki building in central Tokyo – Japan’s first skyscraper – was considered a masterpiece of modern engineering when it was built in 1968.</p><p>Yet in 826, with only pegs and wedges to keep his wooden structure upright, the master builder Kobodaishi had no hesitation in sending his majestic Toji pagoda soaring fifty-five metres into the sky – nearly half as high as the Kasumigaseki skyscraper built some eleven centuries later. Clearly, Japanese <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f1eef3c-b9fa-4102-b1fb-ed2e64407ae0\" data-question=\"4\">carpenters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of the day knew a few tricks about allowing a building to sway and settle itself rather than fight nature’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f20b438-40af-44ed-a85f-25ecbb1a80f0\" data-question=\"4\">forces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. But what sort of tricks?</p><p>The multi-storey pagoda came to Japan from China in the sixth century. As in China, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46ac12a4-3607-45da-b607-0a611479edd8\" data-question=\"9\">were first introduced with Buddhism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and were attached to important temples. The Chinese built their pagodas in brick or stone, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e7c246a-5deb-454e-b2ca-f1108ecc32b0\" data-question=\"5\">inner<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> staircases, and used them in later centuries mainly as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bce205d2-2c3c-4710-aef1-49c5f2bb0b15\" data-question=\"7\">watchtowers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. When the pagoda reached Japan, however, its architecture was freely adapted to local conditions – they were built less high, typically five rather than nine storeys, made mainly of wood and the staircase was dispensed with because the Japanese pagoda did not have any practical use but became more of an art object. Because of the typhoons that batter Japan in the summer, Japanese builders learned to extend the eaves of buildings further beyond the walls. This prevents rainwater gushing down the walls. Pagodas in China and Korea have nothing like the overhang that is found on pagodas in Japan.</p><p>The roof of a Japanese temple building can be made to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ced6216-4146-4082-b253-0f33ff99f84c\" data-question=\"8\">overhang the sides of the structure by fifty per cent or more of the building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>’s overall width. For the same reason, the builders of Japanese pagodas seem to have further increased their weight by choosing to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"32a06e84-2c1e-4606-990b-6ede729a7b04\" data-question=\"6\">cover these extended eaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> not with the porcelain tiles of many Chinese pagodas but with much heavier earthenware tiles.</p><p>But this does not totally explain the great resilience of Japanese pagodas. Is the answer that, like a tall pine tree, the Japanese pagoda – with its massive trunk-like central pillar known as shinbashira – simply flexes and sways during a typhoon or earthquake? For centuries, many thought so. But the answer is not so simple because the startling thing is that the shinbashira actually carries no load at all. In fact, in some pagoda designs, it does not even rest on the ground, but is suspended from the top of the pagoda – hanging loosely down through the middle of the building. The weight of the building is supported entirely by twelve outer and four inner columns.</p><p>And what is the role of the shinbashira, the central pillar? The best way to understand the shinbashira’s role is to watch a video made by Shuzo Ishida, a structural engineer at Kyoto Institute of Technology. Mr Ishida, known to his students as ‘Professor Pagoda’ because of his passion to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6b987cc-03e8-4759-95d7-b7402a5b1d55\" data-question=\"12\">understand the pagoda<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51522d72-c2ee-4511-8d89-362b3f106833\" data-question=\"12\">has built a series of models and tested them on a ‘shake- table’ in his laboratory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. In short, the shinbashira was acting like an enormous stationary pendulum. The ancient craftsmen, apparently without the assistance of very advanced mathematics, seemed to grasp the principles that were, more than a thousand years later, applied in the construction of Japan’s first skyscraper. What those early craftsmen had found by trial and error was that under pressure a pagoda’s loose stack of floors could be made to slither to and fro independent of one another. Viewed from the side, the pagoda seemed to be doing a snake dance – with each consecutive floor moving in the opposite direction to its neighbours above and below. The shinbashira, running up through a hole in the centre of the building, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2ed1bb1-d01e-4caa-a69f-537a964b8a09\" data-question=\"11\">constrained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> individual storeys from moving too far because, after moving a certain distance, they banged into it, transmitting energy away along the column.</p><p>Another strange feature of the Japanese pagoda is that, because the building tapers, with each successive floor plan being smaller than the one below, none of the vertical pillars that carry the weight of the building is connected to its corresponding pillar above. In other words, a five- storey pagoda contains not even one pillar that travels right up through the building to carry the structural loads from the top to the bottom. More surprising is the fact that the individual <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9d82f4b-dc9c-41c7-9fea-e0d7be6b9e14\" data-question=\"10\">storeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> of a Japanese pagoda, unlike their counterparts elsewhere, are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0839b0eb-f6da-4fca-af0b-f626af5b9c7e\" data-question=\"10\">not actually connected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to each other. They are simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc994151-5908-4008-9bd2-22f865185446\" data-question=\"13\">stacked one on top of another<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> like a pile of hats. Interestingly, such a design would not be permitted under current Japanese building regulations.</p><p>And the extra-wide eaves? Think of them as a tightrope walker’s balancing pole. The bigger the mass at each end of the pole, the easier it is for the tightrope walker to maintain his or her balance. The same holds true for a pagoda. ‘With the eaves extending out on all sides like balancing poles,’ says Mr Ishida, ‘the building responds to even the most powerful jolt of an earthquake with a graceful swaying, never an abrupt shaking.’ Here again, Japanese master builders of a thousand years ago anticipated concepts of modern structural engineering.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-4 on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there it impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28639\" id=\"question-wrapper-28639\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"320bceb8-8289-4dc5-aad6-1fab335c1e92\" data-question=\"1\">Only two Japanese pagodas have collapsed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in 1400 years. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28640\" id=\"question-wrapper-28640\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Hanshin earthquake of 1995 <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f5a6ef6f-07ec-460b-b320-54fe6df69946\" data-question=\"2\">destroyed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the pagoda at the Toji temple. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28641\" id=\"question-wrapper-28641\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The other buildings near the Toji pagoda had been built in the last 30 years. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28642\" id=\"question-wrapper-28642\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f1eef3c-b9fa-4102-b1fb-ed2e64407ae0\" data-question=\"4\">builders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of pagodas knew how to absorb some of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f20b438-40af-44ed-a85f-25ecbb1a80f0\" data-question=\"4\">power<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> produced by severe weather conditions. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Classify the following as typical of</p><p><strong>A</strong> both Chinese and Japanese pagodas<br><strong>B</strong> only Chinese pagodas<br><strong>C</strong> only Japanese pagodas</p><p>Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 5-10 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28643\" id=\"question-wrapper-28643\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> easy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e7c246a-5deb-454e-b2ca-f1108ecc32b0\" data-question=\"5\">interior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> access to top </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28644\" id=\"question-wrapper-28644\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"32a06e84-2c1e-4606-990b-6ede729a7b04\" data-question=\"6\">tiles on eaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28645\" id=\"question-wrapper-28645\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> use as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bce205d2-2c3c-4710-aef1-49c5f2bb0b15\" data-question=\"7\">observation post<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28646\" id=\"question-wrapper-28646\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> size of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ced6216-4146-4082-b253-0f33ff99f84c\" data-question=\"8\">eaves up to half the width of the building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28647\" id=\"question-wrapper-28647\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46ac12a4-3607-45da-b607-0a611479edd8\" data-question=\"9\">original religious purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28648\" id=\"question-wrapper-28648\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9d82f4b-dc9c-41c7-9fea-e0d7be6b9e14\" data-question=\"10\">floors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0839b0eb-f6da-4fca-af0b-f626af5b9c7e\" data-question=\"10\">fitting loosely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> over each other </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes11-13 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28649\" id=\"question-wrapper-28649\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In a Japanese pagoda, the shinbashira </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. bears the full weight of the building</li> <li>B. bends under pressure like a tree</li> <li>C. connects the floors with the foundations</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2ed1bb1-d01e-4caa-a69f-537a964b8a09\" data-question=\"11\">stops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the floors moving too far</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28650\" id=\"question-wrapper-28650\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Shuzo Ishida <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51522d72-c2ee-4511-8d89-362b3f106833\" data-question=\"12\">performs experiments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in order to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. improve skyscraper design</li> <li>B. be able to build new pagodas</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6b987cc-03e8-4759-95d7-b7402a5b1d55\" data-question=\"12\">learn about the dynamics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> of pagodas</li> <li>D. understand ancient mathematics</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28651\" id=\"question-wrapper-28651\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The storeys of a Japanese pagoda are </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. linked only by wood</li> <li>B. fastened only to the central pillar</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc994151-5908-4008-9bd2-22f865185446\" data-question=\"13\">fitted loosely on top of each other<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></li> <li>D. joined by special weights</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"320bceb8-8289-4dc5-aad6-1fab335c1e92","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Only two Japanese pagodas have collapsed","passagePhrase":"only two have collapsed"},{"uid":"9f1eef3c-b9fa-4102-b1fb-ed2e64407ae0","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"builders","passagePhrase":"carpenters"},{"uid":"6f20b438-40af-44ed-a85f-25ecbb1a80f0","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"power","passagePhrase":"forces"},{"uid":"46ac12a4-3607-45da-b607-0a611479edd8","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"original religious purpose","passagePhrase":"were first introduced with Buddhism"},{"uid":"8e7c246a-5deb-454e-b2ca-f1108ecc32b0","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"interior","passagePhrase":"inner"},{"uid":"bce205d2-2c3c-4710-aef1-49c5f2bb0b15","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"observation post","passagePhrase":"watchtowers"},{"uid":"0ced6216-4146-4082-b253-0f33ff99f84c","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"eaves up to half the width of the building","passagePhrase":"overhang the sides of the structure by fifty per cent or more of the building"},{"uid":"32a06e84-2c1e-4606-990b-6ede729a7b04","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"tiles on eaves","passagePhrase":"cover these extended eaves"},{"uid":"a6b987cc-03e8-4759-95d7-b7402a5b1d55","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"learn about the dynamics","passagePhrase":"understand the pagoda"},{"uid":"51522d72-c2ee-4511-8d89-362b3f106833","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"performs experiments","passagePhrase":"has built a series of models and tested them on a ‘shake- table’ in his laboratory"},{"uid":"c2ed1bb1-d01e-4caa-a69f-537a964b8a09","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"stops","passagePhrase":"constrained"},{"uid":"e9d82f4b-dc9c-41c7-9fea-e0d7be6b9e14","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"floors","passagePhrase":"storeys"},{"uid":"0839b0eb-f6da-4fca-af0b-f626af5b9c7e","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"fitting loosely","passagePhrase":"not actually connected"},{"uid":"dc994151-5908-4008-9bd2-22f865185446","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"fitted loosely on top of each other","passagePhrase":"stacked one on top of another"}]},"reading_u2_155":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The True Cost of Food</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong> </p><p>For more than forty years the cost of food has been rising. It has now reached a point where a growing number of people believe that it is far too high, and that bringing it down will be one of the great challenges of the twenty first century. That cost, however, is not in immediate cash. In the West at least, most food is now far cheaper to buy in relative terms than it was in 1960. The cost is in the collateral damage of the very methods of food production that have made the food cheaper: in the pollution of water, the enervation of soil, the destruction of wildlife, the harm to animal welfare and the threat to human health caused by modern industrial agriculture.</p><p><strong>B</strong> </p><p>First mechanisation, then mass use of chemical fertilisers and pesticides, then monocultures, then battery rearing of livestock, and now genetic engineering – the onward march of intensive farming has seemed unstoppable in the last half-century, as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c88654a-435b-4789-8b22-5cfd1c08d077\" data-question=\"15\">the yields of produce have soared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. But the damage it has caused has been colossal. In Britain, for example, many of our best-loved <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3f77d765-c7bb-44d9-b2e8-8984b07ed22c\" data-question=\"18\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"faa7ab98-ab6b-4131-8ef8-f2167fa1e873\" data-question=\"18\">farmland<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> birds, such as the skylark, the grey partridge, the lapwing and the corn bunting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"011290ee-91e9-496c-b6fd-be8a08d628ec\" data-question=\"18\">have vanished<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> from huge stretches of countryside, as have even more wild flowers and insects. This is a direct result of the way we have produced our food in the last four decades. Thousands of miles of hedgerows, thousands of ponds, have disappeared from the landscape. The faecal filth of salmon farming has driven wild salmon from many of the sea lochs and rivers of Scotland. Natural soil fertility is dropping in many areas because of continuous industrial fertiliser and pesticide use, while the growth of algae is increasing in lakes because of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c1fa412-a09a-4a66-9d91-d2d7ff4eac88\" data-question=\"17\">fertiliser run-off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</p><p><strong>C</strong> </p><p>Put it all together and it looks like a battlefield, but consumers rarely make the connection at the dinner table. That is mainly because the costs of all this damage are what economists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4550af4-3317-4eff-bca9-f54479a266ac\" data-question=\"16\">refer to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> as externalities: they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"890f54f5-e281-4fc0-a47c-1b17d530bf9f\" data-question=\"16\">outside the main transaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, which is for example producing and selling a field of wheat, and are borne directly by neither producers nor consumers. To many, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"14b45cc3-6dc0-4909-b8a5-c07a9f913249\" data-question=\"20\">the costs may not even appear to be financial at all<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, but merely aesthetic – a terrible shame, but nothing to do with money. And anyway they, as consumers of food, certainly aren’t paying for it, are they?</p><p><strong>D</strong> </p><p>But the costs to society can actually be quantified and, when added up, can amount to staggering sums. A remarkable exercise in doing this has been carried out by one of the world’s leading thinkers on the future of agriculture, Professor Jules Pretty, Director of the Centre for Environment and Society at the University of Essex. Professor Pretty and his colleagues calculated the externalities of British agriculture for one particular year. They added up the costs of repairing the damage it caused, and came up with a total figure of £2,343m. This is equivalent to £208 for every hectare of arable land and permanent pasture, almost as much again as the total government and EU spend on British farming in that year. And according to Professor Pretty, it was a conservative estimate.</p><p><strong>E</strong> </p><p>The costs included: £120m for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84304a2c-6bae-44e9-a161-30e347a7a462\" data-question=\"14\">removal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of pesticides; £16m for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84304a2c-6bae-44e9-a161-30e347a7a462\" data-question=\"14\">removal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of nitrates; £55m for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84304a2c-6bae-44e9-a161-30e347a7a462\" data-question=\"14\">removal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of phosphates and soil; £23m for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84304a2c-6bae-44e9-a161-30e347a7a462\" data-question=\"14\">removal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of the bug Cryptosporidium from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"37d9bd23-2039-4a85-9c4c-c1070f2c59bd\" data-question=\"14\">drinking water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> by water companies; £125m for damage to wildlife habitats, hedgerows and dry stone walls; £1,113m from emissions of gases likely to contribute to climate change; £106m from soil erosion and organic carbon losses; £169m from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"320b76b6-f0d8-4595-bed4-95b9f7156909\" data-question=\"21\">food poisoning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>; and £607m from cattle disease. Professor Pretty <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0f91aa2-e635-4655-b442-1fda567418a5\" data-question=\"22\">draws a simple but memorable conclusion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> from all this: our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f57f9e34-35ba-4fe1-ae9d-9757560bb385\" data-question=\"22\">food bills are actually threefold<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. We are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f57f9e34-35ba-4fe1-ae9d-9757560bb385\" data-question=\"22\">paying for our supposedly cheaper food in three separate ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>: once over the counter, secondly through our taxes, which provide the enormous subsidies propping up modern intensive farming, and thirdly to clean up the mess that modern farming leaves behind.</p><p><strong>F</strong> </p><p>So can the true cost of food be brought down? <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80780dde-41aa-4ce8-b248-33758562256e\" data-question=\"23\">Breaking away from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> industrial agriculture as the solution to hunger may be very hard for some countries, but in Britain, where the immediate need to supply food is less urgent, and the costs and the damage of intensive farming have been clearly seen, it may be more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d474484a-3bf6-41e5-98f2-1cd987c19fd8\" data-question=\"23\">feasible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. The government needs to create sustainable, competitive and diverse farming and food sectors, which will contribute to a thriving and sustainable rural economy, and advance environmental, economic, health, and animal welfare goals.</p><p><strong>G</strong> </p><p>But if industrial agriculture is to be replaced, what is a viable alternative? Professor Pretty feels that organic farming would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c5b79f87-c2db-4ff9-aba5-4134a8378868\" data-question=\"24\">be too big a jump in thinking and in practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c0850a7-fcdd-4716-9c1d-53f277edeba9\" data-question=\"24\">many<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> farmers. Furthermore, the price premium would put the produce out of reach of many poorer consumers. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5210ffeb-0560-46b9-8447-914e0807f471\" data-question=\"25\">is recommending<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> the immediate introduction of a ‘Greener Food Standard’, which would push the market towards more sustainable environmental practices than the current norm, while not requiring the full commitment to organic production. Such a standard would comprise agreed practices for different kinds of farming, covering agrochemical use, soil health, land management, water and energy use, food safety and animal health. It could go a long way, he says, to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b08883b-e8e6-4019-9826-00215fd5332a\" data-question=\"26\">shifting consumers as well as farmers towards a more sustainable system of agriculture.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28652\" id=\"question-wrapper-28652\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a cost involved in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84304a2c-6bae-44e9-a161-30e347a7a462\" data-question=\"14\">purifying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"37d9bd23-2039-4a85-9c4c-c1070f2c59bd\" data-question=\"14\">domestic water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28653\" id=\"question-wrapper-28653\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the stages in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c88654a-435b-4789-8b22-5cfd1c08d077\" data-question=\"15\">the development of the farming industry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28654\" id=\"question-wrapper-28654\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the term used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4550af4-3317-4eff-bca9-f54479a266ac\" data-question=\"16\">describe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"890f54f5-e281-4fc0-a47c-1b17d530bf9f\" data-question=\"16\">hidden costs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28655\" id=\"question-wrapper-28655\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> one effect of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c1fa412-a09a-4a66-9d91-d2d7ff4eac88\" data-question=\"17\">chemicals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> on water sources </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 2? In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28656\" id=\"question-wrapper-28656\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Several <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3f77d765-c7bb-44d9-b2e8-8984b07ed22c\" data-question=\"18\">species of wildlife<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in the British <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"faa7ab98-ab6b-4131-8ef8-f2167fa1e873\" data-question=\"18\">countryside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"011290ee-91e9-496c-b6fd-be8a08d628ec\" data-question=\"18\">are declining<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28657\" id=\"question-wrapper-28657\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The taste of food has deteriorated in recent years. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28658\" id=\"question-wrapper-28658\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The financial costs of environmental damage are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"14b45cc3-6dc0-4909-b8a5-c07a9f913249\" data-question=\"20\">widely recognised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28659\" id=\"question-wrapper-28659\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One of the costs calculated by Professor Pretty was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"320b76b6-f0d8-4595-bed4-95b9f7156909\" data-question=\"21\">illness caused by food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below. Write <strong>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</strong> from the passage.</p><p>Professor Pretty <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0f91aa2-e635-4655-b442-1fda567418a5\" data-question=\"22\">concludes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that our (22)……………….. are higher than most people realise, because we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f57f9e34-35ba-4fe1-ae9d-9757560bb385\" data-question=\"22\">make three different types of payment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. He feels it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d474484a-3bf6-41e5-98f2-1cd987c19fd8\" data-question=\"23\">realistic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> to suggest that Britain should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80780dde-41aa-4ce8-b248-33758562256e\" data-question=\"23\">reduce its reliance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> on (23)………………..<br>Although <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c0850a7-fcdd-4716-9c1d-53f277edeba9\" data-question=\"24\">most<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> farmers would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c5b79f87-c2db-4ff9-aba5-4134a8378868\" data-question=\"24\">be unable to adapt to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> (24)…………………….Professor Pretty <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5210ffeb-0560-46b9-8447-914e0807f471\" data-question=\"25\">wants the government to initiate change by establishing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> what he refers to as a (25)………………He feels this would help to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b08883b-e8e6-4019-9826-00215fd5332a\" data-question=\"26\">change the attitudes of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> both (26)………………….and ………………………..</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28660\" id=\"question-wrapper-28660\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOOD BILLS/COSTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28661\" id=\"question-wrapper-28661\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(MODERN) INTENSIVE FARMING [OR] INDUSTRIAL AGRICULTURE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28662\" id=\"question-wrapper-28662\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ORGANIC FARMING</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28663\" id=\"question-wrapper-28663\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GREENER FOOD STANDARD</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28664\" id=\"question-wrapper-28664\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FARMERS + CONSUMERS</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"6c88654a-435b-4789-8b22-5cfd1c08d077","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the development of the farming industry","passagePhrase":"the yields of produce have soared"},{"uid":"3f77d765-c7bb-44d9-b2e8-8984b07ed22c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"species of wildlife","passagePhrase":"farmland birds, such as the skylark, the grey partridge, the lapwing and the corn bunting"},{"uid":"faa7ab98-ab6b-4131-8ef8-f2167fa1e873","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"countryside","passagePhrase":"farmland"},{"uid":"011290ee-91e9-496c-b6fd-be8a08d628ec","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"are declining","passagePhrase":"have vanished"},{"uid":"3c1fa412-a09a-4a66-9d91-d2d7ff4eac88","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"chemicals","passagePhrase":"fertiliser run-off"},{"uid":"e4550af4-3317-4eff-bca9-f54479a266ac","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"describe","passagePhrase":"refer to"},{"uid":"890f54f5-e281-4fc0-a47c-1b17d530bf9f","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"hidden costs","passagePhrase":"outside the main transaction"},{"uid":"84304a2c-6bae-44e9-a161-30e347a7a462","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"purifying","passagePhrase":"removal ... removal ... removal ... removal"},{"uid":"37d9bd23-2039-4a85-9c4c-c1070f2c59bd","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"domestic water","passagePhrase":"drinking water"},{"uid":"320b76b6-f0d8-4595-bed4-95b9f7156909","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"illness caused by food","passagePhrase":"food poisoning"},{"uid":"f0f91aa2-e635-4655-b442-1fda567418a5","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"concludes","passagePhrase":"draws a simple but memorable conclusion"},{"uid":"f57f9e34-35ba-4fe1-ae9d-9757560bb385","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"make three different types of payment","passagePhrase":"food bills are actually threefold ... paying for our supposedly cheaper food in three separate ways"},{"uid":"80780dde-41aa-4ce8-b248-33758562256e","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"reduce its reliance","passagePhrase":"Breaking away from"},{"uid":"d474484a-3bf6-41e5-98f2-1cd987c19fd8","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"realistic","passagePhrase":"feasible"},{"uid":"c5b79f87-c2db-4ff9-aba5-4134a8378868","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"be unable to adapt to","passagePhrase":"be too big a jump in thinking and in practices"},{"uid":"3c0850a7-fcdd-4716-9c1d-53f277edeba9","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"most","passagePhrase":"many"},{"uid":"5210ffeb-0560-46b9-8447-914e0807f471","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"wants the government to initiate change by establishing","passagePhrase":"is recommending"},{"uid":"0b08883b-e8e6-4019-9826-00215fd5332a","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"change the attitudes of","passagePhrase":"shifting consumers as well as farmers towards a more sustainable system of agriculture."}]},"reading_u2_156":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Makete Integrated Rural Transport Project</strong></p><p><strong>Section A</strong><br>The disappointing results of many conventional road transport projects in Africa led some experts to rethink the strategy by which rural transport problems were to be tackled at the beginning of the 1980s. A request for help in improving the availability of transport within the remote Makete District of south-western Tanzania presented the opportunity to try a new approach.</p><p>The concept of ‘integrated rural transport’ was adopted in the task of examining the transport needs of the rural households in the district. The objective was to reduce the time and effort needed to obtain access to essential goods and services through an improved rural transport system. The underlying assumption was that the time saved would be used instead for activities that would improve the social and economic development of the communities. The Makete Integrated Rural Transport Project (MIRTP) started in 1985 with financial support from the Swiss Development Corporation and was coordinated with the help of the Tanzanian government.</p><p><strong>Section B</strong><br>When the project began, Makete District was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2037269-b38e-4559-8476-4e81d45788ff\" data-question=\"32\">virtually totally isolated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> during the rainy season. The regional road was in such bad shape that access to the main towns was impossible for about three months of the year. Road traffic was extremely rare within the district, and alternative means of transport were restricted to donkeys in the north of the district. People relied primarily on the paths, which were slippery and dangerous during the rains.</p><p>Before solutions could be proposed, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ddb08e42-ad07-4721-89e6-6215a9ad5976\" data-question=\"27\">the problems had to be understood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Little was known about the transport demands of the rural households, so Phase I, between December 1985 and December 1987, focused on research. The socio-economic survey of more than 400 households in the district indicated that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"44ffbe89-925b-4dd2-a0b3-5a06316e0b99\" data-question=\"33\">a household in Makete spent, on average, seven hours a day<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> on transporting themselves and their goods, a figure which seemed extreme but which has also been obtained in surveys in other rural areas in Africa. Interesting facts regarding transport were found: 95% was on foot; 80% was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"628774d3-1c0c-4640-9507-67a45eb297a8\" data-question=\"34\">within<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69075117-6873-44b0-b451-10e1cabc397b\" data-question=\"34\">locality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>; and 70% was related to the collection of water and firewood and travelling to grinding mills.</p><p><strong>Section C</strong><br>Having determined the main transport needs, possible solutions were identified which might reduce the time and burden. During Phase II, from January to February 1991, a number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"713a9a75-1b89-4e11-9a93-6519b8c65561\" data-question=\"28\">approaches were implemented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in an effort to improve mobility and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc264d86-ff96-409d-9c37-c43eaf2a9d57\" data-question=\"28\">access to transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</p><p>An improvement of the road network was considered necessary to ensure the import and export of goods to the district. These improvements were carried out using methods that were heavily dependent on labour.</p><p>In addition to the improvement of roads, these methods provided training in the operation of a mechanical workshop and bus and truck services. However, the difference from the conventional approach was that this time consideration was given to local transport needs outside the road network.</p><p>Most goods were transported along the paths that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"58f1f3c5-3ab2-49ad-bc4a-64d51ee03998\" data-question=\"36\">provide short-cuts up and down the hillsides<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, but the paths were a real safety risk and made the journey on foot even more arduous. It made sense to improve the paths by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b7cd256-0964-4089-9495-9615a5997533\" data-question=\"36\">building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> steps, handrails and footbridges.</p><p>It was uncommon to find means of transport that were more efficient than walking but less technologically advanced than motor vehicles. The use of bicycles was constrained by their high cost and the lack of available spare parts. Oxen were not used at all but donkeys were used by a few households in the northern part of the district. MIRTP focused on what would be most appropriate for the inhabitants of Makete in terms of what was available, how much they could afford and what they were willing to accept. After careful consideration, the project chose the promotion of donkeys – a donkey costs less than a bicycle – and the introduction of a locally manufacturable wheelbarrow.</p><p><strong>Section D</strong><br>At the end of Phase II, it was clear that the selected approaches to Makete’s transport problems had had different degrees of success. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"3f272826-2fc4-4de1-b221-efde0a83f5c9\" data-question=\"31\">Phase III, from March 1991 to March 1993<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, focused on the refinement and institutionalisation of these activities. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4939482b-5108-4e5c-8357-a0c239cd1e19\" data-question=\"39\">The road improvements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> and accompanying maintenance system had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de4ec84d-6029-4811-95c5-dad3e4cc515a\" data-question=\"39\">helped make the district centre accessible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> throughout the year. Essential goods from outside the district had become more readily available at the market, and prices did not fluctuate as much as they had done before.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4439c080-3438-44c3-96f8-f259a90a54b4\" data-question=\"38\">Paths and secondary roads were improved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> only at the request of communities who were willing to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c69de87d-c5f2-4eb2-aad2-e9b383e36d89\" data-question=\"38\">participate in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b7cd256-0964-4089-9495-9615a5997533\" data-question=\"36\">construction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> and maintenance. However, the improved paths impressed the inhabitants, and requests for assistance greatly increased soon after only a few improvements had been completed.</p><p>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0012aa3-5bd1-4307-8887-97de0d9b5cb0\" data-question=\"37\">efforts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5dc637df-97f2-4fa7-8de8-f2a81a76be7a\" data-question=\"37\">improve the efficiency<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> of the existing transport services were not very successful because most of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11051ef5-0848-454d-bee3-2d9adece92e9\" data-question=\"37\">the motorised vehicles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in the district broke down and there were no resources to repair them. Even the introduction of low-cost means of transport was difficult because of the general poverty of the district. The locally manufactured wheelbarrows were still too expensive for all but a few of the households. Modifications to the original design by local carpenters cut production time and costs. Other local carpenters have been trained in the new design so that they can respond to requests. Nevertheless, a locally produced wooden wheelbarrow which costs around 5000 Tanzanian shillings (less than US$20) in Makete, and is about one quarter the cost of a metal wheelbarrow, is still too expensive for most people.</p><p>Donkeys, which were imported to the district, have become more common and contribute, in particular, to the transportation of crops and goods to market. Those who have bought donkeys are mainly from richer households but with an increased supply through local breeding, donkeys should become more affordable. Meanwhile, local initiatives are promoting the renting out of the existing donkeys. It should be noted, however that a donkey, which at 20,000 Tanzanian shillings costs less than a bicycle, is still an investment equal to an average household’s income over half a year This clearly illustrates the need for supplementary measures if one wants to assist the rural poor.</p><p><strong>Section E</strong><br>It would have been easy to criticise the MIRTP for using in the early phases a ‘top-down’ approach, in which decisions were made by experts and officials before being handed down to communities, but it was necessary to start the process from the level of the governmental authorities of the district. It would have been difficult to respond to the requests of villagers and other rural inhabitants without <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87e33d0c-d2c0-4037-acf3-65af6c277604\" data-question=\"29\">the support and understanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d83d25e6-0886-443f-9fcf-fcc9eb9ab0cf\" data-question=\"29\">district authorities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</p><p><strong>Section F</strong><br>Today, nobody in the district argues about the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7fb92176-0ecb-4205-a0a4-451194ba963a\" data-question=\"40\">importance of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> improved paths and inexpensive means of transport. But this is the result of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6b0cd08c-ae33-439d-bc47-fb9b8d4e7ffc\" data-question=\"40\">dedicated work over a long period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, particularly from the officers in charge of community development. They played an essential role in raising awareness and interest among the rural communities. The concept of integrated rural transport is now well established in Tanzania, where a major program of rural transport is just about to start. The experiences from Makete will help in this initiative, and Makete District will act as a reference for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0cf46e70-bf70-4365-bed3-e81ef6a10801\" data-question=\"30\">future work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 3 has six sections, A-F. Choose the correct heading for sections B, C, E and F from the list of headings below.</p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><ul><li>i MIRTP as a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0cf46e70-bf70-4365-bed3-e81ef6a10801\" data-question=\"30\">future model<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></li><li>ii <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ddb08e42-ad07-4721-89e6-6215a9ad5976\" data-question=\"27\">Identifying the main transport problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></li><li>iii Preference for motorised vehicles</li><li>iv Government Authrities’ instructions</li><li>v <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"713a9a75-1b89-4e11-9a93-6519b8c65561\" data-question=\"28\">Initial improvements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in mobility and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc264d86-ff96-409d-9c37-c43eaf2a9d57\" data-question=\"28\">transport modes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></li><li>vi Request for improves transport in Makete</li><li>vii Transport improvements in the northern part of the district</li><li>viii Improvements in the rail network</li><li>ix Effects of initial MIRTP measures</li><li>x <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87e33d0c-d2c0-4037-acf3-65af6c277604\" data-question=\"29\">Co-operation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d83d25e6-0886-443f-9fcf-fcc9eb9ab0cf\" data-question=\"29\">district officials<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></li><li>xi Role of wheelbarrows and donkeys</li></ul><p><strong>Example: Section A vi</strong></p><p><strong>Example: Section D ix</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28665\" id=\"question-wrapper-28665\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28666\" id=\"question-wrapper-28666\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28667\" id=\"question-wrapper-28667\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">X</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28668\" id=\"question-wrapper-28668\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in reading passage 3? In boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet write:</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28669\" id=\"question-wrapper-28669\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> MIRTP was divided into <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"3f272826-2fc4-4de1-b221-efde0a83f5c9\" data-question=\"31\">five phases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28670\" id=\"question-wrapper-28670\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Prior to the start of the MIRTP the Makete district was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2037269-b38e-4559-8476-4e81d45788ff\" data-question=\"32\">almost inaccessible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> during the rainy reason. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28671\" id=\"question-wrapper-28671\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Phase I of MIRTP consisted of a survey of <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"44ffbe89-925b-4dd2-a0b3-5a06316e0b99\" data-question=\"33\">household expenditure on transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28672\" id=\"question-wrapper-28672\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The survey concluded that one-fifth or 20% of the household transport requirement as <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"628774d3-1c0c-4640-9507-67a45eb297a8\" data-question=\"34\">outside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69075117-6873-44b0-b451-10e1cabc397b\" data-question=\"34\">local area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28673\" id=\"question-wrapper-28673\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> MIRTP hopes to improve the movements of goods from Makete district to the country’s capital. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-J below.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-J in boxes 36-39 on your answer sheet.</p><ul><li><strong>A</strong> provided the people of Makete with experience in running bus and truck services.</li><li><strong>B</strong> was especially successful in the northern part of the district.</li><li><strong>C</strong> differed from earlier phases in that the community became less actively involved.</li><li><strong>D</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"58f1f3c5-3ab2-49ad-bc4a-64d51ee03998\" data-question=\"36\">improved paths used for transport up and down hillsides<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</li><li><strong>E</strong> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de4ec84d-6029-4811-95c5-dad3e4cc515a\" data-question=\"39\">no longer a problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> once <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4939482b-5108-4e5c-8357-a0c239cd1e19\" data-question=\"39\">the roads had been improved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</li><li><strong>F</strong> cost less than locally made wheelbarrows.</li><li><strong>G</strong> was done only at the request of local people who were willing to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c69de87d-c5f2-4eb2-aad2-e9b383e36d89\" data-question=\"38\">lend a hand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li><li><strong>H</strong> was at first considered by MIRTP to be affordable for the people of the district.</li><li><strong>I</strong> hindered <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0012aa3-5bd1-4307-8887-97de0d9b5cb0\" data-question=\"37\">attempts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to make the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11051ef5-0848-454d-bee3-2d9adece92e9\" data-question=\"37\">existing transport services<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> more efficient.</li><li><strong>J</strong> was thought to be the most important objective of Phase III.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28674\" id=\"question-wrapper-28674\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Construction of footbridges, steps and handrails </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28675\" id=\"question-wrapper-28675\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Frequent breakdown of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11051ef5-0848-454d-bee3-2d9adece92e9\" data-question=\"37\">buses and trucks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in Makete </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28676\" id=\"question-wrapper-28676\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4439c080-3438-44c3-96f8-f259a90a54b4\" data-question=\"38\">The improvement of secondary roads and paths<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28677\" id=\"question-wrapper-28677\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The isolation of Makete for part of the year </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in box 40 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28678\" id=\"question-wrapper-28678\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Which of the following phrases best describes the main aim of Reading Passage 3? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. to suggest that projects such as MIRTP are needed in other countries</li> <li>B. to describe how MIRTP was implemented and how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7fb92176-0ecb-4205-a0a4-451194ba963a\" data-question=\"40\">successful it was<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></li> <li>C. to examine how MIRTP promoted the use of donkeys</li> <li>D. to warn that projects such as MIRTP are likely to have serious problems</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"d2037269-b38e-4559-8476-4e81d45788ff","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"almost inaccessible","passagePhrase":"virtually totally isolated"},{"uid":"ddb08e42-ad07-4721-89e6-6215a9ad5976","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Identifying the main transport problems","passagePhrase":"the problems had to be understood"},{"uid":"69075117-6873-44b0-b451-10e1cabc397b","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"local area","passagePhrase":"locality"},{"uid":"713a9a75-1b89-4e11-9a93-6519b8c65561","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Initial improvements","passagePhrase":"approaches were implemented"},{"uid":"dc264d86-ff96-409d-9c37-c43eaf2a9d57","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"transport modes","passagePhrase":"access to transport"},{"uid":"58f1f3c5-3ab2-49ad-bc4a-64d51ee03998","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"improved paths used for transport up and down hillsides","passagePhrase":"provide short-cuts up and down the hillsides"},{"uid":"4b7cd256-0964-4089-9495-9615a5997533","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"building ... construction"},{"uid":"4939482b-5108-4e5c-8357-a0c239cd1e19","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"the roads had been improved","passagePhrase":"The road improvements"},{"uid":"de4ec84d-6029-4811-95c5-dad3e4cc515a","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"no longer a problem","passagePhrase":"helped make the district centre accessible"},{"uid":"4439c080-3438-44c3-96f8-f259a90a54b4","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"The improvement of secondary roads and paths","passagePhrase":"Paths and secondary roads were improved"},{"uid":"c69de87d-c5f2-4eb2-aad2-e9b383e36d89","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"lend a hand","passagePhrase":"participate in"},{"uid":"f0012aa3-5bd1-4307-8887-97de0d9b5cb0","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"attempts","passagePhrase":"efforts"},{"uid":"5dc637df-97f2-4fa7-8de8-f2a81a76be7a","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"improve the efficiency"},{"uid":"11051ef5-0848-454d-bee3-2d9adece92e9","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"existing transport services ... buses and trucks","passagePhrase":"the motorised vehicles"},{"uid":"87e33d0c-d2c0-4037-acf3-65af6c277604","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Co-operation","passagePhrase":"the support and understanding"},{"uid":"d83d25e6-0886-443f-9fcf-fcc9eb9ab0cf","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"district officials","passagePhrase":"district authorities"},{"uid":"7fb92176-0ecb-4205-a0a4-451194ba963a","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"successful it was","passagePhrase":"importance of"},{"uid":"6b0cd08c-ae33-439d-bc47-fb9b8d4e7ffc","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"dedicated work over a long period"},{"uid":"0cf46e70-bf70-4365-bed3-e81ef6a10801","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"future model","passagePhrase":"future work"}]},"reading_u2_157":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Ant Intelligence</strong></p><p>When we think of intelligent members of the animal kingdom, the creatures that spring immediately to mind are apes and monkeys. But in fact the social lives of some members of the insect kingdom are sufficiently complex to suggest more than a hint of intelligence. Among these, the world of the ant has come in for considerable scrutiny lately, and the idea that ants demonstrate sparks of cognition has certainly not been rejected by those involved in these investigations.</p><p>Ants store food, repel attackers and use chemical signals to contact one another in case of attack. Such <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7404611c-f22b-4f5a-ba18-63e5fdfcdcd5\" data-question=\"1\">chemical communication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> can be compared to the human <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7404611c-f22b-4f5a-ba18-63e5fdfcdcd5\" data-question=\"1\">use of visual and auditory channels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> (as in religious chants, advertising images and jingles, political slogans and martial music) to arouse and propagate moods and attitudes. The biologist Lewis Thomas wrote Ants are so much like human beings as to be an embarrassment. They farm fungi, raise aphids as livestock, launch armies to war, use chemical sprays to alarm and confuse enemies, capture slaves, engage in child labour, exchange information ceaselessly. They do everything but watch television.</p><p>However, in ants there is no cultural transmission – everything must be encoded in the genes – whereas in humans the opposite is true. Only basic instincts are carried in the genes of a newborn baby, other skills being learned from others in the community as the child grows up. It may seem that this cultural continuity gives us a huge advantage over ants. They have never mastered fire nor progressed. Their fungus farming and aphid herding crafts are sophisticated when compared to the agricultural skills of humans five thousand-years ago but have been totally overtaken by modern human agribusiness.</p><p>Or have they? The farming methods of ants are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15099f5c-f1cd-440c-8d76-199905d19da1\" data-question=\"11\">at least sustainable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. They do not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0015266c-0acf-4e06-9534-20fa11546cbf\" data-question=\"12\">ruin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> environments or use enormous amounts of energy. Moreover, recent evidence suggests that the crop farming of ants may be more sophisticated and adaptable than was thought.</p><p>Ants were farmers fifty million years before humans were. Ants <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"77b7d786-ca9a-42ae-a988-e2c2b351b646\" data-question=\"7\">can’t digest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the cellulose in leaves – but some fungi can. The ants therefore cultivate these fungi in their nests, bringing them leaves to feed on, and then use them as a source of food. Farmer ants secrete <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d746a7d5-ad20-4134-a902-1db607977269\" data-question=\"8\">antibiotics to control other fungi<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> that might act as ‘weeds’, and spread <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54dcc4d7-a15c-4d5c-b652-e1a52d4e0cf3\" data-question=\"9\">waste<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to fertilise the crop.</p><p>It was once thought that the fungus that ants cultivate was a single type that they had propagated, essentially unchanged from the distant past. Not so. Ulrich Mueller of Maryland and his colleagues genetically screened 862 different types of fungi taken from ants’ nests. These turned out to be highly diverse: it seems that ants are continually domesticating new species. Even more impressively, DNA analysis of the fungi suggests that the ants improve or modify the fungi by regularly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f975452-a3fc-469d-841e-c45b8defa19d\" data-question=\"10\">swapping<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> and sharing strains with neighboring ant colonies.</p><p>Whereas prehistoric man had no exposure to urban lifestyles – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be49b25b-3186-481b-8025-de55faf7776f\" data-question=\"2\">the forcing house of intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> – the evidence suggests that ants have lived in urban settings for close on a hundred million years, developing and maintaining underground cities of specialised chambers and tunnels.</p><p>When we survey Mexico City, Tokyo, Los Angeles, we are amazed at what has been accomplished by humans. Yet Hoelldobler and Wilson’s magnificent work for ant lovers, the Ants, describes a supercolony of the ant Formica yessensis on the Ishikari Coast of Hokkaido. This ‘megalopolis’ was reported to be composed of 360 million workers and a million queens living in 4,500 interconnected nests across a territory of 2.7 square kilometers.</p><p>Such enduring and intricately meshed levels of technical achievement outstrip by far anything achieved by our distant ancestors. We hail as masterpieces the cave paintings in southern France and elsewhere, dating back some 20,000 years. Ant societies existed in something like their present form more than seventy million years ago. Beside this, prehistoric man looks technologically primitive. Is this then some kind of intelligence, albeit of a different kind?</p><p>Research conducted at Oxford, Sussex and Zurich Universities has shown that when; desert ants return from a foraging trip, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ae186dd-e91c-4e06-a7ed-1242f4d90ebf\" data-question=\"4\">navigate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f71ac596-3775-4480-8580-a7bb46293d7c\" data-question=\"4\">integrating bearings and distances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, which they continuously update their heads. They combine the evidence of visual landmarks with a mental library of local directions, all within a framework which is consulted and updated. So ants can learn too.</p><p>And in a twelve-year programme of work, Ryabko and Reznikova have found evidence that ants can transmit very complex messages. Scouts who had located food in a maze returned to mobilise their foraging teams. They engaged in contact sessions, at the end of which the scout was removed in order to observe what her team might do. Often the foragers proceeded to the exact spot in the maze where the food had been Elaborate precautions were taken to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1d13c83b-5aff-42f8-a459-d71bf423cd97\" data-question=\"5\">prevent the foraging team using odour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> clues. Discussion now centers on whether the route through the maze is communicated as a ‘left- right sequence of turns or as a ‘compass bearing and distance’ message.</p><p>During the course of this exhaustive study, Reznikova has grown so attached to her laboratory ants that she feels she knows them as individuals – even without the paint spots used to mark them. It’s no surprise that Edward Wilson, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d178f23-0d22-4179-b01a-382a582978bf\" data-question=\"6\">in his essay, ‘In the company of ants’<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, advises readers who ask what to do with the ants in their kitchen to: ‘Watch where you step. Be careful of little lives.’</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write:</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28679\" id=\"question-wrapper-28679\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Ants use the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7404611c-f22b-4f5a-ba18-63e5fdfcdcd5\" data-question=\"1\">same channels of communication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> as humans do. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28680\" id=\"question-wrapper-28680\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> City life is one factor that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be49b25b-3186-481b-8025-de55faf7776f\" data-question=\"2\">encourages the development of intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28681\" id=\"question-wrapper-28681\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Ants can build large cities more quickly than humans do. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28682\" id=\"question-wrapper-28682\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some ants can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ae186dd-e91c-4e06-a7ed-1242f4d90ebf\" data-question=\"4\">find their way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f71ac596-3775-4480-8580-a7bb46293d7c\" data-question=\"4\">making calculations based on distance and position<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28683\" id=\"question-wrapper-28683\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In one experiment, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1d13c83b-5aff-42f8-a459-d71bf423cd97\" data-question=\"5\">foraging teams were able to use their sense of smell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to find food. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28684\" id=\"question-wrapper-28684\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The essay. ‘In the company of ants’ explores ant communication. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary using the list of words, A-O, below. Write the correct letter, A-O, in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>Ants as farmers</strong><br>Ants have sophisticated methods of farming, including herding livestock and growing crops, which are in many ways similar to those used in human agriculture. The ants cultivate a large number of different species of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77232b2b-38f5-4405-b071-7272b6c0bffd\" data-question=\"7\">edible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> fungi which convert (7)………………… into a form which they <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"77b7d786-ca9a-42ae-a988-e2c2b351b646\" data-question=\"7\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77232b2b-38f5-4405-b071-7272b6c0bffd\" data-question=\"7\">can digest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. They use their own natural (8)………………… as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d746a7d5-ad20-4134-a902-1db607977269\" data-question=\"8\">weed-killers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> and also use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54dcc4d7-a15c-4d5c-b652-e1a52d4e0cf3\" data-question=\"9\">unwanted materials<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> as (9)…………………… Genetic analysis shows they constantly upgrade these fungi by developing new species and by (10)………………… species with neighboring ant colonies. In fact, the farming methods of ants could be said to be more advanced than human agribusiness, since they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"76f782bc-7c73-4538-8ad4-a1debded4e89\" data-question=\"13\">use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (11)………………… methods, they do not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0015266c-0acf-4e06-9534-20fa11546cbf\" data-question=\"12\">affect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> the (12)……………… and do not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"76f782bc-7c73-4538-8ad4-a1debded4e89\" data-question=\"13\">waste<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)……………………</p><table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"Table\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tbody><tr><td rowspan=\"1\"><p><strong>A</strong> aphids</p></td><td rowspan=\"1\"><p><strong>B</strong> agricultural</p></td><td rowspan=\"1\"><p><strong>C</strong> cellulose</p></td><td><p><strong>D</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f975452-a3fc-469d-841e-c45b8defa19d\" data-question=\"10\">exchanging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>E</strong> energy</p></td><td><p><strong>F</strong> fertilizers</p></td><td><p><strong>G</strong> food</p></td><td><p><strong>H</strong> fungi</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>I</strong> growing</p></td><td><p><strong>J</strong> interbreeding</p></td><td><p><strong>K</strong> natural</p></td><td><p><strong>L</strong> other species</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>M</strong> secretions</p></td><td><p><strong>N</strong> sustainable</p></td><td><p><strong>O</strong> environment</p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28685\" id=\"question-wrapper-28685\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28686\" id=\"question-wrapper-28686\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">M</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28687\" id=\"question-wrapper-28687\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28688\" id=\"question-wrapper-28688\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28689\" id=\"question-wrapper-28689\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">N</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28690\" id=\"question-wrapper-28690\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">O</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28691\" id=\"question-wrapper-28691\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"15099f5c-f1cd-440c-8d76-199905d19da1","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"at least sustainable"},{"uid":"0015266c-0acf-4e06-9534-20fa11546cbf","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"affect","passagePhrase":"ruin"},{"uid":"d746a7d5-ad20-4134-a902-1db607977269","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"weed-killers","passagePhrase":"antibiotics to control other fungi"},{"uid":"54dcc4d7-a15c-4d5c-b652-e1a52d4e0cf3","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"unwanted materials","passagePhrase":"waste"},{"uid":"6f975452-a3fc-469d-841e-c45b8defa19d","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"exchanging","passagePhrase":"swapping"},{"uid":"be49b25b-3186-481b-8025-de55faf7776f","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"encourages the development of intelligence","passagePhrase":"the forcing house of intelligence"},{"uid":"7ae186dd-e91c-4e06-a7ed-1242f4d90ebf","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"find their way","passagePhrase":"navigate"},{"uid":"f71ac596-3775-4480-8580-a7bb46293d7c","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"making calculations based on distance and position","passagePhrase":"integrating bearings and distances"},{"uid":"6d178f23-0d22-4179-b01a-382a582978bf","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"in his essay, ‘In the company of ants’"},{"uid":"77232b2b-38f5-4405-b071-7272b6c0bffd","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"edible ... can digest","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"76f782bc-7c73-4538-8ad4-a1debded4e89","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"use ... waste","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_158":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Population Movement and Genetics</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong> </p><p>Study of the origins and distribution of human populations used to be based on archaeological and fossil evidence. A number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ec4c359c-852e-419f-bf96-dd9b2ac18cf7\">techniques<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> developed since the 1950s, however, have placed the study of these subjects on a sounder and more objective footing. The best information on early population movements is now being obtained from the ‘archaeology of the living body’, the clues to be found in genetic material.</p><p><strong>B</strong> </p><p>Recent work on the problem of when people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"d1c65701-bdf0-48f3-82be-177afa39a0e4\">first entered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> the Americas is an example of the value of these new techniques. North-east Asia and Siberia have long been accepted as the launching ground for the first human colonisers of the New World*. But was there one major wave of migration across the Bering Strait into the Americas, or several? And when did this event, or events, take place? In recent years, new clues have come from research into genetics, including the distribution of genetic markers in modern Native Americans.</p><p><strong>C</strong> </p><p>An important project, led by the biological anthropologist Robert Williams, focused on the variants (called Gm allotypes) of one particular protein – immunoglobin G — found in the fluid portion of human blood. All proteins ‘drift’, or produce variants, over the generations, and members of an interbreeding human population will share a set of such variants. Thus, by comparing the Gm allotypes of two different populations (e.g. two Indian tribes), one can establish their genetic ‘distance’, which itself can be calibrated to give an indication of the length of time since these populations last <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4ca51a65-44cf-4965-adcf-47e061db1c02\">interbred<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</p><p><strong>D</strong> </p><p>Williams and his colleagues sampled the blood of over 5,000 American Indians in western North America during a twenty- year period. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"8a25f003-abf6-4161-87ed-8aa189708af7\">found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that their Gm allotypes could be divided into two groups, one of which also corresponded to the genetic typing of Central and South American Indians. Other tests showed that the Inuit (or Eskimo) and Aleut formed a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"72635541-c535-4095-b89c-621a8527ca86\">third group<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. From this evidence it was deduced that there had been three major waves of migration across the Bering Strait. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"24\" data-uid=\"88421276-f9f4-4d7d-a546-6f3dc729f5cc\">The first, Paleo-lndian, wave<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> more than 15,000 years ago was ancestral to all Central and South American Indians. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"23\" data-uid=\"a6d363de-5bdb-46c0-8ffa-6084a71955b0\">The second wave,<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> about 14,000-12,000 years ago, brought Na-Dene hunters, ancestors of the Navajo and Apache (who only migrated south from Canada about 600 or 700 years ago). The third wave, perhaps 10,000 or 9,000 years ago, saw the migration from North-east Asia of groups ancestral to the modern Eskimo and Aleut.</p><p><strong>E</strong> </p><p>How far does <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"349bda21-f82e-44a1-8427-8534a1adb22c\">other research support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c6a968d2-d353-4780-ac52-42892fa04136\">these conclusions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>? Geneticist Douglas Wallace has studied mitochondrial DNA in blood samples from three widely separated Native American groups: Pima- Papago Indians in Arizona, Maya Indians on the Yucatdn peninsula, Mexico, and Ticuna Indians in the Upper Amazon region of Brazil. As would have been predicted by Robert Williams’s work, all three groups appear to be descended from the same ancestral (Paleo-lndian) population.</p><p><strong>F</strong> </p><p>There are two other kinds of research that have thrown some light on the origins of the Native American population; they involve the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"8fe9a805-f65f-4aa5-be36-f92265658f31\">study of teeth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and of languages. The biological anthropologist Christy Turner is an expert in the analysis of changing physical characteristics in human teeth. He argues that tooth crowns and roots have a high genetic component, minimally affected by environmental and other factors. Studies carried out by Turner of many thousands of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"3592853e-7521-44bf-b2ef-060fa08729c1\">New and Old World specimens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, both ancient and modern, suggest that the majority of prehistoric Americans are linked to Northern Asian populations by crown and root traits such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e9227921-f218-4790-96a7-78e0951d3415\">incisor shoveling (a scooping out on one or both surfaces of the tooth)<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, single-rooted upper first premolars and triple-rooted lower first molars. According to Turner, this ties in with the idea of a single Paleo-lndian migration out of North Asia, which he sets at before 14,000 years ago by calibrating rates of dental micro-evolution. Tooth analyses also suggest that there were two later migrations of Na-Denes and Eskimo- Aleut.</p><p><strong>G</strong> The linguist Joseph Greenberg has, since the 1950s, argued that all Native American languages belong to a single ‘Amerind’ family, except for Na-Dene and Eskimo-Aleut – a view that gives credence to the idea of three main migrations. Greenberg is in a minority among fellow linguists, most of whom favour the notion of a great many waves of migration to account for the more than 1,000 languages spoken at one time by American Indians. But there is no doubt that the new genetic and dental evidence provides strong backing for Greenberg’s view. Dates given for the migrations should nevertheless be treated with caution, except where supported by hard archaeological evidence.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has seven sections, A-G. Choose the correct headings for sections A-F from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i-x, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><ul><li>i The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"8a25f003-abf6-4161-87ed-8aa189708af7\">results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of the research into blood-variants</li><li>ii <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"8fe9a805-f65f-4aa5-be36-f92265658f31\">Dental evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></li><li>iii Greenberg’s analysis of the dental and linguistic evidence</li><li>iv Developments in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"ec4c359c-852e-419f-bf96-dd9b2ac18cf7\">methods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> used to study early population movements</li><li>v Indian migration from Canada to the U.S.A.</li><li>vi <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"349bda21-f82e-44a1-8427-8534a1adb22c\">Further genetic evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> relating to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"c6a968d2-d353-4780-ac52-42892fa04136\">the three-wave theory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></li><li>vii Long-standing questions about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"d1c65701-bdf0-48f3-82be-177afa39a0e4\">prehistoric migration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> to America</li><li>viii Conflicting views of the three-wave theory, based on non-genetic Evidence</li><li>ix Questions about the causes of prehistoric migration to America</li><li>x How analysis of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"4ca51a65-44cf-4965-adcf-47e061db1c02\">blood-variants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> measures the closeness of the relationship between different populations</li></ul><p><strong>Example Section G viii</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28692\" id=\"question-wrapper-28692\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Passage A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28693\" id=\"question-wrapper-28693\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Passage B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28694\" id=\"question-wrapper-28694\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Passage C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">X</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28695\" id=\"question-wrapper-28695\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Passage D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28696\" id=\"question-wrapper-28696\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Passage E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28697\" id=\"question-wrapper-28697\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Passage F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the form below. Write the correct letter A-F in boxes 20 and 21 on your answer sheet.</p><table cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td><p>Route</p></td><td><p>Period (number of years ago)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(20).............</p></td><td><p>15,000 or more</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>(21).............</p></td><td><p>600 to 700</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><em><img src=\"/media/gg_imgs/test/628a0611a651d3e7ede29c61d41377dddb8dd7a9.jpg\" style=\"height:487px; width:391px\"></em></span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28698\" id=\"question-wrapper-28698\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28699\" id=\"question-wrapper-28699\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 refers to the three-wave theory of early migration to the Americas. It also suggests in which of these three waves the ancestors of various groups of modern native Americans first reached the continent.</p><p>Classify the groups named in the table below as originating from<br><strong>A</strong> the first wave<br><strong>B</strong> the second wave<br><strong>C</strong> the third wave</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28700\" id=\"question-wrapper-28700\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Inuit </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28701\" id=\"question-wrapper-28701\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Apache </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28702\" id=\"question-wrapper-28702\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Pima-Papago </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28703\" id=\"question-wrapper-28703\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Ticuna </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter A, B, C, or D.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28704\" id=\"question-wrapper-28704\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Christy Turner's research involved the examination of </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"e9227921-f218-4790-96a7-78e0951d3415\">teeth from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"26\" data-uid=\"3592853e-7521-44bf-b2ef-060fa08729c1\">prehistoric and modern Americans and Asians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></li> <li>B. thousands of people who live in either the New or the Old World</li> <li>C. dental specimens from the majority of prehistoric Americans</li> <li>D. the eating habits of American and Asian populations</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"ec4c359c-852e-419f-bf96-dd9b2ac18cf7","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"methods","passagePhrase":"techniques"},{"uid":"d1c65701-bdf0-48f3-82be-177afa39a0e4","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"prehistoric migration","passagePhrase":"first entered"},{"uid":"4ca51a65-44cf-4965-adcf-47e061db1c02","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"blood-variants","passagePhrase":"interbred"},{"uid":"8a25f003-abf6-4161-87ed-8aa189708af7","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"results","passagePhrase":"found"},{"uid":"72635541-c535-4095-b89c-621a8527ca86","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"third group"},{"uid":"88421276-f9f4-4d7d-a546-6f3dc729f5cc","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The first, Paleo-lndian, wave"},{"uid":"a6d363de-5bdb-46c0-8ffa-6084a71955b0","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The second wave,"},{"uid":"349bda21-f82e-44a1-8427-8534a1adb22c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Further genetic evidence","passagePhrase":"other research support"},{"uid":"c6a968d2-d353-4780-ac52-42892fa04136","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"the three-wave theory","passagePhrase":"these conclusions"},{"uid":"8fe9a805-f65f-4aa5-be36-f92265658f31","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Dental evidence","passagePhrase":"study of teeth"},{"uid":"3592853e-7521-44bf-b2ef-060fa08729c1","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"prehistoric and modern Americans and Asians","passagePhrase":"New and Old World specimens"},{"uid":"e9227921-f218-4790-96a7-78e0951d3415","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"teeth from","passagePhrase":"incisor shoveling (a scooping out on one or both surfaces of the tooth)"}]},"reading_u2_159":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>Forests are one of the main elements of our natural heritage. The decline of Europe’s forests over the last decade and a half has led to an increasing awareness and understanding of the serious imbalances which threaten them. European countries are becoming increasingly concerned by major threats to European forests, threats which know no frontiers other than those of geography or climate: air pollution, soil deterioration, the increasing number of forest fires and sometimes even the mismanagement of our woodland and forest heritage. There has been a growing awareness of the need for countries to get together to co-ordinate their policies. In December 1990, Strasbourg hosted the first Ministerial Conference on the protection of Europe’s forests. The conference brought together 31 countries from both Western and Eastern Europe. The topics discussed included the coordinated study of the destruction of forests, as well as how to combat forest fires and the extension of European research programs on the forest ecosystem. The preparatory work for the conference had been undertaken at two meetings of experts. Their initial task was to decide which of the many forest problems of concern to Europe involved the largest number of countries and might be the subject of joint action. Those <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f5b1c928-9c02-4e4d-8bf9-bfdd8b03606f\" data-question=\"28\">confined to particular geographical areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, such as countries bordering the Mediterranean or the Nordic countries therefore had to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8184e112-4502-4ccb-b776-d129acd53642\" data-question=\"28\">discarded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. However, this does not mean that in future they will be ignored.</p><p>As a whole, European countries see forests as performing a triple function: biological, economic and recreational. The first is to act as a ‘green lung’ for our planet; by means of photosynthesis, forests produce oxygen through the transformation of solar energy, thus fulfilling what for humans is the essential role of an immense, non-polluting power plant. At the same time, forests provide raw materials for human activities through their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"161d165a-dead-43cc-954a-2eb78ba7ed0b\" data-question=\"29\">constantly renewed production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of wood. Finally, they offer those condemned to spend five days a week in an urban environment an unrivalled area of freedom to unwind and take part in a range of leisure activities, such as hunting, riding and hiking. The economic importance of forests has been understood since the dawn of man – wood was the first fuel. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df2e97d1-e36e-44c6-8503-73aa96c43d17\" data-question=\"30\">The other aspects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> have been recognised <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ff1354b6-be9c-4ff6-a793-1da7a297b625\" data-question=\"30\">only for a few centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> but they are becoming more and more important. Hence, there is a real concern throughout Europe about the damage to the forest environment which threatens these three basic roles.</p><p>The myth of the ‘natural’ forest has survived, yet <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"041150b1-4a32-493c-81c7-4c7cfb1ce55d\" data-question=\"31\">there are effectively no remaining<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> ‘primary’ forests in Europe. All European forests are artificial, having been adapted and exploited by man for thousands of years. This means that a forest policy is vital, that it must <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"51113eb1-dadb-47c6-84db-fe993123a493\" data-question=\"32\">transcend<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28b3fb05-3037-4441-97ce-0715ad9e2186\" data-question=\"32\">national frontiers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> and generations of people, and that it must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fca66c1a-7b9f-40d1-8cba-284e4ca9ddd3\" data-question=\"33\">allow for the inevitable changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> that take place in the forests, in needs, and hence in policy. The Strasbourg conference was one of the first events on such a scale to reach this conclusion. A general declaration was made that ‘a central place in any ecologically coherent forest policy must be given to continuity over time and to the possible effects of unforeseen events, to ensure that the full potential of these forests is maintained.</p><p>That general declaration was accompanied by six detailed resolutions to assist national policy-making. The first proposes the extension and systematisation of surveillance sites to monitor <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9169e12b-9a3e-4a8e-8e31-90987d377397\" data-question=\"34\">forest decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Forest decline is still poorly understood but leads to the loss of a high proportion of a tree’s needles or leaves. The entire continent and the majority of species are now affected: between 30% and 50% of the tree population. The condition appears to result from the cumulative effect of a number of factors, with atmospheric pollutants the principal culprits. Compounds of nitrogen and sulphur dioxide should be particularly closely watched. However, their effects are probably accentuated by climatic factors, such as drought and hard winters, or soil imbalances such as soil acidification, which damages the roots. The second resolution concentrates on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c6c9ef5-6879-49d6-97a3-51f4c5108697\" data-question=\"35\">the need to preserve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the genetic diversity of European forests. The aim is to reverse the decline in the number of tree species or at least to preserve the ‘genetic material’ of all of them. Although forest fires do not affect all of Europe to the same extent, the amount of damage caused the experts to propose as the third resolution that the Strasbourg conference consider the establishment of a European databank on the subject. All information used in the development of national preventative policies would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27741a37-b36f-41db-b8d6-cf3fe81811ef\" data-question=\"36\">become generally available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. The subject of the fourth resolution discussed by the ministers was mountain forests. In Europe, it is undoubtedly the mountain ecosystem which has changed most rapidly and is most at risk. A thinly scattered permanent population and development of leisure activities, particularly skiing, have resulted in significant long-term changes to the local ecosystems. Proposed developments include a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f1a657b-f619-4983-8c18-97fde9b571e6\" data-question=\"37\">preferential research program<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> on mountain forests. The fifth resolution relaunched the European research network on the physiology of trees, called Eurosilva. Eurosilva <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ce90a88-a082-4096-8df0-5af974b12b0f\" data-question=\"38\">should support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> joint European research on tree diseases and their physiological and biochemical aspects. Each country concerned could increase the number of scholarships and other financial support for doctoral theses and research projects in this area. Finally, the conference established the framework for a European research network on forest ecosystems. This would also involve <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"178c162c-5adb-441a-9323-622ce348d4c7\" data-question=\"39\">harmonising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> activities in individual countries as well as identifying a number of priority research topics relating to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d8f536a-0945-44c4-90e8-eb3e681aecde\" data-question=\"40\">protection of forests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. The Strasbourg conference’s main concern was to provide for the future. This was the initial motivation, one now shared by all 31 participants representing 31 European countries. Their final text commits them to on-going discussion between government representatives with responsibility for forests.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28705\" id=\"question-wrapper-28705\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Forest problems of Mediterranean countries are to be discussed at the next meeting of experts. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28706\" id=\"question-wrapper-28706\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Problems in Nordic countries were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8184e112-4502-4ccb-b776-d129acd53642\" data-question=\"28\">excluded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> because they are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f5b1c928-9c02-4e4d-8bf9-bfdd8b03606f\" data-question=\"28\">outside the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> European Economic Community. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28707\" id=\"question-wrapper-28707\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Forests are a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"161d165a-dead-43cc-954a-2eb78ba7ed0b\" data-question=\"29\">renewable source<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of raw material. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28708\" id=\"question-wrapper-28708\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df2e97d1-e36e-44c6-8503-73aa96c43d17\" data-question=\"30\">The biological functions of forests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> were recognised <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ff1354b6-be9c-4ff6-a793-1da7a297b625\" data-question=\"30\">only in the twentieth century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28709\" id=\"question-wrapper-28709\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Natural forests <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"041150b1-4a32-493c-81c7-4c7cfb1ce55d\" data-question=\"31\">still exist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in parts of Europe. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28710\" id=\"question-wrapper-28710\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Forest policy should <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"51113eb1-dadb-47c6-84db-fe993123a493\" data-question=\"32\">be limited by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28b3fb05-3037-4441-97ce-0715ad9e2186\" data-question=\"32\">national boundaries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28711\" id=\"question-wrapper-28711\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Strasbourg conference decided that a forest policy must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fca66c1a-7b9f-40d1-8cba-284e4ca9ddd3\" data-question=\"33\">allow for the possibility of change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following statements issued by the conference.<br>Which <strong>SIX</strong> of the following statements. A-J, refer to the resolutions that were issued?</p><p>Match the statements with the appropriate resolutions (Questions 34-39).</p><ul><li><strong>A</strong> All kinds of species of trees <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c6c9ef5-6879-49d6-97a3-51f4c5108697\" data-question=\"35\">should be preserved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li><li><strong>B</strong> Fragile mountain forests <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f1a657b-f619-4983-8c18-97fde9b571e6\" data-question=\"37\">should be given priority in research programs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</li><li><strong>C</strong> The surviving natural forests of Europe do not need priority treatment.</li><li><strong>D</strong> Research is to be better <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"178c162c-5adb-441a-9323-622ce348d4c7\" data-question=\"39\">co-ordinate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> throughout Europe.</li><li><strong>E</strong> Information on forest fires should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27741a37-b36f-41db-b8d6-cf3fe81811ef\" data-question=\"36\">be collected and shared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</li><li><strong>F</strong> Loss Of leaves from trees should be more extensively and carefully monitored.</li><li><strong>G</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ce90a88-a082-4096-8df0-5af974b12b0f\" data-question=\"38\">Resources should be allocated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> to research into tree diseases.</li><li><strong>H</strong> Skiing should be encouraged in thinly populated areas.</li><li><strong>I</strong> Soil imbalances such as acidification should be treated with compounds of nitrogen and sulphur.</li><li><strong>J</strong> Information is to be systematically gathered on any <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9169e12b-9a3e-4a8e-8e31-90987d377397\" data-question=\"34\">decline in the condition of forests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28712\" id=\"question-wrapper-28712\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Resolution 1 </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">J</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28713\" id=\"question-wrapper-28713\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Resolution 2 </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28714\" id=\"question-wrapper-28714\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Resolution 3 </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28715\" id=\"question-wrapper-28715\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Resolution 4 </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28716\" id=\"question-wrapper-28716\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Resolution 5 </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28717\" id=\"question-wrapper-28717\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Resolution 6 </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter, A. B, C or D. Write the correct letter in box 40 on your answer sheet</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28718\" id=\"question-wrapper-28718\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the best title for Reading Passage 3? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The biological, economic and recreational role of forests</li> <li>B. Plans to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d8f536a-0945-44c4-90e8-eb3e681aecde\" data-question=\"40\">protect the forests of Europe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></li> <li>C. The priority of European research into ecosystems</li> <li>D. Proposals for a world-wide policy on forest management</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"8184e112-4502-4ccb-b776-d129acd53642","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"excluded","passagePhrase":"discarded"},{"uid":"161d165a-dead-43cc-954a-2eb78ba7ed0b","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"renewable source","passagePhrase":"constantly renewed production"},{"uid":"df2e97d1-e36e-44c6-8503-73aa96c43d17","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"The biological functions of forests","passagePhrase":"The other aspects"},{"uid":"28b3fb05-3037-4441-97ce-0715ad9e2186","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"national boundaries","passagePhrase":"national frontiers"},{"uid":"fca66c1a-7b9f-40d1-8cba-284e4ca9ddd3","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"allow for the possibility of change","passagePhrase":"allow for the inevitable changes"},{"uid":"9169e12b-9a3e-4a8e-8e31-90987d377397","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"decline in the condition of forests","passagePhrase":"forest decline"},{"uid":"4c6c9ef5-6879-49d6-97a3-51f4c5108697","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"should be preserved","passagePhrase":"the need to preserve"},{"uid":"27741a37-b36f-41db-b8d6-cf3fe81811ef","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"be collected and shared","passagePhrase":"become generally available"},{"uid":"7f1a657b-f619-4983-8c18-97fde9b571e6","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"should be given priority in research programs","passagePhrase":"preferential research program"},{"uid":"5ce90a88-a082-4096-8df0-5af974b12b0f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"Resources should be allocated","passagePhrase":"should support"},{"uid":"178c162c-5adb-441a-9323-622ce348d4c7","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"co-ordinate","passagePhrase":"harmonising"},{"uid":"2d8f536a-0945-44c4-90e8-eb3e681aecde","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"protect the forests of Europe","passagePhrase":"protection of forests"}]},"reading_u2_160":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Pulling Strings to Build Pyramids</strong></p><p>The pyramids of Egypt were built more than three thousand years ago, and no one knows how. The conventional picture is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5bc679f6-7354-412d-bdcb-9aa1c591262e\" data-question=\"1\">tens of thousands of slaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff4e9c39-c017-4983-a191-340c859303cc\" data-question=\"1\">dragged stones on sledges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. But there is no evidence to back this up. Now a Californian software consultant called Maureen Clemmons has suggested that kites might have been involved. While perusing <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9a2020ae-76a2-4562-9bbe-58da828def81\" data-question=\"2\">a book on the monuments of Egypt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, she noticed a hieroglyph that showed a row of men standing in odd postures. They were holding what looked like ropes that led, via some kind of mechanical system, to a giant bird in the sky. She wondered if perhaps the bird was actually a giant kite, and the men were using it to lift a heavy object.</p><p>Intrigued, Clemmons contacted Morteza Gharib, aeronautics professor at the California Institute of Technology. He was fascinated by the idea. ‘Coming from Iran, I have a keen interest in Middle Eastern science/ he says. He too was puzzled by the picture that had sparked Clemmons’s interest. The object in the sky apparently had wings far too short and wide for a bird. ‘The possibility certainly existed that it was a kite,’ he says. And since he needed a summer project for his student Emilio Graff, investigating the possibility of using kites as heavy lifters seemed like a good idea.</p><p>Gharib and Graff set themselves the task of raising a 4.5-metre stone column from horizontal to vertical, using no source of energy except the wind. Their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"911d2e53-f083-4475-aa0c-367ea3656019\" data-question=\"4\">initial calculations and scale-model wind-tunnel experiments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> convinced them they wouldn’t need a strong wind to lift the 33.5-tonne column. Even a modest force, if sustained over a long time, would do. The key was to use a pulley system that would magnify the applied force. So they rigged up a tent-shaped scaffold directly above the tip of the horizontal column, with pulleys suspended from the scaffold’s apex. The idea was that as one end of the column rose, the base would roll across the ground on a trolley.</p><p>Earlier this year, the team put Clemmons’s unlikely theory to the test, using a 40-square- metre rectangular nylon sail. The kite lifted the column clean off the ground. ‘We were absolutely stunned,’ Gharib says. The instant the sail opened into the wind, a huge force was generated and the column was raised to the vertical in a mere 40 seconds.’</p><p>The wind was blowing at a gentle 16 to 20 kilometres an hour, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2181bd6f-bfee-49e4-b96e-76a82eeba18a\" data-question=\"5\">little more than half what they thought would be needed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. What they had failed to reckon with was what happened when the kite was opened. There was a huge initial force – five times larger than the steady state force,’ Gharib says. This jerk meant that kites could lift huge weights, Gharib realised. Even a 300-tonne column could have been lifted to the vertical with 40 or so men and four or five sails. So Clemmons was right: the pyramid, builders could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f66660ba-b2bb-44f8-b7d6-1cbae73d8b57\" data-question=\"7\">have used kites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4ef6785-4768-4ce5-864d-09bc3b643882\" data-question=\"7\">lift<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bcd8449a-7480-45b6-909c-090e0148ffbc\" data-question=\"7\">massive stones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> into place. Whether they actually did is another matter,’ Gharib says.</p><p>There are no pictures showing the construction of the pyramids, so there is no way to tell what really happened. The evidence for using kites to move large stones is no better or worse than the evidence for the brute force method,’ Gharib says.</p><p>Indeed, the experiments have left many specialists unconvinced. The evidence for kite-lifting is non-existent,’ says Willeke Wendrich, an associate professor of Egyptology at the University of California, Los Angeles. Others feel there is more of a case for the theory. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ede4969e-8b74-46ac-b431-a8b5f6edfd76\" data-question=\"10\">Harnessing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> the wind would not have been a problem for accomplished sailors like the Egyptians. And they are known to have used wooden pulleys, which could have been made strong enough to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a39da103-5da1-4d7b-958a-eaa0272511a4\" data-question=\"8\">bear the weight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of massive blocks of stone. In addition, there is some physical evidence that the ancient Egyptians were interested in flight. A wooden artefact found on the step pyramid at Saqqara <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2ad1936-f6ef-4295-903a-beb9b373d6bc\" data-question=\"11\">looks uncannily like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a modem glider. Although it dates from several hundred years after the building of the pyramids, its sophistication suggests that the Egyptians <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d5c0c22-6e07-46ad-8895-2f39f247fac5\" data-question=\"12\">might have been developing ideas of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> flight for a long time. And other ancient civilisations certainly knew about kites; as early as 1250 BC, the Chinese were using them to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ba0c4b2-15b8-4509-a741-374a966db32a\" data-question=\"13\">deliver<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> messages and dump flaming debris on their foes.</p><p>The experiments might even have practical uses nowadays. There are plenty of places around the globe where people have no access to heavy machinery, but do know how to deal with wind, sailing and basic mechanical principles. Gharib has already been contacted by a civil engineer in Nicaragua, who wants to put up buildings with adobe roofs supported by concrete arches on a site that heavy equipment can’t reach. His idea is to build the arches horizontally, then lift them into place using kites. We’ve given him some design hints,’ says Gharib. We’re just waiting for him to report back.’ So whether they were actually used to build the pyramids or not, it seems that kites may make sensible construction tools in the 21st century AD.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statement with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28719\" id=\"question-wrapper-28719\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is generally believed that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5bc679f6-7354-412d-bdcb-9aa1c591262e\" data-question=\"1\">large numbers of people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff4e9c39-c017-4983-a191-340c859303cc\" data-question=\"1\">needed to build<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> the pyramids. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28720\" id=\"question-wrapper-28720\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Clemmons found a strange hieroglyph <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9a2020ae-76a2-4562-9bbe-58da828def81\" data-question=\"2\">on the wall of an Egyptian monument<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28721\" id=\"question-wrapper-28721\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Gharib had previously done experiments on bird flight. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28722\" id=\"question-wrapper-28722\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Gharib and Graff <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"911d2e53-f083-4475-aa0c-367ea3656019\" data-question=\"4\">tested their theory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> before applying it. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28723\" id=\"question-wrapper-28723\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The success of the actual experiment was due to the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2181bd6f-bfee-49e4-b96e-76a82eeba18a\" data-question=\"5\">high speed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of the wind. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28724\" id=\"question-wrapper-28724\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> They found that, as the kite flew higher, the wind force got stronger. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28725\" id=\"question-wrapper-28725\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The team decided that it was possible <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f66660ba-b2bb-44f8-b7d6-1cbae73d8b57\" data-question=\"7\">to use kites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4ef6785-4768-4ce5-864d-09bc3b643882\" data-question=\"7\">raise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bcd8449a-7480-45b6-909c-090e0148ffbc\" data-question=\"7\">very heavy stones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below. Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>Addition evidence for theory of kite lifting</strong></p><p>The Egyptians had (8)………………, which could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a39da103-5da1-4d7b-958a-eaa0272511a4\" data-question=\"8\">lift large pieces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of (9)……………….., and they knew how to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ede4969e-8b74-46ac-b431-a8b5f6edfd76\" data-question=\"10\">use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> the energy of the wind from their skill as (10)………………. The discovery on one pyramid of an object which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2ad1936-f6ef-4295-903a-beb9b373d6bc\" data-question=\"11\">resembled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a (11)…………….. suggests they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d5c0c22-6e07-46ad-8895-2f39f247fac5\" data-question=\"12\">may have experimented with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12) …………… In addition, over two thousand years ago kites used in china as weapons, as well as for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ba0c4b2-15b8-4509-a741-374a966db32a\" data-question=\"13\">sending<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13)………………</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28726\" id=\"question-wrapper-28726\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(WOODEN) PULLEYS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28727\" id=\"question-wrapper-28727\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STONE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28728\" id=\"question-wrapper-28728\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(ACCOMPLISHED) SAILORS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28729\" id=\"question-wrapper-28729\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(MODERN) GLIDER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28730\" id=\"question-wrapper-28730\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FLIGHT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28731\" id=\"question-wrapper-28731\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MESSAGES</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"5bc679f6-7354-412d-bdcb-9aa1c591262e","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"large numbers of people","passagePhrase":"tens of thousands of slaves"},{"uid":"ff4e9c39-c017-4983-a191-340c859303cc","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"needed to build","passagePhrase":"dragged stones on sledges"},{"uid":"911d2e53-f083-4475-aa0c-367ea3656019","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"tested their theory","passagePhrase":"initial calculations and scale-model wind-tunnel experiments"},{"uid":"f66660ba-b2bb-44f8-b7d6-1cbae73d8b57","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"to use kites","passagePhrase":"have used kites"},{"uid":"b4ef6785-4768-4ce5-864d-09bc3b643882","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"raise","passagePhrase":"lift"},{"uid":"bcd8449a-7480-45b6-909c-090e0148ffbc","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"very heavy stones","passagePhrase":"massive stones"},{"uid":"ede4969e-8b74-46ac-b431-a8b5f6edfd76","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"use","passagePhrase":"Harnessing"},{"uid":"a39da103-5da1-4d7b-958a-eaa0272511a4","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"lift large pieces","passagePhrase":"bear the weight"},{"uid":"d2ad1936-f6ef-4295-903a-beb9b373d6bc","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"resembled","passagePhrase":"looks uncannily like"},{"uid":"5d5c0c22-6e07-46ad-8895-2f39f247fac5","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"may have experimented with","passagePhrase":"might have been developing ideas of"},{"uid":"6ba0c4b2-15b8-4509-a741-374a966db32a","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"sending","passagePhrase":"deliver"}]},"reading_u2_161":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Endless Harvest</strong></p><p>More than two hundred years ago, Russian explorers and fur hunters landed on the Aleutian Islands, a volcanic archipelago in the North Pacific, and learned of <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0e106e6f-a8ba-4520-98e4-c9780356e899\" data-question=\"14\">a land mass that lay farther to the north<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. The islands’ native inhabitants <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0e106e6f-a8ba-4520-98e4-c9780356e899\" data-question=\"14\">called this land mass<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> Aleyska, the ‘Great Land’; today, we know it as Alaska.</p><p>The forty-ninth state to join the United States of America (in 1959), Alaska is fully one-fifth the size of the mainland 48 states combined. It shares, with Canada, the second longest river system in North America and has over half the coastline of the United States. The rivers feed into the Bering Sea and Gulf of Alaska – cold, nutrient-rich waters which support tens of millions of seabirds, and over 400 species of fish, shellfish, crustaceans, and molluscs. Taking advantage of this rich bounty, Alaska’s commercial fisheries have developed into some of the largest in the world.</p><p>According to the Alaska Department of Fish and Game (ADF&amp;G), Alaska’s commercial fisheries landed hundreds of thousands of tonnes of shellfish and herring, and well over a million tonnes of groundfish (cod, sole, perch and pollock) in 2000. The true cultural heart and soul of Alaska’s fisheries, however, is salmon. ‘Salmon,’ notes writer Susan Ewing in The Great Alaska Nature Factbook, ‘pump through Alaska like blood through a heart, bringing rhythmic, circulating nourishment to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7792597e-404e-436f-b784-07acc62c4370\" data-question=\"16\">land, animals and people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.’ The ‘predictable abundance of salmon allowed some native cultures to flourish,’ and ‘dying spawners feed bears, eagles, other animals, and ultimately the soil itself.’ All five species of Pacific salmon – chinook, or king; chum, or dog; coho, or silver; sockeye, or red; and pink, or humpback – spawn in Alaskan waters, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"662f3361-beee-4356-9b3e-ee461c272f3a\" data-question=\"17\">90% of all Pacific salmon commercially caught<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in North America are produced there. Indeed, if Alaska was an independent nation, it would be tire largest producer of wild salmon in the world. During 2000, commercial catches of Pacific salmon in Alaska <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"49dde68e-cda4-44e2-a274-caf857296d15\" data-question=\"18\">exceeded 320,000 tonnes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, with an ex-vessel value of over $260 million.</p><p>Catches have not always been so healthy. Between 1940 and 1959, overfishing led to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3920c45b-dc7f-4eaf-9780-7822a71ff7b9\" data-question=\"19\">crashes in salmon populations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> so severe that in 1953 Alaska was declared a federal disaster area. With the onset of statehood, however, the State of Alaska took over management of its own fisheries, guided by a state constitution which mandates that Alaska’s natural resources be managed on a sustainable basis. At that time, statewide harvests totalled around 25 million salmon. Over the next few decades average catches steadily increased as a result of this policy of sustainable management, until, during the 1990s, annual harvests were <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"00e3dafc-219c-4be0-8920-6b1df32721d0\" data-question=\"20\">well in excess of 100 million<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, several occasions over 200 million fish.</p><p>The primary reason for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b68d3ad3-24b0-454f-831e-5992729da049\" data-question=\"23\">such increases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> is what is known as ‘In-Season Abundance-Based Management’. There are biologists throughout the state constantly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78de9185-fa4e-4a74-ab48-5e6626d042ca\" data-question=\"21\">monitoring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> adult fish as they show up to spawn. The biologists sit in streamside counting towers, study sonar, watch from aeroplanes, and talk to fishermen. The salmon season in Alaska is not pre-set. The fishermen know the approximate time of year when they will be allowed to fish, but on any given day, one or more field biologists in a particular area can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b05b40ef-c454-4379-9cff-d3f174786de8\" data-question=\"22\">put a halt to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> fishing. Even sport fishing can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b05b40ef-c454-4379-9cff-d3f174786de8\" data-question=\"22\">be brought to a halt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. It is this management mechanism <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"630183e7-0220-439d-8e51-fa69343b027a\" data-question=\"21\">that has allowed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> Alaska salmon stocks — and, accordingly, Alaska salmon fisheries — to prosper, even as salmon populations in the rest of the United States are increasingly considered threatened or even endangered.</p><p>In 1999, the Marine Stewardship Council (MSC) commissioned a review of the Alaska salmon fishery. The Council, which was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"694dc55c-e8d4-4fe2-8e36-15036ada9830\" data-question=\"24\">founded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in 1996, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"900626f7-5f0c-49f9-8c52-60e05be5d37d\" data-question=\"24\">certifies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> fisheries that meet high environmental standards, enabling them to use a label that recognises their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ca6f7ab-1f0e-409a-8e4a-ed1c939a7618\" data-question=\"24\">environmental responsibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. The MSC has established a set of criteria by which commercial fisheries can be judged. Recognising the potential benefits of being identified as environmentally responsible, fisheries approach the Council requesting to undergo the certification process. The MSC then appoints a certification committee, composed of a panel of fisheries experts, which gathers information and opinions from fishermen, biologists, government officials, industry representatives, non-governmental organisations and others.</p><p>Some observers thought the Alaska salmon fisheries would not have any chance of certification when, in the months leading up to MSC’s final decision, salmon runs throughout western Alaska completely collapsed. In the Yukon and Kuskokwim rivers, chinook and chum runs were probably the poorest since statehood; subsistence communities throughout the region, who normally have priority over commercial fishing, were devastated.</p><p>The crisis was completely unexpected, but researchers believe it had nothing to do with impacts of fisheries. Rather, they contend, it was almost certainly the result of climatic shifts, prompted in part by cumulative effects of the el nino/la nina phenomenon on Pacific Ocean temperatures, culminating in a harsh winter in which huge numbers of salmon eggs were frozen. It could have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8d0994d2-42c7-4006-9ee2-cc7c03d911fb\" data-question=\"25\">meant the end<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> as far as the certification process was concerned. However, the state reacted quickly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ac6c06a-6b30-4545-bab2-5bad62e80c88\" data-question=\"25\">closing down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> all fisheries, even those necessary for subsistence purposes.</p><p>In September 2000, MSC announced that the Alaska salmon fisheries qualified for certification. Seven companies producing Alaska salmon were immediately <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e416654a-8d1a-4372-bd65-bf28adc8b1ec\" data-question=\"26\">granted permission to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4922ef4-a977-4989-86fa-384394472adc\" data-question=\"26\">display the MSC logo on their products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Certification is for an initial period of five years, with an annual review to ensure that the fishery is continuing to meet the required standards.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2? In boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28732\" id=\"question-wrapper-28732\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The inhabitants of the Aleutian islands <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0e106e6f-a8ba-4520-98e4-c9780356e899\" data-question=\"14\">renamed their islands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> Aleyska </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28733\" id=\"question-wrapper-28733\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Alaska’s fisheries are owned by some of the world’s largest companies. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28734\" id=\"question-wrapper-28734\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7792597e-404e-436f-b784-07acc62c4370\" data-question=\"16\">Life in Alaska<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> is dependent on salmon. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28735\" id=\"question-wrapper-28735\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Ninety per cent of all Pacific salmon caught are sockeye or pink salmon. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28736\" id=\"question-wrapper-28736\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"49dde68e-cda4-44e2-a274-caf857296d15\" data-question=\"18\">More than 320,000 tonnes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of salmon were caught in Alaska in 2000. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28737\" id=\"question-wrapper-28737\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Between 1940 and 1959, there was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3920c45b-dc7f-4eaf-9780-7822a71ff7b9\" data-question=\"19\">a sharp decrease in Alaska’s salmon population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28738\" id=\"question-wrapper-28738\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> During the 1990s, the average number of salmon caught each year <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"00e3dafc-219c-4be0-8920-6b1df32721d0\" data-question=\"20\">was 100 million<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-K. below. Write the correct letter, A-K in boxes 21-26 on your answer sheet.</p><ul><li><strong>A</strong> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"900626f7-5f0c-49f9-8c52-60e05be5d37d\" data-question=\"24\">recognise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> fisheries that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ca6f7ab-1f0e-409a-8e4a-ed1c939a7618\" data-question=\"24\">care for the environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</li><li><strong>B</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b68d3ad3-24b0-454f-831e-5992729da049\" data-question=\"23\">to be successful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</li><li><strong>C</strong> to stop fish from spawning</li><li><strong>D</strong> to set up environmental protection laws.</li><li><strong>E</strong> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b05b40ef-c454-4379-9cff-d3f174786de8\" data-question=\"22\">stop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> people fishing for sport.</li><li><strong>F</strong> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4922ef4-a977-4989-86fa-384394472adc\" data-question=\"26\">label their products using the MSC logo<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</li><li><strong>G</strong> to ensure that fish numbers are sufficient to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"630183e7-0220-439d-8e51-fa69343b027a\" data-question=\"21\">permit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> fishing.</li><li><strong>H</strong> to assist the subsistence communities in the region.</li><li><strong>I</strong> to freeze a huge number of salmon eggs.</li><li><strong>J</strong> to deny certification to the Alaska fisheries.</li><li><strong>K</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ac6c06a-6b30-4545-bab2-5bad62e80c88\" data-question=\"25\">to close down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> all-fisheries.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28739\" id=\"question-wrapper-28739\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In Alaska, biologists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78de9185-fa4e-4a74-ab48-5e6626d042ca\" data-question=\"21\">keep a check on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> adult fish </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28740\" id=\"question-wrapper-28740\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Biologists have the authority </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28741\" id=\"question-wrapper-28741\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In-Season Abundance-Based Management has allowed the Alaska salmon fisheries </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28742\" id=\"question-wrapper-28742\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Marine Stewardship Council (MSC) was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"694dc55c-e8d4-4fe2-8e36-15036ada9830\" data-question=\"24\">established<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28743\" id=\"question-wrapper-28743\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> As a result of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8d0994d2-42c7-4006-9ee2-cc7c03d911fb\" data-question=\"25\">collapse of the salmon runs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> in 1999, the state decided </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">K</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28744\" id=\"question-wrapper-28744\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In September 2000, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e416654a-8d1a-4372-bd65-bf28adc8b1ec\" data-question=\"26\">the MSC allowed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> seven Alaska salmon companies </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7792597e-404e-436f-b784-07acc62c4370","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Life in Alaska","passagePhrase":"land, animals and people"},{"uid":"662f3361-beee-4356-9b3e-ee461c272f3a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"90% of all Pacific salmon commercially caught"},{"uid":"49dde68e-cda4-44e2-a274-caf857296d15","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"More than 320,000 tonnes","passagePhrase":"exceeded 320,000 tonnes"},{"uid":"3920c45b-dc7f-4eaf-9780-7822a71ff7b9","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"a sharp decrease in Alaska’s salmon population","passagePhrase":"crashes in salmon populations"},{"uid":"b68d3ad3-24b0-454f-831e-5992729da049","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"to be successful","passagePhrase":"such increases"},{"uid":"78de9185-fa4e-4a74-ab48-5e6626d042ca","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"keep a check on","passagePhrase":"monitoring"},{"uid":"b05b40ef-c454-4379-9cff-d3f174786de8","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"stop","passagePhrase":"put a halt to ... be brought to a halt"},{"uid":"630183e7-0220-439d-8e51-fa69343b027a","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"permit","passagePhrase":"that has allowed"},{"uid":"694dc55c-e8d4-4fe2-8e36-15036ada9830","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"established","passagePhrase":"founded"},{"uid":"900626f7-5f0c-49f9-8c52-60e05be5d37d","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"recognise","passagePhrase":"certifies"},{"uid":"2ca6f7ab-1f0e-409a-8e4a-ed1c939a7618","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"care for the environment","passagePhrase":"environmental responsibility"},{"uid":"8d0994d2-42c7-4006-9ee2-cc7c03d911fb","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"collapse of the salmon runs","passagePhrase":"meant the end"},{"uid":"8ac6c06a-6b30-4545-bab2-5bad62e80c88","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"to close down","passagePhrase":"closing down"},{"uid":"e416654a-8d1a-4372-bd65-bf28adc8b1ec","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"the MSC allowed","passagePhrase":"granted permission to"},{"uid":"c4922ef4-a977-4989-86fa-384394472adc","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"label their products using the MSC logo","passagePhrase":"display the MSC logo on their products"}]},"reading_u2_162":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Effects of Noise</strong></p><p>In general, it is plausible to suppose that we should prefer peace and quiet to noise. And yet most of us have had the experience of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"31ac2769-446b-489c-9248-33da4e1ae3c8\" data-question=\"27\">having to adjust to sleeping in the mountains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> or the countryside because it was initially ‘too quiet’, an experience that suggests that humans are capable of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"32e18aa8-a449-4e6c-9203-ee6f03dae18f\" data-question=\"27\">adapting to a wide range of noise levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Research supports this view. For example, Glass and Singer (1972) exposed people to short bursts of very loud noise and then measured their ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02b7eae0-c365-4920-bef9-f26f2acca8bc\" data-question=\"35\">work out problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and their physiological reactions to the noise. The noise was quite disruptive at first, but after about four minutes the subjects were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd33ae39-11ee-4ccd-bc0e-243ee94a5e08\" data-question=\"28\">doing just as well on their tasks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> as control subjects who were not exposed to noise. Their physiological arousal also declined quickly to the same levels as those of the control subjects.</p><p>But there are limits to adaptation and loud noise <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"adb43da2-ea12-4970-9259-5be2df707c03\" data-question=\"29\">becomes more troublesome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> if the person is required to concentrate on more than one task. For example, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"30b33f47-5076-4b45-9d32-0491af5ce288\" data-question=\"38\">high noise levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d295fd5-8fad-4b38-ab2d-6b90c6be5827\" data-question=\"39\">interfered with the performance of subjects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> who were required to monitor three dials <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ce9656f-74ee-4191-b087-a02b63d9a5ec\" data-question=\"39\">at a time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, a task not unlike that of an aeroplane pilot or an air-traffic controller (Broadbent, 1957). Similarly, noise did not affect a subject’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e52a4a3c-659e-4b6e-ac04-33d41868509a\" data-question=\"40\">ability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to track a moving line with a steering wheel, but it did interfere with the subject’s ability to repeat numbers while tracking (Finkelman and Glass, 1970).</p><p>Probably the most significant finding from research on noise is that its predictability is more important than how loud it is. We are much more able to ‘tune out’ chronic background noise, even if it is quite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5209c022-7fb5-46db-be46-f190cb7b9ec0\" data-question=\"30\">loud<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, than to work under circumstances with unexpected <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3abb0eb-a961-4981-87c3-1ffe5355cb81\" data-question=\"30\">intrusions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of noise. In the Glass and Singer study, in which subjects were exposed to bursts of noise as they worked on a task, some subjects heard loud bursts and others heard soft bursts. For some subjects, the bursts were spaced exactly one minute apart (predictable noise); others <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4abb68c-4381-492e-8e66-b7a0b8437299\" data-question=\"31\">heard<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> the same amount of noise overall, but the bursts occurred at random intervals (unpredictable noise). Subjects reported finding the predictable and unpredictable noise equally annoying, and all subjects performed at about the same level <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6b08ba0b-b4fb-46d5-b29d-4f22dee01beb\" data-question=\"32\">during the noise portion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of the experiment. But the different noise conditions had quite different after-effects when the subjects were required to proofread written material under conditions of no noise. As shown in Table 1 the unpredictable noise <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b402f0b2-a4d7-4fcf-a078-c59f534e57cb\" data-question=\"33\">produced more errors in the later proofreading task than predictable noise; and soft, unpredictable noise actually produced slightly more errors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> on this task than the loud, predictable noise.</p><p>Apparently, unpredictable noise produces more fatigue than predictable noise, but it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"37dcd7af-5437-4cfa-bf2f-0fe4ae3a279d\" data-question=\"34\">takes a while<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> for this fatigue to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c598f82b-37d4-424d-9302-1a2fefe05ad5\" data-question=\"34\">take its toll on performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</p><p>Predictability is not the only variable that reduces or eliminates the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c84611c-764b-43c4-b989-a05a09fa43e9\" data-question=\"37\">negative effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> of noise. Another is control. If the individual knows that he or she can control the noise, this seems to eliminate both its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c84611c-764b-43c4-b989-a05a09fa43e9\" data-question=\"37\">negative effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> at the time and its after-effects. This is true even if the individual never actually exercises his or her option to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eb621c28-0a22-4a64-8728-3040ae8be8c6\" data-question=\"37\">turn the noise off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> (Glass and Singer, 1972). Just the knowledge that one has control is sufficient.</p><p>The studies discussed so far exposed people to noise for only short periods and only transient effects were studied. But the major worry about noisy environments is that living day after day with chronic noise may produce serious, lasting effects. One study, suggesting that this worry is a realistic one, compared elementary school pupils who attended schools near Los Angeles’s busiest airport with students who attended schools in quiet neighbourhoods (Cohen et al., 1980). It was found that children from the noisy schools had higher blood pressure and were more easily distracted than those who attended the quiet schools. Moreover, there was no evidence of adaptability to the noise. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71b60005-8928-4ddd-bca1-1211b792049e\" data-question=\"36\">In fact, the longer the children had attended the noisy schools, the more distractible they became. The effects also seem to be long lasting.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> A follow-up study showed that children who were moved to less noisy classrooms still showed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b7c1424-72a5-4766-a9b8-1250bbce8d8a\" data-question=\"36\">greater distractibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> one year later than students who had always been in the quiet schools (Cohen et al, 1981). It should be noted that the two groups of children had been carefully matched by the investigators so that they were comparable in age, ethnicity, race, and social class.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28745\" id=\"question-wrapper-28745\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer suggests that people may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"31ac2769-446b-489c-9248-33da4e1ae3c8\" data-question=\"27\">have difficulty sleeping in the mountains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> because </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. humans do not prefer peace and quiet to noise.</li> <li>B. they may be exposed to short bursts of very strange sounds.</li> <li>C. humans prefer to hear a certain amount of noise while they sleep.</li> <li>D. they may have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"32e18aa8-a449-4e6c-9203-ee6f03dae18f\" data-question=\"27\">adapted to a higher noise level in the city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28746\" id=\"question-wrapper-28746\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In noise experiments, Glass and Singer found that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. problem-solving is much easier under quiet conditions.</li> <li>B. physiological arousal prevents the ability to work.</li> <li>C. bursts of noise do not seriously disrupt <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd33ae39-11ee-4ccd-bc0e-243ee94a5e08\" data-question=\"28\">problem-solving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in the long term.</li> <li>D. the physiological arousal of control subjects declined quickly.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28747\" id=\"question-wrapper-28747\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Researchers discovered that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c029cdd5-76fd-4d5c-a75f-f7167293ab04\" data-question=\"29\">high noise levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> are not likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"adb43da2-ea12-4970-9259-5be2df707c03\" data-question=\"29\">interfere with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. successful performance of a single task.</li> <li>B. tasks of pilots or air traffic controllers.</li> <li>C. ability to repeal numbers while tracking moving lines.</li> <li>D. ability to monitor three dials at once.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary using the list of words and phrases, A-J. below. Write the correct letter A-J in boxes 30-34 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>NB You may use any letter more than once.</strong></p><p>Glass and Singer (1972) showed that situations in which there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5209c022-7fb5-46db-be46-f190cb7b9ec0\" data-question=\"30\">intense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> noise have less effect on performance than circumstances in which (30)……………………….. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3abb0eb-a961-4981-87c3-1ffe5355cb81\" data-question=\"30\">noise occurs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Subjects were divided into groups to perform a task. Some heard loud bursts of noise, others sort. For some subjects, the noise was predictable, while for others its occurrence was random. All groups were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4abb68c-4381-492e-8e66-b7a0b8437299\" data-question=\"31\">exposed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> (31)……………………. noise. The predictable noise group (32)……………………. the unpredictable noise group <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6b08ba0b-b4fb-46d5-b29d-4f22dee01beb\" data-question=\"32\">on this task<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. In the second part of the experiment, the four groups were given a proofreading task to complete under conditions of no noise. They were required to check written material for errors. The group which had been exposed to unpredictable noise (33)……………… the group which had been exposed to predictable noise. The group which had been exposed to loud predictable noise performed better than those who” had heard soft, unpredictable bursts. The results suggest that (34)………………………… noise produces fatigue but that this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c598f82b-37d4-424d-9302-1a2fefe05ad5\" data-question=\"34\">manifests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> itself later.</p><ul><li><strong>A</strong> no control over</li><li><strong>B</strong> unexpected</li><li><strong>C</strong> intense</li><li><strong>D</strong> the same amount of</li><li><strong>E</strong> performed better than</li><li><strong>F</strong> performed at about the same level as</li><li><strong>G</strong> no</li><li><strong>H</strong> showed more irritation than</li><li><strong>I</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b402f0b2-a4d7-4fcf-a078-c59f534e57cb\" data-question=\"33\">made more mistakes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> than</li><li><strong>J</strong> different types of</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28748\" id=\"question-wrapper-28748\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28749\" id=\"question-wrapper-28749\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28750\" id=\"question-wrapper-28750\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28751\" id=\"question-wrapper-28751\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28752\" id=\"question-wrapper-28752\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following statements (Questions 35-40) and the list of researchers below. Match each statement with the correct researcher(s), A-E. Write the correct letter A-E, in boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet.</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p><p><strong>List of Researchers</strong></p><ul><li><strong>A</strong> Glass and Singer</li><li><strong>B</strong> Broadbent</li><li><strong>C</strong> Finke man and Glass</li><li><strong>D</strong> Cohen et al.</li><li><strong>E</strong> None of the above</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28753\" id=\"question-wrapper-28753\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Subjects exposed to noise find it difficult at first to concentrate on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02b7eae0-c365-4920-bef9-f26f2acca8bc\" data-question=\"35\">problem-solving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> tasks. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28754\" id=\"question-wrapper-28754\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71b60005-8928-4ddd-bca1-1211b792049e\" data-question=\"36\">Long-term exposure to noise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> can produce <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b7c1424-72a5-4766-a9b8-1250bbce8d8a\" data-question=\"36\">changes in behavior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> which can still be observed a year later. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28755\" id=\"question-wrapper-28755\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c84611c-764b-43c4-b989-a05a09fa43e9\" data-question=\"37\">problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> associated with exposure to noise do not arise if the subject knows they can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eb621c28-0a22-4a64-8728-3040ae8be8c6\" data-question=\"37\">make it stop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28756\" id=\"question-wrapper-28756\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Exposure to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"30b33f47-5076-4b45-9d32-0491af5ce288\" data-question=\"38\">high-pitched noise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> results in more errors than exposure to low-pitched noise </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28757\" id=\"question-wrapper-28757\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d295fd5-8fad-4b38-ab2d-6b90c6be5827\" data-question=\"39\">Subjects find it difficult to perform<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> three tasks <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ce9656f-74ee-4191-b087-a02b63d9a5ec\" data-question=\"39\">at the same time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> when exposed to noise </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28758\" id=\"question-wrapper-28758\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Noise affects a subject’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e52a4a3c-659e-4b6e-ac04-33d41868509a\" data-question=\"40\">capacity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to repeat numbers while carrying out another task. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"31ac2769-446b-489c-9248-33da4e1ae3c8","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"have difficulty sleeping in the mountains","passagePhrase":"having to adjust to sleeping in the mountains"},{"uid":"32e18aa8-a449-4e6c-9203-ee6f03dae18f","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"adapted to a higher noise level in the city","passagePhrase":"adapting to a wide range of noise levels"},{"uid":"02b7eae0-c365-4920-bef9-f26f2acca8bc","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"problem-solving","passagePhrase":"work out problems"},{"uid":"fd33ae39-11ee-4ccd-bc0e-243ee94a5e08","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"problem-solving","passagePhrase":"doing just as well on their tasks"},{"uid":"adb43da2-ea12-4970-9259-5be2df707c03","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"interfere with","passagePhrase":"becomes more troublesome"},{"uid":"30b33f47-5076-4b45-9d32-0491af5ce288","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"high-pitched noise","passagePhrase":"high noise levels"},{"uid":"5d295fd5-8fad-4b38-ab2d-6b90c6be5827","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Subjects find it difficult to perform","passagePhrase":"interfered with the performance of subjects"},{"uid":"1ce9656f-74ee-4191-b087-a02b63d9a5ec","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"at the same time","passagePhrase":"at a time"},{"uid":"e52a4a3c-659e-4b6e-ac04-33d41868509a","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"capacity","passagePhrase":"ability"},{"uid":"5209c022-7fb5-46db-be46-f190cb7b9ec0","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"intense","passagePhrase":"loud"},{"uid":"a3abb0eb-a961-4981-87c3-1ffe5355cb81","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"noise occurs","passagePhrase":"intrusions"},{"uid":"d4abb68c-4381-492e-8e66-b7a0b8437299","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"exposed to","passagePhrase":"heard"},{"uid":"6b08ba0b-b4fb-46d5-b29d-4f22dee01beb","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"on this task","passagePhrase":"during the noise portion"},{"uid":"b402f0b2-a4d7-4fcf-a078-c59f534e57cb","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"made more mistakes","passagePhrase":"produced more errors in the later proofreading task than predictable noise; and soft, unpredictable noise actually produced slightly more errors"},{"uid":"37dcd7af-5437-4cfa-bf2f-0fe4ae3a279d","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"takes a while"},{"uid":"c598f82b-37d4-424d-9302-1a2fefe05ad5","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"manifests","passagePhrase":"take its toll on performance"},{"uid":"4c84611c-764b-43c4-b989-a05a09fa43e9","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"problems","passagePhrase":"negative effects ... negative effects"},{"uid":"eb621c28-0a22-4a64-8728-3040ae8be8c6","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"make it stop","passagePhrase":"turn the noise off"},{"uid":"71b60005-8928-4ddd-bca1-1211b792049e","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Long-term exposure to noise","passagePhrase":"In fact, the longer the children had attended the noisy schools, the more distractible they became. The effects also seem to be long lasting."},{"uid":"0b7c1424-72a5-4766-a9b8-1250bbce8d8a","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"changes in behavior","passagePhrase":"greater distractibility"},{"uid":"c029cdd5-76fd-4d5c-a75f-f7167293ab04","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"high noise levels","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_163":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>A Chronicle of Timekeeping</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong> </p><p>According to archaeological evidence, at least 5,000 years ago, and long before the advent of the Roman Empire, the Babylonians began to measure time, introducing calendars to co-ordinate communal activities, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"e4b60d22-eb54-4f02-ad3e-906e2c49e6cf\">to plan<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"806c33a5-bff8-4d3e-aea4-51e45a287f50\">the shipment of goods and, in particular, to regulate planting and harvesting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. They based their calendars on three natural cycles: the solar day, marked by the successive periods of light and darkness as the earth rotates on its axis; the lunar month, following the phases of the moon as it orbits the earth; and the solar year, defined by the changing seasons that accompany our planet’s revolution around the sun.</p><p><strong>B</strong> </p><p>Before the invention of artificial light, the moon had greater social impact. And, for those living near the equator in particular, its waxing and waning was more conspicuous than the passing of the seasons. Hence, the calendars that were developed at the lower latitudes were influenced more by the lunar cycle than by the solar year. In more northern climes, however, where seasonal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"8e2aa22d-d43e-422e-a5ae-3bb2bd84f2da\">agriculture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> was practised, the solar year became more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"ee5627f9-0e07-421e-9053-2825a80c2e28\">crucial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. As the Roman Empire expanded northward, it organised its activity chart for the most part around the solar year.</p><p><strong>C</strong> </p><p>Centuries before the Roman Empire, the Egyptians had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"34f02432-4e4a-48da-a93f-c250ad9c1f30\">formulated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> a municipal calendar having <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"e3ebbe9c-4fdd-4ea1-8644-7cfb056ef8b6\">12 months of 30 days<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, with five days added to approximate the solar year. Each period of ten days was marked by the appearance of special groups of stars called decans. At the rise of the star Sirius just before sunrise, which occurred around the all-important annual flooding of the Nile, 12 decans could be seen spanning the heavens. The cosmic significance the Egyptians placed in the 12 decans led them to develop a system in which each interval of darkness (and later, each interval of daylight) was divided into a dozen equal parts. These periods became known as temporal hours because their duration varied according to the changing length of days and nights with the passing of the seasons. Summer hours were long, winter ones short; only at the spring and autumn equinoxes were the hours of daylight and darkness equal. Temporal hours, which were first adopted by the Greeks and then the Romans, who disseminated them through Europe, remained in use for more than 2,500 years.</p><p><strong>D</strong> </p><p>In order to track temporal hours during the day, inventors created sundials, which indicate time by the length or direction of the sun’s shadow. The sundial’s counterpart, the water clock, was designed to measure temporal hours at night. One of the first water clocks was a basin with a small hole near the bottom through which the water dripped out. The falling water level denoted the passing hour as it dipped below hour lines inscribed on the inner surface. Although these devices performed satisfactorily around the Mediterranean, they could not always be depended on in the cloudy and often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"00705322-43f6-4063-a264-9ef0e74e7fee\">freezing weather<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of northern Europe.</p><p><strong>E</strong> The advent of the mechanical clock meant that although it could be adjusted to maintain temporal hours, it was naturally suited to keeping equal ones. With these, however, arose the question of when to begin <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"33108062-e1a6-4f8e-b1e9-be09a9b3dd3e\">counting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, and so, in the early 14th century, a number of systems evolved. The schemes that divided the day into 24 equal parts varied according to the start of the count: Italian hours began at sunset, Babylonian hours at sunrise, astronomical hours at midday and ‘great clock’ hours, used for some large public clocks in Germany, at midnight. Eventually these were superseded by ‘small clock’, or French, hours, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"42bd1070-b07f-447b-86d4-4046f1d000d6\">split<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the day into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"5cd52bbc-13ba-453b-8e18-05dbd32c6e72\">two 12-hour periods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> commencing at midnight.</p><p><strong>F</strong> </p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e9ba163c-d9a1-4c09-a2bb-a8ba26785c0c\">The earliest recorded weight-driven mechanical clock was built in 1283<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> in Bedfordshire in England. The revolutionary aspect of this new timekeeper was neither the descending weight that provided its motive force nor the gear wheels (which had been around for at least 1,300 years) that transferred the power; it was the part called the escapement. In the early 1400s came the invention of the coiled spring or fusee which maintained constant force to the gear wheels of the timekeeper despite the changing tension of its mainspring. By the 16th century, a pendulum clock had been devised, but the pendulum swung in a large arc and thus was not very efficient.</p><p><strong>G</strong> </p><p>To address this, a variation on the original escapement was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a5528faa-74a1-4307-be6a-3f8ff216b4c3\">invented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in 1670, in England. It was called the anchor escapement, which was a lever-based device shaped like a ship’s anchor. The motion of a pendulum rocks this device so that it catches and then releases each tooth of the escape wheel, in turn allowing it to turn a precise amount. Unlike the original form used in early pendulum clocks, the anchor escapement permitted the pendulum to travel in a very small arc. Moreover, this invention allowed the use of a long pendulum which could beat once a second and thus led to the development of a new floor standing case design, which became known as the grandfather clock.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>Today, highly accurate timekeeping instruments set the beat for most electronic devices. Nearly all computers contain a quartz-crystal clock to regulate their operation. Moreover, not only do time signals beamed down from Global Positioning System satellites calibrate the functions of precision navigation equipment, they do so as well for mobile phones, instant stock-trading systems and nationwide power-distribution grids. So integral have these time-based technologies become to day-to-day existence that our dependency on them is recognised only when they fail to work.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 1 has eight paragraphs, A-H. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 1- 4 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28928\" id=\"question-wrapper-28928\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of an early timekeeping invention affected by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"00705322-43f6-4063-a264-9ef0e74e7fee\">cold temperatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28929\" id=\"question-wrapper-28929\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"ee5627f9-0e07-421e-9053-2825a80c2e28\">the importance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of geography in the development of the calendar in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"8e2aa22d-d43e-422e-a5ae-3bb2bd84f2da\">farming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> communities </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28930\" id=\"question-wrapper-28930\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"e9ba163c-d9a1-4c09-a2bb-a8ba26785c0c\">the origins of the pendulum clock<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28931\" id=\"question-wrapper-28931\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> details of the simultaneous efforts of different societies to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"33108062-e1a6-4f8e-b1e9-be09a9b3dd3e\">calculate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> time using uniform hours </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following events (Questions 5-8) and the list of nationalities below. Match each event with the correct nationality, A-F. Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 5-8 on your answer sheet.</p><ul><li><strong>A</strong> Babylonians</li><li><strong>B</strong> Egyptians</li><li><strong>C</strong> Greeks</li><li><strong>D</strong> English</li><li><strong>E</strong> Germans</li><li><strong>F</strong> French</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28932\" id=\"question-wrapper-28932\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"34f02432-4e4a-48da-a93f-c250ad9c1f30\">devised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> a civil calendar in which the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"e3ebbe9c-4fdd-4ea1-8644-7cfb056ef8b6\">months were equal in length<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28933\" id=\"question-wrapper-28933\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"42bd1070-b07f-447b-86d4-4046f1d000d6\">divided<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the day into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"5cd52bbc-13ba-453b-8e18-05dbd32c6e72\">two equal halves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28934\" id=\"question-wrapper-28934\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"a5528faa-74a1-4307-be6a-3f8ff216b4c3\">developed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> a new cabinet shape for a type of timekeeper. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28935\" id=\"question-wrapper-28935\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> They created a calendar <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"e4b60d22-eb54-4f02-ad3e-906e2c49e6cf\">to organise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"806c33a5-bff8-4d3e-aea4-51e45a287f50\">public events and work schedules<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Label the diagram below. Write <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage.</p><p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><em><img src=\"/media/gg_imgs/test/57934efd5e2b48d3d4737f822ec59df5415fb60d.jpg\" style=\"height:575px; width:595px\"></em></span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28936\" id=\"question-wrapper-28936\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(SHIP'S) ANCHOR [OR] (AN/THE) ANCHOR</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28937\" id=\"question-wrapper-28937\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(ESCAPE) WHEEL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28938\" id=\"question-wrapper-28938\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TOOTH</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28939\" id=\"question-wrapper-28939\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(LONG) PENDULUM</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28940\" id=\"question-wrapper-28940\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SECOND</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e4b60d22-eb54-4f02-ad3e-906e2c49e6cf","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"to organise","passagePhrase":"to plan"},{"uid":"806c33a5-bff8-4d3e-aea4-51e45a287f50","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"public events and work schedules","passagePhrase":"the shipment of goods and, in particular, to regulate planting and harvesting"},{"uid":"8e2aa22d-d43e-422e-a5ae-3bb2bd84f2da","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"farming","passagePhrase":"agriculture"},{"uid":"ee5627f9-0e07-421e-9053-2825a80c2e28","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"the importance","passagePhrase":"crucial"},{"uid":"34f02432-4e4a-48da-a93f-c250ad9c1f30","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"devised","passagePhrase":"formulated"},{"uid":"e3ebbe9c-4fdd-4ea1-8644-7cfb056ef8b6","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"months were equal in length","passagePhrase":"12 months of 30 days"},{"uid":"00705322-43f6-4063-a264-9ef0e74e7fee","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"cold temperatures","passagePhrase":"freezing weather"},{"uid":"33108062-e1a6-4f8e-b1e9-be09a9b3dd3e","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"calculate","passagePhrase":"counting"},{"uid":"42bd1070-b07f-447b-86d4-4046f1d000d6","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"divided","passagePhrase":"split"},{"uid":"5cd52bbc-13ba-453b-8e18-05dbd32c6e72","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"two equal halves","passagePhrase":"two 12-hour periods"},{"uid":"e9ba163c-d9a1-4c09-a2bb-a8ba26785c0c","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"the origins of the pendulum clock","passagePhrase":"The earliest recorded weight-driven mechanical clock was built in 1283"},{"uid":"a5528faa-74a1-4307-be6a-3f8ff216b4c3","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"developed","passagePhrase":"invented"}]},"reading_u2_164":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL IN THE USA</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong> </p><p>An <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47c7f1d6-aa3f-40f3-8643-64c8825e6360\" data-question=\"14\">accident that occurred in the skies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> over the Grand Canyon in 1956 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc293eb9-08f2-4370-91c7-f5977578bdb1\" data-question=\"14\">resulted in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the establishment of the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) to regulate and oversee the operation of aircraft in the skies over the United States, which were becoming quite congested. The resulting structure of air traffic control has greatly increased the safety of flight in the United States, and similar air traffic control procedures are also in place over much of the rest of the world.</p><p><strong>B</strong> </p><p>Rudimentary air traffic control (АТС) existed well <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f44720e9-05b2-4830-9691-f9367f52d469\" data-question=\"21\">before the Grand Canyon disaster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. As early as the 1920s, the earliest air traffic controllers manually guided aircraft in the vicinity of the airports, using lights and flags, while beacons and flashing lights were placed along cross-country routes to establish the earliest airways. However, this purely visual system was useless in bad weather, and, by the 1930s, radio communication was coming into use for АТС. The first region to have something approximating today’s АТС was New York City, with other major metropolitan areas following soon after.</p><p><strong>C</strong> </p><p>In the 1940s, АТС centres could and did take advantage of the newly developed radar and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4339c89b-f0b2-4f20-a0e7-fa91e86653df\" data-question=\"23\">improved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> radio communication <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1626c5d-fe70-42bd-8bfb-46b94bf95b29\" data-question=\"23\">brought about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> by the Second World War, but the system remained rudimentary. It was only after the creation of the FAA that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f917c1b-39a3-4c10-8fed-240c55aca8be\" data-question=\"15\">full-scale regulation of America’s airspace took place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, and this was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"92c83fc1-bcff-4532-a8de-ab04e320ec28\" data-question=\"15\">fortuitous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f917c1b-39a3-4c10-8fed-240c55aca8be\" data-question=\"15\">the advent of the jet engine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> suddenly resulted in a large number of very fast planes, reducing pilots’ margin of error and practically demanding some set of rules to keep everyone well separated and operating safely in the air.</p><p><strong>D</strong> </p><p>Many people think that АТС consists of a row of controllers sitting in front of their radar screens at the nation’s airports, telling arriving and departing traffic what to do. This is a very <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4131e953-dca9-4c57-a102-5d8b8bc84e0d\" data-question=\"16\">incomplete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> part of the picture. The FAA realised that the airspace over the United States would at any time have many different kinds of planes, flying for many different purposes, in a variety of weather conditions, and the same kind of structure was needed to accommodate all of them.</p><p><strong>E</strong> </p><p>To meet this challenge, the following elements were put into effect. First, АТС extends over virtually the entire United States. In general, from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9d64710-47b2-48ed-9e2d-84e07d257849\" data-question=\"17\">365m above the ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and higher, the entire country is blanketed by controlled airspace. In certain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5ea97e4-88b3-4fbd-a2dd-643d0d8ddfe8\" data-question=\"17\">areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, mainly near airports, controlled airspace extends down to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9d64710-47b2-48ed-9e2d-84e07d257849\" data-question=\"17\">215m above the ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, and, in the immediate vicinity of an airport, all the way down to the surface. Controlled airspace is that airspace in which FAA regulations apply. Elsewhere, in uncontrolled airspace, pilots are bound by fewer regulations. In this way, the recreational pilot who simply wishes to go flying for a while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2dca6c24-075e-48cf-b711-2e40c94209e5\" data-question=\"24\">without all the restrictions imposed by the FAA<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> has only to stay in uncontrolled airspace, below 365m, while the pilot who does want the protection afforded by АТС can easily enter the controlled airspace.</p><p><strong>F</strong> </p><p>The FAA then recognised two types of operating environments. In good <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"65cd5ccc-93c1-4051-bf80-33741daa203a\" data-question=\"18\">meteorological conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, flying would be permitted under <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10c638f6-e61d-4fd7-9c71-235785360175\" data-question=\"18\">Visual Flight Rules (VFR)<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, which suggests a strong reliance on visual cues to maintain an acceptable level of safety. Poor visibility necessitated a set of Instrumental Flight Rules (IFR), under which the pilot relied on altitude and navigational information provided by the plane’s instrument panel to fly safely. On a clear day, a pilot in controlled airspace can choose a VFR or IFR flight plan, and the FAA regulations were devised in a way which accommodates both VFR and IFR operations in the same airspace. However, a pilot can only choose to fly IFR if they possess an instrument rating which is above and beyond the basic pilot’s license that must also be held.</p><p><strong>G</strong> </p><p>Controlled airspace is divided into several different <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57ba3cb0-18f5-4279-be3b-8d8951555a43\" data-question=\"19\">types<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1adfd581-0a4e-4499-b0c3-d84ffd49203f\" data-question=\"19\">designated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> by letters of the alphabet. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f958980-6803-4302-9c2f-6193849a14b3\" data-question=\"24\">Uncontrolled airspace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1adfd581-0a4e-4499-b0c3-d84ffd49203f\" data-question=\"19\">designated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> Class F, while controlled airspace below 5,490m above sea level and not in the vicinity of an airport is Class E. All airspace above 5,490m is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1adfd581-0a4e-4499-b0c3-d84ffd49203f\" data-question=\"19\">designated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> Class A. The reason for the division of Class E and Class A airspace stems from the type of planes operating in them. Generally, Class E airspace is where one finds general aviation aircraft (few of which can climb above 5,490m anyway), and commercial turboprop aircraft. Above 5,490m is the realm of the heavy jets, since jet engines operate more efficiently at higher altitudes. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fbae6e08-2c63-4701-aa28-2b49ec0cc90e\" data-question=\"25\">The difference between Class E and A airspace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> is that in Class A, all operations are IFR, and pilots must be instrument-rated, that is, skilled and licensed in aircraft instrumentation. This is because АТС control of the entire space is essential. Three other types of airspace, Classes D, С and B, govern the vicinity of airports. These correspond roughly to small municipal, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b047d78-3da2-4f92-a0bc-df91ddb265c5\" data-question=\"26\">medium-sized<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> metropolitan and major metropolitan airports respectively, and encompass an increasingly rigorous set of regulations. For example, all a VFR pilot has to do to enter Class С airspace is establish two-way radio contact with АТС. No explicit permission from АТС to enter is needed, although the pilot must continue to obey all regulations governing VFR flight. To enter Class В airspace, such as on approach to a major metropolitan airport, an explicit АТС clearance is required. The private pilot who cruises without permission into this airspace risks losing their license.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading passage 2 has seven paragraphs A-G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs A and C-G from the list below. Write the correct number i-x in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><ul><li>i Disobeying FAA Regulations</li><li>ii <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47c7f1d6-aa3f-40f3-8643-64c8825e6360\" data-question=\"14\">Aviation disaster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc293eb9-08f2-4370-91c7-f5977578bdb1\" data-question=\"14\">prompts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> action</li><li>iii Two <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"92c83fc1-bcff-4532-a8de-ab04e320ec28\" data-question=\"15\">coincidental<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f917c1b-39a3-4c10-8fed-240c55aca8be\" data-question=\"15\">developments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></li><li>iv Setting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9d64710-47b2-48ed-9e2d-84e07d257849\" data-question=\"17\">Altitude<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5ea97e4-88b3-4fbd-a2dd-643d0d8ddfe8\" data-question=\"17\">Zones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></li><li>v An <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4131e953-dca9-4c57-a102-5d8b8bc84e0d\" data-question=\"16\">oversimplified<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> view</li><li>vi Controlling pilots’ licence</li><li>vii <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1adfd581-0a4e-4499-b0c3-d84ffd49203f\" data-question=\"19\">Defining<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> airspace <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57ba3cb0-18f5-4279-be3b-8d8951555a43\" data-question=\"19\">categories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></li><li>viii <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10c638f6-e61d-4fd7-9c71-235785360175\" data-question=\"18\">Setting rules<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"65cd5ccc-93c1-4051-bf80-33741daa203a\" data-question=\"18\">weather conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></li><li>ix Taking of Safety</li><li>x First step towards ATC</li></ul><p><strong>Example – Paragraph B: x</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28941\" id=\"question-wrapper-28941\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28942\" id=\"question-wrapper-28942\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28943\" id=\"question-wrapper-28943\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28944\" id=\"question-wrapper-28944\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28945\" id=\"question-wrapper-28945\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28946\" id=\"question-wrapper-28946\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the given information of the reading passage? In boxes 20-26 on your answer sheet, write:</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28947\" id=\"question-wrapper-28947\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The FAA was created as a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"83fec5df-60a7-45f0-b988-b940114f49b1\" data-question=\"20\">result of the introduction of the jet engine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28948\" id=\"question-wrapper-28948\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Air traffic control started <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f44720e9-05b2-4830-9691-f9367f52d469\" data-question=\"21\">after the Grand Canyon crash<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in 1956. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28949\" id=\"question-wrapper-28949\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Beacons and flashing lights are still used by the ATC today. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28950\" id=\"question-wrapper-28950\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4339c89b-f0b2-4f20-a0e7-fa91e86653df\" data-question=\"23\">improvements were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1626c5d-fe70-42bd-8bfb-46b94bf95b29\" data-question=\"23\">made<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> in radio communication during World War II. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28951\" id=\"question-wrapper-28951\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f958980-6803-4302-9c2f-6193849a14b3\" data-question=\"24\">Class F airspace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> is airspace which is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2dca6c24-075e-48cf-b711-2e40c94209e5\" data-question=\"24\">below 365m and not near airports<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28952\" id=\"question-wrapper-28952\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> All aircraft in class E airspace must use IFR. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28953\" id=\"question-wrapper-28953\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A pilot entering class C airspace is flying over an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b047d78-3da2-4f92-a0bc-df91ddb265c5\" data-question=\"26\">average-sized<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5fd4974-ede1-4b16-a1a3-c43d975f2fe1\" data-question=\"26\">city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"47c7f1d6-aa3f-40f3-8643-64c8825e6360","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Aviation disaster","passagePhrase":"accident that occurred in the skies"},{"uid":"dc293eb9-08f2-4370-91c7-f5977578bdb1","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"prompts","passagePhrase":"resulted in"},{"uid":"4339c89b-f0b2-4f20-a0e7-fa91e86653df","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"improvements were made","passagePhrase":"improved"},{"uid":"c1626c5d-fe70-42bd-8bfb-46b94bf95b29","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"made","passagePhrase":"brought about"},{"uid":"9f917c1b-39a3-4c10-8fed-240c55aca8be","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"developments","passagePhrase":"full-scale regulation of America’s airspace took place ... the advent of the jet engine"},{"uid":"92c83fc1-bcff-4532-a8de-ab04e320ec28","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"coincidental","passagePhrase":"fortuitous"},{"uid":"4131e953-dca9-4c57-a102-5d8b8bc84e0d","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"oversimplified","passagePhrase":"incomplete"},{"uid":"a9d64710-47b2-48ed-9e2d-84e07d257849","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Altitude","passagePhrase":"365m above the ground ... 215m above the ground"},{"uid":"e5ea97e4-88b3-4fbd-a2dd-643d0d8ddfe8","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Zones","passagePhrase":"areas"},{"uid":"2dca6c24-075e-48cf-b711-2e40c94209e5","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"below 365m and not near airports","passagePhrase":"without all the restrictions imposed by the FAA"},{"uid":"65cd5ccc-93c1-4051-bf80-33741daa203a","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"weather conditions","passagePhrase":"meteorological conditions"},{"uid":"10c638f6-e61d-4fd7-9c71-235785360175","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Setting rules","passagePhrase":"Visual Flight Rules (VFR)"},{"uid":"57ba3cb0-18f5-4279-be3b-8d8951555a43","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"categories","passagePhrase":"types"},{"uid":"1adfd581-0a4e-4499-b0c3-d84ffd49203f","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Defining","passagePhrase":"designated ... designated ... designated"},{"uid":"5f958980-6803-4302-9c2f-6193849a14b3","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Class F airspace","passagePhrase":"Uncontrolled airspace"},{"uid":"fbae6e08-2c63-4701-aa28-2b49ec0cc90e","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"The difference between Class E and A airspace"},{"uid":"3b047d78-3da2-4f92-a0bc-df91ddb265c5","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"average-sized","passagePhrase":"medium-sized"},{"uid":"b5fd4974-ede1-4b16-a1a3-c43d975f2fe1","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"city","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_165":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Telepathy</strong></p><p>Since the 1970s, parapsychologists at leading universities and research institutes around the world have risked the derision of sceptical colleagues by putting the various claims for telepathy to the test in dozens of rigorous scientific studies. The results and their implications are dividing even the researchers who uncovered them.</p><p>Some researchers say the results constitute compelling evidence that telepathy is genuine. Other parapsychologists believe the field is on the brink of collapse, having tried to produce definitive scientific proof and failed. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdea644f-e78f-4605-8db0-c4c3cf93a21c\" data-question=\"27\">Sceptics and advocates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> alike do <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d7397e3-76e0-470f-841c-ac1a1eca0fed\" data-question=\"27\">concur on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> one issue, however: that the most impressive evidence so far has come from the so-called ‘ganzfeld’ experiments, a German term that means ‘whole field’. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7e75376-265b-4389-8d2b-888d6692a65b\" data-question=\"28\">Reports of telepathic experiences had by people during meditation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> led parapsychologists to suspect that telepathy might involve ‘signals’ passing between people that were so faint that they were usually swamped by normal brain activity. In this case, such signals might be more easily detected by those experiencing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78d167f8-9494-451e-a666-254cbaf6dd97\" data-question=\"28\">meditation-like tranquility in a relaxing ‘whole field’ of light, sound and warmth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</p><p>The ganzfeld experiment tries to recreate these conditions with participants sitting in soft reclining chairs in a sealed room, listening to relaxing sounds while their eyes are covered with special filters letting in only soft pink light. In early ganzfeld experiments, the telepathy test involved identification of a picture <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34614c37-4938-43f1-b6c6-b59a70b55d8d\" data-question=\"32\">chosen from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> a random selection of four taken from a large image bank. The idea was that a person acting as a ‘sender’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f0019e0-4062-4cd9-8585-a5ba6f297bde\" data-question=\"33\">would attempt to beam the image over to the ‘receiver’ relaxing in the sealed room. Once the session was over<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, this person was asked to identify which of the four images had been used. Random guessing would give a hit-rate of 25 per cent; if telepathy is real, however, the hit-rate would be higher. In 1982, the results from the first ganzfeld studies were analysed by one of its pioneers, the American parapsychologist Charles Honorton. They pointed to typical hit-rates of better than 30 per cent – a small effect, but one which statistical tests suggested could not be put down to chance.</p><p>The implication was that the ganzfeld method had revealed real evidence for telepathy. But there was a crucial flaw in this argument – one routinely overlooked in more conventional areas of science. Just because chance had been ruled out as an explanation did not prove telepathy must exist; there were many other ways of getting positive results. These ranged from ‘sensory leakage’ – where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33919153-e633-4541-a59c-b82d22ac62e6\" data-question=\"34\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d412104f-c935-40d2-864f-0fb216f251e5\" data-question=\"35\">clues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> about the pictures accidentally reach the receiver – to outright fraud. In response, the researchers issued a review of all the ganzfeld studies done up to 1985 to show that 80 per cent had found statistically significant evidence. However, they also agreed that there were still too many problems in the experiments which could lead to positive results, and they drew up a list demanding new standards for future research.</p><p>After this, many researchers switched to autoganzfeld tests – an automated variant of the technique which used computers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"097d4ae8-187f-4fc0-b12e-39cfeabcd7a8\" data-question=\"36\">perform<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> many of the key tasks such as the random selection of images. By minimising human involvement, the idea was to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d3e9af6f-9c0e-4338-bebb-464bbc32bd11\" data-question=\"37\">minimise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> the risk of flawed results. In 1987, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5990ddea-adca-4738-b832-71242d41801f\" data-question=\"38\">results from hundreds of autoganzfeld tests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f9d5959-9ba0-46e4-95b6-ac08ad760081\" data-question=\"38\">studied by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> Honorton in a ‘meta-analysis’, a statistical technique for finding the overall results from a set of studies. Though less compelling than before, the outcome was still impressive.</p><p>Yet some parapsychologists remain disturbed by the lack of consistency between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41f72ba1-9978-41ff-90c2-7a5062e89bfc\" data-question=\"39\">individual ganzfeld studies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Defenders of telepathy point out that demanding impressive evidence from every study ignores one basic statistical fact: it takes large samples to detect small effects. If, as current results suggest, telepathy produces hit-rates only marginally above the 25 per cent expected by chance, it’s unlikely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"161562b9-e83e-4ef1-b678-1ab2ad65f026\" data-question=\"40\">be detected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> by a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33e6c431-1891-4b57-8687-7a25d203aee6\" data-question=\"40\">typical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> ganzfeld study involving around 40 people: the group is just not big enough. Only when many studies are combined in a meta-analysis will the faint signal of telepathy really become apparent. And that is what researchers do seem to be finding.</p><p>What they are certainly not finding, however, is any change in attitude of mainstream scientists: most still totally reject the very idea of telepathy. The problem stems at least in part from the lack of any plausible mechanism for telepathy.</p><p>Various theories have been put forward, many focusing on esoteric ideas from theoretical physics. They include ‘quantum entanglement’, in which events affecting one group of atoms instantly affect another group, no matter how far apart they may be. While physicists have demonstrated entanglement with specially prepared atoms, no-one knows if it also exists between atoms making up human minds. Answering such questions would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d374ebd-6972-4071-96ae-c8cde8ef0006\" data-question=\"29\">transform parapsychology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. This has prompted some researchers to argue that the future lies not in collecting more evidence for telepathy, but in probing possible mechanisms. Some work has begun already, with researchers trying to identify people who are particularly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c1db0d6-dc33-4db6-b32b-01dd3a301fe5\" data-question=\"30\">successful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> in autoganzfeld trials. Early results show that creative and artistic people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24169cc9-2d38-48d7-bac4-e137d6fb218a\" data-question=\"30\">do much better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> than average: in one study at the University of Edinburgh, musicians achieved a hit-rate of 56 per cent. Perhaps more tests like these will eventually give the researchers the evidence they are seeking and strengthen the case for the existence of telepathy.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A —G, below. Write the correct letter, A—G, in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.</p><ul><li><strong>A</strong> the discovery of a mechanism for telepathy.</li><li><strong>B</strong> the need to create a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78d167f8-9494-451e-a666-254cbaf6dd97\" data-question=\"28\">suitable environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> for telepathy.</li><li><strong>C</strong> their claims of a high success rate.</li><li><strong>D</strong> a solution to the problem posed by random guessing.</li><li><strong>E</strong> the significance of the ganzfeld experiments.</li><li><strong>F</strong> a more careful selection of subjects.</li><li><strong>G</strong> a need to keep altering conditions.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28954\" id=\"question-wrapper-28954\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdea644f-e78f-4605-8db0-c4c3cf93a21c\" data-question=\"27\">Researchers with differing attitudes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> towards telepathy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d7397e3-76e0-470f-841c-ac1a1eca0fed\" data-question=\"27\">agree on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28955\" id=\"question-wrapper-28955\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7e75376-265b-4389-8d2b-888d6692a65b\" data-question=\"28\">Reports of experiences during meditation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> indicated </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28956\" id=\"question-wrapper-28956\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Attitudes to parapsychology would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d374ebd-6972-4071-96ae-c8cde8ef0006\" data-question=\"29\">alter drastically<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> with </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28957\" id=\"question-wrapper-28957\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Recent autoganzfeld trials suggest that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c1db0d6-dc33-4db6-b32b-01dd3a301fe5\" data-question=\"30\">success<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> rates will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24169cc9-2d38-48d7-bac4-e137d6fb218a\" data-question=\"30\">improve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> with </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the table below. Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.<br>Write your answers in boxes 31-40 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>TELEPATHY EXPERIMENTS</strong></p><table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"Table\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; margin-left:1px\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Name/Date</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Description</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Result</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Flaw</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Ganzfeld studies</p><p>1982</p></td><td><p>Involved a person acting as a</p><p><strong>31</strong>................ , who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34614c37-4938-43f1-b6c6-b59a70b55d8d\" data-question=\"32\">picked out one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <strong>32</strong>.................. from a random selection of four, and a <strong>33</strong>.................. , who then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f0019e0-4062-4cd9-8585-a5ba6f297bde\" data-question=\"33\">tried to identify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> it.</p></td><td><p>Hit-rates were higher than with random guessing.</p></td><td><p>Positive results could be produced by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33919153-e633-4541-a59c-b82d22ac62e6\" data-question=\"34\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d412104f-c935-40d2-864f-0fb216f251e5\" data-question=\"35\">factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> such as <strong>34</strong>.................. or <strong>35</strong>...................</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Autoganzfeld studies</p><p>1987</p></td><td><p><strong>36</strong>................. were used for key tasks to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d3e9af6f-9c0e-4338-bebb-464bbc32bd11\" data-question=\"37\">limit the amount of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <strong>37</strong>.................. in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"097d4ae8-187f-4fc0-b12e-39cfeabcd7a8\" data-question=\"36\">carrying out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> the tests.</p></td><td><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5990ddea-adca-4738-b832-71242d41801f\" data-question=\"38\">The results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> were then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f9d5959-9ba0-46e4-95b6-ac08ad760081\" data-question=\"38\">subjected to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> a <strong>38</strong> ..............</p></td><td><p>The <strong>39</strong>................. between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41f72ba1-9978-41ff-90c2-7a5062e89bfc\" data-question=\"39\">different test results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"161562b9-e83e-4ef1-b678-1ab2ad65f026\" data-question=\"40\">was put down to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> the fact that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33e6c431-1891-4b57-8687-7a25d203aee6\" data-question=\"40\">sample<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> groups were not <strong>40</strong>.................(as with most ganzfeld studies).</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28958\" id=\"question-wrapper-28958\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SENDER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28959\" id=\"question-wrapper-28959\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PICTURE/IMAGE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28960\" id=\"question-wrapper-28960\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RECEIVER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28961\" id=\"question-wrapper-28961\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SENSORY LEAKAGE [OR] (OUTRIGHT) FRAUD</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28962\" id=\"question-wrapper-28962\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SENSORY LEAKAGE [OR] (OUTRIGHT) FRAUD</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28963\" id=\"question-wrapper-28963\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMPUTERS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28964\" id=\"question-wrapper-28964\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HUMAN INVOLVEMENT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28965\" id=\"question-wrapper-28965\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">META-ANALYSIS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28966\" id=\"question-wrapper-28966\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LACK OF CONSISTENCY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28967\" id=\"question-wrapper-28967\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BIG/LARGE ENOUGH</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"cdea644f-e78f-4605-8db0-c4c3cf93a21c","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Researchers with differing attitudes","passagePhrase":"Sceptics and advocates"},{"uid":"4d7397e3-76e0-470f-841c-ac1a1eca0fed","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"agree on","passagePhrase":"concur on"},{"uid":"b7e75376-265b-4389-8d2b-888d6692a65b","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Reports of experiences during meditation","passagePhrase":"Reports of telepathic experiences had by people during meditation"},{"uid":"78d167f8-9494-451e-a666-254cbaf6dd97","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"suitable environment","passagePhrase":"meditation-like tranquility in a relaxing ‘whole field’ of light, sound and warmth"},{"uid":"34614c37-4938-43f1-b6c6-b59a70b55d8d","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"picked out one","passagePhrase":"chosen from"},{"uid":"6f0019e0-4062-4cd9-8585-a5ba6f297bde","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"tried to identify","passagePhrase":"would attempt to beam the image over to the ‘receiver’ relaxing in the sealed room. Once the session was over"},{"uid":"33919153-e633-4541-a59c-b82d22ac62e6","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"factors","passagePhrase":"clues"},{"uid":"d412104f-c935-40d2-864f-0fb216f251e5","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"factors","passagePhrase":"clues"},{"uid":"097d4ae8-187f-4fc0-b12e-39cfeabcd7a8","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"carrying out","passagePhrase":"perform"},{"uid":"d3e9af6f-9c0e-4338-bebb-464bbc32bd11","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"limit the amount of","passagePhrase":"minimise"},{"uid":"5990ddea-adca-4738-b832-71242d41801f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"The results","passagePhrase":"results from hundreds of autoganzfeld tests"},{"uid":"6f9d5959-9ba0-46e4-95b6-ac08ad760081","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"subjected to","passagePhrase":"studied by"},{"uid":"41f72ba1-9978-41ff-90c2-7a5062e89bfc","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"different test results","passagePhrase":"individual ganzfeld studies"},{"uid":"161562b9-e83e-4ef1-b678-1ab2ad65f026","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"was put down to","passagePhrase":"be detected"},{"uid":"33e6c431-1891-4b57-8687-7a25d203aee6","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"sample","passagePhrase":"typical"},{"uid":"0d374ebd-6972-4071-96ae-c8cde8ef0006","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"alter drastically","passagePhrase":"transform parapsychology"},{"uid":"5c1db0d6-dc33-4db6-b32b-01dd3a301fe5","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"success","passagePhrase":"successful"},{"uid":"24169cc9-2d38-48d7-bac4-e137d6fb218a","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"improve","passagePhrase":"do much better"}]},"reading_u2_166":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Sheet Glass Manufacture: the Float Process</strong></p><p>Glass, which has been made since the time of the Mesopotamians and Egyptians, is little more than a mixture of sand, soda ash and lime. When heated to about 1500 degrees Celsius (°C) this becomes a molten mass that hardens when slowly cooled. The first successful method for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"c06f0b4e-63e9-484a-9a58-d9e5690c6fe5\">making clear, flat glass involved spinning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. This method was very effective as the glass had not touched any surfaces between being soft and becoming hard, so it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"7d7c5066-4923-482f-b347-4405635d60a9\">stayed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> perfectly unblemished, with a ‘fire finish’. However, the process <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"b6ea06d0-8909-4175-b7e0-a57fc7e90833\">took a long time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and was labour intensive.</p><p>Nevertheless, demand for flat glass was very high and glassmakers across the world were looking for a method of making it continuously. The first continuous ribbon process involved squeezing molten glass through two hot rollers, similar to an old mangle. This allowed glass of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9a7a631c-e760-455f-a6a8-efe421efdf3f\">virtually any thickness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to be made non-stop, but the rollers would leave both sides of the glass marked, and these would then need to be ground and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"cd6a6ca9-be41-4560-8a49-90847e99d594\">polished<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. This part of the process rubbed away around 20 per cent of the glass, and the machines were very expensive.</p><p>The float process for making flat glass was invented by Alistair Pilkington. This process allows the manufacture of clear, tinted and coated glass for buildings, and clear and tinted glass for vehicles. Pilkington had been experimenting with improving the melting process, and in 1952 he had the idea of using a bed of molten metal to form the flat glass, eliminating altogether the need for rollers within the float bath. The metal had to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"0cf7270c-7788-41bc-bcd6-cbbadbe1940e\">melt at a temperature less than the hardening point of glass<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (about 600°C), but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"0cf7270c-7788-41bc-bcd6-cbbadbe1940e\">could not boil at a temperature below the temperature of the molten glass<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (about 1500°C). The best metal for the job was tin.</p><p>The rest of the concept relied on gravity, which guaranteed that the surface of the molten metal was perfectly flat and horizontal. Consequently, when pouring molten glass onto the molten tin, the underside of the glass would also be perfectly flat. If the glass were kept hot enough, it would flow over the molten tin until the top surface was also flat, horizontal and perfectly parallel to the bottom surface. Once the glass cooled to 604°C or less it was too hard to mark and could be transported out of the cooling zone by rollers. The glass settled to a thickness of six millimetres because of surface tension interactions between the glass and the tin. By fortunate coincidence, 60 per cent of the flat glass market at that time was for six- millimetre glass.</p><p>Pilkington built a pilot plant in 1953 and by 1955 he had convinced his company to build a full-scale plant. However, it took <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ed39a998-8888-449b-a8d8-be94206df6d8\">14 months of non-stop production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, costing the company £100,000 a month, before the plant produced any usable glass. Furthermore, once they succeeded in making marketable flat glass, the machine was turned off for a service to prepare it for years of continuous production. When it started up again it took another four months to get the process right again. They finally succeeded in 1959 and there are now float plants all over the world, with each able to produce around 1000 tons of glass every day, non-stop for around 15 years.</p><p>Float plants today make glass of near optical quality. Several processes – melting, refining, homogenising – take place simultaneously in the 2000 tonnes of molten glass in the furnace. They occur in separate zones in a complex glass flow driven by high temperatures. It adds up to a continuous melting process, lasting as long as 50 hours, that delivers glass smoothly and continuously to the float bath, and from there to a coating zone and finally a heat treatment zone, where stresses formed during cooling are relieved.</p><p>The principle of float glass is unchanged since the 1950s. However, the product <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"806aa68c-8583-47c4-8503-51219e8285a3\">has changed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> dramatically, from a single thickness of 6.8 mm to a range from sub-millimetre to 25 mm, from a ribbon frequently marred by inclusions and bubbles to almost optical perfection. To ensure the highest quality, inspection takes place at every stage. Occasionally, a bubble is not removed during refining, a sand grain refuses to melt, a tremor in the tin puts ripples into the glass ribbon. Automated on-line inspection does two things. Firstly, it reveals process faults upstream that can be corrected. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"7f106b54-d28e-4c95-ae7b-ded942a0bc0b\">Inspection technology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> allows more than 100 million measurements a second to be made across the ribbon, locating flaws the unaided eye would be unable to see. Secondly, it enables computers downstream to steer cutters around flaws.</p><p>Float glass is sold by the square metre, and at the final stage computers translate customer requirements into patterns of cuts designed to minimise waste.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the table and diagram below. Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Write your answers in boxes 1-8 on your answer sheet.</p> <table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"Table\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; margin-left:2px\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; height:30px; width:144px\"><p style=\"margin-left:41px\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Method</span></strong></p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:none; border-top:1px solid black; height:30px; vertical-align:top; width:23px\"><p> </p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; height:30px; width:314px\"><p style=\"margin-right:122px; text-align:right\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Advantages</span></strong></p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:none; border-top:1px solid black; height:30px; vertical-align:top; width:33px\"><p> </p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; height:30px; width:208px\"><p style=\"margin-right:68px; text-align:right\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Disadvantages</span></strong></p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:35px; width:144px\"><p style=\"margin-left:11px\"><span style=\"color:black\"><strong>(1).</strong>....................... </span></p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:none; border-top:none; height:35px; width:23px\"><p style=\"text-align:center\"> </p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:35px; width:314px\"><p style=\"margin-left:7px\"><span style=\"color:black\">- Glass <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"2\" data-uid=\"7d7c5066-4923-482f-b347-4405635d60a9\">remained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <strong>(2)</strong>.................. </span></p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:none; border-top:none; height:35px; vertical-align:top; width:33px\"><p style=\"margin-left:12px; text-align:center\"><br> </p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:35px; vertical-align:top; width:208px\"><p style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"color:black\">- <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"b6ea06d0-8909-4175-b7e0-a57fc7e90833\">Slow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p style=\"margin-left:8px\"><strong><span style=\"color:black\">- (3)...............</span></strong></p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:none; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:20px; vertical-align:top; width:144px\"><p style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:black\">Ribbon</span></p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px black; border-left:none; border-right:1px black; border-top:none; height:20px; width:23px\"><p style=\"text-align:center\"> </p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:none; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:20px; width:314px\"><p style=\"margin-left:7px\"><span style=\"color:black\">- Could produce glass sheets of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"9a7a631c-e760-455f-a6a8-efe421efdf3f\">varying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <strong>(4)</strong>..........</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:7px\"><span style=\"color:black\">- Non-stop process</span></p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px black; border-left:none; border-right:1px black; border-top:none; height:20px; vertical-align:top; width:33px\"><p> </p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:none; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:20px; vertical-align:top; width:208px\"><p><span style=\"color:black\">- Glass was <strong>(5)</strong>....................</span></p><p><span style=\"color:black\">- 20% of glass <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"cd6a6ca9-be41-4560-8a49-90847e99d594\">rubbed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> away</span></p><p>- Machines were expensive</p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:51px; vertical-align:top; width:144px\"><p style=\"margin-left:11px\"> </p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:none; border-top:none; height:51px; width:23px\"><p style=\"text-align:center\"> </p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:51px; vertical-align:top; width:314px\"><p style=\"margin-left:7px\"> </p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:none; border-top:none; height:51px; vertical-align:top; width:33px\"><p style=\"margin-left:12px; text-align:center\"> </p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:51px; vertical-align:top; width:208px\"><p style=\"margin-left:8px\"> </p></td></tr></tbody></table> <p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><em><img src=\"/media/gg_imgs/test/a59ebd1f27db6ad2ca3c4506fbc92268319f9368.jpg\" style=\"height:224px; width:556px\"></em></span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28968\" id=\"question-wrapper-28968\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPINNING</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28969\" id=\"question-wrapper-28969\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(PERFECTLY) UNBLEMISHED</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28970\" id=\"question-wrapper-28970\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LABO(U)R(-/ )INTENSIVE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28971\" id=\"question-wrapper-28971\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">THICKNESS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28972\" id=\"question-wrapper-28972\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MARKED</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28973\" id=\"question-wrapper-28973\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(MOLTEN) GLASS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28974\" id=\"question-wrapper-28974\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(MOLTEN) TIN/METAL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28975\" id=\"question-wrapper-28975\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ROLLERS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write:</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this<br></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28976\" id=\"question-wrapper-28976\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The metal used in the float process had to have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"0cf7270c-7788-41bc-bcd6-cbbadbe1940e\">specific properties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28977\" id=\"question-wrapper-28977\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Pilkington invested some of his own money in his float plant. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28978\" id=\"question-wrapper-28978\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Pilkington’s first full-scale plant was an <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"ed39a998-8888-449b-a8d8-be94206df6d8\">instant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> commercial success. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28979\" id=\"question-wrapper-28979\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The process invented by Pilkington <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"806aa68c-8583-47c4-8503-51219e8285a3\">has now been improved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28980\" id=\"question-wrapper-28980\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"7f106b54-d28e-4c95-ae7b-ded942a0bc0b\">Computers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> are better than humans at detecting faults in glass. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c06f0b4e-63e9-484a-9a58-d9e5690c6fe5","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"making clear, flat glass involved spinning"},{"uid":"7d7c5066-4923-482f-b347-4405635d60a9","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"remained","passagePhrase":"stayed"},{"uid":"b6ea06d0-8909-4175-b7e0-a57fc7e90833","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Slow","passagePhrase":"took a long time"},{"uid":"9a7a631c-e760-455f-a6a8-efe421efdf3f","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"varying","passagePhrase":"virtually any thickness"},{"uid":"cd6a6ca9-be41-4560-8a49-90847e99d594","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"rubbed","passagePhrase":"polished"},{"uid":"0cf7270c-7788-41bc-bcd6-cbbadbe1940e","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"specific properties","passagePhrase":"melt at a temperature less than the hardening point of glass ... could not boil at a temperature below the temperature of the molten glass"},{"uid":"806aa68c-8583-47c4-8503-51219e8285a3","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"has now been improved","passagePhrase":"has changed"},{"uid":"7f106b54-d28e-4c95-ae7b-ded942a0bc0b","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"Computers","passagePhrase":"Inspection technology"}]},"reading_u2_167":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The Little Ice Age</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong> </p><p>This book will provide a detailed examination of the Little Ice Age and other climatic shifts, but, before I embark on that, let me provide a historical context. We tend to think of climate – as opposed to weather – as something unchanging, yet humanity has been at the mercy of climate change for its entire existence, with at least eight glacial episodes in the past 730,000 years. Our ancestors adapted to the universal but irregular global warming since the end of the last great Ice Age, around 10,000 years ago, with dazzling opportunism. They developed strategies for surviving harsh drought cycles, decades of heavy rainfall or unaccustomed cold; adopted agriculture and stock-raising, which revolutionised human life; and founded the world’s first pre-industrial civilisations in Egypt, Mesopotamia and the Americas. But the price of sudden climate change, in famine, disease and suffering, was often high.</p><p><strong>B</strong> </p><p>The Little Ice Age lasted from roughly 1300 until the middle of the nineteenth century. Only two centuries ago, Europe experienced a cycle of bitterly cold winters; mountain glaciers in the Swiss Alps were the lowest in recorded memory, and pack ice surrounded Iceland for much of the year. The climatic events of the Little Ice Age did more than help shape the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"510f502b-a444-4f9f-b07d-1cf3828271e9\" data-question=\"14\">modern<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> world. They are the deeply important context for the current unprecedented global warming. The Little Ice Age was far from a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"19419fcc-c160-4b19-9e7f-64d74b961df2\" data-question=\"20\">deep freeze<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, however; rather an irregular seesaw of rapid climatic shifts, few lasting more than a quarter-century, driven by complex and still little understood interactions between the atmosphere and the ocean. The seesaw brought <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53b1d1d7-feea-49e4-bad2-62a877d24430\" data-question=\"21\">cycles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of intensely cold winters and easterly winds, then switched abruptly to years of heavy spring and early summer rains, mild winters, and frequent Atlantic storms, or to periods of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c866060-d491-4208-95ed-2706c0f69b31\" data-question=\"22\">droughts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, light northeasterly winds, and summer heat waves.</p><p><strong>C</strong> </p><p>Reconstructing the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0c22d40-a2c8-4eb2-af5b-351b95f4a99c\" data-question=\"18\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d69d5e06-16bc-483e-8f1f-21c32ad20a83\" data-question=\"19\">climate changes of the past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> is extremely difficult, because systematic weather observations began only a few centuries ago, in Europe and North America. Records from India and tropical Africa are even more recent. For the time before records began, we have only ‘proxy records’ reconstructed largely from tree rings and ice cores, supplemented by a few incomplete written accounts. We now have hundreds of tree-ring records from throughout the northern hemisphere, and many from south of the equator, too, amplified with a growing body of temperature data from ice cores drilled in Antarctica, Greenland, the Peruvian Andes, and other locations. We are close to a knowledge of annual summer and winter temperature variations over much of the northern hemisphere going back 600 years.</p><p><strong>D</strong> </p><p>This book is a narrative history of climatic shifts during the past <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3772c563-75ba-4919-86ec-62c84ff2a6d5\" data-question=\"15\">ten centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, and some of the ways in which people in Europe adapted to them. Part One describes the Medieval Warm Period, roughly 900 to 1200. During these three centuries, Norse voyagers from Northern Europe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b07426c-dcef-4313-b065-b16005fa1eec\" data-question=\"25\">explored<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> northern seas, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b07426c-dcef-4313-b065-b16005fa1eec\" data-question=\"25\">settled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> Greenland, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b07426c-dcef-4313-b065-b16005fa1eec\" data-question=\"25\">visited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> North America. It was not a time of uniform warmth, for then, as always since the Great Ice Age, there were constant shifts in rainfall and temperature. Mean European temperatures were about the same as today, perhaps slightly cooler.</p><p><strong>E</strong> </p><p>It is known that the Little Ice Age cooling began in Greenland and the Arctic in about 1200. As the Arctic ice pack spread southward, Norse voyages to the west were rerouted into the open Atlantic, then ended altogether. Storminess increased in the North Atlantic and North Sea. Colder, much wetter weather descended on Europe between 1315 and 1319, when thousands perished in a continent-wide famine. By 1400, the weather had become decidedly more unpredictable and stormier, with sudden shifts and lower temperatures that culminated in the cold decades of the late sixteenth century. Fish were a vital commodity in growing towns and cities, where food supplies were a constant concern. Dried cod and herring were already the staples of the European fish trade, but changes in water temperatures forced fishing fleets to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be1d8910-beba-4483-a104-c4e81099f6e2\" data-question=\"26\">work further offshore<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. The Basques, Dutch, and English developed the first offshore fishing boats adapted to a colder and stormier Atlantic. A gradual agricultural revolution in northern Europe stemmed from concerns over food supplies at a time of rising populations. The revolution involved intensive commercial farming and the growing of animal fodder on land not previously used for crops. The increased productivity from farmland made some countries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7d574bc-d78e-4c0c-b7a6-3776dcccda24\" data-question=\"16\">self-sufficient<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in grain and livestock and offered effective protection against famine.</p><p><strong>F</strong> </p><p>Global temperatures began to rise slowly after 1850, with the beginning of the Modern Warm Period. There was a vast <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"518df281-45d9-4da0-a0df-b006276cccb3\" data-question=\"23\">migration from Europe by land-hungry farmers and others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, to which the famine caused by the Irish potato blight contributed, to North America, Australia, New Zealand, and southern Africa. Millions of hectares of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5e2e472-fb80-4af0-b2f0-30725a3ec4cf\" data-question=\"24\">forest and woodland fell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> before the newcomers’ axes between 1850 and 1890, as intensive European farming methods expanded across the world. The unprecedented land clearance released vast quantities of carbon dioxide into the atmosphere, triggering for the first time <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b95ada0-3887-4049-8cec-58c799c4c41b\" data-question=\"17\">humanly caused<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> global warming. Temperatures climbed more rapidly in the twentieth century as the use of fossil fuels proliferated and greenhouse gas levels continued to soar. The rise has been even steeper since the early 1980s. The Little Ice Age has given way to a new climatic regime, marked by prolonged and steady warming. At the same time, extreme weather events like Category 5 hurricanes are becoming more frequent.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A—F. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs B and D—F from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i—ix, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><ul><li>i Predicting climatic changes</li><li>ii The relevance of the Little Ice Age <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"510f502b-a444-4f9f-b07d-1cf3828271e9\" data-question=\"14\">today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></li><li>iii How cities contribute to climate change</li><li>iv <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b95ada0-3887-4049-8cec-58c799c4c41b\" data-question=\"17\">Human impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e5ebc4d-b3fc-447c-9540-e667f19d5555\" data-question=\"17\">climate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></li><li>v How past climatic conditions can be determined</li><li>vi A growing need for weather records</li><li>vii A study covering <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3772c563-75ba-4919-86ec-62c84ff2a6d5\" data-question=\"15\">a thousand years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></li><li>viii People have always responded to climate change</li><li>ix <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7d574bc-d78e-4c0c-b7a6-3776dcccda24\" data-question=\"16\">Enough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> food at last</li></ul><p>Example Answer Paragraph A viii</p><p>Example Answer Paragraph C v</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28981\" id=\"question-wrapper-28981\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28982\" id=\"question-wrapper-28982\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28983\" id=\"question-wrapper-28983\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IX</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28984\" id=\"question-wrapper-28984\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary using the list of words, A—I, below. Write the correct letter, A—I, in boxes 18-22 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>Weather during the Little Ice Age</strong><br>Documentation of past weather condition is limited: our main sources of knowledge of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0c22d40-a2c8-4eb2-af5b-351b95f4a99c\" data-question=\"18\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d69d5e06-16bc-483e-8f1f-21c32ad20a83\" data-question=\"19\">conditions in the distant past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> are (18)………………. and (19)………………… . We can deduce that the Little Ice Age was a time of (20)…………… , rather than of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"19419fcc-c160-4b19-9e7f-64d74b961df2\" data-question=\"20\">consistent freezing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Within it there were some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53b1d1d7-feea-49e4-bad2-62a877d24430\" data-question=\"21\">periods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of very cold winters, others of (21)…………. and heavy rain, and yet others that saw (22)…………. with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c866060-d491-4208-95ed-2706c0f69b31\" data-question=\"22\">no rain at all<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</p><ul><li>A climatic shifts</li><li>B ice cores</li><li>C tree rings</li><li>D glaciers</li><li>E interactions</li><li>F weather observations</li><li>G heat waves</li><li>H storms </li><li>I written accounts </li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28985\" id=\"question-wrapper-28985\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28986\" id=\"question-wrapper-28986\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28987\" id=\"question-wrapper-28987\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28988\" id=\"question-wrapper-28988\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28989\" id=\"question-wrapper-28989\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Classify the following events as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fe6ed1d-b9dd-491a-8558-da9c18e27e97\" data-question=\"26\">occurring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> during the</p><p><strong>A</strong> Medieval Warm Period<br><strong>B</strong> Little Ice Age<br><strong>C</strong> Modem Warm Period</p><p>Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28990\" id=\"question-wrapper-28990\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Many Europeans started <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"518df281-45d9-4da0-a0df-b006276cccb3\" data-question=\"23\">farming abroad<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28991\" id=\"question-wrapper-28991\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5e2e472-fb80-4af0-b2f0-30725a3ec4cf\" data-question=\"24\">The cutting down of trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> began to affect the climate. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28992\" id=\"question-wrapper-28992\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Europeans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b07426c-dcef-4313-b065-b16005fa1eec\" data-question=\"25\">discovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> other lands. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28993\" id=\"question-wrapper-28993\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Changes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fe6ed1d-b9dd-491a-8558-da9c18e27e97\" data-question=\"26\">took place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be1d8910-beba-4483-a104-c4e81099f6e2\" data-question=\"26\">fishing patterns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"510f502b-a444-4f9f-b07d-1cf3828271e9","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"today","passagePhrase":"modern"},{"uid":"19419fcc-c160-4b19-9e7f-64d74b961df2","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"consistent freezing","passagePhrase":"deep freeze"},{"uid":"53b1d1d7-feea-49e4-bad2-62a877d24430","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"periods","passagePhrase":"cycles"},{"uid":"2c866060-d491-4208-95ed-2706c0f69b31","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"no rain at all","passagePhrase":"droughts"},{"uid":"f0c22d40-a2c8-4eb2-af5b-351b95f4a99c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"conditions in the distant past","passagePhrase":"climate changes of the past"},{"uid":"d69d5e06-16bc-483e-8f1f-21c32ad20a83","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"conditions in the distant past","passagePhrase":"climate changes of the past"},{"uid":"3772c563-75ba-4919-86ec-62c84ff2a6d5","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"a thousand years","passagePhrase":"ten centuries"},{"uid":"3b07426c-dcef-4313-b065-b16005fa1eec","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"discovered","passagePhrase":"explored ... settled ... visited"},{"uid":"be1d8910-beba-4483-a104-c4e81099f6e2","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"fishing patterns","passagePhrase":"work further offshore"},{"uid":"a7d574bc-d78e-4c0c-b7a6-3776dcccda24","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Enough","passagePhrase":"self-sufficient"},{"uid":"518df281-45d9-4da0-a0df-b006276cccb3","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"farming abroad","passagePhrase":"migration from Europe by land-hungry farmers and others"},{"uid":"b5e2e472-fb80-4af0-b2f0-30725a3ec4cf","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"The cutting down of trees","passagePhrase":"forest and woodland fell"},{"uid":"8b95ada0-3887-4049-8cec-58c799c4c41b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Human impact","passagePhrase":"humanly caused"},{"uid":"6e5ebc4d-b3fc-447c-9540-e667f19d5555","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"climate","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"2fe6ed1d-b9dd-491a-8558-da9c18e27e97","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"occurring ... took place","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_168":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The meaning and power of smell</strong></p><p><em>The sense of smell, or olfaction, is powerful. Odours affect us on a physical, psychological and social level. For the most part, however, we breathe in the aromas which surround us without being consciously aware of their importance to us. It is only when the faculty of smell is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36cea9eb-13b2-481c-9ecc-3730080d01b7\" data-question=\"33\">impaired<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> for some reason that we begin to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"42a73701-b4ea-4b2d-8e33-aea538c84fa4\" data-question=\"33\">realise the essential role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> the sense of smell plays in our sense of well-being.</em></p><p><strong>A</strong> </p><p>A survey conducted by Anthony Synott at Montreal’s Concordia University asked participants to comment on how important smell was to them in their lives. It became apparent that smell can evoke strong <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e2549158-1eec-40b2-93de-8cfec7bca95d\" data-question=\"27\">emotional responses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. A scent associated with a good experience can bring a rush of joy, while a foul odour or one associated with a bad memory may make us grimace with disgust. Respondents to the survey noted that many of their olfactory likes and dislikes were based on emotional associations. Such associations can be powerful enough so that odours that we would generally label unpleasant become agreeable, and those that we would generally consider fragrant become disagreeable for particular individuals. The perception of smell, therefore, consists not only of the sensation of the odours themselves, but of the experiences and emotions associated with them.</p><p><strong>B</strong> </p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53593615-e4af-4778-bb69-7e038a246353\" data-question=\"28\">Odours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> are also essential cues in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf5113bb-0d0a-4e3e-92aa-ac200c00f103\" data-question=\"28\">social bonding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. One respondent to the survey believed that there is no true emotional bonding without touching and smelling a loved one. In fact, infants recognise the odours of their mothers soon after birth and adults can often identify their children or spouses by scent. In one well-known test, women and men were able to distinguish by smell alone clothing worn by their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70a21ea9-4557-4d2e-af71-1e9ca19d07c4\" data-question=\"37\">marriage partners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> from similar clothing worn by other people. Most of the subjects would probably never have given much thought to odour as a cue for identifying family members before being involved in the test, but as the experiment revealed, even when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4e5e575-fbb4-4e78-8d37-b11aff985ecf\" data-question=\"34\">not consciously considered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, smells register.</p><p><strong>C</strong> </p><p>In spite of its importance to our emotional and sensory lives, smell is probably the most undervalued sense in many cultures. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"127ce03f-7dee-4acc-a625-8d99b750715c\" data-question=\"29\">The reason<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> often given for the low regard in which smell is held is that, in comparison with its importance among animals, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2e91bd9-34f9-4cd1-b54d-e0d82e56a39d\" data-question=\"35\">the human sense of smell is feeble and undeveloped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. While it is true that the olfactory powers of humans are nothing like as fine as those possessed by certain animals, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0e1f842-8c14-418c-a663-46be1cecd0d6\" data-question=\"35\">they are still remarkably acute<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Our noses are able to recognise thousands of smells, and to perceive odours which are present only in extremely small quantities.</p><p><strong>D</strong> </p><p>Smell, however, is a highly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"733dfac1-407a-4473-868c-c7ab87868c4c\" data-question=\"30\">elusive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> phenomenon. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"346a0482-da1a-4d8a-8eac-9f4fa427a2de\" data-question=\"31\">Odours, unlike colours,<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> for instance, cannot be named in many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af3c000d-e7d8-413d-9fe8-f0cf67b45309\" data-question=\"38\">languages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> because the specific vocabulary simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f23a3517-297b-47cf-982c-d7fca1633631\" data-question=\"38\">doesn’t exist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. ‘It smells like . . .,’ we have to say when describing an odour, struggling to express our olfactory experience. Nor can odours be recorded: there is no effective way to either capture or store them over time. In the realm of olfaction, we must make do with descriptions and recollections. This has implications for olfactory research.</p><p><strong>E</strong> </p><p>Most of the research on smell undertaken to date has been of a physical scientific nature. Significant advances have been made in the understanding of the biological and chemical nature of olfaction, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d4e01bf-2776-42d8-966a-80058316ce8b\" data-question=\"31\">many fundamental questions have yet to be answered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Researchers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af14604f-89ae-42ee-b7be-6594aa6fbb18\" data-question=\"36\">have still to decide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> whether smell is one sense or two – one responding to odours proper and the other registering <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ae20ea2-e718-4d0a-bf0c-1e9aea21a88f\" data-question=\"39\">odourless<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> chemicals in the air. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d4e01bf-2776-42d8-966a-80058316ce8b\" data-question=\"31\">Other unanswered questions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> are whether the nose is the only part of the body affected by odours, and how smells can be measured objectively given the nonphysical components. Questions like these mean that interest in the psychology of smell is inevitably set to play an increasingly important role for researchers.</p><p><strong>F</strong> </p><p>However, smell is not simply a biological and psychological phenomenon. Smell is cultural, hence it is a social and historical phenomenon. Odours are invested with cultural values: smells that are considered to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93e79e01-d4a2-4509-a130-c05b2dd7c547\" data-question=\"40\">offensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> in some cultures may be perfectly acceptable in others. Therefore, our sense of smell is a means of, and model for, interacting with the world. Different smells can provide us with intimate and emotionally charged experiences and the value that we attach to these experiences is interiorised by the members of society in a deeply personal way. Importantly, our commonly held feelings about smells can help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc46761c-a8f9-408c-928c-c9cc4d6e97ce\" data-question=\"32\">distinguish us from other cultures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. The study of the cultural history of smell is, therefore, in a very real sense, an investigation into the essence of human culture.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 3 has six paragraphs, A—F. Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</p><p>Write the correct number, i—viii, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><ul><li>i The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"733dfac1-407a-4473-868c-c7ab87868c4c\" data-question=\"30\">difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> of talking about smells</li><li>ii The role of smell in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf5113bb-0d0a-4e3e-92aa-ac200c00f103\" data-question=\"28\">personal relationships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></li><li>iii <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d4e01bf-2776-42d8-966a-80058316ce8b\" data-question=\"31\">Future studies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"346a0482-da1a-4d8a-8eac-9f4fa427a2de\" data-question=\"31\">smell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></li><li>iv The relationship between the brain and the nose</li><li>v The interpretation of smells as a factor in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc46761c-a8f9-408c-928c-c9cc4d6e97ce\" data-question=\"32\">defining groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></li><li>vi <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"127ce03f-7dee-4acc-a625-8d99b750715c\" data-question=\"29\">Why<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> our sense of smell is not appreciated</li><li>vii Smell is our superior sense</li><li>viii The relationship between smell and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e2549158-1eec-40b2-93de-8cfec7bca95d\" data-question=\"27\">feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28994\" id=\"question-wrapper-28994\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28995\" id=\"question-wrapper-28995\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28996\" id=\"question-wrapper-28996\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28997\" id=\"question-wrapper-28997\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28998\" id=\"question-wrapper-28998\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28999\" id=\"question-wrapper-28999\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29000\" id=\"question-wrapper-29000\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the introduction, we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"42a73701-b4ea-4b2d-8e33-aea538c84fa4\" data-question=\"33\">become aware of the importance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of smell when </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. we discover a new smell</li> <li>B. we experience a powerful smell</li> <li>C. our ability to smell is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36cea9eb-13b2-481c-9ecc-3730080d01b7\" data-question=\"33\">damaged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></li> <li>D. we are surrounded by odours</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29001\" id=\"question-wrapper-29001\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The experiment described in paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. shows how we make use of smell <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4e5e575-fbb4-4e78-8d37-b11aff985ecf\" data-question=\"34\">without realising it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span></li> <li>B. demonstrates that family members have a similar smell</li> <li>C. proves that a sense of smell is learnt</li> <li>D. compares the sense of smell in males and females</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29002\" id=\"question-wrapper-29002\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer doing in paragraph C? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. supporting other research</li> <li>B. making a proposal</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0e1f842-8c14-418c-a663-46be1cecd0d6\" data-question=\"35\">rejecting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2e91bd9-34f9-4cd1-b54d-e0d82e56a39d\" data-question=\"35\">common belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></li> <li>D. describing limitations</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29003\" id=\"question-wrapper-29003\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer suggest about the study of smell in the atmosphere in paragraph E? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The measurement of smell is becoming more accurate</li> <li>B. Researchers believe smell is a purely physical reaction</li> <li>C. Most smells are inoffensive</li> <li>D. Smell <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af14604f-89ae-42ee-b7be-6594aa6fbb18\" data-question=\"36\">is yet to be defined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the sentences below. Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29004\" id=\"question-wrapper-29004\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Tests have shown that odours can help people recognise the………………..belonging to their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70a21ea9-4557-4d2e-af71-1e9ca19d07c4\" data-question=\"37\">husbands and wives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CLOTHING</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29005\" id=\"question-wrapper-29005\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Certain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af3c000d-e7d8-413d-9fe8-f0cf67b45309\" data-question=\"38\">linguistic groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> may have difficulty describing smell because they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f23a3517-297b-47cf-982c-d7fca1633631\" data-question=\"38\">lack<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> the appropriate…………… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VOCABULARY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29006\" id=\"question-wrapper-29006\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The sense of smell may involve response to…………………<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ae20ea2-e718-4d0a-bf0c-1e9aea21a88f\" data-question=\"39\">which do not smell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, in addition to obvious odours. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CHEMICALS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29007\" id=\"question-wrapper-29007\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Odours regarded as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93e79e01-d4a2-4509-a130-c05b2dd7c547\" data-question=\"40\">unpleasant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> in certain……………………….are not regarded as unpleasant in others. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CULTURES</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"36cea9eb-13b2-481c-9ecc-3730080d01b7","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"damaged","passagePhrase":"impaired"},{"uid":"42a73701-b4ea-4b2d-8e33-aea538c84fa4","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"become aware of the importance","passagePhrase":"realise the essential role"},{"uid":"e2549158-1eec-40b2-93de-8cfec7bca95d","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"feelings","passagePhrase":"emotional responses"},{"uid":"53593615-e4af-4778-bb69-7e038a246353","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"Odours"},{"uid":"cf5113bb-0d0a-4e3e-92aa-ac200c00f103","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"personal relationships","passagePhrase":"social bonding"},{"uid":"70a21ea9-4557-4d2e-af71-1e9ca19d07c4","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"husbands and wives","passagePhrase":"marriage partners"},{"uid":"f4e5e575-fbb4-4e78-8d37-b11aff985ecf","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"without realising it","passagePhrase":"not consciously considered"},{"uid":"127ce03f-7dee-4acc-a625-8d99b750715c","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Why","passagePhrase":"The reason"},{"uid":"a2e91bd9-34f9-4cd1-b54d-e0d82e56a39d","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"common belief","passagePhrase":"the human sense of smell is feeble and undeveloped"},{"uid":"f0e1f842-8c14-418c-a663-46be1cecd0d6","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"rejecting","passagePhrase":"they are still remarkably acute"},{"uid":"733dfac1-407a-4473-868c-c7ab87868c4c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"difficulties","passagePhrase":"elusive"},{"uid":"346a0482-da1a-4d8a-8eac-9f4fa427a2de","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"smell","passagePhrase":"Odours, unlike colours,"},{"uid":"af3c000d-e7d8-413d-9fe8-f0cf67b45309","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"linguistic groups","passagePhrase":"languages"},{"uid":"f23a3517-297b-47cf-982c-d7fca1633631","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"lack","passagePhrase":"doesn’t exist"},{"uid":"9d4e01bf-2776-42d8-966a-80058316ce8b","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Future studies","passagePhrase":"many fundamental questions have yet to be answered ... Other unanswered questions"},{"uid":"af14604f-89ae-42ee-b7be-6594aa6fbb18","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"is yet to be defined","passagePhrase":"have still to decide"},{"uid":"2ae20ea2-e718-4d0a-bf0c-1e9aea21a88f","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"which do not smell","passagePhrase":"odourless"},{"uid":"93e79e01-d4a2-4509-a130-c05b2dd7c547","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"unpleasant","passagePhrase":"offensive"},{"uid":"dc46761c-a8f9-408c-928c-c9cc4d6e97ce","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"defining groups","passagePhrase":"distinguish us from other cultures"}]},"reading_u2_169":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Striking Back at Lightning with Lasers</strong></p><p>Seldom is the weather more dramatic than when thunderstorms strike. Their electrical fury inflicts death or serious injury on around 500 people each year in the United States alone. As the clouds roll in, a leisurely round of golf can become a terrifying dice with death – out in the open, a lone golfer may be a lightning bolt’s most inviting target. And there is damage to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eba66131-fe08-43a3-99ea-3b94a8811926\" data-question=\"2\">property<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> too. Lightning damage costs American power companies more than $100 million a year.</p><p>But researchers in the United States and Japan are planning to hit back. Already in laboratory trials they have tested strategies for neutralising the power of thunderstorms, and this winter they will brave real storms, equipped with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da549c2c-e661-4545-93ca-bd129160255e\" data-question=\"1\">an armoury of lasers that they will be pointing towards the heavens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> to discharge thunderclouds before lightning can strike.</p><p>The idea of forcing storm clouds to discharge their lightning on command is not new. In the early 1960s, researchers tried <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e0985393-caba-4f10-bd44-c1ffa32ffb1b\" data-question=\"9\">firing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> rockets trailing wires into thunderclouds to set up an easy discharge path for the huge electric charges that these clouds generate. The technique survives to this day at a test site in Florida run by the University of Florida, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47dd212c-3aba-43f2-adc3-ff6ee0501e38\" data-question=\"3\">with support from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the Electrical Power Research Institute (EPRI), based in California. EPRI, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d2d70bc-7c8d-4240-8bd4-07d231754a98\" data-question=\"4\">is funded by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> power companies, is looking at ways to protect the United States’ power grid from lightning strikes. ‘We can cause the lightning to strike where we want it to using rockets,’ says Ralph Bernstein, manager of lightning projects at EPRI. The rocket site is providing precise measurements of lightning voltages and allowing engineers to check how electrical equipment bears up.</p><p><strong>Bad behaviour</strong></p><p>But while rockets are fine for research, they cannot provide the protection from lightning strikes that everyone is looking for. The rockets cost around $1,200 each, can only be fired at a limited frequency and their failure rate is about 40 per cent. And even when they do trigger lightning, things still do not always go according to plan. ‘Lightning is not perfectly well behaved,’ says Bernstein. ‘Occasionally, it will take a branch and go someplace it wasn’t supposed to go.’</p><p>And anyway, who would want to fire streams of rockets in a populated area? ‘What goes up must come down,’ points out Jean-Claude Diels of the University of New Mexico. Diels is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1738d28-c764-49ea-a975-7079948cfb1b\" data-question=\"5\">leading a project<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47dd212c-3aba-43f2-adc3-ff6ee0501e38\" data-question=\"3\">is backed by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> EPRI, to try to use lasers to discharge lightning safely – and safety is a basic requirement since no one wants to put themselves or their expensive equipment at risk. With around $500,000 invested so far, a promising system is just emerging from the laboratory.</p><p>The idea began some 20 years ago, when high-powered lasers were revealing their ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"52e29318-bec8-49aa-b0ee-fa61f71242c1\" data-question=\"7\">extract<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> electrons out of atoms and create ions. If a laser could generate a line of ionisation in the air <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3aed9e8-3a78-4f17-a680-46ae03efc7d4\" data-question=\"8\">all the way up to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> a storm cloud, this conducting path could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90f3450b-8377-4826-80bd-f3271b92f1a2\" data-question=\"8\">be used to guide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> lightning to Earth, before the electric field becomes strong enough to break down the air in an uncontrollable surge. To stop the laser itself being struck, it would not be pointed straight at the clouds. Instead it would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80e71477-d7c7-4b89-9490-f442fbf20886\" data-question=\"10\">be directed at a mirror<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, and from there into the sky. The mirror would be protected by placing lightning conductors close by. Ideally, the cloud-zapper (gun) would be cheap enough to be installed around all key power installations, and portable enough to be taken to international sporting events to beam up at brewing storm clouds.</p><p><strong>A stumbling block</strong></p><p>However, there is still a big <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"339e50a2-b2ce-40ae-bfe0-baf55673e4e4\" data-question=\"6\">stumbling block<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. The laser is no nifty portable: it’s a monster that takes up a whole room. Diels is trying to cut down the size and says that a laser around the size of a small table is in the offing. He plans to test this more manageable system on live thunderclouds next summer.</p><p>Bernstein says that Diels’s system is attracting lots of interest from the power companies. But they have <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7ebcd29b-4d86-46b2-ac8b-b177a552913d\" data-question=\"11\">not yet come up with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the $5 million that EPRI says will be needed to develop a commercial system, by making the lasers yet smaller and cheaper. ‘I cannot say I have money yet, but I’m working on it,’ says Bernstein. He reckons that the forthcoming <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d0299f2-91ad-4282-8990-c29733b8a19f\" data-question=\"12\">field tests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> will be the turning point – and he’s hoping for good news. Bernstein predicts ‘an avalanche of interest and support’ if all goes well. He expects to see cloud-zappers eventually costing $50,000 to $100,000 each.</p><p>Other scientists could also benefit. With a lightning ‘switch’ at their fingertips, materials scientists could find out what happens when mighty currents meet matter. Diels also hopes to see the birth of ‘interactive meteorology’ – not just forecasting the weather but controlling it. ‘If we could discharge clouds, we might affect the weather,’ he says.</p><p>And perhaps, says Diels, we’ll be able to confront some other meteorological menaces. ‘We think we could prevent hail by inducing lightning,’ he says. Thunder, the shock wave that comes from a lightning flash, is thought to be the trigger for the torrential rain that is typical of storms. A laser thunder factory could shake the moisture out of clouds, perhaps preventing the formation of the giant hailstones that threaten crops. With luck, as the storm clouds gather this winter, laser-toting researchers could, for the first time, strike back.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 1-3 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29008\" id=\"question-wrapper-29008\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The main topic discussed in the text is </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the damage caused to US golf courses and golf players by lightning strikes.</li> <li>B. the effect of lightning on power supplies in the US and in Japan.</li> <li>C. a variety of methods used in trying to control lightning strikes.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da549c2c-e661-4545-93ca-bd129160255e\" data-question=\"1\">a laser technique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> used in trying to control lightning strikes.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29009\" id=\"question-wrapper-29009\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the text, every year lightning </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. does considerable damage to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eba66131-fe08-43a3-99ea-3b94a8811926\" data-question=\"2\">buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> during thunderstorms.</li> <li>B. kills or injures mainly golfers in the United States.</li> <li>C. kills or injures around 500 people throughout the world.</li> <li>D. damages more than 100 American power companies.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29010\" id=\"question-wrapper-29010\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Researchers at the University of Florida and at the University of New Mexico </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47dd212c-3aba-43f2-adc3-ff6ee0501e38\" data-question=\"3\">receive funds from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the same source</li> <li>B. are using the same techniques</li> <li>C. are employed by commercial companies</li> <li>D. are in opposition to each other</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the sentences below. Write <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS.</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29011\" id=\"question-wrapper-29011\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> EPRI <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d2d70bc-7c8d-4240-8bd4-07d231754a98\" data-question=\"4\">receives financial support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> from……………… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POWER COMPANIES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29012\" id=\"question-wrapper-29012\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The advantage of the technique being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1738d28-c764-49ea-a975-7079948cfb1b\" data-question=\"5\">developed by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> Diels is that it can be used …………….. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SAFELY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29013\" id=\"question-wrapper-29013\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The main <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"339e50a2-b2ce-40ae-bfe0-baf55673e4e4\" data-question=\"6\">difficulty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> associated with using the laser equipment is related to its…………….. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SIZE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary using the list of words, A-I, below.<br>Write the correct letter, A-I, in boxes 7-10 on your answer sheet.</p><p>In this method, a laser is used to create a line of ionisation by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"52e29318-bec8-49aa-b0ee-fa61f71242c1\" data-question=\"7\">removing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> electrons from (7) ………………. This laser <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3aed9e8-3a78-4f17-a680-46ae03efc7d4\" data-question=\"8\">is then directed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> at (8) ………………….. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90f3450b-8377-4826-80bd-f3271b92f1a2\" data-question=\"8\">in order to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> control electrical charges, a method which is less dangerous than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e0985393-caba-4f10-bd44-c1ffa32ffb1b\" data-question=\"9\">using<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> (9) ………………….. As a protection for the lasers, the beams <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80e71477-d7c7-4b89-9490-f442fbf20886\" data-question=\"10\">are aimed firstly at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> (10) …………………..</p><ul><li>A cloud-zappers</li><li>B atoms</li><li>C storm clouds</li><li>D mirrors</li><li>E technique</li><li>F ions</li><li>G rockets </li><li>H conductors </li><li>I thunder </li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29014\" id=\"question-wrapper-29014\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29015\" id=\"question-wrapper-29015\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29016\" id=\"question-wrapper-29016\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29017\" id=\"question-wrapper-29017\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?<br>In boxes 11-13 on your answer sheet write:</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29018\" id=\"question-wrapper-29018\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Power companies <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7ebcd29b-4d86-46b2-ac8b-b177a552913d\" data-question=\"11\">have given<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> Diels enough money to develop his laser. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29019\" id=\"question-wrapper-29019\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Obtaining money to improve the lasers will depend on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d0299f2-91ad-4282-8990-c29733b8a19f\" data-question=\"12\">tests in real storms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29020\" id=\"question-wrapper-29020\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Weather forecasters are intensely interested in Diels’s system. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"eba66131-fe08-43a3-99ea-3b94a8811926","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"buildings","passagePhrase":"property"},{"uid":"da549c2c-e661-4545-93ca-bd129160255e","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"a laser technique","passagePhrase":"an armoury of lasers that they will be pointing towards the heavens"},{"uid":"e0985393-caba-4f10-bd44-c1ffa32ffb1b","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"using","passagePhrase":"firing"},{"uid":"47dd212c-3aba-43f2-adc3-ff6ee0501e38","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"receive funds from","passagePhrase":"with support from ... is backed by"},{"uid":"3d2d70bc-7c8d-4240-8bd4-07d231754a98","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"receives financial support","passagePhrase":"is funded by"},{"uid":"a1738d28-c764-49ea-a975-7079948cfb1b","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"developed by","passagePhrase":"leading a project"},{"uid":"52e29318-bec8-49aa-b0ee-fa61f71242c1","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"removing","passagePhrase":"extract"},{"uid":"b3aed9e8-3a78-4f17-a680-46ae03efc7d4","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"is then directed","passagePhrase":"all the way up to"},{"uid":"90f3450b-8377-4826-80bd-f3271b92f1a2","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"in order to","passagePhrase":"be used to guide"},{"uid":"80e71477-d7c7-4b89-9490-f442fbf20886","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"are aimed firstly at","passagePhrase":"be directed at a mirror"},{"uid":"339e50a2-b2ce-40ae-bfe0-baf55673e4e4","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"difficulty","passagePhrase":"stumbling block"},{"uid":"6d0299f2-91ad-4282-8990-c29733b8a19f","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"tests in real storms","passagePhrase":"field tests"}]},"reading_u2_170":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The Nature of Genius</strong></p><p>There has always been an interest in geniuses and prodigies. The word ‘genius’, from the Latin gens (= family) and the term ‘genius’, meaning ‘begetter’, comes from the early Roman cult of a divinity as the head of the family. In its earliest form, genius was concerned with the ability of the head of the family, the paterfamilias, to perpetuate himself. Gradually, genius came to represent a person’s characteristics and thence an individual’s highest attributes derived from his ‘genius’ or guiding spirit. Today, people still look to stars or genes, astrology or genetics, in the hope of finding the source of exceptional abilities or personal characteristics.</p><p>The concept of genius and of gifts has become part of our folk culture, and attitudes are ambivalent towards them. We envy the gifted and mistrust them. In the mythology of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b219a8ba-aef3-48c4-9852-33d4f036354b\" data-question=\"14\">giftedness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, it is popularly believed that if people are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca917880-723f-4323-8c64-90951d2c31d6\" data-question=\"15\">talented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in one area, they must be defective in another, that intellectuals are impractical, that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6a2e923-ad98-4266-9b77-6c948e3c2c5a\" data-question=\"14\">prodigies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> burn too brightly too soon and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"223dca1f-379e-45b9-ad79-f24e2eecdd6b\" data-question=\"14\">burn out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6a2e923-ad98-4266-9b77-6c948e3c2c5a\" data-question=\"14\">gifted people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> are eccentric, that they are physical weaklings, that there’s a thin line between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"38822d56-5ef3-4236-88a1-407e1578080f\" data-question=\"16\">genius<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> and madness, that genius <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca9724e6-a483-4934-a25b-e033f82f1e9c\" data-question=\"16\">runs in families<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6a2e923-ad98-4266-9b77-6c948e3c2c5a\" data-question=\"14\">the gifted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> are so clever they don’t need special help, that giftedness is the same as having a high IQ, that some races are more intelligent or musical or mathematical than others, that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"234a2eb0-ac14-45ab-82a6-531bf43c181c\" data-question=\"17\">genius goes unrecognised and unrewarded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea38139d-881b-4722-b132-92c9033b8a81\" data-question=\"18\">adversity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> makes men wise or that people with gifts <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5b36f274-e6e3-4ad6-8b1b-043b94bcde69\" data-question=\"15\">have a responsibility to use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> them. Language has been enriched with such terms as ‘highbrow’, ‘egghead’, ‘blue-stocking’, ‘wiseacre’, ‘know-all’, ‘boffin’ and, for many, ‘intellectual’ is a term of denigration.</p><p>The nineteenth century saw considerable interest in the nature of genius, and produced not a few studies of famous prodigies. Perhaps for us today, two of the most significant aspects of most of these studies of genius are the frequency with which early encouragement and teaching by parents and tutors had beneficial effects on the intellectual, artistic or musical development of the children but caused great difficulties of adjustment later in their lives, and the frequency with which abilities went unrecognised by teachers and schools. However, the difficulty with the evidence produced by these studies, fascinating as they are in collecting together anecdotes and apparent similarities and exceptions, is that they are not what we would today call norm-referenced. In other words, when, for instance, information is collated about early illnesses, methods of upbringing, schooling, etc., we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"348c17b7-3b73-485e-b6bc-4fbb2c992f5d\" data-question=\"19\">must also take into account information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> from other historical sources about how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe179c3c-5da0-43c2-87d8-35447036ca32\" data-question=\"19\">common or exceptional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> these were at the time. For instance, infant mortality was high and life expectancy much shorter than today, home tutoring was common in the families of the nobility and wealthy, bullying and corporal punishment were common at the best independent schools and, for the most part, the cases studied were members of the privileged classes. It was only with the growth of paediatrics and psychology in the twentieth century that studies could be carried out on a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8317b5c-58fe-45c9-89e8-b5747f083a1c\" data-question=\"20\">more objective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, if still <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55c1c319-0df5-49c2-96cc-844b453b6748\" data-question=\"20\">not always very scientific<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, basis.</p><p>Geniuses, however they are defined, are but the peaks which stand out through the mist of history and are visible to the particular observer from his or her particular vantage point. Change the observers and the vantage points, clear away some of the mist, and a different lot of peaks appear. Genius is a term we apply to those whom we recognise for their outstanding achievements and who stand near the end of the continuum of human abilities which reaches back through the mundane and mediocre to the incapable. There is still much truth in Dr. Samuel Johnson’s observation, ‘The true genius is a mind of large general powers, accidentally determined <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"069cb600-d7f0-45a9-bc70-b47a06dcac1e\" data-question=\"21\">to some particular direction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>’. We may disagree with the ‘general’, for we doubt if all musicians of genius could have become scientists of genius or vice versa, but there is no doubting the accidental determination which nurtured or triggered their gifts into those channels into which they have poured their powers so successfully. Along the continuum of abilities are hundreds of thousands of gifted men and women, boys and girls.</p><p>What we appreciate, enjoy or marvel at in the works of genius or the achievements of prodigies are the manifestations of skills or abilities which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"50761ff6-7971-46d0-9f9e-3955c9831fae\" data-question=\"22\">similar to, but so much superior to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ed0b01d-084f-49b8-bd29-f581cfa76b0d\" data-question=\"22\">our own<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. But that their minds are not different from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ed0b01d-084f-49b8-bd29-f581cfa76b0d\" data-question=\"22\">our own<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> is demonstrated by the fact that the hard-won discoveries of scientists like Kepler or Einstein become the commonplace knowledge of schoolchildren and the once outrageous shapes and colours of an artist like Paul Klee so soon appear on the fabrics we wear. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"97623719-97ed-4df2-a75b-1374ffdbdb17\" data-question=\"23\">does not minimise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> the supremacy of their achievements, which outstrip <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ed0b01d-084f-49b8-bd29-f581cfa76b0d\" data-question=\"22\">our own<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> as the sub-four-minute milers outstrip our jogging.</p><p>To think of geniuses and the gifted as having uniquely different brains is only reasonable if we accept that each human brain is uniquely different. The purpose of instruction is to make us even more different from one another, and in the process of being educated we can learn from the achievements of those more gifted than ourselves. But before we try to emulate geniuses or encourage our children to do so we should note that some of the things we learn from them may prove unpalatable. We may envy their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7230cb48-7b57-4c56-a895-57b6b2fb5b3a\" data-question=\"25\">achievements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7230cb48-7b57-4c56-a895-57b6b2fb5b3a\" data-question=\"25\">fame<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, but we should also recognise <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f29fa38-b13f-4ba5-a8b1-8729ffa4a5b4\" data-question=\"25\">the price they may have paid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> in terms of perseverance, single-mindedness, dedication, restrictions on their personal lives, the demands upon their energies and time, and how often they had to display great courage to preserve their integrity or to make their way to the top.</p><p>Genius and giftedness are relative descriptive terms of no real substance. We may, at best, give them some precision by defining them and placing them in a context but, whatever we do, we should never delude ourselves into believing that gifted children or geniuses are different from the rest of humanity, save in the degree to which they have developed the performance of their abilities.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose <strong>FIVE</strong> letters, A—K. Write the correct letters in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.<br>NB Your answers maybe given in any order.<br>Below are listed some popular beliefs about genius and giftedness.</p><p>Which <strong>FIVE</strong> of these beliefs are reported by the writer of the text?</p><ul><li><strong>A</strong> Truly gifted people are talented in all areas.</li><li><strong>B</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b219a8ba-aef3-48c4-9852-33d4f036354b\" data-question=\"14\">The talents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6a2e923-ad98-4266-9b77-6c948e3c2c5a\" data-question=\"14\">geniuses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> are soon <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"223dca1f-379e-45b9-ad79-f24e2eecdd6b\" data-question=\"14\">exhausted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</li><li><strong>C</strong> Gifted people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5b36f274-e6e3-4ad6-8b1b-043b94bcde69\" data-question=\"15\">should use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca917880-723f-4323-8c64-90951d2c31d6\" data-question=\"15\">gifts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</li><li><strong>D</strong> A genius appears once in every generation.</li><li><strong>E</strong> Genius can be easily destroyed by discouragement.</li><li><strong>F</strong> Genius <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca9724e6-a483-4934-a25b-e033f82f1e9c\" data-question=\"16\">is inherited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</li><li><strong>G</strong> Gifted people are very hard to live with.</li><li><strong>H</strong> People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"234a2eb0-ac14-45ab-82a6-531bf43c181c\" data-question=\"17\">never appreciate true genius<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</li><li><strong>I</strong> Geniuses are natural leaders.</li><li><strong>J</strong> Gifted people develop their greatness through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea38139d-881b-4722-b132-92c9033b8a81\" data-question=\"18\">difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</li><li><strong>K</strong> Genius will always reveal itself.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29021\" id=\"question-wrapper-29021\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/F/H/J</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29022\" id=\"question-wrapper-29022\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/F/H/J</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29023\" id=\"question-wrapper-29023\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/F/H/J</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29024\" id=\"question-wrapper-29024\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/F/H/J</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29025\" id=\"question-wrapper-29025\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C/F/H/J</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2? In boxes 19-26 on your answer sheet, write:</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29026\" id=\"question-wrapper-29026\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Nineteenth-century studies of the nature of genius <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"348c17b7-3b73-485e-b6bc-4fbb2c992f5d\" data-question=\"19\">failed to take into account<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe179c3c-5da0-43c2-87d8-35447036ca32\" data-question=\"19\">uniqueness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of the person’s upbringing. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29027\" id=\"question-wrapper-29027\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Nineteenth-century studies of genius <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55c1c319-0df5-49c2-96cc-844b453b6748\" data-question=\"20\">lacked both<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8317b5c-58fe-45c9-89e8-b5747f083a1c\" data-question=\"20\">objectivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55c1c319-0df5-49c2-96cc-844b453b6748\" data-question=\"20\">proper scientific approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29028\" id=\"question-wrapper-29028\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A true genius has general powers capable of excellence <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"069cb600-d7f0-45a9-bc70-b47a06dcac1e\" data-question=\"21\">in any area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29029\" id=\"question-wrapper-29029\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The skills of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ed0b01d-084f-49b8-bd29-f581cfa76b0d\" data-question=\"22\">ordinary individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"50761ff6-7971-46d0-9f9e-3955c9831fae\" data-question=\"22\">in essence the same as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the skills of prodigies. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29030\" id=\"question-wrapper-29030\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The ease with which truly great ideas are accepted and taken for granted <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"97623719-97ed-4df2-a75b-1374ffdbdb17\" data-question=\"23\">fails to lessen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> their significance. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29031\" id=\"question-wrapper-29031\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Giftedness and genius deserve proper scientific research into their true nature so that all talent may be retained for the human race. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29032\" id=\"question-wrapper-29032\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Geniuses often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f29fa38-b13f-4ba5-a8b1-8729ffa4a5b4\" data-question=\"25\">pay a high price<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to achieve <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7230cb48-7b57-4c56-a895-57b6b2fb5b3a\" data-question=\"25\">greatness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29033\" id=\"question-wrapper-29033\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> To be a genius is worth the high personal cost. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b219a8ba-aef3-48c4-9852-33d4f036354b","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"The talents","passagePhrase":"giftedness"},{"uid":"ca917880-723f-4323-8c64-90951d2c31d6","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"gifts","passagePhrase":"talented"},{"uid":"a6a2e923-ad98-4266-9b77-6c948e3c2c5a","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"geniuses","passagePhrase":"prodigies ... gifted people ... the gifted"},{"uid":"223dca1f-379e-45b9-ad79-f24e2eecdd6b","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"exhausted","passagePhrase":"burn out"},{"uid":"38822d56-5ef3-4236-88a1-407e1578080f","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"genius"},{"uid":"ca9724e6-a483-4934-a25b-e033f82f1e9c","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"is inherited","passagePhrase":"runs in families"},{"uid":"234a2eb0-ac14-45ab-82a6-531bf43c181c","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"never appreciate true genius","passagePhrase":"genius goes unrecognised and unrewarded"},{"uid":"ea38139d-881b-4722-b132-92c9033b8a81","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"difficulties","passagePhrase":"adversity"},{"uid":"5b36f274-e6e3-4ad6-8b1b-043b94bcde69","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"should use","passagePhrase":"have a responsibility to use"},{"uid":"348c17b7-3b73-485e-b6bc-4fbb2c992f5d","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"failed to take into account","passagePhrase":"must also take into account information"},{"uid":"fe179c3c-5da0-43c2-87d8-35447036ca32","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"uniqueness","passagePhrase":"common or exceptional"},{"uid":"e8317b5c-58fe-45c9-89e8-b5747f083a1c","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"objectivity","passagePhrase":"more objective"},{"uid":"55c1c319-0df5-49c2-96cc-844b453b6748","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"lacked both ... proper scientific approach","passagePhrase":"not always very scientific"},{"uid":"50761ff6-7971-46d0-9f9e-3955c9831fae","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"in essence the same as","passagePhrase":"similar to, but so much superior to"},{"uid":"7ed0b01d-084f-49b8-bd29-f581cfa76b0d","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"ordinary individuals","passagePhrase":"our own ... our own ... our own"},{"uid":"97623719-97ed-4df2-a75b-1374ffdbdb17","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"fails to lessen","passagePhrase":"does not minimise"},{"uid":"7230cb48-7b57-4c56-a895-57b6b2fb5b3a","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"greatness","passagePhrase":"achievements ... fame"},{"uid":"5f29fa38-b13f-4ba5-a8b1-8729ffa4a5b4","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"pay a high price","passagePhrase":"the price they may have paid"}]},"reading_u2_171":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>How Does the Biological Clock Tick?</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong> </p><p>Our life span is restricted. Everyone accepts this as ‘biologically’ obvious. ‘Nothing lives forever!’ However, in this statement we think of artificially produced, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"425ad207-47db-494e-89c6-7cff6fcb4fe6\" data-question=\"37\">technical objects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, products which are subjected to natural wear and tear during use. This leads to the result that at some time or other the object stops working and is unusable (‘death’ in the biological sense). But are the wear and tear and loss of function of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"425ad207-47db-494e-89c6-7cff6fcb4fe6\" data-question=\"37\">technical objects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> and the death of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c57917fe-3c87-43d9-9b07-1c33cb26b885\" data-question=\"37\">living organisms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> really similar or comparable?</p><p><strong>B</strong> </p><p>Our ‘dead’ products are ‘static’, closed systems. It is always the basic material which constitutes the object and which, in the natural course of things, is worn down and becomes ‘older*. Ageing in this case must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9a9569f-74b6-4888-9f8d-251bad891702\" data-question=\"33\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3147775a-9172-4659-af31-fd8eba885529\" data-question=\"34\">occur according to the laws<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of physical chemistry and of thermodynamics. Although the same law holds for a living organism, the result of this law <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e3fd2757-f113-4a63-8f71-b85d163f821f\" data-question=\"27\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"284ccefb-c576-46dc-bfa8-403f43d91f25\" data-question=\"37\">is not inexorable in the same way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. At least as long as a biological system <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5267aad-f1ec-4183-920b-f3b8a59da476\" data-question=\"38\">has the ability to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> renew itself it could actually become older without ageing; an organism is an open, dynamic system through which new material continuously flows. Destruction of old material and formation of new material are thus in permanent dynamic equilibrium. The material of which the organism is formed changes continuously. Thus our bodies continuously exchange old substance for new, just like a spring which more or less maintains its form and movement, but in which the water molecules are always different.</p><p><strong>C</strong> </p><p>Thus ageing and death should not be seen as inevitable, particularly as the organism possesses many mechanisms for repair. It is not, in principle, necessary for a biological system to age and die. Nevertheless, a restricted life span, ageing, and then death are basic characteristics of life. The reason for this is easy to recognise: in nature, the existent organisms either adapt or are regularly replaced by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1c7423f2-4b8a-4548-b870-2bc438c033e3\" data-question=\"35\">new types<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Because of changes in the genetic material (mutations) these have new characteristics and in the course of their individual lives they are tested for optimal or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a41798c-640f-4d0e-a973-f1917137a00f\" data-question=\"28\">better adaptation to the environmental conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. Immortality would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b267346d-05ff-4864-8446-497687020929\" data-question=\"36\">disturb<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> this system – it needs room for new and better life. This is the basic problem of evolution.</p><p><strong>D</strong> </p><p>Every organism has a life span which is highly characteristic. There are striking differences in life span between different species, but within one species the parameter is relatively constant. For example, the average duration of human life has hardly changed in thousands of years. Although more and more people attain an advanced age as a result of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1a0d92d-d11c-4cbc-b3da-10860003ea02\" data-question=\"29\">developments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> in medical care and better nutrition, the characteristic upper limit for most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4e87506d-faf8-497c-8303-f271dc3e957f\" data-question=\"29\">remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> 80 years. A further argument against the simple wear and tear theory is the observation that the time within which organisms age lies between a few days (even a few hours for unicellular organisms) and several thousand years, as with mammoth trees.</p><p><strong>E</strong> </p><p>If a life span is a genetically determined biological characteristic, it is logically necessary to propose the existence of an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa5d15c7-c1cc-4ebc-93db-52f396df52d6\" data-question=\"30\">internal clock<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, which in some way measures and controls the ageing process and which finally determines death as the last step in a fixed programme. Like the life span, the metabolic rate has for different organisms a fixed mathematical relationship to the body mass. In comparison to the life span this relationship is ‘inverted’: the larger the organism the lower its metabolic rate. Again this relationship is valid not only for birds, but also, similarly on average within the systematic unit, for all other organisms (plants, animals, unicellular organisms).</p><p><strong>F</strong> </p><p>Animals which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7504ffe-c1ec-4a5e-b9d4-d1ca35386a21\" data-question=\"31\">behave ‘frugally’ with energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> become particularly old, for example, crocodiles and tortoises. Parrots and birds of prey are often held chained up. Thus they are not able to ‘experience life’ and so they attain a high life span in captivity. Animals which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7504ffe-c1ec-4a5e-b9d4-d1ca35386a21\" data-question=\"31\">save energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> by hibernation or lethargy (e.g. bats or hedgehogs) live much longer than those which are always active. The metabolic rate of mice can be reduced by a very low consumption of food (hunger diet). They then may live twice as long as their well fed comrades. Women become distinctly (about 10 per cent) older than men. If you examine the metabolic rates of the two sexes you establish that the higher male metabolic rate roughly accounts for the lower male life span. That means that they live life ‘energetically’ – more intensively, but not for as long.</p><p><strong>G</strong> </p><p>It follows from the above that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"29520518-e2fe-44ca-8a2b-a69b295a2851\" data-question=\"40\">sparing use of energy reserves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> should tend to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88ab9815-1694-455e-8440-e85fcc073c84\" data-question=\"32\">extend life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Extreme high performance sports may lead to optimal cardiovascular performance, but they quite certainly do not prolong life. Relaxation lowers metabolic rate, as does adequate sleep and in general an equable and balanced personality. Each of us can develop his or her own ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"29520518-e2fe-44ca-8a2b-a69b295a2851\" data-question=\"40\">energy saving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> programme’ with a little self-observation, critical self-control and, above all, logical consistency. Experience will show that to live in this way not only increases the life span but is also very healthy. This final aspect should not be forgotten.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A—G. Choose the correct heading for paragraphs B—G from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i—x, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><ul><li>i The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa5d15c7-c1cc-4ebc-93db-52f396df52d6\" data-question=\"30\">biological clock<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></li><li>ii Why dying is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a41798c-640f-4d0e-a973-f1917137a00f\" data-question=\"28\">beneficial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></li><li>iii The ageing process of men and women</li><li>iv <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88ab9815-1694-455e-8440-e85fcc073c84\" data-question=\"32\">Prolonging your life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></li><li>v Limitations of life span</li><li>vi Modes of development of different species</li><li>vii A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4e87506d-faf8-497c-8303-f271dc3e957f\" data-question=\"29\">stable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> life span despite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1a0d92d-d11c-4cbc-b3da-10860003ea02\" data-question=\"29\">improvements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></li><li>viii <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7504ffe-c1ec-4a5e-b9d4-d1ca35386a21\" data-question=\"31\">Energy consumption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></li><li>ix <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e3fd2757-f113-4a63-8f71-b85d163f821f\" data-question=\"27\">Fundamental differences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in ageing of objects and organisms</li><li>x Repair of genetic material</li></ul><p><strong>Example: Paragraph A v</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29034\" id=\"question-wrapper-29034\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IX</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29035\" id=\"question-wrapper-29035\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29036\" id=\"question-wrapper-29036\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29037\" id=\"question-wrapper-29037\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29038\" id=\"question-wrapper-29038\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29039\" id=\"question-wrapper-29039\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the notes below. Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p>• Objects age <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9a9569f-74b6-4888-9f8d-251bad891702\" data-question=\"33\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3147775a-9172-4659-af31-fd8eba885529\" data-question=\"34\">in accordance with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> principles of (33) ………………….. and of (34) ……………………………..<br>• Through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1c7423f2-4b8a-4548-b870-2bc438c033e3\" data-question=\"35\">mutations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, organisms can (35) …………………. better to the environment<br>• (36) ………………… would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b267346d-05ff-4864-8446-497687020929\" data-question=\"36\">pose a serious problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> for the theory of evolution</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29040\" id=\"question-wrapper-29040\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PHYSICAL CHEMISTRY [OR] THERMODYNAMICS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29041\" id=\"question-wrapper-29041\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PHYSICAL CHEMISTRY [OR] THERMODYNAMICS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29042\" id=\"question-wrapper-29042\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ADAPT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29043\" id=\"question-wrapper-29043\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IMMORTALITY</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?<br>In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write:</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer<br><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29044\" id=\"question-wrapper-29044\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The wear and tear theory <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"284ccefb-c576-46dc-bfa8-403f43d91f25\" data-question=\"37\">applies to both<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"425ad207-47db-494e-89c6-7cff6fcb4fe6\" data-question=\"37\">artificial objects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c57917fe-3c87-43d9-9b07-1c33cb26b885\" data-question=\"37\">biological systems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29045\" id=\"question-wrapper-29045\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In principle, it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5267aad-f1ec-4183-920b-f3b8a59da476\" data-question=\"38\">possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> for a biological system to become older without ageing. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29046\" id=\"question-wrapper-29046\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Within seven years, about 90 per cent of a human body is replaced as new. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29047\" id=\"question-wrapper-29047\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"29520518-e2fe-44ca-8a2b-a69b295a2851\" data-question=\"40\">Conserving energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> may help to extend a human’s life. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"425ad207-47db-494e-89c6-7cff6fcb4fe6","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"artificial objects","passagePhrase":"technical objects ... technical objects"},{"uid":"c57917fe-3c87-43d9-9b07-1c33cb26b885","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"biological systems","passagePhrase":"living organisms"},{"uid":"f9a9569f-74b6-4888-9f8d-251bad891702","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"in accordance with","passagePhrase":"occur according to the laws"},{"uid":"3147775a-9172-4659-af31-fd8eba885529","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"in accordance with","passagePhrase":"occur according to the laws"},{"uid":"e3fd2757-f113-4a63-8f71-b85d163f821f","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Fundamental differences","passagePhrase":"is not inexorable in the same way"},{"uid":"d5267aad-f1ec-4183-920b-f3b8a59da476","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"possible","passagePhrase":"has the ability to"},{"uid":"1c7423f2-4b8a-4548-b870-2bc438c033e3","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"mutations","passagePhrase":"new types"},{"uid":"5a41798c-640f-4d0e-a973-f1917137a00f","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"beneficial","passagePhrase":"better adaptation to the environmental conditions"},{"uid":"b267346d-05ff-4864-8446-497687020929","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"pose a serious problem","passagePhrase":"disturb"},{"uid":"c1a0d92d-d11c-4cbc-b3da-10860003ea02","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"improvements","passagePhrase":"developments"},{"uid":"4e87506d-faf8-497c-8303-f271dc3e957f","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"stable","passagePhrase":"remains"},{"uid":"fa5d15c7-c1cc-4ebc-93db-52f396df52d6","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"biological clock","passagePhrase":"internal clock"},{"uid":"c7504ffe-c1ec-4a5e-b9d4-d1ca35386a21","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Energy consumption","passagePhrase":"behave ‘frugally’ with energy ... save energy"},{"uid":"29520518-e2fe-44ca-8a2b-a69b295a2851","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Conserving energy","passagePhrase":"sparing use of energy reserves ... energy saving"},{"uid":"88ab9815-1694-455e-8440-e85fcc073c84","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Prolonging your life","passagePhrase":"extend life"}]},"reading_u2_172":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Land of the Rising Sun</strong></p><p><strong>Section A</strong> </p><p>Japan has a significantly better record in terms of average mathematical attainment than England and Wales. Large sample international comparisons of pupils’ attainments since the 1960s have established that not only did Japanese pupils at age 13 have better scores of average attainment, but there was also a larger proportion of ‘low’ attainers in England, where, incidentally, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96d0d7ee-092d-4fa8-8326-7c2d35bc6e1e\" data-question=\"6\">the variation in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"586e2e83-f042-4e4c-a51d-031afde963ba\" data-question=\"6\">attainment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> scores was much greater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. The percentage of Gross National Product spent on education is reasonably <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d00ca361-1e1a-4fb9-847f-aaa6c74f2f1b\" data-question=\"7\">similar in the two countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, so how is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d00ca361-1e1a-4fb9-847f-aaa6c74f2f1b\" data-question=\"7\">this higher and more consistent attainment in maths<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> achieved?</p><p><strong>Section B</strong> </p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7c42f9d4-d860-42b4-acce-239adc8a1d1b\" data-question=\"1\">Lower secondary schools<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in Japan cover three school years, from the seventh grade (age 13) to the ninth grade (age 15). Virtually all pupils at this stage attend state schools: only 3 per cent are in the private sector. Schools are usually modern in design, set well back from the road and spacious inside. Classrooms are large and pupils sit at single desks in rows. Lessons last for a standardised 50 minutes and are always followed by a 10-minute break, which gives the pupils a chance to let off steam. Teachers begin with a formal address and mutual bowing, and then concentrate on whole-class teaching.</p><p>Classes are large – usually about 40 – and are unstreamed. Pupils stay in the same class for all lessons throughout the school and develop considerable class identity and loyalty. Pupils attend the school in their own neighbourhood, which in theory removes ranking by school. In practice in Tokyo, because of the relative concentration of schools, there is some competition to get into the ‘better’ school in a particular area.</p><p><strong>Section C</strong> </p><p>Traditional ways of teaching form the basis of the lesson and the remarkably quiet classes take their own notes of the points made and the examples demonstrated. Everyone has their own copy of the textbook supplied by the central education authority, Monbusho, as part of the concept of free compulsory education up to the age of 15. These textbooks are, on the whole, small, presumably inexpensive to produce, but well set out and logically developed. (One teacher was particularly keen to introduce colour and pictures into maths textbooks: he felt this would make them more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e90b0c4e-d205-4e65-bd80-91f4d61ee6dc\" data-question=\"10\">accessible to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> pupils brought up in a cartoon culture.) Besides approving textbooks, Monbusho also decides the highly centralised national curriculum and how it is to be delivered.</p><p><strong>Section D</strong> </p><p>Lessons all follow the same <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80d4ae58-ef7b-49a7-93b1-edc2cf249b69\" data-question=\"3\">pattern<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. At the beginning, the pupils put solutions to the homework on the board, then the teachers comment, correct or elaborate as necessary. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"dd459e81-a9d6-4dfe-a8a3-bc76eeee7a68\" data-question=\"9\">Pupils mark<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> their own homework: this is an important principle in Japanese schooling as it enables pupils to see where and why they made a mistake, so that these can be avoided in future. No one minds mistakes or ignorance as long as you are prepared to learn from them.</p><p>After the homework has been discussed, the teacher explains the topic of the lesson, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec93c2ff-c606-4cb6-853b-32f4fe380b3f\" data-question=\"11\">slowly and with a lot of repetition and elaboration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Examples are demonstrated on the board; questions from the textbook are worked through first with the class, and then the class is set questions from the textbook to do individually. Only rarely are supplementary worksheets distributed in a maths class. The impression is that the logical nature of the textbooks and their comprehensive coverage of different types of examples, combined with the relative homogeneity of the class, renders work sheets unnecessary. At this point, the teacher would circulate and make sure that all the pupils were coping well.</p><p><strong>Section E</strong> </p><p>It is remarkable that large, mixed-ability classes could be kept together for maths throughout all their compulsory schooling from 6 to 15. Teachers say that they give individual help at the end of a lesson or after school, setting extra work if necessary. In observed lessons, any <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80538824-16b3-437a-a339-e95cb0d433a0\" data-question=\"4\">strugglers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> would be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62c944d4-e3a8-4c67-87d4-ce3e74117d95\" data-question=\"4\">assisted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> by the teacher or quietly seek help from their neighbour. Carefully fostered class identity makes pupils keen to help each other – anyway, it is in their interests since the class progresses together.</p><p>This scarcely seems adequate help to enable slow learners to keep up. However, the Japanese attitude towards education runs along the lines of ‘if you work hard enough, you can do almost anything’. Parents are kept closely informed of their children’s progress and will play a part in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62c944d4-e3a8-4c67-87d4-ce3e74117d95\" data-question=\"4\">helping<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> their children to keep up with class, sending them to ‘Juku’ (private evening tuition) if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd846ce6-d16e-4a5c-a3e3-3faf72b60d90\" data-question=\"12\">extra help<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> is needed and encouraging them to work harder. It seems to work, at least for 95 per cent of the school population.</p><p><strong>Section F</strong> </p><p>So what are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ed0bc73-690b-4fb2-ba88-3e2698dd4770\" data-question=\"5\">the major contributing factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in the success of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"37a62d8a-5d0f-4631-9e4b-f6229e5d60f8\" data-question=\"5\">maths teaching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>? Clearly, attitudes are important. Education is valued greatly in Japanese culture; maths is recognised as an important compulsory subject throughout schooling; and the emphasis is on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a4809bd-c370-49af-8558-b91112758a29\" data-question=\"13\">hard work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> coupled with a focus on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4b1a781-5da6-4bab-af64-6cce2efff422\" data-question=\"13\">accuracy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</p><p>Other relevant points relate to the supportive attitude of a class towards slower pupils, the lack of competition within a class, and the positive emphasis on learning for oneself and improving one’s own standard. And the view of repetitively boring lessons and learning the facts by heart, which is sometimes quoted in relation to Japanese classes, may be unfair and unjustified. No poor maths lessons were observed. They were mainly good and one or two were inspirational.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 1 has six sections, A—F. Choose the correct heading for sections B—F from the list of headings below.</p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><ul><li>i The influence of Monbusho</li><li>ii Helping <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80538824-16b3-437a-a339-e95cb0d433a0\" data-question=\"4\">less successful students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></li><li>iii The success of compulsory education</li><li>iv Research findings concerning achievements in maths</li><li>v The typical <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80d4ae58-ef7b-49a7-93b1-edc2cf249b69\" data-question=\"3\">format<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of a maths lesson</li><li>vi Comparative expenditure on maths education</li><li>vii Background to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7c42f9d4-d860-42b4-acce-239adc8a1d1b\" data-question=\"1\">middle-years education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in Japan</li><li>viii <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ed0bc73-690b-4fb2-ba88-3e2698dd4770\" data-question=\"5\">The key<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to Japanese successes in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"37a62d8a-5d0f-4631-9e4b-f6229e5d60f8\" data-question=\"5\">maths education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></li><li>ix The role of homework correction</li></ul><p><strong>Example Answer: Section A iv</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29048\" id=\"question-wrapper-29048\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29049\" id=\"question-wrapper-29049\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29050\" id=\"question-wrapper-29050\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29051\" id=\"question-wrapper-29051\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29052\" id=\"question-wrapper-29052\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 1?</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29053\" id=\"question-wrapper-29053\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96d0d7ee-092d-4fa8-8326-7c2d35bc6e1e\" data-question=\"6\">a wider range<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of achievement amongst English pupils studying maths than amongst their Japanese counterparts. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29054\" id=\"question-wrapper-29054\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The percentage of Gross National Product spent on education generally <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d00ca361-1e1a-4fb9-847f-aaa6c74f2f1b\" data-question=\"7\">reflects the level of attainment in mathematics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29055\" id=\"question-wrapper-29055\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Private schools in Japan are more modern and spacious than state-run lower secondary schools. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29056\" id=\"question-wrapper-29056\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"dd459e81-a9d6-4dfe-a8a3-bc76eeee7a68\" data-question=\"9\">Teachers mark<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> homework in Japanese schools. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 10-13 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29057\" id=\"question-wrapper-29057\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Maths textbooks in Japanese schools are </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. cheap for pupils to buy.</li> <li>B. well organised and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e90b0c4e-d205-4e65-bd80-91f4d61ee6dc\" data-question=\"10\">adapted to the needs of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> the pupils.</li> <li>C. written to be used in conjunction with TV programmes.</li> <li>D. not very popular with many Japanese teachers.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29058\" id=\"question-wrapper-29058\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When a new maths topic is introduced, </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. students answer questions on the board.</li> <li>B. students rely entirely on the textbook.</li> <li>C. it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec93c2ff-c606-4cb6-853b-32f4fe380b3f\" data-question=\"11\">carefully and patiently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> explained to the students.</li> <li>D. it is usual for students to use extra worksheets.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29059\" id=\"question-wrapper-29059\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> How do schools deal with students who experience difficulties? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They are given appropriate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd846ce6-d16e-4a5c-a3e3-3faf72b60d90\" data-question=\"12\">supplementary tuition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</li> <li>B. They are encouraged to copy from other pupils.</li> <li>C. They are forced to explain their slow progress.</li> <li>D. They are placed in a mixed-ability class.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29060\" id=\"question-wrapper-29060\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Why do Japanese students tend to achieve relatively high rates of success in maths? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is a compulsory subject in Japan.</li> <li>B. They are used to working without help from others.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a4809bd-c370-49af-8558-b91112758a29\" data-question=\"13\">Much effort is made<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4b1a781-5da6-4bab-af64-6cce2efff422\" data-question=\"13\">correct answers are emphasised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</li> <li>D. There is a strong emphasis on repetitive learning</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"96d0d7ee-092d-4fa8-8326-7c2d35bc6e1e","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"a wider range","passagePhrase":"the variation in attainment scores was much greater"},{"uid":"586e2e83-f042-4e4c-a51d-031afde963ba","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"attainment"},{"uid":"7c42f9d4-d860-42b4-acce-239adc8a1d1b","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"middle-years education","passagePhrase":"Lower secondary schools"},{"uid":"e90b0c4e-d205-4e65-bd80-91f4d61ee6dc","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"adapted to the needs of","passagePhrase":"accessible to"},{"uid":"80d4ae58-ef7b-49a7-93b1-edc2cf249b69","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"format","passagePhrase":"pattern"},{"uid":"ec93c2ff-c606-4cb6-853b-32f4fe380b3f","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"carefully and patiently","passagePhrase":"slowly and with a lot of repetition and elaboration"},{"uid":"80538824-16b3-437a-a339-e95cb0d433a0","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"less successful students","passagePhrase":"strugglers"},{"uid":"62c944d4-e3a8-4c67-87d4-ce3e74117d95","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"assisted ... helping"},{"uid":"dd846ce6-d16e-4a5c-a3e3-3faf72b60d90","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"supplementary tuition","passagePhrase":"extra help"},{"uid":"8ed0bc73-690b-4fb2-ba88-3e2698dd4770","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"The key","passagePhrase":"the major contributing factors"},{"uid":"37a62d8a-5d0f-4631-9e4b-f6229e5d60f8","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"maths education","passagePhrase":"maths teaching"},{"uid":"6a4809bd-c370-49af-8558-b91112758a29","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"Much effort is made","passagePhrase":"hard work"},{"uid":"b4b1a781-5da6-4bab-af64-6cce2efff422","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"correct answers are emphasised","passagePhrase":"accuracy"}]},"reading_u2_173":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Biological Control of Pests</strong></p><p>The continuous and reckless use of synthetic chemicals for the control of pests which pose a threat to agricultural crops and human health is proving to be counter-productive. Apart from engendering widespread <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"316f2aad-8210-415a-9d7e-6ad7fd0ee480\" data-question=\"14\">ecological disorders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, pesticides have contributed to the emergence of a new breed of chemical-resistant, highly lethal superbugs.</p><p>According to a recent study by the Food and Agriculture Organisation (FAO), more than 300 species of agricultural pests <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"becccfd5-ebcd-4083-87fe-9a87f135d1ef\" data-question=\"15\">have developed resistance to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> a wide range of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab393aa5-4fe0-4f50-8f45-e5450e3e81e4\" data-question=\"15\">potent chemicals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Not to be left behind are the disease-spreading pests, about 100 species of which have become immune to a variety of insecticides now in use.</p><p>One glaring disadvantage of pesticides’ application is that, while destroying harmful pests, they also wipe out many useful non-targeted organisms, which keep the growth of the pest population in check. This results in what agroecologists call the ‘treadmill syndrome’. Because of their tremendous breeding potential and genetic diversity, many pests are known to withstand synthetic chemicals and bear <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c56649a-a0e1-496f-a6d5-3b43d0957a8c\" data-question=\"19\">offspring with a built-in resistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> to pesticides.</p><p>The havoc that the ‘treadmill syndrome’ can bring about is well illustrated by what happened to cotton farmers in Central America. In the early 1940s, basking in the glory of chemical- based intensive agriculture, the farmers avidly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96b61893-daf4-44a9-bda9-ef9fa74ebb3c\" data-question=\"16\">took to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> pesticides <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04c414f7-713e-4f3d-8fce-9de4490d0262\" data-question=\"16\">as a sure measure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d14e73f1-007f-444a-ae14-b96cb2f5204a\" data-question=\"16\">to boost crop yield<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. The insecticide was applied eight times a year in the mid-1940s, rising to 28 in a season in the mid-1950s, following the sudden proliferation of three new varieties of chemical- resistant pests.</p><p>By the mid-1960s, the situation took an alarming turn with the outbreak of four more new pests, necessitating pesticide spraying to such an extent that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c59af0cc-8ccd-4ce5-b4e2-f7261d37e5ee\" data-question=\"17\">50% of the financial outlay on cotton<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> production was accounted for by pesticides. In the early 1970s, the spraying frequently reached 70 times a season as the farmers were pushed to the wall by the invasion of genetically stronger insect species.</p><p>Most of the pesticides in the market today remain inadequately tested for properties that cause cancer and mutations as well as for other adverse effects on health, says a study by United States environmental agencies. The United States National Resource Defense Council has found that DDT was the most popular of a long list of dangerous chemicals in use.</p><p>In the face of the escalating perils from indiscriminate applications of pesticides, a more effective and ecologically sound strategy of biological control, involving the selective use of <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8f7c4605-006f-4f6e-93d6-63e8b4e4827c\" data-question=\"20\">natural enemies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of the pest population, is fast gaining popularity – though, as yet, it is a new field with limited potential. The advantage of biological control in contrast to other methods is that it provides a relatively low-cost, perpetual control system with a minimum of detrimental side-effects. When handled by experts, bio-control is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dccdc134-0203-4b34-9838-b2fe992b2dd9\" data-question=\"21\">safe, non-polluting and self-dispersing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</p><p>The Commonwealth Institute of Biological Control (CIBC) in Bangalore, with its global network of research laboratories and field stations, is one of the most active, non-commercial research agencies engaged in pest control by setting natural predators against parasites. CIBC also serves as a clearing-house for the export and import of biological agents for pest control world-wide.</p><p>CIBC successfully used a seed-feeding weevil, native to Mexico, to control the obnoxious parthenium weed, known to exert devious influence on agriculture and human health in both India and Australia. Similarly the Hyderabad-based Regional Research Laboratory (RRL), supported by CIBC, is now trying out an Argentinian weevil for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"112b3726-0f54-4559-9080-9927bb27422f\" data-question=\"25\">eradication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> of water hyacinth, another dangerous weed, which has become a nuisance in many parts of the world. According to Mrs Kaiser Jamil of RRL, ‘The Argentinian weevil does not attack any other plant and a pair of adult bugs could destroy the weed in 4-5 days.’ CIBC is also perfecting the technique for breeding parasites that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20050413-f212-4c9c-9434-2ebf080589cc\" data-question=\"22\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"522b46d3-7e8e-4a0c-9f15-ea23096d1f3a\" data-question=\"23\">prey on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> ‘disapene scale’ insects – notorious defoliants of fruit trees in the US and India.</p><p>How effectively biological control can be pressed into service is proved by the following examples. In the late 1960s, when Sri Lanka’s flourishing coconut groves were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7e56a8a-3829-40de-9e5c-50254f57443b\" data-question=\"24\">plagued<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> by leaf-mining hispides, a larval parasite imported from Singapore brought the pest under control. A natural predator indigenous to India, Neodumetia sangawani, was found useful in controlling the Rhodes grass-scale insect that was devouring forage grass in many parts of the US. By using Neochetina bruci, a beetle native to Brazil, scientists at Kerala Agricultural University freed a 12- kilometre- long canal from the clutches of the weed Salvinia molesta, popularly called ‘African Payal’ in Kerala. About 30,000 hectares of rice fields in Kerala <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"25883c92-0f66-435e-9534-a3b9dd990b06\" data-question=\"26\">are infested by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> this weed.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29061\" id=\"question-wrapper-29061\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The use of pesticides has contributed to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. a change in the way ecologies are classified by agroecologists.</li> <li>B. an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"316f2aad-8210-415a-9d7e-6ad7fd0ee480\" data-question=\"14\">imbalance in many ecologies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> around the world.</li> <li>C. the prevention of ecological disasters in some parts of the world.</li> <li>D. an increase in the range of ecologies which can be usefully farmed.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29062\" id=\"question-wrapper-29062\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Food and Agriculture Organisation has counted more than 300 agricultural pests which </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"becccfd5-ebcd-4083-87fe-9a87f135d1ef\" data-question=\"15\">are no longer responding to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> most pesticides in use</li> <li>B. can be easily controlled through the use of pesticides.</li> <li>C. continue to spread disease in a wide range of crops.</li> <li>D. may be used as part of bio-control’s replacement of pesticides.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29063\" id=\"question-wrapper-29063\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Cotton farmers in Central America <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96b61893-daf4-44a9-bda9-ef9fa74ebb3c\" data-question=\"16\">began to use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> pesticides </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. because of an intensive government advertising campaign.</li> <li>B. in response to the appearance of new varieties of pest.</li> <li>C. as a result of changes in the seasons and the climate.</li> <li>D. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04c414f7-713e-4f3d-8fce-9de4490d0262\" data-question=\"16\">ensure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d14e73f1-007f-444a-ae14-b96cb2f5204a\" data-question=\"16\">more cotton was harvested<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> from each crop.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29064\" id=\"question-wrapper-29064\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> By the mid-1960s, cotton farmers in Central America found that pesticides </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. were wiping out 50% of the pests plaguing the crops.</li> <li>B. were destroying 50% of the crops they were meant to protect.</li> <li>C. were causing a 50% increase in the number of new pests reported.</li> <li>D. were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c59af0cc-8ccd-4ce5-b4e2-f7261d37e5ee\" data-question=\"17\">costing 50% of the total amount<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> they spent on their crops.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 2?<br>In boxes 18-21 on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29065\" id=\"question-wrapper-29065\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Disease-spreading pests respond more quickly to pesticides than agricultural pests do. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29066\" id=\"question-wrapper-29066\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A number of pests are now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c56649a-a0e1-496f-a6d5-3b43d0957a8c\" data-question=\"19\">born with an innate immunity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> to some pesticides. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29067\" id=\"question-wrapper-29067\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Biological control entails using <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8f7c4605-006f-4f6e-93d6-63e8b4e4827c\" data-question=\"20\">synthetic chemicals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to try and change the genetic make-up of the pests’ offspring. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29068\" id=\"question-wrapper-29068\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bio-control is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dccdc134-0203-4b34-9838-b2fe992b2dd9\" data-question=\"21\">free from danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> under certain circumstances. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A—I, below.</p><ul><li>A forage grass</li><li>B rice fields</li><li>C coconut trees</li><li>D fruit trees</li><li>E water hyacinth</li><li>F parthenium weed</li><li>G Brazilian beetles</li><li>H grass-scale insects</li><li>I larval parasites <br> </li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29069\" id=\"question-wrapper-29069\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Disapene scale insects <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20050413-f212-4c9c-9434-2ebf080589cc\" data-question=\"22\">feed on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29070\" id=\"question-wrapper-29070\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Neodumetia sangawani <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"522b46d3-7e8e-4a0c-9f15-ea23096d1f3a\" data-question=\"23\">ate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29071\" id=\"question-wrapper-29071\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Leaf-mining hispides <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7e56a8a-3829-40de-9e5c-50254f57443b\" data-question=\"24\">blighted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29072\" id=\"question-wrapper-29072\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> An Argentinian weevil may be successful in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"112b3726-0f54-4559-9080-9927bb27422f\" data-question=\"25\">wiping out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29073\" id=\"question-wrapper-29073\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Salvinia <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"25883c92-0f66-435e-9534-a3b9dd990b06\" data-question=\"26\">molesta plagues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"316f2aad-8210-415a-9d7e-6ad7fd0ee480","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"imbalance in many ecologies","passagePhrase":"ecological disorders"},{"uid":"becccfd5-ebcd-4083-87fe-9a87f135d1ef","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"are no longer responding to","passagePhrase":"have developed resistance to"},{"uid":"ab393aa5-4fe0-4f50-8f45-e5450e3e81e4","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"potent chemicals"},{"uid":"3c56649a-a0e1-496f-a6d5-3b43d0957a8c","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"born with an innate immunity","passagePhrase":"offspring with a built-in resistance"},{"uid":"96b61893-daf4-44a9-bda9-ef9fa74ebb3c","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"began to use","passagePhrase":"took to"},{"uid":"04c414f7-713e-4f3d-8fce-9de4490d0262","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"ensure","passagePhrase":"as a sure measure"},{"uid":"d14e73f1-007f-444a-ae14-b96cb2f5204a","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"more cotton was harvested","passagePhrase":"to boost crop yield"},{"uid":"c59af0cc-8ccd-4ce5-b4e2-f7261d37e5ee","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"costing 50% of the total amount","passagePhrase":"50% of the financial outlay on cotton"},{"uid":"dccdc134-0203-4b34-9838-b2fe992b2dd9","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"free from danger","passagePhrase":"safe, non-polluting and self-dispersing"},{"uid":"112b3726-0f54-4559-9080-9927bb27422f","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"wiping out","passagePhrase":"eradication"},{"uid":"20050413-f212-4c9c-9434-2ebf080589cc","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"feed on","passagePhrase":"prey on"},{"uid":"522b46d3-7e8e-4a0c-9f15-ea23096d1f3a","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"ate","passagePhrase":"prey on"},{"uid":"f7e56a8a-3829-40de-9e5c-50254f57443b","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"blighted","passagePhrase":"plagued"},{"uid":"25883c92-0f66-435e-9534-a3b9dd990b06","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"molesta plagues","passagePhrase":"are infested by"}]},"reading_u2_174":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Collecting Ant Specimens</strong></p><p>Collecting ants can be as simple as picking up stray ones and placing them in a glass jar, or as complicated as completing an exhaustive survey of all species present in an area and estimating their relative abundances. The exact method used will depend on the final purpose of the collections. For taxonomy, or classification, long series, from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"73b65284-874e-4304-bc2a-fc92a01cecb2\">a single nest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, which contain all castes (workers, including majors and minors, and, if present, queens and males) are desirable, to allow <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"953b5a6d-094f-4d2b-a4b0-13fbf2ac62c0\">the determination of variation within species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. For ecological studies, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"072ebe1a-2968-462a-bc61-2d4493a83cb3\">the most important factor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> is collecting identifiable samples of as many of the different species present as possible. Unfortunately, these methods are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"c6e3647f-1dbf-45ad-b3a1-424bf2f3af5f\">not always<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> compatible. The taxonomist sometimes overlooks whole species in favour of those groups currently under study, while the ecologist often collects only a limited number of specimens of each species, thus reducing their value for taxonomic investigations.</p><p>To collect as wide a range of species as possible, several methods must be used. These include hand collecting, using baits to attract the ants, ground litter sampling, and the use of pitfall traps. Hand collecting consists of searching for ants everywhere they are likely to occur. This includes on the ground, under rocks, logs or other objects on the ground, in rotten wood on the ground or on trees, in vegetation, on tree trunks and under bark. When possible, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"5e1bd26b-3930-4c37-a2de-395d3ea70b80\">collections should be made<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> from nests or foraging columns and at least 20 to 25 individuals collected. This will ensure that all individuals are of the same species, and so increase their value for detailed studies. Since some species are largely nocturnal, collecting should not be confined to daytime. Specimens are collected using an aspirator (often called a pooter), forceps, a fine, moistened paint brush, or fingers, if the ants are known not to sting. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"c6d6b74c-8542-459d-926d-96b861212510\">Individual insects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> are placed in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"c9a09624-d226-48c6-bc1c-e3a13446b7f5\">plastic or glass tubes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> (1.5-3-0 ml capacity for small ants, 5-8 ml for larger ants) containing 75% to 95% ethanol. Plastic tubes with secure tops are better than glass because they are lighter, and do not break as easily if mishandled.</p><p>Baits can be used to attract and concentrate foragers. This often increases the number of individuals collected and attracts species that are otherwise <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"3fbf6f96-80b9-42e5-9ad7-f82696e00e9b\">elusive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. Sugars and meats or oils will attract different species and a range should be utilised. These baits can be placed either on the ground or on the trunks of trees or large shrubs. When placed on the ground, baits should be situated on small paper cards or other flat, light-coloured surfaces, or in test-tubes or vials. This makes it easier to spot ants and to capture them before they can escape into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"38\" data-uid=\"2c1271b6-016f-4b1e-9bd1-e5fe6fc40203\">the surrounding leaf litter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</p><p>Many ants are small and forage primarily in the layer of leaves and other debris on the ground. Collecting these species by hand can be difficult. One of the most successful ways to collect them is to gather the leaf litter in which they are foraging and extract the ants from it. This is most commonly done by placing leaf litter on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"39\" data-uid=\"02e1761f-16fe-4dfa-b765-97fd90f367ba\">a screen over a large funnel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"37\" data-uid=\"60b35b74-0d70-4636-a88c-8e83cd2a63dd\">under some heat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. As the leaf litter dries from above, ants (and other animals) move downward and eventually fall out the bottom and are collected <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"40\" data-uid=\"100e7b66-0ba9-437d-90f5-9133ec8a568e\">in alcohol placed below the funnel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. This method works especially well in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1a9c9523-cf3a-4d59-b364-5b9b65525c0e\">rain forests and marshy areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. A method of improving the catch when using a funnel is to sift the leaf litter through a coarse screen before placing it above the funnel. This will concentrate the litter and remove larger leaves and twigs. It will also allow more litter to be sampled when using a limited number of funnels.</p><p>The pitfall trap is another commonly used tool for collecting ants. A pitfall trap can be any small container placed in the ground with the top level with the surrounding surface and filled with a preservative. Ants are collected when they fall into the trap while foraging. The diameter of the traps can vary from about 18 mm to 10 cm and the number used can vary from a few to several hundred. The size of the traps used is influenced largely by personal preference (although larger sizes are generally better), while the number will be determined by the study being undertaken. The preservative used is usually ethylene glycol or propylene glycol, as <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"2b1ecea8-aaf6-416d-933a-81834b42ac55\">alcohol<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> will evaporate quickly and the traps will dry out. One advantage of pitfall traps is that they can be used to collect over a period of time with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"ccc8b56e-01bf-40e8-8973-fefb4931f20a\">minimal maintenance and intervention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. One disadvantage is that some species are not collected as they either avoid the traps or do not commonly encounter them while foraging.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?<br>In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29074\" id=\"question-wrapper-29074\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Taxonomic research involves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"953b5a6d-094f-4d2b-a4b0-13fbf2ac62c0\">comparing members<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"27\" data-uid=\"73b65284-874e-4304-bc2a-fc92a01cecb2\">one group of ants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29075\" id=\"question-wrapper-29075\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> New species of ant are frequently identified by taxonomists. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29076\" id=\"question-wrapper-29076\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Range is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"29\" data-uid=\"072ebe1a-2968-462a-bc61-2d4493a83cb3\">the key criterion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> for ecological collections. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29077\" id=\"question-wrapper-29077\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A single collection of ants can <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"30\" data-uid=\"c6e3647f-1dbf-45ad-b3a1-424bf2f3af5f\">generally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> be used for both taxonomic and ecological purposes. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Classify the following statements as referring to<br><strong>A</strong> hand collecting<br><strong>B</strong> using bait<br><strong>C</strong> sampling ground litter<br><strong>D</strong> using a pitfall trap</p><p>Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29078\" id=\"question-wrapper-29078\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is preferable to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"31\" data-uid=\"5e1bd26b-3930-4c37-a2de-395d3ea70b80\">take specimens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> from groups of ants. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29079\" id=\"question-wrapper-29079\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is particularly effective for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"32\" data-uid=\"1a9c9523-cf3a-4d59-b364-5b9b65525c0e\">wet habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29080\" id=\"question-wrapper-29080\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is a good method for species which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"33\" data-uid=\"3fbf6f96-80b9-42e5-9ad7-f82696e00e9b\">hard to find<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29081\" id=\"question-wrapper-29081\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"34\" data-uid=\"ccc8b56e-01bf-40e8-8973-fefb4931f20a\">Little time and effort<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> is required. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29082\" id=\"question-wrapper-29082\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Separate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"c9a09624-d226-48c6-bc1c-e3a13446b7f5\">containers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> are used for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"35\" data-uid=\"c6d6b74c-8542-459d-926d-96b861212510\">individual specimens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29083\" id=\"question-wrapper-29083\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"36\" data-uid=\"2b1ecea8-aaf6-416d-933a-81834b42ac55\">Non-alcoholic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> preservative should be used. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Label the diagram below. Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><em><img src=\"/media/gg_imgs/test/523ab076b0183fc9d8617ae49b2802a4ced54021.jpg\" style=\"height:349px; width:515px\"></em></span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29084\" id=\"question-wrapper-29084\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HEAT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29085\" id=\"question-wrapper-29085\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LEAF LITTER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29086\" id=\"question-wrapper-29086\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(COARSE) SCREEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"29087\" id=\"question-wrapper-29087\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ALCOHOL</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"73b65284-874e-4304-bc2a-fc92a01cecb2","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"one group of ants","passagePhrase":"a single nest"},{"uid":"953b5a6d-094f-4d2b-a4b0-13fbf2ac62c0","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"comparing members","passagePhrase":"the determination of variation within species"},{"uid":"072ebe1a-2968-462a-bc61-2d4493a83cb3","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"the key criterion","passagePhrase":"the most important factor"},{"uid":"5e1bd26b-3930-4c37-a2de-395d3ea70b80","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"take specimens","passagePhrase":"collections should be made"},{"uid":"c6d6b74c-8542-459d-926d-96b861212510","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"individual specimens","passagePhrase":"Individual insects"},{"uid":"c9a09624-d226-48c6-bc1c-e3a13446b7f5","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"containers","passagePhrase":"plastic or glass tubes"},{"uid":"3fbf6f96-80b9-42e5-9ad7-f82696e00e9b","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"hard to find","passagePhrase":"elusive"},{"uid":"2c1271b6-016f-4b1e-9bd1-e5fe6fc40203","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the surrounding leaf litter"},{"uid":"02e1761f-16fe-4dfa-b765-97fd90f367ba","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a screen over a large funnel"},{"uid":"60b35b74-0d70-4636-a88c-8e83cd2a63dd","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"under some heat"},{"uid":"100e7b66-0ba9-437d-90f5-9133ec8a568e","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"in alcohol placed below the funnel"},{"uid":"1a9c9523-cf3a-4d59-b364-5b9b65525c0e","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"wet habitats","passagePhrase":"rain forests and marshy areas"},{"uid":"ccc8b56e-01bf-40e8-8973-fefb4931f20a","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Little time and effort","passagePhrase":"minimal maintenance and intervention"}]},"reading_u2_175":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>William Henry Perkin</strong></p><p><em>The man who invented synthetic dyes</em></p><p>William Henry Perkin was born on March 12, 1838, in London, England. As a boy, Perkin’s curiosity prompted early interests in the arts, sciences. photography, and engineering. But it was a chance stumbling upon a run-down, yet functional, laboratory in his late grandfather’s home that solidified the young man`s enthusiasm for chemistry.</p><p>As a student at the City of London School, Perkin became immersed in the study of chemistry. His talent and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1ba4ef93-6576-4e2b-a10c-8a2c0503ac06\" data-question=\"1\">devotion to the subject were perceived by his teacher, Thomas Hall,<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> who encouraged him to attend a series of lectures given by the eminent scientist Michael Faraday at the Royal Institution. Those speeches fired <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7ad1194-ca8d-4d96-914a-84196d499483\" data-question=\"4\">the young chemist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>`s enthusiasm further, and he later went on to attend the Royal College of Chemistry, which he succeeded in entering in 1853, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7ad1194-ca8d-4d96-914a-84196d499483\" data-question=\"4\">at the age of 15<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</p><p>At the time of Perkin’s enrollment, the Royal College of Chemistry was headed by the noted German chemist August Wilhelm Hofmann. Perkin’s scientific gifts soon caught Hofmann’s attention and within two years, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"55666098-fe7c-4fa6-8759-18fbc95efb05\" data-question=\"3\">he became Hofmann’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7ad1194-ca8d-4d96-914a-84196d499483\" data-question=\"4\">youngest assistant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. Not long after that, Perkin made the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7e1443ef-30b0-4075-add2-101933ec68bd\" data-question=\"4\">scientific breakthrough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec17976f-0af4-4119-992c-1f5754ab17ca\" data-question=\"4\">would bring him both fame and fortune<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</p><p>At the time, quinine was the only viable medical treatment for malaria. The drug ls derived from the bark of the cinchona tree, native to South America and by 1856 demand for the drug was surpassing the available supply. Thus, when Hofmann made some passing comments about the desirability of a synthetic substitute for quinine, it was unsurprising that his star pupil was moved to take up the challenge.</p><p>During his vacation in 1856, Perkin spent his time in the laboratory on the top floor of his family’s house. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c1a01c1-7929-4d74-bc43-c90747f4f85d\" data-question=\"6\">was attempting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd697aa2-7b29-4efa-93c7-fe05a7422552\" data-question=\"6\">manufacture quinine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> from aniline, an inexpensive and readily available coal tar waste product. Despite his best efforts, however, he did not end up with quinine. Instead, he produced a mysterious dark sludge. Luckily, Perkins scientific training and nature prompted him to investigate the substance further. Incorporating potassium dichromate and alcohol into the aniline at various stages of the experimental process, he finally produced a deep purple solution. And, proving the truth of the famous scientist Louis Pasteur’s words ‘chance favors only the prepared mind’. Perkin saw the potential of his unexpected find.</p><p>Historically, textile dyes were made from such natural sources as plants and animal excretions. Some of these, such as the glandular mucus of snails, were difficult to obtain and outrageously expensive. Indeed, the purple colour extracted from a snail was once so costly that in society at the time <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"260fdc45-6e5a-47c2-a43f-3d4c7fa6fda6\" data-question=\"8\">only the rich could afford it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. Further, natural dyes tended to be muddy in hue and fade quickly. It was against this backdrop that Perkin‘s discovery was made.</p><p>Perkin quickly grasped that his purple solution could be used to colour fabric, thus making it the world’s first synthetic dye. Realising the importance of this breakthrough, he lost no time in patenting it. But perhaps the most fascinating of all Perkin`s reactions to his find was his nearly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"39e70bbd-f8a1-436a-bb74-0e6e90e310d6\" data-question=\"9\">instant recognition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> that the new dye had commercial <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8afaa024-6c85-411d-8a7b-8d680de2b8b6\" data-question=\"9\">possibilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d425000-f373-4204-9f2e-d5c9a784b200\" data-question=\"10\">Perkin originally named<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> his dye Tyrian Purple, but it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa96b380-83d0-430a-9db8-050fa5923c15\" data-question=\"10\">later became commonly known as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> mauve (from the French for the plant used to make the colour violet). He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebf1d97a-51c7-427e-a3f7-6ccc4c698a9e\" data-question=\"11\">asked advice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of Scottish dye works owner Robert Pullar, who assured him that manufacturing the dye would be well worth it if the colour remained fast (i.e. would not fade) and the cost was relatively low. So, over the fierce objections of his mentor Hofmann, he left college to give birth to the modern chemical industry.</p><p>With the help of his father and brother, Perkin set up a factory not far from London. Utilizing the cheap and plentiful coal tar that was an almost unlimited byproduct of London’s gas street lighting, the dye works began producing the world’s first synthetically dyed material in 1857. The company received a commercial boost from the Empress Eugenio of France, when she decided the new color flattered her. Very soon, mauve was the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"599953c3-628e-45ef-a1af-1969012a6358\" data-question=\"12\">necessary shade for all the fashionable ladies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in that country. Not to be outdone, England`s Queen Victoria also appeared in public wearing a mauve gown, thus making it all the rage in England as well. The dye was bold and fast, and the public clamoured for more. Perkin went back to the drawing board.</p><p>Although Perkins fame was achieved and fortune assured by his first discovery, the chemist continued his research. Among other dyes he developed and introduced were aniline red (1859) and aniline black (1863) and in the late 1860s, Perkin’s green. It is important to note that Perkin’s synthetic dye discoveries had outcomes far beyond the merely decorative. The dyes also became vital to medical research in many ways. For instance, they were used to stain previously invisible microbes and bacteria, allowing researchers to identify such bacilli as tuberculosis. cholera, and anthrax. Artificial dyes continue to play a crucial role today. And, in what would have been particularly pleasing to Perkin, their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c60c8561-da75-4541-9794-8ba9a9e3fb2f\" data-question=\"13\">current use is in the search for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> a vaccine against malaria.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage? In following statements below, choose</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN </strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28250\" id=\"question-wrapper-28250\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1ba4ef93-6576-4e2b-a10c-8a2c0503ac06\" data-question=\"1\">Michael Faraday was the first person to recognise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> Perkin’s ability as a student of chemistry </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28251\" id=\"question-wrapper-28251\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Michael Faraday suggested Perkin should enroll in the Royal College of Chemistry. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28252\" id=\"question-wrapper-28252\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"55666098-fe7c-4fa6-8759-18fbc95efb05\" data-question=\"3\">Perkin employed August Wilhelm Hofmann<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> as his assistant. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28253\" id=\"question-wrapper-28253\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Perkin was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7ad1194-ca8d-4d96-914a-84196d499483\" data-question=\"4\">still young<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> when he made <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7e1443ef-30b0-4075-add2-101933ec68bd\" data-question=\"4\">the discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec17976f-0af4-4119-992c-1f5754ab17ca\" data-question=\"4\">made him rich and famous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28254\" id=\"question-wrapper-28254\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The trees from which quinine is derived grow only in South America. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28255\" id=\"question-wrapper-28255\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Perkin <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c1a01c1-7929-4d74-bc43-c90747f4f85d\" data-question=\"6\">hoped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd697aa2-7b29-4efa-93c7-fe05a7422552\" data-question=\"6\">manufacture a drug<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> from a coal tar waste product. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28256\" id=\"question-wrapper-28256\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Perkin was inspired by the discoveries of the famous scientist Louis Pasteur. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Answer the questions below.</p><p>Choose<strong> NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS </strong>from the passage for each answer.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28257\" id=\"question-wrapper-28257\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Before Perkin’s discovery, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"260fdc45-6e5a-47c2-a43f-3d4c7fa6fda6\" data-question=\"8\">with what group in society was the colour purple associated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(THE/ONLY) RICH</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28258\" id=\"question-wrapper-28258\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What potential did Perkin <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"39e70bbd-f8a1-436a-bb74-0e6e90e310d6\" data-question=\"9\">immediately understand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> that his new dye had? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMMERCIAL (POSSIBILITIES)</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28259\" id=\"question-wrapper-28259\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa96b380-83d0-430a-9db8-050fa5923c15\" data-question=\"10\">the name finally used to refer to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d425000-f373-4204-9f2e-d5c9a784b200\" data-question=\"10\">the first colour Perkin invented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MAUVE (WAS/IS)</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28260\" id=\"question-wrapper-28260\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What was the name of the person Perkin <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebf1d97a-51c7-427e-a3f7-6ccc4c698a9e\" data-question=\"11\">consulted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> before setting up his own dye works? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(ROBERT) PULLAR</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28261\" id=\"question-wrapper-28261\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In what country did Perkin’s newly invented colour first <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"599953c3-628e-45ef-a1af-1969012a6358\" data-question=\"12\">become fashionable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(IN) FRANCE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28262\" id=\"question-wrapper-28262\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the passage, which disease <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c60c8561-da75-4541-9794-8ba9a9e3fb2f\" data-question=\"13\">is now being targeted by researchers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> using synthetic dyes? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MALARIA (IS)</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"d7ad1194-ca8d-4d96-914a-84196d499483","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"still young","passagePhrase":"the young chemist ... at the age of 15 ... youngest assistant"},{"uid":"7e1443ef-30b0-4075-add2-101933ec68bd","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"the discovery","passagePhrase":"scientific breakthrough"},{"uid":"ec17976f-0af4-4119-992c-1f5754ab17ca","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"made him rich and famous","passagePhrase":"would bring him both fame and fortune"},{"uid":"2c1a01c1-7929-4d74-bc43-c90747f4f85d","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"hoped","passagePhrase":"was attempting"},{"uid":"fd697aa2-7b29-4efa-93c7-fe05a7422552","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"manufacture a drug","passagePhrase":"manufacture quinine"},{"uid":"260fdc45-6e5a-47c2-a43f-3d4c7fa6fda6","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"with what group in society was the colour purple associated","passagePhrase":"only the rich could afford it"},{"uid":"39e70bbd-f8a1-436a-bb74-0e6e90e310d6","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"immediately understand","passagePhrase":"instant recognition"},{"uid":"8afaa024-6c85-411d-8a7b-8d680de2b8b6","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"possibilities"},{"uid":"9d425000-f373-4204-9f2e-d5c9a784b200","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the first colour Perkin invented","passagePhrase":"Perkin originally named"},{"uid":"fa96b380-83d0-430a-9db8-050fa5923c15","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the name finally used to refer to","passagePhrase":"later became commonly known as"},{"uid":"ebf1d97a-51c7-427e-a3f7-6ccc4c698a9e","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"consulted","passagePhrase":"asked advice"},{"uid":"599953c3-628e-45ef-a1af-1969012a6358","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"become fashionable","passagePhrase":"necessary shade for all the fashionable ladies"},{"uid":"c60c8561-da75-4541-9794-8ba9a9e3fb2f","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"is now being targeted by researchers","passagePhrase":"current use is in the search for"}]},"reading_u2_176":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>IS THERE ANYBODY OUT THERE?</strong></p><p><em>The Search for Extra-Terrestrial Intelligence</em></p><p>The question of whether we are alone in the Universe has haunted humanity for centuries, but we may now stand poised on the brink of the answer to that question, as we search for radio signals from other intelligent civilizations. This search is often known by the acronym SETI [search for extraterrestrial intelligence], is a difficult one. Although groups around the world have been searching intermittently for three decades, it is only now that we have reached the level of technology where we can make a determined attempt to search all nearby stars for any sign of life.</p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>The primary reason for the search is basic curiosity – the same curiosity about the natural world that drives all pure science. We want to know whether we are alone in the Universe. We want to know whether life evolves naturally if given the right conditions, or whether there is something very special about the Earth to have fostered the variety of life forms that we see around us on the planet. The simple detection of a radio signal will be sufficient to answer this most basic of all questions. In this sense, SETI is another cog in the machinery of pure science which is continually pushing out the horizon of our knowledge. However, there are other reasons for being interested in whether life exists elsewhere. For example, we have had civilization on Earth for perhaps only a few thousand years, and the threats of nuclear war and pollution over the last few decades have told us that our survival may be tenuous. Will we last another two thousand years or will we wipe ourselves out? Since the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3812505-381f-43ac-b26b-93c6ac999030\" data-question=\"18\">lifetime<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6463bc74-5a8d-4f8d-a01b-05db59f3698e\" data-question=\"18\">of a planet like ours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> is several billion years, we can expect that if other civilizations do survive in our galaxy, their ages will range from zero to several billion years. Thus any other civilization that we hear from is likely to be far older on average than ourselves. The mere existence of such a civilization will tell of that long-term survival <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d73e843-dcdb-4294-af8c-46c11e34a6b6\" data-question=\"21\">is possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, and gives us some cause for optimism. It is even possible that the older civilization may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8ff2383-6469-4b45-96b2-54c7e1bf2847\" data-question=\"21\">pass on the benefits of their experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4313bdc-0445-4adb-8b1e-189a26570131\" data-question=\"21\">dealing with threats to survival<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> such as nuclear war and global pollution, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4313bdc-0445-4adb-8b1e-189a26570131\" data-question=\"21\">other threats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> that we haven’t yet discovered</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d481ff10-7b39-4599-894e-7a25b5a39766\" data-question=\"14\">discussing whether we are alone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, most SETI scientists adopt two <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ad98e9e8-563b-45ec-9b6f-d5fc750eff79\" data-question=\"14\">ground rules<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. First. UFOs [Unidentified Flying objects] are generally ignored since most scientists don`t consider the evidence for them to be strong enough to bear serious consideration (although it is also important to keep an open mind in case any really convincing evidence emerges in the future). Second, we make a very conservative assumption that we are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4eb693af-4bc6-4272-a366-85ba9cb7424f\" data-question=\"22\">looking for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> a life form that is pretty well <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70fd9b30-9ffb-4114-9659-4d0c440bd567\" data-question=\"22\">like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> us, since if it differs radically from us we may well not recognize it as a life form, quite apart from whatever we are able to communicate with it. In other words, the life form we are looking for may well have two green heads and seven fingers, but it will nevertheless resemble us in that it should communicate with its fellows. Be interested in the Universe, Live on a planet orbiting a star like our Sun, and perhaps most restrictively have chemistry, like us, based on carbon and water.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>Even when we make these assumptions. our understanding of other life forms is still severely limited. We do not even know. for example, how many stars have planets, and we certainly do not know <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e813639-6fda-4d3d-b4f7-af488df2253c\" data-question=\"15\">how likely it is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f53792fb-99f3-4e9a-8f3d-bc906618fa98\" data-question=\"15\">life will arise naturally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, given the right conditions. However, when we look at the 100 billion stars in our galaxy [the Milky Way], and 100 billion galaxies. In the observable Universe, It seems inconceivable that at least one of these planets does not have a life form on it; in fact, the best educated guess we can make using the little that we do know about the conditions for carbon-based life, leads us to estimate that perhaps one in 100,000 stars might have a life-bearing planet orbiting it. That means that our nearest neighbors are perhaps 1000 light years away. which is almost next door in astronomical terms.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>An alien civilization could choose many different ways of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd39fd27-97a1-43a3-b0fe-1907df5247d9\" data-question=\"16\">sending<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> information across the galaxy, but many of these either require too much energy. or else are severely attenuated while traversing the vast distances across the galaxy. It turns out that. for a given amount of transmitted power: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e6eda795-c18c-4b5f-81f9-aff8673a8bba\" data-question=\"16\">radio waves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in the frequency range 1000 to 3000 MHz travel the greatest distance. and so all searches to date have concentrated on looking for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e6eda795-c18c-4b5f-81f9-aff8673a8bba\" data-question=\"16\">radio waves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in this frequency range. So far there have been a number of searches by various groups around the world, including Australian searches using the radio telescope at Parkes, New South Wales. Until now <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"78857662-ea5d-4d12-a72d-407679cccffb\" data-question=\"24\">there have not been any detections<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> from the few hundred stars which have been searched. The scale of the searches has been increased dramatically since 1992, when the US Congress voted NASA $10 million per year for ten years to conduct a thorough search for extra-terrestrial life. Much of the money in this project is being spent on developing the special hardware needed to search many frequencies at once. The project has two parts. One part is a targeted search using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96d3c30a-4585-4de6-83ab-089090568988\" data-question=\"20\">the world’s largest radio telescopes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. The American-operated telescope in Arecibo. Puerto Rico and the French telescope in Nancy in France. This part of the project is searching the nearest 1000 likely stars with a high sensibility for signals in the frequency range 1000 to 3000 MHz. The other parts of the project is an undirected search which is monitoring all of the space with a lower using the smaller antennas of NASA`s Deep Space Network.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>There is considerable debate over <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2691a715-aff9-4726-86f9-4ba811330df5\" data-question=\"17\">how we should react<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> if we detect <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b5ed042-df0e-4675-87a3-2357b9ceadd7\" data-question=\"17\">a signal from an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74ec7530-1e27-4c29-9ce9-5436e9d83b2a\" data-question=\"19\">alien civilization<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Everybody agrees that we should not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2feac463-5e40-41d8-b82c-6a19e20b6f84\" data-question=\"26\">reply immediately<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Quite apart from the impracticality of sending e reply over such large distances at short notice, it raises a host of ethical questions that would have to be addressed by the global community before any reply could be sent. Would the human race face the culture shock if faced with a superior and much older civilization? Luckily, there is no urgency about this. The stars being searched are hundreds of light years away. so it takes hundreds of years for their signal to reach us, and a further few hundred years for our reply to reach them. It <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"90d98063-98b1-4e51-931a-0adb1e559b1c\" data-question=\"26\">is not important<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, then, if there`s a delay of a few years, or decades, while the human race debates the question of whether to reply and perhaps carefully drafts a reply.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage has five paragraphs, A-E.</p><p>Choose the correct heading for paragraphs B-E from the list of headings below.</p><p>Write the correct number, i-vii</p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><ul><li>I Seeking the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd39fd27-97a1-43a3-b0fe-1907df5247d9\" data-question=\"16\">transmission<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of radio signals from planets</li><li>II <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2691a715-aff9-4726-86f9-4ba811330df5\" data-question=\"17\">Appropriate responses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b5ed042-df0e-4675-87a3-2357b9ceadd7\" data-question=\"17\">signals from other civilisations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></li><li>III Vast distances to Earth’s closest neighbours</li><li>IV <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ad98e9e8-563b-45ec-9b6f-d5fc750eff79\" data-question=\"14\">Assumptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> underlying <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d481ff10-7b39-4599-894e-7a25b5a39766\" data-question=\"14\">the search for extra-terrestrial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></li><li>V Reasons for the search for extra- terrestrial intelligence</li><li>VI Knowledge of extra-terrestrial life forms</li><li>VII <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e813639-6fda-4d3d-b4f7-af488df2253c\" data-question=\"15\">Likelihood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f53792fb-99f3-4e9a-8f3d-bc906618fa98\" data-question=\"15\">life on other planets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></li></ul><p><u><strong>Example:</strong></u><strong> </strong>Paragraph A - Answer: V</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28264\" id=\"question-wrapper-28264\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28265\" id=\"question-wrapper-28265\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28266\" id=\"question-wrapper-28266\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28267\" id=\"question-wrapper-28267\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Answer the questions below.</p><p>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28268\" id=\"question-wrapper-28268\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3812505-381f-43ac-b26b-93c6ac999030\" data-question=\"18\">life expectancy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6463bc74-5a8d-4f8d-a01b-05db59f3698e\" data-question=\"18\">of Earth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SEVERAL BILLION YEARS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28269\" id=\"question-wrapper-28269\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What kind of signals from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74ec7530-1e27-4c29-9ce9-5436e9d83b2a\" data-question=\"19\">other intelligent civilisations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> are SETI scientists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7daada7-8f2b-40bc-8801-768c77df6fa5\" data-question=\"19\">searching for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RADIO (WAVES/SIGNALS)</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28270\" id=\"question-wrapper-28270\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> How many stars are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96d3c30a-4585-4de6-83ab-089090568988\" data-question=\"20\">the world’s most powerful radio telescopes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> searching? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">1000 (LIKELY) (STARS)</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage? In following statements below, choose</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN </strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28271\" id=\"question-wrapper-28271\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Alien civilisations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d73e843-dcdb-4294-af8c-46c11e34a6b6\" data-question=\"21\">may be able to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8ff2383-6469-4b45-96b2-54c7e1bf2847\" data-question=\"21\">help<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> the human race to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4313bdc-0445-4adb-8b1e-189a26570131\" data-question=\"21\">overcome serious problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28272\" id=\"question-wrapper-28272\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> SETI scientists are trying to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4eb693af-4bc6-4272-a366-85ba9cb7424f\" data-question=\"22\">find<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> a life form that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70fd9b30-9ffb-4114-9659-4d0c440bd567\" data-question=\"22\">resembles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> humans in many ways. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28273\" id=\"question-wrapper-28273\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Americans and Australians have co-operated on joint research projects. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28274\" id=\"question-wrapper-28274\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> So far SETI scientists <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"78857662-ea5d-4d12-a72d-407679cccffb\" data-question=\"24\">have picked up radio signals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> from several stars. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28275\" id=\"question-wrapper-28275\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The NASA project attracted criticism from some members of Congress. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28276\" id=\"question-wrapper-28276\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> If a signal from outer space is received, it <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"90d98063-98b1-4e51-931a-0adb1e559b1c\" data-question=\"26\">will be important<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2feac463-5e40-41d8-b82c-6a19e20b6f84\" data-question=\"26\">respond promptly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b3812505-381f-43ac-b26b-93c6ac999030","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"life expectancy","passagePhrase":"lifetime"},{"uid":"6463bc74-5a8d-4f8d-a01b-05db59f3698e","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"of Earth","passagePhrase":"of a planet like ours"},{"uid":"7d73e843-dcdb-4294-af8c-46c11e34a6b6","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"may be able to","passagePhrase":"is possible"},{"uid":"c8ff2383-6469-4b45-96b2-54c7e1bf2847","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"help","passagePhrase":"pass on the benefits of their experience"},{"uid":"b4313bdc-0445-4adb-8b1e-189a26570131","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"overcome serious problems","passagePhrase":"dealing with threats to survival ... other threats"},{"uid":"d481ff10-7b39-4599-894e-7a25b5a39766","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"the search for extra-terrestrial","passagePhrase":"discussing whether we are alone"},{"uid":"ad98e9e8-563b-45ec-9b6f-d5fc750eff79","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Assumptions","passagePhrase":"ground rules"},{"uid":"4eb693af-4bc6-4272-a366-85ba9cb7424f","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"find","passagePhrase":"looking for"},{"uid":"70fd9b30-9ffb-4114-9659-4d0c440bd567","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"resembles","passagePhrase":"like"},{"uid":"9e813639-6fda-4d3d-b4f7-af488df2253c","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Likelihood","passagePhrase":"how likely it is"},{"uid":"f53792fb-99f3-4e9a-8f3d-bc906618fa98","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"life on other planets","passagePhrase":"life will arise naturally"},{"uid":"bd39fd27-97a1-43a3-b0fe-1907df5247d9","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"transmission","passagePhrase":"sending"},{"uid":"e6eda795-c18c-4b5f-81f9-aff8673a8bba","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"radio waves ... radio waves"},{"uid":"96d3c30a-4585-4de6-83ab-089090568988","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the world’s most powerful radio telescopes","passagePhrase":"the world’s largest radio telescopes"},{"uid":"2691a715-aff9-4726-86f9-4ba811330df5","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Appropriate responses","passagePhrase":"how we should react"},{"uid":"1b5ed042-df0e-4675-87a3-2357b9ceadd7","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"signals from other civilisations","passagePhrase":"a signal from an alien civilization"},{"uid":"74ec7530-1e27-4c29-9ce9-5436e9d83b2a","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"other intelligent civilisations","passagePhrase":"alien civilization"},{"uid":"2feac463-5e40-41d8-b82c-6a19e20b6f84","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"respond promptly","passagePhrase":"reply immediately"},{"uid":"b7daada7-8f2b-40bc-8801-768c77df6fa5","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"searching for","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_177":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>THE HISTORY OF THE TORTOISE </strong></p><p>If you go back far enough, everything lived in the sea. At various points in evolutionary history, enterprising individuals within many different animal groups moved out onto the land, sometimes even to the most parched deserts, taking their own private seawater with them in blood and cellular fluids. In addition to the reptiles, birds, mammals and insects which we see all around us, other groups that have succeeded out of water include scorpions, snails, crustaceans such as woodlice and land crabs, millipedes and centipedes, spiders and various worms. And we mustn’t forget the plants, without whose prior <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b8ccae0-e753-4068-8492-de9b7cb9c3ad\" data-question=\"27\">invasion of the land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> none of the other migrations could have happened.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"549edec9-402f-4d54-92b0-4c20d327a0af\" data-question=\"28\">Moving from water to land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> involved <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bf2bac99-230f-4a9d-a60a-9e82713199f4\" data-question=\"28\">a major redesign<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of every aspect of life, including breathing and reproduction. Nevertheless, a good number of thoroughgoing land animals later turned around, abandoned their hard-earned terrestrial re-tooling, and returned to the Water Seals have only gone part way back. They show us what the intermediates might have been like, on the way to extreme cases such as whales and dugongs. Whales (including the small whales we call dolphins) and dugongs, with their close cousins the manatees, ceased to be land creatures altogether and reverted to the full marine habits of their remote ancestors. They don‘t even come ashore to breed. They do, however, still breathe air, having <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1983a94b-702c-411e-86e7-6bdb56f501e1\" data-question=\"29\">never developed anything equivalent to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the gills of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b55738ef-e2dc-486d-adbb-172a081aaa45\" data-question=\"29\">their earlier marine incarnation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Turtles went back to the sea a very long time ago and, like all vertebrate returnees to the water, they breathe air. However, they are, in one respect, less fully given back to the water than whales or dugongs, for turtles still lay their eggs on beaches.</p><p>There is evidence that all modem turtles are descended from a terrestrial ancestor which lived before most of the dinosaurs. There are two key fossils called Progaochelys quenstedtiand Palaeochersis talampayensis dating from early dinosaur times, which appear to be close to the ancestry of all modem turtles and tortoises. You might wonder how we can tell whether fossil animals lived on land or in water, especially if only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c00187d-eae1-4374-a668-8c8f7d7a9228\" data-question=\"32\">fragments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8c9025be-867d-45be-8815-9c41d184cafb\" data-question=\"32\">are found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"18046351-ca86-4faa-8b5b-7e99edbccd8e\" data-question=\"32\">Sometimes it`s obvious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Ichthyosarus were reptilian contemporaries of the dinosaurs, with fins and streamlined bodies. The fossils <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a140a94-fc42-4c7b-ad49-265361f37b11\" data-question=\"30\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7a13303-c50d-4e4d-a698-212fc9639075\" data-question=\"33\">look like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> dolphins and they surely lived like dolphins, in the water. With turtles it is a little less obvious. One way to tell is by measuring the bones of their forelimbs.</p><p>Walter Joyce and Jacques Gauthier, at Yale University, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89890e3e-a757-4e27-8093-7d6f5b684bdb\" data-question=\"34\">obtained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> three measurements in these particular bones of 71 species of living turtles and tortoises. They used <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e52b5b55-7edf-4b64-84d2-4db0edcf246c\" data-question=\"35\">a kind of triangular graph paper to plot<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"38a99322-8730-48d4-9514-0f8d730fd623\" data-question=\"35\">the three measurements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> against one another. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"07399388-702f-4923-895f-45403e4f9524\" data-question=\"36\">All the land tortoise species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9cddcf26-b88f-49e5-82ab-0af75829ec22\" data-question=\"36\">formed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"271c42b2-f7b4-49a4-a04b-ac42f930df06\" data-question=\"36\">tight cluster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26796649-458b-4ff0-a410-12aa508da0ac\" data-question=\"36\">points in the upper part<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of the triangle; all the water turtles cluster in the lower part of the triangular graph. There was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"14591fa5-50cd-400d-93ef-7788ad5142f1\" data-question=\"37\">no overlap<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, except when they added some species that spend time both in water and on land. Sure enough, these amphibious species <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c6bcafbf-f6e1-4901-a4a3-52eb4fcd75b2\" data-question=\"38\">show up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> on the triangular graph approximately half way between the ‘wet cluster’ of sea turtles and the ‘dry cluster’ of land tortoises. ‘The next step was to determine where the fossil fell. The bones of P quenstedti and P. talampayensis leave us in no doubt. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7532a209-e0c5-44f4-9577-3e9f7238cb99\" data-question=\"39\">Their points on the graph<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> are right in the thick of the dry cluster. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af0e0ef6-00ac-4b20-baca-9e55bad57140\" data-question=\"39\">Both these fossils<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> were dry-land tortoises. They come from the era before our turtles returned to the water.</p><p>You might think, therefore, that modem land tortoises have probably stayed on land ever since those early terrestrial times, as most mammals did after a few of them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d94be966-e635-4c30-ae15-d503cad7744a\" data-question=\"31\">went back to the sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. But apparently not. If you draw out the family tree of all modern turtles and tortoises, nearly all the branches are aquatic. Today’s land tortoises constitute a single branch, deeply nested among branches consisting of aquatic turtles. This suggests that modern land tortoises have not stayed on land continuously since the time of P. quenstedti and P. talampayensis. Rather, their ancestors were among those who went back to the water, and they then re-emerged back onto the land in (relatively) more recent times.</p><p>Tortoises therefore represent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9e35865-24d7-4807-81fe-68323624dade\" data-question=\"40\">a remarkable double return<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. In common with all mammals, reptiles and binds, their remote ancestors were marine fish and before that various more or less worm-like creatures stretching back, still in the sea, to the primeval bacteria. Later ancestors lived on land and stayed there for a very large number of generations. Later ancestors still evolved back into the water and became sea turtles. And finally, they returned yet again to the land as tortoises, some of which now live in the driest of deserts.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Answer the questions below.</p><p>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28277\" id=\"question-wrapper-28277\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What had to transfer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b8ccae0-e753-4068-8492-de9b7cb9c3ad\" data-question=\"27\">from sea to land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> before any animals could migrate? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(THE) PLANTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28278\" id=\"question-wrapper-28278\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Which TWO processes are mentioned as those in which animals had to make <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bf2bac99-230f-4a9d-a60a-9e82713199f4\" data-question=\"28\">big changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> as they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"549edec9-402f-4d54-92b0-4c20d327a0af\" data-question=\"28\">moved onto land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BREATHING + REPRODUCTION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28279\" id=\"question-wrapper-28279\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Which physical feature, possessed by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b55738ef-e2dc-486d-adbb-172a081aaa45\" data-question=\"29\">their ancestors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, do whales <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1983a94b-702c-411e-86e7-6bdb56f501e1\" data-question=\"29\">lack<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(THE) GILLS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28280\" id=\"question-wrapper-28280\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Which animals might ichthyosaurs <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a140a94-fc42-4c7b-ad49-265361f37b11\" data-question=\"30\">have resembled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DOLPHINS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage?</p><p>In following statements below, choose</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN </strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28281\" id=\"question-wrapper-28281\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Turtles were among the first group of animals to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d94be966-e635-4c30-ae15-d503cad7744a\" data-question=\"31\">migrate back to the sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28282\" id=\"question-wrapper-28282\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"18046351-ca86-4faa-8b5b-7e99edbccd8e\" data-question=\"32\">always difficult to determine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> where an animal lived when its fossilised remains <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8c9025be-867d-45be-8815-9c41d184cafb\" data-question=\"32\">are incomplete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28283\" id=\"question-wrapper-28283\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The habitat of ichthyosaurs can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7a13303-c50d-4e4d-a698-212fc9639075\" data-question=\"33\">determined by the appearance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of their fossilised remains. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the flow-chart below.</p><p>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Method of determining where the ancestors of turtles and tortoises come from</p><p><strong>Step 1</strong></p><p>71 species of living turtles and tortoises were examined and a total of <strong>34</strong> __________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89890e3e-a757-4e27-8093-7d6f5b684bdb\" data-question=\"34\">were taken from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the bones of their forelimbs.</p><p><strong>Step 2</strong></p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"38a99322-8730-48d4-9514-0f8d730fd623\" data-question=\"35\">The data<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e52b5b55-7edf-4b64-84d2-4db0edcf246c\" data-question=\"35\">was recorded on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> a <strong>35</strong> __________ (necessary for comparing the information).</p><p>Outcome: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"07399388-702f-4923-895f-45403e4f9524\" data-question=\"36\">Land tortoises<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9cddcf26-b88f-49e5-82ab-0af75829ec22\" data-question=\"36\">were represented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> by a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"271c42b2-f7b4-49a4-a04b-ac42f930df06\" data-question=\"36\">dense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <strong>36</strong> __________ of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26796649-458b-4ff0-a410-12aa508da0ac\" data-question=\"36\">points towards the top<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</p><p>Sea turtles were grouped together in the bottom part.</p><p><strong>Step 3</strong></p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"14591fa5-50cd-400d-93ef-7788ad5142f1\" data-question=\"37\">The same data<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> was collected from some living <strong>37</strong> __________ species and added to the other results.</p><p>Outcome: The points for these species <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c6bcafbf-f6e1-4901-a4a3-52eb4fcd75b2\" data-question=\"38\">turned out to be positioned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> about <strong>38</strong> __________ up the triangle between the land tortoises and the sea turtles.</p><p><strong>Step 4</strong></p><p>Bones of P quenstedti and P. talampayensis were examined in a similar way and the results added.</p><p>Outcome: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7532a209-e0c5-44f4-9577-3e9f7238cb99\" data-question=\"39\">The position of the points<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> indicated that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af0e0ef6-00ac-4b20-baca-9e55bad57140\" data-question=\"39\">both these ancient creatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> were <strong>39</strong> __________</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28284\" id=\"question-wrapper-28284\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">3/THREE MEASUREMENTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28285\" id=\"question-wrapper-28285\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(TRIANGULAR) GRAPH</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28286\" id=\"question-wrapper-28286\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CLUSTER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28287\" id=\"question-wrapper-28287\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AMPHIBIOUS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28288\" id=\"question-wrapper-28288\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HALF WAY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28289\" id=\"question-wrapper-28289\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DRY-LAND TORTOISES</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose appropriate options <strong>A, B, C</strong> or <strong>D</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28290\" id=\"question-wrapper-28290\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the writer, the most significant thing about tortoises is that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They are able to adapt to life in extremely dry environments.</li> <li>B. Their original life form was a kind of primeval bacteria</li> <li>C. They have so much in common with sea turtles.</li> <li>D. They have made <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9e35865-24d7-4807-81fe-68323624dade\" data-question=\"40\">the transition from sea to land more than once<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0b8ccae0-e753-4068-8492-de9b7cb9c3ad","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"from sea to land","passagePhrase":"invasion of the land"},{"uid":"549edec9-402f-4d54-92b0-4c20d327a0af","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"moved onto land","passagePhrase":"Moving from water to land"},{"uid":"bf2bac99-230f-4a9d-a60a-9e82713199f4","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"big changes","passagePhrase":"a major redesign"},{"uid":"1983a94b-702c-411e-86e7-6bdb56f501e1","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"lack","passagePhrase":"never developed anything equivalent to"},{"uid":"b55738ef-e2dc-486d-adbb-172a081aaa45","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"their ancestors","passagePhrase":"their earlier marine incarnation"},{"uid":"0c00187d-eae1-4374-a668-8c8f7d7a9228","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fragments"},{"uid":"0a140a94-fc42-4c7b-ad49-265361f37b11","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"have resembled","passagePhrase":"look like"},{"uid":"d7a13303-c50d-4e4d-a698-212fc9639075","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"determined by the appearance","passagePhrase":"look like"},{"uid":"89890e3e-a757-4e27-8093-7d6f5b684bdb","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"were taken from","passagePhrase":"obtained"},{"uid":"e52b5b55-7edf-4b64-84d2-4db0edcf246c","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"was recorded on","passagePhrase":"a kind of triangular graph paper to plot"},{"uid":"38a99322-8730-48d4-9514-0f8d730fd623","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"The data","passagePhrase":"the three measurements"},{"uid":"07399388-702f-4923-895f-45403e4f9524","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Land tortoises","passagePhrase":"All the land tortoise species"},{"uid":"9cddcf26-b88f-49e5-82ab-0af75829ec22","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"were represented","passagePhrase":"formed"},{"uid":"271c42b2-f7b4-49a4-a04b-ac42f930df06","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"dense","passagePhrase":"tight cluster"},{"uid":"26796649-458b-4ff0-a410-12aa508da0ac","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"points towards the top","passagePhrase":"points in the upper part"},{"uid":"14591fa5-50cd-400d-93ef-7788ad5142f1","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"The same data","passagePhrase":"no overlap"},{"uid":"c6bcafbf-f6e1-4901-a4a3-52eb4fcd75b2","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"turned out to be positioned","passagePhrase":"show up"},{"uid":"7532a209-e0c5-44f4-9577-3e9f7238cb99","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"The position of the points","passagePhrase":"Their points on the graph"},{"uid":"af0e0ef6-00ac-4b20-baca-9e55bad57140","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"both these ancient creatures","passagePhrase":"Both these fossils"},{"uid":"d94be966-e635-4c30-ae15-d503cad7744a","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"migrate back to the sea","passagePhrase":"went back to the sea"},{"uid":"e9e35865-24d7-4807-81fe-68323624dade","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"the transition from sea to land more than once","passagePhrase":"a remarkable double return"}]},"reading_u2_178":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Children With Auditory Problems</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Hearing impairment or other auditory function deficit in young children can have a major impact on their development of speech and communication, resulting in a detrimental effect on their ability to learn at school. This is likely to have major consequences for the individual and the population as a whole. The New Zealand Ministry of Health has found from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"443a9b34-ff48-417e-9fa0-3bd94a180ade\" data-question=\"7\">research carried out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> over two decades that 6-10% of children in that country are affected by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"05bc2085-f32b-4ffc-ade4-9898d1aaa9c7\" data-question=\"6\">hearing loss<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>A preliminary study in New Zealand has shown that classroom noise presents a major concern for teachers and pupils. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78730570-346a-4923-ba22-9f45f6284cc1\" data-question=\"11\">Modern teaching practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, the organisation of desks in the classroom, poor classroom acoustics, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54e84230-864a-4f31-9cdb-91778ff7784d\" data-question=\"12\">mechanical means of ventilation such as air-conditioning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> units all contribute to the number of children unable to comprehend the teacher’s voice. Education researchers Nelson and Soli have also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be06d6bc-ba31-42ef-8ee1-0a13b9fa88dd\" data-question=\"3\">suggested that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> recent trends in learning often involve collaborative interaction of multiple minds and tools as much as individual possession of information. This all amounts to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3270593f-432c-4238-ad2c-a82b4ecea9bc\" data-question=\"3\">heightened activity and noise levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, which have the potential to be particularly serious for children experiencing auditory function deficit. Noise in classrooms can only exacerbate their difficulty in comprehending and processing verbal communication with other children and instructions from the teacher.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>Children with auditory function deficit are potentially failing to learn to their maximum potential because of noise levels generated in classrooms. The effects of noise on the ability of children to learn effectively in typical classroom environments are now the subject of increasing concern. The International Institute of Noise Control Engineering (I-INCE), on the advice of the World Health Organization, has established <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79e0c953-403c-4175-b5e6-81dd3d959508\" data-question=\"2\">an international working party<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, which includes New Zealand, to evaluate noise and reverberation control for school rooms.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>While the detrimental effects of noise in classroom situations are not limited to children experiencing disability, those with a disability that affects their processing of speech and verbal communication could be extremely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"76f1b545-8f83-4a8e-9d14-93436f42c85a\" data-question=\"5\">vulnerable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. The auditory function deficits in question include <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57c5e8ce-abaa-4003-881a-458439f15e9d\" data-question=\"5\">hearing impairment, autistic spectrum disorders (ASD) and attention deficit disorders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> (ADD/ADHD).</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Autism is considered a neurological and genetic life-long disorder that causes discrepancies in the way information is processed. This disorder is characterised by interlinking problems with social imagination, social communication and social interaction. According to Janzen, this affects the ability to understand and relate in typical ways to people, understand events and objects in the environment, and understand or respond to sensory stimuli. Autism does not allow learning or thinking in the same ways as in children who are developing normally.</p><p>Autistic spectrum disorders often result in major difficulties in comprehending verbal information and speech processing. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bb8ef859-3908-4e84-8775-5fde7861e9b9\" data-question=\"8\">Those experiencing these disorders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1c209d0a-c57d-49b4-bbcc-205c83c13adc\" data-question=\"8\">find sounds such as crowd noiseand the noise generated by machinery painful and distressing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. This is difficult to scientifically quantify as such extra-sensory stimuli vary greatly from one autistic individual to another. But a child who finds any type of noise in their classroom or learning space intrusive is likely to be adversely affected in their ability to process information.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>The attention deficit disorders are indicative of neurological and genetic disorders and are characterised by difficulties with sustaining attention, effort and persistence, organisation skills and disinhibition. Children experiencing these disorders find it difficult to screen out unimportant information, and focus on everything in the environment rather than attending to a single activity. Background noise in the classroom becomes a major distraction, which can affect their ability to concentrate.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>Children experiencing an auditory function deficit can often find speech and communication very difficult to isolate and process when set against high levels of background noise.</p><p>These levels come from outside activities that penetrate the classroom structure, from teaching activities, and other noise generated inside, which can be exacerbated by room reverberation. Strategies are needed to obtain the optimum classroom construction and perhaps a change in classroom culture and methods of teaching. In particular, the effects of noisy classrooms and activities on those experiencing disabilities in the form of auditory function deficit need thorough investigation. It is probable that many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9d6afd4-e221-4fcf-b650-bb4b1561b6c5\" data-question=\"9\">undiagnosed children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> exist in the education system with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9bfb799f-e9bc-48f7-a65c-3b7ecd5b30aa\" data-question=\"9\">‘invisible‘ disabilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Their needs are less likely to be met than those of children with known disabilities.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>The New Zealand Government has developed a New Zealand Disability Strategy and has embarked on a wide-ranging consultation process. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5766c517-f042-42e9-a648-dd1acf129e54\" data-question=\"1\">strategy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> recognises that people experiencing disability face significant barriers in achieving a full quality of life in areas such as attitude, education, employment and access to services. Objective 3 of the New Zealand Disability Strategy is to ‘Provide the Best Education for Disabled People’ by improving education so that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f80003e9-baf4-46e2-8c62-d324d249abfd\" data-question=\"10\">all children, youth learners and adult learners will have equal opportunities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to learn and develop within their already existing local school. For a successful education, the learning environment is vitally significant, so any effort to improve this is likely to be of great benefit to all children, but especially to those with auditory function disabilities.</p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p>A number of countries are already in the process of formulating their own standards for the control and reduction of classroom noise. New Zealand will probably follow their example. The literature to date on noise in school rooms appears to focus on the effects on schoolchildren in general, their teachers and the hearing impaired. Only limited attention appears to have been given to those students experiencing the other disabilities involving auditory function deficit. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1945cce-1c73-4fed-a8cf-d4c6f1ddf86f\" data-question=\"4\">It is imperative that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3df3a7c5-55bd-46e8-b38c-a4a182c565fe\" data-question=\"13\">the needs of these children are taken into account<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in the setting of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b429d1e-3715-47f2-b09e-e03fbe7865ab\" data-question=\"4\">appropriate international standards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to be promulgated in future.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage has nine sections, A-I.</p><p>Which section contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-I</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28291\" id=\"question-wrapper-28291\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an account of a national <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5766c517-f042-42e9-a648-dd1acf129e54\" data-question=\"1\">policy initiative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28292\" id=\"question-wrapper-28292\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79e0c953-403c-4175-b5e6-81dd3d959508\" data-question=\"2\">a global team<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> effort </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28293\" id=\"question-wrapper-28293\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be06d6bc-ba31-42ef-8ee1-0a13b9fa88dd\" data-question=\"3\">a hypothesis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> as to one reason behind <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3270593f-432c-4238-ad2c-a82b4ecea9bc\" data-question=\"3\">the growth in classroom noise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28294\" id=\"question-wrapper-28294\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1945cce-1c73-4fed-a8cf-d4c6f1ddf86f\" data-question=\"4\">a demand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b429d1e-3715-47f2-b09e-e03fbe7865ab\" data-question=\"4\">suitable worldwide regulations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28295\" id=\"question-wrapper-28295\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a list of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57c5e8ce-abaa-4003-881a-458439f15e9d\" data-question=\"5\">medical conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> which place <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"76f1b545-8f83-4a8e-9d14-93436f42c85a\" data-question=\"5\">some children more at risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> from noise than others </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28296\" id=\"question-wrapper-28296\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the estimated proportion of children in New Zealand with auditory problems </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Answer the questions below.</p><p>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28297\" id=\"question-wrapper-28297\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> For what period of time <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"443a9b34-ff48-417e-9fa0-3bd94a180ade\" data-question=\"7\">has hearing loss in schoolchildren been studied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in New Zealand? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">2/TWO DECADES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28298\" id=\"question-wrapper-28298\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In addition to machinery noise, what other type of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1c209d0a-c57d-49b4-bbcc-205c83c13adc\" data-question=\"8\">noise can upset <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bb8ef859-3908-4e84-8775-5fde7861e9b9\" data-question=\"8\">children with autism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>? <span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CROWD (NOISE)</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28299\" id=\"question-wrapper-28299\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What term is used to describe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9bfb799f-e9bc-48f7-a65c-3b7ecd5b30aa\" data-question=\"9\">the hearing problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9d6afd4-e221-4fcf-b650-bb4b1561b6c5\" data-question=\"9\">schoolchildren which have not been diagnosed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INVISIBLE (DISABILITIES/DISABILITY)</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28300\" id=\"question-wrapper-28300\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What part of the New Zealand Disability Strategy aims to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f80003e9-baf4-46e2-8c62-d324d249abfd\" data-question=\"10\">give schoolchildren equal opportunity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OBJECTIVE 3</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-F</strong>.</p><p>The list below includes factors contributing to classroom noise. Which TWO are mentioned by the writer of the passage?</p><ul><li>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78730570-346a-4923-ba22-9f45f6284cc1\" data-question=\"11\">current teaching methods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span></li><li>B echoing corridors</li><li>C <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54e84230-864a-4f31-9cdb-91778ff7784d\" data-question=\"12\">cooling systems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span></li><li>D large class sizes</li><li>E loud-voiced teachers</li><li>F playground games</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28301\" id=\"question-wrapper-28301\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28302\" id=\"question-wrapper-28302\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose appropriate options <strong>A, B, C</strong> or <strong>D</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28303\" id=\"question-wrapper-28303\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer’s overall purpose in writing this article? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. to compare different methods of dealing with auditory problems</li> <li>B. to provide solutions for overly noisy learning environments</li> <li>C. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3df3a7c5-55bd-46e8-b38c-a4a182c565fe\" data-question=\"13\">increase awareness of the situation of children with auditory problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></li> <li>D. to promote New Zealand as a model for other countries to follow</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"443a9b34-ff48-417e-9fa0-3bd94a180ade","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"has hearing loss in schoolchildren been studied","passagePhrase":"research carried out"},{"uid":"05bc2085-f32b-4ffc-ade4-9898d1aaa9c7","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"hearing loss"},{"uid":"78730570-346a-4923-ba22-9f45f6284cc1","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"current teaching methods","passagePhrase":"Modern teaching practices"},{"uid":"54e84230-864a-4f31-9cdb-91778ff7784d","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"cooling systems","passagePhrase":"mechanical means of ventilation such as air-conditioning"},{"uid":"be06d6bc-ba31-42ef-8ee1-0a13b9fa88dd","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"a hypothesis","passagePhrase":"suggested that"},{"uid":"3270593f-432c-4238-ad2c-a82b4ecea9bc","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"the growth in classroom noise","passagePhrase":"heightened activity and noise levels"},{"uid":"79e0c953-403c-4175-b5e6-81dd3d959508","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"a global team","passagePhrase":"an international working party"},{"uid":"76f1b545-8f83-4a8e-9d14-93436f42c85a","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"some children more at risk","passagePhrase":"vulnerable"},{"uid":"57c5e8ce-abaa-4003-881a-458439f15e9d","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"medical conditions","passagePhrase":"hearing impairment, autistic spectrum disorders (ASD) and attention deficit disorders"},{"uid":"bb8ef859-3908-4e84-8775-5fde7861e9b9","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"children with autism","passagePhrase":"Those experiencing these disorders"},{"uid":"1c209d0a-c57d-49b4-bbcc-205c83c13adc","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"noise can upset children with autism?","passagePhrase":"find sounds such as crowd noiseand the noise generated by machinery painful and distressing"},{"uid":"a9d6afd4-e221-4fcf-b650-bb4b1561b6c5","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"schoolchildren which have not been diagnosed","passagePhrase":"undiagnosed children"},{"uid":"9bfb799f-e9bc-48f7-a65c-3b7ecd5b30aa","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"the hearing problems","passagePhrase":"‘invisible‘ disabilities"},{"uid":"5766c517-f042-42e9-a648-dd1acf129e54","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"policy initiative","passagePhrase":"strategy"},{"uid":"f80003e9-baf4-46e2-8c62-d324d249abfd","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"give schoolchildren equal opportunity","passagePhrase":"all children, youth learners and adult learners will have equal opportunities"},{"uid":"b1945cce-1c73-4fed-a8cf-d4c6f1ddf86f","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"a demand","passagePhrase":"It is imperative that"},{"uid":"3df3a7c5-55bd-46e8-b38c-a4a182c565fe","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"increase awareness of the situation of children with auditory problems","passagePhrase":"the needs of these children are taken into account"},{"uid":"1b429d1e-3715-47f2-b09e-e03fbe7865ab","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"suitable worldwide regulations","passagePhrase":"appropriate international standards"}]},"reading_u2_179":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Venus in Transit</strong></p><p><em>June 2004 saw the first passage., known as a ‘transit` of the planet Venus across the face of the Sun in 122 years. Transits have helped shape our view of the whole Universe, as Heather Cooper and Nigel Henbest explain </em></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>On 8 June 2004, more than half the population of the world were treated to a rare astronomical event. For over six hours, the planet Venus steadily inched its way over the surface of the Sun. This “transit` of Venus was the first since 6 December l882. On that occasion, the American astronomer Professor Simon Newcomb led a party to South Africa to observe the event. They were based at a girls’ school, where – if is alleged – the combined forces of three schoolmistresses outperformed the professionals with the accuracy of their observations.</p><p><strong>B</strong><br>For centuries, transits of Venus have drawn explorers and astronomers alike to the four corners of the globe. And you can put it all down to the extraordinary polymath Edmond Halley. In November 1677, Halley observed a transit of the innermost planet Mercury, from the desolate island of St Helena in the South Pacific. .He realized that from different latitudes, the passage of the planet across the Sun’s disc would appear to differ. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33bfa5d3-d5f5-4aec-98c6-be7e23bbb418\" data-question=\"19\">By timing the transit from two widely-separated locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, teams of astronomers could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f31b781c-bdc6-4b4a-ad86-5ac8049e00e9\" data-question=\"19\">calculate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> the parallax angle – the apparent difference in position of an astronomical body due to a difference in the observer’s position. Calculating this angle would allow astronomers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f31b781c-bdc6-4b4a-ad86-5ac8049e00e9\" data-question=\"19\">measure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> what was then the ultimate goal; the distance of the Earth from the Sun. This distance is known as the ‘astronomical unit` or AU.</p><p><strong>C </strong><br>Halley was aware that the AU was one of the most fundamental of all astronomical measurements. Johannes Kepler, in the early 17*h century, had shown that the distances of the planets from the Sun governed their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c86846ee-9db1-4909-b8ca-15c512eb1513\" data-question=\"20\">orbital speeds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, which were easily measurable. But no-one had found a way to calculate accurate distances to the planets from the Earth. The goal was to measure the AU; then, knowing the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c86846ee-9db1-4909-b8ca-15c512eb1513\" data-question=\"20\">orbital speeds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of all the other planets round the Sun, the scale of the Solar System would fall into place. However, Halley realized that Mercury was so far away that its parallax angle would be very difficult to determine. As Venus was closer to the Earth, its parallax angle would be larger and Halley worked out that by using Venus it would be possible to measure the Sun`s distance to 1 part in 500. But there was as problem: transits of Venus, unlike those of Mercury; are rare. occurring in pairs roughly eight years apart every hundred or so years. Nevertheless, he accurately predicted that Venus would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"45b2d849-ff34-4ac9-b9a3-786b1217431e\" data-question=\"22\">cross the face of the Sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in both 1761 and 1769 – though he <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ab84a3fb-eb6f-4134-a074-b27620cbc333\" data-question=\"22\">didn`t survive to see either<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</p><p><strong>D </strong><br>Inspired by Halley’s suggestion of a way to pin down the scale of the Solar System, teams of British and French astronomers set out on expeditions to places as diverse as India and Siberia. But things weren’t helped by Britain and France being at war. The person who deserves most sympathy is the French astronomer Guillaume Le Gentil. He was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec751ea7-c937-4056-ac93-e23bd8b725f8\" data-question=\"15\">thwarted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> by the fact that the British were besieging his observation site at Pondicherry in India. Fleeing on a French warship crossing the Indian Ocean, Le Gentil <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"977c71cf-9ab2-47c6-ae5e-3ad0a13f96d8\" data-question=\"21\">saw<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> a wonderful transit – but the ship`s pitching and rolling <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0adbdcb-1bec-47ec-b70d-0e820f4fec9a\" data-question=\"21\">ruled out any attempt at making accurate observations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Undaunted, he remained south of the equator, keeping himself busy by studying the islands of Mauritius and Madagascar before setting off to observe the next transit in the Philippines. Ironically after travelling nearly 50,000 kilometres, his <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"5225f9ce-e215-47d2-95c2-5f116ea4ce7f\" data-question=\"23\">view was clouded out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> at the last moment, a very dispiriting experience.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>While the early transit timings were as precise as instruments would allow the measurements were dogged by the ‘black drop’ effect. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1a96c00-67a0-49bd-87f4-2ce77e31cb90\" data-question=\"24\">When Venus begins to cross the Sun’s disc<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6fd1bdcd-8fe6-4225-913c-c08c637d3e6c\" data-question=\"24\">it looks smeared not circular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> – which makes it difficult to establish timings. This is due to diffraction of light. The second problem is that Venus exhibits a halo of light when it is seen just outside the Sun’s disc. While this showed astronomers that Venus was surrounded by a thick layer of gases refracting sunlight around it, both effects <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d75009c8-58e8-445e-b920-029fb7b46562\" data-question=\"17\">made it impossible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to obtain accurate timings.</p><p><strong>F</strong><br>But astronomers labored hard to analyze the results of these expeditions to observe Venus transits. Jonathan Franz Encke, Director of the Belin Observatory, finally determined a value for the AU based on all <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0399a838-3014-47d6-b2cd-16c0a7bc5224\" data-question=\"14\">these parallax measurements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>: 153340,000 km. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0f93775-bc3d-4222-9561-a103f8c85b43\" data-question=\"18\">Reasonably accurate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> for the time, that is quite close to today’s value of 149,597,870 km, determined by radar, which has now superseded transits and all other methods in accuracy. The AU is a cosmic measuring rod, and the basis of how we scale the Universe today <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0399a838-3014-47d6-b2cd-16c0a7bc5224\" data-question=\"14\">The parallax principle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04029a1f-d277-4b57-9a58-8ca58c0be0bb\" data-question=\"14\">can be extended to measure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the distances to the stars. If we look at a star in January – when Earth is at one point in its orbit – it will seem to be in a different position from where it appears six months later. Knowing the width of Earth`s orbit, the parallax shift <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec92fd21-212f-4800-8754-3e4ffa2b8296\" data-question=\"26\">lets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> astronomers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7617660-7640-4338-a0ac-c6f628df3f07\" data-question=\"26\">calculate the distance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</p><p><strong>G </strong></p><p>June 2004’s transit of Venus was thus more of an astronomical spectacle than a scientifically important event. But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"badff64d-f550-4fc1-91a6-970e5d5ffa13\" data-question=\"16\">such transits have paved the way for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> what might prove to be one of the most vital <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6102f2c-01a6-4da8-a5a4-8c92f0db37c9\" data-question=\"16\">breakthroughs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in the cosmos – detecting Earth-sized planets orbiting other stars.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage has seven paragraphs, A-G.</p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-G</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28304\" id=\"question-wrapper-28304\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of different ways in which the parallax principle <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04029a1f-d277-4b57-9a58-8ca58c0be0bb\" data-question=\"14\">has been applied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28305\" id=\"question-wrapper-28305\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of an event which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec751ea7-c937-4056-ac93-e23bd8b725f8\" data-question=\"15\">prevented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> a transit observation </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28306\" id=\"question-wrapper-28306\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a statement about potential future <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6102f2c-01a6-4da8-a5a4-8c92f0db37c9\" data-question=\"16\">discoveries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"badff64d-f550-4fc1-91a6-970e5d5ffa13\" data-question=\"16\">leading on from transit observations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28307\" id=\"question-wrapper-28307\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of physical states connected with Venus which early astronomical instruments <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d75009c8-58e8-445e-b920-029fb7b46562\" data-question=\"17\">failed to overcome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following statements and the list of people below.</p><p>Match each statement with the correct person, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D</p><p><strong>List of Findings</strong></p><ul><li>A Edmond Halley</li><li>B Johannes Kepler</li><li>C Guillaume Le Gentil</li><li>D Johann Franz Encke</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28308\" id=\"question-wrapper-28308\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> He calculated the distance of the Sun from the Earth based on observations of Venus <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0f93775-bc3d-4222-9561-a103f8c85b43\" data-question=\"18\">with a fair degree of accuracy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28309\" id=\"question-wrapper-28309\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> He understood that the distance of the Sun from the Earth could be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f31b781c-bdc6-4b4a-ad86-5ac8049e00e9\" data-question=\"19\">worked out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33bfa5d3-d5f5-4aec-98c6-be7e23bbb418\" data-question=\"19\">comparing observations of a transit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28310\" id=\"question-wrapper-28310\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> He realised that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c86846ee-9db1-4909-b8ca-15c512eb1513\" data-question=\"20\">the time taken by a planet to go round<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> the Sun depends on its distance from the Sun. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28311\" id=\"question-wrapper-28311\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"977c71cf-9ab2-47c6-ae5e-3ad0a13f96d8\" data-question=\"21\">witnessed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> a Venus transit but was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0adbdcb-1bec-47ec-b70d-0e820f4fec9a\" data-question=\"21\">unable to make any calculations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage?</p><p>In following statements below, choose</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN </strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28312\" id=\"question-wrapper-28312\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Halley <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ab84a3fb-eb6f-4134-a074-b27620cbc333\" data-question=\"22\">observed one transit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of the planet Venus. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28313\" id=\"question-wrapper-28313\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Le Gentil <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"5225f9ce-e215-47d2-95c2-5f116ea4ce7f\" data-question=\"23\">managed to observe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> a second Venus transit. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28314\" id=\"question-wrapper-28314\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6fd1bdcd-8fe6-4225-913c-c08c637d3e6c\" data-question=\"24\">The shape of Venus appears distorted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1a96c00-67a0-49bd-87f4-2ce77e31cb90\" data-question=\"24\">it starts to pass in front of the Sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28315\" id=\"question-wrapper-28315\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Early astronomers suspected that the atmosphere on Venus was toxic. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28316\" id=\"question-wrapper-28316\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The parallax principle <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec92fd21-212f-4800-8754-3e4ffa2b8296\" data-question=\"26\">allows<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> astronomers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7617660-7640-4338-a0ac-c6f628df3f07\" data-question=\"26\">work out how far away distant stars are from the Earth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"33bfa5d3-d5f5-4aec-98c6-be7e23bbb418","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"comparing observations of a transit","passagePhrase":"By timing the transit from two widely-separated locations"},{"uid":"f31b781c-bdc6-4b4a-ad86-5ac8049e00e9","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"worked out","passagePhrase":"calculate ... measure"},{"uid":"c86846ee-9db1-4909-b8ca-15c512eb1513","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the time taken by a planet to go round","passagePhrase":"orbital speeds ... orbital speeds"},{"uid":"45b2d849-ff34-4ac9-b9a3-786b1217431e","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"cross the face of the Sun"},{"uid":"ec751ea7-c937-4056-ac93-e23bd8b725f8","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"prevented","passagePhrase":"thwarted"},{"uid":"977c71cf-9ab2-47c6-ae5e-3ad0a13f96d8","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"witnessed","passagePhrase":"saw"},{"uid":"d0adbdcb-1bec-47ec-b70d-0e820f4fec9a","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"unable to make any calculations","passagePhrase":"ruled out any attempt at making accurate observations"},{"uid":"b1a96c00-67a0-49bd-87f4-2ce77e31cb90","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"it starts to pass in front of the Sun","passagePhrase":"When Venus begins to cross the Sun’s disc"},{"uid":"6fd1bdcd-8fe6-4225-913c-c08c637d3e6c","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"The shape of Venus appears distorted","passagePhrase":"it looks smeared not circular"},{"uid":"d75009c8-58e8-445e-b920-029fb7b46562","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"failed to overcome","passagePhrase":"made it impossible"},{"uid":"0399a838-3014-47d6-b2cd-16c0a7bc5224","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"these parallax measurements ... The parallax principle"},{"uid":"d0f93775-bc3d-4222-9561-a103f8c85b43","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"with a fair degree of accuracy","passagePhrase":"Reasonably accurate"},{"uid":"04029a1f-d277-4b57-9a58-8ca58c0be0bb","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"has been applied","passagePhrase":"can be extended to measure"},{"uid":"ec92fd21-212f-4800-8754-3e4ffa2b8296","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"allows","passagePhrase":"lets"},{"uid":"a7617660-7640-4338-a0ac-c6f628df3f07","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"work out how far away distant stars are from the Earth","passagePhrase":"calculate the distance"},{"uid":"badff64d-f550-4fc1-91a6-970e5d5ffa13","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"leading on from transit observations","passagePhrase":"such transits have paved the way for"},{"uid":"d6102f2c-01a6-4da8-a5a4-8c92f0db37c9","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"discoveries","passagePhrase":"breakthroughs"}]},"reading_u2_180":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>A Neuroscientist Reveals How to Think Differently</strong></p><p>In the last decade, a revolution has occurred in the way that scientists think about the brain. We now know that the decisions humans make can be traced to the firing patterns of neurones in specific parts of the brain. These discoveries have led to the field known as neuroeconomics, which studies the brain’s secrets to success in an economic environment that demands innovation and being able to do things differently from competitors. A brain that can do this is an iconoclastic one. Briefly, an iconoclast is a person who does something that others say can’t be done.</p><p>This definition implies that iconoclasts are different from other people, but more precisely, it is their brains that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1080b539-3af4-439b-9a70-709f32b6dc0b\" data-question=\"28\">are different in three distinct ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>: perception, fear response, and social intelligence. Each of these three functions utilizes a different circuit in the brain. Naysayers might suggest that the brain is irrelevant, that thinking in an original, even revolutionary way is more a matter of personality than brain function. But the held of neuroeconomics was born out of the realization that the physical workings of the brain place limitations on the way we make decisions. By understanding these constraints, we begin to understand why some people march to a different drumbeat.</p><p>The first thing to realize is that the brain suffers from limited resources. It has a fixed energy budget, about the same as a 40 watt light bulb, so it has evolved to work as efficiently as possible. This is where most people are impeded from being an iconoclast. For example, when confronted with information streaming from the eyes, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b742a5b0-df35-4af2-a10d-e09cc9f481e2\" data-question=\"29\">the brain will interpret this information in the quickest way possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Thus it will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"678c1c0d-a709-48df-b434-0aa620e164e5\" data-question=\"29\">draw on both past experience and any other source of information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, such as what other people say, to make sense of what it is seeing. This happens all the time. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b742a5b0-df35-4af2-a10d-e09cc9f481e2\" data-question=\"29\">The brain takes shortcuts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that work so well we are hardly ever aware of them. We think our perceptions of the world are real, but they are only biological and electrical rumblings. Perception is not simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e565f94-1d4d-4e25-8e7e-b3f7f7e3b94c\" data-question=\"30\">a product of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> what your eyes or ears transmit to your brain. More than the physical reality of photons or sound waves, perception is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e565f94-1d4d-4e25-8e7e-b3f7f7e3b94c\" data-question=\"30\">a product of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> the brain.</p><p>Perception is central to iconoclasm. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0eb9a575-06ff-4f31-9870-9204b423f5c7\" data-question=\"31\">Iconoclasts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> see things differently to other people. Their brains <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"486a4c80-b312-4757-8e36-b326363836b2\" data-question=\"31\">do not fall into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b2ddab0b-7791-4875-b6d7-86cf57605e38\" data-question=\"31\">efficiency pitfalls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> as much as the average person’s brain. iconoclasts, either because they were born that way or through learning, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"486a4c80-b312-4757-8e36-b326363836b2\" data-question=\"31\">have found ways to work around<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b2ddab0b-7791-4875-b6d7-86cf57605e38\" data-question=\"31\">the perceptual shortcuts that plague most people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Perception is not something that is hardwired into the brain. It is a learned process, which is both a curse and an opportunity for change. The brain faces the fundamental problem of interpreting physical stimuli from the senses.</p><p>Everything the brain sees, hears, or touches has multiple interpretations. The one that is ultimately chosen is simply the brain’s best theory. ln technical terms, these conjectures have their basis in the statistical likelihood of one interpretation over another and are heavily influenced by past experience and, importantly for potential iconoclasts what other people say.</p><p>The best way to see things differently to other people is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e60c6da6-3757-4a72-8173-23f4c622e90f\" data-question=\"32\">bombard the brain with things it has never encountered before<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Novelty releases the perceptual process from the chains of past experience and forces the brain to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11251ff7-b170-4580-ad8e-8d5cfee48792\" data-question=\"32\">make new judgments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Successful iconoclasts <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55743552-9563-48e6-b8fe-ba5b1a1a94da\" data-question=\"33\">have an extraordinary willingness to be exposed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"32e72279-1e95-41e1-8f9f-3bacae0319d4\" data-question=\"33\">what is fresh and different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. Observation of iconoclasts shows that they embrace novelty while most people avoid things that are different.</p><p>The problem with novelty, however, is that lt tends to trigger the brain’s fear system. Fear is a major impediment to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d64291a-a536-4470-b383-8a0a370905ef\" data-question=\"35\">thinking like an iconoclast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"238552bd-0a69-4538-b704-8f181ee3cb31\" data-question=\"35\">stops the average person in his tracks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. There are many types of fear, but the two that inhibit iconoclastic thinking and people generally find difficult to deal with are fear of uncertainty and fear of public ridicule. These may seem like trivial phobias. But fear of public speaking, which everyone must do from time to time, afflicts one-third of the population. This makes it too common to be considered a mental disorder. It is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c0533cbb-d9d6-4666-b79c-5b46aeead5f9\" data-question=\"37\">simply a common variant of human nature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, one which iconoclasts do not let inhibit their reactions</p><p>Finally, to be successful iconoclasts, individuals must sell their ideas to other people. This is where social intelligence comes in. Social intelligence is the ability to understand and manage people in a business setting. ln the last decade, there has been an explosion of knowledge about the social brain and how the brain works when groups coordinate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e326d7df-1af4-48eb-84be-378bbd3ca1be\" data-question=\"38\">decision making<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. Neuroscience has revealed which brain circuits are responsible for functions like understanding what other people think, empathy, fairness, and social identity. These brain regions <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ca23128-05e6-41cd-bb38-3d85d4731066\" data-question=\"39\">play key roles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> in whether people convince others of their ideas. Perception is important in social cognition too. The perception of someone’s enthusiasm, or reputation, can make or break a deal. Understanding how perception becomes intertwined with social <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e326d7df-1af4-48eb-84be-378bbd3ca1be\" data-question=\"38\">decision making<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> shows why successful iconoclasts are so rare.</p><p>Iconoclasts create new opportunities in every area from artistic expression to technology to business They supply creativity and innovation not easily accomplished by committees. Rules aren’t important to them. Iconoclasts face alienation and failure, but can also be a major asset to any organization. It is crucial for success in any field to understand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71ef6b60-0e89-4da9-a2b9-0679f0d46676\" data-question=\"40\">how the iconoclastic mind works<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose appropriate options <strong>A, B, C</strong> or <strong>D</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28317\" id=\"question-wrapper-28317\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Neuroeconomics is a field of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"904511c0-132d-43ae-861b-3bca5f2edb7e\" data-question=\"27\">study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"904511c0-132d-43ae-861b-3bca5f2edb7e\" data-question=\"27\">seeks to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. cause a change in how scientists understand brain chemistry.</li> <li>B. understand how good decisions are made in the brain.</li> <li>C. understand how the brain is linked to achievement in competitive fields.</li> <li>D. trace the specific firing patterns of neurons in different areas of the brain.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28318\" id=\"question-wrapper-28318\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the writer, iconoclasts <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1080b539-3af4-439b-9a70-709f32b6dc0b\" data-question=\"28\">are distinctive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> because </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. they create unusual brain circuits.</li> <li>B. their brains function differently.</li> <li>C. their personalities are distinctive. </li> <li>D. they make decisions easily.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28319\" id=\"question-wrapper-28319\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the writer, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b742a5b0-df35-4af2-a10d-e09cc9f481e2\" data-question=\"29\">the brain works efficiently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> because </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. it uses the eyes quickly.</li> <li>B. it interprets data logically.</li> <li>C. it generates its own energy.</li> <li>D. it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"678c1c0d-a709-48df-b434-0aa620e164e5\" data-question=\"29\">relies on previous events<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28320\" id=\"question-wrapper-28320\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer says that perception is </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. a combination of photons and sound waves.</li> <li>B. a reliable product of what your senses transmit</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e565f94-1d4d-4e25-8e7e-b3f7f7e3b94c\" data-question=\"30\">a result of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> brain processes.</li> <li>D. a process we are usually conscious of.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28321\" id=\"question-wrapper-28321\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the writer, an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0eb9a575-06ff-4f31-9870-9204b423f5c7\" data-question=\"31\">iconoclastic thinker<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. centralises perceptual thinking in one part of the brain.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"486a4c80-b312-4757-8e36-b326363836b2\" data-question=\"31\">avoids<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b2ddab0b-7791-4875-b6d7-86cf57605e38\" data-question=\"31\">cognitive traps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>C. has a brain that is hardwired for learning</li> <li>D. has more opportunities than the average person.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage?</p><p>In following statements below, choose</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN </strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28322\" id=\"question-wrapper-28322\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e60c6da6-3757-4a72-8173-23f4c622e90f\" data-question=\"32\">Exposure to different events<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> forces the brain to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11251ff7-b170-4580-ad8e-8d5cfee48792\" data-question=\"32\">think differently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28323\" id=\"question-wrapper-28323\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Iconoclasts <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55743552-9563-48e6-b8fe-ba5b1a1a94da\" data-question=\"33\">are unusually receptive to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"32e72279-1e95-41e1-8f9f-3bacae0319d4\" data-question=\"33\">new experiences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28324\" id=\"question-wrapper-28324\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Most people are too shy to try different things. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28325\" id=\"question-wrapper-28325\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> If you <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d64291a-a536-4470-b383-8a0a370905ef\" data-question=\"35\">think in an iconoclastic way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, you can easily <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"238552bd-0a69-4538-b704-8f181ee3cb31\" data-question=\"35\">overcome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> fear. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28326\" id=\"question-wrapper-28326\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When concern about embarrassment matters less, other fears become irrelevant. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28327\" id=\"question-wrapper-28327\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Fear of public speaking is a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c0533cbb-d9d6-4666-b79c-5b46aeead5f9\" data-question=\"37\">psychological illness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-E, below.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-E</p><p><strong>List of Endings</strong></p><ul><li>A requires both perceptual and social intelligence skills.</li><li>B focuses on how groups <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e326d7df-1af4-48eb-84be-378bbd3ca1be\" data-question=\"38\">decide on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> an action.</li><li>C works in many fields, both artistic and scientific.</li><li>D leaves one open to criticism and rejection.</li><li>E involves understanding how organisations manage people.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28328\" id=\"question-wrapper-28328\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Thinking like a successful iconoclast is demanding because it </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28329\" id=\"question-wrapper-28329\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The concept of the social brain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ca23128-05e6-41cd-bb38-3d85d4731066\" data-question=\"39\">is useful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> to iconoclasts because it </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28330\" id=\"question-wrapper-28330\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Iconoclasts are generally an asset because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71ef6b60-0e89-4da9-a2b9-0679f0d46676\" data-question=\"40\">their way of thinking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"1080b539-3af4-439b-9a70-709f32b6dc0b","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"are distinctive","passagePhrase":"are different in three distinct ways"},{"uid":"b742a5b0-df35-4af2-a10d-e09cc9f481e2","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"the brain works efficiently","passagePhrase":"the brain will interpret this information in the quickest way possible ... The brain takes shortcuts"},{"uid":"678c1c0d-a709-48df-b434-0aa620e164e5","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"relies on previous events","passagePhrase":"draw on both past experience and any other source of information"},{"uid":"1e565f94-1d4d-4e25-8e7e-b3f7f7e3b94c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"a result of","passagePhrase":"a product of ... a product of"},{"uid":"0eb9a575-06ff-4f31-9870-9204b423f5c7","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"iconoclastic thinker","passagePhrase":"Iconoclasts"},{"uid":"486a4c80-b312-4757-8e36-b326363836b2","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"avoids","passagePhrase":"do not fall into ... have found ways to work around"},{"uid":"b2ddab0b-7791-4875-b6d7-86cf57605e38","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"cognitive traps","passagePhrase":"efficiency pitfalls ... the perceptual shortcuts that plague most people"},{"uid":"e60c6da6-3757-4a72-8173-23f4c622e90f","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Exposure to different events","passagePhrase":"bombard the brain with things it has never encountered before"},{"uid":"11251ff7-b170-4580-ad8e-8d5cfee48792","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"think differently","passagePhrase":"make new judgments"},{"uid":"55743552-9563-48e6-b8fe-ba5b1a1a94da","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"are unusually receptive to","passagePhrase":"have an extraordinary willingness to be exposed to"},{"uid":"32e72279-1e95-41e1-8f9f-3bacae0319d4","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"new experiences","passagePhrase":"what is fresh and different"},{"uid":"1d64291a-a536-4470-b383-8a0a370905ef","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"think in an iconoclastic way","passagePhrase":"thinking like an iconoclast"},{"uid":"e326d7df-1af4-48eb-84be-378bbd3ca1be","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"decide on","passagePhrase":"decision making ... decision making"},{"uid":"8ca23128-05e6-41cd-bb38-3d85d4731066","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"is useful","passagePhrase":"play key roles"},{"uid":"71ef6b60-0e89-4da9-a2b9-0679f0d46676","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"their way of thinking","passagePhrase":"how the iconoclastic mind works"},{"uid":"904511c0-132d-43ae-861b-3bca5f2edb7e","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"study ... seeks to","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_181":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Attitudes to Language</strong></p><p>It is not easy to be systematic and objective about language study. Popular linguistic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"38e7df7c-d46f-4c50-9283-66358b078093\" data-question=\"1\">debate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> regularly deteriorates into invective and polemic. Language belongs to everyone, so most people feel they have a right to hold an opinion about it And <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"38e7df7c-d46f-4c50-9283-66358b078093\" data-question=\"1\">when opinions differ<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, emotions can run high. Arguments can start <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"5643c1be-f5a3-4e87-90de-ee8fc4b916db\" data-question=\"2\">as easily over minor points of usage as over major<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> policies of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c189b607-6c66-4760-9dd3-a85721a8ad7f\" data-question=\"2\">linguistic education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</p><p>Language, more oven is a very public behavior so it is easy for different usages to be noted and criticized No part of society or social behavior is exempt: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5927b2d-9319-41b6-a3b5-935697882243\" data-question=\"3\">linguistic factors influence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7fb63d7b-e866-400a-a037-823042c5dc16\" data-question=\"3\">how we judge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> personality, intelligence, social status, educational standards, job aptitude, and many other areas of identity and social survival. As a result, it is easy to hurt, and to be hurt, when language use is unfeelingly attacked.</p><p>ln its most general sense. prescriptivism is the view that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6b746c5-d6c1-49bc-a243-df221373d6b0\" data-question=\"9\">one variety of language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> has an inherently higher value than others, and that this ought to be imposed on the whole of the speech community. The view is propounded especially in relation to grammar and vocabulary, and frequently with reference to pronunciation. The variety which ls favoured, in this account, ls usually a version of the ‘standard’ written language, especially as encountered in literature, or in the formal spoken language which most closely reflects this style. Adherents to this variety are said to speak or write ‘correctly’; deviations from lt are said to be ‘incorrect`.</p><p>All the main languages have been studied prescriptlvely, especially in the 18th-century approach to the writing of grammars and dictionaries. The aims of these early grammarians were threefold: [a) they wanted to codify the principles of their languages, to show that there was a system beneath the apparent chaos of usage. (b] they wanted a means of settling disputes over usage, and (c] they wanted to point out what they felt to be common errors, in order to ‘improve’ the language. The authoritarian nature of the approach <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b252aa29-74b9-4a9a-8303-21b0c26ba46c\" data-question=\"10\">is best characterized by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> its reliance on ‘rules’ of grammar Some usages are prescribed; to be learnt and followed accurately; others are prescribed to be avoided. ln this early period, there were no half-measures: usage was either right or wrong. and it was the task of the grammarian not simply to record alliterative but to pronounce judgement upon them.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da12cf6c-6bfb-4270-a132-194ad7abf3af\" data-question=\"5\">These attitudes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b316e5a3-1c96-4b6a-8e75-db7bda5a48da\" data-question=\"5\">still with us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, and they motivate a widespread concern that linguistic standards should be maintained. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3be82eb4-09a1-4a90-b81b-defd8ab73420\" data-question=\"11\">Nevertheless<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, there is an alternative <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9988ee23-728e-4766-b09e-c29533f01062\" data-question=\"11\">point of view<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> that is concerned less with standards than with the facts of linguistic usage. This approach ls summarized in the statement that it is the task of the grammarian to describe not prescribe to record the facts of linguistic diversity, and not to attempt the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5c0ca38-72ed-4259-bdd1-229957a10a51\" data-question=\"6\">impossible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> tasks of evaluating language variation or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9fc81c2d-debf-4d3d-886e-a6707ba66fa9\" data-question=\"6\">halting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> language change. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e6f30c7f-2168-4747-9ad1-54e28199f003\" data-question=\"7\">In the second half of the 18th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, we already find advocates of this view, such as Joseph Priestley, whose Rudiments of English Grammar (1761) insists that ‘the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5a46380-321f-4da7-a81e-b0c308884124\" data-question=\"12\">custom of speaking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> is the original and only just standard of any language. `Linguistic issues, it is argued, cannot be solved by logic and legislation. And this view has become the tenet of the modem linguistic approach to grammatical analysis.</p><p>In our own time, the opposition between ‘descriptivists’ and ‘prescriptivists’ has often become extreme. with both sides <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"adbb482f-b08a-45cc-80c7-9752bb931512\" data-question=\"8\">painting unreal pictures of the other<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. Descriptive grammarians have been presented as people who do not care about standards, because of the way they see all forms of usage as equally valid. Prescriptive grammarians have been presented as blind adherents to a historical tradition. The opposition has even been presented in quasi-political terms – of radical liberalism vs elitist conservatism.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage?</p><p>In following statements below, choose</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN </strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28331\" id=\"question-wrapper-28331\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There are understandable reasons why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"38e7df7c-d46f-4c50-9283-66358b078093\" data-question=\"1\">arguments occur<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> about language. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28332\" id=\"question-wrapper-28332\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"5643c1be-f5a3-4e87-90de-ee8fc4b916db\" data-question=\"2\">feel more strongly about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c189b607-6c66-4760-9dd3-a85721a8ad7f\" data-question=\"2\">language education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> than about small differences in language usage. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28333\" id=\"question-wrapper-28333\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7fb63d7b-e866-400a-a037-823042c5dc16\" data-question=\"3\">assessment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of a person’s intelligence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5927b2d-9319-41b6-a3b5-935697882243\" data-question=\"3\">is affected by the way he or she uses language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28334\" id=\"question-wrapper-28334\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Prescriptive grammar books cost a lot of money to buy in the 18th century. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28335\" id=\"question-wrapper-28335\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da12cf6c-6bfb-4270-a132-194ad7abf3af\" data-question=\"5\">Prescriptivism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b316e5a3-1c96-4b6a-8e75-db7bda5a48da\" data-question=\"5\">still exists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> today. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28336\" id=\"question-wrapper-28336\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to descriptivists it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5c0ca38-72ed-4259-bdd1-229957a10a51\" data-question=\"6\">pointless<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> to try to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9fc81c2d-debf-4d3d-886e-a6707ba66fa9\" data-question=\"6\">stop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> language change. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28337\" id=\"question-wrapper-28337\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Descriptivism only appeared <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e6f30c7f-2168-4747-9ad1-54e28199f003\" data-question=\"7\">after the 18th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28338\" id=\"question-wrapper-28338\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Both descriptivists and prescriptivists have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"adbb482f-b08a-45cc-80c7-9752bb931512\" data-question=\"8\">misrepresented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary using the list of words, A-I, below.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-I</p><ul><li>A descriptivists</li><li>B language experts</li><li>C <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5a46380-321f-4da7-a81e-b0c308884124\" data-question=\"12\">popular speech<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span></li><li>D formal language</li><li>E evaluation</li><li>F rules</li><li>G modern linguists</li><li>H prescriptivists</li><li>I change</li></ul><p><strong>The language debate</strong></p><p>According to 9 _______, there is only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6b746c5-d6c1-49bc-a243-df221373d6b0\" data-question=\"9\">one correct form of language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Linguists who take this approach to language <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b252aa29-74b9-4a9a-8303-21b0c26ba46c\" data-question=\"10\">place great importance on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> grammatical 10 _______. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3be82eb4-09a1-4a90-b81b-defd8ab73420\" data-question=\"11\">Conversely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9988ee23-728e-4766-b09e-c29533f01062\" data-question=\"11\">the view of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> 11 _______, such as Joseph Priestley, is that grammar should be based on 12 _______.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28370\" id=\"question-wrapper-28370\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28339\" id=\"question-wrapper-28339\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28340\" id=\"question-wrapper-28340\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28341\" id=\"question-wrapper-28341\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose appropriate options <strong>A, B, C</strong> or <strong>D</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28342\" id=\"question-wrapper-28342\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer’s purpose in Reading Passage 1? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. to argue in favour of a particular approach to writing dictionaries and grammar books</li> <li>B. to present a historical account of differing views of language</li> <li>C. to describe the differences between spoken and written language</li> <li>D. to show how a certain view of language has been discredited</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"38e7df7c-d46f-4c50-9283-66358b078093","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"arguments occur","passagePhrase":"debate ... when opinions differ"},{"uid":"c189b607-6c66-4760-9dd3-a85721a8ad7f","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"language education","passagePhrase":"linguistic education"},{"uid":"d5927b2d-9319-41b6-a3b5-935697882243","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"is affected by the way he or she uses language","passagePhrase":"linguistic factors influence"},{"uid":"7fb63d7b-e866-400a-a037-823042c5dc16","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"assessment","passagePhrase":"how we judge"},{"uid":"d6b746c5-d6c1-49bc-a243-df221373d6b0","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"one correct form of language","passagePhrase":"one variety of language"},{"uid":"b252aa29-74b9-4a9a-8303-21b0c26ba46c","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"place great importance on","passagePhrase":"is best characterized by"},{"uid":"da12cf6c-6bfb-4270-a132-194ad7abf3af","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Prescriptivism","passagePhrase":"These attitudes"},{"uid":"b316e5a3-1c96-4b6a-8e75-db7bda5a48da","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"still exists","passagePhrase":"still with us"},{"uid":"3be82eb4-09a1-4a90-b81b-defd8ab73420","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Conversely","passagePhrase":"Nevertheless"},{"uid":"9988ee23-728e-4766-b09e-c29533f01062","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"the view of","passagePhrase":"point of view"},{"uid":"a5c0ca38-72ed-4259-bdd1-229957a10a51","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"pointless","passagePhrase":"impossible"},{"uid":"9fc81c2d-debf-4d3d-886e-a6707ba66fa9","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"stop","passagePhrase":"halting"},{"uid":"e5a46380-321f-4da7-a81e-b0c308884124","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"popular speech","passagePhrase":"custom of speaking"},{"uid":"adbb482f-b08a-45cc-80c7-9752bb931512","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"misrepresented","passagePhrase":"painting unreal pictures of the other"}]},"reading_u2_182":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Tidal Power</strong></p><p><em>Undersea turbines which produce electricity from the tides are set to become an important source of renewable energy for Britain. It is still too early to predict the extent of the impact they may have. but all the signs are that they will play a significant role in the future.</em></p><p><strong>A. </strong></p><p>Operating on the same principle as wind turbines, the power in sea turbines comes from tidal currents which turn blades similar to ships’ propellers, but, unlike the wind, the tides are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"207137a4-7078-4ec3-923a-62de48104674\">predictable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> and the power input is constant. The technology raises the prospect of Britain becoming self-sufficient in renewable energy and drastically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"c7aa0b7a-8954-4a97-ab85-da29b26d9801\">reducing its carbon dioxide emissions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, if tide, wind and wave power are all developed. Britain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"535fc31d-0de9-4ead-8387-555a3de56835\">would be able to close gas, coal and nuclear power plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and export renewable power to other parts of Europe. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"1e053a7b-968b-41fa-8aa8-08f43f8ff6a3\">Unlike wind power which Britain originally developed and then abandoned for 20 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> allowing the Dutch to make it a major industry, undersea turbines could become <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"1dafacad-4a35-46a8-8671-0af67d03d701\">a big export earner<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> to island nations such as Japan and New Zealand.</p><p><strong>B. </strong></p><p>Tidal sites have already been identified that will produce one-sixth or more of the UK’s power – and at prices competitive with modern gas turbines and undercutting those of the already ailing nuclear industry. One site alone, the Pendand Firth, between Orkney and mainland Scotland, could produce 10% of the country’s electricity with banks of turbines under the sea, and another at Alderney in the Channel islands three times the 1,200 megawatts of Britain’s largest and newest nuclear plant, Sizewell B, in Suffolk. Other sites identified include the Bristol Channel and the west coast of Scotland, particularly the channel between Campbeltown and Northern Ireland.</p><p><strong>C. </strong></p><p>Work on designs for the new turbine blades and sites are well advanced at the University of Southampton‘s sustainable energy research group. The first <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d79b50b9-c9ec-4ad1-893e-31b43aacc797\">station<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> is expected to be installed off Lynmouth in Devon shortly to test the technology in a venture jointly funded by the department of Trade and Industry and the European Union. AbuBakr Bahaj, in charge of the Southampton research. said: The prospects for energy from tidal currents are far better than from wind because the flows of water are predictable and constant. The technology for dealing with the hostile saline environment under the sea has been developed in the North Sea oil industry and much is already known about turbine blade design, because of wind power and ship propellers. There are a few technical difficulties, but I believe in the next nine to ten years we will be installing commercial marine turbine farms.’ Southampton has been awarded £2’l5.U.`D over three years to develop the turbines and is working with Marine Current Turbines. a subsidiary of IT power; on the Lynmouth project. EU research has now identified 1GB potential sites for tidal powen BG% round the coasts of Britain. The best sites are between islands or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"2f880181-690b-44e9-b898-71af94e31284\">around heavily indented coasts where there are strong tidal currents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</p><p><strong>D.</strong></p><p>A marine turbine blade needs to be only one-third of the size of a wind generator to produce three times as much power. The blades will be about 20 metres in diameter so around 30 metres of water is required. Unlike wind power, there are unlikely to be environmental objections. Fish and other creatures are thought unlikely to be at risk from the relatively slow turning blades. Each turbine will be mounted on a tower which will connect to the national power supply grid via underwater cables. The towers will stick out of the water and be lit. to warn shipping, and also be designed to be lifted out of the water for maintenance and to clean seaweed from the blades.</p><p><strong>E.</strong></p><p>Dr Baha has done most work on the Alderrney site, where there are powerful currents. The single undersea turbine farm would produce far more power than needed for the Channel Islands and most would be fed into the French Grid and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"8b8ab57f-e051-4427-acb8-252deb81cac9\">be re-imported into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> Britain via the cable under the Channel.</p><p><strong>F.</strong></p><p>One technical difficulty is cavitation, where low pressure behind a turning blade causes air bubbles. These can cause vibration and damage the blades of the turbines. Dr Bahaj said: ‘We have to test a number of blade types to avoid this happening or at least make sure it does not damage the turbines or reduce performance. Another slight concern is submerged debris floating into the blades. So far we do not know how much of a problem it might be. We will have to make the turbines robust because the sea is a hostile environment. but all the signs that we can do it are good.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage has six paragraphs, A-F.</p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28343\" id=\"question-wrapper-28343\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the location of the first test <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"14\" data-uid=\"d79b50b9-c9ec-4ad1-893e-31b43aacc797\">site<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28344\" id=\"question-wrapper-28344\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a way of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"15\" data-uid=\"8b8ab57f-e051-4427-acb8-252deb81cac9\">bringing the power produced on one site back<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> into Britain </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28345\" id=\"question-wrapper-28345\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"16\" data-uid=\"1e053a7b-968b-41fa-8aa8-08f43f8ff6a3\">previous attempt by Britain to find an alternative source of energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28346\" id=\"question-wrapper-28346\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"17\" data-uid=\"37b2fef5-cc30-4f24-a2a4-998fc5128e14\">the possibility of applying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> technology from another industry </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Which <strong>FIVE </strong>of the following claims about tidal power are made by the writer?</p><ul><li><strong>A. </strong>It is a more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"18\" data-uid=\"207137a4-7078-4ec3-923a-62de48104674\">reliable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> source of energy than wind power.</li><li><strong>B. </strong> It would replace all other forms of energy in Britain.</li><li><strong>C. </strong> Its introduction has come as a result of public pressure.</li><li><strong>D. </strong> It would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"19\" data-uid=\"c7aa0b7a-8954-4a97-ab85-da29b26d9801\">cut down on air pollution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</li><li><strong>E. </strong> It could contribute to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"20\" data-uid=\"535fc31d-0de9-4ead-8387-555a3de56835\">the closure of many existing power stations in Britain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</li><li><strong>F. </strong> It could be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"21\" data-uid=\"1dafacad-4a35-46a8-8671-0af67d03d701\">a means of increasing national income<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</li><li><strong>G. </strong> It could face a lot of resistance from other fuel industries.</li><li><strong>H. </strong> It could be sold more cheaply than any other type of fuel.</li><li><strong>I.</strong> It could compensate for the shortage of inland sites for energy production.</li><li><strong>J. </strong> It is best produced <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"22\" data-uid=\"2f880181-690b-44e9-b898-71af94e31284\">in the vicinity of coastlines with particular features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28347\" id=\"question-wrapper-28347\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/D/E/F/J</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28348\" id=\"question-wrapper-28348\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/D/E/F/J</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28349\" id=\"question-wrapper-28349\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/D/E/F/J</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28350\" id=\"question-wrapper-28350\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/D/E/F/J</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28351\" id=\"question-wrapper-28351\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/D/E/F/J</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Label the diagram below.</p><p>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer</p><p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><em><img src=\"/media/gg_imgs/test/411525c212fd0eb20fa7d65b7f9b5bd18e142fd8.jpg\" style=\"height:569px; width:624px\"></em></span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28352\" id=\"question-wrapper-28352\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MAINTENANCE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28353\" id=\"question-wrapper-28353\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SLOW (TURNING) [OR] SLOW-TURNING</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28354\" id=\"question-wrapper-28354\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LOW PRESSURE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28355\" id=\"question-wrapper-28355\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CAVITATION</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"207137a4-7078-4ec3-923a-62de48104674","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"reliable","passagePhrase":"predictable"},{"uid":"c7aa0b7a-8954-4a97-ab85-da29b26d9801","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"cut down on air pollution","passagePhrase":"reducing its carbon dioxide emissions"},{"uid":"535fc31d-0de9-4ead-8387-555a3de56835","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the closure of many existing power stations in Britain","passagePhrase":"would be able to close gas, coal and nuclear power plants"},{"uid":"1e053a7b-968b-41fa-8aa8-08f43f8ff6a3","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"previous attempt by Britain to find an alternative source of energy","passagePhrase":"Unlike wind power which Britain originally developed and then abandoned for 20 years"},{"uid":"1dafacad-4a35-46a8-8671-0af67d03d701","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"a means of increasing national income","passagePhrase":"a big export earner"},{"uid":"d79b50b9-c9ec-4ad1-893e-31b43aacc797","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"site","passagePhrase":"station"},{"uid":"2f880181-690b-44e9-b898-71af94e31284","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"in the vicinity of coastlines with particular features","passagePhrase":"around heavily indented coasts where there are strong tidal currents"},{"uid":"8b8ab57f-e051-4427-acb8-252deb81cac9","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"bringing the power produced on one site back","passagePhrase":"be re-imported into"},{"uid":"37b2fef5-cc30-4f24-a2a4-998fc5128e14","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"the possibility of applying","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_183":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Information Theory - the Big Data</strong></p><p><em>Information theory lies at the heart of everything – from DVD players and the genetic code of DNA to the physics of the universe at its most fundamental. it has been central to the development of the science of communication, which enables data to be sent electronically and has therefore had a major impact on our lives.</em></p><p><strong>A.</strong></p><p>In April 2002 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"164143ed-1406-4e01-a9b5-b105e1e2bda8\" data-question=\"31\">an event took place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> which demonstrated one of the many applications of information theory. The space probe, Voyager I, launched in 1977, had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd22861e-1fe7-49c4-92c8-002fd98f0d9b\" data-question=\"33\">sent back<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> spectacular <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"328ce0ed-e558-4d55-9688-9654b3c5f1c3\" data-question=\"33\">images<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of Jupiter and Saturn and then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06a7c67b-3136-43ef-b0d3-5af96769f98c\" data-question=\"34\">soared out of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the Solar System on a one-way mission to the stars. After 25 years of exposure to the freezing temperatures of deep space, the probe was beginning to show its age, Sensors and circuits <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b556a655-cc72-407d-b3fa-c4c4ef46d1f0\" data-question=\"35\">were on the brink of failing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and NASA experts realized that they had to do something or lose contact with their probe forever. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e24e69f-be67-493a-b830-9ca6798c3188\" data-question=\"36\">The solution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> was to get a message to Voyager I to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"191f6232-2fd7-44a4-b5ef-9d7cf9897841\" data-question=\"36\">instruct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> it to use spares to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1eef5aa-0b63-4998-aca5-c91d30aaaba6\" data-question=\"36\">change the failing parts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. With the probe 12 billion kilometers from Earth, this was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f182424c-687d-4995-8790-938adc72606d\" data-question=\"36\">not an easy task<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. By means of a radio dish belonging to NASA’s Deep Space Network, the message was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4233dfb-f630-483f-861a-811b33c12ac8\" data-question=\"37\">sent out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> into the depths of space. Even travelling at the speed of light, it took over II hours to reach its target, far beyond the orbit of Pluto. Yet, incredibly, the little probe managed to hear the faint call from its home planet, and successfully made the switchover.</p><p><strong>B.</strong></p><p>It was the Ingest·distance repair job in history, and a triumph for the NASA engineers. But it also highlighted the astonishing power of the techniques developed by American communications engineer Claude Shannon, who had died just a year earlier. Born in 1916 in Petoskey, Michigart. Shannon showed an early talent for maths and for building gadgets, and made breakthroughs in the foundations of computer technology when still a student. While at Bell laboratories, Shannon developed information theory, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6c88c3c-f4a7-4512-87e0-7ed74afe25d3\" data-question=\"29\">shunned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the resulting acclaim. In the 1940s. he singlehandedly created an entire science of communication which has since inveigled its way into a host of applications, from DVDs to satellite communication to bar codes – any area, in short, where data has to be conveyed rapidly yet accurately.</p><p><strong>C.</strong></p><p>This all seems light years away from the down to-earth uses Shannon originally had for his work, which began when he was a 22-year—old graduate engineering student at the prestigious Massachusetts Institute of Technology in 1939. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fcd3d62a-6bef-48ba-8720-7dbb1b199bae\" data-question=\"38\">set out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> with an apparently simple <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2967344-c81a-4c93-97f7-be27548e8b88\" data-question=\"32\">aim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>: to pin down the precise meaning of the concept of ‘information’. The most basic form of information, Shannon argued, is whether something is true or false – which can be captured in the binary unit, or ‘bit’, of the form 1 or 0. Having identified this fundamental unit, Shannon set about defining otherwise vague ideas about information and how to transmit it from place to place. ln the process he discovered something surprising: it is always possible to guarantee information will gel through random interference – ‘noise’ — intact.</p><p><strong>D.</strong></p><p>Noise usually means unwanted sounds which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ac25474-f977-49b1-8353-eb5c8ec38fe1\" data-question=\"27\">interfere with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> genuine information. information theory generalizes this idea via theorems that capture the effects of noise with mathematical precision. In particular, Shannon showed that noise sets a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51845fc5-1e46-4d06-9bbd-ceff7bc47726\" data-question=\"39\">limit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> on the rate at which information can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b3f2520-2e80-4baf-98ba-79005810789a\" data-question=\"27\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e642af4-4e67-4d96-a65b-18bfe356b868\" data-question=\"39\">pass along<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> communication channels while remaining error-free. This rate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18b1d470-3e9e-4769-b8ac-f52d9f1a9e97\" data-question=\"39\">depends on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> the relative strengths of the signal and noise travelling down the communication channel, and on its capacity (its’ bandwidth’). The resulting limit, given in units of bits per second, is the absolute maximum rate of error-free communication given signal strength and noise level. The trick, Shannon showed, is to find ways of packaging up – ‘coding’ – information to cope with the ravages of noise, while staying within the information carrying capacity ‘bandwidth’ – of the communication system being used.</p><p><strong>E. </strong></p><p>Over the years scientists have devised many such coding methods, and they have proved crucial in many technological feats. The Voyager spacecraft transmitted data using codes which added one extra bit for every single bit of information; the result was an error rate of just one bit in 10,000 — and stunningly clear pictures of the planets. Other codes have become parts of everyday life – such as the Universal Product Code, or bar code, which uses a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f06f3b53-215d-4175-a0e4-08bcdc7d6a27\" data-question=\"30\">simple error-detecting system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that ensures supermarket check-out lasers can read the price even on. say, a crumpled bag of crisps. As recently as 1993, engineers made a major breakthrough by discovering so-called turbo codes – <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f3bc3268-d3f4-49fb-b008-e8fa195922a0\" data-question=\"40\">which come very close to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> Shannon’s ultimate limit for the maximum rate that data can be transmitted reliably, and now play a key role in the mobile videophone revolution.</p><p><strong>F.</strong></p><p>Shannon also laid the foundations of more efficient ways of storing information, by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26dfb0f9-6e09-4e14-8354-8fded67092d5\" data-question=\"28\">stripping out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e53becf-fb17-47c3-b533-350856d5cf83\" data-question=\"28\">superfluous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> (‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e53becf-fb17-47c3-b533-350856d5cf83\" data-question=\"28\">redundant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>’) bits from data which contributed little real information. As mobile phone text messages like ‘l CN C U’ show, it is often possible to leave out a lot of data without losing much meaning, As with error correction, however, there’s a limit beyond which messages become too ambiguous. Shannon showed how to calculate this limit, opening the way to the design of compression methods that cram maximum information into the minimum space.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage has six paragraphs, A-F.</p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-F</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28356\" id=\"question-wrapper-28356\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of the factors <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ac25474-f977-49b1-8353-eb5c8ec38fe1\" data-question=\"27\">affecting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b3f2520-2e80-4baf-98ba-79005810789a\" data-question=\"27\">transmission<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of information </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28357\" id=\"question-wrapper-28357\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an example of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e53becf-fb17-47c3-b533-350856d5cf83\" data-question=\"28\">unnecessary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> information can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26dfb0f9-6e09-4e14-8354-8fded67092d5\" data-question=\"28\">be omitted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28358\" id=\"question-wrapper-28358\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to Shannon’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6c88c3c-f4a7-4512-87e0-7ed74afe25d3\" data-question=\"29\">attitude<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to fame </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28359\" id=\"question-wrapper-28359\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> details of a machine capable of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f06f3b53-215d-4175-a0e4-08bcdc7d6a27\" data-question=\"30\">interpreting incomplete information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28360\" id=\"question-wrapper-28360\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a detailed account of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"164143ed-1406-4e01-a9b5-b105e1e2bda8\" data-question=\"31\">an incident<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> involving information theory </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28361\" id=\"question-wrapper-28361\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to what Shannon initially <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2967344-c81a-4c93-97f7-be27548e8b88\" data-question=\"32\">intended<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to achieve in his research </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>The Voyager 1 Space Probe</strong></p><p>• The probe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd22861e-1fe7-49c4-92c8-002fd98f0d9b\" data-question=\"33\">transmitted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> pictures of both 33 ______ and ______, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06a7c67b-3136-43ef-b0d3-5af96769f98c\" data-question=\"34\">then left<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the 34 ______. </p><p>• The freezing temperatures were found to have a negative effect on parts of the space probe. </p><p>• Scientists feared that both the 35 ______ and ______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b556a655-cc72-407d-b3fa-c4c4ef46d1f0\" data-question=\"35\">were about to stop working<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. </p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e24e69f-be67-493a-b830-9ca6798c3188\" data-question=\"36\">The only hope<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> was to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"191f6232-2fd7-44a4-b5ef-9d7cf9897841\" data-question=\"36\">tell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> the probe to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1eef5aa-0b63-4998-aca5-c91d30aaaba6\" data-question=\"36\">replace them with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> 36 ______ - but distance made communication with the probe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f182424c-687d-4995-8790-938adc72606d\" data-question=\"36\">difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </p><p>• A 37 ______ was used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4233dfb-f630-483f-861a-811b33c12ac8\" data-question=\"37\">transmit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> the message at the speed of light.</p><p>• The message was picked up by the probe and the switchover took place.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28362\" id=\"question-wrapper-28362\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">JUPITER + SATURN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28363\" id=\"question-wrapper-28363\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOLAR SYSTEM</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28364\" id=\"question-wrapper-28364\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CIRCUITS + SENSORS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28365\" id=\"question-wrapper-28365\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPARES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28366\" id=\"question-wrapper-28366\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RADIO DISH</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage?</p><p>In following statements below, choose</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN </strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28367\" id=\"question-wrapper-28367\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The concept of describing something as true or false was the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fcd3d62a-6bef-48ba-8720-7dbb1b199bae\" data-question=\"38\">starting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> point for Shannon in his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e4bd86f-5096-4b9f-925f-2e4f16545140\" data-question=\"38\">attempts to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> send messages over distances. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28368\" id=\"question-wrapper-28368\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The amount of information that can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e642af4-4e67-4d96-a65b-18bfe356b868\" data-question=\"39\">sent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51845fc5-1e46-4d06-9bbd-ceff7bc47726\" data-question=\"39\">given<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> time period is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18b1d470-3e9e-4769-b8ac-f52d9f1a9e97\" data-question=\"39\">determined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> with reference to the signal strength and noise level. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28369\" id=\"question-wrapper-28369\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Products have now been developed which can <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f3bc3268-d3f4-49fb-b008-e8fa195922a0\" data-question=\"40\">convey more information than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> Shannon had anticipated as possible. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"164143ed-1406-4e01-a9b5-b105e1e2bda8","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"an incident","passagePhrase":"an event took place"},{"uid":"cd22861e-1fe7-49c4-92c8-002fd98f0d9b","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"transmitted","passagePhrase":"sent back"},{"uid":"328ce0ed-e558-4d55-9688-9654b3c5f1c3","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"images"},{"uid":"06a7c67b-3136-43ef-b0d3-5af96769f98c","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"then left","passagePhrase":"soared out of"},{"uid":"b556a655-cc72-407d-b3fa-c4c4ef46d1f0","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"were about to stop working","passagePhrase":"were on the brink of failing"},{"uid":"1e24e69f-be67-493a-b830-9ca6798c3188","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"The only hope","passagePhrase":"The solution"},{"uid":"191f6232-2fd7-44a4-b5ef-9d7cf9897841","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"tell","passagePhrase":"instruct"},{"uid":"a1eef5aa-0b63-4998-aca5-c91d30aaaba6","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"replace them with","passagePhrase":"change the failing parts"},{"uid":"f182424c-687d-4995-8790-938adc72606d","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"difficult","passagePhrase":"not an easy task"},{"uid":"b4233dfb-f630-483f-861a-811b33c12ac8","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"transmit","passagePhrase":"sent out"},{"uid":"b6c88c3c-f4a7-4512-87e0-7ed74afe25d3","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"attitude","passagePhrase":"shunned"},{"uid":"fcd3d62a-6bef-48ba-8720-7dbb1b199bae","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"starting","passagePhrase":"set out"},{"uid":"d2967344-c81a-4c93-97f7-be27548e8b88","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"intended","passagePhrase":"aim"},{"uid":"3ac25474-f977-49b1-8353-eb5c8ec38fe1","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"affecting","passagePhrase":"interfere with"},{"uid":"51845fc5-1e46-4d06-9bbd-ceff7bc47726","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"given","passagePhrase":"limit"},{"uid":"0b3f2520-2e80-4baf-98ba-79005810789a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"transmission","passagePhrase":"pass along"},{"uid":"3e642af4-4e67-4d96-a65b-18bfe356b868","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"sent","passagePhrase":"pass along"},{"uid":"18b1d470-3e9e-4769-b8ac-f52d9f1a9e97","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"determined","passagePhrase":"depends on"},{"uid":"f06f3b53-215d-4175-a0e4-08bcdc7d6a27","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"interpreting incomplete information","passagePhrase":"simple error-detecting system"},{"uid":"26dfb0f9-6e09-4e14-8354-8fded67092d5","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"be omitted","passagePhrase":"stripping out"},{"uid":"3e53becf-fb17-47c3-b533-350856d5cf83","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"unnecessary","passagePhrase":"superfluous ... redundant"},{"uid":"5e4bd86f-5096-4b9f-925f-2e4f16545140","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"attempts to","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_184":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The Life &amp; Work of Marie Curie</strong></p><p>Marie Curie is probably the most famous woman scientist who has ever lived. Born Maria Sklodowska in Poland in 1867, she is famous for her work on radioactivity, and was twice a winner of the Nobel A Prize. With her husband, Pierre Curie. and Henri Raeqiierel, she was awarded the 1903 Nobel Prize for Physics, and was then <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2e5df02f-d473-46df-8662-4e1a25ea12a7\" data-question=\"1\">sole<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> winner of the 1911 Nobel Prize for Chemistry. She was the first woman to win a Nobel Prize.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59a71ffb-5577-4724-bead-b179f7e4b53d\" data-question=\"2\">From childhood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, Marie was remarkable for her prodigious memory, and at the age of 16 won a gold medal on completion of her secondary education. Because her father lost his savings through bad investment, she then had to take work as a teacher. From her earnings, she was able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e9bb7d1-dbc7-48c7-83be-94f46e033313\" data-question=\"3\">finance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> her sister Bronia’s medical studies in Paris, on the understanding that Bronia would, in turn, later help her to get an education.</p><p>ln 1891 this promise was fulfilled and Marie went to Paris and began to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c39a6297-a60b-40a7-a4a0-890642adb860\" data-question=\"3\">study at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the Sorbonne (the University of Paris). She often worked far into the night and lived on little more than bread and butter and tea. She came first in the examination in the physical sciences in 1893, and in 1894 was placed second in the examination in mathematical sciences It was not until the spring of that year that she was introduced to Pierre Curie.</p><p>Their marriage in 1895 marked the start of a partnership that was soon to achieve results of world significance. Following Henri BecquereI‘s discovery in 1896 of a new phenomenon, which Marie later called ‘radioactivity’, Marie Curie decided to find out if the radioactivity discovered in uranium was to be found in other elements. She discovered that this was true for thorium.</p><p>Tuming her attention to minerals, she found her interest drawn to pitchblende, a mineral whose radioactivity, superior to that of pure uranium, could be explained only by the presence in the ore of small quantities of an unknown substance of very high activity. Pierre Curie joined her in the work that she had undertaken to resolve this problem. and that led to the discovery of the new elements, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b76b9f3c-70ca-4853-bc1c-aad167153c60\" data-question=\"8\">polonium and radium<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. While Pierre Curie devoted himself chiefly to the physical study of the new radiations, Marie Curie struggled to obtain pure radium in the metallic state. This was achieved with the help of the chemist André-Louis Debierne, one of Pierre Curie’s pupils. Based on the results of this research. Marie Curie received her Doctorate of Science, and in 1903 Marie and Pierre shared with Becquerel the Nobel Prize for Physics for the discovery of radioactivity.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b8fd870b-cbc3-4eb6-af4a-a3d0e67bfeba\" data-question=\"4\">The births of Marie’s two daughters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, Irene and Eve, in 1897 and 1904 <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a8bb0872-5099-4be9-968c-953e4123f234\" data-question=\"4\">failed to interrupt her <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3f36db51-8b68-4bd1-b6db-ce37c27a76d3\" data-question=\"4\">scientific work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. She was appointed lecturer in physics at the Ecole Nor-male Supérieure for girls in Sevres, France (1900), and introduced a method of teaching based on experimental demonstrations. In December 1904 she was appointed chief assistant in the laboratory directed by Pierre Curie.</p><p>The sudden death of her husband in 1906 was a bitter blow to Marie Curie. but was also a turning point in her career: henceforth she was to devote all her energy to completing alone the scientific work that they had undertaken. On May 19, 1906, she <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71c96e7f-03c3-438d-9a74-b3c197c708ec\" data-question=\"5\">was appointed to the professorship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> that had been left vacant on her husband’s death, becoming the first woman to teach at the Sorbonne. In 1911 she <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ab9d77f-a3b3-465f-8ab8-6644a8cf56ec\" data-question=\"9\">was awarded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> the Nobel Prize for Chemistry for the isolation of a pure form of radium.</p><p>During World War I, Marie Curie, with the help of her daughter Irene, devoted herself to the development of the use of X—radiography, including the mobile units which came to be known as ‘little Curies’, used for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"524b8027-97c2-4cd2-8fed-31673927d088\" data-question=\"10\">treatment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> of wounded soldiers. ln 1918 the Radium Institute, whose staff Irene had joined, began to operate in earnest, and became a centre for nuclear physics and chemistry. Marie Curie, now at the highest point of her fame and, from 1922, a member of the Academy of Medicine, researched the chemistry of radioactive substances and their medical applications</p><p>ln 1921, accompanied by her two daughters, Marie Curie made a triumphant journey to the United States to raise funds for research on radium. Women there presented her with a gram of radium for her campaign. Marie also gave lectures in Belgium. Brazil, Spain and Czechoslovakia and, in addition, had the satisfaction of seeing the development of the Curie Foundation in Paris. and the inauguration in 1932 in Warsaw of the Radium Institute, where her sister Bronia became the director.</p><p>One of Marie Curie’s outstanding achievements was to have understood the need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4317a6f-30b7-4ac9-bd53-1c1d2dcf6ea4\" data-question=\"11\">accumulate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> intense radioactive sources. not only to treat illness but also to maintain an abundant supply for research. The existence in Paris at the Radium Institute of a stock of 1.5 grams of radium <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e98e0c8d-2a3d-4eab-9195-975c24c0ad06\" data-question=\"12\">made a decisive contribution to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> the success of the experiments undertaken <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15d8de36-1358-447d-8bf5-f0b01f857242\" data-question=\"12\">in the years around 1930<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. This work prepared the way for the discovery of the neutron by Sir James Chadwick and, above all, for the discovery in 1934 by Irene and Frédéric Joliot- Curie of artificial radioactivity. A few months after this discovery, Marie Curie <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d13fcf70-d79f-41e4-8860-1c2db32681e3\" data-question=\"13\">died as a result of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> leukaemia caused by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c9a590d-7aba-486c-a107-757a4b6a61cc\" data-question=\"13\">exposure to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> radiation. She had often carried test tubes containing radioactive isotopes in her pocket, remarking on the pretty blue-green light they gave off.</p><p>Her contribution to physics had been immense, not only in her own work. the importance of which had been demonstrated by her two Nobel Prizes, but because of her influence on subsequent generations of nuclear physicists and chemists.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage?</p><p>In following statements below, choose</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN </strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28371\" id=\"question-wrapper-28371\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Marie Curie’s husband was a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2e5df02f-d473-46df-8662-4e1a25ea12a7\" data-question=\"1\">joint<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> winner of both Marie’s Nobel Prizes. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28372\" id=\"question-wrapper-28372\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Marie became interested in science <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59a71ffb-5577-4724-bead-b179f7e4b53d\" data-question=\"2\">when she was a child<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28373\" id=\"question-wrapper-28373\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Marie was able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c39a6297-a60b-40a7-a4a0-890642adb860\" data-question=\"3\">attend<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the Sorbonne because of her sister’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e9bb7d1-dbc7-48c7-83be-94f46e033313\" data-question=\"3\">financial contribution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28374\" id=\"question-wrapper-28374\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a8bb0872-5099-4be9-968c-953e4123f234\" data-question=\"4\">Marie stopped doing research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> for several years <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b8fd870b-cbc3-4eb6-af4a-a3d0e67bfeba\" data-question=\"4\">when her children were born<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28375\" id=\"question-wrapper-28375\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Marie <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71c96e7f-03c3-438d-9a74-b3c197c708ec\" data-question=\"5\">took over the teaching position<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> her husband had held. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28376\" id=\"question-wrapper-28376\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Marie’s sister Bronia studied the medical uses of radioactivity. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Choose <strong>ONE WORD</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>Marie Curie’s research on radioactivity</strong></p><p>• When uranium was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"697d9b07-840b-4d51-8a75-506d7ab60709\" data-question=\"7\">discovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> to be radioactive, Marie Curie <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"697d9b07-840b-4d51-8a75-506d7ab60709\" data-question=\"7\">found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> that the element called 7 _____ had the same property. </p><p>• Marie and Pierre Curie’s research into the radioactivity of the mineral known as 8 _____ led to the discovery of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b76b9f3c-70ca-4853-bc1c-aad167153c60\" data-question=\"8\">two new elements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. </p><p>• In 1911, Marie Curie <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ab9d77f-a3b3-465f-8ab8-6644a8cf56ec\" data-question=\"9\">received recognition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> for her work on the element 9 _____. </p><p>• Marie and Irene Curie developed X-radiography which was used as a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"524b8027-97c2-4cd2-8fed-31673927d088\" data-question=\"10\">medical technique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> for 10 _____. </p><p>• Marie Curie saw the importance of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4317a6f-30b7-4ac9-bd53-1c1d2dcf6ea4\" data-question=\"11\">collecting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> radioactive material both for research and for cases of 11 _____. </p><p>• The radioactive material stocked in Paris <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e98e0c8d-2a3d-4eab-9195-975c24c0ad06\" data-question=\"12\">contributed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> the discoveries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15d8de36-1358-447d-8bf5-f0b01f857242\" data-question=\"12\">in the 1930s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> of the 12 _____. and of what was known as artificial radioactivity. </p><p>• During her research, Marie Curie <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c9a590d-7aba-486c-a107-757a4b6a61cc\" data-question=\"13\">was exposed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> radiation and as a result she <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d13fcf70-d79f-41e4-8860-1c2db32681e3\" data-question=\"13\">suffered from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> 13 _____.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28377\" id=\"question-wrapper-28377\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">THORIUM</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28378\" id=\"question-wrapper-28378\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PITCHBLENDE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28379\" id=\"question-wrapper-28379\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RADIUM</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28380\" id=\"question-wrapper-28380\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOLDIERS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28381\" id=\"question-wrapper-28381\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ILLNESS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28382\" id=\"question-wrapper-28382\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NEUTRON</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28383\" id=\"question-wrapper-28383\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LEUKAEMIA/LEUKEMIA</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"59a71ffb-5577-4724-bead-b179f7e4b53d","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"when she was a child","passagePhrase":"From childhood"},{"uid":"0e9bb7d1-dbc7-48c7-83be-94f46e033313","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"financial contribution","passagePhrase":"finance"},{"uid":"c39a6297-a60b-40a7-a4a0-890642adb860","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"attend","passagePhrase":"study at"},{"uid":"b76b9f3c-70ca-4853-bc1c-aad167153c60","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"two new elements","passagePhrase":"polonium and radium"},{"uid":"b8fd870b-cbc3-4eb6-af4a-a3d0e67bfeba","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"when her children were born","passagePhrase":"The births of Marie’s two daughters"},{"uid":"3f36db51-8b68-4bd1-b6db-ce37c27a76d3","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"scientific work"},{"uid":"71c96e7f-03c3-438d-9a74-b3c197c708ec","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"took over the teaching position","passagePhrase":"was appointed to the professorship"},{"uid":"8ab9d77f-a3b3-465f-8ab8-6644a8cf56ec","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"received recognition","passagePhrase":"was awarded"},{"uid":"524b8027-97c2-4cd2-8fed-31673927d088","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"medical technique","passagePhrase":"treatment"},{"uid":"e4317a6f-30b7-4ac9-bd53-1c1d2dcf6ea4","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"collecting","passagePhrase":"accumulate"},{"uid":"e98e0c8d-2a3d-4eab-9195-975c24c0ad06","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"contributed to","passagePhrase":"made a decisive contribution to"},{"uid":"15d8de36-1358-447d-8bf5-f0b01f857242","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"in the 1930s","passagePhrase":"in the years around 1930"},{"uid":"d13fcf70-d79f-41e4-8860-1c2db32681e3","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"suffered from","passagePhrase":"died as a result of"},{"uid":"8c9a590d-7aba-486c-a107-757a4b6a61cc","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"was exposed to","passagePhrase":"exposure to"},{"uid":"697d9b07-840b-4d51-8a75-506d7ab60709","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"discovered ... found","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_185":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Young Children’s Sense of Identity</strong></p><p><strong>A. </strong></p><p>A sense of ‘self’ develops in young children by degrees. The process can usefully be thought of in terms of the gradual emergence of two somewhat separate features: the self as a subject, and the self as an object. William James introduced the distinction in 1892, and contemporaries of his, such as Charles Cooley, added to the developing debate. Ever since then psychologists have continued building on the theory.</p><p><strong>B </strong></p><p>According to James, a child’s first step on the road to self-understanding can be seen as the recognition that he or she exists. This is an aspect of the self that he labeled ‘self-as-subject’, and he gave it various elements. These included an awareness of one’s own agency (i.e. one’s power to act) and an awareness of one’s distinctiveness from other people. These features gradually emerge as infants explore their world and interact with caregivers. Cooley (1902) suggested that a sense of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa15a6b0-7dbe-4851-b12e-665268af8085\" data-question=\"21\">self-as-subject<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> was primarily concerned with being able to exercise power. He proposed that the earliest examples of this are an infants attempts to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"05115763-18a4-4f6b-85b9-a629aa65aa69\" data-question=\"21\">control<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> physical objects, such as toys or his or her own limbs. This is followed by attempts to affect the behavior of other people. For example, infants learn that when they cry or smile someone responds to them.</p><p><strong>C </strong></p><p>Another powerful source of information for infants about the effects they can have on the world around them is provided when others <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5495f11b-5879-43e1-8b7d-b22d445af235\" data-question=\"15\">mimic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> them. Many parents spend a lot of time, particularly in the early months, copying their infant’s vocalizations and expressions in addition, young children enjoy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f032e01-2df9-4c48-b074-005940dc90eb\" data-question=\"24\">looking in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> mirrors, where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ce31501-e581-418c-b5d8-e83447492a94\" data-question=\"24\">the movements they can see are dependent upon their own movements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.This is not to say that infants recognize the reflection as their own image (a later development). However, Lewis and Brooks-Gunn (1979) suggest that infants’ developing understanding that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a82b687-6ea6-4e9c-a010-cd7fc8243034\" data-question=\"23\">movements <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06444d4a-6e16-44f9-b4c8-08d2cb939c28\" data-question=\"23\">they see in the mirror<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> are contingent ­on their own, leads to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d16928a-44a1-4542-b0b9-e2f6aca0b5f5\" data-question=\"15\">a growing awareness that they are distinct from other people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. This is because they, and only they can change the reflection in the mirror.</p><p><strong>D</strong> </p><p>This understanding that children gain of themselves as active agents continue to develop in their attempts to co-operate with others in play. Drum (1988) points out that it is in such day-to-day relationships and interactions that the child’s understanding of his· or herself emerges. Empirical <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0493f104-eb27-4555-88f4-05c9a3c863b4\" data-question=\"17\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ac5f180-fb66-4559-99a8-fabb9918b052\" data-question=\"25\">investigations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> the self-as- subject in young children are, however, rather scarce <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"857c45c6-f46e-46b5-aa83-e20dd6f8ab57\" data-question=\"17\">because of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7adf0a70-6181-4346-b36c-eca6ba0f281b\" data-question=\"17\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"429b8448-2cd0-4fa8-9f94-eded43c0b5d2\" data-question=\"25\">difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of communication: even if young infants can reflect on their experience, they certainly cannot express this aspect of the self directly.</p><p><strong>E </strong></p><p>Once Children have acquired a certain level of self-awareness, they begin to place themselves in a whole series of categories, which together play such an important part in defining them uniquely as ‘themselves’. This second step in the development of a full sense of self is what lames called the ‘self-as-object’. This has been seen by many to be the aspect of the self which is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f1114c09-9e12-4d0f-84c8-31c7c5a54330\" data-question=\"19\">most influenced by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13cd41cc-5e9b-4a1c-ac8a-2769b5ded877\" data-question=\"19\">social elements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, since it is made up of social roles (such as student, brother; colleague) and characteristics which derive their meaning from comparison or interaction with other people (such as trustworthiness, shyness, sporting ability).</p><p><strong>F </strong></p><p>Cooley and other researchers suggested a close connection between a person’s own understanding of their identity and other people’s understanding of it. Cooley believed that people build up their sense of identity from the reactions of others to them, and from the view, they believe others have of them He called the self- as-object the ’looking-glass self’, since people come to see themselves as they are reflected in others. Mead (1934) went even further, and saw the self and the social world as inextricably bound together. The self is essentially a social structure, and ­it arises in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6fc71d63-54af-4ab6-9261-2ee2b4727fdf\" data-question=\"20\">social experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2249923a-4a47-4375-a387-2208451791eb\" data-question=\"20\">It is impossible to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> conceive of a self-arising outside of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6fc71d63-54af-4ab6-9261-2ee2b4727fdf\" data-question=\"20\">social experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.’</p><p><strong>G </strong></p><p>Lewis and Brooks-Gunn argued that an important developmental milestone is reached when children become able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c590d691-1b6d-4295-a90f-8ad1af38740e\" data-question=\"16\">recognize<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> themselves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59b92109-fee9-44d4-9d8c-912c71d7fd1b\" data-question=\"16\">visually<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> without the support of seeing contingent movement. This recognition occurs around their second birthday. In one <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a534ae7b-9980-4fde-a18d-5c9f77c41742\" data-question=\"14\">experiment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, Lewis and Brooks-Gunn (1979) dabbed some red powder on the noses of children who were playing in front of a mirror, and then observed how often they touched their noses. The psychologists reasoned that if the children knew what they usually looked like, they would be surprised by the unusual red mark and would start touching it. On the other hand, they found that children of 15 to 18 months are generally not able to recognize themselves unless other cues such as movement are present.</p><p><strong>H </strong></p><p>Finally perhaps the most graphic expressions of self-awareness, in general, can be seen in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebe0456e-b674-4078-9e25-117451ea5691\" data-question=\"22\">the displays of rage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> which are most common from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3652711-5dce-46fd-94c0-1c80c328acda\" data-question=\"22\">18 months to 3 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of age. In a longitudinal study of groups of three or four children, Bronson (1975) found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebe0456e-b674-4078-9e25-117451ea5691\" data-question=\"22\">the intensity of the frustration and anger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7eb98c20-f00b-4f12-9265-32ccb803fd70\" data-question=\"26\">disagreements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> increased sharply between the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3652711-5dce-46fd-94c0-1c80c328acda\" data-question=\"22\">ages of 1 and 2 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. Often, the children’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7eb98c20-f00b-4f12-9265-32ccb803fd70\" data-question=\"26\">disagreements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> involved a struggle over a toy that none of them had played with before or after the tug-of-war: the children seemed to be disputing ownership rather than wanting to play with it. Although it may be less marked in other societies, the link between the sense of ’self’ and of ‘ownership’ is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"248ab55e-8557-48e3-bf4d-cd6b89d21349\" data-question=\"18\">notable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> feature of childhood in Western societies.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage has eight paragraphs, A-H.</p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-H</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28384\" id=\"question-wrapper-28384\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an account of the method used by researchers in a particular <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a534ae7b-9980-4fde-a18d-5c9f77c41742\" data-question=\"14\">study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28385\" id=\"question-wrapper-28385\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the role of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5495f11b-5879-43e1-8b7d-b22d445af235\" data-question=\"15\">imitation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d16928a-44a1-4542-b0b9-e2f6aca0b5f5\" data-question=\"15\">developing a sense of identity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28386\" id=\"question-wrapper-28386\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the age at which children can usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c590d691-1b6d-4295-a90f-8ad1af38740e\" data-question=\"16\">identify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59b92109-fee9-44d4-9d8c-912c71d7fd1b\" data-question=\"16\">a static image of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> themselves </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28387\" id=\"question-wrapper-28387\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"857c45c6-f46e-46b5-aa83-e20dd6f8ab57\" data-question=\"17\">a reason for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7adf0a70-6181-4346-b36c-eca6ba0f281b\" data-question=\"17\">limitations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of scientific <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0493f104-eb27-4555-88f4-05c9a3c863b4\" data-question=\"17\">research into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> ‘self-as-subject’ </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28388\" id=\"question-wrapper-28388\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to a possible link between culture and a particular <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79837e0c-beea-47d4-8a1d-dd2524f8a59f\" data-question=\"18\">form of behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28389\" id=\"question-wrapper-28389\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of the wide range of features that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f1114c09-9e12-4d0f-84c8-31c7c5a54330\" data-question=\"19\">contribute to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> the sense of ‘self-as-object’ </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following findings and the list of researchers below.</p><p>Match each finding with the correct researcher or researchers, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-E</p><p><strong>List of Findings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>A</strong> James</li><li><strong>B</strong> Cooley</li><li><strong>C</strong> Lewis and Brooks-Gunn</li><li><strong>D</strong> Mead</li><li><strong>E</strong> Bronson</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28390\" id=\"question-wrapper-28390\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A sense of identity <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2249923a-4a47-4375-a387-2208451791eb\" data-question=\"20\">can never be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> formed without <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6fc71d63-54af-4ab6-9261-2ee2b4727fdf\" data-question=\"20\">relationships with other people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28391\" id=\"question-wrapper-28391\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A child’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa15a6b0-7dbe-4851-b12e-665268af8085\" data-question=\"21\">awareness of self<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> is related to a sense of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"05115763-18a4-4f6b-85b9-a629aa65aa69\" data-question=\"21\">mastery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> over things and people. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28392\" id=\"question-wrapper-28392\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> At a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3652711-5dce-46fd-94c0-1c80c328acda\" data-question=\"22\">certain age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, children’s sense of identity leads to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebe0456e-b674-4078-9e25-117451ea5691\" data-question=\"22\">aggressive behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28393\" id=\"question-wrapper-28393\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06444d4a-6e16-44f9-b4c8-08d2cb939c28\" data-question=\"23\">Observing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a82b687-6ea6-4e9c-a010-cd7fc8243034\" data-question=\"23\">their own reflection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15e028f4-2c4a-41fa-ade8-daae2c9b9cbd\" data-question=\"23\">contributes to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> children’s self awareness. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below.</p><p>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>How children acquire a sense of identity</strong></p><p>First, children come to realise that they can have an effect on the world around them, for example by handling objects, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ce31501-e581-418c-b5d8-e83447492a94\" data-question=\"24\">causing the image to move<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> when they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f032e01-2df9-4c48-b074-005940dc90eb\" data-question=\"24\">face<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> a <strong>24</strong> ________. This aspect of self-awareness is difficult to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ac5f180-fb66-4559-99a8-fabb9918b052\" data-question=\"25\">research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> directly, because of <strong>25</strong> ________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"429b8448-2cd0-4fa8-9f94-eded43c0b5d2\" data-question=\"25\">problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</p><p>Secondly, children start to become aware of how they are viewed by others. One important stage in this process is the visual recognition of themselves which usually occurs when they reach the age of two. In Western societies at least, the development of self awareness is often linked to a sense of <strong>26</strong> ________, and can lead to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7eb98c20-f00b-4f12-9265-32ccb803fd70\" data-question=\"26\">disputes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28394\" id=\"question-wrapper-28394\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MIRROR</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28395\" id=\"question-wrapper-28395\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMMUNICATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28396\" id=\"question-wrapper-28396\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OWNERSHIP</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"aa15a6b0-7dbe-4851-b12e-665268af8085","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"awareness of self","passagePhrase":"self-as-subject"},{"uid":"05115763-18a4-4f6b-85b9-a629aa65aa69","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"mastery","passagePhrase":"control"},{"uid":"5495f11b-5879-43e1-8b7d-b22d445af235","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"imitation","passagePhrase":"mimic"},{"uid":"2f032e01-2df9-4c48-b074-005940dc90eb","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"face","passagePhrase":"looking in"},{"uid":"7ce31501-e581-418c-b5d8-e83447492a94","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"causing the image to move","passagePhrase":"the movements they can see are dependent upon their own movements"},{"uid":"3a82b687-6ea6-4e9c-a010-cd7fc8243034","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"their own reflection","passagePhrase":"movements they see in the mirror"},{"uid":"06444d4a-6e16-44f9-b4c8-08d2cb939c28","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Observing","passagePhrase":"they see in the mirror"},{"uid":"9d16928a-44a1-4542-b0b9-e2f6aca0b5f5","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"developing a sense of identity","passagePhrase":"a growing awareness that they are distinct from other people"},{"uid":"0493f104-eb27-4555-88f4-05c9a3c863b4","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"research into","passagePhrase":"investigations of"},{"uid":"3ac5f180-fb66-4559-99a8-fabb9918b052","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"research","passagePhrase":"investigations"},{"uid":"857c45c6-f46e-46b5-aa83-e20dd6f8ab57","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"a reason for","passagePhrase":"because of"},{"uid":"7adf0a70-6181-4346-b36c-eca6ba0f281b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"limitations","passagePhrase":"difficulties"},{"uid":"429b8448-2cd0-4fa8-9f94-eded43c0b5d2","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"problems","passagePhrase":"difficulties"},{"uid":"f1114c09-9e12-4d0f-84c8-31c7c5a54330","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"contribute to","passagePhrase":"most influenced by"},{"uid":"13cd41cc-5e9b-4a1c-ac8a-2769b5ded877","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"social elements"},{"uid":"6fc71d63-54af-4ab6-9261-2ee2b4727fdf","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"relationships with other people","passagePhrase":"social experience ... social experience"},{"uid":"2249923a-4a47-4375-a387-2208451791eb","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"can never be","passagePhrase":"It is impossible to"},{"uid":"c590d691-1b6d-4295-a90f-8ad1af38740e","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"identify","passagePhrase":"recognize"},{"uid":"59b92109-fee9-44d4-9d8c-912c71d7fd1b","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"a static image of","passagePhrase":"visually"},{"uid":"a534ae7b-9980-4fde-a18d-5c9f77c41742","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"study","passagePhrase":"experiment"},{"uid":"ebe0456e-b674-4078-9e25-117451ea5691","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"aggressive behaviour","passagePhrase":"the displays of rage ... the intensity of the frustration and anger"},{"uid":"f3652711-5dce-46fd-94c0-1c80c328acda","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"certain age","passagePhrase":"18 months to 3 years ... ages of 1 and 2 years"},{"uid":"7eb98c20-f00b-4f12-9265-32ccb803fd70","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"disputes","passagePhrase":"disagreements ... disagreements"},{"uid":"248ab55e-8557-48e3-bf4d-cd6b89d21349","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"notable"},{"uid":"79837e0c-beea-47d4-8a1d-dd2524f8a59f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"form of behaviour","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"15e028f4-2c4a-41fa-ade8-daae2c9b9cbd","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"contributes to","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_186":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The Development of Museums.</strong></p><p><strong>A </strong></p><p>The conviction that historical relics provide infallible testimony about the past is rooted in the nineteenth and early twentieth centuries, when science was regarded as objective and value free. As one writer observes: ‘Although it is now evident that artifacts are as easily altered as chronicles, public faith in their veracity endures: a tangible relic seems ipso facto real! Such conviction was, until recently, reflected in museum displays. Museums used to look — and some still do — much like storage rooms of objects packed together in showcases: good for scholars who wanted to study the subtle differences in design, but not for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e0d726c-d707-4c3d-96a7-654f3060e281\" data-question=\"31\">the ordinary visitor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. to whom lt all looked alike. Similarly, the information accompanying the objects often made little sense to the lay visitor. The content and format of explanations dated back to a time when the museum was the exclusive domain of the scientific researcher.</p><p><strong>B </strong></p><p>Recently, however, attitudes towards history and the way lt should be presented have altered. The key word in heritage display is now ‘experience the more exciting the better and, if possible, involving all the senses. Good examples of this approach ln the UK are the Jorvik Centre in York; the National Museum of Photography, Elm ­­and Television in Bradford; and the imperial War Museum in London. In the US the trend emerged much earlier. Williamsburg has been a prototype for many heritage developments in other parts of the world. No one can predict where the process will end. On so-called heritage sites, the re-enactment of historical events is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c3ac7f0-8443-446f-b1c5-ecdf726b79fc\" data-question=\"32\">increasingly popular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, and computers will soon provide virtual reality experiences, which will present visitors with a vivid image of the period of their choice, in which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc108703-fe12-42a8-ba39-484ae667673f\" data-question=\"32\">they themselves can act as if part of the historical environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccd59337-ca22-4b92-a448-ffc67729974e\" data-question=\"27\">Such developments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> have been criticised as an intolerable vulgarisation, but the success of many historical theme parks and similar locations suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21f53851-8cdc-4e42-9226-1ed07221b451\" data-question=\"27\">the majority of the public does not share this opinion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</p><p><strong>C </strong></p><p>In a related development, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"015c7655-d144-4f26-ac3c-bbd48ac3e30f\" data-question=\"28\">sharp distinction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> between museum and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3a73d87-b931-4be4-a326-6ef904737437\" data-question=\"28\">heritage sites<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> on the one hand, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3a73d87-b931-4be4-a326-6ef904737437\" data-question=\"28\">theme parks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> on the other, is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a438f56-a966-47c6-867a-aac41fcd49a6\" data-question=\"33\">gradually evaporating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. They already borrow ideas and concepts from one another. For example, museums have adopted storylines for exhibitions, sites have accepted ‘theming’ as a relevant tool, and theme parks are moving towards more authenticity and research-based presentations in zoos, animals are no longer kept in cages, but in great spaces, either ln the open air or in enormous greenhouses, such as the jungle and desert environments .In Burgers’ Zoo In Holland. This particular trend is regarded as one of the major developments in the presentation of natural history in the twentieth century.</p><p><strong>D </strong></p><p>Theme parks are undergoing other changes, too, as they try to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"61e97859-be4d-479d-a9f8-3e5b6fd6642d\" data-question=\"37\">present<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd2c793c-175f-44b1-8885-ec2f3babc982\" data-question=\"37\">serious social and cultural issues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, and move away from fantasy. This development is a response to market forces and, although museums and heritage sites have a special. rather distinct, role to fullfil, they are also operating in a very competitive environment, where visitors make choices on how and where to spend their free time. Heritage and museum experts do not have to invent stories and recreate historical environments to attract their visitors: their assets are already in place. However, exhibits must be both based on artefacts and facts as we know them, and attractively presented. Those <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7c6d850b-4e9a-455c-b7d4-9995746ee56f\" data-question=\"29\">who are professionally engaged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> in the art of interpreting history are thus ln a difficult position, as they must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fef9d2fb-d8bc-4ab5-be90-ac10658495cf\" data-question=\"34\">steer a narrow course between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9e809bf-cd7d-4fd3-964e-0fadeec2d046\" data-question=\"34\">demands of ’evidence’ and ‘attractiveness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> especially given the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4104b246-52ef-4d18-aecd-3c9dbf16ef7a\" data-question=\"29\">increasing need in the heritage industry for income generating activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</p><p><strong>E </strong></p><p>It could be claimed that in order to make everything in heritage more `real` <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2456f218-4037-4557-8f51-33e15d042f14\" data-question=\"30\">historical accuracy must be increasingly altered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. For example, Pithecanthropus erectus is depicted in an Indonesian museum with Malay facial features, because this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fbfbcc86-8ca3-4813-8331-382fb9257a47\" data-question=\"30\">corresponds to public perceptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Similarly, in the Museum of Natural History in Washington, Neanderthal man is shown making a dominant gesture to his wife. Such presentations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"636a35e4-ab1c-43e6-a7d2-82f36cbd5281\" data-question=\"35\">tell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> us more about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fbfbcc86-8ca3-4813-8331-382fb9257a47\" data-question=\"30\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56950e65-d497-4bb6-bbdc-f933fbc3e479\" data-question=\"35\">contemporary perceptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> than about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ee8ec63-fe36-4bff-90cc-e5727465b837\" data-question=\"35\">our ancestors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. There is one compensation, however, for the professionals who make these interpretations: If they did not provide the interpretation, visitors would do it for themselves. based on their own ideas. misconceptions and prejudices. And no matter how exciting the result, it would contain a lot more bias than the presentations provided by experts.</p><p><strong>F </strong></p><p>Human bias is inevitable, but another source of bias in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5dcda01b-0af9-4762-aa08-91d37227dc8c\" data-question=\"36\">representation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of history has to do with the transitory nature of the materials themselves. The simple fact is that not everything from history survives the historical process. Castles, palaces and cathedrals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3325e5a3-254b-44f7-b81f-3d94035683ec\" data-question=\"36\">have a longer lifespan<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> than the dwellings of ordinary people. The same applies to the famishing and other contents of the premises. In a town like Leyden in Holland, which in the seventeenth century was occupied by approximately the same number of inhabitants as today, people lived within the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8f76205-ddb8-4d0e-bc95-174da731b6ec\" data-question=\"39\">walled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> town, an area <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"211f45d7-e07a-4250-87d1-4bbefcb1045f\" data-question=\"39\">more than five times smaller than modern<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> Leyden. In most of the houses, several families lived together in circumstances beyond our imagination. Yet In museums, line period rooms give only an image of the lifestyle of the upper class of that era. No wonder that people who stroll around exhibitions are filled with nostalgia; the evidence in museums indicates that life was so much better in the past. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4dcfc8b4-9b65-4319-9f24-de3faf584844\" data-question=\"40\">This notion is induced by the bias<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> in its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5dcda01b-0af9-4762-aa08-91d37227dc8c\" data-question=\"36\">representation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> in museums and heritage centers.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage has six paragraphs, A-F.</p><p>Choose the correct heading for paragraphs B-E from the list of headings below.</p><p>Write the correct number, i-vii</p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>I.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4104b246-52ef-4d18-aecd-3c9dbf16ef7a\" data-question=\"29\">Commercial pressures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7c6d850b-4e9a-455c-b7d4-9995746ee56f\" data-question=\"29\">people in charge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></li><li><strong>II.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21f53851-8cdc-4e42-9226-1ed07221b451\" data-question=\"27\">Mixed views<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccd59337-ca22-4b92-a448-ffc67729974e\" data-question=\"27\">current changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to museums</li><li><strong>III.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2456f218-4037-4557-8f51-33e15d042f14\" data-question=\"30\">Interpreting the facts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fbfbcc86-8ca3-4813-8331-382fb9257a47\" data-question=\"30\">meet visitor expectations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></li><li><strong>IV.</strong> The international dimension</li><li><strong>V.</strong> Collections of factual evidence</li><li><strong>VI.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"015c7655-d144-4f26-ac3c-bbd48ac3e30f\" data-question=\"28\">Fewer differences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3a73d87-b931-4be4-a326-6ef904737437\" data-question=\"28\">public attractions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></li><li><strong>VII.</strong> Current reviews and suggestions</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28397\" id=\"question-wrapper-28397\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28398\" id=\"question-wrapper-28398\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28399\" id=\"question-wrapper-28399\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28400\" id=\"question-wrapper-28400\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose appropriate options <strong>A, B, C</strong> or <strong>D</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28401\" id=\"question-wrapper-28401\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Compared with today’s museums, those of the past </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. did not present history in a detailed way.</li> <li>B. were not primarily intended for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e0d726c-d707-4c3d-96a7-654f3060e281\" data-question=\"31\">the public<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>C. were more clearly organised.</li> <li>D. preserved items with greater care.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28402\" id=\"question-wrapper-28402\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the writer, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c3ac7f0-8443-446f-b1c5-ecdf726b79fc\" data-question=\"32\">current trends<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> in the heritage industry </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. emphasise <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc108703-fe12-42a8-ba39-484ae667673f\" data-question=\"32\">personal involvement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</li> <li>B. have their origins in York and London.</li> <li>C. rely on computer images.</li> <li>D. reflect minority tastes.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28403\" id=\"question-wrapper-28403\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer says that museums, heritage sites and theme parks </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. often work in close partnership.</li> <li>B. try to preserve separate identities.</li> <li>C. have similar exhibits.</li> <li>D. are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a438f56-a966-47c6-867a-aac41fcd49a6\" data-question=\"33\">less easy to distinguish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> than before.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28404\" id=\"question-wrapper-28404\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer says that in preparing exhibits for museums, experts </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. should pursue a single objective</li> <li>B. have to do a certain amount of language translation.</li> <li>C. should be free from commercial constraints.</li> <li>D. have to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fef9d2fb-d8bc-4ab5-be90-ac10658495cf\" data-question=\"34\">balance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9e809bf-cd7d-4fd3-964e-0fadeec2d046\" data-question=\"34\">conflicting priorities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28405\" id=\"question-wrapper-28405\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In paragraph E, the writer suggests that some museum exhibits </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. fail to match visitor expectations.</li> <li>B. are based on the false assumptions of professionals.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"636a35e4-ab1c-43e6-a7d2-82f36cbd5281\" data-question=\"35\">reveal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> more about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56950e65-d497-4bb6-bbdc-f933fbc3e479\" data-question=\"35\">present beliefs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> than about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ee8ec63-fe36-4bff-90cc-e5727465b837\" data-question=\"35\">the past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> <li>D. allow visitors to make more use of their imagination.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28406\" id=\"question-wrapper-28406\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The passage ends by noting that our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5dcda01b-0af9-4762-aa08-91d37227dc8c\" data-question=\"36\">view<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of history is biased because </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. we fail to use our imagination.</li> <li>B. only very <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3325e5a3-254b-44f7-b81f-3d94035683ec\" data-question=\"36\">durable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> objects remain from the past.</li> <li>C. we tend to ignore things that displease us.</li> <li>D. museum exhibits focus too much on the local area.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the Reading Passage?</p><p>In following statements below, choose</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN </strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28407\" id=\"question-wrapper-28407\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Consumers prefer theme parks which <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"61e97859-be4d-479d-a9f8-3e5b6fd6642d\" data-question=\"37\">avoid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd2c793c-175f-44b1-8885-ec2f3babc982\" data-question=\"37\">serious issues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28408\" id=\"question-wrapper-28408\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> More people visit museums than theme parks. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28409\" id=\"question-wrapper-28409\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8f76205-ddb8-4d0e-bc95-174da731b6ec\" data-question=\"39\">The boundaries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of Leyden <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"211f45d7-e07a-4250-87d1-4bbefcb1045f\" data-question=\"39\">have changed little<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> since the seventeenth century. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"28410\" id=\"question-wrapper-28410\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Museums can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4dcfc8b4-9b65-4319-9f24-de3faf584844\" data-question=\"40\">give a false impression of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> how life used to be. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"1e0d726c-d707-4c3d-96a7-654f3060e281","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"the public","passagePhrase":"the ordinary visitor"},{"uid":"6c3ac7f0-8443-446f-b1c5-ecdf726b79fc","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"current trends","passagePhrase":"increasingly popular"},{"uid":"bc108703-fe12-42a8-ba39-484ae667673f","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"personal involvement","passagePhrase":"they themselves can act as if part of the historical environment"},{"uid":"ccd59337-ca22-4b92-a448-ffc67729974e","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"current changes","passagePhrase":"Such developments"},{"uid":"21f53851-8cdc-4e42-9226-1ed07221b451","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Mixed views","passagePhrase":"the majority of the public does not share this opinion"},{"uid":"015c7655-d144-4f26-ac3c-bbd48ac3e30f","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Fewer differences","passagePhrase":"sharp distinction"},{"uid":"f3a73d87-b931-4be4-a326-6ef904737437","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"public attractions","passagePhrase":"heritage sites ... theme parks"},{"uid":"5a438f56-a966-47c6-867a-aac41fcd49a6","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"less easy to distinguish","passagePhrase":"gradually evaporating"},{"uid":"dd2c793c-175f-44b1-8885-ec2f3babc982","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"serious issues","passagePhrase":"serious social and cultural issues"},{"uid":"7c6d850b-4e9a-455c-b7d4-9995746ee56f","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"people in charge","passagePhrase":"who are professionally engaged"},{"uid":"fef9d2fb-d8bc-4ab5-be90-ac10658495cf","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"balance","passagePhrase":"steer a narrow course between"},{"uid":"f9e809bf-cd7d-4fd3-964e-0fadeec2d046","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"conflicting priorities","passagePhrase":"demands of ’evidence’ and ‘attractiveness"},{"uid":"4104b246-52ef-4d18-aecd-3c9dbf16ef7a","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Commercial pressures","passagePhrase":"increasing need in the heritage industry for income generating activities"},{"uid":"2456f218-4037-4557-8f51-33e15d042f14","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Interpreting the facts","passagePhrase":"historical accuracy must be increasingly altered"},{"uid":"fbfbcc86-8ca3-4813-8331-382fb9257a47","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"meet visitor expectations","passagePhrase":"corresponds to public perceptions ... contemporary perceptions of the world"},{"uid":"636a35e4-ab1c-43e6-a7d2-82f36cbd5281","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"reveal","passagePhrase":"tell"},{"uid":"56950e65-d497-4bb6-bbdc-f933fbc3e479","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"present beliefs","passagePhrase":"contemporary perceptions"},{"uid":"9ee8ec63-fe36-4bff-90cc-e5727465b837","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"the past","passagePhrase":"our ancestors"},{"uid":"5dcda01b-0af9-4762-aa08-91d37227dc8c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"view","passagePhrase":"representation ... representation"},{"uid":"3325e5a3-254b-44f7-b81f-3d94035683ec","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"durable","passagePhrase":"have a longer lifespan"},{"uid":"c8f76205-ddb8-4d0e-bc95-174da731b6ec","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"The boundaries","passagePhrase":"walled"},{"uid":"4dcfc8b4-9b65-4319-9f24-de3faf584844","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"give a false impression of","passagePhrase":"This notion is induced by the bias"}]},"reading_u2_187":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong>Stepwells</strong></span></h2><p><span><em></em></span></p><p><span><em>A millennium ago, stepwells were fundamental to life in the driest parts of India. Although many have been neglected, recent restoration has returned them to their former glory. Richard Cox travelled to north-western India to document these spectacular monuments from a bygone era. </em></span></p><p><span>During the sixth and seventh centuries, the inhabitants of the modern-day states of Gujarat and Rajasthan in North-western India developed a method of gaining access to clean, fresh groundwater during the dry season for drinking, bathing, watering animals and irrigation. However, the significance of this invention – the stepwell – goes beyond its utilitarian application.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"afbd4521-43f7-469c-abd5-f6357e989300\" data-question=\"1\">Unique to the region<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, stepwells are often architecturally complex and vary widely in size and shape. During their heyday, they were places of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62ee8fee-01db-4fd1-98a7-89a23694c070\" data-question=\"2\">gathering, of leisure, of relaxation and of worship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> for villagers of all but the lowest castes. Most stepwells are found dotted around the desert areas of Gujarat (where they are called <em>vav</em>) and Rajasthan (where they are known as <em>baori</em>), while a few also survive in Delhi. Some were located in or near villages as public spaces for the community; others were positioned beside roads as resting places for travellers.</span></p><p><span>As their name suggests, stepwells comprise a series of stone steps descending from ground level to the water source (normally an underground aquifer) as it recedes following the rains. When the water level was high, the user needed only to descend a few steps to reach it; when it was low, several levels would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dca55882-00d6-40dd-8af6-16d4a0495e1b\" data-question=\"5\">have to be negotiated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Some wells are vast, open craters with hundreds of steps paving each sloping side, often in tiers. Others are more elaborate, with long stepped passages leading to the water via several storeys. Built from stone and supported by pillars, they also included pavilions that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0df6f364-56cb-4d4f-b880-8ce641a5bf0f\" data-question=\"6\">sheltered visitors from the relentless heat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. But perhaps the most impressive features are the intricate decorative sculptures that embellish many stepwells, showing activities from fighting and dancing to everyday acts such as women combing their hair and churning butter.</span></p><p><span>Down the centuries, thousands of wells were constructed throughout northwestern India, but the majority have now fallen into disuse; many are derelict and dry, as groundwater has been diverted for industrial use and the wells no longer reach the water table. Their condition hasn’t been helped by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da26c058-2690-4f5c-9c10-404605fb9899\" data-question=\"7\">recent dry spells<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>: southern Rajasthan suffered an eight-year drought between 1996 and 2004.</span></p><p><span>However, some important sites in Gujarat have recently undergone major restoration, and the state government announced in June last year that it plans to restore the stepwells throughout the state.</span></p><p><span>In Patan, the state’s ancient capital, the stepwell of <em>Rani Ki Vav</em> (Queen’s Stepwell) is perhaps the finest current example. It was built by Queen Udayamati during the late 11th century, but became silted up following a flood during the 13th century. But the Archaeological Survey of India began restoring it in the 1960s, and today it’s in pristine condition. At 65 metres long, 20 metres wide and 27 metres deep, <em>Rani Ki Vav</em> features 500 distinct sculptures carved into niches throughout the monument, depicting gods such as Vishnu and Parvati in various incarnations. Incredibly, in January 2001, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"218f05f8-b612-471c-9726-af35ee70636f\" data-question=\"9\">this ancient structure survived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> a devastating earthquake that measured 7.6 on the Richter scale.</span></p><p><span>Another example is the <em>Surya Kund</em> in Modhera, northern Gujarat, next to the Sun Temple, built by King Bhima I in 1026 to honour the sun god Surya. It actually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84a996fc-46fc-423e-8d8e-9f389a1280a5\" data-question=\"11\">resembles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a tank (<em>kund</em> means reservoir or pond) rather than a well, but displays the hallmarks of stepwell architecture, including four sides of steps that descend to the bottom in a stunning <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8617fa7-878c-4c2a-9a01-3d8b0cfac638\" data-question=\"10\">geometrical formation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. The terraces house 108 small, intricately carved shrines between the sets of steps.</span></p><p><span>Rajasthan also has a wealth of wells. The ancient city of Bundi, 200 kilometres south of Jaipur, is renowned for its architecture, including its stepwells. One of the larger examples is <em>Raniji Ki</em> <em>Baori</em>, which was built by the queen of the region, Nathavatji, in 1699. At 46 metres deep, 20 metres wide and 40 metres long, the intricately carved monument is one of 21 <em>baoris</em> commissioned in the Bundi area by Nathavatji.</span></p><p><span>In the old ruined town of Abhaneri, about 95 kilometres east of Jaipur, is <em>Chand Baori</em>, one of India’s oldest and deepest wells; aesthetically, it’s perhaps one of the most dramatic. Built in around 850 AD next to the temple of Harshat Mata, the baori comprises hundreds of zigzagging steps that run along three of its sides, steeply descending 11 storeys, resulting in a striking geometric pattern when seen from afar. On the fourth side, covered verandas supported by ornate pillars <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67e14ae8-4802-4098-bc8b-0b6549711d76\" data-question=\"12\">overlook the steps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Still in public use is <em>Neemrana Ki Baori</em>, located just off the Jaipur–Dehli highway. Constructed in around 1700, it’s nine <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"754b1811-d579-4c47-8d10-951b8b174f14\" data-question=\"13\">storeys deep<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, with the last two levels underwater. At ground level, there are 86 colonnaded openings from where the visitor descends 170 steps to the deepest water source.</span></p><p><span>Today, following years of neglect, many of these monuments to medieval engineering have been saved by the Archaeological Survey of India, which has recognised the importance of preserving them as part of the country’s rich history. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c0fd6a8-122f-48dd-a03b-7adb2fcc776e\" data-question=\"8\">Tourists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> flock to wells in far-flung corners of northwestern India to gaze in wonder at these architectural marvels from 1,000 years ago, which serve as a reminder of both the ingenuity and artistry of ancient civilisations and of the value of water to human existence.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>1–5</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21163\" id=\"question-wrapper-21163\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Examples of ancient stepwells can be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"afbd4521-43f7-469c-abd5-f6357e989300\" data-question=\"1\">found all over the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21164\" id=\"question-wrapper-21164\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Stepwells had a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62ee8fee-01db-4fd1-98a7-89a23694c070\" data-question=\"2\">range of functions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, in addition to those related to water collection. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21165\" id=\"question-wrapper-21165\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The few existing stepwells in Delhi are more attractive than those found elsewhere. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21166\" id=\"question-wrapper-21166\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It took workers many years to build the stone steps characteristic of stepwells. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21167\" id=\"question-wrapper-21167\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The number of steps above the water level in a stepwell <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dca55882-00d6-40dd-8af6-16d4a0495e1b\" data-question=\"5\">altered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> during the course of a year. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Answer the questions below.</p><p>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>6–8</strong> on your answer sheet. </em></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21168\" id=\"question-wrapper-21168\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Which part of some stepwells <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0df6f364-56cb-4d4f-b880-8ce641a5bf0f\" data-question=\"6\">provided shade for people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PAVILIONS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21169\" id=\"question-wrapper-21169\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What type of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da26c058-2690-4f5c-9c10-404605fb9899\" data-question=\"7\">serious climatic event<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, which took place in southern Rajasthan, is mentioned in the article? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DROUGHT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21170\" id=\"question-wrapper-21170\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Who are frequent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c0fd6a8-122f-48dd-a03b-7adb2fcc776e\" data-question=\"8\">visitors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> to stepwells nowadays? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TOURISTS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the table below</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>9-13</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><table><tbody><tr><td width=\"96\"><p><span><strong>Stepwells</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"72\"><p><span><strong>Date</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"180\"><p><span><strong>Features</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"216\"><p><span><strong>Other notes</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"96\"><p><span><strong><em>Rani Ki Vav</em></strong></span></p></td><td width=\"72\"><p><span>Late 11th century</span></p></td><td width=\"180\"><p><span>As many as 500 sculptures decorate the monument</span></p></td><td width=\"216\"><p><span>Restored in the 1960s</span></p><p><span> </span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"218f05f8-b612-471c-9726-af35ee70636f\" data-question=\"9\">Excellent condition, despite<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> the <strong>9</strong>………… of 2001.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"96\"><p><span><strong><em>Surya Kund</em></strong></span></p></td><td width=\"72\"><p><span>1026</span></p></td><td width=\"180\"><p><span>Steps on the <strong>10</strong>………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8617fa7-878c-4c2a-9a01-3d8b0cfac638\" data-question=\"10\">produce a geometric pattern<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span></span></p><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Carved shrines.</span></p></td><td width=\"216\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84a996fc-46fc-423e-8d8e-9f389a1280a5\" data-question=\"11\">Looks more like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a <strong>11</strong>………… than a well.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"96\"><p><span><strong><em>Raniji Ki Baori</em></strong></span></p></td><td width=\"72\"><p><span>1699</span></p></td><td width=\"180\"><p><span>Intricately carved monument</span></p></td><td width=\"216\"><p><span>One of 21 <em>baoris</em> in the area commissioned by Queen Nathavatji</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"96\"><p><span><strong><em>Chand Baori</em></strong></span></p></td><td width=\"72\"><p><span>850 AD</span></p></td><td width=\"180\"><p><span>Steps take you down 11 storeys to the bottom</span></p></td><td width=\"216\"><p><span>Old, deep and very dramatic</span></p><p><span> </span></p><p><span>Has <strong>12</strong>………… which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67e14ae8-4802-4098-bc8b-0b6549711d76\" data-question=\"12\">provide a view of the steps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"96\"><p><span><strong><em>Neemrana Ki Baori</em></strong></span></p></td><td width=\"72\"><p><span>1700</span></p></td><td width=\"180\"><p><span>Has two <strong>13</strong>………… levels.</span></p></td><td width=\"216\"><p><span>Used by public today</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21171\" id=\"question-wrapper-21171\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EARTHQUAKE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21172\" id=\"question-wrapper-21172\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">4 SIDES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21173\" id=\"question-wrapper-21173\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TANK</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21174\" id=\"question-wrapper-21174\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VERANDAS/VERANDAHS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21175\" id=\"question-wrapper-21175\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">UNDERWATER</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"62ee8fee-01db-4fd1-98a7-89a23694c070","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"range of functions","passagePhrase":"gathering, of leisure, of relaxation and of worship"},{"uid":"dca55882-00d6-40dd-8af6-16d4a0495e1b","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"altered","passagePhrase":"have to be negotiated"},{"uid":"0df6f364-56cb-4d4f-b880-8ce641a5bf0f","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"provided shade for people","passagePhrase":"sheltered visitors from the relentless heat"},{"uid":"da26c058-2690-4f5c-9c10-404605fb9899","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"serious climatic event","passagePhrase":"recent dry spells"},{"uid":"218f05f8-b612-471c-9726-af35ee70636f","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Excellent condition, despite","passagePhrase":"this ancient structure survived"},{"uid":"84a996fc-46fc-423e-8d8e-9f389a1280a5","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Looks more like","passagePhrase":"resembles"},{"uid":"a8617fa7-878c-4c2a-9a01-3d8b0cfac638","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"produce a geometric pattern","passagePhrase":"geometrical formation"},{"uid":"67e14ae8-4802-4098-bc8b-0b6549711d76","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"provide a view of the steps","passagePhrase":"overlook the steps"},{"uid":"754b1811-d579-4c47-8d10-951b8b174f14","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"storeys deep"},{"uid":"2c0fd6a8-122f-48dd-a03b-7adb2fcc776e","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"visitors","passagePhrase":"Tourists"}]},"reading_u2_188":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>EUROPEAN TRANSPORT SYSTEMS 1990-2010</strong></span></h2><p><span></span></p><p><span>What have been the trends and what are the prospects for European transport systems?</span></p><p><span><strong>A </strong></span></p><p><span>It is difficult to conceive of vigorous economic growth without an efficient transport system. Although <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6890ae6a-c3de-4b70-95ad-9ccadf9ba241\" data-question=\"22\">modern information technologies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> can reduce the demand for physical transport by facilitating teleworking and teleservices, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"804680e2-dd83-4cd0-b184-0936e6f4d751\" data-question=\"22\">requirement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> for transport continues to increase. There are two key factors behind this trend. For passenger transport, the determining factor is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e7220c1-3439-440c-943a-7bca7da0d234\" data-question=\"14\">spectacular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> growth in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebf0521c-805b-4961-ba92-f2d270318bba\" data-question=\"14\">car<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> use. The number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebf0521c-805b-4961-ba92-f2d270318bba\" data-question=\"14\">car<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>s on European Union (EU) roads saw an increase of three million <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebf0521c-805b-4961-ba92-f2d270318bba\" data-question=\"14\">car<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>s each year from 1990 to 2010, and in the next decade the EU will see a further substantial increase in its fleet.</span></p><p><span><strong>B </strong></span></p><p><span>As far as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe954b74-53fe-4eba-bc73-4a832b11290b\" data-question=\"15\">goods transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> is concerned, growth <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7799755a-025e-42ca-b677-58187d13c839\" data-question=\"15\">is due to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> a large extent to changes in the European economy and its system of production. In the last 20 years, as internal frontiers have been abolished, the EU has moved from a ‘stock’ economy to a ‘flow’ economy. This phenomenon has been emphasised by the relocation of some industries, particularly those which are labour intensive, to reduce production costs, even though the production site is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"13329756-530f-4a1b-84a4-0377ac4a1db1\" data-question=\"23\">hundreds or even thousands of kilometres away from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> the final assembly plant or away from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74df2b5c-e081-445d-a8b2-a54b733f2a26\" data-question=\"23\">users<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>C </strong></span></p><p><span>The strong economic growth expected in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"efcdd661-7d59-4b45-a85c-257e90d32a5d\" data-question=\"16\">countries which are candidates for entry to the EU<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> will also increase transport flows, in particular road haulage traffic. In 1998, some of these countries already exported more than twice their 1990 volumes and imported more than five times their 1990 volumes. And <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"25e23fee-567d-434b-8ba9-d3a2b0bc3be3\" data-question=\"22\">although<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> many candidate countries inherited a transport system which encourages rail, the distribution between modes has tipped sharply in favour of road transport since the 1990s. Between 1990 and 1998, road haulage increased by 19.4%, while during the same period rail haulage decreased by 43.5%, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"25e23fee-567d-434b-8ba9-d3a2b0bc3be3\" data-question=\"22\">although<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> – and this could benefit the enlarged EU – it is still on average at a much higher level than in existing member states.</span></p><p><span><strong>D </strong></span></p><p><span>However, a new imperative-sustainable development – offers an opportunity for adapting the EU’s common transport policy. This objective, agreed by the Gothenburg European Council, has to be achieved by integrating environmental considerations into Community policies, and shifting the balance between modes of transport lies at the heart of its strategy. The ambitious objective can only be fully achieved by 2020, but proposed measures are nonetheless a first <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7eea65a-36b0-43e0-8bbb-5657478422da\" data-question=\"17\">essential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> step towards a sustainable transport system which will ideally be in place <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0d0fccc-543d-415b-abe2-fcf967d9c2bb\" data-question=\"17\">in 30 years’ time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, that is by 2040.</span></p><p><span><strong>E </strong></span></p><p><span>In 1998, energy consumption in the transport sector was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34f8b220-b5f1-470e-83ae-2d2558006079\" data-question=\"18\">to blame for 28% of emissions of CO2, the leading greenhouse gas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. According to the latest estimates, if nothing is done to reverse the traffic growth trend, CO2 emissions from transport can be expected to increase by around 50% to 1,113 billion tonnes by 2020，compared with the 739 billion tonnes recorded <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"362aced0-e6cd-4f26-8898-4f47226b4525\" data-question=\"26\">in 1990<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Once again, road transport is the main culprit since it alone accounts for 84% of the CO2 emissions attributable to transport. Using alternative fuels and improving energy efficiency is thus both an ecological necessity and a technological challenge.</span></p><p><span><strong>F </strong></span></p><p><span>At the same time greater efforts must be made to achieve a modal shift. Such a change cannot be achieved overnight, all the less so after over half a century of constant deterioration in favour of road. This has reached such a pitch that today rail freight services are facing marginalisation, with just 8% of market share, and with international goods trains struggling along at an average speed of 18km/h. Three possible options have emerged.</span></p><p><span><strong>G </strong></span></p><p><span>The first approach would consist of focusing on road transport <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8f84bd1-00f8-45e2-bbe0-5d9a6e954820\" data-question=\"19\">solely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> through pricing. This option would not be accompanied by complementary measures in the other modes of transport. In the short term it might curb the growth in road transport through the better loading ratio of goods vehicles and occupancy rates of passenger vehicles expected as a result of the increase in the price of transport. However, the lack of measures available to revitalise other modes of transport would make it impossible for more sustainable modes of transport to take up the baton.</span></p><p><span><strong>H </strong></span></p><p><span>The second approach also concentrates on road transport pricing but is accompanied by measures to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"143c1795-2648-4db7-b3ec-5369a0e95985\" data-question=\"20\">increase the efficiency<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of the other modes (better quality of services, logistics, technology). However, this approach does not include investment in new infrastructure, nor does it guarantee better regional cohesion. It could help to achieve greater uncoupling than the first approach, but road transport would keep the lion’s share of the market and continue to concentrate on saturated arteries, despite being the most polluting of the modes. It is therefore not enough to guarantee the necessary shift of the balance.</span></p><p><span><strong>I </strong></span></p><p><span>The third approach, which is not new, comprises a series of measures ranging from pricing to revitalising alternative modes of transport and targeting investment in the trans-European network. This integrated approach would allow the market shares of the other modes to return to their 1998 levels and thus <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7e4f7979-d2f5-4ec9-a660-ea0cdc03472b\" data-question=\"21\">make a shift of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> balance. It is far more ambitious than it looks, bearing in mind the historical imbalance in favour of roads for the last fifty years, but would achieve a marked break in the link between road transport growth and economic growth, without placing restrictions on the mobility of people and goods.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Reading Passage 2 has nine paragraphs, <strong>A-I</strong>.</p><p>Choose the correct heading for paragraphs <strong>A-E</strong> and <strong>G-I</strong> from the list of headings below.</p><p><em>Write the correct number, <strong>i-xi</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-21</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><p><strong>i</strong> A fresh and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7eea65a-36b0-43e0-8bbb-5657478422da\" data-question=\"17\">important<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0d0fccc-543d-415b-abe2-fcf967d9c2bb\" data-question=\"17\">long-term<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> goal</p><p><strong>ii</strong> Charging for roads and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"143c1795-2648-4db7-b3ec-5369a0e95985\" data-question=\"20\">improving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> other transport methods</p><p><strong>iii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7799755a-025e-42ca-b677-58187d13c839\" data-question=\"15\">Changes affecting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> the distances <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe954b74-53fe-4eba-bc73-4a832b11290b\" data-question=\"15\">goods may be transported<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></p><p><strong>iv</strong> Taking all the steps necessary to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7e4f7979-d2f5-4ec9-a660-ea0cdc03472b\" data-question=\"21\">change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> transport patterns</p><p><strong>v</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34f8b220-b5f1-470e-83ae-2d2558006079\" data-question=\"18\">The environmental costs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of road transport</p><p><strong>vi</strong> The escalating cost of rail transport</p><p><strong>vii</strong> The need to achieve transport rebalance</p><p><strong>viii</strong> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e7220c1-3439-440c-943a-7bca7da0d234\" data-question=\"14\">rapid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> growth of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebf0521c-805b-4961-ba92-f2d270318bba\" data-question=\"14\">private transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></p><p><strong>ix</strong> Plans to develop major road networks</p><p><strong>x</strong> Restricting road use through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf152234-9292-4d9b-8b33-43dcabee92d1\" data-question=\"19\">charging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> policies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8f84bd1-00f8-45e2-bbe0-5d9a6e954820\" data-question=\"19\">alone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></p><p><strong>xi</strong> Transport trends in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"efcdd661-7d59-4b45-a85c-257e90d32a5d\" data-question=\"16\">countries awaiting EU admission<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></p><p><em>Example Answer</em></p><p>Paragraph <strong>F</strong> <strong>vii</strong></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21184\" id=\"question-wrapper-21184\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21185\" id=\"question-wrapper-21185\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21186\" id=\"question-wrapper-21186\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">XI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21187\" id=\"question-wrapper-21187\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21188\" id=\"question-wrapper-21188\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21189\" id=\"question-wrapper-21189\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">X</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21190\" id=\"question-wrapper-21190\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph H </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21191\" id=\"question-wrapper-21191\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph I </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>22-26</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21192\" id=\"question-wrapper-21192\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"804680e2-dd83-4cd0-b184-0936e6f4d751\" data-question=\"22\">need<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> for transport is growing, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"25e23fee-567d-434b-8ba9-d3a2b0bc3be3\" data-question=\"22\">despite<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6890ae6a-c3de-4b70-95ad-9ccadf9ba241\" data-question=\"22\">technological developments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21193\" id=\"question-wrapper-21193\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> To reduce production costs, some industries have been <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"13329756-530f-4a1b-84a4-0377ac4a1db1\" data-question=\"23\">moved closer to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> their relevant <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74df2b5c-e081-445d-a8b2-a54b733f2a26\" data-question=\"23\">consumers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21194\" id=\"question-wrapper-21194\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Cars are prohibitively expensive in some EU candidate countries. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21195\" id=\"question-wrapper-21195\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Gothenburg European Council was set up 30 years ago. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21196\" id=\"question-wrapper-21196\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> By <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"362aced0-e6cd-4f26-8898-4f47226b4525\" data-question=\"26\">the end of this decade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, CO2 emissions from transport are predicted to reach 739 billion tonnes. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"6890ae6a-c3de-4b70-95ad-9ccadf9ba241","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"technological developments","passagePhrase":"modern information technologies"},{"uid":"804680e2-dd83-4cd0-b184-0936e6f4d751","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"need","passagePhrase":"requirement"},{"uid":"6e7220c1-3439-440c-943a-7bca7da0d234","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"rapid","passagePhrase":"spectacular"},{"uid":"ebf0521c-805b-4961-ba92-f2d270318bba","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"private transport","passagePhrase":"car ... car ... car"},{"uid":"fe954b74-53fe-4eba-bc73-4a832b11290b","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"goods may be transported","passagePhrase":"goods transport"},{"uid":"7799755a-025e-42ca-b677-58187d13c839","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Changes affecting","passagePhrase":"is due to"},{"uid":"74df2b5c-e081-445d-a8b2-a54b733f2a26","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"consumers","passagePhrase":"users"},{"uid":"efcdd661-7d59-4b45-a85c-257e90d32a5d","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"countries awaiting EU admission","passagePhrase":"countries which are candidates for entry to the EU"},{"uid":"25e23fee-567d-434b-8ba9-d3a2b0bc3be3","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"despite","passagePhrase":"although ... although"},{"uid":"d7eea65a-36b0-43e0-8bbb-5657478422da","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"important","passagePhrase":"essential"},{"uid":"a0d0fccc-543d-415b-abe2-fcf967d9c2bb","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"long-term","passagePhrase":"in 30 years’ time"},{"uid":"34f8b220-b5f1-470e-83ae-2d2558006079","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"The environmental costs","passagePhrase":"to blame for 28% of emissions of CO2, the leading greenhouse gas"},{"uid":"c8f84bd1-00f8-45e2-bbe0-5d9a6e954820","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"alone","passagePhrase":"solely"},{"uid":"143c1795-2648-4db7-b3ec-5369a0e95985","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"improving","passagePhrase":"increase the efficiency"},{"uid":"7e4f7979-d2f5-4ec9-a660-ea0cdc03472b","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"change","passagePhrase":"make a shift of"},{"uid":"cf152234-9292-4d9b-8b33-43dcabee92d1","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"charging","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_189":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><h2><span><strong>The psychology of innovation</strong></span></h2><p><span><em></em></span></p><p><span><em>Why are so few companies truly innovative?</em></span></p><p><span>Innovation is key to business survival, and companies put substantial resources into inspiring employees to develop new ideas. There are, nevertheless, people working in luxurious, state-of-the-art centres designed to stimulate innovation who find that their environment <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ca917df6-0969-4a8a-818c-70099e99a182\" data-question=\"36\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ca917df6-0969-4a8a-818c-70099e99a182\" data-question=\"36\">doesn’t make them feel at all creativ<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>e<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. And there are those who don’t have a budget, or much space, but who innovate successfully.</span></p><p><span>For Robert B. Cialdini, Professor of Psychology at Arizona State University, one reason that companies don’t succeed as often as they should is that innovation starts with recruitment. Research shows that the fit between an employee’s values and a company’s values makes a difference to what contribution they make and whether, two years after they join, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ceba64ca-e4e9-4cbf-af7e-de0a273f68f9\" data-question=\"31\">they’re still at the company<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Studies at Harvard Business School show that, although some individuals may be more creative than others, almost every individual <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83b35b8a-64c8-41ca-9f73-3141ba19c5b8\" data-question=\"37\">can be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> creative in the right circumstances.</span></p><p><span>One of the most famous photographs in the story of rock’n’roll emphasises Ciaidini’s views. The 1956 picture of singers Elvis Presley, Carl Perkins, Johnny Cash and Jerry Lee Lewis jamming at a piano in Sun Studios in Memphis tells a hidden story. Sun’s ‘million-dollar quartet’ could have been a quintet. Missing from the picture is Roy Orbison’ a greater natural singer than Lewis, Perkins or Cash. Sam Phillips, who owned Sun, wanted to revolutionise popular music with songs that fused black and white music, and country and blues. Presley, Cash, Perkins and Lewis <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93bb139c-2281-48ce-9654-eeb7423f9b47\" data-question=\"27\">instinctively understood Phillips’s ambition and believed in it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Orbison wasn’t inspired by the goal, and only ever achieved one hit with the Sun label.</span></p><p><span>The value fit matters, says Cialdini, because innovation is, in part, a process of change, and under that pressure we, as a species, behave differently, ‘When things change, we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1208158c-78b8-413f-97e3-75e511eb710d\" data-question=\"32\">are hard-wired to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7232d92-9afc-426b-9327-d3207b7ca2f1\" data-question=\"32\">play it safe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.’ Managers should therefore adopt an approach that appears counterintuitive -they should explain what stands to be lost if the company fails to seize a particular opportunity. Studies show that we invariably <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"438bddb6-8ba6-48df-9bd8-1162494bb767\" data-question=\"33\">take more gambles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e95ea7ef-3b32-4679-9b56-33e2782496ff\" data-question=\"33\">threatened with a loss<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> than when offered a reward.</span></p><p><span>Managing innovation is a delicate art. It’s easy for a company to be pulled in conflicting directions as the marketing, product development, and finance departments each get different feedback from different sets of people. And without a system which ensures collaborative exchanges within the company, it’s also easy for small ‘pockets of innovation’ to disappear. Innovation is a contact sport. You can’t brief people just by saying, ‘We’re going in this direction and I’m going to take you with me.’</span></p><p><span>Cialdini believes that this ‘follow-the-leader syndrome, is dangerous, not least because it encourages bosses to go it alone. ‘It’s been scientifically proven that three people will be better than one at solving problems, even if that one person is the smartest person in the field.’ To prove his point, Cialdini cites an interview with molecular biologist James Watson. Watson, together with Francis Crick, discovered the structure of DNA, the genetic information carrier of all living organisms. ‘When asked how they had cracked the code ahead of an array of highly accomplished rival investigators, he said something that stunned me. He said he and Crick had succeeded because they were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbe7f4ba-f907-46f5-8c2e-53ee8b50127b\" data-question=\"28\">aware that they weren’t the most intelligent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of the scientists pursuing the answer. The smartest scientist was called Rosalind Franklin who, Watson said, “was so intelligent she rarely sought advice”.’</span></p><p><span>Teamwork taps into one of the basic drivers of human behaviour. ‘The principle of social proof is so pervasive that we don’t even recognise it,’ says Cialdini. ‘If your project is being resisted, for example, by a group of veteran employees, ask another old-timer to speak up for it.’ Cialdini is not alone in advocating this strategy. Research shows that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b56cfd5-8617-4d42-8e74-36c8cdbd012e\" data-question=\"40\">peer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> power, used horizontally not vertically, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"45c9aefa-f3be-46dd-9a1d-239854fd58e4\" data-question=\"40\">is much more powerful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> than any boss’s speech.</span></p><p><span>Writing, visualising and prototyping can stimulate the flow of new ideas. Cialdini cites scores of research papers and historical events that prove that even something as simple as writing deepens every individual’s engagement in the project. It is, he says, the reason why all those competitions on breakfast cereal packets encouraged us to write in saying, in no more than 10 words: ‘I like Kellogg’s Com Flakes because… .’ The very act of writing makes us <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33d5d1d6-1908-4824-8935-86aa26df9ad1\" data-question=\"29\">more likely to believe it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Authority doesn’t have to inhibit innovation but it often does. The wrong kind of leadership will lead to what Cialdini calls ‘captainitis, the regrettable tendency of team members to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"693d0e2a-f5c5-4f62-862e-41a2152d7cf3\" data-question=\"34\">opt out of team responsibilities that are properly theirs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>’. He calls it captainitis because, he says, ‘crew members of multipilot aircraft exhibit a sometimes deadly passivity when the flight captain makes a clearly wrong-headed decision’. This behaviour is not, he says, unique to air travel, but can happen in any workplace where the leader is overbearing.</span></p><p><span>At the other end of the scale is the 1980s Memphis design collective, a group of young designers for whom ‘the only rule was that there were no rule’. This environment encouraged a free <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27b387ed-0f23-4097-a309-9af52e742e9e\" data-question=\"35\">interchange<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of ideas, which led to more creativity with form, function, colour and materials that revolutionised attitudes to furniture design.</span></p><p><span>Many theorists believe the ideal boss should lead from behind, taking pride in collective accomplishment and giving credit where it is due. Cialdini says: ‘Leaders should encourage everyone to contribute and simultaneously assure all concerned that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df7d689a-2c2b-4bcd-8398-7485d2914945\" data-question=\"30\">every recommendation is important to making the right decision and will be given full attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.’ The frustrating thing about innovation is that there are many approaches, but no magic formula. However, a manager who wants to create a truly innovative culture can make their job a lot easier by recognising these psychological realities.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>27-30</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21197\" id=\"question-wrapper-21197\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The example of the ‘million-dollar quartet’ underlines the writer’s point about </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. recognising talent.</li> <li>B. working as a team.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93bb139c-2281-48ce-9654-eeb7423f9b47\" data-question=\"27\">having a shared objective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>D. being an effective leader.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21198\" id=\"question-wrapper-21198\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> James Watson suggests that he and Francis Crick won the race to discover the DNA code because they </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbe7f4ba-f907-46f5-8c2e-53ee8b50127b\" data-question=\"28\">conscious of their own limitations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>B. brought complementary skills to their partnership.</li> <li>C. were determined to outperform their brighter rivals.</li> <li>D. encouraged each other to realise their joint ambition.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21199\" id=\"question-wrapper-21199\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer mentions competitions on breakfast cereal packets as an example of how to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. inspire creative thinking.</li> <li>B. generate concise writing.</li> <li>C. promote loyalty to a group.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33d5d1d6-1908-4824-8935-86aa26df9ad1\" data-question=\"29\">strengthen commitment to an idea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21200\" id=\"question-wrapper-21200\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the last paragraph, the writer suggests that it is important for employees to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. be aware of their company’s goals.</li> <li>B. feel that their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df7d689a-2c2b-4bcd-8398-7485d2914945\" data-question=\"30\">contributions are valued<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>C. have respect for their co-workers‟ achievements.</li> <li>D. understand why certain management decisions are made.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, <strong>A-G</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>31-35</strong> on your answer sheet</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"438bddb6-8ba6-48df-9bd8-1162494bb767\" data-question=\"33\">take chances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27b387ed-0f23-4097-a309-9af52e742e9e\" data-question=\"35\">share<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> their ideas.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> become competitive.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> get promotion.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7232d92-9afc-426b-9327-d3207b7ca2f1\" data-question=\"32\">avoid risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"693d0e2a-f5c5-4f62-862e-41a2152d7cf3\" data-question=\"34\">ignore their duties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ceba64ca-e4e9-4cbf-af7e-de0a273f68f9\" data-question=\"31\">remain in their jobs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21201\" id=\"question-wrapper-21201\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Employees whose values match those of their employers are more likely to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21202\" id=\"question-wrapper-21202\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> At times of change, people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1208158c-78b8-413f-97e3-75e511eb710d\" data-question=\"32\">tend to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21203\" id=\"question-wrapper-21203\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> If people are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e95ea7ef-3b32-4679-9b56-33e2782496ff\" data-question=\"33\">aware of what they might lose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, they will often </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21204\" id=\"question-wrapper-21204\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People working under a dominant boss are liable to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21205\" id=\"question-wrapper-21205\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Employees working in organisations with few rules are more likely to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>36-40</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21206\" id=\"question-wrapper-21206\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The physical surroundings in which a person works play a key role in determining their creativity. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21207\" id=\"question-wrapper-21207\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Most people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83b35b8a-64c8-41ca-9f73-3141ba19c5b8\" data-question=\"37\">have the potential to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> creative. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21208\" id=\"question-wrapper-21208\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Teams work best when their members are of equally matched intelligence. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21209\" id=\"question-wrapper-21209\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is easier for smaller companies to be innovative. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21210\" id=\"question-wrapper-21210\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A manager’s approval of an idea <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"45c9aefa-f3be-46dd-9a1d-239854fd58e4\" data-question=\"40\">is more persuasive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> than that of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b56cfd5-8617-4d42-8e74-36c8cdbd012e\" data-question=\"40\">colleague<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"ceba64ca-e4e9-4cbf-af7e-de0a273f68f9","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"remain in their jobs","passagePhrase":"they’re still at the company"},{"uid":"83b35b8a-64c8-41ca-9f73-3141ba19c5b8","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"have the potential to be","passagePhrase":"can be"},{"uid":"93bb139c-2281-48ce-9654-eeb7423f9b47","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"having a shared objective","passagePhrase":"instinctively understood Phillips’s ambition and believed in it"},{"uid":"1208158c-78b8-413f-97e3-75e511eb710d","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"tend to","passagePhrase":"are hard-wired to"},{"uid":"c7232d92-9afc-426b-9327-d3207b7ca2f1","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"avoid risk","passagePhrase":"play it safe"},{"uid":"438bddb6-8ba6-48df-9bd8-1162494bb767","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"take chances","passagePhrase":"take more gambles"},{"uid":"e95ea7ef-3b32-4679-9b56-33e2782496ff","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"aware of what they might lose","passagePhrase":"threatened with a loss"},{"uid":"cbe7f4ba-f907-46f5-8c2e-53ee8b50127b","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"conscious of their own limitations","passagePhrase":"aware that they weren’t the most intelligent"},{"uid":"7b56cfd5-8617-4d42-8e74-36c8cdbd012e","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"colleague","passagePhrase":"peer"},{"uid":"45c9aefa-f3be-46dd-9a1d-239854fd58e4","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"is more persuasive","passagePhrase":"is much more powerful"},{"uid":"33d5d1d6-1908-4824-8935-86aa26df9ad1","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"strengthen commitment to an idea","passagePhrase":"more likely to believe it"},{"uid":"693d0e2a-f5c5-4f62-862e-41a2152d7cf3","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"ignore their duties","passagePhrase":"opt out of team responsibilities that are properly theirs"},{"uid":"27b387ed-0f23-4097-a309-9af52e742e9e","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"share","passagePhrase":"interchange"},{"uid":"df7d689a-2c2b-4bcd-8398-7485d2914945","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"contributions are valued","passagePhrase":"every recommendation is important to making the right decision and will be given full attention"}]},"reading_u2_190":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><h2><span><strong>Tea and the Industrial Revolution</strong></span></h2><p><span><em></em></span></p><p><span><em>A Cambridge professor says that a change in drinking habits was the reason for the Industrial Revolution in Britain. Anjana Abuja reports </em></span></p><p><span><strong><span>A</span> </strong></span></p><p><span>Alan Macfarlane, professor of anthropological science at King’s College, Cambridge has, like other historians, spent decades wrestling with the enigma of the Industrial Revolution. Why did this particular Big Bang – the world-changing birth of industry-happen <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d763ba9-b3e4-4561-b218-b255d08c619f\" data-question=\"1\">in Britain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>? And why did it strike at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d763ba9-b3e4-4561-b218-b255d08c619f\" data-question=\"1\">the end of the 18th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>?</span></p><p><span><strong><span>B</span> </strong></span></p><p><span>Macfarlane compares the puzzle to a combination lock. ‘There are about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd3697dc-fe7d-4e30-aa8d-78951fdc65bc\" data-question=\"2\">20 different factors and all of them need to be present before the revolution can happen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>,’ he says. For industry to take off, there needs to be the technology and power to drive factories, large urban populations to provide cheap labour, easy transport to move goods around, an affluent middle-class willing to buy mass-produced objects, a market-driven economy and a political system that allows this to happen. While this was the case for England, other nations, such as Japan, the Netherlands and France also met some of these criteria but were not industrialising. All these factors must have been necessary. But not sufficient to cause the revolution, says Macfarlane. ‘After all, Holland had everything except coal while China also had many of these factors. Most historians are convinced there are one or two missing factors that you need to open the lock.’</span></p><p><span><strong><span>C</span> </strong></span></p><p><span>The missing factors, he proposes, are to be found in almost even kitchen cupboard. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"236f3c89-4f80-44a9-bb58-13dff4516a4b\" data-question=\"3\">Tea and beer, two of the nation’s favourite drinks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, fuelled the revolution. The antiseptic properties of tannin, the active ingredient in tea, and of hops in beer – plus the fact that both are made with boiled water – allowed urban communities to flourish at close quarters <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f73d5b3d-3423-4f95-b965-557aad6e70bd\" data-question=\"9\">without succumbing to water-borne diseases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> such as dysentery. The theory sounds eccentric but once he starts to explain the detective work that went into his deduction, the scepticism gives way to wary admiration. Macfarlanes case has been strengthened by support from notable quarters – Roy Porter, the distinguished medical historian, recently <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c6fec4fe-db02-42be-b44b-202fff18bfe7\" data-question=\"10\">wrote a favourable appraisal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> of his research.</span></p><p><span><strong><span>D</span> </strong></span></p><p><span>Macfarlane had wondered for a long time how the Industrial Revolution came about. Historians had alighted on one interesting factor around the mid-18th century that required explanation. Between about 1650 and 1740, the population in Britain was static. But then there was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5020bfdb-eae1-46b4-aaeb-d9d5badce53a\" data-question=\"4\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"77f140e3-c8fc-4f31-9d04-618c33b371e1\" data-question=\"11\">a burst in population growth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Macfarlane says: ‘The infant mortality rate halved in the space of 20 years, and this happened in both rural areas and cities, and across all classes. People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"829b1d44-6e8b-4b41-80f0-9234127f1fb2\" data-question=\"4\">suggested four possible causes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Was there a sudden change in the viruses and bacteria around? Unlikely. Was there a revolution in medical science? But this was a century before Lister’s revolution*. Was there a change in environmental conditions? There were improvements in agriculture that wiped out malaria, but these were small gains. Sanitation did not become widespread until the 19th century. The only option left is food. But the height and weight statistics show a decline. So the food must have got worse. Efforts to explain this sudden reduction in child deaths appeared to draw a blank.’</span></p><p><span><strong><span>E</span> </strong></span></p><p><span>This population burst seemed to happen at just the right time to provide labour for the Industrial Revolution. ‘When you start moving towards an industrial revolution, it is economically efficient to have people living close together,’ says Macfarlane. ‘But then you get disease, particularly from human waste.’ Some digging around in historical records revealed that there was a change in the incidence of water-borne disease at that time, especially dysentery. Macfarlane deduced that whatever the British were drinking must have been important in regulating disease. He says, ‘We drank beer. For a long time, the English were protected by the strong antibacterial agent in hops, which were added to help preserve the beer. But in the late 17th century a tax was introduced on malt, the basic ingredient of beer. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8a8ba4b-1c7e-483d-a742-f61329677be0\" data-question=\"5\">The poor turned to water and gin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> and in the 1720s the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27345052-dbc8-4d81-97a6-f83f7796e59a\" data-question=\"13\">mortality rate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ed364cf-2de2-49b3-bfd5-8145440fe226\" data-question=\"13\">began to rise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> again. Then it suddenly dropped again. What caused this?’</span></p><p><span><strong><span>F</span> </strong></span></p><p><span>Macfarlane <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a6004d6-935a-439b-bc3b-48771059c138\" data-question=\"6\">looked to Japan<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, which was also developing large cities about the same time, and also had no sanitation. Water-borne diseases had a much looser grip on the Japanese population than those in Britain. Could it be the prevalence of tea in their culture? Macfarlane then noted that the history of tea in Britain provided an extraordinary coincidence of dates. Tea was relatively expensive until Britain started a direct clipper trade with China in the early 18th century. By the 1740s, about the time that infant mortality was dipping, the drink was common. Macfarlane guessed that the fact that water had to be boiled, together with the stomach-purifying properties of tea meant that the breast milk provided by mothers was healthier than it had ever been. No other European nation sipped tea like the British, which, by Macfarlanes logic, pushed these other countries out of contention for the revolution.</span></p><p><span><strong><span>G</span> </strong></span></p><p><span>But, if tea is a factor in the combination lock, why didn’t Japan forge ahead in a tea-soaked industrial revolution of its own? Macfarlane notes that even though 17th-century Japan had large cities, high literacy rates, even a futures market, it had turned its back on the essence of any work-based revolution by giving up labour-saving devices such as animals, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84c1da91-cbab-49a9-b410-f696a91818e0\" data-question=\"7\">afraid that they would put people out of work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. So, the nation that we now think of as one of the most technologically advanced entered the 19th century having ‘abandoned the wheel’.</span></p><p><span>——–</span></p><p><span>* Joseph Lister was the first doctor to use antiseptic techniques during surgical operations to prevent infections.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Reading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G</strong>.</p><p>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</p><p><em>Write the correct number, <strong>i-ix</strong>, in boxes <strong>1-7</strong> on your answer sheet</em></p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><p><strong>i </strong> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"829b1d44-6e8b-4b41-80f0-9234127f1fb2\" data-question=\"4\">search for the reasons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> for an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5020bfdb-eae1-46b4-aaeb-d9d5badce53a\" data-question=\"4\">increase in population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></p><p><strong>ii</strong> Industrialisation and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84c1da91-cbab-49a9-b410-f696a91818e0\" data-question=\"7\">fear of unemployment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></p><p><strong>iii</strong> The development of cities in Japan</p><p><strong>iv</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d763ba9-b3e4-4561-b218-b255d08c619f\" data-question=\"1\">The time and place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of the Industrial Revolution</p><p><strong>v</strong> The cases of Holland, France and China</p><p><strong>vi</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8a8ba4b-1c7e-483d-a742-f61329677be0\" data-question=\"5\">Changes in drinking habits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in Britain</p><p><strong>vii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"236f3c89-4f80-44a9-bb58-13dff4516a4b\" data-question=\"3\">Two keys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> to Britain’s industrial revolution</p><p><strong>viii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd3697dc-fe7d-4e30-aa8d-78951fdc65bc\" data-question=\"2\">Conditions required<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> for industrialisation</p><p><strong>ix</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a6004d6-935a-439b-bc3b-48771059c138\" data-question=\"6\">Comparisons with Japan<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> lead to the answer</p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"977\" id=\"question-wrapper-977\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"978\" id=\"question-wrapper-978\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"979\" id=\"question-wrapper-979\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"980\" id=\"question-wrapper-980\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"981\" id=\"question-wrapper-981\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"982\" id=\"question-wrapper-982\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IX</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"983\" id=\"question-wrapper-983\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>8-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"984\" id=\"question-wrapper-984\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> China’s transport system was not suitable for industry in the 18th century. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"985\" id=\"question-wrapper-985\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Tea and beer both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f73d5b3d-3423-4f95-b965-557aad6e70bd\" data-question=\"9\">helped to prevent dysentery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> in Britain. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"986\" id=\"question-wrapper-986\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Roy Porter <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c6fec4fe-db02-42be-b44b-202fff18bfe7\" data-question=\"10\">disagrees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> with Professor Macfarlane’s findings. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"987\" id=\"question-wrapper-987\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> After 1740，there was a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"77f140e3-c8fc-4f31-9d04-618c33b371e1\" data-question=\"11\">reduction in population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in Britain. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"988\" id=\"question-wrapper-988\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People in Britain used to make beer at home. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"989\" id=\"question-wrapper-989\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The tax on malt indirectly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ed364cf-2de2-49b3-bfd5-8145440fe226\" data-question=\"13\">caused a rise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27345052-dbc8-4d81-97a6-f83f7796e59a\" data-question=\"13\">death rate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"3d763ba9-b3e4-4561-b218-b255d08c619f","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"The time and place","passagePhrase":"in Britain ... the end of the 18th century"},{"uid":"bd3697dc-fe7d-4e30-aa8d-78951fdc65bc","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Conditions required","passagePhrase":"20 different factors and all of them need to be present before the revolution can happen"},{"uid":"236f3c89-4f80-44a9-bb58-13dff4516a4b","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Two keys","passagePhrase":"Tea and beer, two of the nation’s favourite drinks"},{"uid":"f73d5b3d-3423-4f95-b965-557aad6e70bd","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"helped to prevent dysentery","passagePhrase":"without succumbing to water-borne diseases"},{"uid":"5020bfdb-eae1-46b4-aaeb-d9d5badce53a","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"increase in population","passagePhrase":"a burst in population growth"},{"uid":"829b1d44-6e8b-4b41-80f0-9234127f1fb2","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"search for the reasons","passagePhrase":"suggested four possible causes"},{"uid":"e8a8ba4b-1c7e-483d-a742-f61329677be0","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Changes in drinking habits","passagePhrase":"The poor turned to water and gin"},{"uid":"27345052-dbc8-4d81-97a6-f83f7796e59a","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"death rate","passagePhrase":"mortality rate"},{"uid":"8ed364cf-2de2-49b3-bfd5-8145440fe226","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"caused a rise","passagePhrase":"began to rise"},{"uid":"2a6004d6-935a-439b-bc3b-48771059c138","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Comparisons with Japan","passagePhrase":"looked to Japan"},{"uid":"84c1da91-cbab-49a9-b410-f696a91818e0","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"fear of unemployment","passagePhrase":"afraid that they would put people out of work"}]},"reading_u2_191":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below. </p><h2><strong>Gifted children and learning</strong></h2><p> </p><p><strong>A </strong></p><p>Internationally, ‘giftedness’ is most frequently determined by a score on a general intelligence test, known as an IQ test, which is above a chosen cutoff point, usually at around the top 2-5%. Children’s educational environment contributes to the IQ score and the way intelligence is used. For example, a very close positive relationship was found when children’s IQ scores were compared with their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78af6ee5-e34f-4b6c-91d4-1bfe0e448494\" data-question=\"21\">home educational provision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> (Freeman, 2010). <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0d37b2c-9761-48e7-b34b-c5e7c9ee0864\" data-question=\"21\">The higher the children’s IQ scores<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, especially over IQ 130, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93051e47-eef8-49c1-b760-ab2f7087b74a\" data-question=\"14\">the better the quality of their educational backup<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, measured in terms of reported <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ededb1e6-8e92-45b6-9cf6-5acffa57e71e\" data-question=\"23\">verbal interactions with parents, number of books and activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93051e47-eef8-49c1-b760-ab2f7087b74a\" data-question=\"14\">in their home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> etc. Because IQ tests are decidedly influenced by what the child has learned, they are to some extent measures of current achievement based on age-norms; that is, how well the children have learned to manipulate their knowledge and know-how within the terms of the test. The vocabulary aspect, for example, is dependent on having heard those words. But IQ tests can neither identify the processes of learning and thinking nor predict creativity.</p><p><strong>B </strong></p><p>Excellence does not emerge without appropriate help. To reach an exceptionally high standard in any area very able children need the means to learn, which includes material to work with and focused challenging tuition -and the encouragement to follow their dream. There appears to be a qualitative difference in the way the intellectually highly able think, compared with more average-ability or older <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d9f871c-56b9-483a-af03-cdcda5ac0d26\" data-question=\"24\">pupils<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, for whom <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55070f0c-8f75-44e7-a362-e77d2681d21e\" data-question=\"24\">external regulation by the teacher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> often compensates <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15dd9009-4e84-4175-874c-6338cedb09bc\" data-question=\"24\">for lack of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> internal regulation. To be at their most effective in their self-regulation, all children can be helped to identify their own ways of learning – metacognition – which will include strategies of planning, monitoring, evaluation, and choice of what to learn. Emotional awareness is also part of metacognition, so children should be helped to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a6ad17b-e204-4311-a4cc-b5278f693a55\" data-question=\"25\">aware of their feelings around the area to be learned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, feelings of curiosity or confidence, for example.</p><p><strong>C </strong></p><p>High achievers have been found to use self-regulatory learning strategies more often and more effectively than lower achievers, and are better able to transfer these strategies to deal with unfamiliar tasks. This happens to such a high degree in some children that they appear to be demonstrating talent in particular areas. Overviewing research on the thinking process of highly able children, (Shore and Kanevsky, 1993) put the instructor’s problem succinctly: ‘If they [the gifted] merely think more quickly, then .we need only teach more quickly. If they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8dd4f0d1-63ec-4a08-8eda-59fb0fd03562\" data-question=\"18\">merely make fewer errors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, then we can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"577a3a3f-495c-49bc-ab42-09515a8a6b6c\" data-question=\"18\">shorten the practice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>’. But of course, this is not entirely the case; adjustments have to be made in methods of learning and teaching, to take account of the many ways individuals think.</p><p><strong>D </strong></p><p>Yet in order to learn by themselves, the gifted do need some support from their teachers. Conversely, teachers who have a tendency to ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90b03391-61b7-4fc5-9edd-91eba3789dca\" data-question=\"15\">overdirect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>’ can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93b44351-cfc2-4e1d-855a-6adde6b62d38\" data-question=\"15\">diminish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> their gifted <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12915e99-b340-4413-8f08-0aab9ed243f4\" data-question=\"15\">pupils<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>’ learning autonomy. Although ‘spoon-feeding’ can produce <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12e71ddb-febb-42c1-ad23-69dbc8307772\" data-question=\"26\">extremely high examination results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, these are not always followed by equally impressive life successes. Too much dependence on the teachers risks loss of autonomy and motivation to discover. However, when teachers help pupils to reflect on their own learning and thinking activities, they increase their pupils’ self-regulation. For a young child, it may be just the simple question ‘What have you learned today?’ which helps them to recognise what they are doing. Given that a fundamental goal of education is to transfer the control of learning from teachers to pupils, improving pupils’ learning to learn techniques should be a major outcome of the school experience, especially for the highly competent. There are quite a number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c326af04-63e0-460f-9b47-a2f5a0ebf17d\" data-question=\"17\">new methods which can help, such as child-initiated learning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, ability-peer tutoring, etc. Such practices have been found to be particularly useful for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3bd7788-e17f-4e1e-a2ff-d3e39aa46308\" data-question=\"17\">bright children from deprived areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</p><p><strong>E </strong></p><p>But scientific progress is not all theoretical, knowledge is a so vital to outstanding performance: individuals who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77642eb5-f269-47d1-8040-8df104a6def2\" data-question=\"22\">know a great deal about a specific domain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> will achieve at a higher level than those who do not (Elshout, 1995). Research with creative scientists by Simonton (1988) brought him to the conclusion that above a certain high level, characteristics such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8dc4862b-da9f-4c4c-98d3-82bc50f4b3c0\" data-question=\"19\">independence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> seemed to contribute more to reaching the highest levels of expertise than intellectual skills, due to the great demands of effort and time needed for learning and practice. Creativity in all forms can be seen as expertise mixed with a high level of motivation (Weisberg, 1993).</p><p><strong>F </strong></p><p>To sum up, learning is affected by emotions of both the individual and significant others. Positive emotions facilitate the creative aspects of learning and negative emotions inhibit it. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a6aaf1d-d9b9-4a21-99b3-9e3284271411\" data-question=\"16\">Fear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, for example, can limit the development of curiosity, which is a strong force in scientific advance, because it motivates problem-solving behaviour. In Boekaerts’ (1991) review of emotion the learning of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d2a2709-6ad1-4275-8798-551688c31615\" data-question=\"20\">very high IQ and highly achieving children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, she found <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"153125ed-ff25-4184-9dcf-c042310a08c8\" data-question=\"20\">emotional forces in harness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. They were not only curious, but often had a strong desire to control their environment, improve their learning efficiency and increase their own learning resources.</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, <strong>A-F</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-17</strong> on your answer sheet</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"990\" id=\"question-wrapper-990\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to the influence of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93051e47-eef8-49c1-b760-ab2f7087b74a\" data-question=\"14\">domestic background<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> on the gifted child. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"991\" id=\"question-wrapper-991\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93b44351-cfc2-4e1d-855a-6adde6b62d38\" data-question=\"15\">what can be lost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12915e99-b340-4413-8f08-0aab9ed243f4\" data-question=\"15\">learners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> are given <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90b03391-61b7-4fc5-9edd-91eba3789dca\" data-question=\"15\">too much guidance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"992\" id=\"question-wrapper-992\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to the damaging effects of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a6aaf1d-d9b9-4a21-99b3-9e3284271411\" data-question=\"16\">anxiety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"993\" id=\"question-wrapper-993\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c326af04-63e0-460f-9b47-a2f5a0ebf17d\" data-question=\"17\">examples of classroom techniques<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> which favour <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3bd7788-e17f-4e1e-a2ff-d3e39aa46308\" data-question=\"17\">socially-disadvantaged children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 18-22) and the list of people below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct person or people, <strong>A-E</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-E</strong>, in boxes <strong>18-22</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of People</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Freeman</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> Shore and Kanevsky</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> Elshout</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> Simonton</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> Boekaerts</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"994\" id=\"question-wrapper-994\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"577a3a3f-495c-49bc-ab42-09515a8a6b6c\" data-question=\"18\">Less time can be spent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> on exercises with gifted pupils who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8dd4f0d1-63ec-4a08-8eda-59fb0fd03562\" data-question=\"18\">produce accurate work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"995\" id=\"question-wrapper-995\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8dc4862b-da9f-4c4c-98d3-82bc50f4b3c0\" data-question=\"19\">Self-reliance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> is a valuable tool that helps gifted students reach their goals. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"996\" id=\"question-wrapper-996\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d2a2709-6ad1-4275-8798-551688c31615\" data-question=\"20\">Gifted children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> know how to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"153125ed-ff25-4184-9dcf-c042310a08c8\" data-question=\"20\">channel their feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to assist their learning. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"997\" id=\"question-wrapper-997\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0d37b2c-9761-48e7-b34b-c5e7c9ee0864\" data-question=\"21\">The very gifted child<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> benefits from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78af6ee5-e34f-4b6c-91d4-1bfe0e448494\" data-question=\"21\">appropriate support from close relatives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"998\" id=\"question-wrapper-998\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Really successful students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77642eb5-f269-47d1-8040-8df104a6def2\" data-question=\"22\">have learnt a considerable amount about their subject<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>23-26</strong> on your answer sheet</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"999\" id=\"question-wrapper-999\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One study found a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ededb1e6-8e92-45b6-9cf6-5acffa57e71e\" data-question=\"23\">strong connection between children’s IQ and the availability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of ……………… and ………………. at home. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BOOKS + ACTIVITIES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1000\" id=\"question-wrapper-1000\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d9f871c-56b9-483a-af03-cdcda5ac0d26\" data-question=\"24\">Children of average ability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> seem to need <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55070f0c-8f75-44e7-a362-e77d2681d21e\" data-question=\"24\">more direction from teachers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15dd9009-4e84-4175-874c-6338cedb09bc\" data-question=\"24\">because they do not have<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> ……………… . </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INTERNAL REGULATION [OR] SELF-REGULATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1001\" id=\"question-wrapper-1001\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Meta-cognition involves children <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a6ad17b-e204-4311-a4cc-b5278f693a55\" data-question=\"25\">understanding their own learning strategies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, as well as developing ………………. . </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EMOTIONAL AWARENESS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1002\" id=\"question-wrapper-1002\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Teachers who rely on what is known as ……………… often produce <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12e71ddb-febb-42c1-ad23-69dbc8307772\" data-question=\"26\">sets of impressive grades in class tests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPOON-FEEDING</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"78af6ee5-e34f-4b6c-91d4-1bfe0e448494","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"appropriate support from close relatives","passagePhrase":"home educational provision"},{"uid":"f0d37b2c-9761-48e7-b34b-c5e7c9ee0864","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"The very gifted child","passagePhrase":"The higher the children’s IQ scores"},{"uid":"93051e47-eef8-49c1-b760-ab2f7087b74a","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"domestic background","passagePhrase":"the better the quality of their educational backup ... in their home"},{"uid":"ededb1e6-8e92-45b6-9cf6-5acffa57e71e","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"strong connection between children’s IQ and the availability","passagePhrase":"verbal interactions with parents, number of books and activities"},{"uid":"6d9f871c-56b9-483a-af03-cdcda5ac0d26","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Children of average ability","passagePhrase":"pupils"},{"uid":"55070f0c-8f75-44e7-a362-e77d2681d21e","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"more direction from teachers","passagePhrase":"external regulation by the teacher"},{"uid":"15dd9009-4e84-4175-874c-6338cedb09bc","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"because they do not have","passagePhrase":"for lack of"},{"uid":"1a6ad17b-e204-4311-a4cc-b5278f693a55","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"understanding their own learning strategies","passagePhrase":"aware of their feelings around the area to be learned"},{"uid":"8dd4f0d1-63ec-4a08-8eda-59fb0fd03562","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"produce accurate work","passagePhrase":"merely make fewer errors"},{"uid":"577a3a3f-495c-49bc-ab42-09515a8a6b6c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Less time can be spent","passagePhrase":"shorten the practice"},{"uid":"90b03391-61b7-4fc5-9edd-91eba3789dca","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"too much guidance","passagePhrase":"overdirect"},{"uid":"93b44351-cfc2-4e1d-855a-6adde6b62d38","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"what can be lost","passagePhrase":"diminish"},{"uid":"12915e99-b340-4413-8f08-0aab9ed243f4","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"learners","passagePhrase":"pupils"},{"uid":"12e71ddb-febb-42c1-ad23-69dbc8307772","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"sets of impressive grades in class tests","passagePhrase":"extremely high examination results"},{"uid":"c326af04-63e0-460f-9b47-a2f5a0ebf17d","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"examples of classroom techniques","passagePhrase":"new methods which can help, such as child-initiated learning"},{"uid":"b3bd7788-e17f-4e1e-a2ff-d3e39aa46308","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"socially-disadvantaged children","passagePhrase":"bright children from deprived areas"},{"uid":"77642eb5-f269-47d1-8040-8df104a6def2","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"have learnt a considerable amount about their subject","passagePhrase":"know a great deal about a specific domain"},{"uid":"8dc4862b-da9f-4c4c-98d3-82bc50f4b3c0","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Self-reliance","passagePhrase":"independence"},{"uid":"8a6aaf1d-d9b9-4a21-99b3-9e3284271411","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"anxiety","passagePhrase":"Fear"},{"uid":"4d2a2709-6ad1-4275-8798-551688c31615","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Gifted children","passagePhrase":"very high IQ and highly achieving children"},{"uid":"153125ed-ff25-4184-9dcf-c042310a08c8","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"channel their feelings","passagePhrase":"emotional forces in harness"}]},"reading_u2_192":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>Museums of fine art and their public</strong></span></h2><p><span></span></p><p><span>The fact that people go to the Louvre museum in Paris to see the original painting <em>Mona Lisa</em> when they can see a reproduction anywhere leads us to question some assumptions about the role of museums of fine art in today’s world</span></p><p><span>One of the most famous works of art in the world is Leonardo da Vinci’s <em>Mona Lisa</em>. Nearly everyone who goes to see the original will already be familiar with it from reproductions, but they accept that fine art is more rewardingly viewed in its original form.</span></p><p><span>However, if <em>Mona Lisa</em> was a famous novel, few people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d63b57a-69d9-4cbd-a2c6-9366eeb3d48d\" data-question=\"27\">would bother to go to a museum<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to read <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8bd4c303-a437-4288-a186-c0464dd7f444\" data-question=\"27\">the writer’s actual manuscript<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> rather than a printed reproduction. This might be explained by the fact that the novel has evolved precisely because of technological developments that made it possible to print out <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"512a24f9-1231-4606-b271-88daa3dcdc8f\" data-question=\"27\">huge numbers of texts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, whereas oil paintings have always been produced as unique objects. In addition, it could be argued that the practice of interpreting or ‘reading’ each medium follows different conventions. With novels, the reader attends mainly to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7c4c3f67-1777-4bcd-a43d-b2385713eb2d\" data-question=\"28\">the meaning of words<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> rather than the way they are printed on the page, whereas the ‘reader’ of a painting must attend just as closely to the material form of marks and shapes in the picture as to any ideas they may signify.</span></p><p><span>Yet it has always been possible to make very accurate facsimiles of pretty well any fine art work. The seven surviving versions of <em>Mona Lisa</em> bear witness to the fact that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36d212fe-dfaf-4e2e-875b-7423f9fa2fb7\" data-question=\"29\">in the 16th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, artists seemed perfectly content to assign <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"537477bd-1113-4954-b622-251d95fd828d\" data-question=\"29\">the reproduction of their creations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to their workshop apprentices as regular ‘bread and butter’ work. And <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cc026d42-87ec-4e7a-bd07-b04ef31da0dc\" data-question=\"30\">today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> the task of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48d60282-b19c-48b0-be8c-55642039c1fc\" data-question=\"30\">reproducing pictures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> is incomparably more simple and reliable, with reprographic techniques that allow <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"76bc43f0-2eb5-478a-9af7-ce5adf97b1f5\" data-question=\"30\">the production of high-quality prints made exactly to the original scale, with faithful colour values<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, and even with duplication of the surface relief of the painting.</span></p><p><span>But despite an implicit recognition that the spread of good reproductions can be culturally valuable, museums continue to promote the special status of original work.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d93ec02-5955-4240-960f-02153e392fef\" data-question=\"31\">Unfortunately, this seems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> to place severe limitations on the kind of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccb16018-efbc-41aa-bf06-0c243dcb327b\" data-question=\"31\">experience offered to visitors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>One limitation is related to the way the museum presents its exhibits. As repositories of unique historical objects, art museums are often called ‘treasure houses’. We are reminded of this even before we view a collection by the presence of security guards, attendants, ropes and display cases to keep us away from the exhibits. In many cases, the architectural style of the building further reinforces that notion. In addition, a major collection like that of London’s National Gallery is housed in numerous rooms, each with dozens of works, any one of which is likely to be worth more than all the average visitor possesses. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09b7cf2b-1515-4c9b-9ed0-b2db6e7846a0\" data-question=\"32\">a society that judges the personal status of the individual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> so much by their material worth, it is therefore difficult <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5b2fa139-62cc-41e5-9765-3b77f3a48434\" data-question=\"32\">not to be impressed by one’s own relative ‘worthlessness’<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> in such an environment.</span></p><p><span>Furthermore, consideration of the ‘value’ of the original work in its treasure house setting impresses upon the viewer that, since these works were originally produced, they have been assigned a huge monetary value by some person or institution more powerful than themselves. Evidently, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21eba396-8673-4270-ace8-f3e353552804\" data-question=\"33\">nothing the viewer thinks about the work is going to alter that value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, and so today’s viewer is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e2de6306-edea-48e0-a0aa-de58c2ec31f6\" data-question=\"33\">deterred from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> trying to extend that spontaneous, immediate, self-reliant kind of reading which would originally have met the work.</span></p><p><span>The visitor may then be struck by the strangeness of seeing such <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4f04d782-8c1e-44c9-9459-f9e459fa6cc9\" data-question=\"34\">diverse paintings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, drawings and sculptures brought together in an environment for which they were not originally created. This ‘displacement effect’ is further heightened by the sheer volume of exhibits. In the case of a major collection, there are probably more works on display than we could realistically view in weeks or even months.</span></p><p><span>This is particularly distressing because time seems to be a vital factor in the appreciation of all art forms. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6df24e1d-fd5a-4202-9c96-3f2605a81260\" data-question=\"35\">A fundamental difference between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> paintings and other art forms is that there is no prescribed time over which a painting is viewed. By contrast, the audience encourage an opera or a play over a specific time, which is the duration of the performance. Similarly novels and poems are read in a prescribed temporal sequence, whereas a picture has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aaaef346-62ab-4b52-b9f9-f0c75307b045\" data-question=\"35\">no clear place at which to start viewing, or at which to finish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Thus art works themselves encourage us to view them superficially, without appreciating the richness of detail and labour that is involved.</span></p><p><span>Consequently, the dominant critical approach becomes that of the art historian, a specialised academic approach devoted to ‘discovering the meaning’ of art within the cultural context of its time. This is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"31732a4b-0964-49db-bca1-cec2aaef998b\" data-question=\"37\">in perfect harmony with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> the museum s function, since the approach is dedicated to seeking out and conserving ‘authentic’, original, readings of the exhibits. Again, this seems to put paid to that spontaneous, participators criticism which can be found in abundance in criticism of classic works of literature, but is absent from most art history.</span></p><p><span>The displays of art museums serve as a warning of what critical practices can emerge when spontaneous criticism is suppressed. The museum public, like any other audience, experience art more rewardingly when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"433d7024-2f20-4197-8cc4-adb6227edde2\" data-question=\"38\">given the confidence to express their views<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. If appropriate works of fine art could be rendered permanently accessible to the public by means of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c88e5a5-d1b0-4167-bba6-cde5ca99c5d9\" data-question=\"39\">high-fidelity reproductions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, as literature and music already are, the public may feel somewhat less in awe of them. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9fa5469b-aa60-414c-a6b6-c0716de0f92e\" data-question=\"40\">Unfortunately, that may be too much to ask<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7591decd-4eba-4812-ba30-a009359ad3b0\" data-question=\"40\">those who seek to maintain and control the art establishment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, <strong>A-L</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-L</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>The value attached to original works of art</strong></span></h4><p><span>People go to art museums because they accept the value of seeing an original work of art. But they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d63b57a-69d9-4cbd-a2c6-9366eeb3d48d\" data-question=\"27\">do not go to museums<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to read <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8bd4c303-a437-4288-a186-c0464dd7f444\" data-question=\"27\">original manuscripts of novels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, perhaps because the availability of novels has depended on <strong>27</strong>……………… for so long, and also because with novels, the <strong>28</strong>……………… are the most important thing.</span></p><p><span>However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36d212fe-dfaf-4e2e-875b-7423f9fa2fb7\" data-question=\"29\">in historical times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> artists such as Leonardo were happy to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0bdb37f8-23ec-42be-ae65-93881bbaefa6\" data-question=\"29\">instruct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <strong>29</strong>……………….. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"537477bd-1113-4954-b622-251d95fd828d\" data-question=\"29\">produce copies of their work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cc026d42-87ec-4e7a-bd07-b04ef31da0dc\" data-question=\"30\">these days<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> new methods of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48d60282-b19c-48b0-be8c-55642039c1fc\" data-question=\"30\">reproduction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> allow <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"76bc43f0-2eb5-478a-9af7-ce5adf97b1f5\" data-question=\"30\">excellent replication of surface relief features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> as well as colour and <strong>30</strong>…………….. . </span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d93ec02-5955-4240-960f-02153e392fef\" data-question=\"31\">It is regrettable that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> museums still promote the superiority of original works of art, since this may not be in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccb16018-efbc-41aa-bf06-0c243dcb327b\" data-question=\"31\">interests of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> the <strong>31</strong>……………… .</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> institution <strong>B</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"512a24f9-1231-4606-b271-88daa3dcdc8f\" data-question=\"27\">mass production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <strong>C</strong> mechanical processes</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> public <strong>E</strong> paints <strong>F</strong> artist</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong> size <strong>H</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7c4c3f67-1777-4bcd-a43d-b2385713eb2d\" data-question=\"28\">underlying ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <strong>I </strong> basic technology</span></p><p><span><strong>J</strong> readers <strong>K</strong> picture frames <strong>L</strong> assistants</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1003\" id=\"question-wrapper-1003\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1004\" id=\"question-wrapper-1004\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1005\" id=\"question-wrapper-1005\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">L</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1006\" id=\"question-wrapper-1006\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1007\" id=\"question-wrapper-1007\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>32-35</strong> on your answer sheet</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1008\" id=\"question-wrapper-1008\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer mentions London’s National Gallery to illustrate </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the undesirable cost to a nation of maintaining a huge collection of art.</li> <li>B. the conflict that may arise in society between financial and artistic values.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09b7cf2b-1515-4c9b-9ed0-b2db6e7846a0\" data-question=\"32\">the negative effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> a museum can have on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5b2fa139-62cc-41e5-9765-3b77f3a48434\" data-question=\"32\">visitors’ opinions of themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</li> <li>D. the need to put individual well-being above large-scale artistic schemes.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1009\" id=\"question-wrapper-1009\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer says that today, viewers may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e2de6306-edea-48e0-a0aa-de58c2ec31f6\" data-question=\"33\">be unwilling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> to criticise a because </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. they lack the knowledge needed to support an opinion.</li> <li>B. they fear it may have financial implications.</li> <li>C. they have no real concept of the work’s value.</li> <li>D. they feel their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21eba396-8673-4270-ace8-f3e353552804\" data-question=\"33\">personal reaction is of no significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1010\" id=\"question-wrapper-1010\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the writer, the ‘displacement effect’ on the visitor is caused by </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4f04d782-8c1e-44c9-9459-f9e459fa6cc9\" data-question=\"34\">the variety of works<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> on display and the way they are arranged.</li> <li>B. the impossibility of viewing particular works of art over a long period.</li> <li>C. the similar nature of the paintings and the lack of great works.</li> <li>D. the inappropriate nature of the individual works selected for exhibition.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1011\" id=\"question-wrapper-1011\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer says that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6df24e1d-fd5a-4202-9c96-3f2605a81260\" data-question=\"35\">unlike<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> other forms of art, a painting does not </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. involve direct contact with an audience.</li> <li>B. require a specific location for a performance.</li> <li>C. need the involvement of other professionals.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aaaef346-62ab-4b52-b9f9-f0c75307b045\" data-question=\"35\">have a specific beginning or end<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>36-40</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if the is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1012\" id=\"question-wrapper-1012\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Art history should focus on discovering the meaning of art using a range of media. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1013\" id=\"question-wrapper-1013\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The approach of art historians <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"31732a4b-0964-49db-bca1-cec2aaef998b\" data-question=\"37\">conflicts with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> that of art museums. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1014\" id=\"question-wrapper-1014\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"433d7024-2f20-4197-8cc4-adb6227edde2\" data-question=\"38\">should be encouraged to give their opinions openly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> on works of art. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1015\" id=\"question-wrapper-1015\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Reproductions of fine art should only be sold to the public if they are of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c88e5a5-d1b0-4167-bba6-cde5ca99c5d9\" data-question=\"39\">high quality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1016\" id=\"question-wrapper-1016\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the future, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7591decd-4eba-4812-ba30-a009359ad3b0\" data-question=\"40\">those with power<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9fa5469b-aa60-414c-a6b6-c0716de0f92e\" data-question=\"40\">are likely to encourage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> more people to enjoy art. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"2d63b57a-69d9-4cbd-a2c6-9366eeb3d48d","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"do not go to museums","passagePhrase":"would bother to go to a museum"},{"uid":"8bd4c303-a437-4288-a186-c0464dd7f444","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"original manuscripts of novels","passagePhrase":"the writer’s actual manuscript"},{"uid":"512a24f9-1231-4606-b271-88daa3dcdc8f","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"mass production","passagePhrase":"huge numbers of texts"},{"uid":"7c4c3f67-1777-4bcd-a43d-b2385713eb2d","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"underlying ideas","passagePhrase":"the meaning of words"},{"uid":"36d212fe-dfaf-4e2e-875b-7423f9fa2fb7","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"in historical times","passagePhrase":"in the 16th century"},{"uid":"537477bd-1113-4954-b622-251d95fd828d","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"produce copies of their work","passagePhrase":"the reproduction of their creations"},{"uid":"cc026d42-87ec-4e7a-bd07-b04ef31da0dc","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"these days","passagePhrase":"today"},{"uid":"48d60282-b19c-48b0-be8c-55642039c1fc","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"reproduction","passagePhrase":"reproducing pictures"},{"uid":"76bc43f0-2eb5-478a-9af7-ce5adf97b1f5","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"excellent replication of surface relief features","passagePhrase":"the production of high-quality prints made exactly to the original scale, with faithful colour values"},{"uid":"5d93ec02-5955-4240-960f-02153e392fef","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"It is regrettable that","passagePhrase":"Unfortunately, this seems"},{"uid":"ccb16018-efbc-41aa-bf06-0c243dcb327b","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"interests of","passagePhrase":"experience offered to visitors"},{"uid":"09b7cf2b-1515-4c9b-9ed0-b2db6e7846a0","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"the negative effect","passagePhrase":"a society that judges the personal status of the individual"},{"uid":"5b2fa139-62cc-41e5-9765-3b77f3a48434","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"visitors’ opinions of themselves","passagePhrase":"not to be impressed by one’s own relative ‘worthlessness’"},{"uid":"21eba396-8673-4270-ace8-f3e353552804","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"personal reaction is of no significance","passagePhrase":"nothing the viewer thinks about the work is going to alter that value"},{"uid":"e2de6306-edea-48e0-a0aa-de58c2ec31f6","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"be unwilling","passagePhrase":"deterred from"},{"uid":"4f04d782-8c1e-44c9-9459-f9e459fa6cc9","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"the variety of works","passagePhrase":"diverse paintings"},{"uid":"6df24e1d-fd5a-4202-9c96-3f2605a81260","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"unlike","passagePhrase":"A fundamental difference between"},{"uid":"aaaef346-62ab-4b52-b9f9-f0c75307b045","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"have a specific beginning or end","passagePhrase":"no clear place at which to start viewing, or at which to finish"},{"uid":"433d7024-2f20-4197-8cc4-adb6227edde2","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"should be encouraged to give their opinions openly","passagePhrase":"given the confidence to express their views"},{"uid":"8c88e5a5-d1b0-4167-bba6-cde5ca99c5d9","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"high quality","passagePhrase":"high-fidelity reproductions"},{"uid":"7591decd-4eba-4812-ba30-a009359ad3b0","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"those with power","passagePhrase":"those who seek to maintain and control the art establishment"},{"uid":"0bdb37f8-23ec-42be-ae65-93881bbaefa6","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"instruct","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_193":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions</strong> <strong>1-13</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</p><h2><strong>The Context, Meaning and Scope of Tourism</strong></h2><p> </p><p><strong>A </strong></p><p>Travel has existed since the beginning of time, when primitive man set out, often traversing great distances in search of game, which provided the food and clothing necessary for his survival. Throughout the course of history, people have travelled for purposes of trade, religious conviction, economic gain, war, migration and other equally compelling motivations. In the Roman era, wealthy aristocrats and high government officials also travelled for pleasure. Seaside resorts located at Pompeii and Herculaneum afforded citizens the opportunity to escape to their vacation villas in order to avoid the summer heat of Rome. Travel, except during the Dark Ages, has continued to grow and, throughout recorded history, has played a vital role in the development of civilisations and their economies.</p><p><strong>B </strong></p><p>Tourism in the mass form as we know it today is a distinctly twentieth-century phenomenon. Historians suggest that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61d9767f-9052-4e02-9db9-7bf204292b4b\" data-question=\"1\">advent of mass tourism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> began in England during the industrial revolution with the rise of the middle class and the availability of relatively inexpensive transportation. The creation of the commercial airline industry following the Second World War and the subsequent development of the jet aircraft in the 1950s signalled the rapid growth and expansion of international travel. This growth led to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61d9767f-9052-4e02-9db9-7bf204292b4b\" data-question=\"1\">development of a major new industry: tourism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. In turn, international tourism became the concern of a number of world governments since it not only provided new employment opportunities but also produced a means of earning foreign exchange.</p><p><strong>C </strong></p><p>Tourism today has grown significantly in both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ebfdd39-08f1-46ee-85c6-39c9d447511a\" data-question=\"2\">economic and social importance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. In most industrialised countries over the past few years the fastest growth has been seen in the area of services. One of the largest segments of the service industry, although largely unrecognised as an entity in some of these countries, is travel and tourism. According to the World Travel and Tourism Council (1992), Travel and tourism is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4d7e8e8-1efc-41d6-8770-dcd0984bbdb8\" data-question=\"5\">largest industry in the world on virtually any economic measure including value-added capital investment, employment and tax contributions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. In 1992 ‘the industry’s gross output was estimated to be $3.5 trillion, over 12 per cent of all consumer spending. The travel and tourism industry is the world’s largest employer the almost 130 million jobs, or almost 7 per cent of all employees. This industry is the world’s leading industrial contributor, producing over 6 per cent of the world’s national product and accounting for capital investment in excess of $422 billion in direct indirect and personal taxes each year. Thus, tourism has a profound impact both on the world economy and, because of the educative effect of travel and the effects on employment, on society itself.</p><p><strong>D </strong></p><p>However, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3d951a9-e6b7-40b0-9ea9-1b2023a6b796\" data-question=\"3\">major problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of the travel and tourism industry that have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d1cfcb3-a144-4df1-b523-382444bb7d78\" data-question=\"3\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24416cc7-958d-467d-858e-836b13e07390\" data-question=\"8\">hidden, or obscured, its economic impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> are the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c254e37-d58c-495d-9730-05e223fe0435\" data-question=\"8\">diversity and fragmentation of the industry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> itself. The travel industry includes: hotels, motels and other types of accommodation; restaurants and other food services; transportation services and facilities; amusements, attractions and other leisure facilities; gift shops and a large number of other enterprises. Since many of these businesses also serve local residents, the impact of spending by visitors can easily be overlooked or underestimated. In addition, Meis (1992) points out that the tourism industry involves concepts that have remained amorphous to both analysts and decision makers. Moreover, in all nations this problem has made it difficult for the industry to develop any type of reliable or credible tourism information base in order to estimate the contribution it makes to regional, national and global economies. However, the nature of this very diversity makes travel and tourism ideal vehicles for economic development in a wide variety of countries, regions or communities.</p><p><strong>E </strong></p><p>Once the exclusive province of the wealthy, travel and tourism have become an institutionalised way of life for most of the population. In fact, McIntosh and Goeldner (1990) suggest that tourism has become the largest commodity in international trade for many nations and, for a significant number of other countries, it ranks second or third. For example, tourism is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b35a695d-ec63-4f8c-abd3-6c9092e32204\" data-question=\"11\">major source of income<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in Bermuda, Greece, Italy, Spain, Switzerland and most Caribbean countries. In addition, Hawkins and Ritchie, quoting from data published by the American Express Company, suggest that the travel and tourism industry is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a49a44af-5c60-4d11-b64f-2b4f37893730\" data-question=\"12\">the number one ranked employer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in the Bahamas, Brazil, Canada, France, (the former) West Germany, Hong Kong, Italy, Jamaica, Japan, Singapore, the United Kingdom and the United States. However, because of problems of definition, which directly affect <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6192cf1-3235-4cc5-93f5-8a0678a19aa6\" data-question=\"13\">statistical measurement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7347c3b5-eeaa-453e-8d40-eb9cbc21fdcf\" data-question=\"10\">it is not possible with any degree of certainty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08329e6a-2bfe-48d2-8c72-c818fba6ff73\" data-question=\"10\">provide precise, valid or reliable data<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2371691c-3c5a-4d6a-921b-1f12cd8c75c7\" data-question=\"4\">the extent of world-wide tourism participation or its economic impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. In many cases, similar difficulties arise when attempts are made to measure domestic tourism.</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has five paragraphs, <strong>A-E</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for paragraphs <strong>B-E</strong> from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct number, <strong>i-vii</strong>, in boxes <strong>1-4</strong> on your answer sheet</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Headings</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>i </strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ebfdd39-08f1-46ee-85c6-39c9d447511a\" data-question=\"2\">Economic and social significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of tourism</span></p><p><span><strong>ii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61d9767f-9052-4e02-9db9-7bf204292b4b\" data-question=\"1\">The development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of mass tourism</span></p><p><span><strong>iii</strong> Travel for the wealthy</span></p><p><span><strong>iv</strong> Earning foreign exchange through tourism</span></p><p><span><strong>v</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3d951a9-e6b7-40b0-9ea9-1b2023a6b796\" data-question=\"3\">Difficulty in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d1cfcb3-a144-4df1-b523-382444bb7d78\" data-question=\"3\">recognising the economic effects of tourism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>vi</strong> The contribution of air travel to tourism</span></p><p><span><strong>vii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2371691c-3c5a-4d6a-921b-1f12cd8c75c7\" data-question=\"4\">The world impact of tourism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>viii</strong> The history of travel</span></p><p><span><em>Example Answer</em></span></p><p><span>Paragraph <strong>A</strong> <strong>viii</strong></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21211\" id=\"question-wrapper-21211\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21212\" id=\"question-wrapper-21212\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21213\" id=\"question-wrapper-21213\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21214\" id=\"question-wrapper-21214\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>5-10</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21215\" id=\"question-wrapper-21215\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4d7e8e8-1efc-41d6-8770-dcd0984bbdb8\" data-question=\"5\">The largest employment figures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in the world are found in the travel and tourism industry. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21216\" id=\"question-wrapper-21216\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Tourism contributes over six per cent of the Australian gross national product. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21217\" id=\"question-wrapper-21217\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Tourism has a social impact because it promotes recreation. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21218\" id=\"question-wrapper-21218\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c254e37-d58c-495d-9730-05e223fe0435\" data-question=\"8\">Two main features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of the travel and tourism industry make its economic significance <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24416cc7-958d-467d-858e-836b13e07390\" data-question=\"8\">difficult to ascertain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21219\" id=\"question-wrapper-21219\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Visitor spending is always greater than the spending of residents in tourist areas. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21220\" id=\"question-wrapper-21220\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7347c3b5-eeaa-453e-8d40-eb9cbc21fdcf\" data-question=\"10\">easy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08329e6a-2bfe-48d2-8c72-c818fba6ff73\" data-question=\"10\">show statistically<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> how tourism affects individual economies. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>11-13</strong> on your answer sheet. </em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21221\" id=\"question-wrapper-21221\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In Greece, tourism the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b35a695d-ec63-4f8c-abd3-6c9092e32204\" data-question=\"11\">most important<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> …………….. . </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOURCE OF INCOME [OR] INDUSTRY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21222\" id=\"question-wrapper-21222\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The travel and tourism industry in Jamaica is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a49a44af-5c60-4d11-b64f-2b4f37893730\" data-question=\"12\">the major<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> …………….. . </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EMPLOYER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21223\" id=\"question-wrapper-21223\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The problems associated with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6192cf1-3235-4cc5-93f5-8a0678a19aa6\" data-question=\"13\">measuring international tourism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> are often reflected in the measurement of …………….. . </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DOMESTIC TOURISM</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"61d9767f-9052-4e02-9db9-7bf204292b4b","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"The development","passagePhrase":"advent of mass tourism ... development of a major new industry: tourism"},{"uid":"0ebfdd39-08f1-46ee-85c6-39c9d447511a","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Economic and social significance","passagePhrase":"economic and social importance"},{"uid":"c4d7e8e8-1efc-41d6-8770-dcd0984bbdb8","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"The largest employment figures","passagePhrase":"largest industry in the world on virtually any economic measure including value-added capital investment, employment and tax contributions"},{"uid":"b3d951a9-e6b7-40b0-9ea9-1b2023a6b796","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Difficulty in","passagePhrase":"major problems"},{"uid":"2d1cfcb3-a144-4df1-b523-382444bb7d78","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"recognising the economic effects of tourism","passagePhrase":"hidden, or obscured, its economic impact"},{"uid":"24416cc7-958d-467d-858e-836b13e07390","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"difficult to ascertain","passagePhrase":"hidden, or obscured, its economic impact"},{"uid":"0c254e37-d58c-495d-9730-05e223fe0435","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"Two main features","passagePhrase":"diversity and fragmentation of the industry"},{"uid":"b35a695d-ec63-4f8c-abd3-6c9092e32204","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"most important","passagePhrase":"major source of income"},{"uid":"a49a44af-5c60-4d11-b64f-2b4f37893730","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"the major","passagePhrase":"the number one ranked employer"},{"uid":"b6192cf1-3235-4cc5-93f5-8a0678a19aa6","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"measuring international tourism","passagePhrase":"statistical measurement"},{"uid":"08329e6a-2bfe-48d2-8c72-c818fba6ff73","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"show statistically","passagePhrase":"provide precise, valid or reliable data"},{"uid":"2371691c-3c5a-4d6a-921b-1f12cd8c75c7","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"The world impact of tourism","passagePhrase":"the extent of world-wide tourism participation or its economic impact"}]},"reading_u2_194":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Autumn leaves</strong></span></h2><p><span><em></em></span></p><p><span><em>Canadian writer Jay Ingram investigates the mystery of why leaves turn red in the fall</em></span></p><p><span><strong><span>A</span> </strong></span></p><p><span>One of the most captivating natural events of the year in many areas throughout North America is the turning of the leaves in the fall. The colours are magnificent, but the question of exactly why some trees turn yellow or orange, and others red or purple, is something which has long puzzled scientists.</span></p><p><span><strong>B </strong></span></p><p><span>Summer leaves are green <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9e0fc66-dd88-492c-9aac-c985310c57e8\" data-question=\"17\">because they are full of chlorophyll<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, the molecule that captures sunlight <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88e335b6-8578-4447-a406-5c74a7a41ba6\" data-question=\"17\">converts that energy into new building materials for the tree<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. As fall approaches in the northern hemisphere, the amount of solar energy available declines considerably. For many trees – evergreen conifers being an exception – the best strategy is to abandon photosynthesis* until the spring. So rather than maintaining the now redundant leaves throughout the winter, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9231fb52-d079-4fe2-b441-a5ddf0602aff\" data-question=\"15\">the tree saves its precious resources and discards them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. But before letting its leaves go, the tree dismantles their chlorophyll molecules and ships their valuable nitrogen back into the twigs. As chlorophyll is depleted, other colours that have been dominated by it throughout the summer begin to be revealed. This unmasking <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"919907f0-b4b7-44a1-a94e-d687eeaa7438\" data-question=\"26\">explains the autumn colours of yellow and orange<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, but not the brilliant reds and purples of trees such as the maple or sumac.</span></p><p><span><strong>C </strong></span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd09faf6-ff36-4841-a654-5a1de3f05228\" data-question=\"14\">The source of the red<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> is widely known: it is created by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d83663c7-528a-4b5f-b63c-5169a662b424\" data-question=\"14\">anthocyanins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, water-soluble plant pigments reflecting the red to blue range of the visible spectrum. They belong to a class of sugar-based chemical compounds also known as flavonoids. What’s puzzling is that anthocyanins are actually newly minted, made in the leaves at the same time as the tree is preparing to drop them. But it is hard to make sense of the manufacture of anthocyanins – why should a tree bother making new chemicals in its leaves when it’s already scrambling to withdraw and preserve the ones already there?</span></p><p><span><strong>D </strong></span></p><p><span>Some theories about anthocyanins have argued that they might act as a chemical defence against attacks by insects or fungi, or that they might attract fruit-eating birds or increase a leafs tolerance to freezing. However there are problems with each of these theories, including the fact that leaves are red for such a relatively short period that the expense of energy needed to manufacture the anthocyanins would outweigh any anti-fungal or anti-herbivore activity achieved.</span></p><p><span><strong>E </strong></span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"75c0d1cb-249c-4c69-955b-44300f0b3091\" data-question=\"18\">It has also been proposed that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> trees may produce vivid red colours to convince herbivorous insects that they are healthy and robust and would be easily able to mount chemical defences against infestation. If insects paid attention to such advertisements, they might be prompted to lay their eggs on a duller, and presumably less resistant host. The flaw in this theory lies in the lack of proof to support it. No one has as yet ascertained whether more robust trees sport the brightest leaves, or whether insects make choices according to colour intensity.</span></p><p><span><strong>F </strong></span></p><p><span>Perhaps <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c83ba325-f5a0-497b-a9d3-9e60500b4753\" data-question=\"23\">the most plausible suggestion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> as to why leaves would go to the trouble of making anthocyanins when they’re busy packing up for the winter is the theory known as the ‘light screen’ hypothesis. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aecfc85e-77c4-4825-ae53-53ba6005da13\" data-question=\"24\">sounds paradoxical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, because the idea behind this hypothesis is that the red pigment is made in autumn leaves to protect chlorophyll, the light-absorbing chemical, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8210a9c7-bc7d-40b0-971b-4330f0315e1c\" data-question=\"23\">from too much light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Why does chlorophyll need protection when it is the natural world’s supreme light absorber? Why protect chlorophyll at a time when the tree is breaking it down to salvage as much of it as possible?</span></p><p><span><strong>G </strong></span></p><p><span>Chlorophyll, although exquisitely evolved to capture the energy of sunlight, can sometimes be overwhelmed by it, especially in situations of drought, low temperatures, or nutrient deficiency. Moreover, the problem of oversensitivity to light is even more acute in the fall, when the leaf is busy preparing for winter by dismantling its internal machinery. The energy absorbed by the chlorophyll molecules of the unstable autumn leaf is not immediately channelled into useful products and processes, as it would be in an intact summer leaf. The weakened fall leaf then becomes vulnerable to the highly destructive effects of the oxygen created by the excited chlorophyll molecules.</span></p><p><span><strong>H </strong></span></p><p><span>Even if you had never suspected that this is what was going on when leaves turn red, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd92ecb2-0ba3-475f-af97-59817d0eb051\" data-question=\"16\">there are clues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> out there. One is straightforward: on many trees, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f988efd-1a56-4228-b113-90ea5a369b72\" data-question=\"19\">the leaves that are the reddest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> are those on the side of the tree which gets most sun. Not only that, but the red is brighter on the upper side of the leaf. It has also been recognised for decades that the best conditions for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e367d4b-f89f-492e-bb65-3ab5748f7408\" data-question=\"21\">intense red colours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> are dry, sunny days and cool nights, conditions that nicely match those that make leaves susceptible to excess light. And finally, trees such as maples usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"01073e7a-c7db-4ff3-b794-0a945eb47ebf\" data-question=\"22\">get much redder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the more north you <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c97bab9b-e7f0-47a5-bbde-67e6c7a7e83e\" data-question=\"22\">travel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in the northern hemisphere. It’s colder there, they’re more stressed, their chlorophyll is more sensitive and it needs more sunblock.</span></p><p><span><strong>I </strong></span></p><p><span>What is still not fully understood, however, is why some trees resort to producing red pigments while others don’t bother, and simply reveal their orange or yellow hues. Do these trees have other means at their disposal to prevent overexposure to light in autumn? Their story, though not as spectacular to the eye, will surely turn out to be as subtle and as complex.</span></p><p><span>——-</span></p><p><span>* photosynthesis: the production of new material from sunlight, water and carbon dioxide.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has nine paragraphs, <strong>A-l</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-l</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-18</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once</em>.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21224\" id=\"question-wrapper-21224\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d83663c7-528a-4b5f-b63c-5169a662b424\" data-question=\"14\">substance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> responsible for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd09faf6-ff36-4841-a654-5a1de3f05228\" data-question=\"14\">the red colouration of leaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21225\" id=\"question-wrapper-21225\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the reason why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9231fb52-d079-4fe2-b441-a5ddf0602aff\" data-question=\"15\">trees drop their leaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in autumn </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21226\" id=\"question-wrapper-21226\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd92ecb2-0ba3-475f-af97-59817d0eb051\" data-question=\"16\">some evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> to confirm a theory about the purpose of the red leaves </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21227\" id=\"question-wrapper-21227\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9e0fc66-dd88-492c-9aac-c985310c57e8\" data-question=\"17\">explanation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88e335b6-8578-4447-a406-5c74a7a41ba6\" data-question=\"17\">the function of chlorophyll<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21228\" id=\"question-wrapper-21228\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"75c0d1cb-249c-4c69-955b-44300f0b3091\" data-question=\"18\">a suggestion that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the red colouration in leaves could serve as a warning signal </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>19-22</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>Why believe the ‘light screen’ hypothesis?</strong></span></h4><p><span>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f988efd-1a56-4228-b113-90ea5a369b72\" data-question=\"19\">The most vividly coloured red leaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> are found on the side of the tree facing the <strong>19</strong>…………….. .</span></p><p><span>● The <strong>20</strong>…………… surfaces of leaves contain the most red pigment.</span></p><p><span>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e367d4b-f89f-492e-bb65-3ab5748f7408\" data-question=\"21\">Red leaves are most abundant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> when daytime weather conditions are <strong>21</strong>……………. and sunny.</span></p><p><span>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"01073e7a-c7db-4ff3-b794-0a945eb47ebf\" data-question=\"22\">The intensity of the red colour of leaves increases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> as you <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c97bab9b-e7f0-47a5-bbde-67e6c7a7e83e\" data-question=\"22\">go<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> further <strong>22</strong>……………..</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21229\" id=\"question-wrapper-21229\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SUN(LIGHT)</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21230\" id=\"question-wrapper-21230\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">UPPER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21231\" id=\"question-wrapper-21231\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DRY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21232\" id=\"question-wrapper-21232\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NORTH</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>23-25</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21236\" id=\"question-wrapper-21236\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c83ba325-f5a0-497b-a9d3-9e60500b4753\" data-question=\"23\">likely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> that the red pigments help to protect the leaf from <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8210a9c7-bc7d-40b0-971b-4330f0315e1c\" data-question=\"23\">freezing temperatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21237\" id=\"question-wrapper-21237\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The ‘light screen’ hypothesis would initially <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aecfc85e-77c4-4825-ae53-53ba6005da13\" data-question=\"24\">seem to contradict<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> what is known about chlorophyll. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21238\" id=\"question-wrapper-21238\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Leaves which turn colours other than red are more likely to be damaged by sunlight. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Choose the correct letter <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</p><p><em>Write the correct letter in box <strong>26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21239\" id=\"question-wrapper-21239\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> For which of the following questions does the writer offer an explanation? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. why conifers remain green in winter</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"919907f0-b4b7-44a1-a94e-d687eeaa7438\" data-question=\"26\">how leaves turn orange and yellow in autumn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></li> <li>C. how herbivorous insects choose which trees to lay their eggs in</li> <li>D. why anthocyanins are restricted to certain trees</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e9e0fc66-dd88-492c-9aac-c985310c57e8","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"explanation","passagePhrase":"because they are full of chlorophyll"},{"uid":"88e335b6-8578-4447-a406-5c74a7a41ba6","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"the function of chlorophyll","passagePhrase":"converts that energy into new building materials for the tree"},{"uid":"9231fb52-d079-4fe2-b441-a5ddf0602aff","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"trees drop their leaves","passagePhrase":"the tree saves its precious resources and discards them"},{"uid":"919907f0-b4b7-44a1-a94e-d687eeaa7438","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"how leaves turn orange and yellow in autumn","passagePhrase":"explains the autumn colours of yellow and orange"},{"uid":"dd09faf6-ff36-4841-a654-5a1de3f05228","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"the red colouration of leaves","passagePhrase":"The source of the red"},{"uid":"d83663c7-528a-4b5f-b63c-5169a662b424","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"substance","passagePhrase":"anthocyanins"},{"uid":"75c0d1cb-249c-4c69-955b-44300f0b3091","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"a suggestion that","passagePhrase":"It has also been proposed that"},{"uid":"c83ba325-f5a0-497b-a9d3-9e60500b4753","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"likely","passagePhrase":"the most plausible suggestion"},{"uid":"aecfc85e-77c4-4825-ae53-53ba6005da13","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"seem to contradict","passagePhrase":"sounds paradoxical"},{"uid":"fd92ecb2-0ba3-475f-af97-59817d0eb051","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"some evidence","passagePhrase":"there are clues"},{"uid":"6f988efd-1a56-4228-b113-90ea5a369b72","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"The most vividly coloured red leaves","passagePhrase":"the leaves that are the reddest"},{"uid":"5e367d4b-f89f-492e-bb65-3ab5748f7408","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Red leaves are most abundant","passagePhrase":"intense red colours"},{"uid":"01073e7a-c7db-4ff3-b794-0a945eb47ebf","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"The intensity of the red colour of leaves increases","passagePhrase":"get much redder"},{"uid":"c97bab9b-e7f0-47a5-bbde-67e6c7a7e83e","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"go","passagePhrase":"travel"}]},"reading_u2_195":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</p><p> </p><h2><strong>Beyond the blue horizon</strong></h2><p> </p><p><em>Ancient voyagers who settled the far-flung islands of the Pacific Ocean</em></p><p>An important archaeological <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4785338d-38d9-454a-8886-69bee09c03b7\" data-question=\"28\">discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> on the island of Efate in the Pacific archipelago of Vanuatu has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4785338d-38d9-454a-8886-69bee09c03b7\" data-question=\"28\">revealed traces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of an ancient seafaring people, the distant ancestors of today’s Polynesians. The site came to light <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fdea10f-12d0-43d4-864e-c9dba972256d\" data-question=\"28\">only by chance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. An agricultural worker, digging in the grounds of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"259f59c8-5f4a-4be1-be32-22f394f5f763\" data-question=\"27\">derelict<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> plantation, scraped open a grave – the first of dozens in a burial ground some 3,000 years old. It is the oldest cemetery ever found in the Pacific islands, and it harbors the remains of an ancient people archaeologists call the Lapita.</p><p>They were daring blue-water adventurers who used basic canoes to rove across the ocean. But they were not just explorers. They were also pioneers who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b728cfb9-c2a4-4cf6-bc1e-66a07cbde86f\" data-question=\"29\">carried<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> with them everything they would need to build new lives – their livestock, taro seedlings and stone tools. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"49324ede-ac99-438f-bb5a-e8448f83f087\" data-question=\"29\">Within the span of several centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, the Lapita <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ebbdcea-9f63-4057-8f46-817092e375df\" data-question=\"29\">stretched the boundaries of their world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> from the jungle-clad volcanoes of Papua New Guinea to the loneliest coral outliers of Tonga.</p><p>The Lapita left precious few clues about themselves, but Efate expands the volume of data available to researchers dramatically. The remains of 62 individuals have been uncovered so far, and archaeologists were also thrilled to find six complete Lapita pots. Other items included a Lapita burial urn with modeled birds arranged on the rim as though peering down at the human remains <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"926f6600-9ced-41ad-9e3a-6e8510bddc8c\" data-question=\"31\">sealed inside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1527ece-c74d-410e-861a-ca8fb084d03d\" data-question=\"30\">It’s an important discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>,’ says Matthew Spriggs, professor of archaeology at the Australian National University and head of the international team digging up the site, ‘for it conclusively identifies the remains as Lapita.’</p><p>DNA teased from these human remains may help answer one of the most puzzling questions in Pacific anthropology: did all Pacific islanders spring from one source or many? Was there only one outward migration from a single point in Asia, or several from different points? ‘This represents the best opportunity we’ve had yet,’ says Spriggs, ‘to find out who the Lapita actually were, where they came from, and who their closest descendants are today.’</p><p>There is one stubborn question for which archaeology has yet to provide any answers: how did the Lapita accomplish <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1f5b03f-f8a0-47a5-b939-7eb7618a26e9\" data-question=\"32\">the ancient equivalent of a moon landing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, many times over? No-one has found one of their canoes or any rigging, which could reveal how the canoes were sailed. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33aa72d7-c036-4de0-9ff6-08ccd1074118\" data-question=\"32\">Nor do the oral histories and traditions of later Polynesians offer any insights<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, for they turn into myths long before they reach as far back in time as the Lapita.</p><p>‘All we can say for certain is that the Lapita had canoes that were capable of ocean voyages, and they had the ability to sail them,’ says Geoff Irwin, a professor of archaeology at the University of Auckland. Those sailing skills, he says, were developed and passed down over thousands of years by earlier mariners who worked their way through the archipelagoes of the western Pacific, making short crossings to nearby islands. The real adventure didn’t begin, however, until their Lapita descendants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b2f5f97-2619-47e6-9def-99aa10a1322c\" data-question=\"33\">sailed out of sight of land, with empty horizons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> on every side. This must have been as difficult for them as landing on the moon is for us today. Certainly it distinguished them from their ancestors, but what gave them the courage to launch out on such risky voyages?</p><p>The Lapita's thrust into the Pacific was eastward, against the prevailing trade winds, Irwin notes. Those nagging headwinds, he argues, may have been the key to their success. ‘They could sail out for days into the unknown and assess the area, secure in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"321dcc57-88c8-4581-84d8-aad8e6ad2237\" data-question=\"34\">the knowledge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> that if they didn’t find anything, they could turn about and catch a swift ride back on the trade winds. This is what would have made the whole thing work.’ Once out there, skilled seafarers would have detected abundant leads to follow to land: seabirds, coconuts and twigs carried out to sea by the tides, and the afternoon pile-up of clouds on the horizon which often indicates an island in the distance.</p><p>For returning explorers, successful or not, the geography of their own archipelagoes would have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e1b6af6-20b2-4cb3-b74d-ce7d7fd45e5b\" data-question=\"35\">provided a safety net<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e1b6af6-20b2-4cb3-b74d-ce7d7fd45e5b\" data-question=\"35\">Without this to go by, overshooting their home ports, getting lost and sailing off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> into eternity would have been all too easy. Vanuatu, for example, stretches more than 500 miles in a northwest-southeast trend, its scores of intervisible islands forming a backstop for mariners riding the trade winds home.</p><p>All this presupposes one essential detail, says Atholl Anderson, professor of prehistory at the Australian National University: the Lapita had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11fb0c64-8aab-42ae-b940-95e760a50e3f\" data-question=\"36\">mastered the advanced art of sailing against the wind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. ‘And <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7441c1f2-3504-48dd-8aad-b28c80c6f2ab\" data-question=\"36\">there’s no proof<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> they could do any such thing,’ Anderson says. ‘There has been this assumption they did, and people have built canoes to re-create those early voyages based on that assumption. But nobody has any idea what their canoes looked like or how they were rigged.’</p><p>Rather than give all the credit to human skill, Anderson invokes the winds of chance. El Nino, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89db4c2b-d14d-40b8-a039-6ce9babf9354\" data-question=\"37\">the same climate disruption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> that affects the Pacific today, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02e0cfd5-7062-4708-ae86-5a4a64ef52ef\" data-question=\"37\">may have helped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> scatter the Lapita, Anderson suggests. He points out that climate data obtained from slow-growing corals around the Pacific indicate a series of unusually frequent El Ninos around the time of the Lapita expansion. By reversing the regular east-to-west flow of the trade winds for weeks at a time, these super El Ninos might have taken the Lapita on long unplanned voyages.</p><p>However they did it, the Lapita spread themselves a third of the way across the Pacific, then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa0c5e26-6685-4487-b095-d9f1bac1401d\" data-question=\"39\">called it quits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d477694-4c91-4dad-b329-696fcb83c994\" data-question=\"39\">for reasons known only to them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Ahead lay the vast emptiness of the central Pacific and perhaps they were too thinly stretched to venture farther. They probably never numbered more than a few thousand in total, and in their rapid migration eastward they encountered hundreds of islands – more than 300 in Fiji alone.</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words and phrases, <strong>A-J</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-J</strong>, in boxes <strong>37-31</strong> on your sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>The Éfaté burial site</strong></span></h4><p><span>A 3,000-year-old burial ground of a seafaring people called the Lapita has been found on an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"259f59c8-5f4a-4be1-be32-22f394f5f763\" data-question=\"27\">abandoned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <strong>27</strong>……………. on the Pacific island of Efate. The cemetery, which is a significant <strong>28</strong>…………….. , was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4785338d-38d9-454a-8886-69bee09c03b7\" data-question=\"28\">uncovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fdea10f-12d0-43d4-864e-c9dba972256d\" data-question=\"28\">accidentally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> by an agricultural worker.</span></p><p><span>The Lapita explored and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ebbdcea-9f63-4057-8f46-817092e375df\" data-question=\"29\">colonised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> many Pacific islands <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"49324ede-ac99-438f-bb5a-e8448f83f087\" data-question=\"29\">over several centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b728cfb9-c2a4-4cf6-bc1e-66a07cbde86f\" data-question=\"29\">took<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> many things with them on their voyages including <strong>29</strong>……………… and tools.</span></p><p><span>The burial ground increases the amount of information about the Lapita available to scientists. A team of researchers, led by Matthew Spriggs from the Australian National University, are helping with the excavation of the site. Spriggs believes the <strong>30</strong>………………. which was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1527ece-c74d-410e-861a-ca8fb084d03d\" data-question=\"30\">found at the site is very important<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> since it confirms that the <strong>31</strong>……………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"926f6600-9ced-41ad-9e3a-6e8510bddc8c\" data-question=\"31\">found inside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> are Lapita.</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> proof</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> plantation</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> harbour</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> bones</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> data</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong> archaeological discovery</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong> burial urn</span></p><p><span><strong>H</strong> source</span></p><p><span><strong>I</strong> animals</span></p><p><span><strong>J</strong> maps</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21240\" id=\"question-wrapper-21240\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21241\" id=\"question-wrapper-21241\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21242\" id=\"question-wrapper-21242\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21243\" id=\"question-wrapper-21243\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21244\" id=\"question-wrapper-21244\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Choose the correct letter <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</p><p><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>32-35</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21245\" id=\"question-wrapper-21245\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the writer, there are difficulties explaining how the Lapita accomplished <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1f5b03f-f8a0-47a5-b939-7eb7618a26e9\" data-question=\"32\">their journeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> because </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the canoes that have been discovered offer relatively few clues.</li> <li>B. archaeologists have shown limited interest in this area of research.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33aa72d7-c036-4de0-9ff6-08ccd1074118\" data-question=\"32\">little information relating to this period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33aa72d7-c036-4de0-9ff6-08ccd1074118\" data-question=\"32\">relied upon for accuracy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</li> <li>D. technological advances have altered the way such achievements are viewed.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21246\" id=\"question-wrapper-21246\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the sixth paragraph, what was extraordinary about the Lapita? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b2f5f97-2619-47e6-9def-99aa10a1322c\" data-question=\"33\">sailed beyond the point where land was visible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Their cultural heritage discouraged the expression of fear.</li> <li>C. They were able to build canoes that withstood ocean voyages.</li> <li>D. Their navigational skills were passed on from one generation to the next.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21247\" id=\"question-wrapper-21247\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does ‘This’ refer to in the seventh paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the Lapita’s seafaring talent</li> <li>B. the Lapita s ability to detect signs of land</li> <li>C. the Lapita’s extensive knowledge of the region</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"321dcc57-88c8-4581-84d8-aad8e6ad2237\" data-question=\"34\">the Lapita’s belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> they would be able to return home</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21248\" id=\"question-wrapper-21248\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the eighth paragraph, how was the geography of the region significant? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It played an important role in Lapita culture.</li> <li>B. It meant there were relatively few storms at sea.</li> <li>C. It provided a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e1b6af6-20b2-4cb3-b74d-ce7d7fd45e5b\" data-question=\"35\">navigational aid for the Lapita<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</li> <li>D. It made a large number of islands habitable.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>36-40</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21249\" id=\"question-wrapper-21249\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7441c1f2-3504-48dd-8aad-b28c80c6f2ab\" data-question=\"36\">It is now clear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that the Lapita could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11fb0c64-8aab-42ae-b940-95e760a50e3f\" data-question=\"36\">sail into a prevailing wind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21250\" id=\"question-wrapper-21250\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89db4c2b-d14d-40b8-a039-6ce9babf9354\" data-question=\"37\">Extreme climate conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> may have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02e0cfd5-7062-4708-ae86-5a4a64ef52ef\" data-question=\"37\">played a role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in Lapita migration. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21251\" id=\"question-wrapper-21251\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Lapita learnt to predict the duration of El Ninos. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21252\" id=\"question-wrapper-21252\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d477694-4c91-4dad-b329-696fcb83c994\" data-question=\"39\">remains unclear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> why the Lapita <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa0c5e26-6685-4487-b095-d9f1bac1401d\" data-question=\"39\">halted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> their expansion across the Pacific. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21253\" id=\"question-wrapper-21253\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is likely that the majority of Lapita settled on Fiji. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"4785338d-38d9-454a-8886-69bee09c03b7","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"uncovered","passagePhrase":"discovery ... revealed traces"},{"uid":"2fdea10f-12d0-43d4-864e-c9dba972256d","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"accidentally","passagePhrase":"only by chance"},{"uid":"259f59c8-5f4a-4be1-be32-22f394f5f763","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"abandoned","passagePhrase":"derelict"},{"uid":"b728cfb9-c2a4-4cf6-bc1e-66a07cbde86f","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"took","passagePhrase":"carried"},{"uid":"49324ede-ac99-438f-bb5a-e8448f83f087","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"over several centuries","passagePhrase":"Within the span of several centuries"},{"uid":"8ebbdcea-9f63-4057-8f46-817092e375df","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"colonised","passagePhrase":"stretched the boundaries of their world"},{"uid":"926f6600-9ced-41ad-9e3a-6e8510bddc8c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"found inside","passagePhrase":"sealed inside"},{"uid":"a1527ece-c74d-410e-861a-ca8fb084d03d","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"found at the site is very important","passagePhrase":"It’s an important discovery"},{"uid":"c1f5b03f-f8a0-47a5-b939-7eb7618a26e9","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"their journeys","passagePhrase":"the ancient equivalent of a moon landing"},{"uid":"33aa72d7-c036-4de0-9ff6-08ccd1074118","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"little information relating to this period ... relied upon for accuracy","passagePhrase":"Nor do the oral histories and traditions of later Polynesians offer any insights"},{"uid":"4b2f5f97-2619-47e6-9def-99aa10a1322c","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"sailed beyond the point where land was visible","passagePhrase":"sailed out of sight of land, with empty horizons"},{"uid":"321dcc57-88c8-4581-84d8-aad8e6ad2237","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"the Lapita’s belief","passagePhrase":"the knowledge"},{"uid":"8e1b6af6-20b2-4cb3-b74d-ce7d7fd45e5b","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"navigational aid for the Lapita","passagePhrase":"provided a safety net ... Without this to go by, overshooting their home ports, getting lost and sailing off"},{"uid":"11fb0c64-8aab-42ae-b940-95e760a50e3f","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"sail into a prevailing wind","passagePhrase":"mastered the advanced art of sailing against the wind"},{"uid":"89db4c2b-d14d-40b8-a039-6ce9babf9354","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"Extreme climate conditions","passagePhrase":"the same climate disruption"},{"uid":"02e0cfd5-7062-4708-ae86-5a4a64ef52ef","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"played a role","passagePhrase":"may have helped"},{"uid":"fa0c5e26-6685-4487-b095-d9f1bac1401d","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"halted","passagePhrase":"called it quits"},{"uid":"1d477694-4c91-4dad-b329-696fcb83c994","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"remains unclear","passagePhrase":"for reasons known only to them"}]},"reading_u2_196":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><h2><span><strong>The megafires of California</strong></span></h2><p><span><em></em></span></p><p><span><em>Drought, housing expansion, and oversupply of tinder make for bigger, hotter fires in the western United States</em></span></p><p><span>Wildfires are becoming an increasing menace in the western United States, with Southern California being the hardest hit area. There’s a reason fire squads battling more frequent blazes in Southern California are having such difficulty containing the flames, despite better preparedness than ever and decades of experience fighting fires fanned by the ‘Santa Ana Winds’. The wildfires themselves, experts say, are generally hotter, faster, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"76d679db-1d46-4e71-91d2-ec9f0a71f28e\" data-question=\"1\">spread more erratically<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> than in the past.</span></p><p><span>Megafires, also called ‘siege fires’, are the increasingly frequent blazes that burn 500,000 acres or more – 10 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cfd2b5a-43a8-497b-aa73-f003713659c4\" data-question=\"2\">times the size of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the average forest fire of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4242230f-1067-4b29-9b52-ed7e62ae3cb9\" data-question=\"2\">20 years ago<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Some recent wildfires are among the biggest ever in California in terms of acreage burned, according to state figures and news reports.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5709c986-f227-4db0-8046-f66e5e987b4c\" data-question=\"3\">One explanation for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the trend to more superhot fires is that the region, which usually has dry summers, has had significantly below normal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ee2be8c-b2e9-40c3-a2e6-f337400fca2f\" data-question=\"3\">precipitation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> in many recent years. Another reason, experts say, is related to the century- long policy of the US Forest Service to stop wildfires as quickly as possible.</span></p><p><span>The unintentional consequence has been to halt the natural eradication of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f95a7b7c-c199-44b4-a46e-62949158e926\" data-question=\"4\">underbrush<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, now the primary fuel for megafires.</span></p><p><span>Three other factors contribute to the trend, they add. First is climate change, marked by a 1-degree Fahrenheit rise in average yearly temperature across the western states. Second is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93202072-2302-4afc-92be-7261f818d3f3\" data-question=\"5\">fire seasons that on average are 78 days longer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> than they were 20 years ago. Third is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"117ffc21-5b37-4714-a412-acc340529535\" data-question=\"6\">increased construction of homes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> in wooded areas.</span></p><p><span>‘We are increasingly building our homes in fire-prone ecosystems,’ says Dominik Kulakowski, adjunct professor of biology at Clark University Graduate School of Geography in Worcester, Massachusetts. ‘Doing that in many of the forests of the western US is like building homes on the side of an active volcano.’</span></p><p><span>In California, where population growth has averaged more than 600,000 a year <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b588228a-cd4b-4f87-9082-18defdf3fb4b\" data-question=\"7\">for at least a decade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, more residential housing is being built. ‘What once was open space is now residential homes providing fuel to make fires burn with greater intensity,’ says Terry McHale of the California Department of Forestry firefighters’ union. ‘With so much dryness, so many communities to catch fire, so many fronts to fight, it becomes an almost incredible job.’</span></p><p><span>That said, many experts give California <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0f9b10b4-702e-4e21-8e3c-eef50e606e52\" data-question=\"8\">high marks for making progress on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> preparedness in recent years, after some of the largest fires in state history scorched thousands of acres, burned thousands of homes, and killed numerous people. Stung in the past by criticism of bungling that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c6a3909-2461-4d00-bdb6-eab9779a69b4\" data-question=\"9\">allowed fires to spread when they might have been contained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, personnel are meeting the peculiar challenges of neighborhood – and canyon- hopping fires better than previously, observers say.</span></p><p><span>State promises to provide more up-to-date engines, planes, and helicopters to fight fires have been fulfilled. Firefighters’ unions that in the past complained of dilapidated equipment, old fire engines, and insufficient blueprints for fire safety are now praising the state’s commitment, noting that funding for firefighting has increased, despite huge cuts in many other programs. ‘We are pleased that the current state administration has been very proactive in its support of us, and [has] come through with budgetary support of the infrastructure needs we have long sought,’ says Mr. McHale of the firefighters’ union.</span></p><p><span>Besides providing money to upgrade the fire engines that must traverse the mammoth state and wind along serpentine canyon roads, the state has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3650c143-2dd0-4a63-87b8-f23bd150a2e4\" data-question=\"10\">invested in better command-and-control facilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> as well as in the strategies to run them. ‘In the fire sieges of earlier years, we found that other jurisdictions and states were willing to offer mutual-aid help, but we were not able to communicate adequately with them,’ says Kim Zagaris, chief of the state’s Office of Emergency Services Fire and Rescue Branch.</span></p><p><span>After a commission examined and revamped communications procedures, the statewide response ‘has become far more professional and responsive,’ he says. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e8932b8e-03b8-42dc-8138-a8af590850d8\" data-question=\"12\">There is a sense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> among both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbc50df5-fd5f-4c65-aa49-b5e6a9884c71\" data-question=\"12\">government officials and residents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> that the speed, dedication, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68d7a4b5-18ea-4adc-8653-0b6153e89423\" data-question=\"12\">coordination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> of firefighters from several states and jurisdictions are resulting in greater efficiency than in past ‘siege fire’ situations.</span></p><p><span>In recent years, the Southern California region has improved building codes, evacuation procedures, and procurement of new technology. ‘I am extraordinarily impressed by the improvements we have witnessed,’ says Randy Jacobs, a Southern California- based lawyer who has had to evacuate both his home and business to escape wildfires. ‘Notwithstanding all the damage that will continue to be caused by wildfires, we will <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"bc71e370-1891-4d0f-a725-077550dc220c\" data-question=\"13\">no longer suffer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the loss of life endured in the past because of the fire prevention and firefighting measures that have been put in place,’ he says.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>1-6</strong> on your answer sheet. </em></span></p><h4><span><strong>Wildfires </strong></span></h4><p><span><span>● </span>Characteristics of wildfires and wildfire conditions today compared to the past:</span></p><p><span>– occurrence: more frequent</span></p><p><span>– temperature: hotter</span></p><p><span>– speed: faster</span></p><p><span>– movement: <strong>1</strong>……………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"76d679db-1d46-4e71-91d2-ec9f0a71f28e\" data-question=\"1\">more unpredictably<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p><p><span>– size of fires: <strong>2</strong>……………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cfd2b5a-43a8-497b-aa73-f003713659c4\" data-question=\"2\">greater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> on average than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4242230f-1067-4b29-9b52-ed7e62ae3cb9\" data-question=\"2\">two decades ago<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p><p><span><span>● </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5709c986-f227-4db0-8046-f66e5e987b4c\" data-question=\"3\">Reasons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> wildfires cause more damage today compared to the past:</span></p><p><span>– <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ee2be8c-b2e9-40c3-a2e6-f337400fca2f\" data-question=\"3\">rainfall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>: <strong>3</strong>……………. average</span></p><p><span>– <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f95a7b7c-c199-44b4-a46e-62949158e926\" data-question=\"4\">more brush<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to act as <strong>4</strong>……………..</span></p><p><span>– increase in yearly temperature</span></p><p><span>– <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93202072-2302-4afc-92be-7261f818d3f3\" data-question=\"5\">extended fire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <strong>5</strong>……………..</span></p><p><span>– <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"117ffc21-5b37-4714-a412-acc340529535\" data-question=\"6\">more building of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <strong>6</strong>……………. in vulnerable places </span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1060\" id=\"question-wrapper-1060\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPREAD</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1061\" id=\"question-wrapper-1061\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">10/TEN TIMES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1062\" id=\"question-wrapper-1062\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BELOW</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1063\" id=\"question-wrapper-1063\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FUEL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1064\" id=\"question-wrapper-1064\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SEASONS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1065\" id=\"question-wrapper-1065\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HOMES/HOUSING</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>7-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1066\" id=\"question-wrapper-1066\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The amount of open space in California has diminished <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b588228a-cd4b-4f87-9082-18defdf3fb4b\" data-question=\"7\">over the last ten years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1067\" id=\"question-wrapper-1067\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Many experts believe California <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0f9b10b4-702e-4e21-8e3c-eef50e606e52\" data-question=\"8\">has made little progress in readying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> itself to fight fires. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1068\" id=\"question-wrapper-1068\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Personnel in the past have been criticised for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c6a3909-2461-4d00-bdb6-eab9779a69b4\" data-question=\"9\">mishandling fire containment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1069\" id=\"question-wrapper-1069\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> California has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3650c143-2dd0-4a63-87b8-f23bd150a2e4\" data-question=\"10\">replaced a range of firefighting tools<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1070\" id=\"question-wrapper-1070\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> More firefighters have been hired to improve fire-fighting capacity. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1071\" id=\"question-wrapper-1071\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbc50df5-fd5f-4c65-aa49-b5e6a9884c71\" data-question=\"12\">Citizens and government groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e8932b8e-03b8-42dc-8138-a8af590850d8\" data-question=\"12\">disapprove of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> the efforts of different states and agencies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68d7a4b5-18ea-4adc-8653-0b6153e89423\" data-question=\"12\">working together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1072\" id=\"question-wrapper-1072\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Randy Jacobs believes that loss of life from fires will <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"bc71e370-1891-4d0f-a725-077550dc220c\" data-question=\"13\">continue at the same levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, despite changes made. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"76d679db-1d46-4e71-91d2-ec9f0a71f28e","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"more unpredictably","passagePhrase":"spread more erratically"},{"uid":"5cfd2b5a-43a8-497b-aa73-f003713659c4","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"greater","passagePhrase":"times the size of"},{"uid":"4242230f-1067-4b29-9b52-ed7e62ae3cb9","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"two decades ago","passagePhrase":"20 years ago"},{"uid":"5709c986-f227-4db0-8046-f66e5e987b4c","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Reasons","passagePhrase":"One explanation for"},{"uid":"8ee2be8c-b2e9-40c3-a2e6-f337400fca2f","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"rainfall","passagePhrase":"precipitation"},{"uid":"f95a7b7c-c199-44b4-a46e-62949158e926","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"more brush","passagePhrase":"underbrush"},{"uid":"93202072-2302-4afc-92be-7261f818d3f3","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"extended fire","passagePhrase":"fire seasons that on average are 78 days longer"},{"uid":"117ffc21-5b37-4714-a412-acc340529535","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"more building of","passagePhrase":"increased construction of homes"},{"uid":"b588228a-cd4b-4f87-9082-18defdf3fb4b","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"over the last ten years","passagePhrase":"for at least a decade"},{"uid":"2c6a3909-2461-4d00-bdb6-eab9779a69b4","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"mishandling fire containment","passagePhrase":"allowed fires to spread when they might have been contained"},{"uid":"3650c143-2dd0-4a63-87b8-f23bd150a2e4","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"replaced a range of firefighting tools","passagePhrase":"invested in better command-and-control facilities"},{"uid":"bbc50df5-fd5f-4c65-aa49-b5e6a9884c71","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Citizens and government groups","passagePhrase":"government officials and residents"},{"uid":"68d7a4b5-18ea-4adc-8653-0b6153e89423","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"working together","passagePhrase":"coordination"}]},"reading_u2_197":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Second nature</strong></span></h2><p><span><em></em></span></p><p><span><em>Your personality isn’t necessarily set in stone. With a little experimentation, people can reshape their temperaments and inject passion, optimism, joy and courage into their lives</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A </strong></span></p><p><span>Psychologists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe3c6156-e024-4ed0-bf8b-a2be6bc5c7cb\" data-question=\"14\">have long held that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> a person’s character <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5822652-8acd-457c-9bfb-82c601cef257\" data-question=\"14\">cannot undergo a transformation in any meaningful way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c5224579-430d-4cf4-9cdd-09704f5de2b2\" data-question=\"15\">key traits of personality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"288d710b-a170-4dce-ae4a-e75324b00c73\" data-question=\"15\">determined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> at a very young age. However, researchers have begun looking more closely at ways we can change. Positive psychologists have identified 24 qualities we admire, such as loyalty and kindness, and are studying them to find out why they come so naturally to some people. What they’re discovering is that many of these qualities amount to habitual behaviour that determines the way we respond to the world. The good news is that all this can be learned.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b2bbb953-e402-4f54-b9d6-6f8d0a10db4d\" data-question=\"16\">Some qualities are less challenging to develop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> than others, optimism being one of them. However, developing qualities <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c160aef-ea4c-45fc-9e6a-976fc2744590\" data-question=\"17\">requires mastering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee70b29e-4497-4baa-a0aa-7c062c040491\" data-question=\"17\">a range of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> skills which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"984d0168-e9d5-4a60-b9e6-01e7f6a69d53\" data-question=\"17\">diverse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and sometimes surprising. For example, to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69ad46c8-5349-4dfa-a45a-373a54c1b17b\" data-question=\"18\">bring more joy and passion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> into your life, you <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c898ba4-899e-467c-aff2-cbbe231c3a2b\" data-question=\"18\">must be open to experiencing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> negative emotions. Cultivating such qualities will help you realise your full potential.</span></p><p><span><strong>B </strong></span></p><p><span>‘The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f23968a4-5df1-4aab-a228-e51019a05945\" data-question=\"22\">evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> is good that most personality traits can be altered,’ says Christopher Peterson, professor of psychology at the University of Michigan, who cites himself as an example. Inherently introverted, he realised early on that as an academic, his reticence would prove disastrous in the lecture hall. So he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62392c0f-3601-42fa-8a10-e50326bc9580\" data-question=\"22\">learned to be more outgoing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and to entertain his classes. ‘Now my extroverted behaviour is spontaneous,’ he says.</span></p><p><span><strong>C </strong></span></p><p><span>David Fajgenbaum had to make a similar transition. He was preparing for university, when he had an accident that put an end to his sports career. On campus, he quickly found that beyond ordinary counselling, the university had no services for students who were undergoing physical rehabilitation and suffering from depression like him. He therefore launched <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93533bbd-0a0e-4fc4-b846-af6558a21480\" data-question=\"24\">a support group to help others in similar situations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. He took action despite his own pain – a typical response of an optimist.</span></p><p><span><strong>D </strong></span></p><p><span>Suzanne Segerstrom, professor of psychology at the University of Kentucky, believes that the key to increasing optimism is through cultivating optimistic behaviour, rather than positive thinking. She recommends you train yourself to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ad7283b-a83f-4041-850c-f98db9f7c086\" data-question=\"20\">pay attention to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> good fortune by writing down three positive things that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26821b77-c850-4d41-93e7-f8b6e01db1dd\" data-question=\"20\">come about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> each day. This will help you convince yourself that favourable outcomes actually happen all the time, making it easier to begin taking action.</span></p><p><span><strong>E </strong></span></p><p><span>You can recognise a person who is passionate about a pursuit by the way they are so strongly involved in it. Tanya Streeter’s passion is freediving – the sport of plunging deep into the water without tanks or other breathing equipment. Beginning in 1998, she set nine world records and can hold her breath for six minutes. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c329156-5ec0-457b-a382-78af2f6f2cd9\" data-question=\"23\">The physical stamina<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> required for this sport is intense but the psychological demands are even more overwhelming. Streeter <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eb69569f-6b87-4b51-a872-6e2e29c13faf\" data-question=\"23\">learned to untangle her fears from her judgment of what her body and mind could do<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. ‘In my career as a competitive freediver, there was a limit to what I could do – but it wasn’t anywhere near what I thought it was/ she says.</span></p><p><span><strong>F </strong></span></p><p><span>Finding a pursuit that excites you can improve anyone’s life. The secret about consuming passions, though, according to psychologist Paul Silvia of the University of North Carolina, is that ‘they require discipline, hard work and ability, which is why they are so rewarding.’ Psychologist Todd Kashdan has this advice for those people taking up a new passion: ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e17c345-9e46-4d5e-a2a7-addade831d64\" data-question=\"19\">As a newcomer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, you also have to tolerate and laugh at your own ignorance. You must be willing to accept the negative feelings that come your way,’ he says.</span></p><p><span><strong>G </strong></span></p><p><span>In 2004, physician-scientist Mauro Zappaterra began his PhD research at Harvard Medical School. Unfortunately, he was miserable as his research wasn’t compatible with his curiosity about healing. He finally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8213f935-1499-4460-a720-aa1d6dd3a304\" data-question=\"25\">took a break<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and during eight months in Santa Fe, Zappaterra l<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8213f935-1499-4460-a720-aa1d6dd3a304\" data-question=\"25\">earned about alternative healing techniques<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> not taught at Harvard. When he got back, he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8213f935-1499-4460-a720-aa1d6dd3a304\" data-question=\"25\">switched labs to study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> how cerebrospinal fluid nourishes the developing nervous system. He also vowed to look for the joy in everything, including failure, as this could help him learn about his research and himself.</span></p><p><span>One thing that can hold joy back is a person’s concentration on avoiding failure rather than their looking forward to doing something well. ‘Focusing on being safe might get in the way of your reaching your goals,’ explains Kashdan. For example, are you hoping to get through a business lunch without embarrassing yourself, or are you thinking about how fascinating the conversation might be?</span></p><p><span><strong>H </strong></span></p><p><span>Usually, we think of courage in physical terms but ordinary life demands something else. For marketing executive Kenneth Pedeleose, it meant speaking out against something he thought was ethically wrong. The new manager was intimidating staff so Pedeleose carefully recorded each instance of bullying and eventually took the evidence to a senior director, knowing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48a20030-ca8f-4e5d-807b-2f4499947faa\" data-question=\"26\">his own job security would be threatened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Eventually the manager was the one to go. According to Cynthia Pury, a psychologist at Clemson University, Pedeleose’s story proves the point that courage is not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"703ac5ea-e65f-44db-a5da-25638a31c3d2\" data-question=\"21\">motivated by fearlessness, but by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24d08424-7e36-44ef-b0ca-6cb89174f787\" data-question=\"26\">moral obligation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Pury also believes that people can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbe4c84f-c4a2-45bc-b95f-d37d165c2ef5\" data-question=\"21\">acquire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> courage. Many of her students said that faced with a risky situation, they first tried to calm themselves down, then looked for a way to mitigate the danger, just as Pedeleose did by documenting his allegations.</span></p><p><span>Over the long term, picking up a new character trait may help you move toward being the person you want to be. And in the short term, the effort itself could be surprisingly rewarding, a kind of internal adventure.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>14-18</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span>Psychologists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe3c6156-e024-4ed0-bf8b-a2be6bc5c7cb\" data-question=\"14\">have traditionally believed that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> a personality <strong>14</strong>…………… was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5822652-8acd-457c-9bfb-82c601cef257\" data-question=\"14\">impossible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and that by a <strong>15</strong>…………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c5224579-430d-4cf4-9cdd-09704f5de2b2\" data-question=\"15\">a person’s character<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> tends to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"288d710b-a170-4dce-ae4a-e75324b00c73\" data-question=\"15\">fixed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. This is not true according to positive psychologists, who say that our personal qualities can be seen as habitual behaviour. One of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b2bbb953-e402-4f54-b9d6-6f8d0a10db4d\" data-question=\"16\">easiest qualities to acquire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> is <strong>16</strong>…………….. . However, regardless of the quality, it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c160aef-ea4c-45fc-9e6a-976fc2744590\" data-question=\"17\">necessary to learn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee70b29e-4497-4baa-a0aa-7c062c040491\" data-question=\"17\">a wide variety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"984d0168-e9d5-4a60-b9e6-01e7f6a69d53\" data-question=\"17\">different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <strong>17</strong>…………….. in order for a new quality to develop; for example, a person <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c898ba4-899e-467c-aff2-cbbe231c3a2b\" data-question=\"18\">must understand and feel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> some <strong>18</strong>……………… in order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69ad46c8-5349-4dfa-a45a-373a54c1b17b\" data-question=\"18\">increase their happiness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1073\" id=\"question-wrapper-1073\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRANSFORMATION/CHANGE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1074\" id=\"question-wrapper-1074\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YOUNG AGE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1075\" id=\"question-wrapper-1075\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OPTIMISM</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1076\" id=\"question-wrapper-1076\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SKILLS/TECHNIQUES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1077\" id=\"question-wrapper-1077\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NEGATIVE EMOTIONS/FEELINGS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 19-22) and the list of people below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct person, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>19-22</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of People</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Christopher Peterson</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> David Fajgenbaum</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> Suzanne Segerstrom</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> Tanya Streeter</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> Todd Kashdan</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong> Kenneth Pedeleose</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong> Cynthia Pury</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1078\" id=\"question-wrapper-1078\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People must accept that they do not know much <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e17c345-9e46-4d5e-a2a7-addade831d64\" data-question=\"19\">when first trying something new<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1079\" id=\"question-wrapper-1079\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is important for people to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ad7283b-a83f-4041-850c-f98db9f7c086\" data-question=\"20\">actively notice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> when good things <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26821b77-c850-4d41-93e7-f8b6e01db1dd\" data-question=\"20\">happen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1080\" id=\"question-wrapper-1080\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Courage can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbe4c84f-c4a2-45bc-b95f-d37d165c2ef5\" data-question=\"21\">learned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> once its origins in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"703ac5ea-e65f-44db-a5da-25638a31c3d2\" data-question=\"21\">a sense of responsibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> are understood. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1081\" id=\"question-wrapper-1081\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f23968a4-5df1-4aab-a228-e51019a05945\" data-question=\"22\">possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62392c0f-3601-42fa-8a10-e50326bc9580\" data-question=\"22\">overcome shyness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> when faced with the need to speak in public. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has eight sections, <strong>A-H</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which section contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-H</strong>, in boxes <strong>23-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1082\" id=\"question-wrapper-1082\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a mention of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eb69569f-6b87-4b51-a872-6e2e29c13faf\" data-question=\"23\">rational thinking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> enabled someone to achieve <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c329156-5ec0-457b-a382-78af2f6f2cd9\" data-question=\"23\">physical goals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1083\" id=\"question-wrapper-1083\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an account of how someone <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93533bbd-0a0e-4fc4-b846-af6558a21480\" data-question=\"24\">overcame a sad experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1084\" id=\"question-wrapper-1084\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of how someone decided to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8213f935-1499-4460-a720-aa1d6dd3a304\" data-question=\"25\">rethink their academic career path<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1085\" id=\"question-wrapper-1085\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an example of how someone <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48a20030-ca8f-4e5d-807b-2f4499947faa\" data-question=\"26\">risked his career<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> out of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24d08424-7e36-44ef-b0ca-6cb89174f787\" data-question=\"26\">a sense of duty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"fe3c6156-e024-4ed0-bf8b-a2be6bc5c7cb","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"have traditionally believed that","passagePhrase":"have long held that"},{"uid":"a5822652-8acd-457c-9bfb-82c601cef257","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"impossible","passagePhrase":"cannot undergo a transformation in any meaningful way"},{"uid":"c5224579-430d-4cf4-9cdd-09704f5de2b2","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"a person’s character","passagePhrase":"key traits of personality"},{"uid":"288d710b-a170-4dce-ae4a-e75324b00c73","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"fixed","passagePhrase":"determined"},{"uid":"b2bbb953-e402-4f54-b9d6-6f8d0a10db4d","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"easiest qualities to acquire","passagePhrase":"Some qualities are less challenging to develop"},{"uid":"2c160aef-ea4c-45fc-9e6a-976fc2744590","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"necessary to learn","passagePhrase":"requires mastering"},{"uid":"ee70b29e-4497-4baa-a0aa-7c062c040491","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"a wide variety","passagePhrase":"a range of"},{"uid":"984d0168-e9d5-4a60-b9e6-01e7f6a69d53","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"different","passagePhrase":"diverse"},{"uid":"69ad46c8-5349-4dfa-a45a-373a54c1b17b","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"increase their happiness","passagePhrase":"bring more joy and passion"},{"uid":"0c898ba4-899e-467c-aff2-cbbe231c3a2b","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"must understand and feel","passagePhrase":"must be open to experiencing"},{"uid":"f23968a4-5df1-4aab-a228-e51019a05945","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"possible","passagePhrase":"evidence"},{"uid":"62392c0f-3601-42fa-8a10-e50326bc9580","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"overcome shyness","passagePhrase":"learned to be more outgoing"},{"uid":"93533bbd-0a0e-4fc4-b846-af6558a21480","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"overcame a sad experience","passagePhrase":"a support group to help others in similar situations"},{"uid":"3ad7283b-a83f-4041-850c-f98db9f7c086","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"actively notice","passagePhrase":"pay attention to"},{"uid":"26821b77-c850-4d41-93e7-f8b6e01db1dd","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"happen","passagePhrase":"come about"},{"uid":"6c329156-5ec0-457b-a382-78af2f6f2cd9","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"physical goals","passagePhrase":"The physical stamina"},{"uid":"eb69569f-6b87-4b51-a872-6e2e29c13faf","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"rational thinking","passagePhrase":"learned to untangle her fears from her judgment of what her body and mind could do"},{"uid":"5e17c345-9e46-4d5e-a2a7-addade831d64","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"when first trying something new","passagePhrase":"As a newcomer"},{"uid":"8213f935-1499-4460-a720-aa1d6dd3a304","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"rethink their academic career path","passagePhrase":"took a break ... earned about alternative healing techniques ... switched labs to study"},{"uid":"48a20030-ca8f-4e5d-807b-2f4499947faa","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"risked his career","passagePhrase":"his own job security would be threatened"},{"uid":"703ac5ea-e65f-44db-a5da-25638a31c3d2","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"a sense of responsibility","passagePhrase":"motivated by fearlessness, but by moral obligation"},{"uid":"24d08424-7e36-44ef-b0ca-6cb89174f787","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"a sense of duty","passagePhrase":"moral obligation"},{"uid":"bbe4c84f-c4a2-45bc-b95f-d37d165c2ef5","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"learned","passagePhrase":"acquire"}]},"reading_u2_198":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>When evolution runs backwards</strong></span></h2><p><span><em></em></span></p><p><span><em>Evolution isn’t supposed to run backwards – yet an increasing number of examples show that it does and that it can sometimes represent the future of a species.</em></span></p><p><span>The description of any animal as an ‘evolutionary throwback’ is controversial. For the better part of a century, most biologists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd51e68b-93b7-4681-b08a-16b07bb6cc06\" data-question=\"32\">have been reluctant to use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> those words, mindful of a principle of evolution that says ‘evolution cannot <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78fe9f6f-7cc4-45da-98c1-d2209a88230a\" data-question=\"32\">run backwards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. But as more and more examples come to light and modern genetics enters the scene, that principle is having to be rewritten. Not only are evolutionary throwbacks possible, they sometimes play an important role in the forward march of evolution. </span></p><p><span>The technical term for an evolutionary throwback is an ‘atavism’, from the Latin atavus, meaning forefather. The word has ugly connotations thanks largely to Cesare Lombroso, a 19th-century Italian medic who argued that criminals were born not made and could be identified by certain physical features that were throwbacks to a primitive, sub-human state.</span></p><p><span>While Lombroso was measuring criminals, a Belgian palaeontologist called Louis Dollo was studying fossil records and coming to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5757612d-39fd-4c45-8718-02ccf992d648\" data-question=\"33\">opposite conclusion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. In 1890 he proposed that evolution was irreversible: that ‘an organism is unable to return, even partially, to a previous stage already realised in the ranks of its ancestors. Early 20th-century biologists came to a similar conclusion, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8ce2685-8d76-47b2-9a38-5a4ccf93ec8e\" data-question=\"27\">though they qualified it in terms of probability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, stating that there is no reason why evolution cannot <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78fe9f6f-7cc4-45da-98c1-d2209a88230a\" data-question=\"32\">run backwards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> -it is just very unlikely. And so the idea of irreversibility in evolution stuck and came to be known as ‘Dollo’s law.</span></p><p><span>If Dollo’s law is right, atavisms should occur only very rarely, if at all. Yet almost since the idea took root, exceptions have been cropping up. In 1919, for example, a humpback whale with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f79afa9-9d11-4e02-b1d4-04297e93db08\" data-question=\"28\">a pair of leglike appendages over a metre long, complete with a full set of limb bones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, was caught off Vancouver Island in Canada. Explorer Roy Chapman Andrews argued at the time that the whale must be a throwback to a land-living ancestor. ‘I can see no other explanation,’ he wrote in 1921.</span></p><p><span>Since then, so many other examples have been discovered that it no longer makes sense to say that evolution is as good as irreversible. And this poses a puzzle: how can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c335fb95-adbf-4fb4-80c1-4a05d0b4ad4a\" data-question=\"34\">characteristics that disappeared millions of years ago suddenly reappear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>?</span></p><p><span>In 1994, Rudolf Raff and colleagues at Indiana University in the USA decided to use genetics to put a number on the probability of evolution going into reverse. They reasoned that while some evolutionary changes involve the loss of genes and are therefore irreversible, others may be the result of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"037aedcb-089c-4c15-bc19-a1d537f28099\" data-question=\"29\">genes being switched off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. If these silent genes are somehow switched back on, they argued, long-lost traits could reappear.</span></p><p><span>Raff’s team went on to calculate the likelihood of it happening. Silent genes accumulate random mutations, they reasoned, eventually rendering them useless. So how long can a gene survive in a species if it is no longer used? The team calculated that there is a good chance of silent genes surviving for up to 6 million years in at least a few individuals in a population, and that some might survive as long as 10 million years. In other words, throwbacks are possible, but only to the relatively recent evolutionary past.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b385e47-1a3e-4229-b308-f8fbf8b8da2f\" data-question=\"30\">As a possible example<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, the team pointed to the mole salamanders of Mexico and California. Like most amphibians these begin life in a juvenile ‘tadpole’ state, then metamorphose into the adult form – except for one species, the axolotl, which famously lives its entire life as a juvenile. The simplest explanation for this is that the axolotl lineage alone lost the ability to metamorphose, while others retained it. From a detailed analysis of the salamanders’ family tree, however, it is clear that the other lineages evolved from an ancestor that itself had lost the ability to metamorphose. In other words, metamorphosis in mole salamanders is an atavism. The salamander example fits with Raff’s 10million-year time frame.</span></p><p><span>More recently, however, examples have been reported that break the time limit, suggesting that silent genes may not be the whole story. In a paper published last year, biologist Gunter Wagner of Yale University reported some work on the evolutionary history of a group of South American lizards called Bachia. Many of these have minuscule limbs; some look more like snakes than lizards and a few have completely lost the toes on their hind limbs. Other species, however, sport up to four toes on their hind legs. The simplest explanation is that the toed lineages never lost their toes, but Wagner begs to differ. According to his analysis of the Bachia family tree, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24f70252-39b4-4de6-a3d6-a3e13abae852\" data-question=\"38\">the toed species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> re-evolved toes from toeless ancestors and, what is more, digit <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8670c194-e2e3-4ea7-a404-20679c8d9fb8\" data-question=\"31\">loss and gain has occurred on more than one occasion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> over tens of millions of years.</span></p><p><span>So what’s going on? One possibility is that these traits are lost and then simply reappear, in much the same way that similar structures <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"572a3496-bf5a-4a60-a5e1-50a878e43e3a\" data-question=\"35\">can independently arise in unrelated species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c508e16-4425-4c5d-a52e-6ea4e15eed4a\" data-question=\"35\">such as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the dorsal fins of sharks and killer whales. Another more intriguing possibility is that the genetic information needed to make toes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67dd3ae4-5c53-4045-b8e3-64f70fbf8a62\" data-question=\"36\">somehow survived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> for tens or perhaps hundreds of millions of years in the lizards and was reactivated. These atavistic traits provided an advantage and spread through the population, effectively reversing evolution.</span></p><p><span>But if silent genes degrade within 6 to million years, how can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e0749c2a-8593-4c86-bb70-337d5a51bcf5\" data-question=\"40\">long-lost traits be reactivated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> over longer timescales? The answer may lie in the womb. Early embryos of <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c25637a7-fc5e-4dda-8363-dc41928675c0\" data-question=\"39\">many<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> species develop ancestral <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"601a2ddd-9442-47f4-bce9-4657ab57a8e2\" data-question=\"39\">features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Snake embryos, for example, sprout hind limb buds. Later in development these features disappear thanks to developmental programs that say ‘lose the leg’. If for any reason this does not happen, the ancestral feature may not disappear, leading to an atavism.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1086\" id=\"question-wrapper-1086\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When discussing the theory developed by Louis Dollo, the writer says that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. it was immediately referred to as Dollo’s law.</li> <li>B. it supported the possibility of evolutionary throwbacks.</li> <li>C. it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8ce2685-8d76-47b2-9a38-5a4ccf93ec8e\" data-question=\"27\">was modified<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> by biologists in the early twentieth century.</li> <li>D. it was based on many years of research.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1087\" id=\"question-wrapper-1087\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The humpback whale caught off Vancouver Island is mentioned because of </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the exceptional size of its body.</li> <li>B. the way it exemplifies Dollo’s law.</li> <li>C. the amount of local controversy it caused.</li> <li>D. the reason given for its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f79afa9-9d11-4e02-b1d4-04297e93db08\" data-question=\"28\">unusual features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1088\" id=\"question-wrapper-1088\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is said about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"037aedcb-089c-4c15-bc19-a1d537f28099\" data-question=\"29\">‘silent genes’<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Their numbers vary according to species.</li> <li>B. Raff disagreed with the use of the term.</li> <li>C. They could lead to the re-emergence of certain characteristics.</li> <li>D. They can have an unlimited life span.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1089\" id=\"question-wrapper-1089\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer mentions the mole salamander because </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. it exemplifies what happens in the development of most amphibians.</li> <li>B. it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b385e47-1a3e-4229-b308-f8fbf8b8da2f\" data-question=\"30\">suggests that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> Raff’s theory is correct.</li> <li>C. it has lost and regained more than one ability.</li> <li>D. its ancestors have become the subject of extensive research.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1090\" id=\"question-wrapper-1090\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Which of the following does Wagner claim? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Members of the Bachia lizard family <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8670c194-e2e3-4ea7-a404-20679c8d9fb8\" data-question=\"31\">have lost and regained certain features several times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Evidence shows that the evolution of the Bachia lizard is due to the environment.</li> <li>C. His research into South American lizards supports Raff’s assertions.</li> <li>D. His findings will apply to other species of South American lizards.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, <strong>A-G</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>32-36</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> the question of how certain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c335fb95-adbf-4fb4-80c1-4a05d0b4ad4a\" data-question=\"34\">long-lost traits could reappear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"572a3496-bf5a-4a60-a5e1-50a878e43e3a\" data-question=\"35\">occurrence of a particular feature in different species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>C </strong> parallels drawn between behaviour and appearance.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67dd3ae4-5c53-4045-b8e3-64f70fbf8a62\" data-question=\"36\">the continued existence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of certain genetic information.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> the doubts felt about evolutionary throwbacks.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong> the possibility of evolution <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78fe9f6f-7cc4-45da-98c1-d2209a88230a\" data-question=\"32\">being reversible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong> Dollo’s findings and the convictions held by Lombroso.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1091\" id=\"question-wrapper-1091\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> For a long time biologists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd51e68b-93b7-4681-b08a-16b07bb6cc06\" data-question=\"32\">rejected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1092\" id=\"question-wrapper-1092\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5757612d-39fd-4c45-8718-02ccf992d648\" data-question=\"33\">Opposing views<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> on evolutionary throwbacks are represented by </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1093\" id=\"question-wrapper-1093\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Examples of evolutionary throwbacks have led to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1094\" id=\"question-wrapper-1094\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The shark and killer whale are mentioned to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c508e16-4425-4c5d-a52e-6ea4e15eed4a\" data-question=\"35\">exemplify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1095\" id=\"question-wrapper-1095\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One explanation for the findings of Wagner’s research is </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>37-40</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1096\" id=\"question-wrapper-1096\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Wagner was the first person to do research on South American lizards. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1097\" id=\"question-wrapper-1097\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Wagner believes that Bachia <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24f70252-39b4-4de6-a3d6-a3e13abae852\" data-question=\"38\">lizards with toes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> had toeless ancestors. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1098\" id=\"question-wrapper-1098\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The temporary occurrence of long-lost <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"601a2ddd-9442-47f4-bce9-4657ab57a8e2\" data-question=\"39\">traits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> in embryos is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c25637a7-fc5e-4dda-8363-dc41928675c0\" data-question=\"39\">rare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"1099\" id=\"question-wrapper-1099\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e0749c2a-8593-4c86-bb70-337d5a51bcf5\" data-question=\"40\">Evolutionary throwbacks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> might be caused by developmental problems in the womb. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"bd51e68b-93b7-4681-b08a-16b07bb6cc06","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"rejected","passagePhrase":"have been reluctant to use"},{"uid":"78fe9f6f-7cc4-45da-98c1-d2209a88230a","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"being reversible","passagePhrase":"run backwards ... run backwards"},{"uid":"5757612d-39fd-4c45-8718-02ccf992d648","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Opposing views","passagePhrase":"opposite conclusion"},{"uid":"c8ce2685-8d76-47b2-9a38-5a4ccf93ec8e","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"was modified","passagePhrase":"though they qualified it in terms of probability"},{"uid":"7f79afa9-9d11-4e02-b1d4-04297e93db08","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"unusual features","passagePhrase":"a pair of leglike appendages over a metre long, complete with a full set of limb bones"},{"uid":"c335fb95-adbf-4fb4-80c1-4a05d0b4ad4a","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"long-lost traits could reappear","passagePhrase":"characteristics that disappeared millions of years ago suddenly reappear"},{"uid":"037aedcb-089c-4c15-bc19-a1d537f28099","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"‘silent genes’","passagePhrase":"genes being switched off"},{"uid":"8b385e47-1a3e-4229-b308-f8fbf8b8da2f","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"suggests that","passagePhrase":"As a possible example"},{"uid":"24f70252-39b4-4de6-a3d6-a3e13abae852","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"lizards with toes","passagePhrase":"the toed species"},{"uid":"8670c194-e2e3-4ea7-a404-20679c8d9fb8","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"have lost and regained certain features several times","passagePhrase":"loss and gain has occurred on more than one occasion"},{"uid":"572a3496-bf5a-4a60-a5e1-50a878e43e3a","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"occurrence of a particular feature in different species","passagePhrase":"can independently arise in unrelated species"},{"uid":"3c508e16-4425-4c5d-a52e-6ea4e15eed4a","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"exemplify","passagePhrase":"such as"},{"uid":"67dd3ae4-5c53-4045-b8e3-64f70fbf8a62","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"the continued existence","passagePhrase":"somehow survived"},{"uid":"e0749c2a-8593-4c86-bb70-337d5a51bcf5","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Evolutionary throwbacks","passagePhrase":"long-lost traits be reactivated"},{"uid":"601a2ddd-9442-47f4-bce9-4657ab57a8e2","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"traits","passagePhrase":"features"}]},"reading_u2_199":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong>Crop-growing skyscrapers</strong></span></h2><p><span>By the year 2050, nearly 80% of the Earth’s population will live in urban centres. Applying the most conservative estimates to current demographic trends, the human population will increase by about three billion people by then. An estimated 109 hectares of new land (about 20% larger than Brazil) will be needed to grow enough food to feed them, if traditional farming methods continue as they are practised today. At present, throughout the world, over 80% of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"018b40b6-a6dd-4d4e-be33-668520ca4e46\" data-question=\"9\">land that is suitable for raising crops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> is in use. Historically, some 15% of that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdb2be80-9454-4495-bee7-88841d5bc259\" data-question=\"9\">has been laid waste<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> by poor management practices. What can be done to ensure enough food for the world’s population to live on?</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53090d11-0988-4aed-9343-437b8c6ac786\" data-question=\"1\">The concept of indoor farming is not new<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, since hothouse production of tomatoes and other produce has been in vogue for some time. What is new is the urgent need to scale up this technology to accommodate another three billion people. Many believe an entirely new approach to indoor farming is required, employing cutting-edge technologies. One such proposal is for the ‘Vertical Farm’. The concept is of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af580fc3-c237-4fda-8cf3-c3ffc6ced834\" data-question=\"2\">multi-storey buildings in which food crops are grown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in environmentally controlled conditions. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f13911c4-5ad6-45a7-87a6-bf281e0c8419\" data-question=\"2\">Situated in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the heart of urban centres, they would drastically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"566b7dc3-c093-4f59-8f50-97793958b71a\" data-question=\"2\">reduce the amount of transportation required to bring food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1af85bca-2fe2-41e1-b35c-ca23bafeaeed\" data-question=\"2\">consumers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Vertical farms would need to be efficient, cheap to construct and safe to operate. If successfully implemented, proponents claim, vertical farms offer the promise of urban renewal, sustainable production of a safe and varied food supply (through year-round production of all crops), and the eventual repair of ecosystems that have been sacrificed for horizontal farming.</span></p><p><span>It took humans 10,000 years to learn how to grow most of the crops we now take for granted. Along the way, we despoiled most of the land we worked, often turning verdant, natural ecozones into semi-arid deserts. Within that same time frame, we evolved into an urban species, in which 60% of the human population now lives vertically in cities. This means that, for the majority, we humans have shelter from the elements, yet we subject our food-bearing plants to the rigours of the great outdoors and can do no more than hope for a good weather year. However, more often than not now, due to a rapidly changing climate, that is not what happens. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"734dcdb5-06a6-4bca-b5fe-cf2fb3841d89\" data-question=\"11\">Massive floods, long droughts, hurricanes and severe monsoons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3bf35a63-63b7-42d3-af18-4dd51552909b\" data-question=\"11\">take their toll<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> each year, destroying millions of tons of valuable crops.</span></p><p><span>The supporters of vertical farming claim many potential advantages for the system. For instance, crops <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"72440d28-2de8-472a-a7d9-dad21bbabc57\" data-question=\"10\">would be produced all year round<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, as they would be kept in artificially controlled, optimum growing conditions. There would be no weather-related crop failures due to droughts, floods or pests. All the food could be grown organically, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9560b83a-9a79-4837-9439-dff6a55f6511\" data-question=\"12\">eliminating the need for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> herbicides, pesticides and fertilisers. The system would greatly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"048e1623-89e9-4703-b4ce-d8727ee31ba8\" data-question=\"13\">reduce the incidence of many infectious diseases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> that are acquired at the agricultural interface. Although the system would consume energy, it would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"466b0aa1-1d0e-41d6-8722-14a13eb438dc\" data-question=\"3\">return energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> to the grid via <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1005c387-04d9-4e33-bc1b-8288576d5fd8\" data-question=\"3\">methane generation from composting nonedible parts of plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a4f011bd-89a3-48d7-b3ff-2f8a2d02209a\" data-question=\"4\">would also dramatically reduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> fossil fuel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4988b26-0519-418c-8dac-f6b7019bf635\" data-question=\"4\">use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, by cutting out the need for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09e1826b-ffdf-4df6-8924-818cc580c417\" data-question=\"4\">tractors, ploughs and shipping<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>A major <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98189b42-ed51-46f1-8331-b5abc97137fb\" data-question=\"5\">drawback<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of vertical farming, however, is that the plants would require artificial light. Without it, those plants nearest the windows would be exposed to more sunlight and grow more quickly, reducing the efficiency of the system. Single-storey greenhouses have the benefit of natural overhead light; even so, many still need artificial lighting.</span></p><p><span>A multi-storey facility with no natural overhead light would require far more. Generating enough light could be prohibitively expensive, unless cheap, renewable energy is available, and this appears to be rather a future aspiration than a likelihood for the near future.</span></p><p><span>One <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c322788b-3ee1-476d-9176-4d4544e22cd2\" data-question=\"6\">variation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> on vertical farming that has been developed is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea226315-2957-4827-b6c9-92e52d49f6ab\" data-question=\"6\">grow plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> in stacked trays that move on rails. Moving the trays allows the plants to get enough sunlight. This system is already in operation, and works well within a single-storey greenhouse with light reaching it from above: it Is not certain, however, that it can be made to work without that overhead natural light.</span></p><p><span>Vertical farming is an attempt to address the undoubted problems that we face in producing enough food for a growing population. At the moment, though, more needs to be done to reduce the detrimental impact it would have on the environment, particularly as regards the use of energy. While it is possible that much of our food will be grown in skyscrapers in future, most experts currently believe it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5185e492-ee34-4c7c-aeec-5269423fdba1\" data-question=\"7\">far more likely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> that we will simply use the space available on urban rooftops.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>1-7</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>Indoor farming</strong></span></h4></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"774\" id=\"question-wrapper-774\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53090d11-0988-4aed-9343-437b8c6ac786\" data-question=\"1\">Some food plants, including……………… are already grown indoors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TOMATOES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"775\" id=\"question-wrapper-775\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Vertical farms would be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f13911c4-5ad6-45a7-87a6-bf281e0c8419\" data-question=\"2\">located in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>………………, meaning that there would be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"566b7dc3-c093-4f59-8f50-97793958b71a\" data-question=\"2\">less need to take them long distances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1af85bca-2fe2-41e1-b35c-ca23bafeaeed\" data-question=\"2\">customers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">URBAN CENTRES/CENTERS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"776\" id=\"question-wrapper-776\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Vertical farms could use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1005c387-04d9-4e33-bc1b-8288576d5fd8\" data-question=\"3\">methane from plants and animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"466b0aa1-1d0e-41d6-8722-14a13eb438dc\" data-question=\"3\">produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>……………….. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ENERGY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"777\" id=\"question-wrapper-777\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4988b26-0519-418c-8dac-f6b7019bf635\" data-question=\"4\">consumption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a4f011bd-89a3-48d7-b3ff-2f8a2d02209a\" data-question=\"4\">would be cut<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> because <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09e1826b-ffdf-4df6-8924-818cc580c417\" data-question=\"4\">agricultural vehicles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> would be unnecessary. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOSSIL FUEL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"778\" id=\"question-wrapper-778\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The fact that vertical farms would need……………….. light is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98189b42-ed51-46f1-8331-b5abc97137fb\" data-question=\"5\">disadvantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ARTIFICIAL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"779\" id=\"question-wrapper-779\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c322788b-3ee1-476d-9176-4d4544e22cd2\" data-question=\"6\">form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of vertical farming involves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea226315-2957-4827-b6c9-92e52d49f6ab\" data-question=\"6\">planting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> in……………….. which are not fixed. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(STACKED) TRAYS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"780\" id=\"question-wrapper-780\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5185e492-ee34-4c7c-aeec-5269423fdba1\" data-question=\"7\">most probable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> development is that food will be grown on………………… in towns and cities. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(URBAN) ROOFTOPS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>8-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"781\" id=\"question-wrapper-781\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Methods for predicting the Earth’s population have recently changed. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"782\" id=\"question-wrapper-782\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Human beings are responsible for some of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdb2be80-9454-4495-bee7-88841d5bc259\" data-question=\"9\">destruction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"018b40b6-a6dd-4d4e-be33-668520ca4e46\" data-question=\"9\">food-producing land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"783\" id=\"question-wrapper-783\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The crops produced in vertical farms will <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"72440d28-2de8-472a-a7d9-dad21bbabc57\" data-question=\"10\">depend on the season<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"784\" id=\"question-wrapper-784\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"734dcdb5-06a6-4bca-b5fe-cf2fb3841d89\" data-question=\"11\">Some damage to food crops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3bf35a63-63b7-42d3-af18-4dd51552909b\" data-question=\"11\">caused<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> by climate change. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"785\" id=\"question-wrapper-785\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Fertilisers <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9560b83a-9a79-4837-9439-dff6a55f6511\" data-question=\"12\">will be needed for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> certain crops in vertical farms. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"786\" id=\"question-wrapper-786\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Vertical farming will make plants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"048e1623-89e9-4703-b4ce-d8727ee31ba8\" data-question=\"13\">less likely to be affected by infectious diseases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"018b40b6-a6dd-4d4e-be33-668520ca4e46","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"food-producing land","passagePhrase":"land that is suitable for raising crops"},{"uid":"cdb2be80-9454-4495-bee7-88841d5bc259","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"destruction","passagePhrase":"has been laid waste"},{"uid":"53090d11-0988-4aed-9343-437b8c6ac786","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Some food plants, including……………… are already grown indoors","passagePhrase":"The concept of indoor farming is not new"},{"uid":"af580fc3-c237-4fda-8cf3-c3ffc6ced834","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"multi-storey buildings in which food crops are grown"},{"uid":"f13911c4-5ad6-45a7-87a6-bf281e0c8419","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"located in","passagePhrase":"Situated in"},{"uid":"566b7dc3-c093-4f59-8f50-97793958b71a","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"less need to take them long distances","passagePhrase":"reduce the amount of transportation required to bring food"},{"uid":"1af85bca-2fe2-41e1-b35c-ca23bafeaeed","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"customers","passagePhrase":"consumers"},{"uid":"734dcdb5-06a6-4bca-b5fe-cf2fb3841d89","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Some damage to food crops","passagePhrase":"Massive floods, long droughts, hurricanes and severe monsoons"},{"uid":"3bf35a63-63b7-42d3-af18-4dd51552909b","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"caused","passagePhrase":"take their toll"},{"uid":"048e1623-89e9-4703-b4ce-d8727ee31ba8","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"less likely to be affected by infectious diseases","passagePhrase":"reduce the incidence of many infectious diseases"},{"uid":"466b0aa1-1d0e-41d6-8722-14a13eb438dc","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"produce","passagePhrase":"return energy"},{"uid":"1005c387-04d9-4e33-bc1b-8288576d5fd8","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"methane from plants and animals","passagePhrase":"methane generation from composting nonedible parts of plants"},{"uid":"a4f011bd-89a3-48d7-b3ff-2f8a2d02209a","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"would be cut","passagePhrase":"would also dramatically reduce"},{"uid":"f4988b26-0519-418c-8dac-f6b7019bf635","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"consumption","passagePhrase":"use"},{"uid":"09e1826b-ffdf-4df6-8924-818cc580c417","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"agricultural vehicles","passagePhrase":"tractors, ploughs and shipping"},{"uid":"98189b42-ed51-46f1-8331-b5abc97137fb","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"disadvantage","passagePhrase":"drawback"},{"uid":"c322788b-3ee1-476d-9176-4d4544e22cd2","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"form","passagePhrase":"variation"},{"uid":"ea226315-2957-4827-b6c9-92e52d49f6ab","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"planting","passagePhrase":"grow plants"},{"uid":"5185e492-ee34-4c7c-aeec-5269423fdba1","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"most probable","passagePhrase":"far more likely"}]},"reading_u2_200":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>The Falkirk Wheel</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>A unique engineering achievement</em></span></p><p><span>The Falkirk Wheel in Scotland is the world’s first and only rotating boat lift. Opened in 2002, it is central to the ambitious £84.5m Millennium Link project to restore navigability across Scotland by reconnecting the historic waterways of the Forth &amp; Clyde and Union Canals.</span></p><p><span>The major challenge of the project lays in the fact that the Forth &amp; Clyde Canal is situated 35 metres below the level of the Union Canal. Historically, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7a8c524-2d5d-4446-b7a0-f9a610e1b0e5\" data-question=\"14\">the two canals had been joined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> near the town of Falkirk by <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8c89daaf-94a3-4d87-ba0c-379f315e1830\" data-question=\"14\">a sequence of 11 locks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> – enclosed sections of canal in which the water level could be raised or lowered – that stepped down across a distance of 1.5 km. This had been dismantled in 1933, thereby breaking the link. When the project was launched in 1994, the British Waterways authority were keen to create a dramatic twenty-first-century landmark which would not only be a fitting commemoration of the Millennium, but also a lasting symbol of the economic regeneration of the region.</span></p><p><span>Numerous ideas were submitted for the project, including concepts ranging from rolling eggs to tilting tanks, from giant seesaws to overhead monorails. The eventual winner was a plan for the huge rotating steel boat lift which was to become The Falkirk Wheel. The unique shape of the structure is claimed to have been inspired by various sources, both manmade and natural, most notably a Celtic double headed axe, but also the vast turning propeller of a ship, the ribcage of a whale or the spine of a fish.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72d3069f-ccac-4fc6-8dbc-61fed56cc0ff\" data-question=\"16\">The various parts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of The Falkirk Wheel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"722f88e0-b363-4302-85a3-fc9beb1b8ee5\" data-question=\"16\">were all constructed and assembled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, like one giant toy building set, at Butterley Engineering’s Steelworks in Derbyshire, some 400 km from Falkirk. A team there carefully assembled the 1,200 tonnes of steel, painstakingly fitting the pieces together to an accuracy of just 10 mm to ensure a perfect final fit. In the summer of 2001, the structure was then dismantled and transported on 35 lorries to Falkirk, before all being bolted back together again on the ground, and finally lifted into position in five large sections by crane. The Wheel would need to withstand immense and constantly changing stresses as it rotated, so to make the structure more robust, the steel sections were bolted rather than welded together. Over 45,000 bolt holes were matched with their bolts, and each bolt <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a9ec849-20a0-411d-88e0-d293ac2c4605\" data-question=\"17\">was hand-tightened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The Wheel consists of two sets of opposing axe-shaped arms, attached about 25 metres apart to a fixed central spine. Two diametrically opposed water-filled ‘gondolas’, each with a capacity of 360,000 litres, are fitted between the ends of the arms. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f09ad225-4f43-48e8-bab9-1186978a29f2\" data-question=\"18\">These gondolas always weigh the same<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, whether or not they are carrying boats. This is because, according to Archimedes’ principle of displacement, floating objects displace their own weight in water. So when a boat enters a gondola, the amount of water leaving the gondola weighs exactly the same as the boat. This keeps the Wheel balanced and so, despite its enormous mass, it rotates through 180° in five and a half minutes while using very little power. It takes just 1.5 kilowatt-hours (5.4 MJ) of energy to rotate the Wheel -roughly the same as boiling eight small domestic kettles of water.</span></p><p><span>Boats needing to be lifted up enter the canal basin at the level of the Forth &amp; Clyde Canal and then enter the lower gondola of the Wheel. Two hydraulic steel gates are raised, so as to seal the gondola off from the water in the canal basin. The water between the gates is then pumped out. A hydraulic clamp, which prevents the arms of the Wheel moving while the gondola is docked, is removed, allowing the Wheel to turn. In the central machine room an array of ten hydraulic motors then begins to rotate the central axle. The axle connects to the outer arms of the Wheel, which begin to rotate at a speed of 1/8 of a revolution per minute. As the wheel rotates, the gondolas are kept in the upright position by a simple gearing system. Two eight-metre-wide cogs orbit a fixed inner cog of the same width, connected by two smaller cogs travelling in the opposite direction to the outer cogs – so ensuring that the gondolas always remain level. When the gondola reaches the top, the boat passes straight onto the aqueduct situated 24 metres above the canal basin.</span></p><p><span>The remaining 11 metres of lift needed to reach the Union Canal is achieved by means of a pair of locks. The Wheel could not be constructed to elevate boats over the full 35-metre difference between the two canals, owing to the presence of the historically important <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51fe3ca8-15b7-4299-a808-eb39552aa451\" data-question=\"19\">Antonine Wall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, which was built by the Romans in the second century AD. Boats travel under this wall via a tunnel, then through the locks, and finally on to the Union Canal.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>14-19</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"787\" id=\"question-wrapper-787\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8c89daaf-94a3-4d87-ba0c-379f315e1830\" data-question=\"14\">The Falkirk Wheel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7a8c524-2d5d-4446-b7a0-f9a610e1b0e5\" data-question=\"14\">has linked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the Forth &amp; Clyde Canal with the Union Canal for the first time in their history. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"788\" id=\"question-wrapper-788\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There was some opposition to the design of the Falkirk Wheel at first. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"789\" id=\"question-wrapper-789\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Falkirk Wheel was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"722f88e0-b363-4302-85a3-fc9beb1b8ee5\" data-question=\"16\">initially put together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> at the location where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72d3069f-ccac-4fc6-8dbc-61fed56cc0ff\" data-question=\"16\">its components<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"722f88e0-b363-4302-85a3-fc9beb1b8ee5\" data-question=\"16\">were manufactured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"790\" id=\"question-wrapper-790\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Falkirk Wheel is the only boat lift in the world which has steel sections <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a9ec849-20a0-411d-88e0-d293ac2c4605\" data-question=\"17\">bolted together by hand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"791\" id=\"question-wrapper-791\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f09ad225-4f43-48e8-bab9-1186978a29f2\" data-question=\"18\">The weight of the gondolas varies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> according to the size of boat being carried. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"792\" id=\"question-wrapper-792\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The construction of the Falkirk Wheel site took into account the presence of a nearby <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51fe3ca8-15b7-4299-a808-eb39552aa451\" data-question=\"19\">ancient monument<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Label the diagram below.</p><p>Choose <strong>ONE WORD</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>20-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p><h4><strong>How a boat is lifted on the Falkirk Wheel</strong></h4><p><img alt=\"\" class=\"aligncenter lazyload size-full wp-image-8779\" src=\"/media/ielts_media/img/07_11-1-2-IELTS-Reading-q14-26.jpg\" style=\"height:677px; width:1000px\"></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"793\" id=\"question-wrapper-793\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GATES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"794\" id=\"question-wrapper-794\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CLAMP</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"795\" id=\"question-wrapper-795\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AXLE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"796\" id=\"question-wrapper-796\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COGS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"797\" id=\"question-wrapper-797\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AQUEDUCT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"798\" id=\"question-wrapper-798\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WALL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"799\" id=\"question-wrapper-799\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LOCKS</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"d7a8c524-2d5d-4446-b7a0-f9a610e1b0e5","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"has linked","passagePhrase":"the two canals had been joined"},{"uid":"72d3069f-ccac-4fc6-8dbc-61fed56cc0ff","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"its components","passagePhrase":"The various parts"},{"uid":"722f88e0-b363-4302-85a3-fc9beb1b8ee5","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"initially put together ... were manufactured","passagePhrase":"were all constructed and assembled"},{"uid":"9a9ec849-20a0-411d-88e0-d293ac2c4605","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"bolted together by hand","passagePhrase":"was hand-tightened"},{"uid":"51fe3ca8-15b7-4299-a808-eb39552aa451","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"ancient monument","passagePhrase":"Antonine Wall"}]},"reading_u2_201":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><h2><span><strong>Reducing the Effects of Climate Change</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>Mark Rowe reports on the increasingly ambitious geo-engineering projects being explored by scientists</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>Such is our dependence on fossil fuels, and such is the volume of carbon dioxide already released into the atmosphere, that many experts agree that significant global warming is now inevitable. They believe that the best we can do is keep it at a reasonable level, and at present the only serious option for doing this is cutting back on our carbon emissions. But while a few countries are making major strides in this regard, the majority are having great difficulty even stemming the rate of increase, let alone reversing it. Consequently, an increasing number of scientists are beginning to explore the alternative of geo-engineering — <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0540a401-4883-4098-8cf5-3be9a394977d\" data-question=\"29\">a term which generally refers to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the intentional large-scale manipulation of the environment. According to its proponents, geo-engineering is the equivalent of a backup generator: if Plan A – reducing our dependency on fossil fuels – fails, we require a Plan B, employing grand schemes to slow down or reverse the process of global warming.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Geo-engineering; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0f2e8317-fa43-43a0-a277-3a38b6fcd25e\" data-question=\"28\">has been shown to work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, at least on a small localised scale. For decades, MayDay parades in Moscow have taken place under clear blue skies, aircraft having deposited dry ice, silver iodide and cement powder to disperse clouds. Many of the schemes now suggested look to do the opposite, and reduce the amount of sunlight reaching the planet. The most eye-catching idea of all is suggested by Professor Roger Angel of the University of Arizona. His scheme would employ up to 16 trillion minute spacecraft, each weighing about one gram, to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c20a1715-a1bc-4a06-813c-eb1cd3075064\" data-question=\"30\">form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> a transparent, sunlight-refracting sunshade in an orbit 1.5 million km above the Earth. This could, argues Angel, reduce the amount of light reaching the Earth by two per cent.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>The majority of geo-engineering projects so far carried out — which include planting forests in deserts and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fbd7bcfa-64ed-4993-a961-001e766a5b4c\" data-question=\"31\">depositing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> iron <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a83cfb6d-89a3-4b0d-91bd-600ec68df40b\" data-question=\"31\">in the ocean<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"480cc632-93c2-4865-a0ef-708617a8b505\" data-question=\"32\">stimulate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the growth of algae – have focused on achieving a general cooling of the Earth. But some look specifically at reversing the melting at the poles, particularly the Arctic. The reasoning is that if you replenish the ice sheets and frozen waters of the high latitudes, more light will be reflected back into space, so reducing the warming of the oceans and atmosphere.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>The concept of releasing aerosol sprays into the stratosphere above the Arctic has been proposed by several scientists. This would involve using sulphur or hydrogen sulphide aerosols so that sulphur dioxide would form clouds, which would, in turn, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5b4defa-47ae-401b-8631-62b31b041fd0\" data-question=\"33\">lead to a global dimming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. The idea <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a545709-d214-45df-8ae6-fd5cab50e00c\" data-question=\"27\">is modelled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8351af0-ddac-4750-8cb4-e157d6d26e3f\" data-question=\"27\">historic volcanic explosions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, such as that of Mount Pinatubo in the Philippines in 1991, which led to a short-term cooling of global temperatures by 0.5 °C. Scientists have also scrutinised whether it’s possible to preserve <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ba0f821-b87c-4a27-8ffc-35b803de58c5\" data-question=\"34\">the ice sheets of Greenland<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c486174-1e3d-4f3a-ab16-301bbbab46a0\" data-question=\"34\">reinforced high-tension<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> cables, preventing icebergs from moving into the sea. Meanwhile in the Russian Arctic, geo-engineering plans include the planting of millions of birch trees. Whereas the region's native evergreen pines shade the snow and absorb radiation, birches would shed their leaves in winter, thus <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13e20bc6-5601-40bb-9734-648bc67705da\" data-question=\"35\">enabling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> radiation to be reflected by the snow. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88d51b90-41f7-4cac-8d3c-960983e576ae\" data-question=\"36\">Re-routing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> Russian rivers to increase cold water flow to ice-forming areas could also be used to slow down warming, say some climate scientists.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>But will such schemes ever be implemented? Generally speaking, those who are most cautious about geo-engineering are the scientists involved in the research. Angel says that his plan is ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"60ffaf8e-7e14-4474-b15a-7f5f59240221\" data-question=\"40\">no substitute for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> developing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cfffcd2-3281-4c1d-ba13-44aab5ae3314\" data-question=\"40\">renewable energy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>: the only permanent solution’. And Dr Phil Rasch of the US-based Pacific Northwest National Laboratory is equally guarded about the role of geo-engineering: ‘I think all of us agree that if we were to end geo-engineering on a given day, then the planet would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c5fd87e9-bbe2-4e23-9f4e-935dad598b7b\" data-question=\"37\">return to its pre-engineered condition very rapidly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, and probably within ten to twenty years. That’s certainly something to worry about.’</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>The US National Center for Atmospheric Research has already suggested that the proposal to inject sulphur into the atmosphere might affect rainfall patterns across the tropics and the Southern Ocean. ‘Geo-engineering plans to inject stratospheric aerosols or to seed clouds would act to cool the planet, and act to increase the extent of sea ice,’ says Rasch. ‘But all the models suggest some impact on the distribution of precipitation.’</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>‘A further risk with geo-engineering projects is that you can “overshoot”,’ says Dr Dan Hunt, from the University of Bristol’s School of Geophysical Sciences, who has studied the likely impacts of the sunshade and aerosol schemes on the climate. ‘You may bring global temperatures back to pre-industrial levels, but the risk is that the poles will still be warmer than they should be and the tropics will be cooler than before industrialisation.’ To avoid such a scenario, Lunt says, Angel’s project would have to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fdf58bda-abcd-4a15-99eb-d0015af4c185\" data-question=\"39\">operate at half strength<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>; all of which reinforces his view that the best option is to avoid the need for geo-engineering altogether.</span></p><p><span><strong>H</strong></span></p><p><span>The main reason why geo-engineering is supported by many in the scientific community is that most researchers have little faith in the ability of politicians to agree – and then bring in — the necessary carbon cuts. Even leading conservation organisations see the value of investigating the potential of geo-engineering. According to Dr Martin Sommerkorn, climate change advisor for the World Wildlife Fund’s International Arctic Programme, ‘Human-induced climate change has brought humanity to a position where we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f227b093-56a9-41b3-a9d0-e6b9da057706\" data-question=\"38\">shouldn’t exclude thinking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> thoroughly about this topic and its possibilities.’</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has eight paragraphs <strong>A-H</strong></span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-H</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-29</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"800\" id=\"question-wrapper-800\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of a geo-engineering project based on an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8351af0-ddac-4750-8cb4-e157d6d26e3f\" data-question=\"27\">earlier natural phenomenon<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"801\" id=\"question-wrapper-801\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an example of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0f2e8317-fa43-43a0-a277-3a38b6fcd25e\" data-question=\"28\">successful use of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> geo-engineering </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"802\" id=\"question-wrapper-802\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0540a401-4883-4098-8cf5-3be9a394977d\" data-question=\"29\">common definition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of geo-engineering </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the table below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>30-36</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>GEO-ENGINEERING PROJECTS</strong></span></h4><table><tbody><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span><strong>Procedure</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span><strong>Aim</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span>put a large number of tiny spacecraft into orbit far above Earth</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c20a1715-a1bc-4a06-813c-eb1cd3075064\" data-question=\"30\">create<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> a <strong>30</strong>………….. that would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5b4defa-47ae-401b-8631-62b31b041fd0\" data-question=\"33\">reduce the amount of light reaching Earth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span>place <strong>31</strong>…………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a83cfb6d-89a3-4b0d-91bd-600ec68df40b\" data-question=\"31\">in the sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"480cc632-93c2-4865-a0ef-708617a8b505\" data-question=\"32\">to encourage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <strong>32</strong>…………… to form</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span>release aerosol sprays into the stratosphere</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>to create <strong>33</strong>……………. that would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5b4defa-47ae-401b-8631-62b31b041fd0\" data-question=\"33\">reduce the amount of light reaching Earth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c486174-1e3d-4f3a-ab16-301bbbab46a0\" data-question=\"34\">fix strong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <strong>34</strong>…………… to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ba0f821-b87c-4a27-8ffc-35b803de58c5\" data-question=\"34\">Greenland ice sheets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span></span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>to prevent icebergs moving into the sea</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span>plant trees in Russian Arctic that would lose their leaves in winter</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13e20bc6-5601-40bb-9734-648bc67705da\" data-question=\"35\">allow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the <strong>35</strong>…………… to reflect radiation</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88d51b90-41f7-4cac-8d3c-960983e576ae\" data-question=\"36\">change the direction of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <strong>36</strong>……………</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>to bring more cold water into ice-forming areas</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"803\" id=\"question-wrapper-803\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SUNSHADE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"804\" id=\"question-wrapper-804\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IRON</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"805\" id=\"question-wrapper-805\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ALGAE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"806\" id=\"question-wrapper-806\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CLOUDS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"807\" id=\"question-wrapper-807\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CABLES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"808\" id=\"question-wrapper-808\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SNOW</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"809\" id=\"question-wrapper-809\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RIVERS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions <strong>37-40</strong>) and the list of scientists below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct scientist, <strong>A-D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-D</strong>, in boxes <strong>37-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Scientists</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Roger Angel</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> Phil Rasch</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> Dan Lunt</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> Martin Sommerkorn</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"810\" id=\"question-wrapper-810\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The effects of geo-engineering <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c5fd87e9-bbe2-4e23-9f4e-935dad598b7b\" data-question=\"37\">may not be long-lasting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"811\" id=\"question-wrapper-811\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Geo-engineering is a topic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f227b093-56a9-41b3-a9d0-e6b9da057706\" data-question=\"38\">worth exploring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"812\" id=\"question-wrapper-812\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It may be necessary to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fdf58bda-abcd-4a15-99eb-d0015af4c185\" data-question=\"39\">limit the effectiveness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of geo-engineering projects. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"813\" id=\"question-wrapper-813\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Research into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cfffcd2-3281-4c1d-ba13-44aab5ae3314\" data-question=\"40\">non-fossil-based fuels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"60ffaf8e-7e14-4474-b15a-7f5f59240221\" data-question=\"40\">cannot be replaced by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> geo-engineering. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0540a401-4883-4098-8cf5-3be9a394977d","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"common definition","passagePhrase":"a term which generally refers to"},{"uid":"0f2e8317-fa43-43a0-a277-3a38b6fcd25e","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"successful use of","passagePhrase":"has been shown to work"},{"uid":"c20a1715-a1bc-4a06-813c-eb1cd3075064","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"create","passagePhrase":"form"},{"uid":"fbd7bcfa-64ed-4993-a961-001e766a5b4c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"depositing"},{"uid":"a83cfb6d-89a3-4b0d-91bd-600ec68df40b","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"in the sea","passagePhrase":"in the ocean"},{"uid":"480cc632-93c2-4865-a0ef-708617a8b505","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"to encourage","passagePhrase":"stimulate"},{"uid":"e5b4defa-47ae-401b-8631-62b31b041fd0","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"reduce the amount of light reaching Earth ... reduce the amount of light reaching Earth","passagePhrase":"lead to a global dimming"},{"uid":"0a545709-d214-45df-8ae6-fd5cab50e00c","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"is modelled"},{"uid":"d8351af0-ddac-4750-8cb4-e157d6d26e3f","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"earlier natural phenomenon","passagePhrase":"historic volcanic explosions"},{"uid":"1ba0f821-b87c-4a27-8ffc-35b803de58c5","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Greenland ice sheets","passagePhrase":"the ice sheets of Greenland"},{"uid":"3c486174-1e3d-4f3a-ab16-301bbbab46a0","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"fix strong","passagePhrase":"reinforced high-tension"},{"uid":"13e20bc6-5601-40bb-9734-648bc67705da","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"allow","passagePhrase":"enabling"},{"uid":"88d51b90-41f7-4cac-8d3c-960983e576ae","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"change the direction of","passagePhrase":"Re-routing"},{"uid":"60ffaf8e-7e14-4474-b15a-7f5f59240221","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"cannot be replaced by","passagePhrase":"no substitute for"},{"uid":"5cfffcd2-3281-4c1d-ba13-44aab5ae3314","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"non-fossil-based fuels","passagePhrase":"renewable energy"},{"uid":"c5fd87e9-bbe2-4e23-9f4e-935dad598b7b","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"may not be long-lasting","passagePhrase":"return to its pre-engineered condition very rapidly"},{"uid":"fdf58bda-abcd-4a15-99eb-d0015af4c185","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"limit the effectiveness","passagePhrase":"operate at half strength"},{"uid":"f227b093-56a9-41b3-a9d0-e6b9da057706","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"worth exploring","passagePhrase":"shouldn’t exclude thinking"}]},"reading_u2_202":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><h2><span><strong>Raising the <em>Mary Rose</em></strong></span></h2><p><span><em>How a sixteenth-century warship was recovered from the seabed</em></span></p><p><span>On 19 July 1545, English and French fleets were engaged in a sea battle off the coast of southern England in the area of water called the Solent, between Portsmouth and the Isle of Wight. Among the English vessels was a warship by the name of <em>Mary Rose</em>. Built in Portsmouth some 35 years earlier, she had had a long and successful fighting career, and was a favourite of King Henry VIII. Accounts of what <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"36b096d4-72db-4ce2-903d-9154e5a02293\">happened to the ship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> vary: while witnesses agree that she was not hit by the French, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"669ae5df-e3f5-4fd8-bcdc-2a8d47a3fcd8\">some maintain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> that she was outdated, overladen and sailing too low in the water, others that she was mishandled by undisciplined crew. What is undisputed, however, is that the <em>Mary Rose</em> sank into the Solent that day, taking at least 500 men with her. After the battle, attempts were made to recover the ship, but these failed.</span></p><p><span>The <em>Mary Rose</em> came to rest on the seabed, lying on her starboard (right) side at an angle of approximately 60 degrees. The hull (the body of the ship) acted as a trap for the sand and mud carried by Solent currents. As a result, the starboard side filled rapidly, leaving the exposed port (left) side to be eroded by marine organisms and mechanical degradation. Because of the way the ship sank, nearly all of the starboard half <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"a847ba6b-2354-47ad-a78e-fdf557a4036b\">survived intact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. During the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries, the entire site became covered with a layer of hard grey clay, which minimised further erosion.</span></p><p><span>Then, on 16 June 1836, some fishermen in the Solent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a72b9cd1-458c-4a5b-bbaa-42936149bfee\">found that their equipment was caught o<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>n an underwater obstruction, which turned out to be the <em>Mary Rose</em>. Diver John Deane happened to be exploring another sunken ship nearby, and the fishermen approached him, asking him to free their gear. Deane dived down, and found the equipment caught on a timber protruding slightly from the seabed. Exploring further, he uncovered several other timbers and a bronze gun. Deane <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"6\" data-uid=\"840c8102-cabf-44cb-8f65-a1ab3b13378d\">continued diving on the site intermittently until 1840<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, recovering several more guns, two bows, various timbers, part of a pump and various other small finds.</span></p><p><span>The <em>Mary Rose</em> then faded into obscurity for another hundred years. But in 1965, military historian and amateur diver Alexander McKee, in conjunction with the British Sub-Aqua Club, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"8cb57ce0-7d2d-438b-816d-9c5357d0b108\">initiated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> a project called ‘Solent Ships’. While on paper this was a plan to examine a number of known wrecks in the Solent, what McKee really hoped for was to find the <em>Mary Rose</em>. Ordinary search techniques proved unsatisfactory, so McKee entered into collaboration with Harold E. Edgerton, professor of electrical engineering at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology. In 1967, Edgerton’s side-scan sonar systems revealed a large, unusually shaped object, which McKee believed was the <em>Mary Rose</em>.</span></p><p><span>Further excavations revealed stray pieces of timber and an iron gun. But the climax to the operation came when, on 5 May 1971, part of the ship’s frame was uncovered. McKee and his team now knew for certain that they had found the wreck, but were as yet unaware that it also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ad4ad6f7-ef15-4eac-a771-b247c2668c4b\">housed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> a treasure trove of beautifully preserved <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"7a61266e-63ae-4f9b-a48c-1257254a884c\">artefacts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Interest ^ in the project grew, and in 1979, The Mary Rose Trust was formed, with Prince Charles as its President and Dr Margaret Rule its Archaeological Director. The decision whether or not to salvage the wreck was not an easy one, although an excavation in 1978 had shown that it might be possible to raise the hull. While the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d34fac51-04f7-46eb-ac20-02d6539a7ee4\">original aim was to raise the hull<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> if at all feasible, the operation was not given the go-ahead until January 1982, when all the necessary information was available.</span></p><p><span>An important factor in trying to salvage the <em>Mary Rose</em> was that the remaining hull was an open shell. This led to an important decision being taken: namely to carry out the lifting operation in three very distinct stages. The hull was attached to a lifting frame via a network of bolts and lifting wires. The problem of the hull being sucked back downwards into the mud was overcome by using 12 hydraulic jacks. These raised it a few centimetres over a period of several days, as the lifting frame rose slowly up its four legs. It was only when the hull was hanging freely from the lifting frame, clear of the seabed and the suction effect of the surrounding mud, that the salvage operation progressed to the second stage. In this stage, the lifting frame was fixed to a hook attached to a crane, and the hull was lifted completely clear of the seabed and transferred underwater into the lifting cradle. This required precise positioning to locate the legs into the stabbing guides’ of the lifting cradle. The lifting cradle was designed to fit the hull using archaeological survey drawings, and was fitted with air bags to provide additional cushioning for the hull’s delicate timber framework. The third and final stage was to lift the entire structure into the air, by which time the hull was also supported from below. Finally, on 11 October 1982, millions of people around the world held their breath as the timber skeleton of the Mary Rose was lifted clear of the water, ready to be returned home to Portsmouth.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>1-4</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"814\" id=\"question-wrapper-814\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"669ae5df-e3f5-4fd8-bcdc-2a8d47a3fcd8\">some doubt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> about what <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"1\" data-uid=\"36b096d4-72db-4ce2-903d-9154e5a02293\">caused the Mary Rose to sink<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"815\" id=\"question-wrapper-815\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Mary Rose was the only ship to sink in the battle of 19 July 1545. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"816\" id=\"question-wrapper-816\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Most of one side of the Mary Rose <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"3\" data-uid=\"a847ba6b-2354-47ad-a78e-fdf557a4036b\">lay undamaged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> under the sea. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"817\" id=\"question-wrapper-817\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Alexander McKee knew that the wreck would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"ad4ad6f7-ef15-4eac-a771-b247c2668c4b\">contain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> many valuable <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"4\" data-uid=\"7a61266e-63ae-4f9b-a48c-1257254a884c\">historical objects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions <strong>5-8</strong>) and the list of dates below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct date, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>5-8</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Dates</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> 1836 <strong>E</strong> 1971</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> 1840 <strong>F</strong> 1979</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> 1965 <strong>G</strong> 1982</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> 1967</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"818\" id=\"question-wrapper-818\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A search for the Mary Rose <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"5\" data-uid=\"8cb57ce0-7d2d-438b-816d-9c5357d0b108\">was launched<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"819\" id=\"question-wrapper-819\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One person’s exploration of the Mary Rose site stopped. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"820\" id=\"question-wrapper-820\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It was agreed that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"d34fac51-04f7-46eb-ac20-02d6539a7ee4\">the hull of the Mary Rose should be raised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"821\" id=\"question-wrapper-821\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The site of the Mary Rose was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"8\" data-uid=\"a72b9cd1-458c-4a5b-bbaa-42936149bfee\">found by chance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Label the diagram below.</p><p>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>9-13</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p><h4><strong>Raising the hull of the <em>Mary Rose</em>: Stages one and two</strong></h4><p> <span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><em><img src=\"/media/gg_imgs/test/56664ca3e75a572b65b12635487eb3871722dec9.jpg\" style=\"height:509px; width:498px\"></em></span></span></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"822\" id=\"question-wrapper-822\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(LIFTING) FRAME</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"823\" id=\"question-wrapper-823\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HYDRAULIC JACKS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"824\" id=\"question-wrapper-824\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STABBING GUIDES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"825\" id=\"question-wrapper-825\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(LIFTING) CRADLE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"826\" id=\"question-wrapper-826\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AIR BAGS</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"36b096d4-72db-4ce2-903d-9154e5a02293","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"caused the Mary Rose to sink","passagePhrase":"happened to the ship"},{"uid":"669ae5df-e3f5-4fd8-bcdc-2a8d47a3fcd8","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"some doubt","passagePhrase":"some maintain"},{"uid":"a847ba6b-2354-47ad-a78e-fdf557a4036b","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"lay undamaged","passagePhrase":"survived intact"},{"uid":"a72b9cd1-458c-4a5b-bbaa-42936149bfee","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"found by chance","passagePhrase":"found that their equipment was caught o"},{"uid":"840c8102-cabf-44cb-8f65-a1ab3b13378d","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"continued diving on the site intermittently until 1840"},{"uid":"8cb57ce0-7d2d-438b-816d-9c5357d0b108","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"was launched","passagePhrase":"initiated"},{"uid":"ad4ad6f7-ef15-4eac-a771-b247c2668c4b","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"contain","passagePhrase":"housed"},{"uid":"7a61266e-63ae-4f9b-a48c-1257254a884c","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"historical objects","passagePhrase":"artefacts"},{"uid":"d34fac51-04f7-46eb-ac20-02d6539a7ee4","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"the hull of the Mary Rose should be raised","passagePhrase":"original aim was to raise the hull"}]},"reading_u2_203":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>What destroyed the civilisation of Easter Island?</strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>Easter Island, or Rapu Nui as it is known locally, is home to several hundred ancient human statues – the moai. After this remote Pacific island was settled by the Polynesians, it remained isolated for centuries. All the energy and resources that went into the moai – some of which are ten metres tall and weigh over 7,000 kilos – came from the island itself. Yet when Dutch explorers landed in 1722, they met a Stone Age culture. The moai were carved with stone tools, then transported for many kilometres, without the use of animals or wheels, to massive stone platforms. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"314f1667-dfe0-4e08-9173-8c2580ca2f13\" data-question=\"14\">The identity of the moai builders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> was in doubt until well into the twentieth century. Thor Heyerdahl, the Norwegian ethnographer and adventurer, thought the statues had been created by pre-Inca peoples from Peru. Bestselling Swiss author Erich von Daniken believed they were built by stranded extraterrestrials. Modern science – linguistic, archaeological and genetic evidence – has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4e9099b6-fea2-4172-b825-ab3e46383127\" data-question=\"14\">definitively proved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the moai builders were Polynesians, but not how they moved their creations. Local folklore maintains that the statues walked, while researchers have tended to assume the ancestors dragged the statues somehow, using ropes and logs.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>When the Europeans arrived, Rapa Nui was grassland, with only a few scrawny trees. In the 1970s and 1980s, though, researchers found pollen preserved in lake sediments, which proved the island had been covered in lush palm forests for thousands of years. Only after the Polynesians arrived did those forests disappear. US scientist Jared Diamond believes that the Rapanui people – descendants of Polynesian settlers – wrecked their own environment. They had unfortunately settled on an extremely fragile island – dry, cool, and too remote to be properly fertilised by windblown volcanic ash. When the islanders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe87f29a-87a2-4c5e-8101-037100b464c6\" data-question=\"21\">cleared the forests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> for firewood and farming, the forests didn’t grow back. As trees became scarce and they could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"baa561c4-fc54-4d0c-9e54-54ad812d33a7\" data-question=\"15\">no longer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ec119ef-810e-4333-9a47-b891fad256b0\" data-question=\"22\">construct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> wooden canoes for fishing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d84305e6-b334-441b-a3e8-caec08af9dad\" data-question=\"23\">ate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> birds. Soil erosion <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"baa561c4-fc54-4d0c-9e54-54ad812d33a7\" data-question=\"15\">decreased their crop yields<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Before Europeans arrived, the Rapanui had descended into civil war and cannibalism, he maintains. The collapse of their isolated civilisation, Diamond writes, is a ’worst-case scenario for what may lie ahead of us in our own future’.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>The moai, he thinks, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61f642bc-bb0f-4f67-bc2a-9aa11d0b418b\" data-question=\"16\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"96f89328-4df8-40c9-b8bc-0dddee0b6b22\" data-question=\"26\">accelerated the self-destruction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Diamond interprets them as power displays by rival chieftains who, trapped on a remote little island, lacked other ways of asserting their dominance. They competed by building ever bigger figures. Diamond thinks they laid <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"38a53292-5fab-4416-933b-dc4294430a5e\" data-question=\"16\">the moai<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> on wooden sledges, hauled over log rails, but that required both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4dcdf36-9312-44da-ab7a-38c5fbf90343\" data-question=\"24\">a lot of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> wood and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4dcdf36-9312-44da-ab7a-38c5fbf90343\" data-question=\"24\">a lot of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> people. To feed the people, even more land had to be cleared. When the wood was gone and civil war began, the islanders began toppling the moai. By the nineteenth century none were standing.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>Archaeologists Terry Hunt of the University of Hawaii and Carl Lipo of California State University agree that Easter Island lost its lush forests and that it was an ‘ecological catastrophe’ – but they believe the islanders themselves weren’t to blame. And the moai certainly weren’t. Archaeological excavations indicate that the Rapanui went to heroic efforts to protect the resources of their wind-lashed, infertile fields. They built thousands of circular stone windbreaks and gardened inside them, and used broken volcanic rocks to keep the soil moist. In short, Hunt and Lipo argue, the prehistoric Rapanui were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"75671662-62fc-40a3-908a-998f2abf66d7\" data-question=\"17\">pioneers of sustainable farming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Hunt and Lipo contend that moai-building was an activity that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"96f89328-4df8-40c9-b8bc-0dddee0b6b22\" data-question=\"26\">helped keep the peace between islanders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. They also believe that moving <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d545d818-6bfd-4ddf-9a83-850329c72cf8\" data-question=\"25\">the moai required few people and no wood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, because they were walked upright. On that issue, Hunt and Lipo say, archaeological evidence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4eaeeec6-dcba-4ed6-a444-9b42a9140e3f\" data-question=\"18\">backs up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> Rapanui folklore. Recent experiments indicate that as few as 18 people could, with three strong ropes and a bit of practice, easily manoeuvre a 1,000 kg moai replica a few hundred metres. The figures’ fat bellies tilted them forward, and a D-shaped base allowed handlers to roll and rock them side to side.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>Moreover, Hunt and Lipo are convinced that the settlers were not wholly responsible for the loss of the island’s trees. Archaeological finds of nuts from the extinct Easter Island palm show tiny grooves, made by the teeth of Polynesian rats. The rats arrived along with the settlers, and in just a few years, Hunt and Lipo calculate, they would have overrun the island. They would have prevented the reseeding of the slow-growing palm trees and thereby doomed Rapa Nui’s forest, even without the settlers’ campaign of deforestation. No doubt the rats ate birds’ eggs too. Hunt and Lipo also see no evidence that Rapanui civilisation collapsed when the palm forest did. They think its population grew rapidly and then remained more or less stable until the arrival of the Europeans, who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"14dcbfd8-57b3-457a-9196-51ca441de08b\" data-question=\"19\">introduced deadly diseases to which islanders had no immunity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Then in the nineteenth century slave traders decimated the population, which shrivelled to 111 people by 1877.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>Hunt and Lipo’s vision, therefore, is one of an island <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a41753c3-dd35-4834-b3a6-735ffd51d522\" data-question=\"20\">populated by peaceful and ingenious moai builder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>s and careful stewards of the land, rather than by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a41753c3-dd35-4834-b3a6-735ffd51d522\" data-question=\"20\">reckless destroyers ruining their own environment and society<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. ‘Rather than a case of abject failure, Rapu Nui is an unlikely story of success’, they claim. Whichever is the case, there are surely some valuable lessons which the world at large can learn from the story of Rapa Nui.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct number, <strong>i-ix</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-20</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Headings</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>i </strong> Evidence of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"75671662-62fc-40a3-908a-998f2abf66d7\" data-question=\"17\">innovative environment management practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>ii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4e9099b6-fea2-4172-b825-ab3e46383127\" data-question=\"14\">An undisputed answer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"314f1667-dfe0-4e08-9173-8c2580ca2f13\" data-question=\"14\">a question<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> about the moai</span></p><p><span><strong>iii</strong> The future of the moai statues</span></p><p><span><strong>iv</strong> A theory which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4eaeeec6-dcba-4ed6-a444-9b42a9140e3f\" data-question=\"18\">supports<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f659069-8de5-49ce-99e3-badc57ab5fa8\" data-question=\"18\">local belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>v</strong> The future of Easter Island</span></p><p><span><strong>vi</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a41753c3-dd35-4834-b3a6-735ffd51d522\" data-question=\"20\">Two opposing views<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> about the Rapanui people</span></p><p><span><strong>vii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"14dcbfd8-57b3-457a-9196-51ca441de08b\" data-question=\"19\">Destruction outside the inhabitants’ control<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>viii</strong> How <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"38a53292-5fab-4416-933b-dc4294430a5e\" data-question=\"16\">the statues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61f642bc-bb0f-4f67-bc2a-9aa11d0b418b\" data-question=\"16\">made a situation worse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>ix</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"baa561c4-fc54-4d0c-9e54-54ad812d33a7\" data-question=\"15\">Diminishing food resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"827\" id=\"question-wrapper-827\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"828\" id=\"question-wrapper-828\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IX</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"829\" id=\"question-wrapper-829\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"830\" id=\"question-wrapper-830\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"831\" id=\"question-wrapper-831\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"832\" id=\"question-wrapper-832\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"833\" id=\"question-wrapper-833\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>21-24</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>Jared Diamond’s View</strong></span></h4><p><span>Diamond believes that the Polynesian settlers on Rapa Nui destroyed its forests, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe87f29a-87a2-4c5e-8101-037100b464c6\" data-question=\"21\">cutting down its trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> for fuel and clearing land for <strong>21</strong>……………. Twentieth-century discoveries of pollen prove that Rapu Nui had once been covered in palm forests, which had turned into grassland by the time the Europeans arrived on the island. When the islanders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"792b183b-9147-4ab3-8a84-f2377c2f7480\" data-question=\"22\">were no longer able to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> build the <strong>22</strong>…………… they needed to go fishing, they began using the island’s <strong>23</strong>…………….. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d84305e6-b334-441b-a3e8-caec08af9dad\" data-question=\"23\">as a food source<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, according to Diamond. Diamond also claims that the moai were built to show the power of the island’s chieftains, and that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"428f8fe3-c75c-4adc-ab48-8df274a9a676\" data-question=\"24\">methods of transporting the statues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> needed not only a great number of people, but also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4dcdf36-9312-44da-ab7a-38c5fbf90343\" data-question=\"24\">a great deal of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <strong>24</strong>……………….</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"834\" id=\"question-wrapper-834\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FARMING</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"835\" id=\"question-wrapper-835\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CANOES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"836\" id=\"question-wrapper-836\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BIRDS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"837\" id=\"question-wrapper-837\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WOOD</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letters in boxes <strong>25</strong> and <strong>26</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>On what points do Hunt and Lipo disagree with Diamond?</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> the period when the moai were created</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> how the moai were transported</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> the impact of the moai on Rapanui society</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> how the moai were carved</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> the origins of the people who made the moai</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"838\" id=\"question-wrapper-838\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"839\" id=\"question-wrapper-839\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"314f1667-dfe0-4e08-9173-8c2580ca2f13","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"a question","passagePhrase":"The identity of the moai builders"},{"uid":"4e9099b6-fea2-4172-b825-ab3e46383127","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"An undisputed answer","passagePhrase":"definitively proved"},{"uid":"fe87f29a-87a2-4c5e-8101-037100b464c6","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"cutting down its trees","passagePhrase":"cleared the forests"},{"uid":"baa561c4-fc54-4d0c-9e54-54ad812d33a7","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Diminishing food resources","passagePhrase":"no longer construct wooden canoes for fishing ... decreased their crop yields"},{"uid":"1ec119ef-810e-4333-9a47-b891fad256b0","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"construct"},{"uid":"d84305e6-b334-441b-a3e8-caec08af9dad","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"as a food source","passagePhrase":"ate"},{"uid":"61f642bc-bb0f-4f67-bc2a-9aa11d0b418b","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"made a situation worse","passagePhrase":"accelerated the self-destruction"},{"uid":"38a53292-5fab-4416-933b-dc4294430a5e","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"the statues","passagePhrase":"the moai"},{"uid":"b4dcdf36-9312-44da-ab7a-38c5fbf90343","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"a great deal of","passagePhrase":"a lot of ... a lot of"},{"uid":"75671662-62fc-40a3-908a-998f2abf66d7","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"innovative environment management practices","passagePhrase":"pioneers of sustainable farming"},{"uid":"4eaeeec6-dcba-4ed6-a444-9b42a9140e3f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"supports","passagePhrase":"backs up"},{"uid":"14dcbfd8-57b3-457a-9196-51ca441de08b","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Destruction outside the inhabitants’ control","passagePhrase":"introduced deadly diseases to which islanders had no immunity"},{"uid":"a41753c3-dd35-4834-b3a6-735ffd51d522","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Two opposing views","passagePhrase":"populated by peaceful and ingenious moai builder ... reckless destroyers ruining their own environment and society"},{"uid":"2f659069-8de5-49ce-99e3-badc57ab5fa8","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"local belief","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"792b183b-9147-4ab3-8a84-f2377c2f7480","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"were no longer able to","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"428f8fe3-c75c-4adc-ab48-8df274a9a676","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"methods of transporting the statues","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_204":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</p><p> </p><h2><strong>Neuroaesthetics</strong></h2><p>An <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4bcd4b8e-60fb-4b32-9779-a089afb9a546\" data-question=\"40\">emerging discipline called neuroaesthetics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> is seeking to bring scientific objectivity to the study of art, and has already given us a better understanding of many masterpieces. The blurred imagery of Impressionist paintings seems to stimulate the brain’s amygdala, for instance. Since the amygdala plays a crucial role in our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba6ecbf8-0cfc-48f6-8f5b-ed00370c1ff6\" data-question=\"31\">feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, that finding might explain why many people find these pieces so moving.</p><p>Could the same approach also shed light on abstract twentieth-century pieces, from Mondrian’s geometrical blocks of colour, to Pollock’s seemingly haphazard arrangements of splashed paint on canvas? Sceptics believe that people claim to like such works simply because they are famous. We certainly do have an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e328b076-03e7-45d7-ac29-5494a65d4a3e\" data-question=\"27\">inclination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d825ea2-4943-4a2b-853b-565f85eb4077\" data-question=\"27\">follow the crowd<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. When asked to make simple perceptual decisions such as matching a shape to its rotated image, for example, people often choose a definitively wrong answer if they see others doing the same. It is easy to imagine that this mentality would have even more impact on a fuzzy concept like art appreciation, where there is no right or wrong answer.</p><p>Angelina Hawley-Dolan, of Boston College, Massachusetts, responded to this debate by asking volunteers to view pairs of paintings – either the creations of famous abstract artists or the doodles of infants, chimps and elephants. They then had to judge which they preferred. A third of the paintings were given no captions, while many were labelled incorrectly -volunteers might think they were viewing a chimp’s messy brushstrokes when they were actually seeing an acclaimed masterpiece. In each set of trials, volunteers generally preferred the work of renowned artists, even when they believed it was by an animal or a child. It seems that the viewer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b71b1f53-1b66-444a-9989-0d9947463470\" data-question=\"28\">can sense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5690e61d-05cb-4e1e-8473-893dac25e33e\" data-question=\"28\">the artist’s vision in paintings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, even if they can’t explain why.</p><p>Robert Pepperell, an artist based at Cardiff University, creates ambiguous works that are neither entirely abstract nor clearly representational. In one study, Pepperell and his collaborators asked volunteers to decide how’powerful’they considered an artwork to be, and whether they saw anything familiar in the piece. The longer they took to answer these questions, the more highly they rated the piece under scrutiny, and the greater their neural activity. It would seem that the brain sees these images as puzzles, and the harder it is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cef4f661-2646-4b40-9b1b-571e90e54f0f\" data-question=\"29\">decipher the meaning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, the more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1f3689e0-256b-4515-ad54-7eb57308c3d4\" data-question=\"29\">rewarding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> is the moment of recognition.</p><p>And what about artists such as Mondrian, whose paintings consist exclusively of horizontal and vertical lines encasing blocks of colour? <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b9a8236f-6f5b-4b36-bd94-0a83219d4747\" data-question=\"30\">Mondrian’s works<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> are deceptively simple, but eye-tracking studies confirm that they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba4474de-dac3-4ba7-8cf8-30db2aafec85\" data-question=\"30\">meticulously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f50a04d6-d72e-4c4e-a483-32ac03307de6\" data-question=\"30\">composed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, and that simply rotating a piece radically changes the way we view it. With the originals, volunteers’eyes tended to stay longer on certain places in the image, but with the altered versions they would flit across a piece more rapidly. As a result, the volunteers considered the altered versions less pleasurable when they later rated the work.</p><p>In a similar study, Oshin Vartanian of Toronto University asked volunteers to compare original paintings with ones which he had altered by moving objects around within the frame. He found that almost everyone preferred the original, whether it was a Van Gogh still life or an abstract by Miro. Vartanian also found that changing the composition of the paintings reduced activation in those brain areas linked with meaning and interpretation.</p><p>In another experiment, Alex Forsythe of the University of Liverpool analysed the visual <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d143c184-fe8b-4705-b206-a7543ac95d5f\" data-question=\"32\">intricacy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of different pieces of art, and her results suggest that many artists use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"30a3685f-5499-40f5-89f2-aa899ba2d030\" data-question=\"32\">a key level of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d143c184-fe8b-4705-b206-a7543ac95d5f\" data-question=\"32\">detail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to please the brain. Too little and the work is boring, but too much results in a kind of ‘perceptual overload’, according to Forsythe. What’s more, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"91a4479b-b64a-4a77-89d8-2e25d9c6d600\" data-question=\"33\">appealing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> pieces both abstract and representational, show signs of ‘fractals’ – repeated motifs recurring in different scales, fractals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f5bb931d-e21f-4464-8929-5a2ab686d12b\" data-question=\"33\">are common<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> throughout nature, for example in the shapes of mountain peaks or the branches of trees. It is possible that our visual system, which evolved in the great outdoors, finds it easier to process such patterns.</p><p>It is also intriguing that the brain appears to process movement when we see a handwritten letter, as if we are replaying the writer’s moment of creation. This has led some to wonder whether Pollock’s works feel so dynamic because the brain reconstructs the energetic actions the artist used as he painted. This may be down to our brain’s ‘mirror neurons’, which are known to mimic others’ actions. The hypothesis <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5103fd39-d785-43a8-95b8-682b6d22f1f8\" data-question=\"35\">will need to be thoroughly tested<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, however. It might even be the case that we could use neuroaesthetic studies to understand the longevity of some pieces of artwork. While the fashions of the time might shape what is currently popular, works that are best adapted to our visual system <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"87de94b1-a1d8-4250-8886-6a6f32f8bb7d\" data-question=\"36\">may be the most likely to linger once the trends of previous generations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> have been forgotten.</p><p>It’s still early days for the field of neuroaesthetics – and these studies are probably only a taste of what is to come. It would, however, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e7b84e96-f278-4c4e-b946-6f437ff1dbf6\" data-question=\"37\">be foolish to reduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> art appreciation to a set of scientific laws. We shouldn’t underestimate the importance of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"579e65e9-dea7-46fd-9ab8-fac45e1e3e8f\" data-question=\"38\">the style of a particular artist, their place in history and the artistic environment of their time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. Abstract art offers both a challenge and the freedom to play with different interpretations. In some ways, it’s not so different to science, where we are constantly looking for systems and decoding meaning so that we can view and appreciate the world in a new way.</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>27-30</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"840\" id=\"question-wrapper-840\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the second paragraph, the writer refers to a shape-matching test in order to illustrate </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the subjective nature of art appreciation.</li> <li>B. the reliance of modern art on abstract forms.</li> <li>C. our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e328b076-03e7-45d7-ac29-5494a65d4a3e\" data-question=\"27\">tendency<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d825ea2-4943-4a2b-853b-565f85eb4077\" data-question=\"27\">be influenced by the opinions of others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>D. a common problem encountered when processing visual data.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"841\" id=\"question-wrapper-841\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Angelina Hawley-Dolan’s findings indicate that people </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. mostly favour works of art which they know well.</li> <li>B. hold fixed ideas about what makes a good work of art.</li> <li>C. are often misled by their initial expectations of a work of art.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b71b1f53-1b66-444a-9989-0d9947463470\" data-question=\"28\">have the ability to perceive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5690e61d-05cb-4e1e-8473-893dac25e33e\" data-question=\"28\">the intention behind works of art<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"842\" id=\"question-wrapper-842\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Results of studies involving Robert Pepperell’s pieces suggest that people </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. can appreciate a painting without fully understanding it.</li> <li>B. find it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1f3689e0-256b-4515-ad54-7eb57308c3d4\" data-question=\"29\">satisfying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cef4f661-2646-4b40-9b1b-571e90e54f0f\" data-question=\"29\">work out what a painting represents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>C. vary widely in the time they spend looking at paintings.</li> <li>D. generally prefer representational art to abstract art.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"843\" id=\"question-wrapper-843\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What do the experiments described in the fifth paragraph suggest about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b9a8236f-6f5b-4b36-bd94-0a83219d4747\" data-question=\"30\">the paintings of Mondrian<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They are more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba4474de-dac3-4ba7-8cf8-30db2aafec85\" data-question=\"30\">carefully<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f50a04d6-d72e-4c4e-a483-32ac03307de6\" data-question=\"30\">put together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> than they appear.</li> <li>B. They can be interpreted in a number of different ways.</li> <li>C. They challenge our assumptions about shape and colour.</li> <li>D. They are easier to appreciate than many other abstract works.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, <strong>A-H</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letters, <strong>A-H</strong>, in boxes <strong>31-33</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>Art and the Brain</strong></span></h4><p><span>The discipline of neuroaesthetics aims to bring scientific objectivity to the study of art. Neurological studies of the brain, for example, demonstrate the impact which Impressionist paintings have on our <strong>31</strong>……………. Alex Forsythe of the University of Liverpool believes many artists give their works <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"30a3685f-5499-40f5-89f2-aa899ba2d030\" data-question=\"32\">the precise degree of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <strong>32</strong>……………… which most appeals to the viewer’s brain. She also observes that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"91a4479b-b64a-4a77-89d8-2e25d9c6d600\" data-question=\"33\">pleasing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> works of art often contain certain repeated <strong>33</strong>……………… which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f5bb931d-e21f-4464-8929-5a2ab686d12b\" data-question=\"33\">occur frequently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> in the natural world.</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> interpretation <strong>B</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d143c184-fe8b-4705-b206-a7543ac95d5f\" data-question=\"32\">complexity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <strong>C</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba6ecbf8-0cfc-48f6-8f5b-ed00370c1ff6\" data-question=\"31\">emotions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> movements <strong>E</strong> skill <strong>F</strong> layout</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong> concern <strong>H</strong> images</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"844\" id=\"question-wrapper-844\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"845\" id=\"question-wrapper-845\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"846\" id=\"question-wrapper-846\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>34-39</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"847\" id=\"question-wrapper-847\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Forsythe’s findings contradicted previous beliefs on the function of ‘fractals’ in art. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"848\" id=\"question-wrapper-848\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Certain ideas regarding the link between ‘mirror neurons’ and art appreciation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5103fd39-d785-43a8-95b8-682b6d22f1f8\" data-question=\"35\">require further verification<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"849\" id=\"question-wrapper-849\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People’s taste in paintings <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"87de94b1-a1d8-4250-8886-6a6f32f8bb7d\" data-question=\"36\">depends entirely on the current artistic trends of the period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"850\" id=\"question-wrapper-850\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Scientists <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e7b84e96-f278-4c4e-b946-6f437ff1dbf6\" data-question=\"37\">should seek to define<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> the precise rules which govern <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"731bd4ed-dc0a-47fb-a41d-f10b42e4484d\" data-question=\"37\">people’s reactions to works of art<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"851\" id=\"question-wrapper-851\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Art appreciation should always involve taking into consideration <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"579e65e9-dea7-46fd-9ab8-fac45e1e3e8f\" data-question=\"38\">the cultural context in which an artist worked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"852\" id=\"question-wrapper-852\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is easier to find meaning in the field of science than in that of art. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in box <strong>40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"853\" id=\"question-wrapper-853\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What would be the most appropriate subtitle for the article? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4bcd4b8e-60fb-4b32-9779-a089afb9a546\" data-question=\"40\">Some scientific insights<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> into how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b2fe6e3-e93c-425a-ad19-70d958e17cee\" data-question=\"40\">the brain responds to abstract art<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></li> <li>B. Recent studies focusing on the neural activity of abstract artists</li> <li>C. A comparison of the neurological bases of abstract and representational art</li> <li>D. How brain research has altered public opinion about abstract art</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"4bcd4b8e-60fb-4b32-9779-a089afb9a546","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Some scientific insights","passagePhrase":"emerging discipline called neuroaesthetics"},{"uid":"ba6ecbf8-0cfc-48f6-8f5b-ed00370c1ff6","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"emotions","passagePhrase":"feelings"},{"uid":"e328b076-03e7-45d7-ac29-5494a65d4a3e","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"tendency","passagePhrase":"inclination"},{"uid":"3d825ea2-4943-4a2b-853b-565f85eb4077","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"be influenced by the opinions of others","passagePhrase":"follow the crowd"},{"uid":"b71b1f53-1b66-444a-9989-0d9947463470","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"have the ability to perceive","passagePhrase":"can sense"},{"uid":"5690e61d-05cb-4e1e-8473-893dac25e33e","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"the intention behind works of art","passagePhrase":"the artist’s vision in paintings"},{"uid":"cef4f661-2646-4b40-9b1b-571e90e54f0f","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"work out what a painting represents","passagePhrase":"decipher the meaning"},{"uid":"1f3689e0-256b-4515-ad54-7eb57308c3d4","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"satisfying","passagePhrase":"rewarding"},{"uid":"b9a8236f-6f5b-4b36-bd94-0a83219d4747","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"the paintings of Mondrian","passagePhrase":"Mondrian’s works"},{"uid":"ba4474de-dac3-4ba7-8cf8-30db2aafec85","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"carefully","passagePhrase":"meticulously"},{"uid":"f50a04d6-d72e-4c4e-a483-32ac03307de6","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"put together","passagePhrase":"composed"},{"uid":"d143c184-fe8b-4705-b206-a7543ac95d5f","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"complexity","passagePhrase":"intricacy ... detail"},{"uid":"30a3685f-5499-40f5-89f2-aa899ba2d030","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"the precise degree of","passagePhrase":"a key level of"},{"uid":"91a4479b-b64a-4a77-89d8-2e25d9c6d600","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"pleasing","passagePhrase":"appealing"},{"uid":"f5bb931d-e21f-4464-8929-5a2ab686d12b","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"occur frequently","passagePhrase":"are common"},{"uid":"5103fd39-d785-43a8-95b8-682b6d22f1f8","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"require further verification","passagePhrase":"will need to be thoroughly tested"},{"uid":"579e65e9-dea7-46fd-9ab8-fac45e1e3e8f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"the cultural context in which an artist worked","passagePhrase":"the style of a particular artist, their place in history and the artistic environment of their time"},{"uid":"731bd4ed-dc0a-47fb-a41d-f10b42e4484d","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"people’s reactions to works of art","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"4b2fe6e3-e93c-425a-ad19-70d958e17cee","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"the brain responds to abstract art","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_205":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><h2><span><strong>The story of silk</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>The history of the world’s most luxurious fabric, from ancient China to the present day</em></span></p><p><span>Silk is a fine, smooth material produced from the cocoons – soft protective shells – that are made by mulberry silkworms (insect larvae). Legend has it that it was Lei Tzu, wife of the Yellow Emperor, ruler of China in about 3000 BC, who discovered silkworms. One account of the story goes that as she was taking a walk in her husband’s gardens, she discovered that silkworms were responsible for the destruction of several mulberry trees. She collected a number of cocoons and sat down to have a rest. It just so happened that while she was sipping some tea, one of the cocoons that she had collected <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8cc92492-a3ff-447d-888d-42175267c364\" data-question=\"1\">landed in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> the hot tea and started to unravel into a fine thread. Lei Tzu found that she could wind this thread around her fingers. Subsequently, she persuaded her husband to allow her to rear silkworms on a grove of mulberry trees. She also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28399234-5a96-43b7-b07f-f1b64d142053\" data-question=\"2\">devised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> a special reel to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d1707c9-8932-46ee-afac-367a4f3b21aa\" data-question=\"2\">draw the fibres from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the cocoon into a single thread so that they would be strong enough to be woven into fabric. While it is unknown just how much of this is true, it is certainly known that silk cultivation has existed in China for several millennia.</span></p><p><span>Originally, silkworm farming <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"984782c2-64bb-4eaa-8d00-a0d8b9b3ece1\" data-question=\"3\">was solely restricted to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> women, and it was they who were responsible for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a175672e-a37f-4db0-afc6-261b8f83cf4f\" data-question=\"3\">the growing, harvesting and weaving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. Silk quickly grew into a symbol of status, and originally, only royalty <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec676905-a55b-4b26-aff1-609632cb0433\" data-question=\"4\">were entitled to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a2ef043-fb9f-46cb-8b66-b7006799b19b\" data-question=\"4\">have clothes made of silk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. The rules were gradually relaxed over the years until finally during the Qing Dynasty (1644—1911 AD), even peasants, the lowest caste, were also entitled to wear silk. Sometime during the Han Dynasty (206 BC-220 AD), silk was so prized that it was also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3a4e014-0b56-474e-9f70-4ad2e8462938\" data-question=\"5\">used as a unit of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> currency. Government officials were paid their salary in silk, and farmers paid their taxes in grain and silk. Silk was also used as diplomatic gifts by the emperor. Fishing lines, bowstrings, musical instruments and paper were all made using silk. The earliest <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3784145b-5e53-48c5-b7e6-258e4eb5cb5c\" data-question=\"6\">indication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of silk paper being used was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4a8e3b8b-51d0-454c-a5b6-0234c63dbdbb\" data-question=\"6\">discovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> in the tomb of a noble who is estimated to have died around 168 AD.</span></p><p><span>Demand for this exotic fabric eventually created the lucrative trade route now known as the Silk Road, taking silk westward and bringing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"25364d7f-80ec-4c0d-9f45-9182c2503e50\" data-question=\"7\">gold, silver<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and wool to the East. It was named the Silk Road after its most precious commodity, which was considered to be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2dca966a-2a4a-4c01-af87-1f1b45626fec\" data-question=\"10\">worth more than gold<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. The Silk Road stretched over 6,000 kilometres from Eastern China to the Mediterranean Sea, following the Great Wall of China, climbing the Pamir mountain range, crossing modern-day Afghanistan and going on to the Middle East, with a major trading market in Damascus. From there, the merchandise was shipped across the Mediterranean Sea. Few <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2502c5af-2356-433e-a713-3fc3c7699fc3\" data-question=\"11\">merchants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f7cc2c0-c8fe-4da5-abea-6b807694a8b9\" data-question=\"11\">travelled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the entire route; goods were handled mostly by a series of middlemen.</span></p><p><span>With the mulberry silkworm being native to China, the country was the world’s sole producer of silk for many hundreds of years. The secret of silk-making eventually reached the rest of the world via the Byzantine Empire, which ruled over the Mediterranean region of southern Europe, North Africa and the Middle East during the period 330—1453 AD. According to another legend, monks working for the Byzantine emperor Justinian smuggle silkworm eggs to Constantinople (Istanbul in modern-day Turkey) in 550 AD, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"45e74989-059e-467a-8698-6688b1f07c49\" data-question=\"8\">concealed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> inside hollow bamboo walking canes. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ef6a3e32-79bb-4934-94e6-9a926077ce0e\" data-question=\"12\">The Byzantines were as secretive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> as the Chinese, however, and for many centuries the weaving and trading of silk fabric was a strict imperial monopoly. Then in the seventh century, the Arabs conquered Persia, capturing their magnificent silks in the process.</span></p><p><span>Silk production thus spread through Africa, Sicily and Spain as the Arabs swept, through these lands. Andalusia in southern Spain was Europe’s main silk-producing centre in the tenth century. By the thirteenth century, however, Italy had become Europe’s leader in silk production and export. Venetian merchants traded extensively in silk and encouraged silk growers to settle in Italy. Even now, silk processed in the province of Como in northern Italy enjoys an esteemed reputation.</span></p><p><span>The nineteenth century and industrialisation saw the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5d0b511-f5aa-475d-aa13-4c61f55c6e45\" data-question=\"9\">downfall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of the European silk industry. Cheaper Japanese silk, trade in which was greatly facilitated by the opening of the Suez Canal, was one of the many factors driving the trend. Then in the twentieth century, new manmade fibres, such as nylon, started to be used in what had traditionally been silk products, such as stockings and parachutes. The two world wars, which interrupted the supply of raw material from Japan, also stifled the European silk industry. After the Second World War, Japan’s silk production was restored, with improved production and quality of raw silk. Japan was to remain the world’s biggest producer of raw silk, and practically the only major exporter of raw silk, until the 1970s. However, in more recent decades, China has gradually recaptured its position as the world’s biggest producer and exporter of raw silk and silk yarn. Today, around 125,000 metric tons of silk are produced in the world, and almost two thirds of that production takes place in China.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>1-9</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>THE STORY OF SILK</strong></span></h4><p><span><strong>Early silk production in China</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>•</strong> Around 3000 BC, according to legend:</span></p><p><span>– silkworm cocoon <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8cc92492-a3ff-447d-888d-42175267c364\" data-question=\"1\">fell into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> emperor’s wife’s <strong>1</strong>………………</span></p><p><span>– emperor’s wife <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28399234-5a96-43b7-b07f-f1b64d142053\" data-question=\"2\">invented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> a <strong>2</strong>……………. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d1707c9-8932-46ee-afac-367a4f3b21aa\" data-question=\"2\">pull out silk fibres<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p><p><span><span><strong>•</strong></span> Only <strong>3</strong>……………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"984782c2-64bb-4eaa-8d00-a0d8b9b3ece1\" data-question=\"3\">were allowed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a175672e-a37f-4db0-afc6-261b8f83cf4f\" data-question=\"3\">produce silk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p><span><span><strong>•</strong></span> Only <strong>4</strong>………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec676905-a55b-4b26-aff1-609632cb0433\" data-question=\"4\">were allowed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> wear silk</span></p><p><span><span><strong>•</strong></span> Silk <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3a4e014-0b56-474e-9f70-4ad2e8462938\" data-question=\"5\">used as a form of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <strong>5</strong>……………….</span></p><p><span>– e.g. farmers’ taxes consisted partly of silk</span></p><p><span><span><strong>•</strong></span> Silk used for many purposes</span></p><p><span>– e.g. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3784145b-5e53-48c5-b7e6-258e4eb5cb5c\" data-question=\"6\">evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> found of <strong>6</strong>……………… made from silk around 168 AD</span></p><p><span><strong>Silk reaches rest of world</strong></span></p><p><span><span><strong>• </strong></span>Merchants use Silk Road to take silk westward and bring back <strong>7</strong>…………….. and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"25364d7f-80ec-4c0d-9f45-9182c2503e50\" data-question=\"7\">precious metals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></span></p><p><span><span><strong>• </strong></span>550 AD: <strong>8</strong>……………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"45e74989-059e-467a-8698-6688b1f07c49\" data-question=\"8\">hide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> silkworm eggs in canes and take them to Constantinople</span></p><p><span><span><strong>• </strong></span>Silk production spreads across Middle East and Europe</span></p><p><span><span><strong>• </strong></span>20th century: <strong>9</strong>……………… and other manmade fibres cause <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5d0b511-f5aa-475d-aa13-4c61f55c6e45\" data-question=\"9\">decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> in silk production</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20238\" id=\"question-wrapper-20238\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TEA</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20239\" id=\"question-wrapper-20239\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">REEL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20240\" id=\"question-wrapper-20240\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WOMEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20241\" id=\"question-wrapper-20241\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ROYALTY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20242\" id=\"question-wrapper-20242\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CURRENCY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20243\" id=\"question-wrapper-20243\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PAPER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20244\" id=\"question-wrapper-20244\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WOOL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20245\" id=\"question-wrapper-20245\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MONKS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20246\" id=\"question-wrapper-20246\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NYLON</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information in Reading Passage?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>10-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20247\" id=\"question-wrapper-20247\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2dca966a-2a4a-4c01-af87-1f1b45626fec\" data-question=\"10\">Gold was the most valuable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> material transported along the Silk Road. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20248\" id=\"question-wrapper-20248\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2502c5af-2356-433e-a713-3fc3c7699fc3\" data-question=\"11\">tradesmen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f7cc2c0-c8fe-4da5-abea-6b807694a8b9\" data-question=\"11\">went along<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> certain sections of the Silk Road. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20249\" id=\"question-wrapper-20249\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ef6a3e32-79bb-4934-94e6-9a926077ce0e\" data-question=\"12\">The Byzantines spread the practice of silk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> production across the West. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20250\" id=\"question-wrapper-20250\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Silk yarn makes up the majority of silk currently exported from China. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"8cc92492-a3ff-447d-888d-42175267c364","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"fell into","passagePhrase":"landed in"},{"uid":"28399234-5a96-43b7-b07f-f1b64d142053","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"invented","passagePhrase":"devised"},{"uid":"0d1707c9-8932-46ee-afac-367a4f3b21aa","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"pull out silk fibres","passagePhrase":"draw the fibres from"},{"uid":"984782c2-64bb-4eaa-8d00-a0d8b9b3ece1","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"were allowed to","passagePhrase":"was solely restricted to"},{"uid":"a175672e-a37f-4db0-afc6-261b8f83cf4f","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"produce silk","passagePhrase":"the growing, harvesting and weaving"},{"uid":"ec676905-a55b-4b26-aff1-609632cb0433","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"were allowed to","passagePhrase":"were entitled to"},{"uid":"1a2ef043-fb9f-46cb-8b66-b7006799b19b","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"have clothes made of silk"},{"uid":"a3a4e014-0b56-474e-9f70-4ad2e8462938","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"used as a form of","passagePhrase":"used as a unit of"},{"uid":"3784145b-5e53-48c5-b7e6-258e4eb5cb5c","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"evidence","passagePhrase":"indication"},{"uid":"4a8e3b8b-51d0-454c-a5b6-0234c63dbdbb","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"discovered"},{"uid":"25364d7f-80ec-4c0d-9f45-9182c2503e50","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"precious metals","passagePhrase":"gold, silver"},{"uid":"2502c5af-2356-433e-a713-3fc3c7699fc3","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"tradesmen","passagePhrase":"merchants"},{"uid":"6f7cc2c0-c8fe-4da5-abea-6b807694a8b9","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"went along","passagePhrase":"travelled"},{"uid":"45e74989-059e-467a-8698-6688b1f07c49","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"hide","passagePhrase":"concealed"},{"uid":"e5d0b511-f5aa-475d-aa13-4c61f55c6e45","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"decline","passagePhrase":"downfall"}]},"reading_u2_206":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Great Migrations</strong></span></h2><p><span>Animal migration, however it is defined, is far more than just the movement of animals. It can loosely be described as travel that takes place at regular intervals – often in an annual cycle – that may involve many members of a species, and is rewarded only after a long journey. It suggests inherited instinct. The biologist Hugh Dingle has identified five characteristics that apply, in varying degrees and combinations, to all migrations. They are prolonged movements that carry animals outside familiar habitats; they tend to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cc0cd506-7624-49a0-8374-59a5148ce477\" data-question=\"19\">linear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, not zigzaggy; they involve special behaviours concerning preparation (such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e35e7430-7e6d-46a4-877d-a00ee316bd8f\" data-question=\"20\">overfeeding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>) and arrival; they demand special allocations of energy. And one more: migrating animals maintain an intense attentiveness to the greater mission, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40a3ec4e-bc2e-48b5-acb4-eb4f2ca7e33e\" data-question=\"21\">keeps them undistracted by temptations and undeterred by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d48e3c8-df06-43c4-a4e6-a9b78c7105e7\" data-question=\"21\">challenges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> that would turn other animals aside.</span></p><p><span>An arctic tern, on its 20,000 km flight from the extreme south of South America to the Arctic circle, will take no notice of a nice smelly herring offered from a bird-watcher’s boat along the way. While local gulls will dive voraciously for such <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d9642726-b936-4a44-81be-12e59ba80b21\" data-question=\"14\">handouts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, the tern flies on. Why? The arctic tern <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"408a0b5c-823c-41fc-9485-43a76061d686\" data-question=\"22\">resists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> distraction because it is driven at that moment by an instinctive sense of something we humans find admirable: larger purpose. In other words, it is determined to reach its destination. The bird senses that it can eat, rest and mate later. Right now it is totally focused on the journey; its undivided intent is arrival.</span></p><p><span>Reaching some gravelly coastline in the Arctic, upon which other arctic terns have converged, will serve its larger purpose as shaped by evolution: finding a place, a time, and a set of circumstances in which it can successfully hatch and rear offspring.</span></p><p><span>But migration is a complex issue, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3aa00887-3199-492f-8e03-cf58c7c0ca2d\" data-question=\"15\">biologists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f029819-4d7a-4a39-bdec-28b9e6a63aae\" data-question=\"15\">define it differently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e503eae-c5dd-44ec-b680-922742a56141\" data-question=\"15\">depending in part on what sorts of animals they study. Joe! Berger, of the University of Montana, who works on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> the American pronghorn and other large terrestrial mammals, prefers what he calls a simple, practical definition suited to his beasts: ‘movements from a seasonal home area away to another home area and back again’. Generally the reason for such seasonal back-and-forth movement is to seek resources that aren’t available within a single area year-round.</span></p><p><span>But daily vertical movements by zooplankton in the ocean – upward by night to seek food, downward by day to escape predators – can also be considered migration. So can the movement of aphids when, having depleted the young leaves on one food plant, their offspring then fly onward to a different host plant, with no one aphid ever returning to where it started.</span></p><p><span>Dingle is an evolutionary biologist who studies insects. His definition is more intricate than Berger’s, citing those five features that distinguish migration from other forms of movement. They allow for the fact that, for example, aphids will become sensitive to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"225bc04c-7fd0-427f-a5bc-e04cebbcc6b6\" data-question=\"17\">blue light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> (from the sky) when it’s time for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1c018adb-66da-41e5-ae15-d8946f026868\" data-question=\"17\">takeoff on their big journey<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, and sensitive to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"225bc04c-7fd0-427f-a5bc-e04cebbcc6b6\" data-question=\"17\">yellow light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> (reflected from tender young leaves) when it’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1c018adb-66da-41e5-ae15-d8946f026868\" data-question=\"17\">appropriate to land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Birds will fatten themselves with heavy feeding in advance of a long migrational flight. The value of his definition, Dingle argues, is that it focuses attention on <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"70236642-d2f7-44fc-8ad9-4fd1dab5a51d\" data-question=\"18\">what the phenomenon of wildebeest migration shares with the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> phenomenon of the aphids, and therefore helps guide researchers towards understanding how evolution has produced them all.</span></p><p><span>Human behaviour, however, is having a detrimental impact on animal migration. The pronghorn, which resembles an antelope, though they are unrelated, is the fastest land mammal of the New World. One population, which spends the summer in the mountainous Grand Teton National Park of the western USA, follows a narrow route from its summer range in the mountains, across a river, and down onto the plains. Here they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"123b2191-afc9-4ed5-bb43-3bd3580fa57a\" data-question=\"24\">wait out the frozen months<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, feeding mainly on sagebrush blown clear of snow. These pronghorn are notable for the invariance of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b721f53f-8a26-471d-8af7-c5fade4843ef\" data-question=\"25\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b721f53f-8a26-471d-8af7-c5fade4843ef\" data-question=\"25\">their migration route<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and the severity of its constriction at three bottlenecks. If they can’t pass through each of the three during their spring migration, they can’t reach their bounty of summer grazing; if they can’t pass through again in autumn, escaping south onto those windblown plains, they are likely to die trying to overwinter in the deep snow. Pronghorn, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4124948d-479d-49b5-a319-4fe478d4e28f\" data-question=\"23\">dependent on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"034c7d63-d78e-40e1-8cb8-c0e283193a86\" data-question=\"23\">distance vision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> and speed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c7e18ad-9422-4bb4-87d7-86d691961e28\" data-question=\"23\">keep safe from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> predators, traverse high, open shoulders of land, where they can see and run. At one of the bottlenecks, forested hills rise to form a V, leaving a corridor of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12b012ce-f8bc-4fcc-8e4a-a063e3091a70\" data-question=\"26\">open ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"65813524-9d34-4cd9-987d-5ea2430119f4\" data-question=\"26\">only about 150 metres wide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, filled with private homes. Increasing development is leading toward a crisis for the pronghorn, threatening to choke off their passageway.</span></p><p><span>Conservation scientists, along with some biologists and land managers within the USA’s National Park Service and other agencies, are now working to preserve migrational behaviours, not just species and habitats. A National Forest has recognised the path of the pronghorn, much of which passes across its land, as a protected migration corridor. But neither the Forest Service nor the Park Service can control what happens on private land at a bottleneck. And with certain other migrating species, the challenge is complicated further – by vastly greater distances traversed, more jurisdictions, more borders, more dangers along the way. We will require wisdom and resoluteness to ensure that migrating species can continue their journeying a while longer.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage2?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>14-18</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20251\" id=\"question-wrapper-20251\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Local gulls and migrating arctic terns behave in the same way when offered <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d9642726-b936-4a44-81be-12e59ba80b21\" data-question=\"14\">food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20252\" id=\"question-wrapper-20252\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3aa00887-3199-492f-8e03-cf58c7c0ca2d\" data-question=\"15\">Experts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f029819-4d7a-4a39-bdec-28b9e6a63aae\" data-question=\"15\">definitions of migration tend to vary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e503eae-c5dd-44ec-b680-922742a56141\" data-question=\"15\">according to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> their area of study. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20253\" id=\"question-wrapper-20253\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Very few experts agree that the movement of aphids can be considered migration. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20254\" id=\"question-wrapper-20254\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1c018adb-66da-41e5-ae15-d8946f026868\" data-question=\"17\">Aphids’ journeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> are affected by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"225bc04c-7fd0-427f-a5bc-e04cebbcc6b6\" data-question=\"17\">changes in the light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that they perceive. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20255\" id=\"question-wrapper-20255\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Dingles aim is to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"70236642-d2f7-44fc-8ad9-4fd1dab5a51d\" data-question=\"18\">distinguish between the migratory behaviours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of different species. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, <strong>A-G</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>19-22</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40a3ec4e-bc2e-48b5-acb4-eb4f2ca7e33e\" data-question=\"21\">be discouraged by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d48e3c8-df06-43c4-a4e6-a9b78c7105e7\" data-question=\"21\">difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> travel on open land where they can look out for predators.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e35e7430-7e6d-46a4-877d-a00ee316bd8f\" data-question=\"20\">eat more than they need<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> for immediate purposes.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> be repeated daily.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"408a0b5c-823c-41fc-9485-43a76061d686\" data-question=\"22\">ignore<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> distractions.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong> be governed by the availability of water.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong> follow a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cc0cd506-7624-49a0-8374-59a5148ce477\" data-question=\"19\">straight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> line.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20256\" id=\"question-wrapper-20256\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to Dingle, migratory routes are likely to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20257\" id=\"question-wrapper-20257\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> To prepare for migration, animals are likely to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20258\" id=\"question-wrapper-20258\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> During migration, animals are unlikely to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20259\" id=\"question-wrapper-20259\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Arctic terns illustrate migrating animals’ ability to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>23-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>The migration of pronghorns</strong></span></h4><p><span>Pronghorns <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4124948d-479d-49b5-a319-4fe478d4e28f\" data-question=\"23\">rely on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"034c7d63-d78e-40e1-8cb8-c0e283193a86\" data-question=\"23\">eyesight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> and <strong>23</strong>……………. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c7e18ad-9422-4bb4-87d7-86d691961e28\" data-question=\"23\">avoid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> predators. One particular population’s summer habitat is a national park, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"123b2191-afc9-4ed5-bb43-3bd3580fa57a\" data-question=\"24\">their winter home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> is on the <strong>24</strong>……………… where they go to avoid the danger presented by the snow at that time of year. However, their route between these two areas contains three <strong>25</strong>……………… One problem is the construction of new homes in a narrow <strong>26</strong>……………… of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12b012ce-f8bc-4fcc-8e4a-a063e3091a70\" data-question=\"26\">land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> on the pronghorns’ route.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20260\" id=\"question-wrapper-20260\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPEED</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20261\" id=\"question-wrapper-20261\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PLAINS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20262\" id=\"question-wrapper-20262\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BOTTLENECKS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20263\" id=\"question-wrapper-20263\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CORRIDOR/PASSAGEWAY</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"cc0cd506-7624-49a0-8374-59a5148ce477","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"straight","passagePhrase":"linear"},{"uid":"e35e7430-7e6d-46a4-877d-a00ee316bd8f","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"eat more than they need","passagePhrase":"overfeeding"},{"uid":"40a3ec4e-bc2e-48b5-acb4-eb4f2ca7e33e","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"be discouraged by","passagePhrase":"keeps them undistracted by temptations and undeterred by"},{"uid":"4d48e3c8-df06-43c4-a4e6-a9b78c7105e7","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"difficulties","passagePhrase":"challenges"},{"uid":"d9642726-b936-4a44-81be-12e59ba80b21","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"food","passagePhrase":"handouts"},{"uid":"408a0b5c-823c-41fc-9485-43a76061d686","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"ignore","passagePhrase":"resists"},{"uid":"3aa00887-3199-492f-8e03-cf58c7c0ca2d","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Experts","passagePhrase":"biologists"},{"uid":"6f029819-4d7a-4a39-bdec-28b9e6a63aae","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"definitions of migration tend to vary","passagePhrase":"define it differently"},{"uid":"6e503eae-c5dd-44ec-b680-922742a56141","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"according to","passagePhrase":"depending in part on what sorts of animals they study. Joe! Berger, of the University of Montana, who works on"},{"uid":"225bc04c-7fd0-427f-a5bc-e04cebbcc6b6","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"changes in the light","passagePhrase":"blue light ... yellow light"},{"uid":"1c018adb-66da-41e5-ae15-d8946f026868","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Aphids’ journeys","passagePhrase":"takeoff on their big journey ... appropriate to land"},{"uid":"123b2191-afc9-4ed5-bb43-3bd3580fa57a","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"their winter home","passagePhrase":"wait out the frozen months"},{"uid":"b721f53f-8a26-471d-8af7-c5fade4843ef","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"their migration route ... their migration route"},{"uid":"4124948d-479d-49b5-a319-4fe478d4e28f","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"rely on","passagePhrase":"dependent on"},{"uid":"034c7d63-d78e-40e1-8cb8-c0e283193a86","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"eyesight","passagePhrase":"distance vision"},{"uid":"3c7e18ad-9422-4bb4-87d7-86d691961e28","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"avoid","passagePhrase":"keep safe from"},{"uid":"12b012ce-f8bc-4fcc-8e4a-a063e3091a70","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"land","passagePhrase":"open ground"},{"uid":"65813524-9d34-4cd9-987d-5ea2430119f4","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"only about 150 metres wide"}]},"reading_u2_207":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>Preface to ‘How the other half thinks:</strong></span></h2><h2><span><strong>Adventures in mathematical reasoning’</strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>Occasionally, in some difficult musical compositions, there are beautiful, but easy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"673f882c-14dd-4399-9451-d330d2b7d3a1\" data-question=\"35\">parts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"673f882c-14dd-4399-9451-d330d2b7d3a1\" data-question=\"35\">parts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> so simple a beginner could play them. So it is with mathematics as well. There are some discoveries in advanced mathematics that do not depend on specialized knowledge, not even on algebra, geometry, or trigonometry. Instead they may involve, at most, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2167be4f-7f70-4dd9-ad5c-05491bdc17a8\" data-question=\"36\">a little<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> arithmetic, such as ‘the sum of two odd numbers is even’, and common sense. Each of the eight chapters in this book illustrates this phenomenon. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f902920-21bc-44a3-a780-05c4b800b3e1\" data-question=\"33\">Anyone can understand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> every step in the reasoning.</span></p><p><span>The thinking in each chapter uses at most only elementary arithmetic, and sometimes not even that. Thus all readers will have the chance to participate in a mathematical experience, to appreciate the beauty of mathematics, and to become familiar with its logical, yet intuitive, style of thinking.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>One of my purposes in writing this book is to give readers who haven’t had the opportunity to see and enjoy real mathematics the chance to appreciate the mathematical way of thinking. I want to reveal not only some of the fascinating discoveries, but, more importantly, the reasoning behind them.</span></p><p><span>In that respect, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab322ec7-9737-4a45-b9ff-140b78d12a9f\" data-question=\"28\">this book differs from most books<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> on mathematics written for the general public. Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61e7f07e-664a-45c1-bcba-ac1497bb69d6\" data-question=\"31\">present the lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of colorful mathematicians. Others <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61e7f07e-664a-45c1-bcba-ac1497bb69d6\" data-question=\"31\">describe important applications<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of mathematics. Yet others <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61e7f07e-664a-45c1-bcba-ac1497bb69d6\" data-question=\"31\">go into mathematical procedures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, but assume that the reader is adept in using algebra.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>I hope this book will help bridge that notorious gap that separates the two cultures: the humanities and the sciences, or should I say the right brain (intuitive) and the left brain (analytical, numerical). As the chapters will illustrate, mathematics is not restricted to the analytical and numerical; intuition <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d3225633-36d5-41bc-8e26-0f51d22377dc\" data-question=\"37\">plays a significant role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. The alleged gap can be narrowed or completely overcome by anyone, in part because each of us is far from using the full capacity of either side of the brain. To illustrate our human potential, I cite a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cc0f24b-0606-44d0-9f3f-866803734d16\" data-question=\"30\">structural engineer who is an artist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cc0f24b-0606-44d0-9f3f-866803734d16\" data-question=\"30\">electrical engineer who is an opera singer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cc0f24b-0606-44d0-9f3f-866803734d16\" data-question=\"30\">opera singer who published mathematical research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, and a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cc0f24b-0606-44d0-9f3f-866803734d16\" data-question=\"30\">mathematician who publishes short stories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>Other scientists have written books to explain their fields to non-scientists, but have necessarily had to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c33b0fe8-0b17-4b34-a5a9-14a345c5ac36\" data-question=\"27\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4440bd07-beb1-4e10-a06e-30a568defc50\" data-question=\"38\">omit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> the mathematics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, although it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"52e18def-c2e4-4aa1-8055-b16e695eaa4d\" data-question=\"38\">provides the foundation of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> their theories. The reader must remain a tantalized spectator rather than an involved participant, since the appropriate language for describing the details in much of science is mathematics, whether the subject is expanding universe, subatomic particles, or chromosomes. Though the broad outline of a scientific theory can be sketched intuitively, when a part of the physical universe is finally understood, its description often looks like a page in a mathematics text.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Still, the non-mathematical reader can go far in understanding mathematical reasoning. This book presents the details that illustrate the mathematical style of thinking, which involves sustained, step-by-step analysis, experiments, and insights. You will turn these pages much more slowly than when reading <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5870b50-9520-468b-827d-19aa97b1fd2e\" data-question=\"32\">a novel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5870b50-9520-468b-827d-19aa97b1fd2e\" data-question=\"32\">a newspaper<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. It may help to have a pencil and paper ready to check claims and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd38d12a-2041-4367-871a-989e5d5f4461\" data-question=\"39\">carry out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> experiments.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>As I wrote, I kept in mind two <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1791a8f-9e4c-405a-90e0-fa10424cc684\" data-question=\"34\">types<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> of readers: those who enjoyed mathematics until they were turned off by an unpleasant episode, usually around fifth grade, and mathematics aficionados, who will find much that is new throughout the book.</span></p><p><span>This book also serves readers who simply want to sharpen their analytical skills. Many careers, such as law and medicine, require extended, precise analysis. Each chapter offers practice in following a sustained and closely argued line of thought. That mathematics can develop this skill is shown by these two testimonials:</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>A physician wrote, ‘The discipline of analytical thought processes [in mathematics] <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d1296d2-f930-4300-90ba-8e92dfc1b4e2\" data-question=\"29\">prepared me extremely well for medical school<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. In medicine one is faced with a problem which must be thoroughly analyzed before a solution can be found. The process is similar to doing mathematics.’</span></p><p><span>A lawyer made the same point, “Although I had no background in law – not even one political science course — I did well at one of the best law schools. I <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e9177d8-ddf0-4d10-a1a1-468945b49882\" data-question=\"40\">attribute much of my success there to having learned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, through the study of mathematics, and, in particular, theorems, how to analyze complicated principles. Lawyers who have studied mathematics can master the legal principles in a way that most others cannot.’</span></p><p><span>I hope you will share my delight in watching as simple, even naive, questions lead to remarkable solutions and purely theoretical discoveries find unanticipated applications.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage has seven sections, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which section contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-34</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20264\" id=\"question-wrapper-20264\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to books that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c33b0fe8-0b17-4b34-a5a9-14a345c5ac36\" data-question=\"27\">assume a lack of mathematical knowledge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20265\" id=\"question-wrapper-20265\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the way in which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab322ec7-9737-4a45-b9ff-140b78d12a9f\" data-question=\"28\">this is not a typical book<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> about mathematics </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20266\" id=\"question-wrapper-20266\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> personal examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d1296d2-f930-4300-90ba-8e92dfc1b4e2\" data-question=\"29\">being helped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> by mathematics </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20267\" id=\"question-wrapper-20267\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cc0f24b-0606-44d0-9f3f-866803734d16\" data-question=\"30\">people who each had abilities that seemed incompatible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20268\" id=\"question-wrapper-20268\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61e7f07e-664a-45c1-bcba-ac1497bb69d6\" data-question=\"31\">different focuses of books<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> about mathematics </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20269\" id=\"question-wrapper-20269\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a contrast between reading this book and reading <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5870b50-9520-468b-827d-19aa97b1fd2e\" data-question=\"32\">other kinds of publication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20270\" id=\"question-wrapper-20270\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a claim that the whole of the book <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f902920-21bc-44a3-a780-05c4b800b3e1\" data-question=\"33\">is accessible to everybody<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20271\" id=\"question-wrapper-20271\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to different <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1791a8f-9e4c-405a-90e0-fa10424cc684\" data-question=\"34\">categories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> of intended readers of this book </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>35-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20272\" id=\"question-wrapper-20272\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"673f882c-14dd-4399-9451-d330d2b7d3a1\" data-question=\"35\">areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of both music and mathematics are suitable for someone who is a……………… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BEGINNER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20273\" id=\"question-wrapper-20273\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is sometimes possible to understand advanced mathematics using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2167be4f-7f70-4dd9-ad5c-05491bdc17a8\" data-question=\"36\">no more than a limited knowledge of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>……………… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ARITHMETIC</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20274\" id=\"question-wrapper-20274\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer intends to show that mathematics <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d3225633-36d5-41bc-8e26-0f51d22377dc\" data-question=\"37\">requires<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>……………… thinking, as well as analytical skills. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INTUITIVE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20275\" id=\"question-wrapper-20275\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some books written by………………. have had to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4440bd07-beb1-4e10-a06e-30a568defc50\" data-question=\"38\">leave out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> the mathematics that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"52e18def-c2e4-4aa1-8055-b16e695eaa4d\" data-question=\"38\">is central to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> their theories. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SCIENTISTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20276\" id=\"question-wrapper-20276\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer advises non-mathematical readers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd38d12a-2041-4367-871a-989e5d5f4461\" data-question=\"39\">perform<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>………………. while reading </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EXPERIMENTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20277\" id=\"question-wrapper-20277\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A lawyer found that studying………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e9177d8-ddf0-4d10-a1a1-468945b49882\" data-question=\"40\">helped even more than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> other areas of mathematics in the study of law. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">THEOREMS</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"673f882c-14dd-4399-9451-d330d2b7d3a1","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"areas","passagePhrase":"parts ... parts"},{"uid":"2167be4f-7f70-4dd9-ad5c-05491bdc17a8","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"no more than a limited knowledge of","passagePhrase":"a little"},{"uid":"9f902920-21bc-44a3-a780-05c4b800b3e1","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"is accessible to everybody","passagePhrase":"Anyone can understand"},{"uid":"ab322ec7-9737-4a45-b9ff-140b78d12a9f","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"this is not a typical book","passagePhrase":"this book differs from most books"},{"uid":"61e7f07e-664a-45c1-bcba-ac1497bb69d6","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"different focuses of books","passagePhrase":"present the lives ... describe important applications ... go into mathematical procedures"},{"uid":"d3225633-36d5-41bc-8e26-0f51d22377dc","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"requires","passagePhrase":"plays a significant role"},{"uid":"7cc0f24b-0606-44d0-9f3f-866803734d16","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"people who each had abilities that seemed incompatible","passagePhrase":"structural engineer who is an artist ... electrical engineer who is an opera singer ... opera singer who published mathematical research ... mathematician who publishes short stories"},{"uid":"c33b0fe8-0b17-4b34-a5a9-14a345c5ac36","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"assume a lack of mathematical knowledge","passagePhrase":"omit the mathematics"},{"uid":"4440bd07-beb1-4e10-a06e-30a568defc50","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"leave out","passagePhrase":"omit"},{"uid":"52e18def-c2e4-4aa1-8055-b16e695eaa4d","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"is central to","passagePhrase":"provides the foundation of"},{"uid":"a5870b50-9520-468b-827d-19aa97b1fd2e","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"other kinds of publication","passagePhrase":"a novel ... a newspaper"},{"uid":"bd38d12a-2041-4367-871a-989e5d5f4461","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"perform","passagePhrase":"carry out"},{"uid":"b1791a8f-9e4c-405a-90e0-fa10424cc684","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"categories","passagePhrase":"types"},{"uid":"2d1296d2-f930-4300-90ba-8e92dfc1b4e2","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"being helped","passagePhrase":"prepared me extremely well for medical school"},{"uid":"9e9177d8-ddf0-4d10-a1a1-468945b49882","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"helped even more than","passagePhrase":"attribute much of my success there to having learned"}]},"reading_u2_208":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong>Research using twins</strong></span></h2><p><span>To biomedical researchers all over the world, twins offer a precious opportunity to untangle the influence of genes and the environment – of nature and nurture. Because identical twins come from a single fertilized egg that splits into two, they share virtually the same genetic code. Any differences between them -one twin having younger looking skin, for example – must be due to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e6ee079d-6f1a-4dbd-be76-4dadce854215\" data-question=\"1\">environmental factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> such as less time spent in the sun.</span></p><p><span>Alternatively, by comparing the experiences of identical twins with those of fraternal twins, who come from separate eggs and share on average half their DNA, researchers can quantify the extent to which our genes affect our lives. If identical twins are more similar to each other with respect to an ailment than fraternal twins are, then vulnerability to the disease must be rooted at least in part in heredity.</span></p><p><span>These two lines of research – studying the differences between identical twins to pinpoint the influence of environment, and comparing identical twins with fraternal ones to measure the role of inheritance – have been crucial to understanding the interplay of nature and nurture in determining our personalities, behavior, and vulnerability to disease.</span></p><p><span>The idea of using twins to measure the influence of heredity dates back to 1875, when the English scientist Francis Galton <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72efa53b-67bb-4087-8c74-ef0c4efb4ade\" data-question=\"8\">first suggested<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> the approach (and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4484d098-324c-4b05-ba99-85517bd12cc8\" data-question=\"5\">coined the phrase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> ‘nature and nurture’). But twin studies took a surprising twist in the 1980s, with the arrival of studies into identical twins who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af8a7367-55bc-421e-b80e-6b16b76fb3da\" data-question=\"9\">had been separated at birth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and reunited as adults. Over two decades 137 sets of twins eventually visited Thomas Bouchard’s lab in what became known as the Minnesota Study of Twins Reared Apart. Numerous tests were carried out on the twins, and they were each asked more than 15,000 questions.</span></p><p><span>Bouchard and his colleagues used this mountain of data to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"379963f0-a80d-4ffb-8a69-a053f7cad3d6\" data-question=\"7\">identify how far twins were affected by their genetic makeup<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. The key to their approach was a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a747799e-8510-477d-8bfd-2d0f293a50de\" data-question=\"7\">statistical concept<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> called heritability. in broad terms, the heritability of a trait measures the extent to which differences among members of a population can be explained by differences in their genetics. And wherever Bouchard and other scientists looked, it seemed, they found the invisible hand of genetic influence helping to shape our lives.</span></p><p><span>Lately, however, twin studies have helped lead scientists to a radical new conclusion: that nature and nurture are not the only elemental forces at work. According to a recent field called epigenetics, there is a third factor also in play, one that in some cases serves as a bridge between the environment and our genes, and in others operates on its own to shape who we are.</span></p><p><span>Epigenetic processes are chemical reactions tied to neither <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b8a62a3d-044d-4c43-a2a2-5ce258fee177\" data-question=\"4\">nature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> nor nurture but representing what researchers have called a ‘third component’. These reactions influence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eac62e84-9f71-49d7-9d23-88174e30fc48\" data-question=\"10\">how our genetic code is expressed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>: how each gene is strengthened or weakened, even turned on or off, to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ad3be72-43ae-4905-aa3a-70baabe6f4e8\" data-question=\"11\">build<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> our bones, brains and all the other parts of our bodies.</span></p><p><span>If you think of our DNA as an immense piano keyboard and our genes as the keys – each key symbolizing a segment of DNA responsible for a particular note, or trait, and all the keys combining to make us who we are – then epigenetic processes determine when and how each key can be struck, changing the tune being played.</span></p><p><span>One way the study of epigenetics is revolutionizing our understanding of biology is by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20909b0b-6cbb-44de-962f-bc503a7dfd20\" data-question=\"12\">revealing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> a mechanism by which the environment directly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eaf97173-4ea0-4f09-b8ca-5fde65762cee\" data-question=\"12\">impacts on genes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. Studies of animals, for example, have shown that when a rat <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c4b6c70-484a-4f04-bc64-c32edac7c3f7\" data-question=\"13\">experiences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> stress during pregnancy, it can cause epigenetic changes in a fetus that lead to behavioral problems as the rodent grows up. Other epigenetic processes appear to occur randomly, while others are normal, such as those that guide embryonic cells as they become heart, brain, or liver cells, for example.</span></p><p><span>Geneticist Danielle Reed has worked with many twins over the years and thought deeply about what twin studies have taught us. ‘It’s very clear when you look at twins that much of what they share is hardwired,’ she says. ‘Many things about them are absolutely the same and unalterable. But it’s also clear, when you get to know them, that other things about them are different. Epigenetics is the origin of a lot of those differences, in my view.’</span></p><p><span>Reed credits Thomas Bouchard’s work for today’s surge in twin studies. ‘He was the trailblazer,’ she says. ‘We forget that 50 years ago things like heart disease were thought to be caused entirely by lifestyle. Schizophrenia was thought to be due to poor mothering. Twin studies have allowed us to be more reflective about what people are actually born with and what’s caused by experience.’</span></p><p><span>Having said that, Reed adds, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe9dc7c6-82d6-4058-a96d-0b5654df71b0\" data-question=\"6\">the latest work in epigenetics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> promises to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc08fadc-1895-47d0-b773-b7f6514b6ad3\" data-question=\"6\">take our understanding even further<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. ‘What I like to say is that nature writes some things in pencil and some things in pen,’ she says. ‘Things written in pen you can’t change. That’s DNA. But things written in pencil you can. That’s epigenetics. Now that we’re actually able to look at the DNA and see where the pencil writings are, it’s sort of a whole new world.’</span></p><h4><span><strong></strong></span></h4><h4><span><strong></strong></span></h4></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>1-4</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"889\" id=\"question-wrapper-889\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There may be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e6ee079d-6f1a-4dbd-be76-4dadce854215\" data-question=\"1\">genetic causes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> for the differences in how young the skin of identical twins looks. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"890\" id=\"question-wrapper-890\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Twins are at greater risk of developing certain illnesses than non-twins. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"891\" id=\"question-wrapper-891\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bouchard advertised in newspapers for twins who had been separated at birth. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"892\" id=\"question-wrapper-892\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Epigenetic processes are different from both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b8a62a3d-044d-4c43-a2a2-5ce258fee177\" data-question=\"4\">genetic and environmental processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions <strong>5-9</strong>) and the list of researchers below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct researcher, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>, in boxes <strong>5-9</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Researchers</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Francis Galton</span></p><p><span><strong>B </strong> Thomas Bouchard</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> Danielie Reed </span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"893\" id=\"question-wrapper-893\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4484d098-324c-4b05-ba99-85517bd12cc8\" data-question=\"5\">invented a term<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> used to distinguish two factors affecting human characteristics </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"894\" id=\"question-wrapper-894\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> expressed the view that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe9dc7c6-82d6-4058-a96d-0b5654df71b0\" data-question=\"6\">the study of epigenetics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc08fadc-1895-47d0-b773-b7f6514b6ad3\" data-question=\"6\">increase our knowledge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"895\" id=\"question-wrapper-895\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> developed a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a747799e-8510-477d-8bfd-2d0f293a50de\" data-question=\"7\">mathematical method<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"379963f0-a80d-4ffb-8a69-a053f7cad3d6\" data-question=\"7\">measuring genetic influences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"896\" id=\"question-wrapper-896\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72efa53b-67bb-4087-8c74-ef0c4efb4ade\" data-question=\"8\">pioneered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> research into genetics using twins </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"897\" id=\"question-wrapper-897\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> carried out research into twins who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af8a7367-55bc-421e-b80e-6b16b76fb3da\" data-question=\"9\">had lived apart<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Complete the summary using the list of words, <strong>A-F</strong>, below.</p><p><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>10-13</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p><h4><strong>Epigenetic processes</strong></h4><p>In epigenetic processes, <strong>10</strong>……………. influence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eac62e84-9f71-49d7-9d23-88174e30fc48\" data-question=\"10\">the activity of our genes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, for example in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ad3be72-43ae-4905-aa3a-70baabe6f4e8\" data-question=\"11\">creating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> our internal <strong>11</strong>………….. The study of epigenetic processes is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20909b0b-6cbb-44de-962f-bc503a7dfd20\" data-question=\"12\">uncovering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> a way in which our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eaf97173-4ea0-4f09-b8ca-5fde65762cee\" data-question=\"12\">genes can be affected by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> our <strong>12</strong>……………. One example is that if a pregnant rat <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c4b6c70-484a-4f04-bc64-c32edac7c3f7\" data-question=\"13\">suffers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> stress, the new-born rat may later show problems in its <strong>13</strong>……………….</p><p><strong>A </strong> nurture <strong>B</strong> organs <strong>C</strong> code</p><p><strong>D</strong> chemicals <strong>E</strong> environment <strong>F</strong> behaviour/behavior</p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"898\" id=\"question-wrapper-898\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"899\" id=\"question-wrapper-899\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"900\" id=\"question-wrapper-900\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"901\" id=\"question-wrapper-901\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"72efa53b-67bb-4087-8c74-ef0c4efb4ade","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"pioneered","passagePhrase":"first suggested"},{"uid":"4484d098-324c-4b05-ba99-85517bd12cc8","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"invented a term","passagePhrase":"coined the phrase"},{"uid":"af8a7367-55bc-421e-b80e-6b16b76fb3da","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"had lived apart","passagePhrase":"had been separated at birth"},{"uid":"379963f0-a80d-4ffb-8a69-a053f7cad3d6","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"measuring genetic influences","passagePhrase":"identify how far twins were affected by their genetic makeup"},{"uid":"a747799e-8510-477d-8bfd-2d0f293a50de","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"mathematical method","passagePhrase":"statistical concept"},{"uid":"b8a62a3d-044d-4c43-a2a2-5ce258fee177","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"genetic and environmental processes","passagePhrase":"nature"},{"uid":"eac62e84-9f71-49d7-9d23-88174e30fc48","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the activity of our genes","passagePhrase":"how our genetic code is expressed"},{"uid":"0ad3be72-43ae-4905-aa3a-70baabe6f4e8","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"creating","passagePhrase":"build"},{"uid":"20909b0b-6cbb-44de-962f-bc503a7dfd20","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"uncovering","passagePhrase":"revealing"},{"uid":"eaf97173-4ea0-4f09-b8ca-5fde65762cee","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"genes can be affected by","passagePhrase":"impacts on genes"},{"uid":"5c4b6c70-484a-4f04-bc64-c32edac7c3f7","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"suffers","passagePhrase":"experiences"},{"uid":"fe9dc7c6-82d6-4058-a96d-0b5654df71b0","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"the study of epigenetics","passagePhrase":"the latest work in epigenetics"},{"uid":"dc08fadc-1895-47d0-b773-b7f6514b6ad3","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"increase our knowledge","passagePhrase":"take our understanding even further"}]},"reading_u2_209":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>An Introduction to Film Sound</strong></span></h2><p><span>Though we might think of film as an essentially visual experience, we really cannot afford to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbba3374-7a5b-4cc4-b3be-001377c0c676\" data-question=\"14\">underestimate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56851860-2172-4ab5-a694-ce64a52f8042\" data-question=\"14\">the importance of film sound<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. A meaningful sound track is often as complicated as the image on the screen, and is ultimately just as much the responsibility of the director. The entire sound track consists of three essential ingredients: the human voice, sound effects and music. These three tracks must be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1394aed1-2585-4cec-897e-484ff38be573\" data-question=\"24\">mixed and balanced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> so as to produce the necessary emphases which in turn create desired effects. Topics which essentially refer to the three previously mentioned tracks are discussed below. They include dialogue, synchronous and asynchronous sound effects, and music.</span></p><p><span>Let us start with dialogue. As is the case with stage drama, dialogue serves to tell the story and expresses feelings and motivations of characters as well. Often with film characterization the audience <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"170b7f1e-1ceb-4f01-8e25-1d0f4e47a2fd\" data-question=\"25\">perceives little or no difference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> between the character and the actor. Thus, for example, the actor Humphrey Bogart is the character Sam Spade; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5d2cdc1-f893-48cd-a2f7-2f01393dbccd\" data-question=\"15\">film personality and life personality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a307902b-a32c-4a7a-9d4f-0a4432bdbd5b\" data-question=\"15\">seem to merge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Perhaps this is because the very texture of a performer’s voice supplies an element of character.</span></p><p><span>When voice textures fit the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"75d38ce0-d1dc-47b4-9bef-5c77bf640e1e\" data-question=\"26\">performer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26f450d2-4751-4596-991e-1945fdb98596\" data-question=\"26\">physiognomy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43a1e9d3-8fdc-4ed2-b225-555a08c4a1d3\" data-question=\"26\">gestures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, a whole and very realistic persona emerges. The viewer sees not an actor working at his craft, but another human being struggling with life. It is interesting to note that how dialogue is used and the very amount of dialogue used varies widely among films. For example, in the highly successful science-fiction film 2001, little dialogue was evident, and most of it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1bc91f1a-5326-4a30-bdd7-61f3d1d89cb4\" data-question=\"16\">banal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> and of little intrinsic interest. In this way the film-maker was able to portray what Thomas Sobochack and Vivian Sobochack call, in <em>An Introduction to Film</em>, the ‘inadequacy of human responses when compared with the magnificent technology created by man and the visual beauties of the universe’.</span></p><p><span>The comedy <em>Bringing Up Baby</em>, on the other hand, presents practically non-stop dialogue delivered at breakneck speed. This use of dialogue <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"095e3893-e12e-4f6f-9162-b409b6df9522\" data-question=\"17\">underscores<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> not only the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e000835c-d9d4-43d9-abf8-6fec9ddff1cb\" data-question=\"17\">dizzy quality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of the character played by Katherine Hepburn, but also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e000835c-d9d4-43d9-abf8-6fec9ddff1cb\" data-question=\"17\">the absurdity of the film itself and thus its humor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. The audience is bounced from gag to gag and conversation to conversation; there is no time for audience reflection. The audience is caught up in a whirlwind of activity in simply managing to follow the plot. This film presents pure escapism – largely due to its frenetic dialogue.</span></p><p><span>Synchronous sound effects are those sounds which are synchronized or matched with what is viewed. For example, if the film portrays a character playing the piano, the sounds of the piano are projected. Synchronous sounds contribute to the realism of film and also help to create a particular atmosphere. For example, the ‘click’ of a door being opened may simply serve to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03121473-c471-4e58-be5d-b5e593666ba5\" data-question=\"18\">convince the audience that the image portrayed is real<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, and the audience may only subconsciously note the expected sound. However, if the ‘click’ of an opening door is part of an ominous action such as a burglary, the sound mixer may call attention to the ‘click’ with an increase in volume; this helps to engage the audience in a moment of suspense.</span></p><p><span>Asynchronous sound effects, on the other hand, are not matched with a visible source of the sound on screen. Such sounds are included so as to provide an appropriate emotional nuance, and they may also add to the realism of the film. For example, a film-maker might opt to include the background sound of an ambulance’s siren while the foreground sound and image portrays an arguing couple. The asynchronous ambulance siren underscores the psychic injury incurred in the argument; at the same time the noise of the siren adds to the realism of the film by acknowledging the film’s city setting.</span></p><p><span>We are probably all familiar with background music in films, which has become so ubiquitous as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0cd41c5-dd97-4a60-8105-ea255a29f064\" data-question=\"19\">to be noticeable in its absence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. We are aware that it is used to add emotion and rhythm. Usually not meant to be noticeable, it often provides a tone or an emotional attitude toward the story and /or the characters depicted. In addition, background music often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"39124648-43d6-4989-b63c-f4c6cf44b292\" data-question=\"20\">foreshadows<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> a change in mood. For example, dissonant music may be used in film to indicate an approaching (but not yet visible) menace or disaster.</span></p><p><span>Background music may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51e06061-6d29-4e51-8042-bea860d3fb1c\" data-question=\"22\">aid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> viewer understanding by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a4490cd-ec56-49d5-892b-cc8e42e8d061\" data-question=\"22\">linking scenes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. For example, a particular musical theme associated with an individual character or situation may be repeated at various points in a film in order to remind the audience of salient motifs or ideas.</span></p><p><span>Film sound comprises conventions and innovations. We have come to expect an acceleration of music during car chases and creaky doors in horror films. Yet, it is important to note as well that sound is often brilliantly conceived. The effects of sound are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"19dd9bdc-2ec0-4ae9-9f38-f44230cd1ef9\" data-question=\"23\">often largely subtle and often are noted by only our subconscious minds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. We need to foster an awareness of film sound as well as film space so as to truly appreciate an art form that sprang to life during the twentieth century – the modern film.</span></p><h4><span><strong></strong></span></h4><h4><span><strong></strong></span></h4><h4><span><strong></strong></span></h4></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</p><p><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>14-18</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"902\" id=\"question-wrapper-902\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the first paragraph, the writer makes a point that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the director should plan the sound track at an early stage in filming.</li> <li>B. it would be wrong to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbba3374-7a5b-4cc4-b3be-001377c0c676\" data-question=\"14\">overlook<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56851860-2172-4ab5-a694-ce64a52f8042\" data-question=\"14\">the contribution of sound to the artistry of films<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</li> <li>C. the music industry can have a beneficial influence on sound in film.</li> <li>D. it is important for those working on the sound in a film to have sole responsibility for it.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"903\" id=\"question-wrapper-903\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One reason that the writer refers to Humphrey Bogart is to exemplify </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the importance of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5d2cdc1-f893-48cd-a2f7-2f01393dbccd\" data-question=\"15\">the actor and the character<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a307902b-a32c-4a7a-9d4f-0a4432bdbd5b\" data-question=\"15\">appearing to have similar personalities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</li> <li>B. the audience’s wish that actors are visually appropriate for their roles.</li> <li>C. the value of the actor having had similar feelings to the character.</li> <li>D. the audience’s preference for dialogue to be as authentic as possible.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"904\" id=\"question-wrapper-904\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the third paragraph, the writer suggests that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. audiences are likely to be critical of film dialogue that does not reflect their own experience.</li> <li>B. film dialogue that appears to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1bc91f1a-5326-4a30-bdd7-61f3d1d89cb4\" data-question=\"16\">dull<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> may have a specific purpose.</li> <li>C. filmmakers vary considerably in the skill with which they handle dialogue.</li> <li>D. the most successful films are those with dialogue of a high Quality.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"905\" id=\"question-wrapper-905\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer suggest about Bringing Up </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The plot suffers from the filmmaker’s wish to focus on humorous dialogue.</li> <li>B. The dialogue helps to make it one of the best comedy films ever produced.</li> <li>C. There is a mismatch between the speed of the dialogue and the speed of actions.</li> <li>D. The nature of the dialogue <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"095e3893-e12e-4f6f-9162-b409b6df9522\" data-question=\"17\">emphasises<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e000835c-d9d4-43d9-abf8-6fec9ddff1cb\" data-question=\"17\">key elements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of the film.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"906\" id=\"question-wrapper-906\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer refers to the ‘click’ of a door to make the point that realistic sounds </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. are often used to give the audience a false impression of events in the film.</li> <li>B. may be interpreted in different ways by different members of the audience.</li> <li>C. may be modified in order <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03121473-c471-4e58-be5d-b5e593666ba5\" data-question=\"18\">to manipulate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the audience’s response to the film.</li> <li>D. tend to be more significant in films presenting realistic situations.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</p><p><em>In boxes <strong>19-23</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"907\" id=\"question-wrapper-907\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Audiences are likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0cd41c5-dd97-4a60-8105-ea255a29f064\" data-question=\"19\">be surprised if a film lacks background music<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"908\" id=\"question-wrapper-908\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Background music may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"39124648-43d6-4989-b63c-f4c6cf44b292\" data-question=\"20\">anticipate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> a development in a film. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"909\" id=\"question-wrapper-909\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Background music has more effect on some people than on others. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"910\" id=\"question-wrapper-910\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Background music may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51e06061-6d29-4e51-8042-bea860d3fb1c\" data-question=\"22\">help<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the audience to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a4490cd-ec56-49d5-892b-cc8e42e8d061\" data-question=\"22\">make certain connections within the film<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"911\" id=\"question-wrapper-911\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Audiences <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"19dd9bdc-2ec0-4ae9-9f38-f44230cd1ef9\" data-question=\"23\">tend to be aware of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> how the background music is affecting them. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete each sentence with the correct letter below.</p><p><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-E</strong>, in boxes <strong>24-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p><p><strong>A</strong> when the audience listens to the dialogue.</p><p><strong>B</strong> if the film reflects the audience’s own concerns.</p><p><strong>C</strong> if voice, sound and music are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1394aed1-2585-4cec-897e-484ff38be573\" data-question=\"24\">combined appropriately<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</p><p><strong>D</strong> when the director is aware of how the audience will respond.</p><p><strong>E</strong> when the actor s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26f450d2-4751-4596-991e-1945fdb98596\" data-question=\"26\">appearance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, voice and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43a1e9d3-8fdc-4ed2-b225-555a08c4a1d3\" data-question=\"26\">moves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> are consistent with each other.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"912\" id=\"question-wrapper-912\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The audience’s response to different parts of a film can be controlled </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"913\" id=\"question-wrapper-913\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The feelings and motivations of characters <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"170b7f1e-1ceb-4f01-8e25-1d0f4e47a2fd\" data-question=\"25\">become clear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"914\" id=\"question-wrapper-914\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A character seems to be a real person rather than an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"75d38ce0-d1dc-47b4-9bef-5c77bf640e1e\" data-question=\"26\">actor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"bbba3374-7a5b-4cc4-b3be-001377c0c676","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"overlook","passagePhrase":"underestimate"},{"uid":"56851860-2172-4ab5-a694-ce64a52f8042","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"the contribution of sound to the artistry of films","passagePhrase":"the importance of film sound"},{"uid":"1394aed1-2585-4cec-897e-484ff38be573","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"combined appropriately","passagePhrase":"mixed and balanced"},{"uid":"a5d2cdc1-f893-48cd-a2f7-2f01393dbccd","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the actor and the character","passagePhrase":"film personality and life personality"},{"uid":"a307902b-a32c-4a7a-9d4f-0a4432bdbd5b","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"appearing to have similar personalities","passagePhrase":"seem to merge"},{"uid":"75d38ce0-d1dc-47b4-9bef-5c77bf640e1e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"actor","passagePhrase":"performer"},{"uid":"26f450d2-4751-4596-991e-1945fdb98596","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"appearance","passagePhrase":"physiognomy"},{"uid":"43a1e9d3-8fdc-4ed2-b225-555a08c4a1d3","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"moves","passagePhrase":"gestures"},{"uid":"1bc91f1a-5326-4a30-bdd7-61f3d1d89cb4","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"dull","passagePhrase":"banal"},{"uid":"095e3893-e12e-4f6f-9162-b409b6df9522","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"emphasises","passagePhrase":"underscores"},{"uid":"e000835c-d9d4-43d9-abf8-6fec9ddff1cb","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"key elements","passagePhrase":"dizzy quality ... the absurdity of the film itself and thus its humor"},{"uid":"03121473-c471-4e58-be5d-b5e593666ba5","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"to manipulate","passagePhrase":"convince the audience that the image portrayed is real"},{"uid":"d0cd41c5-dd97-4a60-8105-ea255a29f064","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"be surprised if a film lacks background music","passagePhrase":"to be noticeable in its absence"},{"uid":"39124648-43d6-4989-b63c-f4c6cf44b292","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"anticipate","passagePhrase":"foreshadows"},{"uid":"51e06061-6d29-4e51-8042-bea860d3fb1c","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"help","passagePhrase":"aid"},{"uid":"0a4490cd-ec56-49d5-892b-cc8e42e8d061","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"make certain connections within the film","passagePhrase":"linking scenes"}]},"reading_u2_210":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>‘This Marvellous Invention’</strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>Of all mankind’s manifold creations, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eea9a613-d29c-4131-909a-5bae1d8079a3\" data-question=\"27\">language must take pride of place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Other inventions -the wheel, agriculture, sliced bread – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c9f6f2c3-0421-48ed-b814-fc2043a1bace\" data-question=\"33\">may have transformed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> our material <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93881f0c-34c8-4b74-8e83-a66e6274b563\" data-question=\"33\">existence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, but the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7284b1c-ceb4-4e84-bf9d-6662e7a411a7\" data-question=\"33\">advent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of language is what made us human. Compared to language, all other inventions pale in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c96fb20-e3bc-4b33-99ed-febb742ba970\" data-question=\"34\">significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, since everything we have ever achieved depends on language and originates from it. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4a09d907-f033-4d4f-b6fa-597ca3e0f545\" data-question=\"37\">Without language, we could never<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0546cd99-999b-49d8-b373-9fbd71bfc9b9\" data-question=\"37\">have embarked on our ascent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to unparalleled power over all other animals, and even over nature itself.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>But language is foremost not just because it came first. In its own right it is a tool of extraordinary sophistication, yet based on an idea of ingenious simplicity: ‘this marvellous invention of composing out of twenty-five or thirty sounds that infinite variety of expressions which, whilst having in themselves no likeness to what is in our mind, allow us to disclose to others its whole secret, and to make known to those who cannot penetrate it all that we imagine, and all the various stirrings of our soul’ This was how, in 1660, the renowned French grammarians of the Port-Royal abbey near Versailles <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5cee99a-0d55-4d95-b5dc-eb4012fd121e\" data-question=\"38\">distilled the essence of language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, and no one since has celebrated more eloquently the magnitude of its achievement. Even so, there is just one flaw in all these hymns of praise, for the homage to languages unique accomplishment conceals a simple yet critical incongruity. Language is mankind s greatest invention – except, of course, that it was never invented. This apparent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"975efdb0-e375-48a9-bfb4-aebd563d43bf\" data-question=\"28\">paradox<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> is at the core of our fascination with language, and it holds many of its secrets.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Language often seems so skillfully drafted that one can hardly imagine it as anything other than the perfected handiwork of a master craftsman. How else could this instrument make so much out of barely three dozen measly morsels of sound? In themselves, these configurations of mouth <em>p,f,b,v,t,d,k,g,sh,a,e</em> and so on – amount to nothing more than a few haphazard spits and splutters, random noises with no meaning, no ability to express, no power to explain. But run them through the cogs and wheels of the language machine, let it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6eb6759a-f532-4821-964e-9a2f3488a70c\" data-question=\"29\">arrange them in some very special orders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b21b9baa-f428-4754-9e38-8f1ed151c194\" data-question=\"29\">there is nothing that these meaningless streams of air cannot do<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>: from sighing the interminable boredom of existence to unravelling the fundamental order of the universe.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>The most extraordinary thing about language, however, is that one doesn’t have to be a genius to set its wheels in motion. The language machine <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4194728-0ecc-4bf0-a631-036a248ef8e7\" data-question=\"30\">allows just about everybody<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> from pre-modern foragers in the subtropical savannah, to post-modern philosophers in the suburban sprawl – to tie these meaningless sounds together into an infinite variety of subtle senses, and all apparently without the slightest exertion. Yet it is precisely this deceptive ease which makes language a victim of its own success, since in everyday life its triumphs <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c9da1ba2-bbf1-447f-bb67-6303252dac64\" data-question=\"36\">are usually taken for granted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. The wheels of language run so smoothly that one rarely bothers to stop and think about all the resourcefulness and expertise that must have gone into making it tick. Language conceals art.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Often, it is only the estrangement of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c82263f5-7031-4623-ae5a-ed8ea3c0b910\" data-question=\"31\">foreign tongues, with their many exotic and outlandish features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, that brings home the wonder of languages design. One of the showiest stunts that some languages can pull off is an ability to build up words of breath-breaking length, and thus express in one word what English takes a whole sentence to say. The Turkish word <em>çehirliliçtiremediklerimizdensiniz</em>, to take one example, means nothing less than ‘you are one of those whom we can’t turn into a town-dweller’. (In case you were wondering, this monstrosity really is one word, not merely many different words squashed together – most ol its components cannot even stand up on their own.)</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>And if that sounds like some one-off freak, then consider Sumerian, the language spoken on the banks of the Euphrates some 5,000 years ago by the people who invented writing and thus enabled the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b98f204-a87e-446c-9081-b828217ab08f\" data-question=\"40\">documentation of history<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. A Sumerian word like <em>munintuma’a</em> (‘when he had made it suitable for her’) might seem rather trim compared to the Turkish colossus above. What is so impressive about it, however, is not its lengthiness but rather the reverse – the thrifty compactness of its construction. The word is made up of different slots, each corresponding to a particular portion of meaning. This sleek design allows single sounds to convey useful information, and in fact even the absence of a sound <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"91f7e65f-2c50-437a-aea5-0b657cf26da9\" data-question=\"32\">has been enlisted to express something specific<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. If you were to ask which bit in the Sumerian word corresponds to the pronoun ‘it’ in the English translation ‘when he had made it suitable for her’, then the answer would have to be nothing. Mind you, a very particular kind of nothing: the nothing that stands in the empty slot in the middle. The technology is so fine-tuned then that even a non-sound, when carefully placed in a particular position, has been invested with a specific function. Who could possibly have come up with such a nifty contraption?</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has six paragraphs, <strong>A-F</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for paragraphs <strong>A-F</strong> from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct number, <strong>i-vii</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-32</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Headings</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>i </strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c82263f5-7031-4623-ae5a-ed8ea3c0b910\" data-question=\"31\">Differences between languages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> highlight their impressiveness</span></p><p><span><strong>ii</strong> The way in which a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6eb6759a-f532-4821-964e-9a2f3488a70c\" data-question=\"29\">few sounds are organised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b21b9baa-f428-4754-9e38-8f1ed151c194\" data-question=\"29\">convey a huge range of meaning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>iii</strong> Why the sounds used in different languages are not identical</span></p><p><span><strong>iv</strong> Apparently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"975efdb0-e375-48a9-bfb4-aebd563d43bf\" data-question=\"28\">incompatible characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of language</span></p><p><span><strong>v</strong> Even silence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"91f7e65f-2c50-437a-aea5-0b657cf26da9\" data-question=\"32\">can be meaningful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>vi</strong> Why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eea9a613-d29c-4131-909a-5bae1d8079a3\" data-question=\"27\">language is the most important invention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of all</span></p><p><span><strong>vii</strong> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4194728-0ecc-4bf0-a631-036a248ef8e7\" data-question=\"30\">universal ability to use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> language</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"915\" id=\"question-wrapper-915\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"916\" id=\"question-wrapper-916\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"917\" id=\"question-wrapper-917\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"918\" id=\"question-wrapper-918\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"919\" id=\"question-wrapper-919\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"920\" id=\"question-wrapper-920\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, <strong>A-G</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>33-36</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>The importance of language</strong></span></h4><p><span>The wheel is one invention that has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c9f6f2c3-0421-48ed-b814-fc2043a1bace\" data-question=\"33\">had a major impact on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <strong>33</strong>……………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93881f0c-34c8-4b74-8e83-a66e6274b563\" data-question=\"33\">aspects of life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, but no impact has been as <strong>34</strong>………………. as that of language. Language is very <strong>35</strong>…………………, yet composed of just a small number of sounds.</span></p><p><span>Language appears to be <strong>36</strong>………………… to use. However, its sophistication <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c9da1ba2-bbf1-447f-bb67-6303252dac64\" data-question=\"36\">is often overlooked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> difficult <strong>B</strong> complex <strong>C</strong> original</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> admired <strong>E</strong> material <strong>F </strong> easy</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong> fundamental</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"921\" id=\"question-wrapper-921\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"922\" id=\"question-wrapper-922\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"923\" id=\"question-wrapper-923\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"924\" id=\"question-wrapper-924\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>37-40</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"925\" id=\"question-wrapper-925\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Human beings might <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0546cd99-999b-49d8-b373-9fbd71bfc9b9\" data-question=\"37\">have achieved their present position<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4a09d907-f033-4d4f-b6fa-597ca3e0f545\" data-question=\"37\">without language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"926\" id=\"question-wrapper-926\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Port-Royal grammarians <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5cee99a-0d55-4d95-b5dc-eb4012fd121e\" data-question=\"38\">did justice to the nature of language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"927\" id=\"question-wrapper-927\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A complex idea can be explained more clearly in a sentence than in a single word. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"928\" id=\"question-wrapper-928\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Sumerians were responsible for starting the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b98f204-a87e-446c-9081-b828217ab08f\" data-question=\"40\">recording of events<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"eea9a613-d29c-4131-909a-5bae1d8079a3","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"language is the most important invention","passagePhrase":"language must take pride of place"},{"uid":"c9f6f2c3-0421-48ed-b814-fc2043a1bace","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"had a major impact on","passagePhrase":"may have transformed"},{"uid":"93881f0c-34c8-4b74-8e83-a66e6274b563","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"aspects of life","passagePhrase":"existence"},{"uid":"b7284b1c-ceb4-4e84-bf9d-6662e7a411a7","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"advent"},{"uid":"4c96fb20-e3bc-4b33-99ed-febb742ba970","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"significance"},{"uid":"0546cd99-999b-49d8-b373-9fbd71bfc9b9","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"have achieved their present position","passagePhrase":"have embarked on our ascent"},{"uid":"e5cee99a-0d55-4d95-b5dc-eb4012fd121e","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"did justice to the nature of language","passagePhrase":"distilled the essence of language"},{"uid":"975efdb0-e375-48a9-bfb4-aebd563d43bf","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"incompatible characteristics","passagePhrase":"paradox"},{"uid":"6eb6759a-f532-4821-964e-9a2f3488a70c","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"few sounds are organised","passagePhrase":"arrange them in some very special orders"},{"uid":"b21b9baa-f428-4754-9e38-8f1ed151c194","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"convey a huge range of meaning","passagePhrase":"there is nothing that these meaningless streams of air cannot do"},{"uid":"d4194728-0ecc-4bf0-a631-036a248ef8e7","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"universal ability to use","passagePhrase":"allows just about everybody"},{"uid":"c9da1ba2-bbf1-447f-bb67-6303252dac64","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"is often overlooked","passagePhrase":"are usually taken for granted"},{"uid":"c82263f5-7031-4623-ae5a-ed8ea3c0b910","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Differences between languages","passagePhrase":"foreign tongues, with their many exotic and outlandish features"},{"uid":"1b98f204-a87e-446c-9081-b828217ab08f","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"recording of events","passagePhrase":"documentation of history"},{"uid":"91f7e65f-2c50-437a-aea5-0b657cf26da9","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"can be meaningful","passagePhrase":"has been enlisted to express something specific"}]},"reading_u2_211":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong>Cork</strong></span></h2><p><span>Cork – the thick bark of the cork oak tree (<em>Quercus suber) </em>– is a remarkable material. It is tough, elastic, buoyant, and fire-resistant, and suitable for a wide range of purposes. It has also been used for millennia: the ancient Egyptians sealed their sarcophagi (stone coffins) with cork, while the ancient Greeks and Romans used it for anything from beehives to sandals.</span></p><p><span>And the cork oak itself is an extraordinary tree. Its bark grows up to 20 cm in thickness, insulating the tree like a coat wrapped around the trunk and branches and keeping the inside at a constant 20<sup>o</sup>C all year round. Developed most probably as a defence against forest fires, the bark of the cork oak has a particular cellular structure – with about 40 million cells per cubic centimetre – that technology <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7bd615cf-2835-4ca9-9240-c801b90c103b\" data-question=\"2\">has never succeeded in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4cac5e7-c531-4b65-bac9-d3eee572276c\" data-question=\"2\">replicating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. The cells are filled with air, which is why cork is so buoyant. It also has an elasticity that means you can squash it and watch it spring back to its original size and shape when you release the pressure.</span></p><p><span>Cork oaks grow in a number of Mediterranean countries, including Portugal, Spain, Italy, Greece and Morocco. They flourish in warm, sunny climates where there is a minimum of 400 millimetres of rain per year, and not more than 800 millimetres. Like grape vines, the trees thrive in poor soil, putting down deep roots in search of moisture and nutrients. Southern Portugal’s Alentejo region meets all of these requirements, which explains why, by the early 20th century, this region had become the world’s largest producer of cork, and why today it accounts for roughly half of all cork production around the world.</span></p><p><span>Most cork forests are family-owned. Many of these family businesses, and indeed many of the trees themselves, are around 200 years old. Cork production is, above all, an exercise in patience. From the planting of a cork sapling to the first harvest takes 25 years, and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"67e4b454-44f6-493c-8676-f3c244fef8e8\" data-question=\"3\">a gap of approximately a decade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> must separate harvests from an individual tree. And for top-quality cork, it’s necessary to wait a further 15 or 20 years. You even have to wait for the right kind of summer’s day to harvest cork. If the bark is stripped on a day when it’s too cold – or when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7ff603c-a28b-4f16-806a-009a3b28ef2f\" data-question=\"4\">the air<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c4419769-6eb4-42aa-8fdc-0d0b5be7da0c\" data-question=\"4\">damp<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> – the tree will be damaged.</span></p><p><span>Cork harvesting is a very specialised profession. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"65a83e7a-5c04-49ce-8782-7debd0becef7\" data-question=\"5\">No <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8ee2042d-fe90-451f-8ef5-e367eb721265\" data-question=\"5\">mechanical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> means of stripping cork bark has been invented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, so the job is done by teams of highly skilled workers. First, they make vertical cuts down the bark using small sharp axes, then lever it away in pieces as large as they can manage. The most skilful cork-strippers prise away a semi-circular husk that runs the length of the trunk from just above ground level to the first branches. It is then dried on the ground for about four months, before being taken to factories, where it is boiled to kill any insects that might remain in the cork. Over 60% of cork then goes on to be made into traditional bottle stoppers, with most of the remainder being used in the construction trade. Corkboard and cork tiles are ideal for thermal and acoustic insulation, while granules of cork are used in the manufacture of concrete.</span></p><p><span>Recent years have seen the end of the virtual monopoly of cork as the material for bottle stoppers, due to concerns about the effect it may have on the contents of the bottle. This is caused by a chemical compound called 2,4,6-trichloroanisole (TCA), which forms through the interaction of plant phenols, chlorine and mould. The tiniest concentrations – as little as three or four parts to a trillion – can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71f30d50-5cad-4837-94ce-1fb5c84fd858\" data-question=\"6\">spoil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the taste of the product contained in the bottle. The result has been a gradual yet steady move first towards plastic stoppers and, more recently, to aluminium screw caps. These substitutes are cheaper to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1800e646-dca0-4cbf-a972-dea87fcdac8b\" data-question=\"7\">manufacture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and, in the case of screw caps, move convenient <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98ad97e7-3af4-4799-8e6b-f4adcb384177\" data-question=\"8\">for the user<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The classic cork stopper does have several advantages, however. Firstly, its traditional image is more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d1f62cbb-fb2a-4143-9bab-1352739723d4\" data-question=\"9\">in keeping with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> that of the type of high quality <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23ce5307-fd5f-4a8d-b2c4-9f8daa84ce6b\" data-question=\"9\">goods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> with which it has long been associated. Secondly – and very importantly – cork is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3d62bd0-5b97-4647-8499-108ad0b2fbf4\" data-question=\"10\">a sustainable product<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> that can be recycled <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ce89b4f-709c-4d08-8700-c44d7f98a3cc\" data-question=\"11\">without difficulty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Moreover, cork forests are a resource which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6029a7a-a075-4001-898e-2d18beae62bc\" data-question=\"12\">support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> local biodiversity, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb58969d-3991-4e36-b8fc-d9f5efd04aff\" data-question=\"13\">prevent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> desertification in the regions where they are planted. So, given the current concerns about environmental issues, the future of this ancient material once again looks promising.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>1-5</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"614\" id=\"question-wrapper-614\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The cork oak has the thickest bark of any living tree. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"615\" id=\"question-wrapper-615\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Scientists <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7bd615cf-2835-4ca9-9240-c801b90c103b\" data-question=\"2\">have developed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> a synthetic cork with the same cellular structures as natural cork. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"616\" id=\"question-wrapper-616\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Individual cork oak trees must be left for <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"67e4b454-44f6-493c-8676-f3c244fef8e8\" data-question=\"3\">25 years between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the first and second harvest. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"617\" id=\"question-wrapper-617\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Cork bark should be stripped in <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c4419769-6eb4-42aa-8fdc-0d0b5be7da0c\" data-question=\"4\">dry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7ff603c-a28b-4f16-806a-009a3b28ef2f\" data-question=\"4\">atmospheric conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"618\" id=\"question-wrapper-618\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"65a83e7a-5c04-49ce-8782-7debd0becef7\" data-question=\"5\">The only way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to remove the bark from cork oak trees is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8ee2042d-fe90-451f-8ef5-e367eb721265\" data-question=\"5\">by hand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes bolow.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>6-13</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>Comparison of aluminium screw caps and cork bottle stoppers</strong></span></h3><p><span><strong><u>Advantages of aluminium screw caps</u></strong></span></p><p><span><span>•</span> do not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71f30d50-5cad-4837-94ce-1fb5c84fd858\" data-question=\"6\">affect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the <strong>6</strong>…………………………… of the bottle contents</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> are <strong>7</strong>…………………………….. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1800e646-dca0-4cbf-a972-dea87fcdac8b\" data-question=\"7\">produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></span></p><p><span><span>•</span> are <strong>8</strong>……………………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98ad97e7-3af4-4799-8e6b-f4adcb384177\" data-question=\"8\">to use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong><u>Advantages of cork bottle stoppers</u></strong></span></p><p><span><span>•</span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d1f62cbb-fb2a-4143-9bab-1352739723d4\" data-question=\"9\">suit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> the <strong>9</strong>……………………………… of quality <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23ce5307-fd5f-4a8d-b2c4-9f8daa84ce6b\" data-question=\"9\">products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p><p><span><span>•</span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3d62bd0-5b97-4647-8499-108ad0b2fbf4\" data-question=\"10\">made from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> a <strong>10</strong>……………………………… material</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ce89b4f-709c-4d08-8700-c44d7f98a3cc\" data-question=\"11\">easily<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <strong>11</strong>…………………………….</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> cork forests <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6029a7a-a075-4001-898e-2d18beae62bc\" data-question=\"12\">aid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <strong>12</strong>…………………………………</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> cork forests <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb58969d-3991-4e36-b8fc-d9f5efd04aff\" data-question=\"13\">stop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <strong>13</strong>………………………………. happening</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"619\" id=\"question-wrapper-619\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TASTE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"620\" id=\"question-wrapper-620\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CHEAPER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"621\" id=\"question-wrapper-621\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CONVENIENT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"622\" id=\"question-wrapper-622\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IMAGE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"623\" id=\"question-wrapper-623\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SUSTAINABLE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"624\" id=\"question-wrapper-624\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RECYCLED</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"625\" id=\"question-wrapper-625\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BIODIVERSITY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"626\" id=\"question-wrapper-626\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DESERTIFICATION</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e4cac5e7-c531-4b65-bac9-d3eee572276c","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"replicating"},{"uid":"b7ff603c-a28b-4f16-806a-009a3b28ef2f","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"atmospheric conditions","passagePhrase":"the air"},{"uid":"71f30d50-5cad-4837-94ce-1fb5c84fd858","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"affect","passagePhrase":"spoil"},{"uid":"1800e646-dca0-4cbf-a972-dea87fcdac8b","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"produce","passagePhrase":"manufacture"},{"uid":"98ad97e7-3af4-4799-8e6b-f4adcb384177","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"to use","passagePhrase":"for the user"},{"uid":"d1f62cbb-fb2a-4143-9bab-1352739723d4","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"suit","passagePhrase":"in keeping with"},{"uid":"23ce5307-fd5f-4a8d-b2c4-9f8daa84ce6b","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"products","passagePhrase":"goods"},{"uid":"b3d62bd0-5b97-4647-8499-108ad0b2fbf4","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"made from","passagePhrase":"a sustainable product"},{"uid":"1ce89b4f-709c-4d08-8700-c44d7f98a3cc","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"easily","passagePhrase":"without difficulty"},{"uid":"a6029a7a-a075-4001-898e-2d18beae62bc","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"aid","passagePhrase":"support"},{"uid":"fb58969d-3991-4e36-b8fc-d9f5efd04aff","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"stop","passagePhrase":"prevent"}]},"reading_u2_212":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong><span>COLLECTING AS A HOBBY</span></strong></span></h2><p><span>Collecting must be one of the most varied of human activities, and it’s one that many of us psychologists find fascinating. Many forms of collecting have been dignified with a technical name: an archtophilist collects teddy bears, a philatelist collects postage stamps, and a deltiologist collects postcards. Amassing hundreds or even thousands of postcards, chocolate wrappers or whatever, takes time, energy and money that could surely be put to much more productive use. And yet there are millions of collectors around the world. Why do they do it?</span></p><p><span>There are the people who collect <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f6dd0f22-fe04-4ce0-8a1d-8e6bed5e857b\" data-question=\"14\">because<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> they want to make money – this could be called an instrumental reason for collecting; that is, collecting as a means to an end. They’ll look for, say, antiques that they can buy cheaply and expect to be able to sell at a profit. But there may well be a psychological element, too – buying cheap and selling dear can give the collector <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4f3a9ab-27b6-4a19-9f64-ad062217264e\" data-question=\"15\">a sense of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> triumph. And as selling online is so easy, more and more people are joining in.</span></p><p><span>Many collectors collect to develop their social life, attending meetings of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cc31460c-bfca-4eb0-9844-f32390008131\" data-question=\"16\">a group of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> collectors and exchanging information on items. This is a variant on joining a bridge club or a gym, and similarly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c83da134-389a-4fe1-8054-dad7116c7f8a\" data-question=\"17\">brings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> them into contact with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8a27f19-77df-4f11-93b9-e703f4d229aa\" data-question=\"17\">like-minded people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Another motive for collecting is the desire to find <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74db64f2-12b7-4148-bf1f-fd325795c4e0\" data-question=\"18\">something special<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, or a particular example of the collected item, such as a rare early recording by a particular singer. Some may spend their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebcca100-e0a6-4ee8-ab1f-837e0cb9c4e1\" data-question=\"18\">whole lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7cca692-8e6f-4c9c-8eeb-51e7bc27b262\" data-question=\"19\">a hunt for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> this. Psychologically, this can give a purpose to a life that otherwise feels aimless. There is a danger, though, that if the individual is ever lucky enough to find what they’re looking for, rather than celebrating their success, they may feel empty, now that the goal that drove them on has gone.</span></p><p><span>If you think about collecting postage stamps, another potential reason for it – or, perhaps, a result of collecting – is its educational value. Stamp collecting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13f5ae59-4389-4d99-93cc-f90cc9aafd81\" data-question=\"20\">opens a window to other countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, and to the plants, animals, or famous people shown on their stamps. Similarly, in the 19th century, many collectors amassed fossils, animals and plants from around the globe, and their collections provided a vast amount of information about the natural world. Without those collections, our understanding would be greatly inferior to what it is.</span></p><p><span>In the past – and nowadays, too, though to a lesser extent – a popular form of collecting, particularly among <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b996b903-be9b-4f3b-95ad-301392d89c2a\" data-question=\"21\">boys and men<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, was trainspotting. This might involve trying to see every locomotive of a particular type, using published data that identifies each one, and ticking off each engine as it is seen. Trainspotters <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d9c7a23-b764-4185-96fe-16e0845f1d56\" data-question=\"16\">exchange<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> information, these days often by mobile phone, so they can work out where to go to, to see a particular engine. As a by-product, many practitioners of the hobby become very knowledgeable about railway operations, or the technical specifications of different engine types.</span></p><p><span>Similarly, people who collect dolls may go beyond simply enlarging their collection, and develop an interest in the way that dolls are made, or the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"984d8c10-7336-4af1-9f27-d9476bc4dcfb\" data-question=\"23\">materials that are used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. These have changed over the centuries from the wood that was standard in 16th century Europe, through <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f3f9398e-3f42-4ff2-8743-657d7dd0996b\" data-question=\"23\">the wax and porcelain of later centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, to the plastics of today’s dolls. Or collectors might be inspired to study how dolls reflect notions of what children like, or ought to like.</span></p><p><span>Not all collectors are interested in learning from their hobby, though, so what we might call a psychological reason for collecting is the need for a sense of control, perhaps as a way of dealing with insecurity. Stamps collectors, for instance, arrange their stamps in albums, usually very neatly, organising their collection according to certain commonplace principles – perhaps by country in alphabetical order, or grouping stamps by what they depict – people, birds, maps, and so on.</span></p><p><span>One reason, conscious or not, for <em>what</em> someone chooses to collect is to show the collector’s individualism. Someone who decides to collect something as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6156c6a5-bd4c-49eb-b552-9fdaddf77cd5\" data-question=\"25\">unexpected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> as dos collars, for instance, may be conveying their belief that they must be interesting themselves. And believe it or not, there is at least one dog collar museum in existence, and it grew out of a personal collection.</span></p><p><span>Of course, all hobbies give pleasure, but the common factor in collecting is usually passion: pleasure is putting it far too mildly. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4786de5-d9d7-4000-9b59-32c3288cc8c3\" data-question=\"26\">More than most other hobbies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, collecting can be totally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e3e37ff-1f0c-4cc2-b2b9-93c596970221\" data-question=\"26\">engrossing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, and can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c53ca2bc-ef7f-4d9a-951b-befaf0177f23\" data-question=\"26\">give a strong sense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> of personal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e3e37ff-1f0c-4cc2-b2b9-93c596970221\" data-question=\"26\">fulfilment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. To non-collectors it may appear an eccentric, if harmless, way of spending time, but potentially, collecting has a lot going for it.</span></p><p><span> </span><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the sentences below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>14-21</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"627\" id=\"question-wrapper-627\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer mentions collecting …………………….. as an example of collecting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f6dd0f22-fe04-4ce0-8a1d-8e6bed5e857b\" data-question=\"14\">in order to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> make money. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ANTIQUES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"628\" id=\"question-wrapper-628\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Collectors may get <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4f3a9ab-27b6-4a19-9f64-ad062217264e\" data-question=\"15\">a feeling of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> …………………….. from buying and selling items. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRIUMPH</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"629\" id=\"question-wrapper-629\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cc31460c-bfca-4eb0-9844-f32390008131\" data-question=\"16\">Collectors’ clubs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> provide opportunities to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d9c7a23-b764-4185-96fe-16e0845f1d56\" data-question=\"16\">share<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>…………………………… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INFORMATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"630\" id=\"question-wrapper-630\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Collectors’ clubs <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c83da134-389a-4fe1-8054-dad7116c7f8a\" data-question=\"17\">offer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> ………………………. with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8a27f19-77df-4f11-93b9-e703f4d229aa\" data-question=\"17\">people who have similar interests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CONTACT/MEETINGS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"631\" id=\"question-wrapper-631\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Collecting sometimes involves a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebcca100-e0a6-4ee8-ab1f-837e0cb9c4e1\" data-question=\"18\">life-long<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>………………………. for a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74db64f2-12b7-4148-bf1f-fd325795c4e0\" data-question=\"18\">special item<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HUNT/DESIRE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"632\" id=\"question-wrapper-632\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7cca692-8e6f-4c9c-8eeb-51e7bc27b262\" data-question=\"19\">Searching for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> something particular may prevent people from feeling their life is completely………………………. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AIMLESS/EMPTY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"633\" id=\"question-wrapper-633\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Stamp collecting may be ……………………….. because it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13f5ae59-4389-4d99-93cc-f90cc9aafd81\" data-question=\"20\">provides facts about different countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EDUCATIONAL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"634\" id=\"question-wrapper-634\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> ……………………….. tends to be mostly a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b996b903-be9b-4f3b-95ad-301392d89c2a\" data-question=\"21\">male<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> hobby. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRAINSPOTTING</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in the passage on pages 20 and 21?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>22-26</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"635\" id=\"question-wrapper-635\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The number of people buying dolls has grown over the centuries. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"636\" id=\"question-wrapper-636\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f3f9398e-3f42-4ff2-8743-657d7dd0996b\" data-question=\"23\">Sixteenth century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> European dolls were normally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"984d8c10-7336-4af1-9f27-d9476bc4dcfb\" data-question=\"23\">made of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> wax and porcelain. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"637\" id=\"question-wrapper-637\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Arranging a stamp collection by the size of the stamps is less common than other methods. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"638\" id=\"question-wrapper-638\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Someone who collects <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6156c6a5-bd4c-49eb-b552-9fdaddf77cd5\" data-question=\"25\">unusual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> objects may want others to think he or she is also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6156c6a5-bd4c-49eb-b552-9fdaddf77cd5\" data-question=\"25\">unusual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"639\" id=\"question-wrapper-639\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Collecting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c53ca2bc-ef7f-4d9a-951b-befaf0177f23\" data-question=\"26\">gives a feeling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4786de5-d9d7-4000-9b59-32c3288cc8c3\" data-question=\"26\">other hobbies are unlikely to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e3e37ff-1f0c-4cc2-b2b9-93c596970221\" data-question=\"26\">inspire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f6dd0f22-fe04-4ce0-8a1d-8e6bed5e857b","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"in order to","passagePhrase":"because"},{"uid":"e4f3a9ab-27b6-4a19-9f64-ad062217264e","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"a feeling of","passagePhrase":"a sense of"},{"uid":"cc31460c-bfca-4eb0-9844-f32390008131","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Collectors’ clubs","passagePhrase":"a group of"},{"uid":"c83da134-389a-4fe1-8054-dad7116c7f8a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"offer","passagePhrase":"brings"},{"uid":"c8a27f19-77df-4f11-93b9-e703f4d229aa","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"people who have similar interests","passagePhrase":"like-minded people"},{"uid":"74db64f2-12b7-4148-bf1f-fd325795c4e0","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"special item","passagePhrase":"something special"},{"uid":"ebcca100-e0a6-4ee8-ab1f-837e0cb9c4e1","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"life-long","passagePhrase":"whole lives"},{"uid":"f7cca692-8e6f-4c9c-8eeb-51e7bc27b262","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Searching for","passagePhrase":"a hunt for"},{"uid":"13f5ae59-4389-4d99-93cc-f90cc9aafd81","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"provides facts about different countries","passagePhrase":"opens a window to other countries"},{"uid":"b996b903-be9b-4f3b-95ad-301392d89c2a","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"male","passagePhrase":"boys and men"},{"uid":"7d9c7a23-b764-4185-96fe-16e0845f1d56","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"share","passagePhrase":"exchange"},{"uid":"984d8c10-7336-4af1-9f27-d9476bc4dcfb","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"made of","passagePhrase":"materials that are used"},{"uid":"6156c6a5-bd4c-49eb-b552-9fdaddf77cd5","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"unusual ... unusual","passagePhrase":"unexpected"},{"uid":"b4786de5-d9d7-4000-9b59-32c3288cc8c3","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"other hobbies are unlikely to","passagePhrase":"More than most other hobbies"},{"uid":"2e3e37ff-1f0c-4cc2-b2b9-93c596970221","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"inspire","passagePhrase":"engrossing ... fulfilment"},{"uid":"c53ca2bc-ef7f-4d9a-951b-befaf0177f23","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"gives a feeling","passagePhrase":"give a strong sense"}]},"reading_u2_213":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>What’s the purpose of gaining knowledge?</strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>‘I would found an institution where any person can find instruction in any subject.’ That was the founder’s motto for Cornell University, and it seems an apt characterization of the different university, also in the USA, where I currently teach philosophy. A student can prepare for a career in resort management, engineering, interior design, accounting, music, law enforcement, you name it. But what would the founders of these two institutions have thought of a course called ‘Arson for Profit’? <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d912621-9ce5-4d80-9c86-62646c91f0ae\" data-question=\"27\">I kid you not<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>: we have it on the books. Any undergraduates who have met the academic requirements can sign up for the course in our program in ‘fire science’.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Naturally, the course is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4f39de7a-0f7b-4d70-9444-f0e2e0f36805\" data-question=\"34\">intended for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> prospective arson investigators, who can learn all the tricks of the trade for detecting whether a fire was deliberately set, discovering who did it, and establishing a chain of evidence for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09706a9c-7e6a-4d0f-aea7-0523cb6dd5d2\" data-question=\"36\">effective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> prosecution in a court of law. But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7153551-f986-4251-b2aa-cb921f923ecd\" data-question=\"28\">wouldn’t this also be the perfect course for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b2a41d74-eea3-4dd5-9534-f62a909b295d\" data-question=\"38\">prospective arsonists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> to sign up for? My point is not to criticize academic programs in fire science: they <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e98c159f-0025-4686-98b8-f828c6937879\" data-question=\"39\">are highly welcome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> as part of the increasing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb925213-381c-4cff-a724-a4511bb81d93\" data-question=\"39\">professionalization<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of this and many other occupations. However, it’s not unknown for a firefighter to torch a building. This example suggests how dishonest and illegal behavior, with the help of higher education, can creep into every aspect of public and business life.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>I realized this anew when I was invited to speak before a class in marketing, which is another of our degree programs. The regular instructor is a colleague who appreciates the kind of ethical perspective. I can bring as a philosopher. There are endless ways I could have approached this assignment, but I took my cue from the title of the course: ‘Principles of Marketing’. It made me think to ask the students, ‘Is marketing principled?’ After all, a subject matter can have principles <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7e61273-f3c6-402a-b432-e1134506aa6f\" data-question=\"29\">in the sense of being codified, having rules<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, as with football or chess, without <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7e61273-f3c6-402a-b432-e1134506aa6f\" data-question=\"29\">being principled in the sense of being ethical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Many of the students immediately assumed that the answer to my question about marketing principles was obvious: <em>no</em>. Just look at the ways in which everything under the sun has been marketed; obviously it need not be done in a <em>principled </em>(=ethical) fashion.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>Is that obvious? I made the suggestion, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11907447-c810-40b3-9dce-f87c5934c8d0\" data-question=\"30\">may sound downright crazy in light of the evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, that perhaps marketing is <em>by definition </em>principled. My inspiration for this judgement is the philosopher Immanuel Kant, who argued that any body of knowledge consists of an end (or purpose) and a means.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Let us apply both the terms ‘means’ and ‘end’ to marketing. The students have signed up for a course in order to learn how to market effectively. But to what <em>end</em>? There seem to be two main attitudes toward that question. One is that the answer is obvious: the purpose of marketing is to sell things and to make money. The other attitude is that the <em>purpose </em>of marketing is irrelevant: Each person comes to the program and course with his or her own plans, and these need not even concern the acquisition of marketing expertise as such. My proposal, which I believe would also be Kant’s, is that <em>neither</em> of these attitudes captures the significance of the end to the means for marketing. A field of knowledge or a professional endeavor is defined by both the means <em>and </em>the end; hence <em>both </em><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41292a2a-ec45-4203-8340-61589ae4e572\" data-question=\"31\">deserve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> scrutiny. Students need to study both how to achieve X, and also what X is.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>It is at this point that ‘Arson for Profit’ becomes supremely relevant. That course is presumably all about <em>means</em>: how to detect and prosecute criminal activity. It is therefore assumed that the <em>end </em>is good in an ethical sense. When I ask fire science students to articulate the end, or purpose, of their field, they eventually <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2fa8bec7-0df9-43eb-8ba4-b3480d8ee9cd\" data-question=\"40\">generalize to something like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, ‘The safety and welfare of society,’ which seems right. As we have seen, someone could use the very same knowledge of <em>means </em>to achieve a much less noble end such as personal profit via destructive, dangerous, reckless activity. But <em>we would not call that firefighting</em>. We have a separate word for it: <em>arson. </em>Similarly, if you employed the ‘principles of marketing’ is an unprincipled way, <em>you would not be doing marketing. </em>We have another term for it: <em>fraud. </em>Kant gives the example of a doctor and a poisoner, who use the identical knowledge to achieve their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"839d12ef-40ac-4452-b4d5-932baf43250c\" data-question=\"32\">divergent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c770c89a-8552-42a1-bf77-0ca3558c2318\" data-question=\"32\">ends<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. We would say that one is practicing medicine, the other, murder.</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Reading Passage 3 has six sections, <strong>A-F</strong>.<br>Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.</p><p><em>Write the correct number, i-viii, in boxes <strong>27-32</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><p><strong>i </strong> Courses that require a high level of commitment</p><p><strong>ii</strong> A course title with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7e61273-f3c6-402a-b432-e1134506aa6f\" data-question=\"29\">two meanings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></p><p><strong>iii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41292a2a-ec45-4203-8340-61589ae4e572\" data-question=\"31\">The equal importance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of two key issues</p><p><strong>iv </strong> Applying a theory in an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11907447-c810-40b3-9dce-f87c5934c8d0\" data-question=\"30\">unexpected context<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></p><p><strong>v </strong> The financial benefits of studying</p><p><strong>vi</strong> A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d912621-9ce5-4d80-9c86-62646c91f0ae\" data-question=\"27\">surprising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> course title</p><p><strong>vii </strong> Different names for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"839d12ef-40ac-4452-b4d5-932baf43250c\" data-question=\"32\">different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c770c89a-8552-42a1-bf77-0ca3558c2318\" data-question=\"32\">outcomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></p><p><strong>viii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7153551-f986-4251-b2aa-cb921f923ecd\" data-question=\"28\">The possibility of attracting the wrong kind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of student</p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"640\" id=\"question-wrapper-640\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"641\" id=\"question-wrapper-641\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"642\" id=\"question-wrapper-642\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"643\" id=\"question-wrapper-643\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"644\" id=\"question-wrapper-644\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"645\" id=\"question-wrapper-645\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>33-36</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>The ‘Arson for Profit’ course</strong></span></h3><p><span>This is a university course intended for students who are undergraduates and who are studying <strong>33</strong>………………………. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4f39de7a-0f7b-4d70-9444-f0e2e0f36805\" data-question=\"34\">expectation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> is that they will become <strong>34</strong>…………………………. specialising in arson. The course will help them to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"408c3c62-b586-444e-8107-45b0e4b70f4f\" data-question=\"35\">detect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> cases of arson and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"408c3c62-b586-444e-8107-45b0e4b70f4f\" data-question=\"35\">find<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <strong>35</strong>………………………. of criminal intent, leading to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09706a9c-7e6a-4d0f-aea7-0523cb6dd5d2\" data-question=\"36\">successful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <strong>36</strong>………………………… in the courts.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"646\" id=\"question-wrapper-646\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FIRE SCIENCE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"647\" id=\"question-wrapper-647\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INVESTIGATORS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"648\" id=\"question-wrapper-648\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EVIDENCE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"649\" id=\"question-wrapper-649\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PROSECUTION</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>37-40</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>YES </strong> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO </strong> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN </strong>if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"650\" id=\"question-wrapper-650\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is difficult to attract students onto courses that do not focus on a career. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"651\" id=\"question-wrapper-651\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The ‘Arson for Profit’ course would be useful for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b2a41d74-eea3-4dd5-9534-f62a909b295d\" data-question=\"38\">people intending to set fire to buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"652\" id=\"question-wrapper-652\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Fire science courses <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e98c159f-0025-4686-98b8-f828c6937879\" data-question=\"39\">are too academic to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> help people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb925213-381c-4cff-a724-a4511bb81d93\" data-question=\"39\">to be good at the job of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> firefighting. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"653\" id=\"question-wrapper-653\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer’s fire science students <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2fa8bec7-0df9-43eb-8ba4-b3480d8ee9cd\" data-question=\"40\">provided a detailed definition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> of the purpose of their studies. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"9d912621-9ce5-4d80-9c86-62646c91f0ae","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"surprising","passagePhrase":"I kid you not"},{"uid":"4f39de7a-0f7b-4d70-9444-f0e2e0f36805","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"expectation","passagePhrase":"intended for"},{"uid":"09706a9c-7e6a-4d0f-aea7-0523cb6dd5d2","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"successful","passagePhrase":"effective"},{"uid":"a7153551-f986-4251-b2aa-cb921f923ecd","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The possibility of attracting the wrong kind","passagePhrase":"wouldn’t this also be the perfect course for"},{"uid":"b2a41d74-eea3-4dd5-9534-f62a909b295d","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"people intending to set fire to buildings","passagePhrase":"prospective arsonists"},{"uid":"fb925213-381c-4cff-a724-a4511bb81d93","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"to be good at the job of","passagePhrase":"professionalization"},{"uid":"d7e61273-f3c6-402a-b432-e1134506aa6f","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"two meanings","passagePhrase":"in the sense of being codified, having rules ... being principled in the sense of being ethical"},{"uid":"11907447-c810-40b3-9dce-f87c5934c8d0","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"unexpected context","passagePhrase":"may sound downright crazy in light of the evidence"},{"uid":"41292a2a-ec45-4203-8340-61589ae4e572","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"The equal importance","passagePhrase":"deserve"},{"uid":"839d12ef-40ac-4452-b4d5-932baf43250c","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"different","passagePhrase":"divergent"},{"uid":"c770c89a-8552-42a1-bf77-0ca3558c2318","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"outcomes","passagePhrase":"ends"},{"uid":"408c3c62-b586-444e-8107-45b0e4b70f4f","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"detect ... find","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_214":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions</strong> <strong>1-13</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</p><p> </p><h2><strong>The risks agriculture faces in developing countries</strong></h2><p><em>Synthesis of an online debate*</em></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Two things <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4193bf2d-6f69-4ac3-8381-2e67d0bd0172\" data-question=\"1\">distinguish food production from all other productive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> activities: first, every single person needs food each day and has a right to it; and second, it is hugely dependent on nature. These two unique aspects, one political, the other natural, make food production highly vulnerable and different from any other business. At the same time, cultural values are highly entrenched in food and agricultural systems worldwide.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>Farmers everywhere face major risks, including extreme weather, long-term climate change, and price volatility in input and product markets. However, smallholder farmers in developing countries must in addition deal with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f65910ef-5753-48df-a433-f6639500b7f5\" data-question=\"2\">adverse environments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, both natural, in terms of soil quality, rainfall, etc., and human, in terms of infrastructure, financial systems, markets, knowledge and technology. Counter-intuitively, hunger is prevalent among many smallholder farmers in the developing world.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>Participants in the online debate argued that our biggest challenge is to address the underlying causes of the agricultural system’s inability to ensure sufficient food for all, and they identified as drivers of this problem our dependency on fossil fuels and unsupportive government policies.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>On the question of mitigating the risks farmers face, most essayists called for greater state intervention. In his essay, Kanayo F. Nwanze, President of the International Fund for Agricultural Development, argued that governments can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d94bd61-b27b-4171-b10f-9af5fa5c0418\" data-question=\"9\">significantly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> reduce risks for farmers by providing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7757bb4-75e1-4cef-978f-cc8ec581686e\" data-question=\"9\">basic services<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> like roads to get produce more efficiently to markets, or water and food storage facilities to reduce losses. Sophia Murphy, senior advisor to the Institute for Agriculture and Trade Policy, suggested that the procurement and holding of stocks by governments can also help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a81b45a6-1ae2-4d95-9579-763b86ad8f3c\" data-question=\"8\">mitigate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83fe1510-c781-4231-8f88-76402580d80f\" data-question=\"8\">wild swings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in food prices by alleviating uncertainties about market supply. </p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Shenggen Fan, Director General of the International Food Policy Research Institute, held up <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6b50ed83-7991-4ed5-81a3-fd2ad5b378ca\" data-question=\"6\">social safety nets and public welfare programmes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> in Ethiopia, Brazil and Mexico as valuable ways to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c5b86d4-0b8e-49e1-92c9-3bd7d7d8429e\" data-question=\"6\">address poverty among farming families<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> and reduce their vulnerability to agriculture shocks. However, some commentators responded that cash transfers to poor families do not necessarily translate into increased food security, as these programmes do not always strengthen food production or raise incomes. Regarding <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b48c0d8-488f-42eb-8451-a0dcd0570ef5\" data-question=\"4\">state subsidies for agriculture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, Rokeya Kabir, Executive Director of Bangladesh Nari Progati Sangha, commented in her essay that these ‘have not compensated for the stranglehold exercised by private traders. In fact, studies show that sixty percent of beneficiaries of subsidies are not poor, but rich landowners and non-farmer traders.’</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>Nwanze, Murphy and Fan argued that private risk management tools, like private insurance, commodity futures markets, and rural finance can help small-scale producers mitigate risk and allow for investment in improvements. Kabir warned that financial support schemes often encourage the adoption of high-input agricultural practices, which in the medium term may raise production costs beyond the value of their harvests. Murphy noted that when futures markets become excessively financialised they can contribute to short-term price volatility, which increases farmers’ food insecurity. Many participants and commentators emphasised that greater transparency in markets is needed to mitigate the impact of volatility, and make evident whether adequate stocks and supplies are available. Others contended that agribusiness companies should be held responsible for paying for negative side effects.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>Many essayists mentioned <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"996e0da6-1a1b-4c10-a211-f873e18629f7\" data-question=\"10\">climate change and its consequences for small-scale agriculture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. Fan explained that ‘in addition to reducing crop yields, climate change increases the magnitude and frequency of extreme weather events, which increase smallholder vulnerability.’ The growing unpredictability of weather patterns increases farmers’ difficulty in managing weather-related risks. According to this author, one solution would be to develop crop varieties that are more resilient to new climate trends and extreme weather patterns. Accordingly, Pat Mooney, co-founder and executive director of the ETC Group, suggested that ‘if we are to survive climate change, we must adopt policies that let peasants diversify the plant and animal species and varieties/breeds that make up our menus.’</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>Some participating authors and commentators argued in favour of community-based and autonomous risk management strategies through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1db5c465-dcf1-44a1-abb2-838b81147f5e\" data-question=\"3\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b27b4a9b-c896-4b87-b3fb-ba8f76245b62\" data-question=\"5\">collective action<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> groups, co-operatives or producers’ groups. Such groups enhance market opportunities for small-scale producers, reduce marketing costs and synchronise buying and selling with seasonal price conditions. According to Murphy, ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1db5c465-dcf1-44a1-abb2-838b81147f5e\" data-question=\"3\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b27b4a9b-c896-4b87-b3fb-ba8f76245b62\" data-question=\"5\">collective action<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> offers an important way for farmers to strengthen their political and economic bargaining power, and to reduce their business risks.’ One commentator, Giel Ton, warned that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1db5c465-dcf1-44a1-abb2-838b81147f5e\" data-question=\"3\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b27b4a9b-c896-4b87-b3fb-ba8f76245b62\" data-question=\"5\">collective action<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> does not come as a free good. It takes time, effort and money to organise, build trust and to experiment. Others, like Marcel Vernooij and Marcel Beukeboom, suggested that in order to ‘apply what we already know’, all <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1861897b-e192-4d73-8f46-d7c13c259acc\" data-question=\"13\">stakeholders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, including business, government, scientists and civil society, must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71bfc863-eb53-4f84-8e3e-62122c5e4cf7\" data-question=\"13\">work together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, starting at the beginning of the value chain.</p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p>Some participants explained that market price volatility is often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5ef6244-22e9-4bd0-9a18-3d39f8bae328\" data-question=\"11\">worsened by the presence of intermediary purchasers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> who, taking advantage of farmers’ vulnerability, dictate prices. One commentator suggested farmers can gain greater control over prices and minimise price volatility by selling directly to consumers. Similarly, Sonali Bisht, founder and advisor to the Institute of Himalayan Environmental Research and Education (INHERE), India, wrote that community-supported agriculture, where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da5e9ce5-cc13-43a8-af55-bf649b3d4b27\" data-question=\"7\">consumers invest in local farmers by subscription<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and guarantee producers a fair price, is a risk-sharing model worth more attention. Direct food distribution systems not only encourage small-scale agriculture but also give consumers more control over the food they consume, she wrote.</p><p>———————<br>* The personal names in the text refer to the authors of written contributions to the online debate</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has nine paragraphs, <strong>A-I</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-I</strong>, in boxes <strong>1-3</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"654\" id=\"question-wrapper-654\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to characteristics that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4193bf2d-6f69-4ac3-8381-2e67d0bd0172\" data-question=\"1\">only apply to food production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"655\" id=\"question-wrapper-655\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f65910ef-5753-48df-a433-f6639500b7f5\" data-question=\"2\">challenges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> faced only by farmers in certain parts of the world </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"656\" id=\"question-wrapper-656\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to difficulties in bringing about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1db5c465-dcf1-44a1-abb2-838b81147f5e\" data-question=\"3\">co-operation between farmers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Question 4-9) and the list of people below.<br></span><span>Match each statement with the correct person, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>4-9</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of People</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Kanayo F. Nwanze<br></span><strong>B</strong><span> Sophia Murphy<br></span><strong>C</strong><span> Shenggen Fan<br></span><strong>D</strong><span> Rokeya Kabir<br></span><strong>E</strong><span> Pat Mooney<br></span><strong>F</strong><span> Giel Ton<br></span><strong>G</strong><span> Sonali Bisht</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"657\" id=\"question-wrapper-657\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b48c0d8-488f-42eb-8451-a0dcd0570ef5\" data-question=\"4\">Financial assistance from the government<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> does not always go to the farmers who most need it. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"658\" id=\"question-wrapper-658\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Farmers can benefit from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b27b4a9b-c896-4b87-b3fb-ba8f76245b62\" data-question=\"5\">collaborating as a group<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"659\" id=\"question-wrapper-659\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6b50ed83-7991-4ed5-81a3-fd2ad5b378ca\" data-question=\"6\">Financial assistance from the government<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c5b86d4-0b8e-49e1-92c9-3bd7d7d8429e\" data-question=\"6\">improve the standard of living<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of farmers. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"660\" id=\"question-wrapper-660\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Farmers may be helped if there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da5e9ce5-cc13-43a8-af55-bf649b3d4b27\" data-question=\"7\">financial input by the same individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> who buy from them. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"661\" id=\"question-wrapper-661\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Governments can help to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a81b45a6-1ae2-4d95-9579-763b86ad8f3c\" data-question=\"8\">reduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83fe1510-c781-4231-8f88-76402580d80f\" data-question=\"8\">variation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in prices. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"662\" id=\"question-wrapper-662\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Improvements to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7757bb4-75e1-4cef-978f-cc8ec581686e\" data-question=\"9\">infrastructure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> can have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d94bd61-b27b-4171-b10f-9af5fa5c0418\" data-question=\"9\">major<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> impact on risk for farmers. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E</strong>.<br></span><span>Write the correct letters in boxes </span><strong>10</strong><span> and </span><strong>11</strong><span> on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>Which <strong>TWO</strong> problems are mentioned which affect farmers with small farms in developing countries?</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> lack of demand for locally produced food</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> lack of irrigation programmes</span></p><p><span><strong>C </strong> being unable to get insurance</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"996e0da6-1a1b-4c10-a211-f873e18629f7\" data-question=\"10\">the effects of changing weather patterns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> having to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5ef6244-22e9-4bd0-9a18-3d39f8bae328\" data-question=\"11\">sell their goods to intermediary buyers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span></span><span> </span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"663\" id=\"question-wrapper-663\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D/E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"664\" id=\"question-wrapper-664\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D/E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E</strong>.<br></span><span>Write the correct letters in boxes </span><strong>12</strong><span> and </span><strong>13</strong><span> on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span>Which <strong>TWO</strong> actions are recommended for improving conditions for farmers?</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> reducing the size of food stocks</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> attempting to ensure that prices rise at certain times of the year</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> organising <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71bfc863-eb53-4f84-8e3e-62122c5e4cf7\" data-question=\"13\">co-operation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> between a wide range of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1861897b-e192-4d73-8f46-d7c13c259acc\" data-question=\"13\">interested parties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> encouraging consumers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"63c61837-1221-4e39-a7e5-e7aafbac8889\" data-question=\"12\">take a financial stake<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in farming</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> making customers aware of the reasons for changing food prices</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"665\" id=\"question-wrapper-665\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"666\" id=\"question-wrapper-666\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"4193bf2d-6f69-4ac3-8381-2e67d0bd0172","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"only apply to food production","passagePhrase":"distinguish food production from all other productive"},{"uid":"f65910ef-5753-48df-a433-f6639500b7f5","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"challenges","passagePhrase":"adverse environments"},{"uid":"4d94bd61-b27b-4171-b10f-9af5fa5c0418","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"major","passagePhrase":"significantly"},{"uid":"f7757bb4-75e1-4cef-978f-cc8ec581686e","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"infrastructure","passagePhrase":"basic services"},{"uid":"a81b45a6-1ae2-4d95-9579-763b86ad8f3c","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"reduce","passagePhrase":"mitigate"},{"uid":"83fe1510-c781-4231-8f88-76402580d80f","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"variation","passagePhrase":"wild swings"},{"uid":"6b50ed83-7991-4ed5-81a3-fd2ad5b378ca","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Financial assistance from the government","passagePhrase":"social safety nets and public welfare programmes"},{"uid":"5c5b86d4-0b8e-49e1-92c9-3bd7d7d8429e","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"improve the standard of living","passagePhrase":"address poverty among farming families"},{"uid":"1b48c0d8-488f-42eb-8451-a0dcd0570ef5","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Financial assistance from the government","passagePhrase":"state subsidies for agriculture"},{"uid":"996e0da6-1a1b-4c10-a211-f873e18629f7","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the effects of changing weather patterns","passagePhrase":"climate change and its consequences for small-scale agriculture"},{"uid":"1db5c465-dcf1-44a1-abb2-838b81147f5e","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"co-operation between farmers","passagePhrase":"collective action ... collective action ... collective action"},{"uid":"b27b4a9b-c896-4b87-b3fb-ba8f76245b62","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"collaborating as a group","passagePhrase":"collective action ... collective action ... collective action"},{"uid":"1861897b-e192-4d73-8f46-d7c13c259acc","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"interested parties","passagePhrase":"stakeholders"},{"uid":"71bfc863-eb53-4f84-8e3e-62122c5e4cf7","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"co-operation","passagePhrase":"work together"},{"uid":"b5ef6244-22e9-4bd0-9a18-3d39f8bae328","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"sell their goods to intermediary buyers","passagePhrase":"worsened by the presence of intermediary purchasers"},{"uid":"da5e9ce5-cc13-43a8-af55-bf649b3d4b27","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"financial input by the same individuals","passagePhrase":"consumers invest in local farmers by subscription"},{"uid":"63c61837-1221-4e39-a7e5-e7aafbac8889","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"take a financial stake","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_215":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong><span>The Lost City</span></strong></span></h2><p><span><em>An explorer’s encounter with the ruined city of Machu Picchu, the most famous icon of the Inca civilisation</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>When the US explorer and academic Hiram Bingham arrived in South America in 1911, he was ready for what was to be the greatest achievement of his life: the exploration of the remote hinterland to the west of Cusco, the old capital of the Inca empire in the Andes mountains of Peru. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb869fc9-5c9f-4470-ba61-999a59a6d457\" data-question=\"14\">His goal was to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"65dff785-f106-4164-a446-1f69d2f3df4d\" data-question=\"21\">locate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> the remains of a city called Vitcos, the last <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90dd4083-29ce-4cb3-970b-7b462b947b47\" data-question=\"21\">capital of the Inca civilisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Cusco lies on a high plateau at an elevation of more than 3,000 metres, and Bingham’s plan was to descend from this plateau along the valley of the Urubamba river, which takes a circuitous route down to the Amazon and passes through an area of dramatic canyons and mountain ranges.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>When Bingham and his team set off down the Urubamba in late July, they had an advantage over travelers who had preceded them: a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa3a1626-7497-4c19-8eea-899113e07413\" data-question=\"15\">track had recently been blasted down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> the valley canyon to enable rubber <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebdceba4-d37c-452d-814c-28a6dcf909e2\" data-question=\"25\">to be brought up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> by mules from the jungle. Almost all previous travelers had left the river at Ollantaytambo and taken a high pass across the mountains to rejoin the river lower down, thereby cutting a substantial corner, but also therefore never passing through the area around Machu Picchu.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>On 24 July they were a few days into their descent of the valley. The day began slowly, with Bingham trying to arrange sufficient mules for the next stage of the trek. His companions showed no interest in accompanying him up the nearby hill to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1f7978e4-f5b9-4480-afba-50a973d0967d\" data-question=\"26\">see some ruins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> that a local farmer, Melchor Arteaga, had told them about the night before. The morning was dull and damp, and Bingham also seems to have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea1bb2c8-a1de-45b8-a178-0662ab4a1d1f\" data-question=\"16\">less than keen on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> the prospect of climbing the hill. In his book <em>Lost City of the Incas</em>, he relates that he made the ascent without having the least expectation that he would find anything at the top.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>Bingham writes about the approach in vivid style in his book. First, as he climbs up the hill, he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7f0be63-a427-4ca4-acb1-e3edb51e4109\" data-question=\"17\">describes the ever-present possibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of deadly snakes, ‘capable of making considerable springs when in pursuit of their prey’; not that he sees any. Then there’s a sense of mounting discovery as he comes across great sweeps of terraces, then a mausoleum, followed by monumental staircases and, finally, the grand ceremonial buildings of Machu Picchu. ‘It seemed like an unbelievable dream … the sight held me spellbound …’ he wrote.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>We should remember, however, that <em>Lost City of the Incas </em>is a work of hindsight, not written until 1948, many years after his journey. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb7fc89e-fd3d-4d95-9c48-f78385bb3c2f\" data-question=\"18\">His journal entries of the time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> reveal a much more gradual appreciation of his achievement. He spent the afternoon at the ruins noting down the dimensions of some of the buildings, then descended and rejoined his companions, to whom he seems to have said little about his discovery. At this stage, Bingham <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c3c99513-82c0-435a-ae6c-956289c31414\" data-question=\"23\">didn’t realise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> the extent or the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70eaf2b2-9500-4fd3-89fe-5ae0ac7d2991\" data-question=\"23\">importance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of the site, nor did he realise what use he could make of the discovery.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>However, soon after returning it occurred to him that he could make a name for himself from this discovery. When he came to write the National Geographic magazine article that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3fbcd46b-008c-4364-b104-93bb4f04061b\" data-question=\"19\">broke the story to the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in April 1913, he knew he had to produce a big idea. He wondered whether it could have been the birthplace of the very first Inca, Manco the Great, and whether it could also have been what chroniclers described as ‘the last city of the Incas’. This term refers to Vilcabamba, the settlement where the Incas had fled from Spanish invaders in the 1530s. Bingham made <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dcbd0c5d-2964-4bbe-a8a5-154e40efac43\" data-question=\"24\">desperate attempts to prove this belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> for nearly 40 years. Sadly, his vision of the site as both the beginning and end of the Inca civilisation, while a magnificent one, is inaccurate. We now know that Vilcabamba actually lies 65 kilometres away in the depths of the jungle.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>One question that has perplexed visitors, historians and archaeologists alike ever since Bingham, is why the site seems to have been abandoned before the Spanish Conquest. There are no references to it by any of the Spanish chroniclers – and if they had known of its existence so close to Cusco they would certainly have come in search of gold. An idea which has gained <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e33f5cb-92db-4655-9e5f-cba139f10a3b\" data-question=\"20\">wide acceptance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> over the past few years is that Machu Picchu was a <em>moya</em>, a country estate built by an Inca emperor to escape the cold winters of Cusco, where the elite could enjoy monumental architecture and spectacular views. Furthermore, the particular architecture of Machu Picchu suggests that it was constructed at the time of the greatest of all the Incas, the emperor Pachacuti (c. 1438-71). By custom, Pachacuti’s descendants built other similar estates for their own use, and so Machu Picchu would have been abandoned after his death, some 50 years before the Spanish Conquest.</span></p><p><span> </span><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G</strong>.<br></span><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, <strong>i-viii</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-20</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span><strong>List of headings</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>i</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb7fc89e-fd3d-4d95-9c48-f78385bb3c2f\" data-question=\"18\">Different accounts of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the same journey</span></p><p><span><strong>ii </strong> Bingham gains support</span></p><p><span><strong>iii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e33f5cb-92db-4655-9e5f-cba139f10a3b\" data-question=\"20\">A common belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>iv</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb869fc9-5c9f-4470-ba61-999a59a6d457\" data-question=\"14\">The aim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of the trip</span></p><p><span><strong>v</strong> A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7f0be63-a427-4ca4-acb1-e3edb51e4109\" data-question=\"17\">dramatic description<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>vi</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa3a1626-7497-4c19-8eea-899113e07413\" data-question=\"15\">A new route<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>vii </strong> Bingham <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3fbcd46b-008c-4364-b104-93bb4f04061b\" data-question=\"19\">publishes his theory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>viii</strong> Bingham’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea1bb2c8-a1de-45b8-a178-0662ab4a1d1f\" data-question=\"16\">lack of enthusiasm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"667\" id=\"question-wrapper-667\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"668\" id=\"question-wrapper-668\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"669\" id=\"question-wrapper-669\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"670\" id=\"question-wrapper-670\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"671\" id=\"question-wrapper-671\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"672\" id=\"question-wrapper-672\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"673\" id=\"question-wrapper-673\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>21-24</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN </strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"674\" id=\"question-wrapper-674\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bingham went to South America in search of an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90dd4083-29ce-4cb3-970b-7b462b947b47\" data-question=\"21\">Inca city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"675\" id=\"question-wrapper-675\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bingham <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9680bdce-aea7-45f9-864a-cf4d8530852b\" data-question=\"22\">chose a particular route down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the Urubamba valley because it was the most common route used by travellers. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"676\" id=\"question-wrapper-676\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bingham <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c3c99513-82c0-435a-ae6c-956289c31414\" data-question=\"23\">understood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70eaf2b2-9500-4fd3-89fe-5ae0ac7d2991\" data-question=\"23\">significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of Machu Picchu as soon as he saw it. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"677\" id=\"question-wrapper-677\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bingham returned to Machu Picchu in order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dcbd0c5d-2964-4bbe-a8a5-154e40efac43\" data-question=\"24\">find evidence to support his theory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the sentences below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>25-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"678\" id=\"question-wrapper-678\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The track that took Bingham down the Urubamba valley <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebdceba4-d37c-452d-814c-28a6dcf909e2\" data-question=\"25\">had been created for the transportation of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> ……………………………. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RUBBER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"679\" id=\"question-wrapper-679\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bingham <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1f7978e4-f5b9-4480-afba-50a973d0967d\" data-question=\"26\">found out about the ruins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> of Machu Picchu from a …………………………….. in the Urubamba valley. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FARMER</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"cb869fc9-5c9f-4470-ba61-999a59a6d457","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"The aim","passagePhrase":"His goal was to"},{"uid":"65dff785-f106-4164-a446-1f69d2f3df4d","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"locate"},{"uid":"90dd4083-29ce-4cb3-970b-7b462b947b47","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Inca city","passagePhrase":"capital of the Inca civilisation"},{"uid":"aa3a1626-7497-4c19-8eea-899113e07413","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"A new route","passagePhrase":"track had recently been blasted down"},{"uid":"ebdceba4-d37c-452d-814c-28a6dcf909e2","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"had been created for the transportation of","passagePhrase":"to be brought up"},{"uid":"1f7978e4-f5b9-4480-afba-50a973d0967d","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"found out about the ruins","passagePhrase":"see some ruins"},{"uid":"ea1bb2c8-a1de-45b8-a178-0662ab4a1d1f","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"lack of enthusiasm","passagePhrase":"less than keen on"},{"uid":"f7f0be63-a427-4ca4-acb1-e3edb51e4109","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"dramatic description","passagePhrase":"describes the ever-present possibility"},{"uid":"cb7fc89e-fd3d-4d95-9c48-f78385bb3c2f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Different accounts of","passagePhrase":"His journal entries of the time"},{"uid":"70eaf2b2-9500-4fd3-89fe-5ae0ac7d2991","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"significance","passagePhrase":"importance"},{"uid":"3fbcd46b-008c-4364-b104-93bb4f04061b","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"publishes his theory","passagePhrase":"broke the story to the world"},{"uid":"dcbd0c5d-2964-4bbe-a8a5-154e40efac43","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"find evidence to support his theory","passagePhrase":"desperate attempts to prove this belief"},{"uid":"6e33f5cb-92db-4655-9e5f-cba139f10a3b","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"A common belief","passagePhrase":"wide acceptance"}]},"reading_u2_216":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><h2><span><strong><span>The Benefits of Being Bilingual</span></strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>According to the latest figures, the majority of the world’s population is now bilingual or multilingual, having grown up speaking two or more languages. In the past, such children were considered to be at a disadvantage compared with their monolingual peers. Over the past few decades, however, technological advances have allowed researchers to look more deeply at how bilingualism interacts with and changes the cognitive and neurological systems, thereby <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53ab17ca-6f28-4641-b665-191a125f2031\" data-question=\"32\">identifying several clear benefits of being bilingual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Research shows that when a bilingual person uses one language, the other is active at the same time. When <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cfb1c3d-1245-4530-98ca-04503bcac88d\" data-question=\"39\">we hear a word<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, we don’t hear the entire word all at once: the sounds arrive in sequential order. Long before the word is finished, the brain’s language system begins to guess what that word might be. If you hear ‘can’, you will likely activate words like ‘candy’ and ‘candle’ as well, at least during the earlier stages of word recognition. For bilingual people, this activation is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47fd1091-fce2-4d57-974f-fb07d0e0273b\" data-question=\"28\">not limited to a single language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>; auditory input activates corresponding words regardless of the language to which they belong. Some of the most compelling evidence for this phenomenon, called ‘language co-activation’, comes from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"672c775d-0ea6-498e-9944-7d7648c357a7\" data-question=\"27\">studying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> eye movements. A Russian-English bilingual asked to ‘pick up a marker’ from a set of objects would look more at a stamp than someone who doesn’t know Russian, because the Russian word for ‘stamp’, <em>marka</em>, sounds like the English word he or she heard, ‘marker’. In cases like this, language co-activation occurs because what the listener hears could map onto words in either language.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Having to deal with this persistent linguistic competition <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48f41075-ea3e-49a1-a3de-970e0f3f229c\" data-question=\"40\">can result in difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, however. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5563765-8766-4922-8dfe-d3899b50c0f6\" data-question=\"40\">For instance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, knowing more than one language can cause speakers to name <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"916e9162-44a4-4f20-8b0b-0224c62db964\" data-question=\"34\">pictures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"992b613a-c08a-4e67-8122-b7f61ba9a187\" data-question=\"34\">more slowly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, and can increase ‘tip-of-the-tongue states’, when you can almost, but not quite, bring a word to mind. As a result, the constant juggling of two languages creates a need to control how much a person accesses a language at any given time. For this reason, bilingual people often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"799ce359-beb9-42d7-9a5b-d3d0f42cdde9\" data-question=\"30\">perform better on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> tasks that require conflict management. In the classic Stroop Task, people see a word and are asked to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d561f836-12a4-4214-92e4-51c761d75865\" data-question=\"29\">name the colour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of the word’s font. When the colour and the word match (i.e., the word ‘red’ printed in red), people correctly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d561f836-12a4-4214-92e4-51c761d75865\" data-question=\"29\">name the colour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> more quickly than when the colour and the word don’t match (i.e., the word ‘red’ printed in blue). This occurs because the word itself (‘red’) and its font colour (blue) conflict. Bilingual people often excel at tasks such as this, which top into the ability to ignore competing perceptual information and focus on the relevant aspects of the input. Bilinguals are also better at switching between two tasks; for example, when bilinguals have to switch from categorizing objects by colour (red or green) to categorizing them by shape (circle or triangle), they do so more quickly than monolingual people, reflecting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ac954d8-e467-42a4-892b-c5960268d2b5\" data-question=\"31\">better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> cognitive control when having to make rapid changes of strategy.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>It also seems that the neurological roots of the bilingual advantage extend to brain areas more traditionally associated with sensory processing. When monolingual and bilingual adolescents <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ef75cb8-65da-460b-a8b2-13fd698a6387\" data-question=\"35\">listen to simple speech sounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> without any intervening background noise, they <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d8c5aa89-48ed-40d8-b022-bb7da3c6482f\" data-question=\"35\">show highly similar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> brain stem responses. When researchers play the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6e1393f-512a-46f7-9a0a-8093ec4fe4ad\" data-question=\"37\">same sound<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to both groups <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6e1393f-512a-46f7-9a0a-8093ec4fe4ad\" data-question=\"37\">in the presence of background noise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, however, the bilingual listeners’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"25da5229-d6c8-480f-b663-dbadaf20439a\" data-question=\"37\">neural response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> is considerably larger, reflecting better encoding of the sound’s fundamental frequency, a feature of sound closely related to pitch perception.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Such improvements in cognitive and sensory processing may help a bilingual person to process information in the environment, and help explain why bilingual adults acquire a third language better than monolingual adults master a second language. This advantage may be rooted in the skill of focussing on information about the new language while reducing interference from the languages they already know.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>Research also indicates that bilingual experience may help to keep the cognitive mechanisms sharp by recruiting alternate brain networks to compensate for those that become damaged during aging. Older bilinguals enjoy improved memory relative to monolingual people, which can lead to real-world health benefits. In a study of over 200 patients with Alzheimer’s disease, a degenerative brain disease, bilingual patients reported showing initial symptoms of the disease an average of five years later than monolingual patients. In a follow-up study, researchers compared the brains of bilingual and monolingual patients matched on the severity of Alzheimer’s symptoms. Surprisingly, the bilinguals’ brains had more physical signs of disease than their monolingual counterparts, even though their outward behaviour and abilities were the same. If the brain is an engine, bilingualism may help it to go farther on the same amount of fuel.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>Furthermore, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24bf9c69-7ef3-4090-97cf-0b4e96274346\" data-question=\"38\">benefits associated with bilingual experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> seem to start very early. In one study, researchers taught seven-month-old babies growing up in monolingual or bilingual homes that when they heard a tinkling sound, a puppet appeared on one side of a screen. Halfway through the study, the puppet began appearing on the opposite side of the screen. In order to get a reward, the infants had to adjust the rule they’d learned; only the bilingual babies were able to successfully learn the new rule. This suggests that for very young children, as well as for older people, navigating a multilingual environment imparts advantages that transfer far beyond language.</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the table below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p><table><tbody><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span><strong>Test</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span><strong>Findings</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"672c775d-0ea6-498e-9944-7d7648c357a7\" data-question=\"27\">Observing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the <strong>27</strong>…………………. of Russian-English bilingual people when asked to select certain objects</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>Bilingual people engage <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47fd1091-fce2-4d57-974f-fb07d0e0273b\" data-question=\"28\">both languages simultaneously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>: a mechanism known as <strong>28</strong>…………………..</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span>A test called the <strong>29</strong>…………………, focusing on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d561f836-12a4-4214-92e4-51c761d75865\" data-question=\"29\">naming colours<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>Bilingual people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"799ce359-beb9-42d7-9a5b-d3d0f42cdde9\" data-question=\"30\">are more able to handle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> tasks involving a skill called <strong>30</strong>…………………</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"312\"><p><span>A test involving switching between tasks</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>When changing strategies, bilingual people have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ac954d8-e467-42a4-892b-c5960268d2b5\" data-question=\"31\">superior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <strong>31</strong>…………………..</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"680\" id=\"question-wrapper-680\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EYE MOVEMENTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"681\" id=\"question-wrapper-681\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LANGUAGE CO-ACTIVATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"682\" id=\"question-wrapper-682\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STROOP TASK</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"683\" id=\"question-wrapper-683\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CONFLICT MANAGEMENT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"684\" id=\"question-wrapper-684\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COGNITIVE CONTROL</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</p><p>In boxes <strong>32-36</strong> on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</p><p><strong>NO </strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</p><p><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN </strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"685\" id=\"question-wrapper-685\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53ab17ca-6f28-4641-b665-191a125f2031\" data-question=\"32\">Attitudes towards bilingualism have changed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> in recent years. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"686\" id=\"question-wrapper-686\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bilingual people are better than monolingual people at guessing correctly what words are before they are finished. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"687\" id=\"question-wrapper-687\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bilingual people consistently name <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"916e9162-44a4-4f20-8b0b-0224c62db964\" data-question=\"34\">images<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"992b613a-c08a-4e67-8122-b7f61ba9a187\" data-question=\"34\">faster than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> monolingual people. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"688\" id=\"question-wrapper-688\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bilingual people’s brains <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ef75cb8-65da-460b-a8b2-13fd698a6387\" data-question=\"35\">process single sounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d8c5aa89-48ed-40d8-b022-bb7da3c6482f\" data-question=\"35\">more efficiently than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> monolingual people in all situations. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"689\" id=\"question-wrapper-689\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Fewer bilingual people than monolingual people suffer from brain disease in old age. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>37-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"690\" id=\"question-wrapper-690\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an example of how bilingual and monolingual people’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"25da5229-d6c8-480f-b663-dbadaf20439a\" data-question=\"37\">brains respond<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> differently to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6e1393f-512a-46f7-9a0a-8093ec4fe4ad\" data-question=\"37\">certain type of non-verbal auditory input<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"691\" id=\"question-wrapper-691\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a demonstration of how a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24bf9c69-7ef3-4090-97cf-0b4e96274346\" data-question=\"38\">bilingual upbringing has benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> even before we learn to speak </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"692\" id=\"question-wrapper-692\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of the process by which people identify <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cfb1c3d-1245-4530-98ca-04503bcac88d\" data-question=\"39\">words that they hear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"693\" id=\"question-wrapper-693\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5563765-8766-4922-8dfe-d3899b50c0f6\" data-question=\"40\">reference to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48f41075-ea3e-49a1-a3de-970e0f3f229c\" data-question=\"40\">some negative consequences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> of being bilingual </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"53ab17ca-6f28-4641-b665-191a125f2031","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Attitudes towards bilingualism have changed","passagePhrase":"identifying several clear benefits of being bilingual"},{"uid":"7cfb1c3d-1245-4530-98ca-04503bcac88d","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"words that they hear","passagePhrase":"we hear a word"},{"uid":"47fd1091-fce2-4d57-974f-fb07d0e0273b","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"both languages simultaneously","passagePhrase":"not limited to a single language"},{"uid":"672c775d-0ea6-498e-9944-7d7648c357a7","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Observing","passagePhrase":"studying"},{"uid":"48f41075-ea3e-49a1-a3de-970e0f3f229c","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"some negative consequences","passagePhrase":"can result in difficulties"},{"uid":"b5563765-8766-4922-8dfe-d3899b50c0f6","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"reference to","passagePhrase":"For instance"},{"uid":"916e9162-44a4-4f20-8b0b-0224c62db964","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"images","passagePhrase":"pictures"},{"uid":"799ce359-beb9-42d7-9a5b-d3d0f42cdde9","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"are more able to handle","passagePhrase":"perform better on"},{"uid":"d561f836-12a4-4214-92e4-51c761d75865","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"naming colours","passagePhrase":"name the colour ... name the colour"},{"uid":"1ac954d8-e467-42a4-892b-c5960268d2b5","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"superior","passagePhrase":"better"},{"uid":"8ef75cb8-65da-460b-a8b2-13fd698a6387","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"process single sounds","passagePhrase":"listen to simple speech sounds"},{"uid":"b6e1393f-512a-46f7-9a0a-8093ec4fe4ad","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"certain type of non-verbal auditory input","passagePhrase":"same sound ... in the presence of background noise"},{"uid":"25da5229-d6c8-480f-b663-dbadaf20439a","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"brains respond","passagePhrase":"neural response"},{"uid":"24bf9c69-7ef3-4090-97cf-0b4e96274346","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"bilingual upbringing has benefits","passagePhrase":"benefits associated with bilingual experience"}]},"reading_u2_217":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong><span>Flying tortoises</span></strong></span></h2><p><span><em>An airborne reintroduction programme has helped conservationists take significant steps to protect the endangered Galápagos tortoise.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>Forests of spiny cacti cover much of the uneven lava plains that separate the interior of the Galápagos island of Isabela from the Pacific Ocean. With its five distinct volcanoes, the island resembles a lunar landscape. Only the thick vegetation at the skirt of the often cloud-covered peak of Sierra Negra offers respite from the barren terrain below. This inhospitable environment <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"91dbcdcd-1da2-41f0-995e-9c97914a5c59\" data-question=\"1\">is home to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> the giant Galápagos tortoise. Some time after the Galápagos’s birth, around five million years ago, the islands were colonised by one or more tortoises from mainland South America. As these ancestral tortoises settled on the individual islands, the different populations adapted to their unique environments, giving rise to at least 14 different subspecies. Island life agreed with them. In the absence of significant predators, they grew to become the largest and longest-living tortoises on the planet, weighing more than 400 kilograms, occasionally exceeding 1.8 metres in length and living for more than a century.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Before human arrival, the archipelago’s tortoises numbered in the hundreds of thousands. From the 17th century onwards, pirates <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"402e6405-18b2-4b7e-8d86-3da4a84c932b\" data-question=\"8\">took a few on board<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78a2fd72-1aca-4b86-8480-0d89f855cdc5\" data-question=\"9\">for food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, but the arrival of whaling ships in the 1790s saw <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0ed928c-8650-4cb3-8c31-5b2ac3674e37\" data-question=\"2\">this exploitation grow exponentially<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Relatively immobile and capable of surviving for months without food or water, the tortoises were taken on board these ships to act as food supplies during long ocean passages. Sometimes, their bodies were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d12aaef-2b1b-47e3-9d3e-f818dc4e8baa\" data-question=\"10\">processed into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> high-grade oil. In total, an estimated 200,000 animals were taken from the archipelago before the 20th century. This historical exploitation was then exacerbated when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"224d2e09-802a-4e72-a9db-3c17da6efc0f\" data-question=\"11\">settlers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> came to the islands. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"224d2e09-802a-4e72-a9db-3c17da6efc0f\" data-question=\"11\">They<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> hunted the tortoises and destroyed their habitat to clear land for agriculture. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"224d2e09-802a-4e72-a9db-3c17da6efc0f\" data-question=\"11\">They<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e672c44a-0402-4bd8-b9b3-4a79d2ca4367\" data-question=\"12\">introduced alien species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> – ranging from cattle, pigs, goats, rats and dogs to plants and ants – that either <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee091e5d-2f1b-42ea-b27e-cd6acd880e90\" data-question=\"13\">prey<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> on the eggs and young tortoises or damage or destroy their habitat.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Today, only 11 of the original subspecies survive and of these, several are highly endangered. In 1989, work <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd934cc4-aba4-4067-9404-2dbbd638c80b\" data-question=\"3\">began<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> on a tortoise-breeding centre just outside the town of Puerto Villamil on Isabela, dedicated to protecting the island’s tortoise populations. The centre’s captive-breeding programme proved to be extremely successful, and it eventually had to deal with an overpopulation problem.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>The problem was also a pressing one. Captive-bred tortoises can’t be reintroduced into the wild until they’re at least five years old and weigh at least 4.5 kilograms, at which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cfab726-2c82-41f5-871d-e39902adc4c2\" data-question=\"4\">point<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> their size and weight – and their hardened shells – are sufficient to protect them from predators. But if people wait too long after that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cfab726-2c82-41f5-871d-e39902adc4c2\" data-question=\"4\">point<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, the tortoises eventually become too large to transport.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>For years, repatriation efforts were carried out in small numbers, with the tortoises carried on the backs of men over weeks of long, treacherous hikes along narrow trails. But in November 2010, the environmentalist and Galápagos National Park liaison officer Godfrey Merlin, a visiting private motor yacht captain and a helicopter pilot gathered around a table in a small café in Puerto Ayora on the island of Santa Cruz to work out <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c436e917-f560-4a04-8387-ab77138c894b\" data-question=\"5\">more ambitious reintroduction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. The aim was to use a helicopter to move 300 of the breeding centre’s tortoises to various locations close to Sierra Negra.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>This unprecedented effort was made possible by the owners of the 67-metre yacht While Cloud, who provided the Galápagos National Park with free use of their helicopter and its experienced pilot, as well as the logistical support of the yacht, its captain and crew. Originally an air ambulance, the yacht’s helicopter has a rear double door and a large internal space that’s well suited for cargo, so a custom crate was designed to hold up to 33 tortoises with a total weight of about 150 kilograms. This weight, together with that of the fuel, pilot and four crew, approached the helicopter’s maximum payload, and there were times when it was clearly right on the edge of the helicopter’s capabilities. During a period of three days, a group of volunteers from the breeding centre <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d493db7-e03a-46d2-846e-c67c03449400\" data-question=\"6\">worked around the clock to prepare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the young tortoises for transport. Meanwhile, park wardens, dropped off ahead of time in remote locations, cleared landing sites within the thick brush, cacti and lava rocks.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>Upon their release, the juvenile tortoises quickly spread out over their ancestral territory, investigating their new surroundings and feeding on the vegetation. Eventually, one <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b52e68c3-e451-4c02-a130-5decbb929e6e\" data-question=\"7\">tiny<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> tortoise came across a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4307701-e6c8-49e4-a321-5b80685f209f\" data-question=\"7\">fully grown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> giant who had been lumbering around the island for around a hundred years. The two stood side by side, a powerful symbol of the regeneration of an ancient species.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, <strong>i-viii</strong>, in boxes <strong>1-7</strong> on your answer sheet</span></p><p><span><strong>List of Headings</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>i</strong> The importance of getting the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cfab726-2c82-41f5-871d-e39902adc4c2\" data-question=\"4\">timing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> right</span></p><p><span><strong>ii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b52e68c3-e451-4c02-a130-5decbb929e6e\" data-question=\"7\">Young<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> meets old</span></p><p><span><strong>iii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0ed928c-8650-4cb3-8c31-5b2ac3674e37\" data-question=\"2\">Developments to the disadvantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of tortoise populations</span></p><p><span><strong>iv</strong> Planning a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c436e917-f560-4a04-8387-ab77138c894b\" data-question=\"5\">bigger idea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>v </strong> Tortoises <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"91dbcdcd-1da2-41f0-995e-9c97914a5c59\" data-question=\"1\">populate the islands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>vi </strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d493db7-e03a-46d2-846e-c67c03449400\" data-question=\"6\">Carrying out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> a carefully prepared operation</span></p><p><span><strong>vii </strong> Looking for a home for the islands’ tortoises</span></p><p><span><strong>viii </strong> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd934cc4-aba4-4067-9404-2dbbd638c80b\" data-question=\"3\">start<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of the conservation project</span><span> </span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"694\" id=\"question-wrapper-694\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"695\" id=\"question-wrapper-695\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"696\" id=\"question-wrapper-696\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"697\" id=\"question-wrapper-697\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"698\" id=\"question-wrapper-698\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"699\" id=\"question-wrapper-699\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"700\" id=\"question-wrapper-700\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>8-13</strong> on your answer sheet</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>The decline of the Galápagos tortoise</strong></span></h3><p><span><span><strong>•</strong></span> Originally from mainland South America</span></p><p><span><span><strong>• </strong></span> Numbers on Galápagos islands increased, due to lack of predators</span></p><p><span><span><strong>• </strong></span> 17th century: small numbers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"402e6405-18b2-4b7e-8d86-3da4a84c932b\" data-question=\"8\">taken onto ships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> used by <strong>8</strong>…………………………..</span></p><p><span><span><strong>• </strong></span> 1790s: very large numbers taken onto whaling ships, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78a2fd72-1aca-4b86-8480-0d89f855cdc5\" data-question=\"9\">kept for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <strong>9</strong>……………………………….., and also used <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d12aaef-2b1b-47e3-9d3e-f818dc4e8baa\" data-question=\"10\">to produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <strong>10</strong>……………………………</span></p><p><span><span><strong>• </strong></span> Hunted by <strong>11</strong>…………………………… on the islands</span></p><p><span><span><strong>• </strong></span> Habitat destruction: for the establishment of agriculture and by various <strong>12</strong>………………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e672c44a-0402-4bd8-b9b3-4a79d2ca4367\" data-question=\"12\">not native to the islands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, which also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee091e5d-2f1b-42ea-b27e-cd6acd880e90\" data-question=\"13\">fed on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> baby tortoises and tortoises’ <strong>13</strong>…………………………..</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"701\" id=\"question-wrapper-701\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PIRATES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"702\" id=\"question-wrapper-702\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOOD</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"703\" id=\"question-wrapper-703\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OIL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"704\" id=\"question-wrapper-704\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SETTLERS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"705\" id=\"question-wrapper-705\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPECIES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"706\" id=\"question-wrapper-706\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EGGS</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"91dbcdcd-1da2-41f0-995e-9c97914a5c59","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"populate the islands","passagePhrase":"is home to"},{"uid":"402e6405-18b2-4b7e-8d86-3da4a84c932b","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"taken onto ships","passagePhrase":"took a few on board"},{"uid":"78a2fd72-1aca-4b86-8480-0d89f855cdc5","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"kept for","passagePhrase":"for food"},{"uid":"b0ed928c-8650-4cb3-8c31-5b2ac3674e37","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Developments to the disadvantage","passagePhrase":"this exploitation grow exponentially"},{"uid":"2d12aaef-2b1b-47e3-9d3e-f818dc4e8baa","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"to produce","passagePhrase":"processed into"},{"uid":"224d2e09-802a-4e72-a9db-3c17da6efc0f","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"settlers ... They ... They"},{"uid":"e672c44a-0402-4bd8-b9b3-4a79d2ca4367","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"not native to the islands","passagePhrase":"introduced alien species"},{"uid":"ee091e5d-2f1b-42ea-b27e-cd6acd880e90","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"fed on","passagePhrase":"prey"},{"uid":"cd934cc4-aba4-4067-9404-2dbbd638c80b","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"start","passagePhrase":"began"},{"uid":"5cfab726-2c82-41f5-871d-e39902adc4c2","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"timing","passagePhrase":"point ... point"},{"uid":"c436e917-f560-4a04-8387-ab77138c894b","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"bigger idea","passagePhrase":"more ambitious reintroduction"},{"uid":"2d493db7-e03a-46d2-846e-c67c03449400","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Carrying out","passagePhrase":"worked around the clock to prepare"},{"uid":"b52e68c3-e451-4c02-a130-5decbb929e6e","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Young","passagePhrase":"tiny"},{"uid":"d4307701-e6c8-49e4-a321-5b80685f209f","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"fully grown"}]},"reading_u2_218":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>The Intersection of Health Sciences and Geography</strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>While many diseases that affect humans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c13a1690-f5c3-4aff-b0b2-b1782c91d7c2\" data-question=\"20\">have been eradicated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> due to improvements in vaccinations and the availability of healthcare, there are still areas around the world where certain health issues are more prevalent. In a world that is far more globalised than ever before, people come into contact with one another through travel and living closer and closer to each other. As a result, super-viruses and other infections <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b02ecb24-1b41-4a8c-a449-7bf02b39fa3a\" data-question=\"21\">resistant to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> antibiotics are becoming more and more common.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Geography can often play a very large role in the health concerns of certain populations. For instance, depending on where you live, you will not have the same health concerns as someone who lives in a different geographical region. Perhaps one of the most obvious examples of this idea is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db828534-755f-4dea-b62d-033ecb1d5d35\" data-question=\"22\">malaria-prone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> areas, which are usually tropical regions that foster a warm and damp environment in which the mosquitos that can give people this disease can grow. Malaria is much <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67922261-4248-4eb5-9369-a758a65c3339\" data-question=\"19\">less<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of a problem in high-altitude deserts, for instance.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>In some countries, geographical factors influence the health and well-being of the population in very obvious ways. In many large cities, the wind is not strong enough to clear the air of the massive amounts of smog and pollution that cause <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ae7bdc26-c936-4f7c-ba35-ef6d73059d87\" data-question=\"15\">asthma, lung problems, eyesight issues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and more in the people who live there. Part of the problem is, of course, the massive number of cars being driven, in addition to factories that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f1f4443-0654-4a27-ab21-049c9b71a2d9\" data-question=\"23\">run on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53dd766d-104f-40fa-b48f-220c9a4ffbe7\" data-question=\"23\">coal power<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. The rapid industrialisation of some countries in recent years <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e7d247dc-90ad-43f4-92fa-80337f6b0ef7\" data-question=\"24\">has also led to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the cutting down of forests to allow for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4ed2a6d-b5a9-46a4-af4c-24a09a4b2561\" data-question=\"24\">expansion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of big cities, which makes it even harder to fight the pollution with the fresh air that is produced by plants.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>It is in situations like these that the field of health geography comes into its own. It is an increasingly important area of study in a world where diseases like polio <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7af98aa-8b20-4789-a692-e9d157448a19\" data-question=\"14\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3bd7155c-017d-401c-8db2-cdf2619bfaed\" data-question=\"25\">are re-emerging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, respiratory diseases continue to spread, and malaria-prone areas are still fighting to find a better cure. Health geography is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"622e0552-f54e-498c-a728-cb46208ea8f3\" data-question=\"18\">combination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of, on the one hand, knowledge regarding geography and methods used to analyse and interpret geographical information, and on the other, the study of health, diseases and healthcare practices around the world. The aim of this hybrid science is to create solutions for common geography-based health problems. While people will always be prone to illness, the study of how geography affects our health could lead to the eradication of certain illnesses, and the prevention of others in the future. By understanding why and how we get sick, we can change the way we treat illness and disease specific to certain geographical locations.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>The geography of disease and ill health analyses the frequency with which certain diseases appear in different parts of the world, and overlays the data with the geography of the region, to see if there could be a correlation between the two. Health geographers also study factors that could make certain individuals or a population more likely to be taken ill with a specific health concern or disease, as compared with the population of another area. Health geographers in this field are usually trained as healthcare workers, and have an understanding of basic epidemiology as it relates to the spread of diseases among the population.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>Researchers study the interactions between humans and their environment that could lead to illness (such as asthma in places with high levels of pollution) and work to create a clear way of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8c07dfa-2a9b-4413-bcfa-d90cb1fc31e5\" data-question=\"16\">categorizing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> illnesses, diseases and epidemics into local and global scales. Health geographers can map the spread of illnesses and attempt to identify the reasons behind an increase or decrease in illnesses, as they work to find a way to halt the further spread or re-emergence of diseases in vulnerable populations.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>The second subcategory of health geography is the geography of healthcare provision. This group studies the availability (or lack thereof) of healthcare resources to individuals and populations around the world. In both developed and developing nations there is often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8964e03-8c88-4285-88ef-eb7907da740a\" data-question=\"17\">a very large discrepancy between the options available to people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in different social classes, income brackets, and levels of education. Individuals working in the area of the geography of healthcare provision attempt to assess the levels of healthcare in the area (for instance, it may be very difficult for people to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15003f77-3738-4e12-aefc-aa965375bc1a\" data-question=\"26\">get medical attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> because there is a mountain between their village and the nearest hospital). These researchers are on the frontline of making recommendations regarding policy to international organisations, local government bodies and others.</span></p><p><span><strong>H</strong></span></p><p><span>The field of health geography is often overlooked, but it constitutes a huge area of need in the fields of geography and healthcare. If we can understand how geography affects our health no matter where in the world we are located, we can better treat disease, prevent illness, and keep people safe and well.</span></p><p><span> </span><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has eight sections, <strong>A-H</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-H</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-19</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"707\" id=\"question-wrapper-707\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an acceptance that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7af98aa-8b20-4789-a692-e9d157448a19\" data-question=\"14\">not all diseases can be totally eliminated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"708\" id=\"question-wrapper-708\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ae7bdc26-c936-4f7c-ba35-ef6d73059d87\" data-question=\"15\">physical conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> caused by human behaviour </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"709\" id=\"question-wrapper-709\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8c07dfa-2a9b-4413-bcfa-d90cb1fc31e5\" data-question=\"16\">classifying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> diseases on the basis of how far they extend geographically </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"710\" id=\"question-wrapper-710\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reasons why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8964e03-8c88-4285-88ef-eb7907da740a\" data-question=\"17\">the level of access to healthcare can vary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> within a country </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"711\" id=\"question-wrapper-711\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of health geography as a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"622e0552-f54e-498c-a728-cb46208ea8f3\" data-question=\"18\">mixture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of different academic fields </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"712\" id=\"question-wrapper-712\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of the type of area where a particular illness is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67922261-4248-4eb5-9369-a758a65c3339\" data-question=\"19\">rare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"713\" id=\"question-wrapper-713\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Certain disease <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c13a1690-f5c3-4aff-b0b2-b1782c91d7c2\" data-question=\"20\">have disappeared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, thanks to better ……………………………… and healthcare. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VACCINATIONS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"714\" id=\"question-wrapper-714\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Because there is more contact between people, ………………………………. are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b02ecb24-1b41-4a8c-a449-7bf02b39fa3a\" data-question=\"21\">losing their usefulness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ANTIBIOTICS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"715\" id=\"question-wrapper-715\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db828534-755f-4dea-b62d-033ecb1d5d35\" data-question=\"22\">Disease-causing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> ………………………………. are most likely to be found in hot, damp regions. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MOSQUITO(E)S</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"716\" id=\"question-wrapper-716\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One cause of pollution is ……………………………… that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f1f4443-0654-4a27-ab21-049c9b71a2d9\" data-question=\"23\">burn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> a particular <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53dd766d-104f-40fa-b48f-220c9a4ffbe7\" data-question=\"23\">fuel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FACTORIES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"717\" id=\"question-wrapper-717\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4ed2a6d-b5a9-46a4-af4c-24a09a4b2561\" data-question=\"24\">growth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of cities often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e7d247dc-90ad-43f4-92fa-80337f6b0ef7\" data-question=\"24\">has an impact on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> nearby …………………………….. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FORESTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"718\" id=\"question-wrapper-718\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> …………………………… is one disease that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3bd7155c-017d-401c-8db2-cdf2619bfaed\" data-question=\"25\">is growing after having been eradicated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POLIO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"719\" id=\"question-wrapper-719\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A physical barrier such as a ………………………………. Can prevent people from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15003f77-3738-4e12-aefc-aa965375bc1a\" data-question=\"26\">reaching a hospital<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MOUNTAIN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c13a1690-f5c3-4aff-b0b2-b1782c91d7c2","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"have disappeared","passagePhrase":"have been eradicated"},{"uid":"b02ecb24-1b41-4a8c-a449-7bf02b39fa3a","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"losing their usefulness","passagePhrase":"resistant to"},{"uid":"db828534-755f-4dea-b62d-033ecb1d5d35","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Disease-causing","passagePhrase":"malaria-prone"},{"uid":"67922261-4248-4eb5-9369-a758a65c3339","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"rare","passagePhrase":"less"},{"uid":"ae7bdc26-c936-4f7c-ba35-ef6d73059d87","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"physical conditions","passagePhrase":"asthma, lung problems, eyesight issues"},{"uid":"5f1f4443-0654-4a27-ab21-049c9b71a2d9","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"burn","passagePhrase":"run on"},{"uid":"53dd766d-104f-40fa-b48f-220c9a4ffbe7","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"fuel","passagePhrase":"coal power"},{"uid":"e7d247dc-90ad-43f4-92fa-80337f6b0ef7","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"has an impact on","passagePhrase":"has also led to"},{"uid":"b4ed2a6d-b5a9-46a4-af4c-24a09a4b2561","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"growth","passagePhrase":"expansion"},{"uid":"b7af98aa-8b20-4789-a692-e9d157448a19","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"not all diseases can be totally eliminated","passagePhrase":"are re-emerging"},{"uid":"3bd7155c-017d-401c-8db2-cdf2619bfaed","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"is growing after having been eradicated","passagePhrase":"are re-emerging"},{"uid":"622e0552-f54e-498c-a728-cb46208ea8f3","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"mixture","passagePhrase":"combination"},{"uid":"d8c07dfa-2a9b-4413-bcfa-d90cb1fc31e5","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"classifying","passagePhrase":"categorizing"},{"uid":"e8964e03-8c88-4285-88ef-eb7907da740a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"the level of access to healthcare can vary","passagePhrase":"a very large discrepancy between the options available to people"},{"uid":"15003f77-3738-4e12-aefc-aa965375bc1a","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"reaching a hospital","passagePhrase":"get medical attention"}]},"reading_u2_219":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>Music and the emotions</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>Neuroscientist Jonah Lehrer considers the emotional power of music</em></span></p><p><span>Why does music make us feel? One the one hand, music is a purely abstract art form, devoid of language or explicit ideas. And yet, even though music says little, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78a0cb35-9adf-45aa-8ac7-9a88ba59f5cc\" data-question=\"32\">it still manages to touch us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"620d0ab6-121f-44f1-afa8-0f144bbf199c\" data-question=\"32\">deeply<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. When listening to our favourite songs, our body betrays all the symptoms of emotional arousal. The pupils in our eyes dilate, our pulse and blood pressure rise, the electrical conductance of our skin is lowered, and the cerebellum, a brain region associated with bodily movement, becomes strangely active. Blood is even re-directed to the muscles in our legs. In other words, sound stirs us at our biological roots.</span></p><p><span>A recent paper in <em>Nature Neuroscience </em>by a research team in Montreal, Canada, marks an important step in revealing the precise underpinnings of the potent pleasurable stimulus’ that is music. Although the study involves plenty of fancy technology, including functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI) and ligand-based positron emission tomography (PET) scanning, the experiment itself was rather straightforward. After screening 217 individuals who responded to advertisements requesting people who experience ‘chills’ to instrumental music, the scientists narrowed down the subject pool to ten. They then asked the subjects to bring in their playlist of favourite songs – virtually every genre was represented, from techno to tango – and played them the music while their brain activity was monitored. Because the scientists were combining methodologies (PET and fMRI), they were able to obtain an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ab845e0-1ab3-4c33-8d9f-7add68245777\" data-question=\"33\">impressively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da044bb6-7889-49fb-9e43-78a9240b0901\" data-question=\"33\">exact and detailed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> portrait of music in the brain. The first thing they discovered is that music <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4e608b7-692f-4045-8d33-609f914884cc\" data-question=\"27\">triggers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40f53e20-c804-4afe-a82f-a76aeb7893a4\" data-question=\"27\">the production of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> dopamine – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"94314dda-d691-4eff-afd8-38a995a8017e\" data-question=\"27\">a chemical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> with a key role in setting people’s moods – by the neurons (nerve cells) in both the dorsal and ventral regions of the brain. As these two regions <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8f6dc04-e108-44cd-adf0-26bdb61fdfa6\" data-question=\"28\">have long been linked with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e719d797-68dd-449f-bfb5-de61ddfdfb06\" data-question=\"28\">experience of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> pleasure, this finding isn’t particularly surprising.</span></p><p><span>What is rather more significant is the finding that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c5f1f854-e3b8-4977-a980-1b0559ff1986\" data-question=\"34\">the dopamine neurons in the caudate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> – a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4d9e08b-ee76-4ba7-87d0-01f930ad108f\" data-question=\"29\">region of the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> involved in learning stimulus-response associations, and in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"adfcbf50-0978-4f30-90aa-cf9aa7ddc4bd\" data-question=\"31\">anticipating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> food and other ‘reward’ stimuli – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f65e238c-9930-438e-97c6-b2f655becebf\" data-question=\"29\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a985e71-9b86-4671-b721-fe659978d22f\" data-question=\"37\">were at their most active<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e79b7f67-336c-473e-a3fb-1a781e39bffc\" data-question=\"34\">around 15 seconds before<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the participants’ favourite moments in the music. The researchers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fffafa39-df7c-434c-aba2-830faea6e353\" data-question=\"30\">call this<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> the ‘anticipatory phase’ and argue that the purpose of this activity is to help us predict the arrival of our favourite part. The question, of course, is what all these dopamine neurons are up to. Why are they so active in the period <em>preceding </em>the acoustic climax? After all, we typically associate surges of dopamine with pleasure, with the processing of <em>actual </em>rewards. And yet, this cluster of cells is most active when the ‘chills’ have yet to arrive, when the melodic pattern is still unresolved.</span></p><p><span>One way to answer the question is to look at the music and not the neurons. While music can often seem (at least to the outsider) like a labyrinth of intricate patterns, it turns out that the most important part of every song or symphony is when the patterns break down, when the sound becomes unpredictable. If the music is too obvious, it is annoyingly boring, like an alarm clock. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce615d8e-373b-4c69-af15-65dcfe101d61\" data-question=\"38\">Numerous studies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, after all, have demonstrated that dopamine neurons quickly adapt to predictable rewards. If we know what’s going to happen next, then we don’t get excited. This is why composers often introduce a key note in the beginning of a song, spend most of the rest of the piece in the studious avoidance of the pattern, and then finally repeat it only at the end. The longer we are denied the pattern we expect, the greater the emotional release when the pattern returns, safe and sound.</span></p><p><span>To <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac4ae684-6fb7-4c65-a6ad-679052c0d81b\" data-question=\"35\">demonstrate this psychological principle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, the musicologist Leonard Meyer, in his classic book <em>Emotion and Meaning in Music </em>(1956), analysed the 5th movement of Beethoven’s String Quartet in C-sharp minor, Op. 131. Meyer wanted to show how music is defined by its flirtation with – but not submission to – our expectations of order. Meyer dissected 50 measures (bars) of the masterpiece, showing how Beethoven begins with the clear statement of a rhythmic and harmonic pattern and then, in an ingenious tonal dance, carefully holds off repeating it. What Beethoven does instead is suggest variations of the pattern. He wants to preserve an element of uncertainty in his music, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13f6d148-e390-478b-bde7-3db5b04b25f8\" data-question=\"39\">making our brains beg for the one chord he refuses to give us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Beethoven saves that chord for the end.</span></p><p><span>According to Meyer, it is the suspenseful tension of music, arising out of our unfulfilled expectations, that is the source of the music’s feeling. While earlier theories of music focused on the way a sound can refer to the real world of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f2c64d1-41b2-40ef-a6de-e7e808a0e3ad\" data-question=\"40\">images and experiences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> – its ‘connotative’ meaning – Meyer argued that the emotions we find in music come from the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ffd87315-9402-48df-9270-fefc64bcfffd\" data-question=\"36\">unfolding events<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of the music itself. This ‘embodied meaning’ arises from the patterns the symphony invokes and then ignores. It is this uncertainty that triggers the surge of dopamine in the caudate, as we struggle to figure out what will happen next. We can predict some of the notes, but we can’t predict them all, and that is what keeps us listening, waiting expectantly for our reward, for the pattern to be completed.</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>The Montreal Study</strong></span></h3><p><span>Participants, who were recruited for the study through advertisements, had their brain activity monitored while listening to their favourite music. It was noted that the music <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4e608b7-692f-4045-8d33-609f914884cc\" data-question=\"27\">stimulated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the brain’s neurons to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40f53e20-c804-4afe-a82f-a76aeb7893a4\" data-question=\"27\">release<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"94314dda-d691-4eff-afd8-38a995a8017e\" data-question=\"27\">a substance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> called <strong>27</strong>…………………………. in two of the parts of the brain which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8f6dc04-e108-44cd-adf0-26bdb61fdfa6\" data-question=\"28\">are associated with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e719d797-68dd-449f-bfb5-de61ddfdfb06\" data-question=\"28\">feeling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <strong>28</strong>…………………………..</span></p><p><span>Researchers also observed that the neurons in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4d9e08b-ee76-4ba7-87d0-01f930ad108f\" data-question=\"29\">area of the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> called the <strong>29</strong>……………………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f65e238c-9930-438e-97c6-b2f655becebf\" data-question=\"29\">were particularly active<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> just before the participants’ favourite moments in the music – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fffafa39-df7c-434c-aba2-830faea6e353\" data-question=\"30\">the period known as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> the <strong>30</strong>…………………………. Activity in this part of the brain is associated with the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"adfcbf50-0978-4f30-90aa-cf9aa7ddc4bd\" data-question=\"31\">expectation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of ‘reward’ stimuli such as <strong>31</strong>………………………….</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"720\" id=\"question-wrapper-720\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DOPAMINE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"721\" id=\"question-wrapper-721\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PLEASURE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"722\" id=\"question-wrapper-722\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CAUDATE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"723\" id=\"question-wrapper-723\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ANTICIPATORY PHASE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"724\" id=\"question-wrapper-724\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOOD</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>32-36</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"725\" id=\"question-wrapper-725\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does the writer emphasise in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. how dramatically our reactions to music can vary</li> <li>B. how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"620d0ab6-121f-44f1-afa8-0f144bbf199c\" data-question=\"32\">intense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78a0cb35-9adf-45aa-8ac7-9a88ba59f5cc\" data-question=\"32\">physical responses to music<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> can be</li> <li>C. how little we know about the way that music affects us</li> <li>D. how much music can tell us about how our brains operate</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"726\" id=\"question-wrapper-726\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> what view of the Montreal study does the writer express in the second paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Its aims were innovative.</li> <li>B. The approach was too simplistic.</li> <li>C. It produced some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ab845e0-1ab3-4c33-8d9f-7add68245777\" data-question=\"33\">remarkably<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> precise data.</li> <li>D. The technology used was unnecessarily complex.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"727\" id=\"question-wrapper-727\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer find interesting about the results of the Montreal study? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e79b7f67-336c-473e-a3fb-1a781e39bffc\" data-question=\"34\">the timing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> of participants’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c5f1f854-e3b8-4977-a980-1b0559ff1986\" data-question=\"34\">neural responses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> to the music</li> <li>B. the impact of the music of participants’ emotional state</li> <li>C. the section of participants’ brains which was activated by the music</li> <li>D. the type of music which had the strongest effect on participants’ brains</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"728\" id=\"question-wrapper-728\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Why does the writer refer to Meyer’s work on music and emotion? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. to propose an original theory about the subject</li> <li>B. to offer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac4ae684-6fb7-4c65-a6ad-679052c0d81b\" data-question=\"35\">support for the findings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of the Montreal study</li> <li>C. to recommend the need for further research into the subject</li> <li>D. to present a view which opposes that of the Montreal researchers</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"729\" id=\"question-wrapper-729\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to Leonard Meyer, what causes the listener’s emotional response to music? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the way that the music evokes poignant memories in the listener</li> <li>B. the association of certain musical chords with certain feelings</li> <li>C. the listener’s sympathy with the composer’s intentions</li> <li>D. the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ffd87315-9402-48df-9270-fefc64bcfffd\" data-question=\"36\">internal structure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of the musical composition</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, <strong>A-F</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>37-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A </strong> our response to music depends on our initial emotional state.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> neuron activity decreases if outcomes become predictable.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> emotive music can bring to mind actual <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f2c64d1-41b2-40ef-a6de-e7e808a0e3ad\" data-question=\"40\">pictures and events<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> experiences in our past can influence our emotional reaction to music.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> emotive music <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13f6d148-e390-478b-bde7-3db5b04b25f8\" data-question=\"39\">delays giving listeners what they expect to hear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong> neuron activity <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a985e71-9b86-4671-b721-fe659978d22f\" data-question=\"37\">increases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de0d6aed-e6c5-4ddb-a2c7-124f6b2beaf1\" data-question=\"37\">prior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"66693bef-3598-4f6a-9d0d-e6b5428a3f52\" data-question=\"37\">key points<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in a musical piece.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"730\" id=\"question-wrapper-730\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Montreal researchers discovered that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"731\" id=\"question-wrapper-731\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce615d8e-373b-4c69-af15-65dcfe101d61\" data-question=\"38\">Many studies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> have demonstrated that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"732\" id=\"question-wrapper-732\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Meyer’s analysis of Beethoven’s music shows that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"733\" id=\"question-wrapper-733\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Earlier theories of music suggested that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"78a0cb35-9adf-45aa-8ac7-9a88ba59f5cc","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"physical responses to music","passagePhrase":"it still manages to touch us"},{"uid":"620d0ab6-121f-44f1-afa8-0f144bbf199c","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"intense","passagePhrase":"deeply"},{"uid":"3ab845e0-1ab3-4c33-8d9f-7add68245777","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"remarkably","passagePhrase":"impressively"},{"uid":"da044bb6-7889-49fb-9e43-78a9240b0901","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"exact and detailed"},{"uid":"b4e608b7-692f-4045-8d33-609f914884cc","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"stimulated","passagePhrase":"triggers"},{"uid":"40f53e20-c804-4afe-a82f-a76aeb7893a4","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"release","passagePhrase":"the production of"},{"uid":"94314dda-d691-4eff-afd8-38a995a8017e","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"a substance","passagePhrase":"a chemical"},{"uid":"c8f6dc04-e108-44cd-adf0-26bdb61fdfa6","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"are associated with","passagePhrase":"have long been linked with"},{"uid":"e719d797-68dd-449f-bfb5-de61ddfdfb06","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"feeling","passagePhrase":"experience of"},{"uid":"c5f1f854-e3b8-4977-a980-1b0559ff1986","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"neural responses","passagePhrase":"the dopamine neurons in the caudate"},{"uid":"e4d9e08b-ee76-4ba7-87d0-01f930ad108f","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"area of the brain","passagePhrase":"region of the brain"},{"uid":"adfcbf50-0978-4f30-90aa-cf9aa7ddc4bd","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"expectation","passagePhrase":"anticipating"},{"uid":"f65e238c-9930-438e-97c6-b2f655becebf","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"were particularly active","passagePhrase":"were at their most active"},{"uid":"0a985e71-9b86-4671-b721-fe659978d22f","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"increases","passagePhrase":"were at their most active"},{"uid":"e79b7f67-336c-473e-a3fb-1a781e39bffc","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"the timing","passagePhrase":"around 15 seconds before"},{"uid":"fffafa39-df7c-434c-aba2-830faea6e353","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"the period known as","passagePhrase":"call this"},{"uid":"ce615d8e-373b-4c69-af15-65dcfe101d61","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"Many studies","passagePhrase":"Numerous studies"},{"uid":"ac4ae684-6fb7-4c65-a6ad-679052c0d81b","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"support for the findings","passagePhrase":"demonstrate this psychological principle"},{"uid":"13f6d148-e390-478b-bde7-3db5b04b25f8","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"delays giving listeners what they expect to hear","passagePhrase":"making our brains beg for the one chord he refuses to give us"},{"uid":"7f2c64d1-41b2-40ef-a6de-e7e808a0e3ad","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"pictures and events","passagePhrase":"images and experiences"},{"uid":"ffd87315-9402-48df-9270-fefc64bcfffd","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"internal structure","passagePhrase":"unfolding events"},{"uid":"de0d6aed-e6c5-4ddb-a2c7-124f6b2beaf1","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"prior","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"66693bef-3598-4f6a-9d0d-e6b5428a3f52","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"key points","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_220":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong><span>The History of Glass</span></strong></span></h2><p><span>From our earliest origins, man has been making use of glass. Historians have discovered that a type of natural glass – obsidian – formed in places such as the mouth of a volcano as a result of the intense heat of an eruption melting sand – was first used as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be591d75-4c60-4f4a-b3f4-9c045023ebe9\" data-question=\"1\">tips<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> for spears. Archaeologists have even found evidence of man-made glass which dates back to 4000 BC; this took the form of glazes used for coating stone beads. It was not until 1500 BC, however, that the first hollow glass container was made by covering a sand core with a layer of molten glass.</span></p><p><span>Glass blowing became the most common way to make glass containers from the first century BC. The glass made during this time was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d333377d-5e2b-4ac0-8f59-ced923714ba5\" data-question=\"4\">highly coloured due to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the impurities of the raw material. In the first century AD, methods of creating colourless glass were developed, which was then tinted by the addition of colouring materials. The secret of glass making was taken across Europe by the Romans during this century. However, they guarded the skills and technology required to make glass very closely, and it was not until their empire collapsed in 476 AD that glass-making knowledge became widespread throughout Europe and the Middle East. From the 10th century onwards, the Venetians gained a reputation for technical skill and artistic ability in the making of glass bottles, and many of the city’s craftsmen left Italy to set up glassworks throughout Europe.</span></p><p><span>A major milestone in the history of glass occurred with the invention of lead crystal glass by the English glass manufacturer George Ravenscroft (1632-1683). He attempted to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5bd37332-84e7-4c1f-906a-c9912ac7b33c\" data-question=\"7\">counter the effect of clouding that sometimes occurred in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> blown glass by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1bf71991-78ec-4a3c-8a26-a17ed02b9cb7\" data-question=\"6\">introducing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> lead to the raw materials used in the process. The new glass he created was softer and easier to decorate, and had a higher refractive index, adding to its brilliance and beauty, and it proved invaluable to the optical industry. It is thanks to Ravenscroft’s invention that optical lenses, astronomical telescopes, microscopes and the like became possible.</span></p><p><span>In Britain, the modern glass industry only really started to develop <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a6e3e8d-5186-41c8-a7ff-dda3a970faaa\" data-question=\"8\">after the repeal of the Excise Act<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in 1845. Before that time, heavy taxes had been placed on the amount of glass melted in a glasshouse, and were levied continuously from 1745 to 1845. Joseph Paxton’s Crystal Palace at London’s Great Exhibition of 1851 marked the beginning of glass as a material used in the building industry. This revolutionary new building encouraged the use of glass in public, domestic and horticultural architecture. Glass manufacturing techniques also improved with the advancement of science and the development of better technology.</span></p><p><span>From 1887 onwards, glass making developed from traditional mouth-blowing to a semi-automatic process, after factory-owner HM Ashley introduced a machine capable of producing 200 bottles per hour in Castleford, Yorkshire, England – more than three times <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89184f3e-0cb4-4f59-9f08-6c3183b3f88a\" data-question=\"9\">quicker than any<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> previous production method. Then in 1907, the first fully automated machine was developed in the USA by Michael Owens – <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c829c265-3afa-4bd3-9f22-8cd7d93d54ed\" data-question=\"10\">founder of the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> Owens Bottle Machine Company (later the major manufacturers Owens-Illinois) – and installed in its factory. Owens’ invention could produce an impressive 2,500 bottles per hour. Other developments followed rapidly, but it was not until the First World War, when Britain became out off from essential glass suppliers, that glass became part of the scientific sector. Previous to this, glass had been as a craft rather than a precise science.</span></p><p><span>Today, glass making is big business. It has become a modern, hi-tech industry operating in a fiercely competitive global market where quality, design and service levels are critical to maintaining market share. Modern glass plants are capable of making millions of glass containers a day in many different colours, with green, brown and clear remaining the most popular. Few of us can imagine modern life without glass. It features in almost every aspect of our lives – in our homes, our cars and whenever we sit down to eat or drink. Glass packaging is used for many products, many beverages are sold in glass, as are numerous foodstuffs, as well as medicines and cosmetics.</span></p><p><span>Glass is an ideal material for recycling, and with growing consumer concern for green issues, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de18b628-bf6b-42e1-be72-1f849c7e8dc1\" data-question=\"12\">glass bottles and jars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> are becoming ever more popular. Glass recycling is good news for the environment. It saves used glass containers being sent to landfill. As less energy is needed to melt recycled glass than to melt down raw materials, this also <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ac989692-f2cf-48c8-b2b2-e9aa876f5af7\" data-question=\"13\">saves fuel and production costs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. Recycling also reduces the need for raw materials to be quarried, thus saving precious resources.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>1-8</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>The History of Glass</strong></span></h3><p><span><span>•</span> Early humans used a material called <strong>1</strong>……………………….. to make the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be591d75-4c60-4f4a-b3f4-9c045023ebe9\" data-question=\"1\">sharp points<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of their <strong>2</strong>…………………….</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> 4000 BC: <strong>3</strong>………………………… made of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4876ab53-00b0-4fe7-941c-37541d4093fa\" data-question=\"3\">stone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> were covered in a coating of man-made glass.</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> First century BC: glass <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d333377d-5e2b-4ac0-8f59-ced923714ba5\" data-question=\"4\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c1fb2a3-2050-47a9-92ea-c25bc4956c5f\" data-question=\"5\">was coloured because of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the <strong>4</strong>………………………. in the material.</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> Until 476 AD: Only the <strong>5</strong>………………………… knew <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c1fb2a3-2050-47a9-92ea-c25bc4956c5f\" data-question=\"5\">how to make glass<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> From 10th century: Venetians became famous for making bottles out of glass.</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> 17th century: George Ravenscroft <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1bf71991-78ec-4a3c-8a26-a17ed02b9cb7\" data-question=\"6\">developed a process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> using <strong>6</strong>……………………….. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5bd37332-84e7-4c1f-906a-c9912ac7b33c\" data-question=\"7\">avoid the occurrence of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <strong>7</strong>………………………. in blown glass.</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> Mid-19th century: British glass production developed after <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a6e3e8d-5186-41c8-a7ff-dda3a970faaa\" data-question=\"8\">changes to laws<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> concerning <strong>8</strong>……………………..</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"734\" id=\"question-wrapper-734\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OBSIDIAN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"735\" id=\"question-wrapper-735\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPEARS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"736\" id=\"question-wrapper-736\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BEADS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"737\" id=\"question-wrapper-737\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IMPURITIES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"738\" id=\"question-wrapper-738\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ROMANS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"739\" id=\"question-wrapper-739\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LEAD</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"740\" id=\"question-wrapper-740\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CLOUDING</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"741\" id=\"question-wrapper-741\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TAXES</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>In boxes <strong>9-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"742\" id=\"question-wrapper-742\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In 1887, HM Ashley had the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89184f3e-0cb4-4f59-9f08-6c3183b3f88a\" data-question=\"9\">fastest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> bottle-producing machine that existed at the time. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"743\" id=\"question-wrapper-743\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Michael Owens <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c829c265-3afa-4bd3-9f22-8cd7d93d54ed\" data-question=\"10\">was hired<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> by a large US company to design a fully-automated bottle manufacturing machine for them. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"744\" id=\"question-wrapper-744\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Nowadays, most glass is produced by large international manufacturers. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"745\" id=\"question-wrapper-745\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Concern for the environment is leading to an increased demand for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de18b628-bf6b-42e1-be72-1f849c7e8dc1\" data-question=\"12\">glass containers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"746\" id=\"question-wrapper-746\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ac989692-f2cf-48c8-b2b2-e9aa876f5af7\" data-question=\"13\">more expensive to produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> recycled glass than to manufacture new glass. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"be591d75-4c60-4f4a-b3f4-9c045023ebe9","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"sharp points","passagePhrase":"tips"},{"uid":"d333377d-5e2b-4ac0-8f59-ced923714ba5","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"was coloured because of","passagePhrase":"highly coloured due to"},{"uid":"5bd37332-84e7-4c1f-906a-c9912ac7b33c","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"avoid the occurrence of","passagePhrase":"counter the effect of clouding that sometimes occurred in"},{"uid":"1bf71991-78ec-4a3c-8a26-a17ed02b9cb7","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"developed a process","passagePhrase":"introducing"},{"uid":"3a6e3e8d-5186-41c8-a7ff-dda3a970faaa","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"changes to laws","passagePhrase":"after the repeal of the Excise Act"},{"uid":"89184f3e-0cb4-4f59-9f08-6c3183b3f88a","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"fastest","passagePhrase":"quicker than any"},{"uid":"de18b628-bf6b-42e1-be72-1f849c7e8dc1","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"glass containers","passagePhrase":"glass bottles and jars"},{"uid":"4876ab53-00b0-4fe7-941c-37541d4093fa","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"stone","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"5c1fb2a3-2050-47a9-92ea-c25bc4956c5f","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"was coloured because of ... how to make glass","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_221":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Bring back the big cats</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>It’s time to start returning vanished native animals to Britain, says John Vesty</em></span></p><p><span>There is a poem, written around 598 AD, which describes hunting a mystery animal called a <em>llewyn. </em>But what was it? Nothing seemed to fit, until 2006, when an animal bone, dating from around the same period, was found in the Kinsey Cave in northern England. Until this discovery, the lynx – a large spotted cat with tasselled ears – was presumed to have died out in Britain at least 6,000 years ago, before the inhabitants of these islands took up farming. But the 2006 find, together with three others in Yorkshire and Scotland, is compelling evidence that the lynx and the mysterious <em>llewyn</em> were in fact one and the same animal. If this is so, it would bring forward the tassel-eared cat’s estimated extinction date by roughly 5,000 years.</span></p><p><span>However, this is not quite the last glimpse of the animal in British culture. A 9th-century stone cross from the Isle of Eigg shows, alongside the deer, boar and aurochs pursued by a mounted hunter, a speckled cat with tasselled ears. Were it not for the animal’s backside having worn away with time, we could have been certain, as the lynx’s stubby tail is unmistakable. But even without this key feature, it’s hard to see what else the creature could have been. The lynx is now becoming the totemic animal of a movement that is transforming British environmentalism: rewilding.</span></p><p><span>Rewilding means the mass restoration of damaged ecosystems. It involves letting trees return to places that have been denuded, allowing parts of the seabed to recover from trawling and dredging, permitting rivers to flow freely again. Above all, it means bringing back missing species. One of the most striking findings of modern ecology is that ecosystems without large predators behave in completely different ways from those that retain them. Some of them drive dynamic processes that resonate through the whole food chain, creating niches for hundreds of species that might otherwise struggle to survive. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fc2725c8-4956-4532-8b25-271bb39893e2\" data-question=\"15\">killers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> turn out to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3bc079d1-9959-4637-970b-324af0842fb8\" data-question=\"15\">bringers of life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Such findings present a big challenge to British conservation, which has often selected <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"776f5184-d5f8-452f-a4ba-7965853b059b\" data-question=\"16\">arbitrary assemblages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of plants and animals and sought, at great effort and expense, to prevent them from changing. It has tried to preserve the living world as if it were a jar of pickles, letting nothing in and nothing out, keeping nature in a state of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"776f5184-d5f8-452f-a4ba-7965853b059b\" data-question=\"16\">arrested development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. But ecosystems are not merely collections of species; they are also the dynamic and ever-shifting relationships between them. And this dynamism often depends on large predators.</span></p><p><span>At sea the potential is even greater: by protecting large areas from commercial fishing, we could once more see what 18th-century literature describes: vast shoals of fish being chased by fin and sperm whales, within sight of the English shore. This policy would also greatly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"263658af-fe99-4b06-a44e-4b0896b317fe\" data-question=\"17\">boost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> catches in the surrounding seas; the fishing industry’s insistence on scouring every inch of seabed, leaving no breeding reserves, could not be more damaging to its own interests.</span></p><p><span>Rewilding is a rare example of an environmental movement in which campaigners articulate what they are for rather than only what they are against. One of the reasons why the enthusiasm for rewilding is spreading so quickly in Britain is that it helps to create a more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5a97236-781a-4008-b3d7-b9dc4e6a0fff\" data-question=\"18\">inspiring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> vision than the green movement’s usual promise of ‘Follow us and the world will be slightly less awful than it would otherwise have been.’</span></p><p><span>The lynx presents no threat to human beings: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1eab78e0-4a66-4872-834b-781223bd735d\" data-question=\"19\">there is no known instance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of one <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"738751e3-6ef7-4b8f-8964-f9da971417de\" data-question=\"19\">preying on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> people. It is a specialist predator of roe deer, a species that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f789dde1-4bcb-48b0-b902-904cca93374d\" data-question=\"20\">has exploded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in Britain in recent decades, holding back, by intensive browsing, attempts to re-establish forests. It will also winkle out sika deer: an exotic species that is almost impossible for human beings to control, as it hides in impenetrable plantations of young trees. The attempt to reintroduce this predator marries well with the aim of bringing forests back to parts of our bare and barren uplands. The lynx requires deep cover, and as such presents <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d4f752e-f2a7-47bf-9231-169ac7c28ff6\" data-question=\"21\">little risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> to sheep and other livestock, which are supposed, as a condition of farm subsidies, to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a39347b0-3bd9-41c3-b524-795316d383fc\" data-question=\"21\">kept out of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> the woods.</span></p><p><span>On a recent trip to the Cairngorm Mountains, I heard several conservationists suggest that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fef608d2-65af-4616-8e13-9bb1259de5dd\" data-question=\"22\">the lynx could be reintroduced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> there within 20 years. If <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf8ada88-bee2-423d-9454-b3b331545143\" data-question=\"22\">trees return to the bare hills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> elsewhere in Britain, the big cats could soon follow. There is nothing extraordinary about these proposals, seen from the perspective of anywhere else in Europe. The lynx has now been reintroduced to the Jura Mountains, the Alps, the Vosges in <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9572cba6-51ec-4c53-8aca-c1355001d3b9\" data-question=\"23\">eastern France and the Harz mountains in Germany<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, and has re-established itself in many more places. The European population has tripled since 1970 to roughly 10,000. As with wolves, bears, beavers, boar, bison, moose and many other species, the lynx <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"240bcc91-679b-4cd0-959e-6b9cbc57af25\" data-question=\"25\">has been able to spread<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> as farming has left the hills and people discover that it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b11799bf-0458-4faf-ae9b-b17134344ceb\" data-question=\"26\">more lucrative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> to protect charismatic wildlife than to hunt it, as tourists will pay for the chance to see it. Large-scale rewilding is happening almost everywhere – except Britain.</span></p><p><span>Here, attitudes are just beginning to change. Conservationists are starting to accept that the old preservation-jar model is failing, even on its own terms. Already, projects such as Trees for Life in the Highlands provide a hint of what might be coming. An organisation is being set up that will seek to catalyse the rewilding of land and sea across Britain, its aim being to reintroduce that rarest of species to British ecosystems: hope.</span></p><p><span> </span><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span>Write the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-18</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"747\" id=\"question-wrapper-747\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What did the 2006 discovery of the animal bone reveal about the lynx? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Its physical appearance was very distinctive.</li> <li>B. Its extinction was linked to the spread of farming.</li> <li>C. It vanished from Britain several thousand years ago.</li> <li>D. It survived in Britain longer than was previously thought.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"748\" id=\"question-wrapper-748\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does the writer make about large <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fc2725c8-4956-4532-8b25-271bb39893e2\" data-question=\"15\">predators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in the third paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Their presence can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3bc079d1-9959-4637-970b-324af0842fb8\" data-question=\"15\">increase biodiversity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</li> <li>B. They may cause damage to local ecosystems.</li> <li>C. Their behaviour can alter according to the environment.</li> <li>D. They should be reintroduced only to areas where they were native.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"749\" id=\"question-wrapper-749\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer suggest about British conservation in the fourth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It has failed to achieve its aims.</li> <li>B. It is beginning to change direction.</li> <li>C. It has taken a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"776f5184-d5f8-452f-a4ba-7965853b059b\" data-question=\"16\">misguided approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</li> <li>D. It has focused on the most widespread species.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"750\" id=\"question-wrapper-750\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Protecting large areas of the sea from commercial fishing would result in </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. practical <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"263658af-fe99-4b06-a44e-4b0896b317fe\" data-question=\"17\">benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> for the fishing industry.</li> <li>B. some short-term losses to the fishing industry.</li> <li>C. widespread opposition from the fishing industry.</li> <li>D. certain changes to techniques within the fishing industry.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"751\" id=\"question-wrapper-751\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the author, what distinguishes rewilding from other environmental campaigns? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Its objective is more achievable.</li> <li>B. Its supporters are more articulate.</li> <li>C. Its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5a97236-781a-4008-b3d7-b9dc4e6a0fff\" data-question=\"18\">positive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> message is more appealing.</li> <li>D. It is based on sounder scientific principles.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words and phrases <strong>A-F</strong> below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>19-22</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p><h3><span><strong>Reintroducing the lynx to Britain</strong></span></h3><p><span>There would be many advantages to reintroducing the lynx to Britain. While <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1eab78e0-4a66-4872-834b-781223bd735d\" data-question=\"19\">there is no evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> that the lynx <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"738751e3-6ef7-4b8f-8964-f9da971417de\" data-question=\"19\">has ever put<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <strong>19</strong> …………………….. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"738751e3-6ef7-4b8f-8964-f9da971417de\" data-question=\"19\">in danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, it would reduce the numbers of certain <strong>20</strong>…………………….. whose populations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f789dde1-4bcb-48b0-b902-904cca93374d\" data-question=\"20\">have increased enormously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in recent decades. It would present only a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d4f752e-f2a7-47bf-9231-169ac7c28ff6\" data-question=\"21\">minimal threat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> to <strong>21</strong>…………………….., provided these were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a39347b0-3bd9-41c3-b524-795316d383fc\" data-question=\"21\">kept away from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> lynx habitats. Furthermore, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fef608d2-65af-4616-8e13-9bb1259de5dd\" data-question=\"22\">the reintroduction programme<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> would also link efficiently with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf8ada88-bee2-423d-9454-b3b331545143\" data-question=\"22\">initiatives to return native<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <strong>22</strong>……………………… to certain areas of the country.</span></p><table><tbody><tr><td width=\"162\"><p><span><strong>A</strong> trees</span></p></td><td width=\"204\"><p><span><strong>B</strong> endangered species</span></p></td><td width=\"168\"><p><span><strong>C</strong> hillsides</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"162\"><p><span><strong>D</strong> wild animals</span></p></td><td width=\"204\"><p><span><strong>E</strong> humans</span></p></td><td width=\"168\"><p><span><strong>F</strong> farm animals</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"752\" id=\"question-wrapper-752\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"753\" id=\"question-wrapper-753\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"754\" id=\"question-wrapper-754\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"755\" id=\"question-wrapper-755\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>23-26</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span><span> </span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"756\" id=\"question-wrapper-756\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9572cba6-51ec-4c53-8aca-c1355001d3b9\" data-question=\"23\">Britain could become the first<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> European country to reintroduce the lynx. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"757\" id=\"question-wrapper-757\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The large growth in the European lynx population since 1970 has exceeded conservationists’ expectations. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"758\" id=\"question-wrapper-758\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Changes in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe2060f4-a13f-4690-bdca-51b749605134\" data-question=\"25\">agricultural practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"240bcc91-679b-4cd0-959e-6b9cbc57af25\" data-question=\"25\">have extended<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> the habitat of the lynx in Europe. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"759\" id=\"question-wrapper-759\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It has become apparent that species reintroduction has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b11799bf-0458-4faf-ae9b-b17134344ceb\" data-question=\"26\">commercial advantages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"fc2725c8-4956-4532-8b25-271bb39893e2","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"predators","passagePhrase":"killers"},{"uid":"3bc079d1-9959-4637-970b-324af0842fb8","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"increase biodiversity","passagePhrase":"bringers of life"},{"uid":"776f5184-d5f8-452f-a4ba-7965853b059b","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"misguided approach","passagePhrase":"arbitrary assemblages ... arrested development"},{"uid":"263658af-fe99-4b06-a44e-4b0896b317fe","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"benefits","passagePhrase":"boost"},{"uid":"a5a97236-781a-4008-b3d7-b9dc4e6a0fff","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"positive","passagePhrase":"inspiring"},{"uid":"1eab78e0-4a66-4872-834b-781223bd735d","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"there is no evidence","passagePhrase":"there is no known instance"},{"uid":"738751e3-6ef7-4b8f-8964-f9da971417de","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"has ever put ... in danger","passagePhrase":"preying on"},{"uid":"f789dde1-4bcb-48b0-b902-904cca93374d","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"have increased enormously","passagePhrase":"has exploded"},{"uid":"6d4f752e-f2a7-47bf-9231-169ac7c28ff6","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"minimal threat","passagePhrase":"little risk"},{"uid":"a39347b0-3bd9-41c3-b524-795316d383fc","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"kept away from","passagePhrase":"kept out of"},{"uid":"fef608d2-65af-4616-8e13-9bb1259de5dd","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"the reintroduction programme","passagePhrase":"the lynx could be reintroduced"},{"uid":"cf8ada88-bee2-423d-9454-b3b331545143","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"initiatives to return native","passagePhrase":"trees return to the bare hills"},{"uid":"240bcc91-679b-4cd0-959e-6b9cbc57af25","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"have extended","passagePhrase":"has been able to spread"},{"uid":"b11799bf-0458-4faf-ae9b-b17134344ceb","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"commercial advantages","passagePhrase":"more lucrative"},{"uid":"fe2060f4-a13f-4690-bdca-51b749605134","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"agricultural practices","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_222":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions 27-40</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>UK companies need more effective boards of directors</strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>After a number of serious failures of governance (that is, how they are managed at the highest level), companies in Britain, as well as elsewhere, should consider radical changes to their directors’ roles. It is clear that the role of a board director today is not an easy one. Following the 2008 financial meltdown, which resulted in a deeper and more prolonged period of economic downturn than anyone expected, the search for explanations in the many post-mortems of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ed27279-a00c-480f-ac2a-2e1fe468e5fb\" data-question=\"34\">the crisis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> has meant blame has been spread far and wide. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ad8d48d4-bbbc-415d-be57-2f178920ca24\" data-question=\"27\">Governments, regulators, central banks and auditors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"abad2d6c-441a-4393-b8b3-6c5d26be4d86\" data-question=\"27\">have all been in the frame<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. The role of bank directors and management and their widely publicised failures <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d25462b4-739c-40d4-acb8-fa170736f3d0\" data-question=\"34\">have been extensively picked over and examined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> in reports, inquiries and commentaries.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d55f1376-e187-4e36-8c74-945f4ab76028\" data-question=\"28\">The knock-on effect of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> this scrutiny has been to make the governance of companies in general an issue of intense public debate and has significantly increased the pressures on, and the responsibilities of, directors. At the simplest and most practical level, the time involved in fulfilling the demands of a board directorship has increased significantly, calling into question the effectiveness of the classic model of corporate governance by part-time, independent non-executive directors. Where once a board schedule may have consisted of between eight and ten meetings a year, in many companies the number of events requiring board input and decisions has dramatically risen. Furthermore, the amount of reading and preparation required for each meeting is increasing. Agendas can become overloaded and this can mean <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"01cd2d8c-d734-4612-a27d-63910a6c9e13\" data-question=\"36\">the time for constructive debate must necessarily be restricted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> in favour of getting through the business.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Often, board business is devolved to committees in order to cope with the workload, which may be more efficient but can mean that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"800bedbe-774e-4fa5-b3ab-f28b60c1d8ab\" data-question=\"29\">the board as a whole<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"acb62c5a-913a-4cce-b375-2e0475e16aab\" data-question=\"37\">less involved in fully addressing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> some of the most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b9cded1c-d90f-44da-9892-5d81dee44b51\" data-question=\"29\">important issues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. It is not uncommon for the audit committee meeting to last longer than the main board meeting itself. Process may take the place of discussion and be at the expense of real collaboration, so that boxes are ticked rather than issues tackled.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6b2d712b-526e-40b2-8254-69133718d54e\" data-question=\"30\">radical solution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, which may work for some very large companies whose businesses are extensive and complex, is the professional board, whose members would work up to three or four days a week, supported by their own dedicated staff and advisers. There are obvious risks to this and it would be important to establish clear guidelines for such a board to ensure that it did not step on the toes of management by becoming too engaged in the day-to-day running of the company. Problems of recruitment, remuneration and independence could also arise and this structure would not be appropriate for all companies. However, more professional and better-informed boards would have been particularly appropriate for banks where the executives had access to information that part-time non-executive directors lacked, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b9e28e3-8c99-434b-abe5-7d5fdf63913d\" data-question=\"38\">leaving the latter unable to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> comprehend or anticipate the 2008 crash.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>One of the main criticisms of boards and their directors is that they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89b42c41-e01b-44f2-9280-f5ec6aa2d455\" data-question=\"31\">do not focus sufficiently on longer-term matters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of strategy, sustainability and governance, but instead <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e6021c4-96d2-495a-8d7d-9677512f1d1b\" data-question=\"39\">concentrate too much on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> short-term financial metrics. Regulatory requirements and the structure of the market encourage this behaviour. The tyranny of quarterly reporting can distort board decision-making, as directors have to ‘make the numbers’ every four months to meet the insatiable appetite of the market for more data. This serves to encourage the trading methodology of a certain kind of investor who moves in and out of a stock without engaging in constructive dialogue with the company about strategy or performance, and is simply seeking a short-term financial gain. This effect has been made worse by the changing profile of investors due to the globalisation of capital and the increasing use of automated trading systems. Corporate culture adapts and management teams are largely incentivised to meet financial goals.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>Compensation for chief executives has become a combat zone where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e8be5c4-6531-4923-82ce-7094021ac168\" data-question=\"32\">pitched battles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> between investors, management and board members are fought, often behind closed doors but increasingly frequently in the full glare of press attention. Many would argue that this is in the interest of transparency and good governance as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a699205c-951c-4fe1-a300-9651d6ba17d1\" data-question=\"40\">shareholders use their muscle in the area of pay<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1e5b412-6d66-4e89-b3fe-af7b7d85ee43\" data-question=\"40\">pressure boards to remove<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> underperforming chief executives. Their powers to vote down executive remuneration policies increased when binding votes came into force. The chair of the remuneration committee can be an exposed and lonely role, as Alison Carnwath, chair of Barclays Bank’s remuneration committee, found when she had to resign, having been roundly criticised for trying to defend the enormous bonus to be paid to the chief executive; the irony being that she was widely understood to have spoken out against it in the privacy of the committee.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>The financial crisis stimulated a debate about the role and purpose of the company and a heightened awareness of corporate ethics. Trust in the corporation has been eroded and academics such as Michael Sandel, in his thoughtful and bestselling book <em>What Money Can’t Buy</em>, are questioning the morality of capitalism and the market economy. Boards of companies in all sectors will need to widen their perspective to encompass these issues and this may involve <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec52de1b-6443-4389-872b-ae2e59cd12bb\" data-question=\"33\">a realignment of corporate goals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. We live in challenging times.</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Reading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G</strong></p><p>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</p><p><em>Write the correct number, <strong>i-viii</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-33</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p><p><strong>List of Headings</strong></p><p><strong>i</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e8be5c4-6531-4923-82ce-7094021ac168\" data-question=\"32\">Disputes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> over financial arrangements regarding senior managers</p><p><strong>ii </strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d55f1376-e187-4e36-8c74-945f4ab76028\" data-question=\"28\">The impact on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> companies of being subjected to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d6de258-3cf1-43eb-91e2-450899919777\" data-question=\"28\">close examination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></p><p><strong>iii </strong> The possible need for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec52de1b-6443-4389-872b-ae2e59cd12bb\" data-question=\"33\">fundamental change in every area of business<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></p><p><strong>iv </strong> Many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ad8d48d4-bbbc-415d-be57-2f178920ca24\" data-question=\"27\">external bodies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"abad2d6c-441a-4393-b8b3-6c5d26be4d86\" data-question=\"27\">being held responsible for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> problems</p><p><strong>v </strong> The falling number of board members with broad enough experience</p><p><strong>vi </strong> A risk that not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"800bedbe-774e-4fa5-b3ab-f28b60c1d8ab\" data-question=\"29\">all directors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> take part in solving <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b9cded1c-d90f-44da-9892-5d81dee44b51\" data-question=\"29\">major problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></p><p><strong>vii </strong> Boards <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89b42c41-e01b-44f2-9280-f5ec6aa2d455\" data-question=\"31\">not looking far enough ahead<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></p><p><strong>viii</strong> A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6b2d712b-526e-40b2-8254-69133718d54e\" data-question=\"30\">proposal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to change the way the board operates</p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"760\" id=\"question-wrapper-760\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"761\" id=\"question-wrapper-761\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"762\" id=\"question-wrapper-762\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"763\" id=\"question-wrapper-763\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"764\" id=\"question-wrapper-764\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"765\" id=\"question-wrapper-765\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"766\" id=\"question-wrapper-766\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>34-37</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"767\" id=\"question-wrapper-767\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d25462b4-739c-40d4-acb8-fa170736f3d0\" data-question=\"34\">Close scrutiny<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> of the behaviour of boards has increased since <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ed27279-a00c-480f-ac2a-2e1fe468e5fb\" data-question=\"34\">the economic downturn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"768\" id=\"question-wrapper-768\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Banks have been mismanaged to a greater extent than other businesses. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"769\" id=\"question-wrapper-769\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Board meetings normally <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"01cd2d8c-d734-4612-a27d-63910a6c9e13\" data-question=\"36\">continue for as long as necessary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> to debate matters in full. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"770\" id=\"question-wrapper-770\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Using a committee structure would ensure that board members <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"acb62c5a-913a-4cce-b375-2e0475e16aab\" data-question=\"37\">are fully informed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> about significant issues. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the sentences below.<br></span><span>Choose </span><strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>38-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"771\" id=\"question-wrapper-771\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Before 2008, non-executive directors <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b9e28e3-8c99-434b-abe5-7d5fdf63913d\" data-question=\"38\">were at a disadvantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> because of their lack of ……………………….. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INFORMATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"772\" id=\"question-wrapper-772\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Boards tend to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"816dcd4b-fac5-407b-bb31-2272a2058dd0\" data-question=\"39\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e6021c4-96d2-495a-8d7d-9677512f1d1b\" data-question=\"39\">place too much emphasis on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> …………………………. considerations that are only of short-term relevance. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FINANCIAL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"773\" id=\"question-wrapper-773\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> On <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a699205c-951c-4fe1-a300-9651d6ba17d1\" data-question=\"40\">certain matters, such as pay<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, the board may have to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1e5b412-6d66-4e89-b3fe-af7b7d85ee43\" data-question=\"40\">accept the views<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> of ……………………….. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SHAREHOLDERS/INVESTORS</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"6ed27279-a00c-480f-ac2a-2e1fe468e5fb","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"the economic downturn","passagePhrase":"the crisis"},{"uid":"ad8d48d4-bbbc-415d-be57-2f178920ca24","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"external bodies","passagePhrase":"Governments, regulators, central banks and auditors"},{"uid":"abad2d6c-441a-4393-b8b3-6c5d26be4d86","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"being held responsible for","passagePhrase":"have all been in the frame"},{"uid":"d25462b4-739c-40d4-acb8-fa170736f3d0","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Close scrutiny","passagePhrase":"have been extensively picked over and examined"},{"uid":"d55f1376-e187-4e36-8c74-945f4ab76028","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The impact on","passagePhrase":"The knock-on effect of"},{"uid":"800bedbe-774e-4fa5-b3ab-f28b60c1d8ab","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"all directors","passagePhrase":"the board as a whole"},{"uid":"b9cded1c-d90f-44da-9892-5d81dee44b51","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"major problems","passagePhrase":"important issues"},{"uid":"6b2d712b-526e-40b2-8254-69133718d54e","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"proposal","passagePhrase":"radical solution"},{"uid":"3b9e28e3-8c99-434b-abe5-7d5fdf63913d","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"were at a disadvantage","passagePhrase":"leaving the latter unable to"},{"uid":"89b42c41-e01b-44f2-9280-f5ec6aa2d455","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"not looking far enough ahead","passagePhrase":"do not focus sufficiently on longer-term matters"},{"uid":"3e6021c4-96d2-495a-8d7d-9677512f1d1b","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"place too much emphasis on","passagePhrase":"concentrate too much on"},{"uid":"1e8be5c4-6531-4923-82ce-7094021ac168","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"Disputes","passagePhrase":"pitched battles"},{"uid":"a699205c-951c-4fe1-a300-9651d6ba17d1","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"certain matters, such as pay","passagePhrase":"shareholders use their muscle in the area of pay"},{"uid":"a1e5b412-6d66-4e89-b3fe-af7b7d85ee43","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"accept the views","passagePhrase":"pressure boards to remove"},{"uid":"ec52de1b-6443-4389-872b-ae2e59cd12bb","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"fundamental change in every area of business","passagePhrase":"a realignment of corporate goals"},{"uid":"2d6de258-3cf1-43eb-91e2-450899919777","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"close examination","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_223":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong>Case Study: Tourism New Zealand website</strong></span></h2><p><span>New Zealand is a small country of four million inhabitants, a long-haul flight from all the major tourist-generating markets of the world. Tourism currently makes up 9% of the country’s gross domestic product, and is the country’s largest export sector. Unlike other export sectors, which make products and then sell them overseas, tourism brings its customers to New Zealand. The product is the country itself – the people, the places and the experiences. In 1999, Tourism New Zealand launched a campaign to communicate a new brand position to the world. The campaign focused on New Zealand’s scenic beauty, exhilarating outdoor activities and authentic Maori culture, and it made New Zealand one of the strongest national brands in the world.</span></p><p><span>A key feature of the campaign was the website www.newzealand.com, which provided potential visitors to New Zealand with a single gateway to everything the destination had to offer. The heart of the website was a database of tourism services operators, both those based in New Zealand and those based abroad which offered tourism service to the country. Any tourism-related business could be listed by filling in a simple form. This meant that even the smallest bed and breakfast address or specialist activity provider could gain a web presence with access to an audience of long-haul visitors. In addition, because participating businesses <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46f57b6d-9e9b-4acc-98fd-6765660940c7\" data-question=\"1\">were able to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> update the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08ca064b-3eb2-467d-8a3b-de2dddccefaa\" data-question=\"1\">details<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> they gave <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a12ff375-4621-4774-8d48-591cdfe5aafe\" data-question=\"1\">on a regular basis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, the information provided remained accurate. And to maintain and improve standards, Tourism New Zealand organised a scheme whereby organisations appearing on the website underwent an independent evaluation against a set of agreed national standards of quality. As part of this, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b12a1715-3b73-4eab-bb5d-6a114f6c6a3b\" data-question=\"2\">effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of each business on the environment was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7404e7c3-56e0-4cd1-9151-3e03bd1312ff\" data-question=\"2\">considered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>To communicate the New Zealand experience, the site also carried features relating to famous people and places. One of the most popular was an interview with former New Zealand All Blacks <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"52b24388-e9a8-43fb-a25c-f21f84efe1ed\" data-question=\"3\">rugby<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> captain Tana Umaga. Another feature that attracted a lot of attention was an interactive journey through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ef371184-0d4e-4ba8-9931-a705453d7dbd\" data-question=\"4\">a number of the locations chosen for blockbuster films which had made use of New Zealand’s stunning scenery as a backdrop. As the site developed, additional features were added to help independent travelers devise their own customised itineraries. To make it easier to plan motoring holidays, the site catalogued the most popular driving routes in the country, highlighting different routes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cda1d0e-e502-4338-ab6f-592707b35f2b\" data-question=\"5\">according to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> the season and indicating distances and times.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p><p><span>Later, a Travel Planner feature was added, which allowed visitors to click and ‘bookmark’ places or attractions they were interested in, and then view the results on a map. The Travel Planner offered suggested routes and public transport options between the chosen locations. There were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a4b53fe7-057e-4676-b742-cc16a4611f3a\" data-question=\"6\">also<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> links to accommodation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"07959e09-5bad-45a3-bf63-269a093e1adc\" data-question=\"6\">in the area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. By registering with the website, users could save their Travel Plan and return to it later, or print it out to take on the visit. The website also had a ‘Your Words’ section where anyone could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"533af97b-c5bf-4c7c-b7eb-3f07637ddfbc\" data-question=\"7\">submit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> a blog of their New Zealand travels for possible inclusion on the website.</span></p><p><span>The Tourism New Zealand website won two Webby awards for online achievement and innovation. More importantly perhaps, the growth of tourism to New Zealand was impressive. Overall tourism expenditure increased by an average of 6.9% per year between 1999 and 2004. From Britain, visits to New Zealand grew at an average annual rate of 13% between 2002 and 2006, compared to a rate of 4% overall for British visits abroad.</span></p><p><span>The website was set up to allow both individuals and travel organisations to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d29b6237-efe4-471b-84a6-4d6f745dd7a4\" data-question=\"8\">create itineraries and travel packages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> to suit their own needs and interests. On the website, visitors can search for activities not solely by geographical location, but also by the particular nature of the activity. This is important as research shows that activities are the key driver of visitor satisfaction, contributing 74% to visitor satisfaction, while <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"df0cf986-6f19-44e1-bf2b-961122d7cb75\" data-question=\"10\">transport and accommodation account for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> the remaining 26%. The more activities that visitors undertake, the more satisfied they will be. It has also been found that visitors enjoy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0f575a36-a0ad-41e1-9357-fb39d2789d6a\" data-question=\"11\">cultural activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> most when they are interactive, such as visiting a <em>marae</em> (meeting ground) to learn about traditional Maori life. Many long-haul travelers enjoy such learning experiences, which provide them with stories to take home to their friends and family. In addition, it appears that visitors to New Zealand don’t want to be ‘one of the crowd’ and find activities that involve only a few people more special and meaningful.</span></p><p><span>It could be argued that New Zealand is not a typical destination. New Zealand is a small country with a visitor economy composed mainly of small businesses. It is generally perceived as a safe English-speaking country with a reliable transport infrastructure. Because of the long-haul flight, most visitors stay for longer (average 20 days) and want to see as much of the country as possible on what is often seen as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a024efa7-5521-43c1-996d-6c99760c06ec\" data-question=\"13\">a once-in-a-lifetime visit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. However, the underlying lessons apply anywhere – the effectiveness of a strong brand, a strategy based on unique experiences and a comprehensive and user-friendly website.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the table below.<br></span><span>Choose </span><strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong><span> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>1-7</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><table><tbody><tr><td width=\"186\"><span><strong>Section of website</strong></span></td><td width=\"438\"><span><strong>Comments</strong></span></td></tr><tr><td width=\"186\"><p><span>Database of tourism services</span></p></td><td width=\"438\"><p><span>• easy for tourism-related businesses to get on the list</span></p><p><span><span>• </span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46f57b6d-9e9b-4acc-98fd-6765660940c7\" data-question=\"1\">allowed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> businesses to <strong>1</strong>…………………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08ca064b-3eb2-467d-8a3b-de2dddccefaa\" data-question=\"1\">information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a12ff375-4621-4774-8d48-591cdfe5aafe\" data-question=\"1\">regularly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></span></p><p><span><span>• </span> provided a country-wide <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7404e7c3-56e0-4cd1-9151-3e03bd1312ff\" data-question=\"2\">evaluation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of businesses, including their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b12a1715-3b73-4eab-bb5d-6a114f6c6a3b\" data-question=\"2\">impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> on the <strong>2</strong>………………………..</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"186\"><span>Special features on local topics</span></td><td width=\"438\"><span><span>• </span> e.g. an interview with a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"52b24388-e9a8-43fb-a25c-f21f84efe1ed\" data-question=\"3\">former sports<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <strong>3</strong>……………………………., and an interactive tour of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ef371184-0d4e-4ba8-9931-a705453d7dbd\" data-question=\"4\">various locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> used in <strong>4</strong>……………………….</span></td></tr><tr><td width=\"186\"><span>Information on driving routes</span></td><td width=\"438\"><span><span>• </span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cda1d0e-e502-4338-ab6f-592707b35f2b\" data-question=\"5\">varied depending on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> the <strong>5</strong>……………………………</span></td></tr><tr><td width=\"186\"><span>Travel Planner</span></td><td width=\"438\"><span><span>• </span> included a map showing selected places, details of public transport and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"07959e09-5bad-45a3-bf63-269a093e1adc\" data-question=\"6\">local<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <strong>6</strong>………………………….</span></td></tr><tr><td width=\"186\"><span>‘Your Words’</span></td><td width=\"438\"><span><span>• </span>travelers could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"533af97b-c5bf-4c7c-b7eb-3f07637ddfbc\" data-question=\"7\">send a link<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> to their <strong>7</strong>…………………………</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"454\" id=\"question-wrapper-454\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">UPDATE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"455\" id=\"question-wrapper-455\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ENVIRONMENT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"456\" id=\"question-wrapper-456\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CAPTAIN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"457\" id=\"question-wrapper-457\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FILMS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"458\" id=\"question-wrapper-458\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SEASON</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"459\" id=\"question-wrapper-459\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ACCOMMODATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"460\" id=\"question-wrapper-460\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BLOG</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>8-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"461\" id=\"question-wrapper-461\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The website www.newzealand.com aimed to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d29b6237-efe4-471b-84a6-4d6f745dd7a4\" data-question=\"8\">provide ready-made itineraries and packages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> for travel companies and individual tourists. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"462\" id=\"question-wrapper-462\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It was found that most visitors started searching on the website by geographical location. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"463\" id=\"question-wrapper-463\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to research, 26% of visitor satisfaction is related <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"df0cf986-6f19-44e1-bf2b-961122d7cb75\" data-question=\"10\">to their accommodation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"464\" id=\"question-wrapper-464\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Visitors to New Zealand like to become involved in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0f575a36-a0ad-41e1-9357-fb39d2789d6a\" data-question=\"11\">local culture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"465\" id=\"question-wrapper-465\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Visitors like staying in small hotels in New Zealand rather than in larger ones. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"466\" id=\"question-wrapper-466\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Many visitors feel it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a024efa7-5521-43c1-996d-6c99760c06ec\" data-question=\"13\">unlikely that they will return<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to New Zealand after their visit. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"46f57b6d-9e9b-4acc-98fd-6765660940c7","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"allowed","passagePhrase":"were able to"},{"uid":"08ca064b-3eb2-467d-8a3b-de2dddccefaa","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"information","passagePhrase":"details"},{"uid":"a12ff375-4621-4774-8d48-591cdfe5aafe","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"regularly","passagePhrase":"on a regular basis"},{"uid":"b12a1715-3b73-4eab-bb5d-6a114f6c6a3b","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"impact","passagePhrase":"effect"},{"uid":"7404e7c3-56e0-4cd1-9151-3e03bd1312ff","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"evaluation","passagePhrase":"considered"},{"uid":"52b24388-e9a8-43fb-a25c-f21f84efe1ed","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"former sports","passagePhrase":"rugby"},{"uid":"ef371184-0d4e-4ba8-9931-a705453d7dbd","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"various locations","passagePhrase":"a number of the locations chosen for blockbuster films which had made use of New Zealand’s stunning scenery as a backdrop. As the site developed, additional features were added to help independent travelers devise their own customised itineraries. To make it easier to plan motoring holidays, the site catalogued the most popular driving routes in the country, highlighting different routes according to the season and indicating distances and times."},{"uid":"7cda1d0e-e502-4338-ab6f-592707b35f2b","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"varied depending on","passagePhrase":"according to"},{"uid":"a4b53fe7-057e-4676-b742-cc16a4611f3a","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"also"},{"uid":"07959e09-5bad-45a3-bf63-269a093e1adc","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"local","passagePhrase":"in the area"},{"uid":"533af97b-c5bf-4c7c-b7eb-3f07637ddfbc","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"send a link","passagePhrase":"submit"},{"uid":"0f575a36-a0ad-41e1-9357-fb39d2789d6a","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"local culture","passagePhrase":"cultural activities"},{"uid":"a024efa7-5521-43c1-996d-6c99760c06ec","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"unlikely that they will return","passagePhrase":"a once-in-a-lifetime visit"}]},"reading_u2_224":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Why being bored is stimulating – and useful, too</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>This most common of emotions is turning out to be more interesting than we thought</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>We all know how it feels – it’s impossible to keep your mind on anything, time stretches out, and all the things you could do seem equally unlikely to make you feel better. But defining boredom so that it can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdbc7552-4e7a-4f7b-acc6-c1dc2b99aae6\" data-question=\"14\">be studied in the lab<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10b37446-8d50-43f6-9097-dabb1069250c\" data-question=\"14\">has proved difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. For a start, it can include a lot of other mental states, such as frustration, apathy, depression and indifference. There isn’t even agreement over whether boredom is always a low-energy, flat kind of emotion or whether feeling agitated and restless counts as boredom, too. In his book, <em>Boredom: A Lively History</em>, Peter Toohey at the University of Calgary, Canada, compares it to disgust – an emotion that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41d40fec-0643-4fd6-8691-f7abec3734c0\" data-question=\"20\">motivates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> us to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0f81a321-8bc3-4bbc-9d6d-9f5880075320\" data-question=\"20\">stay away from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> certain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"867fdc63-2163-4d84-b3ea-2d03fa28cf47\" data-question=\"20\">situations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. ‘If disgust protects humans from infection, boredom may protect them from “infectious” social <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"867fdc63-2163-4d84-b3ea-2d03fa28cf47\" data-question=\"20\">situations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>,’ he suggests.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>By asking people about their experiences of boredom, Thomas Goetz and his team at the University of Konstanz in Germany have recently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b7856ed-3a3b-4bfd-ba8b-3634ee1f816f\" data-question=\"15\">identified<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> five <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cef8f52-974d-4a72-a3ec-3cccc7c6cbed\" data-question=\"15\">distinct <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc1d04e1-2e5c-4377-b2ed-703c2cfb9aff\" data-question=\"21\">types<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>: indifferent, calibrating, searching, reactant and apathetic. These can be plotted on two axes – one running left to right, which measures low to high arousal, and the other from top to bottom, which measures how positive or negative the feeling is. Intriguingly, Goetz has found that while people experience all kinds of boredom, they tend to specialise in one. Of the five <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc1d04e1-2e5c-4377-b2ed-703c2cfb9aff\" data-question=\"21\">types<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, the most damaging is ‘reactant’ boredom with its explosive combination of high arousal and negative emotion. The most useful is what Goetz calls ‘indifferent’ boredom: someone isn’t engaged in anything satisfying but still feels relaxed and calm. However, it remains to be seen whether there are any character traits that predict the kind of boredom each of us might be prone to.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Psychologist Sandi Mann at the University of Central Lancashire, UK, goes further. ‘All emotions are there for a reason, including boredom,’ she says. Mann has found that being bored <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e65dd625-5f71-4828-aef4-d029fe89f865\" data-question=\"16\">makes us more creative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. ‘We’re all afraid of being bored but in actual fact it can lead to all kinds of amazing things,’ she says. In experiments published last year, Mann found that people who had been made to feel bored by copying numbers out of the phone book for 15 minutes came up with more creative ideas about how to use a polystyrene cup than a control group. Mann concluded that a passive, boring activity is best for creativity because it allows the mind to wander. In fact, she goes so far as to suggest that we should seek out more boredom in our lives.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>Psychologist John Eastwood at York University in Toronto, Canada, isn’t convinced. ‘If you are in a state of mind-wandering you are not bored,’ he says. ‘In my view, by definition boredom is an undesirable state.’ That doesn’t necessarily mean that it isn’t adaptive, he adds. ‘Pain is adaptive – if we didn’t have physical pain, bad things would happen to us. Does that mean that we should actively cause pain? No. But even if boredom has evolved to help us survive, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eaf4e45e-ce83-44b3-98af-6129f519914c\" data-question=\"17\">can still be toxic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> if allowed to fester.’ For Eastwood, the central feature of boredom is a failure to put our ‘attention system’ into gear. This causes an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c390e9f-1926-4745-a998-098590d866c8\" data-question=\"24\">inability to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> focus on anything, which makes time seem to go painfully slowly. What’s more, your <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"00cc9718-cded-427e-826b-d4f4310ea660\" data-question=\"22\">efforts to improve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the situation can end up making you feel worse. ‘People try to connect with the world and if they are not successful there’s that frustration and irritability,’ he says. Perhaps most worryingly, says Eastwood, repeatedly failing to engage attention can lead to state where we don’t know what to do any more, and no longer care.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Eastwood’s team is now trying to explore why the attention system fails. It’s early days but they think that at least some of it comes down to personality. Boredom proneness has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e99e0fc-4ef3-40e7-adc8-0803e545941f\" data-question=\"18\">been linked with a variety of traits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. People who are motivated by pleasure seem to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7dc4445c-52c8-4934-a389-6686e6e08bfc\" data-question=\"25\">suffer particularly badly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Other <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6339e1f2-c707-4fef-a4ed-e93f9e86a37d\" data-question=\"26\">personality traits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, such as curiosity, are associated with a high boredom threshold. More evidence that boredom has detrimental effects comes from studies of people who are more or less prone to boredom. It seems those who bore easily face poorer prospects in education, their career and even life in general. But of course, boredom itself cannot kill – it’s the things we do to deal with it that may put us in danger. What can we do to alleviate it before it comes to that? Goetz’s group has one suggestion. Working with teenagers, they found that those who ‘approach’ a boring situation – in other words, see that it’s boring and get stuck in anyway – report less boredom than those who try to avoid it by using snacks, TV or social media for distraction.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>Psychologist Francoise Wemelsfelder speculates that our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1fe76d03-73be-4023-86cf-4f41e508f2b5\" data-question=\"19\">over-connected lifestyles might even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b99d779-01a9-45d4-aaf2-3f90992eb5de\" data-question=\"23\">be a new source of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> boredom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. ‘In modern human society there is a lot of overstimulation but still a lot of problems finding meaning,’ she says. So instead of seeking yet more mental stimulation, perhaps we should leave our phones alone, and use boredom to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1fe76d03-73be-4023-86cf-4f41e508f2b5\" data-question=\"19\">motivate us to engage with the world in a more meaningful way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p><p><span> </span><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, <strong>A-F<br></strong></span><span>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, <strong>i-viii</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-19</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span><strong>List of Headings</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>i</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e65dd625-5f71-4828-aef4-d029fe89f865\" data-question=\"16\">The productive outcomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that may result from boredom</span></p><p><span><strong>ii</strong> What teachers can do to prevent boredom </span></p><p><span><strong>iii</strong> A new <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1fe76d03-73be-4023-86cf-4f41e508f2b5\" data-question=\"19\">explanation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1fe76d03-73be-4023-86cf-4f41e508f2b5\" data-question=\"19\">new cure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> for boredom</span></p><p><span><strong>iv </strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10b37446-8d50-43f6-9097-dabb1069250c\" data-question=\"14\">Problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdbc7552-4e7a-4f7b-acc6-c1dc2b99aae6\" data-question=\"14\">a scientific approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to boredom</span></p><p><span><strong>v</strong> A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eaf4e45e-ce83-44b3-98af-6129f519914c\" data-question=\"17\">potential danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> arising from boredom</span></p><p><span><strong>vi</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b7856ed-3a3b-4bfd-ba8b-3634ee1f816f\" data-question=\"15\">Creating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cef8f52-974d-4a72-a3ec-3cccc7c6cbed\" data-question=\"15\">a system of classification<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> for feelings of boredom</span></p><p><span><strong>vii</strong> Age groups most affected by boredom</span></p><p><span><strong>viii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e99e0fc-4ef3-40e7-adc8-0803e545941f\" data-question=\"18\">Identifying those<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> most affected by boredom</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"467\" id=\"question-wrapper-467\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"468\" id=\"question-wrapper-468\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"469\" id=\"question-wrapper-469\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"470\" id=\"question-wrapper-470\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"471\" id=\"question-wrapper-471\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"472\" id=\"question-wrapper-472\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following people (Questions <strong>20-23</strong>) and the list of ideas below.</span></p><p><span>Match each person with the correct idea, <strong>A-E</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-E</strong>, in boxes <strong>20-23</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Ideas</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7470b98f-4b62-4a6e-95f4-2782fa650d60\" data-question=\"23\">The way we live<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> today may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b99d779-01a9-45d4-aaf2-3f90992eb5de\" data-question=\"23\">encourage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> boredom.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> One <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc1d04e1-2e5c-4377-b2ed-703c2cfb9aff\" data-question=\"21\">sort<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of boredom is worse than all the others.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> Levels of boredom may fall in the future.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"00cc9718-cded-427e-826b-d4f4310ea660\" data-question=\"22\">Trying to cope with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> boredom can increase its negative effects.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> Boredom may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41d40fec-0643-4fd6-8691-f7abec3734c0\" data-question=\"20\">encourage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> us to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0f81a321-8bc3-4bbc-9d6d-9f5880075320\" data-question=\"20\">avoid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> an unpleasant <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"867fdc63-2163-4d84-b3ea-2d03fa28cf47\" data-question=\"20\">experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"473\" id=\"question-wrapper-473\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Peter Toohey </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"474\" id=\"question-wrapper-474\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Thomas Goetz </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"475\" id=\"question-wrapper-475\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> John Eastwood </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"476\" id=\"question-wrapper-476\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Francoise Wemelsfelder </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>24-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>Responses to boredom</strong></span></h3><p><span>For John Eastwood, the central feature of boredom is that people cannot <strong>24</strong>……………………………, due to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c390e9f-1926-4745-a998-098590d866c8\" data-question=\"24\">a failure in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> what he calls the ‘attention system’, and as a result they become frustrated and irritable. His team suggests that those for whom <strong>25</strong>……………………….. is an important aim in life may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7dc4445c-52c8-4934-a389-6686e6e08bfc\" data-question=\"25\">have problems in coping with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> boredom, whereas those who have the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6339e1f2-c707-4fef-a4ed-e93f9e86a37d\" data-question=\"26\">characteristic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> of <strong>26</strong>……………………….. can generally cope with it.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"477\" id=\"question-wrapper-477\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOCUS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"478\" id=\"question-wrapper-478\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PLEASURE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"479\" id=\"question-wrapper-479\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CURIOSITY</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"cdbc7552-4e7a-4f7b-acc6-c1dc2b99aae6","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"a scientific approach","passagePhrase":"be studied in the lab"},{"uid":"10b37446-8d50-43f6-9097-dabb1069250c","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Problems","passagePhrase":"has proved difficult"},{"uid":"41d40fec-0643-4fd6-8691-f7abec3734c0","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"encourage","passagePhrase":"motivates"},{"uid":"0f81a321-8bc3-4bbc-9d6d-9f5880075320","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"avoid","passagePhrase":"stay away from"},{"uid":"867fdc63-2163-4d84-b3ea-2d03fa28cf47","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"experience","passagePhrase":"situations ... situations"},{"uid":"2b7856ed-3a3b-4bfd-ba8b-3634ee1f816f","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Creating","passagePhrase":"identified"},{"uid":"7cef8f52-974d-4a72-a3ec-3cccc7c6cbed","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"a system of classification","passagePhrase":"distinct types"},{"uid":"bc1d04e1-2e5c-4377-b2ed-703c2cfb9aff","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"sort","passagePhrase":"types ... types"},{"uid":"e65dd625-5f71-4828-aef4-d029fe89f865","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"The productive outcomes","passagePhrase":"makes us more creative"},{"uid":"eaf4e45e-ce83-44b3-98af-6129f519914c","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"potential danger","passagePhrase":"can still be toxic"},{"uid":"6c390e9f-1926-4745-a998-098590d866c8","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"a failure in","passagePhrase":"inability to"},{"uid":"00cc9718-cded-427e-826b-d4f4310ea660","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Trying to cope with","passagePhrase":"efforts to improve"},{"uid":"8e99e0fc-4ef3-40e7-adc8-0803e545941f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Identifying those","passagePhrase":"been linked with a variety of traits"},{"uid":"7dc4445c-52c8-4934-a389-6686e6e08bfc","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"have problems in coping with","passagePhrase":"suffer particularly badly"},{"uid":"6339e1f2-c707-4fef-a4ed-e93f9e86a37d","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"characteristic","passagePhrase":"personality traits"},{"uid":"1fe76d03-73be-4023-86cf-4f41e508f2b5","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"explanation ... new cure","passagePhrase":"over-connected lifestyles might even be a new source of boredom ... motivate us to engage with the world in a more meaningful way"},{"uid":"7b99d779-01a9-45d4-aaf2-3f90992eb5de","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"encourage","passagePhrase":"be a new source of"},{"uid":"7470b98f-4b62-4a6e-95f4-2782fa650d60","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"The way we live","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_225":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>Artificial artist?</strong></span></h2><h3><span><em>Can computers really create works of art?</em></span></h3><p><span>The Painting Fool is one of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c3023e73-3762-4461-9e17-4ca5c134c0d9\" data-question=\"27\">a growing number<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e75ce23-d360-4749-9eec-3cd58001372a\" data-question=\"27\">computer programs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> which, so their makers claim, possess creative talents. Classical music by an artificial composer has had audiences enraptured, and even tricked them into believing a human was behind the score. Artworks painted by a robot have sold for thousands of dollars and been hung in prestigious galleries. And software has been built which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c3023e73-3762-4461-9e17-4ca5c134c0d9\" data-question=\"27\">creates art that could not have been imagined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> by the programmer.</span></p><p><span>Human beings are the only species to perform sophisticated creative acts regularly. If we can break this process down into computer code, where does that leave human creativity? ‘This is a question at the very core of humanity,’ says Geraint Wiggins, a computational creativity researcher at Goldsmiths, University of London. ‘It scares a lot of people. They are worried that it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cae7c9bb-bcc3-4f06-80fe-cf3eeea90158\" data-question=\"28\">taking something special away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aacc7b42-c729-400c-8140-71d59e4b789a\" data-question=\"28\">what it means to be human<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.’</span></p><p><span>To some extent, we are all familiar with computerised art. The question is: where does the work of the artist stop and the creativity of the computer begin? Consider one of the oldest machine artists, Aaron, a robot that has had paintings exhibited in London’s Tate Modern and the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art. Aaron can pick up a paintbrush and paint on canvas on its own. Impressive perhaps, but it is still little more than a tool to realise the programmer’s own creative ideas.</span></p><p><span>Simon Colton, the designer of the Painting Fool, is keen to make sure his creation doesn’t attract the same criticism. Unlike earlier ‘artists’ such as Aaron, the Painting Fool only needs minimal direction and can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2dce3cd-d38c-4b6a-adb4-84857139eced\" data-question=\"29\">come up with its own concepts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> by going online for material. The software runs its own web searches and trawls through social media sites. It is now beginning to display a kind of imagination too, creating pictures from scratch. One of its original works is a series of fuzzy landscapes, depicting trees and sky. While some might say they have a mechanical look, Colton argues that such reactions arise from people’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"802c76e6-1304-486a-980d-b398a8965ce6\" data-question=\"30\">double standards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> towards software-produced and human-produced art. After all, he says, consider that the Painting Fool painted the landscapes without referring to a photo. ‘If a child painted a new scene from its head, you’d say it has a certain level of imagination,’ he points out. ‘The same should be true of a machine.’ Software bugs can also lead to unexpected results. Some of the Painting Fool’s paintings of a chair came out in black and white, thanks to a technical glitch. This gives the work <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac17f364-7876-4e1d-ac69-3f9221902068\" data-question=\"31\">an eerie, ghostlike quality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Human artists like the renowned Ellsworth Kelly are lauded for limiting their colour palette – so why should computers be any different?</span></p><p><span>Researchers like Colton don’t believe it is right to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c9b56d55-d88b-473a-98e1-17d71fad3326\" data-question=\"32\">measure machine creativity directly to that of humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> who ‘have had millennia to develop our skills’. Others, though, are fascinated by the prospect that a computer might create something as original and subtle as our best artists. So far, only one has come close. Composer David Cope invented a program called Experiments in Musical Intelligence, or EMI. Not only did EMI create compositions in Cope’s style, but also that of the most revered classical composers, including Bach, Chopin and Mozart. Audiences were moved to tears, and EMI even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a31fe974-1ab5-4fc6-9afb-7eb1fd23d0be\" data-question=\"33\">fooled classical music experts into thinking they were hearing genuine Bach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. Not everyone was impressed however. Some, such as Wiggins, have blasted Cope’s work as pseudoscience, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4f42a2b-cfc9-4cc0-ab7d-fa8815a331f6\" data-question=\"34\">condemned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> him for his deliberately vague <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d55288f8-ffbb-46a2-8a50-6bfaf4d511c5\" data-question=\"34\">explanation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> of how the software worked. Meanwhile, Douglas Hofstadter of Indiana University said EMI <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee624c39-0718-4cdd-ad79-ec2c3c923b1d\" data-question=\"35\">created replicas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> which still <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54839b3f-0d13-4fb4-806e-b7809f02e736\" data-question=\"35\">rely completely on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"29ebcda8-4c0a-4975-acc0-e7c819a33a94\" data-question=\"35\">the original artist’s creative impulses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. When audiences found out <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8709b13-5dfa-4553-bafa-6d4fc161859d\" data-question=\"36\">the truth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> they were often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7a33969-44ca-4db2-b08a-a954ad04c8c6\" data-question=\"36\">outraged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> with Cope, and one music lover even tried to punch him. Amid such controversy, Cope destroyed EMI’s vital databases.</span></p><p><span>But why did so many people love the music, yet recoil when the discovered how it was composed? A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6ffc582-96cb-4d02-a302-6e44c02c6473\" data-question=\"38\">study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> by computer scientist David Moffat of Glasgow Caledonian University <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1eec384a-778c-4a78-b730-bc0ae54636fc\" data-question=\"38\">provides a clue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. He asked both expert musicians and non-experts to assess six compositions. The participants weren’t <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54b2b736-4de7-4794-b74e-cb141c8b49b0\" data-question=\"37\">told beforehand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> whether the tunes were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5a946c1-cb21-468b-be3a-8163a49ea8b6\" data-question=\"37\">composed by humans or computers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, but were asked to guess, and then rate how much they liked each one. People who thought the composer was a computer tended to dislike the piece more than those who believed it was human. This was true even among the experts, who might have been expected to be more objective in their analyses.</span></p><p><span>Where does this prejudice come from? Paul Bloom of Yale University has a suggestion: he reckons part of the pleasure we get from art stems from the creative process behind the work. This can give it an ‘irresistible essence’, says Bloom. Meanwhile, experiments by Justin Kruger of New York University <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ad2ce571-a02e-43eb-88f6-a253eb7e601c\" data-question=\"40\">have shown that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> people’s enjoyment of an artwork increases if they think more time and effort was needed to create it. Similarly, Colton thinks that when people experience art, they wonder what the artist might have been thinking or what the artist is trying to tell them. It seems obvious, therefore, that with computers producing art, this speculation is cut short – there’s nothing to explore. But as technology becomes increasingly complex, finding those greater depths in computer art could become possible. This is precisely why Colton asks the Painting Fool to tap into online social networks for its inspiration: hopefully this way it will choose themes that will already be meaningful to us.</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"480\" id=\"question-wrapper-480\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer suggesting about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e75ce23-d360-4749-9eec-3cd58001372a\" data-question=\"27\">computer-produced works<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. People’s acceptance of them can vary considerably.</li> <li>B. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c3023e73-3762-4461-9e17-4ca5c134c0d9\" data-question=\"27\">great deal of progress<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> has already been attained in this field.</li> <li>C. They have had more success in some artistic genres than in others.</li> <li>D. the advances are not as significant as the public believes them to be.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"481\" id=\"question-wrapper-481\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to Geraint Wiggins, why are many people worried by computer art? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is aesthetically inferior to human art.</li> <li>B. It may ultimately supersede human art.</li> <li>C. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cae7c9bb-bcc3-4f06-80fe-cf3eeea90158\" data-question=\"28\">undermines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aacc7b42-c729-400c-8140-71d59e4b789a\" data-question=\"28\">a fundamental human quality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>D. It will lead to a deterioration in human ability.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"482\" id=\"question-wrapper-482\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is a key difference between Aaron and the Painting Fool? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. its programmer’s background</li> <li>B. public response to its work</li> <li>C. the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2dce3cd-d38c-4b6a-adb4-84857139eced\" data-question=\"29\">source of its subject matter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></li> <li>D. the technical standard of its output</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"483\" id=\"question-wrapper-483\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does Simon Colton make in the fourth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Software-produced art is often dismissed as childish and simplistic.</li> <li>B. The same concepts of creativity should not be applied to all forms of art.</li> <li>C. It is unreasonable to expect a machine to be as imaginative as a human being.</li> <li>D. People tend to judge computer art and human art according to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"802c76e6-1304-486a-980d-b398a8965ce6\" data-question=\"30\">different criteria<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"484\" id=\"question-wrapper-484\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer refers to the paintings of a chair as an example of computer art which </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. achieves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac17f364-7876-4e1d-ac69-3f9221902068\" data-question=\"31\">a particularly striking effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> <li>B. exhibits a certain level of genuine artistic skill.</li> <li>C. closely resembles that of a well-known artist.</li> <li>D. highlights the technical limitations of the software.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, <strong>A-G</strong> below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>32-37</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Ideas</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> generating work that was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a31fe974-1ab5-4fc6-9afb-7eb1fd23d0be\" data-question=\"33\">virtually indistinguishable from that of humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54b2b736-4de7-4794-b74e-cb141c8b49b0\" data-question=\"37\">knowing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> whether it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5a946c1-cb21-468b-be3a-8163a49ea8b6\" data-question=\"37\">the work of humans or software<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee624c39-0718-4cdd-ad79-ec2c3c923b1d\" data-question=\"35\">producing work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54839b3f-0d13-4fb4-806e-b7809f02e736\" data-question=\"35\">entirely dependent on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"29ebcda8-4c0a-4975-acc0-e7c819a33a94\" data-question=\"35\">imagination of its creator<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c9b56d55-d88b-473a-98e1-17d71fad3326\" data-question=\"32\">comparing the artistic achievements of humans and computers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>E </strong> revealing the technical <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d55288f8-ffbb-46a2-8a50-6bfaf4d511c5\" data-question=\"34\">details<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> of his program.</span></p><p><span><strong>F </strong> persuading the public to appreciate computer art.</span></p><p><span><strong>G </strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8709b13-5dfa-4553-bafa-6d4fc161859d\" data-question=\"36\">discovering that it was the product of a computer program<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"485\" id=\"question-wrapper-485\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Simon Colton says it is important to consider the long-term view when </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"486\" id=\"question-wrapper-486\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> David Cope’s EMI software surprised people by </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"487\" id=\"question-wrapper-487\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Geraint Wiggins <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4f42a2b-cfc9-4cc0-ab7d-fa8815a331f6\" data-question=\"34\">criticized<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> Cope for not </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"488\" id=\"question-wrapper-488\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Douglas Hofstadter claimed that EMI was </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"489\" id=\"question-wrapper-489\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Audiences who had listened to EMI’s music <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7a33969-44ca-4db2-b08a-a954ad04c8c6\" data-question=\"36\">became angry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> after </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"490\" id=\"question-wrapper-490\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The participants in David Moffat’s study had to assess music without </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>38-40</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"491\" id=\"question-wrapper-491\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Moffat’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6ffc582-96cb-4d02-a302-6e44c02c6473\" data-question=\"38\">research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1eec384a-778c-4a78-b730-bc0ae54636fc\" data-question=\"38\">may help explain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> people’s reactions to EMI. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"492\" id=\"question-wrapper-492\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The non-experts in Moffat’s study all responded in a predictable way. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"493\" id=\"question-wrapper-493\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Justin Kruger’s findings <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ad2ce571-a02e-43eb-88f6-a253eb7e601c\" data-question=\"40\">cast doubt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> on Paul Bloom’s theory about people’s prejudice towards computer art. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c3023e73-3762-4461-9e17-4ca5c134c0d9","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"great deal of progress","passagePhrase":"a growing number ... creates art that could not have been imagined"},{"uid":"0e75ce23-d360-4749-9eec-3cd58001372a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"computer-produced works","passagePhrase":"computer programs"},{"uid":"cae7c9bb-bcc3-4f06-80fe-cf3eeea90158","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"undermines","passagePhrase":"taking something special away"},{"uid":"aacc7b42-c729-400c-8140-71d59e4b789a","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"a fundamental human quality","passagePhrase":"what it means to be human"},{"uid":"d2dce3cd-d38c-4b6a-adb4-84857139eced","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"source of its subject matter","passagePhrase":"come up with its own concepts"},{"uid":"802c76e6-1304-486a-980d-b398a8965ce6","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"different criteria","passagePhrase":"double standards"},{"uid":"ac17f364-7876-4e1d-ac69-3f9221902068","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"a particularly striking effect","passagePhrase":"an eerie, ghostlike quality"},{"uid":"c9b56d55-d88b-473a-98e1-17d71fad3326","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"comparing the artistic achievements of humans and computers","passagePhrase":"measure machine creativity directly to that of humans"},{"uid":"a31fe974-1ab5-4fc6-9afb-7eb1fd23d0be","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"virtually indistinguishable from that of humans","passagePhrase":"fooled classical music experts into thinking they were hearing genuine Bach"},{"uid":"c4f42a2b-cfc9-4cc0-ab7d-fa8815a331f6","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"criticized","passagePhrase":"condemned"},{"uid":"d55288f8-ffbb-46a2-8a50-6bfaf4d511c5","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"details","passagePhrase":"explanation"},{"uid":"ee624c39-0718-4cdd-ad79-ec2c3c923b1d","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"producing work","passagePhrase":"created replicas"},{"uid":"54839b3f-0d13-4fb4-806e-b7809f02e736","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"entirely dependent on","passagePhrase":"rely completely on"},{"uid":"29ebcda8-4c0a-4975-acc0-e7c819a33a94","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"imagination of its creator","passagePhrase":"the original artist’s creative impulses"},{"uid":"c8709b13-5dfa-4553-bafa-6d4fc161859d","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"discovering that it was the product of a computer program","passagePhrase":"the truth"},{"uid":"c7a33969-44ca-4db2-b08a-a954ad04c8c6","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"became angry","passagePhrase":"outraged"},{"uid":"d6ffc582-96cb-4d02-a302-6e44c02c6473","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"research","passagePhrase":"study"},{"uid":"1eec384a-778c-4a78-b730-bc0ae54636fc","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"may help explain","passagePhrase":"provides a clue"},{"uid":"54b2b736-4de7-4794-b74e-cb141c8b49b0","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"knowing","passagePhrase":"told beforehand"},{"uid":"d5a946c1-cb21-468b-be3a-8163a49ea8b6","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"the work of humans or software","passagePhrase":"composed by humans or computers"}]},"reading_u2_226":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions</strong> <strong>1-13</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</p><p> </p><h2><strong>Bringing cinnamon to Europe</strong></h2><p>Cinnamon is a sweet, fragrant spice produced from the inner bark of trees of the genus Cinnamomum, which is native to the Indian sub-continent. It was known in biblical times, and is mentioned in several books of the Bible, both as an ingredient that was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbceb26b-7832-43d0-bb6d-b8d8d8ea4797\" data-question=\"1\">mixed with oils<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> for anointing people’s bodies, and also as a token <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03eac49c-f66a-45fe-8284-094c120f0f24\" data-question=\"2\">indicating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> friendship <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"29d74594-74fd-41f0-a6ba-ed18d2064e8a\" data-question=\"2\">among lovers and friends<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. In ancient Rome, mourners attending funerals burnt cinnamon to create a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"463ec587-e20e-4f58-a6f0-dc46ef5abbb4\" data-question=\"3\">pleasant scent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. Most often, however, the spice found its primary use as an additive to food and drink. In the Middle Ages, Europeans who could afford the spice used it to flavor food, particularly meat, and to impress those around them with their ability to purchase an expensive condiment from the ‘exotic’ East. At a banquet, a host would offer guests a plate with various spices piled upon it as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b142e931-3489-4ebf-b898-cd10271fc461\" data-question=\"4\">a sign of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the wealth at his or her disposal. Cinnamon was also reported to have health benefits, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b247f002-76c8-40fe-a62c-c63bd2a24375\" data-question=\"5\">was thought to cure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"768d6478-a703-46e7-95d4-b2f0610b8b47\" data-question=\"5\">various ailments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, such as indigestion.</p><p>Toward the end of the Middle Ages, the European middle classes began to desire the lifestyle of the elite, including their consumption of spices. This led to a growth in demand for cinnamon and other spices. At that time, cinnamon was transported by Arab merchants, who closely guarded the secret of the source of the spice from potential rivals. They took it from India, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc4a77f0-bc83-43a4-8461-3265ffbc9778\" data-question=\"6\">where it was grown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8bf9a155-d83e-4e83-b8b5-0c5f6126d96a\" data-question=\"7\">on camels via an overland route<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> to the Mediterranean. Their journey ended when they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e3d279f-dad1-4188-9c38-a46bfd8bf13c\" data-question=\"8\">reached<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> Alexandria. European traders sailed there to purchase their supply of cinnamon, then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eb5b9e6e-7ad6-42f2-b0bd-232868214f1b\" data-question=\"9\">brought it back to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> Venice. The spice then travelled from that great trading city to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10f7dfa8-3eef-4f47-b500-5d4af7294552\" data-question=\"9\">markets all around Europe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Because the overland trade route allowed for only small quantities of the spice to reach Europe, and because Venice had a virtual monopoly of the trade, the Venetians could set the price of cinnamon exorbitantly high. These prices, coupled with the increasing demand, spurred the search for new routes to Asia by Europeans eager to take part in the spice trade.</p><p>Seeking the high profits promised by the cinnamon market, Portuguese traders arrived on the island of Ceylon in the Indian Ocean toward the end of the 15th century. Before Europeans arrived on the island, the state had organized the cultivation of cinnamon. People belonging to the ethnic group called the Salagama would peel the bark off young shoots of the cinnamon plant in the rainy season, when the wet bark was more pliable. During the peeling process, they curled the bark into the ‘stick’ shape still associated with the spice today. The Salagama then gave the finished product to the king as a form of tribute. When the Portuguese arrived, they needed to increase production significantly, and so enslaved many other members of the Ceylonese native population, forcing them to work in cinnamon harvesting. In 1518, the Portuguese built a fort on Ceylon, which enabled them to protect the island, so helping them to develop <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"361c1a58-fd3a-493c-9785-7e58b4912537\" data-question=\"10\">a monopoly in the cinnamon trade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> and generate very high profits. In the late 16th century, for example, they enjoyed a tenfold profit when shipping cinnamon over a journey of eight days from Ceylon to India.</p><p>When the Dutch arrived off the coast of southern Asia at the very beginning of the 17th century, they set their sights on displacing the Portuguese as kings of cinnamon. The Dutch allied themselves with Kandy, an inland kingdom on Ceylon. In return for payments of elephants and cinnamon, they protected the native king from the Portuguese. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"b9fd3b6b-0d87-467e-a0de-3bf238087b0a\" data-question=\"11\">By 1649<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, the Dutch <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87ebaa67-b40f-4646-a81e-8f384e7f6ad3\" data-question=\"11\">broke the 150-year Portuguese monopoly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> when they overran and occupied their factories. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"b9fd3b6b-0d87-467e-a0de-3bf238087b0a\" data-question=\"11\">By 1658<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, they had permanently expelled the Portuguese from the island, thereby gaining control of the lucrative cinnamon trade.</p><p>In order to protect their hold on the market, the Dutch, like the Portuguese before them, treated the native inhabitants harshly. Because of the need to boost production and satisfy Europe’s ever-increasing appetite for cinnamon, the Dutch began to alter the harvesting practices of the Ceylonese. Over time, the supply of cinnamon trees on the island became nearly exhausted, due to systematic stripping of the bark. Eventually, the Dutch began cultivating their own cinnamon trees to supplement the diminishing number of wild trees available for use.</p><p>Then, in 1996, the English arrived on Ceylon, thereby displacing the Dutch from their control of the cinnamon monopoly. By the middle of the 19th century, production of cinnamon reached 1,000 tons a year, after a lower grade quality of the spice became acceptable to European tastes. By that time, cinnamon was being grown in other parts of the Indian Ocean region and in the West Indies, Brazil, and Guyana. Not only was a monopoly of cinnamon becoming impossible, but the spice trade overall was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0d460d6d-abff-4f5e-b7a4-132201f31c3d\" data-question=\"13\">diminishing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e46243ec-12e2-409f-8803-a90c6a5bf084\" data-question=\"13\">economic potential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, and was eventually superseded by the rise of trade in coffee, tea, chocolate, and sugar.</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>1-9</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>The Early History of Cinnamon</strong></span></p><table><tbody><tr><td width=\"186\"><p><span><strong>Biblical times:</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"438\"><p><span>added to <strong>1</strong>………………………..</span></p><p><span>used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03eac49c-f66a-45fe-8284-094c120f0f24\" data-question=\"2\">show<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <strong>2</strong>…………………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"29d74594-74fd-41f0-a6ba-ed18d2064e8a\" data-question=\"2\">Between people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"186\"><p><span><strong>Ancient Rome:</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"438\"><p><span>used for its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"463ec587-e20e-4f58-a6f0-dc46ef5abbb4\" data-question=\"3\">sweet smell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> at <strong>3</strong>………………………..</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"186\"><p><span><strong>Middle Ages:</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"438\"><p><span>added to food, especially meat</span></p><p><span>was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b142e931-3489-4ebf-b898-cd10271fc461\" data-question=\"4\">an indication of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> a person’s <strong>4</strong>………………………..</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b247f002-76c8-40fe-a62c-c63bd2a24375\" data-question=\"5\">known as a treatment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> for <strong>5</strong>……………………….. and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"768d6478-a703-46e7-95d4-b2f0610b8b47\" data-question=\"5\">other health problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p><p><span>grown in <strong>6</strong>……………………….</span></p><p><span>merchants used <strong>7</strong>……………………… to bring it to the Mediterranean</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e3d279f-dad1-4188-9c38-a46bfd8bf13c\" data-question=\"8\">arrived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in the Mediterranean at <strong>8</strong>……………………………</span></p><p><span>traders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eb5b9e6e-7ad6-42f2-b0bd-232868214f1b\" data-question=\"9\">took it to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <strong>9</strong>……………………………. and sold it to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10f7dfa8-3eef-4f47-b500-5d4af7294552\" data-question=\"9\">destinations around Europe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"494\" id=\"question-wrapper-494\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OILS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"495\" id=\"question-wrapper-495\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FRIENDSHIP</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"496\" id=\"question-wrapper-496\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FUNERALS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"497\" id=\"question-wrapper-497\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WEALTH</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"498\" id=\"question-wrapper-498\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INDIGESTION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"499\" id=\"question-wrapper-499\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INDIA</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"500\" id=\"question-wrapper-500\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CAMELS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"501\" id=\"question-wrapper-501\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ALEXANDRIA</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"502\" id=\"question-wrapper-502\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VENICE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>10-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"503\" id=\"question-wrapper-503\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Portuguese had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"361c1a58-fd3a-493c-9785-7e58b4912537\" data-question=\"10\">control over the cinnamon trade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> in Ceylon throughout the 16th century. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"504\" id=\"question-wrapper-504\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Dutch <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87ebaa67-b40f-4646-a81e-8f384e7f6ad3\" data-question=\"11\">took over the cinnamon trade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> from the Portuguese <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"b9fd3b6b-0d87-467e-a0de-3bf238087b0a\" data-question=\"11\">as soon as they arrived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in Ceylon. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"505\" id=\"question-wrapper-505\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The trees planted by the Dutch produced larger quantities of cinnamon than the wild trees. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"506\" id=\"question-wrapper-506\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The spice trade <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0d460d6d-abff-4f5e-b7a4-132201f31c3d\" data-question=\"13\">maintained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e46243ec-12e2-409f-8803-a90c6a5bf084\" data-question=\"13\">economic importance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> during the 19th century. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"bbceb26b-7832-43d0-bb6d-b8d8d8ea4797","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"mixed with oils"},{"uid":"03eac49c-f66a-45fe-8284-094c120f0f24","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"show","passagePhrase":"indicating"},{"uid":"29d74594-74fd-41f0-a6ba-ed18d2064e8a","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Between people","passagePhrase":"among lovers and friends"},{"uid":"463ec587-e20e-4f58-a6f0-dc46ef5abbb4","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"sweet smell","passagePhrase":"pleasant scent"},{"uid":"b142e931-3489-4ebf-b898-cd10271fc461","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"an indication of","passagePhrase":"a sign of"},{"uid":"b247f002-76c8-40fe-a62c-c63bd2a24375","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"known as a treatment","passagePhrase":"was thought to cure"},{"uid":"768d6478-a703-46e7-95d4-b2f0610b8b47","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"other health problems","passagePhrase":"various ailments"},{"uid":"dc4a77f0-bc83-43a4-8461-3265ffbc9778","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"where it was grown"},{"uid":"8bf9a155-d83e-4e83-b8b5-0c5f6126d96a","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"on camels via an overland route"},{"uid":"8e3d279f-dad1-4188-9c38-a46bfd8bf13c","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"arrived","passagePhrase":"reached"},{"uid":"eb5b9e6e-7ad6-42f2-b0bd-232868214f1b","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"took it to","passagePhrase":"brought it back to"},{"uid":"10f7dfa8-3eef-4f47-b500-5d4af7294552","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"destinations around Europe","passagePhrase":"markets all around Europe"},{"uid":"361c1a58-fd3a-493c-9785-7e58b4912537","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"control over the cinnamon trade","passagePhrase":"a monopoly in the cinnamon trade"},{"uid":"87ebaa67-b40f-4646-a81e-8f384e7f6ad3","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"took over the cinnamon trade","passagePhrase":"broke the 150-year Portuguese monopoly"},{"uid":"e46243ec-12e2-409f-8803-a90c6a5bf084","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"economic importance","passagePhrase":"economic potential"}]},"reading_u2_227":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Oxytocin</strong></span></h2><h3><span><em>The positive and negative effects of the chemical known as the ‘love hormone’</em></span></h3><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>Oxytocin is a chemical, a hormone produced in the pituitary gland in the brain. It was through various studies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bdb888a5-ac9b-471b-9268-a15238eee335\" data-question=\"21\">focusing on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> animals that scientists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"75a14e5b-a081-4386-9b2e-e818958bb9bb\" data-question=\"21\">first<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> became aware of the influence of oxytocin. They discovered that it helps reinforce the bonds between prairie voles, which mate for life, and triggers the motherly behaviour that sheep show towards their newborn lambs. It is also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70ad7142-35bd-48ab-bd39-a391a7719337\" data-question=\"22\">released<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> by women in childbirth, strengthening the attachment between mother and baby. Few chemicals have as positive a reputation as oxytocin, which is sometimes referred to as the ‘love hormone’. One sniff of it can, it is claimed, make a person more trusting, empathetic, generous and cooperative. It is time, however, to revise this wholly optimistic view. A new wave of studies has shown that its effects vary greatly depending on the person and the circumstances, and it can impact on our social interactions for worse as well as for better.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Oxytocin’s role in human behaviour first emerged in 2005. In a groundbreaking experiments, Markus Heinrichs and his colleagues at the University of Freiburg, Germany, asked volunteers to do an activity in which they could invest money with an anonymous person who was not guaranteed to be honest. The team found the participants who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b40feb9-0123-48fe-8c62-a566c08d575a\" data-question=\"23\">had sniffed oxytocin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> via a nasal spray beforehand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0395f51c-b74f-4f4b-b6dd-bc1339861526\" data-question=\"18\">invested more money<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> than those who received a placebo instead. The study was the start of research into the effects of oxytocin on human interactions. ‘For eight years, it was quite a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b674060a-14dc-4d78-832e-53f507c2fc51\" data-question=\"16\">lonesome field<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>,’ Heinrichs recalls. ‘Now, everyone is interested.’ These follow-up studies have shown that after a sniff of the hormone, people become more charitable, better at reading emotions on others’ faces and at communicating constructively in arguments. Together, the results fuelled the view that oxytocin universally enhanced the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62f508d9-1343-4c98-b037-dbc2d2aef987\" data-question=\"14\">positive aspects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of our social nature.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Then, after a few years, contrasting findings began to emerge. Simone Shamay-Tsoory at the at the University of Haifa, Israel, found that when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4592f7f9-b0d2-4550-9c97-507aab568602\" data-question=\"24\">volunteers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9460064-132d-44ff-ab8b-7b670418c215\" data-question=\"24\">played<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> a competitive game, those who inhaled the hormone showed more pleasure when they beat other players, and felt more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"231f3ba2-8668-4b73-bcb9-473b815cc7a0\" data-question=\"19\">envy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> when others won. What’s more, administering oxytocin also has sharply contrasting outcomes depending on a person’s disposition. Jennifer Bartz from Mount Sinai School of Medicine, New York, found that it improves people’s ability to read emotions, but only if they are not very socially adept to begin with. Her research also shows that oxytocin in fact reduces cooperation in subjects who are particularly anxious or sensitive to rejection.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>Another discovery is that oxytocin’s effects vary depending on who we are interacting with. Studies conducted by Carolyn DeClerck of the University of Antwerp, Belgium, revealed that people who had received a dose of oxytocin actually became <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"97b469d0-9335-4d40-aa69-abda6d18dcba\" data-question=\"25\">less cooperative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> when dealing with complete strangers. Meanwhile, Carsten De Dreu at the University of Amsterdam in the Netherlands discovered that volunteers given oxytocin showed favouritism: Dutch men became quicker to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1fda5ec3-1760-4577-b49e-f1ffccf1adba\" data-question=\"26\">associate positive words<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> with Dutch names than with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"76a413bc-27c5-401c-84f7-513ba217cca6\" data-question=\"26\">foreign ones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, for example. According to De Dreu, oxytocin drives people to care for those in their social circles and defend them from outside dangers. So, it appears that oxytocin strengthens biases, rather than promoting general goodwill, as was previously thought.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>There were signs of these subtleties from the start. Bartz has recently shown that in almost half of the existing research results, oxytocin influenced only certain individuals or in certain circumstances. Where once researchers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac85d006-a3f1-4dce-96c5-66e8f063771b\" data-question=\"17\">took no notice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of such findings, now a more nuanced understanding of oxytocin’s effects is propelling investigations down new lines. To Bartz, the key to understanding what the hormone does lies in pinpointing its core function rather than in cataloguing its seemingly endless effects. There are several hypotheses which are not mutually exclusive. Oxytocin could help to reduce anxiety and fear. Or it could simply motivate people to seek out social connections. She believes that oxytocin acts as a chemical spotlight that shines on social clues – a shift in posture, a flicker of the eyes, a dip in the voice – making people more attuned to their social environment. This would explain why it makes us more likely to look others in the eye and improves our ability to identify emotions. But it could also make things worse for people who are overly sensitive or prone to interpreting social cues in the worst light.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>Perhaps we should not be surprised that the oxytocin story has become more perplexing. The hormone is found in everything from octopuses to sheep, and its evolutionary roots stretch back half a billion years. ‘It’s a very simple and ancient molecule that has been co-opted for many different functions,’ says Sue Carter at the University of Illinois, Chicago, USA. ‘It affects primitive parts of the brain like the amygdala, so <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c1c5e19-f0bf-4c7e-8d05-5b875453ea17\" data-question=\"15\">it’s going to have many effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> on just about everything.’ Bartz agrees. ‘Oxytocin probably does some very basic things, but once you add our higher-order thinking and social situations, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36fc7ff8-2fd7-4f55-a627-872847cf97a9\" data-question=\"20\">these basic processes could manifest in different ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> depending on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0fe2429f-4e01-4c76-a21c-a00c86c79096\" data-question=\"20\">individual differences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and context.’</span></p><p><span> </span><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six section, <strong>A-F</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-17</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"507\" id=\"question-wrapper-507\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to research showing the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62f508d9-1343-4c98-b037-dbc2d2aef987\" data-question=\"14\">beneficial effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of oxytocin on people </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"508\" id=\"question-wrapper-508\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reasons why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c1c5e19-f0bf-4c7e-8d05-5b875453ea17\" data-question=\"15\">the effects of oxytocin are complex<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"509\" id=\"question-wrapper-509\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of a period in which oxytocin <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b674060a-14dc-4d78-832e-53f507c2fc51\" data-question=\"16\">attracted little scientific attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"510\" id=\"question-wrapper-510\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac85d006-a3f1-4dce-96c5-66e8f063771b\" data-question=\"17\">ignoring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> certain aspects of their research data </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following research findings (Questions <strong>18-20</strong>) and the list of researchers below.</span></p><p><span>Match each research finding with the correct researcher, <strong>A-F</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>18-20</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Researchers</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Markus Heinrichs<br></span><span><strong>B</strong> Simone Shamay-Tsoory<br></span><span><strong>C</strong> Jennifer Bartz<br></span><span><strong>D</strong> Carolyn DeClerck<br></span><span><strong>E</strong> Carsten De Dreu<br></span><span><strong>F</strong> Sue Carter</span><span> </span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"511\" id=\"question-wrapper-511\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0395f51c-b74f-4f4b-b6dd-bc1339861526\" data-question=\"18\">are more trusting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> when affected by oxytocin. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"512\" id=\"question-wrapper-512\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Oxytocin increases people’s feelings of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"231f3ba2-8668-4b73-bcb9-473b815cc7a0\" data-question=\"19\">jealousy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"513\" id=\"question-wrapper-513\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36fc7ff8-2fd7-4f55-a627-872847cf97a9\" data-question=\"20\">The effect of oxytocin varies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0fe2429f-4e01-4c76-a21c-a00c86c79096\" data-question=\"20\">one type of person to another<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes <strong>21-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p><h3><span><strong>Oxytocin research</strong></span></h3><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"75a14e5b-a081-4386-9b2e-e818958bb9bb\" data-question=\"21\">The earliest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> findings about oxytocin and bonding came from research <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bdb888a5-ac9b-471b-9268-a15238eee335\" data-question=\"21\">involving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <strong>21</strong>……………………….. It was also discovered that humans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70ad7142-35bd-48ab-bd39-a391a7719337\" data-question=\"22\">produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> oxytocin during <strong>22</strong>………………………… An experiment in 2005, in which participants were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b40feb9-0123-48fe-8c62-a566c08d575a\" data-question=\"23\">given either oxytocin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> or a <strong>23</strong>…………………………, reinforced the belief that the hormone had a positive effect.</span></p><p><span>However, later research suggests that this is not always the case. A study at the University of Haifa where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4592f7f9-b0d2-4550-9c97-507aab568602\" data-question=\"24\">participants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9460064-132d-44ff-ab8b-7b670418c215\" data-question=\"24\">took part in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> a <strong>24</strong>……………………….. revealed the negative emotions which oxytocin can trigger. A study at the University of Antwerp showed people’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"97b469d0-9335-4d40-aa69-abda6d18dcba\" data-question=\"25\">lack of willingness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to help <strong>25</strong>………………………. while under the influence of oxytocin. Meanwhile, research at the University of Amsterdam revealed that people who have been given oxytocin consider <strong>26</strong>……………………….. that are familiar to them in their own country to have more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1fda5ec3-1760-4577-b49e-f1ffccf1adba\" data-question=\"26\">positive associations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"76a413bc-27c5-401c-84f7-513ba217cca6\" data-question=\"26\">those from other cultures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"514\" id=\"question-wrapper-514\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ANIMALS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"515\" id=\"question-wrapper-515\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CHILDBIRTH</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"516\" id=\"question-wrapper-516\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PLACEBO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"517\" id=\"question-wrapper-517\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GAME</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"518\" id=\"question-wrapper-518\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STRANGERS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"519\" id=\"question-wrapper-519\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NAMES</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"bdb888a5-ac9b-471b-9268-a15238eee335","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"involving","passagePhrase":"focusing on"},{"uid":"75a14e5b-a081-4386-9b2e-e818958bb9bb","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"The earliest","passagePhrase":"first"},{"uid":"70ad7142-35bd-48ab-bd39-a391a7719337","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"produce","passagePhrase":"released"},{"uid":"1b40feb9-0123-48fe-8c62-a566c08d575a","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"given either oxytocin","passagePhrase":"had sniffed oxytocin"},{"uid":"0395f51c-b74f-4f4b-b6dd-bc1339861526","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"are more trusting","passagePhrase":"invested more money"},{"uid":"b674060a-14dc-4d78-832e-53f507c2fc51","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"attracted little scientific attention","passagePhrase":"lonesome field"},{"uid":"62f508d9-1343-4c98-b037-dbc2d2aef987","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"beneficial effects","passagePhrase":"positive aspects"},{"uid":"4592f7f9-b0d2-4550-9c97-507aab568602","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"participants","passagePhrase":"volunteers"},{"uid":"e9460064-132d-44ff-ab8b-7b670418c215","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"took part in","passagePhrase":"played"},{"uid":"231f3ba2-8668-4b73-bcb9-473b815cc7a0","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"jealousy","passagePhrase":"envy"},{"uid":"97b469d0-9335-4d40-aa69-abda6d18dcba","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"lack of willingness","passagePhrase":"less cooperative"},{"uid":"1fda5ec3-1760-4577-b49e-f1ffccf1adba","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"positive associations","passagePhrase":"associate positive words"},{"uid":"76a413bc-27c5-401c-84f7-513ba217cca6","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"those from other cultures","passagePhrase":"foreign ones"},{"uid":"ac85d006-a3f1-4dce-96c5-66e8f063771b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"ignoring","passagePhrase":"took no notice"},{"uid":"8c1c5e19-f0bf-4c7e-8d05-5b875453ea17","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the effects of oxytocin are complex","passagePhrase":"it’s going to have many effects"},{"uid":"36fc7ff8-2fd7-4f55-a627-872847cf97a9","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"The effect of oxytocin varies","passagePhrase":"these basic processes could manifest in different ways"},{"uid":"0fe2429f-4e01-4c76-a21c-a00c86c79096","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"one type of person to another","passagePhrase":"individual differences"}]},"reading_u2_228":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>MAKING THE MOST OF TRENDS</strong></span></h2><h3><span><em>Experts from Harvard Business School give advice to managers</em></span></h3><p><span>Most managers can identify the major trends of the day. But in the course of conducting research in a number of industries and working directly with companies, we have discovered that managers often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b7988e8-99e7-40be-895e-8b19c6c180b7\" data-question=\"27\">fail to recognize<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the less obvious but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b94b860-2093-41b7-8a3c-760bdc283279\" data-question=\"27\">profound ways these trends are influencing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"42511e90-6dc4-46f3-92bd-455a7ec43230\" data-question=\"27\">consumers’ aspirations, attitudes, and behaviors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. This is especially true of trends that managers view as peripheral to their core markets.</span></p><p><span>Many ignore trends in their innovation strategies or adopt a wait-and-see approach and let competitors take the lead. At a minimum, such responses mean missed profit opportunities. At the extreme, they can jeopardize a company by ceding to rivals the opportunity to transform the industry. The purpose of this article is twofold: to spur managers to think more expansively about how trends could engender new value propositions in their core markets, and to provide some high-level advice on how to make market research and product development personnel more adept at analyzing and exploiting trends.</span></p><p><span>One strategy, known as ‘infuse and augment’, is to design a product or service that retains most of the attributes and functions of existing products in the category but adds others that address the needs and desires unleashed by a major trend. A case in point in the Poppy range of handbags, which the firm Coach created in response to the economic downturn of 2008. The Coach brand had been a symbol of opulence and luxury for nearly 70 years, and the most obvious reaction to the downturn would have been to lower prices. However, that would have risked cheapening the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d84cfe72-fecc-45e9-9590-c65d821e6222\" data-question=\"28\">brand’s image<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. Instead, they initiated a consumer-research project which revealed that customers were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d9f6fa47-9143-4445-aaf5-ac171c59b33e\" data-question=\"35\">eager<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> to lift themselves and the country out of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03369bc0-039c-4028-93bb-5d270ff5923b\" data-question=\"35\">tough times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Using these insights, Coach launched the lower-priced Poppy handbags, which were in vibrant colors, and looked more youthful and playful than conventional Coach products. Creating the sub-brand allowed Coach to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"443b9d3e-3901-4f83-97b4-de964cdabde0\" data-question=\"37\">avert<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> an across-the-board <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eead0857-f99a-4149-abeb-8bcc4d72bda2\" data-question=\"37\">price cut<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. In contrast to the many companies that responded to the recession by cutting prices, Coach saw the new consumer mindset as an opportunity for innovation and renewal.</span></p><p><span>A further example of this strategy was supermarket Tesco’s response to consumers’ growing concerns about the environment. With that in mind, Tesco, one of the world’s top five retailers, introduced its Greener Living program, which demonstrates the company’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d3bbd10a-cf9c-41ea-9baa-b64b60e7980e\" data-question=\"34\">commitment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> to protecting the environment by involving consumers in ways that produce tangible results. For example, Tesco customers can accumulate points for such activities as reusing bags, recycling cans and printer cartridges, and buying home-insulation materials. Like points earned on regular purchases, these green points can be redeemed for cash. Tesco has not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7e34368-7a72-4995-83ec-1b23dc62be44\" data-question=\"29\">abandoned its traditional retail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> offering but augmented its business with these innovations, thereby infusing its value proposition with a green streak.</span></p><p><span>A more radical strategy is ‘combine and transcend’. This entails combining aspects of the product’s existing value proposition with attributes addressing changes arising from a trend, to create a novel experience – one that may land the company in an entirely new market space. At first glance, spending resources to incorporate elements of a seemingly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0bbf877e-cbd1-44f3-afc2-d180ff0f784c\" data-question=\"36\">irrelevant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> trend into one’s core offerings sounds like it’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8987cc71-a620-4c82-8c30-d1f9e40c003c\" data-question=\"30\">hardly worthwhile<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. But consider Nike’s move to integrate the digital revolution into its reputation for high-performance athletic footwear. In 2006, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"58783bf7-3a32-4fc1-afa7-4b078cabf089\" data-question=\"33\">teamed up with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> technology company Apple to launch Nike+, a digital sports kit comprising a sensor that attaches to the running shoe and a wireless receiver that connects to the user’s iPod. By combining Nike’s original value proposition for amateur athletes with one for digital consumers, the Nike+ sports kit and web interface moved the company from a focus on athletic apparel to a new plane of engagement with its customers.</span></p><p><span>A third approach, known as ‘counteract and reaffirm’, involves developing products or services that stress the values traditionally associated with the category in ways that allow consumers to oppose – or at least temporarily escape from – the aspects of trends they view as undesirable. A product that accomplished this is the ME2, a video game created by Canada’s iToys. By reaffirming the toy category’s association with physical play, the ME2 counteracted some of the widely perceived <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4dc22a91-e9aa-4aa2-a1e8-8488d3366161\" data-question=\"32\">negative impacts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of digital gaming devices. Like other handheld games, the device featured a host of exciting interactive games, a full-color LCD screen, and advanced 3D graphics. What set it apart was that it incorporated the traditional physical component of children’s play: it contained a pedometer, which tracked and awarded points for physical activity (walking, running, biking, skateboarding, climbing stairs). The child could use the points to enhance various virtual skills needed for the video game. The ME2, introduced in mid-2008, catered to kids’ huge desire to play video games while countering the negatives, such as associations with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a262043-cfff-4a1d-a565-164142bf74b7\" data-question=\"31\">lack of exercise and obesity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Once you have gained perspective on how trend-related changes in consumer opinions and behaviors impact on your category, you can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12de9ef3-2a2b-40f2-b5a5-543e38839aad\" data-question=\"38\">determine which of our three<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> innovation strategies to pursue. When your category’s basic value proposition continues to be meaningful for consumers influenced by the trend, the infuse-and-augment strategy will allow you to reinvigorate the category. If analysis reveals an increasing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9634c549-c9a7-4caa-a258-b3e334d46ca1\" data-question=\"40\">disparity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> between your category and consumers’ new focus, your innovations need to transcend the category to integrate the two worlds. Finally, if aspects of the category clash with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e94f22c-deb8-4658-9b15-a12565d94dab\" data-question=\"39\">undesired outcomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of a trend, such as associations with unhealthy lifestyles, there is an opportunity to counteract those changes by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87635597-fa8c-42c1-bf44-f547c2b6e660\" data-question=\"39\">reaffirming the core values of your category<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Trends – technological, economic, environmental, social, or political – that affect how people perceive the world around them and shape what they expect from products and services present firms with unique opportunities for growth.</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"520\" id=\"question-wrapper-520\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the first paragraph, the writer says that most managers </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. fail to spot the key consumer trends of the moment.</li> <li>B. make the mistake of focusing only on the principal consumer trends.</li> <li>C. misinterpret market research data relating to current consumer trends.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b7988e8-99e7-40be-895e-8b19c6c180b7\" data-question=\"27\">are unaware of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b94b860-2093-41b7-8a3c-760bdc283279\" data-question=\"27\">significant impact that trends have on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"42511e90-6dc4-46f3-92bd-455a7ec43230\" data-question=\"27\">consumers’ lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"521\" id=\"question-wrapper-521\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the third paragraph, Coach was anxious to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. follow what some of its competitors were doing.</li> <li>B. maintain its prices throughout its range.</li> <li>C. safeguard its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d84cfe72-fecc-45e9-9590-c65d821e6222\" data-question=\"28\">reputation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> as a manufacturer of luxury goods.</li> <li>D. modify the entire look of its brand to suit the economic climate.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"522\" id=\"question-wrapper-522\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point is made about Tesco’s Greener Living programme? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It did not require Tesco to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7e34368-7a72-4995-83ec-1b23dc62be44\" data-question=\"29\">modify its core business activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>B. It succeeded in attracting a more eco-conscious slientele.</li> <li>C. Its main aim was to raise consumers’ awareness of environmental issues.</li> <li>D. It was not the first time that Tesco had implemented such an initiative.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"523\" id=\"question-wrapper-523\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer suggest about Nike’s strategy? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It was an extremely risky strategy at the time.</li> <li>B. It was a strategy that only a major company could afford to follow.</li> <li>C. It was the type of strategy that would not have been possible in the past.</li> <li>D. It was the kind of strategy which might appear to have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8987cc71-a620-4c82-8c30-d1f9e40c003c\" data-question=\"30\">few obvious benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"524\" id=\"question-wrapper-524\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What was original about the ME2? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It contained technology that had been developed for the sports industry.</li> <li>B. It appealed to young people who were keen to improve their physical fitness.</li> <li>C. It took advantage of a current trend for video games with colourful 3D graphic.</li> <li>D. It was a handheld game that addressed people’s concerns about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a262043-cfff-4a1d-a565-164142bf74b7\" data-question=\"31\">unhealthy lifestyles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions <strong>32-37</strong>) and the list of companies below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct company, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or<strong> D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or<strong> D</strong>, in boxes<strong> 32-37</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of companies</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Coach<br></span><span><strong>B</strong> Tesco<br></span><span><strong>C</strong> Nike<br></span><span><strong>D</strong> iToys</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"525\" id=\"question-wrapper-525\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It turned the notion that its products could have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4dc22a91-e9aa-4aa2-a1e8-8488d3366161\" data-question=\"32\">harmful effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to its own advantage. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"526\" id=\"question-wrapper-526\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It extended its offering by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"58783bf7-3a32-4fc1-afa7-4b078cabf089\" data-question=\"33\">collaborating with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> another manufacturer. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"527\" id=\"question-wrapper-527\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It implemented an incentive scheme to demonstrate its corporate social <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d3bbd10a-cf9c-41ea-9baa-b64b60e7980e\" data-question=\"34\">responsibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"528\" id=\"question-wrapper-528\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It discovered that customers had a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d9f6fa47-9143-4445-aaf5-ac171c59b33e\" data-question=\"35\">positive attitude<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> towards dealing with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03369bc0-039c-4028-93bb-5d270ff5923b\" data-question=\"35\">difficult circumstances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"529\" id=\"question-wrapper-529\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It responded to a growing lifestyle trend in an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0bbf877e-cbd1-44f3-afc2-d180ff0f784c\" data-question=\"36\">unrelated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> product sector. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"530\" id=\"question-wrapper-530\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It successfully <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"443b9d3e-3901-4f83-97b4-de964cdabde0\" data-question=\"37\">avoided<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> having to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eead0857-f99a-4149-abeb-8bcc4d72bda2\" data-question=\"37\">charge its customers less<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> for its core products. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong> below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or<strong> D</strong>, in boxes <strong>38-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> employ a combination of strategies to maintain your consumer base.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12de9ef3-2a2b-40f2-b5a5-543e38839aad\" data-question=\"38\">identify the most appropriate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> innovation strategy to use.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87635597-fa8c-42c1-bf44-f547c2b6e660\" data-question=\"39\">emphasise your brand’s traditional values<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> with the counteract-and-affirm strategy.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> use the combine-and-transcend strategy to integrate the two worlds.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"531\" id=\"question-wrapper-531\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> If there are any trend-related changes impacting on your category, you should </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"532\" id=\"question-wrapper-532\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> If a current trend highlights a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e94f22c-deb8-4658-9b15-a12565d94dab\" data-question=\"39\">negative aspect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of your category, you should </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"533\" id=\"question-wrapper-533\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> If the consumers’ new focus has an increasing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9634c549-c9a7-4caa-a258-b3e334d46ca1\" data-question=\"40\">lack of connection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> with your offering you should </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0b7988e8-99e7-40be-895e-8b19c6c180b7","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"are unaware of","passagePhrase":"fail to recognize"},{"uid":"0b94b860-2093-41b7-8a3c-760bdc283279","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"significant impact that trends have on","passagePhrase":"profound ways these trends are influencing"},{"uid":"42511e90-6dc4-46f3-92bd-455a7ec43230","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"consumers’ lives","passagePhrase":"consumers’ aspirations, attitudes, and behaviors"},{"uid":"d84cfe72-fecc-45e9-9590-c65d821e6222","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"reputation","passagePhrase":"brand’s image"},{"uid":"d9f6fa47-9143-4445-aaf5-ac171c59b33e","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"positive attitude","passagePhrase":"eager"},{"uid":"03369bc0-039c-4028-93bb-5d270ff5923b","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"difficult circumstances","passagePhrase":"tough times"},{"uid":"443b9d3e-3901-4f83-97b4-de964cdabde0","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"avoided","passagePhrase":"avert"},{"uid":"eead0857-f99a-4149-abeb-8bcc4d72bda2","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"charge its customers less","passagePhrase":"price cut"},{"uid":"d3bbd10a-cf9c-41ea-9baa-b64b60e7980e","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"responsibility","passagePhrase":"commitment"},{"uid":"c7e34368-7a72-4995-83ec-1b23dc62be44","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"modify its core business activities","passagePhrase":"abandoned its traditional retail"},{"uid":"0bbf877e-cbd1-44f3-afc2-d180ff0f784c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"unrelated","passagePhrase":"irrelevant"},{"uid":"8987cc71-a620-4c82-8c30-d1f9e40c003c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"few obvious benefits","passagePhrase":"hardly worthwhile"},{"uid":"58783bf7-3a32-4fc1-afa7-4b078cabf089","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"collaborating with","passagePhrase":"teamed up with"},{"uid":"4dc22a91-e9aa-4aa2-a1e8-8488d3366161","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"harmful effects","passagePhrase":"negative impacts"},{"uid":"1a262043-cfff-4a1d-a565-164142bf74b7","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"unhealthy lifestyles","passagePhrase":"lack of exercise and obesity"},{"uid":"12de9ef3-2a2b-40f2-b5a5-543e38839aad","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"identify the most appropriate","passagePhrase":"determine which of our three"},{"uid":"9634c549-c9a7-4caa-a258-b3e334d46ca1","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"lack of connection","passagePhrase":"disparity"},{"uid":"2e94f22c-deb8-4658-9b15-a12565d94dab","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"negative aspect","passagePhrase":"undesired outcomes"},{"uid":"87635597-fa8c-42c1-bf44-f547c2b6e660","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"emphasise your brand’s traditional values","passagePhrase":"reaffirming the core values of your category"}]},"reading_u2_229":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong>The coconut palm</strong></span></h2><p><span>For millennia, the coconut has been central to the lives of Polynesian and Asian peoples. In the western world, on the other hand, coconuts have always been exotic and unusual, sometimes rare. The Italian merchant traveller Marco Polo apparently saw coconuts in South Asia in the late 13th century, and among the mid-14th-century travel writings of Sir John Mandeville there is mention of ‘great Notes of Ynde’ (great Nuts of India). Today, images of palm-fringed tropical beaches are clichés in the west to sell holidays, chocolate bars, fizzy drinks and even romance.</span></p><p><span>Typically, we envisage coconuts as brown cannonballs that, when opened, provide sweet white flesh. But we see only part of the fruit and none of the plant from which they come. The coconut palm has a smooth, slender, grey trunk, up to 30 metres tall. This is an important source of timber for building houses, and is increasingly being used as a replacement for endangered hardwoods in the furniture <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c841ff64-e92f-421e-b5c9-b8ca30b4518c\" data-question=\"1\">construction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> industry. The trunk is surmounted by a rosette of leaves, each of which may be up to six metres long. The leaves have hard veins in their centres which, in many parts of the world, are used as brushes after the green part of the leaf has been stripped away. Immature coconut flowers are tightly clustered together among the leaves at the top of the trunk. The flower stems may be tapped for their sap to produce a drink, and the sap can also be reduced by boiling to produce <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87d679ab-07db-4813-bf5e-67bb158de604\" data-question=\"2\">a type of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> sugar used for cooking.</span></p><p><span>Coconut palms produce as many as seventy fruits per year, weighing more than a kilogram each. The wall of the fruit has three layers: a waterproof outer layer, a fibrous middle layer and a hard, inner layer. The thick fibrous middle layer produces coconut fibre, ‘coir’, which has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe90084a-abc5-443a-8e4e-d3d23ce5a798\" data-question=\"3\">numerous uses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and is particularly important in manufacturing ropes. The woody innermost layer, the shell, with its three prominent ‘eyes’, surrounds the seed. An important product obtained from the shell is charcoal, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d46ed38a-cca0-4ae4-918e-e76ea380cc0b\" data-question=\"4\">is widely used in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> various industries as well as in the home as a cooking fuel. When <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0cb52916-71f3-41e4-81b6-fc3c8723913f\" data-question=\"5\">broken in half<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, the shells are also used as bowls in many parts of Asia.</span></p><p><span>Inside the shell are the nutrients (endosperm) needed by the developing seed. Initially, the endosperm is a sweetish liquid, coconut water, which is enjoyed as a drink, but also provides the hormones which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b433049f-8bf2-49be-ba88-3326d62fa8a1\" data-question=\"6\">encourage other plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> to grow more rapidly and produce higher yields. As the fruit matures, the coconut water gradually solidifies to form the brilliant white, fat-rich, edible flesh or meat. Dried coconut flesh, ‘copra’, is made into coconut oil and coconut milk, which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b46278bb-3307-446c-a2d9-49daf56018b6\" data-question=\"7\">widely used in cooking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in different parts of the world, as well as in cosmetics. A derivative of coconut fat, glycerine, acquired strategic importance in a quite different sphere, as Alfred Nobel introduced the world to his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a79760a-60ab-4bcd-a353-6ccf8e65cc46\" data-question=\"8\">nitroglycerine-based invention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>: dynamite.</span></p><p><span>Their biology would appear to make coconuts the great maritime voyagers and coastal colonizers of the plant world. The large, energy-rich fruits are able to float in water and tolerate salt, but cannot remain viable indefinitely; studies suggest after about 110 days at sea they are no longer able to germinate. Literally cast onto desert island shores, with little more than sand to grow in and exposed to the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"37b49029-42cd-4956-b91c-49f4e8c71e5f\" data-question=\"9\">full glare of the tropical sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, coconut seeds are able to germinate and root. The air pocket in the seed, created as the endosperm solidifies, protects the embryo. In addition, the fibrous fruit wall that helped it to float during the voyage stores moisture that can be taken up by the roots of the coconut seedling as it starts to grow.</span></p><p><span>There have been centuries of academic debate over the origins of the coconut. There were no coconut palms in West Africa, the Caribbean or the east coast of the Americans before the voyages of the European explorers Vasco da Gama and Columbus in the late 15th and early 16th centuries. 16th century trade and human migration patterns reveal that Arab traders and European sailors are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c9ccc339-8563-4269-9c8b-80bbf63255af\" data-question=\"10\">likely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f45bb253-b75c-4006-bc6d-465b1f89359a\" data-question=\"10\">moved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> coconuts from South and Southeast Asia to Africa and then across the Atlantic to the east coast of America. But the origin of coconuts discovered along the west coast of America by 16th century sailors has been the subject of centuries of discussion. Two diametrically opposed origins have been proposed: that they came from Asia, or that they were native to America. Both suggestions have problems. In Asia, there is a large degree of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"081694cb-76db-4098-9917-771a8d061add\" data-question=\"12\">coconut diversity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> and evidence of millennia of human use – but there are no relatives growing in the wild. In America, there are close coconut relatives, but no evidence that coconuts are indigenous. These problems have led to the intriguing suggestion that coconuts originated on coral islands in the Pacific and were dispersed from there.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the table below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>1-8</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"3\" width=\"600\"><p><span><strong>THE COCONUT PALM</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"90\"><p><span><strong>Part</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"198\"><p><span><strong>Description</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span><strong>Uses</strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"90\"><p><span><strong>trunk</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"198\"><p><span>up to 30 metres</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>timber for houses and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c841ff64-e92f-421e-b5c9-b8ca30b4518c\" data-question=\"1\">the making of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <strong>1</strong>……………………..</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"90\"><p><span><strong>leaves</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"198\"><p><span>up to 6 metres long</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>to make brushes</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"90\"><p><span><strong>flowers</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"198\"><p><span>at the top of the trunk</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>stems provide sap, used as a drink or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87d679ab-07db-4813-bf5e-67bb158de604\" data-question=\"2\">a source of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <strong>2</strong>…………………….</span></p></td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"5\" width=\"90\"><p><span><strong>fruits</strong></span></p></td><td width=\"198\"><p><span>outer layer</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span> </span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"198\"><p><span>middle layer (coir fibres)</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>used for <strong>3</strong>………………………,</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"198\"><p><span>Inner layer (shell)</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>a source of <strong>4</strong>…………………….</span></p><p><span>(<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0cb52916-71f3-41e4-81b6-fc3c8723913f\" data-question=\"5\">when halved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>) for <strong>5</strong>…………………….</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"198\"><p><span>coconut water</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>a drink</span></p><p><span>a source of <strong>6</strong>…………………….. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b433049f-8bf2-49be-ba88-3326d62fa8a1\" data-question=\"6\">for other plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"198\"><p><span>coconut flesh</span></p></td><td width=\"312\"><p><span>oil and milk <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b46278bb-3307-446c-a2d9-49daf56018b6\" data-question=\"7\">for cooking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and <strong>7</strong>…………………….</span></p><p><span>glycerine (<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a79760a-60ab-4bcd-a353-6ccf8e65cc46\" data-question=\"8\">an ingredient in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <strong>8</strong>……………………….)</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"534\" id=\"question-wrapper-534\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FURNITURE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"535\" id=\"question-wrapper-535\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SUGAR</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"536\" id=\"question-wrapper-536\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ROPES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"537\" id=\"question-wrapper-537\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CHARCOAL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"538\" id=\"question-wrapper-538\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BOWLS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"539\" id=\"question-wrapper-539\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HORMONES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"540\" id=\"question-wrapper-540\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COSMETICS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"541\" id=\"question-wrapper-541\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DYNAMITE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>9-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"542\" id=\"question-wrapper-542\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Coconut seeds need <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"37b49029-42cd-4956-b91c-49f4e8c71e5f\" data-question=\"9\">shade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> in order to germinate. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"543\" id=\"question-wrapper-543\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Coconuts were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c9ccc339-8563-4269-9c8b-80bbf63255af\" data-question=\"10\">probably<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f45bb253-b75c-4006-bc6d-465b1f89359a\" data-question=\"10\">transported<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to Asia from America in the 16th century. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"544\" id=\"question-wrapper-544\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Coconuts found on the west coast of America were a different type from those found on the east coast. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"545\" id=\"question-wrapper-545\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> All the coconuts found in Asia <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"081694cb-76db-4098-9917-771a8d061add\" data-question=\"12\">are cultivated varieties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"546\" id=\"question-wrapper-546\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Coconuts are cultivated in different ways in America and the Pacific. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c841ff64-e92f-421e-b5c9-b8ca30b4518c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"the making of","passagePhrase":"construction"},{"uid":"87d679ab-07db-4813-bf5e-67bb158de604","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"a source of","passagePhrase":"a type of"},{"uid":"fe90084a-abc5-443a-8e4e-d3d23ce5a798","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"numerous uses"},{"uid":"d46ed38a-cca0-4ae4-918e-e76ea380cc0b","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"is widely used in"},{"uid":"0cb52916-71f3-41e4-81b6-fc3c8723913f","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"when halved","passagePhrase":"broken in half"},{"uid":"b433049f-8bf2-49be-ba88-3326d62fa8a1","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"for other plants","passagePhrase":"encourage other plants"},{"uid":"b46278bb-3307-446c-a2d9-49daf56018b6","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"for cooking","passagePhrase":"widely used in cooking"},{"uid":"5a79760a-60ab-4bcd-a353-6ccf8e65cc46","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"an ingredient in","passagePhrase":"nitroglycerine-based invention"},{"uid":"c9ccc339-8563-4269-9c8b-80bbf63255af","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"probably","passagePhrase":"likely"},{"uid":"f45bb253-b75c-4006-bc6d-465b1f89359a","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"transported","passagePhrase":"moved"},{"uid":"081694cb-76db-4098-9917-771a8d061add","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"are cultivated varieties","passagePhrase":"coconut diversity"}]},"reading_u2_230":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below. </p><h2><strong>How baby talk gives infant brains a boost</strong></h2><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>The typical way of talking to a baby – high-pitched, exaggerated and repetitious – is a source of fascination for linguists who hope to understand how ‘baby talk’ impacts on learning. Most babies start developing their hearing while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3bfe0f0-52a3-457d-b83a-71f98a758884\" data-question=\"25\">still in the womb<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, prompting some hopeful parents to play classical music to their pregnant bellies. Some research even suggests that infants are listening to adult speech as early as 10 weeks before being born, gathering the basic building blocks of their family’s native tongue.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>Early language exposure seems to have benefits to the brain – for instance, studies suggest that babies raised in bilingual homes are better at learning how to mentally prioritize information. So how does the sweet if sometimes absurd sound of infant-directed speech influence a baby’s development? Here are some recent studies that explore the science behind baby talk.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>Fathers don’t use baby talk as often or in the same ways as mothers – and that’s perfectly OK, according to a new study. Mark VanDam of Washington State University at Spokane and colleagues <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e536e2a-3c83-451f-9080-ab32a96b69e9\" data-question=\"18\">equipped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> parents with recording devices and speech-recognition <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6fb1634f-6dee-48cb-b112-0b46fd0e534f\" data-question=\"18\">software<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to study the way they interacted with their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9fe9c180-2289-46ba-8240-68c88fc3a53f\" data-question=\"18\">youngsters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> during a normal day. ‘We found that moms do exactly what you’d expect and what’s been described many times over,’ VanDam explains. ‘But we found that dads aren’t doing the same thing. Dads didn’t <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7b42d43-b264-4555-9b22-cead25edcbe1\" data-question=\"19\">raise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> their pitch or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11e0be37-09a4-4fa4-b5ed-9e5709c2d622\" data-question=\"19\">fundamental<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> frequency when they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"756c4600-e0fc-4067-b7e8-07d2f300dd65\" data-question=\"19\">talked to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> kids.’ Their role may be rooted in what is called the bridge hypothesis, which dates back to 1975. It suggests that fathers use less familial language to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7375c348-be73-4021-bd6d-4983a1dc4af9\" data-question=\"20\">provide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> their children with a bridge to the kind of speech they’ll hear in public. ‘The idea is that a kid gets to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47292bf3-decb-4327-ac0c-aa9ccf89a25d\" data-question=\"16\">practice a certain kind of speech with mom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47292bf3-decb-4327-ac0c-aa9ccf89a25d\" data-question=\"16\">another kind of speech with dad<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, so the kid <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"435ca9b6-bca1-4637-8715-eee5cd4d93c8\" data-question=\"16\">then has a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ddca60dd-099b-49c1-a581-a747debc4425\" data-question=\"21\">wider<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> repertoire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of kinds of speech to practice,’ says VanDam.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>Scientists from the University of Washington and the University of Connecticut collected thousands of 30-second conversations between parents and their babies, fitting 26 children with audio-recording vests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bf727664-7c62-4b88-9a1e-60e0ea33aed6\" data-question=\"22\">captured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> language and sound during a typical eight-hour day. The study found that the more baby talk parents used, the more their youngsters began to babble. And when researchers saw the same babies at age two, they found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c47b93a4-f3c1-4a77-a5e1-93c484c2559f\" data-question=\"23\">frequent baby talk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f9c73d6-1c0b-4ca9-87a7-851a0b7db698\" data-question=\"23\">dramatically<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20e24f8b-8225-4ac2-bbd4-cc2af102c37c\" data-question=\"23\">boosted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> vocabulary, regardless of socioeconomic status. ‘Those children who listened to a lot of baby talk were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3d32fba-888a-41fd-bad4-7de50064e3a0\" data-question=\"17\">talking more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> than the babies that listened to more adult talk or standard speech,’ says Nairán Ramirez-Esparza of the University of Connecticut. ‘We also found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"85292d6d-61f3-4eba-aed3-9c83fc160f0d\" data-question=\"14\">it really matters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> whether you use baby talk in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ae986fc-df59-4bbb-b1a0-d756a5599168\" data-question=\"14\">one-on-one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> context,’ she adds. ‘The more parents use baby talk <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ae986fc-df59-4bbb-b1a0-d756a5599168\" data-question=\"14\">one-on-one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, the more babies babble, and the more they babble, the more words they produce later in life.’</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Another study suggests that parents might want to pair their youngsters up so they can babble more with their own kind. Researchers from McGill University and Université du Québec à Montréal found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bebd89d8-9c20-4c18-83ea-5b6026e739a2\" data-question=\"26\">babies seem to like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> listening to each other rather than to adults – which may be why baby talk is such a universal tool among parents. They played repeating vowel sounds made by a special synthesizing device that mimicked sounds made by either an adult woman or another baby. This way, only the impact of the auditory cues was observed. The team then measured how long each type of sound held the infants’ attention. They found that the ‘infant’ sounds held babies’ attention nearly 40 percent longer. The baby noises also induced more reactions in the listening infants, like smiling or lip moving, which approximates sound making. The team theorizes that this attraction to other infant sounds could help launch the learning process that leads to speech. ‘It may be some property of the sound that is just drawing their attention,’ says study co-author Linda Polka. ‘Or maybe they are really interested in that particular type of sound because they are starting to focus on their own ability to make sounds. We are speculating here but it might catch their attention because they recognize it as a sound they could possibly make.’</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>In a study published in <em>Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences</em>, a total of 57 babies from two slightly different age groups – seven months and eleven and a half months – were played a number of syllables from both their native language (English) and a non-native tongue (Spanish). The infants were placed in a brain-<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a726aa9-119b-429a-ad5d-6d43a5f79560\" data-question=\"24\">activation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> scanner that recorded activity in a brain region known to guide the motor movements that produce speech. The results suggest that listening to baby talk prompts infant brains to start practicing their language skills. ‘Finding <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a726aa9-119b-429a-ad5d-6d43a5f79560\" data-question=\"24\">activation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in the motor areas of the brain when infants are simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27ccb712-adc3-449f-a102-a56d1a1d1227\" data-question=\"15\">listening<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> is significant, because it means the baby brain is engaged <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2153106c-5366-4348-ad88-3e725df8697d\" data-question=\"15\">in trying to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> talk back right from the start, and suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1dbac8d2-ab47-4f9a-9f75-fcae2504d872\" data-question=\"24\">seven-month-olds’ brains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> are already trying to figure out how to make the right movements that will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59c189f4-0501-4169-9fe6-b5780ee1e56c\" data-question=\"15\">produce words<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>,’ says co-author Patricia Kuhl. Another interesting finding was that while the seven-month-olds responded to all speech sounds regardless of language, the brains of the older infants worked harder at the motor <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a726aa9-119b-429a-ad5d-6d43a5f79560\" data-question=\"24\">activation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>s of non-native sounds compared to native sounds. The study may have also uncovered a process by which babies recognize differences between their native language and other tongues.</p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following ideas (Questions <strong>14-17</strong>) and the list of researchers below.<br></span><span>Match each idea with the correct researcher, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-17</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Researchers</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Mark VanDam<br></span><strong>B</strong><span> Nairán Ramirez-Esparza<br></span><strong>C</strong><span> Patricia Kuhl</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"547\" id=\"question-wrapper-547\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"85292d6d-61f3-4eba-aed3-9c83fc160f0d\" data-question=\"14\">the importance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of adults giving babies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ae986fc-df59-4bbb-b1a0-d756a5599168\" data-question=\"14\">individual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> attention when talking to them </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"548\" id=\"question-wrapper-548\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the connection between what babies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27ccb712-adc3-449f-a102-a56d1a1d1227\" data-question=\"15\">hear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> and their own <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2153106c-5366-4348-ad88-3e725df8697d\" data-question=\"15\">efforts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59c189f4-0501-4169-9fe6-b5780ee1e56c\" data-question=\"15\">create speech<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"549\" id=\"question-wrapper-549\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"435ca9b6-bca1-4637-8715-eee5cd4d93c8\" data-question=\"16\">the advantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> for the baby of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47292bf3-decb-4327-ac0c-aa9ccf89a25d\" data-question=\"16\">having two parents each speaking in a different way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"550\" id=\"question-wrapper-550\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the connection between the amount of baby talk babies hear and how much <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3d32fba-888a-41fd-bad4-7de50064e3a0\" data-question=\"17\">vocalising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> they do themselves </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>18-23</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>Research into how parents talk to babies</strong></span></h3><p><span>Researchers at Washington State University <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e536e2a-3c83-451f-9080-ab32a96b69e9\" data-question=\"18\">used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <strong>18</strong>……………………………, together with specialised <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6fb1634f-6dee-48cb-b112-0b46fd0e534f\" data-question=\"18\">computer programs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, to analyse how parents interacted with their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9fe9c180-2289-46ba-8240-68c88fc3a53f\" data-question=\"18\">babies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> during a normal day. The study revealed that <strong>19</strong>………………………… tended not to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7b42d43-b264-4555-9b22-cead25edcbe1\" data-question=\"19\">modify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11e0be37-09a4-4fa4-b5ed-9e5709c2d622\" data-question=\"19\">ordinary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> speech patterns when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"756c4600-e0fc-4067-b7e8-07d2f300dd65\" data-question=\"19\">interacting with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> their babies. According to an idea known as the <strong>20</strong>……………………….., they may use a more adult type of speech to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7375c348-be73-4021-bd6d-4983a1dc4af9\" data-question=\"20\">prepare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> infants for the language they will hear outside the family home. According to the researchers, hearing baby talk from one parent and ‘normal’ language from the other <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ddca60dd-099b-49c1-a581-a747debc4425\" data-question=\"21\">expands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> the baby’s <strong>21</strong>………………………… of types of speech which they can practise.</span></p><p><span>Meanwhile, another study carried out by scientists from the University of Washington and the University of Connecticut <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bf727664-7c62-4b88-9a1e-60e0ea33aed6\" data-question=\"22\">recorded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> speech and sound using special <strong>22</strong>……………………………… that the babies were equipped with. When they studies the babies again at age two, the found that those who had heard <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c47b93a4-f3c1-4a77-a5e1-93c484c2559f\" data-question=\"23\">a lot of baby talk in infancy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> had a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f9c73d6-1c0b-4ca9-87a7-851a0b7db698\" data-question=\"23\">much<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20e24f8b-8225-4ac2-bbd4-cc2af102c37c\" data-question=\"23\">larger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <strong>23</strong>……………………………. Than those who had not.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"551\" id=\"question-wrapper-551\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RECORDING DEVICES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"552\" id=\"question-wrapper-552\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FATHERS/DADS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"553\" id=\"question-wrapper-553\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BRIDGE HYPOTHESIS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"554\" id=\"question-wrapper-554\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">REPERTOIRE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"555\" id=\"question-wrapper-555\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(AUDIO-RECORDING) VESTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"556\" id=\"question-wrapper-556\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VOCABULARY</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, <strong>A-F</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>24-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"557\" id=\"question-wrapper-557\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a726aa9-119b-429a-ad5d-6d43a5f79560\" data-question=\"24\">change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> which occurs in babies’ brain activity <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1dbac8d2-ab47-4f9a-9f75-fcae2504d872\" data-question=\"24\">before the end of their first year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"558\" id=\"question-wrapper-558\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an example of what some parents do for their baby’s benefit <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3bfe0f0-52a3-457d-b83a-71f98a758884\" data-question=\"25\">before birth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"559\" id=\"question-wrapper-559\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a mention of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bebd89d8-9c20-4c18-83ea-5b6026e739a2\" data-question=\"26\">babies’ preference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> for the sounds that other babies make </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a3bfe0f0-52a3-457d-b83a-71f98a758884","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"before birth","passagePhrase":"still in the womb"},{"uid":"3e536e2a-3c83-451f-9080-ab32a96b69e9","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"used","passagePhrase":"equipped"},{"uid":"6fb1634f-6dee-48cb-b112-0b46fd0e534f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"computer programs","passagePhrase":"software"},{"uid":"9fe9c180-2289-46ba-8240-68c88fc3a53f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"babies","passagePhrase":"youngsters"},{"uid":"b7b42d43-b264-4555-9b22-cead25edcbe1","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"modify","passagePhrase":"raise"},{"uid":"11e0be37-09a4-4fa4-b5ed-9e5709c2d622","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"ordinary","passagePhrase":"fundamental"},{"uid":"756c4600-e0fc-4067-b7e8-07d2f300dd65","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"interacting with","passagePhrase":"talked to"},{"uid":"7375c348-be73-4021-bd6d-4983a1dc4af9","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"prepare","passagePhrase":"provide"},{"uid":"47292bf3-decb-4327-ac0c-aa9ccf89a25d","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"having two parents each speaking in a different way","passagePhrase":"practice a certain kind of speech with mom ... another kind of speech with dad"},{"uid":"435ca9b6-bca1-4637-8715-eee5cd4d93c8","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"the advantage","passagePhrase":"then has a wider repertoire"},{"uid":"ddca60dd-099b-49c1-a581-a747debc4425","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"expands","passagePhrase":"wider"},{"uid":"bf727664-7c62-4b88-9a1e-60e0ea33aed6","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"recorded","passagePhrase":"captured"},{"uid":"c47b93a4-f3c1-4a77-a5e1-93c484c2559f","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"a lot of baby talk in infancy","passagePhrase":"frequent baby talk"},{"uid":"7f9c73d6-1c0b-4ca9-87a7-851a0b7db698","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"much","passagePhrase":"dramatically"},{"uid":"20e24f8b-8225-4ac2-bbd4-cc2af102c37c","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"larger","passagePhrase":"boosted"},{"uid":"b3d32fba-888a-41fd-bad4-7de50064e3a0","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"vocalising","passagePhrase":"talking more"},{"uid":"85292d6d-61f3-4eba-aed3-9c83fc160f0d","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"the importance","passagePhrase":"it really matters"},{"uid":"9ae986fc-df59-4bbb-b1a0-d756a5599168","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"individual","passagePhrase":"one-on-one ... one-on-one"},{"uid":"bebd89d8-9c20-4c18-83ea-5b6026e739a2","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"babies’ preference","passagePhrase":"babies seem to like"},{"uid":"3a726aa9-119b-429a-ad5d-6d43a5f79560","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"change","passagePhrase":"activation ... activation ... activation"},{"uid":"27ccb712-adc3-449f-a102-a56d1a1d1227","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"hear","passagePhrase":"listening"},{"uid":"2153106c-5366-4348-ad88-3e725df8697d","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"efforts","passagePhrase":"in trying to"},{"uid":"1dbac8d2-ab47-4f9a-9f75-fcae2504d872","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"before the end of their first year","passagePhrase":"seven-month-olds’ brains"},{"uid":"59c189f4-0501-4169-9fe6-b5780ee1e56c","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"create speech","passagePhrase":"produce words"}]},"reading_u2_231":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>Whatever happened to the Harappan Civilisation?</strong></span></h2><h3><span><em>New research sheds light on the disappearance of an ancient society</em></span></h3><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>The Harappan Civilisation of ancient Pakistan and India flourished 5,000 years ago, but a thousand years later their cities were abandoned. The Harappan Civilisation was a sophisticated Bronze Age society who built ‘megacities’ and traded internationally in luxury craft products, and yet seemed to have left almost no depictions of themselves. But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b7473a7-6a09-48ae-8fd9-f7cc0aa976e4\" data-question=\"29\">their lack of self-imagery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b7473a7-6a09-48ae-8fd9-f7cc0aa976e4\" data-question=\"29\">at a time when the Egyptians were carving and painting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> representations of themselves all over their temples – is only part of the mystery.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>‘There is plenty of archaeological evidence to tell us about the rise of the Harappan Civilisation, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f05549f5-a0b5-4b93-a43b-6f3a3f71f570\" data-question=\"40\">relatively little<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> about its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd944a95-70eb-453f-b516-0d529d45d525\" data-question=\"40\">fall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>,’ explains archaeologist Dr Cameron Petrie of the University of Cambridge. ‘As populations increased, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b432f658-fb5b-4e96-811a-ef1e7e1c7737\" data-question=\"30\">cities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> were built that had great baths, craft workshops, palaces and halls laid out in distinct sectors. Houses were arranged in blocks, with wide main streets and narrow alleyways, and many had their own wells and drainage systems. It was very much a “thriving” civilisation.’ Then around 2100 BC, a transformation began. Streets went uncleaned, buildings started to be abandoned, and ritual structures fell out of use. After their final demise, a millennium passed before really large-scale cities appeared once more in South Asia.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Some have claimed that major glacier-fed rivers changed their course, dramatically affecting the water supply and agriculture; or that the cities could not cope with an increasing population, they exhausted their resource base, the trading economy broke down or they succumbed to invasion and conflict; and yet others that climate change caused an environmental change that affected food and water provision. ‘It is unlikely that there was a single cause for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"336e87d8-b0e1-48eb-8ea2-92b676dd5253\" data-question=\"27\">the decline of the civilisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. But the fact is, until now, we have had little solid evidence from the area for most of the key elements,’ said Petrie. ‘A lot of the archaeological debate has really only been well-argued speculation.’</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>A research team led by Petrie, together with Dr Ravindanath Singh of Banaras Hindu University in India, found early in their investigations that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a944fd44-56fe-4b37-8263-6aada1b3916c\" data-question=\"31\">many of the archaeological sites were not where they were supposed to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, completely altering understanding of the way that this region was inhabited in the past. When they carried out a survey of how the larger area was settled in relation to sources of water, they found inaccuracies in the published geographic locations of ancient settlements ranging from several hundred metres to many kilometres. They realised that any attempts to use the existing data were likely to be fundamentally flawed. Over the course of several seasons of fieldwork they carried out new surveys, finding an astonishing 198 settlement sites that were previously unknown.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Now, research published by Dr Yama Dixit and Professor David Hodell, both from Cambridge’s Department of Earth Sciences, has provided the first definitive evidence for climate change affecting the plains of north-western India, where hundreds of Harappan sites are known to have been situated. The researchers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ecec42ad-8a36-4cf8-a53e-ae33bae560f0\" data-question=\"32\">gathered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> shells of <em>Melanoides tuberculate </em>snails from the sediments of an ancient lake and used geochemical analysis as a means of tracing the climate history of the region. ‘As today, the major source of water into the lake is likely to have been the summer monsoon,’ says Dixit. ‘But we have observed that there was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ef6b0824-a19f-4fb4-a442-24615a01f5cb\" data-question=\"33\">an abrupt change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> about 4,100 years ago, when the amount of evaporation from the lake <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c73f361b-9add-4e84-b4fb-a333e0ec5a29\" data-question=\"34\">exceeded the rainfall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> – indicative of a drought.’ Hodell adds: ‘We <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b26d879-a0ab-4b83-be48-87e7f626de0e\" data-question=\"39\">estimate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> that the weakening of the Indian summer monsoon climate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"647529db-576d-4942-b312-39448d082e76\" data-question=\"39\">lasted about 200 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> before recovering to the previous conditions, which we still see today.’</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>It has long been thought that other great Bronze Age civilisations also declined at a similar time, with a global-scale climate event being seen as the cause. While it is possible that these local-scale processes were linked, the real archaeological interest lies in understanding the impact of these larger-scale events on different environments and different populations. ‘Considering the vast area of the Harappan Civilisation with its variable weather systems,’ explains Singh, ‘it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"16c1e261-df9e-4f13-a582-c0d8a4a2d3f8\" data-question=\"37\">essential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> that we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ed119675-b366-4f73-8bb4-f2ef81f9d4ca\" data-question=\"37\">obtain more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"42259a03-59d7-4927-b313-00f00be9200c\" data-question=\"37\">climate data<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> from areas close to the two great cities at Mohenjodaro and Harappa and also from the Indian Punjab.’</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>Petrie and Singh’s team is now examining archaeological records and trying to understand details of how people led their lives in the region five millennia ago. They are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"468dcd10-dfa3-40eb-acb3-fc349a7afc3a\" data-question=\"35\">analysing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> grains cultivated <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eca1e201-538d-44e3-828a-05973d55bab1\" data-question=\"35\">at the time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, and trying to work out whether they were grown under extreme conditions of water stress, and whether they were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eec1d164-77a8-4ba8-9276-a2b66bceddf6\" data-question=\"35\">adjusting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the combinations of crops they were growing for different weather systems. They are also looking at whether the types of pottery used, and other aspects of their material culture, were distinctive to specific regions or were more similar across larger areas. This gives us insight into the types of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a4d480ec-6555-4223-b3cc-35c73d96891b\" data-question=\"36\">interactive networks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"089b2c6f-d244-4478-b622-c6a2d1a1711c\" data-question=\"36\">the population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> was involved in, and whether those changed.</span></p><p><span><strong>H</strong></span></p><p><span>Petrie believes that archaeologists are in a unique position to investigate how past societies responded to environmental and climatic change. ‘By <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7803ae34-70d9-4205-8f1a-aadeff56a1cf\" data-question=\"38\">investigating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> responses to environmental pressures and threats, we can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9eb4cc0-745f-47b8-a463-cf1c4ff4929a\" data-question=\"28\">learn <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12f8ee22-065a-467d-8640-123ec48bc1b9\" data-question=\"38\">from the past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to engage with the public, and the relevant governmental and administrative bodies, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9eb4cc0-745f-47b8-a463-cf1c4ff4929a\" data-question=\"28\">to be more proactive in issues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> such as the management and administration of water supply, the balance of urban and rural development, and the importance of preserving cultural heritage in the future.’</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has eight paragraphs, <strong>A-H</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter,<strong> A-H</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"560\" id=\"question-wrapper-560\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> proposed explanations for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"336e87d8-b0e1-48eb-8ea2-92b676dd5253\" data-question=\"27\">decline of the Harappan Civilisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"561\" id=\"question-wrapper-561\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9eb4cc0-745f-47b8-a463-cf1c4ff4929a\" data-question=\"28\">present-day application<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of some archaeological research findings </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"562\" id=\"question-wrapper-562\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b7473a7-6a09-48ae-8fd9-f7cc0aa976e4\" data-question=\"29\">a difference<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> between the Harappan Civilisation and another culture of the same period </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"563\" id=\"question-wrapper-563\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of some features of Harappan <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b432f658-fb5b-4e96-811a-ef1e7e1c7737\" data-question=\"30\">urban<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> design </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"564\" id=\"question-wrapper-564\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a944fd44-56fe-4b37-8263-6aada1b3916c\" data-question=\"31\">discovery of errors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> made by previous archaeologists </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>32-36</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>Looking at evidence of climate change</strong></span></h3><p><span>Yama Dixit and David Hodell have found the first definitive evidence of climate change affecting the plains of north-western India thousands of years ago. By <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ecec42ad-8a36-4cf8-a53e-ae33bae560f0\" data-question=\"32\">collecting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the <strong>32</strong>………………………… of snails and analysing them, they discovered evidence of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ef6b0824-a19f-4fb4-a442-24615a01f5cb\" data-question=\"33\">change in water levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> in a <strong>33</strong>……………………….. in the region. This occurred when there <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c73f361b-9add-4e84-b4fb-a333e0ec5a29\" data-question=\"34\">was less<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <strong>34</strong>…………………………….. than evaporation, and suggests that there was an extended period of drought.</span></p><p><span>Petrie and Singh’s team are using archaeological records to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"468dcd10-dfa3-40eb-acb3-fc349a7afc3a\" data-question=\"35\">look at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <strong>35</strong>…………………………… from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eca1e201-538d-44e3-828a-05973d55bab1\" data-question=\"35\">five millennia ago<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, in order to know whether people had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eec1d164-77a8-4ba8-9276-a2b66bceddf6\" data-question=\"35\">adapted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> their agricultural practices to changing climatic conditions. They are also examining objects including <strong>36</strong>………………………….. , so as to find out about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a4d480ec-6555-4223-b3cc-35c73d96891b\" data-question=\"36\">links<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"089b2c6f-d244-4478-b622-c6a2d1a1711c\" data-question=\"36\">inhabitants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of different parts of the region and whether these changed over time.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"565\" id=\"question-wrapper-565\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SHELLS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"566\" id=\"question-wrapper-566\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LAKE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"567\" id=\"question-wrapper-567\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RAINFALL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"568\" id=\"question-wrapper-568\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GRAINS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"569\" id=\"question-wrapper-569\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POTTERY</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.<br></span><span>Look at the following statements (Questions <strong>38-40</strong>) and the list of researchers below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct researcher, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>, in boxes <strong>37-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Researchers</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Cameron Petrie<br></span><span><strong>B</strong> Ravindanath Singh<br></span><span><strong>C</strong> Yama Dixit<br></span><span><strong>D</strong> David Hodell</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"570\" id=\"question-wrapper-570\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ed119675-b366-4f73-8bb4-f2ef81f9d4ca\" data-question=\"37\">Finding further<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> information about changes to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"42259a03-59d7-4927-b313-00f00be9200c\" data-question=\"37\">environmental conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in the region is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"16c1e261-df9e-4f13-a582-c0d8a4a2d3f8\" data-question=\"37\">vital<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"571\" id=\"question-wrapper-571\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7803ae34-70d9-4205-8f1a-aadeff56a1cf\" data-question=\"38\">Examining<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12f8ee22-065a-467d-8640-123ec48bc1b9\" data-question=\"38\">previous patterns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of behaviour may have long-term benefits. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"572\" id=\"question-wrapper-572\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b26d879-a0ab-4b83-be48-87e7f626de0e\" data-question=\"39\">Rough calculations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> indicate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"647529db-576d-4942-b312-39448d082e76\" data-question=\"39\">the approximate length of a period of water shortage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"573\" id=\"question-wrapper-573\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Information about the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd944a95-70eb-453f-b516-0d529d45d525\" data-question=\"40\">decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> of the Harappan Civilisation has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f05549f5-a0b5-4b93-a43b-6f3a3f71f570\" data-question=\"40\">lacking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"8b7473a7-6a09-48ae-8fd9-f7cc0aa976e4","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"a difference","passagePhrase":"their lack of self-imagery ... at a time when the Egyptians were carving and painting"},{"uid":"f05549f5-a0b5-4b93-a43b-6f3a3f71f570","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"lacking","passagePhrase":"relatively little"},{"uid":"bd944a95-70eb-453f-b516-0d529d45d525","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"decline","passagePhrase":"fall"},{"uid":"b432f658-fb5b-4e96-811a-ef1e7e1c7737","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"urban","passagePhrase":"cities"},{"uid":"336e87d8-b0e1-48eb-8ea2-92b676dd5253","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"decline of the Harappan Civilisation","passagePhrase":"the decline of the civilisation"},{"uid":"a944fd44-56fe-4b37-8263-6aada1b3916c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"discovery of errors","passagePhrase":"many of the archaeological sites were not where they were supposed to be"},{"uid":"ecec42ad-8a36-4cf8-a53e-ae33bae560f0","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"collecting","passagePhrase":"gathered"},{"uid":"ef6b0824-a19f-4fb4-a442-24615a01f5cb","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"change in water levels","passagePhrase":"an abrupt change"},{"uid":"9b26d879-a0ab-4b83-be48-87e7f626de0e","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Rough calculations","passagePhrase":"estimate"},{"uid":"647529db-576d-4942-b312-39448d082e76","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"the approximate length of a period of water shortage","passagePhrase":"lasted about 200 years"},{"uid":"16c1e261-df9e-4f13-a582-c0d8a4a2d3f8","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"vital","passagePhrase":"essential"},{"uid":"ed119675-b366-4f73-8bb4-f2ef81f9d4ca","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"Finding further","passagePhrase":"obtain more"},{"uid":"42259a03-59d7-4927-b313-00f00be9200c","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"environmental conditions","passagePhrase":"climate data"},{"uid":"468dcd10-dfa3-40eb-acb3-fc349a7afc3a","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"look at","passagePhrase":"analysing"},{"uid":"eca1e201-538d-44e3-828a-05973d55bab1","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"five millennia ago","passagePhrase":"at the time"},{"uid":"eec1d164-77a8-4ba8-9276-a2b66bceddf6","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"adapted","passagePhrase":"adjusting"},{"uid":"a4d480ec-6555-4223-b3cc-35c73d96891b","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"links","passagePhrase":"interactive networks"},{"uid":"089b2c6f-d244-4478-b622-c6a2d1a1711c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"inhabitants","passagePhrase":"the population"},{"uid":"7803ae34-70d9-4205-8f1a-aadeff56a1cf","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"Examining","passagePhrase":"investigating"},{"uid":"a9eb4cc0-745f-47b8-a463-cf1c4ff4929a","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"present-day application","passagePhrase":"learn from the past ... to be more proactive in issues"},{"uid":"12f8ee22-065a-467d-8640-123ec48bc1b9","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"previous patterns","passagePhrase":"from the past"}]},"reading_u2_232":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions</strong> <strong>1-13</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</p><p> </p><h2><strong>Cutty Sark:</strong> the fastest sailing ship of all time</h2><p>The nineteenth century was a period of great technological development in Britain, and for shipping the major changes were from wind to steam power, and from wood to iron and steel.</p><p>The fastest commercial sailing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51e6ceda-2538-4dcb-a5c6-d65018491ddc\" data-question=\"1\">vessels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of all time were clippers, three-masted ships <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0f2e326c-5948-44a9-a272-7d0ad2cee291\" data-question=\"1\">built to transport goods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> around the world, although some also took passengers. From the 1840s until 1869, when the Suez Canal opened and steam propulsion was replacing sail, clippers dominated world trade. Although many were built, only one has survived more or less intact: <em>Cutty Sark</em>, now on display in Greenwich, southeast London.</p><p><em>Cutty Sark</em>’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33d9de40-08cd-448e-8fae-6687776d174a\" data-question=\"2\">unusual name comes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> from the poem <em>Tam O’Shanter </em>by the Scottish poet Robert Burns. Tam, a farmer, is chased by a witch called Nannie, who is wearing a ‘<em>cutty sark</em>’ – an old Scottish <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d680783e-f04f-4383-9c97-818f875b721d\" data-question=\"2\">name for a short nightdress<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. The witch is depicted in <em>Cutty Sark</em>’s figurehead – the carving of a woman typically at the front of old sailing ships. In legend, and in Burns’s poem, witches cannot cross water, so this was a rather strange choice of name for a ship.</p><p><em>Cutty Sark</em> was built in Dumbarton, Scotland, in 1869, for a shipping company owned by John Willis. To carry out construction, Willis chose a new shipbuilding firm, Scott &amp; Linton, and ensured that the contract with them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"743f37d5-cfd4-4d85-8cec-63754435e729\" data-question=\"3\">put him in a very strong position<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. In the end, the firm was forced out of business, and the ship was finished by a competitor.</p><p>Willis’s company was active in the tea trade between China and Britain, where speed could bring shipowners both profits and prestige, so <em>Cutty Sark</em> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c94e723-a30f-45ab-a19d-517358fd1e2f\" data-question=\"4\">was designed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> make the journey <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ea22793-4cf0-44a6-9656-2dbca4db6dbf\" data-question=\"4\">more quickly than any other<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> ship. On her maiden voyage, in 1870, she set sail from London, carrying large amounts of goods to China. She returned laden with tea, making the journey back to London in four months. However, <em>Cutty Sark</em> never lived up to the high expectations of her owner, as a result of bad winds and various misfortunes. On one occasion, in 1872, the ship and a rival clipper, <em>Thermopylae</em>, left port in China on the same day. Crossing the Indian Ocean, <em>Cutty Sark</em> gained a lead of over 400 miles, but then her rudder was severely damaged in stormy seas, making her impossible to steer. The ship’s crew had the daunting task of repairing the rudder at sea, and only succeeded at the second attempt. <em>Cutty Sark</em> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1af6b1c6-f62b-4c52-a2cd-26256d90e3ca\" data-question=\"5\">reached London<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7cdf4f32-f364-4de3-8419-e31000ab4738\" data-question=\"5\">a week after<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <em>Thermopylae.</em></p><p>Steam ships posed a growing threat to clippers, as their speed and cargo capacity increased. In addition, the opening of the Suez Canal in 1869, the same year that <em>Cutty Sark</em> was launched, had a serious impact. While steam ships could make use of the quick, direct route between the Mediterranean and the Red Sea, the canal was of no use to sailing ships, which needed the much stronger winds of the oceans, and so had to sail a far greater distance. Steam ships <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f2bf167-bfb9-4d05-b179-3c99dfcc92cc\" data-question=\"6\">reduced the journey time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> between Britain and China by approximately two months.</p><p>By 1878, tea traders weren’t interested in <em>Cutty Sark</em>, and instead, she took on the much less prestigious work of carrying any cargo between any two ports in the world. In 1880, violence aboard the ship led ultimately to the replacement of the captain with an incompetent drunkard who stole the crew’s wages. He was suspended from service, and a new captain appointed. This marked a turnaround and the beginning of the most successful <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f96f987d-e1b7-4381-86ef-1cfe0f9ca142\" data-question=\"9\">period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> in <em>Cutty Sark</em>’s working life, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2457a1b-c8cd-423c-931e-98ac225f7e16\" data-question=\"9\">transporting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> wool from Australia to Britain. One such journey took just under 12 weeks, beating every other ship sailing that year by around a month.</p><p>The ship’s next captain, Richard Woodget, was an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"256fe30f-b582-4787-ab1f-a390c440231b\" data-question=\"10\">excellent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> navigator, who got the best out of both his ship and his crew. As a sailing ship, <em>Cutty Sark</em> depended on the strong trade winds of the southern hemisphere, and Woodget took her further south than any previous captain, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0d0cecc-5062-4179-b9f1-3c673c45a8b4\" data-question=\"8\">bringing her dangerously close to icebergs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> off the southern tip of South America. His <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d46870ca-cd52-4e33-aedc-e1ff9b851200\" data-question=\"8\">gamble<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> paid off, though, and the ship was the fastest vessel in the wool trade for ten years.</p><p>As competition from steam ships increased in the 1890s, and <em>Cutty Sark</em> approached the end of her life expectancy, she became less profitable. She was sold to a Portuguese firm, which renamed her <em>Ferreira.</em> For the next 25 years, she again carried miscellaneous cargoes around the world.</p><p>Badly damaged in a gale in 1922, she was put into Falmouth harbor in southwest England, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fc554d83-5388-43b5-9f33-ef7cf55fded0\" data-question=\"11\">for repairs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Wilfred Dowman, a retired sea captain who owned a training vessel, recognised her and tried to buy her, but without success. She returned to Portugal and was sold to another Portuguese company. Dowman was determined, however, and offered a high price: this was accepted, and the ship returned to Falmouth the following year and had her original name restored.</p><p>Dowman used <em>Cutty Sark</em> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e6539940-4209-4576-9daa-e33c37d06a0f\" data-question=\"12\">as a training ship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, and she continued in this role after his death. When she was no longer required, in 1954, she was transferred to dry dock at Greenwich to go on public display. The ship <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8de720fa-652d-457c-aa32-3669528a403e\" data-question=\"13\">suffered from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> fire in 2007, and again, less seriously, in 2014, but now <em>Cutty Sark</em> attracts a quarter of a million visitors a year.</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>1-8</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"574\" id=\"question-wrapper-574\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Clippers were originally intended to be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0f2e326c-5948-44a9-a272-7d0ad2cee291\" data-question=\"1\">used as passenger <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51e6ceda-2538-4dcb-a5c6-d65018491ddc\" data-question=\"1\">ships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"575\" id=\"question-wrapper-575\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Cutty Sark <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33d9de40-08cd-448e-8fae-6687776d174a\" data-question=\"2\">was given the name<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d680783e-f04f-4383-9c97-818f875b721d\" data-question=\"2\">a character in a poem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"576\" id=\"question-wrapper-576\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The contract between John Willis and Scott &amp; Linton <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"743f37d5-cfd4-4d85-8cec-63754435e729\" data-question=\"3\">favoured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> Willis. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"577\" id=\"question-wrapper-577\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> John Willis <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c94e723-a30f-45ab-a19d-517358fd1e2f\" data-question=\"4\">wanted Cutty Sark to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the fastest tea clipper travelling between the UK and China. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"578\" id=\"question-wrapper-578\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Despite storm damage, Cutty Sark <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7cdf4f32-f364-4de3-8419-e31000ab4738\" data-question=\"5\">beat Thermopylae<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> back to London. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"579\" id=\"question-wrapper-579\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The opening of the Suez Canal meant that steam ships could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f2bf167-bfb9-4d05-b179-3c99dfcc92cc\" data-question=\"6\">travel between Britain and China faster<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> than clippers. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"580\" id=\"question-wrapper-580\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Steam ships sometimes used the ocean route <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"913dd227-c56c-4931-8df2-c90ba7f36206\" data-question=\"7\">to travel between London and China<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"581\" id=\"question-wrapper-581\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Captain Woodget put Cutty Sark <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d46870ca-cd52-4e33-aedc-e1ff9b851200\" data-question=\"8\">at risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0d0cecc-5062-4179-b9f1-3c673c45a8b4\" data-question=\"8\">hitting an iceberg<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the sentences below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>9-13</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"582\" id=\"question-wrapper-582\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> After 1880, Cutty Sark <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2457a1b-c8cd-423c-931e-98ac225f7e16\" data-question=\"9\">carried<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> ………………………… as its main cargo during its most successful <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f96f987d-e1b7-4381-86ef-1cfe0f9ca142\" data-question=\"9\">time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WOOL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"583\" id=\"question-wrapper-583\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> As a captain and …………………………., Woodget was very <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"256fe30f-b582-4787-ab1f-a390c440231b\" data-question=\"10\">skilled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NAVIGATOR</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"584\" id=\"question-wrapper-584\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Ferreira went to Falmouth to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fc554d83-5388-43b5-9f33-ef7cf55fded0\" data-question=\"11\">repair damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> that a …………………………. had caused. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GALE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"585\" id=\"question-wrapper-585\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Between 1923 and 1954, Cutty Sark <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e6539940-4209-4576-9daa-e33c37d06a0f\" data-question=\"12\">was used for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> ………………………….. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRAINING</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"586\" id=\"question-wrapper-586\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Cutty Sark has twice been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8de720fa-652d-457c-aa32-3669528a403e\" data-question=\"13\">damaged by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> ………………………… in the 21st century. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FIRE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"51e6ceda-2538-4dcb-a5c6-d65018491ddc","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"ships","passagePhrase":"vessels"},{"uid":"33d9de40-08cd-448e-8fae-6687776d174a","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"was given the name","passagePhrase":"unusual name comes"},{"uid":"743f37d5-cfd4-4d85-8cec-63754435e729","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"favoured","passagePhrase":"put him in a very strong position"},{"uid":"8c94e723-a30f-45ab-a19d-517358fd1e2f","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"wanted Cutty Sark to be","passagePhrase":"was designed to"},{"uid":"3ea22793-4cf0-44a6-9656-2dbca4db6dbf","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"more quickly than any other"},{"uid":"1af6b1c6-f62b-4c52-a2cd-26256d90e3ca","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"reached London"},{"uid":"7f2bf167-bfb9-4d05-b179-3c99dfcc92cc","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"travel between Britain and China faster","passagePhrase":"reduced the journey time"},{"uid":"f96f987d-e1b7-4381-86ef-1cfe0f9ca142","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"time","passagePhrase":"period"},{"uid":"c2457a1b-c8cd-423c-931e-98ac225f7e16","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"carried","passagePhrase":"transporting"},{"uid":"256fe30f-b582-4787-ab1f-a390c440231b","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"skilled","passagePhrase":"excellent"},{"uid":"b0d0cecc-5062-4179-b9f1-3c673c45a8b4","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"hitting an iceberg","passagePhrase":"bringing her dangerously close to icebergs"},{"uid":"d46870ca-cd52-4e33-aedc-e1ff9b851200","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"at risk","passagePhrase":"gamble"},{"uid":"fc554d83-5388-43b5-9f33-ef7cf55fded0","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"repair damage","passagePhrase":"for repairs"},{"uid":"e6539940-4209-4576-9daa-e33c37d06a0f","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"was used for","passagePhrase":"as a training ship"},{"uid":"8de720fa-652d-457c-aa32-3669528a403e","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"damaged by","passagePhrase":"suffered from"},{"uid":"913dd227-c56c-4931-8df2-c90ba7f36206","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"to travel between London and China","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_233":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong><span>SAVING THE SOIL</span></strong></span></h2><p><span><em>More than a third of the Earth’s top layer is at risk. Is there hope for our planet’s most precious resource?</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>More than a third of the world’s soil is endangered, according to a recent UN report. If we don’t slow the decline, all farmable soil could be gone in 60 years. Since soil grows 95% of our food, and sustains human life in other more surprising ways, that is a huge problem.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Peter Groffman, from the Cary Institute of Ecosystem Studies in New York, points out that soil scientists have been warning about the degradation of the world’s soil for decades. At the same time, our understanding of its importance to humans has grown. A single gram of healthy soil might contain 100 million bacteria, as well as other microorganisms such as viruses and fungi, living amid <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"114b3d47-de43-417d-9cab-b9199affe0ba\" data-question=\"14\">decomposing plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and various minerals.</span></p><p><span>That means soils do not just grow our food, but are the source of nearly all our existing antibiotics, and could be our best hope in the fight against antibiotic-resistant bacteria. Soil is also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ae7bf77-a9a7-4869-a4d9-b6350cf907c2\" data-question=\"15\">an ally against climate change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>: as microorganisms within soil digest dead animals and plants, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5070ab52-dbd1-4c34-ad9c-1409dd8ab4d9\" data-question=\"15\">lock in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> their carbon content, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5070ab52-dbd1-4c34-ad9c-1409dd8ab4d9\" data-question=\"15\">holding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> three times the amount of carbon as does the entire atmosphere. Soils also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5070ab52-dbd1-4c34-ad9c-1409dd8ab4d9\" data-question=\"15\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e934874-e606-4e33-a18b-b5283ace0cc7\" data-question=\"16\">store<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> water, preventing flood damage: in the UK, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a458296-676c-4c49-90b3-3ffd4fcea599\" data-question=\"16\">damage to buildings, roads and bridges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> from floods caused by soil degradation costs £233 million every year.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>If the soil loses its ability to perform these functions, the human race could be in big trouble. The danger is not that the soil will disappear completely, but that the microorganisms that give it its special properties will be lost. And once this has happened, it may take the soil thousands of years to recover.</span></p><p><span>Agriculture is by far <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a72c154-0263-4c52-8a96-53b4fc5df3fb\" data-question=\"17\">the biggest problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. In the wild, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e1effb52-a582-4981-9487-ffe6dd1c819b\" data-question=\"23\">when plants grow they remove nutrients from the soil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, but then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e1effb52-a582-4981-9487-ffe6dd1c819b\" data-question=\"23\">when the plants die and decay these nutrients are returned directly to the soil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Humans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1f4807cd-04df-425d-84a9-bc9c83424e36\" data-question=\"18\">tend not to return<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> unused parts of harvested crops directly to the soil to enrich it, meaning that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3317a54b-37b1-48d3-9caf-970c100e8478\" data-question=\"17\">soil gradually becomes less fertile<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. In the past we developed strategies to get around the problem, such as regularly varying the types of crops grown, or leaving fields uncultivated for a season.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>But these practices became inconvenient as populations grew and agriculture had to be run on more commercial lines. A solution came in the early 20<sup>th</sup> century with the Haber-Bosch process for manufacturing ammonium nitrate. Farmers have been putting this synthetic fertiliser on their fields ever since.</span></p><p><span>But over the past few decades, it has become clear this wasn’t such a bright idea. Chemical fertilisers can release polluting nitrous oxide into the atmosphere and excess is often washed away with the rain, releasing nitrogen into rivers. More recently, we have found that indiscriminate use of fertilisers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d82e957c-6da2-412c-a0a0-ed1fabe193d7\" data-question=\"19\">hurts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> the soil itself, turning it acidic and salty, and degrading the soil they are supposed to nourish.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>One of the people looking for a solution to his problem is Pius Floris, who started out running a tree-care business in the Netherlands, and now advises some of the world’s top soil scientists. He came to realise that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1cd1c4b4-cffc-4fd7-84d6-0cd8a8b4329d\" data-question=\"22\">the best way to ensure his trees flourished<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> was to take care of the soil, and has developed a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a4e28840-241f-4605-9155-661d8155bacf\" data-question=\"20\">cocktail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of beneficial bacteria, fungi and humus* to do this. Researchers at the University of Valladolid in Spain recently used this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a4e28840-241f-4605-9155-661d8155bacf\" data-question=\"20\">cocktail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> on soils destroyed by years of fertiliser overuse. When they applied Floris’s mix to the desert-like test plots, a good crop of plants emerged that were not just healthy at the surface, but had roots strong enough to pierce dirt as hard as rock. The few plants that grew in the control plots, fed with traditional fertilisers, were small and weak</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>However, measures like this are not enough to solve the global soil degradation problem. To assess our options on a global scale we first need an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2b89956-cd64-4a10-8746-39048a09ceea\" data-question=\"26\">accurate picture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> of what types of soil are out there, and the problems they face. That’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f41bc8de-426e-48af-bfbc-ad83863630d1\" data-question=\"26\">not easy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. For one thing, there is no agreed international system for classifying soil. In an attempt to unify the different approaches, the UN has created the Global Soil Map project. Researchers from nine countries are working together to create a map linked to a database that can be fed measurements from field surveys, drone surveys, satellite imagery, lab analyses and so on to provide real-time <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0cd15c2e-fb8c-4000-9395-f58df6f188b2\" data-question=\"24\">data<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> on the state of the soil. Within the next four years, they aim to have mapped soils worldwide to a depth of 100 metres, with the results freely accessible to all.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>But this is only a first step. We need ways of presenting the problem that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"264726f7-02c5-4a8a-ac1b-8b77a95db54f\" data-question=\"21\">bring it home to governments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> and the wider public, says Pamela Chasek at the International Institute for Sustainable Development, in Winnipeg, Canada. ‘Most scientists don’t speak language that policy-makers can understand, and vice versa.’ Chasek and her colleagues have proposed a goal of ‘zero net land degradation’. Like the idea of carbon neutrality, it is an easily understood target that can help shape expectations and encourage action.</span></p><p><span>For soils on the brink, that may be too late. Several researchers are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de636e2d-1dbe-4318-af1f-178761a42375\" data-question=\"25\">agitating for the immediate creation of protected zones for endangered soils<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. One difficulty here is defining what these areas should conserve: areas where the greatest soil diversity is present? Or areas of unspoilt soils that could act as a future benchmark of quality?</span></p><p><span>Whatever we do, if we want our soils to survive, we need to take action now.</span></p><p><span> </span><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.<br></span><span>Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>14-17</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>Why soil degradation could be a disaster for humans</strong></span></h3><p><span>Healthy soil contains a large variety of bacteria and other microorganisms, as well as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"114b3d47-de43-417d-9cab-b9199affe0ba\" data-question=\"14\">plant remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and <strong>14</strong> ……………………….. It provides us with food and also with antibiotics, and its function in storing <strong>15</strong> …………………………. has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ae7bf77-a9a7-4869-a4d9-b6350cf907c2\" data-question=\"15\">a significant effect on the climate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. In addition, it prevents <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a458296-676c-4c49-90b3-3ffd4fcea599\" data-question=\"16\">damage to property and infrastructure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> because it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e934874-e606-4e33-a18b-b5283ace0cc7\" data-question=\"16\">holds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <strong>16</strong>……………………………</span></p><p><span>If these microorganisms are lost, soil may lose its special properties. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a72c154-0263-4c52-8a96-53b4fc5df3fb\" data-question=\"17\">The main factor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> contributing to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3317a54b-37b1-48d3-9caf-970c100e8478\" data-question=\"17\">soil degradation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> is the <strong>17</strong>………………………….. carried out by humans.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"587\" id=\"question-wrapper-587\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MINERALS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"588\" id=\"question-wrapper-588\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CARBON</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"589\" id=\"question-wrapper-589\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WATER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"590\" id=\"question-wrapper-590\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AGRICULTURE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, <strong>A-F</strong>, below.<br><em>Write the correct letter,<strong> A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>18-21</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> may improve the number and quality of plants growing there.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> may contain data from up to nine countries.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1f4807cd-04df-425d-84a9-bc9c83424e36\" data-question=\"18\">may not be put back<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> into the soil.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> may help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"264726f7-02c5-4a8a-ac1b-8b77a95db54f\" data-question=\"21\">governments to be more aware of soil-related issues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> may cause <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d82e957c-6da2-412c-a0a0-ed1fabe193d7\" data-question=\"19\">damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> to different aspects of the environment.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong> may be better for use at a global level.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"591\" id=\"question-wrapper-591\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Nutrients contained in the unused parts of harvested crops </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"592\" id=\"question-wrapper-592\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Synthetic fertilisers produced with Haber-Bosch process </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"593\" id=\"question-wrapper-593\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Addition of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a4e28840-241f-4605-9155-661d8155bacf\" data-question=\"20\">mixture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> developed by Pius Floris to the soil </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"594\" id=\"question-wrapper-594\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The idea of zero net soil degradation </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which section contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>22-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"595\" id=\"question-wrapper-595\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to one person’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1cd1c4b4-cffc-4fd7-84d6-0cd8a8b4329d\" data-question=\"22\">motivation for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> a soil-improvement project </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"596\" id=\"question-wrapper-596\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e1effb52-a582-4981-9487-ffe6dd1c819b\" data-question=\"23\">how soil stayed healthy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> before the development of farming </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"597\" id=\"question-wrapper-597\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of different ways of collecting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0cd15c2e-fb8c-4000-9395-f58df6f188b2\" data-question=\"24\">information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> on soil degradation </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"598\" id=\"question-wrapper-598\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de636e2d-1dbe-4318-af1f-178761a42375\" data-question=\"25\">a suggestion for a way of keeping some types of soil safe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> in the near future </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"599\" id=\"question-wrapper-599\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reason why it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f41bc8de-426e-48af-bfbc-ad83863630d1\" data-question=\"26\">difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> to provide an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2b89956-cd64-4a10-8746-39048a09ceea\" data-question=\"26\">overview<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> of soil degradation </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"114b3d47-de43-417d-9cab-b9199affe0ba","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"plant remains","passagePhrase":"decomposing plants"},{"uid":"9ae7bf77-a9a7-4869-a4d9-b6350cf907c2","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"a significant effect on the climate","passagePhrase":"an ally against climate change"},{"uid":"5070ab52-dbd1-4c34-ad9c-1409dd8ab4d9","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"lock in ... holding ... store"},{"uid":"8e934874-e606-4e33-a18b-b5283ace0cc7","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"holds","passagePhrase":"store"},{"uid":"9a458296-676c-4c49-90b3-3ffd4fcea599","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"damage to property and infrastructure","passagePhrase":"damage to buildings, roads and bridges"},{"uid":"8a72c154-0263-4c52-8a96-53b4fc5df3fb","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"The main factor","passagePhrase":"the biggest problem"},{"uid":"e1effb52-a582-4981-9487-ffe6dd1c819b","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"how soil stayed healthy","passagePhrase":"when plants grow they remove nutrients from the soil ... when the plants die and decay these nutrients are returned directly to the soil"},{"uid":"1f4807cd-04df-425d-84a9-bc9c83424e36","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"may not be put back","passagePhrase":"tend not to return"},{"uid":"3317a54b-37b1-48d3-9caf-970c100e8478","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"soil degradation","passagePhrase":"soil gradually becomes less fertile"},{"uid":"d82e957c-6da2-412c-a0a0-ed1fabe193d7","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"damage","passagePhrase":"hurts"},{"uid":"1cd1c4b4-cffc-4fd7-84d6-0cd8a8b4329d","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"motivation for","passagePhrase":"the best way to ensure his trees flourished"},{"uid":"a4e28840-241f-4605-9155-661d8155bacf","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"mixture","passagePhrase":"cocktail ... cocktail"},{"uid":"a2b89956-cd64-4a10-8746-39048a09ceea","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"overview","passagePhrase":"accurate picture"},{"uid":"f41bc8de-426e-48af-bfbc-ad83863630d1","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"difficult","passagePhrase":"not easy"},{"uid":"0cd15c2e-fb8c-4000-9395-f58df6f188b2","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"information","passagePhrase":"data"},{"uid":"264726f7-02c5-4a8a-ac1b-8b77a95db54f","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"governments to be more aware of soil-related issues","passagePhrase":"bring it home to governments"},{"uid":"de636e2d-1dbe-4318-af1f-178761a42375","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"a suggestion for a way of keeping some types of soil safe","passagePhrase":"agitating for the immediate creation of protected zones for endangered soils"}]},"reading_u2_234":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>Book Review</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>The Happiness Industry: How the Government and Big Business Sold Us Well-Being</em></span></p><p><span><em>By William Davies</em></span></p><p><span>‘Happiness is the ultimate goal because it is self-evidently good. If we are asked why happiness matters we can give no further external reason. It just obviously does matter.’ This pronouncement by Richard Layard, an economist and advocate of ‘positive psychology’, summarises the beliefs of many people today. For Layard and others like him, it is obvious that the purpose of government is to promote a state of collective well-being. The only question is how to achieve it, and here positive psychology – a supposed science that not only identifies what makes people happy but also allows their happiness to be measured – can show the way. Equipped with this science, they say, governments can secure happiness in society in a way they never could in the past.</span></p><p><span>It is an astonishingly crude and simple-minded way of thinking, and for that very reason increasingly popular. Those who think in this way are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7863e7d-981c-4896-a86f-be408dcf0b70\" data-question=\"27\">oblivious to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the vast philosophical literature in which the meaning and value of happiness have been explored and questioned, and write as if nothing of any importance had been thought on the subject until it came to their attention. It was the philosopher Jeremy Bentham (1748-1832) who was more than anyone else responsible for the development of this way of thinking. For Bentham it was obvious that the human good consists of pleasure and the absence of pain. The Greek philosopher Aristotle may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"397181bd-5815-43a0-82d8-318857519eb2\" data-question=\"28\">have identified happiness with self-realisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in the 4th century BC, and thinkers throughout the ages may have struggled to reconcile the pursuit of happiness with other human values, but for Bentham all this was mere metaphysics or fiction. Without knowing anything much of him or the school of moral theory he established – since they are by education and intellectual conviction illiterate in the history of ideas – our advocates of positive psychology follow in his tracks in rejecting as outmoded and irrelevant pretty much the entirety of ethical reflection on human happiness to date.</span></p><p><span>But as William Davies notes in his recent book <em>The Happiness Industry</em>, the view that happiness is the only self-evident good is actually a way of limiting moral inquiry. One of the virtues of this rich, lucid and arresting book is that it places the current cult of happiness in a well-defined historical framework. Rightly, Davies his story with Bentham, noting that he was far more than a philosopher. Davies writes, ‘Bentham’s activities were those which we might now associate with a public sector management consultant’. In the 1790s, he wrote to the Home Office suggesting that the departments of government be linked together through a set of ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f38f4c58-9842-41c4-b834-f5c6e4201657\" data-question=\"30\">conversation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> tubes’, and to the Bank of England with a design for a printing device that could produce unforgeable banknotes. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f842646-e5a2-43bf-83d1-98610db8bfe0\" data-question=\"32\">drew up plans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> for a ‘frigidarium’ to keep <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a728791-b172-4629-9e05-35112ebb6d9b\" data-question=\"32\">provisions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> such as meat, fish, fruit and vegetables fresh. His celebrated design for a prison to be known as a ‘Panopticon’, in which prisoners would be kept in solitary confinement while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"971c5132-31dc-4d50-829b-0482229f9819\" data-question=\"33\">being visible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> at all times to the guards, was very nearly adopted. (Surprisingly, Davies does not discuss the fact that Bentham meant his Panopticon not just as a model prison but also as an instrument of control that could be applied to schools and factories.)</span></p><p><span>Bentham was also a pioneer of the ‘science of happiness’. If happiness is to be regarded as a science, it has to be measured, and Bentham suggested two <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"403095bc-fca9-48c3-b7a7-16ece2a07db2\" data-question=\"34\">ways in which this might be done<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Viewing happiness as a complex of pleasurable sensations, he suggested that it might be quantified by measuring the human pulse rate. Alternatively, money could be used as the standard for quantification: if two different goods have the same price, it can be claimed that they produce the same quantity of pleasure in the consumer. Bentham was more attracted by the latter measure. By <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5fffd0fc-b1f0-4f13-a430-d784a479e361\" data-question=\"29\">associating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> money so closely to inner experience, Davies writes, Bentham ‘set the stage for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4a56f732-c2a1-46c5-8898-92c6e5f40487\" data-question=\"29\">the entangling of psychological research and capitalism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that would shape the business practices of the twentieth century’.</span></p><p><span><em>The Happiness Industry </em>describes how the project of a science of happiness has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57d30dcd-7174-4020-9f9d-a3ffbf717ee0\" data-question=\"35\">become integral<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> to capitalism. We learn much that is interesting about how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9f5a904-93e0-42dd-8e11-dfa09e985dec\" data-question=\"35\">economic problems are being redefined and treated as psychological maladies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. In addition, Davies shows how the belief that inner states of pleasure and displeasure can be objectively measured has informed management studies and advertising. The tendency of thinkers such as J B Watson, the founder of behaviourism*, was that human beings could be shaped, or manipulated, by policymakers and managers. Watson had no factual basis for his view of human action. When he became president of the American Psychological Association in 1915, he ‘had <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c70b75aa-9f5a-49da-8e22-560ce0683ea4\" data-question=\"37\">never even studied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> a single human being’: his research had been confined to experiments on white rats. Yet Watson’s reductive model is now widely applied, with ‘behaviour change’ becoming the goal of governments: in Britain, a ‘Behaviour Insights Team’ has been established by the government to study how people can be encouraged, at minimum cost to the public purse, to live in what are considered to be socially desirable ways.</span></p><p><span>Modern <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4aaa1c0e-baff-4acb-9cd9-312729d020d5\" data-question=\"39\">industrial societies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> appear <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a82181d-0c46-481f-bd88-86cff1c04efa\" data-question=\"39\">to need the possibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of ever-increasing happiness to motivate them in their labours. But whatever its intellectual pedigree, the idea that governments should be responsible for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4b064d1-e378-403f-a327-ff3136120253\" data-question=\"40\">promoting happiness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> is always <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"6c80b725-b34b-49b9-ae54-b6ba454de041\" data-question=\"40\">a threat to human freedom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>———————–<br></span><span>* ‘behaviourism’: a branch of psychology which is concerned with observable behaviour</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>27-29</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"600\" id=\"question-wrapper-600\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the reviewer’s attitude to advocates of positive psychology? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They are wrong to reject the ideas of Bentham.</li> <li>B. They are over-influenced by their study of Bentham’s theories.</li> <li>C. They have a fresh new approach to ideas on human happiness.</li> <li>D. They are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7863e7d-981c-4896-a86f-be408dcf0b70\" data-question=\"27\">ignorant about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the ideas they should be considering.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"601\" id=\"question-wrapper-601\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The reviewer refers to the Greek philosopher Aristotle in order to suggest that happiness </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"397181bd-5815-43a0-82d8-318857519eb2\" data-question=\"28\">not be just pleasure and the absence of pain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>B. should not be the main goal of humans.</li> <li>C. is not something that should be fought for.</li> <li>D. is not just an abstract concept.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"602\" id=\"question-wrapper-602\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to Davies, Bentham’s suggestion for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5fffd0fc-b1f0-4f13-a430-d784a479e361\" data-question=\"29\">linking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> the price of goods to happiness was significant because </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. it was the first successful way of assessing happiness.</li> <li>B. it established <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4a56f732-c2a1-46c5-8898-92c6e5f40487\" data-question=\"29\">a connection between work and psychology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>C. it was the first successful example of psychological research.</li> <li>D. it involved consideration of the rights of consumers.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Complete the summary using the list of words <strong>A-G</strong> below.</p><p>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>30-34</strong> on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>Jeremy Bentham</strong></p><p>Jeremy Bentham was active in other areas besides philosophy. In the 1790s he suggested a type of technology to improve <strong>30</strong>……………………… for different Government departments. He developed a new way of printing banknotes to increase <strong>31</strong>………………………… and also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f842646-e5a2-43bf-83d1-98610db8bfe0\" data-question=\"32\">designed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> a method for the <strong>32</strong> …………………………. of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a728791-b172-4629-9e05-35112ebb6d9b\" data-question=\"32\">food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. He also drew up plans for a prison which allowed the <strong>33</strong>…………………………. of prisoners at al times, and believed the same design could be used for other institutions as well. When researching happiness, he investigated <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"403095bc-fca9-48c3-b7a7-16ece2a07db2\" data-question=\"34\">possibilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> for its <strong>34</strong>……………………….., and suggested some methods of doing this.</p><p><strong>A</strong> measurement<br><strong>B</strong> security<br><strong>C</strong> implementation<br><strong>D</strong> profits<br><strong>E</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"971c5132-31dc-4d50-829b-0482229f9819\" data-question=\"33\">observation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span><br><strong>F</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f38f4c58-9842-41c4-b834-f5c6e4201657\" data-question=\"30\">communication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span><br><strong>G</strong> preservation<br></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"603\" id=\"question-wrapper-603\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"604\" id=\"question-wrapper-604\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"605\" id=\"question-wrapper-605\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"606\" id=\"question-wrapper-606\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"607\" id=\"question-wrapper-607\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>35-40</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"608\" id=\"question-wrapper-608\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57d30dcd-7174-4020-9f9d-a3ffbf717ee0\" data-question=\"35\">One strength<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of The Happiness Industry is its discussion of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9f5a904-93e0-42dd-8e11-dfa09e985dec\" data-question=\"35\">relationship between psychology and economics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"609\" id=\"question-wrapper-609\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is more difficult to measure some emotions than others. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"610\" id=\"question-wrapper-610\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Watson’s ideas on behaviourism were supported by research on humans <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c70b75aa-9f5a-49da-8e22-560ce0683ea4\" data-question=\"37\">he carried out before 1915<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"611\" id=\"question-wrapper-611\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Watson’s ideas have been most influential on governments outside America. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"612\" id=\"question-wrapper-612\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a82181d-0c46-481f-bd88-86cff1c04efa\" data-question=\"39\">The need for happiness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> is linked to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4aaa1c0e-baff-4acb-9cd9-312729d020d5\" data-question=\"39\">industrialisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"613\" id=\"question-wrapper-613\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"6c80b725-b34b-49b9-ae54-b6ba454de041\" data-question=\"40\">A main aim of government should be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4b064d1-e378-403f-a327-ff3136120253\" data-question=\"40\">increase the happiness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> of the population. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b7863e7d-981c-4896-a86f-be408dcf0b70","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"ignorant about","passagePhrase":"oblivious to"},{"uid":"397181bd-5815-43a0-82d8-318857519eb2","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"not be just pleasure and the absence of pain","passagePhrase":"have identified happiness with self-realisation"},{"uid":"f38f4c58-9842-41c4-b834-f5c6e4201657","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"communication","passagePhrase":"conversation"},{"uid":"2f842646-e5a2-43bf-83d1-98610db8bfe0","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"designed","passagePhrase":"drew up plans"},{"uid":"6a728791-b172-4629-9e05-35112ebb6d9b","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"food","passagePhrase":"provisions"},{"uid":"971c5132-31dc-4d50-829b-0482229f9819","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"observation","passagePhrase":"being visible"},{"uid":"403095bc-fca9-48c3-b7a7-16ece2a07db2","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"possibilities","passagePhrase":"ways in which this might be done"},{"uid":"5fffd0fc-b1f0-4f13-a430-d784a479e361","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"linking","passagePhrase":"associating"},{"uid":"4a56f732-c2a1-46c5-8898-92c6e5f40487","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"a connection between work and psychology","passagePhrase":"the entangling of psychological research and capitalism"},{"uid":"57d30dcd-7174-4020-9f9d-a3ffbf717ee0","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"One strength","passagePhrase":"become integral"},{"uid":"a9f5a904-93e0-42dd-8e11-dfa09e985dec","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"relationship between psychology and economics","passagePhrase":"economic problems are being redefined and treated as psychological maladies"},{"uid":"4aaa1c0e-baff-4acb-9cd9-312729d020d5","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"industrialisation","passagePhrase":"industrial societies"},{"uid":"1a82181d-0c46-481f-bd88-86cff1c04efa","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"The need for happiness","passagePhrase":"to need the possibility"},{"uid":"e4b064d1-e378-403f-a327-ff3136120253","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"increase the happiness","passagePhrase":"promoting happiness"}]},"reading_u2_235":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong>THE IMPORTANCE OF CHILDREN’S PLAY</strong></span></h2><p><span>Brick by brick, six-year-old Alice is building a magical kingdom. Imagining fairy-tale turrets and fire-breathing dragons, wicked witches and gallant heroes, she’s creating an enchanting world. Although she isn’t aware of it, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da2d3b78-7a88-4f9d-bf03-dc98c3f0fdc6\" data-question=\"1\">this fantasy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> is helping her <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11ed916c-6769-477e-8633-4272a72555b0\" data-question=\"1\">take her first steps towards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> her capacity for creativity and so it will have important repercussions in her adult life.</span></p><p><span>Minutes later, Alice has abandoned the kingdom in favour of playing schools with her younger brother. When she bosses him around as his ‘teacher’, she’s practising how to regulate her emotions through pretence. Later on, when they tire of this and settle down with a board game, she’s learning about the need to follow rules and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3da4217-6e61-424f-b725-9a22ac361fa8\" data-question=\"2\">take turns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> with a partner.</span></p><p><span>‘Play in all its rich variety is one of the highest achievements of the human species,’ says Dr David Whitebread from the Faculty of Education at the University of Cambridge, UK. ‘It underpins how we develop as intellectual, problem-solving adults and is crucial to our success as a highly adaptable species.’</span></p><p><span>Recognizing the importance of play is not new: over two millennia ago, the Greek philosopher Plato extolled its virtues as a means of developing skills for adult life, and ideas about play-based learning have been developing since the 19th century.</span></p><p><span>But we live in changing times, and Whitebread is mindful of a worldwide decline in play, pointing out that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4cb87a81-98fa-4e89-80c0-e24cd4fe1649\" data-question=\"3\">over half<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93a4bce7-1c52-4bc0-960a-4ead73b0a3db\" data-question=\"3\">the people in the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> now live in cities. ‘The opportunities for free play, which I experienced almost every day of my childhood, are becoming increasingly scarce,’ he says. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5897febf-4990-4820-82bf-775b2483a87c\" data-question=\"4\">Outdoor play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"07063615-4144-4256-9e77-cfed7720ec7a\" data-question=\"4\">curtailed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> by perceptions of risk to do with traffic, as well as parents’ increased wish to protect their children from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a060f6d5-0ac4-4c25-94c5-76a2fea84cda\" data-question=\"5\">being the victims of crime<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, and by the emphasis on ‘earlier is better’ which is leading to greater competition <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6701ab61-aa03-4303-99e3-35ebe0c4e53b\" data-question=\"6\">in academic learning and schools<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>International bodies like the United Nations and the European Union have begun to develop policies concerned with children’s right to play, and to consider implications for leisure facilities and educational programmes. But what they often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72f653bb-f653-4d9b-9254-335a8257dfc3\" data-question=\"7\">lack<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> is the evidence to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7bc7a32a-3e4a-42a3-a0bd-d3127693af01\" data-question=\"7\">base policies on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>‘The type of play we are interested in is child-initiated, spontaneous and unpredictable – but, as soon as you ask a five-year-old “to play”, then you as the researcher have intervened,’ explains Dr Sara Baker. ‘And we want to know what the long-term impact of play is. It’s a real challenge.’</span></p><p><span>Dr Jenny Gibson agrees, pointing out that although some of the steps in the puzzle of how and why play is important have been looked at, there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"951fb047-1eb2-4a4c-8837-192b7859b211\" data-question=\"8\">very little data on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> the impact it has on the child’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f87287f7-cbde-4dc2-9580-d466e32ada50\" data-question=\"8\">later<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> life.</span></p><p><span>Now, thanks to the university’s new Centre for Research on Play in Education, Development and Learning (PEDAL), Whitebread, Baker, Gibson and a team of researchers hope to provide evidence on the role played by play in how a child develops.</span></p><p><span>‘A strong possibility is that play supports the early development of children’s self-control,’ explains Baker. ‘This is our ability to develop awareness of our own thinking progresses – it influences how effectively we go about undertaking challenging activities.’</span></p><p><span>In a study carried out by Baker with toddlers and young pre-schoolers, she found that children with greater self-control solved problems more quickly when exploring an unfamiliar set-up requiring scientific reasoning. ‘This sort of evidence makes up think that giving children the chance to play will make them more successful problem-solvers in the long run.’</span></p><p><span>If playful experiences do facilitate this aspect of development, say the researchers, it could be extremely significant for educational practices, because the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b98d752-3599-4f09-9279-e6d218acd3d1\" data-question=\"9\">ability to self-regulate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eb62fc85-f174-4836-9f7f-7cbf4dcf1eb7\" data-question=\"9\">has been shown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"225e1284-510c-4974-8b2c-735d7bae6994\" data-question=\"9\">a key predictor of academic performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Gibson adds: ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df91878c-7066-4220-a28a-832db691a2a6\" data-question=\"10\">Playful behavior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> is also an important indicator of healthy social and emotional development. In my previous research, I investigated how observing children at play can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"adedf586-6bf5-4f03-8319-4bf47271abbf\" data-question=\"10\">give us important clues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06016620-ddeb-40d0-a9ff-5e0f7b9b6903\" data-question=\"10\">their well-being<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> and can even be useful in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06016620-ddeb-40d0-a9ff-5e0f7b9b6903\" data-question=\"10\">the diagnosis of neurodevelopmental disorders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> like autism.’</span></p><p><span>Whitebread’s recent research has involved developing a play-based approach to supporting children’s writing. ‘Many primary school children find writing difficult, but we showed in a previous study that a playful stimulus was far more effective than an instructional one.’ Children wrote longer and better-structured stories when they first played with dolls representing characters in the story. In the latest study, children first created their story with Lego*, with similar results. ‘Many teachers commented that they had always previously had children saying they didn’t know <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0cdc529-2722-41f8-9b56-818699bb6594\" data-question=\"12\">what to write about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. With the Lego building, however, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"357071e5-f261-43d8-bb84-1ff5f17f7ba4\" data-question=\"12\">not a single child said this<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> through the whole year of the project.’</span></p><p><span>Whitebread, who directs PEDAL, trained as a primary school teacher in the early 1970s, when, as he describes, ‘the teaching of young children was largely a quiet backwater, untroubled by any serious intellectual debate or controversy.’ Now, the landscape is very different, with hotly debated topics such as school starting age.</span></p><p><span>‘Somehow <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5aa693bf-1263-40dc-b901-a1a88250a586\" data-question=\"13\">the importance of play has been lost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in recent decades. It’s regarded as something trivial, or even as something negative that contrasts with “work”. Let’s not lose sight of its benefits, and the fundamental contributions it makes to human achievements in the arts, sciences and technology. Let’s make sure children have a rich diet of play experiences.’</span></p><p>———————————-<br> <span>* Lego: coloured plastic building blocks and other pieces that can be joined together</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Complete the notes below.<br>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.<br>Write your answers in boxes <strong>1-8</strong> on your answer sheet.<br></p><p><strong>Children’s play</strong></p><p><strong>Uses of children’s play</strong></p><p>• building <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da2d3b78-7a88-4f9d-bf03-dc98c3f0fdc6\" data-question=\"1\">a ‘magical kingdom’<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> may help develop <strong>1</strong>…………………………………</p><p>• board games involve <strong>2 </strong>……………………………. and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3da4217-6e61-424f-b725-9a22ac361fa8\" data-question=\"2\">turn-taking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></p><p><strong>Recent changes affecting children’s play</strong></p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93a4bce7-1c52-4bc0-960a-4ead73b0a3db\" data-question=\"3\">populations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of <strong>3 </strong>………………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4cb87a81-98fa-4e89-80c0-e24cd4fe1649\" data-question=\"3\">have grown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></p><p>• opportunities for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5897febf-4990-4820-82bf-775b2483a87c\" data-question=\"4\">free play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"07063615-4144-4256-9e77-cfed7720ec7a\" data-question=\"4\">limited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> due to</p><p>– fear of <strong>4</strong> ………………………………</p><p>– fear of <strong>5</strong> ………………………………</p><p>– increased <strong>6</strong> …………………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6701ab61-aa03-4303-99e3-35ebe0c4e53b\" data-question=\"6\">in schools<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></p><p><strong>International policies on children’s play</strong></p><p>• it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72f653bb-f653-4d9b-9254-335a8257dfc3\" data-question=\"7\">difficult to find<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> 7 …………………………… to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7bc7a32a-3e4a-42a3-a0bd-d3127693af01\" data-question=\"7\">support new policies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"951fb047-1eb2-4a4c-8837-192b7859b211\" data-question=\"8\">research needs to study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> the impact of play on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f87287f7-cbde-4dc2-9580-d466e32ada50\" data-question=\"8\">the rest of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> the child’s 8 ……………………………..</p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"294\" id=\"question-wrapper-294\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CREATIVITY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"295\" id=\"question-wrapper-295\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RULES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"296\" id=\"question-wrapper-296\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CITIES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"297\" id=\"question-wrapper-297\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRAFFIC</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"298\" id=\"question-wrapper-298\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CRIME</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"299\" id=\"question-wrapper-299\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMPETITION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"300\" id=\"question-wrapper-300\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EVIDENCE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"301\" id=\"question-wrapper-301\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LIFE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?<br></span><span>In boxes <strong>9-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE </strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"302\" id=\"question-wrapper-302\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Children with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b98d752-3599-4f09-9279-e6d218acd3d1\" data-question=\"9\">good self-control<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eb62fc85-f174-4836-9f7f-7cbf4dcf1eb7\" data-question=\"9\">are known to be likely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"225e1284-510c-4974-8b2c-735d7bae6994\" data-question=\"9\">do well at school<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> later on. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"303\" id=\"question-wrapper-303\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df91878c-7066-4220-a28a-832db691a2a6\" data-question=\"10\">The way a child plays<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"adedf586-6bf5-4f03-8319-4bf47271abbf\" data-question=\"10\">provide information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06016620-ddeb-40d0-a9ff-5e0f7b9b6903\" data-question=\"10\">possible medical problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"304\" id=\"question-wrapper-304\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Playing with dolls was found to benefit girls’ writing more than boys’ writing. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"305\" id=\"question-wrapper-305\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Children <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"357071e5-f261-43d8-bb84-1ff5f17f7ba4\" data-question=\"12\">had problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0cdc529-2722-41f8-9b56-818699bb6594\" data-question=\"12\">thinking up ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> when they first <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0cdc529-2722-41f8-9b56-818699bb6594\" data-question=\"12\">created the story<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> with Lego. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"306\" id=\"question-wrapper-306\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People nowadays regard children’s play as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5aa693bf-1263-40dc-b901-a1a88250a586\" data-question=\"13\">less significant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> than they did in the past. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"da2d3b78-7a88-4f9d-bf03-dc98c3f0fdc6","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"a ‘magical kingdom’","passagePhrase":"this fantasy"},{"uid":"11ed916c-6769-477e-8633-4272a72555b0","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"take her first steps towards"},{"uid":"b3da4217-6e61-424f-b725-9a22ac361fa8","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"turn-taking","passagePhrase":"take turns"},{"uid":"4cb87a81-98fa-4e89-80c0-e24cd4fe1649","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"have grown","passagePhrase":"over half"},{"uid":"93a4bce7-1c52-4bc0-960a-4ead73b0a3db","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"populations","passagePhrase":"the people in the world"},{"uid":"5897febf-4990-4820-82bf-775b2483a87c","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"free play","passagePhrase":"Outdoor play"},{"uid":"07063615-4144-4256-9e77-cfed7720ec7a","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"limited","passagePhrase":"curtailed"},{"uid":"a060f6d5-0ac4-4c25-94c5-76a2fea84cda","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"being the victims of crime"},{"uid":"6701ab61-aa03-4303-99e3-35ebe0c4e53b","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"in schools","passagePhrase":"in academic learning and schools"},{"uid":"72f653bb-f653-4d9b-9254-335a8257dfc3","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"difficult to find","passagePhrase":"lack"},{"uid":"7bc7a32a-3e4a-42a3-a0bd-d3127693af01","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"support new policies","passagePhrase":"base policies on"},{"uid":"951fb047-1eb2-4a4c-8837-192b7859b211","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"research needs to study","passagePhrase":"very little data on"},{"uid":"f87287f7-cbde-4dc2-9580-d466e32ada50","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"the rest of","passagePhrase":"later"},{"uid":"1b98d752-3599-4f09-9279-e6d218acd3d1","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"good self-control","passagePhrase":"ability to self-regulate"},{"uid":"eb62fc85-f174-4836-9f7f-7cbf4dcf1eb7","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"are known to be likely","passagePhrase":"has been shown"},{"uid":"225e1284-510c-4974-8b2c-735d7bae6994","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"do well at school","passagePhrase":"a key predictor of academic performance"},{"uid":"df91878c-7066-4220-a28a-832db691a2a6","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"The way a child plays","passagePhrase":"Playful behavior"},{"uid":"adedf586-6bf5-4f03-8319-4bf47271abbf","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"provide information","passagePhrase":"give us important clues"},{"uid":"06016620-ddeb-40d0-a9ff-5e0f7b9b6903","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"possible medical problems","passagePhrase":"their well-being ... the diagnosis of neurodevelopmental disorders"},{"uid":"d0cdc529-2722-41f8-9b56-818699bb6594","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"thinking up ideas ... created the story","passagePhrase":"what to write about"},{"uid":"5aa693bf-1263-40dc-b901-a1a88250a586","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"less significant","passagePhrase":"the importance of play has been lost"}]},"reading_u2_236":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>The growth of bike-sharing schemes around the world</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>How Dutch engineer Luud Schimmelpennink helped to devise urban bike-sharing schemes</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>The original idea for an urban bike-sharing scheme dates back to a summer’s day in Amsterdam in 1965. Provo, the organization that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a9f2e36-3359-4d95-8abb-874a3bd1cad5\" data-question=\"23\">came up with the idea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4875511a-a427-415b-824f-946920bbfbc5\" data-question=\"23\">a group of Dutch<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> activists who wanted to change society. They believed the scheme, which was known as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d80da758-3139-46d3-aab9-7ddd73842db5\" data-question=\"18\">the Witte Fietsenplan<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a72214f-fa7b-40da-8614-84db562d9594\" data-question=\"18\">was an answer to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1aebb93-77d5-4b88-9ed3-91589d5df446\" data-question=\"24\">perceived threats of air pollution and consumerism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. In the centre of Amsterdam, they painted a small number of used bikes white. They also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"554c6e17-19fa-4a8a-b035-a729422ae0c7\" data-question=\"25\">distributed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> leaflets <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b8685cc-ab80-4265-a7c3-d9d815ab857e\" data-question=\"25\">describing the dangers of cars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and inviting people to use the white bikes. The bikes were then left unlocked at various locations around the city, to be used by anyone in need of transport.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Luud Schimmelpennink, a Dutch industrial engineer who still lives and cycles in Amsterdam, was heavily involved in the original scheme. He recalls how the scheme succeeded in attracting a great deal of attention – particularly when it came to publicising Provo’s aims – but struggled to get off the ground. The police were opposed to Provo’s initiatives and almost <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fafd5115-36c5-4068-af84-23a925db625e\" data-question=\"26\">as soon as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3843de7-99fa-4ed0-832e-a8b5106a5a5b\" data-question=\"26\">the white bikes were distributed around the city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eca388c-a3a1-40c1-a56d-8cd91189bcb3\" data-question=\"26\">removed them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. However, for Schimmelpennink and for bike-sharing schemes in general, this was just the beginning. ‘The first Witte Fietsenplan was just a symbolic thing,’ he says. ‘We painted a few bikes white, that was all. Things got more serious when I became a member of the Amsterdam city council two years later.’</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Schimmelpennink seized this opportunity to present a more elaborate Witte Fietsenplan to the city council. ‘My idea was that the municipality of Amsterdam would distribute 10,000 white bikes over the city, for everyone to use,’ he explains. ‘I made serious calculations. It turned out that a white bicycle – per person, per kilometer – would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4a6c8329-3dfe-4f8a-8a7b-3d49ec3a1981\" data-question=\"17\">cost the municipality only 10% of what it contributed to public transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> per person per kilometer.’ Nevertheless, the council unanimously <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cceb123d-60d4-4ba8-906f-82fedbbf8d78\" data-question=\"15\">rejected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33e861e1-a0ad-4f45-b75e-13f6806fdf80\" data-question=\"15\">plan<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. ‘They said that the bicycle belongs to the past. They saw a glorious future for the car,’ says Schimmelpennink. But he was not in the least discouraged.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>Schimmelpennink never stopped believing in bike-sharing, and in the mid-90s, two Danes asked for his help to set up a system in Copenhagen. The result was the world’s first large-scale bike-share programme. It worked on a deposit: ‘You dropped a coin in the bike and when you returned it, you got your money back.’ After setting up the Danish system, Schimmelpennink decided to try his luck again in the Netherlands – and this time he succeeded in arousing the interest of the Dutch Ministry of Transport. ‘Times had changed,’ he recalls. ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5b3c7f17-b56b-449d-87dc-9cc3dd710c6d\" data-question=\"20\">People had become more environmentally conscious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, and the Danish experiment had proved that bike-sharing was a real possibility.’ A new Witte Fietsenplan was launched in 1999 in Amsterdam. However, riding a white bike was no longer free; it cost one guilder per trip and payment was made with a chip card developed by the Dutch bank Postbank. Schimmelpennink designed conspicuous, sturdy white bikes locked in special racks which could be opened with the chip card – the plan started with 250 bikes, distributed over five stations.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Theo Molenaar, who was a system designer for the project, worked alongside Schimmelpennink. ‘I remember when we were testing the bike racks, he announced that he had already designed better ones. But of course, we had to go through with the ones we had.’ The system, however, was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"52b32db1-e139-4e86-a92b-77f471a1468b\" data-question=\"14\">prone to vandalism and theft<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. ‘After every weekend there would always be a couple of bikes missing,’ Molenaar says. ‘I really have no idea what people did with them, because they could instantly be recognised as white bikes.’ But the biggest blow came when Postbank decided to abolish the chip card, because it wasn’t profitable. ‘That chip card was pivotal to the system,’ Molenaar says. ‘To continue the project we would have needed to set up another system, but the business partner <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"482d914a-7326-4cd2-9dee-d0cda093db50\" data-question=\"19\">had lost interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.’</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>Schimmelpennink was disappointed, but – characteristically – not for long. In 2002 he got a call from the French advertising corporation JC Decaux, who wanted to set up his bike-sharing scheme in Vienna. ‘That went really well. After Vienna, they set up a system in Lyon. Then in 2007, Paris followed. That was a decisive moment in the history of bike-sharing.’ The huge and unexpected success of the Parisian bike-sharing programme, which now boasts more than 20,000 bicycles, inspired cities all over the world to set up their own schemes, all modelled on Schimmelpennink’s. ‘It’s wonderful that this happened,’ he says. ‘But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1125a82-fe6c-4486-8cbe-bbad0342fa2e\" data-question=\"16\">financially I didn’t really benefit from it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, because I never filed for a patent.’</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>In Amsterdam today, 38% of all trips are made by bike and, along with Copenhagen, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a86385c5-ad9f-474e-ab7e-f24c2ab948c6\" data-question=\"21\">is regarded as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> one of the two <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7307b8fa-e72a-4f79-b25e-7ed538fd65bc\" data-question=\"21\">most cycle-friendly capitals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in the world – but the city never got another Witte Fietsenplan. Molenaar believes this may be because everybody in Amsterdam already has a bike. Schimmelpennink, however, cannot see that this changes Amsterdam’s need for a bike-sharing scheme. ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a3b0526-1d54-418d-b12c-b301bca3b052\" data-question=\"22\">People who travel on the underground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> don’t carry their bikes around. But often they need additional transport to reach their final destination.’ Although he thinks it is strange that a city like Amsterdam does not have a successful bike-sharing scheme, he is optimistic about the future. ‘In the ‘60s we didn’t stand a chance because people were prepared to give their lives to keep cars in the city. But that mentality has totally changed. Today everybody longs for cities that are not dominated by cars.’</span></p><p><span> </span><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G</strong>.<br></span><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?<br></span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-18</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"307\" id=\"question-wrapper-307\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"52b32db1-e139-4e86-a92b-77f471a1468b\" data-question=\"14\">how people misused<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> a bike-sharing scheme </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"308\" id=\"question-wrapper-308\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of why a proposed bike-sharing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33e861e1-a0ad-4f45-b75e-13f6806fdf80\" data-question=\"15\">scheme<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cceb123d-60d4-4ba8-906f-82fedbbf8d78\" data-question=\"15\">turned down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"309\" id=\"question-wrapper-309\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to a person being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1125a82-fe6c-4486-8cbe-bbad0342fa2e\" data-question=\"16\">unable to profit their work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"310\" id=\"question-wrapper-310\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4a6c8329-3dfe-4f8a-8a7b-3d49ec3a1981\" data-question=\"17\">the potential savings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> a bike-sharing scheme would bring </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"311\" id=\"question-wrapper-311\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to the problems <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d80da758-3139-46d3-aab9-7ddd73842db5\" data-question=\"18\">a bike-sharing scheme<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a72214f-fa7b-40da-8614-84db562d9594\" data-question=\"18\">was intended to solve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E<br></strong></span><em>Write the correct letters in boxes <strong>19</strong> and <strong>20</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></p><p><span>Which <strong>TWO</strong> of the following statements are made in the text about the Amsterdam bike-sharing scheme of 1999?</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> It was initially opposed by a government department.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> It failed when a partner in the scheme <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"482d914a-7326-4cd2-9dee-d0cda093db50\" data-question=\"19\">withdrew support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> It aimed to be more successful than the Copenhagen scheme.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> It was made possible by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5b3c7f17-b56b-449d-87dc-9cc3dd710c6d\" data-question=\"20\">a change in people’s attitudes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> It attracted interest from a range of bike designers.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"312\" id=\"question-wrapper-312\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"313\" id=\"question-wrapper-313\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E<br></strong><em>Write the correct letters in boxes<strong> 21</strong> and <strong>22</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span>Which <strong>TWO</strong> of the following statements are made in the text about Amsterdam today?</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> The majority of residents would like to prevent all cars from entering the city.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> There is little likelihood of the city having another bike-sharing scheme.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> More trips in the city are made by bike than by any other form of transport.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> A bike-sharing scheme would benefit <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a3b0526-1d54-418d-b12c-b301bca3b052\" data-question=\"22\">residents who use public transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> The city <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a86385c5-ad9f-474e-ab7e-f24c2ab948c6\" data-question=\"21\">has a reputation as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7307b8fa-e72a-4f79-b25e-7ed538fd65bc\" data-question=\"21\">a place that welcomes cyclists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"314\" id=\"question-wrapper-314\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D/E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"315\" id=\"question-wrapper-315\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D/E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>23-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>The first urban bike-sharing scheme</strong></span></h3><p><span>The first bike-sharing scheme <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a9f2e36-3359-4d95-8abb-874a3bd1cad5\" data-question=\"23\">was the idea of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4875511a-a427-415b-824f-946920bbfbc5\" data-question=\"23\">the Dutch group<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> Provo. The people who belonged to this group were<strong> 23</strong>……………………….. They were concerned about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1aebb93-77d5-4b88-9ed3-91589d5df446\" data-question=\"24\">damage to the environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> and about <strong>24 </strong>………………………….., and believed that the bike-sharing scheme would draw attention to these issues. As well as painting some bikes white, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"554c6e17-19fa-4a8a-b035-a729422ae0c7\" data-question=\"25\">handed out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <strong>25</strong> …………………….. that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b8685cc-ab80-4265-a7c3-d9d815ab857e\" data-question=\"25\">condemned the use of cars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>However, the scheme was not a great success: almost <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fafd5115-36c5-4068-af84-23a925db625e\" data-question=\"26\">as quickly as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> Provo <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3843de7-99fa-4ed0-832e-a8b5106a5a5b\" data-question=\"26\">left the bikes around the city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, the <strong>26 </strong>………………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eca388c-a3a1-40c1-a56d-8cd91189bcb3\" data-question=\"26\">Took them away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. According to Schimmelpennink, the scheme was intended to be symbolic. The idea was to get people thinking about the issues.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"316\" id=\"question-wrapper-316\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ACTIVISTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"317\" id=\"question-wrapper-317\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CONSUMERISM</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"318\" id=\"question-wrapper-318\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LEAFLETS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"319\" id=\"question-wrapper-319\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POLICE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"6a9f2e36-3359-4d95-8abb-874a3bd1cad5","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"was the idea of","passagePhrase":"came up with the idea"},{"uid":"4875511a-a427-415b-824f-946920bbfbc5","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"the Dutch group","passagePhrase":"a group of Dutch"},{"uid":"d80da758-3139-46d3-aab9-7ddd73842db5","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"a bike-sharing scheme","passagePhrase":"the Witte Fietsenplan"},{"uid":"2a72214f-fa7b-40da-8614-84db562d9594","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"was intended to solve","passagePhrase":"was an answer to"},{"uid":"c1aebb93-77d5-4b88-9ed3-91589d5df446","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"damage to the environment","passagePhrase":"perceived threats of air pollution and consumerism"},{"uid":"554c6e17-19fa-4a8a-b035-a729422ae0c7","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"handed out","passagePhrase":"distributed"},{"uid":"8b8685cc-ab80-4265-a7c3-d9d815ab857e","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"condemned the use of cars","passagePhrase":"describing the dangers of cars"},{"uid":"fafd5115-36c5-4068-af84-23a925db625e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"as quickly as","passagePhrase":"as soon as"},{"uid":"f3843de7-99fa-4ed0-832e-a8b5106a5a5b","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"left the bikes around the city","passagePhrase":"the white bikes were distributed around the city"},{"uid":"3eca388c-a3a1-40c1-a56d-8cd91189bcb3","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Took them away","passagePhrase":"removed them"},{"uid":"4a6c8329-3dfe-4f8a-8a7b-3d49ec3a1981","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"the potential savings","passagePhrase":"cost the municipality only 10% of what it contributed to public transport"},{"uid":"cceb123d-60d4-4ba8-906f-82fedbbf8d78","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"turned down","passagePhrase":"rejected"},{"uid":"33e861e1-a0ad-4f45-b75e-13f6806fdf80","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"scheme","passagePhrase":"plan"},{"uid":"5b3c7f17-b56b-449d-87dc-9cc3dd710c6d","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"a change in people’s attitudes","passagePhrase":"People had become more environmentally conscious"},{"uid":"52b32db1-e139-4e86-a92b-77f471a1468b","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"how people misused","passagePhrase":"prone to vandalism and theft"},{"uid":"482d914a-7326-4cd2-9dee-d0cda093db50","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"withdrew support","passagePhrase":"had lost interest"},{"uid":"c1125a82-fe6c-4486-8cbe-bbad0342fa2e","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"unable to profit their work","passagePhrase":"financially I didn’t really benefit from it"},{"uid":"a86385c5-ad9f-474e-ab7e-f24c2ab948c6","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"has a reputation as","passagePhrase":"is regarded as"},{"uid":"7307b8fa-e72a-4f79-b25e-7ed538fd65bc","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"a place that welcomes cyclists","passagePhrase":"most cycle-friendly capitals"},{"uid":"2a3b0526-1d54-418d-b12c-b301bca3b052","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"residents who use public transport","passagePhrase":"People who travel on the underground"}]},"reading_u2_237":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>Motivational factors and the hospitality industry</strong></span></h2><p><span>A critical ingredient in the success of hotels is developing and maintaining superior performance from their employees. How is that accomplished? What Human Resource Management (HRM) practices should organizations invest in to acquire and retain great employees?</span></p><p><span>Some hotels aim to provide superior working conditions for their employees. The idea originated from workplaces – usually in the non-service sector – that emphasized fun and enjoyment as part of work-life balance. By contrast, the service sector, and more specifically hotels, has traditionally not extended these practices to address basic employee needs, such as good working conditions.</span></p><p><span>Pfeffer (1994) emphasizes that in order to succeed in a global business environment, organizations must make investment in Human Resource Management (HRM) to allow them to acquire employees who possess better skills and capabilities than their competitors. This investment will be to their competitive advantage. Despite this recognition of the importance of employee development, the hospitality industry has historically been dominated by underdeveloped HR practices (Lucas, 2002).</span></p><p><span>Lucas also points out that ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe2c2a47-a893-45b7-a849-56aae22bc6f4\" data-question=\"29\">the substance of HRM practices does not appear to be designed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> foster constructive relations with employees or to represent a managerial approach that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce542f16-c4d6-4a69-9c89-d7a0bad795be\" data-question=\"29\">enables developing and drawing out the full potential of people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, even though employees may be broadly satisfied with many aspects of their work’ (Lucas, 2002). In addition, or maybe as a result, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2309ef97-283d-4288-9be5-acf5b7b31c0f\" data-question=\"31\">high employee turnover<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> has been a recurring problem throughout the hospitality industry. Among the many cited reasons are low compensation, inadequate benefits, poor working conditions and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8bd738e8-2f7f-4aeb-a39a-71c6fcd06809\" data-question=\"32\">compromised employee morale and attitudes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> (Maroudas et al., 2008).</span></p><p><span>Ng and Sorensen (2008) demonstrated that when managers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d7ccb9c-792f-46ce-90a1-c33aa0e6d6d3\" data-question=\"28\">provide recognition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to employees, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d7ccb9c-792f-46ce-90a1-c33aa0e6d6d3\" data-question=\"28\">motivate employees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f21e73b-b700-41e9-87e9-4a1cc7c12f00\" data-question=\"30\">work together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d7ccb9c-792f-46ce-90a1-c33aa0e6d6d3\" data-question=\"28\">remove obstacles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> preventing effective performance, employees feel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cb849c8-87e1-47eb-8ddc-994b99616580\" data-question=\"28\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64b43611-7e6a-4a68-a445-d69dcf5f5fe9\" data-question=\"30\">more obligated to stay<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> with the company<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. This was succinctly summarized by Michel et al. (2013): ‘[P]roviding support to employees gives them the confidence to perform their jobs better and the motivation to stay with the organization.’ Hospitality organizations can therefore enhance employee motivation and retention through the development and improvement of their working conditions. These conditions are inherently linked to the working environment.</span></p><p><span>While it seems likely that employees’ reactions to their job characteristics could be affected by a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5e278f4-e9fb-49d7-b1e7-779fb6bfb1b4\" data-question=\"33\">predisposition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> to view their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"523ef32a-b7a2-4fca-affa-34730a7b28d9\" data-question=\"33\">work environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6973f1d8-9841-418e-9b75-d221f3dcfbb5\" data-question=\"33\">negatively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, no evidence exists to support this hypothesis (Spector et al., 2000). However, given the opportunity, many people will find something to complain about in relation to their workplace (Poulston, 2009). There is a strong link between the perceptions of employees and particular factors of their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"523ef32a-b7a2-4fca-affa-34730a7b28d9\" data-question=\"33\">work environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> that are separate from the work itself, including company policies, salary and vacations.</span></p><p><span>Such conditions are particularly troubling for the luxury hotel market, where high-quality service, requiring a sophisticated approach to HRM, is recognized as a critical source of competitive advantage (Maroudas et al., 2008). In a real sense, the services of hotel employees represent their industry (Schneider and Bowen, 1993). This representation has commonly been limited to guest experiences. This suggests that there has been a dichotomy between the guest environment provided in luxury hotels and the working conditions of their employees.</span></p><p><span>It is therefore essential for hotel management to develop HRM practices that enable them to inspire and retain competent employees. This requires an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"805dc0df-f210-441a-975e-bb2d19757092\" data-question=\"27\">understand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>ing of what motivates employees at different levels of management and different stages of their careers (Enz and Siguaw, 2000). This implies that it is beneficial for hotel managers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"805dc0df-f210-441a-975e-bb2d19757092\" data-question=\"27\">understand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> what practices are most favorable to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d639b20-ecbb-42e4-bc92-a90b57b86790\" data-question=\"27\">increase employee satisfaction and retention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Herzberg (1966) proposes that people have two major types of needs, the first being extrinsic motivation factors relating to the context in which work is performed, rather than the work itself. These include working conditions and job security. When these factors are unfavorable, job dissatisfaction may result. Significantly, though, just fulfilling <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b73fdc8-9370-4e76-bd8b-fd0f3f937a77\" data-question=\"34\">these needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> does not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee654c6c-cc4d-4d5a-8bb1-31a5734401e0\" data-question=\"34\">result in satisfaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, but only in the reduction of dissatisfaction (Maroudas et al., 2008).</span></p><p><span>Employees also have intrinsic motivation needs or motivators, which include such factors as achievement and recognition. Unlike extrinsic factors, motivator factors may ideally result in job satisfaction (Maroudas et al., 2008). Herzberg’s (1966) theory discusses the need for a ‘balance’ of these two types of needs.</span></p><p><span>The impact of fun as a motivating factor at work has also been explored. For example, Tews, Michel and Stafford (2013) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15120a48-b6fa-4fbd-bd49-843d9600ab07\" data-question=\"36\">conducted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e60989c-9674-40b7-b416-b9d08495a131\" data-question=\"36\">study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> focusing on staff from a chain of themed restaurants in the United States. It was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f40d101b-b12b-4b03-9462-8d1d32879e4b\" data-question=\"37\">found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> that fun activities <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd2b4753-1ab0-4602-8e82-acd374b400c3\" data-question=\"37\">had a favorable impact on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> performance and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56439275-f907-4797-9247-677a79b1c68a\" data-question=\"38\">manager support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> for fun had a favorable impact in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b8c7671-53ed-477f-bfad-09a4be5c9c8f\" data-question=\"38\">reducing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> turnover. Their findings support the view that fun may indeed have a beneficial effect, but the framing of that fun <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f47b6474-b3dc-4d86-91fa-a6bf659cd87b\" data-question=\"39\">must be carefully aligned with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> both organizational goals and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbb6511c-cf98-417e-9c7c-5569fa7e8d11\" data-question=\"40\">employee<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> characteristics. ‘Managers must learn how to achieve the delicate balance of allowing employees the freedom to enjoy themselves at work while simultaneously high levels of performance’ (Tews et al., 2013).</span></p><p><span>Deery (2008) has recommended several actions that can be adopted at the organizational level to retain good staff as well as assist in balancing work and family life. Those particularly appropriate to the hospitality industry include <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d90dcc63-d57d-4cd3-be05-2948c7687577\" data-question=\"35\">allowing adequate breaks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> during the working day, staff functions that involve families, and providing health and well-being opportunities.</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions <strong>27-31</strong>) and the list of researchers below.<br></span><span>Match each statement with the correct researcher, <strong>A-F</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>NB</strong> <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Researchers</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Pfeffer<br></span><span><strong>B</strong> Lucas<br></span><span><strong>C</strong> Maroudas et al.<br></span><span><strong>D</strong> Ng and Sorensen<br></span><span><strong>E</strong> Enz and Siguaw<br></span><span><strong>F</strong> Deery</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"320\" id=\"question-wrapper-320\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Hotel managers need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"805dc0df-f210-441a-975e-bb2d19757092\" data-question=\"27\">know<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> what would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d639b20-ecbb-42e4-bc92-a90b57b86790\" data-question=\"27\">encourage good staff to remain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"321\" id=\"question-wrapper-321\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d7ccb9c-792f-46ce-90a1-c33aa0e6d6d3\" data-question=\"28\">The actions of managers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> may make staff feel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cb849c8-87e1-47eb-8ddc-994b99616580\" data-question=\"28\">they shouldn’t move<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to a different employer. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"322\" id=\"question-wrapper-322\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe2c2a47-a893-45b7-a849-56aae22bc6f4\" data-question=\"29\">Little is done<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> in the hospitality industry to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce542f16-c4d6-4a69-9c89-d7a0bad795be\" data-question=\"29\">help workers improve their skills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"323\" id=\"question-wrapper-323\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Staff <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64b43611-7e6a-4a68-a445-d69dcf5f5fe9\" data-question=\"30\">are less likely to change jobs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f21e73b-b700-41e9-87e9-4a1cc7c12f00\" data-question=\"30\">cooperation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> is encouraged. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"324\" id=\"question-wrapper-324\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Dissatisfaction with pay is not the only reason why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2309ef97-283d-4288-9be5-acf5b7b31c0f\" data-question=\"31\">hospitality workers change jobs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?<br></span><span>In boxes <strong>32-35</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"325\" id=\"question-wrapper-325\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One reason for high staff turnover in the hospitality industry is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8bd738e8-2f7f-4aeb-a39a-71c6fcd06809\" data-question=\"32\">poor morale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"326\" id=\"question-wrapper-326\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Research has shown that staff have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5e278f4-e9fb-49d7-b1e7-779fb6bfb1b4\" data-question=\"33\">tendency<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6973f1d8-9841-418e-9b75-d221f3dcfbb5\" data-question=\"33\">dislike<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"523ef32a-b7a2-4fca-affa-34730a7b28d9\" data-question=\"33\">their workplace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"327\" id=\"question-wrapper-327\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> An improvement in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b73fdc8-9370-4e76-bd8b-fd0f3f937a77\" data-question=\"34\">working conditions and job security<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee654c6c-cc4d-4d5a-8bb1-31a5734401e0\" data-question=\"34\">makes staff satisfied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> with their jobs. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"328\" id=\"question-wrapper-328\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Staff should be allowed to choose when they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d90dcc63-d57d-4cd3-be05-2948c7687577\" data-question=\"35\">take breaks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> during the working day. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>36-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>Fun at work</strong></span></h3><p><span>Tews, Michel and Stafford <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15120a48-b6fa-4fbd-bd49-843d9600ab07\" data-question=\"36\">carried out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> research on staff in an American chain of <strong>36</strong>……………………… . They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f40d101b-b12b-4b03-9462-8d1d32879e4b\" data-question=\"37\">discovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a62a0da5-34d5-493d-9efc-cb809737cbe0\" data-question=\"37\">activities designed for staff<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to have fun <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd2b4753-1ab0-4602-8e82-acd374b400c3\" data-question=\"37\">improved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> their <strong>37</strong>……………………… , and that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56439275-f907-4797-9247-677a79b1c68a\" data-question=\"38\">management involvement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> led to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b8c7671-53ed-477f-bfad-09a4be5c9c8f\" data-question=\"38\">lower<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> staff <strong>38</strong> ………………………….. . They also found that the activities <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f47b6474-b3dc-4d86-91fa-a6bf659cd87b\" data-question=\"39\">needed to fit with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> both the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2496b5cc-8e1f-4d5a-9857-3abc644c1159\" data-question=\"39\">company’s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <strong>39</strong> ………………………….. and the <strong>40</strong> …………………………. Of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbb6511c-cf98-417e-9c7c-5569fa7e8d11\" data-question=\"40\">staff<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. A balance was required between a degree of freedom and maintaining work standards.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"329\" id=\"question-wrapper-329\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RESTAURANTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"330\" id=\"question-wrapper-330\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PERFORMANCE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"331\" id=\"question-wrapper-331\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TURNOVER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"332\" id=\"question-wrapper-332\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GOALS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"333\" id=\"question-wrapper-333\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CHARACTERISTICS</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"fe2c2a47-a893-45b7-a849-56aae22bc6f4","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Little is done","passagePhrase":"the substance of HRM practices does not appear to be designed to"},{"uid":"ce542f16-c4d6-4a69-9c89-d7a0bad795be","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"help workers improve their skills","passagePhrase":"enables developing and drawing out the full potential of people"},{"uid":"2309ef97-283d-4288-9be5-acf5b7b31c0f","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"hospitality workers change jobs","passagePhrase":"high employee turnover"},{"uid":"8bd738e8-2f7f-4aeb-a39a-71c6fcd06809","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"poor morale","passagePhrase":"compromised employee morale and attitudes"},{"uid":"6d7ccb9c-792f-46ce-90a1-c33aa0e6d6d3","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The actions of managers","passagePhrase":"provide recognition ... motivate employees ... remove obstacles"},{"uid":"5f21e73b-b700-41e9-87e9-4a1cc7c12f00","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"cooperation","passagePhrase":"work together"},{"uid":"5cb849c8-87e1-47eb-8ddc-994b99616580","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"they shouldn’t move","passagePhrase":"more obligated to stay with the company"},{"uid":"64b43611-7e6a-4a68-a445-d69dcf5f5fe9","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"are less likely to change jobs","passagePhrase":"more obligated to stay"},{"uid":"d5e278f4-e9fb-49d7-b1e7-779fb6bfb1b4","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"tendency","passagePhrase":"predisposition"},{"uid":"523ef32a-b7a2-4fca-affa-34730a7b28d9","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"their workplace","passagePhrase":"work environment ... work environment"},{"uid":"6973f1d8-9841-418e-9b75-d221f3dcfbb5","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"dislike","passagePhrase":"negatively"},{"uid":"805dc0df-f210-441a-975e-bb2d19757092","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"know","passagePhrase":"understand ... understand"},{"uid":"1d639b20-ecbb-42e4-bc92-a90b57b86790","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"encourage good staff to remain","passagePhrase":"increase employee satisfaction and retention"},{"uid":"2b73fdc8-9370-4e76-bd8b-fd0f3f937a77","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"working conditions and job security","passagePhrase":"these needs"},{"uid":"ee654c6c-cc4d-4d5a-8bb1-31a5734401e0","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"makes staff satisfied","passagePhrase":"result in satisfaction"},{"uid":"15120a48-b6fa-4fbd-bd49-843d9600ab07","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"carried out","passagePhrase":"conducted"},{"uid":"0e60989c-9674-40b7-b416-b9d08495a131","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"study"},{"uid":"f40d101b-b12b-4b03-9462-8d1d32879e4b","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"discovered","passagePhrase":"found"},{"uid":"fd2b4753-1ab0-4602-8e82-acd374b400c3","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"improved","passagePhrase":"had a favorable impact on"},{"uid":"56439275-f907-4797-9247-677a79b1c68a","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"management involvement","passagePhrase":"manager support"},{"uid":"1b8c7671-53ed-477f-bfad-09a4be5c9c8f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"lower","passagePhrase":"reducing"},{"uid":"f47b6474-b3dc-4d86-91fa-a6bf659cd87b","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"needed to fit with","passagePhrase":"must be carefully aligned with"},{"uid":"bbb6511c-cf98-417e-9c7c-5569fa7e8d11","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"staff","passagePhrase":"employee"},{"uid":"d90dcc63-d57d-4cd3-be05-2948c7687577","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"take breaks","passagePhrase":"allowing adequate breaks"},{"uid":"a62a0da5-34d5-493d-9efc-cb809737cbe0","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"activities designed for staff","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"2496b5cc-8e1f-4d5a-9857-3abc644c1159","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"company’s","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_238":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong>Alexander Henderson (1831-1913)</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>Born in Scotland, Henderson emigrated to Canada in 1855 and become a well-known landscape photographer</em></span></p><p><span>Alexander Henderson was born in Scotland in 1831 and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8dd478fe-4ce5-4572-af27-d806a52b138e\" data-question=\"9\">was the son of a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> successful merchant. His grandfather, also called Alexander, had founded the family business, and later became the first chairman of the National Bank of Scotland. The family had extensive landholding in Scotland. Besides its residence in Edinburgh, it owned Press Estate, 650 acres of farmland about 35 miles southeast of the city. The family often stayed at Press Castle, the large mansion on the northern edge of the property, and Alexander <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f0e90224-258f-4527-8f18-e9f738a8f6e1\" data-question=\"1\">spent much of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98f00404-a7eb-48bb-956f-e8f7b3785a0a\" data-question=\"1\">his childhood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in the area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, playing on the beach near Eyemouth or fishing in the streams nearby.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c3a229a1-9f15-400a-b4c2-0e9d910c782f\" data-question=\"2\">Even after he went to school at Murcheston Academy on the outskirts of Edinburgh, Henderson returned to Press at weekends. In 1849 he began a three-year apprenticeship to become an accountant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Although he never liked the prospect of a business career, he stayed with it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd24036b-2cf0-4bbd-9c5e-8f15e3e8888e\" data-question=\"2\">to please his family<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. In October 1855, however, he emigrated to Canada with his wife Agnes Elder Robertson and they settled in Montreal.</span></p><p><span>Henderson learned photography in Montreal around the year 1857 and quickly took it up as a serious amateur. He became a personal friend and colleague of the Scottish – Canadian photographer William Notman. The two men made a photographic excursion to Niagara Falls in 1860 and they cooperated on experiments with magnesium flares as a source of artificial light in 1865. They belonged to the same societies and were among the founding members of the Art Association of Montreal. Henderson acted as chairman of the association’s first meeting, which was held in Notman’s studio on 11 January 1860.</span></p><p><span>In spite of their friendship, their styles of photography <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"facb93a9-5cdf-413e-9a7e-e89adcde598e\" data-question=\"4\">were quite different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. While Notman’s landscapes were noted for their bold realism, Henderson for the first 20 years of his career produced romantic images, showing the strong influence of the British landscape tradition. His artistic and technical progress was rapid and in 1865 he published his first major collection of landscape photographs. The publication had limited circulation (only seven copies have ever been found), and was called <em>Canadian Views and Studies. </em>The contents of each copy vary significantly and have proved a useful source for evaluating Henderson’s early work.</span></p><p><span>In 1866, he gave up his business to open a photographic studio, advertising himself as a portrait and landscape photographer. From about 1870 he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d15aeb17-0a43-4b5c-b3db-8a7c07555164\" data-question=\"6\">dropped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> portraiture to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23142320-7bd2-4e1a-9a22-1bda1c97687c\" data-question=\"6\">specialize in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ada6c069-274c-4b16-9654-6a01b7cae354\" data-question=\"6\">landscape photography and other views<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. His numerous photographs of city life revealed in street scenes, houses, and markets are alive with human activity, and although his favourite subject was landscape he usually composed his scenes around such human pursuits as farming the land, cutting ice on a river, or sailing down a woodland stream. There was sufficient demand for these types of scenes and others he took depicting the lumber trade, steamboats and waterfalls to enable him to make a living. There was little competing hobby or amateur photography before the late 1880s because of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b4783c2-d703-48fb-9469-893c3aa11c9a\" data-question=\"10\">time-consuming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> techniques involved and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1d8cab2-1e83-4b18-81ac-c0d200453249\" data-question=\"10\">the weight of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> equipment. People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d23b31d-9c52-48f6-a766-56a8510402c1\" data-question=\"11\">wanted to buy photographs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> as souvenirs of a trip or as gifts, and catering to this market, Henderson had stock photographs on display at his studio for mounting, framing, or inclusion in albums.</span></p><p><span>Henderson frequently exhibited his photographs in Montreal and abroad, in London, Edinburgh, Dublin, Paris, New York, and Philadelphia. He met with greater success in 1877 and 1878 in New York when he won first prizes in the exhibition held by E and H T Anthony and Company for landscapes using the Lambertype process. In 1878 his work won second prize at the world exhibition in Paris.</span></p><p><span>In the 1890s and 1880s Henderson travelled widely throughout Quebec and Ontario, in Canada, documenting the major cities of the two provinces and many of the villages in Quebec. He was especially fond of the wilderness and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5ab5194-94d0-403e-9716-599be37564a1\" data-question=\"12\">often travelled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> by canoe on the Blanche, du Lièvre, and other noted eastern rivers. He went on several occasions to the Maritimes and in 1872 he sailed by yacht along the lower north shore of the St Lawrence River. That same year, while in the lower St Lawrence River region, he took some photographs of the construction of the Intercolonial Railway. This undertaking led in 1875 to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7363906e-f75c-424d-b1b9-fd55958c6311\" data-question=\"7\">a commission from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the railway to record the principal structures along <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"59de96e5-2543-4e64-a212-db5b1613c8bf\" data-question=\"7\">the almost-completed line<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> connecting Montreal to Halifax. Commissions from other railways followed. In 1876 he photographed bridges on the Quebec, Montreal, Ottawa and Occidental Railway between Montreal and Ottawa. In 1885 he went west along the Canadian Pacific Railway (CPR) as far as Rogers Pass in British Columbia, where he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1dda542e-255c-4e00-b55f-897fb6f3f79e\" data-question=\"13\">took photographs of the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> mountains and the progress of construction.</span></p><p><span>In 1892 Henderson accepted a full-time position with the CPR as manager of a photographic department which he was to set up and administer. His duties included spending four months in the field each year. That summer he made his second trip west, photographing extensively along the railway line as far as Victoria. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ed81d85-a12c-4313-8df4-75437db9839c\" data-question=\"8\">continued in this post until 1897, when he retired<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> completely from photography.</span></p><p><span>When Henderson died in 1913, his huge collection of glass negatives was stored in the basement of his house. Today collections of his work are held at the National Archives of Canada, Ottawa, and the McCord Museum of Canadian History, Montreal.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?<br> </span><span>In boxes <strong>1-8</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"334\" id=\"question-wrapper-334\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Henderson <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f0e90224-258f-4527-8f18-e9f738a8f6e1\" data-question=\"1\">rarely visited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> the area around <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80a028cf-e239-4819-bc32-b86377b1b061\" data-question=\"1\">Press estate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98f00404-a7eb-48bb-956f-e8f7b3785a0a\" data-question=\"1\">when he was younger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"335\" id=\"question-wrapper-335\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Henderson <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c3a229a1-9f15-400a-b4c2-0e9d910c782f\" data-question=\"2\">pursued a business career<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd24036b-2cf0-4bbd-9c5e-8f15e3e8888e\" data-question=\"2\">because it was what his family wanted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"336\" id=\"question-wrapper-336\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Henderson and Notman were surprised by the results of their 1865 experiment. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"337\" id=\"question-wrapper-337\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"facb93a9-5cdf-413e-9a7e-e89adcde598e\" data-question=\"4\">There were many similarities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> between Henderson’s early landscapes and those of Notman. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"338\" id=\"question-wrapper-338\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The studio that Henderson opened in 1866 was close to his home. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"339\" id=\"question-wrapper-339\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Henderson <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d15aeb17-0a43-4b5c-b3db-8a7c07555164\" data-question=\"6\">gave up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> portraiture so that he could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23142320-7bd2-4e1a-9a22-1bda1c97687c\" data-question=\"6\">focus on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ada6c069-274c-4b16-9654-6a01b7cae354\" data-question=\"6\">taking photographs of scenery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"340\" id=\"question-wrapper-340\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When Henderson <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7363906e-f75c-424d-b1b9-fd55958c6311\" data-question=\"7\">began work for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the Intercolonial Railway, the Montreal to Halifax line <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"59de96e5-2543-4e64-a212-db5b1613c8bf\" data-question=\"7\">had been finished<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"341\" id=\"question-wrapper-341\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Henderson’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ed81d85-a12c-4313-8df4-75437db9839c\" data-question=\"8\">last work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> as a photographer was with the Canadian Pacific Railway. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below<br> </span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>9-13</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>Alexander Henderson</strong></span></h3><p><span><strong>Early life</strong></span></p><p><span><span>• </span>was born in Scotland in 1831 – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8dd478fe-4ce5-4572-af27-d806a52b138e\" data-question=\"9\">father was a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <strong>9</strong> …………………………</span></p><p><span><span>• </span>trained as an accountant, emigrated to Canada in 1855</span></p><p><span><strong>Start of a photographic career</strong></span></p><p><span><span>• </span>opened up a photographic studio in 1866</span></p><p><span><span>• </span>took photos of city life, but preferred landscape photography</span></p><p><span><span>• </span>people bought Henderson’s photos because photography <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b4783c2-d703-48fb-9469-893c3aa11c9a\" data-question=\"10\">took up considerable time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> and the <strong>10</strong> ……………………… was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1d8cab2-1e83-4b18-81ac-c0d200453249\" data-question=\"10\">heavy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span></span></p><p><span><span>• </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d23b31d-9c52-48f6-a766-56a8510402c1\" data-question=\"11\">the photographs Henderson sold<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> were <strong>11</strong> …………………………… or souvenirs</span></p><p><span><strong>Travelling as a professional photographer</strong></span></p><p><span><span>• </span>travelled widely in Quebec and Ontario in 1870s and 1880s</span></p><p><span><span>• </span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5ab5194-94d0-403e-9716-599be37564a1\" data-question=\"12\">took many trips<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c2bbc92-e54c-4af8-8137-d58729190cd5\" data-question=\"12\">along eastern rivers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in a <strong>12</strong>…………………………..</span></p><p><span><span>• </span>worked for Canadian railways between 1875 and 1897</span></p><p><span><span>• </span>worked for CPR in 1885 and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1dda542e-255c-4e00-b55f-897fb6f3f79e\" data-question=\"13\">photographed the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <strong>13</strong> …………………………… and the railway at Rogers Pass</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"342\" id=\"question-wrapper-342\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MERCHANT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"343\" id=\"question-wrapper-343\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EQUIPMENT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"344\" id=\"question-wrapper-344\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GIFTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"345\" id=\"question-wrapper-345\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CANOE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"346\" id=\"question-wrapper-346\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MOUNTAINS</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"8dd478fe-4ce5-4572-af27-d806a52b138e","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"father was a","passagePhrase":"was the son of a"},{"uid":"98f00404-a7eb-48bb-956f-e8f7b3785a0a","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"when he was younger","passagePhrase":"his childhood"},{"uid":"c3a229a1-9f15-400a-b4c2-0e9d910c782f","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"pursued a business career","passagePhrase":"Even after he went to school at Murcheston Academy on the outskirts of Edinburgh, Henderson returned to Press at weekends. In 1849 he began a three-year apprenticeship to become an accountant"},{"uid":"dd24036b-2cf0-4bbd-9c5e-8f15e3e8888e","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"because it was what his family wanted","passagePhrase":"to please his family"},{"uid":"d15aeb17-0a43-4b5c-b3db-8a7c07555164","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"gave up","passagePhrase":"dropped"},{"uid":"23142320-7bd2-4e1a-9a22-1bda1c97687c","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"focus on","passagePhrase":"specialize in"},{"uid":"ada6c069-274c-4b16-9654-6a01b7cae354","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"taking photographs of scenery","passagePhrase":"landscape photography and other views"},{"uid":"8b4783c2-d703-48fb-9469-893c3aa11c9a","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"took up considerable time","passagePhrase":"time-consuming"},{"uid":"b1d8cab2-1e83-4b18-81ac-c0d200453249","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"heavy","passagePhrase":"the weight of"},{"uid":"4d23b31d-9c52-48f6-a766-56a8510402c1","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"the photographs Henderson sold","passagePhrase":"wanted to buy photographs"},{"uid":"b5ab5194-94d0-403e-9716-599be37564a1","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"took many trips","passagePhrase":"often travelled"},{"uid":"7363906e-f75c-424d-b1b9-fd55958c6311","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"began work for","passagePhrase":"a commission from"},{"uid":"1dda542e-255c-4e00-b55f-897fb6f3f79e","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"photographed the","passagePhrase":"took photographs of the"},{"uid":"9ed81d85-a12c-4313-8df4-75437db9839c","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"last work","passagePhrase":"continued in this post until 1897, when he retired"},{"uid":"80a028cf-e239-4819-bc32-b86377b1b061","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Press estate","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"9c2bbc92-e54c-4af8-8137-d58729190cd5","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"along eastern rivers","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_239":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Back to the future of skyscraper design</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>Answers to the problem of excessive electricity use by skyscrapers and large public buildings can be found in ingenious but forgotten architectural designs of the 19th and early-20th centuries</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span><em>The Recovery of Natural Environments in Architecture </em>by Professor Alan Short is the culmination of 30 years of research and award-winning green building design by Short and colleagues in Architecture, Engineering, Applied Maths and Earth Sciences at the University of Cambridge.</span></p><p><span>‘The crisis in building design is already here,’ said Short. ‘Policy makers think you can solve energy and building problems with gadgets. You can’t. As global temperatures continue to rise, we are going to continue to squander more and more energy on keeping our buildings mechanically cool until we have run out of capacity.’</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Short is calling for a sweeping reinvention of how skyscrapers and major public buildings are designed – to end the reliance on sealed buildings which exist solely via the ‘life support’ system of vast air conditioning units.</span></p><p><span>Instead, he shows it is entirely possible to accommodate natural ventilation and cooling in large buildings by looking into the past, before <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77fd0129-357c-45b3-9c65-1dce8b1dcf11\" data-question=\"18\">the widespread introduction of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> air conditioning systems, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1aaa0344-93a1-4d52-9cfe-bef2a0046390\" data-question=\"18\">were ‘relentlessly and aggressively marketed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>’ by their inventors.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Short points out that to make most contemporary buildings habitable, they have to be sealed and air conditioned. The energy use and carbon emissions this generates is spectacular and largely unnecessary. Buildings in the West account for 40-50% of electricity usage, generating substantial carbon emissions, and the rest of the world is catching up at a frightening rate. Short regards glass, steel and air-conditioned <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"571b153f-3f12-48ff-9e9c-ba8599ebcae4\" data-question=\"15\">skyscrapers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> as symbols of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5acbfd6-4611-4a4b-aaff-1cc5a16568d4\" data-question=\"15\">status<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, rather than practical ways of meeting our requirements.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>Short’s book highlights a developing and sophisticated art and science of ventilating buildings through the 19th and earlier-20th centuries, including the design <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"634c96ed-5f05-4e66-a2b7-61e3b4e59b3a\" data-question=\"19\">of ingeniously ventilated hospitals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Of particular interest were those built to the designs of John Shaw Billings, including the first Johns Hopkins Hospital in the US city of Baltimore (1873-1889).</span></p><p><span>‘We spent three years digitally modelling Billings’ final designs,’ says Short. ‘We <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fedface-15e4-4778-bef7-8a59ed283f5b\" data-question=\"17\">put pathogens* <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1bc138d3-5f61-437b-8bb6-6b9fcadf7257\" data-question=\"20\">in the airstreams<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"449ef68c-049b-48a6-9eb2-d4379c7e0e84\" data-question=\"20\">modelled for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9fcac67d-7368-463c-a5c5-b889da21c8bd\" data-question=\"21\">someone with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> tuberculosis (TB) coughing in the wards and we found the ventilation systems in the room <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ef5c496-af35-43e3-922f-67241b96e4ed\" data-question=\"21\">would have kept other patients safe from harm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>—————-<br></span><span>* pathogens: microorganisms that can cause disease</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>‘We <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"afc2b31f-00fd-420b-ab33-98bcc2ff9539\" data-question=\"22\">discovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that 19th-century hospital wards could generate up to 24 air changes an hour – that’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34aa3bb7-e0c3-41ce-be55-21fc5b7ef69e\" data-question=\"16\">similar to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> the performance of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba8dae6f-fcc4-4010-8e05-b9973531a69c\" data-question=\"22\">modern-day, computer-controlled operating theatre<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. We believe you could build wards based on these principles now.</span></p><p><span>Single rooms are not appropriate for all patients. Communal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c110b8d6-0993-4ec8-923d-0bcebd62de1e\" data-question=\"23\">wards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> appropriate for certain patients – older people with dementia, for example – would work just as well in today’s hospitals, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46abab8b-2729-40b6-9c1d-55ec22919cd1\" data-question=\"23\">at a fraction of the energy cost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.’</span></p><p><span>Professor Short contends the mindset and skill-sets behind these designs have been completely lost, lamenting the disappearance of expertly designed theatres, opera houses, and other buildings where up to half the volume of the building was given over to ensuring everyone got fresh air.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>Much of the ingenuity present in 19th-century hospital and building design was driven by a panicked public clamouring for buildings that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"92b6d4d7-972b-4743-8cbf-15caf03cba71\" data-question=\"24\">could protect against<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> what <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"95efbdfb-29bb-47f2-af35-ba2de8bac0e0\" data-question=\"25\">was thought to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> the lethal threat of miasmas – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35f99b9e-688f-4a76-90f2-a96998672ea0\" data-question=\"24\">toxic air<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> that spread disease. Miasmas were feared as the principal agents of disease and epidemics for centuries, and were used to explain the spread of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d03c6da2-baa2-4623-ab3b-84cbb9b59685\" data-question=\"26\">infection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa7a9201-9e6e-4224-be45-ed159640f7d0\" data-question=\"26\">from the Middle Ages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> right through to the cholera <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3384dd02-6306-48fe-97bc-c822b5457ba2\" data-question=\"26\">outbreaks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> in London and Paris during the 1850s. Foul air, rather than germs, was believed to be the main driver of ‘hospital fever’, leading to disease and frequent death. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27ebd631-c5c2-4e9e-9d86-e3b8cd5bc9bf\" data-question=\"14\">prosperous steered clear of hospitals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>While miasma theory has been long since disproved, Short has for the last 30 years advocated a return to some of the building design principles produced in its wake.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>Today, huge amounts of a building’s space and construction cost are given over to air conditioning. ‘But I have designed and built a series of buildings over the past three decades which have tried to reinvent some of these ideas and then measure what happens.</span></p><p><span>‘To go forward into our new low-energy, low-carbon future, we would be well advised to look back at design before our high-energy, high-carbon present appeared. What is surprising is what a rich legacy we have abandoned.’</span></p><p><span><strong>H</strong></span></p><p><span>Successful examples of Short’s approach include the Queen’s Building at De Montfort University in Leicester. Containing as many as 2,000 staff and students, the entire building is naturally ventilated, passively cooled and naturally lit, including the two largest auditoria, each seating more than 150 people. The award-winning building uses a fraction of the electricity of comparable buildings in the UK.</span></p><p><span>Short contends that glass skyscrapers in London and around the world will become a liability over the next 20 or 30 years if climate modelling predictions and energy price rises come to pass as expected.</span></p><p><span><strong>I</strong></span></p><p><span>He is convinced that sufficiently cooled skyscrapers using the natural environment can be produced in almost any climate. He and his team have worked on hybrid buildings in the harsh climates of Beijing and Chicago – built with natural ventilation assisted by back-up air conditioning – which, surprisingly perhaps, can be switched off more than half the time on milder days and during the spring and autumn.</span></p><p><span>Short looks at how we might reimagine the cities, offices and homes of the future. Maybe it’s time we changed our outlook.</span></p><p><span> </span><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has nine section, <strong>A-I</strong></span></p><p><span>Which section contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter,<strong> A-I</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-18</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"347\" id=\"question-wrapper-347\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27ebd631-c5c2-4e9e-9d86-e3b8cd5bc9bf\" data-question=\"14\">some people avoided hospitals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in the 19th century </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"348\" id=\"question-wrapper-348\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a suggestion that the popularity of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"571b153f-3f12-48ff-9e9c-ba8599ebcae4\" data-question=\"15\">tall buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e1d8d014-63c2-4494-ba31-c35fdd8c5496\" data-question=\"15\">is linked to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5acbfd6-4611-4a4b-aaff-1cc5a16568d4\" data-question=\"15\">prestige<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"349\" id=\"question-wrapper-349\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34aa3bb7-e0c3-41ce-be55-21fc5b7ef69e\" data-question=\"16\">a comparison between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> the circulation of air in a 19th-century building and modern standards </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"350\" id=\"question-wrapper-350\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> how Short <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fedface-15e4-4778-bef7-8a59ed283f5b\" data-question=\"17\">tested the circulation of air<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in a 19th-century building </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"351\" id=\"question-wrapper-351\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an implication that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1aaa0344-93a1-4d52-9cfe-bef2a0046390\" data-question=\"18\">advertising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> led to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77fd0129-357c-45b3-9c65-1dce8b1dcf11\" data-question=\"18\">the large increase in the use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of air conditioning </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>19-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>Ventilation in 19th-century hospital wards</strong></span></h3><p><span>Professor Alan Short examined the work of John Shaw Billings, who influenced the architectural <strong>19</strong> ……………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"634c96ed-5f05-4e66-a2b7-61e3b4e59b3a\" data-question=\"19\">of hospitals to ensure they had good ventilation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. He calculated that <strong>20</strong> ……………………….. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1bc138d3-5f61-437b-8bb6-6b9fcadf7257\" data-question=\"20\">in the air<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"449ef68c-049b-48a6-9eb2-d4379c7e0e84\" data-question=\"20\">coming from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9fcac67d-7368-463c-a5c5-b889da21c8bd\" data-question=\"21\">patients suffering from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <strong>21</strong>……………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ef5c496-af35-43e3-922f-67241b96e4ed\" data-question=\"21\">would not have harmed other patients<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. He also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"afc2b31f-00fd-420b-ab33-98bcc2ff9539\" data-question=\"22\">found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that the air in <strong>22</strong>…………………………. In hospitals could change as often as in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba8dae6f-fcc4-4010-8e05-b9973531a69c\" data-question=\"22\">modern operating theatre<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. He suggests that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46abab8b-2729-40b6-9c1d-55ec22919cd1\" data-question=\"23\">energy use could be reduced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> by locating more patients in <strong>23</strong> ………………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c110b8d6-0993-4ec8-923d-0bcebd62de1e\" data-question=\"23\">areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>A major reason for improving ventilation in 19th-century hospitals was the demand from the <strong>24</strong> ………………………….. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"92b6d4d7-972b-4743-8cbf-15caf03cba71\" data-question=\"24\">for protection against<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35f99b9e-688f-4a76-90f2-a96998672ea0\" data-question=\"24\">bad air<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"95efbdfb-29bb-47f2-af35-ba2de8bac0e0\" data-question=\"25\">known as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <strong>25</strong> …………………………… These were blamed for the spread of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d03c6da2-baa2-4623-ab3b-84cbb9b59685\" data-question=\"26\">disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> for hundreds of years, including <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3384dd02-6306-48fe-97bc-c822b5457ba2\" data-question=\"26\">epidemics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> of <strong>26</strong>…………………………… in London and Paris <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa7a9201-9e6e-4224-be45-ed159640f7d0\" data-question=\"26\">in the middle of the 19th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"352\" id=\"question-wrapper-352\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DESIGN(S)</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"353\" id=\"question-wrapper-353\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PATHOGENS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"354\" id=\"question-wrapper-354\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TUBERCULOSIS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"355\" id=\"question-wrapper-355\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WARDS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"356\" id=\"question-wrapper-356\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMMUNAL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"357\" id=\"question-wrapper-357\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PUBLIC</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"358\" id=\"question-wrapper-358\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MIASMAS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"359\" id=\"question-wrapper-359\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CHOLERA</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"77fd0129-357c-45b3-9c65-1dce8b1dcf11","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"the large increase in the use","passagePhrase":"the widespread introduction of"},{"uid":"1aaa0344-93a1-4d52-9cfe-bef2a0046390","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"advertising","passagePhrase":"were ‘relentlessly and aggressively marketed"},{"uid":"571b153f-3f12-48ff-9e9c-ba8599ebcae4","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"tall buildings","passagePhrase":"skyscrapers"},{"uid":"d5acbfd6-4611-4a4b-aaff-1cc5a16568d4","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"prestige","passagePhrase":"status"},{"uid":"634c96ed-5f05-4e66-a2b7-61e3b4e59b3a","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"of hospitals to ensure they had good ventilation","passagePhrase":"of ingeniously ventilated hospitals"},{"uid":"2fedface-15e4-4778-bef7-8a59ed283f5b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"tested the circulation of air","passagePhrase":"put pathogens* in the airstreams"},{"uid":"1bc138d3-5f61-437b-8bb6-6b9fcadf7257","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"in the air","passagePhrase":"in the airstreams"},{"uid":"449ef68c-049b-48a6-9eb2-d4379c7e0e84","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"coming from","passagePhrase":"modelled for"},{"uid":"9fcac67d-7368-463c-a5c5-b889da21c8bd","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"patients suffering from","passagePhrase":"someone with"},{"uid":"3ef5c496-af35-43e3-922f-67241b96e4ed","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"would not have harmed other patients","passagePhrase":"would have kept other patients safe from harm"},{"uid":"afc2b31f-00fd-420b-ab33-98bcc2ff9539","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"found","passagePhrase":"discovered"},{"uid":"34aa3bb7-e0c3-41ce-be55-21fc5b7ef69e","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"a comparison between","passagePhrase":"similar to"},{"uid":"ba8dae6f-fcc4-4010-8e05-b9973531a69c","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"modern operating theatre","passagePhrase":"modern-day, computer-controlled operating theatre"},{"uid":"c110b8d6-0993-4ec8-923d-0bcebd62de1e","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"areas","passagePhrase":"wards"},{"uid":"46abab8b-2729-40b6-9c1d-55ec22919cd1","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"energy use could be reduced","passagePhrase":"at a fraction of the energy cost"},{"uid":"92b6d4d7-972b-4743-8cbf-15caf03cba71","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"for protection against","passagePhrase":"could protect against"},{"uid":"95efbdfb-29bb-47f2-af35-ba2de8bac0e0","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"known as","passagePhrase":"was thought to be"},{"uid":"35f99b9e-688f-4a76-90f2-a96998672ea0","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"bad air","passagePhrase":"toxic air"},{"uid":"d03c6da2-baa2-4623-ab3b-84cbb9b59685","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"disease","passagePhrase":"infection"},{"uid":"fa7a9201-9e6e-4224-be45-ed159640f7d0","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"in the middle of the 19th century","passagePhrase":"from the Middle Ages"},{"uid":"3384dd02-6306-48fe-97bc-c822b5457ba2","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"epidemics","passagePhrase":"outbreaks"},{"uid":"27ebd631-c5c2-4e9e-9d86-e3b8cd5bc9bf","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"some people avoided hospitals","passagePhrase":"prosperous steered clear of hospitals"},{"uid":"e1d8d014-63c2-4494-ba31-c35fdd8c5496","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"is linked to","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_240":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong><span>Why companies should welcome disorder</span></strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>Organisation is big business. Whether it is of our lives – all those inboxes and calendars – or how companies are structured, a multi-billion dollar industry helps to meet this need.</span></p><p><span>We have more strategies for time management, project management and self-organisation than at any other time in human history. We <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce8e2abf-6fa3-4d18-b2cb-736ed16acce9\" data-question=\"27\">are told that we ought to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> organize our company, our home life, our week, our day and even our sleep, all as a means to becoming more productive. Every week, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be473f45-c032-4ad9-b24b-8a08786a3fdc\" data-question=\"35\">countless seminars and workshops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> take place around the world to tell a paying public that they ought to structure their lives in order to achieve this.</span></p><p><span>This rhetoric has also crept into the thinking of business leaders and entrepreneurs, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c981c22a-6e44-4ad3-9fa6-a450ec794845\" data-question=\"36\">much to the delight of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6083890a-c52f-43b8-b087-5706da308b77\" data-question=\"36\">self-proclaimed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> perfectionists with the need <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9060d4d8-80e8-4343-b09d-7c9cfa175695\" data-question=\"36\">to get everything right<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. The number of business schools and graduates has massively increased over the past 50 years, essentially teaching people how to organise well.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Ironically, however, the number of business that fail has also steadily increased. Work-related stress has increased. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1be89bd3-d20b-4749-882d-27cdc9392492\" data-question=\"37\">A large proportion of workers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> from all demographics <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e1b07800-080e-42cd-b899-835ad48e42a9\" data-question=\"28\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74d7e40e-af00-4981-b6f5-8171c9321611\" data-question=\"37\">claim to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> dissatisfied with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a69f3b4-ee72-4874-98a9-6cac6ef07536\" data-question=\"28\">the way their work is structured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a69f3b4-ee72-4874-98a9-6cac6ef07536\" data-question=\"28\">the way they are managed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>This begs the question: what has gone wrong? Why is it that on paper the drive for organisation seems a sure shot for increasing productivity, but in reality falls well short of what is expected?</span></p><p><span><b>C</b></span></p><p><span>This has been a problem for a while now. Frederick Taylor was one of the forefathers of scientific management. Writing in the first half of the 20th century, he designed a number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5533a44d-1e78-49b9-8343-57ef60febaa3\" data-question=\"29\">principles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to improve the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2358e364-094f-45b0-92c4-dca3967c1c51\" data-question=\"29\">efficiency of the work process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, which have since become widespread in modern companies. So the approach has been around for a while.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>New research suggests that this obsession with efficiency <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdb7a28b-a5c6-45e2-86e1-c2e7c2949573\" data-question=\"30\">is misguided<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. The problem is not necessarily the management theories or strategies we use to organise our work; it’s the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6912aec7-b982-42c5-ac92-8469cf2648a3\" data-question=\"30\">basic assumptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> we hold in approaching how we work. Here it’s the assumption that order is a necessary condition for productivity. This assumption has also fostered the idea that disorder must be detrimental to organizational productivity. The result is that businesses and people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a48b4560-80ba-41cb-bb3b-703f5d8fecaf\" data-question=\"38\">spend time and money organising themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> for the sake of organising, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d56e8097-b910-4148-891f-ec02795322e4\" data-question=\"38\">rather than actually looking at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2de6ee0-c2c8-4eac-a321-0b6af667656f\" data-question=\"38\">the end goal and usefulness of such an effort<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>What’s more, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e36254c2-5893-4734-a34f-fd67e1a34c11\" data-question=\"31\">recent studies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> show that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04370122-9fb9-4cb1-a314-360bf2cb08d5\" data-question=\"31\">order<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> actually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"640e6cbd-8f3f-4a7a-ab24-9cf1987bbb69\" data-question=\"31\">has diminishing returns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Order does increase productivity to a certain extent, but eventually the usefulness of the process of organisation, and the benefit it yields, reduce until the point where any further increase in order reduces productivity. Some argue that in a business, if the cost of formally structuring something outweighs the benefit of doing it, then that thing ought not to be formally structured. Instead, the resources involved can be better used elsewhere.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>In fact, research shows that, when innovating, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d21c15d3-de42-4276-be6f-0957eb1a5541\" data-question=\"39\">the best approach is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> to create an environment devoid of structure and hierarchy and enable <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1bfe39fd-b572-450a-8b2f-a66bfc6bf831\" data-question=\"39\">everyone involved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"3ea1be66-afb8-4bb2-a4aa-cb17666f7b7c\" data-question=\"39\">engage as one organic group<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. These environments can lead to new solutions that, under conventionally structured environments (filled with bottlenecks in term of information flow, power structures, rules, and routines) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7c63ffe-ea5f-48d2-88ef-ff8a66f6a361\" data-question=\"32\">would never be reached<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>In recent times companies have slowly started to embrace this disorganisation. Many of them embrace it in terms of perception (embracing the idea of disorder, as opposed to fearing it) and in terms of process (putting mechanisms in place to reduce structure).</span></p><p><span>For example, Oticon, a large Danish manufacturer of hearing aids, used what it called <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e241c968-4cb9-40a0-97ec-64e42d1d0e26\" data-question=\"33\">a ‘spaghetti’ structure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> in order to reduce the organisation’s rigid hierarchies. This involved scrapping formal job titles and giving staff huge amounts of ownership over their own time and projects. This approach proved to be highly successful initially, with clear improvements in worker productivity in all facets of the business.</span></p><p><span>In similar fashion, the former chairman of General Electric <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a198fde-02f1-4e42-8a47-88988aa6006e\" data-question=\"40\">embraced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> disorganisation, putting forward <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e241c968-4cb9-40a0-97ec-64e42d1d0e26\" data-question=\"33\">the idea of the ‘boundaryless’ organisation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. Again, it involves breaking down the barriers between different parts of a company and encouraging virtual collaboration and flexible working. Google and a number of other tech companies have embraced (at least in part) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"005c1b36-4a03-4e0d-a069-c99913034eda\" data-question=\"40\">these kinds of flexible structures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, facilitated by technology and strong company values which glue people together.</span></p><p><span><strong>H</strong></span></p><p><span>A word of warning to others thinking of jumping on this bandwagon: the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e36254c2-5893-4734-a34f-fd67e1a34c11\" data-question=\"31\">evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> so far suggests disorder, much like order, also seems to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"787becea-0daf-4f4c-a0fb-2a0fd1da264c\" data-question=\"34\">have diminishing utility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, and can also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"787becea-0daf-4f4c-a0fb-2a0fd1da264c\" data-question=\"34\">have detrimental effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> on performance if overused. Like order, disorder should be embraced only so far as it is useful. But we should not fear it – nor venerate one over the other. This research also shows that we should continually question whether or not our existing assumptions work.</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 3 has eight sections, <strong>A-H<br></strong></span><span>Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.</span></p><p><span>Write the correct number, <strong>i-ix</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-34</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p><p><span><strong>List of Headings</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>i</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e1b07800-080e-42cd-b899-835ad48e42a9\" data-question=\"28\">Complaints<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a69f3b4-ee72-4874-98a9-6cac6ef07536\" data-question=\"28\">the impact of a certain approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>ii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6912aec7-b982-42c5-ac92-8469cf2648a3\" data-question=\"30\">Fundamental beliefs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdb7a28b-a5c6-45e2-86e1-c2e7c2949573\" data-question=\"30\">are in fact incorrect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>iii</strong> Early <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5533a44d-1e78-49b9-8343-57ef60febaa3\" data-question=\"29\">recommendations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> concerning <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2358e364-094f-45b0-92c4-dca3967c1c51\" data-question=\"29\">business activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>iv</strong> Organisations that put <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e241c968-4cb9-40a0-97ec-64e42d1d0e26\" data-question=\"33\">a new approach into practice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>v </strong> Companies that have suffered from changing their approach</span></p><p><span><strong>vi</strong> What people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce8e2abf-6fa3-4d18-b2cb-736ed16acce9\" data-question=\"27\">are increasingly expected to do<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>vii</strong> How to achieve outcomes that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7c63ffe-ea5f-48d2-88ef-ff8a66f6a361\" data-question=\"32\">are currently impossible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>viii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"787becea-0daf-4f4c-a0fb-2a0fd1da264c\" data-question=\"34\">Neither approach guarantees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> continuous improvement</span></p><p><span><strong>ix</strong> Evidence that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04370122-9fb9-4cb1-a314-360bf2cb08d5\" data-question=\"31\">a certain approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> can have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"640e6cbd-8f3f-4a7a-ab24-9cf1987bbb69\" data-question=\"31\">more disadvantages than advantages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"360\" id=\"question-wrapper-360\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"361\" id=\"question-wrapper-361\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"362\" id=\"question-wrapper-362\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"363\" id=\"question-wrapper-363\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"364\" id=\"question-wrapper-364\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IX</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"365\" id=\"question-wrapper-365\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"366\" id=\"question-wrapper-366\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"367\" id=\"question-wrapper-367\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section H </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the sentences below.<br></span><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>35-37</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"368\" id=\"question-wrapper-368\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be473f45-c032-4ad9-b24b-8a08786a3fdc\" data-question=\"35\">Numerous training sessions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"517f20d3-e169-407e-859b-82fb10f78466\" data-question=\"35\">are aimed at people who feel they are not ………………………. enough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PRODUCTIVE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"369\" id=\"question-wrapper-369\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9060d4d8-80e8-4343-b09d-7c9cfa175695\" data-question=\"36\">Being organised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c981c22a-6e44-4ad3-9fa6-a450ec794845\" data-question=\"36\">appeals to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6083890a-c52f-43b8-b087-5706da308b77\" data-question=\"36\">who regard themselves as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> …………………………… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PERFECTIONISTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"370\" id=\"question-wrapper-370\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1be89bd3-d20b-4749-882d-27cdc9392492\" data-question=\"37\">Many people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> feel ……………………….. with aspects of their work. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DISSATISFIED</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?<br></span><span>In boxes <strong>38-40</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"371\" id=\"question-wrapper-371\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Both businesses and people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a48b4560-80ba-41cb-bb3b-703f5d8fecaf\" data-question=\"38\">aim at order<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d56e8097-b910-4148-891f-ec02795322e4\" data-question=\"38\">without really considering<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2de6ee0-c2c8-4eac-a321-0b6af667656f\" data-question=\"38\">its value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"372\" id=\"question-wrapper-372\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Innovation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d21c15d3-de42-4276-be6f-0957eb1a5541\" data-question=\"39\">is most successful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1bfe39fd-b572-450a-8b2f-a66bfc6bf831\" data-question=\"39\">the people involved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"3ea1be66-afb8-4bb2-a4aa-cb17666f7b7c\" data-question=\"39\">have distinct roles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"373\" id=\"question-wrapper-373\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Google was inspired to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a198fde-02f1-4e42-8a47-88988aa6006e\" data-question=\"40\">adopt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"005c1b36-4a03-4e0d-a069-c99913034eda\" data-question=\"40\">flexibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> by the success of General Electric. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"ce8e2abf-6fa3-4d18-b2cb-736ed16acce9","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"are increasingly expected to do","passagePhrase":"are told that we ought to"},{"uid":"be473f45-c032-4ad9-b24b-8a08786a3fdc","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Numerous training sessions","passagePhrase":"countless seminars and workshops"},{"uid":"c981c22a-6e44-4ad3-9fa6-a450ec794845","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"appeals to","passagePhrase":"much to the delight of"},{"uid":"6083890a-c52f-43b8-b087-5706da308b77","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"who regard themselves as","passagePhrase":"self-proclaimed"},{"uid":"9060d4d8-80e8-4343-b09d-7c9cfa175695","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Being organised","passagePhrase":"to get everything right"},{"uid":"1be89bd3-d20b-4749-882d-27cdc9392492","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"Many people","passagePhrase":"A large proportion of workers"},{"uid":"e1b07800-080e-42cd-b899-835ad48e42a9","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Complaints","passagePhrase":"claim to be dissatisfied with"},{"uid":"74d7e40e-af00-4981-b6f5-8171c9321611","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"claim to be"},{"uid":"5a69f3b4-ee72-4874-98a9-6cac6ef07536","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"the impact of a certain approach","passagePhrase":"the way their work is structured ... the way they are managed"},{"uid":"5533a44d-1e78-49b9-8343-57ef60febaa3","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"recommendations","passagePhrase":"principles"},{"uid":"2358e364-094f-45b0-92c4-dca3967c1c51","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"business activities","passagePhrase":"efficiency of the work process"},{"uid":"cdb7a28b-a5c6-45e2-86e1-c2e7c2949573","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"are in fact incorrect","passagePhrase":"is misguided"},{"uid":"6912aec7-b982-42c5-ac92-8469cf2648a3","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Fundamental beliefs","passagePhrase":"basic assumptions"},{"uid":"a48b4560-80ba-41cb-bb3b-703f5d8fecaf","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"aim at order","passagePhrase":"spend time and money organising themselves"},{"uid":"d56e8097-b910-4148-891f-ec02795322e4","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"without really considering","passagePhrase":"rather than actually looking at"},{"uid":"d2de6ee0-c2c8-4eac-a321-0b6af667656f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"its value","passagePhrase":"the end goal and usefulness of such an effort"},{"uid":"e36254c2-5893-4734-a34f-fd67e1a34c11","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"recent studies ... evidence"},{"uid":"04370122-9fb9-4cb1-a314-360bf2cb08d5","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"a certain approach","passagePhrase":"order"},{"uid":"640e6cbd-8f3f-4a7a-ab24-9cf1987bbb69","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"more disadvantages than advantages","passagePhrase":"has diminishing returns"},{"uid":"d21c15d3-de42-4276-be6f-0957eb1a5541","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"is most successful","passagePhrase":"the best approach is"},{"uid":"1bfe39fd-b572-450a-8b2f-a66bfc6bf831","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"the people involved","passagePhrase":"everyone involved"},{"uid":"c7c63ffe-ea5f-48d2-88ef-ff8a66f6a361","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"are currently impossible","passagePhrase":"would never be reached"},{"uid":"e241c968-4cb9-40a0-97ec-64e42d1d0e26","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"a new approach into practice","passagePhrase":"a ‘spaghetti’ structure ... the idea of the ‘boundaryless’ organisation"},{"uid":"3a198fde-02f1-4e42-8a47-88988aa6006e","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"adopt","passagePhrase":"embraced"},{"uid":"005c1b36-4a03-4e0d-a069-c99913034eda","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"flexibility","passagePhrase":"these kinds of flexible structures"},{"uid":"787becea-0daf-4f4c-a0fb-2a0fd1da264c","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Neither approach guarantees","passagePhrase":"have diminishing utility ... have detrimental effects"},{"uid":"517f20d3-e169-407e-859b-82fb10f78466","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"are aimed at people who feel they are not ………………………. enough","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_241":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions</strong> <strong>1-13</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</p><p> </p><h2><strong>The concept of intelligence</strong></h2><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Looked at in one way, everyone knows what intelligence is; looked at in another way, no one does. In other words, people all have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98038e12-bb88-4508-b2fc-0e4c09f56149\" data-question=\"2\">unconscious notions – known as ‘implicit theories’ – of intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f13aae1-fe0d-4e49-8a85-89a8c9344427\" data-question=\"2\">no one knows for certain what it actually is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. This chapter addresses how people conceptualize intelligence, whatever it may actually be.</p><p>But why should we even care what people think intelligence is, as opposed only to valuing whatever it actually is? There are at least four reasons people’s conceptions of intelligence matter.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>First, implicit theories of intelligence drive the way in which people perceive and evaluate their own intelligence and that of others. To better understand the judgments people make about their own and others’ abilities, it is useful to learn about people’s implicit theories. For example, parents’ implicit theories of their children’s language development will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77a612cf-753e-4220-b6d2-e477b0177eec\" data-question=\"1\">determine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> at what ages they will be willing to make various corrections in their children’s speech. More generally, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4154fcf-b755-4fb2-8d2e-f4ddae130c23\" data-question=\"1\">parents’ implicit theories of intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77a612cf-753e-4220-b6d2-e477b0177eec\" data-question=\"1\">determine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8d11d7cc-99f7-455b-b137-a23913e2e5cb\" data-question=\"1\">at what ages they believe their children are ready to perform various cognitive tasks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. Job interviewers will make hiring decisions on the basis of their implicit theories of intelligence. People will decide who to be friends with on the basis of such theories. In sum, knowledge about implicit theories of intelligence is important because this knowledge is so often used by people to make judgments in the course of their everyday lives.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>Second, the implicit theories of scientific investigators ultimately give rise to their explicit theories. Thus it is useful to find out what these implicit theories are. Implicit theories provide a framework that is useful in defining the general scope of a phenomenon – especially a not-well-understood phenomenon. These implicit theories can suggest what aspects of the phenomenon have been more or less attended to in previous investigations.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>Third, implicit theories can be useful when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb99192b-cef0-4f30-a12b-0a360c5ae361\" data-question=\"3\">an investigator<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> suspects that existing explicit theories are wrong or misleading. If an investigation of implicit theories reveals little correspondence between the extant implicit and explicit theories, the implicit theories may be wrong. But the possibility also needs to be taken into account that the explicit theories are wrong and in need of correction or supplementation. For example, some implicit theories of intelligence suggest the need for expansion of some of our explicit theories of the construct.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>Finally, understanding implicit theories of intelligence can help elucidate developmental and cross-cultural differences. As mentioned earlier, people have expectations for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ebc2250-7973-46a6-bada-bfdc419e8a5b\" data-question=\"5\">intellectual performances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1bce0e83-9355-4375-8830-66832dadfc57\" data-question=\"5\">differ<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> for children of different ages. How these expectations differ is in part a function of culture. For example, expectations for children who participate in Western-style schooling are almost certain to be different from those for children who do not participate in such schooling.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>I have suggested that there are three major implicit theories of how intelligence relates to society as a whole (Sternberg, 1997). These might be called Hamiltonian, Jeffersonian, and Jacksonian. These views are not based strictly, but rather, loosely, on the philosophies of Alexander Hamilton, Thomas Jefferson, and Andrew Jackson, three great statesmen in the history of the United States.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>The Hamiltonian view, which is similar to the Platonic view, is that people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"44d91ca2-5ad2-48cc-9f06-e68a820dd214\" data-question=\"10\">are born with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26d3aec4-0ec2-402d-8f70-a5682ad048c6\" data-question=\"10\">different levels of intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> and that those who are less intelligent need the good offices of the more intelligent to keep them in line, whether they are called government officials or, in Plato’s term, philosopher-kings. Herrnstein and Murray (1994) seem to have shared this belief when they wrote about the emergence of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3db56715-9174-4156-99ff-639ee833a7cf\" data-question=\"11\">a cognitive (high-IQ) elite<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, which eventually would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aace56bf-41ce-4191-9036-17d8499f6683\" data-question=\"11\">have to take responsibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> for the largely irresponsible masses of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c43fd6b-23cf-4a33-8cce-c93f438cbf4f\" data-question=\"13\">non-elite (low-IQ) people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> who cannot take care of themselves. Left to themselves, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c43fd6b-23cf-4a33-8cce-c93f438cbf4f\" data-question=\"13\">the unintelligent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> would create, as they always have created, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab817410-fa91-4a59-a78a-bab6dfff6a27\" data-question=\"13\">a kind of chaos<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>The Jeffersonian view is that people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2ecd3cf-f264-4d87-81a0-aea4047ac57b\" data-question=\"7\">should have equal opportunities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, but they do not necessarily avail themselves equally of these opportunities and are not necessarily equally rewarded for their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8237f17c-949b-4d2e-871f-9c74556e158e\" data-question=\"9\">accomplish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>ments. People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d510bbb-461c-460f-8011-0c67ca0f5998\" data-question=\"9\">are rewarded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> for what they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8237f17c-949b-4d2e-871f-9c74556e158e\" data-question=\"9\">accomplish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, if given equal opportunity. Low achievers are not rewarded to the same extent as high achievers. In the Jeffersonian view, the goal of education is not to favor or foster an elite, as in the Hamiltonian tradition, but rather to allow children the opportunities to make full use of the skills they have. My own views are similar to these (Sternberg, 1997).</p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p>The Jacksonian view is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70d0f6fa-951d-4183-bba3-a153d9ecb200\" data-question=\"8\">all people are equal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, not only as human beings but in terms of their competencies – that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70d0f6fa-951d-4183-bba3-a153d9ecb200\" data-question=\"8\">one person would serve as well as another in government or on a jury or in almost any position of responsibility. In this view of democracy, people are essentially intersubstitutable except for specialized skills, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab232762-0e2f-46c5-a05e-41224fb70fb5\" data-question=\"12\">all of which can be learned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. In this view, we do not need or want any institutions that might lead to favoring one group over another.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></p><p><strong>J</strong></p><p>Implicit theories of intelligence and of the relationship of intelligence to society perhaps need to be considered more carefully than they have been because they often serve as underlying presuppositions for explicit theories and even experimental designs that are then taken as scientific contributions. Until scholars are able to discuss their implicit theories and thus their assumptions, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e7495bb-7078-49eb-a7b1-b85c870882e1\" data-question=\"6\">are likely to miss the point of what others are saying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> when discussing their explicit theories and their data.</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has ten sections, <strong>A-J</strong></span></p><p><span>Which section contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-J</strong>, in boxes <strong>1-3</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"374\" id=\"question-wrapper-374\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> information about how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4154fcf-b755-4fb2-8d2e-f4ddae130c23\" data-question=\"1\">non-scientists’ assumptions about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> intelligence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77a612cf-753e-4220-b6d2-e477b0177eec\" data-question=\"1\">influence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8d11d7cc-99f7-455b-b137-a23913e2e5cb\" data-question=\"1\">their behavior towards others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"375\" id=\"question-wrapper-375\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f13aae1-fe0d-4e49-8a85-89a8c9344427\" data-question=\"2\">lack of clarity over<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98038e12-bb88-4508-b2fc-0e4c09f56149\" data-question=\"2\">the definition of intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"376\" id=\"question-wrapper-376\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the point that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb99192b-cef0-4f30-a12b-0a360c5ae361\" data-question=\"3\">a researcher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>’s implicit and explicit theories may be very different </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>4-6</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"377\" id=\"question-wrapper-377\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Slow language development in children is likely to prove disappointing to their parents. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"378\" id=\"question-wrapper-378\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People’s expectations of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ebc2250-7973-46a6-bada-bfdc419e8a5b\" data-question=\"5\">what children should gain from education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1bce0e83-9355-4375-8830-66832dadfc57\" data-question=\"5\">are universal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"379\" id=\"question-wrapper-379\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Scholars may discuss theories <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e7495bb-7078-49eb-a7b1-b85c870882e1\" data-question=\"6\">without fully understanding each other<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Look at the following statements (Questions <strong>7-13</strong>) and the list of theories below.</p><p>Match each statement with the correct theory, <strong>A</strong>,<strong> B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>.</p><p>Write the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>, in boxes <strong>7-13</strong> on your answer sheet.</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p><p><strong>List of Theories</strong></p><p><strong>A</strong> Hamiltonian<br><strong>B</strong> Jeffersonian<br><strong>C</strong> Jacksonian</p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"380\" id=\"question-wrapper-380\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is desirable for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2ecd3cf-f264-4d87-81a0-aea4047ac57b\" data-question=\"7\">same possibilities to be open to everyone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"381\" id=\"question-wrapper-381\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70d0f6fa-951d-4183-bba3-a153d9ecb200\" data-question=\"8\">No section of society should have preferential treatment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> at the expense of another. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"382\" id=\"question-wrapper-382\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People should only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d510bbb-461c-460f-8011-0c67ca0f5998\" data-question=\"9\">gain benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> on the basis of what they actually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8237f17c-949b-4d2e-871f-9c74556e158e\" data-question=\"9\">achieve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"383\" id=\"question-wrapper-383\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26d3aec4-0ec2-402d-8f70-a5682ad048c6\" data-question=\"10\">Variation in intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"44d91ca2-5ad2-48cc-9f06-e68a820dd214\" data-question=\"10\">begins at birth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"384\" id=\"question-wrapper-384\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3db56715-9174-4156-99ff-639ee833a7cf\" data-question=\"11\">intelligent people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aace56bf-41ce-4191-9036-17d8499f6683\" data-question=\"11\">should be in positions of power<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"385\" id=\"question-wrapper-385\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Everyone can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab232762-0e2f-46c5-a05e-41224fb70fb5\" data-question=\"12\">develop the same abilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"386\" id=\"question-wrapper-386\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c43fd6b-23cf-4a33-8cce-c93f438cbf4f\" data-question=\"13\">People of low intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> are likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab817410-fa91-4a59-a78a-bab6dfff6a27\" data-question=\"13\">lead uncontrolled lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"98038e12-bb88-4508-b2fc-0e4c09f56149","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"the definition of intelligence","passagePhrase":"unconscious notions – known as ‘implicit theories’ – of intelligence"},{"uid":"6f13aae1-fe0d-4e49-8a85-89a8c9344427","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"lack of clarity over","passagePhrase":"no one knows for certain what it actually is"},{"uid":"77a612cf-753e-4220-b6d2-e477b0177eec","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"influence","passagePhrase":"determine ... determine"},{"uid":"f4154fcf-b755-4fb2-8d2e-f4ddae130c23","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"non-scientists’ assumptions about","passagePhrase":"parents’ implicit theories of intelligence"},{"uid":"8d11d7cc-99f7-455b-b137-a23913e2e5cb","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"their behavior towards others","passagePhrase":"at what ages they believe their children are ready to perform various cognitive tasks"},{"uid":"cb99192b-cef0-4f30-a12b-0a360c5ae361","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"a researcher","passagePhrase":"an investigator"},{"uid":"0ebc2250-7973-46a6-bada-bfdc419e8a5b","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"what children should gain from education","passagePhrase":"intellectual performances"},{"uid":"44d91ca2-5ad2-48cc-9f06-e68a820dd214","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"begins at birth","passagePhrase":"are born with"},{"uid":"26d3aec4-0ec2-402d-8f70-a5682ad048c6","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"Variation in intelligence","passagePhrase":"different levels of intelligence"},{"uid":"3db56715-9174-4156-99ff-639ee833a7cf","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"intelligent people","passagePhrase":"a cognitive (high-IQ) elite"},{"uid":"aace56bf-41ce-4191-9036-17d8499f6683","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"should be in positions of power","passagePhrase":"have to take responsibility"},{"uid":"4c43fd6b-23cf-4a33-8cce-c93f438cbf4f","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"People of low intelligence","passagePhrase":"non-elite (low-IQ) people ... the unintelligent"},{"uid":"ab817410-fa91-4a59-a78a-bab6dfff6a27","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"lead uncontrolled lives","passagePhrase":"a kind of chaos"},{"uid":"a2ecd3cf-f264-4d87-81a0-aea4047ac57b","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"same possibilities to be open to everyone","passagePhrase":"should have equal opportunities"},{"uid":"8237f17c-949b-4d2e-871f-9c74556e158e","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"achieve","passagePhrase":"accomplish ... accomplish"},{"uid":"2d510bbb-461c-460f-8011-0c67ca0f5998","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"gain benefits","passagePhrase":"are rewarded"},{"uid":"70d0f6fa-951d-4183-bba3-a153d9ecb200","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"No section of society should have preferential treatment","passagePhrase":"all people are equal ... one person would serve as well as another in government or on a jury or in almost any position of responsibility. In this view of democracy, people are essentially intersubstitutable except for specialized skills, all of which can be learned. In this view, we do not need or want any institutions that might lead to favoring one group over another."},{"uid":"ab232762-0e2f-46c5-a05e-41224fb70fb5","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"develop the same abilities","passagePhrase":"all of which can be learned"},{"uid":"9e7495bb-7078-49eb-a7b1-b85c870882e1","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"without fully understanding each other","passagePhrase":"are likely to miss the point of what others are saying"}]},"reading_u2_242":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below. </p><h2><strong>Saving bugs to find new drugs</strong></h2><p><em>Zoologist Ross Piper looks at the potential of insects in pharmaceutical research</em></p><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>More drugs than you might think are derived from, or inspired by, compounds found in living things. Looking to nature for the soothing and curing of our ailments is nothing new – we have been doing it for tens of thousands of years. You only have to look at other primates – such as the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71a69467-b2ec-4fe3-afc2-3297530254a1\" data-question=\"16\">capuchin monkeys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> who rub themselves with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5984eef4-6153-44f3-a772-a13b43c88877\" data-question=\"16\">toxin-oozing millipedes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> to deter mosquitoes, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71a69467-b2ec-4fe3-afc2-3297530254a1\" data-question=\"16\">the chimpanzees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> who use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5984eef4-6153-44f3-a772-a13b43c88877\" data-question=\"16\">noxious forest plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> to rid themselves of intestinal parasites – to realise that our ancient ancestors too probably had a basic grasp of medicine.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>Pharmaceutical science and chemistry built on these ancient foundations and perfected the extraction, characterization, modification and testing of these natural products. Then, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aad01136-52e5-4cbb-8e2d-ad579a6bd0b1\" data-question=\"19\">for a while<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, modern pharmaceutical science <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d90dd661-766a-4b32-a8e6-5b6b13441863\" data-question=\"19\">moved its focus away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> from nature and into the laboratory, designing chemical compounds from scratch. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c361d55-9243-489d-9744-5de852ec35b5\" data-question=\"19\">The main cause of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> this shift is that although there are plenty of promising chemical compounds in nature, finding them is far from easy. Securing sufficient numbers of the organism in question, isolating and characterizing the compounds of interest, and producing large quantities of these compounds are all significant hurdles.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>Laboratory-based drug discovery has achieved varying levels of success, something which has now prompted the development of new approaches focusing once again on natural products. With the ability to mine genomes for useful compounds, it is now evident that we have barely scratched the surface of nature’s molecular diversity. This realization, together with several looming health crises, such as antibiotic resistance, has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08b982f7-cf70-4f41-9d0b-38266623e813\" data-question=\"14\">put bioprospecting – the search for useful compounds in nature – firmly back on the map<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>Insects are the undisputed masters of the terrestrial domain, where they occupy every possible niche. Consequently, they have a bewildering array of interactions with other organisms, something which has driven the evolution of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4016eea9-e6e6-41d2-a21f-dcd3c6645fc7\" data-question=\"21\">an enormous range of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> very interesting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b67d8e5-a8e1-4e94-8a72-c4e196c1e8ad\" data-question=\"21\">compounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26823388-0d76-4e22-a13b-b12df27c8354\" data-question=\"21\">for defensive and offensive purposes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Their remarkable diversity exceeds that of every other group of animals on the planet combined. Yet even though insects are far and away the most diverse animals in existence, their potential as sources of therapeutic compounds is yet to be realised.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>From the tiny proportion of insects that have been investigated, several promising compounds have been identified. For example, alloferon, an antimicrobial compound <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2ae36fc-5a98-429a-b4d5-0be320a923c4\" data-question=\"20\">produced by blow fly larvae<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, is used as an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ef473c04-f869-421e-a0f2-01ace5e80a37\" data-question=\"20\">antiviral and antitumor agent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in South Korea and Russia. The larvae of a few other insect species are being investigated for the potent antimicrobial compounds they produce. Meanwhile, a compound from the venom of the wasp <em>Polybia paulista </em>has potential in cancer treatment.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>Why is it that insects have received relatively little attention in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b9a79bf1-97d2-4cc6-b647-7eee56c946ab\" data-question=\"17\">bioprospecting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>? Firstly, there are so many insects that, without some manner of targeted approach, investigating this huge variety of species is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"978ec41b-2a5a-498c-9b6a-4aedc91d4119\" data-question=\"17\">daunting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> task. Secondly, insects are generally very small, and the glands inside them that secrete potentially useful compounds are smaller still. This can make it difficult to obtain sufficient quantities of the compound for subsequent testing. Thirdly, although we consider insects to be everywhere, the reality of this ubiquity is vast numbers of a few extremely common species. Many insect species are infrequently encountered and very difficult to rear in captivity, which, again, can leave us with insufficient material to work with.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>My colleagues and I at Aberystwyth University in the UK have developed an approach in which we use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c03a30f-cb47-4a35-b230-66727a100de8\" data-question=\"23\">our knowledge of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> ecology as a guide to target our efforts. The creatures <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b33384d2-d07a-4b6f-8199-9ae7e3d00f3e\" data-question=\"24\">that particularly interest us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> are the many insects that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"65b712e1-595a-4314-b70e-e7c220abe91f\" data-question=\"24\">secrete powerful poison for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3712241b-9b0e-4c3a-b592-63b30cd715dd\" data-question=\"24\">subduing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> prey and keeping it fresh for future consumption. There are even more insects that are masters of exploiting filthy habitats, such as faeces and carcasses, where they are regularly challenged by thousands of micro-organisms. These insects have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"436cd5ca-be63-4c62-81dc-39509fad469e\" data-question=\"25\">many antimicrobial compounds for dealing with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> pathogenic bacteria and fungi, suggesting that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"125364a2-24ae-44f9-acbf-2d8d8c075602\" data-question=\"26\">there is certainly potential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> to find many compounds that can serve as or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80f25a8a-8894-4c62-a277-de4e63a4a5c2\" data-question=\"26\">inspire new antibiotics.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>Although natural history knowledge points us in the right direction, it doesn’t solve the problems associated with obtaining useful compounds from insects. Fortunately, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54c8233b-9e3f-40b9-8356-839704b089bc\" data-question=\"15\">it is now possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7288b420-be65-40da-8faa-e32648b3cd3f\" data-question=\"22\">to snip out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the stretches of the insect’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"73505387-83de-4b0e-969a-4f30fda3c682\" data-question=\"22\">DNA that carry the codes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> for the interesting compounds and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5090b0e-2a90-4ef8-af03-70ed5f9e111d\" data-question=\"22\">insert them into cell lines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that allow larger quantities to be produced. And although the road from isolating and characterizing compounds with desirable qualities to developing a commercial product is very long and full of pitfalls, the variety of successful animal-derived pharmaceuticals on the market demonstrates there is a precedent here that is worth exploring.</p><p><strong>I</strong></p><p>With every bit of wilderness that disappears, we deprive ourselves of potential medicines. As much as I’d love to help develop a groundbreaking insect-derived medicine, my main motivation for looking at insects in this way is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"771a3e18-9fe0-4c0a-aff2-3e7e5b742ac7\" data-question=\"18\">conservation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. I sincerely believe that all species, however small and seemingly insignificant, have a right to exist for their own sake. If we can shine a light on the darker recesses of nature’s medicine cabinet, exploring the useful chemistry of the most diverse animals on the planet, I believe we can make people think differently about the value of nature.</p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has nine paragraphs, <strong>A-I</strong></span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-I</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-20</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"387\" id=\"question-wrapper-387\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of factors driving a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08b982f7-cf70-4f41-9d0b-38266623e813\" data-question=\"14\">renewed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> interest in natural medicinal compounds. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"388\" id=\"question-wrapper-388\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> how recent technological advances have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54c8233b-9e3f-40b9-8356-839704b089bc\" data-question=\"15\">made insect research easier<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"389\" id=\"question-wrapper-389\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71a69467-b2ec-4fe3-afc2-3297530254a1\" data-question=\"16\">examples of animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> which use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5984eef4-6153-44f3-a772-a13b43c88877\" data-question=\"16\">medicinal substances from nature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"390\" id=\"question-wrapper-390\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reasons why it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"978ec41b-2a5a-498c-9b6a-4aedc91d4119\" data-question=\"17\">challenging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to use insects in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b9a79bf1-97d2-4cc6-b647-7eee56c946ab\" data-question=\"17\">drug research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"391\" id=\"question-wrapper-391\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to how interest in drug research may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"771a3e18-9fe0-4c0a-aff2-3e7e5b742ac7\" data-question=\"18\">benefit wildlife<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"392\" id=\"question-wrapper-392\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c361d55-9243-489d-9744-5de852ec35b5\" data-question=\"19\">a reason why<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> nature-based medicines <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d90dd661-766a-4b32-a8e6-5b6b13441863\" data-question=\"19\">fell out of favour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aad01136-52e5-4cbb-8e2d-ad579a6bd0b1\" data-question=\"19\">for a period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"393\" id=\"question-wrapper-393\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an example of an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2ae36fc-5a98-429a-b4d5-0be320a923c4\" data-question=\"20\">insect-derived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> medicine in use at the moment </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters,<strong> A-E</strong></span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letters in boxes<strong> 21</strong> and <strong>22</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span>Which <strong>TWO</strong> of the following make insects interesting for drug research?</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> the huge number of individual insects in the world</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4016eea9-e6e6-41d2-a21f-dcd3c6645fc7\" data-question=\"21\">the variety of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> substances insects have developed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26823388-0d76-4e22-a13b-b12df27c8354\" data-question=\"21\">protect themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> the potential <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7288b420-be65-40da-8faa-e32648b3cd3f\" data-question=\"22\">to extract<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5090b0e-2a90-4ef8-af03-70ed5f9e111d\" data-question=\"22\">make use of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"73505387-83de-4b0e-969a-4f30fda3c682\" data-question=\"22\">insects’ genetic codes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> the similarities between different species of insect</span></p><p><span><strong>E </strong> the manageable size of most insects</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"394\" id=\"question-wrapper-394\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"395\" id=\"question-wrapper-395\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span><em>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</em></span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes <strong>23-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</span><span> </span></p><h3><span><strong>Research at Aberystwyth University</strong></span></h3><p><span>Ross Piper and fellow zoologists at Aberystwyth University are using their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c03a30f-cb47-4a35-b230-66727a100de8\" data-question=\"23\">expertise in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <strong>23</strong>………………………… when undertaking bioprospecting with insects. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b33384d2-d07a-4b6f-8199-9ae7e3d00f3e\" data-question=\"24\">are especially interested in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"65b712e1-595a-4314-b70e-e7c220abe91f\" data-question=\"24\">compounds that insects produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3712241b-9b0e-4c3a-b592-63b30cd715dd\" data-question=\"24\">overpower<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> and preserve their <strong>24</strong>…………………………. They are also interested in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"436cd5ca-be63-4c62-81dc-39509fad469e\" data-question=\"25\">compounds which insects use to protect themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> from pathogenic bacteria and fungi found in their <strong>25</strong>………………………… Piper hopes that these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"899a01e3-1fbb-451f-8b6f-9f54ea47cc67\" data-question=\"26\">substances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"125364a2-24ae-44f9-acbf-2d8d8c075602\" data-question=\"26\">will be useful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80f25a8a-8894-4c62-a277-de4e63a4a5c2\" data-question=\"26\">in the development of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> drugs such as <strong>26</strong>……………………………..</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"396\" id=\"question-wrapper-396\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ECOLOGY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"397\" id=\"question-wrapper-397\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PREY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"398\" id=\"question-wrapper-398\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HABITATS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"399\" id=\"question-wrapper-399\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ANTIBIOTICS</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"71a69467-b2ec-4fe3-afc2-3297530254a1","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"examples of animals","passagePhrase":"capuchin monkeys ... the chimpanzees"},{"uid":"5984eef4-6153-44f3-a772-a13b43c88877","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"medicinal substances from nature","passagePhrase":"toxin-oozing millipedes ... noxious forest plants"},{"uid":"aad01136-52e5-4cbb-8e2d-ad579a6bd0b1","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"for a period","passagePhrase":"for a while"},{"uid":"d90dd661-766a-4b32-a8e6-5b6b13441863","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"fell out of favour","passagePhrase":"moved its focus away"},{"uid":"3c361d55-9243-489d-9744-5de852ec35b5","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"a reason why","passagePhrase":"The main cause of"},{"uid":"08b982f7-cf70-4f41-9d0b-38266623e813","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"renewed","passagePhrase":"put bioprospecting – the search for useful compounds in nature – firmly back on the map"},{"uid":"4016eea9-e6e6-41d2-a21f-dcd3c6645fc7","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"the variety of","passagePhrase":"an enormous range of"},{"uid":"7b67d8e5-a8e1-4e94-8a72-c4e196c1e8ad","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"compounds"},{"uid":"26823388-0d76-4e22-a13b-b12df27c8354","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"protect themselves","passagePhrase":"for defensive and offensive purposes"},{"uid":"c2ae36fc-5a98-429a-b4d5-0be320a923c4","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"insect-derived","passagePhrase":"produced by blow fly larvae"},{"uid":"ef473c04-f869-421e-a0f2-01ace5e80a37","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"antiviral and antitumor agent"},{"uid":"b9a79bf1-97d2-4cc6-b647-7eee56c946ab","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"drug research","passagePhrase":"bioprospecting"},{"uid":"978ec41b-2a5a-498c-9b6a-4aedc91d4119","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"challenging","passagePhrase":"daunting"},{"uid":"5c03a30f-cb47-4a35-b230-66727a100de8","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"expertise in","passagePhrase":"our knowledge of"},{"uid":"b33384d2-d07a-4b6f-8199-9ae7e3d00f3e","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"are especially interested in","passagePhrase":"that particularly interest us"},{"uid":"65b712e1-595a-4314-b70e-e7c220abe91f","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"compounds that insects produce","passagePhrase":"secrete powerful poison for"},{"uid":"3712241b-9b0e-4c3a-b592-63b30cd715dd","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"overpower","passagePhrase":"subduing"},{"uid":"436cd5ca-be63-4c62-81dc-39509fad469e","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"compounds which insects use to protect themselves","passagePhrase":"many antimicrobial compounds for dealing with"},{"uid":"125364a2-24ae-44f9-acbf-2d8d8c075602","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"will be useful","passagePhrase":"there is certainly potential"},{"uid":"80f25a8a-8894-4c62-a277-de4e63a4a5c2","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"in the development of","passagePhrase":"inspire new antibiotics."},{"uid":"54c8233b-9e3f-40b9-8356-839704b089bc","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"made insect research easier","passagePhrase":"it is now possible"},{"uid":"7288b420-be65-40da-8faa-e32648b3cd3f","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"to extract","passagePhrase":"to snip out"},{"uid":"73505387-83de-4b0e-969a-4f30fda3c682","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"insects’ genetic codes","passagePhrase":"DNA that carry the codes"},{"uid":"b5090b0e-2a90-4ef8-af03-70ed5f9e111d","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"make use of","passagePhrase":"insert them into cell lines"},{"uid":"771a3e18-9fe0-4c0a-aff2-3e7e5b742ac7","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"benefit wildlife","passagePhrase":"conservation"},{"uid":"899a01e3-1fbb-451f-8b6f-9f54ea47cc67","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"substances","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_243":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong><span>The power of play</span></strong></span></h2><p><span>Virtually every child, the world over, plays. The drive to play is so intense that children will <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2b33be2a-d12f-446f-8da6-629c8e928403\" data-question=\"32\">do so in any circumstances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, for instance when they have no real toys, or when parents do not actively encourage the behavior. In the eyes of a young child, running, pretending, and building are fun. Researchers and educators know that these playful activities benefit the development of the whole child across social, cognitive, physical, and emotional domains. Indeed, play is such an instrumental component to healthy child development that the United Nation High Commission on Human Rights (1989) recognized play as a fundamental right of every child.</span></p><p><span>Yet, while experts continue to expound a powerful argument for the importance of play in children’s lives, the actual time children spend playing continues to decrease. Today, children play eight hours less each week than their counterparts did two decades ago (Elkind 2008). Under pressure of rising academic standards, play is being replaced by test preparation in kindergartens and grade schools, and parents who aim to give their preschoolers a leg up are led to believe that flashcards and educational ‘toys’ are the path to success. Our society has created a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5dbfe22a-8fba-4295-99c2-9365a3803fc2\" data-question=\"33\">false<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe91073c-c891-4c38-825c-b6be9d8690ba\" data-question=\"33\">dichotomy between play and learning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Through play, children learn to regulate their behavior, lay the foundations for later learning in science and mathematics, figure out the complex negotiations of social relationships, build a repertoire of creative problem-solving skills, and so much more. There is also an important role for adults in guiding children through playful learning opportunities.</span></p><p><span>Full consensus on a formal definition of play <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"3ca09297-0d40-4b56-8952-11655d812822\" data-question=\"35\">continues to elude<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the researchers and theorists who study it. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"3ca09297-0d40-4b56-8952-11655d812822\" data-question=\"35\">Definitions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5958d2e5-fc3d-4ab3-aadf-9308067b8857\" data-question=\"27\">range from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"129819c1-9722-4215-9091-b23018a70f27\" data-question=\"27\">discrete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> descriptions of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88480dd4-422b-4fcb-ba9c-77ea7cf88fb8\" data-question=\"27\">various types of play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> such as physical, construction, language, or symbolic play (Miler &amp; Almon 2009), to lists of broad criteria, based on observations and attitudes, that are meant to capture the essence of all play behaviors (e.g. Rubin et al. 1983).</span></p><p><span>A majority of the contemporary definitions of play focus on several key criteria. The founder of the National Institute for Play, Stuart Brown, has described play as ‘anything that spontaneously is done for its own sake’. More specifically, he says it ‘appears purposeless, produces pleasure and joy, [and] leads one to the next stage of mastery’ (as quoted in Tippett 2008). Similarly, Miller and Almon (2009) say that play includes ‘activities that are freely chosen and directed by children and arise from intrinsic motivation’. Often, play is defined along a continuum as more or less playful using the following set of behavioral and dispositional criteria (e.g. Rubin et al. 1983).</span></p><p><span>Play is pleasurable: Children must enjoy the activity or it is not play. It is intrinsically motivated: Children engage in play simply for the satisfaction the behavior itself brings. It has no extrinsically motivated function or goal. Play is process oriented: When children play, the means are more important than the ends. It is freely chosen, spontaneous and voluntary. If a child is pressured, they will likely not think of the activity as play. Play is actively engaged: Players must be physically and/or mentally involved in the activity. Play is non-literal. It involves make-believe.</span></p><p><span>According to this view, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18116f7e-732f-48b9-8ae2-9716885b52e2\" data-question=\"31\">children’s playful behaviors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"65ac7e0d-4101-42fc-b05a-59565ade96ba\" data-question=\"31\">can range<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f93a7d7-d394-42ce-8b0c-a126c38b9188\" data-question=\"31\">in degree from 0% to 100% playful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. Rubin and colleagues did not assign greater weight to any one dimension in determining playfulness; however, other researchers have suggested that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fdde756-2971-4105-ad10-827a70100246\" data-question=\"30\">process orientation and a lack of obvious functional purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> may be the most important <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fdde756-2971-4105-ad10-827a70100246\" data-question=\"30\">aspects of play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> (e.g. Pellegrini 2009).</span></p><p><span>From the perspective of a continuum, play can thus blend with other motives and attitudes that are less playful, such as work. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1240985-45b2-4885-9882-05c86c434d14\" data-question=\"36\">Unlike<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> play, work is typically not viewed as enjoyable and it is extrinsically motivated (i.e. it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b83aae8-0cd7-4618-90af-7abecd4dd5f8\" data-question=\"36\">is goal oriented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>). Researcher Joan Goodman (1994) suggested that hybrid forms of work and play are not a detriment to learning; rather, they can provide optimal contexts for learning. For example, a child may be engaged in a difficult, goal-directed activity set up by their teacher, but they may still be actively engaged and intrinsically motivated. At <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64df00ef-d9ef-40bc-8c7e-54dfc0291eba\" data-question=\"29\">this mid-point between play and work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, the child’s motivation, coupled with guidance from an adult, can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0261d526-b04d-4d9c-a491-f60c855ad2b2\" data-question=\"29\">create robust opportunities for playful learning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Critically, recent research supports the idea that adults can facilitate children’s learning while maintaining a playful approach in interactions known as ‘guided play’ (Fisher et al. 2011). <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa2c2797-a5ca-456b-bf61-a48b14c7716e\" data-question=\"28\">The adult’s role in play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5663f1e1-87fc-49b6-a6f1-d750513cf41a\" data-question=\"28\">varies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> as a function of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e31ae868-51b7-49b7-b40c-9af5a0cfbf77\" data-question=\"28\">their educational goals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and the child’s developmental level (Hirsch-Pasek et al. 2009).</span></p><p><span>Guided play takes two forms. At a very basic level, adults can enrich the child’s environment by providing objects or experiences that promote aspects of a curriculum. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bf5fdfd1-88f0-409c-953c-581e62c34633\" data-question=\"37\">In the more direct form of guided play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, parents or other adults can support children’s play by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"373ccfb7-f128-4ec8-b6c7-305c6c9f4036\" data-question=\"37\">joining in the fun as a co-player<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, raising thoughtful questions, commenting on children’s discoveries, or encouraging <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82fc61e2-dd1b-44a9-8161-c050196eaf1c\" data-question=\"37\">further exploration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> or new facets to the child’s activity. Although <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4cd4dde9-01e8-4be2-9153-41f22f452a37\" data-question=\"38\">playful learning can be somewhat structured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, it must also be child-centered (Nicolopolou et al. 2006). Play should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c602926f-d898-444f-a157-16a0eecc1354\" data-question=\"38\">stem from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> the child’s own desire.</span></p><p><span>Both free and guided play are essential elements in a child-centered approach to playful learning. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e1f63de-6a64-46dd-8953-e28cc4b948e5\" data-question=\"39\">Intrinsically motivated free play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a448ce8-cbc4-4e95-bfd2-0b4b364c10e9\" data-question=\"39\">provides the child with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a081d55c-59ed-4c6e-b987-410e2f4d4357\" data-question=\"39\">true<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> autonomy, while guided play is an avenue through which parents and educators can provide more targeted learning experiences. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"999bbe57-b8c7-4eeb-a202-0d8798b80ee3\" data-question=\"40\">In either case<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, play should be actively engaged, it should be predominantly child-directed, and it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4dc40149-c251-4210-9bca-26be68b676f0\" data-question=\"40\">must be fun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions <strong>27-31</strong>) and the list of researchers below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct researcher, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Researchers</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Elkind<br></span><span><strong>B</strong> Miller &amp; Almon<br></span><span><strong>C</strong> Rubin et al.<br></span><span><strong>D</strong> Stuart Brown<br></span><span><strong>E</strong> Pellegrini<br></span><span><strong>F</strong> Joan Goodman<br></span><span><strong>G</strong> Girsch-Pasek et al.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"400\" id=\"question-wrapper-400\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Play <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5958d2e5-fc3d-4ab3-aadf-9308067b8857\" data-question=\"27\">can be divided into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88480dd4-422b-4fcb-ba9c-77ea7cf88fb8\" data-question=\"27\">a number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"129819c1-9722-4215-9091-b23018a70f27\" data-question=\"27\">separate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> categories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"401\" id=\"question-wrapper-401\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e31ae868-51b7-49b7-b40c-9af5a0cfbf77\" data-question=\"28\">Adults’ intended goals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5663f1e1-87fc-49b6-a6f1-d750513cf41a\" data-question=\"28\">affect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa2c2797-a5ca-456b-bf61-a48b14c7716e\" data-question=\"28\">how they play with children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"402\" id=\"question-wrapper-402\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64df00ef-d9ef-40bc-8c7e-54dfc0291eba\" data-question=\"29\">Combining work with play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0261d526-b04d-4d9c-a491-f60c855ad2b2\" data-question=\"29\">be the best way for children to learn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"403\" id=\"question-wrapper-403\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fdde756-2971-4105-ad10-827a70100246\" data-question=\"30\">Certain elements of play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> are more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7079e2b-b5f3-4fc1-bd1b-c7d2effffc07\" data-question=\"30\">significant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> than others. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"404\" id=\"question-wrapper-404\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18116f7e-732f-48b9-8ae2-9716885b52e2\" data-question=\"31\">Activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"65ac7e0d-4101-42fc-b05a-59565ade96ba\" data-question=\"31\">can be classified<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f93a7d7-d394-42ce-8b0c-a126c38b9188\" data-question=\"31\">on a scale of playfulness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>32-36</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the winter</span></p><p><span><strong>NO </strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"405\" id=\"question-wrapper-405\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Children <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2b33be2a-d12f-446f-8da6-629c8e928403\" data-question=\"32\">need toys in order to play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"406\" id=\"question-wrapper-406\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5dbfe22a-8fba-4295-99c2-9365a3803fc2\" data-question=\"33\">mistake<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> to treat play and learning as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe91073c-c891-4c38-825c-b6be9d8690ba\" data-question=\"33\">separate types of activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"407\" id=\"question-wrapper-407\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Play helps children to develop their artistic talents. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"408\" id=\"question-wrapper-408\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Researchers <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"3ca09297-0d40-4b56-8952-11655d812822\" data-question=\"35\">have agreed on a definition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of play. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"409\" id=\"question-wrapper-409\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Work and play <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1240985-45b2-4885-9882-05c86c434d14\" data-question=\"36\">differ<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> in terms of whether or not they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b83aae8-0cd7-4618-90af-7abecd4dd5f8\" data-question=\"36\">have a target<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span><em>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</em></span></p><p><span>Write your answers in boxes <strong>37-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</span></p><h3><span><strong>Guided play</strong></span></h3><p><span>In the simplest form of guided play, an adult contributes to the environment in which the child is playing. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bf5fdfd1-88f0-409c-953c-581e62c34633\" data-question=\"37\">Alternatively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, an adult <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"373ccfb7-f128-4ec8-b6c7-305c6c9f4036\" data-question=\"37\">can play with a child<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> and develop the play, for instance by <strong>37</strong>…………………….. the child to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82fc61e2-dd1b-44a9-8161-c050196eaf1c\" data-question=\"37\">investigate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> different aspects of their game. Adults can help children to learn through play, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4cd4dde9-01e8-4be2-9153-41f22f452a37\" data-question=\"38\">may make the activity rather structured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, but it should still be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c602926f-d898-444f-a157-16a0eecc1354\" data-question=\"38\">based on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> the child’s <strong>38</strong>…………………………. to play.</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e1f63de-6a64-46dd-8953-e28cc4b948e5\" data-question=\"39\">Play without the intervention of adults<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a448ce8-cbc4-4e95-bfd2-0b4b364c10e9\" data-question=\"39\">gives children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> real <strong>39</strong>………………………….; with adults, play can be <strong>40</strong>………………………… at particular goals. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"999bbe57-b8c7-4eeb-a202-0d8798b80ee3\" data-question=\"40\">all forms of play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> should be an opportunity for children to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4dc40149-c251-4210-9bca-26be68b676f0\" data-question=\"40\">have fun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"410\" id=\"question-wrapper-410\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ENCOURAGING</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"411\" id=\"question-wrapper-411\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DESIRE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"412\" id=\"question-wrapper-412\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AUTONOMY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"413\" id=\"question-wrapper-413\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TARGETED</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"5dbfe22a-8fba-4295-99c2-9365a3803fc2","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"mistake","passagePhrase":"false"},{"uid":"fe91073c-c891-4c38-825c-b6be9d8690ba","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"separate types of activities","passagePhrase":"dichotomy between play and learning"},{"uid":"5958d2e5-fc3d-4ab3-aadf-9308067b8857","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"can be divided into","passagePhrase":"range from"},{"uid":"129819c1-9722-4215-9091-b23018a70f27","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"separate","passagePhrase":"discrete"},{"uid":"88480dd4-422b-4fcb-ba9c-77ea7cf88fb8","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"a number of separate categories","passagePhrase":"various types of play"},{"uid":"18116f7e-732f-48b9-8ae2-9716885b52e2","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Activities","passagePhrase":"children’s playful behaviors"},{"uid":"65ac7e0d-4101-42fc-b05a-59565ade96ba","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"can be classified","passagePhrase":"can range"},{"uid":"6f93a7d7-d394-42ce-8b0c-a126c38b9188","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"on a scale of playfulness","passagePhrase":"in degree from 0% to 100% playful"},{"uid":"2fdde756-2971-4105-ad10-827a70100246","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Certain elements of play","passagePhrase":"process orientation and a lack of obvious functional purpose ... aspects of play"},{"uid":"b1240985-45b2-4885-9882-05c86c434d14","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"differ","passagePhrase":"Unlike"},{"uid":"1b83aae8-0cd7-4618-90af-7abecd4dd5f8","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"have a target","passagePhrase":"is goal oriented"},{"uid":"64df00ef-d9ef-40bc-8c7e-54dfc0291eba","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Combining work with play","passagePhrase":"this mid-point between play and work"},{"uid":"0261d526-b04d-4d9c-a491-f60c855ad2b2","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"be the best way for children to learn","passagePhrase":"create robust opportunities for playful learning"},{"uid":"fa2c2797-a5ca-456b-bf61-a48b14c7716e","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"how they play with children","passagePhrase":"The adult’s role in play"},{"uid":"5663f1e1-87fc-49b6-a6f1-d750513cf41a","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"affect","passagePhrase":"varies"},{"uid":"e31ae868-51b7-49b7-b40c-9af5a0cfbf77","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Adults’ intended goals","passagePhrase":"their educational goals"},{"uid":"bf5fdfd1-88f0-409c-953c-581e62c34633","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"Alternatively","passagePhrase":"In the more direct form of guided play"},{"uid":"373ccfb7-f128-4ec8-b6c7-305c6c9f4036","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"can play with a child","passagePhrase":"joining in the fun as a co-player"},{"uid":"82fc61e2-dd1b-44a9-8161-c050196eaf1c","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"investigate","passagePhrase":"further exploration"},{"uid":"4cd4dde9-01e8-4be2-9153-41f22f452a37","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"may make the activity rather structured","passagePhrase":"playful learning can be somewhat structured"},{"uid":"c602926f-d898-444f-a157-16a0eecc1354","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"based on","passagePhrase":"stem from"},{"uid":"6e1f63de-6a64-46dd-8953-e28cc4b948e5","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Play without the intervention of adults","passagePhrase":"Intrinsically motivated free play"},{"uid":"0a448ce8-cbc4-4e95-bfd2-0b4b364c10e9","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"gives children","passagePhrase":"provides the child with"},{"uid":"a081d55c-59ed-4c6e-b987-410e2f4d4357","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"true"},{"uid":"999bbe57-b8c7-4eeb-a202-0d8798b80ee3","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"all forms of play","passagePhrase":"In either case"},{"uid":"4dc40149-c251-4210-9bca-26be68b676f0","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"have fun","passagePhrase":"must be fun"},{"uid":"a7079e2b-b5f3-4fc1-bd1b-c7d2effffc07","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"significant","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_244":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions</strong> <strong>1-13</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</p><p> </p><h2><strong>The secret of staying young</strong></h2><p><em>Pheidole dentata</em>, a native ant of the south-eastern U.S., isn’t immortal. But scientists have found that it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8e89acd-020c-47ea-b861-c75fae816c2f\" data-question=\"9\">doesn’t seem to show any signs of aging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Old workers ants can do everything just as well as the youngsters, and their brains appear just as sharp. ‘We get a picture that these ants really don’t decline,’ says Ysabel Giraldo, who studies the ants for her doctoral thesis at Boston University.</p><p>Such age-defying feats are rare in the animal kingdom. Naked mole rats can live for almost 30 years and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8e89acd-020c-47ea-b861-c75fae816c2f\" data-question=\"9\">stay fit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e0388f8f-0ed9-4951-8cc8-d7b17b1ca89a\" data-question=\"9\">for nearly their entire lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. They can still reproduce even when old, and they never get cancer. But the vast majority of animals deteriorate with age just like people do. Like the naked mole rat, ants are social creatures that usually live in highly organised colonies. ‘It’s this social complexity that makes <em>P. dentata </em>useful for studying aging in people,’ says Giraldo, now at the California Institute of Technology. Humans are also highly social, a trait that has been connected to healthier aging. By contrast, most animal studies of aging use mice, worms or fruit flies, which all lead much more isolated lives.</p><p>In the lab, <em>P. dentata </em>worker ants typically live <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5906145-68df-4623-841a-8dd896a9491c\" data-question=\"13\">for around 140 days<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. Giraldo focused on ants at four <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46ab12e9-fae4-451b-9666-7515dba06a30\" data-question=\"1\">age ranges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>: 20 to 22 days, 45 to 47 days, 95 to 97 days and 120 to 122 days. Unlike all previous studies, which only estimated how old the ants were, her work tracked the ants from the time the pupae became adults, so she knew <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2033f6f9-0518-49ba-a813-7a7c8b4fbac2\" data-question=\"10\">their exact ages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. Then she put them through a range of tests.</p><p>Giraldo watched how well the ants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e7406ae7-3ef0-4fca-a6aa-3d682173bd1f\" data-question=\"2\">took care of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the young of the colony, recording how often each ant attended to, carried and fed them. She compared how well 20-day-old and 95-day-old ants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59dadcb5-9b2e-47d7-b8cc-0cba07eb9ab8\" data-question=\"3\">followed the telltale scent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> that the insects usually leave to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f1b00ee2-98ad-409c-909c-7820227d6473\" data-question=\"3\">mark a trail to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> food. She tested how ants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9ae0206-65fb-4b2f-a6ec-334221026198\" data-question=\"4\">responded to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> light and also measured how active they were by counting how often ants in a small dish walked across a line. And she experimented with how ants react to live prey: a tethered fruit fly. Giraldo expected the older ants to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34498dfd-29c5-4d7e-ac7c-7263664a1740\" data-question=\"11\">perform<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> poorly in all these tasks. But the elderly insects were all good caretakers and trail-followers – the 95-day-old ants <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"89310a61-570b-40dd-b27d-402293fbe85a\" data-question=\"11\">could track the scent even longer than their younger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> counterparts. They all responded do light well, and the older ants were more active. And when it came to reacting to prey, the older ants attacked <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"473cecfd-e8af-4b4a-94f4-63fdd7f24e13\" data-question=\"5\">the poor fruit fly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> just as aggressively as the young ones did, flaring their mandibles or pulling at the fly’s legs.</p><p>Then Giraldo compared the brains of 20-day-old and 95-day-ole ants, identifying any cells that were close to death. She saw no <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"465419a8-8477-42f8-bd96-9713473740d4\" data-question=\"6\">major differences with age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"465419a8-8477-42f8-bd96-9713473740d4\" data-question=\"6\">nor was there any difference in the location<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of the dying cells, showing that age didn’t seem to affect specific brain functions. Ants and other insects have structures in their brains called mushroom bodies, which are important for processing information, learning and memory. She also wanted to see if aging affects the density of synaptic complexes within these structures – regions <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e8400dc-69c4-45f3-9d85-1f8e49f9f675\" data-question=\"7\">where<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> neurons <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c752ef5c-17a5-4899-817f-d110e30f8070\" data-question=\"7\">come together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. Again, the answer was no. what was more, the old ants didn’t experience any drop in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"567e7d33-4e40-4f96-baff-8679b5ad92a6\" data-question=\"8\">levels of either serotonin or dopamine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> – brain chemicals whose decline often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8db885b4-34d1-4211-953c-f2abb815a56a\" data-question=\"8\">coincides with aging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. In humans, for example, a decrease in serotonin has been linked to Alzheimer’s disease.</p><p>‘This is the first time anyone has looked at both behavioral and neural changes in these ants so thoroughly,’ says Giraldo, who recently published the findings in the <em>Proceeding of the Royal Society B</em>. Scientists have looked at some similar aspects in bees, but the results of recent bee studies were mixed – some studies showed age-related declines, which biologists call senescence, and others didn’t. ‘For now, the study raises more questions than it answers,’ Giraldo says, ‘including how <em>P. dentata </em>stays in such good shape.’</p><p>Also, if the ants don’t deteriorate with age, why do they die at all? Out in the wild, the ants probably <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5906145-68df-4623-841a-8dd896a9491c\" data-question=\"13\">don’t live for a full 140 days<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> thanks to predators, disease and just being in an environment that’s much harsher than the comforts of the lab. ‘The lucky ants that do live into old age may suffer a steep decline just before dying,’ Giraldo says, but she can’t say for sure because her study wasn’t designed to follow an ant’s final moments.</p><p>‘It will be important to extend these findings to other species of social insects,’ says Gene E. Robinson, an entomologist at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign. This ant might be unique, or it might represent a broader pattern among other social bugs with possible clues to the science of aging in larger animals. Either way, it seems that for these ants, age really doesn’t matter.</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answer in boxes <strong>1-8</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>Ysabel Giraldo’s research</strong></span></p><p><span>Focused on a total of <strong>1</strong>………………………….. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46ab12e9-fae4-451b-9666-7515dba06a30\" data-question=\"1\">different age groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of ants, analyzing</span></p><p><span><strong>Behaviour:</strong></span></p><p><span><span>•</span> how well ants <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e7406ae7-3ef0-4fca-a6aa-3d682173bd1f\" data-question=\"2\">looked after<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> their <strong>2</strong> …………………………..</span></p><p><span><span>• </span> their ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f1b00ee2-98ad-409c-909c-7820227d6473\" data-question=\"3\">locate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <strong>3</strong>………………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59dadcb5-9b2e-47d7-b8cc-0cba07eb9ab8\" data-question=\"3\">using a scent trail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p><span><span>•</span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9ae0206-65fb-4b2f-a6ec-334221026198\" data-question=\"4\">the effect that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <strong>4</strong>………………………….. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9ae0206-65fb-4b2f-a6ec-334221026198\" data-question=\"4\">had on them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></span></p><p><span><span>•</span> how <strong>5</strong>…………………………. They attacked <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"473cecfd-e8af-4b4a-94f4-63fdd7f24e13\" data-question=\"5\">prey<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>Brains:</strong></span></p><p><span><span>• </span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"465419a8-8477-42f8-bd96-9713473740d4\" data-question=\"6\">comparison between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> age and the <strong>6</strong>…………………………… of dying cells in the brains of ants</span></p><p><span><span>• </span> condition of synaptic complexes (<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e8400dc-69c4-45f3-9d85-1f8e49f9f675\" data-question=\"7\">areas in which<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <strong>7</strong>…………………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c752ef5c-17a5-4899-817f-d110e30f8070\" data-question=\"7\">meet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>) in the brain’s ‘mushroom bodies’</span></p><p><span><span>• </span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"567e7d33-4e40-4f96-baff-8679b5ad92a6\" data-question=\"8\">level of two<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <strong>8</strong>………………………….. in the brain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8db885b4-34d1-4211-953c-f2abb815a56a\" data-question=\"8\">associated with ageing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"414\" id=\"question-wrapper-414\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOUR/4</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"415\" id=\"question-wrapper-415\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YOUNG</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"416\" id=\"question-wrapper-416\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOOD</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"417\" id=\"question-wrapper-417\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LIGHT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"418\" id=\"question-wrapper-418\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AGGRESSIVELY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"419\" id=\"question-wrapper-419\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LOCATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"420\" id=\"question-wrapper-420\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NEURONS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"421\" id=\"question-wrapper-421\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CHEMICALS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information give in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>9-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"422\" id=\"question-wrapper-422\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Pheidole dentata ants are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f05c29bf-573a-4b4c-9470-7cbc6cf03295\" data-question=\"9\">the only known<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> animals which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8e89acd-020c-47ea-b861-c75fae816c2f\" data-question=\"9\">remain active<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e0388f8f-0ed9-4951-8cc8-d7b17b1ca89a\" data-question=\"9\">for almost their whole lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"423\" id=\"question-wrapper-423\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Ysabel Giraldo was the first person to study Pheidole dentata ants using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2033f6f9-0518-49ba-a813-7a7c8b4fbac2\" data-question=\"10\">precise data about the insects’ ages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"424\" id=\"question-wrapper-424\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The ants in Giraldo’s experiments <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"89310a61-570b-40dd-b27d-402293fbe85a\" data-question=\"11\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34498dfd-29c5-4d7e-ac7c-7263664a1740\" data-question=\"11\">behaved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> as she had predicted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> that they would. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"425\" id=\"question-wrapper-425\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The recent studies of bees used different methods of measuring age-related decline. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"426\" id=\"question-wrapper-426\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Pheidole dentata ants kept in laboratory conditions <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5906145-68df-4623-841a-8dd896a9491c\" data-question=\"13\">tend to live longer lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"d8e89acd-020c-47ea-b861-c75fae816c2f","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"remain active","passagePhrase":"doesn’t seem to show any signs of aging ... stay fit"},{"uid":"e0388f8f-0ed9-4951-8cc8-d7b17b1ca89a","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"for almost their whole lives","passagePhrase":"for nearly their entire lives"},{"uid":"d5906145-68df-4623-841a-8dd896a9491c","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"tend to live longer lives","passagePhrase":"for around 140 days ... don’t live for a full 140 days"},{"uid":"46ab12e9-fae4-451b-9666-7515dba06a30","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"different age groups","passagePhrase":"age ranges"},{"uid":"2033f6f9-0518-49ba-a813-7a7c8b4fbac2","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"precise data about the insects’ ages","passagePhrase":"their exact ages"},{"uid":"e7406ae7-3ef0-4fca-a6aa-3d682173bd1f","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"looked after","passagePhrase":"took care of"},{"uid":"59dadcb5-9b2e-47d7-b8cc-0cba07eb9ab8","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"using a scent trail","passagePhrase":"followed the telltale scent"},{"uid":"f1b00ee2-98ad-409c-909c-7820227d6473","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"locate","passagePhrase":"mark a trail to"},{"uid":"e9ae0206-65fb-4b2f-a6ec-334221026198","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"the effect that ... had on them","passagePhrase":"responded to"},{"uid":"34498dfd-29c5-4d7e-ac7c-7263664a1740","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"behaved","passagePhrase":"perform"},{"uid":"473cecfd-e8af-4b4a-94f4-63fdd7f24e13","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"prey","passagePhrase":"the poor fruit fly"},{"uid":"465419a8-8477-42f8-bd96-9713473740d4","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"comparison between","passagePhrase":"major differences with age ... nor was there any difference in the location"},{"uid":"2e8400dc-69c4-45f3-9d85-1f8e49f9f675","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"areas in which","passagePhrase":"where"},{"uid":"c752ef5c-17a5-4899-817f-d110e30f8070","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"meet","passagePhrase":"come together"},{"uid":"567e7d33-4e40-4f96-baff-8679b5ad92a6","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"level of two","passagePhrase":"levels of either serotonin or dopamine"},{"uid":"8db885b4-34d1-4211-953c-f2abb815a56a","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"associated with ageing","passagePhrase":"coincides with aging"}]},"reading_u2_245":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Why zoos are good</strong></span></h2><h3><span>Scientist David Hone makes the case for zoos</span></h3><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>In my view, it is perfectly possible for many species of animals living in zoos or wildlife parks to have a quality of life as high as, or higher than, in the wild. Animals in good zoos <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eed7ca3-e5e5-4c09-bfe6-5d8db7d2fe7c\" data-question=\"17\">get a varied and high-quality diet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> with all the supplements required, and any <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eed7ca3-e5e5-4c09-bfe6-5d8db7d2fe7c\" data-question=\"17\">illnesses they might have will be treated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Their movement might be somewhat restricted, but they have a safe environment in which to live, and they are spared bullying and social ostracism by others of their kind. They do not suffer from the threat or stress of predators, or the irritation and pain of parasites or injuries. The average captive animal will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aab99554-7d46-4eae-8efa-02348228c103\" data-question=\"18\">have a greater life expectancy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> compared with its wild counterpart, and will not die of drought, of starvation or in the jaws of a predator. A lot of very nasty things happen to truly ‘wild’ animals that simply don’t happen in good zoos, and to view a life that is ‘free’ as one that is automatically ‘good’ is, I think, an error. Furthermore, zoos serve several key purposes.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Firstly, zoos aid conservation. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df8bc8ae-69b5-4b5c-9efa-c2cbd8103a54\" data-question=\"14\">Colossal numbers of species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b80f361b-9d69-4bbe-b653-730dd95fda2e\" data-question=\"14\">are becoming extinct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> across the world, and many more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df8bc8ae-69b5-4b5c-9efa-c2cbd8103a54\" data-question=\"14\">are increasingly threatened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and therefore risk extinction. Moreover, some of these collapses have been sudden, dramatic and unexpected, or were simply discovered very late in the day. A species protected in captivity <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"485ada59-2eb5-4a88-a8e5-8eb44fd77b94\" data-question=\"26\">can be bred up to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> provide a reservoir population against a population crash or extinction in the wild. A good number of species <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"29231f37-725a-4c8e-9ef2-b765c5f18c6e\" data-question=\"19\">only exist in captivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02823555-3dce-47a5-a717-e4fa330d1f3b\" data-question=\"19\">many of these living in zoos<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Still more only exist in the wild because they have been reintroduced from zoos, or have wild populations that have been boosted by captive bred animals. Without these efforts there would be fewer species alive today. Although reintroduction successes are few and far between, the numbers are increasing, and the very fact that species have been saved or reintroduced as a result of captive breeding proves the value of such initiatives.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Zoos also provide education. Many children and adults, especially those in cities, will never see a wild animal beyond a fox or pigeon. While it is true that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db9abb4c-7290-4ae1-bc4e-3f5996892603\" data-question=\"16\">television documentaries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> are becoming ever more detailed and impressive, and many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db9abb4c-7290-4ae1-bc4e-3f5996892603\" data-question=\"16\">natural history specimens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> are on display in museums, there really is nothing to compare with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"589ee4de-94f7-4d81-bd05-64893506da8f\" data-question=\"16\">seeing a living creature in the flesh, hearing it, smelling it, watching what it does<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> and having the time to absorb details. That alone will bring a greater understanding and perspective to many, and hopefully give them a greater appreciation for wildlife, conservation efforts and how they can contribute.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>In addition to this, there is also the education that can take place in zoos through signs, talks and presentations which directly communicate information to visitors about the animals they are seeing and their place in the world. This was an area where zoos used to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"396709d8-09b2-4086-b5d1-c519deaf836e\" data-question=\"21\">be lacking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, but they are now increasingly sophisticated in their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02d18a0f-7959-46b6-907d-d08359d3472c\" data-question=\"21\">communication and outreach work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Many zoos also work directly to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53ae998c-20e3-40ff-9c7d-16593c1da09a\" data-question=\"24\">educate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8031cb83-e8f6-485b-b400-0f9404301688\" data-question=\"24\">conservation workers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in other countries, or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40b00710-dd31-48ce-94c2-5e139ef690a2\" data-question=\"23\">send their animal keepers abroad<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"360ae721-11cf-4064-8594-570df6b384cb\" data-question=\"23\">contribute their knowledge and skills to those working in zoos and reserves, thereby helping to improve conditions and reintroductions all over the world.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Zoos also play a key role in research. If we are to save wild species and restore and repair ecosystems we need to know about how key species live, act and react. Being able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a24794e-8e50-451c-93fc-3fe54c9abebd\" data-question=\"15\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"801783e5-fdb0-4e28-8450-b72f2cdaed95\" data-question=\"22\">undertake research on animals in zoos<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> where there is less risk and fewer variables means real changes can be effected on wild populations. Finding out about, for example, the oestrus cycle of an animal of its breeding rate helps us manage wild populations. Procedures such as capturing and moving at-risk or dangerous individuals are bolstered by knowledge gained in zoos about doses for anaesthetics, and by experience in handling and transporting animals. This can make a real difference to conservation efforts and to the reduction of human-animal conflicts, and can provide a knowledge base for helping with the increasing threats of habitat destruction and other problems.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>In conclusion, considering the many ongoing global threats to the environment, it is hard for me to see zoos as anything other than essential to the long-term survival of numerous species. They are vital not just in terms of protecting animals, but as a means of learning about them to aid those still in the wild, as well as educating and informing the general population about these animals and their world so that they can assist or at least accept <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"083f040d-09f2-4a8b-8fc1-591c6a691d2c\" data-question=\"25\">the need to be more environmentally conscious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Without them, the world would be, and would increasingly become, a much poorer place.</span></p><p><span> </span><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, <strong>A-F</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes<strong> 14-17</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"427\" id=\"question-wrapper-427\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df8bc8ae-69b5-4b5c-9efa-c2cbd8103a54\" data-question=\"14\">how quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> animal species can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b80f361b-9d69-4bbe-b653-730dd95fda2e\" data-question=\"14\">die out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"428\" id=\"question-wrapper-428\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reasons why it is preferable to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a24794e-8e50-451c-93fc-3fe54c9abebd\" data-question=\"15\">study animals in captivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> rather than in the wild </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"429\" id=\"question-wrapper-429\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db9abb4c-7290-4ae1-bc4e-3f5996892603\" data-question=\"16\">two ways of learning about animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> other than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"589ee4de-94f7-4d81-bd05-64893506da8f\" data-question=\"16\">visiting them in zoos<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"430\" id=\"question-wrapper-430\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eed7ca3-e5e5-4c09-bfe6-5d8db7d2fe7c\" data-question=\"17\">reasons why<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> animals in zoos may by healthier than those in the wild </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>18-22</strong> on you answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE </strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE </strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN </strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"431\" id=\"question-wrapper-431\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> An animal is likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aab99554-7d46-4eae-8efa-02348228c103\" data-question=\"18\">live longer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in a zoo than in the wild </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"432\" id=\"question-wrapper-432\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02823555-3dce-47a5-a717-e4fa330d1f3b\" data-question=\"19\">some species in zoos<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"29231f37-725a-4c8e-9ef2-b765c5f18c6e\" data-question=\"19\">can no longer be found in the wild<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"433\" id=\"question-wrapper-433\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Improvements in the quality of TV wildlife documentaries have resulted in increased numbers of zoo visitors. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"434\" id=\"question-wrapper-434\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Zoos have always <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"396709d8-09b2-4086-b5d1-c519deaf836e\" data-question=\"21\">excelled at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02d18a0f-7959-46b6-907d-d08359d3472c\" data-question=\"21\">transmitting information about animals to the public<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"435\" id=\"question-wrapper-435\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"801783e5-fdb0-4e28-8450-b72f2cdaed95\" data-question=\"22\">Studying animals in zoos<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> is less stressful for the animals than studying them in the wild. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><h3><span>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E.</strong></span></h3><p><span><em>Write the correct letters in boxes <strong>23</strong> and <strong>24</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span>Which <strong>TWO</strong> of the following are stated about zoo staff in the text?</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Some take part in television documentaries about animals</span></p><p><span><strong>B </strong> Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40b00710-dd31-48ce-94c2-5e139ef690a2\" data-question=\"23\">travel to overseas locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"360ae721-11cf-4064-8594-570df6b384cb\" data-question=\"23\">join teams in zoos<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> Some get experience with species in the wild before taking up zoo jobs.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53ae998c-20e3-40ff-9c7d-16593c1da09a\" data-question=\"24\">teach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8031cb83-e8f6-485b-b400-0f9404301688\" data-question=\"24\">people who are involved with conservation projects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> Some specialise in caring for species which are under threat.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"436\" id=\"question-wrapper-436\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"437\" id=\"question-wrapper-437\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E</strong></span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letters in boxes <strong>25</strong> and <strong>26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span>Which <strong>TWO</strong> of these beliefs about zoos does the writer mention in the text?</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> They can help children overcome their fears of wild animals.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> They can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"083f040d-09f2-4a8b-8fc1-591c6a691d2c\" data-question=\"25\">increase public awareness of environmental issues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> They can provide employment for a range of professional people.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> They can generate income to support wildlife conservation projects.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> They can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"485ada59-2eb5-4a88-a8e5-8eb44fd77b94\" data-question=\"26\">raise animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> which can later be released into the wild.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"438\" id=\"question-wrapper-438\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"439\" id=\"question-wrapper-439\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"3eed7ca3-e5e5-4c09-bfe6-5d8db7d2fe7c","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"reasons why","passagePhrase":"get a varied and high-quality diet ... illnesses they might have will be treated"},{"uid":"aab99554-7d46-4eae-8efa-02348228c103","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"live longer","passagePhrase":"have a greater life expectancy"},{"uid":"df8bc8ae-69b5-4b5c-9efa-c2cbd8103a54","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"how quickly","passagePhrase":"Colossal numbers of species ... are increasingly threatened"},{"uid":"b80f361b-9d69-4bbe-b653-730dd95fda2e","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"die out","passagePhrase":"are becoming extinct"},{"uid":"485ada59-2eb5-4a88-a8e5-8eb44fd77b94","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"raise animals","passagePhrase":"can be bred up to"},{"uid":"29231f37-725a-4c8e-9ef2-b765c5f18c6e","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"can no longer be found in the wild","passagePhrase":"only exist in captivity"},{"uid":"02823555-3dce-47a5-a717-e4fa330d1f3b","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"some species in zoos","passagePhrase":"many of these living in zoos"},{"uid":"db9abb4c-7290-4ae1-bc4e-3f5996892603","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"two ways of learning about animals","passagePhrase":"television documentaries ... natural history specimens"},{"uid":"589ee4de-94f7-4d81-bd05-64893506da8f","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"visiting them in zoos","passagePhrase":"seeing a living creature in the flesh, hearing it, smelling it, watching what it does"},{"uid":"02d18a0f-7959-46b6-907d-d08359d3472c","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"transmitting information about animals to the public","passagePhrase":"communication and outreach work"},{"uid":"53ae998c-20e3-40ff-9c7d-16593c1da09a","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"teach","passagePhrase":"educate"},{"uid":"8031cb83-e8f6-485b-b400-0f9404301688","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"people who are involved with conservation projects","passagePhrase":"conservation workers"},{"uid":"40b00710-dd31-48ce-94c2-5e139ef690a2","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"travel to overseas locations","passagePhrase":"send their animal keepers abroad"},{"uid":"360ae721-11cf-4064-8594-570df6b384cb","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"join teams in zoos","passagePhrase":"contribute their knowledge and skills to those working in zoos and reserves, thereby helping to improve conditions and reintroductions all over the world."},{"uid":"2a24794e-8e50-451c-93fc-3fe54c9abebd","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"study animals in captivity","passagePhrase":"undertake research on animals in zoos"},{"uid":"801783e5-fdb0-4e28-8450-b72f2cdaed95","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Studying animals in zoos","passagePhrase":"undertake research on animals in zoos"},{"uid":"083f040d-09f2-4a8b-8fc1-591c6a691d2c","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"increase public awareness of environmental issues","passagePhrase":"the need to be more environmentally conscious"}]},"reading_u2_246":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</p><h2>How Bad Is Ocean Garbage, Really?</h2><p>Chelsea Rochman, an ecologist at the University of California, Davis, has been trying to answer a dismal question: Is everything terrible, or are things just very, very bad?</p><p>Rochman is a member of the National Center for Ecological Analysis and Synthesis’s marine-debris working group, a collection of scientists who study, among other things, the growing problem of marine debris, also known as ocean trash. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"6d2107c5-697f-4a75-a57b-2dadc33efb8d\" data-question=\"27\">Plenty of studies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> have sounded alarm bells about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdcd00e7-574d-44d6-8083-e9ef8afabe30\" data-question=\"27\">the state of marine debris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>; in a recent paper published in the journal <em>Ecology</em>, Rochman and her colleagues set out to determine how many of those perceived risks are real.</p><p>Often, Rochman says, scientists will end a paper by speculating about the broader impacts of what they’ve found. For example, a study could show that certain seabirds eat plastic bags, and go on to warn that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b993f59d-8a66-4f7f-bb61-a57e8fd7e3be\" data-question=\"29\">whole bird populations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64c9b91b-8a38-453e-8823-3bc9696439a8\" data-question=\"29\">at risk of dying out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. ‘But the truth was that nobody had yet tested those perceived threats,’ Rochman says. ‘There wasn’t a lot of information.’</p><p>Rochman and her colleagues <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a86d05cd-62d0-4cb9-8888-503f6307bfcc\" data-question=\"30\">examined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> more than a hundred papers on the impacts of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a7db2f3-cf12-4f1f-aabd-de1951d161da\" data-question=\"30\">marine debris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that were published through 2013. Within each paper, they asked what threats scientists had studied – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15bf087d-53fa-42f2-bc5b-1d8841e92165\" data-question=\"30\">366 perceived threats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> in all – and what they’d actually found.</p><p>In 83 percent of cases, the perceived dangers of ocean trash were proven true. In the remaining cases, the working group found the studies had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7d9b378-9d71-465e-9450-40d86bd6b9d1\" data-question=\"31\">weaknesses in design<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> and content which affected the validity of their conclusions – they lacked a control group, for example, or used faulty statistics.</p><p>Strikingly, Rochman says, only one well-designed study <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ab43786f-7487-48c7-9df3-4e714b951e8c\" data-question=\"32\">failed to find<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the effect it was looking for, an investigation of mussels ingesting microscopic bits. The plastic moved from the mussels’ stomachs to their bloodstreams, scientists found, and stayed there for weeks – but didn’t seem to stress out the shellfish.</p><p>While mussels may be fine eating trash, though, the analysis also gave a clearer picture of the many ways that ocean debris <em>is</em> bothersome.</p><p>Within the studies they looked at, most of the proven threats came from plastic debris, rather than other materials like metal or wood. Most of the dangers also involved large <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87463a30-5b60-4492-816e-2ed5fe3fcbb1\" data-question=\"34\">pieces of debris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> – animals getting entangled in trash, for example, or eating it and severely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e542d1a2-a551-4578-a82e-23ca07bdd16e\" data-question=\"34\">injuring themselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</p><p>But a lot of ocean debris is ‘microplastic’, or pieces smaller than five millimeters. These may be ingredients used in cosmetics and toiletries, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd7e022f-cfd8-4b33-8877-522fee910e38\" data-question=\"35\">fibers shed by synthetic clothing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> in the wash, or eroded remnants of larger debris. Compared to the number of studies investigating large-scale debris, Rochman’s group <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06bc3c68-f676-4b6e-bb5c-3913dc9f86e4\" data-question=\"35\">found little research on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the effects of these tiny bits. ‘There are a lot of open questions still for microplastic,’ Rochman says, though she notes that more papers on the subject have been published since 2013, the cutoff point for the group’s analysis.</p><p>There are also, she adds, a lot of open questions about the ways that ocean debris can lead to sea-creature death. Many studies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d49a3756-7d52-4422-b8f9-86da11acebdc\" data-question=\"36\">have looked at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> how plastic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"083eae90-f5b2-44d8-a405-915905bc0ca0\" data-question=\"38\">affects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> an individual animal, or that animal’s tissues or cells, rather than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0165a47-c3a4-4882-b11d-7b5f84f15a91\" data-question=\"36\">whole<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> populations. And in the lab, scientists often use higher concentrations of plastic than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90df0b4a-ecf3-48ed-adee-ccbd0b4ee949\" data-question=\"37\">what’s really in the ocean<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"60909749-bdf2-4ffc-9f02-aa1a35f7e30e\" data-question=\"38\">None of that tells us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0685b3d7-7c50-42ad-8d78-b4396a0f3562\" data-question=\"38\">how many birds or fish or sea turtles could die from plastic pollution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> – or how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26e004cb-196c-4972-bab3-b3e53a52381c\" data-question=\"38\">deaths in one species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> could affect that animal’s predators, or the rest of the ecosystem.</p><p>‘We <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"febec88b-fa3d-4711-999b-739942e25e89\" data-question=\"39\">need to be asking more ecologically relevant questions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>,’ Rochman says. Usually, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"febec88b-fa3d-4711-999b-739942e25e89\" data-question=\"39\">scientists don’t know exactly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> how disasters <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b005e33-94d4-45e5-a1e0-87bb8f04bfca\" data-question=\"39\">such as a tanker accidentally spilling its whole cargo of oil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> and polluting huge areas of the ocean will affect the environment until after they’ve happened. ‘We don’t ask the right questions early enough,’ she says. But if ecologists can understand how the slow-moving effect of ocean trash is damaging ecosystems, they might be able to prevent things from getting worse.</p><p>Asking the right questions can help policy makers, and the public, figure out where to focus their attention. The problems that look or sound most dramatic may not be the best places to start. For example, the name of the ‘Great Pacific Garbage Patch’ – a collection of marine debris in the northern Pacific Ocean – might conjure up a vast, floating trash island. In reality though, much of the debris is tiny or below the surface; a person could sail through the area without seeing any trash at all. A Dutch group called ‘The Ocean Cleanup’ is currently working on plans to put mechanical devices in the Pacific Garbage Patch and similar areas to suck up plastic. But a recent paper used simulations to show that strategically positioning the cleanup devices closer to shore would more effectively reduce pollution over the long term.</p><p>‘I think clearing up some of these misperceptions is really important,’ Rochman says. Among scientists as well as in the media, she says, ‘A lot of the images about strandings and entanglement and all of that cause the perception that plastic debris is killing everything in the ocean.’ Interrogating the existing scientific literature can help ecologists figure out which problems really need addressing, and which ones they’d be better off – like the mussels – absorbing and ignoring.</p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>In boxes <strong>27-33</strong> on you answer sheet, write</span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"440\" id=\"question-wrapper-440\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Rochman and her colleagues <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"6d2107c5-697f-4a75-a57b-2dadc33efb8d\" data-question=\"27\">were the first people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to research <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdcd00e7-574d-44d6-8083-e9ef8afabe30\" data-question=\"27\">the problem of marine debris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"441\" id=\"question-wrapper-441\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The creatures most in danger from ocean trash are certain seabirds. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"442\" id=\"question-wrapper-442\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The studies Rochman has reviewed have already proved that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b993f59d-8a66-4f7f-bb61-a57e8fd7e3be\" data-question=\"29\">populations of some birds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64c9b91b-8a38-453e-8823-3bc9696439a8\" data-question=\"29\">will soon become extinct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"443\" id=\"question-wrapper-443\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Rochman <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a86d05cd-62d0-4cb9-8888-503f6307bfcc\" data-question=\"30\">analysed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> papers on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15bf087d-53fa-42f2-bc5b-1d8841e92165\" data-question=\"30\">different kinds of danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> caused by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a7db2f3-cf12-4f1f-aabd-de1951d161da\" data-question=\"30\">ocean trash<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"444\" id=\"question-wrapper-444\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34c676b0-67ba-4184-8a2b-89fe321d8a9a\" data-question=\"31\">Most of the research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> analysed by Rochman and her colleagues <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7d9b378-9d71-465e-9450-40d86bd6b9d1\" data-question=\"31\">was badly designed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"445\" id=\"question-wrapper-445\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One study examined by Rochman <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ab43786f-7487-48c7-9df3-4e714b951e8c\" data-question=\"32\">was expecting to find<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> that mussels were harmed by eating plastic. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"446\" id=\"question-wrapper-446\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some mussels choose to eat plastic in preference to their natural diet. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose<strong> ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>34-39</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h3><span><strong>Findings related to marine debris</strong></span></h3><p><span><strong>Studies of marine debris found the biggest threats were</strong></span></p><p><span><span>• </span> plastic (not metal or wood)</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87463a30-5b60-4492-816e-2ed5fe3fcbb1\" data-question=\"34\">bits of debris<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> that were <strong>34</strong>………………………….. (<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e542d1a2-a551-4578-a82e-23ca07bdd16e\" data-question=\"34\">harmful to animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>)</span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06bc3c68-f676-4b6e-bb5c-3913dc9f86e4\" data-question=\"35\">There was little research into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <strong>35</strong>…………………………. e.g. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd7e022f-cfd8-4b33-8877-522fee910e38\" data-question=\"35\">from synthetic fibres<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>Drawbacks of the studies examined</strong></span></p><p><span><span>•</span> most of them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d49a3756-7d52-4422-b8f9-86da11acebdc\" data-question=\"36\">focused on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> individual animals, not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0165a47-c3a4-4882-b11d-7b5f84f15a91\" data-question=\"36\">entire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> 36 ………………………..</span></p><p><span><span>•</span> the <strong>37</strong>…………………….. of plastic used in the lab did not always reflect <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90df0b4a-ecf3-48ed-adee-ccbd0b4ee949\" data-question=\"37\">those in the ocean<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></span></p><p><span><span>•</span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"60909749-bdf2-4ffc-9f02-aa1a35f7e30e\" data-question=\"38\">there was insufficient information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> on</span></p><p><span>– <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0685b3d7-7c50-42ad-8d78-b4396a0f3562\" data-question=\"38\">numbers of animals which could be affected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span></span></p><p><span>– <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"083eae90-f5b2-44d8-a405-915905bc0ca0\" data-question=\"38\">the impact of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26e004cb-196c-4972-bab3-b3e53a52381c\" data-question=\"38\">reduction in numbers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> on the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <strong>38</strong>……………………….. of that species</span></p><p><span>– the impact on the ecosystem</span></p><p><span>Rochman says <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"febec88b-fa3d-4711-999b-739942e25e89\" data-question=\"39\">more information is needed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> on the possible impact of future <strong>39</strong>………………………… (<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b005e33-94d4-45e5-a1e0-87bb8f04bfca\" data-question=\"39\">e.g. involving oil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>).</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"447\" id=\"question-wrapper-447\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LARGE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"448\" id=\"question-wrapper-448\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MICROPLASTIC</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"449\" id=\"question-wrapper-449\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POPULATIONS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"450\" id=\"question-wrapper-450\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CONCENTRATIONS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"451\" id=\"question-wrapper-451\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PREDATORS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"452\" id=\"question-wrapper-452\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DISASTERS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in box <strong>40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"453\" id=\"question-wrapper-453\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What would be the best title for this passage? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Assessing the threat of marine debris</li> <li>B. Marine debris: who is to blame?</li> <li>C. A new solution to the problem of marine debris</li> <li>D. Marine debris: the need for international action</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"cdcd00e7-574d-44d6-8083-e9ef8afabe30","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"the problem of marine debris","passagePhrase":"the state of marine debris"},{"uid":"b993f59d-8a66-4f7f-bb61-a57e8fd7e3be","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"populations of some birds","passagePhrase":"whole bird populations"},{"uid":"64c9b91b-8a38-453e-8823-3bc9696439a8","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"will soon become extinct","passagePhrase":"at risk of dying out"},{"uid":"a86d05cd-62d0-4cb9-8888-503f6307bfcc","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"analysed","passagePhrase":"examined"},{"uid":"8a7db2f3-cf12-4f1f-aabd-de1951d161da","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"ocean trash","passagePhrase":"marine debris"},{"uid":"15bf087d-53fa-42f2-bc5b-1d8841e92165","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"different kinds of danger","passagePhrase":"366 perceived threats"},{"uid":"b7d9b378-9d71-465e-9450-40d86bd6b9d1","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"was badly designed","passagePhrase":"weaknesses in design"},{"uid":"87463a30-5b60-4492-816e-2ed5fe3fcbb1","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"bits of debris","passagePhrase":"pieces of debris"},{"uid":"e542d1a2-a551-4578-a82e-23ca07bdd16e","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"harmful to animals","passagePhrase":"injuring themselves"},{"uid":"cd7e022f-cfd8-4b33-8877-522fee910e38","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"from synthetic fibres","passagePhrase":"fibers shed by synthetic clothing"},{"uid":"06bc3c68-f676-4b6e-bb5c-3913dc9f86e4","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"There was little research into","passagePhrase":"found little research on"},{"uid":"d49a3756-7d52-4422-b8f9-86da11acebdc","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"focused on","passagePhrase":"have looked at"},{"uid":"083eae90-f5b2-44d8-a405-915905bc0ca0","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"the impact of a reduction in numbers on the","passagePhrase":"affects"},{"uid":"f0165a47-c3a4-4882-b11d-7b5f84f15a91","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"entire","passagePhrase":"whole"},{"uid":"90df0b4a-ecf3-48ed-adee-ccbd0b4ee949","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"those in the ocean","passagePhrase":"what’s really in the ocean"},{"uid":"60909749-bdf2-4ffc-9f02-aa1a35f7e30e","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"there was insufficient information","passagePhrase":"None of that tells us"},{"uid":"0685b3d7-7c50-42ad-8d78-b4396a0f3562","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"numbers of animals which could be affected","passagePhrase":"how many birds or fish or sea turtles could die from plastic pollution"},{"uid":"26e004cb-196c-4972-bab3-b3e53a52381c","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"reduction in numbers","passagePhrase":"deaths in one species"},{"uid":"febec88b-fa3d-4711-999b-739942e25e89","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"more information is needed","passagePhrase":"need to be asking more ecologically relevant questions ... scientists don’t know exactly"},{"uid":"3b005e33-94d4-45e5-a1e0-87bb8f04bfca","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"e.g. involving oil","passagePhrase":"such as a tanker accidentally spilling its whole cargo of oil"},{"uid":"34c676b0-67ba-4184-8a2b-89fe321d8a9a","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Most of the research","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_247":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong>Nutmeg – a valuable spice</strong></span></h2><p><span>The nutmeg tree, <em>Myristica fragrans</em>, is a large evergreen tree native to Southeast Asia. Until the late 18th century, it only grew in one place in the world: a small group of islands in the Banda Sea, part of the Moluccas – or Spice Islands – in northeastern Indonesia. The tree is thickly branched with dense <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70ef0f9c-994f-4311-b044-f2ec05cafa1c\" data-question=\"1\">foliage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of tough, dark green oval leaves, and produces small, yellow, bell-shaped flowers and pale yellow pear-shaped fruits. The fruit is encased in a flesh husk. When the fruit is ripe, this husk splits into two halves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fc89ff09-a456-4821-bc5d-190984bb033b\" data-question=\"2\">along a ridge running the length of the fruit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Inside is a purple-brown shiny seed, 2-3 cm long by about 2 cm across, surrounded by a lacy red or crimson covering called an ‘aril’. These are the sources of the two spices nutmeg and mace, the former <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b51eae77-d0f6-48ce-980d-47e194f726e1\" data-question=\"3\">being produced from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> the dried seed and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83ba1739-4912-4cb4-b2a8-f0bf6445a77c\" data-question=\"4\">the latter from the aril<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Nutmeg was a highly prized and costly ingredient in European cuisine in the Middle Ages, and was used as a flavouring, medicinal, and preservative agent. Throughout this period, the Arabs were the exclusive <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d89d3c78-c98e-4c74-8b21-c5b83b907cbb\" data-question=\"8\">importers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of the spice to Europe. They sold nutmeg for high prices to merchants based in Venice, but they <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8e5c1409-1bed-4787-b55d-765833a15ad3\" data-question=\"5\">never revealed the exact location<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of the source of this extremely valuable commodity. The Arab-Venetian dominance of the trade finally ended in 1512, when the Portuguese reached the Banda Islands and began exploiting its precious resources.</span></p><p><span>Always in danger of competition from neighbouring Spain, the Portuguese began subcontracting their spice distribution to Dutch traders. Profits began to flow into the Netherlands, and the Dutch commercial fleet swiftly grew into one of the largest in the world. The Dutch quietly gained control of most of the shipping and trading of spices in Northern Europe. Then, in 1580, Portugal fell under Spanish rule, and by the end of the 16th century the Dutch found themselves locked out of the market. As prices for pepper, nutmeg, and other spices soared across Europe, they decided to fight back.</span></p><p><span>In 1602, Dutch merchants founded the VOC, a trading corporation better known as the Dutch East India Company. By 1617, the VOC was the richest commercial operation in the world. The company had 50,000 employees worldwide, with a private army of 30,000 men and a fleet of 200 ships. At the same time, thousands of people across Europe were dying of the plague, a highly contagious and deadly disease. Doctors were desperate for a way to stop the spread of this disease, and they decided nutmeg <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7d1da84-b6a3-48c7-a27e-5589910af7a5\" data-question=\"9\">held the cure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Everybody wanted nutmeg, and many were willing to spare no expense to have it. Nutmeg bought for a few pennies in Indonesia could be sold for 68,000 times its original cost on the streets of London. The only problem was the short supply. And that’s where the Dutch found their opportunity.</span></p><p><span>The Banda Islands were ruled by local sultans who insisted on maintaining a neutral trading policy towards foreign powers. This allowed them to avoid the presence of Portuguese or Spanish troops on their soil, but it also left them unprotected from other invaders. In 1621, the Dutch arrived and took over. Once securely in control of the Bandas, the Dutch went to work protecting their new investment. They concentrated all nutmeg production into a few easily guarded areas, uprooting and destroying any trees outside the plantation zones. Anyone caught growing a nutmeg seedling or carrying seeds without the proper authority was severely punished. In addition, all exported nutmeg was covered with lime to make sure there was no chance <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4bc52387-b737-4d3b-afee-f1b0939e43ea\" data-question=\"10\">a fertile seed which could be grown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> elsewhere would leave the islands. There was only one obstacle to Dutch domination. One of the Banda Islands, a sliver of land called Run, only 3 km long by less than 1 km wide, was under the control of the British. After decades of fighting for control of this tiny island, the Dutch and British arrived at a compromise settlement, the Treaty of Breda, in 1667. Intent on securing their hold over every nutmeg-producing island, the Dutch <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53ff98ad-0e1b-4ca1-a30a-fbca79edcc6f\" data-question=\"11\">offered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a trade: if the British would give them the island of Run, they would in turn give Britain a distant and much less valuable island in North America. The British agreed. That other island was Manhattan, which is how New Amsterdam became New York. The Dutch now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6704c914-c28d-4228-a2fd-60960b9c2b63\" data-question=\"7\">had a monopoly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> over the nutmeg trade which would last for another century.</span></p><p><span>Then, in 1770, a Frenchman named Pierre Poivre successfully <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8419a096-2747-499b-80d4-82dcfe50186f\" data-question=\"12\">smuggled nutmeg plants to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> safety in Mauritius, an island off the coast of Africa. Some of these were later exported to the Caribbean where they thrived, especially on the island of Grenada. Next, in 1778, a volcanic eruption in the Banda region caused a tsunami that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79865920-6341-4c19-bc4c-6086c48d0add\" data-question=\"13\">wiped out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> half the nutmeg groves. Finally, in 1809, the British returned to Indonesia and seized the Banda Islands by force. They returned the islands to the Dutch in 1817, but not before transplanting hundreds of nutmeg seedlings to plantations in several locations across southern Asia. The Dutch nutmeg monopoly was over.</span></p><p><span>Today, nutmeg is grown in Indonesia, the Caribbean, India, Malaysia, Papua New Guinea and Sri Lanka, and world nutmeg production is estimated to average between 10,000 and 12,000 tonnes per year.</span></p><p><span> </span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>1-8</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>The nutmeg tree and fruit</strong></span></h4><p><span>● the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70ef0f9c-994f-4311-b044-f2ec05cafa1c\" data-question=\"1\">leaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of the tree are <strong>1</strong>……………………. in shape</span></p><p><span>● the <strong>2</strong>……………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fc89ff09-a456-4821-bc5d-190984bb033b\" data-question=\"2\">surrounds the fruit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and breaks open when the fruit is ripe</span></p><p><span>● the <strong>3</strong>……………………. is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b51eae77-d0f6-48ce-980d-47e194f726e1\" data-question=\"3\">used to produce the spice nutmeg<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span></span></p><p><span>● the covering known as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83ba1739-4912-4cb4-b2a8-f0bf6445a77c\" data-question=\"4\">the aril is used to produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <strong>4</strong>……………………..</span></p><p><span>● the tree has yellow flowers and fruit</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"141\" id=\"question-wrapper-141\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OVAL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"142\" id=\"question-wrapper-142\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HUSK</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"143\" id=\"question-wrapper-143\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SEED</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"144\" id=\"question-wrapper-144\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MACE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>5-7</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145\" id=\"question-wrapper-145\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the Middle Ages, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8e5c1409-1bed-4787-b55d-765833a15ad3\" data-question=\"5\">most Europeans knew<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> where nutmeg was grown. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"146\" id=\"question-wrapper-146\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The VOC was the world’s first major trading company. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"147\" id=\"question-wrapper-147\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Following the Treaty of Breda, the Dutch <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6704c914-c28d-4228-a2fd-60960b9c2b63\" data-question=\"7\">had control of all<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the islands where nutmeg grew. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the table below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>8-13</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><table><tbody><tr><td width=\"132\"><p><span>Middle Ages</span></p></td><td width=\"414\"><p><span>Nutmeg was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d89d3c78-c98e-4c74-8b21-c5b83b907cbb\" data-question=\"8\">brought to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> Europe by the <strong>8<span>……………</span></strong></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"132\"><p><span>16th century</span></p></td><td width=\"414\"><p><span>European nations took control of the nutmeg trade</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"132\"><p><span>17th century</span></p></td><td width=\"414\"><p><span>Demand for nutmeg grew, as it was believed to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7d1da84-b6a3-48c7-a27e-5589910af7a5\" data-question=\"9\">effective against the disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> known as the <strong>9<span>……………</span></strong></span></p><p><span>The Dutch</span></p><p><span>– took control of the Banda Islands</span></p><p><span>– restricted nutmeg production to a few areas</span></p><p><span>– put <strong>10<span>……………</span></strong> on nutmeg to avoid it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4bc52387-b737-4d3b-afee-f1b0939e43ea\" data-question=\"10\">being cultivated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> outside the islands</span></p><p><span>– finally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53ff98ad-0e1b-4ca1-a30a-fbca79edcc6f\" data-question=\"11\">obtained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the island of <strong>11<span>……………</span></strong> from the British</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"132\"><p><span>Late 18th century</span></p></td><td width=\"414\"><p><span>1770 – nutmeg plants were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8419a096-2747-499b-80d4-82dcfe50186f\" data-question=\"12\">secretly taken to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <strong>12<span>……………</span></strong></span></p><p><span>1778 – half the Banda Islands’ nutmeg plantations were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79865920-6341-4c19-bc4c-6086c48d0add\" data-question=\"13\">destroyed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> by a <strong>13</strong>……………</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"148\" id=\"question-wrapper-148\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ARABS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"149\" id=\"question-wrapper-149\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PLAGUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"150\" id=\"question-wrapper-150\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LIME</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"151\" id=\"question-wrapper-151\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RUN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"152\" id=\"question-wrapper-152\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MAURITIUS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"153\" id=\"question-wrapper-153\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TSUNAMI</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"70ef0f9c-994f-4311-b044-f2ec05cafa1c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"leaves","passagePhrase":"foliage"},{"uid":"fc89ff09-a456-4821-bc5d-190984bb033b","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"surrounds the fruit","passagePhrase":"along a ridge running the length of the fruit"},{"uid":"b51eae77-d0f6-48ce-980d-47e194f726e1","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"used to produce the spice nutmeg","passagePhrase":"being produced from"},{"uid":"83ba1739-4912-4cb4-b2a8-f0bf6445a77c","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"the aril is used to produce","passagePhrase":"the latter from the aril"},{"uid":"d89d3c78-c98e-4c74-8b21-c5b83b907cbb","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"brought to","passagePhrase":"importers"},{"uid":"f7d1da84-b6a3-48c7-a27e-5589910af7a5","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"effective against the disease","passagePhrase":"held the cure"},{"uid":"4bc52387-b737-4d3b-afee-f1b0939e43ea","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"being cultivated","passagePhrase":"a fertile seed which could be grown"},{"uid":"53ff98ad-0e1b-4ca1-a30a-fbca79edcc6f","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"obtained","passagePhrase":"offered"},{"uid":"6704c914-c28d-4228-a2fd-60960b9c2b63","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"had control of all","passagePhrase":"had a monopoly"},{"uid":"8419a096-2747-499b-80d4-82dcfe50186f","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"secretly taken to","passagePhrase":"smuggled nutmeg plants to"},{"uid":"79865920-6341-4c19-bc4c-6086c48d0add","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"destroyed","passagePhrase":"wiped out"}]},"reading_u2_248":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Driverless cars</strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>The automotive sector is well used to adapting to automation in manufacturing. The implementation of robotic car manufacture from the 1970s onwards led to significant cost savings and improvements in the reliability and flexibility of vehicle mass production. A new challenge to vehicle production is now on the horizon and, again, it comes from automation. However, this time it is not to do with the manufacturing process, but with the vehicles themselves.</span></p><p><span>Research projects on vehicle automation are not new. Vehicles with limited self-driving capabilities have been around for more than 50 years, resulting in significant contributions towards driver assistance systems. But since Google announced in 2010 that it had been trialling self-driving cars on the streets of California, progress in this field has quickly gathered pace.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>There are many reasons why technology is advancing so fast. One frequently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0bb776f-2ccb-4092-9fe4-8b9cb9263545\" data-question=\"15\">cited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> motive is safety; indeed, research at the UK’s Transport Research Laboratory has demonstrated that more than 90 percent of road collisions involve human error as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af400ec2-8c68-4e77-be21-c3258a7ebdd6\" data-question=\"19\">a contributory factor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, and it is the primary cause in the vast majority. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"000b8430-00aa-4ec1-90ca-fc80ee1cdc2b\" data-question=\"15\">Automation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> may help to reduce the incidence of this.</span></p><p><span>Another aim is to free the time people spend driving for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa556b73-f015-47de-8673-e0a56f669733\" data-question=\"23\">other purposes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. If the vehicle can do some or all of the driving, it may be possible to be productive, to socialise or simply to relax while automation systems have responsibility for safe control of the vehicle. If the vehicle can do the driving, those who are challenged by existing mobility models – such as older or disabled travellers – may be able to enjoy significantly greater <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"81b4ce06-07be-40ba-b0d9-14fd52544226\" data-question=\"24\">travel autonomy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Beyond these direct benefits, we can consider the wider implications for transport and society, and how manufacturing processes might need to respond as a result. At present, the average car spends more than 90 percent of its life <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"05464c3d-2750-41c9-85e9-77a396779f86\" data-question=\"14\">parked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. Automation means that initiatives for car-sharing become much more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4db2402-c110-45fe-9f75-2ca965ec8ddd\" data-question=\"20\">viable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, particularly in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe978dfc-6590-4a18-bf65-7c09ecd33d3d\" data-question=\"20\">urban areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> with significant travel demand. If a significant proportion of the population choose to use shared automated vehicles, mobility demand can be met by far fewer vehicles.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>The Massachusetts Institute of Technology investigated automated mobility in Singapore, finding that fewer than 30 percent of the vehicles currently used would be required if fully automated car sharing could be implemented. If this is the case, it might mean that we need to manufacture far fewer vehicles to meet demand. However, the number of trips being taken would probably increase, partly because empty vehicles would have to be moved from one customer to the next.</span></p><p><span>Modelling work by the University of Michigan Transportation Research Institute suggests automated vehicles might <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"220ae18c-4bc3-47df-b5c8-0a8c12edbce4\" data-question=\"21\">reduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> vehicle ownership by 43 percent, but that vehicles’ average <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"19779b93-5bb9-4a71-9104-8c1d9be36fd8\" data-question=\"22\">annual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> mileage <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3ada17a-0928-4fa3-87f1-bd2a5714a4d6\" data-question=\"22\">double<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> as a result. As a consequence, each vehicle would be used more intensively, and might need replacing sooner. This faster rate of turnover may mean that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b90af0df-747a-42ea-ad0a-98e80ab5c972\" data-question=\"18\">vehicle production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> will not necessarily decrease</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Automation may prompt other changes in vehicle manufacture. If we move to a model where consumers are tending not to own a single vehicle but to purchase access to a range of vehicle through a mobility provider, drivers will have the freedom to select one that best suits their needs for a particular journey, rather than making a compromise across all their requirements.</span></p><p><span>Since, for most of the time, most of the seats in most cars are unoccupied, this may boost production of a smaller, more efficient range of vehicles that suit the needs of individuals. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a544f03-b6a6-4e34-911c-f20dc94b7969\" data-question=\"16\">Specialised vehicles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> may then be available for exceptional journeys, such as going on a family camping trip or helping a son or daughter move to university.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>There are a number of hurdles to overcome in delivering automated vehicles to our roads. These include the technical difficulties in ensuring that the vehicle works reliably in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f0f1153-e8ef-4b59-ac17-ca7297cd858e\" data-question=\"25\">infinite range of traffic, weather and road situations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> it might encounter; the regulatory challenges in understanding how liability and enforcement might change when drivers are no longer essential for vehicle operation; and the societal changes that may be required for communities to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"85699e74-d75b-4833-866a-ce4ada64c2f6\" data-question=\"26\">trust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"85699e74-d75b-4833-866a-ce4ada64c2f6\" data-question=\"26\">accept<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> automated vehicles as being a valuable part of the mobility landscape.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>It’s clear that there are many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56623a64-8803-4c75-9606-4f20975fd232\" data-question=\"17\">challenges that need to be addressed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> but, through robust and targeted research, these can most probably be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56623a64-8803-4c75-9606-4f20975fd232\" data-question=\"17\">conquered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> within the next 10 years. Mobility will change in such potentially significant ways and in association with so many other technological developments, such as telepresence and virtual reality, that it is hard to make concrete predictions about the future. However, one thing is certain: change is coming, and the need to be flexible in response to this will be vital for those involved in manufacturing the vehicles that will deliver future mobility.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which section contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-18</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"154\" id=\"question-wrapper-154\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to the amount of time when a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"05464c3d-2750-41c9-85e9-77a396779f86\" data-question=\"14\">car is not in use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"155\" id=\"question-wrapper-155\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0bb776f-2ccb-4092-9fe4-8b9cb9263545\" data-question=\"15\">mention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of several advantages of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"000b8430-00aa-4ec1-90ca-fc80ee1cdc2b\" data-question=\"15\">driverless<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> vehicles for individual road-users </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"156\" id=\"question-wrapper-156\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to the opportunity of choosing the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a544f03-b6a6-4e34-911c-f20dc94b7969\" data-question=\"16\">most appropriate vehicle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> for each trip </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"157\" id=\"question-wrapper-157\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an estimate of how long it will take to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56623a64-8803-4c75-9606-4f20975fd232\" data-question=\"17\">overcome a number of problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"158\" id=\"question-wrapper-158\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a suggestion that the use of driverless cars may have no effect on the number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b90af0df-747a-42ea-ad0a-98e80ab5c972\" data-question=\"18\">vehicles manufactured<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>19-22</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>The impact of driverless cars</strong></span></h4><p><span>Figures from the Transport Research Laboratory indicate that most motor accidents are partly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af400ec2-8c68-4e77-be21-c3258a7ebdd6\" data-question=\"19\">due to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <strong>19</strong>……………………., so the introduction of driverless vehicles will result in greater safety. In addition to the direct benefits of automation, it may bring other advantages. For example, schemes for <strong>20</strong>………………………. will be more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4db2402-c110-45fe-9f75-2ca965ec8ddd\" data-question=\"20\">workable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, especially in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe978dfc-6590-4a18-bf65-7c09ecd33d3d\" data-question=\"20\">towns and cities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, resulting in fewer cars on the road.</span></p><p><span>According to the University of Michigan Transportation Research Institute, there could be a 43 percent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"220ae18c-4bc3-47df-b5c8-0a8c12edbce4\" data-question=\"21\">drop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in <strong>21</strong>…………………….. of cars. However, this would mean that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"19779b93-5bb9-4a71-9104-8c1d9be36fd8\" data-question=\"22\">yearly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <strong>22</strong>…………………….. of each car would, on average, be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3ada17a-0928-4fa3-87f1-bd2a5714a4d6\" data-question=\"22\">twice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> as high as it currently is. this would lead to a higher turnover of vehicles, and therefore no reduction in automotive manufacturing.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"159\" id=\"question-wrapper-159\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HUMAN ERROR</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"160\" id=\"question-wrapper-160\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CAR(-)SHARING</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"161\" id=\"question-wrapper-161\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OWNERSHIP</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"162\" id=\"question-wrapper-162\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MILEAGE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letters in boxes <strong>23</strong> and <strong>24</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span>Which <strong>TWO</strong> benefits of automated vehicles does the writer mention?</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Car travellers could enjoy considerable cost savings.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> It would be easier to find parking spaces in urban areas.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> Travellers could spend journeys <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa556b73-f015-47de-8673-e0a56f669733\" data-question=\"23\">doing something other than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> driving.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> People who find driving physically difficult could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"81b4ce06-07be-40ba-b0d9-14fd52544226\" data-question=\"24\">travel independently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><span><strong>E </strong> A reduction in the number of cars would mean a reduction in pollution.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"163\" id=\"question-wrapper-163\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"164\" id=\"question-wrapper-164\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letters in boxes <strong>25</strong> and <strong>26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span>Which <strong>TWO</strong> challenges to automated vehicle development does the writer mention?</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> making sure the general public has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"85699e74-d75b-4833-866a-ce4ada64c2f6\" data-question=\"26\">confidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> in automated vehicles</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> managing the pace of transition from conventional to automated vehicles</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> deciding how to compensate professional drivers who become redundant</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> setting up the infrastructure to make roads suitable for automated vehicles</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> getting automated vehicles to adapt to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f0f1153-e8ef-4b59-ac17-ca7297cd858e\" data-question=\"25\">various different driving conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"165\" id=\"question-wrapper-165\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"166\" id=\"question-wrapper-166\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a0bb776f-2ccb-4092-9fe4-8b9cb9263545","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"mention","passagePhrase":"cited"},{"uid":"af400ec2-8c68-4e77-be21-c3258a7ebdd6","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"due to","passagePhrase":"a contributory factor"},{"uid":"000b8430-00aa-4ec1-90ca-fc80ee1cdc2b","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"driverless","passagePhrase":"Automation"},{"uid":"aa556b73-f015-47de-8673-e0a56f669733","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"doing something other than","passagePhrase":"other purposes"},{"uid":"81b4ce06-07be-40ba-b0d9-14fd52544226","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"travel independently","passagePhrase":"travel autonomy"},{"uid":"05464c3d-2750-41c9-85e9-77a396779f86","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"car is not in use","passagePhrase":"parked"},{"uid":"b4db2402-c110-45fe-9f75-2ca965ec8ddd","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"workable","passagePhrase":"viable"},{"uid":"fe978dfc-6590-4a18-bf65-7c09ecd33d3d","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"towns and cities","passagePhrase":"urban areas"},{"uid":"220ae18c-4bc3-47df-b5c8-0a8c12edbce4","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"drop","passagePhrase":"reduce"},{"uid":"19779b93-5bb9-4a71-9104-8c1d9be36fd8","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"yearly","passagePhrase":"annual"},{"uid":"f3ada17a-0928-4fa3-87f1-bd2a5714a4d6","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"twice","passagePhrase":"double"},{"uid":"b90af0df-747a-42ea-ad0a-98e80ab5c972","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"vehicles manufactured","passagePhrase":"vehicle production"},{"uid":"2a544f03-b6a6-4e34-911c-f20dc94b7969","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"most appropriate vehicle","passagePhrase":"Specialised vehicles"},{"uid":"9f0f1153-e8ef-4b59-ac17-ca7297cd858e","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"various different driving conditions","passagePhrase":"infinite range of traffic, weather and road situations"},{"uid":"85699e74-d75b-4833-866a-ce4ada64c2f6","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"confidence","passagePhrase":"trust ... accept"},{"uid":"56623a64-8803-4c75-9606-4f20975fd232","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"overcome a number of problems","passagePhrase":"challenges that need to be addressed ... conquered"}]},"reading_u2_249":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><h2><span><strong>What is exploration?</strong></span></h2><p><span></span></p><p><span>We are all explores. Our desire to discover, and then share that new-found knowledge, is part of what makes us human – indeed, this has played an important part in our success as a species. Long before the first caveman slumped down beside the fire and grunted news that there were plenty of wildebeest over yonder, our ancestors had learnt the value of sending out scouts to investigate the unknown. This questing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"937b62f1-e89c-4b06-afc6-5379bc10e58e\" data-question=\"27\">nature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of ours undoubtedly helped our species spread around the globe, just as it nowadays no doubt helps the last nomadic Penan maintain their existence in the depleted forests of Borneo, and a visitor negotiate the subways of New York.</span></p><p><span>Over the years, we’ve come to think of explorers as a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f0fcdfe7-0f86-4d94-a18e-9925618d7b24\" data-question=\"28\">peculiar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> breed – different from the rest of us, different from those of us who are merely ‘well travelled’, even; and perhaps there <em>is</em> a type of person more suited to seeking out the new, a type of caveman more inclined to risk venturing out. That, however, doesn’t take away from the fact that we all have this enquiring instinct, even today; and that in all sorts of professions – whether artist, marine biologist or astronomer – borders of the unknown are being tested each day.</span></p><p><span>Thomas Hardy set some of his novels in Egdon Heath, a fictional area of uncultivated land, and used the landscape to suggest the desires and fears of his characters. He is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe63260b-3f70-47fd-93e0-2bf90658e332\" data-question=\"29\">delving into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> matters we all recognise because they are common to humanity. This is surely an act of exploration, and into a world as remote as the author chooses. Explorer and travel writer Peter Fleming talks of the moment when the explorer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1887d8a1-05fd-40f4-a25b-5a93354879fa\" data-question=\"34\">returns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> to the existence he has left behind with his loved ones. The traveller ‘who has for weeks or months seen himself only as a puny and irrelevant alien crawling laboriously over a country in which he has no roots and no background, suddenly encounters his other self, a relatively solid figure, with a place in the minds of certain people’.</span></p><p><span>In this book about the exploration of the earth’s surface, I have confined myself to those whose travels were real and who also aimed at more than personal discovery. But that still left me with another problem: the word ‘explorer’ has become associated with a past era. We think back to a golden age, as if exploration peaked somehow in the 19th century – as if the process of discovery is now on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93b0d7bb-6c6c-40af-b490-61d2d658cc02\" data-question=\"30\">decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, though the truth is that we have named only one and a half million of this planet’s species, and there may be more than 10 million – and that’s not including bacteria. We have studied only 5 per cent of the species we know. We have scarcely mapped the ocean floors, and know even less about ourselves; we fully understand the workings of only 10 per cent of our brains.</span></p><p><span>Here is how some of today’s ‘explorers’ define the word. Ran Fiennes, dubbed the ‘greatest living explorer’, said, ‘An explorer is someone who has done something that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1653543d-597d-44e6-8d90-ad48c6dc20f0\" data-question=\"37\">no human has done before<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> – and also done something scientifically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33e69233-dda7-47b5-b6b2-3a8f85818ad2\" data-question=\"37\">useful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.’ Chris Bonington, a leading mountaineer, felt exploration was to be found in the act of physically touching the unknown: ‘You have to have gone somewhere new.’ Then Robin Hanbury-Tenison, a campaigner <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"588d44b4-119e-4c8a-bb65-617ad2edcf66\" data-question=\"35\">on behalf of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> remote so-called ‘tribal’ peoples, said, ‘A traveller simply records information about some far-off world, and reports back; but an explorer <em>changes </em>the world.’ Wilfred Thesiger, who crossed Arabia’s Empty Quarter in 1946, and belongs to an era of unmechanised <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53e56fa4-8a8a-4da6-b7dc-690b204c45fd\" data-question=\"33\">travel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> now lost to the rest of us, told me, ‘If I’d gone across by camel when I could have gone by car, it would have been a stunt.’ To him, exploration meant bringing back information from a remote place regardless of any great <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf15e703-067d-4c42-843c-9e7d41c79ac8\" data-question=\"36\">self-discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>Each definition is slightly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c188efd-08c6-4a68-bfed-86b905d55521\" data-question=\"31\">different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> – and tends to reflect the field of endeavour of each pioneer. It was the same whoever I asked: the prominent historian would say exploration was a thing of the past, the cutting-edge scientist would say it was of the present. And so on. They each set their own particular criteria; the common factor in their approach being that they all had, unlike many of us who simply enjoy travel or discovering new things, both a very definite objective from the outset and also a desire to record their findings.</span></p><p><span>I’d best declare my own bias. As a writer, I’m interested in the exploration of ideas. I’ve done <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"654a9f0f-8897-4067-ac23-7c2b7efe1f36\" data-question=\"38\">a great many<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> expeditions and each one was unique. I’ve lived for months alone with isolated groups of people all around the world, even two ‘uncontacted <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e09ec686-c610-4c92-8561-095a623e9471\" data-question=\"39\">tribes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>’. But none of these things is of the slightest interest to anyone unless, through my books, I’ve found a new slant, explored a new idea. Why? Because the world has moved on. The time has long passed for the great continental voyages – another walk to the poles, another crossing of the Empty Quarter. We know how the land surface of our planet lies; exploration of it is now down to the details – the habits of microbes, say, or the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f41afd69-ad00-4d8a-a7cc-64b3d069da52\" data-question=\"40\">grazing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> behaviour of buffalo. Aside from the deep sea and deep underground, it’s the era of specialists. However, this is to disregard the role the human mind has in conveying remote places; and this is what <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11b588cd-b7d6-4661-8b5a-e7555c210fe0\" data-question=\"32\">interests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> me: how a fresh interpretation, even of a well-travelled route, can give its readers new insights.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>27-32</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"167\" id=\"question-wrapper-167\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer refers to visitors to New York to illustrate the point that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. exploration is an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"937b62f1-e89c-4b06-afc6-5379bc10e58e\" data-question=\"27\">intrinsic element<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of being human.</li> <li>B. most people are enthusiastic about exploring.</li> <li>C. exploration can lead to surprising results.</li> <li>D. most people find exploration daunting.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"168\" id=\"question-wrapper-168\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the second paragraph, what is the writer’s view of explorers? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Their discoveries have brought both benefits and disadvantages.</li> <li>B. Their main value is in teaching others.</li> <li>C. They act on an urge that is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f0fcdfe7-0f86-4d94-a18e-9925618d7b24\" data-question=\"28\">common to everyone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>D. They tend to be more attracted to certain professions than to others.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"169\" id=\"question-wrapper-169\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer refers to a description of Egdon Heath to suggest that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Hardy was writing about his own experience of exploration.</li> <li>B. Hardy was mistaken about the nature of exploration.</li> <li>C. Hardy’s aim was to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe63260b-3f70-47fd-93e0-2bf90658e332\" data-question=\"29\">investigate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> people’s emotional states.</li> <li>D. Hardy’s aim was to show the attraction of isolation.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"170\" id=\"question-wrapper-170\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the fourth paragraph, the writer refers to ‘a golden age’ to suggest that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the amount of useful information produced by exploration has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93b0d7bb-6c6c-40af-b490-61d2d658cc02\" data-question=\"30\">decreased<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>B. fewer people are interested in exploring than in the 19th century.</li> <li>C. recent developments have made exploration less exciting.</li> <li>D. we are wrong to think that exploration is no longer necessary.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"171\" id=\"question-wrapper-171\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the sixth paragraph, when discussing the definition of exploration, the writer argues that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. people tend to relate exploration to their own professional interests.</li> <li>B. certain people are likely to misunderstand the nature of exploration.</li> <li>C. the generally accepted definition has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c188efd-08c6-4a68-bfed-86b905d55521\" data-question=\"31\">changed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> over time.</li> <li>D. historians and scientists have more valid definitions than the general public.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"172\" id=\"question-wrapper-172\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the last paragraph, the writer explains that he is interested in </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. how someone’s personality is reflected in their choice of places to visit.</li> <li>B. the human ability to cast new light on places that may be familiar.</li> <li>C. how travel writing has evolved to meet changing demands.</li> <li>D. the feelings that writers develop about the places that they explore.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 33-37) and the list of explorers below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct explorer, <strong>A-E</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-E</strong>, in boxes <strong>33-37</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong><em>NB</em></strong><em> You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Explorers</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Peter Fleming</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> Ran Fiennes</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> Chris Bonington</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> Robin Hanbury-Tenison</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong> Wilfred Thesiger</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"173\" id=\"question-wrapper-173\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> He referred to the relevance of the form of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53e56fa4-8a8a-4da6-b7dc-690b204c45fd\" data-question=\"33\">transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> used. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"174\" id=\"question-wrapper-174\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> He described feelings on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1887d8a1-05fd-40f4-a25b-5a93354879fa\" data-question=\"34\">coming back<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> home after a long journey. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"175\" id=\"question-wrapper-175\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> He worked <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"588d44b4-119e-4c8a-bb65-617ad2edcf66\" data-question=\"35\">for the benefit of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> specific groups of people. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"176\" id=\"question-wrapper-176\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> He did not consider <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf15e703-067d-4c42-843c-9e7d41c79ac8\" data-question=\"36\">learning about oneself<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> an essential part of exploration. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"177\" id=\"question-wrapper-177\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> He defined exploration as being both unique and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"33e69233-dda7-47b5-b6b2-3a8f85818ad2\" data-question=\"37\">of value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to others. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>38-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>The writer’s own bias</strong></span></h4><p><span>The writer has experience of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"654a9f0f-8897-4067-ac23-7c2b7efe1f36\" data-question=\"38\">a large number of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <strong>38</strong>………………., and was the first stranger that certain previously <strong>39</strong>………………… <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e09ec686-c610-4c92-8561-095a623e9471\" data-question=\"39\">people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> had encountered. He believes there is no need for further exploration of Earth’s <strong>40</strong>…………………., except to answer specific questions such as how buffalo <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f41afd69-ad00-4d8a-a7cc-64b3d069da52\" data-question=\"40\">eat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"178\" id=\"question-wrapper-178\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(UNIQUE) EXPEDITIONS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"179\" id=\"question-wrapper-179\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">UNCONTACTED/ISOLATED</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"180\" id=\"question-wrapper-180\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(LAND) SURFACE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"937b62f1-e89c-4b06-afc6-5379bc10e58e","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"intrinsic element","passagePhrase":"nature"},{"uid":"fe63260b-3f70-47fd-93e0-2bf90658e332","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"investigate","passagePhrase":"delving into"},{"uid":"1887d8a1-05fd-40f4-a25b-5a93354879fa","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"coming back","passagePhrase":"returns"},{"uid":"93b0d7bb-6c6c-40af-b490-61d2d658cc02","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"decreased","passagePhrase":"decline"},{"uid":"1653543d-597d-44e6-8d90-ad48c6dc20f0","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"no human has done before"},{"uid":"33e69233-dda7-47b5-b6b2-3a8f85818ad2","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"of value","passagePhrase":"useful"},{"uid":"588d44b4-119e-4c8a-bb65-617ad2edcf66","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"for the benefit of","passagePhrase":"on behalf of"},{"uid":"53e56fa4-8a8a-4da6-b7dc-690b204c45fd","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"transport","passagePhrase":"travel"},{"uid":"cf15e703-067d-4c42-843c-9e7d41c79ac8","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"learning about oneself","passagePhrase":"self-discovery"},{"uid":"5c188efd-08c6-4a68-bfed-86b905d55521","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"changed","passagePhrase":"different"},{"uid":"654a9f0f-8897-4067-ac23-7c2b7efe1f36","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"a large number of","passagePhrase":"a great many"},{"uid":"e09ec686-c610-4c92-8561-095a623e9471","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"people","passagePhrase":"tribes"},{"uid":"f41afd69-ad00-4d8a-a7cc-64b3d069da52","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"eat","passagePhrase":"grazing"},{"uid":"11b588cd-b7d6-4661-8b5a-e7555c210fe0","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"interests"}]},"reading_u2_250":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><h2><span><strong>Could urban engineers learn from dance?</strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23aec6c9-e208-453a-ba27-a6c196b09e4c\" data-question=\"6\">The way we travel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> around cities has a major impact on whether they are sustainable. Transportation is estimated to account for 30% of energy consumption in most of the world’s most developed nations, so lowering the need for energy-using vehicles is essential for decreasing the environmental impact of mobility. But as more and more people move to cities, it is important to think about other kinds of sustainable travel too. The ways we travel affect our physical and mental health, our social lives, our access to work and culture, and the air we breathe. Engineers are tasked with changing how we travel round cities through urban design, but the engineering industry still works on the assumptions that led to the creation of the energy-consuming transport systems we have now: the emphasis placed solely on efficiency, speed, and quantitative data. We need radical changes, to make it healthier, more enjoyable, and less environmentally damaging to travel around cities.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>Dance might hold some of the answers. That is not to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"73a9e4ad-1185-4aa7-84d3-9b86af17cdd3\" data-question=\"1\">suggest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> everyone should dance their way to work, however healthy and happy it might make us, but rather that the techniques used by choreographers to experiment with and design movement in dance could provide engineers with tools to stimulate new ideas in city-making. Richard Sennett, an influential urbanist and sociologist who has transformed ideas about the way cities are made, argues that urban design has suffered from a separation between mind and body since the introduction of the architectural blueprint.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>Whereas <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"904d2816-5bc3-4508-b0b3-f5558f1d42fa\" data-question=\"2\">medieval<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> builders improvised and adapted <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea258b9b-b778-4f57-9bc6-292a7228b704\" data-question=\"2\">construction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> through their intimate knowledge of materials and personal experience of the conditions on a site, building designs are now conceived and stored in media technologies that detach the designer from the physical and social realities they are creating. While the design practices created by these new technologies are essential for managing the technical complexity of the modern city, they have the drawback of simplifying reality in the process.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>To illustrate, Sennett discusses the Peachtree Center in Atlanta, USA, a development typical of the modernist approach to urban planning prevalent in the 1970s. Peachtree created a grid of streets and towers intended as a new pedestrian-friendly downtown for Atlanta. According to Sennett, this failed because its designers had invested too much faith in computer-aided design to tell them how it would operate. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8accb99a-065a-49d1-9207-f38d6e2411ec\" data-question=\"4\">failed to take into account<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> that purpose-built street cafés could not operate in the hot sun without the protective awnings common in older buildings, and would need energy-consuming air conditioning instead, or that its giant car park would feel so unwelcoming that it would put people off getting out of their cars. What seems entirely predictable and controllable on screen has unexpected results when translated into reality.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>The same is true in transport engineering, which uses models to predict and shape the way people move through the city. Again, these models are necessary, but they are built on specific world views in which certain forms of efficiency and safety are considered and other experience of the city ignored. Designs that seem logical in models <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4baaf5e5-25e9-48b5-9dc2-cdaa819e1ddf\" data-question=\"5\">appear counter-intuitive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in the actual experience of their users. The guard rails that will be familiar to anyone who has attempted to cross a British road, for example, were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9952c341-9ded-4903-9b9f-44e7bfcd1766\" data-question=\"7\">an engineering solution to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> pedestrian safety based on models that prioritise the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4fbf6fae-e124-4d47-9882-02de8e6d891a\" data-question=\"8\">smooth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"126bb69a-b7b5-46b8-8b62-193d897acf59\" data-question=\"8\">flow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of traffic. On wide major roads, they often guide pedestrians to specific crossing points and slow down their progress across the road by using staggered access points <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7809ba1b-1b0d-402b-ac18-d133f59963ea\" data-question=\"12\">divide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b405697-3a7d-4640-819d-6f3ee7da5682\" data-question=\"9\">crossing into two<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b405697-3a7d-4640-819d-6f3ee7da5682\" data-question=\"9\">one for each carriageway<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. In doing so they make crossings feel longer, introducing psychological <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d9dfe4c-3977-4da6-9349-cd0addef0626\" data-question=\"10\">barriers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> greatly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"58d86aa2-5432-4ae8-a4b5-b948763a1935\" data-question=\"10\">impacting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> those that are the least mobile, and encouraging <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbf93605-000b-4f09-9e70-23a6bfae21f4\" data-question=\"11\">others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> to make dangerous crossings to get around the guard rails. These barriers don’t just make it harder to cross the road: they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7809ba1b-1b0d-402b-ac18-d133f59963ea\" data-question=\"12\">divide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> communities and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4c92f36-9698-4752-a5d1-dd464a5d3dea\" data-question=\"13\">decrease opportunities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> for healthy transport. As a result, many are now being removed, causing disruption, cost, and waste.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>If their designers had had the tools to think with their bodies – like dancers – and imagine how these barriers would feel, there might have been a better solution. In order to bring about fundamental changes to the ways we use our cities, engineering will need to develop a richer understanding of why people move in certain ways, and how this movement affects them. Choreography may not seem an obvious choice for tackling this problem. Yet it shares with engineering the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ddce7051-e616-4cf1-953f-c6378bbe615c\" data-question=\"3\">aim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of designing patterns of movement within limitations of space. It is an art form developed almost entirely by trying out ideas with the body, and gaining instant feedback on how the results feel. Choreographers have deep understanding of the psychological, aesthetic, and physical implications of different ways of moving.</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong></span></p><p><span>Observing the choreographer Wayne McGregor, cognitive scientist David Kirsh described how he ‘thinks with the body’, Kirsh argues that by using the body to simulate outcomes, McGregor is able to imagine solutions that would not be possible using purely abstract thought. This kind of physical knowledge is valued in many areas of expertise, but currently has no place in formal engineering design processes. A suggested method for transport engineers is to improvise design solutions and instant feedback about how they would work from their own experience of them, or model designs at full scale in the way choreographers experiment with groups of dancers. Above all, perhaps, they might learn to design for emotional as well as functional effects.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, in boxes <strong>1-6</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20160\" id=\"question-wrapper-20160\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to an appealing way of using dance that the writer is not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"73a9e4ad-1185-4aa7-84d3-9b86af17cdd3\" data-question=\"1\">proposing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20161\" id=\"question-wrapper-20161\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an example of a contrast between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"904d2816-5bc3-4508-b0b3-f5558f1d42fa\" data-question=\"2\">past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and present approaches to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea258b9b-b778-4f57-9bc6-292a7228b704\" data-question=\"2\">building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20162\" id=\"question-wrapper-20162\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ddce7051-e616-4cf1-953f-c6378bbe615c\" data-question=\"3\">objective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of both dance and engineering </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20163\" id=\"question-wrapper-20163\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to an unforeseen problem arising from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8accb99a-065a-49d1-9207-f38d6e2411ec\" data-question=\"4\">ignoring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the climate </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20164\" id=\"question-wrapper-20164\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> why some measures intended to help people are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4baaf5e5-25e9-48b5-9dc2-cdaa819e1ddf\" data-question=\"5\">being reversed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20165\" id=\"question-wrapper-20165\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23aec6c9-e208-453a-ba27-a6c196b09e4c\" data-question=\"6\">transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> has an impact on human lives </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>7-13</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>Guard rails</strong></span></h4><p><span>Guard rails were introduced on British roads to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9952c341-9ded-4903-9b9f-44e7bfcd1766\" data-question=\"7\">improve the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <strong>7</strong>…………………… of pedestrians, while ensuring that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"126bb69a-b7b5-46b8-8b62-193d897acf59\" data-question=\"8\">movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of <strong>8</strong>……………………. is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4fbf6fae-e124-4d47-9882-02de8e6d891a\" data-question=\"8\">not disrupted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. Pedestrians are led to access points, and encouraged to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b405697-3a7d-4640-819d-6f3ee7da5682\" data-question=\"9\">cross one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <strong>9</strong>…………………….. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b405697-3a7d-4640-819d-6f3ee7da5682\" data-question=\"9\">at a time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>An unintended <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"58d86aa2-5432-4ae8-a4b5-b948763a1935\" data-question=\"10\">effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> is to create psychological <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d9dfe4c-3977-4da6-9349-cd0addef0626\" data-question=\"10\">difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> in crossing the road, particularly for less <strong>10</strong>………………….. people. Another result is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbf93605-000b-4f09-9e70-23a6bfae21f4\" data-question=\"11\">some people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> cross the road in a <strong>11</strong>……………………. way. The guard rails <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7809ba1b-1b0d-402b-ac18-d133f59963ea\" data-question=\"12\">separate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <strong>12</strong>……………………., and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4c92f36-9698-4752-a5d1-dd464a5d3dea\" data-question=\"13\">make it more difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to introduce forms of transport that are <strong>13</strong>…………………….</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20166\" id=\"question-wrapper-20166\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SAFETY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20167\" id=\"question-wrapper-20167\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRAFFIC</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20168\" id=\"question-wrapper-20168\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CARRIAGEWAY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20169\" id=\"question-wrapper-20169\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MOBILE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20170\" id=\"question-wrapper-20170\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DANGEROUS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20171\" id=\"question-wrapper-20171\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMMUNITIES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20172\" id=\"question-wrapper-20172\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HEALTHY</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"23aec6c9-e208-453a-ba27-a6c196b09e4c","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"transport","passagePhrase":"The way we travel"},{"uid":"73a9e4ad-1185-4aa7-84d3-9b86af17cdd3","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"proposing","passagePhrase":"suggest"},{"uid":"904d2816-5bc3-4508-b0b3-f5558f1d42fa","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"past","passagePhrase":"medieval"},{"uid":"ea258b9b-b778-4f57-9bc6-292a7228b704","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"building","passagePhrase":"construction"},{"uid":"8accb99a-065a-49d1-9207-f38d6e2411ec","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"ignoring","passagePhrase":"failed to take into account"},{"uid":"4baaf5e5-25e9-48b5-9dc2-cdaa819e1ddf","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"being reversed","passagePhrase":"appear counter-intuitive"},{"uid":"9952c341-9ded-4903-9b9f-44e7bfcd1766","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"improve the","passagePhrase":"an engineering solution to"},{"uid":"4fbf6fae-e124-4d47-9882-02de8e6d891a","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"not disrupted","passagePhrase":"smooth"},{"uid":"126bb69a-b7b5-46b8-8b62-193d897acf59","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"movement","passagePhrase":"flow"},{"uid":"7809ba1b-1b0d-402b-ac18-d133f59963ea","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"separate","passagePhrase":"divide ... divide"},{"uid":"9b405697-3a7d-4640-819d-6f3ee7da5682","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"cross one ... at a time","passagePhrase":"crossing into two ... one for each carriageway"},{"uid":"1d9dfe4c-3977-4da6-9349-cd0addef0626","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"difficulties","passagePhrase":"barriers"},{"uid":"58d86aa2-5432-4ae8-a4b5-b948763a1935","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"effect","passagePhrase":"impacting"},{"uid":"bbf93605-000b-4f09-9e70-23a6bfae21f4","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"some people","passagePhrase":"others"},{"uid":"f4c92f36-9698-4752-a5d1-dd464a5d3dea","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"make it more difficult","passagePhrase":"decrease opportunities"},{"uid":"ddce7051-e616-4cf1-953f-c6378bbe615c","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"objective","passagePhrase":"aim"}]},"reading_u2_251":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Should we try to bring extinct species back to life?</strong></span></h2><p><span><strong>A</strong></span></p><p><span>The passenger pigeon was a legendary species. Flying in vast numbers across North America, with potentially many millions within a single flock, their migration was once one of nature’s great spectacles. Sadly, the passenger pigeon’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13968edd-bf03-493f-bfd6-4b1db5fab2f9\" data-question=\"17\">existence came to an end<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> on 1 September 1914, when the last living specimen died at Cincinnati Zoo. Geneticist Ben Novak is lead researcher on an ambitious project which now aims to bring the bird back to life through a process known as ‘de-extinction’. The basic premise involves using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62e999af-9235-4ede-bb94-c863951dfca1\" data-question=\"15\">cloning technology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> to turn the DNA of extinct animals into a fertilised embryo, which is carried by the nearest relative still in existence – in this case, the abundant band-tailed pigeon – before being born as a living, breathing animal. Passenger pigeons are one of the pioneering species in this field, but they are far from the only ones on which this cutting-edge technology is being trialled.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong></span></p><p><span>In Australia, the thylacine, more commonly known as the Tasmanian tiger, is another extinct creature which genetic scientists are striving to bring back to life. ‘There is no carnivore now in Tasmania that fills the niche which thylacines once occupied,’ explains Michael Archer of the University of New South Wales. He points out that in the decades since the thylacine went extinct, there has been a spread in a ‘dangerously debilitating’ facial tumour syndrome which threatens the existence of the Tasmanian devils, the island’s other notorious <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0060123-25e8-402f-baed-475538e2d680\" data-question=\"23\">resident<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. Thylacines would have prevented this spread because they would have killed significant numbers of Tasmanian devils. ‘If that contagious cancer had popped up previously, it would have burned out in whatever region it started. The return of thylacines to Tasmania could help to ensure that devils are never again subjected to risks of this kind.’</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong></span></p><p><span>If extinct species can be brought back to life, can humanity begin to correct the damage it has caused to the natural world over the past few millennia? ‘The idea of de-extinction is that we can reverse this process, bringing species that no longer exist back to life,’ says Beth Shapiro of University of California Santa Cruz’s Genomics Institute. ‘I don’t think that we can do this. There is no way to bring back something that is 100 per cent identical to a species that went extinct a long time ago.’ A more practical approach for long-extinct species is to take the DNA of existing species as a template, ready for the insertion of strands of extinct animal DNA to create something new; a hybrid, based on the living species, but which looks and/or acts like the animal which died out.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong></span></p><p><span>This complicated process and questionable outcome begs the question: what is the actual point of this technology? ‘For us, the goal has always been replacing the extinct species with a suitable replacement,’ explains Novak. ‘When it comes to breeding, band-tailed pigeons scatter and make maybe one or two nests per hectare, whereas passenger pigeons were very social and would make 10,000 or more nests in one hectare.’ Since <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c906448d-720f-405b-9b98-1e96c9742f23\" data-question=\"16\">the disappearance of this key species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, ecosystems in the eastern US have suffered, as the lack of disturbance caused by thousands of passenger pigeons wrecking trees and branches means there has been minimal need for regrowth. This has left forests stagnant and therefore unwelcoming to the plants and animals which evolved to help regenerate the forest after a disturbance. According to Novak, a hybridized band-tailed pigeon, with the added nesting habits of a passenger pigeon, could, in theory, re-establish that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b3cad95-64ae-4f20-a7d1-d89614638f94\" data-question=\"25\">forest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> disturbance, thereby creating a habitat necessary for a great many other native species to thrive.</span></p><p><span><strong>E</strong></span></p><p><span>Another popular candidate for this technology is the woolly mammoth. George Church, professor at Harvard Medical School and leader of the Woolly Mammoth Revival Project, has been focusing on cold resistance, the main way in which the extinct woolly mammoth and its nearest living relative, the Asian elephant, differ. By <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee2c4f6a-761e-4ce6-b211-c8a705201e9c\" data-question=\"18\">pinpointing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> which genetic traits <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d1b7020-1cfd-493f-99aa-40b747b0ab8b\" data-question=\"18\">made it possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> for mammoths <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62561573-e048-40de-9060-71a6d6ffeca5\" data-question=\"18\">to survive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the icy climate of the tundra, the project’s goal is to return mammoths, or a mammoth-like species, to the area. ‘My highest priority would be preserving the endangered Asian elephant,’ says Church, ‘expanding their range to the huge ecosystem of the tundra. Necessary adaptations would include <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"084265da-50d2-4a7c-826d-44a1a66de2f4\" data-question=\"20\">smaller<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> ears, thicker hair, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"257fa280-c6a8-4125-8827-ccb1b8fe3509\" data-question=\"21\">and extra<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> insulating fat, all for the purpose of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24d62349-1636-424f-83e7-78d9b00cb865\" data-question=\"19\">reducing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> heat loss in the tundra, and all traits found in the now extinct woolly mammoth.’ This repopulation of the tundra and boreal forests of Eurasia and North America with large mammals could also be a useful factor in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24d62349-1636-424f-83e7-78d9b00cb865\" data-question=\"19\">reducing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> carbon emissions – elephants punch holes through snow and knock down trees, which encourages grass growth. This grass growth would reduce temperature, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7599b093-a2fc-4686-a81a-592c55a3e850\" data-question=\"22\">mitigate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> emissions from melting permafrost.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong></span></p><p><span>While the prospect of bringing extinct animals back to life might capture imaginations, it is, of course, far easier to try to save an existing species which is merely threatened with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"659cbc13-d678-4cd0-b4d8-32922b6cf34f\" data-question=\"14\">extinction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. ‘Many of the technologies that people have in mind when they think about de-extinction can be used as a form of “genetic rescue”,’ explains Shapiro. She prefers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"44a044f9-3671-4827-a5f5-a3434b7327b1\" data-question=\"24\">to focus<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the debate on how this emerging technology could be used to fully understand why various species went extinct in the first place, and therefore how we could use it to make genetic modifications which could prevent mass extinctions in the future. ‘I would also say there’s an incredible moral hazard to not do anything at all,’ she continues. ‘We know that what we are doing today is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a64c16d-a377-4734-9ad1-af74d7d67ad2\" data-question=\"26\">not enough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, and we have to be willing to take some calculated and measured risks.’</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, <strong>A-F</strong>.</span></p><p><span>Which paragraph contains the following information?</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-17</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong><em>NB</em></strong><em> You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20173\" id=\"question-wrapper-20173\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to how further <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"659cbc13-d678-4cd0-b4d8-32922b6cf34f\" data-question=\"14\">disappearance of multiple species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> could be avoided. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20174\" id=\"question-wrapper-20174\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> explanation of a way of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62e999af-9235-4ede-bb94-c863951dfca1\" data-question=\"15\">reproducing an extinct animal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> using the DNA of only that species </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20175\" id=\"question-wrapper-20175\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to a habitat which has suffered following <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c906448d-720f-405b-9b98-1e96c9742f23\" data-question=\"16\">the extinction of a species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20176\" id=\"question-wrapper-20176\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of the exact point at which a particular species <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13968edd-bf03-493f-bfd6-4b1db5fab2f9\" data-question=\"17\">became extinct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>18-22</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>The woolly mammoth revival project</strong></span></h4><p><span>Professor George Church and his team are trying to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee2c4f6a-761e-4ce6-b211-c8a705201e9c\" data-question=\"18\">identify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the <strong>18</strong>…………………… which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d1b7020-1cfd-493f-99aa-40b747b0ab8b\" data-question=\"18\">enabled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> mammoths <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62561573-e048-40de-9060-71a6d6ffeca5\" data-question=\"18\">to live<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in the tundra. The findings could help preserve the mammoth’s close relative, the endangered Asian elephant.</span></p><p><span>According to Church, introducing Asian elephants to the tundra would involve certain physical adaptations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24d62349-1636-424f-83e7-78d9b00cb865\" data-question=\"19\">to minimise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <strong>19</strong>…………………… To survive in the tundra, the species would need to have the mammoth-like features of thicker hair, <strong>20</strong>………………….. of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"084265da-50d2-4a7c-826d-44a1a66de2f4\" data-question=\"20\">a reduced size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"257fa280-c6a8-4125-8827-ccb1b8fe3509\" data-question=\"21\">and more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <strong>21</strong>……………………..</span></p><p><span>Repopulating the tundra with mammoths or Asian elephant/mammoth hybrids would also have an impact on the environment, which could help to reduce temperatures and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7599b093-a2fc-4686-a81a-592c55a3e850\" data-question=\"22\">decrease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <strong>22</strong>……………………</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20177\" id=\"question-wrapper-20177\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GENETIC TRAITS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20178\" id=\"question-wrapper-20178\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HEAT LOSS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20179\" id=\"question-wrapper-20179\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EARS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20180\" id=\"question-wrapper-20180\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(INSULATING) FAT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20181\" id=\"question-wrapper-20181\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(CARBON) EMISSIONS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Look at the following statements (Questions 23-26) and the list of people below.</span></p><p><span>Match each statement with the correct person, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>, in boxes <strong>23-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong><em>NB</em></strong><em> You may use any letter more than once.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of People</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> Ben Novak</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> Michael Archer</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> Beth Shapiro</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20182\" id=\"question-wrapper-20182\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Reintroducing an extinct species to its original habitat could improve the health of a particular <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0060123-25e8-402f-baed-475538e2d680\" data-question=\"23\">species living there<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20183\" id=\"question-wrapper-20183\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is important <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"44a044f9-3671-4827-a5f5-a3434b7327b1\" data-question=\"24\">to concentrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> on the causes of an animal’s extinction. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20184\" id=\"question-wrapper-20184\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A species brought back from extinction could have an important beneficial impact on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b3cad95-64ae-4f20-a7d1-d89614638f94\" data-question=\"25\">the vegetation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> of its habitat. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20185\" id=\"question-wrapper-20185\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Our current efforts at preserving biodiversity are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a64c16d-a377-4734-9ad1-af74d7d67ad2\" data-question=\"26\">insufficient<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"13968edd-bf03-493f-bfd6-4b1db5fab2f9","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"became extinct","passagePhrase":"existence came to an end"},{"uid":"62e999af-9235-4ede-bb94-c863951dfca1","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"reproducing an extinct animal","passagePhrase":"cloning technology"},{"uid":"a0060123-25e8-402f-baed-475538e2d680","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"species living there","passagePhrase":"resident"},{"uid":"c906448d-720f-405b-9b98-1e96c9742f23","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"the extinction of a species","passagePhrase":"the disappearance of this key species"},{"uid":"0b3cad95-64ae-4f20-a7d1-d89614638f94","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"the vegetation","passagePhrase":"forest"},{"uid":"ee2c4f6a-761e-4ce6-b211-c8a705201e9c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"identify","passagePhrase":"pinpointing"},{"uid":"4d1b7020-1cfd-493f-99aa-40b747b0ab8b","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"enabled","passagePhrase":"made it possible"},{"uid":"62561573-e048-40de-9060-71a6d6ffeca5","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"to live","passagePhrase":"to survive"},{"uid":"084265da-50d2-4a7c-826d-44a1a66de2f4","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"a reduced size","passagePhrase":"smaller"},{"uid":"257fa280-c6a8-4125-8827-ccb1b8fe3509","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"and more","passagePhrase":"and extra"},{"uid":"24d62349-1636-424f-83e7-78d9b00cb865","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"to minimise","passagePhrase":"reducing ... reducing"},{"uid":"7599b093-a2fc-4686-a81a-592c55a3e850","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"decrease","passagePhrase":"mitigate"},{"uid":"659cbc13-d678-4cd0-b4d8-32922b6cf34f","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"disappearance of multiple species","passagePhrase":"extinction"},{"uid":"44a044f9-3671-4827-a5f5-a3434b7327b1","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"to concentrate","passagePhrase":"to focus"},{"uid":"8a64c16d-a377-4734-9ad1-af74d7d67ad2","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"insufficient","passagePhrase":"not enough"}]},"reading_u2_252":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</p><p> </p><h2><strong>Having a laugh</strong></h2><p><em>The findings of psychological scientists reveal the importance of humour</em></p><p>Humans start developing a sense of humour as early as six weeks old, when babies begin to laugh and smile in response to stimuli. Laughter is universal across all human cultures and even exists in some form in rats, chimps, and bonobos. Like other human <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f69203b4-d430-4fca-b86e-86943a6ced36\" data-question=\"32\">emotions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> and expressions, laughter and humour <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0649194f-7919-463b-9e77-5e529fb764f7\" data-question=\"27\">provide psychological scientists with rich resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> for studying human psychology, ranging from the development of language to the neuroscience of social perception.</p><p>Theories focusing on the evolution of laughter point to it as an important adaptation for social communication. Take, for example, the recorded laughter in TV comedy shows. Back in 1950, US sound engineer Charley Douglass hated dealing with the unpredictable laughter of live audiences, so started recording his own ‘laugh tracks’. These were intended to help people at home feel like they were in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5ad17f1-e50d-48ae-83a5-83c3f659982f\" data-question=\"28\">social situation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, such as a crowded theatre. Douglass even recorded various types of laughter, as well as mixtures of laughter from men, women, and children. In doing so, he picked up on a quality of laughter that is now interesting researchers: a simple ‘haha’ communicates a remarkable amount of socially relevant information.</p><p>In one study conducted in 2016, samples of laughter from pairs of English-speaking students were recorded at the University of California, Santa Cruz. A team made up of more than 30 psychological scientists, anthropologists, and biologists then played these recording to listeners from 24 diverse societies, from indigenous tribes in New Guinea to city-dwellers in India and Europe. Participants were asked whether they thought the people laughing were friends or strangers. On average, the results were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a1696f3-067c-42aa-8e80-29e883c84b93\" data-question=\"29\">remarkably consistent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>: worldwide, people’s guesses were correct approximately 60% of the time.</p><p>Researchers have also found that different types of laughter serve as codes to complex human social hierarchies. A team led by Christopher Oveis from the University of California, San Diego, found that high-status individuals had different laughs from low-status individuals, and that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"63680f31-1a1e-4658-9261-2ac6f54dd700\" data-question=\"30\">strangers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>’ judgements of an individual’s social status were influenced by the dominant or submissive quality of their laughter. In their study, 48 male college students were randomly assigned to groups of four, with each group composed of two low-status members, who had just joined their college fraternity group, and two high-status members, older students who had been active in the fraternity for at least two years. Laughter was recorded as each student took a turn at being teased by the others, involving the use of mildly insulting nicknames. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9790cb4b-d6db-4a06-b494-687f685b462a\" data-question=\"38\">Analysis revealed that, as expected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, high-status individuals produced more dominant laughs and fewer submissive laughs relative to the low-status individuals. Meanwhile, low-status individuals were more likely to change their laughter based on their position of power; that is, the newcomers produced more dominant laughs when they were in the ‘powerful’ role of teasers. Dominant laughter was higher in pitch, louder, and more variable in tone than submissive laughter.</p><p>A random group of volunteers then listened to an equal number of dominant and submissive laughs from both the high- and low-status individuals, and were asked to estimate the social status of the laughter. In line with predictions, laughers producing dominant laughs were perceived to be significantly higher in status than laughers producing submissive laughs. ‘This was particularly true for low-status individuals, who were rated as significantly higher in status when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b6a38b7-c94a-4af1-931a-e89159047702\" data-question=\"31\">displaying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> a dominant versus submissive laugh,’ Oveis and colleagues note. ‘Thus, by strategically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b6a38b7-c94a-4af1-931a-e89159047702\" data-question=\"31\">displaying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> more dominant laughter when the context allows, low-status individuals may achieve higher status in the eyes of others.’ However, high-status individuals were rated as high-status whether they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b6a38b7-c94a-4af1-931a-e89159047702\" data-question=\"31\">produced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> t<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"410e355c-3b64-4f63-b604-7c898931d407\" data-question=\"31\">heir natural dominant laugh or tried to do a submissive one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</p><p>Another study, conducted by David Cheng and Lu Wang of Australian National University, was based on the hypothesis that humour might provide a respite from tedious situations in the workplace. This ‘mental break’ might facilitate the replenishment of mental resources. To test this theory, the researchers recruited 74 business students, ostensibly for an experiment on perception. First, the students performed a tedious task in which they had to cross out every instance of the letter ‘e’ over two pages of text. The students then were randomly assigned to watch a video clip <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"403ddeb2-b152-45aa-b500-36a5699e62fe\" data-question=\"32\">eliciting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> either humour, contentment, or neutral <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f69203b4-d430-4fca-b86e-86943a6ced36\" data-question=\"32\">feelings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Some watched a clip of the BBC comedy <em>Mr. Bean</em>, others a relaxing scene with dolphins swimming in the ocean, and others a factual video about the management profession.</p><p>The students then completed a task requiring persistence in which they were asked to guess the potential performance of employees based on provided profiles, and were told that making 10 correct assessments in a row would lead to a win. However, the software was programmed such that is was nearly impossible to achieve 10 consecutive correct answers. Participants were allowed to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"399e792a-84ec-4f02-be1f-574a2782176e\" data-question=\"39\">quit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> the task at any point. Students who had watched the <em>Mr. Bean </em>video ended up <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90468a47-3081-45fb-9e30-a334a7734be0\" data-question=\"33\">spending significantly more time working on the task<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, making twice as many predictions as the other two groups.</p><p>Cheng and Wang then replicated these results in a second study, during which they had participants complete long multiplication questions by hand. Again, participants who watched the humorous video spent significantly more time working on this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"788525db-faa3-4c35-be0a-d79cf3aa1df9\" data-question=\"34\">tedious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> task and completed more questions correctly than did the students in either of the other groups.</p><p>‘<span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f62fada5-7969-4831-8f1b-3a153c3f4421\" data-question=\"40\">Although humour has been found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c3f5e116-e50c-4c88-90d8-fc10c44ebb05\" data-question=\"35\">relieve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> stress and facilitate social relationships, traditional view of task performance implies that individuals should avoid things such as humour that may distract them from the accomplishment of task goals,’ Cheng and Wang conclude. ‘We suggest that humour is not only enjoyable but more importantly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0c31c94-8e5b-42f5-a24d-2399d9b51c35\" data-question=\"36\">energising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.’</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20186\" id=\"question-wrapper-20186\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When referring to laughter in the first paragraphs, the writer emphasises </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. its impact on language.</li> <li>B. its function in human culture.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0649194f-7919-463b-9e77-5e529fb764f7\" data-question=\"27\">its value to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> scientific research.</li> <li>D. its universality in animal societies.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20187\" id=\"question-wrapper-20187\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer suggest about Charley Douglass? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. He understood the importance of enjoying humour in a group setting.</li> <li>B. He believed that TV viewers at home needed to be told when to laugh.</li> <li>C. He wanted his shows to appeal to audiences across the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5ad17f1-e50d-48ae-83a5-83c3f659982f\" data-question=\"28\">social spectrum<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>D. He preferred shows where audiences were present in the recording studio.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20188\" id=\"question-wrapper-20188\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What makes the Santa Cruz study particularly significant? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the various different types of laughter that were studied</li> <li>B. the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a1696f3-067c-42aa-8e80-29e883c84b93\" data-question=\"29\">similar results produced by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> a wide range of cultures</li> <li>C. the number of different academic disciplines involved</li> <li>D. the many kinds of people whose laughter was recorded</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20189\" id=\"question-wrapper-20189\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Which of the following happened in the San Diego study? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Some participants became very upset.</li> <li>B. Participants exchanged roles.</li> <li>C. Participants who had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"63680f31-1a1e-4658-9261-2ac6f54dd700\" data-question=\"30\">not met before<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> became friends.</li> <li>D. Some participants were unable to laugh.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20190\" id=\"question-wrapper-20190\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the fifth paragraph, what did the results of the San Diego study suggest? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is clear whether a dominant laugh is produced by a high- or low-status person.</li> <li>B. Low-status individuals in a position of power will still produce submissive laughs.</li> <li>C. The submissive laughs of low- and high-status individuals are surprisingly similar.</li> <li>D. High-status individuals can always be identified by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"410e355c-3b64-4f63-b604-7c898931d407\" data-question=\"31\">their way of laughing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, <strong>A-H</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-H</strong>, in boxes <strong>32-36</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>The benefits of humour</strong></span></h4><p><span>In one study at Australian National University, randomly chosen groups of participants were shown one of three videos, each designed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"403ddeb2-b152-45aa-b500-36a5699e62fe\" data-question=\"32\">generate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> a different kind of <strong>32</strong>………………….. . When all participants were then given a deliberately frustrating task to do, it was found that those who had watched the <strong>33</strong>…………………….. video <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90468a47-3081-45fb-9e30-a334a7734be0\" data-question=\"33\">persisted with the task for longer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> and tried harder to accomplish the task than either of the other two groups.</span></p><p><span>A second study in which participants were asked to perform a particularly <strong>34</strong>……………………… task produced similar results. According to researchers David Cheng and Lu Wang, these findings suggest that humour not only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c3f5e116-e50c-4c88-90d8-fc10c44ebb05\" data-question=\"35\">reduces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <strong>35</strong>…………………… and helps build social connections but it may also have a <strong>36</strong>……………………. Effect on the body and mind.</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> laughter <strong>B</strong> relaxing <strong>C</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"788525db-faa3-4c35-be0a-d79cf3aa1df9\" data-question=\"34\">boring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> anxiety <strong>E </strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0c31c94-8e5b-42f5-a24d-2399d9b51c35\" data-question=\"36\">stimulating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <strong>F</strong> emotion</span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong> enjoyment <strong>H</strong> amusing</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20191\" id=\"question-wrapper-20191\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20192\" id=\"question-wrapper-20192\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20193\" id=\"question-wrapper-20193\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20194\" id=\"question-wrapper-20194\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20195\" id=\"question-wrapper-20195\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?</p><p><em>In boxes <strong>37-40</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</p><p><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</p><p><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20196\" id=\"question-wrapper-20196\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Participants in the Santa Cruz study were more accurate at identifying the laughs of friends than those of strangers. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20197\" id=\"question-wrapper-20197\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The researchers in the San Diego study <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9790cb4b-d6db-4a06-b494-687f685b462a\" data-question=\"38\">were correct in their predictions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> regarding the behaviour of the high-status individuals. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20198\" id=\"question-wrapper-20198\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The participants in the Australian National University study were given a fixed amount of time to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"399e792a-84ec-4f02-be1f-574a2782176e\" data-question=\"39\">complete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> the task focusing on employee profiles. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"20199\" id=\"question-wrapper-20199\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Cheng and Wang’s conclusions <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f62fada5-7969-4831-8f1b-3a153c3f4421\" data-question=\"40\">were in line<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> with established notions regarding task performance. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f69203b4-d430-4fca-b86e-86943a6ced36","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"emotions ... feelings"},{"uid":"0649194f-7919-463b-9e77-5e529fb764f7","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"its value to","passagePhrase":"provide psychological scientists with rich resources"},{"uid":"a5ad17f1-e50d-48ae-83a5-83c3f659982f","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"social spectrum","passagePhrase":"social situation"},{"uid":"6a1696f3-067c-42aa-8e80-29e883c84b93","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"similar results produced by","passagePhrase":"remarkably consistent"},{"uid":"63680f31-1a1e-4658-9261-2ac6f54dd700","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"not met before","passagePhrase":"strangers"},{"uid":"9790cb4b-d6db-4a06-b494-687f685b462a","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"were correct in their predictions","passagePhrase":"Analysis revealed that, as expected"},{"uid":"7b6a38b7-c94a-4af1-931a-e89159047702","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"displaying ... displaying ... produced"},{"uid":"410e355c-3b64-4f63-b604-7c898931d407","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"their way of laughing","passagePhrase":"heir natural dominant laugh or tried to do a submissive one"},{"uid":"403ddeb2-b152-45aa-b500-36a5699e62fe","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"generate","passagePhrase":"eliciting"},{"uid":"90468a47-3081-45fb-9e30-a334a7734be0","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"persisted with the task for longer","passagePhrase":"spending significantly more time working on the task"},{"uid":"788525db-faa3-4c35-be0a-d79cf3aa1df9","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"boring","passagePhrase":"tedious"},{"uid":"c3f5e116-e50c-4c88-90d8-fc10c44ebb05","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"reduces","passagePhrase":"relieve"},{"uid":"b0c31c94-8e5b-42f5-a24d-2399d9b51c35","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"stimulating","passagePhrase":"energising"}]},"reading_u2_253":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><h2><span><strong>Henry Moore (1898-1986)</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>The British sculptor Henry Moore was a leading figure in the 20th-century art world</em></span></p><p><span>Henry Moore was born in Castleford, a small town near Leeds in the north of England. He was the seventh child of Raymond Moore and his wife Mary Baker. He studied at Castleford Grammar School from 1909 to 1915, where his early interest in art was encouraged by his teacher Alice Gostick. After leaving school, Moore hoped to become a sculptor, but instead he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"50cd036d-f25a-4a4b-bca9-14c94aa94671\" data-question=\"1\">complied with his father’s wish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> that he train as a schoolteacher. He had to abandon his training in 1917 when he was sent to France to fight in the First World War.</span></p><p><span>After the war, Moore <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ca850a1-8d56-438a-b2d3-2af9413c9cbb\" data-question=\"2\">enrolled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> at the Leeds School of Art, where he studied for two years. In his first year, he spent most of his time <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"fc1e7522-8a3b-442a-9b47-0bb25eb5cd58\" data-question=\"2\">drawing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Although he wanted to study sculpture, no teacher was appointed until his second year. At the end of that year, he passed the sculpture examination and was awarded a scholarship to the Royal College of Art in London. In September 1921, he moved to London and began three years of advanced study in sculpture.</span></p><p><span>Alongside the instruction he received at the Royal College, Moore visited many of the London museums, particularly the British Museum, which had a wide-ranging collection of ancient sculpture. During these visits, he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dabb4bf1-9bb6-4eca-8af4-8ebf69882c00\" data-question=\"4\">discovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the power and beauty of ancient Egyptian and African sculpture. As he became increasingly interested in these ‘primitive’ forms of art, he turned away from European sculptural traditions.</span></p><p><span>After graduating, Moore spent the first six months of 1925 travelling in France. When he visited the Trocadero Museum in Paris, he was impressed by a cast of a Mayan* sculpture of the rain spirit. It was a male reclining figure with its knees drawn up together, and its head at a right angle to its body. Moore became fascinated with this stone sculpture, which he thought had a power and originality that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"632a0f6d-046a-4247-8ca5-9a0cd7c36a79\" data-question=\"6\">no other stone sculpture possessed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. He himself started carving a variety of subjects in stone, including depiction of reclining women, mother-and-child groups, and masks.</span></p><p><span>Moore’s exceptional talent soon gained recognition, and in 1926 he started work as a sculpture instructor at the Royal College. In 1933, he became a member of a group of young artists called Unit One. The aim of the group was to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02307a86-8ed7-49e0-91e8-698122993673\" data-question=\"7\">convince the English public of the merits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> of the emerging international movement in modern art and architecture.</span></p><p><span>Around this time, Moore moved away from the human figure to experiment with abstract shapes. In 1931, he held an exhibition at the Leicester Galleries in London. His work was enthusiastically welcomed by fellow sculptors, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"813d84fb-b0c9-4411-adb2-0e679d5891fe\" data-question=\"8\">the reviews in the press were extremely negative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> and turned Moore into a notorious figure. There were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b758e559-9a19-420d-bd20-6bed6a800b69\" data-question=\"8\">calls for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> his resignation from the Royal College, and the following year, when his contract expired, he left to start a sculpture department at the Chelsea School of Art in London.</span></p><p><span>Throughout the 1930s, Moore did not show any inclination to please the British public. He became interested in the paintings of the Spanish artist Pablo Picasso, whose work inspired him to distort the human body in a radical way. At times, he seemed to abandon the human figure altogether. The pages of his sketchbooks from this period show his ideas for abstract sculptures that bore little resemblance to the human form.</span></p><p><span>In 1940, during the Second World War, Moore stopped teaching at the Chelsea School and moved to a farmhouse about 20 miles north of London. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d01963d-c93b-46b8-af18-b3a90f063d3d\" data-question=\"9\">shortage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of materials forced him to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca5eb60e-0be9-49a2-b5e2-53433af6a71d\" data-question=\"9\">focus on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> drawing. He did numerous small sketches of Londoners, later turning these ideas into large coloured drawings in his studio. In 1942, he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b398fd47-aa54-40e2-8f0b-4c6eb1d18ffd\" data-question=\"10\">returned to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> Castleford <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f298a455-13ab-4e73-96a4-8cd7be401e87\" data-question=\"10\">to make a series of sketches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> of the miners who worked there.</span></p><p><span>In 1944, Harlow, a town near London, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53f330db-64f7-45a8-b64d-56ee99b41990\" data-question=\"11\">offered Moore a commission for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a sculpture depicting a family. The resulting work signifies a dramatic change in Moore’s style, away from the experimentation of the 1930s towards a more natural and humanistic subject matter. He did dozens of studies in clay for the sculpture, and these were cast in bronze and issued in editions of seven to nine copies each. In this way, Moore’s work <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0dc4576c-d4aa-43ae-ac5a-ea64c5c37d97\" data-question=\"12\">became available to collectors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> all over the world. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7c61cd65-7ce7-48ec-853e-28c5fed89ef7\" data-question=\"13\">boost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to his income <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e509f27-3cad-43b2-8a72-fc37231e144d\" data-question=\"13\">enabled him to take on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> ambitious projects and start working on the scale he felt his sculpture demanded.</span></p><p><span>Critics who had begun to think that Moore had become less revolutionary were proven wrong by the appearance, in 1950, of the first of Moore’s series of standing figures in bronze, with their harsh and angular pierced forms and distinct impression of menace. Moore also varied his subject matter in the 1950s with such works as <em>Warrior with Shield </em>and <em>Falling Warrior</em>. These were rare examples of Moore’s use of the male figure and owe something to his visit to Greece in 1951, when he had the opportunity to study ancient works of art.</span></p><p><span>In his final years, Moore created the Henry Moore Foundation to promote art appreciation and to display his work. Moore was the first modern English sculptor to achieve international critical acclaim and he is still regarded as one of the most important sculptors of the 20th century.</span></p><p><span>—</span></p><p><span>*Mayan: belonging to an ancient civilisation that inhabited parts of current-day Mexico, Guatemala, Belize, El Salvador and Honduras.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>1-7</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"216\" id=\"question-wrapper-216\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> On leaving school, Moore <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"50cd036d-f25a-4a4b-bca9-14c94aa94671\" data-question=\"1\">did what his father wanted him to do<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"217\" id=\"question-wrapper-217\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Moore began <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ca850a1-8d56-438a-b2d3-2af9413c9cbb\" data-question=\"2\">studying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"fc1e7522-8a3b-442a-9b47-0bb25eb5cd58\" data-question=\"2\">sculpture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in his first term at the Leeds School of Art. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"218\" id=\"question-wrapper-218\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When Moore started at the Royal College of Art, its reputation for teaching sculpture was excellent. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"219\" id=\"question-wrapper-219\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Moore <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dabb4bf1-9bb6-4eca-8af4-8ebf69882c00\" data-question=\"4\">became aware<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of ancient sculpture as a result of visiting London Museums. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"220\" id=\"question-wrapper-220\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Trocadero Museum’s Mayan sculpture attracted a lot of public interest. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"221\" id=\"question-wrapper-221\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Moore thought the Mayan sculpture was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"632a0f6d-046a-4247-8ca5-9a0cd7c36a79\" data-question=\"6\">similar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> in certain respects to other stone sculptures. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222\" id=\"question-wrapper-222\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The artists who belonged to Unit One wanted to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02307a86-8ed7-49e0-91e8-698122993673\" data-question=\"7\">make modern art and architecture more popular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>8-13</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>Moore’s career as an artist</strong></span></h4><p><span><strong>1930s</strong></span></p><p><span>● Moore’s exhibition at the Leicester Galleries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"813d84fb-b0c9-4411-adb2-0e679d5891fe\" data-question=\"8\">is criticised by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> the press</span></p><p><span>● Moore is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b758e559-9a19-420d-bd20-6bed6a800b69\" data-question=\"8\">urged to offer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> his <strong>8</strong>………………… and leave the Royal College.</span></p><p><span><strong>1940s</strong></span></p><p><span>● Moore <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca5eb60e-0be9-49a2-b5e2-53433af6a71d\" data-question=\"9\">turns to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> drawing because <strong>9</strong>…………………. for sculpting are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d01963d-c93b-46b8-af18-b3a90f063d3d\" data-question=\"9\">not readily available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></span></p><p><span>● While <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b398fd47-aa54-40e2-8f0b-4c6eb1d18ffd\" data-question=\"10\">visiting his hometown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, Moore <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f298a455-13ab-4e73-96a4-8cd7be401e87\" data-question=\"10\">does some drawings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> of <strong>10</strong>………………….</span></p><p><span>● Moore is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53f330db-64f7-45a8-b64d-56ee99b41990\" data-question=\"11\">employed to produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a sculpture of a <strong>11</strong>…………………</span></p><p><span><strong>● 12</strong>………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0dc4576c-d4aa-43ae-ac5a-ea64c5c37d97\" data-question=\"12\">start to buy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> Moore’s work</span></p><p><span>● Moore’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7c61cd65-7ce7-48ec-853e-28c5fed89ef7\" data-question=\"13\">increased<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> <strong>13</strong>…………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e509f27-3cad-43b2-8a72-fc37231e144d\" data-question=\"13\">makes it possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> for him to do more ambitious sculptures</span></p><p><span><strong>1950s</strong></span></p><p><span>● Moore’s series of bronze figures marks a further change in his style</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223\" id=\"question-wrapper-223\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RESIGNATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"224\" id=\"question-wrapper-224\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MATERIALS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"225\" id=\"question-wrapper-225\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MINERS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"226\" id=\"question-wrapper-226\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FAMILY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"227\" id=\"question-wrapper-227\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COLLECTORS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"228\" id=\"question-wrapper-228\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INCOME</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"50cd036d-f25a-4a4b-bca9-14c94aa94671","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"did what his father wanted him to do","passagePhrase":"complied with his father’s wish"},{"uid":"1ca850a1-8d56-438a-b2d3-2af9413c9cbb","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"studying","passagePhrase":"enrolled"},{"uid":"dabb4bf1-9bb6-4eca-8af4-8ebf69882c00","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"became aware","passagePhrase":"discovered"},{"uid":"02307a86-8ed7-49e0-91e8-698122993673","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"make modern art and architecture more popular","passagePhrase":"convince the English public of the merits"},{"uid":"813d84fb-b0c9-4411-adb2-0e679d5891fe","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"is criticised by","passagePhrase":"the reviews in the press were extremely negative"},{"uid":"b758e559-9a19-420d-bd20-6bed6a800b69","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"urged to offer","passagePhrase":"calls for"},{"uid":"5d01963d-c93b-46b8-af18-b3a90f063d3d","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"not readily available","passagePhrase":"shortage"},{"uid":"ca5eb60e-0be9-49a2-b5e2-53433af6a71d","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"turns to","passagePhrase":"focus on"},{"uid":"b398fd47-aa54-40e2-8f0b-4c6eb1d18ffd","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"visiting his hometown","passagePhrase":"returned to"},{"uid":"f298a455-13ab-4e73-96a4-8cd7be401e87","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"does some drawings","passagePhrase":"to make a series of sketches"},{"uid":"53f330db-64f7-45a8-b64d-56ee99b41990","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"employed to produce","passagePhrase":"offered Moore a commission for"},{"uid":"0dc4576c-d4aa-43ae-ac5a-ea64c5c37d97","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"start to buy","passagePhrase":"became available to collectors"},{"uid":"7c61cd65-7ce7-48ec-853e-28c5fed89ef7","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"increased","passagePhrase":"boost"},{"uid":"0e509f27-3cad-43b2-8a72-fc37231e144d","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"makes it possible","passagePhrase":"enabled him to take on"}]},"reading_u2_254":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below. </p><h2><strong>The Desolenator: producing clean water</strong></h2><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Travelling around Thailand in the 1990s, William Janssen was impressed with the basic rooftop solar heating systems that were on many homes, where energy from the sun was absorbed by a plate and then used to heat water for domestic use. Two decades later Janssen developed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d8e3496-9ff7-4c1c-885d-3cf4433ab0e7\" data-question=\"14\">that basic idea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> he saw in Southeast Asia into a portable device that uses the power from the sun to purify water.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>The Desolenator operates as a mobile desalination unit that can take water from different places, such as the sea, rivers, boreholes and rain, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"754e2c7f-a41b-4c20-acf9-e156953099e7\" data-question=\"15\">purify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> it for human consumption. It is particularly valuable in regions where natural groundwater reserves have been polluted, or where seawater is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7618b935-0562-4081-ad27-1b4bfa47480f\" data-question=\"15\">the only water source<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> available.</p><p>Janssen saw that there was a need for a sustainable way to clean water is both the developing and the developed countries when he moved to the United Arab Emirates and saw large-scale water processing. ‘I was confronted with the enormous carbon footprint that the Gulf nations have because of all of the desalination that they do,’ he says.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>The Desolenator can produce 15 litres of drinking water per day, enough to sustain a family for cooking and drinking. Its main selling point is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dea96ab0-fd0b-4f11-aed2-d4b3347bf0bf\" data-question=\"16\">unlike<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> standard desalination techniques, it doesn’t require a generated power supply: just sunlight. It measures 120 cm by 90 cm, and it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48813b0d-b1c9-4b2e-83bb-39ff4f326c3c\" data-question=\"21\">easy to transport<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, thanks to its two wheels. Water <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd6538c5-301f-4b5f-a9a2-5da68ecf296d\" data-question=\"22\">enters through<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> a pipe, and flows as a thin film between a sheet of double glazing and the surface of a solar panel, where it is heated by the sun. The warm water flows into a small boiler (heated by a solar-powered battery) where it is converted to steam. When the steam cools, it becomes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2fcbce0-9491-4bd7-a5af-10dd3ad679de\" data-question=\"24\">distilled water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. The device has a very simple filter to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4fdc80a-46d9-49cc-b729-c847b54018eb\" data-question=\"23\">trap<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> particles, and this can easily be shaken to remove them. There are two tubes for liquid coming out: one for the waste – salt from seawater, fluoride, etc. – and another for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2fcbce0-9491-4bd7-a5af-10dd3ad679de\" data-question=\"24\">distilled water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. The performance of the unit is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4a3fbedf-2544-486e-aafe-e20df7179cf4\" data-question=\"25\">shown on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> an LCD screen and transmitted to the company which provides servicing when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"381abd91-4ca3-4f31-86ed-aa19fbd3c441\" data-question=\"26\">necessary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>A recent analysis found that at least two-thirds of the world’s population lives with severe water <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74d02df4-b4d0-4af5-89f4-2cf345af2187\" data-question=\"17\">scarcity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> for at least a month every year. Janssen says that be 2030 half of the world’s population will be living with water stress – where the demand exceeds the supply over a certain period of time. ‘It is really important that a sustainable solution is brought to the market that is able to help these people,’ he says. Many countries ‘don’t have the money for desalination plants, which are very expensive to build. They don’t have the money to operate them, they are very maintenance intensive, and they don’t have the money to buy the diesel to run the desalination plants, so it is a really bad situation.’</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>The device is aimed at a wide <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84231531-ed07-44e9-96c0-9cbf2f4dfe36\" data-question=\"18\">variety of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f521fa7f-c7bf-4922-8b5f-9e9d5eafd84d\" data-question=\"18\">users<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> – from homeowners in the developing world who do not have a constant supply of water to people living off the grid in rural parts of the US. The first commercial versions of the Desolenator are expected to be in operation in India early next year, after field tests are carried out. The market for the self-sufficient devices in developing countries is twofold – those who cannot afford the money for the device outright and pay through microfinance, and middle-income homes that can lease their own equipment. ‘People in India don’t pay for a fridge outright; they pay for it over six months. They would put the Desolenator on their roof and hook it up to their municipal supply and they would get very reliable drinking water on a daily basis,’ Janssen says. In the developed world, it is aimed at niche markets where tap water is unavailable – for camping, on boats, or for the military, for instance.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>Prices will vary according to where it is bought. In the developing world, the price will depend on what deal aid organisations can negotiate. In developed countries, it is likely to come in at $1,000 (£685) a unit, said Janssen. ‘We are a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"061dbee1-285c-4dae-a690-5b99820668e3\" data-question=\"19\">venture with a social mission<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. We are aware that the product we have envisioned is mainly finding application in the developing world and humanitarian sector and that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"061dbee1-285c-4dae-a690-5b99820668e3\" data-question=\"19\">this is the way we will proceed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. We do realise, though, that to be a viable company there is a bottom line to keep in mind,’ he says.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>The company itself is based at Imperial College London, although Janssen, its chief executive, still lives in the UAE. It has raised £340,000 in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"453a0bd2-5f13-481f-9466-6f69c04da9e4\" data-question=\"20\">funding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> so far. Within two years, he says, the company aims to be selling 1,000 units a month, mainly in the humanitarian field. They are expected to be sold in areas such as Australia, northern Chile, Peru, Texas and California.</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Reading Passage 2 has nine paragraphs, <strong>A-H</strong></span></p><p><span>Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct number, <strong>i-x</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-20</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>List of Headings</strong></span></p><p><span><strong>i</strong> Getting the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"453a0bd2-5f13-481f-9466-6f69c04da9e4\" data-question=\"20\">finance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> for production</span></p><p><span><strong>ii</strong> An unexpected benefit</span></p><p><span><strong>iii</strong> From initial <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d8e3496-9ff7-4c1c-885d-3cf4433ab0e7\" data-question=\"14\">inspiration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to new product</span></p><p><span><strong>iv</strong> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84231531-ed07-44e9-96c0-9cbf2f4dfe36\" data-question=\"18\">range of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> potential <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f521fa7f-c7bf-4922-8b5f-9e9d5eafd84d\" data-question=\"18\">customers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> for the device</span></p><p><span><strong>v</strong> What makes the device <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dea96ab0-fd0b-4f11-aed2-d4b3347bf0bf\" data-question=\"16\">different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> from alternatives</span></p><p><span><strong>vi</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"754e2c7f-a41b-4c20-acf9-e156953099e7\" data-question=\"15\">Cleaning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> water from <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7618b935-0562-4081-ad27-1b4bfa47480f\" data-question=\"15\">a range of sources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>vii</strong> Overcoming production difficulties</span></p><p><span><strong>viii</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"061dbee1-285c-4dae-a690-5b99820668e3\" data-question=\"19\">Profit not the primary goal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>ix</strong> A warm welcome for the device</span></p><p><span><strong>x</strong> The number of people affected by water <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74d02df4-b4d0-4af5-89f4-2cf345af2187\" data-question=\"17\">shortages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"229\" id=\"question-wrapper-229\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"230\" id=\"question-wrapper-230\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"231\" id=\"question-wrapper-231\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"232\" id=\"question-wrapper-232\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">X</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"233\" id=\"question-wrapper-233\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"234\" id=\"question-wrapper-234\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"235\" id=\"question-wrapper-235\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>21-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>How the Desolenator works</strong></span></h4><p><span>The energy required to operate the Desolenator comes from sunlight. The device can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48813b0d-b1c9-4b2e-83bb-39ff4f326c3c\" data-question=\"21\">be used in different locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, as it has <strong>21</strong>………………… . Water <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd6538c5-301f-4b5f-a9a2-5da68ecf296d\" data-question=\"22\">is fed into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> a pipe, and a <strong>22</strong>………………….. of water flows over a solar panel. The water then enters a boiler, where it turns into steam. Any particles in the water are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4fdc80a-46d9-49cc-b729-c847b54018eb\" data-question=\"23\">caught<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> in a <strong>23</strong>………………… . The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2fcbce0-9491-4bd7-a5af-10dd3ad679de\" data-question=\"24\">purified water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> comes out through one tube, and all types of <strong>24</strong>………………… come out through another. A screen <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4a3fbedf-2544-486e-aafe-e20df7179cf4\" data-question=\"25\">displays<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> the <strong>25</strong>………………… of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67a04bfa-3135-4497-b6a0-2a6789c76716\" data-question=\"25\">device<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, and transmits the information to the company so that they know when the Desolenator <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"381abd91-4ca3-4f31-86ed-aa19fbd3c441\" data-question=\"26\">requires<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <strong>26</strong>…………………. .</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"236\" id=\"question-wrapper-236\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WHEELS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"237\" id=\"question-wrapper-237\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FILM</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"238\" id=\"question-wrapper-238\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FILTER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"239\" id=\"question-wrapper-239\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WASTE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"240\" id=\"question-wrapper-240\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PERFORMANCE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"241\" id=\"question-wrapper-241\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SERVICING</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"4d8e3496-9ff7-4c1c-885d-3cf4433ab0e7","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"inspiration","passagePhrase":"that basic idea"},{"uid":"754e2c7f-a41b-4c20-acf9-e156953099e7","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Cleaning","passagePhrase":"purify"},{"uid":"dea96ab0-fd0b-4f11-aed2-d4b3347bf0bf","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"different","passagePhrase":"unlike"},{"uid":"48813b0d-b1c9-4b2e-83bb-39ff4f326c3c","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"be used in different locations","passagePhrase":"easy to transport"},{"uid":"dd6538c5-301f-4b5f-a9a2-5da68ecf296d","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"is fed into","passagePhrase":"enters through"},{"uid":"a2fcbce0-9491-4bd7-a5af-10dd3ad679de","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"purified water","passagePhrase":"distilled water ... distilled water"},{"uid":"b4fdc80a-46d9-49cc-b729-c847b54018eb","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"caught","passagePhrase":"trap"},{"uid":"4a3fbedf-2544-486e-aafe-e20df7179cf4","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"displays","passagePhrase":"shown on"},{"uid":"381abd91-4ca3-4f31-86ed-aa19fbd3c441","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"requires","passagePhrase":"necessary"},{"uid":"74d02df4-b4d0-4af5-89f4-2cf345af2187","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"shortages","passagePhrase":"scarcity"},{"uid":"84231531-ed07-44e9-96c0-9cbf2f4dfe36","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"range of","passagePhrase":"variety of"},{"uid":"f521fa7f-c7bf-4922-8b5f-9e9d5eafd84d","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"customers","passagePhrase":"users"},{"uid":"061dbee1-285c-4dae-a690-5b99820668e3","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Profit not the primary goal","passagePhrase":"venture with a social mission ... this is the way we will proceed"},{"uid":"453a0bd2-5f13-481f-9466-6f69c04da9e4","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"finance","passagePhrase":"funding"},{"uid":"67a04bfa-3135-4497-b6a0-2a6789c76716","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"device","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_255":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</span></p><p><span></span></p><h2><span><strong>Why fairy tales are really scary tales</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>Some people think that fairy tales are just stories to amuse children, but their universal and enduring appeal may be due to more serious reasons</em></span></p><p><span>People of every culture tell each other fairy tales but the same story often takes a variety of forms in different parts of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"751163b1-afc7-45a0-8c4c-5f778ebc1f49\" data-question=\"27\">world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. In the story of <em>Little Red Riding Hood</em> that European children are familiar with, a young girl on the way to see her grandmother meets a wolf and tells him where she is going. The wolf runs on ahead and disposes of the grandmother, then gets into bed dressed in the grandmother’s clothes to wait for Little Red Riding Hood. You may think you know the story – but which version? In some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e91d1b6f-4956-44d0-b10a-3e857c04104e\" data-question=\"27\">versions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, the wolf swallows up the grandmother, while in others it locks her in a cupboard. In some stories Red Riding Hood gets the better of the wolf on her own, while in others a hunter or a woodcutter hears her cries and comes to her rescue.</span></p><p><span>The universal appeal of these tales is frequently attributed to the idea that they contain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6b87800-835d-43a5-9083-4079689efc93\" data-question=\"28\">cautionary messages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>: in the case of <em>Little Red Riding Hood</em>, to listen to your mother, and avoid talking to strangers. ‘It might be what we find interesting about this story is that it’s got this survival-relevant information in it,’ says anthropologist Jamie Tehrani at Durham University in the UK. But his research suggests otherwise. ‘We have this huge gap in our knowledge about the history and prehistory of storytelling, despite the fact that we know this genre is an incredibly ancient one,’ he says. That hasn’t stopped anthropologists, folklorists* and other academics <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74b8002c-b707-4d67-b25c-83837a0abcfc\" data-question=\"29\">devising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> theories to explain the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"94b2437d-7381-412a-9697-191b3328f054\" data-question=\"29\">importance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of fairy tales in human society. Now Tehrani has found a way to test these ideas, borrowing a technique from evolutionary biologists.</span></p><p><span>To work out the evolutionary history, development and relationships among groups of organisms, biologists compare the characteristics of living species in a process called ‘phylogenetic analysis’. Tehrani has used the same approach to compare related versions of fairy tales to discover how they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8fcee81d-d731-47e9-a65e-f048c5ef860c\" data-question=\"30\">have evolved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> and which elements have survived longest.</span></p><p><span>Tehrani’s analysis focused on <em>Little Red Riding Hood </em>in its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0198ddfd-8b6a-45c0-9391-dfbfc2de9202\" data-question=\"37\">many forms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, which include another Western fairy tale known as <em>The Wolf and the Kids</em>. Checking for variants of these two tales and similar stories from Africa, East Asia and other regions, he ended up with 58 stories recorded from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0c4c8dc-c3f8-442f-aada-a64b50b6b6c2\" data-question=\"31\">oral<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> traditions. Once his phylogenetic analysis had established that they were indeed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"95bd7210-6db3-40f6-8bf0-f8dc90028f41\" data-question=\"32\">related<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, he used the same methods to explore how they have developed and altered over time.</span></p><p><span>First he tested some assumptions about which aspects of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7dbded30-6825-4f31-9aaa-97d48e549831\" data-question=\"33\">the story alter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"153440b4-5c37-4e6e-af75-1eff598a58f3\" data-question=\"33\">least<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> as it evolves, indicating their importance. Folklorists believe that what happens in a story is more central to the story than the characters in it – that visiting a relative, only to be met by a scary animal in disguise, is more fundamental than whether the visitor is a little girl or three siblings, or the animal is a tiger instead of a wolf.</span></p><p><span>However, Tehrani found no significant difference in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c96263f0-6d92-4b30-93b9-599cb1b36428\" data-question=\"34\">rate of evolution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> of incidents compared with that of characters. ‘Certain episodes are very stable because they are crucial to the story, but there are lots of other details that can evolve quite freely,’ he says. Neither did his analysis support the theory that the central section of a story is the most conserved part. He found no significant difference in the flexibility of events there compared with the beginning or the end.</span></p><p><span>But the really big surprise came when he looked at the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b68e97b6-b5dd-46eb-9cd5-99235467b4bb\" data-question=\"35\">cautionary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> elements of the story. ‘Studies on hunter-gatherer folk tales suggest that these narratives include really important information about the environment and the possible dangers that may be faced there – stuff that’s relevant to survival,’ he says. Yet in his analysis such elements were just as flexible as seemingly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10a1c1c4-4272-422f-9609-abfa74dbd070\" data-question=\"35\">trivial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> details. What, then, is important enough to be reproduced from generation to generation?</span></p><p><span>The answer, it would appear, is fear – blood-thirsty and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3f300554-1907-42cc-9ce9-0a3a079844eb\" data-question=\"36\">gruesome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> aspects of the story, such as the eating of the grandmother by the wolf, turned out to be the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78a6faa7-26d3-430f-af91-1139073e933a\" data-question=\"36\">best preserved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of all. Why are these details retained by generations of storytellers, when other features are not? Tehrani has an idea: ‘In an oral context, a story won’t survive because of one great teller. It also needs to be interesting when it’s told by someone who’s not necessarily a great storyteller.’ Maybe being swallowed whole by a wolf, then cut out of its stomach alive is so gripping that it helps the story remain popular, no matter how badly it’s told.</span></p><p><span>Jack Zipes at the University of Minnesota, Minneapolis, is unconvinced by Tehrani’s views on fairy tales. ‘Even if they’re gruesome, they won’t stick unless they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ac21d4b-239f-425a-a970-1ec444a1761c\" data-question=\"38\">matter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>,’ he says. He believes the perennial theme of women as victims in stories like <em>Little Red Riding Hood</em> explains why they continue to feel relevant. But Tehrani <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f574f324-ca0c-4b01-a278-bc9cd584cc0e\" data-question=\"39\">points out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> that although this is often the case in Western versions, it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b209afc-8005-4473-9bd4-977ca584042a\" data-question=\"39\">not always true<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> elsewhere. In Chinese and Japanese versions, often known as <em>The Tiger Grandmother</em>, the villain is a woman, and in both Iran and Nigeria, the victim is a boy.</span></p><p><span>Mathias Clasen at Aarhus University in Denmark isn’t surprised by Tehrani’s findings. ‘Habits and morals change, but the things that scare us, and the fact that we seek out entertainment that’s designed to scare us – those are constant,’ he says. Clasen believes that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70371336-90af-43a1-95cd-c4f1e35ac09e\" data-question=\"40\">scary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> stories teach us what it feels like to be afraid without having to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"38e50dc4-6ab5-4559-9feb-515f70d2d034\" data-question=\"40\">experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> real danger, and so build up resistance to negative emotions.</span></p><p><span>—-</span></p><p><span>*Folklorists: those who study traditional stories</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, <strong>A-F</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-F</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> may be provided through methods used in biological research.</span></p><p><span><strong>B</strong> are the reason for their survival.</span></p><p><span><strong>C</strong> show considerable <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"751163b1-afc7-45a0-8c4c-5f778ebc1f49\" data-question=\"27\">global<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> variation.</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> contain animals which transform to become humans.</span></p><p><span><strong>E </strong> were originally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0c4c8dc-c3f8-442f-aada-a64b50b6b6c2\" data-question=\"31\">spoken<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> rather than written.</span></p><p><span><strong>F</strong> have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74b8002c-b707-4d67-b25c-83837a0abcfc\" data-question=\"29\">developed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> without factual basis.</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"242\" id=\"question-wrapper-242\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In fairy tales, details of the plot </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"243\" id=\"question-wrapper-243\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Tehrani rejects the idea that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6b87800-835d-43a5-9083-4079689efc93\" data-question=\"28\">useful lessons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> for life in fairy tales </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"244\" id=\"question-wrapper-244\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Various theories about the social significance of fairy tales </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"245\" id=\"question-wrapper-245\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Insights into the development of fairy tales </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"246\" id=\"question-wrapper-246\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> All the fairy tales analysed by Tehrani </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, <strong>A-I</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-I</strong>, in boxes <strong>32-36</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>Phylogenetic analysis of <em>Little Red Riding Hood</em></strong></span></h4><p><span>Tehrani used techniques from evolutionary biology to find out if <strong>32</strong>………………….. existed among 58 stories from around the world. He also wanted to know which aspects of the stories had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"153440b4-5c37-4e6e-af75-1eff598a58f3\" data-question=\"33\">fewest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <strong>33</strong>…………………., as he believed these aspects would be the most important ones. Contrary to other beliefs, he found that some <strong>34</strong>……………………. that were included in a story <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c96263f0-6d92-4b30-93b9-599cb1b36428\" data-question=\"34\">tended to change over time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, and that the middle of a story seemed no more important than the other parts. He was also surprised that parts of a story which seemed to provide some sort of <strong>35</strong>…………………. were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10a1c1c4-4272-422f-9609-abfa74dbd070\" data-question=\"35\">unimportant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. The aspect that he found most important in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78a6faa7-26d3-430f-af91-1139073e933a\" data-question=\"36\">story’s survival<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> was <strong>36</strong>…………………</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> ending <strong>B</strong> events <strong>C</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b68e97b6-b5dd-46eb-9cd5-99235467b4bb\" data-question=\"35\">warning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"95bd7210-6db3-40f6-8bf0-f8dc90028f41\" data-question=\"32\">links<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <strong>E</strong> records <strong>F</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7dbded30-6825-4f31-9aaa-97d48e549831\" data-question=\"33\">variations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>G</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3f300554-1907-42cc-9ce9-0a3a079844eb\" data-question=\"36\">horror<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <strong>H</strong> people <strong>I</strong> plot</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"247\" id=\"question-wrapper-247\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"248\" id=\"question-wrapper-248\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"249\" id=\"question-wrapper-249\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"250\" id=\"question-wrapper-250\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"251\" id=\"question-wrapper-251\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>37-40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"252\" id=\"question-wrapper-252\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What method did Jamie Tehrani use to test his ideas about fairy tales? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. He compared oral and written forms of the same stories.</li> <li>B. He looked at many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0198ddfd-8b6a-45c0-9391-dfbfc2de9202\" data-question=\"37\">different forms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> of the same basic story.</li> <li>C. He looked at unrelated stories from many different countries.</li> <li>D. He contrasted the development of fairy tales with that of living creatures.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"253\" id=\"question-wrapper-253\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When discussing Tehrani’s views, Jack Zipes suggests that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Tehrani ignores key changes in the role of women.</li> <li>B. stories which are too horrific are not always taken seriously.</li> <li>C. Tehrani overemphasises the importance of violence in stories.</li> <li>D. features of stories only survive if they have a deeper <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ac21d4b-239f-425a-a970-1ec444a1761c\" data-question=\"38\">significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"254\" id=\"question-wrapper-254\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Why does Tehrani refer to Chinese and Japanese fairy tales? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f574f324-ca0c-4b01-a278-bc9cd584cc0e\" data-question=\"39\">indicate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> that Jack Zipes’ theory is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b209afc-8005-4473-9bd4-977ca584042a\" data-question=\"39\">incorrect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></li> <li>B. to suggest that crime is a global problem</li> <li>C. to imply that all fairy tales have a similar meaning</li> <li>D. to add more evidence for Jack Zipes’ ideas</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"255\" id=\"question-wrapper-255\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does Mathias Clasen believe about fairy tales? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They are a safe way of learning to deal with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70371336-90af-43a1-95cd-c4f1e35ac09e\" data-question=\"40\">fear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> <li>B. They are a type of entertainment that some people avoid.</li> <li>C. They reflect the changing values of our society.</li> <li>D. They reduce our ability to deal with real-world problems.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"751163b1-afc7-45a0-8c4c-5f778ebc1f49","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"global","passagePhrase":"world"},{"uid":"e91d1b6f-4956-44d0-b10a-3e857c04104e","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"versions"},{"uid":"d6b87800-835d-43a5-9083-4079689efc93","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"useful lessons","passagePhrase":"cautionary messages"},{"uid":"74b8002c-b707-4d67-b25c-83837a0abcfc","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"developed","passagePhrase":"devising"},{"uid":"94b2437d-7381-412a-9697-191b3328f054","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"importance"},{"uid":"8fcee81d-d731-47e9-a65e-f048c5ef860c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"have evolved"},{"uid":"0198ddfd-8b6a-45c0-9391-dfbfc2de9202","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"different forms","passagePhrase":"many forms"},{"uid":"f0c4c8dc-c3f8-442f-aada-a64b50b6b6c2","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"spoken","passagePhrase":"oral"},{"uid":"95bd7210-6db3-40f6-8bf0-f8dc90028f41","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"links","passagePhrase":"related"},{"uid":"7dbded30-6825-4f31-9aaa-97d48e549831","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"variations","passagePhrase":"the story alter"},{"uid":"153440b4-5c37-4e6e-af75-1eff598a58f3","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"fewest","passagePhrase":"least"},{"uid":"c96263f0-6d92-4b30-93b9-599cb1b36428","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"tended to change over time","passagePhrase":"rate of evolution"},{"uid":"b68e97b6-b5dd-46eb-9cd5-99235467b4bb","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"warning","passagePhrase":"cautionary"},{"uid":"10a1c1c4-4272-422f-9609-abfa74dbd070","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"unimportant","passagePhrase":"trivial"},{"uid":"3f300554-1907-42cc-9ce9-0a3a079844eb","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"horror","passagePhrase":"gruesome"},{"uid":"78a6faa7-26d3-430f-af91-1139073e933a","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"story’s survival","passagePhrase":"best preserved"},{"uid":"0ac21d4b-239f-425a-a970-1ec444a1761c","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"significance","passagePhrase":"matter"},{"uid":"f574f324-ca0c-4b01-a278-bc9cd584cc0e","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"indicate","passagePhrase":"points out"},{"uid":"8b209afc-8005-4473-9bd4-977ca584042a","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"incorrect","passagePhrase":"not always true"},{"uid":"70371336-90af-43a1-95cd-c4f1e35ac09e","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"fear","passagePhrase":"scary"},{"uid":"38e50dc4-6ab5-4559-9feb-515f70d2d034","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"experience"}]},"reading_u2_256":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on </span><strong>Questions</strong><span> </span><strong>1-13</strong><span> which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><h2><span><strong>The return of the huarango</strong></span></h2><p><span><em>The arid valleys of southern Peru are welcoming the return of a native plant</em></span></p><p><span>The south coast of Peru is a narrow, 2,000-kilometre-long strip of desert squeezed between the Andes and the Pacific Ocean. It is also one of the most fragile ecosystems on Earth. It hardly ever rains there, and the only year-round source of water is located tens of metres below the surface. This is why the huarango tree is so suited to life there: it has the longest roots of any tree in the world. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0858543d-d0c2-4e39-8665-d7b960e1b253\" data-question=\"1\">stretch down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> 50-80 metres and, as well as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e099532-36bb-4475-9947-0a4b34bec357\" data-question=\"1\">sucking up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> water for the tree, they bring it into the higher subsoil, creating a water source for other plant life.</span></p><p><span>Dr David Beresford-Jones, archaeobotanist at Cambridge University, has been studying the role of the huarango tree in landscape change in the Lower Ica Valley in southern Peru. He believes the huarango was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8734e193-1747-456c-8404-cfc53b0034c1\" data-question=\"2\">key<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> to the ancient people’s diet and, because it could reach deep water sources, it allowed local people to withstand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b99b403-cc01-41db-80b9-b4082e3e1c0b\" data-question=\"3\">years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of drought when their other crops failed. But over the centuries huarango trees were gradually replaced with crops. Cutting down native woodland <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5a19f11-1fb4-4494-bda5-92a3c1dc12c6\" data-question=\"4\">leads to erosion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, as there is nothing to keep the soil in place. So when the huarangos go, the land <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee02df6e-09b3-4bd9-b5ec-907642a95e20\" data-question=\"5\">turns into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> a desert. Nothing grows at all in the Lower Ica Valley now.</span></p><p><span>For centuries the huarango tree was vital to the people of the neighbouring Middle Ica Valley too. They grew vegetables under it and ate products made from its seed pods. Its leaves and bark were used for herbal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5d877b4-1625-47cc-a332-0221a72dc4cd\" data-question=\"7\">remedies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, while its branches were used for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"95e1b602-35f2-48b4-9f50-84e6e8bfa6d9\" data-question=\"6\">charcoal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> for cooking and heating, and its trunk was used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59a6aa71-0c67-4d89-a38c-dacc35ac84d5\" data-question=\"8\">build<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> houses. But now it is disappearing rapidly. The majority of the huarango forests in the valley have already been cleared for fuel and agriculture – initially, these were smallholdings, but now they’re huge farms producing crops for the international market.</span></p><p><span>‘Of the forests that were here 1,000 years ago, 99 per cent have already gone,’ says botanist Oliver Whaley from Kew Gardens in London, who, together with ethnobotanist Dr William Milliken, is running a pioneering project to protect and restore the rapidly disappearing habitat. In order to succeed, Whaley needs to get the local people on board, and that has meant overcoming local prejudices. ‘Increasingly aspirational communities think that if you plant food trees in your home or street, it shows you are poor, and still need to grow your own food,’ he says. In order to stop the Middle Ica Valley going the same way as the Lower Ica Valley, Whaley is encouraging locals to love the huarangos again. ‘It’s a process of cultural resuscitation,’ he says. He has already set up a huarango festival to reinstate a sense of pride in their eco-heritage, and has helped local schoolchildren plant thousands of trees.</span></p><p><span>‘In order to get people interested in habitat restoration, you need to plant a tree that is useful to them,’ says Whaley. So, he has been working with local families to attempt to create a sustainable income from the huarangos by turning their products into foodstuffs. ‘Boil up the beans and you get this thick brown syrup like molasses. You can also use it in drinks, soups or stews.’ The pods can be ground into flour to make cakes, and the seeds roasted into a sweet, chocolatey ‘coffee’. ‘It’s packed full of vitamins and minerals,’ Whaley says.</span></p><p><span>And some farmers are already <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2cb7d51a-a2f0-4368-a676-3371f8b0862c\" data-question=\"10\">planting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> huarangos. Alberto Benevides, owner of Ica Valley’s only certified organic farm, which Whaley helped set up, has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2cb7d51a-a2f0-4368-a676-3371f8b0862c\" data-question=\"10\">planting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> the tree for 13 years. He produces syrup and flour, and sells these products at an organic farmers’ market in Lima. His farm is relatively small and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"80cd585b-9aa3-4896-8f7f-1a7c267e02b9\" data-question=\"10\">doesn’t yet provide him with enough to live on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, but he hopes this will change. ‘The organic market is growing rapidly in Peru,’ Benevides says. ‘I am investing in the future.’</span></p><p><span>But even if Whaley can convince the local people to fall in love with the huarango again, there is still the threat of the larger farms. Some of these cut across the forests and break up the corridors that allow the essential movement of mammals, birds and pollen up and down the narrow forest strip. In the hope of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf423438-d40d-4479-babe-3565a8f516c0\" data-question=\"11\">counteracting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> this, he’s persuading farmers to let him plant forest corridors on their land. He believes the extra woodland will also benefit the farms by reducing their water usage through a lowering of evaporation and providing a refuge for bio-control insects.</span></p><p><span>‘If we can record biodiversity and see how it all works, then we’re in a good position to move on from there. Desert habitats can reduce down to very little,’ Whaley explains. ‘It’s <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ef80598b-74d3-43fc-aa1d-954c99301653\" data-question=\"12\">not like<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> a rainforest that needs to have this huge <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d216d1c6-59d2-4a57-a31f-1fd2f7de3f35\" data-question=\"12\">expanse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. Life has always been confined to corridors and islands here. If you just have a few trees left, the population can grow up quickly because it’s used to exploiting water when it arrives.’ He sees his project as a model that has the potential to be rolled out across other arid areas around the world. ‘If we can do it here, in the most fragile system on Earth, then that’s a real message of hope for lots of places, including Africa, where there is drought and they just can’t afford to wait for rain.’</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answer in boxes <strong>1-5</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>The importance of the huarango tree</strong></span></h4><p><span>– its roots can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0858543d-d0c2-4e39-8665-d7b960e1b253\" data-question=\"1\">extend<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> as far as 80 metres into the soil</span></p><p><span>– can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e099532-36bb-4475-9947-0a4b34bec357\" data-question=\"1\">access<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <strong>1</strong>………………… deep below the surface</span></p><p><span>– was a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8734e193-1747-456c-8404-cfc53b0034c1\" data-question=\"2\">crucial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> part of local inhabitants’ <strong>2</strong>………………… a long time ago</span></p><p><span>– helped people to survive <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b99b403-cc01-41db-80b9-b4082e3e1c0b\" data-question=\"3\">periods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> of <strong>3</strong>…………………..</span></p><p><span>– prevents <strong>4</strong>………………… of the soil</span></p><p><span>– prevents land from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee02df6e-09b3-4bd9-b5ec-907642a95e20\" data-question=\"5\">becoming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> a <strong>5</strong>…………………</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21125\" id=\"question-wrapper-21125\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WATER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21126\" id=\"question-wrapper-21126\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DIET</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21127\" id=\"question-wrapper-21127\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DROUGHT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21128\" id=\"question-wrapper-21128\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EROSION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21129\" id=\"question-wrapper-21129\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DESERT</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the table below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>6-8</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" width=\"456\"><h4><span><strong>Traditional uses of the huarango tree</strong></span></h4></td></tr><tr><td width=\"222\"><p><span>Part of tree</span></p></td><td width=\"234\"><p><span>Traditional use</span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"222\"><p><span><strong>6</strong>………………..</span></p></td><td width=\"234\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"95e1b602-35f2-48b4-9f50-84e6e8bfa6d9\" data-question=\"6\">Fuel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"222\"><p><span><strong>7</strong>………………. and ……………….</span></p></td><td width=\"234\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5d877b4-1625-47cc-a332-0221a72dc4cd\" data-question=\"7\">Medicine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td width=\"222\"><p><span><strong>8</strong>………………</span></p></td><td width=\"234\"><p><span><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59a6aa71-0c67-4d89-a38c-dacc35ac84d5\" data-question=\"8\">construction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21130\" id=\"question-wrapper-21130\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(ITS/HUARANGO/THE) BRANCHES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21131\" id=\"question-wrapper-21131\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LEAVES + BARK</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21132\" id=\"question-wrapper-21132\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(ITS/HUARANGO/THE) TRUNK</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>9-13</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21133\" id=\"question-wrapper-21133\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Local families have told Whaley about some traditional uses of huarango products. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21134\" id=\"question-wrapper-21134\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Farmer Alberto Benevides is now <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"80cd585b-9aa3-4896-8f7f-1a7c267e02b9\" data-question=\"10\">making a good profit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> from growing huarangos. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21135\" id=\"question-wrapper-21135\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Whaley needs the co-operation of farmers to help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf423438-d40d-4479-babe-3565a8f516c0\" data-question=\"11\">preserve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the area’s wildlife. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21136\" id=\"question-wrapper-21136\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> For Whaley’s project to succeed, it <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ef80598b-74d3-43fc-aa1d-954c99301653\" data-question=\"12\">needs to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d216d1c6-59d2-4a57-a31f-1fd2f7de3f35\" data-question=\"12\">extended<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> over a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1f7ccb70-a965-4416-84d7-24a551d33733\" data-question=\"12\">very large<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> area. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21137\" id=\"question-wrapper-21137\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Whaley has plans to go to Africa to set up a similar project. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0858543d-d0c2-4e39-8665-d7b960e1b253","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"extend","passagePhrase":"stretch down"},{"uid":"0e099532-36bb-4475-9947-0a4b34bec357","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"access","passagePhrase":"sucking up"},{"uid":"8734e193-1747-456c-8404-cfc53b0034c1","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"crucial","passagePhrase":"key"},{"uid":"7b99b403-cc01-41db-80b9-b4082e3e1c0b","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"periods","passagePhrase":"years"},{"uid":"b5a19f11-1fb4-4494-bda5-92a3c1dc12c6","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"leads to erosion"},{"uid":"ee02df6e-09b3-4bd9-b5ec-907642a95e20","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"becoming","passagePhrase":"turns into"},{"uid":"b5d877b4-1625-47cc-a332-0221a72dc4cd","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"Medicine","passagePhrase":"remedies"},{"uid":"95e1b602-35f2-48b4-9f50-84e6e8bfa6d9","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Fuel","passagePhrase":"charcoal"},{"uid":"59a6aa71-0c67-4d89-a38c-dacc35ac84d5","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"construction","passagePhrase":"build"},{"uid":"2cb7d51a-a2f0-4368-a676-3371f8b0862c","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"planting ... planting"},{"uid":"cf423438-d40d-4479-babe-3565a8f516c0","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"preserve","passagePhrase":"counteracting"},{"uid":"d216d1c6-59d2-4a57-a31f-1fd2f7de3f35","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"extended","passagePhrase":"expanse"},{"uid":"1f7ccb70-a965-4416-84d7-24a551d33733","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"very large","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_257":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p><span>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</span><span> </span></p><h2><span><strong>Silbo Gomero – the whistle ‘language’ of the Canary Islands</strong></span></h2><p><span>La Gomera is one of the Canary Islands situated in the Atlantic Ocean off the northwest coast of Africa. This small volcanic island is mountainous, with steep rocky slopes and deep, wooded ravines, rising to 1,487 metres at its highest peak. It is also home to the best known of the world’s whistle ‘languages’, a means of transmitting information over long distances which is perfectly adapted to the extreme terrain of the island.</span></p><p><span>This ‘language’, known as ‘Silbo’ or ‘Silbo Gomero’ – from the Spanish word for ‘whistle’ – is now shedding light on the language-processing abilities of the human brain, according to scientists. Researchers say that Silbo activates parts of the brain normally associated with spoken language, suggesting that the brain is remarkably flexible in its ability to interpret sounds as language.</span></p><p><span>‘Science has developed the idea of brain areas that are dedicated to language, and we are starting to understand the scope of signals that can be recognised as language,’ says David Corina, co-author of a recent study and associate professor of psychology at the University of Washington in Seattle.</span></p><p><span>Silbo is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe6893c1-5df6-4856-a01f-4a10c5f72df4\" data-question=\"20\">a substitute for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> Spanish, with individual words recoded into whistles which have high- and low-frequency tones. A whistler – or <em>silbador </em>– puts a finger in his or her mouth <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f68fdb4-0dba-4fb9-9350-a677865bbcbc\" data-question=\"21\">to increase the whistle’s pitch<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, while the other hand can be cupped <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb28e16c-ea26-40fe-b703-4ca78f2ca306\" data-question=\"22\">to adjust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the direction of the sound. ‘There is much more ambiguity in the whistled signal than in the spoken signal,’ explains lead researcher Manuel Carreiras, psychology professor at the University of La Laguna on the Canary island of Tenerife. Because whistled ‘words’ can be hard to distinguish, silbadores rely on repetition, as well as awareness of context, to make themselves understood.</span></p><p><span>The silbadores of Gomera are traditionally shepherds and other isolated mountain folk, and their novel means of staying in touch allows them to communicate over distances of up to 10 kilometres. Carreiras explains that silbadores are able to pass a surprising amount of information via their whistles. ‘In daily life they use <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5522c62-2ded-4382-b955-f2a4bfc338ce\" data-question=\"15\">whistles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> to communicate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff83cd45-1020-4147-ab4d-ad6dfdd1cfab\" data-question=\"15\">short commands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, but <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"30142834-3882-4bb1-8e21-6c1d2e98f8e8\" data-question=\"15\">any Spanish sentence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> could be whistled.’ Silbo has proved particularly useful when fires have occurred on the island and rapid <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"640502bd-b417-4376-8574-1545c784603c\" data-question=\"24\">communication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> across large areas has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64326a1c-7e9a-42ed-bb30-6cce9b2d467e\" data-question=\"24\">vital<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</span></p><p><span>The study team used neuroimaging equipment to contrast the brain activity of silbadores while listening to whistled and spoken Spanish. Results showed the left temporal lobe of the brain, which is usually associated with spoken language, was engaged during the processing of Silbo. The researchers found that other key regions in the brain’s frontal lobe also responded to the whistles, including those activated in response to sign language among deaf people. When the experiments were repeated with non-whistlers, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5bc41bcb-21fd-43be-89f1-bd4ff4267a86\" data-question=\"16\">however, activation was observed in all areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of the brain.</span></p><p><span>‘Our results provide more evidence about the flexibility of human capacity for language in a variety of forms,’ Corina says. ‘These data suggest that left-hemisphere language regions are uniquely adapted for communicative purposes, independent of the modality of signal. The non-Silbo speakers were not recognising Silbo as a language. They had nothing to grab onto, so multiple areas of their brains were activated.’</span></p><p><span>Carreiras says the origins of Silbo Gomero remain obscure, but that indigenous Canary Islanders, who were of North African origin, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"5f272e30-172c-4de2-82ad-805e05b1f783\" data-question=\"17\">already had a whistled language<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> when Spain conquered the volcanic islands in the 15th century. Whistled languages survive today in Papua New Guinea, Mexico, Vietnam, Guyana, China, Nepal, Senegal, and a few mountainous pockets in southern Europe. There are thought to be as many as 70 whistled languages <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bb7502c0-07ec-489b-b510-9b019f97d0c9\" data-question=\"18\">still in use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, though <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4b33a7c4-ade9-496d-bb1c-5326bf53a0d7\" data-question=\"18\">only 12<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> have been described and studied scientifically. This form of communication is an adaptation found among cultures where people are often isolated from each other, according to Julien Meyer, a researcher at the Institute of Human Sciences in Lyon, France. ‘They are mostly used in mountains or dense forests,’ he says. ‘Whistled languages are quite clearly defined and represent an original adaptation of the spoken language for the needs of isolated human groups.’</span></p><p><span>But with modern communication technology now widely available, researchers say whistled languages like Silbo are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1e8a74e-ccc2-41da-af9a-7c7a1caec68c\" data-question=\"25\">threatened<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> with extinction. With dwindling numbers of Gomera islanders still fluent in the language, Canaries’ authorities are taking steps to try to ensure its survival. Since 1999, Silbo Gomero <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e97daac-9b90-4f7e-8aa8-0488df5dd155\" data-question=\"19\">has been taught<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in all of the island’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fec65a07-0764-430a-8fc7-6c5942402977\" data-question=\"19\">elementary schools<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. In addition, locals are seeking assistance from the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNESCO). ‘The local authorities are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fda53ab4-e53a-45f8-aae5-e88b230fe0e0\" data-question=\"26\">trying to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2537febf-c623-40e3-8758-f1a1cfccec28\" data-question=\"26\">get<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> an award from the organisation to declare [Silbo Gomero] as something that should be preserved for humanity,’ Carreiras adds.</span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p><p><span><strong></strong></span></p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>14-19</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21138\" id=\"question-wrapper-21138\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> La Gomera is the most mountainous of all the Canary Islands. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21139\" id=\"question-wrapper-21139\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Silbo is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"30142834-3882-4bb1-8e21-6c1d2e98f8e8\" data-question=\"15\">only appropriate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> for short and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff83cd45-1020-4147-ab4d-ad6dfdd1cfab\" data-question=\"15\">simple messages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21140\" id=\"question-wrapper-21140\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the brain-activity study, silbadores and non-whistlers produced <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5bc41bcb-21fd-43be-89f1-bd4ff4267a86\" data-question=\"16\">different results.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21141\" id=\"question-wrapper-21141\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Spanish <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"5f272e30-172c-4de2-82ad-805e05b1f783\" data-question=\"17\">introduced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> Silbo to the islands in the 15th century. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21142\" id=\"question-wrapper-21142\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is precise data available <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4b33a7c4-ade9-496d-bb1c-5326bf53a0d7\" data-question=\"18\">regarding all<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of the whistle languages <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bb7502c0-07ec-489b-b510-9b019f97d0c9\" data-question=\"18\">in existence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> today. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21143\" id=\"question-wrapper-21143\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fec65a07-0764-430a-8fc7-6c5942402977\" data-question=\"19\">children<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of Gomera now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e97daac-9b90-4f7e-8aa8-0488df5dd155\" data-question=\"19\">learn<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> Silbo. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</span></p><p><span><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>20-26</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>Silbo Gomero</strong></span></h4><p><span><strong>How Silbo is produced</strong></span></p><p><span>● high- and low-frequency tones <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe6893c1-5df6-4856-a01f-4a10c5f72df4\" data-question=\"20\">represent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> different sounds in Spanish <strong>20</strong>……………</span></p><p><span>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f68fdb4-0dba-4fb9-9350-a677865bbcbc\" data-question=\"21\">pitch of whistle is controlled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> using silbador’s <strong>21</strong>……………</span></p><p><span><strong>● 22</strong>………….. is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb28e16c-ea26-40fe-b703-4ca78f2ca306\" data-question=\"22\">changed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> with a cupped hand</span></p><p><span><strong>How Silbo is used</strong></span></p><p><span>● has long been used by shepherds and people living in secluded locations</span></p><p><span>● in everyday use for the transmission of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ec29ae3-9d54-419c-8785-b3ec41e48342\" data-question=\"23\">brief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <strong>23</strong>……………</span></p><p><span>● can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"640502bd-b417-4376-8574-1545c784603c\" data-question=\"24\">relay<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64326a1c-7e9a-42ed-bb30-6cce9b2d467e\" data-question=\"24\">essential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> information quickly, e.g. to inform people about <strong>24</strong>……………</span></p><p><span><strong>The future of Silbo</strong></span></p><p><span>● future <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1e8a74e-ccc2-41da-af9a-7c7a1caec68c\" data-question=\"25\">under threat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> because of new <strong>25</strong>……………</span></p><p><span>● Canaries’ authorities <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fda53ab4-e53a-45f8-aae5-e88b230fe0e0\" data-question=\"26\">hoping to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2537febf-c623-40e3-8758-f1a1cfccec28\" data-question=\"26\">receive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> a UNESCO <strong>26</strong>……………. to help preserve it</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21146\" id=\"question-wrapper-21146\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WORDS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21147\" id=\"question-wrapper-21147\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FINGER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21148\" id=\"question-wrapper-21148\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DIRECTION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21254\" id=\"question-wrapper-21254\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMMANDS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21255\" id=\"question-wrapper-21255\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FIRES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21260\" id=\"question-wrapper-21260\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TECHNOLOGY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21257\" id=\"question-wrapper-21257\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AWARD</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"fe6893c1-5df6-4856-a01f-4a10c5f72df4","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"represent","passagePhrase":"a substitute for"},{"uid":"9f68fdb4-0dba-4fb9-9350-a677865bbcbc","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"pitch of whistle is controlled","passagePhrase":"to increase the whistle’s pitch"},{"uid":"fb28e16c-ea26-40fe-b703-4ca78f2ca306","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"changed","passagePhrase":"to adjust"},{"uid":"e5522c62-2ded-4382-b955-f2a4bfc338ce","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"whistles"},{"uid":"ff83cd45-1020-4147-ab4d-ad6dfdd1cfab","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"simple messages","passagePhrase":"short commands"},{"uid":"640502bd-b417-4376-8574-1545c784603c","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"relay","passagePhrase":"communication"},{"uid":"64326a1c-7e9a-42ed-bb30-6cce9b2d467e","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"essential","passagePhrase":"vital"},{"uid":"5bc41bcb-21fd-43be-89f1-bd4ff4267a86","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"different results.","passagePhrase":"however, activation was observed in all areas"},{"uid":"bb7502c0-07ec-489b-b510-9b019f97d0c9","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"in existence","passagePhrase":"still in use"},{"uid":"b1e8a74e-ccc2-41da-af9a-7c7a1caec68c","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"under threat","passagePhrase":"threatened"},{"uid":"5e97daac-9b90-4f7e-8aa8-0488df5dd155","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"learn","passagePhrase":"has been taught"},{"uid":"fec65a07-0764-430a-8fc7-6c5942402977","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"children","passagePhrase":"elementary schools"},{"uid":"fda53ab4-e53a-45f8-aae5-e88b230fe0e0","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"hoping to","passagePhrase":"trying to"},{"uid":"2537febf-c623-40e3-8758-f1a1cfccec28","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"receive","passagePhrase":"get"},{"uid":"3ec29ae3-9d54-419c-8785-b3ec41e48342","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"brief","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_258":{"leftHtml":"<div><div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong> which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</p><p> </p><h2><strong>Environmental practices of big businesses</strong></h2><p>The environmental practices of big businesses are shaped by a fundamental fact that for many of us offend our sense of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5a04b36-139b-4e15-b62c-3113a60f6d96\" data-question=\"27\">justice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Depending on the circumstances, a business may maximize the amount of money it makes, at least in the short term, by damaging the environment and hurting people. That is still the case today for fishermen in an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a35e3514-c84d-4770-bca5-b09d46bb1fb8\" data-question=\"30\">unmanaged fishery without quotas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, and for international <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac0295c7-944e-4ef9-bcce-c5bdbe8d5d2f\" data-question=\"31\">logging companies with short-term leases on tropical rainforest land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in places with corrupt officials and unsophisticated landowners. When government regulation is effective, and when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"381bfc13-9002-4c93-a720-2a8aafbe2f84\" data-question=\"29\">the public is environmentally aware<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, environmentally clean big businesses may out-compete dirty ones, but the reverse <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3285a07f-3c5b-4714-b28e-a8a8d0997b5e\" data-question=\"28\">is likely to be true<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> if government regulation is ineffective and if the public doesn’t care.</p><p>It is easy for the rest of us to blame a business for helping itself by hurting other people. But blaming alone is unlikely to produce change. It ignores the fact that businesses are not charities but profit-making companies, and that publicly owned companies with shareholders are under obligation to those shareholders to maximize profits, provided that they do so by legal means. US laws make a company’s directors legally liable for something termed ‘breach of fiduciary responsibility’ if they knowingly manage a company in a way that reduces profits. The car manufacturer Henry Ford was in fact successfully sued by shareholders in 1919 for raising the minimum wage of his workers to $5 per day: the courts declared that, while Ford’s humanitarian sentiments about his employees were nice, his business existed to make profits for its stockholders.</p><p>Our blaming of businesses also ignores the ultimate responsibility of the public for creating the condition that let a business profit through <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"376b7659-ec36-47e9-9257-dfd0d6bb9dae\" data-question=\"32\">destructive environmental<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> policies. In the long run, it is the public, either directly or through its politicians, that has the power to make such destructive policies unprofitable and illegal, and to make sustainable environmental policies profitable.</p><p>The public can do that by suing businesses for harming them, as happened after the Exxon Valdez disaster, in which over 40,000m<sup>3</sup> of oil were spilled off the coast of Alaska. The public may also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"576d402f-61a0-48b4-8b44-724eb81a1516\" data-question=\"33\">make their opinion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> felt by preferring to buy sustainably harvested products; by making employees of companies with poor track records feel ashamed of their company and complain to their own management; by preferring their governments to award valuable contracts to businesses with a good environmental track record; and by pressing their governments to pass and enforce laws and regulations requiring good environmental practices.</p><p>In turn, big businesses can exert powerful pressure on any suppliers that might ignore public or government pressure. For instance, after the US public became concerned about the spread of a disease known as BSE, which was transmitted to humans through infected meat, the US government’s Food and Drug Administration introduced rules <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79525e8d-515e-4129-bd1b-5a31b49828fe\" data-question=\"34\">demanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> that the meat industry abandon practices associated with the risk of the disease spreading. But for five years the meat packers refused to follow these, claiming that they would be too expensive to obey. However, when a major fast-food company then made the same demands after customer purchases of its hamburgers plummeted, the meat industry <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68491d8d-5cc7-4667-9880-fb5369c7ebc2\" data-question=\"34\">complied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> within weeks. The public’s task is therefore to identify which links in the supply chain are sensitive to public pressure: for instance, fast-food chains or jewelry stores, but not meat packers or gold miners.</p><p>Some readers may be disappointed or outraged that I place the ultimate responsibility for business practices harming the public on the public itself. I also believe that the public must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f2344cd-4f20-4fb9-860a-f1e1406aa07b\" data-question=\"35\">accept the necessity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b99f314c-8946-4706-9e2a-a3ed82b28c02\" data-question=\"35\">higher prices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> for products to cover the added costs, if any, of sound environmental practices. My views may seem to ignore the belief that businesses should act in accordance with moral principles even if this leads to a reduction in their profits. But I think we have to recognize that, throughout human history, in all politically complex human societies, government regulation has arisen precisely because it was found that not only did moral principles need to be made explicit, they also needed to be enforced.</p><p>To me, the conclusion that the public has the ultimate responsibility for the behavior of even the biggest businesses is empowering and hopeful, rather than disappointing. My conclusion is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8189ef88-2d25-45fc-9624-eec94c3e2f65\" data-question=\"37\">not a moralistic one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3245b8cc-2b76-4dde-a059-dd866092f772\" data-question=\"37\">who is right or wrong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3245b8cc-2b76-4dde-a059-dd866092f772\" data-question=\"37\">admirable or selfish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3245b8cc-2b76-4dde-a059-dd866092f772\" data-question=\"37\">a good guy or a bad guy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. In the past, businesses have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5195212b-9726-46f6-986d-92210a4f221f\" data-question=\"38\">changed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> when the public came to expect and require different behavior, to reward businesses for behavior that the public wanted, and to make things difficult for businesses practicing behaviors that the public didn’t want. I predict that in the future, just as in the past, changes in public attitudes will be essential for changes in businesses’ environmental practices.</p><p> </p><p> </p></div></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of words, <strong>A-J</strong>, below.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-J</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-31</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p><h4><span><strong>Big businesses</strong></span></h4><p><span>Many big businesses today are prepared to harm people and the environment in order to make money, and they appear to have no <strong>27</strong>………………. . Lack of <strong>28</strong>……………….. by governments and lack of public <strong>29</strong>………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3285a07f-3c5b-4714-b28e-a8a8d0997b5e\" data-question=\"28\">can lead to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> environmental problems such as <strong>30</strong>……………….. or the destruction of <strong>31</strong>……………….</span></p><p><span><strong>A</strong> funding <strong>B</strong> trees <strong>C</strong> rare species</span></p><p><span><strong>D</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5a04b36-139b-4e15-b62c-3113a60f6d96\" data-question=\"27\">moral standards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <strong>E</strong> control <strong>F </strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"381bfc13-9002-4c93-a720-2a8aafbe2f84\" data-question=\"29\">involvement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></span></p><p><span><strong>G </strong> flooding <strong>H</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a35e3514-c84d-4770-bca5-b09d46bb1fb8\" data-question=\"30\">overfishing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <strong>I</strong> worker support</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21149\" id=\"question-wrapper-21149\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21150\" id=\"question-wrapper-21150\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21151\" id=\"question-wrapper-21151\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21152\" id=\"question-wrapper-21152\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21153\" id=\"question-wrapper-21153\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in boxes <strong>32-34</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21154\" id=\"question-wrapper-21154\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The main idea of the third paragraph is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"376b7659-ec36-47e9-9257-dfd0d6bb9dae\" data-question=\"32\">environmental damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. requires political action if it is to be stopped.</li> <li>B. is the result of ignorance on the part of the public.</li> <li>C. could be prevented by the action of ordinary people.</li> <li>D. can only be stopped by educating business leaders.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21155\" id=\"question-wrapper-21155\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the fourth paragraph, the writer describes ways in which the public can </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. reduce their own individual impact on the environment.</li> <li>B. learn more about the impact of business of the environment.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"576d402f-61a0-48b4-8b44-724eb81a1516\" data-question=\"33\">raise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> awareness of the effects of specific environmental disasters.</li> <li>D. influence the environmental policies of businesses and governments.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21156\" id=\"question-wrapper-21156\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What pressure was exerted by big business in the case of the disease BSE? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Meat packers stopped supplying hamburgers to fast-food chains.</li> <li>B. A fast-food company <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79525e8d-515e-4129-bd1b-5a31b49828fe\" data-question=\"34\">forced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> their meat suppliers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68491d8d-5cc7-4667-9880-fb5369c7ebc2\" data-question=\"34\">follow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the law.</li> <li>C. Meat packers persuaded the government to reduce their expenses.</li> <li>D. A fast-food company encouraged the government to introduce legislation.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span><em>In boxes <strong>35-39</strong> on your answer sheet, write</em></span></p><p><span><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span><strong>NOT</strong> <strong>GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21157\" id=\"question-wrapper-21157\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The public should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f2344cd-4f20-4fb9-860a-f1e1406aa07b\" data-question=\"35\">be prepared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> to fund good environmental practices. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21158\" id=\"question-wrapper-21158\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is a contrast between the moral principles of different businesses. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21159\" id=\"question-wrapper-21159\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8189ef88-2d25-45fc-9624-eec94c3e2f65\" data-question=\"37\">important to make a clear distinction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3245b8cc-2b76-4dde-a059-dd866092f772\" data-question=\"37\">acceptable and unacceptable behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21160\" id=\"question-wrapper-21160\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The public have successfully <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5195212b-9726-46f6-986d-92210a4f221f\" data-question=\"38\">influenced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> businesses in the past. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21161\" id=\"question-wrapper-21161\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the future, businesses will show more concern for the environment. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>.</span></p><p><span><em>Write the correct letter in box <strong>40</strong> on your answer sheet.</em></span></p></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"21162\" id=\"question-wrapper-21162\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What would be the best subheading for this passage? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Will the world survive the threat caused by big businesses?</li> <li>B. How can big businesses be encouraged to be less driven by profit?</li> <li>C. What environmental dangers are caused by the greed of businesses?</li> <li>D. Are big businesses to blame for the damage they cause the environment?</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a5a04b36-139b-4e15-b62c-3113a60f6d96","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"moral standards","passagePhrase":"justice"},{"uid":"a35e3514-c84d-4770-bca5-b09d46bb1fb8","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"overfishing","passagePhrase":"unmanaged fishery without quotas"},{"uid":"ac0295c7-944e-4ef9-bcce-c5bdbe8d5d2f","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"logging companies with short-term leases on tropical rainforest land"},{"uid":"381bfc13-9002-4c93-a720-2a8aafbe2f84","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"involvement","passagePhrase":"the public is environmentally aware"},{"uid":"3285a07f-3c5b-4714-b28e-a8a8d0997b5e","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"can lead to","passagePhrase":"is likely to be true"},{"uid":"376b7659-ec36-47e9-9257-dfd0d6bb9dae","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"environmental damage","passagePhrase":"destructive environmental"},{"uid":"576d402f-61a0-48b4-8b44-724eb81a1516","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"raise","passagePhrase":"make their opinion"},{"uid":"79525e8d-515e-4129-bd1b-5a31b49828fe","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"forced","passagePhrase":"demanding"},{"uid":"68491d8d-5cc7-4667-9880-fb5369c7ebc2","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"follow","passagePhrase":"complied"},{"uid":"7f2344cd-4f20-4fb9-860a-f1e1406aa07b","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"be prepared","passagePhrase":"accept the necessity"},{"uid":"b99f314c-8946-4706-9e2a-a3ed82b28c02","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"higher prices"},{"uid":"3245b8cc-2b76-4dde-a059-dd866092f772","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"acceptable and unacceptable behaviour","passagePhrase":"who is right or wrong ... admirable or selfish ... a good guy or a bad guy"},{"uid":"5195212b-9726-46f6-986d-92210a4f221f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"influenced","passagePhrase":"changed"}]},"reading_u2_259":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 1-13</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 1 given below</em>.</p><h2>Why we need to protect polar bears</h2><p>Polar bears are being increasingly threatened by the effects of climate change, but their disappearance could have far-reaching consequences. They are uniquely adapted to the extreme conditions of the Arctic Circle, where temperatures can reach —40°C. One reason for this is that they have up to 11 centimetres of fat underneath their skin. Humans with comparative levels of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f95bba59-f97d-40fa-aa86-451b8948af38\" data-question=\"1\">adipose tissue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> would be considered obese and would be likely to suffer from diabetes and heart disease. Yet the polar bear experiences <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8fbedf06-12ba-440a-99ed-e887466f8ed5\" data-question=\"1\">no such consequences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.<br><br>A 2014 study by Shi Ping Liu and colleagues sheds light on this mystery. They compared the genetic structure of <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"04462922-cffd-413f-833d-7d4db9f98b89\" data-question=\"2\">polar bears with that of their closest relatives from a warmer climate, the brown bears.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> This allowed them to determine the genes that have allowed polar bears to survive in one of the toughest environments on Earth. Liu and his colleagues found the polar bears <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3cb14a69-3681-414a-bfa8-f6fb3747bf87\" data-question=\"4\">had a gene<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> known as APoB, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4d796a6-9825-4748-93e9-cf002bb0e1d3\" data-question=\"4\">reduces levels of low-density lipoproteins (LDLs)<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> — a form of ‘bad’ cholesterol. In humans, mutations of this gene are associated with increased risk of heart disease. Polar bears may therefore be an important study model to understand heart disease in humans.<br><br>The genome of the polar bear may also provide the solution for another condition, one that particularly affects our older generation: osteoporosis. This is a disease where bones show reduced density, usually caused by insufficient exercise, reduced calcium intake or food starvation. Bone tissue is constantly being remodelled, meaning that bone is added or removed, depending on nutrient availability and the stress that the bone is under. Female polar bears, however, undergo extreme conditions during every pregnancy. Once autumn comes around, these females will dig maternity dens in the snow and will remain there throughout the winter, both before and after the birth of their cubs. This process results in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a9cbeb7-4d07-4f29-86d5-e31a3f8c3475\" data-question=\"5\">about six months of fasting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, where the female bears have to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8737cd00-f1ef-40fe-97cb-a567b931fb5d\" data-question=\"5\">keep themselves and their cubs alive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, depleting their own calcium and calorie reserves. Despite this, their bones remain <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4a53d425-6823-4c55-a903-9a219674e7d9\" data-question=\"6\">strong and dense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.<br><br>Physiologists Alanda Lennox and Allen Goodship found an explanation for this paradox in 2008. They discovered that pregnant bears were able to increase the density of their bones before they started to build their dens. In addition, six months later, when they finally emerged from the den with their cubs, there was no evidence of significant loss of bone density. Hibernating brown bears do not have this capacity and must therefore resort to major bone reformation in the following spring. If the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d06a97a-e31f-4564-96db-9db8e208ca87\" data-question=\"7\">mechanism of bone remodelling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in polar bears can be understood, many bedridden humans, and even astronauts, could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93b0abbd-c3dd-4b1b-8d92-c08740eded8a\" data-question=\"7\">potentially benefit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>.<br><br>The medical benefits of the polar bear for humanity certainly have their importance in our conservation efforts, but these should not be the only factors taken into consideration. We tend to want to protect animals we think are intelligent and possess emotions, such as elephants and primates. Bears, on the other hand, seem <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6825c974-a355-4af7-92a4-dceb4adc0aa9\" data-question=\"8\">to be perceived as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"723eaa9f-1541-4a21-9b21-68f0fce3c744\" data-question=\"8\">stupid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> and in many cases violent. And yet anecdotal evidence from the field challenges those assumptions, suggesting for example that polar bears have good problem-solving abilities. A male bear called GoGo in Tennoji Zoo, Osaka, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5b43e5f9-dc7e-4e92-9935-7790e0f93876\" data-question=\"9\">has even been observed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c65a5e15-c08f-40cc-9bb0-77a55def260c\" data-question=\"9\">making use of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> a tool to manipulate his environment. The bear used a tree branch on multiple occasions to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7eadb371-8618-4c81-9366-2922c989ff49\" data-question=\"10\">dislodge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> a piece of meat hung out of his reach. Problem-solving ability has also been witnessed in wild polar bears, although not as obviously as with GoGo. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e974881-34d5-4598-a0fc-f386f404767d\" data-question=\"11\">A calculated move<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> by a male bear involved running and jumping onto barrels in an attempt <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"199045ff-235a-4e9a-bf27-94a0df5a8cd5\" data-question=\"11\">to get to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a photographer standing on a platform four metres high.<br><br>In other studies, such as one by Alison Annes in 2008, polar bears <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20f841a3-f825-4a75-81d4-ddbafcf019da\" data-question=\"12\">showed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71c39780-c1ab-447a-96b7-b17da1c307eb\" data-question=\"12\">deliberate and focussed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> manipulation. For example, Annes observed bears putting objects in piles and then knocking them over in what <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccef5d80-5901-48bd-abe5-e7e0b0f37eb4\" data-question=\"12\">appeared to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> a game. The study demonstrates that bears are capable of agile and thought-out behaviours. These examples suggest bears have greater creativity and problem-solving abilities than previously thought.<br><br>As for emotions while the evidence is once again anecdotal, many bears have been seen to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fcde07d2-d2d9-47ac-97bc-88d66e73285a\" data-question=\"13\">hit out at ice and snow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> — seemingly out of frustration — when they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d821bf9b-2bdd-4897-a7de-ec36b058210a\" data-question=\"13\">have just missed out on a kill<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. Moreover, polar bears can form unusual relationships with other species, including playing with the dogs used to pull sleds in the Arctic. Remarkably, one hand-raised polar bear called Agee has formed a close relationship with her owner Mark Dumas to the point where they even swim together. This is even more astonishing since polar bears are known to actively hunt humans in the wild.<br><br>If climate change were to lead to their extinction, this would mean not only the loss of potential breakthroughs in human medicine, but more importantly, the disappearance of an intelligent, majestic animal.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</p><p>In boxes 1-7 on your reading answer sheet, write:</p><ul><li>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</li><li>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</li><li>NOT GIVEN If there is no information on this</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23604\" id=\"question-wrapper-23604\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Polar bears suffer from <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8fbedf06-12ba-440a-99ed-e887466f8ed5\" data-question=\"1\">various health problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> due to the build-up of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f95bba59-f97d-40fa-aa86-451b8948af38\" data-question=\"1\">fat under their skin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23605\" id=\"question-wrapper-23605\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The study done by Liu and his colleagues compared <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"04462922-cffd-413f-833d-7d4db9f98b89\" data-question=\"2\">different groups of polar bears<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23606\" id=\"question-wrapper-23606\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Liu and colleagues were the first researchers to compare polar bears and brown bears genetically. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23607\" id=\"question-wrapper-23607\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Polar bears are able <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4d796a6-9825-4748-93e9-cf002bb0e1d3\" data-question=\"4\">to control their levels of bad cholesterol<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3cb14a69-3681-414a-bfa8-f6fb3747bf87\" data-question=\"4\">by genetic means<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23608\" id=\"question-wrapper-23608\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Female polar bears are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8737cd00-f1ef-40fe-97cb-a567b931fb5d\" data-question=\"5\">able to survive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> for about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a9cbeb7-4d07-4f29-86d5-e31a3f8c3475\" data-question=\"5\">six months without food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23609\" id=\"question-wrapper-23609\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It was found that the bones of female polar bears were <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4a53d425-6823-4c55-a903-9a219674e7d9\" data-question=\"6\">very weak<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> when they came out of their dens in spring. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23610\" id=\"question-wrapper-23610\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The polar bear’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d06a97a-e31f-4564-96db-9db8e208ca87\" data-question=\"7\">mechanism for increasing bone density<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> could also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93b0abbd-c3dd-4b1b-8d92-c08740eded8a\" data-question=\"7\">be used by people one day<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the table below.</em></p><p><em>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>8-13 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><table><thead><tr><th>Reasons why polar bears should be protected</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6825c974-a355-4af7-92a4-dceb4adc0aa9\" data-question=\"8\">think of bears as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"723eaa9f-1541-4a21-9b21-68f0fce3c744\" data-question=\"8\">unintelligent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> and <strong>(8) </strong>………………………….<br>However, this may not be true. For example:<br><br>🔘 In Tennoji Zoo, a bear <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5b43e5f9-dc7e-4e92-9935-7790e0f93876\" data-question=\"9\">has been seen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c65a5e15-c08f-40cc-9bb0-77a55def260c\" data-question=\"9\">using<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> a branch as a <strong>(9) </strong>…………………………. This allowed him to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7eadb371-8618-4c81-9366-2922c989ff49\" data-question=\"10\">knock down<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> some <strong>(10) </strong>………………………….<br><br>🔘 A wild polar bear <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e974881-34d5-4598-a0fc-f386f404767d\" data-question=\"11\">worked out a method<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"199045ff-235a-4e9a-bf27-94a0df5a8cd5\" data-question=\"11\">of reaching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> a platform where a <strong>(11)</strong> …………………………. was located.<br><br>🔘 Polar bears have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20f841a3-f825-4a75-81d4-ddbafcf019da\" data-question=\"12\">displayed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> behaviour such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71c39780-c1ab-447a-96b7-b17da1c307eb\" data-question=\"12\">conscious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> manipulation of objects and activity <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccef5d80-5901-48bd-abe5-e7e0b0f37eb4\" data-question=\"12\">similar to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> a <strong>(12) </strong>………………………….<br><br>Bears may also display emotions. For example:<br>🔘 They may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fcde07d2-d2d9-47ac-97bc-88d66e73285a\" data-question=\"13\">make movements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> suggesting <strong>(13)</strong> …………………………. if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d821bf9b-2bdd-4897-a7de-ec36b058210a\" data-question=\"13\">disappointed when hunting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.<br><br>🔘 They may form relationships with other species</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23611\" id=\"question-wrapper-23611\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIOLENT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23612\" id=\"question-wrapper-23612\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TOOL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23613\" id=\"question-wrapper-23613\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MEAT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23614\" id=\"question-wrapper-23614\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PHOTOGRAPHER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23615\" id=\"question-wrapper-23615\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GAME</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23616\" id=\"question-wrapper-23616\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FRUSTRATION</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f95bba59-f97d-40fa-aa86-451b8948af38","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"fat under their skin","passagePhrase":"adipose tissue"},{"uid":"3cb14a69-3681-414a-bfa8-f6fb3747bf87","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"by genetic means","passagePhrase":"had a gene"},{"uid":"c4d796a6-9825-4748-93e9-cf002bb0e1d3","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"to control their levels of bad cholesterol","passagePhrase":"reduces levels of low-density lipoproteins (LDLs)"},{"uid":"1a9cbeb7-4d07-4f29-86d5-e31a3f8c3475","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"six months without food","passagePhrase":"about six months of fasting"},{"uid":"8737cd00-f1ef-40fe-97cb-a567b931fb5d","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"able to survive","passagePhrase":"keep themselves and their cubs alive"},{"uid":"7d06a97a-e31f-4564-96db-9db8e208ca87","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"mechanism for increasing bone density","passagePhrase":"mechanism of bone remodelling"},{"uid":"93b0abbd-c3dd-4b1b-8d92-c08740eded8a","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"be used by people one day","passagePhrase":"potentially benefit"},{"uid":"6825c974-a355-4af7-92a4-dceb4adc0aa9","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"think of bears as","passagePhrase":"to be perceived as"},{"uid":"723eaa9f-1541-4a21-9b21-68f0fce3c744","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"unintelligent","passagePhrase":"stupid"},{"uid":"5b43e5f9-dc7e-4e92-9935-7790e0f93876","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"has been seen","passagePhrase":"has even been observed"},{"uid":"c65a5e15-c08f-40cc-9bb0-77a55def260c","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"using","passagePhrase":"making use of"},{"uid":"7eadb371-8618-4c81-9366-2922c989ff49","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"knock down","passagePhrase":"dislodge"},{"uid":"5e974881-34d5-4598-a0fc-f386f404767d","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"worked out a method","passagePhrase":"A calculated move"},{"uid":"199045ff-235a-4e9a-bf27-94a0df5a8cd5","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"of reaching","passagePhrase":"to get to"},{"uid":"20f841a3-f825-4a75-81d4-ddbafcf019da","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"displayed","passagePhrase":"showed"},{"uid":"71c39780-c1ab-447a-96b7-b17da1c307eb","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"conscious","passagePhrase":"deliberate and focussed"},{"uid":"ccef5d80-5901-48bd-abe5-e7e0b0f37eb4","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"similar to","passagePhrase":"appeared to be"},{"uid":"fcde07d2-d2d9-47ac-97bc-88d66e73285a","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"make movements","passagePhrase":"hit out at ice and snow"},{"uid":"d821bf9b-2bdd-4897-a7de-ec36b058210a","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"disappointed when hunting","passagePhrase":"have just missed out on a kill"}]},"reading_u2_260":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 2 given below</em>.</p><h2>The Step Pyramid of Djoser</h2><p><strong>A.</strong></p><p>The pyramids are the most famous monuments of ancient Egypt and still hold enormous interest for people in the present day. These grand, impressive tributes to the memory of the Egyptian kings have become linked with the country even though <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7765d8c3-930f-4cee-9c5d-051610f42136\" data-question=\"14\">other cultures, such as the Chinese and Mayan, also built pyramids<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7765d8c3-930f-4cee-9c5d-051610f42136\" data-question=\"14\">The evolution of the pyramid form has been written and argued about for centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7805ccaf-a64a-44e0-8ee7-aeeb88e180ff\" data-question=\"14\">there is no question that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, as far as Egypt is concerned, it began with one monument to one king designed by one brilliant architect: <strong>the Step Pyramid of Djoser at Saqqara</strong>.</p><p><strong>B.</strong></p><p>Djoser was the first king of the Third Dynasty of Egypt and the first to build in stone. Prior to Djoser’s reign, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ca45075-b0a1-4826-8410-09b5ab2c599c\" data-question=\"15\">tombs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> were rectangular monuments made of dried clay brick, which covered underground passages where the deceased person was buried. For reasons which remain unclear, Djoser’s main official, whose name was Imhotep, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8560dc13-a318-41a7-8180-48719c219b0f\" data-question=\"15\">conceived of building<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> a taller, more impressive tomb for his king by stacking stone slabs on top of one another, progressively making them smaller, to form the shape now known as the Step Pyramid. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5dd06b65-b6de-4d41-a405-2d2382ef75e0\" data-question=\"25\">Djoser is thought to have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a2860dd-6945-4368-9a44-56e8daf555c8\" data-question=\"25\">reigned for 19 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, but some historians and scholars attribute <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a2860dd-6945-4368-9a44-56e8daf555c8\" data-question=\"25\">a much longer time for his rule<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, owing to the number and size of the monuments he built.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span></p><p><strong>C. </strong></p><p>The Step Pyramid has been thoroughly examined and investigated over the last century, and it is now known that the building process went through many different stages. Historian Marc Van de Mieroop comments on this, writing ‘Much experimentation was involved, which is especially clear in the construction of the pyramid in the center of the complex. It had several plans … before it became the first Step Pyramid in history, piling six levels on top of one another … The weight of the enormous mass was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c14fbe3-e5a0-4ada-8ffd-1789cb321a10\" data-question=\"16\">a challenge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1492e786-fb20-472a-a0ab-b6b8dd470a3a\" data-question=\"16\">for the builders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, who placed the stones at an inward incline in order to prevent the monument breaking up.’<br><br><br><strong>D.</strong><br>When finally completed, the Step Pyramid rose 62 meters high and was the tallest structure of its time. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf7c033b-7e22-4320-b3b3-33d111350874\" data-question=\"17\">The complex in which<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> it was built <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a7be8d1-60d6-49c1-b06f-09c1adb0aa12\" data-question=\"21\">was the size of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> a city in ancient Egypt and included <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"012de590-e7ad-4c58-9125-0d7519369277\" data-question=\"17\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69b385bd-0b06-4d08-a3e5-c65d7e00576f\" data-question=\"22\">a temple, courtyards, shrines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0461ee68-3f73-40e8-b127-f4ad024b9d97\" data-question=\"22\">living quarters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> for the priests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. It covered a region of 16 hectares and was surrounded by a wall 10.5 meters high. The wall had 13 false doors cut into it with only one true entrance cut into the south-east corner; the entire wall was then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a589ad0c-d059-4e12-acf0-a875e26b787d\" data-question=\"23\">ringed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> by a trench 750 meters long and 40 meters wide. The false doors and the trench were incorporated into the complex to discourage unwanted visitors. If someone wished to enter, he or she would have needed to know in advance how to find the location of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27a474da-3c25-4368-b31b-720c86c655ac\" data-question=\"24\">true opening<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in the wall. Djoser was so proud of his accomplishment that he broke the tradition of having only his own name on the monument and had Imhotep’s name carved on it as well.<br><br><br><strong>E.</strong><br>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"586bd371-8c83-4d91-8c7d-0902bef5494f\" data-question=\"18\">burial chamber of the tomb<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, where the king’s body was laid to rest, was dug <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"586bd371-8c83-4d91-8c7d-0902bef5494f\" data-question=\"18\">beneath the base of the pyramid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, surrounded by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"586bd371-8c83-4d91-8c7d-0902bef5494f\" data-question=\"18\">a vast maze of long tunnels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that had rooms off them to discourage robbers. One of the most mysterious discoveries found inside the pyramid was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3648667-decc-476e-ae2e-e6ce21fa8307\" data-question=\"18\">a large number of stone vessels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Over 40,000 of these vessels, of various forms and shapes, were discovered in storerooms of the pyramid’s underground passages. They are inscribed with the names of rulers from the First and Second Dynasties of Egypt and made from different kinds of stone. There is no agreement among scholars and archaeologists on why the vessels were placed in the tomb of Djoser or what they were supposed to represent. The archaeologist Jean-Philippe Lauer, who excavated most of the pyramid and complex, believes they were originally stored and then given a ‘proper burial’ by Djoser in his pyramid to honor his predecessors. There are other historians, however, who claim the vessels were dumped into the shafts as yet another attempt to prevent grave robbers from getting to the king’s burial chamber.</p><p><strong>F. </strong></p><p>Unfortunately, all of the precautions and intricate design of the underground network did not prevent ancient robbers from finding a way in. Djoser’s grave goods, and even his body, were stolen at some point in the past and all archaeologists found were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6da98079-7eeb-4b19-82b3-499c4b5e9cb9\" data-question=\"19\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"81ffa307-7853-43f2-9a11-d094c92d3c3f\" data-question=\"26\">a small number of his valuables<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> overlooked by the thieves. There was enough left throughout the pyramid and its complex, however, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab9801bf-f1b6-4b2a-bbb0-f1c91ad3f63c\" data-question=\"19\">to astonish and amaze the archaeologists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> who excavated it.</p><p><strong>G.</strong></p><p>Egyptologist Miroslav Verner writes, ‘Few monuments hold a place in human history as significant as that of the Step Pyramid in Saqqara … It can be said without exaggeration that this pyramid complex constitutes a milestone in the evolution of monumental stone <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb51d309-c023-4c9c-be70-767fe6bfb330\" data-question=\"20\">architecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in Egypt and in the world as a whole.’ The Step Pyramid was a revolutionary advance in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb51d309-c023-4c9c-be70-767fe6bfb330\" data-question=\"20\">architecture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and became the archetype which all the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11bf6765-f044-4aba-a622-2e51231fefdf\" data-question=\"20\">other great pyramid builders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of Egypt would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"360b1fea-976b-4e16-a41c-3c7631a4f0ae\" data-question=\"20\">follow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Questions 14-20</p><p><em>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, <strong>A-G.</strong></em></p><p><em>Choose the correct heading for paragraphs from the list of headings below.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct number, <strong>i-ix</strong>, in boxes <strong>14-20 </strong>on your answer sheet.</em></p><p> </p><table><thead><tr><th>List of Headings</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>i. </strong>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"586bd371-8c83-4d91-8c7d-0902bef5494f\" data-question=\"18\">areas and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3648667-decc-476e-ae2e-e6ce21fa8307\" data-question=\"18\">artefacts within the pyramid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> itself<br><strong>ii. </strong><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c14fbe3-e5a0-4ada-8ffd-1789cb321a10\" data-question=\"16\">A difficult task<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1492e786-fb20-472a-a0ab-b6b8dd470a3a\" data-question=\"16\">those involved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span><br><strong>iii. </strong>A king who saved his people<br><strong>iv.</strong> A single <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7805ccaf-a64a-44e0-8ee7-aeeb88e180ff\" data-question=\"14\">certainty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> among other <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7765d8c3-930f-4cee-9c5d-051610f42136\" data-question=\"14\">less definite facts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span><br><strong>v.</strong> An overview of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"012de590-e7ad-4c58-9125-0d7519369277\" data-question=\"17\">external<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf7c033b-7e22-4320-b3b3-33d111350874\" data-question=\"17\">buildings and areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span><br><strong>vi. </strong>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb51d309-c023-4c9c-be70-767fe6bfb330\" data-question=\"20\">pyramid design<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11bf6765-f044-4aba-a622-2e51231fefdf\" data-question=\"20\">others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"360b1fea-976b-4e16-a41c-3c7631a4f0ae\" data-question=\"20\">copied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span><br><strong>vii. </strong><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8560dc13-a318-41a7-8180-48719c219b0f\" data-question=\"15\">An idea for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> changing the design of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ca45075-b0a1-4826-8410-09b5ab2c599c\" data-question=\"15\">burial structures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span><br><strong>viii. </strong><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab9801bf-f1b6-4b2a-bbb0-f1c91ad3f63c\" data-question=\"19\">An incredible experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> despite the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6da98079-7eeb-4b19-82b3-499c4b5e9cb9\" data-question=\"19\">few remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span><br><strong>ix. </strong>The answers to some unexpected questions</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23617\" id=\"question-wrapper-23617\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23618\" id=\"question-wrapper-23618\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23619\" id=\"question-wrapper-23619\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23620\" id=\"question-wrapper-23620\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23621\" id=\"question-wrapper-23621\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23622\" id=\"question-wrapper-23622\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23623\" id=\"question-wrapper-23623\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the notes below.</em></p><p><em>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>21-24 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td>The Step Pyramid of Djoser<br><br>The complex that includes the Step Pyramid and its surroundings is considered to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a7be8d1-60d6-49c1-b06f-09c1adb0aa12\" data-question=\"21\">be as big as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> an Egyptian <strong>(21)</strong> …………………………. of the past. The area outside the pyramid included <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0461ee68-3f73-40e8-b127-f4ad024b9d97\" data-question=\"22\">accommodation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> that was occupied by <strong>(22)</strong> …………………………. along with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69b385bd-0b06-4d08-a3e5-c65d7e00576f\" data-question=\"22\">many other buildings and features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.<br><br>A wall ran around the outside of the complex and a number of false entrances were built into this. In addition, a long <strong>(23)</strong> …………………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a589ad0c-d059-4e12-acf0-a875e26b787d\" data-question=\"23\">encircled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> the wall. As a result, any visitors who had not been invited were cleverly prevented from entering the pyramid grounds unless they knew the <strong>(24)</strong> …………………………. of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27a474da-3c25-4368-b31b-720c86c655ac\" data-question=\"24\">real entrance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23624\" id=\"question-wrapper-23624\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CITY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23625\" id=\"question-wrapper-23625\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PRIESTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23626\" id=\"question-wrapper-23626\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRENCH</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23627\" id=\"question-wrapper-23627\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LOCATION</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E.</strong></em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>25</strong> &amp; <strong>26</strong> on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><p><strong>Which TWO of the following points does the writer make about King Djoser?</strong></p><p><strong>A. </strong>Initially he had to be persuaded to build in stone rather than clay.</p><p><strong>B.</strong> There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5dd06b65-b6de-4d41-a405-2d2382ef75e0\" data-question=\"25\">disagreement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> concerning <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a2860dd-6945-4368-9a44-56e8daf555c8\" data-question=\"25\">the length of his reign<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</p><p><strong>C.</strong> He failed to appreciate Imhotep’s part in the design of Step Pyramid.</p><p><strong>D.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"81ffa307-7853-43f2-9a11-d094c92d3c3f\" data-question=\"26\">A few of his possessions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> were still in his tomb when archaeologists found it.</p><p><strong>E.</strong> He criticised the design and construction of other pyramids in Egypt.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23628\" id=\"question-wrapper-23628\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23629\" id=\"question-wrapper-23629\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7765d8c3-930f-4cee-9c5d-051610f42136","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"less definite facts","passagePhrase":"other cultures, such as the Chinese and Mayan, also built pyramids ... The evolution of the pyramid form has been written and argued about for centuries"},{"uid":"7805ccaf-a64a-44e0-8ee7-aeeb88e180ff","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"certainty","passagePhrase":"there is no question that"},{"uid":"5ca45075-b0a1-4826-8410-09b5ab2c599c","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"burial structures","passagePhrase":"tombs"},{"uid":"8560dc13-a318-41a7-8180-48719c219b0f","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"An idea for","passagePhrase":"conceived of building"},{"uid":"5dd06b65-b6de-4d41-a405-2d2382ef75e0","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"disagreement","passagePhrase":"Djoser is thought to have reigned for 19 years, but some historians and scholars attribute a much longer time for his rule, owing to the number and size of the monuments he built."},{"uid":"1a2860dd-6945-4368-9a44-56e8daf555c8","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"the length of his reign","passagePhrase":"reigned for 19 years ... a much longer time for his rule"},{"uid":"9c14fbe3-e5a0-4ada-8ffd-1789cb321a10","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"A difficult task","passagePhrase":"a challenge"},{"uid":"1492e786-fb20-472a-a0ab-b6b8dd470a3a","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"those involved","passagePhrase":"for the builders"},{"uid":"cf7c033b-7e22-4320-b3b3-33d111350874","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"buildings and areas","passagePhrase":"The complex in which"},{"uid":"8a7be8d1-60d6-49c1-b06f-09c1adb0aa12","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"be as big as","passagePhrase":"was the size of"},{"uid":"012de590-e7ad-4c58-9125-0d7519369277","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"external","passagePhrase":"a temple, courtyards, shrines, and living quarters for the priests"},{"uid":"69b385bd-0b06-4d08-a3e5-c65d7e00576f","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"many other buildings and features","passagePhrase":"a temple, courtyards, shrines"},{"uid":"0461ee68-3f73-40e8-b127-f4ad024b9d97","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"accommodation","passagePhrase":"living quarters"},{"uid":"a589ad0c-d059-4e12-acf0-a875e26b787d","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"encircled","passagePhrase":"ringed"},{"uid":"27a474da-3c25-4368-b31b-720c86c655ac","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"real entrance","passagePhrase":"true opening"},{"uid":"586bd371-8c83-4d91-8c7d-0902bef5494f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"areas and artefacts within the pyramid","passagePhrase":"burial chamber of the tomb ... beneath the base of the pyramid ... a vast maze of long tunnels"},{"uid":"a3648667-decc-476e-ae2e-e6ce21fa8307","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"artefacts within the pyramid","passagePhrase":"a large number of stone vessels"},{"uid":"6da98079-7eeb-4b19-82b3-499c4b5e9cb9","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"few remains","passagePhrase":"a small number of his valuables"},{"uid":"81ffa307-7853-43f2-9a11-d094c92d3c3f","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"A few of his possessions","passagePhrase":"a small number of his valuables"},{"uid":"ab9801bf-f1b6-4b2a-bbb0-f1c91ad3f63c","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"An incredible experience","passagePhrase":"to astonish and amaze the archaeologists"},{"uid":"fb51d309-c023-4c9c-be70-767fe6bfb330","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"pyramid design","passagePhrase":"architecture ... architecture"},{"uid":"11bf6765-f044-4aba-a622-2e51231fefdf","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"others","passagePhrase":"other great pyramid builders"},{"uid":"360b1fea-976b-4e16-a41c-3c7631a4f0ae","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"copied","passagePhrase":"follow"}]},"reading_u2_261":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40,</strong> corresponding to Reading Passage 3 given below</em></p><h2>The future of work</h2><p>According to a leading business consultancy, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"245a6c64-d3b5-4bd3-ab5a-c1ebfd1b5233\" data-question=\"27\">3—14% of the global workforce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> will need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec114721-805d-4b76-a1ba-08d15268a904\" data-question=\"27\">switch to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> a different <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"906596e0-ed7f-4685-865c-07d5647ba5c8\" data-question=\"27\">occupation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> within the next 10—15 years, and all workers will need to adapt as their occupations evolve alongside increasingly capable machines. Automation — or ‘embodied artificial intelligence (AI) — is one aspect of the disruptive effects of technology on the labour market. ‘Disembodied AI’, like the algorithms running in our smartphones, is another.<br><br><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"522f3aae-dbf8-4520-98b9-6b843743a4f0\" data-question=\"28\">Dr Stella Pachidi from Cambridge Judge Business School believes that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> some of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3038415c-0415-43fa-8bbc-31160a1e4940\" data-question=\"28\">the most fundamental changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> are happening as a result of the ‘<strong>algorithmication</strong>’ of jobs that are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f17cdac7-1251-4033-bc85-5db5d4d37706\" data-question=\"31\">dependent on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> data rather than on production — the so-called knowledge economy. Algorithms are capable of learning from data to undertake tasks that previously needed human judgement, such as reading legal contracts, analysing medical scans and gathering market intelligence.<br><br>‘In many cases, they can outperform humans,’ says Pachidi. ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce8ea725-058a-443f-9417-113762c34aca\" data-question=\"36\">Organisations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0dfc1d37-de13-4203-8c0a-8669069f960c\" data-question=\"36\">attracted to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> using algorithms because they want to make choices based on what they consider is “perfect information”, as well as to reduce costs and enhance productivity.’<br><br>‘But these enhancements are not without consequences,’ says Pachidi. ‘If routine cognitive tasks are taken over by AI, how do professions develop their future experts?’ she asks. ‘One way of learning about a job is “legitimate peripheral participation”— a novice stands next to experts and learns by observation. If this isn’t happening, then you need to find new ways to learn.’<br><br>Another issue is the extent to which the technology influences or even controls the workforce. For over two years, Pachidi monitored a telecommunications company. ‘The way telecoms salespeople work is through personal and frequent contact with clients, using the benefit of experience to assess a situation and reach a decision. However, the company had started using a[n] … algorithm that defined when account managers should contact certain customers about which kinds of campaigns and what to offer them.’<br><br>The algorithm — usually built by external designers — often becomes the keeper of knowledge, she explains. In cases like this, Pachidi believes, a short-sighted view begins to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9de7a267-a17e-447c-8116-64577a199c7c\" data-question=\"32\">creep into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> working practices whereby workers learn through the ‘algorithm’s eyes’ and become dependent on its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f22dee7-5333-4e51-a24d-94079222fd75\" data-question=\"32\">instructions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. Alternative explorations — where experimentation and human <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28ec9a7c-c839-432d-9959-f19f5c185ec2\" data-question=\"34\">instinct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> lead to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c277b384-e586-4be9-988c-3c7e7dc5b090\" data-question=\"33\">progress and new ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> — are effectively <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"733ce457-e8f6-4b4d-bd18-d72ba7a44a6a\" data-question=\"33\">discouraged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.<br><br>Pachidi and colleagues even observed people developing strategies to make the algorithm <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08bcaee2-ae11-4c1d-93d6-5cae2cfd9be5\" data-question=\"29\">work to their own advantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. ‘We are seeing cases where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e232a8fa-2e4a-462f-b715-afa4e7090511\" data-question=\"29\">workers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> feed the algorithm with false data to reach their targets,’ she reports.<br><br>It’s scenarios like these that many researchers are working to avoid. Their objective is to make AI technologies more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca536abe-8cd3-487d-a24a-e793d34b8b0c\" data-question=\"34\">trustworthy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> and transparent, so that organisations and individuals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af39f119-d873-4f04-89dd-18f8caecfe7e\" data-question=\"38\">understand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> how AI decisions are made. In the meantime, says Pachidi, ‘We need to make sure we fully <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af39f119-d873-4f04-89dd-18f8caecfe7e\" data-question=\"38\">understand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dce82a1c-b6bd-4af9-9ea7-4f4750845cbc\" data-question=\"38\">dilemmas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> that this new world <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a4e7845d-a08e-4ea3-a762-f7d024bbda70\" data-question=\"38\">raises<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> regarding expertise, occupational boundaries and control.’<br><br>Economist Professor Hamish Low believes that the future of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5785c09d-dca0-498d-a0fb-298655ec8d53\" data-question=\"39\">work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> will involve major transitions across the whole life course for everyone: ‘The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b10dc355-1a52-448f-b609-0e5d6f0dd851\" data-question=\"39\">traditional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> trajectory of full-time education followed by full-time work followed by a pensioned retirement is a thing of the past,’ says Low. Instead, he envisages a multistage employment life: one where retraining happens across the life course, and where multiple jobs and no job happen by choice at different stages.<br><br>On the subject of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c226b62b-aa51-44ba-8353-d69a0bea3d60\" data-question=\"35\">job losses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, Low believes the predictions are founded on a fallacy: ‘It assumes that the number of jobs is fixed. If in 30 years, half of 100 jobs are being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebc5c882-3fdd-4fc7-ab27-d1ee78f254cb\" data-question=\"35\">carried out by robots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, that doesn’t <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db23c25e-a281-4d22-985e-126d5b6f429e\" data-question=\"35\">mean<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> we are left with just 50 jobs for humans. The number of jobs will increase: we would expect there to be 150 jobs.’<br><br>Dr Ewan McGaughey, at Cambridge’s Centre for Business Research and King’s College London, agrees that ‘apocalyptic’ views about the future of work are misguided. ‘It’s the laws that restrict the supply of capital to the job market, not the advent of new technologies that causes unemployment.’<br><br>His recently published research answers the question of whether automation, AI and robotics will mean a ‘jobless future’ by looking at the causes of unemployment. ‘History is clear that change can mean redundancies. But social policies can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9e7d61d-1bad-49a3-8365-56e6ded47d77\" data-question=\"30\">tackle this<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> through retraining and redeployment.’<br><br>He adds: ‘If there is going to be change to jobs as a result of AI and robotics then I’d like to see governments seizing the opportunity to improve policy to enforce good job security. We can “reprogramme” the law to prepare for a fairer future of work and leisure.’ McGaughey’s findings are a call to arms to leaders of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa2a402f-8737-4aa8-b261-1bd79ab11ff6\" data-question=\"40\">organisations, governments and banks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"97f52cd1-2001-4e11-953d-0b26bd572625\" data-question=\"40\">pre-empt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> the coming changes with bold new policies that guarantee <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8308de3-1287-4403-9593-dfb33c0c01ec\" data-question=\"40\">full employment, fair incomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> and a thriving economic democracy.<br><br>‘The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"05a57f4e-5fd4-47b7-beca-a6168f4665e9\" data-question=\"37\">promises<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> of these new technologies are astounding. They deliver humankind the capacity to live in a way that nobody could have once imagined,’ he adds. '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c5838f2-cff6-4861-9f77-61782cdf91c1\" data-question=\"37\">Just as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> the industrial revolution brought people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7257f54f-c6c8-4ccb-817d-30cd5b47eaab\" data-question=\"37\">past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> subsistence agriculture, and the corporate revolution enabled mass production, a third revolution has been pronounced. But it will not only be one of technology. The next revolution will be social.'</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose the correct letter- <strong>A,B,C or D.</strong></em></p><p><em>Write your answer in boxes <strong>27</strong>–<strong>30</strong> on your reading answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23630\" id=\"question-wrapper-23630\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The first paragraph tells us about… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the kind of jobs that will be most affected by the growth of AI.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"245a6c64-d3b5-4bd3-ab5a-c1ebfd1b5233\" data-question=\"27\">the extent to which AI will<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ec114721-805d-4b76-a1ba-08d15268a904\" data-question=\"27\">alter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the nature of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"906596e0-ed7f-4685-865c-07d5647ba5c8\" data-question=\"27\">work that people do<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>C. the proportion of the world’s labour force who will have jobs in AI in the future.</li> <li>D. the difference between ways that embodied and disembodied AI will impact on workers.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23631\" id=\"question-wrapper-23631\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the second paragraph, what is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"522f3aae-dbf8-4520-98b9-6b843743a4f0\" data-question=\"28\">Stella Pachidi’s view of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> the ’knowledge economy’? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is having an influence on the number of jobs available.</li> <li>B. It is changing people’s attitudes towards their occupations.</li> <li>C. It is the main reason why the production sector is declining.</li> <li>D. It is a key factor driving current <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3038415c-0415-43fa-8bbc-31160a1e4940\" data-question=\"28\">developments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> in the workplace.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23632\" id=\"question-wrapper-23632\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What did Pachidi observe at the telecommunications company? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. staff disagreeing with the recommendations of AI</li> <li>B. staff feeling resentful about the intrusion of Al in their work</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e232a8fa-2e4a-462f-b715-afa4e7090511\" data-question=\"29\">staff<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> making sure that AI <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08bcaee2-ae11-4c1d-93d6-5cae2cfd9be5\" data-question=\"29\">produces the results that they want<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></li> <li>D. staff allowing AI to carry out tasks they ought to do themselves</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23633\" id=\"question-wrapper-23633\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In his recently published research, Ewan McGaughey… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. challenges the idea that redundancy is a negative thing.</li> <li>B. shows the profound effect of mass unemployment on society.</li> <li>C. highlights some differences between past and future job losses.</li> <li>D. illustrates how changes in the job market can be successfully <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9e7d61d-1bad-49a3-8365-56e6ded47d77\" data-question=\"30\">handled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the summary below.</em></p><p><em>Choose the correct letter,<strong> A-G</strong>.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>31-34 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>A.</strong> pressure<br><strong>B.</strong> satisfaction<br><strong>C.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28ec9a7c-c839-432d-9959-f19f5c185ec2\" data-question=\"34\">intuition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span><br><strong>D.</strong> promotion<br><strong>E. </strong><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4473ce98-63aa-423c-bd6b-393b0f54fe2d\" data-question=\"32\">reliance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span><br><strong>F.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca536abe-8cd3-487d-a24a-e793d34b8b0c\" data-question=\"34\">confidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span><br><strong>G.</strong> information</td></tr></tbody></table><p> </p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>The ‘algorithimication’ of jobs</strong><br><br>Stella Pachidi of Cambridge Judge Business School has been focusing on the <em>algorithmication</em> of jobs which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f17cdac7-1251-4033-bc85-5db5d4d37706\" data-question=\"31\">rely not on production but on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <strong>(31)</strong> …………………………. .<br><br>While monitoring a telecommunications company, Pachidi observed a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9de7a267-a17e-447c-8116-64577a199c7c\" data-question=\"32\">growing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <strong>(32)</strong> …………………………. on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f22dee7-5333-4e51-a24d-94079222fd75\" data-question=\"32\">recommendations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> made by AI, as workers begin to learn through the algorithm’s eyes. Meanwhile, staff are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"733ce457-e8f6-4b4d-bd18-d72ba7a44a6a\" data-question=\"33\">deterred<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> from experimenting and using their own<br><strong>(33)</strong> …………………………. , and are therefore prevented from achieving <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c277b384-e586-4be9-988c-3c7e7dc5b090\" data-question=\"33\">innovation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.<br><br>To avoid the kind of situations which Pachidi observed, researchers are trying to make AI’s decision-making process easier to comprehend, and to increase user’s <strong>(34)</strong> …………………………. with regard to the technology.</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23634\" id=\"question-wrapper-23634\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23635\" id=\"question-wrapper-23635\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23636\" id=\"question-wrapper-23636\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23637\" id=\"question-wrapper-23637\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Look at the following findings (<strong>Questions 35-40</strong>) and the list of people below.</em></p><p><em>Match each finding with the correct researcher- <strong>A, B or C.</strong></em></p><p><em>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-C</strong>, in boxes <strong>35-40 </strong>on your answer sheet.</em></p><p><em><strong>NB</strong> – You may use any letter more than once.</em></p><table><thead><tr><th>List of people</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>A.</strong> Stella Pachidi<br><strong>B.</strong> Hamish Low<br><strong>C. </strong>Ewan McGaughey</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23638\" id=\"question-wrapper-23638\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Greater levels of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebc5c882-3fdd-4fc7-ab27-d1ee78f254cb\" data-question=\"35\">automation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> will not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db23c25e-a281-4d22-985e-126d5b6f429e\" data-question=\"35\">result in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c226b62b-aa51-44ba-8353-d69a0bea3d60\" data-question=\"35\">lower employment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23639\" id=\"question-wrapper-23639\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There are several reasons why AI is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0dfc1d37-de13-4203-8c0a-8669069f960c\" data-question=\"36\">appealing to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce8ea725-058a-443f-9417-113762c34aca\" data-question=\"36\">businesses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23640\" id=\"question-wrapper-23640\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> AI’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"05a57f4e-5fd4-47b7-beca-a6168f4665e9\" data-question=\"37\">potential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to transform people’s lives has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c5838f2-cff6-4861-9f77-61782cdf91c1\" data-question=\"37\">parallels with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> major cultural shifts which occurred in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7257f54f-c6c8-4ccb-817d-30cd5b47eaab\" data-question=\"37\">previous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> eras. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23641\" id=\"question-wrapper-23641\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is important to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af39f119-d873-4f04-89dd-18f8caecfe7e\" data-question=\"38\">be aware of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> the range of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dce82a1c-b6bd-4af9-9ea7-4f4750845cbc\" data-question=\"38\">problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> that AI <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a4e7845d-a08e-4ea3-a762-f7d024bbda70\" data-question=\"38\">causes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23642\" id=\"question-wrapper-23642\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People are going to follow a less <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b10dc355-1a52-448f-b609-0e5d6f0dd851\" data-question=\"39\">conventional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5785c09d-dca0-498d-a0fb-298655ec8d53\" data-question=\"39\">career path<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> than in the past. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23643\" id=\"question-wrapper-23643\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa2a402f-8737-4aa8-b261-1bd79ab11ff6\" data-question=\"40\">Authorities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"97f52cd1-2001-4e11-953d-0b26bd572625\" data-question=\"40\">take measures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to ensure that there will be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8308de3-1287-4403-9593-dfb33c0c01ec\" data-question=\"40\">adequately paid work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> for everyone. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"245a6c64-d3b5-4bd3-ab5a-c1ebfd1b5233","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"the extent to which AI will","passagePhrase":"3—14% of the global workforce"},{"uid":"ec114721-805d-4b76-a1ba-08d15268a904","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"alter","passagePhrase":"switch to"},{"uid":"906596e0-ed7f-4685-865c-07d5647ba5c8","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"work that people do","passagePhrase":"occupation"},{"uid":"522f3aae-dbf8-4520-98b9-6b843743a4f0","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Stella Pachidi’s view of","passagePhrase":"Dr Stella Pachidi from Cambridge Judge Business School believes that"},{"uid":"3038415c-0415-43fa-8bbc-31160a1e4940","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"developments","passagePhrase":"the most fundamental changes"},{"uid":"f17cdac7-1251-4033-bc85-5db5d4d37706","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"rely not on production but on","passagePhrase":"dependent on"},{"uid":"ce8ea725-058a-443f-9417-113762c34aca","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"businesses","passagePhrase":"Organisations"},{"uid":"0dfc1d37-de13-4203-8c0a-8669069f960c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"appealing to","passagePhrase":"attracted to"},{"uid":"9de7a267-a17e-447c-8116-64577a199c7c","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"growing","passagePhrase":"creep into"},{"uid":"2f22dee7-5333-4e51-a24d-94079222fd75","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"recommendations","passagePhrase":"instructions"},{"uid":"28ec9a7c-c839-432d-9959-f19f5c185ec2","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"intuition","passagePhrase":"instinct"},{"uid":"c277b384-e586-4be9-988c-3c7e7dc5b090","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"innovation","passagePhrase":"progress and new ideas"},{"uid":"733ce457-e8f6-4b4d-bd18-d72ba7a44a6a","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"deterred","passagePhrase":"discouraged"},{"uid":"08bcaee2-ae11-4c1d-93d6-5cae2cfd9be5","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"produces the results that they want","passagePhrase":"work to their own advantage"},{"uid":"e232a8fa-2e4a-462f-b715-afa4e7090511","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"staff","passagePhrase":"workers"},{"uid":"ca536abe-8cd3-487d-a24a-e793d34b8b0c","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"confidence","passagePhrase":"trustworthy"},{"uid":"af39f119-d873-4f04-89dd-18f8caecfe7e","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"be aware of","passagePhrase":"understand ... understand"},{"uid":"dce82a1c-b6bd-4af9-9ea7-4f4750845cbc","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"problems","passagePhrase":"dilemmas"},{"uid":"a4e7845d-a08e-4ea3-a762-f7d024bbda70","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"causes","passagePhrase":"raises"},{"uid":"5785c09d-dca0-498d-a0fb-298655ec8d53","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"career path","passagePhrase":"work"},{"uid":"b10dc355-1a52-448f-b609-0e5d6f0dd851","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"conventional","passagePhrase":"traditional"},{"uid":"c226b62b-aa51-44ba-8353-d69a0bea3d60","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"lower employment","passagePhrase":"job losses"},{"uid":"ebc5c882-3fdd-4fc7-ab27-d1ee78f254cb","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"automation","passagePhrase":"carried out by robots"},{"uid":"db23c25e-a281-4d22-985e-126d5b6f429e","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"result in","passagePhrase":"mean"},{"uid":"a9e7d61d-1bad-49a3-8365-56e6ded47d77","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"handled","passagePhrase":"tackle this"},{"uid":"fa2a402f-8737-4aa8-b261-1bd79ab11ff6","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Authorities","passagePhrase":"organisations, governments and banks"},{"uid":"97f52cd1-2001-4e11-953d-0b26bd572625","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"take measures","passagePhrase":"pre-empt"},{"uid":"a8308de3-1287-4403-9593-dfb33c0c01ec","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"adequately paid work","passagePhrase":"full employment, fair incomes"},{"uid":"05a57f4e-5fd4-47b7-beca-a6168f4665e9","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"potential","passagePhrase":"promises"},{"uid":"0c5838f2-cff6-4861-9f77-61782cdf91c1","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"parallels with","passagePhrase":"Just as"},{"uid":"7257f54f-c6c8-4ccb-817d-30cd5b47eaab","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"previous","passagePhrase":"past"},{"uid":"4473ce98-63aa-423c-bd6b-393b0f54fe2d","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"reliance","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_262":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 1-13</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 1 given below</em>.</p><h2>The White Horse of Uffington</h2><p>The cutting of huge figures or <em><strong>geoglyphs</strong></em> into the earth of English hillsides has taken place for more than 3,000 years. There are 56 hill figures scattered around England, with the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e2884e48-532b-4833-87a7-427288ca59c4\" data-question=\"1\">vast majority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> on the chalk <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e66cedc-c435-4534-a12c-d8191c21ca8e\" data-question=\"1\">downlands of the country’s southern counties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. The figures include giants, horses, crosses and regimental badges. Although the majority of these geoglyphs date within the last 300 years or so, there are one or two that are much older.</p><p>The most famous of these figures is perhaps also the most mysterious — <strong>the Uffington White Horse</strong> in Oxfordshire. The White Horse has recently been re-dated and shown to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53b703b4-8560-4f5d-a06c-7ed3c601731b\" data-question=\"3\">even older than its previously assigned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> ancient <em>pre-Roman Iron Age</em> date. More <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"316f0576-c26b-4509-8329-223ef9371755\" data-question=\"4\">controversial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61ea4f4c-c1bf-467a-a2b7-dfc46a88a9b9\" data-question=\"4\">the date of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the enigmatic Long Man of Wilmington in Sussex. While many historians are convinced the figure is prehistoric, others believe that it was the work of an artistic monk from a nearby priory and was created between the 11th and 15th centuries.</p><p>The method of cutting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"934e9be0-bc4c-4b89-8140-5228d09f1d2a\" data-question=\"5\">these huge figures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> was simply to remove the overlying grass to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0cfbab60-301d-4de0-aef1-09eee6d62cc7\" data-question=\"5\">reveal the gleaming white chalk below<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. However, the grass would soon grow over the geoglyph again unless it was regularly cleaned or scoured by a fairly large team of people. One reason that the vast majority of hill figures <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cf31953-6c6a-4e7d-b83c-4e8b37990666\" data-question=\"6\">have disappeared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> is that when the traditions associated with the figures faded, people no longer bothered or remembered to clear away the grass to expose the chalk outline. Furthermore, over hundreds of years the outlines would sometimes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55cddcaf-e67d-4c93-9686-3e94135ab985\" data-question=\"7\">change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> due to people not always cutting in exactly the same place, thus creating a different shape to the original geoglyph. The fact that any ancient hill figures survive at all in England today is testament to the strength and continuity of local customs and beliefs which, in one case at least, must stretch back over millennia.<br><br>The Uffington White Horse is a unique, stylised representation of a horse consisting of a long, sleek back, thin disjointed legs, a streaming tail, and a bird-like beaked head. The elegant creature almost melts into the landscape. The horse is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4597a1b-de9e-4aa5-b711-c3072bbcc670\" data-question=\"9\">situated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> 2.5 km from Uffington village on a steep slope close to the Late Bronze Age (c. 7th century BCE) hillfort of Uffington Castle and below the Ridgeway, a long-distance Neolithic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca7a7a5e-4673-4c0b-8b51-2be59bf72533\" data-question=\"9\">track<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</p><p>The Uffington Horse is also surrounded by Bronze Age burial mounds. It is not far from the Bronze Age cemetery of Lambourn Seven Barrows, which consists of more than 30 well-preserved burial mounds. The carving has been placed in such a way as to make it extremely difficult to see from close quarters, and like many geoglyphs is best appreciated from the air. Nevertheless, there are certain areas of the Vale of the White Horse, the valley containing and named after the enigmatic creature, from which an adequate impression may be gained. Indeed on a clear day the carving can be seen from up to 30 km away.</p><p>The earliest evidence of a horse at Uffington is from the 1070s CE when ‘White Horse Hill’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"875de638-227e-46c6-b862-876088814ecb\" data-question=\"10\">is mentioned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> in documents from the nearby Abbey of Abingdon, and the first reference to the horse itself is soon after, in 1190 CE. However, the carving is believed to date back much further than that. Due to the similarity of the Uffington White Horse to the stylised depictions of horses on 1st century BCE coins, it had been thought that the creature must also date to that period.</p><p>However, in 1995 Optically Stimulated Luminescence (OSL) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a08eb999-db41-4d9b-8119-bd0b8ff000a3\" data-question=\"11\">testing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> was carried out by the Oxford Archaeological Unit on soil from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89db7ef2-1d1c-47cd-8726-090258840d47\" data-question=\"11\">two of the lower layers of the horse’s body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, and from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89db7ef2-1d1c-47cd-8726-090258840d47\" data-question=\"11\">another cut near the base<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. The result was a date for the horse’s construction somewhere between 1400 and 600 BCE — in other words, it had a Late Bronze Age or Early Iron Age origin.</p><p>The latter end of this date range would tie the carving of the horse in with occupation of the nearby Uffington hillfort, indicating that it may represent a tribal emblem marking the land of the inhabitants of the hillfort. Alternatively, the carving may have been carried out during a Bronze or Iron Age ritual. Some researchers see the horse as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd374a31-ec6f-4b0d-be2e-0108d8d622b2\" data-question=\"12\">representing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> the Celtic horse goddess Epona, who was worshipped <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"615ba701-c63c-4c39-bc0f-06b6ed9f64a5\" data-question=\"12\">as a protector<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> of horses, and for her associations with fertility. However, the cult of Epona was not imported from Gaul (France) until around the first century CE. This date is at least six centuries after the Uffington Horse was probably carved. Nevertheless, the horse had great ritual and economic significance during the Bronze and Iron Ages, as attested by its depictions on jewellery and other metal objects. It is possible that the carving represents a goddess in native <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ea8e0ed-5248-4c2e-806e-72a48437e01f\" data-question=\"13\">mythology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, such as Rhiannon, described in later Welsh <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ea8e0ed-5248-4c2e-806e-72a48437e01f\" data-question=\"13\">mythology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> as a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ea8e0ed-5248-4c2e-806e-72a48437e01f\" data-question=\"13\">beautiful woman<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> dressed in gold and riding a white horse.</p><p>The fact that geoglyphs can disappear easily, along with their associated rituals and meaning, indicates that they were never intended to be anything more than temporary gestures. But this does not lessen their importance. These giant carvings are a fascinating glimpse into the minds of their creators and how they viewed the landscape in which they lived.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><strong>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</strong></p><p><em>In boxes <strong>1-8</strong> on your reading answer sheet, write:</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>TRUE</strong></td><td>if the statement agrees with the information</td></tr><tr><td><strong>FALSE</strong></td><td>if the statement contradicts the information</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong></td><td>If there is no information on this</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23644\" id=\"question-wrapper-23644\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e2884e48-532b-4833-87a7-427288ca59c4\" data-question=\"1\">Most<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> geoglyphs in England are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e66cedc-c435-4534-a12c-d8191c21ca8e\" data-question=\"1\">located in a particular area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of the country. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23645\" id=\"question-wrapper-23645\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There are more geoglyphs in the shape of a horse than any other creature. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23646\" id=\"question-wrapper-23646\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A recent dating of the Uffington White Horse indicates that people were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53b703b4-8560-4f5d-a06c-7ed3c601731b\" data-question=\"3\">mistaken about its age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23647\" id=\"question-wrapper-23647\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Historians have <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"316f0576-c26b-4509-8329-223ef9371755\" data-question=\"4\">come to an agreement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61ea4f4c-c1bf-467a-a2b7-dfc46a88a9b9\" data-question=\"4\">the origins of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the Long Man of Wilmington. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23648\" id=\"question-wrapper-23648\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"934e9be0-bc4c-4b89-8140-5228d09f1d2a\" data-question=\"5\">Geoglyphs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> were created by people <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0cfbab60-301d-4de0-aef1-09eee6d62cc7\" data-question=\"5\">placing white chalk on the hillside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23649\" id=\"question-wrapper-23649\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a31d2ee-f0ad-48e3-ac07-674688f622d0\" data-question=\"6\">geoglyphs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> in England are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7cf31953-6c6a-4e7d-b83c-4e8b37990666\" data-question=\"6\">no longer visible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23650\" id=\"question-wrapper-23650\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The shape of some geoglyphs has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55cddcaf-e67d-4c93-9686-3e94135ab985\" data-question=\"7\">altered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> over time. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23651\" id=\"question-wrapper-23651\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The fame of the Uffington White Horse is due to its size. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the notes below.</em></p><p><em>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>9-13 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><table><thead><tr><th>The Uffington White Horse</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><em>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4597a1b-de9e-4aa5-b711-c3072bbcc670\" data-question=\"9\">location<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of the Uffington White Horse:</em><br>🔘 a distance of 2.5 km from Uffington village<br>🔘 near an ancient <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca7a7a5e-4673-4c0b-8b51-2be59bf72533\" data-question=\"9\">road<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> known as the <strong>(9) </strong>………………………….<br>🔘 close to an ancient cemetery that has a number of burial mounds<br><br><em>Dating the Uffington White Horse:</em><br>🔘 first reference to White Horse Hill <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"875de638-227e-46c6-b862-876088814ecb\" data-question=\"10\">appears<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> in <strong>(10) </strong>…………………………. from the 1070s<br>🔘 horses shown on coins from the period 100 BCE – 1 BCE are similar in appearance<br>🔘 according to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a08eb999-db41-4d9b-8119-bd0b8ff000a3\" data-question=\"11\">analysis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89db7ef2-1d1c-47cd-8726-090258840d47\" data-question=\"11\">surrounding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <strong>(11) </strong>…………………………. , the Horse is Late Bronze age/Early Iron age<br><br><em>Possible reasons for creation of the Uffington White Horse:</em><br>🔘 an emblem to indicate land ownership<br>🔘 formed part of an ancient ritual<br>🔘 was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd374a31-ec6f-4b0d-be2e-0108d8d622b2\" data-question=\"12\">a representation of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> goddess Epona – associated with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"615ba701-c63c-4c39-bc0f-06b6ed9f64a5\" data-question=\"12\">protection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> of horses and <strong>(12)</strong> …………………………<br>🔘 was a representation of a Welsh <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ea8e0ed-5248-4c2e-806e-72a48437e01f\" data-question=\"13\">goddess<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> called <strong>(13)</strong> ………………………….</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23652\" id=\"question-wrapper-23652\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RIDGEWAY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23653\" id=\"question-wrapper-23653\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DOCUMENTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23654\" id=\"question-wrapper-23654\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOIL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23655\" id=\"question-wrapper-23655\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FERTILITY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23656\" id=\"question-wrapper-23656\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RHIANNON</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e2884e48-532b-4833-87a7-427288ca59c4","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"Most","passagePhrase":"vast majority"},{"uid":"8e66cedc-c435-4534-a12c-d8191c21ca8e","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"located in a particular area","passagePhrase":"downlands of the country’s southern counties"},{"uid":"53b703b4-8560-4f5d-a06c-7ed3c601731b","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"mistaken about its age","passagePhrase":"even older than its previously assigned"},{"uid":"61ea4f4c-c1bf-467a-a2b7-dfc46a88a9b9","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"the origins of","passagePhrase":"the date of"},{"uid":"934e9be0-bc4c-4b89-8140-5228d09f1d2a","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Geoglyphs","passagePhrase":"these huge figures"},{"uid":"7cf31953-6c6a-4e7d-b83c-4e8b37990666","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"no longer visible","passagePhrase":"have disappeared"},{"uid":"55cddcaf-e67d-4c93-9686-3e94135ab985","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"altered","passagePhrase":"change"},{"uid":"e4597a1b-de9e-4aa5-b711-c3072bbcc670","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"location","passagePhrase":"situated"},{"uid":"ca7a7a5e-4673-4c0b-8b51-2be59bf72533","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"road","passagePhrase":"track"},{"uid":"875de638-227e-46c6-b862-876088814ecb","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"appears","passagePhrase":"is mentioned"},{"uid":"a08eb999-db41-4d9b-8119-bd0b8ff000a3","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"analysis","passagePhrase":"testing"},{"uid":"89db7ef2-1d1c-47cd-8726-090258840d47","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"surrounding","passagePhrase":"two of the lower layers of the horse’s body ... another cut near the base"},{"uid":"dd374a31-ec6f-4b0d-be2e-0108d8d622b2","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"a representation of","passagePhrase":"representing"},{"uid":"615ba701-c63c-4c39-bc0f-06b6ed9f64a5","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"protection","passagePhrase":"as a protector"},{"uid":"9ea8e0ed-5248-4c2e-806e-72a48437e01f","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"goddess","passagePhrase":"mythology ... mythology ... beautiful woman"},{"uid":"6a31d2ee-f0ad-48e3-ac07-674688f622d0","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"geoglyphs","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_263":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 2 given below</em>.</p><h2>I contain multitudes</h2><p><em>Wendy Moore reviews Ed Yong’s book about microbes</em><br><br><strong>Microbes</strong>, most of them bacteria, have populated this planet since long before animal life developed and they will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea53de95-169e-4c9f-9d93-aa1f819e3b2c\" data-question=\"14\">outlive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> us. Invisible to the naked eye, they are ubiquitous. They inhabit the soil, air, rocks and water and are present within every form of life, from seaweed and coral to dogs and humans. And, as Yong explains in his utterly absorbing and hugely important book, we mess with them at our peril.<br><br>Every species has its own colony of microbes, called a <em>‘microbiome’</em>, and these microbes vary not only between species but also between individuals and within different parts of each individual. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"60229910-de95-4fde-a316-612fbd01c4ad\" data-question=\"15\">What is amazing is<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> that while the number of human cells in the average <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35bf2821-69ea-42c9-aea7-802e04ff2238\" data-question=\"15\">person<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> is<br>about 30 trillion, the number of microbial ones is higher — about 39 trillion. At best, Yong informs us, we are only 50 per cent human. Indeed, some scientists even suggest we should think of each species and its microbes as a single unit, dubbed a <em>‘holobiont’</em>.<br><br>In each human there are microbes that live only in the stomach, the mouth or the armpit and by and large they do so peacefully. So ‘bad’ microbes are just microbes out of context. Microbes that sit contentedly in the human gut (where there are more microbes than there are stars in the galaxy) can become deadly if they find their way into the bloodstream. These communities are constantly changing too. The right hand shares just one sixth of its microbes with the left hand. And, of course, we are surrounded by microbes. Every time we eat, we swallow a million microbes in each gram of food; we are continually swapping microbes with other humans, pets and the world at large.<br><br>It’s a fascinating topic and Yong, a young British science journalist, is an extraordinarily adept guide. Writing with lightness and panache, he has a knack of explaining complex science in terms that are both easy to understand and totally enthralling. Yong is on a mission. Leading us gently by the hand, he takes us into the world of microbes — a bizarre, alien planet — in a bid to persuade us to love them as much as he does. By the end, we do.<br><br>For most of human history we had no idea that microbes existed. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ac27822-9dab-48e1-862e-0b4d40ea54ea\" data-question=\"16\">first man to see<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> these extraordinarily potent creatures was a Dutch lens-maker called Antony van Leeuwenhoek in the 1670s. Using microscopes of his own design that could magnify up to 270 times, he examined a drop of water from a nearby lake and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ac27822-9dab-48e1-862e-0b4d40ea54ea\" data-question=\"16\">found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> it teeming with tiny creatures he called <em>‘animalcules’</em>. It wasn’t until nearly two hundred years later that the research of French biologist Louis Pasteur indicated that some microbes caused disease. It was Pasteur’s ‘germ theory’ that gave bacteria the poor image that endures today.<br><br>Yong’s book is in many ways a plea for microbial tolerance, pointing out that while <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"94535fae-2419-40ca-b618-6a188a4bb942\" data-question=\"17\">fewer than one hundred<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> species of bacteria bring <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9a22c0f-2e8c-436a-af13-6bb14736087a\" data-question=\"17\">disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, many thousands more play a vital role in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b92977f6-9909-40a3-b943-716d191643da\" data-question=\"17\">maintaining our health<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. The book also acknowledges that our attitude towards bacteria is not a simple one. We tend to see the dangers posed by bacteria, yet at the same time we are sold yoghurts and drinks that supposedly nurture ‘friendly’ bacteria. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c98444c-5d85-48dd-82e2-e96aeca53040\" data-question=\"18\">In reality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, says Yong, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f917004a-0a7d-4c33-9e78-8f774acce3ba\" data-question=\"18\">bacteria<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> should not be viewed as either friends or foes, villains or heroes. Instead we should realise we have a symbiotic relationship, that can be mutually beneficial or mutually destructive.</p><p>What then do these millions of organisms do? The answer is pretty much everything. New research is now unravelling the ways in which bacteria aid digestion, regulate our immune systems, eliminate toxins, produce vitamins, affect our behaviour and even combat obesity. ‘They actually help us become who we are,’ says Yong. But we are facing a growing problem. Our obsession with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5419b33e-178a-4419-bafe-cde9e11401f0\" data-question=\"20\">hygiene<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, our overuse of antibiotics and our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f701a1a6-0b22-49e8-a13a-18b7065c4a5b\" data-question=\"19\">unhealthy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, low-fibre <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21c41422-09e7-4081-bc47-021c98abb2cf\" data-question=\"19\">diets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b464c42-4eae-496e-a161-36ed84215171\" data-question=\"20\">disrupting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> the bacterial balance and may be responsible for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd156230-fada-453b-8ef0-58dace9565b4\" data-question=\"20\">soaring rates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of allergies and immune problems, such as inflammatory bowel disease (IBD).<br><br>The most recent research actually turns accepted norms upside down. For example, there are studies indicating that the excessive use of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c94e9680-9c94-4349-92ca-c8b5095c6f99\" data-question=\"21\">household<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> detergents and antibacterial products <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff101bab-0cd5-48cb-baea-0e9295a958b8\" data-question=\"21\">actually destroys the microbes that normally keep the more dangerous germs at bay<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. Other studies show that keeping a dog as a pet gives children early <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8cb6238b-b7e7-4115-aefe-c9710e24bf7d\" data-question=\"22\">exposure to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9a24e029-70fd-4f63-ba05-248f2f15d9a8\" data-question=\"22\">a diverse range of bacteria<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, which may help protect them against allergies later.<br><br>The readers of Yong’s book must be prepared for a decidedly unglamorous world. Among the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96def1f7-b5cc-48d4-89a4-a548442d9fb0\" data-question=\"24\">less appealing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> case studies is one about a fungus that is wiping out entire populations of frogs and that can be halted by a rare microbial bacterium. Another is about squid that carry luminescent bacteria that protect them against predators. However, if you can overcome your distaste for some of the investigations, the reasons for Yong’s enthusiasm become clear. The microbial world is a place of wonder. Already, in an attempt to stop mosquitoes spreading dengue fever — a disease that infects 400 million people a year — mosquitoes are being loaded with a bacterium to block the disease. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2155ac21-4191-4043-86d5-a710f885690f\" data-question=\"26\">In the future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, our ability to manipulate microbes means we could construct buildings with useful microbes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02fbac1b-f055-4717-b750-023b608b23b2\" data-question=\"26\">built into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> their walls to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"471c7c1c-b23c-4a89-be3d-83d629549bcf\" data-question=\"26\">fight off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> infections. Just imagine a neonatal hospital ward coated in a specially mixed cocktail of microbes so that babies get the best start in life.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose the correct letter- <strong>A,B,C or D.</strong></em></p><p><em>Write your answer in boxes <strong>14-16</strong> on your reading answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23657\" id=\"question-wrapper-23657\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does the writer make about microbes in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They adapt quickly to their environment.</li> <li>B. The risk they pose has been exaggerated.</li> <li>C. They are more plentiful in animal life than plant life.</li> <li>D. They will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea53de95-169e-4c9f-9d93-aa1f819e3b2c\" data-question=\"14\">continue to exist for longer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> than the human race.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23658\" id=\"question-wrapper-23658\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the second paragraph, the writer is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"60229910-de95-4fde-a316-612fbd01c4ad\" data-question=\"15\">impressed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> by the fact that… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. each species tends to have vastly different microbes.</li> <li>B. some parts of the body contain relatively few microbes.</li> <li>C. the average <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35bf2821-69ea-42c9-aea7-802e04ff2238\" data-question=\"15\">individual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> has more microbial cells than human ones.</li> <li>D. scientists have limited understanding of how microbial cells behave.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23659\" id=\"question-wrapper-23659\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer doing in the fifth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. explaining how a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ac27822-9dab-48e1-862e-0b4d40ea54ea\" data-question=\"16\">discovery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> was made</li> <li>B. comparing scientists’ theories about microbes</li> <li>C. describing confusion among scientists</li> <li>D. giving details of how microbes cause disease</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the summary below.</em></p><p><em>Choose the correct letter,<strong> A-H</strong>.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>17-20 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>A.</strong> solution<br><strong>B.</strong> partnership<br><strong>C.</strong> destruction<br><strong>D.</strong> exaggeration<br><strong>E. </strong><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5419b33e-178a-4419-bafe-cde9e11401f0\" data-question=\"20\">cleanliness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span><br><strong>F.</strong> regulations<br><strong>G.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9a22c0f-2e8c-436a-af13-6bb14736087a\" data-question=\"17\">illness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span><br><strong>H.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21c41422-09e7-4081-bc47-021c98abb2cf\" data-question=\"19\">nutrition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>We should be more tolerant of microbes</strong><br><br>Yong’s book argues that we should be more tolerant of microbes. Many have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b92977f6-9909-40a3-b943-716d191643da\" data-question=\"17\">beneficial effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, and only a relatively <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"94535fae-2419-40ca-b618-6a188a4bb942\" data-question=\"17\">small number<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> lead to <strong>(17)</strong> …………………………. . And although it is misleading to think of microbes as <em>friendly</em>, we should also stop thinking of them as the enemy. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c98444c-5d85-48dd-82e2-e96aeca53040\" data-question=\"18\">In fact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, we should accept that our relationship with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f917004a-0a7d-4c33-9e78-8f774acce3ba\" data-question=\"18\">microbes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> is one based on <strong>(18)</strong> ………………………….<br><br>New research shows that microbes have numerous benefits for humans. Amongst other things, they aid digestion, remove poisons, produce vitamins and may even help reduce obesity. However, there is a growing problem. Our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f701a1a6-0b22-49e8-a13a-18b7065c4a5b\" data-question=\"19\">poor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <strong>(19)</strong> …………………………. , our overuse of antibiotics, and our excessive focus on <strong>(20)</strong> …………………………. are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b464c42-4eae-496e-a161-36ed84215171\" data-question=\"20\">upsetting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> the bacterial balance and may be contributing to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd156230-fada-453b-8ef0-58dace9565b4\" data-question=\"20\">huge increase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in allergies and immune system problems.</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23660\" id=\"question-wrapper-23660\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23661\" id=\"question-wrapper-23661\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23662\" id=\"question-wrapper-23662\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23663\" id=\"question-wrapper-23663\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><strong>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2?</strong></p><p><em>In boxes <strong>21-26</strong> on your reading answer sheet, write:</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>YES</strong></td><td>if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NO</strong></td><td>if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong></td><td>If it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23664\" id=\"question-wrapper-23664\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is possible that using antibacterial products <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c94e9680-9c94-4349-92ca-c8b5095c6f99\" data-question=\"21\">in the home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff101bab-0cd5-48cb-baea-0e9295a958b8\" data-question=\"21\">fails to have the desired effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23665\" id=\"question-wrapper-23665\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is a good idea to ensure that children <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8cb6238b-b7e7-4115-aefe-c9710e24bf7d\" data-question=\"22\">come into contact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9a24e029-70fd-4f63-ba05-248f2f15d9a8\" data-question=\"22\">as few bacteria as possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23666\" id=\"question-wrapper-23666\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Yong’s book contains more case studies than are necessary. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23667\" id=\"question-wrapper-23667\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The case study about bacteria that prevent squid from being attacked may have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96def1f7-b5cc-48d4-89a4-a548442d9fb0\" data-question=\"24\">limited appeal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23668\" id=\"question-wrapper-23668\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Efforts to control dengue fever have been surprisingly successful. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23669\" id=\"question-wrapper-23669\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Microbes that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"471c7c1c-b23c-4a89-be3d-83d629549bcf\" data-question=\"26\">reduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> the risk of infection <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"2155ac21-4191-4043-86d5-a710f885690f\" data-question=\"26\">have already been<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02fbac1b-f055-4717-b750-023b608b23b2\" data-question=\"26\">put inside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> the walls of some hospital wards. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"ea53de95-169e-4c9f-9d93-aa1f819e3b2c","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"continue to exist for longer","passagePhrase":"outlive"},{"uid":"60229910-de95-4fde-a316-612fbd01c4ad","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"impressed","passagePhrase":"What is amazing is"},{"uid":"35bf2821-69ea-42c9-aea7-802e04ff2238","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"individual","passagePhrase":"person"},{"uid":"0ac27822-9dab-48e1-862e-0b4d40ea54ea","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"discovery","passagePhrase":"first man to see ... found"},{"uid":"94535fae-2419-40ca-b618-6a188a4bb942","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"small number","passagePhrase":"fewer than one hundred"},{"uid":"f9a22c0f-2e8c-436a-af13-6bb14736087a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"illness","passagePhrase":"disease"},{"uid":"b92977f6-9909-40a3-b943-716d191643da","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"beneficial effect","passagePhrase":"maintaining our health"},{"uid":"8c98444c-5d85-48dd-82e2-e96aeca53040","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"In fact","passagePhrase":"In reality"},{"uid":"f917004a-0a7d-4c33-9e78-8f774acce3ba","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"microbes","passagePhrase":"bacteria"},{"uid":"5419b33e-178a-4419-bafe-cde9e11401f0","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"cleanliness","passagePhrase":"hygiene"},{"uid":"f701a1a6-0b22-49e8-a13a-18b7065c4a5b","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"poor","passagePhrase":"unhealthy"},{"uid":"21c41422-09e7-4081-bc47-021c98abb2cf","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"nutrition","passagePhrase":"diets"},{"uid":"2b464c42-4eae-496e-a161-36ed84215171","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"upsetting","passagePhrase":"disrupting"},{"uid":"cd156230-fada-453b-8ef0-58dace9565b4","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"huge increase","passagePhrase":"soaring rates"},{"uid":"c94e9680-9c94-4349-92ca-c8b5095c6f99","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"in the home","passagePhrase":"household"},{"uid":"ff101bab-0cd5-48cb-baea-0e9295a958b8","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"fails to have the desired effect","passagePhrase":"actually destroys the microbes that normally keep the more dangerous germs at bay"},{"uid":"8cb6238b-b7e7-4115-aefe-c9710e24bf7d","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"come into contact","passagePhrase":"exposure to"},{"uid":"96def1f7-b5cc-48d4-89a4-a548442d9fb0","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"limited appeal","passagePhrase":"less appealing"},{"uid":"02fbac1b-f055-4717-b750-023b608b23b2","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"put inside","passagePhrase":"built into"},{"uid":"471c7c1c-b23c-4a89-be3d-83d629549bcf","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"reduce","passagePhrase":"fight off"}]},"reading_u2_264":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 3 given below</em>.</p><h2>How to make wise decisions</h2><p>Across cultures, wisdom has been considered one of the most revered human qualities. Although the truly wise may seem few and far between, empirical research examining wisdom suggests that it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43bffe8f-cec8-47c7-adfd-09ec0226f0d8\" data-question=\"27\">isn’t an exceptional trait possessed by a small handful of bearded philosophers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> after all — <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c99f719-f5bb-49c5-b60f-ff799670ae12\" data-question=\"27\">in fact, the latest studies suggest that most of us have the ability to make wise decisions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, given the right context.<br><br>‘It appears that experiential, situational, and cultural <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"007fde8f-c526-4ff7-b969-4867d429b76d\" data-question=\"28\">factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> are even more powerful in shaping wisdom than previously imagined,’ says Associate Professor Igor Grossmann of the University of Waterloo in Ontario, Canada. ‘Recent empirical findings from cognitive, developmental, social, and personality psychology cumulatively suggest that people’s ability to reason wisely varies dramatically across experiential and situational contexts. Understanding the role of such contextual factors offers unique insights into understanding wisdom in daily life, as well as how it can be enhanced and taught.’<br><br>It seems that it’s not so much that some people simply possess wisdom and others lack it, but that our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d22c22d4-769c-4570-b130-0f23a9954141\" data-question=\"29\">ability to reason wisely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> depends on a variety of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdf96e9d-6676-4369-97ea-f4e8b934a4a9\" data-question=\"29\">external factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. ‘It is impossible to characterize thought processes attributed to wisdom without considering the role of contextual factors,’ explains Grossmann. ‘In other words, wisdom is not solely an “inner quality” but rather unfolds as a function of situations people happen to be in. Some situations are more likely to promote wisdom than others.’<br><br>Coming up with a definition of wisdom is challenging, but Grossmann and his colleagues have identified <em>four key characteristics</em> as part of a framework of wise reasoning. One is intellectual <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4d96a52-9376-4c27-82e4-980d0529ff70\" data-question=\"31\">humility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> or recognition of the limits of our own knowledge, and another is appreciation of perspectives <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bddd1f30-b759-41ea-9991-a7b0d3b1e861\" data-question=\"33\">wider than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> the issue at hand. Sensitivity to the possibility of change in social relations is also key, along with compromise or integration of different <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b8304ea-392e-43dd-a3e0-65f50abdb4ae\" data-question=\"32\">attitudes and beliefs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.<br><br>Grossmann and his colleagues have also found that one of the most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35a608d7-658d-4136-b69b-7510e3edb76e\" data-question=\"30\">reliable ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to support wisdom in our own day-to-day decisions is to look at scenarios from a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79cc6c41-7ab8-4c8d-aff0-5f1ee3f35d6e\" data-question=\"34\">third-party perspective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, as though giving advice to a friend. Research suggests that when adopting a first-person viewpoint we focus on ‘the focal features of the environment’ and when we adopt a third-person, ‘observer’ viewpoint we reason more broadly and focus more on interpersonal and moral ideals such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c07472dc-9aa1-4bc4-984e-2c425aa78df3\" data-question=\"35\">justice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and impartiality. Looking at problems from this more expansive viewpoint appears to foster cognitive processes related to wise decisions.<br><br>What are we to do, then, when confronted with situations like a disagreement with a spouse or negotiating a contract at work, that require us to take a personal stake? Grossmann argues that even when we aren’t able to change the situation, we can still evaluate these experiences from different perspectives.<br><br>For example, in one experiment that took place during the peak of a recent economic recession, graduating college seniors were asked to reflect on their job prospects. The students were instructed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"30bd61f6-9782-4d23-849a-fd0bc7f25531\" data-question=\"36\">imagine their career<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> either ‘as if you were a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd3d631f-cea2-48a9-a2a8-a218b1f20f4c\" data-question=\"39\">distant observer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>’ or ‘before your own eyes as if you were right there’. Participants in the group <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"91600b02-f96f-419a-8469-9c05dcc212c3\" data-question=\"36\">assigned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> to the ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd3d631f-cea2-48a9-a2a8-a218b1f20f4c\" data-question=\"39\">distant observer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>’ role displayed more wisdom-related reasoning (intellectual humility and recognition of change) than did participants in the control group.<br><br>In another study, couples in long-term romantic relationships were instructed to visualize an unresolved relationship conflict either through the eyes of an outsider or from their own perspective. Participants then discussed the incident with their partner for 10 minutes, after which they wrote down their thoughts about it. Couples in the ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd3d631f-cea2-48a9-a2a8-a218b1f20f4c\" data-question=\"39\">other’s eyes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>’ condition were significantly more likely to rely on wise reasoning — recognizing others’ perspectives and searching for a compromise — compared to the couples in the egocentric condition.<br><br><strong>‘Ego-decentering</strong> promotes greater focus on others and enables a bigger picture, conceptual view of the experience, affording recognition of intellectual humility and change,’ says Grossmann.<br><br>We might <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13cedd5c-d6d7-460c-b04e-10f4423108a8\" data-question=\"40\">associate wisdom with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> intelligence or particular personality traits, but research shows only a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12452cb3-4348-42ae-a12e-dd1c5fffdae0\" data-question=\"40\">small positive relationship between wise thinking and crystallized intelligence and the personality traits of openness and agreeableness. ‘It is remarkable how much people can vary in their wisdom from one situation to the next, and how much stronger such contextual effects are for understanding the relationship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> between wise judgment and its social and affective outcomes as compared to the generalized “traits”,’ Grossmann explains. ‘That is, knowing how wisely a person behaves in a given situation is more informative for understanding their emotions or likelihood to forgive [or] retaliate as compared to knowing whether the person may be wise “in general”.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose the correct letter- <strong>A,B,C or D.</strong></em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>27</strong>–<strong>30</strong> on your reading answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23670\" id=\"question-wrapper-23670\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does the writer make in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Wisdom appears to be unique to the human race.</li> <li>B. A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43bffe8f-cec8-47c7-adfd-09ec0226f0d8\" data-question=\"27\">basic assumption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> about wisdom <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c99f719-f5bb-49c5-b60f-ff799670ae12\" data-question=\"27\">may be wrong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Concepts of wisdom may depend on the society we belong to.</li> <li>D. There is still much to be discovered about the nature of wisdom.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23671\" id=\"question-wrapper-23671\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does Igor Grossmann suggest about the ability to make wise decisions? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It can vary greatly from one person to another.</li> <li>B. Earlier research into it was based on unreliable data.</li> <li>C. The importance of certain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"007fde8f-c526-4ff7-b969-4867d429b76d\" data-question=\"28\">influences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> on it was underestimated.</li> <li>D. Various branches of psychology define it according to their own criteria.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23672\" id=\"question-wrapper-23672\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to the third paragraph, Grossmann claims that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d22c22d4-769c-4570-b130-0f23a9954141\" data-question=\"29\">level of wisdom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> an individual shows… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. can be greater than they think it is.</li> <li>B. will be different in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdf96e9d-6676-4369-97ea-f4e8b934a4a9\" data-question=\"29\">different circumstances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>C. may be determined by particular aspects of their personality.</li> <li>D. should develop over time as a result of their life experiences.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23673\" id=\"question-wrapper-23673\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is described in the fifth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. a difficulty encountered when attempting to reason wisely</li> <li>B. an example of the type of person who is likely to reason wisely</li> <li>C. a controversial view about the benefits of reasoning wisely</li> <li>D. a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35a608d7-658d-4136-b69b-7510e3edb76e\" data-question=\"30\">recommended strategy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that can help people to reason wisely</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the summary below.</em></p><p><em>Choose the correct letter,<strong> A-J</strong>.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>31-35 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>A.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b8304ea-392e-43dd-a3e0-65f50abdb4ae\" data-question=\"32\">opinions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span><br><strong>B.</strong> confidence<br><strong>C.</strong> view<br><strong>D.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4d96a52-9376-4c27-82e4-980d0529ff70\" data-question=\"31\">modesty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span><br><strong>E. </strong>problems<br><strong>F.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79cc6c41-7ab8-4c8d-aff0-5f1ee3f35d6e\" data-question=\"34\">objectivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span><br><strong>G.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c07472dc-9aa1-4bc4-984e-2c425aa78df3\" data-question=\"35\">fairness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span><br><strong>H.</strong> experiences<br><strong>I. </strong>range<br><strong>J. </strong>reasons</td></tr></tbody></table><p> </p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>The characteristics of wise reasoning</strong><br><br>Igor Grossman and colleagues have established four characteristics which enable us to make wise decisions. It is important to have a certain degree of <strong>(31)</strong> …………………………. regarding the extent of our knowledge, and to take into account <strong>(32)</strong> …………………………. which may not be the same as our own. We should also be able to take a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bddd1f30-b759-41ea-9991-a7b0d3b1e861\" data-question=\"33\">broad<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <strong>(33)</strong> …………………………. of any situation. Another key characteristic is being aware of the likelihood of alterations in the way that people relate to each other.<br><br>Grossmann also believes that it is better to regard scenarios with <strong>(34)</strong> …………………………. . By avoiding the first-person perspective, we focus more on <strong>(35)</strong> …………………………. and on other moral ideals, which in turn leads to wiser decision-making.</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23674\" id=\"question-wrapper-23674\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23675\" id=\"question-wrapper-23675\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23676\" id=\"question-wrapper-23676\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23677\" id=\"question-wrapper-23677\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23678\" id=\"question-wrapper-23678\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><strong>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?</strong></p><p><em>In boxes <strong>36-40</strong> on your reading answer sheet, write:</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>TRUE</strong></td><td>if the statement agrees with the information</td></tr><tr><td><strong>FALSE</strong></td><td>if the statement contradicts the information</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong></td><td>If there is no information on this</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23679\" id=\"question-wrapper-23679\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Students participating in the job prospects experiment <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"91600b02-f96f-419a-8469-9c05dcc212c3\" data-question=\"36\">could choose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> one of two perspectives to take. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23680\" id=\"question-wrapper-23680\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Participants in the couples experiment were aware that they were taking part in a study about wise reasoning. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23681\" id=\"question-wrapper-23681\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the couples experiment, the length of the couples’ relationship had an impact on the results. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23682\" id=\"question-wrapper-23682\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In both experiments, the participants who looked at the situation from a more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd3d631f-cea2-48a9-a2a8-a218b1f20f4c\" data-question=\"39\">detached viewpoint<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> tended to make wiser decisions. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23683\" id=\"question-wrapper-23683\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Grossmann believes that a person’s wisdom is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13cedd5c-d6d7-460c-b04e-10f4423108a8\" data-question=\"40\">determined by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> their intelligence to only a very <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12452cb3-4348-42ae-a12e-dd1c5fffdae0\" data-question=\"40\">limited extent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"43bffe8f-cec8-47c7-adfd-09ec0226f0d8","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"basic assumption","passagePhrase":"isn’t an exceptional trait possessed by a small handful of bearded philosophers"},{"uid":"6c99f719-f5bb-49c5-b60f-ff799670ae12","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"may be wrong","passagePhrase":"in fact, the latest studies suggest that most of us have the ability to make wise decisions"},{"uid":"007fde8f-c526-4ff7-b969-4867d429b76d","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"influences","passagePhrase":"factors"},{"uid":"d22c22d4-769c-4570-b130-0f23a9954141","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"level of wisdom","passagePhrase":"ability to reason wisely"},{"uid":"cdf96e9d-6676-4369-97ea-f4e8b934a4a9","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"different circumstances","passagePhrase":"external factors"},{"uid":"d4d96a52-9376-4c27-82e4-980d0529ff70","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"modesty","passagePhrase":"humility"},{"uid":"bddd1f30-b759-41ea-9991-a7b0d3b1e861","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"broad","passagePhrase":"wider than"},{"uid":"4b8304ea-392e-43dd-a3e0-65f50abdb4ae","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"opinions","passagePhrase":"attitudes and beliefs"},{"uid":"35a608d7-658d-4136-b69b-7510e3edb76e","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"recommended strategy","passagePhrase":"reliable ways"},{"uid":"79cc6c41-7ab8-4c8d-aff0-5f1ee3f35d6e","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"objectivity","passagePhrase":"third-party perspective"},{"uid":"c07472dc-9aa1-4bc4-984e-2c425aa78df3","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"fairness","passagePhrase":"justice"},{"uid":"30bd61f6-9782-4d23-849a-fd0bc7f25531","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"imagine their career"},{"uid":"cd3d631f-cea2-48a9-a2a8-a218b1f20f4c","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"detached viewpoint","passagePhrase":"distant observer ... distant observer ... other’s eyes"},{"uid":"13cedd5c-d6d7-460c-b04e-10f4423108a8","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"determined by","passagePhrase":"associate wisdom with"},{"uid":"12452cb3-4348-42ae-a12e-dd1c5fffdae0","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"limited extent","passagePhrase":"small positive relationship between wise thinking and crystallized intelligence and the personality traits of openness and agreeableness. ‘It is remarkable how much people can vary in their wisdom from one situation to the next, and how much stronger such contextual effects are for understanding the relationship"}]},"reading_u2_265":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 1-13</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 1 given below</em>.</p><h2>Roman shipbuilding and navigation</h2><p>Shipbuilding today is based on science and ships are built using computers and sophisticated tools. Shipbuilding in ancient Rome, however, was more of an art relying on estimation, inherited techniques and personal experience. The Romans were not traditionally sailors but mostly land- based people, who <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1dc93101-8501-4f81-9379-64d73de56a8e\" data-question=\"1\">learned to build ships from the people that they conquered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, namely the Greeks and the Egyptians.<br><br>There are a few surviving written documents that give descriptions and representations of ancient Roman ships, including the sails and rigging. Excavated vessels also provide some clues about ancient shipbuilding techniques. Studies of these have taught us that ancient Roman shipbuilders built the outer hull first, then proceeded with the frame and the rest of the ship. Planks used to build the outer hull were initially sewn together. Starting from the 6th century BCE, they were fixed using a method called mortise and tenon, whereby one plank locked into another without the need for stitching. Then in the first centuries of the current era, Mediterranean shipbuilders shifted to another shipbuilding <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82d8894e-9371-4fa4-a8d0-fb30299cb58d\" data-question=\"3\">method<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, still in use today, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f81ab072-fb0e-4b98-9a90-3c44cfe5a890\" data-question=\"3\">consisted of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"6a4d0696-d2dd-4db4-9864-d03b84da10b9\" data-question=\"3\">building the frame first and then proceeding with the hull<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> and the other components of the ship. This method was more systematic and dramatically shortened ship construction times. The ancient Romans built large merchant ships and warships whose size and technology were unequalled until the 16th century CE.<br><br>Warships were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5b3cc6c9-dcb5-43ce-8750-45c863996ebc\" data-question=\"6\">built<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> to be lightweight and very <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71d2694f-a8ad-4200-997f-b8e9b06e952d\" data-question=\"6\">speedy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. They had to be able to sail near the coast, which is why they had no ballast or excess load and were built with a long, narrow hull. They did not sink when damaged and often would lie crippled on the sea’s surface following naval battles. They had a bronze battering ram, which was used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d2b8c36-989a-4f37-80cb-a3e340d76ac1\" data-question=\"7\">pierce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the timber hulls or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d2b8c36-989a-4f37-80cb-a3e340d76ac1\" data-question=\"7\">break<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the oars of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f2035c8-3ea4-4313-b599-003318221a09\" data-question=\"7\">enemy vessels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. Warships used both wind (sails) and human power (oarsmen) and were therefore very fast. Eventually, Rome’s navy became the largest and most powerful in the Mediterranean, and the Romans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89354929-911f-45f7-b7fe-0cfcceeac0db\" data-question=\"4\">had control over<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> what they therefore called <em><strong>Mare Nostrum </strong></em>meaning ‘our sea’.<br><br>There were many kinds of warship. The ‘trireme was the dominant warship from the 7th to 4th century BCE. It had rowers in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e85696ff-cea5-4441-8bfd-1e2e6c71771a\" data-question=\"8\">top, middle and lower levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, and approximately 50 rowers in each bank. The rowers at the bottom had the most uncomfortable position as they were under the other rowers and were exposed to the water entering through the oar-holes. It is worth noting that contrary to popular perception, rowers were not slaves but mostly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc4030c8-2453-4395-a71f-f0cb359ab9f5\" data-question=\"5\">Roman citizens enrolled in the military<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. The trireme was superseded by larger ships with even more rowers.<br><br>Merchant ships were built to transport lots of cargo over long distances and at a reasonable cost. They had a wider hull, double planting and a solid interior for added stability. Unlike warships, their V-shaped hull was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2021e468-1058-40c1-a093-925d18baa81c\" data-question=\"9\">deep underwater<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, meaning that they could not sail too close to the coast. They usually had two huge side rudders located off the stern and controlled by a small tiller bar connected to a system of cables. They had from one to three masts with large square sails and a small triangular sail at the bow. Just like warships, merchant ships used oarsmen, but coordinating the hundreds of rowers in both types of ship was not an easy task. In order to assist them, music would be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f54beab-20b1-4b1c-b3ac-74984f541983\" data-question=\"11\">played<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> on an instrument, and oars would then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f0dbfa1-6a84-471f-8d35-0bda8c87fba2\" data-question=\"11\">keep time with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> this.<br><br>The cargo on merchant ships included raw materials (e.g. iron bars, copper, marble and granite), and agricultural <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd41082a-f0b9-4a5b-a531-7283387d49eb\" data-question=\"12\">products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (e.g. grain from Egypt’s Nile valley). During the Empire, Rome was a huge city by ancient standards of about one million inhabitants. Goods from all over the world would come to the city through the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ce38e2e-aa01-436e-8d17-b8e0b462983f\" data-question=\"12\">port of Pozzuoli<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> situated west of the bay of Naples in Italy and through the gigantic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ce38e2e-aa01-436e-8d17-b8e0b462983f\" data-question=\"12\">port of Ostia<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> situated at the mouth of the Tiber River. Large merchant ships would approach the destination port and, just like today, be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28efd94e-47c3-4bde-852d-9d786fa529cc\" data-question=\"13\">intercepted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> by a number of towboats that would drag them to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18d03859-94a2-4ae5-a46e-da57d13bd52f\" data-question=\"13\">quay<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.<br><br>The time of travel along the many sailing routes could vary widely. Navigation in ancient Rome did not rely on sophisticated instruments such as compasses but on experience, local knowledge and observation of natural phenomena. In conditions of good visibility, seamen in the Mediterranean often had the mainland or islands in sight, which greatly facilitated navigation. They sailed by noting their position relative to a succession of recognisable landmarks. When weather conditions were not good or where land was no longer visible, Roman mariners estimated directions from the pole star or, with less accuracy, from the Sun at noon. They also estimated directions relative to the wind and swell. Overall, shipping in ancient Roman times resembled shipping today with large vessels regularly crossing the seas and bringing supplies from their Empire.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><strong>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</strong></p><p><em>In boxes <strong>1-5</strong> on your reading answer sheet, write:</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>TRUE</strong></td><td>if the statement agrees with the information</td></tr><tr><td><strong>FALSE</strong></td><td>if the statement contradicts the information</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong></td><td>If there is no information on this</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23684\" id=\"question-wrapper-23684\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Romans’ shipbuilding skills <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1dc93101-8501-4f81-9379-64d73de56a8e\" data-question=\"1\">were passed on to the Greeks and the Egyptians<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23685\" id=\"question-wrapper-23685\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Skilled craftsmen were needed for the mortise and tenon method of fixing planks. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23686\" id=\"question-wrapper-23686\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The later <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82d8894e-9371-4fa4-a8d0-fb30299cb58d\" data-question=\"3\">practice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> used by Mediterranean shipbuilders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f81ab072-fb0e-4b98-9a90-3c44cfe5a890\" data-question=\"3\">involved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"6a4d0696-d2dd-4db4-9864-d03b84da10b9\" data-question=\"3\">building the hull before the frame<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23687\" id=\"question-wrapper-23687\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Romans called the Mediterranean Sea Mare Nostrum because they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89354929-911f-45f7-b7fe-0cfcceeac0db\" data-question=\"4\">dominated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> its use. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23688\" id=\"question-wrapper-23688\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Most rowers on ships were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc4030c8-2453-4395-a71f-f0cb359ab9f5\" data-question=\"5\">people from the Roman army<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the summary below.</em></p><p><em>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>6-13 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><table><thead><tr><th>Warships and Merchant ships</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Warships are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5b3cc6c9-dcb5-43ce-8750-45c863996ebc\" data-question=\"6\">designed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> so they were (6) …………………………. and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71d2694f-a8ad-4200-997f-b8e9b06e952d\" data-question=\"6\">moved quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. They often remained afloat after battles and were able to sail close to land as they lacked any additional weight. A battering ram made of <strong>(7) </strong>…………………………. was included in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"44fa2d68-069d-4eee-9ef9-6636f0fdc36c\" data-question=\"7\">the design for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d2b8c36-989a-4f37-80cb-a3e340d76ac1\" data-question=\"7\">attacking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and damaging the timber and oars of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f2035c8-3ea4-4313-b599-003318221a09\" data-question=\"7\">enemy ships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. Warships, such as the ‘trireme’, had rowers on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e85696ff-cea5-4441-8bfd-1e2e6c71771a\" data-question=\"8\">three different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <strong>(8) </strong>…………………………. .<br><br>Unlike warships, merchant ships had a broad <strong>(9) </strong>…………………………. that lay <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2021e468-1058-40c1-a093-925d18baa81c\" data-question=\"9\">far below the surface of the sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. Merchant ships were steered through the water with the help of large rudders and a tiller bar. They had both square and <strong>(10) </strong>…………………………. sails. On merchant ships and warships, <strong>(11) </strong>…………………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f54beab-20b1-4b1c-b3ac-74984f541983\" data-question=\"11\">was used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> to ensure rowers moved their oars in and out of the water <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f0dbfa1-6a84-471f-8d35-0bda8c87fba2\" data-question=\"11\">at the same time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.<br><br>Quantities of agricultural <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd41082a-f0b9-4a5b-a531-7283387d49eb\" data-question=\"12\">goods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> such as <strong>(12)</strong> ………………………… were transported by merchant ships to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ce38e2e-aa01-436e-8d17-b8e0b462983f\" data-question=\"12\">two main ports<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in Italy. The ships were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28efd94e-47c3-4bde-852d-9d786fa529cc\" data-question=\"13\">pulled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18d03859-94a2-4ae5-a46e-da57d13bd52f\" data-question=\"13\">shore<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> by <strong>(13)</strong> …………………………. . When the weather was clear and they could see islands or land, sailors used landmarks that they knew to help them navigate their route.</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23689\" id=\"question-wrapper-23689\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LIGHTWEIGHT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23690\" id=\"question-wrapper-23690\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BRONZE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23691\" id=\"question-wrapper-23691\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LEVELS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23692\" id=\"question-wrapper-23692\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HULL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23693\" id=\"question-wrapper-23693\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRIANGULAR</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23694\" id=\"question-wrapper-23694\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MUSIC</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23695\" id=\"question-wrapper-23695\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GRAIN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23696\" id=\"question-wrapper-23696\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TOWBOATS</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"82d8894e-9371-4fa4-a8d0-fb30299cb58d","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"practice","passagePhrase":"method"},{"uid":"f81ab072-fb0e-4b98-9a90-3c44cfe5a890","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"involved","passagePhrase":"consisted of"},{"uid":"5b3cc6c9-dcb5-43ce-8750-45c863996ebc","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"designed","passagePhrase":"built"},{"uid":"71d2694f-a8ad-4200-997f-b8e9b06e952d","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"moved quickly","passagePhrase":"speedy"},{"uid":"5d2b8c36-989a-4f37-80cb-a3e340d76ac1","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"attacking","passagePhrase":"pierce ... break"},{"uid":"9f2035c8-3ea4-4313-b599-003318221a09","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"enemy ships","passagePhrase":"enemy vessels"},{"uid":"89354929-911f-45f7-b7fe-0cfcceeac0db","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"dominated","passagePhrase":"had control over"},{"uid":"e85696ff-cea5-4441-8bfd-1e2e6c71771a","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"three different","passagePhrase":"top, middle and lower levels"},{"uid":"bc4030c8-2453-4395-a71f-f0cb359ab9f5","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"people from the Roman army","passagePhrase":"Roman citizens enrolled in the military"},{"uid":"2021e468-1058-40c1-a093-925d18baa81c","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"far below the surface of the sea","passagePhrase":"deep underwater"},{"uid":"2f54beab-20b1-4b1c-b3ac-74984f541983","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"was used","passagePhrase":"played"},{"uid":"9f0dbfa1-6a84-471f-8d35-0bda8c87fba2","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"at the same time","passagePhrase":"keep time with"},{"uid":"bd41082a-f0b9-4a5b-a531-7283387d49eb","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"goods","passagePhrase":"products"},{"uid":"7ce38e2e-aa01-436e-8d17-b8e0b462983f","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"two main ports","passagePhrase":"port of Pozzuoli ... port of Ostia"},{"uid":"28efd94e-47c3-4bde-852d-9d786fa529cc","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"pulled","passagePhrase":"intercepted"},{"uid":"18d03859-94a2-4ae5-a46e-da57d13bd52f","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"shore","passagePhrase":"quay"},{"uid":"44fa2d68-069d-4eee-9ef9-6636f0fdc36c","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"the design for","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_266":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 2 given below</em>.</p><h2>Climate change reveals ancient artefacts in Norway’s glaciers</h2><p><strong>A.</strong><br>Well above the treeline in Norway’s highest mountains, ancient fields of ice are shrinking as Earth’s climate warms. As the ice has vanished, it has been giving up the treasures it has preserved in cold storage for the last 6,000 years — items such as ancient arrows and skis from Viking Age* traders. And those artefacts have provided archaeologists with some surprising insights into how ancient Norwegians made their livings.<br><br><strong>B.</strong><br>Organic materials like textiles and hides are relatively rare finds at archaeological sites. This is because unless they’re <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f8c0ef00-65b5-4d62-8bcf-85169b59a3ac\" data-question=\"20\">protected from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> the microorganisms that cause decay, they tend <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"784dab0c-2a1f-488f-b284-c87f7c2b9c55\" data-question=\"20\">not to last long<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. Extreme cold is one reliable way to keep artefacts relatively fresh for a few thousand years, but once thawed out, these materials experience degradation relatively swiftly.<br><br>With climate change shrinking ice cover around the world, glacial archaeologists need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12247d08-6fa0-47b7-8e34-c8d0f093a267\" data-question=\"19\">race the clock<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> to find newly revealed artefacts, preserve them, and study them. If something fragile dries and is windblown it might very soon be lost to science, or an arrow might be exposed and then covered again by the next snow and remain well-preserved. The unpredictability means that glacial archaeologists have to be systematic in their approach to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb12da64-e72e-499d-bc7a-3de8897ee6a5\" data-question=\"15\">fieldwork<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.<br><br><strong>C.</strong><br>Over a nine-year period, a team of archaeologists, which included Lars Pilo of Oppland County Council, Norway, and James Barrett of the McDonald Institute for Archaeological Research, surveyed patches of ice in Oppland, an area of south-central Norway that is home to some of the country’s highest mountains. Reindeer once <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"45bbceb5-4840-4119-bbdd-97a42959d6c6\" data-question=\"21\">congregated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> on these icy patches in the later summer months to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2bc6d79e-fc72-4c4a-a9b0-8d55fec197f6\" data-question=\"22\">escape<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> biting insects, and from the late Stone Age**, hunters followed. In addition, trade routes threaded through the mountain passes of Oppland, linking settlements in Norway to the rest of Europe.<br><br>The slow but steady movement of glaciers tends to destroy anything at their bases, so the team focused on stationary patches of ice, mostly above 1,400 metres. That ice is found amid fields of frost-weathered boulders, fallen rocks, and exposed bedrock that for nine months of the year is buried beneath snow.<br><br>‘Fieldwork is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a60aebf9-56ac-420e-bbb8-5f558c2ac8c4\" data-question=\"15\">hard work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> — hiking with all our equipment, often camping on permafrost — but very rewarding. You’re rescuing the archaeology, bringing the melting ice to wider attention, discovering a unique environmental history and really connecting with the natural environment,’ says Barrett.<br><br><strong>D.</strong><br>At the edges of the contracting ice patches, archaeologists found more than 2,000 artefacts, which formed a material record that ran from 4,000 BCE to the beginnings of the Renaissance in the 14th century. Many of the artefacts are associated with hunting. Hunters would have easily misplaced <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6899d8c7-8814-4e3d-b4a1-59a585c47911\" data-question=\"14\">arrows<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and they often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f1b354ae-d8a8-4d56-93b6-2b2046999b75\" data-question=\"14\">discarded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> broken <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6899d8c7-8814-4e3d-b4a1-59a585c47911\" data-question=\"14\">bows<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> rather than take them all the way home. Other items could have been used by hunters traversing the high mountain passes of Oppland: all-purpose items like tools, skis, and horse tack.<br><br><strong>E.</strong><br>Barrett’s team radiocarbon-dated 153 of the artefacts and compared those dates to the timing of major environmental changes in the region — such as periods of cooling or warming — and major social and economic shifts — such as the growth of farming settlements and the spread of international trade networks leading up to the Viking Age. They found that some periods had produced lots of artefacts, which indicates that people had been pretty active in the mountains during those times. But there were few or no signs of activity during other periods.<br><br><strong>F.</strong><br>What was surprising, according to Barrett, was the timing of these periods. Oppland’s mountains present daunting terrain and in periods of extreme cold, glaciers could block the higher mountain passes and make travel in the upper reaches of the mountains extremely difficult. Archaeologists assumed people would stick to lower elevations during a time like the Late Antique Little Ice Age, a short period of deeper-than-usual cold from about 536-600 CE. But it turned out that hunters kept regularly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8900c9e0-d4e7-4e42-b613-1b9c34501adf\" data-question=\"23\">venturing into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> the mountains even when the climate turned cold, based on the amount of stuff they had apparently dropped there.<br><br>‘Remarkably, though, the finds from the ice may have continued through this period, perhaps suggesting that the importance of mountain hunting increased to supplement failing agricultural harvests in times of low temperatures,’ says Barrett. A colder turn in the Scandinavian climate would likely have meant widespread <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"312b0ed2-1f08-4f2c-9a4d-e27be454ec94\" data-question=\"16\">crop failures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, so more people would have depended on hunting to make up for those losses.<br><br><strong>G.</strong><br>Many of the artefacts Barrett’s team recovered date from the beginning of the Viking Age, the 700s through to the 900s CE. Trade networks connecting Scandinavia with Europe and the Middle East were expanding around this time. Although we usually think of ships when we think of Scandinavian expansion, these recent discoveries show that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a36961f5-72aa-43dc-b409-4465750c030f\" data-question=\"26\">plenty of goods travelled on overland routes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, like the mountain passes of Oppland. And growing Norwegian towns, along with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"274a074d-076b-4c25-a1c5-a86c89fc3714\" data-question=\"18\">export markets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, would have created a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"803b7715-5ccb-4c2d-b09d-67ef21f19c6f\" data-question=\"25\">booming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> demand for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c114042f-3b9f-4715-be1c-c5e4d5dda795\" data-question=\"18\">hides<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to fight off the cold, as well as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c114042f-3b9f-4715-be1c-c5e4d5dda795\" data-question=\"18\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84c49b9f-408e-4366-aca9-830afd05601b\" data-question=\"25\">antlers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to make useful things like combs. Business must have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1bda3e52-971c-4a01-a89a-9337e56a2681\" data-question=\"25\">good<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> for hunters.<br><br><strong>H.</strong><br>Norway’s mountains are probably still hiding a lot of history — and prehistory — in remote ice patches. When Barrett’s team looked at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f575c9e-8a6b-4fd4-9af8-82cf1992b4a3\" data-question=\"24\">the dates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> for their sample of 153 artefacts, they noticed a gap with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98c3e6a3-9100-4e8d-8fff-c69688c1ae01\" data-question=\"24\">almost no<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> artefacts from about 3,800 to 2,200 BCE. In fact, archaeological finds from that period are rare all over Norway. The researchers say that could be because many of those artefacts have already disintegrated or are still frozen in the ice. That means <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7ed743c-a76f-4ed3-a930-618204345e71\" data-question=\"17\">archaeologists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> could be extracting some of those artefacts from retreating ice <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d6d41d9-9acb-4800-a033-cfe509b2dd38\" data-question=\"17\">in years to come<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Reading Passage 2 has eight sections, <strong>A-H</strong></em></p><p><strong>Which section contains the following information?</strong></p><p><em>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A-H.</strong></em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>14-19</strong> on your reading answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23697\" id=\"question-wrapper-23697\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6899d8c7-8814-4e3d-b4a1-59a585c47911\" data-question=\"14\">weapons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f1b354ae-d8a8-4d56-93b6-2b2046999b75\" data-question=\"14\">left behind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in the mountains </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23698\" id=\"question-wrapper-23698\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a60aebf9-56ac-420e-bbb8-5f558c2ac8c4\" data-question=\"15\">physical difficulties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> involved in an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb12da64-e72e-499d-bc7a-3de8897ee6a5\" data-question=\"15\">archaeological expedition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23699\" id=\"question-wrapper-23699\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"312b0ed2-1f08-4f2c-9a4d-e27be454ec94\" data-question=\"16\">less food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> may have been available </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23700\" id=\"question-wrapper-23700\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to the possibility of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d6d41d9-9acb-4800-a033-cfe509b2dd38\" data-question=\"17\">future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7ed743c-a76f-4ed3-a930-618204345e71\" data-question=\"17\">archaeological discoveries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23701\" id=\"question-wrapper-23701\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c114042f-3b9f-4715-be1c-c5e4d5dda795\" data-question=\"18\">items<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that would have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"274a074d-076b-4c25-a1c5-a86c89fc3714\" data-question=\"18\">traded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23702\" id=\"question-wrapper-23702\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to the pressure archaeologists are under to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12247d08-6fa0-47b7-8e34-c8d0f093a267\" data-question=\"19\">work quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the summary below.</em></p><p><em>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>20-22 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><table><thead><tr><th>Interesting finds at an archaeological site</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Organic materials such as animal skins and textiles are not discovered very often at archaeological sites. They have little <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f8c0ef00-65b5-4d62-8bcf-85169b59a3ac\" data-question=\"20\">protection against<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> (20) …………………………. , which means that they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"784dab0c-2a1f-488f-b284-c87f7c2b9c55\" data-question=\"20\">decay relatively quickly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. But this is not always the case. If temperatures are low enough, fragile artefacts can be preserved for thousands of years.<br><br>A team of archaeologists have been working in the mountains in Oppland in Norway to recover artefacts revealed by shrinking ice cover. In the past, there were trade routes through these mountains and <strong>(21) </strong>…………………………. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"45bbceb5-4840-4119-bbdd-97a42959d6c6\" data-question=\"21\">gathered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> there in the summer months to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2bc6d79e-fc72-4c4a-a9b0-8d55fec197f6\" data-question=\"22\">avoid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> being attacked by <strong>(22)</strong> ………………………… on lower ground. The people who used these mountains left things behind and it is those objects that are of interest to archaeologists.</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23703\" id=\"question-wrapper-23703\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MICROORGANISMS/MICRO-ORGANISMS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23704\" id=\"question-wrapper-23704\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">REINDEER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23705\" id=\"question-wrapper-23705\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INSECTS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E</strong></em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>23 &amp; 24 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><p> </p><p><strong>Which TWO of the following statements does the writer make about the discoveries of Barrett’s team?</strong></p><p><strong>A. </strong>Artefacts found in the higher mountain passes were limited to skiing equipment.</p><p><strong>B.</strong> Hunters <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8900c9e0-d4e7-4e42-b613-1b9c34501adf\" data-question=\"23\">went into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> the mountains even during periods of extreme cold.</p><p><strong>C.</strong> The number of artefacts from certain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f575c9e-8a6b-4fd4-9af8-82cf1992b4a3\" data-question=\"24\">time periods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98c3e6a3-9100-4e8d-8fff-c69688c1ae01\" data-question=\"24\">relatively low<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</p><p><strong>D.</strong> Radiocarbon dating of artefacts produced some unreliable results.</p><p><strong>E. </strong>More artefacts were found in Oppland than at any other mountain site.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23706\" id=\"question-wrapper-23706\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23707\" id=\"question-wrapper-23707\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose <strong>TWO</strong> letters, <strong>A-E</strong></em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>25 &amp; 26 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><p><strong>Which TWO of the following statements does the writer make about the Viking Age?</strong></p><p><strong>A. </strong>Hunters at this time <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1bda3e52-971c-4a01-a89a-9337e56a2681\" data-question=\"25\">benefited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> from an increased <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"84c49b9f-408e-4366-aca9-830afd05601b\" data-question=\"25\">demand for goods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</p><p><strong>B.</strong> The beginning of the period saw the greatest growth in the wealth of Vikings.</p><p><strong>C.</strong> Vikings did <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a36961f5-72aa-43dc-b409-4465750c030f\" data-question=\"26\">not rely on ships alone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> to transport goods.</p><p><strong>D.</strong> Norwegian towns at this time attracted traders from around the world.</p><p><strong>E. </strong>Vikings were primarily interested in their trading links with the Middle East.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23708\" id=\"question-wrapper-23708\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23709\" id=\"question-wrapper-23709\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f8c0ef00-65b5-4d62-8bcf-85169b59a3ac","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"protection against","passagePhrase":"protected from"},{"uid":"784dab0c-2a1f-488f-b284-c87f7c2b9c55","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"decay relatively quickly","passagePhrase":"not to last long"},{"uid":"12247d08-6fa0-47b7-8e34-c8d0f093a267","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"work quickly","passagePhrase":"race the clock"},{"uid":"fb12da64-e72e-499d-bc7a-3de8897ee6a5","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"archaeological expedition","passagePhrase":"fieldwork"},{"uid":"45bbceb5-4840-4119-bbdd-97a42959d6c6","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"gathered","passagePhrase":"congregated"},{"uid":"2bc6d79e-fc72-4c4a-a9b0-8d55fec197f6","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"avoid","passagePhrase":"escape"},{"uid":"a60aebf9-56ac-420e-bbb8-5f558c2ac8c4","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"physical difficulties","passagePhrase":"hard work"},{"uid":"6899d8c7-8814-4e3d-b4a1-59a585c47911","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"weapons","passagePhrase":"arrows ... bows"},{"uid":"f1b354ae-d8a8-4d56-93b6-2b2046999b75","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"left behind","passagePhrase":"discarded"},{"uid":"8900c9e0-d4e7-4e42-b613-1b9c34501adf","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"went into","passagePhrase":"venturing into"},{"uid":"312b0ed2-1f08-4f2c-9a4d-e27be454ec94","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"less food","passagePhrase":"crop failures"},{"uid":"a36961f5-72aa-43dc-b409-4465750c030f","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"not rely on ships alone","passagePhrase":"plenty of goods travelled on overland routes"},{"uid":"274a074d-076b-4c25-a1c5-a86c89fc3714","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"traded","passagePhrase":"export markets"},{"uid":"803b7715-5ccb-4c2d-b09d-67ef21f19c6f","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"booming"},{"uid":"c114042f-3b9f-4715-be1c-c5e4d5dda795","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"items","passagePhrase":"hides ... antlers"},{"uid":"84c49b9f-408e-4366-aca9-830afd05601b","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"demand for goods","passagePhrase":"antlers"},{"uid":"1bda3e52-971c-4a01-a89a-9337e56a2681","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"benefited","passagePhrase":"good"},{"uid":"6f575c9e-8a6b-4fd4-9af8-82cf1992b4a3","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"time periods","passagePhrase":"the dates"},{"uid":"98c3e6a3-9100-4e8d-8fff-c69688c1ae01","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"relatively low","passagePhrase":"almost no"},{"uid":"b7ed743c-a76f-4ed3-a930-618204345e71","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"archaeological discoveries","passagePhrase":"archaeologists"},{"uid":"3d6d41d9-9acb-4800-a033-cfe509b2dd38","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"future","passagePhrase":"in years to come"}]},"reading_u2_267":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 3 given below</em>.</p><h2>Plant ‘thermometer’ triggers springtime growth by measuring night-time heat</h2><p><strong><em>A photoreceptor molecule in plant cells has been found to have a second job as a thermometer after dark – allowing plants </em>to <em>read seasonal temperature changes. Scientists say the discovery could help breed crops that are more resilient to the temperatures expected </em>to <em>result from climate change</em>.</strong><br><br><strong>A.</strong><br>An international team of scientists led by the University of Cambridge has discovered that the ‘thermometer’ molecule in plants enables them to develop according to seasonal temperature changes. Researchers have revealed that molecules called <strong>phytochromes</strong> — used by plants to detect light during the day actually change their function in darkness to become cellular temperature gauges that measure the heat of the night.<br><br>The new findings, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdad94f9-7283-4a46-bb1e-49ab94bb4491\" data-question=\"37\">published<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in the journal <em>Science, </em>show that phytochromes control genetic switches in response to temperature as well as light to dictate plant development.<br><br><strong>B.</strong><br>At night, these molecules change states, and the pace at which they change is ‘directly proportional to temperature’, say scientists, who compare phytochromes to mercury in a thermometer. The warmer it is, the faster the molecular change — stimulating plant growth.<br><br><strong>C.</strong><br>Farmers and gardeners have known for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9c9c43b-e8f2-470c-8eb9-fe088edc9722\" data-question=\"36\">hundreds of years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ac1c1c1-76af-4469-a581-7cab90a8d43e\" data-question=\"36\">how responsive plants are<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> to temperature: warm winters cause many trees and flowers to bud early, something humans have long used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3543eb43-0fb8-4a96-a006-c5ae4fd71fcf\" data-question=\"36\">predict<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> weather and harvest times for the coming year. The latest research pinpoints for the first time a molecular mechanism in plants that reacts to temperature — often triggering the buds of spring we long to see at the end of winter.<br><br><strong>D.</strong><br>With weather and temperatures set to become ever more unpredictable due to climate change, researchers say the discovery that this light-sensing molecule also functions as the internal thermometer in plant cells could help us breed tougher crops. ‘It is estimated that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23028a2a-8f3a-4b48-8175-5a904403d2ef\" data-question=\"28\">agricultural yields<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> will need to double by 2050, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de12ccaf-c073-4cde-af50-9b1c9a135d31\" data-question=\"28\">climate change is a major threat to achieving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> this. Key crops such as wheat and rice are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f6a840ea-6983-4742-8ac1-e645d630b9f1\" data-question=\"29\">sensitive to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d814abf5-1b21-400b-a9df-90a1fdff064f\" data-question=\"29\">high temperatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Thermal stress reduces crop yields by around 10% for every one degree increase in temperature,’ says lead researcher Dr Philip Wigge from Cambridge’s Sainsbury Laboratory. ‘Discovering the molecules that allow plants to sense temperature has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b631202e-4f05-43f0-8427-3cab1640f6f8\" data-question=\"34\">the potential to accelerate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> the breeding of crops resilient to thermal stress and climate change.’<br><br><strong>E.</strong><br>In their active state, phytochrome molecules bind themselves to DNA to restrict plant growth. During the day, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f6af540e-b856-488f-9632-3f3c02d023db\" data-question=\"31\">sunlight activates the molecules, slowing down growth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. If a plant finds itself in shade, phytochromes are quickly inactivated — enabling it to grow faster to find sunlight again. This is how plants compete to escape each other’s shade. ‘Light-driven changes to phytochrome activity occur very fast, in less than a second,’ says Wigge.<br><br>At night, however, it’s a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"259623f7-c9a3-42c1-b761-cd3a56aa4bbb\" data-question=\"32\">different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> story. Instead of a rapid deactivation following sundown, the molecules gradually change from their active to inactive state. This is called ‘dark reversion’. ‘Just as mercury rises in a thermometer, the rate at which phytochromes revert to their inactive state during the night is a direct measure of temperature,’ says Wigge.<br><br><strong>F.</strong><br>‘The lower the temperature, the slower the rate at which phytochromes revert to inactivity, so the molecules spend more time in their active, growth-suppressing state. This is why plants are slower to grow in winter. Warm temperatures accelerate dark reversion, so that phytochromes rapidly reach an inactive state and detach themselves from the plant’s DNA — allowing genes to be expressed and plant growth to resume.’ Wigge believes phytochrome thermo-sensing evolved at a later stage, and co-opted the biological network already used for light-based growth during the downtime of night.<br><br><strong>G.</strong><br>Some plants mainly use day length as an indicator of the season. Other species, such as daffodils, have considerable temperature sensitivity, and can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89887cc3-3e8d-4b7b-bb63-9d8441980476\" data-question=\"38\">flower months in advance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> during a warm winter. In fact, ie discovery of the dual role of phytochromes provides the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d57182df-6846-436e-82b1-347caced0012\" data-question=\"35\">science behind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46cb10a8-4709-40e8-8422-894ac0f079b4\" data-question=\"35\">well-known rhyme long used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> to predict the coming season: oak before ash we’ll have a splash, ash before oak we’re in for a soak.<br><br>Wigge explains: ‘Oak trees rely much more on temperature, likely using phytochromes as thermometers to dictate development, whereas ash trees rely on measuring day length to determine their seasonal timing. A warmer spring, and consequently a higher <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b8770ac0-a617-4901-b2fd-2c883ffe271b\" data-question=\"39\">likeliness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of a hot summer, will result in oak <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b27dede-e6d8-496d-8b14-fc3ad22556b6\" data-question=\"39\">leafing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> before ash. A cold spring will see the opposite. As the British know only too well, a colder summer is likely to be a rain-soaked one.’<br><br><strong>H.</strong><br>The new findings are the culmination of twelve years of research involving <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c930abc-10d6-4afc-9f4e-76594b10d9b0\" data-question=\"33\">scientists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> from Germany, Argentina and the US, as well as the Cambridge team. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd80f0e9-f831-4fff-9294-0adbf69547fc\" data-question=\"40\">work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"377f4583-ba07-40af-a5c8-ef254c7efd1b\" data-question=\"40\">done<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> in a model system, using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12f2cda0-4b96-4bfa-a7f5-353ec1d69dd1\" data-question=\"40\">a mustard plant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> called <em>Arabidopsis, </em>but Wigge says the phytochrome genes necessary for temperature sensing are found in crop plants as well. ‘Recent advances in plant genetics now mean that scientists are able to rapidly identify the genes controlling these processes in crop plants, and even alter their activity using precise molecular “scalpels”,’ adds Wigge. ‘Cambridge is uniquely well-positioned to do this kind of research as we have outstanding collaborators nearby who work on more applied aspects of plant biology, and can help us transfer this new knowledge into the field.’</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><strong>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</strong></p><p><em>In boxes <strong>27-32</strong> on your reading answer sheet, write:</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>TRUE</strong></td><td>if the statement agrees with the information</td></tr><tr><td><strong>FALSE</strong></td><td>if the statement contradicts the information</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong></td><td>If there is no information on this</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23710\" id=\"question-wrapper-23710\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Cambridge scientists’ discovery of the ‘thermometer molecule’ caused surprise among other scientists. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23711\" id=\"question-wrapper-23711\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The target for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23028a2a-8f3a-4b48-8175-5a904403d2ef\" data-question=\"28\">agricultural production<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> by 2050 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de12ccaf-c073-4cde-af50-9b1c9a135d31\" data-question=\"28\">could be missed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23712\" id=\"question-wrapper-23712\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Wheat and rice <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f6a840ea-6983-4742-8ac1-e645d630b9f1\" data-question=\"29\">suffer from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d814abf5-1b21-400b-a9df-90a1fdff064f\" data-question=\"29\">rise in temperatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23713\" id=\"question-wrapper-23713\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It may be possible to develop crops that require less water. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23714\" id=\"question-wrapper-23714\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f6af540e-b856-488f-9632-3f3c02d023db\" data-question=\"31\">Plants grow faster in sunlight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> than in shade. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23715\" id=\"question-wrapper-23715\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Phytochromes change their state at the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"259623f7-c9a3-42c1-b761-cd3a56aa4bbb\" data-question=\"32\">same<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> speed day and night. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Reading Passage 3 has eight sections, <strong>A-H</strong></em></p><p><strong>Which section contains the following information?</strong></p><p><em>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A-H.</strong></em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>33-37</strong> on your reading answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23716\" id=\"question-wrapper-23716\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mentions of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c930abc-10d6-4afc-9f4e-76594b10d9b0\" data-question=\"33\">specialists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> who can make use of the research findings </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23717\" id=\"question-wrapper-23717\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b631202e-4f05-43f0-8427-3cab1640f6f8\" data-question=\"34\">a potential benefit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> of the research findings </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23718\" id=\"question-wrapper-23718\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d57182df-6846-436e-82b1-347caced0012\" data-question=\"35\">scientific support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46cb10a8-4709-40e8-8422-894ac0f079b4\" data-question=\"35\">a traditional saying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23719\" id=\"question-wrapper-23719\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9c9c43b-e8f2-470c-8eb9-fe088edc9722\" data-question=\"36\">traditionally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3543eb43-0fb8-4a96-a006-c5ae4fd71fcf\" data-question=\"36\">making plans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> based on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ac1c1c1-76af-4469-a581-7cab90a8d43e\" data-question=\"36\">plant behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23720\" id=\"question-wrapper-23720\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to where the research has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cdad94f9-7283-4a46-bb1e-49ab94bb4491\" data-question=\"37\">reported<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the sentences below</em>.</p><p><em>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>38</strong>–<strong>40</strong> on your reading answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23721\" id=\"question-wrapper-23721\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Daffodils <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"078f48bb-039f-41fe-aa3b-e533838289e7\" data-question=\"38\">are likely to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"89887cc3-3e8d-4b7b-bb63-9d8441980476\" data-question=\"38\">flower early<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> in response to …………………………….. weather. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WARM (WINTER)</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23722\" id=\"question-wrapper-23722\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> If ash trees <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b27dede-e6d8-496d-8b14-fc3ad22556b6\" data-question=\"39\">come into leaf<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> before oak trees, the weather in …………………………….. will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b8770ac0-a617-4901-b2fd-2c883ffe271b\" data-question=\"39\">probably<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> be wet. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(COLDER) SUMMER</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23723\" id=\"question-wrapper-23723\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd80f0e9-f831-4fff-9294-0adbf69547fc\" data-question=\"40\">research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"377f4583-ba07-40af-a5c8-ef254c7efd1b\" data-question=\"40\">carried out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12f2cda0-4b96-4bfa-a7f5-353ec1d69dd1\" data-question=\"40\">a particular species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> of …………………………….. . </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MUSTARD [OR] MUSTARD PLANT(S)</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"cdad94f9-7283-4a46-bb1e-49ab94bb4491","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"reported","passagePhrase":"published"},{"uid":"e9c9c43b-e8f2-470c-8eb9-fe088edc9722","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"traditionally","passagePhrase":"hundreds of years"},{"uid":"1ac1c1c1-76af-4469-a581-7cab90a8d43e","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"plant behaviour","passagePhrase":"how responsive plants are"},{"uid":"3543eb43-0fb8-4a96-a006-c5ae4fd71fcf","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"making plans","passagePhrase":"predict"},{"uid":"23028a2a-8f3a-4b48-8175-5a904403d2ef","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"agricultural production","passagePhrase":"agricultural yields"},{"uid":"de12ccaf-c073-4cde-af50-9b1c9a135d31","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"could be missed","passagePhrase":"climate change is a major threat to achieving"},{"uid":"f6a840ea-6983-4742-8ac1-e645d630b9f1","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"suffer from","passagePhrase":"sensitive to"},{"uid":"d814abf5-1b21-400b-a9df-90a1fdff064f","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"rise in temperatures","passagePhrase":"high temperatures"},{"uid":"b631202e-4f05-43f0-8427-3cab1640f6f8","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"a potential benefit","passagePhrase":"the potential to accelerate"},{"uid":"89887cc3-3e8d-4b7b-bb63-9d8441980476","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"flower early","passagePhrase":"flower months in advance"},{"uid":"d57182df-6846-436e-82b1-347caced0012","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"scientific support","passagePhrase":"science behind"},{"uid":"46cb10a8-4709-40e8-8422-894ac0f079b4","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"a traditional saying","passagePhrase":"well-known rhyme long used"},{"uid":"b8770ac0-a617-4901-b2fd-2c883ffe271b","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"probably","passagePhrase":"likeliness"},{"uid":"9b27dede-e6d8-496d-8b14-fc3ad22556b6","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"come into leaf","passagePhrase":"leafing"},{"uid":"6c930abc-10d6-4afc-9f4e-76594b10d9b0","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"specialists","passagePhrase":"scientists"},{"uid":"bd80f0e9-f831-4fff-9294-0adbf69547fc","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"research","passagePhrase":"work"},{"uid":"377f4583-ba07-40af-a5c8-ef254c7efd1b","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"carried out","passagePhrase":"done"},{"uid":"12f2cda0-4b96-4bfa-a7f5-353ec1d69dd1","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"a particular species","passagePhrase":"a mustard plant"},{"uid":"078f48bb-039f-41fe-aa3b-e533838289e7","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"are likely to","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_268":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 1-13</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 1 given below</em>.</p><h2>Roman tunnels</h2><p><em><strong>The Romans, who once controlled areas of Europe, North Africa and Asia Minor, adopted the construction techniques of other civilizations to build tunnels in their territories</strong></em><br><br>The Persians, who lived in present-day Iran, were one of the first civilizations to build tunnels that provided a reliable supply of water to human settlements in dry areas. In the early first millennium BCE, they introduced the <em>qanat </em>method of tunnel construction, which consisted of placing posts over a hill in a straight line, to ensure that the tunnel kept to its route, and then digging vertical shafts down into the ground at regular intervals. Underground, workers removed the earth from between the ends of the shafts, creating a tunnel. The excavated soil was taken up to the surface using the shafts, which also provided ventilation during the work. Once the tunnel was completed, it allowed water to flow from the top of a hillside down towards a canal, which supplied water for human use. Remarkably, some <em>qanats </em>built by the Persians 2,700 years ago are still in use today.<br><br>They later passed on their knowledge to the Romans, who also used the <em>qanat </em>method to construct water-supply tunnels for agriculture. Roman <em>qanat </em>tunnels were constructed with vertical shafts dug at intervals of between 30 and 60 meters. The shafts were equipped with handholds and footholds to help those climbing in and out of them and were covered with a wooden or stone lid. To ensure that the shafts were vertical, Romans hung a plumb line from a rod placed across the top of each shaft and made sure that the weight at the end of it hung in the center of the shaft. Plumb lines were also used to measure the depth of the shaft and to determine the slope of the tunnel. The 5.6 kilometer Long Claudius tunnel, built in 41 CE to drain the Fucine Lake in central Italy, had shafts that were up to 122 meters deep, took 11 years to build and involved approximately 30,000 workers.<br><br>By the 6th century BCE, a second method of tunnel construction appeared called the <em>counter- excavation </em>method, in which the tunnel was constructed from both ends. It was used to cut through high mountains when the <em>qanat </em>method was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"ae6a5971-eeec-4120-bfac-813eb7316969\">not a practical alternative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. This method required greater planning and advanced knowledge of surveying, mathematics and geometry as both ends of a tunnel had to meet correctly at the center of the mountain. Adjustments to the direction of the tunnel also had to be made whenever builders encountered geological problems or when it deviated from its set path. They constantly checked the tunnel’s advancing direction, for example, by looking back at the light that penetrated through the tunnel mouth, and made corrections whenever necessary. Large deviations could happen, and they could result in one end of the tunnel not being usable. An inscription written <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f5029066-73e8-4c99-8fd9-5ec714647196\">on the side of a 428-meter tunnel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"e975e344-5b72-48b5-934e-b36b626452b4\">built<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> by the Romans as part of the Saldae aqueduct system in modern-day Algeria, describes how the two teams of builders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"cf6286be-4846-4f0c-919d-b2e1f4bc20d8\">missed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> each other in the mountain and how the later construction of a lateral link between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"363a9d3a-f18e-43dd-8826-0cfbc9d9f1c0\">both corridors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> corrected <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"e7a14ba3-f676-4235-9100-1ffb1deaad1f\">the initial error<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.<br><br>The Romans dug tunnels for their roads using the counter-excavation method, whenever they encountered obstacles such as hills or mountains that were too high for roads to pass over. An example is the 37-meter-long, 6-meter-high, Furlo Pass Tunnel built in Italy in 69-79 CE. Remarkably, a modern road still uses this tunnel today. Tunnels were also built for mineral <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3a99ad29-e1d9-4939-974a-df394f637a39\">extraction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Miners would locate a mineral vein and then pursue it with shafts and tunnels underground. Traces of such tunnels used to mine gold can still be found at the Dolaucothi mines in Wales. When the sole purpose of a tunnel was mineral <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3a99ad29-e1d9-4939-974a-df394f637a39\">extraction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, construction required less planning, as the tunnel route was determined by the mineral vein.<br><br>Roman tunnel projects were carefully planned and carried out. The length of time it took to construct a tunnel depended on the method being used and the type of rock being excavated. The <em>qanat </em>construction method was usually faster than the counter-excavation method as it was more straightforward. This was because the mountain could be excavated not only from the tunnel mouths but also from shafts. The type of rock could also influence construction times. When the rock was hard, the Romans employed a technique called fire quenching which consisted of heating the rock with fire, and then suddenly cooling it with cold water so that it would crack.<br><br>Progress through hard rock could be very slow, and it was not uncommon for tunnels to take years, if not decades, to be built. Construction marks left on a Roman tunnel in Bologna show that the rate of advance through solid rock was 30 centimeters per day. In contrast, the rate of advance of the Claudius tunnel can be calculated at 1.4 meters per day. Most tunnels had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d2bdb871-2419-4559-9395-6803c7593132\">inscriptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> showing the names of patrons who ordered construction and sometimes the name of the architect. For example, the 1.4-kilometer Cevlik tunnel in Turkey, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"85f8f685-d055-4cb9-9943-d5408e8f6421\">built to divert the floodwater threatening<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the harbor of the ancient city of Seleuceia Pieria, had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d2bdb871-2419-4559-9395-6803c7593132\">inscriptions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> on the entrance, still visible today, that also indicate that the tunnel was started in 69 CE and was completed in 81 CE.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Label the diagrams below.</em></p><p><em>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answer in boxes <strong>1-6</strong> on your reading answer sheet, write:</em></p><p><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather,serif\"><span style=\"color:#444444\"><em><img src=\"/media/gg_imgs/test/bacc6eb0ebde3735780887af4e2903e1b7c0f22c.jpg\" style=\"height:643px; width:602px\"></em></span></span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23724\" id=\"question-wrapper-23724\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POSTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23725\" id=\"question-wrapper-23725\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CANAL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23726\" id=\"question-wrapper-23726\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VENTILATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23727\" id=\"question-wrapper-23727\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LID</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23728\" id=\"question-wrapper-23728\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WEIGHT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23729\" id=\"question-wrapper-23729\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CLIMBING</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><strong>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</strong></p><p><em>In boxes <strong>7-10</strong> on your reading answer sheet, write:</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>TRUE</strong></td><td>if the statement agrees with the information</td></tr><tr><td><strong>FALSE</strong></td><td>if the statement contradicts the information</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong></td><td>If there is no information on this</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23730\" id=\"question-wrapper-23730\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The counter-excavation method <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"7\" data-uid=\"ae6a5971-eeec-4120-bfac-813eb7316969\">completely replaced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the qanat method in the 6th century BCE </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23731\" id=\"question-wrapper-23731\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Only experienced builders were employed to construct a tunnel using the counter-excavation method. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23732\" id=\"question-wrapper-23732\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The information about a problem that occurred during the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"e975e344-5b72-48b5-934e-b36b626452b4\">construction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of the Saldae aqueduct system was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-question=\"9\" data-uid=\"f5029066-73e8-4c99-8fd9-5ec714647196\">found in an ancient book<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23733\" id=\"question-wrapper-23733\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"e7a14ba3-f676-4235-9100-1ffb1deaad1f\">The mistake<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> made by the builders of the Saldae aqueduct system was that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"363a9d3a-f18e-43dd-8826-0cfbc9d9f1c0\">the two parts of the tunnel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"10\" data-uid=\"cf6286be-4846-4f0c-919d-b2e1f4bc20d8\">failed to meet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Answer the questions below.</em></p><p><em>Choose <strong>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</strong> from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>11-13</strong> on your reading answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23734\" id=\"question-wrapper-23734\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What type of mineral were the Dolaucothi mines in Wales built to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"11\" data-uid=\"3a99ad29-e1d9-4939-974a-df394f637a39\">extract<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GOLD</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23735\" id=\"question-wrapper-23735\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In addition to the patron, whose name might be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"12\" data-uid=\"d2bdb871-2419-4559-9395-6803c7593132\">carved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> onto a tunnel? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(THE) ARCHITECT('S) (NAME)</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23736\" id=\"question-wrapper-23736\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What part of Seleuceia Pieria was the Çevlik tunnel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-question=\"13\" data-uid=\"85f8f685-d055-4cb9-9943-d5408e8f6421\">built to protect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(THE) HARBOUR/HARBOR</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e975e344-5b72-48b5-934e-b36b626452b4","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"construction","passagePhrase":"built"},{"uid":"cf6286be-4846-4f0c-919d-b2e1f4bc20d8","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"failed to meet","passagePhrase":"missed"},{"uid":"363a9d3a-f18e-43dd-8826-0cfbc9d9f1c0","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"the two parts of the tunnel","passagePhrase":"both corridors"},{"uid":"e7a14ba3-f676-4235-9100-1ffb1deaad1f","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"The mistake","passagePhrase":"the initial error"},{"uid":"3a99ad29-e1d9-4939-974a-df394f637a39","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"extract","passagePhrase":"extraction ... extraction"},{"uid":"d2bdb871-2419-4559-9395-6803c7593132","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"carved","passagePhrase":"inscriptions ... inscriptions"},{"uid":"85f8f685-d055-4cb9-9943-d5408e8f6421","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"built to protect","passagePhrase":"built to divert the floodwater threatening"}]},"reading_u2_269":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 14-26</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 2 given below</em>.</p><h2>Changes in reading habits</h2><p><em><strong>What are the implications of the way we read today?</strong></em><br><br>Look around on your next plane trip. The iPad is the new pacifier for babies and toddlers. Younger school-aged children read stories on smartphones; older kids don’t read at all, but hunch over video games. Parents and other passengers read on tablets or skim a flotilla of email and news feeds. Unbeknown to most of us, an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ae954a4-3a8c-4bc8-a1bc-35dd2ace7996\" data-question=\"14\">invisible, game-changing transformation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> links everyone in this picture: the neuronal circuit that underlies the brain’s ability to read is subtly, rapidly changing and this has implications for everyone from the pre-reading toddler to the expert adult.<br><br>As work in neurosciences indicates, the acquisition of literacy necessitated a new circuit in our species’ brain more than 6,000 years ago. That circuit evolved from a very simple mechanism for decoding basic information, like the number of goats in one’s herd, to the present, highly elaborated reading brain. My research depicts how the present reading brain enables the development of some of our most important intellectual and affective processes: internalized knowledge, analogical reasoning, and inference; perspective-taking and empathy; critical analysis and the generation of insight. Research surfacing in many parts of the world now cautions that each of these essential ‘deep reading’ processes may be under threat as we move into digital- based modes of reading.<br><br>This is not a simple, binary issue of print versus digital reading and technological innovation. As MIT scholar Sherry Turkle has written, we do not err as a society when we innovate <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ca702044-842c-4f14-8e85-3d868db253e1\" data-question=\"15\">but when we ignore<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> what we disrupt or diminish while innovating. In this hinge moment between print and digital cultures, society needs to confront what is diminishing in the expert reading circuit, what our children and older students are not developing, and what we can do about it.<br><br>We know from research that the reading circuit is not given to human beings through a genetic blueprint like vision or language; it needs an environment to develop. Further, it will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b8d55393-f902-41c3-b096-27920a3808e8\" data-question=\"16\">adapt to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70a7054d-5b1b-4b18-8cf2-a3c25129cfcc\" data-question=\"16\">environment’s requirements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> — from different writing systems to the characteristics of whatever medium is used. If the dominant medium advantages processes that are fast, multi-task oriented and well-suited for large volumes of information, like the current digital medium, so will the reading circuit. As UCLA psychologist Patricia Greenfield writes, the result is that less attention and time will be allocated to slower, time-demanding deep reading processes.<br><br>Increasing reports from educators and from researchers in psychology and the humanities bear this out. English literature scholar and teacher Mark Edmundson describes how many college students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"359cb839-c713-4c04-b15f-8955ab7d40fb\" data-question=\"17\">actively avoid the classic literature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of the 19th and 20th centuries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"359cb839-c713-4c04-b15f-8955ab7d40fb\" data-question=\"17\">in favour of something simpler<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> as they no longer have the patience to read longer, denser, more difficult texts. We should be less concerned with students’ <em>‘cognitive impatience’</em>, however, than by what may underlie it: the potential inability of large numbers of students to read with a level of critical analysis sufficient to comprehend the complexity of thought and argument found in more demanding texts.<br><br>Multiple studies show that digital screen use may be causing a variety of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"886097fe-072a-4d9d-94cc-a1a1c4f60909\" data-question=\"18\">troubling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> downstream effects on reading comprehension in older high school and college students. In Stavanger, Norway, psychologist Anne Mangen and her colleagues studied how high school students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a4a05e4-7cbf-4669-8097-a218e42e6031\" data-question=\"19\">comprehend<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> the same material in different mediums. Mangen’s group asked subjects questions about a short story whose plot had universal student appeal; half of the students read the story on a tablet, the other half in paperback. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebb6ad26-fa4b-4813-aca3-078aff18799c\" data-question=\"20\">Results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d77ca91-34ee-4728-a033-fe709c145deb\" data-question=\"20\">indicated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> that students who read on print were superior in their comprehension to screen-reading peers, particularly in their ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68672d08-58ee-48a2-92fa-b855e2efc1da\" data-question=\"20\">sequence detail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and reconstruct the plot in chronological order.<br><br>Ziming Liu from San Jose State University has conducted a series of studies which indicate that the ‘new norm’ in reading is skimming, involving word-spotting and browsing through the text. Many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9bd0a4d5-2658-420e-a449-2b17b87fac7a\" data-question=\"21\">readers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> now use a pattern when reading in which they sample the first line and then word- spot through the rest of the text. When the reading brain skims like this, it reduces time allocated to deep reading processes. In other words, we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6425aaf4-019d-4a6c-af0e-ca0bf88ec386\" data-question=\"22\">don’t have time to grasp complexity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, to understand another’s feelings, to perceive beauty, and to create thoughts of the reader’s own.<br><br>The possibility that critical analysis, empathy and other deep reading processes could become the unintended ‘collateral damage’ of our digital culture is not a straightforward binary issue about print versus digital reading. It is about how we all have begun to read on various mediums and how that changes not only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"377d9748-d3dc-4689-bf83-b5e2df64ede8\" data-question=\"23\">what we read<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, but also the purposes for which we read. Nor is it only about the young. The subtle <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67de1250-5a13-4ea0-8208-704814f7fbaa\" data-question=\"24\">atrophy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> of critical analysis and empathy affects us all <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0f750606-cef3-4d42-8537-6089b2c911dd\" data-question=\"24\">equally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. It affects our ability to navigate a constant bombardment of information. It incentivizes a retreat to the most familiar stores of unchecked information, which require and receive no analysis, leaving us susceptible to false information and irrational ideas.<br><br>There’s an old rule in neuroscience that does not alter with age: use it or lose it. It is a very hopeful principle when applied to critical thought in the reading brain because it implies choice. The story of the changing reading brain is hardly finished. We possess both the science and the technology to identify and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1117d4b8-5e91-42f0-8eb2-766c1d8c9c14\" data-question=\"26\">redress<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> the changes in how we read before they become entrenched. If we work to understand exactly what we will lose, alongside the extraordinary new capacities that the digital world has brought us, there is as much reason for excitement as caution.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose the correct letter , <strong>A, B, C or D.</strong></em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>14-17 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23737\" id=\"question-wrapper-23737\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer’s main point in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Our use of technology is having a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ae954a4-3a8c-4bc8-a1bc-35dd2ace7996\" data-question=\"14\">hidden effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> on us.</li> <li>B. Technology can be used to help youngsters to read.</li> <li>C. Travellers should be encouraged to use technology on planes.</li> <li>D. Playing games is a more popular use of technology than reading.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23738\" id=\"question-wrapper-23738\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What main point does Sherry Turkle make about innovation? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Technological innovation has led to a reduction in print reading.</li> <li>B. We should <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ca702044-842c-4f14-8e85-3d868db253e1\" data-question=\"15\">pay attention to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> what might be lost when innovation occurs.</li> <li>C. We should encourage more young people to become involved in innovation.</li> <li>D. There is a difference between developing products and developing ideas.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23739\" id=\"question-wrapper-23739\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point is the writer making in the fourth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Humans have an inborn ability to read and write.</li> <li>B. Reading can be done using many different mediums.</li> <li>C. Writing systems make unexpected demands on the brain.</li> <li>D. Some brain circuits <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b8d55393-f902-41c3-b096-27920a3808e8\" data-question=\"16\">adjust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70a7054d-5b1b-4b18-8cf2-a3c25129cfcc\" data-question=\"16\">whatever is required of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> them.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23740\" id=\"question-wrapper-23740\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to Mark Edmundson, the attitude of college students… </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. has changed the way he teaches.</li> <li>B. has influenced <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"359cb839-c713-4c04-b15f-8955ab7d40fb\" data-question=\"17\">what they select to read<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</li> <li>C. does not worry him as much as it does others.</li> <li>D. does not match the views of the general public.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the summary using the list of words, <strong>A-H</strong>, below.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct letter, <em><strong>A-H</strong></em></em>,<em> in boxes <strong>18-22 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>A.</strong> fast<br><strong>B.</strong> isolated<br><strong>C.</strong> emotional<br><strong>D.</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"886097fe-072a-4d9d-94cc-a1a1c4f60909\" data-question=\"18\">worrying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span><br><strong>E.</strong> many<br><strong>F. </strong>hard<br><strong>G. </strong>combined<br><strong>H.</strong> thorough</td></tr></tbody></table><p> </p><table><thead><tr><th>Studies on digital screen use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>There have been many studies on digital screen use, showing some (18) …………………………. trends. Psychologist Anne Mangen gave high-school students a short story to read, half using digital and half using print mediums. Her team then used a question &amp; answer technique to find out how <strong>(19) </strong>…………………………. each group’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a4a05e4-7cbf-4669-8097-a218e42e6031\" data-question=\"19\">understanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of the plot was. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebb6ad26-fa4b-4813-aca3-078aff18799c\" data-question=\"20\">The findings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d77ca91-34ee-4728-a033-fe709c145deb\" data-question=\"20\">showed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> a clear pattern in the responses, with those who read screens finding the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68672d08-58ee-48a2-92fa-b855e2efc1da\" data-question=\"20\">order of information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <strong>(20)</strong> ………………………… to recall.<br><br>Studies by Ziming Liu show that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9bd0a4d5-2658-420e-a449-2b17b87fac7a\" data-question=\"21\">students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> are tending to read <strong><strong>(21)</strong> …………………………</strong> words and phrases in a text to save time. This approach, she says, gives the reader a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6425aaf4-019d-4a6c-af0e-ca0bf88ec386\" data-question=\"22\">superficial understanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of the <strong>(22)</strong> ………………………… content of material, leaving no time for thought.</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23741\" id=\"question-wrapper-23741\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23742\" id=\"question-wrapper-23742\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23743\" id=\"question-wrapper-23743\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23744\" id=\"question-wrapper-23744\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23745\" id=\"question-wrapper-23745\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><strong>Do the following statements agree with the the views of the writer in Reading Passage 2?</strong></p><p><em>In boxes <strong>23-26</strong> on your reading answer sheet, write:</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>YES</strong></td><td>if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NO</strong></td><td>if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong></td><td>If it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about it</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23746\" id=\"question-wrapper-23746\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The medium we used to read can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8348fd35-6afe-41de-ac5b-d7f0ecd75e6f\" data-question=\"23\">affect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> our choice of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"377d9748-d3dc-4689-bf83-b5e2df64ede8\" data-question=\"23\">reading content<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23747\" id=\"question-wrapper-23747\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some age groups are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"0f750606-cef3-4d42-8537-6089b2c911dd\" data-question=\"24\">more likely to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> lose their complex reading skills than others. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23748\" id=\"question-wrapper-23748\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> False information has become more widespread in today’s digital era. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23749\" id=\"question-wrapper-23749\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> We still have opportunities to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1117d4b8-5e91-42f0-8eb2-766c1d8c9c14\" data-question=\"26\">rectify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> the problems that technology is presenting. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0ae954a4-3a8c-4bc8-a1bc-35dd2ace7996","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"hidden effect","passagePhrase":"invisible, game-changing transformation"},{"uid":"b8d55393-f902-41c3-b096-27920a3808e8","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"adjust","passagePhrase":"adapt to"},{"uid":"70a7054d-5b1b-4b18-8cf2-a3c25129cfcc","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"whatever is required of","passagePhrase":"environment’s requirements"},{"uid":"359cb839-c713-4c04-b15f-8955ab7d40fb","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"what they select to read","passagePhrase":"actively avoid the classic literature ... in favour of something simpler"},{"uid":"886097fe-072a-4d9d-94cc-a1a1c4f60909","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"worrying","passagePhrase":"troubling"},{"uid":"0a4a05e4-7cbf-4669-8097-a218e42e6031","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"understanding","passagePhrase":"comprehend"},{"uid":"ebb6ad26-fa4b-4813-aca3-078aff18799c","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"The findings","passagePhrase":"Results"},{"uid":"0d77ca91-34ee-4728-a033-fe709c145deb","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"showed","passagePhrase":"indicated"},{"uid":"68672d08-58ee-48a2-92fa-b855e2efc1da","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"order of information","passagePhrase":"sequence detail"},{"uid":"9bd0a4d5-2658-420e-a449-2b17b87fac7a","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"students","passagePhrase":"readers"},{"uid":"6425aaf4-019d-4a6c-af0e-ca0bf88ec386","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"superficial understanding","passagePhrase":"don’t have time to grasp complexity"},{"uid":"377d9748-d3dc-4689-bf83-b5e2df64ede8","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"reading content","passagePhrase":"what we read"},{"uid":"67de1250-5a13-4ea0-8208-704814f7fbaa","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"atrophy"},{"uid":"1117d4b8-5e91-42f0-8eb2-766c1d8c9c14","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"rectify","passagePhrase":"redress"},{"uid":"8348fd35-6afe-41de-ac5b-d7f0ecd75e6f","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"affect","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_270":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><em>You should spend about 20 minutes on <strong>Questions 27-40</strong>, corresponding to Reading Passage 3 given below</em>.</p><h2>Attitudes towards Artificial Intelligence</h2><p><strong>A.</strong><br>Artificial intelligence (AI) can already <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0396c250-0526-4bc8-9fcc-44573d82f2e7\" data-question=\"27\">predict the future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Police forces are using it to map when and where crime is likely to occur. Doctors can use it to predict when a patient is most likely to have a heart attack or stroke. Researchers are even trying to give AI imagination so it can plan for unexpected consequences.<br><br>Many decisions in our lives require a good <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0396c250-0526-4bc8-9fcc-44573d82f2e7\" data-question=\"27\">forecast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, and AI is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"616dff1e-2bd2-4603-9ef2-431a6561cd4b\" data-question=\"27\">almost always better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0396c250-0526-4bc8-9fcc-44573d82f2e7\" data-question=\"27\">forecast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>ing than we are. Yet for all these technological advances, we still seem to deeply lack confidence in Al predictions. Recent cases <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e673d468-6769-42c4-806b-11518216fea2\" data-question=\"33\">show<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bdeeae53-0017-4125-91ae-12b342549736\" data-question=\"33\">people don’t like relying on AI and prefer to trust human experts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, even if these experts are wrong.<br><br>If we want AI to really benefit people, we need to find a way to get people to trust it. To do that, we need to understand why people are so reluctant to trust AI in the first place.<br><br><strong>B.</strong><br>Take the case of Watson for Oncology, one of technology giant IBM’s supercomputer programs. Their attempt to promote this program to cancer doctors was a PR disaster. The AI promised to deliver top-quality recommendations on the treatment of 12 cancers that accounted for 80% of the world’s eases. But when doctors first interacted with Watson, they found themselves in a rather difficult situation. On the one hand, if Watson provided guidance about a treatment that coincided with their own opinions, physicians did not see much point in Watson’s recommendations. The supercomputer was simply telling them what they already knew, and these recommendations did not change the actual treatment.<br><br>On the other hand, if Watson generated a recommendation that contradicted the experts’ opinion, doctors would typically conclude that Watson wasn’t competent. And the machine wouldn’t be able to explain why its treatment was plausible because its machine-learning algorithms were simply too complex to be fully understood by humans. Consequently, this has caused even more suspicion and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c9216749-f344-4c69-b23a-a19418ad3f21\" data-question=\"28\">disbelief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, leading many doctors to ignore the seemingly outlandish AI recommendations and stick to their own expertise.<br><br><strong>C.</strong><br>This is just one example of people s lack of confidence in AI and their reluctance to accept what AI has to offer. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09050c6e-a4ad-4f4e-9ac8-f17835514436\" data-question=\"29\">Trust in other people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> is often based on our understanding of how others think and having experience of their reliability. This helps create a psychological feeling of safety. AI, on the other hand, is still fairly new and unfamiliar to most people. Even if it can be technically explained (and that’s not always the case), AI’s decision-making process is usually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"559de441-fdfa-4e83-8051-b832ff57d7af\" data-question=\"34\">too difficult for most people to comprehend<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. And interacting with something we don’t understand can cause anxiety and give us a sense that we’re <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f6116f41-3259-44bf-b604-cdd18b90982d\" data-question=\"34\">losing control<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.<br><br>Many people are also simply not familiar with many instances of AI actually working, because it often happens in the background. Instead they are acutely aware of instances where AI goes wrong. Embarrassing AI failures receive a disproportionate amount of media attention, emphasising the message that we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fc4459ce-1321-4148-9512-989cce93b1cc\" data-question=\"35\">cannot rely on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> technology. Machine learning is not foolproof, in part because the humans who design it aren’t.<br><br><strong>D.</strong><br>Feelings about AI run deep. In a recent experiment, people from a range of backgrounds were given various sci-fi films about AI to watch and then asked questions about automation in everyday life. It was found that, regardless of whether the film they watched <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06bbdc0e-adbe-4f36-92f8-6e4a02d99f17\" data-question=\"36\">depicted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> AI in a positive or negative light, simply watching a cinematic vision of our technological future <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1cbdb7dc-b444-47c4-bc92-cc0566aa2f2c\" data-question=\"36\">polarised the participants’ attitudes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Optimists became <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64e65946-7bd1-4087-ad18-659cc5bfe6cc\" data-question=\"30\">more extreme<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> in their enthusiasm for AI and sceptics became even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64e65946-7bd1-4087-ad18-659cc5bfe6cc\" data-question=\"30\">more guarded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.<br><br>This suggests people use relevant evidence about AI in a biased manner to support their existing attitudes, a deep-rooted human tendency known as “confirmation bias”. As AI is represented more and more in media and entertainment, it could lead to a society split between those who benefit from AI and those who reject it. More pertinently, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c9c1e34-c52b-45b2-8b44-481f1a8590bf\" data-question=\"38\">refusing to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> accept the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ab7cfc7-740e-431d-913d-75571b9f1dc1\" data-question=\"38\">advantages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> offered by AI could place a large group of people at a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fdf112ed-356d-4137-b8fb-0db40e1e86fe\" data-question=\"38\">serious disadvantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.<br><br><strong>E.</strong><br>Fortunately, we already have some ideas about how to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7be8b147-8930-4134-a450-759f322d248b\" data-question=\"31\">improve trust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in AI. Simply having previous <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c70dac68-abd4-4abe-8f28-931476c7e173\" data-question=\"39\">experience with AI<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"32a82ebc-e0f8-44ea-8441-b1f9d236ed9d\" data-question=\"39\">can significantly improve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> people’s opinions about the technology, as was found in the study mentioned above. Evidence also suggests the more you use other technologies such as the internet, the more you trust them.<br><br>Another solution may be to reveal more about the algorithms which AI uses and the purposes they serve. Several high-profile social media companies and online marketplaces already release transparency reports about government requests and surveillance disclosures. A similar practice for AI could help people have a better understanding of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"201a6a3b-298e-49b1-893d-3fc47c194f45\" data-question=\"31\">the way algorithmic decisions are made<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.<br><br><strong>F.</strong><br>Research suggests that allowing people some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b8deb8f-67c7-4690-8046-07c833d20241\" data-question=\"32\">control over<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1419b532-6059-4c3b-9511-520344ec17c6\" data-question=\"32\">AI decision-making<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> could also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc61ee2b-e853-430c-92f8-63f9272468bd\" data-question=\"32\">improve trust and enable AI to learn from human experience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. For example, one study showed that when people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"911171af-096b-4d6d-9deb-61aa2d5b3eb9\" data-question=\"40\">were allowed the freedom to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> slightly modify an algorithm, they felt more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab0be66c-3fd6-44de-97cd-90c80c0a18b4\" data-question=\"40\">satisfied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> with its decisions, more likely to believe it was superior and more likely to use it in the future.<br><br>We don’t need to understand the intricate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1419b532-6059-4c3b-9511-520344ec17c6\" data-question=\"32\">inner workings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of AI systems, but if people are given a degree of responsibility for how they are implemented, they will be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc61ee2b-e853-430c-92f8-63f9272468bd\" data-question=\"32\">more willing to accept AI into their lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Reading Passage 3 has six sections, <strong>A-F.</strong></em></p><p><em>Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct number, <strong>i-viii</strong>, in boxes <strong>27-32 </strong>on your answer sheet.</em></p><table><thead><tr><th>List of Headings</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>i. </strong>An <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64e65946-7bd1-4087-ad18-659cc5bfe6cc\" data-question=\"30\">increasing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> divergence of attitudes towards AI<br><strong>ii. </strong>Reasons why we have more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09050c6e-a4ad-4f4e-9ac8-f17835514436\" data-question=\"29\">faith in human judgement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> than in AI<br><strong>iii. </strong>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"616dff1e-2bd2-4603-9ef2-431a6561cd4b\" data-question=\"27\">superiority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of AI <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0396c250-0526-4bc8-9fcc-44573d82f2e7\" data-question=\"27\">projections<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> over those made by humans<br><strong>iv.</strong> The process by which AI can help us make good decisions<br><strong>v.</strong> The advantages of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b8deb8f-67c7-4690-8046-07c833d20241\" data-question=\"32\">involving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> users in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1419b532-6059-4c3b-9511-520344ec17c6\" data-question=\"32\">AI processes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span><br><strong>vi. </strong>Widespread <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c9216749-f344-4c69-b23a-a19418ad3f21\" data-question=\"28\">distrust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of an AI innovation<br><strong>vii. </strong><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7be8b147-8930-4134-a450-759f322d248b\" data-question=\"31\">Encouraging openness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> about how AI <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"201a6a3b-298e-49b1-893d-3fc47c194f45\" data-question=\"31\">functions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span><br><strong>viii. </strong>A surprisingly successful AI application</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23750\" id=\"question-wrapper-23750\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23751\" id=\"question-wrapper-23751\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23752\" id=\"question-wrapper-23752\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23753\" id=\"question-wrapper-23753\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23754\" id=\"question-wrapper-23754\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23755\" id=\"question-wrapper-23755\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Section F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose the correct letter , <strong>A, B, C or D.</strong></em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes <strong>33-35 </strong>on your reading answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23756\" id=\"question-wrapper-23756\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer doing in Section A? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. providing a solution to a concern</li> <li>B. justifying an opinion about an issue</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e673d468-6769-42c4-806b-11518216fea2\" data-question=\"33\">highlighting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bdeeae53-0017-4125-91ae-12b342549736\" data-question=\"33\">existence of a problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></li> <li>D. explaining the reasons for a phenomenon</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23757\" id=\"question-wrapper-23757\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> According to Section C, why might some people be reluctant to accept AI? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They are afraid it will replace humans in decision-making jobs.</li> <li>B. Its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"559de441-fdfa-4e83-8051-b832ff57d7af\" data-question=\"34\">complexity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> makes them feel that they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f6116f41-3259-44bf-b604-cdd18b90982d\" data-question=\"34\">at a disadvantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</li> <li>C. They would rather wait for the technology to be tested over a period of time.</li> <li>D. Misunderstandings about how it works make it seem more challenging than it is.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23758\" id=\"question-wrapper-23758\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer say about the media in Section C of the text? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It leads the public to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fc4459ce-1321-4148-9512-989cce93b1cc\" data-question=\"35\">mistrustful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of Al.</li> <li>B. It devotes an excessive amount of attention to Al.</li> <li>C. Its reports of incidents involving AI are often inaccurate.</li> <li>D. It gives the impression that AI failures are due to designer error.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><strong>Do the following statements agree with the the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</strong></p><p><em>In boxes <strong>36-40</strong> on your reading answer sheet, write:</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>YES</strong></td><td>if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NO</strong></td><td>if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong></td><td>If it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about it</td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23759\" id=\"question-wrapper-23759\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Subjective <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"06bbdc0e-adbe-4f36-92f8-6e4a02d99f17\" data-question=\"36\">depictions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of AI in sci-fi films <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1cbdb7dc-b444-47c4-bc92-cc0566aa2f2c\" data-question=\"36\">make people change their opinions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> about automation. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23760\" id=\"question-wrapper-23760\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Portrayals of AI in media and entertainment are likely to become more positive. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23761\" id=\"question-wrapper-23761\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c9c1e34-c52b-45b2-8b44-481f1a8590bf\" data-question=\"38\">Rejection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ab7cfc7-740e-431d-913d-75571b9f1dc1\" data-question=\"38\">possibilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of AI may have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fdf112ed-356d-4137-b8fb-0db40e1e86fe\" data-question=\"38\">negative effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> on many people’s lives. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23762\" id=\"question-wrapper-23762\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c70dac68-abd4-4abe-8f28-931476c7e173\" data-question=\"39\">Familiarity with AI<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"32a82ebc-e0f8-44ea-8441-b1f9d236ed9d\" data-question=\"39\">very little impact on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> people’s attitudes to the technology. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"23763\" id=\"question-wrapper-23763\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> AI applications which users <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"911171af-096b-4d6d-9deb-61aa2d5b3eb9\" data-question=\"40\">are able to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> modify are more likely to gain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab0be66c-3fd6-44de-97cd-90c80c0a18b4\" data-question=\"40\">consumer approval<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0396c250-0526-4bc8-9fcc-44573d82f2e7","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"projections","passagePhrase":"predict the future ... forecast ... forecast"},{"uid":"616dff1e-2bd2-4603-9ef2-431a6561cd4b","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"superiority","passagePhrase":"almost always better"},{"uid":"e673d468-6769-42c4-806b-11518216fea2","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"highlighting","passagePhrase":"show"},{"uid":"bdeeae53-0017-4125-91ae-12b342549736","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"existence of a problem","passagePhrase":"people don’t like relying on AI and prefer to trust human experts"},{"uid":"c9216749-f344-4c69-b23a-a19418ad3f21","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"distrust","passagePhrase":"disbelief"},{"uid":"09050c6e-a4ad-4f4e-9ac8-f17835514436","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"faith in human judgement","passagePhrase":"Trust in other people"},{"uid":"559de441-fdfa-4e83-8051-b832ff57d7af","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"complexity","passagePhrase":"too difficult for most people to comprehend"},{"uid":"f6116f41-3259-44bf-b604-cdd18b90982d","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"at a disadvantage","passagePhrase":"losing control"},{"uid":"fc4459ce-1321-4148-9512-989cce93b1cc","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"mistrustful","passagePhrase":"cannot rely on"},{"uid":"06bbdc0e-adbe-4f36-92f8-6e4a02d99f17","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"depictions","passagePhrase":"depicted"},{"uid":"64e65946-7bd1-4087-ad18-659cc5bfe6cc","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"increasing","passagePhrase":"more extreme ... more guarded"},{"uid":"9c9c1e34-c52b-45b2-8b44-481f1a8590bf","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"Rejection","passagePhrase":"refusing to"},{"uid":"7ab7cfc7-740e-431d-913d-75571b9f1dc1","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"possibilities","passagePhrase":"advantages"},{"uid":"fdf112ed-356d-4137-b8fb-0db40e1e86fe","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"negative effect","passagePhrase":"serious disadvantage"},{"uid":"7be8b147-8930-4134-a450-759f322d248b","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Encouraging openness","passagePhrase":"improve trust"},{"uid":"c70dac68-abd4-4abe-8f28-931476c7e173","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Familiarity with AI","passagePhrase":"experience with AI"},{"uid":"201a6a3b-298e-49b1-893d-3fc47c194f45","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"functions","passagePhrase":"the way algorithmic decisions are made"},{"uid":"4b8deb8f-67c7-4690-8046-07c833d20241","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"involving","passagePhrase":"control over"},{"uid":"1419b532-6059-4c3b-9511-520344ec17c6","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"AI processes","passagePhrase":"AI decision-making ... inner workings"},{"uid":"bc61ee2b-e853-430c-92f8-63f9272468bd","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"improve trust and enable AI to learn from human experience ... more willing to accept AI into their lives"},{"uid":"911171af-096b-4d6d-9deb-61aa2d5b3eb9","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"are able to","passagePhrase":"were allowed the freedom to"},{"uid":"ab0be66c-3fd6-44de-97cd-90c80c0a18b4","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"consumer approval","passagePhrase":"satisfied"}]},"reading_u2_271":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3><strong>The development of the London underground railway</strong></h3><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6950a84e-f361-4150-9b1d-cdadffe6419b\" data-question=\"1\">In the first half of the 1800s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, London’s population <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69b5e935-211f-4971-8097-1314e1155887\" data-question=\"1\">grew at an astonishing rate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, and the central area became increasingly congested. In addition, the expansion of the overground railway network resulted in more and more passengers arriving in the capital. However, in 1846, a Royal Commission decided that the railways should not be allowed to enter the City, the capital’s historic and business centre. The result was that the overground railway stations formed a ring around the City. The area within consisted of poorly built, overcrowded slums and the streets were full of horse-drawn traffic. Crossing the City became a nightmare. It could take an hour and a half to travel 8 km by horse-drawn carriage or bus. Numerous schemes were proposed to resolve these problems, but few succeeded.</p><p>Amongst the most vocal advocates for a solution to London’s traffic problems was Charles Pearson, who worked as a solicitor for the City of London. He saw both social and economic advantages in building an underground railway that would link the overground railway stations together and clear London slums at the same time. His idea was to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbdd2a72-9c8f-48bc-a9c1-e7014dc32ba2\" data-question=\"2\">relocate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ae9400f9-d270-4ffe-ab3e-8c6031c3e4b8\" data-question=\"2\">the poor workers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> who lived in the inner-city slums to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"58f6523a-3351-4357-9283-5f77af0165cf\" data-question=\"2\">newly constructed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> suburbs, and to provide cheap rail travel for them to get to work. Pearson’s ideas <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d32a7b53-dd5a-4b14-9ec4-d257c8e1b0c0\" data-question=\"3\">gained support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> amongst <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9797e2bb-7ef9-4b97-8c94-6870883fc021\" data-question=\"3\">some<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> businessmen and in 1851 he submitted a plan to Parliament. It was rejected, but coincided with a proposal from another group for an underground connecting line, which Parliament passed.</p><p>The two groups merged and established the Metropolitan Railway Company in August 1854. The company’s plan was to construct an underground railway line from the Great Western Railway’s (GWR) station at Paddington to the edge of the City at Farringdon Street - a distance of almost 5 km. The organisation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea02a4fb-6900-4265-b4a1-dda6bfb2a597\" data-question=\"4\">had difficulty in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64931a48-2010-4829-b61f-464c3d9b1484\" data-question=\"4\">raising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the funding for such a radical and expensive <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0e9d354-bc9d-45a6-b743-b3015e90422b\" data-question=\"4\">scheme<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, not least because of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f1fcafcf-e236-4bc6-908e-a34986f87cef\" data-question=\"5\">critical articles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03988431-7348-4de2-9103-0122db904f08\" data-question=\"5\">printed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> by the press. Objectors argued that the tunnels would collapse under the weight of traffic overhead, buildings would be shaken and passengers would be poisoned by the emissions from the train engines. However, Pearson and his partners persisted.</p><p>The GWR, aware that the new line would finally enable them to run trains into the heart of the City, invested almost £250,000 in the scheme. Eventually, over a five-year period, £1m was raised. The chosen route ran beneath existing main roads to minimise the expense of demolishing buildings. Originally scheduled to be completed in 21 months, the construction of the underground line took three years. It was built just below street level using a technique known as ‘cut and cover’. A trench about ten metres wide and six metres deep was dug, and the sides temporarily held up with timber beams. Brick walls were then constructed, and finally a brick arch was added to create a tunnel. A two-metre-deep layer of soil <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c04e91e-d040-42ea-bab7-75a8872a5483\" data-question=\"6\">was laid on top of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the tunnel and the road above rebuilt.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"31826cab-c33a-4e67-bc7d-ffe2bef51d1a\" data-question=\"7\">The Metropolitan line, which opened on 10 January 1863, was the world’s first underground railway<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. On its first day, almost 40,000 passengers were carried between Paddington and Farringdon, the journey taking about 18 minutes. By the end of the Metropolitan’s first year of operation, 9.5 million journeys had been made.</p><p>Even as the Metropolitan began operation, the first extensions to the line were being authorised; these were built over the next five years, reaching Moorgate in the east of London and Hammersmith in the west. The original plan was to pull the trains with steam locomotives, using firebricks in the boilers to provide steam, but these engines were never introduced. Instead, the line used specially designed locomotives that were fitted with water tanks in which steam could be condensed. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64d8bf34-ec99-424a-b809-d6833ad6a467\" data-question=\"9\">smoke and fumes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c0165d9-0cb0-4c3e-9045-768b5cfa887f\" data-question=\"9\">remained a problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, even though ventilation shafts were added to the tunnels.</p><p>Despite the extension of the underground railway, by the 1880s, congestion on London’s streets had become worse. The problem was partly that the existing underground lines formed a circuit around the centre of London and extended to the suburbs, but did not cross the capital’s centre. The ‘cut and cover’ method of construction was not an option in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c136ec67-99c8-4ab2-94cb-3630110a77fd\" data-question=\"10\">this part of the capital<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. The only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71797f37-273c-4ccc-a6f1-a498a38d0cf4\" data-question=\"10\">alternative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> was to tunnel deep underground.</p><p>Although the technology to create these tunnels existed, steam locomotives could not be used in such a confined space. It wasn’t until the development of a reliable electric motor, and a means of transferring power from the generator to a moving train, that the world’s first deep-level electric railway, the City &amp; South London, became possible. The line opened in 1890, and ran from the City to Stockwell, south of the River Thames. The trains were made up of three carriages and driven by electric engines. The carriages were narrow and had tiny <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"418275ad-a4a9-45c9-bb5b-1fb9bd185b11\" data-question=\"11\">windows just below the roof<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> because it was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"418275ad-a4a9-45c9-bb5b-1fb9bd185b11\" data-question=\"11\">thought that passengers would not want to look out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> at the tunnel walls. The line was not without its problems, mainly caused by an unreliable power supply. Although the City &amp; South London Railway was a great technical achievement, it did not make a profit. Then, in 1900, the Central London Railway, known as the ‘Tuppenny Tube’, began operation using new electric locomotives. It was very popular and soon afterwards new railways and extensions were added to the growing tube network. By 1907, the heart of today’s Underground system was in place.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Write your answers in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>The London underground railway</strong></p><p>The problem</p><p>• The 1..........................................of London <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69b5e935-211f-4971-8097-1314e1155887\" data-question=\"1\">increased rapidly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6950a84e-f361-4150-9b1d-cdadffe6419b\" data-question=\"1\">between 1800 and 1850<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></p><p>• The streets were full of horse-drawn vehicles</p><p>The proposed solution</p><p>• Charles Pearson, a solicitor, suggested building an underground railway</p><p>• Building the railway would make it possible to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbdd2a72-9c8f-48bc-a9c1-e7014dc32ba2\" data-question=\"2\">move<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> people to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"58f6523a-3351-4357-9283-5f77af0165cf\" data-question=\"2\">better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> housing in the 2..........................................</p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9797e2bb-7ef9-4b97-8c94-6870883fc021\" data-question=\"3\">A number of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> 3..........................................<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d32a7b53-dd5a-4b14-9ec4-d257c8e1b0c0\" data-question=\"3\">agreed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> with Pearson’s idea</p><p>• The company initially <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea02a4fb-6900-4265-b4a1-dda6bfb2a597\" data-question=\"4\">had problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64931a48-2010-4829-b61f-464c3d9b1484\" data-question=\"4\">getting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the 4..........................................needed for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0e9d354-bc9d-45a6-b743-b3015e90422b\" data-question=\"4\">project<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span></p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f1fcafcf-e236-4bc6-908e-a34986f87cef\" data-question=\"5\">Negative articles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> about the project <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03988431-7348-4de2-9103-0122db904f08\" data-question=\"5\">appeared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in the 5..........................................</p><p>The construction</p><p>• The chosen route did not require many buildings to be pulled down</p><p>• The ‘cut and cover’ method was used to construct the tunnels</p><p>• With the completion of the brick arch, the tunnel <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c04e91e-d040-42ea-bab7-75a8872a5483\" data-question=\"6\">was covered with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> 6..........................................</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40140\" id=\"question-wrapper-40140\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POPULATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40141\" id=\"question-wrapper-40141\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SUBURBS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40142\" id=\"question-wrapper-40142\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BUSINESSMEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40143\" id=\"question-wrapper-40143\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FUNDING</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40144\" id=\"question-wrapper-40144\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PRESS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40145\" id=\"question-wrapper-40145\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOIL</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</p><p>In boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</p><p><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40146\" id=\"question-wrapper-40146\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"31826cab-c33a-4e67-bc7d-ffe2bef51d1a\" data-question=\"7\">Other countries had built underground railways before<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the Metropolitan line opened. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40147\" id=\"question-wrapper-40147\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> More people than predicted travelled on the Metropolitan line on the first day. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40148\" id=\"question-wrapper-40148\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The use of ventilation shafts <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c0165d9-0cb0-4c3e-9045-768b5cfa887f\" data-question=\"9\">failed to prevent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64d8bf34-ec99-424a-b809-d6833ad6a467\" data-question=\"9\">pollution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> in the tunnels. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40149\" id=\"question-wrapper-40149\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71797f37-273c-4ccc-a6f1-a498a38d0cf4\" data-question=\"10\">different approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> from the ‘cut and cover’ technique was required in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c136ec67-99c8-4ab2-94cb-3630110a77fd\" data-question=\"10\">London’s central area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40150\" id=\"question-wrapper-40150\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The windows on City &amp; South London trains <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"418275ad-a4a9-45c9-bb5b-1fb9bd185b11\" data-question=\"11\">were at eye level<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40151\" id=\"question-wrapper-40151\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The City &amp; South London Railway was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f4ac1ef5-1ff4-4da1-a93e-3f2c8dcf35f6\" data-question=\"12\"><span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f4ac1ef5-1ff4-4da1-a93e-3f2c8dcf35f6\" data-question=\"12\">a financial success<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40152\" id=\"question-wrapper-40152\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Trains on the Tuppenny Tube’ nearly always ran on time. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"6950a84e-f361-4150-9b1d-cdadffe6419b","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"between 1800 and 1850","passagePhrase":"In the first half of the 1800s"},{"uid":"69b5e935-211f-4971-8097-1314e1155887","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"increased rapidly","passagePhrase":"grew at an astonishing rate"},{"uid":"cbdd2a72-9c8f-48bc-a9c1-e7014dc32ba2","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"move","passagePhrase":"relocate"},{"uid":"ae9400f9-d270-4ffe-ab3e-8c6031c3e4b8","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the poor workers"},{"uid":"58f6523a-3351-4357-9283-5f77af0165cf","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"better","passagePhrase":"newly constructed"},{"uid":"d32a7b53-dd5a-4b14-9ec4-d257c8e1b0c0","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"agreed","passagePhrase":"gained support"},{"uid":"9797e2bb-7ef9-4b97-8c94-6870883fc021","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"A number of","passagePhrase":"some"},{"uid":"ea02a4fb-6900-4265-b4a1-dda6bfb2a597","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"had problems","passagePhrase":"had difficulty in"},{"uid":"64931a48-2010-4829-b61f-464c3d9b1484","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"getting","passagePhrase":"raising"},{"uid":"b0e9d354-bc9d-45a6-b743-b3015e90422b","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"project","passagePhrase":"scheme"},{"uid":"f1fcafcf-e236-4bc6-908e-a34986f87cef","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"Negative articles","passagePhrase":"critical articles"},{"uid":"03988431-7348-4de2-9103-0122db904f08","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"appeared","passagePhrase":"printed"},{"uid":"0c04e91e-d040-42ea-bab7-75a8872a5483","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"was covered with","passagePhrase":"was laid on top of"},{"uid":"64d8bf34-ec99-424a-b809-d6833ad6a467","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"pollution","passagePhrase":"smoke and fumes"},{"uid":"9c0165d9-0cb0-4c3e-9045-768b5cfa887f","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"failed to prevent","passagePhrase":"remained a problem"},{"uid":"c136ec67-99c8-4ab2-94cb-3630110a77fd","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"London’s central area","passagePhrase":"this part of the capital"},{"uid":"71797f37-273c-4ccc-a6f1-a498a38d0cf4","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"different approach","passagePhrase":"alternative"}]},"reading_u2_272":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3><strong>Stadiums: past, present and future</strong></h3><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Stadiums are among the oldest forms of urban architecture: vast stadiums where the public could watch sporting events were at the centre of western city life as far back as the ancient Greek and Roman Empires, well before the construction of the great medieval cathedrals and the grand 19th- and 20th-century railway stations which dominated urban skylines in later eras.</p><p>Today, however, stadiums are regarded with growing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fedf1e62-8608-4d94-a766-b103566fee3c\" data-question=\"14\">scepticism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. Construction costs can soar above £1 billion, and stadiums finished for major events such as the Olympic Games or the FIFA World Cup have notably fallen into disuse and disrepair.</p><p>But this need not be the case. History shows that stadiums can drive urban development and adapt to the culture of every age. Even today, architects and planners are finding new ways to adapt the mono-functional sports arenas which became emblematic of modernisation during the 20th century.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>The amphitheatre* of Arles in southwest France, with a capacity of 25,000 spectators, is perhaps the best example of just how versatile stadiums can be. Built by the Romans in 90 AD, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"324ef4f2-9501-4bf7-80f6-eaa63e110f57\" data-question=\"18\">became<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> a fortress with four towers after the fifth century, and was then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"324ef4f2-9501-4bf7-80f6-eaa63e110f57\" data-question=\"18\">transformed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> into a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff518b94-5744-4a35-9c73-44df69b18a4b\" data-question=\"19\">village<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> containing more than 200 houses. With the growing interest in conservation during the 19th century, it was converted back into an arena for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"976f4ae9-f3dc-47ff-937d-5b7e2e194e29\" data-question=\"19\">staging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of bullfights, thereby returning the structure to its original <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5422bf1a-fa50-4db1-8929-fa8aed68a08d\" data-question=\"19\">use as a venue for public spectacles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</p><p>Another example is the imposing arena of Verona in northern Italy, with space for 30,000 spectators, which was built 60 years before the Arles amphitheatre and 40 years before Rome’s famous Colosseum. It has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4e50624c-0c73-4528-be69-d42fdb314f25\" data-question=\"20\">endured the centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0361b3d7-1021-40b9-8c78-a9456900a37a\" data-question=\"20\">currently<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> considered one of the world’s prime sites for opera, thanks to its outstanding acoustics.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>The area in the centre of the Italian town of Lucca, known as the Piazza dell’Anfiteatro, is yet another impressive example of an amphitheatre becoming absorbed into the fabric of the city. The site evolved in a similar way to Arles and was progressively filled with buildings from the Middle Ages <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aff4269f-0a0d-4984-9fa7-72f8ea2209b6\" data-question=\"21\">until the 19th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, variously <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b510833a-0e96-4349-99f6-8330e6625f06\" data-question=\"21\">used as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> houses, a salt <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbdad2d7-40b7-42da-9b40-7ba0478f9ce3\" data-question=\"21\">depot<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> and a prison. But rather than reverting to an arena, it became a market square, designed by Romanticist architect Lorenzo Nottolini. Today, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ddb0d917-ae65-4bef-bec4-233e084eaa2d\" data-question=\"22\">ruins<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of the amphitheatre remain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10b75d04-01ec-47d4-a198-0c15f2a46701\" data-question=\"22\">embedded in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the various shops and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c834cea-e891-47ef-bd13-357b6725fcec\" data-question=\"22\">residences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> surrounding the public square.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>There are many similarities between modern stadiums and the ancient amphitheatres intended for games. But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"66ed013a-d6f7-45fe-a6ba-750f6c0998fc\" data-question=\"23\">some of the flexibility was lost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> at the beginning of the 20th century, as stadiums were developed using new products such as steel and reinforced concrete, and made use of bright lights for night-time matches.</p><p>Many such stadiums are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7a7f3e3-8d3b-451c-ab1b-fbe57ac68fd1\" data-question=\"24\">situated in suburban areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, designed for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4521151-614a-4331-a406-4221a36ae59c\" data-question=\"17\">sporting use only<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7a7f3e3-8d3b-451c-ab1b-fbe57ac68fd1\" data-question=\"24\">surrounded by parking lots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. These factors mean that they may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb607ae9-5c1f-4275-8341-177ebbc843d9\" data-question=\"17\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"66ed013a-d6f7-45fe-a6ba-750f6c0998fc\" data-question=\"23\">not be as accessible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to the general public, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb607ae9-5c1f-4275-8341-177ebbc843d9\" data-question=\"17\">require more energy to run<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb607ae9-5c1f-4275-8341-177ebbc843d9\" data-question=\"17\">contribute to urban heat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>But many of today’s most innovative architects see scope for the stadium to help improve the city. Among the current strategies, two seem to be having particular success: the stadium as an urban hub, and as a power plant.</p><p>There’s a growing trend for stadiums <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71dc37ea-7a10-4dbb-bc2a-e70d784a1527\" data-question=\"16\">to be equipped with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> public spaces and services that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df0a6cbb-549e-495e-b9cf-198263f07830\" data-question=\"25\">serve a function<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> beyond sport, such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cc0fbf40-f8e4-4bd6-848a-c85908fbd02d\" data-question=\"16\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40e4da62-a11d-44a8-b3f1-d7d0ef595c43\" data-question=\"25\">hotels, retail outlets, conference centres, restaurants and bars, children’s playgrounds and green space<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Creating mixed-use developments such as this reinforces compactness and multi-functionality, making more efficient use of land and helping to regenerate urban spaces.</p><p>This opens the space up to families and a wider cross-section of society, instead of catering only to sportspeople and supporters. There have been many examples of this in the UK: the mixed-use facilities at Wembley and Old Trafford have become a blueprint for many other stadiums in the world.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>The phenomenon of stadiums as power stations has a<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a152029-ab3d-49bd-8440-0dcd8ae89803\" data-question=\"26\">rise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>n from the idea that energy problems can be overcome by integrating interconnected buildings by means of a smart grid, which is an electricity supply network that uses digital communications technology to detect and react to local changes in usage, without significant energy losses. Stadiums are ideal for these purposes, because their canopies have a large surface area for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a152029-ab3d-49bd-8440-0dcd8ae89803\" data-question=\"26\">fitting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> photovoltaic panels and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a152029-ab3d-49bd-8440-0dcd8ae89803\" data-question=\"26\">rise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> high <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b01e038-da7e-4f29-9925-34b32dc4667b\" data-question=\"26\">enough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (more than 40 metres) to make use of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"927bf609-98c7-4653-855d-257ae5e604a3\" data-question=\"26\">micro wind turbines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</p><p>Freiburg Mage Solar Stadium in Germany is the first of a new wave of stadiums as power plants, which also includes the Amsterdam Arena and the Kaohsiung Stadium. The latter, inaugurated in 2009, has 8,844 photovoltaic panels producing up to 1.14 GWh of electricity annually. This reduces the annual output of carbon dioxide by 660 tons and supplies up to 80 percent of the surrounding area when the stadium is not in use. This is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8e83ec1-3007-43e7-806b-6bfb57760f0f\" data-question=\"15\">proof<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> that a stadium can serve its city, and have a decidedly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e68dbcae-1cbb-4b81-88cd-dbb360652c31\" data-question=\"15\">positive impact in terms of reduction of CO2 emissions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>Sporting arenas have always been central to the life and culture of cities. In every era, the stadium has acquired new value and uses: from military fortress to residential village, public space to theatre and most recently a field for experimentation in advanced engineering. The stadium of today now brings together multiple functions, thus helping cities to create a sustainable future.</p><p><em>*amphitheatre: (especially in Greek and Roman architecture) an open circular or oval building with a central space surrounded by tiers of seats for spectators, for the presentation of dramatic or sporting events</em></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has seven sections, A-G.</p><p>Which section contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40153\" id=\"question-wrapper-40153\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a mention of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fedf1e62-8608-4d94-a766-b103566fee3c\" data-question=\"14\">negative attitudes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> towards stadium building projects </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40154\" id=\"question-wrapper-40154\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> figures <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8e83ec1-3007-43e7-806b-6bfb57760f0f\" data-question=\"15\">demonstrating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e68dbcae-1cbb-4b81-88cd-dbb360652c31\" data-question=\"15\">environmental benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of a certain stadium </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40155\" id=\"question-wrapper-40155\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cc0fbf40-f8e4-4bd6-848a-c85908fbd02d\" data-question=\"16\">the wide range of facilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71dc37ea-7a10-4dbb-bc2a-e70d784a1527\" data-question=\"16\">available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> at some new stadiums </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40156\" id=\"question-wrapper-40156\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb607ae9-5c1f-4275-8341-177ebbc843d9\" data-question=\"17\">disadvantages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of the stadiums built <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4521151-614a-4331-a406-4221a36ae59c\" data-question=\"17\">during a certain era<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below.</p><p>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Write your answers in boxes 18-22 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>Roman amphitheatres</strong></p><p>The Roman stadiums of Europe have proved very versatile. The amphitheatre of Arles, for example, was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"324ef4f2-9501-4bf7-80f6-eaa63e110f57\" data-question=\"18\">converted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> first into a 18........................................................, then into a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff518b94-5744-4a35-9c73-44df69b18a4b\" data-question=\"19\">residential area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and finally into an arena where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5422bf1a-fa50-4db1-8929-fa8aed68a08d\" data-question=\"19\">spectators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> could watch 19.........................................................Meanwhile, the arena in Verona, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4e50624c-0c73-4528-be69-d42fdb314f25\" data-question=\"20\">one of the oldest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> Roman amphitheatres, is famous <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0361b3d7-1021-40b9-8c78-a9456900a37a\" data-question=\"20\">today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> as a venue where 20....................................................... is performed. The site of Lucca’s amphitheatre has also been used <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b510833a-0e96-4349-99f6-8330e6625f06\" data-question=\"21\">for many purposes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aff4269f-0a0d-4984-9fa7-72f8ea2209b6\" data-question=\"21\">over the centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, including the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbdad2d7-40b7-42da-9b40-7ba0478f9ce3\" data-question=\"21\">storage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of 21.........................................................It is now a market square with 22........................................................and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c834cea-e891-47ef-bd13-357b6725fcec\" data-question=\"22\">homes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10b75d04-01ec-47d4-a198-0c15f2a46701\" data-question=\"22\">incorporated into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ddb0d917-ae65-4bef-bec4-233e084eaa2d\" data-question=\"22\">remains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of the Roman amphitheatre.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40157\" id=\"question-wrapper-40157\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FORTRESS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40158\" id=\"question-wrapper-40158\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BULLFIGHTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40159\" id=\"question-wrapper-40159\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OPERA</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40160\" id=\"question-wrapper-40160\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SALT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40161\" id=\"question-wrapper-40161\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SHOPS</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 23 and 24 on your answer sheet.</p><p>When comparing twentieth-century stadiums to ancient amphitheatres in Section D, which TWO negative features does the writer mention?</p><ul><li>A They are less imaginatively designed.</li><li>B They are less spacious.</li><li>C They are in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b7a7f3e3-8d3b-451c-ab1b-fbe57ac68fd1\" data-question=\"24\">less convenient locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>.</li><li>D They are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"66ed013a-d6f7-45fe-a6ba-750f6c0998fc\" data-question=\"23\">less versatile<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</li><li>E They are made of less durable materials.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40162\" id=\"question-wrapper-40162\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40163\" id=\"question-wrapper-40163\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 25 and 26 on your answer sheet.</p><p>Which TWO advantages of modern stadium design does the writer mention?</p><ul><li>A offering improved amenities for the enjoyment of sports events</li><li>B <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df0a6cbb-549e-495e-b9cf-198263f07830\" data-question=\"25\">bringing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40e4da62-a11d-44a8-b3f1-d7d0ef595c43\" data-question=\"25\">community life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> back into the city environment</li><li>C facilitating research into solar and wind energy solutions</li><li>D enabling local residents to reduce their consumption of electricity</li><li>E providing a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b01e038-da7e-4f29-9925-34b32dc4667b\" data-question=\"26\">suitable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> site for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a152029-ab3d-49bd-8440-0dcd8ae89803\" data-question=\"26\">installation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"927bf609-98c7-4653-855d-257ae5e604a3\" data-question=\"26\">renewable power generators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40164\" id=\"question-wrapper-40164\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40165\" id=\"question-wrapper-40165\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"fedf1e62-8608-4d94-a766-b103566fee3c","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"negative attitudes","passagePhrase":"scepticism"},{"uid":"324ef4f2-9501-4bf7-80f6-eaa63e110f57","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"converted","passagePhrase":"became ... transformed"},{"uid":"ff518b94-5744-4a35-9c73-44df69b18a4b","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"residential area","passagePhrase":"village"},{"uid":"976f4ae9-f3dc-47ff-937d-5b7e2e194e29","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"staging"},{"uid":"5422bf1a-fa50-4db1-8929-fa8aed68a08d","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"spectators","passagePhrase":"use as a venue for public spectacles"},{"uid":"4e50624c-0c73-4528-be69-d42fdb314f25","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"one of the oldest","passagePhrase":"endured the centuries"},{"uid":"0361b3d7-1021-40b9-8c78-a9456900a37a","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"today","passagePhrase":"currently"},{"uid":"aff4269f-0a0d-4984-9fa7-72f8ea2209b6","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"over the centuries","passagePhrase":"until the 19th century"},{"uid":"b510833a-0e96-4349-99f6-8330e6625f06","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"for many purposes","passagePhrase":"used as"},{"uid":"cbdad2d7-40b7-42da-9b40-7ba0478f9ce3","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"storage","passagePhrase":"depot"},{"uid":"ddb0d917-ae65-4bef-bec4-233e084eaa2d","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"remains","passagePhrase":"ruins"},{"uid":"10b75d04-01ec-47d4-a198-0c15f2a46701","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"incorporated into","passagePhrase":"embedded in"},{"uid":"4c834cea-e891-47ef-bd13-357b6725fcec","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"homes","passagePhrase":"residences"},{"uid":"66ed013a-d6f7-45fe-a6ba-750f6c0998fc","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"less versatile","passagePhrase":"some of the flexibility was lost ... not be as accessible"},{"uid":"b7a7f3e3-8d3b-451c-ab1b-fbe57ac68fd1","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"less convenient locations","passagePhrase":"situated in suburban areas ... surrounded by parking lots"},{"uid":"c4521151-614a-4331-a406-4221a36ae59c","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"during a certain era","passagePhrase":"sporting use only"},{"uid":"fb607ae9-5c1f-4275-8341-177ebbc843d9","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"disadvantages","passagePhrase":"not be as accessible ... require more energy to run ... contribute to urban heat"},{"uid":"71dc37ea-7a10-4dbb-bc2a-e70d784a1527","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"available","passagePhrase":"to be equipped with"},{"uid":"df0a6cbb-549e-495e-b9cf-198263f07830","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"bringing","passagePhrase":"serve a function"},{"uid":"cc0fbf40-f8e4-4bd6-848a-c85908fbd02d","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"the wide range of facilities","passagePhrase":"hotels, retail outlets, conference centres, restaurants and bars, children’s playgrounds and green space"},{"uid":"40e4da62-a11d-44a8-b3f1-d7d0ef595c43","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"community life","passagePhrase":"hotels, retail outlets, conference centres, restaurants and bars, children’s playgrounds and green space"},{"uid":"1a152029-ab3d-49bd-8440-0dcd8ae89803","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"installation","passagePhrase":"rise ... fitting ... rise"},{"uid":"3b01e038-da7e-4f29-9925-34b32dc4667b","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"suitable","passagePhrase":"enough"},{"uid":"927bf609-98c7-4653-855d-257ae5e604a3","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"renewable power generators","passagePhrase":"micro wind turbines"},{"uid":"d8e83ec1-3007-43e7-806b-6bfb57760f0f","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"demonstrating","passagePhrase":"proof"},{"uid":"e68dbcae-1cbb-4b81-88cd-dbb360652c31","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"environmental benefits","passagePhrase":"positive impact in terms of reduction of CO2 emissions"}]},"reading_u2_273":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3><strong>To catch a king</strong></h3><p><em>Anna Keay reviews Charles Spencers hook about the hunt for King Charles II during the English Civil War of the seventeenth century</em></p><p>Charles Spencer’s latest book, To Catch a King, tells us the story of the hunt for King Charles II in the six weeks after his resounding defeat at the Battle of Worcester in September 1651. And what a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"95130c66-5c4e-4c9d-8c3f-e8e1711179d8\" data-question=\"36\">story<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> it is. After his father was executed by the Parliamentarians in 1649, the young Charles II <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4847a2d-1a14-44f4-af05-c6d49e020732\" data-question=\"28\">sacrificed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> one of the very <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b5aa666-c0df-4d0f-aa9d-9461e007b4c5\" data-question=\"28\">principles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f30babf7-676f-4289-95bb-eaf58d4fa7e6\" data-question=\"28\">his father had died for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df472368-851e-431e-842b-cae29d2f4ce6\" data-question=\"27\">did a deal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> with the Scots, thereby accepting Presbyterianism* as the national religion <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7560846b-346c-473a-b2b1-31130af2d322\" data-question=\"27\">in return for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d95cc53-4a07-4249-abd0-0ebb52a6f218\" data-question=\"27\">being crowned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> King of Scots. His arrival in Edinburgh prompted the English Parliamentary army to invade Scotland in a pre-emptive strike. This was followed by a Scottish invasion of England. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"299c32b7-10d8-42d4-9267-e0a91cda6e09\" data-question=\"29\">The two sides finally faced one another<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> at Worcester in the west of England in 1651. After being comprehensively defeated on the meadows outside the city by the Parliamentarian army, the 21-year-old king found himself the subject of a national manhunt, with a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"020616dc-f97e-410d-9cad-de6735ee8779\" data-question=\"30\">huge sum<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> offered for his capture. Over the following six weeks he managed, through a series of heart-poundingly close <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27f70cd6-86a6-4ffc-81db-da95b9fad068\" data-question=\"29\">escapes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, to evade the Parliamentarians before <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27f70cd6-86a6-4ffc-81db-da95b9fad068\" data-question=\"29\">seeking refuge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f4d4f72-abe1-4b28-84de-326ed1303513\" data-question=\"31\">France<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. For the next nine years, the penniless and defeated Charles wandered around Europe with only a small group of loyal supporters.</p><p>Years later, after his restoration as king, the 50-year-old Charles II requested a meeting with the writer and diarist Samuel Pepys. His intention when asking Pepys to commit his story to paper was to ensure that this most extraordinary episode was never forgotten. Over two three-hour sittings, the king related to him <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"b061d217-b23a-463a-b74a-9cfe6b2b38fc\" data-question=\"33\">in great detail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> his personal recollections of the six weeks he had spent as a fugitive. As the king and secretary settled down (a scene that is surely a gift for a future scriptwriter), Charles commenced his story: ‘<span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"18a901f5-143f-4fe1-8e23-3feef45503b1\" data-question=\"34\">After the battle was so absolutely lost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> as to be beyond hope of recovery, I began to think of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47d8a75b-5172-42f2-856d-d61fb2b3bc8c\" data-question=\"34\">the best way of saving myself<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.’</p><p>One of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18cde615-9b8e-4d28-8864-b5dba6fd615c\" data-question=\"35\">joys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of Spencer’s book, a result not least of its use of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f18d61c4-491c-4b30-9843-640b86d11042\" data-question=\"35\">Charles II’s own narrative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> as well as those of his supporters, is just how close the reader gets to the action. The day-by-day <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8f39ff3-976e-45cf-a05a-59498a3ce3c4\" data-question=\"35\">retelling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e4e5f97-6dc3-4645-8c9e-556a13e7b29c\" data-question=\"37\">fugitives’ doings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"117b284b-4911-41fe-b03e-852ce219c15c\" data-question=\"37\">provides delicious details<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>: the cutting of the king’s long hair with agricultural shears, the use of walnut leaves to dye his pale skin, and the day Charles spent lying on a branch of the great oak tree in Boscobel Wood as the Parliamentary soldiers scoured the forest floor below. Spencer draws out both the humour - such as the preposterous refusal of Charles’s friend Henry Wilmot to adopt disguise on the grounds that it was beneath his dignity - and the emotional tension when the secret of the king’s presence was cautiously revealed to his supporters.</p><p>Charles’s adventures after losing the Battle of Worcester hide the uncomfortable truth that whilst almost everyone in England had been appalled by the execution of his father, they had not welcomed the arrival of his son with the Scots army, but had instead firmly bolted their doors. This was partly because he rode at the head of what looked like a foreign invasion force and partly because, after almost a decade of civil war, people were desperate to avoid it beginning again. This makes it all the more interesting that Charles II himself loved the story so much ever after. As well as retelling it to anyone who would listen, causing eye-rolling among courtiers, he set in train a series of initiatives to memorialise it. There was to be a new order of chivalry, the Knights of the Royal Oak. A series of enormous oil paintings depicting the episode were produced, including a two-metre-wide canvas of Boscobel Wood and a set of six similarly enormous paintings of the king on the run. In 1660, Charles II commissioned the artist John Michael Wright to paint a flying squadron of cherubs* carrying an oak tree to the heavens on the ceiling of his bedchamber. It is hard to imagine many other kings <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e34a2a4a-9dd7-461b-850c-ee2a607975ed\" data-question=\"38\">marking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"99809617-efad-4524-9f46-3af2dabf33fc\" data-question=\"38\">the lowest point in their life so enthusiastically<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, or indeed pulling off such an escape in the first place.</p><p>Charles Spencer is the perfect person to pass the story on to a new generation. His pacey, readable prose steers deftly clear of modern idioms and elegantly brings to life the details of the great tale. He has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f8fa1e22-c8ff-42cd-b2c6-f570cd2975b2\" data-question=\"39\">even-handed sympathy for both<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> the fugitive king and the fierce republican regime that hunted him, and he succeeds in his desire to explore far more of the background of the story than previous books on the subject have done. Indeed, the opening third of the book is about how Charles II found himself at Worcester in the first place, which for some will be reason alone to read To Catch a King.</p><p>The tantalising question left, in the end, is that of what it all meant. Would Charles II have been a different king had these six weeks never happened? The days and nights spent in hiding must have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0356c817-c2da-4f8f-a5bc-b07fbeee2c78\" data-question=\"40\">affected him in some way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Did the need to assume disguises, to survive on wit and charm alone, to use trickery and subterfuge to escape from tight corners help form him? This is the one area where the book doesn’t quite hit the mark. Instead its depiction of Charles II in his final years as an ineffective, pleasure-loving monarch doesn’t do justice to the man (neither is it accurate), or to the complexity of his character. But this one niggle aside, To Catch a King is an excellent read, and those who come to it knowing little of the famous tale will find they have a treat in store.</p><p><em>*Presbyterianism: part of the reformed Protestant religion</em></p><p><em>*cherub: an image of angelic children used in paintings</em></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p style=\"text-align:start\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Complete the summary using the list of phrases, A-J, below.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:start\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Write the correct letter, A-J, in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.</span></p><p style=\"text-align:start\"><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">The story behind the hunt for Charles II</span></strong></p><p style=\"text-align:start\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Charles II’s father was executed by the Parliamentarian forces in 1649. Charles II then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df472368-851e-431e-842b-cae29d2f4ce6\" data-question=\"27\">formed a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> 27..........................................with the Scots, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7560846b-346c-473a-b2b1-31130af2d322\" data-question=\"27\">in order to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d95cc53-4a07-4249-abd0-0ebb52a6f218\" data-question=\"27\">become<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> King of Scots, he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4847a2d-1a14-44f4-af05-c6d49e020732\" data-question=\"28\">abandoned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b5aa666-c0df-4d0f-aa9d-9461e007b4c5\" data-question=\"28\">important<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> 28..........................................that was held by his father and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f30babf7-676f-4289-95bb-eaf58d4fa7e6\" data-question=\"28\">had contributed to his father’s death<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. The opposing sides then met outside Worcester in 1651. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"299c32b7-10d8-42d4-9267-e0a91cda6e09\" data-question=\"29\">battle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> led to a 29..........................................for the Parliamentarians and Charles had to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"27f70cd6-86a6-4ffc-81db-da95b9fad068\" data-question=\"29\">flee<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> for his life. A 30..........................................was offered for Charles’s capture, but after six weeks spent in hiding, he eventually managed to reach the 31..........................................of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5f4d4f72-abe1-4b28-84de-326ed1303513\" data-question=\"31\">continental Europe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</span></p><table style=\"font-family:Times; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-decoration-thickness:initial\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">A. military innovation</span></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"020616dc-f97e-410d-9cad-de6735ee8779\" data-question=\"30\">large reward<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> </span></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">C. widespread conspiracy</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">D. relative safety</span></p></td><td><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">E. new government </span></p></td><td><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">F. decisive victory</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">G. political debate</span></p></td><td><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">H. strategic alliance </span></p></td><td><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">I. popular solution</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">J. religious conviction</span></p></td><td><p> </p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr></tbody></table><p> </p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40166\" id=\"question-wrapper-40166\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40167\" id=\"question-wrapper-40167\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">J</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40168\" id=\"question-wrapper-40168\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40169\" id=\"question-wrapper-40169\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40170\" id=\"question-wrapper-40170\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</p><p>In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write</p><p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</p><p><strong>NO </strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</p><p><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40171\" id=\"question-wrapper-40171\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Charles chose Pepys for the task because he considered him to be trustworthy. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40172\" id=\"question-wrapper-40172\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Charles’s personal recollection of the escape <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"b061d217-b23a-463a-b74a-9cfe6b2b38fc\" data-question=\"33\">lacked sufficient detail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40173\" id=\"question-wrapper-40173\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Charles indicated to Pepys that he had planned his escape <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"18a901f5-143f-4fe1-8e23-3feef45503b1\" data-question=\"34\">before the battle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40174\" id=\"question-wrapper-40174\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8f39ff3-976e-45cf-a05a-59498a3ce3c4\" data-question=\"35\">inclusion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f18d61c4-491c-4b30-9843-640b86d11042\" data-question=\"35\">Charles’s account<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18cde615-9b8e-4d28-8864-b5dba6fd615c\" data-question=\"35\">positive aspect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of the book. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Questions 36-40</p><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40175\" id=\"question-wrapper-40175\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the reviewer’s main purpose in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. to describe what happened during the Battle of Worcester</li> <li>B. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"95130c66-5c4e-4c9d-8c3f-e8e1711179d8\" data-question=\"36\">give an account<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of the circumstances leading to Charles II's escape</li> <li>C. to provide details of the Parliamentarians’ political views</li> <li>D. to compare Charles II’s beliefs with those of his father</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40176\" id=\"question-wrapper-40176\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Why does the reviewer include examples of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6e4e5f97-6dc3-4645-8c9e-556a13e7b29c\" data-question=\"37\">fugitives’ behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in the third paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. to explain how close Charles II came to losing his life</li> <li>B. to suggest that Charles II’s supporters were badly prepared</li> <li>C. to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"117b284b-4911-41fe-b03e-852ce219c15c\" data-question=\"37\">illustrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> how the events of the six weeks are brought to life</li> <li>D. to argue that certain aspects are not as well known as they should be</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40177\" id=\"question-wrapper-40177\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does the reviewer make about Charles II in the fourth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e34a2a4a-9dd7-461b-850c-ee2a607975ed\" data-question=\"38\">chose to celebrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"99809617-efad-4524-9f46-3af2dabf33fc\" data-question=\"38\">what was essentially a defeat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li> <li>B. He misunderstood the motives of his opponents.</li> <li>C. He aimed to restore people’s faith in the monarchy.</li> <li>D. He was driven by a desire to be popular.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40178\" id=\"question-wrapper-40178\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the reviewer say about Charles Spencer in the fifth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. His decision to write the book comes as a surprise.</li> <li>B. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f8fa1e22-c8ff-42cd-b2c6-f570cd2975b2\" data-question=\"39\">takes an unbiased approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> to the subject matter.</li> <li>C. His descriptions of events would be better if they included more detail.</li> <li>D. He chooses language that is suitable for a twenty-first-century audience.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40179\" id=\"question-wrapper-40179\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When the reviewer says the book ‘doesn’t quite hit the mark’, she is making the point that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. it overlooks the impact of events on ordinary people.</li> <li>B. it lacks an analysis of prevalent views on monarchy.</li> <li>C. it omits any references to the deceit practised by Charles II during his time in hiding.</li> <li>D. it fails to address whether Charles M’s experiences had a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0356c817-c2da-4f8f-a5bc-b07fbeee2c78\" data-question=\"40\">lasting influence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> on him.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"95130c66-5c4e-4c9d-8c3f-e8e1711179d8","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"give an account","passagePhrase":"story"},{"uid":"f4847a2d-1a14-44f4-af05-c6d49e020732","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"abandoned","passagePhrase":"sacrificed"},{"uid":"4b5aa666-c0df-4d0f-aa9d-9461e007b4c5","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"important","passagePhrase":"principles"},{"uid":"f30babf7-676f-4289-95bb-eaf58d4fa7e6","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"had contributed to his father’s death","passagePhrase":"his father had died for"},{"uid":"df472368-851e-431e-842b-cae29d2f4ce6","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"formed a","passagePhrase":"did a deal"},{"uid":"7560846b-346c-473a-b2b1-31130af2d322","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"in order to","passagePhrase":"in return for"},{"uid":"9d95cc53-4a07-4249-abd0-0ebb52a6f218","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"become","passagePhrase":"being crowned"},{"uid":"299c32b7-10d8-42d4-9267-e0a91cda6e09","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"battle","passagePhrase":"The two sides finally faced one another"},{"uid":"020616dc-f97e-410d-9cad-de6735ee8779","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"large reward","passagePhrase":"huge sum"},{"uid":"27f70cd6-86a6-4ffc-81db-da95b9fad068","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"flee","passagePhrase":"escapes ... seeking refuge"},{"uid":"5f4d4f72-abe1-4b28-84de-326ed1303513","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"continental Europe","passagePhrase":"France"},{"uid":"47d8a75b-5172-42f2-856d-d61fb2b3bc8c","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"the best way of saving myself"},{"uid":"18cde615-9b8e-4d28-8864-b5dba6fd615c","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"positive aspect","passagePhrase":"joys"},{"uid":"f18d61c4-491c-4b30-9843-640b86d11042","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"Charles’s account","passagePhrase":"Charles II’s own narrative"},{"uid":"d8f39ff3-976e-45cf-a05a-59498a3ce3c4","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"inclusion","passagePhrase":"retelling"},{"uid":"6e4e5f97-6dc3-4645-8c9e-556a13e7b29c","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"fugitives’ behaviour","passagePhrase":"fugitives’ doings"},{"uid":"117b284b-4911-41fe-b03e-852ce219c15c","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"illustrate","passagePhrase":"provides delicious details"},{"uid":"e34a2a4a-9dd7-461b-850c-ee2a607975ed","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"chose to celebrate","passagePhrase":"marking"},{"uid":"99809617-efad-4524-9f46-3af2dabf33fc","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"what was essentially a defeat","passagePhrase":"the lowest point in their life so enthusiastically"},{"uid":"f8fa1e22-c8ff-42cd-b2c6-f570cd2975b2","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"takes an unbiased approach","passagePhrase":"even-handed sympathy for both"},{"uid":"0356c817-c2da-4f8f-a5bc-b07fbeee2c78","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"lasting influence","passagePhrase":"affected him in some way"}]},"reading_u2_274":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</p><h3><strong>The Dead Sea Scrolls</strong></h3><p>In late 1946 or early 1947, three Bedouin teenagers were tending their goats and sheep near the ancient settlement of Qumran, located on the northwest shore of the Dead Sea in what is now known as the West Bank. One of these young shepherds <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8037abeb-a889-493f-b0bb-a2f7b6f8e0d2\" data-question=\"1\">tossed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> a rock into an opening on the side of a cliff and was surprised to hear <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0192013a-fef8-4090-a290-bfbb7082dc15\" data-question=\"1\">a shattering sound<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. He and his companions later <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"989149da-7d7f-4b56-be13-2d33b5d99db0\" data-question=\"2\">entered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the cave and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"646de9b0-7db2-4ea6-81f2-72166146414f\" data-question=\"3\">stumbled across<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72190a2c-6ad2-4b7b-9e08-4f1142c57f59\" data-question=\"3\">a collection of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> large clay <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c614e14d-24f8-4192-8315-6117fed722dd\" data-question=\"3\">jars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, seven of which contained scrolls with writing on them. The teenagers took the seven scrolls to a nearby town where they were sold for a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ca7ebb1-bcc7-4ecc-8b95-e3b9591368a4\" data-question=\"6\">small sum<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> to a local antiquities dealer. Word of the find spread, and Bedouins and archaeologists eventually unearthed tens of thousands of additional scroll fragments from 10 nearby caves; together they make up between 800 and 900 manuscripts. It soon became clear that this was one of the greatest archaeological discoveries ever made.</p><p>The origin of the Dead Sea Scrolls, which were written around 2,000 years ago between 150 BCE and 70 CE, is still the subject of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"17d3f53a-2f61-429e-963e-04b2c73d7b2e\" data-question=\"7\">scholarly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"dedfbf4e-02b0-47c2-8f48-b5cbb684bdb8\" data-question=\"7\">debate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> even today. According to the prevailing theory, they are the work of a population that inhabited the area until Roman troops destroyed the settlement around 70 CE. The area was known as Judea at that time, and the people are thought to have belonged to a group <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b77004f-05ad-4374-a72a-3723c5c9e626\" data-question=\"4\">called<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the Essenes, a devout Jewish sect.</p><p>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62db3328-df19-4bcc-b782-2cbc9f68f433\" data-question=\"5\">majority of the texts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> on the Dead Sea Scrolls are in Hebrew, with some fragments written in an ancient version of its alphabet thought to have fallen out of use in the fifth century BCE. But there are other languages as well. Some scrolls are in Aramaic, the language spoken by many inhabitants of the region from the sixth century BCE to the siege of Jerusalem in 70 CE. In addition, several texts feature translations of the Hebrew Bible into Greek.</p><p>The Dead Sea Scrolls <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8704cc2b-c693-43fb-9238-5e27493cf003\" data-question=\"8\">include fragments from every book<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of the Old Testament of the Bible except for the Book of Esther. The only entire book of the Hebrew Bible preserved among the manuscripts from Qumran is Isaiah; this copy, dated to the first century BCE, is considered the earliest biblical manuscript still in existence. Along with biblical texts, the scrolls include documents about sectarian regulations and religious writings that do not appear in the Old Testament.</p><p>The writing on the Dead Sea Scrolls is mostly in black or occasionally red ink, and the scrolls themselves are nearly all made of either parchment (animal skin) or an early form of paper called ‘papyrus’. The only exception is the scroll numbered 3Q15, which was created out of a combination of copper and tin. Known as the Copper Scroll, this curious document features letters chiselled onto metal - perhaps, as some have theorized, to better withstand the passage of time. One of the most intriguing manuscripts from Qumran, this is a sort of ancient treasure map that lists dozens of gold and silver caches. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43d671bb-4695-4238-a57a-e8a388c0d906\" data-question=\"9\">Using an unconventional vocabulary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43d671bb-4695-4238-a57a-e8a388c0d906\" data-question=\"9\">odd spelling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, it describes 64 underground hiding places that supposedly contain riches buried for safekeeping. None of these hoards have been recovered, possibly because the Romans pillaged Judea during the first century CE. According to various hypotheses, the treasure belonged to local people, or was rescued from the Second Temple before its destruction or never existed to begin with.</p><p>Some of the Dead Sea Scrolls have been on interesting journeys. In 1948, a Syrian Orthodox archbishop known as Mar Samuel acquired four of the original seven scrolls from a Jerusalem shoemaker and part-time antiquity dealer, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a45f20cf-6ad8-4fc5-9e97-9474d44a3b7b\" data-question=\"10\">paying less than $100 for them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. He then travelled to the United States and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7f555c03-b5f1-4a45-a381-aaa9410e4623\" data-question=\"11\">unsuccessfully offered them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> to a number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82489e0d-7132-4350-8a45-d46b14318bb9\" data-question=\"11\">universities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, including Yale. Finally, in 1954, he placed an advertisement in the business newspaper The Wall Street Journal - under the category ‘Miscellaneous Items for Sale’ - that read: ‘Biblical Manuscripts dating back to at least 200 B.C. are for sale. This would be an ideal gift to an educational or religious institution by an individual or group.’ Fortunately, Israeli archaeologist and statesman Yigael Yadin negotiated their purchase and brought the scrolls back to Jerusalem, where they remain to this day.</p><p>In 2017, researchers from the University of Haifa restored and deciphered one of the last untranslated scrolls. The university’s Eshbal Ratson and Jonathan Ben-Dov spent one year reassembling the 60 fragments that make up the scroll. Deciphered from a band of coded text on parchment, the find provides insight into the community of people who wrote it and the 364-day calendar they would have used. The scroll names <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"351e152d-1954-4350-af8e-a1d7056f761a\" data-question=\"12\">celebrations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e54f347-efb7-4e52-94f7-545379629a5e\" data-question=\"12\">indicate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> shifts in seasons and details two <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e431319-dff9-4bae-9780-4a8d97ba5135\" data-question=\"12\">yearly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> religious <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"351e152d-1954-4350-af8e-a1d7056f761a\" data-question=\"12\">events<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> known from another Dead Sea Scroll. Only one more known scroll remains untranslated.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>The Dead Sea Scrolls</strong></p><p>Discovery</p><p>Qumran, 1946/7</p><p>• three Bedouin shepherds in their teens were near an opening on side of cliff</p><p>• heard <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0192013a-fef8-4090-a290-bfbb7082dc15\" data-question=\"1\">a noise of breaking<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> when one teenager <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8037abeb-a889-493f-b0bb-a2f7b6f8e0d2\" data-question=\"1\">threw<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> a 1..........................................</p><p>• teenagers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"989149da-7d7f-4b56-be13-2d33b5d99db0\" data-question=\"2\">went into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the 2..........................................and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"646de9b0-7db2-4ea6-81f2-72166146414f\" data-question=\"3\">found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> a number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c614e14d-24f8-4192-8315-6117fed722dd\" data-question=\"3\">containers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> made of 3..........................................</p><p>The scrolls</p><p>• date from between 150 BCE and 70 CE</p><p>• thought to have been written by group of people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b77004f-05ad-4374-a72a-3723c5c9e626\" data-question=\"4\">known as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> the 4..........................................</p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62db3328-df19-4bcc-b782-2cbc9f68f433\" data-question=\"5\">written mainly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in the 5..........................................language</p><p>• most are on religious topics, written using ink on parchment or papyrus</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40220\" id=\"question-wrapper-40220\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ROCK</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40221\" id=\"question-wrapper-40221\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CAVE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40222\" id=\"question-wrapper-40222\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CLAY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40223\" id=\"question-wrapper-40223\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ESSENES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40224\" id=\"question-wrapper-40224\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HEBREW</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p style=\"text-align:start\">Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</p><p>In boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet, write</p><ul><li><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</li><li><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</li><li><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40225\" id=\"question-wrapper-40225\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Bedouin teenagers who found the scrolls were disappointed by how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ca7ebb1-bcc7-4ecc-8b95-e3b9591368a4\" data-question=\"6\">little money<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> they received for them. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40226\" id=\"question-wrapper-40226\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"dedfbf4e-02b0-47c2-8f48-b5cbb684bdb8\" data-question=\"7\">agreement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> among <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"17d3f53a-2f61-429e-963e-04b2c73d7b2e\" data-question=\"7\">academics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> about the origin of the Dead Sea Scrolls. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40227\" id=\"question-wrapper-40227\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Most of the books of the Bible written on the scrolls are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8704cc2b-c693-43fb-9238-5e27493cf003\" data-question=\"8\">incomplete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40228\" id=\"question-wrapper-40228\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The information on the Copper Scroll is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43d671bb-4695-4238-a57a-e8a388c0d906\" data-question=\"9\">written in an unusual way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40229\" id=\"question-wrapper-40229\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Mar Samuel <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a45f20cf-6ad8-4fc5-9e97-9474d44a3b7b\" data-question=\"10\">was given some of the scrolls as a gift<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40230\" id=\"question-wrapper-40230\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the early 1950s, a number of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82489e0d-7132-4350-8a45-d46b14318bb9\" data-question=\"11\">educational establishments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in the US <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7f555c03-b5f1-4a45-a381-aaa9410e4623\" data-question=\"11\">were keen to buy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> scrolls from Mar Samuel. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40231\" id=\"question-wrapper-40231\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The scroll that was pieced together in 2017 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e54f347-efb7-4e52-94f7-545379629a5e\" data-question=\"12\">contains information about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e431319-dff9-4bae-9780-4a8d97ba5135\" data-question=\"12\">annual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"351e152d-1954-4350-af8e-a1d7056f761a\" data-question=\"12\">occasions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in the Qumran area 2,000 years ago.\" </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40232\" id=\"question-wrapper-40232\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Academics at the University of Haifa are currently researching how to decipher the final scroll. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"8037abeb-a889-493f-b0bb-a2f7b6f8e0d2","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"threw","passagePhrase":"tossed"},{"uid":"0192013a-fef8-4090-a290-bfbb7082dc15","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"a noise of breaking","passagePhrase":"a shattering sound"},{"uid":"989149da-7d7f-4b56-be13-2d33b5d99db0","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"went into","passagePhrase":"entered"},{"uid":"646de9b0-7db2-4ea6-81f2-72166146414f","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"found","passagePhrase":"stumbled across"},{"uid":"72190a2c-6ad2-4b7b-9e08-4f1142c57f59","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a collection of"},{"uid":"c614e14d-24f8-4192-8315-6117fed722dd","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"containers","passagePhrase":"jars"},{"uid":"7ca7ebb1-bcc7-4ecc-8b95-e3b9591368a4","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"little money","passagePhrase":"small sum"},{"uid":"17d3f53a-2f61-429e-963e-04b2c73d7b2e","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"academics","passagePhrase":"scholarly"},{"uid":"7b77004f-05ad-4374-a72a-3723c5c9e626","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"known as","passagePhrase":"called"},{"uid":"62db3328-df19-4bcc-b782-2cbc9f68f433","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"written mainly","passagePhrase":"majority of the texts"},{"uid":"8704cc2b-c693-43fb-9238-5e27493cf003","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"incomplete","passagePhrase":"include fragments from every book"},{"uid":"43d671bb-4695-4238-a57a-e8a388c0d906","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"written in an unusual way","passagePhrase":"Using an unconventional vocabulary ... odd spelling"},{"uid":"82489e0d-7132-4350-8a45-d46b14318bb9","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"educational establishments","passagePhrase":"universities"},{"uid":"351e152d-1954-4350-af8e-a1d7056f761a","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"occasions","passagePhrase":"celebrations ... events"},{"uid":"2e54f347-efb7-4e52-94f7-545379629a5e","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"contains information about","passagePhrase":"indicate"},{"uid":"0e431319-dff9-4bae-9780-4a8d97ba5135","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"annual","passagePhrase":"yearly"}]},"reading_u2_275":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</p><h3><strong>A second attempt at domesticating the tomato</strong></h3><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>It took at least 3,000 years for humans to learn how to domesticate the wild tomato and cultivate it for food. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c281c440-432e-4f1b-8510-c8381dbcc80b\" data-question=\"17\">Now<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> two separate teams in Brazil and China have done it all over again in less than three years. And they have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d13a0337-3a32-4912-8640-a6143e5beba6\" data-question=\"17\">done it better in some ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, as the re-domesticated tomatoes are more nutritious than the ones we eat at present.</p><p>This approach relies on the revolutionary CRISPR genome editing technique, in which changes are deliberately made to the DNA of a living cell, allowing genetic material to be added, removed or altered. The technique could not only improve existing crops, but could also be used to turn thousands of wild plants into useful and appealing foods. In fact, a third team in the US has already begun to do this with a relative of the tomato called the groundcherry.</p><p>This fast-track domestication could help make the world’s food supply healthier and far more resistant to diseases, such as the rust fungus devastating wheat crops.</p><p>'This could transform what we eat,' says Jorg Kudla at the University of Munster in Germany, a member of the Brazilian team. 'There are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0fcb9c7a-263c-4c6c-810d-a559d0bd51cd\" data-question=\"23\">50,000 edible plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6fac9c8a-82a7-4b16-b998-1df01ad3bee2\" data-question=\"23\">in the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, but 90 percent of our energy comes from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9891f25a-3039-4a1e-b963-11575a440ffb\" data-question=\"23\">just 15 crops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.'</p><p>‘We can now mimic the known domestication course of major crops like rice, maize, sorghum or others,’ says Caixia Gao of the Chinese Academy of Sciences in Beijing. Then we might try to domesticate plants that have never been domesticated.’</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>Wild tomatoes, which are native to the Andes region in South America, produce pea-sized fruits. Over many generations, peoples such as the Aztecs and Incas transformed the plant by selecting and breeding plants with mutations* in their genetic structure, which resulted in desirable traits such as larger fruit.</p><p>But every time <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e0a002c0-d266-48db-beb3-2e56e99ea8eb\" data-question=\"15\">a single plant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> with a mutation is taken from a larger population for breeding, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"960f02ca-6790-40e0-92ee-66dd58cdb122\" data-question=\"15\">much genetic diversity is lost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. And sometimes the desirable mutations come with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"960f02ca-6790-40e0-92ee-66dd58cdb122\" data-question=\"15\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b3d6cdd-2776-48e1-be9d-fac351be2f36\" data-question=\"24\">less desirable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> traits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. For instance, the tomato strains grown for supermarkets have lost much of their flavour.</p><p>By comparing the genomes of modern plants to those of their wild relatives, biologists have been working out what genetic changes occurred as plants were domesticated. The teams in Brazil and China have now used this knowledge to reintroduce these changes from scratch while maintaining or even enhancing the desirable traits of wild strains.</p><p><strong>C </strong></p><p>Kudla’s team made six changes altogether. For instance, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4741a283-1d72-4adb-8713-9328d8131b64\" data-question=\"25\">tripled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> the size of fruit by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2d2de96-de9b-4e6b-a356-2c032141040c\" data-question=\"18\">editing a gene called FRUIT WEIGHT<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, and increased the number of tomatoes per truss by editing another called <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2d2de96-de9b-4e6b-a356-2c032141040c\" data-question=\"18\">MULTIFLORA<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</p><p>While the historical domestication of tomatoes reduced levels of the red pigment lycopene - thought to have potential health benefits - the team in Brazil managed to boost it instead. The wild tomato has twice as much lycopene as cultivated ones; the newly domesticated one has five times as much.</p><p>'They are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"764c3832-add8-4e17-89c7-138a69a75758\" data-question=\"18\">quite tasty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>,' says Kudla. ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"764c3832-add8-4e17-89c7-138a69a75758\" data-question=\"18\">A little bit strong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. And <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"764c3832-add8-4e17-89c7-138a69a75758\" data-question=\"18\">very aromatic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.’</p><p>The team in China re-domesticated several strains of wild tomatoes with desirable traits lost in domesticated tomatoes. In this way they managed to create <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"01a01401-9951-4dd9-9cfb-8f13b4795d4c\" data-question=\"14\">a strain resistant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to a common <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a07e927-b581-4061-9c2b-df418678c325\" data-question=\"14\">disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> called bacterial spot race, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2529cfe1-2dcb-43ea-b525-cf40bbae7727\" data-question=\"14\">which can devastate yields<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. They also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"111c3cf3-4299-48ad-9664-03c18d7ae398\" data-question=\"26\">created<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> another strain that is more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74203efb-06cf-456a-ac57-18d9f0bc57a8\" data-question=\"26\">salt tolerant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> - and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"653041fb-019a-4f56-b282-e7adc694bd83\" data-question=\"26\">has higher levels of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> vitamin C.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>Meanwhile, Joyce Van Eck at the Boyce Thompson Institute in New York state decided to use the same approach to domesticate the groundcherry or goldenberry (Physalis pruinosa) for the first time. This fruit looks similar to the closely related Cape gooseberry (Physalis peruviana).</p><p>Groundcherries are already sold to a limited extent in the US but they are hard to produce because the plant has a sprawling growth habit and the small fruits fall off the branches when ripe. Van Eck’s team has edited the plants to increase fruit size, make their growth more compact and to stop fruits dropping. ‘There’s potential for this to be a commercial crop,’ says Van Eck. But she adds that taking the work further <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d8e1ccc-d26c-4196-b8d5-0322f8a3c664\" data-question=\"22\">would be expensive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> because of the need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e63fe81-e724-4ba8-9149-c4c5c9d0dec0\" data-question=\"22\">pay for a licence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> for the CRISPR technology and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e63fe81-e724-4ba8-9149-c4c5c9d0dec0\" data-question=\"22\">get regulatory approval<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>This approach could boost the use of many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"878af82a-3eeb-41e7-bf1f-0ccb032c2971\" data-question=\"20\">obscure plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, says Jonathan Jones of the Sainsbury Lab in the UK. But it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"694582d9-46d2-4ea2-ae79-11ccb247bd71\" data-question=\"20\">will be hard<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> for new foods to grow <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6af87b38-d9a6-4968-a944-9d1d4251f2cc\" data-question=\"20\">so popular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> with farmers and consumers that they become new staple crops, he thinks.</p><p>The three teams already have their eye on other plants that could be ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6b33e6c4-a06a-49ba-823b-f04f1faaa244\" data-question=\"16\">catapulted into the mainstream<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>’, including foxtail, oat-grass and cowpea. By choosing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bdacde29-8890-472d-b784-be00f92c6786\" data-question=\"19\">wild plants that are drought or heat tolerant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, says Gao, we could create crops that will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1996b039-3478-46bb-bc5e-7f0ca73b9d0c\" data-question=\"19\">thrive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> even as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b41c7fc7-22a4-4853-ab0b-ccf67fb29f11\" data-question=\"19\">the planet warms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</p><p>But Kudla <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"318fa176-8357-4bb6-9d63-504e10cb7ed1\" data-question=\"21\">didn’t want to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12b946e4-02bc-4d50-89af-128736b39a09\" data-question=\"21\">reveal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> which species were in his team’s sights, because CRISPR has made the process so easy. ‘Any one with the right skills could go to their lab and do this.’</p><p><em>*mutations: changes in an organism’s genetic structure that can be passed down to later generations</em></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has five sections, A-E.</p><p>Which section contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40233\" id=\"question-wrapper-40233\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"01a01401-9951-4dd9-9cfb-8f13b4795d4c\" data-question=\"14\">a type of tomato that can resist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2529cfe1-2dcb-43ea-b525-cf40bbae7727\" data-question=\"14\">dangerous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a07e927-b581-4061-9c2b-df418678c325\" data-question=\"14\">infection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40234\" id=\"question-wrapper-40234\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"960f02ca-6790-40e0-92ee-66dd58cdb122\" data-question=\"15\">problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> can arise from focusing only on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e0a002c0-d266-48db-beb3-2e56e99ea8eb\" data-question=\"15\">a certain type<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of tomato plant. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40235\" id=\"question-wrapper-40235\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a number of examples of plants that are not cultivated at present but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6b33e6c4-a06a-49ba-823b-f04f1faaa244\" data-question=\"16\">could be useful as food sources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40236\" id=\"question-wrapper-40236\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d13a0337-3a32-4912-8640-a6143e5beba6\" data-question=\"17\">a comparison<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> between the early domestication of the tomato and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c281c440-432e-4f1b-8510-c8381dbcc80b\" data-question=\"17\">more recent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> research </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40237\" id=\"question-wrapper-40237\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a personal reaction to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"764c3832-add8-4e17-89c7-138a69a75758\" data-question=\"18\">the flavour of a tomato<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2d2de96-de9b-4e6b-a356-2c032141040c\" data-question=\"18\">genetically edited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following statements (Questions 19-23) and the list of researchers below. Match each statement with the correct researcher, A-D.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 19-23 on your answer sheet.</p><p><em>NB You may use any letter more than once.</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"vertical-align:middle\"><p>List of Researchers</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>A</p></td><td><p>Jorg Kudla</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>B</p></td><td><p>Caixia Gao</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>Joyce Van Eck</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>D</p></td><td><p>Jonathan Jones</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40238\" id=\"question-wrapper-40238\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Domestication of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bdacde29-8890-472d-b784-be00f92c6786\" data-question=\"19\">certain plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> could allow them to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1996b039-3478-46bb-bc5e-7f0ca73b9d0c\" data-question=\"19\">adapt to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b41c7fc7-22a4-4853-ab0b-ccf67fb29f11\" data-question=\"19\">future environmental challenges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40239\" id=\"question-wrapper-40239\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The idea of growing and eating <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"878af82a-3eeb-41e7-bf1f-0ccb032c2971\" data-question=\"20\">unusual plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"694582d9-46d2-4ea2-ae79-11ccb247bd71\" data-question=\"20\">may not be accepted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6af87b38-d9a6-4968-a944-9d1d4251f2cc\" data-question=\"20\">on a large scale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40240\" id=\"question-wrapper-40240\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"318fa176-8357-4bb6-9d63-504e10cb7ed1\" data-question=\"21\">not advisable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> for the future direction of certain research to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12b946e4-02bc-4d50-89af-128736b39a09\" data-question=\"21\">be made public<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40241\" id=\"question-wrapper-40241\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Present efforts to domesticate one wild fruit are limited by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d8e1ccc-d26c-4196-b8d5-0322f8a3c664\" data-question=\"22\">the costs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> involved. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40242\" id=\"question-wrapper-40242\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Humans only make use of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9891f25a-3039-4a1e-b963-11575a440ffb\" data-question=\"23\">a small proportion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0fcb9c7a-263c-4c6c-810d-a559d0bd51cd\" data-question=\"23\">the plant food available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6fac9c8a-82a7-4b16-b998-1df01ad3bee2\" data-question=\"23\">on Earth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the sentences below.</p><p>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40243\" id=\"question-wrapper-40243\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> An <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b3d6cdd-2776-48e1-be9d-fac351be2f36\" data-question=\"24\">undesirable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> trait such as loss of..........................................may be caused by a mutation in a tomato gene. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FLAVO(U)R</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40244\" id=\"question-wrapper-40244\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> By <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57e72cca-3beb-40f3-b4bd-cf2fbd23f499\" data-question=\"25\">modifying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> one gene in a tomato plant, researchers made the tomato <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4741a283-1d72-4adb-8713-9328d8131b64\" data-question=\"25\">three times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> its original........................................... </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SIZE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40245\" id=\"question-wrapper-40245\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A type of tomato which was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74203efb-06cf-456a-ac57-18d9f0bc57a8\" data-question=\"26\">not badly affected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> by.........................................., and was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"653041fb-019a-4f56-b282-e7adc694bd83\" data-question=\"26\">rich in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> vitamin C, was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"111c3cf3-4299-48ad-9664-03c18d7ae398\" data-question=\"26\">produced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> by a team of researchers in China. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SALT</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c281c440-432e-4f1b-8510-c8381dbcc80b","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"more recent","passagePhrase":"Now"},{"uid":"d13a0337-3a32-4912-8640-a6143e5beba6","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"a comparison","passagePhrase":"done it better in some ways"},{"uid":"0fcb9c7a-263c-4c6c-810d-a559d0bd51cd","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"the plant food available","passagePhrase":"50,000 edible plants"},{"uid":"6fac9c8a-82a7-4b16-b998-1df01ad3bee2","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"on Earth","passagePhrase":"in the world"},{"uid":"9891f25a-3039-4a1e-b963-11575a440ffb","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"a small proportion","passagePhrase":"just 15 crops"},{"uid":"e0a002c0-d266-48db-beb3-2e56e99ea8eb","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"a certain type","passagePhrase":"a single plant"},{"uid":"960f02ca-6790-40e0-92ee-66dd58cdb122","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"problems","passagePhrase":"much genetic diversity is lost ... less desirable traits"},{"uid":"9b3d6cdd-2776-48e1-be9d-fac351be2f36","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"undesirable","passagePhrase":"less desirable"},{"uid":"4741a283-1d72-4adb-8713-9328d8131b64","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"three times","passagePhrase":"tripled"},{"uid":"c2d2de96-de9b-4e6b-a356-2c032141040c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"genetically edited","passagePhrase":"editing a gene called FRUIT WEIGHT ... MULTIFLORA"},{"uid":"764c3832-add8-4e17-89c7-138a69a75758","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"the flavour of a tomato","passagePhrase":"quite tasty ... A little bit strong ... very aromatic"},{"uid":"01a01401-9951-4dd9-9cfb-8f13b4795d4c","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"a type of tomato that can resist","passagePhrase":"a strain resistant"},{"uid":"1a07e927-b581-4061-9c2b-df418678c325","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"infection","passagePhrase":"disease"},{"uid":"2529cfe1-2dcb-43ea-b525-cf40bbae7727","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"dangerous","passagePhrase":"which can devastate yields"},{"uid":"111c3cf3-4299-48ad-9664-03c18d7ae398","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"produced","passagePhrase":"created"},{"uid":"74203efb-06cf-456a-ac57-18d9f0bc57a8","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"not badly affected","passagePhrase":"salt tolerant"},{"uid":"653041fb-019a-4f56-b282-e7adc694bd83","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"rich in","passagePhrase":"has higher levels of"},{"uid":"0d8e1ccc-d26c-4196-b8d5-0322f8a3c664","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"the costs","passagePhrase":"would be expensive"},{"uid":"8e63fe81-e724-4ba8-9149-c4c5c9d0dec0","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"pay for a licence ... get regulatory approval"},{"uid":"878af82a-3eeb-41e7-bf1f-0ccb032c2971","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"unusual plants","passagePhrase":"obscure plants"},{"uid":"694582d9-46d2-4ea2-ae79-11ccb247bd71","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"may not be accepted","passagePhrase":"will be hard"},{"uid":"6af87b38-d9a6-4968-a944-9d1d4251f2cc","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"on a large scale","passagePhrase":"so popular"},{"uid":"6b33e6c4-a06a-49ba-823b-f04f1faaa244","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"could be useful as food sources","passagePhrase":"catapulted into the mainstream"},{"uid":"bdacde29-8890-472d-b784-be00f92c6786","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"certain plants","passagePhrase":"wild plants that are drought or heat tolerant"},{"uid":"1996b039-3478-46bb-bc5e-7f0ca73b9d0c","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"adapt to","passagePhrase":"thrive"},{"uid":"b41c7fc7-22a4-4853-ab0b-ccf67fb29f11","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"future environmental challenges","passagePhrase":"the planet warms"},{"uid":"318fa176-8357-4bb6-9d63-504e10cb7ed1","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"not advisable","passagePhrase":"didn’t want to"},{"uid":"12b946e4-02bc-4d50-89af-128736b39a09","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"be made public","passagePhrase":"reveal"},{"uid":"57e72cca-3beb-40f3-b4bd-cf2fbd23f499","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"modifying","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_276":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</p><h3><strong>Insight or evolution?</strong></h3><p><em>Two scientists consider the origins of discoveries and other innovative behavior</em></p><p>Scientific discovery is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c0a6cba1-1e6a-4d6a-ac6c-d4e706e1765b\" data-question=\"27\">popularly believed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to result from the sheer genius of such intellectual stars as naturalist Charles Darwin and theoretical physicist Albert Einstein. Our view of such unique contributions to science often disregards the person’s prior experience and the efforts of their lesser-known predecessors. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd850140-3bd2-4ff7-8802-1fb6e196e8c2\" data-question=\"37\">Conventional wisdom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> also places great weight on insight in promoting breakthrough scientific achievements, as if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8800c535-80d3-4cbc-9a88-bd522bde6707\" data-question=\"37\">ideas spontaneously pop into someone’s head<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> - fully formed and functional.</p><p>There may be some limited truth to this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7a1fb774-ca65-4068-88cc-52cd425d4bb5\" data-question=\"28\">view<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90315da1-7d56-4f2c-83d7-51e69be594fe\" data-question=\"28\">we believe that it largely misrepresents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> the real nature of scientific discovery, as well as that of creativity and innovation in many other realms of human endeavor.</p><p>Setting aside such greats as Darwin and Einstein - whose monumental contributions are duly celebrated - we suggest that innovation is more a process of trial and error, where two steps forward may sometimes come with one step back, as well as one or more steps to the right or left. This evolutionary view of human innovation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d2a356d-a318-44e6-9b9b-c831ea312097\" data-question=\"29\">undermines the notion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of creative genius and recognizes the cumulative nature of scientific progress.</p><p>Consider one unheralded scientist: John Nicholson, a mathematical physicist working in the 1910s who postulated the existence of‘proto-elements’ in outer space. By combining different numbers of weights of these proto-elements’ atoms, Nicholson could recover the weights of all the elements in the then-known periodic table. These successes are all the more noteworthy given the fact that Nicholson <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9878e10-bbeb-41fc-a83c-538fdd8a598c\" data-question=\"38\">was wrong about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> the presence of proto-elements: they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9878e10-bbeb-41fc-a83c-538fdd8a598c\" data-question=\"38\">do not actually exist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. Yet, amid his often fanciful theories and wild speculations, Nicholson also proposed a novel theory about the structure of atoms. Niels Bohr, the Nobel prize-winning father of modern atomic theory, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba005228-6e0d-44a1-9b4d-6fd538410bd1\" data-question=\"30\">jumped off from this<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> interesting idea to conceive his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1c533f9f-a138-4ff9-9ec7-b052deadb8e7\" data-question=\"30\">now-famous model of the atom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</p><p>What are we to make of this story? One might simply conclude that science is a collective and cumulative enterprise. That may be true, but there may be a deeper insight to be gleaned. We propose that science is constantly evolving, much as species of animals do. In biological systems, organisms may display new characteristics that result from random genetic mutations. In the same way, random, arbitrary or accidental mutations of ideas may help pave the way for advances in science. If mutations prove beneficial, then the animal or the scientific theory will continue to thrive and perhaps reproduce.</p><p>Support for this evolutionary view of behavioral innovation comes from many domains. Consider one example of an influential innovation in US horseracing. The so-called ‘acey-deucy’ stirrup placement, in which the rider’s foot in his left stirrup is placed as much as 25 centimeters lower than the right, is believed to confer important speed advantages when turning on oval tracks. It was developed by a relatively unknown jockey named Jackie Westrope. Had Westrope conducted methodical investigations or examined extensive film records in a shrewd plan to outrun his rivals? Had he foreseen the speed advantage that would be conferred by riding acey-deucy? No. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c0952d8-91a5-47af-b7f4-7ea111fa353c\" data-question=\"31\">He suffered a leg injury, which left him unable to fully bend his left knee<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. His modification just <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be335873-994c-4f16-8649-33b450543276\" data-question=\"31\">happened to coincide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> with enhanced left-hand turning performance. This led to the rapid and widespread adoption of riding acey-deucy by many riders, a racing style which continues in today’s thoroughbred racing.</p><p>Plenty of other stories show that fresh advances can arise from error, misadventure, and also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"124ec7a9-06ff-4745-a343-39a64f781144\" data-question=\"39\">pure serendipity - a happy accident<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. For example, in the early 1970s, two employees of the company 3M each had a problem: Spencer Silver had a product - a glue which was only slightly sticky - and no use for it, while his colleague Art Fry was trying to figure out how to affix temporary bookmarks in his hymn book without damaging its pages. The solution to both these problems was the invention of the brilliantly simple yet phenomenally successful Post-It note. Such examples give lie to the claim that ingenious, designing minds are responsible for human creativity and invention. Far more banal and mechanical forces may be at work; forces that are fundamentally connected to the laws of science.</p><p>The notions of insight, creativity and genius are often invoked, but they remain vague and of doubtful scientific utility, especially when one considers the diverse and enduring contributions of individuals such as Plato, Leonardo da Vinci, Shakespeare, Beethoven, Galileo, Newton, Kepler, Curie, Pasteur and Edison. These notions <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"553320e9-b700-42fb-9faa-9f8d3cdc99d2\" data-question=\"32\">merely label rather than explain the evolution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of human innovations. We need another approach, and there is a promising candidate.</p><p>The Law of Effect was advanced by psychologist Edward Thorndike in 1898, some 40 years after Charles Darwin published his groundbreaking work on biological evolution, On the Origin of Species. This simple law holds that organisms tend to repeat successful behaviors and to refrain from performing unsuccessful ones. Just like Darwin’s Law of Natural Selection, the Law of Effect involves an entirely mechanical <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35798eff-36ee-4a33-a580-8a5eaa3d343a\" data-question=\"34\">process of variation and selection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"655a1ad2-8f2d-4176-b033-f35083fc0794\" data-question=\"34\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ea2042a-dba6-4f41-96c5-1086818db696\" data-question=\"40\">without any end objective in sight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</p><p>Of course, the origin of human innovation demands much further study. In particular, the provenance of the raw material on which the Law of Effect operates is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f3e1d776-ff74-4182-80f1-e8fd0f280d35\" data-question=\"35\">not as clearly known as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> that of the genetic mutations on which the Law of Natural Selection operates. The generation of novel ideas and behaviors may not be entirely random, but constrained by prior successes and failures - of the current individual (such as Bohr) or of predecessors (such as Nicholson).</p><p>The time seems right for abandoning the naive notions of intelligent design and genius, and for scientifically exploring the true origins of creative behavior.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p style=\"text-align:start\">Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40246\" id=\"question-wrapper-40246\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The purpose of the first paragraph is to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. defend particular ideas.</li> <li>B. compare certain beliefs.</li> <li>C. disprove a widely held view.</li> <li>D. outline a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c0a6cba1-1e6a-4d6a-ac6c-d4e706e1765b\" data-question=\"27\">common assumption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40247\" id=\"question-wrapper-40247\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What are the writers doing in the second paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90315da1-7d56-4f2c-83d7-51e69be594fe\" data-question=\"28\">criticising<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7a1fb774-ca65-4068-88cc-52cd425d4bb5\" data-question=\"28\">opinion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></li> <li>B. justifying a standpoint</li> <li>C. explaining an approach</li> <li>D. supporting an argument</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40248\" id=\"question-wrapper-40248\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the third paragraph, what do the writers suggest about Darwin and Einstein? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9d2a356d-a318-44e6-9b9b-c831ea312097\" data-question=\"29\">represent an exception<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to a general rule.</li> <li>B. Their way of working has been misunderstood.</li> <li>C. They are an ideal which others should aspire to.</li> <li>D. Their achievements deserve greater recognition.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40249\" id=\"question-wrapper-40249\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> John Nicholson is an example of a person whose idea </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. established his reputation as an influential scientist.</li> <li>B. was only fully understood at a later point in history.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba005228-6e0d-44a1-9b4d-6fd538410bd1\" data-question=\"30\">laid the foundations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> for someone else’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1c533f9f-a138-4ff9-9ec7-b052deadb8e7\" data-question=\"30\">breakthrough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>D. initially met with scepticism from the scientific community.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40250\" id=\"question-wrapper-40250\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the key point of interest about the ‘acey-deucy’ stirrup placement? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8c0952d8-91a5-47af-b7f4-7ea111fa353c\" data-question=\"31\">simple reason<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> why it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be335873-994c-4f16-8649-33b450543276\" data-question=\"31\">was invented<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></li> <li>B. the enthusiasm with which it was adopted</li> <li>C. the research that went into its development</li> <li>D. the cleverness of the person who first used it</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</p><p>In boxes 32-36 on your answer sheet, write</p><ul><li>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</li><li>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</li><li>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40251\" id=\"question-wrapper-40251\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Acknowledging people such as Plato or da Vinci as geniuses will <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"553320e9-b700-42fb-9faa-9f8d3cdc99d2\" data-question=\"32\">help us understand the process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> by which great minds create new ideas. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40252\" id=\"question-wrapper-40252\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Law of Effect was discovered at a time when psychologists were seeking a scientific reason why creativity occurs. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40253\" id=\"question-wrapper-40253\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Law of Effect states that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"655a1ad2-8f2d-4176-b033-f35083fc0794\" data-question=\"34\">no planning is involved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35798eff-36ee-4a33-a580-8a5eaa3d343a\" data-question=\"34\">behaviour of organisms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40254\" id=\"question-wrapper-40254\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Law of Effect sets out <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f3e1d776-ff74-4182-80f1-e8fd0f280d35\" data-question=\"35\">clear explanations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> about the sources of new ideas and behaviours. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40255\" id=\"question-wrapper-40255\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Many scientists are now turning away from the notion of intelligent design and genius. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div style=\"text-align:start\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">Complete the summary using the list of words, A-G, below.</span></p><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><h4><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">The origins of creative behaviour</span></strong></h4><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd850140-3bd2-4ff7-8802-1fb6e196e8c2\" data-question=\"37\">traditional view<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> of scientific discovery is that breakthroughs happen when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8800c535-80d3-4cbc-9a88-bd522bde6707\" data-question=\"37\">a single great mind has sudden<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> 37...........................................Although this can occur, it is not often the case. Advances are more likely to be the result of a longer process.</span></p><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">In some cases, this process involves 38.........................................., such as Nicholson’s theory about proto-elements. In others, simple necessity may provoke innovation, as with Westrope’s decision to modify the position of his riding stirrups. There is also often an element of 39.........................................., for example, the coincidence of ideas that led to the invention of the Post-It note. With both the Law of Natural Selection and the Law of Effect, there <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ea2042a-dba6-4f41-96c5-1086818db696\" data-question=\"40\">may be no clear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> 40.......................................... involved, but merely a process of variation and selection.</span></p></div><div style=\"text-align:start\"><table><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">A</span></strong></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">invention</span></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">B</span></strong></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">goals</span></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">C</span></strong></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">compromise</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">D</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">G</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9878e10-bbeb-41fc-a83c-538fdd8a598c\" data-question=\"38\">mistakes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span></span></p><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">experiments</span></p></td><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">E</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"124ec7a9-06ff-4745-a343-39a64f781144\" data-question=\"39\">luck<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p></td><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">F</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">inspiration</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40256\" id=\"question-wrapper-40256\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40257\" id=\"question-wrapper-40257\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40258\" id=\"question-wrapper-40258\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40259\" id=\"question-wrapper-40259\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c0a6cba1-1e6a-4d6a-ac6c-d4e706e1765b","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"common assumption","passagePhrase":"popularly believed"},{"uid":"bd850140-3bd2-4ff7-8802-1fb6e196e8c2","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"traditional view","passagePhrase":"Conventional wisdom"},{"uid":"8800c535-80d3-4cbc-9a88-bd522bde6707","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"a single great mind has sudden","passagePhrase":"ideas spontaneously pop into someone’s head"},{"uid":"7a1fb774-ca65-4068-88cc-52cd425d4bb5","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"opinion","passagePhrase":"view"},{"uid":"90315da1-7d56-4f2c-83d7-51e69be594fe","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"criticising","passagePhrase":"we believe that it largely misrepresents"},{"uid":"9d2a356d-a318-44e6-9b9b-c831ea312097","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"represent an exception","passagePhrase":"undermines the notion"},{"uid":"f9878e10-bbeb-41fc-a83c-538fdd8a598c","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"mistakes","passagePhrase":"was wrong about ... do not actually exist"},{"uid":"ba005228-6e0d-44a1-9b4d-6fd538410bd1","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"laid the foundations","passagePhrase":"jumped off from this"},{"uid":"1c533f9f-a138-4ff9-9ec7-b052deadb8e7","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"breakthrough","passagePhrase":"now-famous model of the atom"},{"uid":"8c0952d8-91a5-47af-b7f4-7ea111fa353c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"simple reason","passagePhrase":"He suffered a leg injury, which left him unable to fully bend his left knee"},{"uid":"be335873-994c-4f16-8649-33b450543276","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"was invented","passagePhrase":"happened to coincide"},{"uid":"124ec7a9-06ff-4745-a343-39a64f781144","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"luck","passagePhrase":"pure serendipity - a happy accident"},{"uid":"35798eff-36ee-4a33-a580-8a5eaa3d343a","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"behaviour of organisms","passagePhrase":"process of variation and selection"},{"uid":"655a1ad2-8f2d-4176-b033-f35083fc0794","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"no planning is involved","passagePhrase":"without any end objective in sight"},{"uid":"6ea2042a-dba6-4f41-96c5-1086818db696","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"may be no clear","passagePhrase":"without any end objective in sight"}]},"reading_u2_277":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</p><h3><strong>The thylacine</strong></h3><p>The extinct thylacine, also known as the Tasmanian tiger, was a marsupial* that bore a superficial resemblance to a dog. Its most distinguishing feature was the 13-19 dark brown stripes over its back, beginning at the rear of the body and extending onto the tail. The thylacine’s average nose-to-tail length for adult males was 162.6 cm, compared to 153.7 cm for females.</p><p>The thylacine appeared to occupy most types of terrain except dense rainforest, with open eucalyptus forest thought to be its prime habitat. In terms of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a73393d-d763-447f-be02-2b9240d15d8c\" data-question=\"1\">feeding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac3ebddb-3d46-4a8a-a9f2-ffd9310387f2\" data-question=\"1\">exclusively<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> carnivorous, and its stomach was muscular with an ability to distend so that it could eat large amounts of food at one time, probably an adaptation to compensate for long periods when hunting was unsuccessful and food scarce. The thylacine was not a fast runner and probably caught its prey by exhausting it during a long pursuit. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02830f34-10cb-4ece-aed9-4f64696068e5\" data-question=\"2\">During long-distance chases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, thylacines were likely to have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26f7920a-3f32-4089-a7d2-648c719866b9\" data-question=\"2\">relied more on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> scent than any other sense. They emerged to hunt during the evening, night and early morning and tended to retreat to the hills and forest for shelter during the day. Despite the common name ‘tiger’, the thylacine had a shy, nervous temperament. Although mainly nocturnal, it was sighted moving during the day and some individuals were even recorded basking in the sun.</p><p>The thylacine had an extended breeding season from winter to spring, with indications that some breeding took place throughout the year. The thylacine, like all marsupials, was tiny and hairless when born. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e3873c0f-67b0-44df-90c5-428057f168c0\" data-question=\"3\">Newborns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> crawled into the pouch on the belly of their mother, and attached themselves to one of the four teats, remaining there for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be1723cc-b42f-4fc9-81ed-283641d3952f\" data-question=\"3\">up to three months<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. When old enough to leave the pouch, the young stayed in a lair such as a deep rocky cave, well-hidden nest or hollow log, whilst the mother hunted.</p><p>Approximately 4,000 years ago, the thylacine was widespread throughout New Guinea and most of mainland Australia, as well as the island of Tasmania. The most recent, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"def3061f-7813-4c25-b8d7-3f1d2e644dda\" data-question=\"4\">well-dated occurrence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> of a thylacine on the mainland is a carbon-dated fossil from Murray Cave in Western Australia, which is around 3,100 years old. Its extinction coincided closely with the arrival of wild dogs called dingoes in Australia and a similar predator in New Guinea. Dingoes never reached Tasmania, and most scientists see this as the main reason for the thylacine’s survival there.</p><p>The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1be97247-0af9-46ed-89f2-87e6d0adc812\" data-question=\"6\">dramatic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> decline of the thylacine in Tasmania, which began in the 1830s and continued for a century, is generally attributed to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70e781c9-9913-47ee-876e-a14292005e85\" data-question=\"6\">relentless efforts of sheep farmers and bounty hunters** with shotguns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. While this determined campaign undoubtedly played a large part, it is likely that various other factors also contributed to the decline and eventual extinction of the species. These include competition with wild dogs introduced by European settlers, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80b5cd10-6527-4d18-8940-d729c3f90a2d\" data-question=\"5\">loss<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of habitat along with the <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a2922bd8-58a8-4f82-9944-7756ce4164f2\" data-question=\"5\">disappearance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe95a798-eb4b-449d-ad22-be4170d5a459\" data-question=\"5\">prey species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, and a distemper-like disease which may also have affected the thylacine.</p><p>There was only <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1729c156-1209-4868-af75-af215d39ddc0\" data-question=\"7\">one successful attempt to breed a thylacine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in captivity, at Melbourne Zoo in 1899. This was despite the large numbers that went through some zoos, particularly London Zoo and Tasmania’s Hobart Zoo. The famous naturalist John Gould foresaw the thylacine’s demise when he published his Mammals of Australia between 1848 and 1863, writing, ‘The numbers of this singular animal will speedily diminish, extermination will have its full sway, and it will then, like the wolf of England and Scotland, be recorded as an animal of the past.’</p><p>However, there seems to have been <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d4af5025-3ccc-471f-be99-b4f3b7d54a52\" data-question=\"9\">little public pressure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to preserve the thylacine, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d4af5025-3ccc-471f-be99-b4f3b7d54a52\" data-question=\"9\">nor was much concern expressed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> by scientists at the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5fef4290-3fee-4059-a729-a0091f39bf12\" data-question=\"9\">decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of this species in the decades that followed. A notable exception was T.T. Flynn, Professor of Biology at the University of Tasmania. In 1914, he was sufficiently concerned about the scarcity of the thylacine to suggest that some should be captured and placed on a small island. But it was not until 1929, with the species <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"27dc0cf1-c880-4528-b2ea-04b75f7a9841\" data-question=\"11\">on the very edge of extinction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, that Tasmania’s Animals and Birds Protection Board passed a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4ec995f5-8644-462c-ab6c-3f72dd2996da\" data-question=\"11\">motion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> protecting thylacines only for the month of December, which was thought to be their prime breeding season. The last known wild thylacine to be killed was shot by a farmer in the north-east of Tasmania in 1930, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b3720e6-d1fb-4930-b688-475a4824fac5\" data-question=\"12\">leaving just captive specimens<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. Official protection of the species by the Tasmanian government was introduced in July 1936, 59 days before the last known individual died in Hobart Zoo on 7th September, 1936.</p><p>There have been numerous expeditions and searches for the thylacine over the years, none of which has produced definitive evidence that thylacines still exist. The species was declared extinct by the Tasmanian government in 1986.</p><p><em>*marsupial: a mammal, such as a kangaroo, whose young are born incompletely developed and are typically carried and suckled in a<br>pouch on the mother's belly</em></p><p><em>**bounty hunters: people who are paid a reward for killing a wild animal</em></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONL</strong>Y from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>The thylacine</strong></p><p>Appearance and behaviour</p><p>• looked rather like a dog</p><p>• had a series of stripes along its body and tail</p><p>• ate an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac3ebddb-3d46-4a8a-a9f2-ffd9310387f2\" data-question=\"1\">entirely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> 1..........................................<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8a73393d-d763-447f-be02-2b9240d15d8c\" data-question=\"1\">diet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span></p><p>• probably <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26f7920a-3f32-4089-a7d2-648c719866b9\" data-question=\"2\">depended mainly on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> 2..........................................when hunting</p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e3873c0f-67b0-44df-90c5-428057f168c0\" data-question=\"3\">young<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> spent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be1723cc-b42f-4fc9-81ed-283641d3952f\" data-question=\"3\">first months of life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> inside its mother’s 3..........................................</p><p>Decline and extinction</p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"def3061f-7813-4c25-b8d7-3f1d2e644dda\" data-question=\"4\">last evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> in mainland Australia is a 3,100-year-old 4..........................................</p><p>• probably went extinct in mainland Australia due to animals known as dingoes</p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80b5cd10-6527-4d18-8940-d729c3f90a2d\" data-question=\"5\">reduction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in 5..........................................and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a2922bd8-58a8-4f82-9944-7756ce4164f2\" data-question=\"5\">available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe95a798-eb4b-449d-ad22-be4170d5a459\" data-question=\"5\">sources of food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> were partly responsible for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"80b5cd10-6527-4d18-8940-d729c3f90a2d\" data-question=\"5\">decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in Tasmania</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40300\" id=\"question-wrapper-40300\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CARNIVOROUS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40301\" id=\"question-wrapper-40301\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SCENT</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40302\" id=\"question-wrapper-40302\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POUCH</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40303\" id=\"question-wrapper-40303\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOSSIL</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40304\" id=\"question-wrapper-40304\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HABITAT</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Questions 6-13</p><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet, write</p><ul><li><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</li><li><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</li><li><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40305\" id=\"question-wrapper-40305\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1be97247-0af9-46ed-89f2-87e6d0adc812\" data-question=\"6\">Significant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> numbers of thylacines <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"70e781c9-9913-47ee-876e-a14292005e85\" data-question=\"6\">were killed by humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> from the 1830s onwards. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40306\" id=\"question-wrapper-40306\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1729c156-1209-4868-af75-af215d39ddc0\" data-question=\"7\">Several thylacines were born<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in zoos during the late 1800s. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40307\" id=\"question-wrapper-40307\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> John Gould’s prediction about the thylacine surprised some biologists. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40308\" id=\"question-wrapper-40308\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the early 1900s, many scientists <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d4af5025-3ccc-471f-be99-b4f3b7d54a52\" data-question=\"9\">became worried<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> about the possible <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5fef4290-3fee-4059-a729-a0091f39bf12\" data-question=\"9\">extinction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of the thylacine. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40309\" id=\"question-wrapper-40309\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> T. T. Flynn’s proposal to rehome captive thylacines on an island proved to be impractical. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40310\" id=\"question-wrapper-40310\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There were <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"27dc0cf1-c880-4528-b2ea-04b75f7a9841\" data-question=\"11\">still reasonable numbers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of thylacines in existence when a piece of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4ec995f5-8644-462c-ab6c-3f72dd2996da\" data-question=\"11\">legislation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> protecting the species during their breeding season was passed. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40311\" id=\"question-wrapper-40311\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> From 1930 to 1936, the only known living thylacines were all <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b3720e6-d1fb-4930-b688-475a4824fac5\" data-question=\"12\">in captivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40312\" id=\"question-wrapper-40312\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Attempts to find living thylacines are now rarely made. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"8a73393d-d763-447f-be02-2b9240d15d8c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"diet","passagePhrase":"feeding"},{"uid":"ac3ebddb-3d46-4a8a-a9f2-ffd9310387f2","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"entirely","passagePhrase":"exclusively"},{"uid":"02830f34-10cb-4ece-aed9-4f64696068e5","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"During long-distance chases"},{"uid":"26f7920a-3f32-4089-a7d2-648c719866b9","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"depended mainly on","passagePhrase":"relied more on"},{"uid":"e3873c0f-67b0-44df-90c5-428057f168c0","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"young","passagePhrase":"Newborns"},{"uid":"be1723cc-b42f-4fc9-81ed-283641d3952f","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"first months of life","passagePhrase":"up to three months"},{"uid":"def3061f-7813-4c25-b8d7-3f1d2e644dda","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"last evidence","passagePhrase":"well-dated occurrence"},{"uid":"1be97247-0af9-46ed-89f2-87e6d0adc812","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"Significant","passagePhrase":"dramatic"},{"uid":"70e781c9-9913-47ee-876e-a14292005e85","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"were killed by humans","passagePhrase":"relentless efforts of sheep farmers and bounty hunters** with shotguns"},{"uid":"80b5cd10-6527-4d18-8940-d729c3f90a2d","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"reduction ... decline","passagePhrase":"loss"},{"uid":"fe95a798-eb4b-449d-ad22-be4170d5a459","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"sources of food","passagePhrase":"prey species"},{"uid":"5fef4290-3fee-4059-a729-a0091f39bf12","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"extinction","passagePhrase":"decline"},{"uid":"4ec995f5-8644-462c-ab6c-3f72dd2996da","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"legislation","passagePhrase":"motion"},{"uid":"1b3720e6-d1fb-4930-b688-475a4824fac5","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"in captivity","passagePhrase":"leaving just captive specimens"}]},"reading_u2_278":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</p><h3><strong>Palm oil</strong></h3><p><strong>A</strong></p><p>Palm oil is an edible oil derived from the fruit of the African oil palm tree, and is currently <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8bf32cc-e654-48b3-b06b-96bb9a257064\" data-question=\"16\">the most consumed vegetable oil in the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. It’s almost certainly in the soap we wash with in the morning, the sandwich we have for lunch, and the biscuits we snack on during the day. Why is palm oil so attractive for manufacturers? Primarily because its unique properties - such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5426a8f-dc97-433f-8c44-5cc54981469c\" data-question=\"23\">remaining<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> solid <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e1f668b-fe53-4e61-80bb-c9dc56cf2273\" data-question=\"23\">at room temperature<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> - make it an ideal ingredient for long-term preservation, allowing many packaged foods on supermarket shelves to have ‘best before’ dates of months, even years, into the future.</p><p><strong>B</strong></p><p>Many farmers have seized the opportunity to maximise the planting of oil palm trees. Between 1990 and 2012, the global land area devoted to growing oil palm trees grew from 6 to 17 million hectares, now accounting for around ten percent of total cropland in the entire world. From a mere two million tonnes of palm oil being produced annually globally 50 years ago, there are now around 60 million tonnes produced every single year, a figure looking <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f5b4ee73-81a0-4659-b9d0-f490e3a99587\" data-question=\"18\">likely to double or even triple<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> by the middle of the century.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>However, there are multiple reasons why conservationists cite the rapid spread of oil palm plantations as a major concern. There are countless news stories of deforestation, habitat destruction and dwindling species populations, all as a direct result of land clearing to establish oil palm tree monoculture on an industrial scale, particularly in Malaysia and Indonesia. Endangered <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88cec693-d8a1-4a44-a16c-cd846a9efaa7\" data-question=\"20\">species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> - <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"949709c6-0be4-4bee-8195-6441a93a7a8a\" data-question=\"24\">most famously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the Sumatran orangutan, but also rhinos, elephants, tigers, and numerous other fauna - have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd6fd2e8-acdc-4885-ab86-1488115dddaa\" data-question=\"20\">suffered from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> the unstoppable spread of oil palm plantations.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>‘Palm oil is surely one of the greatest threats to global biodiversity,’ declares Dr Farnon Ellwood of the University of the West of England, Bristol. ‘Palm oil is replacing rainforest, and rainforest is where all the species are. That’s a problem.’ This has led to some radical questions among environmentalists, such as whether consumers should try to boycott palm oil entirely.</p><p>Meanwhile Bhavani Shankar, Professor at London’s School of Oriental and African Studies, argues, ‘It’s easy to say that palm oil is the enemy and we should be against it. It makes for a more dramatic story, and it’s very intuitive. But given the complexity of the argument, I think a much more nuanced story is closer to the truth.’</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>One response to the boycott movement has been the argument for the vital role palm oil plays in lifting many millions of people in the developing world out of poverty. Is it desirable to have palm oil <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5747343-bb7b-405b-92b0-8e0933e975f6\" data-question=\"19\">boycotted, replaced, eliminated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> from the global supply chain, given how many low-income people in developing countries depend on it for their livelihoods? How best to strike a utilitarian balance between these competing factors has become a serious bone of contention.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>Even the deforestation argument isn’t as straightforward as it seems. Oil palm plantations produce at least four and potentially up to ten times more oil per hectare than soybean, rapeseed, sunflower or other competing oils. That immensely high yield - which is predominantly what makes it so profitable - is potentially also an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4cb77aed-337f-415e-8c97-f96e9d08343a\" data-question=\"14\">ecological benefit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. If ten times more palm oil can be produced from a patch of land than any competing oil, then ten times more land would need to be cleared in order to produce the same volume of oil from that competitor.</p><p>As for the question of carbon emissions, the issue really depends on what oil palm trees are replacing. Crops vary in the degree to which they sequester carbon - in other words, the amount of carbon they capture from the atmosphere and store within the plant. The more carbon a plant sequesters, the more it reduces the effect of climate change. As Shankar explains: ‘[Palm oil production] actually sequesters more carbon in some ways than other alternatives. [...] Of course, if you’re cutting down virgin forest it’s terrible - that’s what’s happening in Indonesia and Malaysia, it’s been allowed to get out of hand. But if it’s replacing rice, for example, it might actually sequester more carbon.’</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>The industry is now regulated by a group called the Roundtable on Sustainable Palm Oil (RSPO), consisting of palm growers, retailers, product manufacturers, and other interested parties. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc322096-27a4-42d7-860f-eb47e7f4e812\" data-question=\"21\">Over the past decade or so<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, an agreement <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4bf73a7-de1f-4795-8170-c70dd1c11bf3\" data-question=\"21\">has gradually been reached<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> regarding <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a540668-2e91-4880-82ff-00307d8d15de\" data-question=\"21\">standards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> that producers of palm oil have to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90a199da-4f59-4434-bc64-0fc5f2d99bdf\" data-question=\"15\">meet in order for their product to be regarded as officially 'sustainable'<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> The RSPO insists upon no virgin forest clearing, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98ac489d-78e6-494b-b8a4-963ecee7320d\" data-question=\"22\">transparency<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98ac489d-78e6-494b-b8a4-963ecee7320d\" data-question=\"22\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ad5ad347-0fb9-4233-a76d-9e02365df0fc\" data-question=\"25\">regular assessment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> of carbon stocks, among other criteria. Only once these requirements are fully satisfied is the oil allowed to be sold as certified sustainable palm oil (CSPO). Recent figures show that the RSPO now certifies around 12 million tonnes of palm oil annually, equivalent to roughly 21 percent of the world’s total palm oil production.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>There is even hope that oil palm plantations might not need to be such sterile monocultures, or ‘green deserts’, as Ellwood describes them. New research at Ellwood’s lab hints at <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af97215d-98d2-40ba-afbd-ed882a90f5c4\" data-question=\"17\">one plant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> which might make all the difference. The bird’s nest fern (Asplenium nidus) grows on trees in an epiphytic fashion (meaning it’s dependent on the tree only for support, not for nutrients), and is native to many tropical regions, where as a keystone species it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"964fc098-2cb2-4a3b-abe9-0ddd95386d4f\" data-question=\"17\">performs a vital ecological role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. Ellwood believes that reintroducing the bird’s nest fern into oil palm plantations could potentially allow these areas to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbb3be41-28cb-481b-83b6-bb8b8c980074\" data-question=\"26\">recover<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> their biodiversity, providing a home for all manner of species, from fungi and bacteria, to invertebrates such as insects, amphibians, reptiles and even mammals.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has eight sections, A-H.</p><p>Which section contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40313\" id=\"question-wrapper-40313\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of a range of potential <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4cb77aed-337f-415e-8c97-f96e9d08343a\" data-question=\"14\">environmental advantages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of oil palm tree cultivation </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40314\" id=\"question-wrapper-40314\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> description of an organisation which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"90a199da-4f59-4434-bc64-0fc5f2d99bdf\" data-question=\"15\">controls the environmental impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of palm oil production </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40315\" id=\"question-wrapper-40315\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8bf32cc-e654-48b3-b06b-96bb9a257064\" data-question=\"16\">widespread global use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of palm oil </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40316\" id=\"question-wrapper-40316\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af97215d-98d2-40ba-afbd-ed882a90f5c4\" data-question=\"17\">a particular species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> which could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"964fc098-2cb2-4a3b-abe9-0ddd95386d4f\" data-question=\"17\">benefit the ecosystem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of oil palm plantations </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40317\" id=\"question-wrapper-40317\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> figures illustrating the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f5b4ee73-81a0-4659-b9d0-f490e3a99587\" data-question=\"18\">rapid expansion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of the palm oil industry </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40318\" id=\"question-wrapper-40318\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an economic justification for not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5747343-bb7b-405b-92b0-8e0933e975f6\" data-question=\"19\">opposing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> the palm oil industry </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40319\" id=\"question-wrapper-40319\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88cec693-d8a1-4a44-a16c-cd846a9efaa7\" data-question=\"20\">creatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd6fd2e8-acdc-4885-ab86-1488115dddaa\" data-question=\"20\">badly affected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> by the establishment of oil palm plantations </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 21 and 22 on your answer sheet.</p><p>Which TWO statements are made about the Roundtable on Sustainable Palm Oil (RSPO)?</p><ul><li>A Its membership has grown steadily over the course of the last decade.</li><li>B It demands that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98ac489d-78e6-494b-b8a4-963ecee7320d\" data-question=\"22\">certified producers be open and honest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> about their practices.</li><li>C It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc322096-27a4-42d7-860f-eb47e7f4e812\" data-question=\"21\">took several years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> to establish <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a540668-2e91-4880-82ff-00307d8d15de\" data-question=\"21\">its set of criteria<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> for sustainable palm oil certification.</li><li>D Its regulations regarding sustainability are stricter than those governing other industries.</li><li>E It was formed at the request of environmentalists concerned about the loss of virgin forests.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40320\" id=\"question-wrapper-40320\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40321\" id=\"question-wrapper-40321\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the sentences below.</p><p>Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Write your answers in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40322\" id=\"question-wrapper-40322\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One advantage of palm oil for manufacturers is that it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5426a8f-dc97-433f-8c44-5cc54981469c\" data-question=\"23\">stays<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>..........................................even when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e1f668b-fe53-4e61-80bb-c9dc56cf2273\" data-question=\"23\">not refrigerated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOLID</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40323\" id=\"question-wrapper-40323\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The..........................................is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"949709c6-0be4-4bee-8195-6441a93a7a8a\" data-question=\"24\">the best known of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> the animals suffering habitat loss as a result of the spread of oil palm plantations. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(SUMATRAN) ORANG(-)UTAN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40324\" id=\"question-wrapper-40324\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> As one of its criteria for the certification of sustainable palm oil, the RSPO insists that growers check..........................................<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ad5ad347-0fb9-4233-a76d-9e02365df0fc\" data-question=\"25\">on a routine basis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CARBON STOCKS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40325\" id=\"question-wrapper-40325\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Ellwood and his researchers are looking into whether the bird’s nest fern could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbb3be41-28cb-481b-83b6-bb8b8c980074\" data-question=\"26\">restore<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>..........................................in areas where oil palm trees are grown. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BIODIVERSITY</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a8bf32cc-e654-48b3-b06b-96bb9a257064","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"widespread global use","passagePhrase":"the most consumed vegetable oil in the world"},{"uid":"d5426a8f-dc97-433f-8c44-5cc54981469c","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"stays","passagePhrase":"remaining"},{"uid":"5e1f668b-fe53-4e61-80bb-c9dc56cf2273","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"not refrigerated","passagePhrase":"at room temperature"},{"uid":"f5b4ee73-81a0-4659-b9d0-f490e3a99587","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"rapid expansion","passagePhrase":"likely to double or even triple"},{"uid":"88cec693-d8a1-4a44-a16c-cd846a9efaa7","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"creatures","passagePhrase":"species"},{"uid":"949709c6-0be4-4bee-8195-6441a93a7a8a","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"the best known of","passagePhrase":"most famously"},{"uid":"bd6fd2e8-acdc-4885-ab86-1488115dddaa","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"badly affected","passagePhrase":"suffered from"},{"uid":"b5747343-bb7b-405b-92b0-8e0933e975f6","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"opposing","passagePhrase":"boycotted, replaced, eliminated"},{"uid":"4cb77aed-337f-415e-8c97-f96e9d08343a","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"environmental advantages","passagePhrase":"ecological benefit"},{"uid":"dc322096-27a4-42d7-860f-eb47e7f4e812","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"took several years","passagePhrase":"Over the past decade or so"},{"uid":"b4bf73a7-de1f-4795-8170-c70dd1c11bf3","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"has gradually been reached"},{"uid":"3a540668-2e91-4880-82ff-00307d8d15de","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"its set of criteria","passagePhrase":"standards"},{"uid":"90a199da-4f59-4434-bc64-0fc5f2d99bdf","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"controls the environmental impact","passagePhrase":"meet in order for their product to be regarded as officially 'sustainable'"},{"uid":"98ac489d-78e6-494b-b8a4-963ecee7320d","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"certified producers be open and honest","passagePhrase":"transparency ... regular assessment"},{"uid":"ad5ad347-0fb9-4233-a76d-9e02365df0fc","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"on a routine basis","passagePhrase":"regular assessment"},{"uid":"af97215d-98d2-40ba-afbd-ed882a90f5c4","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"a particular species","passagePhrase":"one plant"},{"uid":"964fc098-2cb2-4a3b-abe9-0ddd95386d4f","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"benefit the ecosystem","passagePhrase":"performs a vital ecological role"},{"uid":"bbb3be41-28cb-481b-83b6-bb8b8c980074","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"restore","passagePhrase":"recover"}]},"reading_u2_279":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</p><p><strong>Building the Skyline: The Birth and Growth of Manhattan’s Skyscrapers</strong></p><p><em>Katharine L. Shester reviews a book by Jason Barr about the development of New York City</em></p><p>In Building the Skyline, Jason Barr takes the reader through a detailed history of New York City. The book <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de0b496b-51aa-4a01-81dd-373129d30870\" data-question=\"27\">combines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"568755cd-a421-4784-a50c-5f61ae52c653\" data-question=\"27\">geology, history, economics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, and a lot of data to explain why business clusters developed where they did and how the early decisions of workers and firms <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"730dbde2-ff9c-4572-afd2-842cd399e612\" data-question=\"27\">shaped the skyline we see today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Building the Skyline is organized into two distinct parts. The first is primarily historical and addresses New York’s settlement and growth from 1609 to 1900; the second deals primarily with the 20th century and is a compilation of chapters commenting on different aspects of New York’s urban development. The tone and organization of the book changes somewhat between the first and second parts, as the latter chapters incorporate aspects of Barr’s related research papers.</p><p>Barr begins <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"39b9eb7d-3c8f-4281-9682-ce70c8dad268\" data-question=\"32\">chapter one<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> by taking the reader on a ‘helicopter time-machine’ ride - <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8e59ec60-93eb-46d6-8cc9-9a7a6eedc5ca\" data-question=\"32\">giving a fascinating account<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of how the New York landscape <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1cddda8d-f270-4c2a-8f6f-3bc92a0860fc\" data-question=\"32\">in 1609<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> might have looked from the sky. He then moves on to a subterranean walking tour of the city, indicating the location of rock and water below the subsoil, before taking the reader back to the surface. His love of the city comes through as he describes various fun facts about the location of the New York residence of early 19th-century vice-president Aaron Burr as well as a number of legends about the city.</p><p>Chapters two and three take the reader up to the Civil War (1861-1865), with chapter two focusing on the early development of land and the implementation of a grid system in 1811. Chapter three focuses on land use before the Civil War. Both chapters are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eb0d1e1-a745-46bd-b3d8-e330ae8787b0\" data-question=\"33\">informative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> and well researched and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eb0d1e1-a745-46bd-b3d8-e330ae8787b0\" data-question=\"33\">set the stage for the economic analysis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> that comes later in the book. I would have liked Barr to expand upon his claim that existing tenements* prevented skyscrapers in certain neighborhoods because ‘likely no skyscraper developer was interested in performing the necessary “slum clearance’”. Later in the book, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f0265b2-2362-457c-8abf-1f030786844a\" data-question=\"28\">Barr makes the claim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> that the depth of bedrock** was not a limiting factor for developers, as foundation costs were a small fraction of the cost of development. At first glance, it is not obvious <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20387238-a685-42f4-a702-bd10e95924c7\" data-question=\"28\">why slum clearance would be limiting, while more expensive foundations would not<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</p><p>Chapter four focuses on immigration and the location of neighborhoods and tenements in the late 19th century. Barr identifies four primary immigrant enclaves and analyzes their locations in terms of the amenities available in the area. Most of these enclaves were located <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7dd85883-61eb-4364-811b-00b18a61ac45\" data-question=\"35\">on the least valuable land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, between the industries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd29e299-aff2-4c2b-a58b-db54657ba258\" data-question=\"35\">located on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the waterfront and the wealthy neighborhoods bordering Central Park.</p><p>Part two of the book begins with a discussion of the economics of skyscraper height. In chapter five, Barr distinguishes between engineering height, economic height, and developer height — where engineering height is the tallest building that can be safely made at a given time, economic height is the height that is most efficient from society’s point of view, and developer height is the actual height chosen by the developer, who is attempting to maximize return on investment.</p><p>Chapter five also has an interesting discussion of the technological advances that led to the construction of skyscrapers. For example, the introduction of iron and steel skeletal frames made thick, load-bearing walls unnecessary, expanding the usable square footage of buildings and increasing the use of windows and availability of natural light. Chapter six then presents data on building height throughout the 20th century and uses regression analysis to ‘predict’ building construction. While less technical than the research paper on which the chapter is based, it is probably <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4f179a18-2b6e-41a7-986b-ced9060f9c2c\" data-question=\"29\">more technical than would be preferred<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"576e07a7-2fa5-4b05-a65d-10a20b1ae05a\" data-question=\"29\">a general audience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</p><p>Chapter seven tackles the ‘bedrock myth’, the assumption that the absence of bedrock close to the surface between Downtown and Midtown New York is the reason for skyscrapers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"742f7830-b6bc-46e3-97f0-ffb0d9885b29\" data-question=\"36\">not being built<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> between the two urban centers. Rather, Barr argues that while deeper bedrock does increase foundation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb388815-372d-4f39-896f-997e2072a0ce\" data-question=\"37\">costs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, these costs were neither <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3774366c-a262-46f9-8d1e-3cce4ad85a1c\" data-question=\"37\">prohibitively high<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> nor were they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3774366c-a262-46f9-8d1e-3cce4ad85a1c\" data-question=\"37\">large<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> compared to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64f63499-01f8-4366-89ed-a576efc3736e\" data-question=\"38\">overall cost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of building a skyscraper. What I enjoyed the most about this chapter was Barr’s discussion of how foundations are actually built. He describes the use of caissons, which enable workers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f793a70-fb0a-4f11-85fa-de4bd0df25b4\" data-question=\"39\">dig down for considerable distances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, often below the water table, until they reach bedrock. Barr’s thorough technological history discusses not only how caissons work, but also the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ebed33e-a35b-4c71-93c0-fd48201bc9ac\" data-question=\"40\">dangers involved<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. While this chapter references empirical research papers, it is a relatively easy read.</p><p>Chapters eight and nine focus on the birth of Midtown and the building boom of the 1920s. Chapter eight contains lengthy discussions of urban economic theory that may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee2e6a1a-c098-458f-a661-c289bbb0eb5a\" data-question=\"30\">serve as a distraction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bded0de0-89d9-4a7d-942e-2ef0be184a3d\" data-question=\"30\">readers primarily interested in New York<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. However, they would be well-suited for undergraduates learning about the economics of cities. In the next chapter, Barr considers two of the primary explanations for the building boom of the 1920s — the first being exuberance, and the second being financing. He uses data to assess the viability of these two explanations and finds that supply and demand factors explain much of the development of the 1920s; though it enabled the boom, cheap credit was not, he argues, the primary cause.</p><p>In the final chapter (chapter 10), Barr discusses another of his empirical papers that estimates Manhattan land values from the mid-19th century to the present day. The data <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"092c671a-cbb4-4361-b3fe-c51b7944d3a7\" data-question=\"31\">work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> that went into these estimations is particularly impressive. Toward the end of the chapter, Barr assesses ‘whether skyscrapers are a cause or an effect of high land values’. He finds that changes in land values predict future building height, but the reverse is not true. The book ends with an epilogue, in which Barr discusses the impact of climate change on the city and makes policy suggestions for New York going forward.</p><p><em>*a tenement: a multi-occupancy building of any sort, but particularly a run-down apartment building or slum building</em></p><p><em>**bedrock: the solid, hard rock in the ground that lies under a loose layer of soil</em></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.</p><p> </p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40326\" id=\"question-wrapper-40326\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does Shester make about Barr’s book in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It gives a highly original explanation for urban development.</li> <li>B. Elements of Barr’s research papers are incorporated throughout the book.</li> <li>C. Other books that are available on the subject have taken a different approach.</li> <li>D. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de0b496b-51aa-4a01-81dd-373129d30870\" data-question=\"27\">covers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"568755cd-a421-4784-a50c-5f61ae52c653\" data-question=\"27\">a range of factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"730dbde2-ff9c-4572-afd2-842cd399e612\" data-question=\"27\">affected the development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of New York.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40327\" id=\"question-wrapper-40327\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> How does Shester respond to the information in the book about tenements? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. She describes the reasons for Barr’s interest.</li> <li>B. She indicates <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20387238-a685-42f4-a702-bd10e95924c7\" data-question=\"28\">a potential problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9f0265b2-2362-457c-8abf-1f030786844a\" data-question=\"28\">Barr’s analysis<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>C. She compares Barr’s conclusion with that of other writers.</li> <li>D. She provides details about the sources Barr used for his research.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40328\" id=\"question-wrapper-40328\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does Shester say about chapter six of the book? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It contains conflicting data.</li> <li>B. It focuses too much on possible trends.</li> <li>C. It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4f179a18-2b6e-41a7-986b-ced9060f9c2c\" data-question=\"29\">too specialised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"576e07a7-2fa5-4b05-a65d-10a20b1ae05a\" data-question=\"29\">most readers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>D. It draws on research that is out of date.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40329\" id=\"question-wrapper-40329\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does Shester suggest about the chapters focusing on the 1920s building boom? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The information should have been organised differently.</li> <li>B. More facts are needed about the way construction was financed.</li> <li>C. The explanation that is given for the building boom is unlikely.</li> <li>D. Some parts will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ee2e6a1a-c098-458f-a661-c289bbb0eb5a\" data-question=\"30\">have limited appeal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bded0de0-89d9-4a7d-942e-2ef0be184a3d\" data-question=\"30\">certain people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40330\" id=\"question-wrapper-40330\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What impresses Shester the most about the chapter on land values? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the broad time period that is covered</li> <li>B. the interesting questions that Barr asks</li> <li>C. the nature of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"092c671a-cbb4-4361-b3fe-c51b7944d3a7\" data-question=\"31\">research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> into the topic</li> <li>D. the recommendations Barr makes for the future</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet, write</p><ul><li>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</li><li>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</li><li>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40331\" id=\"question-wrapper-40331\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The description in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"39b9eb7d-3c8f-4281-9682-ce70c8dad268\" data-question=\"32\">the first chapter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of how New York probably looked from the air <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1cddda8d-f270-4c2a-8f6f-3bc92a0860fc\" data-question=\"32\">in the early 1600s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"8e59ec60-93eb-46d6-8cc9-9a7a6eedc5ca\" data-question=\"32\">lacks interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40332\" id=\"question-wrapper-40332\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Chapters two and three <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eb0d1e1-a745-46bd-b3d8-e330ae8787b0\" data-question=\"33\">prepare the reader well for material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> yet to come. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40333\" id=\"question-wrapper-40333\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The biggest problem for many nineteenth-century New York immigrant neighbourhoods was a lack of amenities. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40334\" id=\"question-wrapper-40334\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the nineteenth century, New York’s immigrant neighbourhoods tended <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd29e299-aff2-4c2b-a58b-db54657ba258\" data-question=\"35\">to concentrate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7dd85883-61eb-4364-811b-00b18a61ac45\" data-question=\"35\">around the harbour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div style=\"text-align:start\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">Write the correct letter, A-J, in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.</span></p><table><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">The bedrock myth</span></strong></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">In chapter seven, Barr indicates how the lack of bedrock close to the surface does</span></p><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">not explain why skyscrapers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"742f7830-b6bc-46e3-97f0-ffb0d9885b29\" data-question=\"36\">are absent from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> 36..........................................He points out that although the cost of foundations increases when bedrock is deep below the surface, this cannot be regarded as 37........................................., especially when compared to 38...........................................</span></p><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">A particularly enjoyable part of the chapter was Barr’s account of how foundations are built. He describes not only how 39......................................... are made possible by the use of caissons, but he also discusses their 40..........................................The chapter is well researched but relatively easy to understand.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p> </p><div style=\"text-align:start\"><table><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">A</span></strong></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">development plans</span></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">B</span></strong></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6f793a70-fb0a-4f11-85fa-de4bd0df25b4\" data-question=\"39\">deep excavations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span></span></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">C</span></strong></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">great distance</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">D</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3774366c-a262-46f9-8d1e-3cce4ad85a1c\" data-question=\"37\">excessive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb388815-372d-4f39-896f-997e2072a0ce\" data-question=\"37\">expense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></span></p></td><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">E</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">impossible tasks</span></p></td><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">F</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ebed33e-a35b-4c71-93c0-fd48201bc9ac\" data-question=\"40\">associated risks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">G</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">water level</span></p></td><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">H</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">specific areas</span></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">I</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64f63499-01f8-4366-89ed-a576efc3736e\" data-question=\"38\">total expenditure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">J</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">construction guidelines</span></p></td><td><p> </p></td><td><p> </p></td><td><p> </p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40335\" id=\"question-wrapper-40335\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40336\" id=\"question-wrapper-40336\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40337\" id=\"question-wrapper-40337\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40338\" id=\"question-wrapper-40338\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40339\" id=\"question-wrapper-40339\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"de0b496b-51aa-4a01-81dd-373129d30870","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"covers","passagePhrase":"combines"},{"uid":"568755cd-a421-4784-a50c-5f61ae52c653","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"a range of factors","passagePhrase":"geology, history, economics"},{"uid":"730dbde2-ff9c-4572-afd2-842cd399e612","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"affected the development","passagePhrase":"shaped the skyline we see today"},{"uid":"39b9eb7d-3c8f-4281-9682-ce70c8dad268","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"the first chapter","passagePhrase":"chapter one"},{"uid":"1cddda8d-f270-4c2a-8f6f-3bc92a0860fc","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"in the early 1600s","passagePhrase":"in 1609"},{"uid":"3eb0d1e1-a745-46bd-b3d8-e330ae8787b0","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"prepare the reader well for material","passagePhrase":"informative ... set the stage for the economic analysis"},{"uid":"9f0265b2-2362-457c-8abf-1f030786844a","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"Barr’s analysis","passagePhrase":"Barr makes the claim"},{"uid":"20387238-a685-42f4-a702-bd10e95924c7","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"a potential problem","passagePhrase":"why slum clearance would be limiting, while more expensive foundations would not"},{"uid":"fd29e299-aff2-4c2b-a58b-db54657ba258","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"to concentrate","passagePhrase":"located on"},{"uid":"4f179a18-2b6e-41a7-986b-ced9060f9c2c","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"too specialised","passagePhrase":"more technical than would be preferred"},{"uid":"576e07a7-2fa5-4b05-a65d-10a20b1ae05a","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"most readers","passagePhrase":"a general audience"},{"uid":"742f7830-b6bc-46e3-97f0-ffb0d9885b29","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"are absent from","passagePhrase":"not being built"},{"uid":"fb388815-372d-4f39-896f-997e2072a0ce","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"expense","passagePhrase":"costs"},{"uid":"3774366c-a262-46f9-8d1e-3cce4ad85a1c","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"excessive","passagePhrase":"prohibitively high ... large"},{"uid":"64f63499-01f8-4366-89ed-a576efc3736e","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"total expenditure","passagePhrase":"overall cost"},{"uid":"6f793a70-fb0a-4f11-85fa-de4bd0df25b4","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"deep excavations","passagePhrase":"dig down for considerable distances"},{"uid":"2ebed33e-a35b-4c71-93c0-fd48201bc9ac","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"associated risks","passagePhrase":"dangers involved"},{"uid":"ee2e6a1a-c098-458f-a661-c289bbb0eb5a","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"have limited appeal","passagePhrase":"serve as a distraction"},{"uid":"bded0de0-89d9-4a7d-942e-2ef0be184a3d","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"certain people","passagePhrase":"readers primarily interested in New York"},{"uid":"092c671a-cbb4-4361-b3fe-c51b7944d3a7","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"research","passagePhrase":"work"}]},"reading_u2_280":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</p><h3><strong>Bats to the rescue</strong></h3><p><em>How Madagascar’s bats are helping to save the rainforest</em></p><p>There are few places in the world where relations between agriculture and conservation are more strained. Madagascar’s forests are being converted to agricultural land at a rate of one percent every year. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9f485ff1-49c8-4440-b233-a83a91e68669\" data-question=\"1\">Much of this destruction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9f485ff1-49c8-4440-b233-a83a91e68669\" data-question=\"1\">fuelled by the cultivation of the country's main staple crop<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>: rice. And a key reason for this destruction is that insect pests are destroying vast quantities of what is grown by local subsistence farmers, leading them to clear forest to create new paddy fields. The result is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"95fde5c7-424d-4218-ada0-526e604ec47c\" data-question=\"2\">devastating habitat and biodiversity loss<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> on the island, but not all species are suffering. In fact, some of the island’s insectivorous bats are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"74fed0ce-003d-4798-91fd-2e53eec2fca7\" data-question=\"2\">currently thriving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> and this has important implications for farmers and conservationists alike.</p><p>Enter University of Cambridge zoologist Ricardo Rocha. He’s passionate about conservation, and bats. More specifically, he’s interested in how bats are responding to human activity and deforestation in particular. Rocha’s new study shows that several species of bats are giving Madagascar’s rice farmers a vital pest control service by feasting on plagues of insects. And this, he believes, can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24714183-df2d-4359-a451-1fe3a92b47f3\" data-question=\"4\">ease the financial pressure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> on farmers to turn forest into fields.</p><p>Bats comprise roughly one-fifth of all mammal species in Madagascar and thirty-six recorded bat species are native to the island, making it one of the most important regions for conservation of this animal group anywhere in the world.</p><p>Co-leading an international team of scientists, Rocha found that several species of indigenous bats are taking advantage of habitat modification to hunt insects swarming above the country’s rice fields. They include the Malagasy mouse-eared bat, Major’s long-fingered bat, the Malagasy white-bellied free-tailed bat and Peters’ wrinkle-lipped bat.</p><p>‘These winner species are providing a valuable free service to Madagascar as biological pest suppressors,’ says Rocha. ‘We found that six species of bat are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e181c6e-5a1e-4e06-b04b-63b59d08e26c\" data-question=\"6\">preying on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> rice pests, including the paddy swarming caterpillar and grass webworm. The damage which these insects cause puts the island’s farmers under huge financial pressure and that encourages deforestation.’</p><p>The study, now published in the journal Agriculture, Ecosystems and Environment, set out to investigate the feeding activity of insectivorous bats in the farmland bordering the Ranomafana National Park in the southeast of the country.</p><p>Rocha and his team used state-of-the-art ultrasonic recorders to record over a thousand bat ‘feeding buzzes’ (echolocation sequences used by bats to target their prey) at 54 sites, in order to identify the favourite feeding spots of the bats. They next used DNA barcoding techniques <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8a58edd-3689-4bbd-b068-eb5f71080ba4\" data-question=\"7\">to analyse<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> droppings collected from bats at the different sites.</p><p>The recordings revealed that bat activity over rice fields was much higher than it was in continuous forest - seven times higher over rice fields which were on flat ground, and sixteen times higher over fields on the sides of hills - leaving no doubt that the animals are preferentially foraging in these man-made ecosystems. The researchers suggest that the bats favour these fields because lack of water and nutrient run-off make these crops more susceptible to insect pest infestations. DNA analysis showed that all six species of bat had fed on economically important insect pests. While the findings indicated that rice farming benefits most from the bats, the scientists also found indications that the bats were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"246a5401-c273-4c37-8915-dffa25563c42\" data-question=\"8\">consuming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> pests of other crops, including the black twig borer (which infests coffee plants), the sugarcane cicada, the macadamia nut-borer, and the sober tabby (a pest of citrus fruits).</p><p>‘The effectiveness of bats as pest controllers has already been proven in the USA and Catalonia,’ said co-author James Kemp, from the University of Lisbon. ‘But our study is the first to show this happening in Madagascar, where the stakes for both farmers and conservationists are so high.’</p><p>Local people may have a further reason to be grateful to their bats. While the animal is often associated with spreading disease, Rocha and his team found evidence that Malagasy bats <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"49c26fef-ec21-4f57-8b7c-56221a59b186\" data-question=\"9\">feed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> not just on crop pests but also on mosquitoes - carriers of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3295291-96c4-44d5-9583-6dbb4df86096\" data-question=\"9\">malaria<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, Rift Valley fever virus and elephantiasis - as well as blackflies, which spread <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3295291-96c4-44d5-9583-6dbb4df86096\" data-question=\"9\">river blindness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</p><p>Rocha points out that the relationship is complicated. When food is scarce, bats <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7aecd00-0375-4701-9064-97fb25c684be\" data-question=\"10\">become a crucial source of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> protein for local people. Even the children will hunt them. And as well as roosting in trees, the bats sometimes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"07864769-bcd2-4fe6-98b6-66446c957943\" data-question=\"11\">roost in buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, but are not welcomed there because they make them unclean. At the same time, however, they are associated with sacred caves and the ancestors, so they can be viewed as beings between worlds, which makes them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82cbe1d1-9f3a-4f45-b70d-297350b793a9\" data-question=\"12\">very significant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in the culture of the people. And one potential problem is that while these bats are benefiting from farming, at the same time deforestation is reducing the places where they can roost, which could have long-term effects on their numbers. Rocha says, ‘With the right help, we hope that farmers can promote this mutually beneficial relationship by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de9d9aa4-6b4e-4ba4-b866-a7cc4829de96\" data-question=\"13\">installing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> bat houses.’</p><p>Rocha and his colleagues believe that maximising bat populations can help to boost crop yields and promote sustainable livelihoods. The team is now calling for further research to quantify this contribution. ‘I’m very optimistic,’ says Rocha. ‘If we give nature a hand, we can speed up the process of regeneration.’</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</p><p>In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write</p><ul><li><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information</li><li><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information</li><li><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40380\" id=\"question-wrapper-40380\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Many Madagascan forests are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9f485ff1-49c8-4440-b233-a83a91e68669\" data-question=\"1\">being destroyed by attacks from insects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40381\" id=\"question-wrapper-40381\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"95fde5c7-424d-4218-ada0-526e604ec47c\" data-question=\"2\">Loss of habitat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"74fed0ce-003d-4798-91fd-2e53eec2fca7\" data-question=\"2\">badly affected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> insectivorous bats in Madagascar. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40382\" id=\"question-wrapper-40382\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Ricardo Rocha has carried out studies of bats in different parts of the world. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40383\" id=\"question-wrapper-40383\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Habitat modification has resulted in indigenous bats in Madagascar <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24714183-df2d-4359-a451-1fe3a92b47f3\" data-question=\"4\">becoming useful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to farmers. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40384\" id=\"question-wrapper-40384\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Malagasy mouse-eared bat is more common than other indigenous bat species in Madagascar. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40385\" id=\"question-wrapper-40385\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Bats may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e181c6e-5a1e-4e06-b04b-63b59d08e26c\" data-question=\"6\">feed on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> paddy swarming caterpillars and grass webworms. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div style=\"text-align:start\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">Complete the table below.</span></p><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.</span></p></div><div style=\"text-align:start\"><table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"vertical-align:middle\"><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">The study carried out by Rocha’s team</span></strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">Aim</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">• to investigate the feeding habits of bats in farmland near the Ranomafana National Park</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">Method</span></strong></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">• ultrasonic recording to identify favourite feeding spots</span></p><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">• DNA <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8a58edd-3689-4bbd-b068-eb5f71080ba4\" data-question=\"7\">analysis of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> bat 7..........................................</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">Findings</span></strong></p></td><td style=\"vertical-align:bottom\"><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">• the bats</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- were most active in rice fields located on hills</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"246a5401-c273-4c37-8915-dffa25563c42\" data-question=\"8\">ate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> pests of rice, 8.........................................., sugarcane, nuts and fruit</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- prevent the spread of disease by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"49c26fef-ec21-4f57-8b7c-56221a59b186\" data-question=\"9\">eating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> 9..........................................and blackflies</span></p><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">• local attitudes to bats are mixed:</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- they provide food <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7aecd00-0375-4701-9064-97fb25c684be\" data-question=\"10\">rich in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> 10..........................................</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"07864769-bcd2-4fe6-98b6-66446c957943\" data-question=\"11\">the buildings where they roost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> become 11..........................................</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82cbe1d1-9f3a-4f45-b70d-297350b793a9\" data-question=\"12\">play an important role<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> in local 12..........................................</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong><span style=\"color:#000000\">Recommendation</span></strong></p></td><td><p><span style=\"color:#000000\">• farmers should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de9d9aa4-6b4e-4ba4-b866-a7cc4829de96\" data-question=\"13\">provide<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> special 13..........................................to support the bat population</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40386\" id=\"question-wrapper-40386\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DROPPINGS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40387\" id=\"question-wrapper-40387\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COFFEE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40388\" id=\"question-wrapper-40388\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MOSQUITOES</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40389\" id=\"question-wrapper-40389\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PROTEIN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40390\" id=\"question-wrapper-40390\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">UNCLEAN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40391\" id=\"question-wrapper-40391\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CULTURE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40392\" id=\"question-wrapper-40392\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HOUSES</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"95fde5c7-424d-4218-ada0-526e604ec47c","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"Loss of habitat","passagePhrase":"devastating habitat and biodiversity loss"},{"uid":"24714183-df2d-4359-a451-1fe3a92b47f3","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"becoming useful","passagePhrase":"ease the financial pressure"},{"uid":"0e181c6e-5a1e-4e06-b04b-63b59d08e26c","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"feed on","passagePhrase":"preying on"},{"uid":"a8a58edd-3689-4bbd-b068-eb5f71080ba4","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"analysis of","passagePhrase":"to analyse"},{"uid":"246a5401-c273-4c37-8915-dffa25563c42","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"ate","passagePhrase":"consuming"},{"uid":"49c26fef-ec21-4f57-8b7c-56221a59b186","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"eating","passagePhrase":"feed"},{"uid":"b3295291-96c4-44d5-9583-6dbb4df86096","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"malaria ... river blindness"},{"uid":"a7aecd00-0375-4701-9064-97fb25c684be","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"rich in","passagePhrase":"become a crucial source of"},{"uid":"07864769-bcd2-4fe6-98b6-66446c957943","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"the buildings where they roost","passagePhrase":"roost in buildings"},{"uid":"82cbe1d1-9f3a-4f45-b70d-297350b793a9","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"play an important role","passagePhrase":"very significant"},{"uid":"de9d9aa4-6b4e-4ba4-b866-a7cc4829de96","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"provide","passagePhrase":"installing"}]},"reading_u2_281":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</p><h3><strong>Does education fuel economic growth?</strong></h3><p><strong>A </strong></p><p>Over the last decade, a huge database about the lives of southwest German villagers between 1600 and 1900 has been compiled by a team led by Professor Sheilagh Ogilvie at Cambridge University’s Faculty of Economics. It includes court records, guild ledgers, parish registers, village censuses, tax lists and - the most recent addition - 9,000 handwritten inventories listing over a million personal possessions belonging to ordinary women and men across three centuries. Ogilvie, who discovered the inventories in the archives of two German communities 30 years ago, believes they may hold the answer to a conundrum that has long puzzled economists: the lack of evidence for a causal link between education and a country’s economic growth.</p><p><strong>B </strong></p><p>As Ogilvie explains, ‘Education helps us to work more productively, invent better technology, and earn more ... surely it must be critical for economic growth? But, if you look back through history, there’s no evidence that having a high literacy rate made a country industrialise earlier.’ Between 1600 and 1900, England had only mediocre literacy rates by European standards, yet its economy grew fast and it was the first country to industrialise. During this period, Germany and Scandinavia had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"44bee5df-af30-4a47-8c2e-a4c75fee813e\" data-question=\"23\">excellent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> literacy rates, but their economies grew slowly and they industrialised late. ‘Modern cross-country analyses have also struggled to find evidence that education <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbcef7d1-0267-4d5e-a803-82b9752573a0\" data-question=\"24\">causes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> economic growth, even though there is plenty of evidence that growth increases education,’ she adds.</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>In the handwritten inventories that Ogilvie is analysing are the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24a710b4-691a-43aa-b6e6-ddbec00fbfcb\" data-question=\"18\">belongings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of women and men at marriage, remarriage and death. From badger skins to Bibles, sewing machines to scarlet bodices - the villagers’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24a710b4-691a-43aa-b6e6-ddbec00fbfcb\" data-question=\"18\">entire worldly goods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> are included. Inventories of agricultural equipment and craft tools reveal economic activities; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd0e51d6-3263-48ce-8bef-98bb0a8dc9f2\" data-question=\"18\">ownership of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> books and education-related objects like pens and slates suggests how people learned. In addition, the tax lists included in the database record the value of farms, workshops, assets and debts; signatures and people’s estimates of their age indicate literacy and numeracy levels; and court records reveal obstacles (such as the activities of the guilds*) that stifled industry.</p><p>Previous studies usually had just one way of linking education with economic growth - the presence of schools and printing presses, perhaps, or school enrolment, or the ability to sign names. According to Ogilvie, the database provides multiple indicators for the same individuals, making it possible to analyse links between literacy, numeracy, wealth, and industriousness, for individual women and men over the long term.</p><p><strong>D</strong></p><p>Ogilvie and her team have been building the vast database of material possessions on top of their full demographic reconstruction of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a206e6b-7ffa-4127-a937-937a9e84507a\" data-question=\"19\">the people who lived in these two German communities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. ‘We can follow the same people - <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a206e6b-7ffa-4127-a937-937a9e84507a\" data-question=\"19\">and their descendants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> - across 300 years of educational and economic change,’ she says. Individual lives have unfolded before their eyes. Stories like that of the 24-year-olds Ana Regina and Magdalena Riethmullerin, who were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"318dbee0-13ee-4e11-bf94-691f899b5af5\" data-question=\"20\">chastised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in 1707 for reading books in church instead of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0201157c-05d8-4617-b340-f7b9c8ca4e8f\" data-question=\"20\">listening<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to the sermon. ‘This tells us they were continuing to develop their reading skills at least a decade after leaving school,’ explains Ogilvie. The database also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4710ac5e-d8ab-4d9e-9db1-09701e452b2f\" data-question=\"16\">reveals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> the case of Juliana Schweickherdt, a 50-year-old spinster living in the small Black Forest community of Wildberg, who was reprimanded in 1752 by the local weavers’ guild for ‘weaving cloth and combing wool, counter to the guild ordinance’. When <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"32a92ffa-c47e-4fd2-b946-8afb32cf8862\" data-question=\"16\">Juliana continued taking jobs reserved for male guild members<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, she was summoned before the guild court and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"806be330-bcdc-4a1e-a7f8-00b1239ed0ba\" data-question=\"21\">told to pay<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> a fine equivalent to one third of a servant’s annual wage. It was a small act of defiance by today’s standards, but it reflects a time when laws in Germany and elsewhere regulated people’s access to labour markets. The dominance of guilds not only prevented people from using their skills, but also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"714c08a3-e23d-4df9-a91e-341df38b72a8\" data-question=\"22\">held back<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> even the simplest industrial innovation.</p><p><strong>E</strong></p><p>The data-gathering phase of the project has been completed and now, according to Ogilvie, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15a903b4-720c-4802-b6c5-0da2bc1a99a0\" data-question=\"14\">it is time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15a903b4-720c-4802-b6c5-0da2bc1a99a0\" data-question=\"14\">to ask the big questions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>’. One way to look at whether education causes economic growth is to ‘hold wealth constant’. This involves following the lives of different people with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f177a695-6f40-48c0-85f8-d971965fbb2f\" data-question=\"14\">the same level of wealth over a period of time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. If wealth is constant, it is possible to discover whether education was, for example, linked to the cultivation of new crops, or to the adoption of industrial innovations like sewing machines. The team will also ask what aspect of education helped people engage more with productive and innovative activities. Was it, for instance, literacy, numeracy, book ownership, years of schooling? Was there a threshold level - a tipping point - that needed to be reached to affect economic performance?</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>Ogilvie hopes to start finding answers to these questions over the next few years. One thing is already clear, she says: the relationship between education and economic growth is far from straightforward. ‘German-speaking central Europe is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"39069740-eb73-4d35-a46b-c6fa2c282a6d\" data-question=\"17\">an excellent laboratory for testing theories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of economic growth,’ she explains. Between 1600 and 1900, literacy rates and book ownership were high and yet the region remained poor. It was also the case that local guilds and merchant associations were extremely powerful and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"00ade57e-208e-41a0-8683-447d414ab356\" data-question=\"26\">legislated against<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> anything that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2dd3886c-ba26-49d3-9f07-5125e3ea0dec\" data-question=\"26\">undermined their monopolies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. In villages throughout the region, guilds <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f114b774-9f50-4758-9c1e-85f8327f6cdf\" data-question=\"25\">blocked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"979618bd-a182-4854-916d-c40337f0d0ee\" data-question=\"25\">labour migration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f114b774-9f50-4758-9c1e-85f8327f6cdf\" data-question=\"25\">resisted changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> that might reduce their influence.</p><p>‘Early findings suggest that the potential benefits of education for the economy can be held back by other barriers, and this has implications for today,’ says Ogilvie. ‘Huge amounts are spent improving education in developing countries, but this spending can fail to deliver economic growth if restrictions block people - especially women and the poor - from using their education in economically productive ways. If economic institutions are poorly set up, for instance, education can’t lead to growth.’</p><p><em>*guild: an association of artisans or merchants which oversees the practice of their craft or trade in a particular area</em></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has six sections, A-F.</p><p>Which section contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40393\" id=\"question-wrapper-40393\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15a903b4-720c-4802-b6c5-0da2bc1a99a0\" data-question=\"14\">the need for research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> to focus on individuals with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f177a695-6f40-48c0-85f8-d971965fbb2f\" data-question=\"14\">a fairly consistent income<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40394\" id=\"question-wrapper-40394\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of the sources the database has been compiled from </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40395\" id=\"question-wrapper-40395\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4710ac5e-d8ab-4d9e-9db1-09701e452b2f\" data-question=\"16\">account<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of one individual’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"32a92ffa-c47e-4fd2-b946-8afb32cf8862\" data-question=\"16\">refusal to obey an order<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40396\" id=\"question-wrapper-40396\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to a region <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"39069740-eb73-4d35-a46b-c6fa2c282a6d\" data-question=\"17\">being particularly suited to research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> into the link between education and economic growth </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40397\" id=\"question-wrapper-40397\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24a710b4-691a-43aa-b6e6-ddbec00fbfcb\" data-question=\"18\">the items<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> included in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd0e51d6-3263-48ce-8bef-98bb0a8dc9f2\" data-question=\"18\">list of personal possessions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below.</p><p>Choose ONE WORD from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Write your answers in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>Demographic reconstruction of two German communities</strong></p><p>The database that Ogilvie and her team has compiled sheds light on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a206e6b-7ffa-4127-a937-937a9e84507a\" data-question=\"19\">lives of a range of individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, as well as those of their 19.........................................., over a 300-year period. For example, Ana Regina and Magdalena Riethmullerin were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"318dbee0-13ee-4e11-bf94-691f899b5af5\" data-question=\"20\">reprimanded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> for reading while they should have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0201157c-05d8-4617-b340-f7b9c8ca4e8f\" data-question=\"20\">paying attention to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> a 20...........................................</p><p>There was also Juliana Schweickherdt, who came to the notice of the weavers’ guild in the year 1752 for breaking guild rules. As a punishment, she was later <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"806be330-bcdc-4a1e-a7f8-00b1239ed0ba\" data-question=\"21\">given<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> a 21...........................................Cases like this illustrate how the guilds could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"714c08a3-e23d-4df9-a91e-341df38b72a8\" data-question=\"22\">prevent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> 22..........................................and stop skilled people from working.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40398\" id=\"question-wrapper-40398\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DESCENDANTS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40399\" id=\"question-wrapper-40399\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SERMON</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40400\" id=\"question-wrapper-40400\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FINE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40401\" id=\"question-wrapper-40401\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INNOVATION</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 23 and 24 on your answer sheet.</p><p>Which TWO of the following statements does the writer make about literacy rates in Section B?</p><ul><li>A Very little research has been done into the link between high literacy rates and improved earnings.</li><li>B Literacy rates in Germany between 1600 and 1900 were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"44bee5df-af30-4a47-8c2e-a4c75fee813e\" data-question=\"23\">very good<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</li><li>C There is strong evidence that high literacy rates in the modern world result in economic growth.</li><li>D England is a good example of how high literacy rates helped a country industrialise.</li><li>E Economic growth can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbcef7d1-0267-4d5e-a803-82b9752573a0\" data-question=\"24\">help to improve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> literacy rates.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40402\" id=\"question-wrapper-40402\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40403\" id=\"question-wrapper-40403\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 25 and 26 on your answer sheet.</p><p>Which TWO of the following statements does the writer make in Section F about guilds in German-speaking Central Europe between 1600 and 1900?</p><ul><li>A They helped young people to learn a skill.</li><li>B They were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f114b774-9f50-4758-9c1e-85f8327f6cdf\" data-question=\"25\">opposed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"979618bd-a182-4854-916d-c40337f0d0ee\" data-question=\"25\">people moving to an area for work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</li><li>C They kept better records than guilds in other parts of the world.</li><li>D They opposed practices that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2dd3886c-ba26-49d3-9f07-5125e3ea0dec\" data-question=\"26\">threatened their control over a trade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</li><li>E They predominantly consisted of wealthy merchants.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40404\" id=\"question-wrapper-40404\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40405\" id=\"question-wrapper-40405\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"44bee5df-af30-4a47-8c2e-a4c75fee813e","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"very good","passagePhrase":"excellent"},{"uid":"cbcef7d1-0267-4d5e-a803-82b9752573a0","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"help to improve","passagePhrase":"causes"},{"uid":"24a710b4-691a-43aa-b6e6-ddbec00fbfcb","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"the items","passagePhrase":"belongings ... entire worldly goods"},{"uid":"fd0e51d6-3263-48ce-8bef-98bb0a8dc9f2","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"list of personal possessions","passagePhrase":"ownership of"},{"uid":"0a206e6b-7ffa-4127-a937-937a9e84507a","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"lives of a range of individuals","passagePhrase":"the people who lived in these two German communities ... and their descendants"},{"uid":"318dbee0-13ee-4e11-bf94-691f899b5af5","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"reprimanded","passagePhrase":"chastised"},{"uid":"0201157c-05d8-4617-b340-f7b9c8ca4e8f","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"paying attention to","passagePhrase":"listening"},{"uid":"4710ac5e-d8ab-4d9e-9db1-09701e452b2f","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"account","passagePhrase":"reveals"},{"uid":"32a92ffa-c47e-4fd2-b946-8afb32cf8862","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"refusal to obey an order","passagePhrase":"Juliana continued taking jobs reserved for male guild members"},{"uid":"806be330-bcdc-4a1e-a7f8-00b1239ed0ba","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"given","passagePhrase":"told to pay"},{"uid":"714c08a3-e23d-4df9-a91e-341df38b72a8","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"prevent","passagePhrase":"held back"},{"uid":"15a903b4-720c-4802-b6c5-0da2bc1a99a0","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"the need for research","passagePhrase":"it is time ... to ask the big questions"},{"uid":"f177a695-6f40-48c0-85f8-d971965fbb2f","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"a fairly consistent income","passagePhrase":"the same level of wealth over a period of time"},{"uid":"39069740-eb73-4d35-a46b-c6fa2c282a6d","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"being particularly suited to research","passagePhrase":"an excellent laboratory for testing theories"},{"uid":"00ade57e-208e-41a0-8683-447d414ab356","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"legislated against"},{"uid":"2dd3886c-ba26-49d3-9f07-5125e3ea0dec","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"threatened their control over a trade","passagePhrase":"undermined their monopolies"},{"uid":"f114b774-9f50-4758-9c1e-85f8327f6cdf","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"opposed","passagePhrase":"blocked ... resisted changes"},{"uid":"979618bd-a182-4854-916d-c40337f0d0ee","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"people moving to an area for work","passagePhrase":"labour migration"}]},"reading_u2_282":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</p><h3><strong>Timur Gareyev - blindfold chess champion</strong></h3><p><strong>A </strong></p><p>Next month, a chess player named Timur Gareyev will take on nearly 50 opponents at once. But that is not the hard part. While his challengers will play the games as normal, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9318783e-f74e-44ee-869e-8a09dce699f1\" data-question=\"33\">Gareyev himself<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> will be blindfolded. Even by world record standards, it sets a high bar for human performance. The 28-year-old already stands out in the rarefied world of blindfold chess. He has a fondness for bright clothes and unusual hairstyles, and he gets his kicks from the adventure sport of BASE jumping. He has already proved himself a strong chess player, too. In a 10-hour chess marathon in 2013, Gareyev played 33 games in his head simultaneously. He won 29 and lost none. The skill has become his brand: he calls himself the Blindfold King.</p><p><strong>B </strong></p><p>But Gareyev’s prowess has drawn interest from beyond the chess-playing community. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"724f9e43-39f0-4643-a17c-7e3501158501\" data-question=\"30\">In the hope of understanding how<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> he and others like him can perform such mental feats, researchers at the University of California in Los Angeles (UCLA) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b333465-6d76-4ab7-87a5-5d82bcd1f0ef\" data-question=\"35\">called him in for tests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. They now have their first results. The ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2375830-ed80-47bb-984c-c906fda89a0f\" data-question=\"36\">play a game of chess with your eyes closed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> is not a far reach for most accomplished players,’ said Jesse Rissman, who runs a memory lab at UCLA. ‘But the thing that’s so remarkable about Timur and a few other individuals is the number of games they can keep active at once. To me it is simply astonishing.’</p><p><strong>C</strong></p><p>Gareyev learned to play chess in his native Uzbekistan when he was six years old. Tutored by his grandfather, he entered his first tournament aged eight and soon became obsessed with competitions. At 16, he was crowned Asia’s youngest ever chess grandmaster. He moved to the US soon after, and as a student helped his university win its first national chess championship. In 2013, Gareyev was ranked the third best chess player in the US.</p><p><strong>D </strong></p><p>To the uninitiated, blindfold chess seems to call for superhuman skill. But displays of the feat go back centuries. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"351c0f3d-7005-42cc-89e0-f7022d6512af\" data-question=\"27\">first recorded game<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in Europe was played in 13th-century Florence. In 1947, the Argentinian grandmaster Miguel Najdorf played 45 simultaneous games in his mind, winning 39 in the 24-hour session.</p><p><strong>E </strong></p><p>Accomplished players can develop the skill of playing blind even without realising it. The nature of the game is to run through possible moves in the mind to see how they play out. From this, regular players <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18ff73eb-0ff3-430b-9610-a4f3b0265c77\" data-question=\"28\">develop a memory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> for the patterns the pieces make, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18ff73eb-0ff3-430b-9610-a4f3b0265c77\" data-question=\"28\">the defences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18ff73eb-0ff3-430b-9610-a4f3b0265c77\" data-question=\"28\">attacks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. ‘You recreate it in your mind,’ said Gareyev. ‘A lot of players are capable of doing what I’m doing.’ The real mental challenge comes from playing multiple games at once in the head. Not only must the positions of each piece on every board be memorised, they must be recalled faithfully when needed, updated with each player’s moves, and then reliably stored again, so the brain can move on to the next board. First moves can be tough to remember because they are fairly uninteresting. But the ends of games are taxing too, as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"076a0f22-668a-44d4-87c3-9541f6078efb\" data-question=\"32\">exhaustion sets in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. When Gareyev is tired, his recall can get patchy. He sometimes makes moves based on only a fragmented memory of the pieces’ positions.</p><p><strong>F</strong></p><p>The scientists <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21fce85c-f742-4015-bb1f-b2e5ae3d420c\" data-question=\"37\">first had<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> Gareyev perform some standard memory tests. These assessed his ability to hold numbers, pictures and words in mind. One classic test measures how many numbers a person can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a6356c7-ce93-4b81-87c1-5f94e8454c64\" data-question=\"38\">repeat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a000d86f-4152-4fcd-b999-c4eebb8efb4f\" data-question=\"38\">forwards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23666141-5667-4539-81fa-45bd3a11949b\" data-question=\"38\">backwards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, soon after hearing them. Most people manage about seven. ‘He was not exceptional on any of these standard tests,’ said Rissman. ‘We <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d82e988-b0b7-4934-b3d5-0059b30a98a7\" data-question=\"29\">didn't find anything other than<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> playing chess that he seems to be supremely gifted at.’ But next came the brain scans. With Gareyev lying down in the machine, Rissman looked at how well connected the various regions of the chess player’s brain were. Though the results are tentative and as yet unpublished, the scans found <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f450bc60-5097-4732-a4b6-ced1aae84f65\" data-question=\"39\">much greater than average<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> communication between parts of Gareyev’s brain that make up what is called the frontoparietal <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7df25526-07e2-4765-91cb-34e1755afc4e\" data-question=\"39\">control network<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Of 63 people scanned alongside the chess player, only one or two scored more highly on the measure. ‘You use this network in almost any complex task. It helps you to allocate attention, keep rules in mind, and work out whether you should be responding or not,’ said Rissman.</p><p><strong>G</strong></p><p>It was not the only hint of something special in Gareyev’s brain. The scans also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af811552-36c9-4260-a1fa-b3c904c9838a\" data-question=\"40\">suggest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> that Gareyev’s visual network is more highly connected to other brain parts than usual. Initial results <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af811552-36c9-4260-a1fa-b3c904c9838a\" data-question=\"40\">suggest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> that the areas of his brain that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ee36f9f-dbbb-4387-85ec-8a9a6122074b\" data-question=\"40\">process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> visual <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f86aaebe-bb48-46f6-bd5e-8e792826da9e\" data-question=\"40\">images<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> - such as chess boards - may have stronger links to other brain regions, and so be more powerful than normal. While the analyses are not finalised yet, they may hold the first clues to Gareyev’s extraordinary ability.</p><p><strong>H</strong></p><p>For the world record attempt, Gareyev hopes to play 47 blindfold games at once in about 16 hours. He will need to win 80% to claim the title. ‘I don’t worry too much about the winning percentage, that’s never been an issue for me,’ he said. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03d91076-73b1-4669-ae4c-9b9649ce0404\" data-question=\"31\">The most important part<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> of blindfold chess for me is that I have found the one thing that I can fully dedicate myself to. I miss having an obsession.’</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 3 has eight paragraphs, A-H.</p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet.</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40406\" id=\"question-wrapper-40406\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"351c0f3d-7005-42cc-89e0-f7022d6512af\" data-question=\"27\">earlier examples<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of blindfold chess </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40407\" id=\"question-wrapper-40407\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an outline of what blindfold chess <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18ff73eb-0ff3-430b-9610-a4f3b0265c77\" data-question=\"28\">involves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40408\" id=\"question-wrapper-40408\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a claim that Gareyev’s skill is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d82e988-b0b7-4934-b3d5-0059b30a98a7\" data-question=\"29\">limited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to chess </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40409\" id=\"question-wrapper-40409\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"724f9e43-39f0-4643-a17c-7e3501158501\" data-question=\"30\">why<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> Gareyev’s skill is of interest to scientists </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40410\" id=\"question-wrapper-40410\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an outline of Gareyev’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03d91076-73b1-4669-ae4c-9b9649ce0404\" data-question=\"31\">priorities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40411\" id=\"question-wrapper-40411\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reason why the last part of a game may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"076a0f22-668a-44d4-87c3-9541f6078efb\" data-question=\"32\">difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?</p><p>In boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet, write</p><ul><li>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</li><li>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</li><li>NOT GIVEN if there is no information about this</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40412\" id=\"question-wrapper-40412\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the forthcoming games, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9318783e-f74e-44ee-869e-8a09dce699f1\" data-question=\"33\">all the participants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> will be blindfolded. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40413\" id=\"question-wrapper-40413\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Gareyev has won competitions in BASE jumping. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40414\" id=\"question-wrapper-40414\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> UCLA is the first university to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b333465-6d76-4ab7-87a5-5d82bcd1f0ef\" data-question=\"35\">carry out research into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> blindfold chess players. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40415\" id=\"question-wrapper-40415\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Good chess players are likely to be able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2375830-ed80-47bb-984c-c906fda89a0f\" data-question=\"36\">play blindfold chess<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below.</p><p>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Write your answers in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.</p><p>How the research was carried out The researchers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21fce85c-f742-4015-bb1f-b2e5ae3d420c\" data-question=\"37\">started<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> by testing Gareyev’s 37..........................................; for example, he was required to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a6356c7-ce93-4b81-87c1-5f94e8454c64\" data-question=\"38\">recall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> a string of 38..........................................<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a000d86f-4152-4fcd-b999-c4eebb8efb4f\" data-question=\"38\">in order<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> and also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23666141-5667-4539-81fa-45bd3a11949b\" data-question=\"38\">in reverse order<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. Although his performance was normal, scans showed an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f450bc60-5097-4732-a4b6-ced1aae84f65\" data-question=\"39\">unusual amount<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of 39..........................................within the areas of Gareyev’s brain that are concerned with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7df25526-07e2-4765-91cb-34e1755afc4e\" data-question=\"39\">directing attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. In addition, the scans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af811552-36c9-4260-a1fa-b3c904c9838a\" data-question=\"40\">raised the possibility<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> of unusual strength in the parts of his brain that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7ee36f9f-dbbb-4387-85ec-8a9a6122074b\" data-question=\"40\">deal with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> 40..........................................<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f86aaebe-bb48-46f6-bd5e-8e792826da9e\" data-question=\"40\">input<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40416\" id=\"question-wrapper-40416\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MEMORY</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40417\" id=\"question-wrapper-40417\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NUMBERS</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40418\" id=\"question-wrapper-40418\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COMMUNICATION</div> </div></div> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"40419\" id=\"question-wrapper-40419\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VISUAL</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"724f9e43-39f0-4643-a17c-7e3501158501","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"why","passagePhrase":"In the hope of understanding how"},{"uid":"9b333465-6d76-4ab7-87a5-5d82bcd1f0ef","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"carry out research into","passagePhrase":"called him in for tests"},{"uid":"d2375830-ed80-47bb-984c-c906fda89a0f","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"play blindfold chess","passagePhrase":"play a game of chess with your eyes closed"},{"uid":"351c0f3d-7005-42cc-89e0-f7022d6512af","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"earlier examples","passagePhrase":"first recorded game"},{"uid":"18ff73eb-0ff3-430b-9610-a4f3b0265c77","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"involves","passagePhrase":"develop a memory ... the defences ... attacks"},{"uid":"076a0f22-668a-44d4-87c3-9541f6078efb","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"difficult","passagePhrase":"exhaustion sets in"},{"uid":"21fce85c-f742-4015-bb1f-b2e5ae3d420c","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"started","passagePhrase":"first had"},{"uid":"9a6356c7-ce93-4b81-87c1-5f94e8454c64","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"recall","passagePhrase":"repeat"},{"uid":"a000d86f-4152-4fcd-b999-c4eebb8efb4f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"in order","passagePhrase":"forwards"},{"uid":"23666141-5667-4539-81fa-45bd3a11949b","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"in reverse order","passagePhrase":"backwards"},{"uid":"1d82e988-b0b7-4934-b3d5-0059b30a98a7","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"limited","passagePhrase":"didn't find anything other than"},{"uid":"f450bc60-5097-4732-a4b6-ced1aae84f65","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"unusual amount","passagePhrase":"much greater than average"},{"uid":"7df25526-07e2-4765-91cb-34e1755afc4e","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"directing attention","passagePhrase":"control network"},{"uid":"af811552-36c9-4260-a1fa-b3c904c9838a","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"raised the possibility","passagePhrase":"suggest ... suggest"},{"uid":"7ee36f9f-dbbb-4387-85ec-8a9a6122074b","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"deal with","passagePhrase":"process"},{"uid":"f86aaebe-bb48-46f6-bd5e-8e792826da9e","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"input","passagePhrase":"images"},{"uid":"03d91076-73b1-4669-ae4c-9b9649ce0404","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"priorities","passagePhrase":"The most important part"}]},"reading_u2_283":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.</p><h3><strong>Urban farming</strong></h3><p><em>In Paris, urban farmers are trying a soil-free approach to agriculture that uses less space and fewer resources. Could it help cities face the threats to our food supplies?</em></p><p>On top of a striking new exhibition hall in southern Paris, the world’s largest urban rooftop farm has started to bear fruit. Strawberries that are small, intensely flavoured and resplendently red sprout abundantly from large plastic tubes. Peer inside and you see the tubes are completely hollow, the roots of dozens of strawberry plants dangling down inside them. From identical vertical tubes nearby <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4499c1cd-fe46-4fbe-9741-2c35a18069dd\" data-question=\"1\">burst row upon row of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> lettuces; near those are aromatic herbs, such as basil, sage and peppermint. Opposite, in narrow, horizontal trays packed not with soil but with coconut fibre, grow cherry tomatoes, shiny aubergines and brightly coloured chards.</p><p>Pascal Hardy, an engineer and sustainable development consultant, began experimenting with vertical farming and aeroponic growing towers — as the soil-free plastic tubes are known — on his Paris apartment block roof five years ago. The urban rooftop space above the exhibition hall is somewhat bigger: 14,000 square metres and almost exactly the size of a couple of football pitches. Already, the team of young urban farmers who tend it have picked, in one day, 3,000 lettuces and 150 punnets of strawberries. When the remaining two thirds of the vast open area are in production, 20 staff will harvest up to 1,000 kg of perhaps 35 different varieties of fruit and vegetables, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"784aecd0-ac17-4b14-a0de-5e6ee24de985\" data-question=\"2\">every day<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. ‘We’re not ever, obviously, going to feed the whole city this way,’ cautions Hardy. ‘In the urban environment you’re working with very significant practical constraints, clearly, on what you can do and where. But if enough unused space can be developed like this, there’s no reason why you shouldn’t eventually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"85d9d03a-e327-4377-b5ee-2b37ee03d738\" data-question=\"3\">target<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"035063e1-8a84-4a89-a716-f9e1396a47d0\" data-question=\"3\">maybe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> between 5% and 10% of consumption.’</p><p>Perhaps most significantly, however, this is a real-life showcase for the work of Hardy’s flourishing urban agriculture consultancy, Agripolis, which is currently fielding enquiries from around the world to design, build and equip a new breed of soil-free inner-city farm. ‘The method’s advantages are many,’ he says. ‘First, I don’t much like the fact that most of the fruit and vegetables we eat have been treated with something like 17 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0305403-11f8-428a-b1c3-9c9ff90d9435\" data-question=\"4\">different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> pesticides, or that the intensive farming techniques that produced them are such huge generators of greenhouse gases. I don’t much like the fact, either, that they’ve travelled an average of 2,000 refrigerated kilometres to my plate, that their quality is so poor, because the varieties are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1827da1c-e835-48b6-ba21-daaea09f6730\" data-question=\"5\">selected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> for their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e484c310-e8e8-4978-a538-22391796c9e5\" data-question=\"5\">capacity to withstand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> such substantial journeys, or that 80% of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebdb1c1d-9de1-4b89-b123-618da1d7116d\" data-question=\"6\">the price I pay<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> goes to wholesalers and transport companies, not the producers.’</p><p>Produce grown using this soil-free method, on the other hand — which relies solely on a small quantity of water, enriched with organic nutrients, pumped around a closed circuit of pipes, towers and trays — is ‘produced up here, and sold locally, just down there. It barely travels at all,’ Hardy says. “You can select <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c57af445-33b8-4de1-88dd-5f5db4626754\" data-question=\"7\">crop varieties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> for their flavour, not their resistance to the transport and storage chain, and you can pick them when they’re really at their best, and not before.’ No soil is exhausted, and the water that gently showers the plants’ roots every 12 minutes is recycled, so the method uses 90% less water than a classic intensive farm for the same yield. Urban farming is not, of course, a new phenomenon. Inner-city agriculture is booming from Shanghai to Detroit and Tokyo to Bangkok. Strawberries <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"149e1144-1cc6-40d7-8820-a39a38074baf\" data-question=\"8\">are being grown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in disused <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"12e25e3c-4c15-4ba5-9f95-5b9cbfdda4d2\" data-question=\"8\">shipping containers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, mushrooms in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24c58b64-7c43-4189-bd2c-98b9376ba374\" data-question=\"8\">underground carparks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. Aeroponic farming, he says, is ‘virtuous’. The equipment weighs little, can be installed on almost any flat surface and is cheap to buy: roughly €100 to €150 per square metre. It is cheap to run, too, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e953117f-54a2-4788-b6b7-05cde38fa34d\" data-question=\"10\">consuming a tiny fraction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> of the electricity used by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a3f3f2a-ba8f-4f47-8052-18c2b6a6541d\" data-question=\"10\">some techniques<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</p><p>Produce <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc69c103-556d-4c16-b4db-ab1e57809953\" data-question=\"11\">grown this way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> typically sells at prices that, while generally higher than those of classic intensive agriculture, are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d992cddb-3db2-4df8-9db9-0b29795d1e51\" data-question=\"11\">lower<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0510b85e-1c73-4af0-a904-bace677207c9\" data-question=\"11\">soil-based<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> organic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2dae3f76-1e65-4290-b599-9cb555e150ca\" data-question=\"11\">growers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. There are limits to what farmers can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5360b348-92a1-495a-868f-54e8744fefaa\" data-question=\"12\">grow this way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, of course, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b29625ab-0110-4984-9937-4612074995f8\" data-question=\"12\">much of the produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> is suited to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7bc060da-a175-493b-ae65-df3c35c14529\" data-question=\"12\">the summer months<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. ‘Root vegetables we cannot do, at least not yet,’ he says. ‘Radishes are OK, but carrots, potatoes, that kind of thing — the roots are simply too long. Fruit trees are obviously not an option. And beans tend to take up a lot of space for not much return.’ Nevertheless, urban farming of the kind being practised in Paris is one part of a bigger and fast-changing picture that is bringing food production closer to our lives.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Questions 1-3</p><p>Complete the sentences below.</p><p>Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS ANDIOR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-3 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>Urban farming in Paris</strong></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145005\" id=\"question-wrapper-145005\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Vertical tubes are used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4499c1cd-fe46-4fbe-9741-2c35a18069dd\" data-question=\"1\">grow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> strawberries, ___________ and herbs. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LETTUCES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145006\" id=\"question-wrapper-145006\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There will eventually be a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"784aecd0-ac17-4b14-a0de-5e6ee24de985\" data-question=\"2\">daily<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> harvest of as much as __________ in weight of fruit and vegetables. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">1(,)000 KG/KILOGRAMS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145007\" id=\"question-wrapper-145007\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"035063e1-8a84-4a89-a716-f9e1396a47d0\" data-question=\"3\">possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> that the farm’s produce will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"85d9d03a-e327-4377-b5ee-2b37ee03d738\" data-question=\"3\">account for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> as much as 10% of the city’s __________ overall. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(FOOD) CONSUMPTION</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Questions 4—7</p><p>Complete the table below.</p><p>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 4-7 on your answer sheet.</p><div><table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border:none; width:602px\"><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"6\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:129px\"><p style=\"margin-left:1px; margin-right:119px; text-align:right\"><strong>Intensive farming versus aeroponic urban farming</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:129px\"> </td><td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:15px\"><p style=\"margin-left:1px; margin-right:55px\"><strong>Growth</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:15px\"><p style=\"margin-left:20px\"><strong>Selection</strong></p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:159px\"><p style=\"margin-left:1px\"><strong>Sale</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:129px\"><p style=\"margin-left:12px; margin-right:53px\"><strong>Intensive farming</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:15px\"><p>- <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0305403-11f8-428a-b1c3-9c9ff90d9435\" data-question=\"4\">wide range of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <strong>4 ________ </strong>used</p><p>- techniques pollute air</p></td><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:142px\"><p>- quality not good</p><p>- varieties of fruit and vegetables <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1827da1c-e835-48b6-ba21-daaea09f6730\" data-question=\"5\">chosen<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e484c310-e8e8-4978-a538-22391796c9e5\" data-question=\"5\">can survive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> long <strong>5 ________</strong></p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:15px\"><p><strong>- 6 ________</strong> receive very little of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ebdb1c1d-9de1-4b89-b123-618da1d7116d\" data-question=\"6\">overall income<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:129px\"><p style=\"margin-left:12px; margin-right:17px\"><strong>Aeroponic urban farming</strong></p></td><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:15px\"><p style=\"margin-left:1px\">- no soil used</p><p style=\"margin-left:1px\">- nutrients added to water, which is recycled</p></td><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:142px\"><p>- <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c57af445-33b8-4de1-88dd-5f5db4626754\" data-question=\"7\">produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> chosen because of its <strong>7________</strong></p></td><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top; width:15px\"> </td></tr></tbody></table></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145008\" id=\"question-wrapper-145008\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PESTICIDES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145009\" id=\"question-wrapper-145009\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">JOURNEYS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145010\" id=\"question-wrapper-145010\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PRODUCERS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145011\" id=\"question-wrapper-145011\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FLAVO(U)R</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet, write</p><p>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information<br>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information<br>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145012\" id=\"question-wrapper-145012\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Urban farming can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"149e1144-1cc6-40d7-8820-a39a38074baf\" data-question=\"8\">take place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> above or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"24c58b64-7c43-4189-bd2c-98b9376ba374\" data-question=\"8\">below ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145013\" id=\"question-wrapper-145013\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some of the equipment used in aeroponic farming can be made by hand. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145014\" id=\"question-wrapper-145014\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Urban farming <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e953117f-54a2-4788-b6b7-05cde38fa34d\" data-question=\"10\">relies more on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> electricity than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a3f3f2a-ba8f-4f47-8052-18c2b6a6541d\" data-question=\"10\">some other types of farming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145015\" id=\"question-wrapper-145015\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Fruit and vegetables <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc69c103-556d-4c16-b4db-ab1e57809953\" data-question=\"11\">grown on an aeroponic urban farm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d992cddb-3db2-4df8-9db9-0b29795d1e51\" data-question=\"11\">cheaper<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0510b85e-1c73-4af0-a904-bace677207c9\" data-question=\"11\">traditionally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> grown organic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2dae3f76-1e65-4290-b599-9cb555e150ca\" data-question=\"11\">produce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145016\" id=\"question-wrapper-145016\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b29625ab-0110-4984-9937-4612074995f8\" data-question=\"12\">Most<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> produce can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5360b348-92a1-495a-868f-54e8744fefaa\" data-question=\"12\">grown on an aeroponic urban farm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7bc060da-a175-493b-ae65-df3c35c14529\" data-question=\"12\">at any time of the year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145017\" id=\"question-wrapper-145017\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Beans take longer to grow on an urban farm than other vegetables. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"4499c1cd-fe46-4fbe-9741-2c35a18069dd","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"grow","passagePhrase":"burst row upon row of"},{"uid":"784aecd0-ac17-4b14-a0de-5e6ee24de985","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"daily","passagePhrase":"every day"},{"uid":"85d9d03a-e327-4377-b5ee-2b37ee03d738","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"account for","passagePhrase":"target"},{"uid":"035063e1-8a84-4a89-a716-f9e1396a47d0","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"possible","passagePhrase":"maybe"},{"uid":"a0305403-11f8-428a-b1c3-9c9ff90d9435","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"wide range of","passagePhrase":"different"},{"uid":"1827da1c-e835-48b6-ba21-daaea09f6730","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"chosen","passagePhrase":"selected"},{"uid":"e484c310-e8e8-4978-a538-22391796c9e5","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"can survive","passagePhrase":"capacity to withstand"},{"uid":"ebdb1c1d-9de1-4b89-b123-618da1d7116d","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"overall income","passagePhrase":"the price I pay"},{"uid":"c57af445-33b8-4de1-88dd-5f5db4626754","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"produce","passagePhrase":"crop varieties"},{"uid":"149e1144-1cc6-40d7-8820-a39a38074baf","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"take place","passagePhrase":"are being grown"},{"uid":"12e25e3c-4c15-4ba5-9f95-5b9cbfdda4d2","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"shipping containers"},{"uid":"24c58b64-7c43-4189-bd2c-98b9376ba374","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"below ground","passagePhrase":"underground carparks"},{"uid":"0a3f3f2a-ba8f-4f47-8052-18c2b6a6541d","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"some other types of farming","passagePhrase":"some techniques"},{"uid":"bc69c103-556d-4c16-b4db-ab1e57809953","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"grown on an aeroponic urban farm","passagePhrase":"grown this way"},{"uid":"d992cddb-3db2-4df8-9db9-0b29795d1e51","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"cheaper","passagePhrase":"lower"},{"uid":"0510b85e-1c73-4af0-a904-bace677207c9","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"traditionally","passagePhrase":"soil-based"},{"uid":"2dae3f76-1e65-4290-b599-9cb555e150ca","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"produce","passagePhrase":"growers"},{"uid":"5360b348-92a1-495a-868f-54e8744fefaa","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"grown on an aeroponic urban farm","passagePhrase":"grow this way"},{"uid":"b29625ab-0110-4984-9937-4612074995f8","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Most","passagePhrase":"much of the produce"}]},"reading_u2_284":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14—26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.</p><h3><strong>Forest management in Pennsylvania, USA</strong></h3><p><em>How managing low-quality wood (also known as low-use wood) for bioenergy can encourage sustainable forest management</em></p><p>A.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1dd4d5d-7dc7-4700-9d4e-2a148e4e58bd\" data-question=\"15\">A tree’s ‘value’<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d004058c-2656-4533-8a7e-fcec8e099370\" data-question=\"15\">depends on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> several <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa324747-835e-4455-8fa9-c71ab83462da\" data-question=\"15\">factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> including its species, size, form, condition, quality, function, and accessibility, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d004058c-2656-4533-8a7e-fcec8e099370\" data-question=\"15\">depends on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> the management goals for a given forest. The same tree can be valued very differently by each person who looks at it. A large, straight black cherry tree has high value as timber to be cut into logs or made into furniture, but for a landowner more interested in wildlife habitat, the real value of that stem (or trunk) may be the food it provides to animals. Likewise, if the tree suffers from black knot disease, its value for timber decreases, but to a woodworker interested in making bowls, it brings an opportunity for a unique and beautiful piece of art.</p><p>B. </p><p>In the past, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cc71c13-aebc-4856-85bf-2b667d55ca63\" data-question=\"14\">Pennsylvania landowners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3fb64d4-a0cd-4d59-87fa-4e893531bb4b\" data-question=\"14\">were solely interested in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0690dcaa-8d6f-4f2c-95da-160e7894a3ee\" data-question=\"14\">the value of their trees as high-quality timber<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. The norm was to remove the stems of highest quality and leave behind <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e201f7f-60e0-4f83-833c-f85559344a64\" data-question=\"18\">poorly formed trees that were not as well suited to the site where they grew<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. This practice, called ‘high-grading’, has left a legacy of ‘low-use wood’ in the forests. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b539102a-fb96-4ce4-a3cb-da68b747e164\" data-question=\"18\">Some people even call these ‘junk trees’<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, and they are abundant in Pennsylvania. These trees have lower economic value for traditional timber markets, compete for growth with higher-value trees, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b0270b4-6104-4cc9-8f40-82c2fb54118a\" data-question=\"14\">shade out desirable regeneration and decrease the health of a stand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>’ leaving it more vulnerable to poor weather and disease. Management that specifically targets low-use wood can help landowners manage these forest health issues, and wood energy markets help promote this.</p><p>C.</p><p>Wood energy markets can accept less expensive wood material of lower quality than would be suitable for traditional timber markets. Most wood used for energy in Pennsylvania is used to produce heat or electricity through combustion. Many schools and hospitals use wood boiler systems to heat and power their facilities, many homes are primarily heated with wood, and some coal plants incorporate wood into their coal streams to produce electricity. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88d23505-a1c2-46b4-ba6b-2affa692ff57\" data-question=\"16\">Wood can also be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> gasified for electrical generation and can even be made into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ea99b6e-4b84-49a5-b247-93eef6f84efe\" data-question=\"16\">liquid fuels like ethanol and gasoline for lorries and cars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. All these products are made primarily from low-use wood. Several tree- and plant-cutting approaches, which could greatly improve the long-term quality of a forest, focus strongly or solely on the use of wood for those markets.</p><p>D.</p><p>One such approach is called a Timber Stand Improvement (TSI) Cut. In a TSI Cut, really poor-quality tree and plant material is cut down to allow more space, light, and other resources to the highest-valued stems that remain. Removing invasive plants might be another primary goal of a TSI Cut. The stems that are left behind might then grow in size and develop more foliage and larger crowns or tops that produce more coverage for wildlife; they have a better chance to regenerate in a less crowded environment. TSI Cuts can be tailored to one farmer’s specific management goals for his or her land.</p><p>E.</p><p>Another approach that might yield a high amount of low-use wood is a Salvage Cut. With the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0b4a469-b775-492e-972c-4a8f5401f584\" data-question=\"17\">many pests and pathogens visiting forests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> including hemlock wooly adelgid, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"edb7b0f7-e9f8-49e7-8076-169fafe69d1c\" data-question=\"17\">Asian longhorned beetle, emerald ash borer, and gypsy moth, to name just a few<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, it is important to remember that those working in the forests can help ease these issues through cutting procedures. These types of cut <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"efd6ebf4-3cf2-4d45-bf35-d5da9d080b94\" data-question=\"19\">reduce the number of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba0d13ca-0f9c-4d4e-8ecb-2cf501eed9c9\" data-question=\"19\">sick trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and seek to manage the future spread of a pest problem. They leave vigorous trees that have stayed healthy enough to survive the outbreak.</p><p>F.</p><p>A Shelterwood Cut, which only takes place in a mature forest that has already been thinned several times, involves removing all the mature trees when other seedlings have become established. This then allows the forester to decide which tree species are regenerated. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6de51036-d8fa-427e-9358-08a23ddbfdea\" data-question=\"21\">leaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> a young forest where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56193ec4-251e-4b70-b529-ab20c2b728ae\" data-question=\"21\">all trees are at a similar point in their growth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. It can also be used to develop a two-tier forest so that there are two harvests and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68fc6cec-5518-401e-9424-50bc62b31855\" data-question=\"20\">the money that comes in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2094e6df-8caa-4aee-8bbd-52dd10c0cd98\" data-question=\"20\">spread out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb0f0518-c4fe-467c-8e64-34cf681511c2\" data-question=\"20\">over a decade or more<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</p><p>G.</p><p>Thinnings and dense and dead wood <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"766664b6-d8df-43d1-bbe6-87b16d370b80\" data-question=\"22\">removal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> for fire <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbe272c0-6a41-44f4-a871-530daf547cb2\" data-question=\"22\">prevention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> also center on the production of low-use wood. However, it is important to remember that some retention of what many would classify as low-use wood is very important. The tops of trees that have been cut down should be left on the site so that their nutrients <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b83dd27f-4818-4969-885d-ab7e2861e506\" data-question=\"23\">cycle back into the soil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. In addition, trees with many cavities <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"439e10b1-e188-4bcf-a167-22877b0253bc\" data-question=\"24\">are extremely important habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d677af96-0fb9-4a3a-a240-84f9ff66f65e\" data-question=\"24\">insect predators like woodpeckers, bats and small mammals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. They help control problem insects and increase the health and resilience of the forest. It is also important to remember that not all small trees are low-use. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b744837-f4c7-4285-8316-96be75c51f68\" data-question=\"25\">For example<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, many species like hawthorn <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e4a77e5-ef14-4bd4-999c-74071ed8532e\" data-question=\"25\">provide food for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> wildlife. Finally, rare species of trees in a forest should also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fed7561d-14b5-46ec-9f48-1aa47ec8ed0c\" data-question=\"26\">stay behind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> as they add to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ad9e76f0-c86c-4f7b-bfb2-df6c8af46bd9\" data-question=\"26\">its structural diversity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-G.<br>Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.</p><p><em>NB You may use any letter more than once.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145018\" id=\"question-wrapper-145018\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b0270b4-6104-4cc9-8f40-82c2fb54118a\" data-question=\"14\">bad outcomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> for a forest when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cc71c13-aebc-4856-85bf-2b667d55ca63\" data-question=\"14\">people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3fb64d4-a0cd-4d59-87fa-4e893531bb4b\" data-question=\"14\">focus only on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0690dcaa-8d6f-4f2c-95da-160e7894a3ee\" data-question=\"14\">its financial reward<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145019\" id=\"question-wrapper-145019\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa324747-835e-4455-8fa9-c71ab83462da\" data-question=\"15\">aspects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of any tree that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d004058c-2656-4533-8a7e-fcec8e099370\" data-question=\"15\">contribute to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b1dd4d5d-7dc7-4700-9d4e-2a148e4e58bd\" data-question=\"15\">its worth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145020\" id=\"question-wrapper-145020\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88d23505-a1c2-46b4-ba6b-2affa692ff57\" data-question=\"16\">potential use of wood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8ea99b6e-4b84-49a5-b247-93eef6f84efe\" data-question=\"16\">help run vehicles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145021\" id=\"question-wrapper-145021\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"edb7b0f7-e9f8-49e7-8076-169fafe69d1c\" data-question=\"17\">examples of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0b4a469-b775-492e-972c-4a8f5401f584\" data-question=\"17\">insects that attack trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145022\" id=\"question-wrapper-145022\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b539102a-fb96-4ce4-a3cb-da68b747e164\" data-question=\"18\">alternative name<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e201f7f-60e0-4f83-833c-f85559344a64\" data-question=\"18\">trees that produce low-use wood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following purposes (Questions 19-21) and the list of timber cuts below.</p><p>Match each purpose with the correct timber cut, A, B or C.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A, B or C, in boxes 19-21 on your answer sheet.</p><p><em>NB You may use any letter more than once.</em></p><p><strong>List of Timber Cuts</strong></p><ul><li>A. a TSI Cut</li><li>B. a Salvage Cut</li><li>C. a Shelterwood Cut</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145023\" id=\"question-wrapper-145023\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"efd6ebf4-3cf2-4d45-bf35-d5da9d080b94\" data-question=\"19\">remove<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba0d13ca-0f9c-4d4e-8ecb-2cf501eed9c9\" data-question=\"19\">trees that are diseased<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145024\" id=\"question-wrapper-145024\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2094e6df-8caa-4aee-8bbd-52dd10c0cd98\" data-question=\"20\">generate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68fc6cec-5518-401e-9424-50bc62b31855\" data-question=\"20\">income<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb0f0518-c4fe-467c-8e64-34cf681511c2\" data-question=\"20\">across a number of years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145025\" id=\"question-wrapper-145025\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6de51036-d8fa-427e-9358-08a23ddbfdea\" data-question=\"21\">create<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> a forest whose <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56193ec4-251e-4b70-b529-ab20c2b728ae\" data-question=\"21\">trees are close in age<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p><p>Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145026\" id=\"question-wrapper-145026\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some dead wood is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"766664b6-d8df-43d1-bbe6-87b16d370b80\" data-question=\"22\">removed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbe272c0-6a41-44f4-a871-530daf547cb2\" data-question=\"22\">avoid the possibility of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> ............ . </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FIRE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145027\" id=\"question-wrapper-145027\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The.......... from the tops of cut trees can help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b83dd27f-4818-4969-885d-ab7e2861e506\" data-question=\"23\">improve soil quality<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NUTRIENTS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145028\" id=\"question-wrapper-145028\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some damaged trees should be left, as their ............ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"439e10b1-e188-4bcf-a167-22877b0253bc\" data-question=\"24\">provide habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d677af96-0fb9-4a3a-a240-84f9ff66f65e\" data-question=\"24\">a range of creatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CAVITIES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145029\" id=\"question-wrapper-145029\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some trees that are small, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b744837-f4c7-4285-8316-96be75c51f68\" data-question=\"25\">such as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> ............ , are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0e4a77e5-ef14-4bd4-999c-74071ed8532e\" data-question=\"25\">a source of food for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b58c1a57-fa84-4a2d-8358-396a86440821\" data-question=\"25\">animals and insects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HAWTHORN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145030\" id=\"question-wrapper-145030\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Any trees that are ............ should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fed7561d-14b5-46ec-9f48-1aa47ec8ed0c\" data-question=\"26\">be left to grow<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, as they add to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ad9e76f0-c86c-4f7b-bfb2-df6c8af46bd9\" data-question=\"26\">the variety of species in the forest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RARE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"b1dd4d5d-7dc7-4700-9d4e-2a148e4e58bd","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"its worth","passagePhrase":"A tree’s ‘value’"},{"uid":"d004058c-2656-4533-8a7e-fcec8e099370","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"contribute to","passagePhrase":"depends on ... depends on"},{"uid":"fa324747-835e-4455-8fa9-c71ab83462da","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"aspects","passagePhrase":"factors"},{"uid":"5cc71c13-aebc-4856-85bf-2b667d55ca63","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"people","passagePhrase":"Pennsylvania landowners"},{"uid":"f3fb64d4-a0cd-4d59-87fa-4e893531bb4b","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"focus only on","passagePhrase":"were solely interested in"},{"uid":"0690dcaa-8d6f-4f2c-95da-160e7894a3ee","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"its financial reward","passagePhrase":"the value of their trees as high-quality timber"},{"uid":"8e201f7f-60e0-4f83-833c-f85559344a64","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"trees that produce low-use wood","passagePhrase":"poorly formed trees that were not as well suited to the site where they grew"},{"uid":"b539102a-fb96-4ce4-a3cb-da68b747e164","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"alternative name","passagePhrase":"Some people even call these ‘junk trees’"},{"uid":"9b0270b4-6104-4cc9-8f40-82c2fb54118a","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"bad outcomes","passagePhrase":"shade out desirable regeneration and decrease the health of a stand"},{"uid":"88d23505-a1c2-46b4-ba6b-2affa692ff57","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"potential use of wood","passagePhrase":"Wood can also be"},{"uid":"8ea99b6e-4b84-49a5-b247-93eef6f84efe","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"help run vehicles","passagePhrase":"liquid fuels like ethanol and gasoline for lorries and cars"},{"uid":"f0b4a469-b775-492e-972c-4a8f5401f584","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"insects that attack trees","passagePhrase":"many pests and pathogens visiting forests"},{"uid":"edb7b0f7-e9f8-49e7-8076-169fafe69d1c","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"examples of","passagePhrase":"Asian longhorned beetle, emerald ash borer, and gypsy moth, to name just a few"},{"uid":"efd6ebf4-3cf2-4d45-bf35-d5da9d080b94","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"remove","passagePhrase":"reduce the number of"},{"uid":"ba0d13ca-0f9c-4d4e-8ecb-2cf501eed9c9","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"trees that are diseased","passagePhrase":"sick trees"},{"uid":"6de51036-d8fa-427e-9358-08a23ddbfdea","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"create","passagePhrase":"leaves"},{"uid":"56193ec4-251e-4b70-b529-ab20c2b728ae","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"trees are close in age","passagePhrase":"all trees are at a similar point in their growth"},{"uid":"68fc6cec-5518-401e-9424-50bc62b31855","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"income","passagePhrase":"the money that comes in"},{"uid":"2094e6df-8caa-4aee-8bbd-52dd10c0cd98","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"generate","passagePhrase":"spread out"},{"uid":"cb0f0518-c4fe-467c-8e64-34cf681511c2","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"across a number of years","passagePhrase":"over a decade or more"},{"uid":"766664b6-d8df-43d1-bbe6-87b16d370b80","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"removed","passagePhrase":"removal"},{"uid":"cbe272c0-6a41-44f4-a871-530daf547cb2","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"avoid the possibility of","passagePhrase":"prevention"},{"uid":"b83dd27f-4818-4969-885d-ab7e2861e506","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"improve soil quality","passagePhrase":"cycle back into the soil"},{"uid":"439e10b1-e188-4bcf-a167-22877b0253bc","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"provide habitats","passagePhrase":"are extremely important habitats"},{"uid":"d677af96-0fb9-4a3a-a240-84f9ff66f65e","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"a range of creatures","passagePhrase":"insect predators like woodpeckers, bats and small mammals"},{"uid":"1b744837-f4c7-4285-8316-96be75c51f68","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"such as","passagePhrase":"For example"},{"uid":"0e4a77e5-ef14-4bd4-999c-74071ed8532e","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"a source of food for","passagePhrase":"provide food for"},{"uid":"fed7561d-14b5-46ec-9f48-1aa47ec8ed0c","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"be left to grow","passagePhrase":"stay behind"},{"uid":"ad9e76f0-c86c-4f7b-bfb2-df6c8af46bd9","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"the variety of species in the forest","passagePhrase":"its structural diversity"},{"uid":"b58c1a57-fa84-4a2d-8358-396a86440821","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"animals and insects","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_285":{"leftHtml":"<div><p>You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27—40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.</p><h3><strong>Conquering Earth’s space junk problem</strong></h3><p><em>Satellites, rocket shards and collision debris are creating major traffic risks in orbit around the planet. Researchers are working to reduce these threats</em></p><p>A.</p><p>Last year, commercial companies, military and civil departments and amateurs sent more than 400 satellites into orbit, over four times the yearly average in the previous decade. Numbers could rise even more sharply if leading space companies follow through on plans to deploy hundreds to thousands of large constellations of satellites to space in the next few years.</p><p>All that traffic can lead to disaster. Ten years ago, a US commercial Iridium satellite <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69ae9ebd-4c5e-4981-bc16-f7475ddf0b1b\" data-question=\"29\">smashed into<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> an inactive Russian communications satellite called Cosmos-2251, creating thousands of new pieces of space shrapnel that now threaten other satellites in low Earth orbit — the zone stretching up to 2,000 kilometres in altitude. Altogether, there are roughly 20,000 human-made objects in orbit, from working satellites to small rocket pieces. And satellite operators can’t steer away from every potential crash, because each move consumes time and fuel that could otherwise be used for the spacecraft’s main job.</p><p>B.</p><p>Concern about space junk goes back to the beginning of the satellite era, but the number of objects in orbit is rising so rapidly that researchers are investigating new ways of attacking the problem. Several teams <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"092e4b58-144b-45aa-ac6c-91b4ec972ac5\" data-question=\"31\">are trying to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> improve methods for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0748fbf7-c090-4910-831a-1bc761912c1c\" data-question=\"31\">assessing what is in orbit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, so that satellite operators can work more efficiently in ever-more-crowded space. Some researchers are now starting to compile a massive data set that includes the best possible information on where everything is in orbit. Others are developing taxonomies of space debris — working on measuring properties such as the shape and size of an object, so that satellite operators know how much to worry about what’s coming their way.</p><p>The alternative, many say, is unthinkable. Just a few uncontrolled space crashes could generate enough debris to set off a runaway cascade of fragments, rendering near Earth space unusable. ‘If we go on like this, we will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a3ef871-0bd3-49fc-bb2f-ceb552fdfda6\" data-question=\"40\">reach a point of no return<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>,’ says Carolin Frueh, an astrodynamical researcher at Purdue University in West Lafayette, Indiana.</p><p>C.</p><p>Even as our ability to monitor space objects increases, so too does the total number of items in orbit. That means companies, governments and other players in space are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"052ba98b-1206-4e5f-ad8c-af91e01c740e\" data-question=\"27\">collaborating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in new ways to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fafe6e4b-4be8-45b2-99d5-789f61b89d50\" data-question=\"27\">avoid a shared threat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. International groups such as the Inter-Agency Space Debris Coordination Committee <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe6e0fc5-9805-4f78-a99c-b4b13ba1ba52\" data-question=\"32\">have developed guidelines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> on space sustainability. Those include inactivating satellites <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88b1d8d9-a9d1-44c3-b64c-f9fcdd5c5ec9\" data-question=\"33\">at the end of their useful life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48e2e851-70f7-4069-b8b9-b34495b6e3c3\" data-question=\"34\">venting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> pressurised materials or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac63bd84-8068-40fe-bb1b-aaa11fd43d4e\" data-question=\"33\">leftover<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> fuel that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7201053-e37d-4e2d-bdb7-4b6f10cf2b2a\" data-question=\"34\">might<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> lead to explosions. The intergovernmental groups also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"63a375d2-656d-4653-86bd-b0d9ae8c38d9\" data-question=\"38\">advise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> lowering satellites deep enough into the atmosphere that they will burn up or disintegrate within 25 years. But so far, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"07e14983-28d4-4dd3-ad7e-71a89699ea5a\" data-question=\"38\">only about half of all missions have abided by this 25-year goal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, says Holger Krag, head of the European Space Agency's space-debris office in Darmstadt, Germany. Operators of the planned large constellations of satellites say they will be responsible stewards in their enterprises in space, but Krag worries that problems could increase, despite their best intentions. ‘What happens to those that fail or go bankrupt?’ he asks. ‘They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd4b16ef-e015-4011-b86c-5cbb761f87c0\" data-question=\"35\">are probably not going to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> spend money to remove their satellites from space.’</p><p>D.</p><p>In theory, given the vastness of space, satellite operators should have plenty of room for all these missions to fly safely without ever nearing another object. So some scientists are tackling the problem of space junk by trying to find out where all the debris is to a high degree of precision. That would alleviate the need for many of the unnecessary manoeuvres that are carried out to avoid potential collisions. ‘If you knew <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3029e18-87b8-49f7-a3db-d3679f903043\" data-question=\"36\">precisely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e193dfe4-0fea-4ec1-8217-9a2067ff1a94\" data-question=\"36\">where everything was<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, you would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3537d979-04e7-442e-bde4-40102af04c94\" data-question=\"36\">almost never have a problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>,’ says Marlon Sorge, a space-debris specialist at the Aerospace Corporation in El Segundo, California.</p><p>E.</p><p>The field is called <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9fc7730b-7470-4d8a-bb6f-7cc63d3167ce\" data-question=\"30\">space traffic management<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, because it’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0e432b2-8b09-4d30-aacf-57e6a4440b1e\" data-question=\"30\">similar to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8527f52-7bf2-4540-913a-172dd1a00274\" data-question=\"30\">managing traffic on the roads or in the air<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Think about a busy day at an airport, says Moriba Jah, an astrodynamicist at the University of Texas at Austin: planes line up in the sky, landing and taking off close to one another in a carefully choreographed routine. Air-traffic controllers know the location of the planes down to one metre in accuracy. The same can’t be said for space debris. Not all objects in orbit are known, and even those included in databases are not tracked consistently.</p><p>F.</p><p>An additional problem is that there is no authoritative catalogue that accurately lists the orbits of all known space debris. Jah illustrates this with a web-based database that he has developed. It draws on several sources, such as catalogues maintained by the US and Russian governments, to visualise where objects are in space. When he types in an identifier for a particular space object, the database draws a purple line to designate its orbit. Only this doesn’t quite work for a number of objects, such as a Russian rocket body designated in the database as object number 32280. When Jah enters that number, the database draws two purple lines: the US and Russian sources contain <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c20f051f-d81e-45d5-8833-3cf3effe00dc\" data-question=\"39\">two completely different orbits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> for the same object. Jah says that it is almost impossible to tell which is correct, unless a third source of information made it possible to cross-correlate.</p><p>Jah describes himself as a space environmentalist: ‘I want to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab11db91-9a57-4c60-8718-bb97a0fb08e8\" data-question=\"28\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5cfc5c6-f393-4544-acca-93b7eba7869c\" data-question=\"28\">make space a place that is safe to operate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, that is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6874b215-6442-42c3-af56-0081f137842e\" data-question=\"37\">free<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7b95488-5c1b-4a03-95bf-d5023b1c716e\" data-question=\"37\">useful for generations to come<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.’ Until that happens, he argues, the space community will continue devolving into a tragedy in which all spaceflight operators are polluting a common resource.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 3 has six sections, A-F.<br>Which section contains the following information?<br>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145031\" id=\"question-wrapper-145031\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"052ba98b-1206-4e5f-ad8c-af91e01c740e\" data-question=\"27\">cooperation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> that takes place to try and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fafe6e4b-4be8-45b2-99d5-789f61b89d50\" data-question=\"27\">minimise risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145032\" id=\"question-wrapper-145032\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab11db91-9a57-4c60-8718-bb97a0fb08e8\" data-question=\"28\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b5cfc5c6-f393-4544-acca-93b7eba7869c\" data-question=\"28\">a person’s aims<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145033\" id=\"question-wrapper-145033\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a description of a major <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69ae9ebd-4c5e-4981-bc16-f7475ddf0b1b\" data-question=\"29\">collision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that occurred in space </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145034\" id=\"question-wrapper-145034\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d0e432b2-8b09-4d30-aacf-57e6a4440b1e\" data-question=\"30\">comparison<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9fc7730b-7470-4d8a-bb6f-7cc63d3167ce\" data-question=\"30\">tracking objects in space<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> and the efficiency of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8527f52-7bf2-4540-913a-172dd1a00274\" data-question=\"30\">transportation system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145035\" id=\"question-wrapper-145035\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"092e4b58-144b-45aa-ac6c-91b4ec972ac5\" data-question=\"31\">efforts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0748fbf7-c090-4910-831a-1bc761912c1c\" data-question=\"31\">classify space junk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below.<br>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>The Inter-Agency Space Debris Coordination Committee</strong></p><p>The committee <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe6e0fc5-9805-4f78-a99c-b4b13ba1ba52\" data-question=\"32\">gives advice on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> how the 32 _______ of space can be achieved. The committee advises that when satellites <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88b1d8d9-a9d1-44c3-b64c-f9fcdd5c5ec9\" data-question=\"33\">are no longer active<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, any <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac63bd84-8068-40fe-bb1b-aaa11fd43d4e\" data-question=\"33\">unused<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> 33 _______ or pressurised material that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d7201053-e37d-4e2d-bdb7-4b6f10cf2b2a\" data-question=\"34\">could<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> cause 34 _______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48e2e851-70f7-4069-b8b9-b34495b6e3c3\" data-question=\"34\">should be removed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</p><p>Although operators of large satellite constellations accept that they have obligations as stewards of space, Holger Krag points out that the operators that become 35 _______ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd4b16ef-e015-4011-b86c-5cbb761f87c0\" data-question=\"35\">are unlikely to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> prioritise removing their satellites from space.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145036\" id=\"question-wrapper-145036\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SUSTAINABILITY</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145037\" id=\"question-wrapper-145037\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FUEL</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145038\" id=\"question-wrapper-145038\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EXPLOSIONS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145039\" id=\"question-wrapper-145039\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BANKRUPT</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following statements (Questions 36-40) and the list of people below.</p><p>Match each statement with the correct person, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.</p><p><em>NB You may use any letter more than once.</em></p><p> </p><p><strong>List of People</strong></p><ul><li>A. Carolin Frueh</li><li>B. Holger Krag</li><li>C. Marlon Sorge</li><li>D. Moriba Jah</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145040\" id=\"question-wrapper-145040\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Knowing the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3029e18-87b8-49f7-a3db-d3679f903043\" data-question=\"36\">exact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e193dfe4-0fea-4ec1-8217-9a2067ff1a94\" data-question=\"36\">location of space junk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> would help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3537d979-04e7-442e-bde4-40102af04c94\" data-question=\"36\">prevent any possible danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145041\" id=\"question-wrapper-145041\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Space should be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6874b215-6442-42c3-af56-0081f137842e\" data-question=\"37\">available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to everyone and should be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c7b95488-5c1b-4a03-95bf-d5023b1c716e\" data-question=\"37\">preserved for the future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145042\" id=\"question-wrapper-145042\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"63a375d2-656d-4653-86bd-b0d9ae8c38d9\" data-question=\"38\">recommendation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> regarding satellites <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"07e14983-28d4-4dd3-ad7e-71a89699ea5a\" data-question=\"38\">is widely ignored<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145043\" id=\"question-wrapper-145043\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c20f051f-d81e-45d5-8833-3cf3effe00dc\" data-question=\"39\">conflicting information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> about where some satellites are in space. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145044\" id=\"question-wrapper-145044\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is a risk we will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a3ef871-0bd3-49fc-bb2f-ceb552fdfda6\" data-question=\"40\">not be able to undo the damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> that occurs in space. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"69ae9ebd-4c5e-4981-bc16-f7475ddf0b1b","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"collision","passagePhrase":"smashed into"},{"uid":"092e4b58-144b-45aa-ac6c-91b4ec972ac5","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"efforts","passagePhrase":"are trying to"},{"uid":"0748fbf7-c090-4910-831a-1bc761912c1c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"classify space junk","passagePhrase":"assessing what is in orbit"},{"uid":"0a3ef871-0bd3-49fc-bb2f-ceb552fdfda6","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"not be able to undo the damage","passagePhrase":"reach a point of no return"},{"uid":"052ba98b-1206-4e5f-ad8c-af91e01c740e","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"cooperation","passagePhrase":"collaborating"},{"uid":"fafe6e4b-4be8-45b2-99d5-789f61b89d50","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"minimise risk","passagePhrase":"avoid a shared threat"},{"uid":"fe6e0fc5-9805-4f78-a99c-b4b13ba1ba52","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"gives advice on","passagePhrase":"have developed guidelines"},{"uid":"88b1d8d9-a9d1-44c3-b64c-f9fcdd5c5ec9","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"are no longer active","passagePhrase":"at the end of their useful life"},{"uid":"48e2e851-70f7-4069-b8b9-b34495b6e3c3","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"should be removed","passagePhrase":"venting"},{"uid":"ac63bd84-8068-40fe-bb1b-aaa11fd43d4e","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"unused","passagePhrase":"leftover"},{"uid":"d7201053-e37d-4e2d-bdb7-4b6f10cf2b2a","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"could","passagePhrase":"might"},{"uid":"63a375d2-656d-4653-86bd-b0d9ae8c38d9","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"recommendation","passagePhrase":"advise"},{"uid":"07e14983-28d4-4dd3-ad7e-71a89699ea5a","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"is widely ignored","passagePhrase":"only about half of all missions have abided by this 25-year goal"},{"uid":"fd4b16ef-e015-4011-b86c-5cbb761f87c0","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"are unlikely to","passagePhrase":"are probably not going to"},{"uid":"b3029e18-87b8-49f7-a3db-d3679f903043","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"exact","passagePhrase":"precisely"},{"uid":"e193dfe4-0fea-4ec1-8217-9a2067ff1a94","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"location of space junk","passagePhrase":"where everything was"},{"uid":"3537d979-04e7-442e-bde4-40102af04c94","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"prevent any possible danger","passagePhrase":"almost never have a problem"},{"uid":"9fc7730b-7470-4d8a-bb6f-7cc63d3167ce","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"tracking objects in space","passagePhrase":"space traffic management"},{"uid":"d0e432b2-8b09-4d30-aacf-57e6a4440b1e","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"comparison","passagePhrase":"similar to"},{"uid":"a8527f52-7bf2-4540-913a-172dd1a00274","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"transportation system","passagePhrase":"managing traffic on the roads or in the air"},{"uid":"c20f051f-d81e-45d5-8833-3cf3effe00dc","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"conflicting information","passagePhrase":"two completely different orbits"},{"uid":"ab11db91-9a57-4c60-8718-bb97a0fb08e8","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"a person’s aims","passagePhrase":"make space a place that is safe to operate"},{"uid":"b5cfc5c6-f393-4544-acca-93b7eba7869c","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"a person’s aims","passagePhrase":"make space a place that is safe to operate"},{"uid":"6874b215-6442-42c3-af56-0081f137842e","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"available","passagePhrase":"free"},{"uid":"c7b95488-5c1b-4a03-95bf-d5023b1c716e","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"preserved for the future","passagePhrase":"useful for generations to come"}]},"reading_u2_286":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3><strong>Stonehenge</strong></h3><p>For centuries, historians and archaeologists have puzzled over the many mysteries of Stonehenge, a prehistoric monument that took an estimated 1,500 years to erect. Located on Salisbury Plain in southern England, it is comprised of roughly 100 massive upright stones placed in a circular layout.</p><p>Archaeologists believe England’s most iconic prehistoric ruin was built in several stages, with the earliest constructed 5,000 or more years ago. First, Neolithic* Britons used primitive tools, which may have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7465b99e-dd31-4c23-a93d-fd11af3c2910\" data-question=\"1\">fashioned out of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> deer antlers, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e36722f-d0b9-49e9-9fc7-bb3a22f7d4b3\" data-question=\"1\">to dig<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> a massive circular ditch and bank, or henge. Deep pits dating back to that era and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be488b5e-abbd-41f1-bb54-5e1146fc97ce\" data-question=\"2\">located<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a0f518a-0702-4eb9-af54-2473a269f261\" data-question=\"2\">within<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> the circle may have once held a ring of timber posts, according to some scholars.</p><p>Several hundred years later, it is thought, Stonehenge’s builders hoisted an estimated 80 bluestones, 43 of which remain today, into standing positions and placed them in either a horseshoe or circular formation. These stones have been traced all the way to the Preseli Hills in Wales, some 300 kilometres from Stonehenge. How, then, did prehistoric builders without sophisticated tools or engineering haul these boulders, which weigh up to four tons, over such a great distance?</p><p>According to one long-standing theory among archaeologists, Stonehenge’s builders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ec32849-4a6b-4139-abb2-9fedc4cb993d\" data-question=\"3\">fashioned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> sledges and rollers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4869cfa6-6046-44c0-a0a2-168e120b9729\" data-question=\"3\">out of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> tree trunks to lug the bluestones from the Preseli Hills. They then transferred the boulders onto rafts and floated them first along the Welsh coast and then up the River Avon toward Salisbury Plain; alternatively, they may have towed each stone with a fleet of vessels. More recent archaeological hypotheses have them transporting the bluestones with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40e8c179-4c2d-4e84-ad04-bb3b6ce35964\" data-question=\"4\">supersized<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> wicker baskets on a combination of ball bearings and long grooved planks, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8dcef5e-5890-4cf5-85cb-2121a7ae9083\" data-question=\"4\">hauled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> by oxen.</p><p>As early as the 1970s, geologists have been adding their voices to the debate over how Stonehenge came into being. Challenging the classic image of industrious builders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"045cf7dd-b972-473d-9e8b-d4c1a515ea85\" data-question=\"5\">pushing, carting, rolling or hauling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> giant stones from faraway Wales, some scientists have suggested that it was glaciers, not humans, that carried the bluestones to Salisbury Plain. Most archaeologists have remained sceptical about this theory, however, wondering how the forces of nature could possibly have delivered the exact number of stones needed to complete the circle.</p><p>The third phase of construction took place around 2000 BCE. At this point, sandstone slabs — known as ‘sarsens’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a85a0d7e-a61d-43fb-a1d0-287270e7fb85\" data-question=\"9\">— were arranged into an outer crescent or ring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>; some were assembled into the iconic three-pieced structures called trilithons that stand tall in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca04d180-94d0-4165-82b5-9d1e54e7a8c5\" data-question=\"9\">the centre<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of Stonehenge. Some 50 of these stones are now visible on the site, which may once have contained many more. Radiocarbon dating has revealed that work continued at Stonehenge until <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"16057d3a-ac02-4eda-a6e2-d77e1c75e1ad\" data-question=\"10\">roughly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> 1600 BCE, with the bluestones in particular <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a63ba8c0-1b18-4be3-9230-a7863902e392\" data-question=\"10\">being repositioned multiple times<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.</p><p>But who were the builders of Stonehenge? In the 17th century, archaeologist John Aubrey <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10ec32af-dc76-489b-8b59-e837f5e74b02\" data-question=\"6\">made the claim that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> Stonehenge was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4327e7a9-adfd-4044-a6bd-7da449149257\" data-question=\"6\">the work of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> druids, who had important religious, judicial and political roles in Celtic” society. This theory was widely popularized by the antiquarian William Stukeley, who had unearthed primitive graves at the site.</p><p>Even today, people who identify as modern druids continue to gather at Stonehenge for the summer solstice. However, in the mid-20th century, radiocarbon dating demonstrated that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"5e3ae296-c833-444a-84f7-fb32d20a0ed3\" data-question=\"11\">Stonehenge stood more than 1,000 years before the Celts inhabited the region<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</p><p>Many modern historians and archaeologists now agree that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0fcd4dfb-5d12-4b48-aa27-33720257fb47\" data-question=\"12\">several distinct tribes of people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> contributed to Stonehenge, each undertaking a different phase of its construction. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ae7144e1-47e9-49c0-b207-e16962ad7d34\" data-question=\"12\">Bones, tools and other artefacts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca7a517b-97b9-44d6-8845-64c77601768f\" data-question=\"12\">found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> on the site seem to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7e96bc5d-f5d4-4062-ba7a-56b0db5d1676\" data-question=\"12\">support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> this hypothesis. The first stage was achieved by Neolithic agrarians who were likely to have been indigenous to the British Isles. Later, it is believed, groups with advanced tools and a more communal way of life left their mark on the site. Some believe that they were immigrants from the European continent, while others maintain that they were probably native Britons, descended from the original builders.</p><p>If the facts surrounding the architects and construction of Stonehenge remain shadowy at best, the purpose of the striking monument is even more of a mystery. While <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"451a7d8a-8fce-4d1c-b1a2-ce9944d50c11\" data-question=\"7\">there is consensus<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> among <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa653a24-01a0-4368-a1f0-0dbf04d8a60c\" data-question=\"7\">the majority of modern scholars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> that Stonehenge once <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2314d831-c61d-432c-adcd-2fabc474ae72\" data-question=\"7\">served the function of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> burial ground, they have yet to determine what other purposes it had.</p><p>In the 1960s, the astronomer Gerald Hawkins suggested that the cluster of megalithic stones <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c69d548-66c9-47bb-b3c0-378afd54fec6\" data-question=\"8\">operated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b805174f-7d93-4cac-8415-1081b9505405\" data-question=\"8\">a form of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> calendar, with different points corresponding to astrological phenomena such as solstices, equinoxes and eclipses occurring at different times of the year. While his theory has received a considerable amount of attention over the decades, critics maintain that Stonehenge’s builders probably lacked the knowledge necessary to predict such events or that England’s dense cloud cover would have obscured their view of the skies.</p><p>More recently, signs of illness and injury in the human remains unearthed at Stonehenge ~ led a group of British archaeologists to speculate that it was considered a place of healing, perhaps because bluestones were thought to have curative powers.</p><p>* Neolithic — The era, also known as the New Stone Age, which began around 12,000 years ago and ended around 3500 BCE</p><p>** Celtic — The Celts were people who lived in Britain and northwest Europe during the Iron Age from 600 BCE to 43 CE</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 43\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the notes below.<br>Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1—8 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">Stonehenge</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">Construction</span></strong></p><p><span style=\"color:#151615\">Stage 1:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">the ditch and henge <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e36722f-d0b9-49e9-9fc7-bb3a22f7d4b3\" data-question=\"1\">were dug<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, possibly using tools <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7465b99e-dd31-4c23-a93d-fd11af3c2910\" data-question=\"1\">made from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> </span><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">1................................. </span></strong></li></ul><ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\"><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">2.................... may have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be488b5e-abbd-41f1-bb54-5e1146fc97ce\" data-question=\"2\">arranged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in deep pits <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6a0f518a-0702-4eb9-af54-2473a269f261\" data-question=\"2\">inside the circle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span></span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color:#151615\">Stage 2:</span></p><ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\"><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">bluestones from the Preseli Hills were placed in standing position</span></li><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">theories about the transportation of the bluestones:</span></li></ul><ul style=\"margin-left:40px\"><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">archaeological:</span></li></ul><ul style=\"list-style-type:circle; margin-left:80px\"><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">builders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4869cfa6-6046-44c0-a0a2-168e120b9729\" data-question=\"3\">used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> </span><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">3................. </span></strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ec32849-4a6b-4139-abb2-9fedc4cb993d\" data-question=\"3\">make<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> sledges and rollers</span></li></ul><ul style=\"list-style-type:circle; margin-left:80px\"><li><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">4......................... </span></strong><span style=\"color:#151615\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a8dcef5e-5890-4cf5-85cb-2121a7ae9083\" data-question=\"4\">pulled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> them on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40e8c179-4c2d-4e84-ad04-bb3b6ce35964\" data-question=\"4\">giant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> baskets</span></li></ul><ul style=\"margin-left:40px\"><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">geological:</span></li></ul><ul style=\"list-style-type:circle; margin-left:80px\"><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">they were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"045cf7dd-b972-473d-9e8b-d4c1a515ea85\" data-question=\"5\">brought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> from Wales by </span><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">5.....................</span></strong></li></ul><p><span style=\"color:#151615\">Stage 3:</span></p><ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\"><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">sandstone slabs were arranged into an outer crescent or ring</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color:#151615\">​​​​​​</span><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">Builders</span></strong></p><ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\"><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10ec32af-dc76-489b-8b59-e837f5e74b02\" data-question=\"6\">theory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> arose in the 17th century that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4327e7a9-adfd-4044-a6bd-7da449149257\" data-question=\"6\">its builders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> were Celtic </span><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">6.........................</span></strong></li></ul><p><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">Purpose</span></strong></p><ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\"><li><span style=\"color:#151615\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa653a24-01a0-4368-a1f0-0dbf04d8a60c\" data-question=\"7\">many experts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> agree it has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2314d831-c61d-432c-adcd-2fabc474ae72\" data-question=\"7\">used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> as a </span><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">7............................ </span></strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">site</span></li><li><span style=\"color:#151615\">in the 1960s, it was suggested that it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c69d548-66c9-47bb-b3c0-378afd54fec6\" data-question=\"8\">worked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b805174f-7d93-4cac-8415-1081b9505405\" data-question=\"8\">a kind of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> </span><strong><span style=\"color:#151615\">8.........................</span></strong></li></ul></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145085\" id=\"question-wrapper-145085\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(DEER) ANTLERS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145086\" id=\"question-wrapper-145086\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">(TIMBER) POSTS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145087\" id=\"question-wrapper-145087\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TREE TRUNKS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145088\" id=\"question-wrapper-145088\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OXEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145089\" id=\"question-wrapper-145089\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GLACIERS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145090\" id=\"question-wrapper-145090\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DRUIDS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145091\" id=\"question-wrapper-145091\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BURIAL</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145092\" id=\"question-wrapper-145092\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CALENDAR</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 44\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</p><p>In boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet, write</p><p>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</p><p>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</p><p>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145093\" id=\"question-wrapper-145093\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> During the third phase of construction, sandstone slabs were placed in both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a85a0d7e-a61d-43fb-a1d0-287270e7fb85\" data-question=\"9\">the outer areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca04d180-94d0-4165-82b5-9d1e54e7a8c5\" data-question=\"9\">the middle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of the Stonehenge site. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145094\" id=\"question-wrapper-145094\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is scientific proof that the bluestones <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a63ba8c0-1b18-4be3-9230-a7863902e392\" data-question=\"10\">stood in the same spot<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> until <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"16057d3a-ac02-4eda-a6e2-d77e1c75e1ad\" data-question=\"10\">approximately<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> 1600 BCE. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145095\" id=\"question-wrapper-145095\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"31a0c9bb-f0f0-4570-b0ed-f968944c8013\" data-question=\"11\">John Aubrey’s claim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> about Stonehenge <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"5e3ae296-c833-444a-84f7-fb32d20a0ed3\" data-question=\"11\">was supported<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> by 20th-century findings. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145096\" id=\"question-wrapper-145096\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ae7144e1-47e9-49c0-b207-e16962ad7d34\" data-question=\"12\">Objects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca7a517b-97b9-44d6-8845-64c77601768f\" data-question=\"12\">discovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> at Stonehenge seem to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7e96bc5d-f5d4-4062-ba7a-56b0db5d1676\" data-question=\"12\">indicate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> that it was constructed by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0fcd4dfb-5d12-4b48-aa27-33720257fb47\" data-question=\"12\">a number of different groups of people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145097\" id=\"question-wrapper-145097\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Criticism of Gerald Hawkins’ theory about Stonehenge has come mainly from other astronomers. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7465b99e-dd31-4c23-a93d-fd11af3c2910","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"made from","passagePhrase":"fashioned out of"},{"uid":"2e36722f-d0b9-49e9-9fc7-bb3a22f7d4b3","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"were dug","passagePhrase":"to dig"},{"uid":"be488b5e-abbd-41f1-bb54-5e1146fc97ce","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"arranged","passagePhrase":"located"},{"uid":"6a0f518a-0702-4eb9-af54-2473a269f261","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"inside the circle","passagePhrase":"within"},{"uid":"1ec32849-4a6b-4139-abb2-9fedc4cb993d","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"make","passagePhrase":"fashioned"},{"uid":"4869cfa6-6046-44c0-a0a2-168e120b9729","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"used","passagePhrase":"out of"},{"uid":"40e8c179-4c2d-4e84-ad04-bb3b6ce35964","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"giant","passagePhrase":"supersized"},{"uid":"a8dcef5e-5890-4cf5-85cb-2121a7ae9083","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"pulled","passagePhrase":"hauled"},{"uid":"045cf7dd-b972-473d-9e8b-d4c1a515ea85","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"brought","passagePhrase":"pushing, carting, rolling or hauling"},{"uid":"a85a0d7e-a61d-43fb-a1d0-287270e7fb85","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"the outer areas","passagePhrase":"— were arranged into an outer crescent or ring"},{"uid":"ca04d180-94d0-4165-82b5-9d1e54e7a8c5","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"the middle","passagePhrase":"the centre"},{"uid":"16057d3a-ac02-4eda-a6e2-d77e1c75e1ad","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"approximately","passagePhrase":"roughly"},{"uid":"10ec32af-dc76-489b-8b59-e837f5e74b02","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"theory","passagePhrase":"made the claim that"},{"uid":"4327e7a9-adfd-4044-a6bd-7da449149257","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"its builders","passagePhrase":"the work of"},{"uid":"0fcd4dfb-5d12-4b48-aa27-33720257fb47","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"a number of different groups of people","passagePhrase":"several distinct tribes of people"},{"uid":"ae7144e1-47e9-49c0-b207-e16962ad7d34","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Objects","passagePhrase":"Bones, tools and other artefacts"},{"uid":"ca7a517b-97b9-44d6-8845-64c77601768f","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"discovered","passagePhrase":"found"},{"uid":"7e96bc5d-f5d4-4062-ba7a-56b0db5d1676","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"indicate","passagePhrase":"support"},{"uid":"451a7d8a-8fce-4d1c-b1a2-ce9944d50c11","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"there is consensus"},{"uid":"aa653a24-01a0-4368-a1f0-0dbf04d8a60c","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"many experts","passagePhrase":"the majority of modern scholars"},{"uid":"2314d831-c61d-432c-adcd-2fabc474ae72","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"used","passagePhrase":"served the function of"},{"uid":"2c69d548-66c9-47bb-b3c0-378afd54fec6","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"worked","passagePhrase":"operated"},{"uid":"b805174f-7d93-4cac-8415-1081b9505405","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"a kind of","passagePhrase":"a form of"},{"uid":"31a0c9bb-f0f0-4570-b0ed-f968944c8013","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"John Aubrey’s claim","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_287":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Living with artificial intelligence</strong></p><p><em>Powertul artificial intelligence (Al) needs to be reliably aligned with human values, but does this mean Al will eventually have to police those values?</em></p><p>This has been the decade of Al, with one astonishing feat after another. A chess- playing Al that can defeat not only all human chess players, but also all previous human programmed chess machines, after learning the game in just four hours? That’s yesterday's news, what’s next? True, these prodigious accomplishments are all in so called narrow Al, where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d1d04035-9536-400f-b3a9-a822f6f6accd\" data-question=\"14\">machines perform highly specialised tasks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. But many experts believe this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21e4b00c-caa0-4928-9162-ed8ab5e2f88e\" data-question=\"14\">restriction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> is very <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d431dae-2e48-4416-98d4-480663b4b4a8\" data-question=\"14\">temporary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b3c8798-9f8b-4be9-8d0c-e5f124910d70\" data-question=\"14\">By mid-century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, we may have artificial general intelligence (AGI) — machines that can achieve human-level performance on the full range of tasks that we ourselves can tackle.</p><p>If so, there’s little reason to think it will stop there. Machines will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b69bd0dd-cf34-48f0-82b7-8a18831c8f18\" data-question=\"15\">be free of many of the physical constraints on human intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Our brains run at slow biochemical processing speeds on the power ofa light bulb, and their size is restricted by the dimensions of the human birth canal. It is remarkable what they accomplish, given these handicaps. But they may be as far from the physical limits of thought as our eyes are from the incredibly powerful Webb Space Telescope.</p><p>Once machines are better than us at designing even smarter machines, progress towards these limits could accelerate. What would this mean for us? Could we ensure a safe and worthwhile coexistence with such machines? On the plus side, Al is already useful and profitable for many things, and super Al might be expected to be super useful, and super profitable. But the more powerful Al becomes, the more important it will be to specify its goals with great care. Folklore is full of tales of people who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d379ca3-c252-4298-84a5-b148420b3554\" data-question=\"16\">ask for the wrong thing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1483dad0-a9c1-44ea-86d4-9d10f6c0f393\" data-question=\"16\">disastrous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> consequences — King Midas, for example, might have wished that everything he touched turned to gold, but didn’t really intend this to apply to his breakfast.</p><p>So we need to create powerful Al machines that are ‘human-friendly’ — that have goals reliably aligned with our own values. One thing that makes this task difficult is that we are far from reliably human-friendly ourselves. We do many terrible things to each other and to many other creatures with whom we share the planet. If superintelligent machines don’t <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4302719d-a651-4596-8694-f20d0b1eab07\" data-question=\"17\">do a lot better than us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, we’ll be in deep trouble. We'll have powerful new intelligence amplifying the dark sides of our own fallible natures.</p><p>For safety’s sake, then, we want the machines to be ethically as well as cognitively superhuman. We want them to aim for the moral high ground, not for the troughs in which many of us spend some of our time. Luckily they'll be smart enough for the job. If there are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6728ca44-484d-4d76-a770-aecf0c642d4f\" data-question=\"18\">routes to the moral high ground<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, they'll be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"458173b9-8006-4c7b-88e5-0a975e85d8ac\" data-question=\"18\">better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> than us at finding them, and steering us in the right direction.</p><p>However, there are two big problems with this utopian vision. One is how we get the machines started on the journey, the other is what it would mean to reach this destination. The ‘getting started’ problem is that we need to tell the machines what they're looking for with sufficient clarity that we can be confident they will find it — whatever ‘it’ actually turns out to be. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9676cdd1-6e94-49f5-b560-368ca3594cab\" data-question=\"19\">won't be easy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, given that we are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb8154f7-c1fc-4339-af7a-86a6a11681ff\" data-question=\"19\">tribal creatures and conflicted about the ideals ourselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. We often ignore the suffering of strangers, and even contribute to it, at least indirectly. How then, do we point machines in the direction of something better?</p><p>As for the ‘destination’ problem, we might, by putting ourselves in the hands of these moral guides and gatekeepers, be sacrificing our own autonomy — an important part of what makes us human. Machines who are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c61a0a00-8f6a-4247-9f93-12cb9bc0001f\" data-question=\"20\">better than us at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> sticking to the moral high ground may be expected to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"419015bf-51dc-4ca7-82e4-62b4181a58b3\" data-question=\"20\">discourage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> some of the lapses we presently take for granted. We might lose our freedom to discriminate in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6664d77-64cf-4fc4-812d-e7f492f5f79b\" data-question=\"20\">favour of our own communities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, for example.</p><p>Loss of freedom to behave badly isn’t always a bad thing, of course: denying ourselves the freedom to put children to work in factories, or to smoke in restaurants are signs of progress. But are we ready for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d78d7488-ec04-44da-a7b9-d779bdf167dc\" data-question=\"22\">ethical silicon police limiting our options<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>? They might be so good at doing it that we won’t notice them; but <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9c84ac76-da0c-4727-8e5c-a23c61827f68\" data-question=\"22\">few of us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> are likely to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10f4e35a-2e9f-4d65-9777-5c33b2b4fa37\" data-question=\"22\">welcome such a future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</p><p>These issues might seem far-fetched, but they are to some extent already here. Al already has some input into <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86acd7d5-8418-4e42-b92a-55ca8377ceeb\" data-question=\"24\">how<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> resources are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b9a3f2ea-c0d9-4f17-ac81-71e74f2ac446\" data-question=\"24\">used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b342199-903b-4367-a6fc-969996a8cceb\" data-question=\"24\">National Health Service (NHS)<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> here in the UK, for example. If it was given a greater role, it might do so much more efficiently than humans can manage, and act in the interests of taxpayers and those who use the health system. However, we’d be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4aafb215-5496-4528-8c50-8cb21852db3e\" data-question=\"26\">depriving<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> some humans (e.g. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c4c9836-f6e1-4bf2-833c-de868d8df810\" data-question=\"25\">senior doctors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>) of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79a4e14a-8137-4828-8f70-6cb3cef18340\" data-question=\"26\">control they presently enjoy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Since we’d want to ensure that people are treated equally and that policies are fair, the goals of Al would need to be specified correctly.</p><p>We have a new powerful technology to deal with —itself, literally, a new way of thinking. For our own safety, we need to point these new thinkers in the right direction, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b922d1c-c014-4a07-af44-3d1b877f9113\" data-question=\"23\">get them to act well for us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. It is not yet clear whether this is possible, but if it is, it will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"262aae4d-d53a-499a-854f-78dc234bdf25\" data-question=\"23\">require a cooperative spirit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, and a willingness to set aside self-interest.</p><p>Both general intelligence and moral reasoning are often thought to be uniquely human capacities. But safety seems to require that we think of them as a package: if we are to give general intelligence to machines, we'll need to give them moral authority, too. And where exactly would that leave human beings? All the more reason to think about the destination now, and to be careful about what we wish for.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 47\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet.</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145098\" id=\"question-wrapper-145098\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does the writer make about Al in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is difficult to predict how quickly Al will progress.</li> <li>B. Much can be learned about the use of Al in chess machines.</li> <li>C. The future is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d431dae-2e48-4416-98d4-480663b4b4a8\" data-question=\"14\">unlikely to see<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21e4b00c-caa0-4928-9162-ed8ab5e2f88e\" data-question=\"14\">limitations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d1d04035-9536-400f-b3a9-a822f6f6accd\" data-question=\"14\">capabilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of Al.</li> <li>D. Experts disagree on which specialised tasks Al will be able to perform.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145099\" id=\"question-wrapper-145099\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer doing in the second paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. explaining why machines will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b69bd0dd-cf34-48f0-82b7-8a18831c8f18\" data-question=\"15\">be able to outperform humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></li> <li>B. describing the characteristics that humans and machines share</li> <li>C. giving information about the development of machine intelligence</li> <li>D. indicating which aspects of humans are the most advanced</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145100\" id=\"question-wrapper-145100\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Why does the writer mention the story of King Midas? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. to compare different visions of progress</li> <li>B. to illustrate that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d379ca3-c252-4298-84a5-b148420b3554\" data-question=\"16\">poorly defined objectives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1483dad0-a9c1-44ea-86d4-9d10f6c0f393\" data-question=\"16\">go wrong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></li> <li>C. to emphasise the need for cooperation</li> <li>D. to point out the financial advantages of a course of action</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145101\" id=\"question-wrapper-145101\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What challenge does the writer refer to in the fourth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. encouraging humans to behave in a more principled way</li> <li>B. deciding which values we want Al to share with us</li> <li>C. creating a better world for all creatures on the planet</li> <li>D. ensuring Al is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4302719d-a651-4596-8694-f20d0b1eab07\" data-question=\"17\">more human-friendly than we are ourselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145102\" id=\"question-wrapper-145102\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer suggest about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b3c8798-9f8b-4be9-8d0c-e5f124910d70\" data-question=\"14\">the future<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of Al in the fifth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The safety of machines will become a key issue.</li> <li>B. It is hard to know what impact machines will have on the world.</li> <li>C. Machines will be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"458173b9-8006-4c7b-88e5-0a975e85d8ac\" data-question=\"18\">superior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to humans in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6728ca44-484d-4d76-a770-aecf0c642d4f\" data-question=\"18\">certain respects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Many humans will oppose machines having a wider role.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145103\" id=\"question-wrapper-145103\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Which of the following best summarises the writer’s argument in the sixth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. More intelligent machines will result in greater abuses of power.</li> <li>B. Machine learning will share very few features with human learning.</li> <li>C. There are a limited number of people with the knowledge to program machines.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb8154f7-c1fc-4339-af7a-86a6a11681ff\" data-question=\"19\">Human shortcomings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> will make creating the machines we need more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9676cdd1-6e94-49f5-b560-368ca3594cab\" data-question=\"19\">difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 48\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 2?</p><p>In boxes 20-23 on your answer sheet, write</p><p>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145104\" id=\"question-wrapper-145104\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Machines with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c61a0a00-8f6a-4247-9f93-12cb9bc0001f\" data-question=\"20\">the ability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to make moral decisions may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"419015bf-51dc-4ca7-82e4-62b4181a58b3\" data-question=\"20\">prevent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> us from promoting the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6664d77-64cf-4fc4-812d-e7f492f5f79b\" data-question=\"20\">interests of our communities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145105\" id=\"question-wrapper-145105\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Silicon police would need to exist in large numbers in order to be effective. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145106\" id=\"question-wrapper-145106\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9c84ac76-da0c-4727-8e5c-a23c61827f68\" data-question=\"22\">Many people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10f4e35a-2e9f-4d65-9777-5c33b2b4fa37\" data-question=\"22\">comfortable with the prospect of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d78d7488-ec04-44da-a7b9-d779bdf167dc\" data-question=\"22\">their independence being restricted by machines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145107\" id=\"question-wrapper-145107\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> If we want to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b922d1c-c014-4a07-af44-3d1b877f9113\" data-question=\"23\">ensure that machines act in our best interests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, we all <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"262aae4d-d53a-499a-854f-78dc234bdf25\" data-question=\"23\">need to work together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 49\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the summary using the list of phrases, A-F, below.<br>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 24—26 on your answer sheet.</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 49\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Al currently has a limited role <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86acd7d5-8418-4e42-b92a-55ca8377ceeb\" data-question=\"24\">in the way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> 24 ___________ are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b9a3f2ea-c0d9-4f17-ac81-71e74f2ac446\" data-question=\"24\">allocated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b342199-903b-4367-a6fc-969996a8cceb\" data-question=\"24\">the health service<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. The positive aspect of Al having a bigger role is that it would be more efficient and lead to patient benefits. However, such a change would result, for example, in certain 25 ___________ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4aafb215-5496-4528-8c50-8cb21852db3e\" data-question=\"26\">not having<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> their current level of 26 ___________ . It is therefore important that Al goals are appropriate so that discriminatory practices could be avoided.</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 49\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><ul><li>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c4c9836-f6e1-4bf2-833c-de868d8df810\" data-question=\"25\">medical practitioners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span></li><li>B specialised tasks</li><li>C. available resources</li><li>D reduced illness</li><li>E <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79a4e14a-8137-4828-8f70-6cb3cef18340\" data-question=\"26\">professional authority<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></li><li>F technology experts</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145108\" id=\"question-wrapper-145108\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145109\" id=\"question-wrapper-145109\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145110\" id=\"question-wrapper-145110\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"d1d04035-9536-400f-b3a9-a822f6f6accd","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"capabilities","passagePhrase":"machines perform highly specialised tasks"},{"uid":"21e4b00c-caa0-4928-9162-ed8ab5e2f88e","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"limitations","passagePhrase":"restriction"},{"uid":"4d431dae-2e48-4416-98d4-480663b4b4a8","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"unlikely to see","passagePhrase":"temporary"},{"uid":"9b3c8798-9f8b-4be9-8d0c-e5f124910d70","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"the future","passagePhrase":"By mid-century"},{"uid":"b69bd0dd-cf34-48f0-82b7-8a18831c8f18","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"be able to outperform humans","passagePhrase":"be free of many of the physical constraints on human intelligence"},{"uid":"7d379ca3-c252-4298-84a5-b148420b3554","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"poorly defined objectives","passagePhrase":"ask for the wrong thing"},{"uid":"1483dad0-a9c1-44ea-86d4-9d10f6c0f393","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"go wrong","passagePhrase":"disastrous"},{"uid":"4302719d-a651-4596-8694-f20d0b1eab07","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"more human-friendly than we are ourselves","passagePhrase":"do a lot better than us"},{"uid":"6728ca44-484d-4d76-a770-aecf0c642d4f","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"certain respects","passagePhrase":"routes to the moral high ground"},{"uid":"458173b9-8006-4c7b-88e5-0a975e85d8ac","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"superior","passagePhrase":"better"},{"uid":"9676cdd1-6e94-49f5-b560-368ca3594cab","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"difficult","passagePhrase":"won't be easy"},{"uid":"fb8154f7-c1fc-4339-af7a-86a6a11681ff","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Human shortcomings","passagePhrase":"tribal creatures and conflicted about the ideals ourselves"},{"uid":"c61a0a00-8f6a-4247-9f93-12cb9bc0001f","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the ability","passagePhrase":"better than us at"},{"uid":"419015bf-51dc-4ca7-82e4-62b4181a58b3","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"prevent","passagePhrase":"discourage"},{"uid":"d6664d77-64cf-4fc4-812d-e7f492f5f79b","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"interests of our communities","passagePhrase":"favour of our own communities"},{"uid":"d78d7488-ec04-44da-a7b9-d779bdf167dc","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"their independence being restricted by machines","passagePhrase":"ethical silicon police limiting our options"},{"uid":"10f4e35a-2e9f-4d65-9777-5c33b2b4fa37","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"comfortable with the prospect of","passagePhrase":"welcome such a future"},{"uid":"86acd7d5-8418-4e42-b92a-55ca8377ceeb","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"in the way","passagePhrase":"how"},{"uid":"b9a3f2ea-c0d9-4f17-ac81-71e74f2ac446","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"allocated","passagePhrase":"used"},{"uid":"0b342199-903b-4367-a6fc-969996a8cceb","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"the health service","passagePhrase":"National Health Service (NHS)"},{"uid":"4aafb215-5496-4528-8c50-8cb21852db3e","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"not having","passagePhrase":"depriving"},{"uid":"6c4c9836-f6e1-4bf2-833c-de868d8df810","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"medical practitioners","passagePhrase":"senior doctors"},{"uid":"79a4e14a-8137-4828-8f70-6cb3cef18340","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"professional authority","passagePhrase":"control they presently enjoy"},{"uid":"2b922d1c-c014-4a07-af44-3d1b877f9113","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"ensure that machines act in our best interests","passagePhrase":"get them to act well for us"},{"uid":"262aae4d-d53a-499a-854f-78dc234bdf25","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"need to work together","passagePhrase":"require a cooperative spirit"}]},"reading_u2_288":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3><strong>An ideal city</strong></h3><p>Leonardo da Vinci's ideal city was centuries ahead of its time</p><p>The word ‘genius’ is universally associated with the name of Leonardo da Vinci. A true Renaissance man, he embodied scientific spirit, artistic talent and humanist sensibilities. Five hundred years have passed since Leonardo died in his home at Chateau du Clos Lucé, outside Tours, France. Yet far from fading into insignificance, his thinking has carried down the centuries and still surprises today.</p><p>The Renaissance marked the transition from the 15th century to modernity and took place after the spread of the plague in the 14th century, which caused a global crisis resulting in some 200 million deaths across Europe and Asia. Today, the world is on the cusp of a climate crisis, which is predicted to cause widespread displacement, extinctions and death, if left unaddressed. Then, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e0c7ba2-4fa8-43e7-94b9-d97b5be569b6\" data-question=\"29\">as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> now, radical solutions were called for to revolutionise the way people lived and safeguard humanity against <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26846b05-f836-4b0e-b689-e8a694446ec0\" data-question=\"29\">catastrophe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</p><p>Around 1486 —after a pestilence that killed half the population in Milan, Italy - Leonardo turned his thoughts to urban planning problems. Following a typical Renaissance trend, he began to work on an ‘ideal city’ project, which — due to its excessive costs — would <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"89778ddc-3d82-490b-941c-7187b87b897d\" data-question=\"30\">remain unfulfilled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Yet given that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7e26e69a-3e2a-4b33-a48f-85827a40b03c\" data-question=\"31\">unsustainable urban models<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04fe6ba3-ccf6-4299-a3fe-fff8afc35ac4\" data-question=\"31\">a key cause of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> global climate change today, it’s only natural to wonder how Leonardo might have changed the shape of modern cities.</p><p>Although the Renaissance is renowned as an era of incredible progress in art and architecture, . it is rarely noted that the 15th century also marked the birth of urbanism as a true academic discipline. The rigour and method behind the conscious conception of a city had been largely missing in Western thought until the moment when prominent Renaissance men pushed forward large-scale urban projects in Italy, such as the reconfiguration of the town of Pienza and the expansion of the city of Ferrara. These works surely inspired Leonardo’s decision to rethink the design of medieval cities; with their winding and overcrowded streets and with houses piled against one another.</p><p>It is not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd789035-ac32-4d89-87bc-7e282ca4e8e3\" data-question=\"34\">easy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> to identify a coordinated vision of Leonardo’s ideal city because of his <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"b64304ad-1234-4990-b695-c1ef32e1c0da\" data-question=\"33\">disordered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> way of working with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1227781f-ff19-4725-867a-0017ca618bf6\" data-question=\"33\">notes and sketches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. But from the largest collection of Leonardo’s papers ever assembled, a series of innovative thoughts can be reconstructed regarding the foundation of a new city along the Ticino River, which runs from Switzerland into Italy and is 248 kilometres long. He designed the city for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd789035-ac32-4d89-87bc-7e282ca4e8e3\" data-question=\"34\">easy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> transport of goods and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ced5d9c-6dbd-419f-b477-396e27ec1a8e\" data-question=\"34\">clean urban spaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, and he wanted a comfortable and spacious city, with well-ordered streets and architecture. He recommended ‘high, strong walls’, with ‘towers and battlements of all necessary and pleasant beauty’.</p><p>His plans for a modern and ‘rational’ city were consistent with Renaissance ideals. But, in keeping with his personality, Leonardo included several <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a56b9676-13d5-485d-8f96-5cfff8f3fe2d\" data-question=\"35\">innovations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> in his urban design. Leonardo wanted the city to be built on several levels, linked with vertical <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13be8ce5-78ee-4c6d-a7b2-ab40e2c1fead\" data-question=\"35\">outdoor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> staircases. This design can be seen in some of today’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa688031-35b5-484d-b493-66b54a90c39c\" data-question=\"35\">high-rise buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> but was unconventional at the time. Indeed, this idea of taking full advantage of the interior spaces wasn’t implemented until the 1920s and 1930s, with the birth of the Modernist movement.</p><p>While in the upper layers of the city, people could walk undisturbed between elegant palaces and streets, the lower layer was the place for services, trade, transport and industry. But the true originality of Leonardo’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a845e50-4de7-4a79-bb5e-e28906c80109\" data-question=\"36\">vision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> was its fusion of architecture and engineering. Leonardo designed extensive hydraulic plants to create artificial canals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d696ed55-77df-4fd3-8a28-5ca0a420192c\" data-question=\"36\">throughout<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> the city. The canals, regulated by clocks and basins, were supposed to make it easier for boats to navigate inland. Leonardo also thought that the width of the streets ought to match the average height of the adjacent houses: a rule still followed in many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9095b25c-3a0e-4053-8abe-7f841c2881d9\" data-question=\"37\">contemporary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> cities across Italy, to allow access to sun and reduce the risk of damage from earthquakes.</p><p>Although some of these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"234a679f-1412-47ee-b2f0-73240185693e\" data-question=\"38\">features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"288ad8c4-124b-4af0-988b-6310eb36935f\" data-question=\"38\">existed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> in Roman cities, before Leonardo’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e0f32926-a6cc-4034-9fd8-3c132072d4f8\" data-question=\"38\">drawings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> there had never been a multi-level, compact modern city which was thoroughly technically conceived. Indeed, it wasn’t <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"81c0afa6-f534-400d-88a9-2285374170dc\" data-question=\"38\">until the 19th century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> that some of his ideas were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"658461a9-48d8-4ec3-8273-e72a58ed5f3b\" data-question=\"38\">applied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. For example, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ec6a6e4-629a-40b4-bb53-a12d3632b418\" data-question=\"39\">the subdivision of the city by function<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> — with services and infrastructures located in the lower levels and wide and well-ventilated boulevards and walkways above for residents — is an idea that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"288ad8c4-124b-4af0-988b-6310eb36935f\" data-question=\"38\">can be found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> in Georges-Eugéne Haussmann’s renovation of Paris under Emperor Napoleon III between 1853 and 1870.</p><p>Today, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac0255a8-5c40-4e43-b6dc-e5e272197c15\" data-question=\"40\">Leonardo’s ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> are not simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e51703ff-07fc-49b3-88e4-ef6eb7796e30\" data-question=\"40\">valid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, they actually suggest a way forward for urban planning. Many scholars think that the compact city, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9fc17d36-89d0-4913-b0bc-097b8c8d01e0\" data-question=\"40\">built upwards instead of outwards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, integrated with nature (especially water systems), with efficient transport infrastructure, could help modern cities become more efficient and sustainable. This is yet another reason why Leonardo was aligned so closely with modern urban planning and centuries ahead of his time.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 52\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27-33 on your answer sheet, write</p></div></div><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information<br>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information<br>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145111\" id=\"question-wrapper-145111\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People first referred to Leonardo da Vinci as a genius 500 years ago. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145112\" id=\"question-wrapper-145112\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The current climate crisis is predicted to cause more deaths than the plague. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145113\" id=\"question-wrapper-145113\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26846b05-f836-4b0e-b689-e8a694446ec0\" data-question=\"29\">challenges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> we face today <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e0c7ba2-4fa8-43e7-94b9-d97b5be569b6\" data-question=\"29\">can be compared to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> those of earlier times. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145114\" id=\"question-wrapper-145114\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Leonardo da Vinci's ‘ideal city’ <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"89778ddc-3d82-490b-941c-7187b87b897d\" data-question=\"30\">was constructed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> in the 15th century. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145115\" id=\"question-wrapper-145115\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7e26e69a-3e2a-4b33-a48f-85827a40b03c\" data-question=\"31\">Poor town planning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04fe6ba3-ccf6-4299-a3fe-fff8afc35ac4\" data-question=\"31\">a major contributor to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> climate change. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145116\" id=\"question-wrapper-145116\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In Renaissance times, local people fought against the changes to Pienza and Ferrara. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145117\" id=\"question-wrapper-145117\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Leonardo da Vinci kept a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"b64304ad-1234-4990-b695-c1ef32e1c0da\" data-question=\"33\">neat, organised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1227781f-ff19-4725-867a-0017ca618bf6\" data-question=\"33\">record of his designs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 53\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the summary below.<br>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 34—40 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong><span style=\"color:black\">Leonardo da Vinci's ideal city</span></strong></p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 53\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p style=\"margin-right:5px\"><span style=\"color:black\">A collection of Leonardo da Vinci's paperwork reveals his design of a new city </span><span style=\"color:black\">beside the Ticino River. This was to provide <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd789035-ac32-4d89-87bc-7e282ca4e8e3\" data-question=\"34\">better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> 34........................ </span><span style=\"color:black\">for trade and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ced5d9c-6dbd-419f-b477-396e27ec1a8e\" data-question=\"34\">a less polluted environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Although Leonardo da Vinci's city shared many of the ideals of his time, some of his innovations were considered unconventional in their design. They included <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a56b9676-13d5-485d-8f96-5cfff8f3fe2d\" data-question=\"35\">features<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> that can be seen in some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa688031-35b5-484d-b493-66b54a90c39c\" data-question=\"35\">tower blocks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> today, such as 35............................ on the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"13be8ce5-78ee-4c6d-a7b2-ab40e2c1fead\" data-question=\"35\">exterior<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> of a building. </span></p><p style=\"margin-right:5px\"><span style=\"color:black\">Leonardo da Vinci wasn't only an architect. His <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a845e50-4de7-4a79-bb5e-e28906c80109\" data-question=\"36\">expertise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> in 36........................... was evident in his plans for artificial canals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d696ed55-77df-4fd3-8a28-5ca0a420192c\" data-question=\"36\">within<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> his ideal city. He also believed that the height of houses should relate to the width of streets in case earthquakes occurred. The design of many cities in Italy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9095b25c-3a0e-4053-8abe-7f841c2881d9\" data-question=\"37\">today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> follows this 37 .........................</span></p><p><span style=\"color:black\">While some cities from 38............................ times have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"234a679f-1412-47ee-b2f0-73240185693e\" data-question=\"38\">aspects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> that can also be found in Leonardo's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e0f32926-a6cc-4034-9fd8-3c132072d4f8\" data-question=\"38\">designs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, his ideas weren't <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"658461a9-48d8-4ec3-8273-e72a58ed5f3b\" data-question=\"38\">put into practice<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"81c0afa6-f534-400d-88a9-2285374170dc\" data-question=\"38\">until long after his death<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. 39 ......................... is one example of a city that was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ec6a6e4-629a-40b4-bb53-a12d3632b418\" data-question=\"39\">redesigned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> in the19th century in the way that Leonardo had envisaged. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac0255a8-5c40-4e43-b6dc-e5e272197c15\" data-question=\"40\">His ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> are also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e51703ff-07fc-49b3-88e4-ef6eb7796e30\" data-question=\"40\">relevant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> to today's world, where building </span><strong><span style=\"color:black\">40 </span></strong><span style=\"color:black\">.........................</span><strong><span style=\"color:black\"> </span></strong><span style=\"color:black\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9fc17d36-89d0-4913-b0bc-097b8c8d01e0\" data-question=\"40\">no longer seems to be the best approach<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145118\" id=\"question-wrapper-145118\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRANSPORT</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145119\" id=\"question-wrapper-145119\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STAIRCASES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145120\" id=\"question-wrapper-145120\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ENGINEERING</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145121\" id=\"question-wrapper-145121\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RULE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145122\" id=\"question-wrapper-145122\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ROMAN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145123\" id=\"question-wrapper-145123\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PARIS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145124\" id=\"question-wrapper-145124\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OUTWARDS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"3e0c7ba2-4fa8-43e7-94b9-d97b5be569b6","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"can be compared to","passagePhrase":"as"},{"uid":"26846b05-f836-4b0e-b689-e8a694446ec0","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"challenges","passagePhrase":"catastrophe"},{"uid":"7e26e69a-3e2a-4b33-a48f-85827a40b03c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"Poor town planning","passagePhrase":"unsustainable urban models"},{"uid":"04fe6ba3-ccf6-4299-a3fe-fff8afc35ac4","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"a major contributor to","passagePhrase":"a key cause of"},{"uid":"fd789035-ac32-4d89-87bc-7e282ca4e8e3","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"better","passagePhrase":"easy ... easy"},{"uid":"1227781f-ff19-4725-867a-0017ca618bf6","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"record of his designs","passagePhrase":"notes and sketches"},{"uid":"5ced5d9c-6dbd-419f-b477-396e27ec1a8e","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"a less polluted environment","passagePhrase":"clean urban spaces"},{"uid":"a56b9676-13d5-485d-8f96-5cfff8f3fe2d","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"features","passagePhrase":"innovations"},{"uid":"13be8ce5-78ee-4c6d-a7b2-ab40e2c1fead","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"exterior","passagePhrase":"outdoor"},{"uid":"aa688031-35b5-484d-b493-66b54a90c39c","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"tower blocks","passagePhrase":"high-rise buildings"},{"uid":"0a845e50-4de7-4a79-bb5e-e28906c80109","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"expertise","passagePhrase":"vision"},{"uid":"d696ed55-77df-4fd3-8a28-5ca0a420192c","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"within","passagePhrase":"throughout"},{"uid":"9095b25c-3a0e-4053-8abe-7f841c2881d9","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"today","passagePhrase":"contemporary"},{"uid":"234a679f-1412-47ee-b2f0-73240185693e","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"aspects","passagePhrase":"features"},{"uid":"288ad8c4-124b-4af0-988b-6310eb36935f","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"existed ... can be found"},{"uid":"e0f32926-a6cc-4034-9fd8-3c132072d4f8","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"designs","passagePhrase":"drawings"},{"uid":"81c0afa6-f534-400d-88a9-2285374170dc","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"until long after his death","passagePhrase":"until the 19th century"},{"uid":"658461a9-48d8-4ec3-8273-e72a58ed5f3b","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"put into practice","passagePhrase":"applied"},{"uid":"3ec6a6e4-629a-40b4-bb53-a12d3632b418","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"redesigned","passagePhrase":"the subdivision of the city by function"},{"uid":"ac0255a8-5c40-4e43-b6dc-e5e272197c15","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"His ideas","passagePhrase":"Leonardo’s ideas"},{"uid":"e51703ff-07fc-49b3-88e4-ef6eb7796e30","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"relevant","passagePhrase":"valid"},{"uid":"9fc17d36-89d0-4913-b0bc-097b8c8d01e0","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"no longer seems to be the best approach","passagePhrase":"built upwards instead of outwards"}]},"reading_u2_289":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3><strong>Materials to take us beyond concrete</strong></h3><p><em>Concrete is everywhere, but it’s bad for the planet, generating large amounts of carbon dioxide — alternatives are being developed</em></p><p>A.</p><p>Concrete is the second most used substance in the global economy, after water — and one of the world’s biggest single sources of greenhouse gas emissions. The chemical process by which cement, the key ingredient of concrete, is created results in large quantities of carbon dioxide. The UN estimates that there will be 9.8 billion people living on the planet by mid-century. They will need somewhere to live. If concrete is the only answer to the construction of new cities, then carbon emissions will soar, aggravating global warming. And so scientists have started innovating with other materials, in a scramble for alternatives to a universal commodity that has underpinned our modern life for many years.</p><p>B.</p><p>The problem with replacing concrete is that it is so very good at what it does. Chris Cheeseman, an engineering professor at Imperial College London, says the key thing to consider is the extent to which concrete is used around the world, and is likely to continue to be used. ‘Concrete is not a high-carbon product. Cement is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02ab9f09-dd5b-4067-8dfd-115070efc0b1\" data-question=\"13\">high carbon<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, but concrete is not. But it is the scale on which it is used that makes it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02ab9f09-dd5b-4067-8dfd-115070efc0b1\" data-question=\"13\">high carbon<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af2f0880-8ae1-46f0-bc95-f921d2fc3448\" data-question=\"13\">The sheer scale of manufacture is so huge<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02ab9f09-dd5b-4067-8dfd-115070efc0b1\" data-question=\"13\">that is the issue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.’</p><p>C. </p><p>Not only are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a88d0dbe-7b68-4fc5-a5ed-03fae623250c\" data-question=\"3\">the ingredients of concrete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> relatively cheap and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98dcff83-9502-4e77-b494-4a0e5f38445b\" data-question=\"3\">found in abundance in most places around the globe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, the stuff itself has marvellous properties: Portland cement, the vital component of concrete, is mouldable and pourable, but quickly sets hard. Cheeseman also notes another advantage: concrete and steel have similar thermal expansion properties, so steel can be used to reinforce concrete, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"99dbb1c8-f372-45d7-8f92-5bf4ec711fb6\" data-question=\"10\">making<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> it far stronger and more flexible as a building material than it could be on its own. According to Cheeseman, all these factors together make concrete hard to beat. ‘Concrete is amazing stuff. Making anything <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9174cba1-61a8-409a-9c00-02bb2e3a2c67\" data-question=\"10\">with similar properties<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> is going to be very <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"817a92b7-7799-4fc8-babc-ed8a22e183f8\" data-question=\"10\">difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.’</p><p>D.</p><p>A possible alternative to concrete is wood. Making buildings from wood may seem like a rather <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93fd4364-d2f5-42f4-91d4-c5c0d12c5bbd\" data-question=\"5\">medieval<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> idea, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3c86e5f-3bca-4133-a20d-8a512284303b\" data-question=\"5\">climate change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> is driving architects <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"974890bb-da3b-4d65-a082-4d94251fff62\" data-question=\"5\">to turn to treated timber as a possible resource<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. Recent years have seen the emergence of tall buildings constructed almost entirely from timber. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c8023b5-dd12-42ff-9b28-e5bddc5dbec4\" data-question=\"2\">Vancouver, Vienna and Brumunddal in Norway<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4ec6c33-6bb6-4816-9ef0-785753ba4fdb\" data-question=\"2\">are all home to constructed tall, wooden buildings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.</p><p>E.</p><p>Using wood to construct buildings, however, is not straightforward. Wood <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34157ebc-65a9-4960-a689-6e5b31d15032\" data-question=\"6\">expands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> as it absorbs moisture from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fba83ae7-e33d-43d8-b154-2f441c3e1002\" data-question=\"6\">the air<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> and is susceptible to pests, not to mention fire. But treating wood and combining it with other materials can improve its properties. Cross-laminated timber is engineered wood. An adhesive is used to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77d450c9-a4f5-4cbf-88bd-f6ceb0c670e9\" data-question=\"7\">stick layers of solid sawn timber together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, crosswise, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"25dbcb98-08a0-4fe5-ae34-7ac41ce32308\" data-question=\"7\">to form<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> building blocks. This material is light but has the strength of concrete and steel. Construction experts say that wooden buildings can be constructed at a greater speed than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68dea5ea-8a0b-43a7-b02b-ebff3fc4f7b1\" data-question=\"8\">ones of concrete and steel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"338c65ba-15ee-4622-90d9-2aa28d29b86b\" data-question=\"8\">the process, it seems, is quieter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</p><p>F.</p><p>Stora Enso is Europe’s biggest supplier of cross-laminated timber, and its vice-president Markus Mannstrom reports that the company is seeing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dbc564b0-43a2-4006-b5d1-088350f058ba\" data-question=\"4\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d9d2307-d2f3-4bc2-9aa0-ba4e0687cbab\" data-question=\"11\">increasing demand globally for building in wood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fc1532af-1468-4af2-9595-55c77c2950b2\" data-question=\"11\">climate change concerns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b7d205b-c5cd-448a-8513-652226456d42\" data-question=\"11\">key driver<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Finland, with its large forests, where Stora Enso is based, has been leading the way, but the company is seeing arise in demand for its timber products across the world, including in Asia. Of course, using timber in a building also locks away the carbon that it absorbed as it grew. But even treated wood has its limitations and only when a wider range of construction projects has been proven in practice <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f57d0f76-99a6-4a4a-a03f-9aca2161561c\" data-question=\"4\">will it be possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to see wood as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3be9648-bf0a-4664-96fa-b47b0682edce\" data-question=\"4\">a real alternative to concrete in constructing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> tall buildings.</p><p>G.</p><p>Fly ash and slag from iron ore are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87ea7cdf-4712-442b-b72d-730d91bbfca8\" data-question=\"1\">possible alternatives to cement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in a concrete mix. Fly ash, a byproduct of coal-burning power plants, can be incorporated into concrete mixes to make up as much as 15 to 30% of the cement, without harming the strength or durability of the resulting mix. Iron-ore slag, a byproduct of the iron-ore smelting process, can be used in a similar way. Their incorporation into concrete mixes has the potential to reduce greenhouse gas emissions.</p><p>But Anna Surgenor, of the UK’s Green Building Council, notes that although these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54800d81-857c-4ed0-8921-c82d91115b0e\" data-question=\"9\">waste products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> can save carbon in the concrete mix, their use is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46d61890-a5c5-43ab-afdc-431d407498fd\" data-question=\"9\">not always straightforward<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. ‘It’s possible to replace the cement content in concrete with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54800d81-857c-4ed0-8921-c82d91115b0e\" data-question=\"9\">waste products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to lower the overall carbon impact. But there are several calculations that need to be considered across | the entire life cycle of the building — these include factoring in where these materials are being shipped from. If they are transported over long distances, using fossil fuels, the use of alternative materials might not make sense from an overall carbon reduction perspective.’</p><p>H.</p><p>While these technologies are all promising ideas, they are either unproven or based on materials that are not abundant. In their overview of innovation in the concrete industry, Felix Preston and Johanna Lehne of the UK’s Royal Institute of International Affairs reached the conclusion that, ‘Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4161d2f2-6141-45c4-977e-7b86e2e7ad4a\" data-question=\"12\">novel cements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> have been discussed for more than a decade within the research community, without breaking through. At present, these alternatives are rarely as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c44d116b-d579-4d07-8bc4-da87a4abb00b\" data-question=\"12\">cost-effective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> as conventional cement, and they face raw-material shortages and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7537dcd9-3d0d-4ed0-83d2-f2498bb20e1c\" data-question=\"12\">resistance from customers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>.’</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 65\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Reading Passage 1 has eight sections, A-H.<br>Which section contains the following information?<br>Write the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 1—4 on your answer sheet.</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145165\" id=\"question-wrapper-145165\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of the industrial processes that create <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87ea7cdf-4712-442b-b72d-730d91bbfca8\" data-question=\"1\">potential raw materials<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> for concrete </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145166\" id=\"question-wrapper-145166\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c8023b5-dd12-42ff-9b28-e5bddc5dbec4\" data-question=\"2\">various locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4ec6c33-6bb6-4816-9ef0-785753ba4fdb\" data-question=\"2\">where high-rise wooden buildings can be found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145167\" id=\"question-wrapper-145167\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an indication of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98dcff83-9502-4e77-b494-4a0e5f38445b\" data-question=\"3\">widely available<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a88d0dbe-7b68-4fc5-a5ed-03fae623250c\" data-question=\"3\">the raw materials of concrete<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> are </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145168\" id=\"question-wrapper-145168\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f57d0f76-99a6-4a4a-a03f-9aca2161561c\" data-question=\"4\">belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dbc564b0-43a2-4006-b5d1-088350f058ba\" data-question=\"4\">more high-rise wooden buildings are needed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> before wood <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a799f55-326c-4381-9588-8cd1786627d2\" data-question=\"4\">can be regarded as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3be9648-bf0a-4664-96fa-b47b0682edce\" data-question=\"4\">a viable construction material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 65\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the summary below.<br>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 5—8 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>Making buildings with wood</strong></p><p style=\"margin-right:43px\">Wood is a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93fd4364-d2f5-42f4-91d4-c5c0d12c5bbd\" data-question=\"5\">traditional<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> building material, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3c86e5f-3bca-4133-a20d-8a512284303b\" data-question=\"5\">current environmental concerns<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> are encouraging <strong>5............................. </strong>to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"974890bb-da3b-4d65-a082-4d94251fff62\" data-question=\"5\">use wood in modern construction projects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. Using wood, however, has its challenges. For example, as <strong>6............................ </strong><strong> </strong>in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fba83ae7-e33d-43d8-b154-2f441c3e1002\" data-question=\"6\">the atmosphere<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> enters wood, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34157ebc-65a9-4960-a689-6e5b31d15032\" data-question=\"6\">increases in size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. In addition, wood is prone to pests and the risk of fire is greater. However, wood can be turned into a better construction material if it is treated and combined with other materials. In one process, <strong>7....................... </strong><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"77d450c9-a4f5-4cbf-88bd-f6ceb0c670e9\" data-question=\"7\">of solid wood are glued together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> to create building blocks. These blocks are lighter than concrete and steel but equal them in strength. Experts say that wooden buildings are an improvement on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68dea5ea-8a0b-43a7-b02b-ebff3fc4f7b1\" data-question=\"8\">those made of concrete and steel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> in terms of the <strong>8.............................. </strong>with which they can be constructed and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"338c65ba-15ee-4622-90d9-2aa28d29b86b\" data-question=\"8\">how much noise is generated by the process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145169\" id=\"question-wrapper-145169\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ARCHITECTS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145170\" id=\"question-wrapper-145170\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MOISTURE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145171\" id=\"question-wrapper-145171\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LAYERS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145172\" id=\"question-wrapper-145172\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPEED</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 66\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Look at the following statements (Questions 9-13) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A, B, C or D.<br>Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.<br>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 66\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 66\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><ul><li>A. Chris Cheeseman</li><li>B. Markus Mannstrom</li><li>C. Anna Surgenor</li><li>D. Felix Preston and Johanna Lehne</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145173\" id=\"question-wrapper-145173\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The environmental advantage of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54800d81-857c-4ed0-8921-c82d91115b0e\" data-question=\"9\">cement alternatives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46d61890-a5c5-43ab-afdc-431d407498fd\" data-question=\"9\">not be as great<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> as initially assumed. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145174\" id=\"question-wrapper-145174\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It would be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"817a92b7-7799-4fc8-babc-ed8a22e183f8\" data-question=\"10\">hard<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to create a construction alternative to concrete that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9174cba1-61a8-409a-9c00-02bb2e3a2c67\" data-question=\"10\">offers so many comparable benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145175\" id=\"question-wrapper-145175\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fc1532af-1468-4af2-9595-55c77c2950b2\" data-question=\"11\">Worries about the environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b7d205b-c5cd-448a-8513-652226456d42\" data-question=\"11\">led to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d9d2307-d2f3-4bc2-9aa0-ba4e0687cbab\" data-question=\"11\">increased interest in wood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> as a construction material. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145176\" id=\"question-wrapper-145176\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c44d116b-d579-4d07-8bc4-da87a4abb00b\" data-question=\"12\">Expense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> has beena factor in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7537dcd9-3d0d-4ed0-83d2-f2498bb20e1c\" data-question=\"12\">negative response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> to the development of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4161d2f2-6141-45c4-977e-7b86e2e7ad4a\" data-question=\"12\">new cements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145177\" id=\"question-wrapper-145177\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"02ab9f09-dd5b-4067-8dfd-115070efc0b1\" data-question=\"13\">environmental damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> caused by concrete is due to it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af2f0880-8ae1-46f0-bc95-f921d2fc3448\" data-question=\"13\">being produced in large quantities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"02ab9f09-dd5b-4067-8dfd-115070efc0b1","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"environmental damage","passagePhrase":"high carbon ... high carbon ... that is the issue"},{"uid":"af2f0880-8ae1-46f0-bc95-f921d2fc3448","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"being produced in large quantities","passagePhrase":"The sheer scale of manufacture is so huge"},{"uid":"a88d0dbe-7b68-4fc5-a5ed-03fae623250c","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"the raw materials of concrete","passagePhrase":"the ingredients of concrete"},{"uid":"98dcff83-9502-4e77-b494-4a0e5f38445b","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"widely available","passagePhrase":"found in abundance in most places around the globe"},{"uid":"99dbb1c8-f372-45d7-8f92-5bf4ec711fb6","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"making"},{"uid":"9174cba1-61a8-409a-9c00-02bb2e3a2c67","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"offers so many comparable benefits","passagePhrase":"with similar properties"},{"uid":"817a92b7-7799-4fc8-babc-ed8a22e183f8","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"hard","passagePhrase":"difficult"},{"uid":"93fd4364-d2f5-42f4-91d4-c5c0d12c5bbd","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"traditional","passagePhrase":"medieval"},{"uid":"a3c86e5f-3bca-4133-a20d-8a512284303b","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"current environmental concerns","passagePhrase":"climate change"},{"uid":"974890bb-da3b-4d65-a082-4d94251fff62","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"use wood in modern construction projects","passagePhrase":"to turn to treated timber as a possible resource"},{"uid":"9c8023b5-dd12-42ff-9b28-e5bddc5dbec4","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"various locations","passagePhrase":"Vancouver, Vienna and Brumunddal in Norway"},{"uid":"d4ec6c33-6bb6-4816-9ef0-785753ba4fdb","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"where high-rise wooden buildings can be found","passagePhrase":"are all home to constructed tall, wooden buildings"},{"uid":"34157ebc-65a9-4960-a689-6e5b31d15032","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"increases in size","passagePhrase":"expands"},{"uid":"fba83ae7-e33d-43d8-b154-2f441c3e1002","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"the atmosphere","passagePhrase":"the air"},{"uid":"77d450c9-a4f5-4cbf-88bd-f6ceb0c670e9","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"of solid wood are glued together","passagePhrase":"stick layers of solid sawn timber together"},{"uid":"25dbcb98-08a0-4fe5-ae34-7ac41ce32308","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"to form"},{"uid":"68dea5ea-8a0b-43a7-b02b-ebff3fc4f7b1","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"those made of concrete and steel","passagePhrase":"ones of concrete and steel"},{"uid":"338c65ba-15ee-4622-90d9-2aa28d29b86b","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"how much noise is generated by the process","passagePhrase":"the process, it seems, is quieter"},{"uid":"dbc564b0-43a2-4006-b5d1-088350f058ba","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"more high-rise wooden buildings are needed","passagePhrase":"increasing demand globally for building in wood"},{"uid":"1d9d2307-d2f3-4bc2-9aa0-ba4e0687cbab","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"increased interest in wood","passagePhrase":"increasing demand globally for building in wood"},{"uid":"fc1532af-1468-4af2-9595-55c77c2950b2","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"Worries about the environment","passagePhrase":"climate change concerns"},{"uid":"2b7d205b-c5cd-448a-8513-652226456d42","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"led to","passagePhrase":"key driver"},{"uid":"f57d0f76-99a6-4a4a-a03f-9aca2161561c","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"belief","passagePhrase":"will it be possible"},{"uid":"a3be9648-bf0a-4664-96fa-b47b0682edce","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"a viable construction material","passagePhrase":"a real alternative to concrete in constructing"},{"uid":"87ea7cdf-4712-442b-b72d-730d91bbfca8","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"potential raw materials","passagePhrase":"possible alternatives to cement"},{"uid":"54800d81-857c-4ed0-8921-c82d91115b0e","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"cement alternatives","passagePhrase":"waste products ... waste products"},{"uid":"46d61890-a5c5-43ab-afdc-431d407498fd","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"not be as great","passagePhrase":"not always straightforward"},{"uid":"4161d2f2-6141-45c4-977e-7b86e2e7ad4a","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"new cements","passagePhrase":"novel cements"},{"uid":"c44d116b-d579-4d07-8bc4-da87a4abb00b","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Expense","passagePhrase":"cost-effective"},{"uid":"7537dcd9-3d0d-4ed0-83d2-f2498bb20e1c","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"negative response","passagePhrase":"resistance from customers"},{"uid":"9a799f55-326c-4381-9588-8cd1786627d2","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"can be regarded as","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_290":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3>The steam car</h3><p><em>The successes and failures of the Doble brothers and their steam cars</em></p><p>A.</p><p>When primitive automobiles first began to appear in the 1800s, their engines were based on steam power. Steam had already enjoyed a long and successful career in the railways, so it was only natural that the technology evolved into a miniaturized version which was separate from the trains. But these early cars <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15afd115-9826-4896-901b-0aede6465a3a\" data-question=\"14\">inherited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> steam’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0980563-0bd1-402d-8786-04dde142781f\" data-question=\"14\">weaknesses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> along with its <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5550bbed-f7ba-4584-bd02-d3e862ef7312\" data-question=\"14\">strengths<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. The boilers had to be lit by hand, and they required about twenty minutes to build up pressure before they could be driven. Furthermore, their water reservoirs only lasted for about thirty miles before needing replenishment. Despite such <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0980563-0bd1-402d-8786-04dde142781f\" data-question=\"14\">shortcomings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, these newly designed self-propelled carriages offered quick transportation, and by the early 1900s it was not uncommon to see such machines shuttling wealthy citizens around town.</p><p>B.</p><p>But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62fd74dc-abf1-44b5-96e9-894050065867\" data-question=\"21\">the glory days<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> of steam cars were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"861feb32-2551-4ddf-ad4f-302b3213d67b\" data-question=\"21\">few<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. A new technology called the Internal Combustion Engine <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c28c2fc4-3beb-4f9f-b953-053c353671c4\" data-question=\"15\">soon appeared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>, which offered the ability to drive down the road just moments after starting up. At first, these noisy gasoline cars were unpopular because they were more complicated to operate and they had difficult hand-crank starters, which were known to break arms when the engines backfired. But in 1912 General Motors introduced the electric starter, and over the following few years <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"385ba854-8758-487b-8dcf-84c0bade6d53\" data-question=\"15\">steam power was gradually phased out<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</p><p>C.</p><p>Even as the market was declining, four brothers made one last effort to rekindle the technology. Between 1906 and 1909, while still attending high school, Abner Doble and his three brothers built their first steam car in their parents’ basement. It comprised parts taken from a wrecked early steam car but reconfigured to drive an engine of their own design. Though it did not run well, the Doble brothers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43e61097-c533-4a29-8f35-f8c8dcb86407\" data-question=\"22\">went on to build a second and third prototype<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> in the following years. Though the Doble boys’ third prototype, nicknamed the Model B, still lacked the convenience of an internal combustion engine, it drew the attention of automobile trade magazines due to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f948692b-4729-4cdf-a9b6-5e70941ed621\" data-question=\"22\">its numerous improvements over previous steam cars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. . The Model B proved to be superior to gasoline automobiles in many ways. Its high-pressure steam drove the engine pistons in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d199d946-44ef-442c-95af-5c598b690a82\" data-question=\"16\">virtual silence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46ed15ee-a050-46ee-b853-5f7471dafc29\" data-question=\"16\">in contrast to clattering gas engines which emitted the aroma of burned hydrocarbons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. Perhaps most impressively, the Model B was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"178499e8-6226-469f-8893-fb9708cd32c3\" data-question=\"16\">amazingly swift<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. It could accelerate from zero to sixty miles per hour in just fifteen seconds, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c250907c-d4a9-4e08-a8e5-33a2f3df0ea5\" data-question=\"16\">a feat described as ‘remarkable acceleration’ by Automobile magazine<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> in 1914.</p><p>D.</p><p>The following year Abner Doble drove the Model B from Massachusetts to Detroit in order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa9199ec-a702-4c18-bd70-c1580cc30448\" data-question=\"23\">seek investment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> in his automobile design, which he used to open the General Engineering Company. He and his brothers immediately began working on the Model C, which was intended to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3900e5d6-c903-4a7c-9980-733ac21b81be\" data-question=\"17\">expand upon the innovations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of the Model B. The brothers added features such as a key-based ignition in the cabin, eliminating the need for the operator to manually<br>ignite the boiler. With these <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3900e5d6-c903-4a7c-9980-733ac21b81be\" data-question=\"17\">enhancements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, the Dobles’ new car company promised a steam vehicle which would provide all of the convenience of a gasoline car, but with much greater speed, much simpler driving controls, and a virtually silent powerplant. By the following April, the General Engineering Company had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce01d656-6134-4c98-b240-d5f616fcd94a\" data-question=\"17\">received 5,390 deposits for Doble Detroits, which were scheduled for delivery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> in early 1918.</p><p>E.</p><p>Later that year Abner Doble delivered <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11e2fe84-7e65-48e0-9379-5dd4d2f8f53b\" data-question=\"18\">unhappy news<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to those eagerly awaiting the delivery of their modern new cars. Those <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"01667ab5-a8dc-4c12-876e-992a9a765d40\" data-question=\"18\">buyers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> who received the handful of completed cars complained that the vehicles were sluggish and erratic, sometimes going in reverse when they should go forward. The new engine design, though innovative, was still plagued with serious glitches.</p><p>F.</p><p>The brothers made one final attempt to produce a viable steam automobile. In early 1924, the Doble brothers shipped a Model E to New York City to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4c03e10-0ee5-4393-9f38-df2e4155fb7f\" data-question=\"19\">be road-tested<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> by the Automobile Club of America. After sitting overnight in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe49194a-71c4-4742-a4ce-f20789bf6fe5\" data-question=\"19\">freezing temperatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, the car was pushed out into the road and left to sit for over an hour in the frosty morning air. At the turn of the key, the boiler lit and reached its operating pressure inside of forty seconds. As they drove the test vehicle further, they found that its evenly distributed weight lent it surprisingly good handling, even though it was so heavy. As <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"786d3f1d-8558-488f-b202-bbf044dc49a0\" data-question=\"24\">the new Doble steamer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> was further developed and tested, its maximum speed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82ac5c85-3243-41ee-a4cb-1e46d84c37a2\" data-question=\"24\">was pushed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> over a hundred miles per hour, and it achieved about fifteen miles per gallon of kerosene with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d644828c-46e0-4f2f-9eae-5472b0d78084\" data-question=\"24\">negligible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> emissions.</p><p>G.</p><p>Sadly, the Dobles’ brilliant steam car never was a financial success. Priced at around $18,000 in 1924, it was popular only among the very wealthy. Plus, it is said that no two Model Es were quite the same, because Abner Doble tinkered endlessly with the design. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a613371e-f53e-4c67-ae13-40410264a61a\" data-question=\"25\">By the time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> the company <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f5662344-dc25-4149-b1ce-19c81764e087\" data-question=\"25\">folded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> in 1931, fewer than fifty of the amazing Model E steam cars had been produced. For his whole career, until his death in 1961, Abner Doble remained adamant that steam-powered automobiles were at least equal to gasoline cars, if not superior. Given the evidence, he may have been right. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"646f8196-c4be-474f-bf8d-8dac48268d85\" data-question=\"26\">Many of the Model E Dobles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> which have survived are still in good working condition, some having been driven over half a million miles <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4fe19409-c69f-4215-934d-ad6666925d38\" data-question=\"26\">with only normal maintenance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. Astonishingly, an unmodified Doble Model E runs clean enough to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa867081-22f0-4980-81d2-155e98e6eccd\" data-question=\"26\">pass<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> the emissions laws in California today, and they are pretty strict. It is true that the technology poses some difficult problems, but you cannot help but wonder how efficient a steam car might be with the benefit of modern materials and computers. Under <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8abb0d47-d085-42c6-8ba6-ac3a0805a2ae\" data-question=\"20\">the current pressure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to improve automotive performance and reduce emissions, it is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b90c92b5-2acd-4fd2-b1ce-0d4ddcd8d5fe\" data-question=\"20\">not unthinkable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> that the steam car may rise again.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 67\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Questions 14-20<br>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-G.<br>Choose the correct heading for each paragraph from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i-viii, in boxes 14—20 on your answer sheet.</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 67\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>List of Headings</p><ul><li>i A period in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe49194a-71c4-4742-a4ce-f20789bf6fe5\" data-question=\"19\">cold conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> before the technology <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4c03e10-0ee5-4393-9f38-df2e4155fb7f\" data-question=\"19\">is assessed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span></li><li>ii Marketing issues lead to failure</li><li>iii <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5550bbed-f7ba-4584-bd02-d3e862ef7312\" data-question=\"14\">Good<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0980563-0bd1-402d-8786-04dde142781f\" data-question=\"14\">bad aspects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of steam technology <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15afd115-9826-4896-901b-0aede6465a3a\" data-question=\"14\">are passed on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></li><li>iv A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b90c92b5-2acd-4fd2-b1ce-0d4ddcd8d5fe\" data-question=\"20\">possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> solution to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8abb0d47-d085-42c6-8ba6-ac3a0805a2ae\" data-question=\"20\">the issues of today<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span></li><li>v <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3900e5d6-c903-4a7c-9980-733ac21b81be\" data-question=\"17\">Further improvements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> lead to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce01d656-6134-4c98-b240-d5f616fcd94a\" data-question=\"17\">commercial orders<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></li><li>vi <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c250907c-d4a9-4e08-a8e5-33a2f3df0ea5\" data-question=\"16\">Positive publicity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> at last for this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d199d946-44ef-442c-95af-5c598b690a82\" data-question=\"16\">quiet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46ed15ee-a050-46ee-b853-5f7471dafc29\" data-question=\"16\">clean,<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"178499e8-6226-469f-8893-fb9708cd32c3\" data-question=\"16\">fast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> vehicle</li><li>vii <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11e2fe84-7e65-48e0-9379-5dd4d2f8f53b\" data-question=\"18\">A disappointing outcome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"01667ab5-a8dc-4c12-876e-992a9a765d40\" data-question=\"18\">customers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></li><li>viii A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"385ba854-8758-487b-8dcf-84c0bade6d53\" data-question=\"15\">better option than the steam car<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c28c2fc4-3beb-4f9f-b953-053c353671c4\" data-question=\"15\">arises<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145178\" id=\"question-wrapper-145178\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145179\" id=\"question-wrapper-145179\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VIII</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145180\" id=\"question-wrapper-145180\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145181\" id=\"question-wrapper-145181\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145182\" id=\"question-wrapper-145182\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145183\" id=\"question-wrapper-145183\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145184\" id=\"question-wrapper-145184\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph G </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 70\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 21—23 on your answer sheet.</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145185\" id=\"question-wrapper-145185\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does the writer make about the steam car in Paragraph B? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62fd74dc-abf1-44b5-96e9-894050065867\" data-question=\"21\">Its success<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"861feb32-2551-4ddf-ad4f-302b3213d67b\" data-question=\"21\">short-lived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.</li> <li>B. Not enough cars were made.</li> <li>C. Car companies found them hard to sell.</li> <li>D. People found them hard to drive.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145186\" id=\"question-wrapper-145186\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When building their first steam car, the Doble brothers </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. constructed all the parts themselves.</li> <li>B. made written notes at each stage of the construction.</li> <li>C. needed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43e61097-c533-4a29-8f35-f8c8dcb86407\" data-question=\"22\">several attempts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> to achieve <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f948692b-4729-4cdf-a9b6-5e70941ed621\" data-question=\"22\">a competitive model<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</li> <li>D. sought the advice of experienced people in the car industry.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145187\" id=\"question-wrapper-145187\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In order to produce the Model C, the Doble brothers </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. moved production to a different city.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa9199ec-a702-4c18-bd70-c1580cc30448\" data-question=\"23\">raised financial capital<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</li> <li>C. employed an additional worker.</li> <li>D. abandoned their earlier designs.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 71\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the summary below.</p><p>Choose ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24—26 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>The Model E</strong></p><p style=\"margin-right:5px\">The Model E was road-tested in 1924 by the Automobile Club of America. They found it easy to drive, despite its weight, and it impressed the spectators. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"786d3f1d-8558-488f-b202-bbf044dc49a0\" data-question=\"24\">A later version of the Model E<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> raised its<strong> 24 </strong>..........................<strong>,</strong> while keeping its emissions <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d644828c-46e0-4f2f-9eae-5472b0d78084\" data-question=\"24\">extremely low<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. The steam car was too expensive for many people and its design was constantly being altered. Under<strong> 25</strong> .......................... cars were produced <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a613371e-f53e-4c67-ae13-40410264a61a\" data-question=\"25\">before<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> the company <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f5662344-dc25-4149-b1ce-19c81764e087\" data-question=\"25\">went out of business<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. However, even today, there are Model Es on the road in the US. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"646f8196-c4be-474f-bf8d-8dac48268d85\" data-question=\"26\">They<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4fe19409-c69f-4215-934d-ad6666925d38\" data-question=\"26\">straightforward to maintain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, and they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa867081-22f0-4980-81d2-155e98e6eccd\" data-question=\"26\">satisfy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> California's <strong>26</strong>.............................. emissions laws. Perhaps today's technology and materials would help us revive the steam car.</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145188\" id=\"question-wrapper-145188\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPEED</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145189\" id=\"question-wrapper-145189\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FIFTY/50 (STEAM)</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145190\" id=\"question-wrapper-145190\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STRICT</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"15afd115-9826-4896-901b-0aede6465a3a","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"are passed on","passagePhrase":"inherited"},{"uid":"f0980563-0bd1-402d-8786-04dde142781f","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"bad aspects","passagePhrase":"weaknesses ... shortcomings"},{"uid":"5550bbed-f7ba-4584-bd02-d3e862ef7312","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Good","passagePhrase":"strengths"},{"uid":"62fd74dc-abf1-44b5-96e9-894050065867","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Its success","passagePhrase":"the glory days"},{"uid":"861feb32-2551-4ddf-ad4f-302b3213d67b","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"short-lived","passagePhrase":"few"},{"uid":"c28c2fc4-3beb-4f9f-b953-053c353671c4","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"arises","passagePhrase":"soon appeared"},{"uid":"385ba854-8758-487b-8dcf-84c0bade6d53","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"better option than the steam car","passagePhrase":"steam power was gradually phased out"},{"uid":"43e61097-c533-4a29-8f35-f8c8dcb86407","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"several attempts","passagePhrase":"went on to build a second and third prototype"},{"uid":"f948692b-4729-4cdf-a9b6-5e70941ed621","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"a competitive model","passagePhrase":"its numerous improvements over previous steam cars"},{"uid":"d199d946-44ef-442c-95af-5c598b690a82","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"quiet","passagePhrase":"virtual silence"},{"uid":"46ed15ee-a050-46ee-b853-5f7471dafc29","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"clean,","passagePhrase":"in contrast to clattering gas engines which emitted the aroma of burned hydrocarbons"},{"uid":"178499e8-6226-469f-8893-fb9708cd32c3","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"fast","passagePhrase":"amazingly swift"},{"uid":"c250907c-d4a9-4e08-a8e5-33a2f3df0ea5","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Positive publicity","passagePhrase":"a feat described as ‘remarkable acceleration’ by Automobile magazine"},{"uid":"fa9199ec-a702-4c18-bd70-c1580cc30448","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"raised financial capital","passagePhrase":"seek investment"},{"uid":"3900e5d6-c903-4a7c-9980-733ac21b81be","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Further improvements","passagePhrase":"expand upon the innovations ... enhancements"},{"uid":"ce01d656-6134-4c98-b240-d5f616fcd94a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"commercial orders","passagePhrase":"received 5,390 deposits for Doble Detroits, which were scheduled for delivery"},{"uid":"11e2fe84-7e65-48e0-9379-5dd4d2f8f53b","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"A disappointing outcome","passagePhrase":"unhappy news"},{"uid":"01667ab5-a8dc-4c12-876e-992a9a765d40","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"customers","passagePhrase":"buyers"},{"uid":"d4c03e10-0ee5-4393-9f38-df2e4155fb7f","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"is assessed","passagePhrase":"be road-tested"},{"uid":"fe49194a-71c4-4742-a4ce-f20789bf6fe5","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"cold conditions","passagePhrase":"freezing temperatures"},{"uid":"786d3f1d-8558-488f-b202-bbf044dc49a0","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"A later version of the Model E","passagePhrase":"the new Doble steamer"},{"uid":"82ac5c85-3243-41ee-a4cb-1e46d84c37a2","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"was pushed to"},{"uid":"d644828c-46e0-4f2f-9eae-5472b0d78084","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"extremely low","passagePhrase":"negligible"},{"uid":"a613371e-f53e-4c67-ae13-40410264a61a","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"before","passagePhrase":"By the time"},{"uid":"f5662344-dc25-4149-b1ce-19c81764e087","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"went out of business","passagePhrase":"folded"},{"uid":"646f8196-c4be-474f-bf8d-8dac48268d85","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"They","passagePhrase":"Many of the Model E Dobles"},{"uid":"4fe19409-c69f-4215-934d-ad6666925d38","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"straightforward to maintain","passagePhrase":"with only normal maintenance"},{"uid":"fa867081-22f0-4980-81d2-155e98e6eccd","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"satisfy","passagePhrase":"pass"},{"uid":"8abb0d47-d085-42c6-8ba6-ac3a0805a2ae","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"the issues of today","passagePhrase":"the current pressure"},{"uid":"b90c92b5-2acd-4fd2-b1ce-0d4ddcd8d5fe","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"possible","passagePhrase":"not unthinkable"}]},"reading_u2_291":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3>The case for mixed-ability classes</h3><p>Picture this scene. It’s an English literature lesson in a UK school, and the teacher has just read an extract from Shakespeare’s Romeo and Juliet with a class of 15-year-olds. He’s given some of the students copies of No Fear Shakespeare, a kid-friendly translation of the original. For three students, even these literacy demands are beyond them. Another girl simply can’t focus and he gives her pens and paper to draw with. The teacher can ask the No Fear group to identify the key characters and maybe provide a tentative plot summary. He can ask most of the class about character development, and five of them might be able to support their statements with textual evidence. Now two curious students are wondering whether Shakespeare advocates living a life of moderation or one of passionate engagement.</p><p>As a teacher myself, I’d think my lesson would be going rather well if the discussion went as described above. But wouldn’t this kind of class work better if there weren’t such a huge gap between the top and the bottom? If we put all the kids who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83dc1df5-ed64-4ccf-ae3a-fbb7607ee1e7\" data-question=\"27\">needed literacy support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> into one class, and all the students who want to discuss <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83dc1df5-ed64-4ccf-ae3a-fbb7607ee1e7\" data-question=\"27\">the virtue of moderation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> into another?</p><p>The practice of ‘streaming’, or ‘tracking’, involves separating students into classes depending on their diagnosed levels of attainment. At a macro level, it requires the establishment of academically selective schools for the brightest students, and comprehensive schools for the rest. Within schools, it means selecting students into a ‘stream’ of general ability, or ‘sets’ of subject- specific ability. The practice is intuitively <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93666256-23c3-426a-bd54-a934c54a981b\" data-question=\"28\">appealing to almost every stakeholder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</p><p>I have heard the mixed-ability model attacked by way of analogy: a group hike. The fittest in the group take the lead and set a brisk pace, only to have to stop and wait every 20 minutes. This is frustrating, and their enthusiasm wanes. Meanwhile, the slowest ones are not only embarrassed but physically struggling to keep up. What’s worse, they never get a long enough break. They honestly just want to quit. Hiking, they feel, is not for them.</p><p>Mixed-ability classes bore students, frustrate parents and burn out teachers. The brightest ones will never summit Mount Qomolangma, and the stragglers won’t enjoy the lovely stroll in the park they are perhaps more suited to. Individuals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e557613-4cda-4f1e-a8ed-456a5fa17175\" data-question=\"29\">suffer at the demands of the collective, mediocrity prevails<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. So: is learning like hiking?</p><p>The current pedagogical paradigm is arguably that of constructivism, which emerged out of the work of psychologist Lev Vygotsky. In the 1930s, Vygotsky <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4cd0934f-b3be-428a-be0e-9e302c5eb785\" data-question=\"36\">emphasised the importance of targeting a student’s specific ‘zone of proximal development’<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> (ZPD). This is the gap between what they can achieve only with support — <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b645bbe2-f516-45ac-b67f-e025c1ca296c\" data-question=\"30\">teachers, textbooks, worked examples, parents and so on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> — and what they can achieve independently. The purpose of teaching is to provide and then gradually remove this ‘scaffolding’ until they are autonomous. If we accept this model, it follows that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d8b3e62-ea7e-4c0f-bf30-6b27835a0f71\" data-question=\"35\">streaming students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> with similar ZPDs would be an efficient and effective solution. And that forcing everyone on the same hike — regardless of aptitude — would be madness.</p><p>Despite all this, there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b2930dc9-88e3-4128-be72-6e061e0b5ca9\" data-question=\"31\">limited empirical evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> to suggest that streaming <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa5aeaa1-79a8-47d4-a1ce-ad32ae2d0b2a\" data-question=\"31\">results in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"754d2c5b-3a51-4442-84fa-8d2ce95eb90c\" data-question=\"31\">better outcomes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> for students. Professor John Hattie, director of the Melbourne Education Research Institute, notes that ‘tracking has minimal effects on learning outcomes’. What is more, streaming appears to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15fc6c62-be7e-4a4a-9dbd-cc8645c7e9ea\" data-question=\"32\">significantly ' — and negatively — affect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> those students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0881fc2c-1f05-4950-8bf9-f1fcda68aa3a\" data-question=\"32\">assigned to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28b90f1b-1451-440a-9692-41d169defdaa\" data-question=\"32\">lowest sets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. These students tend to have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4f7dd11-a00c-47a5-82d4-6bbe55079f31\" data-question=\"33\">much higher representation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9312a816-62d9-4f68-bd6d-1686504db905\" data-question=\"33\">low socioeconomic class<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. Less significant is the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43aff8bd-9ca1-42ed-91ea-a6879e845ecc\" data-question=\"34\">small benefit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> for those <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d12b6d62-eff4-455a-9a03-a4665478646f\" data-question=\"34\">lucky clever students<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> in the higher sets. The overall result is that the smart stay smart and the dumb get dumber, further entrenching the social divide.</p><p>In the latest update of Hattie’s influential meta-analysis of factors influencing student achievement, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e7f0164d-a467-4058-b9b2-6efdfcb68002\" data-question=\"35\">one of the most significant factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> is the teachers’ estimate of achievement. Streaming students by diagnosed achievement automatically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"beb5bc71-e55d-4011-a192-ff766a0acb6c\" data-question=\"35\">limits what the teacher feels the student is capable of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. Meanwhile, in a mixed environment, teachers’ estimates need to be more diverse and flexible.</p><p>While streaming might seem to help teachers effectively target a student’s ZPD, it can underestimate the importance of peer-to-peer learning. A crucial aspect of constructivist theory is the role of the MKO — ‘more- knowledgeable other’ — in knowledge construction. While teachers are traditionally the MKOs in classrooms, the value of knowledgeable student peers must not go unrecognised either.</p><p>I find it amazing to watch students get over an idea to their peers in ways that I would never think of. They operate with different language tools and different social tools from teachers and, having just learnt it themselves, they possess similar cognitive structures to their struggling classmates. There is also something <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43155fb6-6d22-4de8-9527-46bd7a9d1e18\" data-question=\"38\">exciting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"913c21c9-76e5-4c2c-b5ac-2bc8b95288f6\" data-question=\"38\">passing on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> skills and knowledge that you yourself <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b969779-5d14-49a3-ad97-c6322fbb0f22\" data-question=\"38\">have just mastered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> — a certain pride and zeal, a certain freshness to the interaction between ‘teacher’ and ‘learner’ that is often lost by the expert for whom the steps are obvious and the joy of discovery forgotten.</p><p>Having a variety of different abilities in a collaborative learning environment provides valuable resources for helping students meet their learning needs, not to mention improving their communication and social skills. And today, more than ever, we need <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"36e620eb-c09d-40ea-8859-8cdef556a03f\" data-question=\"39\">the many to flourish — not suffer at the expense of a few bright stars<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. Once a year, I go on a hike with my class, a mixed bunch of students. It is challenging. The fittest students realise they need to encourage the reluctant. There are lookouts who report back, and extra items to carry for others. We make it — together.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 74\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145191\" id=\"question-wrapper-145191\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer describes the Romeo and Juliet lesson in order to demonstrate </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. how few students are interested in literature.</li> <li>B. how a teacher handles <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83dc1df5-ed64-4ccf-ae3a-fbb7607ee1e7\" data-question=\"27\">a range of learning needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>C. how unsuitable Shakespeare is for most teenagers.</li> <li>D. how weaker students can disrupt their classmates’ learning.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145192\" id=\"question-wrapper-145192\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer say about streaming in the third paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93666256-23c3-426a-bd54-a934c54a981b\" data-question=\"28\">a very broad appeal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>B. It favours cleverer students.</li> <li>C. It is relatively simple to implement.</li> <li>D. It works better in some schools than others.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145193\" id=\"question-wrapper-145193\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What idea is suggested by the reference to Mount Qomolangma in the fifth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. students following unsuitable paths</li> <li>B. students attempting interesting tasks</li> <li>C. students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e557613-4cda-4f1e-a8ed-456a5fa17175\" data-question=\"29\">not achieving their full potential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></li> <li>D. students not being aware of their limitations</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145194\" id=\"question-wrapper-145194\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the word ‘scaffolding’ in the sixth paragraph refer to? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the factors which prevent a student from learning effectively</li> <li>B. the environment where most of a student’s learning takes place</li> <li>C. the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b645bbe2-f516-45ac-b67f-e025c1ca296c\" data-question=\"30\">assistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> given to a student in their initial stages of learning</li> <li>D. the setting of appropriate learning targets for a student's aptitude</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 75\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the summary using the list of phrases, A-I, below.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-I, in boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet.</p><div class=\"column\"><ul><li>A wrong classes</li><li>B <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"beb5bc71-e55d-4011-a192-ff766a0acb6c\" data-question=\"35\">lower expectations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></li><li>C average learners</li><li>D <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28b90f1b-1451-440a-9692-41d169defdaa\" data-question=\"32\">bottom sets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></li><li>E <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d12b6d62-eff4-455a-9a03-a4665478646f\" data-question=\"34\">brightest pupils<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span></li><li>F <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9312a816-62d9-4f68-bd6d-1686504db905\" data-question=\"33\">disadvantaged backgrounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></li><li>G weaker students</li><li>H <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"754d2c5b-3a51-4442-84fa-8d2ce95eb90c\" data-question=\"31\">higher achievements<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></li><li>I positive impressions</li></ul><p><strong>Is streaming effective?</strong></p></div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 75\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>According to Professor John Hattie of the Melbourne Education Research Institute, there is very <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b2930dc9-88e3-4128-be72-6e061e0b5ca9\" data-question=\"31\">little indication<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> that streaming <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa5aeaa1-79a8-47d4-a1ce-ad32ae2d0b2a\" data-question=\"31\">leads to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <strong>31 ........................... </strong>He points out that, in schools which use streaming, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15fc6c62-be7e-4a4a-9dbd-cc8645c7e9ea\" data-question=\"32\">the most significant impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> is on those students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0881fc2c-1f05-4950-8bf9-f1fcda68aa3a\" data-question=\"32\">placed in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> the <strong>32.............................. , </strong>especially where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4f7dd11-a00c-47a5-82d4-6bbe55079f31\" data-question=\"33\">a large proportion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> of them have <strong>33................................. </strong>Meanwhile, for the <strong>34.............................. </strong><strong>, </strong>there appears to be only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43aff8bd-9ca1-42ed-91ea-a6879e845ecc\" data-question=\"34\">minimal advantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e7f0164d-a467-4058-b9b2-6efdfcb68002\" data-question=\"35\">A further issue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> is that teachers tend to have <strong>35.............................. </strong>of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d8b3e62-ea7e-4c0f-bf30-6b27835a0f71\" data-question=\"35\">students in streamed groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145195\" id=\"question-wrapper-145195\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145196\" id=\"question-wrapper-145196\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145197\" id=\"question-wrapper-145197\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145198\" id=\"question-wrapper-145198\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145199\" id=\"question-wrapper-145199\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 76\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write</p><p>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer<br>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer<br>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145200\" id=\"question-wrapper-145200\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Vygotsky model of education <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4cd0934f-b3be-428a-be0e-9e302c5eb785\" data-question=\"36\">supports the concept of a mixed-ability class<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145201\" id=\"question-wrapper-145201\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some teachers are uncertain about allowing students to take on MKO roles in the classroom. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145202\" id=\"question-wrapper-145202\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"43155fb6-6d22-4de8-9527-46bd7a9d1e18\" data-question=\"38\">rewarding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> to teach knowledge which you have only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b969779-5d14-49a3-ad97-c6322fbb0f22\" data-question=\"38\">recently acquired<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145203\" id=\"question-wrapper-145203\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The priority should be to ensure that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"36e620eb-c09d-40ea-8859-8cdef556a03f\" data-question=\"39\">the highest-achieving students attain their goals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145204\" id=\"question-wrapper-145204\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Taking part in collaborative outdoor activities with teachers and classmates can improve student outcomes in the classroom. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"83dc1df5-ed64-4ccf-ae3a-fbb7607ee1e7","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"a range of learning needs","passagePhrase":"needed literacy support ... the virtue of moderation"},{"uid":"93666256-23c3-426a-bd54-a934c54a981b","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"a very broad appeal","passagePhrase":"appealing to almost every stakeholder"},{"uid":"8e557613-4cda-4f1e-a8ed-456a5fa17175","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"not achieving their full potential","passagePhrase":"suffer at the demands of the collective, mediocrity prevails"},{"uid":"b645bbe2-f516-45ac-b67f-e025c1ca296c","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"assistance","passagePhrase":"teachers, textbooks, worked examples, parents and so on"},{"uid":"1d8b3e62-ea7e-4c0f-bf30-6b27835a0f71","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"students in streamed groups","passagePhrase":"streaming students"},{"uid":"b2930dc9-88e3-4128-be72-6e061e0b5ca9","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"little indication","passagePhrase":"limited empirical evidence"},{"uid":"fa5aeaa1-79a8-47d4-a1ce-ad32ae2d0b2a","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"leads to","passagePhrase":"results in"},{"uid":"754d2c5b-3a51-4442-84fa-8d2ce95eb90c","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"higher achievements","passagePhrase":"better outcomes"},{"uid":"15fc6c62-be7e-4a4a-9dbd-cc8645c7e9ea","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"the most significant impact","passagePhrase":"significantly ' — and negatively — affect"},{"uid":"0881fc2c-1f05-4950-8bf9-f1fcda68aa3a","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"placed in","passagePhrase":"assigned to"},{"uid":"28b90f1b-1451-440a-9692-41d169defdaa","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"bottom sets","passagePhrase":"lowest sets"},{"uid":"e4f7dd11-a00c-47a5-82d4-6bbe55079f31","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"a large proportion","passagePhrase":"much higher representation"},{"uid":"9312a816-62d9-4f68-bd6d-1686504db905","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"disadvantaged backgrounds","passagePhrase":"low socioeconomic class"},{"uid":"43aff8bd-9ca1-42ed-91ea-a6879e845ecc","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"minimal advantage","passagePhrase":"small benefit"},{"uid":"d12b6d62-eff4-455a-9a03-a4665478646f","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"brightest pupils","passagePhrase":"lucky clever students"},{"uid":"e7f0164d-a467-4058-b9b2-6efdfcb68002","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"A further issue","passagePhrase":"one of the most significant factors"},{"uid":"beb5bc71-e55d-4011-a192-ff766a0acb6c","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"lower expectations","passagePhrase":"limits what the teacher feels the student is capable of"},{"uid":"43155fb6-6d22-4de8-9527-46bd7a9d1e18","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"rewarding","passagePhrase":"exciting"},{"uid":"913c21c9-76e5-4c2c-b5ac-2bc8b95288f6","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"passing on"},{"uid":"8b969779-5d14-49a3-ad97-c6322fbb0f22","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"recently acquired","passagePhrase":"have just mastered"}]},"reading_u2_292":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3><strong>Green roofs</strong></h3><p>A.</p><p>Rooftops covered with grass, vegetable gardens and lush foliage are now a common sight in many cities around the world. More and more private companies and city authorities are investing in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be577466-76f6-4ce7-b58a-c55dc2170d68\" data-question=\"7\">green roofs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, drawn to their wide-ranging <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d4334c9-237b-4a2a-bf00-66055260fa99\" data-question=\"6\">benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. Among the benefits are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41022a47-5053-487f-b344-92f910f5d9dc\" data-question=\"6\">saving on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> energy costs, mitigating the risk of floods, making habitats for urban wildlife, tackling air pollution and even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba238d7e-ac60-4f99-9487-94bd8c767d9e\" data-question=\"7\">growing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> food. These increasingly radical urban designs can help cities adapt to the monumental problems they face, such as access to resources and a lack of green space due to development. But the involvement of city authorities, businesses and other institutions is crucial to ensuring their success — as is research investigating different options to suit the variety of rooftop spaces found in cities. The UK is relatively new to developing green roofs, and local governments and institutions are playing a major role in spreading the practice. London is home to much of the UK’s green roof market, mainly due to forward-thinking policies such as the London Plan, which has paved the way to more than doubling the area of green roofs in the capital.</p><p>B.</p><p>Ongoing research is showcasing how green roofs in cities can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c25e1a05-21e0-411e-a2ba-1213a5388a7d\" data-question=\"4\">integrate with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"707632d6-7904-436a-a694-f240f006c377\" data-question=\"4\">‘living walls’<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>: environmentally friendly walls which are partially or completely covered with greenery, including a growing medium, such as soil or water. Research also indicates that green roofs can be integrated with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"707632d6-7904-436a-a694-f240f006c377\" data-question=\"4\">drainage systems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> on the ground, such as street trees, so that the water is managed better and the built environment is made more sustainable. There is also evidence to demonstrate the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6148c04f-fd31-4f84-a022-cb6b4c78d8d5\" data-question=\"8\">social value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of green roofs. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a71f39e7-91ac-43ab-b8c5-63a9a74dc456\" data-question=\"8\">Doctors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> are increasingly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0a45442-900e-4b09-8986-cd062d2a7928\" data-question=\"8\">prescribing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> time spent gardening outdoors for patients dealing with anxiety and depression. And <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7bb9699e-c3f7-4a57-a534-090660300f8a\" data-question=\"9\">research has found that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"949b6568-ba85-4a18-8e6b-062b4c5687ab\" data-question=\"9\">access to even the most basic green spaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> can provide a better quality of life for dementia sufferers and help people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"122ab265-55d3-4d04-aef6-809edcbe1396\" data-question=\"9\">avoid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> obesity.</p><p>C.</p><p>In North America, green roofs have become mainstream, with a wide array of expansive, accessible and food-producing roofs installed in buildings. Again, city leaders and authorities have helped push the movement forward — only recently, San Francisco, USA, created a policy requiring new buildings to have green roofs. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a02f0ae-b67d-48e7-a0c9-993d0e334400\" data-question=\"2\">Toronto<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, Canada, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09d6e070-b54a-4f1a-b8f9-cb721bb0fc50\" data-question=\"2\">has policies dating from the 1990s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, encouraging the development of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"abfbfec9-3b49-43f2-812f-fd97ea7c6122\" data-question=\"2\">urban farms on rooftops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. These countries also benefit from having newer buildings than in many parts of the world, which makes it easier to install green roofs. Being able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b487ad7d-5bf1-4287-901a-8aadc7c41a4b\" data-question=\"10\">keep enough water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> at roof height and distribute it right across the rooftop is crucial to maintaining the plants on any green roof — especially on ‘edible roofs’ where fruit and vegetables are farmed. And it’s much easier to do this in newer buildings, which can typically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b487ad7d-5bf1-4287-901a-8aadc7c41a4b\" data-question=\"10\">hold greater weight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, than to retro-fit old ones. Having a stronger roof also makes it easier to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4481f711-0097-4cfe-a26d-8618f9d002b7\" data-question=\"10\">grow a greater variety of plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>, since the soil can be deeper.</p><p>D.</p><p>For green roofs <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23ae9b26-dcb3-477f-8b75-3116ef71c91c\" data-question=\"1\">to become the norm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> for new developments, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f806f06-76d2-4974-a1d1-567ed5c74851\" data-question=\"1\">there needs to be support<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> from public authorities and private investors. Those responsible for maintaining buildings may have to acquire new skills, such as landscaping, and in some cases, volunteers may be needed to help out. Other considerations include installing drainage paths, meeting health and safety requirements and perhaps allowing access for the public, as well as planning restrictions and disruption from regular activities in and around the buildings during installation. To <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa9f5936-18c1-4d85-8745-6c7f62d57582\" data-question=\"5\">convince<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> investors and developers that installing green roofs is worthwhile, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de2e8cd0-d26b-4b33-b242-55c53158c519\" data-question=\"5\">economic arguments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> are still <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1114b856-5c13-4036-ad93-1a390508b5e3\" data-question=\"5\">the most important<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. The term ‘natural capital’ has been developed to explain the economic value of nature; for example, measuring the money saved by installing natural solutions to protect against flood damage, adapt to climate change or help people lead healthier and happier lives.</p><p>E.</p><p>As the expertise about green roofs grows, official standards have been developed to ensure that they are designed, constructed and maintained properly, and function well. Improvements in the science and technology underpinning green roof development have also led to new variations in the concept. For example, ‘blue roofs’ enable buildings to hold water over longer periods of time, rather than draining it away quickly — crucial in times of heavier rainfall. There are also combinations of green roofs with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0acd52e5-ef0c-41a5-b88b-5c168480fcea\" data-question=\"12\">solar panels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, and ‘brown roofs’ which are wilder in nature and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9bb2f11-425a-478e-bdc9-eba1c187a55a\" data-question=\"12\">maximise biodiversity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. If the trend continues, it could create new jobs and a more vibrant and sustainable local food economy — alongside many other benefits. There are still barriers to overcome, but the evidence so far indicates that green roofs have the potential to transform cities and help them function sustainably long into the future. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca8f9e48-5bbf-4a5c-99d7-17ac6095714c\" data-question=\"3\">The success stories<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68d05127-b1f1-4418-9f53-dbe41bbb0f57\" data-question=\"3\">need to be studied and replicated elsewhere<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, to make green, blue, brown and food-producing roofs the norm in cities around the world.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 88\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Reading Passage 1 has five paragraphs, A-E.<br>Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145245\" id=\"question-wrapper-145245\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of several challenges <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f806f06-76d2-4974-a1d1-567ed5c74851\" data-question=\"1\">to be overcome<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> before a green roof <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23ae9b26-dcb3-477f-8b75-3116ef71c91c\" data-question=\"1\">can be installed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145246\" id=\"question-wrapper-145246\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2a02f0ae-b67d-48e7-a0c9-993d0e334400\" data-question=\"2\">a city<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> where green roofs <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09d6e070-b54a-4f1a-b8f9-cb721bb0fc50\" data-question=\"2\">have been promoted for many years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145247\" id=\"question-wrapper-145247\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a belief that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca8f9e48-5bbf-4a5c-99d7-17ac6095714c\" data-question=\"3\">existing green roofs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"68d05127-b1f1-4418-9f53-dbe41bbb0f57\" data-question=\"3\">should be used as a model for new ones<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145248\" id=\"question-wrapper-145248\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of how green roofs can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c25e1a05-21e0-411e-a2ba-1213a5388a7d\" data-question=\"4\">work in combination with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"707632d6-7904-436a-a694-f240f006c377\" data-question=\"4\">other green urban initiatives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145249\" id=\"question-wrapper-145249\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1114b856-5c13-4036-ad93-1a390508b5e3\" data-question=\"5\">the need<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to make a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fa9f5936-18c1-4d85-8745-6c7f62d57582\" data-question=\"5\">persuasive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de2e8cd0-d26b-4b33-b242-55c53158c519\" data-question=\"5\">argument for the financial benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> of green roofs </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 88\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the summary below.<br>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 6—9 on your answer sheet.</p><p><strong>Advantages of green roofs</strong></p><p>City rooftops covered with greenery have many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d4334c9-237b-4a2a-bf00-66055260fa99\" data-question=\"6\">advantages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. These include lessening the likelihood that floods will occur, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41022a47-5053-487f-b344-92f910f5d9dc\" data-question=\"6\">reducing how much money is spent on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <strong>6 .....................</strong> and creating environments that are suitable for wildlife. In many cases, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be577466-76f6-4ce7-b58a-c55dc2170d68\" data-question=\"7\">they<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> can also be used for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ba238d7e-ac60-4f99-9487-94bd8c767d9e\" data-question=\"7\">producing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <strong>7............................. </strong></p><p style=\"margin-right:14px\">There are also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6148c04f-fd31-4f84-a022-cb6b4c78d8d5\" data-question=\"8\">social benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of green roofs. For example, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a71f39e7-91ac-43ab-b8c5-63a9a74dc456\" data-question=\"8\">medical profession<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0a45442-900e-4b09-8986-cd062d2a7928\" data-question=\"8\">recommends<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span><strong> 8</strong> <strong>..........................</strong> as an activity to help people cope with mental health issues. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7bb9699e-c3f7-4a57-a534-090660300f8a\" data-question=\"9\">Studies have also shown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"949b6568-ba85-4a18-8e6b-062b4c5687ab\" data-question=\"9\">the availability of green spaces<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"122ab265-55d3-4d04-aef6-809edcbe1396\" data-question=\"9\">prevent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> physical problems such as<strong> 9............................. </strong></p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145250\" id=\"question-wrapper-145250\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ENERGY</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145251\" id=\"question-wrapper-145251\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOOD</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145252\" id=\"question-wrapper-145252\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GARDENING</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145253\" id=\"question-wrapper-145253\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OBESITY</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 89\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.<br>Write the correct letters in boxes 10 and 11 on your answer sheet.</p><p>Which TWO advantages of using newer buildings for green roofs are mentioned in Paragraph C of the passage?</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 89\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><ul><li>A. a longer growing season for edible produce</li><li>B. more economical use of water</li><li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b487ad7d-5bf1-4287-901a-8aadc7c41a4b\" data-question=\"10\">greater water-storage capacity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span></li><li>D. ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4481f711-0097-4cfe-a26d-8618f9d002b7\" data-question=\"10\">cultivate more plant types<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span></li><li>E. a large surface area for growing plants</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145254\" id=\"question-wrapper-145254\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145255\" id=\"question-wrapper-145255\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 89\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 12 and 13 on your answer sheet.</p><p>Which TWO aims of new variations on the concept of green roofs are mentioned in Paragraph E of the passage?</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 89\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><ul><li>A. to provide habitats for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9bb2f11-425a-478e-bdc9-eba1c187a55a\" data-question=\"12\">a wide range of species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span></li><li>B. to grow plants successfully even in the wettest climates</li><li>C. to regulate the temperature of the immediate environment</li><li>D. to generate power from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0acd52e5-ef0c-41a5-b88b-5c168480fcea\" data-question=\"12\">a sustainable source<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span></li><li>E. to collect water to supply other buildings</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145256\" id=\"question-wrapper-145256\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145257\" id=\"question-wrapper-145257\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"be577466-76f6-4ce7-b58a-c55dc2170d68","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"they","passagePhrase":"green roofs"},{"uid":"0d4334c9-237b-4a2a-bf00-66055260fa99","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"advantages","passagePhrase":"benefits"},{"uid":"41022a47-5053-487f-b344-92f910f5d9dc","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"reducing how much money is spent on","passagePhrase":"saving on"},{"uid":"ba238d7e-ac60-4f99-9487-94bd8c767d9e","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"producing","passagePhrase":"growing"},{"uid":"c25e1a05-21e0-411e-a2ba-1213a5388a7d","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"work in combination with","passagePhrase":"integrate with"},{"uid":"707632d6-7904-436a-a694-f240f006c377","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"other green urban initiatives","passagePhrase":"‘living walls’ ... drainage systems"},{"uid":"6148c04f-fd31-4f84-a022-cb6b4c78d8d5","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"social benefits","passagePhrase":"social value"},{"uid":"a71f39e7-91ac-43ab-b8c5-63a9a74dc456","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"medical profession","passagePhrase":"Doctors"},{"uid":"b0a45442-900e-4b09-8986-cd062d2a7928","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"recommends","passagePhrase":"prescribing"},{"uid":"7bb9699e-c3f7-4a57-a534-090660300f8a","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"Studies have also shown","passagePhrase":"research has found that"},{"uid":"949b6568-ba85-4a18-8e6b-062b4c5687ab","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"the availability of green spaces","passagePhrase":"access to even the most basic green spaces"},{"uid":"122ab265-55d3-4d04-aef6-809edcbe1396","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"prevent","passagePhrase":"avoid"},{"uid":"2a02f0ae-b67d-48e7-a0c9-993d0e334400","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"a city","passagePhrase":"Toronto"},{"uid":"09d6e070-b54a-4f1a-b8f9-cb721bb0fc50","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"have been promoted for many years","passagePhrase":"has policies dating from the 1990s"},{"uid":"abfbfec9-3b49-43f2-812f-fd97ea7c6122","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"urban farms on rooftops"},{"uid":"b487ad7d-5bf1-4287-901a-8aadc7c41a4b","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"greater water-storage capacity","passagePhrase":"keep enough water ... hold greater weight"},{"uid":"4481f711-0097-4cfe-a26d-8618f9d002b7","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"cultivate more plant types","passagePhrase":"grow a greater variety of plants"},{"uid":"23ae9b26-dcb3-477f-8b75-3116ef71c91c","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"can be installed","passagePhrase":"to become the norm"},{"uid":"7f806f06-76d2-4974-a1d1-567ed5c74851","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"to be overcome","passagePhrase":"there needs to be support"},{"uid":"fa9f5936-18c1-4d85-8745-6c7f62d57582","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"persuasive","passagePhrase":"convince"},{"uid":"de2e8cd0-d26b-4b33-b242-55c53158c519","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"argument for the financial benefits","passagePhrase":"economic arguments"},{"uid":"1114b856-5c13-4036-ad93-1a390508b5e3","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"the need","passagePhrase":"the most important"},{"uid":"0acd52e5-ef0c-41a5-b88b-5c168480fcea","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"a sustainable source","passagePhrase":"solar panels"},{"uid":"e9bb2f11-425a-478e-bdc9-eba1c187a55a","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"a wide range of species","passagePhrase":"maximise biodiversity"},{"uid":"ca8f9e48-5bbf-4a5c-99d7-17ac6095714c","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"existing green roofs","passagePhrase":"The success stories"},{"uid":"68d05127-b1f1-4418-9f53-dbe41bbb0f57","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"should be used as a model for new ones","passagePhrase":"need to be studied and replicated elsewhere"}]},"reading_u2_293":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3>The growth mindset</h3><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"137c5d26-8a8f-4f21-b69b-93b2b92bf7e8\" data-question=\"14\">Over the past century<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, a powerful idea has taken root in the educational landscape. The concept of intelligence as something innate has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88aebe34-6b16-4ca1-8054-951a280f64d0\" data-question=\"14\">supplanted by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the idea that intelligence is not fixed, and that, with the right training, we can be the authors <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"145b8f94-84a0-4113-b344-bd252070527b\" data-question=\"19\">of our own<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c75d672-6d25-479d-ae4b-cef24f9ed584\" data-question=\"19\">cognitive capabilities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. Psychologist Alfred Binet, the developer of the first intelligence tests, was one of many 19th-century scientists who held that earlier view and sought to quantify cognitive ability. Then, in the early 20th century, progressive thinkers revolted against the notion that inherent ability is destiny. Instead, educators such as John Dewey argued that every child’s intelligence could be developed, given the right environment.</p><p>‘Growth mindset theory’ is a relatively new — and extremely popular — version of this idea. In many schools today you will see hallways covered in motivational posters and hear speeches on the mindset of great sporting heroes who simply <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"554621a7-afa8-4100-840d-c41141fe6bd7\" data-question=\"15\">believed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b0e3b8c-68ca-4b25-8c94-6fd6bb7d32e3\" data-question=\"15\">their way to the top<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. A major focus of the growth mindset in schools is coaxing students away from seeing failure as an indication of their ability, and towards seeing it as a chance to improve that ability. As educationalist Jeff Howard noted several decades ago: ‘Smart is not something that you just are, smart is something that you can get.’</p><p>The idea of the growth mindset is based on the work of psychologist Carol Dweck in California in the 1990s. In one key experiment, Dweck divided a group of 10- to 12 year-olds into two groups. All were told that they had achieved a high score onatest but the first group were praised for their intelligence in achieving this, while the others were praised for their effort. The second group — those who had been instilled with a ‘growth mindset’ — were subsequently far more likely to put effort into future tasks. Meanwhile, the former took on only those tasks that would not risk their sense of worth. This group had inferred that success or failure is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"826d1f5d-21ef-4d0a-a42a-a75cf7115148\" data-question=\"16\">due to innate ability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, and this ‘fixed mindset’ had led them to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b26c4859-3495-4ecc-a6fe-22f7951bc602\" data-question=\"16\">fear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of failure and lack of effort. Praising ability actually made the students perform worse, while praising effort emphasised that change was possible.</p><p>One of the greatest impediments to successfully implementing a growth mindset, however, is the education system itself: in many parts of the world, the school climate is obsessed with performance in the form of constant testing, analysing and ranking of students — a key characteristic of the fixed mindset. Nor is it unusual for schools to create a certain cognitive dissonance, when they applaud the benefits of a growth mindset but then hand out fixed target grades in lessons based on performance.</p><p>Aside from the implementation problem, the original growth mindset <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab14609e-0e7f-4c5e-8431-d6038ec44bb5\" data-question=\"22\">research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> has also received harsh criticism. The statistician Andrew Gelman claims that ‘their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4bef3324-4c0c-45d6-9049-4cbde46d09cb\" data-question=\"17\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab14609e-0e7f-4c5e-8431-d6038ec44bb5\" data-question=\"22\">research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> designs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8bcaa7e9-1111-424f-9429-ed66fe4f72a2\" data-question=\"17\">have enough degrees of freedom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that they could take their data to support just about any theory at all’. Professor of Psychology Timothy Bates, who has been trying to replicate Dweck’s work, is finding that the results are repeatedly null. He notes that: ‘People with a growth mindset don’t cope any better with failure ... Kids with the growth mindset <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7e6c6baa-4b61-407a-b7d2-021822417c0b\" data-question=\"22\">aren’t getting better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> grades, either before or after our intervention <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ab14609e-0e7f-4c5e-8431-d6038ec44bb5\" data-question=\"22\">study<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.’</p><p>Much of this criticism is not lost on Dweck, and she <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c72fdbc4-d41e-4664-97b6-3d0784229fca\" data-question=\"23\">deserves great credit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> for responding to it and adapting <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd5ce2b2-fafa-4698-a067-22cb68ad577c\" data-question=\"18\">her work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> accordingly. In fact, she argues that her work has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"97e03e10-bb76-4198-9577-e3b8d7f29557\" data-question=\"18\">misunderstood and misapplied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> in a range of ways. She has also expressed concerns that her theories are being misappropriated in schools by being conflated with the self-esteem movement: ‘For me the growth mindset is a tool for learning and improvement. It’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69646b15-107b-4316-9d83-2f560c63415d\" data-question=\"21\">not just<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> a vehicle for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c81a77c1-5787-4efe-9395-a5b31d0a8834\" data-question=\"21\">making children feel good<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>.’</p><p>But there is another factor at work here. The failure to translate the growth mindset into the classroom might reflect a misunderstanding of the nature of teaching and learning itself. Growth mindset supporters David Yeager and Gregory Walton claim that interventions should be-<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3f83d02c-3d74-4528-8575-994cdee9b544\" data-question=\"20\">delivered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> in a subtle way to maximise their effectiveness. They say that if adolescents <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f998f4bf-2f50-4eb6-ab69-259492983d72\" data-question=\"20\">perceive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> a teacher’s intervention as conveying that they are in need of help, this could undo its intended effects.</p><p>A lot of what drives students is their innate beliefs and how they perceive themselves. There is a strong correlation between self-perception and achievement, but there is evidence to suggest that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"6711d404-c17e-4acc-9463-9cc576e2e2bf\" data-question=\"24\">the actual effect of achievement on self-perception is stronger than the other way round<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. To stand up in a classroom and successfully deliver a good speech is a genuine achievement, and that is likely to be more powerfully motivating than vague notions of ‘motivation’ itself.</p><p>Recent evidence would suggest that growth mindset interventions are not the elixir of student learning that its proponents claim it to be. The growth mindset appears to be a viable construct in the lab, which, when administered in the classroom via targeted interventions, doesn’t seem to work. It is hard to dispute that having faith in the capacity to change is a good attribute for students. Paradoxically, however, that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e887c678-1271-4af9-91e4-03cd70ec4008\" data-question=\"26\">aspiration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5678a8e9-4e54-4017-b4a8-f821dd1c96a8\" data-question=\"26\">not well served<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c1a033c-eaf7-4d1b-94e7-c9a96d8deb6b\" data-question=\"26\">direct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> interventions that try to instil it.</p><p>Motivational posters and talks are often a waste of time, and might well give students a deluded notion of what success actually means. Teaching concrete skills such as how to write an effective introduction to an essay then praising students’ effort in getting there is probably a far better way of improving confidence than telling them how unique they are, or indeed how capable they are of changing their own brains. Perhaps growth mindset works best as a philosophy and not an intervention.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 92\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 14-16 on your answer sheet.</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145258\" id=\"question-wrapper-145258\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What can we learn from the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. where the notion of innate intelligence first began</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"137c5d26-8a8f-4f21-b69b-93b2b92bf7e8\" data-question=\"14\">when ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> about the nature of intelligence began <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88aebe34-6b16-4ca1-8054-951a280f64d0\" data-question=\"14\">to shift<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></li> <li>C. how scientists have responded to changing views of intelligence</li> <li>D. why thinkers turned away from the idea of intelligence being fixed</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145259\" id=\"question-wrapper-145259\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The second paragraph describes how schools encourage students to </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. identify their personal ambitions.</li> <li>B. help each other to realise their goals.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"554621a7-afa8-4100-840d-c41141fe6bd7\" data-question=\"15\">have confidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b0e3b8c-68ca-4b25-8c94-6fd6bb7d32e3\" data-question=\"15\">their potential to succeed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>.</li> <li>D. concentrate on where their particular strengths lie.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145260\" id=\"question-wrapper-145260\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the third paragraph, the writer suggests that students with a fixed mindset </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. tend to be less competitive.</li> <li>B. generally have a low sense of self-esteem.</li> <li>C. will only work hard if they are given constant encouragement.</li> <li>D. are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b26c4859-3495-4ecc-a6fe-22f7951bc602\" data-question=\"16\">afraid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> to push themselves beyond what they see as their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"826d1f5d-21ef-4d0a-a42a-a75cf7115148\" data-question=\"16\">limitations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 93\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Look at the following statements (Questions 17-22) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person or people, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 17-22 on your answer sheet.</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 93\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p><strong>List of People</strong></p><ul><li>A. Alfred Binet</li><li>B. Carol Dweck</li><li>C. Andrew Gelman</li><li>D. Timothy Bates</li><li>E. David Yeager and Gregory Walton</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145261\" id=\"question-wrapper-145261\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4bef3324-4c0c-45d6-9049-4cbde46d09cb\" data-question=\"17\">methodology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> behind the growth mindset studies was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8bcaa7e9-1111-424f-9429-ed66fe4f72a2\" data-question=\"17\">not strict enough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145262\" id=\"question-wrapper-145262\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd5ce2b2-fafa-4698-a067-22cb68ad577c\" data-question=\"18\">The idea of the growth mindset<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"97e03e10-bb76-4198-9577-e3b8d7f29557\" data-question=\"18\">incorrectly interpreted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145263\" id=\"question-wrapper-145263\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c75d672-6d25-479d-ae4b-cef24f9ed584\" data-question=\"19\">Intellectual ability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> is an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ceb9618a-a108-471a-94b9-0c401d2f6246\" data-question=\"19\">unchangeable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> feature of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"145b8f94-84a0-4113-b344-bd252070527b\" data-question=\"19\">each individual<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145264\" id=\"question-wrapper-145264\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The growth mindset should be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3f83d02c-3d74-4528-8575-994cdee9b544\" data-question=\"20\">promoted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> without students <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f998f4bf-2f50-4eb6-ab69-259492983d72\" data-question=\"20\">being aware of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> it. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145265\" id=\"question-wrapper-145265\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The growth mindset is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"69646b15-107b-4316-9d83-2f560c63415d\" data-question=\"21\">not simply<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c81a77c1-5787-4efe-9395-a5b31d0a8834\" data-question=\"21\">boosting students’ morale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145266\" id=\"question-wrapper-145266\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Research shows that the growth mindset <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7e6c6baa-4b61-407a-b7d2-021822417c0b\" data-question=\"22\">has no effect on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e29ece65-902b-497b-9a42-991338a2660f\" data-question=\"22\">academic achievement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 93\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 2? In boxes 23—26 on your answer sheet, write</p><p>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer<br>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer<br>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145267\" id=\"question-wrapper-145267\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Dweck has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"38361130-cdcd-42dc-af7f-cab40df5d3da\" data-question=\"23\">handled criticisms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> of her work <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c72fdbc4-d41e-4664-97b6-3d0784229fca\" data-question=\"23\">in an admirable way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145268\" id=\"question-wrapper-145268\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Students’ <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"6711d404-c17e-4acc-9463-9cc576e2e2bf\" data-question=\"24\">self-perception is a more effective driver of self-confidence than actual achievement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> is. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145269\" id=\"question-wrapper-145269\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Recent evidence about growth mindset interventions has attracted unfair coverage in the media. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145270\" id=\"question-wrapper-145270\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5c1a033c-eaf7-4d1b-94e7-c9a96d8deb6b\" data-question=\"26\">Deliberate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2aa5c270-70b7-45e0-8cf8-7cd9c1aa35d3\" data-question=\"26\">attempts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> to encourage students to strive for high achievement may have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5678a8e9-4e54-4017-b4a8-f821dd1c96a8\" data-question=\"26\">negative effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"137c5d26-8a8f-4f21-b69b-93b2b92bf7e8","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"when ideas","passagePhrase":"Over the past century"},{"uid":"88aebe34-6b16-4ca1-8054-951a280f64d0","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"to shift","passagePhrase":"supplanted by"},{"uid":"145b8f94-84a0-4113-b344-bd252070527b","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"each individual","passagePhrase":"of our own"},{"uid":"9c75d672-6d25-479d-ae4b-cef24f9ed584","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Intellectual ability","passagePhrase":"cognitive capabilities"},{"uid":"554621a7-afa8-4100-840d-c41141fe6bd7","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"have confidence","passagePhrase":"believed"},{"uid":"7b0e3b8c-68ca-4b25-8c94-6fd6bb7d32e3","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"their potential to succeed","passagePhrase":"their way to the top"},{"uid":"826d1f5d-21ef-4d0a-a42a-a75cf7115148","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"limitations","passagePhrase":"due to innate ability"},{"uid":"b26c4859-3495-4ecc-a6fe-22f7951bc602","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"afraid","passagePhrase":"fear"},{"uid":"ab14609e-0e7f-4c5e-8431-d6038ec44bb5","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"research ... research ... study"},{"uid":"4bef3324-4c0c-45d6-9049-4cbde46d09cb","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"methodology","passagePhrase":"research designs"},{"uid":"8bcaa7e9-1111-424f-9429-ed66fe4f72a2","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"not strict enough","passagePhrase":"have enough degrees of freedom"},{"uid":"7e6c6baa-4b61-407a-b7d2-021822417c0b","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"has no effect on","passagePhrase":"aren’t getting better"},{"uid":"c72fdbc4-d41e-4664-97b6-3d0784229fca","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"in an admirable way","passagePhrase":"deserves great credit"},{"uid":"bd5ce2b2-fafa-4698-a067-22cb68ad577c","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"The idea of the growth mindset","passagePhrase":"her work"},{"uid":"97e03e10-bb76-4198-9577-e3b8d7f29557","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"incorrectly interpreted","passagePhrase":"misunderstood and misapplied"},{"uid":"69646b15-107b-4316-9d83-2f560c63415d","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"not simply","passagePhrase":"not just"},{"uid":"c81a77c1-5787-4efe-9395-a5b31d0a8834","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"boosting students’ morale","passagePhrase":"making children feel good"},{"uid":"3f83d02c-3d74-4528-8575-994cdee9b544","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"promoted","passagePhrase":"delivered"},{"uid":"f998f4bf-2f50-4eb6-ab69-259492983d72","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"being aware of","passagePhrase":"perceive"},{"uid":"e887c678-1271-4af9-91e4-03cd70ec4008","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"aspiration"},{"uid":"5678a8e9-4e54-4017-b4a8-f821dd1c96a8","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"negative effect","passagePhrase":"not well served"},{"uid":"5c1a033c-eaf7-4d1b-94e7-c9a96d8deb6b","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Deliberate","passagePhrase":"direct"},{"uid":"ceb9618a-a108-471a-94b9-0c401d2f6246","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"unchangeable","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"e29ece65-902b-497b-9a42-991338a2660f","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"academic achievement","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"38361130-cdcd-42dc-af7f-cab40df5d3da","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"handled criticisms","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"2aa5c270-70b7-45e0-8cf8-7cd9c1aa35d3","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"attempts","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_294":{"leftHtml":"<div><h3>Alfred Wegener: science, exploration and the theory of continental drift</h3><p><em>by Mott T Greene</em></p><p><strong>Introduction</strong></p><p>This is a book about the life and scientific work of Alfred Wegener, whose reputation today rests with his theory of continental displacements, better known as ‘continental drift’. Wegener proposed this theory in 1912 and developed it extensively for nearly 20 years. His book on the subject, The Origin of Continents and Oceans, went through four editions and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"893d37ac-3cf2-48bc-b7fe-0b564b7d201b\" data-question=\"27\">was the focus of an international controversy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in his lifetime and for some years after his death.</p><p>Wegener’s basic idea was that many mysteries about the Earth’s history could be solved if one supposed that the continents moved laterally, rather than supposing that they remained fixed in place. Wegener showed in great detail how such continental movements were plausible and how they worked, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a22fc835-d2ea-48ab-8824-8f09cbdc861f\" data-question=\"29\">using evidence from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c401fea7-1572-42ba-bb2d-64cefd2b8f5f\" data-question=\"29\">a large number of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> sciences including <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6246070c-09ac-4f31-a153-f3ab3b5e8cc3\" data-question=\"29\">geology, geophysics, paleontology, and climatology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Wegener's idea — that the continents move —is at the heart of the theory that guides Earth sciences today: namely plate tectonics. Plate tectonics is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ea5a887d-5cac-49aa-8458-84d5e5285f8f\" data-question=\"30\">in many respects quite different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> from Wegener’s proposal, in the same way that modern evolutionary theory is very different from the ideas Charles Darwin proposed in the 1850s about biological evolution. Yet plate tectonics is a descendant of Alfred Wegener’s theory of continental drift, in quite the same way that modern evolutionary theory is a descendant of Darwin’s theory of natural selection.</p><p>When I started writing about Wegener’s life and work, one of the most <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7c32c59-ad40-446d-b0a1-e13faa947952\" data-question=\"31\">intriguing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> things about him <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"39bea7aa-aea5-4218-ba58-73714cb4264d\" data-question=\"31\">for me<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> was that, although he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"94dc178b-2404-4e30-a256-821d02e76655\" data-question=\"31\">came up with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> a theory on continental drift, he was not a geologist. He trained as an astronomer and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"697a47d3-a496-40da-8db5-796941d4e528\" data-question=\"32\">pursued a career<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> in atmospheric physics. When he proposed the theory of continental displacements in 1912, he was a lecturer in physics and astronomy at the University of Marburg, in southern Germany. However, he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f5c60cbd-f1b8-495e-917a-f31c4201b1b0\" data-question=\"33\">was not an ‘unknown’<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9bf6b883-fea9-41bc-beba-16adaa8a0a62\" data-question=\"34\">In 1906<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> he had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d210979-5083-4a64-88df-01c462a26065\" data-question=\"34\">set a world record<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> (with his brother Kurt) for time aloft in a hot-air balloon: 52 hours. Between 1906 and 1908 he had taken part in a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"66cc7b41-bd1f-48cb-8a72-31022bd9aad2\" data-question=\"35\">highly publicized<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and extremely <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"81e45ddd-14bb-43c5-b2ec-9dc769b1b3c9\" data-question=\"35\">dangerous expedition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> to the coast of northeast Greenland. He had also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0f083b24-22c7-46f6-97e0-4ef316c41352\" data-question=\"36\">made a name for himself<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> amongst a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6db243d-cf96-45d9-bb6e-c6d8c95f5b26\" data-question=\"36\">small circle of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"208ac5f0-2179-45a6-b051-29d9bb6256a1\" data-question=\"36\">meteorologists and atmospheric physicists in Germany<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> as the author of a textbook, Thermodynamics of the Atmosphere (1911), and of a number of interesting scientific papers.</p><p>As important as Wegener’s work on continental drift has turned out to be, it was largely a sideline to his interest in atmospheric physics, geophysics, and paleoclimatology, and thus I have been at great pains to put Wegener’s work on continental drift in the larger context of his other scientific work, and in the even larger context of atmospheric sciences in his lifetime. This is a ‘continental drift book’ only to the extent that Wegener was interested in that topic and later became famous for it. My treatment of his other scientific work is no less detailed, though I certainly have devoted more attention to the reception of his ideas on continental displacement, as they were much more controversial than his other work.</p><p>Readers interested in the specific detail of Wegener’s career will see that he often stopped pursuing a given line of investigation (sometimes for years on end), only to pick it up later. I have tried to provide guideposts to his rapidly shifting interests by characterizing different phases of his life as careers in different sciences, which is reflected in the titles of the chapters. Thus, the index should be a sufficient guide for those interested in a particular aspect of Wegener’s life but perhaps not all of it. My own feeling, however, is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3024094a-9578-4fa9-a874-c99c76aafe85\" data-question=\"37\">the parts do not make as much sense on their own as do all of his activities taken together<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. In this respect I urge readers to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36482da5-1ee9-4867-b17c-dc66999d895f\" data-question=\"37\">try to experience Wegener's life as he lived it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, with all the interruptions, changes of mind, and renewed efforts this entailed.</p><p>Wegener left behind a few published works but, as was standard practice, these reported the results of his work — not the journey he took to reach that point. Only a few hundred of the many thousands of letters he wrote and received in his lifetime have survived and he didn’t keep notebooks or diaries that recorded his life and activities. He was not active (with a few exceptions) in scientific societies, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbd13c78-5064-491a-800f-06f106ebdaed\" data-question=\"38\">did not seek to find influence or advance his ideas through professional contacts and politics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, spending most of his time at home in his study reading and writing, or in the field collecting observations.</p><p>Some famous scientists, such as Newton, Darwin, and Einstein, left mountains of written material behind, hundreds of notebooks and letters numbering in the tens of thousands. Others, like Michael Faraday, left extensive journals of their thoughts and speculations, parallel to their scientific notebooks. The more such material a scientist leaves behind, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"feec0b0e-2735-4995-9323-f53fef285f81\" data-question=\"39\">the better chance a biographer has of forming an accurate picture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of how a scientist's ideas took shape and evolved.</p><p>I am firmly of the opinion that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88813edd-505e-4ce8-b198-8f4af9c8c49b\" data-question=\"40\">most of us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, Wegener included, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7117f0bb-7ed9-47f7-ae3f-dde42afe3b15\" data-question=\"40\">are not in any real sense the authors of our own lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. We plan, think, and act, often with apparent freedom, but most of the time our lives ‘happen to us’, and we only retrospectively turn this happenstance into a coherent narrative of fulfilled intentions. This book, therefore, is a story both of the life and scientific work that Alfred Wegener planned and intended and of the life and scientific work that actually ‘happened to him’. These are, as I think you will soon see, not always the same thing.</p><p>* Paleoclimatology — The study of past climates</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 96\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write</p><p>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145271\" id=\"question-wrapper-145271\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Wegener’s ideas about continental drift <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"893d37ac-3cf2-48bc-b7fe-0b564b7d201b\" data-question=\"27\">were widely disputed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7b95b4c8-09f6-4c9f-b324-6b0183e571fd\" data-question=\"27\">while he was alive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145272\" id=\"question-wrapper-145272\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The idea that the continents remained fixed in place was defended in a number of respected scientific publications. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145273\" id=\"question-wrapper-145273\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Wegener <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a22fc835-d2ea-48ab-8824-8f09cbdc861f\" data-question=\"29\">relied on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c401fea7-1572-42ba-bb2d-64cefd2b8f5f\" data-question=\"29\">a limited range<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6246070c-09ac-4f31-a153-f3ab3b5e8cc3\" data-question=\"29\">scientific fields<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> to support his theory of continental drift. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145274\" id=\"question-wrapper-145274\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ea5a887d-5cac-49aa-8458-84d5e5285f8f\" data-question=\"30\">The similarities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> between Wegener’s theory of continental drift and modern-day plate tectonics are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ea5a887d-5cac-49aa-8458-84d5e5285f8f\" data-question=\"30\">enormous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 96\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the summary using the list of phrases, A-J, below.<br>Write the correct letter, A—J, in boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet.</p><ul><li><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f5c60cbd-f1b8-495e-917a-f31c4201b1b0\" data-question=\"33\">modest fame<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">B vast range</span></li><li><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">C <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d210979-5083-4a64-88df-01c462a26065\" data-question=\"34\">record-breaking achievement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">D research methods</span></li><li><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">E <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6db243d-cf96-45d9-bb6e-c6d8c95f5b26\" data-question=\"36\">select group<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">F <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"697a47d3-a496-40da-8db5-796941d4e528\" data-question=\"32\">professional interests<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">G scientific debate</span></li><li><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">H <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"81e45ddd-14bb-43c5-b2ec-9dc769b1b3c9\" data-question=\"35\">hazardous exploration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">I <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"39bea7aa-aea5-4218-ba58-73714cb4264d\" data-question=\"31\">biographer's perspective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span></span></li><li><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">J narrow investigation</span></li></ul><p><strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">Wegener's life and work</span></strong></p><p><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">One of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f7c32c59-ad40-446d-b0a1-e13faa947952\" data-question=\"31\">remarkable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> things about Wegener from a </span><strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">31 ............................. </span></strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">is that although he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"94dc178b-2404-4e30-a256-821d02e76655\" data-question=\"31\">proposed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> a theory of continental drift, he was not a geologist. His </span><strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">32............................. </span></strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">were limited to atmospheric physics. However, at the time he </span><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">proposed his theory of continental drift in 1912, he was already a person of </span><strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">33................................ </span></strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9bf6b883-fea9-41bc-beba-16adaa8a0a62\" data-question=\"34\">Six years previously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, there had been his </span><strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">34......................... </span></strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">of 52 hours in a hot-air balloon, followed by his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"66cc7b41-bd1f-48cb-8a72-31022bd9aad2\" data-question=\"35\">well-publicised<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> but </span><strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">35.............................. </span></strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">of Greenland's coast. With the publication of his textbook on thermodynamics, he had also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0f083b24-22c7-46f6-97e0-4ef316c41352\" data-question=\"36\">come to the attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of a </span><strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">36................................ </span></strong><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\">of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"208ac5f0-2179-45a6-b051-29d9bb6256a1\" data-question=\"36\">German scientists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</span><span style=\"color:#1a1a1a\"> </span></p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145275\" id=\"question-wrapper-145275\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145276\" id=\"question-wrapper-145276\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145277\" id=\"question-wrapper-145277\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145278\" id=\"question-wrapper-145278\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145279\" id=\"question-wrapper-145279\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145280\" id=\"question-wrapper-145280\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 97\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145281\" id=\"question-wrapper-145281\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is Mott T Greene doing in the fifth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. describing what motivated him to write the book</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3024094a-9578-4fa9-a874-c99c76aafe85\" data-question=\"37\">explaining why<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> it is desirable to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36482da5-1ee9-4867-b17c-dc66999d895f\" data-question=\"37\">read the whole book<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></li> <li>C. suggesting why Wegener pursued so many different careers</li> <li>D. indicating what aspects of Wegener’s life interested him most</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145282\" id=\"question-wrapper-145282\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is said about Wegener in the sixth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. He <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bbd13c78-5064-491a-800f-06f106ebdaed\" data-question=\"38\">was not a particularly ambitious person<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li> <li>B. He kept a record of all his scientific observations.</li> <li>C. He did not adopt many of the scientific practices of the time.</li> <li>D. He enjoyed discussing new discoveries with other scientists.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145283\" id=\"question-wrapper-145283\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does Greene say about some other famous scientists? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Their published works had a greater impact than Wegener’s did.</li> <li>B. They had fewer doubts about their scientific ideas than Wegener did.</li> <li>C. Their scientific ideas were more controversial than Wegener's.</li> <li>D. They are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"feec0b0e-2735-4995-9323-f53fef285f81\" data-question=\"39\">easier subjects to write about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> than Wegener.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"145284\" id=\"question-wrapper-145284\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is Greene’s main point in the final paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is not enough in life to have good intentions.</li> <li>B. People need to plan carefully if they want to succeed.</li> <li>C. People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7117f0bb-7ed9-47f7-ae3f-dde42afe3b15\" data-question=\"40\">have little control over many aspects of their lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> <li>D. It is important that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88813edd-505e-4ce8-b198-8f4af9c8c49b\" data-question=\"40\">people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> ensure they have the freedom to act.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"893d37ac-3cf2-48bc-b7fe-0b564b7d201b","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"were widely disputed","passagePhrase":"was the focus of an international controversy"},{"uid":"a22fc835-d2ea-48ab-8824-8f09cbdc861f","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"relied on","passagePhrase":"using evidence from"},{"uid":"6246070c-09ac-4f31-a153-f3ab3b5e8cc3","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"scientific fields","passagePhrase":"geology, geophysics, paleontology, and climatology"},{"uid":"f7c32c59-ad40-446d-b0a1-e13faa947952","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"remarkable","passagePhrase":"intriguing"},{"uid":"39bea7aa-aea5-4218-ba58-73714cb4264d","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"biographer's perspective","passagePhrase":"for me"},{"uid":"94dc178b-2404-4e30-a256-821d02e76655","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"proposed","passagePhrase":"came up with"},{"uid":"697a47d3-a496-40da-8db5-796941d4e528","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"professional interests","passagePhrase":"pursued a career"},{"uid":"f5c60cbd-f1b8-495e-917a-f31c4201b1b0","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"modest fame","passagePhrase":"was not an ‘unknown’"},{"uid":"9bf6b883-fea9-41bc-beba-16adaa8a0a62","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"Six years previously","passagePhrase":"In 1906"},{"uid":"0d210979-5083-4a64-88df-01c462a26065","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"record-breaking achievement","passagePhrase":"set a world record"},{"uid":"66cc7b41-bd1f-48cb-8a72-31022bd9aad2","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"well-publicised","passagePhrase":"highly publicized"},{"uid":"81e45ddd-14bb-43c5-b2ec-9dc769b1b3c9","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"hazardous exploration","passagePhrase":"dangerous expedition"},{"uid":"0f083b24-22c7-46f6-97e0-4ef316c41352","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"come to the attention","passagePhrase":"made a name for himself"},{"uid":"a6db243d-cf96-45d9-bb6e-c6d8c95f5b26","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"select group","passagePhrase":"small circle of"},{"uid":"208ac5f0-2179-45a6-b051-29d9bb6256a1","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"German scientists","passagePhrase":"meteorologists and atmospheric physicists in Germany"},{"uid":"3024094a-9578-4fa9-a874-c99c76aafe85","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"explaining why","passagePhrase":"the parts do not make as much sense on their own as do all of his activities taken together"},{"uid":"36482da5-1ee9-4867-b17c-dc66999d895f","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"read the whole book","passagePhrase":"try to experience Wegener's life as he lived it"},{"uid":"bbd13c78-5064-491a-800f-06f106ebdaed","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"was not a particularly ambitious person","passagePhrase":"did not seek to find influence or advance his ideas through professional contacts and politics"},{"uid":"feec0b0e-2735-4995-9323-f53fef285f81","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"easier subjects to write about","passagePhrase":"the better chance a biographer has of forming an accurate picture"},{"uid":"88813edd-505e-4ce8-b198-8f4af9c8c49b","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"people","passagePhrase":"most of us"},{"uid":"7117f0bb-7ed9-47f7-ae3f-dde42afe3b15","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"have little control over many aspects of their lives","passagePhrase":"are not in any real sense the authors of our own lives"},{"uid":"7b95b4c8-09f6-4c9f-b324-6b0183e571fd","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"while he was alive","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_295":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>How tennis rackets have changed</strong></p><p>In 2016, the British professional tennis player Andy Murray was ranked as the world’s number one. It was an incredible achievement by any standard - made even more remarkable by the fact that he did this during a period considered to be one of the strongest in the sport’s history, competing against the likes of Rafael Nadal, Roger Federer and Novak Djokovic, to name just a few. Yet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3fe3cab-42f2-40b8-9adf-536719798ae2\" data-question=\"1\">five years previously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, he <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb66afcb-cf41-4446-a217-2cc5a068a9e1\" data-question=\"1\">had been regarded<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c466bf90-9ffa-471b-818a-13ccabaa826f\" data-question=\"1\">a talented outsider who entered but never won the major tournaments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</p><p>Of the changes that account for this transformation, one was visible and widely publicised: in 2011, Murray invited former number one player Ivan Lendl onto his coaching team - a valuable addition that had a visible impact on the player’s playing style. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57877c93-e992-4fdd-9ea5-8c43b4d3cf42\" data-question=\"2\">Another change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> was so subtle as to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4cf72259-d30f-4c5e-a6ab-fdd745c59425\" data-question=\"2\">pass more or less unnoticed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Like many players, Murray has long preferred a racket that consists of two types of string: one for the mains (verticals) and another for the crosses (horizontals). While he continued to use natural string in the crosses, in 2012 he switched to a synthetic string for the mains. A small change, perhaps, but its importance should not be underestimated.</p><p>The modification that Murray made is just one of a number of options available to players looking to tweak their rackets in order to improve their games. ‘Touring professionals have their rackets customised to their specific needs,’ says Colin Triplow, a UK-based professional racket stringer. ‘It’s a highly important part of performance maximisation.’ Consequently, the specific rackets used by the world’s elite are not actually readily available to the public; rather, each racket is individually made to suit the player who uses it. Take the US professional tennis players Mike and Bob Bryan, for example: ‘We’re very particular with our racket specifications,’ they say. ‘All our rackets are sent from our manufacturer to Tampa, Florida, where our frames go through a . . . thorough customisation process.’ They explain how they have adjusted not only racket length, but even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"66e96bb2-47a9-449c-87e0-3d90fea47e07\" data-question=\"8\">experimented with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> different <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"736d483b-8638-4efc-95bc-2bd0a2dd32ce\" data-question=\"8\">kinds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of paint. The rackets they use now <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"47b75617-bace-4743-be5f-9b8909720ff5\" data-question=\"4\">weigh more than the average<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> model and also have a denser string pattern (i.e. more crosses and mains).</p><p>The primary reason for these modifications is simple: as the line between winning and losing becomes thinner and thinner, even these slight changes become more and more important. As a result, players and their teams are becoming increasingly creative with the modifications to their rackets as they look to maximise their competitive advantage.</p><p>Racket modifications mainly date back to the 1970s, when the amateur German tennis player Werner Fischer started playing with the so-called spaghetti-strung racket. It created a string bed that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3e05e38-2055-4838-82af-269102a7a90a\" data-question=\"9\">generated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> so much topspin that it was quickly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8a3e109-1e64-4859-a3a9-efccef3e6f21\" data-question=\"9\">banned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> by the International Tennis Federation. However, within a decade or two, racket modification became a regularity. Today it is, in many ways, an aspect of the game that is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa71c922-305a-4f03-90c5-1d403ab11a28\" data-question=\"10\">equal in significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53833939-58cb-4d07-8ac8-ca8971300a7c\" data-question=\"10\">nutrition<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> or training.</p><p>Modifications can be divided into two categories: those to the string bed and those to the racket frame. The former is far more common than the latter: the choice of the strings and the tension with which they are installed is something that nearly all professional players experiment with. They will continually <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03010b7b-f456-49a9-99ed-e3b9ed5d0fc6\" data-question=\"6\">change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"878f2b81-b3c8-424d-96d4-d0b4da3c19c9\" data-question=\"6\">depending on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> various factors including the court surface, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7284b445-3d61-42af-a162-70b601aaea5a\" data-question=\"6\">climatic conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, and game styles. Some will even change it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"878f2b81-b3c8-424d-96d4-d0b4da3c19c9\" data-question=\"6\">depending on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> how they feel at the time. At one time, all tennis rackets were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"65907288-c2d4-47ad-a87f-2641a63d9478\" data-question=\"11\">strung with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> natural gut made from the outer layer of sheep or cow intestines. This all changed in the early 1990s with the development of synthetic strings that were cheaper and more durable. They are made from three materials: nylon (relatively durable and affordable), Kevlar (too stiff to be used alone) or co-polyester (polyester combined with additives that enhance its performance). Even so, many professional players continue to use a ‘hybrid set-up’, where a combination of both synthetic and natural strings are used.</p><p>Of the synthetics, co-polyester is by far the most widely used. It’s a perfect fit for the style of tennis now played, where players tend to battle it out from the back of the court rather than coming to the net. Studies indicate that the average spin from a co-polyester string is 25% greater than that from natural string or other synthetics. In a sense, the development of co-polyester strings has revolutionised the game.</p><p>However, many players go beyond these basic adjustments to the strings and make changes to the racket frame itself. For example, much of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b44f370-ca48-4dd4-9236-5d491ea57ec1\" data-question=\"7\">serving power<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> of US professional player Pete Sampras was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"067d5551-012e-452d-b934-139442904cc2\" data-question=\"7\">attributed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a783099-8ae1-4669-b4fc-07796f06cd80\" data-question=\"7\">the addition of four to five <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3d66d96-fb1b-4fec-afb1-61632040222d\" data-question=\"12\">lead<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> weights onto his rackets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, and today many professionals have the weight adjusted during the manufacturing process.</p><p>Other changes to the frame involve the handle. Players have individual preferences for the shape of the handle and some will have the handle of one racket moulded onto the frame of a different racket. Other players make different changes. The professional Portuguese player Goncalo Oliveira <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cfaa9ea-e60a-4d2a-8cba-4cdb28ce444c\" data-question=\"13\">replaced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the original grips of his rackets with something thinner because they had previously felt uncomfortable to hold.</p><p>Racket customisation and modification have pushed the standards of the game to greater levels that few could have anticipated in the days of natural strings and heavy, wooden frames, and it’s exciting to see what further developments there will be in the future.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 17\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</p><p>In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 17\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</p><p>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</p><p>NOT GIVEN_ if there is no information on this</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207193\" id=\"question-wrapper-207193\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb66afcb-cf41-4446-a217-2cc5a068a9e1\" data-question=\"1\">People had expected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> Andy Murray to become <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c466bf90-9ffa-471b-818a-13ccabaa826f\" data-question=\"1\">the world’s top tennis player<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3fe3cab-42f2-40b8-9adf-536719798ae2\" data-question=\"1\">at least five years before 2016<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207194\" id=\"question-wrapper-207194\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"57877c93-e992-4fdd-9ea5-8c43b4d3cf42\" data-question=\"2\">The change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> that Andy Murray made to his rackets <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4cf72259-d30f-4c5e-a6ab-fdd745c59425\" data-question=\"2\">attracted a lot of attention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207195\" id=\"question-wrapper-207195\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Most of the world’s top players take a professional racket stringer on tour with them. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207196\" id=\"question-wrapper-207196\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Mike and Bob Bryan use rackets that are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"47b75617-bace-4743-be5f-9b8909720ff5\" data-question=\"4\">light<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> in comparison to the majority of rackets. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207197\" id=\"question-wrapper-207197\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Werner Fischer played with a spaghetti-strung racket that he designed himself. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207198\" id=\"question-wrapper-207198\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7284b445-3d61-42af-a162-70b601aaea5a\" data-question=\"6\">The weather<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"878f2b81-b3c8-424d-96d4-d0b4da3c19c9\" data-question=\"6\">can affect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> how professional players <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"03010b7b-f456-49a9-99ed-e3b9ed5d0fc6\" data-question=\"6\">adjust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the strings on their rackets. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207199\" id=\"question-wrapper-207199\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It was believed that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a783099-8ae1-4669-b4fc-07796f06cd80\" data-question=\"7\">the change Pete Sampras made to his rackets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"067d5551-012e-452d-b934-139442904cc2\" data-question=\"7\">contributed to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> his <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b44f370-ca48-4dd4-9236-5d491ea57ec1\" data-question=\"7\">strong serve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 18\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 18\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p><strong>The tennis racket and how it has changed</strong></p><ul><li> Mike and Bob Bryan <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"66e96bb2-47a9-449c-87e0-3d90fea47e07\" data-question=\"8\">made changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"736d483b-8638-4efc-95bc-2bd0a2dd32ce\" data-question=\"8\">types<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> of 8....................... used on their racket frames.</li><li> Players were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c8a3e109-1e64-4859-a3a9-efccef3e6f21\" data-question=\"9\">not allowed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> to use the spaghetti-strung racket because of the amount of 9................... it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3e05e38-2055-4838-82af-269102a7a90a\" data-question=\"9\">created<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.</li><li> Changes to rackets can be regarded as being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa71c922-305a-4f03-90c5-1d403ab11a28\" data-question=\"10\">as important as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> players’ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53833939-58cb-4d07-8ac8-ca8971300a7c\" data-question=\"10\">diets<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> or the 10 ....................... they do.</li><li> All rackets used to have natural <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"65907288-c2d4-47ad-a87f-2641a63d9478\" data-question=\"11\">strings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> made from the 11 ........................ of animals</li><li> Pete Sampras had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3d66d96-fb1b-4fec-afb1-61632040222d\" data-question=\"12\">Metal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> 12 .................. put into the frames of his rackets.</li><li> Goncalo Oliveira <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cfaa9ea-e60a-4d2a-8cba-4cdb28ce444c\" data-question=\"13\">changed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the 13................... on his racket handles.</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207200\" id=\"question-wrapper-207200\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PAINT</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207201\" id=\"question-wrapper-207201\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TOPSPIN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207202\" id=\"question-wrapper-207202\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRAINING</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207203\" id=\"question-wrapper-207203\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INTESTINES/GUT</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207204\" id=\"question-wrapper-207204\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WEIGHTS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207205\" id=\"question-wrapper-207205\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GRIPS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a3fe3cab-42f2-40b8-9adf-536719798ae2","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"at least five years before 2016","passagePhrase":"five years previously"},{"uid":"cb66afcb-cf41-4446-a217-2cc5a068a9e1","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"People had expected","passagePhrase":"had been regarded"},{"uid":"57877c93-e992-4fdd-9ea5-8c43b4d3cf42","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"The change","passagePhrase":"Another change"},{"uid":"66e96bb2-47a9-449c-87e0-3d90fea47e07","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"made changes","passagePhrase":"experimented with"},{"uid":"736d483b-8638-4efc-95bc-2bd0a2dd32ce","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"types","passagePhrase":"kinds"},{"uid":"a3e05e38-2055-4838-82af-269102a7a90a","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"created","passagePhrase":"generated"},{"uid":"c8a3e109-1e64-4859-a3a9-efccef3e6f21","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"not allowed","passagePhrase":"banned"},{"uid":"aa71c922-305a-4f03-90c5-1d403ab11a28","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"as important as","passagePhrase":"equal in significance"},{"uid":"53833939-58cb-4d07-8ac8-ca8971300a7c","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"diets","passagePhrase":"nutrition"},{"uid":"03010b7b-f456-49a9-99ed-e3b9ed5d0fc6","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"adjust","passagePhrase":"change"},{"uid":"878f2b81-b3c8-424d-96d4-d0b4da3c19c9","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"can affect","passagePhrase":"depending on ... depending on"},{"uid":"7284b445-3d61-42af-a162-70b601aaea5a","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"The weather","passagePhrase":"climatic conditions"},{"uid":"65907288-c2d4-47ad-a87f-2641a63d9478","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"strings","passagePhrase":"strung with"},{"uid":"4b44f370-ca48-4dd4-9236-5d491ea57ec1","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"strong serve","passagePhrase":"serving power"},{"uid":"067d5551-012e-452d-b934-139442904cc2","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"contributed to","passagePhrase":"attributed to"},{"uid":"9a783099-8ae1-4669-b4fc-07796f06cd80","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"the change Pete Sampras made to his rackets","passagePhrase":"the addition of four to five lead weights onto his rackets"},{"uid":"f3d66d96-fb1b-4fec-afb1-61632040222d","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"Metal","passagePhrase":"lead"},{"uid":"5cfaa9ea-e60a-4d2a-8cba-4cdb28ce444c","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"changed","passagePhrase":"replaced"}]},"reading_u2_296":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The pirates of the ancient Mediterranean</strong></p><p><em>In the first and second millennia BCE, pirates sailed around the Mediterranean, attacking ships and avoiding pursuers</em></p><p>A</p><p>When one mentions pirates, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34a4e417-d4e9-4056-84d5-2a1fc5a9f515\" data-question=\"17\">an image<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> springs to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9bf8789-71aa-44b6-9128-cea356513a58\" data-question=\"17\">most<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> people’s minds of a crew of misfits, daredevils and adventurers in command of a tall sailing ship in the Caribbean Sea. Yet from the first to the third millennium BCE, thousands of years before these swashbucklers began spreading fear across the Caribbean, pirates prowled the Mediterranean, raiding merchant ships and threatening vital trade routes. However, despite all efforts and the might of various ancient states, piracy could not be stopped. The situation remained unchanged for thousands of years. Only when the pirates directly threatened the interests of ancient Rome did the Roman Republic organise a massive fleet to eliminate piracy. Under the command of the Roman general Pompey, Rome eradicated piracy, transforming the Mediterranean into '<em>Mare Nostrum'</em> (Our Sea).</p><p>B</p><p>Although piracy in the Mediterranean is first recorded in ancient Egypt during the reign of Pharaoh Amenhotep III (c 1390-1353 BCE), it is reasonable to assume it predated this powerful civilisation. This is partly due to the great importance the Mediterranean held at this time, and partly due to its geography. While the Mediterranean region is predominantly fertile, some parts are rugged and hilly, even mountainous. In the ancient times, the inhabitants of these areas <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"428f1c29-9f5a-433a-a83f-7803e306464c\" data-question=\"21\">relied heavily<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccb648ba-3aad-4ad0-92f4-66b5bcdc6bd7\" data-question=\"21\">on marine resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, including fish and salt. Most had their own boats, possessed good seafaring skills, and unsurpassed knowledge of the local coastline and sailing routes. Thus, it is not surprising that during hardships, these men turned to piracy. Geography itself further benefited the pirates, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1be0ba15-359f-445a-b228-54b909263fa2\" data-question=\"19\">the numerous coves along the coast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> providing places for them to hide their boats and strike undetected. Before the invention of ocean-going caravels* in the 15th century, ships could not easily cross long distances over open water. Thus, in the ancient world most were restricted to a few well-known navigable routes that followed the coastline. Caught in a trap, a slow merchant ship laden with goods had no other option but to surrender. In addition, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"913584cc-8e76-4787-be4c-651a74a437c0\" data-question=\"20\">knowledge of the local area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> helped the pirates to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ac305d4-a962-4658-9bfa-70d2f1882e25\" data-question=\"20\">avoid retaliation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> once a state fleet arrived.</p><p>C</p><p>One should also add that it was not unknown in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74745355-a478-4331-bb88-06385e4f5b2f\" data-question=\"16\">the first and second millennia BCE<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> for governments to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f694f168-7425-4a08-8899-2acbc16684da\" data-question=\"16\">resort to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> pirates’ services, especially during wartime, employing their skills and numbers against their opponents. A pirate fleet would serve in the first wave of attack, preparing the way for the navy. Some of the regions were known for providing safe harbours to pirates, who, in return, boosted the local economy.</p><p>D</p><p>The first known record of a named group of Mediterranean pirates, made during the rule of ancient Egyptian Pharaoh Akhenaten (c 1353-1336 BCE), was in the Amarna Letters. These were extracts of diplomatic correspondence between the pharaoh and his allies, and covered many pressing issues, including piracy. It seems the pharaoh was troubled by two distinct <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f8debb96-6f79-456d-b438-3d18f3b524d7\" data-question=\"14\">pirate groups<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, the Lukka and the Sherden. Despite the Egyptian fleet’s best efforts, the pirates continued to cause substantial disruption to regional commerce. In the letters, the king of Alashiya (modern Cyprus) <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4e90b72c-034e-436b-85e1-49adbfcdb522\" data-question=\"14\">rejected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> Akhenaten’s claims of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7bd334ec-4855-49b7-98ca-597a3ba40572\" data-question=\"14\">connection with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the Lukka (based in modern-day Turkey). The king assured Akhenaten he was prepared to punish any of his subjects involved in piracy.</p><p>E</p><p>The ancient Greek world’s experience of piracy was different from that of Egyptian rulers. While Egypt’s power was land-based, the ancient Greeks relied on the Mediterranean in almost all aspects of life, from trade to warfare. Interestingly, in his works the <em>Iliad</em> and the <em>Odyssey,</em> the ancient Greek writer Homer not only condones, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c0e964ee-6f18-44ab-8c3d-d574842ae5e0\" data-question=\"23\">praises the lifestyle and actions of pirates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. The opinion remained unchanged in the following centuries. The ancient Greek historian Thucydides, for instance, glorified pirates’ daring attacks on ships or even cities. For Greeks, piracy was a part of everyday life. Even <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df0b8f13-1871-42eb-a8b3-cea30b45c4db\" data-question=\"22\">high-ranking members of the state<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1f007dc9-6019-4c8c-b700-5face37faec4\" data-question=\"22\">not beyond engaging in such activities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. According to the Greek orator Demosthenes, in 355 BCE, Athenian ambassadors made a detour from their official travel to capture a ship sailing from Egypt, taking the wealth found onboard for themselves! The Greeks’ liberal approach towards piracy does not mean they always tolerated it, but attempts to curtail piracy were hampered by the large number of pirates operating in the Mediterranean.</p><p>F</p><p>The rising power of ancient Rome required the Roman Republic to deal with piracy in the Mediterranean. While piracy was a serious issue for the Republic, Rome profited greatly from its existence. Pirate raids provided a steady source of slaves, essential for Rome’s agriculture and mining industries. But this arrangement could work only while the pirates left Roman interests alone. Pirate <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c103a3e0-6c98-459b-a939-84be2179c58d\" data-question=\"24\">attacks on grain ships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, which were essential to Roman citizens, led to angry voices in the Senate, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34d1a994-0abe-42fa-a2a8-72e1d7594215\" data-question=\"25\">demanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> punishment of the culprits. Rome, however, did nothing, further encouraging piracy. By the 1st century BCE, emboldened pirates <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"811b6d20-4c11-4724-bb4a-5e1659e608ed\" data-question=\"26\">kidnapped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> prominent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccd6ee7a-f604-473c-bbf0-130312a6a7d5\" data-question=\"26\">Roman dignitaries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b9a0bc0-a41b-4f43-9afd-85815ed9ebfe\" data-question=\"26\">asking for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> a large ransom to be paid. Their most famous hostage was none other than Julius Caesar, captured in 75 BCE.</p><p>G</p><p>By now, Rome was well aware that pirates had outlived their usefulness. The time had come for concerted action. In 67 BCE, a new law granted Pompey vast funds to combat the Mediterranean menace. Taking personal command, Pompey divided the entire Mediterranean into 13 districts, assigning a fleet and commander to each. After <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ffd00241-b2a7-4455-b187-bc2685035c81\" data-question=\"15\">cleansing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> one district of pirates, the fleet would join another in the next district. The process continued until the entire Mediterranean was free of pirates. Although thousands of pirates died at the hands of Pompey’s troops, as a long-term solution to the problem, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe745882-6246-4139-9b94-d2d4df44658e\" data-question=\"18\">many more were offered land in fertile areas located far from the sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Instead of a maritime menace, Rome got productive farmers that further boosted its economy.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 21\"><div class=\"section\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 14—19 on your answer sheet.</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207206\" id=\"question-wrapper-207206\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4e90b72c-034e-436b-85e1-49adbfcdb522\" data-question=\"14\">denial<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7bd334ec-4855-49b7-98ca-597a3ba40572\" data-question=\"14\">involvement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in piracy </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207207\" id=\"question-wrapper-207207\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> details of how a campaign to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ffd00241-b2a7-4455-b187-bc2685035c81\" data-question=\"15\">eradicate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> piracy was carried out </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207208\" id=\"question-wrapper-207208\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a mention of the circumstances in which states in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"74745355-a478-4331-bb88-06385e4f5b2f\" data-question=\"16\">ancient world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f694f168-7425-4a08-8899-2acbc16684da\" data-question=\"16\">make use of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> pirates </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207209\" id=\"question-wrapper-207209\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a reference to how people today <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9bf8789-71aa-44b6-9128-cea356513a58\" data-question=\"17\">commonly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34a4e417-d4e9-4056-84d5-2a1fc5a9f515\" data-question=\"17\">view<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> pirates </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207210\" id=\"question-wrapper-207210\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> an explanation of how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe745882-6246-4139-9b94-d2d4df44658e\" data-question=\"18\">some people were encouraged not to return to piracy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207211\" id=\"question-wrapper-207211\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> a mention of the need for many sailing vessels to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1be0ba15-359f-445a-b228-54b909263fa2\" data-question=\"19\">stay relatively close to land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 21\"><div class=\"section\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 20 and 21 on your answer sheet.</p><p>Which TWO of the following statements does the writer make about inhabitants of the Mediterranean region in the ancient world?</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 21\"><div class=\"section\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><ul><li>A They often used stolen vessels to carry out pirate attacks.</li><li>B They managed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ac305d4-a962-4658-9bfa-70d2f1882e25\" data-question=\"20\">escape capture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> by the authorities because they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"913584cc-8e76-4787-be4c-651a74a437c0\" data-question=\"20\">knew the area so well<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.</li><li>C They paid for information about the routes merchant ships would take.</li><li>D They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"428f1c29-9f5a-433a-a83f-7803e306464c\" data-question=\"21\">depended<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> more <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccb648ba-3aad-4ad0-92f4-66b5bcdc6bd7\" data-question=\"21\">on the sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> for their livelihood than on farming.</li><li>E They stored many of the goods taken in pirate attacks in coves along the coastline.</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207212\" id=\"question-wrapper-207212\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207213\" id=\"question-wrapper-207213\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 22\"><div class=\"section\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 22 and 23 on your answer sheet.</p><p>Which TWO of the following statements does the writer make about piracy and ancient Greece?</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 22\"><div class=\"section\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><ul><li>A. The state estimated that very few people were involved in piracy.</li><li>B. Attitudes towards piracy changed shortly after <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"471773c9-3c8b-4697-8a08-d92f495313bb\" data-question=\"23\">the Iliad and the Odyssey<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> were written.</li><li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df0b8f13-1871-42eb-a8b3-cea30b45c4db\" data-question=\"22\">Important officials<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1f007dc9-6019-4c8c-b700-5face37faec4\" data-question=\"22\">were known to occasionally take part in piracy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</li><li>D. Every citizen regarded pirate attacks on cities as unacceptable.</li><li>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c0e964ee-6f18-44ab-8c3d-d574842ae5e0\" data-question=\"23\">A favourable view of piracy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> is evident in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"471773c9-3c8b-4697-8a08-d92f495313bb\" data-question=\"23\">certain ancient Greek texts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.</li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207214\" id=\"question-wrapper-207214\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207215\" id=\"question-wrapper-207215\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 23\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the summary below.</p><p>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 24—26 on your answer sheet.</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 23\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p><strong>Ancient Rome and piracy</strong></p><p>Piracy was an issue ancient Rome had to deal with, but it also brought some benefits for Rome. For example, pirates supplied slaves that were important for Rome’s industries. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c103a3e0-6c98-459b-a939-84be2179c58d\" data-question=\"24\">attacks on vessels transporting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> 24 ........................ to Rome resulted <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34d1a994-0abe-42fa-a2a8-72e1d7594215\" data-question=\"25\">in calls for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> 25................. for the pirates responsible. Nevertheless, piracy continued, with some pirates <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0b9a0bc0-a41b-4f43-9afd-85815ed9ebfe\" data-question=\"26\">demanding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> a 26 .................... for the return of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccd6ee7a-f604-473c-bbf0-130312a6a7d5\" data-question=\"26\">Roman officials<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> they captured.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207216\" id=\"question-wrapper-207216\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GRAIN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207217\" id=\"question-wrapper-207217\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PUNISHMENT</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207218\" id=\"question-wrapper-207218\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RANSOM</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"34a4e417-d4e9-4056-84d5-2a1fc5a9f515","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"view","passagePhrase":"an image"},{"uid":"a9bf8789-71aa-44b6-9128-cea356513a58","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"commonly","passagePhrase":"most"},{"uid":"428f1c29-9f5a-433a-a83f-7803e306464c","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"depended","passagePhrase":"relied heavily"},{"uid":"ccb648ba-3aad-4ad0-92f4-66b5bcdc6bd7","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"on the sea","passagePhrase":"on marine resources"},{"uid":"1be0ba15-359f-445a-b228-54b909263fa2","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"stay relatively close to land","passagePhrase":"the numerous coves along the coast"},{"uid":"913584cc-8e76-4787-be4c-651a74a437c0","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"knew the area so well","passagePhrase":"knowledge of the local area"},{"uid":"1ac305d4-a962-4658-9bfa-70d2f1882e25","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"escape capture","passagePhrase":"avoid retaliation"},{"uid":"74745355-a478-4331-bb88-06385e4f5b2f","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"ancient world","passagePhrase":"the first and second millennia BCE"},{"uid":"f694f168-7425-4a08-8899-2acbc16684da","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"make use of","passagePhrase":"resort to"},{"uid":"f8debb96-6f79-456d-b438-3d18f3b524d7","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"pirate groups"},{"uid":"4e90b72c-034e-436b-85e1-49adbfcdb522","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"denial","passagePhrase":"rejected"},{"uid":"7bd334ec-4855-49b7-98ca-597a3ba40572","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"involvement","passagePhrase":"connection with"},{"uid":"c0e964ee-6f18-44ab-8c3d-d574842ae5e0","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"A favourable view of piracy","passagePhrase":"praises the lifestyle and actions of pirates"},{"uid":"df0b8f13-1871-42eb-a8b3-cea30b45c4db","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Important officials","passagePhrase":"high-ranking members of the state"},{"uid":"1f007dc9-6019-4c8c-b700-5face37faec4","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"were known to occasionally take part in piracy","passagePhrase":"not beyond engaging in such activities"},{"uid":"c103a3e0-6c98-459b-a939-84be2179c58d","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"attacks on vessels transporting","passagePhrase":"attacks on grain ships"},{"uid":"34d1a994-0abe-42fa-a2a8-72e1d7594215","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"in calls for","passagePhrase":"demanding"},{"uid":"811b6d20-4c11-4724-bb4a-5e1659e608ed","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"kidnapped"},{"uid":"ccd6ee7a-f604-473c-bbf0-130312a6a7d5","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Roman officials","passagePhrase":"Roman dignitaries"},{"uid":"0b9a0bc0-a41b-4f43-9afd-85815ed9ebfe","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"demanding","passagePhrase":"asking for"},{"uid":"ffd00241-b2a7-4455-b187-bc2685035c81","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"eradicate","passagePhrase":"cleansing"},{"uid":"fe745882-6246-4139-9b94-d2d4df44658e","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"some people were encouraged not to return to piracy","passagePhrase":"many more were offered land in fertile areas located far from the sea"},{"uid":"471773c9-3c8b-4697-8a08-d92f495313bb","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"the Iliad and the Odyssey ... certain ancient Greek texts","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_297":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The persistence and peril of misinformation</strong></p><p><em>Brian Southwell looks at how human brains verify information and discusses some of the challenges of battling widespread falsehoods</em></p><p>Misinformation - both deliberately promoted and accidentally shared - is perhaps an inevitable part of the world in which we live, but it is not a new problem. People likely have lied to one another for roughly as long as verbal communication has existed. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e25e699-19bb-48d0-a8e5-e6a786b03089\" data-question=\"27\">Deceiving others<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> can offer an apparent opportunity to gain strategic advantage, to motivate others to action, or even to protect interpersonal bonds. Moreover, people inadvertently have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ed6016c1-1c57-42ac-97c8-cfa29c3c5850\" data-question=\"27\">sharing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e25e699-19bb-48d0-a8e5-e6a786b03089\" data-question=\"27\">inaccurate information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> with one another for thousands of years.</p><p>However, we currently live in an era in which technology enables information to reach large audiences distributed across the globe, and thus the potential for immediate and widespread effects from misinformation now looms larger than in the past. Yet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9628a35-6308-42a4-9e22-e5de9c173399\" data-question=\"28\">the means to correct misinformation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> might<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"436c0005-2752-4f68-bdb6-4130f0a4aeb5\" data-question=\"28\">, over time,<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> be found in those same patterns of mass communication and of the facilitated spread of information.</p><p>The main worry regarding misinformation is its potential to unduly influence attitudes and behavior, leading people to think and act differently than they would if they were correctly informed, as suggested by the research teams of Stephan Lewandowsky of the University of Bristol and Elizabeth Marsh of Duke University, among others. In other words, we worry that misinformation might lead people to hold misperceptions (or false beliefs) and that these misperceptions, especially when they occur among large groups of people, may have detrimental, downstream consequences for health, social harmony, and the political climate.</p><p>At least three observations <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e839c12-e8f4-4553-9a04-2b6bb79ec7b8\" data-question=\"29\">related to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> misinformation in the contemporary mass-media environment <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"609e0e20-0493-424c-8b0f-1f45bf3a3178\" data-question=\"29\">warrant the attention of researchers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, policy makers, and really everyone who watches television, listens to the radio, or reads information online. First of all, people who encounter misinformation tend to believe it, at least initially. Secondly, electronic and print media often do not block many types of misinformation before it appears in content available to large audiences. Thirdly, countering misinformation once it has enjoyed wide exposure can be a resource-intensive effort.</p><p>Knowing what happens when people initially encounter misinformation holds tremendous importance for estimating the potential for subsequent problems. Although it is fairly routine for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e5fec0e-7468-488d-b7e8-7e6d2a8271ad\" data-question=\"31\">individuals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> to come across <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e23139b-4451-4386-85e4-8da040d402e4\" data-question=\"31\">information that is false<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6eda9d01-f618-445c-b73e-19d2798bf364\" data-question=\"31\">the question of exactly how - and when - we mentally label information as true or false<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"550c5f37-2a53-4960-9dee-e309f8ee9503\" data-question=\"31\">has garnered philosophical debate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. The dilemma is neatly summarized by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6256abf-fb31-4cc1-87f3-9b2bed8256a3\" data-question=\"32\">a contrast between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> how the 17th-century philosophers Rene Descartes and Baruch Spinoza described <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"883cbbcc-1742-44be-9511-506ebc69e85a\" data-question=\"32\">human information engagement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6256abf-fb31-4cc1-87f3-9b2bed8256a3\" data-question=\"32\">conflicting predictions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> that only recently have been empirically tested in robust ways. Descartes argued that a person only accepts or rejects information after considering its truth or falsehood; Spinoza argued that people accept all encountered information (or misinformation) by default and then subsequently verify or reject it through a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4e97d39-088b-4907-a5d3-5039882bf02d\" data-question=\"33\">separate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62b7028e-2acc-496b-a24e-214fdcf39170\" data-question=\"33\">cognitive process<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. In recent decades, empirical evidence from the research teams of Erik Asp of the University of Chicago and Daniel Gilbert at Harvard University, among others, has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5291d325-378d-43a7-aeb0-9241bb557d4b\" data-question=\"34\">supported<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> Spinoza’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a2ee1c2-4c31-4bb7-a1c3-c87ad9779a50\" data-question=\"34\">account<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>: people appear to encode all new information as if it were true, even if <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a1ef487-7067-4963-a2d7-5e207fc491ca\" data-question=\"35\">only momentarily<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, and later tag the information as being either true or false, a pattern that seems consistent with the observation that mental resources for skepticism physically <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0147a312-848c-4e27-a2ec-18f4b0172405\" data-question=\"36\">reside in a different part of the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> than the resources used in perceiving and encoding.</p><p>What about our second observation that misinformation often can appear in electronic or print media without being preemptively blocked? In support of this, one might consider the nature of regulatory structures in the United States: regulatory agencies here tend to focus on post hoc detection of broadcast information. Organizations such as the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) offer considerable monitoring and notification functions, but these roles typically do not involve preemptive censoring. The FDA oversees direct-to-consumer prescription drug advertising, for example, and has developed mechanisms such as the ‘Bad Ad’ program, through which people can report advertising in apparent violation of FDA guidelines on drug risks.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd18b12e-f20b-47bf-a6cf-2001a26d4744\" data-question=\"30\">Such programs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, although laudable and useful, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e9eb247-bd80-4500-957e-375a2c5aa976\" data-question=\"30\">do not keep false advertising off the airwaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. In addition, even misinformation that is successfully corrected can continue to affect attitudes. This leads us to our third observation: a campaign to correct misinformation, even if rhetorically compelling, requires resources and planning to accomplish necessary reach and frequency. For corrective campaigns to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d055aea-adbf-4804-b602-2db266fbd486\" data-question=\"37\">be persuasive<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, audiences need to be able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"92c339de-0677-491c-a689-c4a14f86d27e\" data-question=\"37\">comprehend<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> them, which requires either effort to frame messages in ways that are accessible or effort to educate and sensitize audiences to the possibility of misinformation. That some audiences might be unaware of the potential for misinformation also suggests the utility of media literacy efforts as early as elementary school. Even with journalists and scholars pointing to the phenomenon of ‘fake news’, people do not distinguish between demonstrably false stories and those based in fact when scanning and processing written information.</p><p>We live at a time when widespread misinformation is common. Yet at this time many people also are passionately developing potential solutions and remedies. The journey forward undoubtedly will be a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f6f97b91-0f7e-42a6-b9a5-b4b9a68258bd\" data-question=\"39\">long and arduous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> one. Future remedies will require not only continued theoretical consideration but also the development and maintenance of consistent monitoring tools - and a recognition among fellow members of society that claims which find prominence in the media that are insufficiently based in scientific consensus and social reality should be countered. Misinformation arises as a result of human fallibility and human information needs. To overcome the worst effects of the phenomenon, we will need coordinated efforts over time, rather than any singular one-time panacea we could hope to offer.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 26\"><div class=\"section\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.</p></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207219\" id=\"question-wrapper-207219\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does the writer make about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e25e699-19bb-48d0-a8e5-e6a786b03089\" data-question=\"27\">misinformation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Misinformation is a relatively recent phenomenon.</li> <li>B. Some people find it easy to identify misinformation.</li> <li>C. Misinformation changes as it is passed from one person to another.</li> <li>D. There may be a number of reasons for the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ed6016c1-1c57-42ac-97c8-cfa29c3c5850\" data-question=\"27\">spread<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of misinformation.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207220\" id=\"question-wrapper-207220\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer say about the role of technology? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"436c0005-2752-4f68-bdb6-4130f0a4aeb5\" data-question=\"28\">at some point<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> provide us with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9628a35-6308-42a4-9e22-e5de9c173399\" data-question=\"28\">a solution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> to misinformation.</li> <li>B. It could fundamentally alter the way in which people regard information.</li> <li>C. It has changed the way in which organisations use misinformation.</li> <li>D. It has made it easier for people to check whether information is accurate.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207221\" id=\"question-wrapper-207221\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer doing in the fourth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. comparing the different opinions people have of misinformation</li> <li>B. explaining how the effects of misinformation have changed over time</li> <li>C. outlining which issues <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e839c12-e8f4-4553-9a04-2b6bb79ec7b8\" data-question=\"29\">connected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> with misinformation are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"609e0e20-0493-424c-8b0f-1f45bf3a3178\" data-question=\"29\">significant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> today</li> <li>D. describing the attitude of policy makers towards misinformation in the media</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207222\" id=\"question-wrapper-207222\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does the writer make about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd18b12e-f20b-47bf-a6cf-2001a26d4744\" data-question=\"30\">regulation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> in the USA? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The guidelines issued by the FDA need to be simplified.</li> <li>B. Regulation does not affect people’s opinions of new prescription drugs.</li> <li>C. The USA has more regulatory bodies than most other countries.</li> <li>D. Regulation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1e9eb247-bd80-4500-957e-375a2c5aa976\" data-question=\"30\">fails to prevent misinformation from appearing in the media<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 27\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Complete the summary using the list of phrases, A—J, below.</p><p>Write the correct letter, A-J, in boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet.</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 27\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><ul><li>A constant conflict</li><li>B additional evidence</li><li>C <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0147a312-848c-4e27-a2ec-18f4b0172405\" data-question=\"36\">different locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span></li><li>D experimental subjects</li><li><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a1ef487-7067-4963-a2d7-5e207fc491ca\" data-question=\"35\">E short period<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></li><li>F extreme distrust</li><li>G frequent exposure</li><li>H <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62b7028e-2acc-496b-a24e-214fdcf39170\" data-question=\"33\">mental operation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></li><li>I dubious reason</li><li>J <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6256abf-fb31-4cc1-87f3-9b2bed8256a3\" data-question=\"32\">different ideas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span></li></ul><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 27\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p><strong>What happens when people encounter misinformation?</strong></p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 27\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Although <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3e5fec0e-7468-488d-b7e8-7e6d2a8271ad\" data-question=\"31\">people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> have <strong>31 </strong>...............<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e23139b-4451-4386-85e4-8da040d402e4\" data-question=\"31\">. to misinformation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"550c5f37-2a53-4960-9dee-e309f8ee9503\" data-question=\"31\">there is debate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6eda9d01-f618-445c-b73e-19d2798bf364\" data-question=\"31\">precisely how and when we label something as true or untrue.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> The philosophers Descartes and Spinoza had <strong>32</strong> .................. about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"883cbbcc-1742-44be-9511-506ebc69e85a\" data-question=\"32\">how people engage with information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. While Descartes believed that people accept or reject information after considering whether it is true or not, Spinoza argued that people accepted all information they encountered (and by default misinformation) and did not verify or reject it until afterwards.</p><p>Moreover, Spinoza believed that a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4e97d39-088b-4907-a5d3-5039882bf02d\" data-question=\"33\">distinct<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <strong>33</strong>............... is involved in these stages. Recent research has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5291d325-378d-43a7-aeb0-9241bb557d4b\" data-question=\"34\">provided<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> <strong>34</strong>..................... for Spinoza's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a2ee1c2-4c31-4bb7-a1c3-c87ad9779a50\" data-question=\"34\">theory<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> and it would appear that people accept all encountered information as if it were true, even if this is for an <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a1ef487-7067-4963-a2d7-5e207fc491ca\" data-question=\"35\">extremely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <strong>35</strong> ......................., and do not label the information as true or false until later. This is consistent with the fact that the resources for scepticism and the resources for perceiving and encoding are in <strong>36</strong> ............... in the brain.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"column\"><p> </p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207223\" id=\"question-wrapper-207223\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207224\" id=\"question-wrapper-207224\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">J</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207225\" id=\"question-wrapper-207225\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207226\" id=\"question-wrapper-207226\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207227\" id=\"question-wrapper-207227\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207228\" id=\"question-wrapper-207228\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 28\"><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</p><p>In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write</p></div></div><div class=\"layoutArea\"><div class=\"column\"><p>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207229\" id=\"question-wrapper-207229\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Campaigns designed to correct misinformation will fail to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0d055aea-adbf-4804-b602-2db266fbd486\" data-question=\"37\">achieve their purpose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> if people are unable to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"92c339de-0677-491c-a689-c4a14f86d27e\" data-question=\"37\">understand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> them. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207230\" id=\"question-wrapper-207230\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Attempts to teach elementary school students about misinformation have been opposed. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207231\" id=\"question-wrapper-207231\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It may be possible to overcome the problem of misinformation in a <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f6f97b91-0f7e-42a6-b9a5-b4b9a68258bd\" data-question=\"39\">relatively short<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> period. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207232\" id=\"question-wrapper-207232\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The need to keep up with new information is hugely exaggerated in today’s world. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"9e25e699-19bb-48d0-a8e5-e6a786b03089","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"misinformation","passagePhrase":"Deceiving others ... inaccurate information"},{"uid":"ed6016c1-1c57-42ac-97c8-cfa29c3c5850","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"spread","passagePhrase":"sharing"},{"uid":"f9628a35-6308-42a4-9e22-e5de9c173399","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"a solution","passagePhrase":"the means to correct misinformation"},{"uid":"436c0005-2752-4f68-bdb6-4130f0a4aeb5","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"at some point","passagePhrase":", over time,"},{"uid":"8e839c12-e8f4-4553-9a04-2b6bb79ec7b8","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"connected","passagePhrase":"related to"},{"uid":"609e0e20-0493-424c-8b0f-1f45bf3a3178","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"significant","passagePhrase":"warrant the attention of researchers"},{"uid":"3e5fec0e-7468-488d-b7e8-7e6d2a8271ad","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"people","passagePhrase":"individuals"},{"uid":"8e23139b-4451-4386-85e4-8da040d402e4","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":". to misinformation","passagePhrase":"information that is false"},{"uid":"6eda9d01-f618-445c-b73e-19d2798bf364","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"precisely how and when we label something as true or untrue.","passagePhrase":"the question of exactly how - and when - we mentally label information as true or false"},{"uid":"550c5f37-2a53-4960-9dee-e309f8ee9503","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"there is debate","passagePhrase":"has garnered philosophical debate"},{"uid":"b6256abf-fb31-4cc1-87f3-9b2bed8256a3","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"different ideas","passagePhrase":"a contrast between ... conflicting predictions"},{"uid":"883cbbcc-1742-44be-9511-506ebc69e85a","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"how people engage with information","passagePhrase":"human information engagement"},{"uid":"e4e97d39-088b-4907-a5d3-5039882bf02d","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"distinct","passagePhrase":"separate"},{"uid":"62b7028e-2acc-496b-a24e-214fdcf39170","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"mental operation","passagePhrase":"cognitive process"},{"uid":"5291d325-378d-43a7-aeb0-9241bb557d4b","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"provided","passagePhrase":"supported"},{"uid":"1a2ee1c2-4c31-4bb7-a1c3-c87ad9779a50","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"theory","passagePhrase":"account"},{"uid":"3a1ef487-7067-4963-a2d7-5e207fc491ca","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"E short period ... extremely","passagePhrase":"only momentarily"},{"uid":"0147a312-848c-4e27-a2ec-18f4b0172405","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"different locations","passagePhrase":"reside in a different part of the brain"},{"uid":"bd18b12e-f20b-47bf-a6cf-2001a26d4744","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"regulation","passagePhrase":"Such programs"},{"uid":"1e9eb247-bd80-4500-957e-375a2c5aa976","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"fails to prevent misinformation from appearing in the media","passagePhrase":"do not keep false advertising off the airwaves"},{"uid":"0d055aea-adbf-4804-b602-2db266fbd486","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"achieve their purpose","passagePhrase":"be persuasive"},{"uid":"92c339de-0677-491c-a689-c4a14f86d27e","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"understand","passagePhrase":"comprehend"}]},"reading_u2_298":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The Industrial Revolution in Britain</strong></p><p>The Industrial Revolution began in Britain in the mid-1700s and by the 1830s and 1840s had spread to many other parts of the world, including the United States. In Britain, it was a period when a largely rural, agrarian* society was transformed into an industrialised, urban one. Goods that had once been crafted by hand started to be produced in mass quantities by machines in factories, thanks to the invention of steam power and the introduction of new machines and manufacturing techniques in textiles, iron-making and other industries.</p><p>The foundations of the Industrial Revolution date back to the early 1700s, when the English inventor Thomas Newcomen designed the first modern steam engine. Called the 'atmospheric steam engine', Newcomen’s invention was originally used to power machines that pumped water out of mines. In the 1760s, the Scottish engineer James Watt started to adapt one of Newcomen’s models, and succeeded in making it far more efficient. Watt later worked with the English manufacturer Matthew Boulton to invent a new steam engine driven by both the forward and backward strokes of the piston, while the gear <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5fef69e-9a7c-4659-b19a-0b39a19cc5e9\" data-question=\"1\">mechanism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> it was connected to produced rotary <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"966cd57f-5f46-4f39-9f02-367c89487fea\" data-question=\"1\">motion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. It was a key innovation that would allow steam power to spread across British industries.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c616fc2d-2eee-49ec-9c94-68d6498f1637\" data-question=\"2\">The demand for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> coal, which was a relatively cheap energy source, grew rapidly during the Industrial Revolution, as it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51a05ae8-9656-4c5a-9358-24ed2f788c0b\" data-question=\"2\">needed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3de48773-2f04-48cf-9c3e-723301f4cec3\" data-question=\"2\">run<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> not only the factories used to produce manufactured goods, but also steam-powered transportation. In the early 1800s, the English engineer Richard Trevithick built a steam-powered locomotive, and by 1830 goods and passengers were being transported between the industrial centres of Manchester and Liverpool. In addition, steam-powered boats and ships were widely used to carry goods along Britain’s canals as well as across the Atlantic.</p><p>Britain had produced textiles like wool, linen and cotton, for hundreds of years, but prior to the Industrial Revolution, the British textile business was a true ‘cottage industry’, with the work <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4c16103-12c1-4f4b-a5d3-5fa44cf2bc5a\" data-question=\"3\">performed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> in small workshops or even homes by individual spinners, weavers and dyers. Starting in the mid-1700s, innovations like the spinning jenny and the power loom made weaving cloth and spinning yarn and thread much easier. With these machines, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b61d4892-1699-4d46-84f5-f5fb4c145a6e\" data-question=\"4\">relatively little<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> labour was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bf5003ca-a3b3-48bc-b755-b594cd038bfe\" data-question=\"4\">required<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to produce cloth, and the new, mechanised textile factories that opened around the country were quickly able to meet customer demand for cloth both at home and abroad.</p><p>The British iron industry also underwent major change as it adopted new innovations. Chief among the new techniques was the smelting of iron ore with coke (a material made by heating coal) instead of the traditional charcoal. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbc5bcb8-9508-4878-a7af-595b920b8039\" data-question=\"9\">method<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"b3f27b85-31a3-4118-8ca3-7627542d8c98\" data-question=\"9\">cheaper<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09aaf8bb-004f-44d8-bfae-3f9ba355ae15\" data-question=\"5\">produced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"71fbf716-58d2-46e6-a0c6-c870ea08dc2e\" data-question=\"5\">metals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> that were of a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a89e3ca-4c9a-4d2d-a979-a35d9b053686\" data-question=\"5\">higher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> quality, enabling Britain’s iron and steel production to expand in response to demand created by the Napoleonic Wars (1803-15) and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23e3d3c0-b355-428d-9056-d42b635e9ba5\" data-question=\"6\">expansion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of the railways from the 1830s.</p><p>The latter part of the Industrial Revolution also saw key advances in communication methods, as people increasingly saw the need to communicate efficiently over long distances. In 1837, British inventors William Cooke and Charles Wheatstone patented the first commercial telegraphy system. In the 1830s and 1840s, Samuel Morse and other inventors worked on their own versions in the United States. Cooke and Wheatstone’s system was soon used for railway signalling in the UK. As the speed of the new locomotives increased, it was essential to have a fast and effective means of avoiding collisions.</p><p>The impact of the Industrial Revolution on people’s lives was immense. Although many people in Britain had begun moving to the cities from rural areas before the Industrial Revolution, this accelerated dramatically with industrialisation, as the rise of large factories turned smaller towns into major cities in just a few decades. This rapid urbanisation brought significant challenges, as overcrowded cities suffered from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce19b6fc-607a-476d-9efe-6a49e6bfeecc\" data-question=\"7\">pollution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"14feca3d-2e32-4017-a0d7-dd5d9cfb6f8e\" data-question=\"7\">inadequate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> sanitation.</p><p>Although industrialisation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b98eddeb-2485-4909-9959-1adaa15362b1\" data-question=\"11\">increased the country’s economic output overall<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b98eddeb-2485-4909-9959-1adaa15362b1\" data-question=\"11\">improved the standard of living<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> for the middle and upper classes, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e86ab98d-7ef4-4dfd-8d5a-6c760a64efed\" data-question=\"11\">many poor people continued to struggle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. Factory workers had to work long hours in dangerous conditions for extremely low wages. These conditions along with the rapid pace of change fuelled opposition to industrialisation. A group of British workers who became known as ‘Luddites’ were British weavers and textile workers who objected to the increased use of mechanised looms and knitting frames. Many had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ca1b518-6878-4fb8-971d-97fc2ee02eab\" data-question=\"12\">spent years learning their craft<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>, and they feared that unskilled machine operators were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1037559a-a8d7-4a3b-ba2a-b1093f877b6d\" data-question=\"12\">robbing them of their livelihood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. A few desperate weavers began breaking into factories and smashing textile machines. They called themselves Luddites after Ned Ludd, a young apprentice who was rumoured to have wrecked a textile machine in 1779.</p><p>The first major instances of machine breaking took place in 1811 in the city of Nottingham, and the practice soon spread across the country. Machine-breaking Luddites attacked and burned factories, and in some cases they even exchanged gunfire with company guards and soldiers. The workers wanted employers to stop installing new machinery, but the British government responded to the uprisings by making machine-breaking punishable by death. The unrest finally reached its peak in April 1812, when a few Luddites were shot during an attack on a mill near Huddersfield. In the days that followed, other Luddites were arrested, and dozens were hanged or transported to Australia. By 1813, the Luddite resistance had all but vanished.</p><p>* agrarian: relating to the land, especially the use of land for farming</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the notes below.</em></p><p><em>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p><strong>Britain’s Industrial Revolution</strong></p><p><strong>Steam power</strong></p><p>• Newcomen’s steam engine was used in mines to remove water.</p><p>• In Watt and Boulton's steam engine, the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"966cd57f-5f46-4f39-9f02-367c89487fea\" data-question=\"1\">movement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of the 1............................. was linked to a gear <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a5fef69e-9a7c-4659-b19a-0b39a19cc5e9\" data-question=\"1\">system<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.</p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c616fc2d-2eee-49ec-9c94-68d6498f1637\" data-question=\"2\">A greater supply of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> 2..............................was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51a05ae8-9656-4c5a-9358-24ed2f788c0b\" data-question=\"2\">required<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> to power steam engines.</p><p><strong>Textile industry</strong></p><p>• Before the Industrial Revolution, spinners and weavers <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c4c16103-12c1-4f4b-a5d3-5fa44cf2bc5a\" data-question=\"3\">worked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> at home and in 3...............................</p><p>• <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b61d4892-1699-4d46-84f5-f5fb4c145a6e\" data-question=\"4\">Not as much<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> 4 .............................. was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bf5003ca-a3b3-48bc-b755-b594cd038bfe\" data-question=\"4\">needed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> to produce cloth once the spinning jenny and power loom were invented.</p><p><strong>Iron industry</strong></p><p>• Smelting of iron ore with coke <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09aaf8bb-004f-44d8-bfae-3f9ba355ae15\" data-question=\"5\">resulted in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> material that was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a89e3ca-4c9a-4d2d-a979-a35d9b053686\" data-question=\"5\">better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> 5...............................</p><p>• Demand for iron increased with the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23e3d3c0-b355-428d-9056-d42b635e9ba5\" data-question=\"6\">growth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> of the 6...............................</p><p><strong>Communications</strong></p><p>• Cooke and Wheatstone patented the first telegraphy system.</p><p>• The telegraphy system was used to prevent locomotives colliding.</p><p><strong>Urbanisation</strong></p><p>• Small towns turned into cities very quickly.</p><p>• The new cities were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce19b6fc-607a-476d-9efe-6a49e6bfeecc\" data-question=\"7\">dirty<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, crowded and lacked <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"14feca3d-2e32-4017-a0d7-dd5d9cfb6f8e\" data-question=\"7\">sufficient<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> 7...............................</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207233\" id=\"question-wrapper-207233\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PISTON</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207234\" id=\"question-wrapper-207234\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COAL</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207235\" id=\"question-wrapper-207235\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WORKSHOPS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207236\" id=\"question-wrapper-207236\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LABO(U)R</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207237\" id=\"question-wrapper-207237\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">QUALITY</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207238\" id=\"question-wrapper-207238\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RAILWAY(S)</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207239\" id=\"question-wrapper-207239\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SANITATION</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</p><p><em>In boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet, write</em></p><p><em>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</em></p><p><em>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</em></p><p><em>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207240\" id=\"question-wrapper-207240\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Britain’s canal network grew rapidly so that more goods could be transported around the country. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207241\" id=\"question-wrapper-207241\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"b3f27b85-31a3-4118-8ca3-7627542d8c98\" data-question=\"9\">Costs in the iron industry rose<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> when the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cbc5bcb8-9508-4878-a7af-595b920b8039\" data-question=\"9\">technique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> of smelting iron ore with coke was introduced. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207242\" id=\"question-wrapper-207242\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Samuel Morse’s communication system was more reliable than that developed by William Cooke and Charles Wheatstone. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207243\" id=\"question-wrapper-207243\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b98eddeb-2485-4909-9959-1adaa15362b1\" data-question=\"11\">The economic benefits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of industrialisation were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e86ab98d-7ef4-4dfd-8d5a-6c760a64efed\" data-question=\"11\">limited to certain sectors of society<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207244\" id=\"question-wrapper-207244\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ca1b518-6878-4fb8-971d-97fc2ee02eab\" data-question=\"12\">skilled weavers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> believed that the introduction of the new textile machines would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1037559a-a8d7-4a3b-ba2a-b1093f877b6d\" data-question=\"12\">lead to job losses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207245\" id=\"question-wrapper-207245\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There was some sympathy among local people for the Luddites who were arrested near Huddersfield. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a5fef69e-9a7c-4659-b19a-0b39a19cc5e9","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"system","passagePhrase":"mechanism"},{"uid":"966cd57f-5f46-4f39-9f02-367c89487fea","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"movement","passagePhrase":"motion"},{"uid":"c616fc2d-2eee-49ec-9c94-68d6498f1637","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"A greater supply of","passagePhrase":"The demand for"},{"uid":"51a05ae8-9656-4c5a-9358-24ed2f788c0b","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"required","passagePhrase":"needed"},{"uid":"3de48773-2f04-48cf-9c3e-723301f4cec3","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"run"},{"uid":"c4c16103-12c1-4f4b-a5d3-5fa44cf2bc5a","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"worked","passagePhrase":"performed"},{"uid":"b61d4892-1699-4d46-84f5-f5fb4c145a6e","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"Not as much","passagePhrase":"relatively little"},{"uid":"bf5003ca-a3b3-48bc-b755-b594cd038bfe","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"needed","passagePhrase":"required"},{"uid":"cbc5bcb8-9508-4878-a7af-595b920b8039","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"technique","passagePhrase":"method"},{"uid":"09aaf8bb-004f-44d8-bfae-3f9ba355ae15","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"resulted in","passagePhrase":"produced"},{"uid":"71fbf716-58d2-46e6-a0c6-c870ea08dc2e","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"metals"},{"uid":"1a89e3ca-4c9a-4d2d-a979-a35d9b053686","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"better","passagePhrase":"higher"},{"uid":"23e3d3c0-b355-428d-9056-d42b635e9ba5","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"growth","passagePhrase":"expansion"},{"uid":"ce19b6fc-607a-476d-9efe-6a49e6bfeecc","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"dirty","passagePhrase":"pollution"},{"uid":"b98eddeb-2485-4909-9959-1adaa15362b1","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"The economic benefits","passagePhrase":"increased the country’s economic output overall ... improved the standard of living"},{"uid":"e86ab98d-7ef4-4dfd-8d5a-6c760a64efed","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"limited to certain sectors of society","passagePhrase":"many poor people continued to struggle"},{"uid":"2ca1b518-6878-4fb8-971d-97fc2ee02eab","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"skilled weavers","passagePhrase":"spent years learning their craft"},{"uid":"1037559a-a8d7-4a3b-ba2a-b1093f877b6d","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"lead to job losses","passagePhrase":"robbing them of their livelihood"}]},"reading_u2_299":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Athletes and stress</strong></p><p>A</p><p>It isn’t easy being a professional athlete. Not only are the physical demands greater than most people could handle, athletes also face <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ec7d517-7f2d-4bef-9ab4-7557acd9c07f\" data-question=\"16\">intense psychological pressure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> during competition. This is something that British tennis player Emma Raducanu <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96bbf2a0-6714-4e31-8325-99c6b07f991d\" data-question=\"16\">wrote about<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> on social media following her withdrawal from the 2021 Wimbledon tournament. Though the young player had been doing well in the tournament, she began <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ec7d517-7f2d-4bef-9ab4-7557acd9c07f\" data-question=\"16\">having <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4f934eda-b2cf-4334-b139-dcb78b46e422\" data-question=\"23\">difficulty regulating her breathing and heart rate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> during a match, which she later attributed to ‘the accumulation of the excitement and the buzz’.</p><p>B</p><p>For athletes, some level of performance stress is almost unavoidable. But there are many different factors that dictate just how people’s minds and bodies respond to stressful events. Typically, stress is the result of an exchange between two factors: demands and resources. An athlete may feel stressed about an event if they feel the demands on them are greater than they can handle. These demands include the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5d1e5e8-13ba-4e02-adca-6e885a83c16d\" data-question=\"19\">high level of physical and mental effort required to succeed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, and also the athlete’s concerns about the difficulty of the event, their chance of succeeding, and any <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8aacd4fc-294d-415b-8eff-43ef044afd06\" data-question=\"19\">potential dangers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> such as injury. Resources, on the other hand, are a person’s ability to cope with these demands. These include factors such as the competitor’s degree of confidence, how much they believe they can control the situation’s outcome, and whether they’re looking forward to the event or not.</p><p>C</p><p>Each new demand or change in circumstances affects whether a person responds positively or negatively to stress. Typically, the more resources a person feels they have in handling the situation, the more positive their stress response. This positive stress response is called a challenge state. But should the person feel there are too many demands placed on them, the more likely they are to experience a negative stress response - known as a threat state. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2edadd9f-b10a-42ce-b144-3cb272cf4e35\" data-question=\"17\">Research shows<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> that the challenge states lead to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4fde7b2f-42d5-4105-9c7b-4ce2a40d49ed\" data-question=\"17\">good performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, while threat states lead to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"4fde7b2f-42d5-4105-9c7b-4ce2a40d49ed\" data-question=\"17\">poorer performance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. So, in Emma Raducanu’s case, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc451730-fb6f-4c63-8601-6244516ef513\" data-question=\"24\">a much larger audience, higher expectations and facing a more skilful opponent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, may all have led her to feel there were greater demands being placed on her at Wimbledon - but she didn’t have the resources to tackle them. This led to her experiencing a threat response.</p><p>D</p><p>Our challenge and threat responses essentially influence how our body responds to stressful situations, as both <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4146fdb1-158c-4dce-9ead-5d9e540978a7\" data-question=\"14\">affect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> the production of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eeb9b7f2-1861-4c12-8225-3fd03449faed\" data-question=\"14\">adrenaline and cortisol<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> - also known as ‘stress hormones’. During a challenge state, adrenaline increases the amount of blood pumped from the heart and expands the blood vessels, which allows more energy to be delivered to the muscles and brain. This increase of blood and decrease of pressure in the blood vessels has been consistently related to superior sport performance in everything from cricket batting, to golf putting and football penalty taking. But during a threat state, cortisol inhibits the positive effect of adrenaline, resulting in tighter blood vessels, higher blood pressure, slower psychological responses, and a faster heart rate. In short, a threat state makes people more anxious - they make worse decisions and perform more poorly. In tennis players, cortisol has been associated with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd4272c4-890b-4b0b-97ee-0d66cfc72930\" data-question=\"20\">more unsuccessful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> serves and greater anxiety.</p><p>E</p><p>That said, anxiety is also a common experience for athletes when they’re under pressure. Anxiety can increase heart rate and perspiration, cause heart palpitations, muscle tremors and shortness of breath, as well as headaches, nausea, stomach pain, weakness and a desire to escape in more extreme cases. Anxiety can also reduce concentration and self-control and cause overthinking. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c33c836-208a-489d-8742-879eb513aba6\" data-question=\"25\">intensity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> with which a person experiences anxiety depends on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ee22af6-f455-447f-9d33-361f8177033f\" data-question=\"25\">the demands and resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> they have. Anxiety may also manifest itself in the form of excitement or nervousness depending on the stress response. Negative stress responses can be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f94ae76-aa0c-4f8c-9711-e8df37f9bc75\" data-question=\"26\">damaging to both physical and mental health<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> - and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e6dee3e3-0132-4039-b8d2-ffe90526a3bf\" data-question=\"26\">repeated episodes of anxiety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> coupled with negative responses can increase risk of heart disease and depression.</p><p>F</p><p>But there are many <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce03db03-7276-4047-a02c-962521d7c3c4\" data-question=\"15\">ways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> athletes can ensure they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"132c78a7-2b65-490b-9507-80248e6e80a5\" data-question=\"15\">respond positively under pressure<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Positive stress responses can be promoted through the language that they and others - such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a9ac01c-c53b-4604-a6d4-7a2674fd9312\" data-question=\"18\">coaches or parents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> - use. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a9ac01c-c53b-4604-a6d4-7a2674fd9312\" data-question=\"18\">Psychologists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> can also help athletes change how they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac6cc33d-7d1b-4bda-b5d0-bdfbc2b02269\" data-question=\"21\">see<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> their physiological responses - such as helping them <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac6cc33d-7d1b-4bda-b5d0-bdfbc2b02269\" data-question=\"21\">see<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd1fdb1d-a0d9-436b-98ae-4296c3773141\" data-question=\"21\">a higher heart rate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> as excitement, rather than nerves. Developing psychological <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4a14cf8-2d5a-4486-ae4f-e36187160e8b\" data-question=\"22\">skills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, such as visualisation, can also help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86e8c6dd-9c83-4193-a78b-2dce7b013d8b\" data-question=\"22\">decrease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> physiological responses to threat. Visualisation may involve the athlete recreating a mental picture of a time when they performed well, or picturing themselves doing well in the future. This can help create a feeling of control over the stressful event. Recreating competitive pressure during training can also help athletes learn how to deal with stress. An example of this might be scoring athletes against their peers to create a sense of competition. This would increase the demands which players experience compared to a normal training session, while still allowing them to practise coping with stress.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A-F.</p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information?</p><p><em>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p>NB <em>You may use any letter more than once.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207246\" id=\"question-wrapper-207246\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eeb9b7f2-1861-4c12-8225-3fd03449faed\" data-question=\"14\">two chemical compounds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4146fdb1-158c-4dce-9ead-5d9e540978a7\" data-question=\"14\">impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> on performance </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207247\" id=\"question-wrapper-207247\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> examples of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ce03db03-7276-4047-a02c-962521d7c3c4\" data-question=\"15\">strategies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"132c78a7-2b65-490b-9507-80248e6e80a5\" data-question=\"15\">minimising the effects of stress<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207248\" id=\"question-wrapper-207248\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> how a sportsperson <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96bbf2a0-6714-4e31-8325-99c6b07f991d\" data-question=\"16\">accounted for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> their own experience of stress </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207249\" id=\"question-wrapper-207249\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2edadd9f-b10a-42ce-b144-3cb272cf4e35\" data-question=\"17\">study results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> indicating links between stress responses and performance </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207250\" id=\"question-wrapper-207250\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a9ac01c-c53b-4604-a6d4-7a2674fd9312\" data-question=\"18\">people who can influence how athletes perceive their stress responses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the sentences below.</em></p><p><em>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207251\" id=\"question-wrapper-207251\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Performance stress involves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5d1e5e8-13ba-4e02-adca-6e885a83c16d\" data-question=\"19\">many demands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> on the athlete, for example, coping with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8aacd4fc-294d-415b-8eff-43ef044afd06\" data-question=\"19\">the possible risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of.............................. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">INJURY</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207252\" id=\"question-wrapper-207252\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Cortisol can cause tennis players to produce <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fd4272c4-890b-4b0b-97ee-0d66cfc72930\" data-question=\"20\">fewer good<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>............................... </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SERVES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207253\" id=\"question-wrapper-207253\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Psychologists can help athletes to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ac6cc33d-7d1b-4bda-b5d0-bdfbc2b02269\" data-question=\"21\">view<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> their physiological responses as the effect of a positive feeling such as.............................. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EXCITEMENT</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207254\" id=\"question-wrapper-207254\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> ..............................is an example of a psychological <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4a14cf8-2d5a-4486-ae4f-e36187160e8b\" data-question=\"22\">technique<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> which can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86e8c6dd-9c83-4193-a78b-2dce7b013d8b\" data-question=\"22\">reduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"190e80d9-88b9-4505-9df1-c6b746dfb661\" data-question=\"22\">an athlete’s stress responses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VISUALISATION/VISUALIZATION</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct letters in boxes 23 and 24 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p>Which TWO facts about Emma Raducanu’s withdrawal from the Wimbledon tournament are mentioned in the text?</p><ul><li>A the stage at which she dropped out of the tournament</li><li>B <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4f934eda-b2cf-4334-b139-dcb78b46e422\" data-question=\"23\">symptoms of her performance stress<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> at the tournament</li><li>C measures which she had taken to manage her stress levels</li><li>D <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc451730-fb6f-4c63-8601-6244516ef513\" data-question=\"24\">aspects of the Wimbledon tournament<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> which increased her stress levels</li><li>E reactions to her social media posts about her experience at Wimbledon</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207255\" id=\"question-wrapper-207255\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207256\" id=\"question-wrapper-207256\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose TWO letters, A-E.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct letters in boxes 25 and 26 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p>Which TWO facts about anxiety are mentioned in Paragraph E of the text?</p><ul><li>A <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ee22af6-f455-447f-9d33-361f8177033f\" data-question=\"25\">the factors<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> which determine how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c33c836-208a-489d-8742-879eb513aba6\" data-question=\"25\">severe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> it may be</li><li>B how long it takes for its effects to become apparent</li><li>C which of its symptoms is most frequently encountered</li><li>D the types of athletes who are most likely to suffer from it</li><li>E <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f94ae76-aa0c-4f8c-9711-e8df37f9bc75\" data-question=\"26\">the harm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> that can result if athletes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e6dee3e3-0132-4039-b8d2-ffe90526a3bf\" data-question=\"26\">experience it too often<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span></li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207257\" id=\"question-wrapper-207257\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207258\" id=\"question-wrapper-207258\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"6ec7d517-7f2d-4bef-9ab4-7557acd9c07f","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"intense psychological pressure ... having difficulty regulating her breathing and heart rate"},{"uid":"96bbf2a0-6714-4e31-8325-99c6b07f991d","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"accounted for","passagePhrase":"wrote about"},{"uid":"4f934eda-b2cf-4334-b139-dcb78b46e422","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"symptoms of her performance stress","passagePhrase":"difficulty regulating her breathing and heart rate"},{"uid":"e5d1e5e8-13ba-4e02-adca-6e885a83c16d","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"many demands","passagePhrase":"high level of physical and mental effort required to succeed"},{"uid":"8aacd4fc-294d-415b-8eff-43ef044afd06","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"the possible risk","passagePhrase":"potential dangers"},{"uid":"2edadd9f-b10a-42ce-b144-3cb272cf4e35","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"study results","passagePhrase":"Research shows"},{"uid":"dc451730-fb6f-4c63-8601-6244516ef513","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"aspects of the Wimbledon tournament","passagePhrase":"a much larger audience, higher expectations and facing a more skilful opponent"},{"uid":"4146fdb1-158c-4dce-9ead-5d9e540978a7","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"impact","passagePhrase":"affect"},{"uid":"eeb9b7f2-1861-4c12-8225-3fd03449faed","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"two chemical compounds","passagePhrase":"adrenaline and cortisol"},{"uid":"fd4272c4-890b-4b0b-97ee-0d66cfc72930","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"fewer good","passagePhrase":"more unsuccessful"},{"uid":"6c33c836-208a-489d-8742-879eb513aba6","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"severe","passagePhrase":"intensity"},{"uid":"2ee22af6-f455-447f-9d33-361f8177033f","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"the factors","passagePhrase":"the demands and resources"},{"uid":"7f94ae76-aa0c-4f8c-9711-e8df37f9bc75","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"the harm","passagePhrase":"damaging to both physical and mental health"},{"uid":"e6dee3e3-0132-4039-b8d2-ffe90526a3bf","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"experience it too often","passagePhrase":"repeated episodes of anxiety"},{"uid":"ce03db03-7276-4047-a02c-962521d7c3c4","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"strategies","passagePhrase":"ways"},{"uid":"132c78a7-2b65-490b-9507-80248e6e80a5","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"minimising the effects of stress","passagePhrase":"respond positively under pressure"},{"uid":"9a9ac01c-c53b-4604-a6d4-7a2674fd9312","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"people who can influence how athletes perceive their stress responses","passagePhrase":"coaches or parents ... Psychologists"},{"uid":"ac6cc33d-7d1b-4bda-b5d0-bdfbc2b02269","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"view","passagePhrase":"see ... see"},{"uid":"cd1fdb1d-a0d9-436b-98ae-4296c3773141","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"a higher heart rate"},{"uid":"e4a14cf8-2d5a-4486-ae4f-e36187160e8b","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"technique","passagePhrase":"skills"},{"uid":"86e8c6dd-9c83-4193-a78b-2dce7b013d8b","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"reduce","passagePhrase":"decrease"},{"uid":"190e80d9-88b9-4505-9df1-c6b746dfb661","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"an athlete’s stress responses","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_300":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>An inquiry into the existence of the gifted child</strong></p><p>Let us start by looking at a modem ‘genius’, Maryam Mirzakhani, who died at the early age of 40. She was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ea81624-db3e-45b9-a62d-e0618f9dc130\" data-question=\"27\">the only woman to win<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> the Fields Medal - <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6bf441a3-ce57-414c-98b1-6d12f927526c\" data-question=\"27\">the mathematical equivalent of a Nobel prize<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. It would be easy to assume that someone as special as Mirzakhani must have been one of those ‘gifted’ children, those who have an extraordinary ability in a specific sphere of activity or knowledge. But look closer and a different story emerges. Mirzakhani was born in Tehran, Iran. She went to a highly selective girls’ school but maths wasn’t her <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82e82782-a2c1-40d8-843a-194a7bf1574f\" data-question=\"28\">interest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> - reading was. She loved novels and would read anything she could lay her hands on. As for maths, she did rather <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c96ed3ea-efaf-4b6c-bf13-dec64ba27c04\" data-question=\"28\">poorly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> at it for the first couple of years in her middle school, but became interested when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8d70c9c5-fc6e-4fbe-b817-735d08407e6b\" data-question=\"28\">her <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72f4cf74-670c-4e42-81c8-b9f1e8b74a05\" data-question=\"29\">elder brother<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> told her about what he’d learned. He shared a famous <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23657fb2-49a6-4dc2-bf7b-fb520379c241\" data-question=\"29\">maths problem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> from a magazine that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72690858-0746-4b95-8f9e-735db201df70\" data-question=\"29\">fascinated<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> her - and she was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72690858-0746-4b95-8f9e-735db201df70\" data-question=\"29\">hooked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</p><p>In adult life it is clear that she was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7534d078-b2fa-4e97-a43f-89ed62793897\" data-question=\"30\">curious, excited<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> by what she did and also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"faaafba3-4cd2-415c-9968-d0f6de1bd96e\" data-question=\"30\">resolute in the face of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c19c4c6-7e64-4b61-aa3e-e648d2768a47\" data-question=\"30\">setbacks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. One of her comments sums it up. ‘Of course, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea1615c7-2c4b-4308-b5ff-a4aae903a232\" data-question=\"31\">the most<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e63ea502-ce51-487f-992a-831a778e1dd7\" data-question=\"31\">rewarding<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> part is the “Aha” moment, the excitement of discovery and enjoyment of understanding something new . . . But most of the time, doing mathematics for me is like being on a long hike with no trail and no end in sight.’ That trail took her to the heights of original <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fac2ceae-474b-48c2-92f2-ffc635a6acd8\" data-question=\"32\">research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> into mathematics.</p><p>Is her background unusual? Apparently not. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f34abc54-c67d-453a-aa41-710fa18ae728\" data-question=\"33\">Most Nobel prize winners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b23b0db-d2a8-4968-9726-4841e34fb3fc\" data-question=\"33\">were unexceptional in childhood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. Einstein was slow to talk as a baby. He failed the general part of the entry test to Zurich Polytechnic - though they let him in because of high physics and maths scores. He struggled at work initially, but he kept plugging away and eventually rewrote the laws of Newtonian mechanics with his theory of relativity.</p><p>There has been a considerable amount of research on high performance over the last century that suggests it goes way beyond tested intelligence. On top of that, research is clear that brains are flexible, new neural pathways can be created, and IQ isn't fixed. For example, just because you can read stories with hundreds of pages at the age of five doesn’t mean you will still be ahead of your contemporaries in your teens.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccba1374-a552-426e-b5c3-ea92f344a428\" data-question=\"35\">While the jury is out on<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"73d7fe19-8718-4659-af61-750b19df8ca8\" data-question=\"35\">giftedness being innate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and other factors potentially making the difference, what is certain is that the behaviours associated with high levels of performance arc replicable and most can be taught - even traits such as curiosity.</p><p>According to my colleague Prof Deborah Eyre, with whom I’ve collaborated on the book <em>Great Minds and I low to Grow Them</em>, the latest neuroscience and psychological research suggests most individuals can reach levels of performance associated in school with the gifted and talented. However, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8adc9789-5672-45d8-8d23-26a7dd6be66e\" data-question=\"38\">must be taught the right attitudes and approaches to their learning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> and develop the attributes of high performers - curiosity, persistence and hard work, for example - an approach Eyre calls ‘high performance learning’. Critically, they need the right support in developing those approaches at home as well as at school.</p><p>Prof Anders Ericsson, an eminent education psychologist at Florida State University, US, is the co-author of <em>Peak: Secrets from the New Science of Expertise.</em> After research going back to 1980 into diverse achievements, from music to memory to sport, he doesn’t think <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd587913-bf84-4eae-9afa-324ff98c3735\" data-question=\"39\">unique and innate talents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21a1c10c-1ece-4250-8a48-a4c5f2db8024\" data-question=\"39\">at the heart of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> performance. Deliberate practice, that stretches you every step of the way, and around 10,000 hours of it, is what produces the goods. It’s not a magic number - the highest performers move on to doing a whole lot more, of course. Ericsson’s memory research is particularly interesting because random students, trained in memory techniques for the study, went on to outperform others thought to have innately superior memories - those who you might call gifted.</p><p>But it is perhaps the work of Benjamin Bloom, another distinguished American educationist working in the 1980s, that gives the most pause for thought. Bloom’s team looked at a group of extraordinarily high achieving people in disciplines as varied as ballet, swimming, piano, tennis, maths, sculpture and neurology. He found a pattern of parents encouraging and supporting their children, often in areas they enjoyed themselves. Bloom’s outstanding people had worked very hard and consistently at something they had become hooked on when at a young age, and their parents all emerged as having strong work ethics themselves.</p><p>Eyre says we know how high performers learn. From that she has developed a high performing learning approach. She is working on this with a group of schools, both in Britain and abroad. Some spin-off research, which looked in detail at 24 of the 3,000 children being studied who were succeeding despite difficult circumstances, found something remarkable. Half were getting free school meals because of poverty, more than half were living with a single parent, and four in five were living in disadvantaged areas. Interviews uncovered strong evidence of an adult or adults in the child’s life who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87c9cbe7-8e83-4c04-a337-9507c581067f\" data-question=\"40\">valued and supported education<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, either in the immediate or extended family or in the child’s wider community. Children talked about the need to work hard at school, to listen in class and keep trying.</p><p>Let us end with Einstein, the epitome of a genius. He clearly had curiosity, character and determination. He struggled against rejection in early life but was undeterred. Did he think he was a genius or even gifted? He once wrote: ‘It’s not that I’m so smart, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1106971a-82fd-49bc-8b7e-338f8d841c2f\" data-question=\"37\">it’s just that I stay with problems longer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Most people say it is the intellect which makes a great scientist. They are wrong: it is character.’</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the summary using the list of phrases, A-K, below.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct letter, A-K, in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p> </p><p><strong>A </strong><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"82e82782-a2c1-40d8-843a-194a7bf1574f\" data-question=\"28\">appeal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <strong>B </strong><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"faaafba3-4cd2-415c-9968-d0f6de1bd96e\" data-question=\"30\">determined<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> <strong>C</strong> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72690858-0746-4b95-8f9e-735db201df70\" data-question=\"29\">intrigued<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span></p><p><strong>D </strong>single <strong>E </strong>achievement <strong>F </strong>devoted</p><p><strong>G </strong>involved <strong>H </strong>unique <strong>1 </strong>innovative</p><p><strong>J </strong><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e63ea502-ce51-487f-992a-831a778e1dd7\" data-question=\"31\">satisfaction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <strong>K </strong>intent</p><p><strong>Maryam Mirzakhani</strong></p><p>Maryam Mirzakhani is regarded as 27..............................in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6bf441a3-ce57-414c-98b1-6d12f927526c\" data-question=\"27\">the field of mathematics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> because she was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ea81624-db3e-45b9-a62d-e0618f9dc130\" data-question=\"27\">the only female holder<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> of the prestigious Fields Medal - a record that she retained at the time of her death. However, maths held little 28.............................for her as a child and in fact her performance was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c96ed3ea-efaf-4b6c-bf13-dec64ba27c04\" data-question=\"28\">below average<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> until she was 29..............................by a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"23657fb2-49a6-4dc2-bf7b-fb520379c241\" data-question=\"29\">difficult puzzle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> that one of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8d70c9c5-fc6e-4fbe-b817-735d08407e6b\" data-question=\"28\">her <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"72f4cf74-670c-4e42-81c8-b9f1e8b74a05\" data-question=\"29\">siblings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> showed her.</p><p>Later, as a professional mathematician, she had <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7534d078-b2fa-4e97-a43f-89ed62793897\" data-question=\"30\">an inquiring mind<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> and proved herself to be 30..............................<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c19c4c6-7e64-4b61-aa3e-e648d2768a47\" data-question=\"30\">when things did not go smoothly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. She said she got <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea1615c7-2c4b-4308-b5ff-a4aae903a232\" data-question=\"31\">the greatest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> 31..............................from making ground-breaking discoveries and in fact she was responsible for some extremely 32............................. mathematical <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fac2ceae-474b-48c2-92f2-ffc635a6acd8\" data-question=\"32\">studies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207259\" id=\"question-wrapper-207259\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207260\" id=\"question-wrapper-207260\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207261\" id=\"question-wrapper-207261\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207262\" id=\"question-wrapper-207262\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207263\" id=\"question-wrapper-207263\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">J</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207264\" id=\"question-wrapper-207264\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">I</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</p><p><em>In boxes 33-37 on your answer sheet, write</em></p><p><em>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</em></p><p><em>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</em></p><p><em>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207265\" id=\"question-wrapper-207265\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f34abc54-c67d-453a-aa41-710fa18ae728\" data-question=\"33\">Many people who ended up winning prestigious intellectual prizes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b23b0db-d2a8-4968-9726-4841e34fb3fc\" data-question=\"33\">only reached an average standard when young<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207266\" id=\"question-wrapper-207266\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Einstein’s failures as a young man were due to his lack of confidence. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207267\" id=\"question-wrapper-207267\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ccba1374-a552-426e-b5c3-ea92f344a428\" data-question=\"35\">It is difficult to reach agreement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> on whether <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"73d7fe19-8718-4659-af61-750b19df8ca8\" data-question=\"35\">some children are actually born gifted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207268\" id=\"question-wrapper-207268\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Einstein was upset by the public’s view of his life’s work. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207269\" id=\"question-wrapper-207269\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"1106971a-82fd-49bc-8b7e-338f8d841c2f\" data-question=\"37\">Einstein put his success down to the speed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> at which he dealt with scientific questions. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct letter in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207270\" id=\"question-wrapper-207270\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does Eyre believe is needed for children to equal ‘gifted’ standards? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. strict discipline from the teaching staff</li> <li>B. assistance from their peers in the classroom</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8adc9789-5672-45d8-8d23-26a7dd6be66e\" data-question=\"38\">the development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> of a spirit of inquiry towards their studies</li> <li>D. the determination to surpass everyone else’s achievements</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207271\" id=\"question-wrapper-207271\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the result of Ericsson s research? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Very gifted students do not need to work on improving memory skills.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd587913-bf84-4eae-9afa-324ff98c3735\" data-question=\"39\">Being born with a special gift<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> is not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21a1c10c-1ece-4250-8a48-a4c5f2db8024\" data-question=\"39\">the key factor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> in becoming expert.</li> <li>C. Including time for physical exercise is crucial in raising performance.</li> <li>D. 10,000 hours of relevant and demanding work will create a genius.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207272\" id=\"question-wrapper-207272\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the penultimate paragraph, it is stated the key to some deprived children’s success is </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. a regular and nourishing diet at home.</li> <li>B. the loving support of more than one parent.</li> <li>C. a community which has well-funded facilities for learning.</li> <li>D. the guidance of someone who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"87c9cbe7-8e83-4c04-a337-9507c581067f\" data-question=\"40\">recognises the benefits of learning<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"1ea81624-db3e-45b9-a62d-e0618f9dc130","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"the only female holder","passagePhrase":"the only woman to win"},{"uid":"6bf441a3-ce57-414c-98b1-6d12f927526c","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"the field of mathematics","passagePhrase":"the mathematical equivalent of a Nobel prize"},{"uid":"82e82782-a2c1-40d8-843a-194a7bf1574f","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"appeal","passagePhrase":"interest"},{"uid":"c96ed3ea-efaf-4b6c-bf13-dec64ba27c04","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"below average","passagePhrase":"poorly"},{"uid":"8d70c9c5-fc6e-4fbe-b817-735d08407e6b","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"her siblings","passagePhrase":"her elder brother"},{"uid":"72f4cf74-670c-4e42-81c8-b9f1e8b74a05","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"siblings","passagePhrase":"elder brother"},{"uid":"23657fb2-49a6-4dc2-bf7b-fb520379c241","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"difficult puzzle","passagePhrase":"maths problem"},{"uid":"72690858-0746-4b95-8f9e-735db201df70","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"intrigued","passagePhrase":"fascinated ... hooked"},{"uid":"7534d078-b2fa-4e97-a43f-89ed62793897","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"an inquiring mind","passagePhrase":"curious, excited"},{"uid":"faaafba3-4cd2-415c-9968-d0f6de1bd96e","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"determined","passagePhrase":"resolute in the face of setbacks"},{"uid":"6c19c4c6-7e64-4b61-aa3e-e648d2768a47","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"when things did not go smoothly","passagePhrase":"setbacks"},{"uid":"ea1615c7-2c4b-4308-b5ff-a4aae903a232","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"the greatest","passagePhrase":"the most"},{"uid":"e63ea502-ce51-487f-992a-831a778e1dd7","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"satisfaction","passagePhrase":"rewarding"},{"uid":"fac2ceae-474b-48c2-92f2-ffc635a6acd8","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"studies","passagePhrase":"research"},{"uid":"f34abc54-c67d-453a-aa41-710fa18ae728","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Many people who ended up winning prestigious intellectual prizes","passagePhrase":"Most Nobel prize winners"},{"uid":"4b23b0db-d2a8-4968-9726-4841e34fb3fc","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"only reached an average standard when young","passagePhrase":"were unexceptional in childhood"},{"uid":"ccba1374-a552-426e-b5c3-ea92f344a428","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"It is difficult to reach agreement","passagePhrase":"While the jury is out on"},{"uid":"73d7fe19-8718-4659-af61-750b19df8ca8","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"some children are actually born gifted","passagePhrase":"giftedness being innate"},{"uid":"8adc9789-5672-45d8-8d23-26a7dd6be66e","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"the development","passagePhrase":"must be taught the right attitudes and approaches to their learning"},{"uid":"bd587913-bf84-4eae-9afa-324ff98c3735","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Being born with a special gift","passagePhrase":"unique and innate talents"},{"uid":"21a1c10c-1ece-4250-8a48-a4c5f2db8024","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"the key factor","passagePhrase":"at the heart of"},{"uid":"87c9cbe7-8e83-4c04-a337-9507c581067f","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"recognises the benefits of learning","passagePhrase":"valued and supported education"}]},"reading_u2_301":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Archaeologists discover evidence of prehistoric island settlers</strong> </p><p>In early April 2019, Dr Ceri Shipton and his colleagues from Australian National University became the first archaeologists to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7590a119-b46b-4694-98e9-6c7a11a67c7e\" data-question=\"1\">explore<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> Obi, one of many tropical islands in Indonesia’s Maluku Utara province. The research team’s discoveries suggest that the prehistoric people who lived on Obi were adept on both land and sea, hunting in the dense rainforest, foraging on the seashore, and possibly even voyaging between islands.</p><p>The excavations were part of a project to learn more about how people first dispersed from mainland Asia, through the Indonesian archipelago and into the prehistoric continent that once connected Australia and New Guinea. The team’s earlier research suggested that the northernmost islands in the group, known as the Wallacean islands, including Obi, would have offered the easiest migration route. It also seemed likely that these islands were crucial ‘stepping stones’ on humans’ island-hopping voyages through this region millennia ago. But to support this idea, they needed archaeological evidence for humans living in this remote area in the ancient past. So, they travelled to Obi to look for sites that might reveal evidence of early occupation.</p><p>Just inland from the village of Kelo on Obi’s northern coast, Shipton and his colleagues found two caves <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ea13d83-f0a8-4837-87bb-92d59baa472d\" data-question=\"8\">containing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> prehistoric rock shelters that were suitable for excavation. With the permission and help of the local people of Kelo, they dug a small test excavation in each shelter. There they found numerous artefacts, including fragments of axes, some dating to about 14,000 years ago. The earliest axes at Kelo were made using clam shells. Axes made from clam shells from roughly the same time <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"49b2933e-0c8a-40ba-97e1-3d17138c8010\" data-question=\"2\">had also previously been found elsewhere<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in this region, including on the nearby island of Gebe to the northeast. As on Gebe, it is highly likely that Obi’s axes were used in the construction of canoes, thus allowing these early peoples to maintain connections between communities on neighbouring islands.</p><p>The oldest cultural layers from the Kelo site provided the team with the earliest record for human occupation on Obi, dating back around 18,000 years. At this time the climate was drier and colder than today, and the island’s dense rainforests would likely have been much less impenetrable than they are now. Sea levels were about 120 metres lower, meaning <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55ff85ad-b33a-4a09-8cc1-4240f3a7b44b\" data-question=\"3\">Obi was a much larger island<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, encompassing what is today the separate island of Bisa, as well as several other small islands nearby.</p><p>Roughly 11,700 years ago, as the most recent ice age ended, the climate became significantly warmer and wetter, no doubt making Obi’s jungle much thicker. According to the researchers, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"effe1d99-1ce6-41fa-8e8d-ea94d260b104\" data-question=\"5\">it is no coincidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d742e961-b9be-421e-8e8e-9f69eb66363e\" data-question=\"5\">around this time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> the first axes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3fd2ad9a-bbb9-4552-a577-2095323fcbcf\" data-question=\"5\">crafted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> from stone rather than sea shells appear, likely in response to their heavy-duty use for clearing and modification of the increasingly dense rainforest. While stone takes about twice as long to grind into an axe compared to shell, the harder material keeps its sharp edge for longer.</p><p>Judging by the bones which the researchers unearthed in the Kelo caves, people living there mainly <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b071dfc-7f92-4fba-a82b-a525df20a839\" data-question=\"10\">hunted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> the Rothschild’s cuscus, a possum-like creature that still lives on Obi today. As the forest grew more dense, people probably used axes to clear patches of forest and make hunting easier.</p><p>Shipton’s team’s excavation of the shelters at the Kelo site unearthed a volcanic glass substance called obsidian, which must have been brought over from another island, as there is no known source on Obi. It also revealed particular types of beads, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79ad126b-d1d9-4648-a3e9-6684358c32dc\" data-question=\"11\">similar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> to those previously found on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e7e1fa9a-50d5-44fc-afbf-0f4873b10f23\" data-question=\"11\">islands in southern Wallacea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. These finds again support the idea that Obi islanders routinely travelled to other islands.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ed338d98-fde3-4632-a26f-8026bd02b1ca\" data-question=\"7\">The excavations suggest<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> people successfully <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"722228fb-1ee4-4a53-a932-a28c19e2e183\" data-question=\"7\">lived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in the two Kelo shelters for about 10,000 years. But then, about 8,000 years ago, both were abandoned. Did the residents leave Obi completely, or move elsewhere on the island? Perhaps the jungle had grown so thick that axes were no longer a match for the dense undergrowth. Perhaps people simply moved to the coast and turned to fishing rather than hunting as a means of survival.</p><p>Whatever the reason for the departure, there is no evidence for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"722228fb-1ee4-4a53-a932-a28c19e2e183\" data-question=\"7\">use<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> of the Kelo shelters after this time, until about 1,000 years ago, when they were re-occupied by people who owned pottery as well as items made out of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e2a6ef7-0f39-464b-946f-0048c36c7cad\" data-question=\"12\">gold and silver<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. It seems likely, in view of Obi’s location, that this final phase of occupation also saw the Kelo shelters used by people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"748fc0f6-0fbf-4b42-892f-45ad2d77cfd5\" data-question=\"13\">involved in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the historic <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1daa69b-016d-4139-87bc-0724eb3c570e\" data-question=\"13\">trade<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in spices between the Maluku islands and the rest of the world.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</p><p><em>In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write</em></p><p><em>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</em></p><p><em>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</em></p><p><em>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207273\" id=\"question-wrapper-207273\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Archaeological <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7590a119-b46b-4694-98e9-6c7a11a67c7e\" data-question=\"1\">research<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> had taken place on the island of Obi <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"354d210c-6ff2-4945-85cf-8131352038dc\" data-question=\"1\">before the arrival of Ceri Shipton and his colleagues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207274\" id=\"question-wrapper-207274\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> At the Kelo sites, the researchers <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"49b2933e-0c8a-40ba-97e1-3d17138c8010\" data-question=\"2\">found the first clam shell<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> axes ever to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"46d8ec9c-8b9d-437d-973d-816a0e794b04\" data-question=\"2\">discovered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in the region. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207275\" id=\"question-wrapper-207275\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"55ff85ad-b33a-4a09-8cc1-4240f3a7b44b\" data-question=\"3\">The size of Obi today is less than it was<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> 18,000 years ago. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207276\" id=\"question-wrapper-207276\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A change in the climate around 11,700 years ago had a greater impact on Obi than on the surrounding islands. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207277\" id=\"question-wrapper-207277\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The researchers believe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"effe1d99-1ce6-41fa-8e8d-ea94d260b104\" data-question=\"5\">there is a connection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d742e961-b9be-421e-8e8e-9f69eb66363e\" data-question=\"5\">warmer, wetter weather<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56daa0f0-1fdb-4217-bd9e-7a939d50b453\" data-question=\"5\">a change in the material used<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3fd2ad9a-bbb9-4552-a577-2095323fcbcf\" data-question=\"5\">make<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> axes. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207278\" id=\"question-wrapper-207278\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Shipton’s team were surprised to find evidence of the Obi islanders’ hunting practices. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207279\" id=\"question-wrapper-207279\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ed338d98-fde3-4632-a26f-8026bd02b1ca\" data-question=\"7\">It is thought that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> the Kelo shelters were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"722228fb-1ee4-4a53-a932-a28c19e2e183\" data-question=\"7\">occupied<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> continuously until about 1,000 years ago. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the notes below.</em></p><p><em>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p><strong>Archaeological findings on Obi</strong></p><p>Excavations of rock shelters <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ea13d83-f0a8-4837-87bb-92d59baa472d\" data-question=\"8\">inside<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> 8.............................near the village of Kelo revealed:</p><p>• axes from around 14,000 years ago, probably used to make canoes</p><p>• axes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"123fcc00-39af-4e8a-8585-55dfeb4a62c6\" data-question=\"9\">made out of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> 9 ................................dating from around 11,700 years ago</p><p>• 10..............................of an animal: evidence of what ancient islanders <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8b071dfc-7f92-4fba-a82b-a525df20a839\" data-question=\"10\">ate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span></p><p>• evidence of travel between islands:</p><p> - obsidian: a material that is not found naturally on Obi</p><p> - 11..............................which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"79ad126b-d1d9-4648-a3e9-6684358c32dc\" data-question=\"11\">resembled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> ones found on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e7e1fa9a-50d5-44fc-afbf-0f4873b10f23\" data-question=\"11\">other islands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>.</p><p>It is thought that from 8,000 years ago, Obi islanders:</p><p>• may have switched from hunting to fishing</p><p>• had 12..............................as well as items made out of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2e2a6ef7-0f39-464b-946f-0048c36c7cad\" data-question=\"12\">metal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span></p><p>• probably <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"748fc0f6-0fbf-4b42-892f-45ad2d77cfd5\" data-question=\"13\">took part in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> the production and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1daa69b-016d-4139-87bc-0724eb3c570e\" data-question=\"13\">sale<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> of 13..............................</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207280\" id=\"question-wrapper-207280\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CAVES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207281\" id=\"question-wrapper-207281\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STONE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207282\" id=\"question-wrapper-207282\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BONES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207283\" id=\"question-wrapper-207283\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BEADS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207284\" id=\"question-wrapper-207284\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POTTERY</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207285\" id=\"question-wrapper-207285\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPICES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"7590a119-b46b-4694-98e9-6c7a11a67c7e","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"research","passagePhrase":"explore"},{"uid":"3ea13d83-f0a8-4837-87bb-92d59baa472d","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"inside","passagePhrase":"containing"},{"uid":"55ff85ad-b33a-4a09-8cc1-4240f3a7b44b","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"The size of Obi today is less than it was","passagePhrase":"Obi was a much larger island"},{"uid":"effe1d99-1ce6-41fa-8e8d-ea94d260b104","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"there is a connection","passagePhrase":"it is no coincidence"},{"uid":"d742e961-b9be-421e-8e8e-9f69eb66363e","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"warmer, wetter weather","passagePhrase":"around this time"},{"uid":"3fd2ad9a-bbb9-4552-a577-2095323fcbcf","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"make","passagePhrase":"crafted"},{"uid":"8b071dfc-7f92-4fba-a82b-a525df20a839","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"ate","passagePhrase":"hunted"},{"uid":"79ad126b-d1d9-4648-a3e9-6684358c32dc","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"resembled","passagePhrase":"similar"},{"uid":"e7e1fa9a-50d5-44fc-afbf-0f4873b10f23","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"other islands","passagePhrase":"islands in southern Wallacea"},{"uid":"ed338d98-fde3-4632-a26f-8026bd02b1ca","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"It is thought that","passagePhrase":"The excavations suggest"},{"uid":"722228fb-1ee4-4a53-a932-a28c19e2e183","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"occupied","passagePhrase":"lived ... use"},{"uid":"2e2a6ef7-0f39-464b-946f-0048c36c7cad","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"metal","passagePhrase":"gold and silver"},{"uid":"748fc0f6-0fbf-4b42-892f-45ad2d77cfd5","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"took part in","passagePhrase":"involved in"},{"uid":"a1daa69b-016d-4139-87bc-0724eb3c570e","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"sale","passagePhrase":"trade"},{"uid":"46d8ec9c-8b9d-437d-973d-816a0e794b04","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"discovered","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"56daa0f0-1fdb-4217-bd9e-7a939d50b453","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"a change in the material used","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"123fcc00-39af-4e8a-8585-55dfeb4a62c6","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"made out of","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_302":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The global importance of wetlands</strong></p><p>A</p><p>Wetlands are areas where water covers the soil, or is present either at or near the surface of the soil, for all or part of the year. These are complex ecosystems, rich in unique plant and animal life. But according to the World Wide Fund for Nature (WWFN), <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83943f25-f95b-4ce8-9184-2a1daba4e72e\" data-question=\"15\">half<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of the world’s wetlands have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9526ef28-179d-492d-b17d-3bf90d0299d7\" data-question=\"15\">disappeared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> since 1990 - converted or destroyed for commercial development, drainage schemes and the extraction of minerals and peat*. Many of those that remain have been damaged by agricultural pesticides and fertilisers, industrial pollutants, and construction works.</p><p>B</p><p>Throughout history, humans have gathered around wetlands, and their fertile ecosystems have played an important part in human development. Consequently, they are of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d26fca31-2583-46e5-89e2-57ed489d6535\" data-question=\"17\">considerable religious, historical and archaeological<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e2b0674c-e93e-4566-a93b-c06a7b512759\" data-question=\"17\">value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> to many communities around the world. ‘Wetlands directly support the livelihoods and well-being of millions of people,’ says Dr Matthew McCartney, principal researcher and hydrologist at the International Water Management Institute (IWMI). ‘In many developing countries, large numbers of people are dependent on wetland agriculture for their livelihoods.’</p><p>C</p><p>They also serve a crucial environmental purpose. ‘Wetlands are one of the key tools in mitigating climate change across the planet,’ says Pieter van Eijk, head of Climate Adaptation at Wetlands International (WI), pointing to their use as buffers that protect coastal areas from sea-level rise and extreme weather events such as hurricanes and flooding. Wetland coastal forests provide food and water, as well as shelter from storms, and WI and other agencies are working to restore those forests which have been lost. ‘It can be as <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"78959e35-6ce2-4fc4-aba1-ff1c8b9f5e87\" data-question=\"26\">simple<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d18478e9-fcce-4513-8b75-0bbf0e74eaa7\" data-question=\"26\">planting a few trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> per hectare to create shade and substantially change a microclimate,’ he says. ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d18478e9-fcce-4513-8b75-0bbf0e74eaa7\" data-question=\"26\">Implementing climate change projects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> isn’t so much about money.’</p><p>D</p><p>The world’s wetlands are, unfortunately, rich sources for in-demand commodities, such as palm oil and pulpwood. Peatlands - wetlands with a waterlogged organic soil layer - are particularly targeted. When peatlands are drained for cultivation, they become net <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4afe3597-1a29-490c-9fbb-f0700fe8d4a1\" data-question=\"18\">carbon emitters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> instead of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ef7940a-147e-43e0-bf8e-39cad88f71f1\" data-question=\"18\">active carbon stores<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, and, according to Marcel Silvius, head of Climate-smart Land-use at WI, this practice causes six per cent of all global carbon emissions. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"31843bc3-7412-4110-9996-ca5265541f03\" data-question=\"19\">clearance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of peatlands for planting also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de542ac0-5888-4bf5-bc9c-0b926c6d2cf9\" data-question=\"19\">increases the risk<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of forest fires, which release huge amounts of CO2 ‘We’re seeing huge peatland forests with extremely high biodiversity value being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88f186d9-797d-4893-8d10-246d20b5808f\" data-question=\"20\">lost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> for a few decades of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61e9d479-ce14-4d60-a5fd-f6a6f5da7f0f\" data-question=\"20\">oil palm revenues<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>,’ says Silvius.</p><p>E</p><p>The damage starts when logging companies arrive to clear the trees. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8f14286a-2ba3-4f53-ad91-aad2b1dfac55\" data-question=\"21\">dig<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> ditches to enter the peat swamps by boat and then float the logs out the same way. These are then used to drain water out of the peatlands to allow for the planting of corn, oil palms or pulpwood trees. Once the water has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6d563f1-4fc5-412b-97e2-d0eec6ea5b14\" data-question=\"22\">drained away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, bacteria and fungi then break down the carbon in the peat and turn it into CO2 and methane. Meanwhile, the remainder of the solid matter in the peat starts to move downwards, in a process known as subsidence**. Peat comprises 90 per cent water, so this is one of the most alarming consequences of peatland clearances. ‘In the tropics, peat subsides at about four centimetres a year, so within half a century, very large landscapes on Sumatra and Borneo will become flooded as the peat drops below water level,’ says Silvius. ‘It’s a huge catastrophe that’s in preparation. Some provinces will lose 40 per cent of their landmass.’</p><p>F</p><p>And while these industries affect wetlands in ways that can easily be documented, Dr Dave Tickner of the WWFN believes that more subtle impacts can be even more devastating. ‘Sediment run-off and fertilisers can be pretty invisible,’ says Tickner. ‘Over-extraction of water is equally invisible. You do get shock stories about rivers running red, or even catching fire, but there’s seldom one big impact that really hurts a wetland.’ Tickner does not blame anyone for deliberate damage, however. ‘I’ve worked on wetland issues for 20 years and have never met anybody who wanted <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2809af02-cf19-4310-858b-fd3a4bf15303\" data-question=\"25\">to damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> a wetland,’ he says. ‘It isn’t something that people generally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8d1ee22c-de95-4d23-b875-90c7f1841f35\" data-question=\"25\">set out to do<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. Quite often, the effects simply come from people trying to make a living.’</p><p>G</p><p>Silvius also acknowledges the importance of income generation. ‘It’s not that we just want to restore the biodiversity of wetlands - which we do - but we recognise there’s a need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"566cb627-69c7-4886-af9a-5527fa56b1c2\" data-question=\"14\">provide an income<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"17ab3d26-7301-46f5-8412-a53f82a403c8\" data-question=\"14\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5de4238-46db-42cf-abd0-e4a3cf85096e\" data-question=\"23\">local people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.’ This approach is supported by IWMI. ‘The idea is that people in a developing country will only protect wetlands if they value and profit from them,’ says McCartney. ‘For sustainability, it’s essential that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"17ab3d26-7301-46f5-8412-a53f82a403c8\" data-question=\"14\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5de4238-46db-42cf-abd0-e4a3cf85096e\" data-question=\"23\">local people<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3bcd3486-c5ac-470e-8fb9-b99ca118eddc\" data-question=\"23\">involved in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c9617aa-6f1d-4912-b599-f3c063da070c\" data-question=\"23\">wetland planning and decision making and have clear rights to use wetlands<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.’</p><p>H</p><p>The fortunes of wetlands would be improved, Silvius suggests, if more governments recognised their long-term value. ‘Different governments have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d69b095-7fa1-445f-ae8a-68a185a3591d\" data-question=\"24\">different<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> attitudes,’ he says, and goes on to explain that some <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b9eb4bca-1676-4993-8a1a-91c0f0ec4c69\" data-question=\"24\">countries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> place a high priority on restoring wetlands, while others still deny the issue. McCartney is cautiously optimistic, however. ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9e919b7-0b38-4c2a-884a-be4583affb40\" data-question=\"16\">Awareness of the importance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of wetlands is growing,’ he says. ‘It’s true that wetland degradation still continues at a rapid pace, but my impression is that things are slowly changing.’</p><p>* peal: a brown deposit formed by the partial decomposition of vegetation in wet acidic conditions, often cut out and dried for use as fuel</p><p>**subsidence: the sinking of the Earth's surface, most often caused by the removal of resources from the ground</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has eight paragraphs, A-H.</p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information?</p><p><em>Write the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207286\" id=\"question-wrapper-207286\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to the need to ensure that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"17ab3d26-7301-46f5-8412-a53f82a403c8\" data-question=\"14\">inhabitants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> of wetland regions continue to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"566cb627-69c7-4886-af9a-5527fa56b1c2\" data-question=\"14\">benefit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> from them </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207287\" id=\"question-wrapper-207287\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83943f25-f95b-4ce8-9184-2a1daba4e72e\" data-question=\"15\">the proportion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of wetlands which have already been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9526ef28-179d-492d-b17d-3bf90d0299d7\" data-question=\"15\">lost<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207288\" id=\"question-wrapper-207288\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to the idea that people are beginning <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9e919b7-0b38-4c2a-884a-be4583affb40\" data-question=\"16\">to appreciate the value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of wetlands </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207289\" id=\"question-wrapper-207289\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> mention of the cultural <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e2b0674c-e93e-4566-a93b-c06a7b512759\" data-question=\"17\">significance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> of wetlands </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the sentences below.</em></p><p><em>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes 18-22 on your answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207290\" id=\"question-wrapper-207290\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Peatlands which have been drained begin to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4afe3597-1a29-490c-9fbb-f0700fe8d4a1\" data-question=\"18\">release<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>.............................instead of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ef7940a-147e-43e0-bf8e-39cad88f71f1\" data-question=\"18\">storing it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CARBON</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207291\" id=\"question-wrapper-207291\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Once peatland areas have been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"31843bc3-7412-4110-9996-ca5265541f03\" data-question=\"19\">cleared<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>,..............................are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de542ac0-5888-4bf5-bc9c-0b926c6d2cf9\" data-question=\"19\">more likely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> to occur. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FIRES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207292\" id=\"question-wrapper-207292\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"88f186d9-797d-4893-8d10-246d20b5808f\" data-question=\"20\">Clearing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> peatland forests to make way for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61e9d479-ce14-4d60-a5fd-f6a6f5da7f0f\" data-question=\"20\">oil palm plantations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"34962157-b9bf-45c7-9897-f63d0ae6fab3\" data-question=\"20\">destroys<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> the ..............................of the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ffa3b045-3e3f-404a-9614-a1c9aabf5518\" data-question=\"20\">local environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BIODIVERSITY</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207293\" id=\"question-wrapper-207293\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Water is drained out of peatlands through the..............................which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8f14286a-2ba3-4f53-ad91-aad2b1dfac55\" data-question=\"21\">created<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> by logging companies. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DITCHES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207294\" id=\"question-wrapper-207294\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6d563f1-4fc5-412b-97e2-d0eec6ea5b14\" data-question=\"22\">Draining<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> peatlands leads to..............................: a serious problem which can eventually result in coastal flooding and land loss. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SUBSIDENCE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Look at the following statements (Questions 23-26) and the list of experts below.</em></p><p><em>Match each statement with the correct expert, A-D.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct letter, A-D, in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p> </p><p><strong>List of Experts</strong></p><ul><li><strong>A </strong>Matthew McCartney</li><li><strong>B </strong>Pieter van Eijk</li><li><strong>C </strong>Marcel Silvius</li><li><strong>D </strong>Dave Tickner</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207295\" id=\"question-wrapper-207295\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5de4238-46db-42cf-abd0-e4a3cf85096e\" data-question=\"23\">Communities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> living in wetland regions must be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3bcd3486-c5ac-470e-8fb9-b99ca118eddc\" data-question=\"23\">included in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c9617aa-6f1d-4912-b599-f3c063da070c\" data-question=\"23\">discussions about the future of these areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207296\" id=\"question-wrapper-207296\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Official policies towards wetlands <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1d69b095-7fa1-445f-ae8a-68a185a3591d\" data-question=\"24\">vary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> from one <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b9eb4bca-1676-4993-8a1a-91c0f0ec4c69\" data-question=\"24\">nation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> to the next. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207297\" id=\"question-wrapper-207297\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2809af02-cf19-4310-858b-fd3a4bf15303\" data-question=\"25\">cause harm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to wetlands without having any <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8d1ee22c-de95-4d23-b875-90c7f1841f35\" data-question=\"25\">intention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to do so. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207298\" id=\"question-wrapper-207298\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d18478e9-fcce-4513-8b75-0bbf0e74eaa7\" data-question=\"26\">Initiatives to reverse environmental damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> need not be <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"78959e35-6ce2-4fc4-aba1-ff1c8b9f5e87\" data-question=\"26\">complex<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"83943f25-f95b-4ce8-9184-2a1daba4e72e","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"the proportion","passagePhrase":"half"},{"uid":"9526ef28-179d-492d-b17d-3bf90d0299d7","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"lost","passagePhrase":"disappeared"},{"uid":"d26fca31-2583-46e5-89e2-57ed489d6535","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"considerable religious, historical and archaeological"},{"uid":"e2b0674c-e93e-4566-a93b-c06a7b512759","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"significance","passagePhrase":"value"},{"uid":"d18478e9-fcce-4513-8b75-0bbf0e74eaa7","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Initiatives to reverse environmental damage","passagePhrase":"planting a few trees ... Implementing climate change projects"},{"uid":"4afe3597-1a29-490c-9fbb-f0700fe8d4a1","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"release","passagePhrase":"carbon emitters"},{"uid":"6ef7940a-147e-43e0-bf8e-39cad88f71f1","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"storing it","passagePhrase":"active carbon stores"},{"uid":"31843bc3-7412-4110-9996-ca5265541f03","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"cleared","passagePhrase":"clearance"},{"uid":"de542ac0-5888-4bf5-bc9c-0b926c6d2cf9","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"more likely","passagePhrase":"increases the risk"},{"uid":"88f186d9-797d-4893-8d10-246d20b5808f","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Clearing","passagePhrase":"lost"},{"uid":"61e9d479-ce14-4d60-a5fd-f6a6f5da7f0f","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"oil palm plantations","passagePhrase":"oil palm revenues"},{"uid":"8f14286a-2ba3-4f53-ad91-aad2b1dfac55","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"created","passagePhrase":"dig"},{"uid":"a6d563f1-4fc5-412b-97e2-d0eec6ea5b14","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"Draining","passagePhrase":"drained away"},{"uid":"2809af02-cf19-4310-858b-fd3a4bf15303","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"cause harm","passagePhrase":"to damage"},{"uid":"8d1ee22c-de95-4d23-b875-90c7f1841f35","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"intention","passagePhrase":"set out to do"},{"uid":"566cb627-69c7-4886-af9a-5527fa56b1c2","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"benefit","passagePhrase":"provide an income"},{"uid":"17ab3d26-7301-46f5-8412-a53f82a403c8","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"inhabitants","passagePhrase":"local people ... local people"},{"uid":"e5de4238-46db-42cf-abd0-e4a3cf85096e","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Communities","passagePhrase":"local people ... local people"},{"uid":"3bcd3486-c5ac-470e-8fb9-b99ca118eddc","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"included in","passagePhrase":"involved in"},{"uid":"0c9617aa-6f1d-4912-b599-f3c063da070c","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"discussions about the future of these areas","passagePhrase":"wetland planning and decision making and have clear rights to use wetlands"},{"uid":"1d69b095-7fa1-445f-ae8a-68a185a3591d","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"vary","passagePhrase":"different"},{"uid":"b9eb4bca-1676-4993-8a1a-91c0f0ec4c69","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"nation","passagePhrase":"countries"},{"uid":"e9e919b7-0b38-4c2a-884a-be4583affb40","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"to appreciate the value","passagePhrase":"Awareness of the importance"},{"uid":"34962157-b9bf-45c7-9897-f63d0ae6fab3","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"destroys","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"ffa3b045-3e3f-404a-9614-a1c9aabf5518","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"local environment","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_303":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Is the era of artificial speech translation upon us?</strong></p><p>Once the stuff of science fiction, technology that enables people to talk using different languages is now here. But how effective is it?</p><p>Noise, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e16cbb71-df0b-4c23-b889-1a923fd2181b\" data-question=\"27\">Alex Waibel tells me<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, is one of the major <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"489b2f7e-d557-4989-a39d-18538c86cc4a\" data-question=\"27\">challenges<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> that artificial speech translation has to meet. A device may be able to recognise speech in a laboratory, or a meeting room, but will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"489b2f7e-d557-4989-a39d-18538c86cc4a\" data-question=\"27\">struggle<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> to cope with the kind of background noise I can hear in my office surrounding Professor Waibel as he speaks to me from Kyoto station in Japan. I’m struggling to follow him in English, on a scratchy line that reminds me we are nearly 10,000 kilometres apart - and that distance is still an obstacle to communication even if you’re speaking the same language, as we are. We haven’t reached the future yet. If we had, Waibel would have been able to speak more comfortably in his native German and I would have been able to hear his words in English.</p><p>At Karlsruhe Institute of Technology, where he is a professor of computer science, Waibel and his colleagues already give lectures in German that their students can follow in English via an electronic translator. The system generates text that students can read on their laptops or phones, so the process is somewhat similar to subtitling. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"239c60d4-47d3-4e99-a845-e5072a697aa4\" data-question=\"28\">helps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> that lecturers speak clearly, don’t have to compete with background chatter, and say much <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b475995d-b1ee-47ad-95d9-edd8522f357f\" data-question=\"28\">the same thing each year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</p><p>The idea of artificial speech translation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd8a734d-45dd-4c7e-bacd-f64c7f743e2a\" data-question=\"29\">has been around for a long time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Douglas Adams’ science fiction novel, <em>The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy</em>, published in 1979, featured a life form called the 'Babel fish’ which, when placed in the ear, enabled a listener to understand any language in the universe. It came to represent one of those devices that technology enthusiasts dream of long before they become practically realisable, like TVs flat enough to hang on walls: objects that we once could <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"18a847e9-3288-4c77-b08b-434d8036d53d\" data-question=\"29\">only dream of having<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> but that are now <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"18a847e9-3288-4c77-b08b-434d8036d53d\" data-question=\"29\">commonplace<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. Now devices that look like prototype Babel fish have started to appear, riding a wave of advances in artificial translation and voice recognition.</p><p>At this stage, however, they seem to be regarded as eye-catching novelties rather than steps towards what Waibel calls ‘making a language-transparent society’. They tend to be domestic devices or applications suitable for hotel check-ins, for example, providing a practical alternative to speaking traveller’s English. The efficiency of the translator is less important than the social function. However, ‘Professionals are less inclined to be patient in a conversation,’ founder and CEO at Waverly Labs, Andrew Ochoa, observes. To redress this, Waverly is now preparing a new model for professional applications, which entails performance improvements in speech recognition, translation accuracy and the time it takes to deliver the translated speech.</p><p>For a conversation, both speakers need to have devices called Pilots (translator earpieces) in their ears. ‘We find that there’s <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21d6be75-3b34-49d6-a691-dcba62e77be8\" data-question=\"30\">a barrier<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> with sharing one of the earphones with a stranger,’ says Ochoa. That can’t have been <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9f38973b-ca4c-4cf9-ba6c-f0d9067af5c9\" data-question=\"30\">totally unexpected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. The problem would be solved if earpiece translators became sufficiently prevalent that strangers would be likely to already have their own in their ears. Whether that happens, and how quickly, will probably depend not so much on the earpieces themselves, but on the prevalence of voice-controlled devices and artificial translation in general.</p><p>Waibel highlights the significance of certain Asian nations, noting that voice translation has really <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d651bbd-8a60-4133-94fc-413052af5ea8\" data-question=\"31\">taken off<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in countries such as Japan with a range of systems. There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7585d92-97c2-4635-b83f-0c02fa4c62b5\" data-question=\"31\">still a long way to go<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>, though. A translation system needs to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be71d1a6-ec17-4ac4-84ca-f3dd657228c2\" data-question=\"32\">simultaneous<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, like the translator’s voice speaking over the foreign politician being interviewed on the TV, rather than in sections that oblige speakers to pause after every few remarks and wait for the translation to be delivered. It needs to work offline, for situations where internet access isn’t possible, and to address apprehensions about the amount of private speech data accumulating in the cloud, having been sent to servers for processing.</p><p>Systems not only need to cope with physical challenges such as noise, they will also need to be socially aware by addressing people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e38de191-76b5-4fa8-9afd-3c8b99b58112\" data-question=\"33\">in the right way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. Some cultural traditions demand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4df20259-2295-4efc-af1d-e2ea0005eaa1\" data-question=\"33\">solemn respect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> for academic status, for example, and it is only polite to respect this. Etiquette-sensitive artificial translators could relieve people of the need to know these differing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"232cc061-ffe4-424e-8395-ec34217633a5\" data-question=\"34\">cultural norms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. At the same time, they might help to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8f3ec31c-be00-4d18-81b1-1fdf084681c2\" data-question=\"34\">preserve<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> local customs, slowing the spread of habits associated with international English, such as its readiness to get on first-name terms.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b68f3b31-3124-440e-b704-154aabcc5de8\" data-question=\"35\">Professors and other professionals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"96ad74d6-99ef-4f47-b7e8-905e9e163a1c\" data-question=\"35\">will not outsource language awareness to software<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, though. If the technology matures into seamless, ubiquitous artificial speech translation, it will actually add value to language skills. Whether <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a143176-676f-472e-8827-46963ba4e2da\" data-question=\"36\">it will help<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> people conduct <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0d205f6-515a-4c03-991f-e9aef948593f\" data-question=\"36\">their family lives or relationships<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fd3132c-53b7-424f-baf5-77fbdfb6a126\" data-question=\"36\">open to question<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> - though one noteworthy possibility is that it could <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"06dd8110-8e86-4e48-94a8-f6c58a087be0\" data-question=\"37\">overcome the language barriers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> that often arise between generations after <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e2d0872b-0146-440c-b355-ff9739329da9\" data-question=\"37\">migration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, leaving children and their grandparents without a shared language.</p><p>Whatever uses it is put to, though, it will never be as good as the real thing. Even if voicemorphing technology simulates the speaker’s voice, their lip movements won’t match, and they will look like they are in a dubbed movie. The contrast will underline the value of shared languages, and the value of learning them. Sharing a language can promote a sense of belonging and community, as with the international scientists who use English as a lingua franca, where their predecessors used Latin. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61dc999f-10c1-4173-a47c-51118ffa1fcd\" data-question=\"40\">Though the practical need for a common language will diminish, the social value of sharing one will persist.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> And software will never be a substitute for the subtle but vital understanding that comes with knowledge of a language.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct letter in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207299\" id=\"question-wrapper-207299\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the reader learn about the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e16cbb71-df0b-4c23-b889-1a923fd2181b\" data-question=\"27\">conversation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. The speakers are communicating in different languages.</li> <li>B. Neither of the speakers is familiar with their environment.</li> <li>C. The topic of the conversation is difficult for both speakers.</li> <li>D. Aspects of the conversation are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"489b2f7e-d557-4989-a39d-18538c86cc4a\" data-question=\"27\">challenging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> for both speakers.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207300\" id=\"question-wrapper-207300\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"239c60d4-47d3-4e99-a845-e5072a697aa4\" data-question=\"28\">assists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> the electronic translator during lectures at Karlsruhe Institute of Technology? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b475995d-b1ee-47ad-95d9-edd8522f357f\" data-question=\"28\">repeated content<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> of lectures</li> <li>B. the students’ reading skills</li> <li>C. the languages used</li> <li>D. the lecturers’ technical ability</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207301\" id=\"question-wrapper-207301\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When referring to The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, the writer suggests that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. the Babel fish was considered undesirable at the time,</li> <li>B. this book was not seriously intending to predict the future,</li> <li>C. artificial speech translation <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dd8a734d-45dd-4c7e-bacd-f64c7f743e2a\" data-question=\"29\">was not a surprising development<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>,</li> <li>D. some speech translation techniques are better than others.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207302\" id=\"question-wrapper-207302\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer say about sharing earpieces? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is something people will get used to doing.</li> <li>B. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21d6be75-3b34-49d6-a691-dcba62e77be8\" data-question=\"30\">reluctance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to do this is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"9f38973b-ca4c-4cf9-ba6c-f0d9067af5c9\" data-question=\"30\">understandable<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>C. The equipment will be unnecessary in the future.</li> <li>D. It is something few people need to worry about.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-F, below.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 31-34 on your answer sheet.</em></p><ul><li><strong>A </strong>but there are concerns about this.</li><li><strong>B </strong>as systems do not need to conform to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"232cc061-ffe4-424e-8395-ec34217633a5\" data-question=\"34\">standard practices<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.</li><li><strong>C</strong> but they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a7585d92-97c2-4635-b83f-0c02fa4c62b5\" data-question=\"31\">far from perfect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.</li><li><strong>D </strong>despite the noise issues.</li><li><strong>E </strong>because translation is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be71d1a6-ec17-4ac4-84ca-f3dd657228c2\" data-question=\"32\">immediate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</li><li><strong>F </strong>and have an awareness of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4df20259-2295-4efc-af1d-e2ea0005eaa1\" data-question=\"33\">good manners<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207303\" id=\"question-wrapper-207303\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Speech translation methods are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d651bbd-8a60-4133-94fc-413052af5ea8\" data-question=\"31\">developing fast<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> in Japan </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207304\" id=\"question-wrapper-207304\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> TV interviews that use translation voiceover methods are successful </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207305\" id=\"question-wrapper-207305\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Future translation systems should address people <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e38de191-76b5-4fa8-9afd-3c8b99b58112\" data-question=\"33\">appropriately<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207306\" id=\"question-wrapper-207306\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Users may be able to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8f3ec31c-be00-4d18-81b1-1fdf084681c2\" data-question=\"34\">maintain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> their local customs </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</p><p><em>In boxes 35-40 on your answer sheet, write</em></p><p><em>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</em></p><p><em>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</em></p><p><em>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207307\" id=\"question-wrapper-207307\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Language translation systems <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"96ad74d6-99ef-4f47-b7e8-905e9e163a1c\" data-question=\"35\">will be seen as very useful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> throughout <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b68f3b31-3124-440e-b704-154aabcc5de8\" data-question=\"35\">the academic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> and professional worlds. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207308\" id=\"question-wrapper-207308\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The overall <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a143176-676f-472e-8827-46963ba4e2da\" data-question=\"36\">value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> of automated translation to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0d205f6-515a-4c03-991f-e9aef948593f\" data-question=\"36\">family life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fd3132c-53b7-424f-baf5-77fbdfb6a126\" data-question=\"36\">yet to be shown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207309\" id=\"question-wrapper-207309\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Automated translation could <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"06dd8110-8e86-4e48-94a8-f6c58a087be0\" data-question=\"37\">make life more difficult<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e2d0872b-0146-440c-b355-ff9739329da9\" data-question=\"37\">immigrant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> families. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207310\" id=\"question-wrapper-207310\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Visual aspects of language translation are being considered by scientists. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207311\" id=\"question-wrapper-207311\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> International scientists have found English easier to translate into other languages than Latin. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207312\" id=\"question-wrapper-207312\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> As far as language is concerned, there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"61dc999f-10c1-4173-a47c-51118ffa1fcd\" data-question=\"40\">a difference between people’s social and practical needs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"e16cbb71-df0b-4c23-b889-1a923fd2181b","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"conversation","passagePhrase":"Alex Waibel tells me"},{"uid":"489b2f7e-d557-4989-a39d-18538c86cc4a","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"challenging","passagePhrase":"challenges ... struggle"},{"uid":"239c60d4-47d3-4e99-a845-e5072a697aa4","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"assists","passagePhrase":"helps"},{"uid":"b475995d-b1ee-47ad-95d9-edd8522f357f","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"repeated content","passagePhrase":"the same thing each year"},{"uid":"dd8a734d-45dd-4c7e-bacd-f64c7f743e2a","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"was not a surprising development","passagePhrase":"has been around for a long time"},{"uid":"21d6be75-3b34-49d6-a691-dcba62e77be8","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"reluctance","passagePhrase":"a barrier"},{"uid":"4d651bbd-8a60-4133-94fc-413052af5ea8","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"developing fast","passagePhrase":"taken off"},{"uid":"a7585d92-97c2-4635-b83f-0c02fa4c62b5","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"far from perfect","passagePhrase":"still a long way to go"},{"uid":"be71d1a6-ec17-4ac4-84ca-f3dd657228c2","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"immediate","passagePhrase":"simultaneous"},{"uid":"e38de191-76b5-4fa8-9afd-3c8b99b58112","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"appropriately","passagePhrase":"in the right way"},{"uid":"4df20259-2295-4efc-af1d-e2ea0005eaa1","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"good manners","passagePhrase":"solemn respect"},{"uid":"232cc061-ffe4-424e-8395-ec34217633a5","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"standard practices","passagePhrase":"cultural norms"},{"uid":"8f3ec31c-be00-4d18-81b1-1fdf084681c2","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"maintain","passagePhrase":"preserve"},{"uid":"b68f3b31-3124-440e-b704-154aabcc5de8","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"the academic","passagePhrase":"Professors and other professionals"},{"uid":"1a143176-676f-472e-8827-46963ba4e2da","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"value","passagePhrase":"it will help"},{"uid":"a0d205f6-515a-4c03-991f-e9aef948593f","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"family life","passagePhrase":"their family lives or relationships"},{"uid":"2fd3132c-53b7-424f-baf5-77fbdfb6a126","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"yet to be shown","passagePhrase":"open to question"},{"uid":"e2d0872b-0146-440c-b355-ff9739329da9","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"immigrant","passagePhrase":"migration"},{"uid":"61dc999f-10c1-4173-a47c-51118ffa1fcd","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"a difference between people’s social and practical needs","passagePhrase":"Though the practical need for a common language will diminish, the social value of sharing one will persist."}]},"reading_u2_304":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The impact of climate change on butterflies in Britain</strong></p><p>According to conservationists, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7a952717-baab-465a-9d6a-db570d7af514\" data-question=\"1\">populations of around two thirds of butterfly species have declined in Britain over the past 40 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. If this trend continues, it might have unpredictable knock-on effects for other species in the ecosystem. Butterfly eggs develop into caterpillars and these insects, which are the second stage in a new butterfly’s lifecycle, consume vast quantities of plant material, and in turn act as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"99eabb8d-2803-4eaa-908a-f861b081ca62\" data-question=\"2\">prey for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b89a3f5a-9276-4bfe-8e4e-9db10f2c9801\" data-question=\"2\">birds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> as well as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b89a3f5a-9276-4bfe-8e4e-9db10f2c9801\" data-question=\"2\">bats and other small mammals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. Only by arming themselves with an understanding of why butterfly numbers are down can conservationists hope to halt or reverse the decline.</p><p>Butterflies prefer outdoor conditions to be ‘just right’, which means neither too hot nor too cold. Under the conditions of climate change, the temperature at any given time in summer is generally getting warmer, leaving butterflies with the challenge of how to deal with this. One of the main ways in which species are ensuring conditions suit them is by changing the time of year at which they are active and reproduce. Scientists refer to <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e45d354c-8119-4940-925f-25661145e422\" data-question=\"3\">the timing of such lifecycle events<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> as ‘phenology’, so when an animal or plant <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf116443-bba6-4735-b85a-2ab486101670\" data-question=\"3\">starts to do something earlier in the year than it usually does<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, it is said to be ‘advancing its phenology’.</p><p>These advances have been observed already in a wide range of butterflies - indeed, most species are advancing their phenology to some extent. In Britain, as the average spring temperature has increased by roughly 0.5 °C over the past 20 years, species have advanced by between three days and a week on average, to keep in line with cooler temperatures. Is this a sign that butterflies are well equipped to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"107b960c-29cf-44e6-8983-c808ce852080\" data-question=\"5\">cope<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> with climate change, and readily <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"107b960c-29cf-44e6-8983-c808ce852080\" data-question=\"5\">adjust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> to new temperatures? Or are these populations under stress, being dragged along unwillingly by unnaturally fast changes? The answer is still <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"60a06525-016f-4324-83f3-83b932e3132d\" data-question=\"5\">unknown<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, but a new study is seeking to answer these questions.</p><p>First, the researchers pulled together data from millions of records that had been <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f254c252-9ac4-416d-b67e-706f3d03a4ff\" data-question=\"6\">submitted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a349eaa-e8ad-465b-9d9c-5949acc1c79a\" data-question=\"6\">butterfly enthusiasts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> - people who spend their free time observing the activities of different species. This provided information on 130 species of butterflies in Great Britain every year for a 20-year period. They then estimated the abundance and distribution of each species across this time, along with how far north in the country they had moved. The data also, crucially, allowed researchers to estimate subtle changes in what time of the year each species was changing into an adult butterfly.</p><p>Analysing the trends in each variable, the researchers discovered that species with more flexible lifecycles were more likely to be able to benefit from an earlier emergence driven by climate change. Some species are able to go from caterpillar to butterfly twice or more per year, so that the individual butterflies you see flying in the spring are the grandchildren or great-grandchildren of the individuals seen a year previously.</p><p>Among these species, researchers observed that those which have been advancing their phenology the most over the 20-year study period also had the most positive trends in abundance, distribution and northwards extent. For these species, such as Britain’s tiniest butterfly, the dainty Small Blue, whose colonies are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6e82f6d-e6b9-4184-8203-4a9956b89471\" data-question=\"7\">up to a hundred<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> strong, some develop into butterflies <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4fa98db0-698f-436b-a52b-e2e54d453bff\" data-question=\"8\">early in spring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, allowing their summer generations to complete another reproductive cycle by autumn so that more population growth occurs.</p><p>Other species, however, are less flexible and restricted to a single reproductive cycle per year. For these species, there was no evidence of any benefit to emerging earlier. Indeed, worryingly, it was found that the species in this group that specialise in very specific habitat types, often related to the caterpillar’s preferred diet, actually tended to be most at harm from advancing phenology. The beautiful High Brown Fritillary, often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93c64ad5-5a9b-48ce-8f58-8fe19fadb144\" data-question=\"9\">described as<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"997f09e4-e2f5-4241-a26e-956a815d3319\" data-question=\"9\">Britain’s most endangered butterfly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, is in this group. It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9f70bfc-6c59-498f-bf83-419f453e6528\" data-question=\"10\">found only in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> coppiced woodland and limestone pavement habitats. It is also a single-generation butterfly that has advanced its phenology. This suggests that climate change, while undoubtedly not the sole cause, might have played a part in the downfall of this species.</p><p>All is not lost, however. Many of Britain’s single-generation species show the capacity, in continental Europe, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"131df04a-962a-40d3-80f7-3c44c1c97db3\" data-question=\"11\">to add a second generation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> in years that are sufficiently warm. Therefore, as the climate continues to warm, species like the Silver-studded Blue might be able to switch to multiple generations in the UK as well, and so begin to extract benefits from the additional warmth, potentially leading to population increases.</p><p>More immediately, conservationists can arm themselves with all this knowledge to spot the warning signs of species that may be at risk. The White Admiral of southern England, a much sought-after butterfly, experienced a significant increase in numbers from the 1920s but has shown a considerable decline in the past 20 years. This may be because the caterpillar exists solely on a diet of a plant called honeysuckle. But it is also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98c4a1d7-8c1b-4530-a863-09b242e4d030\" data-question=\"13\">likely to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> due to climate change.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</p><p><em>In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write</em></p><p><em>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</em></p><p><em>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</em></p><p><em>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207313\" id=\"question-wrapper-207313\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"7a952717-baab-465a-9d6a-db570d7af514\" data-question=\"1\">Forty years ago, there were fewer butterflies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> in Britain than at present. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207314\" id=\"question-wrapper-207314\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Caterpillars are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"99eabb8d-2803-4eaa-908a-f861b081ca62\" data-question=\"2\">eaten by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b89a3f5a-9276-4bfe-8e4e-9db10f2c9801\" data-question=\"2\">a number of different predators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207315\" id=\"question-wrapper-207315\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> 'Phenology’ is a term used to describe a creature’s ability to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf116443-bba6-4735-b85a-2ab486101670\" data-question=\"3\">alter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"e45d354c-8119-4940-925f-25661145e422\" data-question=\"3\">the location of a lifecycle event<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207316\" id=\"question-wrapper-207316\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some species of butterfly have a reduced lifespan due to spring temperature increases. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207317\" id=\"question-wrapper-207317\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"60a06525-016f-4324-83f3-83b932e3132d\" data-question=\"5\">a clear reason<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"107b960c-29cf-44e6-8983-c808ce852080\" data-question=\"5\">the adaptations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> that butterflies are making to climate change. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207318\" id=\"question-wrapper-207318\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The data used in the study was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f254c252-9ac4-416d-b67e-706f3d03a4ff\" data-question=\"6\">taken from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the work of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5a349eaa-e8ad-465b-9d9c-5949acc1c79a\" data-question=\"6\">amateur butterfly watchers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the notes below.</em></p><p><em>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p> </p><p><strong>Butterflies iin the UK</strong></p><p><strong>The Small Blue</strong></p><p>• lives in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d6e82f6d-e6b9-4184-8203-4a9956b89471\" data-question=\"7\">large<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> 7.............................</p><p>• first appears <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4fa98db0-698f-436b-a52b-e2e54d453bff\" data-question=\"8\">at the start of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> 8.............................</p><p>• completes more than one reproductive cycle per year</p><p><strong>The High Brown Fritillary</strong></p><p>• has one reproductive cycle</p><p>• is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93c64ad5-5a9b-48ce-8f58-8fe19fadb144\" data-question=\"9\">considered to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> more 9..............................<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"997f09e4-e2f5-4241-a26e-956a815d3319\" data-question=\"9\">than other species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></p><p>• its caterpillars occupy <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e9f70bfc-6c59-498f-bf83-419f453e6528\" data-question=\"10\">a limited range<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> of 10.............................</p><p><strong>The Silver-studded Blue</strong></p><p>• is already able <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"131df04a-962a-40d3-80f7-3c44c1c97db3\" data-question=\"11\">to reproduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> twice a year in warm areas of 11.............................</p><p><strong>The White Admiral</strong></p><p>• is found in 12..............................areas of England</p><p>• both climate change and the 13.............................of the caterpillar are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"98c4a1d7-8c1b-4530-a863-09b242e4d030\" data-question=\"13\">possible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> reasons for decline</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207319\" id=\"question-wrapper-207319\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COLONIES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207320\" id=\"question-wrapper-207320\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SPRING</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207321\" id=\"question-wrapper-207321\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ENDANGERED</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207322\" id=\"question-wrapper-207322\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HABITAT(S)</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207323\" id=\"question-wrapper-207323\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EUROPE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207324\" id=\"question-wrapper-207324\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOUTHERN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207325\" id=\"question-wrapper-207325\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DIET</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"99eabb8d-2803-4eaa-908a-f861b081ca62","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"eaten by","passagePhrase":"prey for"},{"uid":"b89a3f5a-9276-4bfe-8e4e-9db10f2c9801","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"a number of different predators","passagePhrase":"birds ... bats and other small mammals"},{"uid":"cf116443-bba6-4735-b85a-2ab486101670","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"alter","passagePhrase":"starts to do something earlier in the year than it usually does"},{"uid":"107b960c-29cf-44e6-8983-c808ce852080","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"the adaptations","passagePhrase":"cope ... adjust"},{"uid":"5a349eaa-e8ad-465b-9d9c-5949acc1c79a","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"amateur butterfly watchers","passagePhrase":"butterfly enthusiasts"},{"uid":"d6e82f6d-e6b9-4184-8203-4a9956b89471","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"large","passagePhrase":"up to a hundred"},{"uid":"4fa98db0-698f-436b-a52b-e2e54d453bff","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"at the start of","passagePhrase":"early in spring"},{"uid":"93c64ad5-5a9b-48ce-8f58-8fe19fadb144","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"considered to be","passagePhrase":"described as"},{"uid":"997f09e4-e2f5-4241-a26e-956a815d3319","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"than other species","passagePhrase":"Britain’s most endangered butterfly"},{"uid":"e9f70bfc-6c59-498f-bf83-419f453e6528","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"a limited range","passagePhrase":"found only in"},{"uid":"131df04a-962a-40d3-80f7-3c44c1c97db3","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"to reproduce","passagePhrase":"to add a second generation"},{"uid":"98c4a1d7-8c1b-4530-a863-09b242e4d030","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"possible","passagePhrase":"likely to be"}]},"reading_u2_305":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Deep-sea mining</strong></p><p>Bacteria from the ocean floor can beat superbugs and cancer. But habitats are at risk from the hunger for marine minerals</p><p>A</p><p>When Professor Mat Upton found that a microbe from a deep-sea sponge was killing pathogenic bugs in his laboratory, he realised it could be a breakthrough in the fight against antibiotic-resistant superbugs, which are responsible for thousands of deaths a year in the UK alone. Further tests confirmed that an antibiotic from the sponge bacteria, found living more than 700 metres under the sea at the Rockall trough in the north-east Atlantic, was previously unknown to science, boosting its potential as a life-saving medicine. But Upton, and other scientists who view the deep ocean and its wealth of unique and undocumented species as a prospecting ground for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2b40127-d9ce-41eb-bb30-26db8a453a93\" data-question=\"20\">new medicines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, fear such potential will be lost in the rush to exploit the deep sea’s equally rich metal and mineral resources.</p><p>B</p><p>‘We’re looking at the bioactive potential of marine resources, to see if there are any more medicines or drugs down there before we destroy it for ever,’ says Upton, a medical microbiologist at the University of Plymouth. Me is among many scientists urging a halt to deep-sea mining, asking for time to weigh up the pros and cons. ‘In sustainability terms, this could be a better way of exploiting the economic potential of the deep sea,’ he argues. Oceanographers using remotely operated vehicles have spotted many new species. Among them have been sea cucumbers with tails allowing them to sail along the ocean floor, and a rare ‘Dumbo’ octopus, found 3,000 metres under the Pacific Ocean, off the coast of California. Any one of these could offer lifesaving potential. Upton estimates it could take up to a decade for a newly discovered antibiotic to become a medicine - but the race towards commercial mining in the ocean abyss has already begun.</p><p>C</p><p>The deep sea contains more nickel, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aac85849-1cc4-4147-904f-876158adfa25\" data-question=\"14\">cobalt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and rare earth metals than all land reserves combined, according to the US Geological Survey. Mining corporations argue that deep-sea exploration could help diversify the supply of metals and point to the fact that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d45a87d-5da7-4e30-ad5e-d320f437422c\" data-question=\"14\">demand<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> for resources such as copper, aluminium, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aac85849-1cc4-4147-904f-876158adfa25\" data-question=\"14\">cobalt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"405568c0-a37b-40cd-bd24-2ed3e56a9a39\" data-question=\"14\">electric car batteries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> and other metals to power technology and smartphones, is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8750468-26e0-4fb4-be48-49c73e8a46f3\" data-question=\"14\">soaring<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. They say that deep-sea mining could yield far superior <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a41cdb6-3097-4efc-8824-5dbe42d7f85b\" data-question=\"24\">ore<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> to land mining with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d89f0129-9bd4-4bb4-8260-0048145daa74\" data-question=\"24\">little, if any, waste<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. Different methods of extraction exist, but most involve <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15e9c82e-fc94-4675-83e7-ca816f85945b\" data-question=\"25\">employing some form of converted machinery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a2a3cbb-15a5-48d8-bb40-3840396928d1\" data-question=\"25\">previously used in terrestrial mining<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to excavate materials from the sea floor, at depths of up to 6,000 metres, then drawing a seawater slurry, containing rock and other solid particles, from the sea floor to ships on the surface. The slurry is then ‘de-watered’ and transferred to another vessel for shipping. Extracted seawater is pumped back down and discharged close to the sea floor.</p><p>D</p><p>But environmental and legal groups have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cff4f8d9-5600-4e4e-9008-653e5decba5b\" data-question=\"26\">urged caution<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>, arguing there are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b48ee1c0-fca1-4d1f-a93c-541e3b8812fd\" data-question=\"26\">potentially massive and unknown ramifications<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> for the environment and for nearby communities, and that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e3176631-1a24-4d1b-a549-2be3b4c3b16a\" data-question=\"17\">global<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ee745e1-66e5-4ad5-acf5-86960e0f907e\" data-question=\"17\">regulatory framework<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4d2fcce-cdae-407e-9f93-e3e694ca29c7\" data-question=\"17\">not yet drafted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. ‘Despite arising in the last half century, the “new global gold rush” of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18e22b03-4caa-4604-ab4f-096035d3dc7a\" data-question=\"19\">deep-sea mining<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> shares many features with past resource scrambles - including a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"14f55b4e-7a3b-4879-861d-fa284a7f35e7\" data-question=\"19\">general disregard<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67d70716-1f39-4c75-97e7-13e0cde10697\" data-question=\"19\">environmental and social impacts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b8fa6f1-a360-410b-a948-78d9756f0ea1\" data-question=\"19\">the marginalisation of indigenous peoples and their rights<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>,’ a paper, written by Julie Hunter and Julian Aguon, from Blue Ocean Law, and Pradeep Singh, from the Center for Marine Environmental Sciences, Bremen, argues. The authors say that knowledge of the deep seabed remains extremely limited. ‘The surface of the Moon, Mars and even Venus <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d435ba5-3a3d-48f8-a702-2745610928fd\" data-question=\"22\">have all been mapped and studied in much greater detail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, leading marine scientists to commonly remark that, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3281f34b-35bb-4a8a-a6f9-0a352d488122\" data-question=\"22\">with respect to the deep sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, “We don’t yet know what we need to know”.’</p><p>E</p><p>Scientific research - including a recent paper in Marine Policy journal - has suggested the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fba15b19-1729-4bd7-9d8a-6483f48941d3\" data-question=\"16\">deep seabed, and hydrothermal vents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, which are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67162600-2071-44bf-bfaf-0b62a7386a79\" data-question=\"16\">created<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> when seawater meets volcanic magma, have crucial impacts upon biodiversity and the global climate. The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3f0315d1-859e-458d-979a-f6d6e1925823\" data-question=\"16\">mineral-rich vents and their surrounds are also home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> to many well-known animals including crustaceans, tubeworms, clams, slugs, anemones and fish. ‘It is becoming increasingly clear that deep-sea mining poses a grave threat to these vital seabed functions,’ the paper says. ‘Extraction methods would produce large sediment plumes and involve the discharge of waste back into the ocean, significantly disturbing seafloor environments,’ the paper continues. ‘On <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59bb96fc-b499-4fb7-90ff-12ef53123318\" data-question=\"23\">deep sea vents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bda72c00-51ec-4b0e-8318-e52828ebc5e9\" data-question=\"23\">scientists are clear<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>,’ says Dr Jon Copley of the National Oceanography Centre, Southampton: ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b72ce364-4bb1-43ba-a461-965a1ff1f215\" data-question=\"23\">we don’t want mining on them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.’</p><p>F</p><p>The oceans <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d94513b-9a80-44cd-af1a-65bc1937d32f\" data-question=\"15\">occupy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3669de3-b927-4071-a925-9bba953cefb8\" data-question=\"15\">around 70%<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of the planet and are relatively unexplored, says Mike Johnston, chief executive of Nautilus, a Canadian underwater exploration company: ‘It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"354a75ba-9c99-4863-9591-e88a2cc57106\" data-question=\"18\">makes sense<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> to explore this untapped potential in an environmentally sustainable way, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4204161-c63e-41f0-832f-ae8ba2b1bb0a\" data-question=\"18\">instead of continually looking at<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64a3d5f5-6046-4e25-b805-5d5dd3ee36f1\" data-question=\"18\">fast depleting land resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> of the planet to meet society’s rising needs.’ Those leading the global rush to place giant mining machines thousands of metres below the sea surface say the environmental impacts will be far lower than on land. But critics say exotic and little-known ecosystems in the deep oceans could be destroyed and must be protected. ‘Mining will be the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d1ae6c97-46f0-486d-b373-ee75f7b3da1b\" data-question=\"21\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4780e19f-c6d1-4d9a-99c3-3ba147801b13\" data-question=\"21\">greatest assault<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"73ef26fb-f355-4877-9d9c-0077724b7fc1\" data-question=\"21\">on deep-sea ecosystems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> ever inflicted by humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>,’ according to hydrothermal vent expert Verena Tunnicliffe, at the University of Victoria in Canada. She argues that active vents must be off-limits for mining to protect the new knowledge and biotechnology spin-offs they can deliver, and that strict controls must be in place elsewhere.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, <strong>A-F.</strong></p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information?</p><p><em>Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-17 on your answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207326\" id=\"question-wrapper-207326\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8750468-26e0-4fb4-be48-49c73e8a46f3\" data-question=\"14\">rapidly increasing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6d45a87d-5da7-4e30-ad5e-d320f437422c\" data-question=\"14\">need<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aac85849-1cc4-4147-904f-876158adfa25\" data-question=\"14\">one raw material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> in the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"405568c0-a37b-40cd-bd24-2ed3e56a9a39\" data-question=\"14\">transport industry<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207327\" id=\"question-wrapper-207327\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3669de3-b927-4071-a925-9bba953cefb8\" data-question=\"15\">a rough estimate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> of the area of the Earth <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d94513b-9a80-44cd-af1a-65bc1937d32f\" data-question=\"15\">covered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> by the oceans </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207328\" id=\"question-wrapper-207328\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> how a particular <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fba15b19-1729-4bd7-9d8a-6483f48941d3\" data-question=\"16\">underwater habitat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, where <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3f0315d1-859e-458d-979a-f6d6e1925823\" data-question=\"16\">minerals and organisms co-exist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67162600-2071-44bf-bfaf-0b62a7386a79\" data-question=\"16\">formed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207329\" id=\"question-wrapper-207329\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> reference to the fact that the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e3176631-1a24-4d1b-a549-2be3b4c3b16a\" data-question=\"17\">countries of the world<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4d2fcce-cdae-407e-9f93-e3e694ca29c7\" data-question=\"17\">yet to agree<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9ee745e1-66e5-4ad5-acf5-86960e0f907e\" data-question=\"17\">rules<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> for the exploration of the seabed </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Look at the following statements (Questions 18-23) and the list of people below.</em></p><p><em>Match each statement with the correct person or people, A-E.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 18-23 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p><em>NB You may use any letter more than once.</em></p><p> </p><p><strong>List of People</strong></p><ul><li><strong>A </strong>Professor Mat Upton</li><li><strong>B</strong> Julie Hunter, Julian Aguon and Pradeep Singh</li><li><strong>C</strong> Dr Jon Copley</li><li><strong>D </strong>Mike Johnston</li><li><strong>E </strong>Verena Tunnicliffe</li></ul></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207330\" id=\"question-wrapper-207330\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f4204161-c63e-41f0-832f-ae8ba2b1bb0a\" data-question=\"18\">A move away from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> the exploration of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"64a3d5f5-6046-4e25-b805-5d5dd3ee36f1\" data-question=\"18\">heavily mined reserves on land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"354a75ba-9c99-4863-9591-e88a2cc57106\" data-question=\"18\">is a good idea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207331\" id=\"question-wrapper-207331\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"67d70716-1f39-4c75-97e7-13e0cde10697\" data-question=\"19\">negative effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"18e22b03-4caa-4604-ab4f-096035d3dc7a\" data-question=\"19\">undersea exploration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> on <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9b8fa6f1-a360-410b-a948-78d9756f0ea1\" data-question=\"19\">local areas and their inhabitants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"14f55b4e-7a3b-4879-861d-fa284a7f35e7\" data-question=\"19\">are being ignored<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207332\" id=\"question-wrapper-207332\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2b40127-d9ce-41eb-bb30-26db8a453a93\" data-question=\"20\">more worthwhile things<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to extract from the sea than minerals. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207333\" id=\"question-wrapper-207333\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d1ae6c97-46f0-486d-b373-ee75f7b3da1b\" data-question=\"21\">No other form of human exploration<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> will have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4780e19f-c6d1-4d9a-99c3-3ba147801b13\" data-question=\"21\">such a destructive impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"73ef26fb-f355-4877-9d9c-0077724b7fc1\" data-question=\"21\">on marine life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> as deep-sea mining. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207334\" id=\"question-wrapper-207334\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2d435ba5-3a3d-48f8-a702-2745610928fd\" data-question=\"22\">More is known about outer space<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> than about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3281f34b-35bb-4a8a-a6f9-0a352d488122\" data-question=\"22\">what lies beneath the oceans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207335\" id=\"question-wrapper-207335\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"59bb96fc-b499-4fb7-90ff-12ef53123318\" data-question=\"23\">one marine life habitat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bda72c00-51ec-4b0e-8318-e52828ebc5e9\" data-question=\"23\">where experts agree<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b72ce364-4bb1-43ba-a461-965a1ff1f215\" data-question=\"23\">mining should not take place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the summary below.</em></p><p><em>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p> </p><p><strong>Mining the sea floor</strong></p><p>Mining corporations believe that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1a41cdb6-3097-4efc-8824-5dbe42d7f85b\" data-question=\"24\">the mineral resources lying under the sea<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> may be superior to those found in the earth. They also say that these can be removed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d89f0129-9bd4-4bb4-8260-0048145daa74\" data-question=\"24\">without producing much<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> 24............................... The extraction is often done by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"15e9c82e-fc94-4675-83e7-ca816f85945b\" data-question=\"25\">adapting the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> 25..............................that has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a2a3cbb-15a5-48d8-bb40-3840396928d1\" data-question=\"25\">already been used to work on land<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. The method of excavation involves removing the seawater from the slurry that is brought up to ships and returning it to the seabed. However, concerned groups strongly believe that 26..............................<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cff4f8d9-5600-4e4e-9008-653e5decba5b\" data-question=\"26\">is necessary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> due to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b48ee1c0-fca1-4d1f-a93c-541e3b8812fd\" data-question=\"26\">the possible number of unidentified consequences<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207336\" id=\"question-wrapper-207336\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">WASTE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207337\" id=\"question-wrapper-207337\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MACHINERY</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207338\" id=\"question-wrapper-207338\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CAUTION</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a2b40127-d9ce-41eb-bb30-26db8a453a93","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"more worthwhile things","passagePhrase":"new medicines"},{"uid":"aac85849-1cc4-4147-904f-876158adfa25","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"one raw material","passagePhrase":"cobalt ... cobalt"},{"uid":"6d45a87d-5da7-4e30-ad5e-d320f437422c","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"need","passagePhrase":"demand"},{"uid":"405568c0-a37b-40cd-bd24-2ed3e56a9a39","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"transport industry","passagePhrase":"electric car batteries"},{"uid":"d8750468-26e0-4fb4-be48-49c73e8a46f3","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"rapidly increasing","passagePhrase":"soaring"},{"uid":"1a41cdb6-3097-4efc-8824-5dbe42d7f85b","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"the mineral resources lying under the sea","passagePhrase":"ore"},{"uid":"d89f0129-9bd4-4bb4-8260-0048145daa74","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"without producing much","passagePhrase":"little, if any, waste"},{"uid":"15e9c82e-fc94-4675-83e7-ca816f85945b","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"adapting the","passagePhrase":"employing some form of converted machinery"},{"uid":"9a2a3cbb-15a5-48d8-bb40-3840396928d1","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"already been used to work on land","passagePhrase":"previously used in terrestrial mining"},{"uid":"cff4f8d9-5600-4e4e-9008-653e5decba5b","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"is necessary","passagePhrase":"urged caution"},{"uid":"b48ee1c0-fca1-4d1f-a93c-541e3b8812fd","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"the possible number of unidentified consequences","passagePhrase":"potentially massive and unknown ramifications"},{"uid":"e3176631-1a24-4d1b-a549-2be3b4c3b16a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"countries of the world","passagePhrase":"global"},{"uid":"9ee745e1-66e5-4ad5-acf5-86960e0f907e","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"rules","passagePhrase":"regulatory framework"},{"uid":"d4d2fcce-cdae-407e-9f93-e3e694ca29c7","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"yet to agree","passagePhrase":"not yet drafted"},{"uid":"18e22b03-4caa-4604-ab4f-096035d3dc7a","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"undersea exploration","passagePhrase":"deep-sea mining"},{"uid":"14f55b4e-7a3b-4879-861d-fa284a7f35e7","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"are being ignored","passagePhrase":"general disregard"},{"uid":"67d70716-1f39-4c75-97e7-13e0cde10697","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"negative effects","passagePhrase":"environmental and social impacts"},{"uid":"9b8fa6f1-a360-410b-a948-78d9756f0ea1","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"local areas and their inhabitants","passagePhrase":"the marginalisation of indigenous peoples and their rights"},{"uid":"2d435ba5-3a3d-48f8-a702-2745610928fd","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"More is known about outer space","passagePhrase":"have all been mapped and studied in much greater detail"},{"uid":"3281f34b-35bb-4a8a-a6f9-0a352d488122","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"what lies beneath the oceans","passagePhrase":"with respect to the deep sea"},{"uid":"fba15b19-1729-4bd7-9d8a-6483f48941d3","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"underwater habitat","passagePhrase":"deep seabed, and hydrothermal vents"},{"uid":"67162600-2071-44bf-bfaf-0b62a7386a79","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"formed","passagePhrase":"created"},{"uid":"3f0315d1-859e-458d-979a-f6d6e1925823","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"minerals and organisms co-exist","passagePhrase":"mineral-rich vents and their surrounds are also home"},{"uid":"59bb96fc-b499-4fb7-90ff-12ef53123318","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"one marine life habitat","passagePhrase":"deep sea vents"},{"uid":"bda72c00-51ec-4b0e-8318-e52828ebc5e9","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"where experts agree","passagePhrase":"scientists are clear"},{"uid":"b72ce364-4bb1-43ba-a461-965a1ff1f215","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"mining should not take place","passagePhrase":"we don’t want mining on them"},{"uid":"2d94513b-9a80-44cd-af1a-65bc1937d32f","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"covered","passagePhrase":"occupy"},{"uid":"a3669de3-b927-4071-a925-9bba953cefb8","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"a rough estimate","passagePhrase":"around 70%"},{"uid":"354a75ba-9c99-4863-9591-e88a2cc57106","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"is a good idea","passagePhrase":"makes sense"},{"uid":"f4204161-c63e-41f0-832f-ae8ba2b1bb0a","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"A move away from","passagePhrase":"instead of continually looking at"},{"uid":"64a3d5f5-6046-4e25-b805-5d5dd3ee36f1","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"heavily mined reserves on land","passagePhrase":"fast depleting land resources"},{"uid":"d1ae6c97-46f0-486d-b373-ee75f7b3da1b","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"No other form of human exploration","passagePhrase":"greatest assault on deep-sea ecosystems ever inflicted by humans"},{"uid":"4780e19f-c6d1-4d9a-99c3-3ba147801b13","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"such a destructive impact","passagePhrase":"greatest assault"},{"uid":"73ef26fb-f355-4877-9d9c-0077724b7fc1","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"on marine life","passagePhrase":"on deep-sea ecosystems"}]},"reading_u2_306":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The Unselfish Gene</strong></p><p>A psychologist gives his view on how humans became self-centred</p><p>There has long been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c77ffeb-c0c2-45de-860b-22806ef2abe2\" data-question=\"27\">a general assumption<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a459565b-8db5-4ccb-8cad-24a6fe87e925\" data-question=\"27\">human beings are essentially selfish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. We’re apparently ruthless, with strong impulses to compete against each other for resources and to accumulate power and possessions. If we are kind to one another, it’s usually because we have ulterior motives. If we are good, it’s only because we have managed to control and transcend our innate selfishness and brutality.</p><p>This bleak view of human nature is closely associated with the science writer Richard Dawkins, whose 1976 book <em>The Selfish Gene</em> became popular because it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11f93a54-6e07-43c8-99d1-5a3819fca892\" data-question=\"28\">fitted so well with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> - and helped to justify - <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"442a4343-fc88-4ab4-9a3c-44b50497addf\" data-question=\"28\">the competitive and individualistic ethos that was so prevalent in late 20th-century societies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. Like many others, Dawkins justifies his views with reference to the field of evolutionary psychology. Evolutionary psychology theorises that present-day human traits developed in prehistoric times, during what is termed the ‘environment of evolutionary adaptedness’.</p><p>Prehistory is usually seen as a period of intense competition, when life was such a brutal battle that only those with traits such as selfishness, aggression and ruthlessness survived. And because survival depended on access to resources - such as rivers, forests and animals - there was bound to be conflict between rival groups, which led to the development <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c31b212-07a6-4a89-90bb-b2788741386f\" data-question=\"37\">of traits such as racism and warfare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. This seems logical. But, in fact, the assumption on which this all rests - that prehistoric life was a desperate struggle for survival - is false.</p><p>It’s important to remember that in the prehistoric era, the world was very sparsely populated. According to some estimates, around 15,000 years ago, the population of Europe was only 29,000, and the population of the whole world was less than half a million. Humans at that time were hunter-gatherers: people who lived by hunting wild animals and collecting wild plants. With such small population densities, it seems <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2262477-5086-4206-a3c0-e9a6395331e2\" data-question=\"29\">unlikely that prehistoric hunter-gatherer groups had to compete against each other for resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> or had any need to develop ruthlessness and competitiveness, or to go to war.</p><p>There is significant evidence to back this notion from contemporary hunter-gatherer groups, who live in the same way as prehistoric humans did. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2c5b4bc-5a29-4ae5-9ece-b3c0223fba7a\" data-question=\"30\">As the anthropologist Bruce Knauft has remarked<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, hunter-gatherers are characterised by ‘<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"14d43064-9852-4d79-a37b-d3223d841885\" data-question=\"31\">extreme political and sexual egalitarianism<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>'. Knauft has observed that individuals in such groups don’t <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b271b417-7b93-4b2e-baf0-bd8c0b1ea746\" data-question=\"30\">accumulate property or possessions and have an ethical obligation to share everything<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. They also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dec524ff-54c7-4654-b9c8-09c21c173468\" data-question=\"32\">have methods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> of preserving egalitarianism by ensuring that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c2707bb-819a-4b06-974d-8b099db0befc\" data-question=\"32\">disparities of status<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> don't arise.</p><p>The !<em>Kung</em> people of southern Africa, for example, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"97e80f1a-72b6-4ca2-94f0-8b0c1f0e0d99\" data-question=\"33\">swap arrows<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> before going hunting and when an animal is killed, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"954d6cc6-0d2f-4def-b316-22889f78ae30\" data-question=\"33\">the acclaim<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> does not go to the person who fired the arrow, but to the person the arrow belongs to. And if a person becomes too domineering, the other members of the group <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ccd0482-ed42-47b3-aa0b-ce05f663be88\" data-question=\"34\">ostracise them, exiling the offender from society<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Typically in such groups, men do not dictate what women do. Women in hunter-gatherer groups worldwide often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8681273f-c083-4681-8921-7f406c47a134\" data-question=\"35\">benefit from a high level of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> autonomy, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0567171-59a4-43ee-8517-8202012671fe\" data-question=\"35\">being able to select their own marriage partners, decide what work they do and work whenever they choose to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. And if a marriage breaks down, they have custody rights over their children.</p><p>Many anthropologists believe that societies such as the !<em>Kung</em> were normal until a few thousand years ago, when population growth led to the development of agriculture and a settled lifestyle. In view of the above, there seems little reason to assume that traits such as racism, warfare and male domination should have been selected by evolution - as they <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"fd91933c-4a46-4ed3-913f-dae6bf5063a0\" data-question=\"37\">would have been of little benefit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in the prehistoric era. Individuals who behaved selfishly and ruthlessly would be less likely to survive, since they would have been ostracised from their groups.</p><p>It makes more sense, then, to see <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c190c2ea-997b-44ab-abbf-0ed79afe3991\" data-question=\"38\">traits such as cooperation, egalitarianism, altruism and peacefulness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8bb42f3-aba1-4af0-876e-0a322f71a079\" data-question=\"38\">innate characteristics of human beings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. These were the traits that were prevalent in human life for tens of thousands of years. So presumably these traits are still strong in us now.</p><p>But if prehistoric life wasn’t really as brutal as has often been assumed, why do modern humans behave so selfishly and ruthlessly? Perhaps these negative traits should be seen as a later development, the result of environmental and psychological factors. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"5e4ba031-55b0-419a-95e2-d8ec99a5a089\" data-question=\"40\">Research has shown repeatedly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"14415a80-70cf-405d-af5b-2857ddf267b5\" data-question=\"40\">when the natural habitats of primates such as apes and gorillas are disrupted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>, they tend to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b880f417-0d0d-4038-a965-f3d0adf1e6d5\" data-question=\"40\">become more violent and hierarchical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</p><p>So, it could well be that the same thing has happened to us. I believe that the end of the hunter-gatherer lifestyle and the advent of farming was connected to a psychological change that occurred in some groups of people. There was a new sense of individuality and separateness, which led to a new selfishness, and ultimately to hierarchical societies, patriarchy and warfare. At any rate, these negative traits appear to have developed so recently that it doesn’t seem feasible to explain them in adaptive or evolutionary terms.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</em></p><p><em>Write the correct letter in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207339\" id=\"question-wrapper-207339\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer doing in the first paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. setting out two opposing views about human nature</li> <li>B. justifying his opinion about our tendency to be greedy</li> <li>C. describing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9c77ffeb-c0c2-45de-860b-22806ef2abe2\" data-question=\"27\">a commonly held belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a459565b-8db5-4ccb-8cad-24a6fe87e925\" data-question=\"27\">people’s behaviour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></li> <li>D. explaining why he thinks that humans act in a selfish manner</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207340\" id=\"question-wrapper-207340\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point is made about Richard Dawkins’ book The Selfish Gene? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Its appeal lay in the radical nature of its ideas.</li> <li>B. Its success was due to the scientific support it offered.</li> <li>C. It presented a view that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11f93a54-6e07-43c8-99d1-5a3819fca892\" data-question=\"28\">was in line with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"442a4343-fc88-4ab4-9a3c-44b50497addf\" data-question=\"28\">the attitudes of its time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.</li> <li>D. It took an innovative approach to the analysis of human psychology.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207341\" id=\"question-wrapper-207341\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer suggest about the prehistoric era in the fourth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Societies were more complex than many people believe.</li> <li>B. Supplies of natural <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c2262477-5086-4206-a3c0-e9a6395331e2\" data-question=\"29\">resources were probably relatively plentiful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> <li>C. Most estimates about population sizes are likely to be inaccurate.</li> <li>D. Humans moved across continents more than was previously thought.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207342\" id=\"question-wrapper-207342\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The writer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d2c5b4bc-5a29-4ae5-9ece-b3c0223fba7a\" data-question=\"30\">refers to Bruce Knauft’s work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> as support for the idea that </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b271b417-7b93-4b2e-baf0-bd8c0b1ea746\" data-question=\"30\">selfishness<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> is a relatively recent development in human societies.</li> <li>B. only people in isolated communities can live in an unselfish manner.</li> <li>C. very few lifestyles have survived unchanged since prehistoric times.</li> <li>D. hunter-gatherer cultures worldwide are declining in number.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><em>Complete the summary below.</em></p><p><em>Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</em></p><p><em>Write your answers in boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet.</em></p><p> </p><p><strong>Contemporary hunter-gatherer societies</strong></p><p>Bruce Knauft’s research shows that contemporary hunter-gatherer societies tend to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"14d43064-9852-4d79-a37b-d3223d841885\" data-question=\"31\">exhibit a high level of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> 31..............................in all areas of life. In these cultures, distributing resources fairly among all members is a moral obligation. These societies also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dec524ff-54c7-4654-b9c8-09c21c173468\" data-question=\"32\">employ strategies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> to prevent <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c2707bb-819a-4b06-974d-8b099db0befc\" data-question=\"32\">differences in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> 32..............................occurring: for example, the <em>IKung</em> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"97e80f1a-72b6-4ca2-94f0-8b0c1f0e0d99\" data-question=\"33\">follow a custom<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> whereby <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"954d6cc6-0d2f-4def-b316-22889f78ae30\" data-question=\"33\">the credit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> for one person’s success at 33..............................is given to another member of the group. Individuals who behave in a 34............................manner are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ccd0482-ed42-47b3-aa0b-ce05f663be88\" data-question=\"34\">punished by being excluded from the group<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, and women have a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8681273f-c083-4681-8921-7f406c47a134\" data-question=\"35\">considerable amount of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> 35..............................in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a0567171-59a4-43ee-8517-8202012671fe\" data-question=\"35\">choices regarding work and marriage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207343\" id=\"question-wrapper-207343\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EGALITARIANISM</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207344\" id=\"question-wrapper-207344\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STATUS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207345\" id=\"question-wrapper-207345\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HUNTING</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207346\" id=\"question-wrapper-207346\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DOMINEERING</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207347\" id=\"question-wrapper-207347\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">AUTONOMY</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3?</p><p><em>In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write</em></p><p><em>YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer</em></p><p><em>NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer</em></p><p><em>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</em></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207348\" id=\"question-wrapper-207348\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Some anthropologists are mistaken about the point when the number of societies such as the IKung began to decline. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207349\" id=\"question-wrapper-207349\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Humans who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2c31b212-07a6-4a89-90bb-b2788741386f\" data-question=\"37\">developed warlike traits<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> in prehistory <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"fd91933c-4a46-4ed3-913f-dae6bf5063a0\" data-question=\"37\">would have had an advantage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> over those who did not. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207350\" id=\"question-wrapper-207350\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c190c2ea-997b-44ab-abbf-0ed79afe3991\" data-question=\"38\">Being peaceful and cooperative<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d8bb42f3-aba1-4af0-876e-0a322f71a079\" data-question=\"38\">a natural way for people to behave<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207351\" id=\"question-wrapper-207351\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Negative traits are more apparent in some modern cultures than in others. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"207352\" id=\"question-wrapper-207352\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Animal research has <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"5e4ba031-55b0-419a-95e2-d8ec99a5a089\" data-question=\"40\">failed to reveal a link<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> between <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"14415a80-70cf-405d-af5b-2857ddf267b5\" data-question=\"40\">changes in the environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> and the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b880f417-0d0d-4038-a965-f3d0adf1e6d5\" data-question=\"40\">emergence of aggressive tendencies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"9c77ffeb-c0c2-45de-860b-22806ef2abe2","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"a commonly held belief","passagePhrase":"a general assumption"},{"uid":"a459565b-8db5-4ccb-8cad-24a6fe87e925","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"people’s behaviour","passagePhrase":"human beings are essentially selfish"},{"uid":"11f93a54-6e07-43c8-99d1-5a3819fca892","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"was in line with","passagePhrase":"fitted so well with"},{"uid":"442a4343-fc88-4ab4-9a3c-44b50497addf","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"the attitudes of its time","passagePhrase":"the competitive and individualistic ethos that was so prevalent in late 20th-century societies"},{"uid":"2c31b212-07a6-4a89-90bb-b2788741386f","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"developed warlike traits","passagePhrase":"of traits such as racism and warfare"},{"uid":"c2262477-5086-4206-a3c0-e9a6395331e2","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"resources were probably relatively plentiful","passagePhrase":"unlikely that prehistoric hunter-gatherer groups had to compete against each other for resources"},{"uid":"d2c5b4bc-5a29-4ae5-9ece-b3c0223fba7a","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"refers to Bruce Knauft’s work","passagePhrase":"As the anthropologist Bruce Knauft has remarked"},{"uid":"14d43064-9852-4d79-a37b-d3223d841885","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"exhibit a high level of","passagePhrase":"extreme political and sexual egalitarianism"},{"uid":"b271b417-7b93-4b2e-baf0-bd8c0b1ea746","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"selfishness","passagePhrase":"accumulate property or possessions and have an ethical obligation to share everything"},{"uid":"dec524ff-54c7-4654-b9c8-09c21c173468","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"employ strategies","passagePhrase":"have methods"},{"uid":"0c2707bb-819a-4b06-974d-8b099db0befc","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"differences in","passagePhrase":"disparities of status"},{"uid":"97e80f1a-72b6-4ca2-94f0-8b0c1f0e0d99","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"follow a custom","passagePhrase":"swap arrows"},{"uid":"954d6cc6-0d2f-4def-b316-22889f78ae30","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"the credit","passagePhrase":"the acclaim"},{"uid":"2ccd0482-ed42-47b3-aa0b-ce05f663be88","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"punished by being excluded from the group","passagePhrase":"ostracise them, exiling the offender from society"},{"uid":"8681273f-c083-4681-8921-7f406c47a134","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"considerable amount of","passagePhrase":"benefit from a high level of"},{"uid":"a0567171-59a4-43ee-8517-8202012671fe","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"choices regarding work and marriage","passagePhrase":"being able to select their own marriage partners, decide what work they do and work whenever they choose to"},{"uid":"c190c2ea-997b-44ab-abbf-0ed79afe3991","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"Being peaceful and cooperative","passagePhrase":"traits such as cooperation, egalitarianism, altruism and peacefulness"},{"uid":"d8bb42f3-aba1-4af0-876e-0a322f71a079","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"a natural way for people to behave","passagePhrase":"innate characteristics of human beings"},{"uid":"14415a80-70cf-405d-af5b-2857ddf267b5","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"changes in the environment","passagePhrase":"when the natural habitats of primates such as apes and gorillas are disrupted"},{"uid":"b880f417-0d0d-4038-a965-f3d0adf1e6d5","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"emergence of aggressive tendencies","passagePhrase":"become more violent and hierarchical"}]},"reading_u2_307":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>The kākāpō</strong></p><p>The kākāpō is a nocturnal, flightless parrot that is critically endangered and one of New Zealand's unique treasures.</p><p>The kākāpō, also known as the owl parrot, is a large, forest-dwelling bird, with a pale owl-like face. Up to 64 cm in length, it has predominantly yellow-green feathers, forward-facing eyes, a large grey beak, large blue feet, and relatively short wings and tail. It is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ab067b14-a3d1-4cdb-86ad-52df40bd04e1\" data-question=\"1\">the world's only<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> flightless parrot, and is also possibly one of the world's longest-living birds, with a reported lifespan of up to 100 years.</p><p>Kākāpō are solitary birds and tend to occupy the same home range for many years. They forage on the ground and climb high into trees. They often leap from trees and flap their wings, but at best manage a controlled descent to the ground. They are entirely vegetarian, with their diet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a25ce8fb-4080-4ad7-84ba-ebb40de971cd\" data-question=\"7\">including the leaves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>, roots and bark of trees as well as bulbs, and fern fronds.</p><p>Kākāpő <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df47d33d-f3bd-438a-b9be-1eefd3dbe98d\" data-question=\"2\">breed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in summer and autumn, but <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c8e4f6fd-73a9-46d6-b001-a27e28a5efa9\" data-question=\"2\">only in years when food is plentiful<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"49a0c85e-2e3b-4ad7-8ee6-c81f2fc7787e\" data-question=\"3\">Males play no part in incubation or chick-rearing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> - <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"49a0c85e-2e3b-4ad7-8ee6-c81f2fc7787e\" data-question=\"3\">females alone incubate eggs and feed the chicks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. The 1-4 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d275cff-20be-4462-a8dd-0e45df985f22\" data-question=\"8\">eggs are laid in soil<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, which is repeatedly turned over before and during incubation. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"49a0c85e-2e3b-4ad7-8ee6-c81f2fc7787e\" data-question=\"3\">The female kākāpō has to spend long periods away from the nest searching for food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, which leaves the unattended eggs and chicks particularly vulnerable to predators.</p><p>Before humans arrived,kākāpō were common throughout New Zealand's forests. However, this all changed with the arrival of the first Polynesian settlers about 700 years ago. For the early settlers, the flightless kākāpō was easy prey. They ate its meat and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e3caa9d9-ce44-416e-9099-433b765eeaba\" data-question=\"9\">used its feathers to make soft cloaks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. With them came the Polynesian dog and rat, which also preyed on kākāpō. By the time European colonisers arrived in the early 1800s, kākāpō had become confined to the central North Island and forested parts of the South Island. The fall in kākāpō number was accelerated by European colonisation. A great deal of habitat was lost through forest clearance, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4d63b47-3103-452c-af23-f5ca9f76196c\" data-question=\"10\">introduced species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> such as deer <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5321d489-a111-407f-b5e0-70ce525de1c2\" data-question=\"10\">depleted the remaining forests of food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. Other predators such as cats, stoats and two more species of rat were also introduced. The kākāpō were in serious trouble.</p><p>In 1894, the New Zealand government launched its first attempt to save the kākāpō. Conservationist Richard Henry led an effort to relocate several hundred of the birds to predator-free Resolution Island in Fiordland. Unfortunately, the island didn't remain predator-free - stoats arrived within six years, eventually destroying the kākāpō population. By the mid-1900s, the kākāpō was practically a lost species. Only a few clung to life in the most isolated parts of New Zealand.</p><p>From 1949 to 1973, the newly formed New Zealand Wildlife Service made over 60 expeditions to find kākāpō, focusing mainly on Fiordland. Six were caught, but there were no females amongst them and all but one died within a few months of captivity. In 1974, a new initiative was launched, and by 1977, 18 more kākāpō were found in Fiordland. However, there were still no females. In 1977, a large population of males was spotted in Rakiura - a large island free from stoats, ferrets and weasels. There were about 200 individuals, and in 1980 <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ec8231f-4068-411f-903b-e8a7e1e6dce4\" data-question=\"11\">it was confirmed females were also present<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. These birds have been the foundation of all subsequent work in managing the species.</p><p>Unfortunately, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5ab500c-cc0e-47c9-a304-e3ba9f973ec4\" data-question=\"5\">predation by feral cats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> on Rakiura Island led to a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5ab500c-cc0e-47c9-a304-e3ba9f973ec4\" data-question=\"5\">rapid decline in kākāpō numbers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. As a result, during 1980-97, the surviving population was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48d2e15b-d83e-499a-b7dc-573ac4b5b1bb\" data-question=\"5\">evacuated to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a111b6fc-2e44-4ec5-a171-91736a2caaba\" data-question=\"5\">three island sanctuaries: Codfish Island, Maud Island and Little Barrier Island<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. However, breeding success was hard to achieve. Rats were found to be a major predator of kakapo chicks and an insufficient number of chicks survived to offset adult mortality. By 1995, although at least 12 chicks had been produced on the islands, only three had survived. The kākāpō population had dropped to 51 birds. The critical situation prompted an urgent review of kākāpō management in New Zealand.</p><p>In 1996, a new Recovery Plan was launched, together with a specialist advisory group called the Kākāpō Scientific and Technical Advisory Committee and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4fa9bc0-bc14-4c17-8656-b330e343ebf4\" data-question=\"12\">a higher amount of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> funding. Renewed steps were taken to control predators on the three islands. Cats were eradicated from Little Barrier Island in 1980, and possums were eradicated from Codfish Island by 1986. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb754d86-16e7-417e-81e9-c888613a1d01\" data-question=\"6\">the population did not start to increase until<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> rats were removed from all three islands, and the birds were more intensively managed. This involved moving the birds between islands, supplementary feeding of adults and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fbe7813-3408-429f-8689-999401df7334\" data-question=\"6\">rescuing and hand-raising any failing chicks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>.</p><p>After the first five years of the Recovery Plan, the population was on target. By 2000, five new females had been produced, and the total population had grown to 62 birds. For the first time, there was cautious optimism for the future of kākāpō and by June 2020, a total of 210 birds was recorded.</p><p>Today, kākāpō management continues to be guided by the kākāpō Recovery Plan. Its key goals are: minimise the loss of genetic diversity in the kākāpō population, restore or maintain sufficient habitat to accommodate the expected increase in the kākāpō population, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1e98e0f-c11f-4f20-ad58-f6250c3ed53e\" data-question=\"13\">ensure stakeholders continue to be fully engaged<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f6d316c0-0036-413f-83c1-6fd6c3fd4a31\" data-question=\"13\">the preservation of the species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write<br><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222954\" id=\"question-wrapper-222954\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There are <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ab067b14-a3d1-4cdb-86ad-52df40bd04e1\" data-question=\"1\">other parrots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> that share the kakapo's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c69c9ffa-e858-445f-82ff-4d0b331d9725\" data-question=\"1\">inability to fly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222955\" id=\"question-wrapper-222955\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Adult kakapo <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"df47d33d-f3bd-438a-b9be-1eefd3dbe98d\" data-question=\"2\">produce chicks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"c8e4f6fd-73a9-46d6-b001-a27e28a5efa9\" data-question=\"2\">every year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222956\" id=\"question-wrapper-222956\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"49a0c85e-2e3b-4ad7-8ee6-c81f2fc7787e\" data-question=\"3\">Adult male kakapo bring food back to nesting females<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222957\" id=\"question-wrapper-222957\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Polynesian rat was a greater threat to the kakapo than Polynesian settlers. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222958\" id=\"question-wrapper-222958\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Kakapo were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48d2e15b-d83e-499a-b7dc-573ac4b5b1bb\" data-question=\"5\">transferred from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> Rakiura Island to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a111b6fc-2e44-4ec5-a171-91736a2caaba\" data-question=\"5\">other locations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> because they were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e5ab500c-cc0e-47c9-a304-e3ba9f973ec4\" data-question=\"5\">at risk from feral cats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222959\" id=\"question-wrapper-222959\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> One Recovery Plan initiative that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fb754d86-16e7-417e-81e9-c888613a1d01\" data-question=\"6\">helped increase the kakapo population size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2fbe7813-3408-429f-8689-999401df7334\" data-question=\"6\">caring for struggling young birds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>New Zealand's kākāpō</strong></p><p><strong>A type of parrot:</strong><br>● diet <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a25ce8fb-4080-4ad7-84ba-ebb40de971cd\" data-question=\"7\">consists of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> fern fronds, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e65b4b25-40fc-497a-9e3f-566cc6e4ad44\" data-question=\"7\">various parts of a tree<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> and (7) ................<br>● nests are created in (8) ................ <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4d275cff-20be-4462-a8dd-0e45df985f22\" data-question=\"8\">where eggs are laid<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>.<br><strong>Arrival of Polynesian settlers</strong><br>● the (9) ................ of the kākāpō were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e3caa9d9-ce44-416e-9099-433b765eeaba\" data-question=\"9\">used to make clothes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>.<br><strong>Arrival of European colonisers</strong><br>● (10) ................ were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e4d63b47-3103-452c-af23-f5ca9f76196c\" data-question=\"10\">an animal which they introduced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5321d489-a111-407f-b5e0-70ce525de1c2\" data-question=\"10\">ate the kākāpō's food sources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>.<br><strong>Protecting kākāpō</strong><br>● Richard Henry, a conservationist, tried to protect the kākāpō.<br>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0ec8231f-4068-411f-903b-e8a7e1e6dce4\" data-question=\"11\">a definite sighting of female kākāpō<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> on Rakiura Island was reported <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"32941170-7346-4b72-a9bc-15f55b7ae6a6\" data-question=\"11\">in the year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> (11) ................<br>● the Recovery Plan included <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b4fa9bc0-bc14-4c17-8656-b330e343ebf4\" data-question=\"12\">an increase in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> (12) ................<br>● a current goal of the Recovery Plan is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c1e98e0f-c11f-4f20-ad58-f6250c3ed53e\" data-question=\"13\">maintain the involvement of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> (13) ................ in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f6d316c0-0036-413f-83c1-6fd6c3fd4a31\" data-question=\"13\">kākāpō protection<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222960\" id=\"question-wrapper-222960\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BULBS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222961\" id=\"question-wrapper-222961\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SOIL</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222962\" id=\"question-wrapper-222962\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FEATHERS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222963\" id=\"question-wrapper-222963\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DEER</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222964\" id=\"question-wrapper-222964\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">1980</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222965\" id=\"question-wrapper-222965\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FUNDING</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222966\" id=\"question-wrapper-222966\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">STAKEHOLDERS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"a25ce8fb-4080-4ad7-84ba-ebb40de971cd","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"consists of","passagePhrase":"including the leaves"},{"uid":"df47d33d-f3bd-438a-b9be-1eefd3dbe98d","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"produce chicks","passagePhrase":"breed"},{"uid":"4d275cff-20be-4462-a8dd-0e45df985f22","qNum":"8","questionPhrase":"where eggs are laid","passagePhrase":"eggs are laid in soil"},{"uid":"e3caa9d9-ce44-416e-9099-433b765eeaba","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"used to make clothes","passagePhrase":"used its feathers to make soft cloaks"},{"uid":"e4d63b47-3103-452c-af23-f5ca9f76196c","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"an animal which they introduced","passagePhrase":"introduced species"},{"uid":"5321d489-a111-407f-b5e0-70ce525de1c2","qNum":"10","questionPhrase":"ate the kākāpō's food sources","passagePhrase":"depleted the remaining forests of food"},{"uid":"0ec8231f-4068-411f-903b-e8a7e1e6dce4","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"a definite sighting of female kākāpō","passagePhrase":"it was confirmed females were also present"},{"uid":"e5ab500c-cc0e-47c9-a304-e3ba9f973ec4","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"at risk from feral cats","passagePhrase":"predation by feral cats ... rapid decline in kākāpō numbers"},{"uid":"48d2e15b-d83e-499a-b7dc-573ac4b5b1bb","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"transferred from","passagePhrase":"evacuated to"},{"uid":"a111b6fc-2e44-4ec5-a171-91736a2caaba","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"other locations","passagePhrase":"three island sanctuaries: Codfish Island, Maud Island and Little Barrier Island"},{"uid":"b4fa9bc0-bc14-4c17-8656-b330e343ebf4","qNum":"12","questionPhrase":"an increase in","passagePhrase":"a higher amount of"},{"uid":"fb754d86-16e7-417e-81e9-c888613a1d01","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"helped increase the kakapo population size","passagePhrase":"the population did not start to increase until"},{"uid":"2fbe7813-3408-429f-8689-999401df7334","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"caring for struggling young birds","passagePhrase":"rescuing and hand-raising any failing chicks"},{"uid":"c1e98e0f-c11f-4f20-ad58-f6250c3ed53e","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"maintain the involvement of","passagePhrase":"ensure stakeholders continue to be fully engaged"},{"uid":"f6d316c0-0036-413f-83c1-6fd6c3fd4a31","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"kākāpō protection","passagePhrase":"the preservation of the species"},{"uid":"c69c9ffa-e858-445f-82ff-4d0b331d9725","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"inability to fly","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"e65b4b25-40fc-497a-9e3f-566cc6e4ad44","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"various parts of a tree","passagePhrase":""},{"uid":"32941170-7346-4b72-a9bc-15f55b7ae6a6","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"in the year","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_308":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Bring elms to Britain</strong></p><p>Mark Rowe investigates attempts to reintroduce elms to Britain</p><p>A. Around 25 million elms, accounting for 90% of all elm trees in the UK, died during the 1960s and '70s of Dutch elm disease. In the aftermath, the elm, once so dominant in the British landscape, was largely forgotten. However, there's now hope the elm may be reintroduced to the countryside of central and southern England. Any reintroduction will start from a very low base. 'The impact of the disease is difficult to picture if you hadn't seen what was there before,' says Matt Elliot of the Woodland Trust. 'You <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36b8286b-4779-412f-85b0-2af38c150ca1\" data-question=\"23\">look at old photographs from the 1960s<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> and it's only then that you realise <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8535525-1516-46f7-94b4-e96f648d6a34\" data-question=\"23\">the impact<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> [elms had] … <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36b8286b-4779-412f-85b0-2af38c150ca1\" data-question=\"23\">They were significant, large trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>... then they were gone.'</p><p>B. The disease is caused by a fungus that blocks the elms' vascular (water, nutrient and food transport) system, causing branches to wilt and die. A first epidemic, which occurred in the 1920s, gradually died down, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ffaa534-1d85-4685-98ca-12bcc08ad50c\" data-question=\"16\">in the '70s a second epidemic was triggered by shipments of elm from Canada<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ffaa534-1d85-4685-98ca-12bcc08ad50c\" data-question=\"16\">The wood came in the form of logs destined for boat building and its intact bark was perfect for the elm bark beetles that spread the deadly fungus<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. This time, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ffaa534-1d85-4685-98ca-12bcc08ad50c\" data-question=\"16\">the beetles carried a much more virulent strain that destroyed the vast majority of British elms.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></p><p>C. Today, elms still exist in the southern English countryside but mostly only in low hedgerows between fields. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ab41039-9e73-438d-855a-c1248a6884a5\" data-question=\"18\">'We have millions of small elms in hedgerows but they get targeted by the beetle as soon as they reach a certain size<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>,' says Karen Russell, co-author of the report 'Where we are with elm'. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ab41039-9e73-438d-855a-c1248a6884a5\" data-question=\"18\">Once the trunk of the elm reaches 10-15 centimetres or so in diameter, it becomes a perfect size for beetles to lay eggs and for the fungus to take hold.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53c40148-a5df-40c3-890c-d883c1c27cb8\" data-question=\"14\">Yet mature specimens have been identified, in counties such as Cambridgeshire, that are hundreds of years old, and have mysteriously escaped the epidemic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21c74567-5d4e-4a1a-897d-8511ffe933b5\" data-question=\"21\">The key<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>, Russell says, is to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53c40148-a5df-40c3-890c-d883c1c27cb8\" data-question=\"14\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21c74567-5d4e-4a1a-897d-8511ffe933b5\" data-question=\"21\">identify and study those trees that have survived<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> and work out why they stood tall when millions of others succumbed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. Nevertheless, opportunities are limited as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f03a2f49-9935-4bf2-b1ab-fb149e1b9f58\" data-question=\"14\">the number of these mature survivors is relatively small<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53c40148-a5df-40c3-890c-d883c1c27cb8\" data-question=\"14\">'What are the reasons for their survival?'<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> asks Russell. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53c40148-a5df-40c3-890c-d883c1c27cb8\" data-question=\"14\">'Avoidance, tolerance, resistance?<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> We don't know where the balance lies between the three. I don't see how it can be entirely down to luck.'</p><p>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c75789a-9784-496f-8d7a-8e6973e3e2e4\" data-question=\"24\">For centuries<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e786ab9c-7a12-4311-ae49-725efe5e7233\" data-question=\"24\">elm ran a close second to oak as the hardwood tree of choice in Britain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> and was in many instances the most prominent tree in the landscape. Not only was elm common in European forests, it became a key component of birch, ash and hazel woodlands. The use of elm is thought to go back to the Bronze Age, when it was widely used for tools. Elm was also the preferred material for shields and early swords. In the 18th century, it was planted more widely and its wood was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe9ea4c9-eeea-448b-a25d-caeb0b6bddd7\" data-question=\"25\">used for items such as storage crates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and flooring. It was also suitable for items that experienced high levels of impact and was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd161b4a-e7de-4ca9-a284-e2be68d490d5\" data-question=\"26\">used to build the keel of the 19th-century sailing ship Cutty Sark<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> as well as mining equipment.</p><p>E. Given how ingrained elm is in British culture, it's unsurprising the tree has many advocates. Amongst them is Peter Bourne of the National Elm Collection in Brighton. 'I saw Dutch elm disease unfold as a small boy,' he says. 'The elm seemed to be part of rural England, but I remember watching trees just lose their leaves and that really stayed with me.' Today, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aff16e20-ec71-49fe-bb86-c206d4d3b033\" data-question=\"17\">the city of Brighton's elms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> total about 17,000. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aff16e20-ec71-49fe-bb86-c206d4d3b033\" data-question=\"17\">Local factors appear to have contributed to their survival<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aff16e20-ec71-49fe-bb86-c206d4d3b033\" data-question=\"17\">Strong winds from the sea make it difficult for the determined elm bark beetle to attack this coastal city's elm population<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. However, the situation is precarious. '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bdc346bb-2d97-44e1-9bdf-38d63037b4e6\" data-question=\"22\">The beetles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> can just march in if we're not careful, as the threat is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fcfcbeba-7d68-49d6-b30f-9b24cd85b3a3\" data-question=\"22\">right on our doorstep<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>,' says Bourne.</p><p>F. Any prospect of the elm returning relies heavily on trees being either resistant to, or tolerant of, the disease. This means a widespread reintroduction would involve existing or new hybrid strains derived from resistant, generally non-native elm species. A new generation of seedlings have been bred and tested to see if they can withstand the fungus by cutting a small slit on the bark and injecting a tiny amount of the pathogen. '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0053a7c7-96a5-40d9-b4cf-a4343cae3e13\" data-question=\"19\">The effects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e08c4550-9a83-45ff-84d8-16edda0526d9\" data-question=\"19\">very quick<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>,' says Russell. 'You return in four to six weeks and trees that are resistant show no symptoms, whereas those that are susceptible <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e08c4550-9a83-45ff-84d8-16edda0526d9\" data-question=\"19\">show leaf loss<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e08c4550-9a83-45ff-84d8-16edda0526d9\" data-question=\"19\">may even have died completely<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>.'</p><p>G. All of this raises questions of social acceptance, acknowledges Russell. 'If we're putting elm back into the landscape, a small element of it is not native are we bothered about that?' <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f13b51d8-033d-4fca-a542-da3f0558a1c9\" data-question=\"15\">For her, the environmental case for reintroducing elm is strong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f13b51d8-033d-4fca-a542-da3f0558a1c9\" data-question=\"15\">'They will host wildlife, which is a good thing.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>' <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f13b51d8-033d-4fca-a542-da3f0558a1c9\" data-question=\"15\">Others are more wary<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. 'On the face of it, it seems like a good idea,' says Elliot. The problem, he suggests, is that, '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f13b51d8-033d-4fca-a542-da3f0558a1c9\" data-question=\"15\">You're replacing a native species with a horticultural analogue<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>*. You're effectively cloning.' <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f13b51d8-033d-4fca-a542-da3f0558a1c9\" data-question=\"15\">There's also the risk of introducing new diseases<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. Rather than plant new elms, the Woodland Trust emphasises providing space to those elms that have survived independently. '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ae2c89c5-a16f-439e-b917-527455357235\" data-question=\"20\">Sometimes the best thing you can do is just give nature time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f678b9df-4b2b-48b5-9dbf-9e6093930800\" data-question=\"20\">recover over time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, you might get <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f678b9df-4b2b-48b5-9dbf-9e6093930800\" data-question=\"20\">resistance<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>,' says Elliot.<br>__________________________<br><em>*horticultural analogue: a cultivated plant species that is genetically similar to an existing species</em></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has seven sections, A-G. Which section contains the following information? NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222967\" id=\"question-wrapper-222967\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Reference to the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"53c40148-a5df-40c3-890c-d883c1c27cb8\" data-question=\"14\">research problems that arise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> from there being <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f03a2f49-9935-4bf2-b1ab-fb149e1b9f58\" data-question=\"14\">only a few surviving large elms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222968\" id=\"question-wrapper-222968\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Details of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f13b51d8-033d-4fca-a542-da3f0558a1c9\" data-question=\"15\">a difference of opinion about the value of reintroducing elms to Britain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222969\" id=\"question-wrapper-222969\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1ffaa534-1d85-4685-98ca-12bcc08ad50c\" data-question=\"16\">how Dutch elm disease was brought into Britain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222970\" id=\"question-wrapper-222970\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A description of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aff16e20-ec71-49fe-bb86-c206d4d3b033\" data-question=\"17\">the conditions that have enabled a location in Britain to escape Dutch elm disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222971\" id=\"question-wrapper-222971\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6ab41039-9e73-438d-855a-c1248a6884a5\" data-question=\"18\">the stage at which young elms become vulnerable to Dutch elm disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following statements (Questions 19-23) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A, B, or C.</p><p>NB You may use any letter more than once.</p><p><strong>List of people</strong><br>A. Matt Elliot<br>B. Karen Russell<br>C. Peter Bourne</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222972\" id=\"question-wrapper-222972\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> If a tree gets infected with Dutch elm disease, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0053a7c7-96a5-40d9-b4cf-a4343cae3e13\" data-question=\"19\">the damage<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e08c4550-9a83-45ff-84d8-16edda0526d9\" data-question=\"19\">rapidly becomes visible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222973\" id=\"question-wrapper-222973\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ae2c89c5-a16f-439e-b917-527455357235\" data-question=\"20\">It may be better to wait<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f678b9df-4b2b-48b5-9dbf-9e6093930800\" data-question=\"20\">see if the mature elms that have survived continue to flourish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222974\" id=\"question-wrapper-222974\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"21c74567-5d4e-4a1a-897d-8511ffe933b5\" data-question=\"21\">There must be an explanation for the survival of some mature elms<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222975\" id=\"question-wrapper-222975\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> We need to be aware that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bdc346bb-2d97-44e1-9bdf-38d63037b4e6\" data-question=\"22\">insects carrying Dutch elm disease<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fcfcbeba-7d68-49d6-b30f-9b24cd85b3a3\" data-question=\"22\">not very far away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222976\" id=\"question-wrapper-222976\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> You understand <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8535525-1516-46f7-94b4-e96f648d6a34\" data-question=\"23\">the effect<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> Dutch elm disease has had when you <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"36b8286b-4779-412f-85b0-2af38c150ca1\" data-question=\"23\">see evidence of how prominent the tree once was<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>Uses of a popular tree</strong><br><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c75789a-9784-496f-8d7a-8e6973e3e2e4\" data-question=\"24\">For hundreds of years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e786ab9c-7a12-4311-ae49-725efe5e7233\" data-question=\"24\">the only tree that was more popular in Britain than elm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> was (24) ............... Starting in the Bronze Age, many tools were made from elm and people also used it to make weapons. In the 18th century, it was grown to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"fe9ea4c9-eeea-448b-a25d-caeb0b6bddd7\" data-question=\"25\">provide wood for boxes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> and (25) ............... Due to its strength, elm was often used for mining equipment and the Cutty Sark's (26) ............... <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd161b4a-e7de-4ca9-a284-e2be68d490d5\" data-question=\"26\">was also constructed from elm<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222977\" id=\"question-wrapper-222977\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">OAK</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222978\" id=\"question-wrapper-222978\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FLOORING</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222979\" id=\"question-wrapper-222979\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">KEEL</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"36b8286b-4779-412f-85b0-2af38c150ca1","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"see evidence of how prominent the tree once was","passagePhrase":"look at old photographs from the 1960s ... They were significant, large trees"},{"uid":"e8535525-1516-46f7-94b4-e96f648d6a34","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"the effect","passagePhrase":"the impact"},{"uid":"1ffaa534-1d85-4685-98ca-12bcc08ad50c","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"how Dutch elm disease was brought into Britain","passagePhrase":"in the '70s a second epidemic was triggered by shipments of elm from Canada ... The wood came in the form of logs destined for boat building and its intact bark was perfect for the elm bark beetles that spread the deadly fungus ... the beetles carried a much more virulent strain that destroyed the vast majority of British elms."},{"uid":"6ab41039-9e73-438d-855a-c1248a6884a5","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"the stage at which young elms become vulnerable to Dutch elm disease","passagePhrase":"'We have millions of small elms in hedgerows but they get targeted by the beetle as soon as they reach a certain size ... Once the trunk of the elm reaches 10-15 centimetres or so in diameter, it becomes a perfect size for beetles to lay eggs and for the fungus to take hold."},{"uid":"53c40148-a5df-40c3-890c-d883c1c27cb8","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"research problems that arise","passagePhrase":"Yet mature specimens have been identified, in counties such as Cambridgeshire, that are hundreds of years old, and have mysteriously escaped the epidemic ... identify and study those trees that have survived and work out why they stood tall when millions of others succumbed ... 'What are the reasons for their survival?' ... 'Avoidance, tolerance, resistance?"},{"uid":"21c74567-5d4e-4a1a-897d-8511ffe933b5","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"There must be an explanation for the survival of some mature elms","passagePhrase":"The key ... identify and study those trees that have survived"},{"uid":"f03a2f49-9935-4bf2-b1ab-fb149e1b9f58","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"only a few surviving large elms","passagePhrase":"the number of these mature survivors is relatively small"},{"uid":"6c75789a-9784-496f-8d7a-8e6973e3e2e4","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"For hundreds of years","passagePhrase":"For centuries"},{"uid":"e786ab9c-7a12-4311-ae49-725efe5e7233","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"the only tree that was more popular in Britain than elm","passagePhrase":"elm ran a close second to oak as the hardwood tree of choice in Britain"},{"uid":"fe9ea4c9-eeea-448b-a25d-caeb0b6bddd7","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"provide wood for boxes","passagePhrase":"used for items such as storage crates"},{"uid":"bd161b4a-e7de-4ca9-a284-e2be68d490d5","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"was also constructed from elm","passagePhrase":"used to build the keel of the 19th-century sailing ship Cutty Sark"},{"uid":"aff16e20-ec71-49fe-bb86-c206d4d3b033","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"the conditions that have enabled a location in Britain to escape Dutch elm disease","passagePhrase":"the city of Brighton's elms ... Local factors appear to have contributed to their survival ... Strong winds from the sea make it difficult for the determined elm bark beetle to attack this coastal city's elm population"},{"uid":"bdc346bb-2d97-44e1-9bdf-38d63037b4e6","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"insects carrying Dutch elm disease","passagePhrase":"The beetles"},{"uid":"fcfcbeba-7d68-49d6-b30f-9b24cd85b3a3","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"not very far away","passagePhrase":"right on our doorstep"},{"uid":"0053a7c7-96a5-40d9-b4cf-a4343cae3e13","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"the damage","passagePhrase":"The effects"},{"uid":"e08c4550-9a83-45ff-84d8-16edda0526d9","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"rapidly becomes visible","passagePhrase":"very quick ... show leaf loss ... may even have died completely"},{"uid":"f13b51d8-033d-4fca-a542-da3f0558a1c9","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"a difference of opinion about the value of reintroducing elms to Britain","passagePhrase":"For her, the environmental case for reintroducing elm is strong ... 'They will host wildlife, which is a good thing. ... Others are more wary ... You're replacing a native species with a horticultural analogue ... There's also the risk of introducing new diseases"},{"uid":"ae2c89c5-a16f-439e-b917-527455357235","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"It may be better to wait","passagePhrase":"Sometimes the best thing you can do is just give nature time"},{"uid":"f678b9df-4b2b-48b5-9dbf-9e6093930800","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"see if the mature elms that have survived continue to flourish","passagePhrase":"recover over time ... resistance"}]},"reading_u2_309":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>How stress affects our judgement</strong></p><p>Some of the most important decisions of our lives occur while we're feeling stressed and anxious. From medical decisions to financial and professional ones, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41bcd342-5320-48a0-adc7-cb3250316522\" data-question=\"27\">we are all sometimes required to weigh up information under stressful conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. But <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41bcd342-5320-48a0-adc7-cb3250316522\" data-question=\"27\">do we become better or worse at processing and using information under such circumstances?<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span></p><p>My colleague and I, both neuroscientists, wanted to investigate how the mind operates under stress, so we visited some local fire stations. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4ae9f95a-7cc8-49e8-ac09-0b2955c0657b\" data-question=\"28\">Firefighters' workdays vary quite a bit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4ae9f95a-7cc8-49e8-ac09-0b2955c0657b\" data-question=\"28\">Some are pretty relaxed<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>; they'll spend their time washing the truck, cleaning equipment, cooking meals and reading. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4ae9f95a-7cc8-49e8-ac09-0b2955c0657b\" data-question=\"28\">Other days can be hectic, with numerous life-threatening incidents to attend to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>; they'll enter burning homes to rescue trapped residents, and assist with medical emergencies. These ups and downs <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20120a12-88a5-40bd-bc82-1119eb401b98\" data-question=\"28\">presented the perfect setting for an experiment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> on how people's ability to use information changes when they feel under pressure.</p><p>We found that perceived threat acted as a trigger for a stress reaction that made the task of processing information easier for the firefighters - but only as long as it conveyed bad news.</p><p>This is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc4d8104-5936-456f-91bd-8e2180bb9fcf\" data-question=\"29\">how we arrived at these results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. We asked the firefighters to estimate their likelihood of experiencing 40 different adverse events in their life, such as being involved in an accident or becoming a victim of card fraud. We then gave them either good news (that their likelihood of experiencing these events was lower than they'd thought) or bad news (that it was higher) and asked them to provide new estimates. </p><p>People are normally quite optimistic - they will <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6316d2a0-d34f-488f-9b58-a473259eaf52\" data-question=\"31\">ignore bad news<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> and embrace the good. This is what happened when the firefighters were relaxed; but when they were under stress, a different pattern emerged. Under these conditions, they <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10dc41c8-5def-46c3-881b-c8d26ff858a1\" data-question=\"32\">became hyper-vigilant to bad news<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, even when it had nothing to do with their job (such as learning that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10dc41c8-5def-46c3-881b-c8d26ff858a1\" data-question=\"32\">the likelihood of card fraud was higher than they'd thought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>), and altered their beliefs in response. In contrast, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b431ddc-3ac8-4e76-957c-a25d5574d78b\" data-question=\"33\">stress didn't change how they responded to good news<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> (such as learning that the likelihood of card fraud was lower than they'd thought).</p><p>Back in our lab, we observed the same pattern in students who were told they had to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"63d191a1-9e27-4f1b-baee-b7f33d681113\" data-question=\"34\">give a surprise public speech<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, which would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"63d191a1-9e27-4f1b-baee-b7f33d681113\" data-question=\"34\">be judged by a panel, recorded and posted online<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Sure enough, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c1df034-5ff9-45b3-9af3-7a1972f0620a\" data-question=\"34\">their cortisol levels spiked, their heart rates went up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> and they suddenly became better at processing unrelated, yet alarming, information about rates of disease and violence.</p><p>When we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"01472757-c58b-4831-a704-77a23e4fa282\" data-question=\"35\">experience stressful events<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"557a42ae-f4df-4713-adb5-6805d3a7b172\" data-question=\"30\">a physiological change is triggered<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that causes us to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e9db1f6-0136-4e8a-b538-5ef903b58c7d\" data-question=\"30\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f67a87e-f823-4155-aef7-75ae1df50277\" data-question=\"35\">take in warnings and focus on what might go wrong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. Brain imaging reveals that this 'switch' is related to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e9db1f6-0136-4e8a-b538-5ef903b58c7d\" data-question=\"30\">a sudden boost in a neural signal<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> important for learning, specifically in response to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e64a8f0f-cc61-4f11-b275-03e950eff25d\" data-question=\"30\">unexpected warning signs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, such as faces expressing fear.</p><p>Such neural engineering could have helped prehistoric humans to survive. When our ancestors found themselves surrounded by hungry animals, they would have benefited from an increased ability to learn about hazards. In a safe environment, however, it would have been wasteful to be on high alert constantly. So, a neural switch that automatically increases or decreases our ability to process warnings in response to changes in our environment could have been useful. In fact, people with clinical depression and anxiety seem unable to switch away from a state in which they absorb all the negative messages around them.</p><p>It is also important to realise that stress travels rapidly from one person to the next. If a co-worker is stressed, we are more likely to tense up and feel stressed ourselves. We don't even need to be in the same room with someone for their emotions to influence our behaviour. Studies show that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa89d96a-3be4-4d5a-b615-97855aaef97e\" data-question=\"36\">if we observe positive feeds on social media<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, such as images of a pink sunset, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08771d56-e81d-42ae-b753-77be3af69b96\" data-question=\"36\">we are more likely to post uplifting messages ourselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa89d96a-3be4-4d5a-b615-97855aaef97e\" data-question=\"36\">If we observe negative posts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>, such as complaints about a long queue at the coffee shop, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08771d56-e81d-42ae-b753-77be3af69b96\" data-question=\"36\">we will in turn create more negative posts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</p><p>In some ways, many of us now live as if we are in danger, constantly ready to tackle demanding emails and text messages, and respond to news alerts and comments on social media. Repeatedly checking your phone, according to a survey conducted by the American Psychological Association, is related to stress. In other words, a pre-programmed physiological reaction, which evolution has equipped us with to help us avoid famished predators, is now being triggered by an online post. Social media posting, according to one study, raises your pulse, makes you sweat, and enlarges your pupils more than most daily activities.</p><p>The fact that <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a811cb91-dcb7-403c-8e47-92a299cf2f30\" data-question=\"38\">stress increases the likelihood that we will focus more on alarming messages<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, together with the fact that it spreads extremely rapidly, can create collective fear that is not always justified. After a stressful public event, such as a natural disaster or major financial crash, there is often a wave of alarming information in traditional and social media, which individuals become very aware of. But that has the effect of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"812b7af3-18df-4cb3-a90a-028d9dfdbfc3\" data-question=\"39\">exaggerating existing danger<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. And so, a reliable pattern emerges - stress is triggered, spreading from one person to the next, which temporarily enhances the likelihood that people will take in negative reports, which increases stress further. As a result, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"812b7af3-18df-4cb3-a90a-028d9dfdbfc3\" data-question=\"39\">trips are cancelled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, even if the disaster took place across the globe; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"812b7af3-18df-4cb3-a90a-028d9dfdbfc3\" data-question=\"39\">stocks are sold<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, even when holding on is the best thing to do.</p><p>The good news, however, is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eb0560a-e86c-487e-885e-8058e51b8ffa\" data-question=\"40\">positive emotions, such as hope, are contagious too, and are powerful in inducing people to act to find solutions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Being aware of the information can help us frame our messages more effectively and become conscientious agents of change.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222980\" id=\"question-wrapper-222980\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the first paragraph, the writer introduces the topic of the text by </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Defining some commonly used terms.</li> <li>B. Questioning a widely held assumption.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"41bcd342-5320-48a0-adc7-cb3250316522\" data-question=\"27\">Mentioning a challenge faced by everyone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Specifying a situation which makes us most anxious.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222981\" id=\"question-wrapper-222981\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does the writer make about firefighters in the second paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4ae9f95a-7cc8-49e8-ac09-0b2955c0657b\" data-question=\"28\">The regular changes of stress levels in their working lives<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"20120a12-88a5-40bd-bc82-1119eb401b98\" data-question=\"28\">make them ideal study subject<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>s.</li> <li>B. The strategies they use to handle stress are of particular interest to researchers.</li> <li>C. The stressful nature of their job is typical of many public service professions.</li> <li>D. Their personalities make them especially well-suited to working under stress.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222982\" id=\"question-wrapper-222982\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is the writer doing in the fourth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Explaining their findings.</li> <li>B. Justifying their approach.</li> <li>C. Setting out their objectives.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc4d8104-5936-456f-91bd-8e2180bb9fcf\" data-question=\"29\">Describing their methodology<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222983\" id=\"question-wrapper-222983\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In the seventh paragraph, the writer describes a <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"557a42ae-f4df-4713-adb5-6805d3a7b172\" data-question=\"30\">mechanism in the brain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> which </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Enables people to respond more quickly to stressful situations.</li> <li>B. Results in increased ability to control our levels of anxiety.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e9db1f6-0136-4e8a-b538-5ef903b58c7d\" data-question=\"30\">Produces heightened sensitivity<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e64a8f0f-cc61-4f11-b275-03e950eff25d\" data-question=\"30\">indications of external threats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Is activated when there is a need to communicate a sense of danger.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-G, below.<br>A. made them feel optimistic.<br>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6316d2a0-d34f-488f-9b58-a473259eaf52\" data-question=\"31\">took relatively little notice of bad news<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.<br>C. responded to negative and positive information in the same way.<br>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"01472757-c58b-4831-a704-77a23e4fa282\" data-question=\"35\">were feeling under stress<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.<br>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"63d191a1-9e27-4f1b-baee-b7f33d681113\" data-question=\"34\">put them in a stressful situation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.<br>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1b431ddc-3ac8-4e76-957c-a25d5574d78b\" data-question=\"33\">behaved in a similar manner, regardless of the circumstances<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>.<br>G. thought <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10dc41c8-5def-46c3-881b-c8d26ff858a1\" data-question=\"32\">it more likely that they would experience something bad<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222984\" id=\"question-wrapper-222984\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> At times when they were relaxed, the firefighters usually ................ </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222985\" id=\"question-wrapper-222985\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The researchers noted that when the firefighters were stressed, they ................ </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222986\" id=\"question-wrapper-222986\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When the firefighters were told good news, they always ................ </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222987\" id=\"question-wrapper-222987\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4c1df034-5ff9-45b3-9af3-7a1972f0620a\" data-question=\"34\">The students' cortisol levels and heart rates were affected<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> when the researchers ................ </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222988\" id=\"question-wrapper-222988\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> In both experiments, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f67a87e-f823-4155-aef7-75ae1df50277\" data-question=\"35\">negative information was processed better<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> when the subjects ................ </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3?</span></p><p><span>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222989\" id=\"question-wrapper-222989\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"08771d56-e81d-42ae-b753-77be3af69b96\" data-question=\"36\">The tone of the content we post on social media<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aa89d96a-3be4-4d5a-b615-97855aaef97e\" data-question=\"36\">tends to reflect the nature of the posts in our feeds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222990\" id=\"question-wrapper-222990\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Phones have a greater impact on our stress levels than other electronic media devices. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222991\" id=\"question-wrapper-222991\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"a811cb91-dcb7-403c-8e47-92a299cf2f30\" data-question=\"38\">The more we read about a stressful public event on social media, the less able we are to take the information<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222992\" id=\"question-wrapper-222992\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Stress created by social media posts can lead us to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"812b7af3-18df-4cb3-a90a-028d9dfdbfc3\" data-question=\"39\">take unnecessary precautions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222993\" id=\"question-wrapper-222993\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eb0560a-e86c-487e-885e-8058e51b8ffa\" data-question=\"40\">Our tendency to be affected by other people's moods can be used in a positive way<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"41bcd342-5320-48a0-adc7-cb3250316522","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"Mentioning a challenge faced by everyone","passagePhrase":"we are all sometimes required to weigh up information under stressful conditions ... do we become better or worse at processing and using information under such circumstances?"},{"uid":"4ae9f95a-7cc8-49e8-ac09-0b2955c0657b","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The regular changes of stress levels in their working lives","passagePhrase":"Firefighters' workdays vary quite a bit ... Some are pretty relaxed ... Other days can be hectic, with numerous life-threatening incidents to attend to"},{"uid":"20120a12-88a5-40bd-bc82-1119eb401b98","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"make them ideal study subject","passagePhrase":"presented the perfect setting for an experiment"},{"uid":"bc4d8104-5936-456f-91bd-8e2180bb9fcf","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"Describing their methodology","passagePhrase":"how we arrived at these results"},{"uid":"6316d2a0-d34f-488f-9b58-a473259eaf52","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"took relatively little notice of bad news","passagePhrase":"ignore bad news"},{"uid":"10dc41c8-5def-46c3-881b-c8d26ff858a1","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"it more likely that they would experience something bad","passagePhrase":"became hyper-vigilant to bad news ... the likelihood of card fraud was higher than they'd thought"},{"uid":"1b431ddc-3ac8-4e76-957c-a25d5574d78b","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"behaved in a similar manner, regardless of the circumstances","passagePhrase":"stress didn't change how they responded to good news"},{"uid":"63d191a1-9e27-4f1b-baee-b7f33d681113","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"put them in a stressful situation","passagePhrase":"give a surprise public speech ... be judged by a panel, recorded and posted online"},{"uid":"4c1df034-5ff9-45b3-9af3-7a1972f0620a","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"The students' cortisol levels and heart rates were affected","passagePhrase":"their cortisol levels spiked, their heart rates went up"},{"uid":"01472757-c58b-4831-a704-77a23e4fa282","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"were feeling under stress","passagePhrase":"experience stressful events"},{"uid":"557a42ae-f4df-4713-adb5-6805d3a7b172","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"mechanism in the brain","passagePhrase":"a physiological change is triggered"},{"uid":"8e9db1f6-0136-4e8a-b538-5ef903b58c7d","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Produces heightened sensitivity","passagePhrase":"take in warnings and focus on what might go wrong ... a sudden boost in a neural signal"},{"uid":"7f67a87e-f823-4155-aef7-75ae1df50277","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"negative information was processed better","passagePhrase":"take in warnings and focus on what might go wrong"},{"uid":"e64a8f0f-cc61-4f11-b275-03e950eff25d","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"indications of external threats","passagePhrase":"unexpected warning signs"},{"uid":"aa89d96a-3be4-4d5a-b615-97855aaef97e","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"tends to reflect the nature of the posts in our feeds","passagePhrase":"if we observe positive feeds on social media ... If we observe negative posts"},{"uid":"08771d56-e81d-42ae-b753-77be3af69b96","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"The tone of the content we post on social media","passagePhrase":"we are more likely to post uplifting messages ourselves ... we will in turn create more negative posts"},{"uid":"812b7af3-18df-4cb3-a90a-028d9dfdbfc3","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"take unnecessary precautions","passagePhrase":"exaggerating existing danger ... trips are cancelled ... stocks are sold"},{"uid":"3eb0560a-e86c-487e-885e-8058e51b8ffa","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Our tendency to be affected by other people's moods can be used in a positive way","passagePhrase":"positive emotions, such as hope, are contagious too, and are powerful in inducing people to act to find solutions"}]},"reading_u2_310":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Manatees</strong></p><p>Manatees, also known as sea cows, are aquatic mammals that belong to a group of animals called Sirenia. This group also contains dugongs. Dugongs and manatees <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0408c24-cb1e-432f-a780-cf184fff7ee6\" data-question=\"1\">look quite alike<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> - they are similar in size, colour and shape, and both have flexible flippers for forelimbs. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c666d2f-531b-40ed-99f3-fda24ebb5f6e\" data-question=\"1\">the manatee has a broad, rounded tail<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, whereas <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c666d2f-531b-40ed-99f3-fda24ebb5f6e\" data-question=\"1\">the dugong's is fluked, like that of a whale.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> There are three species of manatees: the West Indian manatee (Trichechus manatus), the African manatee (Trichechus senegalensis) and the Amazonian manatee (Trichechus inunguis).</p><p>Unlike most mammals, manatees have only six bones in their neck - most others, including humans and giraffes, have seven. This short neck allows a manatee to move its head up and down, but not side to side. To <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c587133-888b-4ec9-914f-79d8d00eabaa\" data-question=\"2\">see something on its left or its right<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, a manatee must <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3577f310-0310-4ed3-aa23-2fdf25b7c914\" data-question=\"2\">turn its entire body<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>, steering with its flippers. Manatees have pectoral flippers but no back limbs, only a tail for propulsion. They do have pelvic bones, however - a leftover from their evolution from a four-legged to a fully aquatic animal. Manatees share some visual similarities to elephants. Like elephants, manatees have thick, wrinkled skin. They also have <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8915c1c5-bbc6-4c73-a512-973f7f4912d5\" data-question=\"3\">some hairs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"05b79f65-15ed-4ba0-978e-7146ecff6c2e\" data-question=\"3\">covering their bodies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> which help them sense vibrations in the water around them.</p><p>Seagrasses and other <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0405504-8b5d-4631-ab0f-54a150e4408d\" data-question=\"4\">marine plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c5cfa663-3c96-4698-8687-9bad61313ef8\" data-question=\"4\">make up most of a manatee's diet<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>. Manatees spend about eight hours each day grazing and uprooting plants. They eat up to 15% of their weight in food each day. African manatees are omnivorous - studies have shown that molluscs and fish make up a small part of their diets. West Indian and Amazonian manatees are both herbivores.</p><p>Manatees' teeth are all molars - flat, rounded teeth for grinding food. Due to manatees' abrasive aquatic plant diet, these teeth get worn down and they eventually fall out, so they continually grow new teeth that get pushed forward to replace the ones they lose. Instead of having incisors to grasp their food, manatees have lips which function like a pair of hands to help <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd85afea-7183-4e5b-8268-71d8cf2e5750\" data-question=\"5\">tear food away from the seafloor<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.</p><p>Manatees are fully aquatic, but as mammals, they need to come up to the surface to 44/130 breathe. When awake, they typically surface every two to four minutes, but they can hold their breath for much longer. Adult manatees sleep underwater for 10-12 hours a day, but they come up for air every 15-20 minutes. Active manatees need to breathe more frequently. It's thought that manatees use their <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d80ea223-f4f5-4445-95db-71fd4b0da9e9\" data-question=\"6\">muscular diaphragm and breathing<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b78bbbb9-545d-4934-9610-45e9383fa900\" data-question=\"6\">adjust<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> their buoyancy. They may use diaphragm contractions to compress and store gas in folds in their large intestine to help them float.</p><p>The West Indian manatee reaches about 3.5 metres long and weighs on average around 500 kilogrammes. It <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86fdf386-c90e-4ce8-ae0b-91bda798d24c\" data-question=\"7\">moves between<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> fresh water and salt water, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86fdf386-c90e-4ce8-ae0b-91bda798d24c\" data-question=\"7\">taking advantage of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"00ff8f04-5c78-4f09-a87b-121cb06ff706\" data-question=\"7\">coastal mangroves and coral reefs, rivers, lakes and inland lagoons<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. There are two subspecies of West Indian manatee: the Antillean manatee is found in waters from the Bahamas to Brazil, whereas the Florida manatee is found in US waters, although some individuals have been recorded in the Bahamas. In winter, the Florida manatee is typically restricted to Florida. When the ambient water temperature drops below 20°C, it takes refuge in naturally and artificially warmed water, such as at the warm-water outfalls from powerplants.</p><p>The African manatee is also about 3.5 metres long and found in the sea along the west coast of Africa, from Mauritania down to Angola. The species also makes use of rivers, with the mammals <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ca06f865-f15d-4069-ba20-ec954874d355\" data-question=\"9\">seen in landlocked countries such as Mali and Niger.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span></p><p>The Amazonian manatee is the smallest species, though it is still a big animal. It grows to about 2.5 metres long and 350 kilogrammes. Amazonian manatees favour calm, shallow waters that are above 23°C. This species is found in fresh water in the Amazon Basin in Brazil, as well as in Colombia, Ecuador and Peru.</p><p>All three manatee species are endangered or at a heightened risk of extinction. The African manatee and Amazonian manatee are both listed as Vulnerable by the International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN). It is estimated that 140,000. Amazonian manatees were killed between 1935 and 1954 for their meat, fat and skin, with the latter used to make leather. In more recent years, African manatee decline has been tied to incidental capture in fishing nets and hunting. Manatee hunting is now illegal in every country the African species is found in.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"891f7f0d-8d0b-427f-bd2c-783269113a1a\" data-question=\"11\">The two subspecies of West Indian manatee<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> are listed as Endangered by the IUCN. Both are also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a230541e-c7ff-4bce-85ae-6f04c4292afd\" data-question=\"11\">expected to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4b3a469b-98d6-439a-917c-f9b611004476\" data-question=\"11\">undergo a decline<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of 20% <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e98d0ca-e060-4823-93f2-235fdde6bc80\" data-question=\"11\">over the next 40 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. A review of almost 1,800 cases of entanglement in fishing nets and of plastic consumption among marine mammals in US waters from 2009 to 2020 found that at least 700 cases involved manatees. The chief cause of death in Florida manatees is boat strikes. However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"224f292b-31de-4469-a1fa-278118b49b1f\" data-question=\"13\">laws in certain parts of Florida<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> now <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dfd86a95-5179-4b92-aec0-149913f2cd0e\" data-question=\"13\">limit boat speeds during winter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dfd86a95-5179-4b92-aec0-149913f2cd0e\" data-question=\"13\">allowing slow-moving manatees more time to respond<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span>.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>Manatees</strong><br><strong>Appearance</strong><br>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f0408c24-cb1e-432f-a780-cf184fff7ee6\" data-question=\"1\">look similar<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> to dugongs, but with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3c666d2f-531b-40ed-99f3-fda24ebb5f6e\" data-question=\"1\">a differently shaped<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> (1) ..................<br><strong>Movement</strong><br>● have fewer neck bones than most mammals<br>● need to use their (2) .................. to help to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3577f310-0310-4ed3-aa23-2fdf25b7c914\" data-question=\"2\">turn their bodies around<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in order to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"6c587133-888b-4ec9-914f-79d8d00eabaa\" data-question=\"2\">look sideways<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span><br>● sense vibrations in the water by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8915c1c5-bbc6-4c73-a512-973f7f4912d5\" data-question=\"3\">means of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> (3) .................. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"05b79f65-15ed-4ba0-978e-7146ecff6c2e\" data-question=\"3\">on their skin<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span><br><strong>Feeding</strong><br>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c5cfa663-3c96-4698-8687-9bad61313ef8\" data-question=\"4\">eat mainly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b0405504-8b5d-4631-ab0f-54a150e4408d\" data-question=\"4\">aquatic vegetation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, such as (4) ..................<br>● grasp and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cd85afea-7183-4e5b-8268-71d8cf2e5750\" data-question=\"5\">pull up plants<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> with their (5) ..................<br><strong>Breathing</strong><br>● come to the surface for air every 2-4 minutes when awake and every 15-20 while sleeping<br>● may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b78bbbb9-545d-4934-9610-45e9383fa900\" data-question=\"6\">regulate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> the (6) .................. of their bodies by using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d80ea223-f4f5-4445-95db-71fd4b0da9e9\" data-question=\"6\">muscles of diaphragm to store air internally<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222994\" id=\"question-wrapper-222994\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TAIL</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222995\" id=\"question-wrapper-222995\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FLIPPERS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222996\" id=\"question-wrapper-222996\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">HAIRS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222997\" id=\"question-wrapper-222997\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SEAGRASSES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222998\" id=\"question-wrapper-222998\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LIPS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"222999\" id=\"question-wrapper-222999\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BUOYANCY</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</span></p><p><span>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information</span></p><p><span>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information</span></p><p><span>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on thi</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223000\" id=\"question-wrapper-223000\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> West Indian manatees <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86fdf386-c90e-4ce8-ae0b-91bda798d24c\" data-question=\"7\">can be found in<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"00ff8f04-5c78-4f09-a87b-121cb06ff706\" data-question=\"7\">a variety of different aquatic habitats<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223001\" id=\"question-wrapper-223001\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The Florida manatee lives in warmer waters than the Antillean manatee. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223002\" id=\"question-wrapper-223002\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The African manatee's range is <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"ca06f865-f15d-4069-ba20-ec954874d355\" data-question=\"9\">limited to coastal waters between the West African countries of Mauritania and Angola<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223003\" id=\"question-wrapper-223003\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The extent of the loss of Amazonian manatees in the mid-twentieth century was only revealed many years later. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223004\" id=\"question-wrapper-223004\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a230541e-c7ff-4bce-85ae-6f04c4292afd\" data-question=\"11\">predicted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"891f7f0d-8d0b-427f-bd2c-783269113a1a\" data-question=\"11\">West Indian manatee populations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> will fall <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5e98d0ca-e060-4823-93f2-235fdde6bc80\" data-question=\"11\">in the coming decades<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223005\" id=\"question-wrapper-223005\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The risk to manatees from entanglement and plastic consumption increased significantly in the period 2009-2020. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223006\" id=\"question-wrapper-223006\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> There is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"224f292b-31de-4469-a1fa-278118b49b1f\" data-question=\"13\">some legislation in place<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dfd86a95-5179-4b92-aec0-149913f2cd0e\" data-question=\"13\">aims to reduce the likelihood of boat strikes on manatees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q13</span></span> in Florida. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"f0408c24-cb1e-432f-a780-cf184fff7ee6","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"look similar","passagePhrase":"look quite alike"},{"uid":"3c666d2f-531b-40ed-99f3-fda24ebb5f6e","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"a differently shaped","passagePhrase":"the manatee has a broad, rounded tail ... the dugong's is fluked, like that of a whale."},{"uid":"6c587133-888b-4ec9-914f-79d8d00eabaa","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"look sideways","passagePhrase":"see something on its left or its right"},{"uid":"3577f310-0310-4ed3-aa23-2fdf25b7c914","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"turn their bodies around","passagePhrase":"turn its entire body"},{"uid":"8915c1c5-bbc6-4c73-a512-973f7f4912d5","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"means of","passagePhrase":"some hairs"},{"uid":"05b79f65-15ed-4ba0-978e-7146ecff6c2e","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"on their skin","passagePhrase":"covering their bodies"},{"uid":"b0405504-8b5d-4631-ab0f-54a150e4408d","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"aquatic vegetation","passagePhrase":"marine plants"},{"uid":"c5cfa663-3c96-4698-8687-9bad61313ef8","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"eat mainly","passagePhrase":"make up most of a manatee's diet"},{"uid":"cd85afea-7183-4e5b-8268-71d8cf2e5750","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"pull up plants","passagePhrase":"tear food away from the seafloor"},{"uid":"d80ea223-f4f5-4445-95db-71fd4b0da9e9","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"muscles of diaphragm to store air internally","passagePhrase":"muscular diaphragm and breathing"},{"uid":"b78bbbb9-545d-4934-9610-45e9383fa900","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"regulate","passagePhrase":"adjust"},{"uid":"86fdf386-c90e-4ce8-ae0b-91bda798d24c","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"can be found in","passagePhrase":"moves between ... taking advantage of"},{"uid":"00ff8f04-5c78-4f09-a87b-121cb06ff706","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"a variety of different aquatic habitats","passagePhrase":"coastal mangroves and coral reefs, rivers, lakes and inland lagoons"},{"uid":"891f7f0d-8d0b-427f-bd2c-783269113a1a","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"West Indian manatee populations","passagePhrase":"The two subspecies of West Indian manatee"},{"uid":"a230541e-c7ff-4bce-85ae-6f04c4292afd","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"predicted","passagePhrase":"expected to"},{"uid":"4b3a469b-98d6-439a-917c-f9b611004476","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"undergo a decline"},{"uid":"5e98d0ca-e060-4823-93f2-235fdde6bc80","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"in the coming decades","passagePhrase":"over the next 40 years"},{"uid":"224f292b-31de-4469-a1fa-278118b49b1f","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"some legislation in place","passagePhrase":"laws in certain parts of Florida"},{"uid":"dfd86a95-5179-4b92-aec0-149913f2cd0e","qNum":"13","questionPhrase":"aims to reduce the likelihood of boat strikes on manatees","passagePhrase":"limit boat speeds during winter ... allowing slow-moving manatees more time to respond"}]},"reading_u2_311":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Procrastination</strong></p><p>A psychologist explains why we put off important tasks and how we can break this habit</p><p>A. Procrastination is the habit of delaying a necessary task, usually by focusing on less urgent, more enjoyable, and easier activities instead. We all do it from time to time. We might be composing a message to a friend who we have to let down, or putting together an important report for college or work; we're doing our best to avoid doing the job at hand, but deep down we know that we should just be getting on with it. Unfortunately, berating ourselves won't stop us procrastinating again. In fact, it's one of the worst things we can do. This matters because, as my research shows, procrastination doesn't just waste time, but is actually linked to other problems, too.</p><p>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0700b492-aa68-492a-b086-bc9f1c579a2c\" data-question=\"14\">Contrary to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9de109d-8664-4aa1-9ae9-5d0ebda66665\" data-question=\"17\">popular belief<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, procrastination is not <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"022579d5-1df4-4d9b-81eb-034571548ebd\" data-question=\"17\">due to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> laziness or poor time management.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> Scientific studies suggest procrastination is, in fact, caused by poor mood management. This makes sense if we consider that people are more likely to put off starting or completing tasks that they are really not keen to do. If just thinking about the task <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4f3d4d9a-4762-4831-9162-d38444072a58\" data-question=\"18\">threatens our sense of self-worth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d848464-cef9-457d-ac1e-4478933c3fb9\" data-question=\"18\">makes us anxious<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>, we will be more likely to put it off. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86d33578-f15a-4711-bedf-b1a735d615be\" data-question=\"16\">Research involving brain imaging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> has found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2bacb742-dfa4-4261-9fa4-73d83215cd27\" data-question=\"16\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d5f2e9f-a26c-4440-b64a-b772b93763e8\" data-question=\"19\">areas of the brain linked to detection of threats and emotion regulation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> are actually different in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9b995e8-da88-4377-be4d-b8cf15f9259d\" data-question=\"19\">people who chronically procrastinate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> compared to those who don't procrastinate frequently.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></p><p>C. Tasks that are emotionally loaded or difficult, such as <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"99dae9e4-066f-4d33-9ad6-e35b7a4261bb\" data-question=\"20\">preparing for exams<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, are prime candidates for procrastination. People with low self-esteem are more likely to procrastinate. Another group of people who <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f274bf8e-a761-4c04-ba95-be45838a0951\" data-question=\"21\">tend to procrastinate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> are perfectionists, who worry their work will be judged harshly by others. We know that if we don't finish that report or complete those home repairs, then what we did can't be evaluated. When we avoid such tasks, we also avoid the negative emotions associated with them. This is rewarding, and it conditions us to use procrastination to repair our mood. If we engage in more enjoyable tasks instead, we get another mood boost. In the long run, however, procrastination isn't an effective way of managing emotions. The 'mood repair' we experience is temporary. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd512ee2-c47a-454d-a426-50d5fd3ae363\" data-question=\"22\">Afterwards<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, people tend to be left with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d1dc98a-746e-4140-9ebe-f9b1229b0890\" data-question=\"22\">a sense of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> guilt that not only <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc606571-a608-4b3c-b097-15d57d27e52a\" data-question=\"22\">increases their negative mood<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, but also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc606571-a608-4b3c-b097-15d57d27e52a\" data-question=\"22\">reinforces their tendency to procrastinate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</p><p>D. So why is this such a problem? When most people think of the costs of procrastination, they think of the toll on productivity. For example, studies have shown that procrastination negatively impacts on student performance. But putting off reading textbooks and writing essays may affect other areas of students' lives. In one study of over 3,000 German students over a six-month period, those who study-related misconduct, such as cheating and plagiarism. But the behaviour that procrastination was most closely linked with was using fraudulent excuses to get deadline extensions. Other research shows that employees on average spend almost a quarter of their workday procrastinating, and again this is linked with negative outcomes. In fact, in one US survey of over 22,000 employees, participants who said they regularly procrastinated <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d032539e-4fe9-4ff9-ac1d-94b0a370fb83\" data-question=\"23\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"459deed9-9402-4ca1-9e5f-4955c626b7ae\" data-question=\"24\">had less annual income<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9801a91e-ce11-4ce6-b91a-c396c3aaf03b\" data-question=\"23\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ca58963-9249-4272-8971-3004c6f0142e\" data-question=\"24\">less employment stability<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. For every one-point increase on a measure of chronic procrastination, annual income decreased by US$15,000.</p><p>E. Procrastination also correlates with serious health and well-being problems. A tendency to procrastinate is linked to poor mental health, including higher levels of depression and anxiety. Across numerous studies, I've found people who regularly procrastinate report a greater number of health issues, such as headaches, flu and colds, and digestive issues. They also experience higher levels of stress and poor sleep quality. They are less likely to practise healthy behaviours, such as eating a healthy diet and regularly exercising, and use destructive coping strategies to manage their stress. In one study of over 700 people, I found people prone to procrastination had a 63% greater risk of poor heart health after accounting for other personality traits and demographics.</p><p>F. Finding better ways of managing our emotions is one route <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f16f4b0c-5745-4860-b671-79aca0e195b9\" data-question=\"25\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f1d18a13-e54e-4af3-b91e-2bc1c8da9ca8\" data-question=\"26\">out of the vicious cycle of procrastination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. An important first step is to manage our environment and how we view the task. There are a number of evidence-based strategies that can help us <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf0a3564-4e5f-4505-9b41-29d7e13a102a\" data-question=\"25\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"341ef209-2ec7-4701-83c2-9113aa0da608\" data-question=\"26\">fend off distractions that can occupy our minds when we should be focusing on the thing we should be getting on with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. For example, reminding ourselves about why the task is important and valuable can increase positive feelings towards it. Forgiving ourselves and feeling compassion when we procrastinate can help break the procrastination cycle. We should admit that we feel bad, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0bd89aa3-fd79-4ad8-a76b-2ce7d63b8dd4\" data-question=\"25\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b79b99ff-1d25-4cd1-9855-11a1fbd60bed\" data-question=\"26\">not be overly critical of ourselves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. We should remind ourselves that we're not the first person to procrastinate, nor the last. Doing this can take the edge off the negative feelings we have about ourselves when we procrastinate. This can all make it easier to get back on track.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information? NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223007\" id=\"question-wrapper-223007\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Mention of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0700b492-aa68-492a-b086-bc9f1c579a2c\" data-question=\"14\">false assumptions about why people procrastinate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223008\" id=\"question-wrapper-223008\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Reference to the realisation that others also procrastinate </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223009\" id=\"question-wrapper-223009\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86d33578-f15a-4711-bedf-b1a735d615be\" data-question=\"16\">Neurological evidence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2bacb742-dfa4-4261-9fa4-73d83215cd27\" data-question=\"16\">a link between procrastination and emotion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>What makes us procrastinate?</strong></p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9de109d-8664-4aa1-9ae9-5d0ebda66665\" data-question=\"17\">Many people think that<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> procrastination is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"022579d5-1df4-4d9b-81eb-034571548ebd\" data-question=\"17\">the result of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> (17) ..................... Others believe it to be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"022579d5-1df4-4d9b-81eb-034571548ebd\" data-question=\"17\">the result of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> an inability to organise time efficiently.</p><p>But scientific studies suggest that procrastination is actually due to poor mood management. The tasks we are most likely to put off are those that could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4f3d4d9a-4762-4831-9162-d38444072a58\" data-question=\"18\">damage our self-esteem<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> or <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d848464-cef9-457d-ac1e-4478933c3fb9\" data-question=\"18\">cause us to feel<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> (18) ..................... when we think about them. Research comparing <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a9b995e8-da88-4377-be4d-b8cf15f9259d\" data-question=\"19\">chronic procrastinators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> with other people even found differences in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7d5f2e9f-a26c-4440-b64a-b772b93763e8\" data-question=\"19\">the brain regions associated with regulating emotions and identifying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> (19) .....................</p><p>Emotionally loaded and difficult tasks often cause us to procrastinate. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"99dae9e4-066f-4d33-9ad6-e35b7a4261bb\" data-question=\"20\">Getting ready to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> take (20) ..................... <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"540bd920-d6e9-49fe-b221-dfe2f931aca2\" data-question=\"20\">might be a typical example<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> of one such task.</p><p>People who are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f274bf8e-a761-4c04-ba95-be45838a0951\" data-question=\"21\">likely to procrastinate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> tend to be either (21) ..................... or those with low self-esteem.</p><p>Procrastination is only a short-term measure for managing emotions. It's often <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd512ee2-c47a-454d-a426-50d5fd3ae363\" data-question=\"22\">followed by<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3d1dc98a-746e-4140-9ebe-f9b1229b0890\" data-question=\"22\">a feeling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> (22) ....................., which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bc606571-a608-4b3c-b097-15d57d27e52a\" data-question=\"22\">worsens our mood and leads to procrastination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223010\" id=\"question-wrapper-223010\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LAZINESS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223011\" id=\"question-wrapper-223011\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">ANXIOUS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223012\" id=\"question-wrapper-223012\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">THREATS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223013\" id=\"question-wrapper-223013\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">EXAMS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223014\" id=\"question-wrapper-223014\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PERFECTIONISTS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223015\" id=\"question-wrapper-223015\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">GUILT</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.<br>Which TWO comparisons between employees who often procrastinate and those who do not are mentioned in the text?<br>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d032539e-4fe9-4ff9-ac1d-94b0a370fb83\" data-question=\"23\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"459deed9-9402-4ca1-9e5f-4955c626b7ae\" data-question=\"24\">Their salaries are lower<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.<br>B. The quality of their work is inferior.<br>C. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9801a91e-ce11-4ce6-b91a-c396c3aaf03b\" data-question=\"23\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ca58963-9249-4272-8971-3004c6f0142e\" data-question=\"24\">don't keep their jobs for as long<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.<br>D. They don't enjoy their working lives as much.<br>E. They have poorer relationships with colleagues.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223016\" id=\"question-wrapper-223016\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223017\" id=\"question-wrapper-223017\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.<br>Which TWO recommendations for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f16f4b0c-5745-4860-b671-79aca0e195b9\" data-question=\"25\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f1d18a13-e54e-4af3-b91e-2bc1c8da9ca8\" data-question=\"26\">getting out of a cycle of procrastination<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> does the writer give?<br>A. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0bd89aa3-fd79-4ad8-a76b-2ce7d63b8dd4\" data-question=\"25\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b79b99ff-1d25-4cd1-9855-11a1fbd60bed\" data-question=\"26\">Not judging ourselves harshly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.<br>B. Setting ourselves manageable aims.<br>C. Rewarding ourselves for tasks achieved.<br>D. Prioritising tasks according to their importance.<br>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cf0a3564-4e5f-4505-9b41-29d7e13a102a\" data-question=\"25\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"341ef209-2ec7-4701-83c2-9113aa0da608\" data-question=\"26\">Avoiding things that stop us concentrating on our tasks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223018\" id=\"question-wrapper-223018\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223019\" id=\"question-wrapper-223019\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A/E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0700b492-aa68-492a-b086-bc9f1c579a2c","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"false assumptions about why people procrastinate","passagePhrase":"Contrary to popular belief, procrastination is not due to laziness or poor time management."},{"uid":"f9de109d-8664-4aa1-9ae9-5d0ebda66665","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"Many people think that","passagePhrase":"popular belief"},{"uid":"022579d5-1df4-4d9b-81eb-034571548ebd","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"the result of ... the result of","passagePhrase":"due to"},{"uid":"4f3d4d9a-4762-4831-9162-d38444072a58","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"damage our self-esteem","passagePhrase":"threatens our sense of self-worth"},{"uid":"7d848464-cef9-457d-ac1e-4478933c3fb9","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"cause us to feel","passagePhrase":"makes us anxious"},{"uid":"86d33578-f15a-4711-bedf-b1a735d615be","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Neurological evidence","passagePhrase":"Research involving brain imaging"},{"uid":"2bacb742-dfa4-4261-9fa4-73d83215cd27","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"a link between procrastination and emotion","passagePhrase":"areas of the brain linked to detection of threats and emotion regulation are actually different in people who chronically procrastinate compared to those who don't procrastinate frequently."},{"uid":"7d5f2e9f-a26c-4440-b64a-b772b93763e8","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"the brain regions associated with regulating emotions and identifying","passagePhrase":"areas of the brain linked to detection of threats and emotion regulation"},{"uid":"a9b995e8-da88-4377-be4d-b8cf15f9259d","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"chronic procrastinators","passagePhrase":"people who chronically procrastinate"},{"uid":"99dae9e4-066f-4d33-9ad6-e35b7a4261bb","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Getting ready to","passagePhrase":"preparing for exams"},{"uid":"f274bf8e-a761-4c04-ba95-be45838a0951","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"likely to procrastinate","passagePhrase":"tend to procrastinate"},{"uid":"bd512ee2-c47a-454d-a426-50d5fd3ae363","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"followed by","passagePhrase":"Afterwards"},{"uid":"3d1dc98a-746e-4140-9ebe-f9b1229b0890","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"a feeling","passagePhrase":"a sense of"},{"uid":"bc606571-a608-4b3c-b097-15d57d27e52a","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"worsens our mood and leads to procrastination","passagePhrase":"increases their negative mood ... reinforces their tendency to procrastinate"},{"uid":"d032539e-4fe9-4ff9-ac1d-94b0a370fb83","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"Their salaries are lower","passagePhrase":"had less annual income"},{"uid":"459deed9-9402-4ca1-9e5f-4955c626b7ae","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Their salaries are lower","passagePhrase":"had less annual income"},{"uid":"9801a91e-ce11-4ce6-b91a-c396c3aaf03b","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"don't keep their jobs for as long","passagePhrase":"less employment stability"},{"uid":"3ca58963-9249-4272-8971-3004c6f0142e","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"don't keep their jobs for as long","passagePhrase":"less employment stability"},{"uid":"f16f4b0c-5745-4860-b671-79aca0e195b9","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"getting out of a cycle of procrastination","passagePhrase":"out of the vicious cycle of procrastination"},{"uid":"f1d18a13-e54e-4af3-b91e-2bc1c8da9ca8","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"getting out of a cycle of procrastination","passagePhrase":"out of the vicious cycle of procrastination"},{"uid":"cf0a3564-4e5f-4505-9b41-29d7e13a102a","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"Avoiding things that stop us concentrating on our tasks","passagePhrase":"fend off distractions that can occupy our minds when we should be focusing on the thing we should be getting on with"},{"uid":"341ef209-2ec7-4701-83c2-9113aa0da608","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Avoiding things that stop us concentrating on our tasks","passagePhrase":"fend off distractions that can occupy our minds when we should be focusing on the thing we should be getting on with"},{"uid":"0bd89aa3-fd79-4ad8-a76b-2ce7d63b8dd4","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"Not judging ourselves harshly","passagePhrase":"not be overly critical of ourselves"},{"uid":"b79b99ff-1d25-4cd1-9855-11a1fbd60bed","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Not judging ourselves harshly","passagePhrase":"not be overly critical of ourselves"},{"uid":"540bd920-d6e9-49fe-b221-dfe2f931aca2","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"might be a typical example","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_312":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Invasion of the Robot Umpires</strong></p><p>A few years ago, Fred DeJesus from Brooklyn, New York became the first umpire in a minor league baseball game to use something called the Automated Ball-Strike System (ABS), often referred to as the 'robo-umpire'. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d3312c9d-ce2b-40e0-bc5d-3806ab997295\" data-question=\"27\">Instead of making any judgments himself about a strike<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>*, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d3312c9d-ce2b-40e0-bc5d-3806ab997295\" data-question=\"27\">DeJesus had decisions fed to him through an earpiece<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, connected to a modified missile-tracking system. The contraption looked like a large black pizza box with one glowing green eye; it was mounted above the press stand.</p><p>Major League Baseball (MLB), who had commissioned the system, wanted human umpires to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"848d2fc0-6a38-46e0-ada2-49b0689d4c17\" data-question=\"33\">announce the calls<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>, just <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96322e79-07c2-43de-bfe6-39ff07eac7a5\" data-question=\"33\">as they would have done in the past<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. When the first pitch came in, a recorded voice told DeJesus it was a strike. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"042ae5be-471d-42f3-a17f-90fe8e94d401\" data-question=\"34\">Previously<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, calling a strike was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1d91b73-0553-4c1e-b37d-03bc0c2e1fc1\" data-question=\"34\">a judgment call on the part of the umpire<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. Even if the batter does not hit the ball, a pitch that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be327bc0-39b5-4536-bb25-e2525e5501dc\" data-question=\"35\">passes through<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> the 'strike zone' (<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea17be0f-0934-4fbf-bd3b-a0a263b3ef3d\" data-question=\"35\">an imaginary zone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> about seventeen inches wide, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62076dea-b65a-4f46-97eb-99e50309f8e5\" data-question=\"35\">stretching<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> from the batter's knees to the middle of his chest) is considered a strike. During that first game, when DeJesus announced calls, there was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dcd74b97-419a-4901-9895-7506b7742aef\" data-question=\"37\">no heckling and no shouted disagreement<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dcd74b97-419a-4901-9895-7506b7742aef\" data-question=\"37\">Nobody said a word<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>.</p><p>For a hundred and fifty years or so, the strike zone has been the game's animating force - <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ed0d738-1fd4-4776-9aed-ce615bfe5118\" data-question=\"36\">countless arguments<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> between a team's manager and the umpire have taken place over its boundaries and whether a ball had crossed through it. The rules of play have evolved in various stages. Today, everyone knows that you may scream your disagreement in an umpire's face, but you must never shout personal abuse at them or touch them. That's a no-no. When the robo-umpires came, however, the arguments stopped.</p><p>During the first robo-umpire season, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1075bf82-8fd7-4def-b647-58054688db0b\" data-question=\"28\">players complained<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> about some strange calls. In response, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3809a40-5c03-4f40-810c-1bbb90a6353f\" data-question=\"28\">MLB decided to tweak the dimensions of the zone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, and the following year the consensus was that ABS is profoundly consistent. MLB says the device is near-perfect, precise to within fractions of an inch. \"It'll reduce controversy in the game, and be good for the game,\" says Rob Manfred, who is Commissioner for MLB. But the question is whether controversy is worth reducing, or whether it is the sign of a human hand. </p><p>A human, at least, yells back. When I spoke with Frank Viola, a coach for Carolina team, he said that ABS works as designed, but that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6103250-3f4c-4954-96d3-8f74bca7ecf2\" data-question=\"38\">it was also unforgiving and pedantic, almost legalistic<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. \"Manfred is a lawyer,\" Viola noted. Some pitchers have complained that, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6103250-3f4c-4954-96d3-8f74bca7ecf2\" data-question=\"38\">compared with a human's, the robot's strike zone seems too precise<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. Viola was once a major-league player himself. When he was pitching, he explained, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6103250-3f4c-4954-96d3-8f74bca7ecf2\" data-question=\"38\">umpires rewarded skill<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>. \"Throw it where you aimed, and it would be a strike, even if it was an inch or two outside. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6103250-3f4c-4954-96d3-8f74bca7ecf2\" data-question=\"38\">There was a dialogue between pitcher and umpire.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>\"</p><p>The executive tasked with running the experiment for MLB is Morgan Sword, who's in charge of baseball operations. According to Sword, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3bb227a-d790-4e37-821a-061a67ca82a1\" data-question=\"39\">ABS was part of a larger project to make baseball more exciting since executives are terrified of losing younger fans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>, as has been the case with horse racing and boxing. He explains how they began the process by asking fans what version of baseball they found most exciting. The results showed that everyone wanted more action: more hits, more defense, more baserunning. This type of baseball essentially hasn't existed since the 1960s, when the hundred-mile-an-hour fastball, which is difficult to hit and control, entered the game. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"233d882c-f121-4751-b4ca-c072718421c6\" data-question=\"30\">It flattened the game into strikeouts, walks, and home runs - a type of play lacking much action.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></p><p>Sword's team brainstormed potential fixes. Any rule that existed, they talked about changing - from changing the bats to changing the geometry of the field. But while all of these were ruled out as potential fixes, ABS was seen as a perfect vehicle for change. According to Sword, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5480ed4f-e8d0-4c22-ab95-2f835caa82ca\" data-question=\"32\">once you get the technology right, you can load any strike zone you want into the system. \"It might be a triangle, or a blob, or something shaped like Texas.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> Over time, as baseball evolves, ABS can allow the zone to change with it.\"</p><p>\"In the past twenty years, sports have moved away from judgment calls. Soccer has Video Assistant Referees (for offside decisions, for example). Tennis has Hawk-Eye (for line calls, for example). For almost a decade, baseball has used instant replay on the base paths. This is widely liked, even if the precision can sometimes cause problems. But these applications deal with something physical: bases, lines, goals. The boundaries of action are precise, delineated like the keys of a piano. This is not the case with ABS and the strike zone. Historically, a certain discretion has been appreciated.”</p><p>I decided to email Alva Noë, a professor at Berkeley University and a baseball fan, for his opinion. \"Hardly a day goes by that I don't wake up and run through the reasons that this [robo-umpires] is such a terrible idea,\" he replied. He later told me, \"<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9641d610-d2c8-43d4-ab7a-5207c1b80fce\" data-question=\"40\">This is part of a movement to use algorithms to take the hard choices of living out of life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.\" Perhaps he's right. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9641d610-d2c8-43d4-ab7a-5207c1b80fce\" data-question=\"40\">We watch baseball to kill time, not to maximize it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Some players I have met take a dissenting stance toward the robots too, believing that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9641d610-d2c8-43d4-ab7a-5207c1b80fce\" data-question=\"40\">accuracy is not the answer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. According to Joe Russo, who plays for a New Jersey team, \"With technology, people just want everything to be perfect. That's not reality. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9641d610-d2c8-43d4-ab7a-5207c1b80fce\" data-question=\"40\">I think perfect would be weird. Your teams are always winning, work is always just great, there's always money in your pocket, your car never breaks down. What is there to talk about?<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>\"<br>___________________________________<br><em>*strike: a strike is when the batter swings at a ball and misses or when the batter does not swing at a ball that passes through the strike zone.</em></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?<br>YES if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br>NO if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br>NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223020\" id=\"question-wrapper-223020\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When DeJesus first used ABS, he <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d3312c9d-ce2b-40e0-bc5d-3806ab997295\" data-question=\"27\">shared decision-making about strikes with it<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223021\" id=\"question-wrapper-223021\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a3809a40-5c03-4f40-810c-1bbb90a6353f\" data-question=\"28\">MLB considered it necessary to amend the size of the strike zone<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> when <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1075bf82-8fd7-4def-b647-58054688db0b\" data-question=\"28\">criticisms were received from players<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223022\" id=\"question-wrapper-223022\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> MLB is keen to justify the money spent on improving the accuracy of ABS's calculations. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223023\" id=\"question-wrapper-223023\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The hundred-mile-an-hour fastball <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"233d882c-f121-4751-b4ca-c072718421c6\" data-question=\"30\">led to a more exciting style of play<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NO</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223024\" id=\"question-wrapper-223024\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The differing proposals for alterations to the baseball bat led to fierce debate on Sword's team. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223025\" id=\"question-wrapper-223025\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5480ed4f-e8d0-4c22-ab95-2f835caa82ca\" data-question=\"32\">ABS makes changes to the shape of the strike zone feasible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">YES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span>Complete the summary using the list of phrases, A-H, below.</span></p><p><span>A. pitch boundary </span></p><p><span>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ed0d738-1fd4-4776-9aed-ce615bfe5118\" data-question=\"36\">numerous disputes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> </span></p><p><span>C. team tactics</span></p><p><span>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a1d91b73-0553-4c1e-b37d-03bc0c2e1fc1\" data-question=\"34\">subjective assessment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> </span></p><p><span>E. widespread approval </span></p><p><span>F. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"96322e79-07c2-43de-bfe6-39ff07eac7a5\" data-question=\"33\">former roles<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span></span></p><p><span>G. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dcd74b97-419a-4901-9895-7506b7742aef\" data-question=\"37\">total silence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> </span></p><p><span>H. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ea17be0f-0934-4fbf-bd3b-a0a263b3ef3d\" data-question=\"35\">perceived area<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span></span></p><p> </p><p><span><strong>Calls by the umpire</strong></span></p><p><span>Even after ABS was developed, MLB still wanted human umpires to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"848d2fc0-6a38-46e0-ada2-49b0689d4c17\" data-question=\"33\">shout out decisions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> as they had in their (33) ................... The umpire's job had, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"042ae5be-471d-42f3-a17f-90fe8e94d401\" data-question=\"34\">at one time<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, required a (34) ................... about whether a ball was a strike. A ball is considered a strike when the batter does not hit it and it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be327bc0-39b5-4536-bb25-e2525e5501dc\" data-question=\"35\">crosses through<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> a (35) ................... <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62076dea-b65a-4f46-97eb-99e50309f8e5\" data-question=\"35\">extending<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> approximately from the batter's knee to his chest. </span></p><p><span>In the past, (36) ................... over strike calls were not uncommon, but today everyone accepts the complete ban on pushing or shoving the umpire. One difference, however, is that during the first game DeJesus used ABS, strike calls were met with (37) ...................</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223026\" id=\"question-wrapper-223026\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223027\" id=\"question-wrapper-223027\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223028\" id=\"question-wrapper-223028\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">H</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223029\" id=\"question-wrapper-223029\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223030\" id=\"question-wrapper-223030\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p><span>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.</span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223031\" id=\"question-wrapper-223031\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does the writer suggest about ABS in the fifth paragraph? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It is bound to make key decisions that are wrong.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a6103250-3f4c-4954-96d3-8f74bca7ecf2\" data-question=\"38\">It may reduce some of the appeal of the game<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li> <li>C. It will lead to the disappearance of human umpires.</li> <li>D. It may increase calls for the rules of baseball to be changed.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223032\" id=\"question-wrapper-223032\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Morgan Sword says that the introduction of ABS </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Was regarded as an experiment without a guaranteed outcome.</li> <li>B. Was intended to keep up with developments in other sports.</li> <li>C. Was a response to changing attitudes about the role of sport.</li> <li>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3bb227a-d790-4e37-821a-061a67ca82a1\" data-question=\"39\">Was an attempt to ensure baseball retained a young audience<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223033\" id=\"question-wrapper-223033\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Why does the writer include the views of Noë and Russo? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. To show that attitudes to technology vary widely.</li> <li>B. To argue that people have unrealistic expectations of sport.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9641d610-d2c8-43d4-ab7a-5207c1b80fce\" data-question=\"40\">To indicate that accuracy is not the same thing as enjoyment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> <li>D. To suggest that the number of baseball fans needs to increase.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"848d2fc0-6a38-46e0-ada2-49b0689d4c17","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"shout out decisions","passagePhrase":"announce the calls"},{"uid":"96322e79-07c2-43de-bfe6-39ff07eac7a5","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"former roles","passagePhrase":"as they would have done in the past"},{"uid":"042ae5be-471d-42f3-a17f-90fe8e94d401","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"at one time","passagePhrase":"Previously"},{"uid":"a1d91b73-0553-4c1e-b37d-03bc0c2e1fc1","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"subjective assessment","passagePhrase":"a judgment call on the part of the umpire"},{"uid":"be327bc0-39b5-4536-bb25-e2525e5501dc","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"crosses through","passagePhrase":"passes through"},{"uid":"ea17be0f-0934-4fbf-bd3b-a0a263b3ef3d","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"perceived area","passagePhrase":"an imaginary zone"},{"uid":"62076dea-b65a-4f46-97eb-99e50309f8e5","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"extending","passagePhrase":"stretching"},{"uid":"dcd74b97-419a-4901-9895-7506b7742aef","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"total silence","passagePhrase":"no heckling and no shouted disagreement ... Nobody said a word"},{"uid":"5ed0d738-1fd4-4776-9aed-ce615bfe5118","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"numerous disputes","passagePhrase":"countless arguments"},{"uid":"1075bf82-8fd7-4def-b647-58054688db0b","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"criticisms were received from players","passagePhrase":"players complained"},{"uid":"a3809a40-5c03-4f40-810c-1bbb90a6353f","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"MLB considered it necessary to amend the size of the strike zone","passagePhrase":"MLB decided to tweak the dimensions of the zone"},{"uid":"a6103250-3f4c-4954-96d3-8f74bca7ecf2","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"It may reduce some of the appeal of the game","passagePhrase":"it was also unforgiving and pedantic, almost legalistic ... compared with a human's, the robot's strike zone seems too precise ... umpires rewarded skill ... There was a dialogue between pitcher and umpire."},{"uid":"b3bb227a-d790-4e37-821a-061a67ca82a1","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"Was an attempt to ensure baseball retained a young audience","passagePhrase":"ABS was part of a larger project to make baseball more exciting since executives are terrified of losing younger fans"},{"uid":"5480ed4f-e8d0-4c22-ab95-2f835caa82ca","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"ABS makes changes to the shape of the strike zone feasible","passagePhrase":"once you get the technology right, you can load any strike zone you want into the system. \"It might be a triangle, or a blob, or something shaped like Texas."},{"uid":"9641d610-d2c8-43d4-ab7a-5207c1b80fce","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"To indicate that accuracy is not the same thing as enjoyment","passagePhrase":"This is part of a movement to use algorithms to take the hard choices of living out of life ... We watch baseball to kill time, not to maximize it ... accuracy is not the answer ... I think perfect would be weird. Your teams are always winning, work is always just great, there's always money in your pocket, your car never breaks down. What is there to talk about?"}]},"reading_u2_313":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Frozen Food</strong></p><p>A US perspective on the development of the frozen food industry</p><p>At some point in history, humans discovered that ice preserved food. There is evidence that winter ice was stored to preserve food in the summer as far back as 10,000 years ago. Two thousand years ago, the inhabitants of South America's Andean mountains had a unique means of conserving potatoes for later consumption. They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11e4b546-5401-44ea-93ce-085c8ff2e991\" data-question=\"1\">froze them overnight<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, then trampled them to squeeze out the moisture, then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11e4b546-5401-44ea-93ce-085c8ff2e991\" data-question=\"1\">dried them in the sun<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aafdac2a-9874-4915-a953-c7fc68314f1d\" data-question=\"1\">preserved their nutritional value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> - if not their aesthetic appeal.</p><p>Natural ice remained the main form of refrigeration until late in the 19th century. In the early 1800s, ship owners from Boston, USA, had enormous blocks of Arctic ice towed all over the Atlantic for the purpose of food preservation. In 1851, railroads first began <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dfe0f0e4-2281-4d4a-b8f8-d7804fc11cc0\" data-question=\"2\">putting blocks of ice in insulated rail cars to send butter<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> from Ogdensburg, New York, to Boston.</p><p>Finally, in 1870, Australian inventors found a way to make 'mechanical ice'. They used a compressor to force a gas - ammonia at first and later Freon - through a condenser. The compressed gas gave up some of its heat as it moved through the condenser. Then the gas was released quickly into a low-pressure evaporator coil where it became liquid and cold. Air was blown over the evaporator coil and then this cooled air passed into an insulated compartment, lowering its temperature to freezing point.</p><p>Initially, this process was invented to keep Australian beer cool even in hot weather. But Australian cattlemen were quick to realize that, if they could put this new invention on a ship, they could export meat across the oceans. In 1880, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de906c35-09b5-4bbf-935a-75df34d7d0e5\" data-question=\"3\">a shipment of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> Australian <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"771c8576-9603-4763-8e2d-ade45db95583\" data-question=\"3\">beef and mutton<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de906c35-09b5-4bbf-935a-75df34d7d0e5\" data-question=\"3\">was sent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span>, frozen, to England. While the food frozen this way was still palatable, there was some deterioration. During the freezing process, crystals formed within the cells of the food, and when the ice expanded and the cells burst, this <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be4098a9-ef38-43fe-ab8a-80d9853153e5\" data-question=\"9\">spoilt the flavor and texture of the food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </p><p>The modern frozen food industry began with the indigenous Inuit people of Canada. In 1912, a biology student in Massachusetts, USA, named Clarence Birdseye, ran out of money and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f667d37a-c306-434d-9829-516e3c8c3b34\" data-question=\"10\">went to Labrador in Canada to trap and trade furs.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> While he was there, he became fascinated with how the Inuit would quickly freeze fish in the Arctic air. The fish looked and tasted fresh even months later.</p><p>Birdseye returned to the USA in 1917 and began developing mechanical freezers capable of quick-freezing food. Birdseye methodically kept inventing better freezers and gradually built a business selling frozen fish from Gloucester, Massachusetts. In 1929, his business was sold and became General Foods, but he stayed with the company as director of research, and his division continued to innovate.</p><p>Birdseye was responsible for several key innovations that made the frozen food industry possible. He developed <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10012bae-9b2e-44a7-ad99-6b8a39e94e16\" data-question=\"4\">quick-freezing techniques<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eda193aa-933d-4ef3-9aaf-6f04c89c0321\" data-question=\"4\">reduced the damage that crystals caused<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, as well as the technique of freezing the product in the package it was to be sold in. He also introduced the use of cellophane, the first <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"060c677a-620e-468b-a29d-fcd24b932c92\" data-question=\"5\">transparent material<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83090c9c-fdcc-47e9-a848-3dc8c09b442d\" data-question=\"5\">food packaging<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>, which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"060c677a-620e-468b-a29d-fcd24b932c92\" data-question=\"5\">allowed consumers to see the quality of the product<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>. Birdseye products also came in convenient size packages that could be prepared with a minimum of effort.</p><p>But there were still obstacles. In the 1930s, few grocery stores could afford to buy freezers for a market that wasn't established yet. So, Birdseye leased inexpensive freezer cases to them. He also leased insulated railroad cars so that he could ship his products nationwide. However, few consumers had freezers large enough or efficient enough to take advantage of the products.</p><p>Sales increased in the early 1940s, when World War II gave a boost to the frozen food industry because tin was being used for munitions. Canned foods were rationed to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"625eb591-1e53-48a9-b6fd-1e0b679a63da\" data-question=\"6\">save tin for the war effort<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, while frozen foods were <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e34e9243-edfe-4327-99cc-8ed3b265f718\" data-question=\"6\">abundant<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> and cheap. Finally, by the 1950s, refrigerator technology had developed far enough to make these appliances affordable for the average family. By 1953, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78023eec-7b3a-4aee-bbfb-2ec46854ec72\" data-question=\"7\">33 million US families<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c089cc8d-90d8-41ac-b526-0a0ff6bad5f4\" data-question=\"7\">owned<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> a refrigerator, and manufacturers were gradually increasing the size of the freezer compartments in them. </p><p>1950s families were also looking for convenience at mealtimes, so the moment was right for the arrival of the 'TV Dinner'. Swanson Foods was a large, nationally recognized producer of canned and frozen poultry. In 1954, the company adapted some of Birdseye's freezing techniques, and with the help of a clever name and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c3ed8dfc-c892-460d-951f-4c14f2621567\" data-question=\"11\">a huge advertising budget<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, it launched the first 'TV Dinner'. This consisted of frozen turkey, potatoes and vegetables <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"df6c060e-2242-4c9a-a623-7dbb0fe31cc7\" data-question=\"12\">served in the same segmented aluminum tray that was used by airlines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span>. The product was an instant success. Within a year, Swanson had sold 13 million TV dinners. American consumers couldn't resist the combination of a trusted brand name, a single-serving package and the convenience of a meal that could be ready after only 25 minutes in a hot oven. By 1959, Americans were spending $2.7 billion annually on frozen foods, and half a billion of that was spent on ready-prepared meals such as the TV Dinner.</p><p>Today, the US frozen food industry has a turnover of over $67 billion annually, with $26.6 billion of that sold to consumers for home consumption. The remaining $40 billion in frozen food sales come through restaurants, cafeterias, hospitals and schools, and that represents a third of the total food service sales.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>The history of frozen food<br>2,000 years ago, South America</strong><br>● People <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"aafdac2a-9874-4915-a953-c7fc68314f1d\" data-question=\"1\">conserved the nutritional value<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> of (1) ......................, using a method of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11e4b546-5401-44ea-93ce-085c8ff2e991\" data-question=\"1\">freezing then drying<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>.<br><strong>1851, USA</strong><br>● (2) ...................... was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dfe0f0e4-2281-4d4a-b8f8-d7804fc11cc0\" data-question=\"2\">kept cool by ice during transportation in specially adapted trains<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span>.<br><strong>1880, Australia</strong><br>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"771c8576-9603-4763-8e2d-ade45db95583\" data-question=\"3\">Two kinds of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> (3) ...................... were the first frozen food <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"de906c35-09b5-4bbf-935a-75df34d7d0e5\" data-question=\"3\">shipped to<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> England.<br><strong>1917 onwards, USA</strong><br>● Clarence Birdseye introduced innovations including:<br>- <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"10012bae-9b2e-44a7-ad99-6b8a39e94e16\" data-question=\"4\">quick-freezing methods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, so that (4) ...................... <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"eda193aa-933d-4ef3-9aaf-6f04c89c0321\" data-question=\"4\">did not spoil the food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.<br>- <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"83090c9c-fdcc-47e9-a848-3dc8c09b442d\" data-question=\"5\">packaging products<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> with (5) ......................, so <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"060c677a-620e-468b-a29d-fcd24b932c92\" data-question=\"5\">the product was visible<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span>.<br><strong>Early 1940s, USA</strong><br>● Frozen food <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e34e9243-edfe-4327-99cc-8ed3b265f718\" data-question=\"6\">became popular<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> because of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"625eb591-1e53-48a9-b6fd-1e0b679a63da\" data-question=\"6\">a shortage of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> (6) ......................<br><strong>1950s, USA</strong><br>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"78023eec-7b3a-4aee-bbfb-2ec46854ec72\" data-question=\"7\">A large number of homes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> now had a (7) ......................</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223034\" id=\"question-wrapper-223034\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">POTATOES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223035\" id=\"question-wrapper-223035\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BUTTER</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223036\" id=\"question-wrapper-223036\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">MEAT</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223037\" id=\"question-wrapper-223037\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CRYSTALS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223038\" id=\"question-wrapper-223038\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CELLOPHANE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223039\" id=\"question-wrapper-223039\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TIN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223040\" id=\"question-wrapper-223040\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">REFRIGERATOR</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?<br>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information<br>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information<br>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223041\" id=\"question-wrapper-223041\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The ice transportation business made some Boston ship owners very wealthy in the early 1800s. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223042\" id=\"question-wrapper-223042\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A disadvantage of the freezing process invented in Australia was that it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"be4098a9-ef38-43fe-ab8a-80d9853153e5\" data-question=\"9\">affected the taste of food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223043\" id=\"question-wrapper-223043\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Clarence Birdseye <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"f667d37a-c306-434d-9829-516e3c8c3b34\" data-question=\"10\">travelled to Labrador in order to learn how the Inuit people froze fish<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223044\" id=\"question-wrapper-223044\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Swanson Foods <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c3ed8dfc-c892-460d-951f-4c14f2621567\" data-question=\"11\">invested a great deal of money in the promotion<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> of the TV Dinner. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223045\" id=\"question-wrapper-223045\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Swanson Foods <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"df6c060e-2242-4c9a-a623-7dbb0fe31cc7\" data-question=\"12\">developed a new style of container<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q12</span></span> for the launch of the TV Dinner. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223046\" id=\"question-wrapper-223046\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The US frozen food industry is currently the largest in the world. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"11e4b546-5401-44ea-93ce-085c8ff2e991","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"freezing then drying","passagePhrase":"froze them overnight ... dried them in the sun"},{"uid":"aafdac2a-9874-4915-a953-c7fc68314f1d","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"conserved the nutritional value","passagePhrase":"preserved their nutritional value"},{"uid":"dfe0f0e4-2281-4d4a-b8f8-d7804fc11cc0","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"kept cool by ice during transportation in specially adapted trains","passagePhrase":"putting blocks of ice in insulated rail cars to send butter"},{"uid":"de906c35-09b5-4bbf-935a-75df34d7d0e5","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"shipped to","passagePhrase":"a shipment of ... was sent"},{"uid":"771c8576-9603-4763-8e2d-ade45db95583","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"Two kinds of","passagePhrase":"beef and mutton"},{"uid":"be4098a9-ef38-43fe-ab8a-80d9853153e5","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"affected the taste of food","passagePhrase":"spoilt the flavor and texture of the food"},{"uid":"10012bae-9b2e-44a7-ad99-6b8a39e94e16","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"quick-freezing methods","passagePhrase":"quick-freezing techniques"},{"uid":"eda193aa-933d-4ef3-9aaf-6f04c89c0321","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"did not spoil the food","passagePhrase":"reduced the damage that crystals caused"},{"uid":"060c677a-620e-468b-a29d-fcd24b932c92","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"the product was visible","passagePhrase":"transparent material ... allowed consumers to see the quality of the product"},{"uid":"83090c9c-fdcc-47e9-a848-3dc8c09b442d","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"packaging products","passagePhrase":"food packaging"},{"uid":"625eb591-1e53-48a9-b6fd-1e0b679a63da","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"a shortage of","passagePhrase":"save tin for the war effort"},{"uid":"e34e9243-edfe-4327-99cc-8ed3b265f718","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"became popular","passagePhrase":"abundant"},{"uid":"78023eec-7b3a-4aee-bbfb-2ec46854ec72","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"A large number of homes","passagePhrase":"33 million US families"},{"uid":"c089cc8d-90d8-41ac-b526-0a0ff6bad5f4","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"owned"},{"uid":"c3ed8dfc-c892-460d-951f-4c14f2621567","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"invested a great deal of money in the promotion","passagePhrase":"a huge advertising budget"}]},"reading_u2_314":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Can the planet’s coral reefs be saved?</strong></p><p>A. Conservationists have put the final touches to a giant artificial reef they have been assembling at the world-renowned Zoological Society of London (London Zoo). Samples of the planet's most spectacular corals - vivid green branching coral, yellow scroll, blue ridge and many more species - have been added to the giant tank along with fish that thrive in their presence: blue tang, clownfish and many others. The reef is in the zoo's new gallery, Tiny Giants, which is dedicated to the minuscule invertebrate creatures that sustain life across the planet. The coral reef tank and its seven-metre-wide window form the core of the exhibition. 'Coral reefs are the most diverse ecosystems on Earth and we want to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09c17ab2-82b4-4fe4-946c-3785d60ed61c\" data-question=\"14\">show people how wonderful they are<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>,' said Paul Pearce-Kelly, senior curator of invertebrates and fish at the Zoological Society of London. 'However, we also want to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09c17ab2-82b4-4fe4-946c-3785d60ed61c\" data-question=\"14\">highlight the research and conservation efforts that are now being carried out to try to save them from the threat of global warming<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>.' They <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09c17ab2-82b4-4fe4-946c-3785d60ed61c\" data-question=\"14\">want people to see what is being done to try to save these wonders.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span></p><p>B. Corals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"85cccbf2-318e-45b6-90e4-3d1e55dc9ac3\" data-question=\"24\">are composed of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> tiny animals, known as polyps, with tentacles for <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a642d1c-7ce9-4caa-bb05-72e0b83ce208\" data-question=\"24\">capturing small marine creatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in the sea water. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db02fc93-eb83-4015-83a9-4b3e2d6f9d06\" data-question=\"15\">These polyps are transparent but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ee2c539-249a-4a6e-84de-ece5efe4c281\" data-question=\"25\">get<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> their brilliant tones of pink, orange, blue, green, etc. from algae that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f67df54f-1c99-4047-8422-aba6225080bd\" data-question=\"25\">live within them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, which in turn <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ee2c539-249a-4a6e-84de-ece5efe4c281\" data-question=\"25\">get<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> protection, while their photosynthesising of the sun's rays provides nutrients for the polyps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. This <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db02fc93-eb83-4015-83a9-4b3e2d6f9d06\" data-question=\"15\">comfortable symbiotic relationship<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> has led to the growth of coral reefs that cover 0.1% of the planet's ocean bed while providing homes for more than 25% of marine species, including fish, molluscs, sponges and shellfish.</p><p>C. As a result, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5c3a927-94da-44f2-961c-a9a3255ea593\" data-question=\"16\">coral reefs are often described as the 'rainforests of the sea'<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, though <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5c3a927-94da-44f2-961c-a9a3255ea593\" data-question=\"16\">the comparison is dismissed by some naturalists, including David Attenborough<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. 'People say you cannot beat the rainforest,' Attenborough has stated. 'But that is simply not true. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5c3a927-94da-44f2-961c-a9a3255ea593\" data-question=\"16\">You go there and the first thing you think is: where ... are the birds? Where are the animals? They are hiding in the trees, of course<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. No, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5c3a927-94da-44f2-961c-a9a3255ea593\" data-question=\"16\">if you want beauty and wildlife, you want a coral reef. Put on a mask and stick your head under the water. The sight is mind-blowing.'<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span></p><p>D. Unfortunately, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35a9c675-8523-468b-99e7-a7cd0616c0b9\" data-question=\"17\">these majestic sights are now under very serious threat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>, with the most immediate problem coming in the form of thermal stress. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3c14601-e9bb-4a4f-bdae-e47cddcb955a\" data-question=\"26\">Rising ocean temperatures<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> are triggering bleaching events that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca6cee36-746b-4a7b-95f8-1f2785cb6ec0\" data-question=\"26\">strip reefs of their colour<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> and eventually kill them. And that is just the start. Other menaces include ocean acidification, sea level increase, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d1ec059c-a70a-4b98-83e8-e6ae3d8e47d4\" data-question=\"20\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eb314b2-283b-40be-83f9-56e88638bca6\" data-question=\"21\">pollution by humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, deoxygenation and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1272d880-3bc6-4721-ae31-e1a909ebc02a\" data-question=\"20\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"122481d5-24d2-44b4-8323-a055988db804\" data-question=\"21\">ocean current changes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>, while the climate crisis is also increasing habitat destruction. As a result, vast areas - including massive chunks of Australia's Great Barrier Reef - have already been destroyed, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35a9c675-8523-468b-99e7-a7cd0616c0b9\" data-question=\"17\">scientists advise that more than 90% of reefs could be lost by 2050 unless urgent action is taken to tackle global heating and greenhouse gas emissions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>. <br>Pearce-Kelly says that coral reefs have to survive really harsh conditions wave erosion and other factors. And 'when things start to go wrong in the oceans, then corals will be the first to react. And that is exactly what we are seeing now. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35a9c675-8523-468b-99e7-a7cd0616c0b9\" data-question=\"17\">Coral reefs are dying and they are telling us that all is not well with our planet.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span>'</p><p>E. However, scientists are trying to pinpoint hardy types of coral that could survive our overheated oceans, and some of this research will be carried out at London Zoo. 'Behind our coral reef tank we have built laboratories where scientists will be studying coral species,' said Pearce-Kelly. One aim will be to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca039c9a-1cda-4074-bd3c-d4d5f06619de\" data-question=\"18\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f6342cd-1e5c-4e50-b921-63497497e4e6\" data-question=\"22\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54eff402-eaf0-4977-b599-b9c12161f09c\" data-question=\"23\">carry out research on species to find those that can survive best in warm, acidic waters<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. Another will be to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca039c9a-1cda-4074-bd3c-d4d5f06619de\" data-question=\"18\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93c1fa67-589f-4024-880e-0b51cd26569c\" data-question=\"22\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b3057ed-e9e7-4f18-b3cd-ed96973ed903\" data-question=\"23\">try to increase coral breeding rates<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. 'Coral spawn just once a year,' he added. 'However, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca039c9a-1cda-4074-bd3c-d4d5f06619de\" data-question=\"18\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93c1fa67-589f-4024-880e-0b51cd26569c\" data-question=\"22\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b3057ed-e9e7-4f18-b3cd-ed96973ed903\" data-question=\"23\">aquarium-based research has enabled some corals to spawn artificially<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, which can assist coral reef restoration efforts<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span>. And if this can be extended for all species, we could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93c1fa67-589f-4024-880e-0b51cd26569c\" data-question=\"22\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b3057ed-e9e7-4f18-b3cd-ed96973ed903\" data-question=\"23\">consider the launching of coral-spawning programmes several times a year<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca039c9a-1cda-4074-bd3c-d4d5f06619de\" data-question=\"18\">That would be a big help in restoring blighted reefs.'<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span></p><p>F. Research in these fields is being conducted in laboratories around the world, with the London Zoo centre linked to this global network. Studies carried out in one centre can then be tested in others. The resulting young coral can then be displayed in the tank in Tiny Giants. 'The crucial point is that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86f95ebf-db50-4d44-8cb6-80ac544bcc97\" data-question=\"19\">the progress we make in making coral better able to survive in a warming world can be shown to the public<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86f95ebf-db50-4d44-8cb6-80ac544bcc97\" data-question=\"19\">encourage them to believe that we can do something to save the planet's reefs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>,' said Pearce-Kelly. 'Saving our coral reefs is now a critically important ecological goal.'</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading 2 has six sections, A-F. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. Write the correct letter, i-vii, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet<br><strong>List of headings</strong><br>i. Tried and tested solutions<br>ii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"db02fc93-eb83-4015-83a9-4b3e2d6f9d06\" data-question=\"15\">Cooperation beneath the waves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span><br>iii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca039c9a-1cda-4074-bd3c-d4d5f06619de\" data-question=\"18\">Working to lessen the problems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span><br>iv. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d5c3a927-94da-44f2-961c-a9a3255ea593\" data-question=\"16\">Disagreement about the accuracy of a certain phrase<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span><br>v. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"09c17ab2-82b4-4fe4-946c-3785d60ed61c\" data-question=\"14\">Two clear educational goals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span><br>vi. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"86f95ebf-db50-4d44-8cb6-80ac544bcc97\" data-question=\"19\">Promoting hope<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span><br>vii. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"35a9c675-8523-468b-99e7-a7cd0616c0b9\" data-question=\"17\">A warning of further trouble ahead<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span></p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223047\" id=\"question-wrapper-223047\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph A </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">V</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223048\" id=\"question-wrapper-223048\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph B </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">II</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223049\" id=\"question-wrapper-223049\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph C </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">IV</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223050\" id=\"question-wrapper-223050\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph D </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VII</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223051\" id=\"question-wrapper-223051\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph E </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">III</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223052\" id=\"question-wrapper-223052\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Paragraph F </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">VI</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.<br>Which TWO of these causes of damage to coral reefs are mentioned by the writer of the text?<br>A. A rising number of extreme storms.<br>B. The removal of too many fish from the sea.<br>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d1ec059c-a70a-4b98-83e8-e6ae3d8e47d4\" data-question=\"20\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3eb314b2-283b-40be-83f9-56e88638bca6\" data-question=\"21\">The contamination of the sea from waste<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.<br>D. Increased disease among marine species.<br>E. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1272d880-3bc6-4721-ae31-e1a909ebc02a\" data-question=\"20\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"122481d5-24d2-44b4-8323-a055988db804\" data-question=\"21\">Alterations in the usual flow of water in the seas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>.<br> </p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223053\" id=\"question-wrapper-223053\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223054\" id=\"question-wrapper-223054\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C/E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose TWO letters, A-E.<br>Which TWO of the following statements are true of the researchers at London Zoo?<br>A. They are hoping to expand the numbers of different corals being bred in laboratories.<br>B. They want to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7f6342cd-1e5c-4e50-b921-63497497e4e6\" data-question=\"22\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"54eff402-eaf0-4977-b599-b9c12161f09c\" data-question=\"23\">identify corals that can cope well with the changed sea conditions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.<br>C. They are looking at ways of creating artificial reefs that corals could grow on.<br>D. They are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"93c1fa67-589f-4024-880e-0b51cd26569c\" data-question=\"22\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3b3057ed-e9e7-4f18-b3cd-ed96973ed903\" data-question=\"23\">trying out methods that would speed up reproduction in some corals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>.<br>E. They are investigating materials that might protect reefs from higher temperatures.<br> </p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223055\" id=\"question-wrapper-223055\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223056\" id=\"question-wrapper-223056\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B/D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223057\" id=\"question-wrapper-223057\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Corals <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"85cccbf2-318e-45b6-90e4-3d1e55dc9ac3\" data-question=\"24\">have<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> a number of (24) ................... which they use to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3a642d1c-7ce9-4caa-bb05-72e0b83ce208\" data-question=\"24\">collect their food<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TENTACLES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223058\" id=\"question-wrapper-223058\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Algae <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2ee2c539-249a-4a6e-84de-ece5efe4c281\" data-question=\"25\">gain<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> (25) ................... from <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f67df54f-1c99-4047-8422-aba6225080bd\" data-question=\"25\">being inside the coral<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PROTECTION</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223059\" id=\"question-wrapper-223059\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f3c14601-e9bb-4a4f-bdae-e47cddcb955a\" data-question=\"26\">Increases in the warmth of the sea water<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> can <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ca6cee36-746b-4a7b-95f8-1f2785cb6ec0\" data-question=\"26\">remove the<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span> (26) ................... from coral. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">COLO(U)R</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"09c17ab2-82b4-4fe4-946c-3785d60ed61c","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"Two clear educational goals","passagePhrase":"show people how wonderful they are ... highlight the research and conservation efforts that are now being carried out to try to save them from the threat of global warming ... want people to see what is being done to try to save these wonders."},{"uid":"85cccbf2-318e-45b6-90e4-3d1e55dc9ac3","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"have","passagePhrase":"are composed of"},{"uid":"3a642d1c-7ce9-4caa-bb05-72e0b83ce208","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"collect their food","passagePhrase":"capturing small marine creatures"},{"uid":"db02fc93-eb83-4015-83a9-4b3e2d6f9d06","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"Cooperation beneath the waves","passagePhrase":"These polyps are transparent but get their brilliant tones of pink, orange, blue, green, etc. from algae that live within them, which in turn get protection, while their photosynthesising of the sun's rays provides nutrients for the polyps ... comfortable symbiotic relationship"},{"uid":"2ee2c539-249a-4a6e-84de-ece5efe4c281","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"gain","passagePhrase":"get ... get"},{"uid":"f67df54f-1c99-4047-8422-aba6225080bd","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"being inside the coral","passagePhrase":"live within them"},{"uid":"d5c3a927-94da-44f2-961c-a9a3255ea593","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"Disagreement about the accuracy of a certain phrase","passagePhrase":"coral reefs are often described as the 'rainforests of the sea' ... the comparison is dismissed by some naturalists, including David Attenborough ... You go there and the first thing you think is: where ... are the birds? Where are the animals? They are hiding in the trees, of course ... if you want beauty and wildlife, you want a coral reef. Put on a mask and stick your head under the water. The sight is mind-blowing.'"},{"uid":"35a9c675-8523-468b-99e7-a7cd0616c0b9","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"A warning of further trouble ahead","passagePhrase":"these majestic sights are now under very serious threat ... scientists advise that more than 90% of reefs could be lost by 2050 unless urgent action is taken to tackle global heating and greenhouse gas emissions ... Coral reefs are dying and they are telling us that all is not well with our planet."},{"uid":"f3c14601-e9bb-4a4f-bdae-e47cddcb955a","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"Increases in the warmth of the sea water","passagePhrase":"Rising ocean temperatures"},{"uid":"ca6cee36-746b-4a7b-95f8-1f2785cb6ec0","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"remove the","passagePhrase":"strip reefs of their colour"},{"uid":"d1ec059c-a70a-4b98-83e8-e6ae3d8e47d4","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"The contamination of the sea from waste","passagePhrase":"pollution by humans"},{"uid":"3eb314b2-283b-40be-83f9-56e88638bca6","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"The contamination of the sea from waste","passagePhrase":"pollution by humans"},{"uid":"1272d880-3bc6-4721-ae31-e1a909ebc02a","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"Alterations in the usual flow of water in the seas","passagePhrase":"ocean current changes"},{"uid":"122481d5-24d2-44b4-8323-a055988db804","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"Alterations in the usual flow of water in the seas","passagePhrase":"ocean current changes"},{"uid":"ca039c9a-1cda-4074-bd3c-d4d5f06619de","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"Working to lessen the problems","passagePhrase":"carry out research on species to find those that can survive best in warm, acidic waters ... try to increase coral breeding rates ... aquarium-based research has enabled some corals to spawn artificially, which can assist coral reef restoration efforts ... That would be a big help in restoring blighted reefs.'"},{"uid":"7f6342cd-1e5c-4e50-b921-63497497e4e6","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"identify corals that can cope well with the changed sea conditions","passagePhrase":"carry out research on species to find those that can survive best in warm, acidic waters"},{"uid":"54eff402-eaf0-4977-b599-b9c12161f09c","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"identify corals that can cope well with the changed sea conditions","passagePhrase":"carry out research on species to find those that can survive best in warm, acidic waters"},{"uid":"93c1fa67-589f-4024-880e-0b51cd26569c","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"trying out methods that would speed up reproduction in some corals","passagePhrase":"try to increase coral breeding rates ... aquarium-based research has enabled some corals to spawn artificially ... consider the launching of coral-spawning programmes several times a year"},{"uid":"3b3057ed-e9e7-4f18-b3cd-ed96973ed903","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"trying out methods that would speed up reproduction in some corals","passagePhrase":"try to increase coral breeding rates ... aquarium-based research has enabled some corals to spawn artificially ... consider the launching of coral-spawning programmes several times a year"},{"uid":"86f95ebf-db50-4d44-8cb6-80ac544bcc97","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"Promoting hope","passagePhrase":"the progress we make in making coral better able to survive in a warming world can be shown to the public ... encourage them to believe that we can do something to save the planet's reefs"}]},"reading_u2_315":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Robots and us</strong></p><p>Three leaders in their fields answer questions about our relationships with robot</p><p>When asked 'Should robots be used to colonise other planets?', cosmology and astrophysics Professor Martin Rees said he believed the solar system would be mapped by robotic craft by the end of the century. 'The next step would be mining of asteroids, enabling fabrication of large structures in space without having to bring all the raw materials from Earth. ... I think this is more realistic and benign than the ... \"terraforming\"* of planets.' He maintains that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5801ebe0-1232-4c15-a65a-653badd7af73\" data-question=\"34\">colonised planets 'should be preserved with a status that is analogous to Antarctica here on Earth<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.'</p><p>On the question of using robots to colonise other planets and exploit mineral resources, engineering Professor Daniel Wolpert replied, 'I don't see a pressing need to colonise other planets unless we can bring [these] resources back to Earth. The vast majority of Earth is currently inaccessible to us. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"749ea391-9832-4691-9777-1e5a1f62843b\" data-question=\"31\">Using robots to gather resources<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"904db01f-38e2-48ea-b4ca-c590042baa4e\" data-question=\"31\">nearer to home<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> would <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"749ea391-9832-4691-9777-1e5a1f62843b\" data-question=\"31\">seem to be a better use of our robotic tools<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>.'</p><p>Meanwhile, for anthropology Professor Kathleen Richardson, the idea of 'colonisation' of other planets seemed morally dubious: 'I think whether we do something on Earth or on Mars <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5801ebe0-1232-4c15-a65a-653badd7af73\" data-question=\"34\">we should always do it in the spirit of a genuine interest in \"the Other\"<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>, not to impose a particular model, but to meet \"the Other\".\"</p><p>In response to the second question, 'How soon will machine intelligence outstrip human intelligence?', <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48a78238-937d-477c-bec9-ea2bbe633191\" data-question=\"35\">Rees mentions robots that are advanced enough to beat humans at chess<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, but then goes on to say, '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48a78238-937d-477c-bec9-ea2bbe633191\" data-question=\"35\">Robots are still limited in their ability to sense their environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>: they can't yet recognise and move the pieces on a real chessboard as cleverly as a child can. Later this century, however, their more advanced successors may relate to their surroundings, and to people, as adeptly as we do. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8cf1e088-8453-4727-9047-2691d9354c92\" data-question=\"30\">Moral questions then arise. ... Should we feel guilty about exploiting [sophisticated robots]? Should we fret if they are underemployed, frustrated, or bored?'<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span></p><p>Wolpert's response to the question about machine intelligence outstripping human intelligence was this: 'In a limited sense it already has. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48a78238-937d-477c-bec9-ea2bbe633191\" data-question=\"35\">Machines can already navigate, remember and search for items with an ability that far outstrips humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. However, there is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"757dec97-eee1-4737-af40-59e205f92980\" data-question=\"29\">no machine that can identify visual objects or speech with the reliability and flexibility of humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>.... <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"757dec97-eee1-4737-af40-59e205f92980\" data-question=\"29\">Expecting a machine close to the creative intelligence of a human within the next 50 years would be highly ambitious.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>'</p><p>Richardson believes that our fear of machines becoming too advanced has more to do with human nature than anything intrinsic to the machines themselves. In her view, it <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47dbade7-e1c5-434e-89a6-bf3fd8d7a1dc\" data-question=\"37\">stems from<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> humans' <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62491640-6669-42c5-ac19-480c802b282a\" data-question=\"37\">tendency to personify<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> inanimate objects: we create machines based on representations of ourselves, imagine that machines think and behave as we do, and therefore see them as an autonomous threat. 'One of the consequences of thinking that the problem lies with machines is that we tend to imagine they are greater and more powerful than they really are and subsequently they become so.'</p><p>This led on to the third question, 'Should we be scared by advances in artificial intelligence?' To this question, Rees replied, 'Those who should be worried are the futurologists who believe in the so-called \"singularity\".** …And another worry is that we are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4240ec7-388b-4cdc-9acc-38c75f28d6af\" data-question=\"27\">increasingly dependent on computer networks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, and that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4240ec7-388b-4cdc-9acc-38c75f28d6af\" data-question=\"27\">these could <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"442a0a67-f494-469f-99c8-227556ab01fa\" data-question=\"38\">behave like a single \"brain\" with a mind of its own<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4240ec7-388b-4cdc-9acc-38c75f28d6af\" data-question=\"27\">with goals that may be contrary to human welfare<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. I think we should <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d02b6e1f-e58d-4779-b2f9-aadd506b91ea\" data-question=\"27\">ensure that robots remain as no more than \"idiot savants\" lacking the capacity to outwit us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, even though they may greatly surpass us in the ability to calculate and process information.'</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"595f8758-3f9d-46b9-8a42-2639b39b85e5\" data-question=\"36\">Wolpert's response was to say that we have already seen the damaging effects of artificial intelligence in the form of computer viruses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. 'But in this case,' he says, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"595f8758-3f9d-46b9-8a42-2639b39b85e5\" data-question=\"36\">'the real intelligence is the malicious designer<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Critically, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"595f8758-3f9d-46b9-8a42-2639b39b85e5\" data-question=\"36\">the benefits of computers outweigh the damage that computer viruses cause<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. Similarly, while there may be misuses of robotics in the near future, the benefits that they will bring are likely to outweigh these negative aspects.'</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"595f8758-3f9d-46b9-8a42-2639b39b85e5\" data-question=\"36\">Richardson's response<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span> to this question was this: 'We need to ask why <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26aaf43c-e1d2-4dd3-a90f-4989d3be6630\" data-question=\"28\">fears of artificial intelligence and robots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> persist; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"393dec68-0dbd-42cb-afff-ecdfe8f68e5e\" data-question=\"28\">none have in fact risen up and challenged human supremacy<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>.' She believes that as robots have never <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26aaf43c-e1d2-4dd3-a90f-4989d3be6630\" data-question=\"28\">shown themselves to be a threat to humans<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>, it seems unlikely that they ever will. In fact, she went on, 'Not all fear [robots]; <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a5a123b-917f-4cc9-9f19-5c12c60eb823\" data-question=\"33\">many people welcome machine intelligence.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>'</p><p>In answer to the fourth question, \"What can science fiction tell us about robotics?', Rees replied, 'I sometimes advise students that it's better to read <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"522f3495-96c4-4e1a-9edf-03b335408618\" data-question=\"32\">first-rate science fiction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> than <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"400db19f-6700-47fd-a1b5-fdc4c39e8c8c\" data-question=\"32\">second-rate science<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> - more stimulating, and perhaps <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d814117f-1503-4a20-b725-f0aae8459e20\" data-question=\"32\">no more likely to be wrong<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>.' As his response, Wolpert commented, 'Science fiction has often been remarkable at predicting the future.... Science fiction has painted a vivid spectrum of possible futures, from cute and helpful robots to dystopian robotic societies. Interestingly, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"358a34c0-41fa-4195-bffa-2179d75ec2fb\" data-question=\"39\">almost no science fiction envisages a future without robots.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>'</p><p>Finally, on the question of science fiction, Richardson pointed out that in modern society, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7a7a038c-1bc9-42c7-824a-e080fd1339d4\" data-question=\"40\">people tend to think there is reality on the one hand, and fiction and fantasy on the other<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. She then explained that the division did not always exist, and that scientists and technologists made this separation because they wanted to carve out the sphere of their work. 'But the divide is not so clear cut, and that is why the worlds seem to collide at times,' she said. '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7a7a038c-1bc9-42c7-824a-e080fd1339d4\" data-question=\"40\">In some cases, we need to bring these different understandings together to get a whole perspective.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> Perhaps then, we won't be so frightened that something we create as a copy of ourselves will be a [threat] to us.’<br>______________________________________<br><em>* terraforming: modifying a planet's atmosphere to suit human needs<br>** singularity: the point when robots will be able to start creating ever more sophisticated versions of themselves</em></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following statements (Questions 27-33) and the list of experts below. Match each statement with the correct expert, A, B or C. NB You may use any letter more than once.<br><strong>List of Experts</strong><br>A. Martin Rees<br>B. Daniel Wolpert<br>C. Kathleen Richardson</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223060\" id=\"question-wrapper-223060\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d4240ec7-388b-4cdc-9acc-38c75f28d6af\" data-question=\"27\">For our own safety<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>, humans will need to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d02b6e1f-e58d-4779-b2f9-aadd506b91ea\" data-question=\"27\">restrict the abilities of robots<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223061\" id=\"question-wrapper-223061\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"26aaf43c-e1d2-4dd3-a90f-4989d3be6630\" data-question=\"28\">The risk of robots harming us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"393dec68-0dbd-42cb-afff-ecdfe8f68e5e\" data-question=\"28\">less serious than humans believe it to be<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223062\" id=\"question-wrapper-223062\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"757dec97-eee1-4737-af40-59e205f92980\" data-question=\"29\">It will take many decades for robot intelligence to be as imaginative as human intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223063\" id=\"question-wrapper-223063\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> We may have to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8cf1e088-8453-4727-9047-2691d9354c92\" data-question=\"30\">start considering whether we are treating robots fairly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223064\" id=\"question-wrapper-223064\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Robots are probably <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"749ea391-9832-4691-9777-1e5a1f62843b\" data-question=\"31\">of more help to us<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> on Earth than in space. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223065\" id=\"question-wrapper-223065\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The ideas in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"522f3495-96c4-4e1a-9edf-03b335408618\" data-question=\"32\">high-quality science fiction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d814117f-1503-4a20-b725-f0aae8459e20\" data-question=\"32\">prove to be just as accurate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> as those found in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"400db19f-6700-47fd-a1b5-fdc4c39e8c8c\" data-question=\"32\">the work of mediocre scientists<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223066\" id=\"question-wrapper-223066\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0a5a123b-917f-4cc9-9f19-5c12c60eb823\" data-question=\"33\">There are those who look forward to robots developing greater intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-D, below.<br>A. robots to explore outer space.<br>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"48a78238-937d-477c-bec9-ea2bbe633191\" data-question=\"35\">advances made in machine intelligence so far<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>.<br>C. changes <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5801ebe0-1232-4c15-a65a-653badd7af73\" data-question=\"34\">made to other planets for our own benefit<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>.<br>D. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"595f8758-3f9d-46b9-8a42-2639b39b85e5\" data-question=\"36\">the harm already done by artificial intelligence<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223067\" id=\"question-wrapper-223067\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Richardson and Rees express <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5801ebe0-1232-4c15-a65a-653badd7af73\" data-question=\"34\">similar views<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span> regarding the ethical aspect of .................. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223068\" id=\"question-wrapper-223068\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Rees and Wolpert share an opinion about the extent of ..................... </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223069\" id=\"question-wrapper-223069\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Wolpert disagrees with Richardson on the question of ................... </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B, C, or D</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223070\" id=\"question-wrapper-223070\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What point does Richardson make about fear of machines? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. It has grown alongside the development of ever more advanced robots.</li> <li>B. It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"47dbade7-e1c5-434e-89a6-bf3fd8d7a1dc\" data-question=\"37\">the result of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> our <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"62491640-6669-42c5-ac19-480c802b282a\" data-question=\"37\">inclination to attribute human characteristics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1696065c-1f69-41f4-96fa-93f5f566406e\" data-question=\"37\">non-human entities<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span></li> <li>C. It has its origins in basic misunderstandings about how <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"1696065c-1f69-41f4-96fa-93f5f566406e\" data-question=\"37\">inanimate objects<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span> function.</li> <li>D. It demonstrates a key difference between human intelligence and machine intelligence.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223071\" id=\"question-wrapper-223071\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What potential advance does Rees see as a cause for concern? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Robots outnumbering people.</li> <li>B. Robots having abilities which humans do not.</li> <li>C. Artificial intelligence <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"442a0a67-f494-469f-99c8-227556ab01fa\" data-question=\"38\">developing independent thought<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Artificial intelligence taking over every aspect of our lives.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223072\" id=\"question-wrapper-223072\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What does Wolpert emphasise in his response to the question about science fiction? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. How science fiction influences our attitudes to robots.</li> <li>B. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"358a34c0-41fa-4195-bffa-2179d75ec2fb\" data-question=\"39\">How fundamental robots are to the science fiction genre<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>.</li> <li>C. How the image of robots in science fiction has changed over time.</li> <li>D. How reactions to similar portrayals of robots in science fiction may vary.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223073\" id=\"question-wrapper-223073\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> What is Richardson doing in her comment about reality and fantasy? </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> <ul> <li>A. Warning people not to confuse one with the other.</li> <li>B. Outlining ways in which one has impacted on the other.</li> <li>C. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"7a7a038c-1bc9-42c7-824a-e080fd1339d4\" data-question=\"40\">Recommending a change of approach in how people view them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>.</li> <li>D. Explaining why scientists have a different perspective on them from other people.</li> </ul> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"5801ebe0-1232-4c15-a65a-653badd7af73","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"made to other planets for our own benefit ... similar views","passagePhrase":"colonised planets 'should be preserved with a status that is analogous to Antarctica here on Earth ... we should always do it in the spirit of a genuine interest in \"the Other\""},{"uid":"749ea391-9832-4691-9777-1e5a1f62843b","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"of more help to us","passagePhrase":"Using robots to gather resources ... seem to be a better use of our robotic tools"},{"uid":"904db01f-38e2-48ea-b4ca-c590042baa4e","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"nearer to home"},{"uid":"48a78238-937d-477c-bec9-ea2bbe633191","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"advances made in machine intelligence so far","passagePhrase":"Rees mentions robots that are advanced enough to beat humans at chess ... Robots are still limited in their ability to sense their environment ... Machines can already navigate, remember and search for items with an ability that far outstrips humans"},{"uid":"8cf1e088-8453-4727-9047-2691d9354c92","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"start considering whether we are treating robots fairly","passagePhrase":"Moral questions then arise. ... Should we feel guilty about exploiting [sophisticated robots]? Should we fret if they are underemployed, frustrated, or bored?'"},{"uid":"757dec97-eee1-4737-af40-59e205f92980","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"It will take many decades for robot intelligence to be as imaginative as human intelligence","passagePhrase":"no machine that can identify visual objects or speech with the reliability and flexibility of humans ... Expecting a machine close to the creative intelligence of a human within the next 50 years would be highly ambitious."},{"uid":"47dbade7-e1c5-434e-89a6-bf3fd8d7a1dc","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"the result of","passagePhrase":"stems from"},{"uid":"62491640-6669-42c5-ac19-480c802b282a","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"inclination to attribute human characteristics","passagePhrase":"tendency to personify"},{"uid":"d4240ec7-388b-4cdc-9acc-38c75f28d6af","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"For our own safety","passagePhrase":"increasingly dependent on computer networks ... these could behave like a single \"brain\" with a mind of its own ... with goals that may be contrary to human welfare"},{"uid":"442a0a67-f494-469f-99c8-227556ab01fa","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"developing independent thought","passagePhrase":"behave like a single \"brain\" with a mind of its own"},{"uid":"d02b6e1f-e58d-4779-b2f9-aadd506b91ea","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"restrict the abilities of robots","passagePhrase":"ensure that robots remain as no more than \"idiot savants\" lacking the capacity to outwit us"},{"uid":"595f8758-3f9d-46b9-8a42-2639b39b85e5","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"the harm already done by artificial intelligence","passagePhrase":"Wolpert's response was to say that we have already seen the damaging effects of artificial intelligence in the form of computer viruses ... 'the real intelligence is the malicious designer ... the benefits of computers outweigh the damage that computer viruses cause ... Richardson's response"},{"uid":"26aaf43c-e1d2-4dd3-a90f-4989d3be6630","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"The risk of robots harming us","passagePhrase":"fears of artificial intelligence and robots ... shown themselves to be a threat to humans"},{"uid":"393dec68-0dbd-42cb-afff-ecdfe8f68e5e","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"less serious than humans believe it to be","passagePhrase":"none have in fact risen up and challenged human supremacy"},{"uid":"0a5a123b-917f-4cc9-9f19-5c12c60eb823","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"There are those who look forward to robots developing greater intelligence","passagePhrase":"many people welcome machine intelligence."},{"uid":"522f3495-96c4-4e1a-9edf-03b335408618","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"high-quality science fiction","passagePhrase":"first-rate science fiction"},{"uid":"400db19f-6700-47fd-a1b5-fdc4c39e8c8c","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"the work of mediocre scientists","passagePhrase":"second-rate science"},{"uid":"d814117f-1503-4a20-b725-f0aae8459e20","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"prove to be just as accurate","passagePhrase":"no more likely to be wrong"},{"uid":"358a34c0-41fa-4195-bffa-2179d75ec2fb","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"How fundamental robots are to the science fiction genre","passagePhrase":"almost no science fiction envisages a future without robots."},{"uid":"7a7a038c-1bc9-42c7-824a-e080fd1339d4","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"Recommending a change of approach in how people view them","passagePhrase":"people tend to think there is reality on the one hand, and fiction and fantasy on the other ... In some cases, we need to bring these different understandings together to get a whole perspective."},{"uid":"1696065c-1f69-41f4-96fa-93f5f566406e","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"non-human entities ... inanimate objects","passagePhrase":""}]},"reading_u2_316":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Georgia O'Keeffe</strong></p><p>For seven decades, Georgia O'Keeffe (1887-1986) was a major figure in American art. Remarkably, she <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"3a63bc24-fa50-4ba6-a931-05618456d031\" data-question=\"8\">remained independent from shifting art trends<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> and <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"3a63bc24-fa50-4ba6-a931-05618456d031\" data-question=\"8\">her work stayed true to her own vision<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span>, which was based on finding the essential, abstract forms in nature. With exceptionally keen powers of observation and great finesse with a paintbrush, she recorded subtle nuances of colour, shape, and light that enlivened her paintings and attracted a wide audience.</p><p>Born in 1887 near Sun Prairie, Wisconsin to cattle breeders Francis and Ida O'Keeffe, Georgia was raised on their farm along with her six siblings. By the time <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c0f3ee4-a142-488a-b530-4962001ebd7a\" data-question=\"9\">she graduated from high school<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span> in 1905, she <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d60aeef-9a80-478d-9384-537521d5cc5d\" data-question=\"9\">had determined to make her way as an artist<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. She studied the techniques of traditional painting at the Art Institute of Chicago school (1905) and the Art Students League of New York (1907-8). After <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f570212a-ce5d-44b5-b456-63b929ac74d7\" data-question=\"1\">attending university<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> and then training college, she <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0aa04155-f6a8-42d4-bb12-6768f82098f7\" data-question=\"1\">became an art teacher<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> and taught in elementary schools, high schools, and colleges in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a51a3477-385b-4968-8613-ef4be333d4ca\" data-question=\"1\">Virginia, Texas, and South Carolina<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> from 1911 to 1918.</p><p>During this period, O'Keeffe began to experiment with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bcf2c37f-e60d-4312-8270-dadde2af973b\" data-question=\"2\">creating abstract compositions<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> in charcoal, and produced a series of innovative drawings that led her art in a new direction. <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d38ce24d-c2d5-44f6-8a98-948b1b4ca119\" data-question=\"10\">She sent some of these drawings to a friend<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> in New York, <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d38ce24d-c2d5-44f6-8a98-948b1b4ca119\" data-question=\"10\">who showed them to art collector and photographer Alfred Stieglitz<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> in January 1916. Stieglitz was impressed, and exhibited the drawings later that year at his gallery on Fifth Avenue, New York City, where the works of many avant-garde artists and photographers were introduced to the American public.</p><p>With Stieglitz's encouragement and promise of financial support, O'Keeffe arrived in New York in June 1918 to begin a career as an artist. For the next three decades, Stieglitz vigorously promoted her work in twenty-two solo exhibitions and numerous group installations. The two were married in 1924. The ups and downs of their personal and professional relationship were recorded in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"30c95e8b-f2c1-41df-9401-302c974083cb\" data-question=\"11\">Stieglitz's celebrated black-and-white portraits of O'Keeffe<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>, taken over the course of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a45b703-fdb3-49bc-ad8d-02ee7334f5f8\" data-question=\"11\">twenty years (1917-37).<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span></p><p>By the mid-1920s, O'Keeffe was recognized as one of America's most important and successful artists, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bb228614-90f7-4014-8090-239f96d84f59\" data-question=\"3\">widely known for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"deb25771-31e2-4109-890a-b12f8a635d73\" data-question=\"3\">the architectural pictures that dramatically depict the soaring skyscrapers of New York.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> But most often, she painted botanical subjects, inspired by annual trips to the Stieglitz family summer home. In her <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af9a2da5-d313-4eb2-82c6-e41232f6295f\" data-question=\"4\">magnified<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"40d819c0-2b80-4324-abe9-37fb988543a7\" data-question=\"4\">images depicting flowers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>, begun in 1924, O'Keeffe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af9a2da5-d313-4eb2-82c6-e41232f6295f\" data-question=\"4\">brings the viewer right into the picture<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span>.</p><p>Enlarging the tiniest details to fill an entire metre-wide canvas emphasized their shapes and lines and made them appear abstract. Such daring compositions helped establish O'Keeffe's reputation as an innovative modernist.</p><p>In 1929, O'Keeffe made her first extended trip to the state of New Mexico. It was a visit that had a lasting impact on her life, and an immediate effect on her work. Over the next two decades she made almost annual trips to New Mexico, staying up to six months there, painting in relative solitude, then returning to New York each winter to exhibit the new work at Stieglitz's gallery. This pattern continued until she moved permanently to New Mexico in 1949.</p><p><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b9392ab-321d-4847-8cca-84822ab79919\" data-question=\"5\">There, O'Keeffe found<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> new inspiration: at first, it was the numerous sun-bleached bones she <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b9392ab-321d-4847-8cca-84822ab79919\" data-question=\"5\">came across<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span> in the state's rugged terrain that sparked her imagination. Two of her earliest and most celebrated Southwestern paintings exquisitely reproduce a cow skull's weathered surfaces, jagged edges, and irregular openings. Later, she also explored another variation on this theme in her large series of Pelvis pictures, which focused on the contrasts between convex and concave surfaces, and solid and open spaces.</p><p>However, it was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f06f376-d55f-42b0-aa1a-445c4a2b68b1\" data-question=\"6\">the region's spectacular landscape<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>, with its unusual geological formations, vivid colours, clarity of light, and exotic vegetation, that held the artist's imagination <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e60f92b-4bc7-421b-92f8-1a40328443a6\" data-question=\"6\">for more than four decades<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span>. Often, she painted the rocks, cliffs, and mountains in striking close-up, just as she had done with her botanical subjects. </p><p>O'Keeffe eventually owned two homes in New Mexico - the first, her summer retreat at Ghost Ranch, was nestled beneath 200-metre cliffs, while the second, used as her winter residence, was in the small town of Abiquiú. While both locales provided a wealth of imagery for her paintings, one feature of the Abiquiú house - the large walled patio with its black door - was particularly inspirational. In more than thirty pictures between 1946 and 1960, she reinvented the patio into an abstract arrangement of geometric shapes.</p><p>From the 1950s into the 1970s, O'Keeffe travelled widely, making trips to Asia, the Middle East, and Europe. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f5ed1352-cb01-4a87-b549-09b073d6a578\" data-question=\"7\">Flying in planes<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> inspired her last two major series – <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d272eb7f-8f95-4270-94b8-0c05923a4ddb\" data-question=\"7\">aerial views of rivers and expansive paintings of the sky<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e12977f1-380f-4ae1-a62e-a9e967fa3663\" data-question=\"7\">viewed from just above clouds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span>. In both series, O'Keeffe increased the size of her canvases, sometimes to mural proportions, reflecting perhaps her newly expanded view of the world. When in 1965 she successfully translated one of her cloud motifs to a monumental canvas measuring 6 metres in length (with the help of assistants), it was an enormous challenge and a special feat for an artist nearing eighty years of age.</p><p>The last two decades of the artist's life were relatively unproductive as ill health and blindness hindered her ability to work. O'Keeffe died in 1986 at the age of ninety-eight, but her rich legacy of some 900 paintings has continued to attract subsequent generations of artists and art lovers who derive inspiration from these very American images.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>The life and work of Georgia O'Keeffe</strong><br>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f570212a-ce5d-44b5-b456-63b929ac74d7\" data-question=\"1\">studied art<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span>, then <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0aa04155-f6a8-42d4-bb12-6768f82098f7\" data-question=\"1\">worked as a<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span> (1) .................. in <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a51a3477-385b-4968-8613-ef4be333d4ca\" data-question=\"1\">various places in the USA<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q1</span></span><br>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bcf2c37f-e60d-4312-8270-dadde2af973b\" data-question=\"2\">created drawings<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q2</span></span> using (2) .................. which were exhibited in New York City<br>● moved to New York and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bb228614-90f7-4014-8090-239f96d84f59\" data-question=\"3\">became famous for<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> her <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"deb25771-31e2-4109-890a-b12f8a635d73\" data-question=\"3\">paintings of the city's<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q3</span></span> (3) ..................<br>● produced a series of innovative <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af9a2da5-d313-4eb2-82c6-e41232f6295f\" data-question=\"4\">close-up<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q4</span></span> paintings of (4) ..................<br>● went to New Mexico and was initially inspired to paint the many (5) .................. that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b9392ab-321d-4847-8cca-84822ab79919\" data-question=\"5\">could be found there<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q5</span></span><br>● continued to paint various features that together formed the dramatic (6) .................. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2f06f376-d55f-42b0-aa1a-445c4a2b68b1\" data-question=\"6\">of New Mexico<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8e60f92b-4bc7-421b-92f8-1a40328443a6\" data-question=\"6\">for over forty years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q6</span></span><br>● <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f5ed1352-cb01-4a87-b549-09b073d6a578\" data-question=\"7\">travelled widely by plane<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> in later years, and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d272eb7f-8f95-4270-94b8-0c05923a4ddb\" data-question=\"7\">painted pictures of clouds and<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span> (7) .................. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e12977f1-380f-4ae1-a62e-a9e967fa3663\" data-question=\"7\">seen from above<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q7</span></span><br> </p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223074\" id=\"question-wrapper-223074\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>1</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TEACHER</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223075\" id=\"question-wrapper-223075\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>2</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CHARCOAL</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223076\" id=\"question-wrapper-223076\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>3</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">SKYSCRAPERS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223077\" id=\"question-wrapper-223077\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>4</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FLOWERS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223078\" id=\"question-wrapper-223078\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>5</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">BONES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223079\" id=\"question-wrapper-223079\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>6</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">LANDSCAPE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223080\" id=\"question-wrapper-223080\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>7</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">RIVERS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?<br>TRUE if the statement agrees with the information<br>FALSE if the statement contradicts the information<br>NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this<br> </p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223081\" id=\"question-wrapper-223081\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>8</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Georgia O'Keeffe's style was <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"3a63bc24-fa50-4ba6-a931-05618456d031\" data-question=\"8\">greatly influenced by the changing fashions in art<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q8</span></span> over the seven decades of her career. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223082\" id=\"question-wrapper-223082\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>9</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> When O'Keeffe <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"0c0f3ee4-a142-488a-b530-4962001ebd7a\" data-question=\"9\">finished high school<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>, she <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5d60aeef-9a80-478d-9384-537521d5cc5d\" data-question=\"9\">had already made her mind up about the career that she wanted<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q9</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223083\" id=\"question-wrapper-223083\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>10</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Alfred Stieglitz first discovered O'Keeffe's work when <span class=\"paraitem antonym\" data-uid=\"d38ce24d-c2d5-44f6-8a98-948b1b4ca119\" data-question=\"10\">she sent some abstract drawings to his gallery<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q10</span></span> in New York City. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FALSE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223084\" id=\"question-wrapper-223084\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>11</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"30c95e8b-f2c1-41df-9401-302c974083cb\" data-question=\"11\">O'Keeffe was the subject of Stieglitz's photographic work<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9a45b703-fdb3-49bc-ad8d-02ee7334f5f8\" data-question=\"11\">for many years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q11</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TRUE</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223085\" id=\"question-wrapper-223085\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>12</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> O'Keeffe's paintings of the patio of her house in Abiquiú were among the artist's favourite works. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223086\" id=\"question-wrapper-223086\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>13</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> O'Keeffe produced a greater quantity of work during the 1950s to 1970s than at any other time in her life. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">NOT GIVEN</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"0c0f3ee4-a142-488a-b530-4962001ebd7a","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"finished high school","passagePhrase":"she graduated from high school"},{"uid":"5d60aeef-9a80-478d-9384-537521d5cc5d","qNum":"9","questionPhrase":"had already made her mind up about the career that she wanted","passagePhrase":"had determined to make her way as an artist"},{"uid":"f570212a-ce5d-44b5-b456-63b929ac74d7","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"studied art","passagePhrase":"attending university"},{"uid":"0aa04155-f6a8-42d4-bb12-6768f82098f7","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"worked as a","passagePhrase":"became an art teacher"},{"uid":"a51a3477-385b-4968-8613-ef4be333d4ca","qNum":"1","questionPhrase":"various places in the USA","passagePhrase":"Virginia, Texas, and South Carolina"},{"uid":"bcf2c37f-e60d-4312-8270-dadde2af973b","qNum":"2","questionPhrase":"created drawings","passagePhrase":"creating abstract compositions"},{"uid":"30c95e8b-f2c1-41df-9401-302c974083cb","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"O'Keeffe was the subject of Stieglitz's photographic work","passagePhrase":"Stieglitz's celebrated black-and-white portraits of O'Keeffe"},{"uid":"9a45b703-fdb3-49bc-ad8d-02ee7334f5f8","qNum":"11","questionPhrase":"for many years","passagePhrase":"twenty years (1917-37)."},{"uid":"bb228614-90f7-4014-8090-239f96d84f59","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"became famous for","passagePhrase":"widely known for"},{"uid":"deb25771-31e2-4109-890a-b12f8a635d73","qNum":"3","questionPhrase":"paintings of the city's","passagePhrase":"the architectural pictures that dramatically depict the soaring skyscrapers of New York."},{"uid":"af9a2da5-d313-4eb2-82c6-e41232f6295f","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"close-up","passagePhrase":"magnified ... brings the viewer right into the picture"},{"uid":"40d819c0-2b80-4324-abe9-37fb988543a7","qNum":"4","questionPhrase":"","passagePhrase":"images depicting flowers"},{"uid":"2b9392ab-321d-4847-8cca-84822ab79919","qNum":"5","questionPhrase":"could be found there","passagePhrase":"There, O'Keeffe found ... came across"},{"uid":"2f06f376-d55f-42b0-aa1a-445c4a2b68b1","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"of New Mexico","passagePhrase":"the region's spectacular landscape"},{"uid":"8e60f92b-4bc7-421b-92f8-1a40328443a6","qNum":"6","questionPhrase":"for over forty years","passagePhrase":"for more than four decades"},{"uid":"f5ed1352-cb01-4a87-b549-09b073d6a578","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"travelled widely by plane","passagePhrase":"Flying in planes"},{"uid":"d272eb7f-8f95-4270-94b8-0c05923a4ddb","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"painted pictures of clouds and","passagePhrase":"aerial views of rivers and expansive paintings of the sky"},{"uid":"e12977f1-380f-4ae1-a62e-a9e967fa3663","qNum":"7","questionPhrase":"seen from above","passagePhrase":"viewed from just above clouds"}]},"reading_u2_317":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>Adapting to the effects of climate change</strong></p><p>A. All around the world, nations are already preparing for, and adapting to, climate change and its impacts. Even if we stopped all CO2 emissions tomorrow, we would continue to see the impact of the CO2 already released since industrial times, with <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c17b2ff7-2177-426a-b011-5ee761add619\" data-question=\"15\">scientists forecasting<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc1c6bee-ef84-4e6a-a584-57c08885a78b\" data-question=\"15\">global warming would continue for around 40 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span>. In the meantime, ice caps would continue to melt and sea levels rise. Some countries and regions will suffer more extreme impacts from these changes than others. It's in these places that innovation is thriving.</p><p>B. In Miami Beach, Florida, USA, seawater isn't just breaching the island city's walls, it's seeping up through the ground, so the only way to save the city is to lift it up above sea level. Starting in the lowest and most vulnerable neighbourhoods, roads have been raised by as much as 61 centimetres. The elevation work was carried out as part of Miami Beach's ambitious but much-needed stormwater-management programme. In addition to the road adaptations, the city has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f59be92f-29fd-4673-9768-e919b56409de\" data-question=\"18\">set up new pumps<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> that can remove up to 75,000 litres of water per minute. In the face of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff0d6a4a-a900-4ce7-a1b2-12ac7c21a415\" data-question=\"25\">floods, climate-mitigation strategies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> have often been overlooked, says Yanira Pineda, a senior sustainability coordinator. She knows that they're essential and that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9f17c96-9315-46ec-a639-030554d69ed8\" data-question=\"25\">the job is far from over<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. 'We know that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a507ac21-80cd-4321-9c17-83dd67191927\" data-question=\"25\">in 20, 30, 40 years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>, we'll need to go back in there and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff0d6a4a-a900-4ce7-a1b2-12ac7c21a415\" data-question=\"25\">adjust to the changing environment<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>,' she says.</p><p>C. Seawalls are a staple strategy for many coastal communities, but on the soft, muddy northern shores of Java, Indonesia, they frequently collapse, further exacerbating coastal erosion. There have been many attempts to restore the island's coastal mangroves: <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b360c5e-0d4b-4cf3-99e3-5e96112510a9\" data-question=\"14\">ecosystems of trees and shrubs that help defend coastal areas<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> by <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b360c5e-0d4b-4cf3-99e3-5e96112510a9\" data-question=\"14\">trapping sediment in their net-like root systems<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b360c5e-0d4b-4cf3-99e3-5e96112510a9\" data-question=\"14\">elevating the sea bed and dampening the energy of waves and tidal currents<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span>. But Susanna Tol of the not-for-profit organisation Wetlands International says that, while hugely popular, the majority of mangrove-planting projects fail. So, Wetlands International <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8f6433c8-65ff-4d17-a738-1836f10c6bee\" data-question=\"19\">started out with<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> a different approach, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"019b438b-66f5-4399-bc4f-fc6b4878239c\" data-question=\"19\">building semi-permeable dams<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span>, made from bamboo poles and brushwood, to mimic the role of mangrove roots and <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af18963a-7b8d-40b9-8234-4a35a4880bb5\" data-question=\"19\">create favourable conditions for mangroves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> to grow back naturally. The programme has seen moderate success, mainly in areas with less subsidence. 'Unfortunately, traditional infrastructure is often single-solution focused,' says Tol. 'For long-term success, it's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd23e76b-d14d-4128-acb1-d03cca79b81b\" data-question=\"23\">critical<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> that we <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4e359f7d-6996-4a2d-b932-4c6631769566\" data-question=\"23\">transition towards multifunctional approaches<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> that embed natural processes and that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb609541-873f-4c4a-9d3c-5d9a7aa6b8ce\" data-question=\"23\">engage and benefit communities and local decision-makers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>.’</p><p>D. As the floodwaters rose in the rice fields of the Mekong Delta in September 2018, four small houses rose with them. Homes in this part of Vietnam are traditionally built on stilts but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"199c9c3c-e1e3-4869-b2fb-6f96ceaa4fe1\" data-question=\"20\">these ones had been built to float<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span>. The modifications were made by the Buoyant Foundation Project, a not-for-profit organisation that has been researching and retrofitting amphibious houses since 2006. 'When I started this,' explains founder Elizabeth English, 'climate change was not on the tip of everybody's tongue, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56933940-7c2b-4e42-855a-e7649152a63a\" data-question=\"26\">this technology is becoming necessary in places that didn't previously need it.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>' It's <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8c12829-0c8a-4e50-84a2-83f83a773969\" data-question=\"16\">much cheaper than permanently elevating houses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>, English explains - <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8c12829-0c8a-4e50-84a2-83f83a773969\" data-question=\"16\">about a third of what it would cost to completely replace a building's foundations<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span>. It also avoids the problem of taller houses being at greater risk from wind damage. Another plus comes from the fact that amphibious structures can be sensitively adapted to meet cultural needs and match the kind of houses that are already common in a community.</p><p>E. Bangladesh is especially vulnerable to climate change. Most of the country is less than a metre above sea level and 80 per cent of its land lies on floodplains. 'Almost 35 million people living on the coastal belt of Bangladesh are currently affected by soil and water salinity,' says Raisa Chowdhury of the international development organisation ICCO Cooperation. Rather than fighting against it, one project is helping communities adapt to salt-affected soils. ICCO Cooperation has been working with 10,000 farmers in Bangladesh to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11aa13dc-35d6-4ac8-9380-130342184183\" data-question=\"21\">start cultivating<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28209b77-a5b7-4121-83dc-f0e75392469c\" data-question=\"21\">naturally salt-tolerant crops<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> in the region. Certain varieties of carrot, potato, kohlrabi, cabbage and beetroot have been found to be better suited to salty soil than the rice and wheat that is typically grown there. Chowdhury says that the results are very visible, comparing a barren plot of land to the 'beautiful, lush green vegetable garden' sitting beside it, in which he and his team have been working with the farmers. Since the project began, farmers trained in saline agriculture have reported increases of two to three more harvests per year.</p><p>F. Greg Spotts from Los Angeles (LA) in the USA is chief sustainability officer of the city's street services department. He leads the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"750af8ab-3560-44c0-912b-f501301fb0a0\" data-question=\"22\">Cool Streets LA programme<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span>, a series of pilot projects, which include the <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cf0f89a-8e88-4615-9fcc-a97433199283\" data-question=\"22\">planting of trees<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> and the installation or a 'cool pavement' system, designed to help reach the city's goal of bringing down its average temperature by 1.5°C. '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51b432af-bfb3-4b31-ac93-85cf69cba551\" data-question=\"24\">Urban cooling<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> is literally <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e2a7010-51f9-4ba6-a76e-4d57ab16ffb4\" data-question=\"24\">a matter of life and death<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> for our future in LA,' says Spotts. Using <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3aa9ca6f-8a44-4bcb-a16a-eed472bdb39a\" data-question=\"17\">a Geographic Information System data mapping tool, the programme identified streets with low tree canopy cover in three of the city's neighbourhoods<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> and covered them with a light-grey, light-reflecting coating, which had already been shown to lower road surface temperature in Los Angeles by 6°C. Spotts says one of these streets, in the Winnetka neighbourhood of San Fernando Valley, can now be seen as a pale crescent, the only cool spot on an otherwise red thermal image, from the International Space Station.</p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A-F. Which paragraph contains the following information?</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223087\" id=\"question-wrapper-223087\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>14</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> How <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"2b360c5e-0d4b-4cf3-99e3-5e96112510a9\" data-question=\"14\">a type of plant functions as a natural protection for coastlines<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q14</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223088\" id=\"question-wrapper-223088\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>15</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"c17b2ff7-2177-426a-b011-5ee761add619\" data-question=\"15\">A prediction<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"dc1c6bee-ef84-4e6a-a584-57c08885a78b\" data-question=\"15\">how long it could take to stop noticing the effects of climate change<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q15</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223089\" id=\"question-wrapper-223089\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>16</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A reference to the fact that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e8c12829-0c8a-4e50-84a2-83f83a773969\" data-question=\"16\">a solution is particularly cost-effective<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q16</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223090\" id=\"question-wrapper-223090\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>17</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A mention of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3aa9ca6f-8a44-4bcb-a16a-eed472bdb39a\" data-question=\"17\">a technology used to locate areas most in need of intervention<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q17</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">F</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the sentences below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223091\" id=\"question-wrapper-223091\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>18</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> The stormwater-management programme in Miami Beach has involved <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f59be92f-29fd-4673-9768-e919b56409de\" data-question=\"18\">the installation of efficient<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q18</span></span> (18) ................. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">PUMPS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223092\" id=\"question-wrapper-223092\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>19</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"019b438b-66f5-4399-bc4f-fc6b4878239c\" data-question=\"19\">The construction of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> (19) ................... was <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"8f6433c8-65ff-4d17-a738-1836f10c6bee\" data-question=\"19\">the first stage of a project<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"af18963a-7b8d-40b9-8234-4a35a4880bb5\" data-question=\"19\">ensure the success of mangroves<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q19</span></span> in Indonesia. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DAMS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223093\" id=\"question-wrapper-223093\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>20</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> As a response to rising floodwaters in the Mekong Delta, a not-for-profit organisation has been <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"199c9c3c-e1e3-4869-b2fb-6f96ceaa4fe1\" data-question=\"20\">building houses that can<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q20</span></span> (20) ................ </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FLOAT</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223094\" id=\"question-wrapper-223094\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>21</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Rising sea levels in Bangladesh have made it necessary to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11aa13dc-35d6-4ac8-9380-130342184183\" data-question=\"21\">introduce<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span> various (21) ............... that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"28209b77-a5b7-4121-83dc-f0e75392469c\" data-question=\"21\">are suitable for areas of high salt content<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q21</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">CROPS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223095\" id=\"question-wrapper-223095\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>22</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"750af8ab-3560-44c0-912b-f501301fb0a0\" data-question=\"22\">A project in LA<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> has <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5cf0f89a-8e88-4615-9fcc-a97433199283\" data-question=\"22\">increased the number of<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q22</span></span> (22) .............. on the city’s streets. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">TREES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following statements (Questions 23-26) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-E.<br><strong>List of People</strong><br>A. Yanira Pineda<br>B. Susanna Tol<br>C. Elizabeth English<br>D. Raisa Chowdhury<br>E. Greg Spotts</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223096\" id=\"question-wrapper-223096\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>23</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> It is <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bd23e76b-d14d-4128-acb1-d03cca79b81b\" data-question=\"23\">essential<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4e359f7d-6996-4a2d-b932-4c6631769566\" data-question=\"23\">adopt strategies<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span> which <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"cb609541-873f-4c4a-9d3c-5d9a7aa6b8ce\" data-question=\"23\">involve and help residents of the region<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q23</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223097\" id=\"question-wrapper-223097\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>24</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"51b432af-bfb3-4b31-ac93-85cf69cba551\" data-question=\"24\">Interventions which reduce heat<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"9e2a7010-51f9-4ba6-a76e-4d57ab16ffb4\" data-question=\"24\">absolutely vital for our survival<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q24</span></span> in this location. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223098\" id=\"question-wrapper-223098\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>25</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"f9f17c96-9315-46ec-a639-030554d69ed8\" data-question=\"25\">More work will need to be done<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a507ac21-80cd-4321-9c17-83dd67191927\" data-question=\"25\">in future decades<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span> to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"ff0d6a4a-a900-4ce7-a1b2-12ac7c21a415\" data-question=\"25\">deal with the impact of rising water levels<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q25</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223099\" id=\"question-wrapper-223099\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>26</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"56933940-7c2b-4e42-855a-e7649152a63a\" data-question=\"26\">The number of locations requiring action to adapt to flooding has grown in recent years<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q26</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"c17b2ff7-2177-426a-b011-5ee761add619","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"A prediction","passagePhrase":"scientists forecasting"},{"uid":"dc1c6bee-ef84-4e6a-a584-57c08885a78b","qNum":"15","questionPhrase":"how long it could take to stop noticing the effects of climate change","passagePhrase":"global warming would continue for around 40 years"},{"uid":"f59be92f-29fd-4673-9768-e919b56409de","qNum":"18","questionPhrase":"the installation of efficient","passagePhrase":"set up new pumps"},{"uid":"ff0d6a4a-a900-4ce7-a1b2-12ac7c21a415","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"deal with the impact of rising water levels","passagePhrase":"floods, climate-mitigation strategies ... adjust to the changing environment"},{"uid":"f9f17c96-9315-46ec-a639-030554d69ed8","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"More work will need to be done","passagePhrase":"the job is far from over"},{"uid":"a507ac21-80cd-4321-9c17-83dd67191927","qNum":"25","questionPhrase":"in future decades","passagePhrase":"in 20, 30, 40 years"},{"uid":"2b360c5e-0d4b-4cf3-99e3-5e96112510a9","qNum":"14","questionPhrase":"a type of plant functions as a natural protection for coastlines","passagePhrase":"ecosystems of trees and shrubs that help defend coastal areas ... trapping sediment in their net-like root systems ... elevating the sea bed and dampening the energy of waves and tidal currents"},{"uid":"8f6433c8-65ff-4d17-a738-1836f10c6bee","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"the first stage of a project","passagePhrase":"started out with"},{"uid":"019b438b-66f5-4399-bc4f-fc6b4878239c","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"The construction of","passagePhrase":"building semi-permeable dams"},{"uid":"af18963a-7b8d-40b9-8234-4a35a4880bb5","qNum":"19","questionPhrase":"ensure the success of mangroves","passagePhrase":"create favourable conditions for mangroves"},{"uid":"bd23e76b-d14d-4128-acb1-d03cca79b81b","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"essential","passagePhrase":"critical"},{"uid":"4e359f7d-6996-4a2d-b932-4c6631769566","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"adopt strategies","passagePhrase":"transition towards multifunctional approaches"},{"uid":"cb609541-873f-4c4a-9d3c-5d9a7aa6b8ce","qNum":"23","questionPhrase":"involve and help residents of the region","passagePhrase":"engage and benefit communities and local decision-makers"},{"uid":"199c9c3c-e1e3-4869-b2fb-6f96ceaa4fe1","qNum":"20","questionPhrase":"building houses that can","passagePhrase":"these ones had been built to float"},{"uid":"56933940-7c2b-4e42-855a-e7649152a63a","qNum":"26","questionPhrase":"The number of locations requiring action to adapt to flooding has grown in recent years","passagePhrase":"this technology is becoming necessary in places that didn't previously need it."},{"uid":"e8c12829-0c8a-4e50-84a2-83f83a773969","qNum":"16","questionPhrase":"a solution is particularly cost-effective","passagePhrase":"much cheaper than permanently elevating houses ... about a third of what it would cost to completely replace a building's foundations"},{"uid":"11aa13dc-35d6-4ac8-9380-130342184183","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"introduce","passagePhrase":"start cultivating"},{"uid":"28209b77-a5b7-4121-83dc-f0e75392469c","qNum":"21","questionPhrase":"are suitable for areas of high salt content","passagePhrase":"naturally salt-tolerant crops"},{"uid":"750af8ab-3560-44c0-912b-f501301fb0a0","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"A project in LA","passagePhrase":"Cool Streets LA programme"},{"uid":"5cf0f89a-8e88-4615-9fcc-a97433199283","qNum":"22","questionPhrase":"increased the number of","passagePhrase":"planting of trees"},{"uid":"51b432af-bfb3-4b31-ac93-85cf69cba551","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"Interventions which reduce heat","passagePhrase":"Urban cooling"},{"uid":"9e2a7010-51f9-4ba6-a76e-4d57ab16ffb4","qNum":"24","questionPhrase":"absolutely vital for our survival","passagePhrase":"a matter of life and death"},{"uid":"3aa9ca6f-8a44-4bcb-a16a-eed472bdb39a","qNum":"17","questionPhrase":"a technology used to locate areas most in need of intervention","passagePhrase":"a Geographic Information System data mapping tool, the programme identified streets with low tree canopy cover in three of the city's neighbourhoods"}]},"reading_u2_318":{"leftHtml":"<div><p><strong>A new role for livestock guard dogs</strong></p><p>Livestock guard dogs, traditionally used to protect farm animals from predators, are now being used to protect the predators themselves</p><p>A. For thousands of years, livestock guard dogs worked alongside shepherds to protect their sheep, goats and cattle from predators such as wolves and bears. But in the 19th and 20th centuries, when such predators were largely exterminated, most guard dogs lost their jobs. In recent years, however, as increased efforts have been made to protect wild animals, predators have become more widespread again. As a result, farmers once more need to protect their livestock, and guard dogs are enjoying an unexpected revival.</p><p>B. Today there are around 50 breeds of guard dogs on duty in various parts of the world. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d78cf352-00af-4eb1-b0c3-bf29d71e5fd3\" data-question=\"31\">These dogs are raised from an early age with the animals they will be watching and eventually these animals become the dog's family<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3bdf828-4d9a-4b87-8e3e-2f87eae60391\" data-question=\"29\">The dogs will place themselves between the livestock and any threat, barking loudly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3bdf828-4d9a-4b87-8e3e-2f87eae60391\" data-question=\"29\">If necessary, they will chase away predators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span>, but often their mere presence is sufficient. '<span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d78cf352-00af-4eb1-b0c3-bf29d71e5fd3\" data-question=\"31\">Their initial training is to make them understand that livestock is going to be their life<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span>,' says Dan Macon, a shepherd with three guard dogs. 'A fluffy white puppy is fun to be around, but <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6f2f120-f8dd-4e51-a0b5-35aa23a7d926\" data-question=\"36\">too much human affection makes it a great dog for guarding the front porch, rather than a great livestock guard dog.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>'</p><p>C. The evidence indicates that guard dogs are highly effective. For example, in Portugal, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5648af5f-424a-47f6-bef1-595365aeb8de\" data-question=\"30\">biologist Silvia Ribeiro<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> has found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da8d84a7-2e75-40ac-aba2-3ac7b36b56d4\" data-question=\"30\">more than 90 per cent of the farmers participating in a programme to train and use guard dogs to protect their herds against attack from wolves rate the performance of the dogs as very good or excellent<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. In <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5648af5f-424a-47f6-bef1-595365aeb8de\" data-question=\"30\">a study carried out in Australia by Linda van Bommel and Chris Johnson at the University of Tasmania<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da8d84a7-2e75-40ac-aba2-3ac7b36b56d4\" data-question=\"30\">more than 65 per cent of herders reported that predation stopped completely after they got the dogs, and almost all the rest saw a decrease in attacks<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span>. 'If they are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"00135711-4b98-440c-9851-cbf33204adc1\" data-question=\"35\">managed and used properly<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, livestock guard dogs are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a81acf28-3254-40dd-8815-6774414c5726\" data-question=\"35\">the most efficient control method<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span> that we have in terms of the amount of livestock that they save from predation,' says van Bommel.</p><p>D. But today's guard dogs also have a new role - to help preserve the predators. It is hoped that reductions in livestock losses can make farmers more tolerant of predators and less likely to kill them. In Namibia, more than 90 per cent of cheetahs live outside protected areas, close to humans raising livestock. As a result, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bb17bbac-8eb8-491a-bce6-a60f7e35e163\" data-question=\"27\">the cheetahs are often held responsible for animal losses, and large numbers have been killed by farmers<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bb17bbac-8eb8-491a-bce6-a60f7e35e163\" data-question=\"27\"><span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5098de3c-967c-4a17-9777-72b1ef1f458b\" data-question=\"32\">When guard dogs were introduced<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, more than 90 per cent of farmers reported <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ce2f6b4-e357-4f2c-8609-0eb06269daaa\" data-question=\"32\">a dramatic reduction in livestock losses<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>, and said that as a result <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ce2f6b4-e357-4f2c-8609-0eb06269daaa\" data-question=\"32\">they were less likely to kill predators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span><span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span>. Julie Young, at Utah State University in the US, believes this result applies widely. 'There is common ground from the livestock perspective and from the conservation perspective,' she says. 'If ranchers don't have a dead cow, they will not make a call to apply for a permit to kill a wolf.'</p><p>E. Looking at all the published evidence, Bethany Smith at Nottingham Trent University in the UK found that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04ace081-ec87-4b78-a36a-4ebcb2c0bc24\" data-question=\"33\">up to 88 per cent of farmers said they no longer killed predators after using dogs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> - but warned that such <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04ace081-ec87-4b78-a36a-4ebcb2c0bc24\" data-question=\"33\">self-reported results<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04a1bc2f-4a17-4d5a-ad1b-d481ad578ce9\" data-question=\"33\">must be taken with a pinch of salt<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. What's more, it is possible that livestock guard dogs merely displace predators to unprotected neighbouring properties, where their fate isn't recorded. 'In some regions, we work with almost every farmer, but in others only one or two have dogs,' says Ribeiro. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"663e55e5-fc77-4158-99cc-4b07cf72fb70\" data-question=\"34\">'If we are not working with everybody, we are transferring the wolf pressure to the neighbour's herd and he can use poison and kill an entire pack of wolves.'<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span></p><p>F. Another concern is whether there may be unintended ecological effects of using guard dogs. Studies suggest that reducing deaths of one type of predator may have a negative impact on other species. The extent of this problem isn't known, but the consequences are clear in Namibia. Cheetahs aren't the only species that cause sheep and goat losses there: other predators also attack livestock. In 2015, researchers reported that in spite of the impact farmers obtaining guard dogs had on cheetahs, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2eb6f4f-d360-4123-8a98-81b2f4a49cd3\" data-question=\"37\">the number of jackals killed by dogs and people actually increased<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>. Guard dogs have other ecological impacts too. They have been found to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11e6bf9d-d6c7-41be-a8ae-9b0766de7c5e\" data-question=\"38\">spread diseases to wild animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, including endangered Ethiopian wolves. They may also <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ac6a105-71d4-4b1c-9bfe-b9bb684a2f70\" data-question=\"39\">compete with other carnivores for food.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> And by creating a 'landscape of fear', their mere presence can influence the behaviour of prey animals.</p><p>G. The evidence so far, however, indicates that these consequences aren't always negative. <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4ef5f1b0-3a28-454e-a37a-cbbc965a2860\" data-question=\"28\">Guard dogs can deliver unexpected benefits by protecting vulnerable wildlife from predators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. For example, their presence has been found to protect birds which build their nests on the ground in fields, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e206bf86-ca99-485b-a64f-098b150dc903\" data-question=\"40\">where foxes would normally raid them<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span>. Indeed, <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4ef5f1b0-3a28-454e-a37a-cbbc965a2860\" data-question=\"28\">Australian researchers are now using dogs to enhance biodiversity and create refuges for species threatened by predation<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span>. So if we can get this right, there may be <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4ef5f1b0-3a28-454e-a37a-cbbc965a2860\" data-question=\"28\">a bright future for guard dogs in promoting harmonious coexistence between humans and wildlife.<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span></p></div>","rightHtml":"<div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Reading Passage 3 has seven paragraphs, A-G. Which paragraph contains the following information? NB You may use any letter more than once.</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223100\" id=\"question-wrapper-223100\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>27</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> An example of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"bb17bbac-8eb8-491a-bce6-a60f7e35e163\" data-question=\"27\">how one predator has been protected by the introduction of livestock guard dogs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q27</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223101\" id=\"question-wrapper-223101\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>28</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> An optimistic suggestion about <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"4ef5f1b0-3a28-454e-a37a-cbbc965a2860\" data-question=\"28\">the possible positive developments in the use of livestock guard dogs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q28</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">G</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223102\" id=\"question-wrapper-223102\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>29</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A description of <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b3bdf828-4d9a-4b87-8e3e-2f87eae60391\" data-question=\"29\">how the methods used by livestock guard dogs help to keep predators away<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q29</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223103\" id=\"question-wrapper-223103\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>30</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5648af5f-424a-47f6-bef1-595365aeb8de\" data-question=\"30\">Claims by different academics<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> that <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"da8d84a7-2e75-40ac-aba2-3ac7b36b56d4\" data-question=\"30\">the use of livestock guard dogs is a successful way of protecting farmers' herds<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q30</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223104\" id=\"question-wrapper-223104\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>31</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> A reference to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"d78cf352-00af-4eb1-b0c3-bf29d71e5fd3\" data-question=\"31\">how livestock guard dogs gain their skills<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q31</span></span> </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Look at the following statements (Questions 32-36) and the list of people below.<br>Match each statement with the correct person, A-E.<br><strong>List of people</strong><br>A. Dan Macon<br>B. Silvia Ribeiro<br>C. Linda van Bommel<br>D. Julie Young<br>E. Bethany Smith</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223105\" id=\"question-wrapper-223105\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>32</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5098de3c-967c-4a17-9777-72b1ef1f458b\" data-question=\"32\">The use of guard dogs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span> may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"3ce2f6b4-e357-4f2c-8609-0eb06269daaa\" data-question=\"32\">save the lives of both livestock and wild animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q32</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">D</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223106\" id=\"question-wrapper-223106\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>33</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04ace081-ec87-4b78-a36a-4ebcb2c0bc24\" data-question=\"33\">Claims of a change in behaviour from those using livestock guard dogs<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"04a1bc2f-4a17-4d5a-ad1b-d481ad578ce9\" data-question=\"33\">may not be totally accurate<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q33</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">E</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223107\" id=\"question-wrapper-223107\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>34</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"663e55e5-fc77-4158-99cc-4b07cf72fb70\" data-question=\"34\">There may be negative results if the use of livestock guard dogs is not sufficiently widespread<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q34</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">B</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223108\" id=\"question-wrapper-223108\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>35</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> Livestock guard dogs are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a81acf28-3254-40dd-8815-6774414c5726\" data-question=\"35\">the best way of protecting farm animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>, as long as the dogs are <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"00135711-4b98-440c-9851-cbf33204adc1\" data-question=\"35\">appropriately handled<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q35</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">C</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223109\" id=\"question-wrapper-223109\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>36</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-text\"> <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"b6f2f120-f8dd-4e51-a0b5-35aa23a7d926\" data-question=\"36\">Teaching a livestock guard dog how to do its work needs a different focus from teaching a house guard dog<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q36</span></span>. </div> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">A</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"question-group-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-wrapper\"> <div class=\"context-content\"> <div><p>Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.</p><p><strong>Unintended ecological effects of using guard dogs</strong><br>In Namibia, livestock guard dogs have been used to protect domestic animals from attacks by cheetahs. This has led to <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"a2eb6f4f-d360-4123-8a98-81b2f4a49cd3\" data-question=\"37\">a rise in the deaths of other predators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q37</span></span>, particularly (37) ............... In addition, it has been suggested that the dogs could have (38) .............., <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"11e6bf9d-d6c7-41be-a8ae-9b0766de7c5e\" data-question=\"38\">which may affect other species<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q38</span></span>, and that they may <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ac6a105-71d4-4b1c-9bfe-b9bb684a2f70\" data-question=\"39\">reduce the amount<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span> of (39) ............... <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"5ac6a105-71d4-4b1c-9bfe-b9bb684a2f70\" data-question=\"39\">available to certain wild animals<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q39</span></span>. On the other hand, these dogs may help birds by protecting their nests. These might otherwise <span class=\"paraitem synonym\" data-uid=\"e206bf86-ca99-485b-a64f-098b150dc903\" data-question=\"40\">be threatened by predators<span class=\"paraitem-question\">Q40</span></span> such as (40) ..................</p></div> </div> </div> <div class=\"questions-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223110\" id=\"question-wrapper-223110\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>37</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">JACKALS</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223111\" id=\"question-wrapper-223111\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>38</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">DISEASES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223112\" id=\"question-wrapper-223112\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>39</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOOD</div> </div> </div></div> </div> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-item-wrapper\"> <div class=\"question-wrapper\" data-qid=\"223113\" id=\"question-wrapper-223113\"> <div class=\"question-number\"> <strong>40</strong> </div> <div class=\"question-content\"> <div class=\"question-answers\"> </div> <div class=\"mt-2 text-success question-correct\">FOXES</div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>","pairs":[{"uid":"d78cf352-00af-4eb1-b0c3-bf29d71e5fd3","qNum":"31","questionPhrase":"how livestock guard dogs gain their skills","passagePhrase":"These dogs are raised from an early age with the animals they will be watching and eventually these animals become the dog's family ... Their initial training is to make them understand that livestock is going to be their life"},{"uid":"b3bdf828-4d9a-4b87-8e3e-2f87eae60391","qNum":"29","questionPhrase":"how the methods used by livestock guard dogs help to keep predators away","passagePhrase":"The dogs will place themselves between the livestock and any threat, barking loudly ... If necessary, they will chase away predators"},{"uid":"b6f2f120-f8dd-4e51-a0b5-35aa23a7d926","qNum":"36","questionPhrase":"Teaching a livestock guard dog how to do its work needs a different focus from teaching a house guard dog","passagePhrase":"too much human affection makes it a great dog for guarding the front porch, rather than a great livestock guard dog."},{"uid":"5648af5f-424a-47f6-bef1-595365aeb8de","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"Claims by different academics","passagePhrase":"biologist Silvia Ribeiro ... a study carried out in Australia by Linda van Bommel and Chris Johnson at the University of Tasmania"},{"uid":"da8d84a7-2e75-40ac-aba2-3ac7b36b56d4","qNum":"30","questionPhrase":"the use of livestock guard dogs is a successful way of protecting farmers' herds","passagePhrase":"more than 90 per cent of the farmers participating in a programme to train and use guard dogs to protect their herds against attack from wolves rate the performance of the dogs as very good or excellent ... more than 65 per cent of herders reported that predation stopped completely after they got the dogs, and almost all the rest saw a decrease in attacks"},{"uid":"00135711-4b98-440c-9851-cbf33204adc1","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"appropriately handled","passagePhrase":"managed and used properly"},{"uid":"a81acf28-3254-40dd-8815-6774414c5726","qNum":"35","questionPhrase":"the best way of protecting farm animals","passagePhrase":"the most efficient control method"},{"uid":"bb17bbac-8eb8-491a-bce6-a60f7e35e163","qNum":"27","questionPhrase":"how one predator has been protected by the introduction of livestock guard dogs","passagePhrase":"the cheetahs are often held responsible for animal losses, and large numbers have been killed by farmers ... When guard dogs were introduced, more than 90 per cent of farmers reported a dramatic reduction in livestock losses, and said that as a result they were less likely to kill predators"},{"uid":"5098de3c-967c-4a17-9777-72b1ef1f458b","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"The use of guard dogs","passagePhrase":"When guard dogs were introduced"},{"uid":"3ce2f6b4-e357-4f2c-8609-0eb06269daaa","qNum":"32","questionPhrase":"save the lives of both livestock and wild animals","passagePhrase":"a dramatic reduction in livestock losses ... they were less likely to kill predators"},{"uid":"04ace081-ec87-4b78-a36a-4ebcb2c0bc24","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"Claims of a change in behaviour from those using livestock guard dogs","passagePhrase":"up to 88 per cent of farmers said they no longer killed predators after using dogs ... self-reported results"},{"uid":"04a1bc2f-4a17-4d5a-ad1b-d481ad578ce9","qNum":"33","questionPhrase":"may not be totally accurate","passagePhrase":"must be taken with a pinch of salt"},{"uid":"663e55e5-fc77-4158-99cc-4b07cf72fb70","qNum":"34","questionPhrase":"There may be negative results if the use of livestock guard dogs is not sufficiently widespread","passagePhrase":"'If we are not working with everybody, we are transferring the wolf pressure to the neighbour's herd and he can use poison and kill an entire pack of wolves.'"},{"uid":"a2eb6f4f-d360-4123-8a98-81b2f4a49cd3","qNum":"37","questionPhrase":"a rise in the deaths of other predators","passagePhrase":"the number of jackals killed by dogs and people actually increased"},{"uid":"11e6bf9d-d6c7-41be-a8ae-9b0766de7c5e","qNum":"38","questionPhrase":"which may affect other species","passagePhrase":"spread diseases to wild animals"},{"uid":"5ac6a105-71d4-4b1c-9bfe-b9bb684a2f70","qNum":"39","questionPhrase":"reduce the amount ... available to certain wild animals","passagePhrase":"compete with other carnivores for food."},{"uid":"4ef5f1b0-3a28-454e-a37a-cbbc965a2860","qNum":"28","questionPhrase":"the possible positive developments in the use of livestock guard dogs","passagePhrase":"Guard dogs can deliver unexpected benefits by protecting vulnerable wildlife from predators ... Australian researchers are now using dogs to enhance biodiversity and create refuges for species threatened by predation ... a bright future for guard dogs in promoting harmonious coexistence between humans and wildlife."},{"uid":"e206bf86-ca99-485b-a64f-098b150dc903","qNum":"40","questionPhrase":"be threatened by predators","passagePhrase":"where foxes would normally raid them"}]}};
